{"job":{"id":20019869,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Durham NC - TASK6310858 - 9/25 - 9am","description":{"html":"<p>&nbsp;<strong><u>WHEN TECH IS ONSITE - CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Step 1:&nbsp;Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Tech:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;&nbsp;- Name:&nbsp;Sharat Kumar Maruwada</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;&nbsp;- Phone #:&nbsp;+1-512-516-4731</u></strong></p><p>---------</p><p>&nbsp;ISSUE</p><p>---------</p><p>SNP out-of-band (OOB) management switch mwarb-oob2 is unreachable (100% ping loss from NetGate to</p><p>10.89.54.6; not visible via LLDP from neighbors oob1 or rc1-1).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>is a physical check(troubleshooting) + power-cycle to recover the existing unit.</p><p><br></p><p>Device details:</p><p>mwarb-oob2 — SNP OOB management switch, MDF/network rack (near oob1, dist1/2, mdf1-4). SN QTWTI21140098.</p><p><br></p><p>--------------</p><p>&nbsp;REQUEST</p><p>--------------</p><p>Note: Preferred dispatch timings : 8:00AM - 4:00PM CST</p><p><br></p><p>Please dispatch TechNet tech to:</p><p>- Locate mwarb-oob2 in the MDF/network rack (labeled oob2). Report status LEDs (off/amber/blinking/normal).</p><p>- Confirm the power cable is seated at the switch and the outlet/PDU, and the outlet is live.</p><p>- Power-cycle: unplug ~30s, plug back in, allow ~15-20 min to boot, report LED status.</p><p>- If it does not power up, try a known-good outlet/PDU port.</p><p>- If still offline and a console port is available, connect via PuTTY and report boot output /</p><p>&nbsp;whether it is stuck at a boot prompt / completely dead.</p><p>- Do NOT unplug or move any other switch, and do NOT remove/replace any SFP — power-cycle only.</p><p>- Photograph the switch front (LEDs) and rack label.</p><p><br></p><p>*Material that might be needed:</p><p>- spare patch cable, console cable for PuTTY check.</p><p><br></p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>&nbsp;WHEN TECH IS ONSITE - CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS</p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Step 1:&nbsp;Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Tech:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- Name:&nbsp;Sharat Kumar Maruwada</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- Phone #:&nbsp;+1-512-516-4731</p><p>Note: If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation - Step 2</p><p><br></p><p>Step 2: Send email:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- To:&nbsp;page-msharatk@amazon.com</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- Cc:&nbsp;wfmprod@service-now.com</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- email subject:&nbsp;RE: &lt;TASK Number&gt;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- body message:&nbsp;name and contact number</p><p>If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation - Step 3</p><p><br></p><p>Step 3: Reply All to the Step 2 email and add:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;- page-field-infrastructure-support-secondary@amazon.com</p><p>Site Access:</p><p>A valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.</p><p>Communication / Microsoft Teams:</p><p>Technician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.</p><p>Field Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.</p><p>Technician must provide updates for:</p><ul><li>Arrival onsite</li><li>Work started</li><li>Progress, delays, or idle time</li><li>Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns</li><li>Completion status before leaving site</li><li>Checkout/departure from site</li></ul><p>Technician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.</p><p>Time, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:</p><p>Technician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.</p><p>Approved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.</p><p>Unsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p>Assigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:</p><p>The technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.</p><p>Documentation / Deliverables:</p><p>All required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.</p><p>Required deliverables may include:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved</li><li>Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable</li><li>Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions</li><li>Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status</li></ul><p>For cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.</p><p>Incomplete Work / Blockers:</p><p>If work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:</p><ul><li>What was completed</li><li>What could not be completed</li><li>Why it could not be completed</li><li>Troubleshooting performed</li><li>Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker</li><li>Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed</li></ul><p>Professional Standards / Confidentiality:</p><p>Technician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.</p><p>Provider Acknowledgment:</p><p>By applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.</p><p>Missing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Required Completion Items:</p><ul><li>Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.</li><li>Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.</li><li>Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.</li><li>Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.</li><li>Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.</li><li>If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.</li><li>Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.</li><li>Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.</li></ul>","markdown":"**WHEN TECH IS ONSITE - CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS**\n\n**---------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Step 1: Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Tech:**\n\n **- Name: Sharat Kumar Maruwada**\n\n **- Phone #: +1-512-516-4731**\n\n\\---------\n\n ISSUE\n\n\\---------\n\nSNP out-of-band (OOB) management switch mwarb-oob2 is unreachable (100% ping loss from NetGate to\n\n10.89.54.6; not visible via LLDP from neighbors oob1 or rc1-1).\n\nis a physical check(troubleshooting) + power-cycle to recover the existing unit.\n\nDevice details:\n\nmwarb-oob2 — SNP OOB management switch, MDF/network rack (near oob1, dist1/2, mdf1-4). SN QTWTI21140098.\n\n\\--------------\n\n REQUEST\n\n\\--------------\n\nNote: Preferred dispatch timings : 8:00AM - 4:00PM CST\n\nPlease dispatch TechNet tech to:\n\n\\- Locate mwarb-oob2 in the MDF/network rack (labeled oob2). Report status LEDs (off/amber/blinking/normal).\n\n\\- Confirm the power cable is seated at the switch and the outlet/PDU, and the outlet is live.\n\n\\- Power-cycle: unplug ~30s, plug back in, allow ~15-20 min to boot, report LED status.\n\n\\- If it does not power up, try a known-good outlet/PDU port.\n\n\\- If still offline and a console port is available, connect via PuTTY and report boot output /\n\n whether it is stuck at a boot prompt / completely dead.\n\n\\- Do NOT unplug or move any other switch, and do NOT remove/replace any SFP — power-cycle only.\n\n\\- Photograph the switch front (LEDs) and rack label.\n\n\\*Material that might be needed:\n\n\\- spare patch cable, console cable for PuTTY check.\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n WHEN TECH IS ONSITE - CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nStep 1: Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Tech:\n\n\\- Name: Sharat Kumar Maruwada\n\n\\- Phone #: +1-512-516-4731\n\nNote: If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation - Step 2\n\nStep 2: Send email:\n\n\\- To: page-msharatk@amazon.com\n\n\\- Cc: wfmprod@service-now.com\n\n\\- email subject: RE: <TASK Number>\n\n\\- body message: name and contact number\n\nIf no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation - Step 3\n\nStep 3: Reply All to the Step 2 email and add:\n\n\\- page-field-infrastructure-support-secondary@amazon.com\n\nSite Access:\n\nA valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.\n\nCommunication / Microsoft Teams:\n\nTechnician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.\n\nField Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.\n\nTechnician must provide updates for:\n\n- Arrival onsite\n- Work started\n- Progress, delays, or idle time\n- Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns\n- Completion status before leaving site\n- Checkout/departure from site\n\nTechnician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.\n\nTime, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:\n\nTechnician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.\n\nApproved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.\n\nUnsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAssigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:\n\nThe technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.\n\nDocumentation / Deliverables:\n\nAll required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.\n\nRequired deliverables may include:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved\n- Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable\n- Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions\n- Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status\n\nFor cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.\n\nIncomplete Work / Blockers:\n\nIf work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:\n\n- What was completed\n- What could not be completed\n- Why it could not be completed\n- Troubleshooting performed\n- Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker\n- Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed\n\nProfessional Standards / Confidentiality:\n\nTechnician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.\n\nProvider Acknowledgment:\n\nBy applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.\n\nMissing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAdditional Required Completion Items:\n\n- Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.\n- Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.\n- Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.\n- Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.\n- Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.\n- If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.\n- Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.\n- Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T09:00","end":"2026-09-25T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 28, 9:00 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $220\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swaro