{"job":{"id":20019045,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Replace Existing Switches with 24-Port Juniper & Test | Connect Existing Circuit/Modem |Remote Support | UPS Drop-Off | Est. Onsite: 1.5hrs","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store</li><li><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional <strong>$30 expense</strong> for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"><u>IMPORTANT NOTE</u></strong><u style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">:</u><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY </strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time</strong></li><li>Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied</li><li><strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense</li><li>Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u> </strong></p><ul><li>Packing Tape</li><li><u>﻿</u>Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity</li><li>Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)</li><li>Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger &amp; Camera</li><li>Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;</li><li>6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)</li><li>Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.</li><li>Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment</li><li>Ethernet Network Cable Toner &amp; Tester</li><li>100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch</li></ul><p><strong><u>On-Site Tasks:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">IMPORTANT</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">:&nbsp;</span><strong>You are required to reference the ‘</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\">Confidential Information</strong><strong>’ section&nbsp;<em><u>IF</u></em>&nbsp;any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted</strong></li><li>Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See customer field '<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">Site Contact Name &amp; Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list&nbsp;</span>MOD/LCON<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">&nbsp;and not a specific person)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty</li><li>At the scheduled install time, call <strong><del>************</del></strong> to check in and work directly with the <del>****</del> team</li><li class=\"