{"job":{"id":20010422,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK | Sheetz 365 Printer Troubleshoot","description":{"html":"<p>This work order is to get our customer back up and running without the need for replacement parts while training onsite staff to resolve printer issues themselves.</p><p><br></p><p>Only accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.</p><p><strong>Must call Work Order Manager to check in and check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>This is a printer troubleshooting/ cleaning WO. No parts will be shipped. Please be sure to bring everything listed in the required tools list below. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>-</strong><u>Required Tools</u><strong>:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard Tool Set</li><li>Nut Drivers or Socket Set</li><li>Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</li><li>A to B USB Cable</li><li>Compressed air/Canned Air</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Cleaning Tools</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cotton swab</li><li>Lint-free cloth</li><li>Brush with soft non-metallic bristles</li><li>Small vacuum cleaner (for debris removal)</li><li>75% Ethanol (for disinfecting)</li><li>99% Isopropyl alcohol (for printhead and platen roller cleaning)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>There are three printers in total across the ARK fleet. Documentation is attached to the work order for each of the different printers you may find on site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Check in with Work Order Manager</strong></li><li>Obtain Keys from site and open up the display cabinet.</li><li>Determine printer type and reference correct documentation.</li><li>Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, and clean as needed.</li><li>Check status light on printer or if the printer is paused.</li><li>Make sure paper is loaded properly.</li><li>Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip.</li><li>Check USB cable to Printer and to PC.</li><li>Call Technical Support to report your findings and to troubleshoot further if needed (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)</li><li><strong>Call Work Order Manager to check out</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.</p><p>346 S Arthur Ave.</p><p>Louisville, CO 80027</p>","markdown":"This work order is to get our customer back up and running without the need for replacement parts while training onsite staff to resolve printer issues themselves.\n\nOnly accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.\n\n**Must call Work Order Manager to check in and check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**This is a printer troubleshooting/ cleaning WO. No parts will be shipped. Please be sure to bring everything listed in the required tools list below.**\n\n**-**Required Tools**:**\n\n- Standard Tool Set\n- Nut Drivers or Socket Set\n- Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth\n- A to B USB Cable\n- Compressed air/Canned Air\n\n**Cleaning Tools**\n\n- Cotton swab\n- Lint-free cloth\n- Brush with soft non-metallic bristles\n- Small vacuum cleaner (for debris removal)\n- 75% Ethanol (for disinfecting)\n- 99% Isopropyl alcohol (for printhead and platen roller cleaning)\n\n**There are three printers in total across the ARK fleet. Documentation is attached to the work order for each of the different printers you may find on site.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n- **Check in with Work Order Manager**\n- Obtain Keys from site and open up the display cabinet.\n- Determine printer type and reference correct documentation.\n- Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, and clean as needed.\n- Check status light on printer or if the printer is paused.\n- Make sure paper is loaded properly.\n- Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip.\n- Check USB cable to Printer and to PC.\n- Call Technical Support to report your findings and to troubleshoot further if needed (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)\n- **Call Work Order Manager to check out**\n\nCompany: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.\n\n346 S Arthur Ave.\n\nLouisville, CO 80027","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T10:00","end":"2026-09-24T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.25,"distance":19},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790246152504}
{"job":{"id":20020237,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GOLFZON America","title":"Golfing Simulator - Install Motion Plate Controller Cable & Test Standing Hydraulics Plate [1-2 hrs]","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking an <strong>AV/low-voltage technician</strong> with experience in Kiosks/PC&nbsp;to perform a <strong>motion plate repair. </strong> Motion plate is currently non-functioning due to swing plate. A replacement cable and controller is currently being shipped to the location. The cable connects the RH (Right-Hand) Motion Plate Controller to the LH Motion Plate Controller</li><li>The technician will work on site with <del>******* </del>remote technical support to install the replacement cable and verify proper Motion Plate operation.</li><li>Estimated duration: 2-3 hours.</li><li><strong>DO NOT TRAVEL TO OR ARRIVE AT THE SITE UNTIL THE SERVICE DATE AND ARRIVAL TIME HAVE BEEN CONFIRMED. </strong>The listed date range is for scheduling purposes only. Please submit your availability. The final service date and arrival window must be coordinated with the customer and confirmed by <del>******* </del>before the technician travels to the site.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Collared shirt, no company logos/emblems.</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Phillips head screwdriver</li><li>Allen key set, socket set, ratchets, extensions</li><li>Impact, and a multi-tool screwdriver</li><li>Full Metric Allen key set (hex key set) 4mm 5mm are important</li><li>Flashlight</li></ul><p><em>Note: Ladders will typically be available onsite.</em></p><ul><li><em>Optional but recommended:</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Protective gloves for ceiling/electrical work</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Small parts tray or magnetic holder</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ul><li>Review the short video provided before arrival.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[VIDEO LINK]<del> </del>https://youtu.be/NYJYFNnd1qI, https://youtu.be/6JOW2FZbLxo</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The technician must confirm they have reviewed provided materials before dispatch</li><li>Contact <del>*******</del> support line prior to arrival to confirm start date/time and align expectations.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check in to the work order, introduce yourself to the onsite contact, and represent <del>*******</del> professionally.</li><li>Call <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*******</del></span> support to be connected with a remote technician to guide you through the process</li><li>Refer to the provided video and instructions to [SUMMARY OF WORK]</li></ol><ul><li>Access swing plate system via floor hatch, inspect prior to repair</li><li>Install replacement cable and/or motion plate controller.</li><li>Verify proper wiring/connections</li><li>Test full motion plate operation after installation and confirm unit raises/lowers properly</li></ul><ol><li>Maintain site cleanliness throughout work.</li><li>After installation, call <del>*******</del> support to complete sensor pointing, calibration, and IP verification.</li><li>If applicable, securely package and drop off any removed or unused hardware to a local UPS location using a provided shipping label.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>Obtain customer signature on work order.</li><li>Upload before/after photos of work area and hardware replacement.</li><li>Provide a verification photo showing motion plate functioning properly.</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, technician should contact <del>*******</del> Support <del>** </del><strong><del>*********************** **</del></strong><del>*</del></li><li><del>***</del>Escalations may be directed to work order manager or support line.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Additional hours, travel, or material expenses must be pre-approved by <del>*******</del> Support prior to billing.</li><li>Technician must call <del>*******</del> Support to request approval before incurring additional costs.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE:</u></strong></p><p>In the event Provider requires five (5) or more hours to complete the Workorder, Provider must contact <del>******* </del>for approval of any additional work hours.</p><p><del>******* </del>reserves the right to terminate this Workorder at any time in the event that Provider’s services are not provided in a professional workmanlike manner in accordance with industry standards. In the event of such termination, <del>******* </del>shall not be liable for payment for any work hours not provided post-termination.</p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking an **AV/low-voltage technician** with experience in Kiosks/PC to perform a **motion plate repair.**  Motion plate is currently non-functioning due to swing plate. A replacement cable and controller is currently being shipped to the location. The cable connects the RH (Right-Hand) Motion Plate Controller to the LH Motion Plate Controller\n- The technician will work on site with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* remote technical support to install the replacement cable and verify proper Motion Plate operation.\n- Estimated duration: 2-3 hours.\n- **DO NOT TRAVEL TO OR ARRIVE AT THE SITE UNTIL THE SERVICE DATE AND ARRIVAL TIME HAVE BEEN CONFIRMED.** The listed date range is for scheduling purposes only. Please submit your availability. The final service date and arrival window must be coordinated with the customer and confirmed by \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* before the technician travels to the site.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Collared shirt, no company logos/emblems.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Phillips head screwdriver\n- Allen key set, socket set, ratchets, extensions\n- Impact, and a multi-tool screwdriver\n- Full Metric Allen key set (hex key set) 4mm 5mm are important\n- Flashlight\n\n*Note: Ladders will typically be available onsite.*\n\n- *Optional but recommended:*\n- Protective gloves for ceiling/electrical work\n- Small parts tray or magnetic holder\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n- Review the short video provided before arrival.\n- \\[VIDEO LINK\\] <https://youtu.be/NYJYFNnd1qI,> <https://youtu.be/6JOW2FZbLxo>\n- The technician must confirm they have reviewed provided materials before dispatch\n- Contact \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support line prior to arrival to confirm start date/time and align expectations.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in to the work order, introduce yourself to the onsite contact, and represent \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* professionally.\n2. Call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support to be connected with a remote technician to guide you through the process\n3. Refer to the provided video and instructions to \\[SUMMARY OF WORK\\]\n\n- Access swing plate system via floor hatch, inspect prior to repair\n- Install replacement cable and/or motion plate controller.\n- Verify proper wiring/connections\n- Test full motion plate operation after installation and confirm unit raises/lowers properly\n\n1. Maintain site cleanliness throughout work.\n2. After installation, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support to complete sensor pointing, calibration, and IP verification.\n3. If applicable, securely package and drop off any removed or unused hardware to a local UPS location using a provided shipping label.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Obtain customer signature on work order.\n2. Upload before/after photos of work area and hardware replacement.\n3. Provide a verification photo showing motion plate functioning properly.\n4. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, technician should contact \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Support \\*\\* **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\***\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*Escalations may be directed to work order manager or support line.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Additional hours, travel, or material expenses must be pre-approved by \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Support prior to billing.\n- Technician must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Support to request approval before incurring additional costs.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE:**\n\nIn the event Provider requires five (5) or more hours to complete the Workorder, Provider must contact \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for approval of any additional work hours.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* reserves the right to terminate this Workorder at any time in the event that Provider’s services are not provided in a professional workmanlike manner in accordance with industry standards. In the event of such termination, \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* shall not be liable for payment for any work hours not provided post-termination.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T10:00","end":"2026-10-02T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":63},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budde