{"job":{"id":20020535,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Down Access Points – Raleigh, NC | 00260098 / SA-291525 / 05169527","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p><p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p><ul><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li><li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>and its reason.</li><li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li><li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Title: Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Down Access Points – Raleigh, NC | 00260098 / SA-291525 / 05169527</p><p> Type of Work: Networking</p><p> Schedule: September 24, 2026 – 13:00 EDT (13:00 EDT)</p><p> Site Name &amp; Address: The StateView Hotel, 2451 Alumni Drive, Raleigh, NC 27696, United States</p><p> WO / SA / Case: 00260098 / SA-291525 / 05169527</p><p> Contact Details:</p><p> Site POC: Andrew Bankston, 919-743-0055</p><p> Engineer: Jerry Shaaban | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p><p> Scope of Work:</p><ul><li>Troubleshoot down access points connected to switch RDUASSW001-5-IDF3.</li><li>Check interface 3/9 – RDUAS-WAP020-4-RM433.</li><li>Check interface 3/7 – RDUAS-WAP018-4-RM425.</li><li>Check interface 3/21 – RDUAS-WAP014-5-RM519.</li><li>Verify switch ports, cabling, connectivity, and AP power/link status.</li><li>Reboot affected equipment as required and perform connectivity testing.</li><li>Document findings and any corrective actions taken.</li><li>Reference Case# 05169527 and FSR 10539-260923-1 as needed.</li><li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li><li> Asset &amp; Location: RDUASSW001-5-IDF3 / RDUAS-WAP020-4-RM433 / RDUAS-WAP018-4-RM425 / RDUAS-WAP014-5-RM519 – IDF3</li><li> Tools Required:</li><li>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</li><li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li><li>Ethernet adapter</li><li>Ethernet cable</li><li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li><li>Cellphone with camera</li><li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit ethernet connections)</li><li>Tone generator</li><li>Console cable and USB adapter</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Crimper</li><li>RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Voltage tester</li><li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li><li>If testing fiber: Laser to verify light continuity, fiber tester, and cleaning kit</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to **specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\nTitle: Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Down Access Points – Raleigh, NC | 00260098 / SA-291525 / 05169527\n\n Type of Work: Networking\n\n Schedule: September 24, 2026 – 13:00 EDT (13:00 EDT)\n\n Site Name & Address: The StateView Hotel, 2451 Alumni Drive, Raleigh, NC 27696, United States\n\n WO / SA / Case: 00260098 / SA-291525 / 05169527\n\n Contact Details:\n\n Site POC: Andrew Bankston, 919-743-0055\n\n Engineer: Jerry Shaaban | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n Scope of Work:\n\n- Troubleshoot down access points connected to switch RDUASSW001-5-IDF3.\n- Check interface 3/9 – RDUAS-WAP020-4-RM433.\n- Check interface 3/7 – RDUAS-WAP018-4-RM425.\n- Check interface 3/21 – RDUAS-WAP014-5-RM519.\n- Verify switch ports, cabling, connectivity, and AP power/link status.\n- Reboot affected equipment as required and perform connectivity testing.\n- Document findings and any corrective actions taken.\n- Reference Case# 05169527 and FSR 10539-260923-1 as needed.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n- Asset & Location: RDUASSW001-5-IDF3 / RDUAS-WAP020-4-RM433 / RDUAS-WAP018-4-RM425 / RDUAS-WAP014-5-RM519 – IDF3\n- Tools Required:\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- If testing fiber: Laser to verify light continuity, fiber tester, and cleaning kit","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00","end":"2026-09-24T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 28, 1:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $260\nRejected: pay do