{"job":{"id":20020860,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"[PPT0997762 #]- DODEA  [274570  #]","description":{"html":"<p><strong>OVERVIEW:</strong></p><p><strong>If the repair doesn't correct the issue, notify the work manager immediately.</strong></p><p>Must take photos of any incomplete work, where it cant be fixed</p><p>This SOW consists of</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>System Number&nbsp;: 5CD35254GS</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Short Description&nbsp;: The customer reported 1QAZ keys not working&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Replacement: None- N/A</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Resolution / Action Plan: Verify Problem exists, follow the steps below to reseat the keyboard cable on the HP Chromebook x360 11 G4, ensure functionality, and document SN on SVR and give to customer. Thank you very much.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please follow the steps below to reseat the keyboard cable on the HP Chromebook x360 11 G4:</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>1. Power off</p><p><br></p><p>Turn the Chromebook off</p><p><br></p><p>Unplug the charger</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>2. Remove the bottom cover</p><p><br></p><p>Flip the Chromebook upside down</p><p><br></p><p>Remove all screws from the bottom</p><p><br></p><p>Pry the bottom cover off and set it aside</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>3. Disconnect the battery (important)</p><p><br></p><p>Find the battery plug</p><p><br></p><p>Gently pull it straight out</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4. Find the keyboard cable</p><p><br></p><p>Look for a wide, flat ribbon cable</p><p><br></p><p>It runs from the keyboard area to the motherboard</p><p><br></p><p>It has a small black flip lock</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>5. Reseat the cable</p><p><br></p><p>Flip the black lock UP</p><p><br></p><p>Pull the ribbon cable straight out</p><p><br></p><p>Slide it back in all the way</p><p><br></p><p>Flip the black lock DOWN to secure it</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>*Do not force anything*</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>6. Put it back together</p><p><br></p><p>Reconnect the battery</p><p><br></p><p>Put the bottom cover back on</p><p><br></p><p>Reinstall the screws</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>7. Test it</p><p><br></p><p>Power on the Chromebook</p><p><br></p><p>Try typing</p><p>Estimated duration will be 2 hours</p><p>POC: <del>******* *** *********** ************** *****</del></p><p><strong>Technician Checklist:</strong></p><ol><li>Technicians are to share their availability with Park Place and they will coordinate the schedule with the Client POC, all visits must be approved by the Client POC and Park Place prior to the schedule. Technician shall not show up to the school unannounced.</li><li>If returning a package, please make sure that there’s return label attached to the package.</li><li>If returning packages, please make sure to have the right documentation for the specific part in their own respective package.</li><li>If an extra part or repair is needed, please indicate properly in the SVR and notify NCS.</li><li>Technician should return the package within 48 hours upon receiving from the POC.</li></ol><p><strong>Requirements/Expectation:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Technician will represent themselves as being a Park Place technician. Do not solicit or hand out business cards; always present yourself as a Park Place Technologies Engineer and not any other company/ your own company.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Only the Customer can initiate a reschedule - if customer requests a reschedule, call Park Place <strong>before </strong>departing the site at <del>***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p><strong>Dress code:</strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Business casual attire is required (Khakis and collared shirt).</p><p><strong><u>Escalations</u>:</strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any signs of physical damage or liquid spill, please STOP and call into tech support at<del> ***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p>2.&nbsp;For technical support, to request a manual or any questions related to the work instructions or site access please contact the Park Place Support Center. at <del>***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p><strong>English Language Requirement -</strong>Business conversations, instructions, and support communications related to completing this SOW are exclusively in English: therefore, technicians must be able to fluently read, speak, write, and understand the English language to allow for communication with on-site contacts and remote support, as well as understanding of scope documents, WO tasks, and other instructions.&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n**If the repair doesn't correct the issue, notify the work manager immediately.**\n\nMust take photos of any incomplete work, where it cant be fixed\n\nThis SOW consists of\n\nSystem Number : 5CD35254GS\n\nShort Description : The customer reported 1QAZ keys not working\n\nReplacement: None- N/A\n\nResolution / Action Plan: Verify Problem exists, follow the steps below to reseat the keyboard cable on the HP Chromebook x360 11 G4, ensure functionality, and document SN on SVR and give to customer. Thank you very much.\n\nPlease follow the steps below to reseat the keyboard cable on the HP Chromebook x360 11 G4:\n\n1\\. Power off\n\nTurn the Chromebook off\n\nUnplug the charger\n\n2\\. Remove the bottom cover\n\nFlip the Chromebook upside down\n\nRemove all screws from the bottom\n\nPry the bottom cover off and set it aside\n\n3\\. Disconnect the battery (important)\n\nFind the battery plug\n\nGently pull it straight out\n\n4\\. Find the keyboard cable\n\nLook for a wide, flat ribbon cable\n\nIt runs from the keyboard area to the motherboard\n\nIt has a small black flip lock\n\n5\\. Reseat the cable\n\nFlip the black lock UP\n\nPull the ribbon cable straight out\n\nSlide it back in all the way\n\nFlip the black lock DOWN to secure it\n\n\\*Do not force anything\\*\n\n6\\. Put it back together\n\nReconnect the battery\n\nPut the bottom cover back on\n\nReinstall the screws\n\n7\\. Test it\n\nPower on the Chromebook\n\nTry typing\n\nEstimated duration will be 2 hours\n\nPOC: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Technician Checklist:**\n\n1. Technicians are to share their availability with Park Place and they will coordinate the schedule with the Client POC, all visits must be approved by the Client POC and Park Place prior to the schedule. Technician shall not show up to the school unannounced.\n2. If returning a package, please make sure that there’s return label attached to the package.\n3. If returning packages, please make sure to have the right documentation for the specific part in their own respective package.\n4. If an extra part or repair is needed, please indicate properly in the SVR and notify NCS.\n5. Technician should return the package within 48 hours upon receiving from the POC.\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n· Technician will represent themselves as being a Park Place technician. Do not solicit or hand out business cards; always present yourself as a Park Place Technologies Engineer and not any other company/ your own company.\n\n· Only the Customer can initiate a reschedule - if customer requests a reschedule, call Park Place **before** departing the site at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n**Dress code:**· Business casual attire is required (Khakis and collared shirt).\n\n**Escalations:**\n\n1\\. Any signs of physical damage or liquid spill, please STOP and call into tech support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n2\\. For technical support, to request a manual or any questions related to the work instructions or site access please contact the Park Place Support Center. at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n**English Language Requirement -**Business conversations, instructions, and support communications related to completing this SOW are exclusively in English: therefore, technicians must be able to fluently read, speak, write, and understand the English language to allow for communication with on-site contacts and remote support, as well as understanding of scope documents, WO tasks, and other instructions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T09:00","end":"2026-10-01T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":240},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":46},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/24/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Site Audit | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 04:00:00 - 07:00:00 GMT-4 | Requested Window (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"202