{"job":{"id":20021644,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DSI","title":"2U85","description":{"html":"<p>Site is currently online with Cradle Points.  The ISP has delivered the primary and secondary modems.  Tech will need to call into the DSI Support to migrate service from the CPs to the circuits.</p><p><br></p><p>Need a tech to check for a cut cable to AP - 1NCA0102U85. Tech will also work with the NOC to troubleshoot the printers.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tech will call DSI support on arrival, for support, and to check out @ 866-966-7569 ext 4</p><p><strong>Complete these steps before opening any equipment boxes or touching any existing network gear.</strong></p><p>Required tools:</p><p>Cable tester</p><p>Tone generator</p><p>Hammer Drill w/ Masonry bit</p><p>6' to 8' ladder</p><p>Standard telcom tools</p><p>Drill w/ assorted bits</p><p>Snips</p><p>Velcro</p><p>Box of cat6 cable</p><p><strong>Network Conversion -</strong></p><p><br></p><p>1. Project Overview</p><p>Provide onsite labor to install and turn up new network infrastructure, migrate designated legacy store devices to the new Juniper environment, validate connectivity, and decommission identified Wash hardware for return to designated location(s). Work is planned as a single daytime visit per store.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Equipment Installation</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Circuit hardware / ISP handoff equipment</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Juniper SSR130</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Juniper EX4100-48MP switches, quantity 2 per store</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Juniper SSR100-RMK router bracket kit, quantity 1 per store</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Juniper SFP-1G-T-C, quantity 2 per store</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Juniper SFPP-10G-SR-C, quantity 4 per store</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;MIST AP43 (white), quantity 5 per store (Some sites, while uncommon, may have a 6th)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CradlePoint W1855C 5G</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CradlePoint 1850C</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Network Cash Drawer</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Xerox MFP 625 Printer</p><p><strong>Callout:</strong>Install five (5) AP43s per store in accordance with the site wireless design.</p><p><br></p><p>3. Installation Activities</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify all shipped equipment is present and undamaged prior to install.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rack, wall-mount, or otherwise securely mount equipment in designated store locations.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install required brackets, optics, patching, and interconnects.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Run, dress, and label new cabling as required between ISP handoff, router, switches, APs, and migrated endpoint locations.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install and connect uplinks between router and switches and complete designated inter-switch uplinks as provided by engineering.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install and connect all APs to designated switch ports.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Apply basic cable management and leave the back of house work area in clean condition.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Label all cables as consistent with T-Mobile requirements.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ground the rack and install grounding materials where applicable.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For W1855 installations, mount in the approved RT PM location, clear of obstructions, positioned for signal reception, and at least 8 feet above ground where exterior mounted.</p>","markdown":"Site is currently online with Cradle Points. The ISP has delivered the primary and secondary modems. Tech will need to call into the DSI Support to migrate service from the CPs to the circuits.\n\nNeed a tech to check for a cut cable to AP - 1NCA0102U85. Tech will also work with the NOC to troubleshoot the printers.\n\nTech will call DSI support on arrival, for support, and to check out @ 866-966-7569 ext 4\n\n**Complete these steps before opening any equipment boxes or touching any existing network gear.**\n\nRequired tools:\n\nCable tester\n\nTone generator\n\nHammer Drill w/ Masonry bit\n\n6' to 8' ladder\n\nStandard telcom tools\n\nDrill w/ assorted bits\n\nSnips\n\nVelcro\n\nBox of cat6 cable\n\n**Network Conversion -**\n\n1\\. Project Overview\n\nProvide onsite labor to install and turn up new network infrastructure, migrate designated legacy store devices to the new Juniper environment, validate connectivity, and decommission identified Wash hardware for return to designated location(s). Work is planned as a single daytime visit per store.\n\n2\\. Equipment Installation\n\n· Circuit hardware / ISP handoff equipment\n\n· Juniper SSR130\n\n· Juniper EX4100-48MP switches, quantity 2 per store\n\n· Juniper SSR100-RMK router bracket kit, quantity 1 per store\n\n· Juniper SFP-1G-T-C, quantity 2 per store\n\n· Juniper SFPP-10G-SR-C, quantity 4 per store\n\n· MIST AP43 (white), quantity 5 per store (Some sites, while uncommon, may have a 6th)\n\n· CradlePoint W1855C 5G\n\n· CradlePoint 1850C\n\n· Network Cash Drawer\n\n· Xerox MFP 625 Printer\n\n**Callout:**Install five (5) AP43s per store in accordance with the site wireless design.\n\n3\\. Installation Activities\n\n· Verify all shipped equipment is present and undamaged prior to install.\n\n· Rack, wall-mount, or otherwise securely mount equipment in designated store locations.\n\n· Install required brackets, optics, patching, and interconnects.\n\n· Run, dress, and label new cabling as required between ISP handoff, router, switches, APs, and migrated endpoint locations.\n\n· Install and connect uplinks between router and switches and complete designated inter-switch uplinks as provided by engineering.\n\n· Install and connect all APs to designated switch ports.\n\n· Apply basic cable management and leave the back of house work area in clean condition.\n\n· Label all cables as consistent with T-Mobile requirements.\n\n· Ground the rack and install grounding materials where applicable.\n\n· For W1855 installations, mount in the approved RT PM location, clear of obstructions, positioned for signal reception, and at least 8 feet above ground where exterior mounted.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T10:00","end":"2026-09-25T13:00","latestStart":"2026-09-25T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":275,"max":275},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":72},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 28, 10:00 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $275\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Site Audit | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 04:00:00 - 07:00:00 GMT-4 | Requested Window (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"20