{"job":{"id":20022449,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Verratech Solutions LLC","title":"MLP-Durham","description":{"html":"<p>Office Consolidation Survey, Workstation &amp; AV Move — Office 2027 — MLP Durham</p><p><strong>Job Number:</strong> S-141-IMC-September 2026</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> 555 S Mangum Street, Durham, NC 27701 — Offices 2008, 2018, 2021 (Origin) → Office 2027 (Destination)</p><p><strong>Date / Time:</strong> September 25, 2026 — 9:00AM</p><p><strong>Cost Center:</strong> 1F31</p><p><strong>User:</strong> Marc Donahue</p><p><strong>Labor Required:</strong> 1 Verratech Network Technician</p><p><strong>POC:</strong> Russell Nys — 917-415-9441</p><p><strong>AV Integrator On-Site Contact:</strong> Jared D. — coordinate upon arrival (CC'd on original request)</p><p><strong>IMPORTANT — IMC REPRESENTATION</strong></p><p>Technician is representing IMC while onsite.</p><ul><li>Maintain professional and discreet conduct</li><li><strong>Do NOT reference Field Nation, Verratech, or any third-party staffing arrangement</strong></li><li>Do not discuss pricing or internal arrangements</li><li>Coordinate directly with the POC or remote support</li><li>Escalate issues before making changes</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>Pre-move survey and consolidation of all workstations and AV gear from Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 into Office 2027. Technician will survey Office 2027 for existing and required data and power capacity, mark up the provided floor plan with port layout, identify any shortfalls in data or power that need to be addressed before the move, and coordinate with the on-site AV integrator Jared D. for AV-specific requirements including the time board. Survey findings will drive the action plan for the full move.</p><p><strong>Tasks</strong></p><p><strong>Pre-Work</strong></p><ol><li>Check in with building management and proceed to Office 2027</li><li>Contact Russell Nys upon arrival to confirm scope before beginning</li><li>Make contact with Jared D. (AV integrator) upon arrival — coordinate AV survey scope and requirements before beginning that portion of the work</li><li>Obtain the attached floor plan layout of desks and AV gear before starting survey</li></ol><p><strong>Office 2027 — Power &amp; Data Survey</strong></p><ol><li>Photograph the full Office 2027 space before any work begins</li><li>Survey all existing data ports in Office 2027 — document location, label, and active or inactive status for each port</li><li>Survey all existing power outlets in Office 2027 — document location and condition</li><li>Cross-reference existing data and power against the floor plan layout for the planned desk and AV positions</li><li>Identify any shortfalls — data ports or power outlets that are missing, inactive, or insufficient for the planned layout</li><li>Mark up the floor plan with all existing port and outlet locations — clearly note shortfalls and any newly required data or power additions</li><li>Trace and tone existing data runs if needed to confirm IDF patch panel termination points</li><li>Photograph all existing ports, outlets, and any identified shortfall areas</li></ol><p><strong>AV Survey — Coordinate with Jared D.</strong></p><ol><li>Walk Office 2027 with Jared D. — confirm AV gear placement per floor plan including the time board</li><li>Identify existing AV infrastructure — display mounts, conduit, and AV cabling in Office 2027</li><li>Note any AV-specific power or data requirements not covered by the general survey</li><li>Document AV shortfalls on the floor plan mark-up</li><li>Confirm with Jared D. any AV pre-work that must be completed before the move can proceed</li><li>Photograph all AV-related areas and infrastructure</li></ol><p><strong>Origin Offices — Inventory (2008, 2018, 2021)</strong></p><ol><li>Photograph and document all workstations and AV gear currently in Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021</li><li>Inventory all equipment to be relocated — make, model, and quantity at each origin office</li><li>Note current data port connections at each origin workstation — confirm port labels for reference during move planning</li><li>Document AV gear in each origin office including the time board — location, connections, and mounting details</li><li>Note any equipment that will require special handling during the move</li></ol><p><strong>Floor Plan Mark-Up &amp; Deliverable</strong></p><ol><li>Complete the mark-up on the provided floor plan — indicate all existing data ports, power outlets, new requirements, and shortfalls</li><li>Clearly annotate where new data drops or power additions are needed before the move can proceed</li><li>Submit completed marked-up floor plan to Russell Nys and Jared D. upon completion</li><li>Provide a written shortfall summary — list of all data and power gaps that must be resolved before move day</li></ol><p><strong>Required Photos</strong></p><ul><li>Office 2027 full overview before survey begins</li><li>All existing data ports — location and status visible</li><li>All existing power outlets — location and condition</li><li>Shortfall areas — missing or inactive ports and outlets</li><li>AV infrastructure in Office 2027</li><li>Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 — all workstations and AV gear documented</li><li>Time board — current location, mounting, and connections</li><li>Completed floor plan mark-up</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables</strong></p><ul><li>Completed and marked-up floor plan — all existing ports, outlets, new requirements, and shortfalls annotated</li><li>Written shortfall summary — all data and power gaps identified with recommended remediation</li><li>Full equipment inventory for Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 — everything to be relocated</li><li>AV requirements confirmed with Jared D. and documented</li><li>Photo documentation uploaded to work order upon completion</li><li>Survey findings submitted to Russell Nys and Jared D. before technician departure</li></ul><p><strong>Completion Criteria</strong></p><p>Job is complete when the full survey of Office 2027 is documented, the floor plan is marked up and submitted, all shortfalls are identified and reported, the equipment inventory for all three origin offices is complete, AV requirements are confirmed with Jared D., and close-out is confirmed with Russell Nys.</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Office Consolidation Survey, Workstation & AV Move — Office 2027 — MLP Durham\n\n**Job Number:** S-141-IMC-September 2026\n\n**Location:** 555 S Mangum Street, Durham, NC 27701 — Offices 2008, 2018, 2021 (Origin) → Office 2027 (Destination)\n\n**Date / Time:** September 25, 2026 — 9:00AM\n\n**Cost Center:** 1F31\n\n**User:** Marc Donahue\n\n**Labor Required:** 1 Verratech Network Technician\n\n**POC:** Russell Nys — 917-415-9441\n\n**AV Integrator On-Site Contact:** Jared D. — coordinate upon arrival (CC'd on original request)\n\n**IMPORTANT — IMC REPRESENTATION**\n\nTechnician is representing IMC while onsite.\n\n- Maintain professional and discreet conduct\n- **Do NOT reference Field Nation, Verratech, or any third-party staffing arrangement**\n- Do not discuss pricing or internal arrangements\n- Coordinate directly with the POC or remote support\n- Escalate issues before making changes\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nPre-move survey and consolidation of all workstations and AV gear from Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 into Office 2027. Technician will survey Office 2027 for existing and required data and power capacity, mark up the provided floor plan with port layout, identify any shortfalls in data or power that need to be addressed before the move, and coordinate with the on-site AV integrator Jared D. for AV-specific requirements including the time board. Survey findings will drive the action plan for the full move.\n\n**Tasks**\n\n**Pre-Work**\n\n1. Check in with building management and proceed to Office 2027\n2. Contact Russell Nys upon arrival to confirm scope before beginning\n3. Make contact with Jared D. (AV integrator) upon arrival — coordinate AV survey scope and requirements before beginning that portion of the work\n4. Obtain the attached floor plan layout of desks and AV gear before starting survey\n\n**Office 2027 — Power & Data Survey**\n\n1. Photograph the full Office 2027 space before any work begins\n2. Survey all existing data ports in Office 2027 — document location, label, and active or inactive status for each port\n3. Survey all existing power outlets in Office 2027 — document location and condition\n4. Cross-reference existing data and power against the floor plan layout for the planned desk and AV positions\n5. Identify any shortfalls — data ports or power outlets that are missing, inactive, or insufficient for the planned layout\n6. Mark up the floor plan with all existing port and outlet locations — clearly note shortfalls and any newly required data or power additions\n7. Trace and tone existing data runs if needed to confirm IDF patch panel termination points\n8. Photograph all existing ports, outlets, and any identified shortfall areas\n\n**AV Survey — Coordinate with Jared D.**\n\n1. Walk Office 2027 with Jared D. — confirm AV gear placement per floor plan including the time board\n2. Identify existing AV infrastructure — display mounts, conduit, and AV cabling in Office 2027\n3. Note any AV-specific power or data requirements not covered by the general survey\n4. Document AV shortfalls on the floor plan mark-up\n5. Confirm with Jared D. any AV pre-work that must be completed before the move can proceed\n6. Photograph all AV-related areas and infrastructure\n\n**Origin Offices — Inventory (2008, 2018, 2021)**\n\n1. Photograph and document all workstations and AV gear currently in Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021\n2. Inventory all equipment to be relocated — make, model, and quantity at each origin office\n3. Note current data port connections at each origin workstation — confirm port labels for reference during move planning\n4. Document AV gear in each origin office including the time board — location, connections, and mounting details\n5. Note any equipment that will require special handling during the move\n\n**Floor Plan Mark-Up & Deliverable**\n\n1. Complete the mark-up on the provided floor plan — indicate all existing data ports, power outlets, new requirements, and shortfalls\n2. Clearly annotate where new data drops or power additions are needed before the move can proceed\n3. Submit completed marked-up floor plan to Russell Nys and Jared D. upon completion\n4. Provide a written shortfall summary — list of all data and power gaps that must be resolved before move day\n\n**Required Photos**\n\n- Office 2027 full overview before survey begins\n- All existing data ports — location and status visible\n- All existing power outlets — location and condition\n- Shortfall areas — missing or inactive ports and outlets\n- AV infrastructure in Office 2027\n- Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 — all workstations and AV gear documented\n- Time board — current location, mounting, and connections\n- Completed floor plan mark-up\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n- Completed and marked-up floor plan — all existing ports, outlets, new requirements, and shortfalls annotated\n- Written shortfall summary — all data and power gaps identified with recommended remediation\n- Full equipment inventory for Offices 2008, 2018, and 2021 — everything to be relocated\n- AV requirements confirmed with Jared D. and documented\n- Photo documentation uploaded to work order upon completion\n- Survey findings submitted to Russell Nys and Jared D. before technician departure\n\n**Completion Criteria**\n\nJob is complete when the full survey of Office 2027 is documented, the floor plan is marked up and submitted, all shortfalls are identified and reported, the equipment inventory for all three origin offices is complete, AV requirements are confirmed with Jared D., and close-out is confirmed with Russell Nys.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T