{"job":{"id":"5127135451","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Endeavor Managed Services","title":"Experienced CCTV Technician Needed - Camera 12 down","description":"<p><strong><em><u>Pre-Dispatch:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Download and print the SR. The SR will need to be signed by the MOD before leaving site. </strong>&nbsp;Please download all documents from the <strong>Documents </strong>section of this assignment.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please also download the MyESP app and make sure you are able to login. If not, please reach out to fe_engagement@endeavor-ms.com.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Scope of Work:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>ISS ticket # SR04399338</strong></p><p><strong>For troubleshooting: Text ISS support at 1-314-648-2956.</strong></p><p><strong>For closing out: Call ISS support at 1-800-249-0192.</strong></p><p><strong>ISS close code and signed SR are needed before leaving the site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech should bring at least 10 BNC connectors, a voltmeter, and both RG6 and RG59 crimp with crimp tool.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>System &amp; Model #: OpenEye</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem: Camera 12 down</strong></p><p><strong>Technician will troubleshoot reported camera down issue. Tech will contact Helpdesk to check-in upon arrival at the location and reconfirm scope if work if needed, Tech must bring a ladder of appropriate size, camera cleaning tools, multimeter, laptop, hotspot and a portable monitor for camera troubleshooting. Technician will check cable, wirings, and the camera if it is getting power, check Power Distribution Unit (PDU) if it supplies power to the cameras, test voltage reading for both the camera and the PDidentify which part is needed so Helpdesk can order the right part, take pictures as needed, after all troubleshooting is done, call Helpdesk to confirm remote view of the camera once verified camera is up debrief with Helpdesk and summarize all troubleshooting steps performed on site. if there are parts included advise if all parts was used, if it is not used, please leave the part at the store and or fill out the return label and shipped it back to Interface.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Specific Scheduling Request: Anytime before 3pm except this Friday</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Cause: Faulty wiring</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Support &amp; Cost Analysis Information Only:</strong></p><p><strong>Name and title of person onsite: James McKeever</strong></p><p><strong>Was the customer Available, Willing and Able to troubleshoot? Yes</strong></p><p><strong>Did the customer request a dispatch instead? No</strong></p><p><br></p><p>RMA Form: Complete link &amp; Return Label provided. https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88</p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Technician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing</p><p>If access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.</p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Required Tools and Materials:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>10 x RG6 and RG59 crip with crimping tool&nbsp;</li><li>10 x BNC connectors</li><li>Voltmeter and Toner Generator.</li><li>8ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Tone generator and inductive wand</li><li>Cabling tools</li><li>Windows based laptop with ethernet patch cable</li><li>Cisco console cable</li><li>USB to serial adapter</li><li>At least 1000 feet of 22AWG 4 conductor solid core plenum cabling</li><li>At least 1000 feet of 22AWG 4 conductor solid core PVC cabling</li><li>Multiple RJ11 and Rj45 keystones and housings (surface and flush mount)</li><li>Valid picture ID</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Important Reminders:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Arrive at the specified date and time.</strong></li><li><strong>Log onsite with Endeavor TAC by calling the phone number displayed in the Special Instructions section.</strong></li><li><strong>Work with the ISS Helpdesk to resolve onsite issue.</strong></li><li><strong>If wait time for ISS Helpdesk exceeds 30 minutes, please reach out to Endeavor TAC for next steps.</strong></li><li><strong>You MUST check-out with the ISS Helpdesk and obtain a close code prior to leaving the site.</strong></li><li><strong>If you encounter issues obtaining a close code, call Endeavor TAC at the phone number displayed in the Special Instructions section.</strong></li><li><strong>ISS close code and signed SR are needed before leaving the site.</strong></li><li><strong>All items in the Deliverables section must be submitted within 24 hours of the dispatch.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Interface Communications Procedures:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>1. The support/logoff number is listed in the Contact List box at the top of the install guide.</strong></p><p><strong>2. The troubleshooting support number listed is TEXT ONLY.</strong></p><p><strong>3. You do NOT have to contact Interface to check in when you arrive.</strong></p><p><strong>4. You MUST work to resolve the issue listed on page 2 of your SR prior to contacting support. If you can resolve the issue without support, you would only be required to contact Interface to log off.</strong></p><p><strong>5. You MUST log off with Interface to obtain a closure code for every dispatch.</strong></p><p><strong>6. If required to leave the site to pick up a part for maintenance, proceed as instructed. Call TAC (1-800-493-0016 option 3) to inform Endeavor of this request.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Dress Code Policy:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Technicians must always present a clean, professional appearance. Technicians are expected to be well-groomed and wear clean clothing, free of holes, tears, or other signs of wear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Shirts</em>:</strong></p><ul><li>Must be a polo shirt, or other collared shirt. T-shirts of any kind are not permitted.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pants</em>:</strong></p><ul><li>Must be Docker style pants or colored denim.</li><li>Jeans must be clean and professional looking. Jeans with holes, rips or fraying are not permitted.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Commitments &amp; Penalties:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Assignment Approval:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Mark your assignment as pending approval within 24 hours of the dispatch.</li><li>If you are unable to mark the assignment complete, please add a message with your concern within 24 hours of the dispatch.</li><li>If the assignment is not marked pending approval and no note is posted within the time frames shown, we will mark it as pending approval on your behalf. This will serve as acceptance of the assignment value listed at the time of closure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Bonus Structure:</em></strong></p><ul><li>A 5% bonus will be awarded if all deliverables are submitted, reviewed, and approved via myESP on the dispatch date.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Penalty Structure:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Arrivals over 15 minutes late without notice will incur a 10% penalty.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Deliverables received after you have left the site or the dispatch is closed:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Within 48 hours of your dispatch a penalty of 10% will be assessed.</li><li>Within 72 hours of your dispatch a penalty of 15% will be assessed.</li><li>Deliverables received after 72 hours are subject to customer acceptance. If they are not accepted by the customer, it can result in non-payment of the assignment.</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T13:00","end":"2026-09-25T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":179.99624844},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":65.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $179.99624844 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Site Audit | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 04:00:00 - 07:00:00 GMT-4 | Requested Window (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end"