{"job":{"id":20022903,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Creative Realities","title":"Freddys 32-0017 - Fayetteville NC | DT1 S3 Swap 2 Techs Required","description":{"html":"<p>********** Scope of Work **********</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">*** Scope of Work ***</strong></p><p>*** TECH MUST CALL CRI UPON ARRIVING TO AND BEFORE LEAVING SITE ***</p><p>MUST Check In with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have before photos ready)</p><p>For any and all Technical Assistance, reach out to Support @ 888-369-3629</p><p>MUST Check Out with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have after photos ready)</p><p><br></p><p>Work with the site contact <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">Site Manager</span> to locate the <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">Replacement Screen</span></p><p>Work with the site contact <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">Site Manager</span> to locate the <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">drive thru screen three</span></p><p>Inspect each replacement item as it is pulled from the boxing to verify condition (take pictures)</p><p>Take pictures of the old equipment before it is removed from its location</p><p>Uninstall and remove the old screen from its location (take pictures)</p><p>Install the replacement screen in its location (take pictures)</p><p>Run and/or connect all cables between the replacement (equipment) and the remaining old equipment</p><p>Verify all functionality of all equipment on site (content, sound, touch, etc.)</p><p><br></p><p>Steps to activate Clarity:</p><p>1) Turn on the Display. It should load up to the Welcome screen.</p><p>2) Select the appropriate language.</p><p>3) You’ll be asked if you want to clone an already configured display or start a basic setup. Select Basic Setup.&nbsp;</p><p>4) Set the “Display Orientation” to Landscape.</p><p>5) Connect the display to the appropriate network (might be Wi-Fi or Wired)</p><p>6) On the Play Via screen, select “URL Launcher” (or “Custom App” depending on the model of the screen). </p><p>7) This will bring you to a new window so that you can enter in the URL that needs to be used. Please enter:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• https://t.signageos.io</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong> This is case sensitive. It all needs to be lower case. Additionally, you need to make sure to enter the “s” in https. Otherwise, it will not work.</p><p><br></p><p>8) On the RM Server screen, select “Skip” </p><p>9) On the TV Source screen, select \"I don’t receive a TV signal”</p><p>10) Set the Time and Date to the correct current information.</p><p>11) Click on “Done”</p><p>12) Press the “Menu” button on the remote</p><p>13) Go down into the “System” settings</p><p>14) Select “Power Control”</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Turn on “Auto Power On”</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Turn on “Network Standby”</p><p>15) Go into the “Eco Solution” settings</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Turn off all of the Eco Solution settings&nbsp;</p><p>16) Go into the “Auto Source Switching”</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Turn off Auto Source Switching</p><p>17) Press the “Home” button on the remote</p><p>18) Go over to the far-left option: URL Launcher (or Custom App)</p><p>19) The screen should start downloading Clarity and eventually show a Hashcode</p><p>20) Call CRI Support at (888) 369-3629 to have the Hashcode entered into the system to activate the screen.</p><p><br></p><p>For a pictured guide on how to activate this screen, please click on the link here:</p><p>https://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/NOC%20Team/EZ_IwVo6qFFNuPw7CN0nj6ABNP_9iyHfmDwx6iinh3rdBA?e=rAx1Nu</p><p><br></p><p>If it is suspected that there is any defective equipment. Please take pictures and collect the following:</p><p>&nbsp;- Make:</p><p>&nbsp;- Model #:</p><p>&nbsp;- Serial #:</p><p>&nbsp;- Additional information may be required to be collected.</p><p><br></p><p>Call the NOC at ​(888) 369-3629 to verify the work</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">IMPORTANT:</strong> You must clean up the site after all work is completed. Leave the area looking as good as (or better than) when you arrived</p><p>Perform additional troubleshooting as necessary</p><p>Old Equipment Instructions:</p><p>Put the old defective screen in the box the new screen was delivered in then leave it in a safe spot on site for the Samsung driver to pick it up. Take photo of where the defective screen is left on site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>IMPORTANT: If you must cancel or reschedule, please call Creative Realities Dispatch at (502) 791-8802.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** List of Required Tools **********</p><p>Some tools on this list will be job specific. If you have any questions about a listed tool, please contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 to discuss.</p><p><br></p><p>USB (wireless) mouse and keyboard</p><p>USB Flash Drive (32GB or higher)</p><p>Test monitor</p><p>Universal remote</p><p>Fully charged laptop with SD Card Reader</p><p>Cat5 tester</p><p>Electrical tester (voltmeter)</p><p>Spare cables (Cat5, VGA, DVI, HDMI, etc.)</p><p>Network and video termination tools</p><p>Impact Drill with standard, metric, and Torx bits</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Zip ties and/or Velcro</p><p>Cleaning materials for screen</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** Check Out **********</p><p>You must submit the signed work order, all required photos to FieldNation then contact Dispatch at <span style=\"color: rgb(191, 191, 191);\">(502) 791-8802 </span>and confirm that you have provided all of the necessary information and documentation prior to leaving the site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** Deliverable Requirements **********</p><p>If any of the equipment onsite is found to be defective. It is your responsibility to capture the Model # and Serial # information for the defective equipment. This information needs to be uploaded to FieldNation so that a replacement can be sourced.</p><p>If any of the deliverables are not retrieved, you will be expected to return to the site without any form of pay increase to retrieve the required deliverables.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If any of the deliverables are not provided within the Work Order, it will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.</p><p><br></p><p>********** DISCLAIMER **********</p><p>You should NEVER use the name of your company while onsite.</p><p><br></p><p>IF YOU NOTICE ANY ISSUES OUTSIDE OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK, YOU MUST DOCUMENT THE ISSUE ON THE WORK ORDER IMMEDIATELY AND TAKE DIGITAL PHOTOS. THEN NOTIFY CREATIVE REALITIES OF THE ISSUE.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you are more than 15 minutes late and we have not heard from you. This ticket will be cancelled and will be reported to FieldNation. You will not be compensated in this event. We need our technicians to be onsite, on-time, every time. We understand that problems do arise. However, we need to be notified of those problems before you become late, not after.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>All dispatch orders require that all the listed deliverables within the Scope of Work be provided in order to be paid out. Any work order that is marked as “Complete” without meeting all of the listed deliverables will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.</p><p>If you fail to abide by the terms and conditions within these instructions and/or by the terms and conditions of FieldNation. This ticket will be closed for zero (0) dollars. By accepting this work order, you acknowledge and agree to these terms.</p><p>You will be given a 48-hour period after the completion of your work to submit for any expense reimbursements and/or budget increase requests. If there are no requests submitted, after the 48-hour mark, the Work Order will be closed and paid based upon the hourly rate.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Scope of Work \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Scope of Work \\*\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\*\\* TECH MUST CALL CRI UPON ARRIVING TO AND BEFORE LEAVING SITE \\*\\*\\*\n\nMUST Check In with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have before photos ready)\n\nFor any and all Technical Assistance, reach out to Support @ 888-369-3629\n\nMUST Check Out with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have after photos ready)\n\nWork with the site contact Site Manager to locate the Replacement Screen\n\nWork with the site contact Site Manager to locate the drive thru screen three\n\nInspect each replacement item as it is pulled from the boxing to verify condition (take pictures)\n\nTake pictures of the old equipment before it is removed from its location\n\nUninstall and remove the old screen from its location (take pictures)\n\nInstall the replacement screen in its location (take pictures)\n\nRun and/or connect all cables between the replacement (equipment) and the remaining old equipment\n\nVerify all functionality of all equipment on site (content, sound, touch, etc.)\n\nSteps to activate Clarity:\n\n1\\) Turn on the Display. It should load up to the Welcome screen.\n\n2\\) Select the appropriate language.\n\n3\\) You’ll be asked if you want to clone an already configured display or start a basic setup. Select Basic Setup.\n\n4\\) Set the “Display Orientation” to Landscape.\n\n5\\) Connect the display to the appropriate network (might be Wi-Fi or Wired)\n\n6\\) On the Play Via screen, select “URL Launcher” (or “Custom App” depending on the model of the screen).\n\n7\\) This will bring you to a new window so that you can enter in the URL that needs to be used. Please enter:\n\n • <https://t.signageos.io>\n\n**NOTE:** This is case sensitive. It all needs to be lower case. Additionally, you need to make sure to enter the “s” in https. Otherwise, it will not work.\n\n8\\) On the RM Server screen, select “Skip”\n\n9\\) On the TV Source screen, select \"I don’t receive a TV signal”\n\n10\\) Set the Time and Date to the correct current information.\n\n11\\) Click on “Done”\n\n12\\) Press the “Menu” button on the remote\n\n13\\) Go down into the “System” settings\n\n14\\) Select “Power Control”\n\n • Turn on “Auto Power On”\n\n • Turn on “Network Standby”\n\n15\\) Go into the “Eco Solution” settings\n\n • Turn off all of the Eco Solution settings\n\n16\\) Go into the “Auto Source Switching”\n\n • Turn off Auto Source Switching\n\n17\\) Press the “Home” button on the remote\n\n18\\) Go over to the far-left option: URL Launcher (or Custom App)\n\n19\\) The screen should start downloading Clarity and eventually show a Hashcode\n\n20\\) Call CRI Support at (888) 369-3629 to have the Hashcode entered into the system to activate the screen.\n\nFor a pictured guide on how to activate this screen, please click on the link here:\n\nhttps://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/NOC%20Team/EZ_IwVo6qFFNuPw7CN0nj6ABNP_9iyHfmDwx6iinh3rdBA?e=rAx1Nu\n\nIf it is suspected that there is any defective equipment. Please take pictures and collect the following:\n\n\\- Make:\n\n\\- Model #:\n\n\\- Serial #:\n\n\\- Additional information may be required to be collected.\n\nCall the NOC at ​(888) 369-3629 to verify the work\n\n**IMPORTANT:** You must clean up the site after all work is completed. Leave the area looking as good as (or better than) when you arrived\n\nPerform additional troubleshooting as necessary\n\nOld Equipment Instructions:\n\nPut the old defective screen in the box the new screen was delivered in then leave it in a safe spot on site for the Samsung driver to pick it up. Take photo of where the defective screen is left on site.\n\nIMPORTANT: If you must cancel or reschedule, please call Creative Realities Dispatch at (502) 791-8802.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* List of Required Tools \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nSome tools on this list will be job specific. If you have any questions about a listed tool, please contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 to discuss.\n\nUSB (wireless) mouse and keyboard\n\nUSB Flash Drive (32GB or higher)\n\nTest monitor\n\nUniversal remote\n\nFully charged laptop with SD Card Reader\n\nCat5 tester\n\nElectrical tester (voltmeter)\n\nSpare cables (Cat5, VGA, DVI, HDMI, etc.)\n\nNetwork and video termination tools\n\nImpact Drill with standard, metric, and Torx bits\n\nLadder\n\nZip ties and/or Velcro\n\nCleaning materials for screen\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Check Out \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nYou must submit the signed work order, all required photos to FieldNation then contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 and confirm that you have provided all of the necessary information and documentation prior to leaving the site.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Deliverable Requirements \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIf any of the equipment onsite is found to be defective. It is your responsibility to capture the Model # and Serial # information for the defective equipment. This information needs to be uploaded to FieldNation so that a replacement can be sourced.\n\nIf any of the deliverables are not retrieved, you will be expected to return to the site without any form of pay increase to retrieve the required deliverables.\n\nIf any of the deliverables are not provided within the Work Order, it will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* DISCLAIMER \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nYou should NEVER use the name of your company while onsite.\n\nIF YOU NOTICE ANY ISSUES OUTSIDE OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK, YOU MUST DOCUMENT THE ISSUE ON THE WORK ORDER IMMEDIATELY AND TAKE DIGITAL PHOTOS. THEN NOTIFY CREATIVE REALITIES OF THE ISSUE.\n\nIf you are more than 15 minutes late and we have not heard from you. This ticket will be cancelled and will be reported to FieldNation. You will not be compensated in this event. We need our technicians to be onsite, on-time, every time. We understand that problems do arise. However, we need to be notified of those problems before you become late, not after.\n\nAll dispatch orders require that all the listed deliverables within the Scope of Work be provided in order to be paid out. Any work order that is marked as “Complete” without meeting all of the listed deliverables will be s