{"job":{"id":20018349,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Strategic Systems, Inc.","title":"Replace 2 Cameras","description":{"html":"<p>Technician will need to check in with our support team upon arrival 937-927-1669<br />\n<br />\nSupport Contact: Ted Saari 504-357-4981<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nThis work order has a specific time allotment. Special permission with details and photos will be need for any overage per customer's approval.<br />\n<br />\nNo Sub techs will be approved unless vetted by Ted from our support team<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nDress Code: Collared shirt, nice jeans, no open toe shoes and good hygiene is necessary for this work order.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nAll cameras must be online before being released from site.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nJob ID# 2609-086638<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nScope of Work:<br />\n(2) Indoor IP Camera Replacement<br />\n<br />\nAdditional scope details:<br />\n- Replace the offline indoor multisite PC camera<br />\n- See attached for PC camera guidelines.<br />\n- Replace the offline indoor multisite camera labeled, \"Back Door\"<br />\n- Verify that camera replacement fixed the problem and do a cable test<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nSpecial Request by Customer:<br />\n<br />\nArrive on site introduce to MOD and check in<br />\n<br />\nReview SOW install notes and attachments<br />\n<br />\nUnbox and take complete inventory. Take pictures of inventory. (alert Help Desk immediately if inventory is incomplete)<br />\n<br />\nRun wire, mount, and install cameras (alert help desk if any issues arise)<br />\n<br />\nConnect cameras and adjust views (notify help desk if any cams are DOA)<br />\n<br />\nTake pictures of completed installation of all installed equipment, and send pictures to helpdesk.<br />\n<br />\nObtain approval of views from POC/View Approver<br />\n<br />\nRelease Tech and check out with MOD<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nList of Materials provided by Tech:<br />\n<br />\nType of Cable: CAT5 Plenum (Bring just in case)<br />\n<br />\nCat6 Plenum Cable is reimbursed at .35 a foot<br />\n<br />\nCat5 Plenum Cable is reimbursed at .30 a foot<br />\n<br />\nSiamese Cable is reimbursed at .35 a foot<br />\n<br />\nEstimated Cable Length: 200ft (Bring just in case)<br />\n<br />\nRJ45 Ends used for terminations will be reimbursed at 1.25 each<br />\n<br />\nLadder or Lift: 10ft Ladder<br />\n<br />\nMiscellaneous Materials: Monitor, mouse, and laptop running windows<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nAll materials used except cable will need to be pre-approved by Strategic<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nList of Hardware provided by Envysion to install:<br />\n(1) PELCO 2MP, Fixed, 2.8mm, Sarix Value Environmental IR Fixed<br />\n*** Second camera was sent by tech support.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nCabling Tool List:<br />\n<br />\n10-12ft Ladder<br />\n<br />\nBasic Hand Tools<br />\n<br />\nBNC Connectors and crimper<br />\n<br />\nCable Punch Down Tool with 66 and 11 blades<br />\n<br />\nCable Tester<br />\n<br />\nCable Ties<br />\n<br />\nCable Toner<br />\n<br />\nCell Phone<br />\n<br />\nCordless Drill<br />\n<br />\nRJ 45 Connector and crimper<br />\n<br />\nPatch Cables – Assorted Sizes<br />\n<br />\nLaptop with Ethernet Cable<br />\n<br />\nMounting Tools<br />\n<br />\nPush/Pull Rods<br />\n<br />\nUSB Keyboard/Mouse<br />\n<br />\nPC monitor<br />\n<br />\nSpot monitor (preferred but not mandated)<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nInformation needed prior to call to check out:<br />\n<br />\nWhere is the NVR located<br />\n<br />\nManager's First &amp; Last Night<br />\n<br />\nWhat device is the NVR getting internet from?<br />\n<br />\nHow many POE ports are available/open on the camera switch not counting uplinks<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nCheck Out Questions:<br />\n<br />\nWhen completing a site, we would like you to call us at 504-357-4981 When calling in Have this information ready:<br />\n<br />\n1. What is the Job ID Number?<br />\n<br />\n2. Where is the Camera power supply physically mounted / Located? (POE, analog power, both are power supplies, and we need to know where they are located so we can share the info with our TS team.)<br />\n<br />\n3. Where is the DVR physically located?<br />\n<br />\n4. What network device are we plugged into? What switch provides us with the internet? Poe is not the correct switch 90% of the time.<br />\n<br />\n5. Which port are we plugged into on the network device?<br />\n<br />\n6. Who was the tech?<br />\n<br />\n7. Who did they check out with onsite? Did we verify that all the systems that were previously connected are still working (phones, music, pos, internet<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nA release code will be provided to you after you answer the checkout questions and send all deliverables to our support team. Please provide the code to our support team.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTime overages must be pre-approved by the support team.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTechnician will need to check out and upload all required deliverables before leaving site 504-357-4981</p>","markdown":"Technician will need to check in with our support team upon arrival 937-927-1669  \n  \nSupport Contact: Ted Saari 504-357-4981  \n  \n  \nThis work order has a specific time allotment. Special permission with details and photos will be need for any overage per customer's approval.  \n  \nNo Sub techs will be approved unless vetted by Ted from our support team  \n  \n  \nDress Code: Collared shirt, nice jeans, no open toe shoes and good hygiene is necessary for this work order.  \n  \n  \n  \nAll cameras must be online before being released from site.  \n  \n  \nJob ID# 2609-086638  \n  \n  \n  \nScope of Work:  \n(2) Indoor IP Camera Replacement  \n  \nAdditional scope details:  \n\\- Replace the offline indoor multisite PC camera  \n\\- See attached for PC camera guidelines.  \n\\- Replace the offline indoor multisite camera labeled, \"Back Door\"  \n\\- Verify that camera replacement fixed the problem and do a cable test  \n  \n  \n  \n  \nSpecial Request by Customer:  \n  \nArrive on site introduce to MOD and check in  \n  \nReview SOW install notes and attachments  \n  \nUnbox and take complete inventory. Take pictures of inventory. (alert Help Desk immediately if inventory is incomplete)  \n  \nRun wire, mount, and install cameras (alert help desk if any issues arise)  \n  \nConnect cameras and adjust views (notify help desk if any cams are DOA)  \n  \nTake pictures of completed installation of all installed equipment, and send pictures to helpdesk.  \n  \nObtain approval of views from POC/View Approver  \n  \nRelease Tech and check out with MOD  \n  \n  \n  \nList of Materials provided by Tech:  \n  \nType of Cable: CAT5 Plenum (Bring just in case)  \n  \nCat6 Plenum Cable is reimbursed at .35 a foot  \n  \nCat5 Plenum Cable is reimbursed at .30 a foot  \n  \nSiamese Cable is reimbursed at .35 a foot  \n  \nEstimated Cable Length: 200ft (Bring just in case)  \n  \nRJ45 Ends used for terminations will be reimbursed at 1.25 each  \n  \nLadder or Lift: 10ft Ladder  \n  \nMiscellaneous Materials: Monitor, mouse, and laptop running windows  \n  \n  \n  \nAll materials used except cable will need to be pre-approved by Strategic  \n  \n  \n  \nList of Hardware provided by Envysion to install:  \n(1) PELCO 2MP, Fixed, 2.8mm, Sarix Value Environmental IR Fixed  \n\\*\\*\\* Second camera was sent by tech support.  \n  \n  \nCabling Tool List:  \n  \n10-12ft Ladder  \n  \nBasic Hand Tools  \n  \nBNC Connectors and crimper  \n  \nCable Punch Down Tool with 66 and 11 blades  \n  \nCable Tester  \n  \nCable Ties  \n  \nCable Toner  \n  \nCell Phone  \n  \nCordless Drill  \n  \nRJ 45 Connector and crimper  \n  \nPatch Cables – Assorted Sizes  \n  \nLaptop with Ethernet Cable  \n  \nMounting Tools  \n  \nPush/Pull Rods  \n  \nUSB Keyboard/Mouse  \n  \nPC monitor  \n  \nSpot monitor (preferred but not mandated)  \n  \n  \n  \nInformation needed prior to call to check out:  \n  \nWhere is the NVR located  \n  \nManager's First & Last Night  \n  \nWhat device is the NVR getting internet from?  \n  \nHow many POE ports are available/open on the camera switch not counting uplinks  \n  \n  \n  \nCheck Out Questions:  \n  \nWhen completing a site, we would like you to call us at 504-357-4981 When calling in Have this information ready:  \n  \n1\\. What is the Job ID Number?  \n  \n2\\. Where is the Camera power supply physically mounted / Located? (POE, analog power, both are power supplies, and we need to know where they are located so we can share the info with our TS team.)  \n  \n3\\. Where is the DVR physically located?  \n  \n4\\. What network device are we plugged into? What switch provides us with the internet? Poe is not the correct switch 90% of the time.  \n  \n5\\. Which port are we plugged into on the network device?  \n  \n6\\. Who was the tech?  \n  \n7\\. Who did they check out with onsite? Did we verify that all the systems that were previously connected are still working (phones, music, pos, internet  \n  \n  \n  \nA release code will be provided to you after you answer the checkout questions and send all deliverables to our support team. Please provide the code to our support team.  \n  \n  \n  \nTime overages must be pre-approved by the support team.  \n  \n  \n  \nTechnician will need to check out and upload all required deliverables before leaving site 504-357-4981","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2.5,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"