{"job":{"id":20023291,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"PPT0982749 Battery Issue","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Service Overview:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>***** ACTION PLAN *****</p><p>------- Created by Team -------</p><p>Created By: Wintel / x86 – Technical Support Engineering, Level 3</p><p>------- Current Issue -------</p><p>The Smart Storage Battery continues to report a failed condition even after it was replaced yesterday.&nbsp;</p><p>Under normal circumstances, the battery should not take this long to charge. This suggests the replacement&nbsp;</p><p>battery may be defective.</p><p><br></p><p>------- Evidence of the Issue -------</p><p>The customer provided iLO screen shots that shows the failed Smart Storage Battery.&nbsp;</p><p>------- Special Instructions -------&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>------- Parts -------</p><p>Quantity: 1</p><p>Part Number: 875238-B21</p><p>Description: HP 12W Smart Storage Battery</p><p>Location:&nbsp;located inside the blade, under the top access panel, and is&nbsp;</p><p>connected to the Smart Array storage controller</p><p>------- Detailed Steps to Resolve -------</p><p>Tech to schedule service with customer.</p><p>Remove the Battery</p><p>Shut down the server blade.</p><p>Remove the blade from the BladeSystem enclosure.</p><p>Remove the top access panel.</p><p>Locate the Smart Storage Battery connected to the storage controller.</p><p>Note the orientation of the battery and cable routing.</p><p>If the battery has a cable connected to the controller, disconnect it, paying attention to wire orientation.</p><p>Remove the battery from its holder.</p><p>Install the New Battery</p><p>Connect the new battery cable to the controller (if applicable).</p><p>Place the battery into the holder in the same orientation as the original.</p><p>Reinstall the top access panel.</p><p>Reinsert the blade into the enclosure.</p><p>Power on the server.</p><p>After Replacement</p><p>Boot into Intelligent Provisioning.</p><p>Open Smart Storage Administrator (SSA).</p><p>Verify the status of:</p><p>Logical Drives</p><p>Physical Drives</p><p>Cache Battery</p><p>If a logical drive is disabled, re-enable it if possible.</p><p>Allow the battery to charge and verify its status changes to healthy.</p><p>Important Note</p><p>The Gen9 battery replacement procedure specifically states that the cache battery may take up to</p><p>approximately 2 hours to fully charge. During this time, Smart Array cache may remain disabled and&nbsp;</p><p>performance can be affected. If the cache remains permanently disabled after the battery has had&nbsp;</p><p>sufficient time to charge, the procedure recommends investigating or replacing the cache DIMM.</p><p>Given your case where the replacement battery still shows failed, I'd verify in SSA:</p><p>Battery status (Charging, Failed, or OK)</p><p>Cache module status</p><p>Controller firmware level</p><p>Whether the new battery part number matches the original</p><p>Those checks will help determine whether you're dealing with a bad replacement battery, a cache module issue,&nbsp;</p><p>or a controller issue.</p><p>Do not leave site until customer is satisfied and all is working.</p><p>Call PPT Service if further help is needed.</p><p><br></p><p>------- Supporting Documents -------</p><p>HPE ProLiant BL460c Gen9 Server Blade</p><p>https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/docDisplay?docId=c04410344&amp;docLocale=en_US</p><p>------- Timeline -------</p><p>Next Steps: Field Engineer to call customer to schedule service and follow Action Plan above.</p><p>Next Owner: Field Engineer</p><p>*****&nbsp;End Action Plan&nbsp;&nbsp;*****</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions</strong></p><p>As a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.</p><p><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:</strong> Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a <strong>$20 USD deduction</strong> from the total work order pay.</p><p><strong>Escalations</strong></p><ol><li>Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li><li>For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li></ol><p>Consumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.</p><p>Upon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).</p><p>Upon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.</p><p>All parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.</p><p>PLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.</p><p>Return of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.</p><p>If a part is removed from a local warehouse:</p><p>A. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>B. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>YOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.</p><p>Acceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:</p><ul><li>State ID</li><li>Driver's License</li><li>US Passport</li></ul><p>ALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:</p><ul><li>Laptop computer</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)</li><li>Standard tool kit</li><li>Static mat and/or static strap</li><li>Heat Sink Paste</li><li>Blank CD's/DVD's</li><li>Portable CD/DVD drive</li><li>USB Flash drive</li><li>Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable</li><li>Hot Spot</li><li>Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed</li></ul><p>Tech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.</p><p>Tech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.</p><p>Tech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:</p><p><strong>NO JEANS</strong></p><p><strong>NO OPEN-TOE SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO GYM SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING</strong></p><p>IMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.</p><p>If the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.</p><p><strong>Software Policy</strong></p><p>Policy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code</p><p>1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.</p><p>2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.</p><p>3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.</p><p>4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner</p><ul><li>5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Service Overview:**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ACTION PLAN \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\------- Created by Team -------\n\nCreated By: Wintel / x86 – Technical Support Engineering, Level 3\n\n\\------- Current Issue -------\n\nThe Smart Storage Battery continues to report a failed condition even after it was replaced yesterday.\n\nUnder normal circumstances, the battery should not take this long to charge. This suggests the replacement\n\nbattery may be defective.\n\n\\------- Evidence of the Issue -------\n\nThe customer provided iLO screen shots that shows the failed Smart Storage Battery.\n\n\\------- Special Instructions -------\n\n\\------- Parts -------\n\nQuantity: 1\n\nPart Number: 875238-B21\n\nDescription: HP 12W Smart Storage Battery\n\nLocation: located inside the blade, under the top access panel, and is\n\nconnected to the Smart Array storage controller\n\n\\------- Detailed Steps to Resolve -------\n\nTech to schedule service with customer.\n\nRemove the Battery\n\nShut down the server blade.\n\nRemove the blade from the BladeSystem enclosure.\n\nRemove the top access panel.\n\nLocate the Smart Storage Battery connected to the storage controller.\n\nNote the orientation of the battery and cable routing.\n\nIf the battery has a cable connected to the controller, disconnect it, paying attention to wire orientation.\n\nRemove the battery from its holder.\n\nInstall the New Battery\n\nConnect the new battery cable to the controller (if applicable).\n\nPlace the battery into the holder in the same orientation as the original.\n\nReinstall the top access panel.\n\nReinsert the blade into the enclosure.\n\nPower on the server.\n\nAfter Replacement\n\nBoot into Intelligent Provisioning.\n\nOpen Smart Storage Administrator (SSA).\n\nVerify the status of:\n\nLogical Drives\n\nPhysical Drives\n\nCache Battery\n\nIf a logical drive is disabled, re-enable it if possible.\n\nAllow the battery to charge and verify its status changes to healthy.\n\nImportant Note\n\nThe Gen9 battery replacement procedure specifically states that the cache battery may take up to\n\napproximately 2 hours to fully charge. During this time, Smart Array cache may remain disabled and\n\nperformance can be affected. If the cache remains permanently disabled after the battery has had\n\nsufficient time to charge, the procedure recommends investigating or replacing the cache DIMM.\n\nGiven your case where the replacement battery still shows failed, I'd verify in SSA:\n\nBattery status (Charging, Failed, or OK)\n\nCache module status\n\nController firmware level\n\nWhether the new battery part number matches the original\n\nThose checks will help determine whether you're dealing with a bad replacement battery, a cache module issue,\n\nor a controller issue.\n\nDo not leave site until customer is satisfied and all is working.\n\nCall PPT Service if further help is needed.\n\n\\------- Supporting Documents -------\n\nHPE ProLiant BL460c Gen9 Server Blade\n\nhttps://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/docDisplay?docId=c04410344&amp;docLocale=en_US\n\n\\------- Timeline -------\n\nNext Steps: Field Engineer to call customer to schedule service and follow Action Plan above.\n\nNext Owner: Field Engineer\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* End Action Plan \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Special Instructions**\n\nAs a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.\n\n**MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:** Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a **$20 USD deduction** from the total work order pay.\n\n**Escalations**\n\n1. Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n2. For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n\nConsumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.\n\nUpon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).\n\nUpon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.\n\nAll parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.\n\nPLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.\n\nReturn of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.\n\nIf a part is removed from a local warehouse:\n\nA. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nB. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nYOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.\n\nAcceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:\n\n- State ID\n- Driver's License\n- US Passport\n\nALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:\n\n- Laptop computer\n- Voltmeter\n- Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)\n- Standard tool kit\n- Static mat and/or static strap\n- Heat Sink Paste\n- Blank CD's/DVD's\n- Portable CD/DVD drive\n- USB Flash drive\n- Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable\n- Hot Spot\n- Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed\n\nTech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.\n\nTech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.\n\nTech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:\n\n**NO JEANS**\n\n**NO OPEN-TOE SHOES**\n\n**NO GYM SHOES**\n\n**NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING**\n\nIMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.\n\nIf the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.\n\n**Software Policy**\n\nPolicy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code\n\n1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.\n\n2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.\n\n3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.\n\n4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner\n\n- 5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T08:00","end":"2026-09-28T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":380,"max":380},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":true,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"ELIGIBLE"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"APPLY","ts":1790271928207}
{"job":{"id":20024020,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Tractor Supply - Network Troubleshoot + Cable Management","description":{"html":"<p>Details of Site/Dispatch</p><ul><li>Account Name:  Tractor Supply</li><li>Site ID / Location Address: Petsense 7100 / 739 N Madison Blvd, Roxboro North Carolina 27573</li><li>Contact Onsite Name &amp; Phone: MOD <del>**********</del></li><li>Severity: Location is hard down</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>General Network Troubleshooting</strong></p><p><strong>Default Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Tech will need to check the primary modem and physical equipment for power or connectivity issues. prove clean surf off of the modem and attempt connection bypass on the router if needed. Site will also need cable clean up and labeling for easier troubleshooting later </p><p>Assist remote support in diagnosing and resolving connectivity issues, cabling problems, or device failures.</p><p></p><p><strong>Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Take pre-work photos</li><li>Connect laptop to device or network drop for diagnostics.</li><li>Perform cable continuity and link tests.</li><li>Reseat cabling and power cycle equipment as directed.</li><li>Validate link status LEDs.</li><li>Document findings and actions taken.</li></ul><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Take photos of any physical damage or environmental concerns found.</span></p><p></p><p>Materials and Required Tools</p><p></p><p>Materials (have extras of all):</p><ul><li>Cat5e cable (at least 200’)</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p>Required Tools:</p><ul><li>Ladder (minimum 10’ A-Frame)</li><li>Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)<ul><li>Can connect to Wi-Fi.</li></ul></li><li>Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor</li><li>Cable Tester<ul><li>Test POE</li></ul></li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)</li><li>Cell Phone<ul><li>with camera and charger</li><li>with ability to connect to Hotspot</li></ul></li><li>Measuring Tools</li><li></li></ul>","markdown":"Details of Site/Dispatch\n\n- Account Name: Tractor Supply\n- Site ID / Location Address: Petsense 7100 / 739 N Madison Blvd, Roxboro North Carolina 27573\n- Contact Onsite Name & Phone: MOD \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Severity: Location is hard down\n\n**General Network Troubleshooting**\n\n**Default Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to check the primary modem and physical equipment for power or connectivity issues. prove clean surf off of the modem and attempt connection bypass on the router if needed. Site will also need cable clean up and labeling for easier troubleshooting later\n\nAssist remote support in diagnosing and resolving connectivity issues, cabling problems, or device failures.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n- Take pre-work photos\n- Connect laptop to device or network drop for diagnostics.\n- Perform cable continuity and link tests.\n- Reseat cabling and power cycle equipment as directed.\n- Validate link status LEDs.\n- Document findings and actions taken.\n\nTake photos of any physical damage or environmental concerns found.\n\nMaterials and Required Tools\n\nMaterials (have extras of all):\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Ladder (minimum 10’ A-Frame)\n- Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)\n  - Can connect to Wi-Fi.\n- Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n  - Test POE\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)\n- Cell Phone\n  - with camera and charger\n  - with ability to connect to Hotspot\n- Measuring Tools\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T10:30","end":"2026-09-25T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":38},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 28, 10:30 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $260\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790272370229}
{"job":{"id":20024182,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teceze","title":"Field Service Engineer - Retail Store Device Health Check","description":{"html":"<strong>Scope of Work</strong><p>Technicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.</p><p>The technician will:</p><ul><li>Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Self-checkout devices</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Handheld scanners</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other related store technology equipment</li><li>Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.</li><li>Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.</li><li>Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.</li><li>Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.</li><li>Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.</li><li>Document all remediation activities completed onsite.</li><li>Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.</li><li>Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.</li><li>Take clear photos when required for documentation.</li><li>Clean up the work area after completing the activity.</li></ul>Unresolved Issues<p>For issues that cannot be resolved onsite:</p><ul><li>Document the device information and issue details.</li><li>Record troubleshooting steps already performed.</li><li>Provide the information to the project team for further action.</li><li>Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.</li></ul>Technician Requirements<ul><li>Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.</li><li>Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.</li><li>Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.</li><li>Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.</li><li>Must provide professional communication with store personnel.</li><li>Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.</li></ul>Visit &amp; Reporting Requirements<p>Technician must provide:</p><ul><li>Check-in/check-out confirmation.</li><li>Completed health-check checklist.</li><li>List of devices checked.</li><li>Issues identified.</li><li>Remediation performed.</li><li>Parts/devices used, if applicable.</li><li>Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.</li><li>Required photos/documentation.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**Technicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.\n\nThe technician will:\n\n- Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:\n- Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment\n- Self-checkout devices\n- Printers\n- Handheld scanners\n- Other related store technology equipment\n- Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.\n- Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.\n- Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.\n- Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.\n- Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.\n- Document all remediation activities completed onsite.\n- Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.\n- Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.\n- Take clear photos when required for documentation.\n- Clean up the work area after completing the activity.\n\nUnresolved IssuesFor issues that cannot be resolved onsite:\n\n- Document the device information and issue details.\n- Record troubleshooting steps already performed.\n- Provide the information to the project team for further action.\n- Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.\n\nTechnician Requirements- Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.\n- Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.\n- Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.\n- Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.\n- Must provide professional communication with store personnel.\n- Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.\n\nVisit & Reporting RequirementsTechnician must provide:\n\n- Check-in/check-out confirmation.\n- Completed health-check checklist.\n- List of devices checked.\n- Issues identified.\n- Remediation performed.\n- Parts/devices used, if applicable.\n- Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.\n- Required photos/documentation.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T08:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790272464479}
{"job":{"id":20024221,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Strata Pointe Technologies, Inc.","title":"IntraSystems-NH - Campers Inn - Selma, NC - Firewall Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>TRAVEL WILL NOT BE APPROVED UNLESS DISCUSSED PRIOR TO WORK ORDER ASSIGNMENT</strong></p><p><strong>TECH TOOLS/MATERIAL STANDARD FOR ALL SITES:</strong></p><ul><li>6' Ladder</li><li>Console cable</li><li>Laptop with Putty or terminal emulation software</li><li>DB-9 to USB adapter for laptop and console cable connection</li><li>Hotspot for internet connection</li><li>Charged Cell phone with clear photo capture capability</li><li>Cat6 Cable - 300' as precautionary for all sites</li><li>Cat6 Patch Cables - 1'-3' as precautionary for all sites</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Label maker</li><li>surface mount jacks (RJ-45)</li><li>RJ-45 termination ends</li><li>RJ-11 termination ends</li><li>Butt Set or analog phone</li><li>punch down tools</li><li>Pull rods</li><li>Wire crimper</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ul><li>Tech to arrive on-site and contact Strata Pointe Project Coordinator - Jagger Simon - 502.373.1639</li><li><strong>Tech to arrive and meet with on-site contact - </strong>Jason Forster - <span style=\"color: rgb(49, 57, 73);\">727-277-0289</span></li><li>We want the tech to call William Walters on his direct line, 603-420-1218, before he begins any work and before he leaves the site for the day.</li><li>Install a FortiGate firewall in the existing rack on top of an available shelf or switch (if necessary).</li><li>Power up the FortiGate</li><li>Move the existing patch cables under IntraSystems direction to the new FortiGate</li><li>Provide 30 minutes to do testing</li><li>Remove the existing Barracuda firewall</li><li>Tech to contact Strata Pointe Project Coordinator for site release - Jagger Simon - 502.373.1639</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Photo of site-specific issue(s)</li><li>Photos of site Network/Telco Room</li><li>Photo of cabling</li><li>Photos of any work completed</li><li>Site notes&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**TRAVEL WILL NOT BE APPROVED UNLESS DISCUSSED PRIOR TO WORK ORDER ASSIGNMENT**\n\n**TECH TOOLS/MATERIAL STANDARD FOR ALL SITES:**\n\n- 6' Ladder\n- Console cable\n- Laptop with Putty or terminal emulation software\n- DB-9 to USB adapter for laptop and console cable connection\n- Hotspot for internet connection\n- Charged Cell phone with clear photo capture capability\n- Cat6 Cable - 300' as precautionary for all sites\n- Cat6 Patch Cables - 1'-3' as precautionary for all sites\n- Cable tester\n- Toner\n- Label maker\n- surface mount jacks (RJ-45)\n- RJ-45 termination ends\n- RJ-11 termination ends\n- Butt Set or analog phone\n- punch down tools\n- Pull rods\n- Wire crimper\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n- Tech to arrive on-site and contact Strata Pointe Project Coordinator - Jagger Simon - 502.373.1639\n- **Tech to arrive and meet with on-site contact -** Jason Forster - 727-277-0289\n- We want the tech to call William Walters on his direct line, 603-420-1218, before he begins any work and before he leaves the site for the day.\n- Install a FortiGate firewall in the existing rack on top of an available shelf or switch (if necessary).\n- Power up the FortiGate\n- Move the existing patch cables under IntraSystems direction to the new FortiGate\n- Provide 30 minutes to do testing\n- Remove the existing Barracuda firewall\n- Tech to contact Strata Pointe Project Coordinator for site release - Jagger Simon - 502.373.1639\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n- Photo of site-specific issue(s)\n- Photos of site Network/Telco Room\n- Photo of cabling\n- Photos of any work completed\n- Site notes","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T07:45","end":"2026-10-07T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":35},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PA