{"job":{"id":"1453728676","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Excis","title":"SOURCING - Cognizant novartis - Durham, NC - Network Support","description":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Network support related requests</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Arrival (Before Reaching the Site)</strong></p><p>-Review the work order, problem description, asset history, and applicable service level agreements (SLAs).</p><p>-Confirm the site location, access instructions, and primary point of contact (POC).</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Onsite Arrival and Execution (During the Visit)</strong></p><p>-Check in with the front desk or site manager immediately upon arrival and wear the required identification badge.</p><p>-Perform a safety assessment of the work area before beginning any work.</p><p>-Update the ticket status to \"Onsite\" or \"Work Started\" to record the arrival time.</p><p>-Join the Microsoft Teams bridge created by CTS and follow all instructions provided by the CTS team while troubleshooting the issue.</p><p>-Keep the remote support team informed often (every hour or more often if visits require constant contact support) and also if any unexpected issues appear.</p><p>-The CTS team will test the system, equipment, or network to verify that the issue has been resolved.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Post-Execution and Departure (After Leaving the Site)</strong></p><p>-Restore the work area to its original condition by removing all debris, replaced parts, and tools.</p><p>-Obtain customer sign-off to confirm completion of the work.</p><p>-Send the Excis SVRs properly completed with Site Poc signatures before leaving the site</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Communication Channel</strong></p><p>Meeting Application: Microsoft Teams (Link TBA)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>* Fully charged Windows laptop (Windows 8 or later) with USB-A ports.</p><p>* USB-C hub if the laptop provides only USB-C ports.’</p><p>* Laptop charger.</p><p>* Active mobile hotspot.</p><p>* Ethernet cables (Cat 5).</p><p>* DB-9 (F) to RJ-45 (M) console cable.</p><p>* DB9-to-USB adapter if the laptop does not have a serial port.</p><p>* Tera Term, Putty (32-bit MSI), and UART drivers.</p><ul><li>* All additional tools required for the task will be specified in the ticket information sent by Remote Support Teams (Ethernet tester, RJ-45 connectors, USB flash drive (minimum 1 GB), Mobile phone, Cable tester, Punch-down tool, Console cable and if any Required software).</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00","end":"2026-09-30T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":80.6,"max":241.8},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80.6,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":11.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $241.8 (countered: $242) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action