{"job":{"id":20024777,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Replace Existing Switches with 24-Port Juniper & Test | Connect Existing Circuit/Modem |Remote Support | UPS Drop-Off | Est. Onsite: 1.5hrs","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store</li><li><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional <strong>$30 expense</strong> for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"><u>IMPORTANT NOTE</u></strong><u style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">:</u><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY </strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time</strong></li><li>Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied</li><li><strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense</li><li>Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u> </strong></p><ul><li>Packing Tape</li><li><u>﻿</u>Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity</li><li>Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)</li><li>Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger &amp; Camera</li><li>Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;</li><li>6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)</li><li>Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.</li><li>Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment</li><li>Ethernet Network Cable Toner &amp; Tester</li><li>100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch</li></ul><p><strong><u>On-Site Tasks:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">IMPORTANT</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">:&nbsp;</span><strong>You are required to reference the ‘</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\">Confidential Information</strong><strong>’ section&nbsp;<em><u>IF</u></em>&nbsp;any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted</strong></li><li>Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See customer field '<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">Site Contact Name &amp; Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list&nbsp;</span>MOD/LCON<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">&nbsp;and not a specific person)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty</li><li>At the scheduled install time, call <strong><del>************</del></strong> to check in and work directly with the <del>****</del> team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Important</strong>: You must work with the <del>****</del> team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed</li><li>Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work</li><li>Confirm the contents in the box with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label</li><li>Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks <strong>(see the attached network diagram for reference):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Only at the direction of the remote support team</u></strong>, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 0-3 = Workstation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 4-5 = Printer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 6-7 = Phones</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 8 = Access Point</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 9 = Gate</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 10 = Future Use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 11 = Kiosk</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 22 = WattBox Network Port</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Locate the Customer Broadband Modem</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Identify the modem’s <strong>Ethernet/network port</strong> providing the broadband connection</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Using a patch cable, connect the modem to <strong>GE1 on the Edge device</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected <strong>link/activity indicators</strong> on both devices</li><li>Wait for <del>****</del> verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating</li><li>Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Close and securely tape the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; <strong>ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label</li><li>Drop off the package at a local UPS location</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Upload the UPS drop-off receipt</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Required On-Site Deliverables:</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email the photos to the <del>****</del> team at <del>*****************</del> Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation</li></ol><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><p>For any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:</p><p><strong>Contact Hours:</strong></p><p><strong><u>8:00 AM &ndash; 5:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>***** ************</del></li><li><del>****** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong><u>2:00 PM &ndash; 11:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>******** ******************</del></li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store\n- **Estimated onsite duration:** 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional **$30 expense** for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).\n- **IMPORTANT NOTE**: **The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location**\n- **CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY**\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n- **Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time**\n- Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied\n- **MUST** have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense\n- Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)\n\n**Dress code:**\n\n- Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Packing Tape\n- ﻿Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity\n- Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)\n- Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger & Camera\n- Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)\n- Label maker\n- 6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)\n- Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.\n- Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment\n- Ethernet Network Cable Toner & Tester\n- 100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling\n- Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits\n\n**Pre-Site requirements:**\n\n- Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **IMPORTANT**: **You are required to reference the ‘****Confidential Information****’ section *IF* any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted**\n2. Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)\n3. See customer field 'Site Contact Name & Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list MOD/LCON and not a specific person)\n4. Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty\n5. At the scheduled install time, call **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to check in and work directly with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team\n6. **Important**: You must work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed\n7. Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work\n8. Confirm the contents in the box with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field\n9. Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label\n10. Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks **(see the attached network diagram for reference):**\n11. **Only at the direction of the remote support team**, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting\n12. Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not\n13. Ports 0-3 = Workstation\n14. Ports 4-5 = Printer\n15. Ports 6-7 = Phones\n16. Port 8 = Access Point\n17. Port 9 = Gate\n18. Port 10 = Future Use\n19. Port 11 = Kiosk\n20. Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)\n21. Port 22 = WattBox Network Port\n22. Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3\n23. **Locate the Customer Broadband Modem**\n24. Identify the modem’s **Ethernet/network port** providing the broadband connection\n25. Using a patch cable, connect the modem to **GE1 on the Edge device**\n26. Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected **link/activity indicators** on both devices\n27. Wait for \\*\\*\\*\\* verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating\n28. Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return\n29. Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box\n30. Close and securely tape the box\n31. Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; **ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL**\n32. Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label\n33. Drop off the package at a local UPS location\n34. **Upload the UPS drop-off receipt**\n35. **Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n36. Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation\n37. Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order\n38. Email the photos to the \\*\\*\\*\\* team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation\n\n**Escalations:**\n\nFor any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:\n\n**Contact Hours:**\n\n**8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**2:00 PM – 11:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T12:30","end":"2026-10-13T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":60},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":43},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790274734887}
{"job":{"id":20024766,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Troubleshoot Marketspark Equipment  Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.","description":{"html":"<p>Location is Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.</p>\n<p>Signal Check Link</p>\n<p>https://location.marketspark.com/#d03e0d52-9a23-4fed-96bb-cbb7dc71d679</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Site Contact John An <del>***** ********</del></p>\n<p><del>********************</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Scope of Work:</p>\n<p>We have a gray box enclosure with the MarketSpark logo that contains an Inhand router and 2 Grandstream ATAs. These provide dial tone for 12 elevator lines, 2 fire lines, and 1 voice line. Currently we are noticing that the VZ sim appears to not be connecting, which is odd as the customer has a VZ cell repeater device in their location that should allow us to connect. The backup sim in the router, the 10T sim, allows us to connect at times but it constantly shows poor signal metrics.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>We are shipping a new VZ sim card to site to replace the VZ sim to see if we come online after that. Please have a laptop near you just in case. This will go in slot 1 of our router and you need a small pin to get the sim tray out. The diagram on the router shows how the sim card fits. You are leaving the 10T card in there. Please contact MKSP after validating that the equipment comes online and validate that the customer cell repeater works as intended as well. Place inbound/outbound test calls.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Prior to leaving site, call MarketSpark support at (844) 335-5153 to properly validate equipment and note key service details. Reference ticket 310732.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*** Tech will need to bring the following tools:</p>\n<p>1) Butt set w/RJ11 adaptor;</p>\n<p>2) Punch Tool;</p>\n<p>3) Tone &amp; Probe;</p>\n<p>4) Cable in case a new run is needed;</p>\n<p>5) Laptop w/AnyDesk &amp; ethernet cable in case we need to console into any device;</p>\n<p>6) Any other telecom tools.</p>","markdown":"Location is Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.\n\nSignal Check Link\n\n<https://location.marketspark.com/#d03e0d52-9a23-4fed-96bb-cbb7dc71d679>\n\nSite Contact John An \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nScope of Work:\n\nWe have a gray box enclosure with the MarketSpark logo that contains an Inhand router and 2 Grandstream ATAs. These provide dial tone for 12 elevator lines, 2 fire lines, and 1 voice line. Currently we are noticing that the VZ sim appears to not be connecting, which is odd as the customer has a VZ cell repeater device in their location that should allow us to connect. The backup sim in the router, the 10T sim, allows us to connect at times but it constantly shows poor signal metrics.\n\nWe are shipping a new VZ sim card to site to replace the VZ sim to see if we come online after that. Please have a laptop near you just in case. This will go in slot 1 of our router and you need a small pin to get the sim tray out. The diagram on the router shows how the sim card fits. You are leaving the 10T card in there. Please contact MKSP after validating that the equipment comes online and validate that the customer cell repeater works as intended as well. Place inbound/outbound test calls.\n\nPrior to leaving site, call MarketSpark support at (844) 335-5153 to properly validate equipment and note key service details. Reference ticket 310732.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Tech will need to bring the following tools:\n\n1\\) Butt set w/RJ11 adaptor;\n\n2\\) Punch Tool;\n\n3\\) Tone & Probe;\n\n4\\) Cable in case a new run is needed;\n\n5\\) Laptop w/AnyDesk & ethernet cable in case we need to console into any device;\n\n6\\) Any other telecom tools.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T10:00","end":"2026-09-30T13:00","latestStart":"2026-09-30T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":26},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 (countered: $225) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790275023213}
