{"job":{"id":20025202,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":" Troubleshoot DVR","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******** * </del></span><del>******************</del></li><li>Technicians can text 'Start' to <del>***** ********</del>. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.</li></ul><p>Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)</p><p><br></p><p>System &amp; Model #:&nbsp;</p><p>Camera system / Hikvision&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>DVR IS OFFLINE&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>TECHNICIAN MUST BRING: Digital Multimeter, BNC Spot Monitor, BNC crimping tool, Crimp on BNC (Not twist)&nbsp;Laptop with ethernet. </p><p>The technician needs to inspect the DVR&nbsp;for power, connection, and functionality issues. </p><p>It's wiring, the PDU and all PVMs. </p><p>If hardware or cabling appears defective, replace or repair it accordingly. </p><p>The technician should test the camera on-site, coordinating with Help Desk to verify the camera feed is working properly from the control center.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Parts Needed:&nbsp;</p><p>None&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Specific Scheduling Request :</p><p>None&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Other Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request: None</p><p><br></p><p>Cause :&nbsp;Not fully determined&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.</li><li>Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.</li><li>All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location</li><li>Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call <del>************ ** ***</del> service desk if support does not transfer.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians can text 'Start' to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.\n\nStatement of Work (Security/Interactive)\n\nSystem & Model #:\n\nCamera system / Hikvision\n\nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem :\n\nDVR IS OFFLINE\n\nTECHNICIAN MUST BRING: Digital Multimeter, BNC Spot Monitor, BNC crimping tool, Crimp on BNC (Not twist) Laptop with ethernet.\n\nThe technician needs to inspect the DVR for power, connection, and functionality issues.\n\nIt's wiring, the PDU and all PVMs.\n\nIf hardware or cabling appears defective, replace or repair it accordingly.\n\nThe technician should test the camera on-site, coordinating with Help Desk to verify the camera feed is working properly from the control center.\n\nParts Needed:\n\nNone\n\nSpecific Scheduling Request :\n\nNone\n\nOther Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request: None\n\nCause : Not fully determined\n\n- Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.\n- Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.\n- All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location\n- Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* service desk if support does not transfer.\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR 