{"job":{"id":20025405,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Simbe","title":"Unbox and Set Up Shelf Inventory Robot and Box Up Current Robot","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">Work MUST be performed by the technician assigned. If Simbe discovers that another provider other than the assigned provider on Field Nation is performing the work, work order will not be approved for payment. Service companies are required to have a profile for each individual technician on Field Nation.</strong></p><p>The technician for this job will be unboxing and setting up a shelf inventory robot, Tally, as well as packing a robot currently at the store into the new robot's box. The technician will meet with the manager, remove the new robot and dock from its box, replace the old robot's dock on the wall with the new dock in the same dock location, and box up the old robot and dock into the new robot's box. The technician will then place the new robot onto the dock and boot it up, and confirm with a Simbe engineer that the new robot is online and working properly.</p><p>For technicians who have done this job before, please note the old robot must be powered off, but the battery disconnection step is no longer required per Hazmat regulations.</p><p><strong>Technician is REQUIRED to provide a cell phone hotspot.</strong>&nbsp;This may be needed to remotely configure Tally's wifi credentials to connect to the store's wifi.</p><p>Docks are mounted to store walls either using metal brackets that are screwed into the walls using a manual screwdriver or electric screwdriver, or if screws can't be used on certain walls such as concrete walls, the docks are mounted with double sticky mounting tape. The technician must provide the tape. Details are below.</p><p><strong>Anchoring VHB Tape</strong></p><p>3M brand “Scotch MOUNT EXTREME” double sided mounting may be needed to adhere dock to wall. This can be purchased at Home Depot and most other hardware stores. If the exact 3M brand shown is not available, any other mounting tape that is rated for “15LB” holding force or more is fine to use.</p>","markdown":"**Work MUST be performed by the technician assigned. If Simbe discovers that another provider other than the assigned provider on Field Nation is performing the work, work order will not be approved for payment. Service companies are required to have a profile for each individual technician on Field Nation.**\n\nThe technician for this job will be unboxing and setting up a shelf inventory robot, Tally, as well as packing a robot currently at the store into the new robot's box. The technician will meet with the manager, remove the new robot and dock from its box, replace the old robot's dock on the wall with the new dock in the same dock location, and box up the old robot and dock into the new robot's box. The technician will then place the new robot onto the dock and boot it up, and confirm with a Simbe engineer that the new robot is online and working properly.\n\nFor technicians who have done this job before, please note the old robot must be powered off, but the battery disconnection step is no longer required per Hazmat regulations.\n\n**Technician is REQUIRED to provide a cell phone hotspot.** This may be needed to remotely configure Tally's wifi credentials to connect to the store's wifi.\n\nDocks are mounted to store walls either using metal brackets that are screwed into the walls using a manual screwdriver or electric screwdriver, or if screws can't be used on certain walls such as concrete walls, the docks are mounted with double sticky mounting tape. The technician must provide the tape. Details are below.\n\n**Anchoring VHB Tape**\n\n3M brand “Scotch MOUNT EXTREME” double sided mounting may be needed to adhere dock to wall. This can be purchased at Home Depot and most other hardware stores. If the exact 3M brand shown is not available, any other mounting tape that is rated for “15LB” holding force or more is fine to use.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00","end":"2026-09-25T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-25T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":18},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790277039471}
