{"job":{"id":20025571,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walmart EOTF Remodel - Permanent  Visit Photo Center Equipment Install Service - 6 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p>You are being contracted to perform the move and install of a Photo Program at a Walmart location. This process will include confirming with support all existing photo equipment on site to be moved, moving hardware to install location, and installation of equipment including connecting everything to the network and testing operation of the equipment.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>Installation 9/30<br /><br />Overview:Move Perm: Walmart Tier Single ;  ; SiteInfo: tech to arrive in am, move equipment to perm location, cont:  Quentin Dales-479-321-9106<br /><br />FIN: <br /><br />Inventory:<br />1. KVM 4 PORT SWITCH KIT <br />2. Isobar Six Outlet Power Strip <br />3. Cat 5 Network Cable, 10 foot <br />4. PS2 to USB Connector Kit <br />5. 16 Port Gigabit Network Switch <br />6. DYMO 450 TURBO PRINTER <br />7. WM DX100 LAD TYPE CABINET MOD KIT <br />8. VNX MOUNT BRACKET (LAD)<br /><br />Equipment:<br />1. CX3240<br />2. EPSON_FF-680W<br />3. (PIC)<br />4. (RipPC) <br />5. VNXT-1.0  QTY 2<br />6. DX400<br />7. SureColor_P7370<br />8. DL650W<br /><br />Upload 5 Photo Deliverables in Install Manager<br /><br />Lab Layout- PC-163NG_L_SS<br /><br /><br /></p><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li><li>Onsite Contact</li></ol><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in on your Walmart Scintilla In-Store app. If you do not have a badge, go to the customer service desk, and notify them you're a vendor representing Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center. Notify them you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need a badge printed, show them your Scintilla In-Store ID badge in the App and when they provide you with a printed copy apply it to your shirt on the upper left side.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the support team at&nbsp;EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616&nbsp;to confirm the following Inventory items are onsite</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All In One PIC Stand (AIO Stand)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Isobar Six Outlet Power Strip</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">WM ENVELOPE HOLDERS</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">M30 TRIMMER COUNTER MOUNT</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ISOBAR 8 STRIP OUTLET</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CAT 5E Network Cable,10 footi, Belkin</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PAN OSTEN DX100 RETRO KIT ( SINGLE)</li></ul><p>3. Confirm with the (MOD) or Photo Center operator you're there to move the photo machines to the permanent location then proceed with moving equipment.</p><p>4. Once equipment is moved to install location, contact support team to bring lab back online.</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Once online, perform test prints including a nozzle test print and production print to verify all printer functionality.</li><li>If parts or supplies are needed contact the support team at EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616&nbsp;to place an order and provide any images of damaged parts.</li><li>Complete the work order, checkout with the (MOD) and get their signature.</li><li>As you leave the Walmart location check out of the Walmart Scintilla In-Store app.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the lab prior to service start.</li><li>Once the lab is moved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test from all printers must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the lab in temporary location.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call&nbsp;EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616 and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $250.00 per service visit for 5 hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li><li><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></li></ul>","markdown":"You are being contracted to perform the move and install of a Photo Program at a Walmart location. This process will include confirming with support all existing photo equipment on site to be moved, moving hardware to install location, and installation of equipment including connecting everything to the network and testing operation of the equipment.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nInstallation 9/30  \n  \nOverview:Move Perm: Walmart Tier Single ; ; SiteInfo: tech to arrive in am, move equipment to perm location, cont: Quentin Dales-479-321-9106  \n  \nFIN:   \n  \nInventory:  \n1\\. KVM 4 PORT SWITCH KIT   \n2\\. Isobar Six Outlet Power Strip   \n3\\. Cat 5 Network Cable, 10 foot   \n4\\. PS2 to USB Connector Kit   \n5\\. 16 Port Gigabit Network Switch   \n6\\. DYMO 450 TURBO PRINTER   \n7\\. WM DX100 LAD TYPE CABINET MOD KIT   \n8\\. VNX MOUNT BRACKET (LAD)  \n  \nEquipment:  \n1\\. CX3240  \n2\\. EPSON\\_FF-680W  \n3\\. (PIC)  \n4\\. (RipPC)   \n5\\. VNXT-1.0 QTY 2  \n6\\. DX400  \n7\\. SureColor\\_P7370  \n8\\. DL650W  \n  \nUpload 5 Photo Deliverables in Install Manager  \n  \nLab Layout- PC-163NG\\_L\\_SS\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n3. Onsite Contact\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in on your Walmart Scintilla In-Store app. If you do not have a badge, go to the customer service desk, and notify them you're a vendor representing Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center. Notify them you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need a badge printed, show them your Scintilla In-Store ID badge in the App and when they provide you with a printed copy apply it to your shirt on the upper left side.\n2. Contact the support team at EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616 to confirm the following Inventory items are onsite\n\n- All In One PIC Stand (AIO Stand)\n- Isobar Six Outlet Power Strip\n- WM ENVELOPE HOLDERS\n- M30 TRIMMER COUNTER MOUNT\n- ISOBAR 8 STRIP OUTLET\n- CAT 5E Network Cable,10 footi, Belkin\n- PAN OSTEN DX100 RETRO KIT ( SINGLE)\n\n3\\. Confirm with the (MOD) or Photo Center operator you're there to move the photo machines to the permanent location then proceed with moving equipment.\n\n4\\. Once equipment is moved to install location, contact support team to bring lab back online.\n\n- Once online, perform test prints including a nozzle test print and production print to verify all printer functionality.\n- If parts or supplies are needed contact the support team at EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616 to place an order and provide any images of damaged parts.\n- Complete the work order, checkout with the (MOD) and get their signature.\n- As you leave the Walmart location check out of the Walmart Scintilla In-Store app.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the lab prior to service start.\n- Once the lab is moved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test from all printers must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the lab in temporary location.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call EOTF Hotline: (888) 336-9616 and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $250.00 per service visit for 5 hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n- *Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T09:00","end":"2026-09-30T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-30T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":300},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":5,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":60},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":360,"estHours":5,"travelExpense":90,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":5,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}}},"reason":"PAYMENT_INSUFFICIENT","rejectDetails":"Rate $50/hr is below base rate $60/hr"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790277933490}
{"job":{"id":"7936423906","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"LEGACY Retail Services","title":"Troubleshoot A/V System and Possible Rerun WHITE Cat 6 w/ Device Install at Retail Store","description":"<p>On arrival you must check in with your brandpoint support rep at 856-382-2645 via text. This number will not receive phone calls.</p><p><br></p><p>Ref:MSG1737232_0jRFXbZblJPjNYZIkryR</p><p><br></p><p>Service request: First Available ETA at 4:30 AM</p><p>Warehouse #: 1587 (Raleigh, NC)</p><p>Number of technicians required: (1)</p><p>Time allocated for SOW: 5.5 hours (Contact PRN support for additional time if required)</p><p><br></p><p>Description: The warehouse would like a technician to Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops, Restore media player connectivity, Connect parts &amp; Restore all TVs with Costco feed, Perform Cable cleanup/management, Verify PRN system wiring, Check HDMI cables from Amp to TVs, Configure TVs to HOME mode, Re-label all cables</p><p>Confirm media player connectivity</p><p><br></p><p>Point of Contact: Jordan</p><p><br></p><p>PRN Doc110uments (Download or view directly from the link)</p><p>• <a href=\"https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork</a></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tools:</p><p>A Cable Label maker is required, and clear scotch tape</p><p>White Cat cable required (300'-400' white CAT6 cable)</p><p>The technician must bring white CAT6 cable, tester/toner, and labels to label cables. cable management supplies</p><p><br></p><p>Check-in: (Before starting any work in the warehouse)</p><p>1. Contact Brandpoint tier 1: 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY or email <a href=\"mailto:checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com</a> and copy costcosupport@stratacache to check-in</p><p>2. PRN/Stratacache tier 1: call support 888-776-5589 (on overnights and weekends also email <a href=\"mailto:costcosupport@stratacache.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">costcosupport@stratacache.com</a>) -- if no answer: BKUP line 415-617-9752</p><p>3. Upon arrival in TV department, locate the site contact listed below</p><p>4. Check in with the point of contact below, review the SOW</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Initial Checks before starting work: (Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo, top right corner of the TVs)</p><p>Enter the building through the back door</p><p>Speak with the point of contact listed above for the TV department</p><p>1. Review the scope of work with the POC</p><p>2. Request the TV remotes' location or the box of remotes to turn on all the TVs</p><p>3. With the TVs turned ON, perform a count of what's playing Costco feed out of the total number of TVs in the department (x out of y)</p><p>4. Take before pictures and email them to the service vendor list above</p><p>4a. Capture pictures of any broken TVs and inform the managers before starting any work</p><p>5. Confirm with the service vendor that the BrightSign player is online</p><p>5a. Proceed to perform the SOW below</p><p><br></p><p>SOW:</p><p>Locate the Super Plate (BrightSign 4K player)</p><p>Start from the Super Plate (4K Player and a batch of Cat6 cables coming down)</p><p>Costco content is the blue/white concierge logo in the top right corner of the TV</p><p>Verify with the vendor that the media player is online</p><p><br></p><p>First priority - Repair/Replace Cat6 drops and connect parts &amp; restore the Costco feed on all TVs</p><p>Second priority - Restore media player connectivity, Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</p><p>Third priority - Survey the TV department if additional parts are requested, Perform cable clean up &amp; management (zip tie HDMI &amp; Cat6 cables)</p><p><br></p><p>- Turn ON all TVs</p><p>- Upon arrival, perform a count of the TVs playing Costco content and the total number of TVs in the department</p><p><br></p><p>Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</p><p><br></p><p>Restore media player connectivity (the PRN Homerun)</p><p>- Troubleshoot the Homerun media player (verify it is fully seated and Cat6 cable is labeled PRN-HR that is connected)</p><p>-- If the Cat6 cable has a link light, contact PRN support 888-776-5589 to verify connectivity</p><p>- Troubleshoot the Homerun Cat6 cable</p><p>- Repair the homerun Cat6 cable if damaged</p><p>-- If the Homerun is damaged near the TV department install an RJ45 biscuit/surface jack in rafters (label jack as PRN HR)</p><p>-- Run a patch cable from the biscuit/surface jack to the media player - label the patch cable \"PRN HR\"</p><p>- Label the Homerun as \"PRN Homerun\" in three places on the Cat6 cable</p><p><br></p><p>Restore Costco content playback on TVs</p><p>- Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops - Manager to identify</p><p>-- For each location verify/take picture of playing Costco feed</p><p>-- Label each drop on both ends (take picture of the label)</p><p>- Connect parts &amp; restore Costco feed on all TVs (except waterfalls and endcaps) - yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</p><p>- Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</p><p>- Connect HDMI cables from the Amp to TVs for Costco content playback</p><p>- Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to OUTPUT 1 port</p><p>- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</p><p><br></p><p>- Verify all Amp dip switches are set correctly</p><p>- Check cables (damaged HDMI &amp; Cat6 drop), repair any damaged Cat6 drop and replace HDMI cables</p><p><br></p><p>Cable management and clean up</p><p>- Perform cable clean-up (remove old unused Cat6 drops)</p><p>- Perform cable management of Cat6 and HDMI cables (secure HDMI and Cat6 cables with zip ties)</p><p>- Re-label all Cat6 drops</p><p><br></p><p>- Configure all TVs to HOME mode</p><p>- Label each Cat6 per instructions in the label guide doc</p><p>- Verify Media player connectivity with support</p><p><br></p><p>- Take lots of before and after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco content</p><p><br></p><p>Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to the HDMI OUTPUT 1 port</p><p>- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</p><p><br></p><p>Re-label all Cat6 cables being used to pass the Costco signal</p><p>- All labels should be legible and clear to read on both ends</p><p>- Label the CAT6 cable the same on both ends (6\" from the connector with a Sharpie and 12\" out with a label maker, wrap with clear scotch tape)</p><p>- CAT6 cable naming scheme: (G1 being gondola/pod)</p><p>- Cat6 Cable drop labeling scheme: G1-4K, G2-4K, G3-4K, and ON</p><p><br></p><p>Cat6 DON'Ts</p><p>- DO NOT USE jumpers on Cat6 cable runs that are passing Costco feed HDMI video signal</p><p><br></p><p>Verify the Extender has a solid BLUE LED = Good operation</p><p>Blue/Green flashing = bad CAT6 or HDMI cable (cannot communicate with transmitter correctly)</p><p>Startech/GEFEN extenders are POE, only the Sender/Transmitter requires power</p><p><br></p><p>Check-out process:</p><p>1. Verify the media player is still ONLINE after the work with the service vendor</p><p>2. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed</p><p>3. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends</p><p>4. TV playing Costco feed playback</p><p><br></p><p>5. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work</p><p>6. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor</p><p>7. Complete the latest manager &amp; technician checklist &amp; upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support</p><p>- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)</p><p><br></p><p>On completion of work, to receive the release code:</p><p>- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache</p><p>- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.</p><p>- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work</p><p>- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist</p><p>Email: <a href=\"mailto:checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com</a> and/or <a href=\"mailto:costcosupport@stratacache.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">costcosupport@stratacache.com</a></p><p>If needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support</p><p><br></p><p>The above check-in and check-out deliverables are required and must be received for the checkout code</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T04:30","end":"2026-09-29T06:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":350},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790278716371}
{"job":{"id":19946749,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Device offline**See required tools**","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;<del>********* *****</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required On-site time/window: 9/14/2026 asap</u></strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Equipment:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Make/Model: LEVEL2TECH</p>\n<p><strong><u>Problem Description:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Service Desk 800-243-5782 / Site Contact Daniel</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Shop Device Offline - Shop AP: Device is showing offline since 9/10/2026, please dispatch a tech to tone/trace to restore a connection as soon as possible Network Switch and Port, if known : Shop Response Time Requested (Hr) : Immediate (SLA 4 Hours) Tech type : Level 2 Network tech</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Technician needs to be prepared to tone, trace, repair, or replace while onsite.</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians are required to use the provided box(es) and all packing materials for shipping equipment. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Failure to package the equipment securely and provide requested photos will result in penalties if the equipment is inbounded and determined to be damaged.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Important Scope/Customer Information:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Any changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial <strong>via phone.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Parts and Support are provided by<del>****** ******* * ** ******* **** ******* ****** *</del></strong> <del>********************</del></p>\n<p>If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this - Contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise</p>\n<p><strong>If additional parts are needed there will be another trip&nbsp;REQUIRED, You MUST contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required online deliverable.</p>\n<p>If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Important Tech Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of<del>****** ******* ** ******* ****</del></li>\n<li>Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival</li>\n<li>Tech MUST package returned equipment security for shipment and upload photos.</li>\n<li>Tech MUST complete online deliverable prior to leaving site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>150 FT Cat 5/6 Cable</li>\n<li>Standard/Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li>\n<li>Laptop, with access to a cellular hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Straps or Velcro</li>\n<li>Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)</li>\n<li>Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment</li>\n<li>Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)</li>\n<li>Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Online Deliverable Requirements | Deliverable Link:&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.jotform.com/250866044689166</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or&nbsp;If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact <del>** ******* **** * **************</del> to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off</li>\n<li>Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device</li>\n<li>Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Upon Arrival at site:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of <del>****** ******* ****</del> to the onsite MOD</li>\n<li>If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot/repair or replace failed component to return failed system to working order</li>\n<li>Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by<del>**</del> Help Desk.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm functionality with XXXXX &amp; provide their name upon closure</li>\n<li>Complete online Deliverable</li>\n<li>Technician to use the box that component arrived in to return failed component utilizing provided return label.&nbsp;All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing.&nbsp;Technician will leave the box at site with the Store Manager or POC for Customer to arrange pickup.</li>\n<li>Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time & only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.**\n\n**YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.**\n\n \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Required On-site time/window: 9/14/2026 asap**\n\n**Equipment:**\n\nMake/Model: LEVEL2TECH\n\n**Problem Description:**\n\n**Service Desk 800-243-5782 / Site Contact Daniel**\n\n**Shop Device Offline - Shop AP: Device is showing offline since 9/10/2026, please dispatch a tech to tone/trace to restore a connection as soon as possible Network Switch and Port, if known : Shop Response Time Requested (Hr) : Immediate (SLA 4 Hours) Tech type : Level 2 Network tech**\n\n**Technician needs to be prepared to tone, trace, repair, or replace while onsite.**\n\nTechnicians are required to use the provided box(es) and all packing materials for shipping equipment. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Failure to package the equipment securely and provide requested photos will result in penalties if the equipment is inbounded and determined to be damaged.\n\n**Important Scope/Customer Information:**\n\nAny changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial **via phone.**\n\n**Parts and Support are provided by\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIf you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this - Contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise\n\n**If additional parts are needed there will be another trip REQUIRED, You MUST contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.**\n\nAll times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required online deliverable.\n\nIf additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies & Procedures #6.\n\n**Important Tech Requirements:**\n\n- Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival\n- Tech MUST package returned equipment security for shipment and upload photos.\n- Tech MUST complete online deliverable prior to leaving site\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- 150 FT Cat 5/6 Cable\n- Standard/Basic hand tools\n- Screwdrivers\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Laptop, with access to a cellular hotspot\n- Cable Straps or Velcro\n- Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)\n- Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment\n- Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)\n- Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)\n\n**Online Deliverable Requirements | Deliverable Link:** <https://essintial.jotform.com/250866044689166>\n\n- Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off\n- Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables\n\n**Upon Arrival at site:**\n\n- Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* to the onsite MOD\n- If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.\n- Troubleshoot/repair or replace failed component to return failed system to working order\n- Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by\\*\\* Help Desk.\n\n**Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:**\n\n- Confirm functionality with XXXXX & provide their name upon closure\n- Complete online Deliverable\n- Technician to use the box that component arrived in to return failed component utilizing provided return label. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Technician will leave the box at site with the Store Manager or POC for Customer to arrange pickup.\n- Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T15:00","end":"2026-09-14T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":148,"max":443},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":147.6,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":30},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/14/2026, 3:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Rest"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2