{"job":{"id":20026278,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LI Group","title":"Retail Store – Device Reset (1 Installer)","description":{"html":"<p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and selink@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">At retail stores nationwide, you will replace one tablet with corresponding security and install new software onto the tablet on the existing Samsung fixture, then refresh digital monitor content, and complete any required VMD updates. Any issues should be troubleshot on-site and escalated to the LIGP contact if needed. Upon completion, teams are responsible for disposing of all trash, cleaning the work area, capturing final photos, obtaining signoff, and submitting deliverables via the site-specific Egnyte link for approval prior to checkout.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><u>BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.</span></p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, and explain your scope of work. Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">provided via emailed excel spreadsheet</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">) via text message and take BEFORE photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\". </span></p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove (1) existing tablet, replace with new tablet on the existing security, and install software onto new tablet. Troubleshoot with your LI Group site contact if needed. </p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Return the removed device to the manager on duty. </p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Update the Digital POP content, and update or remove any other VMD as applicable.</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, watch bands are clasped, fact tag holders are straight, and dispose of any trash. </p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take all required AFTER photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".</p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.</p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Submit all photos to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site. <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $75 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount: </em><a href=\"https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><em>https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App</em></a></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*</em> <em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.</em></p>","markdown":"*\\*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and selink@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.*\n\nAt retail stores nationwide, you will replace one tablet with corresponding security and install new software onto the tablet on the existing Samsung fixture, then refresh digital monitor content, and complete any required VMD updates. Any issues should be troubleshot on-site and escalated to the LIGP contact if needed. Upon completion, teams are responsible for disposing of all trash, cleaning the work area, capturing final photos, obtaining signoff, and submitting deliverables via the site-specific Egnyte link for approval prior to checkout.\n\n**BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):**\n\n1\\. Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.\n\n2\\. Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, and explain your scope of work. Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (**provided via emailed excel spreadsheet**) via text message and take BEFORE photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".\n\n3\\. Remove (1) existing tablet, replace with new tablet on the existing security, and install software onto new tablet. Troubleshoot with your LI Group site contact if needed.\n\n4\\. Return the removed device to the manager on duty.\n\n5\\. Update the Digital POP content, and update or remove any other VMD as applicable.\n\n6\\. Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, watch bands are clasped, fact tag holders are straight, and dispose of any trash.\n\n7\\. Take all required AFTER photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".\n\n8\\. Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.\n\n9\\. Submit all photos to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site.\n\n*\\*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $75 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount:* https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\n\n*\\*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.*\n\n*\\*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.*\n\n*\\** *Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.*\n\n*\\*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.*\n\n*\\*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.*\n\n*\\*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.*\n\n*\\*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.*\n\n*\\*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T10:00","end":"2026-10-13T11:30","latestStart":"2026-10-13T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":44},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790279266739}
{"job":{"id":20025662,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | JPMC MaCD | Install replacement VDI power adapater","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.</strong></li><li><strong>By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page: </strong><u>https://fieldnation.com/work/insight</u></li><li><strong>Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details are available through the recruitment link.</strong></li></ul><p>Insight has been engaged by <del>**** </del>to assist with their Ad Hoc needs. Please make sure to read all standard instructions before accepting OR requesting this workorder.</p><p>Please see tracking before going to site or call <del>******* *************</del> Tracking is added to the ticket the morning of the job if applicable. Look in the shipments section.</p><p>**<strong>CHECK YOUR EMAIL THE MORNING OF REGARDING YOUR ASSIGNED WO **</strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p>!!! BEFORE you mark yourself ONSITE It is essential that you \t<br/>call the Insight team - 1-800-215-8968 \t<br/>Do not leave the site UNTIL you call the Insight team. \t<br/>\t<br/>Chase reference ticket:\t255891083<br/>Chase Contact#: 877-309-8068 Opt 2\t<br/>\t<br/>Unit:\t<br/>SCOPE:\t<br/>Install replacement VDI power adapater\t<br/>\t<br/>\t<br/>Branch contact:\tPriscilla Saul W532356<br/>Date requested:\t9/25/2026<br/></p><p><strong><em><u>Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.</u></em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>UNLESS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.</li><li>&nbsp;Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.</li><li>&nbsp;If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.</li><li>&nbsp;Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.</li><li>Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE: Even if tracking shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><del>*</del><strong><u><del>*** ****</del> Work Order &amp; Support Procedures</u></strong></p><p>A Smartphone is required for all technicians. Unless directed by the <del>***** </del>help-desk at no time should a technician be taking pictures, video, or any recording while inside a <del>***** </del>branch. No laptops or tablets should ever be brought into a banking location. Nothing about the work performed, activities inside the branch, or reference to <del>***** </del>should ever be posted on any social media site.Business casual dress required, no tennis shoes or jeans. You will be turned away if you show up with unprofessional attire.</p><p>No smoking on location.</p><p>Please follow the below procedures, includes information on who to call to initiate support and what information must be documented in the ticket. All required information must be documented for a completed ticket.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>For escalation.</strong></p><p><strong><del>********** **** **** ****** ******* ******* **** ** ******** ** ******* **************</del></strong></p><p><del>* **** *** ******* ******** **** **</del><strong><del>******</del></strong><del>**************</del><strong><del>******</del></strong><del>** *** **** *** **** *** ******* ***** ** **** ************ ***** ** *** ******** *** ***** **** **** *** ******** ******* ** ** ** **** ****** ** **** ******* **** *** *** ******* ****** ** *** ************ ************</del></p><p><strong><u><del>**** *** ******* ***** **** ** ******* **** ****** ******* ******</del></u></strong></p><p><del>* ***** *** ******* ***** **** *** **** *** ****** ** ** ****** ***** **</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Before you leave the site:</u></strong></p><p><del>* ***** **** ********* ******* ** ********** *******</del></p><p><del>* ****** ******** ** *** ***** *********** *** ****** *** ******** ** *** ***********</del></p><p><del>* ****** **** *** **** ** ********* ** *** ********** ************ *** ******* * ********* **** *** **** ******** *** ******** ** ******* *********</del></p><p><strong><em><u>IMPORTANT:</u></em></strong><em>&nbsp;All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation.&nbsp;Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.</em></p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING</u></strong></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional ti