{"job":{"id":20025746,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LI Group","title":"Retail Store – Device Reset (1 Installer)","description":{"html":"<p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and selink@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">At retail stores nationwide, you will replace one tablet with corresponding security and install new software onto the tablet on the existing Samsung fixture, then refresh digital monitor content, and complete any required VMD updates. Any issues should be troubleshot on-site and escalated to the LIGP contact if needed. Upon completion, teams are responsible for disposing of all trash, cleaning the work area, capturing final photos, obtaining signoff, and submitting deliverables via the site-specific Egnyte link for approval prior to checkout.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><u>BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.</span></p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, and explain your scope of work. Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">provided via emailed excel spreadsheet</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">) via text message and take BEFORE photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\". </span></p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove (1) existing tablet, replace with new tablet on the existing security, and install software onto new tablet. Troubleshoot with your LI Group site contact if needed. </p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Return the removed device to the manager on duty. </p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Update the Digital POP content, and update or remove any other VMD as applicable.</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, watch bands are clasped, fact tag holders are straight, and dispose of any trash. </p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take all required AFTER photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".</p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.</p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Submit all photos to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site. <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $75 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount: </em><a href=\"https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><em>https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App</em></a></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*</em> <em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.</em></p>","markdown":"*\\*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and selink@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.*\n\nAt retail stores nationwide, you will replace one tablet with corresponding security and install new software onto the tablet on the existing Samsung fixture, then refresh digital monitor content, and complete any required VMD updates. Any issues should be troubleshot on-site and escalated to the LIGP contact if needed. Upon completion, teams are responsible for disposing of all trash, cleaning the work area, capturing final photos, obtaining signoff, and submitting deliverables via the site-specific Egnyte link for approval prior to checkout.\n\n**BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):**\n\n1\\. Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.\n\n2\\. Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, and explain your scope of work. Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (**provided via emailed excel spreadsheet**) via text message and take BEFORE photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".\n\n3\\. Remove (1) existing tablet, replace with new tablet on the existing security, and install software onto new tablet. Troubleshoot with your LI Group site contact if needed.\n\n4\\. Return the removed device to the manager on duty.\n\n5\\. Update the Digital POP content, and update or remove any other VMD as applicable.\n\n6\\. Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, watch bands are clasped, fact tag holders are straight, and dispose of any trash.\n\n7\\. Take all required AFTER photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\".\n\n8\\. Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.\n\n9\\. Submit all photos to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site.\n\n*\\*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $75 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount:* https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\n\n*\\*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.*\n\n*\\*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.*\n\n*\\** *Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.*\n\n*\\*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.*\n\n*\\*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.*\n\n*\\*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.*\n\n*\\*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.*\n\n*\\*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T10:00","end":"2026-10-09T11:30","latestStart":"2026-10-09T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":52},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MA