{"job":{"id":20027877,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ProAct Services","title":"Safelite| MG Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***CAREFULLY REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED DOCUMENTS BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>GENERAL GUIDELINES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Technicians are not permitted to start work on-site or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager</u>.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The technician accepting the work order should be the technician to check in and out during the agreed-upon visit date.&nbsp;<u>Any</u></strong><u>&nbsp;</u><strong><u>individuals who do not have permission or authorization to be at the location are prohibited from entering or remaining on-site.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Technicians must wear closed-toe shoes. The use of onsite ladders or step stools is not permitted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Upon arrival, the technician must verify that the part numbers, colors, and quantities of the materials received match the list provided by the PCs or attached to the work order. The technician should immediately report any discrepancies with the parts received.&nbsp;<u>No cabling work should begin until a complete inventory check has been performed.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>All new and or reran cabling must go through the patch panel and be patched into the switch.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ensure that all tasks are completed to a satisfactory level, meeting the specified requirements and quality standards.</strong> <strong><u>Everything must be verified with the NOC before job release and approved by ProAct Team.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ensure all fields in your sign-off sheet are completed thoroughly and accurately. Provide detailed notes on any issues or delays encountered during the process. <u>The work order will not be approved if the required information and deliverables are incomplete.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>Technicians are NOT to leave the site until PROACT SERVICES releases them; otherwise, the work order will be penalized.&nbsp;</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>No out-of-the-scope work within your work order will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the ProAct Services Project Manager.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>The technicians will dispose of any trash generated during the installation and perform a general cleaning of areas that may have been affected by the work. This assumes the use of client dumpster(s).</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong>: Complete the requested Safelite service call as per the description below:</p>\n<p>This request is for a technician to swap the MG21 with an M52. A lift is available for your use.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Technician-required parts/materials/tools</u></strong><u>:</u></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard technician toolkit to include an 8ft ladder and laptop</li>\n<li>Please bring equipment for full cable run, if needed.</li>\n<li>Please bring Velcro for cleaning up the cabling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. The cost of materials will be reimbursed only if a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Upon arrival, call and check in with the ProAct Services and NOC contacts listed in this work order.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><del>****** ******** **** ***** ********</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><del>*** ** *************</del>&nbsp;<strong>Reference site number:</strong>4765</li>\n<li><strong>Work with the site contact to locate and inventory the Safelite equipment and cabling materials. Notify the ProAct team of any discrepancies.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>New Equipment: MG52</strong></li>\n<li>Upload all required pre-installation photos</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photo of the network rack BEFORE work</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photoo of the MG outside the building BEFORE work</li>\n<li>Swap the MG21 with the MG52 sent to the site.</li>\n<li>Work with the site contact/manager to check that the internet, all voice, and wifi services are working properly. Ask if they have any other IT-related or hardware-related issues they would like us to communicate back to the Safelite IT team and its managers.&nbsp;<strong>Document this on the sign-off sheet.</strong></li>\n<li>Clean up the site after completion</li>\n<li><strong>Box up and return ship all removed and/or unused network equipment</strong>. Return shipping label is inside the MG52 box.</li>\n<li>Work with the NOC to ensure all network equipment is online and functioning.</li>\n<li>Upload all deliverables and documents required, and call ProAct Services to check out.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Do not leave the site until ProAct Services has released you from the work.</u></strong></li>\n<li>Drop off the equipment at the nearest FedEx, take a photo of the receipt, and upload it to Field Nation or send it to the ProAct Services line.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Upload these photos to Field Nation and let the ProAct Services contact know&nbsp;BEFORE&nbsp;leaving the site</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Sign-off sheet with your check-in and out time, and the POC's name and signature. You can find this document in the work order.</li>\n<li>Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the network rack and the MG21 before the MG swap.</li>\n<li>Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the network rack and the MG52 after the MG swap.</li>\n<li>Drop off receipt of the MG.</li>\n<li>Cable test results for any new cable runs or data drops that require troubleshooting</li>\n<li>Any issue that may arise or that needs to be escalated</li>\n</ol>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*CAREFULLY REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED DOCUMENTS BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER\\*\\*\\***\n\n**GENERAL GUIDELINES:**\n\n- **Technicians are not permitted to start work on-site or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager.**\n- **The technician accepting the work order should be the technician to check in and out during the agreed-upon visit date. Any** **individuals who do not have permission or authorization to be at the location are prohibited from entering or remaining on-site.**\n- **Technicians must wear closed-toe shoes. The use of onsite ladders or step stools is not permitted.**\n- **Upon arrival, the technician must verify that the part numbers, colors, and quantities of the materials received match the list provided by the PCs or attached to the work order. The technician should immediately report any discrepancies with the parts received. No cabling work should begin until a complete inventory check has been performed.**\n- **All new and or reran cabling must go through the patch panel and be patched into the switch.**\n- **Ensure that all tasks are completed to a satisfactory level, meeting the specified requirements and quality standards.** **Everything must be verified with the NOC before job release and approved by ProAct Team.**\n- **Ensure all fields in your sign-off sheet are completed thoroughly and accurately. Provide detailed notes on any issues or delays encountered during the process. The work order will not be approved if the required information and deliverables are incomplete.**\n- **Technicians are NOT to leave the site until PROACT SERVICES releases them; otherwise, the work order will be penalized.**\n- **No out-of-the-scope work within your work order will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the ProAct Services Project Manager.**\n- **The technicians will dispose of any trash generated during the installation and perform a general cleaning of areas that may have been affected by the work. This assumes the use of client dumpster(s).**\n\n**Scope of Work**: Complete the requested Safelite service call as per the description below:\n\nThis request is for a technician to swap the MG21 with an M52. A lift is available for your use.\n\n**Technician-required parts/materials/tools**:\n\n- Standard technician toolkit to include an 8ft ladder and laptop\n- Please bring equipment for full cable run, if needed.\n- Please bring Velcro for cleaning up the cabling.\n\n**Note**:\n\n- The tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. The cost of materials will be reimbursed only if a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided.\n\n**TASKS:**\n\n1. Upon arrival, call and check in with the ProAct Services and NOC contacts listed in this work order.\n2. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **Reference site number:**4765\n4. **Work with the site contact to locate and inventory the Safelite equipment and cabling materials. Notify the ProAct team of any discrepancies.**\n5. **New Equipment: MG52**\n6. Upload all required pre-installation photos\n7. Photo of the network rack BEFORE work\n8. Photoo of the MG outside the building BEFORE work\n9. Swap the MG21 with the MG52 sent to the site.\n10. Work with the site contact/manager to check that the internet, all voice, and wifi services are working properly. Ask if they have any other IT-related or hardware-related issues they would like us to communicate back to the Safelite IT team and its managers. **Document this on the sign-off sheet.**\n11. Clean up the site after completion\n12. **Box up and return ship all removed and/or unused network equipment**. Return shipping label is inside the MG52 box.\n13. Work with the NOC to ensure all network equipment is online and functioning.\n14. Upload all deliverables and documents required, and call ProAct Services to check out.\n15. **Do not leave the site until ProAct Services has released you from the work.**\n16. Drop off the equipment at the nearest FedEx, take a photo of the receipt, and upload it to Field Nation or send it to the ProAct Services line.\n\n**Upload these photos to Field Nation and let the ProAct Services contact know BEFORE leaving the site**:\n\n1. Sign-off sheet with your check-in and out time, and the POC's name and signature. You can find this document in the work order.\n2. Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the network rack and the MG21 before the MG swap.\n3. Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the network rack and the MG52 after the MG swap.\n4. Drop off receipt of the MG.\n5. Cable test results for any new cable runs or data drops that require troubleshooting\n6. Any issue that may arise or that needs to be escalated","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":40},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":17