{"job":{"id":19864769,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"POS Register Refresh, NIC Card & Handheld Scanners - Tech 2 Day 1","description":{"html":"<p>Scopes to be done :</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>POS Register Refresh</p>\n<p>UPS NIC Card Refresh</p>\n<p>POS Handheld Scanners</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PRE-SITE REQUIREMENT – NIC CARD SCREWS</u></strong>:</p>\n<p>Prior to traveling to the site, technicians are required to have M3-.50 x 6mm screws available for NIC card installation. These screws may not be available onsite and are necessary to properly secure the NIC card.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Please purchase and bring at least one (1) packet of M3-.50 x 6mm screws. They are typically sold in packs of four for approximately $1.50–$1.60 and can be found at most hardware stores, including Home Depot, Lowe’s, and Ace Hardware.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Do not arrive onsite without the required screws. Please obtain them prior to traveling to the site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope 1:</strong><strong>2026 POS Refresh</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace NCR 7607 registers with Elo hardware.</p>\n<p>Shift : Overnight (Dayside for Optical/Pharmacy)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old hardware, install Elo CPUs, cash drawers, printers, guest displays, space poles, and touch screen monitors, connect peripherals. Contact DS for OS build.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Palletize old CPUs and apply the Bill of Lading (BOL) and shipping labels.</strong><strong>Pallet must NOT go into CRC area.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Palletize old peripherals (cash drawers, printers, screen monitors, etc.) and placed in the CRC area.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Photo Checklist:</strong> Front, side and rear photos for all registers with a visible placard. Upload the photo</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Antennas installed and pointing UP</li>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Photo from the side angle that clearly shows the Y-cable installed correctly</li>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Display mounted firmly on top of the pole. Swivels left / right and tilts up / down without disconnecting from mount</li>\n<li>Need to see retainer clips, cable going into side hole, &amp; locking collar</li>\n<li>Cable comes out of the bottom hole on the side of the monitor pole facing the receipt printer</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope 2:</strong><strong>2026 UPS NIC Card Refresh</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace RDU101 NIC with RDU120 NIC on specified UPS units.</p>\n<p>Shift : Before store opens / Overnight</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Unbox NIC, provide MAC address to DS, swap NIC card, and reconnect Ethernet.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Place old NIC on CRC pallet</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Photo of installed NIC with green link light and cables secured. Upload the photo</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope 3:</strong><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n<ul>\n<li>Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li>NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li>ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</strong></li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;<em>﻿</em></p>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet&nbsp;<strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in&nbsp;<strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong>&nbsp;and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><strong>866-835-7877</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Option 1 → Technical Support (Enterprise Retail)</li>\n<li>Option 5 → Target Support</li>\n<li>Option 3 → Target Bundle Projects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a&nbsp;CompuCom&nbsp;representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Scopes to be done :\n\nPOS Register Refresh\n\nUPS NIC Card Refresh\n\nPOS Handheld Scanners\n\n**PRE-SITE REQUIREMENT – NIC CARD SCREWS**:\n\nPrior to traveling to the site, technicians are required to have M3-.50 x 6mm screws available for NIC card installation. These screws may not be available onsite and are necessary to properly secure the NIC card.\n\nPlease purchase and bring at least one (1) packet of M3-.50 x 6mm screws. They are typically sold in packs of four for approximately $1.50–$1.60 and can be found at most hardware stores, including Home Depot, Lowe’s, and Ace Hardware.\n\nDo not arrive onsite without the required screws. Please obtain them prior to traveling to the site.\n\n**Scope 1:****2026 POS Refresh**\n\n**Overview:** Replace NCR 7607 registers with Elo hardware.\n\nShift : Overnight (Dayside for Optical/Pharmacy)\n\n- **Preparation:** Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old hardware, install Elo CPUs, cash drawers, printers, guest displays, space poles, and touch screen monitors, connect peripherals. Contact DS for OS build.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Palletize old CPUs and apply the Bill of Lading (BOL) and shipping labels.****Pallet must NOT go into CRC area.**\n  - **Palletize old peripherals (cash drawers, printers, screen monitors, etc.) and placed in the CRC area.**\n\n**Photo Checklist:** Front, side and rear photos for all registers with a visible placard. Upload the photo\n\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Antennas installed and pointing UP\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Photo from the side angle that clearly shows the Y-cable installed correctly\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Display mounted firmly on top of the pole. Swivels left / right and tilts up / down without disconnecting from mount\n- Need to see retainer clips, cable going into side hole, & locking collar\n- Cable comes out of the bottom hole on the side of the monitor pole facing the receipt printer\n\n**Scope 2:****2026 UPS NIC Card Refresh**\n\n**Overview:** Replace RDU101 NIC with RDU120 NIC on specified UPS units.\n\nShift : Before store opens / Overnight\n\n- **Installation Tasks:** Unbox NIC, provide MAC address to DS, swap NIC card, and reconnect Ethernet.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Place old NIC on CRC pallet**\n- Photo of installed NIC with green link light and cables secured. Upload the photo\n\n**Scope 3:****2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable). \n  - Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n  - NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n  - ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n  - **Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet**\n  - No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.\n\n *﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n**866-835-7877**\n\n- Option 1 → Technical Support (Enterprise Retail)\n- Option 5 → Target Support\n- Option 3 → Target Bundle Projects\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a CompuCom representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-27T21:30","end":"2026-09-27T32:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":368},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":10.5,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Sun, Sep 27, 9:30 PM\nChecked: Mon, Sep 28, Tue, Sep 29, Wed, Sep 30, Thu, Oct 1 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790284471393}
{"job":{"id":19864413,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"POS Register Refresh, NIC Card & Handheld Scanners - Tech 1 Day 1","description":{"html":"<p>Scopes to be done :</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>POS Register Refresh</p>\n<p>UPS NIC Card Refresh</p>\n<p>POS Handheld Scanners</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PRE-SITE REQUIREMENT – NIC CARD SCREWS</u></strong>:</p>\n<p>Prior to traveling to the site, technicians are required to have M3-.50 x 6mm screws available for NIC card installation. These screws may not be available onsite and are necessary to properly secure the NIC card.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Please purchase and bring at least one (1) packet of M3-.50 x 6mm screws. They are typically sold in packs of four for approximately $1.50–$1.60 and can be found at most hardware stores, including Home Depot, Lowe’s, and Ace Hardware.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Do not arrive onsite without the required screws. Please obtain them prior to traveling to the site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope 1:</strong><strong>2026 POS Refresh</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace NCR 7607 registers with Elo hardware.</p>\n<p>Shift : Overnight (Dayside for Optical/Pharmacy)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old hardware, install Elo CPUs, cash drawers, printers, guest displays, space poles, and touch screen monitors, connect peripherals. Contact DS for OS build.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Palletize old CPUs and apply the Bill of Lading (BOL) and shipping labels.</strong><strong>Pallet must NOT go into CRC area.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Palletize old peripherals (cash drawers, printers, screen monitors, etc.) and placed in the CRC area.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Photo Checklist:</strong> Front, side and rear photos for all registers with a visible placard. Upload the photo</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Antennas installed and pointing UP</li>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Photo from the side angle that clearly shows the Y-cable installed correctly</li>\n<li>A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)</li>\n<li>Display mounted firmly on top of the pole. Swivels left / right and tilts up / down without disconnecting from mount</li>\n<li>Need to see retainer clips, cable going into side hole, &amp; locking collar</li>\n<li>Cable comes out of the bottom hole on the side of the monitor pole facing the receipt printer</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope 2:</strong><strong>2026 UPS NIC Card Refresh</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace RDU101 NIC with RDU120 NIC on specified UPS units.</p>\n<p>Shift : Before store opens / Overnight</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Unbox NIC, provide MAC address to DS, swap NIC card, and reconnect Ethernet.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Place old NIC on CRC pallet</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Photo of installed NIC with green link light and cables secured. Upload the photo</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope 3:</strong><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n<ul>\n<li>Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li>NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li>ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</strong></li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;<em>﻿</em></p>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet&nbsp;<strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in&nbsp;<strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong>&nbsp;and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><strong>866-835-7877</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Option 1 → Technical Support (Enterprise Retail)</li>\n<li>Option 5 → Target Support</li>\n<li>Option 3 → Target Bundle Projects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a&nbsp;CompuCom&nbsp;representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Scopes to be done :\n\nPOS Register Refresh\n\nUPS NIC Card Refresh\n\nPOS Handheld Scanners\n\n**PRE-SITE REQUIREMENT – NIC CARD SCREWS**:\n\nPrior to traveling to the site, technicians are required to have M3-.50 x 6mm screws available for NIC card installation. These screws may not be available onsite and are necessary to properly secure the NIC card.\n\nPlease purchase and bring at least one (1) packet of M3-.50 x 6mm screws. They are typically sold in packs of four for approximately $1.50–$1.60 and can be found at most hardware stores, including Home Depot, Lowe’s, and Ace Hardware.\n\nDo not arrive onsite without the required screws. Please obtain them prior to traveling to the site.\n\n**Scope 1:****2026 POS Refresh**\n\n**Overview:** Replace NCR 7607 registers with Elo hardware.\n\nShift : Overnight (Dayside for Optical/Pharmacy)\n\n- **Preparation:** Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old hardware, install Elo CPUs, cash drawers, printers, guest displays, space poles, and touch screen monitors, connect peripherals. Contact DS for OS build.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Palletize old CPUs and apply the Bill of Lading (BOL) and shipping labels.****Pallet must NOT go into CRC area.**\n  - **Palletize old peripherals (cash drawers, printers, screen monitors, etc.) and placed in the CRC area.**\n\n**Photo Checklist:** Front, side and rear photos for all registers with a visible placard. Upload the photo\n\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Antennas installed and pointing UP\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Photo from the side angle that clearly shows the Y-cable installed correctly\n- A visible and clearly legible placard (e.g. TxxxxREGxxxx)\n- Display mounted firmly on top of the pole. Swivels left / right and tilts up / down without disconnecting from mount\n- Need to see retainer clips, cable going into side hole, & locking collar\n- Cable comes out of the bottom hole on the side of the monitor pole facing the receipt printer\n\n**Scope 2:****2026 UPS NIC Card Refresh**\n\n**Overview:** Replace RDU101 NIC with RDU120 NIC on specified UPS units.\n\nShift : Before store opens / Overnight\n\n- **Installation Tasks:** Unbox NIC, provide MAC address to DS, swap NIC card, and reconnect Ethernet.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Place old NIC on CRC pallet**\n- Photo of installed NIC with green link light and cables secured. Upload the photo\n\n**Scope 3:****2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable). \n  - Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n  - NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n  - ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n  - **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n  - **Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet**\n  - No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.\n\n *﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n**866-835-7877**\n\n- Option 1 → Technical Support (Enterprise Retail)\n- Option 5 → Target Support\n- Option 3 → Target Bundle Projects\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a CompuCom representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-27T21:30","end":"2026-09-27T32:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":368},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":10.5,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Sun, Sep 27, 9:30 PM\nChecked: Mon, Sep 28, Tue, Sep 29, Wed, Sep 30, Thu, Oct 1 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790284493348}
