{"job":{"id":20031727,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"TROUBLESHOOT DATA REMOTE /MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/ MULTIMETER-DIS152262","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 8775206829 Ticket 11889424<br/><br/>MetTel — Support & Repair dispatch request: Location is reporting issues will the alarm line connectivity.  <br/><br/>We will need to troubleshoot with the GNOC to isolate the cause of the issue<br/>We will need to test the lines from the back of the PIAB and the handoff to the alarm panel with a butt set.<br/><br/>null<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 8775206829 Ticket 11889424  \n  \nMetTel — Support & Repair dispatch request: Location is reporting issues will the alarm line connectivity.   \n  \nWe will need to troubleshoot with the GNOC to isolate the cause of the issue  \nWe will need to test the lines from the back of the PIAB and the handoff to the alarm panel with a butt set.  \n  \nnull  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00","end":"2026-09-28T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":38},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790339017689}
{"job":{"id":20031914,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home - Pair Misc. Devices","description":{"html":"<p><strong>YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.</strong></p>Smart Home - Pair Misc. Devices<p>Connect the control hub if provided, allow 10 minutes to boot, and have Smart Home Support pair the existing lock/keypad, up to two thermostats, and one to four sensors as applicable. Install supplied sensors where required. Identify each device and whether it was installed or only paired.</p><p><strong>Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.</strong></p>1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM<p><strong>For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.</strong></p><p>Call immediately if:</p><ul><li>You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.</li><li>The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.</li><li>Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.</li><li>You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.</li></ul><p><strong>If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.</strong></p><p>For access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.</p><p>An FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.</p>2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS<p>Install and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.</p><p>For supplied sensors being installed, mount in the specified locations and remove battery pull tabs as directed for activation. Confirm each sensor with support.</p>3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT<p><strong>Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern</strong></p><p>Call with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.</p>4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORT<p>Upload:</p><ul><li>Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.</li><li>Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.</li><li>Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.</li></ul><p><strong>Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:</strong></p><p><strong>Device/location | Work performed | Final result</strong></p><p>Example: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.</p><p>Distinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.</p><p><strong>“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.</strong></p>5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMS<p>Only the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.</p><p>Completion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.</p><p>For resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.</p>","markdown":"**YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.**\n\nSmart Home - Pair Misc. DevicesConnect the control hub if provided, allow 10 minutes to boot, and have Smart Home Support pair the existing lock/keypad, up to two thermostats, and one to four sensors as applicable. Install supplied sensors where required. Identify each device and whether it was installed or only paired.\n\n**Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.**\n\n1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM**For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.**\n\nCall immediately if:\n\n- You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.\n- The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.\n- Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.\n- You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.\n\n**If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.**\n\nFor access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.\n\nAn FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.\n\n2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTSInstall and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.\n\nFor supplied sensors being installed, mount in the specified locations and remove battery pull tabs as directed for activation. Confirm each sensor with support.\n\n3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT**Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern**\n\nCall with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.\n\n4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORTUpload:\n\n- Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.\n- Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.\n- Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.\n\n**Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:**\n\n**Device/location | Work performed | Final result**\n\nExample: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.\n\nDistinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.\n\n**“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.**\n\n5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMSOnly the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.\n\nCompletion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.\n\nFor resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T09:00","end":"2026-10-05T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790341398473}
{"job":{"id":20029305,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Applied Network Services","title":"MUST KNOW POTS KNOW HOW TO CROSS CONNECT AND HAVE BUTT SETT - Activation/Install -11727512","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><strong>Firm start time, please do not be late. Job should take roughly 2-3hrs</strong></p><p><strong>-------PLEASE READ SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE REQUESTING OR ACCEPTING---</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Firm start time, please do not be late.</strong></p><p><strong>***Upon arrival - tech to call remote support<del> </del></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><del>****** ********* * ************</del></strong></p><p><strong>If you have trouble reaching assigned remote support, please call&nbsp;844-905-9779 for assistance</strong></p><p>Provide ANS # or TKT #...Do not mention&nbsp;<strong>FIELD NATION</strong>&nbsp;or provide Field Nation ID.</p><p><strong>Do not Mention Field Nation!</strong></p><p><strong>***Tech must have valid Identification</strong></p><p><strong>***Tech must have Laptop with Ethernet adapter-Should have Team viewer loaded</strong></p><p><strong>***Tech must have Butt Sett with Toner and wand FOR ANY POTS RELATED SERVICES</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;***Tech SHOULD have at least 100 Cat5e Cable in case a cable run is needed - all Materials used must be documented and will be reimbursed at industry rate or at cost with receipt.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***IMPORTANT - IF A CABLE RUN IS REQUIRED BUT YOU ARE UNABLE TO COMPLETE DUE TO DIFFICULTY OR TOTAL TIME IT WOULD TAKE, PLEASE PERFORM SURVEY, DO NOT SHARE PRICING WITH CUSTOMER. PROVIDE QUOTE ON THE PLATE FORM AS TIME AND MATERIALS.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>*****IMPORTANT - UPON COMPLETION - MUST SEND PHOTO OF&nbsp;<u>SIGNED&nbsp;</u>WORK ORDER TO REMOTE SUPPORT AS WELL AS UPLOAD TO FIELD NATION*****</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>The business you are visiting is</strong>&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><del>********* ***********</del></strong><strong><del>*************</del>You have been hired by Applied Network Services who has been contracted for this job by&nbsp;</strong><del>******</del></p><p><strong>If you have&nbsp;<u>ANY</u>&nbsp;questions on this work order, need to make changes, extend time, etc&nbsp;<u>DO NOT ASK THE ONSITE CUSTOMER and DO NOT ASK&nbsp;</u></strong><del>******</del><strong>&nbsp;Please send us a note ON THE PLATFORM or TEXT Charles 914-355-9520 IF RESPONSE TIME IS SLOW</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>On Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Upon entry, introduce yourself to the on-site manager as&nbsp;</strong><u>Applied Network Services</u>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<del>************</del>and he/she&nbsp;will escort you to the work area.Please call upon arrival and work with contact on all connections.&nbsp;Local contact is&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><del>****** *********</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p>SEE INSTALLATION VIDEO FOR GUIDANCE</p><p><br></p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zrqC_uOY1t8 -&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p><strong>***PLEASE NOTE - IF A CABLE RUN IS REQUIRED FOR ANY WORK ON SITE, DO NOT SHARE PRICING WITH CUSTOMER. SURVEY THE WORK, PROVIDE QUOTE ON THE PLATE FORM AS TIME AND MATERIALS.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Single Dispatch - Porting TNs (Rack and Stack &amp; Cross Connect/Port/Go Live) EQUIPMENT RACK AND STACK + GO LIVE TECH TO BE PROVIDED BOXED METTEL EQUIPMENT RACK AND STACK AT THE DMARC ANTENNAS TO BE MOUNTED AND INSTALLED TEST OVER LTE AND VERIFY DIAL TONE ON THE METTEL EQUIPMENT WAN CONNECTION MAY BE REQUIRED TECH TO SURVEY AND IDENTIFY THE FOLLOWING LINES PIAB CONFIGURATION DETAILS: Specialty Line(s): 9193301103-voice 9193301203-alarm 9193301215-alarm CROSS CONNECTS TO BE COMPLETED FOR PORTING LINES PRE-PORT TESTING TO BE COMPLETED (VERIFY DIAL TONE, INBOUND AND OUTBOUND TEST CALLS/FAX) METTEL TO ACTIVATE THE PORT FINAL TESTING TO BE COMPLETED TECH WILL NEED: BUTT-SET, BRIDGE CLIPS, TONER, MULTI-METER AND LABEL MAKER LCON: Amanda Bell (919) 322-1550 </span>abell@sandpiper.us.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> Project Contact Person: CHRISTINE ROSA Project Contact Email: </span>crosa@bbhnow.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> Project Contact Phone: 234-438-1253 Project Contact Cell: 234-650-0966 PLEASE ASSIGN A TECH FAMILIAR WITH PIAB AND POTS CROSS CONNECTS Notes: PIAB Depot project install, please have tech survey the existing PIAB device SN 701587 on site to locate porting TNs, confirm lines on site and use case, install new MetTel DataRemote device and trigger port and cross-connect. Tech to provide LCON with old device so it can be returned to MetTel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Please call Bryant Espindola 212-359-5129 when you arrive on site. If not reachable, please call remote support toll free # 844-905-9779 for assistance. Provide bruin ticket site number 11727512 to MetTel Rep.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port ,Multimeter wire tester ,Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches ,Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer) ,Biscuit jacks ,Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters ,4-6 ft’ ladder ,Butt Set ,RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors ,100’ extension cord ,Digital Camera ,100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device ,Cell phone w/Hotspot device ,Punch down tool</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attach pics in Field Nation and send to contact if requested.</strong></p><p>*Copy of work order ---&gt;Must get signature from customer - If customer is NOT on site or able to sign, must clearly write that on work order</p><p>*Photos of work performed in field:</p><p>*If equipment installed - take photo of that with close ups and full room picture.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>*Any photos asked of by remote support</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Additional Technician Equipment/Materials:</u></strong></p><p>Cat 5E cable and cable ends (75ft-100ft)</p><p>cable crimper</p><p>Corded/cordless Drill</p><p>Misc mounting hardware</p><p>4-6ft ladder</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ATTENTION:</u></strong></p><p><em>Please check in and out onsite using GPS on the Field Nation app. This is how time onsite is confirmed and it non-negotiable.&nbsp;Failure to do so will result in a penalty.</em></p><p><em>Please also complete your work order for payment same day by midnight. Delays may result in a denial of add-on costs (i.e materials, extra travel, extra time, etc.) and/or a penalty.</em></p><p><em>Please PRINT ANS SIGNOFF SHEET and have the onsite contact sign.</em></p><p><em>Please be prepared with technician equipment listed.</em></p>","markdown":"**Firm start time, please do not be late. Job should take roughly 2-3hrs**\n\n**-------PLEASE READ SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE REQUESTING OR ACCEPTING---**\n\n**Firm start time, please do not be late.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Upon arrival - tech to call remote support** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If you have trouble reaching assigned remote support, please call 844-905-9779 for assistance**\n\nProvide ANS # or TKT #...Do not mention **FIELD NATION** or provide Field Nation ID.\n\n**Do not Mention Field Nation!**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Tech must have valid Identification**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Tech must have Laptop with Ethernet adapter-Should have Team viewer loaded**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Tech must have Butt Sett with Toner and wand FOR ANY POTS RELATED SERVICES**\n\n **\\*\\*\\*Tech SHOULD have at least 100 Cat5e Cable in case a cable run is needed - all Materials used must be documented and will be reimbursed at industry rate or at cost with receipt.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT - IF A CABLE RUN IS REQUIRED BUT YOU ARE UNABLE TO COMPLETE DUE TO DIFFICULTY OR TOTAL TIME IT WOULD TAKE, PLEASE PERFORM SURVEY, DO NOT SHARE PRICING WITH CUSTOMER. PROVIDE QUOTE ON THE PLATE FORM AS TIME AND MATERIALS.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT - UPON COMPLETION - MUST SEND PHOTO OF SIGNED WORK ORDER TO REMOTE SUPPORT AS WELL AS UPLOAD TO FIELD NATION\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**The business you are visiting is** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*****\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*You have been hired by Applied Network Services who has been contracted for this job by** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**If you have ANY questions on this work order, need to make changes, extend time, etc DO NOT ASK THE ONSITE CUSTOMER and DO NOT ASK** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **Please send us a note ON THE PLATFORM or TEXT Charles 914-355-9520 IF RESPONSE TIME IS SLOW**\n\n**On Site Instructions:**\n\n**Upon entry, introduce yourself to the on-site manager as** Applied Network Services for \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*and he/she will escort you to the work area.Please call upon arrival and work with contact on all connections. Local contact is **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nSEE INSTALLATION VIDEO FOR GUIDANCE\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zrqC_uOY1t8 -\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*PLEASE NOTE - IF A CABLE RUN IS REQUIRED FOR ANY WORK ON SITE, DO NOT SHARE PRICING WITH CUSTOMER. SURVEY THE WORK, PROVIDE QUOTE ON THE PLATE FORM AS TIME AND MATERIALS.**\n\nSingle Dispatch - Porting TNs (Rack and Stack & Cross Connect/Port/Go Live) EQUIPMENT RACK AND STACK + GO LIVE TECH TO BE PROVIDED BOXED METTEL EQUIPMENT RACK AND STACK AT THE DMARC ANTENNAS TO BE MOUNTED AND INSTALLED TEST OVER LTE AND VERIFY DIAL TONE ON THE METTEL EQUIPMENT WAN CONNECTION MAY BE REQUIRED TECH TO SURVEY AND IDENTIFY THE FOLLOWING LINES PIAB CONFIGURATION DETAILS: Specialty Line(s): 9193301103-voice 9193301203-alarm 9193301215-alarm CROSS CONNECTS TO BE COMPLETED FOR PORTING LINES PRE-PORT TESTING TO BE COMPLETED (VERIFY DIAL TONE, INBOUND AND OUTBOUND TEST CALLS/FAX) METTEL TO ACTIVATE THE PORT FINAL TESTING TO BE COMPLETED TECH WILL NEED: BUTT-SET, BRIDGE CLIPS, TONER, MULTI-METER AND LABEL MAKER LCON: Amanda Bell (919) 322-1550 abell@sandpiper.us.com Project Contact Person: CHRISTINE ROSA Project Contact Email: crosa@bbhnow.com Project Contact Phone: 234-438-1253 Project Contact Cell: 234-650-0966 PLEASE ASSIGN A TECH FAMILIAR WITH PIAB AND POTS CROSS CONNECTS Notes: PIAB Depot project install, please have tech survey the existing PIAB device SN 701587 on site to locate porting TNs, confirm lines on site and use case, install new MetTel DataRemote device and trigger port and cross-connect. Tech to provide LCON with old device so it can be returned to MetTel.\n\nPlease call Bryant Espindola 212-359-5129 when you arrive on site. If not reachable, please call remote support toll free # 844-905-9779 for assistance. Provide bruin ticket site number 11727512 to MetTel Rep.\n\nFully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port ,Multimeter wire tester ,Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches ,Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer) ,Biscuit jacks ,Crimpers & Wirecutters ,4-6 ft’ ladder ,Butt Set ,RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors ,100’ extension cord ,Digital Camera ,100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device ,Cell phone w/Hotspot device ,Punch down tool\n\n**Attach pics in Field Nation and send to contact if requested.**\n\n\\*Copy of work order --->Must get signature from customer - If customer is NOT on site or able to sign, must clearly write that on work order\n\n\\*Photos of work performed in field:\n\n\\*If equipment installed - take photo of that with close ups and full room picture.\n\n\\*Any photos asked of by remote support\n\n**Additional Technician Equipment/Materials:**\n\nCat 5E cable and cable ends (75ft-100ft)\n\ncable crimper\n\nCorded/cordless Drill\n\nMisc mounting hardware\n\n4-6ft ladder\n\n**ATTENTION:**\n\n*Please check in and out onsite using GPS on the Field Nation app. This is how time onsite is confirmed and it non-negotiable. Failure to do so will result in a penalty.*\n\n*Please also complete your work order for payment same day by midnight. Delays may result in a denial of add-on costs (i.e materials, extra travel, extra time, etc.) and/or a penalty.*\n\n*Please PRINT ANS SIGNOFF SHEET and have the onsite contact sign.*\n\n*Please be prepared with technician equipment listed.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T10:00","end":"2026-10-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790341766010}
{"job":{"id":20032006,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"R3 Services","title":"Toast POS Printer and POS Line Test/Repair/Install","description":{"html":"<p>Arrive on site and identify yourself to the manager on duty as a field tech from R3 Services here to check the cellular backup internet device in the office, then call us to check in at 203-714-8021.</p><p><strong>C</strong>heck the Ethernet cable going to this device and physically inspect the line for possible issues. May need to reterminate the ends if there is an issue.</p><p>They need to be installed with immaculate cable management; absolutely nothing should be hanging out or visible/in the way. Attention to detail is a must for this job.&nbsp;Please provide the pictures before leaving the premises and confirm with the remote technician that they have been received.</p><p>Please bring:</p><ul><li>Laptop with an Ethernet adapter</li><li>Network cable tester</li><li>Tone generator and probe</li><li>RJ45 crimper and termination tools</li><li>RJ45 connectors</li><li>Spare Cat5e or Cat6 patch cables</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Labeling materials</li></ul>","markdown":"Arrive on site and identify yourself to the manager on duty as a field tech from R3 Services here to check the cellular backup internet device in the office, then call us to check in at 203-714-8021.\n\n**C**heck the Ethernet cable going to this device and physically inspect the line for possible issues. May need to reterminate the ends if there is an issue.\n\nThey need to be installed with immaculate cable management; absolutely nothing should be hanging out or visible/in the way. Attention to detail is a must for this job. Please provide the pictures before leaving the premises and confirm with the remote technician that they have been received.\n\nPlease bring:\n\n- Laptop with an Ethernet adapter\n- Network cable tester\n- Tone generator and probe\n- RJ45 crimper and termination tools\n- RJ45 connectors\n- Spare Cat5e or Cat6 patch cables\n- Basic hand tools\n- Screwdrivers\n- Labeling materials","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-26T09:30","end":"2026-09-26T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":75},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790342585501}
{"job":{"id":20032066,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"Tesla Charger Wi‑Fi Configuration & Connectivity Validation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code: Business Casual</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>Smartphone or tablet with <strong>Tesla One</strong> app installed</p><p>Laptop with Wi‑Fi capability (recommended)</p><p>Mobile phone for coordination with EPLUS and Tesla Commercial Support</p><p>Basic hand tools (if access panels are required)</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Camera-enabled device for documentation and photos</p><p>PPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)</p><p><br></p>Scope<ul><li>Provide onsite support to configure <strong>(2) Tesla EV chargers</strong> for Wi‑Fi connectivity.</li><li>Utilize the <strong>Tesla One</strong> mobile application to connect to and configure each charger.</li><li>Coordinate with EPLUS and/or Tesla Commercial Support during the service visit as needed.</li><li>Access each charger's configuration interface through the Tesla One app.</li></ul>Wi‑Fi Configuration<p>Configure both chargers with the following wireless network settings:</p><ul><li><strong>SSID:</strong> MAR_WP</li><li><strong>Security:</strong> WPA2</li><li><strong>Password:</strong> i5P#neHD4RdX</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> Network is <strong>hidden</strong></li></ul>Tesla Access Requirements<ul><li>Technician may need to:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Scan the QR code located on the back of each Tesla charger.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact Tesla Commercial Support to obtain the charger access password if required.</li><li>Work directly with Tesla Support for any configuration or connectivity issues encountered during setup.</li></ul>Testing &amp; Validation<ul><li>Verify both chargers successfully connect to the specified Wi‑Fi network.</li><li>Confirm chargers establish communication with the Tesla network/backend services.</li><li>Verify chargers report online status after configuration.</li><li>Perform basic troubleshooting within scope if connectivity issues are encountered.</li><li>Document any errors, signal issues, or configuration challenges.</li></ul>Documentation<ul><li>Record connectivity status for both chargers.</li><li>Document any support interactions with Tesla.</li><li>Take photos of charger status screens/indicators if requested.</li><li>Update the Field Nation work order with detailed completion notes and testing results.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival&nbsp;</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check in with SG net.</li><li>&nbsp;Call EV support</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Before and After pictures</li><li>Notes</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet</li><li><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Contact SGNet</strong></p>","markdown":"**Dress Code: Business Casual**\n\n·\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nSmartphone or tablet with **Tesla One** app installed\n\nLaptop with Wi‑Fi capability (recommended)\n\nMobile phone for coordination with EPLUS and Tesla Commercial Support\n\nBasic hand tools (if access panels are required)\n\nFlashlight\n\nCamera-enabled device for documentation and photos\n\nPPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)\n\nScope- Provide onsite support to configure **(2) Tesla EV chargers** for Wi‑Fi connectivity.\n- Utilize the **Tesla One** mobile application to connect to and configure each charger.\n- Coordinate with EPLUS and/or Tesla Commercial Support during the service visit as needed.\n- Access each charger's configuration interface through the Tesla One app.\n\nWi‑Fi ConfigurationConfigure both chargers with the following wireless network settings:\n\n- **SSID:** MAR\\_WP\n- **Security:** WPA2\n- **Password:** i5P#neHD4RdX\n- **Note:** Network is **hidden**\n\nTesla Access Requirements- Technician may need to:\n- Scan the QR code located on the back of each Tesla charger.\n- Contact Tesla Commercial Support to obtain the charger access password if required.\n- Work directly with Tesla Support for any configuration or connectivity issues encountered during setup.\n\nTesting & Validation- Verify both chargers successfully connect to the specified Wi‑Fi network.\n- Confirm chargers establish communication with the Tesla network/backend services.\n- Verify chargers report online status after configuration.\n- Perform basic troubleshooting within scope if connectivity issues are encountered.\n- Document any errors, signal issues, or configuration challenges.\n\nDocumentation- Record connectivity status for both chargers.\n- Document any support interactions with Tesla.\n- Take photos of charger status screens/indicators if requested.\n- Update the Field Nation work order with detailed completion notes and testing results.\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with SG net.\n2. Call EV support\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Before and After pictures\n2. Notes\n3. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet\n- **Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n**Contact SGNet**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T10:00","end":"2026-09-28T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790342791102}
{"job":{"id":20032152,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tip N Ring Inc.","title":"MON 9/28 @ 10AM - ATM Meet - 4G Router is down - verify power, reseat WIC / SIM, reboot","description":{"html":"<p>SOW:</p><p>**ATM MEET&nbsp;MONDAY 9/28 AT 10AM ET.**</p><p><strong>CALL</strong><del> *** * ************* ****** *</del> TO CHECK IN UPON ARRIVAL ON SITE.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;TECH IS TO CALL <del>*** </del>AGAIN WITHIN 15 MINUTES OF SCHEDULED MEET TIME IF UNABLE TO LOCATE THE OTHER TECHNICIAN.</strong></p><p><strong>WORK NEEDED</strong>: 4G ROUTER IN ATM IS DOWN.&nbsp;IDENTIFY POWER SOURCE AND VERIFY POWER CABLE IS FULLY SEATED IN ROUTER. POWER&nbsp;DOWN ROUTER. RESEAT EHWIC AND SIM CARDS IN ROUTER. WILL NEED TO PULL OUT EHWIC&nbsp;CARD FULLY – SIM CARD LOCATED ON THE BOTTOM OF THE CARD. **TAKE PHOTOS OF FRONT AND BACK OF SIM CARD** BRING ROUTER BACK UP.&nbsp;WORK WITH TNR NETWORK SUPPORT ON ADJUSTING WIRELESS ANTENNA FOR OPTIMAL SIGNAL.</p><p>*NOTE – 4G ROUTERS CAN TAKE 10-15 MINUTES TO FULLY BOOT UP. WAIT THAT AMOUNT OF TIME AND SEE IF THE ATM TECH CAN BRING THE ATM BACK IN SERVICE. IF NOT, HAVE THEM REBOOT ATM AND TRY AGAIN.</p><p><del>*** **************</del></p><p><del>***** ****** ***********************</del></p><p><strong>REQUIRED&nbsp;PICTURES</strong>:&nbsp;ROUTER, ATM, SIM CARD (FRONT AND BACK), 4G ANTENNAS (BEFORE AND AFTER)</p><p><strong><em>**********************************************************************</em></strong></p><p><strong>PLEASE NOTE:&nbsp;<u>ALL REQUIRED PHOTOS MUST BE UPLOADED AND APPROVED BY TIP-N-RING&nbsp;BEFORE&nbsp;LEAVING SITE.</u>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;IF YOU FAIL TO UPLOAD THE PHOTOS AND/OR FAIL TO CALL US TO CONFIRM THAT THEY WERE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU LEAVE THE SITE, YOU WILL&nbsp;<strong><u>NOT BE PAID</u></strong>&nbsp;FOR ANY TIME ONSITE.&nbsp;WE ALLOW FOR UP TO 15 MINUTES TO CLEAN THE AREA, TAKE PHOTOS, AND UPLOAD THEM TO US.&nbsp;IF YOU NEED ADDITIONAL TIME PAST THE 15 MINUTES ALLOWED, YOU MUST NOTIFY US BEFORE THAT TIME HAS ELAPSED, OR ANYTIME PAST THE 15 MINUTES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.</p><p><strong>**YOU ARE&nbsp;<u>NOT&nbsp;</u>ALLOWED TO COMMUNICATE DIRECTLY WITH OUR CLIENTS OR PROVIDE THEM WITH YOUR CONTACT INFORMATION. ALL COMMUNICATION NEEDS TO BE THROUGH TIP N RING - NO EXCEPTIONS!!**</strong></p><p><strong><em>***********************************************************************</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>YOUR ACCEPTANCE OF THIS WORK ORDER SERVES AS YOUR SPECIFIC AGREEMENT MADE TO ABIDE BY ALL MANDATES OF THE FIELD NATION QUALITY ASSURANCE POLICY. IF FOR ANY REASON, THE PROVIDER WHO REPORTS TO SITE IS DIFFERENT THAN THE ONE ASSIGNED, THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELLED. SHOULD THIS OCCUR, NO CANCELLATION FEE&nbsp;OR PRE-AGREED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL BE PAID, AND THE VIOLATION OF THE PROVIDER QUALITY ASSURANCE POLICY WILL BE REPORTED TO FIELD NATION. IF YOU ARE A SERVICE COMPANY AND WISH TO SEND A DIFFERENT PROVIDER THAN THE ONE ASSIGNED, YOU MUST REQUEST A SWAP, AND THAT SWAP MUST BE ACCEPTED PRIOR THE SERVICE WINDOW.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>CALL&nbsp;<del>*** * ************</del>, OPTION 1 UPON ARRIVAL ON SITE. TECH MUST LIST ON WORK ORDER MATERIALS USED WHILE ON SITE.</p><p>WO AUTHORIZED FOR 1 HR MAX, IF MORE TIME IS NEEDED PLEASE CALL<strong>&nbsp;</strong><del>**** **** ** ******************</del>TO ADVISE AND FOR APPROVAL OF ADDITIONAL TIME.</p><p>TECH MUST HAVE:</p><ul><li>LAPTOP</li><li>CABLE TONER</li><li>CAT 5 CABLE TESTER,CERTIFIER OR WIRE MAP TESTER</li><li>CAT5E OR 6 CABLING</li><li>CAT5E JACKS AND WALL PLATES</li><li>110 PUNCH TOOL</li><li>STANDARD TECH TOOLS</li><li>ASSORTED PATCH CORDS</li></ul><p><br></p><p>TECH MUST BE ABLE TO PROVIDE STANDARD CAT 5E CABLING MATERIALS. It is the technician's responsibility to add all materials on the paperwork and list them as expenses on the website. If listed on the paperwork and website, technician will be reimbursed for them in line with industry standards; receipts may be requested. It is not the buyer's responsibility to reimburse for materials not listed on the website.</p><p><br></p><p>Before any tech is dispatched to site, tech should read over the service order and review the work being requested and&nbsp;<strong>arrive onsite with all appropriate tools</strong>, fully prepared to perform the work being&nbsp;requested</p><p>Required tools:</p><ul><li>a butt set available for each call</li><li>basic telephony/data tools</li><li>necessary tools for the work requested: CAT 5E cable,&nbsp;jacks, etc. (will be reimbursed per itemization, pre-approval&nbsp;of materials expense required)&nbsp;</li><li>Standard ladder</li></ul><p>A copy of the service request order (paperwork) must be:</p><ul><li>taken to site by your technician(s)</li><li>filled out completely, including but not limited to the&nbsp;tech’s check in and out times and any materials supplied</li><li>signed by the site contact</li><li>uploaded into the Work Order before checking out</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Provider will need to upload, or email to buyer, pictures of their work while still on site.&nbsp;Once a tech is released from site, we will allow 15 minutes for clean-up and the uploading of paperwork and photos. Any time beyond this will not be approved for payment without prior authorization from support.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Pictures will need to be reviewed and verified by WO Manager/ RMAT&nbsp;<strong>before&nbsp;</strong>checking out. The following pictures are required:</p><ul><li>The termination that has an issue</li><li>Any cabling that you troubleshot/touched</li><li>Any cabling that was reterminated</li></ul><p>Once provider marks work order as 'Work Done', buyer will then process order for payment and approval could take a maximum of 14 days.</p>","markdown":"SOW:\n\n\\*\\*ATM MEET MONDAY 9/28 AT 10AM ET.\\*\\*\n\n**CALL** \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* TO CHECK IN UPON ARRIVAL ON SITE.\n\n **TECH IS TO CALL \\*\\*\\* AGAIN WITHIN 15 MINUTES OF SCHEDULED MEET TIME IF UNABLE TO LOCATE THE OTHER TECHNICIAN.**\n\n**WORK NEEDED**: 4G ROUTER IN ATM IS DOWN. IDENTIFY POWER SOURCE AND VERIFY POWER CABLE IS FULLY SEATED IN ROUTER. POWER DOWN ROUTER. RESEAT EHWIC AND SIM CARDS IN ROUTER. WILL NEED TO PULL OUT EHWIC CARD FULLY – SIM CARD LOCATED ON THE BOTTOM OF THE CARD. \\*\\*TAKE PHOTOS OF FRONT AND BACK OF SIM CARD\\*\\* BRING ROUTER BACK UP. WORK WITH TNR NETWORK SUPPORT ON ADJUSTING WIRELESS ANTENNA FOR OPTIMAL SIGNAL.\n\n\\*NOTE – 4G ROUTERS CAN TAKE 10-15 MINUTES TO FULLY BOOT UP. WAIT THAT AMOUNT OF TIME AND SEE IF THE ATM TECH CAN BRING THE ATM BACK IN SERVICE. IF NOT, HAVE THEM REBOOT ATM AND TRY AGAIN.\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED PICTURES**: ROUTER, ATM, SIM CARD (FRONT AND BACK), 4G ANTENNAS (BEFORE AND AFTER)\n\n***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\****\n\n**PLEASE NOTE: ALL REQUIRED PHOTOS MUST BE UPLOADED AND APPROVED BY TIP-N-RING BEFORE LEAVING SITE.**  IF YOU FAIL TO UPLOAD THE PHOTOS AND/OR FAIL TO CALL US TO CONFIRM THAT THEY WERE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU LEAVE THE SITE, YOU WILL **NOT BE PAID** FOR ANY TIME ONSITE. WE ALLOW FOR UP TO 15 MINUTES TO CLEAN THE AREA, TAKE PHOTOS, AND UPLOAD THEM TO US. IF YOU NEED ADDITIONAL TIME PAST THE 15 MINUTES ALLOWED, YOU MUST NOTIFY US BEFORE THAT TIME HAS ELAPSED, OR ANYTIME PAST THE 15 MINUTES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.\n\n**\\*\\*YOU ARE NOT ALLOWED TO COMMUNICATE DIRECTLY WITH OUR CLIENTS OR PROVIDE THEM WITH YOUR CONTACT INFORMATION. ALL COMMUNICATION NEEDS TO BE THROUGH TIP N RING - NO EXCEPTIONS!!\\*\\***\n\n***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*