{"job":{"id":20032194,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TPX Communications","title":"Replacing Customer own Cradle Point with TPx Cradle Point ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><p>Replacing</p><ul><li>Customer own Cradle Point</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">With TPx Cradle Point&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Cradle point is located in the roof of the store</p><p><em>\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"</em></p><p><em>\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"</em></p><p><em>Please make sure to mark</em> <strong><em>'On My Way</em></strong><em>' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”</em></p><p><em>Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.</em></p><p><strong>DRESS CODE</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual or professional attire required</li><li>No other company logos or branding permitted (TPX branding only, if applicable)</li><li>Closed-toe shoes required (no sandals)</li><li>Safety gear must be worn if site requires (PPE)</li><li>Present yourself professionally as a TPX representative</li></ul><p><strong>PRE-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Review the Scope of Work and its requirements.</li><li>Call TPx Support with any questions or clarification about the Scope of Work</li></ul><p><strong>ON-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Check In on the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Call TPx Support&nbsp;to check in 833-294-6642&nbsp;before entering premises. <em>If after</em><strong><em>5pm</em></strong><em>PST, press</em> <strong><em>option 3</em></strong> <em>leave a message.</em></li><li>Introduce yourself as representative of TPX and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Call into Bridge Number on Time (bridge #<del>************** *** *** ***</del>) scheduled: (time) <del>** ** ****</del></li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;POST-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Confirm deliverables are complete</li><li>Enter Close out notes and any client feedback into Order</li><li>Clean-up work materials from installation (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)</li><li>Call TPX Communications from customer’s site to check out<strong>833-294-6642 (</strong>If after 6pm PST, press<strong>option 3</strong> leave a message &amp; we will follow up next Business day)</li><li>Enter Release Code (Given by the Support at the time of close out)</li><li>Check out in Field Nation Portal</li></ul><p><strong>ESCALATIONS</strong></p><ul><li>Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site <strong>833-294-6642</strong></li><li>DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform outside of the scope work, call TPx Support<strong>833-294-6642</strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><p><strong><u>Requirements:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li><li>Windows&nbsp;7 or 10&nbsp;Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li><li>Active Email Address</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)</li><li>AnyDesk</li><li>Aeroadmin</li><li>HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li><li>FTP Client</li><li>TFTP Server software</li><li>MircoSIP (SIP call testing- https://www.microsip.org/)</li><li>Wireshark</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING</strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet Patch Cable</li><li>Cisco Console Cable​</li><li>USB to DB9 male serial Cable</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><ul><li>Buttset</li><li>Line man’s test set or analog test set</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool</li><li>Snips</li><li>Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Drill/ Dry wall screws</li><li>4’ ladder</li><li>CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)</li><li>Pre-made crossover cables</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors</li><li>Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)</li><li>Power inverter</li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\nReplacing\n\n- Customer own Cradle Point\n- With TPx Cradle Point\n\nCradle point is located in the roof of the store\n\n*\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"*\n\n*\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"*\n\n*Please make sure to mark* ***'On My Way****' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”*\n\n*Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.*\n\n**DRESS CODE**\n\n- Business casual or professional attire required\n- No other company logos or branding permitted (TPX branding only, if applicable)\n- Closed-toe shoes required (no sandals)\n- Safety gear must be worn if site requires (PPE)\n- Present yourself professionally as a TPX representative\n\n**PRE-SITE WORK**\n\n- Review the Scope of Work and its requirements.\n- Call TPx Support with any questions or clarification about the Scope of Work\n\n**ON-SITE WORK**\n\n- Check In on the Field Nation Portal\n- Call TPx Support to check in 833-294-6642 before entering premises. *If after****5pm****PST, press* ***option 3*** *leave a message.*\n- Introduce yourself as representative of TPX and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal\n- Call into Bridge Number on Time (bridge #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*) scheduled: (time) \\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **POST-SITE WORK**\n\n- Confirm deliverables are complete\n- Enter Close out notes and any client feedback into Order\n- Clean-up work materials from installation (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)\n- Call TPX Communications from customer’s site to check out**833-294-6642 (**If after 6pm PST, press**option 3** leave a message & we will follow up next Business day)\n- Enter Release Code (Given by the Support at the time of close out)\n- Check out in Field Nation Portal\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site **833-294-6642**\n- DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform outside of the scope work, call TPx Support**833-294-6642**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n- Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n- Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n- Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP**\n\n- Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)\n- AnyDesk\n- Aeroadmin\n- HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n- FTP Client\n- TFTP Server software\n- MircoSIP (SIP call testing- <https://www.microsip.org/)>\n- Wireshark\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING**\n\n- Ethernet Patch Cable\n- Cisco Console Cable​\n- USB to DB9 male serial Cable\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\n- Buttset\n- Line man’s test set or analog test set\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool\n- Snips\n- Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks\n- Tone Generator and Wand\n- Drill/ Dry wall screws\n- 4’ ladder\n- CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)\n- Pre-made crossover cables\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors\n- Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)\n- Power inverter","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30","end":"2026-11-12T16:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790344280310}
