tart":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790352042173}
{"job":{"id":"5964258165","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #267314- RANDOLPH, VA - Equipment Board Installation / RAS","description":"<p># Scope of Work: Replacing Customer Analog Lines</p><p>## Pre-Application Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>Before submitting your application for any upcoming job:</p><p><br></p><p>* Verify your availability to avoid last-minute cancellations.</p><p>* Ensure smooth coordination by committing to the scheduled time.</p><p>* Analog skills are mandatory for this assignment.</p><p><br></p><p>**Important:**</p><p><br></p><p>* Technicians must not leave the site until all required pictures and the signed Work Order are provided to Tech Americas.</p><p>* Hard start time and date.</p><p>* Date or time cannot be rescheduled by any means.</p><p>* Analog skills are mandatory.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## PIAB Already Racked and Stacked</p><p><br></p><p>In many cases, the PIAB will already be installed on-site, making connection to the customer’s switch highly likely.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Check-In and Check-Out Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>* **Check-In:** Call 281-668-3211, option 3 upon arrival.</p><p>* **Check-Out:** Call 281-668-3211, option 3 immediately after completion.</p><p>* Failure to call for both check-in and check-out may result in payment deduction or no payment.</p><p>* If delayed in getting a response, email check-in/out details (site name, arrival/departure times, and POC name) to [support@tech-americas.com](mailto:support@tech-americas.com).</p><p>* Do not leave the site until all required photos and the signed Work Order are submitted to [documents@tech-americas.com](mailto:documents@tech-americas.com).</p><p>* Assigned date and time cannot be rescheduled.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Tech Americas Contacts</p><p><br></p><p>**Aida Flores:** 210-830-7125 | [aflores@tech-americas.com](mailto:aflores@tech-americas.com)</p><p>**Rafael Aparicio:** (216) 998-4955 | [raparicio@tech-americas.com](mailto:raparicio@tech-americas.com)</p><p>**Cesar Ayala:** (409) 340-0869 | [caayala@tech-americas.com](mailto:caayala@tech-americas.com)</p><p>**Elias Garcia:** (409) 340-0872 | [esgarcia@tech-americas.com](mailto:esgarcia@tech-americas.com)</p><p>**Cristo Guevara:** (254) 308-6718 | [cguevara@tech-americas.com](mailto:cguevara@tech-americas.com)</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Check-In / Check-Out Procedure</p><p><br></p><p>### 1. Check-In</p><p><br></p><p>* Call Tech Americas upon arrival.</p><p>* Introduce yourself to the POC (name, company, and purpose of visit).</p><p>* Verify POC identity.</p><p>* If the POC is unavailable, call Tech Americas Support immediately.</p><p>* Log arrival time.</p><p><br></p><p>### 2. Check-Out</p><p><br></p><p>* Call Tech Americas immediately after job completion.</p><p>* Confirm the site has been restored to its original condition.</p><p>* Obtain the POC signature on the Work Order.</p><p>* Submit the signed WO and required photos to [documents@tech-americas.com](mailto:documents@tech-americas.com) within 24 hours.</p><p>* Do not leave the site until all required documentation has been submitted.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Identification Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>**Federal Sites:** Must carry one of the following:</p><p><br></p><p>* State-Issued Enhanced Driver’s License or Enhanced Real ID</p><p>* U.S. Passport / Passport Card</p><p>* DHS Trusted Traveler Cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</p><p>* DoD ID</p><p>* Permanent Resident Card</p><p>* Tribal Nation ID</p><p>* HSPD-12 PIV Card</p><p>* Other approved federal identification</p><p><br></p><p>**Non-Federal Sites:** Standard driver’s license or state-issued ID unless otherwise specified.</p><p><br></p><p>If ID is rejected, contact Tech Americas Support immediately.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Pre-Installation Tasks (On-Site)</p><p><br></p><p>1. Introduce yourself to the POC and explain the purpose of the visit.</p><p>2. Locate the MTL equipment in the telecom room.</p><p>3. Take clear before photos of the equipment, telecom room, and DMARC connections.</p><p>4. Verify LTE/Cell signal (-85 dBm minimum).</p><p>5. Verify existing analog lines using a working butt set and compare them with the provided inventory.</p><p>6. Trace and identify the lines that will be replaced.</p><p>7. Check for permits if equipment or cable mounting is required.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Installation Process</p><p><br></p><p>1. Mount the MetTel Communications Board as required.</p><p>2. Mount the MIMO antenna.</p><p>3. Connect cables according to the installation requirements.</p><p>4. Replace and/or connect the customer analog lines as instructed.</p><p>5. Verify and test all lines.</p><p>6. Coordinate with MetTel Remote Support for final validation.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## PIAB to Customer Switch Connection</p><p><br></p><p>* Connect the PIAB to the customer switch when required or as instructed by Tech Americas/POC.</p><p>* Follow all required approval and documentation procedures.</p><p>* Take clear before and after photos of all connections.</p><p>* Perform validation testing, including:</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;* Dial tone</p><p>&nbsp;* Inbound calls</p><p>&nbsp;* Outbound calls</p><p>&nbsp;* 933 address verification when applicable</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## MANDATORY EXPERIENCE, TOOLS AND MATERIALS</p><p><br></p><p>The technician must have experience with **Analog/POTS lines, alarm cutovers, line tracing, direct alarm-panel connections, and PIAB/Data Remote installations.**</p><p><br></p><p>**DO NOT ACCEPT THIS ASSIGNMENT WITHOUT THE REQUIRED EXPERIENCE.**</p><p><br></p><p>### Required Equipment</p><p><br></p><p>* Full 300-ft box/reel of CAT5e or CAT6 cable</p><p>* Cross-connect wire, RJ11/RJ45 jacks, and modular plugs</p><p>* Working butt set with RJ11</p><p>* 66/110 punch-down tool</p><p>* Toner, probe, cable tester/toner, and crimper</p><p>* Digital multimeter</p><p>* 2-way and 3-way splitter adapters</p><p>* 10–12 ft ladder</p><p>* Drill and mounting hardware</p><p>* Label maker, Sharpie, tie wraps, and Velcro</p><p>* Laptop with Ethernet and TeamViewer or AnyDesk</p><p>* Serial/USB adapter and console cable</p><p>* Mobile hotspot or reliable internet</p><p>* Smartphone with camera</p><p><br></p><p>**Important:** Verify all required tools and sufficient cable before traveling to the site. Missing required experience, tools, or cable may result in removal from the assignment and **no payment**.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Documentation Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>* Take clear before-and-after photos of the equipment, connections, and completed work.</p><p>* Complete and submit the Line Verification Form as a PDF.</p><p>* Obtain the customer's signed Work Order.</p><p>* Submit the signed WO and all required documentation to:</p><p>&nbsp;**[documents@tech-americas.com](mailto:documents@tech-americas.com)**</p><p>* Documentation must be submitted immediately after job completion or within 24 hours at the latest.</p><p>* Failure to submit the required documentation within this timeframe may result in the job being closed without payment.</p><p><br></p><p>---</p><p><br></p><p>## Contingency Plans</p><p><br></p><p>* **POC Unavailable:** Contact Tech Americas for a backup contact.</p><p>* **Equipment Failure:** Report the issue to Tech Americas and await instructions.</p><p>* **Poor Signal:** Connect to the customer switch or use an approved antenna extension as directed.</p><p>* **Access Denial:** Contact Tech Americas and site security immediately.</p><p>* **Line/Analog Issue:** Document the issue, contact Tech Americas Support, and do not make unauthorized changes.</p><p><br></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T11:30","end":"2026-09-28T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":72},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790352055172}
