{"job":{"id":20033400,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Install Package Room w/ Electronic Door Strike & Retrofit","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER YOU AGREE TO THE ITEMS LISTED.READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME AND ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>CONTACTS &amp; SUPPORT-You will be speaking directly with our customer for support.&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>BACKGROUND</u></strong></p><p>Parcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR Services is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>WORK ORDER OVERVIEW</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>Please schedule tech to go onsite and complete the rest of the installation. tech will be installing door strike with system. we may have to do a retrofit for this as well. make sure tech has hotspot with them in the event site doesn't have internet. </u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Perform&nbsp;<strong>maintenance&nbsp;</strong>on&nbsp;Parcel Pending automated package locker system to ensure system is fully functional.&nbsp;<strong>Details below. (must be able to troubleshoot with Customer Support Staff)</strong></p><p><strong>***Please do NOT contact the property unless instructed by Parcel Pending or ASR.***</strong></p><p><strong>Regardless if tracking for parts is provided or not, please show up at your scheduled time.&nbsp;You will be paid for your time on site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION</u></strong></p><p>Install Door Strike for Automated Package Locker System</p><p>The following has been reported, but upon arrival you may be asked to check other issues while on site.</p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>O-Droid Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li></ul><p>General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.</p><p><strong>ASR Project Number: 887</strong></p><p><strong><u>TOOL REQUIREMENT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Corded or Cordless Oscillating Multi-tool</strong></li><li><strong>Corded or Cordless Drill</strong></li><li><strong>Drill Bit Set</strong></li><li><strong>Lineman Scissors</strong></li><li><strong>Butt Connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Wire Crimpers</strong></li><li><strong>Wire Cutters</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Multimeter</strong></li><li><strong>100’ Fish Tape</strong></li><li><strong>25’ Tape Measure</strong></li><li><strong>Ladder - 4' or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with Camera and ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;<strong>(for checking in and out)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment).&nbsp;Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><strong>Print, review, and bring to site:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Package Room version 2</strong><strong>.pdf</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss any payment or scheduling discrepancies with the property manager or Parcel Pending (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Remember you are a professional and your appearance, Speech, behavior and tidiness of the completed work must be becoming of such.&nbsp;The end user and customer must have confidence in your abilities.&nbsp;</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Your time starts on site when you check in with Mark or Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone numbers in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Please use the Zoho Work Order Update Link that was emailed to you. (En route, On Site, Complete, Support Needed)</strong></li><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call ASR immediately.</strong></li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion. Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.</strong></li><li>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</li><li>You must conduct yourself in a professional manner.&nbsp;</li><li>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</li><li>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support&nbsp;(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\"</strong>&nbsp;unless instructed by Technical Support.</li><li><strong>Upon completion of service, leave the Locker Key in Box 1 -IMPORTANT&nbsp;</strong>Missing Key may be charged&nbsp;$50.00 and whatever the site deems.&nbsp;If you are unable to open Box 1, please tape the key to the top of the Main Tower.(take pictures of where key is left onsite and or get the name of person key is left with.</li><li>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call ASR.</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong><u>If technician leaves site and pictures have not been reviewed and approved,&nbsp;technician will need to return within 24 hours at no cost to ASR.</u></strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, and name of person that released tech from site. parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion (Odroid, Add-On Board, etc.), a return label will included with part replacement.</p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain.&nbsp;Parts will need to be shipped within 24 hours.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT-If technician leaves site and pictures have not been reviewed and approved,&nbsp;technician will need to return within 24 hours at no cost to ASR.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that.</strong></p>","markdown":"**BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER YOU AGREE TO THE ITEMS LISTED.READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING.**\n\n**YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME AND ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\nThe name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.\n\nBe sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.\n\n**CONTACTS & SUPPORT-You will be speaking directly with our customer for support. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.**\n\n**BACKGROUND**\n\nParcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR Services is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**WORK ORDER OVERVIEW**\n\n**Please schedule tech to go onsite and complete the rest of the installation. tech will be installing door strike with system. we may have to do a retrofit for this as well. make sure tech has hotspot with them in the event site doesn't have internet.**\n\nPerform **maintenance** on Parcel Pending automated package locker system to ensure system is fully functional. **Details below. (must be able to troubleshoot with Customer Support Staff)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please do NOT contact the property unless instructed by Parcel Pending or ASR.\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Regardless if tracking for parts is provided or not, please show up at your scheduled time. You will be paid for your time on site.**\n\n**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION**\n\nInstall Door Strike for Automated Package Locker System\n\nThe following has been reported, but upon arrival you may be asked to check other issues while on site.\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- O-Droid Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n\nGeneral Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.\n\n**ASR Project Number: 887**\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Corded or Cordless Oscillating Multi-tool**\n- **Corded or Cordless Drill**\n- **Drill Bit Set**\n- **Lineman Scissors**\n- **Butt Connectors**\n- **Wire Crimpers**\n- **Wire Cutters**\n- **Digital Multimeter**\n- **100’ Fish Tape**\n- **25’ Tape Measure**\n- **Ladder - 4' or higher**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **Smart Phone with Camera and ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** **(for checking in and out)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Print, review, and bring to site:**\n\n- **Package Room version 2****.pdf**\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss any payment or scheduling discrepancies with the property manager or Parcel Pending (NO exceptions)**\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n**Remember you are a professional and your appearance, Speech, behavior and tidiness of the completed work must be becoming of such. The end user and customer must have confidence in your abilities.**\n\n- **Your time starts on site when you check in with Mark or Rodrigo.** (Phone numbers in Confidential Information)\n- **Please use the Zoho Work Order Update Link that was emailed to you. (En route, On Site, Complete, Support Needed)**\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call ASR immediately.**\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion. Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.**\n- You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.\n- You must conduct yourself in a professional manner.\n- All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.\n- Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\"** unless instructed by Technical Support.\n- **Upon completion of service, leave the Locker Key in Box 1 -IMPORTANT** Missing Key may be charged $50.00 and whatever the site deems. If you are unable to open Box 1, please tape the key to the top of the Main Tower.(take pictures of where key is left onsite and or get the name of person key is left with.\n- If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call ASR.\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **If technician leaves site and pictures have not been reviewed and approved, technician will need to return within 24 hours at no cost to ASR.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, and name of person that released tech from site. parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\nIf any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion (Odroid, Add-On Board, etc.), a return label will included with part replacement.\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain. Parts will need to be shipped within 24 hours.**\n\n**PAYMENT-If technician leaves site and pictures have not been reviewed and approved, technician will need to return within 24 hours at no cost to ASR.**\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by ASR.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.\n\n**Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T10:00","end":"2026-09-29T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":18},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00: