you are the ShopperTrak Technician from NET and you will be working on the ShopperTrak traffic counting system. If the store manager is not available, speak with the manager on duty. If the manager refuses to allow the service or has questions call NET help desk at 608-827-2271.  \n  \nContact ShopperTrak to log in at 312-529-5304 opt 2, 2, 1. BE PATIENT. Hold times of 15 minutes can be expected. DO NOT leave a message for ShopperTrak at anytime, they will NOT call you back. DO NOT hang up while on hold. If hold time exceeds 15 minutes, remain on hold with ShopperTrak and contact NET immediately using a different line at 608-827-2271. When the ShopperTrak Agent answers provide the following information:  \n\\*Your name (first and last)  \n\\*Your company name (NET)  \n\\*Store number  \n\\*Time you arrived onsite\n\nLabel the cable at all locations (device end, switch end, and port itself) with “ST”, “ShopperTrak”, or “Customer Counter” and submit photo  \nRemove the lens covers  \n\\*\\*\\*If there is equipment to return, then -  \n-Report to NET the contact information (Name and Phone #; Store number is acceptable) of who was given the equipment to return.   \n-Send a picture of the return shipping label with the tracking number legible.  \n  \nOrbit 8 Installation Guide and all required materials listed within  \n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Tech should be prepared with patching materials in case of orbit relocation\\*\\*\\*\\*  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n3\\) Testing  \nYou will be testing with ShopperTrak today. Once ready to test call ShopperTrak at (312) 529-5304 option 2.  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n4\\) Pictures  \nTECH SHOULD BRING SMARTPHONE. Tech will need to send photos of any equipment replaced or relocated FROM SITE to include the back of all devices and the return label (if applicable)   \n  \nSend pictures to DSS@nettechnology.com  \n  \nEmail subject line MUST read \\[XXXXXX\\] where XXXXXX = WO number on NET Purchase order (usually starting with a 1.)  \n  \nIf you encounter issues please try to find an open WiFi hotspot nearby and try sending again on wireless signal or ask NET for mobile app.  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n5\\) Log-Out  \nShopperTrak will provide you with check IN and check OUT codes upon completion of the service. Record these on your Work Order as NET requires these upon logout.\n\nBe respectful to the store managers  \nLogout with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271(Option 3)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T08:30","end":"2026-09-29T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":210},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790352121785}
{"job":{"id":20034152,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"Imbox Breakdown device(Machine Not Spraying)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*******PLEASE READ ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*********</strong></p><p><strong><u>-----------------THIS IS FOR A SHOE PROTECTION SPRAY KIOSK------------------------</u></strong></p><p><em>-------------------------ALL GUIDES ARE PROVIDED BELOW-----------------------------</em></p><p>***TECH WILL NEED ALL EQUIPMENT FROM REQUIRED LIST BELOW***</p><p><strong><em>Please read the entire work order before requesting this job.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Please read the attached documentation and print out the installation check list as needed before service.</strong></p><p><strong><em>TECH: Please call Work Order Manager (see ticket) when you first arrive. If additional technical assistance is needed, please reach out to WO manager to connect to support.</em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(28, 37, 46);\">522010559 -</span><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">machine is not spraying - got a right error column - but can see its moving</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">1. replace nozzzles</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">1. replace filters</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">2. DEO pump swap if available</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">3. Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">4. Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">5. Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses. Bring a syringe (IM550500) if available to clear the air from the pump if pump swap not performed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">6. Replace top filter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">7. Deep clean</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">Any parts not used please send back to POSRG</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>!!!!Run Diagnostics report and take picture, send to WOM before starting troubleshooting!!!!!!!ref. imbox touch screen nav guide pg 8 and 9.</u></strong></p><p>run a diagnostic report- send results to WO ( <strong>determine if fuse needs replacing)</strong></p><p><strong>Do a spray test first before following troubleshooting steps. see pg 6-7 nozzle replacement guide.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>2.Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.</p><p>3.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.</p><p>4.4.Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses.</p><p>5. replace check valves, suction lids, and quick connectors</p><p>1. Replace nozzles and filters if spraying and if needed.<strong>(spray nozzle replacement guide)</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">Ensure when replacing that nozzles are oriented in the correct direction, and that the hoses are fastened properly</span></p><p>2. If machine is not spraying do a Fluid Cannister Fix <strong>(fluid cannister guide)</strong></p><p>3,Inspect weld on straws inside of fluid cannister. Swap quick connectors.</p><p>4.Disconnect both input and output of spray pump. Using compressed air insert through input of pump and try to unclog spray pump.</p><p>5. If it's not spraying after quick fixes, swap the spray pump with deo pump.<strong>PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP</strong>. <strong>(deo swap guide)</strong></p><p>6. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid</p><p>7. do test treatment again, record a video and send as deliverable to WOM<strong>(spray nozzle replacement guide pg 6 and7)</strong></p><p>8. Do steps 4 and 5 again.</p><p>9.deep cleaning of top chamber.</p><p>.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.</p><p>Check fluid cannister straw and quick connect coupling, see if it has teflon tape applied to it, if not, apply teflon tape to the threads. Make sure the quick connect and the straw are tight, it should not be able to wiggle it. 3. If it's not spraying after the fluid cannister fix and nozzle replacement, swap the spray pump with deo pump. PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP. 4. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid 5. do test treatment, record a video and send as deliverable 6. Do steps 4 and 5 again. 7.deep cleaning of top chamber. 8. replace fuse (if needed, check diagnostic report first</p><p>Send back the old check valve. Write the machine's serial number and the task number on a piece of paper.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><em>If any pieces are missing from the shipped unit please inform the work order manager immediately.</em></p><p><strong><del>***</del>Failure to check in may result in a loss of compensation and any travel expenses.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be Paid</u></strong></p><p><strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>check in/out with POSRG work order manager.</p><p>The Imbox has been tested and is functioning before departure.</p><p>Complete the check list and attach photos to the work order.</p><p>Leave detailed closing notes.</p><p><strong><u>Duration on Site</u></strong></p><p>An experienced technician can be done in about 2 hours.If more time is needed the technician is required to call the work order manager to get approval. Failure to get approval will result in nonpayment.</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools</u></strong></p><p>Tools:</p><ul><li>Torx bit bet (T6 – T30)</li><li>Precision screwdriver set</li><li>Screwdriver set</li><li>Digital multimeter</li><li>Curved needle nose</li><li>Socket set (5.5mm, 10mm, etc.)</li><li>2 Adjustable wrenches</li><li>Wrench set</li><li>Flashlight/ light</li></ul><p>Materials:</p><ul><li>Teflon Tape</li><li>Electrical Tape</li><li>Compressed Air (Duster)</li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*PLEASE READ ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**-----------------THIS IS FOR A SHOE PROTECTION SPRAY KIOSK------------------------**\n\n*-------------------------ALL GUIDES ARE PROVIDED BELOW-----------------------------*\n\n\\*\\*\\*TECH WILL NEED ALL EQUIPMENT FROM REQUIRED LIST BELOW\\*\\*\\*\n\n***Please read the entire work order before requesting this job.***\n\n**Please read the attached documentation and print out the installation check list as needed before service.**\n\n***TECH: Please call Work Order Manager (see ticket) when you first arrive. If additional technical assistance is needed, please reach out to WO manager to connect to support.***\n\n522010559 -machine is not spraying - got a right error column - but can see its moving\n\n1\\. replace nozzzles\n\n1\\. replace filters\n\n2\\. DEO pump swap if available\n\n3\\. Check the Canister & Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.\n\n4\\. Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle\n\n5\\. Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses. Bring a syringe (IM550500) if available to clear the air from the pump if pump swap not performed\n\n6\\. Replace top filter\n\n7\\. Deep clean\n\nAny parts not used please send back to POSRG\n\n**!!!!Run Diagnostics report and take picture, send to WOM before starting troubleshooting!!!!!!!ref. imbox touch screen nav guide pg 8 and 9.**\n\nrun a diagnostic report- send results to WO ( **determine if fuse needs replacing)**\n\n**Do a spray test first before following troubleshooting steps. see pg 6-7 nozzle replacement guide.**\n\n2.Check the Canister & Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.\n\n3.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.\n\n4.4.Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses.\n\n5\\. replace check valves, suction lids, and quick connectors\n\n1\\. Replace nozzles and filters if spraying and if needed.**(spray nozzle replacement guide)**\n\nEnsure when replacing that nozzles are oriented in the correct direction, and that the hoses are fastened properly\n\n2\\. If machine is not spraying do a Fluid Cannister Fix **(fluid cannister guide)**\n\n3,Inspect weld on straws inside of fluid cannister. Swap quick connectors.\n\n4.Disconnect both input and output of spray pump. Using compressed air insert through input of pump and try to unclog spray pump.\n\n5\\. If it's not spraying after quick fixes, swap the spray pump with deo pump.**PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP**. **(deo swap guide)**\n\n6\\. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid\n\n7\\. do test treatment again, record a video and send as deliverable to WOM**(spray nozzle replacement guide pg 6 and7)**\n\n8\\. Do steps 4 and 5 again.\n\n9.deep cleaning of top chamber.\n\n.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.\n\nCheck fluid cannister straw and quick connect coupling, see if it has teflon tape applied to it, if not, apply teflon tape to the threads. Make sure the quick connect and the straw are tight, it should not be able to wiggle it. 3. If it's not spraying after the fluid cannister fix and nozzle replacement, swap the spray pump with deo pump. PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP. 4. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid 5. do test treatment, record a video and send as deliverable 6. Do steps 4 and 5 again. 7.deep cleaning of top chamber. 8. replace fuse (if needed, check diagnostic report first\n\nSend back the old check valve. Write the machine's serial number and the task number on a piece of paper.\n\n*If any pieces are missing from the shipped unit please inform the work order manager immediately.*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Failure to check in may result in a loss of compensation and any travel expenses.**\n\n**Required Deliverables to be Paid**\n\n**MUST** check in/out with POSRG work order manager.\n\nThe Imbox has been tested and is functioning before departure.\n\nComplete the check list and attach photos to the work order.\n\nLeave detailed closing notes.\n\n**Duration on Site**\n\nAn experienced technician can be done in about 2 hours.If more time is needed the technician is required to call the work order manager to get approval. Failure to get approval will result in nonpayment.\n\n**Required Tools**\n\nTools:\n\n- Torx bit bet (T6 – T30)\n- Precision screwdriver set\n- Screwdriver set\n- Digital multimeter\n- Curved needle nose\n- Socket set (5.5mm, 10mm, etc.)\n- 2 Adjustable wrenches\n- Wrench set\n- Flashlight/ light\n\nMaterials:\n\n- Teflon Tape\n- Electrical Tape\n- Compressed Air (Duster)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T11:00","end":"2026-09-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":18},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 (countered: $210) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790352690174}
{"job":{"id":20034322,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Cortland Midtown East The Avenues - AP troubleshooting  #322143","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong>&nbsp;<em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Raleigh NC 27604</em></p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.</em></p><p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW):</strong>&nbsp;Troubleshoot AP.AP is offline. Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired.</p><p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong>&nbsp;to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li><li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</li><li><strong>Represent the brand</strong>&nbsp;with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li><li><strong>Do not overshare technical or internal details</strong>with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.</li></ul><p>⚠️&nbsp;<em>If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></p><p><strong>Required Experience:</strong></p><ul><li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)</li><li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li><li>Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination</li></ul><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)</li></ul><p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p><ul><li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li><li>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.</li></ul><p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p><p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p><p>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</p><ul><li>Why This Matters:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li><li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li></ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** *Raleigh NC 27604*\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW):** Troubleshoot AP.AP is offline. Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare technical or internal details**with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.\n\n⚠️ *If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience:**\n\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\nIt is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T09:00","end":"2026-09-28T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":225},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"s