{"job":{"id":20034407,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Cortland Midtown East Vue 64 - AP troubleshooting  - #321919","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Residential Property –</strong>&nbsp;<em>Raleigh NC 27604</em></p>\n<p><em>Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW):</strong>&nbsp;Troubleshoot AP.Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired. LADDER IS REQUIRED.</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong>&nbsp;to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li>\n<li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</li>\n<li><strong>Represent the brand</strong>&nbsp;with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not overshare technical or internal details</strong>with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>⚠️&nbsp;<em>If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Required Experience:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)</li>\n<li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li>\n<li>Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li>\n<li>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p>\n<p>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Why This Matters:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li>\n<li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** *Raleigh NC 27604*\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW):** Troubleshoot AP.Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired. LADDER IS REQUIRED.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare technical or internal details**with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.\n\n⚠️ *If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience:**\n\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\nIt is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T10:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":225},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00