{"job":{"id":20034724,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"call forward position issue||*Troubleshooting*","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work: Store states call forward position is not working. Check to see what the actual issue is. If it is not lighting up or calling it may be unplugged at the button power or LED panel. Check all cables and plugs and make sure it is plugged into a working grounded orange outlet. If the button is working/calling but the light on the pole is not lighting up then the LED is probably disconnected. To check if the PDU LED is unplugged - Remove faceplate and make sure LED is securely connected. To check if LED is disconnected, you do NOT need to remove full PDU head. If you are not sure how to access the LED panel without removing full PDU, TEXT Jess for help and pic. For QB2 buttons may need to be reset. First check the version of the button turn button over and look for V2, V3 or V4 printed or written underneath. V3 cannot be reprogrammed. they are single program. hard coded. button will need to be replaced. please confirm if all buttons on the queue line are the same version. V2 buttons - press and hold the button until it starts to fast blink under your fingers (about 15 seconds until fast blink). When it fast blinks tap it once. V4 buttons - under the button where the cable comes in there is a small reset button - press and hold for 3 seconds and release. The top of the button should be fast blinking. When it fast blinks tap it once. When finished programming, go back to hub and arrow down to save/exit. Make sure you are the home screen before testing. IF PARTS ARE REQUESTED-NEEDED, DO NOT CLOSE TICKET – LEAVE OPEN AS PENDING. TICKET WILL BE ESCALATED WITH TRACKING INFO. Text Jess a picture of the part needed and button for confirmation of 