{"job":{"id":20035403,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Kronos Clock Install WITH NEW CABLE RUN","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW CONTACTS IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong> <u>Install Kronos Clock with NEW Cat6 Cable Run (1 clock per site at most sites)</u></p>\n<p><strong><u>Tech will provide all materials necessary (cable, connectors, jacks, wall plates, labels, and any additional materials needed) and will be reimbursed. Full List below.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Tech must bring 8-10' ladder to run cable above ceiling where necessary.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Tech must follow all instructions below</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Arrive at site and check in with Netview Project Manager and the onsite customer contact (contact info in Confidential Information section of this work order)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Confirm with site contact how many clocks they have to install. (1 clock per site at most locations)</li>\n<li>Dial into bridge to advise you are onsite and beginning to survey the area (link in Confidential Information section of this work order)</li>\n<li><strong><u>Complete below steps for each clock.</u></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take pictures of old time clock upon arrival.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Survey site/clock area to determine length of new cable run (<strong>NOTE: YOU CANNOT USE EXSISTING CABLE AS CURRENT TIME CLOCK IS NOT TO BE DISCONNECTED OR TOUCHED</strong>)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Cable run cable path will be from nearest MDF or IDF to wall clock location.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Clock should be mounted directly next to the existing clock and connect it to the existing network (the clock uses POE).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complete NEW cable run and terminations</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect cable to network and Kronos Clock</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Label cable using label maker (not handwritten)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power on Kronos Clock</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Program Kronos Clock following instructions from home screen and provided by support</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify with bridge support the clock is successfully online</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">After clock is installed, connected and support confirms it is online, you will work with the site contact to enable, test and validate the clock connection, troubleshooting any issues.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tape Notice on the clock covering the entire clock (see example picture attached) - Tech must print this notice prior to arriving onsite.</li>\n<li>Take picture of labeled cable at the rack end showing the label</li>\n<li>Take pictures of new wall clock/location showing the full room with the clock centered in the picture and a close up of the clock showing the home screen after it is online.</li>\n<li>Take picture of new time clock with printed \"NOTICE\" fully covering clock.</li>\n<li>Contact Netview and confirm the install is complete and pictures are uploaded before leaving site.</li>\n<li>Document old time clock(s) on attached \"Inventory List and Sign Off\" form. Take a picture of that form and upload it to this work order.</li>\n<li>Have site contact sign the sign off document confirming work is complete.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools AND Materials:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>(1) box of Cat6 cable</strong></li>\n<li><strong>RJ45 connectors</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Faceplate</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Label Maker</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Laptop:</strong> With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ladder</strong> (8'-10' ladder)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>View Less</p>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW CONTACTS IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:** Install Kronos Clock with NEW Cat6 Cable Run (1 clock per site at most sites)\n\n**Tech will provide all materials necessary (cable, connectors, jacks, wall plates, labels, and any additional materials needed) and will be reimbursed. Full List below.**\n\n**Tech must bring 8-10' ladder to run cable above ceiling where necessary.**\n\n**Tech must follow all instructions below**\n\n1. Arrive at site and check in with Netview Project Manager and the onsite customer contact (contact info in Confidential Information section of this work order)\n2. Confirm with site contact how many clocks they have to install. (1 clock per site at most locations)\n3. Dial into bridge to advise you are onsite and beginning to survey the area (link in Confidential Information section of this work order)\n4. **Complete below steps for each clock.**\n5. Take pictures of old time clock upon arrival.\n6. Survey site/clock area to determine length of new cable run (**NOTE: YOU CANNOT USE EXSISTING CABLE AS CURRENT TIME CLOCK IS NOT TO BE DISCONNECTED OR TOUCHED**)\n7. Cable run cable path will be from nearest MDF or IDF to wall clock location.\n8. Clock should be mounted directly next to the existing clock and connect it to the existing network (the clock uses POE).\n9. Complete NEW cable run and terminations\n10. Connect cable to network and Kronos Clock\n11. Label cable using label maker (not handwritten)\n12. Power on Kronos Clock\n13. Program Kronos Clock following instructions from home screen and provided by support\n14. Verify with bridge support the clock is successfully online\n15. After clock is installed, connected and support confirms it is online, you will work with the site contact to enable, test and validate the clock connection, troubleshooting any issues.\n16. Tape Notice on the clock covering the entire clock (see example picture attached) - Tech must print this notice prior to arriving onsite.\n17. Take picture of labeled cable at the rack end showing the label\n18. Take pictures of new wall clock/location showing the full room with the clock centered in the picture and a close up of the clock showing the home screen after it is online.\n19. Take picture of new time clock with printed \"NOTICE\" fully covering clock.\n20. Contact Netview and confirm the install is complete and pictures are uploaded before leaving site.\n21. Document old time clock(s) on attached \"Inventory List and Sign Off\" form. Take a picture of that form and upload it to this work order.\n22. Have site contact sign the sign off document confirming work is complete.\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n**Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.**\n\n**The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.**\n\n**Required Tools AND Materials:**\n\n- **(1) box of Cat6 cable**\n- **RJ45 connectors**\n- **Faceplate**\n- **Label Maker**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)\n\nView Less","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T10:00","end":"2026-10-02T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":36},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790358526724}
