 the Trader Joe's Helpdesk, please wait 5 min before trying again. Once you dial their number, please press option 2 to speak with a helpdesk coordinator.\n- ***Do not contact TDJ for support or work instructions, you must reach out to Pomeroy for support, if you reach out to TDJ for support, a penalty will be applied to the work order.***\n\n***﻿***\n\n**Dress Code**: Business casual. Need to maintain a Professional appearance.\n\n**Required Items to bring:**\n\n- Basic Tool Set\n\n**\\*Only accept this job if you have all the required tools and are able to make the required time frame.\\***\n\n**Technical Documentation:**\n\n**Technical Resource Site:** <https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703>\n\n<https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-whole-unit-removalreplacement>\n\n<https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-bios-settings>\n\n**Login ID:** fieldnation@client.pomeroy.com\n\n**Login PW:** If not provided in Messages section, please call Pomeroy Dispatch Center\n\n**Parts Shipment:**\n\n- Parts (if required) will be couriered to the site; arrival is typically within 4 hours of ticket creation. Please verify with the Pomeroy Dispatch Center that any part(s) has been delivered to resolve issue.\n- You may be scheduled to arrive prior to part arrival, due to SLA, please troubleshoot in advance to determine if part is actually required.\n\n**Parts Handling Requirements:**\n\n1. Parts return is the responsibility of the assigned Provider. DO NOT LEAVE PARTS ONSITE, unless authorized by Pomeroy.\n2. If parts are left onsite, work order will not be approved until parts are confirmed shipped.\n3. Required part must be dropped off asap to UPS: If work order was serviced during business hours, required part must be dropped off the same day until 7PM local time or UPS closing time. If work order was serviced during non-business hours, required part must be dropped off the next day by 12:00PM (noon) local time.\n4. You must use the return label that comes inside the box shipped by Pomeroy, for additional return labels, please advise Pomeroy Dispatch Center to arrange for label(s) to be sent to you.\n5. Save shipment drop off receipts in case there are issues tracking or recovering the equipment after it is dropped off.\n6. Provider may also be held financially responsible for equipment lost due to negligence or failure to follow instruction.\n7. Ship parts to Pomeroy using return label. Parts must be taken from the store and shipped, unless specified by Pomeroy. Do not leave parts onsite even if asked by TDJ Staff/Service Desk.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T20:30","end":"2026-09-25T22:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":70},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790360030519}
{"job":{"id":20012009,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Promotion Technology Group","title":"Sally Ignited #3350 - Burlington NC - Audio System Only- Proj #13283","description":{"html":"<p><strong>2 Trips Required</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Trip #1 - 10/3/26 - Decom. Test Existing Audio System and report any issues. Remove speakers/Mounting - package to be reused. Tie speaker wire up in ceiling to be reused.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Trip #2 - 10/14/26 - Reinstall speakers - Test Audio</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Order SOW:&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Sally Ignited 3350</p>\n<p><strong>System Overview:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG is not providing a screen at this location. PTG is under the impression there is an existing audio system in this space. There will be a change order for audio equipment if there are no speakers in the space when we arrive.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing audio system, including the amplifier, music player, and two ceiling speakers, will remain in service. **<u>PTG Tech MUST test equipment and provide status prior to speaker removal.**</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will provide temporary handling and reinstallation of the one affected existing ceiling speaker as required to accommodate remodeling activities and ceiling replacement by others.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>System Components</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Existing Equipment to be Reused:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Existing ceiling speakers</li>\n<li>Existing amplifier</li>\n<li>Existing OFE music player</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Client-Supplied Items:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>120V/20A duplex power outlet at display location</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Site Visit 1 – Existing Speaker Removal</strong></p>\n<p><strong>During this initial site visit, PTG technicians will:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Test Existing Equipment on site and report findings to PTG PM</li>\n<li>Remove the existing ceiling speaker(s) from the ACT ceiling</li>\n<li>Disconnect speaker wiring as required</li>\n<li>Place the speaker in a protected storage position above the ceiling grid to allow ceiling tile replacement by others</li>\n<li>Leave the existing amplifier and OFE music player undisturbed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>No new equipment installation will occur during this visit.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This visit is scheduled for weekend labor rates and has been priced accordingly.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site Visit 2 – Speaker Reinstallation</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will return to the site to complete the final installation work.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Audio System Description</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will reinstall the affected existing ceiling speaker into the new ACT ceiling. Final speaker placement will be field verified during installation.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing amplifier and OFE music player will remain in place and will be reconnected to the existing speaker system.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing speaker wiring is assumed to be reusable and will be field verified during installation. Any required replacement, repair, or new speaker wiring will be addressed via Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing amplifier is assumed to be functional and compatible with the reinstalled speaker system. Functionality will be field verified during installation. Any required repair or replacement of the amplifier will be addressed via Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Technicians must arrive with:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Network crimp and cut tools</li>\n<li>Network tester</li>\n<li>Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before leaving the site, the PTG technician must:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please test the audio equipment to confirm existing system works during 1st visit.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify functionality of the reinstalled speaker system</li>\n<li>Label installed A/V equipment as required</li>\n<li>Provide basic operational overview to store management personnel</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>All OFE must be onsite and in working condition prior to the scheduled installation dates. If OFE is found to be faulty, missing, or incompatible, additional labor or replacement equipment may require a Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>General Notes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Weekend labor rates apply to the initial site visit</li>\n<li>Work areas must be accessible during scheduled installation dates</li>\n<li>No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Exclusions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This Scope of Work does not include:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.</li>\n<li>Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations</li>\n<li>Ceiling tile replacement</li>\n<li>Structural reinforcement or seismic support</li>\n<li>Millwork or cabinetry modifications</li>\n<li>Patching, painting, or decorative finishing</li>\n<li>Permit acquisition or fees unless otherwise noted</li>\n<li>Prevailing wage or union labor unless otherwise stated</li>\n<li>Lifts or scaffolding unless otherwise stated</li>\n<li>Network configuration, IP provisioning, or connectivity troubleshooting beyond physical patching of the CAT5e infrastructure</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**2 Trips Required**\n\n**Trip #1 - 10/3/26 - Decom. Test Existing Audio System and report any issues. Remove speakers/Mounting - package to be reused. Tie speaker wire up in ceiling to be reused.**\n\n**Trip #2 - 10/14/26 - Reinstall speakers - Test Audio**\n\nOrder SOW:\n\nSally Ignited 3350\n\n**System Overview:**\n\n**PTG is not providing a screen at this location. PTG is under the impression there is an existing audio system in this space. There will be a change order for audio equipment if there are no speakers in the space when we arrive.**\n\n**The existing audio system, including the amplifier, music player, and two ceiling speakers, will remain in service. \\*\\*PTG Tech MUST test equipment and provide status prior to speaker removal.\\*\\***\n\n**PTG will provide temporary handling and reinstallation of the one affected existing ceiling speaker as required to accommodate remodeling activities and ceiling replacement by others.**\n\n**System Components**\n\n**Existing Equipment to be Reused:**\n\n- Existing ceiling speakers\n- Existing amplifier\n- Existing OFE music player\n\n**Client-Supplied Items:**\n\n- 120V/20A duplex power outlet at display location\n\n**Site Visit 1 – Existing Speaker Removal**\n\n**During this initial site visit, PTG technicians will:**\n\n- Test Existing Equipment on site and report findings to PTG PM\n- Remove the existing ceiling speaker(s) from the ACT ceiling\n- Disconnect speaker wiring as required\n- Place the speaker in a protected storage position above the ceiling grid to allow ceiling tile replacement by others\n- Leave the existing amplifier and OFE music player undisturbed\n\n**No new equipment installation will occur during this visit.**\n\n**This visit is scheduled for weekend labor rates and has been priced accordingly.**\n\n**Site Visit 2 – Speaker Reinstallation**\n\n**PTG will return to the site to complete the final installation work.**\n\n**Audio System Description**\n\n**PTG will reinstall the affected existing ceiling speaker into the new ACT ceiling. Final speaker placement will be field verified during installation.**\n\n**The existing amplifier and OFE music player will remain in place and will be reconnected to the existing speaker system.**\n\n**The existing speaker wiring is assumed to be reusable and will be field verified during installation. Any required replacement, repair, or new speaker wiring will be addressed via Change Order.**\n\n**The existing amplifier is assumed to be functional and compatible with the reinstalled speaker system. Functionality will be field verified during installation. Any required repair or replacement of the amplifier will be addressed via Change Order.**\n\n**Technicians must arrive with:**\n\n- Network crimp and cut tools\n- Network tester\n- Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\n**Before leaving the site, the PTG technician must:**\n\n**Please test the audio equipment to confirm existing system works during 1st visit.**\n\n- Verify functionality of the reinstalled speaker system\n- Label installed A/V equipment as required\n- Provide basic operational overview to store management personnel\n\n**Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)**\n\n**All OFE must be onsite and in working condition prior to the scheduled installation dates. If OFE is found to be faulty, missing, or incompatible, additional labor or replacement equipment may require a Change Order.**\n\n**General Notes**\n\n- Weekend labor rates apply to the initial site visit\n- Work areas must be accessible during scheduled installation dates\n- No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval\n\n**Exclusions**\n\n**This Scope of Work does not include:**\n\n- High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.\n- Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations\n- Ceiling tile replacement\n- Structural reinforcement or seismic support\n- Millwork or cabinetry modifications\n- Patching, painting, or decorative finishing\n- Permit acquisition or fees unless otherwise noted\n- Prevailing wage or union labor unless otherwise stated\n- Lifts or scaffolding unless otherwise stated\n- Network configuration, IP provisioning, or connectivity troubleshooting beyond physical patching of the CAT5e infrastructure","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-03T07:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-03T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790361807595}
{"job":{"id":20012010,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Promotion Technology Group","title":"Sally Ignited #3350 - Burlington NC - Audio System Only- Proj #13283","description":{"html":"<p><strong>2 Trips Required</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Trip #1 - 10/3/26 - Decom. Test Existing Audio System and report any issues. Remove speakers/Mounting - package to be reused. Tie speaker wire up in ceiling to be reused.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Trip #2 - 10/14/26 - Reinstall speakers - Test Audio</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Order SOW:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Sally Ignited 3350</strong></p>\n<p><strong>System Overview:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG is not providing a screen at this location. PTG is under the impression there is an existing audio system in this space. There will be a change order for audio equipment if there are no speakers in the space when we arrive.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing audio system, including the amplifier, music player, and two ceiling speakers, will remain in service. **<u>PTG Tech MUST test equipment and provide status prior to speaker removal.**</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will provide temporary handling and reinstallation of the one affected existing ceiling speaker as required to accommodate remodeling activities and ceiling replacement by others.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>System Components</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Existing Equipment to be Reused:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Existing ceiling speakers</li>\n<li>Existing amplifier</li>\n<li>Existing OFE music player</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Client-Supplied Items:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>120V/20A duplex power outlet at display location</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Site Visit 1 – Existing Speaker Removal</strong></p>\n<p><strong>During this initial site visit, PTG technicians will:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Test Existing Equipment on site and report findings to PTG PM</li>\n<li>Remove the existing ceiling speaker(s) from the ACT ceiling</li>\n<li>Disconnect speaker wiring as required</li>\n<li>Place the speaker in a protected storage position above the ceiling grid to allow ceiling tile replacement by others</li>\n<li>Leave the existing amplifier and OFE music player undisturbed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>No new equipment installation will occur during this visit.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This visit is scheduled for weekend labor rates and has been priced accordingly.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site Visit 2 – Speaker Reinstallation</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will return to the site to complete the final installation work.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Audio System Description</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PTG will reinstall the affected existing ceiling speaker into the new ACT ceiling. Final speaker placement will be field verified during installation.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing amplifier and OFE music player will remain in place and will be reconnected to the existing speaker system.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing speaker wiring is assumed to be reusable and will be field verified during installation. Any required replacement, repair, or new speaker wiring will be addressed via Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The existing amplifier is assumed to be functional and compatible with the reinstalled speaker system. Functionality will be field verified during installation. Any required repair or replacement of the amplifier will be addressed via Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Technicians must arrive with:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Network crimp and cut tools</li>\n<li>Network tester</li>\n<li>Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before leaving the site, the PTG technician must:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please test the audio equipment to confirm existing system works during 1st visit.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify functionality of the reinstalled speaker system</li>\n<li>Label installed A/V equipment as required</li>\n<li>Provide basic operational overview to store management personnel</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>All OFE must be onsite and in working condition prior to the scheduled installation dates. If OFE is found to be faulty, missing, or incompatible, additional labor or replacement equipment may require a Change Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>General Notes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Weekend labor rates apply to the initial site visit</li>\n<li>Work areas must be accessible during scheduled installation dates</li>\n<li>No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Exclusions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This Scope of Work does not include:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.</li>\n<li>Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations</li>\n<li>Ceiling tile replacement</li>\n<li>Structural reinforcement or seismic support</li>\n<li>Millwork or cabinetry modifications</li>\n<li>Patching, painting, or decorative finishing</li>\n<li>Permit acquisition or fees unless otherwise noted</li>\n<li>Prevailing wage or union labor unless otherwise stated</li>\n<li>Lifts or scaffolding unless otherwise stated</li>\n<li>Network configuration, IP provisioning, or connectivity troubleshooting beyond physical patching of the CAT5e infrastructure</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2 Trips Required**\n\n**Trip #1 - 10/3/26 - Decom. Test Existing Audio System and report any issues. Remove speakers/Mounting - package to be reused. Tie speaker wire up in ceiling to be reused.**\n\n**Trip #2 - 10/14/26 - Reinstall speakers - Test Audio**\n\n**Order SOW:**\n\n**Sally Ignited 3350**\n\n**System Overview:**\n\n**PTG is not providing a screen at this location. PTG is under the impression there is an existing audio system in this space. There will be a change order for audio equipment if there are no speakers in the space when we arrive.**\n\n**The existing audio system, including the amplifier, music player, and two ceiling speakers, will remain in service. \\*\\*PTG Tech MUST test equipment and provide status prior to speaker removal.\\*\\***\n\n**PTG will provide temporary handling and reinstallation of the one affected existing ceiling speaker as required to accommodate remodeling activities and ceiling replacement by others.**\n\n**System Components**\n\n**Existing Equipment to be Reused:**\n\n- Existing ceiling speakers\n- Existing amplifier\n- Existing OFE music player\n\n**Client-Supplied Items:**\n\n- 120V/20A duplex power outlet at display location\n\n**Site Visit 1 – Existing Speaker Removal**\n\n**During this initial site visit, PTG technicians will:**\n\n- Test Existing Equipment on site and report findings to PTG PM\n- Remove the existing ceiling speaker(s) from the ACT ceiling\n- Disconnect speaker wiring as required\n- Place the speaker in a protected storage position above the ceiling grid to allow ceiling tile replacement by others\n- Leave the existing amplifier and OFE music player undisturbed\n\n**No new equipment installation will occur during this visit.**\n\n**This visit is scheduled for weekend labor rates and has been priced accordingly.**\n\n**Site Visit 2 – Speaker Reinstallation**\n\n**PTG will return to the site to complete the final installation work.**\n\n**Audio System Description**\n\n**PTG will reinstall the affected existing ceiling speaker into the new ACT ceiling. Final speaker placement will be field verified during installation.**\n\n**The existing amplifier and OFE music player will remain in place and will be reconnected to the existing speaker system.**\n\n**The existing speaker wiring is assumed to be reusable and will be field verified during installation. Any required replacement, repair, or new speaker wiring will be addressed via Change Order.**\n\n**The existing amplifier is assumed to be functional and compatible with the reinstalled speaker system. Functionality will be field verified during installation. Any required repair or replacement of the amplifier will be addressed via Change Order.**\n\n**Technicians must arrive with:**\n\n- Network crimp and cut tools\n- Network tester\n- Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\n**Before leaving the site, the PTG technician must:**\n\n**Please test the audio equipment to confirm existing system works during 1st visit.**\n\n- Verify functionality of the reinstalled speaker system\n- Label installed A/V equipment as required\n- Provide basic operational overview to store management personnel\n\n**Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)**\n\n**All OFE must be onsite and in working condition prior to the scheduled installation dates. If OFE is found to be faulty, missing, or incompatible, additional labor or replacement equipment may require a Change Order.**\n\n**General Notes**\n\n- Weekend labor rates apply to the initial site visit\n- Work areas must be accessible during scheduled installation dates\n- No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval\n\n**Exclusions**\n\n**This Scope of Work does not include:**\n\n- High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.\n- Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations\n- Ceiling tile replacement\n- Structural reinforcement or seismic support\n- Millwork or cabinetry modifications\n- Patching, painting, or decorative finishing\n- Permit acquisition or fees unless otherwise noted\n- Prevailing wage or union labor unless otherwise stated\n- Lifts or scaffolding unless otherwise stated\n- Network configuration, IP provisioning, or connectivity troubleshooting beyond physical patching of the CAT5e infrastructure","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T07:00","end":"2026-10-14T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-14T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790361857947}
