s, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n- These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- **Penalties Apply IF you do not**\n- PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!\n- Do Not Call **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** if you are exceeding **4 Hours Onsite**\n- Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site\n- Techs **MUST** Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site\n\n**Required Skills:** Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well\n\n**Scope of Work Overview:**\n\nTech to submit all deliverables, previous tech did not submit any.\n\n- **Scope of Work:** Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 \"Pendant Speakers\" by mounting to the ceiling. Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V–15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.\n- **Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsi