{"job":{"id":19910483,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Install Door Strike for Automated Package Locker System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER YOU AGREE TO THE ITEMS LISTED.READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME AND ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><u>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></p><p><u>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CONTACTS &amp; SUPPORT-You will be speaking directly with our customer for support.&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>BACKGROUND</u></strong></p><p>Parcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR Services is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><strong><u>WORK ORDER OVERVIEW</u></strong></p><p>Perform&nbsp;<strong>maintenance&nbsp;</strong>on&nbsp;Parcel Pending automated package locker system to ensure system is fully functional.&nbsp;<strong>Details below. (must be able to troubleshoot with Customer Support Staff)</strong></p><p><strong><u>***Please do NOT contact the property unless instructed by Parcel Pending or ASR Services.***</u></strong></p><p><strong>Regardless if tracking for parts is provided or not, please show up at your scheduled time.&nbsp;You will be paid for your time on site.</strong></p><p><strong>**Please contact Mark or Rodrigo when arriving.&nbsp;Do NOT work on lockers until you have contacted them.** (Phone numbers in confidential information)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION</u></strong></p><p>Install Door Strike for Automated Package Locker System</p><p>The following has been reported, but upon arrival you may be asked to check other issues while on site.</p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>O-Droid Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li></ul><p>General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.</p><p><strong>ASR Project Number: 887</strong></p><p><strong><u>TOOL REQUIREMENT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Corded or Cordless Oscillating Multi-tool</strong></li><li><strong>Corded or Cordless Drill</strong></li><li><strong>Drill Bit Set</strong></li><li><strong>Lineman Scissors</strong></li><li><strong>Butt Connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Wire Crimpers</strong></li><li><strong>Wire Cutters</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Multimeter</strong></li><li><strong>100’ Fish Tape</strong></li><li><strong>25’ Tape Measure</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with Camera and ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;<strong>(for checking in and out)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment).&nbsp;Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring to site the attached PDFs:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Strike Release Installation Guide V.2.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss any payment or scheduling discrepancies with the property manager or Parcel Pending (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Your time starts on site when you check in with Mark or Rodrigo.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>(Phone numbers in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call ASR immediately.</strong></li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion. Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.</strong></li><li>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</li><li>You must conduct yourself in a professional manner.</li><li>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</li><li>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support&nbsp;(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\"</strong>&nbsp;unless instructed by Technical Support.</li><li><strong>Upon completion of service, leave the Locker Key in Box 1</strong></li><li>If you are unable to open Box 1, please tape the key to the top of the Main Tower.</li><li><strong>If the property manager insists on leaving the key with them, YOU MUST call Mark or Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone numbers in Confidential Information)&nbsp;</li><li>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call ASR.</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, and name of person that released tech from site. parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion (Odroid, Add-On Board, etc.), a return label will included with part replacement.</p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain.&nbsp;Parts will need to be shipped within 24 hours.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 1 additional hour paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER YOU AGREE TO THE ITEMS LISTED.READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING.**\n\n**YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME AND ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\nThe name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.\n\nBe sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.\n\n**CONTACTS & SUPPORT-You will be speaking directly with our customer for support. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.**\n\n**BACKGROUND**\n\nParcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR Services is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**WORK ORDER OVERVIEW**\n\nPerform **maintenance** on Parcel Pending automated package locker system to ensure system is fully functional. **Details below. (must be able to troubleshoot with Customer Support Staff)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please do NOT contact the property unless instructed by Parcel Pending or ASR Services.\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Regardless if tracking for parts is provided or not, please show up at your scheduled time. You will be paid for your time on site.**\n\n**\\*\\*Please contact Mark or Rodrigo when arriving. Do NOT work on lockers until you have contacted them.\\*\\* (Phone numbers in confidential information)**\n\n**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION**\n\nInstall Door Strike for Automated Package Locker System\n\nThe following has been reported, but upon arrival you may be asked to check other issues while on site.\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- O-Droid Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n\nGeneral Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.\n\n**ASR Project Number: 887**\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Corded or Cordless Oscillating Multi-tool**\n- **Corded or Cordless Drill**\n- **Drill Bit Set**\n- **Lineman Scissors**\n- **Butt Connectors**\n- **Wire Crimpers**\n- **Wire Cutters**\n- **Digital Multimeter**\n- **100’ Fish Tape**\n- **25’ Tape Measure**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **Smart Phone with Camera and ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** **(for checking in and out)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring to site the attached PDFs:**\n\n- Strike Release Installation Guide V.2.pdf\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss any payment or scheduling discrepancies with the property manager or Parcel Pending (NO exceptions)**\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **Your time starts on site when you check in with Mark or Rodrigo.** (Phone numbers in Confidential Information)\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call ASR immediately.**\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion. Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.**\n- You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.\n- You must conduct yourself in a professional manner.\n- All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.\n- Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\"** unless instructed by Technical Support.\n- **Upon completion of service, leave the Locker Key in Box 1**\n- If you are unable to open Box 1, please tape the key to the top of the Main Tower.\n- **If the property manager insists on leaving the key with them, YOU MUST call Mark or Rodrigo.** (Phone numbers in Confidential Information)\n- If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call ASR.\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, and name of person that released tech from site. parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\nIf any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion (Odroid, Add-On Board, etc.), a return label will included with part replacement.\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain. Parts will need to be shipped within 24 hours.**\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 1 additional hour paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by ASR.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T09:30","end":"2026-09-28T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790366068483}
{"job":{"id":20037688,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"Logitech conference room install","description":{"html":"<strong>In Scope</strong><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>Logitech Conference Room Buildout&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Working with customer remote support disconnect current server</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place devices in customer provided boxes when applicable&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Seal and label packages when applicable&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place server in customer designated location&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Another vendor will be responsible for server disposal</li><li>Notate equipment quantity, type, model, and serial</li><li>Take photos before and after decommissioning</li><li>For relocations and replacements tech will ensure all cabling is labeled or will label all cables at both ends to ensure devices are reconnected/connected properly&nbsp;</li><li>Unpack and inspect customer provided server</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Some locations may have two servers</li><li>Confirmation and review of accurate inventory</li><li>Confirm all necessary site-specific mounting materials are present</li><li>Physical installation of mounting bracket or hardware to device</li><li>Installation of wire manager, if applicable&nbsp;</li><li>Identify location for installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Utilize elevation or customer identified location if provided</li><li>Physical installation of device utilizing industry standard methods and best practices</li><li>Route and connect power to the power source</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Utilize cable management systems if present</li><li>Labeling of the devices per customer standards and naming schemes when applicable&nbsp;</li><li>Connect Ethernet cables in accordance with port mappings when provided</li><li>Power up the device</li><li>Clean up workspace and dunnage&nbsp;</li></ul><br><p><strong><u>Additional Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong>%description.html%</strong></p><p><br></p>Customer Responsibilities&nbsp;<p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide site details&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Location of server</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Special environment conditions&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rack type&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Provide back-end support for escalated issues</li><li>Provide port mapping when required</li><li>Provide rack elevation when specific location is required</li><li>Provide naming schemes when required</li><li>Provide a waste receptacle for dunnage</li></ul>&nbsp;Assumptions<p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Velocity assumes that installation location such as a rack or cabinet has available space and power is available for the devices to be installed</li><li>Standard construction exists</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sheetrock and metal or wood studs</li><li>Ceilings are 14 ft in height</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ceiling heights higher than 14 ft may require a lift</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Lifts will be billed as actuals and additional fees may apply</li><li>Velocity assumes that the network equipment is pre-configured</li><li>Assumes technician will have a laptop and console cable&nbsp;</li><li>Assumes Velocity to provide the following materials:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Labels&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Velcro&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Grounding Kit&nbsp;</li></ul><br><strong>Deliverables</strong><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photos of completed installation (all photos must be labeled with site name and description)&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photo of rack/cabinet before installing equipment or before decommissioning/removing any equipment&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photos at a distance showing cable management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photo close-up to show labeling&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photos showing devices powered on&nbsp;</strong></p>&nbsp;Out of Scope<p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Velocity will consider the following tasks as out of scope unless specific instructions are provided by the customer accompanied by Customer IT support</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Configuring of the devices</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Troubleshooting ISP connectivity issues</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Troubleshooting misconfigurations</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Troubleshooting Customer IT personnel remote access issues</li><li>Removing any&nbsp;existing equipment or debris from site</li><li>Provision of materials unless specifically requested</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cable manager</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Patch Panels</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Racks&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If these items are needed the AE will provide a separate BOM&nbsp;</li><li>Providing waste receptacle</li></ul>","markdown":"**In Scope****Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace**\n\n﻿Logitech Conference Room Buildout\n\n- Working with customer remote support disconnect current server\n- Place devices in customer provided boxes when applicable\n- Seal and label packages when applicable\n- Place server in customer designated location\n- Another vendor will be responsible for server disposal\n- Notate equipment quantity, type, model, and serial\n- Take photos before and after decommissioning\n- For relocations and replacements tech will ensure all cabling is labeled or will label all cables at both ends to ensure devices are reconnected/connected properly\n- Unpack and inspect customer provided server\n- Some locations may have two servers\n- Confirmation and review of accurate inventory\n- Confirm all necessary site-specific mounting materials are present\n- Physical installation of mounting bracket or hardware to device\n- Installation of wire manager, if applicable\n- Identify location for installation\n- Utilize elevation or customer identified location if provided\n- Physical installation of device utilizing industry standard methods and best practices\n- Route and connect power to the power source\n- Utilize cable management systems if present\n- Labeling of the devices per customer standards and naming schemes when applicable\n- Connect Ethernet cables in accordance with port mappings when provided\n- Power up the device\n- Clean up workspace and dunnage\n\n  \n**Additional Information:**\n\n**%description.html%**\n\nCustomer Responsibilities **Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace**\n\n**· Provide site details**\n\n**o Location of server**\n\n**o Special environment conditions**\n\n**o Rack type**\n\n- Provide back-end support for escalated issues\n- Provide port mapping when required\n- Provide rack elevation when specific location is required\n- Provide naming schemes when required\n- Provide a waste receptacle for dunnage\n\n Assumptions**Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace**\n\n- Velocity assumes that installation location such as a rack or cabinet has available space and power is available for the devices to be installed\n- Standard construction exists\n- Sheetrock and metal or wood studs\n- Ceilings are 14 ft in height\n- Ceiling heights higher than 14 ft may require a lift\n- Lifts will be billed as actuals and additional fees may apply\n- Velocity assumes that the network equipment is pre-configured\n- Assumes technician will have a laptop and console cable\n- Assumes Velocity to provide the following materials:\n- Labels\n- Velcro\n- Tie Wraps\n- Grounding Kit\n\n  \n**Deliverables****Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace**\n\n**· Photos of completed installation (all photos must be labeled with site name and description)**\n\n**o Photo of rack/cabinet before installing equipment or before decommissioning/removing any equipment**\n\n**o Photos at a distance showing cable management**\n\n**o Photo close-up to show labeling**\n\n**o Photos showing devices powered on**\n\n Out of Scope**Network Equipment Installation, Relocate, Decommission, Replace**\n\n- Velocity will consider the following tasks as out of scope unless specific instructions are provided by the customer accompanied by Customer IT support\n- Configuring of the devices\n- Troubleshooting ISP connectivity issues\n- Troubleshooting misconfigurations\n- Troubleshooting Customer IT personnel remote access issues\n- Removing any existing equipment or debris from site\n- Provision of materials unless specifically requested\n- Cable manager\n- Patch Panels\n- Racks\n- If these items are needed the AE will provide a separate BOM\n- Providing waste receptacle","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T09:00","end":"2026-09-28T19:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":600,"max":600},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":true,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"ELIGIBLE"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},