{"job":{"id":20037824,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2724881","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Dishwasher : Brand Unknown : 1</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\">%description.html%</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n- **Dishwasher : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n%description.html%\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T08:00","end":"2026-09-25T09:00","latestStart":"2026-09-25T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":47},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/25/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790367244100}
{"job":{"id":20038018,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Go Back to uninstall Starlink and for cut over at Comfort & Affordable Care Agency LLC","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.</p>\n<p><strong>Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>SEND TECH TO UNINSTALL STARLINK AND FOR CUT OVER TO SPECTRUM.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Punctuality &amp; Assignment Rules</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.</li>\n<li>Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.</li>\n<li>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill, level, and stud finder</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>6-pin RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.\n\n**Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs**\n\n***SEND TECH TO UNINSTALL STARLINK AND FOR CUT OVER TO SPECTRUM.***\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).\n\nPunctuality & Assignment Rules\n\n- Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.\n- Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.\n- If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill, level, and stud finder\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- 6-pin RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T09:00","end":"2026-09-29T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790367619967}
{"job":{"id":20038093,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Product Protection Solutions Inc","title":"EAS System Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong><u>This job needs to get Scheduled Ahead of Time, if a Technician gets assigned, they CANNOT just show up to the store. No expenses will be approved unless work was scheduled ahead of time.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Tech will need to work with tech support to troubleshoot and connect the stores system to the network. Test and Tune all EAS Systems and network to gain connectivity while following the instructions of our tech support to get device back online. Take pictures of work area before and after any work is done.</u></strong></li><li>YOU&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>HAVE A MINI USB CABLE. NOT MICRO!</li><li>YOU <strong>MUST </strong>HAVE A WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM!</li><li>Connecting remotely to PPS support team</li><li>Walking repeatedly through EAS detection field and relaying detection results to PPS support team.</li><li>Upon arrival, tech will contact store manager to explain purpose of service call and to obtain anti-theft security tags (photo “RFID tag”) for use during system testing.&nbsp;Additionally, contact PPS support for detailed instructions and remote log-in and determination on best approach to connect to the system.</li><li>Upon completion and prior to leaving site, tech will obtain signature from manager on sign-off document and upload to Field Nation.</li><li>EAS system driver Link: https://qdppstg.sharepoint.com/:f:/s/FieldTechWorkspace/EtES6L5R7-1NsLurh2MDh-EBxqS7qrzezJZ-LEzBjQTrmQ?e=qcIbJb</li><li>NOTE:&nbsp;Driver must be downloaded directly to computer without using flash drive or other removable media.&nbsp;</li><li>TeamViewer Download Link:&nbsp;TeamViewer Windows Download for Remote Desktop access and collaboration</li><li>It is incumbent on technician to arrive at job site prepared, having met all requirements.&nbsp;Time spent installing drivers, downloading TeamViewer or otherwise seeking out required hardware will not be compensated.</li><li><strong><u>No additional expenses will be approved unless included as part of a counter offer, or approved while on the job site.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"- **This job needs to get Scheduled Ahead of Time, if a Technician gets assigned, they CANNOT just show up to the store. No expenses will be approved unless work was scheduled ahead of time.**\n- **Tech will need to work with tech support to troubleshoot and connect the stores system to the network. Test and Tune all EAS Systems and network to gain connectivity while following the instructions of our tech support to get device back online. Take pictures of work area before and after any work is done.**\n- YOU **MUST** HAVE A MINI USB CABLE. NOT MICRO!\n- YOU **MUST** HAVE A WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM!\n- Connecting remotely to PPS support team\n- Walking repeatedly through EAS detection field and relaying detection results to PPS support team.\n- Upon arrival, tech will contact store manager to explain purpose of service call and to obtain anti-theft security tags (photo “RFID tag”) for use during system testing. Additionally, contact PPS support for detailed instructions and remote log-in and determination on best approach to connect to the system.\n- Upon completion and prior to leaving site, tech will obtain signature from manager on sign-off document and upload to Field Nation.\n- EAS system driver Link: <https://qdppstg.sharepoint.com/:f:/s/FieldTechWorkspace/EtES6L5R7-1NsLurh2MDh-EBxqS7qrzezJZ-LEzBjQTrmQ?e=qcIbJb>\n- NOTE: Driver must be downloaded directly to computer without using flash drive or other removable media.\n- TeamViewer Download Link: TeamViewer Windows Download for Remote Desktop access and collaboration\n- It is incumbent on technician to arrive at job site prepared, having met all requirements. Time spent installing drivers, downloading TeamViewer or otherwise seeking out required hardware will not be compensated.\n- **No additional expenses will be approved unless included as part of a counter offer, or approved while on the job site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T08:00","end":"2026-10-02T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":175,"max":175},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $175 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790367677358}
{"job":{"id":19864227,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Handheld Scanner upgrade - Tech 2","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p><strong><u>The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The registers must be shut down</u>,</strong> then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,<strong><u>THEN</u></strong> reboot the register.</p>\n<p>This is in the doc., page 6</p>\n<p>This should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes to ATR process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)</strong></li>\n<li>If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware</li>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.<em>﻿</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet <strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in <strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong> and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><del>************</del></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>****** * *** ********* ******* *********** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** ****** ********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a<del>********</del>representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\n**The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.**\n\n**The registers must be shut down,** then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,**THEN** reboot the register.\n\nThis is in the doc., page 6\n\nThis should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n- Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n\nChanges to ATR process:\n\n- **Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)**\n- If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware\n- **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n- Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet\n- No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.*﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T08:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:45"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":201},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":5.75,"distance":44},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":345,"estHours":5.75,"travelExpense":70,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790367943207}
{"job":{"id":20039204,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Site Survey for Automated Locker System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.</strong></p><p>Overview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.</p><p>Background: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Main Contacts</u></strong></p><p><strong>Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)</strong></p><p>Please call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.</p><ul><li><strong><u>We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.</u></strong></li></ul><p>Tech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</p><p>Indoor Zhilai -&nbsp;-</p><p>HIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:</strong></p><p>Technician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.</p><p>Work order may NOT be rescheduled.&nbsp;Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.&nbsp;Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.</strong></li><li><strong>AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.</strong></li><li><strong>Stud Finder</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;(for checking in and out)</li><li><strong>Digital Camera</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attachment:</strong></p><p>0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf&nbsp;- Print and bring to site.</p><p>=======================</p><p>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</p><p>DIRECTIONS</p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location</li><li>Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of room where locker will be installed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.</li></ul><ol><li>Take the photos outline in the instructions.</li><li>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</li><li>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out</li><li><strong>Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</strong></li><li><strong>Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.</strong></li></ol><p>=======================</p><p>Site Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.**\n\nOverview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.\n\nBackground: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**Main Contacts**\n\n**Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)**\n\nPlease call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.\n\n- **We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.**\n- **For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.**\n\nTech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3\n\n**READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\nTechnician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.\n\nWork order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum**\n- **Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.**\n- **AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.**\n- **Stud Finder**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** (for checking in and out)\n- **Digital Camera**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachment:**\n\n0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf - Print and bring to site.\n\n=======================\n\nREAD THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location\n2. Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:\n\n- Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.\n- Measurements of room where locker will be installed.\n- Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.\n\n1. Take the photos outline in the instructions.\n2. Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.\n3. Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out\n4. **Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n5. **Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.**\n\n=======================\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T10:00","end":"2026-09-28T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790370618598}
{"job":{"id":20039412,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Onsitework LLC","title":"TV Repair","description":{"html":"<p>Note: Take a Print out of the attached file and get sign on it by EU using pen(Mandatory)</p><p>Issue: Samsung\t65\" Half screen is black, 6 yrs, on table</p><p>To fix a Samsung 65\" TV with a half-black screen, start by performing a hard power reset and checking your external source connections</p><p>Quick Troubleshooting Steps</p><ul><li><strong>Power Cycle:</strong> Unplug the TV from the wall, press and hold the physical power button on the TV for 15 seconds, wait a few minutes, and plug it back in. </li><li><strong>Check the Menu:</strong> Press the <strong>Home</strong> or <strong>Menu</strong> button on your remote. If the black section covers the built-in TV menu, the issue is internal. If the menu looks normal, the problem is likely an external device or cable. </li><li><strong>Inspect HDMI Connections:</strong> Unplug your HDMI cables, clean the ports, and reconnect them securely to an alternate HDMI port on the TV. Try a different cable to rule out a faulty wire. </li><li><strong>Adjust Settings:</strong> Turn off features like <strong>Local Dimming</strong> (under Expert Picture Settings) and <strong>Brightness Optimisation</strong> (under Power and Energy Saving), as these can occasionally cause uneven display panels or dim zones. </li><li><strong>Run a Picture Test:</strong> Navigate to Samsung Support Guide via your settings menu (<span class=\"ql-font-monospace\">Support</span> &gt; <span class=\"ql-font-monospace\">Self Diagnosis</span> &gt; <span class=\"ql-font-monospace\">Picture Test</span>) to check if the panel itself registers the display error</li></ul><p>It is mandatory to open the back panel if any hardware issue is suspected. Clear pictures of the faulty component must be taken, and proper testing using a multimeter must be performed.</p><p>If a hardware fault is confirmed, you are required to clearly mention the exact faulty part along with the TV model number in the work order sheet and submitted in fieldnation with in 24 hours. Failure to follow these instructions will be considered incomplete work.</p>","markdown":"Note: Take a Print out of the attached file and get sign on it by EU using pen(Mandatory)\n\nIssue: Samsung 65\" Half screen is black, 6 yrs, on table\n\nTo fix a Samsung 65\" TV with a half-black screen, start by performing a hard power reset and checking your external source connections\n\nQuick Troubleshooting Steps\n\n- **Power Cycle:** Unplug the TV from the wall, press and hold the physical power button on the TV for 15 seconds, wait a few minutes, and plug it back in.\n- **Check the Menu:** Press the **Home** or **Menu** button on your remote. If the black section covers the built-in TV menu, the issue is internal. If the menu looks normal, the problem is likely an external device or cable.\n- **Inspect HDMI Connections:** Unplug your HDMI cables, clean the ports, and reconnect them securely to an alternate HDMI port on the TV. Try a different cable to rule out a faulty wire.\n- **Adjust Settings:** Turn off features like **Local Dimming** (under Expert Picture Settings) and **Brightness Optimisation** (under Power and Energy Saving), as these can occasionally cause uneven display panels or dim zones.\n- **Run a Picture Test:** Navigate to Samsung Support Guide via your settings menu (Support > Self Diagnosis > Picture Test) to check if the panel itself registers the display error\n\nIt is mandatory to open the back panel if any hardware issue is suspected. Clear pictures of the faulty component must be taken, and proper testing using a multimeter must be performed.\n\nIf a hardware fault is confirmed, you are required to clearly mention the exact faulty part along with the TV model number in the work order sheet and submitted in fieldnation with in 24 hours. Failure to follow these instructions will be considered incomplete work.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-26T09:00","end":"2026-09-26T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-26T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":70},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":68},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790371692381}
{"job":{"id":20039568,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CPT Network Solutions, Inc.","title":"Qbit Player Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>High Level Overview</u></strong></p><p>Technicians&nbsp;are&nbsp;to&nbsp;replace&nbsp;the existing Mood Media device with the Qbit audio play system.</p><p>This job is expected to take 30 minutes to one hour.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools to Bring to Site:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Standard&nbsp;technician&nbsp;toolset</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Phone</li><li>Spare Cat6 cables (3ft and 6ft)</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Butt Set</li><li>Punch-Down Tool and Wire Strippers</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check-In&nbsp;and&nbsp;Coordination</li><li>Remove&nbsp;Mood Media device</li><li>Mount and connect Qbit device</li><li>Call QSIC to confirm connectivity</li><li>Test audio in store</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables</u></strong></p><ol><li>Picture&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;QSIC&nbsp;player&nbsp;installed</li><li>Photos&nbsp;of&nbsp;Completed&nbsp;Install</li></ol>","markdown":"**High Level Overview**\n\nTechnicians are to replace the existing Mood Media device with the Qbit audio play system.\n\nThis job is expected to take 30 minutes to one hour.\n\n**Required Tools to Bring to Site:**\n\n1. Standard technician toolset\n2. Label Maker\n3. Screwdrivers\n4. Phone\n5. Spare Cat6 cables (3ft and 6ft)\n6. Cable tester\n7. Butt Set\n8. Punch-Down Tool and Wire Strippers\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1. Check-In and Coordination\n2. Remove Mood Media device\n3. Mount and connect Qbit device\n4. Call QSIC to confirm connectivity\n5. Test audio in store\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n1. Picture of the new QSIC player installed\n2. Photos of Completed Install","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T08:00","end":"2026-10-05T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHou