ludes:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>DSI Technical Installation Guide</li><li>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan</li><li>Service Acceptance Form (SAF)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Payment Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Payment Amounts:</u> </strong> $130.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate:</u></strong> $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15-minute increments. <strong>T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.</strong></p><p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain <u>pre-approval</u> for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Store Revisits:</u></strong> Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):</u></strong></p><p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. <strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Any site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).</p><p><strong><u>Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe</li></ul><p><strong><u>SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:</u></strong><em>&nbsp;All below dates are from the day of the installation date.</em></p><ul><li>1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​</li><li>2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.</li><li>The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- submit the outstanding item(s) or,</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</li><li><strong>The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.</strong> <strong>30% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.</strong></li><li>5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.</li></ul><p>- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p><p>- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p><p>- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Expectations &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Allowed: </strong> Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts</p><p><strong>Not Allowed:</strong> Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).</p><p><strong><u>Presentation:</u></strong></p><p>Technicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.</p><p><strong><u>Travel Arrangements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.</li><li>Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.</li><li>Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Deductions:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.</p>","markdown":"**Scope of Services**: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n**Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.**\n\n**Pre-Installation inventory** of new hardware at the store location.\n\n**Installation Steps:** Installation must be followed step by step using the Technical Installation Guide. A high-level overview of the steps are as follows:\n\nReplace existing HP printer on fixed registers. In most cases, the existing printer cable can be reused to power the new printer and provide the registers with connectivity. An Ethernet cable will need to be run from the front switch to each new fixed register printer.\n\n- (Registers that have the H400 receipt printer prior to install will need to have USB cables run for the new printer).\n- The lowest numbered printers will be installed on the fixed registers.\n\nHave manager test all fixed registers – should be completed prior to store open.\n\nReplace the existing receipt printer at each docked mobile register.\n\n- Proceeding numbered printers will be installed at the docked mobile stations.\n- Spare mobile printer(s) with a power bank will be the last in the numbered order.\n\nReplace the generic roll of paper included and install the brand specific paper from the existing printers.\n\nSwap bottom and back panels for front printer (if necessary).\n\nHave manager test all wireless printers using store iPad.\n\nPackage the de-installed HP and Zebra printers for return and place the return label on the box and move to a location designated by the MOD.\n\nCall End Client to validate the installed hardware and check out.\n\nUpload all deliverables to Direct Source via mobile App.\n\n**Check out with Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site** to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code on the SAF (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\nSubmittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due no later than **24 hours** of site completion to the Direct Source Portal.\n\n- Photos should be uploaded while on site, however, if this is not possible photos must be uploaded within 24 hours.\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools & Hardware:**\n\nTechnician is required to have the following list of equipment and materials that will be used throughout the Technician's agreed upon assignment to this project.\n\nStandard Technician Toolkit (screwdrivers, drill with full bit set, cutting knife, scissors, electrical tape, packaging tape, etc.)\n\nCell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier\n\nPrinted copy of the Technical Guide and any other required project paperwork. Digital copy of the guide is acceptable; must be on tablet or laptop.\n\n- The DSI \"SAF\" must be printed unless you have a way to fill it out and have the manager sign it digitally.\n\nSharpie\n\nBlack Velcro\n\n**Spare Patch Cables (20-25 ft) – enough to match the register counts at each location; to be supplied by Technician and will be reimbursed if site requires its use**\n\nCanned Air (or mini vac) to use when needed\n\n**Power Strip – to be supplied by Technician and will be reimbursed if site requires its use**\n\n**Project Preparation/ Orientation:**\n\n**The Technician who will be onsite**, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. **Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.**\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting**: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).\n\n- Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.\n- Photos need to include a notecard or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. \\[EX: J. Doe, #4321 04/08/2026\\]\n- Required deliverables include the following:\n\n\\- Completed Service Acceptance Form (SAF)\n\n\\- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:**\n\nDirect Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. **Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.**\n\n**Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:**\n\n- DSI Technical Installation Guide\n- Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan\n- Service Acceptance Form (SAF)\n\n**Payment Information:**\n\n**Payment Amounts:**  $130.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate:** $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15-minute increments. **T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.**\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits:** Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\nAny site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).\n\n**Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:**\n\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&M + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe\n\n**SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:** *All below dates are from the day of the installation date.*\n\n- 1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​\n- 2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.\n- The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:\n- - submit the outstanding item(s) or,\n- - return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n- **The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.** **30% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.**\n- 5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.\n\n\\- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\n\\- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\n\\- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.\n\n**Expectations & Requirements:**\n\nDirect Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n**Allowed:**  Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts\n\n**Not Allowed:** Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).\n\n**Presentation:**\n\nTechnicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.\n\n**Travel Arrangements:**\n\n- Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.\n- Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.\n- Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.\n- Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.\n\n**Deductions:**\n\nDirect Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":130},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790372732400}
{"job":{"id":20039895,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - APs Down","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Need to align the tech Mon-Fri, 7AM EST.</p><p>Required 19ft lift.</p><p><br></p><p>Requirement Details:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Impacted Device: Aruba 635</p><p>2. Location: Food Lion - 2101 Princeton</p><p>3. Problem Statement: std2101ap05 , std2101ap01 , std2101ap90 , std2101ap03 showing down Need to take console of aps.</p><p><br></p><p>4. What troubleshooting has been completed: Noticed that std2101ap05 , std2101ap01 , std2101ap90 , std2101ap03 showing down Need to take console of aps.</p><p>Verified switch port configuration, tried to bounce the respective ports with no success</p><p><br></p><p>Aps are showing online in switch with ip but not in central . Not able to take console .</p><p><br></p><p>Console cable is required and may be need to shift aps from stack 1 to different stack</p><p><br></p><p>5. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:</p><p>• Laptop with good internet connection and teams installed. laptop should be able to take console.</p><p>• Compatible console cable, short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required.</p><p><br></p><p>6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:</p><p>• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.</p><p>• Need to run the cable test.</p><p>• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.</p><p>• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.</p><p>• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.</p><p>• Need to check the network connectivity once the APs are online.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Need to align the tech Mon-Fri, 7AM EST.\n\nRequired 19ft lift.\n\nRequirement Details:\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: Aruba 635\n\n2\\. Location: Food Lion - 2101 Princeton\n\n3\\. Problem Statement: std2101ap05 , std2101ap01 , std2101ap90 , std2101ap03 showing down Need to take console of aps.\n\n4\\. What troubleshooting has been completed: Noticed that std2101ap05 , std2101ap01 , std2101ap90 , std2101ap03 showing down Need to take console of aps.\n\nVerified switch port configuration, tried to bounce the respective ports with no success\n\nAps are showing online in switch with ip but not in central . Not able to take console .\n\nConsole cable is required and may be need to shift aps from stack 1 to different stack\n\n5\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:\n\n• Laptop with good internet connection and teams installed. laptop should be able to take console.\n\n• Compatible console cable, short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required.\n\n6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:\n\n• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.\n\n• Need to run the cable test.\n\n• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.\n\n• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.\n\n• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.\n\n• Need to check the network connectivity once the APs are online.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T07:00","end":"2026-09-29T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":43},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790374186797}
