{"job":{"id":20039984,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Decommissioning of Workstations, Servers, Network Equipment, and/or Related Assets - P15-Southern Pines-MACD Closure","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Technician will work with the Site Contact and Field Services Support Engineer to complete a Site Shutdown / Decommission, including packing and preparing end user and network equipment for shipment pickup per engineering direction.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Technician must complete the following:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Aptos;\">﻿</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Description of Problem: Please bring 3-4 med size boxes, bubble wrap and packing tape. You will need to pack and ship end user equipment and network gear. Please leave the rack and cables there. End user equipment may include, tablets, laptops, all cisco phones, MiFi&#39;s, cell phones, IGEL&#39;s and Dell 24&quot; monitors with HDMI ports.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Network gear includes:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Firewall-FGT81FTK22013802</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">AP-PU231FTH22012026</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Switch-S424EFTF21002581</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Forti-Extender-FX511FTQ21001460</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No one will be on site use door code: Press 2&amp;4 together and then 3 and then Unlock</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PM: <del>****** ****** ** ************ ** ************ ****************************</del></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>DECOMMISSION / PACK AND PREP FOR SHIPMENT PICKUP:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Bring 3-4 medium size boxes, packing tape, and bubble wrap to pack and prepare end user and network equipment for shipment pickup.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">End user equipment may include laptops, tablets, monitors, desk phones, conference phones, keyboards, mice, docking stations, and related peripherals.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Coordinate with Support to ensure all network equipment is properly turned down prior to removal.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Remove required network equipment as directed (Firewall, switches, access points, Forti Extender, etc.).</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Document all equipment model numbers and serial numbers.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Securely pack all equipment to prevent damage during shipment pickup.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Prepare assets for transport or decommission per </span><del>*******</del><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">-provided instructions.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Ensure equipment is boxed and prepared for shipment pickup as directed.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>TOOL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">See attached document - READ ME - </span><em style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Work Order Tool Requirements</em><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> (Available to Review </span><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">BEFORE</strong><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> assignment)</span></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>DELIVERABLE REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Create an itemized list of equipment and serial numbers packed into each box.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Take photos of each device serial number and label accordingly.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Take photos of each box with labels visible and document which equipment is in each box in the work order.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>CHECK-IN PROCEDURES:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Upon arrival at site, technician is required to complete the following check-in steps in this order:</span></p><ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Call Field Services Support Engineer - </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ****** ** ************ ** ************ ****************************</del></strong></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Provider Reference Number - </span>00735263 P15</li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Contact the Site Point of Contact (Building Access) - </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ****** ** ************ ** ************ ****************************</del></strong></li></ol><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">WARNING</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">: </span><em style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Failure to complete the check-in steps will result in delay in approval of work order.</em></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>REIMBURSEMENT REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">See attachment - READ ME</strong><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> - </span><em style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Required Reimbursement Process Acknowledgment</em><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> (Available to Review </span><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">BEFORE</strong><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> assignment)</span></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>WORK ORDER COMPLIANCE:</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">See attachment - READ ME </strong><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">- </span><em style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Work Order Compliance Acknowledgement</em><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> (Available to Review </span><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">BEFORE</strong><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"> assignment)</span></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>WORK ORDER REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Check in and out in Work Order Platform while onsite. No exceptions.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">One site visit per work order. Do not log multiple visits on a single work order.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">If a revisit is required:</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Close out the current work order</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Contact Work Order Manager (<del>*******</del>) immediately</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Any onsite issues must be reported to the Work Order Manager (<del>*******</del>) immediately.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Do not mention work order platform to site staff or customers.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>SITE REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Government-issued photo ID required for entry</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">All technician names must be submitted in advance</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Check-in with site contacts representing <del>******* ***** ********</del></span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Technicians are required to arrive fully equipped (customer tools not permitted)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Business-casual attire and professional conduct are required</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><u>FINAL REMINDER:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">Review the Confidential Section, Policies and Procedures, and ALL attachments associated with this work order prior to performing the dispatch.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\">If any attached documents and/or information within the Work Order Description and/or Confidential Section conflicts with any policies or procedures listed elsewhere in this work order, the attached documents and/or information in the Work Order Description/Confidential Section take precedence.</span></p>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\nTechnician will work with the Site Contact and Field Services Support Engineer to complete a Site Shutdown / Decommission, including packing and preparing end user and network equipment for shipment pickup per engineering direction.\n\nTechnician must complete the following:\n\n﻿\n\n**Description of Problem: Please bring 3-4 med size boxes, bubble wrap and packing tape. You will need to pack and ship end user equipment and network gear. Please leave the rack and cables there. End user equipment may include, tablets, laptops, all cisco phones, MiFi's, cell phones, IGEL's and Dell 24\" monitors with HDMI ports.**\n\n**Network gear includes:**\n\n**Firewall-FGT81FTK22013802**\n\n**AP-PU231FTH22012026**\n\n**Switch-S424EFTF21002581**\n\n**Forti-Extender-FX511FTQ21001460**\n\n**No one will be on site use door code: Press 2&4 together and then 3 and then Unlock**\n\n**PM: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**DECOMMISSION / PACK AND PREP FOR SHIPMENT PICKUP:**\n\n- Bring 3-4 medium size boxes, packing tape, and bubble wrap to pack and prepare end user and network equipment for shipment pickup.\n- End user equipment may include laptops, tablets, monitors, desk phones, conference phones, keyboards, mice, docking stations, and related peripherals.\n- Coordinate with Support to ensure all network equipment is properly turned down prior to removal.\n- Remove required network equipment as directed (Firewall, switches, access points, Forti Extender, etc.).\n- Document all equipment model numbers and serial numbers.\n- Securely pack all equipment to prevent damage during shipment pickup.\n- Prepare assets for transport or decommission per \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*-provided instructions.\n- Ensure equipment is boxed and prepared for shipment pickup as directed.\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENTS:**\n\nSee attached document - READ ME - *Work Order Tool Requirements* (Available to Review **BEFORE** assignment)\n\n**DELIVERABLE REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n- Create an itemized list of equipment and serial numbers packed into each box.\n- Take photos of each device serial number and label accordingly.\n- Take photos of each box with labels visible and document which equipment is in each box in the work order.\n\n**CHECK-IN PROCEDURES:**\n\nUpon arrival at site, technician is required to complete the following check-in steps in this order:\n\n1. Call Field Services Support Engineer - **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n2. Provider Reference Number - 00735263 P15\n3. Contact the Site Point of Contact (Building Access) - **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nWARNING: *Failure to complete the check-in steps will result in delay in approval of work order.*\n\n**REIMBURSEMENT REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n**See attachment - READ ME** - *Required Reimbursement Process Acknowledgment* (Available to Review **BEFORE** assignment)\n\n**WORK ORDER COMPLIANCE:**\n\n**See attachment - READ ME** - *Work Order Compliance Acknowledgement* (Available to Review **BEFORE** assignment)\n\n**WORK ORDER REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n- Check in and out in Work Order Platform while onsite. No exceptions.\n- One site visit per work order. Do not log multiple visits on a single work order.\n- If a revisit is required:\n- Close out the current work order\n- Contact Work Order Manager (\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*) immediately\n- Any onsite issues must be reported to the Work Order Manager (\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*) immediately.\n- Do not mention work order platform to site staff or customers.\n\n**SITE REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians are required to arrive fully equipped (customer tools not permitted)\n- Business-casual attire and professional conduct are required\n\n**FINAL REMINDER:**\n\nReview the Confidential Section, Policies and Procedures, and ALL attachments associated with this work order prior to performing the dispatch.\n\nIf any attached documents and/or information within the Work Order Description and/or Confidential Section conflicts with any policies or procedures listed elsewhere in this work order, the attached documents and/or information in the Work Order Description/Confidential Section take precedence.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T10:00","end":"2026-10-05T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":61},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 (countered: $300) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS