{"job":{"id":"9347070233","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Cheesecake Factory - 8AM install CPE, complete cutover","description":"<p>Granite install a New CPE (Customer Premises Equipment) to the customer’s location with pre-configured services for Direct Internet Access (DIA) and will cut the customer over to the new CPE.</p><p><br></p><p>Upon arrival the Granite Technician will review the scope of work with the local Cheesecake Factory Manager.</p><p>Site work will take place on Cheesecake backboard but in certain instances if equipment is actually in a Manager's rack, technician is to discontinue work, take pictures, and report back to Granite so we can report back to Cheesecake factory for direction</p><p><br></p><p>The Granite Technician will take site photos of the Cheesecake Factory installation areas.</p><p>General Summary: We remove the intermediary Granite CPE from between the Grid Jack in the customer’s suite and Cheesecake’s Equipment to provide DIA directly from the Grid Jack.</p><p><br></p><p>Process: Schedule a coordinated hotcut:</p><p>a. All changes will be made during the coordinated hotcut.</p><p>b. Public Ips will be provided on the bridge.</p><p><br></p><p>Required Reps:</p><p>i. Granite IW</p><p>ii. Granite Network infrastructure Representative</p><p>iii. Cheesecake Engineer with Remote Access to make config changes to their equipment onsite.</p><p><br></p><p>Config Change process:</p><p>a. Default the IDF port the service is built too.</p><p>b. Run Grid Service Activation workflow on the existing IDF/port</p><p>i. This workflow takes 2-5 minutes.</p><p>ii. Workflow allocates Public Ips</p><p><br></p><p>IW:</p><p>a. Tech disconnects the Granite CPE that is currently connected to the Grid Jack.</p><p>b. Take cable from Customer LAN Port on Granite CPE that was just connected and plug into Grid Jack.</p><p>c. The above work can be performed simultaneously as a Granite Network infrastructure Representative is working on the config changes to minimize downtime.</p><p><br></p><p>Cheesecake Engineer:</p><p>a. Will need to re-configure their interface that is connecting to the Grid Jack with the new Public IP range allocated from the Grid Service Activaiton work flow.</p><p>b. Confirm the correct interface on their port is up and confirm they have internet access.</p><p><br></p><p>Down Time:</p><p>a. This entire process will probably take 5-10 minutes depending on how fast the IW tech can remove the Granite CPE and plug Cheesecake’s Equipment into the Grid Jack.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":14.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":35,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790533637190}
{"job":{"id":20041983,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"IW Technologies","title":"Variety Wholesalers Pin Pad Refresh","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Summary of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>IW Technologies is looking for a technician to complete a pin pad replacement at a local retailer. The scope includes replacing the existing pin pads, installing the switch, configuring and testing the devices. Please record each pin pad serial number with its corresponding lane number. Pack the existing pin pads and Verifone cables in the original tamper-safe white packaging, and drop the box off at FedEx.</p>\n<p><strong>QTY of Lanes: 4</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID</li>\n<li>Velcro</li>\n<li>1.25\" hole saw w/drill</li>\n<li>Variety of Phillips screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Loctite to use on the pin pad screws for the mount</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Visit Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>Be sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order</p>\n<p>Confirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</p>\n<p><strong>Onsite Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198</p>\n<p>Mount the new pinpad in the <strong>same location as the old pinpad</strong>.</p>\n<p>Use the <strong>provided patch cables</strong> to connect the pinpad to the switch.</p>\n<p>The switch must have <strong>3 cables connected</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 1:</strong> Existing CAT 5 from the biscuit jack under the register.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 2:</strong> Connect a new CAT 5 patch cable to the biscuit jack, with the other end connected to<strong>Port 2</strong>.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 3:</strong> CAT 5 cable from the pinpad.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mount the switch on the <strong>left side</strong>, with the<strong>link lights visible</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Verify the access codes and IP address before entering them</strong> to avoid issues with the pinpad.</p>\n<p>Pack the <strong>old pinpads only</strong> for return.<strong>Do not include the stands or old cables.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Please review the Pinpad Refresh Field Services Guide for the full scope of work and installation instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Clean up Area</strong></p>\n<p>Call IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.</p>\n<p>Check In Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Check Out Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Store Contact Name:</p>\n<p>Record the serial numbers of all installed pin pads</p>\n<p>Return Tracking #:</p>\n<p>Store Check Out Contact:</p>\n<p>Picture of Completed Work:</p>\n<p><strong>Close-Out Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check out on the Field Nation App</p>\n<p>Ensure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables</p>\n<p>Leave defective parts onsite</p>\n<p>Submit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.</p>","markdown":"**Summary of Work:**\n\nIW Technologies is looking for a technician to complete a pin pad replacement at a local retailer. The scope includes replacing the existing pin pads, installing the switch, configuring and testing the devices. Please record each pin pad serial number with its corresponding lane number. Pack the existing pin pads and Verifone cables in the original tamper-safe white packaging, and drop the box off at FedEx.\n\n**QTY of Lanes: 4**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID\n- Velcro\n- 1.25\" hole saw w/drill\n- Variety of Phillips screwdrivers\n- Loctite to use on the pin pad screws for the mount\n\n**Pre-Visit Instructions:**\n\nBe sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order\n\nConfirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\n**Onsite Tasks:**\n\nCheck in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198\n\nMount the new pinpad in the **same location as the old pinpad**.\n\nUse the **provided patch cables** to connect the pinpad to the switch.\n\nThe switch must have **3 cables connected**:\n\n- **Port 1:** Existing CAT 5 from the biscuit jack under the register.\n- **Port 2:** Connect a new CAT 5 patch cable to the biscuit jack, with the other end connected to**Port 2**.\n- **Port 3:** CAT 5 cable from the pinpad.\n\nMount the switch on the **left side**, with the**link lights visible**.\n\n**Verify the access codes and IP address before entering them** to avoid issues with the pinpad.\n\nPack the **old pinpads only** for return.**Do not include the stands or old cables.**\n\n- Please review the Pinpad Refresh Field Services Guide for the full scope of work and installation instructions.\n\n**Clean up Area**\n\nCall IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.\n\nCheck In Time: (local)\n\nCheck Out Time: (local)\n\nStore Contact Name:\n\nRecord the serial numbers of all installed pin pads\n\nReturn Tracking #:\n\nStore Check Out Contact:\n\nPicture of Completed Work:\n\n**Close-Out Tasks:**\n\nCheck out on the Field Nation App\n\nEnsure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables\n\nLeave defective parts onsite\n\nSubmit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T07:45","end":"2026-10-13T09:45"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"unit