{"job":{"id":20041805,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Swarovski LV Cable rough-in & terminations - Day 2 Assist","description":{"html":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.<br/>For non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.<br/>Do not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.<br/><br/>SOW:<br/>Call to check in and out with Spencer Sr PM Abby Stetson 351-218-9097.<br/><br/>Techs will be on site to rough-in all data & speaker cabling, install the patch panel & terminate/label. <br/>   o GC will install the rack - should be installed already. If not, let PM know and we can push to have it installed ASAP.<br/>Techs will also complete all terminations - let PM know if there is any millwork not in place (ex. cashwrap). We will have to revisit to complete those locations. <br/>Make sure to label all cables on BOTH ends and patch panel!!!<br/><br/>• Cashwrap - 8 cables total<br/>   o 4 per bay<br/>   o If there is only a single register bay, still needs wired for two (for future temp holiday register, etc)<br/>   o Cables usually are terminated to a box or two in the base of the cashwrap and then we use patchcords to connect the devices<br/>• Manager's Office - 4 cables total<br/>   o Faceplate can be above or below the desk - depends on how it is set up. Use your best judgement depending on the site<br/>• CCTV cameras - 1 cable per camera plus traffic counter. Use site specific floor plans<br/>   o Cables will need to be terminated to an RJ45 and left poking out of the ceiling<br/>   o If ceiling is not in, leave terminated cables in a service loop. We will need to revisit to poke the cables through<br/>• 2 per digital display screen (1 is a spare)<br/>   o Terminate to an RJ45 end - this cable will direct connect to the back of the TV <br/>• 1 per AP (usually only one AP located towards the center/back of the salesfloor)<br/>   o Use best judgement for placement. These are small spaces so coverage usually isn't an issue<br/><br/>• Speakers - daisy chained <br/>   o Use site-specific plan – need to coordinate with GC<br/>   o We run the speaker cables and leave a service loop. The GC will follow and install the speakers and connect the wires<br/><br/>Patch Panel ports:<br/>1-18: POS, Mgr Desk, AP, & center kiosk (if applicable)<br/>19-39: Cameras & Digital Displays<br/><br/>Deliverables to swarovskiprojects@spencertech.com","markdown":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.  \nFor non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.  \nDo not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.  \n  \nSOW:  \nCall to check in and out with Spencer Sr PM Abby Stetson 351-218-9097.  \n  \nTechs will be on site to rough-in all data & speaker cabling, install the patch panel & terminate/label.   \n o GC will install the rack - should be installed already. If not, let PM know and we can push to have it installed ASAP.  \nTechs will also complete all terminations - let PM know if there is any millwork not in place (ex. cashwrap). We will have to revisit to complete those locations.   \nMake sure to label all cables on BOTH ends and patch panel!!!  \n  \n• Cashwrap - 8 cables total  \n o 4 per bay  \n o If there is only a single register bay, still needs wired for two (for future temp holiday register, etc)  \n o Cables usually are terminated to a box or two in the base of the cashwrap and then we use patchcords to connect the devices  \n• Manager's Office - 4 cables total  \n o Faceplate can be above or below the desk - depends on how it is set up. Use your best judgement depending on the site  \n• CCTV cameras - 1 cable per camera plus traffic counter. Use site specific floor plans  \n o Cables will need to be terminated to an RJ45 and left poking out of the ceiling  \n o If ceiling is not in, leave terminated cables in a service loop. We will need to revisit to poke the cables through  \n• 2 per digital display screen (1 is a spare)  \n o Terminate to an RJ45 end - this cable will direct connect to the back of the TV   \n• 1 per AP (usually only one AP located towards the center/back of the salesfloor)  \n o Use best judgement for placement. These are small spaces so coverage usually isn't an issue  \n  \n• Speakers - daisy chained   \n o Use site-specific plan – need to coordinate with GC  \n o We run the speaker cables and leave a service loop. The GC will follow and install the speakers and connect the wires  \n  \nPatch Panel ports:  \n1-18: POS, Mgr Desk, AP, & center kiosk (if applicable)  \n19-39: Cameras & Digital Displays  \n  \nDeliverables to swarovskiprojects@spencertech.com","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.