{"job":{"id":20040239,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Hosted VoIP Install for GT Cylinder Exchange & Truck Repair - Goldsboro","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP &amp; Data Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>2 - Routers</p>\n<p>3 - Corded VoIP Phones</p>\n<p>1 - 2 Port ATA</p>\n<p>2 - Antennas for Cellular Internet</p>\n<p>2 - Cellular Internet Modems</p>\n<p>There are 2 buildings. Internet will be installed in each building. Phones are installed in only 1 of the buildings.</p>\n<p>Cutover over to new internet circuits</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached <strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.</li>\n<li>Contact support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>Network/cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n<li>Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install new equipment.</li>\n<li>Complete all tests on the checklist with support.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP & Data Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n2 - Routers\n\n3 - Corded VoIP Phones\n\n1 - 2 Port ATA\n\n2 - Antennas for Cellular Internet\n\n2 - Cellular Internet Modems\n\nThere are 2 buildings. Internet will be installed in each building. Phones are installed in only 1 of the buildings.\n\nCutover over to new internet circuits\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached **Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.\n- Contact support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- Network/cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n- Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install new equipment.\n- Complete all tests on the checklist with support.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T09:00","end":"2026-10-08T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":54},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790533909171}
{"job":{"id":20040241,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Installation of Cellular Internet for GT Cylinder Exchange & Truck Repair - Dudley","description":{"html":"<p><strong>ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>1 - Antenna for Cellular Internet</p>\n<p>1 - Cellular Internet Modem</p>\n<p>Cutover to new internet circuit</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>This is an <strong>ATA/Gateway installation only</strong> — no new phones will be installed.</li>\n<li>Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached<strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n<li>See <strong>gateway install scope.pdf</strong> for detailed installation guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.</li>\n<li>Check in with support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable</li>\n<li>Minimum 16 RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1 - Antenna for Cellular Internet\n\n1 - Cellular Internet Modem\n\nCutover to new internet circuit\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- This is an **ATA/Gateway installation only** — no new phones will be installed.\n- Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached**Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n- See **gateway install scope.pdf** for detailed installation guidelines.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.\n- Check in with support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable\n- Minimum 16 RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nIf another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00","end":"2026-10-01T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":56},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite | MED-530 | 03982724 | PolyRove Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790533915055}
{"job":{"id":"1993224428","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Shelf Level Retail Solutions LLC","title":"8381C - BUG SOOTHER MAX 8OZ - Merchandising QR code placement. and product purchase","description":"<p>Before Visit: Print off 1 page of the QR code promotion and cut out two of the QR promotions. Bring tape with you to the store. During store visits, reps will perform the following tasks: 1. Check to ensure the assigned sidekick display is located on the sales floor. 2. If the display is not on the sales floor, work with the store manager to locate the display and place it on the sales floor. Sidekick was supposed to be set out for 4th of July promo. 3. If the manager states that the display has already been broken down, ask whether it is possible to merchandise the product in a feature location. 4. Verify that the display price tag is properly placed on the display. If it is missing, work with the manager to obtain and place the correct display price tag. 5. Replenish and straighten product on the display to ensure it is full and properly merchandised. 6. Tape both copies of the QR code promo sheets to the side of the sidekick display. 6. Take clear photos of the completed display on the sales floor with the QR codes taped to the display. If display placement is not permitted, take photos of the product on the shelf instead. 7. Purchase 4 units of each sku for a total of 8 units.</p><p>Visit Wrap-up: • If you receive pushback on any requested task during the visit, document the reason provided and capture the store manager's name in your reporting.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-27T09:41","end":"2026-09-27T13:41"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":32},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":0},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/27/2026, 9:41:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T