{"job":{"id":20042529,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Fiber Technician Needed with Fiber Splicing Tools to Replace Fiber Connection and Restore Switch Link – Greenville, NC | 00260031 / SA-291821 / Case-05278595","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p>\n<p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: <strong>Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong> to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li>\n<li>Note: <strong>Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong> explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li>\n<li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to<strong>specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong> and its reason.</li>\n<li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong>the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li>\n<li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Title: Fiber Technician Needed with Tools to Replace Fiber Connection and Restore Switch Link – Greenville, NC | 00260031 / SA-291821 / Case-05278595</p>\n<p>Type of Work: Fiber</p>\n<p>Schedule: September 26, 2026 – 02:30 PM EDT (02:30 PM EDT conversion)</p>\n<p>Site Name &amp; Address: The Landing Student Living, 1920 Exchange Drive, Greenville, NC 27858, United States</p>\n<p>WO / SA / Case: 00260031 / SA-291821 / 5278595</p>\n<p>Contact Details:</p>\n<p>Site POC: Ryce Garcia, 252-321-6783</p>\n<p>Engineer: Technet | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p>\n<p>Scope of Work:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dispatch a qualified fiber technician with a fiber splicer and appropriate fiber tools.</li>\n<li>Replace the existing suspected faulty/obsolete LC-ST fiber connection with a compatible single-mode LC-to-LC fiber connection.</li>\n<li>Bring LC-to-LC single-mode connectors, pigtail, and coupler required to complete the replacement.</li>\n<li>Location: IDF3 - Building 3.</li>\n<li>Device: Ruckus ICX7150-24-4X10GR / ICX7150-24-2X10G, Asset: NC-LAND-IDF3sw.</li>\n<li>Serial Number: FEG3831S001; MAC: C8:03:F5:1C:AA:88; IP: 10.1.0.6.</li>\n<li>Parent Device/Switch: NC-LAND-MDFCoreswA; Port Mapping: 1/4/2; Monitoring Source/System: SF.</li>\n<li>Fiber was previously cleaned and a bend at the IDF was corrected, restoring optical power at the MDF, but the switch remains unreachable/unmanageable.</li>\n<li>Replace the current LC-ST connection and verify the fiber/SFP link.</li>\n<li>Verify parent switch port 1/4/2 and confirm switch management reachability and restoration of service.</li>\n<li>If applicable, check SFP status, fiber light/continuity, and physical connections after replacement.</li>\n<li>Reboot/power-cycle the switch only if required and approved to restore service.</li>\n<li>Label any newly installed/replaced fiber components or connections as appropriate.</li>\n<li>Document any remaining fiber loss or issues preventing restoration.</li>\n<li>Reference prior troubleshooting: fiber cleaning and bend correction restored optical power at MDF; no OTDR was previously available.</li>\n<li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done</li>\n<li>Asset &amp; Location: NC-LAND-IDF3sw – IDF3 - Building 3</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tools Required:</p>\n<p>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</p>\n<p>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</p>\n<p>Ethernet adapter</p>\n<p>Ethernet cable</p>\n<p>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</p>\n<p>Cellphone with camera</p>\n<p>Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit Ethernet connections)</p>\n<p>Tone generator</p>\n<p>Console cable and USB adapter</p>\n<p>Label maker</p>\n<p>Crimper</p>\n<p>RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)</p>\n<p>Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)</p>\n<p>Voltage tester</p>\n<p>Screwdrivers and security bits</p>\n<p>Laser to verify fiber light continuity</p>\n<p>Fiber tester</p>\n<p>Fiber cleaning kit</p>\n<p>Fiber splicer</p>\n<p>LC-to-LC single-mode fiber connectors</p>\n<p>Single-mode fiber pigtails</p>\n<p>LC-to-LC fiber couplers</p>\n<p>Correct compatible fiber connector for the existing fiber/SFP connection</p>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to**specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\nTitle: Fiber Technician Needed with Tools to Replace Fiber Connection and Restore Switch Link – Greenville, NC | 00260031 / SA-291821 / Case-05278595\n\nType of Work: Fiber\n\nSchedule: September 26, 2026 – 02:30 PM EDT (02:30 PM EDT conversion)\n\nSite Name & Address: The Landing Student Living, 1920 Exchange Drive, Greenville, NC 27858, United States\n\nWO / SA / Case: 00260031 / SA-291821 / 5278595\n\nContact Details:\n\nSite POC: Ryce Garcia, 252-321-6783\n\nEngineer: Technet | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\nScope of Work:\n\n- Dispatch a qualified fiber technician with a fiber splicer and appropriate fiber tools.\n- Replace the existing suspected faulty/obsolete LC-ST fiber connection with a compatible single-mode LC-to-LC fiber connection.\n- Bring LC-to-LC single-mode connectors, pigtail, and coupler required to complete the replacement.\n- Location: IDF3 - Building 3.\n- Device: Ruckus ICX7150-24-4X10GR / ICX7150-24-2X10G, Asset: NC-LAND-IDF3sw.\n- Serial Number: FEG3831S001; MAC: C8:03:F5:1C:AA:88; IP: 10.1.0.6.\n- Parent Device/Switch: NC-LAND-MDFCoreswA; Port Mapping: 1/4/2; Monitoring Source/System: SF.\n- Fiber was previously cleaned and a bend at the IDF was corrected, restoring optical power at the MDF, but the switch remains unreachable/unmanageable.\n- Replace the current LC-ST connection and verify the fiber/SFP link.\n- Verify parent switch port 1/4/2 and confirm switch management reachability and restoration of service.\n- If applicable, check SFP status, fiber light/continuity, and physical connections after replacement.\n- Reboot/power-cycle the switch only if required and approved to restore service.\n- Label any newly installed/replaced fiber components or connections as appropriate.\n- Document any remaining fiber loss or issues preventing restoration.\n- Reference prior troubleshooting: fiber cleaning and bend correction restored optical power at MDF; no OTDR was previously available.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done\n- Asset & Location: NC-LAND-IDF3sw – IDF3 - Building 3\n\nTools Required:\n\nMicrosoft Teams installed and available to chat\n\nLaptop (Windows) and power adapter\n\nEthernet adapter\n\nEthernet cable\n\nMobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n\nCellphone with camera\n\nWire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit Ethernet connections)\n\nTone generator\n\nConsole cable and USB adapter\n\nLabel maker\n\nCrimper\n\nRJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n\nKeystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n\nVoltage tester\n\nScrewdrivers and security bits\n\nLaser to verify fiber light continuity\n\nFiber tester\n\nFiber cleaning kit\n\nFiber splicer\n\nLC-to-LC single-mode fiber connectors\n\nSingle-mode fiber pigtails\n\nLC-to-LC fiber couplers\n\nCorrect compatible fiber connector for the existing fiber/SFP connection","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T10:00","end":"2026-09-28T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":80},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":260,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":115,