nd will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future.&nbsp;Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue.&nbsp;DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release.&nbsp;Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.</p><p><strong>Readiness Policy:&nbsp;</strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>On My Way:&nbsp;</strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</p><p><strong>Arriving Late:</strong>&nbsp;All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</p><p><strong>Changing Resources:</strong>&nbsp;By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Expense Approval:</strong>&nbsp;Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</p><p><strong>Additional 