{"job":{"id":20043857,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Freightsnap","title":"Replace IP Camera on Measuring Equipment in Trucking Terminal","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**THE SITE DOES NOT HAVE A 12' A-FRAME LADDER FOR THIS SO YOU WILL NEED TO PROVIDE ONE TO REACH THIS EQUIPMENT COMFORTABLY (NORMAL EXTENSION LADDERS DO NOT WORK)</strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p><p>We have a piece of equipment in a warehouse setting that automatically captures the dimensions of freight. The unit has 2 POE cameras attached to it, all attached to aluminum \"arms\" on the unit's frame and surrounding bollards. We would like you to replace one of these with a new camera we have shipped to the site. We will work with you remotely to help guide the adjustment and pull the camera's image up on a nearby monitor. We can also answer any questions you may have.</p><p>PICTURE EXAMPLE BELOW OF HOW THIS NEEDS TO BE MOUNTED AS WELL AS A PICTURE EXAMPLE OF OUR MEASURING UNIT</p><p>The existing camera is very similar or possibly identical to the new camera that will be installed. You may be able to use the existing mount and just twist off the old camera and twist on the new camera. If not, there will be a new mount in the box that the camera was sent in and it is simply help in place by a small machine bolt, washer and hex nut.</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tool for cutting cable ties if necessary</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Ties</strong></li><li><strong>Phillips Head Screw Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Pliers, wrenches (hand tools to remove mounting hardware)</strong></li><li><strong>12' A-Frame Ladder (NECESSARY FOR REACHING THE EQUIPMENT)</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*THE SITE DOES NOT HAVE A 12' A-FRAME LADDER FOR THIS SO YOU WILL NEED TO PROVIDE ONE TO REACH THIS EQUIPMENT COMFORTABLY (NORMAL EXTENSION LADDERS DO NOT WORK)**\n\n**Overview:**\n\nWe have a piece of equipment in a warehouse setting that automatically captures the dimensions of freight. The unit has 2 POE cameras attached to it, all attached to aluminum \"arms\" on the unit's frame and surrounding bollards. We would like you to replace one of these with a new camera we have shipped to the site. We will work with you remotely to help guide the adjustment and pull the camera's image up on a nearby monitor. We can also answer any questions you may have.\n\nPICTURE EXAMPLE BELOW OF HOW THIS NEEDS TO BE MOUNTED AS WELL AS A PICTURE EXAMPLE OF OUR MEASURING UNIT\n\nThe existing camera is very similar or possibly identical to the new camera that will be installed. You may be able to use the existing mount and just twist off the old camera and twist on the new camera. If not, there will be a new mount in the box that the camera was sent in and it is simply help in place by a small machine bolt, washer and hex nut.\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- **Tool for cutting cable ties if necessary**\n- **Cable Ties**\n- **Phillips Head Screw Driver**\n- **Pliers, wrenches (hand tools to remove mounting hardware)**\n- **12' A-Frame Ladder (NECESSARY FOR REACHING THE EQUIPMENT)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T09:00","end":"2026-09-29T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":175,"max":250},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":175},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":48},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 30, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $250\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790603800934}
{"job":{"id":20032416,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ProAct Services","title":"Safelite| MG Replacement and Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***CAREFULLY REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED DOCUMENTS BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER***</strong></p><p><strong>GENERAL GUIDELINES:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Technicians are not permitted to start work on-site or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager</u>.</strong></li><li><strong>The technician accepting the work order should be the technician to check in and out during the agreed-upon visit date.&nbsp;<u>Any</u></strong><u>&nbsp;</u><strong><u>individuals who do not have permission or authorization to be at the location are prohibited from entering or remaining on-site.</u></strong></li><li><strong>Technicians must wear closed-toe shoes. The use of onsite ladders or step stools is not permitted.</strong></li><li><strong>Upon arrival, the technician must verify that the part numbers, colors, and quantities of the materials received match the list provided by the PCs or attached to the work order. The technician should immediately report any discrepancies with the parts received.&nbsp;<u>No cabling work should begin until a complete inventory check has been performed.</u></strong></li><li><strong>All new and or reran cabling must go through the patch panel and be patched into the switch.</strong></li><li><strong>Ensure that all tasks are completed to a satisfactory level, meeting the specified requirements and quality standards.</strong> <strong><u>Everything must be verified with the NOC before job release and approved by ProAct Team.</u></strong></li><li><strong>Ensure all fields in your sign-off sheet are completed thoroughly and accurately. Provide detailed notes on any issues or delays encountered during the process. <u>The work order will not be approved if the required information and deliverables are incomplete.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Technicians are NOT to leave the site until PROACT SERVICES releases them; otherwise, the work order will be penalized.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>No out-of-the-scope work within your work order will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the ProAct Services Project Manager.</u></strong></li><li><strong>The technicians will dispose of any trash generated during the installation and perform a general cleaning of areas that may have been affected by the work. This assumes the use of client dumpster(s).</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong>: Complete the requested Safelite service call as per the description below:</p><p>Determine the optimal cellular tower location with the strongest signal using the WeBoost application, and obtain approval from the ProAct Services team for the proposed placement. Once approved, coordinate with ProAct Services and the GC/EC to plan any required core drilling, penetration, and sleeving to properly route cabling from the rack to the MG location. Mount the J-pipe and MG device on the exterior of the building, and conduct testing with the NOC. If you have any questions or concerns, please don’t hesitate to contact the ProAct Services team.</p><p><strong>Reminders</strong>:</p><ul><li>The work order could take more than 4 hours to complete.&nbsp;<strong>Please do not schedule any other work close to this installation schedule.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Technician is required to download the WeBoost app to locate the nearest cell tower and determine the signal strength</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Link to the App Store app: https://apps.apple.com/us/app/weboost/id1611974453</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Link to the Google Play Store app: </u></strong>https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.wilsonelectronics.weboost</li><li>Technicians are not permitted to start work onsite or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager.</li></ul><p><strong><u>REQUIRED MATERIALS/TOOLS:</u></strong></p><p>The tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. T<u>he cost of materials will only be reimbursed if the materials were used during the visit and a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided</u>.</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder below 8'</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cable weatherproofing/sealant</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Velcro, wire ties</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drilling tools</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Standard Low Voltage tool kit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any materials that might be needed for this type of installation</li></ul><p><strong>Note</strong>:</p><ul><li>The tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. The cost of materials will be reimbursed only if a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TASKS:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Upon arrival, call and check in with the ProAct Services and NOC contacts listed in this work order.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ******** **** ***** ********</del></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*** ** *************</del></span> <strong>Reference site number: 3814</strong></li><li><strong>Work with the site contact to locate and inventory the Safelite equipment and cabling materials. Notify the ProAct team of any discrepancies.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CS34O-0 / UN884019904/10CAT6 - Outdoor Rated - Black - 1000' Spool (.25/1)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">3M TALC 3M Fire Barrier Moldable Putty (1)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">JP75SBC50-L20 3/4\" J-hooks - Metal/Nylon w/screw on BC (10)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">106150 CAT6 RJ45 Modular Connectors (1)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">105073 CAT6 RJ45 Strain Relief Boots (1)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">UTP28SP3BU 3' CAT6 Patch Cables - Slim - Blue (1)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">BT974778 10 INCH J-POLE MOUNT ACCESSORYKIT (1)</li><li>Use the WeBoost app to determine the best cellular&nbsp;tower location with the optimum signal strength.&nbsp;</li><li>Determine with the PM (Carl \"Cj\" Betts) and ProAct Team the appropriate placement of the Cellular Backup device on the exterior of the&nbsp;building based on the above results.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>The MG should be facing the direction towards the nearest cell tower, and installed near the edge of the roof, so that the antennas are above the roof line.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Take close-up and wide-angle photos of the proposed location for the MG device and send them to the ProAct Team. Additionally, include screenshots from the \"WeBoost\" application showing the cellular signal test results and the nearest tower location</strong></li><li>Work with the PM or GC/EC to determine the core drilling/penetration and sleeving to properly run cabling and&nbsp;mount the Cellular Backup on the exterior of the building.&nbsp;</li><li>Determine cable pathway for the new CAT6 run.&nbsp;</li><li>Once the pathway has been approved by the PM, run a pathway and pull up to 250’ of CAT6 plenum outdoor Ethernet cable from the MDF to the customer&nbsp;approved location determined during the survey.</li><li>Terminate the Ethernet cable to the Cellular Backup with an RJ45 modular jack/strain relief boot and to an&nbsp;existing open Ethernet port on the patch panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Provide continuity testing of the Ethernet cable.&nbsp;Take a photo of the cable test result and upload on the work order.</li><li>Cross-connect the Ethernet cable between the patch panel and the predetermined/preconfigured POE switch&nbsp;port.&nbsp;</li><li>Install the Cellular Backup on J-pole using the customer-provided documentation.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Put weatherproofing/water sealant on the penetration/sleeving</strong></li><li>Work with the site contact/manager to check that the internet, all voice, and wifi services are working properly. Ask if they have any other IT-related or hardware-related issues they would like us to communicate back to the Safelite IT team and its managers.&nbsp;<strong>Document this on the sign-off sheet.</strong></li><li>Clean up the site after completion</li><li><strong>Box up and return ship all removed and/or unused network equipment</strong>. The return shipping label is inside the new MG device box.</li><li>Work with the NOC to ensure all network equipment is online and functioning. <strong>The NOC must confirm all equipment are online.</strong></li><li>Upload all deliverables and documents required, and call ProAct Services to check out.</li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site until ProAct Services has released you from the work.</u></strong></li><li>Drop off the equipment at the nearest FedEx, take a photo of the receipt, and upload it to Field Nation or send it to the ProAct Services line.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Upload these photos to Field Nation and let the ProAct Services contact know&nbsp;BEFORE&nbsp;leaving the site</strong>:</p><ol><li>Sign off sheet with your check-in and out time and the POC's name and signature. You can find this document in the work order.</li><li>Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the existing modem.</li><li>Take pre-installation photos upon your arrival:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Proposed location of the MG device. Include close-up and wide-angle photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screenshot of the cellular signal test and nearest tower location from the \"WeBoost\" application</li><li>Take post-installation photos:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final location of the MG device (close-up and wide-view photos)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screenshot of the cellular signal test from the \"WeBoost\" application or any test receipts.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos of the cable pathways inside the building, showing how the cables were routed from the rack to the MG location. Ensure that all cables are neatly arranged with no obstructions or messy cabling. <strong>Additionally, include a photo of the clear silicone or sealant that was applied.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photo of the patch panel and switch ports used for the MG. Ensure that the ports and cables are labeled properly</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Cable test result for the MG cable run</strong></li><li>Provide the following information to the ProAct team once installation is complete</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Total length of cable used for the MG installation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Patch panel and switch port numbers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Name of the NOC that verified the MG's functionality and connectivity.</li><li>Photo of the device that needs to be returned to Safelite and contact information of the site POC and drop off receipt (if applicable)</li><li>Any test receipts</li><li>Any issue that may arise or that needs to be escalated,</li></ol><p><strong><u>Change Control:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any changes to the scope, timeline, or budget of this project must be approved through the change control process. Any proposed changes must be documented, including the reason for the change, the impact on the project timeline, budget, and resources, and any necessary adjustments to the SOW.</li><li>The change control process will involve a review by the project manager and project coordinator.</li><li><strong><u>No work, out of the scope of work within your work order, will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the Project Manager</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*CAREFULLY REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED DOCUMENTS BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER\\*\\*\\***\n\n**GENERAL GUIDELINES:**\n\n- **Technicians are not permitted to start work on-site or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager.**\n- **The technician accepting the work order should be the technician to check in and out during the agreed-upon visit date. Any** **individuals who do not have permission or authorization to be at the location are prohibited from entering or remaining on-site.**\n- **Technicians must wear closed-toe shoes. The use of onsite ladders or step stools is not permitted.**\n- **Upon arrival, the technician must verify that the part numbers, colors, and quantities of the materials received match the list provided by the PCs or attached to the work order. The technician should immediately report any discrepancies with the parts received. No cabling work should begin until a complete inventory check has been performed.**\n- **All new and or reran cabling must go through the patch panel and be patched into the switch.**\n- **Ensure that all tasks are completed to a satisfactory level, meeting the specified requirements and quality standards.** **Everything must be verified with the NOC before job release and approved by ProAct Team.**\n- **Ensure all fields in your sign-off sheet are completed thoroughly and accurately. Provide detailed notes on any issues or delays encountered during the process. The work order will not be approved if the required information and deliverables are incomplete.**\n- **Technicians are NOT to leave the site until PROACT SERVICES releases them; otherwise, the work order will be penalized.**\n- **No out-of-the-scope work within your work order will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the ProAct Services Project Manager.**\n- **The technicians will dispose of any trash generated during the installation and perform a general cleaning of areas that may have been affected by the work. This assumes the use of client dumpster(s).**\n\n**Scope of Work**: Complete the requested Safelite service call as per the description below:\n\nDetermine the optimal cellular tower location with the strongest signal using the WeBoost application, and obtain approval from the ProAct Services team for the proposed placement. Once approved, coordinate with ProAct Services and the GC/EC to plan any required core drilling, penetration, and sleeving to properly route cabling from the rack to the MG location. Mount the J-pipe and MG device on the exterior of the building, and conduct testing with the NOC. If you have any questions or concerns, please don’t hesitate to contact the ProAct Services team.\n\n**Reminders**:\n\n- The work order could take more than 4 hours to complete. **Please do not schedule any other work close to this installation schedule.**\n- **Technician is required to download the WeBoost app to locate the nearest cell tower and determine the signal strength**\n- Link to the App Store app: <https://apps.apple.com/us/app/weboost/id1611974453>\n- **Link to the Google Play Store app:** <https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.wilsonelectronics.weboost>\n- Technicians are not permitted to start work onsite or stay inside the location without a POC/Manager.\n\n**REQUIRED MATERIALS/TOOLS:**\n\nThe tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. The cost of materials will only be reimbursed if the materials were used during the visit and a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided.\n\n- Ladder below 8'\n- Cable weatherproofing/sealant\n- Velcro, wire ties\n- Drilling tools\n- Standard Low Voltage tool kit\n- Any materials that might be needed for this type of installation\n\n**Note**:\n\n- The tech will need to provide the tools and materials required to complete this job. The cost of materials will be reimbursed only if a receipt or cost breakdown of parts is provided.\n\n**TASKS:**\n\n1. Upon arrival, call and check in with the ProAct Services and NOC contacts listed in this work order.\n2. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **Reference site number: 3814**\n4. **Work with the site contact to locate and inventory the Safelite equipment and cabling materials. Notify the ProAct team of any discrepancies.**\n5. CS34O-0 / UN884019904/10CAT6 - Outdoor Rated - Black - 1000' Spool (.25/1)\n6. 3M TALC 3M Fire Barrier Moldable Putty (1)\n7. JP75SBC50-L20 3/4\" J-hooks - Metal/Nylon w/screw on BC (10)\n8. 106150 CAT6 RJ45 Modular Connectors (1)\n9. 105073 CAT6 RJ45 Strain Relief Boots (1)\n10. UTP28SP3BU 3' CAT6 Patch Cables - Slim - Blue (1)\n11. BT974778 10 INCH J-POLE MOUNT ACCESSORYKIT (1)\n12. Use the WeBoost app to determine the best cellular tower location with the optimum signal strength.\n13. Determine with the PM (Carl \"Cj\" Betts) and ProAct Team the appropriate placement of the Cellular Backup device on the exterior of the building based on the above results.\n14. **The MG should be facing the direction towards the nearest cell tower, and installed near the edge of the roof, so that the antennas are above the roof line.**\n15. **Take close-up and wide-angle photos of the proposed location for the MG device and send them to the ProAct Team. Additionally, include screenshots from the \"WeBoost\" application showing the cellular signal test results and the nearest tower location**\n16. Work with the PM or GC/EC to determine the core drilling/penetration and sleeving to properly run cabling and mount the Cellular Backup on the exterior of the building.\n17. Determine cable pathway for the new CAT6 run.\n18. Once the pathway has been approved by the PM, run a pathway and pull up to 250’ of CAT6 plenum outdoor Ethernet cable from the MDF to the customer approved location determined during the survey.\n19. Terminate the Ethernet cable to the Cellular Backup with an RJ45 modular jack/strain relief boot and to an existing open Ethernet port on the patch panel.\n20. Provide continuity testing of the Ethernet cable. Take a photo of the cable test result and upload on the work order.\n21. Cross-connect the Ethernet cable between the patch panel and the predetermined/preconfigured POE switch port.\n22. Install the Cellular Backup on J-pole using the customer-provided documentation.\n23. **Put weatherproofing/water sealant on the penetration/sleeving**\n24. Work with the site contact/manager to check that the internet, all voice, and wifi services are working properly. Ask if they have any other IT-related or hardware-related issues they would like us to communicate back to the Safelite IT team and its managers. **Document this on the sign-off sheet.**\n25. Clean up the site after completion\n26. **Box up and return ship all removed and/or unused network equipment**. The return shipping label is inside the new MG device box.\n27. Work with the NOC to ensure all network equipment is online and functioning. **The NOC must confirm all equipment are online.**\n28. Upload all deliverables and documents required, and call ProAct Services to check out.\n29. **Do not leave the site until ProAct Services has released you from the work.**\n30. Drop off the equipment at the nearest FedEx, take a photo of the receipt, and upload it to Field Nation or send it to the ProAct Services line.\n\n**Upload these photos to Field Nation and let the ProAct Services contact know BEFORE leaving the site**:\n\n1. Sign off sheet with your check-in and out time and the POC's name and signature. You can find this document in the work order.\n2. Close-up AND wide-angle photo of the existing modem.\n3. Take pre-installation photos upon your arrival:\n4. Proposed location of the MG device. Include close-up and wide-angle photos\n5. Screenshot of the cellular signal test and nearest tower location from the \"WeBoost\" application\n6. Take post-installation photos:\n7. Final location of the MG device (close-up and wide-view photos)\n8. Screenshot of the cellular signal test from the \"WeBoost\" application or any test receipts.\n9. Photos of the cable pathways inside the building, showing how the cables were routed from the rack to the MG location. Ensure that all cables are neatly arranged with no obstructions or messy cabling. **Additionally, include a photo of the clear silicone or sealant that was applied.**\n10. Photo of the patch panel and switch ports used for the MG. Ensure that the ports and cables are labeled properly\n11. **Cable test result for the MG cable run**\n12. Provide the following information to the ProAct team once installation is complete\n13. Total length of cable used for the MG installation.\n14. Patch panel and switch port numbers\n15. Name of the NOC that verified the MG's functionality and connectivity.\n16. Photo of the device that needs to be returned to Safelite and contact information of the site POC and drop off receipt (if applicable)\n17. Any test receipts\n18. Any issue that may arise or that needs to be escalated,\n\n**Change Control:**\n\n- Any changes to the scope, timeline, or budget of this project must be approved through the change control process. Any proposed changes must be documented, including the reason for the change, the impact on the project timeline, budget, and resources, and any necessary adjustments to the SOW.\n- The change control process will involve a review by the project manager and project coordinator.\n- **No work, out of the scope of work within your work order, will be agreed upon or completed without prior approval from the Project Manager**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T08:00","end":"2026-10-01T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":360,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T