{"job":{"id":20051481,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - AP Down","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Required 26ft. Scissor lift.</p><p>Need to align the tech Mon-Fri, 8 AM EST.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>1. Impacted Device: Aruba APs-635(std2536ap12)</p><p>2. Location: Food Lion - 2536 Sanford</p><p>3. Problem Statement: Aruba APs-635(std2536ap12)</p><p>4. What troubleshooting has been completed: During troubleshooting,Observed that AP std2536ap12 is Down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.Sending dispatch to check the physical connectivity.</p><p><br></p><p>5. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:</p><p>• Laptop with good internet connection. Before visiting the location, please make sure that laptop should be able to take console.</p><p>• Technician should have admin access of laptop.</p><p>• console cable (proprietary, micro-B USB physical jack) which should be compatible with ARUBA 635 Access Point.</p><p>• Microsoft Teams should be installed in Laptop. Ladder may be required, to access the AP.</p><p>• Short cable, Cable tester, path cables are required.</p><p><br></p><p>6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:</p><p><br></p><p>• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.</p><p>• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.</p><p>• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.</p><p>•Need to test the cable run for the AP.</p><p>• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.</p><p>• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Required 26ft. Scissor lift.\n\nNeed to align the tech Mon-Fri, 8 AM EST.\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: Aruba APs-635(std2536ap12)\n\n2\\. Location: Food Lion - 2536 Sanford\n\n3\\. Problem Statement: Aruba APs-635(std2536ap12)\n\n4\\. What troubleshooting has been completed: During troubleshooting,Observed that AP std2536ap12 is Down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.Sending dispatch to check the physical connectivity.\n\n5\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:\n\n• Laptop with good internet connection. Before visiting the location, please make sure that laptop should be able to take console.\n\n• Technician should have admin access of laptop.\n\n• console cable (proprietary, micro-B USB physical jack) which should be compatible with ARUBA 635 Access Point.\n\n• Microsoft Teams should be installed in Laptop. Ladder may be required, to access the AP.\n\n• Short cable, Cable tester, path cables are required.\n\n6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:\n\n• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.\n\n• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.\n\n• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.\n\n•Need to test the cable run for the AP.\n\n• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.\n\n• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":35},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790633808124}
