{"job":{"id":20051147,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"RACK & STACK EQUIPMENT / VERIFY CONNECTIVITY WITH REMOTE TEAM / MB2795703 (AWS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p><br>- Tech will arrive on-site at 12:30 pm ET/local time<br>- Tech will contact the LCON above upon arrival to access the service location.<br>- Tech should take the opportunity to locate the demarc and the circuit<br>- Tech will take pictures of all the devices to share them with the remote engineer<br>- Any questions should be directed to the remote engineer<br>- ‎At  1:00 pm ET/ local time, the Tech will join the Masergy Site Verification bridge to work with an SDNet engineer.</p><br/><br/><p><br>Parts Required and Parts Return Instructions:  <br><br>-  At a minimum, tech should have a working laptop that has 1G NIC card, a working console cable that matches the equipment list provided, a working Wi-Fi connection, and the ability to load Teamviewer on the laptop (with appropriate drivers), for use, if needed. <br><br>- Be sure to leave any unused parts or accessories with the local contacts. <br> </p><br/><br/><p><em>Review the </em><strong><em><u>“Confidential Section”</u></em></strong><em> listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including </em></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Circuit location and ID</li><li>Equipment details</li><li>Icon info</li><li>Bridge line #</li></ul><br/><br/><p><span style=\"color: #1f1f1f;\">Please bring a </span><span style=\"color: #f40505;\">NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. </span><span style=\"color: #1f1f1f;\">This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements</span></p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger &amp; TeamViewer Installed</li><li>Hot Spot or Internet Dongle</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger</li><li>Console Cable <span style=\"color: #ea0505;\">(Please see attached images for reference)</span></li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)</li></ul><br/><br/><p><em>*Additional Tools Requested*</em></p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Mandatory to be released from the site by the Remote Engineer once the equipment is confirmed online &amp; photos are verified.</li></ul><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Photo ID required</li><li>Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>******* ******** ****** ************** *******</del></li><li>Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n  \n  \n\\  \n\\- Tech will arrive on-site at 12:30 pm ET/local time  \n\\- Tech will contact the LCON above upon arrival to access the service location.  \n\\- Tech should take the opportunity to locate the demarc and the circuit  \n\\- Tech will take pictures of all the devices to share them with the remote engineer  \n\\- Any questions should be directed to the remote engineer  \n\\- ‎At 1:00 pm ET/ local time, the Tech will join the Masergy Site Verification bridge to work with an SDNet engineer.\n\n  \n  \n  \nParts Required and Parts Return Instructions:   \n  \n\\- At a minimum, tech should have a working laptop that has 1G NIC card, a working console cable that matches the equipment list provided, a working Wi-Fi connection, and the ability to load Teamviewer on the laptop (with appropriate drivers), for use, if needed.   \n  \n\\- Be sure to leave any unused parts or accessories with the local contacts.\n\n  \n  \n*Review the* ***“Confidential Section”*** *listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including*\n\n  \n  \n- Circuit location and ID\n- Equipment details\n- Icon info\n- Bridge line #\n\n  \n  \nPlease bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements\n\n  \n  \n**Tool Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger & TeamViewer Installed\n- Hot Spot or Internet Dongle\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Cell Phone - with Charger\n- Console Cable (Please see attached images for reference)\n- Spare Patch Cables & Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)\n\n  \n  \n*\\*Additional Tools Requested\\**\n\n  \n  \n**Site Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Mandatory to be released from the site by the Remote Engineer once the equipment is confirmed online & photos are verified.\n\n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T12:30","end":"2026-10-05T16:30"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":30,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":64},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"st