{"job":{"id":"5584489522","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Retail Technology Group","title":"Panera - Access Point Upgrade - tall ladder required","description":"<p>Overview:</p><p>Replace existing legacy Cisco Meraki wireless access points with new Cisco Meraki MR36 access points at the designated Panera location. Work is to be completed during the approved service window.</p><p><br></p><p>Access Points - Cisco Meraki MR32, MR33, MR34 and MR42 to be replaced with MR36</p><p><br></p><p>Cafe Scope:</p><p>Access Point - Three-Four (3-4) MR36s </p><p><br></p><p>REQUIRED: 12-15ft ladder</p><p><br></p><p>Contacts:</p><p>RTG PM: Max Dyer - 314.756.3302 </p><p>Panera Project Support/Testing: 314.984.3000 Silent opt 6</p><p>Panera HD - 314.984.3000 opt 7</p><p>Panera NOC - 314.984.3130 opt 3</p><p><br></p><p>RTG Technician shall:</p><p>i) Call the cafe manager on the day of install to confirm closing time of the cafe to coordinate arrival.</p><p>ii) Upon arrival onsite, call Panera Project Support to check in.</p><p>iii) Confirm that all hardware intended to be removed and\\or installed are located at the cafe.</p><p>iv) Review the scope of work with the manager.</p><p>v) Confirm with manager the time the manager will be leaving. NOTE tech will need access to managers office, ensure manager does not lock you out!</p><p>vi) If the manager is leaving before work is completed then confirm if a baker will be present in the cafe</p><p><br></p><p>ACCESS POINTS - can start when manager confirms cafe is closed</p><p>NETWORK SWITCH - must wait until manager has completed end of day</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>ACCESS POINTS - If in scope:</p><p>Refer to Installation Guide for specific details:</p><p>i) Take before photos of the existing network access points.</p><p>ii) Deinstall the existing access points.</p><p>iii) Install the new access points.</p><p>iv) Contact Panera NOC to complete configuration, testing, and validation steps.</p><p>v) Contact Panera Project Support to complete configuration, testing, and validation steps.</p><p>vi) Take “after” photos of access points.</p><p>vii) Package deinstalled equipment in packaging that new equipment came in.</p><p>viii) Ship deinstalled equipment back to RTG’s warehouse for future disposition.</p><p>ix) Setting Alarm if managers or bakers are not onsite. The HIS Team/Overnight Project Support Team will</p><p>provide alarm code.</p><p>x) If a cafe manager is still on-site, the RTG Technician must checkout with the cafe manager as well</p><p><br></p><p>Rollback</p><p>i) If 1 or more of the new network access point or switch replacements cannot be completed, all existing access points must be returned to their original state prior to the start of the activity.</p><p><br></p><p>NETWORK SWITCH - If in scope:</p><p>Refer to Installation Guide for specific details:</p><p>i) Take before photos of the existing network switch.</p><p>ii) Deinstall the existing network switch. (BE SURE to note specific cables/ports to ensure new switch is connected properly - LABEL CABLES BEFORE DISCONNECTING SO YOU KNOW WHERE TO RECONNECT)</p><p>iii) Install the new network switch.</p><p>iv) Contact Panera NOC to complete configuration, testing, and validation steps.</p><p>v) Contact Panera Project Support to complete configuration, testing to ensure all devices are online and working, and validation steps.</p><p>vi) Take “after” photos of the network switch.</p><p>vii) Package deinstalled equipment in packaging that new equipment came in.</p><p>viii) Ship deinstalled equipment back to RTG’s warehouse for future disposition.</p><p>ix) Setting Alarm if managers or bakers are not onsite. The HIS Team/Overnight Project Support Team will</p><p>provide alarm code.</p><p>x) If a cafe manager is still on-site, the RTG Technician must checkout with the cafe manager as well.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>ROLLBACK</p><p>i) If the Network Switch cannot be completed, NOC may instruct Tech to reinstall the existing network switch.</p><p>ii) If 1 or more of the new access points cannot be completed, all existing access points must be reinstalled.</p><p>iii) Verify functionality with Panera NOC, then Project Support.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>TECH MUST BRING THE FOLLOWING:</p><p>- LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE IN CASE TROUBLESHOOTING OR CONFIGURATION IS REQUIRED</p><p>- A MINIMUM OF THREE 6' NETWORK PATCH CABLES IN CASE THERE ARE ISSUES WITH EXISTING CABLES (NOTE THE QTY USED FOR REIMBURSEMENT)</p><p>-EXTRA RACK SCREWS *NOT REQUIRED BUT HELPFUL IN CASE THE SCREWS SHIPPED DO NOT FIT THE EXISTING RACK</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>*MUST CONTACT PANERA PROJECT SUPPORT WHEN FINISHED TO CHECK OUT</p><p>** MUST UPLOAD PHOTOS OF SHIPPING RECEIPT TO WM TICKET</p><p><br></p><p>Notes:</p><p>Do not dispose of any removed access points</p><p>Package and handle all removed equipmeny according to the provided return or shipping instructions</p><p>Coordinate with Panera support before leaving to ensure the system is working as intended</p><p><br></p><p>Tools:</p><p>Screwdriver set (Phillips &amp; Flathead)</p><p>Nut driver set</p><p>Adjustable wrench</p><p>Pliers (Needle Nose &amp; Lineman's)</p><p>Wire strippers/cutters</p><p>Utility knife</p><p>Tape measure</p><p>Level</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Power Tools</p><p>Cordless Drill/Driver</p><p>Impact Driver</p><p>Drill Bit Set</p><p>Zip Ties</p><p>Velcro Straps</p><p>Electrical Tape</p><p>Labels</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Tool Bag</p><p>Extension Cord</p><p>Power Strip</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T14:30","end":"2026-10-08T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":64.70172505,"max":194.10517515},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":64.70172505,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":17.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $194.10517515 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-