{"job":{"id":20033998,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Troubleshoot Network","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.</em></strong></p><p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong>  Troubleshoot network.  Shop has no current network access</p><ul><li>Work with bridge support to troubleshoot and determine why the shop network is offline</li><li>Be prepared to replace cable if needed (Bring Cat6 cable)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Additional required materials and tools listed below.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">﻿</span></p><p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p><p>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</p><p>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>(1) box of CAT6 Cable </strong></li><li><strong>RJ45's</strong></li><li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li><li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li><li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li><li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop:</strong>&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li><li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li><li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li><strong>Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(8'-10' ladder)</li></ul>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n***TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.***\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:** Troubleshoot network. Shop has no current network access\n\n- Work with bridge support to troubleshoot and determine why the shop network is offline\n- Be prepared to replace cable if needed (Bring Cat6 cable)\n- Additional required materials and tools listed below.\n\n﻿\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nPlease ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.\n\nThe technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- **(1) box of CAT6 Cable**\n- **RJ45's**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T10:00","end":"2026-09-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"dist