{"job":{"id":20047248,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #237010 - POS on CBU | Omada Equipment Offline in Portal | Tech Requested","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><br><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> TP-LINK OMADA ER605 VPN ROUTER WARRANTY REPLACEMENT, NETWORK RACK TOPOLOGY AUDIT, PROVISIONING, RETURN LOGISTICS STAGING &amp; DUAL VERIFICATION</p><p><br></p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p>A network technician is required on-site to decommission a defective <strong>TP-Link Omada ER605 VPN Router</strong> and install a brand-new warranty replacement ER605 unit shipped directly to the location.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will conduct a comprehensive network rack topology audit with remote Support—mapping all incoming WAN ISP modem connections, core switch uplinks, Access Points, POS terminals, audio gateways, and CCTV drops. After swapping the hardware, the technician will coordinate directly with remote <strong>Activations</strong> to adopt the replacement ER605 into the Omada SDN Controller matrix (or configure static/DHCP WAN parameters), verify firewall routing, and confirm that all store operational systems are fully functional.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET RETURN STAGING MANDATE:</strong> A return shipping label has been provided in the shipment box. Carefully box up the defective ER605 unit and its original power supply into the replacement packaging. Affix the provided return shipping label securely to the outside of the box, seal it tightly with packaging tape, and hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area for return carrier pickup. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong> Record the return tracking number in the ticket notes prior to departure.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must receive explicit operational, topology, and network routing confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; PARTS</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for direct IP discovery, local ER605 web GUI standalone access, gateway ping sweeps, and speed testing)</li><li><strong>Pre-Fabricated Cat5e/6 Patch Cords (Assorted Lengths: 3ft, 7ft):</strong> Truck stock to replace any degraded network patch cables connecting WAN modems or switches</li><li><strong>Cable Tester &amp; Wire Toner</strong> (For verifying data drop continuity between the router, ISP modems, and network switches)</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits &amp; Precision Screwdrivers</strong> (For mounting or positioning hardware)</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong>, Label Maker, packaging tape, and permanent marker</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong>PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main IT network rack and collect the newly shipped replacement ER605 box and return label.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the cutover sequence, MAC address, serial number, and WAN configuration specs (DHCP/Static/PPPoE) before disconnecting active lines.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 2: NETWORK RACK TOPOLOGY AUDIT &amp; DECOMMISSIONING</strong><ol><li><strong>TOPOLOGY AUDIT (CRITICAL):</strong> Review and confirm the complete network rack topology with Support before removing any cables. Document and tag all interconnecting drops:</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Port 1 (WAN):</strong> ISP Modem / Fiber Gateway feed</li><li><strong>Port 2 (LAN):</strong> Primary Core Network Switch uplink</li><li><strong>Downstream Nodes:</strong> Omada Access Points, POS credit card terminals, Cloud Cover audio players, and NVR security systems</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>GRACEFUL SHUTDOWN:</strong> Power down the defective ER605 router under Support guidance. Disconnect power and Ethernet patch cords, then unmount or remove the unit from the rack frame/shelf.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 3: REPLACEMENT ER605 INSTALLATION &amp; CABLING</strong><ol><li><strong>HARDWARE MOUNTING:</strong> Securely position or rack-mount the replacement TP-Link ER605 router in the network cabinet.</li><li><strong>INTERFACE LANDING:</strong> Land the verified network cables into their exact corresponding ports on the new ER605 chassis:</li></ol><ul><li>ISP Modem drop to <strong>Port 1 (WAN)</strong></li><li>Core Switch drop to <strong>Port 2 (LAN)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>POWER INTEGRATION:</strong> Connect the power adapter directly into a battery-backed outlet on the rack UPS.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 4: PROVISIONING, OMADA ADOPTION &amp; SYSTEM AUDIT</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER RESTORATION &amp; ADOPTION:</strong> Power on the replacement ER605. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Provide remote support with the new unit's <strong>MAC Address and Serial Number</strong> to trigger Omada Controller adoption and push WAN/LAN subnets.</li><li><strong>DIAGNOSTIC VERIFICATION:</strong> Plug your diagnostic laptop into an open LAN switch port:</li></ol><ul><li>Perform continuous ping sweeps to local gateways ($192.168.x.x$ / $10.x.x.x$) and public DNS ($8.8.8.8$).</li><li>Run an internet speed test to confirm full ISP throughput.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>FULL SYSTEM OPERATIONAL AUDIT:</strong> Walk the facility with the store manager and verify with Support that <strong>ALL</strong> site systems maintain uninterrupted operational status:</li></ol><ul><li>POS registers and credit card processing</li><li>Wireless SSIDs broadcasting from Omada Access Points</li><li>Streaming audio media players</li><li>Back-office manager PCs and IP cameras</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 5: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:</strong> Carefully box up the defective warranty ER605 router and its power adapter into the replacement unit's box.</li><li><strong>LABELING &amp; HANDOVER:</strong> Affix the provided <strong>return shipping label</strong> securely to the outside of the box and seal it tightly with packaging tape. Hand the package directly to the MOD or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area for return carrier pickup. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Neatly bundle and dress all patch cables inside the rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Clean up packaging materials and dust, leaving the rack room completely spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New ER605 Router Installed &amp; Active:</strong> Close-up photo showing the replacement ER605 router mounted, powered on, with active WAN and LAN link LEDs.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Laptop Network Verification:</strong> Photo displaying your Ethernet-connected laptop screen showing successful IP configuration, ping sweep results, and passing speed test.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Boxed Defective ER605 w/ Return Label Attached:</strong> Clear photo showing the old defective unit boxed, sealed, with the provided return shipping label clearly visible prior to carrier pickup.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire IT network rack with the cabinet door OPEN</strong>, showing neat Velcro cable management.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and area surrounding the rack are swept completely clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that the replacement ER605 is fully adopted, WAN/LAN interfaces are stable, network rack topology is confirmed, and store telemetry is 100% operational.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Demonstrate active store system operations to the store manager, confirm return hardware staging, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update internal ticket notes detailing the exact Serial Numbers and MAC Addresses of both old and new ER605 units, WAN IP details, the <strong>Return Shipping Tracking Number</strong> from the label, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n  \n**TICKET SUMMARY:** TP-LINK OMADA ER605 VPN ROUTER WARRANTY REPLACEMENT, NETWORK RACK TOPOLOGY AUDIT, PROVISIONING, RETURN LOGISTICS STAGING & DUAL VERIFICATION\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A network technician is required on-site to decommission a defective **TP-Link Omada ER605 VPN Router** and install a brand-new warranty replacement ER605 unit shipped directly to the location.\n\nThe technician will conduct a comprehensive network rack topology audit with remote Support—mapping all incoming WAN ISP modem connections, core switch uplinks, Access Points, POS terminals, audio gateways, and CCTV drops. After swapping the hardware, the technician will coordinate directly with remote **Activations** to adopt the replacement ER605 into the Omada SDN Controller matrix (or configure static/DHCP WAN parameters), verify firewall routing, and confirm that all store operational systems are fully functional.\n\n**DEFECTIVE ASSET RETURN STAGING MANDATE:** A return shipping label has been provided in the shipment box. Carefully box up the defective ER605 unit and its original power supply into the replacement packaging. Affix the provided return shipping label securely to the outside of the box, seal it tightly with packaging tape, and hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area for return carrier pickup. **Do not remove hardware from the property.** Record the return tracking number in the ticket notes prior to departure.\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must receive explicit operational, topology, and network routing confirmation from remote **Activations** and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & PARTS**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for direct IP discovery, local ER605 web GUI standalone access, gateway ping sweeps, and speed testing)\n- **Pre-Fabricated Cat5e/6 Patch Cords (Assorted Lengths: 3ft, 7ft):** Truck stock to replace any degraded network patch cables connecting WAN modems or switches\n- **Cable Tester & Wire Toner** (For verifying data drop continuity between the router, ISP modems, and network switches)\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits & Precision Screwdrivers** (For mounting or positioning hardware)\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties**, Label Maker, packaging tape, and permanent marker\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main IT network rack and collect the newly shipped replacement ER605 box and return label.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the cutover sequence, MAC address, serial number, and WAN configuration specs (DHCP/Static/PPPoE) before disconnecting active lines.\n\n**PHASE 2: NETWORK RACK TOPOLOGY AUDIT & DECOMMISSIONING**1. **TOPOLOGY AUDIT (CRITICAL):** Review and confirm the complete network rack topology with Support before removing any cables. Document and tag all interconnecting drops:\n\n- **Port 1 (WAN):** ISP Modem / Fiber Gateway feed\n- **Port 2 (LAN):** Primary Core Network Switch uplink\n- **Downstream Nodes:** Omada Access Points, POS credit card terminals, Cloud Cover audio players, and NVR security systems\n\n1. **GRACEFUL SHUTDOWN:** Power down the defective ER605 router under Support guidance. Disconnect power and Ethernet patch cords, then unmount or remove the unit from the rack frame/shelf.\n\n**PHASE 3: REPLACEMENT ER605 INSTALLATION & CABLING**1. **HARDWARE MOUNTING:** Securely position or rack-mount the replacement TP-Link ER605 router in the network cabinet.\n2. **INTERFACE LANDING:** Land the verified network cables into their exact corresponding ports on the new ER605 chassis:\n\n- ISP Modem drop to **Port 1 (WAN)**\n- Core Switch drop to **Port 2 (LAN)**\n\n1. **POWER INTEGRATION:** Connect the power adapter directly into a battery-backed outlet on the rack UPS.\n\n**PHASE 4: PROVISIONING, OMADA ADOPTION & SYSTEM AUDIT**1. **POWER RESTORATION & ADOPTION:** Power on the replacement ER605. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Provide remote support with the new unit's **MAC Address and Serial Number** to trigger Omada Controller adoption and push WAN/LAN subnets.\n2. **DIAGNOSTIC VERIFICATION:** Plug your diagnostic laptop into an open LAN switch port:\n\n- Perform continuous ping sweeps to local gateways ($192.168.x.x$ / $10.x.x.x$) and public DNS ($8.8.8.8$).\n- Run an internet speed test to confirm full ISP throughput.\n\n1. **FULL SYSTEM OPERATIONAL AUDIT:** Walk the facility with the store manager and verify with Support that **ALL** site systems maintain uninterrupted operational status:\n\n- POS registers and credit card processing\n- Wireless SSIDs broadcasting from Omada Access Points\n- Streaming audio media players\n- Back-office manager PCs and IP cameras\n\n**PHASE 5: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**1. **DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:** Carefully box up the defective warranty ER605 router and its power adapter into the replacement unit's box.\n2. **LABELING & HANDOVER:** Affix the provided **return shipping label** securely to the outside of the box and seal it tightly with packaging tape. Hand the package directly to the MOD or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area for return carrier pickup. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n3. **CLEANUP:** Neatly bundle and dress all patch cables inside the rack using **Velcro ties**. Clean up packaging materials and dust, leaving the rack room completely spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New ER605 Router Installed & Active:** Close-up photo showing the replacement ER605 router mounted, powered on, with active WAN and LAN link LEDs.\n- \\[ \\] **Laptop Network Verification:** Photo displaying your Ethernet-connected laptop screen showing successful IP configuration, ping sweep results, and passing speed test.\n- \\[ \\] **Boxed Defective ER605 w/ Return Label Attached:** Clear photo showing the old defective unit boxed, sealed, with the provided return shipping label clearly visible prior to carrier pickup.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire IT network rack with the cabinet door OPEN**, showing neat Velcro cable management.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and area surrounding the rack are swept completely clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that the replacement ER605 is fully adopted, WAN/LAN interfaces are stable, network rack topology is confirmed, and store telemetry is 100% operational.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Demonstrate active store system operations to the store manager, confirm return hardware staging, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update internal ticket notes detailing the exact Serial Numbers and MAC Addresses of both old and new ER605 units, WAN IP details, the **Return Shipping Tracking Number** from the label, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T19:00","end":"2026-09-29T21:00","latestStart":"2026-09-29T21:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 1, 9:00 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $200\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026