{"job":{"id":20045537,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"IRM START | QSIC Pendant Speaker Installation [Tech 1 / Lead Tech] This ticket will be assigned as requested is terms are agreed to.","description":{"html":"<p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician</u></strong></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Important</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></li><li>These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</li><li><strong>Penalties Apply IF you do not</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do Not Call&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong>&nbsp;if you are exceeding&nbsp;<strong>4 Hours Onsite</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>&nbsp;<strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">\"Pendant Speakers\" by mounting to the ceiling.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V&ndash;15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.</span></li><li><strong><u>Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide &ndash;</u></strong>&nbsp;any questions or issues need to be escalated to the&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li>Techs <strong>MUST</strong> PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!</li><li><strong><u>Techs&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.</li><li>Technicians (Tech 1/Lead &amp; Assist)&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;complete the Essintial Online Deliverable &ndash; Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.</li><li><strong>Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work&nbsp;</strong>-<strong>One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech</strong>&nbsp;and the other technician will be designated as an&nbsp;<strong>Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST</strong>.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Communication Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>ALL installation questions must go to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;call&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite &ndash; You MUST obtain approval!!!</strong></li><li>Technicians <strong>MUST</strong> Check-In and Check-Out with the <strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li><li>Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi</li><li>Standard Hand Tools</li><li>10Ft-12Ft Ladder</li><li>Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)</li><li>Long fiberglass push rods</li><li>wire strippers</li><li>Electrical Dykes</li><li>Utility Knife</li><li>Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors</li><li>Multi-meter&nbsp;- Capable of reading Ohms</li><li>Small Alan wrench &ndash; for pendant lock</li><li>Small Phillips and flat head screw driver</li><li>Micro flathead screwdriver</li><li>Laser Distance Measure &amp; Tape Measure</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Government Issued ID</li><li>LOA &ndash; Letter of Authorization</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Bill of Material:</u></strong>&nbsp;Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;FIRM START TIME!!!! YOU MUST ARRIVE AT ONTIME BASED ON THE START TIME SET BY ESSINTIAL. You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;</strong>4 Hours, If you are approaching that time, you must contact&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Technical Support&nbsp;</strong>to gain approval. If you cannot start work immediately, please reach out to Essintial and gain guidance.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li><li>&nbsp;This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(247, 10, 10);\"><em><u>Important Note:&nbsp;</u></em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>LOA &ndash; Letter of Authorization -&nbsp;DG Media Network Audio System Installation</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link [</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">MUST BE PRINTED</strong><strong>]</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk42/DWfTfK4eWhH6.idtwsbiv2oPzIZBbP.VLjiAt6hIisI</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dollar General Installation Guide &ndash; 2026</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk41/ED1SkYNAzCnYrokC3tVlbVa4ZHs4Qr_TyUc80z_oDYE</li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&ndash;if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager: Introduce yourself as the QSIC Technician onsite for the Speaker Install Project, present the LOA and Verify Store Number</strong></li><li><strong>Call &amp; Check-In with</strong> the <strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>REFER TO and FOLLOW Instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide - Any questions escalate to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li><strong>Ensure you clean up after yourself and dispose of any trash</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm device operation with Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Complete and Submit Online Deliverable</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to upload requested photos (Tech 1 / Lead Tech)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">Call &amp; Check-Out</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">&nbsp;with the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">to review/gain deliverable approval and perform your final check out</span></li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code</li><li>Provide DETAILED notes of the work that took place including any problems and resolutions steps taken</li><li>Provide DETAILED notes of any problems onsite that would have caused a delay over 4 hours<span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related Questions and Any Issues onsite / Related to the scope of work should be escalated directly to the&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Out of Scope Information</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>If you are asked to do anything onsite that is outside of the work scope on this work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.</li><li>If the instruction you are receiving onsite deviates from what is listed on your work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.</li><li>If the work onsite is about to go over the scoped/estimated time onsite, you MUST call Essintial immediately to provide the reason for going over that timeframe. You will also be required to provide this reason upon close out on your Online Deliverable.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**IMPORTANT:**\n\n- **You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician**\n- **Important**: Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite\n- **Dress Code: Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n- These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- **Penalties Apply IF you do not**\n- PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!\n- Do Not Call **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** if you are exceeding **4 Hours Onsite**\n- Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site\n- Techs **MUST** Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site\n\n**Required Skills:** Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well\n\n**Scope of Work Overview:**\n\n- **Scope of Work:** Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 \"Pendant Speakers\" by mounting to the ceiling. Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V–15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.\n- **Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide –** any questions or issues need to be escalated to the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- Techs **MUST** PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!\n- **Techs MUST** stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.\n- Technicians (Tech 1/Lead & Assist) **MUST** complete the Essintial Online Deliverable – Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.\n- **Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work** -**One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech** and the other technician will be designated as an **Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST**.\n\n**Communication Requirements**\n\n- ALL installation questions must go to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- **Tech MUST** call **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite – You MUST obtain approval!!!**\n- Technicians **MUST** Check-In and Check-Out with the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- 6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi\n- Standard Hand Tools\n- 10Ft-12Ft Ladder\n- Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)\n- Long fiberglass push rods\n- wire strippers\n- Electrical Dykes\n- Utility Knife\n- Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors\n- Multi-meter - Capable of reading Ohms\n- Small Alan wrench – for pendant lock\n- Small Phillips and flat head screw driver\n- Micro flathead screwdriver\n- Laser Distance Measure & Tape Measure\n- Velcro\n- Label maker\n- Government Issued ID\n- LOA – Letter of Authorization\n\n**Bill of Material:** Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n **SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** FIRM START TIME!!!! YOU MUST ARRIVE AT ONTIME BASED ON THE START TIME SET BY ESSINTIAL. You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n- **Estimated Duration:** 4 Hours, If you are approaching that time, you must contact **Essintial Technical Support** to gain approval. If you cannot start work immediately, please reach out to Essintial and gain guidance.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.** Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **LOA – Letter of Authorization - DG Media Network Audio System Installation** **Link \\[****MUST BE PRINTED****\\]**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk42/DWfTfK4eWhH6.idtwsbiv2oPzIZBbP.VLjiAt6hIisI>\n- **Dollar General Installation Guide – 2026** **Link**: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk41/ED1SkYNAzCnYrokC3tVlbVa4ZHs4Qr_TyUc80z_oDYE\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER**–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager: Introduce yourself as the QSIC Technician onsite for the Speaker Install Project, present the LOA and Verify Store Number**\n- **Call & Check-In with** the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n**ONSITE:**\n\n- REFER TO and FOLLOW Instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide - Any questions escalate to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- **Ensure you clean up after yourself and dispose of any trash**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- Confirm device operation with Onsite POC\n- **Complete and Submit Online Deliverable** (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):\n- Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details\n- Tech will be asked to upload requested photos (Tech 1 / Lead Tech)\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.\n- **Call & Check-Out** with the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** to review/gain deliverable approval and perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code\n- Provide DETAILED notes of the work that took place including any problems and resolutions steps taken\n- Provide DETAILED notes of any problems onsite that would have caused a delay over 4 hours\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related Questions and Any Issues onsite / Related to the scope of work should be escalated directly to the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n **Out of Scope Information:**\n\n- If you are asked to do anything onsite that is outside of the work scope on this work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the instruction you are receiving onsite deviates from what is listed on your work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the work onsite is about to go over the scoped/estimated time onsite, you MUST call Essintial immediately to provide the reason for going over that timeframe. You will also be required to provide this reason upon close out on your Online Deliverable.\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** **Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T07:45","end":"2026-10-08T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":190},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":36},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $190 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00