{"job":{"id":20051727,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Trick Dog Technology","title":"Decommission Network Equipment, Ship Back to Client, and E-Waste Select Equipment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Pre-Visit:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You will be arriving onsite as a Trick Dog Technician, please introduce yourself to the End User(s) accordingly. (Do NOT reference Field Nation while on-site at any time)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dress Code is Business Casual​ (Khakis/clean jeans, collared shirt, closed-toed shoes)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You are NOT to discuss pricing with anyone at any time other than with Trick Dog</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><u>Check in and out on Platform with GPS Enabled</u></p>\n<p>**NOTE: Do not discuss Pricing or Mention Field Nation**</p>\n<p>Technical Contact: <strong><del>**** ******* ************</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Any Escalated Issues: Trick Dog: 800-643-6079</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Completion Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>End-User's Signature on Completion Report</li>\n<li>Documentation (Pictures) of Work Completed -<strong>Note:</strong> Please <u>Label</u> Pictures for Identification</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work&nbsp;</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> The location is shutting down and the assigned tech will de-install all of the noted equipment, bubble wrap and return to <del>*** *****</del> using the supplied Fedex shipping labels. The assigned tech will also e-waste recycle the battery back-up UPS, along with the Trendnet and Lantronix network switches.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Please Bring:</strong> Packing Boxes, Packaging Materials, Bubble Wrap, 8ft Ladder, CAT6 Cabling/Patch Cables, Toner/Tester/Termination Tools and Ends, Cable Management Material, Labels, Handtools, Laptop with Hotspot, and Console Cable</p>\n<p>*All Material Reimbursed Separately</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>﻿Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide all tools and materials necessary to complete network decomission</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check in with Technical Contact and site contact upon arrival</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify equipment location(s) with site contact</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Inventory equipment, verify no damage or missing items</p>\n<p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Report any issues to Project Manager and site contact</p>\n<p>Decommission the following pieces of equipment:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cisco 9200 24 port switch</li>\n<li>AT&amp;T ANIRA U120</li>\n<li>Meraki wireless access point</li>\n<li>UPS battery back-up</li>\n<li>POE injector on wall behind rack</li>\n<li>OpenEye surveillance system and related Trendnet / Lantronix network switches.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once removed package the Cisco switch, ANIRA device, Meraki access point and POE injector securely in boxes with plenty of bubble wrap and packing materials.</p>\n<p>Prepare the following equipment for e-waste/recyle:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>UPS battery back-up</li>\n<li>Trendnet / Lantronix network switches</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once everything is prepared transport the equipment being shipped back to the client to FedEX and use the client provided shipping labels.</p>\n<p>Transport the other equipment for e-waste/recycling.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clean up debris (if applicable) and dispose on site in area as designated by site contact</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify with site contact that all gear has been successfully removed</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take pictures of completed decommission</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check out with TDT and site contact prior to departing site</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Ticket Closeout: Required for Payment!</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If out of scope if requested, you must fill out the <em>Change Order</em> attachment.&nbsp;No additional approvals will be granted without this documentation.</li>\n<li>Please upload at <em>Minimum</em> 5 photos. Take close up pictures of the hardware that you worked with and far away pictures of the entire work area</li>\n<li>Provide detailed <em>Closing Notes</em> which include how long you were onsite and exactly what was done.&nbsp;If additional work&nbsp;is needed, list it here.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>The onsite contact must sign the attached <em>Sign Off</em>sheet.&nbsp;Pictures of signatures will not be approved.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Trick Dog Standard Suggested Tool Kit</u> (if you think you MIGHT need it, bring it!):</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;BRING DRILL if installing a TV</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Laptop</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Smart Phone</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Phone tools (toners, punch down tools, crimpers, etc.)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Cat 5/6 tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch down tools, etc.)</p>\n<p>· Cat5e/Cat6 Cabling</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Basic hand tools (screwdriver kit, etc)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Voltage meter/Tone Generator and Probe</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Assortment of parts, including but not limited to, wall jacks, patch-cords, cabling connectors, etc.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;Ladder</p>","markdown":"**Pre-Visit:**\n\n· You will be arriving onsite as a Trick Dog Technician, please introduce yourself to the End User(s) accordingly. (Do NOT reference Field Nation while on-site at any time)\n\n· Dress Code is Business Casual​ (Khakis/clean jeans, collared shirt, closed-toed shoes)\n\n· You are NOT to discuss pricing with anyone at any time other than with Trick Dog\n\nCheck in and out on Platform with GPS Enabled\n\n\\*\\*NOTE: Do not discuss Pricing or Mention Field Nation\\*\\*\n\nTechnical Contact: **\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Any Escalated Issues: Trick Dog: 800-643-6079**\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n- End-User's Signature on Completion Report\n- Documentation (Pictures) of Work Completed -**Note:** Please Label Pictures for Identification\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Description:** The location is shutting down and the assigned tech will de-install all of the noted equipment, bubble wrap and return to \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* using the supplied Fedex shipping labels. The assigned tech will also e-waste recycle the battery back-up UPS, along with the Trendnet and Lantronix network switches.\n\n**Please Bring:** Packing Boxes, Packaging Materials, Bubble Wrap, 8ft Ladder, CAT6 Cabling/Patch Cables, Toner/Tester/Termination Tools and Ends, Cable Management Material, Labels, Handtools, Laptop with Hotspot, and Console Cable\n\n\\*All Material Reimbursed Separately\n\n**﻿Instructions:**\n\n· Provide all tools and materials necessary to complete network decomission\n\n· Check in with Technical Contact and site contact upon arrival\n\n· Verify equipment location(s) with site contact\n\n· Inventory equipment, verify no damage or missing items\n\no Report any issues to Project Manager and site contact\n\nDecommission the following pieces of equipment:\n\n- Cisco 9200 24 port switch\n- AT&T ANIRA U120\n- Meraki wireless access point\n- UPS battery back-up\n- POE injector on wall behind rack\n- OpenEye surveillance system and related Trendnet / Lantronix network switches.\n\nOnce removed package the Cisco switch, ANIRA device, Meraki access point and POE injector securely in boxes with plenty of bubble wrap and packing materials.\n\nPrepare the following equipment for e-waste/recyle:\n\n- UPS battery back-up\n- Trendnet / Lantronix network switches\n\nOnce everything is prepared transport the equipment being shipped back to the client to FedEX and use the client provided shipping labels.\n\nTransport the other equipment for e-waste/recycling.\n\n· Clean up debris (if applicable) and dispose on site in area as designated by site contact\n\n· Verify with site contact that all gear has been successfully removed\n\n· Take pictures of completed decommission\n\n· Check out with TDT and site contact prior to departing site\n\n**Ticket Closeout: Required for Payment!**\n\n- If out of scope if requested, you must fill out the *Change Order* attachment. No additional approvals will be granted without this documentation.\n- Please upload at *Minimum* 5 photos. Take close up pictures of the hardware that you worked with and far away pictures of the entire work area\n- Provide detailed *Closing Notes* which include how long you were onsite and exactly what was done. If additional work is needed, list it here.\n- The onsite contact must sign the attached *Sign Off*sheet. Pictures of signatures will not be approved.\n\n**Trick Dog Standard Suggested Tool Kit (if you think you MIGHT need it, bring it!):**\n\n· BRING DRILL if installing a TV\n\n· Laptop\n\n· Smart Phone\n\n· Phone tools (toners, punch down tools, crimpers, etc.)\n\n· Cat 5/6 tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch down tools, etc.)\n\n· Cat5e/Cat6 Cabling\n\n· Basic hand tools (screwdriver kit, etc)\n\n· Voltage meter/Tone Generator and Probe\n\n· Assortment of parts, including but not limited to, wall jacks, patch-cords, cabling connectors, etc.\n\n· Ladder","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T09:00","end":"2026-10-02T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":21},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790638033159}
{"job":{"id":20052057,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Trick Dog Technology","title":"Install M.2 Boot Device(s) and Mounting Hardware in Nutanix Server","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Pre-Visit:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You will be arriving onsite as a <del>*** ********** *********</del> Technician, please introduce yourself to the End User(s) accordingly. (Do NOT reference Field Nation while on-site at any time)</li>\n<li>Print attached work order and any additional attachments, bring with you to site</li>\n<li>Dress Code is Business Casual​ (Khakis/clean jeans, collared shirt, closed-toed shoes)</li>\n<li>You are NOT to discuss pricing with anyone at any time other than with Trick Dog</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><u>Check in and out on Platform with GPS Enabled</u></p>\n<p>**NOTE: Do not discuss Pricing or Mention Field Nation**</p>\n<p>Technical Contact: <del>** ********** **** **** ********** ************</del></p>\n<p><strong>Any Escalated Issues: Trick Dog: 800-643-6079</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Daily Project Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician is to provide daily progress/completion information prior to leaving site (To include work performed/completed and status of remaining work) - Messageboard Updates or calls are acceptable</li>\n<li>Documentation (Pictures) of all Cabling is required - Pictures to include visibility of cable management at both end points (closet and device) - <strong>Note:</strong> Please Label all Pictures upon upload</li>\n<li>Documentation (Pictures) of all devices implemented (or worked on) - Pictures need to also include workspace to confirm SOW work area has been cleaned - <strong>Note:</strong> Please Label all Pictures upon upload</li>\n<li>Note: Any work requested outside of the scope will need to be documented in Change Order (attachment) and will need approval prior to completing</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work&nbsp;</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\n<p>Install M.2 boot device(s) and the associated mounting hardware in existing, racked Nutanix server.</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Provided Materials (Reimbursement in Additional Expenses)</strong>:</p>\n<p>If expenses are necessary to complete the services (hardware/software/supplies), these will be billed back to the customer</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Task List:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide all tools necessary to complete the project</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Required Skillset: Field Engineer experienced with enterprise server hardware and data center procedures</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Required: Supply standard ESD-safe hand tools and follow appropriate electrostatic-discharge precautions</li>\n<li>Check in with Project Manager upon arrival</li>\n<li>Complete the following tasks:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check in and comply with all site security, escort, safety, and access requirements</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Locate and positively identify the designated Nutanix NX-1175S-g8 server</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow the approved server shutdown or maintenance procedure communicated for the dispatch</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the customer-supplied M.2 boot device(s) in server</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Swap the HBA controller with the correct one client has previously shipped on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Recable the HBA with the storage drives via the cables provided on site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note: Client will handle all post installation imaging, AOS/AHV activities, configuration, testing, and commissioning</li>\n<li>Take pictures of the completed project</li>\n<li>Check out with Project Manager and site contact prior to departing site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Trick Dog Standard Suggested Tool Kit</u> (if you think you MIGHT need it, bring it!):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Smart Phone</li>\n<li>Cat 5/6 Cabling and Tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch down tools, etc.)</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools (screwdriver kit, etc)</li>\n<li>Assortment of parts, including but not limited to, wall jacks, patch-cords, cabling connectors, etc.</li>\n<li>Ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Ticket Closeout: Required for Payment!</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If out of scope if requested, you must fill out the <em>Change Order</em> attachment.&nbsp;No additional approvals will be granted without this documentation.</li>\n<li>Please upload at <em>Minimum</em> 5 photos. Take close up pictures of the hardware that you worked with and far away pictures of the entire work area</li>\n<li>Provide detailed <em>Closing Notes</em> which include how long you were onsite and exactly what was done.&nbsp;If additional work&nbsp;is needed, list it here.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>The onsite contact must sign the attached <em>Sign Off</em>sheet.&nbsp;Pictures of signatures will not be approved.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Pre-Visit:**\n\n- You will be arriving onsite as a \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Technician, please introduce yourself to the End User(s) accordingly. (Do NOT reference Field Nation while on-site at any time)\n- Print attached work order and any additional attachments, bring with you to site\n- Dress Code is Business Casual​ (Khakis/clean jeans, collared shirt, closed-toed shoes)\n- You are NOT to discuss pricing with anyone at any time other than with Trick Dog\n\nCheck in and out on Platform with GPS Enabled\n\n\\*\\*NOTE: Do not discuss Pricing or Mention Field Nation\\*\\*\n\nTechnical Contact: \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Any Escalated Issues: Trick Dog: 800-643-6079**\n\n**Daily Project Requirements:**\n\n- Technician is to provide daily progress/completion information prior to leaving site (To include work performed/completed and status of remaining work) - Messageboard Updates or calls are acceptable\n- Documentation (Pictures) of all Cabling is required - Pictures to include visibility of cable management at both end points (closet and device) - **Note:** Please Label all Pictures upon upload\n- Documentation (Pictures) of all devices implemented (or worked on) - Pictures need to also include workspace to confirm SOW work area has been cleaned - **Note:** Please Label all Pictures upon upload\n- Note: Any work requested outside of the scope will need to be documented in Change Order (attachment) and will need approval prior to completing\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Description:**\n\nInstall M.2 boot device(s) and the associated mounting hardware in existing, racked Nutanix server.\n\n**Technician Provided Materials (Reimbursement in Additional Expenses)**:\n\nIf expenses are necessary to complete the services (hardware/software/supplies), these will be billed back to the customer\n\n**Technician Task List:**\n\n- Provide all tools necessary to complete the project\n- Required Skillset: Field Engineer experienced with enterprise server hardware and data center procedures\n- Required: Supply standard ESD-safe hand tools and follow appropriate electrostatic-discharge precautions\n- Check in with Project Manager upon arrival\n- Complete the following tasks:\n- Check in and comply with all site security, escort, safety, and access requirements\n- Locate and positively identify the designated Nutanix NX-1175S-g8 server\n- Follow the approved server shutdown or maintenance procedure communicated for the dispatch\n- Install the customer-supplied M.2 boot device(s) in server\n- Swap the HBA controller with the correct one client has previously shipped on-site\n- Recable the HBA with the storage drives via the cables provided on site\n- Note: Client will handle all post installation imaging, AOS/AHV activities, configuration, testing, and commissioning\n- Take pictures of the completed project\n- Check out with Project Manager and site contact prior to departing site\n\n**Trick Dog Standard Suggested Tool Kit (if you think you MIGHT need it, bring it!):**\n\n- Laptop\n- Smart Phone\n- Cat 5/6 Cabling and Tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch down tools, etc.)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdriver kit, etc)\n- Assortment of parts, including but not limited to, wall jacks, patch-cords, cabling connectors, etc.\n- Ladder\n\n**Ticket Closeout: Required for Payment!**\n\n- If out of scope if requested, you must fill out the *Change Order* attachment. No additional approvals will be granted without this documentation.\n- Please upload at *Minimum* 5 photos. Take close up pictures of the hardware that you worked with and far away pictures of the entire work area\n- Provide detailed *Closing Notes* which include how long you were onsite and exactly what was done. If additional work is needed, list it here.\n- The onsite contact must sign the attached *Sign Off*sheet. Pictures of signatures will not be approved.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":180,"max":180},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":52},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"