{"job":{"id":"9209244225","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install","description":"DESCRIPTION: SOW - EPIK Single Visit Install <br>*************************************************************************************<br>Technician will be working with the Granite Project Team and the Epik Activations Team on the bridge below. Please dial into the bridge below to assist with the cutover: 929-229-2436, Passcode: 700 704 512#<br>We will be connecting to Switch 2, Port 26 for network connection.<br>We will only be cutting over sites fire and security lines, the site may or may not have a fax line, this is NOT to be cutover.<br> <br>Before Arrival <br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival. <br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK: <br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo <br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below. <br>On Arrival <br>1.Check in on WorkMarket. <br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location. <br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work. <br>EPIK Install Requirements <br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik. <br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location.  <br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard. <br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on. <br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions. <br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard: <br>https://wizard.epik.io <br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned. <br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES <br>7.If not already stated in the TNs to be wired section of your ticket, confirm with site contact if there are fire alarm, security alarm, elevator or e911 lines on site. If so, notify activations of any port configuration changes that need to be made and complete testing with the fire, security or elevator monitoring companies. <br>8.For any lines that cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number. <br>9.If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready. <br>Checkout Requirement <br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line. <br>2.Confirm Activations has released you. <br>3.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables. <br>4.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket. <br>5.Check out on WorkMarket. <br> <br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket. <br> <br>Required Deliverables <br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout: <br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install. <br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block. <br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable. <br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet. <br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions. <br> <br> <br>Required Tools <br>•Laptop <br>•Smartphone with hotspot <br>•Tone generator and wand <br>•66/110 punch tool <br>•Butt set <br>•       Infrared Temperature Gun  <br>•Electrician scissors <br>•Step ladder <br>•Flashlight/headlamp <br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper <br>•Ethernet cable tester <br>•Impact drill / cordless drill <br>•Masonry bits <br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits <br>•Needle-nose pliers <br>•Label maker and label tape <br>•Cat3 or better cable <br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable <br>•Cross-connect wire <br>•Gel-crimp connectors <br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware <br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks <br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini <br>************************************************************************************* <br> <br>PM SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS GUIDELINES <br>Special Instructions <br>Install Location <br>Enter where the EPIK device should be installed, including MDF/IDF/telco room location, wall/rack/shelf mounting instructions, and access notes. <br>________________________________________ <br>Cable Runs <br>Enter any required cable runs, cable type, distance, start/end points, and whether ladder, lift, ceiling access, or special tools are needed. <br>________________________________________ <br>Network Information <br>Enter switch name, switch port, DHCP/static IP details, VLAN info, and customer network escalation contact. <br>________________________________________ <br>External Antenna <br>Enter whether an external antenna is required, where it should be mounted, and any cable path or photo requirements. <br>________________________________________ <br>Special Testing <br>Enter any customer-specific testing that must be completed, including specific TNs, fax, alarm, elevator, hunt group, auto attendant, or other required testing. <br>________________________________________ <br>Customer Contacts <br>Enter primary LCON, backup contact, customer IT contact, site manager, and escalation contacts. <br>________________________________________ <br>Vendor / Third-Party Info <br>Enter any VTM, customer tech, alarm vendor, elevator vendor, fax vendor, MSP, or other third-party contact information.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":14.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 12, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790686319019}
{"job":{"id":"1950837865","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tekumo","title":"**CERTIFIED WEIGHTS AND MEASURES** SCANNER SCALE - NCR 7878-5001 - APEX, NC","description":"<p><strong><u>**WHILE ONSITE, YOU ARE TO REPRESENT&nbsp;</u></strong><u>POMEROY&nbsp;</u><strong><u>ONLY**</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Technical Support :</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Pomeroy Technical Support - 704-414-5111 Open 8am-8pm EST&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Techs need to send a message in the platform immediately if they’re going beyond TIME TO TASK for client approval.&nbsp;<strong>*** TECHS WILL BE ONLY PAID FOR ALLOTTED TIME UNLESS THEY GET APPROVAL FROM TEKUMO FOR AN EXTENSION ***&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Technicians must provide full closeout notes, photos and answers to all custom field questions prior to departing the site. Failure to update ticket on the same day of completion may result in the ticket being cancelled with $0 pay.</p><p><strong><em>Technicians are NOT to reach out customers nor clients regarding payment(s) for ANY reason. If this is NOT followed, you will be blocked from completing future work.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p>Recalibrate or Replace Scanner Scale (NCR 7878) on ECO 6 On Site Contact Name: Manager On Duty On Site Contact Phone: 8667112534 On Site Contact Email: Problem Type: WILL NOT CALIBRATE Location Subtype: ECO 6 Lane Number (if applicable): ECO 6 Client Ticket Number/External Reference ID: REQ2905388</p><p><br></p><p>TRS Link: https://trs.pomeroy.com/aldi-foods/scalesscanners/scanner-scale/datalogic-9800i</p><p>Arrival Time:&nbsp;If parts are shipped then track parts and run call within 2 hours of delivery. If not run the call between 9 am and 3 pm the day the call is due.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Print the scanner tags (attached) and bring them with you.&nbsp;Needed in case the scanner needs to be programmed.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview: </u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prior to Arrival - Read the full Scope of work</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prior to Arrival - Open and review the instructions for this scope of work,</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate the equipment/parts</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take “Before” photos of the Equipment location.</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>If support is needed, contact Pomeroy @</strong> <strong>704-414-5111</strong></p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Do not contact Aldi for support, unless instructed to do so by Pomeroy</em></strong></p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Complete the service Tasks and verify the device functionality</p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take “After” photos and MOD signature</p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All Parts are sent to the site : See Below for Recovery Details:</p><ul><li>If the parts were shipped via UPS you are required to take the parts with you and return them to Pomeroy with the label provided.<strong> If Support advises you otherwise it is NOT Correct. </strong>If you do not have a label, please reach out Tekumo to request one. If the parts were shipped via FedEx, the part stays onsite unless the customer asks you to ship it back.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p>10.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upload full closing notes</p><p>11.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Drop the parts off at the Carrier (Fed Ex or UPS) and log the return tracking number. If a return label is needed please contact Tekumo Via the ticket portal&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Tools Required</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Only accept this job if you have all the required tools and are able to make the required time frame.</strong></p><ul><li>Basic Set of Tools (pliers, screw drivers, cutters, etc.)</li><li>PS2 Keyboard</li><li>VGA monitor and cable</li><li>Attached Documents with printed out scan bars</li><li>Certified Weights and Measures Kit w/seals</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Only accept this job if you have all the required tools, and are able to make the required time frame.</p><p><strong><u>Parts Handling:</u></strong></p><ul><li>It is the responsibility of the assigned tech to track parts. Tekumo will provide tracking numbers for any shipped parts when they become available.</li><li>Tekumo is NOT responsible for techs arriving before parts and will NOT compensate for unnecessary trips or wait time.</li><li>Parts are shipped direct to store (If no tracking number has been provided by 10am the morning of the assignment, it is up to YOU, the Provider, to call the Pomeroy Dispatch Center to get the tracking number.&nbsp;If no parts onsite, continue troubleshooting and if determined parts are needed and they are not onsite, you are clear to leave the site.</li><li>Part shipped may be exact replacement or an upgrade. Contact Pomeroy Level 2 support to verify the model shipped before reporting a wrong part has been shipped.</li><li>All Parts are sent to the site : See Below for Recovery Details:</li><li>If the parts were shipped via UPS you are required to take the parts with you and return them to Pomeroy with the label provided.<strong> If Support advises you otherwise it is NOT Correct. </strong>If you do not have a label, please reach out Tekumo to request one. If the parts were shipped via FedEx, the part stays onsite unless the customer asks you to ship it back.&nbsp;</li><li><strong> Technician may be charged a $50 penalty if parts are not returned.</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Expectations and Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses must be preauthorized prior to accepting work order.</li><li>Clear and detailed notes describing all equipment locations and troubleshooting steps taken, results, and next steps (if applicable).</li><li>Before and after photos of the equipment location. Ensure photos include points of reference to identify equipment location.</li><li>Photos of serial numbers for all equipment, tracking numbers on packaging (if applicable), damaged or missing or wrong components, obstructions in accessing equipment, etc.</li><li>Record the names and titles of anyone involved in troubleshooting or confirming equipment is operational including&nbsp;on&nbsp;site personnel, GSD or Pomeroy Support.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>The Technician must provide full closeout notes, photos and answers to all custom field questions prior to departing the site. Failure to update ticket on the same day of completion may result in the ticket being cancelled with $0 pay.&nbsp;NA will be considered an unacceptable response</strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T15:00","end":"2026-09-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":49.5,"max":99},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":49.5,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $99 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.00