er – Required software including PuTTY</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of troubleshooting**:\n\nInstall connectivity from MDF to IDF. Media converters and SFP's.\n\nINC20179511\n\n**Business Hours Incident Response Bridge link:**\n\n**<https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/26809198614046?p=p4xHzUyAuo92c1AvpG>**\n\n**After Hours Incident Response Bridge Link:**\n\n**Microsoft Teams meeting**\n\n**Join:** <https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/29422196459548?p=rBtWwVHLDFnXA1ZmYR>\n\nMeeting ID: 294 221 964 595 48\n\nPasscode: bU2PZ6r9\n\n**IMPORTANT:** REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!\n\n**Technician’s Required Toolkit**\n\nTechnicians are **REQUIRED** to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper\n\nuse of each of the following tools **PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE**:\n\n **Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)**\n\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download, install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- Cellular hotspot (optional)\n\n**Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n\n- 8’ Step Ladder\n- Hook and Loop (“Velcro”) strips / roll (for cable management)\n- Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)\n- with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves\n- (to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (12’ minimum)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with\n- PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Crossover cable – Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables\n- Rollover cable – Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory\n- RJ45 crossover adapter (male–female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) – Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs\n- Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch – Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities\n- PoE injector – Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available\n- Windows laptop computer – Required software including PuTTY","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T16:00","end":"2026-09-30T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":350,"max":350},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":53},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":117,"baseAmount":350,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":80,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start