{"job":{"id":"8450700532","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install PDU","description":"<p># SCOPE OF WORK</p><p><br></p><p>Survey site and follow latest MOP instructions. Install PDU near PIAB and carrier modems. Follow checklist if carrier EQ or customer EQ are in different locations. PIAB SN: 701731 DIA CKT: 30.RBBT.119977 SPECTRUM 50 M 131565401 BB CKT:30.RBCB.138012 Spectrum D600.0M/U35.0M 8349100121278338</p><p><br></p><p># REQUIRED MATERIALS</p><p><br></p><p>- Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port</p><p>- Multimeter wire tester</p><p>- Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches</p><p>- Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer)</p><p>- Biscuit jacks</p><p>- Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters</p><p>- 4-6 ft' ladder</p><p>- Butt Set</p><p>- RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors</p><p>- 100' extension cord</p><p>- Digital Camera</p><p>- 100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device</p><p>- Cell phone w/Hotspot device</p><p>- Punch down tool</p><p><br></p><p>*Tech MUST work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number and Mettel ticket in the confidential field section*</p><p>___________________________________________________________________________________________________</p><p>Flat rate covers up to 2 hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</p><p><br></p><p>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</p><p><br></p><p>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered ?Cancelled?, not ?Aborted?. </p><p><br></p><p>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00","end":"2026-10-08T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790688804827}
{"job":{"id":20000703,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Deinstall old and install new pin pads from each POS and/or SCO lane","description":{"html":"<p>Need Ross trained tech(s) for 7 lane pin pad refresh project.</p>\n<p>Tech(s) will download vendor authorization letter, tech checkin-checkout document, and pin pad install guideand review before arrival.</p>\n<p>Text Shyft PM confirming your arrival, contact store MOD, show vendor authorization letter and government issued ID (drivers license), &amp; call command center upon arrival.</p>\n<p>Working with MOD and Command Center representative, deinstall old and install new pin pads from each POS and/or SCO lane.</p>\n<p>Phone #'s and conference ID# can be found in confidential information of your work order.</p>\n<p>At end of day, tech(s) must check out with Ross IT hotline and text Shyft PM before leaving site.</p>\n<p><strong>NOTE:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>DO NOT</strong> leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.</li>\n<li><strong>Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please message any rate counter offers, but do not request bundle as-is unless you are in agreement with the rate and schedule</strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Need Ross trained tech(s) for 7 lane pin pad refresh project.\n\nTech(s) will download vendor authorization letter, tech checkin-checkout document, and pin pad install guideand review before arrival.\n\nText Shyft PM confirming your arrival, contact store MOD, show vendor authorization letter and government issued ID (drivers license), & call command center upon arrival.\n\nWorking with MOD and Command Center representative, deinstall old and install new pin pads from each POS and/or SCO lane.\n\nPhone #'s and conference ID# can be found in confidential information of your work order.\n\nAt end of day, tech(s) must check out with Ross IT hotline and text Shyft PM before leaving site.\n\n**NOTE:**\n\n- **DO NOT** leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.\n- **Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.**\n- **Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.**\n- **Please message any rate counter offers, but do not request bundle as-is unless you are in agreement with the rate and schedule**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T21:45","end":"2026-10-20T26:39"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4.9,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09