{"job":{"id":20054427,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Firm Start | New Store Install - LEAD Technician","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Seeking:</strong> A technician with experience in installing Rack and Stack Network Equipment and POS Terminal and its Peripherals.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Scope:</strong> To assemble a 22U floor cabinet on wheels&nbsp;and install a patch panel, Switch, and PDU. You will also be installing POS Terminals, Cash Drawers, Pin pads and Printers and 9 CCTV Cameras and cable terminations. </li><li>Tech is required to follow detailed instructions, and work with remote support during the installation process and be able to troubleshoot if needed.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Estimated duration:</strong>&nbsp;6-8 hours&nbsp;</li><li><strong>THIS IS A HARD START, AND YOU MUST BE ON TIME </strong>(penalties will be applied if you are late). You are required to stay on-site until the work is complete and you are properly released by the bridgeline.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>IMPORTANT!!! </strong>WHEN you arrive on-site, YOU MUST CALL TO CHECK IN WITH EES TECH SUPPORT and GC (GC is your on site contact)</li><li><strong>Essintial Technical Support Lead - Johnothen Oldaker -</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em><u>717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.</u></em></strong></li><li><strong>DELIVERABLES:</strong> Lead Technician&nbsp;will need to take pictures of all installed equipment (see below for specifics)&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Standard tool kit with Basic hand tools&nbsp;</li><li>Smartphone and charger (must have phone, camera, and internet ability)&nbsp;</li><li>Government issued photo ID (must be original, not a copy or photo of)&nbsp;</li><li>110 punchdown tool&nbsp;</li><li>Data cable toner&nbsp;</li><li>Date cable tester&nbsp;</li><li>RJ45 Crimp tool&nbsp;</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cordless Drill/Driver</li><li>Technician to bring some face plates and keystones as a backup.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Essintial Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial&nbsp;PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE</u></strong><u>):</u></p><ul><li>You will be asked to confirm site details</li><li>You will be asked to provide Check-In and Check-Out Times&nbsp;</li><li>You will be asked to upload various photos from your visit. [ LEAD TECHNICIAN ]</li><li>You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes</li><li>You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature</li><li>You will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Print/Watch all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site. Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>POPMART Install Guide</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003okif/A3QgSJCBWwvTcDHP2eNgcWf8ByF9rPk6kdZNtC_XAOU<strong>&nbsp;</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>WATCH THE INSTALL VIDEO:</strong>https://essintial.sharepoint.com/:v:/s/EESDigitalCollateral/IQBsnZS-VHcGSZ6FI6CmNYruAc4WPQ7CzAocSEULi3JE5lw?e=AvOuxu&amp;referrer=Outlook.Desktop&amp;referrerScenario=email-linkwithembed</li><li><strong>Confirm the start date and time</strong>&nbsp;- You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted</li><li>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</li></ol><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ol><li><strong>Check In Requirements- Follow in order</strong>&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER –&nbsp;</strong>if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CHECK IN with GC – General Contractor/Onsite POC- </strong>Technician will introduce themselves to as the Partner Tech Technician onsite to complete the Network and POS installation&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CALL Essintial Support Lead Johnothen Oldaker -</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em><u>717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.</u></em>- TO go over Site readiness and walk through the SCOPE.</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Audit inventory of new equipment onsite and notify Essintial of any discrepancies. </strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Start the installation - Refer to Installation Guide</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Assemble network floor cabinet on wheels</strong>&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Install Network Equipment.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install (9) CCTV Cameras and cable terminations.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Confirm with Marty that this is online.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once confirmed, start on the POS Terminal installation.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inform Marty that you are complete with the POS installation and Confirm that all equipment is Online</li><li>Take photos of the below:&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Installed FULL network rack</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Above the counter POS Terminal&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Below the counter POS Terminal&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">(9) Installed CCTV Cameras</li><li><strong>Submit &amp; Complete EES Online Deliverable photos and call to Johnothen <u>BEFORE LEAVING SITE for approval</u></strong>.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Call /Get released from the site byJohnothen Oldaker -</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em><u>717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.</u></em></strong></li></ol><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables / Closeout Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ol><li><strong>Check-Out with Onsite POC</strong></li><li><strong>Complete &amp; Submit Essintial Online Deliverable&nbsp;(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO leaving the site / getting released from the site)</strong></li><li><strong>CHECK OUT WITH</strong> <strong>Johnothen Oldaker -</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em><u>717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.</u></em></strong>&nbsp;– to review/approve/ensure your deliverables are completed and get released from the site</li><li><strong>CHECK OUT OF YOUR WORK ORDER-</strong> If you are unable to do so, make sure that you call into Essintial Projects Team&nbsp;@ 855-612-2183</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> </strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Dress Code: Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: </strong>no jeans or holes, collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p><strong> </strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements: </strong>Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time<strong>.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong> </strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Access/Hardware Issues:</strong> please reach out to the Essintial <strong>Lead Technical Support Agent</strong> -<strong>Johnothen Oldaker -</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em><u>717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.</u></em> [Secondary/Backup - contact</strong> Essintial Tech Support at 717-516-3009]</p><p><strong> </strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- **Seeking:** A technician with experience in installing Rack and Stack Network Equipment and POS Terminal and its Peripherals.\n- **Scope:** To assemble a 22U floor cabinet on wheels and install a patch panel, Switch, and PDU. You will also be installing POS Terminals, Cash Drawers, Pin pads and Printers and 9 CCTV Cameras and cable terminations.\n- Tech is required to follow detailed instructions, and work with remote support during the installation process and be able to troubleshoot if needed.\n- **Estimated duration:** 6-8 hours\n- **THIS IS A HARD START, AND YOU MUST BE ON TIME** (penalties will be applied if you are late). You are required to stay on-site until the work is complete and you are properly released by the bridgeline.\n- **IMPORTANT!!!** WHEN you arrive on-site, YOU MUST CALL TO CHECK IN WITH EES TECH SUPPORT and GC (GC is your on site contact)\n- **Essintial Technical Support Lead - Johnothen Oldaker -** ***717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.***\n- **DELIVERABLES:** Lead Technician will need to take pictures of all installed equipment (see below for specifics)\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Standard tool kit with Basic hand tools\n- Smartphone and charger (must have phone, camera, and internet ability)\n- Government issued photo ID (must be original, not a copy or photo of)\n- 110 punchdown tool\n- Data cable toner\n- Date cable tester\n- RJ45 Crimp tool\n- Label maker\n- Velcro\n- Cordless Drill/Driver\n- Technician to bring some face plates and keystones as a backup.\n\n**Essintial Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE**):\n\n- You will be asked to confirm site details\n- You will be asked to provide Check-In and Check-Out Times\n- You will be asked to upload various photos from your visit. \\[ LEAD TECHNICIAN \\]\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- You will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Print/Watch all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site. Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.\n2. **POPMART Install Guide**: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003okif/A3QgSJCBWwvTcDHP2eNgcWf8ByF9rPk6kdZNtC_XAOU\n3. **WATCH THE INSTALL VIDEO:**<https://essintial.sharepoint.com/:v:/s/EESDigitalCollateral/IQBsnZS-VHcGSZ6FI6CmNYruAc4WPQ7CzAocSEULi3JE5lw?e=AvOuxu&amp;referrer=Outlook.Desktop&amp;referrerScenario=email-linkwithembed>\n4. **Confirm the start date and time** - You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted\n5. Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **Check In Requirements- Follow in order**\n2. **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER –** if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n3. **CHECK IN with GC – General Contractor/Onsite POC-** Technician will introduce themselves to as the Partner Tech Technician onsite to complete the Network and POS installation\n4. **CALL Essintial Support Lead Johnothen Oldaker -** ***717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.*- TO go over Site readiness and walk through the SCOPE.**\n5. **Audit inventory of new equipment onsite and notify Essintial of any discrepancies.**\n6. **Start the installation - Refer to Installation Guide**\n7. **Assemble network floor cabinet on wheels**\n8. **Install Network Equipment.**\n9. Install (9) CCTV Cameras and cable terminations.\n10. **Confirm with Marty that this is online.**\n11. Once confirmed, start on the POS Terminal installation.\n12. Inform Marty that you are complete with the POS installation and Confirm that all equipment is Online\n13. Take photos of the below:\n14. Installed FULL network rack\n15. Above the counter POS Terminal\n16. Below the counter POS Terminal\n17. (9) Installed CCTV Cameras\n18. **Submit & Complete EES Online Deliverable photos and call to Johnothen BEFORE LEAVING SITE for approval**.\n19. **Call /Get released from the site byJohnothen Oldaker -** ***717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.***\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables / Closeout Requirements:**\n\n1. **Check-Out with Onsite POC**\n2. **Complete & Submit Essintial Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO leaving the site / getting released from the site)**\n3. **CHECK OUT WITH** **Johnothen Oldaker -** ***717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.*** – to review/approve/ensure your deliverables are completed and get released from the site\n4. **CHECK OUT OF YOUR WORK ORDER-** If you are unable to do so, make sure that you call into Essintial Projects Team @ 855-612-2183\n\n**Dress Code: Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required:** no jeans or holes, collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Physical Requirements:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time**.**\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Site Access/Hardware Issues:** please reach out to the Essintial **Lead Technical Support Agent** -**Johnothen Oldaker -** ***717-516-3036 - you MUST ask to be transferred to Johnothen when you call.* \\[Secondary/Backup - contact** Essintial Tech Support at 717-516-3009\\]\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:45","end":"2026-10-02T16:45"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976620 - 2312 Bridgeport Dr | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790688995653}
{"job":{"id":20054741,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"Replace the POS Unit for POS 3# - est. < 2 hrs onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.</strong></p><ul><li>You will represent yourself as an <del>***</del> Representative</li><li>INC# and FWKD# in the work order information</li><li><strong><u>Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order</u></strong>.</li><li>Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.</li><li>The defective part must be returned in the box with the&nbsp;provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.</li><li>Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.</li><li>Drop the return package off at UPS store.</li><li>If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.</li><li>Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.</li><li>Must Check In/Out with <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li>Must take before and after photos of the unit</li><li>Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTES:</strong></p><ol><li>Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!&nbsp;</li><li>Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.&nbsp;</li><li>Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.&nbsp;</li><li>All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.&nbsp;</li><li>Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.&nbsp;</li><li>The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><em><u>READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Escalation Process: </strong>If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li><strong>Readiness Policy: </strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>On My Way: </strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</li><li><strong>Arriving Late:</strong> All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</li><li><strong>Changing Resources:</strong> By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</li><li><strong>Expense Approval:</strong> Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</li><li><strong>Wait Time: </strong>If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.</li><li><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong> If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Out-of-Scope Work: </strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Returning Parts:</strong> Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"***NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion***\n\n**Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.**\n\n- You will represent yourself as an \\*\\*\\* Representative\n- INC# and FWKD# in the work order information\n- **Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order**.\n- Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.\n- The defective part must be returned in the box with the provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.\n- Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.\n- Drop the return package off at UPS store.\n- If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.\n- Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.\n- Must Check In/Out with \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Must take before and after photos of the unit\n- Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n\n1. Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!\n2. Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.\n3. Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.\n4. All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.\n5. Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.\n6. The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.\n\n***READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order***\n\n- **Escalation Process:** If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Readiness Policy:** The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted. Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.\n- **On My Way:** When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.\n- **Arriving Late:** All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order. Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.\n- **Changing Resources:** By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.\n- **Dress Code:** Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n- **Expense Approval:** Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.\n- **Wait Time:** If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.\n- **Additional Time On-site:** If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.\n- **Out-of-Scope Work:** If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident. Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n- **Returning Parts:** Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T13:55","end":"2026-09-29T15:55"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":130},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":53},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-01T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + S