{"job":{"id":19993871,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Install 3 Access Points (2 Techs Required)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.</em></strong></p><p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work: </u></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Install 2 Access Points and Starlink</strong></p><ul><li>1 Indoor Access Point (AP) to be installed inside the shop building.</li><li>2 Outdoor Access Points (APs) to be installed in the parking area to improve wireless coverage.</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">For the installation, new network cabling will need to be run from the network switch to all three access points. </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">The estimated cable length for each AP is approximately 250 feet.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Tech will need to bring approximately 750' of Cat6 cable (should take more just in case).</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Additional required materials and tools listed below.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">﻿</span></p><p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p><p>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</p><p>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>(1) box of CAT6 Cable </strong></li><li><strong>RJ45's</strong></li><li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li><li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li><li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li><li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop:</strong>&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li><li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li><li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li><strong>Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(8'-10' ladder)</li></ul>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n***TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.***\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:** **Install 2 Access Points and Starlink**\n\n- 1 Indoor Access Point (AP) to be installed inside the shop building.\n- 2 Outdoor Access Points (APs) to be installed in the parking area to improve wireless coverage.\n- For the installation, new network cabling will need to be run from the network switch to all three access points.\n- The estimated cable length for each AP is approximately 250 feet.\n- Tech will need to bring approximately 750' of Cat6 cable (should take more just in case).\n- Additional required materials and tools listed below.\n\n﻿\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nPlease ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.\n\nThe technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- **(1) box of CAT6 Cable**\n- **RJ45's**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T09:00","end":"2026-10-02T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":78},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790691481397}
{"job":{"id":20054420,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Encore Technologies","title":"Macy's - Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary *MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT*","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK OVERVIEW: </strong>Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary *MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT*&nbsp;</p><p>TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS: Background check and Drugscreen</p><p>EXPECTED AMOUNT OF TIME ONSITE: 1 hour</p><p>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Tech must obtain packing materials, box that is 20x20x20 and bubble wrap.  Packing materials will be reimbursed up to $20.  If over $20 will need to call into dispatch <del>************</del> for authorization</p><p>TOOLS NEEDED:</p><p>FULL DETAILS:</p><ul><li>WORK HAS TO BE COMPLETED PRIOR TO STORE OPENING AS THIS IS INVASIVE WORK THAT WILL CAUSE AN OUTAGE OF UP TO 30 MINTUES.</li><li>Technician will meet with Store Loal Contact and be provided to the POS or MDF room.</li><li>Technician must join Bridge that is provided for this work upon arrival at site to work with Verizon Network Engineer</li><li>Locate Primary and Secondary versa boxes (These will be either Lanner or Advantec)</li><li>Confirm with Verizon Network Engineer that correct boxes have been found.</li><li>Once Verizon Network Engineer gives the direction on the bridge technician will unplug the MPLS circuit from the Primary Versa.</li><li>Technician will then move the broadband/dedicated internet circuit from the Secondary Versa to now vacant Primary Versa slot.</li><li>After the circuit move is complete and confirmed functioning correctly, trace the removed MPLS circuit to the Verizon beas box.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verizon beas box is normally an Overture 1400</li><li>Technician will ensure no other circuit is connected to this device.</li><li>When confirmed no additional circuits connected proceed with removing device</li><li>Device will be packed for shipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Technician MUST take pictures of device wrapped in bubble wrap and placed in the shipping box.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Pictures must be attached to assignment for payment approval</strong></li><li>Once packed appropriately and pictures taken technician will provide box to store management to ship back to Verizon</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technician must get sign off on the assignment from the member of store management that equipment to be shipped back has been provided to</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**WORK OVERVIEW:** Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary \\*MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT\\*\n\nTECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS: Background check and Drugscreen\n\nEXPECTED AMOUNT OF TIME ONSITE: 1 hour\n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Tech must obtain packing materials, box that is 20x20x20 and bubble wrap. Packing materials will be reimbursed up to $20. If over $20 will need to call into dispatch \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for authorization\n\nTOOLS NEEDED:\n\nFULL DETAILS:\n\n- WORK HAS TO BE COMPLETED PRIOR TO STORE OPENING AS THIS IS INVASIVE WORK THAT WILL CAUSE AN OUTAGE OF UP TO 30 MINTUES.\n- Technician will meet with Store Loal Contact and be provided to the POS or MDF room.\n- Technician must join Bridge that is provided for this work upon arrival at site to work with Verizon Network Engineer\n- Locate Primary and Secondary versa boxes (These will be either Lanner or Advantec)\n- Confirm with Verizon Network Engineer that correct boxes have been found.\n- Once Verizon Network Engineer gives the direction on the bridge technician will unplug the MPLS circuit from the Primary Versa.\n- Technician will then move the broadband/dedicated internet circuit from the Secondary Versa to now vacant Primary Versa slot.\n- After the circuit move is complete and confirmed functioning correctly, trace the removed MPLS circuit to the Verizon beas box.\n- Verizon beas box is normally an Overture 1400\n- Technician will ensure no other circuit is connected to this device.\n- When confirmed no additional circuits connected proceed with removing device\n- Device will be packed for shipment\n- Technician MUST take pictures of device wrapped in bubble wrap and placed in the shipping box.\n- **Pictures must be attached to assignment for payment approval**\n- Once packed appropriately and pictures taken technician will provide box to store management to ship back to Verizon\n- **Technician must get sign off on the assignment from the member of store management that equipment to be shipped back has been provided to**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":50},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z",