{"job":{"id":"2461317337","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768","description":"Flexedge TJX hard down<br><br>Issue: Flexedge is hard down<br><br><br>ConnectWise NOC ticket: 6998768<br><br><br><br>CPEGRT0000018674<br>2039231176<br>https://157.96.244.45/routers/CPEGRT0000018674<br><br><br>Frontier<br>CID:63/KRGN/176983//FTNC/<br><br>Ticket#: INC9315540<br><br>Security Access Code: 190384<br><br>63/KRGN/176983//FTNC/<br>Tech must locate carrier NID for CID:63/KRGN/176983//FTNC/  and verify the lights as well as power status. <br><br><br>Scope of Work:   <br><br><br>Tech must check in via Work Market and be ready to start the Scope of Work.  <br><br><br>Tech must call Granite TJX NOC Networking @ 844-562-2859, option 1 to work with a rep. If tech is unable to reach NOC team, tech must leave a voicemail requesting a call back.  <br><br><br>Tech must locate Granite Flexedge/Silicom. (Will either have NSOID: CPEGRT0000018674or S/N: 2039231176<br><br><br>3a. Tech must verify the power and lights on both the Flexedge and carrier NID. <br>3b. Tech must work with Granite NOC to troubleshoot and verify the Flexedge status<br><br>Once Flexedge is back online:<br>  <br><br><br>Tech must connect laptop directly to the Flexedge LAN port and have laptop NIC set for DHCP (FortiGate should already be connected to this port so there should be a cable the tech can use.)<br><br><br><br>**** Port is using DHCP, so Granite NOC will need to clear DHCP bind prior to tech connecting ****<br><br><br>4a. Tech must utilize the same cable and unplug it from WAN1 on the FortiGate and then plug into laptop. <br><br>4b. If unable to surf off the Flexedge, tech must replace patch cable. <br><br>4c. If able to surf, tech will need run speed and ping testing. <br><br><br>If needed Granite NOC rep must remote into tech laptop and verify provisioned speeds from managed router directly connected to LAN port with customer equipment removed either by assigning IP or via DHCP, depending on configuration <br><br><br>Once tech confirmed speeds at the managed router, send results to NetOpsAccess@granitenet.com and assigned rep with subject DIA/NI ticket # 6571012<br><br><br>If speeds are poor at managed router, tech must setup console session so NetOps Access rep can review configuration, speed/duplex and check for any errors.  <br><br><br>If there is no managed router issue and speeds are still poor take the managed router to the DMARC NID and test again.  <br><br><br>If speeds are still poor, iPerf testing must be performed.  <br><br><br><br><br>If carrier tech is needed for any reason, Granite NOC Rep must schedule carrier tech and obtain approval to release from the TJX NOC. <br>After work is complete, tech must locate customer equipment and reconnect to the managed router.  <br>Granite NOC rep must confirm connectivity with customer contact TJX NOC at 855-859-2821 Option 1, 1, 2 prior to releasing tech.   Approval to release required from customer NOC or from tier 2 tech or higher if customer   NOC is not available  <br>Tech must clean up, complete close-outs, and check out via Work Market.     Required Equipment: Laptop with integrated Ethernet port. Laptop must have Windows 7 or higher   with admin rights and must have all Windows updates installed for security purposes. Laptop must have   PuTTY and the latest version of TeamViewer installed. Cell phone. Unlimited mobile hotspot. Chargers   for laptop, hotspot, and cell phone. On-site equipment is a   Flexedge/Silicom, a USB-A to RJ45 Straight-through console cable is required. Electrical extension cord (25 feet minimum). 6-foot step   ladder. At least 2 complete Ethernet surface jacks. Ethernet cable tester. Cat5e/cat6 cable (150 feet   minimum). At least 4 RJ-45 wall jacks and plates","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T11:00","end":"2026-09-29T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourly