{"job":{"id":"2594121526","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Upcoming TU/Cutover | Securitas Security Systems | 04567771 | Morrisville, NC,","description":"Network Maintenance – Please absorb all Charges <br><br>Please Read the SOW in its entirety prior to moving forward <br><br>Objective of this deployment is to migrate the existing BB circuit to a newly installed BB circuit while confirming all peripheral equipment maintains full functionality. Prior to departure Granite technician must confirm with the site’s LCON location is now operational on Granite provided access and the customer’s existing equipment <br><br>Scheduled Date/time: 10/6/2026 @1pm EST<br><br><br>Call the LCON for access, 15 minutes prior to arrival<br><br>a. LCON:  Stacey Messing | 973-494-7969<br><br>Advise LCON you are there to upgrade their internet bandwidth per the corporate office Broadband Network Maintenance Project.<br><br>a. You will complete prep work and then check in with LCON before proceeding with cutover \\(5-10 minutes of downtime\\). <br>b. Once LCON gives approval to move forward, Locate the old and new AT&amp;T Fiber circuit. Confirm if extension is needed. <br>i. If extension is needed, this must be completed<br><br><br>Call Activation Queue - 877-855-1146 Option 1 for turning up the new circuit. Run the speed test \\(www.speedtest.net\\) of the new circuit connected to your laptop only. Take a screenshot of this as well. IPs are listed below<br><br><br>See Activation ticket: **#7003481**<br>Activation Queue Phone number: 877-855-1146 Option 1. <br><br><br>Take pictures of the following and send to SISupport@granitenet.com<br><br>a. Before migration: Picture of router/switch from roughly 6 feet away that captures the whole rack. <br>b. Screenshot of speed test <br><br><br>Let LCON know you are ready to proceed with the upgrade and confirm you can take the store down for about 5-10 minutes. Once approved, move to cutover.<br><br><br>Cutover Part: <br><br><br>Please reach out to the IT Contact listed below to perform the Cutover portion \\(changing IPs\\) connecting the new Broadband Circuit to the customer’s equipment.<br><br>a. Work with the IT Contact while moving the patch cable from the old circuit to the new circuit <br><br><br>Once the new circuit is connected and configurations are implementation by IT Contact, kindly check with the LCON onsite if their devices are working as expected<br><br><br>IT Contact information: <br>Stacey Messing | Phone: 973-494-7969<br><br>Escalation Contact: •TU Escalation - 8888601365 <br><br>Required MATERIALS: <br>Laptop PC \\(Windows 2000 or higher\\) with administrator login AC power adapter internet access \\(cell/mobile card or hotspot\\) DB-9 serial cable &amp; serial port on laptop or USB-to-serial adapter Console Cable 4G card AC extension cord cell phone with charger <br><br>LEGACY \\(CUSTOMER\\) <br>Circuit Info: <br>Existing CID: 314122948<br>Existing Carrier: ATT<br>Modem type: n/a<br>Serial Number: D93LA1HM990908<br>MAC Address:EC:C3:02:27:F0:D0<br><br>New Circuit Info: <br>CID: 346135425<br>Model: Nokia BGW320-505<br>Serial Number: N93UD6BM110395<br>MAC Address: 0c:88:32:cb:68:90<br>Carrier: ATT<br>IP Address/Range: 108.252.100.137-108.252.100.141<br>Default Gateway: 108.252.100.142<br>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248<br>Speed:300.0 Mbps/300.0 Mbps","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:00","end":"2026-10-06T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":6.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null},"reason":"PAYMENT_INSUFFICIENT","rejectDetails":"Rate $50/hr is below base rate $65/hr"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790693504297}
{"job":{"id":19949427,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NetFabric","title":"SD-WAN Implementation - Site 163","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Seeking experienced Network Field Technicians to perform Aruba SD-WAN appliance migrations at customer locations, including equipment installation, WAN/LAN cutovers, AdTran removal, photo documentation, coordination with remote network engineers via bridge calls, connectivity validation, and customer sign-off.</span></li><li>Tech is required to provide email for bridge call, join bridge call when onsite, provide pre &amp; post work photo’s &amp; get sign off from the customer onsite once work has been completed. DO NOT LEAVE SITE UNTIL RELEASED BY CUSTOMER.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1.5 hours</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>To maintain a professional image and ensure safety and functionality in the field, all Field Services Technicians are expected to adhere to the following dress code guidelines:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>1. General Appearance</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Clothing must be clean, well-maintained, and free of holes, rips, or excessive wear.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Personal hygiene must be maintained at all times.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong><strong>2. Required Attire</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Polo or button-down shirt&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Work pants or durable khakis (no jeans unless explicitly approved).</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or work boots appropriate for walking, climbing, or standing for extended </span>periods.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>3. Prohibited Attire</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Shorts, sweatpants, or athletic wear.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Sandals, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Clothing with offensive language, graphics, or logos unrelated to the company.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Excessive jewelry or </span>accessories that may pose a safety risk.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li><em>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers – Flathead &amp; Phillips, pliers, wire cutters/strippers, crimping tool, adjustable wrench, Allen (hex key) wrenches, tape measure</em></li><li><em>Cable tester, punch down tool, butt set, RJ45 crimping tool</em></li><li><em>Laptop with terminal software</em></li><li><em>Smartphone w/ camera and charger</em></li></ul><p><br></p>Installation ProcedureStep 1 - Stage New Device<ol><li>Locate the new Aruba SD-WAN appliance.</li><li>Place the device on the designated rack shelf.</li><li>Connect power to the Belkin power strip connected to the APC UPS.</li><li>Verify the device powers on successfully.</li></ol>Step 2 - Join Engineering Bridge<ol><li>Join the conference bridge provided in the work order.</li><li>Maintain communication with remote Massey Engineering throughout the migration.</li><li>Do not perform WAN or LAN cutovers until instructed.</li></ol>Step 3 - WAN Cutover<ol><li>Locate WAN1 cable on the existing Aruba appliance.</li><li>When directed:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Remove WAN1 cable from existing appliance.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Move WAN1 cable to WAN1 port on new Aruba appliance.</li></ul><ol><li>Wait for remote engineer confirmation that the SD-WAN tunnel is established.</li></ol>Step 4 - LAN Cutover<ol><li>Inform site contact there will be a brief internet interruption.</li><li>Under direction of Massey Engineering:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Move LAN1 cable from old Aruba appliance to new Aruba appliance.</li></ul><ol><li>Verify connection LEDs illuminate appropriately.</li></ol>Step 5 - Voice Validation<ol><li>Allow phones to automatically re-register.</li><li>Confirm with site personnel that phones reconnect and service is restored.</li><li>Report any issues immediately to remote engineering.</li></ol><p><br></p>Decommission Existing Appliance<ol><li>Remove old Aruba appliance from rack shelf/tray.</li><li>Place old device into original Aruba shipping box.</li><li>If original box is unavailable, use packaging from the new unit.</li><li>Ensure all removed equipment is packed securely.</li></ol>Validation &amp; Sign-Off<p>Before leaving site:</p>Verify<ul><li>Internet access operational</li><li>Phones operational</li><li>No visible alarms on new Aruba appliance</li><li>Site staff confirms operational status</li><li>Remote Massey Engineering confirms successful migration</li></ul>Return Equipment<ul><li>Provide the boxed old Aruba appliance to the office administrator or designated site representative.</li></ul>Obtain Completion Sign-Off<p>Collect:</p><ul><li>Site contact name</li><li>Signature from Onsite Manager</li><li>Date and time completed</li></ul>Required Closeout Photos<p>Upload the following photos:</p><ol><li>New Aruba appliance installed in rack</li><li>Power connections</li><li>WAN/LAN connections</li><li>Completed rack overview</li><li>Old Aruba appliance packaged for return</li><li>Site sign-off within Field Nation work order</li></ol><p><br></p>Completion Requirements<p>A work order will not be considered complete until:</p><ul><li>Migration is successfully completed.</li><li>Required photos are uploaded.</li><li>Validation with remote engineering is completed.</li><li>Site operational confirmation is received.</li><li>Sign-off information is submitted.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking experienced Network Field Technicians to perform Aruba SD-WAN appliance migrations at customer locations, including equipment installation, WAN/LAN cutovers, AdTran removal, photo documentation, coordination with remote network engineers via bridge calls, connectivity validation, and customer sign-off.\n- Tech is required to provide email for bridge call, join bridge call when onsite, provide pre & post work photo’s & get sign off from the customer onsite once work has been completed. DO NOT LEAVE SITE UNTIL RELEASED BY CUSTOMER.\n- Estimated duration will be 1.5 hours\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nTo maintain a professional image and ensure safety and functionality in the field, all Field Services Technicians are expected to adhere to the following dress code guidelines:\n\n **1. General Appearance**\n\n- Clothing must be clean, well-maintained, and free of holes, rips, or excessive wear.\n- Personal hygiene must be maintained at all times.\n\n **2. Required Attire**\n\n- Polo or button-down shirt\n- Work pants or durable khakis (no jeans unless explicitly approved).\n- Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or work boots appropriate for walking, climbing, or standing for extended periods.\n\n **3. Prohibited Attire**\n\n- Shorts, sweatpants, or athletic wear.\n- Sandals, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n- Clothing with offensive language, graphics, or logos unrelated to the company.\n- Excessive jewelry or accessories that may pose a safety risk.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- *Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers – Flathead & Phillips, pliers, wire cutters/strippers, crimping tool, adjustable wrench, Allen (hex key) wrenches, tape measure*\n- *Cable tester, punch down tool, butt set, RJ45 crimping tool*\n- *Laptop with terminal software*\n- *Smartphone w/ camera and charger*\n\nInstallation ProcedureStep 1 - Stage New Device1. Locate the new Aruba SD-WAN appliance.\n2. Place the device on the designated rack shelf.\n3. Connect power to the Belkin power strip connected to the APC UPS.\n4. Verify the device powers on successfully.\n\nStep 2 - Join Engineering Bridge1. Join the conference bridge provided in the work order.\n2. Maintain communication with remote Massey Engineering throughout the migration.\n3. Do not perform WAN or LAN cutovers until instructed.\n\nStep 3 - WAN Cutover1. Locate WAN1 cable on the existing Aruba appliance.\n2. When directed:\n\n- Remove WAN1 cable from existing appliance.\n- Move WAN1 cable to WAN1 port on new Aruba appliance.\n\n1. Wait for remote engineer confirmation that the SD-WAN tunnel is established.\n\nStep 4 - LAN Cutover1. Inform site contact there will be a brief internet interruption.\n2. Under direction of Massey Engineering:\n\n- Move LAN1 cable from old Aruba appliance to new Aruba appliance.\n\n1. Verify connection LEDs illuminate appropriately.\n\nStep 5 - Voice Validation1. Allow phones to automatically re-register.\n2. Confirm with site personnel that phones reconnect and service is restored.\n3. Report any issues immediately to remote engineering.\n\nDecommission Existing Appliance1. Remove old Aruba appliance from rack shelf/tray.\n2. Place old device into original Aruba shipping box.\n3. If original box is unavailable, use packaging from the new unit.\n4. Ensure all removed equipment is packed securely.\n\nValidation & Sign-OffBefore leaving site:\n\nVerify- Internet access operational\n- Phones operational\n- No visible alarms on new Aruba appliance\n- Site staff confirms operational status\n- Remote Massey Engineering confirms successful migration\n\nReturn Equipment- Provide the boxed old Aruba appliance to the office administrator or designated site representative.\n\nObtain Completion Sign-OffCollect:\n\n- Site contact name\n- Signature from Onsite Manager\n- Date and time completed\n\nRequired Closeout PhotosUpload the following photos:\n\n1. New Aruba appliance installed in rack\n2. Power connections\n3. WAN/LAN connections\n4. Completed rack overview\n5. Old Aruba appliance packaged for return\n6. Site sign-off within Field Nation work order\n\nCompletion RequirementsA work order will not be considered complete until:\n\n- Migration is successfully completed.\n- Required photos are uploaded.\n- Validation with remote engineering is completed.\n- Site operational confirmation is received.\n- Sign-off information is submitted.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00","end":"2026-10-09T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":160},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"