{"job":{"id":20056814,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CPT Network Solutions, Inc.","title":"Training PC Refresh & FedEx Drop Off ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>:: JOB DETAILS ::</u></strong></p><p><strong>1 Technician Approved</strong></p>High Level Overview:<p>This site has a Windows 10 device slated for replacement. The legacy device will either be a Training PC or a Timeclock Tablet. The new device will either be a laptop or desktop. Device type and serial number listed below.</p><p>Legacy Device Type: Lenovo Training PC</p><p>Legacy Device Serial Number: MJ0BRNBM</p><p>New Device Type: Dell Laptop</p><p>New Device Serial Number: 7JYV4J4</p>Tech Required Tools/Materials:<ul><li>(1) Medium-Sized Box and Packing Materials (~20x16x15). Box will need to fit a monitor and small PC unit.</li><li>Standard cabling tools</li><li>Cable toner/tester</li><li>Spare patch cables, mod ends, jacks, etc.</li><li>Printed-out copy of the new device log-in instructions, provided by CPT.</li></ul>Scope of Work (SOW):Part 1: Win 10 Device Replacement<ul><li>Upon arrival on site, contact CPT for check-in.</li><li>Verify the serial number/model of the equipment slated for replacement with CPT.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The equipment will either be a training PC or a timeclock windows tablet.</li><li>Work with the site to locate the device and confirm the serial number. Take a photo of the device before de-installing.</li><li>De-install the device. Device will need to be boxed-up and shipped with a Fedex label.</li><li>NOTE: The PC may be attached to the monitor in an all-in-one setup. You may have to uninstall the PC from the monitor as shown in the attachment</li><li>Site should have provided a Fedex shipping label. If the site does NOT have a label, contact CPT immediately.</li><li>Install the replacement laptop/desktop.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note that if the new device is a laptop, it should be a 1-to-1 swap with the existing device, and use the same monitors and peripherals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If it is a desktop, there may be a new monitor stand in which the PC will need to be mounted to the back of the monitor via 4x thumb screws. If there is no new monitor, install the PC on the desk</li><li>Once the new PC is installed, verify that the site can log-in using the provided log-in instructions and that the PC is connected to the site network.</li><li>Inform the store that someone from the corporate help desk will be reaching out for software configurations, printers, scanners, drivers, etc.</li></ul><p><strong>NOTE</strong>: The return label should be in the box with the PC log-in instructions. If the return label is not in the box or the site has thrown it away, contact CPT immediately</p>Part 2: De-Install and Fedex Drop-Off<ul><li>Box the de-installed device with the technician-provided box and packing materials.</li><li>Take a photo of the boxed-up material with the label and tracking # visible.</li><li>Take the labeled and boxed-up PC and/or timeclock tablet off-site to be returned via Fedex.</li><li>Fedex packages can be dropped off at Fedex locations or partner retailers.</li><li>Take a photo of any receipt provided by the Fedex location or retail partner.</li><li>Contact CPT to confirm drop-off and close-out.</li></ul>Deliverables:<p><strong>Send required deliverables to photos@cptnetworks.com</strong></p><ul><li>Photo of the legacy device before de-install.</li><li>Photo of the serial number on the legacy device.</li><li>Photo of the legacy device boxed-up.</li><li>Photo of the shipping label on the box with visible tracking.</li><li>Wide angle photo from the front of the new computer setup</li><li>Photo of the serial number on the new device.</li><li>Photo of cable management behind monitor</li><li>Photo of any receipt provided by the Fedex Store or Retail Partner after drop-off.</li><li><br></li></ul><p><strong><u>:: Company Information ::</u></strong></p><p>A copy of our internal work order will be provided. This is to be used for sign-off with the customer. The file will be uploaded into the Documents section after we assign the job.</p><p><strong><u>Materials used and billing for materials used:</u></strong> Any materials provided during this request, please message us to verify the pricing before closing the WO.&nbsp;We have guidelines based on average field tech prices and we compare with big box stores such as Home Depot. Must be itemized in expense tab description (Example: (1) Jack @ 3.50,etc.)</p><p><strong><u>Base pay + Time on site requirements:</u></strong></p><p><u>1 hour minimum</u> <em>unless otherwise approved.</em></p><p><strong><u>Anything past this time will be approved in 1/4 hour increments @ accepted rates. THIS IS FOR THE TIME ON-SITE.</u></strong></p><p>-Technician's time billed MUST match the check-in and check-out time done with our support team.&nbsp;NO EXCEPTIONS.</p><p>-Do not check-in on this app or with our office until you arrived inside the location.</p><p>-Any discrepancies or failure to call our support team as noted in this scope, will cause a delay in payment and/or possible non-payment.</p><p><strong><u>Deliverables</u>:</strong></p><ol><li><strong><u>Signed CPT Work Order</u></strong>: We will provide a copy of our internal work order. A copy of our signed work order must be uploaded</li><li><strong><u>Check-in/out:</u></strong> You are are required to call us to check-in and to check-out. I<strong><u>f this is not followed</u></strong> it may lead to non-payment. Calling to check-in and out with our support team is REQUIRED. <strong>Hold times may be required. </strong></li><li>Our support team is required to follow protocols for each out our customers and we may need to call their help desk to be released based on customer/location. <strong>Messages from this platform after assignment may not be monitored, our contact numbers should be called for all issues.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Photos</u></strong>: Photos are required during troubleshooting of this request, send to photos@cptnetworks.com</li></ol><p><strong><em>﻿Photo Examples</em>: I</strong>nstalling anything \"NEW\" please take photos of new equipment, connections, jack/label, etc. Reference CPT WO# an Subject. When boxing any old equipment, please take photos of packed equipment before and after sealing box to ensure packed properly.</p><p><strong>Site Contact:</strong>&nbsp;Manager on Duty</p><p><strong><u>Upon arrival to job site:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Once you have arrived to the job site, you are required to call into our office to \"CHECK-IN\", this is required. Messages from this platform are not monitored by support after the assignment.<strong>Hold times may be required.</strong></li><li>You will be asked to provide your CPT work order #, your name, and your contact number.</li><li>Work Order # and our contact Phone Number will be given once work order is assigned.</li><li>All questions and/or troubleshooting should be done with CPT support (at the same number as provided for check-in).</li></ol><p><strong><u>BEFORE LEAVING JOB SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Tech must call CPT to check-out with CPT support before leaving site.</li><li>Our customer's help desk may need to be contacted before leaving site.</li><li>IF YOU DO NOT CONTACT US BEFORE LEAVING THE JOB SITE TO CHECK-OUT WITH OUR SUPPORT THIS MAY EFFECT YOUR PAYMENT.</li><li>You are required to call and speak with our support for payment to be processed.</li><li>Hold Times may be required.</li><li>Messages from this platform while on-site are not monitored by our support team.</li></ul><p>1) Review resolution to issue reported with CPT Tech Support.</p><p>2) Confirm your time-on-site and off-site with CPT Tech Support. You will not be approved for any extra time if it was not confirmed with our support group when checking out.</p><p>3) Have Manager sign the CPT Work Order (not the Field Nation work order). Do not leave any copies on site. Upload the signed form when closing this job request.</p><p>You must communicate with our office via phone call for any delays or issues. Do not message through the platform.</p>","markdown":"**:: JOB DETAILS ::**\n\n**1 Technician Approved**\n\nHigh Level Overview:This site has a Windows 10 device slated for replacement. The legacy device will either be a Training PC or a Timeclock Tablet. The new device will either be a laptop or desktop. Device type and serial number listed below.\n\nLegacy Device Type: Lenovo Training PC\n\nLegacy Device Serial Number: MJ0BRNBM\n\nNew Device Type: Dell Laptop\n\nNew Device Serial Number: 7JYV4J4\n\nTech Required Tools/Materials:- (1) Medium-Sized Box and Packing Materials (~20x16x15). Box will need to fit a monitor and small PC unit.\n- Standard cabling tools\n- Cable toner/tester\n- Spare patch cables, mod ends, jacks, etc.\n- Printed-out copy of the new device log-in instructions, provided by CPT.\n\nScope of Work (SOW):Part 1: Win 10 Device Replacement- Upon arrival on site, contact CPT for check-in.\n- Verify the serial number/model of the equipment slated for replacement with CPT.\n- The equipment will either be a training PC or a timeclock windows tablet.\n- Work with the site to locate the device and confirm the serial number. Take a photo of the device before de-installing.\n- De-install the device. Device will need to be boxed-up and shipped with a Fedex label.\n- NOTE: The PC may be attached to the monitor in an all-in-one setup. You may have to uninstall the PC from the monitor as shown in the attachment\n- Site should have provided a Fedex shipping label. If the site does NOT have a label, contact CPT immediately.\n- Install the replacement laptop/desktop.\n- Note that if the new device is a laptop, it should be a 1-to-1 swap with the existing device, and use the same monitors and peripherals.\n- If it is a desktop, there may be a new monitor stand in which the PC will need to be mounted to the back of the monitor via 4x thumb screws. If there is no new monitor, install the PC on the desk\n- Once the new PC is installed, verify that the site can log-in using the provided log-in instructions and that the PC is connected to the site network.\n- Inform the store that someone from the corporate help desk will be reaching out for software configurations, printers, scanners, drivers, etc.\n\n**NOTE**: The return label should be in the box with the PC log-in instructions. If the return label is not in the box or the site has thrown it away, contact CPT immediately\n\nPart 2: De-Install and Fedex Drop-Off- Box the de-installed device with the technician-provided box and packing materials.\n- Take a photo of the boxed-up material with the label and tracking # visible.\n- Take the labeled and boxed-up PC and/or timeclock tablet off-site to be returned via Fedex.\n- Fedex packages can be dropped off at Fedex locations or partner retailers.\n- Take a photo of any receipt provided by the Fedex location or retail partner.\n- Contact CPT to confirm drop-off and close-out.\n\nDeliverables:**Send required deliverables to photos@cptnetworks.com**\n\n- Photo of the legacy device before de-install.\n- Photo of the serial number on the legacy device.\n- Photo of the legacy device boxed-up.\n- Photo of the shipping label on the box with visible tracking.\n- Wide angle photo from the front of the new computer setup\n- Photo of the serial number on the new device.\n- Photo of cable management behind monitor\n- Photo of any receipt provided by the Fedex Store or Retail Partner after drop-off.\n- \n\n**:: Company Information ::**\n\nA copy of our internal work order will be provided. This is to be used for sign-off with the customer. The file will be uploaded into the Documents section after we assign the job.\n\n**Materials used and billing for materials used:** Any materials provided during this request, please message us to verify the pricing before closing the WO. We have guidelines based on average field tech prices and we compare with big box stores such as Home Depot. Must be itemized in expense tab description (Example: (1) Jack @ 3.50,etc.)\n\n**Base pay + Time on site requirements:**\n\n1 hour minimum *unless otherwise approved.*\n\n**Anything past this time will be approved in 1/4 hour increments @ accepted rates. THIS IS FOR THE TIME ON-SITE.**\n\n-Technician's time billed MUST match the check-in and check-out time done with our support team. NO EXCEPTIONS.\n\n-Do not check-in on this app or with our office until you arrived inside the location.\n\n-Any discrepancies or failure to call our support team as noted in this scope, will cause a delay in payment and/or possible non-payment.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n1. **Signed CPT Work Order**: We will provide a copy of our internal work order. A copy of our signed work order must be uploaded\n2. **Check-in/out:** You are are required to call us to check-in and to check-out. I**f this is not followed** it may lead to non-payment. Calling to check-in and out with our support team is REQUIRED. **Hold times may be required.**\n3. Our support team is required to follow protocols for each out our customers and we may need to call their help desk to be released based on customer/location. **Messages from this platform after assignment may not be monitored, our contact numbers should be called for all issues.**\n4. **Photos**: Photos are required during troubleshooting of this request, send to photos@cptnetworks.com\n\n***﻿Photo Examples*: I**nstalling anything \"NEW\" please take photos of new equipment, connections, jack/label, etc. Reference CPT WO# an Subject. When boxing any old equipment, please take photos of packed equipment before and after sealing box to ensure packed properly.\n\n**Site Contact:** Manager on Duty\n\n**Upon arrival to job site:**\n\n1. Once you have arrived to the job site, you are required to call into our office to \"CHECK-IN\", this is required. Messages from this platform are not monitored by support after the assignment.**Hold times may be required.**\n2. You will be asked to provide your CPT work order #, your name, and your contact number.\n3. Work Order # and our contact Phone Number will be given once work order is assigned.\n4. All questions and/or troubleshooting should be done with CPT support (at the same number as provided for check-in).\n\n**BEFORE LEAVING JOB SITE:**\n\n- Tech must call CPT to check-out with CPT support before leaving site.\n- Our customer's help desk may need to be contacted before leaving site.\n- IF YOU DO NOT CONTACT US BEFORE LEAVING THE JOB SITE TO CHECK-OUT WITH OUR SUPPORT THIS MAY EFFECT YOUR PAYMENT.\n- You are required to call and speak with our support for payment to be processed.\n- Hold Times may be required.\n- Messages from this platform while on-site are not monitored by our support team.\n\n1\\) Review resolution to issue reported with CPT Tech Support.\n\n2\\) Confirm your time-on-site and off-site with CPT Tech Support. You will not be approved for any extra time if it was not confirmed with our support group when checking out.\n\n3\\) Have Manager sign the CPT Work Order (not the Field Nation work order). Do not leave any copies on site. Upload the signed form when closing this job request.\n\nYou must communicate with our office via phone call for any delays or issues. Do not message through the platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-30T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":41},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-01T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika tooth"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790699670374}
{"job":{"id":20057332,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Indoor Zhilai - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">SYSTEM DOWN || Service Call - - ONCE ONSITE TEXT MATT AT 949.490.7077. If no response within 5 minutes, call Field Service line&nbsp;949.317.4169</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- No parts sent out</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for 10/2 before 10am, Local Time</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to:&nbsp;Restore system down - Check in with leasing office &amp; retrieve key - Send picture of network test and open all boxes! </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Standard Tools Required (Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord)</span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nSYSTEM DOWN || Service Call - - ONCE ONSITE TEXT MATT AT 949.490.7077. If no response within 5 minutes, call Field Service line 949.317.4169\n\n\\- No parts sent out\n\n\\- Requesting tech for 10/2 before 10am, Local Time\n\n\\- Need to: Restore system down - Check in with leasing office & retrieve key - Send picture of network test and open all boxes!\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n\\- Standard Tools Required (Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord)\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:00","end":"2026-10-02T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-02T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976588 - 3239 South Church St | EPIK Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cu