{"job":{"id":20057382,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Herman Tech Crew, LLC","title":"Experienced A/V Tech to Assist Lead Install Samsung Video Wall, 12818; Durham, NC 10/13/26","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU&nbsp;<u>READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.</u></strong></p><p>Please Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done, in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p><p>You will be assisting a Lead Tech with performing a video Wall installation &amp; integration. Tasks can include all or some of the following:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Unpacking and Testing Video wall cabinets</li><li>Installing and aligning video wall modules</li><li>Installing mount / frame kit</li><li>Must be detail focused</li><li>Must be able to lift 75lbs</li><li>Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><u>Failure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site</u>.&nbsp;Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression.&nbsp;If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.</p><p><strong><em>Mounting Tools:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits</li><li>Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)</li><li>Box knife</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>PPE</em></strong></p><ul><li><u>If Noted and Required: You are required to have basic PPE</u> (<em>Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves</em>) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><u>DO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS</u>. Any additional parts or materials must be secured by the Lead Tech on site. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the <u>Project Manager</u> listed on this work order <u>IMMEDIATELY</u> any such purchases require <u>PRE-AUTHORIZATION</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>HERMAN GUIDELINES</u></strong></p><p><strong>Schedule:</strong>&nbsp;Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical.&nbsp;Any overtime hours <u>MUST be PRE-APPROVED</u>&nbsp;by the Project Manager.</p><p><strong>Running late/Unable to make it</strong>: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via&nbsp;<u>&nbsp;phone</u>&nbsp;IMMEDIATELY.</p><p><strong>Switching Workers:</strong>&nbsp;Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project.</p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).</p><p><strong>Heights:</strong>&nbsp;Must be comfortable working off a ladder.</p><p><strong>Site Conditions:</strong>&nbsp;Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)</p><p><strong>Parking Instructions:</strong>&nbsp;If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order.&nbsp;We cannot accept handwritten receipts.</p><p><strong>Security Instructions:&nbsp;</strong>Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times</p><p><strong>Transportation:&nbsp;</strong>Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.</p><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li>Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.</li><li>Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.</li><li>Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.</li><li>Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.</li><li>No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite &amp; in from of the customer</li><li>If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site</li><li>Do NOT place tools on furniture.&nbsp;</li><li>SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE</u></strong></p><ol><li>Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete&nbsp;a Field Report for <u>EACH</u> <u>DAY</u> worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><u>ON-SITE TASKS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check into your Work Order</li><li>Call the&nbsp;<em>LOCATION CONTACT</em>&nbsp;at the phone number provided on this work order&nbsp;upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site</li><li>Obtain completed and signed field report</li><li>With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done</li><li>Obtain Signature</li><li>Check out of Work Order</li></ol><p><strong>Any expenses&nbsp;<u>MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU</u>&nbsp;on the work order and&nbsp;<u>MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT</u>.​</strong></p>","markdown":"**BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.**\n\nPlease Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done, in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\nYou will be assisting a Lead Tech with performing a video Wall installation & integration. Tasks can include all or some of the following:\n\n- Unpacking and Testing Video wall cabinets\n- Installing and aligning video wall modules\n- Installing mount / frame kit\n- Must be detail focused\n- Must be able to lift 75lbs\n- Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go\n\n**REQUIRED EQUIPMENT**\n\nFailure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site. Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression. If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.\n\n***Mounting Tools:***\n\n- Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits\n- Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)\n- Box knife\n\n***PPE***\n\n- If Noted and Required: You are required to have basic PPE (*Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves*) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.\n\nDO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS. Any additional parts or materials must be secured by the Lead Tech on site. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the Project Manager listed on this work order IMMEDIATELY any such purchases require PRE-AUTHORIZATION\n\n**HERMAN GUIDELINES**\n\n**Schedule:** Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical. Any overtime hours MUST be PRE-APPROVED by the Project Manager.\n\n**Running late/Unable to make it**: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via  phone IMMEDIATELY.\n\n**Switching Workers:** Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project.\n\n**Dress Code:** You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).\n\n**Heights:** Must be comfortable working off a ladder.\n\n**Site Conditions:** Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)\n\n**Parking Instructions:** If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order. We cannot accept handwritten receipts.\n\n**Security Instructions:** Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times\n\n**Transportation:** Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT**\n\n- Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.\n- Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.\n- Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.\n- Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.\n- No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite & in from of the customer\n- If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site\n- Do NOT place tools on furniture.\n- SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order\n\n**BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE**\n\n1. Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete a Field Report for EACH DAY worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\n1. Check into your Work Order\n2. Call the *LOCATION CONTACT* at the phone number provided on this work order upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site\n3. Obtain completed and signed field report\n4. With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done\n5. Obtain Signature\n6. Check out of Work Order\n\n**Any expenses MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU on the work order and MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT.​**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T08:00","end":"2026-10-13T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Oct 13, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-29T14:00: