{"job":{"id":"5605824575","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"EPIK Device RMA Swap Old Box SN 2022230181  New Box SN 2039230572","description":"&lt;&lt; EPIK EQUIPMENT REPLACEMENT &gt;&gt; PoLTE / Epik Activations  <br>SN: (Old Box 2022230181  New Box 2039230572) <br><br><br><br>•Call into Granite NOC at 844-492-2557 (OPT. 4 then OPT. 1) to start SoW.<br>•Locate the following Granite-provided Equipment: Epik Edge(s) Old Box 2022230181  New Box 2039230572<br>•Tech must take pictures of the EPIK 66 block and any/all connected 66 blocks and demarcations throughout the run to the connected equipment and send pictures to the NOC for further record. <br>•Once punch downs are confirmed to be correct and no shorts are apparent on the line, installation of the new device can commence:<br>•Uninstall the EPIK device that is deemed to be defective <br>•Install New EPIK router in same location<br>•Work with NOC to cross connect (if needed) and test numbers <br>•If pre-existing wiring is in use, do NOT disconnect existing equipment without first checking in with the NOC team.<br>•Complete Inbound and Outbound testing for each device:  phones, fax, fire, burglar, etc.<br>•Troubleshoot if required and as requested by NOC. <br>•NOC technician MUST click the “Integrate” button on new device once box swap is complete. Monitoring should be disabled on old device and enabled on new device. <br><br>ONCE INSTALL IS COMPLETE:<br><br>•Tech must package up defective equipment in the same box the new device came in. The return shipping label should be included and added onto the box. Once the device is packaged up, tech must inform MOD or LCON where the package is to be dropped off at local UPS store. <br>•****Approval to release required from EPIK rep and Granite IW****","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T01:00","end":"2026-09-29T04:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours