{"job":{"id":20052914,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"P3 Global Services","title":"**HEXED/ICE AGE** banner replacement - PLEASE, READ THE SERVICE DESCRIPTION COMPLETELY","description":{"html":"<p>PLEASE MAKE SURE HEXED SIDE IS THE ONE SHOWING.</p><p>SEE ATTACHED IMAGE OF WHAT THE BANNER STAND LOOKS LIKE.</p><p><strong><em><u>By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you do not do the install for any reason out of your control. Any request for travel pay MUST be made as a counter-offer before job is accepted.&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Please do not call concerning schedule changes, missing pieces, etc. Only call if urgent, all other issues please send a message within Field Nation. ALMOST ALL ISSUES ARE NOT URGENT AND SHOULD BE SENT VIA MESSAGE.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Please upload only ONE photo... either the completed banner or the manager's signature. Please do not upload ANY other photos.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE BANNER FROM THEATRE PREMISES.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>ANY delays beyond the stated schedule MUST be reported to Vision Media as soon as you know you will be late.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Please, do not send counter offers via message. All counter offers must be sent using the counter offer option in Field Nation.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>A banner is a vinyl sign that hangs from the ceiling or on a wall. Vision Media cannot tell you if a ladder or lift will be required as we do not know where the theatre will ask for the banner to be hung. You are NOT responsible for bringing any ladder or lift with you. If the theatre requires a ladder or lift and they cannot provide one for you, it will be considered as a denied install.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Banner should never touch the floor. If the banner touches the floor, the area is not large enough. Request that manager find another spot.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DO NOT INSTALL ANY OTHER ITEM WITHOUT FIRST GETTING APPROVAL FROM VISION MEDIA. IF YOU INSTALL AN ITEM OTHER THAN WHAT THE ORDER IS FOR, YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em> WORK ORDER MUST BE CLOSED OUT&nbsp;<u>BEFORE 9AM EASTERN THE DAY AFTER THE DEADLINE</u>. Failure to do so could result in a 10% penalty or removal from the job.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> Note: Theatres will only allow installs Monday through Thursday. Do NOT attempt installs on Friday, Saturday, Sunday or holidays unless work order specifically notes it should be done or you have made arrangements with theatre management. Install can be done early if banner has delivered.&nbsp;<u>Do not go to the theatre if tracking has not been uploaded. Send a message to Vision Media via Field Nation messenger requesting tracking information.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>Package will be shipping directly to the theatre. Please check tracking at bottom of details tab before heading to the theatre.</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Looking for smart hand technicians to complete simple setup of banner Displays</li><li>Banner for the motion picture \"HEXED/ICE AGE”&nbsp;</li><li>Please note that the only time requirement set forth by Vision Media is that the job be complete by the due date. Other than that, any specific dates/times are between you and the theatre and<strong>&nbsp;do not need communicated to P3 GLOBAL</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Please reach out to us via messages/email/phone only if there are issues or questions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-Site</u></strong></p><ol><li>Contact theater before leaving for site to verify that it is open. If you cannot reach site with the number in the work order, please Google the number. <strong>Do NOT ask if banner is on site, use tracking for this. Do NOT tell them you are calling to install a banner. You MUST go on site to receive any payment.</strong></li><li>Read the service description completely.</li><li>Set ETA.&nbsp;<strong>Please note, we will use this ETA to determine when the job will be done so please set it accurately. If you miss your ETA, we will begin questioning.</strong></li><li>Print out of the work order</li><li>Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived.&nbsp;<strong><u>If package has not arrived, DO NOT GO TO SITE. Send a message through Field Nation to Vision Media so we can research.</u></strong></li><li><br></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Upon arrival:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Check-in using the mobile app, unless there is a problem then contact Vision Media at&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(77, 77, 76);\">(661) 702-5153&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;if Monday-Friday between 9AM and 5:30PM PT. Otherwise, send message on Field Nation.&nbsp;Please only call if urgent. We have too many jobs to be taking superfluous&nbsp;calls. Most questions are answered below.</li><li>Ask for a manager to retrieve the package.</li><li>Hang the banner in a location of the theatre manager's choosing.</li><li>Instructions and tools (if needed) are supplied in the box.&nbsp;<strong><u>DO NOT MODIFY THE BANNER IN ANY WAY. BANNER MUST BE HANGING FOR JOB TO BE CONSIDERED COMPLETE.</u></strong></li><li>Take a photo from approx 20 ft away. The photo must clearly show the item in the theatre surroundings. If the install cannot happen for any reason, please try to get a copy of the work order signed by a manager and upload a photo of that.&nbsp;<strong><u>Also, under no circumstances should you upload photos of different items with the same title, damaged pieces, outside of theatre, items for different titles, etc.</u></strong></li><li>Please upload only ONE photo, stand back while taking the picture so we are able to see the item in the theater setting (or, in case of denial, upload ONLY ONE photo of the work order signed by the manager on duty. If manager refuses to sign, upload a photo of \"REFUSED TO SIGN\" written on a piece of paper).</li><li>Get Manager on duty's name.</li><li>Make sure to close out the&nbsp;work order&nbsp;with notes.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong><u> If Unable to Install, Follow instructions below:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you are unable to install. There is no need to call concerning any of the issues below.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If you can't install, follow these steps:&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li><strong>If item is unable to be installed, request that theatre keep item for possible FedEx/ UPS pickup. If missing pieces, please note which specific pieces in closing notes and request theatre keep item for future install once replacement pieces arrive. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE BANNER FROM THE THEATRE.</strong></li><li><strong>Check out of WO</strong></li><li><strong>Enter Close out notes of why you couldn't perform install</strong></li><li><strong>Take a picture of Manager Signature on WO as to Confirm they don't want the install to occur.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Leave the item with the theatre manager.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Enter a discount to bring payment down to $20. If this is not done, work order will be marked incomplete delaying payment.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p>Examples of denied install reasons:</p><ul><li>Already installed by theatre (in this case, we still need a photo of the installed banner)</li><li>Not Playing Movie</li><li>Item Too Large</li><li>No Room to Accommodate at this Time -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre does not have room at this time. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. Please note the date after which they believe they will have room.</strong></li><li>Requires Corporate Approval&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre requires corporate approval. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.</strong></li><li>Content is Inappropriate</li><li>Theatre Requests Later Installation Date -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. Please note the date which they request an install.</strong></li><li>Theatre Does Not Display this Item</li><li>Theatre Unable to Locate Item -&nbsp;<strong>If tracking shows delivered, please close out work order. If tracking does not show delivered, please keep open and return once delivered.</strong></li><li>Missing/Damaged Pieces -&nbsp;<strong>Please note the specific parts missing/damaged by the number in the instruction guide in your closing notes. DO NOT UPLOAD PHOTOS OF DAMAGED PIECES.</strong></li><li>Release Date Too Far Out -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.</strong></li><li>Installed but not Functioning (please give further explanation)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>--- Very Important Additional Information ---</strong></p><ul><li>Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived.</li><li>Please review any attached instructions to confirm that you can complete the job in the allotted time and are comfortable with the agreed upon pay rate.</li><li>Please read the service description completely. This will answer 99% of the questions you may have.</li><li>If you go on-site before the theatre opens or before the item arrives, you will be asked to return without additional compensation.</li><li>Please adhere to the ETA that you enter. We monitor when jobs will be completed by this time.</li><li>Please note, we are only a fulfilment company and do not manufacture or design any of the items you will be installing. We will provide the manufacturer's instructions (when provided to us); but any questions about assembly will need to go to the manufacture (noted in the work order or on the instruction sheet).</li><li>The agreed upon price covers all of your transportation expenses (fuel, taxi, Uber, tolls, etc), travel time, Field Nation fees and install time.</li><li><br></li></ul>","markdown":"PLEASE MAKE SURE HEXED SIDE IS THE ONE SHOWING.\n\nSEE ATTACHED IMAGE OF WHAT THE BANNER STAND LOOKS LIKE.\n\n***By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you do not do the install for any reason out of your control. Any request for travel pay MUST be made as a counter-offer before job is accepted.***\n\n**Please do not call concerning schedule changes, missing pieces, etc. Only call if urgent, all other issues please send a message within Field Nation. ALMOST ALL ISSUES ARE NOT URGENT AND SHOULD BE SENT VIA MESSAGE.**\n\n***Please upload only ONE photo... either the completed banner or the manager's signature. Please do not upload ANY other photos.***\n\n**UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE BANNER FROM THEATRE PREMISES.**\n\n***ANY delays beyond the stated schedule MUST be reported to Vision Media as soon as you know you will be late.***\n\n***Please, do not send counter offers via message. All counter offers must be sent using the counter offer option in Field Nation.***\n\n**A banner is a vinyl sign that hangs from the ceiling or on a wall. Vision Media cannot tell you if a ladder or lift will be required as we do not know where the theatre will ask for the banner to be hung. You are NOT responsible for bringing any ladder or lift with you. If the theatre requires a ladder or lift and they cannot provide one for you, it will be considered as a denied install.**\n\n**Banner should never touch the floor. If the banner touches the floor, the area is not large enough. Request that manager find another spot.**\n\n**DO NOT INSTALL ANY OTHER ITEM WITHOUT FIRST GETTING APPROVAL FROM VISION MEDIA. IF YOU INSTALL AN ITEM OTHER THAN WHAT THE ORDER IS FOR, YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.**\n\n**Overview**\n\n ***WORK ORDER MUST BE CLOSED OUT BEFORE 9AM EASTERN THE DAY AFTER THE DEADLINE. Failure to do so could result in a 10% penalty or removal from the job.***\n\n **Note: Theatres will only allow installs Monday through Thursday. Do NOT attempt installs on Friday, Saturday, Sunday or holidays unless work order specifically notes it should be done or you have made arrangements with theatre management. Install can be done early if banner has delivered. Do not go to the theatre if tracking has not been uploaded. Send a message to Vision Media via Field Nation messenger requesting tracking information.**\n\n**Package will be shipping directly to the theatre. Please check tracking at bottom of details tab before heading to the theatre.**\n\n- Looking for smart hand technicians to complete simple setup of banner Displays\n- Banner for the motion picture \"HEXED/ICE AGE”\n- Please note that the only time requirement set forth by Vision Media is that the job be complete by the due date. Other than that, any specific dates/times are between you and the theatre and **do not need communicated to P3 GLOBAL**.\n- Please reach out to us via messages/email/phone only if there are issues or questions.\n\n**Pre-Site**\n\n1. Contact theater before leaving for site to verify that it is open. If you cannot reach site with the number in the work order, please Google the number. **Do NOT ask if banner is on site, use tracking for this. Do NOT tell them you are calling to install a banner. You MUST go on site to receive any payment.**\n2. Read the service description completely.\n3. Set ETA. **Please note, we will use this ETA to determine when the job will be done so please set it accurately. If you miss your ETA, we will begin questioning.**\n4. Print out of the work order\n5. Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived. **If package has not arrived, DO NOT GO TO SITE. Send a message through Field Nation to Vision Media so we can research.**\n6. \n\n**Upon arrival:**\n\n1. Check-in using the mobile app, unless there is a problem then contact Vision Media at (661) 702-5153  if Monday-Friday between 9AM and 5:30PM PT. Otherwise, send message on Field Nation. Please only call if urgent. We have too many jobs to be taking superfluous calls. Most questions are answered below.\n2. Ask for a manager to retrieve the package.\n3. Hang the banner in a location of the theatre manager's choosing.\n4. Instructions and tools (if needed) are supplied in the box. **DO NOT MODIFY THE BANNER IN ANY WAY. BANNER MUST BE HANGING FOR JOB TO BE CONSIDERED COMPLETE.**\n5. Take a photo from approx 20 ft away. The photo must clearly show the item in the theatre surroundings. If the install cannot happen for any reason, please try to get a copy of the work order signed by a manager and upload a photo of that. **Also, under no circumstances should you upload photos of different items with the same title, damaged pieces, outside of theatre, items for different titles, etc.**\n6. Please upload only ONE photo, stand back while taking the picture so we are able to see the item in the theater setting (or, in case of denial, upload ONLY ONE photo of the work order signed by the manager on duty. If manager refuses to sign, upload a photo of \"REFUSED TO SIGN\" written on a piece of paper).\n7. Get Manager on duty's name.\n8. Make sure to close out the work order with notes.\n\n **If Unable to Install, Follow instructions below:**\n\n**By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you are unable to install. There is no need to call concerning any of the issues below.**\n\n**If you can't install, follow these steps:**\n\n1. **If item is unable to be installed, request that theatre keep item for possible FedEx/ UPS pickup. If missing pieces, please note which specific pieces in closing notes and request theatre keep item for future install once replacement pieces arrive. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE BANNER FROM THE THEATRE.**\n2. **Check out of WO**\n3. **Enter Close out notes of why you couldn't perform install**\n4. **Take a picture of Manager Signature on WO as to Confirm they don't want the install to occur.**\n5. **Leave the item with the theatre manager.**\n6. **Enter a discount to bring payment down to $20. If this is not done, work order will be marked incomplete delaying payment.**\n\nExamples of denied install reasons:\n\n- Already installed by theatre (in this case, we still need a photo of the installed banner)\n- Not Playing Movie\n- Item Too Large\n- No Room to Accommodate at this Time - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre does not have room at this time. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. Please note the date after which they believe they will have room.**\n- Requires Corporate Approval - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre requires corporate approval. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.**\n- Content is Inappropriate\n- Theatre Requests Later Installation Date - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. Please note the date which they request an install.**\n- Theatre Does Not Display this Item\n- Theatre Unable to Locate Item - **If tracking shows delivered, please close out work order. If tracking does not show delivered, please keep open and return once delivered.**\n- Missing/Damaged Pieces - **Please note the specific parts missing/damaged by the number in the instruction guide in your closing notes. DO NOT UPLOAD PHOTOS OF DAMAGED PIECES.**\n- Release Date Too Far Out - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.**\n- Installed but not Functioning (please give further explanation)\n\n**--- Very Important Additional Information ---**\n\n- Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived.\n- Please review any attached instructions to confirm that you can complete the job in the allotted time and are comfortable with the agreed upon pay rate.\n- Please read the service description completely. This will answer 99% of the questions you may have.\n- If you go on-site before the theatre opens or before the item arrives, you will be asked to return without additional compensation.\n- Please adhere to the ETA that you enter. We monitor when jobs will be completed by this time.\n- Please note, we are only a fulfilment company and do not manufacture or design any of the items you will be installing. We will provide the manufacturer's instructions (when provided to us); but any questions about assembly will need to go to the manufacture (noted in the work order or on the instruction sheet).\n- The agreed upon price covers all of your transportation expenses (fuel, taxi, Uber, tolls, etc), travel time, Field Nation fees and install time.\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T12:00","end":"2026-10-08T22:00"},"payRange":{"min":25,"max":25},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":0.25,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/28/2026, 12:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-28T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"s