{"job":{"id":20051037,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axper","title":"Talbots 402 - Only Top-Tier Cabling Technicians Need Apply   Think You re Up for the Challenge?","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Short Description</strong></p><p>Talbots Store &ndash; IP People-Counter Camera Installation and Cabling</p><p>Installation for advanced cabling technicians, two technicians are required.</p><p>The store is equipped with 2 entrances to be cabled from each entrance to the back office. The access to the ceiling appears to be limited. </p><p>A site survey (15-20 min.) is mandatory at least one week before the installation to evaluate the cable route, required materials, ceiling conditions and equipment needed. </p><p>Included in estimated pay rate:</p><p>Survey: $150</p><p>Travel Fees: $55</p><p>Material and consumable: $65 (per entrance) </p><p>Labor for two technicians</p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install IP people-counter camera near the store entrance. Usually around 3 feet from the door, centered as much as possible.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Run and terminate one network cable from the network room to the camera.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Test and label the cable.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide completion photos and cable-test results.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Estimated duration: 3-4 hours on site for both technicians.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work must begin at 6:00 a.m. (The store opens at 10:00 a.m.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Strong cabling experience.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Two technicians must be present.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Properly equipped for difficult cable routes</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cat5e or better solid-copper cable; appropriate CMP/plenum-rated cable when required; no CCA.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Termination tools, cable tester, toner, fish rods, fish tape, drill and appropriate ladder 8 feet and up.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Check-In and Installation</strong></p><p><strong>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon arrival, technicians must call Axper before starting <u>1-866-658-2360 option 470</u></strong>.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The store opens at 10am. Axper will communicate with you a 9 am for a check point if the installation is not yet completed.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any additional work or material must be approved by Axper before proceeding. Technicians must receive Axper's approval before leaving the site.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any issues must be reported immediately to<strong><u> Axper 1-866-658-2360 option 470&nbsp;</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**Short Description**\n\nTalbots Store – IP People-Counter Camera Installation and Cabling\n\nInstallation for advanced cabling technicians, two technicians are required.\n\nThe store is equipped with 2 entrances to be cabled from each entrance to the back office. The access to the ceiling appears to be limited.\n\nA site survey (15-20 min.) is mandatory at least one week before the installation to evaluate the cable route, required materials, ceiling conditions and equipment needed.\n\nIncluded in estimated pay rate:\n\nSurvey: $150\n\nTravel Fees: $55\n\nMaterial and consumable: $65 (per entrance)\n\nLabor for two technicians\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n\\- Install IP people-counter camera near the store entrance. Usually around 3 feet from the door, centered as much as possible.\n\n\\- Run and terminate one network cable from the network room to the camera.\n\n\\- Test and label the cable.\n\n\\- Provide completion photos and cable-test results.\n\n\\- Estimated duration: 3-4 hours on site for both technicians.\n\n\\- Work must begin at 6:00 a.m. (The store opens at 10:00 a.m.)\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\n\\- Strong cabling experience.\n\n\\- Two technicians must be present.\n\n\\- Properly equipped for difficult cable routes\n\n\\- Cat5e or better solid-copper cable; appropriate CMP/plenum-rated cable when required; no CCA.\n\n\\- Termination tools, cable tester, toner, fish rods, fish tape, drill and appropriate ladder 8 feet and up.\n\n**Check-In and Installation**\n\n**- Upon arrival, technicians must call Axper before starting 1-866-658-2360 option 470**.\n\n\\- The store opens at 10am. Axper will communicate with you a 9 am for a check point if the installation is not yet completed.\n\n\\- Any additional work or material must be approved by Axper before proceeding. Technicians must receive Axper's approval before leaving the site.\n\n\\- Any issues must be reported immediately to **Axper 1-866-658-2360 option 470**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T06:00","end":"2026-10-13T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":815,"max":815},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Oct 13, 6:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)