{"job":{"id":20057574,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Please adhere to the following mandatory guidelines for all site visits:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not leave the site</strong>without prior permission from myself and our team or the DCC team.</p>\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Do not contact the POC</strong>(Point of Contact) before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Dress Code- Business Casuals.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not discuss the</strong> payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mandatory Do's &amp; Don’ts</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. Dress Code- Business Casuals.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2. Do not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Ticket Type: <strong>Network (DIGI INSTALLATION)</strong></p>\n<p>Date &amp; Time: <strong>01st Oct, 9:30 ET</strong></p>\n<p>Visit Type- <strong>Hourly&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>1.Mandatory Dos &amp; Don'ts:</p>\n<p>Dress Code- Business Casuals.</p>\n<p>Do not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>2.Clinic ID: 3252&nbsp;</p>\n<p>3.Facility address: 76 OLD ROCK SPRING CEMETARY RD, PITTSBORO, NC 27312</p>\n<p>4.Clinic working hours: 09:00 ET</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>8.Short description of the reported issue:</p>\n<p>DIGI installation.</p>\n<p>9.If L1/L2 is required: L2</p>\n<p>10.Mandate Action required:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p>\n<p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.</p>\n<p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).</p>\n<p>-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p>\n<p>-10 ft data cable.</p>\n<p>-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch</p>\n<p>-Cable tester&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Tone generator&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Toner</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>12.Scope of Work:&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Technician must be capable of connecting power cords, ethernet cables, using network patch panels, and mounting the hardware using hand tools. Tools that will be needed at a minimum are screwdrivers, side cutters or scissors. Technician will have to contact <strong>Daryl</strong> prior and while onsite during the installation</p>\n<p>13.After the completion of Visit:</p>\n<p>Update the SVR with Resolution Steps</p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**Please adhere to the following mandatory guidelines for all site visits:**\n\n**1. Do not leave the site**without prior permission from myself and our team or the DCC team.\n\n2\\. **Do not contact the POC**(Point of Contact) before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n3\\. **Dress Code- Business Casuals.**\n\n**4. Do not discuss the** payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\n**Mandatory Do's & Don’ts**\n\n**1. Dress Code- Business Casuals.**\n\n**2. Do not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.**\n\nTicket Type: **Network (DIGI INSTALLATION)**\n\nDate & Time: **01st Oct, 9:30 ET**\n\nVisit Type- **Hourly**\n\n1.Mandatory Dos & Don'ts:\n\nDress Code- Business Casuals.\n\nDo not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.\n\n2.Clinic ID: 3252\n\n3.Facility address: 76 OLD ROCK SPRING CEMETARY RD, PITTSBORO, NC 27312\n\n4.Clinic working hours: 09:00 ET\n\n8.Short description of the reported issue:\n\nDIGI installation.\n\n9.If L1/L2 is required: L2\n\n10.Mandate Action required:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support\n\n11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:\n\n-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).\n\n-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-10 ft data cable.\n\n-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch\n\n-Cable tester\n\n-Tone generator\n\n-Toner\n\n12.Scope of Work:\n\nTechnician must be capable of connecting power cords, ethernet cables, using network patch panels, and mounting the hardware using hand tools. Tools that will be needed at a minimum are screwdrivers, side cutters or scissors. Technician will have to contact **Daryl** prior and while onsite during the installation\n\n13.After the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the SVR with Resolution Steps","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T09:30","end":"2026-10-01T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":26},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000