{"job":{"id":20058724,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Deployment of new POS, network, and CCTV equipment for acquisition - Lead Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong><u>TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS.  ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT.  ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">A 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date.&nbsp;At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy <del>*** ****</del> network and hardware with the new <del>*****</del> equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.</span></p><p><strong><em>The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.</em></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</li><li>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Deployment Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><ul><li>Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos</li><li>Install Network Rack Equipment</li></ul><p>----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch</p><p>----You will need to work with you <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem</p><ul><li>Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)</li></ul><p>----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed</p><p>----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs</p><p>----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important</p><ul><li>Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity</li><li>Install Multifunction Printer&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Install i-Gel Cubics PCs</li><li>Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)</li><li>Install Cameras</li><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with <del>*****</del> IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS. ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT. ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nA 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date. At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* network and hardware with the new \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.\n\n***The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.***\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Deployment Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n- Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos\n- Install Network Rack Equipment\n\n\\----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch\n\n\\----You will need to work with you \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem\n\n- Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)\n\n\\----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed\n\n\\----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs\n\n\\----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important\n\n- Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity\n- Install Multifunction Printer\n- Install i-Gel Cubics PCs\n- Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)\n- Install Cameras\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T10:00","end":"2026-10-19T30:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":1300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":20,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 19, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 19, Tue, Oct 20, Wed, Oct 21, Thu, Oct 22, Fri, Oct 23 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{