Scope of Work:**\n\nA 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date. At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* network and hardware with the new \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.\n\n***The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.***\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Deployment Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n- Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos\n- Install Network Rack Equipment\n\n\\----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch\n\n\\----You will need to work with you \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem\n\n- Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)\n\n\\----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed\n\n\\----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs\n\n\\----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important\n\n- Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity\n- Install Multifunction Printer\n- Install i-Gel Cubics PCs\n- Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)\n- Install Cameras\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T10:00","end":"2026-10-19T30:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":1100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":20,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 19, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 19, Tue, Oct 20, Wed, Oct 21, Thu, Oct 22, Fri, Oct 23 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T0