{"job":{"id":20058860,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Deployment of new POS, network, and CCTV equipment for acquisition - Assistant Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span><u>TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS. ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT. ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">A 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date.&nbsp;At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy <del>*** ****</del> network and hardware with the new <del>*****</del> equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.</span></p><p><strong><em>The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.</em></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</li><li>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Deployment Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><ul><li>Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos</li><li>Install Network Rack Equipment</li></ul><p>----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch</p><p>----You will need to work with you <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem</p><ul><li>Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)</li></ul><p>----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed</p><p>----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs</p><p>----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important</p><ul><li>Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity</li><li>Install Multifunction Printer&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Install i-Gel Cubics PCs</li><li>Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)</li><li>Install Cameras</li><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with <del>*****</del> IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**﻿TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS. ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT. ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nA 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date. At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* network and hardware with the new \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.\n\n***The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.***\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Deployment Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n- Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos\n- Install Network Rack Equipment\n\n\\----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch\n\n\\----You will need to work with you \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem\n\n- Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)\n\n\\----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed\n\n\\----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs\n\n\\----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important\n\n- Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity\n- Install Multifunction Printer\n- Install i-Gel Cubics PCs\n- Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)\n- Install Cameras\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T10:00","end":"2026-10-14T30:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":1100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":20,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790709096306}
{"job":{"id":20058798,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Device offline**See required tools**","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;<del>********* *****</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required On-site time/window: 9/30/2026</u></strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Equipment:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Make/Model: LEVEL2VOICE</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Problem Description:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Mahmood Ibrahim 786-506-9116</p>\n<p>Burger King Device Offline</p>\n<p>Please check if the Drive thru director is on the same vlan as the chef, if not, tech will have to contact the HME Vendor to change the ip and get it on the same vlan as chef Network Switch and Port, if known : PLEASE SCHEULE THIS FOR 9/30 in the Morning Response Time Requested (Hr) : Scheduled (non-SLA) Tech type : Level 2 Network Voice tech</p>\n<p>Technician needs to be prepared to tone, trace, repair, or replace while onsite.</p>\n<p>Technicians are required to use the provided box(es) and all packing materials for shipping equipment. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Failure to package the equipment securely and provide requested photos will result in penalties if the equipment is inbounded and determined to be damaged.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Important Scope/Customer Information:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Any changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial <strong>via phone.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Parts and Support are provided by<del>****** ******* * ** ******* **** ******* ****** *</del></strong> <del>********************</del></p>\n<p>If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this - Contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise</p>\n<p><strong>If additional parts are needed there will be another trip&nbsp;REQUIRED, You MUST contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required online deliverable.</p>\n<p>If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Important Tech Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of<del>****** ******* ** ******* ****</del></li>\n<li>Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival</li>\n<li>Tech MUST package returned equipment security for shipment and upload photos.</li>\n<li>Tech MUST complete online deliverable prior to leaving site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>150 FT Cat 5/6 Cable</li>\n<li>Standard/Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li>\n<li>Laptop, with access to a cellular hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Straps or Velcro</li>\n<li>Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)</li>\n<li>Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment</li>\n<li>Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)</li>\n<li>Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Online Deliverable Requirements | Deliverable Link:&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.jotform.com/250866044689166</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or&nbsp;If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact <del>** ******* **** * **************</del> to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off</li>\n<li>Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device</li>\n<li>Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Upon Arrival at site:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of <del>****** ******* ****</del> to the onsite MOD</li>\n<li>If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot/repair or replace failed component to return failed system to working order</li>\n<li>Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by<del>**</del> Help Desk.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm functionality with XXXXX &amp; provide their name upon closure</li>\n<li>Complete online Deliverable</li>\n<li>Technician to use the box that component arrived in to return failed component utilizing provided return label.&nbsp;All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing.&nbsp;Technician will leave the box at site with the Store Manager or POC for Customer to arrange pickup.</li>\n<li>Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time & only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.**\n\n**YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.**\n\n \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Required On-site time/window: 9/30/2026**\n\n**Equipment:**\n\nMake/Model: LEVEL2VOICE\n\n**Problem Description:**\n\nMahmood Ibrahim 786-506-9116\n\nBurger King Device Offline\n\nPlease check if the Drive thru director is on the same vlan as the chef, if not, tech will have to contact the HME Vendor to change the ip and get it on the same vlan as chef Network Switch and Port, if known : PLEASE SCHEULE THIS FOR 9/30 in the Morning Response Time Requested (Hr) : Scheduled (non-SLA) Tech type : Level 2 Network Voice tech\n\nTechnician needs to be prepared to tone, trace, repair, or replace while onsite.\n\nTechnicians are required to use the provided box(es) and all packing materials for shipping equipment. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Failure to package the equipment securely and provide requested photos will result in penalties if the equipment is inbounded and determined to be damaged.\n\n**Important Scope/Customer Information:**\n\nAny changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial **via phone.**\n\n**Parts and Support are provided by\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIf you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this - Contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise\n\n**If additional parts are needed there will be another trip REQUIRED, You MUST contact Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.**\n\nAll times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required online deliverable.\n\nIf additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies & Procedures #6.\n\n**Important Tech Requirements:**\n\n- Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival\n- Tech MUST package returned equipment security for shipment and upload photos.\n- Tech MUST complete online deliverable prior to leaving site\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- 150 FT Cat 5/6 Cable\n- Standard/Basic hand tools\n- Screwdrivers\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Laptop, with access to a cellular hotspot\n- Cable Straps or Velcro\n- Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)\n- Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment\n- Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)\n- Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)\n\n**Online Deliverable Requirements | Deliverable Link:** <https://essintial.jotform.com/250866044689166>\n\n- Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off\n- Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables\n\n**Upon Arrival at site:**\n\n- Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* to the onsite MOD\n- If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.\n- Troubleshoot/repair or replace failed component to return failed system to working order\n- Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by\\*\\* Help Desk.\n\n**Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:**\n\n- Confirm functionality with XXXXX & provide their name upon closure\n- Complete online Deliverable\n- Technician to use the box that component arrived in to return failed component utilizing provided return label. All equipment must be securely packaged and technicians should take photos of the package before sealing it to ensure proper packing. Technician will leave the box at site with the Store Manager or POC for Customer to arrange pickup.\n- Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-30T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":47},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 1, 9:00 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $180\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi -