{"job":{"id":20059557,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Assist Technician | Firm Start | Overnight Store Remodel - Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Remaining Scope:1.Rewire 6x Access points to the MDF.-Rewire the 6 access points that are plugged into ports 20-25 on switch H2 in the Assistant managers office (toning as necessary to identify which APs these are). Punch into main patch panels and patch into H1-H2 ports 20-25.2.Locate H2 and H3 switch in Cash office. Validate there are no more devices showing activity lights on the ports. If you see any you will need to tone them and get new lines run for those devices.-Move H2 to MDF and box up H3 to hand to manager to return to corporate. Once switch is moved to the MDF, reconnect to network by patching H2 port 49 to H1 port 50.Cash office IDF Rack Removal- Uninstall IDF rack mounting hardware and patch panel. Dispose of these and pull old cabling high into the ceiling and cut, making sure none of the cables are in use Switch - REQ1492469Cash Office Switch Move3. Install Learning Center computers / TV Security Code: 862384</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Seeking an Assist</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Over Multiple</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">NIGHTs</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store's cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 