{"job":{"id":20059477,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Lead Technician | Firm Start | Overnight Store Remodel - Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Remaining Scope:1.Rewire 6x Access points to the MDF.-Rewire the 6 access points that are plugged into ports 20-25 on switch H2 in the Assistant managers office (toning as necessary to identify which APs these are). Punch into main patch panels and patch into H1-H2 ports 20-25.2.Locate H2 and H3 switch in Cash office. Validate there are no more devices showing activity lights on the ports. If you see any you will need to tone them and get new lines run for those devices.-Move H2 to MDF and box up H3 to hand to manager to return to corporate. Once switch is moved to the MDF, reconnect to network by patching H2 port 49 to H1 port 50.Cash office IDF Rack Removal- Uninstall IDF rack mounting hardware and patch panel. Dispose of these and pull old cabling high into the ceiling and cut, making sure none of the cables are in use Switch - REQ1492469Cash Office Switch Move3. Install Learning Center computers / TV Security Code: 862384</span></p><p><br></p><p>Seeking Lead<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;<strong>Over Multiple</strong>&nbsp;<strong>NIGHTs</strong>. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store's cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.</p><ul><li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">responsible</span>&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;</span>[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li><li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li><li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose \"In progress\" to avoid losing work.]</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; 