hile onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Remaining Scope:1.Rewire 6x Access points to the MDF.-Rewire the 6 access points that are plugged into ports 20-25 on switch H2 in the Assistant managers office (toning as necessary to identify which APs these are). Punch into main patch panels and patch into H1-H2 ports 20-25.2.Locate H2 and H3 switch in Cash office. Validate there are no more devices showing activity lights on the ports. If you see any you will need to tone them and get new lines run for those devices.-Move H2 to MDF and box up H3 to hand to manager to return to corporate. Once switch is moved to the MDF, reconnect to network by patching H2 port 49 to H1 port 50.Cash office IDF Rack Removal- Uninstall IDF rack mounting hardware and patch panel. Dispose of these and pull old cabling high into the ceiling and cut, making sure none of the cables are in use Switch - REQ1492469Cash Office Switch Move3. Install Learning Center computers / TV Security Code: 862384\n\nSeeking an Assist Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store's cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*