{"job":{"id":20062540,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Camera – Troubleshooting – PTZ 2","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p>Tech needs to troubleshoot PTZ 2 camera located By the Shoes Sign</p>\n<p>• Archived view from camera -<del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></p>\n<p>• Tech will need to tone/test network run between camera and Switch H5</p>\n<p>• Check for a biscuit jack/network junction, which may be located in the ceiling along the cable path.</p>\n<p>• If a biscuit jack is located:</p>\n<p>o Inspect and re-punch the connections as needed, or</p>\n<p>o Terminate the network cable with an RJ45 connector and connect it directly to the camera,</p>\n<p>bypassing the biscuit jack.</p>\n<p>• Once troubleshooting and cabling work are complete, contact the TJX Help Desk at <del>************</del>, Option 1 →</p>\n<p>Option 8 → Option 1 for testing and verification.</p>\n<p>• If you are unable to reach the TJX Help Desk or do not receive a callback within 15 minutes, or require</p>\n<p>additional technical assistance, contact: Shyft/AVT National Technical Support at <del>************</del>, Option 3</p>\n<p>Device/Host Name:Qnp-6250</p>\n<p>Model Name:Hanawah</p>\n<p>IP Address:.<del>**</del></p>\n<p>MAC address:<del>**</del></p>\n<p>Camera Location:By the shoe sign</p>\n<p>Camera Height:12ft</p>\n<p>Ceiling Height:12ft</p>\n<p>Site Security Code: <del>******</del></p>\n<p>Customer Incident: <del>**********</del></p>\n<p>Estimated time: 2 hours</p>\n<p>Review the triage guide</p>\n<p><del>***********************************************</del></p>\n<p><strong>!!! Please provide the ceiling height in your closing notes !!!</strong></p>\n<p>Please call TJX help desk first before calling NTS</p>\n<p>TJX help desk: <del>************</del> option 1 option 8 option 1</p>\n<p>For additional technical assistance after calling TJX help desk, please call Shyft Services National Tech Support at<del>************</del>, opt 3.</p>\n<p>Troubleshooting steps:</p>\n<p>Problem: Offline camera High Level Steps:</p>\n<p>https://uploads.tdsynnex.com/f/9196e395aad63282</p>\n<p>1. Locate camera</p>\n<p>2. Locate switch port via label, TJX helpdesk, NTS L2 Support. Camera will be connected to either switch H5 or H6(except Sierra Trading Post stores)</p>\n<p>If unable to locate the tone-out cable, or work with support</p>\n<p>3. Reseat cable</p>\n<p>4. Try a different open port between 1-39</p>\n<p>5. Remove camera and plug directly into switch</p>\n<p>Required Technician Skills:</p>\n<p>Network Troubleshooting</p>\n<p>POS Support</p>\n<p>CCTV/PTZ Support</p>\n<p>Audio/Video Support</p>\n<p>Low voltage cabling</p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>Anti-Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat</p>\n<p>Laptop</p>\n<p>USB to serial connector</p>\n<p>Putty</p>\n<p>NULL Modem cable</p>\n<p>Ethernet cable</p>\n<p>Laptop Power pack</p>\n<p>Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet</p>\n<p>Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30</p>\n<p>Flashlight</p>\n<p>Digital Voltmeter</p>\n<p>Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - TeamViewer—The Digital Workplace Platform</p>\n<p>Velcro Straps</p>\n<p>Cross-over cable</p>\n<p>Standard screwdriver and security bits</p>\n<p>Thermal paste</p>\n<p>Alcohol Wipe</p>\n<p>Digital cable tester</p>\n<p>Digital Tone generator</p>\n<p>Punch down tool</p>\n<p>Crimping tools</p>\n<p>RJ45 crimper</p>\n<p>RJ45 connectors</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Support Process (Important)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ******</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong>If you encounter an issue while onsite:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Contact the <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong> and work through the issue with them.</li>\n<li>If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.</li>\n<li>If the issue is <strong>not resolved after working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ************ ****** * ****** * ****** *</del></strong>, then contact <strong>Shyft/NTS Support</strong> for further assistance.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>will be instructed to contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>first before additional support is provided.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Completion Requirements:</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Closing Notes</strong> – <strong>Should entered prior to leaving the site and should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.</strong> If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be a detailed and concise statement about the work performed.<strong>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\nTech needs to troubleshoot PTZ 2 camera located By the Shoes Sign\n\n• Archived view from camera -\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• Tech will need to tone/test network run between camera and Switch H5\n\n• Check for a biscuit jack/network junction, which may be located in the ceiling along the cable path.\n\n• If a biscuit jack is located:\n\no Inspect and re-punch the connections as needed, or\n\no Terminate the network cable with an RJ45 connector and connect it directly to the camera,\n\nbypassing the biscuit jack.\n\n• Once troubleshooting and cabling work are complete, contact the TJX Help Desk at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, Option 1 →\n\nOption 8 → Option 1 for testing and verification.\n\n• If you are unable to reach the TJX Help Desk or do not receive a callback within 15 minutes, or require\n\nadditional technical assistance, contact: Shyft/AVT National Technical Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, Option 3\n\nDevice/Host Name:Qnp-6250\n\nModel Name:Hanawah\n\nIP Address:.\\*\\*\n\nMAC address:\\*\\*\n\nCamera Location:By the shoe sign\n\nCamera Height:12ft\n\nCeiling Height:12ft\n\nSite Security Code: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCustomer Incident: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nEstimated time: 2 hours\n\nReview the triage guide\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**!!! Please provide the ceiling height in your closing notes !!!**\n\nPlease call TJX help desk first before calling NTS\n\nTJX help desk: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* option 1 option 8 option 1\n\nFor additional technical assistance after calling TJX help desk, please call Shyft Services National Tech Support at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, opt 3.\n\nTroubleshooting steps:\n\nProblem: Offline camera High Level Steps:\n\n<https://uploads.tdsynnex.com/f/9196e395aad63282>\n\n1\\. Locate camera\n\n2\\. Locate switch port via label, TJX helpdesk, NTS L2 Support. Camera will be connected to either switch H5 or H6(except Sierra Trading Post stores)\n\nIf unable to locate the tone-out cable, or work with support\n\n3\\. Reseat cable\n\n4\\. Try a different open port between 1-39\n\n5\\. Remove camera and plug directly into switch\n\nRequired Technician Skills:\n\nNetwork Troubleshooting\n\nPOS Support\n\nCCTV/PTZ Support\n\nAudio/Video Support\n\nLow voltage cabling\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nAnti-Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat\n\nLaptop\n\nUSB to serial connector\n\nPutty\n\nNULL Modem cable\n\nEthernet cable\n\nLaptop Power pack\n\nCell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet\n\nSet of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30\n\nFlashlight\n\nDigital Voltmeter\n\nTeam-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - TeamViewer—The Digital Workplace Platform\n\nVelcro Straps\n\nCross-over cable\n\nStandard screwdriver and security bits\n\nThermal paste\n\nAlcohol Wipe\n\nDigital cable tester\n\nDigital Tone generator\n\nPunch down tool\n\nCrimping tools\n\nRJ45 crimper\n\nRJ45 connectors\n\n**Technician Support Process (Important)**\n\n**Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If you encounter an issue while onsite:**\n\n1. Contact the **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*** and work through the issue with them.\n2. If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.\n3. If the issue is **not resolved after working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\***, then contact **Shyft/NTS Support** for further assistance.\n\n**Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****will be instructed to contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****first before additional support is provided.**\n\n***Completion Requirements:***\n\n**Closing Notes** – **Should entered prior to leaving the site and should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.** If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be a detailed and concise statement about the work performed.**Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.**\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T07:00","end":"2026-09-30T08:45","latestStart":"2026-09-30T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.75,"distance":79},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition o