{"job":{"id":20063829,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | QSIC Pendant Speaker Installation [Tech 1 / Lead Tech] This ticket will be assigned as requested is terms are agreed to.","description":{"html":"<p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician</u></strong></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Important</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></li><li>These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</li><li><strong>Penalties Apply IF you do not</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do Not Call&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong>&nbsp;if you are exceeding&nbsp;<strong>4 Hours Onsite</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>&nbsp;<strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">\"Pendant Speakers\" by mounting to the ceiling.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V&ndash;15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.</span></li><li><strong><u>Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide &ndash;</u></strong>&nbsp;any questions or issues need to be escalated to the&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li>Techs <strong>MUST</strong> PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!</li><li><strong><u>Techs&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.</li><li>Technicians (Tech 1/Lead &amp; Assist)&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;complete the Essintial Online Deliverable &ndash; Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.</li><li><strong>Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work&nbsp;</strong>-<strong>One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech</strong>&nbsp;and the other technician will be designated as an&nbsp;<strong>Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST</strong>.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Communication Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>ALL installation questions must go to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;call&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite &ndash; You MUST obtain approval!!!</strong></li><li>Technicians <strong>MUST</strong> Check-In and Check-Out with the <strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li><li>Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi</li><li>Standard Hand Tools</li><li>10Ft-12Ft Ladder</li><li>Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)</li><li>Long fiberglass push rods</li><li>wire strippers</li><li>Electrical Dykes</li><li>Utility Knife</li><li>Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors</li><li>Multi-meter&nbsp;- Capable of reading Ohms</li><li>Small Alan wrench &ndash; for pendant lock</li><li>Small Phillips and flat head screw driver</li><li>Micro flathead screwdriver</li><li>Laser Distance Measure &amp; Tape Measure</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Government Issued ID</li><li>LOA &ndash; Letter of Authorization</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Bill of Material:</u></strong>&nbsp;Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;FIRM START TIME!!!! YOU MUST ARRIVE AT ONTIME BASED ON THE START TIME SET BY ESSINTIAL. You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;</strong>4 Hours, If you are approaching that time, you must contact&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Technical Support&nbsp;</strong>to gain approval. If you cannot start work immediately, please reach out to Essintial and gain guidance.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself 