{"job":{"id":"7937467795","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Kinettix","title":"FSDP-2629-273022 - FATPIPE INSTALLATION &amp; Configuration","description":"<p>Assist&nbsp;with&nbsp;racking,&nbsp;configuring,&nbsp;and&nbsp;integrating&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;customers?&nbsp;network.&nbsp;Test&nbsp;the&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;to&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;connectivity&nbsp;and&nbsp;traffic&nbsp;passing.</p><p>1.&nbsp;You&nbsp;may&nbsp;contact&nbsp;us&nbsp;through&nbsp;email:&nbsp;support@fatpipeinc.com,&nbsp;by&nbsp;calling:&nbsp;1-800-724-8521;&nbsp;Ext&nbsp;3.</p><p>Prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;scheduled&nbsp;installation&nbsp;Teams&nbsp;meeting,&nbsp;please&nbsp;have&nbsp;the&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;unit(s)&nbsp;unboxed&nbsp;and&nbsp;powered&nbsp;on&nbsp;and&nbsp;follow&nbsp;the&nbsp;steps&nbsp;below&nbsp;for&nbsp;initial&nbsp;access:</p><p>1.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;assign&nbsp;192.168.0.10&nbsp;IP&nbsp;and&nbsp;subnet&nbsp;mask&nbsp;255.255.255.0&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;or&nbsp;MAC&nbsp;laptop&nbsp;and&nbsp;connect&nbsp;it&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;interface&nbsp;labeled&nbsp;LAN&nbsp;(or&nbsp;WAN1)&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;device.</p><p>2.&nbsp;From&nbsp;the&nbsp;browser&nbsp;please&nbsp;go&nbsp;to&nbsp;192.168.0.1&nbsp;IP.&nbsp;This&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;default&nbsp;LAN&nbsp;IP&nbsp;of&nbsp;FatPipe.</p><p>3.&nbsp;The&nbsp;default&nbsp;login&nbsp;is&nbsp;Administrator&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;blank&nbsp;password.</p><p>4.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;use&nbsp;WiFi&nbsp;on&nbsp;this&nbsp;laptop&nbsp;to&nbsp;access&nbsp;internet&nbsp;and&nbsp;join&nbsp;the&nbsp;Teams&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;so&nbsp;you&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;able&nbsp;to&nbsp;share&nbsp;the&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;UI&nbsp;screen.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>NOTE:</strong></p><p>The technician must be a U.S. citizen, possess a valid ID to present to the site contact, and wear a high-visibility vest and business casual attire.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Once&nbsp;onsite:</p><ul><li>The&nbsp;technician&nbsp;must&nbsp;call&nbsp;the&nbsp;Kinettix&nbsp;Dispatch&nbsp;line&nbsp;for&nbsp;check-in.</li><li>The&nbsp;technician&nbsp;must&nbsp;present&nbsp;a&nbsp;valid&nbsp;ID&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;POC&nbsp;and&nbsp;introduce&nbsp;themselves&nbsp;as&nbsp;representing&nbsp;Kinettix&nbsp;on&nbsp;behalf&nbsp;of&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;to&nbsp;install&nbsp;or&nbsp;troubleshoot&nbsp;FatPipe&nbsp;devices.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop with charger</li><li>Phone with camera</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Hotspot connection</li><li>8-12ft Ladder</li><li>Spool of Cat6 Cable</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Crimp tool</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Labeler</li><li>Velcro Ties</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Basic Cabling Tools</li><li>All necessary tools and materials to complete the scope.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Special&nbsp;Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;Requirements:&nbsp;Ensure&nbsp;connectivity&nbsp;and&nbsp;passing&nbsp;traffic</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T10:00","end":"2026-10-01T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":0},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790775591735}
{"job":{"id":"5605824575","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"EPIK Device RMA Swap Old Box SN 2022230181  New Box SN 2039230572","description":"&lt;&lt; EPIK EQUIPMENT REPLACEMENT &gt;&gt; PoLTE / Epik Activations  <br>SN: (Old Box 2022230181  New Box 2039230572) <br><br><br><br>•Call into Granite NOC at 844-492-2557 (OPT. 4 then OPT. 1) to start SoW.<br>•Locate the following Granite-provided Equipment: Epik Edge(s) Old Box 2022230181  New Box 2039230572<br>•Tech must take pictures of the EPIK 66 block and any/all connected 66 blocks and demarcations throughout the run to the connected equipment and send pictures to the NOC for further record. <br>•Once punch downs are confirmed to be correct and no shorts are apparent on the line, installation of the new device can commence:<br>•Uninstall the EPIK device that is deemed to be defective <br>•Install New EPIK router in same location<br>•Work with NOC to cross connect (if needed) and test numbers <br>•If pre-existing wiring is in use, do NOT disconnect existing equipment without first checking in with the NOC team.<br>•Complete Inbound and Outbound testing for each device:  phones, fax, fire, burglar, etc.<br>•Troubleshoot if required and as requested by NOC. <br>•NOC technician MUST click the “Integrate” button on new device once box swap is complete. Monitoring should be disabled on old device and enabled on new device. <br><br>ONCE INSTALL IS COMPLETE:<br><br>•Tech must package up defective equipment in the same box the new device came in. The return shipping label should be included and added onto the box. Once the device is packaged up, tech must inform MOD or LCON where the package is to be dropped off at local UPS store. <br>•****Approval to release required from EPIK rep and Granite IW****","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T14:30","end":"2026-09-29T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":168.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/29/2026, 2:30:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"2 ticket"},{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790777769260}
{"job":{"id":20064315,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"[ConnectWise Ticket#]","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> G135MA AMPLIFIER &amp; VOLUME CONTROL DECOMMISSIONING, NEW JBL NCS SERIES AMPLIFIER &amp; NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT &amp; SITE DISPOSAL STAGING</p><p><br></p><p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong></p><p>An audio and network technician is required on-site to decommission a legacy <strong>G135MA Amplifier</strong> and analog volume control wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and install a new <strong>JBL NCS Series Commercial Amplifier</strong> integrated with a <strong>Networked Volume Control</strong> wall controller.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will perform a layer-1 line diagnostics audit on all speaker trunk runs (measuring resistance $\\Omega$ and checking for ground faults) before connecting speaker loads to the replacement amplifier. The technician will unmount the legacy G135MA amplifier and analog volume control, install the new JBL NCS amplifier into the IT/audio rack, land a Cat5e/6 Ethernet drop to connect the new networked volume control to the local switch network, and coordinate directly with remote <strong>Activations</strong> to assign IP addresses, configure network controller binding, and push audio telemetry.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>AMPLIFIER SAFETY &amp; CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATE:</strong> Always keep utility power <strong>OFF</strong> or isolated while terminating speaker connections. Do <strong>NOT</strong> power on or land speaker trunk lines on the new JBL NCS amplifier until multimeter line impedance ($\\Omega$) and ground-fault checks confirm the speaker runs are completely safe ($&gt;\\infty\\Omega$ to chassis ground).</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DECOMMISSIONED ASSET DISPOSAL STAGING MANDATE:</strong> Carefully box up the decommissioned G135MA amplifier, its power cord, and the old volume control plate into empty hardware packaging. Write <strong>\"DECOMMISSIONED AUDIO HARDWARE - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> in bold permanent marker on the box and set it aside in an out-of-the-way, designated IT storage area for local removal by site staff. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must receive explicit operational, IP binding, and audio balance confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for JBL NCS amplifier web GUI access, IP discovery, network volume control binding, gateway ping sweeps, and audio portal verification)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter &amp; RJ45 Cable Tester / Wire Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for measuring speaker line impedance $\\Omega$, short-to-ground leaks, and 8-pin Cat5e/6 network drop continuity)</li><li><strong>Small Precision Screwdriver Set</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for Euroblock/Phoenix terminal block connectors on the JBL NCS amplifier and networked volume controller)</li><li><strong>Cat5e/6 &amp; Low-Voltage Audio Supplies:</strong> Pre-fabricated patch cords, RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, 16/2 or 18/2 speaker wire, strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>6–8ft Step Ladder</strong> (Required for accessing wall controller wire runs or overhead speaker junction points)</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits &amp; Mounting Hardware</strong> (For rack mounting hardware and wall plate mounting)</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong>, Label Maker, packaging tape, and permanent marker</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPSPHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong></p><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/IT rack and the volume control wall location. Collect the newly shipped hardware boxes (<strong>JBL NCS Series Amp</strong>, <strong>Networked Volume Control</strong>).</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the cutover sequence, network subnet parameters, and speaker zone mapping before disconnecting active equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING &amp; MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT</strong></p><ol><li><strong>G135MA DECOMMISSIONING:</strong> Turn <strong>OFF</strong> utility power to the legacy G135MA amplifier. Disconnect and label all input audio feeds, volume control wires, and speaker output leads. Unmount the G135MA amplifier and remove the legacy analog volume control wall plate.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Set your <strong>multimeter</strong> to measure resistance ($\\Omega$) across all speaker trunk leads. Confirm expected 70V High-Z or Low-Z circuit impedance parameters.</li><li>Measure resistance from each speaker lead to local rack/chassis ground to verify zero ground leaks. Resolve any short circuits before landing wire on the replacement amplifier.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>NETWORK CONTROL LINE VERIFICATION:</strong> Connect your cable tester to the Cat5e/6 network drop servicing the volume control location. Verify 8-pin T568B continuity back to the core network switch.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>PHASE 3: JBL NCS AMPLIFIER &amp; NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION</strong></p><ol><li><strong>HARDWARE MOUNTING:</strong> Securely rack-mount or shelf-position the new JBL NCS series amplifier in the IT/audio rack cabinet.</li><li><strong>NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL MOUNTING:</strong> Install the new networked volume control module into the wall ring/junction box. Connect the verified Cat5e/6 network cable to the rear RJ45 port and fasten the wall plate flush to the wall.</li><li><strong>AUDIO INTERACTION WIRING:</strong> Land verified speaker terminal blocks into the designated 70V/100V output channels on the rear panel of the JBL NCS amplifier. Reconnect media player input lines into the designated audio input ports.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>PHASE 4: SYSTEM PROVISIONING, AUDIO AUDIT &amp; DUAL VERIFICATION</strong></p><ol><li><strong>POWER ON &amp; IP DISCOVERY:</strong> Power <strong>ON</strong> the JBL NCS amplifier and ensure the networked volume control receives PoE/AC power. Connect your Windows/diagnostic laptop to the audio switch network.</li><li><strong>ACTIVATIONS BINDING &amp; PROVISIONING:</strong> Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Provide remote support with the MAC Address and Serial Numbers for both the JBL NCS amplifier and the networked volume controller. Allow Support to assign IP profiles and bind the networked volume control to the NCS amplifier DSP matrix.</li><li><strong>LIVE VOLUME &amp; ZONE AUDIT:</strong> Trigger test music playback. Rotate/toggle the new networked volume controller to confirm responsive, smooth audio attenuation across all store zones with zero distortion or latency.</li><li><strong>ZONE WALK TEST:</strong> Walk all audio zones with the store manager and Support to verify clear background music coverage.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong></p><ol><li><strong>DISPOSAL STAGING:</strong> Carefully box up the decommissioned G135MA amplifier, its power cable, and the old volume control plate into empty hardware packaging.</li><li><strong>LABELING &amp; PLACEMENT:</strong> Write <strong>\"DECOMMISSIONED AUDIO HARDWARE - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> clearly on the box in permanent marker. Place the box neatly out of the way in the store's designated IT/back-office storage area. <strong>Do not remove this equipment from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Dress all power and audio cabling inside the rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Clean up wire trimmings, insulation scraps, and packaging waste, leaving the volume control wall area and server room floor spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong></p><ul><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Speaker Line Readings:</strong> Clear photo displaying multimeter resistance ($\\Omega$) test readings taken on the speaker lines prior to landing wires on the new amplifier.</li><li>[ ] <strong>New JBL NCS Amp Installed &amp; Active:</strong> Close-up photo showing the replacement JBL NCS series amplifier mounted, powered on, with clean cable dressing and active status LEDs.</li><li>[ ] <strong>New Networked Volume Control Installed:</strong> Photo showing the new networked volume control module cleanly mounted and level on the wall.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Laptop Network Verification:</strong> Photo displaying your laptop screen showing JBL NCS web GUI diagnostics, active IP assignments, or controller binding confirmation.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Decommissioned G135MA Hardware:</strong> Photo showing the old G135MA amplifier and volume control boxed, clearly labeled <strong>\"STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and set aside in the IT storage area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network / Audio Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire IT/audio rack cabinet with the door OPEN</strong>, showing neat Velcro cable dressing.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept completely clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong></p><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that JBL NCS IP discovery, networked volume control binding, speaker line impedance, and audio stream telemetry are 100% operational.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback and networked volume control operation, show them the staged legacy equipment location, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update internal ticket notes detailing multimeter readings ($\\Omega$), MAC Addresses and Serial Numbers for the JBL NCS amp and networked volume control, assigned IP addresses, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n**TICKET SUMMARY:** G135MA AMPLIFIER & VOLUME CONTROL DECOMMISSIONING, NEW JBL NCS SERIES AMPLIFIER & NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT & SITE DISPOSAL STAGING\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**\n\nAn audio and network technician is required on-site to decommission a legacy **G135MA Amplifier** and analog volume control wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and install a new **JBL NCS Series Commercial Amplifier** integrated with a **Networked Volume Control** wall controller.\n\nThe technician will perform a layer-1 line diagnostics audit on all speaker trunk runs (measuring resistance $\\\\Omega$ and checking for ground faults) before connecting speaker loads to the replacement amplifier. The technician will unmount the legacy G135MA amplifier and analog volume control, install the new JBL NCS amplifier into the IT/audio rack, land a Cat5e/6 Ethernet drop to connect the new networked volume control to the local switch network, and coordinate directly with remote **Activations** to assign IP addresses, configure network controller binding, and push audio telemetry.\n\n**AMPLIFIER SAFETY & CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATE:** Always keep utility power **OFF** or isolated while terminating speaker connections. Do **NOT** power on or land speaker trunk lines on the new JBL NCS amplifier until multimeter line impedance ($\\\\Omega$) and ground-fault checks confirm the speaker runs are completely safe ($>\\\\infty\\\\Omega$ to chassis ground).\n\n**DECOMMISSIONED ASSET DISPOSAL STAGING MANDATE:** Carefully box up the decommissioned G135MA amplifier, its power cord, and the old volume control plate into empty hardware packaging. Write **\"DECOMMISSIONED AUDIO HARDWARE - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** in bold permanent marker on the box and set it aside in an out-of-the-way, designated IT storage area for local removal by site staff. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must receive explicit operational, IP binding, and audio balance confirmation from remote **Activations** and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & SUPPLIES**\n\n- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for JBL NCS amplifier web GUI access, IP discovery, network volume control binding, gateway ping sweeps, and audio portal verification)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter & RJ45 Cable Tester / Wire Toner** (**Mandatory** for measuring speaker line impedance $\\\\Omega$, short-to-ground leaks, and 8-pin Cat5e/6 network drop continuity)\n- **Small Precision Screwdriver Set** (**Mandatory** for Euroblock/Phoenix terminal block connectors on the JBL NCS amplifier and networked volume controller)\n- **Cat5e/6 & Low-Voltage Audio Supplies:** Pre-fabricated patch cords, RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, 16/2 or 18/2 speaker wire, strippers, and snips\n- **6–8ft Step Ladder** (Required for accessing wall controller wire runs or overhead speaker junction points)\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits & Mounting Hardware** (For rack mounting hardware and wall plate mounting)\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties**, Label Maker, packaging tape, and permanent marker\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPSPHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**\n\n1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/IT rack and the volume control wall location. Collect the newly shipped hardware boxes (**JBL NCS Series Amp**, **Networked Volume Control**).\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the cutover sequence, network subnet parameters, and speaker zone mapping before disconnecting active equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING & MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT**\n\n1. **G135MA DECOMMISSIONING:** Turn **OFF** utility power to the legacy G135MA amplifier. Disconnect and label all input audio feeds, volume control wires, and speaker output leads. Unmount the G135MA amplifier and remove the legacy analog volume control wall plate.\n2. **MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT:**\n\n- Set your **multimeter** to measure resistance ($\\\\Omega$) across all speaker trunk leads. Confirm expected 70V High-Z or Low-Z circuit impedance parameters.\n- Measure resistance from each speaker lead to local rack/chassis ground to verify zero ground leaks. Resolve any short circuits before landing wire on the replacement amplifier.\n\n1. **NETWORK CONTROL LINE VERIFICATION:** Connect your cable tester to the Cat5e/6 network drop servicing the volume control location. Verify 8-pin T568B continuity back to the core network switch.\n\n**PHASE 3: JBL NCS AMPLIFIER & NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION**\n\n1. **HARDWARE MOUNTING:** Securely rack-mount or shelf-position the new JBL NCS series amplifier in the IT/audio rack cabinet.\n2. **NETWORKED VOLUME CONTROL MOUNTING:** Install the new networked volume control module into the wall ring/junction box. Connect the verified Cat5e/6 network cable to the rear RJ45 port and fasten the wall plate flush to the wall.\n3. **AUDIO INTERACTION WIRING:** Land verified speaker terminal blocks into the designated 70V/100V output channels on the rear panel of the JBL NCS amplifier. Reconnect media player input lines into the designated audio input ports.\n\n**PHASE 4: SYSTEM PROVISIONING, AUDIO AUDIT & DUAL VERIFICATION**\n\n1. **POWER ON & IP DISCOVERY:** Power **ON** the JBL NCS amplifier and ensure the networked volume control receives PoE/AC power. Connect your Windows/diagnostic laptop to the audio switch network.\n2. **ACTIVATIONS BINDING & PROVISIONING:** Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Provide remote support with the MAC Address and Serial Numbers for both the JBL NCS amplifier and the networked volume controller. Allow Support to assign IP profiles and bind the networked volume control to the NCS amplifier DSP matrix.\n3. **LIVE VOLUME & ZONE AUDIT:** Trigger test music playback. Rotate/toggle the new networked volume controller to confirm responsive, smooth audio attenuation across all store zones with zero distortion or latency.\n4. **ZONE WALK TEST:** Walk all audio zones with the store manager and Support to verify clear background music coverage.\n\n**PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**\n\n1. **DISPOSAL STAGING:** Carefully box up the decommissioned G135MA amplifier, its power cable, and the old volume control plate into empty hardware packaging.\n2. **LABELING & PLACEMENT:** Write **\"DECOMMISSIONED AUDIO HARDWARE - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** clearly on the box in permanent marker. Place the box neatly out of the way in the store's designated IT/back-office storage area. **Do not remove this equipment from the property.**\n3. **CLEANUP:** Dress all power and audio cabling inside the rack using **Velcro ties**. Clean up wire trimmings, insulation scraps, and packaging waste, leaving the volume control wall area and server room floor spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**\n\n- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Speaker Line Readings:** Clear photo displaying multimeter resistance ($\\\\Omega$) test readings taken on the speaker lines prior to landing wires on the new amplifier.\n- \\[ \\] **New JBL NCS Amp Installed & Active:** Close-up photo showing the replacement JBL NCS series amplifier mounted, powered on, with clean cable dressing and active status LEDs.\n- \\[ \\] **New Networked Volume Control Installed:** Photo showing the new networked volume control module cleanly mounted and level on the wall.\n- \\[ \\] **Laptop Network Verification:** Photo displaying your laptop screen showing JBL NCS web GUI diagnostics, active IP assignments, or controller binding confirmation.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Decommissioned G135MA Hardware:** Photo showing the old G135MA amplifier and volume control boxed, clearly labeled **\"STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and set aside in the IT storage area.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network / Audio Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire IT/audio rack cabinet with the door OPEN**, showing neat Velcro cable dressing.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept completely clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**\n\n1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that JBL NCS IP discovery, networked volume control binding, speaker line impedance, and audio stream telemetry are 100% operational.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback and networked volume control operation, show them the staged legacy equipment location, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update internal ticket notes detailing multimeter readings ($\\\\Omega$), MAC Addresses and Serial Numbers for the JBL NCS amp and networked volume control, assigned IP addresses, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T08:00","end":"2026-10-05T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-05T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":250},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790778142969}
