{"job":{"id":20064465,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Interface Security Systems","title":"VIDEO / Day 1 Equipment Deinstall ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>: </strong></p><p><strong>THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 &amp; 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS &amp; EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT. </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Day 1 Saturday 10/3:</strong><u style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\"> </u><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Deinstall all cameras on sales floor except the door frame camera. Move POS wire to where the new POS will be. Put all cameras in the box and give to GC to leave in the back office near our equipment for return trip. </span></p><p><br></p><p><u>Please read this section</u></p><p>TECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END</p><p>TECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE</p><p>TECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.</p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required</u>:</strong></p><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wireless Hot Spot Device</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder, 8’ step ladder.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8” Torpedo Level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diagonal Cuters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adjustable wrench</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug</li><li>Wire Tracer/Toner</li><li>25’ Tape Measure</li><li>Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks</li><li>3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)</li><li>Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits</li><li>Smart Phone</li><li>Required Materials and Supplies:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fastener Assortment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)</li><li>Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors</li></ul><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"</u></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For iPhone:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For Android:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Console Cable or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder - 8' minimum.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Standard Networking Tool Kit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable stripper</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">7 level screw driver.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fish Tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps.</li><li>10. Sharpie or Label Maker.</li><li>11. Network cable tester.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation POCs</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION</li><li>PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Dress and look appropriate for the job.</li><li>No ripped/cut pants.</li><li>Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Non-used Parts:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 & 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS & EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT.**\n\n**Day 1 Saturday 10/3:** Deinstall all cameras on sales floor except the door frame camera. Move POS wire to where the new POS will be. Put all cameras in the box and give to GC to leave in the back office near our equipment for return trip.\n\nPlease read this section\n\nTECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END\n\nTECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE\n\nTECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"\n\n- Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)\n- Wireless Hot Spot Device\n- Ladder, 8’ step ladder.\n- Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):\n- \\#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers\n- 1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers\n- Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver\n- 8” Torpedo Level\n- Diagonal Cuters\n- Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)\n- Adjustable wrench\n- Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug\n- Wire Tracer/Toner\n- 25’ Tape Measure\n- Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks\n- 3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)\n- Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits\n- Smart Phone\n- Required Materials and Supplies:\n- CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’\n- RJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n- Fastener Assortment\n- Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)\n- Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"\n\n- Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.\n- For iPhone:\n- Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.\n- Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.\n- For Android:\n- Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.\n- Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.\n- Console Cable or Adapter.\n- Ladder - 8' minimum.\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit.\n- Network Cable stripper\n- Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.\n- 7 level screw driver.\n- Fish Tape.\n- 18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.\n- RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.\n- Tie Wraps.\n- 10. Sharpie or Label Maker.\n- 11. Network cable tester.\n\n**Escalation POCs:**\n\n- TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION\n- PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Dress and look appropriate for the job.\n- No ripped/cut pants.\n- Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.\n\n**Non-used Parts:**\n\n- **If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-03T10:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounter