{"job":{"id":20064452,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Tractor Supply - Palo Alto Ion Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>The onsite Field Service Technician will work with a remote CIS support engineer to replace two existing Palo Alto Prisma SD-WAN ION 2000 appliances with new ION 1200-S appliances at an active retail location. The technician will primarily perform physical installation, cabling, equipment identification, testing assistance, documentation, and removal/packaging of the legacy equipment. All network configuration and backend changes will be performed remotely by CIS.</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Field Technician Scope:</strong></p><ul><li>Check in with CIS&#39;s remote technical support and the onsite Manager on Duty (MOD) and confirm access to the network rack/cabinet.</li><li>Locate and verify the replacement ION 1200-S appliances, power supplies, mounting trays, cabling, and associated hardware.</li><li>Identify the existing primary and backup ION 2000 appliances and associated WAN/LAN connections.</li><li>Take clear before-work photographs of the network rack, existing equipment, cabling, and port connections.</li><li>Physically label the new primary and backup ION appliances as directed by the remote CIS engineer.</li><li>Install and secure the supplied mounting trays and new ION 1200-S appliances in the network rack/cabinet.</li><li>Connect power and required inter-device cabling to the new appliances.</li><li>Move existing cellular WAN, broadband WAN, and LAN/switch connections from the legacy appliances to the new appliances as directed by CIS.</li><li>Manually reboot the onsite cellular gateway/Inseego device and broadband modem when instructed.</li><li>Verify and/or reseat network cables when requested by the remote support team during testing.</li><li>Remain onsite and available while CIS remotely validates appliance connectivity, VPN connectivity, HA operation, and store network connectivity.</li><li>Coordinate with the MOD to validate critical store services, including POS/registers, workstation connectivity, Wi-Fi, phones, and printers.</li><li>If required, assist with physical rollback by reconnecting the original equipment and cabling under CIS direction.</li><li>Once final approval is received, remove the legacy ION 2000 appliances and associated mounting hardware.</li><li>Package the legacy appliances, power supplies, and mounting hardware using the provided return materials and shipping labels.</li><li>Perform final cable management and leave the network rack/cabinet clean and orderly.</li><li>Provide required completion photographs, including final rack condition, appliance cabling/ports, and packaged return equipment.</li><li>Provide legacy equipment serial numbers and any requested closeout information to the remote CIS support resource.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Technician Requirements:</strong></p><p>Technician should have standard network field-service tools and be comfortable identifying, mounting, labeling, connecting, disconnecting, and documenting enterprise network equipment. The technician must follow remote CIS direction and should not move production network cabling or remove legacy equipment until specifically authorized.</p><p></p><p><strong>Materials - **Please have extras of all of the below:</strong></p><ul><li>Cat5e cable (at least 200’)</li><li>QTY 8 - 12mm M6 screws</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p>Required Tools:</p><ul><li>Laptop w/Power supply</li><li>Headphones (Bluetooth or wired)</li><li>Windows 10 (Caution: do not use a laptop with Windows 7 or earlier)</li><li>With Ethernet port OR USB – Ethernet Adaptor</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>General purpose tools for mounting equipment (e.g., power drill, screwdriver etc.)</li><li>Cell Phone w/full battery and Charger (camera required)</li><li>Cellular Hotspot</li><li>Standard Measuring tools</li><li>Ladder/ Folding Ladder of at least 6’</li></ul>","markdown":"The onsite Field Service Technician will work with a remote CIS support engineer to replace two existing Palo Alto Prisma SD-WAN ION 2000 appliances with new ION 1200-S appliances at an active retail location. The technician will primarily perform physical installation, cabling, equipment identification, testing assistance, documentation, and removal/packaging of the legacy equipment. All network configuration and backend changes will be performed remotely by CIS.\n\n**Field Technician Scope:**\n\n- Check in with CIS's remote technical support and the onsite Manager on Duty (MOD) and confirm access to the network rack/cabinet.\n- Locate and verify the replacement ION 1200-S appliances, power supplies, mounting trays, cabling, and associated hardware.\n- Identify the existing primary and backup ION 2000 appliances and associated WAN/LAN connections.\n- Take clear before-work photographs of the network rack, existing equipment, cabling, and port connections.\n- Physically label the new primary and backup ION appliances as directed by the remote CIS engineer.\n- Install and secure the supplied mounting trays and new ION 1200-S appliances in the network rack/cabinet.\n- Connect power and required inter-device cabling to the new appliances.\n- Move existing cellular WAN, broadband WAN, and LAN/switch connections from the legacy appliances to the new appliances as directed by CIS.\n- Manually reboot the onsite cellular gateway/Inseego device and broadband modem when instructed.\n- Verify and/or reseat network cables when requested by the remote support team during testing.\n- Remain onsite and available while CIS remotely validates appliance connectivity, VPN connectivity, HA operation, and store network connectivity.\n- Coordinate with the MOD to validate critical store services, including POS/registers, workstation connectivity, Wi-Fi, phones, and printers.\n- If required, assist with physical rollback by reconnecting the original equipment and cabling under CIS direction.\n- Once final approval is received, remove the legacy ION 2000 appliances and associated mounting hardware.\n- Package the legacy appliances, power supplies, and mounting hardware using the provided return materials and shipping labels.\n- Perform final cable management and leave the network rack/cabinet clean and orderly.\n- Provide required completion photographs, including final rack condition, appliance cabling/ports, and packaged return equipment.\n- Provide legacy equipment serial numbers and any requested closeout information to the remote CIS support resource.\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\nTechnician should have standard network field-service tools and be comfortable identifying, mounting, labeling, connecting, disconnecting, and documenting enterprise network equipment. The technician must follow remote CIS direction and should not move production network cabling or remove legacy equipment until specifically authorized.\n\n**Materials - \\*\\*Please have extras of all of the below:**\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- QTY 8 - 12mm M6 screws\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Laptop w/Power supply\n- Headphones (Bluetooth or wired)\n- Windows 10 (Caution: do not use a laptop with Windows 7 or earlier)\n- With Ethernet port OR USB – Ethernet Adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General purpose tools for mounting equipment (e.g., power drill, screwdriver etc.)\n- Cell Phone w/full battery and Charger (camera required)\n- Cellular Hotspot\n- Standard Measuring tools\n- Ladder/ Folding Ladder of at least 6’","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T14:00","end":"2026-10-20T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790779539796}
{"job":{"id":20064464,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The InSite Group","title":"Q16427 Retail Fixture Replacement Best Buy","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">2 Person Job.  1 lead and 1 helper are REQUIRED.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">SOW: FULL INSTALL GUIDE IS ATTACHED.  PLEASE READ AND CALL IF YOU NEED TO DISCUSS.</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive on site and check in with Project Manager</li><li>Locate the pallet containing the display fixture and small box containing electronics \"staged in the stockroom\"</li><li>Locate and Unmerchandise and Remove one end cap (completely remove from sales floor) and empty 4' of the T-Gondola attached to new display will install</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(End Cap only) parts must be discarded off site when removed</li><li>Disassemble the crate and begin installing the new fixture</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Detailed assembly instructions will be provided</li><li>Under the 4' of T-Gondola that has been emptied \"locate power and route the power cable\"</li><li>Once assembled you will plug in all equipment \"clearly labeled\" and test power</li><li>There will be security devices to attach to a lift shelf and electronics to install to the security devices</li><li>Install a monitor \"all materials provided\"</li><li>Power on all displays and setup Wi-Fi connection using QR code instruction prompts from your personal phone</li><li>After display/ electronic installation is complete, you will place shelf talkers and labels on the display</li><li>Clean up all fingerprints/ dispose of all packing materials</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Timeline:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> Thursday September 17th 6:00PM - 10PM (ONLY)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"> 2 people Required</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;Work in the back until last client leaves.&nbsp;Set up and be out of store by 10 PM</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Tools required/ not supplied:</strong></p><ul><li>Utility knife</li><li>Rubber hammer/ mallet</li><li>Cleaning supplies \" non-ammonia window cleaner and microfiber cloths \"</li><li>Basic tool kit</li><li>Drill/Drill Bits</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables</strong>:</p><p>Before Install Photos</p><p>Photos of all sides of endcap</p><p>Straight on Photo of Endcap</p><p>Straight on Photo of Endcap From a Distance</p><p><br></p><p><em>Deliverables will be submitted via Weblink and Field Nation Portal</em></p><p><em>Weblink to be provided before install</em></p>","markdown":"2 Person Job. 1 lead and 1 helper are REQUIRED.\n\n**SOW: FULL INSTALL GUIDE IS ATTACHED. PLEASE READ AND CALL IF YOU NEED TO DISCUSS.**\n\n- Arrive on site and check in with Project Manager\n- Locate the pallet containing the display fixture and small box containing electronics \"staged in the stockroom\"\n- Locate and Unmerchandise and Remove one end cap (completely remove from sales floor) and empty 4' of the T-Gondola attached to new display will install\n- (End Cap only) parts must be discarded off site when removed\n- Disassemble the crate and begin installing the new fixture\n- Detailed assembly instructions will be provided\n- Under the 4' of T-Gondola that has been emptied \"locate power and route the power cable\"\n- Once assembled you will plug in all equipment \"clearly labeled\" and test power\n- There will be security devices to attach to a lift shelf and electronics to install to the security devices\n- Install a monitor \"all materials provided\"\n- Power on all displays and setup Wi-Fi connection using QR code instruction prompts from your personal phone\n- After display/ electronic installation is complete, you will place shelf talkers and labels on the display\n- Clean up all fingerprints/ dispose of all packing materials\n\n**Timeline:** Thursday September 17th 6:00PM - 10PM (ONLY)\n\n 2 people Required\n\n Work in the back until last client leaves. Set up and be out of store by 10 PM\n\n**Tools required/ not supplied:**\n\n- Utility knife\n- Rubber hammer/ mallet\n- Cleaning supplies \" non-ammonia window cleaner and microfiber cloths \"\n- Basic tool kit\n- Drill/Drill Bits\n\n**Deliverables**:\n\nBefore Install Photos\n\nPhotos of all sides of endcap\n\nStraight on Photo of Endcap\n\nStraight on Photo of Endcap From a Distance\n\n*Deliverables will be submitted via Weblink and Field Nation Portal*\n\n*Weblink to be provided before install*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T09:30","end":"2026-10-02T13:30","latestStart":"2026-10-02T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":500,"max":500},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":125,"baseAmount":500,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline 