{"job":{"id":20064673,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Troubleshoot Marketspark Equipment  Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.","description":{"html":"<p>Location is Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.</p>\n<p>MarketSpark <strong>WO-00024698</strong></p>\n<p>Zendesk Ticket Number 310732</p>\n<p>Signal Check Link</p>\n<p>https://location.marketspark.com/#d03e0d52-9a23-4fed-96bb-cbb7dc71d679</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Site Contact John An <del>***** ********</del></p>\n<p><del>********************</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Scope of Work:</p>\n<p>We have a gray box enclosure with the MarketSpark logo that contains an Inhand router and 2 Grandstream ATAs. These provide dial tone for 12 elevator lines, 2 fire lines, and 1 voice line. Currently we are noticing that the VZ sim appears to not be connecting, which is odd as the customer has a VZ cell repeater device in their location that should allow us to connect. The backup sim in the router, the 10T sim, allows us to connect at times but it constantly shows poor signal metrics.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>We are shipping a new VZ sim card to site to replace the VZ sim to see if we come online after that. Please have a laptop near you just in case. This will go in slot 1 of our router and you need a small pin to get the sim tray out. The diagram on the router shows how the sim card fits. You are leaving the 10T card in there. Please contact MKSP after validating that the equipment comes online and validate that the customer cell repeater works as intended as well. Place inbound/outbound test calls.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Prior to leaving site, call MarketSpark support at (844) 335-5153 to properly validate equipment and note key service details. Reference ticket 310732.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*** Tech will need to bring the following tools:</p>\n<p>1) Butt set w/RJ11 adaptor;</p>\n<p>2) Punch Tool;</p>\n<p>3) Tone &amp; Probe;</p>\n<p>4) Cable in case a new run is needed;</p>\n<p>5) Laptop w/AnyDesk &amp; ethernet cable in case we need to console into any device;</p>\n<p>6) Any other telecom tools.</p>","markdown":"Location is Novo-Nordisk API M1-US.\n\nMarketSpark **WO-00024698**\n\nZendesk Ticket Number 310732\n\nSignal Check Link\n\n<https://location.marketspark.com/#d03e0d52-9a23-4fed-96bb-cbb7dc71d679>\n\nSite Contact John An \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nScope of Work:\n\nWe have a gray box enclosure with the MarketSpark logo that contains an Inhand router and 2 Grandstream ATAs. These provide dial tone for 12 elevator lines, 2 fire lines, and 1 voice line. Currently we are noticing that the VZ sim appears to not be connecting, which is odd as the customer has a VZ cell repeater device in their location that should allow us to connect. The backup sim in the router, the 10T sim, allows us to connect at times but it constantly shows poor signal metrics.\n\nWe are shipping a new VZ sim card to site to replace the VZ sim to see if we come online after that. Please have a laptop near you just in case. This will go in slot 1 of our router and you need a small pin to get the sim tray out. The diagram on the router shows how the sim card fits. You are leaving the 10T card in there. Please contact MKSP after validating that the equipment comes online and validate that the customer cell repeater works as intended as well. Place inbound/outbound test calls.\n\nPrior to leaving site, call MarketSpark support at (844) 335-5153 to properly validate equipment and note key service details. Reference ticket 310732.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Tech will need to bring the following tools:\n\n1\\) Butt set w/RJ11 adaptor;\n\n2\\) Punch Tool;\n\n3\\) Tone & Probe;\n\n4\\) Cable in case a new run is needed;\n\n5\\) Laptop w/AnyDesk & ethernet cable in case we need to console into any device;\n\n6\\) Any other telecom tools.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T10:00","end":"2026-10-02T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-02T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":26},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 (countered: $225) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790780365177}
{"job":{"id":20064650,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"A+ Mobile","title":"Fayetteville, NC -- Test Fiber, Repair if possible","description":{"html":"<p>We are A+ MOBILE TECHS -- <strong>Please bring the appropriate test equipment like a Fiber Optics Continuity Tester OTDR or Fluke DSX 5000/8000 or equivalent test set to fault locate.</strong></p>\n<p><u>Client</u>: Fay Block concrete block manufacturer 130 Builders Blvd, Fayetteville, NC</p>\n<p><u>WO CONTACTS</u>:</p>\n<p>Bill Warren best contact cell 910-813-2215</p>\n<p>Find distance to fault then...</p>\n<p><strong>Temporary restore service if at all possible.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Then draw a sketch of the facility. Show me where the fiber starts at the MDF and where it stops at the IDF. Take photos of each MDF/IDF wide view and close up.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What is the distance from A to B? Snap a photo of the type of fiber cable that exists now. Is it single mode is it multi mode? What type is it OM2 50/125 ?</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Check to see if there is a conduit between the buildings and if it is reusable. Can we pull in a new fiber? or do we need to install buried conduit.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>How far is it between buildings if we need to install a new conduit.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Then give me a list of all materials i.e., a fiber splice tray/patch panel for each end the length of fiber cable required</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Take a photo of each of the switches close up and wide view . We may need to upgrade to better fiber switches. Please recommend to me what you prefer i.e. Cisco 9350 etc.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Lastly how many 8 hour days will it take one or two fiber techs. Is this a one man job or do we need two fiber techs to replace the network</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech Must bring an 8ft Ladder in case the fiber is cut above the demolished construction office area up in the ceiling.</li>\n<li>A+ MOBILE TECHS’ MANDATORY TIMESHEET IS ATTACHED, PRINT OUT AND BRING IT WITH YOU TO SIGN IN/OUT.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Scope</u></strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Test the Fiber connection between MDF to IDF.</li>\n<li>Tech to bring basic Fiber Optics Continuity Tester.</li>\n<li>restore service if possible</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Changes to SOW -- Change Orders</u>:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Any Alterations or deviations from original work request specifications involving extra labor and/or materials that generate additional charges must be submitted as a CHANGE ORDER REQUEST in writing to the A+ Mobile Techs' WO Manager, and they must then be approved by our Client and communicated back to onsite tech in writing prior to commencement of work on the change order.</p>\n<p><strong><u>A+ Mobile Techs' WO Manager</u>:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>James Williams 859-785-3771 or 513-633-1194 (after hours number)</p>\n<p><strong><u>TIMESHEETS:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>A+ Mobile Techs' TIMESHEETS ARE MANDATORY</strong>. We have attached a Timesheet for you to print out and bring with you to sign in/out upon every arrival and departure to/from the site. We do not use or accept the Field Nation e-timesheets.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Time to Complete Estimation</u>:&nbsp;&lt;2 to 4 hours. We have agreed to pay the tech a 4 hour minimum plus travel</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>ONSITE WORK PROCEDURE PUNCH LIST:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on site and meet Onsite Client Contacts (POCs - see below for a list of onsite POCs)</li>\n<li><strong>GET TIMESHEET SIGNED (sign-in)</strong></li>\n<li>Tech to get situated get shown around the site</li>\n<li><strong><em>Please complete the SOW as instructed above.</em></strong></li>\n<li>Clean up work areas as necessary&nbsp;-&nbsp;DO NOT LEAVE TRASH LAYING AROUND</li>\n<li>Perform walk-thru with Onsite Client Contact&nbsp;to demonstrate work performed and that all is functional</li>\n<li>Document installation photos&nbsp;--&nbsp;<strong>UPLOAD PHOTOS TO WO before GETTING TIMESHEET SIGNED AND DEPARTING SITE</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Upload close-out notes and&nbsp;<em>parts &amp; materials (inventory)</em>&nbsp;used to WO before DEPARTING SITE. Once this portion is complete, then:</strong></li>\n<li><strong>GET TIMESHEET SIGNED (sign-out)&nbsp;by Onsite Client Contact - (Mandatory)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Take a legible photo of the signed Timesheet and upload it to WO before DEPARTING SITE - (Mandatory)</strong></li>\n<li>Check-out/depart the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>We pay for Materials as per the Materials Rates Field Nation.pdf List attached to this work order</strong></p>","markdown":"We are A+ MOBILE TECHS -- **Please bring the appropriate test equipment like a Fiber Optics Continuity Tester OTDR or Fluke DSX 5000/8000 or equivalent test set to fault locate.**\n\nClient: Fay Block concrete block manufacturer 130 Builders Blvd, Fayetteville, NC\n\nWO CONTACTS:\n\nBill Warren best contact cell 910-813-2215\n\nFind distance to fault then...\n\n**Temporary restore service if at all possible.**\n\n**Then draw a sketch of the facility. Show me where the fiber starts at the MDF and where it stops at the IDF. Take photos of each MDF/IDF wide view and close up.**\n\n**What is the distance from A to B? Snap a photo of the type of fiber cable that exists now. Is it single mode is it multi mode? What type is it OM2 50/125 ?**\n\n**Check to see if there is a conduit between the buildings and if it is reusable. Can we pull in a new fiber? or do we need to install buried conduit.**\n\n**How far is it between buildings if we need to install a new conduit.**\n\n**Then give me a list of all materials i.e., a fiber splice tray/patch panel for each end the length of fiber cable required**\n\n**Take a photo of each of the switches close up and wide view . We may need to upgrade to better fiber switches. Please recommend to me what you prefer i.e. Cisco 9350 etc.**\n\n**Lastly how many 8 hour days will it take one or two fiber techs. Is this a one man job or do we need two fiber techs to replace the network**\n\n- Tech Must bring an 8ft Ladder in case the fiber is cut above the demolished construction office area up in the ceiling.\n- A+ MOBILE TECHS’ MANDATORY TIMESHEET IS ATTACHED, PRINT OUT AND BRING IT WITH YOU TO SIGN IN/OUT.\n\n**Scope**:\n\n- Test the Fiber connection between MDF to IDF.\n- Tech to bring basic Fiber Optics Continuity Tester.\n- restore service if possible\n\n**Changes to SOW -- Change Orders:**\n\nAny Alterations or deviations from original work request specifications involving extra labor and/or materials that generate additional charges must be submitted as a CHANGE ORDER REQUEST in writing to the A+ Mobile Techs' WO Manager, and they must then be approved by our Client and communicated back to onsite tech in writing prior to commencement of work on the change order.\n\n**A+ Mobile Techs' WO Manager:**\n\nJames Williams 859-785-3771 or 513-633-1194 (after hours number)\n\n**TIMESHEETS:**\n\n**A+ Mobile Techs' TIMESHEETS ARE MANDATORY**. We have attached a Timesheet for you to print out and bring with you to sign in/out upon every arrival and departure to/from the site. We do not use or accept the Field Nation e-timesheets.\n\n**Time to Complete Estimation: <2 to 4 hours. We have agreed to pay the tech a 4 hour minimum plus travel**\n\n**ONSITE WORK PROCEDURE PUNCH LIST:**\n\n- Arrive on site and meet Onsite Client Contacts (POCs - see below for a list of onsite POCs)\n- **GET TIMESHEET SIGNED (sign-in)**\n- Tech to get situated get shown around the site\n- ***Please complete the SOW as instructed above.***\n- Clean up work areas as necessary - DO NOT LEAVE TRASH LAYING AROUND\n- Perform walk-thru with Onsite Client Contact to demonstrate work performed and that all is functional\n- Document installation photos -- **UPLOAD PHOTOS TO WO before GETTING TIMESHEET SIGNED AND DEPARTING SITE**\n- **Upload close-out notes and *parts & materials (inventory)* used to WO before DEPARTING SITE. Once this portion is complete, then:**\n- **GET TIMESHEET SIGNED (sign-out) by Onsite Client Contact - (Mandatory)**\n- **Take a legible photo of the signed Timesheet and upload it to WO before DEPARTING SITE - (Mandatory)**\n- Check-out/depart the site.\n\n**We pay for Materials as per the Materials Rates Field Nation.pdf List attached to this work order**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T17:30","end":"2026-10-01T21:30"},"payRange":{"min":135,"max":540},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":135,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":56},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":135,"baseAmount":540,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z