{"job":{"id":20054420,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Encore Technologies","title":"Macy's - Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary *MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT*","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK OVERVIEW: </strong>Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary *MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT*&nbsp;</p><p>TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS: Background check and Drugscreen</p><p>EXPECTED AMOUNT OF TIME ONSITE: 1 hour</p><p>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Tech must obtain packing materials, box that is 20x20x20 and bubble wrap.  Packing materials will be reimbursed up to $20.  If over $20 will need to call into dispatch <del>************</del> for authorization</p><p>TOOLS NEEDED:</p><p>FULL DETAILS:</p><ul><li>WORK HAS TO BE COMPLETED PRIOR TO STORE OPENING AS THIS IS INVASIVE WORK THAT WILL CAUSE AN OUTAGE OF UP TO 30 MINTUES.</li><li>Technician will meet with Store Loal Contact and be provided to the POS or MDF room.</li><li>Technician must join Bridge that is provided for this work upon arrival at site to work with Verizon Network Engineer</li><li>Locate Primary and Secondary versa boxes (These will be either Lanner or Advantec)</li><li>Confirm with Verizon Network Engineer that correct boxes have been found.</li><li>Once Verizon Network Engineer gives the direction on the bridge technician will unplug the MPLS circuit from the Primary Versa.</li><li>Technician will then move the broadband/dedicated internet circuit from the Secondary Versa to now vacant Primary Versa slot.</li><li>After the circuit move is complete and confirmed functioning correctly, trace the removed MPLS circuit to the Verizon beas box.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verizon beas box is normally an Overture 1400</li><li>Technician will ensure no other circuit is connected to this device.</li><li>When confirmed no additional circuits connected proceed with removing device</li><li>Device will be packed for shipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Technician MUST take pictures of device wrapped in bubble wrap and placed in the shipping box.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Pictures must be attached to assignment for payment approval</strong></li><li>Once packed appropriately and pictures taken technician will provide box to store management to ship back to Verizon</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technician must get sign off on the assignment from the member of store management that equipment to be shipped back has been provided to</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**WORK OVERVIEW:** Move Dedicated Internet Circuit from Secondary to Primary \\*MUST JOIN BRIDGE PRIOR TO TOUCHING EQUIPMENT\\*\n\nTECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS: Background check and Drugscreen\n\nEXPECTED AMOUNT OF TIME ONSITE: 1 hour\n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Tech must obtain packing materials, box that is 20x20x20 and bubble wrap. Packing materials will be reimbursed up to $20. If over $20 will need to call into dispatch \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for authorization\n\nTOOLS NEEDED:\n\nFULL DETAILS:\n\n- WORK HAS TO BE COMPLETED PRIOR TO STORE OPENING AS THIS IS INVASIVE WORK THAT WILL CAUSE AN OUTAGE OF UP TO 30 MINTUES.\n- Technician will meet with Store Loal Contact and be provided to the POS or MDF room.\n- Technician must join Bridge that is provided for this work upon arrival at site to work with Verizon Network Engineer\n- Locate Primary and Secondary versa boxes (These will be either Lanner or Advantec)\n- Confirm with Verizon Network Engineer that correct boxes have been found.\n- Once Verizon Network Engineer gives the direction on the bridge technician will unplug the MPLS circuit from the Primary Versa.\n- Technician will then move the broadband/dedicated internet circuit from the Secondary Versa to now vacant Primary Versa slot.\n- After the circuit move is complete and confirmed functioning correctly, trace the removed MPLS circuit to the Verizon beas box.\n- Verizon beas box is normally an Overture 1400\n- Technician will ensure no other circuit is connected to this device.\n- When confirmed no additional circuits connected proceed with removing device\n- Device will be packed for shipment\n- Technician MUST take pictures of device wrapped in bubble wrap and placed in the shipping box.\n- **Pictures must be attached to assignment for payment approval**\n- Once packed appropriately and pictures taken technician will provide box to store management to ship back to Verizon\n- **Technician must get sign off on the assignment from the member of store management that equipment to be shipped back has been provided to**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":50},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790782511991}
{"job":{"id":20065216,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"WiLine Networks","title":"DECOMM Helper","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience with outdoor wireless antenna, cabling and networking.</li><li><strong>Please send us your SHIP TO address in the Field Nation Messages section once assigned.&nbsp;We will be shipping parts to you for the installation.</strong></li><li><strong>PURPOSE OF VISIT - Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools required:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">6’ ladder required</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">hand tools including wrenches and sockets and cable cutters</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">drill motor with bits</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">rope and bucket to lower equipment off the roof</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">PPE required</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Tech must follow scope of work and not deviate.</li><li>Tech must arrive on time.</li><li>Tech is not to discuss which Carriers we use or Speed Test results we use with the customer!!!</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">We are providing WILINE DIA Service</span></li><li>Tech is not to leave site until ALL pictures are available for Project Manager to view.</li><li>Requested photos must be uploaded during the visit. Photos uploaded after the visit will not be approved.</li><li>Photos must be labeled.</li><li>Failure to check-In and check-out may result in penalties.</li><li><strong>STRICLY REQUIRED: Business casual pants, no shorts (slack or kaki), collar shirt no pictures or writing on it, and no flip flops or sandals.</strong></li><li>Represent yourself as a WiLine Engineer.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">TECHNICIAN IS REQUIRED TO TAKE SAFETY CLASS AND RETURN THE COMPLETED CERTIFICATION PRIOR TO GOING TO SITE OR THEY WILL NOT BE ALLOWED INSIDE THE BUILDING.&nbsp;SEE ATTACHED DOCUMENTATION.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>** ****** * ****** *** ************* * *** ***** ********** *** ******** ****** ** *****</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Service Type: Service Call</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Shipping parts?&nbsp;Y/N: No – Tech will be returning parts</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Working with NPE Y/N:&nbsp;No</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Target Tech Onsite Date:&nbsp;10/2</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Target Tech Onsite Time:&nbsp;12:00 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Times are flexible. Y/N:&nbsp;No</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>********* **** ******** *********************** *******</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>********* ***** ******** *******************************</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>********* ***** ******** *******************</del></span><del>****************************</del></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Contact Name:&nbsp;&nbsp;TBD</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Contact Phone number:&nbsp;TBD</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>**** ***************** ***** ********** *** ******** ****** ** *****</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>************ ***** ******</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Access Hours:&nbsp;8:00 AM to 3:00 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Requested tech name and Field Nation ID:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">CSR or RT#:&nbsp;<del>******</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Estimate labor hours: 2</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">MAX labor hours:&nbsp;2</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">PURPOSE OF SERVICE CALL/SCOPE OF WORK: Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Scope/Onsite Description:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS PLEASE READ:&nbsp;DO NOT REMOVE THE GROMMETS FROM THE RADIOS CUT THE CABLES BELOW THE GROMMET, THIS REDUCES DAMAGE TO THE RADIO WHEN RETURNING TO US.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact LPOC and let them know you are onsite, also check out with them</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact <del>**** ******* ** ************</del> when arriving onsite</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Decomm all equipment</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">First remove CPE with power supply and 4 POEs and Fiber handoff with fiber cable</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Take pictures before and after removing and upload to the ticket</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Take pictures of antennas before and after removing with cables cut at the bottom of the antennas</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Remove Inseego antennas, when removing antenna</span><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">, </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">do not remove grommet covering the cable as this</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">damages the antenna, cut the cable below the grommet only.&nbsp;Take pictures of the antenna showing the cut cable and upload to the ticket.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Remove or cut external wiring</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Return equipment to us with label to be provided</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Work order is not complete until equipment has been dropped off at UPS location</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact Suzy for equipment to be shipped back to us</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Upload all pictures to ticket when complete</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact <del>**** ************</del> prior to leaving site</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">SAFETY TRAINING REQUIRED</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ADDITITONAL HOURS and ESCALATION PROCESS:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Additional hours past MAX hours MUST get Project Manager approval.&nbsp;&nbsp;Labor overage past MAX hours that are not pre-approved, will not be paid.</strong></li><li>If the Project Manager is not reachable, contact the WiLine support team at&nbsp;908-651-9350&nbsp;or WilIne@patstaffing.com.</li><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with the Project Coordinator. Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;Project Coordinator or WiLine support team.</li><li><strong>Additional Travel &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong> Travel expense (over 50 miles) must be pre-approved via counteroffer during your request</li></ul><p><strong><u>Lift Penalty</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Any additional charges incurred, such as extra lift rentals fees due to changes in the technician’s schedule, will be the responsibility of the technician. These additional fees will be charged back accordingly.</p><p><strong><u>Parts Plan</u>:&nbsp;</strong>In the event a technician is in possession of installation or return parts, payment will not be approved/issued until a receipt of proof of return is provided. In most cases, return parts will be boxed and left at the site. A shipping label will be provided. Take photo of boxed part in the area left, and upload it to the work order.</p><p><strong><u>Professionalism</u></strong>: We adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations &amp; timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations.</p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience with outdoor wireless antenna, cabling and networking.\n- **Please send us your SHIP TO address in the Field Nation Messages section once assigned. We will be shipping parts to you for the installation.**\n- **PURPOSE OF VISIT - Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back**\n\n**Tools required:**\n\n- 6’ ladder required\n- hand tools including wrenches and sockets and cable cutters\n- drill motor with bits\n- rope and bucket to lower equipment off the roof\n- PPE required\n\n**Special Instructions:**\n\n- Tech must follow scope of work and not deviate.\n- Tech must arrive on time.\n- Tech is not to discuss which Carriers we use or Speed Test results we use with the customer!!!\n- We are providing WILINE DIA Service\n- Tech is not to leave site until ALL pictures are available for Project Manager to view.\n- Requested photos must be uploaded during the visit. Photos uploaded after the visit will not be approved.\n- Photos must be labeled.\n- Failure to check-In and check-out may result in penalties.\n- **STRICLY REQUIRED: Business casual pants, no shorts (slack or kaki), collar shirt no pictures or writing on it, and no flip flops or sandals.**\n- Represent yourself as a WiLine Engineer.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables**\n\n**TECHNICIAN IS REQUIRED TO TAKE SAFETY CLASS AND RETURN THE COMPLETED CERTIFICATION PRIOR TO GOING TO SITE OR THEY WILL NOT BE ALLOWED INSIDE THE BUILDING. SEE ATTACHED DOCUMENTATION.**\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nService Type: Service Call\n\nShipping parts? Y/N: No – Tech will be returning parts\n\nWorking with NPE Y/N: No\n\nTarget Tech Onsite Date: 10/2\n\nTarget Tech Onsite Time: 12:00 PM\n\nTimes are flexible. Y/N: No\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nSite Contact Name: TBD\n\nSite Contact Phone number: TBD\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nSite Access Hours: 8:00 AM to 3:00 PM\n\nRequested tech name and Field Nation ID:\n\nCSR or RT#: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nEstimate labor hours: 2\n\nMAX labor hours: 2\n\nPURPOSE OF SERVICE CALL/SCOPE OF WORK: Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back\n\nScope/Onsite Description:\n\n**SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS PLEASE READ: DO NOT REMOVE THE GROMMETS FROM THE RADIOS CUT THE CABLES BELOW THE GROMMET, THIS REDUCES DAMAGE TO THE RADIO WHEN RETURNING TO US.**\n\nContact LPOC and let them know you are onsite, also check out with them\n\nContact \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when arriving onsite\n\nDecomm all equipment\n\nFirst remove CPE with power supply and 4 POEs and Fiber handoff with fiber cable\n\nTake pictures before and after removing and upload to the ticket\n\nTake pictures of antennas before and after removing with cables cut at the bottom of the antennas\n\nRemove Inseego antennas, when removing antenna, **do not remove grommet covering the cable as this** **damages the antenna, cut the cable below the grommet only. Take pictures of the antenna showing the cut cable and upload to the ticket.**\n\nRemove or cut external wiring\n\nReturn equipment to us with label to be provided\n\nWork order is not complete until equipment has been dropped off at UPS location\n\nContact Suzy for equipment to be shipped back to us\n\nUpload all pictures to ticket when complete\n\nContact \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* prior to leaving site\n\nSAFETY TRAINING REQUIRED\n\n**ADDITITONAL HOURS and ESCALATION PROCESS:**\n\n- **Additional hours past MAX hours MUST get Project Manager approval. Labor overage past MAX hours that are not pre-approved, will not be paid.**\n- If the Project Manager is not reachable, contact the WiLine support team at 908-651-9350 or WilIne@patstaffing.com.\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with the Project Coordinator. Any issues or questions should be escalated to Project Coordinator or WiLine support team.\n- **Additional Travel & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** Travel expense (over 50 miles) must be pre-approved via counteroffer during your request\n\n**Lift Penalty:** Any additional charges incurred, such as extra lift rentals fees due to changes in the technician’s schedule, will be the responsibility of the technician. These additional fees will be charged back accordingly.\n\n**Parts Plan:** In the event a technician is in possession of installation or return parts, payment will not be approved/issued until a receipt of proof of return is provided. In most cases, return parts will be boxed and left at the site. A shipping label will be provided. Take photo of boxed part in the area left, and upload it to the work order.\n\n**Professionalism**: We adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations & timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T12:00","end":"2026-10-02T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"