{"job":{"id":20055009,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Bijora Inc","title":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)","description":{"html":"<p>Job Overview</p>\n<p>AKIRA is seeking an experienced <strong>Network Cable Technician to serve as the a low voltage technician (Tech 2)</strong> for a<strong>20,000 sq ft retail store build</strong> at Crabtree Valley Mall.</p>\n<p>The Technician will be responsible for <strong>running CAT6 cabling</strong></p>\n<p>Primary work will include structured cabling installation and mounting network/security equipment throughout the store.</p>\n<p>The <strong>AKIRA IT Project Manager, Hugo, will be onsite managing the project and coordinating all work with the technicians.</strong></p>\n<p>The low voltage technician must be comfortable <strong>working with other technicians, maintaining organization, and ensuring installation standards are followed.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Project Infrastructure</p>\n<p>The store deployment includes:</p>\n<p>• <strong>26 Security Cameras</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>2 to 4 People Counters</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>4 Wireless Access Points</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong></p>\n<p>Scope of work may change during installation depending on layout adjustments or coverage needs. <strong>Technicians must be flexible and able to adapt to project needs.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Scope of Work</p>\n<p>The low voltage technician will primarily be responsible for:</p>\n<p>• <strong>Mounting and installing security cameras</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>Mounting wireless access points</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>Installing people counter devices</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>Assisting with network rack installation and uplink cabling</strong></p>\n<p>• <strong>Coordinating cable runs with additional technicians onsite</strong></p>\n<p>Work Hours Requirement</p>\n<p>• <strong>All technicians must be onsite and ready to begin work at 7:30 AM each day. (First day start at 12:30PM)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Professional Expectations</p>\n<p>Technicians are expected to maintain <strong>clean and professional installations</strong> at all times.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Organization</p>\n<p>• Proper cable routing and cable management</p>\n<p>• Clean and organized installation areas</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Cleanup</p>\n<p>Technicians <strong>must clean up after themselves each day</strong>, including:</p>\n<p>• Removing scrap cable</p>\n<p>• Cleaning installation debris</p>\n<p>• Organizing materials and work areas</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Installation Standards</p>\n<p>• All cable runs must be <strong>clean, organized, and professionally installed</strong></p>\n<p>• Sloppy cable management will not be accepted</p>\n<p>• Technicians who fail to maintain installation standards may be removed from the project</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Job Completion Requirement</p>\n<p>This is a <strong>completion-based project</strong>.</p>\n<p>Technicians are expected to:</p>\n<p>• Work efficiently with the installation team</p>\n<p>• Assist where needed to keep the project moving forward</p>\n<p>• Remain onsite until assigned installation work is completed</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Required Experience</p>\n<p>• Experience running <strong>CAT5e / CAT6 in commercial environments</strong></p>\n<p>• Experience mounting <strong>cameras and wireless access points</strong></p>\n<p>• Experience working in <strong>large retail or open environments preferred</strong></p>\n<p>• Comfortable working with ladders or lifts</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Provided Materials</p>\n<p>AKIRA will provide all installation materials required for the project, including:</p>\n<p>• CAT6 cabling</p>\n<p>• Security cameras</p>\n<p>• Wireless access points</p>\n<p>• People counter devices</p>\n<p>• Network switches</p>\n<p>• Mounting hardware and additional installation materials</p>\n<p>Technicians are <strong>only required to bring their own tools</strong> necessary to complete the installation.</p>\n<p>Standard low-voltage tools such as termination tools, testers, and hand tools are expected.</p>","markdown":"Job Overview\n\nAKIRA is seeking an experienced **Network Cable Technician to serve as the a low voltage technician (Tech 2)** for a**20,000 sq ft retail store build** at Crabtree Valley Mall.\n\nThe Technician will be responsible for **running CAT6 cabling**\n\nPrimary work will include structured cabling installation and mounting network/security equipment throughout the store.\n\nThe **AKIRA IT Project Manager, Hugo, will be onsite managing the project and coordinating all work with the technicians.**\n\nThe low voltage technician must be comfortable **working with other technicians, maintaining organization, and ensuring installation standards are followed.**\n\nProject Infrastructure\n\nThe store deployment includes:\n\n• **26 Security Cameras**\n\n• **2 to 4 People Counters**\n\n• **4 Wireless Access Points**\n\n**Note:**\n\nScope of work may change during installation depending on layout adjustments or coverage needs. **Technicians must be flexible and able to adapt to project needs.**\n\nScope of Work\n\nThe low voltage technician will primarily be responsible for:\n\n• **Mounting and installing security cameras**\n\n• **Mounting wireless access points**\n\n• **Installing people counter devices**\n\n• **Assisting with network rack installation and uplink cabling**\n\n• **Coordinating cable runs with additional technicians onsite**\n\nWork Hours Requirement\n\n• **All technicians must be onsite and ready to begin work at 7:30 AM each day. (First day start at 12:30PM)**\n\nProfessional Expectations\n\nTechnicians are expected to maintain **clean and professional installations** at all times.\n\nOrganization\n\n• Proper cable routing and cable management\n\n• Clean and organized installation areas\n\nCleanup\n\nTechnicians **must clean up after themselves each day**, including:\n\n• Removing scrap cable\n\n• Cleaning installation debris\n\n• Organizing materials and work areas\n\nInstallation Standards\n\n• All cable runs must be **clean, organized, and professionally installed**\n\n• Sloppy cable management will not be accepted\n\n• Technicians who fail to maintain installation standards may be removed from the project\n\nJob Completion Requirement\n\nThis is a **completion-based project**.\n\nTechnicians are expected to:\n\n• Work efficiently with the installation team\n\n• Assist where needed to keep the project moving forward\n\n• Remain onsite until assigned installation work is completed\n\nRequired Experience\n\n• Experience running **CAT5e / CAT6 in commercial environments**\n\n• Experience mounting **cameras and wireless access points**\n\n• Experience working in **large retail or open environments preferred**\n\n• Comfortable working with ladders or lifts\n\nProvided Materials\n\nAKIRA will provide all installation materials required for the project, including:\n\n• CAT6 cabling\n\n• Security cameras\n\n• Wireless access points\n\n• People counter devices\n\n• Network switches\n\n• Mounting hardware and additional installation materials\n\nTechnicians are **only required to bring their own tools** necessary to complete the installation.\n\nStandard low-voltage tools such as termination tools, testers, and hand tools are expected.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T12:30","end":"2026-10-05T36:30"},"payRange":{"min":1400,"max":1400},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":24,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 5, 12:30 PM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 5, Tue, Oct 6, Wed, Oct 7, Thu, Oct 8, Fri, Oct 9 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790783316128}
{"job":{"id":20065267,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Interface Security Systems","title":"VIDEO / Day 1 Equipment Deinstall","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 &amp; 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS &amp; EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Day 1 Saturday 10/3:</strong><u style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\"> </u><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Deinstall all cameras on sales floor except the door frame camera. Move POS wire to where the new POS will be. Put all cameras in the box and give to GC to leave in the back office near our equipment for return trip.</span></p><p><br></p><p><u>Please read this section</u></p><p>TECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END</p><p>TECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE</p><p>TECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.</p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required</u>:</strong></p><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wireless Hot Spot Device</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder, 8’ step ladder.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8” Torpedo Level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diagonal Cuters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adjustable wrench</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug</li><li>Wire Tracer/Toner</li><li>25’ Tape Measure</li><li>Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks</li><li>3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)</li><li>Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits</li><li>Smart Phone</li><li>Required Materials and Supplies:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fastener Assortment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)</li><li>Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors</li></ul><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"</u></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For iPhone:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For Android:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Console Cable or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder - 8' minimum.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Standard Networking Tool Kit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable stripper</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">7 level screw driver.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fish Tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps.</li><li>10. Sharpie or Label Maker.</li><li>11. Network cable tester.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation POCs</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION</li><li>PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Dress and look appropriate for the job.</li><li>No ripped/cut pants.</li><li>Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Non-used Parts:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 & 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS & EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT.**\n\n**Day 1 Saturday 10/3:** Deinstall all cameras on sales floor except the door frame camera. Move POS wire to where the new POS will be. Put all cameras in the box and give to GC to leave in the back office near our equipment for return trip.\n\nPlease read this section\n\nTECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END\n\nTECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE\n\nTECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"\n\n- Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)\n- Wireless Hot Spot Device\n- Ladder, 8’ step ladder.\n- Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):\n- \\#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers\n- 1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers\n- Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver\n- 8” Torpedo Level\n- Diagonal Cuters\n- Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)\n- Adjustable wrench\n- Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug\n- Wire Tracer/Toner\n- 25’ Tape Measure\n- Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks\n- 3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)\n- Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits\n- Smart Phone\n- Required Materials and Supplies:\n- CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’\n- RJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n- Fastener Assortment\n- Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)\n- Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"\n\n- Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.\n- For iPhone:\n- Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.\n- Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.\n- For Android:\n- Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.\n- Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.\n- Console Cable or Adapter.\n- Ladder - 8' minimum.\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit.\n- Network Cable stripper\n- Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.\n- 7 level screw driver.\n- Fish Tape.\n- 18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.\n- RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.\n- Tie Wraps.\n- 10. Sharpie or Label Maker.\n- 11. Network cable tester.\n\n**Escalation POCs:**\n\n- TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION\n- PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Dress and look appropriate for the job.\n- No ripped/cut pants.\n- Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.\n\n**Non-used Parts:**\n\n- **If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-03T10:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":100,"baseAmount":300,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":70,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T17:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790783348514}
{"job":{"id":20065269,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Interface Security Systems","title":"VIDEO / Day 2 Camera Reinstall","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 &amp; 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS &amp; EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT.</strong></p><p>Upon arrival at the site—but before entering the location—initiate the check-in process by texting “Start” to 314-208-2475. SIS TTU</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Day 2 10/13:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\"> Return and reinstall all sales floor cameras with the POS camera in its new spot. The view needs to be of the POS from the side and also picking up the front door in the background. Work with TTU to test the alarm system and video for VV.</span></p><p><strong><u>BOM:</u></strong></p><p>(1) DP-DC2710 - UNIVERSAL CRIMP-ON SET BNC CONN TRUE 75 OHMS 10/PK</p><p>(500FT) WIRE-RG59SIAMPL5CW - RG59/182STR-UPL PLENUM SIAMESE WHITE - 500' BOX</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">(1) 0E-DCMPIG10P - MALE BARREL CONNECTOR WITH 3' PIGTAI</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">L</strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>Please read this section</u></p><p>TECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END</p><p>TECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE</p><p>TECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.</p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required</u>:</strong></p><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wireless Hot Spot Device</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder, 8’ step ladder.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8” Torpedo Level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diagonal Cuters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adjustable wrench</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug</li><li>Wire Tracer/Toner</li><li>25’ Tape Measure</li><li>Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks</li><li>3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)</li><li>Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits</li><li>Smart Phone</li><li>Required Materials and Supplies:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fastener Assortment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)</li><li>Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors</li></ul><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"</u></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For iPhone:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For Android:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Console Cable or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder - 8' minimum.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Standard Networking Tool Kit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable stripper</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">7 level screw driver.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fish Tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps.</li><li>10. Sharpie or Label Maker.</li><li>11. Network cable tester.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation POCs</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION</li><li>PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Dress and look appropriate for the job.</li><li>No ripped/cut pants.</li><li>Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Non-used Parts:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**THIS IS A 2 DAY WO. PLEASE ACCEPT BOTH DAY 1 & 2. PARTS WILL SHIP TO TECH FOR DAY 2. PLEASE PROVIDE SHIPPING ADDRESS & EMAIL UPON ASSIGNMENT.**\n\nUpon arrival at the site—but before entering the location—initiate the check-in process by texting “Start” to 314-208-2475. SIS TTU\n\n**Day 2 10/13:** Return and reinstall all sales floor cameras with the POS camera in its new spot. The view needs to be of the POS from the side and also picking up the front door in the background. Work with TTU to test the alarm system and video for VV.\n\n**BOM:**\n\n(1) DP-DC2710 - UNIVERSAL CRIMP-ON SET BNC CONN TRUE 75 OHMS 10/PK\n\n(500FT) WIRE-RG59SIAMPL5CW - RG59/182STR-UPL PLENUM SIAMESE WHITE - 500' BOX\n\n(1) 0E-DCMPIG10P - MALE BARREL CONNECTOR WITH 3' PIGTAI**L**\n\nPlease read this section\n\nTECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END\n\nTECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE\n\nTECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"\n\n- Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)\n- Wireless Hot Spot Device\n- Ladder, 8’ step ladder.\n- Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):\n- \\#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers\n- 1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers\n- Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver\n- 8” Torpedo Level\n- Diagonal Cuters\n- Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)\n- Adjustable wrench\n- Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug\n- Wire Tracer/Toner\n- 25’ Tape Measure\n- Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks\n- 3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)\n- Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits\n- Smart Phone\n- Required Materials and Supplies:\n- CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’\n- RJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n- Fastener Assortment\n- Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)\n- Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"\n\n- Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.\n- For iPhone:\n- Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.\n- Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.\n- For Android:\n- Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.\n- Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.\n- Console Cable or Adapter.\n- Ladder - 8' minimum.\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit.\n- Network Cable stripper\n- Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.\n- 7 level screw driver.\n- Fish Tape.\n- 18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.\n- RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.\n- Tie Wraps.\n- 10. Sharpie or Label Maker.\n- 11. Network cable tester.\n\n**Escalation POCs:**\n\n- TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION\n- PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Dress and look appropriate for the job.\n- No ripped/cut pants.\n- Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.\n\n**Non-used Parts:**\n\n- **If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T10:00","end":"2026-10-13T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":400,"max":400},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $400 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790783355182}
{"job":{"id":20065671,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Connect Broadband Circuit to Router","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME&nbsp;</strong><strong>(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>Please bring assorted patch cables up to and including 30 ft in length - preferably CAT6 but at least CAT5</strong></p><p><strong>Connect Broadband Circuit to Cradlepoint</strong></p><p>Service</p><p>Bandwidth|Link 500M/20M Broadband Internet (Spectrum)</p><p>Circuit ID</p><p>8349120112627053</p><p>Access Provider Circuit ID</p><p><br></p><p>Carrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address</p><p>Wireless MAC: 0833edd9f9c3</p><p>Wireless Make: Askey</p><p>Wireless Model: sax1v1k</p><p>| Data Mac: 94f7be4474c0</p><p>Data Make: Sercomm</p><p>Data Model: ES2251</p><p>DeMarc Location</p><p><br></p><p>Hand Off Type</p><p>Copper/Electrical/RJ45</p><p>Network Information <strong style=\"color: white;\">Public</strong></p><p>IP Address Block: 96.10.213.40/29</p><p>Gateway: 96.10.213.41</p><p>Usable IP Range: 96.10.213.42 - 96.10.213.46</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Document existing/legacy modem and take pictures.&nbsp;Trace the Cradlepoint WAN port and determine what's providing internet today.&nbsp;Take a picture of both the device and the MAC address sticker and upload them to FN platform.&nbsp;(OR NOTE NO LEGACY CKT)</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:</strong></p><p><strong>You have a hard start at 8 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the restaurant, ETC please do.</strong></p><p><strong>Perform the scope of work below exactly as it is written. The purpose of the scope of work is to connect the newly installed circuit listed above to the customer’s cradlepoint router. Do not interact with any other devices on site.</strong></p><p><strong>You must bring the following items to qualify for this work order:</strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Toner and wand</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Laptop with Ethernet port</strong></p><p><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ladder</strong></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when en route to site for ETA.</li><li>Upon arrival, check in with Dispatch via phone at 385-533-9167 &amp; obtain Check In Code</li><li>Touch base with the onsite contact - <strong>&lt;</strong>Wendy White 469-663-4979<strong>&gt;</strong></li><li>Take “before” pictures of the network cabinet in the manager’s office.</li><li>Locate the circuit listed above. Connect your laptop and confirm you can browse the internet from the circuit.</li><li>Perform a speed test and screenshot the result.</li><li>Test the IP’s and screenshot the result.</li><li>Locate the cradlepoint above the doorway in the manager’s office. Tone out to find the cable going from the WAN port on the cradlepoint to the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk (across the room). Find the other end of the cable</li><li>If the other end of the cable is plugged into anything, <strong>stop</strong> and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and <strong>await further instructions</strong></li><li>If the other end of the cable is <strong>not</strong> plugged into anything, plug it into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Use the MAC ID listed at the top of this work order to confirm you are plugging into the correct device. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint, check above the dropped ceiling tile to see if there is a cable coiled above the ceiling. Plug 1 end into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and safely route the other end over the ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. P the other end into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and no cable coiled above the dropped ceiling tile that you can find, run a new cable safely above the dropped ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. Plug it into the new modem and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 to notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you cannot find a way to safely run a new cable, complete a site survey for the labor and materials to return and safely run the new cable.</li><li>Check if WIFI light is lit on the broadband modem and let dispatch coordinator know at 385-533-9167 if so.</li><li>Complete cable management.</li><li>Take “after” pictures of the IT cabinet in the manager’s office.</li><li>Check out with dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and get checkout code.</li></ol>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME** **(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**Please bring assorted patch cables up to and including 30 ft in length - preferably CAT6 but at least CAT5**\n\n**Connect Broadband Circuit to Cradlepoint**\n\nService\n\nBandwidth|Link 500M/20M Broadband Internet (Spectrum)\n\nCircuit ID\n\n8349120112627053\n\nAccess Provider Circuit ID\n\nCarrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address\n\nWireless MAC: 0833edd9f9c3\n\nWireless Make: Askey\n\nWireless Model: sax1v1k\n\n| Data Mac: 94f7be4474c0\n\nData Make: Sercomm\n\nData Model: ES2251\n\nDeMarc Location\n\nHand Off Type\n\nCopper/Electrical/RJ45\n\nNetwork Information **Public**\n\nIP Address Block: 96.10.213.40/29\n\nGateway: 96.10.213.41\n\nUsable IP Range: 96.10.213.42 - 96.10.213.46\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.248\n\n**Document existing/legacy modem and take pictures. Trace the Cradlepoint WAN port and determine what's providing internet today. Take a picture of both the device and the MAC address sticker and upload them to FN platform. (OR NOTE NO LEGACY CKT)**\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n**You have a hard start at 8 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the restaurant, ETC please do.**\n\n**Perform the scope of work below exactly as it is written. The purpose of the scope of work is to connect the newly installed circuit listed above to the customer’s cradlepoint router. Do not interact with any other devices on site.**\n\n**You must bring the following items to qualify for this work order:**\n\n**1. Toner and wand**\n\n**2. Laptop with Ethernet port**\n\n**3. Ladder**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n1. Enable GPS when en route to site for ETA.\n2. Upon arrival, check in with Dispatch via phone at 385-533-9167 & obtain Check In Code\n3. Touch base with the onsite contact - **<**Wendy White 469-663-4979**>**\n4. Take “before” pictures of the network cabinet in the manager’s office.\n5. Locate the circuit listed above. Connect your laptop and confirm you can browse the internet from the circuit.\n6. Perform a speed test and screenshot the result.\n7. Test the IP’s and screenshot the result.\n8. Locate the cradlepoint above the doorway in the manager’s office. Tone out to find the cable going from the WAN port on the cradlepoint to the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk (across the room). Find the other end of the cable\n9. If the other end of the cable is plugged into anything, **stop** and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and **await further instructions**\n10. If the other end of the cable is **not** plugged into anything, plug it into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Use the MAC ID listed at the top of this work order to confirm you are plugging into the correct device. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.\n11. If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint, check above the dropped ceiling tile to see if there is a cable coiled above the ceiling. Plug 1 end into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and safely route the other end over the ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. P the other end into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.\n12. If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and no cable coiled above the dropped ceiling tile that you can find, run a new cable safely above the dropped ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. Plug it into the new modem and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 to notify.\n13. If you cannot find a way to safely run a new cable, complete a site survey for the labor and materials to return and safely run the new cable.\n14. Check if WIFI light is lit on the broadband modem and let dispatch coordinator know at 385-533-9167 if so.\n15. Complete cable management.\n16. Take “after” pictures of the IT cabinet in the manager’s office.\n17. Check out with dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and get checkout code.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T08:00","end":"2026-10-07T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790784397638}
{"job":{"id":20064927,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Momentara","title":"Remove Metro Ad From Amazon Locker - C316953 ( EASY WORK - 10 minutes or less at each site)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:&nbsp;Amazon Locker Ad DEINSTALL</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Provider is to arrive and contact owner or manager on duty to alert them that you are there to install the advertising campaign assigned to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;If they have any questions, they can call 1-800-525-8762.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Remove vinyl ad from Amazon Locker and throw away. This should take around 30 minutes. You'll have to peel off the vinyl, it typically is easier done in warmer weather or when the sun is shining on it</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK: Amazon Locker Ad DEINSTALL**\n\n**Provider is to arrive and contact owner or manager on duty to alert them that you are there to install the advertising campaign assigned to you. If they have any questions, they can call 1-800-525-8762.**\n\n**Remove vinyl ad from Amazon Locker and throw away. This should take around 30 minutes. You'll have to peel off the vinyl, it typically is easier done in warmer weather or when the sun is shining on it**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T00:00","end":"2026-10-05T02:00","latestStart":"2026-10-05T23:59"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":55},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":39},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $55 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"star