{"job":{"id":20066037,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Kohls Replace Cash Drawer, Iron Gray, Key 9952","description":{"html":"SOW: -Tech to replace Cash Drawer on register #4<br/>*****Tech MUST box up cash drawer, till and cable*****<br/>!!! REQUIREMENTS FOR JOB CHECK-IN AND TIME APROVAL HAVE BEEN UPDATED PlEASE READ !!!<br/><br/>-Tech must take pictures of POS devices in box prior to unpacking and attach pictures to work order.  (Pictures can be emailed to dellservice@spencertech.com)<br/>-Tech must follow attached SOW guide<br/>-This work order requires tech to take a before and after photo of all surrounding cables pertaining to this scope of work. Tech MUST NOT leave the site until their Spencer Service agent approves their photos during check out. Tech MUST send photos to DellService@Spencertech.com The Request ID MUST be added to the subject line.<br/><br/>It is required that you follow these guidelines while visiting a Kohl’s location:<br/>-Maintain a positive and respectful attitude towards the customer, fellow employees, contractors, and all others that you Interact with at all times.<br/>-Ensure that your appearance is neat, clean, and that you are properly dressed per the Spencer dress code.<br/>-All complaints are to be taken to the Spencer Field Manager away from the hearing of others.<br/><br/>Required Tools:<br/>-Camera or Smart Phone to take before and after photos.<br/>-Cable testers<br/>-Spare patch cables/Ethernet cables<br/>-Basic tools (Screwdriver, Wire Cutters, Allen Wrenches)<br/>-Extra Keyboard and Mouse.<br/>-Consumables to Cable Manage (Zip-ties, Cable Ties, Twist ties, Label Maker)<br/>#4 Allen Wrench<br/><br/>Checkin Requirements:<br/>-Head inside the store and check in at the Customer Service Desk (for New Stores, check in at the Welcome Desk at the main entrance).<br/>- Tech must retrieve replacement equipment from associate and provide the following during check in call.<br/>       - Return Tracking provided in box with new device <br/>       - Confirm Register # you will be working on<br/>-Provide INC# to store associate and fill out visitor log.<br/>-Tech must take photos of the Device and all the cables for the device before any work is done.<br/><br/>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN<br/>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app<br/>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1<br/>   <br/>While Onsite:<br/>--Tech must follow attached SOW guide<br/>-Tech is required to work with Kohls Team: 262-703-1515<br/>      When dialing 262-703-1515, the following message is played:<br/>      Thank you for reaching the Kohls team.<br/>      Press 1 for store hardware issues.<br/>      Press 2 for network-related issues.<br/>-Tech must perform all work detailed in SOW.<br/>-Take photos of the new installation to provide to Spencer upon checkout. Include all cable connections and cable management.<br/>- It is mandatory that ALL time exceeding the expected duration is approved by the Service team PRIOR to that time being<br/>Please call 844-464-1910 opt 2 as soon as you realize you may not be able to complete the scope of work in the allotted time and provide an update as to why and how much additional time would be needed.<br/><br/>Checkout Requirements:<br/>-Tech must check-out with the Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (844-464-1910, Opt 2) <br/>-Technician is required to send photos from the Job to Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (DellService@SpencerTech.com) The photos should Include all before and after photos for all cables and devices.<br/>-Technician must box up old equipment and provide it to the Manager on Duty.<br/>-Sign out at Kohl’s Customer Service Desk.<br/>    <br/>Deliverables:<br/>-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com; DellService@SpencerTech.com<br/>-Names of the Manager(s) and Support agents you talked with.<br/>-Photos of all cables and devices before work was done and after work was done.<br/>-Return tracking number of the returning part(s).","markdown":"SOW: -Tech to replace Cash Drawer on register #4  \n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Tech MUST box up cash drawer, till and cable\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*  \n!!! REQUIREMENTS FOR JOB CHECK-IN AND TIME APROVAL HAVE BEEN UPDATED PlEASE READ !!!  \n  \n-Tech must take pictures of POS devices in box prior to unpacking and attach pictures to work order. (Pictures can be emailed to dellservice@spencertech.com)  \n-Tech must follow attached SOW guide  \n-This work order requires tech to take a before and after photo of all surrounding cables pertaining to this scope of work. Tech MUST NOT leave the site until their Spencer Service agent approves their photos during check out. Tech MUST send photos to DellService@Spencertech.com The Request ID MUST be added to the subject line.  \n  \nIt is required that you follow these guidelines while visiting a Kohl’s location:  \n-Maintain a positive and respectful attitude towards the customer, fellow employees, contractors, and all others that you Interact with at all times.  \n-Ensure that your appearance is neat, clean, and that you are properly dressed per the Spencer dress code.  \n-All complaints are to be taken to the Spencer Field Manager away from the hearing of others.  \n  \nRequired Tools:  \n-Camera or Smart Phone to take before and after photos.  \n-Cable testers  \n-Spare patch cables/Ethernet cables  \n-Basic tools (Screwdriver, Wire Cutters, Allen Wrenches)  \n-Extra Keyboard and Mouse.  \n-Consumables to Cable Manage (Zip-ties, Cable Ties, Twist ties, Label Maker)  \n\\#4 Allen Wrench  \n  \nCheckin Requirements:  \n-Head inside the store and check in at the Customer Service Desk (for New Stores, check in at the Welcome Desk at the main entrance).  \n\\- Tech must retrieve replacement equipment from associate and provide the following during check in call.  \n\\- Return Tracking provided in box with new device   \n\\- Confirm Register # you will be working on  \n-Provide INC# to store associate and fill out visitor log.  \n-Tech must take photos of the Device and all the cables for the device before any work is done.  \n  \n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN  \n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app  \n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1  \n   \nWhile Onsite:  \n\\--Tech must follow attached SOW guide  \n-Tech is required to work with Kohls Team: 262-703-1515  \n When dialing 262-703-1515, the following message is played:  \n Thank you for reaching the Kohls team.  \n Press 1 for store hardware issues.  \n Press 2 for network-related issues.  \n-Tech must perform all work detailed in SOW.  \n-Take photos of the new installation to provide to Spencer upon checkout. Include all cable connections and cable management.  \n\\- It is mandatory that ALL time exceeding the expected duration is approved by the Service team PRIOR to that time being  \nPlease call 844-464-1910 opt 2 as soon as you realize you may not be able to complete the scope of work in the allotted time and provide an update as to why and how much additional time would be needed.  \n  \nCheckout Requirements:  \n-Tech must check-out with the Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (844-464-1910, Opt 2)   \n-Technician is required to send photos from the Job to Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (DellService@SpencerTech.com) The photos should Include all before and after photos for all cables and devices.  \n-Technician must box up old equipment and provide it to the Manager on Duty.  \n-Sign out at Kohl’s Customer Service Desk.  \n   \nDeliverables:  \n-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com; DellService@SpencerTech.com  \n-Names of the Manager(s) and Support agents you talked with.  \n-Photos of all cables and devices before work was done and after work was done.  \n-Return tracking number of the returning part(s).","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T11:00","end":"2026-10-01T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-01T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790786452523}
{"job":{"id":20066046,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"JPI Companies","title":"Jobsite Trailer IT Install – RDU251701MG Durham - Green Hill","description":{"html":"<p>JPI is seeking an experienced team to complete a standardized IT installation at a construction jobsite office trailer. All managed technology (Meraki gateway, Starlink kits, rack enclosure, TV, NEAT Bar and NEAT Pad, monitors, iPads, printer) is provided by JPI IT Operations, pre-configured and asset-tagged. The technician performs the physical installation, cabling, mounting, patching, labeling, and connectivity testing per JPI's written Standard Operating Procedure, which is attached to the work order upon assignment.</p><p>SCOPE OF WORK (estimated 14 labor hours):</p><p>1. Network backboard and rack (approx. 4 hrs): Install a 2'x4' plywood backboard above the trailer network box, assemble and mount a 6U wall-mount rack enclosure, install the Meraki MX68CW, connect two Starlink WAN uplinks, extend or terminate data drops as needed, patch all drops per the JPI port map, and label every cable at both ends.</p><p>2. Starlink installation (approx. 4 hrs): Assemble two non-penetrating roof mounts, ballast with contractor-supplied sandbags or concrete blocks, mount and align two Starlink dishes using the Starlink app, route cables down the trailer exterior through weatherproof grommets into the rack, secure exterior runs with UV-rated ties, and confirm both uplinks active in the Meraki dashboard with JPI IT Ops.</p><p>3. Audiovisual (approx. 2.5 hrs): Wall-mount a 55–65\" commercial display with the bottom edge exactly 50\" from the floor (verified with a level), mount a NEAT Bar centered directly below and a NEAT Pad 2–3\" to the lower right, patch to designated ports, route cabling in wall runway, and complete an end-to-end Teams test call.</p><p>4. Workstations (approx. 1.5 hrs): Set up four workstations (one dual-monitor, three single-monitor), connect surge-protected power and wireless keyboard/mouse dongles, run and terminate Cat6 drops to each desk, terminate and label one spare drop, test every drop with a cable verifier, and confirm network connectivity at each station.</p><p>5. iPad kiosks (approx. 1.5 hrs): Mount two lockable iPad kiosk enclosures near the main entrance (1 ft from door, level with light switches, 6–8\" apart), mount a power strip, conceal cabling in channel, install iPads, confirm Wi-Fi, and test the Procore app.</p><p>6. Printer (approx. 45 min): Position the leased multifunction printer at the designated wall, connect power, run a Cat6 drop to the designated port, confirm network connectivity, and complete a test print from a workstation.</p><p>CONTRACTOR-SUPPLIED MATERIALS (at provider's cost; verify quantities before mobilizing): 2'x4' x 3/4\" plywood backboard (sealed or painted); 100–200 ft bulk Cat6 and Cat6-rated RJ45 plugs and boots; RJ45 female-to-female couplers; surface-mount cable raceway or tray (1/2\"–1-1/2\") with fittings; exterior conduit or raceway and weatherproof grommets for Starlink penetrations; drywall screws, lag bolts, wall anchors, and washers rated for the trailer wall substrate and mounted loads; velcro straps; interior and UV-resistant exterior zip ties; 8–10 concrete blocks, bricks, or sandbags per roof mount (two mounts).</p><p>CONTRACTOR-SUPPLIED TOOLS (JPI does not furnish tools on site): cordless drill with driver and drill bits; stud finder; 24\"–48\" level; screwdrivers and socket set; tape measure; cable snips, stripper, and RJ45 crimper; cable tester or continuity verifier; industrial label maker (Brady, Brother, or Dymo) with label stock; ladder rated for the work height plus fall protection where required; smartphone or laptop for the Starlink app and photo uploads.</p><p>SITE CONDITIONS: Active construction site. Hard hat and safety vest required at all times; safety glasses during drilling and mounting; gloves during roof and mount work. Trailer has a hard ceiling (not drop tile): no overhead cable runs; all cabling is wall-routed in raceway. Trailer may be slightly out of level; use a level for all mounts and do not reference ceiling or trim. Roof work requires a rated ladder and fall protection as the site safety program requires. Site access is coordinated by the JPI Superintendent; check in at the site office on arrival.</p><p>DELIVERABLES AND ACCEPTANCE: Installation is complete only when the JPI 17-item verification checklist is passed and the sign-off page is signed by the technician, JPI IT Operations, the JPI Operations Support Center, and the Superintendent. Required uploads: as-built photos of each installed area (rack and enclosure, Meraki wiring, roof mounts, AV wall, each workstation, kiosks, printer), cable test results, and the signed sign-off page. Payment is released on approval of these deliverables. Port assignments must not be changed in the field; any deviation requires documented JPI IT Ops approval.</p><p>PREFERRED EXPERIENCE: Structured and low-voltage cabling with RJ45 termination; Cisco Meraki appliance installation; Starlink or satellite dish mounting; commercial display and video bar mounting; work on active construction sites.</p>","markdown":"JPI is seeking an experienced team to complete a standardized IT installation at a construction jobsite office trailer. All managed technology (Meraki gateway, Starlink kits, rack enclosure, TV, NEAT Bar and NEAT Pad, monitors, iPads, printer) is provided by JPI IT Operations, pre-configured and asset-tagged. The technician performs the physical installation, cabling, mounting, patching, labeling, and connectivity testing per JPI's written Standard Operating Procedure, which is attached to the work order upon assignment.\n\nSCOPE OF WORK (estimated 14 labor hours):\n\n1\\. Network backboard and rack (approx. 4 hrs): Install a 2'x4' plywood backboard above the trailer network box, assemble and mount a 6U wall-mount rack enclosure, install the Meraki MX68CW, connect two Starlink WAN uplinks, extend or terminate data drops as needed, patch all drops per the JPI port map, and label every cable at both ends.\n\n2\\. Starlink installation (approx. 4 hrs): Assemble two non-penetrating roof mounts, ballast with contractor-supplied sandbags or concrete blocks, mount and align two Starlink dishes using the Starlink app, route cables down the trailer exterior through weatherproof grommets into the rack, secure exterior runs with UV-rated ties, and confirm both uplinks active in the Meraki dashboard with JPI IT Ops.\n\n3\\. Audiovisual (approx. 2.5 hrs): Wall-mount a 55–65\" commercial display with the bottom edge exactly 50\" from the floor (verified with a level), mount a NEAT Bar centered directly below and a NEAT Pad 2–3\" to the lower right, patch to designated ports, route cabling in wall runway, and complete an end-to-end Teams test call.\n\n4\\. Workstations (approx. 1.5 hrs): Set up four workstations (one dual-monitor, three single-monitor), connect surge-protected power and wireless keyboard/mouse dongles, run and terminate Cat6 drops to each desk, terminate and label one spare drop, test every drop with a cable verifier, and confirm network connectivity at each station.\n\n5\\. iPad kiosks (approx. 1.5 hrs): Mount two lockable iPad kiosk enclosures near the main entrance (1 ft from door, level with light switches, 6–8\" apart), mount a power strip, conceal cabling in channel, install iPads, confirm Wi-Fi, and test the Procore app.\n\n6\\. Printer (approx. 45 min): Position the leased multifunction printer at the designated wall, connect power, run a Cat6 drop to the designated port, confirm network connectivity, and complete a test print from a workstation.\n\nCONTRACTOR-SUPPLIED MATERIALS (at provider's cost; verify quantities before mobilizing): 2'x4' x 3/4\" plywood backboard (sealed or painted); 100–200 ft bulk Cat6 and Cat6-rated RJ45 plugs and boots; RJ45 female-to-female couplers; surface-mount cable raceway or tray (1/2\"–1-1/2\") with fittings; exterior conduit or raceway and weatherproof grommets for Starlink penetrations; drywall screws, lag bolts, wall anchors, and washers rated for the trailer wall substrate and mounted loads; velcro straps; interior and UV-resistant exterior zip ties; 8–10 concrete blocks, bricks, or sandbags per roof mount (two mounts).\n\nCONTRACTOR-SUPPLIED TOOLS (JPI does not furnish tools on site): cordless drill with driver and drill bits; stud finder; 24\"–48\" level; screwdrivers and socket set; tape measure; cable snips, stripper, and RJ45 crimper; cable tester or continuity verifier; industrial label maker (Brady, Brother, or Dymo) with label stock; ladder rated for the work height plus fall protection where required; smartphone or laptop for the Starlink app and photo uploads.\n\nSITE CONDITIONS: Active construction site. Hard hat and safety vest required at all times; safety glasses during drilling and mounting; gloves during roof and mount work. Trailer has a hard ceiling (not drop tile): no overhead cable runs; all cabling is wall-routed in raceway. Trailer may be slightly out of level; use a level for all mounts and do not reference ceiling or trim. Roof work requires a rated ladder and fall protection as the site safety program requires. Site access is coordinated by the JPI Superintendent; check in at the site office on arrival.\n\nDELIVERABLES AND ACCEPTANCE: Installation is complete only when the JPI 17-item verification checklist is passed and the sign-off page is signed by the technician, JPI IT Operations, the JPI Operations Support Center, and the Superintendent. Required uploads: as-built photos of each installed area (rack and enclosure, Meraki wiring, roof mounts, AV wall, each workstation, kiosks, printer), cable test results, and the signed sign-off page. Payment is released on approval of these deliverables. Port assignments must not be changed in the field; any deviation requires documented JPI IT Ops approval.\n\nPREFERRED EXPERIENCE: Structured 