{"job":{"id":20066388,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Interface Security Systems","title":"INTERACTIVE / Camera Install + Camera Move & Pendant Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:</strong></p><p>Upon arrival at the site—but before entering the location—initiate the check-in process by texting “Start” to 314-208-2475.</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Install front door/ height strip camera.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Move Camera three over to behind the POS area. It needs to see POS 2 as well as the safe. It will need a pendant. The drop-down ceiling track doesn't run over the POS area.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">A 12 foot ladder will be required</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Tech must bring the following tools to complete installation:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">1. Spot monitor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">2. Multi-meter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">3. Coax BNC Crimp Tool/Compression toll</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">4. RJ59 crimping/stripping tool</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">5. 12ft ladder&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">6. Drill, in case drilling into beams is needed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">SOW attached.</span></p><p><u>Please read this section</u></p><p>TECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END</p><p>TECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE</p><p>TECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.</p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required</u>:</strong></p><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wireless Hot Spot Device</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder, 8’ step ladder.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8” Torpedo Level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diagonal Cuters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adjustable wrench</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug</li><li>Wire Tracer/Toner</li><li>25’ Tape Measure</li><li>Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks</li><li>3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)</li><li>Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits</li><li>Smart Phone</li><li>Required Materials and Supplies:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fastener Assortment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)</li><li>Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors</li></ul><p><u>IF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"</u></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For iPhone:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For Android:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Console Cable or Adapter.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ladder - 8' minimum.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Standard Networking Tool Kit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable stripper</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">7 level screw driver.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fish Tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tie Wraps.</li><li>10. Sharpie or Label Maker.</li><li>11. Network cable tester.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation POCs</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION</li><li>PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Dress and look appropriate for the job.</li><li>No ripped/cut pants.</li><li>Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Non-used Parts:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nUpon arrival at the site—but before entering the location—initiate the check-in process by texting “Start” to 314-208-2475.\n\nInstall front door/ height strip camera.\n\nMove Camera three over to behind the POS area. It needs to see POS 2 as well as the safe. It will need a pendant. The drop-down ceiling track doesn't run over the POS area.\n\nA 12 foot ladder will be required\n\nTech must bring the following tools to complete installation:\n\n1\\. Spot monitor\n\n2\\. Multi-meter\n\n3\\. Coax BNC Crimp Tool/Compression toll\n\n4\\. RJ59 crimping/stripping tool\n\n5\\. 12ft ladder\n\n6\\. Drill, in case drilling into beams is needed\n\nSOW attached.\n\nPlease read this section\n\nTECH MUST REQUEST EXPENSES ON THE FRONT END\n\nTECH MUST REVIEW ALL ATTACHMENTS IN FULL BEFORE GETTING TO SITE\n\nTECH MUST RECIEVE COMPLETION CODE BEFORE PAYMENT APPROVED.\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND WORK WITH INSTALL SUPPORT USING GUIDE IN ATTACHMENTS\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Intrusion, Card Access, CCTV or Interactive\"\n\n- Laptop Computer – with screen sharing application installed, (preference is AnyDesk)\n- Wireless Hot Spot Device\n- Ladder, 8’ step ladder.\n- Alarm/Security Standard Tool Kit, (Including, but not limited to):\n- \\#1, #2 and #3 Phillips Head Screwdrivers\n- 1/4”, 3/16 and 5/16” Flat-Blade Screwdrivers\n- Phillips and Flat-Blade “Tweaker” Screwdriver\n- 8” Torpedo Level\n- Diagonal Cuters\n- Wire Strippers, (capable to 22 gage stranded)\n- Adjustable wrench\n- Crimping tool – RJ45 Plug\n- Wire Tracer/Toner\n- 25’ Tape Measure\n- Fish Tape or “Green” Sticks\n- 3/8” 18-Volt Cordless Drill, w/ Spare Batery, (“Hammer” func�on recommended but not required)\n- Set of Standard Jobber and Masonry Drill Bits\n- Smart Phone\n- Required Materials and Supplies:\n- CAT6 Wire – Minimum 500’\n- RJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n- Fastener Assortment\n- Tie Wraps, (“ZIP Ties)\n- Splice Caps, (“B” Connectors\n\nIF Work Order is for \"Network and UcaaS\"\n\n- Smart Phone with WIFI Analyzer App.\n- For iPhone:\n- Download the \"Airport Utility\" app from the Apple App Store.\n- Enable \"WIFI Scanner\" in app settings.\n- For Android:\n- Download the \"WIFI Analyzer\" app from the Google Play Store.\n- Choose 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz and click the test icon.\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port or Adapter.\n- Console Cable or Adapter.\n- Ladder - 8' minimum.\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit.\n- Network Cable stripper\n- Network Cable crimper – for most 45 ends.\n- 7 level screw driver.\n- Fish Tape.\n- 18 Volt Cordless Drill and Drill Bits for all Materials.\n- RJ45 Connectors and Crimp Tool.\n- Tie Wraps.\n- 10. Sharpie or Label Maker.\n- 11. Network cable tester.\n\n**Escalation POCs:**\n\n- TECH MUST FOLLOW ATTACHED SOP/ CHOOSE INSTALL OPTION\n- PLEASE READ GUIDE IN FULL AS ESCALATION EMAILS ARE ON LAST PAGE\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Dress and look appropriate for the job.\n- No ripped/cut pants.\n- Boots recommended but no open-toed shoes.\n\n**Non-used Parts:**\n\n- **If there are any parts that were shipped to site that weren't used. Please fill out Fed Ex return form included in the part shipment box. After this form has been filled out, please return package with form to the nearest FedEx Facility for the part to be returned to Interface Security. Please note the tracking number in close notes**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T10:00","end":"2026-10-09T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":400,"max":400},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":43},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $400 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 | FE offline |  noc: 6998768 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790788808702}
{"job":{"id":20066497,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Hilton SD-WAN: Meraki Router Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ONSITE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Download &amp; Install the ServiceNow App:</strong></p><ul><li>Follow the attached instructions to install the app on your device.</li></ul><p><strong>Account Setup &amp; Login:</strong></p><ul><li>On the login screen, click \"Forgot Password.\"</li><li>Enter your email address twice when prompted.</li><li>You will receive an SMS message on the device you're using to complete the setup.</li><li>Use the link provided in the SMS to set your password and complete your account setup.</li><li>If you encounter any issues during the setup process or have any questions, please don't hesitate to reach out for assistance.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Install Meraki Switch</li><li>Install Server&nbsp;</li><li>Install Network Printers</li><li>Work with Support to complete cutover and confirm connectivity</li><li>Collect required collateral and check out with Support</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools/Skillset:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Server/Networking/Workstation experience</li><li>CompTIA A+, Net+, MCSE, MCP equivalent classroom training and 2+ years related industry experience or minimum of 3+</li><li>years minimum related industry experience.</li><li>Ability to comprehend industry standard network connectivity, navigation and software installation</li><li>Standard computer tool kit to include</li><li>Philips screwdriver</li><li>Flat head screwdriver</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Charged Cell phone preferably an Android or iPhone with charger</li><li>Box Cutter</li><li>Pen</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cable</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to 2hrs onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $25 an hour</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment.&nbsp;All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.&nbsp;If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ONSITE:**\n\n**Download & Install the ServiceNow App:**\n\n- Follow the attached instructions to install the app on your device.\n\n**Account Setup & Login:**\n\n- On the login screen, click \"Forgot Password.\"\n- Enter your email address twice when prompted.\n- You will receive an SMS message on the device you're using to complete the setup.\n- Use the link provided in the SMS to set your password and complete your account setup.\n- If you encounter any issues during the setup process or have any questions, please don't hesitate to reach out for assistance.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Install Meraki Switch\n- Install Server\n- Install Network Printers\n- Work with Support to complete cutover and confirm connectivity\n- Collect required collateral and check out with Support\n\n**Required Tools/Skillset:**\n\n- Server/Networking/Workstation experience\n- CompTIA A+, Net+, MCSE, MCP equivalent classroom training and 2+ years related industry experience or minimum of 3+\n- years minimum related industry experience.\n- Ability to comprehend industry standard network connectivity, navigation and software installation\n- Standard computer tool kit to include\n- Philips screwdriver\n- Flat head screwdriver\n- Flashlight\n- Charged Cell phone preferably an Android or iPhone with charger\n- Box Cutter\n- Pen\n- Laptop\n- Console cable\n\n***Flat rate covers up to 2hrs onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $25 an hour***\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.***\n\n***All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:00","end":"2026-10-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":70},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":35}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":47},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790789883205}
{"job":{"id":20066781,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tie National, LLC","title":"SonicWALL - troubleshoot/Configuration Laptop, Patch Cables, Hot Spot Required","description":{"html":"<p>Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159490.</p><p><br></p><p>If you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.</p><p><br></p><p>Description of work requested:&nbsp;&nbsp;An onsite technician is required to troubleshoot a new SonicWall appliance.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will be responsible for the following:.</p><ul><li>Verify the following network connections:</li><li><strong>X0</strong> – Cisco Switch</li><li><strong>X1</strong> – Cable Modem</li><li><strong>X2</strong> – Cellular Backup (if applicable)</li><li>Inspect and verify all network cabling and connections throughout the site.</li><li>Check the operational status of the cable modem, SonicWall, Cisco switch, and all related network equipment.</li><li>Test the internet connection and phone system to confirm all services are fully operational before leaving the site.</li><li>Coordinate with Tie National throughout the installation and troubleshooting process and provide status updates as needed.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Mobile hotspot (for troubleshooting, if required)</li><li>Patch cables of varying lengths</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Gateway IP: 66.57.30.197</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252</p><p>First IP: 66.57.30.198</p><p>Last IP: 66.57.30.198</p><p>DNS1: 209.18.47.61</p><p>DNS2: 209.18.47.62</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The technician must confirm that the firewall is configured correctly and that all network services are functioning properly before closing out the visit.</p><p><br></p><p>Tie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit; before and after pictures of network area, server rack, cable management must be taken and uploaded to portal prior to leaving site.</p>","markdown":"Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159490.\n\nIf you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.\n\nDescription of work requested: An onsite technician is required to troubleshoot a new SonicWall appliance.\n\nThe technician will be responsible for the following:.\n\n- Verify the following network connections:\n- **X0** – Cisco Switch\n- **X1** – Cable Modem\n- **X2** – Cellular Backup (if applicable)\n- Inspect and verify all network cabling and connections throughout the site.\n- Check the operational status of the cable modem, SonicWall, Cisco switch, and all related network equipment.\n- Test the internet connection and phone system to confirm all services are fully operational before leaving the site.\n- Coordinate with Tie National throughout the installation and troubleshooting process and provide status updates as needed.\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Mobile hotspot (for troubleshooting, if required)\n- Patch cables of varying lengths\n\nGateway IP: 66.57.30.197\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.252\n\nFirst IP: 66.57.30.198\n\nLast IP: 66.57.30.198\n\nDNS1: 209.18.47.61\n\nDNS2: 209.18.47.62\n\nThe technician must confirm that the firewall is configured correctly and that all network services are functioning properly before closing out the visit.\n\nTie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit; before and after pictures of network area, server rack, cable management must be taken and uploaded to portal prior to leaving site.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00","end":"2026-09-30T16:00"},