o return ship any unused parts.</li>\n<li>TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL *PROVIDER* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. *OR* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION &amp; TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT. CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 **Canada - 647-496-1288 (CA-ON), 506-300-3307 (CA-NB) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER - 364847227 **WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. **CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!</li>\n<li>Zone 509 false alarms, Rear Door serial # 01489690, Troubleshoot zone, Make adjustments to contact as necessary, Test with SSS Support to make sure it is normal before departure. Allow 1 hour</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"- **Zone 509 false alarms, Rear Door serial # 01489690, Troubleshoot zone, Make adjustments to contact as necessary, Test with SSS Support to make sure it is normal before departure. Allow 1 hour**\n\n- **\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION**\n- **﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.**\n- IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.\n\n- RECEIVING / Security Systems / Burglar - Door Contact / Door Contact Problem / The location of the doors and receiving it is a one pin contact. We have had false alarms by the police dispatched twice when the wind hits the door we need a better contact. W\n- FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.\n- \\*\\*BEFORE LEAVING SITE\\*\\*\\* Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members\n- \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.\n- TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL \\*PROVIDER\\* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. \\*OR\\* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION & TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT. CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 \\*\\*Canada - 647-496-1288 (CA-ON), 506-300-3307 (CA-NB) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER - 364847227 \\*\\*WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. \\*\\*CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!\n- Zone 509 false alarms, Rear Door serial # 01489690, Troubleshoot zone, Make adjustments to contact as necessary, Test with SSS Support to make sure it is normal before departure. Allow 1 hour","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T10:00","end":"2026-10-07T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790793091837}
{"job":{"id":20067144,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Migration","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s &amp; locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>***NOTE: TECH IS NOT TO DISCUSS PAY, RATES OR ANY FINANCIAL INFORMATION WITH THE CUSTOMER ONSITE OR ON THE BRIDGE. IF TECH HAS QUESTIONS ABOUT TIME ONSITE OR PAY, THEY MUST REACH OUT TO NETVIEW. NETVIEW CONTACTS ARE CLEARLY NOTED IN THE CONFIDENTIAL SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER***</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>TECH IS TO REMAIN ONSITE UNTIL CALLING NETVIEW AND WE HAVE COLLECTED ALL DELIVERABLES.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Field services technicians onsite to de-install the network devices from the existing racks and install replacement hardware in the same rack locations. (See attached instructions)</p>\n<p>a. Site Assessment</p>\n<p>b. Firewall Replacement</p>\n<p>c. Wireless Access Point Installation</p>\n<p>d. Rack Cleanup &amp; Cable Management</p>\n<p>e. E911 Compliance Verification</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)</li>\n<li>After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info will be emailed to tech)</li>\n<li><strong>After checking in the first task the tech must complete is walking the site to perform a site survey. Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), location and number of AP's onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li><em>Techs will need to fill out and provide multiple documents (User Acceptance Testing doc, MOP doc, Pictures noted below)</em></li>\n<li>Take pictures of rack and devices in rack prior to beginning any work onsite. (Picture Requirements Noted Below in Required Deliverables)</li>\n<li>Tech to label all cables before disconnecting anything if not already labeled</li>\n<li>Techs should be able to reuse current cable onsite, but must test ALL cable and show pictures of cable test results</li>\n<li><u>ALL CABLING MUST BE NEAT, CLEAN, ZIP TIED AND LOOK PROFESSIONAL (regardless of the state of the cable when arriving onsite)</u></li>\n<li>Handoff of old network equipment to Customer site contact - Pictures and \"Packing List\" of old equipment required as noted in Required Deliverables</li>\n<li>Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of work area MUST be taken&nbsp;<u>before</u>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<u>after</u>&nbsp;work is completed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Before Pics Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Full Rack, Close Up of each device in Rack that will be replace, New Inventory as you are unpacking boxes and Old AP's before removing from bracket</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>After Pics Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Full Rack, Close up of each new device in rack, Old devices in box to be shipped with a list of items in that box (packing list must show model &amp; serial #), Close up of the packing list for old equipment,</em></li>\n<li><em>ACCESS POINT PICTURES: Close pic of all AP's, Wide pic of all AP's (wide pic should be standing back showing the full room with the AP centered in pic)</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the AP is not currently mounted on the ceiling it will have to be moved and mounted on the ceiling during the migration. The survey tech must provide a marked picture showing the best location on the ceiling for that AP to be moved to. You can simply mark the picture with a red X or Circle showing the location the AP should be mounted.</li>\n<li><em>Any cable test results if cables had to be tested.</em></li>\n<li><em>Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.</em></li>\n<li><em>Time Clock - If you install a time clock you must upload a picture of the time clock. Not all sites will be installing a time clock. A installation quide will be attached if your site has a time clock to be installed.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Documents Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Completed User Acceptance Testing Document (3 Pages)</em></li>\n<li><em>Customer will keep the completed document onsite, you are to take a picture of all 3 pages and upload those pictures to this work order.</em></li>\n<li><em>MOP document: You will be provided a MOP breaking down the entire process for this assignment. In this document is a list of the devices you will be replacing onsite. You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on that list AND a brief location of that device.</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc</em></li>\n<li>ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DEVICES TO BE REPLACED:</u></strong>&nbsp;A MOP document listing all devices to be relocated/replaced will be attached to this work order prior to going to site. That MOP document we will attached 2-3 days prior to your visit. This document is critical as it notes all devices to be swapped and instructions on the process required by the end customer.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Box of CAT6 Cable - May not be needed but tech must have in case any cable needs to be replaced.</li>\n<li>Label maker to label cables</li>\n<li>Various Cat6 Patch Cables (3 foot, 6 foot, 10 foot)</li>\n<li>RJ45 Connectors</li>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li>Standard Cabling Tools</li>\n<li>Crimping Tool</li>\n<li>Velcro for cable management</li>\n<li>Laptop:&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li>Console Cable</li>\n<li>Mobile Hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Tester</li>\n<li>Ladder&nbsp;(8'-10')</li>\n<li>Lift will be ordered if necessary</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>You are done with the physical migration portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"***NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s & locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!***\n\n***\\*\\*\\*NOTE: TECH IS NOT TO DISCUSS PAY, RATES OR ANY FINANCIAL INFORMATION WITH THE CUSTOMER ONSITE OR ON THE BRIDGE. IF TECH HAS QUESTIONS ABOUT TIME ONSITE OR PAY, THEY MUST REACH OUT TO NETVIEW. NETVIEW CONTACTS ARE CLEARLY NOTED IN THE CONFIDENTIAL SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER\\*\\*\\****\n\n**TECH IS TO REMAIN ONSITE UNTIL CALLING NETVIEW AND WE HAVE COLLECTED ALL DELIVERABLES.**\n\n**SOW:**\n\nField services technicians onsite to de-install the network devices from the existing racks and install replacement hardware in the same rack locations. (See attached instructions)\n\na. Site Assessment\n\nb. Firewall Replacement\n\nc. Wireless Access Point Installation\n\nd. Rack Cleanup & Cable Management\n\ne. E911 Compliance Verification\n\n**DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)\n2. After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info will be emailed to tech)\n3. **After checking in the first task the tech must complete is walking the site to perform a site survey. Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), location and number of AP's onsite**.\n4. *Techs will need to fill out and provide multiple documents (User Acceptance Testing doc, MOP doc, Pictures noted below)*\n5. Take pictures of rack and devices in rack prior to beginning any work onsite. (Picture Requirements Noted Below in Required Deliverables)\n6. Tech to label all cables before disconnecting anything if not already labeled\n7. Techs should be able to reuse current cable onsite, but must test ALL cable and show pictures of cable test results\n8. ALL CABLING MUST BE NEAT, CLEAN, ZIP TIED AND LOOK PROFESSIONAL (regardless of the state of the cable when arriving onsite)\n9. Handoff of old network equipment to Customer site contact - Pictures and \"Packing List\" of old equipment required as noted in Required Deliverables\n10. Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)**\n\n- Pictures of work area MUST be taken before and after work is completed.\n\n**Before Pics Required:**\n\n- *Full Rack, Close Up of each device in Rack that will be replace, New Inventory as you are unpacking boxes and Old AP's before removing from bracket*\n\n**After Pics Required:**\n\n- *Full Rack, Close up of each new device in rack, Old devices in box to be shipped with a list of items in that box (packing list must show model & serial #), Close up of the packing list for old equipment,*\n- *ACCESS POINT PICTURES: Close pic of all AP's, Wide pic of all AP's (wide pic should be standing back showing the full room with the AP centered in pic)*\n- If the AP is not currently mounted on the ceiling it will have to be moved and mounted on the ceiling during the migration. The survey tech must provide a marked picture showing the best location on the ceiling for that AP to be moved to. You can simply mark the picture with a red X or Circle showing the location the AP should be mounted.\n- *Any cable test results if cables had to be tested.*\n- *Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.*\n- *Time Clock - If you install a time clock you must upload a picture of the time clock. Not all sites will be installing a time clock. A installation quide will be attached if your site has a time clock to be installed.*\n\n**Documents Required:**\n\n- *Completed User Acceptance Testing Document (3 Pages)*\n- *Customer will keep the completed document onsite, you are to take a picture of all 3 pages and upload those pictures to this work order.*\n- *MOP document: You will be provided a MOP breaking down the entire process for this assignment. In this document is a list of the devices you will be replacing onsite. You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on that list AND a brief location of that device.*\n- *Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location*\n- *Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc*\n- ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES\n- *Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)*\n\n**DEVICES TO BE REPLACED:** A MOP document listing all devices to be relocated/replaced will be attached to this work order prior to going to site. That MOP document we will attached 2-3 days prior to your visit. This document is critical as it notes all devices to be swapped and instructions on the process required by the end customer.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- Box of CAT6 Cable - May not be needed but tech must have in case any cable needs to be replaced.\n- Label maker to label cables\n- Various Cat6 Patch Cables (3 foot, 6 foot, 10 foot)\n- RJ45 Connectors\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- Standard Cabling Tools\n- Crimping Tool\n- Velcro for cable management\n- Laptop: With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Cable Tester\n- Ladder (8'-10')\n- Lift will be ordered if necessary\n\n**You are done with the physical migration portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:00","end":"2026-10-06T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":360},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK S