{"job":{"id":20066275,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Installation of ATA and Starlink for Strickly Auto","description":{"html":"<p><strong>ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>1 Starlink Kit</p>\n<p>1 4port ATA</p>\n<p>1 Router</p>\n<p>Will need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point</p>\n<p>Drill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit</p>\n<p>9/16 in hex socket or wrench</p>\n<p>Marker</p>\n<p>Level</p>\n<p>- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).</p>\n<p>- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.</p>\n<p>- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.</p>\n<p>- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.</p>\n<p>- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.</p>\n<p>- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.</p>\n<p>-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).</p>\n<p>Will need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.</p>\n<p>See example pictures of the mount being used.</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>This is an <strong>ATA/Gateway installation only</strong> — no new phones will be installed.</li>\n<li>Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached<strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n<li>See <strong>gateway install scope.pdf</strong> for detailed installation guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.</li>\n<li>Check in with support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable</li>\n<li>Minimum 16 RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1 Starlink Kit\n\n1 4port ATA\n\n1 Router\n\nWill need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point\n\nDrill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit\n\n9/16 in hex socket or wrench\n\nMarker\n\nLevel\n\n\\- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).\n\n\\- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.\n\n\\- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.\n\n\\- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.\n\n\\- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.\n\n\\- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.\n\n-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).\n\nWill need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.\n\nSee example pictures of the mount being used.\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- This is an **ATA/Gateway installation only** — no new phones will be installed.\n- Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached**Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n- See **gateway install scope.pdf** for detailed installation guidelines.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.\n- Check in with support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable\n- Minimum 16 RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nIf another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T11:00","end":"2026-10-20T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":27},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790794898970}
{"job":{"id":"4184354952","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Level 10","title":"Five Below | Install AP(s) Only | LIFT REQ","description":"<p>Overview</p><p><br></p><p>Level 10 tech will be onsite to perform an equipment upgrade to the access points. Check the location profile of each workorder for the specific access points that will be replaced. Not all access points will be upgraded, it varies by site. Work will start before store hours; it is imperative that all specified access points have been installed, tested, and the lift has been removed from site prior to store open. Tech must call into Level 10 Support to test and validate all access points are online. All the old equipment removed will get boxed up and placed in the Level 10 box that was shipped to site. Affix the return label that was sent in the box over the existing label for equipment to get shipped back to Level 10. Contact UPS to schedule a pickup, note the confirmation in CompanyCam checklist. Complete the CompanyCam checklist and have it reviewed and approved by Level 10 Support prior to leaving stie.</p><p><br></p><p>COMPANY CAM USAGE:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Go to this URL:<a href=\"https://app.companycam.com/projects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://app.companycam.com/projects</a></p><p><br></p><p>2. Enter any of these Usernames:</p><p><br></p><p>CompanyCam@Level10.com</p><p>CompanyCam2@Level10.com</p><p>CompanyCam3@Level10.com</p><p><br></p><p>3. Enter this Password: Level10!L10</p><p><br></p><p>4. Search for your Project by Site - Enter \"Customer and (site number)\"</p><p><br></p><p>5. Click on \"To Do's\"</p><p><br></p><p>6. Click on \"Checklists\"</p><p><br></p><p>7. Select appropriate checklist.</p><p><br></p><p>8. Upload all photos to the specified Checklist Only.</p><p><br></p><p>Tools Required</p><ul><li>Power &amp; Impact Drill 18v min.</li><li>Assorted drill, masonry, and driver bits</li><li>Fully charged Labeler w/white backed labels and black font</li><li>Fully charged phone w/Digital Camera and w/CompanyCam app installed</li><li>Velcro for cable management above the ceiling</li><li>Tie Wraps for cable management above the ceiling</li><li>Razor Knife</li><li>Sharpie/Permanent Marker</li><li>Cable Push/Pull Rods, fiberglass Fish Sticks, Glow Rods</li><li>Punch Down Tool w/66 &amp; 110 blades</li><li>Modular RJ45 Crimper</li><li>Data Tester</li><li>Toner w/Probe</li><li>Ladder 8ft min. (a multi-position ladder is recommended)</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Electrician Scissors</li><li>Screwdriver Flatblade, Assorted</li><li>Screwdriver Phillips, Assorted</li><li>Allen Wrench Set</li><li>Torx Set w/Security</li><li>Level</li><li>Tape Measure 35ft</li><li>Pliers, Long Nose</li><li>Pliers, Lineman</li></ul><p><strong>Support Contact</strong></p><ul><li>Tech will need to contact (800) 807-1733 to check in/out and to report any issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Documentation</strong></p><ul><li>Five Below Refresh Network and Equipment - AP Only</li><li>Companycam checklist</li></ul><p><strong>Special Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Level 10 Technician will be required to work on a scissor lift in a new construction environment. Level 10 tech is responsible for providing all PPE as required by the General Contractor onsite.</li></ul><p>Deliverables</p><ul><li>Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Expected Duration: 1.5 Hrs.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T08:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":143.14206373},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":53