{"job":{"id":20067177,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Equipment Configuration/Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Please note:</u></strong></p><p><strong>We will be providing 75 feet of cabling for the access point installation. The access point and cable run will be directed to the drive-through area; if no drive-through is present, The run should be installed to the center of the café. If the full length of cabling is not required, any remaining cable should be neatly coiled and secured above the ceiling tiles in a professional manner.</strong></p><p>*****************************************************************</p><p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p><u>﻿</u><p><strong>Task ID:</strong> 5365504<br /><strong>PON:</strong> 507306<br /><strong>Account Name:</strong> Tropical Smoothie Cafe - NC-135 - New Cafe<br /><strong>Service Address:</strong> 831 S Main St, Rolesville, NC 27571</p>\r\n<p><strong>Managed Networks</strong><br /><br /><strong>Equipment to install:</strong><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;1 x Firewall / SDWAN<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;1 x Switch<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;1 x Access Point<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;1 x Phone<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;1 x Wattbox<br /><br /><br />Tech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.</p></p><p>*****************************************************************</p><p><strong>**10-12 foot A-Frame ladder needed**</strong></p><p>Tech is required to mount a 4u/6u rack. Toggle bolts will be provided.</p><p>Tech must bring tools to mount/install wall network cabinet (Drill with ½” bit.)</p><p>The network cabinet/rack must be properly and securely mounted to the wall.</p><p>Please provide clear installation photos showing:</p><p>A side-angle photo of the cabinet/rack showing that it is securely attached to the wall.</p><p>An interior photo showing the mounting hardware, including the bolts and washers, where visible, confirming that the cabinet has been properly secured.</p><p>Photos should be clear enough for Spectrotel to verify that the cabinet is securely mounted and that all required mounting hardware has been installed.</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Download the SOW for this workorder HERE:</u></strong></p><p>https://cdn0030.qrcodechimp.com/qr/PROD/60a69e75883c08084e1ebdb3/fm/tropical_smoothie_caf_-_field_nations_install_template.pdf</p><p><br></p><p>Final example with equipment location and cable routing:</p><p></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Experience Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cisco Router &amp; Switch connectivity knowledge</li><li>Basic Networking WAN/LAN connectivity</li><li>Setting Static IP Address &amp; Speed Testing from Laptop</li><li>Tech must have experience with VOIP phone &amp; ATA troubleshooting and low voltage internal Wiring, cross connect and termination.</li><li>Experience with customer LAN switches &amp; patch panels.</li><li>Properly Terminating analog/Ethernet wiring to telco 110/66 block, patch panel or biscuit jacks.</li><li>Use cable tester to verify shorts or opens on the line.</li><li>All new cabling must be properly draped and secured without obstruction of other equipment or wiring.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Material and Equipment</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Tools required for Site Survey and Installation</strong></p><ul><li>4G Wi-Fi/Hot Spot to connect remotely.</li><li>Able working laptop with RJ45 Connection port</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Tools to mount/install Wall network cabinet (Drill with ½” bit.)</li><li>Readily available CAT5e/CAT6 Cabling, RJ45 jacks, RJ45 mod ends for patch cords - if needed.</li><li>Toner/Wand</li><li>10-12 Ft Ladder to replace AP's</li><li>Valid photo ID</li></ul><p><strong>If job requires Significant wiring work , the tech must provide the following before leaving the site:</strong></p><ul><li>Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):</li><li>Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details):</li><li>Estimated Distance (ft):</li><li>Conduit/path Confirmed Available:</li><li>Estimate Labor Man Hours:</li><li>Estimate of ALL Materials &amp; Cost:</li><li>Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>﻿♦ ON TIME ARRIVAL IS VERY IMPORTANT</strong></p><p>Dispatch is related to a coordinated porting of lines from a different provider. There is a time sensitive work to complete. <strong><u>Arriving on time is crucial.</u></strong> <strong>PLEASE CONTACT SPECTROTEL ON ANY DELAYS.</strong></p><p>The technician should have AnyDesk (www.anydesk.com) and TeamViewer installed for remote access support requests.</p><p>The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)</p><p><strong>﻿♦ Contacts</strong></p><p>Please reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</p><p>You must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.</p><p><strong>♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables</strong></p><p>Detailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.</p><p>We request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.</p><p>Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.</p><p>Please provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order. Limit to a max of 30 pictures.</p><p>If a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.</p>","markdown":"**Please note:**\n\n**We will be providing 75 feet of cabling for the access point installation. The access point and cable run will be directed to the drive-through area; if no drive-through is present, The run should be installed to the center of the café. If the full length of cabling is not required, any remaining cable should be neatly coiled and secured above the ceiling tiles in a professional manner.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**SOW**\n\n﻿\n\n**Task ID:** 5365504  \n**PON:** 507306  \n**Account Name:** Tropical Smoothie Cafe - NC-135 - New Cafe  \n**Service Address:** 831 S Main St, Rolesville, NC 27571\n\n**Managed Networks**  \n  \n**Equipment to install:**  \n 1 x Firewall / SDWAN  \n 1 x Switch  \n 1 x Access Point  \n 1 x Phone  \n 1 x Wattbox  \n  \n  \nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*10-12 foot A-Frame ladder needed\\*\\***\n\nTech is required to mount a 4u/6u rack. Toggle bolts will be provided.\n\nTech must bring tools to mount/install wall network cabinet (Drill with ½” bit.)\n\nThe network cabinet/rack must be properly and securely mounted to the wall.\n\nPlease provide clear installation photos showing:\n\nA side-angle photo of the cabinet/rack showing that it is securely attached to the wall.\n\nAn interior photo showing the mounting hardware, including the bolts and washers, where visible, confirming that the cabinet has been properly secured.\n\nPhotos should be clear enough for Spectrotel to verify that the cabinet is securely mounted and that all required mounting hardware has been installed.\n\n\\------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Download the SOW for this workorder HERE:**\n\nhttps://cdn0030.qrcodechimp.com/qr/PROD/60a69e75883c08084e1ebdb3/fm/tropical_smoothie_caf_-_field_nations_install_template.pdf\n\nFinal example with equipment location and cable routing:\n\n**Experience Requirements**\n\n- Cisco Router & Switch connectivity knowledge\n- Basic Networking WAN/LAN connectivity\n- Setting Static IP Address & Speed Testing from Laptop\n- Tech must have experience with VOIP phone & ATA troubleshooting and low voltage internal Wiring, cross connect and termination.\n- Experience with customer LAN switches & patch panels.\n- Properly Terminating analog/Ethernet wiring to telco 110/66 block, patch panel or biscuit jacks.\n- Use cable tester to verify shorts or opens on the line.\n- All new cabling must be properly draped and secured without obstruction of other equipment or wiring.\n\n**Material and Equipment**\n\n**Tools required for Site Survey and Installation**\n\n- 4G Wi-Fi/Hot Spot to connect remotely.\n- Able working laptop with RJ45 Connection port\n- Velcro\n- Tools to mount/install Wall network cabinet (Drill with ½” bit.)\n- Readily available CAT5e/CAT6 Cabling, RJ45 jacks, RJ45 mod ends for patch cords - if needed.\n- Toner/Wand\n- 10-12 Ft Ladder to replace AP's\n- Valid photo ID\n\n**If job requires Significant wiring work , the tech must provide the following before leaving the site:**\n\n- Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):\n- Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details):\n- Estimated Distance (ft):\n- Conduit/path Confirmed Available:\n- Estimate Labor Man Hours:\n- Estimate of ALL Materials & Cost:\n- Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift).\n\n**﻿♦ ON TIME ARRIVAL IS VERY IMPORTANT**\n\nDispatch is related to a coordinated porting of lines from a different provider. There is a time sensitive work to complete. **Arriving on time is crucial.** **PLEASE CONTACT SPECTROTEL ON ANY DELAYS.**\n\nThe technician should have AnyDesk (www.anydesk.com) and TeamViewer installed for remote access support requests.\n\nThe technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)\n\n**﻿♦ Contacts**\n\nPlease reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.\n\nYou must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.\n\n**♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables**\n\nDetailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.\n\nWe request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.\n\nSubsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.\n\nPlease provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order. Limit to a max of 30 pictures.\n\nIf a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T09:00","end":"2026-10-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368