{"job":{"id":20068073,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"BlueSky IT Partners","title":"Ethernet Jack Install and Connect - Dunn, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>SOW Summary:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>install and run an ethernet jack in an office space to connect a printer to.</li>\n<li><strong>See the confidential section for additional information</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Onsite Steps</u></strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Step 1: Call BlueSky Work Order Manager by phone to check in BEFORE going inside or contacting customer!&nbsp;Get a CHECK-IN CODE.&nbsp;Review the CONFIDENTIAL INFO section for any added info for this job.</li>\n<li>Step 2: Meet local contact. Get their name.&nbsp;Call technical support to complete work as outlined below.&nbsp;Get name of main Tech Support rep(s) you work with.</li>\n<li>Step 3: Complete any required documents/pictures.</li>\n<li>Step 4: Verify full operation with the local customer and support team before leaving the site</li>\n<li>Step 5; Upload all required pictures and deliverables to this work order and enter your closing notes WHILE STILL ONSITE.&nbsp;The BlueSky WO Mgr will review site pictures and may ask for a few more if needed.</li>\n<li>Step 6: After your site pictures are uploaded to this job, CALL the Bluesky Work Order Manager by phone to check out BEFORE LEAVING SITE!&nbsp;Get a CHECK-OUT CODE!.&nbsp;<strong>THIS IS REQUIRED FOR FULL PAYMENT.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Note to the technician(s) - BlueSky does show numerous penalties, these are due to the 1% of technicians who cause issues onsite. With proper communication before, during, and after the dispatch BlueSky can waive penalties and add bonuses. Please do not assume this will automatically apply to the work order you are working for us.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong><u>:</u></p>\n<p>As we navigate the never-ending changes due to the worldwide pandemic, we are all faced with new work and safety obstacles. BlueSky is committed to providing a safe work environment for everyone without having to cut costs for our technicians. Please refer to the changes in our pay structure outlined below.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Field Nation fees are a cost associated with the technicians and are deductible on your taxes. BlueSky is assessed taxes on work orders separately. In an attempt to keep costs down, BlueSky does not pass the taxes onto the technicians and will not reimburse technicians for their fees.</li>\n<li>Flat rate offers are not accepted, They must be broken down to itemize hourly pay.</li>\n<li>All technicians/providers MUST have their own Field Nation profile. If you are a service company, the work order must be reassigned to servicing technician/provider PRIOR to arrival - no exceptions</li>\n<li>It is<strong>&nbsp;IMPERATIVE THAT YOU ARRIVE AT THE SCHEDULED TIME. This cannot be stressed enough</strong></li>\n<li>If you have any issues on site,&nbsp;<strong>contact Blue Sky work order contact immediately</strong></li>\n<li>Onsite contact is limited to MOD/LCON only.&nbsp;<strong>Do not socialize with support staff</strong></li>\n<li>All required deliverables and close-out notes must be provided while the technician is still onsite. This is to ensure all necessary data is received and the technician is paid for his/her time</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Required tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li>\n<li>Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li>\n<li>Active Email Address</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Teamviewer 12; HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li>\n<li>Microsoft Word, Excel</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ethernet Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cable</li>\n<li>USB to DB9</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Buttset</li>\n<li>RJ11/RJ45 Crimper (crimper ends and bulk cable)</li>\n<li>Snips/Diagonal cutter</li>\n<li>66/110 Punchdown Tool</li>\n<li>Probe/Toner</li>\n<li>Zipties or Velcro (PREFERRED)</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers or Cordless Drill with assorted bits and screws for mounting equipment</li>\n<li>Stepladder</li>\n<li>Cell Phone with camera</li>\n<li>Label Maker</li>\n<li>Proper PPE Gear (Facemasks, hand sanitizer, gloves)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>Required pictures/deliverables TO BE UPLOADED WHILE STILL ON SITE:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pictures of the work area before starting.</li>\n<li>Pictures of the server room, network rack, and equipment.</li>\n<li>Pictures of the equipment worked on installed and operating properly.</li>\n<li>List all Conference Call Personnel and their Departments in your Close Out Notes</li>\n<li>Provide info and Upload pictures of all installed, removed, and or existing equipment Serial Numbers</li>\n<li>Any speed tests results</li>\n<li>Pictures of the work area after clean-up.</li>\n</ol>","markdown":"**SOW Summary:**\n\n- install and run an ethernet jack in an office space to connect a printer to.\n- **See the confidential section for additional information**\n\n**Onsite Steps**:\n\n- Step 1: Call BlueSky Work Order Manager by phone to check in BEFORE going inside or contacting customer! Get a CHECK-IN CODE. Review the CONFIDENTIAL INFO section for any added info for this job.\n- Step 2: Meet local contact. Get their name. Call technical support to complete work as outlined below. Get name of main Tech Support rep(s) you work with.\n- Step 3: Complete any required documents/pictures.\n- Step 4: Verify full operation with the local customer and support team before leaving the site\n- Step 5; Upload all required pictures and deliverables to this work order and enter your closing notes WHILE STILL ONSITE. The BlueSky WO Mgr will review site pictures and may ask for a few more if needed.\n- Step 6: After your site pictures are uploaded to this job, CALL the Bluesky Work Order Manager by phone to check out BEFORE LEAVING SITE! Get a CHECK-OUT CODE!. **THIS IS REQUIRED FOR FULL PAYMENT.**\n- **Note to the technician(s) - BlueSky does show numerous penalties, these are due to the 1% of technicians who cause issues onsite. With proper communication before, during, and after the dispatch BlueSky can waive penalties and add bonuses. Please do not assume this will automatically apply to the work order you are working for us.**\n\n**Overview**:\n\nAs we navigate the never-ending changes due to the worldwide pandemic, we are all faced with new work and safety obstacles. BlueSky is committed to providing a safe work environment for everyone without having to cut costs for our technicians. Please refer to the changes in our pay structure outlined below.\n\n- Field Nation fees are a cost associated with the technicians and are deductible on your taxes. BlueSky is assessed taxes on work orders separately. In an attempt to keep costs down, BlueSky does not pass the taxes onto the technicians and will not reimburse technicians for their fees.\n- Flat rate offers are not accepted, They must be broken down to itemize hourly pay.\n- All technicians/providers MUST have their own Field Nation profile. If you are a service company, the work order must be reassigned to servicing technician/provider PRIOR to arrival - no exceptions\n- It is **IMPERATIVE THAT YOU ARRIVE AT THE SCHEDULED TIME. This cannot be stressed enough**\n- If you have any issues on site, **contact Blue Sky work order contact immediately**\n- Onsite contact is limited to MOD/LCON only. **Do not socialize with support staff**\n- All required deliverables and close-out notes must be provided while the technician is still onsite. This is to ensure all necessary data is received and the technician is paid for his/her time\n\n**Required tools:**\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n1. Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n2. Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n3. Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE**\n\n1. Teamviewer 12; HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n2. Microsoft Word, Excel\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES**\n\n1. Ethernet Patch Cables\n2. Cisco Console Cable\n3. USB to DB9\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS**\n\n1. Buttset\n2. RJ11/RJ45 Crimper (crimper ends and bulk cable)\n3. Snips/Diagonal cutter\n4. 66/110 Punchdown Tool\n5. Probe/Toner\n6. Zipties or Velcro (PREFERRED)\n7. Screwdrivers or Cordless Drill with assorted bits and screws for mounting equipment\n8. Stepladder\n9. Cell Phone with camera\n10. Label Maker\n11. Proper PPE Gear (Facemasks, hand sanitizer, gloves)\n\n**Required pictures/deliverables TO BE UPLOADED WHILE STILL ON SITE:**\n\n1. Pictures of the work area before starting.\n2. Pictures of the server room, network rack, and equipment.\n3. Pictures of the equipment worked on installed and operating properly.\n4. List all Conference Call Personnel and their Departments in your Close Out Notes\n5. Provide info and Upload pictures of all installed, removed, and or existing equipment Serial Numbers\n6. Any speed tests results\n7. Pictures of the work area after clean-up.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:30","end":"2026-10-06T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":38},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":300,"estHours":5,"travelExpense":60,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.