{"job":{"id":"2102119657","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"ASD","title":"AUTOZONE 00411- TROUBLESHOOT CAMERAS and REMOVE NON WORKING PVMs (if there's any)","description":"<p><strong>READ CAREFULLY:</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><em>The store need not to be notified prior to your arrival</em></li><li><em>When applying for this job you must include the proposed service date/time which you will be on site performing work. Include specific day and no more than a 2 hour time range of arrival.</em></li><li><em>We have a 5 day SLA on each tickets. Do not schedule a week after the original schedule date.</em></li><li><em>In case you are to send a different tech to site, you are REQUIRED to let us know in advance and that tech needs to have a separate onforce ticket.</em></li><li><em>Introduce yourself as an ISSKY technician.</em></li><li><em>Failure to check in/out means you did not go to site.</em></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK: </strong></p><p><strong>(</strong>I NEED THIS JOB DONE BETWEEN 8AM AND 3PM ONLY.)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>CAMERAS 8/9 ARE DOWN, ( ONE IS EXTERIOR, NOT SURE ABOUT THE OTHER, ALSO PVM IN BACK DOWN</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Technician please check in with your Vendor PM who will reach out to ISS-KY before starting work.</p><p>Please send before and after pictures of all work.</p><p>Remove old non-working monitor. Completely remove monitor and any unnecessary mounting hardware.</p><p>Remove/secure any excess cabling.</p><p>Install new monitor, power supply, and possibly front door or attached cam if it is on the WO.</p><p>It may be necessary to create a new RG-59 BNC patch cable to connect the new PVM directly to the green output of the existing or new camera.</p><p>Have a VGA monitor to connect to DVR to view and confirm cameras views as need.</p><p>Troubleshoot any additional PVMs on-site and remove dead monitors, power supplies, mounting hardware and secure cabling.</p><p>Please hide all views before leaving site and send a confirmation picture. Check out with your Vendor PM before leaving.</p><p><br></p><p>IMPORTANT PLEASE READ!!!!!</p><ul><li>You <u>MUST</u> have a handheld/ portable monitor with you to be able to see the camera view - THIS IS A REQUIREMENT OF THE CLIENT.</li><li>REFRAIN FROM FILMING OR RECORDING WHILE ON SITE OR DOING SERVICE CALLS AND UPLOADING THEM IN ALL SOCIAL MEDIA PLATFORMS.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Please call ASD Support Contact at 828-212-4285 once you're onsite so I can conference you with our customer support for further info about the scope. You will work with Dwayne and Autozone Support while you're onsite and they will also be the ones to check us out and approve the work done.</li><li>Check and correct DVR settings</li><li>Make sure to rename the cameras accordingly.</li><li>Do not leave any new equipment at stores or risk not receiving payment</li><li>Refrain from telling the SM about more service that the store needs. Report any other outstanding issue/s directly to ASD, not to the SM or store staff.<em>(For example, all cameras need to be rewired - or - you need x and y cameras to be added - or a and b cameras are going bad. Instead, let us know on your notes.)</em></li><li>A 30 days work guarantee applies to this work order.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Upon assignment of the work order, you must provide the exact date and time as to when you are planning to do the job within the timeframe provided.</p><p><br></p><p>Ensure all camera positions are adjusted per AZ spec. All replacement and added cameras must be installed in the ceiling tile. The photo is just a sample, do not be misled. Be prepared to run cable just in case the existing cable is bad. Check and correct network settings if it doesn't match what we have on your checklist.</p><p><br></p><p>PLEASE READ work order and REVIEW ALL attachments. PRINT the Logging into IP screen document as most of these stores have poor cellular signal. You need to be able to work independently.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T08:00","end":"2026-10-07T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":185.18518519},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $185.18518519 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790802271675}
{"job":{"id":20069111,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pomeroy","title":"PROJECT CALL - NCR XR7 POS TERMINAL: (REPLACE AND REIMAGE REGISTER 09 AT STORE 791)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Ticket Description from Customer:</u></strong></p><p>PLEASE CALL THE HELP DESK WITH ETA</p><p>XR7 IS ON SITE, PNY DRIVE ONSITE</p><p>PLEASE SCHEDULE A TECH TO REPLACE AND REIMAGE REGISTER 09 AT STORE 791</p><p>PLEASE SET FOR EITHER BEFORE OR AFTER STORE HOURS -- AVAILABLE WINDOWS OF -- 7AM - 9AM OR 8:30PM - 10PM.</p><p>PLEASE BRING A WIRED USB KEYBOARD, AS WELL AS THE INSTRUCTIONS ON HOW TO REIMAGE A WIRED XR7.</p><p>BEFORE STARTING, PLEASE DISCONNECT SIGCAP FROM XR7; KEEP THE SIG CAP UNPLUGGED THROUGHOUT THE ENTIRE REIMAGE PROCESS*</p><p>PLEASE REPLACE AND THEN REIMAGE THE REGISTER.</p><p>ONCE PROMPTED, YOU'LL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION:</p><p><br></p><p>REIMAGE INFORMATION*</p><p>REIMAGE SHOULD TAKE ABOUT 1 HOUR TO COMPLETE (START TO FINISH)</p><p><br></p><p>POS HOST NAME: 0791reg09 (REG MUST BE LOWERCASE)</p><p>IP ADDRESS: 172.22.216.29 /26</p><p>DEFAULT ROUTE: 172.22.216.1</p><p>TEST SYSTEM: C_PRODUCTION</p><p>Primary DNS Server IP Address: 10.242.145.19</p><p>Secondary DNS server IP address: 10.246.145.19</p><p><br></p><p>WHEN PROMPTED REBOOT THE LANE.</p><p>IF LANE REBOOTS AND THERE IS A RED X ON THE BOTTOM RIGHT OF THE SCREEN, CALL HELP DESK TO REISSUE THE DATA CACHE.</p><p>PLEASE CALL WITH AN ETA AND AGAIN ONCE COMPLETED AND CONFIRMED WORKING WITH A MANAGER. PLEASE DRIVE CAREFULLY AND HAVE A GOOD DAY!</p><p><br></p><p>On Site Contact Name:&nbsp;</p><p>On Site Contact Phone:&nbsp;</p><p>On Site Contact Email:&nbsp;</p><p>Problem Type: CMOS BATTERY ERROR</p><p>Location Subtype:&nbsp;</p><p>Lane Number (if applicable): 9</p><p>Client Ticket Number/External Reference ID: ITSD-291053</p><p><strong><u>Lane Number: 9</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Contact Directory</u></strong></p><p><strong>Pomeroy Dispatch Center: 704-414-5131 Operating: 24/7/365</strong></p><ul><li>Check-in/Check-out, Scheduling/Delays getting to site, Additional time on site, Shipping, TRS Password, <strong>After-Hours Support 8PM-8AM EST</strong>, Expenses preauthorization, all expenses must be preauthorized.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Pomeroy TSS – Technical Support: 704-414-5111 Operating: 8AM-8PM EST/365</strong></p><ul><li>Technical support, Documentation walkthrough, will engage TDJ support if required. <strong>***Do not contact TDJ for support.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Trader Joe’s Service Desk: 855-844-8679 (Option #2) Operating: 4:30AM-11:30PM PST</strong></p><ul><li>Provider must Check-in with TDJ prior to beginning work and Check-out after work is completed.</li><li>If you can't reach the Trader Joe's Helpdesk, please wait 5 min before trying again. Once you dial their number, please press option 2 to speak with a helpdesk coordinator.</li><li><strong><em>Do not contact TDJ for support or work instructions, you must reach out to Pomeroy for support, if you reach out to TDJ for support, a penalty will be applied to the work order. </em></strong></li></ul><p><strong><em>﻿</em></strong></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u></strong>: Business casual. Need to maintain a Professional appearance.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Items to bring:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Basic Tool Set</li></ul><p><strong>*Only accept this job if you have all the required tools and are able to make the required time frame.*</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technical Documentation:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Technical Resource Site:</strong> https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703</p><p>https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-whole-unit-removalreplacement</p><p>https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-bios-settings</p><p><strong>Login ID:</strong> fieldnation@client.pomeroy.com</p><p><strong>Login PW:&nbsp;</strong>If not provided in Messages section, please call Pomeroy Dispatch Center</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Parts Shipment:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Parts (if required) will be couriered to the site; arrival is typically within 4 hours of ticket creation. Please verify with the Pomeroy Dispatch Center that any part(s) has been delivered to resolve issue.</li><li>You may be scheduled to arrive prior to part arrival, due to SLA, please troubleshoot in advance to determine if part is actually required.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Parts Handling Requirements:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Parts return is the responsibility of the assigned Provider. DO NOT LEAVE PARTS ONSITE, unless authorized by Pomeroy.</li><li>&nbsp;If parts are left onsite, work order will not be approved until parts are confirmed shipped.</li><li>&nbsp;Required part must be dropped off asap to UPS: If work order was serviced during business hours, required part must be dropped off the same day until 7PM local time or UPS closing time. If work order was serviced during non-business hours, required part must be dropped off the next day by 12:00PM (noon) local time.</li><li>&nbsp;You must use the return label that comes inside the box shipped by Pomeroy, for additional return labels, please advise Pomeroy Dispatch Center to arrange for label(s) to be sent to you.</li><li>Save shipment drop off receipts in case there are issues tracking or recovering the equipment after it is dropped off.</li><li>Provider may also be held financially responsible for equipment lost due to negligence or failure to follow instruction.</li><li>Ship parts to Pomeroy using return label.&nbsp;Parts must be taken from the store and shipped, unless specified by Pomeroy.&nbsp;Do not leave parts onsite even if asked by TDJ Staff/Service Desk.</li></ol>","markdown":"**Ticket Description from Customer:**\n\nPLEASE CALL THE HELP DESK WITH ETA\n\nXR7 IS ON SITE, PNY DRIVE ONSITE\n\nPLEASE SCHEDULE A TECH TO REPLACE AND REIMAGE REGISTER 09 AT STORE 791\n\nPLEASE SET FOR EITHER BEFORE OR AFTER STORE HOURS -- AVAILABLE WINDOWS OF -- 7AM - 9AM OR 8:30PM - 10PM.\n\nPLEASE BRING A WIRED USB KEYBOARD, AS WELL AS THE INSTRUCTIONS ON HOW TO REIMAGE A WIRED XR7.\n\nBEFORE STARTING, PLEASE DISCONNECT SIGCAP FROM XR7; KEEP THE SIG CAP UNPLUGGED THROUGHOUT THE ENTIRE REIMAGE PROCESS\\*\n\nPLEASE REPLACE AND THEN REIMAGE THE REGISTER.\n\nONCE PROMPTED, YOU'LL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION:\n\nREIMAGE INFORMATION\\*\n\nREIMAGE SHOULD TAKE ABOUT 1 HOUR TO COMPLETE (START TO FINISH)\n\nPOS HOST NAME: 0791reg09 (REG MUST BE LOWERCASE)\n\nIP ADDRESS: 172.22.216.29 /26\n\nDEFAULT ROUTE: 172.22.216.1\n\nTEST SYSTEM: C\\_PRODUCTION\n\nPrimary DNS Server IP Address: 10.242.145.19\n\nSecondary DNS server IP address: 10.246.145.19\n\nWHEN PROMPTED REBOOT THE LANE.\n\nIF LANE REBOOTS AND THERE IS A RED X ON THE BOTTOM RIGHT OF THE SCREEN, CALL HELP DESK TO REISSUE THE DATA CACHE.\n\nPLEASE CALL WITH AN ETA AND AGAIN ONCE COMPLETED AND CONFIRMED WORKING WITH A MANAGER. PLEASE DRIVE CAREFULLY AND HAVE A GOOD DAY!\n\nOn Site Contact Name:\n\nOn Site Contact Phone:\n\nOn Site Contact Email:\n\nProblem Type: CMOS BATTERY ERROR\n\nLocation Subtype:\n\nLane Number (if applicable): 9\n\nClient Ticket Number/External Reference ID: ITSD-291053\n\n**Lane Number: 9**\n\n**Contact Directory**\n\n**Pomeroy Dispatch Center: 704-414-5131 Operating: 24/7/365**\n\n- Check-in/Check-out, Scheduling/Delays getting to site, Additional time on site, Shipping, TRS Password, **After-Hours Support 8PM-8AM EST**, Expenses preauthorization, all expenses must be preauthorized.\n\n**Pomeroy TSS – Technical Support: 704-414-5111 Operating: 8AM-8PM EST/365**\n\n- Technical support, Documentation walkthrough, will engage TDJ support if required. **\\*\\*\\*Do not contact TDJ for support.**\n\n**Trader Joe’s Service Desk: 855-844-8679 (Option #2) Operating: 4:30AM-11:30PM PST**\n\n- Provider must Check-in with TDJ prior to beginning work and Check-out after work is completed.\n- If you can't reach the Trader Joe's Helpdesk, please wait 5 min before trying again. Once you dial their number, please press option 2 to speak with a helpdesk coordinator.\n- ***Do not contact TDJ for support or work instructions, you must reach out to Pomeroy for support, if you reach out to TDJ for support, a penalty will be applied to the work order.***\n\n***﻿***\n\n**Dress Code**: Business casual. Need to maintain a Professional appearance.\n\n**Required Items to bring:**\n\n- Basic Tool Set\n\n**\\*Only accept this job if you have all the required tools and are able to make the required time frame.\\***\n\n**Technical Documentation:**\n\n**Technical Resource Site:** <https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703>\n\n<https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-whole-unit-removalreplacement>\n\n<https://trs.pomeroy.com/trader-joes/pos/terminal/ncr-realpos-xr7-7703/trader-joes-ncr-7703-bios-settings>\n\n**Login ID:** fieldnation@client.pomeroy.com\n\n**Login PW:** If not provided in Messages section, please call Pomeroy Dispatch Center\n\n**Parts Shipment:**\n\n- Parts (if required) will be couriered to the site; arrival is typically within 4 hours of ticket creation. Please verify with the Pomeroy Dispatch Center that any part(s) has been delivered to resolve issue.\n- You may be scheduled to arrive prior to part arrival, due to SLA, please troubleshoot in advance to determine if part is actually required.\n\n**Parts Handling Requirements:**\n\n1. Parts return is the responsibility of the assigned Provider. DO NOT LEAVE PARTS ONSITE, unless authorized by Pomeroy.\n2. If parts are left onsite, work order will not be approved until parts are confirmed shipped.\n3. Required part must be dropped off asap to UPS: If work order was serviced during business hours, required part must be dropped off the same day until 7PM local time or UPS closing time. If work order was serviced during non-business hours, required part must be dropped off the next day by 12:00PM (noon) local time.\n4. You must use the return label that comes inside the box shipped by Pomeroy, for additional return labels, please advise Pomeroy Dispatch Center to arrange for label(s) to be sent to you.\n5. Save shipment drop off receipts in case there are issues tracking or recovering the equipment after it is dropped off.\n6. Provider may also be held financially responsible for equipment lost due to negligence or failure to follow instruction.\n7. Ship parts to Pomeroy using return label. Parts must be taken from the store and shipped, unless specified by Pomeroy. Do not leave parts onsite even if asked by TDJ Staff/Service Desk.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T20:30","end":"2026-09-30T22:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":70},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"