*Required Technician Skills:*\n\n*Network Troubleshooting*\n\n*POS Support*\n\n*CCTV/PTZ Support*\n\n*Audio/Video Support*\n\n*Low voltage cabling*\n\n*Required Tools:*\n\n*Anti-Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat*\n\n*Laptop*\n\n*USB to serial connector*\n\n*Putty*\n\n*NULL Modem cable*\n\n*Ethernet cable*\n\n*Laptop Power pack*\n\n*Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet*\n\n*Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30*\n\n*Flashlight*\n\n*Digital Voltmeter*\n\n*Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - TeamViewer—The Digital Workplace Platform*\n\n*Velcro Straps*\n\n*Cross-over cable*\n\n*Standard screwdriver and security bits*\n\n*Thermal paste*\n\n*Alcohol Wipe*\n\n*Digital cable tester*\n\n*Digital Tone generator*\n\n*Punch down tool*\n\n*Crimping tools*\n\n*RJ45 crimper*\n\n*RJ45 connectors*\n\n**Technician Support Process (Important)**\n\n**Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If you encounter an issue while onsite:**\n\n1. Contact the **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*** and work through the issue with them.\n2. If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.\n3. If the issue is **not resolved after working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\***, then contact **Shyft/NTS Support** for further assistance.\n\n**Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****will be instructed to contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****first before additional support is provided.**\n\n***Completion Requirements:***\n\n**Closing Notes** – **Should entered prior to leaving the site and should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.** If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be a detailed and concise statement about the work performed.**Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.**\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T07:00","end":"2026-09-30T08:45","latestStart":"2026-09-30T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.75,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/30/2026, 7:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00: