{"job":{"id":20069394,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - 300ft Cable Run","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong><p>\"Need a cable tech to locate the cable in the MDF and repair the line</p><p>Need&nbsp;to check the cabling for Western Union Machine to MDF switch.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch notes -</p><p>1. Which piece of equipment it is: sw1561a</p><p>2. Where it is: Food Lion - 1561 Sedalia</p><p>3. What its DNS is: 10.25.134.5</p><p>4. What the problem is: Money Order machine offline is down</p><p>5. What troubleshooting has been completed: Gi1/0/46, Gi2/0/36 is down</p><p>6. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed: Console cable, Laptop with good internet speed, USB, Power cable and LAN cable</p>7. The steps expected for the technician to preform while onsite: We will require console access to login to these devices\"<p><br></p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\"Need a cable tech to locate the cable in the MDF and repair the line\n\nNeed to check the cabling for Western Union Machine to MDF switch.\n\nDispatch notes -\n\n1\\. Which piece of equipment it is: sw1561a\n\n2\\. Where it is: Food Lion - 1561 Sedalia\n\n3\\. What its DNS is: 10.25.134.5\n\n4\\. What the problem is: Money Order machine offline is down\n\n5\\. What troubleshooting has been completed: Gi1/0/46, Gi2/0/36 is down\n\n6\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed: Console cable, Laptop with good internet speed, USB, Power cable and LAN cable\n\n7. The steps expected for the technician to preform while onsite: We will require console access to login to these devices\"**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00","end":"2026-10-02T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":50},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790806728163}
{"job":{"id":20069516,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teceze","title":"Field Service Engineer - Retail Store Device Health Check","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>Technicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.</p><p>The technician will:</p><ul><li>Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Self-checkout devices</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Handheld scanners</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other related store technology equipment</li><li>Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.</li><li>Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.</li><li>Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.</li><li>Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.</li><li>Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.</li><li>Document all remediation activities completed onsite.</li><li>Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.</li><li>Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.</li><li>Take clear photos when required for documentation.</li><li>Clean up the work area after completing the activity.</li></ul><p>Unresolved Issues</p><p>For issues that cannot be resolved onsite:</p><ul><li>Document the device information and issue details.</li><li>Record troubleshooting steps already performed.</li><li>Provide the information to the project team for further action.</li><li>Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.</li></ul><p>Technician Requirements</p><ul><li>Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.</li><li>Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.</li><li>Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.</li><li>Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.</li><li>Must provide professional communication with store personnel.</li><li>Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.</li></ul><p>Visit &amp; Reporting Requirements</p><p>Technician must provide:</p><ul><li>Check-in/check-out confirmation.</li><li>Completed health-check checklist.</li><li>List of devices checked.</li><li>Issues identified.</li><li>Remediation performed.</li><li>Parts/devices used, if applicable.</li><li>Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.</li><li>Required photos/documentation.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\nTechnicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.\n\nThe technician will:\n\n- Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:\n- Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment\n- Self-checkout devices\n- Printers\n- Handheld scanners\n- Other related store technology equipment\n- Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.\n- Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.\n- Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.\n- Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.\n- Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.\n- Document all remediation activities completed onsite.\n- Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.\n- Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.\n- Take clear photos when required for documentation.\n- Clean up the work area after completing the activity.\n\nUnresolved Issues\n\nFor issues that cannot be resolved onsite:\n\n- Document the device information and issue details.\n- Record troubleshooting steps already performed.\n- Provide the information to the project team for further action.\n- Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.\n\nTechnician Requirements\n\n- Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.\n- Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.\n- Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.\n- Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.\n- Must provide professional communication with store personnel.\n- Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.\n\nVisit & Reporting Requirements\n\nTechnician must provide:\n\n- Check-in/check-out confirmation.\n- Completed health-check checklist.\n- List of devices checked.\n- Issues identified.\n- Remediation performed.\n- Parts/devices used, if applicable.\n- Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.\n- Required photos/documentation.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00","end":"2026-10-02T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":265,"max":265},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $265 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13