{"job":{"id":"7024793289","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Move | Priority 3 | 09/29/2026 | Hard Start","description":"*** Non-standard tools requested:  Non-Standard Tools and Materials Required:\n<br>\n<br>200 feet of Cat6 cabling\n<br>Keystones\n<br>Tall ladder ***\n<br>\n<br>Service technician needed on site to move Cabling from current location Locate the camera on site that is not on. to new location Run new wiring for camera.\n<br>\n<br>The technician should test with the following technical contacts: \n<br>• Testing contact #1: Robyn Fleming who can be reached via phone at (646) 513-2484 or email at robynfleming@veg.com.\n<br>• Testing contact #2: Diego Higuera who can be reached via phone at (646) 513-2484 or email at diegohiguera@veg.com.\n<br>\n<br>Previous ticket 6956023 was closed with incomplete work. Camera 1 is online; however, Camera 17 remains offline and is not connected to the network.\n<br>\n<br>Please dispatch a technician for Tuesday, September 29, 2026, at 9:30 AM ET.\n<br>\n<br>Scope of Work:\n<br>\n<br>Locate Camera 17 and identify its switch and port connection.\n<br>Check power, connectivity, cabling, patch cables, and terminations. Repair or replace faulty components as needed.\n<br>Coordinate with the VEG Networking Team while onsite to verify the camera is online and functioning before leaving.\n<br>Document findings, repairs, and confirmed switch/port mapping.\n<br>\n<br>Non-Standard Tools and Materials Required:\n<br>\n<br>200 feet of Cat6 cabling\n<br>Keystones\n<br>Tall ladder\n<br>\n<br>Please ensure the technician arrives with all requested tools and materials. Confirm dispatch and provide technician details. Do not close the ticket until the Networking Team verifies restoration.\n<br>\n<br>VEG is an emergency veterinary hospital. Please do not ask hospital employees to reboot network equipment.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T09:30","end":"2026-09-30T13:30"},"payRange