{"job":{"id":"3762779372","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tekumo","title":"Thermal Printer Repair","description":"<p><strong><em><u>Introduction</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>All onsite personnel must represent themselves exclusively as General Data (GDC) while on customer sites. Under no circumstances should a technician reference or represent Tekumo or any other entity.</u></strong></p><p>This Statement of Work (SOW) outlines the service procedures for a Thermal printer repair request. Tekumo will dispatch a qualified technician to troubleshoot and repair the designated Thermal printer at the customer's location.</p><p>Support Name</p><p><strong>GENERAL DATA Support Phone</strong></p><p><strong>Support Phone</strong></p><p><strong>800-245-5029 ext. 3000</strong></p><p>In the event you cannot reach Tekumo Support please Contact additional support per Special instructions. Please identify yourself as a Technician working with Tekumo and provide the Tekumo ticket number</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Update Closing notes and revisit notes for any parts ordered</p><p><strong>Description from Customer:</strong></p><p>KEN CAPRON</p><p>434-822-3393</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>ZEBRA 220XI II</p><p>SN:&nbsp;2006248</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>ISSUE:&nbsp;PRINT IS VERY FAINT</p><p>2. <strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p>The technician will perform the following tasks:</p><ul><li><strong>Upon Ticket Acceptance:</strong>&nbsp;Provide an estimated arrival time (ETA) within the requested time window on the service platform.</li><li><strong>Parts Verification:</strong>&nbsp;Check the \"Parts and Logistics\" or \"Shipments\" section for any pre-ordered parts. Confirm parts are delivered before arriving on-site. All parts remain in the technician's possession unless otherwise instructed. The technician is responsible for returning any unused, core, or defective parts.</li><li><strong>Customer Contact:</strong>&nbsp;Contact the end user upon traveling to the location. If unable to reach the end user, immediately contact Tekumo dispatch.</li><li><strong>Arrival Procedures:</strong></li><li>Check-in with Tekumo dispatch via platform or by calling 719-900-4525.Introduce yourself to the designated site contact and follow any entry procedures.</li><li><strong>Device Verification:</strong></li><li>Locate the device listed in the \"Custom Fields\" section. Verify the model and serial number match the work order. If there's a mismatch, confirm the device with the site contact. If confirmed, obtain approval from Tekumo dispatch to proceed.</li><li><strong>Device Repair:</strong></li><li>Check device error logs. Clean, troubleshoot, and evaluate the device. Replace or order necessary parts to repair the device.</li><li><strong>Additional Support:</strong></li><li>If parts fail to resolve the issue, or further troubleshooting or parts are required, contact the technician support listed in the \"Support Details\".</li><li><strong>Failure to contact support while physically in the vicinity of the unit(s) you are working on could result in penalties, delays and/or non-payment.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Parts Return:</strong></li><li>If parts were used, contact the Parts Recovery department before leaving the site. All returns must be made within 10 days of the ticket closing, otherwise cost of missing parts will be deducted from the cost of the labor. (refer to \"Special/confidential Instructions\" for details).</li><li><strong>Customer Sign-off:</strong></li><li>Obtain a customer signature on the Field Service Report (FSR) before departure. An FSR is mandatory for each service visit.</li><li><strong>Failure to load all deliverables prior to departure, and to complete the repair may result in penalties, delays and/or non-payment.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;3. <strong><u>Deliverables</u></strong></p><ul><li>Signed Field Service Report (FSR)</li><li>Close out notes: This should always include what was done to complete SOW and any parts replaced.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>4. <strong><u>Dress Code</u></strong></p><p>Business casual attire is required for technicians. This includes:</p><ul><li>Slacks or nice jeans (no holes)</li><li>Collared shirt (polo or long sleeve, with minimal or no logos)</li><li>Closed-toe shoes (sandals are not acceptable)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>5. <strong><u>Required Tools</u></strong></p><ul><li>Smartphone</li><li>Vacuum cleaner</li><li>Alcohol swabs</li><li>Q-tips</li><li>Rags</li><li>Soft bristle brush</li><li>Canned air</li><li>Light machine oil</li><li>Allen wrenches (metric and standard)</li><li>Digital voltmeter</li><li>Assortment of Phillips and flat screwdrivers</li><li>Laptop with a wireless hotspot</li></ul><p><br></p><p>6. <strong><u>Additional Notes</u></strong></p><ul><li>Technicians are responsible for adhering to all Tekumo dispatch instructions and following customer site safety protocols.</li><li>Any deviations from the SOW or unexpected situations must be reported to Tekumo dispatch immediately.</li><li>REPLACEMENT PRINTERS ARE NOT AN OPTION TO DISCUSS WITH ANYONE ONSITE.</li><li>REPAIR IS REQUIRED ON ALL DEVICES</li><li>Only support can make the determination, should a printer need to be replaced.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>This SOW serves as a guideline for the Thermal printer service. Tekumo reserves the right to modify the SOW based on unforeseen circumstances or additional client requirements.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T09:00","end":"2026-10-02T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":67.5},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $67.5 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2