{"job":{"id":20071212,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CoreTech National","title":"Zebra 220Xi II – Faint Print","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technicians must call the end user with their ETA before arriving onsite. Failure to do so may result in non-payment.</strong></p><p><strong>Call the site contact</strong> and provide your ETA before arrival. (Check FN Message for Details)</p><p>For assistance, call <strong>408-434-5004</strong>.</p><p><strong>Management approval is required</strong> for any additional fees or expenses before they are incurred. Call <strong>408-434-5004</strong> for approval.</p><p><strong>List all required part numbers</strong> on the work order. Payment will not be approved without them.</p><p>If a <strong>toner is defective</strong>, attach a photo of the <strong>toner barcode</strong> (not the box), formatted like <strong>2XXXXXX-MXXXX</strong>.</p><p><strong>Customer signatures are required</strong> for all tickets.&nbsp;</p><p>+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(205, 55, 69);\">Pertinent Information</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(205, 55, 69);\">CTN Work Order#:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(205, 55, 69);\">Item To Be Worked On:</strong></p><p>ZEBRA 220XI II SN:&nbsp;2006248</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(205, 55, 69);\">Description of Issues: </strong>PRINT IS VERY FAINT</p>Scope of Work<ul><li>Inspect the Zebra 220Xi II for the reported faint print issue.</li><li>Check the printhead, platen roller, ribbon, and media settings.</li><li>Clean and adjust the printhead and other applicable components as needed.</li><li>Verify print darkness and print quality settings.</li><li>Test the printer after adjustments to confirm proper print quality.</li><li>Provide findings and recommendations if the issue persists.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(205, 55, 69);\">Tools: </strong>Phillips screwdriver set, Torx set, needle-nose pliers, multimeter, laptop, USB/Ethernet cables, flashlight, ESD strap, 90–99% isopropyl alcohol, lint-free cloth/swabs, compressed air, labels and ribbon.</p><p><strong>+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Required Actions: \"**Failure to comply with WO instructions or reporting procedures could result in Reduction or Non-Payment of this work order. ****</u></em></strong></p><ol><li>Contact the site and provide your ETA.</li><li>Verify parts are onsite (if applicable).</li><li>Record arrival and completion times.</li><li>Contact Backline Support if needed.</li><li>List all required part numbers.</li><li>Test the unit with the End User and attach a photo, video, or test print.</li><li>Return parts if required.</li><li>Do <strong>not</strong> discuss pay with the customer.</li><li>Do <strong>not</strong> discuss OEM parts, toner, or ink with the customer.</li><li>For print quality issues, attach multiple photos.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><em>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>IF THE UNIT HAS ANY SIGN OF ABNORMAL DAMAGE (CUTS ON ROLLERS, EXCESSIVE TONER SPILLAGE, BENT FRAME, CRACKED DISPLAYS, WATER DAMAGE, ETC...) PLEASE DOCUMENT THIS WITH PICTURES OR VIDEOS PRIOR TO WORKING ON THE UNIT AND CONTACT DISPATCH IMMEDIATELY.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**Technicians must call the end user with their ETA before arriving onsite. Failure to do so may result in non-payment.**\n\n**Call the site contact** and provide your ETA before arrival. (Check FN Message for Details)\n\nFor assistance, call **408-434-5004**.\n\n**Management approval is required** for any additional fees or expenses before they are incurred. Call **408-434-5004** for approval.\n\n**List all required part numbers** on the work order. Payment will not be approved without them.\n\nIf a **toner is defective**, attach a photo of the **toner barcode** (not the box), formatted like **2XXXXXX-MXXXX**.\n\n**Customer signatures are required** for all tickets.\n\n+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n\n**Pertinent Information**\n\n**CTN Work Order#:**\n\n**Item To Be Worked On:**\n\nZEBRA 220XI II SN: 2006248\n\n**Description of Issues:** PRINT IS VERY FAINT\n\nScope of Work- Inspect the Zebra 220Xi II for the reported faint print issue.\n- Check the printhead, platen roller, ribbon, and media settings.\n- Clean and adjust the printhead and other applicable components as needed.\n- Verify print darkness and print quality settings.\n- Test the printer after adjustments to confirm proper print quality.\n- Provide findings and recommendations if the issue persists.\n\n**Tools:** Phillips screwdriver set, Torx set, needle-nose pliers, multimeter, laptop, USB/Ethernet cables, flashlight, ESD strap, 90–99% isopropyl alcohol, lint-free cloth/swabs, compressed air, labels and ribbon.\n\n**+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++**\n\n***Required Actions: \"\\*\\*Failure to comply with WO instructions or reporting procedures could result in Reduction or Non-Payment of this work order. \\*\\*\\*\\****\n\n1. Contact the site and provide your ETA.\n2. Verify parts are onsite (if applicable).\n3. Record arrival and completion times.\n4. Contact Backline Support if needed.\n5. List all required part numbers.\n6. Test the unit with the End User and attach a photo, video, or test print.\n7. Return parts if required.\n8. Do **not** discuss pay with the customer.\n9. Do **not** discuss OEM parts, toner, or ink with the customer.\n10. For print quality issues, attach multiple photos.\n\n***SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS***\n\n***IF THE UNIT HAS ANY SIGN OF ABNORMAL DAMAGE (CUTS ON ROLLERS, EXCESSIVE TONER SPILLAGE, BENT FRAME, CRACKED DISPLAYS, WATER DAMAGE, ETC...) PLEASE DOCUMENT THIS WITH PICTURES OR VIDEOS PRIOR TO WORKING ON THE UNIT AND CONTACT DISPATCH IMMEDIATELY.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:30","end":"2026-10-02T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":55},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $80 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790859585347}
{"job":{"id":"1419895693","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"SYBEX SUPPORT SERVICES LLC","title":"IT Support","description":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:-</strong></p><p>Site- 3123&nbsp;&nbsp;Need to check&nbsp;interface 1/0/45 to 1/0/48</p><p>Need to check AP Switch port interface 1/0/45 to 1/0/48 physically</p><p><br></p><p><strong>FIELD TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><p>Hardware:</p><p>• Laptop with ethernet port (RJ45) and serial port (both can be via usb adaptor)</p><p>• The rights to change IP address on laptop</p><p>• Working Console cable, both RJ45 type and mini-usb type</p><p>• Null-modem cable (serial crosscable)</p><p>•Crossover and straight Ethernet cables</p><p>•USB drive 4GB FAT32 formatted is mandatory to have in the activity by FE</p><p>•USB drive 8,16,32GB is optional</p><p>•Basic tool sets (screwdrivers, plyers, wire cutter, hex keys, cable stripper etc.)</p><p>•Cell phone with decent camera and 4G connectivity for console access to remote engineers</p><p>•Decent headphones to have hands free during activities</p><p>•Cable ties and accessories to tidy up cabling activities</p><p>•Portable power bank and charging cable for their phone just in case phone battery goes flat – more as reminder</p><p><br></p><p>Software:</p><p>• SecureCRT</p><p>• Putty</p><p>• Teams</p><p>• Zoom</p><p>• TFTP server/client (TFTP64)</p><p>• InSSIDer</p><p>• Netspot – can download a free version in case need to scan and look for hidden AP above the ceiling etc.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T10:00","end":"2026-10-02T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":30,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":39.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 6, 2:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $120\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790859627308}
{"job":{"id":19864673,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Handheld Scanner upgrade - Tech 2","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p><strong><u>The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The registers must be shut down</u>,</strong> then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,<strong><u>THEN</u></strong> reboot the register.</p>\n<p>This is in the doc., page 6</p>\n<p>This should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes to ATR process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)</strong></li>\n<li>If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware</li>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.<em>﻿</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet <strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in <strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong> and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><del>************</del></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>****** * *** ********* ******* *********** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** ****** ********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a<del>********</del>representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\n**The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.**\n\n**The registers must be shut down,** then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,**THEN** reboot the register.\n\nThis is in the doc., page 6\n\nThis should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n- Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n\nChanges to ATR process:\n\n- **Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)**\n- If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware\n- **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n- Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet\n- No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.*﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T08:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":245},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":420,"estHours":7,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790859643620}
{"job":{"id":19864010,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Handheld Scanner upgrade - Tech 1","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p><strong><u>The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The registers must be shut down</u>,</strong> then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,<strong><u>THEN</u></strong> reboot the register.</p>\n<p>This is in the doc., page 6</p>\n<p>This should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes to ATR process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)</strong></li>\n<li>If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware</li>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.<em>﻿</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet <strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in <strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong> and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><del>************</del></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>****** * *** ********* ******* *********** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** ****** ********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a<del>********</del>representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\n**The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.**\n\n**The registers must be shut down,** then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,**THEN** reboot the register.\n\nThis is in the doc., page 6\n\nThis should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n- Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n\nChanges to ATR process:\n\n- **Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)**\n- If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware\n- **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n- Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet\n- No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.*﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T08:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":245},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":420,"estHours":7,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1790859651887}
{"job":{"id":20070727,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home-Thermostat Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong>YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.</strong></p>Smart Home-Thermostat Swap<p>Replace one existing thermostat, have Smart Home Support pair it, and verify operation.</p><p><strong>Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.</strong></p>1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM<p><strong>For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.</strong></p><p>Call immediately if:</p><ul><li>You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.</li><li>The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.</li><li>Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.</li><li>You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.</li></ul><p><strong>If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.</strong></p><p>For access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.</p><p>An FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.</p>2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS<p><strong>THERMOSTAT POWER MUST BE OFF</strong></p><p>Before disconnecting or connecting thermostat wires:</p><ul><li>Identify and shut off the furnace/air-handler and any other power source supplying the thermostat.</li><li>Verify power is absent at the thermostat wiring using an appropriate meter. Thermostat OFF mode, a blank screen, or an assumed breaker label is not proof.</li><li>Photograph the shutoff used and original wiring. Record how you verified power was off.</li><li>If you cannot identify or verify the correct shutoff, stop and contact the Site Manager.</li></ul><p><strong>If you fail to shut off power to the air handler and blow a fuse during thermostat work, you must replace the fuse with the correct type and rating and restore operation at your own expense. If you do not correct the issue, the work order will be closed without payment to cover the cost of dispatching an emergency repair technician.</strong></p><p>Photograph completed thermostat wiring before attaching the display. Restore power and verify heating/cooling operation as appropriate for the equipment and conditions. Report any failed or unperformed test.</p><p>Install and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.</p>3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT<p><strong>Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern</strong></p><p>Call with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.</p>4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORT<p>Upload:</p><ul><li>Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.</li><li>For thermostat wiring work: power-shutoff, original wiring, completed wiring, and installed-device photos.</li><li>Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.</li><li>Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.</li></ul><p><strong>Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:</strong></p><p><strong>Device/location | Work performed | Final result</strong></p><p>Example: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.</p><p>Distinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.</p><p><strong>“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.</strong></p>5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMS<p>Only the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.</p><p>Completion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.</p><p>For resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.</p>","markdown":"**YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.**\n\nSmart Home-Thermostat SwapReplace one existing thermostat, have Smart Home Support pair it, and verify operation.\n\n**Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.**\n\n1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM**For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.**\n\nCall immediately if:\n\n- You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.\n- The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.\n- Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.\n- You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.\n\n**If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.**\n\nFor access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.\n\nAn FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.\n\n2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS**THERMOSTAT POWER MUST BE OFF**\n\nBefore disconnecting or connecting thermostat wires:\n\n- Identify and shut off the furnace/air-handler and any other power source supplying the thermostat.\n- Verify power is absent at the thermostat wiring using an appropriate meter. Thermostat OFF mode, a blank screen, or an assumed breaker label is not proof.\n- Photograph the shutoff used and original wiring. Record how you verified power was off.\n- If you cannot identify or verify the correct shutoff, stop and contact the Site Manager.\n\n**If you fail to shut off power to the air handler and blow a fuse during thermostat work, you must replace the fuse with the correct type and rating and restore operation at your own expense. If you do not correct the issue, the work order will be closed without payment to cover the cost of dispatching an emergency repair technician.**\n\nPhotograph completed thermostat wiring before attaching the display. Restore power and verify heating/cooling operation as appropriate for the equipment and conditions. Report any failed or unperformed test.\n\nInstall and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.\n\n3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT**Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern**\n\nCall with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.\n\n4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORTUpload:\n\n- Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.\n- For thermostat wiring work: power-shutoff, original wiring, completed wiring, and installed-device photos.\n- Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.\n- Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.\n\n**Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:**\n\n**Device/location | Work performed | Final result**\n\nExample: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.\n\nDistinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.\n\n**“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.**\n\n5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMSOnly the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.\n\nCompletion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.\n\nFor resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T10:00","end":"2026-10-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":31},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summa