)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790885356542}
{"job":{"id":20077068,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pipeline Networks, Inc.","title":"MarSha Medspa - Garner - 171 Mast Drive - 48H Dispatch - Podium Network Survey  and Phone Set up","description":{"html":"<p>When the customer asks why we are onsite, you can tell them:</p><ol><li>This is a <u>network survey</u> on behalf of PODIUM (The new VOIP provider).</li><li>We will <strong><u>not</u></strong><u> be disconnecting</u> any of your existing phones; just getting everything prepared for the eventual cut over to PODIUM services.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Call Pipeline to <strong><em><u>CHECK IN and to CHECK OUT</u></em></strong> at <strong>949-333-3339</strong></p><ul><li>Leave a message with your name and location name if you get voicemail.</li><li>GET A SIGNATURE FROM THE POC WHEN LEAVING.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>BEFORE WALKING IN:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You are working for Pipeline Networks</li><li>You are on site <strong><em>on</em></strong> <strong><em>behalf of&nbsp;</em></strong><strong style=\"color: black;\"><em>the onboarding partner, Podium.</em></strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\"><em>Podium is the VOIP provider</em></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SITE DETAILS:</u></strong></p><p>48H Dispatch Podium\nPodium Network Survey and Phone Setup\n<p>LOCAL POC: Mariya Shaikh\n<br>\n<br>HARDWARE DETAILS FOR THIS SITE:\n<br>DESK PHONES: 1\n<br>SOFT PHONES: qty\n<br>CORDLESS PHONES: qty\n<br>\n<br>Do they Have Paging?   no\n<br>Door Access Control?  no\n<br>\n<br>PORTING DATE: TBD\n<b><b></p></p><p>\"SOFT PHONES\" are software-based and do not have any device to install. Podium will place the software needed onto the customer's account.</p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p>We will start by testing the network. Based on our findings, we will then determine whether or not the phones can be installed same day. If we can uplink the new phones <u>without disrupting the current phones,</u> we will do so. All phones are pre-configured.</p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;MUST BRING LAPTOP WITH ETHERNET ADAPTOR (Must be Windows or Mac based software only. Linux will be turned away)</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect to the <u>end of the network (last device furthest from modem)</u></p><p>Example: Modem goes to Router, then to switch.<span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><strong><em>Connect to Switch. </em></strong>Example: Modem to Router, no switches.<span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><strong><em>Connect to Router</em></strong></p><p>3. Please open the link (<strong>https://pipelinenetworks.screenconnect.com</strong>) to allow remote access to our network engineers.</p><p>4. Enter the 4-digit INTERNAL WORK ORDER NUMBER found at the top of the ticket.</p><p>a. Once connected, contact check in number [949-333-3339] <em><u>within the first 20 minutes on site</u></em> <strong>to be connected with an engineer.</strong></p><p>b. This will provide remote access to the customer's network and will be shared with our engineers.</p><p>c. We will contact you via your cell phone # provided.</p><p>d. With your help, we will complete the network survey form.</p><p><strong><u>WHILE YOU ARE WAITING FOR THE ENGINEER TO CONNECT TO YOUR LAPTOP, PLEASE GATHER THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION and </u></strong><u>place in closeout notes.</u></p><ol><li>Report <u>existing </u>phone type: <strong>Analog, PBX, or VOIP.</strong></li><li>Please run both of the following tests and <u>upload photos to the work order</u>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">www.Speedtest.net</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;https://networktest.twilio.com/?usenewvoiceips=true</li><li>Discover if customer has an IT Manager/3rd party IT. If so, ask for contact information and place in your closeout notes.</li><li>Assemble and stage all phones (see site details above). Ask the customer where they want the phones placed and prepare them to be connected. *** <u>DO NOT DISCONNECT</u> THE EXISTING PHONES ****</li><li>We will need to confirm proper cabling to each location where phones are placed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If they do not have the correct cabling, we will need to <u>estimate</u> how long it will take to resolve the cabling, both time needed and length of cable.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If possible, run/install the cable same day<em> </em><strong><em><u>with permission</u></em></strong><em> </em>from Pipeline Networks.</li><li>Take account of the <u>model numbers </u>of any and all network switches.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NOTE how many total ports the switch has and how many ports are available</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;TAKE PHOTOS:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Include photos of <u>all phone locations</u>; need to be uploaded to ticket.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Include photos of <u>all network equipment</u>; need to be uploaded to ticket.</li></ol><p><br></p>","markdown":"When the customer asks why we are onsite, you can tell them:\n\n1. This is a network survey on behalf of PODIUM (The new VOIP provider).\n2. We will **not** be disconnecting any of your existing phones; just getting everything prepared for the eventual cut over to PODIUM services.\n\nCall Pipeline to ***CHECK IN and to CHECK OUT*** at **949-333-3339**\n\n- Leave a message with your name and location name if you get voicemail.\n- GET A SIGNATURE FROM THE POC WHEN LEAVING.\n\n**BEFORE WALKING IN:**\n\n- You are working for Pipeline Networks\n- You are on site ***on*** ***behalf of*** ***the onboarding partner, Podium.***\n- ***Podium is the VOIP provider***\n\n**SITE DETAILS:**\n\n48H Dispatch Podium Podium Network Survey and Phone Setup\n\nLOCAL POC: Mariya Shaikh   \n  \nHARDWARE DETAILS FOR THIS SITE:   \nDESK PHONES: 1   \nSOFT PHONES: qty   \nCORDLESS PHONES: qty   \n  \nDo they Have Paging? no   \nDoor Access Control? no   \n  \nPORTING DATE: TBD\n\n\"SOFT PHONES\" are software-based and do not have any device to install. Podium will place the software needed onto the customer's account.\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\nWe will start by testing the network. Based on our findings, we will then determine whether or not the phones can be installed same day. If we can uplink the new phones without disrupting the current phones, we will do so. All phones are pre-configured.\n\n1\\. MUST BRING LAPTOP WITH ETHERNET ADAPTOR (Must be Windows or Mac based software only. Linux will be turned away)\n\n2\\. Connect to the end of the network (last device furthest from modem)\n\nExample: Modem goes to Router, then to switch. ***Connect to Switch.*** Example: Modem to Router, no switches. ***Connect to Router***\n\n3\\. Please open the link (**<https://pipelinenetworks.screenconnect.com>**) to allow remote access to our network engineers.\n\n4\\. Enter the 4-digit INTERNAL WORK ORDER NUMBER found at the top of the ticket.\n\na. Once connected, contact check in number \\[949-333-3339\\] *within the first 20 minutes on site* **to be connected with an engineer.**\n\nb. This will provide remote access to the customer's network and will be shared with our engineers.\n\nc. We will contact you via your cell phone # provided.\n\nd. With your help, we will complete the network survey form.\n\n**WHILE YOU ARE WAITING FOR THE ENGINEER TO CONNECT TO YOUR LAPTOP, PLEASE GATHER THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION and** place in closeout notes.\n\n1. Report existing phone type: **Analog, PBX, or VOIP.**\n2. Please run both of the following tests and upload photos to the work order:\n3. www.Speedtest.net\n4. <https://networktest.twilio.com/?usenewvoiceips=true>\n5. Discover if customer has an IT Manager/3rd party IT. If so, ask for contact information and place in your closeout notes.\n6. Assemble and stage all phones (see site details above). Ask the customer where they want the phones placed and prepare them to be connected. \\*\\*\\* DO NOT DISCONNECT THE EXISTING PHONES \\*\\*\\*\\*\n7. We will need to confirm proper cabling to each location where phones are placed.\n8. If they do not have the correct cabling, we will need to estimate how long it will take to resolve the cabling, both time needed and length of cable.\n9. If possible, run/install the cable same day ***with permission*** from Pipeline Networks.\n10. Take account of the model numbers of any and all network switches.\n11. NOTE how many total ports the switch has and how many ports are available\n12. TAKE PHOTOS:\n13. Include photos of all phone locations; need to be uploaded to ticket.\n14. Include photos of all network equipment; need to be uploaded to ticket.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T12:00","end":"2026-10-05T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":21},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790887296391}
{"job":{"id":20074577,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walmart - Fuji DL650 Inkjet Printer - Image Quality Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services performing service on a Walmart DL650 printer located in the Photo Center. The service will be troubleshooting the operations of the kiosk with our support team based on the specific service notes below and any parts sent that we determine need to be replaced to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>Troubleshoot ongoing image quality issues with support and ensure printer is fully functional<br /><br />No parts/TS only</p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>No Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.</p><p><strong><u>WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:</em></p><p>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm DL650 support documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li>Review the pump cap video as you may have to clean the print head. https://fx3.training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBTDNHRK</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the&nbsp;<strong>Customer Service desk</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;notify them&nbsp;that you are a vendor&nbsp;representing&nbsp;<strong>Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center</strong>. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla&nbsp;In‑Store&nbsp;ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the&nbsp;<strong>upper left side of your shirt</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>nozzle test print</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;at least 50&nbsp;test&nbsp;prints, to confirm printer functionality.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to remotely&nbsp;validate&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>DL650 printer functionality</strong>, confirm deliverables, and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location</strong>. All returns must be dropped off at a&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup center</strong>, and a&nbsp;<strong>receipt must be&nbsp;retained</strong>&nbsp;to confirm transfer of possession.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature</strong>, and check out of the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>&nbsp;before leaving the location.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><em>Post-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Take the return parts package to a local&nbsp;<strong>FedEx Pickup Center</strong>, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is&nbsp;<strong>not compensated&nbsp;</strong>for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.</li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the <strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>, <strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>, <strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong> and <strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li><li>If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services performing service on a Walmart DL650 printer located in the Photo Center. The service will be troubleshooting the operations of the kiosk with our support team based on the specific service notes below and any parts sent that we determine need to be replaced to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nTroubleshoot ongoing image quality issues with support and ensure printer is fully functional  \n  \nNo parts/TS only\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nNo Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.\n\n**WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:**\n\n*Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:*\n\n<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK>\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm DL650 support documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Voltmeter\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. Review the pump cap video as you may have to clean the print head. <https://fx3.training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBTDNHRK>\n3. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n4. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app**. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the **Customer Service desk** and notify them that you are a vendor representing **Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center**. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla In‑Store ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the **upper left side of your shirt**.\n2. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n3. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n4. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n5. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **nozzle test print** and at least 50 test prints, to confirm printer functionality.\n6. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to remotely validate the **DL650 printer functionality**, confirm deliverables, and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n7. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n8. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n9. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n10. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n11. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n12. **Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location**. All returns must be dropped off at a **FedEx pickup center**, and a **receipt must be retained** to confirm transfer of possession.\n13. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, obtain their **signature**, and check out of the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app** before leaving the location.\n\n*Post-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Take the return parts package to a local **FedEx Pickup Center**, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is **not compensated** for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n- If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T09:00","end":"2026-10-01T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-01T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":85},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/1/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790887763448}
{"job":{"id":20077257,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom","description":{"html":"<p><b>INC#: </b>00736638 - ATT</p><br><p><b>JHA Survey Link: </b>https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdyhkQ7ZAJoTyHijGQw9bQzXOB10pwInMwDVhxIqW4IPR9r9g/viewform?usp=pp_url&amp;entry.294247664=PIVITAL%2CINC&amp;entry.1982354729=UNITED+STATES&amp;entry.1165025588=Raleigh&amp;entry.1821361314=00736638&amp;entry.860366398=00736638+-+ATT+DC+Decom&amp;entry.865848292=ericsson.jha%40pivital.com</p><br><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance </li><li>Check-in with site contacts as representing <del>********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment </li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li></ul>","markdown":"**INC#:** 00736638 - ATT\n\n  \n**JHA Survey Link:** https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdyhkQ7ZAJoTyHijGQw9bQzXOB10pwInMwDVhxIqW4IPR9r9g/viewform?usp=pp_url&amp;entry.294247664=PIVITAL%2CINC&amp;entry.1982354729=UNITED+STATES&amp;entry.1165025588=Raleigh&amp;entry.1821361314=00736638&amp;entry.860366398=00736638+-+ATT+DC+Decom&amp;entry.865848292=ericsson.jha%40pivital.com\n\n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts as representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T08:00","end":"2026-10-12T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":360},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $360 (countered: $360) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790888092983}
{"job":{"id":20077318,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Nerds On Site","title":"Set up printer, Synology NAS, mac computer","description":{"html":"<p><em>* Requesting provider must be the one who performs service. If you need to contact WO manager leading up to or during WO, </em><strong><em>DO NOT use FN messaging or text message</em></strong><em>; call them at the T# provided to you at time of assignment. Failure to do so will result in 20% reduction in pay.</em></p><p><em>* If provider does not/will not check in within 15 mins of the scheduled time, call client first to give them ETA then call WO manager to provide ETA. If not done, we reserve right to reduce WO pay. If the provider needs to reschedule, it's provider's responsibility to call the client and reschedule.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>------<u> Service Description </u>------</strong></p><p>Client is looking for some help to set up their Mac computers, printer and Synology NAS and have them talking to each other. Provider will be tasked with setting up the clients printer, NAS and mac computer to be working together.</p><p><strong>Important</strong>: The client you service will see your closing notes and your check-in/check-out time. It must be reflective of the time/work on-site. If the provider needs to return for additional work/installation/etc or if time will go over estimated time to complete the work, additional pay will be added to this WO at $50/hr, the provider must call buyer at 2-hr mark, and the provider responsible for showing client what part(s) to buy, where/how, and returning to complete the work/replace parts. A second WO will not be created. Receipts/invoices required from provider for reimbursement. By requesting this work order you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this Work Order, for a minimum period of 15-business days</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual clean/fresh presentable clothing. No holes in socks. No coffee-stained clothing.</li><li>Do not smoke/vape just prior to on site appointment.</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Present Identification immediately at entry</li><li>Place protective shoe covers on foot ware or remove shoes <em>(NEVER walk on floor surfaces with wet and/or dirty shoes).&nbsp;Take off shoe covers and replace if the tech must leave the home or walk in unfinished areas of home and then going back on finished surfaces.</em></li><li>Discuss with the homeowner the work to be done what what will take place</li><li>Ensure area where work to be done is fit, given the nature of the work, and explain any issues you could see arising to client prior to start</li><li>Discuss any potential damage, cosmetic or otherwise that may occur as a result of work being done</li><li><em>Place any toolbox or materials onto a clean drop cloth</em></li><li>Final clean-up of job site</li><li>Review you work/solution with the client upon completion and provide training for installed products</li><li>Have the client digitally sign the service sign-off form to acknowledge service completion</li><li>Notify the client how to reach out to Nerds On Site in case of further questions</li><li>Complete the notes with details of the work done/steps taken, and mark complete.</li></ol><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables to Receive Payment</strong></p><ul><li>client signature</li><li>Client's email address</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process</strong></p><ul><li>DO NOT discuss pricing, billing, etc. with the end client.</li><li>If issues arise while on-site, <u>call</u> the WO manager.</li><li>Do not remove client devices from client's property.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Services Policy</strong></p><p>These services may be included in this work order, and the pricing on your work order will be adjusted to match the requested services. These are available to the homeowner for an additional fee:</p><ul><li>Additional hours and expenses (material, travel, etc.) must be pre-approved by work order manage by calling them immediately, before the additional work is performed. Additional pay is priced at $50/hr, but must be pre-approved by WO manager.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>This Non-Disclosure Agreement (\"Agreement\") is made between Nerds On Site (\"Company\") and the technician (\"Technician\") (collectively referred to as \"Parties\") on the day the technician (\"Technician\") confirms this work order..</strong></p><p><br></p><p>1. Purpose</p><p>The Parties hereby agree to enter into this Agreement to protect the Company's confidential information and maintain the integrity of the client relationship. The Technician shall not engage in self-promotion or work directly with the Company's clients during or for 12 months after completing the work order. The Technician is expected to exclusively represent the Company during the work order duration.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Confidential Information</p><p>During the work order, the Technician may have access to confidential and proprietary information belonging to the Company, including but not limited to, client lists, client data, trade secrets, business strategies, financial information, software, and other proprietary information (collectively referred to as \"Confidential Information\").</p><p><br></p><p>3. Non-Disclosure and Non-Competition</p><p>a) The Technician agrees to maintain the confidentiality of all Confidential Information received during the work order. The Technician shall not disclose, distribute, or otherwise make the Confidential Information available to any third party without the Company's prior written consent.</p><p>b) The Technician shall not engage in any form of self-promotion, solicit business, or provide services to the Company's clients, directly or indirectly, during or following 12 months following the completion of the work order.</p><p><br></p><p>4. Client Communication</p><p>a) Any inquiries or requests for future work from the client during or after the work order should be directed solely to the Company.</p><p>b) The Technician shall immediately notify the Company of any such questions or requests and will not engage in any talks or negotiations with the client without the Company's express written consent.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Return of Confidential Information</p><p>Upon completion of the work order or termination of this Agreement, the Technician shall promptly return all Confidential Information, including any copies, notes, or materials, to the Company.</p><p><br></p><p>6. Remedies</p><p>The Technician acknowledges that any violation of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm to the Company. In addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, the Company shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief to prevent or curtail any actual or threatened breach of this Agreement by the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p>7. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</p><p>This Agreement shall be governed by and construed under the laws of <strong>[Jurisdiction]</strong>. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of <strong>[Jurisdiction]</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>8. Entire Agreement</p><p>This Agreement is the entire understanding between the Parties about the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, and agreements, whether oral or written.</p><p><br></p><p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have executed this Non-Disclosure Agreement as of the date first above written.</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Nerds On Site</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Technician's Name</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Date</p>","markdown":"*\\* Requesting provider must be the one who performs service. If you need to contact WO manager leading up to or during WO,* ***DO NOT use FN messaging or text message****; call them at the T# provided to you at time of assignment. Failure to do so will result in 20% reduction in pay.*\n\n*\\* If provider does not/will not check in within 15 mins of the scheduled time, call client first to give them ETA then call WO manager to provide ETA. If not done, we reserve right to reduce WO pay. If the provider needs to reschedule, it's provider's responsibility to call the client and reschedule.*\n\n**------ Service Description ------**\n\nClient is looking for some help to set up their Mac computers, printer and Synology NAS and have them talking to each other. Provider will be tasked with setting up the clients printer, NAS and mac computer to be working together.\n\n**Important**: The client you service will see your closing notes and your check-in/check-out time. It must be reflective of the time/work on-site. If the provider needs to return for additional work/installation/etc or if time will go over estimated time to complete the work, additional pay will be added to this WO at $50/hr, the provider must call buyer at 2-hr mark, and the provider responsible for showing client what part(s) to buy, where/how, and returning to complete the work/replace parts. A second WO will not be created. Receipts/invoices required from provider for reimbursement. By requesting this work order you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this Work Order, for a minimum period of 15-business days\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual clean/fresh presentable clothing. No holes in socks. No coffee-stained clothing.\n- Do not smoke/vape just prior to on site appointment.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Present Identification immediately at entry\n2. Place protective shoe covers on foot ware or remove shoes *(NEVER walk on floor surfaces with wet and/or dirty shoes). Take off shoe covers and replace if the tech must leave the home or walk in unfinished areas of home and then going back on finished surfaces.*\n3. Discuss with the homeowner the work to be done what what will take place\n4. Ensure area where work to be done is fit, given the nature of the work, and explain any issues you could see arising to client prior to start\n5. Discuss any potential damage, cosmetic or otherwise that may occur as a result of work being done\n6. *Place any toolbox or materials onto a clean drop cloth*\n7. Final clean-up of job site\n8. Review you work/solution with the client upon completion and provide training for installed products\n9. Have the client digitally sign the service sign-off form to acknowledge service completion\n10. Notify the client how to reach out to Nerds On Site in case of further questions\n11. Complete the notes with details of the work done/steps taken, and mark complete.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables to Receive Payment**\n\n- client signature\n- Client's email address\n\n**Escalation Process**\n\n- DO NOT discuss pricing, billing, etc. with the end client.\n- If issues arise while on-site, call the WO manager.\n- Do not remove client devices from client's property.\n\n**Additional Services Policy**\n\nThese services may be included in this work order, and the pricing on your work order will be adjusted to match the requested services. These are available to the homeowner for an additional fee:\n\n- Additional hours and expenses (material, travel, etc.) must be pre-approved by work order manage by calling them immediately, before the additional work is performed. Additional pay is priced at $50/hr, but must be pre-approved by WO manager.\n\n**This Non-Disclosure Agreement (\"Agreement\") is made between Nerds On Site (\"Company\") and the technician (\"Technician\") (collectively referred to as \"Parties\") on the day the technician (\"Technician\") confirms this work order..**\n\n1\\. Purpose\n\nThe Parties hereby agree to enter into this Agreement to protect the Company's confidential information and maintain the integrity of the client relationship. The Technician shall not engage in self-promotion or work directly with the Company's clients during or for 12 months after completing the work order. The Technician is expected to exclusively represent the Company during the work order duration.\n\n2\\. Confidential Information\n\nDuring the work order, the Technician may have access to confidential and proprietary information belonging to the Company, including but not limited to, client lists, client data, trade secrets, business strategies, financial information, software, and other proprietary information (collectively referred to as \"Confidential Information\").\n\n3\\. Non-Disclosure and Non-Competition\n\na) The Technician agrees to maintain the confidentiality of all Confidential Information received during the work order. The Technician shall not disclose, distribute, or otherwise make the Confidential Information available to any third party without the Company's prior written consent.\n\nb) The Technician shall not engage in any form of self-promotion, solicit business, or provide services to the Company's clients, directly or indirectly, during or following 12 months following the completion of the work order.\n\n4\\. Client Communication\n\na) Any inquiries or requests for future work from the client during or after the work order should be directed solely to the Company.\n\nb) The Technician shall immediately notify the Company of any such questions or requests and will not engage in any talks or negotiations with the client without the Company's express written consent.\n\n5\\. Return of Confidential Information\n\nUpon completion of the work order or termination of this Agreement, the Technician shall promptly return all Confidential Information, including any copies, notes, or materials, to the Company.\n\n6\\. Remedies\n\nThe Technician acknowledges that any violation of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm to the Company. In addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, the Company shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief to prevent or curtail any actual or threatened breach of this Agreement by the Technician.\n\n7\\. Governing Law and Jurisdiction\n\nThis Agreement shall be governed by and construed under the laws of **\\[Jurisdiction\\]**. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of **\\[Jurisdiction\\]**.\n\n8\\. Entire Agreement\n\nThis Agreement is the entire understanding between the Parties about the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, and agreements, whether oral or written.\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have executed this Non-Disclosure Agreement as of the date first above written.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nNerds On Site\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nTechnician's Name\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nDate","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T12:00","end":"2026-10-06T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":24},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z"