{"job":{"id":20077223,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Infinavate Consultancy Services, LLC","title":"Multimedia - Mood Media Player Patching | Assessment | Installation of new Retail Radio | Bring qty (3) WHITE patch Cables - min 5ft","description":{"html":"<p>Upon arriving and checking in with the Site Contact, the Field Technician must do the following:</p><p><br></p><p>***** IMPORTANT ***** Please <strong>DO NOT sign into the work order 15 minutes PRIOR to the official start time. </strong>The CLIENT will NOT pay outside of the assigned times.</p><p>***** IMPORTANT ***** <strong>Start Times and Release Times are monitored and recorded</strong> for the client, and pay is based on the correct times. Enter your close-out notes while ONSITE</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Serial Number and Ethernet Mac Address of NEW Brightsign device</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>S/N:</strong> 29F649002792</p><p><strong>Ethernet MAC Address:</strong> 90AC3F33D72A</p><p><br></p><p><strong> <u>Safety First</u></strong></p><ul><li>Always wear protective eyewear, especially when going into a ceiling or dusty areas</li><li>Always wear protective Shoes</li><li>Always wear a yellow vest in warehouse or outdoor areas</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>General</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">a-Take high-resolution pictures of the full front/back of the IT rack (Before/After) | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">b. Collect and log the serial number of the Media Device and add it to the OTHER field along with the MAC Address. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work 01</u></strong>: Use this link to access the document needed for the assessment</p><p>https://nam04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapp.smartsheet.com%2Fb%2Fform%2F019ee0b40b3270b99fbc9ccdaf3b5e00&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmhamilton%40infinavate.com%7C2a0050eb79864349850508dee6a1ff02%7C1b6b559c76ad4ee58febcd710272869d%7C0%7C0%7C639201780606359904%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C4000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=5%2BRxrWBHbf%2BLNeWDqjkam%2BCiB3lY4MIz1TzismUB35M%3D&amp;reserved=0</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work 02</u></strong>: Network Cable Trace/Label/Patch of new</p><p>1-Take a high-resolution image of the Area of Concern prior to any new runs/repair/troubleshooting | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.</p><p>Switchports have changed – Audio 3/0/46</p><ol><li>PDA Closet | Mood Media || 1x Wall Jack – Port Trace/Label/Patch | Patch to 3/0/46 Color Patch: White / 5-7Ft. (Patch panel – Cisco 9300) series switch.</li><li>Test connectivity.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of work 03</u>:</strong> Check the Digital Signage TV by the front reception desk to see if there is a Data Jack behind the TV</p><ol><li>Work with the ICS team as we may have you trace that port and connect the Digital Signage TV to Switch 03 PORT #47 with a white patch cable</li></ol><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: inherit;\"><u>ALL Corresponding ports to the above New Cable Runs &amp;/or Cable Trace /WALL-JACKS on the switch must PASS: Continuity/PoE/Flash Test.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Provided Documentation (s) / Instruction (s</u>)</strong>:</p><p>Floor plan (See attachment)</p><p>Technician Tools List Requirements &amp; STD Color Code Patch Cable (See attachment)</p><p>CSL I&amp;T Rack Power Mapping Standard (See attachment)</p><p>CSL I&amp;T Rack | Equipment Install Location Standard (See attachment)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Completion</u></strong></p><p>a- Confirm with point of contact that all New Runs/Wall jacks/ports are operational.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Technician Tools Checklist</u></strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>Cable/Port Tester w/PoE Functions</p><p>Console Cable | Already Configured/Setup on laptop</p><p>MS Teams installed and ready for use</p><p>Laptop with Windows OS with updates Installed. | Dual NIC (Wi-Fi &amp; Ethernet) <strong>Required</strong></p><p>Cross-over network patch cable WHITE - 5ft</p><p>Color Coded: Data/Voice/Fax Jacks (assorted pack)&nbsp;</p><p>Labeling Machine (Portable)&nbsp;</p><p>CAT6E Cable Spool (Slim-Run | (Preferred)&nbsp;</p><p>Ladder | 5ft-7Ft</p><p>Surface Molding Kit (if necessary) / Gang box with faceplate</p><p>Cable Fishing Rods | 10-15ft&nbsp;</p><p>Patch Cables Color: Orange / Red / Grey / Purple / Blue / White / Yellow / Black / Green</p><p><strong><u>**Only use this color code for patching from patch-panel to switch**</u></strong>&nbsp;- Attached to the WO</p>","markdown":"Upon arriving and checking in with the Site Contact, the Field Technician must do the following:\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IMPORTANT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Please **DO NOT sign into the work order 15 minutes PRIOR to the official start time.** The CLIENT will NOT pay outside of the assigned times.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IMPORTANT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **Start Times and Release Times are monitored and recorded** for the client, and pay is based on the correct times. Enter your close-out notes while ONSITE\n\n**Serial Number and Ethernet Mac Address of NEW Brightsign device**\n\n**S/N:** 29F649002792\n\n**Ethernet MAC Address:** 90AC3F33D72A\n\n **Safety First**\n\n- Always wear protective eyewear, especially when going into a ceiling or dusty areas\n- Always wear protective Shoes\n- Always wear a yellow vest in warehouse or outdoor areas\n\n**General**\n\na-Take high-resolution pictures of the full front/back of the IT rack (Before/After) | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.\n\nb. Collect and log the serial number of the Media Device and add it to the OTHER field along with the MAC Address.\n\n**Scope of Work 01**: Use this link to access the document needed for the assessment\n\n<https://nam04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapp.smartsheet.com%2Fb%2Fform%2F019ee0b40b3270b99fbc9ccdaf3b5e00&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmhamilton%40infinavate.com%7C2a0050eb79864349850508dee6a1ff02%7C1b6b559c76ad4ee58febcd710272869d%7C0%7C0%7C639201780606359904%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C4000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=5%2BRxrWBHbf%2BLNeWDqjkam%2BCiB3lY4MIz1TzismUB35M%3D&amp;reserved=0>\n\n**Scope of Work 02**: Network Cable Trace/Label/Patch of new\n\n1-Take a high-resolution image of the Area of Concern prior to any new runs/repair/troubleshooting | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.\n\nSwitchports have changed – Audio 3/0/46\n\n1. PDA Closet | Mood Media || 1x Wall Jack – Port Trace/Label/Patch | Patch to 3/0/46 Color Patch: White / 5-7Ft. (Patch panel – Cisco 9300) series switch.\n2. Test connectivity.\n\n**Scope of work 03:** Check the Digital Signage TV by the front reception desk to see if there is a Data Jack behind the TV\n\n1. Work with the ICS team as we may have you trace that port and connect the Digital Signage TV to Switch 03 PORT #47 with a white patch cable\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n **ALL Corresponding ports to the above New Cable Runs &/or Cable Trace /WALL-JACKS on the switch must PASS: Continuity/PoE/Flash Test.**\n\n**Provided Documentation (s) / Instruction (s)**:\n\nFloor plan (See attachment)\n\nTechnician Tools List Requirements & STD Color Code Patch Cable (See attachment)\n\nCSL I&T Rack Power Mapping Standard (See attachment)\n\nCSL I&T Rack | Equipment Install Location Standard (See attachment)\n\n**Completion**\n\na- Confirm with point of contact that all New Runs/Wall jacks/ports are operational.\n\n**Required Technician Tools Checklist**:\n\nCable/Port Tester w/PoE Functions\n\nConsole Cable | Already Configured/Setup on laptop\n\nMS Teams installed and ready for use\n\nLaptop with Windows OS with updates Installed. | Dual NIC (Wi-Fi & Ethernet) **Required**\n\nCross-over network patch cable WHITE - 5ft\n\nColor Coded: Data/Voice/Fax Jacks (assorted pack)\n\nLabeling Machine (Portable)\n\nCAT6E Cable Spool (Slim-Run | (Preferred)\n\nLadder | 5ft-7Ft\n\nSurface Molding Kit (if necessary) / Gang box with faceplate\n\nCable Fishing Rods | 10-15ft\n\nPatch Cables Color: Orange / Red / Grey / Purple / Blue / White / Yellow / Black / Green\n\n**\\*\\*Only use this color code for patching from patch-panel to switch\\*\\*** - Attached to the WO","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T20:00","end":"2026-10-13T22:00"},"payRange":{"min":58,"max":116},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":58,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":39},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $116 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"