{"job":{"id":20077733,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #303348 - (STRSPRT-1749455) 6662 - General Phone Issues","description":{"html":"<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;***Tech must call TRCA 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with us. ***</p><p>BEFORE GOING TO SITE, ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS.&nbsp; TECH IS NOT TO CALL O'REILLY CORPORATE FOR ANYTHING OTHER THAN INSTRUCTED IN THE TICKET ****TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY****</p><p>Please note: Tech must NEVER call O’Reilly Corporate office for phone system support. If assistance is needed, please contact TRCA at 855-278-0090.</p><p>Once tech has completed their troubleshooting they WILL need to verify with O'Reilly corporate that all issues are resolved to their satisfaction. 417-427-1313.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>PLEASE NOTE: IF NEW OR REPLACEMENT PHONE SYSTEM EQUIPMENT IS NEEDED, PLEASE PROVIDE MODEL # TO THE TRCA REP DURING CLOSE OUT PROCESS.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>The scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Please dispatch a technician to store 6662 to run a phone line for an analog cordless phone.</p><p>The store received an analog AT&amp;T cordless phone and needs an RJ11 jack installed at the ISS desk.</p><p>Please have the tech run the line and set the phone up for the store.</p><p>The due date for service is 10/6/2026.</p><p>Please have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Documentation</strong>:</p><p>Document all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.</p><p>Maintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Take pictures of completed work at various angles.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Submit pictures for the following areas:</p><p>-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)</p><p>-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office</p><p>-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office</p><p>-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)</p><p>-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area</p><p>Confirm the following:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)</p><p>-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:</p><p># of pin pads</p><p># of thin client terminals</p><p># of laser printers</p><p># of thermal printers</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician is responsible for:</strong></p><p>Providing all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Ensuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to safety guidelines and protocols.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Completing the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Promptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Conducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Collaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Communicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Maintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>To Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :</strong></p><p><strong>In addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.</strong></p><p><strong>IF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.</strong></p><p><strong>*******************</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*Tech must call TRCA 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with us. \\*\\*\\*\n\nBEFORE GOING TO SITE, ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS. TECH IS NOT TO CALL O'REILLY CORPORATE FOR ANYTHING OTHER THAN INSTRUCTED IN THE TICKET \\*\\*\\*\\*TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nPlease note: Tech must NEVER call O’Reilly Corporate office for phone system support. If assistance is needed, please contact TRCA at 855-278-0090.\n\nOnce tech has completed their troubleshooting they WILL need to verify with O'Reilly corporate that all issues are resolved to their satisfaction. 417-427-1313.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE: IF NEW OR REPLACEMENT PHONE SYSTEM EQUIPMENT IS NEEDED, PLEASE PROVIDE MODEL # TO THE TRCA REP DURING CLOSE OUT PROCESS.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nThe scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:\n\nPlease dispatch a technician to store 6662 to run a phone line for an analog cordless phone.\n\nThe store received an analog AT&T cordless phone and needs an RJ11 jack installed at the ISS desk.\n\nPlease have the tech run the line and set the phone up for the store.\n\nThe due date for service is 10/6/2026.\n\nPlease have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.\n\n **Documentation**:\n\nDocument all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.\n\nMaintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.\n\nTake pictures of completed work at various angles.\n\nSubmit pictures for the following areas:\n\n-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)\n\n-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office\n\n-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office\n\n-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)\n\n-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area\n\nConfirm the following:\n\n-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)\n\n-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:\n\n\\# of pin pads\n\n\\# of thin client terminals\n\n\\# of laser printers\n\n\\# of thermal printers\n\n**The technician is responsible for:**\n\nProviding all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)\n\nEnsuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.\n\nAdhering to safety guidelines and protocols.\n\nCompleting the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)\n\nPromptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.\n\nConducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.\n\nCollaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.\n\nCommunicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.\n\nAdhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.\n\nMaintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.\n\n**To Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :**\n\n**In addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.**\n\n**IF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T08:00","end":"2026-10-06T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":28},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/1/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T