{"job":{"id":20079510,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Tech to install 1 WB","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>﻿Important Generic Scope Details</strong>:&nbsp;You are being scoped to complete the Installation of a&nbsp;<strong>Digital Wall Board</strong>&nbsp;<u>and/or</u>&nbsp;<strong>TV</strong>&nbsp;(size varies). Please see Problem Description/Scope of Work section for specific service request details.</p><p><strong>Important:</strong>Do Not to Exceed 1 HR ONSITE (per device) without approval from Essintial - At 1 hour onsite (per device), if scope is not complete you MUST call Essintial at 855-612-2183 to obtain approval to exceed.</p><p><strong>Important:&nbsp;</strong>Technicians&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;Check-In,&nbsp;Verify/Complete Device Verification,&nbsp;Upload Photos,&nbsp;Check-Out&nbsp;(<em>obtain completion code by calling CheckedUp Helpdesk)</em>, and&nbsp;Complete&nbsp;the Customers&nbsp;<strong><em>\"Work Order Verification\"</em></strong>&nbsp;Link (Real Time). The Link MUST FULLY BE COMPLTED&nbsp;<strong><em>PRIOR</em></strong>&nbsp;to leaving the site (see special instructions above on where to obtain the link &amp; how to complete the link)</p><p><strong>Important:DO NOT CALL ONSITE POC UNLESS YOU ARE ONSITE AND NEED ACCESS – If you are running late or cannot make it to site you MUST call Essintial.</strong></p><p><strong>Important</strong>: If you are scoped to service a&nbsp;<strong><u>TV</u></strong>&nbsp;(Install / Swap / troubleshooting) – Tech&nbsp;<strong><u>MUST</u></strong>&nbsp;<strong>HARDWIRE</strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;IF POC refuses to allow HARDWIRE….</p><ul><li>Tech MUST report a valid reason&nbsp;<strong><u>WHY</u></strong></li><li>Tech MUST make sure the WIFI is set to a&nbsp;<strong><u>PRIVATE</u></strong>&nbsp;WIFI and&nbsp;<strong><u>NOT</u></strong>&nbsp;<strong><u>GUEST</u></strong>&nbsp;WIFI</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-site time/window: 1 hour</strong></p><p><em>**IF YOU ARE UNABLE TO MEET THIS YOU MUST NOTIFY ESSINTIAL VIA PHONE CALL (855-612-2183)**</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Problem Description / Scope of Work Instructions :</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(29, 31, 37);\">Tech to install 1 WB</span></p><p><br></p><p>***Tech to Call Help Desk to Check In and Check Out, PRIOR to leaving the site. 855-465-4884</p><p>***Please contact Essintial Support 717-516-3009 with any questions or concerns***</p><p>***Please make sure to have the POC Signature on the WO Link PRIOR to leaving the site.***</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Please bring firmware update materials, also a PC. The WB MUST be on the Private WiFi.</p><p>Firmware Update Processes:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14HZEooARs_DM43mIL3Sd7bFkV5zR2djO&nbsp;(Select the model from the list)</p><p><br></p><p>CheckedUp Verification Link&nbsp; https://checkedup.my.salesforce-sites.com/fieldService/spworkordercheckin?id=0WOPq00000PiaZG</p><p><strong>Scope Specific Folder Links</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Installations Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zVY-hoQtbZpkMxX7BOVAzCWQLCY-w_e-?usp=drive_link&nbsp;</li><li>Android 12 IMAGE Update Files Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LO7a2iJ2QnR1f2gnZZZhh5Zg26hPtJ37?usp=drive_link</li><li>&nbsp;HMN Media Player Training Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1pzyuBWhlXyz3QOTT6rUFcv5kvg77q0ku?usp=drive_link</li><li>Troubleshooting Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PId7ic9-yMyA1NnrPUya45MoUGIES6Am?usp=drive_link</li><li>Troubleshooting Documentation As Of 1-15-24 Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1UKLAEr7mrGJS3S3r3IKowl0KpNVQJF4K?usp=drive_link</li><li>Tech Requirements/WO Link Management Folder:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12B_SUY87IZoMI0oL6bI9TkoEBIJFI1gn?usp=drive_link</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Important Requirements/Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Important Technical Documentation - You MUST review and refer to documentations prior to and while onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check you Scope of Work Instructions for specific documentation call outs based on your scope</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All Technical Documentation can be found using this link, use the folders within the links which are broken down by type of scopes (copy &amp;&nbsp;paste into browser):&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ip_LmthXsZxHcQa3SvYGIntFDXewb_M-</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any issues finding the correct documents please reach out to Ess L1 Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</li><li>Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent themselves as a<strong>CheckedUp</strong>Technician while onsite.</li><li>&nbsp;<strong>Estimated Onsite Hours</strong> = 1 Hour PER Device (must obtain approval to exceed)</li><li>Do Not to Exceed 1 HR ONSITE (per device) without approval from Essintial - At 1 hour onsite (per device), if scope is not complete you MUST call Essintial at 855-612-2183 to obtain approval.</li><li>Refer to Scope of Work Details for any special important technician information/requirements- I.E Special Work Order Verification Link Instructions (photo requirements), special tool requirements, parts order/return information, special photo requirements , special onsite instructions, etc.</li><li>Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>Check-In</u>and<u>Check-Out</u>with<strong>CheckedUp Help Desk at<del>*********** ********</del></strong></li><li>Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>Check-In</u>via<strong><u>Work Order Verification Link</u></strong></li><li>Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong><u>Check Out</u>via<strong><u>Work Order Verification Link</u></strong>(complete Device Verification), then call CheckedUp Helpdesk to check out and obtain the completion code needed to complete the Link</li><li>Tech<strong>&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;</strong>gain approval from Essintial If the end customer/onsite poc ask to have the device be installed on a stand or table mount and this is not specified in scope / CheckedUp did not advise so originally.</li><li>Technician&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;complete the Customers Work Order Verification Link PRIOR to leaving the sit<strong>e&nbsp;</strong>(see special instructions below on how to complete the link)</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Important Site Information:</strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as a CheckedUp Technician while onsite.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</li><li>Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li><li>If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.&nbsp;</li><li>IF YOU ARE UNABLE TO COMPLETE THE SCOPE AS DEFINED IN THE GUIDE &amp; YOUR WORK ORDER YOU MUST CALL THE CHECKEDUP HELPDESK AND ESSINTIAL PRIOR TO LEAVING THE SITE</li><li>All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.</li><li>If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Material</strong>:</p><ul><li>***Please Also Refer to Scope of Work Details for specific tool call outs reported by the customer***</li><li>Printed Documentation must be with you onsite – all documents found in the provided google drive, select the folder(s) that best applies to your specific scope</li><li><strong>100ft cat 5 Cable Pull (PER TV)</strong>-&nbsp;if working on a Work Order that has at least 1 Tv (all types of WOs including troubleshooting)</li><li><strong>10ft Panduit (White) (PER TV)</strong>&nbsp;- if working on a Work Order that has at least 1 Tv (all types of WOs including troubleshooting)</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has phone, camera, and internet ability (for photos and online deliverable)</li><li>Stud finder&nbsp;</li><li>Tape measure</li><li>Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Phillips drill bit 12” extension (used for inserting the locking screws)</li><li>Awl (to assist in making holes in wall and cord cover for the screws to be installed)</li><li>Small level (for leveling the wall bracket)</li><li>2-foot level (for leveling the cord cover)</li><li>Cable Cutter/diagonal cutters (for trimming the cord cover)&nbsp;or&nbsp;hacksaw for cutting cord covers</li><li>Crimper</li><li>RJ45 Ends</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Razorblade</li><li>Cordless Drill- Only use if necessary, for concrete walls, avoid making noise in the office</li><li>Drill bits for sheetrock/concrete walls behind sheetrock</li><li>Hammer to tap in the anchors in the case of concrete walls</li><li>USB Windows keyboard</li><li>USB mouse</li><li>Step ladder (for tv installation if installing TV, DO NOT stand on office chairs)</li><li>Windows Laptop</li><li>USB Stick</li><li>USB- Mini USB cable</li><li>Toggle bolts</li><li>Hex Nuts &amp; Machine Screws (specifically for Articulating Mounts)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>**Customers Work Order Verification Link (Online Real Time Deliverable)&nbsp;**</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>This&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;be started upon arrival and fully completed&nbsp;PRIOR&nbsp;to leaving the site location</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Technician&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;use the provided verification link to Check-In, Verify/Complete Device Verification, Upload Photos, and Check-Out Real Time ( Link must fully be completed prior to leaving the site).&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;LINK CAN BE FOUND IN THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND REF. FIELDS OF YOUR TICKET</p><ul><li>Tech MUST check-in on wo verification link</li><li>Tech MUST upload photos on wo verification link</li><li>Tech MUST check-out on wo verficiation link</li><li>Tech MUST complete the link while onsite ( Verify Device(s), Check-Out, and Complete )</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Work Order Specific Link</em></strong><em>:&nbsp;</em>refer to problem description and/or custom fields of your work order.</p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>WO Link Completion Steps / Video Link [How To]</em></strong>:&nbsp;See Steps below&nbsp;<em>OR</em>&nbsp;Click this link to watch a quick tutorial on completing the Work Order Verification Link:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VmABXd_bllzGxXPBsSBxEBnyRvBcD-0I/view</p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>WO Link Completion Steps:</em></strong></p><ol><li>Refer to problem description for any special call out’s</li><li>Click the provided Work Order Verification Link</li><li>Verify the Work Order #, # of Devices, &amp; Site information</li><li>Click “View Devices”</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Select the Device you are working on (<em>If Multiple Devices – repeat these steps for each device</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Enter what Room/Site and Floor # the device is located in/on</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Enter Notes – i.e. your visit/equipment completion notes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check the box “Connected &amp; Playing Content”</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload a photo of the working device/device playing content</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Click “Device Verification”</li><li>View Device Verification Results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you get ALL GREEN checks&nbsp;-&nbsp;Click COMPLETE ASSET</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you get any RED checks – call the CheckedUp Help Desk for assistance</li><li>Repeat Steps 5-11 for each Device</li><li>Click “Complete Order” once all devices have been verified</li><li>At Confirmation Page – contact Help Desk to check out and obtain agent name &amp; confirmation code</li><li>Using the provided Confirmation Code - enter it into the WO Link to fully complete the online deliverable</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Arriving On Time:</strong> You are required to be onsite&nbsp;<strong>no later than</strong>&nbsp;your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face&nbsp;penalties/non-payment.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements:</strong></p><p>Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Photographic Deliverable Requirement- You are REQUIRED to capture &amp; submit all of the photos asked of you by your assigned support technician.</strong></p><p>Your deliverables photos MUST be uploaded to your work order via the online App and MUST be submitted&nbsp;PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.You are required to be onsite&nbsp;<strong>no later than</strong>&nbsp;your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face&nbsp;penalties/non-payment.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Confirmation, Cancellation &amp; Reimbursements:</strong></p><ul><li>You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time</li><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Upon Arrival at site:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER&nbsp;</strong>–&nbsp;if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;to check in.&nbsp;</li><li>Check-In on the Customers Online Work Order Verification Link</li><li>Check-In with Onsite POC and Introduce yourself as a CheckedUp Technician</li><li>Call and Check-In with the Checked-Up Help Desk @<del>*********** ********</del></li><li>&nbsp;Tech MUST contact Essintial at 855-612-2183 for approval to exceed the estimated hours.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements - MUST be completed PRIOR to leaving site:</strong></p><ul><li>Follow/Complete the <strong>“Device Verification &amp; Check-Out”</strong> steps on the customers online<strong>Work Order Verification Link</strong> (Device Verification &amp; Check Out)</li><li>Call the<strong>Checked-Up Help Desk</strong> @&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>to <strong>Check-Out</strong> and <strong>Obtain Work Order Link Completion Code</strong></li><li>Complete the customers <strong>Work Order Verification Link</strong> by entering in the provided Completion Code and the name of the helpdesk agent.</li><li>Call the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Visit/Completion Notes:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Visit Notes</li><li>Name of the CheckedUp Help Desk Agent who checked out / released the technician from the site?</li><li>Did the technician complete the Customers Work Order Verification Link? If so, what is confirmation code that the help desk provided during check out?</li><li># of Devices Installed?</li><li>What issues (if any) did they run into on site?</li><li>Were you requested by the customer drop anything off at FedEx? If so, what is the Return Tracking # (if applicable)</li><li>Did you exceed your estimated onsite hour(s) ? If so, who approved this?</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attachments/Links - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technical Documentation/Instructions &amp; Videos (<em>All Guides/Instructions – copy and paste into Browser</em>)</strong>:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ip_LmthXsZxHcQa3SvYGIntFDXewb_M-</p><p><br></p><p><strong>WO Link Completion Steps / Video Link [<em>How To Complete WO Link</em>]:</strong></p><ul><li>Click this link to watch a quick tutorial on completing the Work Order Verification Link:&nbsp;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VmABXd_bllzGxXPBsSBxEBnyRvBcD-0I/view</li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time & only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.**\n\n**YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.**\n\n**﻿Important Generic Scope Details**: You are being scoped to complete the Installation of a **Digital Wall Board** and/or **TV** (size varies). Please see Problem Description/Scope of Work section for specific service request details.\n\n**Important:**Do Not to Exceed 1 HR ONSITE (per device) without approval from Essintial - At 1 hour onsite (per device), if scope is not complete you MUST call Essintial at 855-612-2183 to obtain approval to exceed.\n\n**Important:** Technicians **MUST** Check-In, Verify/Complete Device Verification, Upload Photos, Check-Out (*obtain completion code by calling CheckedUp Helpdesk)*, and Complete the Customers ***\"Work Order Verification\"*** Link (Real Time). The Link MUST FULLY BE COMPLTED ***PRIOR*** to leaving the site (see special instructions above on where to obtain the link & how to complete the link)\n\n**Important:DO NOT CALL ONSITE POC UNLESS YOU ARE ONSITE AND NEED ACCESS – If you are running late or cannot make it to site you MUST call Essintial.**\n\n**Important**: If you are scoped to service a **TV** (Install / Swap / troubleshooting) – Tech **MUST** **HARDWIRE** – IF POC refuses to allow HARDWIRE….\n\n- Tech MUST report a valid reason **WHY**\n- Tech MUST make sure the WIFI is set to a **PRIVATE** WIFI and **NOT** **GUEST** WIFI\n\n**Required On-site time/window: 1 hour**\n\n*\\*\\*IF YOU ARE UNABLE TO MEET THIS YOU MUST NOTIFY ESSINTIAL VIA PHONE CALL (855-612-2183)\\*\\**\n\n**Problem Description / Scope of Work Instructions :** Tech to install 1 WB\n\n\\*\\*\\*Tech to Call Help Desk to Check In and Check Out, PRIOR to leaving the site. 855-465-4884\n\n\\*\\*\\*Please contact Essintial Support 717-516-3009 with any questions or concerns\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*Please make sure to have the POC Signature on the WO Link PRIOR to leaving the site.\\*\\*\\*\n\nPlease bring firmware update materials, also a PC. The WB MUST be on the Private WiFi.\n\nFirmware Update Processes: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14HZEooARs_DM43mIL3Sd7bFkV5zR2djO&nbsp;(Select the model from the list)\n\nCheckedUp Verification Link <https://checkedup.my.salesforce-sites.com/fieldService/spworkordercheckin?id=0WOPq00000PiaZG>\n\n**Scope Specific Folder Links**\n\n- Installations Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zVY-hoQtbZpkMxX7BOVAzCWQLCY-w_e-?usp=drive_link&nbsp;\n- Android 12 IMAGE Update Files Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LO7a2iJ2QnR1f2gnZZZhh5Zg26hPtJ37?usp=drive_link\n- HMN Media Player Training Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1pzyuBWhlXyz3QOTT6rUFcv5kvg77q0ku?usp=drive_link\n- Troubleshooting Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PId7ic9-yMyA1NnrPUya45MoUGIES6Am?usp=drive_link\n- Troubleshooting Documentation As Of 1-15-24 Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1UKLAEr7mrGJS3S3r3IKowl0KpNVQJF4K?usp=drive_link\n- Tech Requirements/WO Link Management Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12B_SUY87IZoMI0oL6bI9TkoEBIJFI1gn?usp=drive_link\n\n**Important Requirements/Information:**\n\n- Important Technical Documentation - You MUST review and refer to documentations prior to and while onsite\n- Check you Scope of Work Instructions for specific documentation call outs based on your scope\n- All Technical Documentation can be found using this link, use the folders within the links which are broken down by type of scopes (copy & paste into browser): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ip_LmthXsZxHcQa3SvYGIntFDXewb_M-\n- Any issues finding the correct documents please reach out to Ess L1 Technical Support @ 717-516-3009\n- Techs **MUST** represent themselves as a**CheckedUp**Technician while onsite.\n- **Estimated Onsite Hours** = 1 Hour PER Device (must obtain approval to exceed)\n- Do Not to Exceed 1 HR ONSITE (per device) without approval from Essintial - At 1 hour onsite (per device), if scope is not complete you MUST call Essintial at 855-612-2183 to obtain approval.\n- Refer to Scope of Work Details for any special important technician information/requirements- I.E Special Work Order Verification Link Instructions (photo requirements), special tool requirements, parts order/return information, special photo requirements , special onsite instructions, etc.\n- Tech **MUST** Check-InandCheck-Outwith**CheckedUp Help Desk at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- Tech **MUST** Check-Invia**Work Order Verification Link**\n- Tech **MUST** Check Outvia**Work Order Verification Link**(complete Device Verification), then call CheckedUp Helpdesk to check out and obtain the completion code needed to complete the Link\n- Tech **MUST** gain approval from Essintial If the end customer/onsite poc ask to have the device be installed on a stand or table mount and this is not specified in scope / CheckedUp did not advise so originally.\n- Technician **MUST** complete the Customers Work Order Verification Link PRIOR to leaving the sit**e** (see special instructions below on how to complete the link)\n\n**Important Site Information:**\n\n- You must represent yourself as a CheckedUp Technician while onsite.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n- If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.\n- IF YOU ARE UNABLE TO COMPLETE THE SCOPE AS DEFINED IN THE GUIDE & YOUR WORK ORDER YOU MUST CALL THE CHECKEDUP HELPDESK AND ESSINTIAL PRIOR TO LEAVING THE SITE\n- All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.\n- If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies & Procedures #6.\n\n**Required Tools & Material**:\n\n- \\*\\*\\*Please Also Refer to Scope of Work Details for specific tool call outs reported by the customer\\*\\*\\*\n- Printed Documentation must be with you onsite – all documents found in the provided google drive, select the folder(s) that best applies to your specific scope\n- **100ft cat 5 Cable Pull (PER TV)**- if working on a Work Order that has at least 1 Tv (all types of WOs including troubleshooting)\n- **10ft Panduit (White) (PER TV)** - if working on a Work Order that has at least 1 Tv (all types of WOs including troubleshooting)\n- Cell Phone or other device that has phone, camera, and internet ability (for photos and online deliverable)\n- Stud finder\n- Tape measure\n- Phillips screwdriver\n- Phillips drill bit 12” extension (used for inserting the locking screws)\n- Awl (to assist in making holes in wall and cord cover for the screws to be installed)\n- Small level (for leveling the wall bracket)\n- 2-foot level (for leveling the cord cover)\n- Cable Cutter/diagonal cutters (for trimming the cord cover) or hacksaw for cutting cord covers\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 Ends\n- Cable Tester\n- Razorblade\n- Cordless Drill- Only use if necessary, for concrete walls, avoid making noise in the office\n- Drill bits for sheetrock/concrete walls behind sheetrock\n- Hammer to tap in the anchors in the case of concrete walls\n- USB Windows keyboard\n- USB mouse\n- Step ladder (for tv installation if installing TV, DO NOT stand on office chairs)\n- Windows Laptop\n- USB Stick\n- USB- Mini USB cable\n- Toggle bolts\n- Hex Nuts & Machine Screws (specifically for Articulating Mounts)\n\n***\\*\\*Customers Work Order Verification Link (Online Real Time Deliverable) \\*\\****\n\n**This MUST be started upon arrival and fully completed PRIOR to leaving the site location**\n\nTechnician **MUST** use the provided verification link to Check-In, Verify/Complete Device Verification, Upload Photos, and Check-Out Real Time ( Link must fully be completed prior to leaving the site).\n\n LINK CAN BE FOUND IN THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND REF. FIELDS OF YOUR TICKET\n\n- Tech MUST check-in on wo verification link\n- Tech MUST upload photos on wo verification link\n- Tech MUST check-out on wo verficiation link\n- Tech MUST complete the link while onsite ( Verify Device(s), Check-Out, and Complete )\n\n***Work Order Specific Link****:* refer to problem description and/or custom fields of your work order.\n\n***WO Link Completion Steps / Video Link \\[How To\\]***: See Steps below *OR* Click this link to watch a quick tutorial on completing the Work Order Verification Link: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VmABXd_bllzGxXPBsSBxEBnyRvBcD-0I/view\n\n***WO Link Completion Steps:***\n\n1. Refer to problem description for any special call out’s\n2. Click the provided Work Order Verification Link\n3. Verify the Work Order #, # of Devices, & Site information\n4. Click “View Devices”\n5. Select the Device you are working on (*If Multiple Devices – repeat these steps for each device*)\n6. Enter what Room/Site and Floor # the device is located in/on\n7. Enter Notes – i.e. your visit/equipment completion notes\n8. Check the box “Connected & Playing Content”\n9. Upload a photo of the working device/device playing content\n10. Click “Device Verification”\n11. View Device Verification Results\n12. If you get ALL GREEN checks - Click COMPLETE ASSET\n13. If you get any RED checks – call the CheckedUp Help Desk for assistance\n14. Repeat Steps 5-11 for each Device\n15. Click “Complete Order” once all devices have been verified\n16. At Confirmation Page – contact Help Desk to check out and obtain agent name & confirmation code\n17. Using the provided Confirmation Code - enter it into the WO Link to fully complete the online deliverable\n\n**Arriving On Time:** You are required to be onsite **no later than** your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay. **NOTE:** **You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face penalties/non-payment.**\n\n**Physical Requirements:**\n\nMust be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.\n\n**Photographic Deliverable Requirement- You are REQUIRED to capture & submit all of the photos asked of you by your assigned support technician.**\n\nYour deliverables photos MUST be uploaded to your work order via the online App and MUST be submitted PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.You are required to be onsite **no later than** your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay. **NOTE:** **You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face penalties/non-payment.**\n\n**Confirmation, Cancellation & Reimbursements:**\n\n- You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n\n**Upon Arrival at site:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER** – if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- Check-In on the Customers Online Work Order Verification Link\n- Check-In with Onsite POC and Introduce yourself as a CheckedUp Technician\n- Call and Check-In with the Checked-Up Help Desk @\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Tech MUST contact Essintial at 855-612-2183 for approval to exceed the estimated hours.\n\n**Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements - MUST be completed PRIOR to leaving site:**\n\n- Follow/Complete the **“Device Verification & Check-Out”** steps on the customers online**Work Order Verification Link** (Device Verification & Check Out)\n- Call the**Checked-Up Help Desk** @ \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*to **Check-Out** and **Obtain Work Order Link Completion Code**\n- Complete the customers **Work Order Verification Link** by entering in the provided Completion Code and the name of the helpdesk agent.\n- Call the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n\n**Visit/Completion Notes:**\n\n- Detailed Visit Notes\n- Name of the CheckedUp Help Desk Agent who checked out / released the technician from the site?\n- Did the technician complete the Customers Work Order Verification Link? If so, what is confirmation code that the help desk provided during check out?\n- \\# of Devices Installed?\n- What issues (if any) did they run into on site?\n- Were you requested by the customer drop anything off at FedEx? If so, what is the Return Tracking # (if applicable)\n- Did you exceed your estimated onsite hour(s) ? If so, who approved this?\n\n**Attachments/Links - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:**\n\n**Technical Documentation/Instructions & Videos (*All Guides/Instructions – copy and paste into Browser*)**: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ip_LmthXsZxHcQa3SvYGIntFDXewb_M-\n\n**WO Link Completion Steps / Video Link \\[*How To Complete WO Link*\\]:**\n\n- Click this link to watch a quick tutorial on completing the Work Order Verification Link: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VmABXd_bllzGxXPBsSBxEBnyRvBcD-0I/view","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:30","end":"2026-11-03T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":38},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times D