{"job":{"id":20079985,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teceze","title":"Field Service Engineer - Retail Store Device Health Check","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>Technicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.</p><p>The technician will:</p><ul><li>Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Self-checkout devices</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Handheld scanners</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other related store technology equipment</li><li>Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.</li><li>Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.</li><li>Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.</li><li>Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.</li><li>Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.</li><li>Document all remediation activities completed onsite.</li><li>Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.</li><li>Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.</li><li>Take clear photos when required for documentation.</li><li>Clean up the work area after completing the activity.</li></ul><p>Unresolved Issues</p><p>For issues that cannot be resolved onsite:</p><ul><li>Document the device information and issue details.</li><li>Record troubleshooting steps already performed.</li><li>Provide the information to the project team for further action.</li><li>Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.</li></ul><p>Technician Requirements</p><ul><li>Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.</li><li>Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.</li><li>Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.</li><li>Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.</li><li>Must provide professional communication with store personnel.</li><li>Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.</li></ul><p>Visit &amp; Reporting Requirements</p><p>Technician must provide:</p><ul><li>Check-in/check-out confirmation.</li><li>Completed health-check checklist.</li><li>List of devices checked.</li><li>Issues identified.</li><li>Remediation performed.</li><li>Parts/devices used, if applicable.</li><li>Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.</li><li>Required photos/documentation.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\nTechnicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.\n\nThe technician will:\n\n- Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:\n- Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment\n- Self-checkout devices\n- Printers\n- Handheld scanners\n- Other related store technology equipment\n- Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.\n- Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.\n- Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.\n- Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.\n- Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.\n- Document all remediation activities completed onsite.\n- Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.\n- Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.\n- Take clear photos when required for documentation.\n- Clean up the work area after completing the activity.\n\nUnresolved Issues\n\nFor issues that cannot be resolved onsite:\n\n- Document the device information and issue details.\n- Record troubleshooting steps already performed.\n- Provide the information to the project team for further action.\n- Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.\n\nTechnician Requirements\n\n- Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.\n- Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.\n- Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.\n- Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.\n- Must provide professional communication with store personnel.\n- Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.\n\nVisit & Reporting Requirements\n\nTechnician must provide:\n\n- Check-in/check-out confirmation.\n- Completed health-check checklist.\n- List of devices checked.\n- Issues identified.\n- Remediation performed.\n- Parts/devices used, if applicable.\n- Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.\n- Required photos/documentation.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T09:00","end":"2026-10-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":50},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790950134976}
{"job":{"id":19966989,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Direct Source","title":"POS and Register Refresh","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Services:</u></strong></p><p>An overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:</p><ul><li>Check in with Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site to check in.</li><li>Pre-Installation inventory of new hardware at the store location.</li><li>Installation of firewall grounding cable on back-office rack/switch. (select stores)</li><li>Complete back-up of PC1</li><li>Installation of HP Registers and Monitors</li><li>Installation of peripherals:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Epson Receipt Printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cash Drawers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Data Logic Flatbed Scanners</li><li>Test all register equipment with peripherals</li><li>Installation of EDA52 PDT</li><li>Installation of PC2/Thin Client in the breakroom/stockroom</li><li>Move Thin Client into breakroom/stockroom</li><li>Installation of Lexmark Laser Printer in the office</li><li>Installation of HIP printer</li><li>Testing of Thin Client and Laser Printer</li><li>&nbsp;Use a laser tape measure to measure ceiling heights in the sales floor and stockroom. Record the ceiling heights and ceiling types/materials on the SAF, and report them to the DSI Support Desk.</li><li>Clean-up of all legacy equipment and work areas need to be neat</li><li>Package all old equipment to return to Greentech or Direct Source per installation guide</li><li>Obtain a full set of deliverables per installation guide</li><li>Ensure a placard with Store Number, Date, Register Number, and Tech Name is used in all images provided</li><li>&nbsp;Check out with Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code on the SAF (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</li><li>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal via the Mobile App.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Technician Required Equipment, Tools, &amp; Hardware:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician is required to have the following list of equipment and materials that will be used throughout the Technician's agreed upon assignment to this project.</p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p><p>Standard Tool Kit (multi-size screw drivers, hammer, pliers, tape measurer, hex key set etc.)</p><p>Corded or cordless Drill with fully charged battery and back-up battery, and drill bits.</p><p>Flexible Bit Extender</p><p>Cable Tester/Toner</p><p>EZ Out</p><p>Qty 3 - #10 ¾ inch self-tapping screws&nbsp;<strong>PER REGISTER/LANE</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>For use on wooden counters</strong></li><li>&nbsp;Tech must supply these for each monitor. Lane counts available on DSI Portal.</li></ul><p><strong>Qty 4&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"><u>PER REGISTER/LANE</u>&nbsp;</strong>-<strong>&nbsp;M4 x 0.7, 10mm Metric Pan Head Phillips</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;For use mounting new HP monitors to existing pole mounts.</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech must supply 4 screws for each monitor. Lane counts available on DSI Portal.</li></ul><p><strong>Qty 1 </strong>&ndash; Ground lug</p><p><strong>Qty 1 </strong>&ndash; 10-32 machine screw (rack screw) only used if you're attaching directly to the data rack and not the WattBox)</p><p><strong>Qty 1 </strong>&ndash; Eyelet ring terminal</p><p><strong>Qty 1 </strong>&ndash; External tooth lock washers</p><p>Laser tape measure for measuring ceiling heights in the sales floor and stockroom.</p><p>Black Velcro to secure cables as needed (Zip ties are not acceptable).</p><p>Elmer's Natural Wood Filler</p><p>Sharpies/Markers</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Canned Air (recommended)</p><p>Packing Tape (as back up if not available at store)</p><p>Crimper/wire snips</p><p>Sandpaper or wire brush</p><p>Cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier.</p><p>Printed copy of the Technical Guide and any other required project paperwork.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Project Summary:</u>&nbsp;</strong>The Technician shall provide services to DSI and their client for the purpose of and installation of registers nationwide. As a whole, Direct Source is providing hardware integration and installation services. All Services provided by the Technician herein are subject to the terms set forth in this Agreement.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Project Schedule</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Direct Source's project duration is May 2026 to October 2026. The Technician is to refer to the specific schedule provided on the Direct Source Portal for specific site start/end dates. Because the project includes specific coordination of labor resources and specific hardware arrival requirements, Direct Source or the End Customer are the only parties authorized to change the assigned Technician's schedule. Schedules CANNOT be changed or adjusted by the Technician. Direct Source shall not be responsible for any costs or expenses incurred by the Technician as a result of the change in schedule.</p><p>All installation work completed by the Technician shall be Sunday through Wednesday after store close local time. Technician may not work outside of these dates and times without permission from DSI Project Management and is expected to stay on site until work is complete or the Technician has been released by the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Project Preparation/ Orientation</u>:&nbsp;The Technician who will be onsite</strong>, must complete a mandatory&nbsp;conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned install unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician's will learn Direct Source's and End Client's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>NEW DSI Technician Requirements Only:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Successful completion of a criminal background/credit check will be required for any new technician to Direct Source Inc.</li><li>Failure to successfully pass a criminal background/credit check will result in the disqualification of the Technician to participate in any End Customer or other DSI projects.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Payment Amounts</u>:</strong>&nbsp;Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel.&nbsp;No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing.&nbsp;For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p><p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate</u>:</strong>&nbsp;$60.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total of estimated hours of onsite time as designated per store, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15- minute increments.&nbsp;T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.</p><p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain&nbsp;<strong><u>pre-approval</u></strong>&nbsp;for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p><p><strong><u>Store Revisits</u></strong>: Store revisits will be paid at $60.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables &amp; Reporting:</u></strong>&nbsp;Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide.&nbsp;All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal at the time of check out via the Mobile app. SAF is due within 24 hours of install completion.</p><ul><li>Required deliverables are the following:</li><li>Completed Service Acceptance Form (SAF)</li><li>Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions that are listed in the back of the installation guide.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Direct Source Obligations:</u></strong>&nbsp;Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules,&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">including quantity of registers and which devices will be swapped at each location.</span>.&nbsp;All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.</p><p>Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:</p><p>DSI Technical (Installation) Guide.</p><p>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan.</p><p>Service Acceptance Form (SAF)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR)</u>:</strong></p><p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk.&nbsp;<strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Provider - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of provider, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge.</li><li>Any site that is RESCHEDULED; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed</li><li>Any Site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee</li><li>Any sire that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Service Acceptance:</u></strong>&nbsp;All service tasks must be completed, in order, as specified in the Technical Guide unless otherwise expressly approved by the DSI Project Manager in writing. Local End Customer DOES NOT have the authorization to change service tasks. If the End Customer is asking for you to do any out of scope work, call the DSI Help Desk immediately.</p><p>Failure to fully and accurately complete or deliver on time, all required deliverables, or failure to deliver Services would result in the Service Order being deemed incomplete.&nbsp;Direct Source agrees to notify the Technician within 5 days of the site's completion, the specific nature of any such failure to conform to the contracted service and afford the Technician the opportunity to remedy such failure in a mutually agreeable and timely fashion.</p><p><strong><u>Service Level Agreements:&nbsp;</u>&nbsp;</strong><em>All below dates are from the day of the installation date.</em></p><p>Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p><p>Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Provider received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p><p>DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deductions:&nbsp;</u></strong>Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged.&nbsp;Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Provider and its providers. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Expectations &amp; Requirements</u></strong><u>:</u>&nbsp;Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times.&nbsp;Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><p><strong><u>Allowed:</u></strong>&nbsp;Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts</p><p><strong><u>Not Allowed:</u></strong>&nbsp;Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Presentation:</u></strong></p><p>Technicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion.&nbsp;If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to remove Technician from the project.&nbsp;Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.</p><p><strong>Travel Arrangements:</strong></p><ul><li>Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.</li><li>Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.</li><li>Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.</li><li>Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p><strong>1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to the Direct Source Portal - No Fee Incurred</strong></p><p><strong>2 Business Days (Late penalties&nbsp;30% per affected site Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld):&nbsp;</strong>If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.&nbsp;The Technician will have up to the&nbsp;3rd&nbsp;business day to:&nbsp;<strong>A)</strong>&nbsp;submit the outstanding item(s) or&nbsp;<strong>B)</strong>&nbsp;return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</p><p><strong>5 Business Days (Late penalties&nbsp;The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables):&nbsp;</strong>In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables, will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the affected site(s).</p><p>Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide and that is not received by the end of&nbsp;business&nbsp;of scheduled installation date.&nbsp;&nbsp;This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p><p>Late fee penalties will not be waived unless the Technician received written notice from the Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p>","markdown":"**Scope of Services:**\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n- Check in with Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site to check in.\n- Pre-Installation inventory of new hardware at the store location.\n- Installation of firewall grounding cable on back-office rack/switch. (select stores)\n- Complete back-up of PC1\n- Installation of HP Registers and Monitors\n- Installation of peripherals:\n- Epson Receipt Printers\n- Cash Drawers\n- Data Logic Flatbed Scanners\n- Test all register equipment with peripherals\n- Installation of EDA52 PDT\n- Installation of PC2/Thin Client in the breakroom/stockroom\n- Move Thin Client into breakroom/stockroom\n- Installation of Lexmark Laser Printer in the office\n- Installation of HIP printer\n- Testing of Thin Client and Laser Printer\n- Use a laser tape measure to measure ceiling heights in the sales floor and stockroom. Record the ceiling heights and ceiling types/materials on the SAF, and report them to the DSI Support Desk.\n- Clean-up of all legacy equipment and work areas need to be neat\n- Package all old equipment to return to Greentech or Direct Source per installation guide\n- Obtain a full set of deliverables per installation guide\n- Ensure a placard with Store Number, Date, Register Number, and Tech Name is used in all images provided\n- Check out with Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code on the SAF (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n- Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal via the Mobile App.\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools, & Hardware:** Technician is required to have the following list of equipment and materials that will be used throughout the Technician's agreed upon assignment to this project.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\nStandard Tool Kit (multi-size screw drivers, hammer, pliers, tape measurer, hex key set etc.)\n\nCorded or cordless Drill with fully charged battery and back-up battery, and drill bits.\n\nFlexible Bit Extender\n\nCable Tester/Toner\n\nEZ Out\n\nQty 3 - #10 ¾ inch self-tapping screws **PER REGISTER/LANE**\n\n- **For use on wooden counters**\n- Tech must supply these for each monitor. Lane counts available on DSI Portal.\n\n**Qty 4** **PER REGISTER/LANE** - **M4 x 0.7, 10mm Metric Pan Head Phillips**\n\n- For use mounting new HP monitors to existing pole mounts.\n- Tech must supply 4 screws for each monitor. Lane counts available on DSI Portal.\n\n**Qty 1** – Ground lug\n\n**Qty 1** – 10-32 machine screw (rack screw) only used if you're attaching directly to the data rack and not the WattBox)\n\n**Qty 1** – Eyelet ring terminal\n\n**Qty 1** – External tooth lock washers\n\nLaser tape measure for measuring ceiling heights in the sales floor and stockroom.\n\nBlack Velcro to secure cables as needed (Zip ties are not acceptable).\n\nElmer's Natural Wood Filler\n\nSharpies/Markers\n\nFlashlight\n\nCanned Air (recommended)\n\nPacking Tape (as back up if not available at store)\n\nCrimper/wire snips\n\nSandpaper or wire brush\n\nCell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier.\n\nPrinted copy of the Technical Guide and any other required project paperwork.\n\n**Project Summary:** The Technician shall provide services to DSI and their client for the purpose of and installation of registers nationwide. As a whole, Direct Source is providing hardware integration and installation services. All Services provided by the Technician herein are subject to the terms set forth in this Agreement.\n\n**Project Schedule:** Direct Source's project duration is May 2026 to October 2026. The Technician is to refer to the specific schedule provided on the Direct Source Portal for specific site start/end dates. Because the project includes specific coordination of labor resources and specific hardware arrival requirements, Direct Source or the End Customer are the only parties authorized to change the assigned Technician's schedule. Schedules CANNOT be changed or adjusted by the Technician. Direct Source shall not be responsible for any costs or expenses incurred by the Technician as a result of the change in schedule.\n\nAll installation work completed by the Technician shall be Sunday through Wednesday after store close local time. Technician may not work outside of these dates and times without permission from DSI Project Management and is expected to stay on site until work is complete or the Technician has been released by the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager.\n\n**Project Preparation/ Orientation: The Technician who will be onsite**, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned install unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician's will learn Direct Source's and End Client's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.\n\n**NEW DSI Technician Requirements Only:**\n\n- Successful completion of a criminal background/credit check will be required for any new technician to Direct Source Inc.\n- Failure to successfully pass a criminal background/credit check will result in the disqualification of the Technician to participate in any End Customer or other DSI projects.\n\n**Payment Amounts:** Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate:** $60.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total of estimated hours of onsite time as designated per store, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15- minute increments. T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain **pre-approval** for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits**: Store revisits will be paid at $60.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting:** Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal at the time of check out via the Mobile app. SAF is due within 24 hours of install completion.\n\n- Required deliverables are the following:\n- Completed Service Acceptance Form (SAF)\n- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions that are listed in the back of the installation guide.\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:** Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules, including quantity of registers and which devices will be swapped at each location.. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.\n\nDirect Source Project Related Documents includes:\n\nDSI Technical (Installation) Guide.\n\nDirect Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan.\n\nService Acceptance Form (SAF)\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\n**Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:**\n\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Provider - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of provider, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&M + Contracted Trip Charge.\n- Any site that is RESCHEDULED; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed\n- Any Site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee\n- Any sire that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed.\n\n**Service Acceptance:** All service tasks must be completed, in order, as specified in the Technical Guide unless otherwise expressly approved by the DSI Project Manager in writing. Local End Customer DOES NOT have the authorization to change service tasks. If the End Customer is asking for you to do any out of scope work, call the DSI Help Desk immediately.\n\nFailure to fully and accurately complete or deliver on time, all required deliverables, or failure to deliver Services would result in the Service Order being deemed incomplete. Direct Source agrees to notify the Technician within 5 days of the site's completion, the specific nature of any such failure to conform to the contracted service and afford the Technician the opportunity to remedy such failure in a mutually agreeable and timely fashion.\n\n**Service Level Agreements:** *All below dates are from the day of the installation date.*\n\nLate deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\nLate fee penalties will not be waived unless Provider received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\nDSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.\n\n**Deductions:** Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Provider and its providers. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.\n\n**Expectations & Requirements**: Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n**Allowed:** Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts\n\n**Not Allowed:** Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).\n\n**Presentation:**\n\nTechnicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to remove Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.\n\n**Travel Arrangements:**\n\n- Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.\n- Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.\n- Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.\n- Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n**1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to the Direct Source Portal - No Fee Incurred**\n\n**2 Business Days (Late penalties 30% per affected site Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld):** If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding. The Technician will have up to the 3rd business day to: **A)** submit the outstanding item(s) or **B)** return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n\n**5 Business Days (Late penalties The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables):** In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables, will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the affected site(s).\n\nLate deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide and that is not received by the end of business of scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\nLate fee penalties will not be waived unless the Technician received written notice from the Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T20:00","end":"2026-10-20T28:00"},"payRange":{"min":480,"max":480},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-1