{"job":{"id":"9660460088","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"JTI NETWORK LLC","title":"(VARICH03/0017887) - WM - Installation Phase - 10-12FT LADDER + PPE REQUIRED","description":"<p><strong>Good, clean and constant communication before the activity and while work on site is essential.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ONLY LEAVE THE SITE AFTER COMPLETING THE TASK.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Note: Field Engineer needs to carry photo identity proof (Driving license or any govt affiliated photo ID).</u></em></strong></p><p>====================================================</p><p>Firewalls to be replaced: TBD</p><p>Access Points to be replaced: TBD</p><p>=====================================================</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Summary:</em></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><em>Execute halfday site surveys and halfday installs across a multiple site retail program. Tasks include racking firewalls, establishing console access for remote configuration, swapping APs using existing cabling/brackets, and documenting work with photo standards and site visit reports.</em></li><li><em>Key responsibilities:</em></li><li><em>Conduct physical site surveys: AP location validation; rack/power/cable pathway checks; photo documentation</em></li><li><em>Install activities: mount firewalls hardware; connect power/ethernet; establish console session per runbook</em></li><li><em>Replace APs; verify link/PoE; tidy rack/cabling; restore site to working order</em></li><li><em>Adhere to runbooks, checklists, and remote engineer instructions; join bridge calls on arrival/departure</em></li><li><em>Submit complete documentation (photos, survey forms, SVR) within 24 hours</em></li><li><em>Minimum qualifications:</em></li><li><em>1-3 years in Smart Hands/field services; competent with rack hardware, console connectivity, and AP swaps</em></li><li><em>Basic networking knowledge (Layer 1 and 2, PoE, port identification) and terminal/console tools</em></li><li><em>Strong documentation habits (clear photos, accurate notes); English communication with remote NOC/engineers</em></li><li><em>Safety awareness: ladder use and work-at-height for ceiling APs; PPE compliance per site policy</em></li><li><em>Reliable transportation; ability to meet retail scheduling windows; smartphone with data for checkings/photos</em></li><li><em>Tools required:</em></li><li><em>Laptop with terminal emulator (e.g., PuTTY), USB?serial drivers; console cables/adapters</em></li><li><em>Hand tools set; cage nuts/screws; labeler and consumables; Velcro; patch cords; flashlight</em></li><li><em>Smartphone with camera; mobile hotspot; access to collaboration apps (Teams/Zoom) as directed</em></li><li><em>Ladder familiarity; ability to bring/use ladder when required by dispatch</em></li><li><em>Nice to have (preferred):</em></li><li><em>Experience in high?volume retail rollouts; basic Aruba/Fortinet familiarity (physical handling, LEDs, console pinouts)</em></li><li><em>Light cable testing tools (tone/probe) and ability to trace/label drops</em></li><li><em>Working conditions:</em></li><li><em>Halfday survey/install windows; some after?hours as scheduled; repetitive, details oriented tasks across many sites</em></li><li><em>Reporting line:</em></li></ul><p><em>Reports to Program Dispatch/PM; follows instructions from remote implementation engineers during console/config steps</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Migration will be performed at this stage of the Project.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-10T13:00","end":"2026-10-10T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":0},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"}