{"job":{"id":20082443,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"Troubleshoot (1) WAP - 10ft Ladder Needed","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code: </strong></p><p>Business Casual</p>Background<ul><li>Provide onsite support to troubleshoot <strong>(1) Wireless Access Point (WAP)</strong> that was previously installed.</li><li>The WAP is experiencing connectivity and/or operational issues and requires onsite diagnosis and remediation.</li></ul>Scope of Work<ul><li>Coordinate with EPLUS and/or remote engineering support upon arrival.</li><li>Access and inspect the installed WAP located in a <strong>12 ft drop-ceiling environment</strong>.</li><li>Verify physical installation, mounting integrity, and cabling connections.</li><li>Inspect network cabling between the WAP, patch panel, and switch.</li><li>Verify switch port status and PoE connectivity.</li><li>Test network cabling and validate end-to-end connectivity.</li><li>Confirm the WAP is receiving power and network connectivity.</li><li>Check for patching, configuration, connectivity, or cabling-related issues.</li><li>Reseat and reconnect network cables as needed.</li><li>Assist remote support with diagnostics, testing, and validation.</li><li>Verify the WAP successfully connects to the network and functions properly.</li><li>Perform basic troubleshooting within scope to restore service.</li><li>Document findings and any issues requiring escalation.</li><li>Maintain a clean and safe work area throughout the visit.</li><li>Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photos.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong></p><p><strong>Ladder suitable for 12 ft ceiling height</strong></p><p>Laptop with Ethernet port (or USB-to-Ethernet adapter)</p><p>Network cable tester</p><p>Patch cables (Cat5e/Cat6)</p><p>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)</p><p>Flashlight or headlamp for above-ceiling visibility</p><p>Labeling materials</p><p>Mobile phone for coordination with EPLUS and remote support</p><p>Camera-enabled device for documentation and photos</p><p>PPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements </em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Check your email for the sign‑off form, which will be sent the day before the dispatch from Eplus. Notify SGNet if you do not receive the email.</li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks </em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent E-Plus while onsite</li><li>&nbsp;Check in with SGNet at the 888 number in Confidential Section</li><li>&nbsp;Work with Verizon Support</li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Completed Verizon sign-off form</li><li>Check out of work order with SG to review deliverables and receive check-out code</li><li>Before and After Pictures</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process: </strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy </strong></p><p>Contact SGNet</p>","markdown":"**Dress Code:**\n\nBusiness Casual\n\nBackground- Provide onsite support to troubleshoot **(1) Wireless Access Point (WAP)** that was previously installed.\n- The WAP is experiencing connectivity and/or operational issues and requires onsite diagnosis and remediation.\n\nScope of Work- Coordinate with EPLUS and/or remote engineering support upon arrival.\n- Access and inspect the installed WAP located in a **12 ft drop-ceiling environment**.\n- Verify physical installation, mounting integrity, and cabling connections.\n- Inspect network cabling between the WAP, patch panel, and switch.\n- Verify switch port status and PoE connectivity.\n- Test network cabling and validate end-to-end connectivity.\n- Confirm the WAP is receiving power and network connectivity.\n- Check for patching, configuration, connectivity, or cabling-related issues.\n- Reseat and reconnect network cables as needed.\n- Assist remote support with diagnostics, testing, and validation.\n- Verify the WAP successfully connects to the network and functions properly.\n- Perform basic troubleshooting within scope to restore service.\n- Document findings and any issues requiring escalation.\n- Maintain a clean and safe work area throughout the visit.\n- Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photos.\n\n**Required Tools & Equipment**\n\n**Ladder suitable for 12 ft ceiling height**\n\nLaptop with Ethernet port (or USB-to-Ethernet adapter)\n\nNetwork cable tester\n\nPatch cables (Cat5e/Cat6)\n\nBasic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)\n\nFlashlight or headlamp for above-ceiling visibility\n\nLabeling materials\n\nMobile phone for coordination with EPLUS and remote support\n\nCamera-enabled device for documentation and photos\n\nPPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves)\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Check your email for the sign‑off form, which will be sent the day before the dispatch from Eplus. Notify SGNet if you do not receive the email.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent E-Plus while onsite\n2. Check in with SGNet at the 888 number in Confidential Section\n3. Work with Verizon Support\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Completed Verizon sign-off form\n2. Check out of work order with SG to review deliverables and receive check-out code\n3. Before and After Pictures\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\nContact SGNet","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T09:15","end":"2026-10-08T11:15"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.86086023095905},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low V