{"job":{"id":20082754,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Staley Technologies","title":"Tech with LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE is Needed to replace existing firewall.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech with LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE is Needed to replace existing firewall.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Customer Notes: Replacement of Firewall.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>It's a relatively simple process:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Plug in the new firewall (shipped to school)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Move the cables from the old firewall to the new firewall, keeping them plugged into the same port (e/g cable from port 1 on old firewall goes to port 1 on new firewall, but keep in mind the ports moved around a bit on the latest model. See attached picture for color coded diagram of what goes where)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Test to confirm everything is working right (Please let me know when you are doing the installation as I will need to make a change on my end as well)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Unplug old firewall and ship it back in the new firewall packaging.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>IT Support – Zach Bresser 989-708-4444</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Onsite Contact: Sherry Ballentine (919) 695-9900</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Call 501-320-4738 for access issues, general technical support.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>EXPECTATIONS - TECH REQUIREMENTS</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>===========================</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MUST have Staley badge and it MUST be visible on your person.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MUST conduct yourself in a professional manner within Staley’s code of conduct.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MUST work with the senior management personnel for review, work, test and signoff.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MUST work with Customer Support to ensure proper updates take place.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>STANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>USB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>USB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>PRECISE SCREWDRIVERS</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>WIRE STRIPPERS</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>CRIMPER</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>TONER</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>LABELMAKER</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>CABLE TESTER</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Contact Staley Support 501-320-4738 with tool issues.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>DO NOT tell Customer you don’t have the tools needed.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MATERIALS</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>QTY DESCRIPTION</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>======================================</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>~ Velcro</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>DO NOT tell the customer you don’t have the materials needed.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>TASK</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>1) Meet with site personnel/management and introduce yourself.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>a) Review details of service request with store personnel/management.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>2) Replace firewall - Plug in the new firewall</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Move the cables from the old firewall to the new firewall, keeping them plugged into the same port (e/g cable from port 1 on old firewall goes to port 1 on new firewall, but keep in mind the ports moved around a bit on the latest model. See attached picture for color coded diagram of what goes where)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Test to confirm everything is working right (Please let me know when you are doing the installation as I will need to make a change on my end as well)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*Unplug old firewall and ship it back in the new firewall packaging.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>a) IT Support – Zach Bresser 989-708-4444</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>3) Take Before and After Pictures - Check out with IT Support before leaving the site</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>4) Test results (required) attach to work order or Email to ServiceDocs@staleyinc.com within 24 hours of leaving the site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>a) Subject line of the email should contain the following: “ST-XXXXXX Test Results\".</p>","markdown":"**DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE**\n\nTech with LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE is Needed to replace existing firewall.\n\n.\n\nCustomer Notes: Replacement of Firewall.\n\nIt's a relatively simple process:\n\nPlug in the new firewall (shipped to school)\n\nMove the cables from the old firewall to the new firewall, keeping them plugged into the same port (e/g cable from port 1 on old firewall goes to port 1 on new firewall, but keep in mind the ports moved around a bit on the latest model. See attached picture for color coded diagram of what goes where)\n\nTest to confirm everything is working right (Please let me know when you are doing the installation as I will need to make a change on my end as well)\n\nUnplug old firewall and ship it back in the new firewall packaging.\n\n.\n\nIT Support – Zach Bresser 989-708-4444\n\n.\n\nOnsite Contact: Sherry Ballentine (919) 695-9900\n\nCall 501-320-4738 for access issues, general technical support.\n\n\\--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEXPECTATIONS - TECH REQUIREMENTS\n\n===========================\n\nMUST have Staley badge and it MUST be visible on your person.\n\nMUST conduct yourself in a professional manner within Staley’s code of conduct.\n\nMUST work with the senior management personnel for review, work, test and signoff.\n\nMUST work with Customer Support to ensure proper updates take place.\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:\n\n.\n\nSTANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)\n\nLAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE\n\nUSB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR\n\nUSB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE\n\nPRECISE SCREWDRIVERS\n\nWIRE STRIPPERS\n\nCRIMPER\n\nTONER\n\nLABELMAKER\n\nCABLE TESTER\n\n.\n\nContact Staley Support 501-320-4738 with tool issues.\n\nDO NOT tell Customer you don’t have the tools needed.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMATERIALS\n\nQTY DESCRIPTION\n\n======================================\n\n~ Velcro\n\n.\n\nDO NOT tell the customer you don’t have the materials needed.\n\n\\----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTASK\n\n.\n\n1\\) Meet with site personnel/management and introduce yourself.\n\na) Review details of service request with store personnel/management.\n\n.\n\n2\\) Replace firewall - Plug in the new firewall\n\nMove the cables from the old firewall to the new firewall, keeping them plugged into the same port (e/g cable from port 1 on old firewall goes to port 1 on new firewall, but keep in mind the ports moved around a bit on the latest model. See attached picture for color coded diagram of what goes where)\n\nTest to confirm everything is working right (Please let me know when you are doing the installation as I will need to make a change on my end as well)\n\n\\*Unplug old firewall and ship it back in the new firewall packaging.\n\na) IT Support – Zach Bresser 989-708-4444\n\n.\n\n3\\) Take Before and After Pictures - Check out with IT Support before leaving the site\n\n.\n\n4\\) Test results (required) attach to work order or Email to ServiceDocs@staleyinc.com within 24 hours of leaving the site.\n\na) Subject line of the email should contain the following: “ST-XXXXXX Test Results\".","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T16:00","end":"2026-10-05T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":11.562571347313002},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 (countered: $280) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790957415454}
{"job":{"id":20082673,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | KIOSK SSD Card Swaps","description":{"html":"<p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Important</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician is installing SSD Card in Drivers Shower Kiosk. PC/POS hardware, SSD/HD swap, Windows OS basics, follow written procedures, basic</p><p>troubleshooting.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Task:</strong>&nbsp;Swap/replace SSD(s) and apply new asset tag(s) on Driver/Shower kiosks (1–3 devices/site). Follow the SSD Swap Guide for the step-by-step procedure.</li><li><strong>Represent yourself as:</strong>&nbsp;Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America.</li><li><strong>Possible kiosk locations (vary by site):</strong>&nbsp;Front Counter, Truck Side, Truck Service Building. (Store General Manager will know what kiosk are in scope and where the kiosk are located)</li><li><strong>Kiosk naming (location):</strong>&nbsp;01=Front Counter, 02=Truck Side, 03=Truck Service Building.</li><li><strong>Pre-test app:</strong>&nbsp;Download TA TruckSmart&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;arriving (used for post-swap testing; see guide).</li><li><strong>Parts at site:</strong>&nbsp;New SSD(s) + asset tag(s) shipped to Store GM (white box with colored label). If missing, contact TSC Support.</li><li><strong>Handle panels carefully:</strong>&nbsp;tabs are fragile.</li><li><strong>Asset tag rule:</strong>&nbsp;Remove old tags from screen + base, then place the new tag&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">ON THE BASE ONLY (NOT THE SCREEN).</strong></li><li><strong>Return old SSD(s):</strong>&nbsp;Put old SSD(s) in the bag from the new SSD(s), re-box, apply return label, and hand to the Store GM. (Capture a photo of the contents inside the box before closing)</li><li><strong>Deliverable (required before leaving):</strong>&nbsp;Submit deliverable + required photos and have it reviewed/approved by Essintial Project Tech Support&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;you depart.</li><li><strong>Deliverable Photo Requirements!!!</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Required photos:</strong>&nbsp;(1) New asset tag installed on base. (2) Kiosk powered on showing both payment options available (not greyed out). (3) SSD Card packed up inside the return box</li><li>Technicians are&nbsp;<strong>REQUIRED</strong>&nbsp;to complete an Essintial Online Deliverable + have the deliverable reviewed/approved&nbsp;<strong>PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to leaving the site. Contact&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support Team at&nbsp;717-516-3009.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Access Issues / Technical Issues Encountered Onsite</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Escalate to TSC Support</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Standard/Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Anti-Static Wrist Strap (Tether grounded, not air gapped),</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Important Technician Information &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">These are LIVE environments, and technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;Be Respectful</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">You Must be able to lift/carry 50 lbs and work standing, kneeling, and bending for extended periods.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Work will be completed during 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM Eastern</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;</strong>1-2 Hours, expect 15-30 minutes per device</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>