{"job":{"id":20089042,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Schedule Turn Up - Store #606: 1477 Boone Station Dr, Burlington, NC 27215 - 00151364","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*******CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! ********</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>Guidecx Project: https://app.guidecx.com/app/projects/7d9d534e-26d6-430f-82f1-8e218a13d397</p>\n<p>Project Manager: Anna Cond</p>\n<p>DISPATCH REQUEST</p>\n<p>Address:</p>\n<p>1477 Boone Station Dr.</p>\n<p>Burlington, NC 27215</p>\n<p>Company Name: Five Below- Store #606</p>\n<p>Dispatch date/time: Tuesday- 10/6/26- Tech to arrive by 10am</p>\n<p>Local Contact: Manager on Duty</p>\n<p>PLEASE NOTE- We already have a 24M/3M ATT Broadband Circuit up at this location and this Spectrum circuit will be replacing that here. Please make sure that the tech removes any ATT equipment and recycles it*</p>\n<p>We are installing a new 500M/20M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP&gt; Spectrum. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit; ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point-of-sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.</p>\n<p>Spectrum Circuit IP Info:</p>\n<p><del>******* ** ******** ************</del></p>\n<p><del>******* ** ******** ************</del></p>\n<p><del>** ****** ***** ***************</del></p>\n<p>PLEASE NOTE- We already have a 24M/3M ATT Broadband Circuit up at this location and this Spectrum circuit will be replacing that here. Please make sure that the tech removes any ATT equipment and recycles it*</p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<p>• Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************</del></p>\n<p>• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</p>\n<p>• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</p>\n<p>• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),<strong>350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools</strong>. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <strong>206-494-6399</strong></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email <strong>turnups@sangoma.com</strong> with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call<strong>206-494-6399</strong>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nGuidecx Project: <https://app.guidecx.com/app/projects/7d9d534e-26d6-430f-82f1-8e218a13d397>\n\nProject Manager: Anna Cond\n\nDISPATCH REQUEST\n\nAddress:\n\n1477 Boone Station Dr.\n\nBurlington, NC 27215\n\nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #606\n\nDispatch date/time: Tuesday- 10/6/26- Tech to arrive by 10am\n\nLocal Contact: Manager on Duty\n\nPLEASE NOTE- We already have a 24M/3M ATT Broadband Circuit up at this location and this Spectrum circuit will be replacing that here. Please make sure that the tech removes any ATT equipment and recycles it\\*\n\nWe are installing a new 500M/20M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP> Spectrum. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit; ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point-of-sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.\n\nSpectrum Circuit IP Info:\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nPLEASE NOTE- We already have a 24M/3M ATT Broadband Circuit up at this location and this Spectrum circuit will be replacing that here. Please make sure that the tech removes any ATT equipment and recycles it\\*\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n\n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),**350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools**. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at **206-494-6399**\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email **turnups@sangoma.com** with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call**206-494-6399**with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T10:00","end":"2026-10-06T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":45.169131915633955},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790973981585}
{"job":{"id":20089259,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"#298308 Cabling and 1 Outdoor Verkada Camera and Gateway Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>TECHNICIAN CHECK-IN &amp; CHECK-OUT</strong></p><p><strong>• Call TRCA at (940) 381-8569 immediately upon arrival and before departure.</strong></p><p><strong>• You will receive check-in/out codes — write these on the TRCA Work Order.</strong></p><p><strong>CONTACTS</strong></p><p>Site Contact: <del>*** ***** ** ***</del></p><p>Verkada Configuration Contact: <del>****** *********** ** ********* *** ****** ******* *** **** **** *************** ***** ** ***** ************</del></p><p><strong>BEFORE YOU BEGIN</strong></p><p>Read the attached Full Scope of Work PDF and attachments carefully. If you have questions, call TRCA before going on site.</p><p><strong>REFERENCE DOCUMENTS</strong></p><p>• Full Scope of Work PDF</p><p>• Floor Plan</p><p>• Verkada Install Form</p><p>• Camera Installation Mistakes to Avoid</p><p>• PROPERLY SEALING OUTDOOR CAMERAS - MUST READ IF OUTDOOR CAMERAS ARE BEING INSTALLED</p><p>• DRAIN WIRE IMPORTANCE PLEASE READ</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">GC31-E Installation Instructions</span></p><p><strong>HELPFUL RESOURCES</strong></p><p>• All Verkada install/setup guides are available for free:</p><p>• https://www.verkada.com/docs</p><p>• Type the product part number into the search bar to view guides and videos.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>For Basic Troubleshooting if needed:</strong></p><p>Test the cable, confirm it passes.</p><p>Verify link light on the switch port and power light on the switch port.</p><p>Take camera directly to the switch and short wire it on the port, give it 3-4 minutes, notate the LED blinking lights.</p><p>Camera LED Status Indicators:</p><p>https://help.verkada.com/verkada-cameras/installation/camera-led-status-indicators</p><p>24/7 Verkada Support: (<del>**** ******** ***</del> Before calling, TRCA will need to provide you with support token, the customer ID and the phone number.</p><p>IMPORTANT!!! If Verkada offers to do an RMA the following email address MUST be provided to them: amy.bourzikas@trca.com</p><p><br></p><p><strong>HARDWARE INVENTORY &amp; DOCUMENTATION – MANDATORY</strong></p><p>Inventory all Verkada hardware immediately upon arrival.</p><p>!! Report any missing items to TRCA immediately.</p><p>While completing the camera inventory, please follow the steps below to ensure a smooth setup in Verkada Command:</p><p><strong>Labeling Boxes:</strong></p><p>• As you unpack and inventory the cameras, label each camera box according to its planned location on the floor plan (e.g., CAM 1, CAM 2, CAM 3, etc.).</p><p>• These labels should correspond to the designated camera locations on the project’s floor plan.</p><p><strong>Install Form:</strong></p><p>• On the install form, in the first column (next to each camera’s part #), write the camera number (CAM #) that corresponds to its labeled location.</p><p>• Double-check that each camera number matches its planned location on the floor plan.</p><p><strong>Submit Documentation:</strong></p><p>• Once the form is complete, send it to SST@TRCA.com.</p><p>• This documentation will be used to correctly set up and label the cameras within Verkada Command.</p><p>If you have any questions or need clarification during the process, don’t hesitate to reach out to TRCA.</p><p><strong>SHIPMENT NOTES AND EQUIPMENT RESPONSIBILITY</strong></p><p><strong>Items shipped to site by TRCA:</strong></p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;GC31-E-HW&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;GC31 Cellular Gateway, Outdoor</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ACC-POE-90W-E-NA&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Outdoor 90W PoE++ (802.3bt-2018) Injector,</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CD53-256E-HW&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verkada CD53-E Outdoor Dome Camera,</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ACC-MNT-ANGLE-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verkada Angle mount&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Items provided by technician:</strong></p><p>50ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6 Cable&nbsp;</p><p>3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;RJ45</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;weather proof sealant 1 tube</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6 outdoor patch cord 3' white</p><p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc. consumables/ mounting hardware, cables , power strip/surge protector if needed and possible power/extension cord to be provided by the tech.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>NETWORK PROTOCOL</strong></p><p>• Do not plug any switch into the network (even temporarily) without prior TRCA approval.</p><p><strong>INSTALLATION SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><p>Installation and cabling for 1 Verkada camera, 1 Cellular Gateway, and 1 ACC-POE-Injector for the gateway.</p><p>Camera and gateway are to be installed at ladder serviceable height.&nbsp;</p><p>There is power inside the building but will require an extension cord to reach.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Communicate work areas to site contact and provide notice if anything must be moved to avoid delays.</p><p>• Pull and label cable for cameras (if cabling is already in place, skip this step)</p><p>• Provide 5' service loop on rack side and 10' loop on camera side. (For future relocation if needed by client.)</p><p>• Mount all cameras and any peripherals for camera installation</p><p>• Contact the config POC listed at the top of the work order to test all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations).</p><p>• Confirm all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations) with site contact</p><p>*Note: If working on a large install (multiple buildings or areas in a large building), as you get cameras up in an area of the building, please make sure to go ahead and aim them while there as best as you can and then check with the site contact to make sure the view is what they want. This will hopefully prevent the need to relocate the lift back to this area again for aiming.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT INSTALLATION NOTES:</strong></p><p>• Install at ladder-serviceable height unless higher is required for the desired view.</p><p>• Avoid obstruction from shelves, signage, or stock.</p><p>• Secure cables neatly with screw hole tie wraps or similar. No exposed or hanging runs.</p><p>• Mount height generally 10'; max is 20'.</p><p>• Each cable pull requires a 5' service loop at the rack side and 10' at the device side.</p><p>• Scissor lift work requires your own harness to be worn at all times.</p><p><strong>FINAL DELIVERABLES – Due Within 48 Hours of Completion</strong></p><p>Submit via email to SST@TRCA.com or upload as directed:</p><p>• First and last name of the person onsite with whom functionality was confirmed</p><p>• Name of TRCA IT Projects Team contact who assisted with final testing</p><p>• Final photo set of completed work</p><p>• Final labeled photo of the network rack with visible camera patch ports</p><p>• Completed Verkada Install Form</p><p>• Signed TRCA Work Order (signed by site contact/client)</p><p><strong>BEFORE LEAVING SITE, TECHNICIAN MUST CALL TRCA (940-381-8569) TO CHECK OUT.</strong></p><p><strong>You will receive a check-out code that must be written on the TRCA Work Order.</strong></p>","markdown":"**TECHNICIAN CHECK-IN & CHECK-OUT**\n\n**• Call TRCA at (940) 381-8569 immediately upon arrival and before departure.**\n\n**• You will receive check-in/out codes — write these on the TRCA Work Order.**\n\n**CONTACTS**\n\nSite Contact: \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\n\nVerkada Configuration Contact: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**BEFORE YOU BEGIN**\n\nRead the attached Full Scope of Work PDF and attachments carefully. If you have questions, call TRCA before going on site.\n\n**REFERENCE DOCUMENTS**\n\n• Full Scope of Work PDF\n\n• Floor Plan\n\n• Verkada Install Form\n\n• Camera Installation Mistakes to Avoid\n\n• PROPERLY SEALING OUTDOOR CAMERAS - MUST READ IF OUTDOOR CAMERAS ARE BEING INSTALLED\n\n• DRAIN WIRE IMPORTANCE PLEASE READ\n\nGC31-E Installation Instructions\n\n**HELPFUL RESOURCES**\n\n• All Verkada install/setup guides are available for free:\n\n• <https://www.verkada.com/docs>\n\n• Type the product part number into the search bar to view guides and videos.\n\n**For Basic Troubleshooting if needed:**\n\nTest the cable, confirm it passes.\n\nVerify link light on the switch port and power light on the switch port.\n\nTake camera directly to the switch and short wire it on the port, give it 3-4 minutes, notate the LED blinking lights.\n\nCamera LED Status Indicators:\n\n<https://help.verkada.com/verkada-cameras/installation/camera-led-status-indicators>\n\n24/7 Verkada Support: (\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Before calling, TRCA will need to provide you with support token, the customer ID and the phone number.\n\nIMPORTANT!!! If Verkada offers to do an RMA the following email address MUST be provided to them: amy.bourzikas@trca.com\n\n**HARDWARE INVENTORY & DOCUMENTATION – MANDATORY**\n\nInventory all Verkada hardware immediately upon arrival.\n\n!! Report any missing items to TRCA immediately.\n\nWhile completing the camera inventory, please follow the steps below to ensure a smooth setup in Verkada Command:\n\n**Labeling Boxes:**\n\n• As you unpack and inventory the cameras, label each camera box according to its planned location on the floor plan (e.g., CAM 1, CAM 2, CAM 3, etc.).\n\n• These labels should correspond to the designated camera locations on the project’s floor plan.\n\n**Install Form:**\n\n• On the install form, in the first column (next to each camera’s part #), write the camera number (CAM #) that corresponds to its labeled location.\n\n• Double-check that each camera number matches its planned location on the floor plan.\n\n**Submit Documentation:**\n\n• Once the form is complete, send it to SST@TRCA.com.\n\n• This documentation will be used to correctly set up and label the cameras within Verkada Command.\n\nIf you have any questions or need clarification during the process, don’t hesitate to reach out to TRCA.\n\n**SHIPMENT NOTES AND EQUIPMENT RESPONSIBILITY**\n\n**Items shipped to site by TRCA:**\n\n1 GC31-E-HW GC31 Cellular Gateway, Outdoor\n\n1 ACC-POE-90W-E-NA Outdoor 90W PoE++ (802.3bt-2018) Injector,\n\n1 CD53-256E-HW Verkada CD53-E Outdoor Dome Camera,\n\n1 ACC-MNT-ANGLE-1 Verkada Angle mount\n\n**Items provided by technician:**\n\n50ft CAT6 Cable\n\n3 RJ45\n\n1 weather proof sealant 1 tube\n\n1 CAT6 outdoor patch cord 3' white\n\n1 misc. consumables/ mounting hardware, cables , power strip/surge protector if needed and possible power/extension cord to be provided by the tech.\n\n**NETWORK PROTOCOL**\n\n• Do not plug any switch into the network (even temporarily) without prior TRCA approval.\n\n**INSTALLATION SCOPE OF WORK**\n\nInstallation and cabling for 1 Verkada camera, 1 Cellular Gateway, and 1 ACC-POE-Injector for the gateway.\n\nCamera and gateway are to be installed at ladder serviceable height.\n\nThere is power inside the building but will require an extension cord to reach.\n\nCommunicate work areas to site contact and provide notice if anything must be moved to avoid delays.\n\n• Pull and label cable for cameras (if cabling is already in place, skip this step)\n\n• Provide 5' service loop on rack side and 10' loop on camera side. (For future relocation if needed by client.)\n\n• Mount all cameras and any peripherals for camera installation\n\n• Contact the config POC listed at the top of the work order to test all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations).\n\n• Confirm all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations) with site contact\n\n\\*Note: If working on a large install (multiple buildings or areas in a large building), as you get cameras up in an area of the building, please make sure to go ahead and aim them while there as best as you can and then check with the site contact to make sure the view is what they want. This will hopefully prevent the need to relocate the lift back to this area again for aiming.\n\n**IMPORTANT INSTALLATION NOTES:**\n\n• Install at ladder-serviceable height unless higher is required for the desired view.\n\n• Avoid obstruction from shelves, signage, or stock.\n\n• Secure cables neatly with screw hole tie wraps or similar. No exposed or hanging runs.\n\n• Mount height generally 10'; max is 20'.\n\n• Each cable pull requires a 5' service loop at the rack side and 10' at the device side.\n\n• Scissor lift work requires your own harness to be worn at all times.\n\n**FINAL DELIVERABLES – Due Within 48 Hours of Completion**\n\nSubmit via email to SST@TRCA.com or upload as directed:\n\n• First and last name of the person onsite with whom functionality was confirmed\n\n• Name of TRCA IT Projects Team contact who assisted with final testing\n\n• Final photo set of completed work\n\n• Final labeled photo of the network rack with visible camera patch ports\n\n• Completed Verkada Install Form\n\n• Signed TRCA Work Order (signed by site contact/client)\n\n**BEFORE LEAVING SITE, TECHNICIAN MUST CALL TRCA (940-381-8569) TO CHECK OUT.**\n\n**You will receive a check-out code that must be written on the TRCA Work Order.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":40.06245304368875},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790974640230}
{"job":{"id":20091176,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Far Out Solutions","title":"Network Setup & hardware installation - The Grove","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Service Description:&nbsp;</strong>Network Setup &amp; hardware installation - The Grove</p><p> </p><p> </p><p>Technician will be representing themselves as a<strong>&nbsp;<em>Far Out Solutions</em> Technician.</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual<strong> </strong>Please refrain when possible from branded uniforms/shirts, etc.&nbsp;You are there representing Far Out Solutions only. Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer.&nbsp;NO SHORTS or open shoes&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Laptop (Windows) with Ethernet port &amp; USB Type A, Ethernet Patch Cords (3ft, 6ft, 9ft, etc...) CAT5E, Ethernet tools (Crimper, Toner&amp;Tester, plugs/connectors), Basic handyman tools (Screwdriver, stud finder, pliers, etc..) &amp; basic power tools like a drill., Label Maker, Mobile device with hotspot connectivity enabled/active</p><p><br></p><p> <strong>Scope of Work:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Install and configure the new firewall/gateway according to the approved network design and project requirements.</p><p>Label and document all existing network switch connections prior to migration to ensure proper port mapping and connectivity.</p><p>Transfer network connections from the existing switch to the new switch while maintaining proper cable organization and port assignments.</p><p>Verify network connectivity onsite after the migration, including internet access, LAN communication, and connectivity of critical devices.</p><p>Perform post-installation testing and validation to ensure all network services are functioning as expected.</p><p>Capture photos of the installation, cabling, and completed work for documentation and project records.</p><p>Coordinate with the remote technical support team throughout the implementation to assist with configuration, validation, and troubleshooting.</p><p>Document the completed work, testing results, and any findings observed during the implementation.</p><p><br></p><p> <strong>Attached <em>Far Out Solutions</em> Work order is required for payment. If required paper work is not completed, you will NOT get paid.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>***Do NOT discuss pricing, under ANY circumstance, with ANYONE except your direct contacts at FOS. If the customer is unsure about their pricing you are to refer them back to FOS so we can clarify.</strong>***&nbsp;</p><p><strong>The technician has&nbsp;</strong><u>24 Hrs. from the assignment END time to upload the Required Work Order</u>&nbsp;to the platform and any other pertinent paperwork required. Failure to comply will result in a<strong>&nbsp;reduction in pay.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>UPON SUCCESSFUL COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER, CUSTOMER SATISFACTION VERIFICATION, AND WORK ORDER IS IN A WORK DONE STATUS, WORK WILL BE APPROVED WITHIN SEVEN (7) BUSINESS DAYS FROM COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> UPON ACCEPTANCE OF THIS PROJECT, NO PAY INCREASE WILL BE ACCEPTED, UNLESS IT IS APPROVED BY PROJECT MANAGER BEFORE PROJECT IS COMPLETED. IF PROJECT MANAGER IS NOT IN THE OFFICE, SEND A MESSAGE THROUGH FIELD NATION THAT WILL BE REVIEWED WHEN PROJECT MANAGER RETURNS. ON PROJECTS WITH MAXIMUM TIME LIMITS, YOU NEED TO GET THE APPROVAL FROM THE TICKET MANAGER. ALL SITUATIONS WILL BE HANDLED ON A CASE BY CASE BASIS.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Parts Requirements:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Under no circumstances is the technician to leave the customer site with any hardware without obtaining <strong><em>Far Out Solutions</em></strong> approval.</p><p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>For services completed we pay a minimum of 1 hour and then in 15-minute increments thereafter based on the times shown on the Work Order signature page. Please note that we do not pay travel time unless it is agreed upon&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;being assigned for the work order.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>*** READ BELOW AS THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT REGARDING YOUR PAY!!!! ***</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Technician is to guarantee workmanship on all Far Out Solutions service events. If you fail to fully complete the services requested, provide quality work and/or satisfy the customer, or properly fill out the work order signature page, we reserve the right to deny payment in part or in full. If service is not billable to the customer due to the technicians’ error or customer handling, service will not be payable.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Tech must agree to warranty work performed, until the end of business 7 days following day of service. If there is a call&nbsp;back related to this service event, tech will go back to site at no charge with another work order.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>**Please allow 7 business days AFTER paperwork and resolution is uploaded for work order to be approved for invoicing status**</strong></p>","markdown":"**Service Description:** Network Setup & hardware installation - The Grove\n\nTechnician will be representing themselves as a ***Far Out Solutions* Technician.**\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual Please refrain when possible from branded uniforms/shirts, etc. You are there representing Far Out Solutions only. Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer. NO SHORTS or open shoes\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\nLaptop (Windows) with Ethernet port & USB Type A, Ethernet Patch Cords (3ft, 6ft, 9ft, etc...) CAT5E, Ethernet tools (Crimper, Toner&Tester, plugs/connectors), Basic handyman tools (Screwdriver, stud finder, pliers, etc..) & basic power tools like a drill., Label Maker, Mobile device with hotspot connectivity enabled/active\n\n **Scope of Work:**\n\nInstall and configure the new firewall/gateway according to the approved network design and project requirements.\n\nLabel and document all existing network switch connections prior to migration to ensure proper port mapping and connectivity.\n\nTransfer network connections from the existing switch to the new switch while maintaining proper cable organization and port assignments.\n\nVerify network connectivity onsite after the migration, including internet access, LAN communication, and connectivity of critical devices.\n\nPerform post-installation testing and validation to ensure all network services are functioning as expected.\n\nCapture photos of the installation, cabling, and completed work for documentation and project records.\n\nCoordinate with the remote technical support team throughout the implementation to assist with configuration, validation, and troubleshooting.\n\nDocument the completed work, testing results, and any findings observed during the implementation.\n\n **Attached *Far Out Solutions* Work order is required for payment. If required paper work is not completed, you will NOT get paid.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Do NOT discuss pricing, under ANY circumstance, with ANYONE except your direct contacts at FOS. If the customer is unsure about their pricing you are to refer them back to FOS so we can clarify.**\\*\\*\\*\n\n**The technician has** 24 Hrs. from the assignment END time to upload the Required Work Order to the platform and any other pertinent paperwork required. Failure to comply will result in a **reduction in pay.**\n\n**UPON SUCCESSFUL COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER, CUSTOMER SATISFACTION VERIFICATION, AND WORK ORDER IS IN A WORK DONE STATUS, WORK WILL BE APPROVED WITHIN SEVEN (7) BUSINESS DAYS FROM COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER.**\n\n **UPON ACCEPTANCE OF THIS PROJECT, NO PAY INCREASE WILL BE ACCEPTED, UNLESS IT IS APPROVED BY PROJECT MANAGER BEFORE PROJECT IS COMPLETED. IF PROJECT MANAGER IS NOT IN THE OFFICE, SEND A MESSAGE THROUGH FIELD NATION THAT WILL BE REVIEWED WHEN PROJECT MANAGER RETURNS. ON PROJECTS WITH MAXIMUM TIME LIMITS, YOU NEED TO GET THE APPROVAL FROM THE TICKET MANAGER. ALL SITUATIONS WILL BE HANDLED ON A CASE BY CASE BASIS.**\n\n**Parts Requirements:**\n\nUnder no circumstances is the technician to leave the customer site with any hardware without obtaining ***Far Out Solutions*** approval.\n\n**Compensation:**\n\nFor services completed we pay a minimum of 1 hour and then in 15-minute increments thereafter based on the times shown on the Work Order signature page. Please note that we do not pay travel time unless it is agreed upon **before** being assigned for the work order.\n\n***\\*\\*\\* READ BELOW AS THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT REGARDING YOUR PAY!!!! \\*\\*\\****\n\n***Technician is to guarantee workmanship on all Far Out Solutions service events. If you fail to fully complete the services requested, provide quality work and/or satisfy the customer, or properly fill out the work order signature page, we reserve the right to deny payment in part or in full. If service is not billable to the customer due to the technicians’ error or customer handling, service will not be payable.***\n\n***Tech must agree to warranty work performed, until the end of business 7 days following day of service. If there is a call back related to this service event, tech will go back to site at no charge with another work order.***\n\n**\\*\\*Please allow 7 business days AFTER paperwork and resolution is uploaded for work order to be approved for invoicing status\\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00","end":"2026-10-05T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7.555223188703634},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:0