{"job":{"id":20091460,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Voyix - Restaurants","title":"Tech for Point of Sale - Site Inspection","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech to bring powered SATA cable to USB device.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Complete Inventory on the hardware delivered to the site</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Complete a walk through with the customer to collect photos of the locations where hardware will later be Installed.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Link to detailed Onsite Site Inspection Scope of Work: </span><del>****************************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Link to Fast Fields Form: </span><del>****************************</del><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\"><del> ** </del></span><del>****************************************************************************************************</del><del>**</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Link to Item List - Tiny URL: </span><del>****************************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Link to Inventory Discovery - Tiny URL: </span><del>****************************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact Information details:</strong></p><p>Call Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin <span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">9762</span>, then enter QuickBase number <span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">102212</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>**NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attached Documentation</strong> - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole</p><p><br></p><p><strong>BASICS</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears</li><li>Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in</li><li>Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn</li><li>Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over</li><li>No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn</li><li>NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site</li></ul><p><strong>Behavior:</strong></p><ul><li>Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support</li><li>Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite</li><li>No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite</li><li>No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff</li><li>No music to be played, including through headphones</li><li>Follow all direction of the remote support contact</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;Documents:</strong></p><ul><li>NCR WO</li><li>Installation Documentation</li><li>Installation Checklist (Printed Copy or Signable Electronic Version)</li><li>NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info</li><li>Any other Supporting Documents Provided</li></ul><p><strong>TOOLING</strong></p><p><strong>Standard Tooling:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>32G Thumb drive</li><li>Data transfer cable &amp; USB to SATA docking station</li><li>Screwdriver set - Standard &amp; Precision</li><li>Adjustable, Allen &amp; Socket wrench sets</li><li>Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester</li><li>Wire Cutters</li><li>Level</li><li>Outlet tester</li><li>USB keyboard &amp; Mouse</li><li>Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes &amp; bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)</li><li>Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management</li><li>Box, Electrical &amp; Masking tape</li><li>Assorted screws &amp; anchors</li><li>Packing Tape</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE</strong></p><p><strong>Hardware</strong>: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface.&nbsp;DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location.&nbsp;Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cable Management: </strong>Cable Management must be done in a neat and professional manner. Cable routing needs to be considered carefully.&nbsp;Cabling should be bundled neatly and secured using zip ties or Velcro.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Drilling: </strong>Do not drill any holes unless approved by remote support</p><p><strong>Do Not Disrupt: </strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Clean as You Go:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers</span>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Questions or Concerns: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support </span>immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation<span style=\"color: black;\">.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>Timelines: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Cancellation Policy:</u></em> </strong></p><p><strong>Turnaways</strong>&nbsp;-</p><ul><li><strong>Arrival up to 1 hour</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to $50</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>1 hour - 2 hours</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate -</strong>&nbsp;<strong>If work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>Travel Expense</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional hours</strong></p><ul><li><strong>To Ensure Payment Approval</strong>&nbsp;- Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours</li><li><strong>Anticipated Expenses</strong>&nbsp;like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT</strong></p><ul><li>Physical Aloha Site Key (resembles a USB thumb drive) must be kept in a safe location prior to plugging into Back Office Server</li></ul>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**Tech to bring powered SATA cable to USB device.**\n\nComplete Inventory on the hardware delivered to the site\n\nComplete a walk through with the customer to collect photos of the locations where hardware will later be Installed.\n\nLink to detailed Onsite Site Inspection Scope of Work: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLink to Fast Fields Form: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLink to Item List - Tiny URL: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLink to Inventory Discovery - Tiny URL: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Contact Information details:**\n\nCall Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin 9762, then enter QuickBase number 102212\n\n**\\*\\*NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.**\n\n**Attached Documentation** - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole\n\n**BASICS**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears\n- Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in\n- Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn\n- Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over\n- No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn\n- NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n- Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support\n- Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite\n- No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite\n- No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff\n- No music to be played, including through headphones\n- Follow all direction of the remote support contact\n\n **Documents:**\n\n- NCR WO\n- Installation Documentation\n- Installation Checklist (Printed Copy or Signable Electronic Version)\n- NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info\n- Any other Supporting Documents Provided\n\n**TOOLING**\n\n**Standard Tooling:**\n\n- Laptop\n- 32G Thumb drive\n- Data transfer cable & USB to SATA docking station\n- Screwdriver set - Standard & Precision\n- Adjustable, Allen & Socket wrench sets\n- Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester\n- Wire Cutters\n- Level\n- Outlet tester\n- USB keyboard & Mouse\n- Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes & bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)\n- Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management\n- Box, Electrical & Masking tape\n- Assorted screws & anchors\n- Packing Tape\n\n**BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE**\n\n**Hardware**: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface. DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location. Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed\n\n**Cable Management:** Cable Management must be done in a neat and professional manner. Cable routing needs to be considered carefully. Cabling should be bundled neatly and secured using zip ties or Velcro.\n\n**Drilling:** Do not drill any holes unless approved by remote support\n\n**Do Not Disrupt:**\n\n- You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.\n- Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.\n\n**Clean as You Go:** Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers\n\n**Questions or Concerns:** Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation.\n\n**Timelines:** If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.\n\n***Cancellation Policy:***\n\n**Turnaways** -\n\n- **Arrival up to 1 hour**\n- **Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to $50**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **1 hour - 2 hours**\n- **Hourly Rate -** **If work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **Travel Expense**\n- **Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment**\n\n**Additional hours**\n\n- **To Ensure Payment Approval** - Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours\n- **Anticipated Expenses** like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion\n\n**IMPORTANT**\n\n- Physical Aloha Site Key (resembles a USB thumb drive) must be kept in a safe location prior to plugging into Back Office Server","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T11:00","end":"2026-10-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.40657582200953},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790977925059}
{"job":{"id":20091419,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Replace Existing Switches with 24-Port Juniper & Test | Connect Existing Circuit/Modem |Remote Support | UPS Drop-Off | Est. Onsite: 1.5hrs","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store</li><li><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional <strong>$30 expense</strong> for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"><u>IMPORTANT NOTE</u></strong><u style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">:</u><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY </strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time</strong></li><li>Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied</li><li><strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense</li><li>Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u> </strong></p><ul><li>Packing Tape</li><li><u>﻿</u>Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity</li><li>Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)</li><li>Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger &amp; Camera</li><li>Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;</li><li>6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)</li><li>Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.</li><li>Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment</li><li>Ethernet Network Cable Toner &amp; Tester</li><li>100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch</li></ul><p><strong><u>On-Site Tasks:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">IMPORTANT</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">:&nbsp;</span><strong>You are required to reference the ‘</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\">Confidential Information</strong><strong>’ section&nbsp;<em><u>IF</u></em>&nbsp;any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted</strong></li><li>Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See customer field '<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">Site Contact Name &amp; Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list&nbsp;</span>MOD/LCON<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">&nbsp;and not a specific person)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty</li><li>At the scheduled install time, call <strong><del>************</del></strong> to check in and work directly with the <del>****</del> team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Important</strong>: You must work with the <del>****</del> team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed</li><li>Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work</li><li>Confirm the contents in the box with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label</li><li>Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks <strong>(see the attached network diagram for reference):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Only at the direction of the remote support team</u></strong>, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 0-3 = Workstation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 4-5 = Printer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 6-7 = Phones</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 8 = Access Point</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 9 = Gate</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 10 = Future Use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 11 = Kiosk</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 22 = WattBox Network Port</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Locate the Customer Broadband Modem</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Identify the modem’s <strong>Ethernet/network port</strong> providing the broadband connection</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Using a patch cable, connect the modem to <strong>GE1 on the Edge device</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected <strong>link/activity indicators</strong> on both devices</li><li>Wait for <del>****</del> verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating</li><li>Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Close and securely tape the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; <strong>ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label</li><li>Drop off the package at a local UPS location</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Upload the UPS drop-off receipt</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Required On-Site Deliverables:</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email the photos to the <del>****</del> team at <del>*****************</del> Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation</li></ol><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><p>For any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:</p><p><strong>Contact Hours:</strong></p><p><strong><u>8:00 AM &ndash; 5:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>***** ************</del></li><li><del>****** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong><u>2:00 PM &ndash; 11:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>******** ******************</del></li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store\n- **Estimated onsite duration:** 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional **$30 expense** for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).\n- **IMPORTANT NOTE**: **The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location**\n- **CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY**\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n- **Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time**\n- Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied\n- **MUST** have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense\n- Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)\n\n**Dress code:**\n\n- Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Packing Tape\n- ﻿Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity\n- Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)\n- Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger & Camera\n- Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)\n- Label maker\n- 6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)\n- Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.\n- Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment\n- Ethernet Network Cable Toner & Tester\n- 100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling\n- Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits\n\n**Pre-Site requirements:**\n\n- Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **IMPORTANT**: **You are required to reference the ‘****Confidential Information****’ section *IF* any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted**\n2. Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)\n3. See customer field 'Site Contact Name & Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list MOD/LCON and not a specific person)\n4. Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty\n5. At the scheduled install time, call **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to check in and work directly with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team\n6. **Important**: You must work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed\n7. Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work\n8. Confirm the contents in the box with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field\n9. Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label\n10. Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks **(see the attached network diagram for reference):**\n11. **Only at the direction of the remote support team**, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting\n12. Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not\n13. Ports 0-3 = Workstation\n14. Ports 4-5 = Printer\n15. Ports 6-7 = Phones\n16. Port 8 = Access Point\n17. Port 9 = Gate\n18. Port 10 = Future Use\n19. Port 11 = Kiosk\n20. Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)\n21. Port 22 = WattBox Network Port\n22. Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3\n23. **Locate the Customer Broadband Modem**\n24. Identify the modem’s **Ethernet/network port** providing the broadband connection\n25. Using a patch cable, connect the modem to **GE1 on the Edge device**\n26. Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected **link/activity indicators** on both devices\n27. Wait for \\*\\*\\*\\* verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating\n28. Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return\n29. Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box\n30. Close and securely tape the box\n31. Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; **ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL**\n32. Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label\n33. Drop off the package at a local UPS location\n34. **Upload the UPS drop-off receipt**\n35. **Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n36. Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation\n37. Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order\n38. Email the photos to the \\*\\*\\*\\* team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation\n\n**Escalations:**\n\nFor any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:\n\n**Contact Hours:**\n\n**8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**2:00 PM – 11:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T12:30","end":"2026-10-21T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":60},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":59.29073628861697},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM"