{"job":{"id":"9515043737","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Geeks On Site","title":"COMPUTER TECH (Desktop Dell Win 11) - RESIDENTIAL","description":"<p><strong>If interested in this ticket please apply with the counteroffer, date of service if different and the arrival time.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>WORK DESCRIPTION:</strong></p><p>Desktop Dell Win 11 The customer recently moved and set up his computer but is unable to get the monitor to turn on or display properly. Please inspect the monitor, computer connections, cables, power, and related hardware thoroughly to determine the cause and restore proper display functionality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>A PHYSICAL INVOICE IS NOT REQUIRED FOR THIS ASSIGNMENT.</p><p>You are REQUIRED to download and use the ZOHO FSM app. The digital invoice is generated by completing and submitting the Service Report within the app.</p><p><br></p><p>Failure to properly submit the Service Report may result in payment delays and may ultimately lead to non-payment.</p><p><br></p><p><a href=\"https://help.zoho.com/portal/en/kb/fsm/mobilize-your-workforce/articles/fsm-mobile-app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">IN CASE YOU HAVEN'T DOWNLOADED IT YET, USE THIS LINK:</a></p><p><br></p><p><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10niXVd6KdCwNZ-ImAGmoTdfVGtlCzRrb/view?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"><em> CHECK THE GUIDE TO USE THE ZOHO FSM</em></a></p><p><br></p><p><em>Quick Manual - Zoho FSM App</em></p><p><em>1. Open the service appointment.</em></p><p><em>2. Click Start Work to begin.</em></p><p><em>3. Go to Quick Actions - Service Report.</em></p><p><em>4. Fill in Technician Feedback + Service Summary.</em></p><p><em>5. Add your signature - Save - Next.</em></p><p><em>6. Enter client feedback + rating.</em></p><p><em>7. Have clients sign - Save &amp; Create the invoice.</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Text us at&nbsp;(833) 337-7386&nbsp;If you need assistance with the app, DO NOT CALL.</em></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-04T08:00","end":"2026-10-04T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":21.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790979809267}
{"job":{"id":20080478,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong>Provider to ensure the SVR attached to this Work Order is filled, signed by POC and uploaded back here.</strong></li><li><strong>Images required</strong></li><li><strong>Provider to represent as Fresenius IT Support when onsite﻿</strong></li></ul><p>Ticket Type: <strong>Network</strong></p><p>Date &amp; Time: <strong>05th Oct, 09:00am&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Visit Type- Hourly&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1.Mandatory Dos &amp; Don'ts:</p><p>Dress Code- Business Casuals.</p><p>Do not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.</p><p><br></p><p>8.Short description of the reported issue:</p><p>APs connected to the incorrect ports. Move AP connections on SW2.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>9.If L1/L2 is required: L2</p><p>10.Mandate Action required:</p><p><br></p><p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p><p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.</p><p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support</p><p><br></p><p>11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:</p><p><br></p><p>-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).</p><p>-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p><p>-10 ft data cable.</p><p>-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch</p><p>-Cable tester&nbsp;</p><p>-Tone generator&nbsp;</p><p>-Toner</p><p><br></p><p>12.Scope of Work:&nbsp;</p><p>Move AP connected to port 45 to Port 4 on SW2. Also move AP connected to port 1 to port 5 on SW2.</p><p>Contact Donny Clinton for network support when onsite before making the change.</p><p><br></p><p>13.After the completion of Visit:</p><p>Update the SVR with Resolution Steps</p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch contact details&nbsp;</p><p>EUXDispatch@freseniusmedicalcare.com</p><ul><li>+12014997693</li></ul>","markdown":"- **Provider to ensure the SVR attached to this Work Order is filled, signed by POC and uploaded back here.**\n- **Images required**\n- **Provider to represent as Fresenius IT Support when onsite﻿**\n\nTicket Type: **Network**\n\nDate & Time: **05th Oct, 09:00am**\n\nVisit Type- Hourly\n\n1.Mandatory Dos & Don'ts:\n\nDress Code- Business Casuals.\n\nDo not discuss the payrate onsite with the customer or other employees.\n\n8.Short description of the reported issue:\n\nAPs connected to the incorrect ports. Move AP connections on SW2.\n\n9.If L1/L2 is required: L2\n\n10.Mandate Action required:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support\n\n11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:\n\n-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).\n\n-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-10 ft data cable.\n\n-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch\n\n-Cable tester\n\n-Tone generator\n\n-Toner\n\n12.Scope of Work:\n\nMove AP connected to port 45 to Port 4 on SW2. Also move AP connected to port 1 to port 5 on SW2.\n\nContact Donny Clinton for network support when onsite before making the change.\n\n13.After the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the SVR with Resolution Steps\n\nDispatch contact details\n\nEUXDispatch@freseniusmedicalcare.com\n\n- +12014997693","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T08:45","end":"2026-10-05T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLabor