{"job":{"id":20095269,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"GAP - Network Troubleshoot","description":{"html":"<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>SOW: Title: PagerDuty: NSG:s05966cwsw08 : 10.174.128.38 : Gold : Store 8 Port switch is Down for continuous 30 Min</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable</p>\n<p>Switch (S/n: Q2AX-KAPJ-KQX9) is located in (reg 7 8 )</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (switch name 01) : port XX.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>When on site, check in with Store Network at<del>**************</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.</p>\n<p>If any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.</p>\n<p>If we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.</p>\n<p>To reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>After performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>For more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>Basic Tools</p>\n<p>working laptop with the updated driver</p>\n<p>Console Cables</p>\n<p>Cat5 Cable</p>\n<p>Cable tester</p>\n<p>Internet dongle</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>While Onsite:</p>\n<p>- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Checkout Requirements:</p>\n<p>-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)</p>\n<p>-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Deliverables:</p>\n<p>-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com</p>\n<p>-MOD email for Survey</p>","markdown":"Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:\n\nSOW: Title: PagerDuty: NSG:s05966cwsw08 : 10.174.128.38 : Gold : Store 8 Port switch is Down for continuous 30 Min\n\nPlease ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable\n\nSwitch (S/n: Q2AX-KAPJ-KQX9) is located in (reg 7 8 )\n\nTech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (switch name 01) : port XX.\n\nWhen on site, check in with Store Network at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.\n\nTech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.\n\nIf any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.\n\nIf we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.\n\nIf the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.\n\nIf there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.\n\nTo reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.\n\nAfter performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions\n\nFor more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nBasic Tools\n\nworking laptop with the updated driver\n\nConsole Cables\n\nCat5 Cable\n\nCable tester\n\nInternet dongle\n\nCheck In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.\n\nWhile Onsite:\n\n\\- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2\n\nCheckout Requirements:\n\n-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)\n\n-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com\n\n-MOD email for Survey","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T11:00","end":"2026-10-05T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.701467607464195},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":70,"baseAmount":280,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1791199146654}
{"job":{"id":19863725,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Handheld Scanner upgrade - Tech 2","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p><strong><u>The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The registers must be shut down</u>,</strong> then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,<strong><u>THEN</u></strong> reboot the register.</p>\n<p>This is in the doc., page 6</p>\n<p>This should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes to ATR process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)</strong></li>\n<li>If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware</li>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.<em>﻿</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet <strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in <strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong> and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><del>************</del></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>****** * *** ********* ******* *********** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** ****** ********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a<del>********</del>representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\n**The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.**\n\n**The registers must be shut down,** then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,**THEN** reboot the register.\n\nThis is in the doc., page 6\n\nThis should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n- Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n\nChanges to ATR process:\n\n- **Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)**\n- If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware\n- **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n- Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet\n- No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.*﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T16:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":298},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":8.5,"distance":12.071670422674183},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":510,"estHours":8.5,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10