{"job":{"id":"1018181250","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Service Ticket #6998771 - 2024231204: Device is Offline","description":"Required Equipment: <br>IMPORTANT: Tech must bring and have ready a USB → DB9 Female cable and a USB → Mini-USB serial cable for console access.<br>Tech will need a patch cord, a splitter and a minimum of 3 filters, Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone and charger, Multimeter, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder,  Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Pencil and/or Marker, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, Cross-Connect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, USB → DB9 Female cable, USB → Mini-USB serial cable. <br><br>IMPORTANT: Tech must bring and have ready a USB → DB9 Female cable and a USB → Mini-USB serial cable for console access.<br>** USB to RS232 Adapter with PL2303 Chipset, 6.6ft USB 2.0 Male to RS232 Female DB9 Serial Converter Cable  - for gen 3/3.5 **<br><br>Issue: 2024231204: Device is Offline Please work with NOC to restore<br><br>Service Ticket #6998771<br><br>EPIK SERIAL #: 2024231204<br>LOCATION: PS-Brook Circle - EPIK - 05438688<br><br>PORT 1 - TN 8048261477 Voice<br><br><br>Scope Of Work:<br><br>*** IMPORTANT: Tech must call into Work Market to check in and out upon arrival and before departing the site. ***<br>Tech will call into Granite NOC at 844.492.2557 opt. 4 , then opt 1 to start the scope of work.<br><br>PLEASE NOTE: There is no voicemail for the IW call queue. If you cannot get through to the NOC, pressing option 1 will prompt a callback from the next available NOC tech.<br><br><br>Device Offline Template: <br><br>1.Locate EPIK Edge device.<br>a.Take clear pictures of all light statuses and confirm that the Green power LED is lit. <br>2.Confirm LTE paddles are positioned away from each other at a 45 degree angle. <br>a.Reboot device if paddle position was changed and confirm with NOC if issue has been resolved.<br>3.Confirm if there is an ethernet connection connected to eth0/1. <br>a.If so, remove ethernet connection and reboot device. Confirm with NOC if issue has been resolved.<br>b.If device comes online over LTE with ethernet connection removed, share “Granite EPIK Network Configuration” document with customer’s IT team to confirm network device is configured to handoff an IP via DHCP and all ports and Ips are properly whitelisted. <br>4.If device remains offline, perform the following actions and have NOC escalate to EPIK Engineering to setup a loal console session for further investigation: <br>a.Connect tech’s laptop to eth0/2 of the EPIK device and set the following static Ips:<br>i.IP: 172.17.17.234<br>ii.Subnet: 255.255.255.0<br>iii.Gateway: 172.17.17.254                                                 <br>b.Open a command prompt and ping 172.17.17.254. <br>c.If a response is received, open an Anydesk session and share AnyDeskID with EPIK Engineering team.<br>5.EPIK Engineering team will further advise on further steps.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00","end":"2026-10-02T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":136.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 136.4mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-