{"job":{"id":"2533898299","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"04301368 || 8460 Times Dispatch Blvd || EPIK Cutover and Test","description":"DESCRIPTION: SOW - EPIK Cutover &amp; Test <br><br>please call into Activations : (833) 719-8378 <br><br>************************************************************************************* <br><br>Before Arrival <br><br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival. <br><br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK: <br><br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo <br><br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below. <br><br>On Arrival <br><br>1.Check in on WorkMarket. <br><br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location. <br><br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work. <br><br>EPIK Install Requirements <br><br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik. <br><br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location.  <br><br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard. <br><br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on. <br><br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions. <br><br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard: <br><br>https://wizard.epik.io <br><br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned. <br><br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES <br><br>Checkout Requirement <br><br>1.Confirm Activations has released you. <br><br>2.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables. <br><br>3.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket. <br><br>4.Check out on WorkMarket. <br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket. <br><br>Required Deliverables <br><br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout: <br><br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install. <br><br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block. <br><br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable. <br><br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet. <br><br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions. <br><br>Required Tools <br><br>•Laptop <br><br>•Smartphone with hotspot <br><br>•Tone generator and wand <br><br>•66/110 punch tool <br><br>•Butt set <br><br>       Infrared Temperature Gun  <br><br>•Electrician scissors <br><br>•Step ladder <br><br>•Flashlight/headlamp <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper <br><br>•Ethernet cable tester <br><br>•Impact drill / cordless drill <br><br>•Masonry bits <br><br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits <br><br>•Needle-nose pliers <br><br>•Label maker and label tape <br><br>•Cat3 or better cable <br><br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable <br><br>•Cross-connect wire <br><br>•Gel-crimp connectors <br><br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks <br><br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini <br><br>************************************************************************************* <br><br>PM SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS GUIDELINES <br><br>Special Instructions <br><br>Install Location <br><br>Enter where the EPIK device should be installed, including MDF/IDF/telco room location, wall/rack/shelf mounting instructions, and access notes. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Cable Runs <br><br>Enter any required cable runs, cable type, distance, start/end points, and whether ladder, lift, ceiling access, or special tools are needed. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Network Information <br><br>Enter switch name, switch port, DHCP/static IP details, VLAN info, and customer network escalation contact. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>External Antenna <br><br>Enter whether an external antenna is required, where it should be mounted, and any cable path or photo requirements. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Special Testing <br><br>Enter any customer-specific testing that must be completed, including specific TNs, fax, alarm, elevator, hunt group, auto attendant, or other required testing. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Customer Contacts <br><br>Enter primary LCON, backup contact, customer IT contact, site manager, and escalation contacts. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Vendor / Third-Party Info <br><br>Enter any VTM, customer tech, alarm vendor, elevator vendor, fax vendor, MSP, or other third-party contact information.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T11:00","end":"2026-10-02T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":350},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":110.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 110.5mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791205371872}
{"job":{"id":20097133,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ReSource Point of Sale LLC","title":"Test/Repair network issues, bring TP-Link/Netgear switch (5 Port switch only): Checkers#447","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**Please note that if you do not have a properly verified time on check in and check out with the Hi.Auto team, then approval of additional time onsite will be delayed, and approval of work order will be delayed. Thanks for understanding.**</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>﻿**If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite**</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>**TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED,&nbsp;<u>PRIOR</u>&nbsp;TO ASSIGNMENT**</em></strong></p>\n<p><u>We need the Revisit Checklist.PDF filled out, signed, and uploaded (can be photo copied to a new PDF, or photos of actual document filled out and signed are also acceptable).</u></p>\n<p><strong><u>Support: 631-392-8918, Hi.Auto Support Group</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Basic Overview:</u></strong> The Onsite Tech will be doing guided troubleshooting of the Hi Auto drive-thru detector/timer system. Going over connections and making sure cables are secure to try and repair or isolate the failed device or connection. There could be issues with speakers, speaker wiring, other low voltage wiring that is not CAT5.</p>\n<p>Tech should be mechanically well versed and able to follow instructions, and communicate effectively with the support team.</p>\n<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>STEP 1)</u> <em><u>﻿</u></em><u>COMMUNICATE W/MGR ON DUTY:</u></strong> Contact the store Manager (See Site Contacts) to introduce yourself as the Tech &amp; what you will be servicing for their site</p>\n<ul>\n<li>.<strong><u>If you call the store and no one answers, note it in the Message section and proceed to the store.</u></strong>&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>STEP 2) DESCRIPTION FRM HI-AUTO HELPDESK</u></strong>: Need a Tech to bring a replacement TP-link or Netgear switch just in case its needed. Tech to&nbsp;troubleshoot network issues and work with Support to get issues resolved. Make any repairs needed to get their issues resolved asap. <strong><em>SEE PICTURES UNDER CLIENT DOCUMENTS.</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Equipment:&nbsp;TP-Link/ netgear switch (5 Port switch only),&nbsp;laptop, monitor, mouse, keyboard, HDMI cables, network tester, spare network cables, RJ45 heads, normal tools, multimeter</li>\n<li>Our team will assist remotely. Please reach out to Support rep William at (910) 996 5857 EXT: 111</li>\n<li>Also see attached a <strong><em><u>checklist under CLIENT DOCUMENTS</u></em></strong>. The checklist must be signed by the manager on site.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Tools/Materials Requested:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Voltage Multimeter</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Double sided tape</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Zip ties or velcro straps</strong></p>\n<p>Bring basic hand tools, drill, drill bits of various sizes.</p>\n<p>Wire strippers and wire cutters.</p>\n<p>Bring wire nuts, zip ties, cell phone with camera, etc.</p>\n<p>CAT5 cable, RJ45 male and female terminations.</p>\n<p>CAT5 cable tester.</p>\n<p>Low voltage toning device.</p>\n<p>Laptop with network port.</p>\n<p>Cell phone with wireless capabilities and a good working camera.</p>\n<p>Google Grive app for iPhone or Android.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Liabilities and Warranty Information - Store Management</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Limitation of Liability:</em></strong><em>&nbsp;In all events, RPOS will not be responsible for any lost, stolen, or damaged materials. Customer hereby agree that Resource Point of Sale LLC shall not be liable to Customer, or any third party, for (1) any liability claims, loss, damages or expense of any kind arising directly or indirectly out of services provided herein for (2) any incidental or consequential damages, however caused, and Customer agrees to indemnify and hold Company harmless against such liabilities, claims, losses, damages (consequential or otherwise) or expenses, or actions in respect thereof, asserted or brought against Company by or in right of third parties or for (3) any punitive damages. For purposes of this Agreement, incidental or consequential damages shall include, but not be limited to, loss of anticipated revenues, income, profits or savings; loss of or damage to business reputation or good will; loss of Customers; loss of business or financial opportunity; or any other indirect or special damages of any kind categorized as consequential or incidental damages under the law of the State of Illinois.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em>Services Warranty.</em></strong><em>&nbsp;Company warrants that all Services performed pursuant to this Agreement will be performed in accordance with the general standards and practices of the point of sale services industry in existence at the time the Services are being performed. The Services provided under this SOW shall be warranted for a period of (5) days following the satisfactory completion of any services under the SOW. Any warranty claim must be made in writing within the allotted (5) days, after the acceptance of the service. RPOS’s sole obligation and customers exclusive remedy in respect thereof is to re-perform the service.</em></p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*Please note that if you do not have a properly verified time on check in and check out with the Hi.Auto team, then approval of additional time onsite will be delayed, and approval of work order will be delayed. Thanks for understanding.\\*\\***\n\n***﻿\\*\\*If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite\\*\\****\n\n***\\*\\*TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED, PRIOR TO ASSIGNMENT\\*\\****\n\nWe need the Revisit Checklist.PDF filled out, signed, and uploaded (can be photo copied to a new PDF, or photos of actual document filled out and signed are also acceptable).\n\n**Support: 631-392-8918, Hi.Auto Support Group**\n\n**Basic Overview:** The Onsite Tech will be doing guided troubleshooting of the Hi Auto drive-thru detector/timer system. Going over connections and making sure cables are secure to try and repair or isolate the failed device or connection. There could be issues with speakers, speaker wiring, other low voltage wiring that is not CAT5.\n\nTech should be mechanically well versed and able to follow instructions, and communicate effectively with the support team.\n\n\\----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**STEP 1) *﻿*COMMUNICATE W/MGR ON DUTY:** Contact the store Manager (See Site Contacts) to introduce yourself as the Tech & what you will be servicing for their site\n\n- .**If you call the store and no one answers, note it in the Message section and proceed to the store.**\n\n**STEP 2) DESCRIPTION FRM HI-AUTO HELPDESK**: Need a Tech to bring a replacement TP-link or Netgear switch just in case its needed. Tech to troubleshoot network issues and work with Support to get issues resolved. Make any repairs needed to get their issues resolved asap. ***SEE PICTURES UNDER CLIENT DOCUMENTS.***\n\n- Equipment: TP-Link/ netgear switch (5 Port switch only), laptop, monitor, mouse, keyboard, HDMI cables, network tester, spare network cables, RJ45 heads, normal tools, multimeter\n- Our team will assist remotely. Please reach out to Support rep William at (910) 996 5857 EXT: 111\n- Also see attached a ***checklist under CLIENT DOCUMENTS***. The checklist must be signed by the manager on site.\n\n**Tools/Materials Requested:**\n\n**Voltage Multimeter**\n\n**Double sided tape**\n\n**Zip ties or velcro straps**\n\nBring basic hand tools, drill, drill bits of various sizes.\n\nWire strippers and wire cutters.\n\nBring wire nuts, zip ties, cell phone with camera, etc.\n\nCAT5 cable, RJ45 male and female terminations.\n\nCAT5 cable tester.\n\nLow voltage toning device.\n\nLaptop with network port.\n\nCell phone with wireless capabilities and a good working camera.\n\nGoogle Grive app for iPhone or Android.\n\n**Liabilities and Warranty Information - Store Management**\n\n***Limitation of Liability:*** *In all events, RPOS will not be responsible for any lost, stolen, or damaged materials. Customer hereby agree that Resource Point of Sale LLC shall not be liable to Customer, or any third party, for (1) any liability claims, loss, damages or expense of any kind arising directly or indirectly out of services provided herein for (2) any incidental or consequential damages, however caused, and Customer agrees to indemnify and hold Company harmless against such liabilities, claims, losses, damages (consequential or otherwise) or expenses, or actions in respect thereof, asserted or brought against Company by or in right of third parties or for (3) any punitive damages. For purposes of this Agreement, incidental or consequential damages shall include, but not be limited to, loss of anticipated revenues, income, profits or savings; loss of or damage to business reputation or good will; loss of Customers; loss of business or financial opportunity; or any other indirect or special damages of any kind categorized as consequential or incidental damages under the law of the State of Illinois.*\n\n***Services Warranty.*** *Company warrants that all Services performed pursuant to this Agreement will be performed in accordance with the general standards and practices of the point of sale services industry in existence at the time the Services are being performed. The Services provided under this SOW shall be warranted for a period of (5) days following the satisfactory completion of any services under the SOW. Any warranty claim must be made in writing within the allotted (5) days, after the acceptance of the service. RPOS’s sole obligation and customers exclusive remedy in respect thereof is to re-perform the service.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T10:30","end":"2026-10-05T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":44.08529303601679},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary