{"job":{"id":20097793,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Tractor Supply - Palo Alto Ion Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>The onsite Field Service Technician will work with a remote CIS support engineer to replace two existing Palo Alto Prisma SD-WAN ION 2000 appliances with new ION 1200-S appliances at an active retail location. The technician will primarily perform physical installation, cabling, equipment identification, testing assistance, documentation, and removal/packaging of the legacy equipment. All network configuration and backend changes will be performed remotely by CIS.</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Field Technician Scope:</strong></p><ul><li>Check in with CIS&#39;s remote technical support and the onsite Manager on Duty (MOD) and confirm access to the network rack/cabinet.</li><li>Locate and verify the replacement ION 1200-S appliances, power supplies, mounting trays, cabling, and associated hardware.</li><li>Identify the existing primary and backup ION 2000 appliances and associated WAN/LAN connections.</li><li>Take clear before-work photographs of the network rack, existing equipment, cabling, and port connections.</li><li>Physically label the new primary and backup ION appliances as directed by the remote CIS engineer.</li><li>Install and secure the supplied mounting trays and new ION 1200-S appliances in the network rack/cabinet.</li><li>Connect power and required inter-device cabling to the new appliances.</li><li>Move existing cellular WAN, broadband WAN, and LAN/switch connections from the legacy appliances to the new appliances as directed by CIS.</li><li>Manually reboot the onsite cellular gateway/Inseego device and broadband modem when instructed.</li><li>Verify and/or reseat network cables when requested by the remote support team during testing.</li><li>Remain onsite and available while CIS remotely validates appliance connectivity, VPN connectivity, HA operation, and store network connectivity.</li><li>Coordinate with the MOD to validate critical store services, including POS/registers, workstation connectivity, Wi-Fi, phones, and printers.</li><li>If required, assist with physical rollback by reconnecting the original equipment and cabling under CIS direction.</li><li>Once final approval is received, remove the legacy ION 2000 appliances and associated mounting hardware.</li><li>Package the legacy appliances, power supplies, and mounting hardware using the provided return materials and shipping labels.</li><li>Perform final cable management and leave the network rack/cabinet clean and orderly.</li><li>Provide required completion photographs, including final rack condition, appliance cabling/ports, and packaged return equipment.</li><li>Provide legacy equipment serial numbers and any requested closeout information to the remote CIS support resource.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Technician Requirements:</strong></p><p>Technician should have standard network field-service tools and be comfortable identifying, mounting, labeling, connecting, disconnecting, and documenting enterprise network equipment. The technician must follow remote CIS direction and should not move production network cabling or remove legacy equipment until specifically authorized.</p><p></p><p><strong>Materials - **Please have extras of all of the below:</strong></p><ul><li>Cat5e cable (at least 200’)</li><li>QTY 8 - 12mm M6 screws</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p>Required Tools:</p><ul><li>Laptop w/Power supply</li><li>Headphones (Bluetooth or wired)</li><li>Windows 10 (Caution: do not use a laptop with Windows 7 or earlier)</li><li>With Ethernet port OR USB – Ethernet Adaptor</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>General purpose tools for mounting equipment (e.g., power drill, screwdriver etc.)</li><li>Cell Phone w/full battery and Charger (camera required)</li><li>Cellular Hotspot</li><li>Standard Measuring tools</li><li>Ladder/ Folding Ladder of at least 6’</li></ul>","markdown":"The onsite Field Service Technician will work with a remote CIS support engineer to replace two existing Palo Alto Prisma SD-WAN ION 2000 appliances with new ION 1200-S appliances at an active retail location. The technician will primarily perform physical installation, cabling, equipment identification, testing assistance, documentation, and removal/packaging of the legacy equipment. All network configuration and backend changes will be performed remotely by CIS.\n\n**Field Technician Scope:**\n\n- Check in with CIS's remote technical support and the onsite Manager on Duty (MOD) and confirm access to the network rack/cabinet.\n- Locate and verify the replacement ION 1200-S appliances, power supplies, mounting trays, cabling, and associated hardware.\n- Identify the existing primary and backup ION 2000 appliances and associated WAN/LAN connections.\n- Take clear before-work photographs of the network rack, existing equipment, cabling, and port connections.\n- Physically label the new primary and backup ION appliances as directed by the remote CIS engineer.\n- Install and secure the supplied mounting trays and new ION 1200-S appliances in the network rack/cabinet.\n- Connect power and required inter-device cabling to the new appliances.\n- Move existing cellular WAN, broadband WAN, and LAN/switch connections from the legacy appliances to the new appliances as directed by CIS.\n- Manually reboot the onsite cellular gateway/Inseego device and broadband modem when instructed.\n- Verify and/or reseat network cables when requested by the remote support team during testing.\n- Remain onsite and available while CIS remotely validates appliance connectivity, VPN connectivity, HA operation, and store network connectivity.\n- Coordinate with the MOD to validate critical store services, including POS/registers, workstation connectivity, Wi-Fi, phones, and printers.\n- If required, assist with physical rollback by reconnecting the original equipment and cabling under CIS direction.\n- Once final approval is received, remove the legacy ION 2000 appliances and associated mounting hardware.\n- Package the legacy appliances, power supplies, and mounting hardware using the provided return materials and shipping labels.\n- Perform final cable management and leave the network rack/cabinet clean and orderly.\n- Provide required completion photographs, including final rack condition, appliance cabling/ports, and packaged return equipment.\n- Provide legacy equipment serial numbers and any requested closeout information to the remote CIS support resource.\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\nTechnician should have standard network field-service tools and be comfortable identifying, mounting, labeling, connecting, disconnecting, and documenting enterprise network equipment. The technician must follow remote CIS direction and should not move production network cabling or remove legacy equipment until specifically authorized.\n\n**Materials - \\*\\*Please have extras of all of the below:**\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- QTY 8 - 12mm M6 screws\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Laptop w/Power supply\n- Headphones (Bluetooth or wired)\n- Windows 10 (Caution: do not use a laptop with Windows 7 or earlier)\n- With Ethernet port OR USB – Ethernet Adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General purpose tools for mounting equipment (e.g., power drill, screwdriver etc.)\n- Cell Phone w/full battery and Charger (camera required)\n- Cellular Hotspot\n- Standard Measuring tools\n- Ladder/ Folding Ladder of at least 6’","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00","end":"2026-10-26T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":59.36632366621624},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791210446307}
{"job":{"id":20077974,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Genlogs","title":"Sensor Reboot.- NC.I95.SB.87 (#0318)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>Please note that this work location is outdoors and may require traversing through snow, mud, or otherwise to get to the sensor site.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><p>In the event of an outage at a site that is not resolved automatically by either power restoration or our integrated failsafe mechanisms, the Trident sensor may require physical intervention in order to reboot the unit.</p><p><strong>You will need:</strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Volt meter</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wire cutters (<em>for tamper-proof lock</em>)</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Flathead screwdriver (<em>for twist-lock cabinets</em>)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Pre-visit site review call with the Work Order Manager at <del>***** ********</del></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Process:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Locate the <del>*******</del> hardware cabinet</strong> – Typically mounted at ground level, the control unit should sit adjacent to the electrical panel on the structure. Depending on the Trident model, you may need to cut the tamper-proof lock or use a screwdriver to unlock the cabinet</li><li><strong>Confirm power at the hardware cabinet and electrical panel </strong>– Confirm power delivery to our hardware cabinet as well as the electrical panel in order to root out if it is a power issue and whether that is on the main breaker panel (utility side) or the load side (delivery to our box)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If power issue is identified, please report your findings to the <del>*******</del> team</li><li><strong>Reboot CPU and Peplink router</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If cellular and status lights are not displaying on the router, following the router reboot steps found in the <em>Router Troubleshooting &amp; SIM Installation</em> process to reconnect it to the network</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Confirm the CPU is powered on by checking for faint-blue light emitting from the power button. Press and hold the power button for 15s, then release, followed by a single press and release</li><li><strong>Confirm all internal connections are seated and secured tightly</strong> – Double check all cable connections, especially those that deliver power to hardware, as they can become dislodged over time</li></ol><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific photo requirements are dependent on the tasks performed and will be communicated upon the resolution of the issue</li><li>Confirmation from <del>*******</del> team that work has been completed or approval to leave site has been given.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Communication Directory: </strong></p><ul><li>If clarification, issues or questions is needed on work order, discuss with&nbsp;Work Order Manager at <del>***** ********</del></li><li>IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact:</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE: During your visit, please perform a general visual inspection of the site. If you observe any abnormal or unusual conditions—including, but not limited to, billboard damage, electrical issues, installation deficiencies, loose or exposed wiring, missing conduits, unsealed penetrations, signs of tampering, or any other condition that appears out of the ordinary—please document the issue with clear photos and notify us immediately before leaving the site.</strong></p>","markdown":"***Please note that this work location is outdoors and may require traversing through snow, mud, or otherwise to get to the sensor site.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nIn the event of an outage at a site that is not resolved automatically by either power restoration or our integrated failsafe mechanisms, the Trident sensor may require physical intervention in order to reboot the unit.\n\n**You will need:**\n\n● Volt meter\n\n● Wire cutters (*for tamper-proof lock*)\n\n● Flathead screwdriver (*for twist-lock cabinets*)\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Pre-visit site review call with the Work Order Manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Process:**\n\n1. **Locate the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* hardware cabinet** – Typically mounted at ground level, the control unit should sit adjacent to the electrical panel on the structure. Depending on the Trident model, you may need to cut the tamper-proof lock or use a screwdriver to unlock the cabinet\n2. **Confirm power at the hardware cabinet and electrical panel** – Confirm power delivery to our hardware cabinet as well as the electrical panel in order to root out if it is a power issue and whether that is on the main breaker panel (utility side) or the load side (delivery to our box)\n3. If power issue is identified, please report your findings to the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team\n4. **Reboot CPU and Peplink router**\n5. If cellular and status lights are not displaying on the router, following the router reboot steps found in the *Router Troubleshooting & SIM Installation* process to reconnect it to the network\n6. Confirm the CPU is powered on by checking for faint-blue light emitting from the power button. Press and hold the power button for 15s, then release, followed by a single press and release\n7. **Confirm all internal connections are seated and secured tightly** – Double check all cable connections, especially those that deliver power to hardware, as they can become dislodged over time\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n- Specific photo requirements are dependent on the tasks performed and will be communicated upon the resolution of the issue\n- Confirmation from \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team that work has been completed or approval to leave site has been given.\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- If clarification, issues or questions is needed on work order, discuss with Work Order Manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact:\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager\n\n**NOTE: During your visit, please perform a general visual inspection of the site. If you observe any abnormal or unusual conditions—including, but not limited to, billboard damage, electrical issues, installation deficiencies, loose or exposed wiring, missing conduits, unsealed penetrations, signs of tampering, or any other condition that appears out of the ordinary—please document the issue with clear photos and notify us immediately before leaving the site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T08:00","end":"2026-10-15T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":165},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35.686879904764865},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/5/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10