{"job":{"id":20098349,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SHI - Corp Services","title":"**MUST HAVE REAL ID - READ REQUIREMENTS** VOIP (2) | Thin client (2) | Pin Pad (1) | Printer - Removal | Install | Config ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope Summary:</u></strong></p><p>Perform inventory, remove old, install new, Configure and test the following:</p><ul><li>VoIP Phones</li><li>Pin Pads</li><li>Printer</li><li>Thin Clients</li></ul><p><strong>**All work outlined below has been approved; any work out-of-scope will require authorization from the Work Order Manager.</strong></p><p><strong><u>PRE-SITE INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p><ol><li>MUST Review INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS before going onsite (Attached)</li><li>MUST print Inventory Checklist (Attached)</li><li>MUST print Checkout Form (Attached)&nbsp;</li><li>Review this Work Order in its entirety</li></ol><p><br></p><p>1.\tVerify Inventory with inventory list attached to work order.&nbsp;Note – pin pads are shipped separately</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>VOIP PHONES:</u></strong></p><ol><li>REVIEW CISCO VOIP INSTALL PDF (attached)</li><li>Verify Phone MAC addresses and Count from Inventory Checklist</li><li>Assemble the phone bases and install handset and cord</li><li>Start installing phones</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>NOTE: </strong>They are NOT assigned to any particular area</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>NOTE:</strong> THE THIN CLIENTS ARE DAISY CHAINED TO PHONES</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unplug the network cable and the thin client cable from OLD phone</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install NEW phone - connect network cable ONLY</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">WAIT until the phone is completely powered on and showing call screen</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect (NEW OR EXISTING) thin client cable to phone (may need to reboot thin client)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Make test call TO/FROM phone</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Have customer log into the thin client - verify connectivity</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">UPLOAD PICTURE OF NEWLY INSTALLED PHONE FOR EACH WORKSTATION</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PIN PADS: </u></strong></p><ol><li>Verify Pin Pads</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work order manager will give you list of pin pad serials and MACs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Before installing - Make sure the cords in the box go with the pin pad in same box – the cords have the MAC addresses on them</li><li>Remove old pin pad #1 and install NEW pin pad #1</li><li>Activate Pin Pad #1 – text work order manager when online, wait for activation code&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Activation code will be received from support to work order manager.&nbsp;A pop up will show on the pin pad when ready to enter the code</li><li>Install and Activate rest of Pin Pads: PP2, PP3, etc. text work order manager when ready for activation codes.&nbsp;</li><li>Upload pictures of new Pin Pads (label pictures, PP1, PP2, ETC)</li><li>Collect all old pin pads, upload a photo, and place them in the box.</li></ol><p><strong><u>PRINTER:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Install the printer – replace old printer that has the fax line (DO NOT update any settings)&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Notify work order manager when printer is plugged into network and fax line connected</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For the initial set up questions – answer NO to all</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable health apps – NO</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable print from USB – NO</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable web updates – NO</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable Auto send – NO</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">DO NOT update any fax settings</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of old printer + serial (label picture)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of new printer powered on showing menu + serial (label picture)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Support configures the printer remotely – work order manager will let you know when to send a test fax.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Test Fax number: 470-300-7965 (some sites need the “1” before area code)</li></ol><p><strong><u>THIN CLIENTS:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Install all the thin clients&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Start with TC01 at front of store and work your way back of store</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of stacked OLD thin clients</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of each NEW thin clients + Monitor with corresponding TC (label pictures)</li><li>Have associates log into thin clients</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Username: “store number”@nationalvision.com&nbsp;&nbsp;Password: Store’s email password</li><li>Notify work order manager when all or most thin clients are installed (Support will run the printer scripts)</li><li>Work order manager will let you know when store associates can start test printing&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Have Associates Test Printing</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Let work order manager know if there are any issues</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Let associates know the new scan steps on new printer: home screen scroll to &gt; Quicksets &gt; select - papercapture-xxxx</li></ol><p><strong><u>PACK UP EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><ol><li>All <strong><u>OLD equipment </u></strong>- pack in box, SEAL with tape and mark on box <strong>\"SHIP TO GEORGIA COMPUTERS\"</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Shipping label will be sent to manager from support</li><li><strong>ANY NEW UN-USED/EXTRA EQUIPMENT</strong> – will be <strong>sent back to SHI “Knox”</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of serial numbers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mark on checkout list which equipment needs to be sent back</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place in SEPARATE BOX and give to manager</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Shipping label will be sent to manager from support</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>&nbsp;DELIVERABLES: </strong>(see examples on last page)</p><p>LABEL EACH PICTURE WITH STORE NUMBER – DEVICE NUMBER - NEW OR OLD&nbsp;</p><p>•\tGroup old Pin Pads together and upload picture</p><p>•\tTake picture of each NEW pin pad</p><p>•\tStack old TC to side and upload picture</p><p>•\tTake picture of NEW TC showing bar code and monitor logged in&nbsp;</p><p>•\tTake picture of old printer and serial</p><p>•\tTake picture of new printer, serial, test fax</p><p>•\tTake picture of boxed up OLD equipment</p><p>•\tTake picture of NEW Un-used / EXTRA equipment being sent back to SHI “Knox”</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>NOTE:</strong> IF you need to join the “bridge” – here is the number.&nbsp;Your work order manager will let you know if you need to join call to troubleshoot with support.&nbsp;+1 567-202-9816,,774512330#</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cable</li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Keystones</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Patch Cables</li><li>Working Label Maker - with labels</li><li>Cat6 Cable - approx. 200ft</li></ul><p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p><p>Please call the work order manager for any questions or issues while on-site</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed</li><li>Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job</li><li>Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost below</li><li>Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Material Reimbursement:</u></strong></p><p>Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot</p><p>Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea</p><p>Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea</p><p>Faceplate $3.50 / ea</p><p>Keystones $5.00/ea</p><p>Cable ends $2.50/ea</p>","markdown":"**Scope Summary:**\n\nPerform inventory, remove old, install new, Configure and test the following:\n\n- VoIP Phones\n- Pin Pads\n- Printer\n- Thin Clients\n\n**\\*\\*All work outlined below has been approved; any work out-of-scope will require authorization from the Work Order Manager.**\n\n**PRE-SITE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. MUST Review INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS before going onsite (Attached)\n2. MUST print Inventory Checklist (Attached)\n3. MUST print Checkout Form (Attached)\n4. Review this Work Order in its entirety\n\n1\\. Verify Inventory with inventory list attached to work order. Note – pin pads are shipped separately\n\n**VOIP PHONES:**\n\n1. REVIEW CISCO VOIP INSTALL PDF (attached)\n2. Verify Phone MAC addresses and Count from Inventory Checklist\n3. Assemble the phone bases and install handset and cord\n4. Start installing phones\n5. **NOTE:** They are NOT assigned to any particular area\n6. **NOTE:** THE THIN CLIENTS ARE DAISY CHAINED TO PHONES\n7. Unplug the network cable and the thin client cable from OLD phone\n8. Install NEW phone - connect network cable ONLY\n9. WAIT until the phone is completely powered on and showing call screen\n10. Connect (NEW OR EXISTING) thin client cable to phone (may need to reboot thin client)\n11. Make test call TO/FROM phone\n12. Have customer log into the thin client - verify connectivity\n13. UPLOAD PICTURE OF NEWLY INSTALLED PHONE FOR EACH WORKSTATION\n\n**PIN PADS:**\n\n1. Verify Pin Pads\n2. Work order manager will give you list of pin pad serials and MACs\n3. Before installing - Make sure the cords in the box go with the pin pad in same box – the cords have the MAC addresses on them\n4. Remove old pin pad #1 and install NEW pin pad #1\n5. Activate Pin Pad #1 – text work order manager when online, wait for activation code\n6. Activation code will be received from support to work order manager. A pop up will show on the pin pad when ready to enter the code\n7. Install and Activate rest of Pin Pads: PP2, PP3, etc. text work order manager when ready for activation codes.\n8. Upload pictures of new Pin Pads (label pictures, PP1, PP2, ETC)\n9. Collect all old pin pads, upload a photo, and place them in the box.\n\n**PRINTER:**\n\n1. Install the printer – replace old printer that has the fax line (DO NOT update any settings)\n2. Notify work order manager when printer is plugged into network and fax line connected\n3. For the initial set up questions – answer NO to all\n4. Enable health apps – NO\n5. Enable print from USB – NO\n6. Enable web updates – NO\n7. Enable Auto send – NO\n8. DO NOT update any fax settings\n9. Upload picture of old printer + serial (label picture)\n10. Upload picture of new printer powered on showing menu + serial (label picture)\n11. Support configures the printer remotely – work order manager will let you know when to send a test fax.\n12. Test Fax number: 470-300-7965 (some sites need the “1” before area code)\n\n**THIN CLIENTS:**\n\n1. Install all the thin clients\n2. Start with TC01 at front of store and work your way back of store\n3. Upload picture of stacked OLD thin clients\n4. Upload picture of each NEW thin clients + Monitor with corresponding TC (label pictures)\n5. Have associates log into thin clients\n6. Username: “store number”@nationalvision.com Password: Store’s email password\n7. Notify work order manager when all or most thin clients are installed (Support will run the printer scripts)\n8. Work order manager will let you know when store associates can start test printing\n9. Have Associates Test Printing\n10. Let work order manager know if there are any issues\n11. Let associates know the new scan steps on new printer: home screen scroll to > Quicksets > select - papercapture-xxxx\n\n**PACK UP EQUIPMENT**\n\n1. All **OLD equipment** - pack in box, SEAL with tape and mark on box **\"SHIP TO GEORGIA COMPUTERS\"**\n2. Upload picture\n3. Shipping label will be sent to manager from support\n4. **ANY NEW UN-USED/EXTRA EQUIPMENT** – will be **sent back to SHI “Knox”**\n5. Upload picture of serial numbers\n6. Mark on checkout list which equipment needs to be sent back\n7. Place in SEPARATE BOX and give to manager\n8. Shipping label will be sent to manager from support\n\n **DELIVERABLES:** (see examples on last page)\n\nLABEL EACH PICTURE WITH STORE NUMBER – DEVICE NUMBER - NEW OR OLD\n\n• Group old Pin Pads together and upload picture\n\n• Take picture of each NEW pin pad\n\n• Stack old TC to side and upload picture\n\n• Take picture of NEW TC showing bar code and monitor logged in\n\n• Take picture of old printer and serial\n\n• Take picture of new printer, serial, test fax\n\n• Take picture of boxed up OLD equipment\n\n• Take picture of NEW Un-used / EXTRA equipment being sent back to SHI “Knox”\n\n**NOTE:** IF you need to join the “bridge” – here is the number. Your work order manager will let you know if you need to join call to troubleshoot with support. +1 567-202-9816,,774512330#\n\n**Required Tools Needed:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cable\n- Cable Toner\n- Keystones\n- Crimper\n- Patch Cables\n- Working Label Maker - with labels\n- Cat6 Cable - approx. 200ft\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nPlease call the work order manager for any questions or issues while on-site\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nPolo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed\n- Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job\n- Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost below\n- Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.\n\n**Material Reimbursement:**\n\nCat6 Cables .52 cents per foot\n\nCat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea\n\nCat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea\n\nFaceplate $3.50 / ea\n\nKeystones $5.00/ea\n\nCable ends $2.50/ea","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T08:00","end":"2026-10-27T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":56.97587196488124},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791211174873}
