{"job":{"id":20099780,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Armor Security","title":"7 Brew Granite 8 Camera System Installation (Cables already ran)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Install 8 Cameras and Monitor with Mount</strong></p>\n<p>Mount TV Monitor as far into the corner as possible and as close to the ceiling as possible</p>\n<p><strong>All photos &amp; tasks must be uploaded in the Armor App and completed before payment will be approved.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Tech must bring a monitor, keyboard and mouse</u></strong> for troubleshooting</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>NOTE: If permanent power is not yet installed at site, you will be asked to return on a separate ticket to complete connection and verification of system.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Equipment provided:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>NVR</li>\n<li>Pre-labeled IP Cameras (3 Interior Turrets, 5 Exterior Bullets)</li>\n<li>32\" Monitor with mount</li>\n<li>Layout Drawing (in box and attached to Work Order)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>RJ45 tools (crimper, tester, tips)</li>\n<li>Cordless Drill w/ #2 Philips bit or #2 Philips Screw driver</li>\n<li>Silicone weather sealant</li>\n<li>6' ladder</li>\n<li>Little giant ladder</li>\n<li>Normal hand tools</li>\n<li>1 1/2\" Sheetrock screws</li>\n<li>3\" Sheetrock screws (For Outside Cameras)</li>\n<li>Monitor</li>\n<li>Keyboard and mouse</li>\n<li>Headlamp/flashlight</li>\n<li>100' Cat5 Cable (just in case)</li>\n<li><strong>See Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.​</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Work Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>All cameras must be placed in the correct location according to layout drawing as shown below by IP address (see layout)</li>\n<li>All cables must be labeled on both ends with labels provided by Armor (in the 101 camera box)</li>\n<li>When mounting the cameras, all cable must be concealed and ceiling tiles must be down and flat</li>\n<li>Install NVR on top shelf of IT rack in the bathroom with switch on top of NVR, connected to Fortinet Switch Port 2</li>\n<li>Monitor securely mounted inside on drop pole on front Drive-Side of building as high and far into the corner as possible (see layout)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Be sure to use the correct camera in the correct location (per provided floor plan):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>101 -Ext Back Door</li>\n<li>102 - Ext Front</li>\n<li>103 - Ext Shot Side 1</li>\n<li>104 - Ext Shot Side 2</li>\n<li>105 - Ext Milk Side</li>\n<li>106 - Back of Shop (Front of stand opposite side of the monitor looking back into the prep area)</li>\n<li>107 - Back Door</li>\n<li>108 - Front of Shop (Back of prep area looking toward front of stand)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>If there are any questions about camera views, TEXT OR CALL THE WORK ORDER MANAGER!</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Before leaving - you must:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clean all the areas you worked and make sure all the ceiling tiles are back in&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Verify the camera angles by texting a photo of all camera views on the monitor to the Work Order Manager</li>\n<li>Verify cable maintenance by texting a photo of all the cables in the office to the Work Order Manager</li>\n<li>Take any unused equipment with you to ship back to Work Order Manager (request return shipping label)</li>\n<li>Verify that the Work Order Manager can login to the system</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>** All unused equipment must be returned to Armor Security with its original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label. **</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>If, for whatever reason, we have to reschedule based on our error, i.e. equipment not being on site, we will pay $30 travel fee.&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p><strong>By accepting the work order you are agreeing to Armor Security’s Standard Instructions and Policies &amp; Procedures terms.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Install 8 Cameras and Monitor with Mount**\n\nMount TV Monitor as far into the corner as possible and as close to the ceiling as possible\n\n**All photos & tasks must be uploaded in the Armor App and completed before payment will be approved.**\n\n**Tech must bring a monitor, keyboard and mouse** for troubleshooting\n\n**NOTE: If permanent power is not yet installed at site, you will be asked to return on a separate ticket to complete connection and verification of system.**\n\n**Equipment provided:**\n\n- NVR\n- Pre-labeled IP Cameras (3 Interior Turrets, 5 Exterior Bullets)\n- 32\" Monitor with mount\n- Layout Drawing (in box and attached to Work Order)\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- RJ45 tools (crimper, tester, tips)\n- Cordless Drill w/ #2 Philips bit or #2 Philips Screw driver\n- Silicone weather sealant\n- 6' ladder\n- Little giant ladder\n- Normal hand tools\n- 1 1/2\" Sheetrock screws\n- 3\" Sheetrock screws (For Outside Cameras)\n- Monitor\n- Keyboard and mouse\n- Headlamp/flashlight\n- 100' Cat5 Cable (just in case)\n- **See Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.​**\n\n**Work Completion Requirements:**\n\n1. All cameras must be placed in the correct location according to layout drawing as shown below by IP address (see layout)\n2. All cables must be labeled on both ends with labels provided by Armor (in the 101 camera box)\n3. When mounting the cameras, all cable must be concealed and ceiling tiles must be down and flat\n4. Install NVR on top shelf of IT rack in the bathroom with switch on top of NVR, connected to Fortinet Switch Port 2\n5. Monitor securely mounted inside on drop pole on front Drive-Side of building as high and far into the corner as possible (see layout)\n\n**Be sure to use the correct camera in the correct location (per provided floor plan):**\n\n- 101 -Ext Back Door\n- 102 - Ext Front\n- 103 - Ext Shot Side 1\n- 104 - Ext Shot Side 2\n- 105 - Ext Milk Side\n- 106 - Back of Shop (Front of stand opposite side of the monitor looking back into the prep area)\n- 107 - Back Door\n- 108 - Front of Shop (Back of prep area looking toward front of stand)\n\n**If there are any questions about camera views, TEXT OR CALL THE WORK ORDER MANAGER!**\n\n**Before leaving - you must:**\n\n- Clean all the areas you worked and make sure all the ceiling tiles are back in\n- Verify the camera angles by texting a photo of all camera views on the monitor to the Work Order Manager\n- Verify cable maintenance by texting a photo of all the cables in the office to the Work Order Manager\n- Take any unused equipment with you to ship back to Work Order Manager (request return shipping label)\n- Verify that the Work Order Manager can login to the system\n\n\\*\\* All unused equipment must be returned to Armor Security with its original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label. \\*\\*\n\n*If, for whatever reason, we have to reschedule based on our error, i.e. equipment not being on site, we will pay $30 travel fee.*\n\n**By accepting the work order you are agreeing to Armor Security’s Standard Instructions and Policies & Procedures terms.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T10:00","end":"2026-10-16T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":21.61890777478729},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"st