{"job":{"id":19990385,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #299448 - KMS Install - 10-7-26 @ 10:30 PM - Durham, NC","description":{"html":"<p>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction. The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************</p><p>DISPATCH ETA: 10-07 -26 @ 10:30 PM </p><p>This site will have 11 - KMS monitors</p><p>This should only take 10-12 hours.</p><p><br></p><p>You must read all documentation before arriving on site.</p><p>You must follow the SOW and Sign Off document to the letter.</p><p>You must follow \"pictures needed document\".</p><p>Be sure to take before pictures as well as completion pictures which instructions for are outlined in the SOW.</p><p>Before pictures of each terminal before swap out, to prevent any he said/she said.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************</p><p><br></p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA @ 940-323-2600</p><p>TECH MUST CALL MARIO CASAS AT <del>************</del> WHEN YOU ARRIVE AND AFTER FIRST TERMINAL INSTALL AND UPON COMPLETION.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>TRCA will call you the day before. You must answer your phone or call back ASAP to confirm that you are still good to go for the morning appointment.</p><p>TRCA will call you 1 to 2 hours prior of time scheduled to confirm again. You must answer you phone again to confirm. This is per our customer.</p><p>****************************************************************** </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cheesecake Factory is using a new terminal, the Toshiba 810F terminals. The supporting docs are written specifically for this terminal and show specifically where all of the peripherals will need to be connected and how the terminals are mounted to either the stand or brackets along with the proper cable management</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Project Description &amp; Scope of Work</p><p>Replace all existing PAR M7700 &amp; 6150 Front Desk terminals with Toshiba 810E terminals. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>MUST: AFTER EACH TERMINAL INSTALL, TECH MUST CONTACT MARIO CASAS AND SEND PICTURES TO TEST AND GET APPROVAL OF INSTALLATION AND CABLE MANAGEMENT.</p><p>IF IT IS NOT DONE PROPERLY AS PER THE ATTACHED INSTALL GUIDE, THE TECH WILL NEED TO FIX AND CONTACT MARIO AND SEND PICTURES AGAIN. THEN AND ONLY THEN CAN YOU MOVE TO THE NEXT TERMINAL.</p><p>DO NOT INSTALL THE NEXT TERMINAL UNTIL YOU HAVE APPROVAL OF HOW IT SHOULD BE INSTALLED AND TESTED BY MARIO CASAS.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment &amp; Supplies</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Toshiba 810E Terminals (configured and labeled by name)</p><p>Silver Screws for Monitors on Channel</p><p>Long shaft Phillips Screwdriver for tilt brackets</p><p>Velcro (Do NOT use wire ties)</p><p>(9) 7ft Black Patch Cables</p><p>(2) 3ft Black Null Modem for Expo &amp; Runner; (1) GLC Pasta Monitor</p><p>7ft Black Null Modem for FQM</p><p>(6) 90 Degree Power Cord for Channel Power Supplies</p><p>“Extras Bag” This will contain a 10ft CATV &amp; 2 extra 7ft power cables – You will only use these items as needed</p><p>Printer Cable for 810E Runner, Expo &amp; FQM (COM port1) – 3ft RJ45 to DB25M</p><p><br></p><p>Power drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to install stands</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Charged Camera Phone</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment &amp; Supplies to be Provided by Technician</p><p>Power Drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to remove/install brackets</p><p>Charged Camera Phone</p><p>Velcro</p><p>Gloves - as some of the terminals may be dirty.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Scope of Work</p><p>Replace all existing KMS terminals on the Expo &amp; Cook’s line with Toshiba 810E terminals.</p><p>Note: Before disassembling any stations, ask the managers if they currently have issues with any equipment related to this exchange (specifically printers); have them test printing for you (or use their card to do so) so that you do not spend time troubleshooting (previously) broken printers at the end of install.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Arrive at 10:30 PM; check in with the Manager; locate equipment and compare against shipping manifest.</p><p>Replace KMS Monitors, power supplies &amp; CATV cables; organize power, printer and data cables with Velcro.</p><p>Test KMS Monitors &amp; attached peripherals.</p><p>Take front and back pictures of installed equipment.</p><p>Re-box the old equipment in Toshiba boxes and add shipping label; these will go to Homeboys Disposal.</p><p>Walkthrough with manager on duty to validate installation or discuss issues.</p><p>You will work with remote engineer contact Mario Casas with CBS at <del>************</del></p><p>Locate equipment and verify amount on-site; if the number doesn’t match, contact Mario.</p><p>Guests may still be in the restaurant when you arrive; if so, start un-boxing all the equipment in the back of the house in an area not being used by staff or a closed dining room at the management’s discretion.</p><p>There will be cleaners in the restaurant cleaning until morning. We have asked the managers to tell the cleaners to work around you and clean the cooks’ line last; ask managers to remind the cleaners again.</p><p>Start with the Expo line (Runner, Expo, and FQM) and work your way onto the cook’s line.</p><p>If a monitor is powered off, before removing, turn it back on so you know which monitor you are replacing (read the name on the screen, not the sticker, because it is not always correct). Turn off, unplug cables from monitor &amp; place to the side.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Items/Information to Retrieve from Closing Manager</p><p>Arrive on-site at time provided by your project manager; introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty (MOD) as the CBS Technician who will be performing the overnight KMS installation. Let them know you will need the below items before they leave for the night. Ask them to direct you to the shipment of equipment from CBS. Verify the amount against the order detail list; if anything is missing, contact your Project Manager, immediately. Once equipment inventory has been verified and the area you will be working in is closed down for the night (all food/stations are covered) you can begin installing.</p><p>• Manger MAG Card; This will be used for tested after install.</p><p>• Reimaging Thumb Drive; This will only be needed if any terminals do not load properly from PKI SETUP.</p><p>• FedEx Pickup Location; You will need to ask the managers where to put the boxes of old equipment after install.</p><p>• Shipping Tape; This will used to pack up the outgoing equipment, once the installation is complete.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>THIS IS A MUST PICTURES:</p><p>Example pictures show what the installation should look like when complete. There are additional pictures for the POS and KMS that show the testing of the devices and what the expectation is once those devices have been installed. As requested, the tech should be taking a picture of each station as that station is completed and sending those pictures immediately to Mario Casas for his review. This is to avoid any issues with asking for pictures after the tech has left the site and should also avoid any issues or questions about cable management with the terminals that are being installed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment Disposal</p><p>Box the 7700 &amp; 6150 PAR equipment, when possible, always pack 2 par terminals, power supplies and data cables ONLY in 1 Toshiba 810 box with protective covering.</p><p>Ask Manager for packaging tape. Seal and attach the provided UPS shipping label over the old label for Homeboy’s disposal. OST will contact UPS to schedule pick up.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Pictures:</p><p>NOTE: - Need before and after pictures of each terminal and cable management. THIS IS A MUST</p><p>Take Pictures (Pictures are VERY IMPORTANT and used throughout the year for troubleshoot &amp; remodels)</p><p>- At each location take a full front &amp; back view of monitors &amp; brackets plus cable organization.</p><p>- E-mail pictures or upload to pmt@trca.com before leaving site.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cheesecake Factory has asked us to relay to the techs doing the work is that they want clear pictures of work completed. The docs I have address what kind of pictures we need for each TLP completed. Cheesecake Factory is also asking that we submit pictures to them with 24 hours of completion of the TLP. We would greatly appreciate if you could assist us in getting these pictures submitted in a timely manner.</p>","markdown":"Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction. The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nDISPATCH ETA: 10-07 -26 @ 10:30 PM\n\nThis site will have 11 - KMS monitors\n\nThis should only take 10-12 hours.\n\nYou must read all documentation before arriving on site.\n\nYou must follow the SOW and Sign Off document to the letter.\n\nYou must follow \"pictures needed document\".\n\nBe sure to take before pictures as well as completion pictures which instructions for are outlined in the SOW.\n\nBefore pictures of each terminal before swap out, to prevent any he said/she said.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA @ 940-323-2600\n\nTECH MUST CALL MARIO CASAS AT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* WHEN YOU ARRIVE AND AFTER FIRST TERMINAL INSTALL AND UPON COMPLETION.\n\nTRCA will call you the day before. You must answer your phone or call back ASAP to confirm that you are still good to go for the morning appointment.\n\nTRCA will call you 1 to 2 hours prior of time scheduled to confirm again. You must answer you phone again to confirm. This is per our customer.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCheesecake Factory is using a new terminal, the Toshiba 810F terminals. The supporting docs are written specifically for this terminal and show specifically where all of the peripherals will need to be connected and how the terminals are mounted to either the stand or brackets along with the proper cable management\n\nProject Description & Scope of Work\n\nReplace all existing PAR M7700 & 6150 Front Desk terminals with Toshiba 810E terminals.\n\nMUST: AFTER EACH TERMINAL INSTALL, TECH MUST CONTACT MARIO CASAS AND SEND PICTURES TO TEST AND GET APPROVAL OF INSTALLATION AND CABLE MANAGEMENT.\n\nIF IT IS NOT DONE PROPERLY AS PER THE ATTACHED INSTALL GUIDE, THE TECH WILL NEED TO FIX AND CONTACT MARIO AND SEND PICTURES AGAIN. THEN AND ONLY THEN CAN YOU MOVE TO THE NEXT TERMINAL.\n\nDO NOT INSTALL THE NEXT TERMINAL UNTIL YOU HAVE APPROVAL OF HOW IT SHOULD BE INSTALLED AND TESTED BY MARIO CASAS.\n\nEquipment & Supplies\n\nToshiba 810E Terminals (configured and labeled by name)\n\nSilver Screws for Monitors on Channel\n\nLong shaft Phillips Screwdriver for tilt brackets\n\nVelcro (Do NOT use wire ties)\n\n(9) 7ft Black Patch Cables\n\n(2) 3ft Black Null Modem for Expo & Runner; (1) GLC Pasta Monitor\n\n7ft Black Null Modem for FQM\n\n(6) 90 Degree Power Cord for Channel Power Supplies\n\n“Extras Bag” This will contain a 10ft CATV & 2 extra 7ft power cables – You will only use these items as needed\n\nPrinter Cable for 810E Runner, Expo & FQM (COM port1) – 3ft RJ45 to DB25M\n\nPower drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to install stands\n\nCharged Camera Phone\n\nEquipment & Supplies to be Provided by Technician\n\nPower Drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to remove/install brackets\n\nCharged Camera Phone\n\nVelcro\n\nGloves - as some of the terminals may be dirty.\n\n Scope of Work\n\nReplace all existing KMS terminals on the Expo & Cook’s line with Toshiba 810E terminals.\n\nNote: Before disassembling any stations, ask the managers if they currently have issues with any equipment related to this exchange (specifically printers); have them test printing for you (or use their card to do so) so that you do not spend time troubleshooting (previously) broken printers at the end of install.\n\nArrive at 10:30 PM; check in with the Manager; locate equipment and compare against shipping manifest.\n\nReplace KMS Monitors, power supplies & CATV cables; organize power, printer and data cables with Velcro.\n\nTest KMS Monitors & attached peripherals.\n\nTake front and back pictures of installed equipment.\n\nRe-box the old equipment in Toshiba boxes and add shipping label; these will go to Homeboys Disposal.\n\nWalkthrough with manager on duty to validate installation or discuss issues.\n\nYou will work with remote engineer contact Mario Casas with CBS at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLocate equipment and verify amount on-site; if the number doesn’t match, contact Mario.\n\nGuests may still be in the restaurant when you arrive; if so, start un-boxing all the equipment in the back of the house in an area not being used by staff or a closed dining room at the management’s discretion.\n\nThere will be cleaners in the restaurant cleaning until morning. We have asked the managers to tell the cleaners to work around you and clean the cooks’ line last; ask managers to remind the cleaners again.\n\nStart with the Expo line (Runner, Expo, and FQM) and work your way onto the cook’s line.\n\nIf a monitor is powered off, before removing, turn it back on so you know which monitor you are replacing (read the name on the screen, not the sticker, because it is not always correct). Turn off, unplug cables from monitor & place to the side.\n\nItems/Information to Retrieve from Closing Manager\n\nArrive on-site at time provided by your project manager; introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty (MOD) as the CBS Technician who will be performing the overnight KMS installation. Let them know you will need the below items before they leave for the night. Ask them to direct you to the shipment of equipment from CBS. Verify the amount against the order detail list; if anything is missing, contact your Project Manager, immediately. Once equipment inventory has been verified and the area you will be working in is closed down for the night (all food/stations are covered) you can begin installing.\n\n• Manger MAG Card; This will be used for tested after install.\n\n• Reimaging Thumb Drive; This will only be needed if any terminals do not load properly from PKI SETUP.\n\n• FedEx Pickup Location; You will need to ask the managers where to put the boxes of old equipment after install.\n\n• Shipping Tape; This will used to pack up the outgoing equipment, once the installation is complete.\n\nTHIS IS A MUST PICTURES:\n\nExample pictures show what the installation should look like when complete. There are additional pictures for the POS and KMS that show the testing of the devices and what the expectation is once those devices have been installed. As requested, the tech should be taking a picture of each station as that station is completed and sending those pictures immediately to Mario Casas for his review. This is to avoid any issues with asking for pictures after the tech has left the site and should also avoid any issues or questions about cable management with the terminals that are being installed.\n\nEquipment Disposal\n\nBox the 7700 & 6150 PAR equipment, when possible, always pack 2 par terminals, power supplies and data cables ONLY in 1 Toshiba 810 box with protective covering.\n\nAsk Manager for packaging tape. Seal and attach the provided UPS shipping label over the old label for Homeboy’s disposal. OST will contact UPS to schedule pick up.\n\nPictures:\n\nNOTE: - Need before and after pictures of each terminal and cable management. THIS IS A MUST\n\nTake Pictures (Pictures are VERY IMPORTANT and used throughout the year for troubleshoot & remodels)\n\n\\- At each location take a full front & back view of monitors & brackets plus cable organization.\n\n\\- E-mail pictures or upload to pmt@trca.com before leaving site.\n\nCheesecake Factory has asked us to relay to the techs doing the work is that they want clear pictures of work completed. The docs I have address what kind of pictures we need for each TLP completed. Cheesecake Factory is also asking that we submit pictures to them with 24 hours of completion of the TLP. We would greatly appreciate if you could assist us in getting these pictures submitted in a timely manner.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T22:30","end":"2026-10-07T34:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":660},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":12,"distance":11.449036227090321},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Oct 7, 10:30 PM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 7, Thu, Oct 8, Fri, Oct 9 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791216190685}
{"job":{"id":20100565,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"PPT1029332 Power Supply Issue","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Service Overview:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> </p><p><strong>**** ACTION PLAN *****</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>------- Created by Team -------</strong></p><p>PPT L3 Support</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>------ Current Issue -------</strong></p><p><strong>Intermittent power failures on Apollo 2000 chassis</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------ Evidence of the Issue -------</strong></p><p>Customer reports, server node IML logs.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------ Special Instructions -------</strong></p><p><strong>Have server administrator copy/backup any HDD/RAID controller encryption keys and passwords before any hardware replacement.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------ Parts -------</strong></p><p>(Qty 1) 879834-001 = Apollo 2xxx PDB Board</p><p><br></p><p><strong>(Note: If a TPM is installed in the system a TPM will need to be ordered as well as the system board if a system board is needed)</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------ Detailed Steps to Resolve -------</strong></p><p><strong>Tech to schedule service with customer.</strong></p><p><strong>Action plan will require full chassis outage.</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Power down all blades in the Apollo 2600 chassis with serial number 2M29430423</li><li>Uncable the chassis, making sure to label or note where all cables go for recabling</li><li>Extend the chassis to the service position, or remove from the rack</li><li>Follow the procedure for removing and replacing the PDB Assembly (starts on page 44 of the HPE Apollo 2000 Gen10 Chassis Maintenance and Service Guide, linked in supporting documents)</li><li>Once replaced, rerack or return the chassis to operating position, and recable the chassis</li><li>Power up the chassis and blades</li><li>Confirm no additional or new errors are present in the iLO of the blades</li><li>Monitor for recurrence</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------ Supporting Documents -------</strong></p><p>HPE Apollo 2000 Gen10 Chassis Maintenance and Service Guide</p><p>https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/docDisplay?docId=a00027940en_us&amp;docLocale=en_US</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>------- Timeline -------</strong></p><p><strong>Next Steps: </strong>Field Engineer to call customer to schedule service and follow Action Plan above.</p><p><strong>Next Owner</strong>: Field Engineer</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>*****&nbsp;End Action Plan&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;*****</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions</strong></p><p>As a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.</p><p><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:</strong> Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a <strong>$20 USD deduction</strong> from the total work order pay.</p><p><strong>Escalations</strong></p><ol><li>Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li><li>For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li></ol><p>Consumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.</p><p>Upon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).</p><p>Upon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.</p><p>All parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.</p><p>PLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.</p><p>Return of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.</p><p>If a part is removed from a local warehouse:</p><p>A. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>B. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>YOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.</p><p>Acceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:</p><ul><li>State ID</li><li>Driver's License</li><li>US Passport</li></ul><p>ALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:</p><ul><li>Laptop computer</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)</li><li>Standard tool kit</li><li>Static mat and/or static strap</li><li>Heat Sink Paste</li><li>Blank CD's/DVD's</li><li>Portable CD/DVD drive</li><li>USB Flash drive</li><li>Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable</li><li>Hot Spot</li><li>Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed</li></ul><p>Tech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.</p><p>Tech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.</p><p>Tech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:</p><p><strong>NO JEANS</strong></p><p><strong>NO OPEN-TOE SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO GYM SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING</strong></p><p>IMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.</p><p>If the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.</p><p><strong>Software Policy</strong></p><p>Policy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code</p><p>1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.</p><p>2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.</p><p>3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.</p><p>4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner</p><ul><li>5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Service Overview:**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* ACTION PLAN \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**------- Created by Team -------**\n\nPPT L3 Support\n\n**------ Current Issue -------**\n\n**Intermittent power failures on Apollo 2000 chassis**\n\n**------ Evidence of the Issue -------**\n\nCustomer reports, server node IML logs.\n\n**------ Special Instructions -------**\n\n**Have server administrator copy/backup any HDD/RAID controller encryption keys and passwords before any hardware replacement.**\n\n**------ Parts -------**\n\n(Qty 1) 879834-001 = Apollo 2xxx PDB Board\n\n**(Note: If a TPM is installed in the system a TPM will need to be ordered as well as the system board if a system board is needed)**\n\n**------ Detailed Steps to Resolve -------**\n\n**Tech to schedule service with customer.**\n\n**Action plan will require full chassis outage.**\n\n- Power down all blades in the Apollo 2600 chassis with serial number 2M29430423\n- Uncable the chassis, making sure to label or note where all cables go for recabling\n- Extend the chassis to the service position, or remove from the rack\n- Follow the procedure for removing and replacing the PDB Assembly (starts on page 44 of the HPE Apollo 2000 Gen10 Chassis Maintenance and Service Guide, linked in supporting documents)\n- Once replaced, rerack or return the chassis to operating position, and recable the chassis\n- Power up the chassis and blades\n- Confirm no additional or new errors are present in the iLO of the blades\n- Monitor for recurrence\n\n**------ Supporting Documents -------**\n\nHPE Apollo 2000 Gen10 Chassis Maintenance and Service Guide\n\nhttps://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/docDisplay?docId=a00027940en_us&amp;docLocale=en_US\n\n**------- Timeline -------**\n\n**Next Steps:** Field Engineer to call customer to schedule service and follow Action Plan above.\n\n**Next Owner**: Field Engineer\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* End Action Plan \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Special Instructions**\n\nAs a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.\n\n**MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:** Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a **$20 USD deduction** from the total work order pay.\n\n**Escalations**\n\n1. Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n2. For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n\nConsumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.\n\nUpon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).\n\nUpon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.\n\nAll parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.\n\nPLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.\n\nReturn of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.\n\nIf a part is removed from a local warehouse:\n\nA. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nB. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nYOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.\n\nAcceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:\n\n- State ID\n- Driver's License\n- US Passport\n\nALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:\n\n- Laptop computer\n- Voltmeter\n- Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)\n- Standard tool kit\n- Static mat and/or static strap\n- Heat Sink Paste\n- Blank CD's/DVD's\n- Portable CD/DVD drive\n- USB Flash drive\n- Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable\n- Hot Spot\n- Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed\n\nTech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.\n\nTech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.\n\nTech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:\n\n**NO JEANS**\n\n**NO OPEN-TOE SHOES**\n\n**NO GYM SHOES**\n\n**NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING**\n\nIMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.\n\nIf the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.\n\n**Software Policy**\n\nPolicy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code\n\n1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.\n\n2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.\n\n3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.\n\n4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner\n\n- 5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T08:00","end":"2026-10-07T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":380,"max":380},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":7.037388443886853},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":190,"baseAmount":380,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1791216331906}
{"job":{"id":20100797,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Titan Protection","title":"Crescent Construction - Replacement of Sim in Mounted Virtual Officer","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting and resolving security camera connectivity issues.</li><li>Tech is required to diagnose and fix connectivity problems between security cameras and the monitoring system or network. This may include checking wiring, verifying network settings, and ensuring proper software configurations.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>12 ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Crimpers</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Volt Meter</li><li>Socket Set</li><li>Torx Screwdriver Set</li><li>Phillips Screwdriver Set</li><li>Allen Wrenches</li><li>Smartphone or Tablet with Camera</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)</li><li>Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.</li><li>Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.</li><li>If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).</li><li>Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).</li><li>Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.</li><li>Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.</li><li>Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.</li><li>Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.</li><li>Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.&nbsp;</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.</li><li>Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting and resolving security camera connectivity issues.\n- Tech is required to diagnose and fix connectivity problems between security cameras and the monitoring system or network. This may include checking wiring, verifying network settings, and ensuring proper software configurations.\n- Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 12 ft A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Crimpers\n- Cable Tester\n- Volt Meter\n- Socket Set\n- Torx Screwdriver Set\n- Phillips Screwdriver Set\n- Allen Wrenches\n- Smartphone or Tablet with Camera\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.\n2. Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)\n3. Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.\n2. Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.\n3. Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.\n4. If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).\n5. Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).\n6. Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.\n7. Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.\n8. Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.\n2. Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.\n3. Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.\n- Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.\n- Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10-08T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":325},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":125},"additional":{"units":2,"a