{"job":{"id":20102378,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Rack and stack of a single server","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Install 1 new server [ThinkSystem SR250 V3]</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Basic Scope:</strong> Technician needed onsite to install new server [ThinkSystem SR250 V3], per <del>***** </del>supplied documentation with connectivity of a single external USB hard drive. Once racked and cabled, the server will need to be validated by the remote team and will require a series of photos. New Equipment and Installation Material will be shipped to site prior to the scheduled date. Device Details and Device S/N(s) will be provided. Site will have 1 New Server Needing Installed.</li><li><strong>Quantity of engineers required:</strong> 1 engineers</li><li><strong>Tools required:</strong> Basic hand tools, Windows based laptop with Wi-Fi and Ethernet capabilities. One strait through RJ45 patch cable (3ft to 6ft in length).</li><li><strong>Supplies required:</strong> Velcro or cable straps</li><li><strong>Number of devices within scope:</strong> QTY 1 ThinkSystem SR250 V3</li><li><strong>Hardware assembly requirements:</strong> Following Lenovo Provided Install guide, install rails and server, install USB Drive and Set Drive on top of the server</li><li><strong>Cabling requirements:</strong> Per provided documentation</li><li><strong>Connectivity to customer network:</strong> Customer assisted</li><li><strong>Estimated duration per engineer:</strong> Approx. 4 hours per engineer, per day</li><li><strong>Service date(s) and times:</strong> Service scheduled 9AM</li><li><strong>Primary point of contact:</strong><del> ***** ****** *** ************ ** ******* ***** *** ************</del></li><li><strong>Remote validation point of contact:</strong> <del>***** ***** ************** ** ****** ****** **************</del></li><li><strong>Technical contact(s):</strong><del> ***** ***** ************** ** ****** ****** **************</del></li><li><strong>Important Photo Requirement </strong>&ndash; Tech MUST take an AFTER Photo(s)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Image of front of server with rack door opened so we can see a clean fit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Image showing the rack door shut to ensure server is properly secured</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Image of where the USB drive is placed in server, preferable like the example image in documentation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If rack is not wall mounted and allows access to the back, please send a photo of the back of the server showing cable placements</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Image of XClarity ID card with MAC.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Important Scope/Customer Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong>• DO NOT update the FN application with your onsite time UNTIL you have ARRIVED at the entrance of the building.</strong></p><p><strong>• Please understand that your check in and check out times are immediately visible to the customer and an escalation will be raised if you are not actually there. Failures will be reported to FN</strong></p><p><strong>• Techs must arrive to site on time and must check in with <del>********* </del>Project Team. The onsite and offsite times you report to the help desk MUST MATCH the times you report into your work order.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-Calls to Tech:</u></strong></p><p><strong>A phone call will be made to you 24 hours prior to the scheduled date to confirm your commitment. An additional 2 hour pre-call will be made too. If for some reason you do not answer nor reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a Contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;</strong><u>not</u>&nbsp;be granted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Upon Arrival To Site</u></strong></p><p><strong>Tech to call int<del>* ***** ******* **** * ***** **********</del> Contacts: Main Contact: <del>***** ****** ******* ************* ****** ******** ******* ***** ******* ************</del></strong></p><p><strong>If onsite customer attempts to add or change the scope that was defined to you during your review with support, call <del>***** ***** ************** ** ****** ****** ************** </del>and advise. Do not tell customer you are unable to complete the scope, wait for further instructions from <del>********* </del>and/or Lenovo.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Prior to leave site</u></strong></p><p><strong>Submit your deliverable so it can be reviewed prior to you leaving site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Once you have submitted, call <del>***** ***** ************** ** ****** ****** **************</del> who will work with Lenovo to get you released from site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Attachments</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>Hardware Checklist</strong> <strong>-</strong> This is a form filled out by the customer explaining the work needed. Please be sure to review and discuss any questions with the client</p><p><strong>Installation Guides -</strong> These must be printed out and reviewed prior to attending the site. If there are any questions please reach out before proceeding.</p><p><strong>Sign Off Form -</strong> You MUST print this release form and take it with you to site. The form must be filled out in its entirety, all arrival and departure times MUST match what is reported to <del>********* </del>when you call them to check in. This form must be signed by the Site contact and be submitted back to <del>********* </del>within 24 hours of completing the service event. <strong>Note:</strong> Incomplete sign off forms will result in penalties. This information is required for us to be paid therefore it will affect your pay if not signed, completed and submitted within 24 hours of completing the service event.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>-^-^-<strong> Attachment &amp; Work Guide Links</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> (1 of 1) Regal Lenovo Server Install Documentation</strong></p><p><strong>Link: </strong><a href=\"https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005FikD/8D5pXzP6YXY0nMLaAphU.vbGfC6P5taIn..OpIlwnY8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005FikD/8D5pXzP6YXY0nMLaAphU.vbGfC6P5taIn..OpIlwnY8</a></p><p><br></p><p><strong>--- End Of Attachment &amp; Work Guide Links</strong> -_-_-</p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Install 1 new server \\[ThinkSystem SR250 V3\\]**\n\n- **Basic Scope:** Technician needed onsite to install new server \\[ThinkSystem SR250 V3\\], per \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* supplied documentation with connectivity of a single external USB hard drive. Once racked and cabled, the server will need to be validated by the remote team and will require a series of photos. New Equipment and Installation Material will be shipped to site prior to the scheduled date. Device Details and Device S/N(s) will be provided. Site will have 1 New Server Needing Installed.\n- **Quantity of engineers required:** 1 engineers\n- **Tools required:** Basic hand tools, Windows based laptop with Wi-Fi and Ethernet capabilities. One strait through RJ45 patch cable (3ft to 6ft in length).\n- **Supplies required:** Velcro or cable straps\n- **Number of devices within scope:** QTY 1 ThinkSystem SR250 V3\n- **Hardware assembly requirements:** Following Lenovo Provided Install guide, install rails and server, install USB Drive and Set Drive on top of the server\n- **Cabling requirements:** Per provided documentation\n- **Connectivity to customer network:** Customer assisted\n- **Estimated duration per engineer:** Approx. 4 hours per engineer, per day\n- **Service date(s) and times:** Service scheduled 9AM\n- **Primary point of contact:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Remote validation point of contact:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Technical contact(s):** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Important Photo Requirement** – Tech MUST take an AFTER Photo(s)\n- Image of front of server with rack door opened so we can see a clean fit\n- Image showing the rack door shut to ensure server is properly secured\n- Image of where the USB drive is placed in server, preferable like the example image in documentation\n- If rack is not wall mounted and allows access to the back, please send a photo of the back of the server showing cable placements\n- Image of XClarity ID card with MAC.\n\n**Important Scope/Customer Information:**\n\n**• DO NOT update the FN application with your onsite time UNTIL you have ARRIVED at the entrance of the building.**\n\n**• Please understand that your check in and check out times are immediately visible to the customer and an escalation will be raised if you are not actually there. Failures will be reported to FN**\n\n**• Techs must arrive to site on time and must check in with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Project Team. The onsite and offsite times you report to the help desk MUST MATCH the times you report into your work order.**\n\n**Pre-Calls to Tech:**\n\n**A phone call will be made to you 24 hours prior to the scheduled date to confirm your commitment. An additional 2 hour pre-call will be made too. If for some reason you do not answer nor reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a Contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will** not be granted.\n\n**Upon Arrival To Site**\n\n**Tech to call int\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Contacts: Main Contact: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If onsite customer attempts to add or change the scope that was defined to you during your review with support, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and advise. Do not tell customer you are unable to complete the scope, wait for further instructions from \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and/or Lenovo.**\n\n**Prior to leave site**\n\n**Submit your deliverable so it can be reviewed prior to you leaving site.**\n\n**Once you have submitted, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* who will work with Lenovo to get you released from site.**\n\n**Attachments:**\n\n**Hardware Checklist** **-** This is a form filled out by the customer explaining the work needed. Please be sure to review and discuss any questions with the client\n\n**Installation Guides -** These must be printed out and reviewed prior to attending the site. If there are any questions please reach out before proceeding.\n\n**Sign Off Form -** You MUST print this release form and take it with you to site. The form must be filled out in its entirety, all arrival and departure times MUST match what is reported to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when you call them to check in. This form must be signed by the Site contact and be submitted back to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* within 24 hours of completing the service event. **Note:** Incomplete sign off forms will result in penalties. This information is required for us to be paid therefore it will affect your pay if not signed, completed and submitted within 24 hours of completing the service event.\n\n-^-^- **Attachment & Work Guide Links**\n\n **(1 of 1) Regal Lenovo Server Install Documentation**\n\n**Link:** [](https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005FikD/8D5pXzP6YXY0nMLaAphU.vbGfC6P5taIn..OpIlwnY8)<https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005FikD/8D5pXzP6YXY0nMLaAphU.vbGfC6P5taIn..OpIlwnY8>\n\n**--- End Of Attachment & Work Guide Links** -\\_-\\_-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T10:15","end":"2026-10-15T12:15"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.431450719811579},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791219311605}
{"job":{"id":20102815,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Outdoor Boteng - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - Once onsite, Text Scott at&nbsp;(949) 393-1241. If unavailable, call Field Service line&nbsp;949-317-4169</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Parts delivered: FedEx 878104849695</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for 10/7 10:00 a.m EST</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: replace solenoid in locker that won't close. Get locker key and package of parts from office upon arrival. </span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nOutdoor Boteng - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - Once onsite, Text Scott at (949) 393-1241. If unavailable, call Field Service line 949-317-4169\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Parts delivered: FedEx 878104849695\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Requesting tech for 10/7 10:00 a.m EST\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Need to: replace solenoid in locker that won't close. Get locker key and package of parts from office upon arrival.\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T10:00","end":"2026-10-07T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-07T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.850682911780015},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791220477981}
{"job":{"id":20102751,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | Hilton SD-WAN | Router Install | Schedule date/time is FIRM","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**IMPORTANT** MUST Call into Hilton Bridge BEFORE starting Install. If this is not done, a 10% penalty will be applied. Hilton Support will email you the Bridge Line number before you arrive on site. Please check your spam messages if you have not received this email before arrival on site.</strong></p><p><strong>Please Note: These workorders require back-end support for the routers to be configured and as such the start times are unable to be changed. Please do not request the workorder if you are unable to support the existing schedule. If you determine you will not be able to support the existing schedule, please remove yourself from the workorder. If you need assistance in removing yourself from the workorder please see: </strong>Cannot Make Assignment (fieldnation.com). <strong>Early arrival to site is not available without prior approval from Insight.</strong> Also, Once the workorder is assigned and if you have not done a Hilton SD-WAN workorder in the past a 5-to-10-minute screening call will be made to you.</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong>&nbsp;Install one (1) Meraki Router</p><p><strong>Dress</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Code:</strong>&nbsp;Business Casual</p><p><strong>Tools Needed:</strong></p><p>• Copy of this Field Procedure document </p><p>• Smart Phone fully charged with charger</p><p>• Hands Free Headset (Bluetooth capable)</p><p><strong>•&nbsp;Windows 10/11 Intel compatible Laptop fully charged with Ethernet port enabled and power supply</strong></p><p>• Cat 5 cable(s)</p><p>• Sharpie, Pen &amp; note pad</p><p>• Snips (Scissors)</p><p>• Box Cutters</p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><p>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</p><p>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</p><p>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</p><p>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</p><p>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</p><p>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</p><p>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</p><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><p>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</p><p>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* MUST Call into Hilton Bridge BEFORE starting Install. If this is not done, a 10% penalty will be applied. Hilton Support will email you the Bridge Line number before you arrive on site. Please check your spam messages if you have not received this email before arrival on site.**\n\n**Please Note: These workorders require back-end support for the routers to be configured and as such the start times are unable to be changed. Please do not request the workorder if you are unable to support the existing schedule. If you determine you will not be able to support the existing schedule, please remove yourself from the workorder. If you need assistance in removing yourself from the workorder please see:** Cannot Make Assignment (fieldnation.com). **Early arrival to site is not available without prior approval from Insight.** Also, Once the workorder is assigned and if you have not done a Hilton SD-WAN workorder in the past a 5-to-10-minute screening call will be made to you.\n\n**Scope:** Install one (1) Meraki Router\n\n**Dress** **Code:** Business Casual\n\n**Tools Needed:**\n\n• Copy of this Field Procedure document\n\n• Smart Phone fully charged with charger\n\n• Hands Free Headset (Bluetooth capable)\n\n**• Windows 10/11 Intel compatible Laptop fully charged with Ethernet port enabled and power supply**\n\n• Cat 5 cable(s)\n\n• Sharpie, Pen & note pad\n\n• Snips (Scissors)\n\n• Box Cutters\n\n**Penalties/Deductions**:\n\n10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.\n\n10% Deduction for being unprepared.\n\nTech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.\n\nUnauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.\n\n**Terms for Travel:**\n\nPayment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate\n\nIf provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n\nIf submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n\nTolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\n**Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite**:\n\nTechnician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n\nIf additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n\n IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n\nTech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:00","end":"2026-10-12T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":135},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":7.744201242684556},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $135 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.0