{"job":{"id":20103988,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Install NIC on APC unit and connect to switch","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">*﻿***MUST FOLLOW THESE STEPS / HAVE THESE TOOLS / SEE ATTACHMENTS***</span></p><p><strong><del>*** *** ****** ** ******** *********** *** * ******** **********</del></strong></p><p>Follow the instructions listed in the confidential portion of the ticket upon arrival onsite. YOU MUST CONTACT the NOC team listed and work with them throughout the visit. The NOC team MUST confirm everything is fully operational before leaving the site. Failure to follow the onsite process and/or failure to contact the required contacts will result in delays in payment up to non-payment.</p><p><strong><del>******** ******* </del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(229, 229, 229); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-e5e5e5, #d8d4cf);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">RITM3314374</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Description</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(229, 229, 229); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-e5e5e5, #d8d4cf);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">NIC for the APC unit has been delivered to the branch. We need a technician to install the NIC on the APC unit and connect it to an available switch port</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(229, 229, 229); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-e5e5e5, #d8d4cf);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Please bring long and short patch cables</span></p><p><br></p><p><u style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Let the NOC team know right away if you spot anything out of the ordinary.</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">REQUIRED TOOLS:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Valid photo ID</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Laptop</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Console cable</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Fully-charged smartphone w/camera</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Strong Hotspot capabilities</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Toolkit w/screwdrivers</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Known Working/New Cat5/6 Ethernet Patch cables</span></p><p>Must bring 8-10 feet ladder</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES:</strong></p><ol><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Customer signed timesheet - </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><u>NO EXCEPTIONS</u></strong></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Pics of completed work - including test results</span></li><li>Picture of network room/rack</li><li>Detailed closing notes</li><li>NOTE/Take a picture anything that seems odd or out of place (Ei. old unused equipment on rack or in the network room).</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-181818, #d9d6d1);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">****DO NOT LEAVE THE SITE UNTIL RELEASED BY REMOTE AND ONSITE CONFIRMS ALL WORKING AND SIGNS TIMESHEET**** W</strong><strong>ithout the required deliverables/documentation submitted after completion, <u>payment cannot be guaranteed.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Code of Conduct:</strong></p><p><strong><em>The technician scheduled for this work order must be the technician who attends onsite. If it is discovered that a different technician attended the site without prior notice or approval, the job will be considered unauthorized, and payment/completion will NOT be approved.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Always maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>All conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Personal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Any deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.</em></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Drug Policy/Dress Code;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Do not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.</strong></p><p><strong>Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>DO NOT mention Field Nation or ServicePoint to anyone onsite. Only reference the client that we are representing while onsite at the location.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts and out of scope work MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"\\*﻿\\*\\*\\*MUST FOLLOW THESE STEPS / HAVE THESE TOOLS / SEE ATTACHMENTS\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nFollow the instructions listed in the confidential portion of the ticket upon arrival onsite. YOU MUST CONTACT the NOC team listed and work with them throughout the visit. The NOC team MUST confirm everything is fully operational before leaving the site. Failure to follow the onsite process and/or failure to contact the required contacts will result in delays in payment up to non-payment.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** RITM3314374\n\n**Description**\n\nNIC for the APC unit has been delivered to the branch. We need a technician to install the NIC on the APC unit and connect it to an available switch port\n\nPlease bring long and short patch cables\n\nLet the NOC team know right away if you spot anything out of the ordinary.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\nValid photo ID\n\nLaptop\n\nConsole cable\n\nFully-charged smartphone w/camera\n\nStrong Hotspot capabilities\n\nToolkit w/screwdrivers\n\nKnown Working/New Cat5/6 Ethernet Patch cables\n\nMust bring 8-10 feet ladder\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES:**\n\n1. Customer signed timesheet - **NO EXCEPTIONS**\n2. Pics of completed work - including test results\n3. Picture of network room/rack\n4. Detailed closing notes\n5. NOTE/Take a picture anything that seems odd or out of place (Ei. old unused equipment on rack or in the network room).\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*DO NOT LEAVE THE SITE UNTIL RELEASED BY REMOTE AND ONSITE CONFIRMS ALL WORKING AND SIGNS TIMESHEET\\*\\*\\*\\* W****ithout the required deliverables/documentation submitted after completion, payment cannot be guaranteed.**\n\n**Code of Conduct:**\n\n***The technician scheduled for this work order must be the technician who attends onsite. If it is discovered that a different technician attended the site without prior notice or approval, the job will be considered unauthorized, and payment/completion will NOT be approved.***\n\n***Always maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.***\n\n***All conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.***\n\n***Personal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.***\n\n***Any deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.***\n\n**Drug Policy/Dress Code;**\n\n***Do not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.***\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n**Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.**\n\n**Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.**\n\n***DO NOT mention Field Nation or ServicePoint to anyone onsite. Only reference the client that we are representing while onsite at the location.***\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.***\n\n***All site aborts and out of scope work MUST be approved by ServicePoint.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:00","end":"2026-10-06T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-06T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":120},