{"job":{"id":20105201,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vimenture","title":"Telecom Line Audit Tag and Trace (POTS) POTS/Fiber | MUST HAVE A BUTTSET WITH RJ11 OPTION","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in analog POTS/fiber lines to perform a telecom audit and identify usage on each line.<strong><u>THIS JOB REQUIRES YOU TO HAVE A BUTTSET WITH AN RJ11 PORT OPTION</u></strong>.</li>\n<li><strong><u>FAILURE TO REVIEW THE SPREADSHEET WITH THE WORK ORDER MANAGER BEFORE CHECKING OUT MAY LEAD TO DISPUTE/CANCELATION OF THE WORK ORDER. CONTACT <del>************</del> IF YOU CAN'T GET HOLD OF THE WORK ORDER MANAGER.</u></strong></li>\n<li>Photos are required of each DMARC location and the specific 66 blocks/modems, together with the MAC address for the lines.</li>\n<li>Property has analog/fiber/cable lines that need to be located, usage identified and determine if the line has dial tone, and document in the provided spreadsheet.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Exact DMARC location for each line is crucial for this project and must be detailed on the spreadsheet. (ex. Building 1, Floor 2, Telecom Closet by Unit 1104)</u></strong></li>\n<li>Property may have a combinations of copper POTS, POTS over Fiber, Cable Coax Lines and Cellular Lines. All telecom lines need to toned, tested, tagged and the use determined. We must know what device and it's purpose that's connected to each phone line.</li>\n<li>Location may have multiple buildings with different addresses. Document different buildings and addresses associated to each line.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Do not disconnect phone lines from Fire Panel</u></strong> systems until Property Staff has put system in Test Mode, if applicable.</li>\n<li><strong><u>YOU ARE REQUIRED TO CONTACT<del>************</del>TO REVIEW THE SPREADSHEET BEFORE CHECKING OUT.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>AUDIT RESULTS SPREADSHEET MUST BE UPLOADED INTO FIELD NATION IMMEDIATELY PRIOR TO CHECKING OUT OF THE SITE FOR US TO CONFIRM WE HAVE ALL THE INFORMATION WE REQUIRE. Failure to upload requested Excel files may result in up to 50% job penalty and/or forfeiture/cancellation of work order for incomplete or late work.</u></strong></li>\n<li>The job start time is flexible, but please confirm so we can make the site team aware.</li>\n<li>Job is approved for up to 1 hour. contact work order manager if you need additional time.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> be the technician performing the work on-site.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tools Required (<em>must haves)</em>:</strong>​</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Buttset with an RJ11, Camera, Punch down Tool, Cable</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Audit:</strong></p>\n<p>All telephone lines (VoIP systems, and utility lines)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>​</p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Review and call work order manager with any questions</li>\n<li>Download Audit Spreadsheet</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check-in to work order.</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the onsite manager from<del>***************</del></li>\n<li>Review telecom audit spreadsheet - will need to complete all columns for each line. <strong><u>If you find additional lines NOT listed, please add it with appropriate information.</u></strong></li>\n<li>Call your mobile number when checking for dial tone. Screenshot of the test calls/call logs must be uploaded as proof of the dial tone.</li>\n<li>Locate analog/fiber/coax/cellular lines for identification, check for dial tone, and determine if lines are in use.</li>\n<li>Photos are required of each DMARC location and the specific 66 blocks/modems for the lines.</li>\n<li>We need the floor, the building number, and the building address as often different buildings have different addresses, what floor and closet it is in and the closet label.&nbsp;<strong>Example,&nbsp;CenturyLink line 555-555-5555 is for Elevator 1 in building 1 at 322 s main St. 1st floor telecom closet 66 block post 2.</strong>&nbsp;**These details are nonnegotiable.&nbsp;You will be paid the time you need to trace each line, its use and exact location.</li>\n<li>Property may have a combinations of copper POTS, POTS over Fiber, Cable Coax Lines and Cellular Lines. All telecom lines need to toned, tested, tagged and the use determined.</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Exact DMARC location for each line is<em><u>crucial</u></em> for this project and must be detailed on the spreadsheet. (ex. Building 1, Floor 2, Telecom Closet by Unit 1104)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Note the number, dial tone yes or no and identify its usage on the attached spreadsheet. Every location may have multiple Demarc's and building so be sure to ask for a service manager to provide assistance. This is an absolute non-negotiable requirement.</li>\n<li>Audit results spreadsheet must be uploaded into Field Nation immediately prior to checking out of the site for us to confirm we have all the information we require. <strong><u>Failure to upload requested Excel files may result in up to 50% job penalty and/or forfeiture/cancellation of work order for incomplete or late work.</u></strong></li>\n<li>Upload it in Excel format. Contact WO Manager to confirm all good.</li>\n<li>Collect signature from onsite manager.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>​<strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Upload Completed Telecom Audit Spreadsheet. This spreadsheet must be in .xls format and editable. screenshots, handwritten will not be acceptable.</li>\n<li>Check-out of work order in Field Nation app</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>​<strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p>Contact work order manager if any of the following are true:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>​If clarification is needed on site survey request, please contact us here via Direct Message.</li>\n<li><del>******* *** **** ***** ****** **************************</del>if on site manager is not available.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.</u></strong> Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers.&nbsp;Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.</li>\n<li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must pre-approved by calling<del>************</del>&nbsp;If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in analog POTS/fiber lines to perform a telecom audit and identify usage on each line.**THIS JOB REQUIRES YOU TO HAVE A BUTTSET WITH AN RJ11 PORT OPTION**.\n- **FAILURE TO REVIEW THE SPREADSHEET WITH THE WORK ORDER MANAGER BEFORE CHECKING OUT MAY LEAD TO DISPUTE/CANCELATION OF THE WORK ORDER. CONTACT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IF YOU CAN'T GET HOLD OF THE WORK ORDER MANAGER.**\n- Photos are required of each DMARC location and the specific 66 blocks/modems, together with the MAC address for the lines.\n- Property has analog/fiber/cable lines that need to be located, usage identified and determine if the line has dial tone, and document in the provided spreadsheet.\n- **Exact DMARC location for each line is crucial for this project and must be detailed on the spreadsheet. (ex. Building 1, Floor 2, Telecom Closet by Unit 1104)**\n- Property may have a combinations of copper POTS, POTS over Fiber, Cable Coax Lines and Cellular Lines. All telecom lines need to toned, tested, tagged and the use determined. We must know what device and it's purpose that's connected to each phone line.\n- Location may have multiple buildings with different addresses. Document different buildings and addresses associated to each line.\n- **Do not disconnect phone lines from Fire Panel** systems until Property Staff has put system in Test Mode, if applicable.\n- **YOU ARE REQUIRED TO CONTACT\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*TO REVIEW THE SPREADSHEET BEFORE CHECKING OUT.**\n- **AUDIT RESULTS SPREADSHEET MUST BE UPLOADED INTO FIELD NATION IMMEDIATELY PRIOR TO CHECKING OUT OF THE SITE FOR US TO CONFIRM WE HAVE ALL THE INFORMATION WE REQUIRE. Failure to upload requested Excel files may result in up to 50% job penalty and/or forfeiture/cancellation of work order for incomplete or late work.**\n- The job start time is flexible, but please confirm so we can make the site team aware.\n- Job is approved for up to 1 hour. contact work order manager if you need additional time.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** be the technician performing the work on-site.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.\n\n**Tools Required (*must haves)*:**​\n\n- Buttset with an RJ11, Camera, Punch down Tool, Cable\n\n**Scope of Audit:**\n\nAll telephone lines (VoIP systems, and utility lines)\n\n​\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Review and call work order manager with any questions\n2. Download Audit Spreadsheet\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order.\n2. Introduce yourself to the onsite manager from\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Review telecom audit spreadsheet - will need to complete all columns for each line. **If you find additional lines NOT listed, please add it with appropriate information.**\n4. Call your mobile number when checking for dial tone. Screenshot of the test calls/call logs must be uploaded as proof of the dial tone.\n5. Locate analog/fiber/coax/cellular lines for identification, check for dial tone, and determine if lines are in use.\n6. Photos are required of each DMARC location and the specific 66 blocks/modems for the lines.\n7. We need the floor, the building number, and the building address as often different buildings have different addresses, what floor and closet it is in and the closet label. **Example, CenturyLink line 555-555-5555 is for Elevator 1 in building 1 at 322 s main St. 1st floor telecom closet 66 block post 2.** \\*\\*These details are nonnegotiable. You will be paid the time you need to trace each line, its use and exact location.\n8. Property may have a combinations of copper POTS, POTS over Fiber, Cable Coax Lines and Cellular Lines. All telecom lines need to toned, tested, tagged and the use determined.\n\n- **Exact DMARC location for each line is*crucial* for this project and must be detailed on the spreadsheet. (ex. Building 1, Floor 2, Telecom Closet by Unit 1104)**\n\n1. Note the number, dial tone yes or no and identify its usage on the attached spreadsheet. Every location may have multiple Demarc's and building so be sure to ask for a service manager to provide assistance. This is an absolute non-negotiable requirement.\n2. Audit results spreadsheet must be uploaded into Field Nation immediately prior to checking out of the site for us to confirm we have all the information we require. **Failure to upload requested Excel files may result in up to 50% job penalty and/or forfeiture/cancellation of work order for incomplete or late work.**\n3. Upload it in Excel format. Contact WO Manager to confirm all good.\n4. Collect signature from onsite manager.\n\n​***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Upload Completed Telecom Audit Spreadsheet. This spreadsheet must be in .xls format and editable. screenshots, handwritten will not be acceptable.\n2. Check-out of work order in Field Nation app\n\n​**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact work order manager if any of the following are true:\n\n- ​If clarification is needed on site survey request, please contact us here via Direct Message.\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*if on site manager is not available.\n\n**Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- **Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.** Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must pre-approved by calling\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T14:00","end":"2026-10-15T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":4.3567178650381475},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000