{"job":{"id":20105603,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #296719 - Swarovski - #1063 - Crabtree Valley Mall- Physical Mounting cameras - no config - site precabled","description":{"html":"<p>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage.&nbsp;If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders.&nbsp;Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay.&nbsp;Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only.&nbsp;If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction.&nbsp;The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">TECHNICIAN MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA WHEN ARRIVING AND LEAVING SITE @ 940-323-2600 AND REQUEST TO SPEAK WITH A TRCA IMPLEMENTATION ENGINEER (BRIAN, DREW, OR EMMITT).</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">The technician must submit all deliverables PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"><del>****** ******** **** *************** **** ****** ************</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">TRCA Approved Time on Site: 6 hours</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">*** ANY ADDITIONAL HOURS, ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR DEVIATIONS FROM THE SCOPE OF WORK, MUST BE APPROVED IN ADVANCE BY TRCA. FAILURE TO NOTIFY TRCA MAY RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT.***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">UPON CHECK IN TECH WILL NEED TO LABEL EACH CAMERA BOX 1-8. BASED ON THE CAMERA PLACEMENT MAP TECH WILL NEED TO INSTALL EACH CAMERA ACCORDING TO THE # ON THE BOX TO THE # LOCATION ON THE CAMERA PLACEMENT MAP.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">TECH MUST ALSO RETRIEVE PRE-INSTALL PHOTOS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">-Photos of each camera location BEFORE installation.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">-Photos of existing network</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">-Photos of each camera box showing mac address with the # written above.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Scope of Work: Physical installation of qty 1 RetailNext Aurora Traffic Counter (TC) camera, qty seven (7) RetailNext Video surveillance cameras, and qty. 1 RetailNext RN1000 server/DVR. Site has been pre-cabled. This is the physical mounting of the cameras only. No configuration or testing of cameras. A camera placement map is attached for reference. A RetailNext server will need to be mounted in the customer supplied IT Rack.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">The Installation Guide is attached to the ticket with more detailed instructions and is to be taken to the site for reference during the installation.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Devices to be Installed:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Qty Device</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">1 Aurora Camera Supplied by RetailNext (TC)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">2 CAM-AXIS-M4327-P Full View Cameras (F)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">4 CAM-AXIS-M3086-V Wide View Camera (W)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">1 CAM-AXIS-M3085-V Medium View Cameras (M)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">1 RetailNext server SVR-RN1000-DT R4</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Technical Support for Installation: (940) 323-2600 and ask for TRCA Implementation Engineer, Brian, Drew, or Emmitt</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Required Tools and Materials:</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Tools:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Laptop</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">25-48 V PoE Injector</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">WiFi Hotspot</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">CAT5e/6 crimping tools</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Screwdriver (Phillips and flat)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Drill</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Extension cord and surge protector</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Cable toner/Tone tester</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Cable certifier</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Ladder tall enough to reach camera height.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Spirit level (DO NOT USE A PHONE APP)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Materials:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Spare patch cable (factory tested)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">RJ45 heads</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">RJ45 boots</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Drywall screws and anchors</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Additional shimming material (plastic/metal) that may be needed to level the camera on a drop pole or drop tile ceiling.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Deliverables Required for Payment:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Photos of Installed Equipment Per Implementation Engineer direction</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Manager Sign Off</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">**All deliverables must be returned to TRCA within 24 hours of job completion. **</span></p>","markdown":"Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction. The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.\n\nTECHNICIAN MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA WHEN ARRIVING AND LEAVING SITE @ 940-323-2600 AND REQUEST TO SPEAK WITH A TRCA IMPLEMENTATION ENGINEER (BRIAN, DREW, OR EMMITT).\n\nThe technician must submit all deliverables PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTRCA Approved Time on Site: 6 hours\n\n**\\*\\*\\* ANY ADDITIONAL HOURS, ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR DEVIATIONS FROM THE SCOPE OF WORK, MUST BE APPROVED IN ADVANCE BY TRCA. FAILURE TO NOTIFY TRCA MAY RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT.\\*\\*\\***\n\nUPON CHECK IN TECH WILL NEED TO LABEL EACH CAMERA BOX 1-8. BASED ON THE CAMERA PLACEMENT MAP TECH WILL NEED TO INSTALL EACH CAMERA ACCORDING TO THE # ON THE BOX TO THE # LOCATION ON THE CAMERA PLACEMENT MAP.\n\n**TECH MUST ALSO RETRIEVE PRE-INSTALL PHOTOS**\n\n-Photos of each camera location BEFORE installation.\n\n-Photos of existing network\n\n-Photos of each camera box showing mac address with the # written above.\n\nScope of Work: Physical installation of qty 1 RetailNext Aurora Traffic Counter (TC) camera, qty seven (7) RetailNext Video surveillance cameras, and qty. 1 RetailNext RN1000 server/DVR. Site has been pre-cabled. This is the physical mounting of the cameras only. No configuration or testing of cameras. A camera placement map is attached for reference. A RetailNext server will need to be mounted in the customer supplied IT Rack.\n\nThe Installation Guide is attached to the ticket with more detailed instructions and is to be taken to the site for reference during the installation.\n\nDevices to be Installed:\n\nQty Device\n\n1 Aurora Camera Supplied by RetailNext (TC)\n\n2 CAM-AXIS-M4327-P Full View Cameras (F)\n\n4 CAM-AXIS-M3086-V Wide View Camera (W)\n\n1 CAM-AXIS-M3085-V Medium View Cameras (M)\n\n1 RetailNext server SVR-RN1000-DT R4\n\nTechnical Support for Installation: (940) 323-2600 and ask for TRCA Implementation Engineer, Brian, Drew, or Emmitt\n\nRequired Tools and Materials:\n\nTools:\n\nLaptop\n\n25-48 V PoE Injector\n\nWiFi Hotspot\n\nCAT5e/6 crimping tools\n\nScrewdriver (Phillips and flat)\n\nDrill\n\nExtension cord and surge protector\n\nCable toner/Tone tester\n\nCable certifier\n\nLadder tall enough to reach camera height.\n\nSpirit level (DO NOT USE A PHONE APP)\n\nMaterials:\n\nSpare patch cable (factory tested)\n\nRJ45 heads\n\nRJ45 boots\n\nDrywall screws and anchors\n\nAdditional shimming material (plastic/metal) that may be needed to level the camera on a drop pole or drop tile ceiling.\n\nDeliverables Required for Payment:\n\n\\- Photos of Installed Equipment Per Implementation Engineer direction\n\n\\- Manager Sign Off\n\n\\*\\*All deliverables must be returned to TRCA within 24 hours of job completion. \\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":420},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":4.558136427491954},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $420 (countered: $420) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791229022016}
{"job":{"id":20000767,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Swap 4 Label Printers","description":{"html":"<p>Workorder Instructions:</p>\n<p>• Swap 4 Label Printers according to the Install guide Starbucks Biloxon Printer Mobile Guide V1.9 or newer:<del>***********************************************</del></p>\n<p>• Hardware &amp; Testing: Replace cup labeling printers and verify operation with the Starbucks Helpdesk. Reminder: Do not touch POS printers; they are strictly out of scope.</p>\n<p>• Cable Management: Bring approximately twelve (4\") Velcro strips. Use these for cable management as needed. The use of zip ties is strictly prohibited.</p>\n<p>• Documentation &amp; Release: Immediately upload photos as instructed in the install guide. You must remain on-site until the Shyft Project Desk confirms the photos meet customer requirements. To ensure a prompt release, the Project Desk prioritizes these reviews as soon as photos are received.</p>\n<p>• iPhone Users: To ensure your photos upload correctly, change your camera format setting from High Efficiency (HEIC) to Most Compatible (JPG) before taking pictures.</p>\n<p>• Equipment Removal: Remove the old printers from the store and drop them off at a Fed Ex or Purolator location within 48 hours of job completion.</p>\n<p>• Site Security: . You must bring the key shipped to you prior going to the store. Before leaving, lock the front door and arm the security alarm in accordance with store procedures. Please retain the store key after completing the visit, as it may be required for future assignments at other store locations.</p>\n<p>***NOTE*** Please check the Confidential Information section for PM and Help Desk / Command Center numbers.</p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT</strong> leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.</p>\n<p><strong>Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please message any rate counter offers, but do not request bundle as-is unless you are in agreement with the rate and schedule</strong></p>","markdown":"Workorder Instructions:\n\n• Swap 4 Label Printers according to the Install guide Starbucks Biloxon Printer Mobile Guide V1.9 or newer:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• Hardware & Testing: Replace cup labeling printers and verify operation with the Starbucks Helpdesk. Reminder: Do not touch POS printers; they are strictly out of scope.\n\n• Cable Management: Bring approximately twelve (4\") Velcro strips. Use these for cable management as needed. The use of zip ties is strictly prohibited.\n\n• Documentation & Release: Immediately upload photos as instructed in the install guide. You must remain on-site until the Shyft Project Desk confirms the photos meet customer requirements. To ensure a prompt release, the Project Desk prioritizes these reviews as soon as photos are received.\n\n• iPhone Users: To ensure your photos upload correctly, change your camera format setting from High Efficiency (HEIC) to Most Compatible (JPG) before taking pictures.\n\n• Equipment Removal: Remove the old printers from the store and drop them off at a Fed Ex or Purolator location within 48 hours of job completion.\n\n• Site Security: . You must bring the key shipped to you prior going to the store. Before leaving, lock the front door and arm the security alarm in accordance with store procedures. Please retain the store key after completing the visit, as it may be required for future assignments at other store locations.\n\n\\*\\*\\*NOTE\\*\\*\\* Please check the Confidential Information section for PM and Help Desk / Command Center numbers.\n\n**DO NOT** leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.\n\n**Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.**\n\n**Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.**\n\n**Please message any rate counter offers, but do not request bundle as-is unless you are in agreement with the rate and schedule**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T22:00","end":"2026-10-22T25:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35.72501429219358},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 0