{"job":{"id":20105910,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ambiance Systems","title":"Service Call - 70 Volt Audio System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Description: No Music</strong></p><p>TAO BA 235 has signal but no output to speakers.</p><p>Please check all connections at the amp, volume control and first speaker.  See original install plan and Field Service Report attached.</p><p>Ladder to 14ft max required</p><p>Help Desk Agent notes:</p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BA-235</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Signal active; no output to speakers.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Verified speaker wires.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">VC - 4 &gt; 8; no change.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">VC or first speaker is preventing the signal from reaching the speaker</em><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">s</span></p><p><strong>Notes:</strong></p><p>Please take photos of all work completed. You will need to upload a video of the amplifier operating and the speakers working. I recommend using your cell phone set on video and record a walk-through of the store starting with the amplifier and holding the phone under each speaker to record the music playing. As it is difficult to remember stores, I would recommend starting with a shot of your paperwork with the store number and address on it for a reference and then complete the walk-through. </p><p>Our goal is to have the service call completed in one trip and your labor/travel time to complete this work is not to exceed the agreed upon amount. No additional monies will be paid for this service call without prior approval and authorization in writing.</p><p><strong><em><u>Ambiance Systems requires photo/video documentation of all completed work. No work orders will be approved without it - no exceptions!</u></em></strong></p><p>***Do not remove any equipment from the site without written permission from Ambiance Systems. This includes equipment that may be damaged or no longer working (considered trash). The customer is responsible for disposal of all items.</p><p><strong>Recommended Equipment:</strong></p><p>Keyboard &amp; Mouse</p><p>Tools to strip, crimp, field&nbsp;terminate and punch-down the most commonly used home theater, security, audio,&nbsp;telecom, Cat5 and home automation connectors including F-Connectors, RCA&nbsp;connectors, BNC,RJ-11 and RJ-45 modular plugs and jacks.</p><p>Universal crimping system with&nbsp;adapters for mini and full size BNC connectors</p><p>Strippers for CAT 5, 6, 6E,&nbsp;coax, speaker wire</p><p>Push rods and 60 foot Fish&nbsp;Tape.&nbsp;</p><p>Wire and cable continuity tester, digital meter, tone generator and&nbsp;probe.</p><p>Standard electrical scissors, cutters</p><p>Small screwdriver set for Phoenix and other screw type connectors</p><p>Battery powered drill with bits and adapters</p><p>Electrical circuit plug in tester</p><p>Socket sets ¼ and 3/8 drive</p><p>Tape measure</p><p>Hammer</p><p>Soldering kit</p><p>Ladders – 4’, 8’, 10’, 12’ </p><p>Digital meter</p><p>Cable and wire tester</p><p>Tone generator and probe</p><p>Extension cords</p><p>Drop light</p>","markdown":"**Description: No Music**\n\nTAO BA 235 has signal but no output to speakers.\n\nPlease check all connections at the amp, volume control and first speaker. See original install plan and Field Service Report attached.\n\nLadder to 14ft max required\n\nHelp Desk Agent notes:\n\n*BA-235*\n\n*Signal active; no output to speakers.*\n\n*Verified speaker wires.*\n\n*VC - 4 > 8; no change.*\n\n*VC or first speaker is preventing the signal from reaching the speaker*s\n\n**Notes:**\n\nPlease take photos of all work completed. You will need to upload a video of the amplifier operating and the speakers working. I recommend using your cell phone set on video and record a walk-through of the store starting with the amplifier and holding the phone under each speaker to record the music playing. As it is difficult to remember stores, I would recommend starting with a shot of your paperwork with the store number and address on it for a reference and then complete the walk-through.\n\nOur goal is to have the service call completed in one trip and your labor/travel time to complete this work is not to exceed the agreed upon amount. No additional monies will be paid for this service call without prior approval and authorization in writing.\n\n***Ambiance Systems requires photo/video documentation of all completed work. No work orders will be approved without it - no exceptions!***\n\n\\*\\*\\*Do not remove any equipment from the site without written permission from Ambiance Systems. This includes equipment that may be damaged or no longer working (considered trash). The customer is responsible for disposal of all items.\n\n**Recommended Equipment:**\n\nKeyboard & Mouse\n\nTools to strip, crimp, field terminate and punch-down the most commonly used home theater, security, audio, telecom, Cat5 and home automation connectors including F-Connectors, RCA connectors, BNC,RJ-11 and RJ-45 modular plugs and jacks.\n\nUniversal crimping system with adapters for mini and full size BNC connectors\n\nStrippers for CAT 5, 6, 6E, coax, speaker wire\n\nPush rods and 60 foot Fish Tape.\n\nWire and cable continuity tester, digital meter, tone generator and probe.\n\nStandard electrical scissors, cutters\n\nSmall screwdriver set for Phoenix and other screw type connectors\n\nBattery powered drill with bits and adapters\n\nElectrical circuit plug in tester\n\nSocket sets ¼ and 3/8 drive\n\nTape measure\n\nHammer\n\nSoldering kit\n\nLadders – 4’, 8’, 10’, 12’\n\nDigital meter\n\nCable and wire tester\n\nTone generator and probe\n\nExtension cords\n\nDrop light","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:00","end":"2026-10-06T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-06T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":195,"max":195},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":52.7