2 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1791237591234}
{"job":{"id":20107434,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teceze","title":"Field Service Engineer - Retail Store Device Health Check","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>Technicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.</p><p>The technician will:</p><ul><li>Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Self-checkout devices</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Handheld scanners</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other related store technology equipment</li><li>Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.</li><li>Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.</li><li>Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.</li><li>Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.</li><li>Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.</li><li>Document all remediation activities completed onsite.</li><li>Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.</li><li>Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.</li><li>Take clear photos when required for documentation.</li><li>Clean up the work area after completing the activity.</li></ul><p>Unresolved Issues</p><p>For issues that cannot be resolved onsite:</p><ul><li>Document the device information and issue details.</li><li>Record troubleshooting steps already performed.</li><li>Provide the information to the project team for further action.</li><li>Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.</li></ul><p>Technician Requirements</p><ul><li>Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.</li><li>Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.</li><li>Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.</li><li>Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.</li><li>Must provide professional communication with store personnel.</li><li>Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.</li></ul><p>Visit &amp; Reporting Requirements</p><p>Technician must provide:</p><ul><li>Check-in/check-out confirmation.</li><li>Completed health-check checklist.</li><li>List of devices checked.</li><li>Issues identified.</li><li>Remediation performed.</li><li>Parts/devices used, if applicable.</li><li>Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.</li><li>Required photos/documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\nTechnicians will visit assigned retail stores to perform a checklist-based health check of store technology equipment.\n\nThe technician will:\n\n- Perform health checks on retail technology devices, including:\n- Point-of-Sale (POS) equipment\n- Self-checkout devices\n- Printers\n- Handheld scanners\n- Other related store technology equipment\n- Follow the provided device health-check checklist and procedures.\n- Use the Retail Device Diagnostic Tool when access is provided.\n- Identify device health issues and perform basic troubleshooting/remediation where possible.\n- Replace or use available support devices/parts when provided and authorized.\n- Record all devices checked and document any issues identified.\n- Document all remediation activities completed onsite.\n- Record any unresolved issues that require follow-up.\n- Maintain an accurate daily activity/visit report.\n- Take clear photos when required for documentation.\n- Clean up the work area after completing the activity.\n\nUnresolved Issues\n\nFor issues that cannot be resolved onsite:\n\n- Document the device information and issue details.\n- Record troubleshooting steps already performed.\n- Provide the information to the project team for further action.\n- Do not perform any work outside the approved scope without prior authorization.\n\nTechnician Requirements\n\n- Previous experience with retail technology / POS / network / IT hardware is preferred.\n- Comfortable working independently at retail store locations.\n- Able to follow detailed checklists and procedures.\n- Must have a smartphone for communication, documentation, and photos.\n- Must provide professional communication with store personnel.\n- Must arrive on time and complete the assigned store visit within the approved service window.\n\nVisit & Reporting Requirements\n\nTechnician must provide:\n\n- Check-in/check-out confirmation.\n- Completed health-check checklist.\n- List of devices checked.\n- Issues identified.\n- Remediation performed.\n- Parts/devices used, if applicable.\n- Unresolved issues requiring follow-up.\n- Required photos/documentation.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T09:15","end":"2026-10-06T14:15","latestStart":"2026-10-06T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":53.94894363256799},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 7, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $200\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026