{"job":{"id":20107618,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Valcom Audio System – Troubleshooting – Cabling","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work:</em></p>\n<p><em>IMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 70V audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do</em></p>\n<p><em>not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Tech required to troubleshoot the Valcom System and its audio cabling. Tech is required to verify status of the current Valcom 2003 system and trace cabling from speakers to the Valcom unit.</em></p>\n<p><em>This work will need to be done outside business hours (evenings). A lift is required to access cables and speakers in the store.</em></p>\n<p><em>Pictures are required of the front and back of the BG2120, the Valcom terminations, and any other components in the audio flow.</em></p>\n<p><em>Technician will need to check the voltage at the Valcom to ensure -24v are coming to the Valcom unit from its Power Supply.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>• Required Tools:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Wired headphones</em></p>\n<p><em>o Alligator clip leads</em></p>\n<p><em>o Toner and probe kit</em></p>\n<p><em>o Self-powered butt set</em></p>\n<p><em>• On-Site Procedure:</em></p>\n<p><em>• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Locate a 4\" x 5\" box labeled \"Music.\"</em></p>\n<p><em>• Verify the Music box:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Has power.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Has a headphone cable connected to the side.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Trace the headphone cable and determine where it terminates.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Take clear photos of the following:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Plywood/backboard in the electrical room and/or rack room.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Equipment rack.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Any audio equipment present.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Music box and associated cabling, where possible.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at<del>*************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>opt. 3, opt. 5 for further troubleshooting.</em></p>\n<p><em>Replacing wall mounted speaker with Bos</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: None of the Ceiling Speakers connected to the Valcom are working</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 4-6 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site?:(y/n)</em></p>\n<p><em>Please review the repair plans in the link below</em></p>\n<p><em>(put the direct link here)</em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>If assistance is needed, please call: <del>************ ****** * *</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA</em></p>\n<p><strong>Technician Support Process (Important)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ******</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong>If you encounter an issue while onsite:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Contact the <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong> and work through the issue with them.</li>\n<li>If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.</li>\n<li>If the issue is <strong>not resolved after working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ************ ****** * ****** * ****** *</del></strong>, then contact <strong>Shyft/NTS Support</strong> for further assistance.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>will be instructed to contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>first before additional support is provided.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work:*\n\n*IMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 70V audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do*\n\n*not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.*\n\n*• Tech required to troubleshoot the Valcom System and its audio cabling. Tech is required to verify status of the current Valcom 2003 system and trace cabling from speakers to the Valcom unit.*\n\n*This work will need to be done outside business hours (evenings). A lift is required to access cables and speakers in the store.*\n\n*Pictures are required of the front and back of the BG2120, the Valcom terminations, and any other components in the audio flow.*\n\n*Technician will need to check the voltage at the Valcom to ensure -24v are coming to the Valcom unit from its Power Supply.*\n\n*• Required Tools:*\n\n*o Wired headphones*\n\n*o Alligator clip leads*\n\n*o Toner and probe kit*\n\n*o Self-powered butt set*\n\n*• On-Site Procedure:*\n\n*• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room.*\n\n*• Locate a 4\" x 5\" box labeled \"Music.\"*\n\n*• Verify the Music box:*\n\n*o Has power.*\n\n*o Has a headphone cable connected to the side.*\n\n*• Trace the headphone cable and determine where it terminates.*\n\n*• Take clear photos of the following:*\n\n*o Plywood/backboard in the electrical room and/or rack room.*\n\n*o Equipment rack.*\n\n*o Any audio equipment present.*\n\n*o Music box and associated cabling, where possible.*\n\n*• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*opt. 3, opt. 5 for further troubleshooting.*\n\n*Replacing wall mounted speaker with Bos*\n\n*Site Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Customer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Clients present issue: None of the Ceiling Speakers connected to the Valcom are working*\n\n*Estimated time: 4-6 hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site?:(y/n)*\n\n*Please review the repair plans in the link below*\n\n*(put the direct link here)*\n\n*Other Instructions:*\n\n*If assistance is needed, please call: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*