{"job":{"id":19975949,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s &amp; locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) &amp; 1 AP(s)</u></strong></p>\n<p>Vendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:</p>\n<p>• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.</p>\n<p>• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.</p>\n<p>• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.</p>\n<p>• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.</p>\n<p>• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location</p>\n<p>• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.</p>\n<p>• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)</li>\n<li>After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)</li>\n<li><strong>After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.</strong></li>\n<li>Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of all items and devices surveyed</li>\n<li><em>Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Documents Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></li>\n<li><em>You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc</em></li>\n<li>ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li>Velcro for cable management</li>\n<li>Laptop:&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li>Console Cable</li>\n<li>Mobile Hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Tester</li>\n<li>Ladder&nbsp;(8'-10')</li>\n<li>Lift will be ordered if necessary</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"***NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s & locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!***\n\n**Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n\n**SOW:**\n\n**LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) & 1 AP(s)**\n\nVendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:\n\n• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.\n\n• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.\n\n• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.\n\n• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.\n\n• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.\n\n• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.\n\n• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location\n\n• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.\n\n• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer\n\n**DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)\n2. After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)\n3. **After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.**\n4. **NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.**\n5. Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)**\n\n- Pictures of all items and devices surveyed\n- *Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.*\n\n**Documents Required:**\n\n- **Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n- *You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.*\n- *Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location*\n- *Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc*\n- ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES\n- *Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)*\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- Velcro for cable management\n- Laptop: With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Cable Tester\n- Ladder (8'-10')\n- Lift will be ordered if necessary\n\n**You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":56.8269573276726},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791239478643}
{"job":{"id":20107771,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Lead Technician | Firm Start | Overnight Store Remodel - Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Remaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD</p><ul><li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">responsible</span>&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;</span>[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li><li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li><li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the Remote Support Team Bridge Line details -&nbsp;</strong>If you were not provided with one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Call &amp; Check-In with the <del>***</del> RTC Remote Technician Team via the provided Bridge Line</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation.</strong></p><ul><li>Perform a Walkthrough with MOD - refer to the install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li><li>Perform Inventory - refer to install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li><li>Work with Remote Bridge Line to determine if Site is ready to begin work for the night or if the night’s work needs aborted.</li><li>Continue to work with / provide updates to the Remote Bridge Line, closure to the end of the night you may be required to provide more frequent updates.</li><li>Some nights and/or mornings you will be working with the General Contractor Onsite and Store MOD to obtain/provide updates and/or complete specific task.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At Frontline Completion and Overall Store Remodel Completion]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li><li><strong>Check-Out with <del>***</del> Remote RTC Team via Bridge Line</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Remaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD\n\n- Lead Tech is responsible for reviewing and referring to ALL provided Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation \\[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC & STORE SPECIFIC Documentation\\] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.\n- Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** join and work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** review Nightly Scope of Work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** at the beginning of each **NIGHT**. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.\n- **Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Store Completion Deliverables \\[Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel\\]:**\n- FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE \\[ FRONTLINE COMPLETION & FULL STORE COMPLETION\\]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the **\\*\\*\\* REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.** \\[If deliverable session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.\\]\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* - Tool & Material List Document** **Link** (download to view full document): <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Estimated Duration: Multiple Days** estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n***Important Site Information / Requirements:***\n\n- You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n **Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.** Please **READ & REVIEW** all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **General Project Specific & STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link \\[VERY IMPORTANT\\]****:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\_Install Guides** **Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):** <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ>\n- **\\*\\*\\* Remodel - Tool & Material List** **Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8>\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to y