{"job":{"id":20109583,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Creative Realities","title":"NCEL 528265 - (Vass NC) | Black Screen","description":{"html":"<p>********** Scope of Work **********</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">*** Scope of Work ***</strong></p><p>*** TECH MUST CALL CRI UPON ARRIVING TO AND BEFORE LEAVING SITE ***</p><p>MUST Check In with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have before photos ready)</p><p>For any and all Technical Assistance, reach out to Support @ 888-369-3629</p><p>MUST Check Out with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have after photos ready)</p><p><br></p><p>REQUIRED EQUIPMENT:</p><p>&nbsp;- Laptop with SD Card Reader</p><p>&nbsp;- Spare Micro SD Card</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">NOTE</strong>: The Micro SD Card should be Class 10 SDXC card (with Full Size adaptor) to have as a back-up.&nbsp;</p><p>(EX: https://www.bestbuy.com/site/pny-32gb-microsdhc-uhs-i-memory-card/6327962.p?skuId=6327962)</p><p><br></p><p>Work with the site contact: <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">Site Manager</span> to locate the <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">528265-Circle K-Kiosk</span></p><p>The site has reported <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">their screen not displaying content</span></p><p>The Player appears to be offline in <span style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">device is online in ReflectView</span></p><p>The screens should be getting their content from a BrightSign Player</p><p>&nbsp;- This Player will be utilizing an HDMI cable to deliver the content</p><p>Verify that none of the cables have any physical damage or wear and tear</p><p>Verify that all cables are firmly plugged into all equipment</p><p>Verify that the Player has link lights</p><p>Trace the Ethernet cable back to the switch and verify that there are link lights on the switch</p><p>Utilize a cable tester to verify that the Ethernet cable is good</p><p>Reboot the Player and see if it displays a valid IP Address on boot-up</p><p><br></p><p>We may need to reconfigure the Player</p><p>Prior to arriving onsite, please download the following .zip file from:</p><p>NC Lottery XT2145https://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:u:/g/NOC%20Team/IQC5FHk-YhPyRbh1oMZYC0W7AVg8BWLnjcI8EqAWtbbYyLU?e=6OEbS0</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">NOTE</strong>: A pictured guide for reconfiguring the Player can be found at the following link:</p><p><u>https://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/NOC%20Team/EbDeM9iDHslBoonUxiShvL0B22xdIcS-gYzmgrMj2wX1ow?e=DoMs8M</u></p><p><br></p><p>Isolate the reason that the Player is offline</p><p>Resolve the issue and get the Player online again</p><p>Verify all functionality of the screen (content, sound, touch, etc.)</p><p><br></p><p>If it is suspected that there is any defective equipment. Please take pictures and collect the following:</p><p>&nbsp;- Make:</p><p>&nbsp;- Model #:</p><p>&nbsp;- Serial #:</p><p>&nbsp;- Additional information may be required to be collected.</p><p><br></p><p>Call the NOC at ​(888) 369-3629 to verify the work</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(204, 0, 0);\">IMPORTANT</strong>: You must clean up the site after all work is completed. Leave the area looking as good as (or better than) when you arrived</p><p>Perform additional troubleshooting as necessary</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>IMPORTANT: If you must cancel or reschedule, please call Creative Realities Dispatch at (502) 791-8802.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** List of Required Tools **********</p><p>Some tools on this list will be job specific. If you have any questions about a listed tool, please contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 to discuss.</p><p><br></p><p>USB (wireless) mouse and keyboard</p><p>USB Flash Drive (32GB or higher)</p><p>Test monitor</p><p>Universal remote</p><p>Fully charged laptop with SD Card Reader</p><p>Cat5 tester</p><p>Electrical tester (voltmeter)</p><p>Spare cables (Cat5, VGA, DVI, HDMI, etc.)</p><p>Network and video termination tools</p><p>Impact Drill with standard, metric, and Torx bits</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Zip ties and/or Velcro</p><p>Cleaning materials for screen</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** Check Out **********</p><p>You must submit the signed work order, all required photos to FieldNation then contact Dispatch at <span style=\"color: rgb(191, 191, 191);\">(502) 791-8802 </span>and confirm that you have provided all of the necessary information and documentation prior to leaving the site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>********** Deliverable Requirements **********</p><p>If any of the equipment onsite is found to be defective. It is your responsibility to capture the Model # and Serial # information for the defective equipment. This information needs to be uploaded to FieldNation so that a replacement can be sourced.</p><p>If any of the deliverables are not retrieved, you will be expected to return to the site without any form of pay increase to retrieve the required deliverables.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If any of the deliverables are not provided within the Work Order, it will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.</p><p><br></p><p>********** DISCLAIMER **********</p><p>You should NEVER use the name of your company while onsite.</p><p><br></p><p>IF YOU NOTICE ANY ISSUES OUTSIDE OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK, YOU MUST DOCUMENT THE ISSUE ON THE WORK ORDER IMMEDIATELY AND TAKE DIGITAL PHOTOS. THEN NOTIFY CREATIVE REALITIES OF THE ISSUE.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you are more than 15 minutes late and we have not heard from you. This ticket will be cancelled and will be reported to FieldNation. You will not be compensated in this event. We need our technicians to be onsite, on-time, every time. We understand that problems do arise. However, we need to be notified of those problems before you become late, not after.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>All dispatch orders require that all the listed deliverables within the Scope of Work be provided in order to be paid out. Any work order that is marked as “Complete” without meeting all of the listed deliverables will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.</p><p>If you fail to abide by the terms and conditions within these instructions and/or by the terms and conditions of FieldNation. This ticket will be closed for zero (0) dollars. By accepting this work order, you acknowledge and agree to these terms.</p><p>You will be given a 48-hour period after the completion of your work to submit for any expense reimbursements and/or budget increase requests. If there are no requests submitted, after the 48-hour mark, the Work Order will be closed and paid based upon the hourly rate.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Scope of Work \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Scope of Work \\*\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\*\\* TECH MUST CALL CRI UPON ARRIVING TO AND BEFORE LEAVING SITE \\*\\*\\*\n\nMUST Check In with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have before photos ready)\n\nFor any and all Technical Assistance, reach out to Support @ 888-369-3629\n\nMUST Check Out with Dispatch @ (502) 791-8802 (have after photos ready)\n\nREQUIRED EQUIPMENT:\n\n\\- Laptop with SD Card Reader\n\n\\- Spare Micro SD Card\n\n**NOTE**: The Micro SD Card should be Class 10 SDXC card (with Full Size adaptor) to have as a back-up.\n\n(EX: <https://www.bestbuy.com/site/pny-32gb-microsdhc-uhs-i-memory-card/6327962.p?skuId=6327962)>\n\nWork with the site contact: Site Manager to locate the 528265-Circle K-Kiosk\n\nThe site has reported their screen not displaying content\n\nThe Player appears to be offline in device is online in ReflectView\n\nThe screens should be getting their content from a BrightSign Player\n\n\\- This Player will be utilizing an HDMI cable to deliver the content\n\nVerify that none of the cables have any physical damage or wear and tear\n\nVerify that all cables are firmly plugged into all equipment\n\nVerify that the Player has link lights\n\nTrace the Ethernet cable back to the switch and verify that there are link lights on the switch\n\nUtilize a cable tester to verify that the Ethernet cable is good\n\nReboot the Player and see if it displays a valid IP Address on boot-up\n\nWe may need to reconfigure the Player\n\nPrior to arriving onsite, please download the following .zip file from:\n\nNC Lottery XT2145<https://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:u:/g/NOC%20Team/IQC5FHk-YhPyRbh1oMZYC0W7AVg8BWLnjcI8EqAWtbbYyLU?e=6OEbS0>\n\n**NOTE**: A pictured guide for reconfiguring the Player can be found at the following link:\n\n<https://creativerealities.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/NOC%20Team/EbDeM9iDHslBoonUxiShvL0B22xdIcS-gYzmgrMj2wX1ow?e=DoMs8M>\n\nIsolate the reason that the Player is offline\n\nResolve the issue and get the Player online again\n\nVerify all functionality of the screen (content, sound, touch, etc.)\n\nIf it is suspected that there is any defective equipment. Please take pictures and collect the following:\n\n\\- Make:\n\n\\- Model #:\n\n\\- Serial #:\n\n\\- Additional information may be required to be collected.\n\nCall the NOC at ​(888) 369-3629 to verify the work\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You must clean up the site after all work is completed. Leave the area looking as good as (or better than) when you arrived\n\nPerform additional troubleshooting as necessary\n\nIMPORTANT: If you must cancel or reschedule, please call Creative Realities Dispatch at (502) 791-8802.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* List of Required Tools \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nSome tools on this list will be job specific. If you have any questions about a listed tool, please contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 to discuss.\n\nUSB (wireless) mouse and keyboard\n\nUSB Flash Drive (32GB or higher)\n\nTest monitor\n\nUniversal remote\n\nFully charged laptop with SD Card Reader\n\nCat5 tester\n\nElectrical tester (voltmeter)\n\nSpare cables (Cat5, VGA, DVI, HDMI, etc.)\n\nNetwork and video termination tools\n\nImpact Drill with standard, metric, and Torx bits\n\nLadder\n\nZip ties and/or Velcro\n\nCleaning materials for screen\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Check Out \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nYou must submit the signed work order, all required photos to FieldNation then contact Dispatch at (502) 791-8802 and confirm that you have provided all of the necessary information and documentation prior to leaving the site.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Deliverable Requirements \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIf any of the equipment onsite is found to be defective. It is your responsibility to capture the Model # and Serial # information for the defective equipment. This information needs to be uploaded to FieldNation so that a replacement can be sourced.\n\nIf any of the deliverables are not retrieved, you will be expected to return to the site without any form of pay increase to retrieve the required deliverables.\n\nIf any of the deliverables are not provided within the Work Order, it will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* DISCLAIMER \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nYou should NEVER use the name of your company while onsite.\n\nIF YOU NOTICE ANY ISSUES OUTSIDE OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK, YOU MUST DOCUMENT THE ISSUE ON THE WORK ORDER IMMEDIATELY AND TAKE DIGITAL PHOTOS. THEN NOTIFY CREATIVE REALITIES OF THE ISSUE.\n\nIf you are more than 15 minutes late and we have not heard from you. This ticket will be cancelled and will be reported to FieldNation. You will not be compensated in this event. We need our technicians to be onsite, on-time, every time. We understand that problems do arise. However, we need to be notified of those problems before you become late, not after.\n\nAll dispatch orders require that all the listed deliverables within the Scope of Work be provided in order to be paid out. Any work order that is marked as “Complete” without meeting all of the listed deliverables will be subject to a penalty of 20% docked off of its pay.\n\nIf you fail to abide by the terms and conditions within these instructions and/or by the terms and conditions of FieldNation. This ticket will be closed for zero (0) dollars. By accepting this work order, you acknowledge and agree to these terms.\n\nYou will be given a 48-hour period after the completion of your work to submit for any expense reimbursements and/or budget increase requests. If there are no requests submitted, after the 48-hour mark, the Work Order will be closed and paid based upon the hourly rate.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T11:00","end":"2026-10-08T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":92,"max":184},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":92,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":52.65210667885856},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $184 (countered: $184) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:0