{"job":{"id":"1834349046","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05622465-MAR1530-EPIK Survey and Install","description":"DESCRIPTION: SOW - EPIK Single Visit Install<br>***********************************************************************<br>Before Arrival<br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival.<br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK:<br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo<br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below.<br>On Arrival<br>1.Check in on WorkMarket.<br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location.<br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work.<br>EPIK Install Requirements<br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik.<br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location. <br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard.<br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on.<br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions.<br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard:<br>https://wizard.epik.io<br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned.<br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES<br>7.If not already stated in the TNs to be wired section of your ticket, confirm with site contact if there are fire alarm, security alarm, elevator or e911 lines on site. If so, notify activations of any port configuration changes that need to be made and complete testing with the fire, security or elevator monitoring companies.<br>8.For any lines that cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number.<br>9.If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready.<br>Checkout Requirement<br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line.<br>2.Confirm Activations has released you.<br>3.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables.<br>4.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket.<br>5.Check out on WorkMarket.<br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket.<br><br>Required Deliverables<br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout:<br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install.<br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block.<br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable.<br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet.<br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions.<br><br><br>Required Tools<br>•Laptop<br>•Smartphone with hotspot<br>•Tone generator and wand<br>•66/110 punch tool<br>•Butt set<br>•       Infrared Temperature Gun <br>•Electrician scissors<br>•Step ladder<br>•Flashlight/headlamp<br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper<br>•Ethernet cable tester<br>•Impact drill / cordless drill<br>•Masonry bits<br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits<br>•Needle-nose pliers<br>•Label maker and label tape<br>•Cat3 or better cable<br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable<br>•Cross-connect wire<br>•Gel-crimp connectors<br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware<br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks<br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini<br>************************************************************************","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T07:00","end":"2026-10-16T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":60,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1791289532229}
{"job":{"id":20108413,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"Store IT/POS Equipment Removal, Packing and Shipment- Will order and ship to provider residence prior to WO date","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview: Complete Deinstallation of Electronic Equipment for Store Closure. Complete Inventory and securely package equipment. Boxes will be left onsite for scheduled truck carrier to pick up between 2-4pm local. If the driver arrives before complete call DST to notify them that the driver must wait. Pick up is between 2pm and 4pm.</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in basic electronic deinstallation.&nbsp;Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale experience.</li><li>Tech is required to deinstall all POS equipment and back office equipment to include the server, monitor and printer.</li><li>Tech is required print inventory list prior to arrival, complete the inventory list during the removal, and submit to DST upon completion for verification of equipment</li><li>Tech will be required to pack deinstalled equipment with packing material that is provided.</li><li>No network cabling is to be packed with equipment, please trash onsite.</li><li>A detailed deinstallation guide is provided to the assigned provider</li><li>Tech will be shipped the following materials to arrive prior to service date, provider to provide shipping address.</li><li>1-Closed store box 34x34x24</li><li>4-Closed store box 24x24x24</li><li>1-Closed store box 17x12x11</li><li>1-BUBBLE WRAP</li><li>1-ULINE PACKING TAPE</li><li>Estimated duration will be 5 hours.</li><li>All Photos must be uploaded to the work order <strong><u>BEFORE</u></strong> checkout code will be given.</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Print out and have copy of the inventory check list that is located on <u>pages 6 - 8</u> in the deinstall manual. A photo of it filled out is a requirement to complete this work order.</strong></li><li><strong>Bring the shipped packing materials with you to site.</strong></li><li>Check you are at the store number situated on your work request. The store number can be situated on the front window of the Store, on the off chance that you don't discover the store number posted, ask store staff, General Contractor, or Field Consultant on location.</li><li>&nbsp;If no one onsite or unable to confirm, please contact the Deployment Support Team.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************ **** *</del></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****************</del></span></li></ul><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks (Overview- Step by step process attached in the document section of the work order)</em></strong></p><ul><li>Remove and pack all 7MD devices and their peripherals (if present).</li><li>Pack all power cables with like devices, keep peripherals packed with associated cable (ie receipt printer).</li><li>Remove, disassemble and pack the mobile check out (if present).</li><li>Remove, disassemble and pack the self check out.</li><li>Remove IPMOM for store to return<strong> **IPMOM is not to be packed into the boxes with the other equipment**</strong></li><li>Remove and pack all back office equipment.</li><li>Remove POS peripherals (receipt printers, POS scanner, cash drawer and pin pads) from each POS location.</li><li>Remove and pack store communication equipment.</li></ul><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Wide shot of sales counter upon arrival from employee side of counter. Should be a wide shot showing all POS's including shelving under POS's.</li><li>Back office upon arrival. Should be a wide shot showing full desk and installed equipment as well as the wall mounted network and fuel equipment if applicable.</li><li>Any damaged equipment please take picture and upload to misc. folder</li><li>Provide a picture of the network equipment in box. ARUBA network equipment MUST be packed in its own separate box.</li><li>Picture of each box with contents BEFORE boxes are taped shut.</li><li>Picture of the completed inventory checklist so DST can review it.</li><li>Picture of inventory checklist placed in one of the boxes.</li><li>Picture of back office, wide shot to capture all network equipment has been removed and back office computer equipment removed from desk.</li><li>Picture of all boxes taped shut next to each other&nbsp;and marked up with store info<strong><em> .</em></strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>Additional Contacts:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span> Deployment Support team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************ **** *</del></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****************</del></span></li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Mini Screw Driver set&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">6-8 foot Ladder</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Sharpie or marker of some sort</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Cell Phone with the ability to send photos</span></li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Work order questions- contact work order manager </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ******* ************</del></strong></li><li>Contact <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*** ********** ******* ****</del></span></li><li>&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿Please read below.</strong></p><p><strong>Call Before Starting Work:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure you call the provided number,&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong><strong>, before commencing any work. Hours of operation are 7:00 am - 7:00 pm CST, there will be no support outside of these hours therefore will not be able to checkin prior to 7am CST.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-In for Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will provide a&nbsp;<strong>check-in number, marking the official start of your work for timekeeping purposes.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-Out to End Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;When your work is&nbsp;<strong>finished, contact the agent again to obtain a check-out number, signifying the official end of your work.</strong></p><p><strong>*********** MAKE SURE ALL WORK IS COMPLETE (INCLUDING SITE CLEANUP) BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH DST AS THAT WILL BE TIME OF RECORD - WE WANT TO AVOID TIME DISCREPANCIES FOR PAYMENT APPROVAL. **********</strong></p><p><strong>Record Based on Agent Timestamps:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will record the&nbsp;<strong>timestamps for both check-in and check-out, serving as the official record of your work duration.</strong></p><p><strong>Include Codes in Work Order:</strong>&nbsp;Remember to incorporate these check-in and check-out codes into your work order to ensure approval for payment.</p><p>By following these guidelines, you'll guarantee accurate timekeeping and a smooth approval process for your work order.</p><p><strong><u>Turn away fee:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>In the event of a site turn away</u></strong>&nbsp;(Something wrong when arriving at store that prevents our install - some examples: network down, equipment lost, store refusing install, no power) provider will be paid a $50 cancellation fee, and will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future.&nbsp;Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue.&nbsp;DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release.&nbsp;Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.</p><p><strong>Readiness Policy:&nbsp;</strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>On My Way:&nbsp;</strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</p><p><strong>Arriving Late:</strong>&nbsp;All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</p><p><strong>Changing Resources:</strong>&nbsp;By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Expense Approval:</strong>&nbsp;Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</p><p><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong>&nbsp;If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order.</p><p><strong>Out-of-Scope Work:&nbsp;</strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the scope stated above, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid at <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order.</p><p>If work order specifies the need to return parts.</p><p><strong>Returning Parts:</strong>&nbsp;Return Waybills will be found in the original package the part was shipped to you in. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is being tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</p>","markdown":"**Overview: Complete Deinstallation of Electronic Equipment for Store Closure. Complete Inventory and securely package equipment. Boxes will be left onsite for scheduled truck carrier to pick up between 2-4pm local. If the driver arrives before complete call DST to notify them that the driver must wait. Pick up is between 2pm and 4pm.**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in basic electronic deinstallation. Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale experience.\n- Tech is required to deinstall all POS equipment and back office equipment to include the server, monitor and printer.\n- Tech is required print inventory list prior to arrival, complete the inventory list during the removal, and submit to DST upon completion for verification of equipment\n- Tech will be required to pack deinstalled equipment with packing material that is provided.\n- No network cabling is to be packed with equipment, please trash onsite.\n- A detailed deinstallation guide is provided to the assigned provider\n- Tech will be shipped the following materials to arrive prior to service date, provider to provide shipping address.\n- 1-Closed store box 34x34x24\n- 4-Closed store box 24x24x24\n- 1-Closed store box 17x12x11\n- 1-BUBBLE WRAP\n- 1-ULINE PACKING TAPE\n- Estimated duration will be 5 hours.\n- All Photos must be uploaded to the work order **BEFORE** checkout code will be given.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n- **Print out and have copy of the inventory check list that is located on pages 6 - 8 in the deinstall manual. A photo of it filled out is a requirement to complete this work order.**\n- **Bring the shipped packing materials with you to site.**\n- Check you are at the store number situated on your work request. The store number can be situated on the front window of the Store, on the off chance that you don't discover the store number posted, ask store staff, General Contractor, or Field Consultant on location.\n- If no one onsite or unable to confirm, please contact the Deployment Support Team.\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n***On-Site Tasks (Overview- Step by step process attached in the document section of the work order)***\n\n- Remove and pack all 7MD devices and their peripherals (if present).\n- Pack all power cables with like devices, keep peripherals packed with associated cable (ie receipt printer).\n- Remove, disassemble and pack the mobile check out (if present).\n- Remove, disassemble and pack the self check out.\n- Remove IPMOM for store to return **\\*\\*IPMOM is not to be packed into the boxes with the other equipment\\*\\***\n- Remove and pack all back office equipment.\n- Remove POS peripherals (receipt printers, POS scanner, cash drawer and pin pads) from each POS location.\n- Remove and pack store communication equipment.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables:***\n\n- Wide shot of sales counter upon arrival from employee side of counter. Should be a wide shot showing all POS's including shelving under POS's.\n- Back office upon arrival. Should be a wide shot showing full desk and installed equipment as well as the wall mounted network and fuel equipment if applicable.\n- Any damaged equipment please take picture and upload to misc. folder\n- Provide a picture of the network equipment in box. ARUBA network equipment MUST be packed in its own separate box.\n- Picture of each box with contents BEFORE boxes are taped shut.\n- Picture of the completed inventory checklist so DST can review it.\n- Picture of inventory checklist placed in one of the boxes.\n- Picture of back office, wide shot to capture all network equipment has been removed and back office computer equipment removed from desk.\n- Picture of all boxes taped shut next to each other and marked up with store info ***.***\n\n **Additional Contacts:**\n\n- \\*\\*\\* Deployment Support team\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Mini Screw Driver set\n- Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver\n- 6-8 foot Ladder\n- Sharpie or marker of some sort\n- Cell Phone with the ability to send photos\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- **Work order questions- contact work order manager** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- Contact \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\***\n\n**﻿Please read below.**\n\n**Call Before Starting Work:** Ensure you call the provided number, **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*****, before commencing any work. Hours of operation are 7:00 am - 7:00 pm CST, there will be no support outside of these hours therefore will not be able to checkin prior to 7am CST.**\n\n**Check-In for Time Tracking:** The agent will provide a **check-in number, marking the official start of your work for timekeeping purposes.**\n\n**Check-Out to End Time Tracking:** When your work is **finished, contact the agent again to obtain a check-out number, signifying the official end of your work.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* MAKE SURE ALL WORK IS COMPLETE (INCLUDING SITE CLEANUP) BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH DST AS THAT WILL BE TIME OF RECORD - WE WANT TO AVOID TIME DISCREPANCIES FOR PAYMENT APPROVAL. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Record Based on Agent Timestamps:** The agent will record the **timestamps for both check-in and check-out, serving as the official record of your work duration.**\n\n**Include Codes in Work Order:** Remember to incorporate these check-in and check-out codes into your work order to ensure approval for payment.\n\nBy following these guidelines, you'll guarantee accurate timekeeping and a smooth approval process for your work order.\n\n**Turn away fee:**\n\n**In the event of a site turn away** (Something wrong when arriving at store that prevents our install - some examples: network down, equipment lost, store refusing install, no power) provider will be paid a $50 cancellation fee, and will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future. Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue. DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release. Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.\n\n**Readiness Policy:** The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted. Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.\n\n**On My Way:** When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.\n\n**Arriving Late:** All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order. Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.\n\n**Changing Resources:** By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.\n\n**Dress Code:** Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n**Expense Approval:** Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.\n\n**Additional Time On-site:** If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n\n**Out-of-Scope Work:** If you are asked to perform work beyond the scope stated above, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident. Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid at $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n\nIf work order specifies the need to return parts.\n\n**Returning Parts:** Return Waybills will be found in the original package the part was shipped to you in. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is being tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T09:30","end":"2026-10-13T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":55.67620102816074},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791289544612}
{"job":{"id":20108487,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"Task is installing a ZPE Nodegrid SR Device","description":{"html":"<p>Provider must introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.</p><p><strong>Please note:</strong></p><ul><li>All deliverables are required and may lead to delayed payment for the ticket if not provided.</li><li>Any travel expenses need to be confirmed before dispatch, failure to confirm these expenses may result in the denial of their payment.</li><li>Time onsite is not guaranteed. Tickets are set for two hours but may be shorter or longer. One hour minimum will be paid on the ticket, after this it will be paid at the hourly rate for the time logged onsite. Any other minimum rates (i.e. 2hrs or more onsite) will need to be put in as a counter and confirmed before dispatch. Failure to confirm these rates may result in the denial of their payment.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Required while onsite:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All techs will require a valid <u>Drivers License</u> or <u>Government issued photo ID</u>.</li><li>Must be prepared to show the WO and/or provide the TSD number located in this ticket.</li><li>Techs will have a manager or other form of management accompany them while onsite, especially while off the sales floor in the stockrooms, manager offices, etc.</li><li>Failure to follow these policies may result in non-payment of the ticket.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Job Details: </strong></p><p><br></p><p>Task is installing a ZPE Nodegrid SR Device:</p><p>Process overview:</p><p>*Serial ZPE ports are the ones on the right side of the device.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>1) Connect Serial ZPE port 1 to 1581FW-1 Console port (Palo Alto Firewall), console port is on the right side of MGMT port and label cable as \"ZPE Port 1 --- FW1 Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2) Connect Serial ZPE port 3 to 1581Router Console port (Router Cisco 3945) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 3 --- Router Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>3) Connect serial ZPE port 4 to 1581MDF1-1 Console port (MDF1 switch 1) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 4 --- MDF1-1 Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4) Connect Serial ZPE port 5 to 1581MDF1-2 Console port (MDF1 switch 2) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 5 --- MDF1-2 Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>5) Connect Serial ZPE port 6 to 1581MDF1-3 Console port (MDF1 switch 3) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 6 --- MDF1-3 Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>6) Connect Serial ZPE port 7 to Vertiv UPS serial port and label cable as \"ZPE Port 7 --- Vertiv Console\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>7) Connect ZPE ETH 0 port to MDF1-4 gi4/0/1 port and label cable as \"ZPE ETH 0\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>8) Connect temperature/humidity sensor to USB port of ZPE. Mount to the network rack. Make sure it is out in the open and not covered or directly behind an appliance exhaust.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>9) Connect power cable to powerhouse</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>10) Turn device on.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Technician will troubleshoot a suspected bad data run with the assistance of the <del>******* ****</del>.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Job Length:</strong></p><p>This job will typically take no more than 2 hours. If work takes longer than 2 hours, provide a detailed update as to why.</p><p><strong>Here is each step of our process:</strong></p><ul><li>Check in with Central Dispatch Call Center</li><li>Check in with <del>******* ****</del></li><li>Check in with Manager on Duty (MOD)</li><li>Fill out and submit Job Hazard Analysis (JHA)&nbsp;(see attached) Wachter requests this be done within 30 minutes of arrival onsite.</li><li>Take pictures of work area before starting work</li><li>Work with the MOD to locate the suspected bad data run.&nbsp;</li><li>If device can be repaired without a lift using on-hand material, proceed with repair. If repair cannot be completed and a lift is required, notify Central Dispatch Call Center</li><li>Take “after” pictures and pictures of the cable test.&nbsp;Additionally, if unable to complete take a picture of work area to illustrate why.</li><li>Check out with <del>******* ******** </del>Document the name of the person you speak with.</li><li>Check out with Central Dispatch Call Center</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Path:</strong></p><ol><li>Dispatch:&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************ **** *</del></span></li><li><strong>PC: Ricky&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ************</del></span></li><li><strong>PM: Sky</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*********** ************</del></span></li><li><strong>PM II: Shana&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ************</del></span></li></ol><strong>Please note the photos required when checking out:</strong><ol><li><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>1. Cable Test Results</strong></li><li><strong>Provide test results for all cables, including cable ID/location, test type, pass/fail, and photos/screenshots. If a test cannot be performed, explain why.</strong></li><li><strong>2. Cable Runs</strong></li><li><strong>Document all cabling installed/modified: cable type, length of each run, device/location served, route taken, termination points/labels, and any pathway deviations or obstacles.</strong></li><li><strong>3. Device Status &amp; Documentation</strong></li><li><strong>Provide online/offline status, link light status (switch + device), and photos for any offline/faulty hardware. Include photos of each device worked on: final installation, cabling/ports, and serial/model/asset tags.</strong></li><li><strong>4. Photos &amp; Materials Used</strong></li><li><strong>Submit before-and-after photos for all work completed (cabling, device installs, mounting changes, cleanup, etc.). Provide a full itemized list of all materials used, including cable types/quantities, connectors/terminations, devices, and consumables.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><p>Cable Tester (CAT5)</p><p>PPE (Steel toe boots, hard hat, safety goggles, reflective vest)</p><p>RJ45 jacks for cat5 cabling</p><p>Faceplate / Surface mount box</p><p>CAT5 Patch Cables</p><p>Tips for cat5 cabling</p><p>Box of Cat5 Cabling</p><p>Punch Down Tool</p><p>Snips</p><p>RJ45 crimper</p><p><strong>Deliverables: </strong></p><p>Completed Job Hazard Analysis From within 30 minutes of arriving onsite</p><p>Cable test</p><p>Functional device</p>","markdown":"Provider must introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.\n\n**Please note:**\n\n- All deliverables are required and may lead to delayed payment for the ticket if not provided.\n- Any travel expenses need to be confirmed before dispatch, failure to confirm these expenses may result in the denial of their payment.\n- Time onsite is not guaranteed. Tickets are set for two hours but may be shorter or longer. One hour minimum will be paid on the ticket, after this it will be paid at the hourly rate for the time logged onsite. Any other minimum rates (i.e. 2hrs or more onsite) will need to be put in as a counter and confirmed before dispatch. Failure to confirm these rates may result in the denial of their payment.\n\n**Required while onsite:**\n\n- All techs will require a valid Drivers License or Government issued photo ID.\n- Must be prepared to show the WO and/or provide the TSD number located in this ticket.\n- Techs will have a manager or other form of management accompany them while onsite, especially while off the sales floor in the stockrooms, manager offices, etc.\n- Failure to follow these policies may result in non-payment of the ticket.\n\n**Job Details:**\n\nTask is installing a ZPE Nodegrid SR Device:\n\nProcess overview:\n\n\\*Serial ZPE ports are the ones on the right side of the device.\n\n1\\) Connect Serial ZPE port 1 to 1581FW-1 Console port (Palo Alto Firewall), console port is on the right side of MGMT port and label cable as \"ZPE Port 1 --- FW1 Console\"\n\n2\\) Connect Serial ZPE port 3 to 1581Router Console port (Router Cisco 3945) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 3 --- Router Console\"\n\n3\\) Connect serial ZPE port 4 to 1581MDF1-1 Console port (MDF1 switch 1) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 4 --- MDF1-1 Console\"\n\n4\\) Connect Serial ZPE port 5 to 1581MDF1-2 Console port (MDF1 switch 2) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 5 --- MDF1-2 Console\"\n\n5\\) Connect Serial ZPE port 6 to 1581MDF1-3 Console port (MDF1 switch 3) and label cable as \"ZPE Port 6 --- MDF1-3 Console\"\n\n6\\) Connect Serial ZPE port 7 to Vertiv UPS serial port and label cable as \"ZPE Port 7 --- Vertiv Console\"\n\n7\\) Connect ZPE ETH 0 port to MDF1-4 gi4/0/1 port and label cable as \"ZPE ETH 0\"\n\n8\\) Connect temperature/humidity sensor to USB port of ZPE. Mount to the network rack. Make sure it is out in the open and not covered or directly behind an appliance exhaust.\n\n9\\) Connect power cable to powerhouse\n\n10\\) Turn device on.\n\nTechnician will troubleshoot a suspected bad data run with the assistance of the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n**Job Length:**\n\nThis job will typically take no more than 2 hours. If work takes longer than 2 hours, provide a detailed update as to why.\n\n**Here is each step of our process:**\n\n- Check in with Central Dispatch Call Center\n- Check in with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Check in with Manager on Duty (MOD)\n- Fill out and submit Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) (see attached) Wachter requests this be done within 30 minutes of arrival onsite.\n- Take pictures of work area before starting work\n- Work with the MOD to locate the suspected bad data run.\n- If device can be repaired without a lift using on-hand material, proceed with repair. If repair cannot be completed and a lift is required, notify Central Dispatch Call Center\n- Take “after” pictures and pictures of the cable test. Additionally, if unable to complete take a picture of work area to illustrate why.\n- Check out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Document the name of the person you speak with.\n- Check out with Central Dispatch Call Center\n\n**Escalation Path:**\n\n1. Dispatch: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n2. **PC: Ricky** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. **PM: Sky**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n4. **PM II: Shana** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Please note the photos required when checking out:**1. **REQUIRED DELIVERABLES.**\n2. **1. Cable Test Results**\n3. **Provide test results for all cables, including cable ID/location, test type, pass/fail, and photos/screenshots. If a test cannot be performed, explain why.**\n4. **2. Cable Runs**\n5. **Document all cabling installed/modified: cable type, length of each run, device/location served, route taken, termination points/labels, and any pathway deviations or obstacles.**\n6. **3. Device Status & Documentation**\n7. **Provide online/offline status, link light status (switch + device), and photos for any offline/faulty hardware. Include photos of each device worked on: final installation, cabling/ports, and serial/model/asset tags.**\n8. **4. Photos & Materials Used**\n9. **Submit before-and-after photos for all work completed (cabling, device installs, mounting changes, cleanup, etc.). Provide a full itemized list of all materials used, including cable types/quantities, connectors/terminations, devices, and consumables.**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\nCable Tester (CAT5)\n\nPPE (Steel toe boots, hard hat, safety goggles, reflective vest)\n\nRJ45 jacks for cat5 cabling\n\nFaceplate / Surface mount box\n\nCAT5 Patch Cables\n\nTips for cat5 cabling\n\nBox of Cat5 Cabling\n\nPunch Down Tool\n\nSnips\n\nRJ45 crimper\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\nCompleted Job Hazard Analysis From within 30 minutes of arriving onsite\n\nCable test\n\nFunctional device","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T07:00","end":"2026-10-07T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58.44225972644292},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z