{"job":{"id":20110553,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"EV Charger Wi‑Fi Connectivity Troubleshooting & Network Validation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code: Business Casual</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>Laptop with Wi‑Fi and Ethernet capability</p><p>Ethernet cable</p><p>Mobile hotspot (recommended)</p><p>Mobile phone for coordination with EPLUS, remote support, and property contact</p><p>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)</p><p>Network troubleshooting tools</p><p>Wi‑Fi analyzer software/application (recommended)</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Camera-enabled device for documentation and photos</p><p>PPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)</p><p><br></p><strong>Reported Issue</strong><ul><li>EV chargers at the site are currently unable to connect to the network.</li><li>A previous troubleshooting attempt was unsuccessful.</li><li>Property management has advised that updates have been made to the site's Wi‑Fi network and requests advance notice of the technician's ETA so onsite personnel can be available to assist during the service visit.</li></ul><strong>Scope of Work</strong><ul><li>Provide onsite support to troubleshoot and restore connectivity for the affected EV charging stations.</li><li>Coordinate with EPLUS, remote support personnel, and the property contact throughout the visit.</li><li>Verify charger power status and confirm all affected chargers are operational.</li><li>Inspect and validate network, Wi‑Fi, and communication settings on the chargers.</li><li>Verify the updated Wi‑Fi network information provided by the property.</li><li>Test charger connectivity to the current Wi‑Fi network.</li><li>Verify internet access and network stability at the charger locations.</li><li>Confirm communication between the chargers and the management platform.</li><li>Perform basic troubleshooting, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi‑Fi connectivity verification</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Signal strength testing</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Network configuration validation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Router/access point connectivity checks</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power cycling equipment if directed</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Charger communication testing</li><li>Assist EPLUS remote support with diagnostics and validation.</li><li>Verify chargers successfully reconnect to the network and return online.</li><li>Document any network, hardware, or site issues identified during troubleshooting.</li><li>If connectivity cannot be restored onsite, gather detailed findings and assist with escalation.</li></ul><br><strong>Documentation</strong><ul><li>Take photos of:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Charger status indicators/screens</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Network equipment (router, access point, etc.)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any identified issues or damage</li><li>Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photo documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival&nbsp;</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check in with SG net.</li><li>&nbsp;Call EV support</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Before and After pictures</li><li>Notes</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet</li><li><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Contact SGNet</strong></p>","markdown":"**Dress Code: Business Casual**\n\n·\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nLaptop with Wi‑Fi and Ethernet capability\n\nEthernet cable\n\nMobile hotspot (recommended)\n\nMobile phone for coordination with EPLUS, remote support, and property contact\n\nBasic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)\n\nNetwork troubleshooting tools\n\nWi‑Fi analyzer software/application (recommended)\n\nFlashlight\n\nCamera-enabled device for documentation and photos\n\nPPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)\n\n**Reported Issue**- EV chargers at the site are currently unable to connect to the network.\n- A previous troubleshooting attempt was unsuccessful.\n- Property management has advised that updates have been made to the site's Wi‑Fi network and requests advance notice of the technician's ETA so onsite personnel can be available to assist during the service visit.\n\n**Scope of Work**- Provide onsite support to troubleshoot and restore connectivity for the affected EV charging stations.\n- Coordinate with EPLUS, remote support personnel, and the property contact throughout the visit.\n- Verify charger power status and confirm all affected chargers are operational.\n- Inspect and validate network, Wi‑Fi, and communication settings on the chargers.\n- Verify the updated Wi‑Fi network information provided by the property.\n- Test charger connectivity to the current Wi‑Fi network.\n- Verify internet access and network stability at the charger locations.\n- Confirm communication between the chargers and the management platform.\n- Perform basic troubleshooting, including:\n- Wi‑Fi connectivity verification\n- Signal strength testing\n- Network configuration validation\n- Router/access point connectivity checks\n- Power cycling equipment if directed\n- Charger communication testing\n- Assist EPLUS remote support with diagnostics and validation.\n- Verify chargers successfully reconnect to the network and return online.\n- Document any network, hardware, or site issues identified during troubleshooting.\n- If connectivity cannot be restored onsite, gather detailed findings and assist with escalation.\n\n  \n**Documentation**- Take photos of:\n- Charger status indicators/screens\n- Network equipment (router, access point, etc.)\n- Any identified issues or damage\n- Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photo documentation.\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with SG net.\n2. Call EV support\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Before and After pictures\n2. Notes\n3. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet\n- **Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n**Contact SGNet**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T10:00","end":"2026-10-07T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-07T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.674895351249788},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791293306720}
{"job":{"id":"2887180351","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"03523072 || 8460 TIMES DISPATCH || EPIK Cutover and Test Revisit","description":"SOW - EPIK Cutover &amp; Test <br><br>please call into Activations : (833) 719-8378 <br><br>************************************************************************************* <br><br>Before Arrival <br><br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival. <br><br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK: <br><br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo <br><br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below. <br><br>On Arrival <br><br>1.Check in on WorkMarket. <br><br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location. <br><br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work. <br><br>EPIK Install Requirements <br><br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik. <br><br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location.  <br><br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard. <br><br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on. <br><br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions. <br><br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard: <br><br>https://wizard.epik.io <br><br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned. <br><br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES <br><br>Checkout Requirement <br><br>1.Confirm Activations has released you. <br><br>2.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables. <br><br>3.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket. <br><br>4.Check out on WorkMarket. <br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket. <br><br>Required Deliverables <br><br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout: <br><br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install. <br><br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block. <br><br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable. <br><br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet. <br><br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions. <br><br>Required Tools <br><br>•Laptop <br><br>•Smartphone with hotspot <br><br>•Tone generator and wand <br><br>•66/110 punch tool <br><br>•Butt set <br><br>       Infrared Temperature Gun  <br><br>•Electrician scissors <br><br>•Step ladder <br><br>•Flashlight/headlamp <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper <br><br>•Ethernet cable tester <br><br>•Impact drill / cordless drill <br><br>•Masonry bits <br><br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits <br><br>•Needle-nose pliers <br><br>•Label maker and label tape <br><br>•Cat3 or better cable <br><br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable <br><br>•Cross-connect wire <br><br>•Gel-crimp connectors <br><br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks <br><br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini <br><br>************************************************************************************* <br><br>PM SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS GUIDELINES <br><br>Special Instructions <br><br>Install Location <br><br>Enter where the EPIK device should be installed, including MDF/IDF/telco room location, wall/rack/shelf mounting instructions, and access notes. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Cable Runs <br><br>Enter any required cable runs, cable type, distance, start/end points, and whether ladder, lift, ceiling access, or special tools are needed. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Network Information <br><br>Enter switch name, switch port, DHCP/static IP details, VLAN info, and customer network escalation contact. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>External Antenna <br><br>Enter whether an external antenna is required, where it should be mounted, and any cable path or photo requirements. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Special Testing <br><br>Enter any customer-specific testing that must be completed, including specific TNs, fax, alarm, elevator, hunt group, auto attendant, or other required testing. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Customer Contacts <br><br>Enter primary LCON, backup contact, customer IT contact, site manager, and escalation contacts. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Vendor / Third-Party Info <br><br>Enter any VTM, customer tech, alarm vendor, elevator vendor, fax vendor, MSP, or other third-party contact information.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:30","end":"2026-10-12T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":142.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 142.8mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-