{"job":{"id":20113793,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DataMax Service, Inc","title":"\"ASAP\"  Kiosk Needing service at correctional facility's Visitor or Admin/Processing area","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><em>Note: This is for a correctional facility but restricted to the visitor or administrative/processing areas.</em><strong><em> There is zero exposure to inmates' living quarters or socializing areas. </em></strong><em> The admin/processing areas are highly secure but may have </em><strong><em><u>very limited exposure</u></em></strong><em> to inmates that are being processed into the facility.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work</u></strong>: We need a technician with kiosk experience and some cabling experience. The facility has a kiosk that is no longer in service and needs to be remedied through diagnosis and troubleshooting or replacement of parts.<strong> Review the Special Notes to Tech for the specific information regarding the issue at this facility</strong>. Be sure all connectivity has been re/established and is confirmed by Support/Help Desk.</p><p>Diligently review and complete all Tasks listed on this WO.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-visit Task supplemental instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If POC is not reachable, add a tag to this WO immediately. </strong></li><li><strong>Do NOT go to site until contact is made with the POC thru phone and/or email. </strong></li><li><strong>MUST set ETA, confirm keys and parts (if needed) with POC BEFORE going to site. </strong></li></ul><p><strong>** Tech will NOT be compensated for time onsite if the above is not completed. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Check In/Checkout Procedure.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check in and out on the platform and be sure your GPS is turned on!</li><li>Call Client Support at<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>**************</del></strong>&nbsp;once in front of the equipment to be serviced. Work with Support to diagnose or replaced any applicable replacement equipment so they can validate.</li><li>Do not leave the site without the name of the person at Client Support that released you.</li><li>Work Orders Must be closed out within 24 hours of completion.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Important Facility Entry Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Read and Adhere to the attached <strong><u>site conduct rules and guidelines</u></strong> document</li><li>NO weapons, alcohol, drugs, or contraband.</li><li>Only the assigned tech is authorized in the facility</li><li>Avoid communication with inmates or trustees.</li><li>Inventory all tools brought into the facility.</li><li>Do not leave any tools or belongings on-site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>See custom fields area for Standard Tools required</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Additional required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>$1 bill/coins&nbsp;(for testing Coin &amp; Bill Acceptors)</li><li>Cloth/wipes</li><li>Allen Wrench Set (Metric &amp; Standard)</li><li>Hex Bit Set with extensions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>NETWORK TOOLS Required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Spare CAT5E 50-100'</li><li>Crimper/Termination Tool</li><li>RJ45 terminations</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Cable Tester</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Name of Client Support person that you checked-out with</li><li>Zebra Thermal Printer's 80mm paper guide</li><li>Loaded paper roll and interior of the Kiosk showing wire management</li><li>Return Tracking# if applicable</li><li>POC Signature on your WO (Call <del>******* </del>if you are waiting more than 20 minutes for a signature.)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>All additional charges and expenses must be submitted as part of a counter-offer prior to work order assignment or be explicitly pre-approved by the assigned PC/PM or Work Order Manager. Any costs not submitted or approved in advance may not be eligible for reimbursement or approval. In all cases, technicians must check out with the assigned PC before leaving the site if requesting any increase, out-of-scope, or travel-related charges. Additionally, all submitted charges must be supported by valid receipts or proof of purchase to be considered for reimbursement. DataMax Services reserves the right to deny any additional expenses that do not comply with our policies, procedures, and SOW guidelines.</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"*Note: This is for a correctional facility but restricted to the visitor or administrative/processing areas.* ***There is zero exposure to inmates' living quarters or socializing areas.***  *The admin/processing areas are highly secure but may have* ***very limited exposure*** *to inmates that are being processed into the facility.*\n\n**Scope Of Work**: We need a technician with kiosk experience and some cabling experience. The facility has a kiosk that is no longer in service and needs to be remedied through diagnosis and troubleshooting or replacement of parts. **Review the Special Notes to Tech for the specific information regarding the issue at this facility**. Be sure all connectivity has been re/established and is confirmed by Support/Help Desk.\n\nDiligently review and complete all Tasks listed on this WO.\n\n**Pre-visit Task supplemental instructions:**\n\n- **If POC is not reachable, add a tag to this WO immediately.**\n- **Do NOT go to site until contact is made with the POC thru phone and/or email.**\n- **MUST set ETA, confirm keys and parts (if needed) with POC BEFORE going to site.**\n\n**\\*\\* Tech will NOT be compensated for time onsite if the above is not completed.**\n\n**Check In/Checkout Procedure.**\n\n- Check in and out on the platform and be sure your GPS is turned on!\n- Call Client Support at **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** once in front of the equipment to be serviced. Work with Support to diagnose or replaced any applicable replacement equipment so they can validate.\n- Do not leave the site without 