{"job":{"id":"8130053452","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Reality Interactive","title":"Spectrum: 5308 - Fayetteville, NC - Tech visit to troubleshoot MAW TV","description":"<p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Approximate Visit Length</u></strong>: 1 hour(s)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>A laptop with an Ethernet port</li><li>Working Ethernet Cable</li><li>Smartphone with Camera</li><li>Screwdriver (multi-bit)</li><li>USB Keyboard and Mouse</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>5-8ft ladder</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Recommended but not required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Power drill with drill bits</li><li>Cable snake</li><li>Spare 3/4\" spacers</li><li>Level</li><li>RJ45 Crimper</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Electronics Duster</li><li>Duct Tape</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Instructions</u></strong></p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact and obtain any necessary hardware</li><li>Call into Reality @860-852-5035 to check in and review SOW</li><li>Make your way to the MAW TV and carefully pull the TV forward.</li><li>Power on the TV and verify it stays powered on.</li><li>Check the TV power cable at both ends and make sure it is secure and not loose, damaged, pinched, or under tension.</li><li>Check the power outlet/power strip and confirm it is providing stable power.</li><li>If needed, test the TV with a known-good power cable and/or power source.</li><li>Slowly push the TV back into position while monitoring the TV.</li><li>If the TV powers off while being pushed back, check which cable or connection is being pulled, pinched, or moved.</li><li>Reposition and secure all wiring so cables have enough slack and are not pinched behind the TV.</li><li>If the TV stays powered on but the screen goes black, reseat the HDMI cable and test with a known-good HDMI cable if needed.</li><li>Work with RI Support for additional troubleshooting if the issue continues.</li><li>Verify the TV remains powered on in its final position and the correct MAW content is playing.</li><li>Take photos of all associated experiences with content on their screens and any associated hardware.</li><li>Additional testing or photos may be requested by RI Support</li><li>Upload all photos and required documentation before you leave the site</li><li>Any FedEx drop-offs require photo proof (i.e., receipt picture)</li></ol><p><br></p><p><em>Please understand additional troubleshooting steps may be asked by the Reality Interactive Support Team during the visit to ensure all needs are met.</em></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T22:00","end":"2026-10-09T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-1