{"job":{"id":20112796,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Printer Install Tech WITH HELPER Government Issued ID (non-expired) Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>For all technical issues on site call </strong><strong>1-972-581-9842</strong></p><p><strong>Conference ID: 485 568 415 #</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Scope:</u></em></strong> Installation of 6 Lexmark device(s).</p><p><strong>Installs:</strong></p><p>2x MX632 with 57X9528 ISD,&nbsp;38S2910&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;250 Sheet Tray</p><p>3x MC822 with 25B2900 550 sheet tray</p><p>1x ST9917<strong> (no debrief for this device) </strong></p><p><strong>Deinstalls:</strong></p><p>45146PHH3H23R-ST9720</p><p>45146PHH3H2P4-ST9720</p><p>701655HH05LCK-MX611</p><p>701655HH05KZ0-MX611</p><p>74635C66014BK-MX812</p><p>70165PHH06BND-MX611</p><p>701655HH05KX9-MX611</p><p>701655HH05KYG-MX611</p><p>40635C6602FPX-MS812</p><p>70165PHH06LC9-MX611</p><p>74635C6601F9G-MX810</p><p>74635C66011ZW-MX812</p><p><strong><em>Firmware link- </em></strong>(Please see task list)</p><p>There are 3 Firmware files and one Auto Deploy Tool.</p><p>Please extract onto 2 USB thumb drives so that the following files are visible.&nbsp;</p><p>USB must be 2.0. DO NOT USE 3.0</p><p>MX632: MXTSN.250.217.fls</p><p>MX822 &amp; MX826: TGW.250.217.fls (same file for both devices)</p><p>ST9917: MSNSN.250.217.fls</p><p>TruistDeploy-2.0.0.fls</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Required Deliverables: </u></em></strong>(Also listed in task)</p><ul><li>Debrief form for each new printer: Both pages must be completely filled out and signed by the customer and technician.</li><li>Asset report for each new device: must have valid IP</li><li>Network report for each new device: must have valid IP</li><li>Asset report for each deinstall device: photo of asset tag can be used if needed</li><li>Asset tag form for each new device: must be signed by the customer</li><li>Training form: signed by the technician and the POC</li><li>Photo of installed equipment: Include scanner glass if present</li><li>Photo Front of device with device tag applied and CAC Reader installed (If applicable)</li><li>Photo of all deinstalled devices. Verify serial numbers listed in custom field</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:** **For all technical issues on site call** **1-972-581-9842**\n\n**Conference ID: 485 568 415 #**\n\n***Scope:*** Installation of 6 Lexmark device(s).\n\n**Installs:**\n\n2x MX632 with 57X9528 ISD, 38S2910 250 Sheet Tray\n\n3x MC822 with 25B2900 550 sheet tray\n\n1x ST9917 **(no debrief for this device)**\n\n**Deinstalls:**\n\n45146PHH3H23R-ST9720\n\n45146PHH3H2P4-ST9720\n\n701655HH05LCK-MX611\n\n701655HH05KZ0-MX611\n\n74635C66014BK-MX812\n\n70165PHH06BND-MX611\n\n701655HH05KX9-MX611\n\n701655HH05KYG-MX611\n\n40635C6602FPX-MS812\n\n70165PHH06LC9-MX611\n\n74635C6601F9G-MX810\n\n74635C66011ZW-MX812\n\n***Firmware link-*** (Please see task list)\n\nThere are 3 Firmware files and one Auto Deploy Tool.\n\nPlease extract onto 2 USB thumb drives so that the following files are visible.\n\nUSB must be 2.0. DO NOT USE 3.0\n\nMX632: MXTSN.250.217.fls\n\nMX822 & MX826: TGW.250.217.fls (same file for both devices)\n\nST9917: MSNSN.250.217.fls\n\nTruistDeploy-2.0.0.fls\n\n***Required Deliverables:*** (Also listed in task)\n\n- Debrief form for each new printer: Both pages must be completely filled out and signed by the customer and technician.\n- Asset report for each new device: must have valid IP\n- Network report for each new device: must have valid IP\n- Asset report for each deinstall device: photo of asset tag can be used if needed\n- Asset tag form for each new device: must be signed by the customer\n- Training form: signed by the technician and the POC\n- Photo of installed equipment: Include scanner glass if present\n- Photo Front of device with device tag applied and CAC Reader installed (If applicable)\n- Photo of all deinstalled devices. Verify serial numbers listed in custom field\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary & Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T21:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":510},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":12,"distance":54.309109684636496},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Oct 22, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Thu, Oct 22, Fri, Oct 23, Mon, Oct 26 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791306594457}
{"job":{"id":20112745,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2731602","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Treadmill : Peloton : 1</li><li>Fitness Equipment : Tonal : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Treadmill : Peloton : 1\n\\- Fitness Equipment : Tonal : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T08:00","end":"2026-10-06T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-06T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17.55960299289465},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/6/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791306618738}
{"job":{"id":"4952489758","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #267314- Equipment Board Installation - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED","description":"<p><br></p><p>******* HARD START TIME AND DATE *******</p><p><br></p><p>******* DATE CAN NOT BE RESCHEDULED BY ANY MEANS *******</p><p><br></p><p>******* ANALOG SKILLS ARE A MUST *******</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>1. Check-In / Check-Out Requirements</strong></p><p>✅ <strong>Technician MUST call Tech Americas at (281) 668-3211 (Option 3):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Upon Arrival (Check-In)</strong></li><li><strong>Immediately After Completing the Job (Check-Out)</strong></li></ul><p>⚠️ <strong>Failure to complete both calls will result in payment deductions or no payment.</strong></p><p>⏱️ <strong>Hard Start Time &amp; Date — This cannot be rescheduled under any circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If unable to reach by phone:</strong></p><p>Send an email to: <strong>support@tech-americas.com</strong></p><p>Include:</p><ul><li>Your name</li><li>Job site address</li><li>Check-in or check-out time</li><li>Description of issue or delay</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Contact Numbers</strong></p><p>If you encounter any issues (e.g., dispatch, check-in/out, equipment), contact the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Evelyn Vasquez</strong> – (346) 615-1333 | eavasquez@tech-americas.com</li><li><strong>Aida Flores</strong> – (210) 830-7125 | aflores@tech-americas.com</li><li><strong>Erick Vasquez</strong> – (832) 913-1539 | egvasquez@tech-americas.com</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>3. General Scope Overview</strong></p><p>The technician will:</p><ul><li>Replace <strong>existing analog lines</strong></li><li>Install and configure customer equipment</li><li>Ensure <strong>all lines are tested for dial tone</strong></li><li>Work with Customer Remote Support for final validation</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>4. On-Site Procedure (After Check-In)</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Notify site personnel</strong> (clerk) of your presence and purpose</li><li><strong>Locate the customer equipment</strong> (\"Big Blue Box\")</li><li><strong>Take Before Pictures</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li>Close-up of the equipment</li><li>Wide-angle of the telecom room</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Assess Environment</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li>Identify area with <strong>strongest LTE signal</strong> in the telecom room</li><li>Confirm with POC:</li><li>Do all listed lines exist?</li><li>Are all lines in use?</li><li>Are any lines shared? <em>(Shared lines are not supported – call Tech Americas)</em></li><li>Are any DSL lines present? <em>(Call Tech Americas if yes)</em></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>5. Installation Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Mount <strong>Customer Communications Board</strong> in LTE signal-rich area</li><li>Power on the unit</li><li>Mount <strong>MIMO antenna</strong> high and 3+ feet away from electrical panels</li><li>Connect ONLY to:</li><li><em>9090:</em> Cell 1 Main / Cell 1 DIV</li><li><em>9010:</em> LTE Main / LTE DIV</li><li>❌ <strong>Do NOT use Wi-Fi ports or outer terminals</strong></li><li>Connect cables from the surface mount box to PIAB (CDS 9010/9090)</li><li>Confirm <strong>dial tone</strong> on all lines</li><li>Test <strong>inbound/outbound calls</strong></li><li>Match phone numbers with surface mount box labels</li><li>Use service loop to extend cable to customer DMARC</li><li>Contact Tech Americas for <strong>Customer Remote Support Session</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>6. Extended Connectivity Instructions (if required)</strong></p><p>If poor LTE signal is detected or WAN must be routed to an existing switch:</p><p><strong>WAN Connection Tasks</strong>:</p><ul><li>Connect PIAB WAN port to <strong>dedicated switch port</strong> (info provided by MetTel)</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment</strong>:</p><ul><li>Patch cords: 10ft, 25ft, 50ft</li><li>If over 50ft run:</li><li>300ft CAT5/CAT6</li><li>RJ45 and RJ11 connectors</li><li>Crimping tool</li><li>8ft ladder</li><li>Hammer drill</li><li>2-way splitter</li></ul><p><strong>Testing and Completion</strong>:</p><ul><li>Coordinate with Customer for validation</li><li>Test all lines for dial tone and 933 site location playback</li><li>Photograph final setup (if allowed)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>7. Mandatory Identification for Federal Access</strong></p><p><strong>Technician must present one of the following IDs at site access checkpoints</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Enhanced Driver’s License</strong> or <strong>Enhanced ID</strong></li><li>OR standard ID <strong>plus one</strong> of:</li><li>U.S. Passport / Passport Card</li><li>DHS Trusted Traveler Cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</li><li>U.S. DoD ID (including dependents)</li><li>Permanent Resident Card</li><li>Border Crossing Card</li><li>Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe ID (including ETCs)</li><li>HSPD-12 PIV Card</li><li>Foreign Government Passport</li><li>Canadian Provincial License / Indian Affairs Canada Card</li><li>TWIC</li><li>Employment Authorization Card (I-766)</li><li>Merchant Mariner Credential</li><li>Veteran Health ID (VHIC)</li></ul><p><strong>Failure to comply with ID requirements may lead to denied access and forfeited payment.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>8. Required Tools – Must Be On-Site</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop (with serial port or USB adapter + TeamViewer)</li><li>Console cable</li><li>4G hotspot / MIFI / phone tether</li><li>Cable toner</li><li>Punch down tool</li><li>Lineman’s handset (Buttset – NOT homemade)</li><li>Cable crimper</li><li>Electrical multimeter</li><li>300’ CAT5e cable</li><li>Cross connect wire</li><li>6’-8’ ladder</li><li>RJ45 &amp; RJ11 jacks</li><li>2 &amp; 3-way splitters</li><li>Modular plugs</li><li>Standard power drill</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>9. Collateral – Submit After Completion</strong></p><p><strong>Photo Documentation</strong> (Before &amp; After)</p><p><strong>Signed Work Order</strong></p><p><strong>Send Immediately To:</strong></p><p><strong>documents@tech-americas.com</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>﻿**** Dress Code ****</strong></p><p><br></p><p>All technicians must dress professionally while on site:</p><ul><li>Plain T-shirt (preferably polo)</li><li>Jeans or khakis (not tattered or torn)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>** Important – Compliance Requirement **</p><ul><li>If a customer issues a complaint regarding inappropriate dress code, payment will be at risk due to non-compliance.</li><li>Technicians must also maintain proper hygiene and avoid strong or unpleasant odors, as these may create escalations with the customer and jeopardize payment.</li></ul><p>Consistent professionalism in appearance and presentation is required to protect both Tech Americas’ reputation and technician assignments.</p><p><br></p><p>All communication MUST be done over the phone or direct emails to us. If you arrive at the site and do not contact us, we will mark it as a nonvalid visit, if no response on the same day of the dispatch, thus CANCELING THE TICKET WITH NO PAYMENT.</p><p><br></p><p><em><u>FAILURE TO FOLLOW THE ABOVE AND BELOW ON-SITE STEPS COULD RESULT IN NO PAY FOR WORK NOT COMPLETED PROPERLY</u></em></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T11:00","end":"2026-10-14T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":72},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30