{"job":{"id":20110560,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"2i-T LLC","title":"Experienced Network Field Technician for UPS installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope Summary:</strong></p><p>2i-T requires an experienced <strong>Lead Field Technician</strong> to perform the <strong>installation of one (1) GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN</strong> <strong>UPS</strong>, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification &amp; removal.</p><p>This is a <strong>Vertiv customer site</strong>, and the technician must represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> professionally while onsite. YOU <strong>MUST</strong> READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.</p><p><strong>SITE &amp; CONTACT INFORMATION</strong></p><p><strong>Remote Engineering Contact:</strong> Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068</p><p><strong>Customer:</strong> Vertiv (per dispatch details)</p><p><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES &amp; TASKS</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.</li><li>Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.</li><li>Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.</li><li>Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.</li><li>Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.</li><li>Install new Vertiv <strong>GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN</strong> UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.</li><li>Configure <strong>RDU101 network interface cards</strong> and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.</li><li><strong>Upgrade firmware</strong> using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.</li><li>Apply provided <strong>Vertiv service tags</strong> and verify unit labeling.</li><li>Capture and upload required photos:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Units powered and plugged into outlets</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit</li><li>Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.</li><li>Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.</li><li>Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; EQUIPMENT</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed</li><li>Multimeter</li><li>Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)</li><li>Mobile hotspot or tethering capability</li><li>Battery bank / phone charger</li><li>Standard hand tools, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Torx T-10 bit</li><li>PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area</li><li>Insulated tools recommended</li></ul><p><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></p><ul><li>Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).</li><li>Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.</li><li>Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.</li><li>Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.</li><li>Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.</li></ul><p><strong>ON-SITE CONDUCT &amp; COMMUNICATION</strong></p><ul><li>Represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.</li><li>Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.</li><li>Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.</li><li>Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.</li></ul><p><strong>DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.</li><li>Updated firmware confirmation.</li><li>Service tags applied.</li><li>Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.</li><li>Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.</li></ul><p><strong>NOTES</strong></p><ul><li>All work performed under Vertiv authorization.</li><li>Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.</li><li>Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.</li><li>Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.</li></ul><p><strong>MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING</strong></p><p>We published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.</p><p><strong>This training is free of charge</strong> (other than your time), takes roughly <strong>1.5 hours</strong>, and once completed:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you <em>cannot</em> normally obtain at no cost.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.</p><p>To be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.</p><p>If you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.</p><p>Looking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.</p>","markdown":"**Scope Summary:**\n\n2i-T requires an experienced **Lead Field Technician** to perform the **installation of one (1) GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN** **UPS**, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification & removal.\n\nThis is a **Vertiv customer site**, and the technician must represent **Vertiv** professionally while onsite. YOU **MUST** READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.\n\n**SITE & CONTACT INFORMATION**\n\n**Remote Engineering Contact:** Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068\n\n**Customer:** Vertiv (per dispatch details)\n\n**RESPONSIBILITIES & TASKS**\n\n- Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.\n- Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.\n- Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.\n- Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.\n- Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.\n- Install new Vertiv **GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN** UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.\n- Configure **RDU101 network interface cards** and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.\n- **Upgrade firmware** using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.\n- Apply provided **Vertiv service tags** and verify unit labeling.\n- Capture and upload required photos:\n- Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)\n- Units powered and plugged into outlets\n- Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit\n- Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.\n- Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.\n- Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS & EQUIPMENT**\n\n- Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed\n- Multimeter\n- Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)\n- Mobile hotspot or tethering capability\n- Battery bank / phone charger\n- Standard hand tools, including:\n- Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits\n- Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver\n- Torx T-10 bit\n- PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area\n- Insulated tools recommended\n\n**QUALIFICATIONS**\n\n- Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).\n- Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.\n- Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.\n- Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.\n- Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.\n\n**ON-SITE CONDUCT & COMMUNICATION**\n\n- Represent **Vertiv** while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.\n- Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.\n- Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.\n- Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.\n\n**DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.\n- Updated firmware confirmation.\n- Service tags applied.\n- Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.\n- Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.\n\n**NOTES**\n\n- All work performed under Vertiv authorization.\n- Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.\n- Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.\n- Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.\n\n**MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING**\n\nWe published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.\n\n**This training is free of charge** (other than your time), takes roughly **1.5 hours**, and once completed:\n\n· You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.\n\n· You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.\n\n· You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you *cannot* normally obtain at no cost.\n\n· We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.\n\nTo be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.\n\nIf you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.\n\nLooking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":145},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.78559070548684},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $145 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791306658544}
{"job":{"id":20112284,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #303483 - (STRSPRT-1745974) 7247 - Fortinet Port Security","description":{"html":"<p>****TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY</p><p>BEFORE GOING TO SITE AND ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS.&nbsp;*********</p><p>Tech must call TRCA at 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with our OST department.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Scope of Work:</p><p>The scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:</p><p><br></p><p>Please dispatch a technician to store 7247 to test and repair or replace a cable for the surveyor/HVAC controller. The patch cable connects to Switch 2 Port 34. We see that these cables fail a cable test, it is possible that the zipped too tight.</p><p>The due date for service is 10/9/26.</p><p>Please have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;Documentation:</p><p>Document all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.</p><p>Maintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Take pictures of completed work at various angles.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Submit pictures for the following areas:</p><p>-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)</p><p>-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office</p><p>-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office</p><p>-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)</p><p>-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area</p><p>Confirm the following:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)</p><p>-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:</p><p># of pin pads</p><p># of thin client terminals</p><p># of laser printers</p><p># of thermal printers</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The technician is responsible for:</p><p>Providing all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Ensuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to safety guidelines and protocols.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Completing the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Promptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Conducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Collaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Communicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Maintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>To Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :</p><p>In addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.</p><p>IF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.</p><p>*******************</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before leaving site, call O'Reilly Help Desk at:</p><p>417-427-1313 to confirm all connectivity on the network.</p><p>Tech must have with him/her onsite in case any repairs need to be made.</p><p>8' ladder</p><p>Cable tester</p><p>RJ45 jacks</p><p>White CAT5 cable</p><p>Orange yellow and/or blue patch cables</p><p>Take before &amp; after photos and submit to TRCA before leaving site*</p><p>Label Maker - DO NOT USE A SHARPIE OR PEN WHEN LABELING</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*\\*TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY\n\nBEFORE GOING TO SITE AND ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTech must call TRCA at 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with our OST department.\n\nScope of Work:\n\nThe scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:\n\nPlease dispatch a technician to store 7247 to test and repair or replace a cable for the surveyor/HVAC controller. The patch cable connects to Switch 2 Port 34. We see that these cables fail a cable test, it is possible that the zipped too tight.\n\nThe due date for service is 10/9/26.\n\nPlease have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.\n\n Documentation:\n\nDocument all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.\n\nMaintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.\n\nTake pictures of completed work at various angles.\n\nSubmit pictures for the following areas:\n\n-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)\n\n-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office\n\n-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office\n\n-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)\n\n-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area\n\nConfirm the following:\n\n-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)\n\n-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:\n\n\\# of pin pads\n\n\\# of thin client terminals\n\n\\# of laser printers\n\n\\# of thermal printers\n\nThe technician is responsible for:\n\nProviding all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)\n\nEnsuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.\n\nAdhering to safety guidelines and protocols.\n\nCompleting the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)\n\nPromptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.\n\nConducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.\n\nCollaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.\n\nCommunicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.\n\nAdhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.\n\nMaintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.\n\nTo Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :\n\nIn addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.\n\nIF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nBefore leaving site, call O'Reilly Help Desk at:\n\n417-427-1313 to confirm all connectivity on the network.\n\nTech must have with him/her onsite in case any repairs need to be made.\n\n8' ladder\n\nCable tester\n\nRJ45 jacks\n\nWhite CAT5 cable\n\nOrange yellow and/or blue patch cables\n\nTake before & after photos and submit to TRCA before leaving site\\*\n\nLabel Maker - DO NOT USE A SHARPIE OR PEN WHEN LABELING","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T08:00","end":"2026-10-09T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":67.51318445017249},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/6/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000