{"job":{"id":20111720,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Brandpoint Services","title":"2 Techs Needed - Menu Board Swap, configuration and drop off","description":{"html":"<p>Please text Brandpoint Services at 856-382-2645 when you are on your way, when you arrive onsite, and when you are ready to leave to review work. You will receive your checkout code after you submit your photos, sign off and receipt from dropping off the screen at FedEx.</p><p>We are swapping out a defective display for a new one. (usually a black spot on defective unit)</p><p>We are taking the defective unit and packing it in the new box, and will be dropping it off at a local FedEx the same/next business day.</p><p>After Replacement call support to ensure correct content is up on the new screen.</p><p>Photos and Sign Off Sheet/Checklist needed before leaving site.</p><p>Photo of drop off receipt needed (Boxes are large so need a large SUV, van or pickup)</p><p>MUST HAVE TORX SECURITY BITS/SCREWDRIVERS</p><p>You are responsible for checking the weather before going to site. An ODMB should not be performed in the rain.</p><p>We want to avoid the lunch rush of noon to 1PM arrival.</p><p>CONFIRM FEDEX TRACKING BEFORE GOING TO SITE!&nbsp;A TRIP CHARGE WILL NOT BE ISSUED FOR SITE VISITS AND THE MONITOR HAS NOT ARRIVED YET.</p><p>Trip Charges are $150 if we are unable to complete the swap in its entirety. (IE no key or refused to work)</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Please text Brandpoint Services at 856-382-2645 when you are on your way, when you arrive onsite, and when you are ready to leave to review work. You will receive your checkout code after you submit your photos, sign off and receipt from dropping off the screen at FedEx.\n\nWe are swapping out a defective display for a new one. (usually a black spot on defective unit)\n\nWe are taking the defective unit and packing it in the new box, and will be dropping it off at a local FedEx the same/next business day.\n\nAfter Replacement call support to ensure correct content is up on the new screen.\n\nPhotos and Sign Off Sheet/Checklist needed before leaving site.\n\nPhoto of drop off receipt needed (Boxes are large so need a large SUV, van or pickup)\n\nMUST HAVE TORX SECURITY BITS/SCREWDRIVERS\n\nYou are responsible for checking the weather before going to site. An ODMB should not be performed in the rain.\n\nWe want to avoid the lunch rush of noon to 1PM arrival.\n\nCONFIRM FEDEX TRACKING BEFORE GOING TO SITE! A TRIP CHARGE WILL NOT BE ISSUED FOR SITE VISITS AND THE MONITOR HAS NOT ARRIVED YET.\n\nTrip Charges are $150 if we are unable to complete the swap in its entirety. (IE no key or refused to work)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00","end":"2026-10-08T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":0.401964775975059},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"menu board\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791306707050}
{"job":{"id":20115308,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"2026 Starlink Service Support - Basic Troubleshooting  - No Parts","description":{"html":"<p><strong></strong></p><p><strong><b></b></strong></p><p><b>2025 Starlink Service Support - Basic Troubleshooting - NO parts sent</b></p><p><b>**Tech will need to bring a laptop with RJ45 Compatibility.**</b></p><p><b>webapp.starlink.com</b></p><p><b><span></span></b></p><p><b><span><strong>Have WJID and City/State when calling to check in.</strong></span></b></p><p><b><span><strong>&#65279;Check in: 855-609-9292 Opt 2, Opt 1</strong></span></b></p><p><b><span><strong>Check Out:&#160;479-879-3183</strong></span></b></p><p></p><p><b>Overview:&#160;</b><span>This guide provides steps for troubleshooting a malfunctioning Starlink device. The device may have a link, but still experiencing issues. Follow the below steps before calling the&#160;</span><b>Help Desk Contacts</b><span>&#160;below.</span></p><p>Be sure to check your messages for your incident number from Noah Parsons or Linda Stone, the help desk will need that.</p><p><b>Steps to Complete</b></p><p>1.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Tasks: Locate the Starlink device. Ensure it is:<br/><br/></p><p>A.&#160; Upright, and has the cable plugged into it.</p><p><span>B.&#160; Locate the power supply unit (PSU) and ensure the cables are seated properly at the PSU and switch. PSU should have a white light on it.</span></p><p>C.&#160; &#160;Listen to the dish for odd noises. A low electrical hum is normal, but loud or clicking sounds are not.</p><p>D.&#160; &#160;Power cycle the device by unplugging the three cables on the bottom of the power supply for 30 seconds.<br/></p><p>E.&#160; &#160;Power back up the device and check for a link light at the port. If there is no link light call the support line to inform them and see if they want to try additional steps such as another power cycle or new port.</p><p><span>F.&#160; &#160;</span><span>Connect the ethernet cable to your laptop and go to webapp.starlink.com take a picture of the dashboard when it loads.&#160;</span></p><p><br/></p><p>2.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Validation: Get your incident number from the direct messages and then call the <b>HELP DESK&#160;</b>&#160;for your store type below, informing them of steps taken and see if they would like to try other steps.<br/><b>(THE HELP DESK WILL NOT HELP YOU WITHOUT THE INCIDENT NUMBER, DO NOT SKIP THAT STEP.)</b></p><p><b>Help Desk Contacts:&#160;</b></p><p><i>Wal-Mart, Sam's Club or Neighborhood Market:&#160;<b>479-277-2674</b></i><b></b></p><p><i>Walmart DC Sites:&#160;<b>479-802-5458</b>&#160;(Option 1, Option 1, Option 1).</i></p><p>3. D<b>eliverables:</b></p><p></p><p><span><span>a.<span>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </span></span></span><span>Photo of the current dish</span></p><p><span><span>b.<span>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </span></span></span><span>Photo of the power supply location</span></p><p><span><span>c.<span>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </span></span></span><span>Photo of the port and switch</span></p><p><span><span>d.<span>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </span></span></span><span>Roof eight to determine what kind of lift is needed if a return trip is needed.</span></p><p></p><p>e.&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Photo of the cabinet location from the ground if not in the UPC room.</p><p>f.&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Photo of the starlink dashboard from webapp.starlink.com</p><p></p><p></p><p><b>Escalation Contacts</b></p><p><b>Project Manager: Linda Stone 479-879-3183</b></p><p><br/></p><p></p>","markdown":"**2025 Starlink Service Support - Basic Troubleshooting - NO parts sent**\n\n**\\*\\*Tech will need to bring a laptop with RJ45 Compatibility.\\*\\***\n\n**webapp.starlink.com**\n\n****Have WJID and City/State when calling to check in.****\n\n****﻿Check in: 855-609-9292 Opt 2, Opt 1****\n\n****Check Out: 479-879-3183****\n\n**Overview:** This guide provides steps for troubleshooting a malfunctioning Starlink device. The device may have a link, but still experiencing issues. Follow the below steps before calling the **Help Desk Contacts** below.\n\nBe sure to check your messages for your incident number from Noah Parsons or Linda Stone, the help desk will need that.\n\n**Steps to Complete**\n\n1\\. Tasks: Locate the Starlink device. Ensure it is:\n\nA. Upright, and has the cable plugged into it.\n\nB. Locate the power supply unit (PSU) and ensure the cables are seated properly at the PSU and switch. PSU should have a white light on it.\n\nC. Listen to the dish for odd noises. A low electrical hum is normal, but loud or clicking sounds are not.\n\nD. Power cycle the device by unplugging the three cables on the bottom of the power supply for 30 seconds.\n\nE. Power back up the device and check for a link light at the port. If there is no link light call the support line to inform them and see if they want to try additional steps such as another power cycle or new port.\n\nF. Connect the ethernet cable to your laptop and go to webapp.starlink.com take a picture of the dashboard when it loads.\n\n2\\. Validation: Get your incident number from the direct messages and then call the **HELP DESK**  for your store type below, informing them of steps taken and see if they would like to try other steps.  \n**(THE HELP DESK WILL NOT HELP YOU WITHOUT THE INCIDENT NUMBER, DO NOT SKIP THAT STEP.)**\n\n**Help Desk Contacts:**\n\n*Wal-Mart, Sam's Club or Neighborhood Market: **479-277-2674***\n\n*Walmart DC Sites: **479-802-5458** (Option 1, Option 1, Option 1).*\n\n3\\. D**eliverables:**\n\na. Photo of the current dish\n\nb. Photo of the power supply location\n\nc. Photo of the port and switch\n\nd. Roof eight to determine what kind of lift is needed if a return trip is needed.\n\ne. Photo of the cabinet location from the ground if not in the UPC room.\n\nf. Photo of the starlink dashboard from webapp.starlink.com\n\n**Escalation Contacts**\n\n**Project Manager: Linda Stone 479-879-3183**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T12:00","end":"2026-10-06T16:00","latestStart":"2026-10-06T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7.1945402876803035},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Workmarket Roma ticket"},{"start":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Dana doctor"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z