{"job":{"id":20115620,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Telco Holdings Inc","title":"Wake Forest, NC - Install Printer - 10/7","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Provider, Please Read the following:</u></strong></p>\n<p>By accepting this assignment, you confirm you have reviewed and understand all attached documentation, including floor plans and SOW documents.</p>\n<p>Tobacco and vape use is prohibited onsite at all times, including inside, outside, and in personal vehicles while checked in or obtaining materials for this work order.</p>\n<p>Technicians must maintain business-casual attire. No flip-flops, torn clothing, tank tops, shorts, hats, open/excessively revealing clothing, or athletic wear. Clean jeans and sneakers are acceptable.</p>\n<p>The NTE listed on the work order is an estimated labor allowance only and does not guarantee payable hours.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Service Address &amp; Details:</p>\n<p>Service Ticket number: 637868 - Priority 2&nbsp;- High Printer - New Device Setup: Heather - printer</p>\n<p>Client Location Name: Guardian Dentistry Partners | Supremia Dentistry</p>\n<p>Client Location Address: 1704 South Main St Suite 110, Wake Forest, NC 27587</p>\n<p>Number of Technicians: 1</p>\n<p>Technician Type: Smart Hands</p>\n<p>****Technician MUST present as on-site for ThincForward Inc.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Access Hours:</p>\n<p>Preferred Days/Times for On Site Dispatch: Wednesday 10/7 @ 8am EST or Thursday 10/8 @ 8am EST</p>\n<p>NTE: 2 hours</p>\n<p>****Business casual attire required – no flip flops, open toed shoes, or torn clothing.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Tools/Equipment Required:</p>\n<p>Laptop and Hot spot for internet access</p>\n<p>Cable Tester and Toner</p>\n<p>Screw drivers.</p>\n<p>Spare Patch Cords (Length varies)</p>\n<p>Spare Keystone Jacks for replacement of bad ones</p>\n<p>Butt Set if troubleshooting Telecom Issues</p>\n<p>Cable ties/cable management options for general cleanup where needed</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><del>***** **** ******* **** *** ******* ********* ***** ******** ************************************************************************************************</del></p>\n<p><del>********* ******* ******* ***********</del></p>\n<p><del>************ ******** ******* * ************</del></p>\n<p>*Please call and leave a message if there is no answer.&nbsp;If your call is not returned in 15 minutes, please call in again and if there is no answer, please call your Dispatcher/Work Order Manager for support.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Scope Of Work:</p>\n<p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>1) Upon arrival call your work order manager/dispatch contact to check in on site.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2) Once checked in please call the Technical Support Contact (ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600) to review SOW and then proceed to the front desk to check in with the site contact.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>3) Introduce yourself to the site contact as onsite as ThincForward and briefly review the SOW you will be completing.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>4) Detailed Scope of Work: **Smart Hands technician needed on site to: **The new printer arrived at the office. Tech will install the new printer the office shows and get it connected to the office's network. Call the IT Helpdesk so we can get it added to the needed PCs and confirm it works.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>5) Take images of ALL completed work on site including cabling, jacks/faceplates, and replaced equipment in functional order.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>6) *Old Equipment:*&nbsp;If you have replaced equipment on site, please follow the notes below regarding what to do with the old items.</p>\n<p>Please dispose of the old equipment.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>7) Once SOW is completed, Technician(s) must confirm all equipment on site is up and operational, and technician(s) must speak with technical support prior to leaving the site to ensure SOW is complete and to ensure there are no delays in payment.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>8) Once the site and support have confirmed work is completed, technician(s) must check out with the work order manager/dispatch contact to sign out of the location.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Deliverables:</p>\n<p>- Images of ALL completed work.</p>\n<p>- Name of person worked with on site and in support.</p>\n<p>- Confirmation that work area has been completely cleaned and is dust free.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>***DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered.&nbsp;*</strong></p>\n<p><strong>﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager.&nbsp;Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call Work Order Manager regarding You