{"job":{"id":"7319357123","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"DataMax Services, Inc","title":"Kiosk Needing service at correctional facility's Visitor or Admin/Processing area","description":"<p><strong><em>Note:</em></strong><em> This is for a correctional facility but restricted to the visitor or administrative/processing areas.</em><strong><em>&nbsp;<u>There is zero exposure to inmates' living quarters or socializing areas</u>.&nbsp;</em></strong><em>The admin/processing areas are highly secure but may have&nbsp;</em><strong><em><u>very limited exposure</u></em></strong><em>&nbsp;to inmates that are being processed into the facility.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work</u></strong>: We need a technician with kiosk experience and some cabling experience. The facility has a kiosk that is no longer in service and needs to be remedied through diagnosis and troubleshooting or replacement of parts.<strong>&nbsp;Review the Special Notes to Tech for the specific information regarding the issue at this facility</strong>. Be sure all connectivity has been re/established and is confirmed by Support/Help Desk.</p><p>Diligently review and complete all Tasks listed on this WO.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-visit Task supplemental instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If POC is not reachable, add a tag/report a problem to this WO immediately.</strong></li><li><strong>Do NOT go to site until contact is made with the POC thru phone and/or email.</strong></li><li><strong>MUST set ETA, confirm keys and parts (if needed) with POC BEFORE going to site.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>** Tech will NOT be compensated for time onsite if the above is not completed.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Check In/Checkout Procedure.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check in and out on the platform and <strong>be sure your GPS is turned on.</strong></li><li>Call Client Support at<strong>&nbsp;1-800-864-5986</strong>&nbsp;once in front of the equipment to be serviced. Work with Support to diagnose or replaced any applicable replacement equipment so they can validate.</li><li>Do not leave the site without the name of the person at Client Support that you worked with and released you.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Important Facility Entry Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Read and Adhere to the attached&nbsp;<strong><u>site conduct rules and guidelines</u></strong>&nbsp;document</li><li>NO weapons, alcohol, drugs, or contraband.</li><li>Only the assigned tech is authorized in the facility</li><li>Avoid communication with inmates or trustees.</li><li>Inventory all tools brought into the facility.</li><li>Do not leave any tools or belongings on-site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>See custom fields area for Standard Tools required</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Additional required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>$1 bill/coins&nbsp;(for testing Coin &amp; Bill Acceptors)</li><li>Cloth/wipes</li><li>Allen Wrench Set (Metric &amp; Standard)</li><li>Hex Bit Set with extensions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>NETWORK TOOLS Required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Spare CAT5E 50-100'</li><li>Crimper/Termination Tool</li><li>RJ45 terminations</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Cable Tester</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Name of Client Support person that you checked-out with</li><li>Picture of loaded paper roll and interior of the Kiosk showing wire management</li><li>Return Tracking# if applicable - Enter Zeros if no tracking #</li><li>POC Signature on your WO (Call&nbsp;DataMax&nbsp;if you are waiting more than 20 minutes for a signature.)</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T10:00","end":"2026-10-06T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":105},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":8.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/6/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"star