{"job":{"id":20115962,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cloud5 Communications","title":"Hosted - GRs down","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of Work: Site is saying ALL guest rooms have no dial tone. The phones are up and registered and all the Adtrans and the Grandstream are online and connected, the amphenol cables on the back of the secondary units may have been dislodged. Need to check connectivity, ensure they're secure, and test some rooms.</p>\n<p>Case Number: CS00138694</p>\n<p>The dispatch should be scheduled on or between: 10/07 +</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>NOTE: The on-site tech must call Cloud5-hosted support at 1-786-977-6900 upon checking in and checking out. Upon checkout, they should report the visit's status and obtain a release number before leaving the site. Before departure, consult with the GM regarding any potential phone issues. Engage Cloud5 and inform them if you are equipped to address these issues.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>NOTE: The following equipment is a must have. Without it, we cannot get local access to our equipment and will likely need to dismiss the tech.</p>\n<p>• Charged WINDOWS laptop with a functional ethernet port with latest version of Teamviewer installed.</p>\n<p>• Working USB to DB9 (RS232) cable for console access to the Cloud5 Adtran (Most cables only work on windows 10 and earlier)</p>\n<p>• DB9 to Male - DB9 to Female (Recommend cables over gender changers since most USB Serial cables are not more than few feet in length)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech support is available only from 8:00 am to 7:00 pm local time. Any work beyond the pre-scheduled duration requires Cloud5's approval, and the work order must be endorsed by hotel personnel.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>The tech will need:</p>\n<p>• Basic hand tools</p>\n<p>• Punch-Down Tool</p>\n<p>• Test Set / Butt Set</p>\n<p>• Jacks</p>\n<p>• Adapters</p>\n<p>• Toners and Trackers</p>\n<p>• Line Cords</p>\n<p>• Cross Connect Wire</p>\n<p>• Breakout Box (mini tester)</p>\n<p>• Ladder</p>\n<p>• Fully charged cell phone</p>\n<p>• SSH and SFTP client</p>\n<p>• The latest version of Teamviewer</p>\n<p>• Hotspot</p>\n<p>• Serial cable</p>\n<p>• Camera</p>\n<p>• RJ45 crimp tool</p>\n<p>• RJ45 CAT5e male and female connectors</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician Dress Code: Smart casual (e.g., polo shirt, no ripped jeans).</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician Check-In/Check-Out Requirements:</p>\n<p>The assigned technician is required to perform both check-in and check-out procedures with onsite personnel and Cloud5 Remote Support throughout the service engagement.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check-In Procedure:</p>\n<p>Upon arrival, the technician must:</p>\n<p>-Check in with the designated onsite contact.</p>\n<p>-Immediately contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm arrival.</p>\n<p>-Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked in.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check-Out Procedure:</p>\n<p>Upon completion of all work, the technician must:</p>\n<p>-Check out with the onsite contact.</p>\n<p>-Contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm completion of work.</p>\n<p>-Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked out.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Compliance Requirement:</p>\n<p>Adherence to these procedures is mandatory and failure to complete them may result in delays to payment processing and/or forfeiture of payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>***Per Cloud5 Policy, you may not enter into any occupied guest room without an escort from the site***</p>\n<p>NOTE: ON SITE TECH MUST CALL CLOUD5 SUPPORT (phone # will be available once assigned) TO REPORT STATUS OF VISIT AND RECEIVE RELEASE NUMBER BEFORE LEAVING SITE. PLEASE ALSO CHECK WITH GM BEFORE LEAVING SITE FOR ANY OTHER POSSIBLE PHONE ISSUES. Tech support is ONLY available between 8:00AM and 5:00PM Local Time. ANYTHING OVER THE ALLOTTED SCHEDULED TIME MUST BE APPROVED BY CLOUD5 PERSONNEL AND WORK ORDER MUST BE SIGNED BY HOTEL PERSONNEL (Please make sure to print work order).</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>***Necessary Telecom Tools*** - Punch-Down Tool - Test Set / Butt-Set - Jacks - Serial cables - Adapters - Toners and Trackers - Line Cords - Cross Connect Wire - Breakout box (mini-tester) - Laptop - Screwdrivers - <strong>DB9 to Male - DB9 to Female - Putty Program Installed - Teamviewer(always latest version)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician dress-code should be smart casual (polo, no ripped jeans)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please allow more than 2 hours (request expire time) when making your request.</p>","markdown":"Scope of Work: Site is saying ALL guest rooms have no dial tone. The phones are up and registered and all the Adtrans and the Grandstream are online and connected, the amphenol cables on the back of the secondary units may have been dislodged. Need to check connectivity, ensure they're secure, and test some rooms.\n\nCase Number: CS00138694\n\nThe dispatch should be scheduled on or between: 10/07 +\n\nNOTE: The on-site tech must call Cloud5-hosted support at 1-786-977-6900 upon checking in and checking out. Upon checkout, they should report the visit's status and obtain a release number before leaving the site. Before departure, consult with the GM regarding any potential phone issues. Engage Cloud5 and inform them if you are equipped to address these issues.\n\nNOTE: The following equipment is a must have. Without it, we cannot get local access to our equipment and will likely need to dismiss the tech.\n\n• Charged WINDOWS laptop with a functional ethernet port with latest version of Teamviewer installed.\n\n• Working USB to DB9 (RS232) cable for console access to the Cloud5 Adtran (Most cables only work on windows 10 and earlier)\n\n• DB9 to Male - DB9 to Female (Recommend cables over gender changers since most USB Serial cables are not more than few feet in length)\n\nTech support is available only from 8:00 am to 7:00 pm local time. Any work beyond the pre-scheduled duration requires Cloud5's approval, and the work order must be endorsed by hotel personnel.\n\nThe tech will need:\n\n• Basic hand tools\n\n• Punch-Down Tool\n\n• Test Set / Butt Set\n\n• Jacks\n\n• Adapters\n\n• Toners and Trackers\n\n• Line Cords\n\n• Cross Connect Wire\n\n• Breakout Box (mini tester)\n\n• Ladder\n\n• Fully charged cell phone\n\n• SSH and SFTP client\n\n• The latest version of Teamviewer\n\n• Hotspot\n\n• Serial cable\n\n• Camera\n\n• RJ45 crimp tool\n\n• RJ45 CAT5e male and female connectors\n\nTechnician Dress Code: Smart casual (e.g., polo shirt, no ripped jeans).\n\nTechnician Check-In/Check-Out Requirements:\n\nThe assigned technician is required to perform both check-in and check-out procedures with onsite personnel and Cloud5 Remote Support throughout the service engagement.\n\nCheck-In Procedure:\n\nUpon arrival, the technician must:\n\n-Check in with the designated onsite contact.\n\n-Immediately contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm arrival.\n\n-Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked in.\n\nCheck-Out Procedure:\n\nUpon completion of all work, the technician must:\n\n-Check out with the onsite contact.\n\n-Contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm completion of work.\n\n-Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked out.\n\nCompliance Requirement:\n\nAdherence to these procedures is mandatory and failure to complete them may result in delays to payment processing and/or forfeiture of payment.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Per Cloud5 Policy, you may not enter into any occupied guest room without an escort from the site\\*\\*\\*\n\nNOTE: ON SITE TECH MUST CALL CLOUD5 SUPPORT (phone # will be available once assigned) TO REPORT STATUS OF VISIT AND RECEIVE RELEASE NUMBER BEFORE LEAVING SITE. PLEASE ALSO CHECK WITH GM BEFORE LEAVING SITE FOR ANY OTHER POSSIBLE PHONE ISSUES. Tech support is ONLY available between 8:00AM and 5:00PM Local Time. ANYTHING OVER THE ALLOTTED SCHEDULED TIME MUST BE APPROVED BY CLOUD5 PERSONNEL AND WORK ORDER MUST BE SIGNED BY HOTEL PERSONNEL (Please make sure to print work order).\n\n\\*\\*\\*Necessary Telecom Tools\\*\\*\\* - Punch-Down Tool - Test Set / Butt-Set - Jacks - Serial cables - Adapters - Toners and Trackers - Line Cords - Cross Connect Wire - Breakout box (mini-tester) - Laptop - Screwdrivers - **DB9 to Male - DB9 to Female - Putty Program Installed - Teamviewer(always latest version)**\n\nTechnician dress-code should be smart casual (polo, no ripped jeans)\n\nPlease allow more than 2 hours (request expire time) when making your request.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T11:00","end":"2026-10-07T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-07T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13.569371701747437},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"st