{"job":{"id":20089259,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"#298308 Cabling and 1 Outdoor Verkada Camera and Gateway Installation**NO WEEKENDS**MATERIAL REQUIRED","description":{"html":"<p><strong>TECHNICIAN CHECK-IN &amp; CHECK-OUT</strong></p>\n<p><strong>• Call TRCA at (940) 381-8569 immediately upon arrival and before departure.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>• You will receive check-in/out codes — write these on the TRCA Work Order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>CONTACTS</strong></p>\n<p>Site Contact: <del>*** ***** ** ***</del></p>\n<p>Verkada Configuration Contact: <del>****** *********** ** ********* *** ****** ******* *** **** **** *************** ***** ** ***** ************</del></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE YOU BEGIN</strong></p>\n<p>Read the attached Full Scope of Work PDF and attachments carefully. If you have questions, call TRCA before going on site.</p>\n<p><strong>REFERENCE DOCUMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>• Full Scope of Work PDF</p>\n<p>• Floor Plan</p>\n<p>• Verkada Install Form</p>\n<p>• Camera Installation Mistakes to Avoid</p>\n<p>• PROPERLY SEALING OUTDOOR CAMERAS - MUST READ IF OUTDOOR CAMERAS ARE BEING INSTALLED</p>\n<p>• DRAIN WIRE IMPORTANCE PLEASE READ</p>\n<p>GC31-E Installation Instructions</p>\n<p><strong>HELPFUL RESOURCES</strong></p>\n<p>• All Verkada install/setup guides are available for free:</p>\n<p>• https://www.verkada.com/docs</p>\n<p>• Type the product part number into the search bar to view guides and videos.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>For Basic Troubleshooting if needed:</strong></p>\n<p>Test the cable, confirm it passes.</p>\n<p>Verify link light on the switch port and power light on the switch port.</p>\n<p>Take camera directly to the switch and short wire it on the port, give it 3-4 minutes, notate the LED blinking lights.</p>\n<p>Camera LED Status Indicators:</p>\n<p>https://help.verkada.com/verkada-cameras/installation/camera-led-status-indicators</p>\n<p>24/7 Verkada Support: (<del>**** ******** ***</del> Before calling, TRCA will need to provide you with support token, the customer ID and the phone number.</p>\n<p>IMPORTANT!!! If Verkada offers to do an RMA the following email address MUST be provided to them: amy.bourzikas@trca.com</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>HARDWARE INVENTORY &amp; DOCUMENTATION – MANDATORY</strong></p>\n<p>Inventory all Verkada hardware immediately upon arrival.</p>\n<p>!! Report any missing items to TRCA immediately.</p>\n<p>While completing the camera inventory, please follow the steps below to ensure a smooth setup in Verkada Command:</p>\n<p><strong>Labeling Boxes:</strong></p>\n<p>• As you unpack and inventory the cameras, label each camera box according to its planned location on the floor plan (e.g., CAM 1, CAM 2, CAM 3, etc.).</p>\n<p>• These labels should correspond to the designated camera locations on the project’s floor plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Install Form:</strong></p>\n<p>• On the install form, in the first column (next to each camera’s part #), write the camera number (CAM #) that corresponds to its labeled location.</p>\n<p>• Double-check that each camera number matches its planned location on the floor plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Submit Documentation:</strong></p>\n<p>• Once the form is complete, send it to SST@TRCA.com.</p>\n<p>• This documentation will be used to correctly set up and label the cameras within Verkada Command.</p>\n<p>If you have any questions or need clarification during the process, don’t hesitate to reach out to TRCA.</p>\n<p><strong>SHIPMENT NOTES AND EQUIPMENT RESPONSIBILITY</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Items shipped to site by TRCA:</strong></p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;GC31-E-HW&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;GC31 Cellular Gateway, Outdoor</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ACC-POE-90W-E-NA&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Outdoor 90W PoE++ (802.3bt-2018) Injector,</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CD53-256E-HW&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verkada CD53-E Outdoor Dome Camera,</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ACC-MNT-ANGLE-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verkada Angle mount&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Items provided by technician:</strong></p>\n<p>50ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6 PLENUM Cable&nbsp;- MUST BE 100% COPPER - CCA CABLE IS PROHIBITED</p>\n<p>3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;RJ45</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;weather proof sealant 1 tube</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6 outdoor patch cord 3' white</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc. consumables/ mounting hardware, cables , power strip/surge protector if needed and possible power/extension cord to be provided by the tech.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>NETWORK PROTOCOL</strong></p>\n<p>• Do not plug any switch into the network (even temporarily) without prior TRCA approval.</p>\n<p><strong>INSTALLATION SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\n<p>Installation and cabling for 1 Verkada camera, 1 Cellular Gateway, and 1 ACC-POE-Injector for the gateway.</p>\n<p>Camera and gateway are to be installed at ladder serviceable height.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>There is power inside the building but will require an extension cord to reach.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Communicate work areas to site contact and provide notice if anything must be moved to avoid delays.</p>\n<p>• Pull and label cable for cameras (if cabling is already in place, skip this step)</p>\n<p>• Provide 5' service loop on rack side and 10' loop on camera side. (For future relocation if needed by client.)</p>\n<p>• Mount all cameras and any peripherals for camera installation</p>\n<p>• Contact the config POC listed at the top of the work order to test all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations).</p>\n<p>• Confirm all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations) with site contact</p>\n<p>*Note: If working on a large install (multiple buildings or areas in a large building), as you get cameras up in an area of the building, please make sure to go ahead and aim them while there as best as you can and then check with the site contact to make sure the view is what they want. This will hopefully prevent the need to relocate the lift back to this area again for aiming.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>IMPORTANT INSTALLATION NOTES:</strong></p>\n<p>• Install at ladder-serviceable height unless higher is required for the desired view.</p>\n<p>• Avoid obstruction from shelves, signage, or stock.</p>\n<p>• Secure cables neatly with screw hole tie wraps or similar. No exposed or hanging runs.</p>\n<p>• Mount height generally 10'; max is 20'.</p>\n<p>• Each cable pull requires a 5' service loop at the rack side and 10' at the device side.</p>\n<p>• Scissor lift work requires your own harness to be worn at all times.</p>\n<p><strong>FINAL DELIVERABLES – Due Within 48 Hours of Completion</strong></p>\n<p>Submit via email to SST@TRCA.com or upload as directed:</p>\n<p>• First and last name of the person onsite with whom functionality was confirmed</p>\n<p>• Name of TRCA IT Projects Team contact who assisted with final testing</p>\n<p>• Final photo set of completed work</p>\n<p>• Final labeled photo of the network rack with visible camera patch ports</p>\n<p>• Completed Verkada Install Form</p>\n<p>• Signed TRCA Work Order (signed by site contact/client)</p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE LEAVING SITE, TECHNICIAN MUST CALL TRCA (940-381-8569) TO CHECK OUT.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>You will receive a check-out code that must be written on the TRCA Work Order.</strong></p>","markdown":"**TECHNICIAN CHECK-IN & CHECK-OUT**\n\n**• Call TRCA at (940) 381-8569 immediately upon arrival and before departure.**\n\n**• You will receive check-in/out codes — write these on the TRCA Work Order.**\n\n**CONTACTS**\n\nSite Contact: \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\n\nVerkada Configuration Contact: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**BEFORE YOU BEGIN**\n\nRead the attached Full Scope of Work PDF and attachments carefully. If you have questions, call TRCA before going on site.\n\n**REFERENCE DOCUMENTS**\n\n• Full Scope of Work PDF\n\n• Floor Plan\n\n• Verkada Install Form\n\n• Camera Installation Mistakes to Avoid\n\n• PROPERLY SEALING OUTDOOR CAMERAS - MUST READ IF OUTDOOR CAMERAS ARE BEING INSTALLED\n\n• DRAIN WIRE IMPORTANCE PLEASE READ\n\nGC31-E Installation Instructions\n\n**HELPFUL RESOURCES**\n\n• All Verkada install/setup guides are available for free:\n\n• <https://www.verkada.com/docs>\n\n• Type the product part number into the search bar to view guides and videos.\n\n**For Basic Troubleshooting if needed:**\n\nTest the cable, confirm it passes.\n\nVerify link light on the switch port and power light on the switch port.\n\nTake camera directly to the switch and short wire it on the port, give it 3-4 minutes, notate the LED blinking lights.\n\nCamera LED Status Indicators:\n\n<https://help.verkada.com/verkada-cameras/installation/camera-led-status-indicators>\n\n24/7 Verkada Support: (\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Before calling, TRCA will need to provide you with support token, the customer ID and the phone number.\n\nIMPORTANT!!! If Verkada offers to do an RMA the following email address MUST be provided to them: amy.bourzikas@trca.com\n\n**HARDWARE INVENTORY & DOCUMENTATION – MANDATORY**\n\nInventory all Verkada hardware immediately upon arrival.\n\n!! Report any missing items to TRCA immediately.\n\nWhile completing the camera inventory, please follow the steps below to ensure a smooth setup in Verkada Command:\n\n**Labeling Boxes:**\n\n• As you unpack and inventory the cameras, label each camera box according to its planned location on the floor plan (e.g., CAM 1, CAM 2, CAM 3, etc.).\n\n• These labels should correspond to the designated camera locations on the project’s floor plan.\n\n**Install Form:**\n\n• On the install form, in the first column (next to each camera’s part #), write the camera number (CAM #) that corresponds to its labeled location.\n\n• Double-check that each camera number matches its planned location on the floor plan.\n\n**Submit Documentation:**\n\n• Once the form is complete, send it to SST@TRCA.com.\n\n• This documentation will be used to correctly set up and label the cameras within Verkada Command.\n\nIf you have any questions or need clarification during the process, don’t hesitate to reach out to TRCA.\n\n**SHIPMENT NOTES AND EQUIPMENT RESPONSIBILITY**\n\n**Items shipped to site by TRCA:**\n\n1 GC31-E-HW GC31 Cellular Gateway, Outdoor\n\n1 ACC-POE-90W-E-NA Outdoor 90W PoE++ (802.3bt-2018) Injector,\n\n1 CD53-256E-HW Verkada CD53-E Outdoor Dome Camera,\n\n1 ACC-MNT-ANGLE-1 Verkada Angle mount\n\n**Items provided by technician:**\n\n50ft CAT6 PLENUM Cable - MUST BE 100% COPPER - CCA CABLE IS PROHIBITED\n\n3 RJ45\n\n1 weather proof sealant 1 tube\n\n1 CAT6 outdoor patch cord 3' white\n\n1 misc. consumables/ mounting hardware, cables , power strip/surge protector if needed and possible power/extension cord to be provided by the tech.\n\n**NETWORK PROTOCOL**\n\n• Do not plug any switch into the network (even temporarily) without prior TRCA approval.\n\n**INSTALLATION SCOPE OF WORK**\n\nInstallation and cabling for 1 Verkada camera, 1 Cellular Gateway, and 1 ACC-POE-Injector for the gateway.\n\nCamera and gateway are to be installed at ladder serviceable height.\n\nThere is power inside the building but will require an extension cord to reach.\n\nCommunicate work areas to site contact and provide notice if anything must be moved to avoid delays.\n\n• Pull and label cable for cameras (if cabling is already in place, skip this step)\n\n• Provide 5' service loop on rack side and 10' loop on camera side. (For future relocation if needed by client.)\n\n• Mount all cameras and any peripherals for camera installation\n\n• Contact the config POC listed at the top of the work order to test all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations).\n\n• Confirm all cameras and viewing stations (if site has viewing stations) with site contact\n\n\\*Note: If working on a large install (multiple buildings or areas in a large building), as you get cameras up in an area of the building, please make sure to go ahead and aim them while there as best as you can and then check with the site contact to make sure the view is what they want. This will hopefully prevent the need to relocate the lift back to this area again for aiming.\n\n**IMPORTANT INSTALLATION NOTES:**\n\n• Install at ladder-serviceable height unless higher is required for the desired view.\n\n• Avoid obstruction from shelves, signage, or stock.\n\n• Secure cables neatly with screw hole tie wraps or similar. No exposed or hanging runs.\n\n• Mount height generally 10'; max is 20'.\n\n• Each cable pull requires a 5' service loop at the rack side and 10' at the device side.\n\n• Scissor lift work requires your own harness to be worn at all times.\n\n**FINAL DELIVERABLES – Due Within 48 Hours of Completion**\n\nSubmit via email to SST@TRCA.com or upload as directed:\n\n• First and last name of the person onsite with whom functionality was confirmed\n\n• Name of TRCA IT Projects Team contact who assisted with final testing\n\n• Final photo set of completed work\n\n• Final labeled photo of the network rack with visible camera patch ports\n\n• Completed Verkada Install Form\n\n• Signed TRCA Work Order (signed by site contact/client)\n\n**BEFORE LEAVING SITE, TECHNICIAN MUST CALL TRCA (940-381-8569) TO CHECK OUT.**\n\n**You will receive a check-out code that must be written on the TRCA Work Order.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":40.06245304368875},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 (countered: $210) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791312657965}
{"job":{"id":"6967155297","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"Please check in and out with Property Manager<br>If the survey runs over 2 hours you need to get permission from the Property Manager to continue and please let them know about how much longer would be needed<br>Please survey for all fire alarms, burg alarms, elevators, pool phones(voice), fax<br>If there are different building on the property there are probably fire alarms in each one<br>Please work with Property Manager to make sure we get the correct information<br>If you have any issues please reach out to Hilal 9194246791 or 919-870-5080<br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2. Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>4. Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>5. Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>6. Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br> <br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Infrared Temperature Gun\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T10:00","end":"2026-09-30T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":4.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/30/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T15:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T18:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"s