{"job":{"id":20117968,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #231952 - Sensor Bypassed | Back Door Sensor Replacement ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><br><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> BACK DOOR WIRED-CONTACT SENSOR REPLACEMENT, LEGACY HARDWARE DECOMMISSIONING, PANEL PAIRING / ZONE TESTING &amp; DUAL VERIFICATION</p><p><br></p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p>A security technician is required on-site to troubleshoot, decommission, and replace a failing or defective <strong>Back Door</strong> alarm sensor with a brand-new <strong>wired-contact sensor and magnet assembly</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will carefully unmount and completely remove all old, failing, or unused sensor hardware from the back door frame and leaf. After cleaning the mounting surface of old adhesive residue, the technician will mount the new wired-contact sensor and magnet ($\\le 0.5\\text{ inches}$ air gap tolerance) and securely route and land the low-voltage wire leads into the designated auxiliary terminal block (transmitter or panel input).</p><p><br></p><p>Once physically installed and wired, the technician will coordinate directly with remote <strong>Activations</strong> to pair/enroll the hardware, confirm correct panel zone/loop programming, and execute functional door open/close trip tests. The technician must ensure the Back Door zone reports fault and restore telemetry accurately to the central alarm panel before leaving.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>LEGACY HARDWARE DECOMMISSIONING &amp; DISPOSAL MANDATE:</strong> The technician <strong>MUST</strong> remove all legacy or defective door sensor bodies, backplates, and contact magnets from the target door panel and frame to prevent magnetic/RF interference. Place all removed legacy hardware neatly into an empty box, label it clearly as <strong>\"DECOMMISSIONED DOOR SENSOR - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area or manager's office. Do not remove hardware from the property.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must receive explicit operational and zone telemetry confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for alarm panel interface diagnostics, communicator checks, or gateway troubleshooting)</li><li><strong>New Wired-Contact Sensor &amp; Magnet Assembly</strong> (On-site / shipped hardware)</li><li><strong>22/2 Low-Voltage Alarm Wire &amp; B-Connectors / Gel-Filled Beans</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for extending contact leads to auxiliary terminals)</li><li><strong>Small Precision Screwdriver Set &amp; Hand Tools</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for micro-terminal blocks inside transmitter bodies/panel zones)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter &amp; Wire Strippers / Crimpers</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for checking loop continuity $\\Omega$)</li><li><strong>Surface Cleaning Pads / Alcohol Wipes</strong> (For stripping old tape residue off door frames)</li><li><strong>Self-Tapping Screws (6 x ¾\" Phillips) &amp; Heavy-Duty Mounting Tape</strong> (For securing sensor and magnet)</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill &amp; Precision Bits</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> Adhesive wire clips, packaging tape, and permanent marker</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong>PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the Back Door sensor location and collect the newly shipped wired-contact replacement unit.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the hardwired scope, confirm target zone number for the Back Door, and verify expected panel loop settings before unmounting hardware.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING &amp; HARDWIRED SENSOR INSTALLATION</strong><ol><li><strong>DECOMMISSIONING:</strong> Carefully unmount and completely remove the old, failing Back Door sensor, backplate, and magnet.</li><li><strong>SURFACE PREPARATION:</strong> Clean the mounting surfaces thoroughly using alcohol wipes/adhesive remover to strip away grease, dirt, and old tape residue.</li><li><strong>HARDWIRED CONTACT MOUNTING:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Securely mount the new wired-contact body to the stationary door frame/header using screws or heavy-duty mounting tape.</li><li>Securely mount the corresponding magnet to the moving door panel.</li><li><strong>Gap Tolerance:</strong> Ensure alignment notches match and the physical air gap between sensor and magnet is <strong>0.5 inches or less</strong> ($\\le 0.5\\text{ inches}$) when the door is fully closed and latched.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>TERMINAL WIRING:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Route and land the 2-conductor wire leads from the new contact directly onto the hardwired input terminals (<strong>NC / COM</strong>) of the door transmitter or panel expansion module. Tighten terminal screws firmly.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 3: PANEL PAIRING, TELEMETRY TESTING &amp; ACTIVATIONS VERIFICATION</strong><ol><li><strong>PROGRAMMING &amp; PAIRING AUDIT:</strong> Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Have remote support confirm the Back Door zone is correctly paired/enrolled and configured for the proper hardwired loop input.</li><li><strong>FUNCTIONAL ZONE TRIP &amp; RESTORE TESTS:</strong> Open and close the Back Door multiple times:</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Door Open:</strong> Confirm Activations receives an instantaneous \"Zone Open / Fault\" telemetry signal on the designated zone.</li><li><strong>Door Closed:</strong> Confirm Activations receives an instantaneous \"Zone Closed / Restored\" telemetry signal on the designated zone.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>KEYPAD STATUS AUDIT:</strong> Confirm the local alarm keypad reflects real-time door state changes and displays a clear \"Ready to Arm\" status when the door is closed, with zero active trouble codes.</li><li><strong>MOD DEMONSTRATION:</strong> Demonstrate physical open/close operation of the Back Door to the store manager, showing fault-free keypad response.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 4: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:</strong> Box up all old removed door sensors and hardware. Write <strong>\"DECOMMISSIONED DOOR SENSOR - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> clearly on the package in bold permanent marker and stage it in the store's IT room or manager's office. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Clean up wire insulation scraps, tape backing, drill dust, and packaging wrappers. Ensure the entryway and surrounding floor spaces are left completely spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Back Door Wired Contact Installed:</strong> Close-up photo showing the replacement wired contact and magnet cleanly installed and aligned ($\\le 0.5\\text{ inches}$ gap) on the back door header and panel.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Hardwired Terminal Block Wiring:</strong> Clear photo showing wire leads landed securely onto the internal terminal blocks/auxiliary inputs of the transmitter/panel.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Restored Clear Keypad Status:</strong> Photo showing the alarm keypad displaying a fault-free \"Ready to Arm\" status with the back door closed.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Hardware:</strong> Photo showing the old door sensor hardware boxed, labeled <strong>\"STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and set aside in the IT storage area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network / Alarm Panel Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire IT network / alarm panel rack cabinet with the door OPEN</strong>.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the floor and frame around the back door work area are swept completely clean of installation debris.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that the new wired door contact is successfully paired/enrolled, real-time open/close telemetry is confirmed, and the panel is clear of all trouble conditions.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Demonstrate proper operation of the hardwired back door sensor to the store manager, confirm keypad \"Ready to Arm\" status, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed sensor replacement, system validation, and site cleanliness.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update internal ticket notes detailing the installation of the wired contact, confirmation of pairing/loop programming, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n  \n**TICKET SUMMARY:** BACK DOOR WIRED-CONTACT SENSOR REPLACEMENT, LEGACY HARDWARE DECOMMISSIONING, PANEL PAIRING / ZONE TESTING & DUAL VERIFICATION\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A security technician is required on-site to troubleshoot, decommission, and replace a failing or defective **Back Door** alarm sensor with a brand-new **wired-contact sensor and magnet assembly**.\n\nThe technician will carefully unmount and completely remove all old, failing, or unused sensor hardware from the back door frame and leaf. After cleaning the mounting surface of old adhesive residue, the technician will mount the new wired-contact sensor and magnet ($\\\\le 0.5\\\\text{ inches}$ air gap tolerance) and securely route and land the low-voltage wire leads into the designated auxiliary terminal block (transmitter or panel input).\n\nOnce physically installed and wired, the technician will coordinate directly with remote **Activations** to pair/enroll the hardware, confirm correct panel zone/loop programming, and execute functional door open/close trip tests. The technician must ensure the Back Door zone reports fault and restore telemetry accurately to the central alarm panel before leaving.\n\n**LEGACY HARDWARE DECOMMISSIONING & DISPOSAL MANDATE:** The technician **MUST** remove all legacy or defective door sensor bodies, backplates, and contact magnets from the target door panel and frame to prevent magnetic/RF interference. Place all removed legacy hardware neatly into an empty box, label it clearly as **\"DECOMMISSIONED DOOR SENSOR - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area or manager's office. Do not remove hardware from the property.\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must receive explicit operational and zone telemetry confirmation from remote **Activations** and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & SUPPLIES**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for alarm panel interface diagnostics, communicator checks, or gateway troubleshooting)\n- **New Wired-Contact Sensor & Magnet Assembly** (On-site / shipped hardware)\n- **22/2 Low-Voltage Alarm Wire & B-Connectors / Gel-Filled Beans** (**Mandatory** for extending contact leads to auxiliary terminals)\n- **Small Precision Screwdriver Set & Hand Tools** (**Mandatory** for micro-terminal blocks inside transmitter bodies/panel zones)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter & Wire Strippers / Crimpers** (**Mandatory** for checking loop continuity $\\\\Omega$)\n- **Surface Cleaning Pads / Alcohol Wipes** (For stripping old tape residue off door frames)\n- **Self-Tapping Screws (6 x ¾\" Phillips) & Heavy-Duty Mounting Tape** (For securing sensor and magnet)\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill & Precision Bits**\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** Adhesive wire clips, packaging tape, and permanent marker\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the Back Door sensor location and collect the newly shipped wired-contact replacement unit.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the hardwired scope, confirm target zone number for the Back Door, and verify expected panel loop settings before unmounting hardware.\n\n**PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING & HARDWIRED SENSOR INSTALLATION**1. **DECOMMISSIONING:** Carefully unmount and completely remove the old, failing Back Door sensor, backplate, and magnet.\n2. **SURFACE PREPARATION:** Clean the mounting surfaces thoroughly using alcohol wipes/adhesive remover to strip away grease, dirt, and old tape residue.\n3. **HARDWIRED CONTACT MOUNTING:**\n\n- Securely mount the new wired-contact body to the stationary door frame/header using screws or heavy-duty mounting tape.\n- Securely mount the corresponding magnet to the moving door panel.\n- **Gap Tolerance:** Ensure alignment notches match and the physical air gap between sensor and magnet is **0.5 inches or less** ($\\\\le 0.5\\\\text{ inches}$) when the door is fully closed and latched.\n\n1. **TERMINAL WIRING:**\n\n- Route and land the 2-conductor wire leads from the new contact directly onto the hardwired input terminals (**NC / COM**) of the door transmitter or panel expansion module. Tighten terminal screws firmly.\n\n**PHASE 3: PANEL PAIRING, TELEMETRY TESTING & ACTIVATIONS VERIFICATION**1. **PROGRAMMING & PAIRING AUDIT:** Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Have remote support confirm the Back Door zone is correctly paired/enrolled and configured for the proper hardwired loop input.\n2. **FUNCTIONAL ZONE TRIP & RESTORE TESTS:** Open and close the Back Door multiple times:\n\n- **Door Open:** Confirm Activations receives an instantaneous \"Zone Open / Fault\" telemetry signal on the designated zone.\n- **Door Closed:** Confirm Activations receives an instantaneous \"Zone Closed / Restored\" telemetry signal on the designated zone.\n\n1. **KEYPAD STATUS AUDIT:** Confirm the local alarm keypad reflects real-time door state changes and displays a clear \"Ready to Arm\" status when the door is closed, with zero active trouble codes.\n2. **MOD DEMONSTRATION:** Demonstrate physical open/close operation of the Back Door to the store manager, showing fault-free keypad response.\n\n**PHASE 4: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**1. **DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:** Box up all old removed door sensors and hardware. Write **\"DECOMMISSIONED DOOR SENSOR - STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** clearly on the package in bold permanent marker and stage it in the store's IT room or manager's office. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Clean up wire insulation scraps, tape backing, drill dust, and packaging wrappers. Ensure the entryway and surrounding floor spaces are left completely spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Back Door Wired Contact Installed:** Close-up photo showing the replacement wired contact and magnet cleanly installed and aligned ($\\\\le 0.5\\\\text{ inches}$ gap) on the back door header and panel.\n- \\[ \\] **Hardwired Terminal Block Wiring:** Clear photo showing wire leads landed securely onto the internal terminal blocks/auxiliary inputs of the transmitter/panel.\n- \\[ \\] **Restored Clear Keypad Status:** Photo showing the alarm keypad displaying a fault-free \"Ready to Arm\" status with the back door closed.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Hardware:** Photo showing the old door sensor hardware boxed, labeled **\"STAGED FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and set aside in the IT storage area.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network / Alarm Panel Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire IT network / alarm panel rack cabinet with the door OPEN**.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the floor and frame around the back door work area are swept completely clean of installation debris.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that the new wired door contact is successfully paired/enrolled, real-time open/close telemetry is confirmed, and the panel is clear of all trouble conditions.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Demonstrate proper operation of the hardwired back door sensor to the store manager, confirm keypad \"Ready to Arm\" status, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed sensor replacement, system validation, and site cleanliness.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update internal ticket notes detailing the installation of the wired contact, confirmation of pairing/loop programming, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:30","end":"2026-10-08T09:30","latestStart":"2026-10-08T09:45"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":13.640072037852644},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"displays\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791316328739}
{"job":{"id":20048634,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SHI - Corp Services","title":"Tech to perform site survey | Site: 5535 - Raleigh North, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Summary:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform a physical site survey and document current network, wireless, cabling, rack, power, access, and safety conditions. The survey must provide sufficient detail for deployment planning, remediation decisions, risk tracking, and any potential change request.</li><li>Technician to perform the below tasks in order to complete the site survey.</li><li>Following the site survey, we will reach out to schedule you to run the cable data drops, cable paths and install access points per the marked-up floor plans reviewed during the site survey. We will also schedule at least one assist(you may request an assist, or we can find an assist) and rent a lift.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be requested to bring enough Cat6 cable, cabling materials and white single/double faceplates as identified during this site survey for the remediation visit.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Download</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> and </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">review </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">the attached instructions document BEFORE going onsite.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Site Survey Form</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Confirm Work Order Status</span></li></ol><p><strong><u>Onsite Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong>** Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation **</strong></p><p><strong><u>Once Onsite:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Text the WO manager upon arrival</li><li><strong>Call technical support to check in</strong></li><li>&nbsp;Locate and introduce yourself to the onsite contact</li><li>Walk with the onsite contact to complete the site survey</li><li>&nbsp;Upload picture of (Complete TASK in the below section)</li><li>Complete the site survey form</li><li><strong>Call technical support to check out with </strong></li><li>Text the WO manager before leaving the site</li></ol><p><strong><u>New Build: </u></strong>Walk the site while reviewing the marked up(if provided) floor plans to identify where data drops are, and the cable run paths(ensure there are no obstructions, etc), where APs will be installed, how much cat6 cable you will need provide and white face plates required.</p><ol><li><strong><u>Review the attached marked-up floor plan and update the Site Survey Form</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">APs will be installed and what size lift is required to install them</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Determine if any warehouse cable drops/AP installations are over 300ft from the office MDF closet</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review and validate data drops, and the cable run paths(ensure there are no obstructions, etc)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">MDF closet - determine how many electrical outlets are in this, close the door and review phone signal, provide the amount of service bars</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do we need Cat6 cable run, cabling materials and white face plates(single/double) will be required</li></ol><p><strong><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Measuring Tools: Tape measures, laser distance meters, and measuring wheels are vital for taking accurate measurements of the site.</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Camera/Phone</li></ul><p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Please call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite</span></li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be paid:</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Deliverables on task list must be provided and approved prior to leaving site</span></li></ul><p><strong><u>Stipulations and Penalties:</u></strong></p><p><strong>** Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order OR Runbook - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a 25% deduction of payment **</strong></p><ul><li>Out of Scope Work performed without WO manager consent will not be approved and compensated</li><li>All technicians must have a completed background check on fil<u>e&nbsp;</u></li></ul>","markdown":"**Summary:**\n\n- Perform a physical site survey and document current network, wireless, cabling, rack, power, access, and safety conditions. The survey must provide sufficient detail for deployment planning, remediation decisions, risk tracking, and any potential change request.\n- Technician to perform the below tasks in order to complete the site survey.\n- Following the site survey, we will reach out to schedule you to run the cable data drops, cable paths and install access points per the marked-up floor plans reviewed during the site survey. We will also schedule at least one assist(you may request an assist, or we can find an assist) and rent a lift.\n- You will be requested to bring enough Cat6 cable, cabling materials and white single/double faceplates as identified during this site survey for the remediation visit.\n\n**Pre-Site Instructions:**\n\n1. **Download** and **review** the attached instructions document BEFORE going onsite.\n2. Site Survey Form\n3. Confirm Work Order Status\n\n**Onsite Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\* Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation \\*\\***\n\n**Once Onsite:**\n\n1. Text the WO manager upon arrival\n2. **Call technical support to check in**\n3. Locate and introduce yourself to the onsite contact\n4. Walk with the onsite contact to complete the site survey\n5. Upload picture of (Complete TASK in the below section)\n6. Complete the site survey form\n7. **Call technical support to check out with**\n8. Text the WO manager before leaving the site\n\n**New Build:** Walk the site while reviewing the marked up(if provided) floor plans to identify where data drops are, and the cable run paths(ensure there are no obstructions, etc), where APs will be installed, how much cat6 cable you will need provide and white face plates required.\n\n1. **Review the attached marked-up floor plan and update the Site Survey Form**\n2. APs will be installed and what size lift is required to install them\n3. Determine if any warehouse cable drops/AP installations are over 300ft from the office MDF closet\n4. Review and validate data drops, and the cable run paths(ensure there are no obstructions, etc)\n5. MDF closet - determine how many electrical outlets are in this, close the door and review phone signal, provide the amount of service bars\n6. Do we need Cat6 cable run, cabling materials and white face plates(single/double) will be required\n\n**Required Tools Needed:**\n\n- Measuring Tools: Tape measures, laser distance meters, and measuring wheels are vital for taking accurate measurements of the site.\n- Laptop\n- Camera/Phone\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- Please call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes\n\n**Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n- Deliverables on task list must be provided and approved prior to leaving site\n\n**Stipulations and Penalties:**\n\n**\\*\\* Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order OR Runbook - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a 25% deduction of payment \\*\\***\n\n- Out of Scope Work performed without WO manager consent will not be approved and compensated\n- All technicians must have a completed background check on file","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T08:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount"