{"job":{"id":20116813,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Mashura","title":"Vet Clinic |Smart Inventory Cabinet & Drawer Hardware Troubleshooting Support","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*** This is a high-priority client. No rescheduling will be permitted after assignment. By requesting this work order, you confirm that you are available to arrive and complete the service on the scheduled date.*** </strong></p><p><strong><u>Parts Delivery Verification Requirement</u></strong></p><p><strong>Provider is responsible for verifying that all required parts have been delivered to the service location prior to traveling to the site. Providers must not dispatch or arrive on-site without first confirming delivery using the tracking information provided within the work order.</strong></p><p><strong>If a Provider arrives on-site without verifying that the required parts have been delivered, Mashura reserves the right to cancel the work order without compensation ($0.00). In such cases, return trip charges, travel expenses, or any additional compensation associated with a subsequent visit will not be reimbursed.</strong></p><p><strong><u>If the Provider determines that the required parts will not arrive before the scheduled service window, the Provider must immediately submit a Schedule Change Request through the platform or notify the Work Order Manager so the work order can be rescheduled accordingly. Providers who proactively communicate delays and follow the instructions outlined in the work order will be supported in minimizing any impact to their timeliness metrics.</u></strong></p><p><strong>By accepting this work order, the Provider acknowledges that they have read, understood, and agree to comply with all terms and conditions contained within the work order, including the Parts Delivery Verification Requirement. Failure to comply with these requirements may result in cancellation of the work order without compensation.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in hardware troubleshooting, drawer controller systems, and low-voltage equipment repair.</li><li>Tech is required to repair/replace shipped out parts, including controller boards, drawer boards, ribbon cables, latches, sensors, or drawer slides as needed.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours, depending on troubleshooting findings and parts replacement required.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual or technician attire appropriate for a healthcare/clinical environment</li><li>Closed-toe shoes required</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard technician toolkit</li><li>Phillips screwdriver set</li><li>Nut driver set</li><li>Barrel keys (603 and 44825 key provided onsite)</li><li>Flashlight/headlamp</li><li>Cable cutters for zip ties</li><li>ESD-safe handling equipment recommended</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Review all attached SOP documentation prior to dispatch.</li><li>Review the custom field for parts sent</li><li>Confirm site contact, arrival time, and access requirements before arriving onsite.</li><li>Verify all replacement parts have been received onsite.</li><li>Review cabinet power down and power up procedures before beginning work.</li><li>Contact support if clarification is needed before dispatch.</li></ul><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Check-in to the work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Cubex.</li><li>Take clear photos of the cabinet and work area before beginning work.</li><li>Power down the cabinet correctly before servicing:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Flip the switch on the back top left of the cabinet above the power cord</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Press the button on the bottom right-hand corner of the monitor</li><li>Access the appropriate cabinet section:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Top section for drawers 1&ndash;3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Bottom section for drawers 4&ndash;8</li><li>Replace components as needed, may include any of the following:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drawer Board</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Controller Board</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Rotary Latch/Hard-Stop Latch</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drawer Sensor Cable</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ribbon Cables</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Black Ribbon Cable on Drawer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drawer Slides</li><li>Follow SOP procedures exactly when disconnecting cables, removing screws, and replacing hardware components.</li><li>Use caution when removing drawers to avoid damaging cables, boards, and fragile plastic components.</li><li>After replacing equipment, power the cabinet back on in the correct order:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drawers first</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Monitor second</li><li>Contact Support at 866-907-0860 for testing and validation after repairs are completed.</li><li>Upload detailed completion notes outlining troubleshooting steps performed, parts replaced, and final cabinet status.</li><li>Clean the work area and confirm system functionality with the on-site contact prior to departure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Photos before work begins</li><li>Photos of all replaced components</li><li>Photos of completed repair and powered-on cabinet</li><li>Detailed technician closing notes documenting troubleshooting performed</li><li>Support testing confirmation/code if provided</li><li>On-site contact name and signature (if required)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss with the assigned work order manager or support team.</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Cubex Support team at 866-907-0860.</li><li>Contact Support at 866-907-0860 for post-repair testing and troubleshooting assistance.</li><li>Any damaged equipment, missing parts, or site delays must be reported immediately before leaving the site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours must be pre-approved before continuing work beyond the approved scope.</li><li>Any material purchases or travel-related expenses require prior approval and receipt submission.</li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\* This is a high-priority client. No rescheduling will be permitted after assignment. By requesting this work order, you confirm that you are available to arrive and complete the service on the scheduled date.\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Parts Delivery Verification Requirement**\n\n**Provider is responsible for verifying that all required parts have been delivered to the service location prior to traveling to the site. Providers must not dispatch or arrive on-site without first confirming delivery using the tracking information provided within the work order.**\n\n**If a Provider arrives on-site without verifying that the required parts have been delivered, Mashura reserves the right to cancel the work order without compensation ($0.00). In such cases, return trip charges, travel expenses, or any additional compensation associated with a subsequent visit will not be reimbursed.**\n\n**If the Provider determines that the required parts will not arrive before the scheduled service window, the Provider must immediately submit a Schedule Change Request through the platform or notify the Work Order Manager so the work order can be rescheduled accordingly. Providers who proactively communicate delays and follow the instructions outlined in the work order will be supported in minimizing any impact to their timeliness metrics.**\n\n**By accepting this work order, the Provider acknowledges that they have read, understood, and agree to comply with all terms and conditions contained within the work order, including the Parts Delivery Verification Requirement. Failure to comply with these requirements may result in cancellation of the work order without compensation.**\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in hardware troubleshooting, drawer controller systems, and low-voltage equipment repair.\n- Tech is required to repair/replace shipped out parts, including controller boards, drawer boards, ribbon cables, latches, sensors, or drawer slides as needed.\n- Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours, depending on troubleshooting findings and parts replacement required.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual or technician attire appropriate for a healthcare/clinical environment\n- Closed-toe shoes required\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Standard technician toolkit\n- Phillips screwdriver set\n- Nut driver set\n- Barrel keys (603 and 44825 key provided onsite)\n- Flashlight/headlamp\n- Cable cutters for zip ties\n- ESD-safe handling equipment recommended\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Review all attached SOP documentation prior to dispatch.\n- Review the custom field for parts sent\n- Confirm site contact, arrival time, and access requirements before arriving onsite.\n- Verify all replacement parts have been received onsite.\n- Review cabinet power down and power up procedures before beginning work.\n- Contact support if clarification is needed before dispatch.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n- Check-in to the work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Cubex.\n- Take clear photos of the cabinet and work area before beginning work.\n- Power down the cabinet correctly before servicing:\n- Flip the switch on the back top left of the cabinet above the power cord\n- Press the button on the bottom right-hand corner of the monitor\n- Access the appropriate cabinet section:\n- Top section for drawers 1–3\n- Bottom section for drawers 4–8\n- Replace components as needed, may include any of the following:\n- Drawer Board\n- Controller Board\n- Rotary Latch/Hard-Stop Latch\n- Drawer Sensor Cable\n- Ribbon Cables\n- Black Ribbon Cable on Drawer\n- Drawer Slides\n- Follow SOP procedures exactly when disconnecting cables, removing screws, and replacing hardware components.\n- Use caution when removing drawers to avoid damaging cables, boards, and fragile plastic components.\n- After replacing equipment, power the cabinet back on in the correct order:\n- Drawers first\n- Monitor second\n- Contact Support at 866-907-0860 for testing and validation after repairs are completed.\n- Upload detailed completion notes outlining troubleshooting steps performed, parts replaced, and final cabinet status.\n- Clean the work area and confirm system functionality with the on-site contact prior to departure.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n- Photos before work begins\n- Photos of all replaced components\n- Photos of completed repair and powered-on cabinet\n- Detailed technician closing notes documenting troubleshooting performed\n- Support testing confirmation/code if provided\n- On-site contact name and signature (if required)\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss with the assigned work order manager or support team.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Cubex Support team at 866-907-0860.\n- Contact Support at 866-907-0860 for post-repair testing and troubleshooting assistance.\n- Any damaged equipment, missing parts, or site delays must be reported immediately before leaving the site.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours must be pre-approved before continuing work beyond the approved scope.\n- Any material purchases or travel-related expenses require prior approval and receipt submission.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T08:00","end":"2026-10-08T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.956550014971288},"r