{"job":{"id":20118728,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Safely-You","title":"WiFi Camera Installation (qty: 1) - Smartphone & Teams Required","description":{"html":"<p>Installation Overview:</p><p><strong><u>This will be for the installation of QTY: 1 WiFi sensors - Tech is to provide raceway (Additional cost added for raceway)</u></strong></p><p>Work location is a senior living facility—you may be entering the private residences of and interacting with seniors with memory impairment. You will be acting as a representative of SafelyYou on site—any negative feedback about your behavior on site will invalidate you for future work orders.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong></p><p>Ability to communicate, dress, and behave in a professional, kind, and respectful manner is<strong>MANDATORY.</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>While the Guardian Pro sensor is a camera in some sense,<strong><em><u>please only refer to the Guardian Pro as a Fall Detection sensor</u></em></strong><em><u>,</u></em><strong><em><u>Guardian Pro, or sensor when working in the community.</u></em></strong></li><li>Call SafelyYou field manager <strong>before entering the facility</strong>. You will coordinate with the field manager via Microsoft Teams on your phone where they will guide you with any questions you may have during the installation.</li><li>Cleaning each area worked in is mandatory.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Once assigned to this ticket, you will be added to this site's Teams chat where all future communication regarding the install will take place.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Smart phone</li><li>Cordless drill (Impact not recommended)</li><li>4-6’ Step Ladder</li><li>8-10’ A Frame Ladder</li><li>Heat gun</li><li>Receptacle Outlet Tester</li><li>Drywall Screws</li><li>Drywall anchors</li><li>Vacuum/cleaning wipes/Broom</li><li>Microfiber Cloth</li><li>Basic HandTools- Mini &amp; Reg. Phillips &amp; Flathead Drivers-Needle Nose Pliers-Flush Cuts</li></ul><p><strong>SOW:</strong></p><ul><li>Coordinate with your field manager on teams prior to install to receive site address and contact information.</li><li>On the day of install, meet with your PoC at the community to gain entry and locate your inventory</li><li>Mounting raceway, installing outlet cover, running a power cord through raceway, mounting sensor.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be provided an in-depth guide of the installation process in the Teams chat you will be added to</li><li>Clean up all working areas.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Before and After photos of work area/installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Race way is installed as instructed (Close up and wide view)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sensor location (close up and wide view)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work area cleaned and furniture moved back to original placement</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Outlet cover is neat and level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Door tag placement (Close up and far away including entire door frame+tag)</li><li>Final Walkthrough document signed by MD or ED (Upload document to WO)</li></ul>","markdown":"Installation Overview:\n\n**This will be for the installation of QTY: 1 WiFi sensors - Tech is to provide raceway (Additional cost added for raceway)**\n\nWork location is a senior living facility—you may be entering the private residences of and interacting with seniors with memory impairment. You will be acting as a representative of SafelyYou on site—any negative feedback about your behavior on site will invalidate you for future work orders.\n\n**IMPORTANT:**\n\nAbility to communicate, dress, and behave in a professional, kind, and respectful manner is**MANDATORY.**\n\n- While the Guardian Pro sensor is a camera in some sense,***please only refer to the Guardian Pro as a Fall Detection sensor****,****Guardian Pro, or sensor when working in the community.***\n- Call SafelyYou field manager **before entering the facility**. You will coordinate with the field manager via Microsoft Teams on your phone where they will guide you with any questions you may have during the installation.\n- Cleaning each area worked in is mandatory.\n\n**Once assigned to this ticket, you will be added to this site's Teams chat where all future communication regarding the install will take place.**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Smart phone\n- Cordless drill (Impact not recommended)\n- 4-6’ Step Ladder\n- 8-10’ A Frame Ladder\n- Heat gun\n- Receptacle Outlet Tester\n- Drywall Screws\n- Drywall anchors\n- Vacuum/cleaning wipes/Broom\n- Microfiber Cloth\n- Basic HandTools- Mini & Reg. Phillips & Flathead Drivers-Needle Nose Pliers-Flush Cuts\n\n**SOW:**\n\n- Coordinate with your field manager on teams prior to install to receive site address and contact information.\n- On the day of install, meet with your PoC at the community to gain entry and locate your inventory\n- Mounting raceway, installing outlet cover, running a power cord through raceway, mounting sensor.\n- You will be provided an in-depth guide of the installation process in the Teams chat you will be added to\n- Clean up all working areas.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Before and After photos of work area/installation\n- Race way is installed as instructed (Close up and wide view)\n- Sensor location (close up and wide view)\n- Work area cleaned and furniture moved back to original placement\n- Outlet cover is neat and level\n- Door tag placement (Close up and far away including entire door frame+tag)\n- Final Walkthrough document signed by MD or ED (Upload document to WO)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:00","end":"2026-10-12T10:30","latestStart":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":13.568801359068662},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectD