{"job":{"id":20118932,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Install 2 POS systems at an Auntie Anne's - WhatsApp Necessary","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Service Description</u></strong></p><p>Install 2 POS Terminals at an Auntie Anne’s for Zones.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>On Time Arrival Mandatory</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Scope of&nbsp;Work</u></strong></p><p>Zones is refreshing POS systems at Auntie Anne’s. All equipment should already be shipped to the site for assembly.&nbsp;Attached to the work order is a runbook detailing how to assemble and test the New POS Terminals. A technician will be required to complete the following:</p><p>Installation of 1 or more Terminals, KDS, Kiosk, along with their accessory components.Installing unmanaged hub\\switches.Installing power strips. Installing KDS\\Display arms ONLY if the holes are pre-drilled. (Terminating ends of cables, short runs of ethernet cabling, assisting with Firewall installation, assisting with mounting something in a rack).&nbsp;Customer to provide ladder if needed.</p><ol><li>Upon arrival - Check In with your Zones work order manager. Introduce yourself to the MOD. Ask them to print a receipt to validate store location.</li><li>Log in<strong> to </strong><del>*****************</del> (Credentials should be found in the messages section of your work order. If you cannot locate it ask your Zones work order manager.)</li><li>Verify the Inventory is onsite, begin unboxing, and take photos.</li><li>Begin installing the New Terminals, starting with Terminal 1.</li><li>Take care to note the placements of all Terminal equipment in the Runbook. Cable management is a priority and will be completed after testing.</li><li>Have the MOD test Terminal 1. If troubleshooting is needed make sure you are communicating with your Zones Work Order Manager.</li><li>Repeat steps 3-5 with each POS Terminal.</li><li>With testing complete on all terminals.</li><li>Cable manage the cables under the POS Terminals . Cable Management is a Priority!</li><li>Bag up the trash and break down the boxes.</li><li>Take photos upon completion. Upload the photos to the nterprise work order. (Instructions on completion form).</li><li>Collect a digital sign off on the nterprise portal.</li><li>Upon completion - Check Out with your Zones work order manager. Do not leave the site until after the Zones work order manager has had a chance to review all deliverables.</li></ol><p>Once FN ticket is accepted, tech will receive instructions on usage of Zones's nterprise portal. nterprise portal is where photos and completion form.</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">If site conditions prevent installation, please contact Zones Work order Manager ASAP.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Installations are to be performed during business hours.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">All technical questions and questions about the work order must go through the Zones Work Order Manager.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Parts instructions</u>:</strong></p><ol><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Tech is responsible for cleaning up the work area, breaking down boxes, and bagging the trash.</span></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Duration Onsite</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> Experienced technicians should be done in no more than 4 hrs.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Install Date and Time</u>:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is Mandatory. Do not request this work order if you cannot meet this schedule requirement.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Required&nbsp;Deliverables&nbsp;to be paid:</strong></p><ol><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Sign Off</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Arrival Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Pre-Start Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Inventory Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Testing Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Complete POS Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Old Removed Equipment Photos as detailed in the Runbook</span></li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Work&nbsp;Order&nbsp;Acceptance:</u></strong></p><ol><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Do not request the&nbsp;Work&nbsp;order&nbsp;if you do not have the required tools or are unable to meet the scheduled date and time.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Tech must verify that the equipment is not damaged on arrival. If damaged, the Tech must contact their work order manager before proceeding with the install.</span></li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Business Casual</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(85, 85, 85);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Standard Tool Kit</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Small Screw Driver Set</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Snips</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">5' Patch cables(10)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">About 12' x 3/4 or 1/2 Velcro to wrap cables </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">About 12 pairs of 1-2\" long Double-sided lock tight Velcro to attach power bricks, QU Box and coiled cables to sides of cabinets</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Camera or Smart Phone</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">2 Large Trash Bags</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black;\">We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH NEW ASSIGNMENTS.</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**Service Description**\n\nInstall 2 POS Terminals at an Auntie Anne’s for Zones.\n\n**On Time Arrival Mandatory**\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nZones is refreshing POS systems at Auntie Anne’s. All equipment should already be shipped to the site for assembly. Attached to the work order is a runbook detailing how to assemble and test the New POS Terminals. A technician will be required to complete the following:\n\nInstallation of 1 or more Terminals, KDS, Kiosk, along with their accessory components.Installing unmanaged hub\\\\switches.Installing power strips. Installing KDS\\\\Display arms ONLY if the holes are pre-drilled. (Terminating ends of cables, short runs of ethernet cabling, assisting with Firewall installation, assisting with mounting something in a rack). Customer to provide ladder if needed.\n\n1. Upon arrival - Check In with your Zones work order manager. Introduce yourself to the MOD. Ask them to print a receipt to validate store location.\n2. Log in **to** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (Credentials should be found in the messages section of your work order. If you cannot locate it ask your Zones work order manager.)\n3. Verify the Inventory is onsite, begin unboxing, and take photos.\n4. Begin installing the New Terminals, starting with Terminal 1.\n5. Take care to note the placements of all Terminal equipment in the Runbook. Cable management is a priority and will be completed after testing.\n6. Have the MOD test Terminal 1. If troubleshooting is needed make sure you are communicating with your Zones Work Order Manager.\n7. Repeat steps 3-5 with each POS Terminal.\n8. With testing complete on all terminals.\n9. Cable manage the cables under the POS Terminals . Cable Management is a Priority!\n10. Bag up the trash and break down the boxes.\n11. Take photos upon completion. Upload the photos to the nterprise work order. (Instructions on completion form).\n12. Collect a digital sign off on the nterprise portal.\n13. Upon completion - Check Out with your Zones work order manager. Do not leave the site until after the Zones work order manager has had a chance to review all deliverables.\n\nOnce FN ticket is accepted, tech will receive instructions on usage of Zones's nterprise portal. nterprise portal is where photos and completion form.\n\nIf site conditions prevent installation, please contact Zones Work order Manager ASAP.\n\nInstallations are to be performed during business hours.\n\nAll technical questions and questions about the work order must go through the Zones Work Order Manager.\n\n**Parts instructions:**\n\n1. Tech is responsible for cleaning up the work area, breaking down boxes, and bagging the trash.\n\n**Duration Onsite:**  Experienced technicians should be done in no more than 4 hrs.\n\n**Install Date and Time:** is Mandatory. Do not request this work order if you cannot meet this schedule requirement.\n\n**Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n1. Sign Off\n2. Arrival Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n3. Pre-Start Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n4. Inventory Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n5. Testing Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n6. Complete POS Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n7. Old Removed Equipment Photos as detailed in the Runbook\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1. Do not request the Work order if you do not have the required tools or are unable to meet the scheduled date and time.\n2. Tech must verify that the equipment is not damaged on arrival. If damaged, the Tech must contact their work order manager before proceeding with the install.\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Small Screw Driver Set\n- Snips\n- 5' Patch cables(10)\n- About 12' x 3/4 or 1/2 Velcro to wrap cables\n- About 12 pairs of 1-2\" long Double-sided lock tight Velcro to attach power bricks, QU Box and coiled cables to sides of cabinets\n- Camera or Smart Phone\n- 2 Large Trash Bags\n\nWe appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.\n\n- THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH NEW ASSIGNMENTS.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":480,"max":480},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":4.558136427491954},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791320540398}
