{"job":{"id":20118877,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pilot Services","title":"XDR DEVICE MIRROR CONNECTION","description":{"html":"CALL INTO DISPATCH UPON ARRIVAL/DEPARTURE AT 888-745-6898 OPT 2. <br/><br/>Reference number: <br/><br/>Please arrive 5-10 mins early. If checking in before 7am or checking out after 6pm CT please dial \"0\" to be transferred to the on-call person.<br/><br/>DATE: 10/16 @ 12pm ET<br/><br/>1. SCOPE: PHASE 2 XDR INSTALLATION -- LAN PORT (13) MIRROR PORT (12) <br/><br/>Return to each site and connect the gray cable left disconnected during Phase 1. The gray cable is already connected to the XDR device’s Mirror port; the technician will connect its loose end to the designated switch port (indicated on the attached spreadsheet under Mirror Port.<br/><br/>Standard site visit<br/>1. Contact site prior to visit to notify site manager.<br/>2. Tech to check in with site manager<br/>3. Locate the XDR device and identify the switch used for its existing LAN connection. Marc said the mirror connection should use that same switch, including at sites where it is in an IDF rather than the MDF.<br/>4. Check Marc’s site spreadsheet for the designated Mirror Port number.<br/>5. Connect the loose end of the gray cable to that port.<br/>6. Contact Marc at or Ryland so he can verify the connection before the technician leaves.<br/><br/><br/>LCON CONTACT:<br/>Name:SITE MANAGER <br/>Number:919/929-2160<br/><br/><br/>2. DELIVERABLES:  Photos are needed before/after completed work upload photos on the platform<br/><br/>- Photos of before/after completed work<br/>- Description of the work that was completed including name of ENG and LCON<br/>- Materials used<br/>- Signed work order<br/><br/>3. REQUIRED STANDARD TOOLS: Butt set, toner, basic hand tools, crimpers, laptop, 300ft CAT6, 8ft ladder, jacks, loopback cable and Cisco console cable<br/><br/><br/>Tech must get pre-approval PRIOR TO DOING ANY WORK OUTSIDE OF ABOVE LISTED SCOPE.<br/><br/>By accepting this ticket, it is the expectation of Pilot GT, the work will be completed by the resources accepting the ticket, not a party working on their behalf.<br/><br/><br/><br/><br/>PILOT Global Technologies <br/>1891 Bay Scott Cir, STE 109<br/>Naperville, IL 60540<br/>PHONE: 888-745-6898<br/><br/>EMAIL: <br/>SERVICE@pilotgt.com<br/>BILLING@PILOTGT.COM - All invoices must include the service address, service date(s), and our work order (PO) number. For toll reimbursement, please provide a receipt or screenshot that clearly shows the toll charge along with the date and time of the transaction.","markdown":"CALL INTO DISPATCH UPON ARRIVAL/DEPARTURE AT 888-745-6898 OPT 2.   \n  \nReference number:   \n  \nPlease arrive 5-10 mins early. If checking in before 7am or checking out after 6pm CT please dial \"0\" to be transferred to the on-call person.  \n  \nDATE: 10/16 @ 12pm ET  \n  \n1\\. SCOPE: PHASE 2 XDR INSTALLATION -- LAN PORT (13) MIRROR PORT (12)   \n  \nReturn to each site and connect the gray cable left disconnected during Phase 1. The gray cable is already connected to the XDR device’s Mirror port; the technician will connect its loose end to the designated switch port (indicated on the attached spreadsheet under Mirror Port.  \n  \nStandard site visit  \n1\\. Contact site prior to visit to notify site manager.  \n2\\. Tech to check in with site manager  \n3\\. Locate the XDR device and identify the switch used for its existing LAN connection. Marc said the mirror connection should use that same switch, including at sites where it is in an IDF rather than the MDF.  \n4\\. Check Marc’s site spreadsheet for the designated Mirror Port number.  \n5\\. Connect the loose end of the gray cable to that port.  \n6\\. Contact Marc at or Ryland so he can verify the connection before the technician leaves.  \n  \n  \nLCON CONTACT:  \nName:SITE MANAGER   \nNumber:919/929-2160  \n  \n  \n2\\. DELIVERABLES: Photos are needed before/after completed work upload photos on the platform  \n  \n\\- Photos of before/after completed work  \n\\- Description of the work that was completed including name of ENG and LCON  \n\\- Materials used  \n\\- Signed work order  \n  \n3\\. REQUIRED STANDARD TOOLS: Butt set, toner, basic hand tools, crimpers, laptop, 300ft CAT6, 8ft ladder, jacks, loopback cable and Cisco console cable  \n  \n  \nTech must get pre-approval PRIOR TO DOING ANY WORK OUTSIDE OF ABOVE LISTED SCOPE.  \n  \nBy accepting this ticket, it is the expectation of Pilot GT, the work will be completed by the resources accepting the ticket, not a party working on their behalf.  \n  \n  \n  \n  \nPILOT Global Technologies   \n1891 Bay Scott Cir, STE 109  \nNaperville, IL 60540  \nPHONE: 888-745-6898  \n  \nEMAIL:   \nSERVICE@pilotgt.com  \nBILLING@PILOTGT.COM - All invoices must include the service address, service date(s), and our work order (PO) number. For toll reimbursement, please provide a receipt or screenshot that clearly shows the toll charge along with the date and time of the transaction.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":45},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":17.61835082776199},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $45 (countered: $60) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z"