{"job":{"id":"2506954180","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"9AM Hard Start: H and M Cutover_US0590","description":"<p>**REQUIRED TOOLS**</p><p>Laptop (10/100 network card or better) with Ethernet port (or adapter)</p><p>Console Cable</p><p>Velcro Straps</p><p>Phillips, Slotted and Torx bits</p><p>Label maker</p><p>Charger</p><p>Assorted patch cables</p><p>Printed files on Workmarket Ticket</p><p><br></p><p>General Summary: We remove the intermediary Granite CPE from between the Grid Jack in the customer’s suite and H&amp;M Equipment to be provided DIA directly from the Grid Jack.</p><p><br></p><p>Overview:</p><p>STEP 1: Locate GRID jack located in customer’s suite. Refer to Circuit Info - Call Granite Activations @ 877-855-1146</p><p>STEP 2: Work with H&amp;M IT Support on the bridge with Granite Activations - Refer to attached Diagram</p><p>STEP 3: Change Configuration</p><p>STEP 4: Check edgeboot Status (if installed)</p><p>STEP 5: Confirm Functionality with Local Contact </p><p>STEP 6: Gather Deliverables</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 1: Arrival &amp; Site Verification - Call Granite Activations @ 877-855-1146</p><p>-Introduce yourself to the local contact at H&amp;M prior to beginning work.</p><p>-Document the current condition of the network equipment rack or equipment backboard by taking pictures before beginning any work on the site.</p><p>-Call Granite Activations @ 877-855-1146 | OPT 1: Cable/DSL | OPT 2: DIA | OPT 3: GRID</p><p>-Get Granite Rep’s name and provide Granite Ticket #.</p><p>-Have Granite Rep join the bridge. Tech should join the bridge as well. H&amp;M Support will be on the bridge.</p><p>-IMPORTANT: Plug the laptop into the Netgear to connect to the internet.</p><p>-Make connections into their Aruba router &amp; connect EBPro ethernet into customer switch.</p><p>IMPORTANT: Tech MUST join the bridge using the LINK through the laptop rather than dialing in.</p><p><br></p><p>LINK: PENDING</p><p>Bridge #: +1 929-229-2436 | Passcode #: PENDING</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 2: Work with Granite Rep and H&amp;M IT Support - Diagram attached to ticket</p><p>-All changes will be made during the coordinated hotcut.</p><p>-Public IPs will be provided on the bridge.</p><p>-Configure the provided public IP in your laptop and plug directly into the GRID jack to test.</p><p>-Make sure that the speed test is 80 to 90% of the contacted bandwidth speed specified on the ticket. </p><p>-Record the speed test in the bridge chat and provide screenshots/pictures.</p><p>-Once the speed test is successful, proceed to cut over the circuit to the customer premise equipment.</p><p>-Refer to the attached Diagram.</p><p><br></p><p>Edgeboot SN: 2026261956 (Already Installed) - Confirm with Activations Rep device status is still good.</p><p><br></p><p>***CIRCUIT INFO***</p><p>Carrier/Bandwidth: Granite 30MBPS/30MBPS</p><p>Circuit MAC/NSO ID: 79503</p><p>Circuit Demarc/IDF: IDF5</p><p>GRID Switch: 5</p><p>GRID Port: 17</p><p>DHCP: 143.170.6.202 - 206</p><p>Gateway: 143.170.6.201</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 3: Change Configuration</p><p>-Default the IDF port the service is built to.</p><p>-Run Grid Service Activation workflow on the existing IDF/port </p><p>-This workflow takes 2-5 minutes. Workflow allocates Public IPs.</p><p>-Tech disconnects the Granite CPE that is currently connected to the Grid Jack.</p><p>-Take cable from Customer LAN Port on Granite CPE that was just connected and plug into Grid Jack.</p><p>-The above work can be performed simultaneously as a Granite Representative is working on the config changes to minimize downtime.</p><p>-Will need to re-configure their interface that is connecting to the Grid Jack with the new Public IP range allocated from the Grid Service Activation work flow.</p><p>-Confirm the correct interface on their port is up and confirm they have internet access.</p><p>-This entire process will probably take 5-10 minutes depending on how fast the IW tech can remove the Granite CPE and plug H&amp;M’s Equipment into the Grid Jack.</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 4: Check edgeboot Status (if installed)</p><p>-Check with Granite Rep if edgeboot still shows active and has good status. Provide edgeboot SN.</p><p>-Confirm edgeboot is NOT plugged into the UPS and is instead plugged into the PDU. PDU should be plugged into the wall, NOT UPS. Take pictures.</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 5: Confirm Functionality with Local Contact</p><p>-After successful cutover of the circuit to the customer premise equipment, we are ready to have the end users test the internet connection.</p><p>-Test the new internet circuit by doing multiple speed tests and recording the speed test results after cutting over. Screenshots/pictures must be provided as part of the closeout pictures and can be posted on the call bridge also.</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 6: Gather Deliverables</p><p>Required Deliverables:</p><p>-Picture of cabinet/backboard (close up and wide)</p><p>-Pictures of speed tests (directly from GRID jack) </p><p>-Pictures of edgeboot and showing where it’s plugged in.</p><p>-Confirm that the H&amp;M local contact has completed testing all applications successfully prior to departure</p><p>-MUST get a signature prior to leaving the site that all items are tested and completed</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T09:00","end":"2026-10-14T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","