{"job":{"id":20119940,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Splice Communications","title":"Check Devices and Building Connections for VOIP Phones","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Mandatory Scope Discussion</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have <strong>not previously completed work for this specific project phase</strong> must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.</p>\n<p>If contacted, please plan to attend. <strong>Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technician needed to work with remote support on the following:</p>\n<p>VOIP phones are not working, need technician to check their setup. customer needs the device and the connections to be checked on the building</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS / IMPORTANT NOTES -</u></strong></p>\n<p>1 - After checking in with Splice, please call into<del>******</del> Remote support:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Support Phone -</strong><strong data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><del>************</del></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Support Contact -</strong><del>***** ****** *****</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Case Number -</strong><del>********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>2 - Required Tools - Laptop, Paper Clip, PoE tester, Butt set or working Analog Phone, RJ11, RJ45, Step Ladder</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Duration:2 hours</p>\n<p>&nbsp;Experience:</p>\n<p>Technician will need to be proficient with VOIP (Voice over IP) hardware installation and mounting procedures.&nbsp;Will need to understand cut sheets and number porting pertaining to phone swaps.&nbsp;Will also need to have cabling experience, able to crimp, test, tone, and punch down cables as needed.&nbsp;Should have basic network knowledge and be able to configure static IP and other TCP/IP settings on laptop, as well as configure cable connections.&nbsp;Will need to communicate and work well with bridge lines and remote technical contacts via patch and console cable connections over Microsoft Teams, Teamviewer, Putty, etc.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity</li>\n<li>Microsoft Teams</li>\n<li>Teamviewer</li>\n<li>Putty</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cable</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)</li>\n<li>Smartphone</li>\n<li>Hot spot</li>\n<li>Socket setHex/Allen key set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested.&nbsp;Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task.&nbsp;All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site.&nbsp;There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:</u></strong></p>\n<p>CAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS/DELIVERABLES:</u></strong></p>\n<p>PLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL.&nbsp;CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DRESS CODE:</strong></p>\n<p>Business casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.).&nbsp;This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**Mandatory Scope Discussion**\n\nTechnicians who have **not previously completed work for this specific project phase** must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.\n\nIf contacted, please plan to attend. **Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:**\n\nTechnician needed to work with remote support on the following:\n\nVOIP phones are not working, need technician to check their setup. customer needs the device and the connections to be checked on the building\n\n**TASKS / IMPORTANT NOTES -**\n\n1 - After checking in with Splice, please call into\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Remote support:\n\n- **Support Phone -****\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- **Support Contact -**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Case Number -**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n2 - Required Tools - Laptop, Paper Clip, PoE tester, Butt set or working Analog Phone, RJ11, RJ45, Step Ladder\n\n**JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:**\n\nDuration:2 hours\n\n Experience:\n\nTechnician will need to be proficient with VOIP (Voice over IP) hardware installation and mounting procedures. Will need to understand cut sheets and number porting pertaining to phone swaps. Will also need to have cabling experience, able to crimp, test, tone, and punch down cables as needed. Should have basic network knowledge and be able to configure static IP and other TCP/IP settings on laptop, as well as configure cable connections. Will need to communicate and work well with bridge lines and remote technical contacts via patch and console cable connections over Microsoft Teams, Teamviewer, Putty, etc.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity\n- Microsoft Teams\n- Teamviewer\n- Putty\n- Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- Label maker\n- Patch Cables\n- Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)\n- Smartphone\n- Hot spot\n- Socket setHex/Allen key set\n\n**As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.**\n\n**IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:**\n\nCAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.\n\n**TASKS/DELIVERABLES:**\n\nPLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL. CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.\n\n**DRESS CODE:**\n\nBusiness casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.). This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10-08T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.083037644271025},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.0