{"job":{"id":20120173,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Guest-Tek","title":"Troubleshoot  wireless access point Ruckus [H550] [ 192.168.225.180] in [room 422] is not working","description":{"html":"<p>###########################################</p><p>&nbsp;### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###</p><p>############################################</p><p><br></p><p>===== IMPORTANT – PLEASE READ CAREFULLY =====</p><p><br></p><p>Technicians/TPC are required to review the “Vendor Etiquette” guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.</p><p><br></p><p>By proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.</p><p><br></p><p>Any non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.</p><p><br></p><p>Once on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)</p><p><br></p><p>It is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.</p><p><br></p><p>STEP #1 - Contact GNOC upon arrival onsite at 1-866-509-1010 EXT. 4504 (HSIA) and refer to the ticket number# <span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">P# 1798948 / C# 1799105</span></p><p><br></p><p>STEP #2 - If there is no response or a delay of more than 15 minutes, send a CHECK-IN email and request a callback to:</p><p>Escalation.Managers@guest-tek.com&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>techdispatch@guest-tek.com&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Include reference: P# <span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">1798948 </span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Important Requirements Before Leaving Site: A work order signature sheet with a physical (paper) signature from the property is mandatory before departure along with their name and designation.</p><p><br></p><p>NO DIGITAL SIGNATURES ARE ALLOWED — ONLY PAPER SIGNATURES WILL BE ACCEPTED.</p><p><br></p><p>All issues must be fully resolved before leaving the site.</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>Property Information</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(15, 97, 161);\">Sheraton Chapel Hill</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Problem Summary/Description</strong></p><p>Wireless access point Ruckus <strong>[H550] [</strong> 192.168.225.180<strong>]&nbsp;[room 422</strong>] is not working</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Troubleshooting Performed</strong></p><p>Added this new spare AP to the network and WLC it's not coming up</p><p>Hard reboot has been done</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope Of Works</strong></p><p>Contact and check in with GNOC Agent</p><p>Verify power to unit</p><p>Check the cable connection between Server and [core] in [location]</p><p>Swap power cords if necessary</p><p>Restart the unit and check the lights on the equipment&nbsp;</p><p>Test with known working power injector</p><p>Test another POE port on switch</p><p>Test with known working equipment</p><p>Replace (RJ45) cable ends if necessary</p><p>Check for any line issues in the cable run</p><p>To label cables if not labelled</p><p>Notify GNOC of any cable run issues found</p><p>If the equipment is beyond repairs work with NOC and try to place a temporary solution</p><p>Work with the GNOC Agent to identify all our equipment in the MDF and IDFs and properly identify downlinks to ensure all is connected as outlined in the workbook</p><p>Confirm with GNOC agent proper configuration in the equipment affected and any other switch indicated by GNOC</p><p>Work with the GNOC Agent on further steps to bring the offline AP or SWITCH(ES) back online</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Skill Set</strong></p><p>Working with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.</p><p>Re-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary</p><p>Experience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Tool Set</strong></p><p>Cat5 Crimper</p><p>Spare RJ45 plugs</p><p>Cat 5 Line tester</p><p>Laptop with fully charged battery for testing</p><p>Digital Camera to send photos of the site to GNOC if requested (Camera phones acceptable if with flash, minimum 3 megapixel)</p><p>Console cable for Ethernet Switch and/or Console cable compatible with Switch on-site (Provide Switch brand and model) with necessary adapters (if required)</p><p>Label machine</p>","markdown":"\\###########################################\n\n ### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###\n\n\\############################################\n\n===== IMPORTANT – PLEASE READ CAREFULLY =====\n\nTechnicians/TPC are required to review the “Vendor Etiquette” guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.\n\nBy proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.\n\nAny non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.\n\nOnce on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)\n\nIt is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.\n\nSTEP #1 - Contact GNOC upon arrival onsite at 1-866-509-1010 EXT. 4504 (HSIA) and refer to the ticket number# P# 1798948 / C# 1799105\n\nSTEP #2 - If there is no response or a delay of more than 15 minutes, send a CHECK-IN email and request a callback to:\n\nEscalation.Managers@guest-tek.com\n\ntechdispatch@guest-tek.com\n\nInclude reference: P# 1798948\n\nImportant Requirements Before Leaving Site: A work order signature sheet with a physical (paper) signature from the property is mandatory before departure along with their name and designation.\n\nNO DIGITAL SIGNATURES ARE ALLOWED — ONLY PAPER SIGNATURES WILL BE ACCEPTED.\n\nAll issues must be fully resolved before leaving the site.\n\n========================\n\n**Property Information**\n\nSheraton Chapel Hill\n\n**Problem Summary/Description**\n\nWireless access point Ruckus **\\[H550\\] \\[** 192.168.225.180**\\] \\[room 422**\\] is not working\n\n**Troubleshooting Performed**\n\nAdded this new spare AP to the network and WLC it's not coming up\n\nHard reboot has been done\n\n**Scope Of Works**\n\nContact and check in with GNOC Agent\n\nVerify power to unit\n\nCheck the cable connection between Server and \\[core\\] in \\[location\\]\n\nSwap power cords if necessary\n\nRestart the unit and check the lights on the equipment\n\nTest with known working power injector\n\nTest another POE port on switch\n\nTest with known working equipment\n\nReplace (RJ45) cable ends if necessary\n\nCheck for any line issues in the cable run\n\nTo label cables if not labelled\n\nNotify GNOC of any cable run issues found\n\nIf the equipment is beyond repairs work with NOC and try to place a temporary solution\n\nWork with the GNOC Agent to identify all our equipment in the MDF and IDFs and properly identify downlinks to ensure all is connected as outlined in the workbook\n\nConfirm with GNOC agent proper configuration in the equipment affected and any other switch indicated by GNOC\n\nWork with the GNOC Agent on further steps to bring the offline AP or SWITCH(ES) back online\n\n**Technician Skill Set**\n\nWorking with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.\n\nRe-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary\n\nExperience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation)\n\n**Technician Tool Set**\n\nCat5 Crimper\n\nSpare RJ45 plugs\n\nCat 5 Line tester\n\nLaptop with fully charged battery for testing\n\nDigital Camera to send photos of the site to GNOC if requested (Camera phones acceptable if with flash, minimum 3 megapixel)\n\nConsole cable for Ethernet Switch and/or Console cable compatible with Switch on-site (Provide Switch brand and model) with necessary adapters (if required)\n\nLabel machine","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T11:00","end":"2026-10-07T15:00"},"payRange":{