{"job":{"id":20121056,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Break Fix PPT1018925 Pfizer Inc","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Service Overview:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> [Description of service details]</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Case Action Summary</strong></p><p><strong>Summary:</strong></p><p><strong>Action plan:</strong></p><p>***** ACTION PLAN *****</p><p>Multiple PCI cassette issues</p><p>*** Parts Required:&nbsp;</p><p>Quantity: 4</p><p>Part Number: 7089613</p><p>Specs:&nbsp;x16 PCI Express Carrier</p><p>Location:&nbsp;slots 4 and 7&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>*** Special Instructions:&nbsp;</p><p>Inspect replacement part for damage prior to using.</p><p>*** Current Issue:&nbsp;</p><p>Affects : /SYS/RCSA/PCIE4/CAR /SYS/RCSA/PCIE7/CAR</p><p>*** Evidence of Issue:&nbsp;</p><p>Affects : /SYS/RCSA/PCIE4/CAR /SYS/RCSA/PCIE7/CAR</p><p>*** Resolution Steps:</p><p>1. Inspect Replacement part for damage.</p><p>2.Note - Removing PCIe card carriers while the server is at the OpenBoot prompt is not supported. The server must be either powered off, or booted into the Oracle Solaris OS.</p><p>3. Replace the PCIE carrier 4 7 while system powered off.&nbsp;</p><p>*** Supporting Documents:&nbsp;</p><p>*** Backline AEG for escalations:Sun / Oracle team</p><p>Call in for Backline support with any questions. Have your Astea ticket number and call the FE Hotline at 800-497-3738 option 2, or engage your local Park Place Technologies Support Center using the appropriate toll-free phone number listed here:&nbsp;https://www.parkplacetechnologies.com/contact-us/</p><p>If unable to obtain assistance through the FE Hotline or Support Center, have Engineering Support contact the product Backline team first, and if needed, the On-Call product engineer.</p><p>*** Timeline:</p><p>Next steps:&nbsp;FE to order parts and schedule service</p><p>Next owner:&nbsp;FE</p><p>***** END ACTION PLAN *****</p><p><strong>Actions taken:</strong></p><p><strong>Internal notes:</strong></p><p><strong>Next steps:</strong></p><p><strong>Special Instructions</strong></p><p>As a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.</p><p><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:</strong> Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a <strong>$20 USD deduction</strong> from the total work order pay.</p><p><strong>Escalations</strong></p><ol><li>Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li><li>For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.</li></ol><p>Consumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.</p><p>Upon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).</p><p>Upon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.</p><p>If after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.</p><p>All parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.</p><p>PLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.</p><p>Return of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.</p><p>If a part is removed from a local warehouse:</p><p>A. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>B. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.</p><p>YOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.</p><p>Acceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:</p><ul><li>State ID</li><li>Driver's License</li><li>US Passport</li></ul><p>ALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:</p><ul><li>Laptop computer</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)</li><li>Standard tool kit</li><li>Static mat and/or static strap</li><li>Heat Sink Paste</li><li>Blank CD's/DVD's</li><li>Portable CD/DVD drive</li><li>USB Flash drive</li><li>Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable</li><li>Hot Spot</li><li>Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed</li></ul><p>Tech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.</p><p>Tech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.</p><p>Tech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:</p><p><strong>NO JEANS</strong></p><p><strong>NO OPEN-TOE SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO GYM SHOES</strong></p><p><strong>NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING</strong></p><p>IMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.</p><p>If the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.</p><p><strong>Software Policy</strong></p><p>Policy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code</p><p>1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.</p><p>2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.</p><p>3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.</p><p>4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner</p><ul><li>5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Service Overview:**\n\n**Scope of Work:** \\[Description of service details\\]\n\n**Case Action Summary**\n\n**Summary:**\n\n**Action plan:**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ACTION PLAN \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nMultiple PCI cassette issues\n\n\\*\\*\\* Parts Required:\n\nQuantity: 4\n\nPart Number: 7089613\n\nSpecs: x16 PCI Express Carrier\n\nLocation: slots 4 and 7\n\n\\*\\*\\* Special Instructions:\n\nInspect replacement part for damage prior to using.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Current Issue:\n\nAffects : /SYS/RCSA/PCIE4/CAR /SYS/RCSA/PCIE7/CAR\n\n\\*\\*\\* Evidence of Issue:\n\nAffects : /SYS/RCSA/PCIE4/CAR /SYS/RCSA/PCIE7/CAR\n\n\\*\\*\\* Resolution Steps:\n\n1\\. Inspect Replacement part for damage.\n\n2.Note - Removing PCIe card carriers while the server is at the OpenBoot prompt is not supported. The server must be either powered off, or booted into the Oracle Solaris OS.\n\n3\\. Replace the PCIE carrier 4 7 while system powered off.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Supporting Documents:\n\n\\*\\*\\* Backline AEG for escalations:Sun / Oracle team\n\nCall in for Backline support with any questions. Have your Astea ticket number and call the FE Hotline at 800-497-3738 option 2, or engage your local Park Place Technologies Support Center using the appropriate toll-free phone number listed here: <https://www.parkplacetechnologies.com/contact-us/>\n\nIf unable to obtain assistance through the FE Hotline or Support Center, have Engineering Support contact the product Backline team first, and if needed, the On-Call product engineer.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Timeline:\n\nNext steps: FE to order parts and schedule service\n\nNext owner: FE\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* END ACTION PLAN \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Actions taken:**\n\n**Internal notes:**\n\n**Next steps:**\n\n**Special Instructions**\n\nAs a representative of PPT, we expect that you will maintain the highest standards of customer service and professionalism at all times when interacting with our customers. Please treat customers with respect and diplomacy, and in the event of an issue, escalate your concerns directly to Global AOM (Call us at 800-343-4654 option 9) for conflict resolution instead of engaging the customer.\n\n**MANDATORY CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICY:** Check-in and check-out are strictly required. Failure to perform either check-in or check-out will result in a **$20 USD deduction** from the total work order pay.\n\n**Escalations**\n\n1. Any issues unrelated to technical support: call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n2. For onsite technical support, please reach out to the \"Remote Support/L2 contact\" indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues reaching the Remote Support/L3 contact, please call Park Place Support at (800) 343-4654, option 9.\n\nConsumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place AOM team immediately.\n\nUpon arrival you must check in with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf you require technical assistance at that time, you must call Park Place Support at 800-497-3738 option 2 at least 1 hour before arrival for Advanced Engineering Group (L2/L3) assistance (only if you require assistance with the provided action plan — you are not required to call if you fully understand the Action Plan that was provided to you).\n\nUpon departing you must also check out with PPT 800-343-4654 option 9.\n\nIf after hours and a Manager is needed, call Support Center to engage Duty Manager 800-497-3738 option 1 or 2; if response is greater than 30 minutes for a call back, reach out to the AOM Global Team 800-343-4654 opt. 9.\n\nAll parts, excluding bad Disk Drives (please leave bad drives onsite unless customer requests it to be removed; if removed, drives must be disposed of at either a Certified Disposal facility or returned to Park Place Technologies for destruction), must be removed from site upon completion of call.\n\nPLEASE ask if any parts are returnable. If a part is needed back, you must request a return label to return the part from Global AOM.\n\nReturn of Equipment: Techs are responsible to properly package and immediately ship back parts needed to be returned (parts with RMA). Note: NO work orders will be approved until we are able to track the shipment.\n\nIf a part is removed from a local warehouse:\n\nA. Tech must complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nB. If the part is not used, then it must be returned to the local warehouse during business hours 8:00AM–5:00PM local time. Please check with Global AOM before returning the part to the locker, or request a return label from them depending on distance, and complete the entry of pertinent information in the log book.\n\nYOU MUST have at least one valid form of physical identification in order to run this service call.\n\nAcceptable IDs include the following, and it cannot be expired or in paper form:\n\n- State ID\n- Driver's License\n- US Passport\n\nALL appropriate tools/equipment will be needed including:\n\n- Laptop computer\n- Voltmeter\n- Standard communication cables (Cisco console cable, Ethernet Straight-through and crossover cable, Null Modem Serial Cable, and a USB to serial cable/adapter)\n- Standard tool kit\n- Static mat and/or static strap\n- Heat Sink Paste\n- Blank CD's/DVD's\n- Portable CD/DVD drive\n- USB Flash drive\n- Necessary cables and Diagnostic CD/USB if required in call notes; Null Modem Serial Cable\n- Hot Spot\n- Diagnostic CD such as Dell Asset CD or HP Smart Start: it will be listed in the Action Plan if needed\n\nTech is required to have basic knowledge and experience replacing parts and troubleshooting servers.\n\nTech will be required to wear business casual attire; trousers/khakis and a collared polo/dress shirt.\n\nTech must come with good personal hygiene and be dressed business casual. This means the following:\n\n**NO JEANS**\n\n**NO OPEN-TOE SHOES**\n\n**NO GYM SHOES**\n\n**NO WRINKLED OR RIPPED/TORN CLOTHING**\n\nIMPORTANT: Certified Partner is NOT to reschedule a call with the customer if he/she cannot make it to site — must contact Global AOM. Customer is always able to reschedule.\n\nIf the CP cannot do the service call at the customer's scheduled time, then CP must call Global AOM and update that they are unable to do the call. At this time, Global AOM will look for a different Technical Resource.\n\n**Software Policy**\n\nPolicy limiting PPT Support for OEM Software, Firmware, Code\n\n1.0 Purpose: Park Place Technologies adheres to a strict process of policy distribution to all employees and certified partners that represent Park Place Technologies. It is the responsibility of every employee and partner to read, understand, and acknowledge receipt of each policy.\n\n2.0 Policy: It is the policy of Park Place Technologies (PPT) to follow all U.S. and International copyright laws and not provide, distribute, alter, update, or provide links for OEM firmware or software to customers.\n\n3.0 Scope: This Policy applies to all PPT employees, contractors, and designees.\n\n4.0 Terms, Definitions, and Acronyms: CP – Certified Partner\n\n- 5.0 Procedure: CPs that engage with PPT customers are instructed to refuse requests from customers for PPT to provide any type of proprietary OEM Software/Firmware or patches. Should the customer have a concern with this policy, the CP shall escalate the issue to Global AOM.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.456107788158139},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-07T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"Amazon wholefoods return"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summ