{"job":{"id":20121305,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":" Troubleshoot Camera System","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******** * </del></span><del>******************</del></li><li>Technicians can text 'Start' to <del>***** ********</del>. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.</li></ul><p>System &amp; Model #:&nbsp;&nbsp;HIK</p><p>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :&nbsp;</p><p>Technician needs to be onsite to troubleshoot and restore both local and remote feed of camera system. Coordinate with HD if a part is needed for replacement.</p><ul><li>Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.</li><li>Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.</li><li>All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location</li><li>Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call <del>************ ** ***</del> service desk if support does not transfer.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians can text 'Start' to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.\n\nSystem & Model #: HIK\n\nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem :\n\nTechnician needs to be onsite to troubleshoot and restore both local and remote feed of camera system. Coordinate with HD if a part is needed for replacement.\n\n- Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.\n- Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.\n- All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location\n- Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* service desk if support does not transfer.\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN \\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).\n- Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc\n- Picture of RMA form & return label applied; if applicable\n- Release Code\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 11)\n- Operating system must be fully licensed and updated\n- · Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Buttset\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Drill\n- 12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete\n- 8' Ladder\n- Phone/Ethernet Wiring\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Contact Name & Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**\n\n**Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T08:00","end":"2026-10-07T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-07T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":43.501428764357605},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/7/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T20:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-07T15:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"DMV"},{"start":"2026-10-07T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"Amazon wholefoods return"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.0