{"job":{"id":"9209244225","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install","description":"DESCRIPTION: SOW - EPIK Single Visit Install <br>\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*<br>Technician will be working with the Granite Project Team and the Epik Activations Team on the bridge below. Please dial into the bridge below to assist with the cutover: 929-229-2436, Passcode: 905 484 289#<br>We will be connecting to Switch 2, Port 26 for network connection.<br>We will only be cutting over sites fire and security lines, the site may or may not have a fax line, this is NOT to be cutover.<br>  <br>Before Arrival <br>1. Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival. <br>2. Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK: <br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo <br>1. Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below. <br>On Arrival <br>1. Check in on WorkMarket. <br>2. Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location. <br>3. Review the Special Instructions before starting work. <br>EPIK Install Requirements <br>1. Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik. <br>2. If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location.  <br>3. Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard. <br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on. <br>1. If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions. <br>2. Log into the EPIK Install Wizard: <br>https://wizard.epik.io <br>1. Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned. <br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES <br>1. If not already stated in the TNs to be wired section of your ticket, confirm with site contact if there are fire alarm, security alarm, elevator or e911 lines on site. If so, notify activations of any port configuration changes that need to be made and complete testing with the fire, security or elevator monitoring companies. <br>2. For any lines that cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number. <br>3. If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready. <br>Checkout Requirement <br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line. <br>2. Confirm Activations has released you. <br>3. Submit all WorkMarket deliverables. <br>4. Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket. <br>5. Check out on WorkMarket. <br>  <br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket. <br>  <br>Required Deliverables <br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout: <br>1. Photo of completed EPIK install. <br>2. Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block. <br>3. List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable. <br>4. Customer signed sign-out sheet. <br>5. Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions. <br>  <br>  <br>Required Tools <br>•\tLaptop <br>•\tSmartphone with hotspot <br>•\tTone generator and wand <br>•\t66/110 punch tool <br>•\tButt set <br>•\t       Infrared Temperature Gun  <br>•\tElectrician scissors <br>•\tStep ladder <br>•\tFlashlight/headlamp <br>•\tRJ11/RJ45 crimper <br>•\tEthernet cable tester <br>•\tImpact drill / cordless drill <br>•\tMasonry bits <br>•\tScrewdrivers / driver bits <br>•\tNeedle-nose pliers <br>•\tLabel maker and label tape <br>•\tCat3 or better cable <br>•\tCat6 Ethernet cable <br>•\tCross-connect wire <br>•\tGel-crimp connectors <br>•\tCable ties and mounting hardware <br>•\tRJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks <br>•\tConsole cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini <br>\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* <br>  <br>PM SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS GUIDELINES <br>Special Instructions <br>Install Location <br>Enter where the EPIK device should be installed, including MDF/IDF/telco room location, wall/rack/shelf mounting instructions, and access notes. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>Cable Runs <br>Enter any required cable runs, cable type, distance, start/end points, and whether ladder, lift, ceiling access, or special tools are needed. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>Network Information <br>Enter switch name, switch port, DHCP/static IP details, VLAN info, and customer network escalation contact. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>External Antenna <br>Enter whether an external antenna is required, where it should be mounted, and any cable path or photo requirements. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>Special Testing <br>Enter any customer-specific testing that must be completed, including specific TNs, fax, alarm, elevator, hunt group, auto attendant, or other required testing. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>Customer Contacts <br>Enter primary LCON, backup contact, customer IT contact, site manager, and escalation contacts. <br>\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ <br>Vendor / Third-Party Info <br>Enter any VTM, customer tech, alarm vendor, elevator vendor, fax vendor, MSP, or other third-party contact information.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":14.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 12, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 10/07/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary