{"job":{"id":20122712,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Total Technology Services","title":"Checked Up - Replace (8) 32\" Wallboard","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech to replace 8 WBs</span></p><p>*** <strong>Please Note for Cable Cover</strong> - We cannot use the self adhesive sticky on the back of the cord covering. The cord covering must be secured to the wall with screws or nails. Failure to do this correctly may delay payment.</p><p><strong><u>Complete links while onsite:</u></strong></p><p>https://checkedup.my.salesforce-sites.com/fieldService/spworkordercheckin?id=0WOPq00000PiewD</p><p>CheckedUp help desk phone number is in confidential section</p><p>** Printed Documentation must be with you onsite***</p><ul><li>Stud finder&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Tape measure</li><li>Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Phillips drill bit 12” extension (used for inserting the locking screws)</li><li>Awl (to assist in making holes in wall and cord cover for the screws to be installed)</li><li>Small level (for leveling the wall bracket)</li><li>2-foot level (for leveling the cord cover)</li><li>Cable Cutter/diagonal cutters (for trimming the cord cover)</li><li>or hacksaw for cutting cord covers</li><li>Razorblade</li><li>Cordless Drill- Only use if necessary, for concrete walls, avoid making noise in the office</li><li>Drill bits for sheetrock/concrete walls behind sheetrock</li><li>Hammer to tap in the anchors in the case of concrete walls</li><li>USB Windows keyboard</li><li>USB mouse</li><li>Step ladder (for tv installation if installing TV, DO NOT stand on office chairs)</li><li>Smartphone for photos</li><li>Laptop for troubleshooting sites network &amp; firmware update</li><li>Toggle bolts</li><li>100ft Ethernet Cable</li><li>32gb Flash Drive</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Photos Required:&nbsp;(per device)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Picture of each asset installed and playing content</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Picture of UDID of each asset installed</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The UDID (Unit ID) can be obtained by pressing and holding on the house button in the lower left of the screen.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check out notes confirming if each asset is online and CheckedUp rep who confirmed</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check Out notes explaining if all assets could not be installed- need detailed reasoning</p><p><strong>Equipment must be tested out of the box before installation. This is to ensure the equipment is not damaged or defective. If this step is skipped and damaged/defective equipment is installed, it may result in non-payment. Installing damaged or broken equipment is not acceptable.</strong></p><p><strong>**If you arrive per the scheduled time and notify TTS immediately that the site is not ready for the service for any reason included but not limited to parts not on site, site is closed, or site contact / support not available, TTS agrees to reimburse for a 1-hour minimum rate before closing the work order. If a fixed rate or quoted amount was confirmed rather than an hourly rate, TTS will pay $50 for the on-site cancellation. If travel was agreed upon, that amount will be paid in lieu of an hourly or fixed rate.**</strong></p><p><strong>﻿Windows 10 Laptop and 32gb flash drive are required materials for this job. If the assigned provider does not bring these materials, we will request a $50 discount be applied to the work order.</strong></p>","markdown":"Tech to replace 8 WBs\n\n\\*\\*\\* **Please Note for Cable Cover** - We cannot use the self adhesive sticky on the back of the cord covering. The cord covering must be secured to the wall with screws or nails. Failure to do this correctly may delay payment.\n\n**Complete links while onsite:**\n\n<https://checkedup.my.salesforce-sites.com/fieldService/spworkordercheckin?id=0WOPq00000PiewD>\n\nCheckedUp help desk phone number is in confidential section\n\n\\*\\* Printed Documentation must be with you onsite\\*\\*\\*\n\n- Stud finder\n- Tape measure\n- Phillips screwdriver\n- Phillips drill bit 12” extension (used for inserting the locking screws)\n- Awl (to assist in making holes in wall and cord cover for the screws to be installed)\n- Small level (for leveling the wall bracket)\n- 2-foot level (for leveling the cord cover)\n- Cable Cutter/diagonal cutters (for trimming the cord cover)\n- or hacksaw for cutting cord covers\n- Razorblade\n- Cordless Drill- Only use if necessary, for concrete walls, avoid making noise in the office\n- Drill bits for sheetrock/concrete walls behind sheetrock\n- Hammer to tap in the anchors in the case of concrete walls\n- USB Windows keyboard\n- USB mouse\n- Step ladder (for tv installation if installing TV, DO NOT stand on office chairs)\n- Smartphone for photos\n- Laptop for troubleshooting sites network & firmware update\n- Toggle bolts\n- 100ft Ethernet Cable\n- 32gb Flash Drive\n\nPhotos Required: (per device)\n\n· Picture of each asset installed and playing content\n\n· Picture of UDID of each asset installed\n\no The UDID (Unit ID) can be obtained by pressing and holding on the house button in the lower left of the screen.\n\n· Check out notes confirming if each asset is online and CheckedUp rep who confirmed\n\n· Check Out notes explaining if all assets could not be installed- need detailed reasoning\n\n**Equipment must be tested out of the box before installation. This is to ensure the equipment is not damaged or defective. If this step is skipped and damaged/defective equipment is installed, it may result in non-payment. Installing damaged or broken equipment is not acceptable.**\n\n**\\*\\*If you arrive per the scheduled time and notify TTS immediately that the site is not ready for the service for any reason included but not limited to parts not on site, site is closed, or site contact / support not available, TTS agrees to reimburse for a 1-hour minimum rate before closing the work order. If a fixed rate or quoted amount was confirmed rather than an hourly rate, TTS will pay $50 for the on-site cancellation. If travel was agreed upon, that amount will be paid in lieu of an hourly or fixed rate.\\*\\***\n\n**﻿Windows 10 Laptop and 32gb flash drive are required materials for this job. If the assigned provider does not bring these materials, we will request a $50 discount be applied to the work order.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T11:30","end":"2026-11-02T19:30"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":360},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":14.104828235436795},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 