{"job":{"id":20123914,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"WatchMeGrow","title":"WatchMeGrow - Repair or Replace IP Camera","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:</strong> https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html</p><p><strong>Equipment Needed:</strong>&nbsp;RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter</span>, Multimeter Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit</p><p><strong>Description:</strong>&nbsp;One IP camera connected to our server at a childcare center is no longer giving us a good video feed. Please follow the required troubleshooting in the instructions below. WatchMeGrow Technical staff is on hand during repair to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will need to call us upon arrival to check in and prior to leaving to check out.</p><p><strong>!!IMPORTANT!!</strong></p><ul><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Licensing and Permits:</strong> Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.</p><p><strong>Safety</strong>: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.</p><p>If you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.</p><p><strong>Photos:</strong> Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.</p><p><strong>Call to Sign In/Out:</strong> Please call <del>************</del> to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.</p><p><strong>***&nbsp;Buyer approval required on all appointments that differ from the service date&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Required Troubleshooting:</strong>&nbsp;Please diagnose and repair video signal loss with the camera(s) listed.</p><ol><li>Call WatchMeGrow (<del>************</del>) to check in when onsite.</li><li>Replace all RJ-45 crimps between the camera and PoE switch.</li><li>Call WatchMeGrow so we can attempt to connect to the camera after replacing the crimps.</li><li>Test cable continuity with network cable tester to ensure the cable is not damaged. If the cable fails the test, please call WMG.</li><li>Move the affected camera's cable to a different port on the PoE switch. Call WatchMeGrow so we can see if we can access the camera on the new PoE port. If we can't, please proceed to the next step.</li><li>To rule out issues with the cable run, remove the camera from the mount and connect it directly to the switch using a short patch cable.</li><li>Replace the camera and call WatchMeGrow so that we can configure the camera and ensure it is working properly. Note: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.</li><li>Aim the camera to WMG and the customer's specifications.</li><li>Troubleshoot to resolve any lingering issues.</li><li>Call WatchMeGrow to check out when finished.</li></ol><p><strong>Camera Location:</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Front Entrance View 1 (ID 21) 192.168.4.121</span></p><p><strong>Sign Off:&nbsp;</strong>Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.</p>","markdown":"**You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:** <https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html>\n\n**Equipment Needed:** RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter, Multimeter Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit\n\n**Description:** One IP camera connected to our server at a childcare center is no longer giving us a good video feed. Please follow the required troubleshooting in the instructions below. WatchMeGrow Technical staff is on hand during repair to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will need to call us upon arrival to check in and prior to leaving to check out.\n\n**!!IMPORTANT!!**\n\n- **WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.**\n- **WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.**\n- **WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.**\n\n**Licensing and Permits:** Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.\n\n**Safety**: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.\n\nIf you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.\n\n**Photos:** Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.\n\n**Call to Sign In/Out:** Please call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Buyer approval required on all appointments that differ from the service date**\n\n**Required Troubleshooting:** Please diagnose and repair video signal loss with the camera(s) listed.\n\n1. Call WatchMeGrow (\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*) to check in when onsite.\n2. Replace all RJ-45 crimps between the camera and PoE switch.\n3. Call WatchMeGrow so we can attempt to connect to the camera after replacing the crimps.\n4. Test cable continuity with network cable tester to ensure the cable is not damaged. If the cable fails the test, please call WMG.\n5. Move the affected camera's cable to a different port on the PoE switch. Call WatchMeGrow so we can see if we can access the camera on the new PoE port. If we can't, please proceed to the next step.\n6. To rule out issues with the cable run, remove the camera from the mount and connect it directly to the switch using a short patch cable.\n7. Replace the camera and call WatchMeGrow so that we can configure the camera and ensure it is working properly. Note: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.\n8. Aim the camera to WMG and the customer's specifications.\n9. Troubleshoot to resolve any lingering issues.\n10. Call WatchMeGrow to check out when finished.\n\n**Camera Location:** Front Entrance View 1 (ID 21) 192.168.4.121\n\n**Sign Off:** Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T09:00","end":"2026-10-16T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-16T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":46.143042444773506},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start"