{"job":{"id":20124065,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"C1 Technical Services, LLC","title":"Opening Day Support - 6 Hours","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with 2 years experience in troubleshooting and maintenance of equipment in quick service restaurant.</li><li>Tech is required to work with Chipotle IT Support Team to provide boots on the ground troubleshooting and maintenance for opening day of restaurant.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 6 hours. Technician is required to remain onsite, in dining area, for the entirety of the 6 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Neat and clean appearance. Can wear denim, but must be free of stains, rips, and tears. NO shorts.</li><li>Must wear collared shirt: Button down or polo shirt are acceptable. Cannot wear T-shirt or tank top.</li><li>PPE: non slip shoes required, technician will be on ladders and in kitchen areas.</li><li>No visible tattoos on neck or face and no facial piercings.</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required: </strong>must haves</p><ul><li>Cable tester, laptop, cell phone.</li><li>Any tools necessary to run network line, terminate for use, and to troubleshoot all equipment in quick service restaurant.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>Confirm via text to Lead Project Manager <del>****** *************</del>. This needs to be done the day before work is scheduled to begin.</li><li>Take/upload photo of store front and location before beginning work.</li></ol><p><strong><em>Job Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order</li><li>Check-in with Chipotle Go-Live support staff that is onsite.</li><li>Work with designated IT Support staff to go through preopening Check List. Upload photos of all equipment tested and receipts generated during testing.</li><li>Communicate any and all troubleshooting to CMG Support Team first. Alert C1 Technical Services Project Manager of any issues that are being worked on with CMG Support Team. Upload photos of any equipment that needs troubleshooting and any receipts generated during troubleshooting process.</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><strong><em>Required Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Upload photo of store front before completing work</li><li>UPLOAD PHOTOS OF EVERYTHING TESTED BEFORE IT CHECK OUT.</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><p>Contact WO Manager if the following are true:</p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with Project Manager <del>****** *************</del></li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to Project Manager <del>****** *************</del></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>List how you will handle additional expenses here.</li><li>List how you will handle additional hours here.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Example: Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App</span></p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with 2 years experience in troubleshooting and maintenance of equipment in quick service restaurant.\n- Tech is required to work with Chipotle IT Support Team to provide boots on the ground troubleshooting and maintenance for opening day of restaurant.\n- Estimated duration will be 6 hours. Technician is required to remain onsite, in dining area, for the entirety of the 6 hours.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Neat and clean appearance. Can wear denim, but must be free of stains, rips, and tears. NO shorts.\n- Must wear collared shirt: Button down or polo shirt are acceptable. Cannot wear T-shirt or tank top.\n- PPE: non slip shoes required, technician will be on ladders and in kitchen areas.\n- No visible tattoos on neck or face and no facial piercings.\n\n**Tools Required:** must haves\n\n- Cable tester, laptop, cell phone.\n- Any tools necessary to run network line, terminate for use, and to troubleshoot all equipment in quick service restaurant.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre Requirements***\n\n1. Confirm via text to Lead Project Manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. This needs to be done the day before work is scheduled to begin.\n2. Take/upload photo of store front and location before beginning work.\n\n***Job Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order\n2. Check-in with Chipotle Go-Live support staff that is onsite.\n3. Work with designated IT Support staff to go through preopening Check List. Upload photos of all equipment tested and receipts generated during testing.\n4. Communicate any and all troubleshooting to CMG Support Team first. Alert C1 Technical Services Project Manager of any issues that are being worked on with CMG Support Team. Upload photos of any equipment that needs troubleshooting and any receipts generated during troubleshooting process.\n5. Check-out of work order\n\n***Required Deliverables***\n\n1. Upload photo of store front before completing work\n2. UPLOAD PHOTOS OF EVERYTHING TESTED BEFORE IT CHECK OUT.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact WO Manager if the following are true:\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with Project Manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to Project Manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- List how you will handle additional expenses here.\n- List how you will handle additional hours here.\n\nExample: Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":360},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":15.117075692548228},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   