{"job":{"id":20124259,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"Starlink Install","description":{"html":"Starlink – Troubleshoot &amp; Replace if Needed<p><strong>GOAL: Resolve the Starlink issue in ONE VISIT.</strong></p><p>Troubleshoot first. <strong>If service cannot be restored, complete the full replacement using the equipment and lift provided.</strong></p>Before Arrival<ul><li>Review ticket for <strong>INC, KITP, dish location, switch/port, tracking, and site-specific information</strong>.</li><li><strong>Lift and replacement Starlink equipment have been provided.</strong></li><li>Bring required <strong>cinder blocks – Baird mount requires 8 total.</strong> Check current mount set up to confirm how many are already onsite. Tech may need to leave site to gather more.</li></ul><p><strong>Check In:</strong> 855-609-9292 — Opt. 2, Opt. 1</p><p><strong>Check Out / Questions:</strong> 479-879-3183</p>1. Troubleshoot First<ul><li>Locate dish, PSU, cabling, and assigned switch port.</li><li>Verify all connections are fully seated.</li><li>Confirm <strong>PSU has power/white light</strong> and check switch port for link/activity.</li><li>Check dish for abnormal clicking/loud noises. A low hum is normal.</li><li>Disconnect all 3 PSU cables for <strong>30 seconds</strong>, reconnect, and allow system to boot.</li><li>Recheck switch link/activity.</li><li>Call NOC with the <strong>INC number</strong> to validate status and complete any additional troubleshooting requested.</li></ul><p><strong>Walmart / Sam's / NHM NOC:</strong> 479-277-2674</p><p><strong>Walmart DC:</strong> 479-802-5458 — Opt. 1, Opt. 1, Opt. 1</p><p><strong>STARLINK ONLINE?</strong></p><p><strong>YES → Validate with NOC. Do NOT replace equipment. Proceed to Step 3. Do not leave equipment on site.</strong></p><p><strong>NO → Proceed immediately with full replacement.</strong></p>2. Replace Starlink<ul><li>Remove defective Starlink equipment.</li><li>Existing dish cable may be <strong>cut and used as a pull string</strong> for the new cable.</li><li>Install Baird mount with <strong>8 – 8x8x16 cinder blocks</strong>. Tech may need to leave site to gather necessary amount, 4 bricks is not enough and will cause return trips and extra costs if missed.</li><li>Connect: <strong>Dish → Dish Cable → PSU → Switch Cable → Assigned Switch Port</strong></li><li>Call NOC with <strong>INC/KITP</strong> and validate the replacement.</li><li><strong>Do not leave until NOC confirms Starlink is online and operational.</strong></li></ul>3. Return Equipment<ul><li>Box defective equipment and any unused replacement equipment requiring return. <strong>Purchase a box if needed.</strong></li><li>Discard/recycle old Starlink legs unless instructed otherwise.</li><li>Apply provided return label and return equipment to <strong>FedEx</strong>.</li><li>Provide photo of <strong>FedEx tracking/receipt</strong>.</li></ul>Required Deliverables<p>Photos of <strong>dish, PSU, cabling, switch/port, completed mount/ballast with 8 bricks if replaced, and FedEx receipt if equipment is returned.</strong></p><p><strong>Linda Stone – PM:</strong> 479-879-3183</p><p><strong>Noah Parsons – PC:</strong> 479-225-3348</p>","markdown":"Starlink – Troubleshoot & Replace if Needed\n\n**GOAL: Resolve the Starlink issue in ONE VISIT.**\n\nTroubleshoot first. **If service cannot be restored, complete the full replacement using the equipment and lift provided.**\n\nBefore Arrival- Review ticket for **INC, KITP, dish location, switch/port, tracking, and site-specific information**.\n- **Lift and replacement Starlink equipment have been provided.**\n- Bring required **cinder blocks – Baird mount requires 8 total.** Check current mount set up to confirm how many are already onsite. Tech may need to leave site to gather more.\n\n**Check In:** 855-609-9292 — Opt. 2, Opt. 1\n\n**Check Out / Questions:** 479-879-3183\n\n1. Troubleshoot First- Locate dish, PSU, cabling, and assigned switch port.\n- Verify all connections are fully seated.\n- Confirm **PSU has power/white light** and check switch port for link/activity.\n- Check dish for abnormal clicking/loud noises. A low hum is normal.\n- Disconnect all 3 PSU cables for **30 seconds**, reconnect, and allow system to boot.\n- Recheck switch link/activity.\n- Call NOC with the **INC number** to validate status and complete any additional troubleshooting requested.\n\n**Walmart / Sam's / NHM NOC:** 479-277-2674\n\n**Walmart DC:** 479-802-5458 — Opt. 1, Opt. 1, Opt. 1\n\n**STARLINK ONLINE?**\n\n**YES → Validate with NOC. Do NOT replace equipment. Proceed to Step 3. Do not leave equipment on site.**\n\n**NO → Proceed immediately with full replacement.**\n\n2. Replace Starlink- Remove defective Starlink equipment.\n- Existing dish cable may be **cut and used as a pull string** for the new cable.\n- Install Baird mount with **8 – 8x8x16 cinder blocks**. Tech may need to leave site to gather necessary amount, 4 bricks is not enough and will cause return trips and extra costs if missed.\n- Connect: **Dish → Dish Cable → PSU → Switch Cable → Assigned Switch Port**\n- Call NOC with **INC/KITP** and validate the replacement.\n- **Do not leave until NOC confirms Starlink is online and operational.**\n\n3. Return Equipment- Box defective equipment and any unused replacement equipment requiring return. **Purchase a box if needed.**\n- Discard/recycle old Starlink legs unless instructed otherwise.\n- Apply provided return label and return equipment to **FedEx**.\n- Provide photo of **FedEx tracking/receipt**.\n\nRequired DeliverablesPhotos of **dish, PSU, cabling, switch/port, completed mount/ballast with 8 bricks if replaced, and FedEx receipt if equipment is returned.**\n\n**Linda Stone – PM:** 479-879-3183\n\n**Noah Parsons – PC:** 479-225-3348","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10-08T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payTyp