{"job":{"id":20125157,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Johnston & Murphy New Store Installation **3 Days**","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">SITE INFORMATION</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Site ID</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: GEN01868JM</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Service Request Number(s):</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\"> SR04379417 / SR04379416</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Site Name</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: Johnston &amp; Murphy</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Street Address</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: 6910 FAYETTEVILLE RD, SPC 1170, DURHAM, NC 27713</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Parts Being Sent</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: To Tech – Please advise shipping address</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to check-in via tect chat - </span>text “Start” to <del>************</del>.You will receive 2 messages back. First will confirm you have been connected and the second will ask if you are onsite for 1 - New Installation or 2 - Service, you will always respond back \"1\". <strong>**review PDF attached on process &amp; directions to escalate if support not responsive within 20 minutes (Step 2) </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">SCOPE OF WORK</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: See attached IG for full SOW – This is a “New Store” Installation. PM will provide layout ahead of install once customer provides. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;Installation Guide: </span>https://interfacesystems.mcoutput.com/genig/Content/Network%20Installation%20Guides/Genesco/Individual%20Scopes/Prior%20to%20Entering.htm</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 1: 10/20 @ 9AM </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Prewire - Prewire of the site before the ceilings or walls are closed. CAT5e cabling to be run and coiled up in final locations in preparation for next visit.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 2: 10/27 @ 9AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">New Store Day 1 - Install the network cabinet and patch panel.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 3: 10/28 @ 9AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">New Store Day 3 - Install WAP, Media shelf cabling, E-Stat cabling, and phone</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**SITE INFORMATION**\n\n**Site ID**: GEN01868JM\n\n**Service Request Number(s):** SR04379417 / SR04379416\n\n**Site Name**: Johnston & Murphy\n\n**Street Address**: 6910 FAYETTEVILLE RD, SPC 1170, DURHAM, NC 27713\n\n**Parts Being Sent**: To Tech – Please advise shipping address\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to check-in via tect chat - text “Start” to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.You will receive 2 messages back. First will confirm you have been connected and the second will ask if you are onsite for 1 - New Installation or 2 - Service, you will always respond back \"1\". **\\*\\*review PDF attached on process & directions to escalate if support not responsive within 20 minutes (Step 2)**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**: See attached IG for full SOW – This is a “New Store” Installation. PM will provide layout ahead of install once customer provides.\n\n Installation Guide: <https://interfacesystems.mcoutput.com/genig/Content/Network%20Installation%20Guides/Genesco/Individual%20Scopes/Prior%20to%20Entering.htm>\n\nDay 1: 10/20 @ 9AM\n\nPrewire - Prewire of the site before the ceilings or walls are closed. CAT5e cabling to be run and coiled up in final locations in preparation for next visit.\n\nDay 2: 10/27 @ 9AM\n\nNew Store Day 1 - Install the network cabinet and patch panel.\n\nDay 3: 10/28 @ 9AM\n\nNew Store Day 3 - Install WAP, Media shelf cabling, E-Stat cabling, and phone\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN \\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).\n- Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc\n- Picture of RMA form & return label applied; if applicable\n- Release Code\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 11)\n- Operating system must be fully licensed and updated\n- · Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Buttset\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Drill\n- 12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete\n- 8' Ladder\n- Phone/Ethernet Wiring\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Contact Name & Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**\n\n**Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-20T29:00"},"payRange":{"min":900,"max":900},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":20,"distance":11.24984582774906},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Oct 20, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 20, Wed, Oct 21, Thu, Oct 22, Fri, Oct 23 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791393572524}
{"job":{"id":20125081,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Staley Technologies","title":"Tech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace data cable and jack for PC in Receiving.","description":{"html":"<p><u>DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE</u></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Tech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace data cable and jack for PC in Receiving.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Device with Issue</strong>: Desktop</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Location of Device</strong>: Receiving</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Customer Notes</strong>: Club - 215 | &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Tech needed to T.R.R. data line to DT215REC03</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Tech needs to TRR the data cable, ports, switch and run new data lines, if needed.</p>\n<p>Tech should capture the location, switch number, and port assignment before departing the club</p>\n<p>Tech should take pictures before and after working in the IDF/MDF</p>\n<p>Tech upon arrival and after repairs should work with the NOC for verification and validation</p>\n<p><strong>IT-NOC 833-722-3102. NOC must validate Phone/Printer/Desktop/Register before releasing the tech</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Tech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled</p>\n<p>Example: Club211IDF1before, Club211IDF1after and so on</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>Usually, they will be in the following places:</p>\n<p>IDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office</p>\n<p>MDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Failure to do so will result in a penalty.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Access related issues</strong>: Make sure you go to the back of the store and ring the door buzzer after hours.&nbsp;If you still cannot gain access, call the Staley support desk 501.320.4738.&nbsp;Any calls made, a voicemail is expected, stating your reason for the call.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Closeout Notes:</strong> Make sure everything that occurred during the Visit is called out in the close out notes.&nbsp;Phone calls and texts will not be used in lieu of providing detailed and concise closeout notes</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Work Summary:</strong> Trace and repair cabling. Verify cable is connected to the correct switch port. If repairs cannot be made, install a new cable. Verify the device is online.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Switch Ports (Non-PCI/VLAN 101) at:</strong></p>\n<p>MDF&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Switch Ports 0 – 18</p>\n<p>IDF&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Switch Ports 0 – 19</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Incomplete Sites:</strong>If you cannot complete your site for any reason, call Staley Support 501-320-4738</p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Important Information: Anytime you are bringing a lift into or out of a customer facility, whether through a doorway or overhead door, you must bring the lift to a complete stop before going through the entry.&nbsp;You must walk around the entire lift looking for any obstacles.&nbsp;Be sure to check the height of the cage vs the height of the entry.&nbsp;&nbsp;Be sure to check the width of the lift vs the width of the entry.&nbsp;Only when that has been completed and you are sure there are no potential contact points may you continue forward with the lift.&nbsp;<u>If there is trouble with the lift, please call the number on the side of the equipment for support and let Staley Technologies know of the issues.</u></strong></p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>MATERIALS</strong></p>\n<p><strong>QTY&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;DESCRIPTION</strong></p>\n<p>=======================</p>\n<p>250’&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6, WH, Plenum</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1 Port Faceplate</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;RJ45</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5’ CAT6 Patch Cables Blue</p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS</strong></p>\n<p>---------</p>\n<p>Tech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:</p>\n<p>LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE</p>\n<p>USB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR</p>\n<p>USB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE</p>\n<p>PRECISE SCREWDRIVERS</p>\n<p>PUNCH TOOL W 66/110 BLADES</p>\n<p>WIRE STRIPPERS</p>\n<p>CRIMPER</p>\n<p>TONER</p>\n<p>LABELMAKER</p>\n<p>CABLE TESTER</p>\n<p>STANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)</p>\n<p>8’ to 10’ LADDER</p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;NOTES</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>*&nbsp;&nbsp;White, Plenum CAT6 cable is required for all permanent cable runs.</p>\n<p>** Velcro on ALL non-permanent wire management. Including power cords and AC Adapters.</p>\n<p>** DO NOT install any surface mount boxes in the MDF or any IDF's.</p>\n<p>** If ports don’t exist, you will need to install a new 24-port patch panel.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>ATTENTION: Any IDF's in the Club with surface mount boxes must be corrected.</p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>1) Meet with store personnel/management and introduce yourself.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a) Review details of service requests with store personnel/management.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>2) Troubleshoot the network cable run from PC in<strong>Receiving</strong> to the customers nearest IDF or MDF.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a) Capture before pictures of the equipment and work area.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;b) Test network cable and determine faults. Repair as needed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Test the cable.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Repair as needed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Test the cable again to verify it has been repaired.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;c) If cable is damaged beyond repair, you will need to run a new drop.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Run 1 new data cable from the nearest IDF/MDF to PC location</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Terminate/Test/Label new data cable</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Patch in the newly installed data cable per site guidelines.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;d) If cable is confirmed to be good, Deli computer will boot up</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;e) Make sure <strong>PC in Receiving</strong> is connected to a switch port mentioned in the “<strong>Switch Ports:”</strong> section of the work order.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>IDF: ______ Patch Panel# _____ Port# _____ =&gt; Switch Name: ______Port# _____&nbsp;</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>TEST RESULTS FOR EACH CABLE(S) WILL BE REQUIRED AT CHECKOUT.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>3) Contact BJ's Support at 833-722-3102 Opt. 1 and verify the device is connected to the network<strong>.&nbsp;</strong>If the tech remains on hold for 10 minutes or longer when calling into the BJ’s support desk, the tech should then call into the Staley support desk 501-320-4738. SSD will send an email with the technician’s name and phone number along with an explanation that they are onsite and need assistance.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Failure to do so will result in a penalty.</p>\n<p>4) Required Pictures:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a)&nbsp;<strong>PC in</strong> <strong>Receiving</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;b)&nbsp;&nbsp;Patch Panel ports</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;c)&nbsp;&nbsp;Switch ports</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;d)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><u>CABLE TEST RESULTS</u></strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;e) . Tech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>Usually, they will be in the following places:</p>\n<p>IDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office</p>\n<p>MDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled</p>\n<p>Example: Club211IDF1before, Club211IDF1after and so on</p>","markdown":"DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE\n\nTech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace data cable and jack for PC in Receiving.\n\n.\n\n**Device with Issue**: Desktop\n\n.\n\n**Location of Device**: Receiving\n\n.\n\n**Customer Notes**: Club - 215 |\n\nTech needed to T.R.R. data line to DT215REC03\n\n.\n\nTech needs to TRR the data cable, ports, switch and run new data lines, if needed.\n\nTech should capture the location, switch number, and port assignment before departing the club\n\nTech should take pictures before and after working in the IDF/MDF\n\nTech upon arrival and after repairs should work with the NOC for verification and validation\n\n**IT-NOC 833-722-3102. NOC must validate Phone/Printer/Desktop/Register before releasing the tech**\n\n.\n\nTech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\n.\n\nPictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled\n\nExample: Club211IDF1before, Club211IDF1after and so on\n\n.\n\nIf any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\nUsually, they will be in the following places:\n\nIDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office\n\nMDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club\n\n.\n\nFailure to do so will result in a penalty.\n\n.\n\n**Access related issues**: Make sure you go to the back of the store and ring the door buzzer after hours. If you still cannot gain access, call the Staley support desk 501.320.4738. Any calls made, a voicemail is expected, stating your reason for the call.\n\n.\n\n**Closeout Notes:** Make sure everything that occurred during the Visit is called out in the close out notes. Phone calls and texts will not be used in lieu of providing detailed and concise closeout notes\n\n.\n\n**Work Summary:** Trace and repair cabling. Verify cable is connected to the correct switch port. If repairs cannot be made, install a new cable. Verify the device is online.\n\n.\n\n**Switch Ports (Non-PCI/VLAN 101) at:**\n\nMDF Switch Ports 0 – 18\n\nIDF Switch Ports 0 – 19\n\n.\n\n**Incomplete Sites:**If you cannot complete your site for any reason, call Staley Support 501-320-4738\n\n**.**\n\n**Important Information: Anytime you are bringing a lift into or out of a customer facility, whether through a doorway or overhead door, you must bring the lift to a complete stop before going through the entry. You must walk around the entire lift looking for any obstacles. Be sure to check the height of the cage vs the height of the entry. Be sure to check the width of the lift vs the width of the entry. Only when that has been completed and you are sure there are no potential contact points may you continue forward with the lift. If there is trouble with the lift, please call the number on the side of the equipment for support and let Staley Technologies know of the issues.**\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**MATERIALS**\n\n**QTY DESCRIPTION**\n\n=======================\n\n250’ CAT6, WH, Plenum\n\n1 1 Port Faceplate\n\n1 RJ45\n\n1 5’ CAT6 Patch Cables Blue\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**TOOLS**\n\n\\---------\n\nTech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:\n\nLAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE\n\nUSB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR\n\nUSB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE\n\nPRECISE SCREWDRIVERS\n\nPUNCH TOOL W 66/110 BLADES\n\nWIRE STRIPPERS\n\nCRIMPER\n\nTONER\n\nLABELMAKER\n\nCABLE TESTER\n\nSTANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)\n\n8’ to 10’ LADDER\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n **NOTES**\n\n\\* White, Plenum CAT6 cable is required for all permanent cable runs.\n\n\\*\\* Velcro on ALL non-permanent wire management. Including power cords and AC Adapters.\n\n\\*\\* DO NOT install any surface mount boxes in the MDF or any IDF's.\n\n\\*\\* If ports don’t exist, you will need to install a new 24-port patch panel.\n\n.\n\nATTENTION: Any IDF's in the Club with surface mount boxes must be corrected.\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n **TASKS**\n\n.\n\n1\\) Meet with store personnel/management and introduce yourself.\n\n a) Review details of service requests with store personnel/management.\n\n.\n\n2\\) Troubleshoot the network cable run from PC in**Receiving** to the customers nearest IDF or MDF.\n\n a) Capture before pictures of the equipment and work area.\n\n b) Test network cable and determine faults. Repair as needed.\n\n\\- Test the cable.\n\n\\- Repair as needed.\n\n\\- Test the cable again to verify it has been repaired.\n\n c) If cable is damaged beyond repair, you will need to run a new drop.\n\n\\- Run 1 new data cable from the nearest IDF/MDF to PC location\n\n\\- Terminate/Test/Label new data cable\n\n\\- Patch in the newly installed data cable per site guidelines.\n\n d) If cable is confirmed to be good, Deli computer will boot up\n\n e) Make sure **PC in Receiving** is connected to a switch port mentioned in the “**Switch Ports:”** section of the work order.\n\n.\n\nIDF: \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ Patch Panel# \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ Port# \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ => Switch Name: \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_Port# \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n.\n\nTEST RESULTS FOR EACH CABLE(S) WILL BE REQUIRED AT CHECKOUT.\n\n.\n\n3\\) Contact BJ's Support at 833-722-3102 Opt. 1 and verify the device is connected to the network**.** If the tech remains on hold for 10 minutes or longer when calling into the BJ’s support desk, the tech should then call into the Staley support desk 501-320-4738. SSD will send an email with the technician’s name and phone number along with an explanation that they are onsite and need assistance.\n\n.\n\nFailure to do so will result in a penalty.\n\n4\\) Required Pictures:\n\n a) **PC in** **Receiving**\n\n b) Patch Panel ports\n\n c) Switch ports\n\n d) **CABLE TEST RESULTS**\n\n e) . Tech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\n.\n\nIf any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\nUsually, they will be in the following places:\n\nIDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office\n\nMDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club\n\n.\n\nPictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled\n\nExample: Club211IDF1before, Club211IDF1after and so on","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T21:45","end":"2026-10-08T25:45"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.94523465480207},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Thu, Oct 8, 9:45 PM\nChecked: Thu, Oct 8, Fri, Oct 9, Mon, Oct 12 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","sum