ST FOLLOW THE WORK INSTRUCTIONS TO BE SUCCESSFUL.***</strong></p><ul><li>Confirm you have the required tools. (listed work instruction tools are a MUST)</li><li>Review the Work Instructions prior to arriving onsite</li><li>Covid safe PPE and&nbsp;<strong>Professional work behavior expected onsite at all times</strong></li><li><strong>Ensure timely arrival on-site, check in with the site POC</strong></li><li><strong>Locate AccuVax kiosk and confirm serial number</strong></li></ul><p>Call TruMed Support and review the Scope of Work if you have any questions or concerns, if you are having issues reaching Support call Darrell (858) 240-5229 to expedite help.</p><ul><li><strong>Never</strong> remove the interior panel unless directed by TruMed Support Tech</li><li><strong>Never</strong> move the robot by hand unless directed TruMed Support Tech</li><li><strong>ALWAYS&nbsp;</strong>fully assemble the unit after you are done</li><li><strong>This repair can take 2-4 hours</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>If you have time constraints state them up front</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(182, 66, 76);\">Travel &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(182, 66, 76);\"> Travel expense under 60 miles round trip, or over .70 / mile, will not be approved. All requests must be pre-approved via counteroffer.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Payments are processed within a reasonable timeframe following completion of services.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work OVERVIEW**\n\nReported Issues: \\*\\*must bring heat gun and duct tape\\*\\*  \nReplace drip tray for larger one  \nMelt ice and add insulation tape as needed  \nVerify area is dry before adding insulation tubing  \nAPPLY DUCT TAPE TO INSULATION  \nPerform PM  \nPerform leak check. Tracking: No Parts Required\n\n**PM/Leak Check**\n\n**﻿Video Tutorials Below**\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**You MUST have the tools listed in the file: TOOLS REQUIRED TO GET PAID.**\n\n**Scope Specific Tools**\n\n- Heat Gun\n- T20 Torx Driver\n- T10 Torx Driver\n- 2.5mm Allen key\n- 4 mm Allen key or Flat Head Screwdriver\n- **DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS**\n\n **Essential Hardware**\n\n- **Torx tools**\n- T20 Torx Driver\n- T10 Torx Driver\n- T5 Torx Driver\n- 1.3 mm driver\n- Sharpie\n- 4mm 2.5mm Allen wrench set\n- T20, T10, T8 Driver or T-Tool\n- Torx key set (T20, T15, T10, T8, T5)\n- Mini ratchet with T30, T20, T15, T10, T8, T5 bits\n- Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool\n- Digital multimeter / voltmeter\n- Handheld vacuum\n- Needle-nose pliers\n- Standard pliers\n- Channel-lock pliers\n- 4\" (small) zip ties\n- Electrical tape\n- Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)\n\n**Cleaning & Advanced Repair**\n\n- Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)\n- Heat gun (required for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Alcohol wipes\n- Window cleaner\n- Paper towels\n- Nitrile gloves\n- Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws\n- 10-amp automotive fuse\n- 15-amp automotive fuse\n\n**Convenience & Specialty Tools**\n\n- Sharpie or permanent marker\n- EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor\n- Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)\n- Tool bag or hard case carrier\n- Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)\n\n**Professional Conduct Requirements**\n\n- Arrive fit for duty\n- No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work\n- No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite\n- Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited\n- Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is obtained\n- Comply with all customer site policies, security requirements, and safety procedures\n\n**Physical Requirements**\n\n- Ability to safely lift up to 30 lbs. overhead\n- Ability to safely lift up to 60 lbs. at ground level\n- Ability to kneel, crouch, bend, and work at floor level for extended periods\n- Ability to work in pharmacies, clinics, healthcare facilities, offices, equipment rooms, and commercial environments\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Professional and clean attire. No hats or baseball caps; only collared shirts without business logos are allowed.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*YOU MUST FOLLOW THE WORK INSTRUCTIONS TO BE SUCCESSFUL.\\*\\*\\***\n\n- Confirm you have the required tools. (listed work instruction tools are a MUST)\n- Review the Work Instructions prior to arriving onsite\n- Covid safe PPE and **Professional work behavior expected onsite at all times**\n- **Ensure timely arrival on-site, check in with the site POC**\n- **Locate AccuVax kiosk and confirm serial number**\n\nCall TruMed Support and review the Scope of Work if you have any questions or concerns, if you are having issues reaching Support call Darrell (858) 240-5229 to expedite help.\n\n- **Never** remove the interior panel unless directed by TruMed Support Tech\n- **Never** move the robot by hand unless directed TruMed Support Tech\n- **ALWAYS** fully assemble the unit after you are done\n- **This repair can take 2-4 hours**. **If you have time constraints state them up front**.\n\n**Travel & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** Travel expense under 60 miles round trip, or over .70 / mile, will not be approved. All requests must be pre-approved via counteroffer.\n\n**Payments are processed within a reasonable timeframe following completion of services.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T09:00","end":"2026-10-13T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-13T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":195},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11.071242433163944},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.0