{"job":{"id":"5905934304","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance***","description":"\"Requesting assistance to:<br><br>1) Locate new Granite-provided broadband and or/ DIA service<br>2) Extend new service to Burlington’s network rack/cabinet (if needed)<br>3) Test/validate new service<br>4) Confirm with carrier that modem/router onsite is set to IP Passthrough/Bridge modem<br>5) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) modem and/or FlexEdge router to new EdgebootPro equipment for power in accordance to port mapping guide listed below.<br>6) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) and EdgebootPro to existing Burlington-provided Fortinet firewall ethernet ports in accordance to port mapping guide listed below.<br>7) Confirm AC and ethernet connectivity via Edgeboot.io<br>8) Once complete, request Granite Field Service technician to contact Burlington’s Managed Service Provider (Acuative) to perform health check on applicable Fortinet firewall ports new equipment is now connected to<br><br>***NETWORK DIAGRAM ATTACHED AS REFERENCED***<br><br>***DO NOT ADJUST BURLINGTON EDGEBOOT PROFILE UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES***<br><br>***NETWORK CUTOVER TO TAKE PLACE AT LATER DATE***<br><br>***TECHNICIAN MUST CALL INTO ACTIVATIONS AND THEN MERGE ACCUATIVE INTO CALL FOR A SIGN OFF CODE***<br><br>***ALL DIA SERVICES FOR BURLINGTON INCLUDES A FLEXEDGE DEVICE REGARDLESS WHETHER ON OR OFF-NET.***<br><br>***EDGEBOOT ETH 0 TO BE USED FOR MONITORING NEW INTERNET SERVICE, ETH 1 TO PROVIDE NEW LTE SERVICE. IMPORTANT- ETH1 on Edgeboot Pro is configured as LAN by default.***<br><br>New service details are below:\"<br>Customer:Burlington<br><br>Site Type:C-1<br><br>Acuative NOC Phone Number:1-888-835-7687, Option 1<br><br>WAN Details:<br>Type:Cable<br>ISP:Spectrum<br>Bandwidth:1G/50<br>Circuit ID:8349100122568943<br>Demarc:C4:50:9C:91:81:E8<br>IP:Dynamic<br>GW:Dynamic<br>Su