{"job":{"id":20125609,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TeleSol IT B.V.","title":"T105886: install Spectrum Service (1G speeds ,Anydesk, Zoho Assist, Teamviewer installed; portable hotspot; console cable)","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">You are required to provide your email address</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"> so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR).&nbsp;</span>Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.</li><li><strong>Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.</strong> If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The bridge will open at the top of the hour. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.</span></li><li><strong>Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent</strong>. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!</strong></li><li>Please <strong>introduce yourself</strong> as working on behalf of Telesol Group for<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></strong><strong>.</strong> The equipment being installed is for&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></span>.</li><li><strong>Never use long distance calls </strong>unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Work Type: Professional Install</p><p>Conference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.</p><p>Additional task details provided in&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of work</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">We have already installed the service and equipment, HOWEVER, the speed was not working well. We got Spectrum to do some fixing and troubleshooting. Please retest speed.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\"><del>*** </del>Engineer once the order is done please fill out the MONITORING TAB.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Please install Spectrum Service with GTT Engineer remotely on the bridge.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Demarc is: Wireless MAC: 74:37:5f:2f:80:f1</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Wireless Make: SercommCorporation</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Wireless Model: sax1v1r</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Data Mac: 74:37:5f:2f:80:f1</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Data Make: SercommCorporation</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Data Model: sax1v1r</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Spectrum Service ID: 8349100131550320</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Tech will need laptop supporting 1G speeds, Please have Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed; portable hotspot; AND console cable – PLEASE MAKE SURE.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Required Tool List for any GTT Request:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">The following equipment must be taken as standard to all interventions:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, screw drivers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Label Maker</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Mobile phone with charger</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk): Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Cisco micro USB to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Server Rack Screws</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- (4-6) Ethernet cables</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">- Fiber Jumpers are also preferred but not required:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cable(s)</span></p><p><strong><u>Special access requirements (if any)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Special tools (if any)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tool List</strong></p><ul><li>Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)</li><li>Mobile phone with charger</li><li>Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</li><li>Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</li><li>Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to <strong>1000 Mbps (1G)</strong>, Teamveiwer software installed</li><li>Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)</li><li>Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):</li><li>Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</li><li>1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</li><li>Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</li><li>(4-6) Ethernet cables</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Preferred but not required</em></strong></p><ul><li>SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables</li><li>Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process</strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;noc@telesolgroup.com</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Contact</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\"><em>&nbsp;number - ​USA Toll-free:&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em><u><del>** ***** ********</del></u></em></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"- **All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol.** Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.\n- **You are required to provide your email address** so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR). Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.\n- **Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.** If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.\n- **The bridge will open at the top of the hour.** In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.\n- **Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent**. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.\n- **The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!**\n- Please **introduce yourself** as working on behalf of Telesol Group for **\\*\\*\\*****.** The equipment being installed is for \\*\\*\\*.\n- **Never use long distance calls** unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.\n\nWork Type: Professional Install\n\nConference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.\n\nAdditional task details provided in *Confidential Information* section below.\n\n**Scope of work**\n\nWe have already installed the service and equipment, HOWEVER, the speed was not working well. We got Spectrum to do some fixing and troubleshooting. Please retest speed.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Engineer once the order is done please fill out the MONITORING TAB.\n\nPlease install Spectrum Service with GTT Engineer remotely on the bridge.\n\nDemarc is: Wireless MAC: 74:37:5f:2f:80:f1\n\nWireless Make: SercommCorporation\n\nWireless Model: sax1v1r\n\nData Mac: 74:37:5f:2f:80:f1\n\nData Make: SercommCorporation\n\nData Model: sax1v1r\n\nSpectrum Service ID: 8349100131550320\n\nTech will need laptop supporting 1G speeds, Please have Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed; portable hotspot; AND console cable – PLEASE MAKE SURE.\n\nRequired Tool List for any GTT Request:\n\nThe following equipment must be taken as standard to all interventions:\n\n\\- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, screw drivers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.)\n\n\\- Label Maker\n\n\\- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot).\n\n\\- Mobile phone with charger\n\n\\- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n\n\\- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)\n\n\\- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk): Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed\n\n\\- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:\n\n\\- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use\n\n\\- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco micro USB to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Server Rack Screws\n\n\\- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n\n\\- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Fiber Jumpers are also preferred but not required:\n\nSC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cable(s)\n\n**Special access requirements (if any)**\n\n**Special tools (if any)**\n\n**Required Tool List**\n\n- Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment\n- Label Maker\n- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)\n- Mobile phone with charger\n- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)\n- Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to **1000 Mbps (1G)**, Teamveiwer software installed\n- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)\n- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):\n- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:\n- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use\n- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter\n- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n***Preferred but not required***\n\n- SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables\n- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.\n\n**Escalation Process**\n\n- ***Any issues or questions should be escalated to noc@telesolgroup.com***\n- ***Contact*** ***number - ​USA Toll-free:*** ***\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\****","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T11:30","end":"2026-10-13T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.38848859942174},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"}