{"job":{"id":20125779,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Computech Technology Services","title":"Need A Technician Onsite to Reconfigure Router w/Remote Support - See Description","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST&nbsp;*<u>CALL <del>***** ********</del>* OR TEXT *<del>***** ********</del>*</u>&nbsp;TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.</strong></p><p>We need a technician to visit our clients site to reconfigure the router onsite. Router is a TP-Link Omada, and tech will need to be familiar with typical router DHCP functions. Tech <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> have a laptop in order to assist with remote configuration.</p><p><strong>Tech will work with the customers remote network admin <del>******** ****** ************ ** ************</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Materials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.</p><p><strong>Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Punch Tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Push/Pull Rods</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Ladder(s)</li><li>Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)</li></ul><p><strong>Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):</strong></p><ul><li>​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks</li><li>External Keystone Biscuits</li><li>Keystone Faceplates</li><li>Mudrings</li><li>Misc Patch Cable(s)</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.</li><li>Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.</li><li>Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.</li><li>ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.</li></ul><p><strong>Material Compensation:</strong></p><p>PLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:</p><p>Item - Pre-Approved Pricing</p><p>Cat5e Riser - $0.18ft</p><p>Cat5e Plenum - $0.22ft</p><p>Cat6 Riser - $0.25ft</p><p>Cat6 Plenum - $0.28ft</p><p>RG59/RG6 - $0.12ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Siamese RG59 - $0.15ft</p><p>Cat5e Jack - $3.00ea</p><p>Cat6 Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- $3.75ea</p><p>Faceplate - $1.30ea</p><p>Surface Mount Box - $1.50ea</p><p>Patch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea</p><p>BNC Connectors - $3.00ea</p><p>Modular Plug - $0.55ea</p><p>Power Strip - $6.00ea</p><p>4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea</p><p>2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea</p><p>Cable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea</p><p>Patch Panel - Negotiable/at cost</p><p>Telco 66block - Negotiable/at cost</p><p><br></p><p>Tech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.</p><p>At ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.</p>","markdown":"**Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST \\*CALL \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* OR TEXT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.**\n\nWe need a technician to visit our clients site to reconfigure the router onsite. Router is a TP-Link Omada, and tech will need to be familiar with typical router DHCP functions. Tech **MUST** have a laptop in order to assist with remote configuration.\n\n**Tech will work with the customers remote network admin \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nMaterials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.\n\n**Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:**\n\n- Punch Tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Toner\n- Buttset\n- Push/Pull Rods\n- Fish Tape\n- Ladder(s)\n- Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)\n\n**Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):**\n\n- ​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable\n- Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks\n- External Keystone Biscuits\n- Keystone Faceplates\n- Mudrings\n- Misc Patch Cable(s)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.\n- Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.\n- Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.\n- ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.\n\n**Material Compensation:**\n\nPLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:\n\nItem - Pre-Approved Pricing\n\nCat5e Riser - $0.18ft\n\nCat5e Plenum - $0.22ft\n\nCat6 Riser - $0.25ft\n\nCat6 Plenum - $0.28ft\n\nRG59/RG6 - $0.12ft\n\nSiamese RG59 - $0.15ft\n\nCat5e Jack - $3.00ea\n\nCat6 Jack - $3.75ea\n\nFaceplate - $1.30ea\n\nSurface Mount Box - $1.50ea\n\nPatch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea\n\nBNC Connectors - $3.00ea\n\nModular Plug - $0.55ea\n\nPower Strip - $6.00ea\n\n4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea\n\n2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea\n\nCable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea\n\nPatch Panel - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTelco 66block - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.\n\nAt ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10