{"job":{"id":20126252,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"Wal-Mart [5292 LPR], CCTV Tech","description":{"html":"<p>THE TECHNICIAN WILL WORK WITH WACHTER CCTV SUPPORT TO BRING BACK THE LPR19 CAMERA BY USING THE TROUBLE SHOOTING STEPS REQUIRED BY THE WAL-MART LPR TEAM GUIDELINES AND ALSO ADJUST THE FOV. THE FOV MUST BE APPROVED BY THE WAL-MART LPR TEAM BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE.</p><p><strong>**********DO NOT CALL WAL-MART GS SERVICES**********S</strong></p><p><strong>Tech must work with Wachter CCTV support to 3-way call into GS services team to verify view 856-222-0643 - Option 1, put 131153. Please escalate if you have any issues contacting the CCTV support team to get these views verified. If you are waiting more than 15 minutes, please escalate.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Wachter PM team can provide all prints, maps, and layouts needed to service</strong></p><p>Walmart LPR Technician Troubleshooting &amp; Site Visit Requirements</p><p>Required Tools and Equipment</p><p>Technician must have the following tools available onsite:</p><p>•\tIPC Tester</p><p>•\tLaptop</p><p>•\tCable Tester</p><p>•\tVoltage Meter</p><p>•\tCamera Tester</p><p>•\tRJ-45 Crimp Tool</p><p>•\tRJ-45 Tips</p><p>•\tBNC Connectors</p><p>Required Check-In and Project Coordinator Contact</p><p>After checking in with the bridge, the technician must contact Project Coordinator Thomas Cope at:</p><p>Thomas Cope: 479-257-2392</p><p>The technician must also contact Thomas before leaving the site after checking out on the bridge to confirm that nothing else is needed or required.</p><p>Support Phone Numbers</p><p>Wachter CCTV Support: 856-222-0643</p><p>•\tSelect Option 1</p><p>•\tEnter Job # 131153</p><p>Wren: 1-800-881-2249</p><p>Distribution Center (DC) Network Operations Center (NOC): 479-802-5458</p><p>•\tSelect Option 1</p><p>•\tSelect Option 1</p><p>Store Network Operations Center (NOC): 479-277-4126</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Troubleshooting Requirements</p><p>1. Follow Walmart LPR Program Guidelines</p><p>Technicians must follow all guidelines and troubleshooting procedures outlined in the Walmart LPR Program documents, including all troubleshooting steps, FOV requirements, installation requirements, and other applicable procedures.</p><p>2. Notify CCTV Support of LPR Requirements</p><p>When contacting Wachter CCTV Support, the technician must inform them that the Walmart LPR Program documents are being followed. This is required to ensure the technician and support team are working from the same requirements and procedures.</p><p>3. Troubleshoot the Complete Camera System</p><p>The technician is responsible for troubleshooting the camera and all other equipment associated with the camera system, when applicable, including:</p><p>•\tCamera</p><p>•\tUbiquiti AP</p><p>•\tInjector</p><p>•\tConverter</p><p>•\tSolar Panel</p><p>•\tGridless Unit</p><p>•\tWireless Bridge</p><p>Solar-Powered Pole Cameras</p><p>If the camera is part of a solar-powered setup on a pole, the technician must test the following at the pole using a laptop:</p><p>•\tCamera</p><p>•\tUbiquiti AP</p><p>•\tConverter</p><p>•\tNetwork connectivity</p><p>The technician must also check the wireless bridge located on the store side.</p><p>If trees or other obstructions may be interfering with the wireless signal, the technician must provide photos documenting the issue and showing that the APs do not have a connection.</p><p>Camera Short-Cabled to Switch or Pole</p><p>If the camera is short cabled directly to the switch and/or pole, the technician must provide photos showing that the camera is online.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Replacement Part Requirements</p><p>4. Required Model and Serial Number Photos</p><p>If replacement parts are determined to be necessary, the technician must provide clear photos of them:</p><p>•\tModel number of the bad camera</p><p>•\tSerial numbers of the bad camera</p><p>•\tModel number of the Gridless Unit, when applicable</p><p>•\tSerial number of the Gridless Unit, when applicable</p><p>These photos require deliverables for replacement parts.</p><p>5. Document Support Contacts</p><p>The technician must obtain and document the name of every person spoken with during troubleshooting, including:</p><p>•\tWachter CCTV Support</p><p>•\tGridless Support</p><p>•\tNetwork Operations/NOC</p><p>•\tWren</p><p>•\tAny other support personnel involved</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Return Trip Requirements</p><p>6. Document Everything Needed for a Return Trip</p><p>If a return trip is required, the technician must provide complete details regarding what is needed to complete the work.</p><p>This must include, when applicable:</p><p>•\tParts required</p><p>•\tQuantity of each part</p><p>•\tCable type and amount required</p><p>•\tOther materials required</p><p>•\tTools or equipment required</p><p>•\tEstimated labor/time needed</p><p>•\tPreferred work time-based on-site requirements</p><p>•\tAP or Manager contact information</p><p>•\tAny site access requirements</p><p>•\tAny other information needed to schedule and complete the return trip</p><p>Any return trip must be discussed with the Project Coordinator (PC) before proceeding.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>RMA / Warranty Replacement Requirements</p><p>7. RMA Parts Must Be Returned</p><p>If the technician is replacing a camera or Gridless Unit under an RMA/warranty replacement, the defective part must be shipped back using the return address provided on the supplied return shipping label.</p><p>If a return shipping label is not included with the replacement part, the technician must contact the Project Coordinator listed in the contact information to obtain one.</p><p>Once the defective RMA part is boxed and ready for shipment, the technician must provide:</p><p>1.\tA photo showing the part properly boxed and ready for shipment.</p><p>2.\tA drop-off receipt showing that the RMA return has been shipped.</p><p>No RMA part may be left onsite under any circumstances.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Required Test Results and Photos</p><p>8. Document All Testing</p><p>Photos and/or screenshots of all applicable test results must be provided with the completed service documentation.</p><p>Required documentation may include:</p><p>•\tScreenshots showing cameras online</p><p>•\tCable test results</p><p>•\tCamera tester results</p><p>•\tVoltage readings/results</p><p>•\tPhotos of the Gridless Unit showing the status lights</p><p>•\tPhotos of APs and associated equipment</p><p>•\tPhotos of network connections</p><p>•\tPhotos of any identified damage or obstructions</p><p>•\tPhotos of model and serial numbers when replacement parts are required</p><p>All test results must be clearly documented and submitted.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Camera FOV Requirements</p><p>9. FOV Adjustment and Approval</p><p>The FOV (Field of View) of every camera listed in the work order must be adjusted with Wachter CCTV Support.</p><p>After the FOV has been adjusted:</p><p>1.\tWachter CCTV Support must provide screenshots of the adjusted FOVs.</p><p>2.\tThe screenshots must be sent to the Walmart LPR Team for approval.</p><p>3.\tThe technician must receive confirmation that the FOVs have been approved before leaving the site.</p><p>The technician must not leave the site until FOV approval has been obtained for all cameras listed in the work order.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Final Site Closeout</p><p>10. Final Call with Project Coordinator</p><p>Before leaving the site, the technician must:</p><p>1.\tComplete all required troubleshooting and testing.</p><p>2.\tConfirm all cameras and associated equipment are functioning as required.</p><p>3.\tConfirm all required FOV adjustments have been completed and approved.</p><p>4.\tConfirm all required photos, screenshots, and test results have been obtained.</p><p>5.\tCheck out with the bridge.</p><p>6.\tAfter checking out with the bridge, call Project Coordinator Thomas Cope at 479-257-2392.</p><p>7.\tConfirm with Thomas that nothing else is needed or required before leaving the site.</p><p>Technicians must not leave the site without completing the final call with the Project Coordinator.</p>","markdown":"THE TECHNICIAN WILL WORK WITH WACHTER CCTV SUPPORT TO BRING BACK THE LPR19 CAMERA BY USING THE TROUBLE SHOOTING STEPS REQUIRED BY THE WAL-MART LPR TEAM GUIDELINES AND ALSO ADJUST THE FOV. THE FOV MUST BE APPROVED BY THE WAL-MART LPR TEAM BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*DO NOT CALL WAL-MART GS SERVICES\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*S**\n\n**Tech must work with Wachter CCTV support to 3-way call into GS services team to verify view 856-222-0643 - Option 1, put 131153. Please escalate if you have any issues contacting the CCTV support team to get these views verified. If you are waiting more than 15 minutes, please escalate.**\n\n**Wachter PM team can provide all prints, maps, and layouts needed to service**\n\nWalmart LPR Technician Troubleshooting & Site Visit Requirements\n\nRequired Tools and Equipment\n\nTechnician must have the following tools available onsite:\n\n• IPC Tester\n\n• Laptop\n\n• Cable Tester\n\n• Voltage Meter\n\n• Camera Tester\n\n• RJ-45 Crimp Tool\n\n• RJ-45 Tips\n\n• BNC Connectors\n\nRequired Check-In and Project Coordinator Contact\n\nAfter checking in with the bridge, the technician must contact Project Coordinator Thomas Cope at:\n\nThomas Cope: 479-257-2392\n\nThe technician must also contact Thomas before leaving the site after checking out on the bridge to confirm that nothing else is needed or required.\n\nSupport Phone Numbers\n\nWachter CCTV Support: 856-222-0643\n\n• Select Option 1\n\n• Enter Job # 131153\n\nWren: 1-800-881-2249\n\nDistribution Center (DC) Network Operations Center (NOC): 479-802-5458\n\n• Select Option 1\n\n• Select Option 1\n\nStore Network Operations Center (NOC): 479-277-4126\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nTroubleshooting Requirements\n\n1\\. Follow Walmart LPR Program Guidelines\n\nTechnicians must follow all guidelines and troubleshooting procedures outlined in the Walmart LPR Program documents, including all troubleshooting steps, FOV requirements, installation requirements, and other applicable procedures.\n\n2\\. Notify CCTV Support of LPR Requirements\n\nWhen contacting Wachter CCTV Support, the technician must inform them that the Walmart LPR Program documents are being followed. This is required to ensure the technician and support team are working from the same requirements and procedures.\n\n3\\. Troubleshoot the Complete Camera System\n\nThe technician is responsible for troubleshooting the camera and all other equipment associated with the camera system, when applicable, including:\n\n• Camera\n\n• Ubiquiti AP\n\n• Injector\n\n• Converter\n\n• Solar Panel\n\n• Gridless Unit\n\n• Wireless Bridge\n\nSolar-Powered Pole Cameras\n\nIf the camera is part of a solar-powered setup on a pole, the technician must test the following at the pole using a laptop:\n\n• Camera\n\n• Ubiquiti AP\n\n• Converter\n\n• Network connectivity\n\nThe technician must also check the wireless bridge located on the store side.\n\nIf trees or other obstructions may be interfering with the wireless signal, the technician must provide photos documenting the issue and showing that the APs do not have a connection.\n\nCamera Short-Cabled to Switch or Pole\n\nIf the camera is short cabled directly to the switch and/or pole, the technician must provide photos showing that the camera is online.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nReplacement Part Requirements\n\n4\\. Required Model and Serial Number Photos\n\nIf replacement parts are determined to be necessary, the technician must provide clear photos of them:\n\n• Model number of the bad camera\n\n• Serial numbers of the bad camera\n\n• Model number of the Gridless Unit, when applicable\n\n• Serial number of the Gridless Unit, when applicable\n\nThese photos require deliverables for replacement parts.\n\n5\\. Document Support Contacts\n\nThe technician must obtain and document the name of every person spoken with during troubleshooting, including:\n\n• Wachter CCTV Support\n\n• Gridless Support\n\n• Network Operations/NOC\n\n• Wren\n\n• Any other support personnel involved\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nReturn Trip Requirements\n\n6\\. Document Everything Needed for a Return Trip\n\nIf a return trip is required, the technician must provide complete details regarding what is needed to complete the work.\n\nThis must include, when applicable:\n\n• Parts required\n\n• Quantity of each part\n\n• Cable type and amount required\n\n• Other materials required\n\n• Tools or equipment required\n\n• Estimated labor/time needed\n\n• Preferred work time-based on-site requirements\n\n• AP or Manager contact information\n\n• Any site access requirements\n\n• Any other information needed to schedule and complete the return trip\n\nAny return trip must be discussed with the Project Coordinator (PC) before proceeding.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nRMA / Warranty Replacement Requirements\n\n7\\. RMA Parts Must Be Returned\n\nIf the technician is replacing a camera or Gridless Unit under an RMA/warranty replacement, the defective part must be shipped back using the return address provided on the supplied return shipping label.\n\nIf a return shipping label is not included with the replacement part, the technician must contact the Project Coordinator listed in the contact information to obtain one.\n\nOnce the defective RMA part is boxed and ready for shipment, the technician must provide:\n\n1\\. A photo showing the part properly boxed and ready for shipment.\n\n2\\. A drop-off receipt showing that the RMA return has been shipped.\n\nNo RMA part may be left onsite under any circumstances.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nRequired Test Results and Photos\n\n8\\. Document All Testing\n\nPhotos and/or screenshots of all applicable test results must be provided with the completed service documentation.\n\nRequired documentation may include:\n\n• Screenshots showing cameras online\n\n• Cable test results\n\n• Camera tester results\n\n• Voltage readings/results\n\n• Photos of the Gridless Unit showing the status lights\n\n• Photos of APs and associated equipment\n\n• Photos of network connections\n\n• Photos of any identified damage or obstructions\n\n• Photos of model and serial numbers when replacement parts are required\n\nAll test results must be clearly documented and submitted.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nCamera FOV Requirements\n\n9\\. FOV Adjustment and Approval\n\nThe FOV (Field of View) of every camera listed in the work order must be adjusted with Wachter CCTV Support.\n\nAfter the FOV has been adjusted:\n\n1\\. Wachter CCTV Support must provide screenshots of the adjusted FOVs.\n\n2\\. The screenshots must be sent to the Walmart LPR Team for approval.\n\n3\\. The technician must receive confirmation that the FOVs have been approved before leaving the site.\n\nThe technician must not leave the site until FOV approval has been obtained for all cameras listed in the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nFinal Site Closeout\n\n10\\. Final Call with Project Coordinator\n\nBefore leaving the site, the technician must:\n\n1\\. Complete all required troubleshooting and testing.\n\n2\\. Confirm all cameras and associated equipment are functioning as required.\n\n3\\. Confirm all required FOV adjustments have been completed and approved.\n\n4\\. Confirm all required photos, screenshots, and test results have been obtained.\n\n5\\. Check out with the bridge.\n\n6\\. After checking out with the bridge, call Project Coordinator Thomas Cope at 479-257-2392.\n\n7\\. Confirm with Thomas that nothing else is needed or required before leaving the site.\n\nTechnicians must not leave the site without completing the final call with the Project Coordinator.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10-08T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":11.655358840675095},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Oct 8, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Thu, Oct 8, Fri, Oct 9, Mon, Oct 12 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summ