{"job":{"id":20126619,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CrossCom","title":"Walmart - Digital Lock 2026","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Note:  Visit is to run a cable from the closest IDF to the AP office.  Relocate the OKM device to the AP office from the IDF behind the customer service counter.</strong></p><p>Technician is required onsite to complete the following:&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Arrive at site, check in with the Crosscom Project Team @&nbsp;800-820-9229 then check in with store manager and present letter of authorization.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>2. Locate device to be installed, Usually held in AP office, Claims, or UPC office. Box 12x12x6 box and has a large white label saying: “Ecosystem Kit IR4 and Replace Plus side neon Yellow label”</strong></p><p><strong>NOTE: When calling into support, please have the following information available.</strong></p><ul><li>Switch name</li><li>Port number</li><li>MAC address</li><li>IP address</li><li>Physical location of the device if not in the AP office</li></ul><p>3. Identify if there is an existing cable in the AP office that can be used to connect the new device.</p><p>4.If an existing cable is available, the technician shall test and terminate the cable with a mod plug and connect to the new device.</p><p><strong>5. If no cable is available, the technician will run a new cable&nbsp;to the closest switch (approx. 100'). If a lift is required, Request to use store and move forward, if do not receive permission for daytime lift in area required, a return trip will be scheduled to complete the cable run after hours..</strong></p><p>6. Connect the cable to the provided device. Device to be placed on a desk or cabinet as agreed with AP office resources.</p><p>a. Run Set up on device using WM Install code 90124. before calling Verify screen displays Link: UP below connecting screen.</p><p>7. Work with CrossCom's L2 to provision port &amp; register MAC for the new device using VLAN 46.</p><p>8. Obtain manager's sign off.</p><p>9. Clean up and capture deliverables.</p><p>10. Check out with deployment support.</p><p><strong>****tech will need to provide the name of the switch ( for ex GM-1) port used , FULL MAC ADDRESS OF THE DEVICE</strong></p><p>*******Please be aware that per incident PENALTIES will apply as follows. Any penalties incurred will be deducted from technician payment.&nbsp;Technician agrees to these terms when accepting contract.*******</p><p>&nbsp;No Call/No Shows $150</p><p>&nbsp;Missing Sign Off $50 (after 2 days) $100 (after 8 days)</p><p>&nbsp;Leaving during the install $100</p><p>&nbsp;Failing to have CrossCom Badge. $50&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>* Trips: 1 technician will be required for 1 trip and the work will take place during normal business hours.</p><p>* Tools needed: Smartphone, standard hand tools, cable tester</p><p>* The technician will log in and out with CrossCom Project Team @ 800-820-9229..</p><p>* Deliverables will be required to validate work completion and quality. All deliverables must upload through vendor portal prior to leaving work site. Failure to provide deliverables will result in nonpayment.</p>","markdown":"**Note: Visit is to run a cable from the closest IDF to the AP office. Relocate the OKM device to the AP office from the IDF behind the customer service counter.**\n\nTechnician is required onsite to complete the following:\n\n**1. Arrive at site, check in with the Crosscom Project Team @ 800-820-9229 then check in with store manager and present letter of authorization.**\n\n**2. Locate device to be installed, Usually held in AP office, Claims, or UPC office. Box 12x12x6 box and has a large white label saying: “Ecosystem Kit IR4 and Replace Plus side neon Yellow label”**\n\n**NOTE: When calling into support, please have the following information available.**\n\n- Switch name\n- Port number\n- MAC address\n- IP address\n- Physical location of the device if not in the AP office\n\n3\\. Identify if there is an existing cable in the AP office that can be used to connect the new device.\n\n4.If an existing cable is available, the technician shall test and terminate the cable with a mod plug and connect to the new device.\n\n**5. If no cable is available, the technician will run a new cable to the closest switch (approx. 100'). If a lift is required, Request to use store and move forward, if do not receive permission for daytime lift in area required, a return trip will be scheduled to complete the cable run after hours..**\n\n6\\. Connect the cable to the provided device. Device to be placed on a desk or cabinet as agreed with AP office resources.\n\na. Run Set up on device using WM Install code 90124. before calling Verify screen displays Link: UP below connecting screen.\n\n7\\. Work with CrossCom's L2 to provision port & register MAC for the new device using VLAN 46.\n\n8\\. Obtain manager's sign off.\n\n9\\. Clean up and capture deliverables.\n\n10\\. Check out with deployment support.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*tech will need to provide the name of the switch ( for ex GM-1) port used , FULL MAC ADDRESS OF THE DEVICE**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Please be aware that per incident PENALTIES will apply as follows. Any penalties incurred will be deducted from technician payment. Technician agrees to these terms when accepting contract.\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n No Call/No Shows $150\n\n Missing Sign Off $50 (after 2 days) $100 (after 8 days)\n\n Leaving during the install $100\n\n Failing to have CrossCom Badge. $50\n\n\\* Trips: 1 technician will be required for 1 trip and the work will take place during normal business hours.\n\n\\* Tools needed: Smartphone, standard hand tools, cable tester\n\n\\* The technician will log in and out with CrossCom Project Team @ 800-820-9229..\n\n\\* Deliverables will be required to validate work completion and quality. All deliverables must upload through vendor portal prior to leaving work site. Failure to provide deliverables will result in nonpayment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T05:00","end":"2026-10-13T07:00"},"payRange":{"min":265,"max":265},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":25.23522108171556},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"displays\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:0