{"job":{"id":20127111,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SHI - Corp Services","title":"INC4477084 - KinderCare - Calls intermittently dropping","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***JOB REQUESTS COMPLETED BACKGROUND CHECK AND DRUG TEST***</strong></p><p><strong>***If working on 8*8 do not factory reset the system unless told by remote support***</strong></p><p><strong>﻿*** This location does not have VOIP! ***</strong></p><p><strong><u>Issue</u></strong></p><p>Calls intermittently dropping- happens randomly</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Calls intermittently dropping- happens randomly</p><p>Is the issue Telecom related? (Y)</p><p>If so, please list all lines at the center found in site info. (919) 954-7662 and 919 870 1704</p><p>What is the brand and model of phones at the center? AT&amp;T TL86103</p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>What has been done/Troubleshooting: LEC has come out on 9/22/26 and made repairs on their end but confirmed static and dropped calls may continue due to inside wiring. Also, center has recently replaced phones.</p><p>What we need from SHI: Please assess inside wiring and phone system to repair issue</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><p>Basic networking toolkit</p><p>Tester / Toner / Buzz phone</p><p>Cat6</p><p>RJ45 / RJ11</p><p>Wall jacks</p><p>Wall plates</p><p>Labeler</p><p>Velcro for cable management</p><p>Ladder</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Please call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite</span></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Material Reimbursement:</u></strong></p><p>Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot</p><p>Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea</p><p>Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea</p><p>Faceplate $3.50 / ea</p><p>Keystones $5.00/ea</p><p>Cable ends $2.50/ea</p><p>Velcro strips .75 cents each</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost above</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">NOTE: any cable runs performed - must include validation - labeling, pass/fail tests, and show cable length. Service loops - no longer than 10-12 ft. </span></li><li>Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*JOB REQUESTS COMPLETED BACKGROUND CHECK AND DRUG TEST\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*If working on 8\\*8 do not factory reset the system unless told by remote support\\*\\*\\***\n\n**﻿\\*\\*\\* This location does not have VOIP! \\*\\*\\***\n\n**Issue**\n\nCalls intermittently dropping- happens randomly\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nCalls intermittently dropping- happens randomly\n\nIs the issue Telecom related? (Y)\n\nIf so, please list all lines at the center found in site info. (919) 954-7662 and 919 870 1704\n\nWhat is the brand and model of phones at the center? AT&T TL86103\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhat has been done/Troubleshooting: LEC has come out on 9/22/26 and made repairs on their end but confirmed static and dropped calls may continue due to inside wiring. Also, center has recently replaced phones.\n\nWhat we need from SHI: Please assess inside wiring and phone system to repair issue\n\n **Required Tools Needed:**\n\nBasic networking toolkit\n\nTester / Toner / Buzz phone\n\nCat6\n\nRJ45 / RJ11\n\nWall jacks\n\nWall plates\n\nLabeler\n\nVelcro for cable management\n\nLadder\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nPlease call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nPolo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes\n\n**Material Reimbursement:**\n\nCat6 Cables .52 cents per foot\n\nCat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea\n\nCat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea\n\nFaceplate $3.50 / ea\n\nKeystones $5.00/ea\n\nCable ends $2.50/ea\n\nVelcro strips .75 cents each\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed\n- Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job\n- Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost above\n- NOTE: any cable runs performed - must include validation - labeling, pass/fail tests, and show cable length. Service loops - no longer than 10-12 ft.\n- Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T09:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-12T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7.989467864267257},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},