{"job":{"id":20126977,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Troubleshoot Power Issues for Self-Checkout Register #4 & 9 *power checking tools required*","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TRAVEL</u></strong></p><ul><li>Travel expense will not be approved after ticket is accepted. A counter-offer must be made and accepted in order for travel expense to be covered.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>START TIME</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>DO NOT ARRIVE ON SITE OR PERFORM ANY WORK PRIOR TO THE HARD START</strong></li><li>Start time is a hard start because Savers support will not be available until 8:00am MST and no work can be performed outside of support hours.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE</u></strong></p><ul><li>Contact the Work Order Manager to check in</li><li>Troubleshoot power issues for&nbsp;<strong><u>SCO 4 &amp; 9</u></strong>. Ensure that the power cable is good and connected correctly. Verify UPS is both receiving power from outlet and providing power to SCO. Ensure that the power button is not stuck. Refer to the attached troubleshooting guide for further details.</li><li>Perform test transaction with manager to ensure SCO is functioning as it should (reach out to the Technical Help contact if it doesn't; additional configuration may be needed).</li><li>Take a photo of the robot screen after repairs (refer to \"Robot Screen Instructions\" attached to this Field Nation work order)</li><li>Have the manager sign the TDX Tech work order (attached to this Field Nation work order) confirming completion of scope.</li><li>Contact the Work Order Manager to check out</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p><ul><li>Photo of SCO functioning</li><li>Photo of voided test transaction receipt</li><li>Photo of the completed and signed (by the technician and the manager) TDX Tech work order</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TOOLS / MATERIALS REQUIRED</u></strong></p><ul><li>USB Keyboard</li><li>TDX Tech work order (attached to this Field Nation work order &amp; must be submitted for payment)</li><li>Digital camera&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Basic cabling tool kit</li></ul>","markdown":"**TRAVEL**\n\n- Travel expense will not be approved after ticket is accepted. A counter-offer must be made and accepted in order for travel expense to be covered.\n\n**START TIME**\n\n- **DO NOT ARRIVE ON SITE OR PERFORM ANY WORK PRIOR TO THE HARD START**\n- Start time is a hard start because Savers support will not be available until 8:00am MST and no work can be performed outside of support hours.\n\n**SCOPE**\n\n- Contact the Work Order Manager to check in\n- Troubleshoot power issues for **SCO 4 & 9**. Ensure that the power cable is good and connected correctly. Verify UPS is both receiving power from outlet and providing power to SCO. Ensure that the power button is not stuck. Refer to the attached troubleshooting guide for further details.\n- Perform test transaction with manager to ensure SCO is functioning as it should (reach out to the Technical Help contact if it doesn't; additional configuration may be needed).\n- Take a photo of the robot screen after repairs (refer to \"Robot Screen Instructions\" attached to this Field Nation work order)\n- Have the manager sign the TDX Tech work order (attached to this Field Nation work order) confirming completion of scope.\n- Contact the Work Order Manager to check out\n\n**DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Photo of SCO functioning\n- Photo of voided test transaction receipt\n- Photo of the completed and signed (by the technician and the manager) TDX Tech work order\n\n**TOOLS / MATERIALS REQUIRED**\n\n- USB Keyboard\n- TDX Tech work order (attached to this Field Nation work order & must be submitted for payment)\n- Digital camera\n- Basic cabling tool kit","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T10:00","end":"2026-10-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":55},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLabo