{"job":{"id":20127831,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TruMed Systems","title":"Vaccine Management Machine - Heater Pan Swap - 01464","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work OVERVIEW</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Reported Issues: Perform Resistance Checks.<br/>De-ice unit.<br/>Swap parts if Resistance Checks failed.<br/>Ensure EPS is regreased properly.<br/>Assist with post repair tests. FedEx Tracking: 878275348359</span></p><p>Evaporator fan failure occurred. Clear the ice/grease buildup, troubleshoot the Evaporator fan. Replace the Heater pan assembly (if Applicable), Install Flow Balancer (if applicable). Install the Battery safety kit (insulator shield, inline fuse cable, rubber insulating edges/cable ties) (if Applicable)<strong> Must have Heat Gun, Voltage Meter and review and have tool's listed in the Work Instructions (AV0024_ Work Instruction_Repairs Behind EPS_Rev K.pdf) or you could be penalized or not paid for the Service Cal</strong>l</p><p><strong><em>High-quality photos of completed work are crucial for our engineering team. Please ensure that the photos are detailed, clear, and encompass all areas where ice buildup has occurred over time.</em></strong></p><p><strong>﻿Video Tutorials Below</strong></p><p>PAN JOB VIDEO:</p><p>https://youtu.be/aU2_NebvhpQART Part 1</p><p><br></p><p>https://youtu.be/06UWLcsTeA8 Part 2</p><p><br></p><p>https://youtu.be/nNNaMOXogcw Part 3</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*** ** **** *** **** ** *** **** </del></span><del>****************************</del></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*** ** ******* ******** **** *************</del></span><del>*******************************************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>You MUST have the tools listed in the file: TOOLS REQUIRED TO GET PAID.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope Specific Tools</strong></p><ul><li>PPE</li><li>Voltage Meter</li><li>T20 Torx Driver (10-inch)</li><li>T10 Torx Driver</li><li>T20 Torx Bit (¼\" or ⅜\" drive)</li><li>Ratchet with ¼\" or ⅜\" socket (compatible with T20 Torx bit)</li><li>Paper Towels</li><li>Heat Gun</li><li>Putty Knife</li><li>Digital Multimeter</li><li>Box Cutter / Utility Knife</li><li>Wire Cutters</li><li>Aluminum Tape</li><li>Alcohol Pads</li><li>Industrial Cotton Swabs</li><li>\"FAIL\" Stickers</li><li>Staples</li><li>Gloves</li></ul><p>Important: A ratchet and T20 Torx bit combination (or equivalent tool capable of accessing recessed fasteners) is mandatory for this work and must be available onsite.</p><ul><li>Mini Ratchet with Adjustable Gooseneck Head</li><li>¼\" or ⅜\" Socket Adapter (compatible with T20 Torx bit)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Essential Hardware</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Torx tools</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>T20 Torx Dri</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T10 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T5 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1.3 mm driver&nbsp;</li><li>Sharpie</li><li>6mm, 5mm, 4mm, 3mm, 2.5mm, 2mm Allen wrench set</li><li>T20, T10, T8 Driver or T-Tool</li><li>Torx key set (T20, T15, T10, T8, T5)</li><li>Mini ratchet with T30, T20, T15, T10, T8, T5 bits</li><li>Standard 4&ndash;6\" Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Wire stripping tool</li><li>Wire crimping tool</li><li>Wire butt connectors</li><li>13mm crescent wrench</li><li>Socket set with ratchet including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6.5mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">7mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">10mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">11mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">13mm</li><li>Digital multimeter / voltmeter</li><li>Handheld vacuum</li><li>Needle-nose pliers</li><li>Standard pliers</li><li>Channel-lock pliers</li><li>Extendable magnetic pickup tool for dropped screws</li><li>Tool magnetizer for retaining screws on driver heads</li><li>Utility knife</li><li>X-Acto knife</li><li>4\" (small) zip ties</li><li>Electrical tape</li><li>Suction cup (90 lb. rating)</li><li>Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)</li></ul><p><strong>Cleaning &amp; Advanced Repair</strong></p><ul><li>Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)</li><li>Heat gun (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Alcohol wipes</li><li>Window cleaner</li><li>Paper towels</li><li>Nitrile gloves</li><li>Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws</li><li>10-amp automotive fuse</li><li>15-amp automotive fuse</li></ul><p><strong>Convenience &amp; Specialty Tools</strong></p><ul><li>Sharpie or permanent marker</li><li>EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor</li><li>Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)</li><li>Tool bag or hard case carrier</li><li>Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Professional Conduct Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive fit for duty</li><li>No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work</li><li>No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite</li><li>Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited</li><li>Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is obtained</li><li>Comply with all customer site policies, security requirements, and safety procedures</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Ability to safely lift up to 30 lbs. overhead</li><li>Ability to safely lift up to 60 lbs. at ground level</li><li>Ability to kneel, crouch, bend, and work at floor level for extended periods</li><li>Ability to work in pharmacies, clinics, healthcare facilities, offices, equipment rooms, and commercial environments</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</strong>Profe