{"job":{"id":20127871,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Router Install & Cutover for GT Cylinder Exchange & Truck Repair - Dudley","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP &amp; Data Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>1 - Router</p>\n<p>Cutover over to new internet circuit</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached <strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.</li>\n<li>Contact support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>Network/cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n<li>Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install new equipment.</li>\n<li>Complete all tests on the checklist with support.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP & Data Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1 - Router\n\nCutover over to new internet circuit\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached **Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.\n- Contact support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- Network/cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n- Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install new equipment.\n- Complete all tests on the checklist with support.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00","end":"2026-10-08T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":56.45490252881845},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite ticket2"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.