{"job":{"id":20123888,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"GP - DMB Troubleshooting (Service Call)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE CHECK IN / OUT WITH CIS PRO SERVICE TEAM: (PLEASE NOTE YOU ONLY NEED TO CHECK IN WITH ONE OF US):<del>************</del></strong></p><p></p><p>TECHNICAL CONTACT: <del>*****************************************</del></p><p>LOCAL CONTACT: <del>***************************</del></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">*******</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">YOU WILL BE ASKED FOR YOU EMAIL AND WILL BE ADDED TO THE CHECK IN EMAIL AND ALL COMMUNICATION REGARDING DISPATCH IS TO BE DONE THROUGH CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN*****</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">If you have any questions not tech related to the dispatch call CIS for escalation to Project Manager</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><p>CIS needs (1) FST to assist with the following:</p><ol><li>Check in with CIS</li><li>Check in with the MOD</li><li>Check in on Email Chain created by CIS <ol><li>MB01 and MB03 is offline</li><li>manager on duty is unable to troubleshoot</li><li>Need to troubleshoot offline controllers</li><li>need to check power and ethernet cable connection.</li><li>need to ensure that network switch is on</li><li>manager on duty is unable to troubleshoot</li></ol></li><li>Assist with any additional troubleshooting requested by support</li><li><strong>Email tech support to confirm equipment worked on is ready for testing - someone will call you to walk through this</strong></li><li>Take Pictures of all work done onsite - <span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Must be before and after photos of all work done</span><ol><li>Email all pictures to tech support email chain for approval</li></ol></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Complete JotForm by clicking on this link </span>https://form.jotform.com/222515459741054 (This is not the Field Nation Survey)<ol><li>Exit code strictly for JotForm: <del>****</del></li><li>Please ensure you enter your email address to receive a email address <ol><li>Once email completion confirmation received, save a copy via PDF and send to tech support email chain for approval</li></ol></li></ol></li><li>When tech support approves pictures have send JotForm on email chain for exit code.</li><li>Once exit code is received call CIS to be released</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">TECH IS NOT TO LEAVE SITE UNTIL EXIT CODE IS RECEIVED FROM TECH SUPPORT - IF TECH LEAVES PRIOR TO GETTING EXIT CODE TECH MUST RETURN TO SITE - FAILURE TO DO SO WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT OF WO</strong></li><li>Check out with CIS - <span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">DO NOT CHECK OUT WITH CIS UNTIL EXIT CODE IS RECEIVED</span></li></ol><p> </p><p> </p><p><strong>Equipment required</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Laptop w/ Ethernet Port &amp; Charger</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Small Monitor</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">USB Keyboard</span></li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>10&#39; Ladder</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong> Materials</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">**Please have extras of all the below:</strong></p><ul><li>Cat6 Plenum cable (at least 200’)</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat6 Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">****NOTE: ALL PHOTOS MUST BE LABELED AS TO WHAT THE PICTURE IS WHEN UPLOADING TO WO - PENALTIES WILL BE APPLIED IF THIS IS NOT DONE*****</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>DELIVERABLES:</strong></p><ul><li>PHOTOS OF WORK DONE - EMAILED TO SUPPORT CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN</li><li>WORKMAN&#39;S COMP WAIVER (ATTACHED) UPLOADED TO FN WO</li><li>MANAGERS SIGN OFF (ATTACHED) EMAILED TO SUPPORT CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN AND FN WO</li></ul><p></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Before the tech leaves the site, they MUST call to check out with CIS PRO SERVICE TEAM in order to close the work order out - failure to do this will result in Penalty fees applied to work order.</strong></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE CHECK IN / OUT WITH CIS PRO SERVICE TEAM: (PLEASE NOTE YOU ONLY NEED TO CHECK IN WITH ONE OF US):\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nTECHNICAL CONTACT: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLOCAL CONTACT: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***YOU WILL BE ASKED FOR YOU EMAIL AND WILL BE ADDED TO THE CHECK IN EMAIL AND ALL COMMUNICATION REGARDING DISPATCH IS TO BE DONE THROUGH CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If you have any questions not tech related to the dispatch call CIS for escalation to Project Manager**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\nCIS needs (1) FST to assist with the following:\n\n1. Check in with CIS\n2. Check in with the MOD\n3. Check in on Email Chain created by CIS \n  1. MB01 and MB03 is offline\n  2. manager on duty is unable to troubleshoot\n  3. Need to troubleshoot offline controllers\n  4. need to check power and ethernet cable connection.\n  5. need to ensure that network switch is on\n  6. manager on duty is unable to troubleshoot\n4. Assist with any additional troubleshooting requested by support\n5. **Email tech support to confirm equipment worked on is ready for testing - someone will call you to walk through this**\n6. Take Pictures of all work done onsite - Must be before and after photos of all work done\n  1. Email all pictures to tech support email chain for approval\n7. Complete JotForm by clicking on this link <https://form.jotform.com/222515459741054> (This is not the Field Nation Survey)\n  1. Exit code strictly for JotForm: \\*\\*\\*\\*\n  2. Please ensure you enter your email address to receive a email address \n      1. Once email completion confirmation received, save a copy via PDF and send to tech support email chain for approval\n8. When tech support approves pictures have send JotForm on email chain for exit code.\n9. Once exit code is received call CIS to be released\n10. **TECH IS NOT TO LEAVE SITE UNTIL EXIT CODE IS RECEIVED FROM TECH SUPPORT - IF TECH LEAVES PRIOR TO GETTING EXIT CODE TECH MUST RETURN TO SITE - FAILURE TO DO SO WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT OF WO**\n11. Check out with CIS - DO NOT CHECK OUT WITH CIS UNTIL EXIT CODE IS RECEIVED\n\n**Equipment required**\n\n- Laptop w/ Ethernet Port & Charger\n- Small Monitor\n- USB Keyboard\n- Console Cable\n- Cable Tester\n- Fish Tape\n- Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- 10' Ladder\n\n **Materials**\n\n**\\*\\*Please have extras of all the below:**\n\n- Cat6 Plenum cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat6 Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Velcro Strips\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*NOTE: ALL PHOTOS MUST BE LABELED AS TO WHAT THE PICTURE IS WHEN UPLOADING TO WO - PENALTIES WILL BE APPLIED IF THIS IS NOT DONE\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**DELIVERABLES:**\n\n- PHOTOS OF WORK DONE - EMAILED TO SUPPORT CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN\n- WORKMAN'S COMP WAIVER (ATTACHED) UPLOADED TO FN WO\n- MANAGERS SIGN OFF (ATTACHED) EMAILED TO SUPPORT CHECK IN EMAIL CHAIN AND FN WO\n\n**Before the tech leaves the site, they MUST call to check out with CIS PRO SERVICE TEAM in order to close the work order out - failure to do this will result in Penalty fees applied to work order.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T10:00","end":"2026-10-08T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":320},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":80}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":36.96199310948261},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791420961277}
{"job":{"id":20129247,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240 Walgreens Printer Exchange - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. The specific scope is to exchange the existing printer with a replacement unit, testing the operations to ensure proper functionality and image quality. Then packing the old unit using the container from the replacement unit for pickup.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>CX3240<br />KZ4011515<br />Please open a service ticket for Walgreens #07505 in response to a Walgreens Corporate escalation. This location has had 6 service calls on their CX3240 in the past 3 months. I would like to request a printer swap due to the service history and escalation. Please schedule the call for RIMG.<br /><br />@Amy Berlew - swap pending your approval.<br /><br />Best regards,<br />David Smith<br />Tracking: 878329968773<br /><br />FIN: 223847<br /><br /></p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Operations Manual (attached to work order)</li><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Install Guide (attached to work order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li>Confirm the printer exchange tracking by going to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the printer exchange is delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Fuji CX3240 Assembly Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************</del></p><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Check in with the Manager on Duty. Inform them that you are representing Fujifilm Technical Services and that you are there to perform the CX3240F printer exchange, and ask them to locate the replacement unit.</li><li>Contact the support team at&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to confirm the steps needed to complete the exchange.</li><li>Follow the replacement process using the guide attached to this work order.</li><li>You will need 2 people (one per side) to lift the printer off the expansion trays safely. Please work with the MOD onsite for a second person to assist.</li><li>After completing the printer exchange<strong>&nbsp;, MAKE SURE</strong>&nbsp;that the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement printer and installed in the return printer.</li><li>After completing the printer exchange, confirm the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement unit and installed on the return unit.</li><li>Perform 2 test prints from each paper tray, totaling a minimum of 10 prints.</li><li>Contact our support team at&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;to confirm the deliverables and review the printer exchange return process.</li><li>Package the printer being returned following the steps provided in the exchange guide.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the (MOD), and get their signature.</li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the orange shipping caps removed from the replacement unit.</li><li>Image of the orange shipping caps installed on the return unit.</li><li>Images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.</li><li>Image of the printer in the return box with the cover off to confirm it is the right side up and seated in the bottom side of the packaging (handles located at the bottom).</li><li>Image each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <del>***** ********</del> and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. The specific scope is to exchange the existing printer with a replacement unit, testing the operations to ensure proper functionality and image quality. Then packing the old unit using the container from the replacement unit for pickup.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nCX3240  \nKZ4011515  \nPlease open a service ticket for Walgreens #07505 in response to a Walgreens Corporate escalation. This location has had 6 service calls on their CX3240 in the past 3 months. I would like to request a printer swap due to the service history and escalation. Please schedule the call for RIMG.  \n  \n@Amy Berlew - swap pending your approval.  \n  \nBest regards,  \nDavid Smith  \nTracking: 878329968773  \n  \nFIN: 223847\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Operations Manual (attached to work order)\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Install Guide (attached to work order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. Confirm the printer exchange tracking by going to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** the printer exchange is delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Fuji CX3240 Assembly Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Check in with the Manager on Duty. Inform them that you are representing Fujifilm Technical Services and that you are there to perform the CX3240F printer exchange, and ask them to locate the replacement unit.\n2. Contact the support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the steps needed to complete the exchange.\n3. Follow the replacement process using the guide attached to this work order.\n4. You will need 2 people (one per side) to lift the printer off the expansion trays safely. Please work with the MOD onsite for a second person to assist.\n5. After completing the printer exchange **, MAKE SURE** that the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement printer and installed in the return printer.\n6. After completing the printer exchange, confirm the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement unit and installed on the return unit.\n7. Perform 2 test prints from each paper tray, totaling a minimum of 10 prints.\n8. Contact our support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the deliverables and review the printer exchange return process.\n9. Package the printer being returned following the steps provided in the exchange guide.\n10. Complete the work order, check out with the (MOD), and get their signature.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the orange shipping caps removed from the replacement unit.\n- Image of the orange shipping caps installed on the return unit.\n- Images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.\n- Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.\n- Image of the printer in the return box with the cover off to confirm it is the right side up and seated in the bottom side of the packaging (handles located at the bottom).\n- Image each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T11:00","end":"2026-10-08T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-08T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.444484706088215},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite ticket2"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791421085889}
{"job":{"id":20129910,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Source 1 Solutions","title":"9684 - Switch Migration (Fortigate) - Hillsborough, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>General:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Must bring sign off form onsite and have it completed by POC to be paid.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Expect between 2-4 hours of work to complete.</li><li>Must take and upload pre &amp; post completion photos.</li><li>Will be provided troubleshooting steps document and wiring diagram once assigned.</li><li>Will be provided site POC.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p><p>Overview: Responsible for delivering on site services for “Rack and Stack” of 2x FortiGate 101F, into customer provided data racks and connect the cables to the new equipment and ensure network activity lights are on. Tech will then hand over to customer's team to ensure the new equipment auto configures (successfully completes Fortinet’s zero touch provisioning process) and is operating correctly. If there are issues, the tech will move the cables back to the original equipment. Leaving the newly racked equipment in place.</p><p>Once complete: place the old velo cloud device and USBs in the smaller box that had cables/accessories and hand it to the site point of contact.</p><p>SD-WAN Upgrade</p><p>• The engineer will carry out the installation including:</p><p>• Locate Fortinet equipment sent to site by Customer.</p><p>o The shipment will include two (2) Fortinet 101F appliances.</p><p>o Identify location of existing VeloCloud solution.</p><p>o Physical installation into a communications rack using the standard mounting kit provided with the part or parts and cage nuts &amp; bolts provided by the POC. If the part is to be desk mounted, then the FSE will attach desk mount kit provided and place part or parts in place.</p><p>o Engineer will connect FortiGate’s network &amp; intra device cabling in accordance with the customer/WWT supplied patching schedule.</p><p>o Engineer will connect device power to open sockets.</p><p>o Configuration of the FortiGate will be carried out by the end client</p><p>o Establish WAN connectivity for Fortinet devices per mutually agreed upon process to allow devices to obtain configuration from OEM cloud management platform.</p><p>o Upon confirmation of configuration download, establish connectivity for new</p><p>Fortinet 101F devices to End User network per mutually agreed upon</p><p>processes.</p><p>o Validate connectivity and functionality for new Fortinet solution per mutually</p><p>agreed upon processes while working with Customer/End User remote support</p><p>personnel.</p><p>• Engineer complete installation of all FortiGate’s and once confirmed that all installed FortiGate’s are accessible and are installed in accordance with expectations.</p><p>• Following physical deployment, the Engineer will tidy the work area, place packaging in an area advised by the POC.</p><p>• Decommission existing VeloCloud SD-WAN solution and provide to End User for final disposition.</p><p>• The Engineer will obtain sign off from the POC and will send to the HTECH Project Co Ordinator.</p><p>• The engineer will leave site, advising the Project Coordinator of departure time.</p><p>• The Project Co Ordinator will contact the POC to advise that the site has been signed off and to obtain service feedback.</p><p><strong><u>Installation Instructions:</u></strong></p><p><strong>*Devices should not be Powered on from the get-go.&nbsp;Connect the devices to the power on 4th&nbsp;step.*</strong></p><ol><li>Rack the Master unit above the Backup unit.</li><li>Connect the wan1 port of each Fortigate into the core switch available ports. [Except port 47/48 they will be used later]</li><li>Connect HA1 of master to the HA1 of secondary . And HA2 of master will connect to the HA2 of the firewall.</li><li>AT THIS POINT THE FORTIGATE ARE READY TO BE POWERED ON . CONNECT THE MASTER UNIT [UPPER] INTO POWER FIRST AND THEN THE BACKUP [BOTTOM]</li><li>Everything going well it should take about 30 min for firmware upgrade/ config push. If there is any issue troubleshooting Document will come into play.</li><li>Connect the WAN1[ATT] and WAN2[Verizon] interfaces now and port11 [or port12 as well if there is switch stack] to the Core switch as per the diagram connections. MGMT interfaces of each FortiGate can also be connected now as well.</li></ol><ul><li>In the Excel Sheet which will be shared there are 2 columns one with the master FortiGate SNO which will be mounted on the Top and the backup FortiGate SNO which will be mounted in the bottom.</li><li>The Wiring diagram is attached as well . In some cases, we might have the Core switch interfaces designated for FortiGate already used up by something else . In that case we will coordinate with the smart hands and use other available ports in the core switch.</li><li>Must make sure the only the designated devices[S.No] are installed at the correct address.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Label Maker to label the cables</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Mobile with&nbsp;hotspot capability</li><li>Laptop (Please bring charger with you onsite)</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Screwdriver Kit</li><li>Internet Dongle</li><li>USB</li><li>Spare Ethernet Cables</li><li>Any other tools required&nbsp;for task</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables</strong></p><p>-&nbsp;Signoff sheet</p><p>- Ontime Arrival</p><p>- Onsite/Offsite reporting to the IT Team</p><p>- Pictures when and where required by the IT Team</p>","markdown":"**General:**\n\n- **Must bring sign off form onsite and have it completed by POC to be paid.**\n- Expect between 2-4 hours of work to complete.\n- Must take and upload pre & post completion photos.\n- Will be provided troubleshooting steps document and wiring diagram once assigned.\n- Will be provided site POC.\n\n**Scope:**\n\nOverview: Responsible for delivering on site services for “Rack and Stack” of 2x FortiGate 101F, into customer provided data racks and connect the cables to the new equipment and ensure network activity lights are on. Tech will then hand over to customer's team to ensure the new equipment auto configures (successfully completes Fortinet’s zero touch provisioning process) and is operating correctly. If there are issues, the tech will move the cables back to the original equipment. Leaving the newly racked equipment in place.\n\nOnce complete: place the old velo cloud device and USBs in the smaller box that had cables/accessories and hand it to the site point of contact.\n\nSD-WAN Upgrade\n\n• The engineer will carry out the installation including:\n\n• Locate Fortinet equipment sent to site by Customer.\n\no The shipment will include two (2) Fortinet 101F appliances.\n\no Identify location of existing VeloCloud solution.\n\no Physical installation into a communications rack using the standard mounting kit provided with the part or parts and cage nuts & bolts provided by the POC. If the part is to be desk mounted, then the FSE will attach desk mount kit provided and place part or parts in place.\n\no Engineer will connect FortiGate’s network & intra device cabling in accordance with the customer/WWT supplied patching schedule.\n\no Engineer will connect device power to open sockets.\n\no Configuration of the FortiGate will be carried out by the end client\n\no Establish WAN connectivity for Fortinet devices per mutually agreed upon process to allow devices to obtain configuration from OEM cloud management platform.\n\no Upon confirmation of configuration download, establish connectivity for new\n\nFortinet 101F devices to End User network per mutually agreed upon\n\nprocesses.\n\no Validate connectivity and functionality for new Fortinet solution per mutually\n\nagreed upon processes while working with Customer/End User remote support\n\npersonnel.\n\n• Engineer complete installation of all FortiGate’s and once confirmed that all installed FortiGate’s are accessible and are installed in accordance with expectations.\n\n• Following physical deployment, the Engineer will tidy the work area, place packaging in an area advised by the POC.\n\n• Decommission existing VeloCloud SD-WAN solution and provide to End User for final disposition.\n\n• The Engineer will obtain sign off from the POC and will send to the HTECH Project Co Ordinator.\n\n• The engineer will leave site, advising the Project Coordinator of departure time.\n\n• The Project Co Ordinator will contact the POC to advise that the site has been signed off and to obtain service feedback.\n\n**Installation Instructions:**\n\n**\\*Devices should not be Powered on from the get-go. Connect the devices to the power on 4th step.\\***\n\n1. Rack the Master unit above the Backup unit.\n2. Connect the wan1 port of each Fortigate into the core switch available ports. \\[Except port 47/48 they will be used later\\]\n3. Connect HA1 of master to the HA1 of secondary . And HA2 of master will connect to the HA2 of the firewall.\n4. AT THIS POINT THE FORTIGATE ARE READY TO BE POWERED ON . CONNECT THE MASTER UNIT \\[UPPER\\] INTO POWER FIRST AND THEN THE BACKUP \\[BOTTOM\\]\n5. Everything going well it should take about 30 min for firmware upgrade/ config push. If there is any issue troubleshooting Document will come into play.\n6. Connect the WAN1\\[ATT\\] and WAN2\\[Verizon\\] interfaces now and port11 \\[or port12 as well if there is switch stack\\] to the Core switch as per the diagram connections. MGMT interfaces of each FortiGate can also be connected now as well.\n\n- In the Excel Sheet which will be shared there are 2 columns one with the master FortiGate SNO which will be mounted on the Top and the backup FortiGate SNO which will be mounted in the bottom.\n- The Wiring diagram is attached as well . In some cases, we might have the Core switch interfaces designated for FortiGate already used up by something else . In that case we will coordinate with the smart hands and use other available ports in the core switch.\n- Must make sure the only the designated devices\\[S.No\\] are installed at the correct address.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Label Maker to label the cables\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Mobile with hotspot capability\n- Laptop (Please bring charger with you onsite)\n- Console Cable\n- Screwdriver Kit\n- Internet Dongle\n- USB\n- Spare Ethernet Cables\n- Any other tools required for task\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n\\- Signoff sheet\n\n\\- Ontime Arrival\n\n\\- Onsite/Offsite reporting to the IT Team\n\n\\- Pictures when and where required by the IT Team","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T12:00","end":"2026-10-20T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":23.826617771492778},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21