{"job":{"id":20129937,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Source 1 Solutions","title":"9684 - Switch Migration (Fortigate) - Raleigh, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>General:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Must bring sign off form onsite and have it completed by POC to be paid.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Expect between 2-4 hours of work to complete.</li><li>Must take and upload pre &amp; post completion photos.</li><li>Will be provided troubleshooting steps document and wiring diagram once assigned.</li><li>Will be provided site POC.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p><p>Overview: Responsible for delivering on site services for “Rack and Stack” of 2x FortiGate 101F, into customer provided data racks and connect the cables to the new equipment and ensure network activity lights are on. Tech will then hand over to customer's team to ensure the new equipment auto configures (successfully completes Fortinet’s zero touch provisioning process) and is operating correctly. If there are issues, the tech will move the cables back to the original equipment. Leaving the newly racked equipment in place.</p><p>Once complete: place the old velo cloud device and USBs in the smaller box that had cables/accessories and hand it to the site point of contact.</p><p>SD-WAN Upgrade</p><p>• The engineer will carry out the installation including:</p><p>• Locate Fortinet equipment sent to site by Customer.</p><p>o The shipment will include two (2) Fortinet 101F appliances.</p><p>o Identify location of existing VeloCloud solution.</p><p>o Physical installation into a communications rack using the standard mounting kit provided with the part or parts and cage nuts &amp; bolts provided by the POC. If the part is to be desk mounted, then the FSE will attach desk mount kit provided and place part or parts in place.</p><p>o Engineer will connect FortiGate’s network &amp; intra device cabling in accordance with the customer/WWT supplied patching schedule.</p><p>o Engineer will connect device power to open sockets.</p><p>o Configuration of the FortiGate will be carried out by the end client</p><p>o Establish WAN connectivity for Fortinet devices per mutually agreed upon process to allow devices to obtain configuration from OEM cloud management platform.</p><p>o Upon confirmation of configuration download, establish connectivity for new</p><p>Fortinet 101F devices to End User network per mutually agreed upon</p><p>processes.</p><p>o Validate connectivity and functionality for new Fortinet solution per mutually</p><p>agreed upon processes while working with Customer/End User remote support</p><p>personnel.</p><p>• Engineer complete installation of all FortiGate’s and once confirmed that all installed FortiGate’s are accessible and are installed in accordance with expectations.</p><p>• Following physical deployment, the Engineer will tidy the work area, place packaging in an area advised by the POC.</p><p>• Decommission existing VeloCloud SD-WAN solution and provide to End User for final disposition.</p><p>• The Engineer will obtain sign off from the POC and will send to the HTECH Project Co Ordinator.</p><p>• The engineer will leave site, advising the Project Coordinator of departure time.</p><p>• The Project Co Ordinator will contact the POC to advise that the site has been signed off and to obtain service feedback.</p><p><strong><u>Installation Instructions:</u></strong></p><p><strong>*Devices should not be Powered on from the get-go.&nbsp;Connect the devices to the power on 4th&nbsp;step.*</strong></p><ol><li>Rack the Master unit above the Backup unit.</li><li>Connect the wan1 port of each Fortigate into the core switch available ports. [Except port 47/48 they will be used later]</li><li>Connect HA1 of master to the HA1 of secondary . And HA2 of master will connect to the HA2 of the firewall.</li><li>AT THIS POINT THE FORTIGATE ARE READY TO BE POWERED ON . CONNECT THE MASTER UNIT [UPPER] INTO POWER FIRST AND THEN THE BACKUP [BOTTOM]</li><li>Everything going well it should take about 30 min for firmware upgrade/ config push. If there is any issue troubleshooting Document will come into play.</li><li>Connect the WAN1[ATT] and WAN2[Verizon] interfaces now and port11 [or port12 as well if there is switch stack] to the Core switch as per the diagram connections. MGMT interfaces of each FortiGate can also be connected now as well.</li></ol><ul><li>In the Excel Sheet which will be shared there are 2 columns one with the master FortiGate SNO which will be mounted on the Top and the backup FortiGate SNO which will be mounted in the bottom.</li><li>The Wiring diagram is attached as well . In some cases, we might have the Core switch interfaces designated for FortiGate already used up by something else . In that case we will coordinate with the smart hands and use other available ports in the core switch.</li><li>Must make sure the only the designated devices[S.No] are installed at the correct address.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Label Maker to label the cables</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Mobile with&nbsp;hotspot capability</li><li>Laptop (Please bring charger with you onsite)</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Screwdriver Kit</li><li>Internet Dongle</li><li>USB</li><li>Spare Ethernet Cables</li><li>Any other tools required&nbsp;for task</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables</strong></p><p>-&nbsp;Signoff sheet</p><p>- Ontime Arrival</p><p>- Onsite/Offsite reporting to the IT Team</p><p>- Pictures when and where required by the IT Team</p>","markdown":"**General:**\n\n- **Must bring sign off form onsite and have it completed by POC to be paid.**\n- Expect between 2-4 hours of work to complete.\n- Must take and upload pre & post completion photos.\n- Will be provided troubleshooting steps document and wiring diagram once assigned.\n- Will be provided site POC.\n\n**Scope:**\n\nOverview: Responsible for delivering on site services for “Rack and Stack” of 2x FortiGate 101F, into customer provided data racks and connect the cables to the new equipment and ensure network activity lights are on. Tech will then hand over to customer's team to ensure the new equipment auto configures (successfully completes Fortinet’s zero touch provisioning process) and is operating correctly. If there are issues, the tech will move the cables back to the original equipment. Leaving the newly racked equipment in place.\n\nOnce complete: place the old velo cloud device and USBs in the smaller box that had cables/accessories and hand it to the site point of contact.\n\nSD-WAN Upgrade\n\n• The engineer will carry out the installation including:\n\n• Locate Fortinet equipment sent to site by Customer.\n\no The shipment will include two (2) Fortinet 101F appliances.\n\no Identify location of existing VeloCloud solution.\n\no Physical installation into a communications rack using the standard mounting kit provided with the part or parts and cage nuts & bolts provided by the POC. If the part is to be desk mounted, then the FSE will attach desk mount kit provided and place part or parts in place.\n\no Engineer will connect FortiGate’s network & intra device cabling in accordance with the customer/WWT supplied patching schedule.\n\no Engineer will connect device power to open sockets.\n\no Configuration of the FortiGate will be carried out by the end client\n\no Establish WAN connectivity for Fortinet devices per mutually agreed upon process to allow devices to obtain configuration from OEM cloud management platform.\n\no Upon confirmation of configuration download, establish connectivity for new\n\nFortinet 101F devices to End User network per mutually agreed upon\n\nprocesses.\n\no Validate connectivity and functionality for new Fortinet solution per mutually\n\nagreed upon processes while working with Customer/End User remote support\n\npersonnel.\n\n• Engineer complete installation of all FortiGate’s and once confirmed that all installed FortiGate’s are accessible and are installed in accordance with expectations.\n\n• Following physical deployment, the Engineer will tidy the work area, place packaging in an area advised by the POC.\n\n• Decommission existing VeloCloud SD-WAN solution and provide to End User for final disposition.\n\n• The Engineer will obtain sign off from the POC and will send to the HTECH Project Co Ordinator.\n\n• The engineer will leave site, advising the Project Coordinator of departure time.\n\n• The Project Co Ordinator will contact the POC to advise that the site has been signed off and to obtain service feedback.\n\n**Installation Instructions:**\n\n**\\*Devices should not be Powered on from the get-go. Connect the devices to the power on 4th step.\\***\n\n1. Rack the Master unit above the Backup unit.\n2. Connect the wan1 port of each Fortigate into the core switch available ports. \\[Except port 47/48 they will be used later\\]\n3. Connect HA1 of master to the HA1 of secondary . And HA2 of master will connect to the HA2 of the firewall.\n4. AT THIS POINT THE FORTIGATE ARE READY TO BE POWERED ON . CONNECT THE MASTER UNIT \\[UPPER\\] INTO POWER FIRST AND THEN THE BACKUP \\[BOTTOM\\]\n5. Everything going well it should take about 30 min for firmware upgrade/ config push. If there is any issue troubleshooting Document will come into play.\n6. Connect the WAN1\\[ATT\\] and WAN2\\[Verizon\\] interfaces now and port11 \\[or port12 as well if there is switch stack\\] to the Core switch as per the diagram connections. MGMT interfaces of each FortiGate can also be connected now as well.\n\n- In the Excel Sheet which will be shared there are 2 columns one with the master FortiGate SNO which will be mounted on the Top and the backup FortiGate SNO which will be mounted in the bottom.\n- The Wiring diagram is attached as well . In some cases, we might have the Core switch interfaces designated for FortiGate already used up by something else . In that case we will coordinate with the smart hands and use other available ports in the core switch.\n- Must make sure the only the designated devices\\[S.No\\] are installed at the correct address.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Label Maker to label the cables\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Mobile with hotspot capability\n- Laptop (Please bring charger with you onsite)\n- Console Cable\n- Screwdriver Kit\n- Internet Dongle\n- USB\n- Spare Ethernet Cables\n- Any other tools required for task\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n\\- Signoff sheet\n\n\\- Ontime Arrival\n\n\\- Onsite/Offsite reporting to the IT Team\n\n\\- Pictures when and where required by the IT Team","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00","end":"2026-10-21T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":2.8537882851244225},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-12T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05999131-Durham - Site #9927-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},