–6\" Phillips screwdriver\n- Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool\n- Wire cutters\n- Wire stripping tool\n- Wire crimping tool\n- Wire butt connectors\n- 13mm crescent wrench\n- Socket set with ratchet including:\n- 6mm\n- 6.5mm\n- 7mm\n- 8mm\n- 10mm\n- 11mm\n- 12mm\n- 13mm\n- Digital multimeter / voltmeter\n- Handheld vacuum\n- Needle-nose pliers\n- Standard pliers\n- Channel-lock pliers\n- Extendable magnetic pickup tool for dropped screws\n- Tool magnetizer for retaining screws on driver heads\n- Utility knife\n- X-Acto knife\n- 4\" (small) zip ties\n- Electrical tape\n- Suction cup (90 lb. rating)\n- Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)\n\n**Cleaning & Advanced Repair**\n\n- Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)\n- Heat gun (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Alcohol wipes\n- Window cleaner\n- Paper towels\n- Nitrile gloves\n- Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws\n- 10-amp automotive fuse\n- 15-amp automotive fuse\n\n**Convenience & Specialty Tools**\n\n- Sharpie or permanent marker\n- EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor\n- Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)\n- Tool bag or hard case carrier\n- Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)\n\n**Professional Conduct Requirements**\n\n- Arrive fit for duty\n- No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work\n- No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite\n- Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited\n- Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is obtained\n- Comply with all customer site policies, security requirements, and safety procedures\n\n**Physical Requirements**\n\n- Ability to safely lift up to 30 lbs. overhead\n- Ability to safely lift up to 60 lbs. at ground level\n- Ability to kneel, crouch, bend, and 