{"job":{"id":20124191,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"HH Services1. Inc.","title":"Network Rack Installation & Cable Management","description":{"html":"A technician is needed to install network rack, UPS, move equipment to the rack at a dental office on Friday, 10/9/26 at 1:00pm.<p><br></p><p><strong>Office Hours: </strong>Monday–Thursday: 8:00 AM–5:00 PM and Friday: 8:00 AM–1:00 PM</p><p><strong>Please contact the remote technician/dispatcher prior to beginning work. The remote technician will need to safely power down the server before any equipment is moved or disconnected.</strong></p><p>Technician will:</p><ol><li><strong>Install the network rack</strong> in the designated network room/location.</li><li><strong>Move existing network switches</strong> into the new rack and securely mount them.</li><li><strong>Move ISP/carrier equipment</strong> into the network rack, where applicable and where cable length permits.</li><li><strong>Organize and properly wire all network equipment</strong> within the rack.</li><li><strong>Move any additional equipment that can reasonably be relocated into the rack</strong> to create a clean and organized network room.</li><li><strong>Clean up and manage all cabling</strong>, including:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Route cables neatly within the rack.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Use appropriate cable management practices.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Avoid unnecessary cable loops or loose/hanging cables.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure cables are properly secured and do not interfere with equipment ventilation or access.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Configure the PDUs/power strips as follows:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect <strong>one PDU/network power strip to the UPS</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the <strong>second PDU/network power strip directly to building power</strong>.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Server power connections:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect one of the server's power cables to the PDU that is connected to the <strong>UPS</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the server's second power cable to the PDU that is connected to <strong>building power</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This provides redundant power to the server from separate power sources.</li></ul><ol><li>Once all equipment has been installed and cabling is organized, <strong>verify all connections are secure and equipment is properly powered</strong>.</li><li>Coordinate with the remote technician before powering the server back on and confirm that network equipment and the server are operational.</li></ol>Completion Requirements<ul><li>Network rack securely installed.</li><li>Switches and ISP equipment properly mounted/positioned in the rack.</li><li>Equipment neatly organized.</li><li>All cables routed and secured neatly.</li><li>UPS and building-power connections correctly configured.</li><li>Server connected to both power sources as specified above.</li><li>Verify network connectivity and equipment operation with the remote technician.</li><li>Provide photos of the completed rack and network room upon completion.</li></ul><p>Contact information is in the confidential section of the work order and will be available once assigned.</p><p>As this is a medical practice, it's important to adhere to HIPAA and PHI guidelines. While this request does not involve interacting with any patients or accessing confidential information, we kindly ask that you ensure no patients or sensitive information appear in any photos.</p>","markdown":"A technician is needed to install network rack, UPS, move equipment to the rack at a dental office on Friday, 10/9/26 at 1:00pm.\n\n**Office Hours:** Monday–Thursday: 8:00 AM–5:00 PM and Friday: 8:00 AM–1:00 PM\n\n**Please contact the remote technician/dispatcher prior to beginning work. The remote technician will need to safely power down the server before any equipment is moved or disconnected.**\n\nTechnician will:\n\n1. **Install the network rack** in the designated network room/location.\n2. **Move existing network switches** into the new rack and securely mount them.\n3. **Move ISP/carrier equipment** into the network rack, where applicable and where cable length permits.\n4. **Organize and properly wire all network equipment** within the rack.\n5. **Move any additional equipment that can reasonably be relocated into the rack** to create a clean and organized network room.\n6. **Clean up and manage all cabling**, including:\n\n- Route cables neatly within the rack.\n- Use appropriate cable management practices.\n- Avoid unnecessary cable loops or loose/hanging cables.\n- Ensure cables are properly secured and do not interfere with equipment ventilation or access.\n\n1. **Configure the PDUs/power strips as follows:**\n\n- Connect **one PDU/network power strip to the UPS**.\n- Connect the **second PDU/network power strip directly to building power**.\n\n1. **Server power connections:**\n\n- Connect one of the server's power cables to the PDU that is connected to the **UPS**.\n- Connect the server's second power cable to the PDU that is connected to **building power**.\n- This provides redundant power to the server from separate power sources.\n\n1. Once all equipment has been installed and cabling is organized, **verify all connections are secure and equipment is properly powered**.\n2. Coordinate with the remote technician before powering the server back on and confirm that network equipment and the server are operational.\n\nCompletion Requirements- Network rack securely installed.\n- Switches and ISP equipment properly mounted/positioned in the rack.\n- Equipment neatly organized.\n- All cables routed and secured neatly.\n- UPS and building-power connections correctly configured.\n- Server connected to both power sources as specified above.\n- Verify network connectivity and equipment operation with the remote technician.\n- Provide photos of the completed rack and network room upon completion.\n\nContact information is in the confidential section of the work order and will be available once assigned.\n\nAs this is a medical practice, it's important to adhere to HIPAA and PHI guidelines. While this request does not involve interacting with any patients or accessing confidential information, we kindly ask that you ensure no patients or sensitive information appear in any photos.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00","end":"2026-10-09T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":195},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.343667761767334},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Oct 9, 1:00 PM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 9, Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cu