{"job":{"id":"4610148837","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"vendor meet - fire panel","description":"Required Equipment:  <br>IMPORTANT: Tech must bring and have ready a USB → DB9 Female cable(USB to RS232 Adapter with PL2303 Chipset)  and a USB → Mini-USB serial cable for console access. <br>Tech will need a patch cord, a splitter and a minimum of 3 filters, La ptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone and charger, Multimeter, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder,  Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Pencil and/or Marker, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, Cross-Connect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, USB → DB9 Female cable, USB → Mini-USB serial cable.  USB to RS232 Adapter with PL2303 Chipset, 6.6ft USB 2.0 Male to RS232 Female DB9 Serial Converter Cable  - for gen 3/3.5<br> <br> <br>Scope Of Work: <br>*** IMPORTANT: Tech must call into Work Market to check in and out upon arrival and before departing the site. *** <br>***Tech will call into Granite NOC at 844.492.2557 opt 1 to start the scope of work.*** <br> <br>PLEASE NOTE: There is no voicemail for the IW call queue. If you cannot get through to the NOC, pressing option 1 will prompt a callback from the next available NOC tech. <br> <br>IMPORTANT: Tech must bring and have ready a USB → DB9 Female cable and a USB → Mini-USB serial cable for console access. <br> <br><br>1. Have fire alarm panel placed in test mode. On site contact should know the monitoring station contact, but the number should also be written on the alarm panel itself somewhere. Test mode will be needed for at least 1 hour.  <br>2. Tech will call into Granite NOC at 844.492.2557 opt 1 to start the scope of work. <br>3. Test line integrity with buttset <br>1. Remove cross connection to CPE <br>2. Placed buttset on 66 block pairs and test inbound/outbound calling <br>3. Replace cross connection and trace line to any other existing cross connection, repeat IB/OB test there <br>Continue this process all the way to the alarm panel, remove the connection to the panel and repeat IB/OB test there.  <br>4. Once lines are verified as working, reconnect alarm panel and remove the leads to the backup battery on the panel. This should force the panel to place a call to the monitoring station. <br> <br>NOC should review call recordings via the Epik portal, make recommendations based on results (timing issues, dropped audio, etc); repeat step 4 with NOC until communications have been restored. The monitoring station contact should be able to confirm that all signals have been received and the alarm panel should show no errors. <br>-Tech must be released by Granite NOC <br>-Tech must clean up and complete close-out notes with Work Market.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T08:00","end":"2026-10-16T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":127.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 127.6mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-1