{"job":{"id":20130643,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Fortitude Nicsa Global Limited","title":"FNG REF# ST010776 || WOT0016281 || NAUSDURHA0318 || Critical Link Down Alert | Research Triangle Park, USA","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: black;\">Hello Team,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Please see the ticket details for the visit on </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Friday 9th October 8:30 AM LT</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> at BASF Site and please share the FE details regarding this request as soon as possible.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Schedule Detail: - Friday 9th October 8:30 AM LT</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Task Description: - </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">usattap0101-trcks-01SW01 - Critical Link Down Alert - Oper Down alert</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">SOW: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Need to check the mentioned interface, including port and cabling status</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Site Address: - </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">141 Engelhard Road, Attapulgus, 39815, United States of America</span></p><p><strong>Local POC Detail: -</strong></p><p>Name-Todd Thornton</p><p>phone-+1 919 547-2323</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Engineer Need to carry:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Data card (mobile data) + mobile phone</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Console cable and laptop (with admin account)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Kindly note that engineer needs to share report before leaving the site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Safety Equipment -</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Field Engineer Access - Field engineer allowed, pre-registration required</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Hardware In/Out - To be communicated to site access contact and instructions will be provided</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Technical Contact -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Registration Information - Engineer details to be provided in advance to site access contact</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Required Documents -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Photography Allowed - Allowed, network devices only</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Special Remarks, Notices and Reminders :</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">· Engineer must be dressed in business casual attire with proper footwear (Full-sleeve shirt, long trousers, Closed shoes).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">· Engineer must carry basic Safety PPE Equipment Kit - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety glasses, earplugs)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">· Engineer must bring: Data card (mobile data) or Internet Dongle, Mobile phone, Console cable, Laptop (with admin account), and Label printer.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Regarding laptop, Engineer must confirm it is an Opensource Company-provided laptop if been asked by POC or Remote team onsite.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must join using the Teams credentials provided by FNG, not their personal account. In case of any issues, please contact the FNG Service Desk Team.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must carry a valid government ID card for site access.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must not mention being a freelancer or contractor. They must introduce themselves as FNG employees or direct contractors.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· If travelling by Public Transport, Engineer must not discuss anything about it with the Local POC.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must contact the POC upon arrival. If not able to reach POC, escalate immediately to your leadership team and inform FNG.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must not leave site until all work is approved by FNG internally and the Remote Team at Tech Mahindra.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· Engineer must ensure the FE Report is signed by the POC confirming the work completion (unless unavailable).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;· BASF Client is very sensitive – Engineer must not discuss anything apart from work-related communication while they are onsite.</span></p>","markdown":"Hello Team,\n\nPlease see the ticket details for the visit on **Friday 9th October 8:30 AM LT** at BASF Site and please share the FE details regarding this request as soon as possible.\n\n**Schedule Detail: - Friday 9th October 8:30 AM LT**\n\n**Task Description: -** usattap0101-trcks-01SW01 - Critical Link Down Alert - Oper Down alert\n\n**SOW:** Need to check the mentioned interface, including port and cabling status\n\n**Site Address: -** 141 Engelhard Road, Attapulgus, 39815, United States of America\n\n**Local POC Detail: -**\n\nName-Todd Thornton\n\nphone-+1 919 547-2323\n\n**Engineer Need to carry:**\n\nData card (mobile data) + mobile phone\n\nConsole cable and laptop (with admin account)\n\n**Kindly note that engineer needs to share report before leaving the site.**\n\n**Safety Equipment -**\n\nField Engineer Access - Field engineer allowed, pre-registration required\n\nHardware In/Out - To be communicated to site access contact and instructions will be provided\n\nTechnical Contact -\n\nRegistration Information - Engineer details to be provided in advance to site access contact\n\nRequired Documents -\n\nPhotography Allowed - Allowed, network devices only\n\nSpecial Remarks, Notices and Reminders :\n\n· Engineer must be dressed in business casual attire with proper footwear (Full-sleeve shirt, long trousers, Closed shoes).\n\n· Engineer must carry basic Safety PPE Equipment Kit - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety glasses, earplugs)\n\n· Engineer must bring: Data card (mobile data) or Internet Dongle, Mobile phone, Console cable, Laptop (with admin account), and Label printer.\n\n · Regarding laptop, Engineer must confirm it is an Opensource Company-provided laptop if been asked by POC or Remote team onsite.\n\n · Engineer must join using the Teams credentials provided by FNG, not their personal account. In case of any issues, please contact the FNG Service Desk Team.\n\n · Engineer must carry a valid government ID card for site access.\n\n · Engineer must not mention being a freelancer or contractor. They must introduce themselves as FNG employees or direct contractors.\n\n · If travelling by Public Transport, Engineer must not discuss anything about it with the Local POC.\n\n · Engineer must contact the POC upon arrival. If not able to reach POC, escalate immediately to your leadership team and inform FNG.\n\n · Engineer must not leave site until all work is approved by FNG internally and the Remote Team at Tech Mahindra.\n\n · Engineer must ensure the FE Report is signed by the POC confirming the work completion (unless unavailable).\n\n · BASF Client is very sensitive – Engineer must not discuss anything apart from work-related communication while they are onsite.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T09:45","end":"2026-10-09T13:45"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":270},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7.037388443886853},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Oct 9, 9:45 AM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 9, Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct