{"job":{"id":20130903,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DiverseNet","title":"Troubleshoot Server Battery/Install Network Card/Cable Management","description":{"html":"<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTES</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician must upload all deliverables before calling DiverseNet to check out or leaving site</li>\n<li>Technician must call to check in and out with DiverseNet to receive full payment</li>\n<li>Technician must arrive during the given time frame to receive full payment</li>\n<li>Any out of scope work, or time logged past the not to exceed amount, must be approved by DiverseNet to receive payment</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>SKILLS, TOOLS, MATERIALS AND DRESS CODE</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>Skills</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Low Voltage Cabling&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Networking</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools/Materials</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with a physical network port OR a USB network adapter (RJ45) and must have HDMI, VGA</li>\n<li>Smartphone with camera</li>\n<li>Cat5 Tester</li>\n<li>Cable Toner and Wand</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Crimper (Cat-5)</li>\n<li>FlashLight</li>\n<li>Network Termination Tools</li>\n<li>Video Termination Tools</li>\n<li>Basic Handtools</li>\n<li>Spare VGA, DVI and Cat5 Patch Cables (for testing)</li>\n<li>Extension Cord</li>\n<li>Tape Measure</li>\n<li>Velcro</li>\n<li>8ft Ladder</li>\n<li>Coax Cable</li>\n<li>Cat5e Data Cable</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Close toed shoes</li>\n<li>Long pants</li>\n<li>Collared shirt</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>CHECK IN INSTRUCTIONS AND ESCALATION</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li>We will be representing&nbsp;<del>******</del> while on site.</li>\n<li>Check in with DiverseNet at&nbsp;317-536-6000 opt 2 and reference case number&nbsp;00051700\n<ul>\n<li>Ask for&nbsp;<strong><u>DiverseNet&nbsp;Check in code</u></strong> (<u>Required for Payment</u>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Check in with&nbsp;<del>******** ******</del>&nbsp;to verify location of equipment</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use the following escalation path for all issues onsite:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>IT Contact : Jeff Franklin</li>\n<li>If first&nbsp;contact is non-responsive call&nbsp;DiverseNet at&nbsp;317-536-6000 opt 2</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>DESCRIPTION OF WORK</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p>Onsite Contact: Kimberly Hurley</p>\n<p>IT Contact : Jeff Franklin (Flying in from Dallas that week)</p>\n<p>Location: 1010 Arnold St.</p>\n<p>Greensboro, NC</p>\n<p>27405</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>• Get 10g network card installed in Bree's computer and the one that's not set up yet, move the cables to the 10g switch side.</p>\n<p>• Figure out where the network cable in the back runs to in the server room.</p>\n<p>• Server room battery backup is beeping.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>DELIVERABLE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li>\n<li>Pictures of Work Done</li>\n<li>Picture of Equipment&nbsp;Connected (if applicable, include Serial Number)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>CHECK OUT INSTRUCTIONS</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out with&nbsp;<del>******** ******</del> and verify equipment is working properly</li>\n<li>Check out&nbsp;with DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 x2\n<ul>\n<li>Ask for <strong><u>DiverseNet Check Out code</u></strong>(Required for Payment)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Technician must upload all deliverables before calling DiverseNet to check out or leaving site\n- Technician must call to check in and out with DiverseNet to receive full payment\n- Technician must arrive during the given time frame to receive full payment\n- Any out of scope work, or time logged past the not to exceed amount, must be approved by DiverseNet to receive payment\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**SKILLS, TOOLS, MATERIALS AND DRESS CODE**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**Skills**\n\n- Low Voltage Cabling\n- Networking\n\n**Tools/Materials**\n\n- Laptop with a physical network port OR a USB network adapter (RJ45) and must have HDMI, VGA\n- Smartphone with camera\n- Cat5 Tester\n- Cable Toner and Wand\n- Multimeter\n- Crimper (Cat-5)\n- FlashLight\n- Network Termination Tools\n- Video Termination Tools\n- Basic Handtools\n- Spare VGA, DVI and Cat5 Patch Cables (for testing)\n- Extension Cord\n- Tape Measure\n- Velcro\n- 8ft Ladder\n- Coax Cable\n- Cat5e Data Cable\n\n**Dress Code**\n\n- Close toed shoes\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**CHECK IN INSTRUCTIONS AND ESCALATION**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- We will be representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* while on site.\n- Check in with DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 opt 2 and reference case number 00051700 \n  - Ask for **DiverseNet Check in code** (Required for Payment)\n- Check in with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to verify location of equipment\n\nUse the following escalation path for all issues onsite:\n\n1. IT Contact : Jeff Franklin\n2. If first contact is non-responsive call DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 opt 2\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**DESCRIPTION OF WORK**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\nOnsite Contact: Kimberly Hurley\n\nIT Contact : Jeff Franklin (Flying in from Dallas that week)\n\nLocation: 1010 Arnold St.\n\nGreensboro, NC\n\n27405\n\n• Get 10g network card installed in Bree's computer and the one that's not set up yet, move the cables to the 10g switch side.\n\n• Figure out where the network cable in the back runs to in the server room.\n\n• Server room battery backup is beeping.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**DELIVERABLE REQUIREMENTS**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- Pictures of Work Done\n- Picture of Equipment Connected (if applicable, include Serial Number)\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**CHECK OUT INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Check out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and verify equipment is working properly\n- Check out with DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 x2 \n  - Ask for **DiverseNet Check Out code**(Required for Payment)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T09:00","end":"2026-10-19T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-19T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":50},"additional":{"units":3,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":59.08577924675283},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.0