{"job":{"id":20131112,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Troubleshoot Cabling","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT INFORMATION:</strong></p><p><strong>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage.&nbsp;If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders.&nbsp;Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay.&nbsp;Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only.&nbsp;If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction.&nbsp;The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</strong></p><p>-------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">**** Work must be complete before the location opens and this could be an issue if the tech does not arrive on site, so arriving on time is extremely important. ****</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">IMMEDIATELY AFTER CHECKING IN WITH TRCA @ 940-565-5000 AND RECEIVING A CHECK IN CODE, THE TECH MUST CALL<del> ***** ******* * ************ *** * * ****** ******** *****</del></span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">TECH MUST CHECK TRACKING AND CONFIRM PARTS WERE DELIVERED BEFORE GOING TO SITE. (WHEN APPLICABLE, TRCA WILL LET YOU KNOW WHEN THIS IS THE CASE)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">&nbsp;Equipment/Technical Requirements:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Laptop</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- (1) Console Cable to connect to Console Port on Aruba 650/S1500/7010</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Terminal Emulation Software (PuTTY/Tera Term/SecureCRT/etc)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Hotspot with 4G Internet Access </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Ability to Tether LAPTOP from Hotspot</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Ability to join LogMeIn Rescue/LogMeIn 123 remote access website via Hotspot connection</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Ability to install software (PuTTY/Tera Term/Wireshark/etc) on Laptop should it become required </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Misc patch cables</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Cat 6 cable spool, crimper, and jacks to make custom length cable.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- At least 8' ladder for replacing APs</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">SOW: </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Site has indicated that Ziosk devices are not connecting. Requesting dispatch to review/correct site cabling.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">See connection to port 4 – please trace and verify placement.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">BEFORE checking out with TRCA, the tech must call <del>***** ******* * ************ *** * ** ***** ****</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Tech will need to document the name of the support rep they checked out with.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- When working with support and sending pictures, please use<del> </del></span><del>*****************</del><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"><del> </del></span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Required Deliverables Within (24) Hours of Completion:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- TECH MUST GET CLEAR PICTURES OF AP PLACEMENT, CABLE MANAGEMENT AND ANY EQUIPMENT THE TECH REPLACED OR TROUBLESHOT.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Completion pictures of any adds/moves/changes.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- If any cables are ran/re-terminated/tested - the tech must upload their test results showing each cable they touched has passed.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">* Cable test results- the cable tests must include the labeling to show which cable was tested and passed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">* The tech can do this by taking a picture of their cable tester showing 'pass'.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- If there is defective hardware; TRCA will need the make, model, and a picture of the device(s).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Customer sign off.</span></p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT INFORMATION:**\n\n**Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction. The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.**\n\n\\-------------------------------------------\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* Work must be complete before the location opens and this could be an issue if the tech does not arrive on site, so arriving on time is extremely important. \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIMMEDIATELY AFTER CHECKING IN WITH TRCA @ 940-565-5000 AND RECEIVING A CHECK IN CODE, THE TECH MUST CALL \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTECH MUST CHECK TRACKING AND CONFIRM PARTS WERE DELIVERED BEFORE GOING TO SITE. (WHEN APPLICABLE, TRCA WILL LET YOU KNOW WHEN THIS IS THE CASE)\n\n Equipment/Technical Requirements:\n\n\\- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.\n\n\\- Laptop\n\n\\- (1) Console Cable to connect to Console Port on Aruba 650/S1500/7010\n\n\\- Terminal Emulation Software (PuTTY/Tera Term/SecureCRT/etc)\n\n\\- Hotspot with 4G Internet Access\n\n\\- Ability to Tether LAPTOP from Hotspot\n\n\\- Ability to join LogMeIn Rescue/LogMeIn 123 remote access website via Hotspot connection\n\n\\- Ability to install software (PuTTY/Tera Term/Wireshark/etc) on Laptop should it become required\n\n\\- Misc patch cables\n\n\\- Cat 6 cable spool, crimper, and jacks to make custom length cable.\n\n\\- At least 8' ladder for replacing APs\n\nSOW:\n\nSite has indicated that Ziosk devices are not connecting. Requesting dispatch to review/correct site cabling.\n\nSee connection to port 4 – please trace and verify placement.\n\nBEFORE checking out with TRCA, the tech must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\- Tech will need to document the name of the support rep they checked out with.\n\n\\- When working with support and sending pictures, please use \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nRequired Deliverables Within (24) Hours of Completion:\n\n\\- TECH MUST GET CLEAR PICTURES OF AP PLACEMENT, CABLE MANAGEMENT AND ANY EQUIPMENT THE TECH REPLACED OR TROUBLESHOT.\n\n\\- Completion pictures of any adds/moves/changes.\n\n\\- If any cables are ran/re-terminated/tested - the tech must upload their test results showing each cable they touched has passed.\n\n\\* Cable test results- the cable tests must include the labeling to show which cable was tested and passed\n\n\\* The tech can do this by taking a picture of their cable tester showing 'pass'.\n\n\\- If there is defective hardware; TRCA will need the make, model, and a picture of the device(s).\n\n\\- Customer sign off.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T09:00","end":"2026-10-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.48158811203817},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-1