{"job":{"id":20131492,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"WiLine Networks","title":"Decomm Site, Remove Antennas, Wiring, CPE And Ship Parts Back   ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience with outdoor wireless antenna, cabling and networking.</li><li><strong>Please send us your SHIP TO address in the Field Nation Messages section once assigned.&nbsp;We will be shipping parts to you for the installation.</strong></li></ul><p><strong> PURPOSE OF VISIT - </strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools required:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">6’ ladder to remove equipment at backboard if needed</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">SAFETY HARNESS FOR BOTH TECHNICIANS IS REQUIRED</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">PPE REQUIRED, HARD HAT, BRIGHT VEST, STEEL TOE SHOES, GLOVES AND GOGGLES</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">hand tools including wrenches and sockets and cable cutters</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">drill motor with bits</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">rope and bucket to lower equipment off the roof</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">SAFETY CERTIFICATION IS REQUIRED TO ENTER THE BUILDING</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">TECHNICIAN IS REQUIRED TO TAKE SAFETY CLASS AND RETURN THE COMPLETED CERTIFICATION PRIOR TO GOING TO SITE OR THEY WILL NOT BE ALLOWED INSIDE THE BUILDING.&nbsp;SEE ATTACHED DOCUMENTATION.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Tech must follow scope of work and not deviate.</li><li>Tech must arrive on time.</li><li>Tech is not to discuss which Carriers we use or Speed Test results we use with the customer!!!</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">We are providing WILINE DIA Service</span></li><li>Tech is not to leave site until ALL pictures are available for Project Manager to view.</li><li>Requested photos must be uploaded during the visit. Photos uploaded after the visit will not be approved.</li><li>Photos must be labeled.</li><li>Failure to check-In and check-out may result in penalties.</li><li><strong>STRICLY REQUIRED: Business casual pants, no shorts (slack or kaki), collar shirt no pictures or writing on it, and no flip flops or sandals.</strong></li><li>Represent yourself as a WiLine Engineer.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>** ****** * ****** *** ************* * *** ***** ********** *** ******** ****** ** *****</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Service Type: Service Call</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Shipping parts?&nbsp;Y/N: No – Tech will be returning parts</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Working with NPE Y/N:&nbsp;No</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Target Tech Onsite Date:&nbsp;10/19</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Target Tech Onsite Time:&nbsp;10:00 AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Times are flexible. Y/N:&nbsp;No</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>********* **** ******** *********************** *******</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\"><del>********* ***** ******** *******************************</del></span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Requestor Email (Project Coordinator):&nbsp;</span>suzy.cepress@teladapters.com</p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Contact Name:&nbsp;&nbsp;TBD</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Contact Phone number:&nbsp;TBD</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Address:&nbsp;590 Tyler Industrial Ct, Southern Pines, NC 28387</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Company/Site Name: Amazon</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Site Access Hours:&nbsp;8:00 AM to 3:00 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Requested tech name and Field Nation ID:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">CSR or RT#:&nbsp;486800</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Estimate labor hours: 3 hours per tech</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">MAX labor hours:&nbsp;6 hours total</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">PURPOSE OF SERVICE CALL/SCOPE OF WORK: Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Scope/Onsite Description:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS PLEASE READ:&nbsp;DO NOT REMOVE THE GROMMETS FROM THE RADIOS CUT THE CABLES BELOW THE GROMMET, THIS REDUCES DAMAGE TO THE RADIO WHEN RETURNING TO US.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact LPOC and let them know you are onsite, also check out with them</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact Suzy Cepress at <del>************</del> when arriving onsite</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Decomm all equipment</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">First remove CPE with power supply and 4 POEs and Fiber handoff with fiber cable</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Take pictures before and after removing and upload to the ticket</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Take pictures of antennas before and after removing with cables cut</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Remove Inseego antennas, when removing antenna, </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">do not remove grommet covering the cable as this</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">damages the antenna, cut the cable below the grommet only.&nbsp;Take pictures of the antenna showing the cut cable and upload to the ticket.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Remove or cut external wiring</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Return equipment to us with label to be provided</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Work order is not complete until equipment has been dropped off at UPS location</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact Suzy for equipment to be shipped back to us</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Upload all pictures to ticket when complete</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Contact <del>**** ************ </del>prior to leaving site</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ADDITITONAL HOURS and ESCALATION PROCESS:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Additional hours past MAX hours MUST get Project Manager approval.&nbsp;&nbsp;Labor overage past MAX hours that are not pre-approved, will not be paid.</strong></li><li>If the Project Manager is not reachable, contact the WiLine support team at&nbsp;908-651-9350&nbsp;or WilIne@patstaffing.com.</li><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with the Project Coordinator. Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;Project Coordinator or WiLine support team.</li><li><strong>Additional Travel &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong> Travel expense (over 50 miles) must be pre-approved via counteroffer during your request</li></ul><p><strong><u>Lift Penalty</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Any additional charges incurred, such as extra lift rentals fees due to changes in the technician’s schedule, will be the responsibility of the technician. These additional fees will be charged back accordingly.</p><p><strong><u>Parts Plan</u>:&nbsp;</strong>In the event a technician is in possession of installation or return parts, payment will not be approved/issued until a receipt of proof of return is provided. In most cases, return parts will be boxed and left at the site. A shipping label will be provided. Take photo of boxed part in the area left, and upload it to the work order.</p><p><strong><u>Professionalism</u></strong>: We adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations &amp; timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations.</p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience with outdoor wireless antenna, cabling and networking.\n- **Please send us your SHIP TO address in the Field Nation Messages section once assigned. We will be shipping parts to you for the installation.**\n\n **PURPOSE OF VISIT -**\n\n- **Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back**\n\n**Tools required:**\n\n- 6’ ladder to remove equipment at backboard if needed\n- SAFETY HARNESS FOR BOTH TECHNICIANS IS REQUIRED\n- PPE REQUIRED, HARD HAT, BRIGHT VEST, STEEL TOE SHOES, GLOVES AND GOGGLES\n- hand tools including wrenches and sockets and cable cutters\n- drill motor with bits\n- rope and bucket to lower equipment off the roof\n- SAFETY CERTIFICATION IS REQUIRED TO ENTER THE BUILDING\n\n**TECHNICIAN IS REQUIRED TO TAKE SAFETY CLASS AND RETURN THE COMPLETED CERTIFICATION PRIOR TO GOING TO SITE OR THEY WILL NOT BE ALLOWED INSIDE THE BUILDING. SEE ATTACHED DOCUMENTATION.**\n\n**Special Instructions:**\n\n- Tech must follow scope of work and not deviate.\n- Tech must arrive on time.\n- Tech is not to discuss which Carriers we use or Speed Test results we use with the customer!!!\n- We are providing WILINE DIA Service\n- Tech is not to leave site until ALL pictures are available for Project Manager to view.\n- Requested photos must be uploaded during the visit. Photos uploaded after the visit will not be approved.\n- Photos must be labeled.\n- Failure to check-In and check-out may result in penalties.\n- **STRICLY REQUIRED: Business casual pants, no shorts (slack or kaki), collar shirt no pictures or writing on it, and no flip flops or sandals.**\n- Represent yourself as a WiLine Engineer.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables**\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nService Type: Service Call\n\nShipping parts? Y/N: No – Tech will be returning parts\n\nWorking with NPE Y/N: No\n\nTarget Tech Onsite Date: 10/19\n\nTarget Tech Onsite Time: 10:00 AM\n\nTimes are flexible. Y/N: No\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nRequestor Email (Project Coordinator): suzy.cepress@teladapters.com\n\nSite Contact Name: TBD\n\nSite Contact Phone number: TBD\n\nSite Address: 590 Tyler Industrial Ct, Southern Pines, NC 28387\n\nCompany/Site Name: Amazon\n\nSite Access Hours: 8:00 AM to 3:00 PM\n\nRequested tech name and Field Nation ID:\n\nCSR or RT#: 486800\n\nEstimate labor hours: 3 hours per tech\n\nMAX labor hours: 6 hours total\n\nPURPOSE OF SERVICE CALL/SCOPE OF WORK: Decomm site, remove antennas, wiring, CPE and ship parts back\n\nScope/Onsite Description:\n\n**SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS PLEASE READ: DO NOT REMOVE THE GROMMETS FROM THE RADIOS CUT THE CABLES BELOW THE GROMMET, THIS REDUCES DAMAGE TO THE RADIO WHEN RETURNING TO US.**\n\nContact LPOC and let them know you are onsite, also check out with them\n\nContact Suzy Cepress at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when arriving onsite\n\nDecomm all equipment\n\nFirst remove CPE with power supply and 4 POEs and Fiber handoff with fiber cable\n\nTake pictures before and after removing and upload to the ticket\n\nTake pictures of antennas before and after removing with cables cut\n\nRemove Inseego antennas, when removing antenna, **do not remove grommet covering the cable as this** **damages the antenna, cut the cable below the grommet only. Take pictures of the antenna showing the cut cable and upload to the ticket.**\n\nRemove or cut external wiring\n\nReturn equipment to us with label to be provided\n\nWork order is not complete until equipment has been dropped off at UPS location\n\nContact Suzy for equipment to be shipped back to us\n\nUpload all pictures to ticket when complete\n\nContact \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* prior to leaving site\n\n**ADDITITONAL HOURS and ESCALATION PROCESS:**\n\n- **Additional hours past MAX hours MUST get Project Manager approval. Labor overage past MAX hours that are not pre-approved, will not be paid.**\n- If the Project Manager is not reachable, contact the WiLine support team at 908-651-9350 or WilIne@patstaffing.com.\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with the Project Coordinator. Any issues or questions should be escalated to Project Coordinator or WiLine support team.\n- **Additional Travel & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** Travel expense (over 50 miles) must be pre-approved via counteroffer during your request\n\n**Lift Penalty:** Any additional charges incurred, such as extra lift rentals fees due to changes in the technician’s schedule, will be the responsibility of the technician. These additional fees will be charged back accordingly.\n\n**Parts Plan:** In the event a technician is in possession of installation or return parts, payment will not be approved/issued until a receipt of proof of return is provided. In most cases, return parts will be boxed and left at the site. A shipping label will be provided. Take photo of boxed part in the area left, and upload it to the work order.\n\n**Professionalism**: We adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations & timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T10:00","end":"2026-10-19T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":59.6100333166579},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","s