{"job":{"id":20131983,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pursuant Health","title":"Tighten/Repair BP Mandrel / Repair Kinked Hose, Replace BP Cuff / Hose, Replace the BP Pump and Install Calibration Decal, Replace Decal(s) and PM Kiosk","description":{"html":"<ul><li>A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. <strong>Failure to obtain Release Code</strong> will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.</li><li>CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.</li><li>CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site&#39;s WIFI connection.</li><li>REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox</li><li><strong>Secure the BP Mandrel to the kiosk firmly, and ensure there are no kinks in the BP Hose.</strong><br /><ul><li>Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVBP</li></ul></li><li><strong>Replace the BP Cuff and Hose</strong><br /><ul><li>Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff</li></ul></li><li><strong>Replace the Blood Pressure Pump and Calibration Decal</strong><br /><ul><li>Remove old BP Calibration decal.</li><li>Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.</li><li>Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the links below:</li><li>Blood Pressure Pump: https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump</li><li>Decal Placement: https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump-Decal</li><li>After installing the pump and decal, take a photo of the Calibration Decal and upload to your Work Order.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Replace the Barcode Scanner Decal</strong><br /><ul><li>Remove old and/or damaged decal.</li><li>Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.</li><li>Please refer to the link below for correct placement:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVDecals</li></ul></li><li><strong>Replace the ESD Sensitivity Decal</strong><br /><ul><li>Remove old and/or damaged decal.</li><li>Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.</li><li>Please refer to the link below for correct placement:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVDecals</li></ul></li><li>STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.</li></ul>","markdown":"- A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. **Failure to obtain Release Code** will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.\n- CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.\n- CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site's WIFI connection.\n- REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: <https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox>\n- **Secure the BP Mandrel to the kiosk firmly, and ensure there are no kinks in the BP Hose.**  \n  \n  - Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVBP>\n- **Replace the BP Cuff and Hose**  \n  \n  - Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff>\n- **Replace the Blood Pressure Pump and Calibration Decal**  \n  \n  - Remove old BP Calibration decal.\n  - Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.\n  - Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the links below:\n  - Blood Pressure Pump: <https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump>\n  - Decal Placement: <https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump-Decal>\n  - After installing the pump and decal, take a photo of the Calibration Decal and upload to your Work Order.\n- **Replace the Barcode Scanner Decal**  \n  \n  - Remove old and/or damaged decal.\n  - Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.\n  - Please refer to the link below for correct placement:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVDecals>\n- **Replace the ESD Sensitivity Decal**  \n  \n  - Remove old and/or damaged decal.\n  - Remove any old sticker residue and clean the area before placing new decal.\n  - Please refer to the link below for correct placement:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVDecals>\n- STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T09:00","end":"2026-10-14T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-14T09:45"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":55.55525224991613},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end"