{"job":{"id":20132146,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Telco Holdings Inc","title":"Legacy equipment clean up in Live Clinic","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong>Upon assignment you are acknowledging that you have reviewed and understand all of the attached documentation (including but not limited to site floor plans and in depth SOW documents) </strong></li><li><strong>Once you have called your work order manager to check in, you MUST CALL the Ivy Help Desk Line to verify SOW before proceeding 484-713-9992 </strong></li><li><strong>All SOW questions/concerns should be relayed to 484-713-9992</strong></li><li><strong>TECH MUST SHOP VAC AND CLEAN UP SITE PRIOR TO LEAVING</strong></li></ul><p>SOW is also attached to the Work Order</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;Read the whole SOW before starting work!!</em></strong></p><p>Call WOM when arriving, when leaving and any questions.</p><p><strong><em>Upon arrival on-site, check-in and introduce yourself and that you are with Thinc Forward to do a legacy equipment site clean out. </em></strong></p><p>You are 0nsite on behalf of ITBP: James Sullivan<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">.</span></p><p>Be courteous and respectful of the environment and employees.</p><p>Any challenges or issues, immediately reach out to your work order manager (WOM).</p><p>Be mindful of your environment - language and comments.</p><p>1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Edgeboot in box:</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On the white rack, next to the standing rack there is a box “Granite Edgeboot”. This is to be shipped back to THI</p><p>2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Legacy Printer and PCs:</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove old printer and PCs.</p><p>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;They are to be put in a box in the network closet.</p><p>3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Legacy phones:</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove all legacy phones from the desk or wherever they are.</p><p>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;They are to be put in a box in the network closet.</p><p>4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Legacy Modem:</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This is to be disconnected and given to a person at the front desk.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Put the name of the person you handed it to in the work order.</p><p>5)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Legacy Network standing rack:</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cut all cables from patch panel and coil up and secure above the drop ceiling.</p><p>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove of old patch panels and dispose of.</p><p>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove all equipment from the rack and put in a box in the network room.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All patch cables are to be disposed of.</p><p>d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Servers at the bottom of the standing rack are to be removed and boxed up.</p><p>e.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Battery backup is to be powered down, alarms silenced and put in box in the network room</p><p>f.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rack is to be clean of all debris when done. NOTHING HANGING.</p><p>6)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Shipping will need to be expensed.</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ship to:</p><p> Jonathan Bromley</p><p>Ticket #<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">600288</span></p><p> C/O Telco Holdings, Inc.</p><p>1161 McDermott Drive,</p><p> Suite 260,</p><p> West Chester, PA 19380</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Parts will need to be purchased before job and bring to job site:</em></strong></p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3, large boxes to put equipment in</p><p><strong><em>Pictures needed:</em></strong></p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Overall Network room, showing empty standing rack and boxes.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Old AT&amp;T Modem showing S/N.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;New Modem showing S/N and MAC address</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peplink label on back showing S/N</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Edgeboot sticker showing S/N</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cato label showing S/N</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All legacy equipment, showing where it is.</p><p>General:</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech is responsible for removing and disposing of all trash from the site.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech is to take pictures of all work. Close up shots and overall location shots</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ceilings are 8’. Bring Ladder.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Before leaving make sure all equipment that was up when you arrived is up.</p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><em>By accepting this project, you understand and agree it is required to have all the necessary tools &amp; equipment to complete the job tasks detailed in the Statement of Work. If all work is not completed according to the SOW, a dispute will be submitted, and wages could be garnished.</em></strong></p><p>1 Techs, up to 4 hours.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ***</strong></p><p><strong>*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered.&nbsp;*</strong></p><p><strong>﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager.&nbsp;Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.</strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ol><li><strong>Call</strong>&nbsp;your assigned Work Order Manager to check in onsite</li><li><strong>Call</strong>&nbsp;484-713-9992 regarding Call Ivy Rehab Project Management line to check in and verify work being requested</li><li><strong>After work has been completed, ensure work area is cleaned up</strong></li><li><strong>Upload/take photo</strong>&nbsp;of Provide Images of all completed work</li><li><strong>Collect signature</strong>&nbsp;from Collect a signature from your local contact onsite</li><li><strong>Call</strong>&nbsp;484-713-9992 regarding Call the Ivy Rehab Project Management line to check out of site and verify all work has been completed</li><li>Call your assigned Work Order Manager to check out of site</li><li>Only If applicable - Return equipment to closest UPS Store and provide Tracking Info</li></ol>","markdown":"- **Upon assignment you are acknowledging that you have reviewed and understand all of the attached documentation (including but not limited to site floor plans and in depth SOW documents)**\n- **Once you have called your work order manager to check in, you MUST CALL the Ivy Help Desk Line to verify SOW before proceeding 484-713-9992**\n- **All SOW questions/concerns should be relayed to 484-713-9992**\n- **TECH MUST SHOP VAC AND CLEAN UP SITE PRIOR TO LEAVING**\n\nSOW is also attached to the Work Order\n\n ***Read the whole SOW before starting work!!***\n\nCall WOM when arriving, when leaving and any questions.\n\n***Upon arrival on-site, check-in and introduce yourself and that you are with Thinc Forward to do a legacy equipment site clean out.***\n\nYou are 0nsite on behalf of ITBP: James Sullivan.\n\nBe courteous and respectful of the environment and employees.\n\nAny challenges or issues, immediately reach out to your work order manager (WOM).\n\nBe mindful of your environment - language and comments.\n\n1\\) Edgeboot in box:\n\na. On the white rack, next to the standing rack there is a box “Granite Edgeboot”. This is to be shipped back to THI\n\n2\\) Legacy Printer and PCs:\n\na. Remove old printer and PCs.\n\nb. They are to be put in a box in the network closet.\n\n3\\) Legacy phones:\n\na. Remove all legacy phones from the desk or wherever they are.\n\nb. They are to be put in a box in the network closet.\n\n4\\) Legacy Modem:\n\na. This is to be disconnected and given to a person at the front desk.\n\n i. Put the name of the person you handed it to in the work order.\n\n5\\) Legacy Network standing rack:\n\na. Cut all cables from patch panel and coil up and secure above the drop ceiling.\n\nb. Remove of old patch panels and dispose of.\n\nc. Remove all equipment from the rack and put in a box in the network room.\n\n i. All patch cables are to be disposed of.\n\nd. Servers at the bottom of the standing rack are to be removed and boxed up.\n\ne. Battery backup is to be powered down, alarms silenced and put in box in the network room\n\nf. Rack is to be clean of all debris when done. NOTHING HANGING.\n\n6\\) Shipping will need to be expensed.\n\na. Ship to:\n\n Jonathan Bromley\n\nTicket #600288\n\n C/O Telco Holdings, Inc.\n\n1161 McDermott Drive,\n\n Suite 260,\n\n West Chester, PA 19380\n\n***Parts will need to be purchased before job and bring to job site:***\n\n\\- 3, large boxes to put equipment in\n\n***Pictures needed:***\n\n\\- Overall Network room, showing empty standing rack and boxes.\n\n\\- Old AT&T Modem showing S/N.\n\n\\- New Modem showing S/N and MAC address\n\n\\- Peplink label on back showing S/N\n\n\\- Edgeboot sticker showing S/N\n\n\\- Cato label showing S/N\n\n\\- All legacy equipment, showing where it is.\n\nGeneral:\n\n\\- Tech is responsible for removing and disposing of all trash from the site.\n\n\\- Tech is to take pictures of all work. Close up shots and overall location shots\n\n\\- Ceilings are 8’. Bring Ladder.\n\n\\- Before leaving make sure all equipment that was up when you arrived is up.\n\n***By accepting this project, you understand and agree it is required to have all the necessary tools & equipment to complete the job tasks detailed in the Statement of Work. If all work is not completed according to the SOW, a dispute will be submitted, and wages could be garnished.***\n\n1 Techs, up to 4 hours.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered. \\***\n\n**﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager. Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.**\n\n1. **Call** your assigned Work Order Manager to check in onsite\n2. **Call** 484-713-9992 regarding Call Ivy Rehab Project Management line to check in and verify work being requested\n3. **After work has been completed, ensure work area is cleaned up**\n4. **Upload/take photo** of Provide Images of all completed work\n5. **Collect signature** from Collect a signature from your local contact onsite\n6. **Call** 484-713-9992 regarding Call the Ivy Rehab Project Management line to check out of site and verify all work has been completed\n7. Call your assigned Work Order Manager to check out of site\n8. Only If applicable - Return equipment to closest UPS Store and provide Tracking Info","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-14T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":21.753707174134878},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (co