{"job":{"id":"3398425843","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey","description":"\"Please check in and out with Property Manager<br>If the survey runs over 2 hours you need to get permission from the Property Manager to continue and please let them know about how much longer would be needed<br>Please survey for all fire alarms, burg alarms, elevators, pool phones\\(voice\\), fax<br>If there are different building on the property there are probably fire alarms in each one<br>Please work with Property Manager to make sure we get the correct information<br>If you have any issues please reach out to Hilal 9194246791 or 919-870-5080<br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER \\(LCON\\)<br>1\\. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL\\.<br>2\\. Check in and out through Work Market\\. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3\\. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard\\.epik\\.io to begin the Survey process\\. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard\\.  \\(Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used\\.\\)<br>4\\. Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard\\.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team\\.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site\\.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process\\.<br>5\\. Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results\\.<br>6\\. Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey\\. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services\\. <br> <br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool \\(66 &amp; 110\\) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws \\(drywall, masonry, wood\\), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable \\(for analog devices\\), Cat6 Ethernet Cable \\(for data connections\\), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Infrared Temperature Gun\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T10:00","end":"2026-09-16T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":235},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":20.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/16/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791479240629}
{"job":{"id":20132603,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Site Survey for Automated Locker System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.</strong></p><p>Overview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.</p><p>Background: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Main Contacts</u></strong></p><p><strong>Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)</strong></p><p>Please call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.</p><ul><li><strong><u>We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.</u></strong></li></ul><p>Tech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</p><p>Indoor Zhilai -&nbsp;-</p><p>HIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:</strong></p><p>Technician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.</p><p>Work order may NOT be rescheduled.&nbsp;Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.&nbsp;Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.</strong></li><li><strong>AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.</strong></li><li><strong>Stud Finder</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;(for checking in and out)</li><li><strong>Digital Camera</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attachment:</strong></p><p>0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf&nbsp;- Print and bring to site.</p><p>=======================</p><p>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</p><p>DIRECTIONS</p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location</li><li>Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of room where locker will be installed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.</li></ul><ol><li>Take the photos outline in the instructions.</li><li>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</li><li>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out</li><li><strong>Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</strong></li><li><strong>Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.</strong></li></ol><p>=======================</p><p>Site Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.**\n\nOverview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.\n\nBackground: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**Main Contacts**\n\n**Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)**\n\nPlease call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.\n\n- **We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.**\n- **For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.**\n\nTech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3\n\n**READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\nTechnician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.\n\nWork order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum**\n- **Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.**\n- **AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.**\n- **Stud Finder**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** (for checking in and out)\n- **Digital Camera**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachment:**\n\n0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf - Print and bring to site.\n\n=======================\n\nREAD THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location\n2. Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:\n\n- Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.\n- Measurements of room where locker will be installed.\n- Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.\n\n1. Take the photos outline in the instructions.\n2. Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.\n3. Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out\n4. **Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n5. **Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.**\n\n=======================\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T09:30","end":"2026-10-09T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11.38097942170361},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co