{"job":{"id":20132642,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | QSIC Pendant Speaker Installation [Revisit]","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong><em>(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p>\n<p>Revisit to take a complete set of deliverable and relocate ava</p>\n<p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong><em>(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p>\n<p>Pendant Speakers</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Important</strong> : Technicians&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;read the&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>entire work order and all provided documentation</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</li>\n<li><strong>Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Not allowed</strong> : T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</li>\n<li>These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</li>\n<li><strong>Penalties Apply IF you do not</strong></li>\n<li><strong>PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Do Not Call&nbsp;&nbsp;Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;if you are exceeding&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>4 Hours Onsite</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Techs&nbsp;&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Revisit to take a complete set of deliverable and relocate ava</li>\n<li><strong><u>Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide –</u>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;any questions or issues need to be escalated to the&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Techs MUST</strong> PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!</li>\n<li><strong><u>Techs&nbsp;</u>&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.</li>\n<li>Technicians (Tech 1/Lead &amp; Assist)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;complete the Essintial Online Deliverable – Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.</li>\n<li><strong>Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;- <strong>One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;and the other technician will be designated as an&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST</strong> .&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Communication Requirements</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>ALL installation questions must go to&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;call&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite – You MUST obtain approval!!!</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Technicians MUST</strong> Check-In and Check-Out with the <strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)</li>\n<li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li>\n<li>Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi</li>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools</li>\n<li>10Ft-12Ft Ladder</li>\n<li>Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)</li>\n<li>Long fiberglass push rods</li>\n<li>wire strippers</li>\n<li>Electrical Dykes</li>\n<li>Utility Knife</li>\n<li>Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors</li>\n<li>Multi-meter - Capable of reading Ohms</li>\n<li>Small Alan wrench – for pendant lock</li>\n<li>Small Phillips and flat head screw driver</li>\n<li>Micro flathead screwdriver</li>\n<li>Laser Distance Measure &amp; Tape Measure</li>\n<li>Velcro</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Government Issued ID</li>\n<li>LOA – Letter of Authorization</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Bill of Material:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;FIRM START TIME!!!! Y