{"job":{"id":"8145065101","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"IW for Thurs 10/8 4-6PM EDT Hard Start to Install New FEX 511G | Repair tkt 7034659","description":"P1 Approved by Granite<br>Granite NOC Repair Ticket #: 7034659<br>Choice Ticket #: 7037065<br><br>Objective: Replace current FEX-511G with new 511G(The old 511G has a SN of FXN51GS225002791)<br><br>Scope Of Work:<br>1.Tech must check in with Granite Valvoline Support 833-363-8677 to clarify any SOW issues. Granite NOC will stay on the line with the tech to complete device swap. <br>2. Replace FEX211E. Tech must locate shipment and provide the serial number of the new FEX. Authorize the new FEX (deauthorize the old FEX and delete from Fortigate). Move SIM cards over from old to new FEX. <br>3.Using tech's laptop, connect to port 1 on the FEX-511G and go to https://192.168.200.99/ to access the FEX GUI. Upgrade FEX-511G firmware to v7.6.4 using firmware image file transferred to tech's laptop. <br>4.Granite NOC is to MAKE SURE the FEX is pulling an IP. Once FEX is online pulling an IP, run a short ping test to confirm no packet loss. <br>5.Tech will take pictures of all work performed and submit as part of closeouts. Tech must also find return label and return old device back to Granite. <br>6.Tech must call Granite Valvoline Support 833-363-8677 prior to departing the site.<br><br>Required Equipment: Tech will need bring a laptop and charger with Windows 7 or higher and admin rights to prove connectivity, Cisco Console Cable, Hot spot capability,<br> Cable Certifier capable of displaying length, a patch cord, a splitter and a minimum of 3 filters. Cell phone, Cell phone charger, buttset and Minimum of 150’ of Cat5e cable.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-08T16:00","end":"2026-10-08T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":80.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":nul