{"job":{"id":20125477,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Catcon Products","title":"Lumen ODU2002 Router","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in network equipment installs and configuration.</li><li>Tech is required to install an InHand ODU2002 Unit&nbsp;</li><li><strong>If possible, the installation will be performed externally. The technician will need to evaluate the site for an existing or provided wall or roof penetration that can accommodate a CAT6 cable to be routed back to the customer's IT room. Possible existing external access points may include external lights, cameras, or conduits that bring power or telecommunications lines into the building. When using an existing penetration make sure the ODU installation will not interfere with lighting or cameras. <u>The technician is not allowed to create any new wall or roof penetrations.</u> If the customer has not provided external access or existing penetration, the installation would take place inside. The selected indoor location will be verified with a speed test. </strong></li><li>Estimated duration will be 1 - 4 Hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code: </strong></p><ul><li>Business Casual</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong><em> </em></p><ul><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Screwdriver (flat &amp; philip)</li><li>Zip ties</li><li>Cutter</li><li>Laptop with ethernet cable</li><li>Ladder</li><li>Ability to cut and replace ethernet connector on cable if required.</li><li>Assorted Hardware for mounting the ODU to different surfaces. Brackets are supplied with the device.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements </em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Please review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.</li><li>&nbsp;Print off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.</li><li>Watch installation video guide prior to arriving onsite <a href=\"https://youtu.be/sKNAT2EcsX4\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/sKNAT2EcsX4</a></li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks </em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.</li><li>Every ODU2002 product shipped from the factory includes common accessories. Includes 100ft ethernet cable and surge protector. After you receive the product, please check carefully. If you find any missing or damaged parts, please contact 10T Solutions support. <del>*************</del></li><li>Every unit shipped from the factory has been configured and tested. No configuration setup is required.</li><li>Equipment Installation:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power supply: ODU2002 is powered by 802.af standard (50V/0.3A), please pay attention to the power voltage level.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Environmental requirements: working temperature: -30℃～70℃, storage temperature: -40℃～85℃.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Support to be mounted with bracket. Mount away from heat source or strong electromagnetic interference. Confirm that the installation position is strong enough to support the weight of the equipment and its installation accessories.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check for cables and antennas required for installation.</li><li>Attach Antennas</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach eight antennas to the TNC connectors marked 5G/5G MIMO/Wi-Fi and GNSS.</li><li><strong>Choosing a Location for Mounting the Device</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Mount the router as high as possible. Location of the device will have the greatest effect on performance. If external access is not available and the device is installed inside, locating near a window or on an external wall as high as possible is best practice. Placing the ODU on a shelf or in a rack is not acceptable. It must be mounted on a wall. If the LCON instructs that it must be located in a specific location, document on the acceptance sheet and locate as instructed.</strong></li><li>Install the mounting plate.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the mounting plate to the ODU2002 using screws. Please make sure the top side facing upwards.</li><li>Wall- mounted installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the adjustable base on the wall in the desired angle and position.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the mounted ODU2002 to the base. Tighten the mounting bolts to lock the ODU2002 in place</li><li>Pole -mounted installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the adjustable base on the pole in the desired angle and position.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the mounted ODU2002 to the base. Tighten the mounting bolts to lock the ODU2002 in place.</li><li>Connect the Ethernet Cable</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please make sure that the ethernet cable is inserted into the device in a standardized way. If not, the crystal head may be damaged when installing the waterproof PG head.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">When removing the ethernet cable, the waterproof PG head must be removed first, and then the crystal head connected to the device must be removed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please confirm the diameter of Ethernet cable is between 4.8 mm to 6.5 mm.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please ensure the cable glands are properly assembled to prevent leaks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cut the Ethernet cable to the appropriate length according to the distance from the ODU to the power supply and pass it through the bracket.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Use the ethernet cable after the crystal head is processed and pass through the waterproof PG head in the order shown in the figure below.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Schematic diagram of patch cable passing through waterproof head</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Insert the Ethernet cable into the network port of the device and tighten the waterproof head in the order of B, C, D, E to complete the installation.</li><li>Connect PoE Power Adapter</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect one end of the Ethernet cable to the PoE 2.5G LAN1 port and plug the other end into the 802.af(50V/0.3A) PoE Adapter or a router/switch with 802.3af port.</li><li>&nbsp;Network Connections</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>You will not make any connections to customer equipment. Any connections via LAN will be made by the customer.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If installing for internet backup, connect an existing internet to the WAN port if the customer has supplied the cable.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">WiFi can be enabled by request to Lumen or 10T support <del>************</del>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. If speeds are still below minimum call 10T support at </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></strong><strong>. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Report.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><p><strong>All Deliverables must be uploaded immediately upon completion.</strong></p><ol><li>Upload before and after photos</li><li>Upload Cellular Speed Test Screenshot.</li><li>Complete 10T Solutions Acceptance Sheet.</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process: </strong></p><p>Any issue with the installation call the 10T Support Hotline. <del>************</del></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with <del>*************</del></li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to <del>*************</del></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy </strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Any additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in network equipment installs and configuration.\n- Tech is required to install an InHand ODU2002 Unit\n- **If possible, the installation will be performed externally. The technician will need to evaluate the site for an existing or provided wall or roof penetration that can accommodate a CAT6 cable to be routed back to the customer's IT room. Possible existing external access points may include external lights, cameras, or conduits that bring power or telecommunications lines into the building. When using an existing penetration make sure the ODU installation will not interfere with lighting or cameras. The technician is not allowed to create any new wall or roof penetrations. If the customer has not provided external access or existing penetration, the installation would take place inside. The selected indoor location will be verified with a speed test.**\n- Estimated duration will be 1 - 4 Hours.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business Casual\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Screwdriver (flat & philip)\n- Zip ties\n- Cutter\n- Laptop with ethernet cable\n- Ladder\n- Ability to cut and replace ethernet connector on cable if required.\n- Assorted Hardware for mounting the ODU to different surfaces. Brackets are supplied with the device.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Please review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.\n2. Print off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.\n3. Watch installation video guide prior to arriving onsite [](https://youtu.be/sKNAT2EcsX4)<https://youtu.be/sKNAT2EcsX4>\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.\n2. Every ODU2002 product shipped from the factory includes common accessories. Includes 100ft ethernet cable and surge protector. After you receive the product, please check carefully. If you find any missing or damaged parts, please contact 10T Solutions support. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Every unit shipped from the factory has been configured and tested. No configuration setup is required.\n4. Equipment Installation:\n5. Power supply: ODU2002 is powered by 802.af standard (50V/0.3A), please pay attention to the power voltage level.\n6. Environmental requirements: working temperature: -30℃～70℃, storage temperature: -40℃～85℃.\n7. Support to be mounted with bracket. Mount away from heat source or strong electromagnetic interference. Confirm that the installation position is strong enough to support the weight of the equipment and its installation accessories.\n8. Check for cables and antennas required for installation.\n9. Attach Antennas\n10. Attach eight antennas to the TNC connectors marked 5G/5G MIMO/Wi-Fi and GNSS.\n11. **Choosing a Location for Mounting the Device**\n12. **Mount the router as high as possible. Location of the device will have the greatest effect on performance. If external access is not available and the device is installed inside, locating near a window or on an external wall as high as possible is best practice. Placing the ODU on a shelf or in a rack is not acceptable. It must be mounted on a wall. If the LCON instructs that it must be located in a specific location, document on the acceptance sheet and locate as instructed.**\n13. Install the mounting plate.\n14. Attach the mounting plate to the ODU2002 using screws. Please make sure the top side facing upwards.\n15. Wall- mounted installation\n16. Install the adjustable base on the wall in the desired angle and position.\n17. Attach the mounted ODU2002 to the base. Tighten the mounting bolts to lock the ODU2002 in place\n18. Pole -mounted installation\n19. Install the adjustable base on the pole in the desired angle and position.\n20. Attach the mounted ODU2002 to the base. Tighten the mounting bolts to lock the ODU2002 in place.\n21. Connect the Ethernet Cable\n22. Please make sure that the ethernet cable is inserted into the device in a standardized way. If not, the crystal head may be damaged when installing the waterproof PG head.\n23. When removing the ethernet cable, the waterproof PG head must be removed first, and then the crystal head connected to the device must be removed.\n24. Please confirm the diameter of Ethernet cable is between 4.8 mm to 6.5 mm.\n25. Please ensure the cable glands are properly assembled to prevent leaks.\n26. Cut the Ethernet cable to the appropriate length according to the distance from the ODU to the power supply and pass it through the bracket.\n27. Use the ethernet cable after the crystal head is processed and pass through the waterproof PG head in the order shown in the figure below.\n28. Schematic diagram of patch cable passing through waterproof head\n29. Insert the Ethernet cable into the network port of the device and tighten the waterproof head in the order of B, C, D, E to complete the installation.\n30. Connect PoE Power Adapter\n31. Connect one end of the Ethernet cable to the PoE 2.5G LAN1 port and plug the other end into the 802.af(50V/0.3A) PoE Adapter or a router/switch with 802.3af port.\n32. Network Connections\n33. **You will not make any connections to customer equipment. Any connections via LAN will be made by the customer.**\n34. If installing for internet backup, connect an existing internet to the WAN port if the customer has supplied the cable.\n35. WiFi can be enabled by request to Lumen or 10T support \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n36. **Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. If speeds are still below minimum call 10T support at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*****. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Report.**\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n**All Deliverables must be uploaded immediately upon completion.**\n\n1. Upload before and after photos\n2. Upload Cellular Speed Test Screenshot.\n3. Complete 10T Solutions Acceptance Sheet.\n4. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nAny issue with the installation call the 10T Support Hotline. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-18T08:00","end":"2026-11-18T10:00","latestStart":"2026-11-18T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":36.0726635521234},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-08T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-E