{"job":{"id":20131809,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axiom Service Management LLC","title":"Diagnose and Repair - Zebra ZT410 - Main Drive Belt Replacement ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Work order description:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Issue: Main Drive belt replacement</p>\n<p>Part Number: 79866M-C</p>\n<p>Part Description: Zebra ZT410 Main Drive Belt (203dpi)</p>\n<p>FedEx Number: n/a</p>\n<p><strong><u>Service manuals can be found at:</u>&nbsp;</strong>https://www.synergyitx.com/manuals</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p>\n<p>1. Do not bid on a Work Order unless you are qualified to work on the specified equipment.</p>\n<p>2. If awaiting dispatch instructions for a call, contact your dispatcher before proceeding to the onsite location.</p>\n<p>3. While onsite, providers are to exclusively represent themselves as HP technicians.</p>\n<p>4. Providers are authorized to work solely on the device specified in their Work Orders. Requests for additional work on other units should be directed to the customer's help desk.</p>\n<p>5. Providers must call dispatch after arriving onsite if experiencing any issues, including difficulties in locating the printer, finding parts, or the user.</p>\n<p>6. Exceptional customer service and communication are crucial for all service tickets. Providers are expected to adhere to general instructions. Failure to comply may result in delayed or non-payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Providers are expected to adhere to a Business Casual dress code. This includes:</p>\n<p>- Slacks or Nice Jeans with no holes</p>\n<p>- Collared Shirt: Polo or Long Sleeve (Shirts with no logos or small logos are preferred)</p>\n<p>- Closed-toe Safety Shoes/Boots with protective Toe</p>\n<p>- Hard Hat and Vest</p>\n<p><strong><u>Required/Recommended Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Providers should come prepared with the necessary tools for efficient service. These can include: Smart Phone, Vacuum, Alcohol, Q-tips, Wipes, Soft Bristle Brush, Canned Air, Light Machine Oil, Allen Wrenches (Metric and Standard), Digital Voltmeter, Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers, and a Laptop and Wireless Hotspot.</p>\n<p><strong><u>NDA will need to be signed prior to work on site</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Please note that it is the technician's responsibility to provide images of all unused parts before closing the work order. Unused parts should not be left at the customer site. The technician must retain the parts and return them once the return label is provided.</u></strong></p>\n<p>It is very difficult to arrange returns after the 15-day return period has passed, so your prompt cooperation is greatly appreciated.</p>\n<p>Going forward, please ensure that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Images of all unused parts (including serial numbers) are shared at the time of case closure.</li>\n<li>Unused parts are not left at the customer site.</li>\n<li>Unused parts are retained by the technician and returned promptly upon receipt of the return label.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**Work order description:**\n\nIssue: Main Drive belt replacement\n\nPart Number: 79866M-C\n\nPart Description: Zebra ZT410 Main Drive Belt (203dpi)\n\nFedEx Number: n/a\n\n**Service manuals can be found at:** <https://www.synergyitx.com/manuals>\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1\\. Do not bid on a Work Order unless you are qualified to work on the specified equipment.\n\n2\\. If awaiting dispatch instructions for a call, contact your dispatcher before proceeding to the onsite location.\n\n3\\. While onsite, providers are to exclusively represent themselves as HP technicians.\n\n4\\. Providers are authorized to work solely on the device specified in their Work Orders. Requests for additional work on other units should be directed to the customer's help desk.\n\n5\\. Providers must call dispatch after arriving onsite if experiencing any issues, including difficulties in locating the printer, finding parts, or the user.\n\n6\\. Exceptional customer service and communication are crucial for all service tickets. Providers are expected to adhere to general instructions. Failure to comply may result in delayed or non-payment.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nProviders are expected to adhere to a Business Casual dress code. This includes:\n\n\\- Slacks or Nice Jeans with no holes\n\n\\- Collared Shirt: Polo or Long Sleeve (Shirts with no logos or small logos are preferred)\n\n\\- Closed-toe Safety Shoes/Boots with protective Toe\n\n\\- Hard Hat and Vest\n\n**Required/Recommended Tools:**\n\nProviders should come prepared with the necessary tools for efficient service. These can include: Smart Phone, Vacuum, Alcohol, Q-tips, Wipes, Soft Bristle Brush, Canned Air, Light Machine Oil, Allen Wrenches (Metric and Standard), Digital Voltmeter, Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers, and a Laptop and Wireless Hotspot.\n\n**NDA will need to be signed prior to work on site**\n\n**Please note that it is the technician's responsibility to provide images of all unused parts before closing the work order. Unused parts should not be left at the customer site. The technician must retain the parts and return them once the return label is provided.**\n\nIt is very difficult to arrange returns after the 15-day return period has passed, so your prompt cooperation is greatly appreciated.\n\nGoing forward, please ensure that:\n\n- Images of all unused parts (including serial numbers) are shared at the time of case closure.\n- Unused parts are not left at the customer site.\n- Unused parts are retained by the technician and returned promptly upon receipt of the return label.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T08:00","end":"2026-10-13T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":20.87584785103218},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RT