{"job":{"id":20136159,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Installation of ATA and Starlink for Rimmers Garage","description":{"html":"<p><strong>ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>1 2port ATA</p>\n<p>1 Router</p>\n<p>1 Starlink Kit</p>\n<p>Will need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point</p>\n<p>Drill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit</p>\n<p>9/16 in hex socket or wrench</p>\n<p>Marker</p>\n<p>Level</p>\n<p>- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).</p>\n<p>- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.</p>\n<p>- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.</p>\n<p>- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.</p>\n<p>- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.</p>\n<p>- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.</p>\n<p>-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).</p>\n<p>Will need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.</p>\n<p>See example pictures of the mount being used.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>This is an <strong>ATA/Gateway installation only</strong> — no new phones will be installed.</li>\n<li>Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached<strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n<li>See <strong>gateway install scope.pdf</strong> for detailed installation guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.</li>\n<li>Check in with support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable</li>\n<li>Minimum 16 RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**ATA / Gateway Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog telephone experience to install an ATA (Analog Telephone Adapter) / Gateway to provide phone and fax service. Must have working knowledge of 66 block connections and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1 2port ATA\n\n1 Router\n\n1 Starlink Kit\n\nWill need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point\n\nDrill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit\n\n9/16 in hex socket or wrench\n\nMarker\n\nLevel\n\n\\- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).\n\n\\- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.\n\n\\- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.\n\n\\- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.\n\n\\- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.\n\n\\- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.\n\n-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).\n\nWill need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.\n\nSee example pictures of the mount being used.\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- This is an **ATA/Gateway installation only** — no new phones will be installed.\n- Complete work within the maximum time listed on the attached**Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n- See **gateway install scope.pdf** for detailed installation guidelines.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed per the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Use a hands-free device to stay in contact with support throughout the installation.\n- Check in with support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e/CAT6 cable\n- Minimum 16 RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nIf another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install the ATA/Gateway and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":25.137745053806206},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791500605039}
{"job":{"id":20136161,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Site Survey for ADtran/PRI and ATA and Starlink at Rimmers Garage","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Telco/VoIP Installer – Pre-Install Site Survey</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions requires an experienced technician to conduct a Site Survey prior to phone service installation.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Planned Equipment for Install</p>\n<p>1 2port ATA</p>\n<p>1 Router</p>\n<p>1 Starlink Kit</p>\n<p>Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).</p>\n<p>Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.</p>\n<p>Determine length of cable needed to connect dish from the power supply/router location. Basic kit i 49.2 ft long advise if longer will be needed.</p>\n<p>See example pictures of the mount being used.</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify equipment listed in the <strong>gateway install scope.pdf</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Possible Adtran Deployment</strong> — Document<strong>all analog phone numbers</strong> found and note whether each is from a PBX or Telco provider.</li>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit (as applicable).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Scope of Survey</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify <strong>only</strong> the equipment listed above and on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Base your survey strictly on these items.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Strict Scope Control (Critical)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Do <strong>not</strong> discuss concerns, needs, equipment changes, network issues, or recommendations with the site contact.</li>\n<li>Do <strong>not</strong> answer questions outside the defined scope.</li>\n<li>Direct all issues to UGS only.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure to follow scope requirements will result in non-payment for time on-site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Punctuality</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on time — the customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.</li>\n<li>Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.</li>\n<li>Notify UGS immediately if you will be late.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Call Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call in for check-in to receive site-specific instructions.</li>\n<li>Call for check-out and survey review <strong>before leaving the site</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Submission Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Upload the Site Survey Form and all required photos the<strong>same day</strong>.</li>\n<li>Late submission will result in a 50% payment penalty (Survey work orders only).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Installation Priority</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The technician who performs the Site Survey receives priority for the installation.</li>\n<li>If bundled with installation, acceptance commits you to both the Survey and Install dates.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Alarm Notice</p>\n<p>Before disconnecting any alarm phone line, inform the customer. Disconnecting may cause audible alerts and, in rare cases, trigger the alarm.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>PRI / Adtran Sites – Additional Requirements</p>\n<p><strong>Only applicable if the site has a PRI/Adtran.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A T1 crossover cable may be required at install. Pinout diagram is attached.</li>\n<li>You will need a <strong>DB9 (RS232 serial) to USB adapter</strong> to program the Adtran from your laptop. Recommended adapter: Sabrent USB to Serial Adapter</li>\n<li>Can be sourced locally if needed (same as USB-to-serial console cable; longer cable or USB extension may be required).</li>\n<li>Photo of the Adtran model used is attached.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Reference Documents</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ATA, PRI Survey Documents.pdf</li>\n<li>gateway install scope.pdf</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>ONLY IF THE SITE HAS A PRI/ADTRAN WILL THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTIONS BE APPLICABLE.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Attached is the pinout needed at the install portion of this to make a T1 crossover cable if needed. Will also need a DBN (RS232 serial 9 min to USB adapter cable) for us to use your laptop to program the adtran. Photo of adtran we use attached as well.</li>\n<li>Can source the cable locally if needed. Should be same as USB to serial for console but will need a longer one or USB ext if you have the short adapter.</li>\n<li>https://www.amazon.com/Sabrent-RS-232-Adapter-Prolific-SBT-USC6K/dp/B000A1KD1K/ref=asc_df_B000A1KD1K/?tag=hyprod-20&amp;linkCode=df0&amp;hvadid=312824707815&amp;hvpos=&amp;hvnetw=g&amp;hvrand=11908894597563970069&amp;hvpone=&amp;hvptwo=&amp;hvqmt=&amp;hvdev=c&amp;hvdvcmdl=&amp;hvlocint=&amp;hvlocphy=9028295&amp;hvtargid=pla-570414526203&amp;th=1</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Telco/VoIP Installer – Pre-Install Site Survey**\n\nUnified Global Solutions requires an experienced technician to conduct a Site Survey prior to phone service installation.\n\nPlanned Equipment for Install\n\n1 2port ATA\n\n1 Router\n\n1 Starlink Kit\n\nDownload Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).\n\nChoose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.\n\nDetermine length of cable needed to connect dish from the power supply/router location. Basic kit i 49.2 ft long advise if longer will be needed.\n\nSee example pictures of the mount being used.\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- Verify equipment listed in the **gateway install scope.pdf**.\n- **Possible Adtran Deployment** — Document**all analog phone numbers** found and note whether each is from a PBX or Telco provider.\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit (as applicable).\n\nScope of Survey\n\n- Verify **only** the equipment listed above and on the Field Nation work order.\n- Base your survey strictly on these items.\n\nStrict Scope Control (Critical)\n\n- Do **not** discuss concerns, needs, equipment changes, network issues, or recommendations with the site contact.\n- Do **not** answer questions outside the defined scope.\n- Direct all issues to UGS only.\n- **Failure to follow scope requirements will result in non-payment for time on-site.**\n\nPunctuality\n\n- Arrive on time — the customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.\n- Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.\n- Notify UGS immediately if you will be late.\n\nCall Requirements\n\n- Call in for check-in to receive site-specific instructions.\n- Call for check-out and survey review **before leaving the site**.\n\nSubmission Requirements\n\n- Upload the Site Survey Form and all required photos the**same day**.\n- Late submission will result in a 50% payment penalty (Survey work orders only).\n\nInstallation Priority\n\n- The technician who performs the Site Survey receives priority for the installation.\n- If bundled with installation, acceptance commits you to both the Survey and Install dates.\n\nAlarm Notice\n\nBefore disconnecting any alarm phone line, inform the customer. Disconnecting may cause audible alerts and, in rare cases, trigger the alarm.\n\nPRI / Adtran Sites – Additional Requirements\n\n**Only applicable if the site has a PRI/Adtran.**\n\n- A T1 crossover cable may be required at install. Pinout diagram is attached.\n- You will need a **DB9 (RS232 serial) to USB adapter** to program the Adtran from your laptop. Recommended adapter: Sabrent USB to Serial Adapter\n- Can be sourced locally if needed (same as USB-to-serial console cable; longer cable or USB extension may be required).\n- Photo of the Adtran model used is attached.\n\nReference Documents\n\n- ATA, PRI Survey Documents.pdf\n- gateway install scope.pdf\n\n**ONLY IF THE SITE HAS A PRI/ADTRAN WILL THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTIONS BE APPLICABLE.**\n\n- Attached is the pinout needed at the install portion of this to make a T1 crossover cable if needed. Will also need a DBN (RS232 serial 9 min to USB adapter cable) for us to use your laptop to program the adtran. Photo of adtran we use attached as well.\n- Can source the cable locally if needed. Should be same as USB to serial for console but will need a longer one or USB ext if you have the short adapter.\n- https://www.amazon.com/Sabrent-RS-232-Adapter-Prolific-SBT-USC6K/dp/B000A1KD1K/ref=asc_df_B000A1KD1K/?tag=hyprod-20&amp;linkCode=df0&amp;hvadid=312824707815&amp;hvpos=&amp;hvnetw=g&amp;hvrand=11908894597563970069&amp;hvpone=&amp;hvptwo=&amp;hvqmt=&amp;hvdev=c&amp;hvdvcmdl=&amp;hvlocint=&amp;hvlocphy=9028295&amp;hvtargid=pla-570414526203&amp;th=1","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T10:00","end":"2026-10-13T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":25.137745053806206},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791500611436}
{"job":{"id":"3797534366","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Reality Interactive","title":"Spectrum: 5471 - Garner, NC - Tech Visit to Troubleshoot Rep Wall TV","description":"<p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Approximate Visit Length</u></strong>: 1 hour(s)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>A laptop with an Ethernet port</li><li>Working Ethernet Cable</li><li>Smartphone with Camera</li><li>Screwdriver (multi-bit)</li><li>USB Keyboard and Mouse</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>5-8ft ladder</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Recommended but not required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Power drill with drill bits</li><li>Cable snake</li><li>Spare 3/4\" spacers</li><li>Level</li><li>RJ45 Crimper</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Electronics Duster</li><li>Duct Tape</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Instructions</u></strong></p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact and obtain any necessary hardware</li><li>Call into Reality @860-852-5035 to check in and review SOW</li><li>Make your way to the affected TV&nbsp;</li><li>Verify the TV is&nbsp;powered on&nbsp;</li><li>If the TV is not powered on,&nbsp;Try to power on with remote&nbsp;</li><li>If does not power on, check rocker switch in back is in the on position&nbsp;</li><li>If does not power on unplug power, hold power button 20 seconds,&nbsp;plug back in and try.&nbsp;</li><li>If it still does not power on call RI tech to troubleshoot further&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>If the TV is powered on but has a black screen&nbsp;</li><li>Turn TV off,&nbsp;unplug all devices and cables from Tv except power.&nbsp;</li><li>Note the location of each cable&nbsp;</li><li>Power on the TV&nbsp;</li><li>Does the screen say No Signal?&nbsp;</li><li>If so work with RI Tech to troubleshoot content issues&nbsp;</li><li>If not work with RI tech and Samsung to troubleshoot TV&nbsp;</li><li><br></li><li>Take photos of all associated experiences with content on their screens and any associated hardware.</li><li>Additional testing or photos may be requested by RI Support</li><li>Upload all photos and required documentation before you leave the site</li><li>Any FedEx drop-offs require photo proof (i.e., receipt picture)</li></ol><p><br></p><p><em>Please understand additional troubleshooting steps may be asked by the Reality Interactive Support Team during the visit to ensure all needs are met.</em></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T10:00","end":"2026-10-13T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P2 SIP IW (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791502267848}
{"job":{"id":20136272,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"LEAD Technician | Overnight Store Remodeling - Network/Cabling/POS (Full 8+ Hours Onsite)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining scope: 1. Install and validate:#36  Compactor (.083)#38  Loading Dock (.086)#47  IP Speaker (.166)#18  Cash Office Hallway (.042)2. Project Closeout Confirm beam clamps obtained and install remaining devices requiring them Install remaining camera covers Correct cable management and add J-hooks where needed Remove old cameras after cutover Final CCTV validation with management Site cleanup Palletize old equipment for removal Move lift outside of site for pickup Manager walkthrough Customer signoff Security Code: 845643</p><p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>SOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present</p></BR><p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Seeking Lead<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;<strong>Over Multiple</strong>&nbsp;<strong>NIGHTs</strong>. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.</p><ul><li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">responsible</span>&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;</span>[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li><li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li><li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>***</del>  umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del> REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>***************************************************