{"job":{"id":20136635,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PC Pal Global","title":"Clinic Gateway Upgrade - 2 Units","description":{"html":"<p>We are seeking a technician to perform the following scope:</p><ul><li>Meet the on-site contact and locate a pair (2) of Watchguard gateway devices.</li><li>Identify and temporarily label up to four (4) cables per device to facilitate their correct migration during the service activity.</li><li>Join the provided conference bridge with the Remote Engineering Support Team to begin the cutover effort and coordinate testing.</li><li>Unplug each Watchguard device, disconnect all cables, and remove each device from the rack (one at a time - pausing between each migration for testing).&nbsp;</li><li>Rack a pair of new Cisco 8200 Series routers in place of each Watchguard appliance with a single PSU each and power-on.</li><li>Patch links from previous devices into the new Cisco 8200 Series ports per client provided patch matrix.</li><li>Ensure link on interfaces and advise the remote engineer that testing can begin.</li><li>Following validation of device 1, install device 2 in a similar manner. Once all devices have been validated, confirm completion with remote engineer and site contact.</li><li>Remove all debris to on-site dumpster or pursuant to local trash management strategy.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Specialty tools required:</p><ul><li>A laptop with a Cisco console cable (and appropriate adapter for the cable to operate on the laptop)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Photo deliverables required:</p><ul><li>Before close-up photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced</li><li>Before wide angle photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced</li><li>After close-up photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced</li><li>After wide angle photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced</li></ul>","markdown":"We are seeking a technician to perform the following scope:\n\n- Meet the on-site contact and locate a pair (2) of Watchguard gateway devices.\n- Identify and temporarily label up to four (4) cables per device to facilitate their correct migration during the service activity.\n- Join the provided conference bridge with the Remote Engineering Support Team to begin the cutover effort and coordinate testing.\n- Unplug each Watchguard device, disconnect all cables, and remove each device from the rack (one at a time - pausing between each migration for testing).\n- Rack a pair of new Cisco 8200 Series routers in place of each Watchguard appliance with a single PSU each and power-on.\n- Patch links from previous devices into the new Cisco 8200 Series ports per client provided patch matrix.\n- Ensure link on interfaces and advise the remote engineer that testing can begin.\n- Following validation of device 1, install device 2 in a similar manner. Once all devices have been validated, confirm completion with remote engineer and site contact.\n- Remove all debris to on-site dumpster or pursuant to local trash management strategy.\n\nSpecialty tools required:\n\n- A laptop with a Cisco console cable (and appropriate adapter for the cable to operate on the laptop)\n\nPhoto deliverables required:\n\n- Before close-up photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced\n- Before wide angle photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced\n- After close-up photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced\n- After wide angle photo of all equipment in scope to be replaced","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T16:00","end":"2026-10-21T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":10.727498431376464},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13: