{"job":{"id":20136754,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240 Walgreens Printer Exchange [PRINTER ONSITE] - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. The specific scope is to exchange the existing printer with a replacement unit, testing the operations to ensure proper functionality and image quality. Then packing the old unit using the container from the replacement unit for pickup.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>Exchange printer that was delivered yesterdy and verify functionality with support. This call is high visibility, please be in consistent contact with support to update them<br /><br />PARTS ONSITE</p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>No Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Operations Manual (attached to work order)</li><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Install Guide (attached to work order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li>Confirm the printer exchange tracking by going to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the printer exchange is delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Fuji CX3240 Assembly Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************</del></p><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Check in with the Manager on Duty. Inform them that you are representing Fujifilm Technical Services and that you are there to perform the CX3240F printer exchange, and ask them to locate the replacement unit.</li><li>Contact the support team at&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to confirm the steps needed to complete the exchange.</li><li>Follow the replacement process using the guide attached to this work order.</li><li>You will need 2 people (one per side) to lift the printer off the expansion trays safely. Please work with the MOD onsite for a second person to assist.</li><li>After completing the printer exchange<strong>&nbsp;, MAKE SURE</strong>&nbsp;that the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement printer and installed in the return printer.</li><li>After completing the printer exchange, confirm the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement unit and installed on the return unit.</li><li>Perform 2 test prints from each paper tray, totaling a minimum of 10 prints.</li><li>Contact our support team at&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;to confirm the deliverables and review the printer exchange return process.</li><li>Package the printer being returned following the steps provided in the exchange guide.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the (MOD), and get their signature.</li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the orange shipping caps removed from the replacement unit.</li><li>Image of the orange shipping caps installed on the return unit.</li><li>Images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.</li><li>Image of the printer in the return box with the cover off to confirm it is the right side up and seated in the bottom side of the packaging (handles located at the bottom).</li><li>Image each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <del>***** ********</del> and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. The specific scope is to exchange the existing printer with a replacement unit, testing the operations to ensure proper functionality and image quality. Then packing the old unit using the container from the replacement unit for pickup.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nExchange printer that was delivered yesterdy and verify functionality with support. This call is high visibility, please be in consistent contact with support to update them  \n  \nPARTS ONSITE\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nNo Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Operations Manual (attached to work order)\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Install Guide (attached to work order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. Confirm the printer exchange tracking by going to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** the printer exchange is delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Fuji CX3240 Assembly Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Check in with the Manager on Duty. Inform them that you are representing Fujifilm Technical Services and that you are there to perform the CX3240F printer exchange, and ask them to locate the replacement unit.\n2. Contact the support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the steps needed to complete the exchange.\n3. Follow the replacement process using the guide attached to this work order.\n4. You will need 2 people (one per side) to lift the printer off the expansion trays safely. Please work with the MOD onsite for a second person to assist.\n5. After completing the printer exchange **, MAKE SURE** that the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement printer and installed in the return printer.\n6. After completing the printer exchange, confirm the orange shipping caps have been removed from the replacement unit and installed on the return unit.\n7. Perform 2 test prints from each paper tray, totaling a minimum of 10 prints.\n8. Contact our support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the deliverables and review the printer exchange return process.\n9. Package the printer being returned following the steps provided in the exchange guide.\n10. Complete the work order, check out with the (MOD), and get their signature.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the orange shipping caps removed from the replacement unit.\n- Image of the orange shipping caps installed on the return unit.\n- Images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.\n- Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.\n- Image of the printer in the return box with the cover off to confirm it is the right side up and seated in the bottom side of the packaging (handles located at the bottom).\n- Image each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T09:00","end":"2026-10-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-09T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"ty