warovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"},{"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Weitz LVL12 - Sensor Maintenance & Gateway Installation"},{"start":"2026-10-05T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Network Cable Technician – Low Voltage Tech 1 (AKIRA Crabtree Valley)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791514669878}
{"job":{"id":20137183,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Interface Security Systems","title":"VIDEO>  SERVICE>  CAMERAS DOWN MORE THAN 50 PERCENT","description":{"html":"PO# PO1103314<br/>Special Instructions for Tech: <br/>SR #: <br/>Closeout Info: Please Text STS HD Phone# - (314) 648-2956 for troubleshooting and/or closing out.<br/>Technician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing<br/>If access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.<br/><br/>Interface Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)<br/><br/>System & Model #: <br/><br/>Camera system / Hikvision <br/><br/>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :  <br/><br/>DVR IS OFFLINE<br/><br/>TECHNICIAN MUST BRING: Digital Multimeter, BNC Spot Monitor, BNC crimping tool, Crimp on BNC (Not twist)  Laptop with ethernet. The technician needs to inspect the DVR  for power, connection, and functionality issues. It's wiring, the PDU and all PVMs. If hardware or cabling appears defective, replace or repair it accordingly. The technician should test the camera on-site, coordinating with Help Desk to verify the camera feed is working properly from the control center.   <br/><br/>Parts Needed: <br/><br/>None <br/><br/>Specific Scheduling Request :<br/><br/> None <br/><br/>Other Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request: None<br/><br/>Cause : <br/><br/>Not fully determined <br/><br/>RMA Form: Complete link & Return Label provided. https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88   <br/><br/>Text with Interface Support:  STS: 1-314-648-2956<br/><br/>Support & Cost Analysis Information Only: <br/>Name and title of person onsite: None <br/>Was the customer Available, Willing and Able to troubleshoot? No , no troubleshooting can be done with the customer <br/>Did the customer request a dispatch instead? No","markdown":"PO# PO1103314  \nSpecial Instructions for Tech:   \nSR #:   \nCloseout Info: Please Text STS HD Phone# - (314) 648-2956 for troubleshooting and/or closing out.  \nTechnician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing  \nIf access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.  \n  \nInterface Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)  \n  \nSystem & Model #:   \n  \nCamera system / Hikvision   \n  \nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem :   \n  \nDVR IS OFFLINE  \n  \nTECHNICIAN MUST BRING: Digital Multimeter, BNC Spot Monitor, BNC crimping tool, Crimp on BNC (Not twist) Laptop with ethernet. The technician needs to inspect the DVR for power, connection, and functionality issues. It's wiring, the PDU and all PVMs. If hardware or cabling appears defective, replace or repair it accordingly. The technician should test the camera on-site, coordinating with Help Desk to verify the camera feed is working properly from the control center.   \n  \nParts Needed:   \n  \nNone   \n  \nSpecific Scheduling Request :  \n  \n None   \n  \nOther Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request: None  \n  \nCause :   \n  \nNot fully determined   \n  \nRMA Form: Complete link & Return Label provided. <https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88>   \n  \nText with Interface Support: STS: 1-314-648-2956  \n  \nSupport & Cost Analysis Information Only:   \nName and title of person ons