{"job":{"id":"8876043970","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #269429 -  PIAB Disconnection","description":"<p>Upon Arrival:</p><p>Check in with Tech Americas by calling (281) 668-3211.</p><p>If there’s no answer, email support@tech-americas.com with the TA Incident # in the subject line.</p><p>Upon Completion:</p><p>Check out immediately after finishing the job by calling (281) 668-3211.</p><p>If there’s no answer, email support@tech-americas.com with the TA Incident # in the subject line.</p><p>Communication Requirements:</p><p>All communication must be via phone or email directly with Tech Americas.</p><p>Failure to check in upon arrival will result in the visit being deemed invalid, potentially affecting payment.</p><p>Failure to check out on the same day as the dispatch may result in cancellation of the ticket without payment.</p><p>Important Note: Failure to follow the on-site steps outlined below may result in non-payment for incomplete or improperly completed work.</p><p><br></p><p>****** SCOPE OF WORK ******</p><p>Please send IW to disconnect PIAB</p><p>Box it up</p><p>Hand to PM to be shipped back to ............via USPS</p><p>Access is 9 AM - 4:30 PM</p><p><br></p><p>****** CALL-IN INSTRUCTIONS ******</p><p><br></p><p>WORKING Windows laptop with an RJ45 port Laptop charger Adtran console cable serial 1200881E1 Wireless hotspot Laptop must have: Putty, Hyper Team, Secure CRT or other WORKING terminal software NIC (capable of static and DHCP) Cell phone Cell phone charger Air card for laptop Butt Set - know the difference between the tip and the ring Multimeter: Validate Tip and Ring Voltage Toner: for Identify existing in house wiring to extend circuits Punch down tool: Accurately punch down circuit know the difference between the tip and the ring Cable tester: Validate cables RJ45-to-serial/D89 cable Biscuit Jacks: RJ11 and RJ45 Crimping tool: Ability to make RJ11 and RJ45jacks and terminate ends efficiently RJ45/11 connectors Extra cat5 patch cables (various lengths) Console Cable - RS232 MALE serial console cable for Cisco/Velo RJ45-to-serial/D89 cable Ethernet Loopback Plug: For Data Remote testing Patch Cables - Minimum of 3 PC tool-set (screwdriver set, including Phillips head with small head) Zip ties and/or Velcro.</p><p><br></p><p>****** SPECIAL MATERIALS NEEDED FOR DISPATCH ******</p><p>Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port ,Multimeter wire tester ,Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches ,Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer) ,Biscuit jacks ,Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters ,4-6 ft’ ladder ,Butt Set ,RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors ,100’ extension cord ,Digital Camera ,100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device ,Cell phone w/Hotspot device ,Punch down tool</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please call to .............. upon arrival</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tool Requirements</p><p>Required Tools:</p><p>Phillips and flathead screwdrivers</p><p>Impact tool with 66 and 110 blades (for termination and cutting)</p><p>Tone generator and receiver</p><p>Telephone test set (butt set)</p><p>RJ11 6-position, 4-conductor module (for testing/toning)</p><p>RJ11 and RJ45 crimp tools</p><p>Electrician scissors and/or Cat5e wire strippers</p><p>Needle-nose pliers</p><p>Medium hammer drill/driver with assorted masonry bits (including 5/16” and 3/8” diameters)</p><p>Extended-length masonry bits (up to 3/8”) for thick walls or cinder blocks</p><p>3/8” U-style staple gun with staples</p><p>Label maker with black text on white label tape</p><p>Sharpie permanent marker pens</p><p>Small bubble level</p><p>Laptop with wired Ethernet port, serial-to-USB console, and terminal software (e.g., PuTTY or CRT)</p><p>Mobile phone with a high-quality camera and charger</p><p>Extra battery pack for phone</p><p>Consumable Items (carry as needed):</p><p>Cable ties (assorted lengths and sizes) for cable management</p><p>300+ feet of Cat5e or Cat6 cable</p><p>RJ11/12 