{"job":{"id":"5724694343","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #269344- Install PIAB / IB - OB calls test","description":"<p>Upon Arrival:</p><p>Check in with Tech Americas by calling (281) 668-3211.</p><p>If there’s no answer, email support@tech-americas.com with the TA Incident # in the subject line.</p><p>Upon Completion:</p><p>Check out immediately after finishing the job by calling (281) 668-3211.</p><p>If there’s no answer, email support@tech-americas.com with the TA Incident # in the subject line.</p><p>Communication Requirements:</p><p>All communication must be via phone or email directly with Tech Americas.</p><p>Failure to check in upon arrival will result in the visit being deemed invalid, potentially affecting payment.</p><p>Failure to check out on the same day as the dispatch may result in cancellation of the ticket without payment.</p><p>Important Note: Failure to follow the on-site steps outlined below may result in non-payment for incomplete or improperly completed work.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****** SCOPE OF WORK ******</p><p>Install PIAB, connect to sites phones, inform site of new DIDs, test IB/OB Calls.</p><p><br></p><p>****** CALL-IN INSTRUCTIONS ******</p><p>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit ........................ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.</p><p>This dispatch requires tech to have State Issued Enhanced Drivers License or Enhanced ID or must carry one of the following:</p><p>•U.S. passport</p><p>•U.S. passport card</p><p>•DHS trusted traveler cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</p><p>•U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents</p><p>•Permanent resident card</p><p>•Border crossing card</p><p>•An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe, including Enhanced Tribal Cards (ETCs).</p><p>•HSPD-12 PIV card</p><p>•Foreign government-issued passport</p><p>•Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card</p><p>•Transportation worker identification credential</p><p>•U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)</p><p>•U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential</p><p>•Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)</p><p><br></p><p>This is a Federal facility with a high level of security. Be prepared to follow the sites strict security protocol. Technician must have a fully charged laptop and be able to connect to Data Remote LAN 1 port to do a speed test. Standard install tools, Butt set, tone generator 66/110 punch down tool and phone cable with RJ11, RJ45 connectors and associated crimping tool in case we need to make longer cable runs from Data Remote to the Phones, Fax machine and Alarm panel. Tech will need 150 ft of cable in case we need to run cable extensions. It would be helpful if Tech had RJ11 to RJ45 adapters, which could mitigate some long cable runs.</p><p><br></p><p>****** INFORMATION FOR TECH *****</p><p>Please call Mettel upon arrival please call remote support toll free #........................ for assistance. Provide the Mettel Ticket site number ......................... to SD Rep.</p><p><br></p><p>****** SPECIAL MATERIALS NEEDED FOR DISPATCH ******</p><p>Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port ,Multimeter wire tester ,Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches ,Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer) ,Biscuit jacks ,Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters ,4-6 ft’ ladder ,Butt Set ,RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors ,100’ extension cord ,Digital Camera ,100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device ,Cell phone w/Hotspot device ,Punch down tool</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tool Requirements</p><p>Required Tools:</p><p>Phillips and flathead screwdrivers</p><p>Impact tool with 66 and 110 blades (for termination and cutting)</p><p>Tone generator and receiver</p><p>Telephone test set (butt set)</p><p>RJ11 6-position, 4-conductor module (for testing/toning)</p><p>RJ11 and RJ45 crimp tools</p><p>Electrician scissors and/or Cat5e wire strippers</p><p>Needle-nose pliers</p><p>Medium hammer drill/driver with assorted masonry bits (including 5/16” and 3/8” diameters)</p><p>Extended-length masonry bits (up to 3/8”) for thick walls or cinder blocks</p><p>3/8” U-style staple gun with staples</p><p>Label maker with black text on white label tape</p><p>Sharpie permanent marker pens</p><p>Small bubble level</p><p>Laptop with wired Ethernet port, serial-to-USB console, and terminal software (e.g., PuTTY or CRT)</p><p>Mobile phone with a high-quality camera and charger</p><p>Extra battery pack for phone</p><p>Consumable Items (carry as needed):</p><p>Cable ties (assorted lengths and sizes) for cable management</p><p>300+ feet of Cat5e or Cat6 cable</p><p>RJ11/12 plug modules (one 6-position, 2-conductor plug per PIAB line interface)</p><p>RJ45 Cat5e plug modules (for wireline internet options)</p><p>Scotch locks (for splicing/extending 22-24 AWG twisted pair telco wire)</p><p>1” to 1-1/4” drywall screws</p><p>Black electrical tape</p><p>Fish tape (50’, optional but recommended)</p><p>Extra 9V batteries for test tools</p><p>Clear silicone sealer (for exterior wall penetrations)</p><p>Standard wall-mount telephone jacks (interior/exterior) for analog phones or callboxes</p><p>Additional Requirement:</p><p>Bring a laptop with TeamViewer, console cable, and internet access for on-site configuration and troubleshooting.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Work Order and Documentation Submission</p><p>Work Order Requirements:</p><p>Complete and sign the Tech Americas Work Order emailed to you after assignment. Include:</p><p>On-site and off-site times</p><p>MOD name and signature</p><p>Submit the signed work order and required photos to documents@tech-americas.com.</p><p>Required Photos:</p><p>Before and after installation images</p><p>Before and after unboxing photos (if equipment was received and unpacked)</p><p>Photos of old equipment’s location and condition</p><p>For speed tests or cable toning, provide photos or screenshots with clear documentation</p><p>Photos of all new cabling labels (label all cables appropriately)</p><p>Submission Process:</p><p>Email all deliverables to documents@tech-americas.com.</p><p>Contact Tech Americas via phone (281) 668-3211 or email (support@tech-americas.com) to confirm receipt and acceptance of submissions.</p><p>Failure to submit complete documentation may require a warranty visit at no additional cost to Tech Americas. If the technician does not return for a required warranty visit, the cost of a replacement visit may be deducted from their payment.</p><p>If No Work Is Performed:</p><p>Take site photos before leaving and email them to documents@tech-americas.com.</p><p>Contact Tech Americas via phone (281) 668-3211 or email (support@tech-americas.com) before departure to document the situation and avoid non-payment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Payment Processing</p><p>Payment processing begins once all required deliverables (work order, photos, etc.) are received at documents@tech-americas.com.</p><p>Incomplete or missing deliverables may result in payment delays or deductions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Critical Communication Rule</p><p>Discuss agreements or payment issues only with Tech Americas, not with the end customer or client.</p><p>Why: This ensures professionalism and protects client relationships.</p><p>How: Contact Tech Americas at (281) 668-3211 or support@tech-americas.com for all agreement or payment-related questions.</p><p>Consequences: Unauthorized discussions with clients may result in termination of contract.</p><p>Acknowledgment: You must confirm adherence to this rule on the work order form.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T11:00","end":"2026-10-13T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":108.1},"result":{"eligib