{"job":{"id":20138102,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TPX Communications","title":"Move config to WAN0 from LAN1, and confirm if circuit comes up on WAN0.","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><p>Move config to WAN0 from LAN1, and confirm if circuit comes up on WAN0.</p><p>Document any removed equipment &amp; hand over to customer onsite.</p><p>Any delays or request outside the SOW call 833-294-6642 for approval.</p><p>Need laptop w/ANYDESK, hotspot, console cables, &amp; spare patch cables.</p><p><br></p><p><em>\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"</em></p><ul><li><em>\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"</em></li></ul><p><em>“Please make sure to mark 'On My Way' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”</em></p><p><em>﻿Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.</em></p><p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li><li>Windows&nbsp;7 or 10&nbsp;Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li><li>Active Email Address</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)</li><li>AnyDesk</li><li>Aeroadmin</li><li>HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li><li>FTP Client</li><li>TFTP Server software</li><li>MircoSIP (SIP call testing-&nbsp;https://www.microsip.org/)</li><li>Wireshark</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING</strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet Patch Cable</li><li>Cisco Console Cable​</li><li>USB to DB9 male serial Cable</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><ul><li>Buttset</li><li>Line man’s test set or analog test set</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool</li><li>Snips</li><li>Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Drill/ Dry wall screws</li><li>4’ ladder</li><li>CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)</li><li>Pre-made crossover cables</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors</li><li>Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>PRE-SITE WORK</u></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Acknowledge you have read and understand the Scope Of Work and its requirements</li><li>Print a copy of this scope of work and bring it to site</li><li>Call <del>*** </del>Support with any question or clarification about the Scope Of Work</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>ON SITE WORK</u></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Check In on the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Introduce yourself as representative of <del>*** **************</del></li><li>Check in with the on-site contact and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Call into <del>*** </del>Repair at <del>************* **** *******</del></li><li>Troubleshoot and resolve the repair issues at site.</li><li>Upload pictures of equipment powered up</li><li>Upload pictures of cable connections on devices&nbsp;</li><li>Upload a picture of speed test results from Laptop</li><li>Clean up work materials from install (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>POST-SITE WORK</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm deliverables are complete</li><li>Enter Close out notes into Order</li><li>Check out in Field Nation Portal provide full detailed notes on what was done on site.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site @ <del>************</del></li><li>DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform out of the scope work, call <del>***</del> Support.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY</u></strong></p><ul><li>Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved, the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\nMove config to WAN0 from LAN1, and confirm if circuit comes up on WAN0.\n\nDocument any removed equipment & hand over to customer onsite.\n\nAny delays or request outside the SOW call 833-294-6642 for approval.\n\nNeed laptop w/ANYDESK, hotspot, console cables, & spare patch cables.\n\n*\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"*\n\n- *\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"*\n\n*“Please make sure to mark 'On My Way' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”*\n\n*﻿Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.*\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n- Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n- Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n- Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP**\n\n- Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)\n- AnyDesk\n- Aeroadmin\n- HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n- FTP Client\n- TFTP Server software\n- MircoSIP (SIP call testing- <https://www.microsip.org/)>\n- Wireshark\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING**\n\n- Ethernet Patch Cable\n- Cisco Console Cable​\n- USB to DB9 male serial Cable\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\n- Buttset\n- Line man’s test set or analog test set\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool\n- Snips\n- Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks\n- Tone Generator and Wand\n- Drill/ Dry wall screws\n- 4’ ladder\n- CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)\n- Pre-made crossover cables\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors\n- Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)\n\nPRE-SITE WORK\n\n- Acknowledge you have read and understand the Scope Of Work and its requirements\n- Print a copy of this scope of work and bring it to site\n- Call \\*\\*\\* Support with any question or clarification about the Scope Of Work\n\nON SITE WORK\n\n- Check In on the Field Nation Portal\n- Introduce yourself as representative of \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Check in with the on-site contact and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal\n- Call into \\*\\*\\* Repair at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*