{"job":{"id":20138034,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Firm Start | TA/BK Expo & PHU Pre-Site Cabling Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong></p><p>You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Skills: </u></strong></p><p>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling and Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician. Technician MUST be familiar with low voltage ethernet cables installation through various ceiling types, terminate Shielded CAT6 cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work: </u></strong></p><p>Technician needed to perform site surveys at designated Burger King locations within Travel Center (TA) / Petro locations to identify network and power conditions for a potential equipment move. The goal of this survey is to validate site conditions, determine cable paths, and generate a precise Bill of Materials (BOM) for the subsequent installation phase. The Technician will visit the site to audit the existing infrastructure and determine requirements for new runs supporting Expo Printer, Expo Monitor, and Product Holding Unit (PHU).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(4, 4, 240);\">• ** Ethernet Data Tester / Toner</strong></p><p>• **Outlet Tester: To verify Ground and Polarity on power outlets.</p><p>• Standard Hand Tools: Screwdrivers, pliers, measuring tape.</p><p>• Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</p><p>• Camera with (High Resolution): this can be the camera on your phone, as long as it has high MP/quality. ****If you do not use the camera on your phone then you will need a way to get the photos to an online deliverable form while onsite; i.e transferring photos from camera to your phone so you can upload them to an online deliverable while onsite****</p><p>• Laser / Tape Distance Measure</p><p>• Flashlight / Headlamp: High-lumen for ceiling/under-counter inspection.</p><p>• Pen / Pencil</p><p>• Laptop - not required</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE</u></strong><u>:</u></p><p>Start time&nbsp;varies - see work order schedule for exact arrival time. Sites are generally scheduled to be completed during normal business hours.</p><p>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Estimated Duration: </u></strong></p><p>Less than 2 Hours</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code: </u></strong></p><p>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Arrival Requirements / Confirmations:</strong></p><p>• You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</p><p>• You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</p><p>• If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;REMOVED&nbsp;and&nbsp;REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;from the work order.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Arrival Instructions:</u></strong></p><p>• CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER: If you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</p><p>• CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager - Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers and advise what you are there to complete.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Onsite Instructions: </u></strong></p><p>• Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA).</p><p>• These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. Be Respectful and limit any disruptions while on site.&nbsp;</p><p>• Tech will work with the Site Point of Contact to identify existing equipment and potential future install locations. Work with the Site Point of Contact to identify the Comcast network stack, which will be the origin for any new cable runs. Photos must be clear and match the requested subject.</p><p>• All surveyed datapoints will be collected via Online Deliverable Survey (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE).</p><p><strong>• ⚠️Deliverable Survey should be <u>opened &amp; started at the beginning of service appointment</u> and filled out as work progresses.</strong></p><p>• Survey link can be found in the custom fields section of your work order - this link cannot be re-used across visits or locations. </p><p>• Survey progress can be saved as technician progresses.</p><p>• If you cannot complete survey while conducting work, use the following offline summary to help guide you :</p><p>o\t&gt; Expo Printer Survey:</p><p>o\tIdentify where the Expo Printer is located currently</p><p>o\tWorking with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is sufficient data/power at the Expo Station, to support moving the Expo Printer to the Expo Station.</p><p>o\tIf data/power is needed, document the requirements and cable run.</p><p>o\t&gt; Expo Monitor Survey:</p><p>o\tWorking with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is sufficient data/power at the Expo Station, to support installation of an Expo Monitor and KDS (Kitchen Display System) mini-PC/Thin Client at the Expo Station.</p><p>o\tIf data/power is needed, document the requirements and cable run.</p><p>o\t&gt; PHU (Product Holding Unit) Survey:</p><p>o\tWorking with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is an available data jack near the PHU, which will allow for a safe and secure run that does not subject the cable to heat or risk of snag.</p><p>o\tIf data is needed, document the requirements and cable run.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Important Tech Information &amp; Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>• </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA) while on site.</strong></p><p>• Tech is required to follow instructions called out in their work order and any provided technical documentation / checklist. Any questions or issues please escalate to Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</p><p>• Tech MUST complete an Essintial Online Deliverable PRIOR to leaving the site + have them reviewed/approved by Ess Tech Support</p><p>• Techs MUST call and check-out with the Essintial Tech Support @ 717-516-3009 to perform a final check out and have your DELIVERABLES reviewed/approval BEFORE you LEAVE SITE THE SITE</p><p>• Escalations / Remote Support &ndash; Contact Essintial Technical Support at 717-516-3009[</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><p>Government Issued ID</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><p>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</p><p>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REVISITS: </u></strong></p><p>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Attachments </u></strong>- All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:</p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:**\n\nYou MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)\n\n**Required Skills:**\n\nMid-Level Low Voltage Cabling and Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician. Technician MUST be familiar with low voltage ethernet cables installation through various ceiling types, terminate Shielded CAT6 cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope Of Work:**\n\nTechnician needed to perform site surveys at designated Burger King locations within Travel Center (TA) / Petro locations to identify network and power conditions for a potential equipment move. The goal of this survey is to validate site conditions, determine cable paths, and generate a precise Bill of Materials (BOM) for the subsequent installation phase. The Technician will visit the site to audit the existing infrastructure and determine requirements for new runs supporting Expo Printer, Expo Monitor, and Product Holding Unit (PHU).\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n**• \\*\\* Ethernet Data Tester / Toner**\n\n• \\*\\*Outlet Tester: To verify Ground and Polarity on power outlets.\n\n• Standard Hand Tools: Screwdrivers, pliers, measuring tape.\n\n• Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n\n• Camera with (High Resolution): this can be the camera on your phone, as long as it has high MP/quality. \\*\\*\\*\\*If you do not use the camera on your phone then you will need a way to get the photos to an online deliverable form while onsite; i.e transferring photos from camera to your phone so you can upload them to an online deliverable while onsite\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• Laser / Tape Distance Measure\n\n• Flashlight / Headlamp: High-lumen for ceiling/under-counter inspection.\n\n• Pen / Pencil\n\n• Laptop - not required\n\n**SCHEDULE**:\n\nStart time varies - see work order schedule for exact arrival time. Sites are generally scheduled to be completed during normal business hours.\n\nYou are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n**Estimated Duration:**\n\nLess than 2 Hours\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nProfessional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n\n**Pre-Arrival Requirements / Confirmations:**\n\n• You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n\n• You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n\n• If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be REMOVED and REMOVE YOURSELF from the work order.\n\n**Arrival Instructions:**\n\n• CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER: If you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n\n• CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager - Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers and advise what you are there to complete.\n\n**Onsite Instructions:**\n\n• Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA).\n\n• These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. Be Respectful and limit any disruptions while on site.\n\n• Tech will work with the Site Point of Contact to identify existing equipment and potential future install locations. Work with the Site Point of Contact to identify the Comcast network stack, which will be the origin for any new cable runs. Photos must be clear and match the requested subject.\n\n• All surveyed datapoints will be collected via Online Deliverable Survey (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE).\n\n**• ⚠️Deliverable Survey should be opened & started at the beginning of service appointment and filled out as work progresses.**\n\n• Survey link can be found in the custom fields section of your work order - this link cannot be re-used across visits or locations.\n\n• Survey progress can be saved as technician progresses.\n\n• If you cannot complete survey while conducting work, use the following offline summary to help guide you :\n\no > Expo Printer Survey:\n\no Identify where the Expo Printer is located currently\n\no Working with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is sufficient data/power at the Expo Station, to support moving the Expo Printer to the Expo Station.\n\no If data/power is needed, document the requirements and cable run.\n\no > Expo Monitor Survey:\n\no Working with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is sufficient data/power at the Expo Station, to support installation of an Expo Monitor and KDS (Kitchen Display System) mini-PC/Thin Client at the Expo Station.\n\no If data/power is needed, document the requirements and cable run.\n\no > PHU (Product Holding Unit) Survey:\n\no Working with the Site Point of Contact, determine whether there is an available data jack near the PHU, which will allow for a safe and secure run that does not subject the cable to heat or risk of snag.\n\no If data is needed, document the requirements and cable run.\n\n**Additional Important Tech Information & Requirements:**\n\n**•** **You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA) while on site.**\n\n• Tech is required to follow instructions called out in their work order and any provided technical documentation / checklist. Any questions or issues please escalate to Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009\n\n• Tech MUST complete an Essintial Online Deliverable PRIOR to leaving the site + have them reviewed/approved by Ess Tech Support\n\n• Techs MUST call and check-out with the Essintial Tech Support @ 717-516-3009 to perform a final check out and have your DELIVERABLES reviewed/approval BEFORE you LEAVE SITE THE SITE\n\n• Escalations / Remote Support – Contact Essintial Technical Support at 717-516-3009\\[\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\nGovernment Issued ID\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\nAll expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n\nTechnicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.\n\n**REVISITS:**\n\nThis WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Attachments** - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T13:45","end":"2026-10-23T15:45"},"payRange":{"min":165,"max":165},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":47.5824388325848},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791557691490}
{"job":{"id":20138192,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Firm Start | TA/BK Expo & PHU Cabling Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong></p><p>You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Skills: </u></strong></p><p>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling and Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician. Technician MUST be familiar with low voltage ethernet cables installation through various ceiling types, terminate Shielded CAT6 cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work: </u></strong></p><p>Based on the previously completed survey, technician will be visiting site to run cable at designated Burger King locations within Travel Center (TA) / Petro locations in advance of a potential equipment move. Tech should work with SME to determine BOM and purchase equipment to bring to the site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(4, 4, 240);\">• ** Ethernet Data Tester / Toner</strong></p><p>• **Outlet Tester: To verify Ground and Polarity on power outlets.</p><p>• Standard Hand Tools: Screwdrivers, pliers, measuring tape.</p><p>• Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</p><p>• Camera with (High Resolution): this can be the camera on your phone, as long as it has high MP/quality. ****If you do not use the camera on your phone then you will need a way to get the photos to an online deliverable form while onsite; i.e transferring photos from camera to your phone so you can upload them to an online deliverable while onsite****</p><p>• Laser / Tape Distance Measure</p><p>• Flashlight / Headlamp: High-lumen for ceiling/under-counter inspection.</p><p>• Pen / Pencil</p><p>• Laptop - not required</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE</u></strong><u>:</u></p><p>Tech will work overnight.</p><p>You 