{"job":{"id":20138915,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"M-CO Data Services LLC","title":"Permit Required - Thirty-One CABLE Pre-wire - CAT6 PLENUM DROPS IN A BUSINESS OFFICE (Remodel / NEW CONSTRUCTION) , Terminations required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>YOU WILL NEED A PERMIT APPLICATION AND PASSED INSPECTION NOTICE ON ALL PERMITS TO BE PAID FOR THE WORK.</strong></p><p><strong><u>PERMIT INSTRUCTIONS:</u></strong></p><p>****You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be able to pull a low voltage permit to accept this work order.&nbsp;<em><u>Once assigned you have 14 days to upload picture of the submitted permit application to the work order&nbsp;</u></em>. The technician is responsible for the inspections and closing out the permit once the site is completed. In some cases the GC of the site may help with the inspections but that varies from site to site.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Terminations and faceplates are required. See details below.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT APPROVAL</strong></p><p>• Get approval from Shawn Gadea or Jerilyn Mayhak before going on-site.</p><p>• Sites may not be ready.</p><p>• No pay for unapproved visits.</p><p>• We don’t cover wasted trips.</p><p><strong>GENERAL RULES</strong></p><p>• Check in/out using GPS — no check, no pay.</p><p>• You’re paid only for time worked, not your full day.</p><p>• Fixed rate = complete job. No extra pay for parts, time, or travel.</p><p>• Trip charges/minimums must be pre-approved.</p><p>• Bring all tools, wire, ladders — no borrowing.</p><p>• <strong>Please note that MCO is not liable or responsible for your Field Nation fees. Please do not add your fees to the expenses. (Unless this is approved and noted in the work order messages)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCHEDULING</strong></p><p>• Confirm a firm ETA within the job window.</p><p>• GC will be notified of your time. Also, post an update on Field Nation.</p><p>• No fake ETAs — missed appointments = is frowned upon and can result in negative review or block.</p><p>• No surprise site visits — must be approved by MCO</p><p>• Working Hours: Monday–Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM only.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK (Cabling)</strong></p><p>• Follow the attached print exactly.</p><p>• Contact M-CO if the prints don’t match the onsite setup.</p><p>•<strong> <u>DO NOT</u></strong> modify the scope without approval.</p><p>• <strong><u>DO NOT</u> TIE ONTO EXISTING CABLES OR THE CEILING GRID. YOU MUST BE PREPARED TO INSTALL YOUR OWN RINGS OR J-HOOKS (WHERE ACCEPTABLE) FOR CABLE SUPPORT</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Wire Pulls (Thirty-One Total CAT6 Plenum Cables)</strong></p><p>• Run all cables from the Branch Office Controller (BOC) to the designated locations in the Edward Jones suite, per the attached prints. Boxes and conduit are typically pre-installed. If missing, contact Shawn Gadea or Jerilyn Mayhak immediately.</p><p>• Before starting, verify with the GC that the construction plans match the M-CO scope. If there's any discrepancy or additional work, contact M-CO first.</p><p>A typical setup for the pre-wire is:</p><p>• BOA (101) Runs: 5 cables, 2 Single Gang Boxes, Labels: (1), (2), (3), (4), (5) at both ends</p><p>• FA (102) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (6), (7) at both ends</p><p>• Workstation/Conference (106) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (8), (9) at both ends</p><p>• Other Drops (as shown on print) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (10), (11) at both ends</p><p>• Label both ends.</p><p>• Take photos of all work.</p><p>• Terminate and faceplate the workstations. Leave 10ft service loops supported above ceiling at the BOC and terminate using white female RJ45 CAT6 HD Keystones. (This is specified by the client. See client documents for photo)</p><p>• Use J-hooks/bridle rings for support (every 4').</p><p>All cables must be Cat 6 Plenum (minimum), 4-pair, and labeled clearly on both ends.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>D-MARC EXTENSION (4 Total – CAT6 Plenum)</strong></p><p>• Home run only – no splices.</p><p>• Runs:</p><p>1x Cat 6 (circuit) → Single Gang Box @ BOC</p><p>3x Cat 6 (voice) → Separate Box @ BOC</p><p>Conduit should be ready. If not, contact M-CO.</p><p>See attached Diagram A and instructions.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SUPPLIES &amp; RATES</strong></p><p>Item Rate</p><p>• Cat 6 Plenum $0.45/ft</p><p>• Single Gang Box $0.50 ea</p><p>• Double Gang Box $1.50 ea</p><p>• Bridle Rings (Box) $60/100 ct</p><p>• Helper Rate $40/hour</p><p>• Travel may be paid at the federal reimbursement rate of $.76/mile. Please note: The first 30 miles to site and the last 30 miles from site is&nbsp;<strong><u>NOT</u></strong>&nbsp;calculated in the mileage reimbursement amount.</p><p><strong>(Example: 100 mi round trip - 60mi. = 40miles) This must be agreed upon prior to accepting the work order</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>BEFORE LEAVING</strong></p><p>• Submit photos of cable footage (start &amp; finish).</p><p>• Clean up your materials — no scrap left behind.</p><p>• Terminations are required and need to be completed before calling for final inspection</p><p><strong>IF ANYTHING’S OFF</strong></p><p>• Call M-CO immediately for anything out of scope, unusual, or unsafe.</p><p>• Do not follow instructions from the GC or the property manager without M-CO approval.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact:</strong></p><p>• Shawn Gadea: 314-369-6859</p><p>• Jerilyn Mayhak: 314-495-5867</p>","markdown":"**YOU WILL NEED A PERMIT APPLICATION AND PASSED INSPECTION NOTICE ON ALL PERMITS TO BE PAID FOR THE WORK.**\n\n**PERMIT INSTRUCTIONS:**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*You **MUST** be able to pull a low voltage permit to accept this work order. *Once assigned you have 14 days to upload picture of the submitted permit application to the work order* . The technician is responsible for the inspections and closing out the permit once the site is completed. In some cases the GC of the site may help with the inspections but that varies from site to site.\n\n**Terminations and faceplates are required. See details below.**\n\n**DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT APPROVAL**\n\n• Get approval from Shawn Gadea or Jerilyn Mayhak before going on-site.\n\n• Sites may not be ready.\n\n• No pay for unapproved visits.\n\n• We don’t cover wasted trips.\n\n**GENERAL RULES**\n\n• Check in/out using GPS — no check, no pay.\n\n• You’re paid only for time worked, not your full day.\n\n• Fixed rate = complete job. No extra pay for parts, time, or travel.\n\n• Trip charges/minimums must be pre-approved.\n\n• Bring all tools, wire, ladders — no borrowing.\n\n• **Please note that MCO is not liable or responsible for your Field Nation fees. Please do not add your fees to the expenses. (Unless this is approved and noted in the work order messages)**\n\n**SCHEDULING**\n\n• Confirm a firm ETA within the job window.\n\n• GC will be notified of your time. Also, post an update on Field Nation.\n\n• No fake ETAs — missed appointments = is frowned upon and can result in negative review or block.\n\n• No surprise site visits — must be approved by MCO\n\n• Working Hours: Monday–Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM only.\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK (Cabling)**\n\n• Follow the attached print exactly.\n\n• Contact M-CO if the prints don’t match the onsite setup.\n\n• **DO NOT** modify the scope without approval.\n\n• **DO NOT TIE ONTO EXISTING CABLES OR THE CEILING GRID. YOU MUST BE PREPARED TO INSTALL YOUR OWN RINGS OR J-HOOKS (WHERE ACCEPTABLE) FOR CABLE SUPPORT**\n\n**Wire Pulls (Thirty-One Total CAT6 Plenum Cables)**\n\n• Run all cables from the Branch Office Controller (BOC) to the designated locations in the Edward Jones suite, per the attached prints. Boxes and conduit are typically pre-installed. If missing, contact Shawn Gadea or Jerilyn Mayhak immediately.\n\n• Before starting, verify with the GC that the construction plans match the M-CO scope. If there's any discrepancy or additional work, contact M-CO first.\n\nA typical setup for the pre-wire is:\n\n• BOA (101) Runs: 5 cables, 2 Single Gang Boxes, Labels: (1), (2), (3), (4), (5) at both ends\n\n• FA (102) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (6), (7) at both ends\n\n• Workstation/Conference (106) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (8), (9) at both ends\n\n• Other Drops (as shown on print) Runs: 2 cables, 1 Single Gang Box, Labels: (10), (11) at both ends\n\n• Label both ends.\n\n• Take photos of all work.\n\n• Terminate and faceplate the workstations. Leave 10ft service loops supported above ceiling at the BOC and terminate using white female RJ45 CAT6 HD Keystones. (This is specified by the client. See client documents for photo)\n\n• Use J-hooks/bridle rings for support (every 4').\n\nAll cables must be Cat 6 Plenum (minimum), 4-pair, and labeled clearly on both ends.\n\n**D-MARC EXTENSION (4 Total – CAT6 Plenum)**\n\n• Home run only – no splices.\n\n• Runs:\n\n1x Cat 6 (circuit) → Single Gang Box @ BOC\n\n3x Cat 6 (voice) → Separate Box @ BOC\n\nConduit should be ready. If not, contact M-CO.\n\nSee attached Diagram A and instructions.\n\n**SUPPLIES & RATES**\n\nItem Rate\n\n• Cat 6 Plenum $0.45/ft\n\n• Single Gang Box $0.50 ea\n\n• Double Gang Box $1.50 ea\n\n• Bridle Rings (Box) $60/100 ct\n\n• Helper Rate $40/hour\n\n• Travel may be paid at the federal reimbursement rate of $.76/mile. Please note: The first 30 miles to site and the last 30 miles from site is **NOT** calculated in the mileage reimbursement amount.\n\n**(Example: 100 mi round trip - 60mi. = 40miles) This must be agreed upon prior to accepting the work order**\n\n**BEFORE LEAVING**\n\n• Submit photos of cable footage (start & finish).\n\n• Clean up your materials — no scrap left behind.\n\n• Terminations are required and need to be completed before calling for final inspection\n\n**IF ANYTHING’S OFF**\n\n• Call M-CO immediately for anything out of scope, unusual, or unsafe.\n\n• Do not follow instructions from the GC or the property manager without M-CO approval.\n\n**Contact:**\n\n• Shawn Gadea: 314-369-6859\n\n• Jerilyn Mayhak: 314-495-5867","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-23T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":560},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":63.42596406929024},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - 