{"job":{"id":20139072,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Silverlane Technology","title":"Install Voip phones","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p>SNOW TICKET: SCTASK0469135</p><p><strong><u>Install &amp; Provision:</u></strong></p><p>8x phones</p><p>1x mg52 with Verizon sim</p><p>1x mg52 power supply</p><p><br></p><p>Please make sure you have ALL 3 documents signed before uploading to Field Nation</p><p>Organize and secure all cables with wire ties, ensuring that no unplanned outages occur during the process.</p><p>See&nbsp;the&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.</p><p><br></p><p>Some or all of this equipment may require troubleshooting and resolution:</p><ul><li>Ubiquiti P2P (point-2-point) devices</li><li>PoE Injectors</li></ul><p>Existing cable runs may require troubleshooting and resolution</p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Standard Toolkit</li><li>Laptop with charger</li><li>Cellphone with charger</li><li>Hotspot or Internet dongle</li><li>Ladder (at least 8-12')</li><li>Cabling Toolkit</li></ul><p><u>Cabling Toolkit Requirements</u><strong><u>:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cable repair tools including Cat6 crimp connectors</li><li>Cable pulling tools, Cable termination tools, etc</li><li>Network cable tester, toner, probe, etc</li><li>Wide variety of heavy-duty tools for installation on a variety of materials (wood, metal, drywall, etc)</li><li>Heavy-duty drill, drill bits for metal, wood, drywall, etc</li><li>Various screws, nuts, bolts, fasteners, cable ties, etc</li></ul><p><u>Cabling Material Requirements (reimbursable if needed during troubleshooting):</u></p><ul><li>Cat6 (non-plenum) cabling materials (indoor cabling for indoor runs / outdoor cabling required for outdoor runs)</li><li>Cable tips, keystone jacks, biscuit jacks, etc</li><li>Wallplates, junction boxes, etc</li><li>Patch cables, cable management supplies, etc</li><li>Misc supplies associated with cable runs, device installation, etc</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check-in with the work order manager prior to entering the site for dispatch details</li><li>The job requires tech to report directly to the main office to check-in upon arrival to the site</li><li>Locate any shipped equipment and capture serial numbers from boxes with photos</li><li>Immediately call work order manager to discuss all issues and resolutions</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required</li><li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts as representing Silverlane</li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li></ul>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\nSNOW TICKET: SCTASK0469135\n\n**Install & Provision:**\n\n8x phones\n\n1x mg52 with Verizon sim\n\n1x mg52 power supply\n\nPlease make sure you have ALL 3 documents signed before uploading to Field Nation\n\nOrganize and secure all cables with wire ties, ensuring that no unplanned outages occur during the process.\n\nSee the *Confidential Information* section listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.\n\nSome or all of this equipment may require troubleshooting and resolution:\n\n- Ubiquiti P2P (point-2-point) devices\n- PoE Injectors\n\nExisting cable runs may require troubleshooting and resolution\n\n**Tool Requirements:**\n\n- Standard Toolkit\n- Laptop with charger\n- Cellphone with charger\n- Hotspot or Internet dongle\n- Ladder (at least 8-12')\n- Cabling Toolkit\n\nCabling Toolkit Requirements**:**\n\n- Cable repair tools including Cat6 crimp connectors\n- Cable pulling tools, Cable termination tools, etc\n- Network cable tester, toner, probe, etc\n- Wide variety of heavy-duty tools for installation on a variety of materials (wood, metal, drywall, etc)\n- Heavy-duty drill, drill bits for metal, wood, drywall, etc\n- Various screws, nuts, bolts, fasteners, cable ties, etc\n\nCabling Material Requirements (reimbursable if needed during troubleshooting):\n\n- Cat6 (non-plenum) cabling materials (indoor cabling for indoor runs / outdoor cabling required for outdoor runs)\n- Cable tips, keystone jacks, biscuit jacks, etc\n- Wallplates, junction boxes, etc\n- Patch cables, cable management supplies, etc\n- Misc supplies associated with cable runs, device installation, etc\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Check-in with the work order manager prior to entering the site for dispatch details\n- The job requires tech to report directly to the main office to check-in upon arrival to the site\n- Locate any shipped equipment and capture serial numbers from boxes with photos\n- Immediately call work order manager to discuss all issues and resolutions\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts as representing Silverlane\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:30","end":"2026-10-20T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":65.66035408882145},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-1