{"job":{"id":20138193,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Firm Start | TA/BK Expo & PHU Cabling Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong></p><p>You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Skills: </u></strong></p><p>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling and Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician. Technician MUST be familiar with low voltage ethernet cables installation through various ceiling types, terminate Shielded CAT6 cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work: </u></strong></p><p>Based on the previously completed survey, technician will be visiting site to run cable at designated Burger King locations within Travel Center (TA) / Petro locations in advance of a potential equipment move. Tech should work with SME to determine BOM and purchase equipment to bring to the site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(4, 4, 240);\">• ** Ethernet Data Tester / Toner</strong></p><p>• **Outlet Tester: To verify Ground and Polarity on power outlets.</p><p>• Standard Hand Tools: Screwdrivers, pliers, measuring tape.</p><p>• Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</p><p>• Camera with (High Resolution): this can be the camera on your phone, as long as it has high MP/quality. ****If you do not use the camera on your phone then you will need a way to get the photos to an online deliverable form while onsite; i.e transferring photos from camera to your phone so you can upload them to an online deliverable while onsite****</p><p>• Laser / Tape Distance Measure</p><p>• Flashlight / Headlamp: High-lumen for ceiling/under-counter inspection.</p><p>• Pen / Pencil</p><p>• Laptop - not required</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE</u></strong><u>:</u></p><p>Tech will work overnight.</p><p>You 