{"job":{"id":20139509,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"JOHNSTON & MURPHY New Store Installation **3 DAYS**","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">SITE INFORMATION</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Site ID</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: GEN01547JMR</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Service Request Number(s):</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\"> SR04380953 / SR04380952</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Site Name</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">JOHNSTON &amp; MURPHY 071547_GEN01547JMR</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Street Address</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: 4325 GLENWOOD AVE, STE 2106, RALEIGH, NC 27612</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Parts Being Sent</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">: To Tech</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to check-in via tect chat - </span>text “Start” to <del>************</del>.You will receive 2 messages back. First will confirm you have been connected and the second will ask if you are onsite for 1 - New Installation or 2 - Service, you will always respond back \"1\". <strong>**review PDF attached on process &amp; directions to escalate if support not responsive within 20 minutes (Step 2) </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">SCOPE OF WORK</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">See attached layout &amp; IG for full SOW – This is a “New Store” Installation.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 1: Prewire  10/15 @ 9AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Prewire of the site before the ceilings or walls are closed. CAT5e cabling to be run and coiled up in final locations in preparation for next visit.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 2: New Store Day 1 10/22 @ 9AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Install the network cabinet and patch panel.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Day 3: New Store Day 3 10/27 @ 9AM </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Install WAP, Media shelf cabling, E-Stat cabling, and phone</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Installation Guide: </span>https://interfacesystems.mcoutput.com/genig/Content/Network%20Installation%20Guides/Genesco/Individual%20Scopes/Prior%20to%20Entering.htm</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**SITE INFORMATION**\n\n**Site ID**: GEN01547JMR\n\n**Service Request Number(s):** SR04380953 / SR04380952\n\n**Site Name**:  JOHNSTON & MURPHY 071547\\_GEN01547JMR\n\n**Street Address**: 4325 GLENWOOD AVE, STE 2106, RALEIGH, NC 27612\n\n**Parts Being Sent**: To Tech\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to check-in via tect chat - text “Start” to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.You will receive 2 messages back. First will confirm you have been connected and the second will ask if you are onsite for 1 - New Installation or 2 - Service, you will always respond back \"1\". **\\*\\*review PDF attached on process & directions to escalate if support not responsive within 20 minutes (Step 2)**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**:\n\nSee attached layout & IG for full SOW – This is a “New Store” Installation.\n\nDay 1: Prewire 10/15 @ 9AM\n\nPrewire of the site before the ceilings or walls are closed. CAT5e cabling to be run and coiled up in final locations in preparation for next visit.\n\nDay 2: New Store Day 1 10/22 @ 9AM\n\nInstall the network cabinet and patch panel.\n\nDay 3: New Store Day 3 10/27 @ 9AM\n\nInstall WAP, Media shelf cabling, E-Stat cabling, and phone\n\nInstallation Guide: <https://interfacesystems.mcoutput.com/genig/Content/Network%20Installation%20Guides/Genesco/Individual%20Scopes/Prior%20to%20Entering.htm>\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN \\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).\n- Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc\n- Picture of RMA form & return label applied; if applicable\n- Release Code\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 11)\n- Operating system must be fully licensed and updated\n- · Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Buttset\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Drill\n- 12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete\n- 8' Ladder\n- Phone/Ethernet Wiring\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Contact Name & Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**\n\n**Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T09:00","end":"2026-10-15T29:00"},"payRange":{"min":800,"max":800},"payType":"fixed","payStructur