{"job":{"id":20139716,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Food Lion 1484 Raleigh, NC - Cable Run and Install AP19 - Two Technicians Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope Notes</u></strong></p><p>-Add new AP19 outside Produce Prep area, including cable run.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>This scope of work requires TWO technicians.</strong></p><p><strong>Both technicians will need WhatsApp installed on their phone</strong></p><p><strong>Tech Must Be Lift Certified.</strong></p><p><strong>All Deliverables must be uploaded to FN prior to leaving site, unless returning materials.</strong></p><p><strong>Close out notes and marking the WO complete must be done after the equipment is shipped out. Please notify POC with receipt and tracking information.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ ME!!!!</strong></p><p>Check-in on the Field Nation App</p><p>Introduce yourself to the MOD</p><p>Walk through site and locate all delivered hardware (2 or 3 boxes with green label that says \"HOLD FOR TECHNICIAN\").</p><p>Provide photo of shipped materials, marking anything that is missing.</p><p>Provide photo of return label (if applicable).</p><p>Utilizing the attached AP Survey, find the location where the AP will go on the roof.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>INDOOR AP SWAP</strong>:</p><p>After MOD gives the Green Light. Wait for networking to shut down location and give the go ahead to swap AP01(Controller), Wait for NOC/ POC to give the go ahead to swap the rest of the APs</p><p>Swap the remaining APs in the most efficient manner. Numerical order is not necessary.</p><p>Provide a photo of EACH installed AP as you go.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TESTING</strong>:</p><p>Once final AP is installed, Connect to the guest Wi-Fi (take a screenshot of splash page and post to the chat) and do a walk-through of the location testing the signal strength. Indoor and outdoor.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>POST TEST:</strong></p><p>Walk through with the MOD and complete the checklist confirming all networked devices are fully functional</p><p>Move Lift back to where we found it and attach a picture to your FN WO. Include the lift ID number in the photo.</p><p>Receive Signoff from MOD&nbsp;</p><p><u>ALL dismounted APs :</u></p><p>Inside each box, include the store inventory list per box with the enclosed devices highlighted, circled, checked, etc. on the list.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>In each box, maybe where the return address is, include the brand name, store number and x of x boxes. As an example, Giant Food 1234. Box 1 of 3</p><p>Shipping labels to return old equipment will be sent with the new APs.</p><p>You are responsible for shipping equipment to recycling center. If shipping next morning Attach Tracking to FN WO before closing out. (This is required, WOs will not be paid out unless all deliverables are in.)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Skill Set &amp; Tools Required:</strong></p><p><strong><em>WhatsApp </em></strong>for efficient group communication&nbsp;</p><p>PPE - Hi-Vis shirt or vest and face mask if required by site</p><p>Steel Toe Boots, Safety Glasses, Lift Harness (This is required, if you don't own one, they are sold for about $20 at HD.)</p><p>Adjustable Ladder or 10' A-Frame</p><p>Standard RJ45 hand tools - Stripper, crimps, cat6a Mod Ends</p><p>Smartphone for communication while onsite</p><p>Laptop with hotspot</p><p>Network Equipment Experience Required</p><p>Working Camera</p><p>100 ft extension cord \"In case lift needs to be charged\"</p><p>Aruba Console Cable</p><p>Putty Installed**(this must be done before we arrive)</p><p>Microsoft Teams Installed**(This must be done before we arrive.)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Total installation must be complete BEFORE the store opens for business.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope Notes**\n\n-Add new AP19 outside Produce Prep area, including cable run.\n\n**This scope of work requires TWO technicians.**\n\n**Both technicians will need WhatsApp installed on their phone**\n\n**Tech Must Be Lift Certified.**\n\n**All Deliverables must be uploaded to FN prior to leaving site, unless returning materials.**\n\n**Close out notes and marking the WO complete must be done after the equipment is shipped out. Please notify POC with receipt and tracking information.**\n\n**READ ME!!!!**\n\nCheck-in on the Field Nation App\n\nIntroduce yourself to the MOD\n\nWalk through site and locate all delivered hardware (2 or 3 boxes with green label that says \"HOLD FOR TECHNICIAN\").\n\nProvide photo of shipped materials, marking anything that is missing.\n\nProvide photo of return label (if applicable).\n\nUtilizing the attached AP Survey, find the location where the AP will go on the roof.\n\n**INDOOR AP SWAP**:\n\nAfter MOD gives the Green Light. Wait for networking to shut down location and give the go ahead to swap AP01(Controller), Wait for NOC/ POC to give the go ahead to swap the rest of the APs\n\nSwap the remaining APs in the most efficient manner. Numerical order is not necessary.\n\nProvide a photo of EACH installed AP as you go.\n\n**TESTING**:\n\nOnce final AP is installed, Connect to the guest Wi-Fi (take a screenshot of splash page and post to the chat) and do a walk-through of the location testing the signal strength. Indoor and outdoor.\n\n**POST TEST:**\n\nWalk through with the MOD and complete the checklist confirming all networked devices are fully functional\n\nMove Lift back to where we found it and attach a picture to your FN WO. Include the lift ID number in the photo.\n\nReceive Signoff from MOD\n\nALL dismounted APs :\n\nInside each box, include the store inventory list per box with the enclosed devices highlighted, circled, checked, etc. on the list.\n\nIn each box, maybe where the return address is, include the brand name, store number and x of x boxes. As an example, Giant Food 1234. Box 1 of 3\n\nShipping labels to return old equipment will be sent with the new APs.\n\nYou are responsible for shipping equipment to recycling center. If shipping next morning Attach Tracking to FN WO before closing out. (This is required, WOs will not be paid out unless all deliverables are in.)\n\n**Skill Set & Tools Required:**\n\n***WhatsApp*** for efficient group communication\n\nPPE - Hi-Vis shirt or vest and face mask if required by site\n\nSteel Toe Boots, Safety Glasses, Lift Harness (This is required, if you don't own one, they are sold for about $20 at HD.)\n\nAdjustable Ladder or 10' A-Frame\n\nStandard RJ45 hand tools - Stripper, crimps, cat6a Mod Ends\n\nSmartphone for communication while onsite\n\nLaptop with hotspot\n\nNetwork Equipment Experience Required\n\nWorking Camera\n\n100 ft extension cord \"In case lift needs to be charged\"\n\nAruba Console Cable\n\nPutty Installed\\*\\*(this must be done before we arrive)\n\nMicrosoft Teams Installed\\*\\*(This must be done before we arrive.)\n\n**Total installation must be complete BEFORE the store opens for business.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T08:00","end":"2026-10-19T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":520},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":130,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":5.28645232627915},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":130,"baseAmount":520,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-