{"job":{"id":20134334,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Valuance AI","title":"All Animals Veterinary Hospital: Detailed Site Audit of Devices, Closets, Cabling, Telephony","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Join the Teams Meeting Bridge when you check in, before you enter the site.</strong></p><p><strong>The survey link will be sent 30 minutes to 1 hour before the start time.</strong></p><p>Valuance AI is seeking an experienced, detail‑oriented field technician to perform a comprehensive&nbsp;<strong>Infrastructure &amp; Network Site Audit</strong>&nbsp;using the Valuance AI Site Survey web application. This audit documents the current‑state environment across:</p><ul><li>Network infrastructure</li><li>Telephony/VOIP systems</li><li>Structured cabling</li><li>Wi‑Fi</li><li>Workstations and peripherals</li><li>Servers and UPS systems</li><li>Imaging equipment (X‑ray, dental, ultrasound)</li><li>Life‑safety and analog lines</li></ul><p>The technician will follow the&nbsp;<strong>VAI Site Audit SOP</strong>, which includes evaluating MDF/IDF rooms, photographing all equipment, identifying cabling issues, and capturing performance snapshots such as wired/wireless speed tests and Wi‑Fi observations. All findings feed directly into the VAI Site Audit Report, Executive Summary, and Network/Device Inventory used to build upgrade recommendations.</p><p>The onsite workflow includes checking in with the VAI PM, meeting with the Hospital Manager (HM), conducting an HM interview, and performing a full building walkthrough starting with MDF/IDFs. The technician will inspect and photograph:</p><ul><li>Network closets, racks, cabling pathways</li><li>Patch panels, switches, APs</li><li>Telephony handsets, PBX/analog components</li><li>Workstations, printers, imaging devices</li><li>Any areas requiring new cabling drops</li></ul><p>Additional tasks include mapping AP locations, identifying Wi‑Fi dead zones, validating cabling labels, capturing MOS/jitter/latency feedback, and documenting VOIP migration readiness.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Login to Valuance AI Site Audit,</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>You’ve been assigned a site survey. This survey is required to gather the information needed for our project.&nbsp;</p><p>Please follow the steps below to access and complete your survey:&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 1: Invitation Email</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;You will receive an account‑creation email from&nbsp;<strong>Base44</strong>&nbsp;(the platform hosting our application). This will be sent to the email you provided&nbsp;Valuance&nbsp;AI.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Action:</strong>&nbsp;Look for an email with a subject similar to&nbsp;<em>“You’ve been invited to join…”</em>. If you don’t see it, please check your spam/junk folder.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 2: Create Your Account</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;The invitation email includes a link to set up your account.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Action:</strong>&nbsp;Click the link and create your password to activate your account.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 3: Log In</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;Once your account is created, log in to the&nbsp;<strong>VAI Intelligent IT Survey</strong>&nbsp;application.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Action:</strong>&nbsp;Use your email&nbsp;and the password you just created.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 4: Access Your Survey</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;After logging in, you will be taken directly to the survey assigned to you—no searching required.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Action:</strong>&nbsp;Complete each section. Your progress saves automatically.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Important Notes</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Survey Completion:</strong>&nbsp;Once you submit the survey, your access to the application will automatically be removed.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Support:</strong>&nbsp;If you have any issues with account setup, login, or accessing the survey, please contact&nbsp;<strong>Cam Berow, cberow@valuanceai.com</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Valuance AI Expectations Onsite</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor at all times while interacting with hospital staff, vendors, and clients.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Be proactive in communicating with <strong>Valuance AI project management and remote support</strong> regarding arrival, progress, delays, site conditions, service-impacting issues, and project completion. Keep the <strong>Hospital Manager (HM)</strong> informed of any site-related concerns, operational impacts, access needs, or service interruptions.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Be mindful that veterinary hospitals are active patient-care environments and minimize disruption to staff, patients, and daily operations whenever possible.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Exercise discretion and professionalism when working in exam rooms, treatment areas, surgery spaces, kennels, and other patient-care environments.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Maintain a clean, organized work area and remove debris throughout the project.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Immediately communicate any scope concerns, pathway challenges, material shortages, or unforeseen conditions before proceeding.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Be courteous, respectful, and solution-oriented when interacting with hospital staff and management.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Protect existing infrastructure and maintain operational services whenever possible.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Follow all site-specific safety and infection-control requirements.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thoroughly document completed work with accurate photos, testing results, and project notes.</p><p>Thank you for your prompt attention to this assignment.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Sincerely,</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>The VAI PMO Team</strong>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:**\n\n**Join the Teams Meeting Bridge when you check in, before you enter the site.**\n\n**The survey link will be sent 30 minutes to 1 hour before the start time.**\n\nValuance AI is seeking an experienced, detail‑oriented field technician to perform a comprehensive **Infrastructure & Network Site Audit** using the Valuance AI Site Survey web application. This audit documents the current‑state environment across:\n\n- Network infrastructure\n- Telephony/VOIP systems\n- Structured cabling\n- Wi‑Fi\n- Workstations and peripherals\n- Servers and UPS systems\n- Imaging equipment (X‑ray, dental, ultrasound)\n- Life‑safety and analog lines\n\nThe technician will follow the **VAI Site Audit SOP**, which includes evaluating MDF/IDF rooms, photographing all equipment, identifying cabling issues, and capturing performance snapshots such as wired/wireless speed tests and Wi‑Fi observations. All findings feed directly into the VAI Site Audit Report, Executive Summary, and Network/Device Inventory used to build upgrade recommendations.\n\nThe onsite workflow includes checking in with the VAI PM, meeting with the Hospital Manager (HM), conducting an HM interview, and performing a full building walkthrough starting with MDF/IDFs. The technician will inspect and photograph:\n\n- Network closets, racks, cabling pathways\n- Patch panels, switches, APs\n- Telephony handsets, PBX/analog components\n- Workstations, printers, imaging devices\n- Any areas requiring new cabling drops\n\nAdditional tasks include mapping AP locations, identifying Wi‑Fi dead zones, validating cabling labels, capturing MOS/jitter/latency feedback, and documenting VOIP migration readiness.\n\n**Login to Valuance AI Site Audit,**\n\nYou’ve been assigned a site survey. This survey is required to gather the information needed for our project.\n\nPlease follow the steps below to access and complete your survey:\n\n**Step 1: Invitation Email**\n\n You will receive an account‑creation email from **Base44** (the platform hosting our application). This will be sent to the email you provided Valuance AI.\n\n **Action:** Look for an email with a subject similar to *“You’ve been invited to join…”*. If you don’t see it, please check your spam/junk folder.\n\n**Step 2: Create Your Account**\n\n The invitation email includes a link to set up your account.\n\n **Action:** Click the link and create your password to activate your account.\n\n**Step 3: Log In**\n\n Once your account is created, log in to the **VAI Intelligent IT Survey** application.\n\n **Action:** Use your email and the password you just created.\n\n**Step 4: Access Your Survey**\n\n After logging in, you will be taken directly to the survey assigned to you—no searching required.\n\n **Action:** Complete each section. Your progress saves automatically.\n\n**Important Notes**\n\n- **Survey Completion:** Once you submit the survey, your access to the application will automatically be removed.\n- **Support:** If you have any issues with account setup, login, or accessing the survey, please contact **Cam Berow, cberow@valuanceai.com**\n\n**Valuance AI Expectations Onsite**\n\n• Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor at all times while interacting with hospital staff, vendors, and clients.\n\n• Be proactive in communicating with **Valuance AI project management and remote support** regarding arrival, progress, delays, site conditions, service-impacting issues, and project completion. Keep the **Hospital Manager (HM)** informed of any site-related concerns, operational impacts, access needs, or service interruptions.\n\n• Be mindful that veterinary hospitals are active patient-care environments and minimize disruption to staff, patients, and daily operations whenever possible.\n\n• Exercise discretion and professionalism when working in exam rooms, treatment areas, surgery spaces, kennels, and other patient-care environments.\n\n• Maintain a clean, organized work area and remove debris throughout the project.\n\n• Immediately communicate any scope concerns, pathway challenges, material shortages, or unforeseen conditions before proceeding.\n\n• Be courteous, respectful, and solution-oriented when interacting with hospital staff and management.\n\n• Protect existing infrastructure and maintain operational services whenever possible.\n\n• Follow all site-specific safety and infection-control requirements.\n\n• Thoroughly document completed work with accurate photos, testing results, and project notes.\n\nThank you for your prompt attention to this assignment.\n\n**Sincerely,**\n\n **The VAI PMO Team**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T09:00","end":"2026-10-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":36.650526392206004},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 19, 9:00 AM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $450 · listed maximum: $300\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-Th