{"job":{"id":20140608,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"3 AP Replacement | 1 Lead Tech + 1 Spotter | Training Required | Lead Tech Must Have Lift & OSHA Fall Protection Cert","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.</li><li>Estimated duration: 3 hours.</li><li><strong>Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.</strong></li><li><strong>Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.</strong></li><li><strong>Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.</strong></li><li><strong>Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)</strong></li></ul><p>Scope of Work</p><p>Dispatch <strong>1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter</strong> to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of <strong>3 wireless access points</strong>.</p><p><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> Approximately<strong>3 hours</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Staffing Requirement</p><p>This work order requires:</p><ul><li><strong>1 Lead Field Technician</strong></li><li><strong>1 Spotter</strong></li></ul><p>Both resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.</p><p><strong>Do not dispatch only one person.</strong></p><p>The Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.</p><p><br></p><p>Mandatory Training &amp; Certification Requirements</p><p><strong>Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.</strong></p><p>The <strong>Lead Technician must also have:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Valid Lift Certification</strong></li><li><strong>Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate</strong></li><li><strong>Proper lift safety harness available onsite</strong></li></ul><p>The Spotter does <strong>not</strong> require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.</p><p><br></p><p>Work to Be Completed</p><ol><li>Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.</li><li>Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.</li><li>Complete a <strong>1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs</strong>.</li><li>Replace APs one at a time.</li><li>Record and photograph the <strong>serial number and MAC address</strong> of each new AP before installation.</li><li>Remove the existing AP.</li><li>Install the replacement AP in the same location.</li><li>Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.</li><li>Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.</li><li>Repeat the process for all 3 APs.</li><li>Complete final validation with the onsite POC.</li><li>Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.</li><li>Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.</li></ol><p><strong>Required Photos / Deliverables</strong></p><p><strong>For each AP, provide clear photos showing:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>New AP serial number</strong></li><li><strong>New AP MAC address</strong></li><li><strong>AP fully installed</strong></li><li><strong>AP securely mounted</strong></li><li><strong>Final completed installation</strong></li></ul><p>All required <strong>VCOs, photos, and other deliverables</strong> must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.</p><p><br></p><p>PPE Requirement</p><p>Full PPE is mandatory for both resources:</p><ul><li>Hard hat</li><li>Safety glasses</li><li>Safety vest</li><li>Steel-toe boots</li></ul><p>For the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:</p><ul><li><strong>Lift harness is mandatory</strong></li></ul><p>Both resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.</p><p><br></p><p>Before Going Onsite</p><p>At least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:</p><ul><li>Lead Technician assigned</li><li>Spotter assigned</li><li>Technician and Spotter contact information submitted</li><li>Required Amazon/site training completed for both</li><li>Lead Technician Lift Certification verified</li><li>Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified</li><li>Avetta/site access requirements completed</li><li>Full PPE available</li><li>Lift harness available for Lead Technician</li><li>Site address confirmed</li><li>Scheduled arrival time confirmed</li><li>Required tools available</li><li>Lift requirement understood</li><li>Scope and deliverables reviewed</li></ul><p>Completion Requirement</p><p>The WO will only be considered complete after:</p><ul><li>All 3 APs have been replaced</li><li>All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC</li><li>Required serial/MAC photos have been captured</li><li>Final installation photos have been captured</li><li>All required deliverables have been submitted</li><li>Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with<strong>Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947</strong></li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to<strong>mbaroi@techhubps.com</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time</li><li>Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.\n- Estimated duration: 3 hours.\n- **Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.**\n- **Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.**\n- **Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.**\n- **Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- **Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)**\n\nScope of Work\n\nDispatch **1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter** to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of **3 wireless access points**.\n\n**Estimated onsite duration:** Approximately**3 hours**\n\nStaffing Requirement\n\nThis work order requires:\n\n- **1 Lead Field Technician**\n- **1 Spotter**\n\nBoth resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.\n\n**Do not dispatch only one person.**\n\nThe Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.\n\nMandatory Training & Certification Requirements\n\n**Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.**\n\nThe **Lead Technician must also have:**\n\n- **Valid Lift Certification**\n- **Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate**\n- **Proper lift safety harness available onsite**\n\nThe Spotter does **not** require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.\n\nWork to Be Completed\n\n1. Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.\n2. Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.\n3. Complete a **1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs**.\n4. Replace APs one at a time.\n5. Record and photograph the **serial number and MAC address** of each new AP before installation.\n6. Remove the existing AP.\n7. Install the replacement AP in the same location.\n8. Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.\n9. Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.\n10. Repeat the process for all 3 APs.\n11. Complete final validation with the onsite POC.\n12. Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.\n13. Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.\n\n**Required Photos / Deliverables**\n\n**For each AP, provide clear photos showing:**\n\n- **New AP serial number**\n- **New AP MAC address**\n- **AP fully installed**\n- **AP securely mounted**\n- **Final completed installation**\n\nAll required **VCOs, photos, and other deliverables** must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.\n\nPPE Requirement\n\nFull PPE is mandatory for both resources:\n\n- Hard hat\n- Safety glasses\n- Safety vest\n- Steel-toe boots\n\nFor the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:\n\n- **Lift harness is mandatory**\n\nBoth resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.\n\nBefore Going Onsite\n\nAt least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:\n\n- Lead Technician assigned\n- Spotter assigned\n- Technician and Spotter contact information submitted\n- Required Amazon/site training completed for both\n- Lead Technician Lift Certification verified\n- Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified\n- Avetta/site access requirements completed\n- Full PPE available\n- Lift harness available for Lead Technician\n- Site address confirmed\n- Scheduled arrival time confirmed\n- Required tools available\n- Lift requirement understood\n- Scope and deliverables reviewed\n\nCompletion Requirement\n\nThe WO will only be considered complete after:\n\n- All 3 APs have been replaced\n- All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC\n- Required serial/MAC photos have been captured\n- Final installation photos have been captured\n- All required deliverables have been submitted\n- Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with**Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947**\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to**mbaroi@techhubps.com**\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time\n- Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T14:30","end":"2026-10-12T19:15"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4.75,"distance":11.947825927799878},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 12, 2:30 PM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05809722 - VEG - Cary NC - Managed Starlink Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"