{"job":{"id":20141619,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Schedule Turn Up - Store #6425: 3771 Ramsey St, Fayetteville, NC 28311 -  00042570","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*******CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! ********</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>Guidecx Project: https://app.guidecx.com/app/projects/15e23968-7ef7-4bbc-bcb4-31490072b289</p>\n<p>Project Manager: Anna Cond</p>\n<p>DISPATCH REQUEST</p>\n<p>Address:</p>\n<p>3771 Ramsey St.</p>\n<p>Fayetteville, NC 28311</p>\n<p>Company Name: Five Below- Store #6425</p>\n<p>Dispatch date/time: Monday- 10/12/26- Tech to arrive by 10am</p>\n<p>Local Contact: Manager on Duty</p>\n<p>We are installing a new 500M/20M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP&gt; Spectrum. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit, ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point-of-sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.</p>\n<p><del>******** ******* ** *****</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ** ******* ************</del></p>\n<p><del>******* *** ************</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ** ****** *************************</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ***** ***************</del></p>\n<p><del>*** ******** ************</del></p>\n<p><del>*** ********** ************</del></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<p>• Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************</del></p>\n<p>• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</p>\n<p>• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</p>\n<p>• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),<strong>350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools</strong>. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <strong>206-494-6399</strong></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email <strong>turnups@sangoma.com</strong> with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call<strong>206-494-6399</strong>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nGuidecx Project: <https://app.guidecx.com/app/projects/15e23968-7ef7-4bbc-bcb4-31490072b289>\n\nProject Manager: Anna Cond\n\nDISPATCH REQUEST\n\nAddress:\n\n3771 Ramsey St.\n\nFayetteville, NC 28311\n\nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #6425\n\nDispatch date/time: Monday- 10/12/26- Tech to arrive by 10am\n\nLocal Contact: Manager on Duty\n\nWe are installing a new 500M/20M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP> Spectrum. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit, ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point-of-sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n\n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),**350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools**. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at **206-494-6399**\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email **turnups@sangoma.com** with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call**206-494-6399**with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T10:00","end":"2026-10-12T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":53.74664726689396},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z"