{"job":{"id":20142901,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":" Troubleshoot Camera","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******** * </del></span><del>******************</del></li><li>Technicians can text 'Start' to <del>***** ********</del>. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">System &amp; Model #:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Hikvision</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Video feed is lagging due to bad cradle point performance. SOW: Tech is to check if they are able to relocate the cradle point in order for it to get better signals. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech is to check the DVR feed after and make sure the DVR has a more consistent feed and no issues with recording. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech is to determine if an external antenna is required for the cradle point to get better signals, or if a SIM replacement is needed. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech is to reach out to helpdesk with findings. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech is to bring all necessary tools and a ladder.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Parts Needed:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">n/a</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Specific Scheduling Request :</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">None</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Other Open Work Orders ? Combine Dispatch Request:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">None</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cause :</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Bad connection / cradle point signal</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.</li><li>Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.</li><li>All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location</li><li>Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call <del>************ ** ***</del> service desk if support does not transfer.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians can text 'Start' to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.\n\nStatement of Work (Security/Interactive)\n\nSystem & Model #:\n\nHikvision\n\nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem :\n\nVideo feed is lagging due to bad cradle point performance. SOW: Tech is to check if they are able to relocate the cradle point in order for it to get better signals.\n\nTech is to check the DVR feed after and make sure the DVR has a more consistent feed and no issues with recording.\n\nTech is to determine if an external antenna is required for the cradle point to get better signals, or if a SIM replacement is needed.\n\nTech is to reach out to helpdesk with findings.\n\nTech is to bring all necessary tools and a ladder.\n\nParts Needed:\n\nn/a\n\nSpecific Scheduling Request :\n\nNone\n\nOther Open Work Orders ? Combine Dispatch Request:\n\nNone\n\nCause :\n\nBad connection / cradle point signal\n\n- Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.\n- Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.\n- All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location\n- Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* service desk if support does not transfer.\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN \\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).\n- Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc\n- Picture of RMA form & return label applied; if applicable\n- Release Code\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 11)\n- Operating system must be fully licensed and updated\n- · Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Buttset\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Drill\n- 12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete\n- 8' Ladder\n- Phone/Ethernet Wiring\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Contact Name & Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**\n\n**Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T08:00","end":"2026-10-09T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-09T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":8.766766448920245},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/9/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"FW: Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T1