{"job":{"id":20143293,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Splice Communications","title":"RETURN VISIT | Phase 1 - Windows 10 Device Documentation and Removal","description":{"html":"<p><strong>﻿PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A CALIBER COLLISION TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mandatory Scope Discussion</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have <strong>not previously completed work for this specific project phase</strong> must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.</p>\n<p>If contacted, please plan to attend. <strong>Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Assessment Consideration Notice:</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have completed the required assessment will be prioritized for consideration. Providers who have not completed the assessment may not be eligible for assignment.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work – Caliber Return Visit | Windows 10 Device Removal</strong></p>\n<p>Technician needed to go onsite to locate and remove an existing Windows 10 device identified by serial number<strong>42TLNK3</strong> and prepare the equipment for Recycling ITAD/e-waste.</p>\n<p>Upon arrival, technician must meet with the General Manager or Manager on Duty and explain that the purpose of the visit is to locate a specific legacy Windows 10 device that needs to be removed from service.</p>\n<p>Technician must locate the device with Serial Number:<strong>42TLNK3</strong>. The device may be located within or near the network rack/MDF, so technician must carefully inspect the network equipment area. If the device is not found there, technician must check the existing Dell workstations onsite and coordinate with the manager to inspect the location where e-waste/decommissioned equipment is currently being stored.</p>\n<p><strong>Once the device is located, technician must:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Take clear pictures of the device, including a picture clearly showing serial number <strong>42TLNK3</strong></li>\n<li>Identify and document the type of device/equipment on attached Data Collection Spreadsheet with the required information for this device.</li>\n<li>Decommission the device as applicable and prepare it for Recycling ITAD/e-waste.</li>\n<li>Place a clearly visible sticky note or label on the equipment stating “E-Waste.”</li>\n<li>Take clear final pictures showing the device with the “E-Waste” label visibly attached.</li>\n<li>Leave the equipment in the designated e-waste location as directed by the onsite manager.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Before leaving the site, technician must verify that all required pictures have been collected and that the Recycling tab has been updated completely. Technician must then call project support to review the completed work and check out before leaving the location.</p>\n<p><strong>JOB DURATION</strong></p>\n<p>1.5hs approximately.</p>\n<p><strong>EXPERIENCE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Technical Skills &amp; Installation Experience</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Proficient in workstation deployments (hardware, dual monitors, peripherals, connectivity)</li>\n<li>Strong knowledge of structured cabling and cable management standards (routing, Velcro, labeling)</li>\n<li>Understanding of network connectivity (routers, firewalls, switches, APs) and basic troubleshooting</li>\n<li>Experience installing/configuring network devices, running Cat6, and working with PoE</li>\n<li>Ability to coordinate with remote support/NOC for provisioning, testing, and validation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Field Operations &amp; Site Work</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience working in MDF/IDF environments and performing site surveys</li>\n<li>Ability to document infrastructure with photos and provide clear reporting</li>\n<li>Skilled in equipment decommissioning, staging, and inventory tracking</li>\n<li>Comfortable working on ladders, in ceilings, and in active business environments</li>\n<li>Maintains clean work practices, organization, and professionalism onsite</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/ Ethernet</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers / hex set</li>\n<li>Cable tester</li>\n<li>8-10 ft step ladder - for internal use</li>\n<li>Tone/probe (preferred)</li>\n<li>Must have and use appropriate PPE (Personal Protective Equipment), including safety glasses, gloves, high-visibility vest, hard hat, and proper work boots</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>MATERIALS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Velcro cable management</li>\n<li>Keystone jacks (as needed)</li>\n<li>Patch cables</li>\n<li>Labeling materials</li>\n<li>General install consumables</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>PARTS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lenovo workstation packages (client provided)</li>\n<li>PoE injector (client provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>IMPORTANT CONTACTS &amp; ESCALATION PATH</strong></p>\n<p>CAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.</p>\n<p><u>Escalate for:</u></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Login issues</li>\n<li>Missing applications</li>\n<li>Cellular device not online</li>\n<li>Unsafe install conditions</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED TASKS / DELIVERABLES</strong></p>\n<p>1. Check-in with Splice Service Manager upon arrival</p>\n<p>2. Reach out to technical contacts as required</p>\n<p>3. Take BEFORE photos</p>\n<p>4. Validate scope with GM</p>\n<p>5. Install workstation hardware</p>\n<p>6. Validate user login and applications</p>\n<p>7. Decommission and consolidate equipment</p>\n<p>8. Perform network site survey</p>\n<p>9. Install cellular backup (if applicable)</p>\n<p>10. Coordinate validation with Engineering/NOC</p>\n<p>11. Take AFTER photos</p>\n<p>12. Check-out with Splice Service Manager</p>\n<p>13. Submit deliverables within 24 hours</p>","markdown":"**﻿PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A CALIBER COLLISION TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**Mandatory Scope Discussion**\n\nTechnicians who have **not previously completed work for this specific project phase** must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.\n\nIf contacted, please plan to attend. **Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.**\n\n**Assessment Consideration Notice:**\n\nTechnicians who have completed the required assessment will be prioritized for consideration. Providers who have not completed the assessment may not be eligible for assignment.\n\n**Scope of Work – Caliber Return Visit | Windows 10 Device Removal**\n\nTechnician needed to go onsite to locate and remove an existing Windows 10 device identified by serial number**42TLNK3** and prepare the equipment for Recycling ITAD/e-waste.\n\nUpon arrival, technician must meet with the General Manager or Manager on Duty and explain that the purpose of the visit is to locate a specific legacy Windows 10 device that needs to be removed from service.\n\nTechnician must locate the device with Serial Number:**42TLNK3**. The device may be located within or near the network rack/MDF, so technician must carefully inspect the network equipment area. If the device is not found there, technician must check the existing Dell workstations onsite and coordinate with the manager to inspect the location where e-waste/decommissioned equipment is currently being stored.\n\n**Once the device is located, technician must:**\n\n- Take clear pictures of the device, including a picture clearly showing serial number **42TLNK3**\n- Identify and document the type of device/equipment on attached Data Collection Spreadsheet with the required information for this device.\n- Decommission the device as applicable and prepare it for Recycling ITAD/e-waste.\n- Place a clearly visible sticky note or label on the equipment stating “E-Waste.”\n- Take clear final pictures showing the device with the “E-Waste” label visibly attached.\n- Leave the equipment in the designated e-waste location as directed by the onsite manager.\n\nBefore leaving the site, technician must verify that all required pictures have been collected and that the Recycling tab has been updated completely. Technician must then call project support to review the completed work and check out before leaving the location.\n\n**JOB DURATION**\n\n1.5hs approximately.\n\n**EXPERIENCE**\n\n**Technical Skills & Installation Experience**\n\n- Proficient in workstation deployments (hardware, dual monitors, peripherals, connectivity)\n- Strong knowledge of structured cabling and cable management standards (routing, Velcro, labeling)\n- Understanding of network connectivity (routers, firewalls, switches, APs) and basic troubleshooting\n- Experience installing/configuring network devices, running Cat6, and working with PoE\n- Ability to coordinate with remote support/NOC for provisioning, testing, and validation\n\n**Field Operations & Site Work**\n\n- Experience working in MDF/IDF environments and performing site surveys\n- Ability to document infrastructure with photos and provide clear reporting\n- Skilled in equipment decommissioning, staging, and inventory tracking\n- Comfortable working on ladders, in ceilings, and in active business environments\n- Maintains clean work practices, organization, and professionalism onsite\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS**\n\n- Laptop w/ Ethernet\n- Screwdrivers / hex set\n- Cable tester\n- 8-10 ft step ladder - for internal use\n- Tone/probe (preferred)\n- Must have and use appropriate PPE (Personal Protective Equipment), including safety glasses, gloves, high-visibility vest, hard hat, and proper work boots\n\n**As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.**\n\n**MATERIALS**\n\n- Velcro cable management\n- Keystone jacks (as needed)\n- Patch cables\n- Labeling materials\n- General install consumables\n\n**PARTS**\n\n- Lenovo workstation packages (client provided)\n- PoE injector (client provided)\n\n**IMPORTANT CONTACTS & ESCALATION PATH**\n\nCAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.\n\nEscalate for:\n\n- Login issues\n- Missing applications\n- Cellular device not online\n- Unsafe install conditions\n\n**REQUIRED TASKS / DELIVERABLES**\n\n1\\. Check-in with Splice Service Manager upon arrival\n\n2\\. Reach out to technical contacts as required\n\n3\\. Take BEFORE photos\n\n4\\. Validate scope with GM\n\n5\\. Install workstation hardware\n\n6\\. Validate user login and applications\n\n7\\. Decommission and consolidate equipment\n\n8\\. Perform network site survey\n\n9\\. Install cellular backup (if applicable)\n\n10\\. Coordinate validation with Engineering/NOC\n\n11\\. Take AFTER photos\n\n12\\. Check-out with Splice Service Manager\n\n13\\. Submit deliverables within 24 hours","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T09:00","end":"2026-10-13T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":75},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":9.620702801999888},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitors\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791581465942}
{"job":{"id":20143387,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"3 AP Replacement | 1 Lead Tech + 1 Spotter | Training Required | Lead Tech Must Have Lift & OSHA Fall Protection Cert","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.</li><li>Estimated duration: 3 hours.</li><li><strong>Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.</strong></li><li><strong>Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.</strong></li><li><strong>Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.</strong></li><li><strong>Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)</strong></li></ul><p>Scope of Work</p><p>Dispatch <strong>1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter</strong> to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of <strong>3 wireless access points</strong>.</p><p><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> Approximately<strong>3 hours</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Staffing Requirement</p><p>This work order requires:</p><ul><li><strong>1 Lead Field Technician</strong></li><li><strong>1 Spotter</strong></li></ul><p>Both resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.</p><p><strong>Do not dispatch only one person.</strong></p><p>The Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.</p><p><br></p><p>Mandatory Training &amp; Certification Requirements</p><p><strong>Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.</strong></p><p>The <strong>Lead Technician must also have:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Valid Lift Certification</strong></li><li><strong>Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate</strong></li><li><strong>Proper lift safety harness available onsite</strong></li></ul><p>The Spotter does <strong>not</strong> require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.</p><p><br></p><p>Work to Be Completed</p><ol><li>Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.</li><li>Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.</li><li>Complete a <strong>1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs</strong>.</li><li>Replace APs one at a time.</li><li>Record and photograph the <strong>serial number and MAC address</strong> of each new AP before installation.</li><li>Remove the existing AP.</li><li>Install the replacement AP in the same location.</li><li>Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.</li><li>Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.</li><li>Repeat the process for all 3 APs.</li><li>Complete final validation with the onsite POC.</li><li>Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.</li><li>Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.</li></ol><p><strong>Required Photos / Deliverables</strong></p><p><strong>For each AP, provide clear photos showing:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>New AP serial number</strong></li><li><strong>New AP MAC address</strong></li><li><strong>AP fully installed</strong></li><li><strong>AP securely mounted</strong></li><li><strong>Final completed installation</strong></li></ul><p>All required <strong>VCOs, photos, and other deliverables</strong> must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.</p><p><br></p><p>PPE Requirement</p><p>Full PPE is mandatory for both resources:</p><ul><li>Hard hat</li><li>Safety glasses</li><li>Safety vest</li><li>Steel-toe boots</li></ul><p>For the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:</p><ul><li><strong>Lift harness is mandatory</strong></li></ul><p>Both resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.</p><p><br></p><p>Before Going Onsite</p><p>At least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:</p><ul><li>Lead Technician assigned</li><li>Spotter assigned</li><li>Technician and Spotter contact information submitted</li><li>Required Amazon/site training completed for both</li><li>Lead Technician Lift Certification verified</li><li>Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified</li><li>Avetta/site access requirements completed</li><li>Full PPE available</li><li>Lift harness available for Lead Technician</li><li>Site address confirmed</li><li>Scheduled arrival time confirmed</li><li>Required tools available</li><li>Lift requirement understood</li><li>Scope and deliverables reviewed</li></ul><p>Completion Requirement</p><p>The WO will only be considered complete after:</p><ul><li>All 3 APs have been replaced</li><li>All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC</li><li>Required serial/MAC photos have been captured</li><li>Final installation photos have been captured</li><li>All required deliverables have been submitted</li><li>Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with<strong>Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947</strong></li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to<strong>mbaroi@techhubps.com</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time</li><li>Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.\n- Estimated duration: 3 hours.\n- **Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.**\n- **Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.**\n- **Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.**\n- **Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- **Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)**\n\nScope of Work\n\nDispatch **1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter** to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of **3 wireless access points**.\n\n**Estimated onsite duration:** Approximately**3 hours**\n\nStaffing Requirement\n\nThis work order requires:\n\n- **1 Lead Field Technician**\n- **1 Spotter**\n\nBoth resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.\n\n**Do not dispatch only one person.**\n\nThe Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.\n\nMandatory Training & Certification Requirements\n\n**Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.**\n\nThe **Lead Technician must also have:**\n\n- **Valid Lift Certification**\n- **Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate**\n- **Proper lift safety harness available onsite**\n\nThe Spotter does **not** require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.\n\nWork to Be Completed\n\n1. Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.\n2. Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.\n3. Complete a **1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs**.\n4. Replace APs one at a time.\n5. Record and photograph the **serial number and MAC address** of each new AP before installation.\n6. Remove the existing AP.\n7. Install the replacement AP in the same location.\n8. Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.\n9. Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.\n10. Repeat the process for all 3 APs.\n11. Complete final validation with the onsite POC.\n12. Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.\n13. Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.\n\n**Required Photos / Deliverables**\n\n**For each AP, provide clear photos showing:**\n\n- **New AP serial number**\n- **New AP MAC address**\n- **AP fully installed**\n- **AP securely mounted**\n- **Final completed installation**\n\nAll required **VCOs, photos, and other deliverables** must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.\n\nPPE Requirement\n\nFull PPE is mandatory for both resources:\n\n- Hard hat\n- Safety glasses\n- Safety vest\n- Steel-toe boots\n\nFor the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:\n\n- **Lift harness is mandatory**\n\nBoth resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.\n\nBefore Going Onsite\n\nAt least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:\n\n- Lead Technician assigned\n- Spotter assigned\n- Technician and Spotter contact information submitted\n- Required Amazon/site training completed for both\n- Lead Technician Lift Certification verified\n- Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified\n- Avetta/site access requirements completed\n- Full PPE available\n- Lift harness available for Lead Technician\n- Site address confirmed\n- Scheduled arrival time confirmed\n- Required tools available\n- Lift requirement understood\n- Scope and deliverables reviewed\n\nCompletion Requirement\n\nThe WO will only be considered complete after:\n\n- All 3 APs have been replaced\n- All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC\n- Required serial/MAC photos have been captured\n- Final installation photos have been captured\n- All required deliverables have been submitted\n- Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with**Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947**\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to**mbaroi@techhubps.com**\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time\n- Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T14:30","end":"2026-10-12T19:15"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4.75,"distance":11.947825927799878},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 12, 2:30 PM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13, Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791582132541}
{"job":{"id":20058860,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Deployment of new POS, network, and CCTV equipment for acquisition - Assistant Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span><u>TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS. ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT. ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">A 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date.&nbsp;At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy <del>*** ****</del> network and hardware with the new <del>*****</del> equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.</span></p><p><strong><em>The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.</em></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</li><li>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Deployment Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><ul><li>Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos</li><li>Install Network Rack Equipment</li></ul><p>----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch</p><p>----You will need to work with you <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem</p><ul><li>Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)</li></ul><p>----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed</p><p>----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs</p><p>----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important</p><ul><li>Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity</li><li>Install Multifunction Printer&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Install i-Gel Cubics PCs</li><li>Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)</li><li>Install Cameras</li><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with <del>*****</del> IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**﻿TECHS MUST LABEL BOTH ENDS OF CABLES CLEARLY WITH A PRINTED TAG. SHARPIE MARKS AND UNLABELED BISCUITS WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED AND MATERIALS MAY NOT BE REIMBURSED IF YOU WE MUST REPLACE YOUR RUNS. ANY RUN NOT CLEARLY LABELED AT BOTH JACKS IS INCOMPLETE BY THE STANDARDS OF THIS PROJECT. ALL NEW CABLES MUST BE RUN TO FINAL NETWORK LOCATION AFTER CUTOVER NOT THE TEMPORARY NETWORK STACK.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nA 2-day site visit to prep low-voltage cabling, network, and all IT equipment so that the site can be cutover at a later date. At the end of this visit, the site will still be running off the legacy \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* network and hardware with the new \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* equipment staged and ready to install during cutover.\n\n***The following work order template is for the 2-day Deployment visit only. Please review the work order page below and all documents in the documents section prior to arriving on your first site.***\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Deployment Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n- Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos\n- Install Network Rack Equipment\n\n\\----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch\n\n\\----You will need to work with you \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem\n\n- Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)\n\n\\----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed\n\n\\----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs\n\n\\----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important\n\n- Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity\n- Install Multifunction Printer\n- Install i-Gel Cubics PCs\n- Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)\n- Install Cameras\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T10:00","end":"2026-10-14T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":1040},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":16,"distance":16.61055715075782},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end"