{"job":{"id":20143741,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"FFF Enterprises / RightNow Inventory","title":"Service Visit - New Cabinet Installation - MBRx 10740","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in basic IT hardware installation, and possibly software installation.</li><li>Tech is required to assist with the cabinet installation.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 2 hrs. Each cabinet will take around 2 hrs. to complete. The number of cabinets for the location is listed within this work order for reference (field called '# of cabinets').</li><li><strong>Technician is expected to check-in onsite via phone or text within 15 minutes of work order start time</strong></li><li><strong>This is a single person job, unless otherwise notated.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Onsite Do's &amp; Don'ts:</strong></p><ul><li>DO dress Business casual.</li><li>DO provide identification via Field Nation badge</li><li>DO greet our customer with a SMILE and a positive attitude.</li><li>DON'T use the customer's property.</li><li>DON'T bring any unauthorized visitors to the site.</li></ul><p><strong>COVID-19 Onsite Protocol</strong>: Comply with all onsite Health/COVID instructions (i.e wear masks, complete temperature checks, use hand sanitizer, etc.)</p><p><strong>Tools Required:&nbsp;</strong><em>must haves - If you are missing any of the below tools, please do not accept this work order.</em></p><ul><li>Cell Phone with Camera</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><ul><li>Tech is required to assist with the cabinet installation.</li></ul><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>Confirm assignment of work order and set start time.</li><li><strong>Review all tasks and procedures to ensure knowledge and awareness of what is required when on site.</strong></li><li>Provide final confirmation via the Field Nation work order the day prior to the scheduled service visit.</li><li>Call or message the work order manager with any questions/concerns</li><li><strong>Download and save/print identification badge located in the client documents section of the work order.</strong></li><li>Complete all listed tasks.</li></ol><p><strong><u>DAY OF TASKS (prior to arriving to site):</u></strong></p><ol><li>Text \"On my Way\" and Work Order Number or Your Name to<del>************</del>&nbsp;30-60 minutes prior to arrival.</li><li>Mark on my way within Field Nation App</li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks: This includes an overview of what needs to be completed onsite.</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order on Field Nation interface.</li><li>Upon arrival to site, text \"On Site\" to<del>*************</del></li><li><strong>Technician is expected to check-in onsite via phone or text within 15 minutes of work order start time</strong></li><li>Call the location contact (See contacts section) to introduce yourself and request access to the MinibarRx cabinet to be serviced.</li><li>Call Tech Support at&nbsp;<del>****************** ******* ** **** ****** **</del>&nbsp;once in front of the MinibarRx cabinet to be serviced.</li><li>Complete service following instructions provided by Tech Support/Service Team member by phone.</li><li>Upload photos of completed work. Photos should include Cabinet's location in the facility and any cosmetic damage to the cabinet</li><li>Call&nbsp;<del>************ ******* ** **** ****** **</del>&nbsp;to confirm successful connection of cabinet and to complete check out process.</li><li>Upon completion of job, before departure, text \"Job Complete\" to&nbsp;<del>*************</del></li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>Call Tech Support to check in and check out of work order</li><li>Photos of completed work</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>For assistance in reaching location contact or finding the cabinet to be serviced, text&nbsp;<del>************</del>&nbsp;or call <del>************ ******* ***</del></li><li>For technical support relating to repair of cabinet, call<del>************ ******* ** **** ****** **</del></li><li>Any other issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;<del>******* **** ** ***** ********************* ********* ** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours will be payed at $100/hour</li><li>Additional expenses related to the work order (ie: Parking fees, tolls, etc.) require documentation&nbsp;<strong><u>prior</u></strong>&nbsp;to approval.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RNI will not pay for gas, unless negotiated in a counter offer.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tolls will be approved on a case by case basis. The toll receipt must show&nbsp;<strong><u>DATE &amp; TIME</u></strong>, to confirm it aligns within the timeframe of the On My Way Status.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in basic IT hardware installation, and possibly software installation.\n- Tech is required to assist with the cabinet installation.\n- Estimated duration will be 2 hrs. Each cabinet will take around 2 hrs. to complete. The number of cabinets for the location is listed within this work order for reference (field called '# of cabinets').\n- **Technician is expected to check-in onsite via phone or text within 15 minutes of work order start time**\n- **This is a single person job, unless otherwise notated.**\n\n**Onsite Do's & Don'ts:**\n\n- DO dress Business casual.\n- DO provide identification via Field Nation badge\n- DO greet our customer with a SMILE and a positive attitude.\n- DON'T use the customer's property.\n- DON'T bring any unauthorized visitors to the site.\n\n**COVID-19 Onsite Protocol**: Comply with all onsite Health/COVID instructions (i.e wear masks, complete temperature checks, use hand sanitizer, etc.)\n\n**Tools Required:** *must haves - If you are missing any of the below tools, please do not accept this work order.*\n\n- Cell Phone with Camera\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Tech is required to assist with the cabinet installation.\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Confirm assignment of work order and set start time.\n2. **Review all tasks and procedures to ensure knowledge and awareness of what is required when on site.**\n3. Provide final confirmation via the Field Nation work order the day prior to the scheduled service visit.\n4. Call or message the work order manager with any questions/concerns\n5. **Download and save/print identification badge located in the client documents section of the work order.**\n6. Complete all listed tasks.\n\n**DAY OF TASKS (prior to arriving to site):**\n\n1. Text \"On my Way\" and Work Order Number or Your Name to\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* 30-60 minutes prior to arrival.\n2. Mark on my way within Field Nation App\n\n***On-Site Tasks: This includes an overview of what needs to be completed onsite.***\n\n1. Check-in to work order on Field Nation interface.\n2. Upon arrival to site, text \"On Site\" to\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. **Technician is expected to check-in onsite via phone or text within 15 minutes of work order start time**\n4. Call the location contact (See contacts section) to introduce yourself and request access to the MinibarRx cabinet to be serviced.\n5. Call Tech Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* once in front of the MinibarRx cabinet to be serviced.\n6. Complete service following instructions provided by Tech Support/Service Team member by phone.\n7. Upload photos of completed work. Photos should include Cabinet's location in the facility and any cosmetic damage to the cabinet\n8. Call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* to confirm successful connection of cabinet and to complete check out process.\n9. Upon c