{"job":{"id":20144262,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240 Printer Service - Image Quality Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>Install consumable parts and troubleshoot ongoing image quality issues on new printer<br /><br />PARTS SHIPPED: Verify delivery of parts before arriving onsite. Tracking will be added to \"Shipments\" once it becomes available. </p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p>California Ink &amp; Toner Waste Compliance Requirements</p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>IF</strong> parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>IF</strong> parts were received, take a picture of all the parts, packaging and part manifest. This will be used as a reference at the end of service to ensure any parts being returned are packed correctly.</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>production print to verify the printer functionality.</strong></li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to confirm deliverables and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All&nbsp;<strong>used and unused parts</strong>&nbsp;must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to&nbsp;determine&nbsp;return or disposal requirements.&nbsp;Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li>The parts return packages must be dropped off at the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup counter&nbsp;</strong>inside the Walgreens location<strong>.&nbsp;</strong>You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, and obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature.</strong></li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If parts are shipped, picture of the packaging, the parts received and the part manifest.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the inside the printer to show it is clean.</li><li>Image of the outside of the printer to show the condition it was left in after service.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the&nbsp;<strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>,&nbsp;<strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>,&nbsp;<strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nInstall consumable parts and troubleshoot ongoing image quality issues on new printer  \n  \nPARTS SHIPPED: Verify delivery of parts before arriving onsite. Tracking will be added to \"Shipments\" once it becomes available.\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCalifornia Ink & Toner Waste Compliance Requirements\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n2. **IF** parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n3. **IF** parts were received, take a picture of all the parts, packaging and part manifest. This will be used as a reference at the end of service to ensure any parts being returned are packed correctly.\n4. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n5. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **production print to verify the printer functionality.**\n6. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n7. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n8. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n9. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n10. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n11. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n12. The parts return packages must be dropped off at the **FedEx pickup counter** inside the Walgreens location**.** You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.\n13. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, and obtain their **signature.**\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If parts are shipped, picture of the packaging, the parts received and the part manifest.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of 30 test prints with at least one print from each paper tray showing good quality.\n- Image of the inside the printer to show it is clean.\n- Image of the outside of the printer to show the condition it was left in after service.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T11:00","end":"2026-10-12T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-12T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.444484706088215},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","sum