{"job":{"id":20148014,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TailWind Voice & Data, Inc.","title":"Q1, K1 EOL Swaps","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Objective Statement: </strong></p><p>Q1, K1 EOL Swaps</p><p><br></p><p>Work with BBI NOC throughout dispatch after sending before photos</p><p>Email subject line- OBS3452, send before photos with that subject line so they know it is you and then call BBI NOC. Leave voicemail if they do not answer.</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>• Standard ICT technician tools and “Van Stock” materials including but not limited to:</p><p>• 10ft “A” frame Ladder&nbsp;</p><p>• Electronic Label Maker (example: P-Touch)</p><p>• Spare CAT 5E/6 Keystone jacks</p><p>• Spare CAT6 UTP Cable&nbsp;</p><p>• UTP Cable Termination tools</p><p>• Cable Toner &amp; UTP Tester/ Certifier&nbsp;</p><p>• VELCRO</p><p>• Shop Vac&nbsp;</p><p>• Misc. mounting hardware, zip-ties, plastic wall cleats, variety of drywall/wood screws</p><p><strong>Required Deliverable Format: Technician will be asked to complete a specific JotForm to collect the appropriate deliverables. This is a required task.</strong></p><p>****PICTURES CANNOT BE SENT IN A LINK, MUST BE IN THE EMAIL****</p><p>*Refer to Install Guide if provided*</p><p><br></p><p>Before and After Installation: - Email all before and after photos with the Subject line including Site ID: OBS3452 Before or After&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Email all photos to: mdelpozzo@Bloominbrands.com &amp; ITImplementation@bloominbrands.com and call BBI NOC (656) 207-5541 once sent for both Before and After.</p><p><br></p><p>• Complete Deliverables form https://form.jotform.com/261873933206057 prior to checking out with Tailwind</p><p><br></p><p>There are standard BBI deliverables for anytime a technician is working on the network rack. They will need these in addition to other requested SOW photos.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Standard Network Rack Photos:</p><p>a)&nbsp;Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)</p><p>b)&nbsp;Customer network rack (door open)</p><p>c) Any Work location exceptions (i.e. broken ceiling tiles, poor cable management, unsecured rack, missing door or side(s), etc.)</p><p><br></p><p>Additional Requested Photos: Tailwind Signed work order</p><p><strong>TailWind Requirements: </strong></p><ul><li>Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.</li><li>Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.</li><li>Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.</li><li>Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Objective Statement:**\n\nQ1, K1 EOL Swaps\n\nWork with BBI NOC throughout dispatch after sending before photos\n\nEmail subject line- OBS3452, send before photos with that subject line so they know it is you and then call BBI NOC. Leave voicemail if they do not answer.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n• Standard ICT technician tools and “Van Stock” materials including but not limited to:\n\n• 10ft “A” frame Ladder\n\n• Electronic Label Maker (example: P-Touch)\n\n• Spare CAT 5E/6 Keystone jacks\n\n• Spare CAT6 UTP Cable\n\n• UTP Cable Termination tools\n\n• Cable Toner & UTP Tester/ Certifier\n\n• VELCRO\n\n• Shop Vac\n\n• Misc. mounting hardware, zip-ties, plastic wall cleats, variety of drywall/wood screws\n\n**Required Deliverable Format: Technician will be asked to complete a specific JotForm to collect the appropriate deliverables. This is a required task.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*PICTURES CANNOT BE SENT IN A LINK, MUST BE IN THE EMAIL\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*Refer to Install Guide if provided\\*\n\nBefore and After Installation: - Email all before and after photos with the Subject line including Site ID: OBS3452 Before or After\n\nEmail all photos to: mdelpozzo@Bloominbrands.com & ITImplementation@bloominbrands.com and call BBI NOC (656) 207-5541 once sent for both Before and After.\n\n• Complete Deliverables form <https://form.jotform.com/261873933206057> prior to checking out with Tailwind\n\nThere are standard BBI deliverables for anytime a technician is working on the network rack. They will need these in addition to other requested SOW photos.\n\nStandard Network Rack Photos:\n\na) Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)\n\nb) Customer network rack (door open)\n\nc) Any Work location exceptions (i.e. broken ceiling tiles, poor cable management, unsecured rack, missing door or side(s), etc.)\n\nAdditional Requested Photos: Tailwind Signed work order\n\n**TailWind Requirements:**\n\n- Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.\n- Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.\n- Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)\n- Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.\n- Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.\n- Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.\n- Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T08:30","end":"2026-10-27T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":62.35341835514052},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791814139722}
{"job":{"id":20148310,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Inter Prompt Global - IPGlobal247","title":"Freelance Network in | Military Site| H&F at store 344615 | CAMP LEJEUNE, NC USA","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Kindly read all the details mentioned below carefully and let us know if there is any concern before accepting the WO. Provider to download and read the Manual is a must.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong>: HUB Bypass</p>\n<p><strong>Cable Roll</strong>- 300ft</p>\n<p><strong>Ladder</strong>: Not required</p>\n<p><strong>This is a military site and tech needs to carry Real ID with Star and reach out to store 2days in advance so that his access can be processed.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Equipment's Tech needs to carry:</strong> Tech needs to carry a Laptop with TeamViewer installed, LAN cable patch cord, cable tester, Crimping tool, console cables, CAT6 cable and also requires a good hotspot for fast internet connectivity.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Need these documents before reached the site:</u></strong></p>\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Valid driver’s license</p>\n<p>2. Any 2 valid form of photo IDs</p>\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vehicle registration (Actual DMV paper copy and current. Not car tags)</p>\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Current vehicle registration (Paper form or even insurance app will work)</p>\n<p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If driving rental you must have rental agreement on hand.</p>\n<p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Social Security #</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>*Special Instructions: *</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Field engineer (FE) to provide pre-work photos of racks and the site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share a screenshot of the meeting.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to provide photos of devices (both new and old) with clearly visible serial numbers.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to send frequent updates every 30 minutes while on-site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share post-work photos upon completion of the task.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to provide a list of consumables used and their costs after completing the work.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share the site visit report signed by the Point of Contact (POC) before leaving&nbsp;the&nbsp;site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Once the activity is confirmed; kindly do not back out from the WO. Also, we cannot change the scheduled time and date after confirmation from the client.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿<u>If the work window is for 02 to 03 hours and the remote engineer team asks the provider to stay on-site. Kindly stay on site, as the provider will be paid by the additional hourly rate, in order to have a successful activity and a positive business relationship.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Material Costs must be shared with the invoice, It can be engineer's company letter head or from the vendor. Without the Material Invoice, such expenses will not be approved.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Materials to be as per actual Cat6e cable to charged at (50 Cents) per ft. and other materials cost as per actual amount attach screenshot for cost verification if purchased online.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the access is not arranged due to some reason, the Field Engineer is requested to be near the site within a 01-02 Miles radius, to have their access arranged and for activity completion. However, the waiting time will be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The engineer cannot leave the site unless the onsite POC allows him to leave after the successful completion of the activity.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>*****Engineer to report the work progress update (within every 30 minutes), to our IT Team through a WhatsApp group created by our team and to Remote Engineer (RE) team over teams is a must.******</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A Detailed task manual is attached for reference.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sharing sample picture of DB9 to USB console cable for Adtran router.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>***Incomplete work or the provider leaving the site without the Remote engineer's approval will result in escalation and payment will not be made.***</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Time spent on site will be compensated for additional hours by the engineer even after the activity is completed. So that the remote engineer can check and confirm the status of the work done.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Activity goes more than 8 hours, an additional 40 USD per hour will be paid.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The provider must never perform any work or services or business with the customer, while they are executing the task in the task execution time frame.</strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Kindly read all the details mentioned below carefully and let us know if there is any concern before accepting the WO. Provider to download and read the Manual is a must.**\n\n**Scope of Work**: HUB Bypass\n\n**Cable Roll**- 300ft\n\n**Ladder**: Not required\n\n**This is a military site and tech needs to carry Real ID with Star and reach out to store 2days in advance so that his access can be processed.**\n\n**Equipment's Tech needs to carry:** Tech needs to carry a Laptop with TeamViewer installed, LAN cable patch cord, cable tester, Crimping tool, console cables, CAT6 cable and also requires a good hotspot for fast internet connectivity.\n\n**Need these documents before reached the site:**\n\n1\\. Valid driver’s license\n\n2\\. Any 2 valid form of photo IDs\n\n3\\. Vehicle registration (Actual DMV paper copy and current. Not car tags)\n\n4\\. Current vehicle registration (Paper form or even insurance app will work)\n\n5\\. If driving rental you must have rental agreement on hand.\n\n6\\. Social Security #\n\n**\\*Special Instructions: \\***\n\n- **Field engineer (FE) to provide pre-work photos of racks and the site.**\n- **FE to share a screenshot of the meeting.**\n- **FE to provide photos of devices (both new and old) with clearly visible serial numbers.**\n- **FE to send frequent updates every 30 minutes while on-site.**\n- **FE to share post-work photos upon completion of the task.**\n- **FE to provide a list of consumables used and their costs after completing the work.**\n- **FE to share the site visit report signed by the Point of Contact (POC) before leaving the site.**\n- **Once the activity is confirmed; kindly do not back out from the WO. Also, we cannot change the scheduled time and date after confirmation from the client.**\n- **﻿If the work window is for 02 to 03 hours and the remote engineer team asks the provider to stay on-site. Kindly stay on site, as the provider will be paid by the additional hourly rate, in order to have a successful activity and a positive business relationship.**\n- **Material Costs must be shared with the invoice, It can be engineer's company letter head or from the vendor. Without the Material Invoice, such expenses will not be approved.**\n- **Materials to be as per actual Cat6e cable to charged at (50 Cents) per ft. and other materials cost as per actual amount attach screenshot for cost verification if purchased online.**\n- **If the access is not arranged due to some reason, the Field Engineer is requested to be near the site within a 01-02 Miles radius, to have their access arranged and for activity completion. However, the waiting time will be compensated.**\n- **The engineer cannot leave the site unless the onsite POC allows him to leave after the successful completion of the activity.**\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Engineer to report the work progress update (within every 30 minutes), to our IT Team through a WhatsApp group created by our team and to Remote Engineer (RE) team over teams is a must.\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- **A Detailed task manual is attached for reference.**\n- **Sharing sample picture of DB9 to USB console cable for Adtran router.**\n- **\\*\\*\\*Incomplete work or the provider leaving the site without the Remote engineer's approval will result in escalation and payment will not be made.\\*\\*\\***\n- **Time spent on site will be compensated for additional hours by the engineer even after the activity is completed. So that the remote engineer can check and confirm the status of the work done.**\n- **Activity goes more than 8 hours, an additional 40 USD per hour will be paid.**\n- **The provider must never perform any work or services or business with the customer, while they are executing the task in the task execution time frame.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T09:00","end":"2026-10-13T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":115.33307949835606},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 115.33307949835606mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791816368500}
