{"job":{"id":20085223,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"IW Technologies","title":"Variety Wholesalers Pin Pad Refresh","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Summary of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>IW Technologies is looking for a technician to complete a pin pad replacement at a local retailer. The scope includes replacing the existing pin pads, installing the switch, configuring and testing the devices. Please record each pin pad serial number with its corresponding lane number. Pack the existing pin pads and Verifone cables in the original tamper-safe white packaging, and drop the box off at FedEx.</p>\n<p><strong>QTY of Lanes: 3</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID</li>\n<li>Velcro</li>\n<li>1.25\" hole saw w/drill</li>\n<li>Variety of Phillips screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Loctite to use on the pin pad screws for the mount</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Visit Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>Be sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order</p>\n<p>Confirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</p>\n<p><strong>Onsite Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198</p>\n<p>Mount the new pinpad in the <strong>same location as the old pinpad</strong>.</p>\n<p>Use the <strong>provided patch cables</strong> to connect the pinpad to the switch.</p>\n<p>The switch must have <strong>3 cables connected</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 1:</strong> Existing CAT 5 from the biscuit jack under the register.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 2:</strong> Connect a new CAT 5 patch cable to the biscuit jack, with the other end connected to<strong>Port 2</strong>.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Port 3:</strong> CAT 5 cable from the pinpad.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mount the switch on the <strong>left side</strong>, with the<strong>link lights visible</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Verify the access codes and IP address before entering them</strong> to avoid issues with the pinpad.</p>\n<p>Pack the <strong>old pinpads only</strong> for return.<strong>Do not include the stands or old cables.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Please review the Pinpad Refresh Field Services Guide for the full scope of work and installation instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Clean up Area</strong></p>\n<p>Call IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.</p>\n<p>Check In Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Check Out Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Store Contact Name:</p>\n<p>Record the serial numbers of all installed pin pads</p>\n<p>Return Tracking #:</p>\n<p>Store Check Out Contact:</p>\n<p>Picture of Completed Work:</p>\n<p><strong>Close-Out Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check out on the Field Nation App</p>\n<p>Ensure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables</p>\n<p>Leave defective parts onsite</p>\n<p>Submit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.</p>","markdown":"**Summary of Work:**\n\nIW Technologies is looking for a technician to complete a pin pad replacement at a local retailer. The scope includes replacing the existing pin pads, installing the switch, configuring and testing the devices. Please record each pin pad serial number with its corresponding lane number. Pack the existing pin pads and Verifone cables in the original tamper-safe white packaging, and drop the box off at FedEx.\n\n**QTY of Lanes: 3**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID\n- Velcro\n- 1.25\" hole saw w/drill\n- Variety of Phillips screwdrivers\n- Loctite to use on the pin pad screws for the mount\n\n**Pre-Visit Instructions:**\n\nBe sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order\n\nConfirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\n**Onsite Tasks:**\n\nCheck in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198\n\nMount the new pinpad in the **same location as the old pinpad**.\n\nUse the **provided patch cables** to connect the pinpad to the switch.\n\nThe switch must have **3 cables connected**:\n\n- **Port 1:** Existing CAT 5 from the biscuit jack under the register.\n- **Port 2:** Connect a new CAT 5 patch cable to the biscuit jack, with the other end connected to**Port 2**.\n- **Port 3:** CAT 5 cable from the pinpad.\n\nMount the switch on the **left side**, with the**link lights visible**.\n\n**Verify the access codes and IP address before entering them** to avoid issues with the pinpad.\n\nPack the **old pinpads only** for return.**Do not include the stands or old cables.**\n\n- Please review the Pinpad Refresh Field Services Guide for the full scope of work and installation instructions.\n\n**Clean up Area**\n\nCall IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.\n\nCheck In Time: (local)\n\nCheck Out Time: (local)\n\nStore Contact Name:\n\nRecord the serial numbers of all installed pin pads\n\nReturn Tracking #:\n\nStore Check Out Contact:\n\nPicture of Completed Work:\n\n**Close-Out Tasks:**\n\nCheck out on the Field Nation App\n\nEnsure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables\n\nLeave defective parts onsite\n\nSubmit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T07:45","end":"2026-10-26T09:45"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":69.82511801233511},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791817141403}
{"job":{"id":20148616,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"WatchMeGrow","title":"WatchMeGrow - IP System - (2) New IP Camera Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:</strong> https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html</p><p><strong>Equipment Needed:</strong>&nbsp;RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6 Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter</span>, Multimeter, PLENUM Cat6 Cabling, Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit</p><p><strong>Description:&nbsp;</strong>Our client, a busy childcare center, would like to add&nbsp;(2) exterior IP cameras to their school. We will need you to run wire and install&nbsp;the cameras at this location. Cameras will be provided and available onsite. You will need to connect the camera to the server at the head end. WMG technical staff is on hand during this project to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will be required to call to check in upon arrival and call to check out before leaving.</p><p><strong>Project Budget:</strong> Below are the project budget numbers. It is imperative that all work to be completed under the scope of this budget. If the scope of work is going to require additional time and/or labor, please halt the project and call WatchMeGrow immediately to get approval. Additional billed labor is nearly impossible to get approved after the project is completed. The materials cost of cable and crimps are already factored into the wiring budget below. <strong>WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval.</strong></p><p><strong>Wiring:</strong></p><ul><li>2 Cat6 Wire Runs x $135 = $270</li></ul><p><strong>Labor:</strong></p><ul><li>2 hours x $75 = $150</li></ul><p><strong>Camera Location: </strong>to be installed in the parking lot</p><p>Note: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.</p><p><strong>Licensing and Permits:</strong> Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.</p><p><strong>Safety</strong>: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.</p><p>If you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.</p><p><strong>Photos:</strong> Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.</p><p><strong>Call to Sign In/Out:</strong> Please call <del>***** ********</del> to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.</p><p><strong>Sign Off:</strong> Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>!!IMPORTANT!!</strong></p><ul><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:** <https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html>\n\n**Equipment Needed:** RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6 Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter, Multimeter, PLENUM Cat6 Cabling, Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit\n\n**Description:** Our client, a busy childcare center, would like to add (2) exterior IP cameras to their school. We will need you to run wire and install the cameras at this location. Cameras will be provided and available onsite. You will need to connect the camera to the server at the head end. WMG technical staff is on hand during this project to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will be required to call to check in upon arrival and call to check out before leaving.\n\n**Project Budget:** Below are the project budget numbers. It is imperative that all work to be completed under the scope of this budget. If the scope of work is going to require additional time and/or labor, please halt the project and call WatchMeGrow immediately to get approval. Additional billed labor is nearly impossible to get approved after the project is completed. The materials cost of cable and crimps are already factored into the wiring budget below. **WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval.**\n\n**Wiring:**\n\n- 2 Cat6 Wire Runs x $135 = $270\n\n**Labor:**\n\n- 2 hours x $75 = $150\n\n**Camera Location:** to be installed in the parking lot\n\nNote: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.\n\n**Licensing and Permits:** Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.\n\n**Safety**: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.\n\nIf you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.\n\n**Photos:** Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.\n\n**Call to Sign In/Out:** Please call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.\n\n**Sign Off:** Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.\n\n**!!IMPORTANT!!**\n\n- **WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.**\n- **WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.**\n- **WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T09:00","end":"2026-10-19T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-19T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":420,"max":420},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":5.732287297048123},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00: