hat cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number. <br><br>9.If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready. <br><br>Checkout Requirement <br><br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line. <br><br>2.Confirm Activations has released you. <br><br>3.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables. <br><br>4.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket. <br><br>5.Check out on WorkMarket. <br><br> <br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket. <br><br> <br><br>Required Deliverables <br><br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout: <br><br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install. <br><br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block. <br><br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable. <br><br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet. <br><br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions. <br><br> <br><br> <br><br>Required Tools <br><br>•Laptop <br><br>•Smartphone with hotspot <br><br>•Tone generator and wand <br><br>•66/110 punch tool <br><br>•Butt set <br><br>       Infrared Temperature Gun  <br><br>•Electrician scissors <br><br>•Step ladder <br><br>•Flashlight/headlamp <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper <br><br>•Ethernet cable tester <br><br>•Impact drill / cordless drill <br><br>•Masonry bits <br><br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits <br><br>•Needle-nose pliers <br><br>•Label maker and label tape <br><br>•Cat3 or better cable <br><br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable <br><br>•Cross-connect wire <br><br>•Gel-crimp connectors <br><br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware <br><br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks <br><br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini <br><br>************************************************************************************* <br><br> <br><br>PM SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS GUIDELINES <br><br>Special Instructions <br><br>Install Location <br><br>Enter where the EPIK device should be installed, including MDF/IDF/telco room location, wall/rack/shelf mounting instructions, and access notes. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Cable Runs <br><br>Enter any required cable runs, cable type, distance, start/end points, and whether ladder, lift, ceiling access, or special tools are needed. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Network Information <br><br>Enter switch name, switch port, DHCP/static IP details, VLAN info, and customer network escalation contact. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>External Antenna <br><br>Enter whether an external antenna is required, where it should be mounted, and any cable path or photo requirements. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Special Testing <br><br>Enter any customer-specific testing that must be completed, including specific TNs, fax, alarm, elevator, hunt group, auto attendant, or other required testing. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Customer Contacts <br><br>Enter primary LCON, backup contact, customer IT contact, site manager, and escalation contacts. <br><br>________________________________________ <br><br>Vendor / Third-Party Info <br><br>Enter any VTM, customer tech, alarm vendor, elevator vendor, fax vendor, MSP, or other third-party contact information. \"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":51.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"