{"job":{"id":20153643,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Troubleshoot/ Network Equipment Install / NETOP-1158176 / MB865163","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>CPI1 circuit is hard down</p><p>Verify power and cabling to the circuit, reboot the ISP router/modem</p><p>Verify cabling between the ISP router/modem and the FortiSwitch</p><p><br></p><p><em>Review the </em><strong><em><u>“Confidential Section”</u></em></strong><em> listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including</em></p><ul><li>Circuit location and ID</li><li>Equipment details</li><li>Icon info</li><li>Bridge line #</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">Please bring a </span><span style=\"color: rgb(244, 5, 5);\">NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements</span></p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger &amp; TeamViewer Installed</li><li>Hot Spot or Internet Dongle</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger</li><li>Console Cable <span style=\"color: rgb(234, 5, 5);\">(Please see attached images for reference)</span></li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)</li></ul><p><em style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 14px;\">*Additional Tools Requested*</em></p><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Mandatory for all deliverables to be submitted while onsite in the parking lot to ensure site approval.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID required</li><li>Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>******* ******** ****** ************** *******</del></li><li>Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nCPI1 circuit is hard down\n\nVerify power and cabling to the circuit, reboot the ISP router/modem\n\nVerify cabling between the ISP router/modem and the FortiSwitch\n\n*Review the* ***“Confidential Section”*** *listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including*\n\n- Circuit location and ID\n- Equipment details\n- Icon info\n- Bridge line #\n\nPlease bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements\n\n**Tool Requirements:**\n\n- WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger & TeamViewer Installed\n- Hot Spot or Internet Dongle\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Cell Phone - with Charger\n- Console Cable (Please see attached images for reference)\n- Spare Patch Cables & Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)\n\n*\\*Additional Tools Requested\\**\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Mandatory for all deliverables to be submitted while onsite in the parking lot to ensure site approval.\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T20:00","end":"2026-10-14T24:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12.824105374483128},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062262-301 Prison Camp Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062271-3224 Old Hillsborough Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062284-600 S 3rd Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062291-2100 Eldon Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062301-1731 N NC 87-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062256-1714 W Davis Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062275-4751 NC 62-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062287-2229 Broadview Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062274-502 N Graham Hopedale Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062289-311 E Pine Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791887865259}
{"job":{"id":20153631,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Box Up Robot","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Work MUST be performed by the technician assigned. If Simbe discovers that another provider other than the assigned provider on Field Nation is performing the work, work order will not be approved for payment. Service companies are required to have a profile for each individual technician on Field Nation.</strong></p><p>Technician needed to box it up in original packaging.</p><ul><li>Take photos of the robot, note any damage</li></ul>","markdown":"**Work MUST be performed by the technician assigned. If Simbe discovers that another provider other than the assigned provider on Field Nation is performing the work, work order will not be approved for payment. Service companies are required to have a profile for each individual technician on Field Nation.**\n\nTechnician needed to box it up in original packaging.\n\n- Take photos of the robot, note any damage","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T09:00","end":"2026-10-14T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-14T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":48.61990680377151},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062262-301 Prison Camp Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062271-3224 Old Hillsborough Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062284-600 S 3rd Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062291-2100 Eldon Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062301-1731 N NC 87-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062256-1714 W Davis Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062275-4751 NC 62-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062287-2229 Broadview Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062274-502 N Graham Hopedale Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062289-311 E Pine Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791887871120}
{"job":{"id":20151112,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"RMA Replacement w/ Install and Training","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*** PLEASE REVIEW THE WORK ORDER IN FULL AS REQUIREMENTS AND PROTOCOL CAN CHANGE ***</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>EXPECTATIONS &amp; OBJECTIVE</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Approximately 1.25 - 2&nbsp;hours on-site in a residential setting, with a customer experiencing hearing loss.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Patience, empathy, and kindness&nbsp;are&nbsp;paramount to ensuring the customer is confident in using their phone before leaving the site!&nbsp;</li>\n<li>All&nbsp;steps and relevant information require review and verification by ClearCaptions' Support (listed in Contacts) before&nbsp;Work&nbsp;Order can be marked complete.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Trainer-tech to:&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong><u>Install&nbsp;a replacement phone and retrain the customer, following the standard below, and as provided under&nbsp;additional&nbsp;directions if/when unique troubleshooting steps are applicable.</u></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Confirm Phone Kit Contents:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ClearCaptions Phone (CCP)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Handset&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Phone Cord&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Power Adaptor&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Ethernet Cable&nbsp;</li>\n<li>RJ-11 Splitter&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><em>*If any parts&nbsp;missing, tech will need to call into support and request SPO. </em></strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Phone removal and set-up:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Disconnect and remove existing ClearCaptions phone&nbsp;and set aside&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Connect the replacement phone to the&nbsp;customers'&nbsp;network:&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Ethernet:&nbsp;Plug cable into router/modem and CCP.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Wi-Fi:&nbsp;Connect to the customer’s network using the Setup Wizard.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Reconnect phone to landline (if applicable)&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Install replacement phone:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Confirm successful registration&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Re-activate VoIP service (if applicable)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Confirmed activation success&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Test Dial Tone on all phones in home&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Confirm dial tone present&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Test Incoming Call&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Test Outgoing Call&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Confirm Captions are displaying properly&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Confirm phone is working as intended&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Retrain customer on phone usage following Installation Checklist&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Final Confirmation:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Customer confirms all services working properly&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Customer has no&nbsp;additional&nbsp;questions&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Contact Support at <del>************</del> to confirm successful service before closing the work order.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Tech to package up and return&nbsp;disconnected&nbsp;phone&nbsp;(if applicable)&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>﻿<u>Your (technician's)&nbsp;additional&nbsp;troubleshooting directions for this visit, beyond standards listed:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><em>Please assist customer with setting up replacement Clear Captions phone and make sure he can make and receive calls prior to leaving thank you. If you need any assistance during your visit reach out to our support at 866-868-8695.</em>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>SCHEDULING &amp; ARRIVAL</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ClearCaptions does not accept Technician requests to reschedule, as the hard start time has been coordinated with the end customer. If required for an unexpected reason,&nbsp;Technician&nbsp;must Report a Problem on the work&nbsp;order&nbsp;selecting “I Can’t Make My Assignment”.&nbsp;This enables ClearCaptions to&nbsp;attempt&nbsp;re-assignment without&nbsp;impacting&nbsp;our&nbsp;customer.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Tech must&nbsp;proceed&nbsp;to installation&nbsp;appointment&nbsp;as scheduled even if a customer does not respond to the required 24-hour advance courtesy call or their number is \"disconnected\"</em></strong><em>.</em> Customers are hard of hearing so may not realize you&nbsp;attempted&nbsp;to call until their caption phone and service is fully functional.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Check-in + Check-out must be within 1 mile of site.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Please arrive at&nbsp;start&nbsp;time of WO</em></strong>. Too early or too late can disrupt the customer and the ability to complete the WO. We will not approve requests to edit time logs.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Customer&nbsp;must be present for entirety of service&nbsp;visit&nbsp;(the registered user listed as the Location Contact in the Work Order).</em></strong></li>\n<li>If&nbsp;customer&nbsp;is not home and not reachable <strong><em>after 15 min of hard start time</em></strong><em>,</em> to confirm&nbsp;if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site, or&nbsp;to report&nbsp;that an installation cannot be completed in full for any reason call Support at <del>************</del>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>You must garner ClearCaptions' permission to leave site to allow for customer coordination, incomplete troubleshooting, and prevent rescheduling where reasonable.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Detailed information&nbsp;regarding&nbsp;contacting customers and Clear&nbsp;Captions’&nbsp;scheduling protocol can be found within Documents under “<em>Customer Contact and Installation Scheduling Policy</em>”.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUISITES</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The&nbsp;replacement&nbsp;phone kit&nbsp;will already&nbsp;be on site.<strong> <em>The kit does NOT include&nbsp;required&nbsp;tools listed</em>.</strong>&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>No agent other than the assigned provider is&nbsp;permitted&nbsp;to be onsite or complete service&nbsp;visit&nbsp;even if&nbsp;agent&nbsp;is part of a service company.</em></strong>&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Techs&nbsp;are prohibited from mounting the&nbsp;caption&nbsp;phone and/or creating any structural changes to a work site. This&nbsp;is including&nbsp;includes&nbsp;but&nbsp;is&nbsp;not limited to drilling holes and running&nbsp;cable.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Recording and/or&nbsp;retaining&nbsp;customer login credentials or personal information is&nbsp;strictly prohibited.</em></strong>&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>DRESS CODE</u>:</strong> Our requirement is that providers show up clean and presentable wearing&nbsp;business casual&nbsp;attire. Slacks or jeans (no holes/patches), closed-toed shoes, and a polo shirt, NO hats during installation.&nbsp;<strong> </strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PRE-SERVICE CALLOUTS</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><em>Review the required tutorials, linked in your Tasks.</em></strong> These are designed to help make you and this service visit successful!&nbsp;</li>\n<li>A full flip through \"<em>Phone Guide</em>\" for training the customer can be accessed here: <strong>https://rb.gy/ifegij</strong>.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Review the Service Repair work order in full and complete/confirm Prep tasks.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PAYMENTS</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><em>To be paid in full, Providers must</em></strong>: Complete all required job elements in entirety.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>All travel must be&nbsp;submitted&nbsp;in&nbsp;a counteroffer and be pre-approved prior to assignment. We do not honor travel pay&nbsp;submitted&nbsp;after Work Order acceptance and/or completion. Tools/cables used must have an uploaded receipt&nbsp;for&nbsp;pay out.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>At no point are&nbsp;Techs&nbsp;permitted&nbsp;to request payment from customers.</em></strong>&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Use of&nbsp;\"Discounts\" feature to adjust pay is prohibited.</em></strong> Please document any issues under “Report a Problem” from the Work Order for proper review and adjustments.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Detailed information regarding ClearCaptions’ payment structure can be found within Client Documents under&nbsp;\"<em>Work&nbsp;Order Payment Policy</em>\".&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>SERVICE ISSUES</u>:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call Support at <del>************</del> for issues preventing the&nbsp;servicing&nbsp;as described.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>VoIP Conversion guidance is available in the <em>Attached Files</em> link under Additional Information &gt; Client Documents.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong><em>Using your own or a customer's cellular 'hotspot' to connect a customer's phone to&nbsp;internet&nbsp;is&nbsp;strictly prohibited. Dedicated home internet service is&nbsp;required&nbsp;for caption service. Home internet is acceptable if delivered via a cellular network, and shared internet in assisted/group living facilities will suffice if/when connectivity speeds are sufficient.</em></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>COMPLIANCE &amp; REPORTING</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>This is NOT an emergency line. Do NOT call this number for installation help, scheduling issues, or general questions.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations,&nbsp;or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:</li>\n<li><del>*********</del><del>***</del>&nbsp;|&nbsp;Compliance@ClearCaptions.com</li>\n<li>&nbsp;All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator,&nbsp;or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website:&nbsp;https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\* PLEASE REVIEW THE WORK ORDER IN FULL AS REQUIREMENTS AND PROTOCOL CAN CHANGE \\*\\*\\***\n\n**EXPECTATIONS & OBJECTIVE:**\n\n- Approximately 1.25 - 2 hours on-site in a residential setting, with a customer experiencing hearing loss.\n- Patience, empathy, and kindness are paramount to ensuring the customer is confident in using their phone before leaving the site!\n- All steps and relevant information require review and verification by ClearCaptions' Support (listed in Contacts) before Work Order can be marked complete.\n- Trainer-tech to:\n\n**Install a replacement phone and retrain the customer, following the standard below, and as provided under additional directions if/when unique troubleshooting steps are applicable.**\n\n**Confirm Phone Kit Contents:**\n\n- ClearCaptions Phone (CCP)\n- Handset\n- Phone Cord\n- Power Adaptor\n- Ethernet Cable\n- RJ-11 Splitter\n\n***\\*If any parts missing, tech will need to call into support and request SPO.***\n\n**Phone removal and set-up:**\n\n1. Disconnect and remove existing ClearCaptions phone and set aside\n2. Connect the replacement phone to the customers' network:\n3. Ethernet: Plug cable into router/modem and CCP.\n4. Wi-Fi: Connect to the customer’s network using the Setup Wizard.\n5. Reconnect phone to landline (if applicable)\n\n**Install replacement phone:**\n\n1. Confirm successful registration\n2. Re-activate VoIP service (if applicable)\n3. Confirmed activation success\n4. Test Dial Tone on all phones in home\n5. Confirm dial tone present\n6. Test Incoming Call\n7. Test Outgoing Call\n8. Confirm Captions are displaying properly\n9. Confirm phone is working as intended\n10. Retrain customer on phone usage following Installation Checklist\n\n**Final Confirmation:**\n\n1. Customer confirms all services working properly\n2. Customer has no additional questions\n3. Contact Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm successful service before closing the work order.\n4. Tech to package up and return disconnected phone (if applicable)\n\n**﻿Your (technician's) additional troubleshooting directions for this visit, beyond standards listed:**\n\n*Please assist customer with setting up replacement Clear Captions phone and make sure he can make and receive calls prior to leaving thank you. If you need any assistance during your visit reach out to our support at 866-868-8695.*\n\n**SCHEDULING & ARRIVAL:**\n\n- ClearCaptions does not accept Technician requests to reschedule, as the hard start time has been coordinated with the end customer. If required for an unexpected reason, Technician must Report a Problem on the work order selecting “I Can’t Make My Assignment”. This enables ClearCaptions to attempt re-assignment without impacting our customer.\n- ***Tech must proceed to installation appointment as scheduled even if a customer does not respond to the required 24-hour advance courtesy call or their number is \"disconnected\"****.* Customers are hard of hearing so may not realize you attempted to call until their caption phone and service is fully functional.\n- Check-in + Check-out must be within 1 mile of site.\n- ***Please arrive at start time of WO***. Too early or too late can disrupt the customer and the ability to complete the WO. We will not approve requests to edit time logs.\n- ***Customer must be present for entirety of service visit (the registered user listed as the Location Contact in the Work Order).***\n- If customer is not home and not reachable ***after 15 min of hard start time****,* to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site, or to report that an installation cannot be completed in full for any reason call Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n- You must garner ClearCaptions' permission to leave site to allow for customer coordination, incomplete troubleshooting, and prevent rescheduling where reasonable.\n- Detailed information regarding contacting customers and Clear Captions’ scheduling protocol can be found within Documents under “*Customer Contact and Installation Scheduling Policy*”.\n\n**REQUISITES:**\n\n- The replacement phone kit will already be on site. ***The kit does NOT include required tools listed*.**\n- ***No agent other than the assigned provider is permitted to be onsite or complete service visit even if agent is part of a service company.***\n- Techs are prohibited from mounting the caption phone and/or creating any structural changes to a work site. This is including includes but is not limited to drilling holes and running cable.\n- ***Recording and/or retaining customer login credentials or personal information is strictly prohibited.***\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Our requirement is that providers show up clean and presentable wearing business casual attire. Slacks or jeans (no holes/patches), closed-toed shoes, and a polo shirt, NO hats during installation.\n\n**PRE-SERVICE CALLOUTS:**\n\n- ***Review the required tutorials, linked in your Tasks.*** These are designed to help make you and this service visit successful!\n- A full flip through \"*Phone Guide*\" for training the customer can be accessed here: **<https://rb.gy/ifegij>**.\n- Review the Service Repair work order in full and complete/confirm Prep tasks.\n\n**PAYMENTS:**\n\n- ***To be paid in full, Providers must***: Complete all required job elements in entirety.\n- All travel must be submitted in a counteroffer and be pre-approved prior to assignment. We do not honor travel pay submitted after Work Order acceptance and/or completion. Tools/cables used must have an uploaded receipt for pay out.\n- ***At no point are Techs permitted to request payment from customers.***\n- ***Use of \"Discounts\" feature to adjust pay is prohibited.*** Please document any issues under “Report a Problem” from the Work Order for proper review and adjustments.\n- Detailed information regarding ClearCaptions’ payment structure can be found within Client Documents under \"*Work Order Payment Policy*\".\n\n**SERVICE ISSUES:**\n\n- Call Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for issues preventing the servicing as described.\n- VoIP Conversion guidance is available in the *Attached Files* link under Additional Information > Client Documents.\n- ***Using your own or a customer's cellular 'hotspot' to connect a customer's phone to internet is strictly prohibited. Dedicated home internet service is required for caption service. Home internet is acceptable if delivered via a cellular network, and shared internet in assisted/group living facilities will suffice if/when connectivity speeds are sufficient.***\n\n**COMPLIANCE & REPORTING**\n\n**This is NOT an emergency line. Do NOT call this number for installation help, scheduling issues, or general questions.**\n\n- If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations, or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* | Compliance@ClearCaptions.com\n- All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator, or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website: <https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts>","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T08:00","end":"2026-10-16T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":43,"max":43},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":42.5,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":43.4249904133311},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $43 (countered: $60) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062262-301 Prison Camp Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062271-3224 Old Hillsborough Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start