{"job":{"id":20152928,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Remove old PCs / Install new PCs (3x) |Est: 2 Hrs| Drill, Velcro, Basic hand tools","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience&nbsp;installing desktop POS setups</li><li>Tech is required to swap out 3 old computers and install 3 new computers, confirm everything is functional.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 2 Hours</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</em></p><ul><li><em>﻿Drill</em></li><li><em>Impact Driver</em></li><li><em>Wire Cutters, strippers</em></li><li><em>Velcro</em></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">***(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>Pre-Site Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent <strong>Zenxeon</strong> while onsite</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>On-Site Tasks:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Take a picture before completing any work in each computer location.</li><li>Remove the old desktop underneath the counter. Along with keyboard and mouse. (New peripherals in the box)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Need to remove/install one counter at a time so that the workers have access to books throughout the process.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If there is any older credit card readers not being used, please remove those too (ie Verifone VX805)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please make sure you are installing the correct computer at each location (C1 for counter 1, O1 in the office, etc)</li><li><strong>Tech will also need to remove the old computer, mouse and keyboard in the managers office</strong>. Please confirm with manager onsite which computer is being removed before doing anything.</li><li>Leave any computer mounts attached to side of counter. Confirm they are secure and not crooked. New computer should fit into current mount.</li><li>It is important to manage cables accordingly while installing new computer.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please use <strong>Velcro ties </strong>for ease of use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Manage cables underneath and on top of the counter</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please leave some slack in the cables running to the monitor (for ease of movement)</li><li>Please confirm with support that we see all 3 new computers online</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ul><li>Upload pictures:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Before decommissioning</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">After installation</li><li>Call Zenxeon for assistance on testing these devices and to confirm deliverables</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Communication Directory:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with&nbsp;Zenxeon Support 916 312 3220 press 7</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;Dallis or Alex</li><li>IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact: Kim 916 312 3220 ext 117</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience installing desktop POS setups\n- Tech is required to swap out 3 old computers and install 3 new computers, confirm everything is functional.\n- Estimated duration will be 2 Hours\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- *﻿Drill*\n- *Impact Driver*\n- *Wire Cutters, strippers*\n- *Velcro*\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements:***\n\n- Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent **Zenxeon** while onsite\n\n***On-Site Tasks:***\n\n- Take a picture before completing any work in each computer location.\n- Remove the old desktop underneath the counter. Along with keyboard and mouse. (New peripherals in the box)\n- **Need to remove/install one counter at a time so that the workers have access to books throughout the process.**\n- **If there is any older credit card readers not being used, please remove those too (ie Verifone VX805)**\n- Please make sure you are installing the correct computer at each location (C1 for counter 1, O1 in the office, etc)\n- **Tech will also need to remove the old computer, mouse and keyboard in the managers office**. Please confirm with manager onsite which computer is being removed before doing anything.\n- Leave any computer mounts attached to side of counter. Confirm they are secure and not crooked. New computer should fit into current mount.\n- It is important to manage cables accordingly while installing new computer.\n- Please use **Velcro ties** for ease of use\n- Manage cables underneath and on top of the counter\n- Please leave some slack in the cables running to the monitor (for ease of movement)\n- Please confirm with support that we see all 3 new computers online\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Upload pictures:\n- Before decommissioning\n- After installation\n- Call Zenxeon for assistance on testing these devices and to confirm deliverables\n- Check-out of work order\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with Zenxeon Support 916 312 3220 press 7\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to Dallis or Alex\n- IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact: Kim 916 312 3220 ext 117\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00","end":"2026-10-14T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-14T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.514044932533205},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062262-301 Prison Camp Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062271-3224 Old Hillsborough Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062284-600 S 3rd Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062291-2100 Eldon Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062301-1731 N NC 87-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062256-1714 W Davis Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062275-4751 NC 62-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062287-2229 Broadview Drive-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062274-502 N Graham Hopedale Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062289-311 E Pine Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1791887975933}
{"job":{"id":20152734,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Revisit- Printer Install Tech with helper Government Issued ID (non-expired) Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>For all technical issues on site call&nbsp;1-972-581-9842</strong></p><p><strong>Conference ID: 485 568 415 #</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Scope:</u></em></strong>&nbsp;Installation of Lexmark device(s).</p><p>Please see printer model(s) listed in the custom field</p><p><strong>***Revisit- MX822 not onsite at original visit***</strong></p><p><strong><em>Firmware link-&nbsp;</em></strong>(Please see task list)</p><p>There are 3 Firmware files and one Auto Deploy Tool.</p><p>Please extract onto 2 USB thumb drives so that the following files are visible.&nbsp;</p><p>USB must be 2.0. DO NOT USE 3.0</p><p>MX632: MXTSN.250.217.fls</p><p>MX822 &amp; MX826: TGW.250.217.fls (same file for both devices)</p><p>ST9917: MSNSN.250.217.fls</p><p>TruistDeploy-2.0.0.fls</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Required Deliverables:&nbsp;</u></em></strong>(Also listed in task)</p><ul><li>Debrief form for each new printer: Both pages must be completely filled out and signed by the customer and technician.</li><li>Asset report for each new device: must have valid IP</li><li>Network report for each new device: must have valid IP</li><li>Asset report for each deinstall device: photo of asset tag can be used if needed</li><li>Asset tag form for each new device: must be signed by the customer</li><li>Training form: signed by the technician and the POC</li><li>Photo of installed equipment: Include scanner glass if present</li><li>Photo Front of device with device tag applied and CAC Reader installed (If applicable)</li><li>Photo of all deinstalled devices. Verify serial numbers listed in custom field</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:** **For all technical issues on site call 1-972-581-9842**\n\n**Conference ID: 485 568 415 #**\n\n***Scope:*** Installation of Lexmark device(s).\n\nPlease see printer model(s) listed in the custom field\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Revisit- MX822 not onsite at original visit\\*\\*\\***\n\n***Firmware link-*** (Please see task list)\n\nThere are 3 Firmware files and one Auto Deploy Tool.\n\nPlease extract onto 2 USB thumb drives so that the following files are visible.\n\nUSB must be 2.0. DO NOT USE 3.0\n\nMX632: MXTSN.250.217.fls\n\nMX822 & MX826: TGW.250.217.fls (same file for both devices)\n\nST9917: MSNSN.250.217.fls\n\nTruistDeploy-2.0.0.fls\n\n***Required Deliverables:*** (Also listed in task)\n\n- Debrief form for each new printer: Both pages must be completely filled out and signed by the customer and technician.\n- Asset report for each new device: must have valid IP\n- Network report for each new device: must have valid IP\n- Asset report for each deinstall device: photo of asset tag can be used if needed\n- Asset tag form for each new device: must be signed by the customer\n- Training form: signed by the technician and the POC\n- Photo of installed equipment: Include scanner glass if present\n- Photo Front of device with device tag applied and CAC Reader installed (If applicable)\n- Photo of all deinstalled devices. Verify serial numbers listed in custom field\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary & Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T09:00","end":"2026-10-15T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17.247615191817108},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062264-612 Apple Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062283-320 Ivey Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062272-5827 Church Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T19:00:00.000Z","s