{"job":{"id":20152111,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"RLDGM1082A - CHATHAM, NC - Model Home Network Re-config - Dispatch - Move Cradlepoint","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: black;\">Could you please schedule ExpoIT to visit this model and relocate the Cradlepoint and WAN Orbi to the closet where the Starlink equipment is installed? They should then connect the Cradlepoint directly to the Starlink connection.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">This approach will eliminate the cabling between the Starlink equipment and the media panel, simplifying the network setup and reducing potential points of failure. And the same time they are moving the Security camera to the Orbi as well.</span></p><p><strong>﻿<u>REFER TO DOCUMENTS IN THIS LINK:&nbsp;</u></strong><u><del>************************************</del></u><u>!</u></p><p><strong><u>This WO could consist of the following,</u></strong></p><ul><li>Swapping over network connection from cellular to ISP</li><li>Configuring the printer and helping user print</li><li>(AS SIMPLE AS PLUGGING ISP INTO WAN PORT ON CRADLEPOINT)</li><li>Need to make sure music is playing on the Sonos equipment. May require a Sonos restart.</li><li>Take pictures and screenshots of speed test</li><li>work with expoIT to ensure everything is up and function</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REFER TO ATTACHED MODEL CONNECTION DIAGRAM!</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>﻿</u>Sales Model Network Connection - 2024 06 03.pdf</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Photo Requirements </u><em><u>(updated April 2025)</u></em><u>:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Group photo showing the equipment in the main location (black box, Cradlepoint, Orbi router, etc)</li><li>Take photos of the equipment you are troubleshooting/repairing (including serial numbers and location of that equipment)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos of before and after issue resolution</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screenshots of error(s) if any</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screenshot(s) post resolution</li><li>If any equipments are being replaced, along with the details of the equipment capture the below</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Equipment in return box(es) – taped</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Label(s) on return box</li></ul>","markdown":"Could you please schedule ExpoIT to visit this model and relocate the Cradlepoint and WAN Orbi to the closet where the Starlink equipment is installed? They should then connect the Cradlepoint directly to the Starlink connection.\n\nThis approach will eliminate the cabling between the Starlink equipment and the media panel, simplifying the network setup and reducing potential points of failure. And the same time they are moving the Security camera to the Orbi as well.\n\n**﻿REFER TO DOCUMENTS IN THIS LINK:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*!\n\n**This WO could consist of the following,**\n\n- Swapping over network connection from cellular to ISP\n- Configuring the printer and helping user print\n- (AS SIMPLE AS PLUGGING ISP INTO WAN PORT ON CRADLEPOINT)\n- Need to make sure music is playing on the Sonos equipment. May require a Sonos restart.\n- Take pictures and screenshots of speed test\n- work with expoIT to ensure everything is up and function\n\n**REFER TO ATTACHED MODEL CONNECTION DIAGRAM!**\n\n**﻿Sales Model Network Connection - 2024 06 03.pdf**\n\n**Photo Requirements *(updated April 2025)*:**\n\n- Group photo showing the equipment in the main location (black box, Cradlepoint, Orbi router, etc)\n- Take photos of the equipment you are troubleshooting/repairing (including serial numbers and location of that equipment)\n- Photos of before and after issue resolution\n- Screenshots of error(s) if any\n- Screenshot(s) post resolution\n- If any equipments are being replaced, along with the details of the equipment capture the below\n- Equipment in return box(es) – taped\n- Label(s) on return box","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T10:00","end":"2026-10-16T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":27.937311312811776},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062264-612 Apple Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062283-320 Ivey Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062272-5827 Church Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-07T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062286-7718 Sylvan Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062255-720 Walker Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062266-609 Ray Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062281-1025 Trollinger Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062299-1307 S Church Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062262-301 Prison Camp Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062271-3224 Ol