{"job":{"id":20148247,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"HP LJ M725 - Device displays \"98.00.0C\" error. The error persists after power cycling.","description":{"html":"⁠Customer Reference:    --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- STAPLES TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n--- INSTRUCTIONS ---<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nPlease provide ETA for service<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTechnician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed.<br />\n(Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.)<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nFor any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nInitial notes: HP LJ M725 - Device displays &quot;98.00.0C&quot; error. The error persists after power cycling. <br />\n<br />\n<br />\nClean and Troubleshoot<br />\nPer Support:Need tech on site with laptop, crossover cable, current printer driver and a USB drive of 4GB or less with current printer firmware. Tech should print off a configuration page, remove all options (sheet feeders, duplexers,etc.) reseat formatter, dimm and eio devices, do nvram reset, load new firmware, update the driver if necessary, confirm printer configuration settings and have user test all features.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nA techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed.<br />\nhttps://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login <br />\ntechlink user name and password are the call number 1132488<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n**It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to**<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n**Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nGeneral Instructions for All Calls-<br />\nVerify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed.<br />\nConfirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts.<br />\nIf a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count.<br />\nDo not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead.<br />\nIf the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding.<br />\nAfter service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR.<br />\nIf facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n⁠","markdown":"⁠Customer Reference: --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- STAPLES TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS  \n  \n  \n\\--- INSTRUCTIONS ---  \n  \n  \nPlease provide ETA for service  \n  \n  \nTech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG.  \n  \n  \nTechnician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed.  \n(Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.)  \n  \n  \nFor any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2.  \n  \n  \nInitial notes: HP LJ M725 - Device displays \"98.00.0C\" error. The error persists after power cycling.   \n  \n  \nClean and Troubleshoot  \nPer Support:Need tech on site with laptop, crossover cable, current printer driver and a USB drive of 4GB or less with current printer firmware. Tech should print off a configuration page, remove all options (sheet feeders, duplexers,etc.) reseat formatter, dimm and eio devices, do nvram reset, load new firmware, update the driver if necessary, confirm printer configuration settings and have user test all features.  \n  \n  \nA techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed.  \n<https://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login>   \ntechlink user name and password are the call number 1132488  \n  \n  \n\\*\\*It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to\\*\\*  \n  \n  \n\\*\\*Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval.  \n  \n  \nGeneral Instructions for All Calls-  \nVerify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed.  \nConfirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts.  \nIf a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count.  \nDo not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead.  \nIf the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding.  \nAfter service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR.  \nIf facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.  \n  \n  \n⁠","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-12T08:00","end":"2026-10-13T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17.40009401059097},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked 