{"job":{"id":20145634,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"DISPATCH REQUEST - 261003-TR0024-S1- Kernersville, USA","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p>&nbsp;FE Need to replace Switch with the help of GNOC Engineer&nbsp;.</p><p><strong>Any Other Site Requirements for Engineer</strong></p><p>FE Need to carry Windows Laptop with extra LAN cables.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Important:</u></strong></p><p>Tech should have Webex or Blue jeans in his laptop, so he can provide remote access.</p><p><strong>Task Requirement:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>1- Faulty device needs to be carry with you after the task is completed</p><p>2- Customer will provide shipping label - the tech needs to drop off the device to the nearby courier place.</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Step by Step Instructions for the Field Engineer:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">1</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer assigned and dispatched to customer site and must arrive on site 15 minutes before the SLA/Request shown above</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">2</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer arrives at customer site and calls or emails the <del>*** </del>GOCC (service desk) to confirm they are on site</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">3</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer makes contact with the onsite contact</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">4</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer arrives to the faulty part and calls the technical contact number if this has been provided</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">5</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer verifies the job required to be carried out with the technical contact</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">6</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer performs the required work and will call the <del>********* </del>GOCC (service desk) if the engineer requires any technical assistance or guidance. They must also call in if there are any issues onsite meaning that they will be required onsite for longer than 2 hours. <del>********* </del>GOCC (service desk) is the first point of contact and not the customer.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">7</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer calls the <del>*********</del>GOCC (service desk) when he/she has finished the job onsite to confirm how the fault was resolved and request approval to leave site</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">8</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer completes the Site Visit Report provided by <del>*********</del>&nbsp;GOCC (service desk) and gets this signed by the onsite contact</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">9</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer to send the completed Site Visit Report back to the <del>***************</del>GOCC (service desk) within 48 hours of job completion</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">10</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125);\">Engineer MUST label all defective parts</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">ON-SITE ENGINEER REQUIREMENTS: The on-site engineer must have the following capabilities:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- English speaking plus local language</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Suitably skilled to be able to complete this task.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">TOOL REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Customer ID Badge (if required)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Mobile phone and charger</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Laptop and charger</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- TeamViewer installed on laptop</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Console cable (DB9)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- 2 x Cat5E Patch cables, 10 and 3 metre</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RH45-DB9 Female)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screw Driver.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Digital Camera</span></p><p><strong><del>**** *************** *** </del></strong></p><p><strong>Tools Requirement:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Customer ID Badge (if required)</span></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Mobile phone and charger</span></p><ul><li>Windows Laptop with WIFI Access with admin rights.</li></ul><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;TeamViewer, Cisco Webex, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Blue jeans, Installed on your Laptop.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Console cable (DB9)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li>Extra Ethernet Patch Cables (3 patch Cables 12 -15 ft. in length - Will be reimburse accordingly when it is used, Receipt must be shared)</li></ul><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RJ45-DB9 Female)</span></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screwdriver.</span></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: black;\">Digital Camera</span></p><ul><li>Terminal Server Emulator (Putty, Secure CRT) Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45</li><li>USB Drivers if using USB connection RS232.</li><li>Mobile Hotspot for tethering</li><li>VELCRO Straps for rack cable management/patch cords</li><li>USB Flash drive (At least 32 or above GB)</li><li>Screwdriver&nbsp;Set (Phillips Set &amp; Torx Set)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong> <u>Terms &amp; Conditions:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>﻿</u>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Please remain professional demeanor while on site. Do not engage in any conversation with local site contacts or any staff members unrelated to work.&nbsp;<strong>Keep all conversations strictly work-related.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Engineer must carry a valid ID for access; access won't be granted without it.</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not <strong>represent FIELDNATION</strong> on site unless specified, check with our support team for clarification.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Technician must stay onsite until task completion; </strong>leaving without<strong> Gaichu technical team's authorization </strong>results in<strong> no payment </strong>and task deemed<strong> Incomplete. IMPORTANT</strong></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong> </strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Share onsite <strong>Time IN</strong> and <strong>Time Out</strong> with the technical team before leaving.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rude behavior </strong>is not acceptable onsite and will lead to disciplinary action</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wear professional clothing for the task.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>All tools mentioned in the work order must be taken to the site; if any tools reported to be missing while you are onsite, and work affected because of it will result in no payment.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take all tools mentioned in the work order to the site; missing tools affecting work will result in no payment. IMPORTANT</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Share all expenses (Travel, Gas, Parking &amp; Toll) before accepting the Work Order. No additional expenses will be approved after the task. <strong>IMPORTANT</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Do not bring unauthorized persons onsite without written confirmation; non-compliance will result in unpaid Work Order and be seen as a security breach.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Share receipts for materials purchased or used onsite for reimbursement; payment won't be authorized without relevant receipts.</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Please take pictures before and after the execution of work.</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take <strong>Before</strong> and <strong>After</strong> pictures of the work execution.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect <strong>Console Cable</strong> <strong>or USB to DB9 Converter</strong> to laptop and share the <strong>Device Manager</strong> picture showing <strong>COM PORT</strong> before starting the task to confirm proper driver installation.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please see below the WhatsApp requirement for all future Field nation tasks:</p><p><strong>Please install WhatsApp application in your smart phone and send WhatsApp message containing FN WO if you need any technical assistance and when you are onsite then reach out to below contact persons:</strong></p><p><strong>Kiran Arshad:</strong>&nbsp;+92 330 5000523</p><p><strong>Mehreen Arshad:</strong>&nbsp;+92 330 5000522</p><p><strong>Kashan Ul Haq:</strong>&nbsp;+92 347 9859366&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please visit below links to install WhatsApp and to add WhatsApp contacts.</p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaRsRytz1NQ</p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65IHJAgXIyY&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>If you have any query regarding schedule or payment you need to reach out to below contact details:</strong></p><p><strong>Ammar Ibrahim +92 319 6241457</strong></p><p><strong>Safwan Sajjad: +92 336 5509218</strong></p><p><strong>Jawad Jami: +92 314 0916262</strong></p>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n FE Need to replace Switch with the help of GNOC Engineer .\n\n**Any Other Site Requirements for Engineer**\n\nFE Need to carry Windows Laptop with extra LAN cables.\n\n**Important:**\n\nTech should have Webex or Blue jeans in his laptop, so he can provide remote access.\n\n**Task Requirement:**\n\n1- Faulty device needs to be carry with you after the task is completed\n\n2- Customer will provide shipping label - the tech needs to drop off the device to the nearby courier place.\n\nStep by Step Instructions for the Field Engineer:\n\n1\n\nEngineer assigned and dispatched to customer site and must arrive on site 15 minutes before the SLA/Request shown above\n\n2\n\nEngineer arrives at customer site and calls or emails the \\*\\*\\* GOCC (service desk) to confirm they are on site\n\n3\n\nEngineer makes contact with the onsite contact\n\n4\n\nEngineer arrives to the faulty part and calls the technical contact number if this has been provided\n\n5\n\nEngineer verifies the job required to be carried out with the technical contact\n\n6\n\nEngineer performs the required work and will call the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* GOCC (service desk) if the engineer requires any technical assistance or guidance. They must also call in if there are any issues onsite meaning that they will be required onsite for longer than 2 hours. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* GOCC (service desk) is the first point of contact and not the customer.\n\n7\n\nEngineer calls the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*GOCC (service desk) when he/she has finished the job onsite to confirm how the fault was resolved and request approval to leave site\n\n8\n\nEngineer completes the Site Visit Report provided by \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* GOCC (service desk) and gets this signed by the onsite contact\n\n9\n\nEngineer to send the completed Site Visit Report back to the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*GOCC (service desk) within 48 hours of job completion\n\n10\n\nEngineer MUST label all defective parts\n\n**ON-SITE ENGINEER REQUIREMENTS: The on-site engineer must have the following capabilities:**\n\n\\- English speaking plus local language\n\n\\- Suitably skilled to be able to complete this task.\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n\\- Customer ID Badge (if required)\n\n\\- Mobile phone and charger\n\n\\- Laptop and charger\n\n\\- TeamViewer installed on laptop\n\n\\- Console cable (DB9)\n\n\\- 2 x Cat5E Patch cables, 10 and 3 metre\n\n\\- Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RH45-DB9 Female)\n\n\\- Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screw Driver.\n\n\\- Digital Camera\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\n\n**Tools Requirement:**\n\n· Customer ID Badge (if required)\n\n· Mobile phone and charger\n\n- Windows Laptop with WIFI Access with admin rights.\n\n· TeamViewer, Cisco Webex, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Blue jeans, Installed on your Laptop.\n\n· Console cable (DB9)\n\n- Extra Ethernet Patch Cables (3 patch Cables 12 -15 ft. in length - Will be reimburse accordingly when it is used, Receipt must be shared)\n\n· Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RJ45-DB9 Female)\n\n· Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screwdriver.\n\n· Digital Camera\n\n- Terminal Server Emulator (Putty, Secure CRT) Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45\n- USB Drivers if using USB connection RS232.\n- Mobile Hotspot for tethering\n- VELCRO Straps for rack cable management/patch cords\n- USB Flash drive (At least 32 or above GB)\n- Screwdriver Set (Phillips Set & Torx Set)\n\n **Terms & Conditions:**\n\n**﻿·** Please remain professional demeanor while on site. Do not engage in any conversation with local site contacts or any staff members unrelated to work. **Keep all conversations strictly work-related.**\n\n**· Engineer must carry a valid ID for access; access won't be granted without it.**\n\n· Do not **represent FIELDNATION** on site unless specified, check with our support team for clarification.\n\n**· Technician must stay onsite until task completion;** leaving without **Gaichu technical team's authorization** results in **no payment** and task deemed **Incomplete. IMPORTANT**\n\n · Share onsite **Time IN** and **Time Out** with the technical team before leaving.\n\n**· Rude behavior** is not acceptable onsite and will lead to disciplinary action\n\n**· Wear professional clothing for the task.**\n\n**·** All tools mentioned in the work order must be taken to the site; if any tools reported to be missing while you are onsite, and work affected because of it will result in no payment.\n\n**· Take all tools mentioned in the work order to the site; missing tools affecting work will result in no payment. IMPORTANT**\n\n**·** Share all expenses (Travel, Gas, Parking & Toll) before accepting the Work Order. No additional expenses will be approved after the task. **IMPORTANT**\n\n**·** Do not bring unauthorized persons onsite without written confirmation; non-compliance will result in unpaid Work Order and be seen as a security breach.\n\n**· Share receipts for materials purchased or used onsite for reimbursement; payment won't be authorized without relevant receipts.**\n\n· **Please take pictures before and after the execution of work.**\n\n· Take **Before** and **After** pictures of the work execution.\n\n· Connect **Console Cable** **or USB to DB9 Converter** to laptop and share the **Device Manager** picture showing **COM PORT** before starting the task to confirm proper driver installation.\n\n· Please see below the WhatsApp requirement for all future Field nation tasks:\n\n**Please install WhatsApp application in your smart phone and send WhatsApp message containing FN WO if you need any technical assistance and when you are onsite then reach out to below contact persons:**\n\n**Kiran Arshad:** +92 330 5000523\n\n**Mehreen Arshad:** +92 330 5000522\n\n**Kashan Ul Haq:** +92 347 9859366\n\nPlease visit below links to install WhatsApp and to add WhatsApp contacts.\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaRsRytz1NQ>\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65IHJAgXIyY&nbsp;>\n\n**If you 