{"job":{"id":20155328,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Install 3–5 PAX A35 payment devices","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technician will be installing approximately 3–5 PAX A35 payment devices at the assigned Wendy’s location. All PAX A35 devices, mounting brackets, cables, and required installation materials are expected to be onsite prior to arrival.</strong></p><p><strong>Estimated time:</strong> Up to 2 hours of combined travel and onsite labor are included in the standard service. Additional time may be billable if delays are caused by missing equipment, site-access issues, unavailable power/network connectivity, or other conditions outside the technician’s control.</p><p><strong>Technician requirements:</strong> Bring all standard tools necessary to mount and secure the PAX A35 devices. No procurement of equipment, structured cabling, electrical work, kiosk/register modification, POS programming, network remediation, or payment-system configuration is included in this scope.</p>1. Site Arrival &amp; Preparation<ul><li>Check in with the designated Wendy’s restaurant contact.</li><li>Confirm that all PAX A35 devices and required mounting hardware are onsite and accessible.</li><li>Locate the PAX A35 devices and applicable mounting brackets.</li><li>Confirm the existing kiosks/registers are ready to receive the devices.</li><li>Verify required power and network connections are available.</li><li>Identify the installation locations for each PAX A35.</li><li>Inspect the installation area and notify the support contact of any conditions that would prevent installation.</li></ul>2. PAX A35 Device Installation<ul><li>Install approximately 3–5 PAX A35 devices at the assigned location.</li><li>Mount each PAX A35 using the provided bracket.</li><li>Install devices on existing kiosks or at the applicable register/POS position.</li><li>Secure each device properly and ensure the mounting hardware is installed correctly.</li><li>Connect the applicable power and communication cables.</li><li>Keep cabling neat and secure as part of the physical installation.</li></ul>3. Device Startup &amp; Basic Validation<ul><li>Power on each installed PAX A35 device.</li><li>Allow each device to begin its standard startup/connectivity process.</li><li>Confirm each device is receiving power.</li><li>Verify each device is securely mounted.</li><li>Perform basic physical validation to confirm the device is beginning the expected connection/startup process.</li><li>Do <strong>not</strong> perform payment application configuration, merchant configuration, key injection, POS configuration, backend activation, or network configuration.</li></ul>4. Exceptions &amp; Escalation<ul><li>Notify the designated support contact of any issue preventing successful installation.</li><li>Document missing equipment, incorrect brackets, inaccessible equipment, unavailable power/network connectivity, or other site-readiness issues.</li><li>Document any conditions that differ from the provided scope.</li><li>Do not perform work outside the defined physical installation scope unless specifically authorized.</li></ul>5. Installation Closeout<ul><li>Confirm all devices included in the scheduled scope have been physically mounted, connected, and powered on.</li><li>Take a photo of each installed PAX A35 device.</li><li>Document the number of devices installed.</li><li>Document the installation status and any exceptions.</li><li>Add technician notes regarding any issues encountered onsite.</li><li>Submit all required installation photos and closeout documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Technician will be installing approximately 3–5 PAX A35 payment devices at the assigned Wendy’s location. All PAX A35 devices, mounting brackets, cables, and required installation materials are expected to be onsite prior to arrival.**\n\n**Estimated time:** Up to 2 hours of combined travel and onsite labor are included in the standard service. Additional time may be billable if delays are caused by missing equipment, site-access issues, unavailable power/network connectivity, or other conditions outside the technician’s control.\n\n**Technician requirements:** Bring all standard tools necessary to mount and secure the PAX A35 devices. No procurement of equipment, structured cabling, electrical work, kiosk/register modification, POS programming, network remediation, or payment-system configuration is included in this scope.\n\n1. Site Arrival & Preparation- Check in with the designated Wendy’s restaurant contact.\n- Confirm that all PAX A35 devices and required mounting hardware are onsite and accessible.\n- Locate the PAX A35 devices and applicable mounting brackets.\n- Confirm the existing kiosks/registers are ready to receive the devices.\n- Verify required power and network connections are available.\n- Identify the installation locations for each PAX A35.\n- Inspect the installation area and notify the support contact of any conditions that would prevent installation.\n\n2. PAX A35 Device Installation- Install approximately 3–5 PAX A35 devices at the assigned location.\n- Mount each PAX A35 using the provided bracket.\n- Install devices on existing kiosks or at the applicable register/POS position.\n- Secure each device properly and ensure the mounting hardware is installed correctly.\n- Connect the applicable power and communication cables.\n- Keep cabling neat and secure as part of the physical installation.\n\n3. Device Startup & Basic Validation- Power on each installed PAX A35 device.\n- Allow each device to begin its standard startup/connectivity process.\n- Confirm each device is receiving power.\n- Verify each device is securely mounted.\n- Perform basic physical validation to confirm the device is beginning the expected connection/startup process.\n- Do **not** perform payment application configuration, merchant configuration, key injection, POS configuration, backend activation, or network configuration.\n\n4. Exceptions & Escalation- Notify the designated support contact of any issue preventing successful installation.\n- Document missing equipment, incorrect brackets, inaccessible equipment, unavailable power/network connectivity, or other site-readiness issues.\n- Document any conditions that differ from the provided scope.\n- Do not perform work outside the defined physical installation scope unless specifically authorized.\n\n5. Installation Closeout- Confirm all devices included in the scheduled scope have been physically mounted, connected, and powered on.\n- Take a photo of each installed PAX A35 device.\n- Document the number of devices installed.\n- Document the installation status and any exceptions.\n- Add technician notes regarding any issues encountered onsite.\n- Submit all required installation photos and closeout documentation.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T02:00","end":"2026-10-19T04:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":48.48861749391414},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000