{"job":{"id":20155577,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Experienced Network Field Technician for UPS installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope Summary:</strong></p><p>2i-T requires an experienced <strong>Lead Field Technician</strong> to perform the <strong>installation of one (1) </strong><strong style=\"color: black;\">GXT5-6000MVRT4UXLN</strong> <strong>UPS</strong>, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification &amp; removal.</p><p>This is a <strong>Vertiv customer site</strong>, and the technician must represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> professionally while onsite. YOU <strong>MUST</strong> READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.</p><p><strong>SITE &amp; CONTACT INFORMATION</strong></p><p><strong>Remote Engineering Contact:</strong> Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068</p><p><strong>Customer:</strong> Vertiv (per dispatch details)</p><p><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES &amp; TASKS</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.</li><li>Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.</li><li>Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.</li><li>Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.</li><li>Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.</li><li>Install new Vertiv <strong style=\"color: black;\">GXT5-6000MVRT4UXLN</strong> UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.</li><li>Configure <strong>RDU101 network interface cards</strong> and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.</li><li><strong>Upgrade firmware</strong> using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.</li><li>Apply provided <strong>Vertiv service tags</strong> and verify unit labeling.</li><li>Capture and upload required photos:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Units powered and plugged into outlets</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit</li><li>Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.</li><li>Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.</li><li>Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; EQUIPMENT</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed</li><li>Multimeter</li><li>Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)</li><li>Mobile hotspot or tethering capability</li><li>Battery bank / phone charger</li><li>Standard hand tools, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Torx T-10 bit</li><li>PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area</li><li>Insulated tools recommended</li></ul><p><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></p><ul><li>Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).</li><li>Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.</li><li>Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.</li><li>Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.</li><li>Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.</li></ul><p><strong>ON-SITE CONDUCT &amp; COMMUNICATION</strong></p><ul><li>Represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.</li><li>Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.</li><li>Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.</li><li>Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.</li></ul><p><strong>DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.</li><li>Updated firmware confirmation.</li><li>Service tags applied.</li><li>Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.</li><li>Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.</li></ul><p><strong>NOTES</strong></p><ul><li>All work performed under Vertiv authorization.</li><li>Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.</li><li>Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.</li><li>Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.</li></ul><p><strong>MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING</strong></p><p>We published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.</p><p><strong>This training is free of charge</strong> (other than your time), takes roughly <strong>1.5 hours</strong>, and once completed:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you <em>cannot</em> normally obtain at no cost.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.</p><p>To be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.</p><p>If you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.</p><p>Looking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.</p>","markdown":"**Scope Summary:**\n\n2i-T requires an experienced **Lead Field Technician** to perform the **installation of one (1)** **GXT5-6000MVRT4UXLN** **UPS**, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification & removal.\n\nThis is a **Vertiv customer site**, and the technician must represent **Vertiv** professionally while onsite. YOU **MUST** READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.\n\n**SITE & CONTACT INFORMATION**\n\n**Remote Engineering Contact:** Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068\n\n**Customer:** Vertiv (per dispatch details)\n\n**RESPONSIBILITIES & TASKS**\n\n- Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.\n- Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.\n- Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.\n- Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.\n- Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.\n- Install new Vertiv **GXT5-6000MVRT4UXLN** UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.\n- Configure **RDU101 network interface cards** and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.\n- **Upgrade firmware** using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.\n- Apply provided **Vertiv service tags** and verify unit labeling.\n- Capture and upload required photos:\n- Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)\n- Units powered and plugged into outlets\n- Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit\n- Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.\n- Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.\n- Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS & EQUIPMENT**\n\n- Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed\n- Multimeter\n- Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)\n- Mobile hotspot or tethering capability\n- Battery bank / phone charger\n- Standard hand tools, including:\n- Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits\n- Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver\n- Torx T-10 bit\n- PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area\n- Insulated tools recommended\n\n**QUALIFICATIONS**\n\n- Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).\n- Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.\n- Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.\n- Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.\n- Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.\n\n**ON-SITE CONDUCT & COMMUNICATION**\n\n- Represent **Vertiv** while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.\n- Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.\n- Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.\n- Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.\n\n**DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.\n- Updated firmware confirmation.\n- Service tags applied.\n- Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.\n- Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.\n\n**NOTES**\n\n- All work performed under Vertiv authorization.\n- Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.\n- Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.\n- Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.\n\n**MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING**\n\nWe published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.\n\n**This training is free of charge** (other than your time), takes roughly **1.5 hours**, and once completed:\n\n· You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.\n\n· You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.\n\n· You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you *cannot* normally obtain at no cost.\n\n· We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.\n\nTo be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.\n\nIf you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.\n\nLooking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T16:00","end":"2026-10-19T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":145},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":65.9703193879613