{"job":{"id":20156076,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Troubleshoot / Replace / Install Wireless Access Point","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Check-in with C3IS Support 972-429-6659 opt. 1 when you arrive on site.</u></strong></p><p><strong>TECH MUST CONTACT SUPPORT BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE TO CONFIRM JOB COMPLETION OR WORK ORDER WILL NOT BE PAID. MUST BE ABLE TO DRIVE LIFT</strong></p><p><strong>======================================================================</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Subject </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">INC2081194</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Store 543 - Network: apvitamin-nc0543 Offline - INC2081194</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Full Description</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">AP Name: apvitamin-nc0543</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Switch/Port: as01-nc0543 / Port 46</span></p><p><br></p><p>Replacement AP being delivered 10/13</p><p>FedEx Tracking # 878389020986</p><p><br></p><p><strong>======================================================================</strong></p><ul><li>Unmount the AP and test the cable. (upload test results to work order).</li><li>If the cable passes, Plug the AP directly in to the switch and call Sprouts Support.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with support and let them know the cable has been certified.</li><li>If cable test fails, please re-terminate both ends of the cable and test again.</li><li>Confirm the MAC Address / Serial Number of the AP with Sprouts Support to confirm you are troubleshooting/replacing the correct AP. Must upload pics of serial number/MAC address. This is required if we are to RMA equipment.</li><li>If the AP doesn't power on when plugged directly into the switch, please attempt a factory reset by pressing and holding the reset button. This is required before we make an RMA attempt.</li><li>If the cable fails, re-terminate the device end and upload a picture of the removed end and re-test the cable.</li><li>If the cable fails again, call C3IS support.</li><li>If the cable passes, Plug the AP directly in to the switch and call Sprouts support.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with support and let them know the cable has been certified.</li><li>All exterior APs along with an AP in the coolers/freezers must have a drip loop and the penetration must be sealed with silicon. Picture attached of a WAP with a drip loop.</li><li>Cooler APs should have surface mount box and patch cable mounted above the cooler (picture attached)</li><li>Upload pictures of completed work and enter close out notes including the name of the Sprouts support technician.</li><li>Cameras, APs, and Speakers may require a lift. On-site staff will not be aware if there was a lift ordered or delivered. Please confirm with C3 if a lift has been ordered. C3 staff can locate the lift via GPS.</li></ul><p><strong>======================================================================</strong></p><p><strong>Support Contact is Sprouts Help Desk @ 480.385.2300 opt. 1&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Hard Starts:</strong> Work orders marked as a Hard Start are NOT flexible. You must arrive at the exact time listed.</p><p><strong>Time Windows:</strong> Generally flexible, but you must update your ETA in the app if your arrival time changes.</p><p><strong>No Ticket, No Pay:</strong> Each visit requires a separate work order. Techs appearing on-site without a corresponding ticket will not be paid.</p><p><strong>Lift Requirements:</strong> Many of our APs and cameras will require a lift to access. Must be able to drive a lift. If you accept the WO and can't complete the job because you can't drive the lift you won't be paid.</p><p><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> Additional fees added after acceptance will be denied.</p><p><strong>Closeout:</strong> All notes, photos, and hardware documentation must be uploaded before leaving the premises. See Confidential Section for specific requirements.</p>","markdown":"**Check-in with C3IS Support 972-429-6659 opt. 1 when you arrive on site.**\n\n**TECH MUST CONTACT SUPPORT BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE TO CONFIRM JOB COMPLETION OR WORK ORDER WILL NOT BE PAID. MUST BE ABLE TO DRIVE LIFT**\n\n**======================================================================**\n\nSubject **INC2081194**\n\nStore 543 - Network: apvitamin-nc0543 Offline - INC2081194\n\nFull Description\n\nAP Name: apvitamin-nc0543\n\nSwitch/Port: as01-nc0543 / Port 46\n\nReplacement AP being delivered 10/13\n\nFedEx Tracking # 878389020986\n\n**======================================================================**\n\n- Unmount the AP and test the cable. (upload test results to work order).\n- If the cable passes, Plug the AP directly in to the switch and call Sprouts Support.\n- Work with support and let them know the cable has been certified.\n- If cable test fails, please re-terminate both ends of the cable and test again.\n- Confirm the MAC Address / Serial Number of the AP with Sprouts Support to confirm you are troubleshooting/replacing the correct AP. Must upload pics of serial number/MAC address. This is required if we are to RMA equipment.\n- If the AP doesn't power on when plugged directly into the switch, please attempt a factory reset by pressing and holding the reset button. This is required before we make an RMA attempt.\n- If the cable fails, re-terminate the device end and upload a picture of the removed end and re-test the cable.\n- If the cable fails again, call C3IS support.\n- If the cable passes, Plug the AP directly in to the switch and call Sprouts support.\n- Work with support and let them know the cable has been certified.\n- All exterior APs along with an AP in the coolers/freezers must have a drip loop and the penetration must be sealed with silicon. Picture attached of a WAP with a drip loop.\n- Cooler APs should have surface mount box and patch cable mounted above the cooler (picture attached)\n- Upload pictures of completed work and enter close out notes including the name of the Sprouts support technician.\n- Cameras, APs, and Speakers may require a lift. On-site staff will not be aware if there was a lift ordered or delivered. Please confirm with C3 if a lift has been ordered. C3 staff can locate the lift via GPS.\n\n**======================================================================**\n\n**Support Contact is Sprouts Help Desk @ 480.385.2300 opt. 1**\n\n**Hard Starts:** Work orders marked as a Hard Start are NOT flexible. You must arrive at the exact time listed.\n\n**Time Windows:** Generally flexible, but you must update your ETA in the app if your arrival time changes.\n\n**No Ticket, No Pay:** Each visit requires a separate work order. Techs appearing on-site without a corresponding ticket will not be paid.\n\n**Lift Requirements:** Many of our APs and cameras will require a lift to access. Must be able to drive a lift. If you accept the WO and can't complete the job because you can't drive the lift you won't be paid.\n\n**Trip Charges:** Additional fees added after acceptance will be denied.\n\n**Closeout:** All notes, photos, and hardware documentation must be uploaded before leaving the premises. See Confidential Section for specific requirements.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T07:00","end":"2026-10-14T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":20.198946478239108},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 