{"job":{"id":20153962,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Insight | JPMC MaCD | Pin Pads","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.</strong></li><li><strong>By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page: </strong><u>https://fieldnation.com/work/insight</u></li><li><strong>Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details are available through the recruitment link.</strong></li></ul><p>Insight has been engaged by <del>**** </del>to assist with their Ad Hoc needs. Please make sure to read all standard instructions before accepting OR requesting this workorder.</p><p>Please see tracking before going to site or call <del>******* *************</del> Tracking is added to the ticket the morning of the job if applicable. Look in the shipments section.</p><p>**<strong>CHECK YOUR EMAIL THE MORNING OF REGARDING YOUR ASSIGNED WO **</strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p>Insight | JPMC MaCD | See Scope In Service Description<br/><br/>\"***BEFORE you mark yourself ONSITE It is essential that you call the Insight team - 1-800-215-8968. <br/><br/>Do not leave the site UNTIL you call the Insight team.  Contact Insight for instruction***<br/><br/>Date: 10/29/26<br/><br/>Scope - Follow the instructions in the process guide you will be emailed before the site visit. There is no tier 2 check in or out unless you need technical assistance. Please read entire guide paying special attention to the troubleshooting steps. If the steps do not work, please call the number for tier 2 support in the guide. <br/><br/>Confirm with the point of contact if there are any more pin pads that will be needed for customer facing workstations.<br/><br/>Unplug and prepare to ship any pin pads left in the drive through.<br/><br/>Pack old Pin Pads in the box the new equipment came in and ask the site to request a label from Banker's Assist, if there is not a return label in the box. <br/><br/>Number of Pin Pads and Wedges: 2<br/><br/>Tools Needed by Tech:  Phillips Screwdriver #2, Pair of Pliers, Alcohol Wipes, Ruler/Tape measure. No Power tools.<br/><br/>*Required Deliverables*<br/><br/>Upload pictures of:<br/><br/>Pin Pad ready screen and placement on each workstation<br/><br/>Close up picture of the Pin Pad serial number<br/><br/>Add the serial number to your Field Nation closing notes\"</p><p><strong><em><u>Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.</u></em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>UNLESS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.</li><li>&nbsp;Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.</li><li>&nbsp;If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.</li><li>&nbsp;Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.</li><li>Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE: Even if tracking shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><del>*</del><strong><u><del>*** ****</del> Work Order &amp; Support Procedures</u></strong></p><p>A Smartphone is required for all technicians. Unless directed by the <del>***** </del>help-desk at no time should a technician be taking pictures, video, or any recording while inside a <del>***** </del>branch. No laptops or tablets should ever be brought into a banking location. Nothing about the work performed, activities inside the branch, or reference to <del>***** </del>should ever be posted on any social media site.Business casual dress required, no tennis shoes or jeans. You will be turned away if you show up with unprofessional attire.</p><p>No smoking on location.</p><p>Please follow the below procedures, includes information on who to call to initiate support and what information must be documented in the ticket. All required information must be documented for a completed ticket.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>For escalation.</strong></p><p><strong><del>********** **** **** ****** ******* ******* **** ** ******** ** ******* **************</del></strong></p><p><del>* **** *** ******* ******** **** **</del><strong><del>******</del></strong><del>**************</del><strong><del>******</del></strong><del>** *** **** *** **** *** ******* ***** ** **** ************ ***** ** *** ******** *** ***** **** **** *** ******** ******* ** ** ** **** ****** ** **** ******* **** *** *** ******* ****** ** *** ************ ************</del></p><p><strong><u><del>**** *** ******* ***** **** ** ******* **** ****** ******* ******</del></u></strong></p><p><del>* ***** *** ******* ***** **** *** **** *** ****** ** ** ****** ***** **</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Before you leave the site:</u></strong></p><p><del>* ***** **** ********* ******* ** ********** *******</del></p><p><del>* ****** ******** ** *** ***** *********** *** ****** *** ******** ** *** ***********</del></p><p><del>* ****** **** *** **** ** ********* ** *** ********** ************ *** ******* * ********* **** *** **** ******** *** ******** ** ******* *********</del></p><p><strong><em><u>IMPORTANT:</u></em></strong><em>&nbsp;All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation.&nbsp;Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.</em></p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING</u></strong></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li><li>IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</li><li>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</li></ul><p><em>You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.</em></p>","markdown":"**Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work**\n\n- **We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.**\n- **By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page:** <https://fieldnation.com/work/insight>\n- **Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details are available through the recruitment link.**\n\nInsight has been engaged by \\*\\*\\*\\* to assist with their Ad Hoc needs. Please make sure to read all standard instructions before accepting OR requesting this workorder.\n\nPlease see tracking before going to site or call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Tracking is added to the ticket the morning of the job if applicable. Look in the shipments section.\n\n\\*\\***CHECK YOUR EMAIL THE MORNING OF REGARDING YOUR ASSIGNED WO \\*\\***\n\n**SCOPE:**\n\nInsight | JPMC MaCD | See Scope In Service Description  \n  \n\"\\*\\*\\*BEFORE you mark yourself ONSITE It is essential that you call the Insight team - 1-800-215-8968.   \n  \nDo not leave the site UNTIL you call the Insight team. Contact Insight for instruction\\*\\*\\*  \n  \nDate: 10/29/26  \n  \nScope - Follow the instructions in the process guide you will be emailed before the site visit. There is no tier 2 check in or out unless you need technical assistance. Please read entire guide paying special attention to the troubleshooting steps. If the steps do not work, please call the number for tier 2 support in the guide.   \n  \nConfirm with the point of contact if there are any more pin pads that will be needed for customer facing workstations.  \n  \nUnplug and prepare to ship any pin pads left in the drive through.  \n  \nPack old Pin Pads in the box the new equipment came in and ask the site to request a label from Banker's Assist, if there is not a return label in the box.   \n  \nNumber of Pin Pads and Wedges: 2  \n  \nTools Needed by Tech: Phillips Screwdriver #2, Pair of Pliers, Alcohol Wipes, Ruler/Tape measure. No Power tools.  \n  \n\\*Required Deliverables\\*  \n  \nUpload pictures of:  \n  \nPin Pad ready screen and placement on each workstation  \n  \nClose up picture of the Pin Pad serial number  \n  \nAdd the serial number to your Field Nation closing notes\"\n\n***Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.***\n\n **UNLESS:**\n\n- it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.\n- Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.\n- If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.\n- Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.\n- Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE: Even if tracking shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.**\n\n\\***\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* Work Order & Support Procedures**\n\nA Smartphone is required for all technicians. Unless directed by the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* help-desk at no time should a technician be taking pictures, video, or any recording while inside a \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* branch. No laptops or tablets should ever be brought into a banking location. Nothing about the work performed, activities inside the branch, or reference to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* should ever be posted on any social media site.Business casual dress required, no tennis shoes or jeans. You will be turned away if you show up with unprofessional attire.\n\nNo smoking on location.\n\nPlease follow the below procedures, includes information on who to call to initiate support and what information must be documented in the ticket. All required information must be documented for a completed ticket.\n\n**For escalation.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n**Before you leave the site:**\n\n\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n***IMPORTANT:*** *All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation. Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.*\n\n**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nTerms for Travel:\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\nTerms for Additional Time being Required:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n- IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n- Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00","end":"2026-10-29T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructur