{"job":{"id":20156938,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Assisting Networking Team Project   | SMARTHands | Device Testing  ONLY - UAT Device Testing Afterwards","description":{"html":"<p>Upon arriving and checking in with the Site Contact, the Field Technician must do the following:</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Safety First</u></strong></p><ul><li>Always wear protective eyewear, especially when going into a ceiling or dusty areas</li><li>Always wear protective Shoes</li><li>Always wear a yellow vest in warehouse or outdoor areas</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>General</u></strong></p><p>a-Take high-resolution pictures of the full front/back of the IT rack (Before/After) | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.</p><p>b. Collect and log the serial number of all CyberPower UPS | Take a good quality picture of the SN sticker/label of each UPS.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work 01</u></strong>: The Remote Networking team will do the upgrades; you will provide the additional SMARTHands support &amp; Testing of 10 - 15 devices in the center. It's called Center User Acceptance Testing (UAT)</p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Smart Hands Assistance</span></p><p><span style=\"color: inherit;\">1-Take hi-resolution of Area of Concern prior to any new runs/repair/troubleshooting | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.</span></p><ol><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">MDF Room | I&amp;T Rack: 1x Smart Hands Assist to Plasma Network &amp; Masergy Teams.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: inherit;\">Test connectivity. UAT required.</span></li></ol><p><br></p><p>Any and ALL Corresponding ports to the above New Cable Runs &amp;/or Cable Trace /WALL-JACKS on the switch must PASS: Continuity/PoE/Flash Test.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Provided Documentation (s) / Instruction (s</u>)</strong>:</p><p>Floor plan (See attachment)</p><p>Technician Tools List Requirements &amp; STD Color Code Patch Cable (See attachment)</p><p>CSL I&amp;T Rack Power Mapping Standard (See attachment)</p><p>CSL I&amp;T Rack | Equipment Install Location Standard (See attachment)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Completion</u></strong></p><p>Center User Test Document is completed&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Technician Tools Checklist</u></strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>Cable/Port Tester w/PoE Functions</p><p>Console Cable | Already Configured/Setup on laptop</p><p>MS Teams is installed and ready for use</p><p>Laptop with Windows OS with updates installed. | Dual NIC (Wi-Fi &amp; Ethernet) <strong>Required</strong></p><p>Cross-over network patch cables - Minimum 5ft</p><p>Labeling Machine (Portable)&nbsp;</p><p>CAT6E Cable Spool (Slim-Run | (Preferred)&nbsp;</p><p>Patch Cables Color: Orange / Red / Grey / Purple / Blue / White / Yellow / Black / Green</p><p><br></p><p><u>First and Last 6 ports of every switch in the 9300 stacks are reserved for CSL network team access ONLY!&nbsp;</u></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>**Only use this color code for patching from patch-panel to switch**</u></strong>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"Upon arriving and checking in with the Site Contact, the Field Technician must do the following:\n\n**Safety First**\n\n- Always wear protective eyewear, especially when going into a ceiling or dusty areas\n- Always wear protective Shoes\n- Always wear a yellow vest in warehouse or outdoor areas\n\n **General**\n\na-Take high-resolution pictures of the full front/back of the IT rack (Before/After) | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.\n\nb. Collect and log the serial number of all CyberPower UPS | Take a good quality picture of the SN sticker/label of each UPS.\n\n**Scope of Work 01**: The Remote Networking team will do the upgrades; you will provide the additional SMARTHands support & Testing of 10 - 15 devices in the center. It's called Center User Acceptance Testing (UAT)\n\nSmart Hands Assistance\n\n1-Take hi-resolution of Area of Concern prior to any new runs/repair/troubleshooting | This is a requirement and must be completed to move on to the next step.\n\n1. MDF Room | I&T Rack: 1x Smart Hands Assist to Plasma Network & Masergy Teams.\n2. Test connectivity. UAT required.\n\nAny and ALL Corresponding ports to the above New Cable Runs &/or Cable Trace /WALL-JACKS on the switch must PASS: Continuity/PoE/Flash Test.\n\n**Provided Documentation (s) / Instruction (s)**:\n\nFloor plan (See attachment)\n\nTechnician Tools List Requirements & STD Color Code Patch Cable (See attachment)\n\nCSL I&T Rack Power Mapping Standard (See attachment)\n\nCSL I&T Rack | Equipment Install Location Standard (See attachment)\n\n**Completion**\n\nCenter User Test Document is completed\n\n**Required Technician Tools Checklist**:\n\nCable/Port Tester w/PoE Functions\n\nConsole Cable | Already Configured/Setup on laptop\n\nMS Teams is installed and ready for use\n\nLaptop with Windows OS with updates installed. | Dual NIC (Wi-Fi & Ethernet) **Required**\n\nCross-over network patch cables - Minimum 5ft\n\nLabeling Machine (Portable)\n\nCAT6E Cable Spool (Slim-Run | (Preferred)\n\nPatch Cables Color: Orange / Red / Grey / Purple / Blue / White / Yellow / Black / Green\n\nFirst and Last 6 ports of every switch in the 9300 stacks are reserved for CSL network team access ONLY!\n\n**\\*\\*Only use this color code for patching from patch-panel to switch\\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T19:45","end":"2026-10-15T21:45"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.824105374483128},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","end":