{"job":{"id":20157245,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"ARK Compact | Automated Return Kiosk Installation & Config ","description":{"html":"<p>This WO is to install a New Amazon Return Kiosk at an Amazon Returns Location.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Unit credentials:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>kiosk_username:</strong> SHYOUNGSVILLEUS1HWY</li><li><strong>kiosk_pwd:</strong> SHEETZ27596</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>MUST CALL WO Manager TO CHECK IN AND CHECK OUT</strong></p><p>Main Kiosk Support Line: Mon – Fri: 6:00am – 6:00pm MST</p><p><strong>(303) 661-1664</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></p><p>You may need to depalletize and move the Kiosk to the desired location.</p><p><strong><u>KIOSK Weighs 225lbs</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Dolly/ Hand Truck (Can use sites if available)</li><li>Standard Tool Set (At least a Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver, preferably multiple sizes and lengths)</li><li>Nut driver set (At least an 11/32\" &amp; 3/8\")</li><li>T-15 Torx Bit</li><li>Mini USB Cable</li><li>Compressed Air / Canned Air</li><li>A to B USB Cable (Std Printer Cable)</li><li>Electronic Safety Wipes/Soft Cloth</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation Attached:</strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Compact_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf</p><p>- This guide is the installation guide to follow and guide you through the installation steps.</p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<strong>20211215_ARK@WFM Associate Training Manual_v2</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-This guide is for training and get you familiar with the kiosk and application.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><ol><li>Once on site, call WO Manager to check in.</li><li>Meet with onsite POC to locate the kiosk.</li><li>Open the kiosk and inspect for any damages.</li><li>Follow the attached installation guide (<strong>Compact_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf</strong>).</li><li>Make sure power is connected and the unit is powered on.</li><li>Carefully load the label roll into the printer and center the sensor if not already aligned with the indicator.</li><li>Call <strong>KIOSK Support</strong> to confirm the unit is online, checking in, and properly configured.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Network:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>WIFI SSID:</strong> AmzKiosk</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>WIFI PW:</strong>3XNHdLa!kQlVRYq</li><li>Do not leave the site unless released by our <strong>KIOSK Support Team</strong> or unless a new return date has been agreed upon if any issues arise.</li></ol>","markdown":"This WO is to install a New Amazon Return Kiosk at an Amazon Returns Location.\n\n**Unit credentials:**\n\n- **kiosk\\_username:** SHYOUNGSVILLEUS1HWY\n- **kiosk\\_pwd:** SHEETZ27596\n\n**MUST CALL WO Manager TO CHECK IN AND CHECK OUT**\n\nMain Kiosk Support Line: Mon – Fri: 6:00am – 6:00pm MST\n\n**(303) 661-1664**\n\n**Special Instructions:**\n\nYou may need to depalletize and move the Kiosk to the desired location.\n\n**KIOSK Weighs 225lbs**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Dolly/ Hand Truck (Can use sites if available)\n- Standard Tool Set (At least a Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver, preferably multiple sizes and lengths)\n- Nut driver set (At least an 11/32\" & 3/8\")\n- T-15 Torx Bit\n- Mini USB Cable\n- Compressed Air / Canned Air\n- A to B USB Cable (Std Printer Cable)\n- Electronic Safety Wipes/Soft Cloth\n\n**Documentation Attached:**\n\n**1.** Compact\\_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf\n\n\\- This guide is the installation guide to follow and guide you through the installation steps.\n\n**2.**  **20211215\\_ARK@WFM Associate Training Manual\\_v2**\n\n -This guide is for training and get you familiar with the kiosk and application.\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n1. Once on site, call WO Manager to check in.\n2. Meet with onsite POC to locate the kiosk.\n3. Open the kiosk and inspect for any damages.\n4. Follow the attached installation guide (**Compact\\_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf**).\n5. Make sure power is connected and the unit is powered on.\n6. Carefully load the label roll into the printer and center the sensor if not already aligned with the indicator.\n7. Call **KIOSK Support** to confirm the unit is online, checking in, and properly configured.\n8. **Network:**\n9. **WIFI SSID:** AmzKiosk\n10. **WIFI PW:**3XNHdLa!kQlVRYq\n11. Do not leave the site unless released by our **KIOSK Support Team** or unless a new return date has been agreed upon if any issues arise.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T13:00","end":"2026-10-13T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-13T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":27.074055998145674},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062260-1712 Vaughn Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062270-2630 Buckingham Road-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068252-BJs Club 151- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068292-BJs Club 215- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 IT SUPPORT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Incident #269224 - ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T22:00:00.00