{"job":{"id":20157415,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"PFCB9927 | EC1000 to EC2000 Controller Upgrade","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong>Seeking a technician with<strong>proven EMS (Energy Management Systems) experience to</strong> <strong>upgrade EC1K to EC2K. Move over all communication wiring and power cabling. Apply network settings. Verify with Support all peripherals are online and the EC2K serial number is updated and configured on GEM platform.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site/Customer: PF Changs</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Professional work attire; closed-toe shoes and a safety vest may be required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Materials/Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Multimeter</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cable toner/tester</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wire strippers, termination tools</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Phone with photo/email capability</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic HVAC tools</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Materials shipping to site:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>(Qty 1) EC-2000-21</strong></p>\n<p><strong>(Qty 1) 02-10005-1</strong></p>\n<p><strong>(Qty 1) PS-24V-ENC-BP</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Schedule Confirmation:</strong> You must confirm the scheduled date and time frame with the project manager before arriving on-site to ensure Support Staff availability.</li>\n<li><strong>Review FULL SOW.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Review the training video attached to the client documents section of the WO.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reference Case:</strong> Keep Case #<strong><del>********</del></strong> available for all communications.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:EC1000 to EC2000 Controller Upgrade</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician dispatch to upgrade EC1K to EC2K. Move over all communication wiring and power cabling. Apply network settings. Verify with Support all peripherals are online and the EC2K serial number is updated and configured on GEM platform.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>*</strong> Power for EMS controller is listed on Panel k1b, Breaker 32.</p>\n<p><strong>**</strong> Network connection is on Switch 2 Port 29</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Check-In Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact GridPoint Support upon arrival:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*****</del></strong><del>************</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*****</del></strong><del>************</del></li>\n<li>Technician must check in and check out with GridPoint.</li>\n<li>Reference <strong>Case #<del>********</del></strong><del>*</del></li>\n<li>Contact GridPoint Support prior to leaving the site to review findings and final device status.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Controller Upgrade</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace the existing <strong>EC1000 controller</strong> with the new <strong>EC2000 controller</strong>.</li>\n<li>All equipment is currently communicating. This visit is an equipment upgrade to newer hardware.</li>\n<li>Transfer all wiring and network connections to the replacement controller.</li>\n<li>Enter the network information provided by GridPoint Support. PFCB is on <strong>DHCP</strong>.</li>\n<li>Verify the EC2000 controller successfully connects to the GridPoint platform.</li>\n<li>Confirm all existing peripherals reconnect following the upgrade.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Documentation Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide photos of:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Existing EC1000 controller</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">New EC2000 controller</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Before and after power supply if replaced</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Controller wiring and network connections</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final completed installation</li>\n<li>Submit all photos to GridPoint before leaving the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Material Return</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Old equipment does not need to be returned.</li>\n<li>Unused equipment should be returned</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Required Tools &amp; Materials</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Multimeter</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cable toner/tester</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wire strippers, termination tools</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Phone with photo/email capability</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic HVAC tools</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Communication Directory:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>GridPoint Support:</strong> Please <del>**** ************ ** **** ************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counteroffer when requesting the work in order to get approved.</li>\n<li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by the WO Manager.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Count &amp; NTE Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The vendor must determine <strong>before dispatch whether</strong> <strong>two technicians</strong> are required to complete the work.</li>\n<li>If two technicians are needed, the vendor <strong>must contact GridPoint for approval</strong> prior to dispatch, as this will result in an <strong>NTE increase</strong>.</li>\n<li>If GridPoint did not request more than one technician and no approval was received, <strong>GridPoint will not accept charges</strong> for the second technician.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Repair Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The technician is <strong>not permitted to repair any RTUs</strong>.</li>\n<li>GridPoint is <strong>not responsible for repairs</strong> to the customer’s HVAC system.</li>\n<li>The technician may <strong>advise the site manager</strong> of any HVAC issues needing repair, but <strong>GridPoint cannot authorize or approve</strong> those repairs through this dispatch.</li>\n<li>GridPoint <strong>will not accept or pay</strong> for any repair charges that were not explicitly approved.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**Seeking a technician with**proven EMS (Energy Management Systems) experience to** **upgrade EC1K to EC2K. Move over all communication wiring and power cabling. Apply network settings. Verify with Support all peripherals are online and the EC2K serial number is updated and configured on GEM platform.**\n\n**Site/Customer: PF Changs**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Professional work attire; closed-toe shoes and a safety vest may be required.\n\n**Materials/Tools Required:**\n\n· Multimeter\n\n· Cable toner/tester\n\n· CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire\n\n· Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver\n\n· Wire strippers, termination tools\n\n· Phone with photo/email capability\n\n· Basic HVAC tools\n\n**Materials shipping to site:**\n\n**(Qty 1) EC-2000-21**\n\n**(Qty 1) 02-10005-1**\n\n**(Qty 1) PS-24V-ENC-BP**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Schedule Confirmation:** You must confirm the scheduled date and time frame with the project manager before arriving on-site to ensure Support Staff availability.\n- **Review FULL SOW.**\n- **Review the training video attached to the client documents section of the WO.**\n- **Reference Case:** Keep Case #**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** available for all communications.\n\n**Scope of Work:EC1000 to EC2000 Controller Upgrade**\n\nTechnician dispatch to upgrade EC1K to EC2K. Move over all communication wiring and power cabling. Apply network settings. Verify with Support all peripherals are online and the EC2K serial number is updated and configured on GEM platform.\n\n**\\*** Power for EMS controller is listed on Panel k1b, Breaker 32.\n\n**\\*\\*** Network connection is on Switch 2 Port 29\n\n**Check-In Requirements**\n\n- Contact GridPoint Support upon arrival:\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technician must check in and check out with GridPoint.\n- Reference **Case #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\n- Contact GridPoint Support prior to leaving the site to review findings and final device status.\n\n**Controller Upgrade**\n\n- Replace the existing **EC1000 controller** with the new **EC2000 controller**.\n- All equipment is currently communicating. This visit is an equipment upgrade to newer hardware.\n- Transfer all wiring and network connections to the replacement controller.\n- Enter the network information provided by GridPoint Support. PFCB is on **DHCP**.\n- Verify the EC2000 controller successfully connects to the GridPoint platform.\n- Confirm all existing peripherals reconnect following the upgrade.\n\n**Documentation Requirements**\n\n- Provide photos of:\n- Existing EC1000 controller\n- New EC2000 controller\n- Before and after power supply if replaced\n- Controller wiring and network connections\n- Final completed installation\n- Submit all photos to GridPoint before leaving the site.\n\n**Material Return**\n\n- Old equipment does not need to be returned.\n- Unused equipment should be returned\n\n**Technician Required Tools & Materials**\n\n· Multimeter\n\n· Cable toner/tester\n\n· CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire\n\n· Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver\n\n· Wire strippers, termination tools\n\n· Phone with photo/email capability\n\n· Basic HVAC tools\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- **GridPoint Support:** Please \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counteroffer when requesting the work in order to get approved.\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by the WO Manager.\n\n**Technician Count & NTE Requirements**\n\n- The vendor must determine **before dispatch whether** **two technicians** are required to complete the work.\n- If two technicians are needed, the vendor **must contact GridPoint for approval** prior to dispatch, as this will result in an **NTE increase**.\n- If GridPoint did not request more than one technician and no approval was received, **GridPoint will not accept charges** for the second technician.\n\n**Repair Limitations**\n\n- The technician is **not permitted to repair any RTUs**.\n- GridPoint is **not responsible for repairs** to the customer’s HVAC system.\n- The technician may **advise the site manager** of any HVAC issues needing repair, but **GridPoint cannot authorize or approve** those repairs through this dispatch.\n- GridPoint **will not accept or pay** for any repair charges that were not explicitly approved.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T11:00","end":"2026-10-16T15:00","latestStart":"2026-10-16T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":21.694274612211906},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":75,"baseAmount":300,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":40,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T22:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":420,"mode":"hours"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham R