{"job":{"id":"3484286170","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance***","description":"\"***DEMARC EXTENSION LIKELY NEEDED FROM CARRIER (IF VERIZON OR FRONTIER) ONT WITHIN ELECTRICAL ROOM TO BURLINGTON'S IT ROOM/CABINET, PLEASE BE PREPARED WITH TECHS AND LIFT TO COMPLETE WORK***<br><br>***GRANITE CORE BRIDGE, GRANITE ACCESS ACTIVATIONS BRIDGE, CIRCUIT DETAILS, EQUIPMENT DETAILS POSTED IN SOW BELOW***<br><br>Requesting assistance to:<br><br>1) Call into Granite Core Team Bridge to confirm arrival<br>2) Locate new Granite-provided broadband and or/ DIA service<br>3) Extend new service to Burlington’s network rack/cabinet (if needed)<br>4) Test/validate new service<br>5) With Access Activations assistance, confirm with carrier that modem/router onsite is set to IP Passthrough/Bridge modem<br>6) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) modem and/or FlexEdge router to new EdgebootPro equipment for power in accordance to port mapping guide listed below.<br>7) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) and EdgebootPro to existing Burlington-provided Fortinet firewall ethernet ports in accordance to port mapping guide listed below<br>8) Once complete, request Granite Field Service technician to contact Burlington’s Managed Service Provider (HCL) to perform health check on applicable Fortinet firewall ports new equipment is now connected to.<br>9) Locate the existing Cradlepoint LTE Router<br>10) Document the Cradlepoint LTE Router location in close out notes<br>11) Using provided SIM card (will be shipped in separate envelope and held in the manager’s office), insert into the spare SIM 2 slot on the Cradlepoint<br><br>***NETWORK DIAGRAM ATTACHED AS REFERENCED***<br><br>***ONCE STEPS 1-7 ARE COMPLETE, PLEASE CONTACT BURLINGTON’S MANAGED SERVIE PROVIDE (HCL) @ TBD***<br><br>***TECHNICIAN MUST CALL INTO GRANITE ACCESS ACTIVATIONS TEAM. REP WILL THEN MERGE ACCUATIVE INTO CALL FOR A SIGN OFF CODE***<br><br>***JOB NOT COMPLETE UNTIL ALL STEPS ARE PERFORMED***<br><br>***NETWORK CUTOVER TO TAKE PLACE AT LATER DATE***<br><br>***ALL DIA SERVICES FOR BURLINGTON INCLUDES AN EPIKE EDGE/FLEXEDGE DEVICE REGARDLESS WHETHER ON OR OFF-NET. EPIK EDGE/FLEXEDGE DEVICE WILL COME IN SAME PACKAGE AS EDGEBOOT***<br><br>New service details are below:\"<br>Granite Core Bridge:Bridge: 929-229-2436, Passcode:688838204#<br>Granite Activation:877-855-1146 Option 1 (BB), Option 2 (DIA)<br>Activations Ticket #7017261<br>HCL NOC Phone Number:TBD<br>WAN Details:<br>Type:Cable<br>ISP:Spectrum<br>Bandwidth:1G/50<br>Circuit ID:<br>Demarc:<br>IP:Dynamic<br>GW:Dynamic<br>Subnet:Dynamic<br>DNS1:Dynamic<br>DNS2:Dynamic<br>EdgebootPro Serial #:2034261760<br>Edgeboot FedEx/UPS (DIA ORDER ONLY, PLEASE DISREGARD FOR BROADBAND PRODUCTS):1Z7X569X0103663697<br>Equipment FedEx/UPS (DIA ORDER ONLY, PLEASE DISREGARD FOR BROADBAND PRODUCTS):-<br><br>\"AC/Ethernet Port Mapping Guide:<br><br>Edgeboot AC Ports:<br><br>Port 1: DIA FlexEdge (WHERE APPLICABLE)<br>Port 2: Broadband Modem<br>Port 3: None<br>Port4: None<br><br>Edgeboot/New Circuit Ethernet Cross Connect:<br>New DIA Circuit: FortiGate Port 2 (WHERE APPLICABLE)<br>New Broadband Circuit: FortiGate Port 3<br>Edgeboot Port 0: FortiGate Port 5<br>Edgeboot Port 1: FortiGate Port 4<br>Edgeboot Console Port: FortiGate Console Port (via provided console cable included with EdgebootPro)\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":27.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":50,"payStructure":null},"reason":"PAYMENT_INSUFFICIENT","rejectDetails":"Rate $50/hr is below base rate $65/hr"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-1