{"job":{"id":20157167,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Google Nest Wi-fi Pro Nest Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p><em>* Requesting provider must be the one who performs service. If you need to contact WO manager leading up to or during WO, </em><strong><em>DO NOT use FN messaging or text message</em></strong><em>; call them at the T# provided to you at time of assignment. Failure to do so will result in 20% reduction in pay.</em></p><p><em>* If provider does not/will not check in within 15 mins of the scheduled time, call client first to give them ETA then call WO manager to provide ETA. If not done, we reserve right to reduce WO pay. If the provider needs to reschedule, it's provider's responsibility to call the client and reschedule.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>------<u> Service Description </u>------</strong></p><p>The client has a Google Nest Wi-fi Pro nest system. They are using one point as router. They have 5 points: 2 are about 5 years old and 3 are about 2 months old. They have Spectrum ISP. They are getting slow speed, connectivity challenges, lagged performance and needs it sorted out or resolved. The provider will be responsible for getting the/a home network set up for the client so that it's satisfactory for their use. See below re add'l pay after 1st visit/2 hours.</p><p><strong>Important</strong>: The client you service will see your closing notes and your check-in/check-out time. It must be reflective of the time/work on-site. If the provider needs to return for additional work/installation/etc or if time will go over estimated time to complete the work, additional pay will be added to this WO at $50/hr, the provider must call buyer at 2-hr mark, and the provider responsible for showing client what part(s) to buy, where/how, and returning to complete the work/replace parts. A second WO will not be created. Receipts/invoices required from provider for reimbursement. By requesting this work order you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this Work Order, for a minimum period of 15-business days</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual clean/fresh presentable clothing. No holes in socks. No coffee-stained clothing.</li><li>Do not smoke/vape just prior to on site appointment.</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Present Identification immediately at entry</li><li>Place protective shoe covers on foot ware or remove shoes <em>(NEVER walk on floor surfaces with wet and/or dirty shoes).&nbsp;Take off shoe covers and replace if the tech must leave the home or walk in unfinished areas of home and then going back on finished surfaces.</em></li><li>Discuss with the homeowner the work to be done what what will take place</li><li>Ensure area where work to be done is fit, given the nature of the work, and explain any issues you could see arising to client prior to start</li><li>Discuss any potential damage, cosmetic or otherwise that may occur as a result of work being done</li><li><em>Place any toolbox or materials onto a clean drop cloth</em></li><li>Final clean-up of job site</li><li>Review you work/solution with the client upon completion and provide training for installed products</li><li>Have the client digitally sign the service sign-off form to acknowledge service completion</li><li>Notify the client how to reach out to Nerds On Site in case of further questions</li><li>Complete the notes with details of the work done/steps taken, and mark complete.</li></ol><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables to Receive Payment</strong></p><ul><li>Client signature</li><li>Client's email address</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process</strong></p><ul><li>DO NOT discuss pricing, billing, etc. with the end client.</li><li>If issues arise while on-site, <u>call</u> the WO manager.</li><li>Do not remove client devices from client's property.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Services Policy</strong></p><p>These services may be included in this work order, and the pricing on your work order will be adjusted to match the requested services. These are available to the homeowner for an additional fee:</p><ul><li>Additional hours and expenses (material, travel, etc.) must be pre-approved by work order manage by calling them immediately, before the additional work is performed. Additional pay is priced at $50/hr, but must be pre-approved by WO manager.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>This Non-Disclosure Agreement (\"Agreement\") is made between Nerds On Site (\"Company\") and the technician (\"Technician\") (collectively referred to as \"Parties\") on the day the technician (\"Technician\") confirms this work order..</strong></p><p><br></p><p>1. Purpose</p><p>The Parties hereby agree to enter into this Agreement to protect the Company's confidential information and maintain the integrity of the client relationship. The Technician shall not engage in self-promotion or work directly with the Company's clients during or for 12 months after completing the work order. The Technician is expected to exclusively represent the Company during the work order duration.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Confidential Information</p><p>During the work order, the Technician may have access to confidential and proprietary information belonging to the Company, including but not limited to, client lists, client data, trade secrets, business strategies, financial information, software, and other proprietary information (collectively referred to as \"Confidential Information\").</p><p><br></p><p>3. Non-Disclosure and Non-Competition</p><p>a) The Technician agrees to maintain the confidentiality of all Confidential Information received during the work order. The Technician shall not disclose, distribute, or otherwise make the Confidential Information available to any third party without the Company's prior written consent.</p><p>b) The Technician shall not engage in any form of self-promotion, solicit business, or provide services to the Company's clients, directly or indirectly, during or following 12 months following the completion of the work order.</p><p><br></p><p>4. Client Communication</p><p>a) Any inquiries or requests for future work from the client during or after the work order should be directed solely to the Company.</p><p>b) The Technician shall immediately notify the Company of any such questions or requests and will not engage in any talks or negotiations with the client without the Company's express written consent.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Return of Confidential Information</p><p>Upon completion of the work order or termination of this Agreement, the Technician shall promptly return all Confidential Information, including any copies, notes, or materials, to the Company.</p><p><br></p><p>6. Remedies</p><p>The Technician acknowledges that any violation of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm to the Company. In addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, the Company shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief to prevent or curtail any actual or threatened breach of this Agreement by the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p>7. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</p><p>This Agreement shall be governed by and construed under the laws of <strong>[Jurisdiction]</strong>. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of <strong>[Jurisdiction]</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>8. Entire Agreement</p><p>This Agreement is the entire understanding between the Parties about the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, and agreements, whether oral or written.</p><p><br></p><p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have executed this Non-Disclosure Agreement as of the date first above written.</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Nerds On Site</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Technician's Name</p><p><br></p><p>___________________________</p><p>Date</p>","markdown":"*\\* Requesting provider must be the one who performs service. If you need to contact WO manager leading up to or during WO,* ***DO NOT use FN messaging or text message****; call them at the T# provided to you at time of assignment. Failure to do so will result in 20% reduction in pay.*\n\n*\\* If provider does not/will not check in within 15 mins of the scheduled time, call client first to give them ETA then call WO manager to provide ETA. If not done, we reserve right to reduce WO pay. If the provider needs to reschedule, it's provider's responsibility to call the client and reschedule.*\n\n**------ Service Description ------**\n\nThe client has a Google Nest Wi-fi Pro nest system. They are using one point as router. They have 5 points: 2 are about 5 years old and 3 are about 2 months old. They have Spectrum ISP. They are getting slow speed, connectivity challenges, lagged performance and needs it sorted out or resolved. The provider will be responsible for getting the/a home network set up for the client so that it's satisfactory for their use. See below re add'l pay after 1st visit/2 hours.\n\n**Important**: The client you service will see your closing notes and your check-in/check-out time. It must be reflective of the time/work on-site. If the provider needs to return for additional work/installation/etc or if time will go over estimated time to complete the work, additional pay will be added to this WO at $50/hr, the provider must call buyer at 2-hr mark, and the provider responsible for showing client what part(s) to buy, where/how, and returning to complete the work/replace parts. A second WO will not be created. Receipts/invoices required from provider for reimbursement. By requesting this work order you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this Work Order, for a minimum period of 15-business days\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual clean/fresh presentable clothing. No holes in socks. No coffee-stained clothing.\n- Do not smoke/vape just prior to on site appointment.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Present Identification immediately at entry\n2. Place protective shoe covers on foot ware or remove shoes *(NEVER walk on floor surfaces with wet and/or dirty shoes). Take off shoe covers and replace if the tech must leave the home or walk in unfinished areas of home and then going back on finished surfaces.*\n3. Discuss with the homeowner the work to be done what what will take place\n4. Ensure area where work to be done is fit, given the nature of the work, and explain any issues you could see arising to client prior to start\n5. Discuss any potential damage, cosmetic or otherwise that may occur as a result of work being done\n6. *Place any toolbox or materials onto a clean drop cloth*\n7. Final clean-up of job site\n8. Review you work/solution with the client upon completion and provide training for installed products\n9. Have the client digitally sign the service sign-off form to acknowledge service completion\n10. Notify the client how to reach out to Nerds On Site in case of further questions\n11. Complete the notes with details of the work done/steps taken, and mark complete.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables to Receive Payment**\n\n- Client signature\n- Client's email address\n\n**Escalation Process**\n\n- DO NOT discuss pricing, billing, etc. with the end client.\n- If issues arise while on-site, call the WO manager.\n- Do not remove client devices from client's property.\n\n**Additional Services Policy**\n\nThese services may be included in this work order, and the pricing on your work order will be adjusted to match the requested services. These are available to the homeowner for an additional fee:\n\n- Additional hours and expenses (material, travel, etc.) must be pre-approved by work order manage by calling them immediately, before the additional work is performed. Additional pay is priced at $50/hr, but must be pre-approved by WO manager.\n\n**This Non-Disclosure Agreement (\"Agreement\") is made between Nerds On Site (\"Company\") and the technician (\"Technician\") (collectively referred to as \"Parties\") on the day the technician (\"Technician\") confirms this work order..**\n\n1\\. Purpose\n\nThe Parties hereby agree to enter into this Agreement to protect the Company's confidential information and maintain the integrity of the client relationship. The Technician shall not engage in self-promotion or work directly with the Company's clients during or for 12 months after completing the work order. The Technician is expected to exclusively represent the Company during the work order duration.\n\n2\\. Confidential Information\n\nDuring the work order, the Technician may have access to confidential and proprietary information belonging to the Company, including but not limited to, client lists, client data, trade secrets, business strategies, financial information, software, and other proprietary information (collectively referred to as \"Confidential Information\").\n\n3\\. Non-Disclosure and Non-Competition\n\na) The Technician agrees to maintain the confidentiality of all Confidential Information received during the work order. The Technician shall not disclose, distribute, or otherwise make the Confidential Information available to any third party without the Company's prior written consent.\n\nb) The Technician shall not engage in any form of self-promotion, solicit business, or provide services to the Company's clients, directly or indirectly, during or following 12 months following the completion of the work order.\n\n4\\. Client Communication\n\na) Any inquiries or requests for future work from the client during or after the work order should be directed solely to the Company.\n\nb) The Technician shall immediately notify the Company of any such questions or requests and will not engage in any talks or negotiations with the client without the Company's express written consent.\n\n5\\. Return of Confidential Information\n\nUpon completion of the work order or termination of this Agreement, the Technician shall promptly return all Confidential Information, including any copies, notes, or materials, to the Company.\n\n6\\. Remedies\n\nThe Technician acknowledges that any violation of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm to the Company. In addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, the Company shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief to prevent or curtail any actual or threatened breach of this Agreement by the Technician.\n\n7\\. Governing Law and Jurisdiction\n\nThis Agreement shall be governed by and construed under the laws of **\\[Jurisdiction\\]**. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of **\\[Jurisdiction\\]**.\n\n8\\. Entire Agreement\n\nThis Agreement is the entire understanding between the Parties about the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, and agreements, whether oral or written.\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have executed this Non-Disclosure Agreement as of the date first above written.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nNerds On Site\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nTechnician's Name\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nDate","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T14:00","end":"2026-10-14T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":8.927719161896894},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is belo