{"job":{"id":20157136,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"LEAD Technician | Overnight Store Remodeling - Network/Cabling/POS (Full 8+ Hours Onsite)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong><em>(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p>\n<p>Remaining Scope:</p>\n<p>1.Rewire 6x Access points to the MDF.</p>\n<p>-Rewire the 6 access points that are plugged into ports 20-25 on switch H2 in the Assistant managers office (toning as necessary to identify which APs these are). Punch into main patch panels and patch into H1-H2 ports 20-25.</p>\n<p>2. Locate H2 and H3 switch in Cash office. Validate there are no more devices showing activity lights on the ports. If you see any you will need to tone them and get new lines run for those devices.</p>\n<p>-Move H2 to MDF and box up H3 to hand to manager to return to corporate. Once switch is moved to the MDF, reconnect to network by patching H2 port 49 to H1 port 50.</p>\n<p>Cash office IDF Rack Removal</p>\n<p>- Uninstall IDF rack mounting hardware and patch panel. Dispose of these and pull old cabling high into the ceiling and cut, making sure none of the cables are in use Switch</p>\n<p>- REQ1492469</p>\n<p>Cash Office Switch Move</p>\n<p>3. Install Learning Center computers / TV</p>\n<p>Security Code: 862384</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Seeking Lead<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;<strong>Over Multiple</strong>&nbsp;<strong>NIGHTs</strong>. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;responsible&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li>\n<li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li>\n<li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li>\n<li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li>\n<li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li>\n<li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li>\n<li>Technicians&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;read the&nbsp;<u>entire work order and all provided documentation</u>&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the<del>***</del> umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li>\n<li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li>\n<li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li>\n<li><strong><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR<del>***</del> REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li>\n<li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li>\n<li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Government Issued ID</li>\n<li><strong>Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li>\n<li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li>\n<li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li>\n<li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li>\n<li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li>\n<li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li>\n<li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong>READ &amp; REVIEW</strong>&nbsp;all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del> Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li>\n<li><strong><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li>\n<li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li>\n<li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li>\n<li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the Remote Support Team Bridge Line details -&nbsp;</strong>If you were not provided with one, please escalate to Essintial</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li>\n<li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call &amp; Check-In with the <del>***</del> RTC Remote Technician Team via the provided Bridge Line</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with <del>***</del> Remote RTC Team while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Perform a Walkthrough with MOD - refer to the install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li>\n<li>Perform Inventory - refer to install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li>\n<li>Work with Remote Bridge Line to determine if Site is ready to begin work for the night or if the night’s work needs aborted.</li>\n<li>Continue to work with / provide updates to the Remote Bridge Line, closure to the end of the night you may be required to provide more frequent updates.</li>\n<li>Some nights and/or mornings you will be working with the General Contractor Onsite and Store MOD to obtain/provide updates and/or complete specific task.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li>\n<li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At Frontline Completion and Overall Store Remodel Completion]:</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li>\n<li><strong>Check-Out with <del>***</del> Remote RTC Team via Bridge Line</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li>\n<li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li>\n<li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>***</del> Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li>\n<li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li>\n<li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:***(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining Scope:\n\n1.Rewire 6x Access points to the MDF.\n\n-Rewire the 6 access points that are plugged into ports 20-25 on switch H2 in the Assistant managers office (toning as necessary to identify which APs these are). Punch into main patch panels and patch into H1-H2 ports 20-25.\n\n2\\. Locate H2 and H3 switch in Cash office. Validate there are no more devices showing activity lights on the ports. If you see any you will need to tone them and get new lines run for those devices.\n\n-Move H2 to MDF and box up H3 to hand to manager to return to corporate. Once switch is moved to the MDF, reconnect to network by patching H2 port 49 to H1 port 50.\n\nCash office IDF Rack Removal\n\n\\- Uninstall IDF rack mounting hardware and patch panel. Dispose of these and pull old cabling high into the ceiling and cut, making sure none of the cables are in use Switch\n\n\\- REQ1492469\n\nCash Office Switch Move\n\n3\\. Install Learning Center computers / TV\n\nSecurity Code: 862384\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking Lead Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.\n\n- Lead Tech is responsible for reviewing and referring to ALL provided Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation \\[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC & STORE SPECIFIC Documentation\\] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.\n- Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** join and work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** review Nightly Scope of Work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** at the beginning of each **NIGHT**. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.\n- **Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Store Completion Deliverables \\[Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel\\]:**\n- FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE \\[ FRONTLINE COMPLETION & FULL STORE COMPLETION\\]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the **\\*\\*\\* REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.** \\[If deliverable session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.\\]\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the\\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR\\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* - Tool & Material List Document** **Link** (download to view full document): <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Estimated Duration: Multiple Days** estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n***Important Site Information / Requirements:***\n\n- You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n **Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.** Please **READ & REVIEW** all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **General Project Specific & STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link \\[VERY IMPORTANT\\]****:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\_Install Guides** **Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):** <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ>\n- **\\*\\*\\* Remodel - Tool & Material List** **Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8>\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1** **Link**: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial**\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- **Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site**\n- **Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n- **Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the Remote Support Team Bridge Line details -** If you were not provided with one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -** Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR & provide the **SECURITY CODE to gain access**\n- **Call & Check-In with the \\*\\*\\* RTC Remote Technician Team via the provided Bridge Line**\n\n**ONSITE: Work with \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team while onsite & refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation.**\n\n- Perform a Walkthrough with MOD - refer to the install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process\n- Perform Inventory - refer to install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process\n- Work with Remote Bridge Line to determine if Site is ready to begin work for the night or if the night’s work needs aborted.\n- Continue to work with / provide updates to the Remote Bridge Line, closure to the end of the night you may be required to provide more frequent updates.\n- Some nights and/or mornings you will be working with the General Contractor Onsite and Store MOD to obtain/provide updates and/or complete specific task.\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- **Complete Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Store Completion Deliverables \\[Not Nightly but At Frontline Completion and Overall Store Remodel Completion\\]:**\n- FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE \\[ FRONTLINE COMPLETION & FULL STORE COMPLETION\\]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the **\\*\\*\\* REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.** \\[If deliverable session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.\\]\n- **Check-Out with \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team via Bridge Line**\n- **Check-Out** with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC\n- **Call** - Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line\n- All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-18T20:15","end":"2026-10-18T30:15"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":500},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":43.9113826