{"job":{"id":20159000,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Tech for Site Survey & Discovery -1505","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Summary:</u></strong> Technician to complete a Site Survey &amp; Discovery assessment for future wireless, network infrastructure, and structured cabling upgrades</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Review survey documentation</li><li>Bring camera-enabled device and documentation tools.</li><li>Confirm ETA <strong><u>BEFORE heading</u></strong> to site</li></ul><p><strong>﻿** Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation **</strong></p><p><strong><u>Once Onsite:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Call / Text WO manager upon arrival -- Provide work order number</li><li>Locate and introduce yourself to the onsite contact</li><li>Perform an onsite physical survey of all designated areas within the facility</li><li>Validate available floorplans, facility drawings, evacuation maps, and site documentation against actual site conditions</li><li>Identify and document wall construction types including drywall, concrete block, concrete walls, metal barriers, glass walls, paint booths, storage areas, and other RF-impacting structures</li><li>Measure and map out each wall height, width and length note it on the floor plan as well in closing notes.</li><li>Confirm with the work order manager to go over each wall type and information</li></ol><p><strong><u>Tools:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Camera</li><li>laptop/tablet</li><li>tape measure</li><li>flashlight</li><li>standard hand tools</li><li>wheel tape and a laser/digital measuring</li></ol><p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Please call/text work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual is required. No T-shirts, logos, or tennis shoes are allowed (work boots are acceptable).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be paid:</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li>Completed site assessment forms documenting facility conditions, infrastructure observations, installation constraints</li><li>Floor Plan with AP placement</li><li>Photos and video documentation of site conditions, network infrastructure, cabling pathways, work areas, and installation locations.</li><li>Site notes</li></ol><p><strong>****Any delays on site must be added to closeout notes***</strong></p><p><strong>***Please ensure to check in and out with technical support via call AND with work order manager via TEXT, both are mandatory. Or if you need any clarification***</strong></p><p><strong><u>Stipulations and Penalties:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Unprepared penalty--50% of labor--A technician that has to reschedule because he/she left tools/ materials needed that was clearly listed on the Work order or reasonably would be required to complete the described task in the service description will forfeit 50% of earnings</li><li>Incomplete Work Order---60% of labor--If a work order is incomplete due to the fault of the provider and a revisit is refused the work order is subject to a 60% penalty</li><li>Late Penalty--10% of labor--Late fee of 10% earnings will be applied to any tech that is more than 30 mins late without prior notice</li><li><strong>Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation</strong></li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Summary:** Technician to complete a Site Survey & Discovery assessment for future wireless, network infrastructure, and structured cabling upgrades\n\n**Pre-Site Instructions:**\n\n- Review survey documentation\n- Bring camera-enabled device and documentation tools.\n- Confirm ETA **BEFORE heading** to site\n\n**﻿\\*\\* Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation \\*\\***\n\n**Once Onsite:**\n\n1. Call / Text WO manager upon arrival -- Provide work order number\n2. Locate and introduce yourself to the onsite contact\n3. Perform an onsite physical survey of all designated areas within the facility\n4. Validate available floorplans, facility drawings, evacuation maps, and site documentation against actual site conditions\n5. Identify and document wall construction types including drywall, concrete block, concrete walls, metal barriers, glass walls, paint booths, storage areas, and other RF-impacting structures\n6. Measure and map out each wall height, width and length note it on the floor plan as well in closing notes.\n7. Confirm with the work order manager to go over each wall type and information\n\n**Tools:**\n\n1. Camera\n2. laptop/tablet\n3. tape measure\n4. flashlight\n5. standard hand tools\n6. wheel tape and a laser/digital measuring\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- Please call/text work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite\n\n**Dress Code**\n\n- Business casual is required. No T-shirts, logos, or tennis shoes are allowed (work boots are acceptable).\n\n**Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n1. Completed site assessment forms documenting facility conditions, infrastructure observations, installation constraints\n2. Floor Plan with AP placement\n3. Photos and video documentation of site conditions, network infrastructure, cabling pathways, work areas, and installation locations.\n4. Site notes\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*Any delays on site must be added to closeout notes\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please ensure to check in and out with technical support via call AND with work order manager via TEXT, both are mandatory. Or if you need any clarification\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Stipulations and Penalties:**\n\n- Unprepared penalty--50% of labor--A technician that has to reschedule because he/she left tools/ materials needed that was clearly listed on the Work order or reasonably would be required to complete the described task in the service description will forfeit 50% of earnings\n- Incomplete Work Order---60% of labor--If a work order is incomplete due to the fault of the provider and a revisit is refused the work order is subject to a 60% penalty\n- Late Penalty--10% of labor--Late fee of 10% earnings will be applied to any tech that is more than 30 mins late without prior notice\n- **Any actions not listed below must be approved by WO manager in order to receive compensation**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T09:00","end":"2026-10-14T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":19.64423007585146},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Upcoming TU/Cutover | Endura Products | 04866063 | Stokesdale, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Incident #269224 - ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062266-609 Ray Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Camera Install + Cable Run - Durham, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068252-BJs Club 151- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T16:00: