{"job":{"id":20156967,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Walmart - Fire Fly 2026 - Receiving Installs - Gateways + Door Bridges - 2x techs required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>RETURN SCOPE:</strong></p>\n<p>Physical Install complete, Switch was full, cables were coiled. Switch has been upgraded. Must return to site, configure gateways/deploy site. Confirm runs</p>\n<p><strong>TECH MATERIAL:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Come prepared with CAT5E just in case cable runs are missing or damaged</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>PREVIOUS SCOPE</strong></p>\n<p>Two Techs Required**</p>\n<p><strong>TECH PROVIDED MATERIAL (REIMBURSED)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>RJ45 Modular Connectors x10</li>\n<li>5e Rj45 Jack Insert White x18</li>\n<li>1/2\" EMT conduit straps x40</li>\n<li>1/2\" EMT conduit, 10 foot&nbsp;8x</li>\n<li>1/2\" EMT conduit set screw couplers 8x</li>\n<li>1/2\" EMT conduit set screw connector 8x</li>\n<li>Cat 5e Patch Cord - 5 Ft, White 10x</li>\n<li>Cat 5e Patch Cord - 7 Ft, White&nbsp;10x</li>\n<li>1 Port Surface Mount Box&nbsp;-2x</li>\n<li>1 Port Faceplate White -8x</li>\n<li>1-Gang Metallic Weatherproof Box with (3) 1/2 inch -8x</li>\n<li>Tapcon Screws 3/16\" x 1-1/4\" - AVG. 50&nbsp;- 2x</li>\n<li>Miscellaneous Fasteners</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TECH REQUIRED TOOLS:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Camera/Smart Phone</li>\n<li>Label Maker</li>\n<li>CAT5E Tester</li>\n<li>10 foot ladder</li>\n<li>Use Store lift or ordered lift depending on store size</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>SITE PREP: (FOLLOW INSTALL GUIDE, SERVICE DESCRIPTION IS AN OVERVIEW)</strong></p>\n<p>Confirm site specific Gateway placement map.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>·Download the install guide</p>\n<p>·Locate the STORE LIFT</p>\n<p>·Locate Dock Doors in the Grocery Receiving area.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>·Locate NEAREST IDF &amp; Call CrossCom at 800-820-9229, L2 will assist in determining which ports to use for the gateway and Bridges.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>·Crosscom will provide the&nbsp;\"Authorization Code\" if the URL asks for it&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>UPDATING GATEWAY:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide the number of doors to Crosscom, Provide the Gateway numbers on your site map in the receiving area</li>\n<li>SHORT CABLE the Gateway to the configured port to begin the update process</li>\n<li>This will allow it to process updates while we run cable to SAVE TIME on site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DATA RUNS:</strong></p>\n<p>·Exposed vertical cable runs MUST be installed in 1/2\" EMT conduit up to the Red iron.</p>\n<p>-Install Gangbox/SMB/Faceplate at the bottom of the conduit. Use patch cables to connect the bridge to the jack</p>\n<p>·Install, terminate, LABEL and test (8x) Cat 5e data cables, 1 for each gateway and bridge, 2 per door.</p>\n<p>·The cables will be run from the Gateway devices installed at the site map locations to the closest IDF&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>After the gateway runs are done, take them off the short cables and mount them to their specified location (GATEWAY SITE MAP)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>BRIDGE INSTALL:</strong></p>\n<p>·Install Bridge brackets, Bridges, foam blocks &amp; smart QR labels on both sides of each loading dock door.</p>\n<p>·Register bridge devices through customer platform &amp; run performance test.</p>\n<p>-Patch cables should be zip tied to the mounting arm and plugged into the installed jack</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Review BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE - Checklist - Photo</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Contact CrossCom Project Team with issues, questions and configurations @800-820-9229.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Failure to provide deliverables and online confirmation may result in nonpayment</p>","markdown":"**RETURN SCOPE:**\n\nPhysical Install complete, Switch was full, cables were coiled. Switch has been upgraded. Must return to site, configure gateways/deploy site. Confirm runs\n\n**TECH MATERIAL:**\n\n**Come prepared with CAT5E just in case cable runs are missing or damaged**\n\n**PREVIOUS SCOPE**\n\nTwo Techs Required\\*\\*\n\n**TECH PROVIDED MATERIAL (REIMBURSED)**\n\n- RJ45 Modular Connectors x10\n- 5e Rj45 Jack Insert White x18\n- 1/2\" EMT conduit straps x40\n- 1/2\" EMT conduit, 10 foot 8x\n- 1/2\" EMT conduit set screw couplers 8x\n- 1/2\" EMT conduit set screw connector 8x\n- Cat 5e Patch Cord - 5 Ft, White 10x\n- Cat 5e Patch Cord - 7 Ft, White 10x\n- 1 Port Surface Mount Box -2x\n- 1 Port Faceplate White -8x\n- 1-Gang Metallic Weatherproof Box with (3) 1/2 inch -8x\n- Tapcon Screws 3/16\" x 1-1/4\" - AVG. 50 - 2x\n- Miscellaneous Fasteners\n\n**TECH REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Camera/Smart Phone\n- Label Maker\n- CAT5E Tester\n- 10 foot ladder\n- Use Store lift or ordered lift depending on store size\n\n**SITE PREP: (FOLLOW INSTALL GUIDE, SERVICE DESCRIPTION IS AN OVERVIEW)**\n\nConfirm site specific Gateway placement map.\n\n·Download the install guide\n\n·Locate the STORE LIFT\n\n·Locate Dock Doors in the Grocery Receiving area.\n\n·Locate NEAREST IDF & Call CrossCom at 800-820-9229, L2 will assist in determining which ports to use for the gateway and Bridges.\n\n·Crosscom will provide the \"Authorization Code\" if the URL asks for it\n\n**UPDATING GATEWAY:**\n\n- Provide the number of doors to Crosscom, Provide the Gateway numbers on your site map in the receiving area\n- SHORT CABLE the Gateway to the configured port to begin the update process\n- This will allow it to process updates while we run cable to SAVE TIME on site.\n\n**DATA RUNS:**\n\n·Exposed vertical cable runs MUST be installed in 1/2\" EMT conduit up to the Red iron.\n\n-Install Gangbox/SMB/Faceplate at the bottom of the conduit. Use patch cables to connect the bridge to the jack\n\n·Install, terminate, LABEL and test (8x) Cat 5e data cables, 1 for each gateway and bridge, 2 per door.\n\n·The cables will be run from the Gateway devices installed at the site map locations to the closest IDF\n\n**After the gateway runs are done, take them off the short cables and mount them to their specified location (GATEWAY SITE MAP)**\n\n**BRIDGE INSTALL:**\n\n·Install Bridge brackets, Bridges, foam blocks & smart QR labels on both sides of each loading dock door.\n\n·Register bridge devices through customer platform & run performance test.\n\n-Patch cables should be zip tied to the mounting arm and plugged into the installed jack\n\nReview BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE - Checklist - Photo\n\nContact CrossCom Project Team with issues, questions and configurations @800-820-9229.\n\nFailure to provide deliverables and online confirmation may result in nonpayment","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T08:00","end":"2026-10-22T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":350,"max":350},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":75.1652212970702},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $350 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Upcoming TU/Cutover | Endura Products | 04866063 | Stokesdale, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Incident #269224 - ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062266-609 Ray Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000