me.\n- All travel needs to be pre-approved **before assignment.**\n\n**Additional Site Instructions**\n\nTech to address the issue of the Down AP at RM 405 (HLT-RDUCY-36-405-AP050).\n\nTech to Check/Test the Cables of below APs as its getting error.. (Ethernet uplink speed degraded) might related to a cable issue (working on bouncing the port already... )\n\nAlerting APs:\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-315-AP041\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-318-AP042\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-403-AP048\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-416-AP055\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-500-AP060\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-609-AP080\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-613-AP082\n\nHLT-RDUCY-36-617-AP084\n\n**POC: Noah Latta**\n\n**Required skillsets:**\n\n- Router/switch/firewall configuration & troubleshooting\n- Wireless AP installs and testing (heat mapping experience is a plus)\n- Knowledge of TCP/IP, VLANs, DHCP, DNS\n- Ability to work with ticketing systems & follow case documentation processes\n\n**Scope:**\n\n**Pre-site**\n\n- Print out the attached Allbridge work order and bring to site.*This is a mandatory requirement.*\n\n**Onsite**\n\n- Contact Allbridge Dispatch at **1-516-394-4648**upon arrival\n- Introduce yourself to the customer as a representative of**Allbridge and Allbridge only**\n- Follow the Work Order Process outlined in Section B\n- Adhere to the assigned tasks and maintain professionalism\n- Update the end user on the status of repairs and/or next steps\n\n**Post site**\n\n- Complete the printed out Allbridge Work Order and obtain the customer's signature. *Failure to comply will result in non-payment.*\n- **Upload a photo of the completed Allbridge Work Order to FN**\n- Call **1-516-394-4648** to provide closeout notes and checkout with Allbridge Dispatch\n\n⚠️ **DISCLAIMER:** *Failure to check out with Allbridge by phone before leaving the job site may result in non-payment.*\n\n**Required tools:**\n\n- Laptop- with serial connector, Nic card and WIFI\n- Smartphone\n- Cat 5/6 tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch-down tools, etc.)\n- RJ45 cable tester – LinkRunner or similar\n- DB9 and DB25 testers\n- Serial cable (DB9)\n- Cisco console cable\n- Basic hand tools\n- Ladder - 7Ft\n- Voltage meter\n- Assortment of parts, including but not limited to wall jacks, patch cords, cabling connectors, etc.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T08:00","end":"2026-10-15T09:00","latestStart":"2026-10-15T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":9.529044829914348},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 (countered: $60) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Incident #269224 - ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062266-609 Ray Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Camera Install + Cable Run - Durham, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068252-BJs Club 151- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068292-BJs Club 215- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068254-BJs Club 357- EPIK-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-27T12:00:00.000Z","end