{"job":{"id":20159513,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"DATA REMOTE PORT/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/ MULTIMETER-DIS153311","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 385-262-3460 Ticket 11513392<br/><br/>***PIAB Cross Connect/Port***                               <br/> <br/>Call Porter Phelps at 8017081956  when on site.  <br/><br/>PIAB Device is already installed, customer has requested for us to port in an additional two lines (FA Lines). Additional Voip Line tickets  11977501 & 11977505 were submitted for this and the port is requested via this ticket 11513392. <br/><br/>List of TNs. <br/><br/>919.777.0186/919.777.0187<br/><br/>                                 <br/>-Technician to locate MetTel DataRemote CDS9090 board/equipment<br/>-MetTel will verify LTE/SIM status and SIP line registration<br/>-Technician will Confirm 0V on inside wiring before connecting to CDS-9090 FXS ports<br/>-Technician will, using appropriate punchdown tool, Cross-connect each analog line (fax, alarm, elevator, voice) from punch down block to the appropriate FXS port<br/>-Tech will test FX lines using butt set, very inbound/outbound call tests on each line (call 933 to simulate 911)<br/>-For Alarm Lines: Tech will have on site contact alarm company to place alarm panel into test mode.<br/>-For Alarm Lines: Confirm alarm panel signal transmission (e.g., Contact ID, SIA, Pulse)<br/>-Validate e911 address registration and line status reporting<br/>-Tech will label all lines with new numbers and text pictures of label to (332) 216-0897<br/> <br/>REQUIRED PHOTOS:<br/>1. Full picture of Network room and DMARC<br/>2. Location of where equipment will be installed<br/>3. Customer equipment that will be attached MTL equipment<br/>4. Cross connections/cabling of lines to be cross connected to MTL equipment<br/>5. Picture of Fire Panel with door closed<br/>6. Picture of Fire Panel with door open<br/>7. Picture of Wireless unit if currently on Cellular<br/>8. Picture of Burglar Alarm Panel with door closed<br/>9. Picture of Burglar Alarm Panel with door open<br/>10. Picture of elevator panel<br/>11. Picture of Fax Machine<br/>12. Picture of Fax Machine display pad<br/>13. Picture Signed Work Order<br/><br/>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/><br/>null<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 385-262-3460 Ticket 11513392  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*PIAB Cross Connect/Port\\*\\*\\*   \n   \nCall Porter Phelps at 8017081956 when on site.   \n  \nPIAB Device is already installed, customer has requested for us to port in an additional two lines (FA Lines). Additional Voip Line tickets 11977501 & 11977505 were submitted for this and the port is requested via this ticket 11513392.   \n  \nList of TNs.   \n  \n919.777.0186/919.777.0187  \n  \n   \n-Technician to locate MetTel DataRemote CDS9090 board/equipment  \n-MetTel will verify LTE/SIM status and SIP line registration  \n-Technician will Confirm 0V on inside wiring before connecting to CDS-9090 FXS ports  \n-Technician will, using appropriate punchdown tool, Cross-connect each analog line (fax, alarm, elevator, voice) from punch down block to the appropriate FXS port  \n-Tech will test FX lines using butt set, very inbound/outbound call tests on each line (call 933 to simulate 911)  \n-For Alarm Lines: Tech will have on site contact alarm company to place alarm panel into test mode.  \n-For Alarm Lines: Confirm alarm panel signal transmission (e.g., Contact ID, SIA, Pulse)  \n-Validate e911 address registration and line status reporting  \n-Tech will label all lines with new numbers and text pictures of label to (332) 216-0897  \n   \nREQUIRED PHOTOS:  \n1\\. Full picture of Network room and DMARC  \n2\\. Location of where equipment will be installed  \n3\\. Customer equipment that will be attached MTL equipment  \n4\\. Cross connections/cabling of lines to be cross connected to MTL equipment  \n5\\. Picture of Fire Panel with door closed  \n6\\. Picture of Fire Panel with door open  \n7\\. Picture of Wireless unit if currently on Cellular  \n8\\. Picture of Burglar Alarm Panel with door closed  \n9\\. Picture of Burglar Alarm Panel with door open  \n10\\. Picture of elevator panel  \n11\\. Picture of Fax Machine  \n12\\. Picture of Fax Machine display pad  \n13\\. Picture Signed Work Order  \n  \nMetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n  \nnull  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T10:00","end":"2026-10-26T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":31.11346625532336},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-1