{"job":{"id":20159456,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Qbuster - Call forward is not working for all positions, Troubleshoot, Call Helpdesk once on site","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work: The technician is required to address the issue of call forwarding not functioning across all positions in the Qbuster system. The technician must inspect each position to identify the source of the problem, ensuring that the speaker bar is powered on, set to AUX (not Bluetooth), and the volume is appropriately adjusted. If necessary, reboot the system and verify the monitor settings, ensuring the input is set to HDMI 1. Troubleshoot or replace parts as described in the service appointment. If parts are required, the technician must text Jess at <del>************</del> with an update and a picture of the part needed for confirmation of the system version. For version 2 and version 4 call button programming, refer to the workplan link provided (the version number will be on the back side of the call button). The name of the Manager on Duty (MOD) must be noted in the service appointment comments, as the service appointment cannot be closed without this information. Be specific with comments. If Jessica has been notified and parts are needed, do not close the service appointment; leave it as incomplete. The case will be updated with the tracking number for the required part.</em></p>\n<p><em><del>**********************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: Call forward is not working for all positions</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hrs</em></p>\n<p><em>Part pickup required: No</em></p>\n<p><em><del>**** ******** **** * ******</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>******** ********* **********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Helpdesk number of the customer: (Q-Buster)/Jessica<del>**************</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>****** *************** *** * ** * **** ********** *** ** *** * *********** ********</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>****** ****** *** ****** ***** ** *** **** *****</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>***********************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>If assistance is needed, please call:<del>************************ * *</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work: The technician is required to address the issue of call forwarding not functioning across all positions in the Qbuster system. The technician must inspect each position to identify the source of the problem, ensuring that the speaker bar is powered on, set to AUX (not Bluetooth), and the volume is appropriately adjusted. If necessary, reboot the system and verify the monitor settings, ensuring the input is set to HDMI 1. Troubleshoot or replace parts as described in the service appointment. If parts are required, the technician must text Jess at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* with an update and a picture of the part needed for confirmation of the system version. For version 2 and version 4 call button programming, refer to the workplan link provided (the version number will be on the back side of the call button). The name of the Manager on Duty (MOD) must be noted in the service appointment comments, as the service appointment cannot be closed without this information. Be specific with comments. If Jessica has been notified and parts are needed, do not close the service appointment; leave it as incomplete. The case will be updated with the tracking number for the required part.*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\