{"job":{"id":20159551,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Service Ticket #238051 - backdoor sensor bypassed | Replacement needed","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">TICKET SUMMARY:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> GENERAL WIRELESS DOOR ALARM SENSOR INSTALLATION &amp; SYSTEM PAIRING</span></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">A technician is required on-site to install, mount, pair, and commission a wireless door alarm contact sensor at the</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> Back Door</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">The technician will physically mount the wireless sensor and contact magnet, execute wireless panel enrollment in direct coordination with remote </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">Activations</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">, verify RF signal strength, and validate real-time zone fault and restore telemetry.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">DEFECTIVE ASSET HANDLING:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> Upon successful installation and system confirmation, any defective legacy sensor being replaced must be </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">placed in a designated, out-of-the-way area on-site</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> for local disposal by the location's staff. Do not remove defective hardware from the property unless explicitly instructed otherwise by Support.</span></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; PARTS</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT!</strong> (Mandatory in the event network, gateway, or alarm panel interface troubleshooting is required)</li><li><strong>6 x ¾\" Self-Drilling Screws (Phillips Head)</strong> (Mandatory for securing mounting brackets into metal door frames or structural casing)</li><li><strong>Small Precision Screwdriver Set</strong> (Required for micro-terminal adjustments, casing latches, or backplate mounting)</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill &amp; Driver Bits</strong></li><li><strong>8Ft Ladder</strong> (For overhead door frames, header access, or high sensor placements)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter</strong> (For verifying battery voltage and panel power levels)</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to <strong>the Back Door</strong> and hand over the new wireless sensor equipment provided for the job.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the scope and confirm target zone numbers with remote support before mounting or enrolling hardware.</li></ol><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 2: PHYSICAL WIRELESS SENSOR INSTALLATION</strong><ol><li><strong>PREPARATION:</strong> If replacing a failed unit, unmount the legacy sensor and magnet assembly. Clean the mounting surface of all adhesive residue or dirt.</li><li><strong>BATTERY INITIALIZATION:</strong> Remove the protective pull-tab or insert fresh batteries into the new wireless sensor housing. Verify the internal status LED blinks to confirm power-up.</li><li><strong>PHYSICAL MOUNTING:</strong> Utilizing your power drill and the <strong>6 x ¾\" self-drilling Phillips head screws</strong> (or manufacturer-approved heavy-duty mounting tape/brackets), securely mount:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Sensor Body:</strong> Attached to the stationary door frame or header casing.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Magnet Unit:</strong> Attached to the moving door panel, perfectly aligned parallel to the sensor's alignment notches.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Gap Tolerance:</em> Ensure the air gap between magnet and sensor meets manufacturer specifications (typically $\\le 0.5\\text{ inches}$) when the door is fully latched.</li></ul><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 3: WIRELESS ENROLLMENT &amp; SYSTEM TESTING</strong><ol><li><strong>PANEL PAIRING:</strong> Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Follow their instructions to trigger the sensor's tamper switch or serial transmission to enroll/pair the wireless ID into the central alarm panel matrix under the designated zone.</li><li><strong>FUNCTIONAL ZONE TESTING:</strong> Open and close the target door multiple times. Confirm with Support that real-time \"Zone Open / Fault\" and \"Zone Closed / Restored\" telemetry populates accurately on the monitoring dashboard.</li><li><strong>MOD VERIFICATION:</strong> Demonstrate the physical open/close operation of the door to the store manager and confirm the keypads/panels reflect the correct status without false alarms.</li></ol><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 4: ASSET STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:</strong> Place any old, defective sensor hardware neatly in the store's designated \"out of the way\" area (e.g., manager's office or IT storage rack) for site disposal. <strong>Do not remove this equipment from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Clean up all metal drill shavings, packaging wrappers, and battery tabs. Ensure the door frame and surrounding floor are left completely clean and presentable.</li></ol><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Wireless Sensor Mounted:</strong> Close-up photo showing the new wireless sensor and magnet cleanly installed and aligned on the door and frame.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Sensor (If Applicable):</strong> A photo showing the old, defective sensor set aside in the location's designated out-of-the-way area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network / Alarm Panel Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire network/IT rack with the cabinet door OPEN</strong>.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the floor and frame around the target door are swept completely clean of installation debris.</li></ul><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>MOD ACCEPTANCE:</strong> Confirm with the store manager that the door is fully operational and integrated with their security system.</li><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming complete sensor installation, system validation, and site cleanliness.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support. Update internal notes detailing the exact serial numbers/zone IDs used for the door and close out the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n**TICKET SUMMARY:** GENERAL WIRELESS DOOR ALARM SENSOR INSTALLATION & SYSTEM PAIRING\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A technician is required on-site to install, mount, pair, and commission a wireless door alarm contact sensor at the **Back Door**.\n\nThe technician will physically mount the wireless sensor and contact magnet, execute wireless panel enrollment in direct coordination with remote **Activations**, verify RF signal strength, and validate real-time zone fault and restore telemetry.\n\n**DEFECTIVE ASSET HANDLING:** Upon successful installation and system confirmation, any defective legacy sensor being replaced must be **placed in a designated, out-of-the-way area on-site** for local disposal by the location's staff. Do not remove defective hardware from the property unless explicitly instructed otherwise by Support.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & PARTS**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT!** (Mandatory in the event network, gateway, or alarm panel interface troubleshooting is required)\n- **6 x ¾\" Self-Drilling Screws (Phillips Head)** (Mandatory for securing mounting brackets into metal door frames or structural casing)\n- **Small Precision Screwdriver Set** (Required for micro-terminal adjustments, casing latches, or backplate mounting)\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill & Driver Bits**\n- **8Ft Ladder** (For overhead door frames, header access, or high sensor placements)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter** (For verifying battery voltage and panel power levels)\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to **the Back Door** and hand over the new wireless sensor equipment provided for the job.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the scope and confirm target zone numbers with remote support before mounting or enrolling hardware.\n\n**PHASE 2: PHYSICAL WIRELESS SENSOR INSTALLATION**1. **PREPARATION:** If replacing a failed unit, unmount the legacy sensor and magnet assembly. Clean the mounting surface of all adhesive residue or dirt.\n2. **BATTERY INITIALIZATION:** Remove the protective pull-tab or insert fresh batteries into the new wireless sensor housing. Verify the internal status LED blinks to confirm power-up.\n3. **PHYSICAL MOUNTING:** Utilizing your power drill and the **6 x ¾\" self-drilling Phillips head screws** (or manufacturer-approved heavy-duty mounting tape/brackets), securely mount:\n\n- **Sensor Body:** Attached to the stationary door frame or header casing.\n- **Magnet Unit:** Attached to the moving door panel, perfectly aligned parallel to the sensor's alignment notches.\n- *Gap Tolerance:* Ensure the air gap between magnet and sensor meets manufacturer specifications (typically $\\\\le 0.5\\\\text{ inches}$) when the door is fully latched.\n\n**PHASE 3: WIRELESS ENROLLMENT & SYSTEM TESTING**1. **PANEL PAIRING:** Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411). Follow their instructions to trigger the sensor's tamper switch or serial transmission to enroll/pair the wireless ID into the central alarm panel matrix under the designated zone.\n2. **FUNCTIONAL ZONE TESTING:** Open and close the target door multiple times. Confirm with Support that real-time \"Zone Open / Fault\" and \"Zone Closed / Restored\" telemetry populates accurately on the monitoring dashboard.\n3. **MOD VERIFICATION:** Demonstrate the physical open/close operation of the door to the store manager and confirm the keypads/panels reflect the correct status without false alarms.\n\n**PHASE 4: ASSET STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**1. **DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:** Place any old, defective sensor hardware neatly in the store's designated \"out of the way\" area (e.g., manager's office or IT storage rack) for site disposal. **Do not remove this equipment from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Clean up all metal drill shavings, packaging wrappers, and battery tabs. Ensure the door frame and surrounding floor are left completely clean and presentable.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Wireless Sensor Mounted:** Close-up photo showing the new wireless sensor and magnet cleanly installed and aligned on the door and frame.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Sensor (If Applicable):** A photo showing the old, defective sensor set aside in the location's designated out-of-the-way area.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network / Alarm Panel Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire network/IT rack with the cabinet door OPEN**.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the floor and frame around the target door are swept completely clean of installation debris.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **MOD ACCEPTANCE:** Confirm with the store manager that the door is fully operational and integrated with their security system.\n2. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming complete sensor installation, system validation, and site cleanliness.\n3. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support. Update internal notes detailing the exact serial numbers/zone IDs used for the door and close out the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T13:00","end":"2026-10-15T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-15T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":21.29976811498447},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Incident #269224 - ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06062266-609 Ray Street-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Camera Install + Cable Run - Durham, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 06068252-BJs