{"job":{"id":20171918,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Helper Tech for Lead Tech","description":{"html":"Job Description: Fiber Installation Helper Technician<p><strong>Position:</strong> Low-Voltage / Fiber Installation Helper</p><p><strong>Job Site:</strong> Apartment Construction Project</p><p><strong>Reports To:</strong> Lead Technician</p>Job Summary<p>The Fiber Installation Helper Technician assists the Lead Technician with installing fiber-optic cabling throughout an apartment construction building. This position requires hands-on construction labor, safe material handling, and the ability to work efficiently in an active construction environment.</p>Responsibilities<ul><li>Assist the Lead Technician with pulling, routing, and organizing fiber-optic cables throughout the building.</li><li>Transport and stage cable, tools, ladders, and installation materials.</li><li>Assist with installing cable pathways, supports, J-hooks, and other low-voltage infrastructure as directed.</li><li>Maintain proper cable handling practices to prevent damage, kinks, and excessive bending.</li><li>Keep work areas clean, organized, and free of debris.</li><li>Follow instructions, construction drawings, and job-site procedures.</li><li>Work safely on ladders and in designated ceiling spaces or other approved work areas.</li><li>Coordinate with the Lead Technician and other construction trades to maintain productivity.</li><li>Report safety hazards, damaged materials, and installation issues to the Lead Technician.</li></ul>Required Qualifications<ul><li>Proficient in general construction labor and physical work associated with IT and low-voltage installations.</li><li>Ability to lift and carry materials, climb ladders, bend, kneel, and stand for extended periods.</li><li>Ability to use basic hand tools and assist with cable installation.</li><li>Dependable, punctual, and able to follow instructions.</li><li>Ability to work as part of a team in a fast-paced construction environment.</li><li>Previous experience in telecommunications, structured cabling, or fiber installation is preferred.</li></ul>Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) and Safety<p><strong>Required PPE must be worn at all times as specified by site rules</strong>, including:</p><ul><li>Hard hat</li><li>Safety glasses</li><li>High-visibility vest</li><li>Work gloves appropriate for the task</li><li>Safety-toe work boots</li><li>Hearing protection and other PPE when required</li></ul><p>The technician must follow all job-site safety rules, attend required safety briefings, maintain good housekeeping, and immediately report unsafe conditions. Never enter restricted areas or perform work without proper authorization and training.</p>Performance Expectations<p>The Helper Technician is expected to arrive on time, maintain a strong work ethic, follow the Lead Technician’s direction, protect materials and equipment, and complete assigned tasks safely and efficiently.</p><p><strong>Primary Goal:</strong> Support the successful installation of fiber-optic cabling throughout the apartment construction project while maintaining quality, safety, and productivity.</p>","markdown":"Job Description: Fiber Installation Helper Technician\n\n**Position:** Low-Voltage / Fiber Installation Helper\n\n**Job Site:** Apartment Construction Project\n\n**Reports To:** Lead Technician\n\nJob SummaryThe Fiber Installation Helper Technician assists the Lead Technician with installing fiber-optic cabling throughout an apartment construction building. This position requires hands-on construction labor, safe material handling, and the ability to work efficiently in an active construction environment.\n\nResponsibilities- Assist the Lead Technician with pulling, routing, and organizing fiber-optic cables throughout the building.\n- Transport and stage cable, tools, ladders, and installation materials.\n- Assist with installing cable pathways, supports, J-hooks, and other low-voltage infrastructure as directed.\n- Maintain proper cable handling practices to prevent damage, kinks, and excessive bending.\n- Keep work areas clean, organized, and free of debris.\n- Follow instructions, construction drawings, and job-site procedures.\n- Work safely on ladders and in designated ceiling spaces or other approved work areas.\n- Coordinate with the Lead Technician and other construction trades to maintain productivity.\n- Report safety hazards, damaged materials, and installation issues to the Lead Technician.\n\nRequired Qualifications- Proficient in general construction labor and physical work associated with IT and low-voltage installations.\n- Ability to lift and carry materials, climb ladders, bend, kneel, and stand for extended periods.\n- Ability to use basic hand tools and assist with cable installation.\n- Dependable, punctual, and able to follow instructions.\n- Ability to work as part of a team in a fast-paced construction environment.\n- Previous experience in telecommunications, structured cabling, or fiber installation is preferred.\n\nPersonal Protective Equipment (PPE) and Safety**Required PPE must be worn at all times as specified by site rules**, including:\n\n- Hard hat\n- Safety glasses\n- High-visibility vest\n- Work gloves appropriate for the task\n- Safety-toe work boots\n- Hearing protection and other PPE when required\n\nThe technician must follow all job-site safety rules, attend required safety briefings, maintain good housekeeping, and immediately report unsafe conditions. Never enter restricted areas or perform work without proper authorization and training.\n\nPerformance ExpectationsThe Helper Technician is expected to arrive on time, maintain a strong work ethic, follow the Lead Technician’s direction, protect materials and equipment, and complete assigned tasks safely and efficiently.\n\n**Primary Goal:** Support the successful installation of fiber-optic cabling throughout the apartment construction project while maintaining quality, safety, and productivity.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T08:00","end":"2026-10-15T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6.5,"distance":25.367090673831907},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792062139089}
{"job":{"id":20169935,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"SDWAN Cutover- (Overnight schedule, materials need to be picked up prior at hold location)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Pre-Onsite Work:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>Equipment/Materials will be shipped directly to the technician assigned or to Fedex hold facility as close to the store as possible. Assigned technician MUST pick up equipment prior to the scheduled date and send confirmation this has been completed. This will be a precheck task, with all delivery/tracking info in the confidential section. There will be TWO packages to pick up at FedEx, one containing the (2) SDWAN Routers, Cradlepoint, and pre-labeled patch cables, and the second package will contain 200&#39; of cat6a, keystones, and biscuit jacks.</strong></p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Scope of Work on Site: This is after hours work- please check start time</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Check in with store manager, and locate the store&#39;s &quot;Control Room&quot; (Note: this is an overnight assignment, the store will be closed once you begin work, and you will have to remain on site until the morning shift arrives to open the store. Be sure you have all tools with you and not in your vehicle, as you will be unable to retrieve them from outside the store once the installation begins.</li><li>Confirm there is space on rack for new equipment, and confirm rack is compatible with <strong>included mounting hardware</strong></li><li><strong><u>Locate and test new Verizon circuit</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Install four extensions from the patch panel on the rack to the new Verizon circuit on the wall (located in the same room)</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Install CAT6a for cutover for refreshed Cradlepoint to Vera as per the installation guide with remote support</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Label all newly installed cables clearly and legibly with label maker</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Technician must arrive on time. Remote engineers will be on a live bridge awaiting your arrival. Check-in with site contacts representing </u></strong><span style=\"background-color: #162741; color: #ffffff;\"><del>*******</del></span></li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Note: Included keystones are Leviton Atlas X1 self-crimping keystones. Please familiarize yourself with how these terminate prior to going to the site by watching this video:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9aDbsVKiV1k</p><br/><br/><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.</em></p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong>Tool Requirement:</strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>Note: extending the circuit may be required. Tech will need to be prepared to terminate cables while on site without issue.</strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li><strong>Charged Cell Phone</strong> (with charger)- you may be asked to share your video, ensure this is not an issue</li><li><strong>Government-Issued Photo ID</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop (WIN10) with charger</strong></li><li><strong>Label Maker with correct label stock:</strong></li></ul><br/><br/><p>1/2” Black on White, Flexible ID (Patch Cables)</p><br/><br/><p>NO FLAGS — wrap label fully around the cable</p><br/><br/><p>Labeling details will come from remote engineer on bridge line</p><br/><br/><ul><li>Basic CAT6/RJ45 termination tools</li><li>Cable tester with Pass/Fail identifier</li><li>Standard networking tool kit (RJ45, biscuits, etc.)</li><li>Hotspot / internet dongle</li><li>Laptop with an ethernet port, or gigabit+ usb ethernet dongle, with Charger</li><li>Cell phone with Charger</li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong>Site Security Requirements:</strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance </li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <span style=\"background-color: #162741; color: #ffffff;\"><del>*******</del></span></li><li><strong><u>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment </u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Professional environment expects professional conduct and clean business casual attire</u></strong></li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p>","markdown":"**Pre-Onsite Work:**\n\n  \n  \n**Equipment/Materials will be shipped directly to the technician assigned or to Fedex hold facility as close to the store as possible. Assigned technician MUST pick up equipment prior to the scheduled date and send confirmation this has been completed. This will be a precheck task, with all delivery/tracking info in the confidential section. There will be TWO packages to pick up at FedEx, one containing the (2) SDWAN Routers, Cradlepoint, and pre-labeled patch cables, and the second package will contain 200' of cat6a, keystones, and biscuit jacks.**\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Scope of Work on Site: This is after hours work- please check start time**\n\n  \n  \n- Check in with store manager, and locate the store's \"Control Room\" (Note: this is an overnight assignment, the store will be closed once you begin work, and you will have to remain on site until the morning shift arrives to open the store. Be sure you have all tools with you and not in your vehicle, as you will be unable to retrieve them from outside the store once the installation begins.\n- Confirm there is space on rack for new equipment, and confirm rack is compatible with **included mounting hardware**\n- **Locate and test new Verizon circuit**\n- **Install four extensions from the patch panel on the rack to the new Verizon circuit on the wall (located in the same room)**\n- **Install CAT6a for cutover for refreshed Cradlepoint to Vera as per the installation guide with remote support**\n- **Label all newly installed cables clearly and legibly with label maker**\n- **Technician must arrive on time. Remote engineers will be on a live bridge awaiting your arrival. Check-in with site contacts representing** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Note: Included keystones are Leviton Atlas X1 self-crimping keystones. Please familiarize yourself with how these terminate prior to going to the site by watching this video:**\n\n  \n  \n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9aDbsVKiV1k>\n\n  \n  \n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.*\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n  \n  \n**Note: extending the circuit may be required. Tech will need to be prepared to terminate cables while on site without issue.**\n\n  \n  \n- **Charged Cell Phone** (with charger)- you may be asked to share your video, ensure this is not an issue\n- **Government-Issued Photo ID**\n- **Laptop (WIN10) with charger**\n- **Label Maker with correct label stock:**\n\n  \n  \n1/2” Black on White, Flexible ID (Patch Cables)\n\n  \n  \nNO FLAGS — wrap label fully around the cable\n\n  \n  \nLabeling details will come from remote engineer on bridge line\n\n  \n  \n- Basic CAT6/RJ45 termination tools\n- Cable tester with Pass/Fail identifier\n- Standard networking tool kit (RJ45, biscuits, etc.)\n- Hotspot / internet dongle\n- Laptop with an ethernet port, or gigabit+ usb ethernet dongle, with Charger\n- Cell phone with Charger\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment**\n- **Professional environment expects professional conduct and clean business casual attire**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-01T21:30","end":"2026-11-01T29:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":8.720300327595531},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792062151703}
{"job":{"id":20171872,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"A/V Install - Durham, NC - 11/2 ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU&nbsp;<u>READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.</u></strong></p><p>Please Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.</p><p><strong><u>PLEASE REVIEW</u></strong> - Any travel cost incurred would need to be reviewed by the provider and made up front when acceptance of the work order - Parking, materials, etc. are <strong><u>paid/ approved with receipts- only - provide some other documentation of the payment. Or it is up to WO manger discretion. </u></strong></p><p>Please review the <strong><u>HERMAN GUIDELINES portion below</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p><p>Attached </p><p>Summary This document presents a time and materials proposal for Professional Services to be provided to ICF CONSULTING GROUP (ICF) for audio-visual services and equipment. The goal of this project is to migrate these conference rooms away from using Poly OS and Poly Realconnect, as Realconnect is end of life. In some rooms, existing equipment needs to be updated or replaced as part of this project.</p><ul><li>Help unload equipment, stage and unbox equipment</li><li>Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go</li></ul><p><strong><u>BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE</u></strong></p><ol><li>Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete&nbsp;a Field Report for <u>EACH</u> <u>DAY</u> worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><u>ON-SITE TASKS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check into your Work Order</li><li>Call the&nbsp;<em>LOCATION CONTACT</em>&nbsp;at the phone number provided on this work order&nbsp;upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site</li><li>Obtain completed and signed field report</li><li>With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done</li><li>Obtain Signature</li><li>Check out of Work Order</li></ol><p><strong>Any expenses&nbsp;<u>MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU</u>&nbsp;on the work order and&nbsp;<u>MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT</u>.​</strong></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><u>Failure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site</u>.&nbsp;Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression.&nbsp;If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.</p><p><strong><em>Mounting Tools:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits</li><li>Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)</li><li>Stud Finder</li><li>Bubble level</li><li>Hammer</li><li>Drywall saw</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Box knife</li><li>Socket set (SAE/metric)</li></ul><p><strong><em>Cabling Tools:</em></strong></p><ul><li>RJ45 crimper for Category cable (5-6)</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Punch down tool</li></ul><p><strong><em>PPE</em></strong></p><ul><li><u>You are required to have basic PPE</u> (<em>Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves</em>) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>DO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS</u></strong>. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the <u>Project Manager</u> listed on this work order<strong> <u>IMMEDIATELY</u> </strong>any such purchases require<strong> <u>PRE-AUTHORIZATION</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>HERMAN GUIDELINES - PLEASE READ</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Schedule:</u></strong><u> Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical. Any overtime hours</u><strong><u> MUST be PRE-APPROVED </u></strong><u>by the Project Manager.</u></p><p><u>All workorders are time and materials - which means please bill your actual time onsite / alongside with sign off proof. the document is found in the documents section of this work order. Your closeouts must be accompanied by this document - will not be accepted if sign by yourself - this is coverage that you were completed and released from site by the client - </u></p><p><u>Any cancellation outside of Field Nation's set window which states in the 24 hrs. window - Will be on a case-by-case bases - approved by the workorder manager - this does not approve hours that were scheduled. Work order manager will need to review situation and document - possible 2hr trip fee will be issued to the technician that showed up to site - (ONTIME)</u></p><p><strong>Running late/Unable to make it</strong>: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via<u> phone or message IMMEDIATELY</u>. use the report problem.</p><p><strong><u>Switching Workers:</u></strong><u>&nbsp;Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project or possible NONpayment of workorder.</u></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. No Shorts, Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button-down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).</p><p><strong>Heights:</strong>&nbsp;Must be comfortable working off a ladder.</p><p><strong>Site Conditions:</strong>&nbsp;Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)</p><p><strong>Parking Instructions:</strong>&nbsp;If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order.&nbsp;We cannot accept handwritten receipts.</p><p><strong>Security Instructions:&nbsp;</strong>Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times</p><p><strong>Transportation:&nbsp;</strong>Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.</p><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li>Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.</li><li>Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.</li><li>Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.</li><li>Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.</li><li>No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite &amp; in from of the customer</li><li>If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site</li><li>Do NOT place tools on furniture.&nbsp;</li><li>SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order</li></ul>","markdown":"**BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.**\n\nPlease Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.\n\n**PLEASE REVIEW** - Any travel cost incurred would need to be reviewed by the provider and made up front when acceptance of the work order - Parking, materials, etc. are **paid/ approved with receipts- only - provide some other documentation of the payment. Or it is up to WO manger discretion.**\n\nPlease review the **HERMAN GUIDELINES portion below**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\nAttached\n\nSummary This document presents a time and materials proposal for Professional Services to be provided to ICF CONSULTING GROUP (ICF) for audio-visual services and equipment. The goal of this project is to migrate these conference rooms away from using Poly OS and Poly Realconnect, as Realconnect is end of life. In some rooms, existing equipment needs to be updated or replaced as part of this project.\n\n- Help unload equipment, stage and unbox equipment\n- Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go\n\n**BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE**\n\n1. Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete a Field Report for EACH DAY worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\n1. Check into your Work Order\n2. Call the *LOCATION CONTACT* at the phone number provided on this work order upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site\n3. Obtain completed and signed field report\n4. With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done\n5. Obtain Signature\n6. Check out of Work Order\n\n**Any expenses MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU on the work order and MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT.​**\n\n**REQUIRED EQUIPMENT**\n\nFailure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site. Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression. If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.\n\n***Mounting Tools:***\n\n- Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits\n- Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)\n- Stud Finder\n- Bubble level\n- Hammer\n- Drywall saw\n- Pliers\n- Box knife\n- Socket set (SAE/metric)\n\n***Cabling Tools:***\n\n- RJ45 crimper for Category cable (5-6)\n- Wire cutters\n- Cable tester\n- Punch down tool\n\n***PPE***\n\n- You are required to have basic PPE (*Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves*) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.\n\n**DO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS**. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the Project Manager listed on this work order **IMMEDIATELY** any such purchases require **PRE-AUTHORIZATION**\n\n**HERMAN GUIDELINES - PLEASE READ**\n\n**Schedule:** Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical. Any overtime hours **MUST be PRE-APPROVED** by the Project Manager.\n\nAll workorders are time and materials - which means please bill your actual time onsite / alongside with sign off proof. the document is found in the documents section of this work order. Your closeouts must be accompanied by this document - will not be accepted if sign by yourself - this is coverage that you were completed and released from site by the client -\n\nAny cancellation outside of Field Nation's set window which states in the 24 hrs. window - Will be on a case-by-case bases - approved by the workorder manager - this does not approve hours that were scheduled. Work order manager will need to review situation and document - possible 2hr trip fee will be issued to the technician that showed up to site - (ONTIME)\n\n**Running late/Unable to make it**: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via phone or message IMMEDIATELY. use the report problem.\n\n**Switching Workers:** Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project or possible NONpayment of workorder.\n\n**Dress Code:** You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. No Shorts, Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button-down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).\n\n**Heights:** Must be comfortable working off a ladder.\n\n**Site Conditions:** Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)\n\n**Parking Instructions:** If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order. We cannot accept handwritten receipts.\n\n**Security Instructions:** Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times\n\n**Transportation:** Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT**\n\n- Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.\n- Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.\n- Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.\n- Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.\n- No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite & in from of the customer\n- If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site\n- Do NOT place tools on furniture.\n- SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T09:00","end":"2026-11-02T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":21.096336945572546},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792062162300}
