{"job":{"id":20171745,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Package Solutions - Troubleshooting (82709)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements</u>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Please review Resource videos below and attached Client Documents for better understanding of system. (Note: Not all videos/documents may be necessary.)</li>\n<li>Check tracking for parts ensuring that they've arrived before going on-site. (If no tracking provided below, call Luxer Support.)</li>\n<li>Check shipping address for parts, if site does not have an office parts may be held by UPS Store.</li>\n<li>Sign Technician NDA <strong>(</strong><strong><u>REQUIRED TO RECIEVE PAYMENT</u></strong><strong>):</strong><del>**************************************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Check-In</u>:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check-in with on-site staff.</li>\n<li>Check-in with our support at&nbsp;<strong><del>************</del></strong>&nbsp;to get codes and review scope.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Job Details</u>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Calling into support for check-in/out is mandatory, additional calls can be made for any troubleshooting assistance.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope</u>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Type of Request:</strong></p>\n<p>Tech Only</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Reason for Visit:</strong></p>\n<p>Full System Down</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Property Details:</strong></p>\n<p>Tower at Carraway Village</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Address:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>350 Carraway Crossing Chapel Hill, North Carolina 27516</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Special Tools Needed:</strong></p>\n<p>-</p>\n<p>**For Internet:</p>\n<p>- Ethernet Tester</p>\n<p>- Laptop w/ Ethernet Port with Firefox Installed</p>\n<p>- Line Toner</p>\n<p>- Device w/ HotSpot Functionality</p>\n<p>- Ethernet cable terminals (RJ45)</p>\n<p>- Ethernet cable terminating tool (RJ45)</p>\n<p>- Precision Screwdriver Set, iFixit or equivalent</p>\n<p>-</p>\n<p>**For Power:</p>\n<p>- Wire Crimper</p>\n<p>- Outlet Tester</p>\n<p>- Volt-Meter</p>\n<p>- Precision Screwdriver Set</p>\n<p>- iFixit or equivalent</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Parts Needed:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope:</strong></p>\n<p>Full System Down Inspection:</p>\n<p>Network &amp; Router:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm router is connected and receiving live internet.</li>\n<li>Test/inspect ethernet connections and document speed (Minimum 1.5MB/s upload speed).</li>\n<li>Contact LuxerOne support at 916 252 5590 to gain access to the router and view attached devices on the network.</li>\n<li>Verify all devices are accounted for.</li>\n<li>If devices are missing, restore their connectivity.</li>\n<li>If property internet is not live, request the property reboot their Luxer modem (OOS for technician).</li>\n<li>If successful, reboot Luxer Netgear router as well.</li>\n<li>if you are able toconfirm that the Luxer router is receiving active internet from the property.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Lockers iPad(s):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact LuxerOne support at 916 252 5590 to disable single-app-mode and to verify the iPad is reporting as ‘Alive.’.</li>\n<li>Access the iPad by opening the Main control bay and removing the iPad from the mounting plate.</li>\n<li>If wired, confirm adapters are connected properly.</li>\n<li>If connected via Wi-Fi, ensure the iPad is connected to SSID ‘LuxerOne’ and forget all other networks.</li>\n<li>**Note: If the Lockers has a ThermoElectric Cooler (TEC) attached to the docking plate, the iPad can still be removed via the thumb screws.</li>\n<li>Power cycle the system's iPad by holding the POWER and HOME buttons until the screen goes blank. If the iPad screen is stuck in data sync afterwards, then call the support number below.</li>\n<li>Otherwise, proceed to next step.</li>\n<li>If the Control Board, wiring, and iPad are operational, contact the technician support team at 916-252-5590 to conduct several test deliveries and pick-ups.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>On the Luxer One App:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Log into the Manager Interface using the 8-digit manager code (if the iPad did not automatically sync, you may select “Re-sync” on this page to ensure it does).</li>\n<li>Test opening the door(s) by opening them individually. **DO NOT USE ‘OPEN ALL LOCKERS’ command as it floods Control Boards with voltage**</li>\n<li>If testing was successful, secure the iPad back into the enclosure and reconnect all cables.</li>\n<li>Confirm the iPad is charging and still opening locks after repositioning.</li>\n<li>If the Control Board, wiring, and iPad are operational, contact the technician support team at 916-252-5590 to conduct several test deliveries and pick-ups.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Check-Out</u>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out with technical support&nbsp;<strong><del>**************</del></strong>&nbsp;to ensure the issue has been resolved and that system is functional.</li>\n<li>Check out with the on-site staff demonstrating that the issue has been resolved.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with support</u>:&nbsp;</strong><strong><del>************</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Resources:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Lock Replacement:</strong></p>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eklOvGnzzVo&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=11</p>\n<p><strong>Accessing the Control Board:</strong></p>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oxQo9IvMuuI&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=12</p>","markdown":"**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Please review Resource videos below and attached Client Documents for better understanding of system. (Note: Not all videos/documents may be necessary.)\n- Check tracking for parts ensuring that they've arrived before going on-site. (If no tracking provided below, call Luxer Support.)\n- Check shipping address for parts, if site does not have an office parts may be held by UPS Store.\n- Sign Technician NDA **(****REQUIRED TO RECIEVE PAYMENT****):**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check-In:**\n\n- Check-in with on-site staff.\n- Check-in with our support at **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to get codes and review scope.\n\n**Job Details:**\n\n**Calling into support for check-in/out is mandatory, additional calls can be made for any troubleshooting assistance.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\n**Type of Request:**\n\nTech Only\n\n**Reason for Visit:**\n\nFull System Down\n\n**Property Details:**\n\nTower at Carraway Village\n\n**Address:**\n\n**350 Carraway Crossing Chapel Hill, North Carolina 27516**\n\n**Special Tools Needed:**\n\n-\n\n\\*\\*For Internet:\n\n\\- Ethernet Tester\n\n\\- Laptop w/ Ethernet Port with Firefox Installed\n\n\\- Line Toner\n\n\\- Device w/ HotSpot Functionality\n\n\\- Ethernet cable terminals (RJ45)\n\n\\- Ethernet cable terminating tool (RJ45)\n\n\\- Precision Screwdriver Set, iFixit or equivalent\n\n-\n\n\\*\\*For Power:\n\n\\- Wire Crimper\n\n\\- Outlet Tester\n\n\\- Volt-Meter\n\n\\- Precision Screwdriver Set\n\n\\- iFixit or equivalent\n\n**Parts Needed:**\n\n**Scope:**\n\nFull System Down Inspection:\n\nNetwork & Router:\n\n- Confirm router is connected and receiving live internet.\n- Test/inspect ethernet connections and document speed (Minimum 1.5MB/s upload speed).\n- Contact LuxerOne support at 916 252 5590 to gain access to the router and view attached devices on the network.\n- Verify all devices are accounted for.\n- If devices are missing, restore their connectivity.\n- If property internet is not live, request the property reboot their Luxer modem (OOS for technician).\n- If successful, reboot Luxer Netgear router as well.\n- if you are able toconfirm that the Luxer router is receiving active internet from the property.\n\nLockers iPad(s):\n\n- Contact LuxerOne support at 916 252 5590 to disable single-app-mode and to verify the iPad is reporting as ‘Alive.’.\n- Access the iPad by opening the Main control bay and removing the iPad from the mounting plate.\n- If wired, confirm adapters are connected properly.\n- If connected via Wi-Fi, ensure the iPad is connected to SSID ‘LuxerOne’ and forget all other networks.\n- \\*\\*Note: If the Lockers has a ThermoElectric Cooler (TEC) attached to the docking plate, the iPad can still be removed via the thumb screws.\n- Power cycle the system's iPad by holding the POWER and HOME buttons until the screen goes blank. If the iPad screen is stuck in data sync afterwards, then call the support number below.\n- Otherwise, proceed to next step.\n- If the Control Board, wiring, and iPad are operational, contact the technician support team at 916-252-5590 to conduct several test deliveries and pick-ups.\n\nOn the Luxer One App:\n\n- Log into the Manager Interface using the 8-digit manager code (if the iPad did not automatically sync, you may select “Re-sync” on this page to ensure it does).\n- Test opening the door(s) by opening them individually. \\*\\*DO NOT USE ‘OPEN ALL LOCKERS’ command as it floods Control Boards with voltage\\*\\*\n- If testing was successful, secure the iPad back into the enclosure and reconnect all cables.\n- Confirm the iPad is charging and still opening locks after repositioning.\n- If the Control Board, wiring, and iPad are operational, contact the technician support team at 916-252-5590 to conduct several test deliveries and pick-ups.\n\n**Check-Out:**\n\n- Check out with technical support **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to ensure the issue has been resolved and that system is functional.\n- Check out with the on-site staff demonstrating that the issue has been resolved.\n\n**If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with support:** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Resources:**\n\n**Lock Replacement:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eklOvGnzzVo&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=11>\n\n**Accessing the Control Board:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oxQo9IvMuuI&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=12>","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T10:00","end":"2026-10-15T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-15T16:30"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":95},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":55},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":29.958360206850625},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $95 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792062209253}
{"job":{"id":20171106,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Package Solutions - Troubleshooting (78348)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements</u>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Please review Resource videos below and attached Client Documents for better understanding of system. (Note: Not all videos/documents may be necessary.)</li>\n<li>Check tracking for parts ensuring that they've arrived before going on-site. (If no tracking provided below, call Luxer Support.)</li>\n<li>Check shipping address for parts, if site does not have an office parts may be held by UPS Store.</li>\n<li>Sign Technician NDA <strong>(</strong><strong><u>REQUIRED TO RECIEVE PAYMENT</u></strong><strong>):</strong><del>**************************************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Check-In</u>:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check-in with on-site staff.</li>\n<li>Check-in with our support at&nbsp;<strong><del>************</del></strong>&nbsp;to get codes and review scope.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Job Details</u>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>CALL TECHNICAL SUPPORT REGARDING ANY TROUBLESHOOTING ASSISTANCE!!!</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*Have a laptop with a non-chromium based web browser(Firefox/Safari) and ethernet port ready.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope</u>:</strong></p>\n<p>- Test the lock for lockers: 15, 16, 17</p>\n<p>- If the lock clicks, adjust the latch until the door opens and closes smoothly</p>\n<p>- If the lock does not click, proceed to remove it; if the harness is secured and it will not click, replace it</p>\n<p>- Replace the lock by following the How to Replace a lock guide.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>- Once the lock is replaced, test it.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>- Contact tech support for further assistance if the door still doesn’t open.</p>\n<p>- If the door opens, test all the doors 2x to ensure all are swinging open.</p>\n<p>- If you notice any other doors not swinging open, align the latches of locker doors.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>- Replace the control board for lockers 1 - 17</p>\n<p>- Remove the old Control Board leave disconnected from power and ethernet for about 1-2 minutes and replace with the new control board.</p>\n<p>- Wait about 2 minutes after re-connecting power and ethernet back in and go to the iPad screen to the Set Up Servers tab.</p>\n<p>- Underneath the black horizontal line there should be an unassigned device that you will select and hit add new.</p>\n<p>- Call Luxer One support at 916-252-5590 to help you with the next phase to add into Admin and set up.</p>\n<p>- On the iPad screen select open one of the lockers to check if it opens or if you hear the locker click. If not we will troubleshoot from there.</p>\n<p>- Do a test delivery from the iPad with the carrier code given to you from Luxer One, then pick up the package with a new pick-up code to complete the test.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>- With the MoFi router provided, swap out the current router connections within the system to the MoFi and attach their live line into the WAN port on the MoFi</p>\n<p>- Install the add-on antenna’s with LuxerOne support with the adapter and test the cellular strength</p>\n<p>- Route the antenna’s and rods to the silicone punch out near the top right of the locker bank where the iPad is located</p>\n<p>- Check for connectivity intermittently with the system to ensure iPad does not go into a Data Sync</p>\n<p>- Conduct test a delivery and pickup with LuxerOne and check on camera stability and deliveries are being cataloged correctly</p>\n<p>- Demonstrate the MoFi placed into the system and that the system is operational now being on its own network</p>\n<p>- Take a photo of the SIM card from the previous MoFi, and submit the photo to your ticket.</p>\n<p>- Let the Technical Support team know the current SIM card number that is installed.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Check-Out</u>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out with technical support&nbsp;<strong><del>**************</del></strong>&nbsp;to ensure the issue has been resolved and that system is functional.</li>\n<li>Check out with the on-site staff demonstrating that the issue has been resolved.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with support</u>:&nbsp;</strong><strong><del>************</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Resources:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Mofi Install:</u></strong></p>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nbDEL6ULFF8&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=28</p>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=86u9qGSJ5PY&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=29</p>","markdown":"**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Please review Resource videos below and attached Client Documents for better understanding of system. (Note: Not all videos/documents may be necessary.)\n- Check tracking for parts ensuring that they've arrived before going on-site. (If no tracking provided below, call Luxer Support.)\n- Check shipping address for parts, if site does not have an office parts may be held by UPS Store.\n- Sign Technician NDA **(****REQUIRED TO RECIEVE PAYMENT****):**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check-In:**\n\n- Check-in with on-site staff.\n- Check-in with our support at **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to get codes and review scope.\n\n**Job Details:**\n\n**CALL TECHNICAL SUPPORT REGARDING ANY TROUBLESHOOTING ASSISTANCE!!!**\n\n**\\*Have a laptop with a non-chromium based web browser(Firefox/Safari) and ethernet port ready.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\n\\- Test the lock for lockers: 15, 16, 17\n\n\\- If the lock clicks, adjust the latch until the door opens and closes smoothly\n\n\\- If the lock does not click, proceed to remove it; if the harness is secured and it will not click, replace it\n\n\\- Replace the lock by following the How to Replace a lock guide.\n\n\\- Once the lock is replaced, test it.\n\n\\- Contact tech support for further assistance if the door still doesn’t open.\n\n\\- If the door opens, test all the doors 2x to ensure all are swinging open.\n\n\\- If you notice any other doors not swinging open, align the latches of locker doors.\n\n\\- Replace the control board for lockers 1 - 17\n\n\\- Remove the old Control Board leave disconnected from power and ethernet for about 1-2 minutes and replace with the new control board.\n\n\\- Wait about 2 minutes after re-connecting power and ethernet back in and go to the iPad screen to the Set Up Servers tab.\n\n\\- Underneath the black horizontal line there should be an unassigned device that you will select and hit add new.\n\n\\- Call Luxer One support at 916-252-5590 to help you with the next phase to add into Admin and set up.\n\n\\- On the iPad screen select open one of the lockers to check if it opens or if you hear the locker click. If not we will troubleshoot from there.\n\n\\- Do a test delivery from the iPad with the carrier code given to you from Luxer One, then pick up the package with a new pick-up code to complete the test.\n\n\\- With the MoFi router provided, swap out the current router connections within the system to the MoFi and attach their live line into the WAN port on the MoFi\n\n\\- Install the add-on antenna’s with LuxerOne support with the adapter and test the cellular strength\n\n\\- Route the antenna’s and rods to the silicone punch out near the top right of the locker bank where the iPad is located\n\n\\- Check for connectivity intermittently with the system to ensure iPad does not go into a Data Sync\n\n\\- Conduct test a delivery and pickup with LuxerOne and check on camera stability and deliveries are being cataloged correctly\n\n\\- Demonstrate the MoFi placed into the system and that the system is operational now being on its own network\n\n\\- Take a photo of the SIM card from the previous MoFi, and submit the photo to your ticket.\n\n\\- Let the Technical Support team know the current SIM card number that is installed.\n\n**Check-Out:**\n\n- Check out with technical support **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to ensure the issue has been resolved and that system is functional.\n- Check out with the on-site staff demonstrating that the issue has been resolved.\n\n**If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with support:** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Resources:**\n\n**Mofi Install:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nbDEL6ULFF8&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=28>\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=86u9qGSJ5PY&amp;list=PLd70puW1-kb2R6ZALYd5iYDnJ87idOudx&amp;index=29>","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T10:00","end":"2026-10-15T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":155},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":75},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14.42598808161084},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $155 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792062215706}
{"job":{"id":20171176,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"VOIP Phone Troubleshooting and Building Connectivity Inspection","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Mandatory Scope Discussion</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have <strong>not previously completed work for this specific project phase</strong> must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.</p>\n<p>If contacted, please plan to attend. <strong>Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technician needed to work with remote support on the following:</p>\n<p>VOIP phones are not working, need technician to check their setup.customer needs the device and the connections to be checked on the building</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS / IMPORTANT NOTES -</u></strong></p>\n<p>1 - After checking in with Splice, please call into<del>******</del> Remote support:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Support Phone -</strong><strong data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><del>************</del></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Support Contact -</strong><del>****** ******</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Case Number -</strong><del>********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>2 - Required Tools - Laptop, Paper Clip, PoE tester, Butt set or working Analog Phone, RJ11, RJ45, Step Ladder</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Duration:2 hours</p>\n<p>&nbsp;Experience:</p>\n<p>Technician will need to be proficient with VOIP (Voice over IP) hardware installation and mounting procedures.&nbsp;Will need to understand cut sheets and number porting pertaining to phone swaps.&nbsp;Will also need to have cabling experience, able to crimp, test, tone, and punch down cables as needed.&nbsp;Should have basic network knowledge and be able to configure static IP and other TCP/IP settings on laptop, as well as configure cable connections.&nbsp;Will need to communicate and work well with bridge lines and remote technical contacts via patch and console cable connections over Microsoft Teams, Teamviewer, Putty, etc.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity</li>\n<li>Microsoft Teams</li>\n<li>Teamviewer</li>\n<li>Putty</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cable</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)</li>\n<li>Smartphone</li>\n<li>Hot spot</li>\n<li>Socket setHex/Allen key set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested.&nbsp;Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task.&nbsp;All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site.&nbsp;There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:</u></strong></p>\n<p>CAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS/DELIVERABLES:</u></strong></p>\n<p>PLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL.&nbsp;CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DRESS CODE:</strong></p>\n<p>Business casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.).&nbsp;This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**Mandatory Scope Discussion**\n\nTechnicians who have **not previously completed work for this specific project phase** must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.\n\nIf contacted, please plan to attend. **Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:**\n\nTechnician needed to work with remote support on the following:\n\nVOIP phones are not working, need technician to check their setup.customer needs the device and the connections to be checked on the building\n\n**TASKS / IMPORTANT NOTES -**\n\n1 - After checking in with Splice, please call into\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Remote support:\n\n- **Support Phone -****\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- **Support Contact -**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Case Number -**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n2 - Required Tools - Laptop, Paper Clip, PoE tester, Butt set or working Analog Phone, RJ11, RJ45, Step Ladder\n\n**JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:**\n\nDuration:2 hours\n\n Experience:\n\nTechnician will need to be proficient with VOIP (Voice over IP) hardware installation and mounting procedures. Will need to understand cut sheets and number porting pertaining to phone swaps. Will also need to have cabling experience, able to crimp, test, tone, and punch down cables as needed. Should have basic network knowledge and be able to configure static IP and other TCP/IP settings on laptop, as well as configure cable connections. Will need to communicate and work well with bridge lines and remote technical contacts via patch and console cable connections over Microsoft Teams, Teamviewer, Putty, etc.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity\n- Microsoft Teams\n- Teamviewer\n- Putty\n- Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- Label maker\n- Patch Cables\n- Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)\n- Smartphone\n- Hot spot\n- Socket setHex/Allen key set\n\n**As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.**\n\n**IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:**\n\nCAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.\n\n**TASKS/DELIVERABLES:**\n\nPLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL. CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.\n\n**DRESS CODE:**\n\nBusiness casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.). This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":26.020947570286438},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlo