{"job":{"id":20169607,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Vanguard Security Device Install (Two Person Install)","description":{"html":"<p>The assignment is to install Vanguard security equipment and devices in a Verizon. <strong>Each location will require two (2) installers.</strong></p><p>The Verizon team will be uninstalling items for a store reset the night before each phase, and the assigned techs will install them in their new position the next morning.</p><p><strong>Once you accept the work order, if you have not completed installs for this client, for us, you will need to provide an email address and complete a certification quiz to prove you have read and understand the instructions. There will also be an invite sent for a training session on Teams so that my team can walk through the scope with you to insure you fully understand the scope and requirements. If both of these are not completed, you will be removed from the work order.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><p>• Upon accepting this work order, installer must provide an email address so that a teams meeting can be scheduled for a live training session, and after the session the tech will be provided with a link to a certification quiz that must be completed before arriving on site. If not completed prior to day of install you will not be permitted on site.</p><p>• This scope document must be printed off and brought with you. If you don't have it the manager will turn you away and you will not be paid for the day. The manager must sign off on this document to show that you brought it with you.</p><p>• Installer must also have either printed off install instructions with them, or loaded to a mobile device for review during the install.</p><p>• If the MOD feels that you have not properly reviewed the install guides and are not qualified for the install they have the authority to remove you from the site, so make sure you review the attached install guides and video links.</p><p>• Job will require basic hand tools to complete, there are a few specialty screwdrivers required and the store has these in their toolkit. You may use power tools to install devices, but final tightening must be done by hand to avoid over tightening so that the staff is able to remove devices for future change outs.</p><p>• Once you arrive on site, call your project manager to check in before walking into the store. Contact is James Thompson, 865-314-3958.</p><p>• After checking in with PM, check in with the on site manager. Explain that you are there to reinstall the Vanguard Security Devices. They will provide you with a planogram and show you where the devices have been stored during the reset. After this you may not ask the manager or store team any questions regarding the install steps.</p><p>• All other questions and issues must be addressed with your PM. So as you have questions, step outside and call James Thompson.</p><p>• Take before photos showing the provided devices and the tables you are directed to.</p><p>• Follow the planogram provided by the manager and adhere to the provided install guides/videos to install all devices.</p><p>• At each store there will be approximately 54 devices, the following devices are what to expect on average. The exact total will vary from store to store:</p><p>-<strong> Titan L2QD</strong>: 9 per store (Standard) 36-40 per store (High Security)</p><p>- https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-titan-l2qd/</p><p>- <strong>CR338</strong>: 34-37 per store (Standard), 6 per store (High Security)</p><p>- https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-cr361/</p><p>- <strong>Titan Watch</strong>: 7- 9 Per store - scan QR code in the install guide below</p><p>- <strong>Encores</strong>: 1 - 2 per store - https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-encore/</p><p>• Once all devices are installed, take photos of the tables showing completed work.</p><p>• Upload all photos, sign off sheet, and signed Scope of Work document.</p><p>• Call your PM to check out before leaving the site.</p><p><strong>Install Dates:</strong></p><p>The install dates are predetermined and are firm. You cannot change the date!</p><p><strong>Install Days/Hours:</strong></p><p>The install times are predetermined and are firm. You must be onsite at the scheduled time.</p><p><strong>Estimated Time On Site:</strong></p><p>4 to 6 hours - Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.</p><p><strong>Additional Information:</strong></p><p>1. The scope I provide is the most current information we have been provided and is subject to minor adjustments by the Project Manager as new information is received. The PM will provide you with the finalized information, and tell you what the communication, documentation, and photo requirements are for this assignment.</p><p>2. Please make sure you have all of the necessary tools/equipment needed for the assignment.</p><p>3. All deliverables (Before Photos, Completion Photos, and Sign Off) must be submitted in full and approved prior to being paid for the assignment.</p><p>4. Approximate Hours to Complete is an estimate based on past jobs of similar scope. Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.</p><p>5. Any fees for mileage or tolls need to be discussed and approved in advance or they will be denied.</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"The assignment is to install Vanguard security equipment and devices in a Verizon. **Each location will require two (2) installers.**\n\nThe Verizon team will be uninstalling items for a store reset the night before each phase, and the assigned techs will install them in their new position the next morning.\n\n**Once you accept the work order, if you have not completed installs for this client, for us, you will need to provide an email address and complete a certification quiz to prove you have read and understand the instructions. There will also be an invite sent for a training session on Teams so that my team can walk through the scope with you to insure you fully understand the scope and requirements. If both of these are not completed, you will be removed from the work order.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n• Upon accepting this work order, installer must provide an email address so that a teams meeting can be scheduled for a live training session, and after the session the tech will be provided with a link to a certification quiz that must be completed before arriving on site. If not completed prior to day of install you will not be permitted on site.\n\n• This scope document must be printed off and brought with you. If you don't have it the manager will turn you away and you will not be paid for the day. The manager must sign off on this document to show that you brought it with you.\n\n• Installer must also have either printed off install instructions with them, or loaded to a mobile device for review during the install.\n\n• If the MOD feels that you have not properly reviewed the install guides and are not qualified for the install they have the authority to remove you from the site, so make sure you review the attached install guides and video links.\n\n• Job will require basic hand tools to complete, there are a few specialty screwdrivers required and the store has these in their toolkit. You may use power tools to install devices, but final tightening must be done by hand to avoid over tightening so that the staff is able to remove devices for future change outs.\n\n• Once you arrive on site, call your project manager to check in before walking into the store. Contact is James Thompson, 865-314-3958.\n\n• After checking in with PM, check in with the on site manager. Explain that you are there to reinstall the Vanguard Security Devices. They will provide you with a planogram and show you where the devices have been stored during the reset. After this you may not ask the manager or store team any questions regarding the install steps.\n\n• All other questions and issues must be addressed with your PM. So as you have questions, step outside and call James Thompson.\n\n• Take before photos showing the provided devices and the tables you are directed to.\n\n• Follow the planogram provided by the manager and adhere to the provided install guides/videos to install all devices.\n\n• At each store there will be approximately 54 devices, the following devices are what to expect on average. The exact total will vary from store to store:\n\n\\- **Titan L2QD**: 9 per store (Standard) 36-40 per store (High Security)\n\n\\- <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-titan-l2qd/>\n\n\\- **CR338**: 34-37 per store (Standard), 6 per store (High Security)\n\n\\- <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-cr361/>\n\n\\- **Titan Watch**: 7- 9 Per store - scan QR code in the install guide below\n\n\\- **Encores**: 1 - 2 per store - <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-encore/>\n\n• Once all devices are installed, take photos of the tables showing completed work.\n\n• Upload all photos, sign off sheet, and signed Scope of Work document.\n\n• Call your PM to check out before leaving the site.\n\n**Install Dates:**\n\nThe install dates are predetermined and are firm. You cannot change the date!\n\n**Install Days/Hours:**\n\nThe install times are predetermined and are firm. You must be onsite at the scheduled time.\n\n**Estimated Time On Site:**\n\n4 to 6 hours - Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.\n\n**Additional Information:**\n\n1\\. The scope I provide is the most current information we have been provided and is subject to minor adjustments by the Project Manager as new information is received. The PM will provide you with the finalized information, and tell you what the communication, documentation, and photo requirements are for this assignment.\n\n2\\. Please make sure you have all of the necessary tools/equipment needed for the assignment.\n\n3\\. All deliverables (Before Photos, Completion Photos, and Sign Off) must be submitted in full and approved prior to being paid for the assignment.\n\n4\\. Approximate Hours to Complete is an estimate based on past jobs of similar scope. Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.\n\n5\\. Any fees for mileage or tolls need to be discussed and approved in advance or they will be denied.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T06:00","end":"2026-11-03T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":600,"max":600},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":44.3504752116396},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":120,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":5,"travelExpense":70,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T15:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T1