{"job":{"id":20025853,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Switch and Router Replacement 5817b","description":{"html":"<p><strong>U.S. ARMY RECRUITING DIVISION – ROUTER &amp; SWITCH UPGRADE</strong></p>\n<p>REQUEST TECHNICIAN PROFICIENT IN BROADBAND, ROUTER, SWITCH, AND INDUSTRY STANDARD TELECOMMUNICATIONS WIRING. TECH MUST PROVIDE ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIALS REQUIRED TO PERFORM THE WORK.</p>\n<p><strong>REQUEST:</strong> WORK WILL CONSIST OF SWAPPING THE EXISTING MERAKI ROUTER AND CISCO SWITCH(ES) WITH THE NEW EQUIPMENT AND CONNECTING CABLES AS SPECIFIED BY THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER.</p>\n<p>TECH TO BE ON SITE BETWEEN THE HOURS OF <strong>0900-1600 EST</strong> FOR SUPPORT.</p>\n<p>TECH SHALL LEAVE ALL OLD ROUTERS, SWITCHES, CABLES, ZOOM EQUIPMENT, AND ANY OTHER EQUIPMENT REMOVED OR ASKED TO BE TAKEN DOWN WITH THE ON-SITE POC.</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE MAKE CONTACT WITH THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER PRIOR TO BEGINNING ANY INSTALLATION OR DISCONNECTING ANY EXISTING NETWORK EQUIPMENT @ 928-998-9129. PLEASE PROVIDE THE NAME OF THE ENGINEER WORKED WITH IN THE CLOSEOUT NOTES.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>TECH SHALL NOTIFY THE ON-SITE POC PRIOR TO DISCONNECTING ANY NETWORK EQUIPMENT AND ADVISE THE POC THAT THE NETWORK WILL BE TEMPORARILY DOWN DURING THE ROUTER AND SWITCH UPGRADE.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>MERAKI MX68CW ROUTER UPGRADE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>TO BE INSTALLED:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1EA CISCO MERAKI MX68CW ROUTER</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>PLACE THE CISCO MERAKI MX68CW ON THE EXISTING NETWORK EQUIPMENT SHELF.</li>\n<li>REMOVE PLASTIC SLEEVES FROM WI-FI ANTENNAS AND ADJUST ANTENNAS AS NEEDED.</li>\n<li>MOVE ALL REQUIRED CABLES FROM THE LEGACY ERSN ROUTER TO THE MERAKI ROUTER.</li>\n<li>VERIFY CORRECT CABLING BASED ON THE FOLLOWING REAR PORT LAYOUT:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PORT 1 – WAB/INTERNET</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PORT 3 – PRINTER #1</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PORT 4 – PRINTER #2</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PORT 11 – WAP #1</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PORT 12 – WAP #2</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>VALIDATE CONNECTIVITY:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CONNECT TO RSN WIRELESS NETWORK</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CONNECT TO IKROME/RECRUITER ZONE</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">TEST PRINTING</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TECH TO TEST CONNECTIVITY WITH PRIMARY BROADBAND ENGINEER AND ENSURE MERAKI ROUTER IS FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>CISCO SWITCH LIFECYCLE UPGRADE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>TO BE INSTALLED:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>2EA CISCO 9300 SWITCH – 24 PORT</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>ATTACH INCLUDED MOUNTING BRACKETS AND MOUNT SWITCHES TO RACK. (SEE INSTRUCTIONS)</li>\n<li>INSTALL POWER SUPPLIES. (SEE INSTRUCTIONS)</li>\n<li>CONNECT NETWORK CABLES AS SPECIFIED BY THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER.</li>\n<li>VALIDATE CONNECTIVITY:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CONNECT TO DOD-NET WIRELESS NETWORK</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CONNECT TO RSN WIRED NETWORK</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CONNECT TO IKROME/RECRUITER ZONE</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">TEST PRINTING</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TECH TO TEST CONNECTIVITY WITH PRIMARY BROADBAND ENGINEER AND ENSURE SWITCHES ARE UP AND FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.</strong></p>\n<p>SIM CARD PROVIDER: T-MOBILE</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>CABLE MANAGEMENT AND ORGANIZATION</strong></p>\n<p>REQUEST TECH TO CLEAN-UP ASSOCIATED U.S. ARMY EQUIPMENT AND WIRING TO EXTREME PROFESSIONAL STANDARDS.</p>\n<p>TECH TO ORGANIZE ASSOCIATED U.S. ARMY EQUIPMENT, CABLE, AND EQUIPMENT IN A NEAT AND PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</p>\n<p>TECH TO DRESS ASSOCIATED CABLES TO BE NEAT, ORGANIZED, AND PROPERLY SECURED USING TIES, TIE MOUNTS, OR OTHER APPROPRIATE CABLE MANAGEMENT METHODS AS REQUIRED.</p>\n<p><strong>ONLY IF INSTRUCTED BY THE NMB TEAM</strong>, TECH TO REMOVE CABLES NOT IN USE AND REPLACE ANY RED CABLES OR PATCH CORDS.</p>\n<p><strong>REQUEST:</strong> TECHNICIAN TO LABEL CABLES TO IDENTIFY THE FOLLOWING CONNECTIONS:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>LINK TO RSN ROUTER (1)</li>\n<li>LINK TO BACKUP ROUTER (1)</li>\n<li>LINK TO IMO SWITCH (1)</li>\n<li>LINK TO WAPS (2-4)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED PHOTOS</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. BEFORE SETUP PICTURE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2. DATA PLATE WITH THE SERIAL NUMBER OF NEW EQUIPMENT TO BE INSTALLED</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3. REAR VIEW OF NEW SWITCH(ES) SHOWING POWER CABLES CONNECTED</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4. FRONT VIEW OF NEW SWITCH(ES) SHOWING CORRECT CABLES CONNECTED</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5. AFTER PICTURE TO VERIFY ALL WORK PERFORMED AS INSTRUCTED</strong></p>\n<p><strong>6. WIDE-ANGLE PHOTO OF THE FULL INSTALLATION ENVIRONMENT FOR OVERALL VERIFICATION</strong></p>\n<p>TECH TO TAKE DIGITAL PICTURES AT A RESOLUTION EQUAL TO OR BETTER THAN <strong>5 MEGAPIXELS</strong> IN <strong>JPEG FORMAT</strong>.</p>\n<p>TECH'S PICTURES SHALL BE CLEAR AND USABLE FOR REVIEW, INSPECTION, AND ACCEPTANCE OF SERVICES PERFORMED.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>GENERAL REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>ANY WORK OUTSIDE THE APPROVED SCOPE OF WORK REQUIRES PRIOR APPROVAL FROM USAREC G6 TELECOM.</li>\n<li>TECH SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PICKING UP ALL<strong>WORK-RELATED TRASH AND DEBRIS</strong> GENERATED DURING THE INSTALLATION AND DISPOSING OF IT OFF-SITE.</li>\n<li>TECH SHALL LEAVE ALL REMOVED EQUIPMENT DESIGNATED FOR THE POC AT THE SITE AND SHALL NOT DISPOSE OF OR REMOVE SUCH EQUIPMENT FROM THE SITE.</li>\n<li>ALL WORK TO BE PERFORMED IN A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</li>\n<li>TECH SHALL CONFIRM WITH THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER THAT ALL INSTALLED EQUIPMENT AND REQUIRED NETWORK SERVICES ARE FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**U.S. ARMY RECRUITING DIVISION – ROUTER & SWITCH UPGRADE**\n\nREQUEST TECHNICIAN PROFICIENT IN BROADBAND, ROUTER, SWITCH, AND INDUSTRY STANDARD TELECOMMUNICATIONS WIRING. TECH MUST PROVIDE ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIALS REQUIRED TO PERFORM THE WORK.\n\n**REQUEST:** WORK WILL CONSIST OF SWAPPING THE EXISTING MERAKI ROUTER AND CISCO SWITCH(ES) WITH THE NEW EQUIPMENT AND CONNECTING CABLES AS SPECIFIED BY THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER.\n\nTECH TO BE ON SITE BETWEEN THE HOURS OF **0900-1600 EST** FOR SUPPORT.\n\nTECH SHALL LEAVE ALL OLD ROUTERS, SWITCHES, CABLES, ZOOM EQUIPMENT, AND ANY OTHER EQUIPMENT REMOVED OR ASKED TO BE TAKEN DOWN WITH THE ON-SITE POC.\n\n**PLEASE MAKE CONTACT WITH THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER PRIOR TO BEGINNING ANY INSTALLATION OR DISCONNECTING ANY EXISTING NETWORK EQUIPMENT @ 928-998-9129. PLEASE PROVIDE THE NAME OF THE ENGINEER WORKED WITH IN THE CLOSEOUT NOTES.**\n\n**TECH SHALL NOTIFY THE ON-SITE POC PRIOR TO DISCONNECTING ANY NETWORK EQUIPMENT AND ADVISE THE POC THAT THE NETWORK WILL BE TEMPORARILY DOWN DURING THE ROUTER AND SWITCH UPGRADE.**\n\n**MERAKI MX68CW ROUTER UPGRADE**\n\n**TO BE INSTALLED:**\n\n- **1EA CISCO MERAKI MX68CW ROUTER**\n\n1. PLACE THE CISCO MERAKI MX68CW ON THE EXISTING NETWORK EQUIPMENT SHELF.\n2. REMOVE PLASTIC SLEEVES FROM WI-FI ANTENNAS AND ADJUST ANTENNAS AS NEEDED.\n3. MOVE ALL REQUIRED CABLES FROM THE LEGACY ERSN ROUTER TO THE MERAKI ROUTER.\n4. VERIFY CORRECT CABLING BASED ON THE FOLLOWING REAR PORT LAYOUT:\n\n- **PORT 1 – WAB/INTERNET**\n- **PORT 3 – PRINTER #1**\n- **PORT 4 – PRINTER #2**\n- **PORT 11 – WAP #1**\n- **PORT 12 – WAP #2**\n\n1. VALIDATE CONNECTIVITY:\n\n- CONNECT TO RSN WIRELESS NETWORK\n- CONNECT TO IKROME/RECRUITER ZONE\n- TEST PRINTING\n\n**TECH TO TEST CONNECTIVITY WITH PRIMARY BROADBAND ENGINEER AND ENSURE MERAKI ROUTER IS FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.**\n\n**CISCO SWITCH LIFECYCLE UPGRADE**\n\n**TO BE INSTALLED:**\n\n- **2EA CISCO 9300 SWITCH – 24 PORT**\n\n1. ATTACH INCLUDED MOUNTING BRACKETS AND MOUNT SWITCHES TO RACK. (SEE INSTRUCTIONS)\n2. INSTALL POWER SUPPLIES. (SEE INSTRUCTIONS)\n3. CONNECT NETWORK CABLES AS SPECIFIED BY THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER.\n4. VALIDATE CONNECTIVITY:\n\n- CONNECT TO DOD-NET WIRELESS NETWORK\n- CONNECT TO RSN WIRED NETWORK\n- CONNECT TO IKROME/RECRUITER ZONE\n- TEST PRINTING\n\n**TECH TO TEST CONNECTIVITY WITH PRIMARY BROADBAND ENGINEER AND ENSURE SWITCHES ARE UP AND FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.**\n\nSIM CARD PROVIDER: T-MOBILE\n\n**CABLE MANAGEMENT AND ORGANIZATION**\n\nREQUEST TECH TO CLEAN-UP ASSOCIATED U.S. ARMY EQUIPMENT AND WIRING TO EXTREME PROFESSIONAL STANDARDS.\n\nTECH TO ORGANIZE ASSOCIATED U.S. ARMY EQUIPMENT, CABLE, AND EQUIPMENT IN A NEAT AND PROFESSIONAL MANNER.\n\nTECH TO DRESS ASSOCIATED CABLES TO BE NEAT, ORGANIZED, AND PROPERLY SECURED USING TIES, TIE MOUNTS, OR OTHER APPROPRIATE CABLE MANAGEMENT METHODS AS REQUIRED.\n\n**ONLY IF INSTRUCTED BY THE NMB TEAM**, TECH TO REMOVE CABLES NOT IN USE AND REPLACE ANY RED CABLES OR PATCH CORDS.\n\n**REQUEST:** TECHNICIAN TO LABEL CABLES TO IDENTIFY THE FOLLOWING CONNECTIONS:\n\n- LINK TO RSN ROUTER (1)\n- LINK TO BACKUP ROUTER (1)\n- LINK TO IMO SWITCH (1)\n- LINK TO WAPS (2-4)\n\n**REQUIRED PHOTOS**\n\n**1. BEFORE SETUP PICTURE**\n\n**2. DATA PLATE WITH THE SERIAL NUMBER OF NEW EQUIPMENT TO BE INSTALLED**\n\n**3. REAR VIEW OF NEW SWITCH(ES) SHOWING POWER CABLES CONNECTED**\n\n**4. FRONT VIEW OF NEW SWITCH(ES) SHOWING CORRECT CABLES CONNECTED**\n\n**5. AFTER PICTURE TO VERIFY ALL WORK PERFORMED AS INSTRUCTED**\n\n**6. WIDE-ANGLE PHOTO OF THE FULL INSTALLATION ENVIRONMENT FOR OVERALL VERIFICATION**\n\nTECH TO TAKE DIGITAL PICTURES AT A RESOLUTION EQUAL TO OR BETTER THAN **5 MEGAPIXELS** IN **JPEG FORMAT**.\n\nTECH'S PICTURES SHALL BE CLEAR AND USABLE FOR REVIEW, INSPECTION, AND ACCEPTANCE OF SERVICES PERFORMED.\n\n**GENERAL REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- ANY WORK OUTSIDE THE APPROVED SCOPE OF WORK REQUIRES PRIOR APPROVAL FROM USAREC G6 TELECOM.\n- TECH SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PICKING UP ALL**WORK-RELATED TRASH AND DEBRIS** GENERATED DURING THE INSTALLATION AND DISPOSING OF IT OFF-SITE.\n- TECH SHALL LEAVE ALL REMOVED EQUIPMENT DESIGNATED FOR THE POC AT THE SITE AND SHALL NOT DISPOSE OF OR REMOVE SUCH EQUIPMENT FROM THE SITE.\n- ALL WORK TO BE PERFORMED IN A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.\n- TECH SHALL CONFIRM WITH THE NMB/BROADBAND ENGINEER THAT ALL INSTALLED EQUIPMENT AND REQUIRED NETWORK SERVICES ARE FULLY OPERATIONAL BEFORE LEAVING SITE.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-10T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":325},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":11.73189810442892},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $325 (countered: $325) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},