{"job":{"id":20168679,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"NBT: 854409 - Diagnose and Repair (Zebra - 220Xi4) Thermal Barcode Label Printer.  NOT RECEIPT PRINTERS!","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Please bring a laptop with you onsite; they are considered an essential tool for all onsite repairs.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\">﻿PLEASE NOTE: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\">These printers are about the size of a tower PC and about 60 pounds in weight. They are not inkjet or laser printers, nor are they coupon/receipt printers. This is also not a printer “hot swap,” but </span><u style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\">requires</u><span style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\"> repair experience. The expectation from our customers (and from us) is that you have a working knowledge of the printer and would only call into tech support if all your known troubleshooting steps are exhausted.</span></p><p><strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION below has been updated. Please read and understand once work order is assigned to you.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>W/O#&nbsp;</strong>854409&nbsp;</p><p><strong>S/N: </strong>17J170400503</p><p><strong>Problem Description: </strong>Contract/SLA: 10/12 - This printer seems to have a NIC that is not functional. Have tested current LAN port with other printers. Also, connected printer to another known working LAN port.</p><p><strong>SLA: 10/12</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&gt;&gt; Technician will be responsible for calling the point of contact (POC) listed on the Field Service Report (uploaded under Client Documents). <strong>You must speak to a live person and confirm the ETA; leaving a voicemail will not suffice as a confirmed ETA. </strong><u>If you are having difficulties reaching a live person, please call or message Dispatch and we will ask them to call you.</u></p><p>To Check In or Check Out, please call Dispatch at 864-635-0351, <strong>in addition to </strong>checking in and out on the platform.</p><p>For Tech Support, please call <span style=\"color: black;\">864-635-0352 </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">BEFORE LEAVING SITE. </strong>If you are onsite over 1.5 hours, you must call NewBold tech support (864-635-0352)</p><p><strong><u>Techs will need to return any new, unused parts to NewBold -- and the RMA closed by the warehouse -- before payment can be approved. DO NOT RETURN USED/BAD PARTS!</u></strong></p><p><strong>Penalties will be applied as follows:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Not calling the POC before going onsite (but allowed to fix printer) = $10.00 </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Not calling the POC before going onsite and gets turned away = No Pay for that trip</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Not calling Dispatch to check in and check out of a site = $10.00</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Missing test prints/config printout/PH test/etc = $10.00 </span></li><li>Going o<span style=\"color: black;\">ver 24 hours (working days) without submitting completed paperwork = $10.00 </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Forgetting laptop, firmware, or any other tools = No pay on return trip</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Forgetting to take photos of damaged parts = </span> <span style=\"color: black;\">$10.00 </span></li></ul>","markdown":"**Please bring a laptop with you onsite; they are considered an essential tool for all onsite repairs.**\n\n**﻿PLEASE NOTE:** These printers are about the size of a tower PC and about 60 pounds in weight. They are not inkjet or laser printers, nor are they coupon/receipt printers. This is also not a printer “hot swap,” but requires repair experience. The expectation from our customers (and from us) is that you have a working knowledge of the printer and would only call into tech support if all your known troubleshooting steps are exhausted.\n\n**CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION below has been updated. Please read and understand once work order is assigned to you.**\n\n**W/O#** 854409\n\n**S/N:** 17J170400503\n\n**Problem Description:** Contract/SLA: 10/12 - This printer seems to have a NIC that is not functional. Have tested current LAN port with other printers. Also, connected printer to another known working LAN port.\n\n**SLA: 10/12**\n\n\\>> Technician will be responsible for calling the point of contact (POC) listed on the Field Service Report (uploaded under Client Documents). **You must speak to a live person and confirm the ETA; leaving a voicemail will not suffice as a confirmed ETA.** If you are having difficulties reaching a live person, please call or message Dispatch and we will ask them to call you.\n\nTo Check In or Check Out, please call Dispatch at 864-635-0351, **in addition to** checking in and out on the platform.\n\nFor Tech Support, please call 864-635-0352 **BEFORE LEAVING SITE.** If you are onsite over 1.5 hours, you must call NewBold tech support (864-635-0352)\n\n**Techs will need to return any new, unused parts to NewBold -- and the RMA closed by the warehouse -- before payment can be approved. DO NOT RETURN USED/BAD PARTS!**\n\n**Penalties will be applied as follows:**\n\n- Not calling the POC before going onsite (but allowed to fix printer) = $10.00\n- Not calling the POC before going onsite and gets turned away = No Pay for that trip\n- Not calling Dispatch to check in and check out of a site = $10.00\n- Missing test prints/config printout/PH test/etc = $10.00\n- Going over 24 hours (working days) without submitting completed paperwork = $10.00\n- Forgetting laptop, firmware, or any other tools = No pay on return trip\n- Forgetting to take photos of damaged parts =  $10.00","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T09:00","end":"2026-10-15T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-15T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":205,"max":205},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2