{"job":{"id":"4937029149","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Starlink Survey + Installation (BRING 15' EXTENSION LADDER) (HARD START TIME)","description":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong>*IF A LIFT IS REQUIRED, TECHNICIAN MUST HAVE LIFT EXPERIENCE AND MUST BE CERTIFIED* </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must have Valid ID for Site Access.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>TECH APP REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><p><strong>• MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch. A link will be sent via text message.</strong></p><p><strong>• If you do not receive the link, visit </strong><a href=\"https://dispatch.bruin.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"><strong>https://dispatch.bruin.com/</strong></a><strong> to manually look up and start the dispatch.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>This work order is to perform a site survey to assess Installation requirements for a<strong> Starlink Satellite System </strong>plus execute the installation during a single dispatch. Tech to survey mounting location, cable pathway, and overall feasibility.</p><p><br></p><p>MetTel will be providing the <strong>Peak Sled Mount</strong> for this site. <strong>Tech <u>MUST </u>bring 4 Cinderblocks &amp; a 15' Extension Ladder.</strong> The technician is expected to assess that the mount sent is appropriate based on site conditions and install accordingly.<strong> <u>If the mount is NOT viable, the technician must contact ServicePoint TAC immediately to review the situation. TAC will bridge MetTel into the call to review the findings and determine next steps.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If the installation can be completed during the same visit—based on site conditions, scope alignment, and available materials—the technician is authorized to proceed with the installation upon confirmation. In this case, the job will be treated as a full installation, and tech will be compensated accordingly.<u> If installation cannot be completed on this visit (helper or lift needed, different mount required, misc materials needed, etc) this visit will be treated and compensated as a survey only with a future revisit for the install.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>• Starlink will connect to SD-WAN.</p><p>• If unable to complete the installation on this visit, the technician is to perform a Site Survey.</p><p><br></p><p>Starlink KIT: KIT4P00119084KM8 Tracking:</p><p>• Package 1: 383739087955</p><p>• Package 2: 383739089086</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Installation Details:</u></strong></p><p>• ServicePoint was not contracted to perform a site survey before this installation.</p><p>• If the installation cannot be completed during this dispatch, the technician is to perform a Site Survey.</p><p>• Install a Starlink Performance Gen 3 Satellite System.</p><p>• Peak Sled Mount will be provided for the installation.</p><p>• This is a 1-floor brick structure.</p><p>• Identify a suitable mounting location for the Starlink antenna.</p><p>• Evaluate the installation area for a clear FOV (Field of View) to ensure optimal signal.</p><p>• Do not perform roof penetrations.</p><p>• Side-wall penetration may be performed if required.</p><p>• Evaluate existing penetration points first and use/enlarge existing points when possible, provided doing so does not risk building or existing cable damage.</p><p>• Assess the cable distance to the DMARC/Network Closet to determine the appropriate cable pathway and power requirements.</p><p>• If the network closet is in a different location than the DMARC, determine the required distance for the DMARC extension.</p><p>• Before clearing the site, work with the client support center to validate that the Starlink system is installed and functioning correctly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Installation Requirements:</u></strong></p><p>• Starlink Performance Gen 3 Dish</p><p>• Peak Sled Mount</p><p>• 1 technician</p><p>• 15 ft extension ladder</p><p>• Standard installation tools</p><p>• Cinder blocks</p><p>• Cable clips</p><p>• Silicone sealant</p><p><br></p><p>1. Cable Pathway Installation Evaluation:</p><p>• Expected to meet the supplied OEM cable distance.</p><p>• The total pathway from the antenna to the DMARC/Network Closet must remain within the supplied OEM cable length.</p><p>• If there is not a reliable and clean power option within the OEM cable distance, the end user will be responsible for providing the required power.</p><p>• An extension may be required from the DMARC to the MDF/Network Closet if the DMARC and MDF/Network Closet are in different locations.</p><p>• Verify the cable pathway during installation.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Mount Type:</p><p>• Proposed Mounting Solution: Peak Sled Mount (TECH MUST BRING 4 CINDERBLOCKS)</p><p>• Install the Starlink Performance Gen 3 dish using the Peak Sled Mount.</p><p>• Evaluate the placement of the mount to ensure a clear FOV (Field of View) for optimal signal.</p><p>• This is a 1-floor brick structure.</p><p>• Ensure the mount is properly secured for the site conditions.</p><p>• Cinder blocks may be used as required for the Peak Sled Mount.</p><p><br></p><p>3. Penetration Needed: Will Evaluate During Installation Visit</p><p>• Do not perform roof penetrations.</p><p>• Evaluate existing penetration points first.</p><p>• Existing penetration points may be enlarged if doing so does not create a risk of building damage or damage to existing cables.</p><p>• Side-wall penetration points will be evaluated to determine the best location for cables/power to enter the building and provide connectivity for the Starlink system.</p><p>• If a side-wall penetration is required, ensure the penetration is properly sealed after installation.</p><p>• Seal the penetration with appropriate silicone sealant.</p><p>• Create a drip loop near the point of entry to prevent water from entering the building through the cable entry point.</p><p><br></p><p>4. Conduit Run Required: NO</p><p>• No conduit run is currently required.</p><p>• Conduit may be required if site conditions determine that additional cable protection is necessary.</p><p>• Notify the appropriate project contact if conduit is determined to be necessary during installation.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Cable Extension Required: NO</p><p>• Estimated Distance: 50–100 FT</p><p>• No cable extension is currently required.</p><p>• Verify the actual cable pathway during installation.</p><p>• Maintain the cable within the supplied OEM cable distance.</p><p>• Create a drip loop near the point of entry.</p><p>• Ensure water cannot flow into the building through the cable entry point.</p><p>• Seal the entry point with appropriate silicone sealant.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Personnel and Equipment:</u></strong></p><p>1. Number of Technicians Required:</p><p>• 1 Engineer</p><p>• Estimated Time: 3–4 Hours</p><p><br></p><p>2. Ladder/Lift Requirements:</p><p>• Ladder Type Required: 15 FT Extension Ladder</p><p><br></p><p>3. Safety Gear:</p><p>• Technician must wear appropriate safety gear while working on site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>4. Additional Materials — TECH TO PROVIDE:</strong></p><p><strong>• Cable Clips (20 Pack)</strong></p><p><strong>• Cinder Blocks (4)</strong></p><p><strong>• Silicone Sealant</strong></p><p><strong>• 15 FT Extension Ladder</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Under no circumstances should the technician leave site until formally released by both ServicePoint TAC and MetTel.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope Details:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Arrival and Site Check-In:</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive on site at the scheduled time and check in with ServicePoint TAC and on-site contact.</li><li>Verify all Starlink and SD-WAN equipment has been received and matches the provided inventory list.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Starlink Survey + Possible Installation:</strong></p><ul><li>Review the provided mounting option from MetTel.</li><li>Select and install the most suitable mount based on site conditions.</li><li>If mount type is NOT viable, contact ServicePoint TAC immediately for guidance.</li><li>Mount and align the Starlink dish ensuring optimal signal strength. Ensure dish is facing either North or Northwest.</li><li>Route and secure the Starlink cabling to the designated equipment location (MDF or IDF as applicable).</li><li>Connect the Starlink power supply and network interface to the designated router or SD-WAN device.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Testing:</strong></p><ul><li>Follow MetTel’s direction during testing and verification.</li><li>Confirm connectivity, speed, and redundancy meet the expected performance metrics.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Completion and Sign-Off:</strong></p><ul><li>Remain on site until both ServicePoint TAC and MetTel confirm all testing is complete and the site is fully operational.</li><li>Obtain verbal and/or written release from both TAC and MetTel prior to leaving site.</li><li>Submit photos of installation, any test results, and completion notes per standard ServicePoint procedures. Make sure sign off sheet is completed fully and signed by LCON.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Release Condition:</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Technician is not authorized to leave site until ServicePoint TAC and MetTel confirm release.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please note that ServicePoint TAC will be reaching out throughout the techs time onsite to request updates. Please be professional as this is a request from our customer.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong></p><p><strong>**DO NOT EVER PENETRATE THROUGH THE ROOF - IF PENETRATION IS REQUIRED, WILL BE THROUGH THE SIDE WALL**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>15' Extension Ladder</strong></li><li><strong>Fully Charged Laptop w/Ethernet Port</strong></li><li><strong>Cinderblocks (REQUIRED FOR SLED MOUNT): 4</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Clips (20 Pack)</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone Sealant</strong></li><li>Drill w/ assortment of bits (Sheetrock, Wood, Concrete,etc)</li><li>Smart Phone with Hot Spot functionality</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>Cat5e patch cables for testing</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Cat5e cable tester</li><li>Toner and wand</li><li>150ft Cat5e cable</li><li>RJ45 modular ends&nbsp;</li><li>Safety Gear: The technicians will wear appropriate safety gear while working on the site.</li></ul><p><strong><em>**Technician is responsible for purchasing this and will be reimbursed for this expense with a receipt.**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>TECH MUST REVIEW SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS ONCE ASSIGNED</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to four hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $40 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are being dispatched to perform a site survey. If only the survey is completed, technicians will be compensated at the agreed-upon survey rate.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>If the survey transitions into a full installation during the same visit, technicians may proceed upon approval and will be compensated at the pre-approved installation rate for the full scope of work. </em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>If installation work is performed, the applicable installation rate will replace the survey rate for that visit and technician will be expected to add their increase within 24 hours of successful completion. If total onsite time exceeds the standard duration included in the agreed rate, additional time will be compensated at $50 per hour unless otherwise specified.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment.&nbsp;All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All travel must be request prior to Service Point accepting offer. If travel is requested after job has been completed, it will be declined. </em></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.&nbsp;If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T09:45","end":"2026-10-26T13:45"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":5.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"00736638 - ATT DC Decom"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792080144972}
