{"job":{"id":20179318,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"GAP - Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 8<del>**********</del>0, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>SOW: Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable</p>\n<p>Switch (S/n: Q3LM-W53C-Z7AP) is located inside the manager's office.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (sw01) : port 05.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>When on site, check in with Store Network at 1-800-869-8490</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.</p>\n<p>If any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.</p>\n<p>If we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.</p>\n<p>To reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>After performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>For more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>Basic Tools</p>\n<p>working laptop with the updated driver</p>\n<p>Console Cables</p>\n<p>Cat5 Cable</p>\n<p>Cable tester</p>\n<p>Internet dongle</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>While Onsite:</p>\n<p>- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Checkout Requirements:</p>\n<p>-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)</p>\n<p>-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Deliverables:</p>\n<p>-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com</p>\n<p>-MOD email for Survey</p>","markdown":"Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 8\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*0, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:\n\nSOW: Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting\n\nPlease ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable\n\nSwitch (S/n: Q3LM-W53C-Z7AP) is located inside the manager's office.\n\nTech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (sw01) : port 05.\n\nWhen on site, check in with Store Network at 1-800-869-8490\n\nTech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.\n\nTech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.\n\nIf any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.\n\nIf we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.\n\nIf the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.\n\nIf there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.\n\nTo reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.\n\nAfter performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions\n\nFor more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nBasic Tools\n\nworking laptop with the updated driver\n\nConsole Cables\n\nCat5 Cable\n\nCable tester\n\nInternet dongle\n\nCheck In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.\n\nWhile Onsite:\n\n\\- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2\n\nCheckout Requirements:\n\n-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)\n\n-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com\n\n-MOD email for Survey","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T11:00","end":"2026-10-16T15:00","latestStart":"2026-10-16T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12.23279659568661},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (12.23279659568661mi reported + 10mi padding = 22.232796595686608mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"