rds AP\n\n**Site Address**: - 2 TW Alexander Drive, Research Triangle Park, 27709, United States of America\n\n**Local POC Detail**: -\n\nName : Todd Thornton\n\nMobile: : +1-919-706-2178\n\n**FE should carry:**\n\n FE Mandatory Equipment: Standard : Datacard ( mobile data ) + mobile phone\n\nConsole cable+laptop ( with admin account and a full version of Microsoft teams)\n\n **Note: A one-line visit report will not be accepted. The Field Engineer must provide a detailed site visit report covering all activities completed, any pending items, issues encountered, and the status. The report must be shared with the team before the FE leaves the site.**\n\n **FE Mandatory Equipment:**\n\n Safety Equipment - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety glasses, long sleeved shirt, long ...\n\n**Safety Equipment -** Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety glasses, long sleeved shirt, long ...\n\nField Engineer Access - Field engineer allowed, pre-registration required\n\nHardware In/Out - To be communicated to site access contact and instructions will be provided\n\nTechnical Contact - Christy Morgan\n\nRegistration Information - Engineer details to be provided in advance to site access contact\n\nRequired Documents - BASF Background Check, Proof of Drugs\n\nPhotography Allowed - Allowed, network devices only\n\n**Questions to Confirm Before Visit:**\n\n· Is the FE able to communicate basic in Local Language along with English?\n\n· Is the FE travelling by Public Transport or Private Car?\n\n· If travelling by Public Transport, please share the mode of transport with total travel time.\n\n**Special Remarks, Notices and Reminders :**\n\n· Engineer must be dressed in business casual attire with proper footwear (Full-sleeve shirt, long trousers, Closed shoes).\n\n· Engineer must carry basic Safety PPE Equipment Kit - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety glasses, earplugs)\n\n· Engineer must bring: Data card (mobile data) or Internet Dongle, Mobile phone, Console cable, Laptop (with admin account), and Label printer.\n\n· Regarding laptop, Engineer must confirm it is an Opensource Company-provided laptop if been asked by POC or Remote team onsite.\n\n· Engineer must join using the Teams credentials provided by FNG, not their personal account. In case of any issues, please contact the FNG Service Desk Team.\n\n· Engineer must carry a valid government ID card for site access.\n\n· Engineer must not mention being a freelancer or contractor. They must introduce themselves as FNG employees or direct contractors.\n\n· If travelling by Public Transport, Engineer must not discuss anything about it with the Local POC.\n\n· Engineer must contact the POC upon arrival. If not able to reach POC, escalate immediately to your leadership team and inform FNG.\n\n· Engineer must not leave site until all work is approved by FNG internally and the Remote Team at Tech Mahindra.\n\n· Engineer must ensure the FE Report is signed by the POC confirming the work completion (unless unavailable).\n\n· BASF Client is very sensitive – Engineer must not discuss anything apart from work-related communication while they are onsite","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-16T11:00","end":"2026-10-16T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":20.43137912421468},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":40,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T19:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.00