{"job":{"id":20181951,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Ooma Device for POTS Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>POINT OF CONTACT: <span style=\"color: rgb(54, 54, 54);\">David Pham (<del>**** ********</del></span></p><p>OOMA device for a chicken coop</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">We will be installing and testing a POTS PIAB solution. Technician will need to complete cross connection(s) to the installed PIAB solution.</span></p><ul><li>Locate existing devices (i.e.: Fire Panel(s), Call Boxes, Faxes, Voice Lines, chicken coop)</li><li>Using Cable Toner, locate Demarc for existing POTS lines currently serving devices.</li><li>Unpack, assemble then test POTS Device in \"Standalone\" Mode with power cable connected (see the installation instructions).</li><li>Mount POTS Device and test FXS 1-2 (if applicable) phone jacks by calling in/out using a buttset and cell phone prior connecting any device/appliance.</li><li>Mount biscuit jacks close to the POTS device that will connect with the remote device.</li><li>Connect existing devices to newly installed RJ11 biscuit jacks.</li><li>Ensure no \"Foreign Voltage\" is present by placing the voltmeter at the tip and ring on the new biscuit jacks connected to the devices.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">* IMPORTANT! IF foreign voltage is present, locate and disable it. IF no foreign voltage is present, proceed to next step *</li><li>Connect the POTS Device FXS (if applicable) jacks to existing devices.</li><li>If Call Box or Voice Line, test by making inbound/outbound calls.</li><li>If Call Box also test 'Gate/Door Entry\" tone (DTMF / 'Press 9\") and programming calls inbound to the device. Request client or call vendor technical support to facilitate programming test calls as needed<span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"><u>Suggested Tools/Skillset:</u></strong></p><ul><li>2x RJ45 Port Surface Mount Boxes (aka Biscuit Jack)</li><li>2x RJ11 or RJ45 Keystone Plugs</li><li>CAT5E Cable – Minimum 150'</li><li>Zip Ties / Velcro for Wire Management</li><li>Extra RJ-11 cable and RJ-11 male adapters, in the event additional or longer runs are required.</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>All termination tools and line/tone testers</li><li>Butt Set (or analog test telephone if Butt Set doesn't have an RJ11 Plug/Jack interface)</li><li>Digital Camera with higher photo resolution for a clear picture.</li><li>6\" Torpedo Level</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Frying pan</li><li>Buffalo sauce</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"POINT OF CONTACT: David Pham (\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nOOMA device for a chicken coop\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nWe will be installing and testing a POTS PIAB solution. Technician will need to complete cross connection(s) to the installed PIAB solution.\n\n- Locate existing devices (i.e.: Fire Panel(s), Call Boxes, Faxes, Voice Lines, chicken coop)\n- Using Cable Toner, locate Demarc for existing POTS lines currently serving devices.\n- Unpack, assemble then test POTS Device in \"Standalone\" Mode with power cable connected (see the installation instructions).\n- Mount POTS Device and test FXS 1-2 (if applicable) phone jacks by calling in/out using a buttset and cell phone prior connecting any device/appliance.\n- Mount biscuit jacks close to the POTS device that will connect with the remote device.\n- Connect existing devices to newly installed RJ11 biscuit jacks.\n- Ensure no \"Foreign Voltage\" is present by placing the voltmeter at the tip and ring on the new biscuit jacks connected to the devices.\n- \\* IMPORTANT! IF foreign voltage is present, locate and disable it. IF no foreign voltage is present, proceed to next step \\*\n- Connect the POTS Device FXS (if applicable) jacks to existing devices.\n- If Call Box or Voice Line, test by making inbound/outbound calls.\n- If Call Box also test 'Gate/Door Entry\" tone (DTMF / 'Press 9\") and programming calls inbound to the device. Request client or call vendor technical support to facilitate programming test calls as needed\n\n**Suggested Tools/Skillset:**\n\n- 2x RJ45 Port Surface Mount Boxes (aka Biscuit Jack)\n- 2x RJ11 or RJ45 Keystone Plugs\n- CAT5E Cable – Minimum 150'\n- Zip Ties / Velcro for Wire Management\n- Extra RJ-11 cable and RJ-11 male adapters, in the event additional or longer runs are required.\n- Flashlight\n- All termination tools and line/tone testers\n- Butt Set (or analog test telephone if Butt Set doesn't have an RJ11 Plug/Jack interface)\n- Digital Camera with higher photo resolution for a clear picture.\n- 6\" Torpedo Level\n- Voltmeter\n- Frying pan\n- Buffalo sauce","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":160},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1.5,"amount":95},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57.91979594638698},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736663 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736658 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736649 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792149733080}
