{"job":{"id":20197947,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pomeroy","title":"Replace an Intel NUC (Media Player) on a LED Wall","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of work: Replace an Intel NUC on a LED Wall</p><p>Tech will need to bring an HDMI cable in case it is needed for the install</p><p>Tech will need to check in with the coordinator</p><p>Tech will need to remove the old device and install the new device</p><p>Tech will need to take pictures of the bottom of the old device AND of the new device and send to coordinator</p><p>Tech will need to work with the coordinator to get content displaying on the screen correctly</p><p>Tech will need to send pictures to the coordinator</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Once all of this has been completed, tech will need to check out with coordinator to make sure everything is correct before leaving the store</span></p>","markdown":"Scope of work: Replace an Intel NUC on a LED Wall\n\nTech will need to bring an HDMI cable in case it is needed for the install\n\nTech will need to check in with the coordinator\n\nTech will need to remove the old device and install the new device\n\nTech will need to take pictures of the bottom of the old device AND of the new device and send to coordinator\n\nTech will need to work with the coordinator to get content displaying on the screen correctly\n\nTech will need to send pictures to the coordinator\n\nOnce all of this has been completed, tech will need to check out with coordinator to make sure everything is correct before leaving the store","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T11:00","end":"2026-10-20T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":135},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":43.00312772512563},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 21, 2:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $135\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792420419889}
{"job":{"id":20197213,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Assist Lead tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>Assist Lead technician</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>WIN10 Laptop – with Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone - with Charger</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit</li>\n<li>Black Ink Pens - for documentation</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Background check required</li>\n<li>Check-in with site contacts</li>\n<li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Data Center Do's and Don'ts</strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Do:</strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Follow all safety protocols&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)</li>\n<li>Wear comfortable, layered clothing.</li>\n<li>Communicate proactively</li>\n<li>Maintain a clean workspace</li>\n<li>Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.</li>\n<li>No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering&nbsp;approved area</li>\n<li>ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands</li>\n<li>If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Don’t:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.</li>\n<li>Don’t remove any cables. The&nbsp;<del>******</del>&nbsp;certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.</li>\n<li>Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)</li>\n<li>No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...</li>\n<li>No Hitch Hiking on badge scans&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Do not prop doors or cages open</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Scope:**\n\n  \n  \nAssist Lead technician\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n  \n  \n- WIN10 Laptop – with Charger\n- Smartphone - with Charger\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Black Ink Pens - for documentation\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check required\n- Check-in with site contacts\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n\n  \n  \n**Data Center Do's and Don'ts**\n\n  \n  \n**Do:**\n\n  \n  \n- Follow all safety protocols\n- Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)\n- Wear comfortable, layered clothing.\n- Communicate proactively\n- Maintain a clean workspace\n- Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.\n- No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering approved area\n- ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands\n- If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Don’t:**\n\n  \n  \n- Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.\n- Don’t remove any cables. The \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.\n- Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)\n- No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...\n- No Hitch Hiking on badge scans\n- Do not prop doors or cages open","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T10:30","end":"2026-10-20T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":60},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":30,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.68755983414495},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.