r general questions.</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations,&nbsp;or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:</li><li><del>*********</del><del>***</del>&nbsp;|&nbsp;Compliance@ClearCaptions.com</li><li>&nbsp;All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator,&nbsp;or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website:&nbsp;https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TROUBLESHOOTING</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span> for any issues, and/or to report and solution a phone's failure to auto update</li><li><u>For Cat5 Set-ups</u>: Plug the end of the Cat 5 Ethernet cable with the ferrite box into the phone</li><li>VoIP-PSTN Conversion Guide: Located in Additional Information &gt; Attached Files</li></ul>","markdown":"**Join us in making an impact! ClearCaptions is dedicated to helping customers live a more independent life by connecting them to their loved ones via a captioned phone.**\n\nWork order is located in a RESIDENTIAL SETTING with HARD-OF-HEARING and/or ELDERLY CUSTOMERS.\n\n- Patience, empathy, and kindness are paramount.\n- Thorough, hands-on customer training is imperative to the successful completion of this work order.\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\n**Before Site Visit:** *Approximately 30 minutes*\n\n- Review all work order details, execute 24-hour advance customer courtesy call/text/voicemail, re-familiarize self on installation process via guidance material.\n- Phone kit will be onsite (kit does NOT include additional required tools listed).\n\n**At Site Visit:** *Approximately 1.25 - 2 hours*\n\n- Your Objective: Customer is satisfied and able to use the fully operational phone independently and confidently by the time you leave site.\n- PHASE 1 - Customer Registration: *Approximately 15-30 minutes*\n- Register and validate customer's identity, then unpack and set-up their phone. Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.\n- PHASE 2 - Phone Set-up: *Approximately 15-30 minutes*\n- Unpack and set-up customer's phone, in desired and effective location\n- Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.\n- PHASE 3 - Customer Training: *Approximately 45-60 minutes*\n- Once customer registration, identity validation and phone installation are complete, the remainder of your visit should focus on training the customer to use their new phone with confidence and satisfaction.\n- This includes but is not limited to: placing and receiving test calls, adding contacts, setting up voicemail and/or connecting their current service, configuring their settings, and connecting them to ClearCaptions for the required Welcome Call.\n- **Additional site-visit callouts**:\n\n%description.html%\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES & EXPECTATIONS**\n\n**Assignment:**\n\n- ***DO NOT send or bring any unauthorized persons to the customer's home****,* including those part of a service company. Only the tech assigned to the WO is allowed onsite.\n\n**Visit Preparation:**\n\n- Review the work order details and acknowledge (in Tasks) the guidance material attached to the work order to ensure a successful visit.\n- ***Download and reference the Installation Checklist for detailed, step-by-step set-up requirements and customer training best practice*.**\n- The easy to read, flip through Phone Guide for training the customer can be found here: **<https://rb.gy/i4mdjy>** (PDF version for print or download is Documents section of the work order.)\n- Dress Code: Clean and presentable business casual attire. Slacks or jeans (no holes/patches), closed-toed shoes, and a polo shirt. No hats.\n\n**Scheduling & Arrival:**\n\n- ClearCaptions does not accept Technician requests to reschedule, as the hard start time has been coordinated with the end customer. If required for an unexpected reason, tech must Report a Problem on the work order selecting “I Can’t Make My Assignment”. This enables ClearCaptions to attempt re-assignment without impacting our customer.\n- ***Technician must proceed to installation appointment as scheduled even if a customer does not respond to the required 24-hour advance courtesy call or their number is \"disconnected\"****.* Customers are hard or hearing so may not realize you attempted to call until they have their new phone and ClearCaptions service.\n- Check-in + Check-out must be within 1 mile of site.\n- ***You will be able to access the Customer Information when you are ON SITE and checked in*.**\n- ***Please arrive at start time of WO***. Too early or too late can disrupt the customer and the ability to complete the WO. We will not approve requests to edit time logs.\n- If customer is not home and not reachable ***after 15 min of hard start time****,* to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site, or to report that an installation cannot be completed in full for any reason: call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. You must garner ClearCaptions' permission to leave site to allow for customer coordination, incomplete troubleshooting, and prevent rescheduling where reasonable.\n\n**When on Site:**\n\n- The correct customer must be present for the entirety of the install (the registered user is listed under the Location Contact in this WO).\n- ***Using your own or a customer's cellular 'hotspot' to connect a customer's phone to internet is strictly prohibited. Dedicated home internet service is required for caption service. Home internet is acceptable if delivered via a cellular network, and shared internet in assisted/group living facilities will suffice if/when connectivity speeds are sufficient.***\n- ***Do not mount the phone and/or create any structural changes while onsite, even if customer requests it*.** This includes, but is not limited to: drilling holes, running cables.\n- If an installation cannot be completed in full and/or is cancelled for specific reasons ClearCaptions will confirm return requirements. Call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for further directions and use the pre-paid mailing label included in the phone kit box. Remember to enter this tracking number from the label into the Custom Field: \"Return Tracking Number\", as necessary.\n- Customer's ***Username and Password*** are located under Buyer Custom Fields in the Work Order. If this information is not viewable ensure you are correctly checked in onsite and call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n- If a Technician encounters any threatening behavior from customer, caregiver, or persons on site upon arrival or during the site visit, they must use their judgement to leave the premise. Once in safety, please contact ClearCaptions Support immediately thereafter to report at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n**Technician Payment:**\n\n- The fixed rate is inclusive of the full scope.\n- All travel charges must be pre-approved via a counter offer prior to assignment and back-up receipts required at close out. We do not honor requests for travel expenses after assignment.\n- Expenses for tools/equipment must be requested with an uploaded receipt.\n- ***Requesting or accepting any form of payment directly from a customer is in direct violation of ClearCaptions and FN Terms & Conditions, and will result in further escalation*.**\n- ***Use of \"Discounts\" feature to adjust pay is prohibited.*** Please document any issues under “Report a Problem” from the Work Order for proper review and adjustments.\n\n**EXPECTATIONS & REQUIREMENTS FOR FULL PAYMENT**\n\n1. Registration and Consent Completed: Facilitate customer in completing registration and signing required consent documentation via Customer Portal. Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.\n2. Customer ID Validation Passed: Facilitate customer in completing identity validation in our Customer Portal (“DMS”). Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.\n3. Paired Phone: Customer’s device is installed in accordance with work order guidelines (VoIP or PSTN) and connected (paired) for captioning functionality. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n4. Welcome Call Completed: Facilitate customer with dialing into required line and associated case closed. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n5. Customer Training: Training executed in full and customer demonstrates clear understanding and usage competency. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n6. Work Order Task Completion: All required work order tasks are completed fully and accurately.\n\n**CUSTOMER IDENTITY VALIDATION & CONSENT**\n\n- Please note that identity validation protocol is to be conducted and registration consents signed by customer via ClearCaptions' Portal outside of the in-phone set-up to gain consent and validate the customer's identity, as required by the FCC. Link provided in Task list.\n- ***ONLY THE CUSTOMER can accept terms and consent. DO NOT consent on the customer's behalf***; doing so is against compliance policy and will result in non-payment, being blocked by ClearCaptions, and filing a report to Field Nation Resolution for review. If at any point the customer expresses concern over the service, to request a copy of what they signed, or to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site contact CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- THIS MUST BE COMPLETED IN FULL BEFORE UNBOXING THE PHONE.\n- If customer documentation upload is required, it must be legible to pass: no blur or content outside of the borders of the qualifying document. If they do not have proper documentation, please proceed and let ClearCaptions know during Welcome Call.\n- ***ONLY the camera feature built into the DMS platform may be used to capture customer information***. DO NOT use your device, and DO NOT upload any customer personal data into FN WO. Only upload to the DMS Platform.\n- If customer requests copy of the electronic records they signed, please advise them that they will need to retrieve them from ClearCaptions corporate. Contact CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n**COMPLIANCE & REPORTING**\n\n**This is NOT an emergency line. Do NOT call this number for installation help, scheduling issues, or general questions.**\n\n- If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations, or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* | Compliance@ClearCaptions.com\n- All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator, or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website: <https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts>\n\n**TROUBLESHOOTING**\n\n- Call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for any issues, and/or to report and solution a phone's failure to auto update\n- For Cat5 Set-ups: Plug the end of the Cat 5 Ethernet cable with the ferrite box into the phone\n- VoIP-PSTN Conversion Guide: Located in Additional Information > Attached Files","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-26T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":44.09065698787557},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792420564243}
