{"job":{"id":20193699,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"x REF #T20261014.0320 - Sanford, NC - Site Survey","description":{"html":"<strong>FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL</strong><br><strong>MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>** </del></strong><strong>SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested</strong><br><strong>Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code</strong><ul><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.</li><li><strong>Client Representation:</strong> You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.</li><li><strong>Platform Discretion:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> mention or discuss <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ****** </del></span>or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work/On-site Task:</strong><p>A technician is dispatched to a client site to <strong>document, photograph, and inventory all IT, network, and supporting systems</strong> — giving <del>******* ***** </del>a complete picture of the environment before any work or onboarding begins.</p><p>This is a thorough <strong>pre-deployment IT audit</strong> — the technician essentially creates a complete snapshot of the client's physical and network infrastructure so <del>******* ***** </del>can plan and execute whatever work comes next with full site awareness.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools / materials needed while onsite: </strong>Camera and notepad</p><p><strong>Documentation &amp; Photos</strong></p><p>• Please provide photos first thing for review while still onsite</p><p>• Send photos to <del>***************************</del></p><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong> Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li></ul><p><strong>Wrap-Up &amp; Site Exit</strong></p><p>• Confirm completion with on-call resource.</p><p>• Review collected information for completeness.</p><p>• Ensure no tools or materials are left behind.</p><p>• Leave IT and work areas clean and orderly.</p><p>• Thank the site contact before departure.</p><p><br></p><p><strong> Deliverables Summary</strong></p><p>At completion of the site survey, the following must be provided:</p><p>• Floor plan with access point locations marked</p><p>• Photo set (MDF, IDFs, network equipment, ISP demarc, power)</p><p>• Full inventory list with make/model/serial numbers</p><p>• Notes on risks, limitations, and client concerns</p><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p><strong>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p><strong>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</strong></p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be automatically rejected</strong>.</li></ul>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE & PROTOCOL**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE** **\\*\\*** **SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism & Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**A technician is dispatched to a client site to **document, photograph, and inventory all IT, network, and supporting systems** — giving \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* a complete picture of the environment before any work or onboarding begins.\n\nThis is a thorough **pre-deployment IT audit** — the technician essentially creates a complete snapshot of the client's physical and network infrastructure so \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* can plan and execute whatever work comes next with full site awareness.\n\n**Tools / materials needed while onsite:** Camera and notepad\n\n**Documentation & Photos**\n\n• Please provide photos first thing for review while still onsite\n\n• Send photos to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- **Documentation:** Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n\n**Wrap-Up & Site Exit**\n\n• Confirm completion with on-call resource.\n\n• Review collected information for completeness.\n\n• Ensure no tools or materials are left behind.\n\n• Leave IT and work areas clean and orderly.\n\n• Thank the site contact before departure.\n\n **Deliverables Summary**\n\nAt completion of the site survey, the following must be provided:\n\n• Floor plan with access point locations marked\n\n• Photo set (MDF, IDFs, network equipment, ISP demarc, power)\n\n• Full inventory list with make/model/serial numbers\n\n• Notes on risks, limitations, and client concerns\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\n**By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\n**All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.**\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\n- **Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":29.923688679536625},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:0