{"job":{"id":20193292,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Install Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Scope: Installation/replacement of 1 500 sheet staple finisher on CX833</p><p>SN: 7566436010RF1</p><p>For Konica Minolta B/F Service dispatch, please contact Eric Twitty (NCDOR Sys Admin) at 919-754-2461 ( Eric.Twitty@ncdor.gov.) for the Admin Password for device configuration access should it be required</p><p><br></p><p>If Tech is unable to reach work order POC, please call the Service Desk at 919-754-2323 select Opt 3.&nbsp;</p><p>Some offices are open on certain days, please contact the NCDOR Service Desk to arrange the best time to go onsite.</p><p>Tech should call Service Desk at 919 754 2323 Opt 3 for the close out of service tickets.</p><p>Tech should provide the Physical Location 1 information to the Service Desk once onsite so they can easily assist.&nbsp;The Physical Location 1 data is the device tag.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>COVID 19 Guidelines, please comply:</strong></p><p>1) Demonstrate that you are fully vaccinated or submit COVID-19 test results if unvaccinated or partially vaccinated.</p><p>2) Wear a face covering where required, regardless of vaccination status.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:**\n\nScope: Installation/replacement of 1 500 sheet staple finisher on CX833\n\nSN: 7566436010RF1\n\nFor Konica Minolta B/F Service dispatch, please contact Eric Twitty (NCDOR Sys Admin) at 919-754-2461 ( Eric.Twitty@ncdor.gov.) for the Admin Password for device configuration access should it be required\n\nIf Tech is unable to reach work order POC, please call the Service Desk at 919-754-2323 select Opt 3.\n\nSome offices are open on certain days, please contact the NCDOR Service Desk to arrange the best time to go onsite.\n\nTech should call Service Desk at 919 754 2323 Opt 3 for the close out of service tickets.\n\nTech should provide the Physical Location 1 information to the Service Desk once onsite so they can easily assist. The Physical Location 1 data is the device tag.\n\n**COVID 19 Guidelines, please comply:**\n\n1\\) Demonstrate that you are fully vaccinated or submit COVID-19 test results if unvaccinated or partially vaccinated.\n\n2\\) Wear a face covering where required, regardless of vaccination status.\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary & Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.984908097951537},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792420954252}
{"job":{"id":20193022,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Special Order Systems","title":"CAD Installation and Testing (T20261006.0090)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Work Order Overview – Installation and Cutover Procedure</strong></p><p>Installation Overview and Process</p><ul><li>&nbsp;Physical installation of 2 HP Collectors</li><li>&nbsp;Physical network and serial connections</li><li>&nbsp;Virtual Machine software installation</li><li>&nbsp;CAD Core software installation</li><li>&nbsp;Internet access confirmation</li><li>&nbsp;Validate remote access in the HP Collectors</li></ul><p>Equipment will be on site.&nbsp;Check with the POC for the equipment</p><p>Pre-Installation Meeting:</p><p>A 60-minute prep meeting will be scheduled a few days before the installation.</p><p>During this meeting, we’ll review the installation and cutover process and address any questions.</p><p>This meeting can be conducted remotely, and you can check in and out for time tracking purposes.</p><p>Since it occurs off-site, you may add this time to the tail end of the installation date.</p><strong><u>On-Site Process:</u></strong><ol><li><strong>Check In with Helpdesk</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upon arrival, call the <strong>Helpdesk </strong>at <strong>800-595-2640</strong> to record your check-in time.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Helpdesk will record your <strong>check-in and check-out times</strong>.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Check in with the location POC.</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Meet the <strong>location point of contact (POC), Chief Roland Nenni </strong>at<strong> 585-746-6453</strong> for site access.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be escorted to the <strong>Server Room</strong> where the devices will be installed.</li></ul><ol><li><strong> Call the Axon Project Manager:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Call the <strong>Axon PM, Russ St. Myers</strong> at <strong>206-696-6669</strong> for live guidance from remote support.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide <strong>remote support access</strong> to your laptop.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow instructions from remote support.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will stay on the support call for the entirety of the installation and cutover.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once remote support confirms the installation is complete, you’ll be released from the site. Don’t forget to call the Helpdesk again to record your check-out time.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tech will need the following items with them on-site:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Laptop (with Microsoft Teams)</li><li>Valid Driver's License</li><li>Phone with Camera</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>USB to RJ45 and/or Serial to RJ45 Console Cable (must have the ability to console from a laptop into Firewalls, Switches and Routers)</li><li>Interface for connecting to remote servers such as puTTy or Wireshark on a computer.</li></ul><p><strong>On Site Appearance and Conduct:&nbsp;ZERO TOLERANCE</strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer.&nbsp;Close toe shoes, business casual, khakis, jeans, and a collared shirt are required.&nbsp;Khaki/jeans pants and shirts are expected to be clean and without holes.&nbsp;No company logos or print. No hats.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Always be respectful, professional and courteous with the end-user.&nbsp;All communication with the end user shall be in conjunction with the current SOW.&nbsp;All other communication is forbidden.&nbsp;Tech is not to communicate with any site contacts in regards to scheduling or pay, only contact your helpdesk representative.&nbsp;Tech is not to mention Field Nation to end users in any shape or form.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>In the event of a potential issue onsite, you are to remove yourself from the site to avoid confrontation and contact your helpdesk representative immediately to discuss the next steps in coming up with a resolution.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Disrespect or failure to uphold our company image to the customer will not be tolerated. It will result in a cancelation with zero compensation and the loss of any future opportunities with our company.&nbsp;</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 65);\">SCHEDULING &amp; ARRIVAL:</strong></p><ul><li>TEAMSOS operates on a Hard Start schedule to ensure the best possible service experience for our customers.</li><li><strong><em><u>We do not permit Rescheduling or Cancellations, but if/when it’s required</u></em></strong>: Techs must contact TEAMSOS to request at least 48 hrs. in advance of the work order date and time via Support at&nbsp;800-595-2640.</li><li>Check-in/Check-out must be completed while onsite. If installation cannot start or be completed for any reason, you must garner TEAMSOS approval prior to exiting site.</li><li><strong><em><u>If you arrive “late”</u></em></strong>: Your arrival time will not be adjusted, and when past Field Nation’s 15-minute grace period will impact your timeliness rating. We will not take calls requesting arrival time overrides, so please plan accordingly.</li><li><strong>Please note there are penalties associated with arriving late and checking in/out off-site.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**Work Order Overview – Installation and Cutover Procedure**\n\nInstallation Overview and Process\n\n- Physical installation of 2 HP Collectors\n- Physical network and serial connections\n- Virtual Machine software installation\n- CAD Core software installation\n- Internet access confirmation\n- Validate remote access in the HP Collectors\n\nEquipment will be on site. Check with the POC for the equipment\n\nPre-Installation Meeting:\n\nA 60-minute prep meeting will be scheduled a few days before the installation.\n\nDuring this meeting, we’ll review the installation and cutover process and address any questions.\n\nThis meeting can be conducted remotely, and you can check in and out for time tracking purposes.\n\nSince it occurs off-site, you may add this time to the tail end of the installation date.\n\n**On-Site Process:**1. **Check In with Helpdesk**\n\n- Upon arrival, call the **Helpdesk** at **800-595-2640** to record your check-in time.\n- The Helpdesk will record your **check-in and check-out times**.\n\n1. **Check in with the location POC.**\n\n- Meet the **location point of contact (POC), Chief Roland Nenni** at **585-746-6453** for site access.\n- You will be escorted to the **Server Room** where the devices will be installed.\n\n1. **Call the Axon Project Manager:**\n\n- Call the **Axon PM, Russ St. Myers** at **206-696-6669** for live guidance from remote support.\n- Provide **remote support access** to your laptop.\n- Follow instructions from remote support.\n- You will stay on the support call for the entirety of the installation and cutover.\n- Once remote support confirms the installation is complete, you’ll be released from the site. Don’t forget to call the Helpdesk again to record your check-out time.\n\n**Tech will need the following items with them on-site:**\n\n- Laptop (with Microsoft Teams)\n- Valid Driver's License\n- Phone with Camera\n- Label Maker\n- Cable Toner\n- USB to RJ45 and/or Serial to RJ45 Console Cable (must have the ability to console from a laptop into Firewalls, Switches and Routers)\n- Interface for connecting to remote servers such as puTTy or Wireshark on a computer.\n\n**On Site Appearance and Conduct: ZERO TOLERANCE**\n\n- **Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer. Close toe shoes, business casual, khakis, jeans, and a collared shirt are required. Khaki/jeans pants and shirts are expected to be clean and without holes. No company logos or print. No hats.**\n- **Always be respectful, professional and courteous with the end-user. All communication with the end user shall be in conjunction with the current SOW. All other communication is forbidden. Tech is not to communicate with any site contacts in regards to scheduling or pay, only contact your helpdesk representative. Tech is not to mention Field Nation to end users in any shape or form.**\n- **In the event of a potential issue onsite, you are to remove yourself from the site to avoid confrontation and contact your helpdesk representative immediately to discuss the next steps in coming up with a resolution.**\n- **Disrespect or failure to uphold our company image to the customer will not be tolerated. It will result in a cancelation with zero compensation and the loss of any future opportunities with our company.**\n\n**SCHEDULING & ARRIVAL:**\n\n- TEAMSOS operates on a Hard Start schedule to ensure the best possible service experience for our customers.\n- ***We do not permit Rescheduling or Cancellations, but if/when it’s required***: Techs must contact TEAMSOS to request at least 48 hrs. in advance of the work order date and time via Support at 800-595-2640.\n- Check-in/Check-out must be completed while onsite. If installation cannot start or be completed for any reason, you must garner TEAMSOS approval prior to exiting site.\n- ***If you arrive “late”***: Your arrival time will not be adjusted, and when past Field Nation’s 15-minute grace period will impact your timeliness rating. We will not take calls requesting arrival time overrides, so please plan accordingly.\n- **Please note there are penalties associated with arriving late and checking in/out off-site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:45","end":"2026-10-26T14:45"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":390},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":52.57537009975463},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":390,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":80,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792420981993}
{"job":{"id":"5176677417","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"DataMax Services, Inc","title":"Angier Police Department Revisit","description":"<p>This work order is for the installation of hardware and the running of cable and wire for the Axon Interview Rooms project for policed departments.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will work the Axon representative (TSM) on site to validate all installed devices and cable/wire runs. The TSM will be responsible for approving device placements, any hardware configuration or programming, and leading the tech through getting all cameras aimed and focused.</p><p><br></p><p>All required tools and materials are listed in the attached document \"Axon Interview Room Tools &amp; Materials Requirements.docx.\"</p><p><br></p><p>The document \"Axon Interview Room SOW.pdf\" document details the installation standard and procedure for all devices that can be included in an interview room installation.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>MATERIALS: </u>All consumable materials like 18 gauge wire, CAT6, jacks, low voltage rings, and general hardware are all included in the \"all in\" fixed price agreed upon with the technician unless a different pay structure is discussed and approved in advance.</strong></p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>BUDGET &amp; SCOPE INCREASES:</u> Any out of scope or challenges on site that will require extra time and/or extra pay must be cleared with the Datamax PM while the work is in progress. Although the Axon TSM may acknowledge and approve extra work, the Datamax PM must clear it with the Axon PM to request a budget increase. If this info is not reported until later, the work may already have been invoiced. Please report all out of scope and time increases immediately. Your Datamax PM will also re-confirm any additions with you during your completion check out call.</strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-20T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":600},"p