{"job":{"id":"7738333186","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #268267 - ALARM CUTOVER &amp; GO LIVE (PH3) - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED","description":"<p>------------------------------ SCOPE OF WORK ------------------------------</p><p>JOB: MetTel Data Remote Installation and Analog/POTS Line Cutover</p><p><br></p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>MANDATORY EXPERIENCE, TOOLS AND MATERIALS</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>The technician must have experience with Analog/POTS lines, alarm cutovers, line tracing, direct alarm-panel connections, and PIAB/Data Remote installations.</p><p><br></p><p>DO NOT ACCEPT THIS ASSIGNMENT WITHOUT THE REQUIRED EXPERIENCE.</p><p><br></p><p>Required equipment:</p><p>• Full 300-ft box/reel of CAT5e or CAT6 cable</p><p>• Cross-connect wire, RJ11/RJ45 jacks, and modular plugs</p><p>• Working Butt Set with RJ11</p><p>• 66/110 punch-down tool</p><p>• Toner, probe, cable tester/toner, and crimper</p><p>• Digital multimeter</p><p>• 2-way and 3-way splitter adapters</p><p>• 10–12 ft ladder</p><p>• Drill and mounting hardware</p><p>• Label maker, Sharpie, tie wraps, and Velcro</p><p>• Laptop with Ethernet and TeamViewer or AnyDesk</p><p>• Serial/USB adapter and console cable</p><p>• Mobile hotspot or reliable internet</p><p>• Smartphone with camera</p><p><br></p><p>Verify all tools and sufficient cable before traveling. Missing experience, tools, or cable may result in removal and no payment.</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>• HARD START DATE/TIME. No rescheduling.</p><p>• Late arrival resulting in dismissal = no payment.</p><p>• Do not leave until Support releases you.</p><p>• Pictures and signed Work Order are required before leaving.</p><p>• Valid Enhanced Real ID, Enhanced Driver’s License, or another accepted federal identification document is required.</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>1. CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>-Check in with the Postmaster or site contact upon arrival.</p><p>-Call Tech Americas for check-in and check-out:</p><p>281-668-3211, Option 3</p><p>-If no response, email the details to:</p><p>support@tech-americas.com</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Failure to call both may result in payment deduction or no payment.</p><p>Contacts:</p><p>- Aida Flores: 210-830-7125 | aflores@tech-americas.com</p><p>- Rafael Aparicio: (216) 998-4955 | raparicio@tech-americas.com</p><p>- Cesar Ayala: (409) 340-0869 | caayala@tech-americas.com</p><p>- Elias Garcia: (409) 340-0872 | esgarcia@tech-americas.com</p><p>- Cristo Guevara: (254) 308-6718 | cguevara@tech-americas.com</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>2. INSTALLATION AND CUTOVER</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Before starting, provide Support with the package status, equipment model, and serial numbers.</p><p>• Mount and power on the MetTel Data Remote/PIAB.</p><p>• Install it near the alarm panel or telecom room.</p><p>• Use the location with the best LTE/cellular signal.</p><p>• Mount the MIMO antenna high and at least 3 ft from electrical panels.</p><p>• Follow the attached Installation Guide.</p><p>• Relocate the PIAB/Data Remote if directed by Support.</p><p>Identify and trace all existing lines:</p><p>• Voice</p><p>• Fax</p><p>• Elevator</p><p>• Burglar Alarm</p><p>• Fire Alarm</p><p><br></p><p>Only POTS lines are compatible. Report VoIP, SIP, digital, or virtual lines immediately.</p><p>Alarm lines must connect directly from the alarm panel to the Data Remote. No unauthorized splices, bridges, or intermediate connections.</p><p>Before touching alarm lines:</p><p>• Confirm the lines being cut over with Support.</p><p>• Wait for Support authorization.</p><p>• Confirm the alarm is in Test Mode.</p><p>After cutover, test all affected lines and wait for Support confirmation before leaving.</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>3. SITE SURVEY IF WORK CANNOT BE COMPLETED</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>If installation cannot be completed due to access, missing keys, technical obstructions, missing equipment, or incompatible infrastructure, complete the Full Site Survey before leaving.</p><p>Include:</p><p>• Device Health: Pass / Fail</p><p>• Panel Access: Yes / No</p><p>• Key Available: Yes / No</p><p>• Lock Number</p><p>• Site Mainline</p><p>• Required cable-run distance</p><p>• Obstructions and materials required</p><p>• Pictures of all findings</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>4. REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Provide:</p><p>• Equipment and serial-number sticker</p><p>• Alarm panel closed and open</p><p>• Key lock/panel number if no key is available</p><p>• Alarm keypad</p><p>• Mounting location before and after</p><p>• Completed installation and powered equipment</p><p>• All connections and cable routes</p><p>• Materials used</p><p>• Before and after pictures</p><p>• Signed Work Order</p><p>Send pictures and the signed Work Order before leaving the site.</p><p>All deliverables must also be emailed within 24 hours to:</p><p>documents@tech-americas.com</p><p>Missing deliverables will result in the job being closed without payment.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T10:00","end":"2026-10-07T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/7/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-08T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite ticket2"},{"start":"2026-10-07T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika Ortodont"},{"start":"2026-10-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"FW: Vinson Service_ISS Call"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792421070372}
{"job":{"id":20198790,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ GO LIVE / MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS153981","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3856226647 Ticket 11974146<br/><br/>\"**RACK & STACK + GO LIVE **  <br/>       <br/>Call George McMahon at 3856226647   when on site.  <br/><br/>***MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/><br/>RACK & STACK + GO LIVE<br/><br/>NO PORT NEW NUMBERS<br/><br/>LCON:Joshua Blake / Mark Card (336) 503-5635<br/>   <br/>-Data Remote CDS-9090 <br/>-MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit<br/>-Tech to locate equipment.<br/>-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.<br/>-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.<br/>-Attach antennas and power on.<br/>-MetTel will validate configurations.<br/>-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net<br/>-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.<br/>-Validate e911 address on one each line.<br/>-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.<br/>If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.<br/>-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.<br/>-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.<br/>-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.<br/>-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.<br/>-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.\"\"\"\"<br/><br/>null<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3856226647 Ticket 11974146  \n  \n\"\\*\\*RACK & STACK + GO LIVE \\*\\*   \n   \nCall George McMahon at 3856226647 when on site.   \n  \n\\*\\*\\*MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n  \nRACK & STACK + GO LIVE  \n  \nNO PORT NEW NUMBERS  \n  \nLCON:Joshua Blake / Mark Card (336) 503-5635  \n   \n-Data Remote CDS-9090   \n-MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit  \n-Tech to locate equipment.  \n-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.  \n-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.  \n-Attach antennas and power on.  \n-MetTel will validate configurations.  \n-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net  \n-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.  \n-Validate e911 address on one each line.  \n-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.  \nIf voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.  \n-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.  \n-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.  \n-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.  \n-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.  \n-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.\"\"\"\"  \n  \nnull  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":53.995277132415744},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-19T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Signature Aviation - Install - GSO 1060 PTI Drive, Greensboro, NC 27409 (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792421076735}
{"job":{"id":20192622,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Firm Start | Replace power adapter ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES. CALL TO CHECK IN 855-612-2183.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in <strong>Network Cabling</strong> and <strong>POS system installations. Must be able troubleshoot and work with remote support.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech is required to follow detailed instructions, troubleshoot, and work with remote support during the installation process.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Scope of Work</u> -</strong>Technician needed onsite to swap out power adapter on the pin pad for Kiosk 2 on the front counter. Tech will work with Essintial and KFC support to complete all installation and required testing steps. Must be able to follow written as well as verbal instructions.</li><li>Tech will need to work with support to patch into requested port numbers on the switch to liven up the kiosks.</li><li>Tech <strong>MUST</strong> be able to Tone, test, and trouble shoot network runs.</li><li><strong>Must have Microsoft Teams on your phone for support chat. You will conduct a walk through with the remote support team prior to starting installation.</strong></li><li><strong>Estimated duration is 6 hours.</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Fully Charged smartphone or other device that has phone, camera, internet ability (for online deliverable), and WITH Microsoft Teams Installed.</li><li>Cell Phone Charger - preferred Fast Charger with appropriate cord</li><li>Government- issued Photo ID (original, not photo of or a copy)</li><li>Basic / Standard Hand Tools</li><li>Measuring Tap</li><li>Cable scissors or diagonal cutters</li><li>Box Opener (Knife, box cutter, scissors, etc)</li><li>Cable Ties - Bring Velcro &amp; Zip Ties (We can NOT use Velcro in the kitchen)</li><li>Cabling Termination Tools</li><li>Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)</li><li>Drill &amp; standard drill bits with <strong>fully charged batteries and charger</strong></li><li><strong><u>Screw driver (Phillips #2 bit is most common)</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Hammer drill</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Masonry Bits</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Label Maker</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>2-inch hole saw (at least 2 inches deep as well)</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Tin snips, Diagonal cutters, or Lineman pliers (Need to cut 1/8\" steel cable)</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Materials Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Blue Category 6 cable</li><li>Cat 6 Data Jacks</li><li>Cat 6 RJ45 Mod Tips</li><li>Surface mount biscuits</li><li>Misc. Mounting hardware</li></ul><p><strong><u>Note</u></strong> -DO NOT BRING 100/75/50ft premade patch cables</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Onsite Remote Support Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Link:&nbsp;</strong><strong>https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9</strong></li><li><strong>Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298</strong></li><li><strong>Passcode: pqnBC5</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Print&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site. Please review all the attachments prior to arriving onsite.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Site Specific Documents [ I.E. Floor Maps/Floor Plans, Inventory List ] -</strong>&nbsp;Any site specific documentation will be attached to your work order prior to your visit.</li><li><strong>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</strong></li><li><strong>Download Microsoft Teams and ensure that it works on your phone.&nbsp;</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Check In Requirements- Follow in order</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER–&nbsp;</strong>Arrive onsite no earlier than 30 min. prior to start time.&nbsp;If you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Site Access:&nbsp;</strong>Start at the back service door and knock, if you get no answer, then proceed to the front door and knock. If you still have no response, then reach out the Microsoft Teams Support Chat for instruction.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CHECK IN with the Manager on duty (MOD) and introduce yourself as the Essintial Technician there to complete an install</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Have the manager direct you to the recently received shipment.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Take Inventory</strong>&nbsp;- Once you have located the equipment, please utilize the provided sheet and begin the inventory process.&nbsp;Once you have completed the inventory, please use the Microsoft teams link to join the Essintial KFC support chat.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>CHECK IN via Microsoft Teams with the Essintial/KFC Support team -&nbsp;</strong><strong>https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9</strong></li><li><strong>Start the Installation - Refer to Provided Installation Guide &amp; any other technical documents for step by step instructions:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with the manager on duty (MOD) to verify they have completed&nbsp;<strong>\"Start of Day</strong>\" on the back-office PC</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with the Essintial support team to determine the&nbsp;<strong>predesignated mounting location - THIS could be on the Front Counter, on a kiosk TABLE or on a WALL.</strong></li><li>Once the mounting location has been decided, check to make sure that we have at least&nbsp;<strong>2 power outlets installed</strong>. We will also need<strong>&nbsp;2 network drops&nbsp;per kiosk run</strong> the desired location [<strong>&nbsp;Ensure Power and LAN wall-outlets are available at proposed kiosk location.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Power should already be installed prior to your visit, if power is not available -&nbsp;</strong>we will need to reschedule to get power installed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>In most cases data will NOT be installed -&nbsp;</strong>we will need to run the required network drops.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once you have the data cables installed, we will need to get with the KFC Support Desk and complete the&nbsp;<strong>\"Network Switch Configurations\".</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Complete</strong>&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>\"Kiosk Hardware Assembly\"</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once assembled, place Kiosks in designated location and upload a picture to the Essintial/KFC support chat for final approval before permanently mounting.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mount the kiosk, and complete all power and data connections.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify Kiosk Functionality</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with Essintial and KFC to ensure the devices come online and connect to the network.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mount or hang the included<strong>ORDER</strong> sign as described in the kiosk playbook.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables / Closeout Requirements [ PRIOR to leaving the site ]</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Essintial Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial&nbsp;PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to confirm site details</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to provide requested information and photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to obtain Manager's signature</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Record the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables. You will be required to provide this code at final close out</li><li><strong>CHECK OUT with the Essintial/KFC Support team via Microsoft Teams -&nbsp;</strong><strong>https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9</strong></li><li><strong>CHECK OUT OF YOUR WORK ORDER-If you are unable to do so, make sure that you call into Essintial Projects Team</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:&nbsp;Any issues or questions related to the scope of work should be escalated to&nbsp;the Essintial/KFC Support team via this link&nbsp;-&nbsp;</strong><strong>https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Link:&nbsp;</strong><strong>https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9</strong></p><p><strong>Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298</strong></p><p><strong>Passcode: pqnBC5</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>KFC Support Desk -</strong> (800)435-7532 silent option 9</p><p>KFC SD Hours: 8 am - 3 pm Eastern Time.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no jeans or holes, collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements:&nbsp;</strong>Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:&nbsp;</strong>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind. Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time</p><p><strong>Out of Scope:&nbsp;</strong>Time over the allotted hours onsite must be detailed as to why the tech went over.&nbsp;(Note: Any delay due to the technician's skill-set, errors, not following directions, etc. will not be honored or approved)</p><p>Acceptable Reasons:</p><ul><li><strong>Site/lane access delays</strong></li><li><strong>Missing equipment</strong></li><li><strong>Delays in accessing equipment</strong></li><li><strong>Troubleshooting</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time & only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.**\n\n**YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES. CALL TO CHECK IN 855-612-2183.**\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in **Network Cabling** and **POS system installations. Must be able troubleshoot and work with remote support.**\n- **Tech is required to follow detailed instructions, troubleshoot, and work with remote support during the installation process.**\n- **Scope of Work -**Technician needed onsite to swap out power adapter on the pin pad for Kiosk 2 on the front counter. Tech will work with Essintial and KFC support to complete all installation and required testing steps. Must be able to follow written as well as verbal instructions.\n- Tech will need to work with support to patch into requested port numbers on the switch to liven up the kiosks.\n- Tech **MUST** be able to Tone, test, and trouble shoot network runs.\n- **Must have Microsoft Teams on your phone for support chat. You will conduct a walk through with the remote support team prior to starting installation.**\n- **Estimated duration is 6 hours.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Fully Charged smartphone or other device that has phone, camera, internet ability (for online deliverable), and WITH Microsoft Teams Installed.\n- Cell Phone Charger - preferred Fast Charger with appropriate cord\n- Government- issued Photo ID (original, not photo of or a copy)\n- Basic / Standard Hand Tools\n- Measuring Tap\n- Cable scissors or diagonal cutters\n- Box Opener (Knife, box cutter, scissors, etc)\n- Cable Ties - Bring Velcro & Zip Ties (We can NOT use Velcro in the kitchen)\n- Cabling Termination Tools\n- Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)\n- Drill & standard drill bits with **fully charged batteries and charger**\n- **Screw driver (Phillips #2 bit is most common)**\n- **Hammer drill**\n- **Masonry Bits**\n- **Label Maker**\n- **2-inch hole saw (at least 2 inches deep as well)**\n- **Tin snips, Diagonal cutters, or Lineman pliers (Need to cut 1/8\" steel cable)**\n\n**Materials Required:**\n\n- Blue Category 6 cable\n- Cat 6 Data Jacks\n- Cat 6 RJ45 Mod Tips\n- Surface mount biscuits\n- Misc. Mounting hardware\n\n**Note** -DO NOT BRING 100/75/50ft premade patch cables\n\n**Onsite Remote Support Information:**\n\n**Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info**\n\n- **Link:** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n- **Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298**\n- **Passcode: pqnBC5**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. **Print all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site. Please review all the attachments prior to arriving onsite.**\n2. **Site Specific Documents \\[ I.E. Floor Maps/Floor Plans, Inventory List \\] -** Any site specific documentation will be attached to your work order prior to your visit.\n3. **Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted.**\n4. **Download Microsoft Teams and ensure that it works on your phone.**\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **Check In Requirements- Follow in order**\n2. **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER–** Arrive onsite no earlier than 30 min. prior to start time. If you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n3. **Site Access:** Start at the back service door and knock, if you get no answer, then proceed to the front door and knock. If you still have no response, then reach out the Microsoft Teams Support Chat for instruction.\n4. **CHECK IN with the Manager on duty (MOD) and introduce yourself as the Essintial Technician there to complete an install**\n5. **Have the manager direct you to the recently received shipment.**\n6. **Take Inventory** - Once you have located the equipment, please utilize the provided sheet and begin the inventory process. Once you have completed the inventory, please use the Microsoft teams link to join the Essintial KFC support chat.\n7. **CHECK IN via Microsoft Teams with the Essintial/KFC Support team -** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n8. **Start the Installation - Refer to Provided Installation Guide & any other technical documents for step by step instructions:**\n9. Work with the manager on duty (MOD) to verify they have completed **\"Start of Day**\" on the back-office PC\n10. Work with the Essintial support team to determine the **predesignated mounting location - THIS could be on the Front Counter, on a kiosk TABLE or on a WALL.**\n11. Once the mounting location has been decided, check to make sure that we have at least **2 power outlets installed**. We will also need **2 network drops per kiosk run** the desired location \\[ **Ensure Power and LAN wall-outlets are available at proposed kiosk location.**\n12. **Power should already be installed prior to your visit, if power is not available -** we will need to reschedule to get power installed.\n13. **In most cases data will NOT be installed -** we will need to run the required network drops.\n14. Once you have the data cables installed, we will need to get with the KFC Support Desk and complete the **\"Network Switch Configurations\".**\n15. **Complete** the **\"Kiosk Hardware Assembly\"**\n16. Once assembled, place Kiosks in designated location and upload a picture to the Essintial/KFC support chat for final approval before permanently mounting.\n17. Mount the kiosk, and complete all power and data connections.\n18. Verify Kiosk Functionality\n19. Work with Essintial and KFC to ensure the devices come online and connect to the network.\n20. Mount or hang the included**ORDER** sign as described in the kiosk playbook.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables / Closeout Requirements \\[ PRIOR to leaving the site \\]**\n\n- **Complete Essintial Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):**\n- You will be asked to confirm site details\n- You will be asked to provide requested information and photos\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager's signature\n- Record the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables. You will be required to provide this code at final close out\n- **CHECK OUT with the Essintial/KFC Support team via Microsoft Teams -** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n- **CHECK OUT OF YOUR WORK ORDER-If you are unable to do so, make sure that you call into Essintial Projects Team**\n\n**Escalation Process: Any issues or questions related to the scope of work should be escalated to the Essintial/KFC Support team via this link -** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n\n**Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info:**\n\n**Link:** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n\n**Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298**\n\n**Passcode: pqnBC5**\n\n**KFC Support Desk -** (800)435-7532 silent option 9\n\nKFC SD Hours: 8 am - 3 pm Eastern Time.\n\n**Dress Code:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no jeans or holes, collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Physical Requirements:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind. Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time\n\n**Out of Scope:** Time over the allotted hours onsite must be detailed as to why the tech went over. (Note: Any delay due to the technician's skill-set, errors, not following directions, etc. will not be honored or approved)\n\nAcceptable Reasons:\n\n- **Site/lane access delays**\n- **Missing equipment**\n- **Delays in accessing equipment**\n- **Troubleshooting**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:30","end":"2026-10-22T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":51.20416434054694},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum thr