{"job":{"id":20192532,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Troubleshooting - Damage Assessment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Job Details:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Work Summary:</strong> Troubleshooting/Damage Assessment for Electronics/Appliances</li><li><strong>Location:</strong> Boydton, VA 23917</li><li><strong>Client Contact:</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******* ******** * *************</del></span></li><li><strong>Required Materials:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reference \"Client Documents\" section for all relevant and necessary documentation.</li><li><strong>Technician is needed to inspect, test, photograph, and document findings for the following claimed items:</strong></li></ul><p><strong>***You are REQUIRED to request and document any and all invoices ***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Panel</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Hot Water Heater Steibel Eltron</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Mini Fridge</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Pool Hayward Aquavac 600</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Pool Blaster Max (Pool vac)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Dentair Water &amp; Pool Automation Easy Touch (Display)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-(8) electric Tiki Torches</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Speakers (24)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Outlet @ pool cabinet</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Jacuzzi Tub - Master Upper (Phpotos Only)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-TVs (6)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-(2) Breathe Audio Elevate - Model BA-6640M (Amplifier)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Russound Digital Amp A2100</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Yamaha Receiver RX-V571</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Teac Stereo Tuner T-R670</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Teac Compact Disc Player PD-D2610</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-LG Blu Ray</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Direct TV Box</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Yamaha Music Cast</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-(2) Sets Surround Sound Speakers</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Projector</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 51, 56);\">-Oven</span></p><p><br></p><p>*** <strong>YOU ARE</strong> authorized to inspect any additional electronics/appliances the owner may present to you. ***</p><p>*** Should any of the aforementioned items be unavailable for inspection and documentation, notate reason in spreadsheet. ***</p><ul><li><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>*** NEW *** PDF/Digital Business Card available once assigned to the Work Order. To be used ONLY when handling assignments on behalf of our company.</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>*** NEW *** Access 24/7 Real Time AI Technician Support:</u></strong> <del>**************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technicians are encouraged to wear a face covering during the inspection and/or have them available to wear, if needed.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos must be uploaded in JPEG/JPG format.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photo Labeling is <strong>REQUIRED</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos of the electrical panel and power meter/meter box are <strong>REQUIRED</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Online spreadsheet for inspection findings will be accessible once the work order is assigned.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><del>************** ********* </del><del>***************************************</del><del>******</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><del>****** ******** </del><em><u><del>**** ******** ********</del></u></em><strong><em><u><del> </del></u></em></strong><del>****************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Claimed loss type is&nbsp;</strong><em>LIGHTNING</em>.&nbsp;<strong><u>TECHNICIAN SHOULD MAKE AN INDEPENDENT DAMAGE CAUSATION ASSESSMENT BASED ON HIS/HER ONSITE TESTING.</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>﻿</u>&gt;&gt; Check breaker panel &gt;&gt; Test power supply line(s) for continuity w/ Multimeter, or for voltage with Voltage Tester &gt;&gt; Test for proper voltage at the applicable source &gt;&gt; Run Device &gt;&gt; Document all performance observations &gt;&gt; Photograph all testing results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>You&nbsp;must</strong>&nbsp;complete all the tasks listed and submit fully completed work order with labeled photos within 24 hours of appointment time. If more time is needed due to scope and/or number of items, discuss with our office <strong>PRIOR TO</strong> inspection.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>All items must be listed individually on the spreadsheet</strong>. Cannot put 2 or more items on one line of the spreadsheet (Examples:&nbsp;5 Speakers listed in the work order require 5 individual entries in the spreadsheet or 10 light fixtures require 10 individual entries in the spreadsheet)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Please be discrete and confidential with your findings – though your opinions will influence our reporting, only the insurance company can make the ultimate determination of coverage or payout. *** Reference the&nbsp;<u>Keeping Findings Discreet</u>&nbsp;document for suggestions on what to say if asked about findings. ***</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>If you feel there is anything that is urgent or that is mentioned by the owner as urgent to them, call and let us know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Required Tools and Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Multimeter</li><li>Camera (or camera phone that takes quality photos)</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Tape measure</li><li>Ladder (4'6')</li><li>Basic toolkit</li><li>Standard 25 50' Edison 120 VAC extension cord</li><li>IEC to Edison (10A, 2-slot &amp; 3-slot) 120 VAC power supply cords</li><li>Temperature gauge (infrared thermometer or temp. adapter for a multimeter)</li><li>Non-contact Voltage Tester</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Face covering (<strong>recommended</strong>)</li><li>Casual professional attire (<strong>no logos</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Work Overview:</strong></p><p><strong>Pre-Work:</strong></p><ol><li>Set start time.</li><li>Read the entire work order, including scope of work, standard instructions, and confidential information instructions.</li><li>Check all required tools and equipment.</li><li>Ensure a face covering is available, if needed on-site.</li><li>Review the CLAIMED LOSS TYPE (<em>LIGHTNING</em>) and be prepared to assess causation.</li></ol><p><strong>On-Site:</strong></p><ol><li>Provide a courtesy call to the insured 30 minutes prior to arrival. If call is not answered, <strong>PROCEED TO SITE.</strong></li><li>Check-in with the insured upon site arrival.</li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Business card: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Your digital business card is attached. When on-site for an inspection, present it to the point of contact for identification. It may help to download and save it to your phone for easy access. Should any identification issues arise on-site, please advise the contact to reach our office at <del>***** ********</del>.</span></li><li>Obtain the insured's signature on the PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.</li><li>Take at least (2) clear quality photos of EACH claimed item.</li><li>Test EVERY claimed item for functionality or continuity with a multimeter.</li><li>Document all performance observations.</li><li>Photograph all testing results.</li><li>Inquire with the insured about replacement or repair invoices.</li><li>Take and upload photos of the power meter/meter box <strong>-AND-</strong> electrical panel.</li><li>Be discreet and confidential with findings.</li><li>In case of any urgent occurrence, contact the <strong>our office</strong> immediately. If afterhours, contact <strong>Emergency After-Hours Tech Line</strong>.</li></ol><p><strong>Post-Work:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload a completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes on item information and testing procedures (each item must be listed individually).</li><li>Rename each JPEG photo file with a description of the inspected item.</li><li>Upload photos of all inspected items.</li><li>Upload photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts.</li><li>Upload the signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.</li><li>Upload the signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT.</li><li>Enter detailed Close Out Notes summarizing the assessment, explaining the cause of damage (if any), and including information provided by the insured.</li></ol><p><strong>Required Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes or online spreadsheet with detailed testing notes</li><li>Renamed JPEG photos of claimed items</li><li>Photos of power meter/meter box <strong>-AND-</strong> electrical panel</li><li>Photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts</li><li>Signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT</li><li>Signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT</li><li>Detailed Close Out Notes</li></ul><p><strong>*** Failure to complete all of the above will result in non-payment for order. We are not paid by our client for late or incomplete work. ***</strong></p><p><strong>Please review and confirm your understanding of the work order details. If you have any questions or require further information, contact our office prior to proceeding with the work. Thank you for your attention to detail and commitment to completing this job efficiently and professionally.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Job Details:**\n\n- **Work Summary:** Troubleshooting/Damage Assessment for Electronics/Appliances\n- **Location:** Boydton, VA 23917\n- **Client Contact:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Required Materials:**\n- Reference \"Client Documents\" section for all relevant and necessary documentation.\n- **Technician is needed to inspect, test, photograph, and document findings for the following claimed items:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*You are REQUIRED to request and document any and all invoices \\*\\*\\***\n\n-Panel\n\n-Hot Water Heater Steibel Eltron\n\n-Mini Fridge\n\n-Pool Hayward Aquavac 600\n\n-Pool Blaster Max (Pool vac)\n\n-Dentair Water & Pool Automation Easy Touch (Display)\n\n-(8) electric Tiki Torches\n\n-Speakers (24)\n\n-Outlet @ pool cabinet\n\n-Jacuzzi Tub - Master Upper (Phpotos Only)\n\n-TVs (6)\n\n-(2) Breathe Audio Elevate - Model BA-6640M (Amplifier)\n\n-Russound Digital Amp A2100\n\n-Yamaha Receiver RX-V571\n\n-Teac Stereo Tuner T-R670\n\n-Teac Compact Disc Player PD-D2610\n\n-LG Blu Ray\n\n-Direct TV Box\n\n-Yamaha Music Cast\n\n-(2) Sets Surround Sound Speakers\n\n-Projector\n\n-Oven\n\n\\*\\*\\* **YOU ARE** authorized to inspect any additional electronics/appliances the owner may present to you. \\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* Should any of the aforementioned items be unavailable for inspection and documentation, notate reason in spreadsheet. \\*\\*\\*\n\n- **Special Instructions:**\n- **\\*\\*\\* NEW \\*\\*\\* PDF/Digital Business Card available once assigned to the Work Order. To be used ONLY when handling assignments on behalf of our company.**\n- **\\*\\*\\* NEW \\*\\*\\* Access 24/7 Real Time AI Technician Support:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Technicians are encouraged to wear a face covering during the inspection and/or have them available to wear, if needed.**\n- Photos must be uploaded in JPEG/JPG format.\n- Photo Labeling is **REQUIRED**.\n- Photos of the electrical panel and power meter/meter box are **REQUIRED**.\n- Online spreadsheet for inspection findings will be accessible once the work order is assigned.\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* *\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Claimed loss type is** *LIGHTNING*. **TECHNICIAN SHOULD MAKE AN INDEPENDENT DAMAGE CAUSATION ASSESSMENT BASED ON HIS/HER ONSITE TESTING.**\n- ﻿>> Check breaker panel >> Test power supply line(s) for continuity w/ Multimeter, or for voltage with Voltage Tester >> Test for proper voltage at the applicable source >> Run Device >> Document all performance observations >> Photograph all testing results\n- **You must** complete all the tasks listed and submit fully completed work order with labeled photos within 24 hours of appointment time. If more time is needed due to scope and/or number of items, discuss with our office **PRIOR TO** inspection.\n- **All items must be listed individually on the spreadsheet**. Cannot put 2 or more items on one line of the spreadsheet (Examples: 5 Speakers listed in the work order require 5 individual entries in the spreadsheet or 10 light fixtures require 10 individual entries in the spreadsheet)\n- **Please be discrete and confidential with your findings – though your opinions will influence our reporting, only the insurance company can make the ultimate determination of coverage or payout. \\*\\*\\* Reference the Keeping Findings Discreet document for suggestions on what to say if asked about findings. \\*\\*\\***\n- **If you feel there is anything that is urgent or that is mentioned by the owner as urgent to them, call and let us know.**\n\n**Required Tools and Equipment:**\n\n- Multimeter\n- Camera (or camera phone that takes quality photos)\n- Laptop\n- Tape measure\n- Ladder (4'6')\n- Basic toolkit\n- Standard 25 50' Edison 120 VAC extension cord\n- IEC to Edison (10A, 2-slot & 3-slot) 120 VAC power supply cords\n- Temperature gauge (infrared thermometer or temp. adapter for a multimeter)\n- Non-contact Voltage Tester\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Face covering (**recommended**)\n- Casual professional attire (**no logos**)\n\n**Work Overview:**\n\n**Pre-Work:**\n\n1. Set start time.\n2. Read the entire work order, including scope of work, standard instructions, and confidential information instructions.\n3. Check all required tools and equipment.\n4. Ensure a face covering is available, if needed on-site.\n5. Review the CLAIMED LOSS TYPE (*LIGHTNING*) and be prepared to assess causation.\n\n**On-Site:**\n\n1. Provide a courtesy call to the insured 30 minutes prior to arrival. If call is not answered, **PROCEED TO SITE.**\n2. Check-in with the insured upon site arrival.\n3. **Business card:** Your digital business card is attached. When on-site for an inspection, present it to the point of contact for identification. It may help to download and save it to your phone for easy access. Should any identification issues arise on-site, please advise the contact to reach our office at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n4. Obtain the insured's signature on the PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.\n5. Take at least (2) clear quality photos of EACH claimed item.\n6. Test EVERY claimed item for functionality or continuity with a multimeter.\n7. Document all performance observations.\n8. Photograph all testing results.\n9. Inquire with the insured about replacement or repair invoices.\n10. Take and upload photos of the power meter/meter box **-AND-** electrical panel.\n11. Be discreet and confidential with findings.\n12. In case of any urgent occurrence, contact the **our office** immediately. If afterhours, contact **Emergency After-Hours Tech Line**.\n\n**Post-Work:**\n\n1. Upload a completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes on item information and testing procedures (each item must be listed individually).\n2. Rename each JPEG photo file with a description of the inspected item.\n3. Upload photos of all inspected items.\n4. Upload photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts.\n5. Upload the signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.\n6. Upload the signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT.\n7. Enter detailed Close Out Notes summarizing the assessment, explaining the cause of damage (if any), and including information provided by the insured.\n\n**Required Deliverables:**\n\n- Completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes or online spreadsheet with detailed testing notes\n- Renamed JPEG photos of claimed items\n- Photos of power meter/meter box **-AND-** electrical panel\n- Photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts\n- Signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT\n- Signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT\n- Detailed Close Out Notes\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Failure to complete all of the above will result in non-payment for order. We are not paid by our client for late or incomplete work. \\*\\*\\***\n\n**Please review and confirm your understanding of the work order details. If you have any questions or require further information, contact our office prior to proceeding with the work. Thank you for your attention to detail and commitment to completing this job efficiently and professionally.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T08:00","end":"2026-11-02T15:00","latestStart":"2026-11-02T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":402.5,"max":402.5},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":69.69888054855116},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"available