{"job":{"id":20197162,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Assist Lead tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p>Assist Lead technician</p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>WIN10 Laptop – with Charger</li><li>Smartphone - with Charger</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Black Ink Pens - for documentation</li></ul><br/><br/><p>  </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required </li><li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance </li><li>Background check required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts</li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment </li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li></ul><br/><br/><p><strong>Data Center Do&#39;s and Don&#39;ts</strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>Do:</strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Follow all safety protocols </li><li>Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)</li><li>Wear comfortable, layered clothing.</li><li>Communicate proactively</li><li>Maintain a clean workspace</li><li>Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.</li><li>No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering approved area</li><li>ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands</li><li>If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal</li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong>Don’t:</strong> </p><br/><br/><ul><li>Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.</li><li>Don’t remove any cables. The <del>******</del> certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.</li><li>Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)</li><li>No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...</li><li>No Hitch Hiking on badge scans </li><li>Do not prop doors or cages open</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope:**\n\n  \n  \nAssist Lead technician\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n  \n  \n- WIN10 Laptop – with Charger\n- Smartphone - with Charger\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Black Ink Pens - for documentation\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check required\n- Check-in with site contacts\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n\n  \n  \n**Data Center Do's and Don'ts**\n\n  \n  \n**Do:**\n\n  \n  \n- Follow all safety protocols\n- Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)\n- Wear comfortable, layered clothing.\n- Communicate proactively\n- Maintain a clean workspace\n- Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.\n- No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering approved area\n- ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands\n- If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Don’t:**\n\n  \n  \n- Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.\n- Don’t remove any cables. The \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.\n- Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)\n- No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...\n- No Hitch Hiking on badge scans\n- Do not prop doors or cages open","actions":[]},