{"job":{"id":20199602,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Global Onsite Corporation","title":"Starlink Survey and Quote - PUBS-PUBS-42-S-Caro-7901","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><em><u>Please see Word Document attached and fill out and return to the email address listed below. Document is called 'Starlink Site Survey Form</u></em></strong></p><p>\t<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">                    </span></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;BEFORE YOU ARRIVE: <strong>Ensure you have the Starlink App loaded on your Smart Phone.</strong> </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\t&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">  </span></p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon Arrival, Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If there are any access issues or other unexpected issues during the scheduled event, please advise the Dispatch team ASAP so they can work toward resolution</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check-in and introduce yourself to the Onsite Contact.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Perform Survey</p><p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Identify the Telco Closet</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take Images</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ii.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Record in Provided Survey Checklist</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;iii.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Power</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;iv.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Rack / Shelf Space</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;v.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Patch distance to Network Switch</p><p>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Using the Starlink App, Identify the optimal Antenna Mounting Location</p><p>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Consider MOUNT required for Professional Installation</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take Images of Mount Location</p><p>d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Cable Distance from Optional Antenna Location to Telco Closet</p><p>e.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Work Effort and Process to extend COAX from Antenna to Telco Closet</p><p>f.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Ladder / Lift Requirements</p><p>g.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify Ceiling Height</p><p>h.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Complete the attached STARLINK survey form</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ALL DELIVERABLE SHOULD BE RETURNED TO </span>Dispatch@GLOBALIQ.IO<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> IMMEDIATELY UPON COMPLETION OF THE SURVEY PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.</span></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Completed Survey form</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ii.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures:</p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Telco Room</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Mounting Location</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;General pathway</p><p>j.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972) 597-9000 option 3) to check out and review survey findings.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;REMINDER:</p><p>Starlink needs a clear view of the sky so it can stay connected with satellites as they move overhead. Objects that obstruct the connection between your Starlink and the satellite, such as a tree branch, pole, or roof, will cause service interruptions. </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\tClick here for video guidance on obstructions</p><p>\t&nbsp;</p><p>  </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>To find a location with a clear view of the sky:</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>  </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">  </span></p><p>Use the “<strong>Check for Obstructions</strong>” tool to find an install location that will deliver the best service.</p><p>If you can not find a clear field of view from the ground level, consider installing it in an elevated location, like a roof, pole, or wall.</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Deliverables needed:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of before and after completed scope</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Signed workorder</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirmation all equipment is working and visible, scope completed</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Send deliverables to <u>dispatch@globaliq.io</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Once confirmed the scope is complete, call Global Onsite at 972-597-9000 OPT 3 to check</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>TOOLKIT:</u></em></strong></p><p>Mask required</p><p>Standard install/removal toolkit</p><p>6' ladder</p><p>Laptop with TeamViewer preinstalled</p><p>Cell phone with network connection</p><p>CAT6 cable</p><p>RJ45 tips</p><p>Crimps/crimpers</p><p>Snips</p><p>Test set</p><p>Adtran and Cisco console cable</p><p>Ethernet to USB dongle</p><p>DB9 male to USB dongle</p><p>***Any other tools necessary to complete the scope of work</p>","markdown":"***Please see Word Document attached and fill out and return to the email address listed below. Document is called 'Starlink Site Survey Form***\n\n1\\. BEFORE YOU ARRIVE: **Ensure you have the Starlink App loaded on your Smart Phone.**\n\n2\\. Upon Arrival, Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.\n\na. If there are any access issues or other unexpected issues during the scheduled event, please advise the Dispatch team ASAP so they can work toward resolution\n\n3\\. Check-in and introduce yourself to the Onsite Contact.\n\n4\\. Perform Survey\n\na. Identify the Telco Closet\n\n i. Take Images\n\n ii. Record in Provided Survey Checklist\n\n iii. Verify Power\n\n iv. Verify Rack / Shelf Space\n\n v. Verify Patch distance to Network Switch\n\nb. Using the Starlink App, Identify the optimal Antenna Mounting Location\n\nc. Consider MOUNT required for Professional Installation\n\n i. Take Images of Mount Location\n\nd. Verify Cable Distance from Optional Antenna Location to Telco Closet\n\ne. Verify Work Effort and Process to extend COAX from Antenna to Telco Closet\n\nf. Verify Ladder / Lift Requirements\n\ng. Verify Ceiling Height\n\nh. Complete the attached STARLINK survey form\n\ni. ALL DELIVERABLE SHOULD BE RETURNED TO Dispatch@GLOBALIQ.IO IMMEDIATELY UPON COMPLETION OF THE SURVEY PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.\n\n i. Completed Survey form\n\n ii. Pictures:\n\n1\\. Telco Room\n\n2\\. Mounting Location\n\n3\\. General pathway\n\nj. Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972) 597-9000 option 3) to check out and review survey findings.\n\n5\\. REMINDER:\n\nStarlink needs a clear view of the sky so it can stay connected with satellites as they move overhead. Objects that obstruct the connection between your Starlink and the satellite, such as a tree branch, pole, or roof, will cause service interruptions.\n\n Click here for video guidance on obstructions\n\n*To find a location with a clear view of the sky:*\n\nUse the “**Check for Obstructions**” tool to find an install location that will deliver the best service.\n\nIf you can not find a clear field of view from the ground level, consider installing it in an elevated location, like a roof, pole, or wall.\n\no\n\n**Deliverables needed:**\n\n**1. Pictures of before and after completed scope**\n\n**2. Signed workorder**\n\n**3. Confirmation all equipment is working and visible, scope completed**\n\n**4. Send deliverables to dispatch@globaliq.io**\n\n**Once confirmed the scope is complete, call Global Onsite at 972-597-9000 OPT 3 to check**\n\n***TOOLKIT:***\n\nMask required\n\nStandard install/removal toolkit\n\n6' ladder\n\nLaptop with TeamViewer preinstalled\n\nCell phone with network connection\n\nCAT6 cable\n\nRJ45 tips\n\nCrimps/crimpers\n\nSnips\n\nTest set\n\nAdtran and Cisco console cable\n\nEthernet to USB dongle\n\nDB9 male to USB dongle\n\n\\*\\*\\*Any other tools necessary to complete the scope of work","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T10:00","end":"2026-10-26T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":20.505931121899657},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792429979590}
{"job":{"id":20197213,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Assist Lead tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>Assist Lead technician</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>WIN10 Laptop – with Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone - with Charger</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit</li>\n<li>Black Ink Pens - for documentation</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Background check required</li>\n<li>Check-in with site contacts</li>\n<li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Data Center Do's and Don'ts</strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Do:</strong></p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Follow all safety protocols&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)</li>\n<li>Wear comfortable, layered clothing.</li>\n<li>Communicate proactively</li>\n<li>Maintain a clean workspace</li>\n<li>Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.</li>\n<li>No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering&nbsp;approved area</li>\n<li>ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands</li>\n<li>If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal</li>\n</ul>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Don’t:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.</li>\n<li>Don’t remove any cables. The&nbsp;<del>******</del>&nbsp;certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.</li>\n<li>Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)</li>\n<li>No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...</li>\n<li>No Hitch Hiking on badge scans&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Do not prop doors or cages open</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Scope:**\n\n  \n  \nAssist Lead technician\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n  \n  \n- WIN10 Laptop – with Charger\n- Smartphone - with Charger\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Black Ink Pens - for documentation\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check required\n- Check-in with site contacts\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n\n  \n  \n**Data Center Do's and Don'ts**\n\n  \n  \n**Do:**\n\n  \n  \n- Follow all safety protocols\n- Use mechanical lifts for heavy equipment (40 – 50+ lbs)\n- Wear comfortable, layered clothing.\n- Communicate proactively\n- Maintain a clean workspace\n- Stay in your approved work area. If you do not know where to go, please reach out to the POC. Reminder most likely there are cameras recording your actions.\n- No video, photos or META glasses are permitted ever, remove them before entering approved area\n- ALWAYS use your static discharge wrist bands\n- If issued badge, wear it so it is always visible to site personal\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Don’t:**\n\n  \n  \n- Start any work without instruction from the NVIDIA.\n- Don’t remove any cables. The \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* certified tech will be responsible for all cabling.\n- Take photos without authorization or bring unauthorized items into the data center (food, drinks, electronics, thumb drives)\n- No food or drink...EVER, not even personal water bottles....ever...\n- No Hitch Hiking on badge scans\n- Do not prop doors or cages open","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T10:30","end":"2026-10-22T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.68755983414495},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792429992449}
{"job":{"id":20199428,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Cable run from Switch to DLink","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>-<strong>Make sure to bring at least 78 ft (24 meters) of LAN cable</strong> to replace the cable connected from Port2 MS225 going to D link switch</p><p><br></p><p>-Make sure that the cable will go through the conduit making the cable not exposed</p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>Please provide images of all work completed onsite.</p><p>Provide detailed close out notes including all work done onsite, any issues or delays, MOD&#39;s name, Support&#39;s name, and if a revisit is needed.</p><p>Must provided receipt or invoice for all expenses or materials</p><p> </p><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.</em></p><p>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</p><p>Each site visit will require its own work order.</p><p>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><ul><li>300 Feet Cat 6 (Will be reimbursed up to $0.35 per/foot)</li><li>RJ45 connectors (Will be reimbursed up to $0.50 per/connector)</li><li>RJ45 crimping tool</li><li>Wire stripper / Cable scissors</li><li>Faceplates and Cat 6 jacks</li><li>Cable/Continuity Tester</li><li>8-10 foot Ladder</li><li>Spare patch cables</li><li>Zip ties / Velcro for cable management</li><li>Standard Tool Kit - including flat and Phillips screwdrivers in various sizes and needle nose pliers</li><li>Permanent marker</li><li>Digital Camera/Phone</li><li>Label maker</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Do Not Post Any Customer Photos On Social Media</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required</li><li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Background check is required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>**********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>PPE – As Required by location</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n-**Make sure to bring at least 78 ft (24 meters) of LAN cable** to replace the cable connected from Port2 MS225 going to D link switch\n\n-Make sure that the cable will go through the conduit making the cable not exposed\n\nPlease provide images of all work completed onsite.\n\nProvide detailed close out notes including all work done onsite, any issues or delays, MOD's name, Support's name, and if a revisit is needed.\n\nMust provided receipt or invoice for all expenses or materials\n\n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.*\n\nDo not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n\nEach site visit will require its own work order.\n\nIf a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n\n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n- 300 Feet Cat 6 (Will be reimbursed up to $0.35 per/foot)\n- RJ45 connectors (Will be reimbursed up to $0.50 per/connector)\n- RJ45 crimping tool\n- Wire stripper / Cable scissors\n- Faceplates and Cat 6 jacks\n- Cable/Continuity Tester\n- 8-10 foot Ladder\n- Spare patch cables\n- Zip ties / Velcro for cable management\n- Standard Tool Kit - including flat and Phillips screwdrivers in various sizes and needle nose pliers\n- Permanent marker\n- Digital Camera/Phone\n- Label maker\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Do Not Post Any Customer Photos On Social Media\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check is required\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- PPE – As Required by location","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T06:00","end":"2026-10-20T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":105},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":44.238479785437434},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 21, 2:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $105\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revis