{"job":{"id":20198984,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Xerox IT Solutions, LLC","title":"Certainty- Network Installation- Fayetteville, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technical Contact / Sign-Out:</strong> GRNetwork – 312-500-3443</p>\n<p><strong>Site Contact:</strong> <del>***** ********* *** ************</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong>\n<p>Technician is needed to install, mount, cable, and test Cisco Meraki network equipment at the Certainty office.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<strong><u>Technician Must Bring</u></strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Ladder</li>\n<li>Drill and/or screwdriver</li>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Patch cables / Cat5e or Cat6 cabling</li>\n<li>Coax cables/cabling</li>\n<li>Standard installation hand tools</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<strong><u>Service Tasks</u></strong>\n<ol>\n<li>Assemble and install the rack and patch panel.</li>\n<li>Connect a Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cable from <strong>ISP modem Port 1</strong> to <strong>Internet 1 on the Cisco Meraki MX68 firewall</strong>.</li>\n<li>Verify wall ports are active and receiving data connectivity to a <strong>10.60 IP address</strong>.</li>\n<li>Connect <strong>Switch Port 48</strong> to <strong>Firewall Port 10</strong>.</li>\n<li>Mount the switch, firewall, and wireless access point.</li>\n<li>Test patch cable runs from the Cisco Meraki MX68 firewall.</li>\n<li>Patch into applicable wall ports and verify wired network connectivity.</li>\n<li>Connect the <strong>MR33/MR36 access point to PoE Port 11 on the MX68</strong>.</li>\n<li>Connect applicable IT equipment to the Cisco Meraki firewall/switch, including laptops, printers, VoIP phones, copiers, scanners, etc.</li>\n<li>Connect and verify the printer.</li>\n<li>Ensure <strong>all cabling is clean, organized, and properly managed</strong>.</li>\n<li>Complete final testing with LCON.</li>\n<li><strong>Before leaving the site, call the Rate Network Team at 312-500-3443 for final sign-out and approval.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<br />\n<strong><u>Completion Requirements</u></strong>\n<ul>\n<li>All specified equipment installed and mounted.</li>\n<li>Network connections tested and verified.</li>\n<li>Cabling organized.</li>\n<li>Printer connected.</li>\n<li>Final testing completed with LCON.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not leave the site without receiving sign-out/approval from the Rate Network Team.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**Technical Contact / Sign-Out:** GRNetwork – 312-500-3443\n\n**Site Contact:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Scope of Work**Technician is needed to install, mount, cable, and test Cisco Meraki network equipment at the Certainty office.\n\n**Technician Must Bring**- Ladder\n- Drill and/or screwdriver\n- Laptop\n- Patch cables / Cat5e or Cat6 cabling\n- Coax cables/cabling\n- Standard installation hand tools\n\n**Service Tasks**1. Assemble and install the rack and patch panel.\n2. Connect a Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cable from **ISP modem Port 1** to **Internet 1 on the Cisco Meraki MX68 firewall**.\n3. Verify wall ports are active and receiving data connectivity to a **10.60 IP address**.\n4. Connect **Switch Port 48** to **Firewall Port 10**.\n5. Mount the switch, firewall, and wireless access point.\n6. Test patch cable runs from the Cisco Meraki MX68 firewall.\n7. Patch into applicable wall ports and verify wired network connectivity.\n8. Connect the **MR33/MR36 access point to PoE Port 11 on the MX68**.\n9. Connect applicable IT equipment to the Cisco Meraki firewall/switch, including laptops, printers, VoIP phones, copiers, scanners, etc.\n10. Connect and verify the printer.\n11. Ensure **all cabling is clean, organized, and properly managed**.\n12. Complete final testing with LCON.\n13. **Before leaving the site, call the Rate Network Team at 312-500-3443 for final sign-out and approval.**\n\n  \n**Completion Requirements**- All specified equipment installed and mounted.\n- Network connections tested and verified.\n- Cabling organized.\n- Printer connected.\n- Final testing completed with LCON.\n- **Do not leave the site without receiving sign-out/approval from the Rate Network Team.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T10:00","end":"2026-10-21T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":43.85213426008207},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts