{"job":{"id":20200882,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Meraki Deinstallation (Hard Start)","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of Work:</p><p>Meet with POC</p><p>Confirm equipment on site and collect ISP and SSID info</p><p>Remove equipment provided by customer</p><p>Prepare and package equipment to be returned</p><p>Collect required collateral and check out with Service Point support</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Materials:</p><p>LAN Tester,</p><p>RJ-45 Connector,</p><p>Label Maker</p><p>Cabling tools ( Push rods, Wire snake)</p><p>Cat5e cable tester</p><p>RJ45 crimper/Punch down tool</p><p>RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</p><p>Cat6 Keystone Jack</p><p>Zip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps</p><p><br></p><p>Required Collateral:</p><p>Photos of equipment removed/packaged</p><p>Checklist</p><p>Sign off</p><p>Any end points onsite</p><p>Confirmation equipment is working</p><p><br></p><p>**THESE LOCATIONS ARE GROUP HOMES**</p><p><br></p><p>Professionalism &amp; Respect &mdash; Treat the location as someone's home, not simply a job site. Be courteous, professional, and respectful of residents, caregivers, and the POC.</p><p><br></p><p>Empathy &amp; Patience &mdash; Be understanding and patient with individuals who may have intellectual, developmental, behavioral, mobility, or communication challenges.</p><p><br></p><p>Clear Communication &mdash; Introduce yourself, explain the purpose of the visit, confirm the scope with the POC, and communicate before entering rooms, moving items, or removing equipment.</p><p><br></p><p>Situational Awareness &amp; Adaptability &mdash; Recognize when a resident may be uncomfortable or distressed. Be willing to pause or adjust the work and follow the caregiver/POC's direction.</p><p><br></p><p>Discretion &amp; Respect for Privacy &mdash; Protect residents' dignity and privacy. Do not ask unnecessary personal or medical questions, discuss what is observed in the home, or take unauthorized photos.</p><p><br></p><p>Professional Appearance &amp; Dress &mdash; Technicians are entering managed residential homes and are expected to maintain a clean, professional appearance. A polo-style shirt is preferred. T-shirts with logos, graphics, or messaging and hats should not be worn. Pants should be clean, professional, free of holes, and not visibly worn or damaged. Shoes should be clean and appropriate for performing technical work safely.</p>","markdown":"Scope of Work:\n\nMeet with POC\n\nConfirm equipment on site and collect ISP and SSID info\n\nRemove equipment provided by customer\n\nPrepare and package equipment to be returned\n\nCollect required collateral and check out with Service Point support\n\nRequired Materials:\n\nLAN Tester,\n\nRJ-45 Connector,\n\nLabel Maker\n\nCabling tools ( Push rods, Wire snake)\n\nCat5e cable tester\n\nRJ45 crimper/Punch down tool\n\nRJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n\nCat6 Keystone Jack\n\nZip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps\n\nRequired Collateral:\n\nPhotos of equipment removed/packaged\n\nChecklist\n\nSign off\n\nAny end points onsite\n\nConfirmation equipment is working\n\n\\*\\*THESE LOCATIONS ARE GROUP HOMES\\*\\*\n\nProfessionalism & Respect — Treat the location as someone's home, not simply a job site. Be courteous, professional, and respectful of residents, caregivers, and the POC.\n\nEmpathy & Patience — Be understanding and patient with individuals who may have intellectual, developmental, behavioral, mobility, or communication challenges.\n\nClear Communication — Introduce yourself, explain the purpose of the visit, confirm the scope with the POC, and communicate before entering rooms, moving items, or removing equipment.\n\nSituational Awareness & Adaptability — Recognize when a resident may be uncomfortable or distressed. Be willing to pause or adjust the work and follow the caregiver/POC's direction.\n\nDiscretion & Respect for Privacy — Protect residents' dignity and privacy. Do not ask unnecessary personal or medical questions, discuss what is observed in the home, or take unauthorized photos.\n\nProfessional Appearance & Dress — Technicians are entering managed residential homes and are expected to maintain a clean, professional appearance. A polo-style shirt is preferred. T-shirts with logos, graphics, or messaging and hats should not be worn. Pants should be clean, professional, free of holes, and not visibly worn or damaged. Shoes should be clean and appropriate for performing technical work safely.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T11:00","end":"2026-10-23T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":29.550252779213558},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"