{"job":{"id":20199016,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Cisco Certified or Cisco Experienced Technician Required to perform a router and switch upgrades","description":{"html":"<p>CCNA or Equivalent experienced Network Technician required to perform Cisco router and Cisco to Dell switch upgrade.</p>\n<p>Tech must have experience providing remote console access as a Smart-Hands for Cisco router &amp; switch replacements and upgrades.</p>\n<p>Tech must bring multiple various length patch cables, working Laptop with terminal emulator (puTTY or Tera Term), team viewer, usb to serial adapter, Cisco console cable cell phone with hotspot and charger, hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.), machine labeler with label tape, 4 pair tester, toner, Butt Set and speed-out bit set.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive onsite and check in with PM/WO manager</li>\n<li>Meet with location contact and receive new Cisco 8200 router and Dell E3248PXE-ON and gain access to comm room.</li>\n<li>Unbox and assemble new router and switch, ensuring to capture photos of SN and entire device prior to installation.</li>\n<li>If possible, install new router and switch right below/above existing router and switch and power up both devices (Advise if issues with either)- Please ensure you do not unplug anything until instructed</li>\n<li>Join conference bridge at designated time and follow instructions given by customer NOC resource (see confidential section for conference bridge details)</li>\n<li>After completion, please ensure all trash is picked up and thrown away</li>\n<li>Old devices (Cisco ENCS router and Cisco 3650 switch) will be set aside in comm room for disposal company to pick up<strong><u>or</u></strong> you may be requested to box up old equipment and drop off at nearby FedEx store.</li>\n<li>Work with users to test daily tasks as directed on bridge (site contact to test email, intranet, printing, wireless and regularly used platforms)</li>\n<li>Upload all required photos to tasks section of the WO</li>\n<li>Confirm all deliverables are approved with PM/WO manager prior to leaving site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>General Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>-Review all provided supplemental documentation provided BEFORE arriving at site</p>\n<p>-Must arrive on time</p>\n<p>-Tech must be professional at all times.</p>\n<p>-Tech must check in with PM upon arrival to the site and must check out with the PM before leaving the site.</p>\n<p>-Tech must communicate with the PM during the upgrade activity as needed.</p>\n<p>-Tech must adhere to the general requirements, details are in the attached documentation.</p>\n<p>-Follow switch port map and direction from PM resource.</p>\n<p>-Follow directions for equipment removal &amp; replacement</p>\n<p>-Be methodical and precise when performing cable labeling &amp; re-patching activities—small errors during patching can and will result in significant troubleshooting times. Time preparing for these activities prior to shutdown is well-spent.</p>","markdown":"CCNA or Equivalent experienced Network Technician required to perform Cisco router and Cisco to Dell switch upgrade.\n\nTech must have experience providing remote console access as a Smart-Hands for Cisco router & switch replacements and upgrades.\n\nTech must bring multiple various length patch cables, working Laptop with terminal emulator (puTTY or Tera Term), team viewer, usb to serial adapter, Cisco console cable cell phone with hotspot and charger, hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.), machine labeler with label tape, 4 pair tester, toner, Butt Set and speed-out bit set.\n\n- Arrive onsite and check in with PM/WO manager\n- Meet with location contact and receive new Cisco 8200 router and Dell E3248PXE-ON and gain access to comm room.\n- Unbox and assemble new router and switch, ensuring to capture photos of SN and entire device prior to installation.\n- If possible, install new router and switch right below/above existing router and switch and power up both devices (Advise if issues with either)- Please ensure you do not unplug anything until instructed\n- Join conference bridge at designated time and follow instructions given by customer NOC resource (see confidential section for conference bridge details)\n- After completion, please ensure all trash is picked up and thrown away\n- Old devices (Cisco ENCS router and Cisco 3650 switch) will be set aside in comm room for disposal company to pick up**or** you may be requested to box up old equipment and drop off at nearby FedEx store.\n- Work with users to test daily tasks as directed on bridge (site contact to test email, intranet, printing, wireless and regularly used platforms)\n- Upload all required photos to tasks section of the WO\n- Confirm all deliverables are approved with PM/WO manager prior to leaving site\n\n**General Requirements**\n\n-Review all provided supplemental documentation provided BEFORE arriving at site\n\n-Must arrive on time\n\n-Tech must be professional at all times.\n\n-Tech must check in with PM upon arrival to the site and must check out with the PM before leaving the site.\n\n-Tech must communicate with the PM during the upgrade activity as needed.\n\n-Tech must adhere to the general requirements, details are in the attached documentation.\n\n-Follow switch port map and direction from PM resource.\n\n-Follow directions for equipment removal & replacement\n\n-Be methodical and precise when performing cable labeling & re-patching activities—small errors during patching can and will result in significant troubleshooting times. Time preparing for these activities prior to shutdown is well-spent.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-02T08:00","end":"2026-12-02T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":350},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":5,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":12.234109520468671},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $350 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-04T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-05T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430079480}
{"job":{"id":20199013,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ProTel Communication","title":"Network Installation - Firewall","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>PROTEL NETWORK SOLUTIONS</u></strong>&nbsp;is seeking an experienced technician for the following:</p><p>Replace current Fortigate 60E with new Fortigate 81F</p><p>Call support and navigate through steps to bring online.</p><p>Must be experienced in network hardware installation and configuration</p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Task:</strong> Unbox, Rack-Mount, and Perform Initial Configuration of FortiGate Firewall</li><li><strong>Estimated Time:</strong> 1.5 – 2 Hours</li><li><strong>Required Tools:</strong> RJ-45 Ethernet cables, console cable, terminal client (PuTTY/TeraTerm)</li></ul><p><strong>INSTALLATION STEPS</strong></p><p><strong> Physical Mounting &amp; Power</strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unpack the FortiGate unit and verify all hardware components (power adapter, console cable, mounting kit).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Secure the unit in the server rack using the included rack ears and screws.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect power supplies to a redundant power source/PDU and verify the front panel Power LED turns solid green.</li></ul><p><strong> Network Wiring</strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the <strong>WAN1 / Port 1</strong> interface to your ISP gateway/modem using a Cat6 cable.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the <strong>MGMT</strong> or <strong>Port 2/LAN</strong> interface to your internal network switch or directly to your deployment laptop.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>MUST HAVE (Laptop, Console Cable, Extra cat5e/cat6 Cable for replacement, if necessary, Cable tester, jacks/mounts for termination, etc..)</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Important Requirements AND Deliverables for Processing and Billing:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Make sure to bring required equipment needed for this type of service work.</li><li>Upload before and after pictures of all work performed and completed. <strong>Label your photos</strong>.</li><li>State your findings and work completed in the closeout notes.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Check In / Support</u></strong> (<em>See below for contact info in \"confidential information.\"</em>)</p><ul><li>The technician<u>&nbsp;</u><strong><u>must check in, check out and review deliverables</u></strong>&nbsp;with Protel: NICK</li><li>TECH SUPPORT: MAX</li><li>POC / MOD:&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Additional Requirements</u>:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>DO NOT mention Field Nation onsite</strong></li><li><strong>Technician represents&nbsp;Protel Communication&nbsp;at all times</strong></li><li><strong>No logo shirts or uniforms permitted</strong></li><li><strong>No work outside the SOW will be paid without prior approval</strong></li><li><strong>Additional time requires approval before proceeding</strong></li><li><strong>All photos and documentation must be uploaded prior to departure</strong></li><li><strong>Please ensure the work area is thoroughly cleaned upon completion and left in a neat, presentable, and professional condition.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Buyer has set its provider material reimbursement pricing.</u></strong></p><p>• Non Plenum Cat5e&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;$0.15 per foot</p><p>• Plenum Cat5e&nbsp;&nbsp;- $0.27 per foot</p><p>• Cat5e Keystone - $4.00 each</p><p>• Non Plenum Cat6&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;$0.23 per foot</p><p>• Plenum Cat6 - $0.49 per foot</p><p>• Cat6 Keystone&nbsp;&nbsp;- $6.00 each</p><p>• 1/2/3/4/6 Port Faceplates&nbsp;&nbsp;- $2.60 each</p><p>• Single Gang Low Volt Box For Faceplate&nbsp;&nbsp;- $4.50 each</p><p>• 7' - 15' Patch Cables&nbsp;&nbsp;- $12 each</p><p>• 1' - 6' Patch Cables&nbsp;&nbsp;- $10 each</p><p>• Surface Mount 2 Port Surface Mount Box - $3.75 each</p><p>· Surface Mount 1 Port Surface Mount Box - $2.75 each</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>** We thank you for following the work order instructions and for your attention to detail. We truly appreciate your service and professionalism, and we look forward to building a positive working relationship and the opportunity to collaborate on future work orders. **</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**PROTEL NETWORK SOLUTIONS** is seeking an experienced technician for the following:\n\nReplace current Fortigate 60E with new Fortigate 81F\n\nCall support and navigate through steps to bring online.\n\nMust be experienced in network hardware installation and configuration\n\n- **Task:** Unbox, Rack-Mount, and Perform Initial Configuration of FortiGate Firewall\n- **Estimated Time:** 1.5 – 2 Hours\n- **Required Tools:** RJ-45 Ethernet cables, console cable, terminal client (PuTTY/TeraTerm)\n\n**INSTALLATION STEPS**\n\n **Physical Mounting & Power**\n\n- Unpack the FortiGate unit and verify all hardware components (power adapter, console cable, mounting kit).\n- Secure the unit in the server rack using the included rack ears and screws.\n- Connect power supplies to a redundant power source/PDU and verify the front panel Power LED turns solid green.\n\n **Network Wiring**\n\n- Connect the **WAN1 / Port 1** interface to your ISP gateway/modem using a Cat6 cable.\n- Connect the **MGMT** or **Port 2/LAN** interface to your internal network switch or directly to your deployment laptop.\n\n***MUST HAVE (Laptop, Console Cable, Extra cat5e/cat6 Cable for replacement, if necessary, Cable tester, jacks/mounts for termination, etc..)***\n\n**Important Requirements AND Deliverables for Processing and Billing:**\n\n- Make sure to bring required equipment needed for this type of service work.\n- Upload before and after pictures of all work performed and completed. **Label your photos**.\n- State your findings and work completed in the closeout notes.\n\n**Check In / Support** (*See below for contact info in \"confidential information.\"*)\n\n- The technician **must check in, check out and review deliverables** with Protel: NICK\n- TECH SUPPORT: MAX\n- POC / MOD:\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- **DO NOT mention Field Nation onsite**\n- **Technician represents Protel Communication at all times**\n- **No logo shirts or uniforms permitted**\n- **No work outside the SOW will be paid without prior approval**\n- **Additional time requires approval before proceeding**\n- **All photos and documentation must be uploaded prior to departure**\n- **Please ensure the work area is thoroughly cleaned upon completion and left in a neat, presentable, and professional condition.**\n\n**Buyer has set its provider material reimbursement pricing.**\n\n• Non Plenum Cat5e - $0.15 per foot\n\n• Plenum Cat5e - $0.27 per foot\n\n• Cat5e Keystone - $4.00 each\n\n• Non Plenum Cat6 - $0.23 per foot\n\n• Plenum Cat6 - $0.49 per foot\n\n• Cat6 Keystone - $6.00 each\n\n• 1/2/3/4/6 Port Faceplates - $2.60 each\n\n• Single Gang Low Volt Box For Faceplate - $4.50 each\n\n• 7' - 15' Patch Cables - $12 each\n\n• 1' - 6' Patch Cables - $10 each\n\n• Surface Mount 2 Port Surface Mount Box - $3.75 each\n\n· Surface Mount 1 Port Surface Mount Box - $2.75 each\n\n**\\*\\* We thank you for following the work order instructions and for your attention to detail. We truly appreciate your service and professionalism, and we look forward to building a positive working relationship and the opportunity to collaborate on future work orders. \\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.768438920162226},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:0