 IT staff to complete tasks as per the final checklist which will be onsite. Work will include:<br/>- Ensure credit card machine is in it's final place<br/>- Ensure all PCs and Printers are online<br/>- Assist in any troubleshooting as the onsite operations teams completes their testing checklist.<br/>- Verify data drops are documented on the as built diagram.<br/>- Assist in any final adjustments requested by Corporate IT (remote) and the BPI PM<br/>-----------------------------<br/>MONDAY GO LIVE DAY:<br/>- Be onsite for any support that may be required during initial go live. Tech will remain onsite until released which will be no earlier than 11am.<br/>    - Release must come from the BPI PM prior to leaving site and will be verified with the onsite Ops Integration Manager, remote IT lead and BPI PM assigned.<br/>-----------------------------<br/><br/>DELIVERABLES:<br/>1. Photos as requested<br/>2. As Built Updated<br/>","markdown":"This is a 3-day WO, Tuesday (Prep), Saturday (Testing) & Monday (Go Live Support)  \n  \nSUMMARY:  \nThis is the Software and Business Conversion, migrating these users to their new Point of Sale and Inventory Management system, the support is to ensure that all necessary IT equipment and connections are ready, and verify that infrastructure is documented and supportable going forward.  \nRelease each day will require sign off from onsite Ops PM, Remote IT PM and your BP Innovations project coordinator.  \n  \n\\--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \nTECH REQUIRED EQUIPMENT:  \n\\- Laptop, Console Cable, & HotSpot  \n\\- All standard tools as listed in the WO  \n  \nTECH REQUIRED MATERIALS (in addition to standard tools & materials):  \n\\- At least 300' of Cat6 Cable and at least 4 Cat6 Jacks to be used only if needed.  \n  \n\\--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n  \nTUESDAY ADVANCED PREP VISIT:  \nTech will work with BPI PM, Remote Customer IT staff and onsite Integration Manager to complete tasks as per the final checklist. Work will include:  \n\\- Swapping out a few devices such as:  \n\\- Network Printer for Shipping (aka \"Varsity Printer\")  \n\\- TEMP CONNECT the credit card machines and verify  \n\\- Check scanner (USB connection)  \n\\- Tone & test any data drops that may get equipment connected and update the as built diagram for the site  \n\\- Install any new PCs or Printers (estimated 0 - 3 devices, final count is site and situation specific)  \n\\- Running data drop(s) only if needed for new equipment (i.e. Shipping Printer)  \n\\-----------------------------  \nSATURDAY TESTING DAY:  \nTech will work with BPI PM and Customer IT staff to complete tasks as per the final checklist which will be onsite. Work will include:  \n\\- Ensure credit card machine is in it's final place  \n\\- Ensure all PCs and Printers are online  \n\\- Assist in any troubleshooting as the onsite operations teams completes their testing checklist.  \n\\- Verify data drops are documented on the as built diagram.  \n\\- Assist in any final adjustments requested by Corporate IT (remote) and the BPI PM  \n\\-----------------------------  \nMONDAY GO LIVE DAY:  \n\\- Be onsite for any support that may be required during initial go live. Tech will remain onsite until released which will be no earlier than 11am.  \n\\- Release must come from the BPI PM prior to leaving site and will be verified with the onsite Ops Integration Manager, remote IT lead and BPI PM assigned.  \n\\-----------------------------  \n  \nDELIVERABLES:  \n1\\. Photos as requested  \n2\\. As Built Updated","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-07T09:00","end":"2026-11-07T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":43.2553736831442},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 (countered: $280) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430214744}
{"job":{"id":20178322,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Network Cutover of all IT Equipment - Assistant Tech (prepare for 8 hours and potential cabling)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">A 5-6 hour site visit to cut the network and all IT equipment from the legacy Pep Boys to the new Mavis Tire network and IT equipment.&nbsp;All Pep Boys equipment will be de-installed and packed for pick up.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</li><li>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Cutover Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned Mavis IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned Mavis IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><p>----Prior to leaving site, the following must be completed:</p><ul><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Pictures to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with Mavis IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nA 5-6 hour site visit to cut the network and all IT equipment from the legacy Pep Boys to the new Mavis Tire network and IT equipment. All Pep Boys equipment will be de-installed and packed for pick up.\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Cutover Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned Mavis IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned Mavis IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n\\----Prior to leaving site, the following must be completed:\n\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Pictures to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with Mavis IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00","end":"2026-10-27T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":330},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":50.542248267326876},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $330 (countered: $360) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430242920}
{"job":{"id":20191652,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Akkodis, formerly Modis","title":"PC Refresh, Memory / Win 11Upgrades ","description":{"html":"<p>This project initiative is focused on the systematic replacement of end-of-life (EOL) laptops across the organization.</p><p>In parallel, the engagement includes upgrading desktop systems to Windows 11.</p><p>Additionally, the project emphasizes performance optimization through memory upgrades. Functional RAM modules from decommissioned devices are carefully recovered, tested, and redeployed to enhance the performance of active laptops that remain within their service lifecycle.</p><p>Overall, the initiative aims to improve device efficiency, extend hardware usability for NFI Industries</p><p><strong><u>***DO NOT DISCUSS YOUR COMPENSATION &amp; CLIENT CONTACT DETAILS (STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL) WITH ANYONE OUTSIDE OF AKKODIS***</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Read all the below instructions carefully:</u></strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;Instructional Note for Technicians:</strong> Please ensure the team thoroughly reviews the service description, Runbook, and checklist documents to fully understand the instructions. Upon task completion, they are required to:</p><ul><li>Update the checklist.</li><li>Obtain a signature from the site Point of Contact.</li><li>Upload a photo of the signed document to the work order.</li><li>For every site unless the memory will be reused, please have the technician package it in the laptop box along with the old laptop.</li></ul><p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please contact the Primary Point of Contact after check In at site and after completion of work don't leave the site without informing the support contact and get their signature.</strong></p><p><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Failing the above instructions will strictly lead to work order cancellation or may hamper the pay.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Post successful completion of the work on site, please enter complete close out notes along with deliverables attached which is mandatory before marking the work order completed.</strong></p><p><strong>In order to be paid for this work order ALL work must be completed: replacement, testing, return, requested photos and most all maintaining professionalism onsite.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>﻿Mandatory Technical Briefing :&nbsp;</strong>At least 48 hours before the scheduled task, the technician&nbsp;<strong>must</strong>&nbsp;call the&nbsp;<strong>NFI IT Team</strong>&nbsp;using the provided contact numbers. The goal is to verify technical requirements and address site-specific questions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Verification:</strong>&nbsp;The technician must log the name of the NFI IT representative they spoke with in the Field Nation notes.</li><li><strong>Inquiry Protocol (Pre-Site):</strong>&nbsp;Direct all&nbsp;<strong>technical</strong>&nbsp;questions to the NFI IT Team and all&nbsp;<strong>scope/logistics</strong>&nbsp;questions to the Akkodis Team at least 48 hours prior to arrival.</li><li><strong>Communication Standards:</strong>&nbsp;Prompt acknowledgment of all Akkodis emails and messages is mandatory. Responses are expected within&nbsp;<strong>4 hours</strong>&nbsp;during business days.</li><li><strong>On-Site Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Technicians must be fully self-sufficient and prepared upon arrival. Avoid asking repeated questions on-site that are explicitly covered in the&nbsp;<strong>NFI Runbook</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Scope documents</strong>. Failure to follow the Runbook may lead to performance escalations or rating deductions.</li><li><strong>Required Tools &amp; Hardware Verification:</strong>&nbsp;The technician must confirm they possess all necessary hardware and tools required for the task&nbsp;prior to traveling to the site.</li><li><strong>The \"First Hour\" Milestone:</strong>&nbsp;Technicians must provide a quick status update via the call or Field Nation after the&nbsp;<strong>first 60 minutes</strong>&nbsp;on-site (e.g., \"First 3 devices completed\").&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Workflow:</strong></p><p><strong>below are the device types NFI (Client)would like to have for each of the desktops. please add this to the list as part of the checklist.</strong></p><p>Pack station</p><p>Shipping station</p><p>eCommerce station</p><p>VAS station</p><p>Cubiscan station</p><p>Returns station</p><p>Warehouse TV station</p><p>Mobile cart station</p><p></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"This project initiative is focused on the systematic replacement of end-of-life (EOL) laptops across the organization.\n\nIn parallel, the engagement includes upgrading desktop systems to Windows 11.\n\nAdditionally, the project emphasizes performance optimization through memory upgrades. Functional RAM modules from decommissioned devices are carefully recovered, tested, and redeployed to enhance the performance of active laptops that remain within their service lifecycle.\n\nOverall, the initiative aims to improve device efficiency, extend hardware usability for NFI Industries\n\n**\\*\\*\\*DO NOT DISCUSS YOUR COMPENSATION & CLIENT CONTACT DETAILS (STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL) WITH ANYONE OUTSIDE OF AKKODIS\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Read all the below instructions carefully:**\n\n**1. Instructional Note for Technicians:** Please ensure the team thoroughly reviews the service description, Runbook, and checklist documents to fully understand the instructions. Upon task completion, they are required to:\n\n- Update the checklist.\n- Obtain a signature from the site Point of Contact.\n- Upload a photo of the signed document to the work order.\n- For every site unless the memory will be reused, please have the technician package it in the laptop box along with the old laptop.\n\n**2. Please contact the Primary Point of Contact after check In at site and after completion of work don't leave the site without informing the support contact and get their signature.**\n\n**3.** **Failing the above instructions will strictly lead to work order cancellation or may hamper the pay.**\n\n**4. Post successful completion of the work on site, please enter complete close out notes along with deliverables attached which is mandatory before marking the work order completed.**\n\n**In order to be paid for this work order ALL work must be completed: replacement, testing, return, requested photos and most all maintaining professionalism onsite.**\n\n- **﻿Mandatory Technical Briefing :** At least 48 hours before the scheduled task, the technician **must** call the **NFI IT Team** using the provided contact numbers. The goal is to verify technical requirements and address site-specific questions.\n- **Verification:** The technician must log the name of the NFI IT representative they spoke with in the Field Nation notes.\n- **Inquiry Protocol (Pre-Site):** Direct all **technical** questions to the NFI IT Team and all **scope/logistics** questions to the Akkodis Team at least 48 hours prior to arrival.\n- **Communication Standards:** Prompt acknowledgment of all Akkodis emails and messages is mandatory. Responses are expected within **4 hours** during business days.\n- **On-Site Execution:** Technicians must be fully self-sufficient and prepared upon arrival. Avoid asking repeated questions on-site that are explicitly covered in the **NFI Runbook** or **Scope documents**. Failure to follow the Runbook may lead to performance escalations or rating deductions.\n- **Required Tools & Hardware Verification:** The technician must confirm they possess all necessary hardware and tools required for the task prior to traveling to the site.\n- **The \"First Hour\" Milestone:** Technicians must provide a quick status update via the call or Field Nation after the **first 60 minutes** on-site (e.g., \"First 3 devices completed\").\n\n**Workflow:**\n\n**below are the device types NFI (Client)would like to have for each of the desktops. please add this to the list as part of the checklist.**\n\nPack station\n\nShipping station\n\neCommerce station\n\nVAS station\n\nCubiscan station\n\nReturns station\n\nWarehouse TV station\n\nMobile cart station","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T09:00","end":"2026-11-11T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4.5,"distance":64.88250510333793},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430253110}
{"job":{"id":20200881,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Meraki Deinstallation (Hard Start)","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of Work:</p><p>Meet with POC</p><p>Confirm equipment on site and collect ISP and SSID info</p><p>Remove equipment provided by customer</p><p>Prepare and package equipment to be returned</p><p>Collect required collateral and check out with Service Point support</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Materials:</p><p>LAN Tester,</p><p>RJ-45 Connector,</p><p>Label Maker</p><p>Cabling tools ( Push rods, Wire snake)</p><p>Cat5e cable tester</p><p>RJ45 crimper/Punch down tool</p><p>RJ45 Jacks and Plugs</p><p>Cat6 Keystone Jack</p><p>Zip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps</p><p><br></p><p>Required Collateral:</p><p>Photos of equipment removed/packaged</p><p>Checklist</p><p>Sign off</p><p>Any end points onsite</p><p>Confirmation equipment is working</p><p><br></p><p>**THESE LOCATIONS ARE GROUP HOMES**</p><p><br></p><p>Professionalism &amp; Respect &mdash; Treat the location as someone's home, not simply a job site. Be courteous, professional, and respectful of residents, caregivers, and the POC.</p><p><br></p><p>Empathy &amp; Patience &mdash; Be understanding and patient with individuals who may have intellectual, developmental, behavioral, mobility, or communication challenges.</p><p><br></p><p>Clear Communication &mdash; Introduce yourself, explain the purpose of the visit, confirm the scope with the POC, and communicate before entering rooms, moving items, or removing equipment.</p><p><br></p><p>Situational Awareness &amp; Adaptability &mdash; Recognize when a resident may be uncomfortable or distressed. Be willing to pause or adjust the work and follow the caregiver/POC's direction.</p><p><br></p><p>Discretion &amp; Respect for Privacy &mdash; Protect residents' dignity and privacy. Do not ask unnecessary personal or medical questions, discuss what is observed in the home, or take unauthorized photos.</p><p><br></p><p>Professional Appearance &amp; Dress &mdash; Technicians are entering managed residential homes and are expected to maintain a clean, professional appearance. A polo-style shirt is preferred. T-shirts with logos, graphics, or messaging and hats should not be worn. Pants should be clean, professional, free of holes, and not visibly worn or damaged. Shoes should be clean and appropriate for performing technical work safely.</p>","markdown":"Scope of Work:\n\nMeet with POC\n\nConfirm equipment on site and collect ISP and SSID info\n\nRemove equipment provided by customer\n\nPrepare and package equipment to be returned\n\nCollect required collateral and check out with Service Point support\n\nRequired Materials:\n\nLAN Tester,\n\nRJ-45 Connector,\n\nLabel Maker\n\nCabling tools ( Push rods, Wire snake)\n\nCat5e cable tester\n\nRJ45 crimper/Punch down tool\n\nRJ45 Jacks and Plugs\n\nCat6 Keystone Jack\n\nZip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps\n\nRequired Collateral:\n\nPhotos of equipment removed/packaged\n\nChecklist\n\nSign off\n\nAny end points onsite\n\nConfirmation equipment is working\n\n\\*\\*THESE LOCATIONS ARE GROUP HOMES\\*\\*\n\nProfessionalism & Respect — Treat the location as someone's home, not simply a job site. Be courteous, professional, and respectful of residents, caregivers, and the POC.\n\nEmpathy & Patience — Be understanding and patient with individuals who may have intellectual, developmental, behavioral, mobility, or communication challenges.\n\nClear Communication — Introduce yourself, explain the purpose of the visit, confirm the scope with the POC, and communicate before entering rooms, moving items, or removing equipment.\n\nSituational Awareness & Adaptability — Recognize when a resident may be uncomfortable or distressed. Be willing to pause or adjust the work and follow the caregiver/POC's direction.\n\nDiscretion & Respect for Privacy — Protect residents' dignity and privacy. Do not ask unnecessary personal or medical questions, discuss what is observed in the home, or take unauthorized photos.\n\nProfessional Appearance & Dress — Technicians are entering managed residential homes and are expected to maintain a clean, professional appearance. A polo-style shirt is preferred. T-shirts with logos, graphics, or messaging and hats should not be worn. Pants should be clean, professional, free of holes, and not visibly worn or damaged. Shoes should be clean and appropriate for performing technical work safely.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":29.749534800106826},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430259141}
{"job":{"id":20178583,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ClearCaptions","title":"Internet Caption Phone (PSTN) Installation and Training","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Join us in making an impact! ClearCaptions is dedicated to helping customers live a more independent life by connecting them to their loved ones via a captioned phone.</strong></p><p>Work order is located in a<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\"> </span><u>RESIDENTIAL SETTING</u> with <u>HARD-OF-HEARING</u> and/or <u>ELDERLY CUSTOMERS</u>.</p><ul><li>Patience, empathy, and kindness are paramount.</li><li>Thorough, hands-on customer training is imperative to the successful completion of this work order.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong></p><p><strong>Before Site Visit:</strong> <em>Approximately 30 minutes</em><strong> </strong></p><ul><li>Review all work order details, execute 24-hour advance customer courtesy call/text/voicemail, re-familiarize self on installation process via guidance material.</li><li>Phone kit will be onsite (kit does NOT include additional required tools listed).</li></ul><p><strong>At Site Visit:</strong><em> Approximately 1.25 - 2 hours</em></p><ul><li><u>Your Objective</u>: Customer is satisfied and able to use the fully operational phone independently and confidently by the time you leave site.</li><li><u>PHASE 1 - Customer Registration</u>: <em>Approximately 15-30 minutes</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Register and validate customer's identity, then unpack and set-up their phone. Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.</li><li><u>PHASE 2 - Phone Set-up</u>: <em>Approximately 15-30 minutes</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unpack and set-up customer's phone, in desired and effective location</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.</li><li><u>PHASE 3 - Customer Training</u>: <em>Approximately 45-60 minutes</em></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once customer registration, identity validation and phone installation are complete, the remainder of your visit should focus on training the customer to use their new phone with confidence and satisfaction.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This includes but is not limited to: placing and receiving test calls, adding contacts, setting up voicemail and/or connecting their current service, configuring their settings, and connecting them to ClearCaptions for the required Welcome Call.</li><li><u>Additional site-visit callouts</u>: %description.html%</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT NOTES &amp; EXPECTATIONS</u></strong></p><p><strong>Assignment:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><em><u>DO NOT send or bring any unauthorized persons to the customer's home</u></em></strong><em><u>,</u></em> including those part of a service company. Only the tech assigned to the WO is allowed onsite.</li></ul><p><strong>Visit Preparation:</strong></p><ul><li>Review the work order details and acknowledge (in Tasks) the guidance material attached to the work order to ensure a successful visit.</li><li><strong><em><u>Download and reference the Installation Checklist for detailed, step-by-step set-up requirements and customer training best practice</u></em>.</strong></li><li>The easy to read, flip through Phone Guide for training the customer can be found here:&nbsp;<strong>https://rb.gy/i4mdjy</strong> (PDF version for print or download is Documents section of the work order.)</li><li>Dress Code: Clean and presentable business casual attire. Slacks or jeans (no holes/patches), closed-toed shoes, and a polo shirt. No hats.</li></ul><p><strong>Scheduling &amp; Arrival:</strong></p><ul><li>ClearCaptions does not accept Technician&nbsp;requests to reschedule, as the hard start time has been coordinated with the end customer.&nbsp;If required for an unexpected reason,&nbsp;tech must Report a Problem on the work&nbsp;order&nbsp;selecting “I Can’t Make My Assignment”.&nbsp;This enables ClearCaptions to&nbsp;attempt&nbsp;re-assignment without&nbsp;impacting&nbsp;our&nbsp;customer.&nbsp;</li><li><strong><em><u>Technician must proceed to installation appointment as scheduled even if a customer does not respond to the required 24-hour advance courtesy call or their number is \"disconnected\"</u></em></strong><em>.</em> Customers are hard or hearing so may not realize you attempted to call until they have their new phone and ClearCaptions service.</li><li>Check-in + Check-out must be within 1 mile of site.</li><li><strong><em><u>You will be able to access the Customer Information when you are ON SITE and checked in</u></em>. </strong></li><li><strong><em><u>Please arrive at start time of WO</u></em></strong>. Too early or too late can disrupt the customer and the ability to complete the WO. We will not approve requests to edit time logs.</li><li>If customer is not home and not reachable <strong><em><u>after 15 min of hard start time</u></em></strong><em><u>,</u></em> to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site, or to report that an installation cannot be completed in full for any reason: call CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>. You must garner ClearCaptions' permission to leave site to allow for customer coordination, incomplete troubleshooting, and prevent rescheduling where reasonable.</li></ul><p><strong>When on Site:</strong></p><ul><li>The correct customer must be present for the entirety of the install (the registered user is listed under the Location Contact in this WO).</li><li><strong><em><u>Using your own or a customer's cellular 'hotspot' to connect a customer's phone to internet is strictly prohibited. Dedicated home internet service is required for caption service. Home internet is acceptable if delivered via a cellular network, and shared internet in assisted/group living facilities will suffice if/when connectivity speeds are sufficient.</u></em></strong></li><li><strong><em><u>Do not mount the phone and/or create any structural changes while onsite, even if customer requests it</u></em>.</strong> This includes, but is not limited to: drilling holes, running cables.</li><li>If an installation cannot be completed in full and/or is cancelled for specific reasons ClearCaptions will confirm return requirements. Call CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span> for further directions and use the pre-paid mailing label included in the phone kit box. Remember to enter this tracking number from the label into the Custom Field: \"Return Tracking Number\", as necessary.</li><li>Customer's&nbsp;<strong><em><u>Username&nbsp;and&nbsp;Password</u></em>&nbsp;</strong>are located under Buyer Custom Fields in the Work Order.&nbsp;If this information is not viewable ensure you are correctly checked in onsite and call CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>.</li><li>If a Technician encounters any threatening behavior from customer, caregiver, or persons on site upon arrival or during the site visit, they must use their judgement to leave the premise. Once in safety, please contact ClearCaptions Support immediately thereafter to report at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>.</li></ul><p><strong>Technician Payment:</strong></p><ul><li>The fixed rate is inclusive of the full scope.</li><li>All travel charges must be pre-approved via a counter offer prior to assignment and back-up receipts required at close out. We do not honor requests for travel expenses after assignment.</li><li>Expenses for tools/equipment must be requested with an uploaded receipt.</li><li><strong><em><u>Requesting or accepting any form of payment directly from a customer is in direct violation of ClearCaptions and FN Terms &amp; Conditions, and will result in further escalation</u></em>.</strong></li><li><strong><em><u>Use of \"Discounts\" feature to adjust pay is prohibited.</u></em></strong>&nbsp;Please document any issues under “Report a Problem” from the Work Order for proper review and adjustments.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>EXPECTATIONS &amp; REQUIREMENTS FOR FULL PAYMENT</u></strong></p><ol><li><u style=\"color: black;\">Registration and Consent Completed</u>: <span style=\"color: black;\">Facilitate customer in completing registration and signing required consent documentation via Customer Portal. Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.</span></li><li><u style=\"color: black;\">Customer ID Validation Passed</u>: <span style=\"color: black;\">Facilitate customer in completing identity validation in our Customer Portal (“DMS”). Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.</span></li><li><u>Paired Phone</u>: <span style=\"color: black;\">Customer’s device is installed in accordance with work order guidelines (VoIP or PSTN) and connected (paired) for captioning functionality. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.</span></li><li><u>Welcome Call Completed</u>: <span style=\"color: black;\">Facilitate customer with dialing into required line and associated case closed. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.</span></li><li><u>Customer Training</u>: <span style=\"color: black;\">Training executed in full and customer demonstrates clear understanding and usage competency. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.</span></li><li><u style=\"color: black;\">Work Order Task Completion</u><span style=\"color: black;\">: All required work order tasks are completed fully and accurately.</span></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CUSTOMER IDENTITY VALIDATION &amp; CONSENT</u></strong></p><ul><li>Please note that identity validation protocol is to be conducted and registration consents signed by customer via ClearCaptions' Portal outside of the in-phone set-up to gain consent and validate the customer's identity, as required by the FCC. Link provided in Task list.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\"><em><u>ONLY THE CUSTOMER can accept terms and consent.&nbsp;DO NOT&nbsp;consent on the customer's behalf</u></em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">; doing so is against compliance policy and will result in non-payment, being blocked by ClearCaptions, and filing a report to Field Nation Resolution for review. If at any point the customer expresses concern over the service, to request a copy of what they signed, or to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site contact CC Support </span> at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*************</del></span></li><li>THIS MUST BE COMPLETED IN FULL <u>BEFORE UNBOXING THE PHONE</u>.</li><li>If customer documentation upload is required, it must be legible to pass: no blur or content outside of the borders of the qualifying document. If they do not have proper documentation, please proceed and let ClearCaptions know during Welcome Call.</li><li><strong><em><u>ONLY the camera feature built into the DMS platform may be used to capture customer information</u></em></strong>. DO NOT use your device, and DO NOT upload any customer personal data into FN WO. Only upload to the DMS Platform.</li><li>If customer requests copy of the electronic records they signed, please advise them that they will need to retrieve them from ClearCaptions corporate. Contact CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>COMPLIANCE &amp; REPORTING</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">This is NOT an emergency line. Do NOT call this number for installation help, scheduling issues, or general questions.</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations,&nbsp;or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:</li><li><del>*********</del><del>***</del> |&nbsp;Compliance@ClearCaptions.com</li><li>&nbsp;All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator,&nbsp;or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website: https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TROUBLESHOOTING</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call CC Support at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span> for any issues, and/or to report and solution a phone's failure to auto update</li><li><u>For Cat5 Set-ups</u>: Plug the end of the Cat 5 Ethernet cable with the ferrite box into the phone</li><li>VoIP-PSTN Conversion Guide: Located in Additional Information &gt; Attached Files</li></ul>","markdown":"**Join us in making an impact! ClearCaptions is dedicated to helping customers live a more independent life by connecting them to their loved ones via a captioned phone.**\n\nWork order is located in a RESIDENTIAL SETTING with HARD-OF-HEARING and/or ELDERLY CUSTOMERS.\n\n- Patience, empathy, and kindness are paramount.\n- Thorough, hands-on customer training is imperative to the successful completion of this work order.\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\n**Before Site Visit:** *Approximately 30 minutes*\n\n- Review all work order details, execute 24-hour advance customer courtesy call/text/voicemail, re-familiarize self on installation process via guidance material.\n- Phone kit will be onsite (kit does NOT include additional required tools listed).\n\n**At Site Visit:** *Approximately 1.25 - 2 hours*\n\n- Your Objective: Customer is satisfied and able to use the fully operational phone independently and confidently by the time you leave site.\n- PHASE 1 - Customer Registration: *Approximately 15-30 minutes*\n- Register and validate customer's identity, then unpack and set-up their phone. Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.\n- PHASE 2 - Phone Set-up: *Approximately 15-30 minutes*\n- Unpack and set-up customer's phone, in desired and effective location\n- Be prepared to troubleshoot per attached installation guidance to ensure successful phone registration, pairing, and connectivity.\n- PHASE 3 - Customer Training: *Approximately 45-60 minutes*\n- Once customer registration, identity validation and phone installation are complete, the remainder of your visit should focus on training the customer to use their new phone with confidence and satisfaction.\n- This includes but is not limited to: placing and receiving test calls, adding contacts, setting up voicemail and/or connecting their current service, configuring their settings, and connecting them to ClearCaptions for the required Welcome Call.\n- Additional site-visit callouts: %description.html%\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES & EXPECTATIONS**\n\n**Assignment:**\n\n- ***DO NOT send or bring any unauthorized persons to the customer's home****,* including those part of a service company. Only the tech assigned to the WO is allowed onsite.\n\n**Visit Preparation:**\n\n- Review the work order details and acknowledge (in Tasks) the guidance material attached to the work order to ensure a successful visit.\n- ***Download and reference the Installation Checklist for detailed, step-by-step set-up requirements and customer training best practice*.**\n- The easy to read, flip through Phone Guide for training the customer can be found here: **<https://rb.gy/i4mdjy>** (PDF version for print or download is Documents section of the work order.)\n- Dress Code: Clean and presentable business casual attire. Slacks or jeans (no holes/patches), closed-toed shoes, and a polo shirt. No hats.\n\n**Scheduling & Arrival:**\n\n- ClearCaptions does not accept Technician requests to reschedule, as the hard start time has been coordinated with the end customer. If required for an unexpected reason, tech must Report a Problem on the work order selecting “I Can’t Make My Assignment”. This enables ClearCaptions to attempt re-assignment without impacting our customer.\n- ***Technician must proceed to installation appointment as scheduled even if a customer does not respond to the required 24-hour advance courtesy call or their number is \"disconnected\"****.* Customers are hard or hearing so may not realize you attempted to call until they have their new phone and ClearCaptions service.\n- Check-in + Check-out must be within 1 mile of site.\n- ***You will be able to access the Customer Information when you are ON SITE and checked in*.**\n- ***Please arrive at start time of WO***. Too early or too late can disrupt the customer and the ability to complete the WO. We will not approve requests to edit time logs.\n- If customer is not home and not reachable ***after 15 min of hard start time****,* to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site, or to report that an installation cannot be completed in full for any reason: call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. You must garner ClearCaptions' permission to leave site to allow for customer coordination, incomplete troubleshooting, and prevent rescheduling where reasonable.\n\n**When on Site:**\n\n- The correct customer must be present for the entirety of the install (the registered user is listed under the Location Contact in this WO).\n- ***Using your own or a customer's cellular 'hotspot' to connect a customer's phone to internet is strictly prohibited. Dedicated home internet service is required for caption service. Home internet is acceptable if delivered via a cellular network, and shared internet in assisted/group living facilities will suffice if/when connectivity speeds are sufficient.***\n- ***Do not mount the phone and/or create any structural changes while onsite, even if customer requests it*.** This includes, but is not limited to: drilling holes, running cables.\n- If an installation cannot be completed in full and/or is cancelled for specific reasons ClearCaptions will confirm return requirements. Call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for further directions and use the pre-paid mailing label included in the phone kit box. Remember to enter this tracking number from the label into the Custom Field: \"Return Tracking Number\", as necessary.\n- Customer's ***Username and Password*** are located under Buyer Custom Fields in the Work Order. If this information is not viewable ensure you are correctly checked in onsite and call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n- If a Technician encounters any threatening behavior from customer, caregiver, or persons on site upon arrival or during the site visit, they must use their judgement to leave the premise. Once in safety, please contact ClearCaptions Support immediately thereafter to report at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n**Technician Payment:**\n\n- The fixed rate is inclusive of the full scope.\n- All travel charges must be pre-approved via a counter offer prior to assignment and back-up receipts required at close out. We do not honor requests for travel expenses after assignment.\n- Expenses for tools/equipment must be requested with an uploaded receipt.\n- ***Requesting or accepting any form of payment directly from a customer is in direct violation of ClearCaptions and FN Terms & Conditions, and will result in further escalation*.**\n- ***Use of \"Discounts\" feature to adjust pay is prohibited.*** Please document any issues under “Report a Problem” from the Work Order for proper review and adjustments.\n\n**EXPECTATIONS & REQUIREMENTS FOR FULL PAYMENT**\n\n1. Registration and Consent Completed: Facilitate customer in completing registration and signing required consent documentation via Customer Portal. Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.\n2. Customer ID Validation Passed: Facilitate customer in completing identity validation in our Customer Portal (“DMS”). Verified by ClearCaptions on Welcome Call and/or Account records at work order dispositioning.\n3. Paired Phone: Customer’s device is installed in accordance with work order guidelines (VoIP or PSTN) and connected (paired) for captioning functionality. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n4. Welcome Call Completed: Facilitate customer with dialing into required line and associated case closed. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n5. Customer Training: Training executed in full and customer demonstrates clear understanding and usage competency. Verified by ClearCaptions at work order dispositioning.\n6. Work Order Task Completion: All required work order tasks are completed fully and accurately.\n\n**CUSTOMER IDENTITY VALIDATION & CONSENT**\n\n- Please note that identity validation protocol is to be conducted and registration consents signed by customer via ClearCaptions' Portal outside of the in-phone set-up to gain consent and validate the customer's identity, as required by the FCC. Link provided in Task list.\n- ***ONLY THE CUSTOMER can accept terms and consent. DO NOT consent on the customer's behalf***; doing so is against compliance policy and will result in non-payment, being blocked by ClearCaptions, and filing a report to Field Nation Resolution for review. If at any point the customer expresses concern over the service, to request a copy of what they signed, or to confirm if an approved Power-of-Attorney is on site contact CC Support  at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- THIS MUST BE COMPLETED IN FULL BEFORE UNBOXING THE PHONE.\n- If customer documentation upload is required, it must be legible to pass: no blur or content outside of the borders of the qualifying document. If they do not have proper documentation, please proceed and let ClearCaptions know during Welcome Call.\n- ***ONLY the camera feature built into the DMS platform may be used to capture customer information***. DO NOT use your device, and DO NOT upload any customer personal data into FN WO. Only upload to the DMS Platform.\n- If customer requests copy of the electronic records they signed, please advise them that they will need to retrieve them from ClearCaptions corporate. Contact CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n**COMPLIANCE & REPORTING**\n\n**This is NOT an emergency line. Do NOT call this number for installation help, scheduling issues, or general questions.**\n\n- If you observe fraud, customer eligibility issues (no hearing loss), regulatory non-compliance, data privacy violations, or ethical concerns during installation, contact ClearCaptions Compliance:\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* | Compliance@ClearCaptions.com\n- All reports are investigated confidentially with whistleblower protections. You may also report to the FCC, TRS Fund Administrator, or law enforcement agencies. Additional information can be found on the FCC website: <https://www.fcc.gov/ipcts>\n\n**TROUBLESHOOTING**\n\n- Call CC Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for any issues, and/or to report and solution a phone's failure to auto update\n- For Cat5 Set-ups: Plug the end of the Cat 5 Ethernet cable with the ferrite box into the phone\n- VoIP-PSTN Conversion Guide: Located in Additional Information > Attached Files","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-24T10:00","end":"2026-10-24T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":86.63947500058995},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:0