{"job":{"id":20186803,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Quality Sign and Marquee","title":"Disney: Ice Age: Boiling Point Standee","description":{"html":"<p>BE SURE TO CHECK THE THEATRE SHOW TIMES PRIOR TO ARRIVAL (Via Google), QSM WILL NOT PAY FOR VISITS WHERE THE THEATRE WAS NOT YET OPEN FOR THE DAY. ANY WORK ORDER SUBMITTED FOR PAYMENT BECAUSE THE THEATRE WAS CLOSED AT THE TIME OF ARRIVAL WILL BE DENIED. PROVIDER ACCEPTING THE WORK MUST BE THE PROVIDER COMPLETING THE TASK.</p><p>BE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER, YOU AGREE TO THE FOLLOWING:</p><p>If the provider is unable to complete the standee for any reason, they agree to reduce the work order to a total trip charge of $30.00, this includes if the theatre refuses the installation or cannot locate the standee.</p><p>If the provider arrives and finds the standee is already installed, they must inspect to make sure it is built properly, take the necessary photos and submit for <strong>HALF (50%)</strong> of the installation rate.</p><p>SCOPE OF WORK:</p><p>The provider is asked to confirm the standee has arrived (tracking attached to this workorder) before visiting the location. Once confirmed, plan to visit the location, locate the pre-shipped theatrical standee for<strong> Ice Age: Boiling Point</strong>, build the display according to the attached instruction sheet, and place in a prominent location within the theatre lobby. We are requesting (2) installation photos, 1 showing the standee properly installed and 1 showing the placement in the theatre. Keep in mind we want to see the display from a distance so we can see what is around the display.</p><p>The average installer has completed the standee in <strong>1-2 hours</strong>, please plan accordingly. The Instruction Sheet can be downloaded from the link below, please familiarize yourself with it before heading to your locations.</p><p>THIS IS A CHALLENGING INSTALLATION, THE INSTRUCTIONS MUST BE REVIEWED AND UNDERSTOOD PRIOR TO VISITING THE LOCATION.</p>","markdown":"BE SURE TO CHECK THE THEATRE SHOW TIMES PRIOR TO ARRIVAL (Via Google), QSM WILL NOT PAY FOR VISITS WHERE THE THEATRE WAS NOT YET OPEN FOR THE DAY. ANY WORK ORDER SUBMITTED FOR PAYMENT BECAUSE THE THEATRE WAS CLOSED AT THE TIME OF ARRIVAL WILL BE DENIED. PROVIDER ACCEPTING THE WORK MUST BE THE PROVIDER COMPLETING THE TASK.\n\nBE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER, YOU AGREE TO THE FOLLOWING:\n\nIf the provider is unable to complete the standee for any reason, they agree to reduce the work order to a total trip charge of $30.00, this includes if the theatre refuses the installation or cannot locate the standee.\n\nIf the provider arrives and finds the standee is already installed, they must inspect to make sure it is built properly, take the necessary photos and submit for **HALF (50%)** of the installation rate.\n\nSCOPE OF WORK:\n\nThe provider is asked to confirm the standee has arrived (tracking attached to this workorder) before visiting the location. Once confirmed, plan to visit the location, locate the pre-shipped theatrical standee for **Ice Age: Boiling Point**, build the display according to the attached instruction sheet, and place in a prominent location within the theatre lobby. We are requesting (2) installation photos, 1 showing the standee properly installed and 1 showing the placement in the theatre. Keep in mind we want to see the display from a distance so we can see what is around the display.\n\nThe average installer has completed the standee in **1-2 hours**, please plan accordingly. The Instruction Sheet can be downloaded from the link below, please familiarize yourself with it before heading to your locations.\n\nTHIS IS A CHALLENGING INSTALLATION, THE INSTRUCTIONS MUST BE REVIEWED AND UNDERSTOOD PRIOR TO VISITING THE LOCATION.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T12:00","end":"2026-10-30T22:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8.583671285987108},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"Listen Audio Book"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430428337}
{"job":{"id":20187421,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Network Cutover of all IT Equipment - Assistant Tech 2 (prepare for 8 hours and potential cabling)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">A 5-6 hour site visit to cut the network and all IT equipment from the legacy Pep Boys to the new Mavis Tire network and IT equipment.&nbsp;All Pep Boys equipment will be de-installed and packed for pick up.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</li><li>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Cutover Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><p>----Prior to leaving site, the following must be completed:</p><ul><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Pictures to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with <del>*****</del> IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nA 5-6 hour site visit to cut the network and all IT equipment from the legacy Pep Boys to the new Mavis Tire network and IT equipment. All Pep Boys equipment will be de-installed and packed for pick up.\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)\n- 2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Cutover Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n\\----Prior to leaving site, the following must be completed:\n\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Pictures to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00","end":"2026-10-26T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":330},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":11.79135493027718},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $330 (countered: $360) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792430439003}
{"job":{"id":20184386,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Mesmerize","title":"Poster Installation | 10 Minutes Per Site | $20/site","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>**All travel expenses must be approved prior to being assigned.**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>﻿**All work performed and materials submitted must be authentic and unaltered; AI-generated content or images are not accepted. Violations will be reported to Field Nation per platform guidelines.**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Mailing address required upon acceptance of job. Lack of communication on provider side will be seen as provider abandoning job and job will be re-posted after 2 days of no communication.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>**<u>IMPORTANT</u>: We will be mailing the materials directly to you for this work order. The dates, as such, are tentative until materials have been delivered to you.**</strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p><p>Providers will visit sites listed on the work order to install posters. Good quality photos of the poster will be needed at all sites.</p><p><strong><u>PRE-SITE</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide mailing address in work order messages</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Review attached example photos in work order for quality standards</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Confirm site's hours of operation prior to arriving as they may be different than what is on the work order</strong></p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Complete any Prep Tasks in the Field Nation app</p><p><strong><u>TASKS FOR THE JOB WILL INCLUDE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Receive package(s) of&nbsp;posters</li><li>Enter location on list (<strong><u>Routing is up to you, please ensure the location is open before visiting by either looking it up online or calling them)</u></strong>.</li><li><strong>Speak to the manager/staff on duty, politely introduce yourself in a professional manner. Ask if you can install the poster(s)</strong></li><li><strong>Please place the poster(s) flat on an interior wall (not outside). Avoid installing on a window, counter, or drink cooler, if possible</strong></li><li><strong>Please avoid using tape to hang the poster(s). There is self-adhesive on the back of the poster(s)</strong></li><li>Once all materials are posted: Upload required photos in the Field Nation app</li><li>After photos have been uploaded, add closeout notes in the Field Nation app, thank them and move on to the next site</li></ul><p><strong>FAQ:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Provider must have permission to post materials on site. If you do not have permission to post the materials, please take a photo of the outside of the building and upload to Field Nation. Provider will be paid even if the location refuses the materials as long as Provider has taken a photo of the building as proof of visit.</strong></li><li><strong>Poster must be fully adhered and flat on the inside wall (no loose corners and/or edges) or Provider will be asked to return to site(s) in order to correct the work for no additional compensation. If Provider refuses to correct any issues, they will not be paid for any incorrect work done at site(s).</strong></li><li><strong>Take straight on photos, not from the side. We must be able to see the whole poster in the photo. Any photo(s) taken from an angle or where the entire poster is not visible, Provider will be asked to retake photo(s), or we will not pay for that site.</strong></li><li><strong>When you have finished the work order, please ask work order manager for return label to return any unused materials.</strong></li><li><strong>If you run into any issues or have any questions, please communicate through Field Nation messages so our entire team can assist you.</strong></li></ol>","markdown":"**\\*\\*All travel expenses must be approved prior to being assigned.\\*\\***\n\n**﻿\\*\\*All work performed and materials submitted must be authentic and unaltered; AI-generated content or images are not accepted. Violations will be reported to Field Nation per platform guidelines.\\*\\***\n\n**Mailing address required upon acceptance of job. Lack of communication on provider side will be seen as provider abandoning job and job will be re-posted after 2 days of no communication.**\n\n**\\*\\*IMPORTANT: We will be mailing the materials directly to you for this work order. The dates, as such, are tentative until materials have been delivered to you.\\*\\***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nProviders will visit sites listed on the work order to install posters. Good quality photos of the poster will be needed at all sites.\n\n**PRE-SITE**\n\n1\\. Provide mailing address in work order messages\n\n2\\. Review attached example photos in work order for quality standards\n\n3\\. **Confirm site's hours of operation prior to arriving as they may be different than what is on the work order**\n\n4\\. Complete any Prep Tasks in the Field Nation app\n\n**TASKS FOR THE JOB WILL INCLUDE:**\n\n- Receive package(s) of posters\n- Enter location on list (**Routing is up to you, please ensure the location is open before visiting by either looking it up online or calling them)**.\n- **Speak to the manager/staff on duty, politely introduce yourself in a professional manner. Ask if you can install the poster(s)**\n- **Please place the poster(s) flat on an interior wall (not outside). Avoid installing on a window, counter, or drink cooler, if possible**\n- **Please avoid using tape to hang the poster(s). There is self-adhesive on the back of the poster(s)**\n- Once all materials are posted: Upload required photos in the Field Nation app\n- After photos have been uploaded, add closeout notes in the Field Nation app, thank them and move on to the next site\n\n**FAQ:**\n\n1. **Provider must have permission to post materials on site. If you do not have permission to post the materials, please take a photo of the outside of the building and upload to Field Nation. Provider will be paid even if the location refuses the materials as long as Provider has taken a photo of the building as proof of visit.**\n2. **Poster must be fully adhered and flat on the inside wall (no loose corners and/or edges) or Provider will be asked to return to site(s) in order to correct the work for no additional compensation. If Provider refuses to correct any issues, they will not be paid for any incorrect work done at site(s).**\n3. **Take straight on photos, not from the side. We must be able to see the whole poster in the photo. Any photo(s) taken from an angle or where the entire poster is not visible, Provider will be asked to retake photo(s), or we will not pay for that site.**\n4. **When you have finished the work order, please ask work order manager for return label to return any unused materials.**\n5. **If you run into any issues or have any questions, please communicate through Field Nation messages so our entire team can assist you.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T09:00","end":"2026-10-19T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-19T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":20,"max":20},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":27.97675367609465},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/19/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"Listen Audio Book"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summ