{"job":{"id":20140786,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Worldlink Integration Group","title":"Replacement Kiosk Installation - Ticket Number # 05818704","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:</strong></p><p><strong>- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out</strong></p><p><strong>- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)</strong></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>COMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** **************** ** *** ************ ********</del></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ******** ************</del></strong></p><p><strong>After checking in with Worldlink: 210-756-8651</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Tech to meet with On-site contact: Contact information in the \"location notes\" of this work order. <strong><u>The technician must contact World Link support before starting work and inform World Link when the task is finished. A conference call will then be arranged with the Nextep Helpdesk Desk to confirm the tasks completed.</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*** *** ****** ****** **** ***** ** ****** *** ********* ******* **** ******* *** *********</del></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>-Basic tool kit</p><p>-Screwdriver</p><p>-USB keyboard</p><p>-Security Hex key/Allen wrench set</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Install the replacement kiosk, connect all required hardware and peripherals, and verify that the kiosk is powered on and functioning properly.</p><p>Check in with the onsite contact upon arrival.</p><p>Locate the existing kiosk and the replacement unit.</p><p>Verify that the replacement kiosk and required components are available and free from visible damage.</p><p>Safely disconnect and remove the existing kiosk, if applicable.</p><p>Assemble and install the replacement kiosk in the designated location.</p><p>Connect power, network, and all applicable peripherals.</p><p>Ensure all cables and connections are secure and properly organized.</p><p>Power on the replacement kiosk and verify that it starts up correctly.</p><p>Confirm network connectivity and that connected peripherals are recognized.</p><p>Contact the support team for software installation, configuration, or additional troubleshooting if required.</p><p>Test the kiosk to confirm it is operational.</p><p>Do not make unauthorized hardware, software, or network configuration changes.</p><p>Technicians must check in and out with World Link, on-site Contact, and Nextep Support to collaborate to finish the tasks and confirm the photos.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Pictures</strong></p><p>Existing kiosk before removal, if applicable</p><p>Replacement kiosk and components before installation</p><p>Installation in progress</p><p>Power and network connections</p><p>Connected peripherals</p><p>Completed kiosk installation</p><p>Powered-on kiosk and final setup</p><p>Any damaged or missing components</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p>- Basic work order form completely filled out and signed</p><p>Photos:</p><p>- Picture of work completed, showing everything fully functional</p><p><br></p><p><strong>\"All the docs attached to this WO, are for internal use and not to be left with the on-site staffs\"</strong></p><p><strong>Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p><p><strong>Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p>","markdown":"**WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:**\n\n**- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out**\n\n**- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)**\n\n**IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.**\n\nCOMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**After checking in with Worldlink: 210-756-8651**\n\nTech to meet with On-site contact: Contact information in the \"location notes\" of this work order. **The technician must contact World Link support before starting work and inform World Link when the task is finished. A conference call will then be arranged with the Nextep Helpdesk Desk to confirm the tasks completed.**\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n-Basic tool kit\n\n-Screwdriver\n\n-USB keyboard\n\n-Security Hex key/Allen wrench set\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nInstall the replacement kiosk, connect all required hardware and peripherals, and verify that the kiosk is powered on and functioning properly.\n\nCheck in with the onsite contact upon arrival.\n\nLocate the existing kiosk and the replacement unit.\n\nVerify that the replacement kiosk and required components are available and free from visible damage.\n\nSafely disconnect and remove the existing kiosk, if applicable.\n\nAssemble and install the replacement kiosk in the designated location.\n\nConnect power, network, and all applicable peripherals.\n\nEnsure all cables and connections are secure and properly organized.\n\nPower on the replacement kiosk and verify that it starts up correctly.\n\nConfirm network connectivity and that connected peripherals are recognized.\n\nContact the support team for software installation, configuration, or additional troubleshooting if required.\n\nTest the kiosk to confirm it is operational.\n\nDo not make unauthorized hardware, software, or network configuration changes.\n\nTechnicians must check in and out with World Link, on-site Contact, and Nextep Support to collaborate to finish the tasks and confirm the photos.\n\n**Required Pictures**\n\nExisting kiosk before removal, if applicable\n\nReplacement kiosk and components before installation\n\nInstallation in progress\n\nPower and network connections\n\nConnected peripherals\n\nCompleted kiosk installation\n\nPowered-on kiosk and final setup\n\nAny damaged or missing components\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n\\- Basic work order form completely filled out and signed\n\nPhotos:\n\n\\- Picture of work completed, showing everything fully functional\n\n**\"All the docs attached to this WO, are for internal use and not to be left with the on-site staffs\"**\n\n**Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)**\n\n**Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-20T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":90},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17.609270032088773},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792436002563}
{"job":{"id":20201466,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"TruGreen Network Refresh | Site: 5535 Raleigh, NC","description":{"html":"<p>Network Equipment Refresh</p>\n<p>Equipment being Shipped &amp; Work to be done:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>(2) Juniper EX4000-48MP - with SFPs</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To be placed in existing MDF floor rack</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Removing the old Cisco 2960x Switches</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reconnect patch panels to new Juniper switches</li>\n<li>(4) Juniper Mist AP45</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To be placed in accordance with the attached diagram</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Remove the existing Cisco AP</li>\n<li>(1) APC Smart-UPS</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To be placed on the bottom existing floor rack</li>\n<li>(1) APC Nema PDU</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To be mounted in the MDF floor rack</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect New Juniper Switches to APC PDU</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect existing Fortinet FW and ISP equipment power to APC PDU</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Before Going Onsite</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Review the entire work order.</li>\n<li>Review all attached installation instructions.</li>\n<li>Review the site-specific floor plan / AP diagram.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Minimum Required Tools</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Console cable</li>\n<li>Cable toner/tester</li>\n<li>Working label maker with labels</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>Patch cables</li>\n<li>Cat6 cable, keystones, and cable ends when required</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Upon Arrival</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Locate the MDF/network rack.</li>\n<li>Locate the existing equipment being replaced.</li>\n<li>Verify the new equipment before installation.</li>\n<li>Inspect the work area for anything that may prevent completion.</li>\n<li>Contact the Work Order Manager if site conditions or equipment do not match the work order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Testing &amp; Verification</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify all installed equipment has power.</li>\n<li>Verify all required network connections are connected.</li>\n<li>Test new or modified cabling when applicable.</li>\n<li>Contact the designated network/technical support for configuration or validation when required.</li>\n<li>Report equipment, cabling, port, or connectivity issues before leaving the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Deliverables</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Minimum Before Photos listed in task list</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Minimum After Photos listed in task list</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Before photos must be taken before any equipment or cabling is disconnected. After photos must clearly show the completed work. All required photos and documentation must be uploaded to the work order before leaving the site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Minimum Requirements Before Leaving Site</p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT LEAVE THE SITE UNTIL THE REQUIRED WORK IS COMPLETE OR THE WORK ORDER MANAGER HAS BEEN CONTACTED.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete all assigned installation tasks.</li>\n<li>Complete all required cabling and connections.</li>\n<li>Complete required testing and validation.</li>\n<li>Complete all required documentation.</li>\n<li>Take all required photos.</li>\n<li>Upload required documents and photos to the work order.</li>\n<li>Report anything that could not be completed.</li>\n<li>Report missing, damaged, or incorrect equipment.</li>\n<li>Obtain approval for additional onsite time with work order manager <strong>before</strong> exceeding the estimated time.</li>\n<li>Contact the Work Order Manager before leaving if any part of the scope remains incomplete.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Material Reimbursement:</strong></p>\n<p>Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot</p>\n<p>Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea</p>\n<p>Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea</p>\n<p>Faceplate $3.50 / ea</p>\n<p>Keystones $5.00/ea</p>\n<p>Cable ends $2.50/ea&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p>\n<p>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The minimum requirements state that additional onsite time must be approved before the estimated time has elapsed and that leaving without contacting the Work Order Manager when tasks are not correctly completed can result in a minimum 25% payment deduction.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Escalation</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact the Work Order Manager with any questions or issues while onsite.</li>\n<li>Immediately report anything preventing completion of the scope.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not leave the site with unresolved or incomplete work without contacting the Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Network Equipment Refresh\n\nEquipment being Shipped & Work to be done:\n\n- (2) Juniper EX4000-48MP - with SFPs\n- To be placed in existing MDF floor rack\n- Removing the old Cisco 2960x Switches\n- Reconnect patch panels to new Juniper switches\n- (4) Juniper Mist AP45\n- To be placed in accordance with the attached diagram\n- Remove the existing Cisco AP\n- (1) APC Smart-UPS\n- To be placed on the bottom existing floor rack\n- (1) APC Nema PDU\n- To be mounted in the MDF floor rack\n- Connect New Juniper Switches to APC PDU\n- Connect existing Fortinet FW and ISP equipment power to APC PDU\n\nBefore Going Onsite\n\n- Review the entire work order.\n- Review all attached installation instructions.\n- Review the site-specific floor plan / AP diagram.\n\nMinimum Required Tools\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cable\n- Cable toner/tester\n- Working label maker with labels\n- Crimper\n- Patch cables\n- Cat6 cable, keystones, and cable ends when required\n\nUpon Arrival\n\n- Check in with the onsite contact.\n- Locate the MDF/network rack.\n- Locate the existing equipment being replaced.\n- Verify the new equipment before installation.\n- Inspect the work area for anything that may prevent completion.\n- Contact the Work Order Manager if site conditions or equipment do not match the work order.\n\nTesting & Verification\n\n- Verify all installed equipment has power.\n- Verify all required network connections are connected.\n- Test new or modified cabling when applicable.\n- Contact the designated network/technical support for configuration or validation when required.\n- Report equipment, cabling, port, or connectivity issues before leaving the site.\n\nDeliverables\n\n- **Minimum Before Photos listed in task list**\n- **Minimum After Photos listed in task list**\n- **Before photos must be taken before any equipment or cabling is disconnected. After photos must clearly show the completed work. All required photos and documentation must be uploaded to the work order before leaving the site.**\n\nMinimum Requirements Before Leaving Site\n\n**DO NOT LEAVE THE SITE UNTIL THE REQUIRED WORK IS COMPLETE OR THE WORK ORDER MANAGER HAS BEEN CONTACTED.**\n\n- Complete all assigned installation tasks.\n- Complete all required cabling and connections.\n- Complete required testing and validation.\n- Complete all required documentation.\n- Take all required photos.\n- Upload required documents and photos to the work order.\n- Report anything that could not be completed.\n- Report missing, damaged, or incorrect equipment.\n- Obtain approval for additional onsite time with work order manager **before** exceeding the estimated time.\n- Contact the Work Order Manager before leaving if any part of the scope remains incomplete.\n\n**Material Reimbursement:**\n\nCat6 Cables .52 cents per foot\n\nCat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea\n\nCat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea\n\nFaceplate $3.50 / ea\n\nKeystones $5.00/ea\n\nCable ends $2.50/ea\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nPolo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes\n\nThe minimum requirements state that additional onsite time must be approved before the estimated time has elapsed and that leaving without contacting the Work Order Manager when tasks are not correctly completed can result in a minimum 25% payment deduction.\n\nEscalation\n\n- Contact the Work Order Manager with any questions or issues while onsite.\n- Immediately report anything preventing completion of the scope.\n- **Do not leave the site with unresolved or incomplete work without contacting the Work Order Manager.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T08:00","end":"2026-11-02T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":360},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":14.14407540358088},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $360 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792436211712}
