:</strong></p><p>-Basic tool kit</p><p>-Screwdriver</p><p>-USB keyboard</p><p>-Security Hex key/Allen wrench set</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Install the replacement kiosk, connect all required hardware and peripherals, and verify that the kiosk is powered on and functioning properly.</p><p>Check in with the onsite contact upon arrival.</p><p>Locate the existing kiosk and the replacement unit.</p><p>Verify that the replacement kiosk and required components are available and free from visible damage.</p><p>Safely disconnect and remove the existing kiosk, if applicable.</p><p>Assemble and install the replacement kiosk in the designated location.</p><p>Connect power, network, and all applicable peripherals.</p><p>Ensure all cables and connections are secure and properly organized.</p><p>Power on the replacement kiosk and verify that it starts up correctly.</p><p>Confirm network connectivity and that connected peripherals are recognized.</p><p>Contact the support team for software installation, configuration, or additional troubleshooting if required.</p><p>Test the kiosk to confirm it is operational.</p><p>Do not make unauthorized hardware, software, or network configuration changes.</p><p>Technicians must check in and out with World Link, on-site Contact, and Nextep Support to collaborate to finish the tasks and confirm the photos.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Pictures</strong></p><p>Existing kiosk before removal, if applicable</p><p>Replacement kiosk and components before installation</p><p>Installation in progress</p><p>Power and network connections</p><p>Connected peripherals</p><p>Completed kiosk installation</p><p>Powered-on kiosk and final setup</p><p>Any damaged or missing components</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p>- Basic work order form completely filled out and signed</p><p>Photos:</p><p>- Picture of work completed, showing everything fully functional</p><p><br></p><p><strong>\"All the docs attached to this WO, are for internal use and not to be left with the on-site staffs\"</strong></p><p><strong>Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p><p><strong>Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p>","markdown":"**WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:**\n\n**- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out**\n\n**- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)**\n\n**IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.**\n\nCOMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**After checking in with Worldlink: 210-756-8651**\n\nTech to meet with On-site contact: Contact information in the \"location notes\" of this work order. **The technician must contact World Link support before starting work and inform World Link when the task is finished. A conference call will then be arranged with the Nextep Helpdesk Desk to confirm the tasks completed.**\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n-Basic tool kit\n\n-Screwdriver\n\n-USB keyboard\n\n-Security Hex key/Allen wrench set\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nInstall the replacement kiosk, connect all required hardware and peripherals, and verify that the kiosk is powered on and functioning properly.\n\nCheck in with the onsite contact upon arrival.\n\nLocate the existing kiosk and the replacement unit.\n\nVerify that the replacement kiosk and required components are available and free from visible damage.\n\nSafely disconnect and remove the existing kiosk, if applicable.\n\nAssemble and install the replacement kiosk in the designated location.\n\nConnect power, network, and all applicable peripherals.\n\nEnsure all cables and connections are secure and properly organized.\n\nPower on the replacement kiosk and verify that it starts up correctly.\n\nConfirm network connectivity and that connected peripherals are recognized.\n\nContact the support team for software installation, configuration, or additional troubleshooting if required.\n\nTest the kiosk to confirm it is operational.\n\nDo not make unauthorized hardware, software, or network configuration changes.\n\nTechnicians must check in and out with World Link, on-site Contact, and Nextep Support to collaborate to finish the tasks and confirm the photos.\n\n**Required Pictures**\n\nExisting kiosk before removal, if applicable\n\nReplacement kiosk and components before installation\n\nInstallation in progress\n\nPower and network connections\n\nConnected peripherals\n\nCompleted kiosk installation\n\nPowered-on kiosk and final setup\n\nAny damaged or missing components\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n\\- Basic work order form completely filled out and signed\n\nPhotos:\n\n\\- Picture of work completed, showing everything fully functional\n\n**\"All the docs attached to this WO, are for internal use and not to be left with the on-site staffs\"**\n\n**Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)**\n\n**Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":90},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17.609270032088773},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"ac