{"job":{"id":20203146,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #238856 - Music Down | AMP replacement ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">TICKET SUMMARY:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER &amp; CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT &amp; RACK OPTIMIZATION</span></p><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">A technician is required on-site to install a new </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> and a </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">CSR-V Volume Control</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack to ensure long-term serviceability.</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATORY RULE:</strong> The technician must test all speaker line impedance ($\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect every speaker transformer tap to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.</li><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:</strong> Upon successful installation, box up the legacy hardware and stage it in a designated \"out of the way\" area on-site for local site disposal. Do not remove old equipment from the property.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for audio interface checks and local network verification)</li><li><strong>6–8ft Ladder &amp; Pull Rods / Fish Tape</strong> (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line)</li><li><strong>Multimeter &amp; Cable Tester / Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for speaker line impedance, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)</li><li><strong>Cat5e/6 &amp; 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:</strong> RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill &amp; Bits</strong> (Including mounting hardware for rack installation)</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong> (preferred) or zip ties, <strong>Label Maker</strong>, and packaging tape</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack and the volume control location. Collect the newly shipped JBL hardware box.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the SOW with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 2: CABLE PULL &amp; MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT</strong><ol><li><strong>CAT6 HOME RUN:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the <strong>T568B Standard</strong> and test continuity with your cable tester.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER WIRE TESTING:</strong> Power off the existing amplifier. Use your <strong>multimeter</strong> to measure and log resistance ($\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.</li><li><strong>TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:</strong> Access every 70V speaker in the facility using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load <strong>does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating</strong>.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT HOLD:</strong> Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). <strong>DO NOT</strong> power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION &amp; RACK OVERHAUL</strong><ol><li><strong>HARDWARE MOUNTING:</strong> Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new <strong>JBL CSA140Z</strong> amplifier in the rack frame and mount the <strong>CSR-V</strong> volume control on the wall.</li><li><strong>RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:</strong> Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.</li><li><strong>LABELING:</strong> Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 <strong>\"Volume Control\"</strong> and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier input block.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING &amp; VERIFICATION</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER ON:</strong> Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.</li><li><strong>AUDIO AUDIT:</strong> Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback and responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL &amp; CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:</strong> Box up the old hardware, mark it clearly as <strong>\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and stage it in the store's designated storage area. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drill dust, and packaging waste. Ensure the rack closet and volume control areas are left spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Amp &amp; Managed Rack:</strong> Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (<strong>Full view, cabinet door OPEN</strong>).</li><li>[ ] <strong>New CSR-V Installed:</strong> Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Readings:</strong> Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance measurements taken on the speaker lines.</li><li>[ ] <strong>T568B Termination Close-up:</strong> Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Hardware:</strong> Photo showing the old equipment boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support that audio telemetry and volume control performance are 100% operational.</li><li><strong>MOD:</strong> Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings, tap settings verified, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n**TICKET SUMMARY:** JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER & CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT & RACK OPTIMIZATION\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A technician is required on-site to install a new **JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier** and a **CSR-V Volume Control** wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack to ensure long-term serviceability.\n\n- **VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.\n- **SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATORY RULE:** The technician must test all speaker line impedance ($\\\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect every speaker transformer tap to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.\n- **DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:** Upon successful installation, box up the legacy hardware and stage it in a designated \"out of the way\" area on-site for local site disposal. Do not remove old equipment from the property.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & SUPPLIES**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for audio interface checks and local network verification)\n- **6–8ft Ladder & Pull Rods / Fish Tape** (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line)\n- **Multimeter & Cable Tester / Toner** (**Mandatory** for speaker line impedance, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)\n- **Cat5e/6 & 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:** RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill & Bits** (Including mounting hardware for rack installation)\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties** (preferred) or zip ties, **Label Maker**, and packaging tape\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack and the volume control location. Collect the newly shipped JBL hardware box.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the SOW with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: CABLE PULL & MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT**1. **CAT6 HOME RUN:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the **T568B Standard** and test continuity with your cable tester.\n2. **SPEAKER WIRE TESTING:** Power off the existing amplifier. Use your **multimeter** to measure and log resistance ($\\\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.\n3. **TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:** Access every 70V speaker in the facility using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load **does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating**.\n4. **SUPPORT HOLD:** Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). **DO NOT** power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.\n\n**PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION & RACK OVERHAUL**1. **HARDWARE MOUNTING:** Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new **JBL CSA140Z** amplifier in the rack frame and mount the **CSR-V** volume control on the wall.\n2. **RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:** Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using **Velcro ties**. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.\n3. **LABELING:** Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 **\"Volume Control\"** and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier input block.\n\n**PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING & VERIFICATION**1. **POWER ON:** Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.\n2. **AUDIO AUDIT:** Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback and responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.\n\n**PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL & CLEANUP**1. **STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:** Box up the old hardware, mark it clearly as **\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and stage it in the store's designated storage area. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drill dust, and packaging waste. Ensure the rack closet and volume control areas are left spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Amp & Managed Rack:** Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (**Full view, cabinet door OPEN**).\n- \\[ \\] **New CSR-V Installed:** Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.\n- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Readings:** Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance measurements taken on the speaker lines.\n- \\[ \\] **T568B Termination Close-up:** Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Hardware:** Photo showing the old equipment boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support that audio telemetry and volume control performance are 100% operational.\n- **MOD:** Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings, tap settings verified, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T08:45"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":250},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":18.477368189003485},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05976601 - 707 Green Valley Road, Pinnacle Bank, epik survey  (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Angier Police Department Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792438571341}
{"job":{"id":20203153,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GPD Holdings","title":"Uninstall Kiosk and Prep for Shipping - Must Source Pallet","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong></p><ul><li>Uninstall and remove a CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk and prepare for shipment</li><li><strong>You must acquire and bring a pallet and necessary packing/shipping supplies with you</strong> for this work order.</li><li>An angle grinder is required for this job – see “Required Equipment” below</li><li>To complete this job, you will be required to:</li></ul><ol><li>Unbolt and remove the kiosk</li><li>Disconnect the kiosk from power</li><li>Grind down anchors with angle grinder</li><li>Lock and secure the kiosk</li><li>Return the keys with the included prepaid label</li></ol><p><strong>This work order REQUIRES KEYS to access and service a kiosk! Do not head to job site without verifying that you have the correct keys first!</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Provided Equipment:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Keys</li><li>Return shipping label</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Equipment:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Digital camera or smartphone</li><li>Safety glasses</li><li>Stretch wrap</li><li>Packing tape</li><li>Shipping label (1 copy)</li><li>Bill of lading (3 copies)</li><li>Pallet</li><li>Ratchet straps</li><li>Angle grinder</li><li>Metal cut-off wheels</li><li>3/4 in OR 19mm flex head wrench, flex head ratcheting wrench, or socket &amp; flex head ratchet (a non flex head wrench may also work, however the available space inside the machine is limited)</li><li>Utility knife/scissors/snips</li><li>Metric wrench or socket set</li><li>Screwdriver set</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Provide shipping address to receive keys (overnighted to you via UPS once address is provided)</li><li>Provider <strong>must set</strong> an ETA</li><li>Print (1) copy of shipping label and (3) copies the bill of lading</li><li>Acquire necessary equipment to pack up kiosk for shipping (stretch wrap, ratchet straps, pallet)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>On Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Greet store owner/clerk, introduce yourself as a technician with CoinFlip. Advise them that you will be removing the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk and give an estimated time to completion.</li><li>Locate the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk.</li><li>Call CoinFlip Technician Support for initial check-in</li><li>Using access codes provided by CoinFlip, unlock and unbolt the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk.</li><li>Lift the kiosk off of the mounting studs.</li><li>Disconnect the kiosk from it’s power source. Feed and tuck the power cable into the back of the kiosk.</li><li><strong>Take a photo of the unbolted secured kiosk for your required deliverables.</strong></li><li>Use an angle grinder to flush the anchors down to the floor once the kiosk is removed.</li><li><strong>Take a photo of the ground down anchors for your required deliverables.</strong></li><li>Wrap the kiosk with stretch wrap to give it protection while it is in transit.</li><li>Secure the kiosk to the pallet with ratchet straps.</li><li>Affix the shipping label and one copy of the bill of lading to the kiosk securely, covering them fully with clear packing tape.</li><li>Loosely attach the remaining two copies of the bill of lading to the kiosk. These will be removed by the freight driver when they arrive to pickup the kiosk.</li><li><strong>Take a photo of the packed up kiosk as required for your deliverables.</strong></li><li><strong>Take a photo of the shipping label/BOL placement for your required deliverables.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Post Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Package up and drop off keys to UPS using provided return label. This must be done on the SAME or NEXT day after the job takes place. Take a photo of drop-off receipt from UPS for your required deliverables. This step is REQUIRED for the work order to be considered complete unless discussed otherwise.</li><li>Upload any additional relevant photos</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**\n\n- Uninstall and remove a CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk and prepare for shipment\n- **You must acquire and bring a pallet and necessary packing/shipping supplies with you** for this work order.\n- An angle grinder is required for this job – see “Required Equipment” below\n- To complete this job, you will be required to:\n\n1. Unbolt and remove the kiosk\n2. Disconnect the kiosk from power\n3. Grind down anchors with angle grinder\n4. Lock and secure the kiosk\n5. Return the keys with the included prepaid label\n\n**This work order REQUIRES KEYS to access and service a kiosk! Do not head to job site without verifying that you have the correct keys first!**\n\n**Provided Equipment:**\n\n- Keys\n- Return shipping label\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- Digital camera or smartphone\n- Safety glasses\n- Stretch wrap\n- Packing tape\n- Shipping label (1 copy)\n- Bill of lading (3 copies)\n- Pallet\n- Ratchet straps\n- Angle grinder\n- Metal cut-off wheels\n- 3/4 in OR 19mm flex head wrench, flex head ratcheting wrench, or socket & flex head ratchet (a non flex head wrench may also work, however the available space inside the machine is limited)\n- Utility knife/scissors/snips\n- Metric wrench or socket set\n- Screwdriver set\n\n**Pre Site Instructions:**\n\n- Provide shipping address to receive keys (overnighted to you via UPS once address is provided)\n- Provider **must set** an ETA\n- Print (1) copy of shipping label and (3) copies the bill of lading\n- Acquire necessary equipment to pack up kiosk for shipping (stretch wrap, ratchet straps, pallet)\n\n**On Site Instructions:**\n\n1. Greet store owner/clerk, introduce yourself as a technician with CoinFlip. Advise them that you will be removing the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk and give an estimated time to completion.\n2. Locate the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk.\n3. Call CoinFlip Technician Support for initial check-in\n4. Using access codes provided by CoinFlip, unlock and unbolt the CoinFlip Bitcoin ATM kiosk.\n5. Lift the kiosk off of the mounting studs.\n6. Disconnect the kiosk from it’s power source. Feed and tuck the power cable into the back of the kiosk.\n7. **Take a photo of the unbolted secured kiosk for your required deliverables.**\n8. Use an angle grinder to flush the anchors down to the floor once the kiosk is removed.\n9. **Take a photo of the ground down anchors for your required deliverables.**\n10. Wrap the kiosk with stretch wrap to give it protection while it is in transit.\n11. Secure the kiosk to the pallet with ratchet straps.\n12. Affix the shipping label and one copy of the bill of lading to the kiosk securely, covering them fully with clear packing tape.\n13. Loosely attach the remaining two copies of the bill of lading to the kiosk. These will be removed by the freight driver when they arrive to pickup the kiosk.\n14. **Take a photo of the packed up kiosk as required for your deliverables.**\n15. **Take a photo of the shipping label/BOL placement for your required deliverables.**\n\n**Post Site Instructions:**\n\n- Package up and drop off keys to UPS using provided return label. This must be done on the SAME or NEXT day after the job takes place. Take a photo of drop-off receipt from UPS for your required deliverables. This step is REQUIRED for the work order to be considered complete unless discussed otherwise.\n- Upload any additional relevant photos","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T10:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:30","latestStart":"2026-10-22T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":180,"max":180},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":47.315066799465455},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T0