><span style=\"color: black;\">by Public Transport, please share the mode of transport with total travel time.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Special</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Remarks, Notices and Reminders:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Engineer must</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">be dressed in business casual attire with proper footwear (Full-sleeve shirt,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">long trousers, Closed shoes).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Engineer must</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">carry basic Safety PPE Equipment Kit - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">glasses, earplugs)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Engineer must</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">bring: Data card (mobile data) or Internet Dongle, Mobile phone, Console cable,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Laptop (with admin account), and Label printer.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Regarding laptop, Engineer must confirm it is an Opensource</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Company-provided laptop if been asked by POC or Remote team onsite.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Engineer must join using the Teams credentials provided by FNG,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">not their personal account. In case of any issues, please contact the FNG</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Service Desk Team.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Engineer must carry a valid government ID card for site access.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Engineer must not mention being a freelancer or contractor. They</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">must introduce themselves as FNG employees or direct contractors.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; If travelling by Public Transport, Engineer must not discuss</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">anything about it with the Local POC.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Engineer must</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">contact the POC upon arrival. If not able to reach POC, escalate immediately to</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">your leadership team and inform FNG.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; Engineers must not leave site until all work is approved by FNG</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">internally and the Remote Team at Tech Mahindra.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; · Engineer must ensure the FE Report is signed by the POC</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">confirming the work completion (unless unavailable).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">o&nbsp;&nbsp; BASF Client is very sensitive – Engineer must not discuss anything</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">apart from work-related communication while they are onsite.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p>","markdown":"**Task description: -**  FE for below location Audio gate decom support at location .\n\n**Decommissioning Activities-**\n\nTechM team will perform the logical decommissioning and confirm completion to the FnG team.\n\nFE will safely disconnect and remove all cables from the rack.\n\nFE will remove the network devices from the rack.\n\nPack the hardware securely and hand it over to the local site contact.\n\nCapture and share the following details:\n\nNumber of boxes\n\nBox dimensions (L × W × H)\n\nWeight of each box\n\n**Expected Deliverables-**\n\nHardware packed and handed over to the local site contact.\n\nDecommissioning confirmation from TechM.\n\nPacking details including:\n\nNumber of boxes\n\nBox size/dimensions\n\nBox weight(s)\n\nEquipment to be brought by FE:\n\n1 Laptop with Windows 11 OS installed/updated.\n\n• Cisco USB Console Cable RJ45.\n\n• MS Teams desktop application installed.\n\n• Device labelling kit.\n\nNumber of Audio gateway – 3 devices .\n\n**Note : Kindly share the cost for Packing material carry out at the site. required material once decom completed , pack the devices and handover to local team**\n\n**Share the document of FE ,Background document and photo id**\n\n**Safety equipment** – Standard\n\n·\n\nEngineer must\n\ncarry the basic Safety PPE Kit – Standard (helmet, safety shoes, safety\n\nglasses, and earplugs).\n\n**Site address: -**\n\n**Local POC Detail: -**\n\nName:\n\nGEORGE MCEVOY\n\nMobile: +1-919-628-9024, Fax: +1 919 547-7572\n\nTodd Thornton\n\n'+1-919-706-2178\n\nDarryl Hurley\n\n'+1-919-624-3402\n\n **Safety equipment -**\n\no Field Engineer Access - Field engineer allowed, pre-registration\n\nrequired\n\no Hardware In/Out - To be communicated to site access contact and\n\ninstructions will be provided\n\no Technical Contact -\n\no Registration Information - Engineer details to be provided in\n\nadvance to site access contact\n\no Required Documents -\n\no Photography Allowed - Allowed, network devices only\n\n·\n\n**Questions**\n\n**to Confirm Before Visit:**\n\n·\n\nIs the FE\n\nable to communicate basic in Local Language along with\n\n English?\n\n·\n\n Is the\n\nFE travelling by Public Transport or Private Car?\n\n·\n\nIf traveling\n\nby Public Transport, please share the mode of transport with total travel time.\n\n·\n\n**Special**\n\n**Remarks, Notices and Reminders:**\n\n·\n\nEngineer must\n\nbe dressed in business casual attire with proper footwear (Full-sleeve shirt,\n\nlong trousers, Closed shoes).\n\n·\n\nEngineer must\n\ncarry basic Safety PPE Equipment Kit - Standard (Helmet, safety shoes, safety\n\nglasses, earplugs)\n\n·\n\nEngineer must\n\nbring: Data card (mobile data) or Internet Dongle, Mobile phone, Console cable,\n\nLaptop (with admin account), and Label printer.\n\no Regarding laptop, Engineer must confirm it is an Opensource\n\nCompany-provided laptop if been asked by POC or Remote team onsite.\n\no Engineer must join using the Teams credentials provided by FNG,\n\nnot their personal account. In case of any issues, please contact the FNG\n\nService Desk Team.\n\no Engineer must carry a valid government ID card for site access.\n\no Engineer must not mention being a freelancer or contractor. They\n\nmust introduce themselves as FNG employees or direct contractors.\n\no If travelling by Public Transport, Engineer must not discuss\n\nanything about it with the Local POC.\n\n·\n\nEngineer must\n\ncontact the POC upon arrival. If not able to reach POC, escalate immediately to\n\nyour leadership team and inform FNG.\n\no Engineers must not leave site until all work is approved by FNG\n\ninternally and the Remote Team at Tech Mahindra.\n\no · Engineer must ensure the FE Report is signed by the POC\n\nconfirming the work completion (unless unavailable).\n\no BASF Client is very sensitive – Engineer must not discuss anything\n\napart from work-related communication while they are onsite.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T09:00","end":"2026-1