{"job":{"id":20206000,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LI Group","title":"Retail Store – Soundbar Refresh (1 Installer)","description":{"html":"<p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and katherinef@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">This Work Order is an estimated 60-90-minute scope. This work requires 1 installer onsite (You must be the lead installer). You cannot sub out this work or have someone else in your company do it for you. The scheduled date and start time cannot be changed as they are confirmed dates and times with our client and these are time sensitive installs.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">At retail locations nationwide, you will update the existing soundbar fixture with new graphics, new media content, and ensure everything is working upon completion. Once refreshed, you will dispose of all trash, clean up your work area, obtain signoff, and take final photos. All deliverables must be submitted via the site specific Egnyte link to get approval to check out. </span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><u>BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.</span></p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">provided via emailed excel spreadsheet</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">) via text message.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, explain your scope of work, and locate the Samsung fixture. </span></p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Replace with newly shipped back graphic using existing hardware. </p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Replace the magnetic graphic on the front of the display. </p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove the current SD card media content and insert the new SD card into the media player located on the back of the fixture and complete the update process per instructions.</p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, disposing of the removed graphic and all trash. </p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.</p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take all required photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\" and submit to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site. <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $70 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount: </em><a href=\"https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><em>https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App</em></a></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*</em> <em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.</em></p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.</em></p>","markdown":"*\\*If additional travel compensation or a counteroffer is required on this bundle, you must discuss it with the Project Manager and receive approval prior to work start. Send an email to leahb@ligp.com and katherinef@ligp.com with the counter and we will get back to you to discuss. Message on the work order is not an acceptable Counter/Travel Request as it may be missed.*\n\nThis Work Order is an estimated 60-90-minute scope. This work requires 1 installer onsite (You must be the lead installer). You cannot sub out this work or have someone else in your company do it for you. The scheduled date and start time cannot be changed as they are confirmed dates and times with our client and these are time sensitive installs.\n\nAt retail locations nationwide, you will update the existing soundbar fixture with new graphics, new media content, and ensure everything is working upon completion. Once refreshed, you will dispose of all trash, clean up your work area, obtain signoff, and take final photos. All deliverables must be submitted via the site specific Egnyte link to get approval to check out.\n\n**BASIC Scope of Work (Refer to FULL SOW/Install Guide in Attachments):**\n\n1\\. Arrive onsite at the scheduled date and time. The schedule is confirmed and cannot be moved for any reason.\n\n2\\. Check in with your assigned LIGP Project Team Contact (**provided via emailed excel spreadsheet**) via text message.\n\n3\\. Upon arrival, greet the manager on duty, explain your scope of work, and locate the Samsung fixture.\n\n4\\. Replace with newly shipped back graphic using existing hardware.\n\n5\\. Replace the magnetic graphic on the front of the display.\n\n6\\. Remove the current SD card media content and insert the new SD card into the media player located on the back of the fixture and complete the update process per instructions.\n\n7\\. Clean up the workspace, including making sure all devices cords are tucked into the fixture, disposing of the removed graphic and all trash.\n\n8\\. Fill out the entire exit document and receive sign off from the manager on duty.\n\n9\\. Take all required photos per the \"Deliverable Requirements\" and submit to your site specific Egnyte link. Once your Project Team Contact approves them, you may leave the site.\n\n*\\*Aborted sites (meaning no work could be completed onsite) will be subject to a discounted rate of $50 for your visit and time. You must discount your work order by $70 so that the total payment will be $50. Previously agreed travel will be approved on top of this. Aborted sites still must obtain all deliverables (photos and signoff). Link to instructions for provider discount:* https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/How-To-Add-A-Discount-On-A-Work-Order-Web-App\n\n*\\*Work Orders will be paid typically a week after completion (as long as all required deliverables have been received). Payments will be processed by the Friday deadline each week but not guaranteed prior to that point regardless of Provider Premium Account Status. If a work order has not been paid after this time period, send an email to the Project Manager (or Assistant Project Manager) whose contact is listed in the documentation. Work Orders with additional expenses may take longer for payment to be processed as additional review is required prior to approval.*\n\n*\\*Routes are bundled and one tech can only accept one route. Please apply for desired route. You may apply to multiple routes in one area but we will only be able to assign one route since these dates/times are set. If you apply, you must take all jobs within the bundle.*\n\n*\\** *Estimated time onsite is a projected average for most installs. First time performing scope is expected to take longer, each site after should be near estimate.*\n\n*\\*Fixed payment is for completed scope and submitted/approved deliverables (as well as travel if specified). Estimated time listed does not reflect an hourly rate.*\n\n*\\*All deliverables must be sent and signed off by your assigned project contact BEFORE you leave each site. Work orders will not be paid unless this takes place. If you are missing any of the required deliverables listed in the documentation, the work order will not be paid.*\n\n*\\*You will need to read all attached documentation and the \"Welcome\" Email (sent to you 1-2 days prior to the install date) BEFORE arriving onsite. This will allow you to ask questions prior to the install and know the scope of work so you will not need to dig through the documentation for the first time onsite. Your project team contact will be in that email. We will also be holding multiple training conference calls prior to project start.*\n\n*\\*SOW must be followed without issue. Escalate to project team contact with any issue large or small.*\n\n*\\*Attached documentation may be updated with additional photos and best practices.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T06:00","end":"2026-11-09T07:30","latestStart":"2026-11-09T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":56.91598636976438},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493000108}
{"job":{"id":20205135,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Solari Service","title":"Onsite - TV FOR ROCKINGHAM - Rockingham, NC 28379, USA","description":{"html":"<p><em style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">The estimated time for completion is [3] hours</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Skill Requirements:</strong></p><p>N/A</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scope of Work/Steps:</strong></p><p>Arrive on-site and greet Cristina Antunes</p><p>-scope out the cafeteria and see where the user will want us to have the TV mounted and setup.</p><p>-Need to check and see if there's any nearby power sockets,</p><p>-Check if the WiFi is good in the location for a laptop</p><p>-see how viable the location is for what GGI is wanting for this one. Will want to see how much work will need to be done for the setup.</p><p>-Relay information to RTO for determination between support work and project work.</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Equipment Needed/Bring:</strong></p><p>N/A</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Terms and Conditions:</strong></p><p>Check-In / Check-Out Requirements</p><ul><li>Technician must check in and check out through the Field Nation platform.</li><li>Technician must remain onsite for the full approved service duration unless otherwise instructed by the Work Order Manager.</li><li>GPS and timestamp verification may be required.</li></ul><p>Communication Requirements</p><ul><li>Technician must maintain active communication before, during, and after the service event.</li><li>Technician must respond to calls/messages from dispatch or project management in a timely manner.</li><li>Failure to communicate delays, issues, or inability to complete work may result in reduced ratings and payment disputes.</li></ul><p>Arrival &amp; Professional Conduct</p><ul><li>Technician must arrive on time and dressed professionally.</li><li>Technician must behave respectfully toward store staff, customers, and management at all times.</li><li>Smoking, inappropriate language, harassment, or unprofessional behavior onsite will not be tolerated.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Photos &amp; Deliverables</p><p>Technician must upload all required deliverables before leaving site, including:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Asset labels/serial numbers</li><li>Cable routing photos</li><li>Speed tests or screenshots if applicable</li><li>Manager/customer sign-off where required</li><li>Detailed completion notes</li></ul><p>Blurry or incomplete documentation may delay approval and payment.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cabling Work</p><ul><li>No cabling work should be performed without prior approval if additional material or extended cable runs are required.</li><li>Technician must immediately notify the project manager if materials onsite are insufficient.</li><li>Partial or temporary cable runs should not be completed unless specifically approved.</li></ul><p>Escalation Procedure</p><p>Technician must immediately escalate:</p><ul><li>Missing equipment</li><li>Incorrect parts</li><li>Site access issues</li><li>Network outages</li><li>Unsafe conditions</li><li>Scope changes</li><li>Any issue preventing completion</li></ul><p>Unauthorized scope changes may not be compensated.</p><p><br></p><p>Safety Compliance</p><p>Technician agrees to follow all local safety regulations and site-specific safety requirements.</p><p>Technician is responsible for using ladders, electrical equipment, and tools safely.</p><p><br></p><p>Payment Terms</p><ul><li>Payment will only be processed after all deliverables are uploaded and approved.</li><li>False check-ins, inaccurate reporting, or incomplete work may result in payment disputes.</li><li>Additional work outside approved scope requires prior written approval through Field Nation messaging.</li></ul><p>Cancellation Policy</p><ul><li>If technician cancels within 24 hours of scheduled service, this may impact future work opportunities.</li><li>Repeated last-minute cancellations may result in removal from preferred technician lists.</li></ul><p>Confidentiality</p><p>Any customer information, credentials, network details, or business operations observed onsite must remain confidential and may not be shared with third parties.</p><p><br></p><p>Damage &amp; Liability</p><p>Technician is responsible for any damage caused due to negligence, misuse of tools, or failure to follow instructions.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion Standards</p><p>Work is considered complete only after:</p><ul><li>Customer confirms completion</li><li>Required testing is performed</li><li>All deliverables are uploaded</li><li>Project manager approves the work performed</li></ul>","markdown":"*The estimated time for completion is \\[3\\] hours*\n\n**Skill Requirements:**\n\nN/A\n\n**Scope of Work/Steps:**\n\nArrive on-site and greet Cristina Antunes\n\n-scope out the cafeteria and see where the user will want us to have the TV mounted and setup.\n\n-Need to check and see if there's any nearby power sockets,\n\n-Check if the WiFi is good in the location for a laptop\n\n-see how viable the location is for what GGI is wanting for this one. Will want to see how much work will need to be done for the setup.\n\n-Relay information to RTO for determination between support work and project work.\n\n**Equipment Needed/Bring:**\n\nN/A\n\n**Terms and Conditions:**\n\nCheck-In / Check-Out Requirements\n\n- Technician must check in and check out through the Field Nation platform.\n- Technician must remain onsite for the full approved service duration unless otherwise instructed by the Work Order Manager.\n- GPS and timestamp verification may be required.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Technician must maintain active communication before, during, and after the service event.\n- Technician must respond to calls/messages from dispatch or project management in a timely manner.\n- Failure to communicate delays, issues, or inability to complete work may result in reduced ratings and payment disputes.\n\nArrival & Professional Conduct\n\n- Technician must arrive on time and dressed professionally.\n- Technician must behave respectfully toward store staff, customers, and management at all times.\n- Smoking, inappropriate language, harassment, or unprofessional behavior onsite will not be tolerated.\n\nPhotos & Deliverables\n\nTechnician must upload all required deliverables before leaving site, including:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Asset labels/serial numbers\n- Cable routing photos\n- Speed tests or screenshots if applicable\n- Manager/customer sign-off where required\n- Detailed completion notes\n\nBlurry or incomplete documentation may delay approval and payment.\n\nCabling Work\n\n- No cabling work should be performed without prior approval if additional material or extended cable runs are required.\n- Technician must immediately notify the project manager if materials onsite are insufficient.\n- Partial or temporary cable runs should not be completed unless specifically approved.\n\nEscalation Procedure\n\nTechnician must immediately escalate:\n\n- Missing equipment\n- Incorrect parts\n- Site access issues\n- Network outages\n- Unsafe conditions\n- Scope changes\n- Any issue preventing completion\n\nUnauthorized scope changes may not be compensated.\n\nSafety Compliance\n\nTechnician agrees to follow all local safety regulations and site-specific safety requirements.\n\nTechnician is responsible for using ladders, electrical equipment, and tools safely.\n\nPayment Terms\n\n- Payment will only be processed after all deliverables are uploaded and approved.\n- False check-ins, inaccurate reporting, or incomplete work may result in payment disputes.\n- Additional work outside approved scope requires prior written approval through Field Nation messaging.\n\nCancellation Policy\n\n- If technician cancels within 24 hours of scheduled service, this may impact future work opportunities.\n- Repeated last-minute cancellations may result in removal from preferred technician lists.\n\nConfidentiality\n\nAny customer information, credentials, network details, or business operations observed onsite must remain confidential and may not be shared with third parties.\n\nDamage & Liability\n\nTechnician is responsible for any damage caused due to negligence, misuse of tools, or failure to follow instructions.\n\nCompletion Standards\n\nWork is considered complete only after:\n\n- Customer confirms completion\n- Required testing is performed\n- All deliverables are uploaded\n- Project manager approves the work performed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00","end":"2026-10-21T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":87.3736322118648},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end