{"job":{"id":20205578,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK | Sheetz 776|Package Sensor Replacement","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Must call WO Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p><p><strong>The technician is responsible for returning defective parts. Do not leave any parts on site, WO will not be paid until defective parts are mailed back.</strong></p><p><strong>NOTE: Call WO Manager and do not go to site if part has not delivered by your scheduled time.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><p><strong>Phillips Screwdriver (small)</strong></p><p><strong>Nut Driver Set</strong></p><p><strong>Compressed Air</strong></p><p><strong>Microfiber/Cleaning Cloth</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Issue: One or more package sensors within the Automated Returns Unit onsite is damaged/ giving faulty readings. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Cap Sensor Reading Test:</strong></p><p>Have site reconcile all returns within the ARK</p><p>Remove the bin &amp; cart</p><p>Flip bin upside down and place back on cart</p><p>Roll bin &amp; cart back into kiosk compartment</p><p>Call KIS to verify reading within admin menu</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work: </strong></p><ul><li>Check in with WO Manager</li><li><strong><u>PLEASE Replace all parts sent regardless of conditions onsite!</u></strong></li><li><strong>Removal:</strong></li><li>Disconnect sensor cables cable</li><li>Remove two small screws holding the sensor to the mount.</li><li>Check cable for damage</li><li>Mount new sensor using same hardware.</li><li>Connect cable</li><li>Test with Customer</li><li><strong>Call WO Manager to Check out</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.</p><p>346 S Arthur Ave.</p><p>Louisville, CO 80027</p>","markdown":"**Must call WO Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**The technician is responsibl