{"job":{"id":20205134,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Aethon","title":"Safety Check on Mobile delivery robot | Est. Time on Site: 1-2 hrs","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in PC repair, electronic experience, network troubleshooting, mechanical comprehension and customer service skills.&nbsp;</li><li>Please verify parts have been delivered before checking in. Call Level2 Service Team if not delivered to see if work can begin without delivery.</li><li>Technicians will be required to call Aethon Level 2 Service team to Check In, assist in repair, and investigation.&nbsp;</li><li>Overall scope will include working directly on TUG robot (AGV), Tug network, or additional infrastructure components (PC and Network Interface equipment).</li><li>May be working on multiple devices within the same facility.</li><li>We provide an estimate of the hours needed to perform the task. If the job exceeds that estimate we may continue to work with you until resolved.</li></ul><p><strong>Work Order Summary:</strong></p><ul><li>We will be doing a safety and preventive maintenance check on delivery robot for Lab</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Preferred slacks and polo shirt or button down shirt.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop ( able to connect with Cat5, manually configure IP address, ping network equipment, have \"ssh\" software for example Putty )&nbsp;</li><li>Network Patch Cable 6' minimum&nbsp;</li><li>25 ft Tape measure&nbsp;</li><li>T15 Torx Screwdriver&nbsp;</li><li>Heavy Duty Scraper&nbsp;</li><li>Adjustable Wrench QTY 2 PER TOOLKIT***&nbsp;</li><li>Craftsman No. 2 x 4 in. Screwdriver, Phillips&nbsp;</li><li>Craftsman No. 1x3 in. Screwdriver, Phillips&nbsp;</li><li>Craftsman 3/16 x 4 in. Screwdriver, Slotted&nbsp;</li><li>Craftsman 26pc. Std &amp; Metric Ball End Hex Key Set&nbsp;</li><li>Craftsman 13pc Hex Key Set, Ball End Metric Craftsman 1/2 in. Wrench, 6 pt. Combination&nbsp;</li><li>Allway 6-in-1 Putty Knife&nbsp;</li><li>3/4” 6pt. ½ in. drive Socket Universal Tool Precision Screwdriver Set (11pc)&nbsp;</li><li>5\" Mini Needle Nose Pliers Item Techni Tool&nbsp;</li><li>6\" Long Needle Nose Pliers Technic&nbsp;</li><li>4 1/2\"Mini Diagonal Pliers Techni Tool&nbsp;</li><li>Radio Shack digital multimeter Part&nbsp;</li><li>USB Compact Flash Card Reader&nbsp;</li><li>5-in-1 Painter's Tool with Stainless Steel Blade&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Prior to arrival, review service requests&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Upon arrival to facility, call into our Level 2 service team <del>**** ************* **** ******</del> to notify of arrival and receive work instructions.</li><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** </del></span>while onsite&nbsp;</li><li>Service team will be able to confirm what equipment will need to be worked on, and what location the equipment is in.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;If needed, Level 2 service team will then share what onsite contact must be met and updated.&nbsp;</li><li>Hardware replacement documentation will be provided prior to entry, or while onsite.</li></ul><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-out of work order</li><li>Provide the following information;&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Repair Tug/System.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Test equipment with L2 to confirm resolution.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Facilitate return of used/broken parts.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide customers with updates.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide customer name to L2.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Communicate off site time with L2 prior to departure</li><li>Capture the following pictures;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Missing or damaged parts.</li></ul><p><strong>Communication Directory:&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li>First call&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><del>************ </del>Contact Level2 for all Service Requests 2.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If unable to place a long distance call, use 1-866-873-9796, When asked to press a number for department, press * ( asterisk ) <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">1-866-873-9796,1-866-873-9796</span></li><li>After 5 minutes&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><del>*************** ***** ******** ** *** **** </del>Contact Level2 for all Service Requests, make second attempt&nbsp;</li><li>Immediately if no one is reached&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><del>**************</del>, our Help Desk is staffed 24x7, and can assist in routing your call to one of our Level2 Service Technicians or take a message&nbsp;</li><li>After 10 minutes without call back ,&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email <del>***************** </del>for our service group, if you have not been able to reach one of our Helpdesk or Level2 Service Technicians.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Include in email your name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.&nbsp;</li><li>After 30 minutes of no call back</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(Team Lead Cell Phone) Contact for assistance in reaching a Service Technician&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Leave a message with name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.</li><li>&nbsp;6. After 30 minutes of no call back&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">a. <del>************</del> Technical Service Manager, Contact for assistance in reaching a Service Technician&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Leave a message with name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.&nbsp;</li><li>7. After 10 minutes, start at Step 1.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in PC repair, electronic experience, network troubleshooting, mechanical comprehension and customer service skills.\n- Please verify parts have been delivered before checking in. Call Level2 Service Team if not delivered to see if work can begin without delivery.\n- Technicians will be required to call Aethon Level 2 Service team to Check In, assist in repair, and investigation.\n- Overall scope will include working directly on TUG robot (AGV), Tug network, or additional infrastructure components (PC and Network Interface equipment).\n- May be working on multiple devices within the same facility.\n- We provide an estimate of the hours needed to perform the task. If the job exceeds that estimate we may continue to work with you until resolved.\n\n**Work Order Summary:**\n\n- We will be doing a safety and preventive maintenance check on delivery robot for Lab\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Preferred slacks and polo shirt or button down shirt.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop ( able to connect with Cat5, manually configure IP address, ping network equipment, have \"ssh\" software for example Putty )\n- Network Patch Cable 6' minimum\n- 25 ft Tape measure\n- T15 Torx Screwdriver\n- Heavy Duty Scraper\n- Adjustable Wrench QTY 2 PER TOOLKIT\\*\\*\\*\n- Craftsman No. 2 x 4 in. Screwdriver, Phillips\n- Craftsman No. 1x3 in. Screwdriver, Phillips\n- Craftsman 3/16 x 4 in. Screwdriver, Slotted\n- Craftsman 26pc. Std & Metric Ball End Hex Key Set\n- Craftsman 13pc Hex Key Set, Ball End Metric Craftsman 1/2 in. Wrench, 6 pt. Combination\n- Allway 6-in-1 Putty Knife\n- 3/4” 6pt. ½ in. drive Socket Universal Tool Precision Screwdriver Set (11pc)\n- 5\" Mini Needle Nose Pliers Item Techni Tool\n- 6\" Long Needle Nose Pliers Technic\n- 4 1/2\"Mini Diagonal Pliers Techni Tool\n- Radio Shack digital multimeter Part\n- USB Compact Flash Card Reader\n- 5-in-1 Painter's Tool with Stainless Steel Blade\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n- Prior to arrival, review service requests\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n- Upon arrival to facility, call into our Level 2 service team \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to notify of arrival and receive work instructions.\n- Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* while onsite\n- Service team will be able to confirm what equipment will need to be worked on, and what location the equipment is in.\n- If needed, Level 2 service team will then share what onsite contact must be met and updated.\n- Hardware replacement documentation will be provided prior to entry, or while onsite.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Check-out of work order\n- Provide the following information;\n- Repair Tug/System.\n- Test equipment with L2 to confirm resolution.\n- Facilitate return of used/broken parts.\n- Provide customers with updates.\n- Provide customer name to L2.\n- Communicate off site time with L2 prior to departure\n- Capture the following pictures;\n- Missing or damaged parts.\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n1. First call\n2. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Contact Level2 for all Service Requests 2.\n3. If unable to place a long distance call, use 1-866-873-9796, When asked to press a number for department, press \\* ( asterisk ) 1-866-873-9796,1-866-873-9796\n4. After 5 minutes\n5. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* Contact Level2 for all Service Requests, make second attempt\n6. Immediately if no one is reached\n7. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, our Help Desk is staffed 24x7, and can assist in routing your call to one of our Level2 Service Technicians or take a message\n8. After 10 minutes without call back ,\n9. Email \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for our service group, if you have not been able to reach one of our Helpdesk or Level2 Service Technicians.\n10. Include in email your name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.\n11. After 30 minutes of no call back\n12. (Team Lead Cell Phone) Contact for assistance in reaching a Service Technician\n13. Leave a message with name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.\n14. 6. After 30 minutes of no call back\n15. a. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Technical Service Manager, Contact for assistance in reaching a Service Technician\n16. Leave a message with name, call back number, and facility the ticket was generated for.\n17. 7. After 10 minutes, start at Step 1.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T07:00","end":"2026-10-20T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-20T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":17.247955671232212},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $180\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10