{"job":{"id":20205130,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s &amp; locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) &amp; 0 AP(s)</u></strong></p>\n<p>Vendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:</p>\n<p>• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.</p>\n<p>• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.</p>\n<p>• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.</p>\n<p>• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.</p>\n<p>• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location</p>\n<p>• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.</p>\n<p>• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)</li>\n<li>After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)</li>\n<li><strong>After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.</strong></li>\n<li>Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of all items and devices surveyed</li>\n<li><em>Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Documents Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></li>\n<li><em>You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc</em></li>\n<li>ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li>Velcro for cable management</li>\n<li>Laptop:&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li>Console Cable</li>\n<li>Mobile Hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Tester</li>\n<li>Ladder&nbsp;(8'-10')</li>\n<li>Lift will be ordered if necessary</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"***NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s & locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!***\n\n**Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n\n**SOW:**\n\n**LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) & 0 AP(s)**\n\nVendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:\n\n• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.\n\n• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.\n\n• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.\n\n• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.\n\n• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.\n\n• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.\n\n• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location\n\n• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.\n\n• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer\n\n**DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)\n2. After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)\n3. **After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.**\n4. **NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.**\n5. Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)**\n\n- Pictures of all items and devices surveyed\n- *Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.*\n\n**Documents Required:**\n\n- **Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n- *You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.*\n- *Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location*\n- *Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc*\n- ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES\n- *Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)*\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- Velcro for cable management\n- Laptop: With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Cable Tester\n- Ladder (8'-10')\n- Lift will be ordered if necessary\n\n**You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":36.753603508743296},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493156148}
{"job":{"id":20203573,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Printer Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;DO NOT TAKE FIRMWARE TO SITE. </p><p>Scope: Installation of MX532adwe/MS531dw</p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:** DO NOT TAKE FIRMWARE TO SITE.\n\nScope: Installation of MX532adwe/MS531dw\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary & Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T09:00","end":"2026-11-12T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-12T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":170},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":44.830079383758004},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493194646}
{"job":{"id":20203185,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axper","title":"Lane Bryant 6494 - 3D camera IP reassignment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>The job requirements and the complete scope of work and details are located in the attached document titled \"Lane Bryant IP reassingment.pdf\"</strong>. It is <strong>MANDATORY</strong> to read it before applying for this work order and before the start date scheduled in the work order. If the scope of work reveals itself to be different than the actual situation, while performing the work order, if you encounter any unplanned issue or if you have any question, please make sure to call <strong>Axper Support at 866-658-2360 ext.1</strong> and an agent will answer your questions and advise you on the steps to follow.</p><p><strong>Mandatory equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Basic telecom tools (RJ45 tester, crimper, toner, ect.);</li><li>Laptop (Windows based OS with Wifi capabilities and ethernet port);</li><li>PoE injector (PoE Output Power 54VDC/15.4W | Power Pin Assignment 1/2(+), 3/6(-));</li><li>Spare cable bulk and patch cables;</li></ul><p><u>Port counter is connected to:</u> 1</p><p><u>Desired IP address:</u> <span style=\"color: black;\">10.227.105.18</span></p><p><strong><u>Make sure to bring a ladder (at least 10ft in A-frame)</u></strong></p><p><strong>The following summarized service description does not replace the attached scope of work document in any way.</strong></p><p><u>Summary:</u> We will need a technician to connect the people counter currently installed on site to their POE injector via the cable run and reconfigure the IP address to the one we provided.<strong>The technician will need to call Axper Support to check in and check out.</strong></p>","markdown":"**The job requirements and the complete scope of work and details are located in the attached document titled \"Lane Bryant IP reassingment.pdf\"**. It is **MANDATORY** to read it before applying for this work order and before the start date scheduled in the work order. If the scope of work reveals itself to be different than the actual situation, while performing the work order, if you encounter any unplanned issue or if you have any question, please make sure to call **Axper Support at 866-658-2360 ext.1** and an agent will answer your questions and advise you on the steps to follow.\n\n**Mandatory equipment:**\n\n- Basic telecom tools (RJ45 tester, crimper, toner, ect.);\n- Laptop (Windows based OS with Wifi capabilities and ethernet port);\n- PoE injector (PoE Output Power 54VDC/15.4W | Power Pin Assignment 1/2(+), 3/6(-));\n- Spare cable bulk and patch cables;\n\nPort counter is connected to: 1\n\nDesired IP address: 10.227.105.18\n\n**Make sure to bring a ladder (at least 10ft in A-frame)**\n\n**The following summarized service description does not replace the attached scope of work document in any way.**\n\nSummary: We will need a technician to connect the people counter currently installed on site to their POE injector via the cable run and reconfigure the IP address to the one we provided.**The technician will need to call Axper Support to check in and check out.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T10:30","end":"2026-10-22T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":75},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":45.390877383363105},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493212685}
{"job":{"id":20204321,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - APs Down/Test and Replace Cabling","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Please find the below dispatch note:</p><p><br></p><p>Requirement Overview:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Impacted Device: AIR-CAP2702E-B-K9</p><p>2. Location: Food Lion - 1078 Burlington</p><p>3. Issue Summary: AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Need to check the physical connectivity</p><p>4. Troubleshooting Summary (Completed Remotely)</p><p>Observed that AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.</p><p>Sending dispatch to check the physical connectivity</p><p>Needs to get the console access of the AP for the further investigation.</p><p>5. Requirements for Field Technician</p><p>Please ensure the technician is equipped with the following tools and software:</p><p>Laptop with a stable internet connection.</p><p>Putty installed on the laptop for console access.</p><p>Admin access to the laptop.</p><p>Console cable – USB to RJ45 (compatible with Cisco).</p><p>Microsoft Teams installed for remote collaboration.</p><p>Short Ethernet cable, cable tester, and patch cables.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>6. Onsite Action Plan</p><p>Upon arrival at the location, the technician is expected to:</p><p>Connect with the HCL Wireless Team via Microsoft Teams troubleshooting bridge.</p><p>Access the AP via console using Putty if required.</p><p>Provide console access to the Wireless Team.</p><p>Test connectivity using patch cables and cable tester.</p><p>Perform a factory reset if required.</p><p>Note: Please ensure that all actions are coordinated with the HCL Wireless Team during the visit to ensure proper configuration and validation.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Please find the below dispatch note:\n\nRequirement Overview:\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: AIR-CAP2702E-B-K9\n\n2\\. Location: Food Lion - 1078 Burlington\n\n3\\. Issue Summary: AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Need to check the physical connectivity\n\n4\\. Troubleshooting Summary (Completed Remotely)\n\nObserved that AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.\n\nSending dispatch to check the physical connectivity\n\nNeeds to get the console access of the AP for the further investigation.\n\n5\\. Requirements for Field Technician\n\nPlease ensure the technician is equipped with the following tools and software:\n\nLaptop with a stable internet connection.\n\nPutty installed on the laptop for console access.\n\nAdmin access to the laptop.\n\nConsole cable – USB to RJ45 (compatible with Cisco).\n\nMicrosoft Teams installed for remote collaboration.\n\nShort Ethernet cable, cable tester, and patch cables.\n\n6\\. Onsite Action Plan\n\nUpon arrival at the location, the technician is expected to:\n\nConnect with the HCL Wireless Team via Microsoft Teams troubleshooting bridge.\n\nAccess the AP via console using Putty if required.\n\nProvide console access to the Wireless Team.\n\nTest connectivity using patch cables and cable tester.\n\nPerform a factory reset if required.\n\nNote: Please ensure that all actions are coordinated with the HCL Wireless Team during the visit to ensure proper configuration and validation.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T07:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":39.5564995301347},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $220\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00