{"job":{"id":20203888,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Printer Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;DO NOT TAKE FIRMWARE TO SITE. </p><p>Scope: Installation of MX532adwe/MS531dw</p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:** DO NOT TAKE FIRMWARE TO SITE.\n\nScope: Installation of MX532adwe/MS531dw\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary & Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-30T09:00","end":"2026-11-30T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-30T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":170},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45.49447395182684},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-01T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-02T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-04T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-05T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493237813}
{"job":{"id":20204015,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Hilton SD-WAN: Meraki Router Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ONSITE:</u></strong></p><p>Step 1. Before entering the site, CHECK IN with the Insight Command Center (ICC).</p><ul><li>Call 1.800.359.2620 option 1</li></ul><p>Step 2. You will receive an email from Insight with your Bridge contact prior to the site. Please contact your Bridge person once you have checked in with the ICC.</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Install Meraki Switch</li><li>Install Server&nbsp;</li><li>Install Network Printers</li><li>Work with Support to complete cutover and confirm connectivity</li><li>Collect required collateral and check out with Support</li><li><strong>Must have a laptop and console cable to complete job</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools/Skillset:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Server/Networking/Workstation experience</li><li>CompTIA A+, Net+, MCSE, MCP equivalent classroom training and 2+ years related industry experience or minimum of 3+</li><li>years minimum related industry experience.</li><li>Ability to comprehend industry standard network connectivity, navigation and software installation</li><li>Standard computer tool kit to include</li><li>Philips screwdriver</li><li>Flat head screwdriver</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Charged Cell phone preferably an Android or iPhone with charger</li><li>Box Cutter</li><li>Pen</li><li><strong>Laptop</strong></li><li><strong>Console cable</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to 2hrs onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $25 an hour</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment.&nbsp;All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.&nbsp;If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ONSITE:**\n\nStep 1. Before entering the site, CHECK IN with the Insight Command Center (ICC).\n\n- Call 1.800.359.2620 option 1\n\nStep 2. You will receive an email from Insight with your Bridge contact prior to the site. Please contact your Bridge person once you have checked in with the ICC.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Install Meraki Switch\n- Install Server\n- Install Network Printers\n- Work with Support to complete cutover and confirm connectivity\n- Collect required collateral and check out with Support\n- **Must have a laptop and console cable to complete job**\n\n**Required Tools/Skillset:**\n\n- Server/Networking/Workstation experience\n- CompTIA A+, Net+, MCSE, MCP equivalent classroom training and 2+ years related industry experience or minimum of 3+\n- years minimum related industry experience.\n- Ability to comprehend industry standard network connectivity, navigation and software installation\n- Standard computer tool kit to include\n- Philips screwdriver\n- Flat head screwdriver\n- Flashlight\n- Charged Cell phone preferably an Android or iPhone with charger\n- Box Cutter\n- Pen\n- **Laptop**\n- **Console cable**\n\n***Flat rate covers up to 2hrs onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $25 an hour***\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.***\n\n***All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":70},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":35}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":7.744201242684556},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792493272087}
{"job":{"id":20203124,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | Hilton SD-WAN | Router Install | Schedule date/time is FIRM","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**IMPORTANT** MUST Call into Hilton Bridge BEFORE starting Install. If this is not done, a 10% penalty will be applied. Hilton Support will email you the Bridge Line number before you arrive on site. Please check your spam messages if you have not received this email before arrival on site.</strong></p><p><strong>Please Note: These workorders require back-end support for the routers to be configured and as such the start times are unable to be changed. Please do not request the workorder if you are unable to support the existing schedule. If you determine you will not be able to support the existing schedule, please remove yourself from the workorder. If you need assistance in removing yourself from the workorder please see: </strong>Cannot Make Assignment (fieldnation.com). <strong>Early arrival to site is not available without prior approval from Insight.</strong> Also, Once the workorder is assigned and if you have not done a Hilton SD-WAN workorder in the past a 5-to-10-minute screening call will be made to you.</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong>&nbsp;Install one (1) Meraki Router</p><p><strong>Dress</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Code:</strong>&nbsp;Business Casual</p><p><strong>Tools Needed:</strong></p><p>• Copy of this Field Procedure document </p><p>• Smart Phone fully charged with charger</p><p>• Hands Free Headset (Bluetooth capable)</p><p><strong>•&nbsp;Windows 10/11 Intel compatible Laptop fully charged with Ethernet port enabled and power supply</strong></p><p>• Cat 5 cable(s)</p><p>• Sharpie, Pen &amp; note pad</p><p>• Snips (Scissors)</p><p>• Box Cutters</p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><p>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</p><p>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</p><p>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</p><p>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</p><p>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</p><p>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</p><p>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</p><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><p>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</p><p>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* MUST Call into Hilton Bridge BEFORE starting Install. If this is not done, a 10% penalty will be applied. Hilton Support will email you the Bridge Line number before you arrive on site. Please check your spam messages if you have not received this email before arrival on site.**\n\n**Please Note: These workorders require back-end support for the routers to be configured and as such the start times are unable to be changed. Please do not request the workorder if you are unable to support the existing schedule. If you dete