{"job":{"id":20207571,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Install Zebra Printer","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p>Site Contact <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Bobby <del>******</del></span></p><p><del>**************************</del></p><p><br></p><p>The installation scope includes:</p><p><br></p><p>* Unpack and place the printer in the location designated by the plant?s quality team.</p><p><br></p><p>* Connect power and Ethernet. (provide a 10ft Patch Cable as needed)</p><p><br></p><p>* Load labels and thermal ribbon, then calibrate the printer.</p><p><br></p><p>* Coordinate with our IT team to apply the assigned network settings and verify connectivity.</p><p><br></p><p>* Complete a test print and confirm proper label alignment.</p><p><br></p><p>Location is receiving the printer, labels, and ribbon. We will coordinate power and network readiness and provide onsite contacts and installation instructions before the visits.</p><p><br></p><p>Tech <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> contact Champion support prior to checking out. Contact information listed in confidential section</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li><li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work.&nbsp;&nbsp;We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client. (Messaging on Field Nation is not sufficient communication when canceling or notifying of delay)</li><li>Check In Steps (<u>please follow order</u>)</li><li>Check In via FN Portal</li><li>Check In with Netfor at&nbsp;&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li><li>Complete installation per SOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by&nbsp;Netfor.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who requested the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li><li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li></ol><ul><li><strong>NOTE:&nbsp;<u>*** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER ***</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li><li>Check out with Netfor at&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li></ol><ul><li><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p><p>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Cat6 Cabling</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><ul><li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li><li>Pictures of area before working</li><li>Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed</li><li>Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)</li></ul>","markdown":"**SOW**\n\nSite Contact Bobby \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nThe installation scope includes:\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Unpack and place the printer in the location designated by the plant?s quality team.\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Connect power and Ethernet. (provide a 10ft Patch Cable as needed)\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Load labels and thermal ribbon, then calibrate the printer.\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Coordinate with our IT team to apply the assigned network settings and verify connectivity.\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Complete a test print and confirm proper label alignment.\n\nLocation is receiving the printer, labels, and ribbon. We will coordinate power and network readiness and provide onsite contacts and installation instructions before the visits.\n\nTech **MUST** contact Champion support prior to checking out. Contact information listed in confidential section\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client. (Messaging on Field Nation is not sufficient communication when canceling or notifying of delay)\n3. Check In Steps (please follow order)\n4. Check In via FN Portal\n5. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n6. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who requested the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n7. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n\n- **NOTE: \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER \\*\\*\\***\n\n1. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n2. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n\n- **REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).**\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- 8' Ladder\n- Cat6 Cabling\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- Pictures of area before working\n- Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed\n- Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":36.98848989162489},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $195\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z