{"job":{"id":"5443752640","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"P1 visit for primary DIA hard-down condition","description":"**Issue:**<br>Primary DIA circuit is hard down. The customer reports the same trouble has recurred; Layer 1 and Layer 2 were verified. Pronghorn diagnostics showed 100% packet loss with the provider-facing interface up and BGP active, indicating the customer-side neighbor was unreachable. No carrier outage or carrier dispatch has been established, and an on-site Granite visit is needed.<br><br>CIRCUIT DETAILS<br>Service Type: DIA<br>Carrier: SPECTRUM<br>CXR Circuit ID: 91.L1XX.012185..CHTR<br>NSO ID: CPEGRT0000006443<br>WAN IP: N/A<br>WAN Gateway: N/A<br>MAC Address: N/A<br><br>**Required Equipment:**<br>- A laptop: Windows 10 or higher with admin rights, ethernet ports gig capable of speeds over 1G, and charger to prove connectivity, a patch cord, a splitter, and a minimum of 3 filters. Cell phone, Cell phone charger, butt set and Minimum of 150’ of cable. Cat5e/or higher, Coax and console cable.<br><br>**Other Required Equipment:**<br>- mobile hot spot, 500ft cat5e/cat6 cable, usb 2.0 drive w/ 16gb storage, console, At least 4 Biscuit Jacks<br><br>**General Info:**<br>- Granite Managed Router: Yes<br>- Customer Contact: Michael Radley, 9109122375<br>- NOC Call Back: DIA Repair at 844-492-2557 option 3<br><br>**Configuration:**<br>- WAN Configuration: IP Quantity 0<br>- LAN IP Scheme: Network Address 143.170.115.72, Gateway 143.170.115.73, Subnet 255.255.255.248, IP Quantity 0, Usable Address Range 143.170.115.73, 143.170.115.74, 143.170.115.75, 143.170.115.76, 143.170.115.77, 143.170.115.78, Broadcast Address 143.170.115.79<br>- Port Configuration: Port Speed 500, VLAN 1824<br>- IP Info: 143.170.115.73, 143.170.115.74, 143.170.115.75, 143.170.115.76, 143.170.115.77, 143.170.115.78<br>- Static IP Information: Usable Address Range 143.170.115.73, 143.170.115.74, 143.170.115.75, 143.170.115.76, 143.170.115.77, 143.170.115.78, Gateway 143.170.115.73, Subnet 255.255.255.248<br>- Provisioned Speed: 500<br>- Carrier: SPECTRUM<br>- Access Type: FE<br>- Circuit Bandwidth: 500<br>- Onnet/offnet: On-net<br><br>**SOW:**<br>- Check in via WorkMarket.<br>- Locate the Granite provided modem/router. Record make, model, and serial number in the ticket.<br>- Granite Managed Router Verification<br>  - Identify: Manufacturer, Model, serial number, host name, interface handoff type<br>  - Verify router power status<br>  - Verify Wan and Lan are up<br>  - Document any alarm, fault, or warning indicators<br>- Verify router is properly connected to both carrier and customer equipment<br>- Take a photo of the equipment and site as found.<br>- verify NID light status indicates normal operation.<br>- If off-net copper hand-off: Verify surf directly off carrier NID utilizing WAN usable and gateway<br>- If fiber handoff: Verify cabling/clean and roll fiber<br>- If on-net: and no surf at end of extension take router to demarc and bypass extension even if cable tests ok to cable tester<br>- Inspect patch cabling between carrier handoff and Granite equipment.<br>- Inspect patch cabling between Granite equipment and customer equipment<br>- Document all wiring repairs completed onsite<br>- Connect laptop directly to the Granite router LAN handoff.<br>  - If On Net: we can ONLY test off the Granite Router, we are unable to test from the NID,<br>  - If Off Net: we can test directly from the NID, but if there is a Granite Router start with testing at that device<br>  - If DHCP is enabled, obtain address via DHCP.<br>  - If Static IP information is provided in the Configuration section above, manually assign information.<br>  - If connectivity cannot be established using documented settings, proceed to Escalation Criteria.<br>- Verify and document<br>  - IP assignment<br>  - Gateway reachability<br>  - Internet connectivity<br>  - Carrier Handoff Verification<br>  - Verify physical connectivity.<br>  - Verify link light status.<br>- Using technician laptop connected directly to the Granite router LAN handoff: Ping-500 “ping –n 500 8.8.8.8” record<br>  - Packet loss percentage<br>  - Average latency<br>  - Maximum latency<br>- Run 3 speed tests from a laptop directly connected to the Granite router. Record:<br>  - Download speed<br>  - Upload speed<br>  - Latency<br>  - Jitter (if available)<br>- Identify Fault:<br>  - Customer Equipment<br>  - Customer LAN<br>  - Granite Managed Router<br>  - Carrier Circuit<br>  - Physical Layer/Cabling<br>  - No Trouble Found<br>- Reconnect customer equipment.<br>- Verify physical link status.<br>- Confirm customer equipment establishes connectivity.<br>- Verify customer equipment can browse externally if access is available.<br>- Document any customer-owned equipment concerns.<br>- Confirm connectivity with LCON and MCON if required. See General Info<br>- Validate service restoration criteria<br>- Upload pictures onto WorkMarket<br>- Contact Granite NOC after all testing and isolation steps have been completed. Or escalation is needed. See Escalation criteria. If not connected to a live person within 15 minutes accept the call back request<br>- Complete closeout and check out via WorkMarket<br><br>**Service Restoration Success Criteria:**<br>- Modem/Granite Router is online<br>- Power, online lights are normal<br>- Technician can browse from a laptop connected directly to modem<br>- IP Address obtained or assigned correctly<br>- 2 successful speed tests completed<br>- 500-ping test completed with acceptable results<br>- Customer equipment reconnected<br>- Photos and test results uploaded<br><br>**Escalation Criteria:**<br>- Physical Layer Issues<br>  - No power to carrier equipment or Granite-managed router<br>  - Carrier handoff down or no link light present<br>  - Damaged cabling or infrastructure requiring carrier repair<br>- Connectivity Issues<br>  - Unable to obtain an IP address<br>  - Unable to reach the configured gateway<br>  - Unable to browse the internet from a direct connection<br>  - WAN or LAN interface remains down after validation<br>- Performance Issues<br>  - Speed tests below 80% of provisioned bandwidth<br>  - Packet loss exceeds 5%<br>  - Elevated latency or jitter impacting service<br>  - Performance issues persist when testing directly from the Granite-managed router<br>- Customer Impact<br>  - Customer equipment cannot reconnect after testing<br>  - Customer remains unable to access services after troubleshooting is complete<br>- Carrier Engagement Required<br>  - Issue persists after local equipment, cabling, and router validation<br>  - Carrier trouble ticket or dispatch is required<br>  - Testing indicates the fault exists beyond the customer premises or Granite-managed equipment","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T07:00","end":"2026-10-20T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/20/2026, 7:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792504144853}
{"job":{"id":20207944,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Innover Digital","title":"30 min job - Zebra Scanning Device Replacement & Pairing with RDF40 (201512560-1, 201512560-2 & 201512560-3)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Swapping the old Zebra scanning device with the new one, replace the battery from the old device to the new one.</li>\n<li>Turn on the device and pairing the new VC83 / MC93 device with the RFD40 scanner (if any).</li>\n<li>Request a functionality validation to the Chick-Fil-A representative and get the work order form signed.</li>\n<li>Returning the old scanning device using the UPS return label to the UPS store</li>\n<li>DO NOT VISIT THE SITE DURING LUNCH HOURS.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Picture of the old device serial #</li>\n<li>Picture of the new device serial #</li>\n<li>Picture of the packaging slip</li>\n<li>Picture of the UPS receipt post drop off</li>\n<li>Attach the work order acknowledgement form with the signature of the manager on duty or by on-site contact. Please print the form before you go on-site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>DRESS CODE: Polo or button-up, clean and unripped jeans, close toed-shoes</li>\n<li>Face mask is&nbsp;REQUIRED. Please follow social distancing guidelines while onsite.</li>\n<li>Timely arrival to site</li>\n<li>Zebra Scanning Device picked up from the specified UPS RAP location.</li>\n<li>Remain onsite &amp; put the battery in the new device taken from the faulty one</li>\n<li>Check the equipment to ensure it is working fine</li>\n<li>Drop the collected defective device to the specified UPS location.</li>\n<li>All manuals attached below</li>\n<li>Chick-Fil-A will enroll you in their visitor log, you will receive an email to enroll by filling in basic details. Once completed you will receive a QR code which you need to save or print and presents the&nbsp;<strong>QR code</strong>&nbsp;to security. Security scans/validates the QR code and confirms the visit&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>PRESITE</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive at the specified UPS Location and collect the new replacement spares.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>&nbsp;ONSITE</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive to site introduce yourself to onsite contact as Zebra Fasttrack Smart Hand.</li>\n<li>Check if the serial number of the defective device matches (not more than 3 digits can be allowed for a mismatch) as per what is mentioned in the work order (In case of incorrect serial number, follow special instructions)</li>\n<li>Open the box and check the contents, take out the new device in front of the customer</li>\n<li>Replace the battery from the old device to the new one, turn on the new device.</li>\n<li>Carry out the instructions</li>\n<li>Hand the device to the customer to perform a thorough check of the new device to ensure it is working fine</li>\n<li>Take pictures of the defective device’s serial number and the replacement device</li>\n<li>Take the old device, place it in the box and paste the return label on the box</li>\n<li>Call Zebra Helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide swap update (In case of unsuccessful swap, follow special instructions) &amp; collect the completion code while still on site</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>POST SITE</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Return the defective device to the UPS RAP store from where the good part was picked up</li>\n<li>Once the return package is delivered to the UPS RAP, call Zebra helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094)&nbsp;to provide status</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS :</u></strong></p>\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Unit to be collected does not match the defective SN in RMA?</p>\n<p>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If unit is a different model and/or has a different serial number than what is mentioned in the RMA, the faulty unit should be a Zebra VC83 or MC93 and the serial number should match to complete the swap with the new device.</p>\n<p>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer should be informed that their unit does not match that of the RMA then the swap cannot be completed and the new device will be returned back</p>\n<p>c. If Dead on Arrival - Use the return label and return the device to the UPS store.</p>\n<p>d. These devices should not have accessories on them but if for some reason a device does, they should be moved to the replacement unit.</p>\n<p>Note1: Not all sites have RFD 40 Scanner.</p>\n<p>e. The scope of the onsite activity only covers the VC83 or MC93 unit; therefore, any problem or issue associated with the RFD8500 must be reported separately to the help desk for troubleshooting.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>f. Battery should be pulled from old unit and swapped to the replacement unit.</p>\n<p>No action is required for the SIM Card.</p>\n<p>Pair the VC83 or MC93 unit to the RFD40.</p>\n<p>Request functionality validation from the customer representative.</p>\n<p><strong>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the damage has caused the battery to leak and become dangerous Smart Hands should not leave the replacement unit and request that the customer calls the Zebra helpdesk for advice.</strong></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\n- Swapping the old Zebra scanning device with the new one, replace the battery from the old device to the new one.\n- Turn on the device and pairing the new VC83 / MC93 device with the RFD40 scanner (if any).\n- Request a functionality validation to the Chick-Fil-A representative and get the work order form signed.\n- Returning the old scanning device using the UPS return label to the UPS store\n- DO NOT VISIT THE SITE DURING LUNCH HOURS.\n\n**DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Picture of the old device serial #\n- Picture of the new device serial #\n- Picture of the packaging slip\n- Picture of the UPS receipt post drop off\n- Attach the work order acknowledgement form with the signature of the manager on duty or by on-site contact. Please print the form before you go on-site.\n\n**REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- DRESS CODE: Polo or button-up, clean and unripped jeans, close toed-shoes\n- Face mask is REQUIRED. Please follow social distancing guidelines while onsite.\n- Timely arrival to site\n- Zebra Scanning Device picked up from the specified UPS RAP location.\n- Remain onsite & put the battery in the new device taken from the faulty one\n- Check the equipment to ensure it is working fine\n- Drop the collected defective device to the specified UPS location.\n- All manuals attached below\n- Chick-Fil-A will enroll you in their visitor log, you will receive an email to enroll by filling in basic details. Once completed you will receive a QR code which you need to save or print and presents the **QR code** to security. Security scans/validates the QR code and confirms the visit\n\n**PRESITE**\n\n- Arrive at the specified UPS Location and collect the new replacement spares.\n\n **ONSITE**\n\n- Arrive to site introduce yourself to onsite contact as Zebra Fasttrack Smart Hand.\n- Check if the serial number of the defective device matches (not more than 3 digits can be allowed for a mismatch) as per what is mentioned in the work order (In case of incorrect serial number, follow special instructions)\n- Open the box and check the contents, take out the new device in front of the customer\n- Replace the battery from the old device to the new one, turn on the new device.\n- Carry out the instructions\n- Hand the device to the customer to perform a thorough check of the new device to ensure it is working fine\n- Take pictures of the defective device’s serial number and the replacement device\n- Take the old device, place it in the box and paste the return label on the box\n- Call Zebra Helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide swap update (In case of unsuccessful swap, follow special instructions) & collect the completion code while still on site\n\n**POST SITE**\n\n- Return the defective device to the UPS RAP store from where the good part was picked up\n- Once the return package is delivered to the UPS RAP, call Zebra helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide status\n\n**SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS :**\n\n1\\. Unit to be collected does not match the defective SN in RMA?\n\na. If unit is a different model and/or has a different serial number than what is mentioned in the RMA, the faulty unit should be a Zebra VC83 or MC93 and the serial number should match to complete the swap with the new device.\n\nb. Customer should be informed that their unit does not match that of the RMA then the swap cannot be completed and the new device will be returned back\n\nc. If Dead on Arrival - Use the return label and return the device to the UPS store.\n\nd. These devices should not have accessories on them but if for some reason a device does, they should be moved to the replacement unit.\n\nNote1: Not all sites have RFD 40 Scanner.\n\ne. The scope of the onsite activity only covers the VC83 or MC93 unit; therefore, any problem or issue associated with the RFD8500 must be reported separately to the help desk for troubleshooting.\n\nf. Battery should be pulled from old unit and swapped to the replacement unit.\n\nNo action is required for the SIM Card.\n\nPair the VC83 or MC93 unit to the RFD40.\n\nRequest functionality validation from the customer representative.\n\n**c. If the damage has caused the battery to leak and become dangerous Smart Hands should not leave the replacement unit and request that the customer calls the Zebra helpdesk for advice.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T11:00","end":"2026-10-21T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":34.401997444724856},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $80 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start"