/p><p><strong>Tools &amp; Materials</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Stud finder (joist-capable)</p><p>· Drill + drill bits</p><p>· Screwdriver</p><p>· Level</p><p>· Tape measure</p><p>· Pencil</p><p>· Socket wrench (sometimes needed for lag bolts)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Inventory</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Inventory items included in the TV box, should include the following:</p><p>· TV with stand (remove stand for mounting)</p><p>· Remote with two double AA batteries</p><p>· Power cord</p><p>· Ceiling/pole mount kit (shipped to site)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Locate Joists</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Use a stud finder to locate ceiling joists or structural framing. Mark at least two joists. Your mount must anchor into joists or structural framing for safety.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Mark Mounting Holes</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Hold the ceiling plate against the ceiling:</p><p>· Align it with the joists you marked</p><p>· Use a level to ensure it’s straight</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Mount the Ceiling Plate and Pole</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Drive lag bolts through the ceiling plate and into the joists</p><p>· Tighten securely</p><p>· Double-check that the plate is level</p><p>· Attach the pole to the ceiling plate, then attach the mounting plate to the TV (with a second person holding the TV if possible)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Final Check</strong></p><p><br></p><p>· Ensure the TV is level</p><p>· Confirm it’s firmly attached to the pole</p><p>· Gently test stability</p>","markdown":"**Overview**\n\n**﻿**Seeking a technician experienced in mounting 40\"+ TVs/displays, including ceiling and pole mounts.\n\nTask: Mount one 40\" TV on a ceiling/pole mount, connect it to Wi-Fi, and complete the activation script.\n\nTime: Estimated onsite time: 2 hours.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nInstall one (1) 40\" TV with a ceiling/pole mount at the location the store owner selects. Secure the mount to ceiling joists or structural framing, route power to the nearest outlet, connect to Wi-Fi, and verify content is displaying properly.\n\nCommunicate with the work order manager in real time if anything comes up.\n\nConfirm the mounting location with the store owner before drilling. If the ceiling cannot support the mount at the chosen location, call the work order manager to get approval on an alternate location.\n\n**Dress Code**\n\nBusiness casual; presentable for an active kitchen/commercial environment.\n\n**Tools Required**\n\n6-8 ft ladder\n\n6-8 ft extension cord\n\nDrop cloths (mandatory to protect food prep areas)\n\nSmall vacuum/shop vac (mandatory for immediate dust cleanup)\n\nStud finder (joist-capable) and level (minimum 2 ft)\n\nCordless drill/driver with bits for ceiling joists and structural framing\n\nTape measure and basic hand tool kit\n\nSecond person to help lift the TV overhead (recommended)\n\nSmartphone/tablet for photos and PurPulse check-ins\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements**\n\nReview all provided documentation and installation/activation scripts.\n\nCall or text PurTera Dispatch upon arrival.\n\n**On-Site Tasks**\n\nCheck in with the store owner or manager and confirm the mounting location before drilling.\n\nLay drop cloths before any cutting, drilling, or mounting, including directly below the work area.\n\nLocate joists or structural framing and securely mount the ceiling plate or pole to them.\n\nRoute power to the nearest outlet; document any extension cord use as temporary.\n\nConnect to store Wi-Fi and complete the activation script.\n\nTake clear before-and-after photos of the equipment and work area.\n\nRecord the monitor serial number.\n\n**Work Order Title**\n\nTV Mounting & Wi-Fi Setup: Ceiling/Pole Mount (40\" Display)\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables**\n\nPhoto: TV powered on and displaying assigned content (required for payment)\n\nPhoto: Wide shot showing mounting location context\n\nPhoto: Legible serial number tag\n\nPhoto: Site left clean, with no debris or packaging\n\nData: Serial number, mounting location confirmed by owner, and SSID connected to\n\nConfirmation: Installation script completed and activation verified\n\nSignature: Store Manager signature, or documented reason if unavailable\n\nPayment / Hours / Expenses Policy\n\nFixed fee: $150.00 flat rate.\n\nTravel expenses must be submitted as a counter-offer when requesting the work.\n\nAny additional hours must be requested and approved by the WO Manager before continuing work.\n\nParts: No out-of-pocket purchases; all hardware is shipped to site.\n\nRevisits require a new work order unless caused by technician workmanship.\n\nClean up the work area and confirm completion with the onsite contact.\n\n**TV Installation**\n\nNOTE: The items are general guidelines; ensure you follow the manufacturer’s installation instructions.\n\n**Tools & Materials**\n\n· Stud finder (joist-capable)\n\n· Drill + drill bits\n\n· Screwdriver\n\n· Level\n\n· Tape measure\n\n· Pencil\n\n· Socket wrench (sometimes needed for lag bolts)\n\n**Inventory**\n\n· Inventory items included in the TV box, should include the following:\n\n· TV with stand (remove stand for mounting)\n\n· Remote with two double AA batteries\n\n· Power cord\n\n· Ceiling/pole mount kit (shipped to site)\n\n**Locate Joists**\n\n· Use a stud finder to locate ceiling joists or structural framing. Mark at least two joists. Your mount must anchor into joists or structural framing for safety.\n\n**Mark Mounting Holes**\n\n· Hold the ceiling plate against the ceiling:\n\n· Align it with the joists you marked\n\n· Use a level to ensure it’s straight\n\n**Mount the Ceiling Plate and Pole**\n\n· Drive lag bolts through the ceiling plate and into the joists\n\n· Tighten securely\n\n· Double-check that the plate is level\n\n· Attach the pole to the ceiling plate, then attach the mounting plate to the TV (with a second person holding the TV if possible)\n\n**Final Check**\n\n· Ensure the TV is level\n\n· Confirm it’s firmly attached to the pole\n\n· Gently test stability","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":45.513639437885566},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792506011141}
{"job":{"id":20208162,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"WatchMeGrow","title":"WatchMeGrow - IP System - New IP Camera Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:</strong> https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html</p><p><strong>Equipment Needed:</strong>&nbsp;RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6 Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter</span>, Multimeter, PLENUM Cat6 Cabling, Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit</p><p><strong>Description:&nbsp;</strong>Our client, a busy childcare center, would like to add&nbsp;(1) interior IP camera to their school. We will need you to run wire and install&nbsp;the camera at this location. It will be provided and available onsite. You will need to connect the camera to the server at the head end. WMG technical staff is on hand during this project to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will be required to call to check in upon arrival and call to check out before leaving.</p><p><strong>Project Budget:</strong> Below are the project budget numbers. It is imperative that all work to be completed under the scope of this budget. If the scope of work is going to require additional time and/or labor, please halt the project and call WatchMeGrow immediately to get approval. Additional billed labor is nearly impossible to get approved after the project is completed. The materials cost of cable and crimps are already factored into the wiring budget below. <strong>WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval.</strong></p><p><strong>Wiring:</strong></p><ul><li>1 Cat6 Wire Runs x $135 = $135</li></ul><p><strong>Labor:</strong></p><ul><li>1.5 hours x $75 = $112.50</li></ul><p><strong>Camera Location: </strong>PreK classroom - opposite existing camera.</p><p>Note: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.</p><p><strong>Licensing and Permits:</strong> Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.</p><p><strong>Safety</strong>: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.</p><p>If you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.</p><p><strong>Photos:</strong> Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.</p><p><strong>Call to Sign In/Out:</strong> Please call <del>***** ********</del> to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.</p><p><strong>Sign Off:</strong> Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>!!IMPORTANT!!</strong></p><ul><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.</strong></li><li><strong>WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**You are required to follow CDC guidelines to protect against spreading the Covid-19 Virus:** <https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/index.html>\n\n**Equipment Needed:** RJ-45 crimps, RJ-45 crimping tool, Network cable tester, Cat-6 Patch cables, Step Ladder, Laptop, Monitor w/ VGA Adapter, Multimeter, PLENUM Cat6 Cabling, Silicone (to seal exterior camera mounts and exterior penetrations), T10 Torx Security Bit\n\n**Description:** Our client, a busy childcare center, would like to add (1) interior IP camera to their school. We will need you to run wire and install the camera at this location. It will be provided and available onsite. You will need to connect the camera to the server at the head end. WMG technical staff is on hand during this project to assist in any configuration or troubleshooting needed. You will be required to call to check in upon arrival and call to check out before leaving.\n\n**Project Budget:** Below are the project budget numbers. It is imperative that all work to be completed under the scope of this budget. If the scope of work is going to require additional time and/or labor, please halt the project and call WatchMeGrow immediately to get approval. Additional billed labor is nearly impossible to get approved after the project is completed. The materials cost of cable and crimps are already factored into the wiring budget below. **WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval.**\n\n**Wiring:**\n\n- 1 Cat6 Wire Runs x $135 = $135\n\n**Labor:**\n\n- 1.5 hours x $75 = $112.50\n\n**Camera Location:** PreK classroom - opposite existing camera.\n\nNote: if this is an exterior camera, please make sure to use your silicone to weatherproof the installation.\n\n**Licensing and Permits:** Must obtain or hold licensing and permits as required by the service area. It is your responsibility to verify these requirements with the GC, Superintendant or local authorities.\n\n**Safety**: If children are in the immediate vicinity of your ladder, no work can be done until the center's staff has removed the children from your workspace.\n\nIf you must work in the attic space above a classroom, you need to coordinate with the center staff to have the children removed from the classroom prior to accessing the ceiling, or at the very least, have the teacher in that room move the children to the opposite side from which you will be working. If the center staff cannot accommodate that request, please halt work immediately and notify WatchMeGrow.\n\n**Photos:** Please send us photos of your work upon completion. Photographs are required prior to payment processing.\n\n**Call to Sign In/Out:** Please call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to sign in upon arrival and out before departure.\n\n**Sign Off:** Please print off work order and bring to work site for client sign off. Please also sign below client signature.\n\n**!!IMPORTANT!!**\n\n- **WatchMeGrow will not pay for out-of-scope work without prior approval by the Project Manager.**\n- **WatchMeGrow works on agreed/fixed budgets prior to technician arriving onsite. If any additional time or charges are needed by the technician they MUST be requested and approved prior to completing onsite visit.**\n- **WatchMeGrow will NOT pay for any additional charges that have not been approved by Project Manager prior to technician leaving the worksite.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":247.5,"max":247.5},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":17.538133292275393},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792506054787}
{"job":{"id":20199049,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 063","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13121281</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK & TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13121281\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":50.20756313023004},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792506267535}
{"job":{"id":20208469,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2740028","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>TV : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Speaker : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Computer : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- TV : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Speaker : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Computer : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.51301287939706},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792507753506}
{"job":{"id":20208655,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"T: T20261019.6526  - Durham, NC - Server Room & Rack Cleanup Site Survey, Equipment Audit, & Infrastructure Mapping","description":{"html":"<strong>FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL</strong><br><strong>MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE <del>** </del>SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested</strong><br><strong>Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code</strong><ul><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.</li><li><strong>Client Representation:</strong> You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.</li><li><strong>Platform Discretion:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> mention or discuss <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ****** </del></span>or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work/On-site Task:</strong><br><strong>1. Arrival, Check-In &amp; Etiquette</strong><ul><li>Arrive on-site during the scheduled window:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Primary:</strong> Thursday, October 22, 2026 (09:00 AM – 10:00 AM EDT)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Alternate:</strong> Friday, October 23, 2026 (09:00 AM – 10:00 AM EDT)</li><li>Check in with the location contact and introduce yourself as representing <strong><del>******* *****</del></strong><del>*</del></li><li><strong>CRITICAL INSTRUCTION:</strong> Do <strong>NOT</strong> ask local staff any technical questions. Direct all technical queries to the <strong><del>** **** ***</del></strong><del>*</del></li><li>Call the <strong><del>** **** ***</del></strong><del> </del>upon arrival to open the task and log start time.</li></ul><br><strong>2. Physical Rack &amp; Room Audit</strong><ul><li>Measure and record server room and rack dimensions (height, width, depth, rack unit spaces).</li><li>Audit how racks are anchored (floor bolts, wall mounts, overhead ladder racks).</li><li>Inspect AC power locations, wall outlet placements, and existing Power Distribution Units (PDUs/APCs).</li><li>Audit LAN cabling and fiber maintenance loops to assess cable cleanup requirements.</li><li>Document available/open ports on patch panels and switches.</li></ul><br><strong>3. Hardware &amp; Rail Kit Audit</strong><ul><li>Record exact make, model, and serial numbers for all racked servers, storage arrays, switches, firewalls, and APC UPS units (to determine required rail kits).</li><li>Identify any unsupported hardware, loose cabling, or safety risks in the rack area.</li></ul><br><strong>4. Sign-Off &amp; Checkout</strong><ul><li>Review survey completeness with the <strong>DQ Tech POC</strong>.</li><li>Upload required photo deliverables to Field Nation and call the DQ Tech POC for final check-out.</li></ul><br><strong>Deliverables: Photos to Upload</strong><p>Before checking out, upload the following clear photos:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Room &amp; Rack Wide Shots:</strong> Wide-angle photos showing the entire server room, layout, and front/rear of all server racks.</li><li><strong>Rack Mounts &amp; Anchoring:</strong> Photos showing how racks are secured to the floor, walls, or ceiling ladder racks.</li><li><strong>Power &amp; Outlets:</strong> Photos showing wall AC outlets, PDU placements, and power feed connections.</li><li><strong>LAN &amp; Fiber Cabling Loops:</strong> Close-up photos of switch/patch panel cabling, fiber runs, and existing maintenance loops.</li><li><strong>Equipment Model &amp; Serial Labels:</strong> Photos of model/serial tags for all servers, switches, and APC UPS units.</li><li><strong>Patch Panel Open Ports:</strong> Close-up photos showing available/open punch-downs on patch panels.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li><strong>Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC)</strong> <em>(for notes and documentation)</em></li><li><strong>Measuring Tape &amp; Flashlight / Headlamp</strong> <em>(for room, rack, and rail dimensions)</em></li><li><strong>Basic Hand Tools</strong> (screwdrivers, wire snips)</li><li><strong>Velcro straps ONLY</strong> <em>(Zip ties strictly prohibited)</em></li><li><strong>Smartphone / Camera</strong> for detailed photo deliverables</li></ul><p><br></p><p>For <u>pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact</u>, please check the <strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION</strong> below.</p><p><br></p><strong>DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)</li><li><strong>Record</strong>: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong> Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong> Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within <strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><br>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE & PROTOCOL**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE \\*\\* SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism & Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**  \n**1. Arrival, Check-In & Etiquette**- Arrive on-site during the scheduled window:\n- **Primary:** Thursday, October 22, 2026 (09:00 AM – 10:00 AM EDT)\n- **Alternate:** Friday, October 23, 2026 (09:00 AM – 10:00 AM EDT)\n- Check in with the location contact and introduce yourself as representing **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\n- **CRITICAL INSTRUCTION:** Do **NOT** ask local staff any technical questions. Direct all technical queries to the **\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\n- Call the **\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*** upon arrival to open the task and log start time.\n\n  \n**2. Physical Rack & Room Audit**- Measure and record server room and rack dimensions (height, width, depth, rack unit spaces).\n- Audit how racks are anchored (floor bolts, wall mounts, overhead ladder racks).\n- Inspect AC power locations, wall outlet placements, and existing Power Distribution Units (PDUs/APCs).\n- Audit LAN cabling and fiber maintenance loops to assess cable cleanup requirements.\n- Document available/open ports on patch panels and switches.\n\n  \n**3. Hardware & Rail Kit Audit**- Record exact make, model, and serial numbers for all racked servers, storage arrays, switches, firewalls, and APC UPS units (to determine required rail kits).\n- Identify any unsupported hardware, loose cabling, or safety risks in the rack area.\n\n  \n**4. Sign-Off & Checkout**- Review survey completeness with the **DQ Tech POC**.\n- Upload required photo deliverables to Field Nation and call the DQ Tech POC for final check-out.\n\n  \n**Deliverables: Photos to Upload**Before checking out, upload the following clear photos:\n\n- **Full Room & Rack Wide Shots:** Wide-angle photos showing the entire server room, layout, and front/rear of all server racks.\n- **Rack Mounts & Anchoring:** Photos showing how racks are secured to the floor, walls, or ceiling ladder racks.\n- **Power & Outlets:** Photos showing wall AC outlets, PDU placements, and power feed connections.\n- **LAN & Fiber Cabling Loops:** Close-up photos of switch/patch panel cabling, fiber runs, and existing maintenance loops.\n- **Equipment Model & Serial Labels:** Photos of model/serial tags for all servers, switches, and APC UPS units.\n- **Patch Panel Open Ports:** Close-up photos showing available/open punch-downs on patch panels.\n\n**Required Tools & Equipment**- **Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC)** *(for notes and documentation)*\n- **Measuring Tape & Flashlight / Headlamp** *(for room, rack, and rail dimensions)*\n- **Basic Hand Tools** (screwdrivers, wire snips)\n- **Velcro straps ONLY** *(Zip ties strictly prohibited)*\n- **Smartphone / Camera** for detailed photo deliverables\n\nFor pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact, please check the **CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION** below.\n\n**DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:**- **Documentation:** Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)\n- **Record**: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nBy accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-22T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.06048761829354},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792508613119}
{"job":{"id":"5494262871","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"FieldStar IT","title":"LifePoint Springstone (Triangle Springs Changes)-Phones","description":"<p>LifePoint Phone System Migration</p><p>Existing Provider: Lingo</p><p>New Provider: Zoom</p><p><br></p><p>Duration: 1</p><p>Day 1: Staging, Inventory &amp; Preparation&amp;Phone Porting, Cutover &amp; Testing</p><p><br></p><p>only 18 phones</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Project Overview</strong></p><p>Two qualified onsite technicians will assist the migration from Lingo to Zoom, working with remote engineers to inventory and deploy phones, stage and install AudioCodes voice gateways, and support cutover and testing. This high-priority project requires technical readiness, communication, and adherence to the approved run book.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Staging, Inventory &amp; Preparation</strong></p><p>Objective: Prepare the site, equipment, and phones for migration.</p><p><br></p><p>Onsite Technician Responsibilities:</p><ul><li>Arrive on time, check in with the designated onsite Point of Contact (POC), and join the emailed conference bridge to coordinate with remote engineering.</li><li>Locate Zoom phones, AudioCodes gateways, and accessories. Inventory all equipment and report missing, damaged, or incorrect items.</li><li>Review the phone deployment workbook; verify extensions, phone assignments, locations, and MAC addresses. Identify the receptionist's phone by MAC address and confirm its location with the POC.</li><li>Confirm priority users and departments with the customer and establish the deployment order. Distribute phones to designated desks and workstations per the workbook.</li><li>Walk the site and document the number and locations of wall-mounted phones.</li><li>Locate telecom closets, network switches, existing voice gateways, and associated Amphenol cabling.</li><li>Unbox, stage, and rack new AudioCodes gateways as directed by remote engineering.</li><li>Identify and document existing gateway connections, switch names, and relevant ports for the remote team.</li><li>Confirm equipment readiness and escalate issues that could affect the scheduled port.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Phone Porting, Cutover &amp; Testing</strong></p><p>Objective: Provide onsite assistance to remote engineering during the Lingo-to-Zoom cutover.</p><p><br></p><p>Onsite Technician Responsibilities:</p><ul><li>Check in with the POC, join the bridge, review the cutover run book, and confirm instructions with remote engineering.</li><li>Locate existing gateways and verify connections documented during staging.</li><li>Only as directed, move the Ethernet cable from the legacy gateway to WAN Port 1 on the new AudioCodes gateway (never the LAN port).</li><li>For additional gateways, identify available ports on the same switch and provide switch names and port details to the remote team.</li><li>Assist with gateway connections, console access, and troubleshooting under engineering direction.</li><li>Power-cycle phones as instructed to initiate provisioning, firmware updates, and required reboots; support activation and configuration troubleshooting.</li><li>Prioritize receptionist phones and other business-critical users specified by the customer.</li><li>Assist remote engineering with inbound/outbound call, extension, and phone-function testing. Investigate failed registration, provisioning, activation, and network connectivity.</li><li>Disconnect or remove legacy equipment only with explicit remote engineering authorization.</li><li>Verify phone and gateway tasks, document unresolved issues, and report completion status to remote engineering and Fieldstar IT.</li><li>Obtain remote engineering clearance before leaving the site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables</strong>:</p><ul><li>Cutover and AudioCodes connectivity support completed as directed.</li><li>Provisioning, reboot, firmware, activation, and functional testing support provided.</li><li>Outstanding issues documented and escalated; remote engineering completion clearance received.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Technician Tools &amp; Equipment</strong></p><p>The technicians must bring working equipment:</p><ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet and console connectivity.</li><li>Charged cell phone and charger.</li><li>Butt set; Ethernet patch cables; console cable.</li><li>Laptop adapters required for direct device connections.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Verify all tools work before arrival.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Conference Bridge &amp; Communication Requirements</strong></p><p>Both technicians must remain engaged and communicate consistently with remote engineering:</p><ul><li>Join the bridge on arrival, remain available, and check in at least every 30 minutes (or more frequently if requested).</li><li>Announce extended off-bridge tasks and estimated return times; notify the team before lunch or breaks.</li><li>Provide updates when helping the POC or onsite employees, and clearly communicate each technician's responsibilities and progress.</li><li>Immediately escalate technical issues, missing equipment, delays, or barriers to completion.</li><li>Never disconnect from the bridge or leave the site without notifying the remote team and securing approval.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Unresponsiveness, unexplained departures, and failure to communicate work status are unacceptable.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technical Requirements &amp; Important Instructions</strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>AudioCodes Gateway Connectivity:</u></p><ul><li>Connect Ethernet to WAN Port 1, never the LAN port.</li><li>Validate switch names and port assignments with remote engineering.</li><li>Do not disconnect production equipment or make gateway changes without engineer authorization; follow all engineer instructions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Phone Deployment:</u></p><ul><li>Follow the approved workbook for extensions, locations, MAC addresses, and device placement.</li><li>Prioritize receptionist and business-critical phones.</li><li>Phones may require power cycling, firmware updates, or multiple provisioning reboots. Report failures to register or activate.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Equipment Handling:</u></p><ul><li>Document existing cabling or equipment concerns and keep work areas clean and organized.</li><li>Do not remove, relocate, or dispose of legacy equipment without authorization.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Professional Conduct &amp; Site Expectations</strong></p><p>Technicians represent Fieldstar IT and its partners and must:</p><ul><li>Communicate respectfully and professionally with customers, onsite staff, and engineers, regardless of others' tone or informality.</li><li>Avoid personal remarks, inappropriate jokes, and non-work conversations on customer conference bridges.</li><li>Follow onsite POC and authorized engineer instructions.</li><li>Direct scheduling conflicts and concerns to Fieldstar IT, not the customer.</li><li>Obtain project-team clearance before departing.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation &amp; Completion Requirements</strong></p><p>Before leaving on either day, provide:</p><ul><li>Summary of completed tasks, inventory results, and any discrepancies.</li><li>Updated phone deployment status and applicable switch/gateway connection details.</li><li>Before-and-after photos of equipment and installation areas.</li><li>Outstanding issues, recommended follow-up, and any completion blockers.</li><li>Confirmation that remote engineering has authorized departure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation &amp; Scope Management</strong></p><p>Immediately notify Fieldstar IT of technical delays, missing items, unexpected conditions, or additional work. Technicians must not independently change the agreed scope, schedule return visits, make unauthorized changes, or leave without informing the project team. Additional troubleshooting or time must be coordinated through Fieldstar IT.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Project Completion Criteria</strong></p><p>The engagement is complete when:</p><ul><li>All staging, inventory, and deployment tasks are finished.</li><li>Gateway connectivity and scheduled cutover support are completed as directed.</li><li>Phone functionality is tested to the extent possible with remote engineers.</li><li>Open issues are documented, communicated, and escalated as appropriate.</li><li>Remote engineering confirms technicians are no longer needed onsite.</li><li>Fieldstar IT receives the final work summary, photos, and required documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Final Note: Success depends on qualified technicians, working tools, responsive communication, and close coordination with remote engineering. Both technicians must review this scope and the accompanying run book before arrival and follow them throughout both visits.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T08:00","end":"2026-10-29T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":650},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":4.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":650,"estHours":10,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792509411322}
