{"job":{"id":20209328,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Equipment Configuration/Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE NOTE </strong>--Spectrotel will be sending an antenna with 40ft of cable that will be installed alongside the new Cradlepoint.&nbsp;</p><p>Should the signal not be sufficient at the rack, we will move the antenna around the store to see where we can improve signal.</p><p>If the cradlepoint has good signal, the antenna will still be installed and mounted next to the cradlepoint.</p><p>If the antenna needs to be mounted outdoors, STOP immediately and inform Spectrotel Provisioning.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p>Technician must bring a working laptop with ability to connect ethernet handoff for internet equipment speed testing.</p><p><p><b>Task ID:</b> 5274387<br />\n<b>PON:</b> 502848<br />\n<b>Account Name:</b> Papa Johns - Store # 3692 - NC<br />\n<b>Service Address:</b> 101 W Cornelius Harnett Blvd, Lillington, NC 27546</p>\n<p><b>Smart Hands</b><br />\n<br />\n<b>Special Notes:</b> Internet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.88.54<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 184.71.236.166<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 184.71.236.165<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: B0:F5:30:C9:6A:E0<br />\nNotes: Modem Manufacturer:<br />\nHitron<br />\nModem Model:<br />\nCODA-5810<br />\nSerial No:<br />\n321-AN6025C01BB0<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.74<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 24.82.12.126<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.12.125<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: B0:F5:30:CE:5C:A0<br />\nNotes: Model: <br />\nHitron Coda 5810<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.61<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 24.82.11.182<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.11.181<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: D0:EE:47:0E:01:60<br />\nNotes: Modem Model: Hitron Coda 5810<br />\nSN:  AN6026306294<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.157<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 24.82.71.126<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.71.125<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: D0:EE:47:04:E0:00<br />\nNotes: Modem Make / Model : Hitron Coda 5810<br />\nSN:  AN6026203447<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.177<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 184.68.245.222<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 184.68.245.221<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: D0:EE:47:0F:7C:B0<br />\nNotes: Modem Make / Model : Hitron Coda 5810<br />\nSN:  AN6026309CEA<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.88.126<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 24.82.14.38<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.14.37<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: D0:EE:47:0F:7E:B0<br />\nNotes: SN:  AN6026309CEC<br />\nMac Address:  D0:EE:47:0F:7E:B0<br />\nModel: Hitron Coda 5810<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.65<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.180<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 72.38.174.46<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 72.38.174.45<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: A8C2462FD91C<br />\nNotes: Gemtek Modem<br />\nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):<br />\nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.103.142.120<br />\nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):<br />\nIP Address: 71.12.24.166<br />\nLAN IP Gateway: 71.12.24.165<br />\nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252<br />\nMAC: 74375f58b1a5/1c9ecc8b66c9<br />\nNotes: Wireless Make: SercommCorporation<br />\nWireless Model: sax1v1r<br />\nData Make: Technicolor<br />\nData Model: ET2251<br />\n<br />\nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.</p>\n</p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field tech will check in on site with Customer Manager on Duty can call into Spectrotel Activations for instructions.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field tech to locate Spectrotel shipment and prepare to unbox</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Shipment contents will include:</p><p>1)&nbsp;&nbsp;Cradlepoint R980 wireless router</p><p><strong><u>PART 1</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>- Unbox and mount Cradlepoint near existing network rack</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Run provided antenna cable to closest exterior wall&nbsp;</p><p> Mount and connect antenna to cabling</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate an unused 120V power source to power the Cradlepoint</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once online, work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Proof.ovh.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speed.cloudflare.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speedof.me</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>**NOTE** wireless speed requirement of 10Mbps Download / 5Mbps Upload.&nbsp;If that speed is not obtained, follow the Webbing SIM change procedure to change to another carrier tower until the desired speed test is achieved.</em></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate recently installed Spectrotel broadband circuit (either cable modem or broadband fiber modem)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect laptop to Broadband ISP device with IPs provided by Spectrotel activations</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Run speed tests to the sites mentioned earlier</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once speed tests are approved on broadband and wireless, We will begin the WAN cutover process.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PART 2</u></strong></p><p>- Assist in moving existing WAN connections as per guidance from Spectrotel and Customer's security vendor - CBTS</p><p>- Upon Spectrotel's instructions to proceed locate and remove the existing wireless backup connection to the existing MERAKI MX67.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Unplug ethernet cable from existing wireless device and plug into the new Cradlepoint port 1</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CBTS will confirm that the MX67 is operational on the new backup</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CBTS will reconfigure the WAN port for the new circuit</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once CBTS confirms, advise Field tech to unplug ethernet cable from existing carrier modem and connect to the NEW Spectrotel modem/router</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CBTS will confirm that the Meraki is operational on the new circuit and contact the store manager to begin local device testing</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon site testing completion, request confirmation from CBTS to post in the WebEx chat that service is GOOD, working and we can dismiss our field technician.</p><p>- Take 4 photos of the deployment and label each then upload to Field Nations:</p><p>-\tCradlepoint</p><p>-\tCarrier Modem</p><p>-\tMeraki with cable connections</p><p>-\tEntire network rack</p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p>You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.</p><p><strong>♦ Contacts</strong></p><p>Please reach out to Spectrotel in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</p><p>You must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.</p><p><strong>♦ Material and Equipment Requirements</strong></p><p>Tech MUST have inside their bag when arriving to the building **NON-NEGOTIABLE**. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.</p><p>FULL Charged Windows Laptop with Gigabit RJ45 ethernet port &amp; Power Supply, with console cable and HOTSPOT</p><p>Minimum 6 ft ladder, 8-10 A frame is preferred</p><p>Cordless Battery-Operated Drill with Assorted Drill Bits</p><p>Wall Mounting Anchors for Sheetrock / Wood / Metal / Concrete</p><p>Cat5 or CAT6 cabling, 100-200 ft</p><p>Jacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper, wire ties, wire straps, drywall anchors and screws</p><p>The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>**The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)**</strong></p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables</strong></p><p>Detailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.</p><p>We request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.</p><p>Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.</p><p>Please provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.</p><p>If a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE NOTE** --Spectrotel will be sending an antenna with 40ft of cable that will be installed alongside the new Cradlepoint.\n\nShould the signal not be sufficient at the rack, we will move the antenna around the store to see where we can improve signal.\n\nIf the cradlepoint has good signal, the antenna will still be installed and mounted next to the cradlepoint.\n\nIf the antenna needs to be mounted outdoors, STOP immediately and inform Spectrotel Provisioning.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**SOW**\n\nTechnician must bring a working laptop with ability to connect ethernet handoff for internet equipment speed testing.\n\n**Task ID:** 5274387  \n**PON:** 502848  \n**Account Name:** Papa Johns - Store # 3692 - NC  \n**Service Address:** 101 W Cornelius Harnett Blvd, Lillington, NC 27546\n\n**Smart Hands**  \n  \n**Special Notes:** Internet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.88.54  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 184.71.236.166  \nLAN IP Gateway: 184.71.236.165  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: B0:F5:30:C9:6A:E0  \nNotes: Modem Manufacturer:  \nHitron  \nModem Model:  \nCODA-5810  \nSerial No:  \n321-AN6025C01BB0  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.74  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 24.82.12.126  \nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.12.125  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: B0:F5:30:CE:5C:A0  \nNotes: Model:   \nHitron Coda 5810  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.61  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 24.82.11.182  \nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.11.181  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: D0:EE:47:0E:01:60  \nNotes: Modem Model: Hitron Coda 5810  \nSN: AN6026306294  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.157  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 24.82.71.126  \nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.71.125  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: D0:EE:47:04:E0:00  \nNotes: Modem Make / Model : Hitron Coda 5810  \nSN: AN6026203447  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.177  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 184.68.245.222  \nLAN IP Gateway: 184.68.245.221  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: D0:EE:47:0F:7C:B0  \nNotes: Modem Make / Model : Hitron Coda 5810  \nSN: AN6026309CEA  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.88.126  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 24.82.14.38  \nLAN IP Gateway: 24.82.14.37  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: D0:EE:47:0F:7E:B0  \nNotes: SN: AN6026309CEC  \nMac Address: D0:EE:47:0F:7E:B0  \nModel: Hitron Coda 5810  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.90.65  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.98.89.180  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 72.38.174.46  \nLAN IP Gateway: 72.38.174.45  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: A8C2462FD91C  \nNotes: Gemtek Modem  \nInternet Access Over Wireless (IOW Wireless Data):  \nLAN Usable IP Range: 38.103.142.120  \nInternet Access Over Cable (IOC):  \nIP Address: 71.12.24.166  \nLAN IP Gateway: 71.12.24.165  \nLAN Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252  \nMAC: 74375f58b1a5/1c9ecc8b66c9  \nNotes: Wireless Make: SercommCorporation  \nWireless Model: sax1v1r  \nData Make: Technicolor  \nData Model: ET2251  \n  \nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n· Field tech will check in on site with Customer Manager on Duty can call into Spectrotel Activations for instructions.\n\n· Field tech to locate Spectrotel shipment and prepare to unbox\n\n· Shipment contents will include:\n\n1\\) Cradlepoint R980 wireless router\n\n**PART 1**\n\n\\- Unbox and mount Cradlepoint near existing network rack\n\n Run provided antenna cable to closest exterior wall\n\n Mount and connect antenna to cabling\n\n· Locate an unused 120V power source to power the Cradlepoint\n\n· Once online, work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier\n\n· Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:\n\no Proof.ovh.net\n\no Speed.cloudflare.net\n\no Speedof.me\n\n· *\\*\\*NOTE\\*\\* wireless speed requirement of 10Mbps Download / 5Mbps Upload. If that speed is not obtained, follow the Webbing SIM change procedure to change to another carrier tower until the desired speed test is achieved.*\n\n· Locate recently installed Spectrotel broadband circuit (either cable modem or broadband fiber modem)\n\n· Connect laptop to Broadband ISP device with IPs provided by Spectrotel activations\n\n· Run speed tests to the sites mentioned earlier\n\n· Once speed tests are approved on broadband and wireless, We will begin the WAN cutover process.\n\n**PART 2**\n\n\\- Assist in moving existing WAN connections as per guidance from Spectrotel and Customer's security vendor - CBTS\n\n\\- Upon Spectrotel's instructions to proceed locate and remove the existing wireless backup connection to the existing MERAKI MX67.\n\n· Unplug ethernet cable from existing wireless device and plug into the new Cradlepoint port 1\n\n· CBTS will confirm that the MX67 is operational on the new backup\n\n· CBTS will reconfigure the WAN port for the new circuit\n\n· Once CBTS confirms, advise Field tech to unplug ethernet cable from existing carrier modem and connect to the NEW Spectrotel modem/router\n\n· CBTS will confirm that the Meraki is operational on the new circuit and contact the store manager to begin local device testing\n\n· Upon site testing completion, request confirmation from CBTS to post in the WebEx chat that service is GOOD, working and we can dismiss our field technician.\n\n\\- Take 4 photos of the deployment and label each then upload to Field Nations:\n\n\\- Cradlepoint\n\n\\- Carrier Modem\n\n\\- Meraki with cable connections\n\n\\- Entire network rack\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\nYou must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.\n\n**♦ Contacts**\n\nPlease reach out to Spectrotel in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.\n\nYou must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.\n\n**♦ Material and Equipment Requirements**\n\nTech MUST have inside their bag when arriving to the building \\*\\*NON-NEGOTIABLE\\*\\*. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.\n\nFULL Charged Windows Laptop with Gigabit RJ45 ethernet port & Power Supply, with console cable and HOTSPOT\n\nMinimum 6 ft ladder, 8-10 A frame is preferred\n\nCordless Battery-Operated Drill with Assorted Drill Bits\n\nWall Mounting Anchors for Sheetrock / Wood / Metal / Concrete\n\nCat5 or CAT6 cabling, 100-200 ft\n\nJacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper, wire ties, wire straps, drywall anchors and screws\n\nThe provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.\n\n**\\*\\*The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)\\*\\***\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables**\n\nDetailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.\n\nWe request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.\n\nSubsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.\n\nPlease provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.\n\nIf a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T10:00","end":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":32.09535227328958},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12