{"job":{"id":"8395524345","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"***Burlington | WAN Testing/Validation, EB Install, Cross Connect Assistance***","description":"\"***DEMARC EXTENSION LIKELY NEEDED FROM CARRIER (IF VERIZON OR FRONTIER) ONT WITHIN ELECTRICAL ROOM TO BURLINGTON'S IT ROOM/CABINET, PLEASE BE PREPARED WITH TECHS AND LIFT TO COMPLETE WORK***<br><br>***GRANITE CORE BRIDGE, GRANITE ACCESS ACTIVATIONS BRIDGE, CIRCUIT DETAILS, EQUIPMENT DETAILS POSTED IN SOW BELOW***<br><br>Requesting assistance to:<br><br>1) Call into Granite Core Team Bridge to confirm arrival<br>2) Locate new Granite-provided broadband and or/ DIA service<br>3) Extend new service to Burlington’s network rack/cabinet (if needed)<br>4) Test/validate new service<br>5) With Access Activations assistance, confirm with carrier that modem/router onsite is set to IP Passthrough/Bridge modem<br>6) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) modem and/or FlexEdge router to new EdgebootPro equipment for power in accordance to port mapping guide listed below.<br>7) Connect new Granite-provided Internet service(s) and EdgebootPro to existing Burlington-provided Fortinet firewall ethernet ports in accordance to port mapping guide listed below<br>8) Once complete, request Granite Field Service technician to contact Burlington’s Managed Service Provider (HCL) to perform health check on applicable Fortinet firewall ports new equipment is now connected to.<br>9) Locate the existing Cradlepoint LTE Router<br>10) Document the Cradlepoint LTE Router location in close out notes<br>11) Using provided SIM card (will be shipped in separate envelope and held in the manager’s office), insert into the spare SIM 2 slot on the Cradlepoint<br><br>***NETWORK DIAGRAM ATTACHED AS REFERENCED***<br><br>***ONCE STEPS 1-7 ARE COMPLETE, PLEASE CONTACT BURLINGTON’S MANAGED SERVIE PROVIDE (HCL) @ TBD***<br><br>***TECHNICIAN MUST CALL INTO GRANITE ACCESS ACTIVATIONS TEAM. REP WILL THEN MERGE ACCUATIVE INTO CALL FOR A SIGN OFF CODE***<br><br>***JOB NOT COMPLETE UNTIL ALL STEPS ARE PERFORMED***<br><br>***NETWORK CUTOVER TO TAKE PLACE AT LATER DATE***<br><br>***ALL DIA SERVICES FOR BURLINGTON INCLUDES AN EPIKE EDGE/FLEXEDGE DEVICE REGARDLESS WHETHER ON OR OFF-NET. EPIK EDGE/FLEXEDGE DEVICE WILL COME IN SAME PACKAGE AS EDGEBOOT***<br><br>New service details are below:\"<br>Granite Core Bridge:Bridge: 929-229-2436, Passcode: 688838204#<br>Granite Activation:877-855-1146 Option 1 (BB), Option 2 (DIA)<br>Activations Ticket #7063981<br>HCL NOC Phone Number:314-924-3537 (email: HCL_DEO@burlington.com)<br>WAN Details:<br>Type:DIA<br>ISP:Spectrum<br>Bandwidth:50M<br>Circuit ID:91.L1XX.021212..CHTR<br>Demarc:SERVER ROOM<br>IP:Dynamic<br>GW:Dynamic<br>Subnet:Dynamic<br>DNS1:Dynamic<br>DNS2:Dynamic<br>EdgebootPro Serial #:<br>Edgeboot FedEx/UPS (DIA ORDER ONLY, PLEASE DISREGARD FOR BROADBAND PRODUCTS):<br>Equipment FedEx/UPS (DIA ORDER ONLY, PLEASE DISREGARD FOR BROADBAND PRODUCTS):<br><br>\"AC/Ethernet Port Mapping Guide:<br><br>Edgeboot AC Ports:<br><br>Port 1: DIA FlexEdge (WHERE APPLICABLE)<br>Port 2: Broadband Modem<br>Port 3: None<br>Port4: None<br><br>Edgeboot/New Circuit Ethernet Cross Connect:<br>New DIA Circuit: FortiGate Port 2 (WHERE APPLICABLE)<br>New Broadband Circuit: FortiGate Port 3<br>Edgeboot Port 0: FortiGate Port 5<br>Edgeboot Port 1: FortiGate Port 4<br>Edgeboot Console Port: FortiGate Console Port (via provided console cable included with EdgebootPro)\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T09:00","end":"2026-10-26T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":57.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792514909925}
{"job":{"id":20210127,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2740863","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Streaming Device : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Streaming Device : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T08:00","end":"2026-10-20T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-20T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":35.816224648163995},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792515266045}
{"job":{"id":20210129,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK Compact | Automated Return Kiosk Installation & Config ","description":{"html":"<p>This WO is to install a New Amazon Return Kiosk at an Amazon Returns Location.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Unit credentials:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>kiosk_username:</strong> TBA</li>\n<li><strong>kiosk_pwd:</strong> TBA</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>MUST CALL WO Manager TO CHECK IN AND CHECK OUT</strong></p>\n<p>Main Kiosk Support Line: Mon – Fri: 6:00am – 6:00pm MST</p>\n<p><strong>(303) 661-1664</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>You may need to depalletize and move the Kiosk to the desired location.</p>\n<p><strong><u>KIOSK Weighs 225lbs</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dolly/ Hand Truck (Can use sites if available)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Set (At least a Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver, preferably multiple sizes and lengths)</li>\n<li>Nut driver set (At least an 11/32\" &amp; 3/8\")</li>\n<li>T-15 Torx Bit</li>\n<li>Mini USB Cable</li>\n<li>Compressed Air / Canned Air</li>\n<li>A to B USB Cable (Std Printer Cable)</li>\n<li>Electronic Safety Wipes/Soft Cloth</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Documentation Attached:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Compact_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf</p>\n<p>- This guide is the installation guide to follow and guide you through the installation steps.</p>\n<p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<strong>20211215_ARK@WFM Associate Training Manual_v2</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-This guide is for training and get you familiar with the kiosk and application.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Once on site, call WO Manager to check in.</li>\n<li>Meet with onsite POC to locate the kiosk.</li>\n<li>Open the kiosk and inspect for any damages.</li>\n<li>Follow the attached installation guide (<strong>Compact_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf</strong>).</li>\n<li>Make sure power is connected and the unit is powered on.</li>\n<li>Carefully load the label roll into the printer and center the sensor if not already aligned with the indicator.</li>\n<li>Call <strong>KIOSK Support</strong> to confirm the unit is online, checking in, and properly configured.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Network:</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>WIFI SSID:</strong> AmzKiosk</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>WIFI PW:</strong>3XNHdLa!kQlVRYq</li>\n<li>Do not leave the site unless released by our <strong>KIOSK Support Team</strong> or unless a new return date has been agreed upon if any issues arise.</li>\n</ol>","markdown":"This WO is to install a New Amazon Return Kiosk at an Amazon Returns Location.\n\n**Unit credentials:**\n\n- **kiosk\\_username:** TBA\n- **kiosk\\_pwd:** TBA\n\n**MUST CALL WO Manager TO CHECK IN AND CHECK OUT**\n\nMain Kiosk Support Line: Mon – Fri: 6:00am – 6:00pm MST\n\n**(303) 661-1664**\n\n**Special Instructions:**\n\nYou may need to depalletize and move the Kiosk to the desired location.\n\n**KIOSK Weighs 225lbs**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Dolly/ Hand Truck (Can use sites if available)\n- Standard Tool Set (At least a Phillips and Flathead Screwdriver, preferably multiple sizes and lengths)\n- Nut driver set (At least an 11/32\" & 3/8\")\n- T-15 Torx Bit\n- Mini USB Cable\n- Compressed Air / Canned Air\n- A to B USB Cable (Std Printer Cable)\n- Electronic Safety Wipes/Soft Cloth\n\n**Documentation Attached:**\n\n**1.** Compact\\_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf\n\n\\- This guide is the installation guide to follow and guide you through the installation steps.\n\n**2.**  **20211215\\_ARK@WFM Associate Training Manual\\_v2**\n\n -This guide is for training and get you familiar with the kiosk and application.\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n1. Once on site, call WO Manager to check in.\n2. Meet with onsite POC to locate the kiosk.\n3. Open the kiosk and inspect for any damages.\n4. Follow the attached installation guide (**Compact\\_AMZInstallDocumentation2025.pdf**).\n5. Make sure power is connected and the unit is powered on.\n6. Carefully load the label roll into the printer and center the sensor if not already aligned with the indicator.\n7. Call **KIOSK Support** to confirm the unit is online, checking in, and properly configured.\n8. **Network:**\n9. **WIFI SSID:** AmzKiosk\n10. **WIFI PW:**3XNHdLa!kQlVRYq\n11. Do not leave the site unless released by our **KIOSK Support Team** or unless a new return date has been agreed upon if any issues arise.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00","end":"2026-10-20T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-20T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":52.52159339563594},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round 