{"job":{"id":20210287,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294091 / 05294062","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p>\n<p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed on your phone and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: <strong>Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong> to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li>\n<li>Note: <strong>Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong> explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li>\n<li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to<strong>specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong> and its reason.</li>\n<li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong>the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li>\n<li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Title:</strong> Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294091 / 05294062</p>\n<p><strong>Type of Work:</strong> Networking</p>\n<p><strong>Schedule:</strong> October 20, 2026 – 3:00 PM-5:00 PM EDT (3:00 PM-5:00 PM EDT)</p>\n<p><strong>Site Name &amp; Address:</strong> Spark Spring Lake Fayetteville NC, 103 Brook Lane, Spring Lake, NC 28390, USA</p>\n<p><strong>WO / SA / Case:</strong> 00262449 / SA-294091 / 05294062</p>\n<p><strong>Contact Details:</strong> Site POC: Vanessa Bell, 910-436-1900</p>\n<p>Engineer: TBD | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Investigate intermittent connectivity caused by flapping switch HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05.</li>\n<li>Locate and inspect Cisco Meraki MS350-24P switch (Serial: Q2WP-7PNP-75FL) located on the 2nd Floor.</li>\n<li>Verify switch power source and inspect UPS, breakers, and electrical outlet condition.</li>\n<li>Test alternate power cord if available.</li>\n<li>Determine whether the UPS may be contributing to the switch flapping issue.</li>\n<li>Verify Ethernet uplink connectivity to parent switch HLT-FAYSR-425-MDF-CS01 (Port 6).</li>\n<li>Inspect and reseat Ethernet and fiber connections.</li>\n<li>Test spare Ethernet patch cables and spare SFP modules as needed.</li>\n<li>Verify operational status of installed SFPs and fiber links.</li>\n<li>Provide console access/session if requested by remote support.</li>\n<li>If issue persists, assist remote support with troubleshooting and potential Meraki hardware replacement assessment.</li>\n<li>Document findings, corrective actions performed, and impact to services.</li>\n<li>Capture photos of switch, cabling, UPS, power source, SFPs, and any identified issues.</li>\n<li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Asset &amp; Location:</strong> HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05 (Cisco Meraki MS350-24P) – 2nd Floor</p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</li>\n<li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet cable</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li>\n<li>Cellphone with camera</li>\n<li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)</li>\n<li>Tone generator</li>\n<li>Console cable and USB adapter</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>RJ45 plugs (cat5e and cat6)</li>\n<li>Keystone jacks (cat5e and cat6)</li>\n<li>Voltage tester</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li>\n<li>SFP modules</li>\n<li>Ethernet patch cables</li>\n<li>Spare fiber patch cables</li>\n<li>Fiber cleaning kit</li>\n<li>Laser to verify light continuity</li>\n<li>Fiber tester</li>\n<li>Spare power cord</li>\n<li>Flashlight</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed on your phone and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to**specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\n**Title:** Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294091 / 05294062\n\n**Type of Work:** Networking\n\n**Schedule:** October 20, 2026 – 3:00 PM-5:00 PM EDT (3:00 PM-5:00 PM EDT)\n\n**Site Name & Address:** Spark Spring Lake Fayetteville NC, 103 Brook Lane, Spring Lake, NC 28390, USA\n\n**WO / SA / Case:** 00262449 / SA-294091 / 05294062\n\n**Contact Details:** Site POC: Vanessa Bell, 910-436-1900\n\nEngineer: TBD | TECHNET Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Investigate intermittent connectivity caused by flapping switch HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05.\n- Locate and inspect Cisco Meraki MS350-24P switch (Serial: Q2WP-7PNP-75FL) located on the 2nd Floor.\n- Verify switch power source and inspect UPS, breakers, and electrical outlet condition.\n- Test alternate power cord if available.\n- Determine whether the UPS may be contributing to the switch flapping issue.\n- Verify Ethernet uplink connectivity to parent switch HLT-FAYSR-425-MDF-CS01 (Port 6).\n- Inspect and reseat Ethernet and fiber connections.\n- Test spare Ethernet patch cables and spare SFP modules as needed.\n- Verify operational status of installed SFPs and fiber links.\n- Provide console access/session if requested by remote support.\n- If issue persists, assist remote support with troubleshooting and potential Meraki hardware replacement assessment.\n- Document findings, corrective actions performed, and impact to services.\n- Capture photos of switch, cabling, UPS, power source, SFPs, and any identified issues.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset & Location:** HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05 (Cisco Meraki MS350-24P) – 2nd Floor\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (cat5e and cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (cat5e and cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- SFP modules\n- Ethernet patch cables\n- Spare fiber patch cables\n- Fiber cleaning kit\n- Laser to verify light continuity\n- Fiber tester\n- Spare power cord\n- Flashlight","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T15:00","end":"2026-10-20T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":50.41857574694509},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $260\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00