{"job":{"id":"8605095193","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"FieldStar IT","title":"LifePoint Springstone (Triangle Springs Hospital)-Phones","description":"<p>LifePoint Phone System Migration</p><p><br></p><p>Existing Provider: Lingo</p><p>New Provider: Zoom</p><p><br></p><p>Duration: 2 Days |</p><p><br></p><p>Day 1: Staging, Inventory &amp; Preparation</p><p><br></p><p>Day 2: Phone Porting, Cutover &amp; Testing</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Project Overview</strong></p><p>Two qualified onsite technicians will assist the migration from Lingo to Zoom, working with remote engineers to inventory and deploy phones, stage and install AudioCodes voice gateways, and support cutover and testing. This high-priority project requires technical readiness, communication, and adherence to the approved run book.</p><p><br></p><p><u>Day 1-Staging, Inventory &amp; Preparation</u></p><p>Objective: Prepare the site, equipment, and phones for migration.</p><p><br></p><p>Onsite Technician Responsibilities:</p><ul><li>Arrive on time, check in with the designated onsite Point of Contact (POC), and join the emailed conference bridge to coordinate with remote engineering.</li><li>Locate Zoom phones, AudioCodes gateways, and accessories. Inventory all equipment and report missing, damaged, or incorrect items.</li><li>Review the phone deployment workbook; verify extensions, phone assignments, locations, and MAC addresses. Identify the receptionist's phone by MAC address and confirm its location with the POC.</li><li>Confirm priority users and departments with the customer and establish the deployment order. Distribute phones to designated desks and workstations per the workbook.</li><li>Walk the site and document the number and locations of wall-mounted phones.</li><li>Locate telecom closets, network switches, existing voice gateways, and associated Amphenol cabling.</li><li>Unbox, stage, and rack new AudioCodes gateways as directed by remote engineering.</li><li>Identify and document existing gateway connections, switch names, and relevant ports for the remote team.</li><li>Confirm equipment readiness and escalate issues that could affect the scheduled port.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Day 1 Deliverables:</u></p><ul><li>Completed equipment inventory, phone assignments, and deployment verification.</li><li>Phones placed at their designated locations; AudioCodes gateways staged and racked.</li><li>Wall-mounted phone counts and locations; network/gateway connectivity documented.</li><li>Discrepancies and potential cutover concerns reported; Day 2 site readiness confirmed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Day 2-Phone Porting, Cutover &amp; Testing</u></p><p>Objective: Provide onsite assistance to remote engineering during the Lingo-to-Zoom cutover.</p><p><br></p><p>Onsite Technician Responsibilities:</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Check in with the POC, join the bridge, review the cutover run book, and confirm instructions with remote engineering.</li><li>Locate existing gateways and verify connections documented during staging.</li><li>Only as directed, move the Ethernet cable from the legacy gateway to WAN Port 1 on the new AudioCodes gateway (never the LAN port).</li><li>For additional gateways, identify available ports on the same switch and provide switch names and port details to the remote team.</li><li>Assist with gateway connections, console access, and troubleshooting under engineering direction.</li><li>Power-cycle phones as instructed to initiate provisioning, firmware updates, and required reboots; support activation and configuration troubleshooting.</li><li>Prioritize receptionist phones and other business-critical users specified by the customer.</li><li>Assist remote engineering with inbound/outbound call, extension, and phone-function testing. Investigate failed registration, provisioning, activation, and network connectivity.</li><li>Disconnect or remove legacy equipment only with explicit remote engineering authorization.</li><li>Verify phone and gateway tasks, document unresolved issues, and report completion status to remote engineering and Fieldstar IT.</li><li>Obtain remote engineering clearance before leaving the site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Day 2 Deliverables:</u></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Cutover and AudioCodes connectivity support completed as directed.</li><li>Provisioning, reboot, firmware, activation, and functional testing support provided.</li><li>Outstanding issues documented and escalated; remote engineering completion clearance received.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Technician Tools &amp; Equipment</strong></p><p>Both technicians must bring working equipment:</p><ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet and console connectivity.</li><li>Charged cell phone and charger.</li><li>Butt set; Ethernet patch cables; console cable.</li><li>Laptop adapters required for direct device connections.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Verify all tools work before arrival.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Conference Bridge &amp; Communication Requirements</strong></p><p>Both technicians must remain engaged and communicate consistently with remote engineering:</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Join the bridge on arrival, remain available, and check in at least every 30 minutes (or more frequently if requested).</li><li>Announce extended off-bridge tasks and estimated return times; notify the team before lunch or breaks.</li><li>Provide updates when helping the POC or onsite employees, and clearly communicate each technician's responsibilities and progress.</li><li>Immediately escalate technical issues, missing equipment, delays, or barriers to completion.</li><li>Never disconnect from the bridge or leave the site without notifying the remote team and securing approval.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Unresponsiveness, unexplained departures, and failure to communicate work status are unacceptable.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technical Requirements &amp; Important Instructions</strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>AudioCodes Gateway Connectivity:</u></p><ul><li>Connect Ethernet to WAN Port 1, never the LAN port.</li><li>Validate switch names and port assignments with remote engineering.</li><li>Do not disconnect production equipment or make gateway changes without engineer authorization; follow all engineer instructions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Phone Deployment:</u></p><ul><li>Follow the approved workbook for extensions, locations, MAC addresses, and device placement.</li><li>Prioritize receptionist and business-critical phones.</li><li>Phones may require power cycling, firmware updates, or multiple provisioning reboots. Report failures to register or activate.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Equipment Handling:</u></p><ul><li>Document existing cabling or equipment concerns and keep work areas clean and organized.</li><li>Do not remove, relocate, or dispose of legacy equipment without authorization.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Professional Conduct &amp; Site Expectations</strong></p><p>Technicians represent Fieldstar IT and its partners and must:</p><ul><li>Communicate respectfully and professionally with customers, onsite staff, and engineers, regardless of others' tone or informality.</li><li>Avoid personal remarks, inappropriate jokes, and non-work conversations on customer conference bridges.</li><li>Follow onsite POC and authorized engineer instructions.</li><li>Direct scheduling conflicts and concerns to Fieldstar IT, not the customer.</li><li>Obtain project-team clearance before departing.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation &amp; Completion Requirements</strong></p><p>Before leaving on either day, provide:</p><ul><li>Summary of completed tasks, inventory results, and any discrepancies.</li><li>Updated phone deployment status and applicable switch/gateway connection details.</li><li>Before-and-after photos of equipment and installation areas.</li><li>Outstanding issues, recommended follow-up, and any completion blockers.</li><li>Confirmation that remote engineering has authorized departure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation &amp; Scope Management</strong></p><p>Immediately notify Fieldstar IT of technical delays, missing items, unexpected conditions, or additional work. Technicians must not independently change the agreed scope, schedule return visits, make unauthorized changes, or leave without informing the project team. Additional troubleshooting or time must be coordinated through Fieldstar IT.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Project Completion Criteria</strong></p><p>The engagement is complete when:</p><p><br></p><ul><li>All staging, inventory, and deployment tasks are finished.</li><li>Gateway connectivity and scheduled cutover support are completed as directed.</li><li>Phone functionality is tested to the extent possible with remote engineers.</li><li>Open issues are documented, communicated, and escalated as appropriate.</li><li>Remote engineering confirms technicians are no longer needed onsite.</li><li>Fieldstar IT receives the final work summary, photos, and required documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Final Note: Success depends on qualified technicians, working tools, responsive communication, and close coordination with remote engineering. Both technicians must review this scope and the accompanying run book before arrival and follow them throughout both visits.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-26T24:00"},"payRange":{"min":119.26605505,"max":1908.2568808},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":119.26605505,"estLaborHours":16,"distance":7.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Mon, Oct 26, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 26, Tue, Oct 27, Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:3