{"job":{"id":20210691,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"SDWAN Cutover- Type 1 (Cables will be shipped directly to the tech or Fedex hold)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ol><li><strong><u>Fill out the Provider Custom Field Shipping_Information</u></strong></li></ol><br/><br/><p>This can be your home address if there are not issues having packages delivered and someone is available to sign for the packages. There will be qty 4-7ft red cables shipped. See attached photo for reference of package</p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>OR this can be shipped to a Fedex HOLD facility. You can use this link if you do not have a preferred hold location. </u></strong><strong><u>Find FedEx at Walgreens locations</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Pre-Onsite Work:</u></strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>Equipment/Materials will be shipped directly to the technician assigned or to Fedex hold facility as close to the store as possible. Assigned technician MUST pick up equipment prior to the scheduled date and send confirmation this has been completed. This will be a precheck task, with all delivery/tracking info being sent to your email.</strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>The materials being shipped will be 7ft red patch cables. The quantity will be either 2 cables or 4 cabled depending on how many circuits there are at this location.</strong></p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong><u>Scope of Work on Site: This is after hours work- please check start time</u></strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Check in with store manager, then locate the store&#39;s &quot;Control Room&quot; Control Room Code <del>*******</del>.</li><li><strong><u>Locate and test new Verizon circuit</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Install CAT6a for cutover</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Label all newly installed cables clearly and legibly with label maker</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Technician must arrive on time. Remote engineers will be on a live bridge awaiting your arrival. Check-in with site contacts representing </u></strong><del>*******</del></li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.</em></p><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong>Tool Requirement:</strong></p><br/><br/><p><strong>Note: extending the circuit may be required. Tech will need to be prepared to terminate cables while on site without issue.</strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li><strong>Charged Cell Phone</strong> (with charger)- you may be asked to share your video, ensure this is not an issue</li><li><strong>Government-Issued Photo ID</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop (WIN10) with ethernet port and charger</strong></li><li><strong>Label Maker with correct label stock:</strong></li></ul><br/><br/><p>1/2” Black on White, Flexible ID (Patch Cables)</p><br/><br/><p>NO FLAGS — wrap label fully around the cable</p><br/><br/><p>Labeling details will come from remote engineer on bridge line</p><br/><br/><ul><li>Basic CAT6/RJ45 termination tools</li><li>Cable tester with Pass/Fail identifier</li><li>Standard networking tool kit (RJ45, biscuits, etc.)</li><li>Hotspot / internet dongle</li><li>Laptop with an ethernet port, or gigabit+ usb ethernet dongle, with Charger</li><li>Cell phone with Charger</li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p><br/><br/><p><strong>Site Security Requirements:</strong></p><br/><br/><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance </li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>*******</del></li><li><strong><u>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment </u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Professional environment expects professional conduct and clean business casual attire</u></strong></li></ul><br/><br/><p> </p>","markdown":"**AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED**\n\n  \n  \n1. **Fill out the Provider Custom Field Shipping\\_Information**\n\n  \n  \nThis can be your home address if there are not issues having packages delivered and someone is available to sign for the packages. There will be qty 4-7ft red cables shipped. See attached photo for reference of package\n\n  \n  \n**OR this can be shipped to a Fedex HOLD facility. You can use this link if you do not have a preferred hold location.** **Find FedEx at Walgreens locations**\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Pre-Onsite Work:**\n\n  \n  \n**Equipment/Materials will be shipped directly to the technician assigned or to Fedex hold facility as close to the store as possible. Assigned technician MUST pick up equipment prior to the scheduled date and send confirmation this has been completed. This will be a precheck task, with all delivery/tracking info being sent to your email.**\n\n  \n  \n**The materials being shipped will be 7ft red patch cables. The quantity will be either 2 cables or 4 cabled depending on how many circuits there are at this location.**\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Scope of Work on Site: This is after hours work- please check start time**\n\n  \n  \n- Check in with store manager, then locate the store's \"Control Room\" Control Room Code \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n- **Locate and test new Verizon circuit**\n- **Install CAT6a for cutover**\n- **Label all newly installed cables clearly and legibly with label maker**\n- **Technician must arrive on time. Remote engineers will be on a live bridge awaiting your arrival. Check-in with site contacts representing** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.*\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n  \n  \n**Note: extending the circuit may be required. Tech will need to be prepared to terminate cables while on site without issue.**\n\n  \n  \n- **Charged Cell Phone** (with charger)- you may be asked to share your video, ensure this is not an issue\n- **Government-Issued Photo ID**\n- **Laptop (WIN10) with ethernet port and charger**\n- **Label Maker with correct label stock:**\n\n  \n  \n1/2” Black on White, Flexible ID (Patch Cables)\n\n  \n  \nNO FLAGS — wrap label fully around the cable\n\n  \n  \nLabeling details will come from remote engineer on bridge line\n\n  \n  \n- Basic CAT6/RJ45 termination tools\n- Cable tester with Pass/Fail identifier\n- Standard networking tool kit (RJ45, biscuits, etc.)\n- Hotspot / internet dongle\n- Laptop with an ethernet port, or gigabit+ usb ethernet dongle, with Charger\n- Cell phone with Charger\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n  \n  \n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment**\n- **Professional environment expects professional conduct and clean business casual attire**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T03:30","end":"2026-10-27T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":9.904471729471007},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 28, 1:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $450 · listed maximum: $210\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000