{"job":{"id":20210693,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pomeroy","title":"Tory Burch POS and Server Preventative Maintenance","description":{"html":"<p>Tory Burch Preventative Maintenance- POS and Server. Perform preventative maintenance and visual inspection of registers and server.</p><p>Please ensure you are on time, arriving at 9 am. Penalties for late arrivals will be imposed.</p><p>Upon arrival, check in with Pomeroy coordinator.</p><p>Call <del>*****</del> support line promptly at 9:00 am and check in with the analyst.</p><p>Work with analyst on tasks in the checklist, including cleaning dust, confirming fan is operational and testing peripherals attached to the register. The analyst will walk you through removing the head cover from the register, using the small push button on the back.</p><p>Perform a visual inspection of the server and report failures. Clean any airflow blockages.</p><p>Take a picture of the server and surrounding area.<strong> The model number and serial number of the server must be clearly visible.</strong></p><p>Complete the checklist and submit to work order creator prior to leaving the site.</p><p>Checkout with analyst on <del>*****</del> support line.</p><p>Preventative maintenance work will take between 1 to 2 hours.</p><p><strong>Required Technician Tools/Materials:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Paper towels</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Lint free cloths</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Canned air</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Windex </span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Paper clip&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Screwdriver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Pliers</span></li></ul>","markdown":"Tory Burch Preventative Maintenance- POS and Server. Perform preventative maintenance and visual inspection of registers and server.\n\nPlease ensure you are on time, arriving at 9 am. Penalties for late arrivals will be imposed.\n\nUpon arrival, check in with Pomeroy coordinator.\n\nCall \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support line promptly at 9:00 am and check in with the analyst.\n\nWork with analyst on tasks in the checklist, including cleaning dust, confirming fan is operational and testing peripherals attached to the register. The analyst will walk you through removing the head cover from the register, using the small push button on the back.\n\nPerform a visual inspection of the server and report failures. Clean any airflow blockages.\n\nTake a picture of the server and surrounding area. **The model number and serial number of the server must be clearly visible.**\n\nComplete the checklist and submit to work order creator prior to leaving the site.\n\nCheckout with analyst on \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support line.\n\nPreventative maintenance work will take between 1 to 2 hours.\n\n**Required Technician Tools/Materials:**\n\n- Paper towels\n- Lint free cloths\n- Canned air\n- Windex\n- Paper clip\n- Screwdriver\n- Pliers","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T09:00","end":"2026-10-28T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":32.20320046785529},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792518977252}
{"job":{"id":20210897,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Server CPU & RAM upgrade on single PowerEdge R720 - OPPTY 1037913","description":{"html":"<p>Final Server </p><p><br></p><p>You will be replacing the RAM and CPU in one of six PowerEdge R720 servers on site. This is the first visit, and follow-on visits for the remaining 5 servers may be routed to you first if this is successful visit.</p><p>Please review the following scope. If you do not feel comfortable with or are unfamiliar with the process involved, please do not request this assignment.</p><p>The six server asset tags are: H7XV842, H7XT842, 1S1HD42, 1S1JD42, 1S0LD42, 1S0KD42. You will only service one for this assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>o Customer IT will place the host in maintenance mode and evacuate VMs prior to service.</p><p>o Confirm system shutdown.</p><p>o Remove and replace two (2) existing Xeon E5-2643 v2 CPUs with new Xeon E5-2697 v2 CPUs.</p><p>o Install eight (8) net new DIMMs.</p><p>o Power on and request post-upgrade validation.</p><p>o Leave old CPUs with site contact.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Customer-provided Equipment List:</strong></p><p>o Intel Xeon E5-2697 v2 CPUs (Qty 12).</p><p>o RAM DIMMs (up to 48).</p><p>o Thermal paste.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools to Bring: </strong></p><ul><li>Standard tool kit.</li><li>Electrostatic wrist guard.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email aimee.evans@parkplacetech.com or call 678-857-4121 and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment, locked doors or cabinets, or POC not available to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing aimee.evans@parkplacetech.com or call 678-857-4121 will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow any printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided.</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, label maker, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to attend a pre-call to go over scope and expectations.</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Technicians agree to remain professional onsite, per our Code of Conduct, including referring all complaints directly to Park Place Technologies and not our customers.</li><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation, follow directions or lack of technical ability. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"Final Server\n\nYou will be replacing the RAM and CPU in one of six PowerEdge R720 servers on site. This is the first visit, and follow-on visits for the remaining 5 servers may be routed to you first if this is successful visit.\n\nPlease review the following scope. If you do not feel comfortable with or are unfamiliar with the process involved, please do not request this assignment.\n\nThe six server asset tags are: H7XV842, H7XT842, 1S1HD42, 1S1JD42, 1S0LD42, 1S0KD42. You will only service one for this assignment.\n\n**Assignment Scope:**\n\no Customer IT will place the host in maintenance mode and evacuate VMs prior to service.\n\no Confirm system shutdown.\n\no Remove and replace two (2) existing Xeon E5-2643 v2 CPUs with new Xeon E5-2697 v2 CPUs.\n\no Install eight (8) net new DIMMs.\n\no Power on and request post-upgrade validation.\n\no Leave old CPUs with site contact.\n\n**Customer-provided Equipment List:**\n\no Intel Xeon E5-2697 v2 CPUs (Qty 12).\n\no RAM DIMMs (up to 48).\n\no Thermal paste.\n\n**Tools to Bring:**\n\n- Standard tool kit.\n- Electrostatic wrist guard.\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email aimee.evans@parkplacetech.com or call 678-857-4121 and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment, locked doors or cabinets, or POC not available to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing aimee.evans@parkplacetech.com or call 678-857-4121 will ensure we are notified quickly.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow any printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, label maker, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to attend a pre-call to go over scope and expectations.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- Technicians agree to remain professional onsite, per our Code of Conduct, including referring all complaints directly to Park Place Technologies and not our customers.\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation, follow directions or lack of technical ability. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":380,"max":380},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7.726445125499078},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 28, 1:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $450 · listed maximum: $380\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Insta