{"job":{"id":20211446,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Allergy Partners-  Installs","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.</p>\n<p>Must be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.</p>\n<p>Working with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.</p>\n<p>Will need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs</p>\n<p><u>Will be Need to use Company Cam - There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos. Will set you up with access This is MUST for Competion!!</u></p>\n<p>Will Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>DO NOT REMOVE THE EDGE WATER IT IS NESSESARY FOR THE PHONE SYSTEM!!!!&nbsp;DO NOT REMOVE!!!&nbsp;LEAVE!!!</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to work with other technicians.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Distance from sites (no travel provided).</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attend required training.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On the bridge at all times.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have reliable transportation.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Follow the directions from the bridge and</p>\n<p><strong>A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counter offers, and we do not allow substitutions.</strong></p>","markdown":"WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.\n\nMust be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.\n\nWorking with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.\n\nWill need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs\n\nWill be Need to use Company Cam - There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos. Will set you up with access This is MUST for Competion!!\n\nWill Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.\n\n***DO NOT REMOVE THE EDGE WATER IT IS NESSESARY FOR THE PHONE SYSTEM!!!! DO NOT REMOVE!!! LEAVE!!!***\n\n**This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs.**\n\n**Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center.**\n\n**Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:**\n\n· Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)\n\n· Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score\n\n· Ability to work with other technicians.\n\n· Distance from sites (no travel provided).\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n· Attend required training.\n\n· On the bridge at all times.\n\n· Have reliable transportation.\n\n· Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.\n\n· Follow the directions from the bridge and\n\n**A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counter offers, and we do not allow substitutions.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T08:30","end":"2026-10-23T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":4.86018273315094},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":75,"baseAmount":450,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792522273296}
{"job":{"id":"1951926300","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"White Eagle Technologies","title":"Tv Repair of 75 inches HISENSE LED tv","description":"<p>The SOW/Service Description is below. DO NOT EVER MENTION you are with Work Market. Only identify yourself as a White Eagle Tech.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scheduling</u></strong></p><ul><li>Tech will contact us if ANY scheduling change is to be made</li><li><strong><em><u>We will contact the customer</u></em></strong>&nbsp;to update and change the schedule and communicate ANY schedule changes to us via messages or a phone call.</li><li>ALL dates and times are hard dates and times unless tech contacts us to get them changed or works through the office.</li><li>TV repairs will be done Monday - Friday.</li><li>TV repairs done on weekends are done at buyer approval ONLY and must be documented in the message in the work order.</li><li>Tech will meet with the customer at the appointed time</li><li>Tech will confirm the work order or remove it.&nbsp;If you can not make it to the site CALL the office and speak to someone</li><li>Techs that show up late, WITHOUT leaving a message or calling risk being Blocked permanently.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tech Support:</u></strong></p><ul><li>tech support, IS only available Monday through Friday from 8 am CST to 4 pm CST ONLY</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Service Description:</u></strong></p><p>We are looking for a technician with TV repair experience. Familiar with OLED, LED, Digital, and SmartTV repair issues.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p><p>On this work order, you are required to complete the following:</p><ol><li>Repair TV</li><li>Parts are sent to the customer.</li><li>Return parts (if needed).</li><li>&nbsp;Please call Blue Eagle dispatch 316 313 2627 to verify if parts need to be returned. (Return label will be provided) DO NOT leave parts with the client. The provider is responsible for shipping back parts.</li><li>Upload all deliverables needed to this work order and enter closing notes.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAY:</u></strong></p><p>You may put an SLI in for the work order. It will be reviewed, once this is reviewed and agreed on. The only adjustment will be made if there are any additional trips. We may close the work order out and reissue you another work order at the same price as first agreed on. Do not try to renegotiate the work order after you accept it this will be denied. This work order is a fixed-rate job, please remember that. Once all Deliverables are included the return of parts is required. All work orders will be approved on Friday of the week and then will be paid on the following Friday. Unless prior arrangements are agreed upon in writing. Please document the work order and who approves.</p><ol><li>All work orders after 15 days will get a label Pending cancellation this is your warring to close the work order out for full pay.</li><li>All work orders will be closed out after 30 days and all pay will be forfeited</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Problem of the TV: <strong>No picture, no sound, has power.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>TV is MOUNTED, CUSTOMER CAN HELP</p><p> *Model: 75R6E1</p><p>*S/N: 75G1943V2H02465</p><p>*Brand: HISENSE</p><p><br></p><p><strong>MAIN BOARD&nbsp;</strong> and <strong>POWER BOARD&nbsp;</strong>are sent to the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;Parts that need to be returned are the responsibility of the provider. DO NOT leave parts with the client.</p><p><br></p><p>DURING REPAIR: -DO NOT REPLACE PARTS IF NO PROBLEM IS FOUND WITH A KNOWN WORKING DEVICE</p><p><br></p><p>If repair is unsuccessful please transfer to tech support or call us before going out of the site</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TAKE MANDATORY PHOTOS FOR ALL ONSITE REPAIRS:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><ul><li>TV OSD Menu screenshot when testing with a known working device (TV powered on &amp; all 4 corners should be visible)&nbsp;</li><li>Model/SN sticker -Unsuccessful Scenario Photos:&nbsp;</li><li>Photo of TV layout with the back cover off *ADH/Infestation</li><li>Provide a photo of the damage found&nbsp;</li><li>WiFi/Network Issue: Clear photo of Advance Network Menu Settings&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Incorrect part: Provide a clear photo of the original part # &amp; incorrect replacement part #&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Provider Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>The technician will go on-site and repair a TV.</li><li>The provider must check in and check out on the portal, via the mobile app only</li><li>Must have a good working attitude.</li><li>Follow the dress code.</li></ul><ol><li>&nbsp;Jeans, Good repair, no holes, and clean</li><li>The shirt is colored, in good repair no holes, and clean</li><li>Shoes, No open toe, ie sandals flip flops, or heels</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tech must have the following tools they must bring to All repairs:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Electrician Tool Set:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>DVD or other video output device</strong>&nbsp;(to check the video from an external source)</li><li><em><u>All Samsung TV repairs Must have Tool</u></em>: BN81-14946B To remove the back.</li><li>Video on how to remove the back of the tv's:https://youtu.be/P3fpZXVObbM?si=fHjY8DgcEMVZ5KBW</li><li><br></li><li><strong>Various types of video cables:</strong>&nbsp;HDMI, Component, Coaxial</li><li><strong>Multi-Meter (Electrical Voltage Test Device):</strong>&nbsp;Capable of measuring AC/DC voltage, and detecting standard readings within cables, connectors, and outlets</li><li><strong>Anti-Static Blanket:</strong>&nbsp;The protective blanket should be large enough to service a 70-80” LCD/LED television to reduce the chances of breakage throughout the repair</li><li><strong>Digital Camera:</strong>&nbsp;The camera function on any smartphone should suffice</li><li><strong>Flash Light:</strong>&nbsp;Used to inspect the panel screen for any damage if the TV is unable to power on before the repair</li><li><strong>15-foot Ethernet Cable:</strong>&nbsp;Used to (a) bypass any WiFi router issues, (b) update the firmware in case of insufficient WiFi strength, (c) verify if the TV is within suggested proximity of the router</li><li><strong>Service Remotes</strong>: Ensure to get OEM service remotes to access the service menu (e.g., Samsung). The remotes can be acquired from the OEM directly or from retailers such as Amazon or eBay.</li><li><strong>USB Flash Drive:</strong>&nbsp;Needed to update firmware on TV brands such as Sony and Sharp</li><li>&nbsp;<strong>WiFi Hotspot:</strong>&nbsp;Typically can be found on newer smartphones, and can be used to verify the TV’s wifi functionality without having to troubleshoot any external router/WiFi issues.</li><li>Various sized screwdrivers, pliers, wire stripper, scissors, electrical tape</li></ul><ol><li>Will verify the model and S/N before starting work.</li><li>Take the necessary photos.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><u>Required repair photos (for both successful and unsuccessful repairs):</u></strong></p><ul><li>TV OSD menu shot when testing with a known working device (TV should be powered on and all 4 corners with standby light on bezel should be visible)</li><li>Product service sticker (clear photo of Model/SN information)</li><li>Photo of the internal component layout with the TV back cover off (All connections are correct and secure)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Unsuccessful scenario-based photos:</u></strong></p><ul><li>ADH/Infestation: Provide a detailed photo of the damage found</li><li>WiFi/Network Issue: Provide a clear photo of the Advance Network Menu Settings</li><li>Incorrect part: Provide a clear photo of the original part number and the incorrect replacement part number</li><li><u>If the panel does not show video we need a photo of the tv on the screen face down and power on. For most, tv's you can remove the cable between the power board and the main. </u></li></ul><p><strong><u>In the case of customer no-show (Customer denied repair):</u></strong></p><ul><li>Please contact our service desk for assistance with contacting the customer at 316-313-2627. Do not leave the customer’s residence during an appointment window without our authorization (If no response from us, continue with the following process)</li><li>Take a photo of the customer’s home with the address visible for documentation that the technician was onsite (Do not clear photo properties with time stamp information)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Provide a tracking number for all returned parts. If any damage is found before beginning work please call, and document the damage DO NOT mark this work order as done until you have entered the tracking numbers for the devices you are sending back to our office. Work orders marked \"Done\" by technicians without tracking numbers entered into the work order will have the work order assigned back to them for proper completion and entering of tracking numbers.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T11:00","end":"2026-10-23T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":59.09090909},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":27.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522280465}
{"job":{"id":20211458,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"NCR POS Base Unit Swap - Reg 6","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:</u></strong></p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE</p><p>The site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.</p><p>Technician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.</p><p>Technician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.</p><p>Technician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.</p><p>Technician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.</p><p>Technician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.</p><p>Technician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.</p><p>Technician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.</p><p>Technician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.</p><p>Technician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.</p><p>Technician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.</p><p>After the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.</p><p>After signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the</p><p>next message box should request the register number.</p><p>After entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.</p><p>Technician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.</p><p>**If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!**</p><p>Technician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.</p><p>Technician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.</p><p>Technician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"><del>** ** *** **** **** ** *********** *** ******** ****** *** ***** *** ************ ** * ****** **********</del></span></p><p><strong> **If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.</strong></p><p><strong> If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!**</strong></p><p><strong> **If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately**</strong></p><p>​</p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Required to be paid</u></strong></p><ol><li>Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.</li><li>Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)</li><li>Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done&nbsp;<u>before</u>&nbsp;any work is done.</li><li>Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.</li><li>Technician&nbsp;must take pictures of any equipment worked on&nbsp;<u>after</u>&nbsp;the work is done.</li><li>Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. <strong><u>TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> ** Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Requirements:</u></strong></p><ol><li>​Technician must be familiar with data cabling</li><li>Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable</li><li>Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Part Requirements:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><em><u>IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.</u></em></p><p>Up to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors,&nbsp;Ethernet cables,&nbsp;Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable</p><p><em><u>**POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot**</u></em></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\n**INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE>\n\nThe site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.\n\nTechnician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.\n\nTechnician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.\n\nTechnician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.\n\nTechnician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.\n\nTechnician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.\n\nTechnician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.\n\nTechnician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.\n\nTechnician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.\n\nTechnician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.\n\nTechnician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.\n\nAfter the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.\n\nAfter signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the\n\nnext message box should request the register number.\n\nAfter entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.\n\nTechnician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.\n\n\\*\\*If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!\\*\\*\n\nTechnician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.\n\nTechnician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.\n\nTechnician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **\\*\\*If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.**\n\n **If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!\\*\\***\n\n **\\*\\*If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately\\*\\***\n\n​\n\n**Deliverables Required to be paid**\n\n1. Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.\n2. Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)\n3. Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.\n4. Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.\n5. Technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.\n6. Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. **TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS**\n\n **\\*\\* Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay\\*\\***\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n1. ​Technician must be familiar with data cabling\n2. Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable\n3. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment\n\n**Part Requirements:**\n\n*IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.*\n\nUp to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors, Ethernet cables, Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 & RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable\n\n*\\*\\*POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot\\*\\**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T12:00","end":"2026-10-27T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11.920137696654699},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522334418}
{"job":{"id":20211477,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"NCR POS Base Unit Swap - Reg 1","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:</u></strong></p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE</p><p>The site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.</p><p>Technician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.</p><p>Technician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.</p><p>Technician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.</p><p>Technician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.</p><p>Technician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.</p><p>Technician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.</p><p>Technician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.</p><p>Technician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.</p><p>Technician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.</p><p>Technician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.</p><p>After the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.</p><p>After signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the</p><p>next message box should request the register number.</p><p>After entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.</p><p>Technician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.</p><p>**If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!**</p><p>Technician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.</p><p>Technician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.</p><p>Technician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"><del>** ** *** **** **** ** *********** *** ******** ****** *** ***** *** ************ ** * ****** **********</del></span></p><p><strong> **If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.</strong></p><p><strong> If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!**</strong></p><p><strong> **If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately**</strong></p><p>​</p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Required to be paid</u></strong></p><ol><li>Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.</li><li>Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)</li><li>Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done&nbsp;<u>before</u>&nbsp;any work is done.</li><li>Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.</li><li>Technician&nbsp;must take pictures of any equipment worked on&nbsp;<u>after</u>&nbsp;the work is done.</li><li>Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. <strong><u>TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> ** Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Requirements:</u></strong></p><ol><li>​Technician must be familiar with data cabling</li><li>Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable</li><li>Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Part Requirements:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><em><u>IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.</u></em></p><p>Up to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors,&nbsp;Ethernet cables,&nbsp;Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable</p><p><em><u>**POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot**</u></em></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\n**INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE>\n\nThe site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.\n\nTechnician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.\n\nTechnician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.\n\nTechnician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.\n\nTechnician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.\n\nTechnician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.\n\nTechnician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.\n\nTechnician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.\n\nTechnician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.\n\nTechnician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.\n\nTechnician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.\n\nAfter the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.\n\nAfter signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the\n\nnext message box should request the register number.\n\nAfter entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.\n\nTechnician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.\n\n\\*\\*If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!\\*\\*\n\nTechnician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.\n\nTechnician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.\n\nTechnician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **\\*\\*If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.**\n\n **If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!\\*\\***\n\n **\\*\\*If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately\\*\\***\n\n​\n\n**Deliverables Required to be paid**\n\n1. Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.\n2. Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)\n3. Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.\n4. Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.\n5. Technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.\n6. Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. **TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS**\n\n **\\*\\* Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay\\*\\***\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n1. ​Technician must be familiar with data cabling\n2. Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable\n3. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment\n\n**Part Requirements:**\n\n*IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.*\n\nUp to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors, Ethernet cables, Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 & RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable\n\n*\\*\\*POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot\\*\\**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T12:00","end":"2026-10-27T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11.920137696654699},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522399067}
{"job":{"id":20211382,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gaichu Managed Services","title":"DISPATCH REQUEST - 3275464 - Danville, US- (IMPORTANT: Pictures of cables required for confirmation of this dispatch)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Note:</strong></p><p>Kindly share clear pictures of the following cables along with your Request and Counter Offer:</p><ul><li>Console Cable (RJ45 to USB or Serial to RJ45)</li><li>USB-A Male to Mini-USB Male Cable</li><li>LAN Cable</li><li>Windows based Laptop</li></ul><p>These images are required for verification before we proceed with the site visit.</p><p>Please send the pictures to <strong>dispatch@gaichums.com</strong> along with your <strong>Field Nation Work Order number</strong>.</p><p>Sample pictures are attached for your reference in the WO.</p><p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p><p>&nbsp;Special Instructions for Tech:</p><p><del>******* ********* **********</del></p><p><del>******** ***** ****** **** *** ** ****** * ***** ******** *** *************** ****** ******* ****</del></p><p>Technician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing</p><p>If access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.</p><p><br></p><p>________________________________________________________________________________</p><p>Interface Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)</p><p>System &amp; Model #:</p><p>Openeye</p><p>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :</p><ul><li>Technician must bring headlight restoration/cleaning and polishing of camera covers/lenses to improve image clarity and overall camera performance and all necessary equipment.</li><li>Inspect and verify the video quality of all CCTV cameras, with special attention to:</li><li>Camera 4 | Camera 5 | Camera 6 | Camera 7 and Camera 8 and ensure the above-mentioned cameras are providing clear, sharp, and good-quality images, and make any necessary adjustments to focus, angle, or lens condition.</li><li>Also technician must review the recording playback and storage system on-site to verify that all cameras are recording continuously and properly, review the recording playback and storage system on-site to verify that all cameras are recording continuously and properly and confirm that there are no interruptions in recording and that footage can be successfully retrieved from the system.</li></ul><p>Parts Needed:</p><p>Not needed</p><p>Specific Scheduling Request :</p><p>NONE</p><p>Other Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request:</p><p>NONE</p><p>Cause :</p><p><strong><u>Site Representation:</u> </strong><del>*********</del></p><p><strong><u>INSTUCTIONS:</u></strong></p><p>Please Do not accept the WO if you do not have below cables:</p><ul><li><strong>Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable along with drivers installed (Pictures Attached)</strong></li><li><strong>Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45 (Pictures Attached)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Tech needs to bring Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable (Picture attached for reference) - PLEASE VERIFY BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER.</strong></p><p><strong>Make sure tech has Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable - Driver installed as well (Driver is attached in Files) - PLEASE VERIFY BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER</strong>.</p><p>&nbsp;The FE should not identify themselves as a <strong>GAICHU Tech</strong>.</p><p>Any onsite issues need to be reported to us immediately. This includes any scope questions or questions around materials.</p><p>The assigned FE should be familiar with the scope prior to rolling to site. We provide the SR and the Install Guide for this reason. We ask that this be reviewed as early as possible to avoid extra time on site and any issues that may arise otherwise.</p><p><strong>Our Primary mode of communication with engineer will be WhatsApp, please install prior to the task and if any issue please reach out to team for alternative mode of communication.</strong></p><p><strong>Tech needs to take approval from technical team prior to using any material and receipt/invoice needs to be uploaded for approval.</strong></p><p><strong> <u>Task Requirement:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong>1- Faulty device needs to be carry with you after the task is completed</strong></p><p><strong>2- Customer will provide shipping label - the tech needs to drop off the device to the nearby courier place.</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech to capture the details if the store / Whitebox device is grounded or not.</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Material Receipt:</strong> If a technician plans to use personal materials, they must present a receipt with the material cost for payment approval. If a receipt cannot be provided, the technician may not use personal materials on-site. They should visit a nearby store, purchase needed materials, and submit the receipt for approval. If materials are unavailable nearby and no receipt can be provided, the technician should not use personal materials, and the activity will need rescheduling.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>RMA pictures:</strong> Following pictures are must to capture for device shipment&nbsp;</p><p>Photo of sealed box with return label&nbsp;</p><p>Photo of the completed equipment return form.&nbsp;</p><p>Return tracking number.</p><p>FedEx receipt</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Requirement:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Windows Laptop </u></strong>with WIFI Access with <strong><em>admin rights</em></strong></li><li>TeamViewer, Cisco WebEx, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Blue jeans, Installed on your Laptop.</li><li>Terminal Server Emulator (Putty, Secure CRT)</li><li>Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable along with drivers installed.</li><li>Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45</li><li>USB Drivers if using USB connection RS232.</li><li>Mobile Hotspot for tethering</li><li>Extra Ethernet Patch Cables (3 patch Cables 12 -15 ft. in length - Will be reimburse accordingly when it is used, Receipt must be shared)</li><li>VELCRO Straps for rack cable management/patch cords</li><li>USB Flash drive (Atleast 32 or above GB)</li><li>RJ45 Jacks</li><li>Crimping Tools</li><li>Ethernet Tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Screwdriver Set</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Cat5/6 Cable Role</li><li>Mobile Phone with Nano &amp; Micro Sim Compatible</li><li><strong>Ladder 10 Feet A Frame</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"><u>Terms &amp; Conditions:</u></strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Please remain professional demeanor while on site. Do not engage in any conversation with local site contacts or any staff members unrelated to work.&nbsp;<strong>Keep all conversations strictly work-related.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Engineer must carry a valid ID for access; access won't be granted without it.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not represent FIELDNATION</strong> on site unless specified, check with our support team for clarification.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Technician must stay onsite until task completion; </strong>leaving without<strong> GAICHU technical team's authorization </strong>results in<strong> no payment </strong>and task deemed<strong> Incomplete. ***IMPORTANT***</strong></p><p><strong> </strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Share onsite <strong>Time IN</strong> and <strong>Time Out</strong> with the technical team before leaving.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rude behavior </strong>is not acceptable onsite and will lead to disciplinary action</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wear professional clothing for the task.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>All tools mentioned in the work order must be taken to the site; if any tools reported to be missing while you are onsite, and work affected because of it will result in no payment.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take all tools mentioned in the work order to the site; missing tools affecting work will result in no payment. ***IMPORTANT***</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Share all expenses (Travel, Gas, Parking &amp; Toll) before accepting the Work Order. No additional expenses will be approved after the task. <strong>***IMPORTANT***</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Do not bring unauthorized persons onsite without written confirmation; non-compliance will result in unpaid Work Order and be seen as a security breach.</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Share receipts for materials purchased or used onsite for reimbursement; payment won't be authorized without relevant receipts.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please take pictures before and after the execution of work.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take Before</strong> and <strong>After</strong> pictures of the work execution.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect <strong>Console Cable</strong> <strong>or USB to DB9 Converter</strong> to laptop and share the <strong>Device Manager</strong> picture showing <strong>COM PORT</strong> before starting the task to confirm proper driver installation.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please see below the WhatsApp requirement for all future Field nation tasks:</p><p><strong>Please install WhatsApp application in your smart phone and send WhatsApp message containing FN WO if you need any technical assistance and when you are onsite then reach out to below contact persons:</strong></p><p><strong>Tayyaba Munawar:</strong> +92 332 5456738</p><p><strong>Mehreen Arshad:</strong> +92 330 5000522</p><p><strong>Hamza Malik:</strong> ‪+92 325 9182128‬</p><p><strong>Kashan Ul Haq:</strong> +92 347 9859366&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please visit the links below to install WhatsApp and to add WhatsApp contacts.</p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaRsRytz1NQ</p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65IHJAgXIyY&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>If you have any query regarding schedule or payment you need to reach out to below contact details:</strong></p><p><strong>Ammar Ibrahim +92 319 6241457</strong></p><p><strong>Safwan Sajjad: +92 336 5509218</strong></p><p><strong>Jawad Jami: +92 314 0916262</strong></p>","markdown":"**Note:**\n\nKindly share clear pictures of the following cables along with your Request and Counter Offer:\n\n- Console Cable (RJ45 to USB or Serial to RJ45)\n- USB-A Male to Mini-USB Male Cable\n- LAN Cable\n- Windows based Laptop\n\nThese images are required for verification before we proceed with the site visit.\n\nPlease send the pictures to **dispatch@gaichums.com** along with your **Field Nation Work Order number**.\n\nSample pictures are attached for your reference in the WO.\n\n**SOW:**\n\n Special Instructions for Tech:\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTechnician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing\n\nIf access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nInterface Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)\n\nSystem & Model #:\n\nOpeneye\n\nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem :\n\n- Technician must bring headlight restoration/cleaning and polishing of camera covers/lenses to improve image clarity and overall camera performance and all necessary equipment.\n- Inspect and verify the video quality of all CCTV cameras, with special attention to:\n- Camera 4 | Camera 5 | Camera 6 | Camera 7 and Camera 8 and ensure the above-mentioned cameras are providing clear, sharp, and good-quality images, and make any necessary adjustments to focus, angle, or lens condition.\n- Also technician must review the recording playback and storage system on-site to verify that all cameras are recording continuously and properly, review the recording playback and storage system on-site to verify that all cameras are recording continuously and properly and confirm that there are no interruptions in recording and that footage can be successfully retrieved from the system.\n\nParts Needed:\n\nNot needed\n\nSpecific Scheduling Request :\n\nNONE\n\nOther Open Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request:\n\nNONE\n\nCause :\n\n**Site Representation:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**INSTUCTIONS:**\n\nPlease Do not accept the WO if you do not have below cables:\n\n- **Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable along with drivers installed (Pictures Attached)**\n- **Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45 (Pictures Attached)**\n\n**Tech needs to bring Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable (Picture attached for reference) - PLEASE VERIFY BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Make sure tech has Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable - Driver installed as well (Driver is attached in Files) - PLEASE VERIFY BEFORE ACCEPTING THE WORK ORDER**.\n\n The FE should not identify themselves as a **GAICHU Tech**.\n\nAny onsite issues need to be reported to us immediately. This includes any scope questions or questions around materials.\n\nThe assigned FE should be familiar with the scope prior to rolling to site. We provide the SR and the Install Guide for this reason. We ask that this be reviewed as early as possible to avoid extra time on site and any issues that may arise otherwise.\n\n**Our Primary mode of communication with engineer will be WhatsApp, please install prior to the task and if any issue please reach out to team for alternative mode of communication.**\n\n**Tech needs to take approval from technical team prior to using any material and receipt/invoice needs to be uploaded for approval.**\n\n **Task Requirement:**\n\n**1- Faulty device needs to be carry with you after the task is completed**\n\n**2- Customer will provide shipping label - the tech needs to drop off the device to the nearby courier place.**\n\n**• Tech to capture the details if the store / Whitebox device is grounded or not.**\n\n**• Material Receipt:** If a technician plans to use personal materials, they must present a receipt with the material cost for payment approval. If a receipt cannot be provided, the technician may not use personal materials on-site. They should visit a nearby store, purchase needed materials, and submit the receipt for approval. If materials are unavailable nearby and no receipt can be provided, the technician should not use personal materials, and the activity will need rescheduling.\n\n• **RMA pictures:** Following pictures are must to capture for device shipment\n\nPhoto of sealed box with return label\n\nPhoto of the completed equipment return form.\n\nReturn tracking number.\n\nFedEx receipt\n\n**Tools Requirement:**\n\n- **Windows Laptop** with WIFI Access with ***admin rights***\n- TeamViewer, Cisco WebEx, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Blue jeans, Installed on your Laptop.\n- Terminal Server Emulator (Putty, Secure CRT)\n- Mini USB 2.0 Device Cable along with drivers installed.\n- Standard CISCO Console Cable DB9 to RJ45 or USB to RJ45\n- USB Drivers if using USB connection RS232.\n- Mobile Hotspot for tethering\n- Extra Ethernet Patch Cables (3 patch Cables 12 -15 ft. in length - Will be reimburse accordingly when it is used, Receipt must be shared)\n- VELCRO Straps for rack cable management/patch cords\n- USB Flash drive (Atleast 32 or above GB)\n- RJ45 Jacks\n- Crimping Tools\n- Ethernet Tester\n- Toner\n- Label Maker\n- Screwdriver Set\n- Cable Tester\n- Cat5/6 Cable Role\n- Mobile Phone with Nano & Micro Sim Compatible\n- **Ladder 10 Feet A Frame**\n\n**Terms & Conditions:**\n\n**·** Please remain professional demeanor while on site. Do not engage in any conversation with local site contacts or any staff members unrelated to work. **Keep all conversations strictly work-related.**\n\n**· Engineer must carry a valid ID for access; access won't be granted without it.**\n\n**· Do not represent FIELDNATION** on site unless specified, check with our support team for clarification.\n\n**· Technician must stay onsite until task completion;** leaving without **GAICHU technical team's authorization** results in **no payment** and task deemed **Incomplete. \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\*\\***\n\n · Share onsite **Time IN** and **Time Out** with the technical team before leaving.\n\n**· Rude behavior** is not acceptable onsite and will lead to disciplinary action\n\n**· Wear professional clothing for the task.**\n\n**·** All tools mentioned in the work order must be taken to the site; if any tools reported to be missing while you are onsite, and work affected because of it will result in no payment.\n\n**· Take all tools mentioned in the work order to the site; missing tools affecting work will result in no payment. \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\*\\***\n\n**·** Share all expenses (Travel, Gas, Parking & Toll) before accepting the Work Order. No additional expenses will be approved after the task. **\\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\*\\***\n\n**·** Do not bring unauthorized persons onsite without written confirmation; non-compliance will result in unpaid Work Order and be seen as a security breach.\n\n**· Share receipts for materials purchased or used onsite for reimbursement; payment won't be authorized without relevant receipts.**\n\n**· Please take pictures before and after the execution of work.**\n\n**· Take Before** and **After** pictures of the work execution.\n\n· Connect **Console Cable** **or USB to DB9 Converter** to laptop and share the **Device Manager** picture showing **COM PORT** before starting the task to confirm proper driver installation.\n\n· Please see below the WhatsApp requirement for all future Field nation tasks:\n\n**Please install WhatsApp application in your smart phone and send WhatsApp message containing FN WO if you need any technical assistance and when you are onsite then reach out to below contact persons:**\n\n**Tayyaba Munawar:** +92 332 5456738\n\n**Mehreen Arshad:** +92 330 5000522\n\n**Hamza Malik:** ‪+92 325 9182128‬\n\n**Kashan Ul Haq:** +92 347 9859366\n\nPlease visit the links below to install WhatsApp and to add WhatsApp contacts.\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaRsRytz1NQ>\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65IHJAgXIyY&nbsp;>\n\n**If you have any query regarding schedule or payment you need to reach out to below contact details:**\n\n**Ammar Ibrahim +92 319 6241457**\n\n**Safwan Sajjad: +92 336 5509218**\n\n**Jawad Jami: +92 314 0916262**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:45","end":"2026-10-21T12:45"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":190},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":62.35424494057629},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $190\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522537058}
{"job":{"id":20209682,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 491","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13131133</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK & TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13131133\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11.041054978754964},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522678053}
{"job":{"id":20209824,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 493","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13131146</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK & TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13131146\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":15.999358184546761},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engi