NTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK & TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13131146\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":19.87454542445283},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792522760602}
{"job":{"id":"1951926300","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"White Eagle Technologies","title":"Tv Repair of 75 inches HISENSE LED tv","description":"<p>The SOW/Service Description is below. DO NOT EVER MENTION you are with Work Market. Only identify yourself as a White Eagle Tech.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scheduling</u></strong></p><ul><li>Tech will contact us if ANY scheduling change is to be made</li><li><strong><em><u>We will contact the customer</u></em></strong>&nbsp;to update and change the schedule and communicate ANY schedule changes to us via messages or a phone call.</li><li>ALL dates and times are hard dates and times unless tech contacts us to get them changed or works through the office.</li><li>TV repairs will be done Monday - Friday.</li><li>TV repairs done on weekends are done at buyer approval ONLY and must be documented in the message in the work order.</li><li>Tech will meet with the customer at the appointed time</li><li>Tech will confirm the work order or remove it.&nbsp;If you can not make it to the site CALL the office and speak to someone</li><li>Techs that show up late, WITHOUT leaving a message or calling risk being Blocked permanently.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tech Support:</u></strong></p><ul><li>tech support, IS only available Monday through Friday from 8 am CST to 4 pm CST ONLY</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Service Description:</u></strong></p><p>We are looking for a technician with TV repair experience. Familiar with OLED, LED, Digital, and SmartTV repair issues.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p><p>On this work order, you are required to complete the following:</p><ol><li>Repair TV</li><li>Parts are sent to the customer.</li><li>Return parts (if needed).</li><li>&nbsp;Please call Blue Eagle dispatch 316 313 2627 to verify if parts need to be returned. (Return label will be provided) DO NOT leave parts with the client. The provider is responsible for shipping back parts.</li><li>Upload all deliverables needed to this work order and enter closing notes.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAY:</u></strong></p><p>You may put an SLI in for the work order. It will be reviewed, once this is reviewed and agreed on. The only adjustment will be made if there are any additional trips. We may close the work order out and reissue you another work order at the same price as first agreed on. Do not try to renegotiate the work order after you accept it this will be denied. This work order is a fixed-rate job, please remember that. Once all Deliverables are included the return of parts is required. All work orders will be approved on Friday of the week and then will be paid on the following Friday. Unless prior arrangements are agreed upon in writing. Please document the work order and who approves.</p><ol><li>All work orders after 15 days will get a label Pending cancellation this is your warring to close the work order out for full pay.</li><li>All work orders will be closed out after 30 days and all pay will be forfeited</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Problem of the TV: <strong>No picture, no sound, has power.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>TV is MOUNTED, CUSTOMER CAN HELP</p><p>*Model: 75R6E1</p><p>*S/N: 75G1943V2H02465</p><p>*Brand: HISENSE</p><p><br></p><p><strong>MAIN BOARD&nbsp;</strong> and <strong>POWER BOARD&nbsp;</strong>are sent to the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;Parts that need to be returned are the responsibility of the provider. DO NOT leave parts with the client.</p><p><br></p><p>DURING REPAIR: -DO NOT REPLACE PARTS IF NO PROBLEM IS FOUND WITH A KNOWN WORKING DEVICE</p><p><br></p><p>If repair is unsuccessful please transfer to tech support or call us before going out of the site</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TAKE MANDATORY PHOTOS FOR ALL ONSITE REPAIRS:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><ul><li>TV OSD Menu screenshot when testing with a known working device (TV powered on &amp; all 4 corners should be visible)&nbsp;</li><li>Model/SN sticker -Unsuccessful Scenario Photos:&nbsp;</li><li>Photo of TV layout with the back cover off *ADH/Infestation</li><li>Provide a photo of the damage found&nbsp;</li><li>WiFi/Network Issue: Clear photo of Advance Network Menu Settings&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Incorrect part: Provide a clear photo of the original part # &amp; incorrect replacement part #&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Provider Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>The technician will go on-site and repair a TV.</li><li>The provider must check in and check out on the portal, via the mobile app only</li><li>Must have a good working attitude.</li><li>Follow the dress code.</li></ul><ol><li>&nbsp;Jeans, Good repair, no holes, and clean</li><li>The shirt is colored, in good repair no holes, and clean</li><li>Shoes, No open toe, ie sandals flip flops, or heels</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tech must have the following tools they must bring to All repairs:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Electrician Tool Set:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>DVD or other video output device</strong>&nbsp;(to check the video from an external source)</li><li><em><u>All Samsung TV repairs Must have Tool</u></em>: BN81-14946B To remove the back.</li><li>Video on how to remove the back of the tv's:https://youtu.be/P3fpZXVObbM?si=fHjY8DgcEMVZ5KBW</li><li><br></li><li><strong>Various types of video cables:</strong>&nbsp;HDMI, Component, Coaxial</li><li><strong>Multi-Meter (Electrical Voltage Test Device):</strong>&nbsp;Capable of measuring AC/DC voltage, and detecting standard readings within cables, connectors, and outlets</li><li><strong>Anti-Static Blanket:</strong>&nbsp;The protective blanket should be large enough to service a 70-80” LCD/LED television to reduce the chances of breakage throughout the repair</li><li><strong>Digital Camera:</strong>&nbsp;The camera function on any smartphone should suffice</li><li><strong>Flash Light:</strong>&nbsp;Used to inspect the panel screen for any damage if the TV is unable to power on before the repair</li><li><strong>15-foot Ethernet Cable:</strong>&nbsp;Used to (a) bypass any WiFi router issues, (b) update the firmware in case of insufficient WiFi strength, (c) verify if the TV is within suggested proximity of the router</li><li><strong>Service Remotes</strong>: Ensure to get OEM service remotes to access the service menu (e.g., Samsung). The remotes can be acquired from the OEM directly or from retailers such as Amazon or eBay.</li><li><strong>USB Flash Drive:</strong>&nbsp;Needed to update firmware on TV brands such as Sony and Sharp</li><li>&nbsp;<strong>WiFi Hotspot:</strong>&nbsp;Typically can be found on newer smartphones, and can be used to verify the TV’s wifi functionality without having to troubleshoot any external router/WiFi issues.</li><li>Various sized screwdrivers, pliers, wire stripper, scissors, electrical tape</li></ul><ol><li>Will verify the model and S/N before starting work.</li><li>Take the necessary photos.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><u>Required repair photos (for both successful and unsuccessful repairs):</u></strong></p><ul><li>TV OSD menu shot when testing with a known working device (TV should be powered on and all 4 corners with standby light on bezel should be visible)</li><li>Product service sticker (clear photo of Model/SN information)</li><li>Photo of the internal component layout with the TV back cover off (All connections are correct and secure)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Unsuccessful scenario-based photos:</u></strong></p><ul><li>ADH/Infestation: Provide a detailed photo of the damage found</li><li>WiFi/Network Issue: Provide a clear photo of the Advance Network Menu Settings</li><li>Incorrect part: Provide a clear photo of the original part number and the incorrect replacement part number</li><li><u>If the panel does not show video we need a photo of the tv on the screen face down and power on. For most, tv's you can remove the cable between the power board and the main. </u></li></ul><p><strong><u>In the case of customer no-show (Customer denied repair):</u></strong></p><ul><li>Please contact our service desk for assistance with contacting the customer at 316-313-2627. Do not leave the customer’s residence during an appointment window without our authorization (If no response from us, continue with the following process)</li><li>Take a photo of the customer’s home with the address visible for documentation that the technician was onsite (Do not clear photo properties with time stamp information)</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Provide a tracking number for all returned parts. If any damage is found before beginning work please call, and document the damage DO NOT mark this work order as done until you have entered the tracking numbers for the devices you are sending back to our office. Work orders marked \"Done\" by technicians without tracking numbers entered into the work order will have the work order assigned back to them for proper completion and entering of tracking numbers.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T12:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":59.09090909},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":27.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T19:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-14T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-17T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Call Mom"},{"start":"2026-10-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"L1 support interview"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792523144295}
{"job":{"id":20200061,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CallRevu","title":"VoIP Phone Installation - Southpoint Honda Hudson","description":{"html":"<p>We have a customer who is migrating to a new phone system. The project is on-going and we have set a date for the phone's to be cut over. You will be expected to check in with the Project Manager via phone call when you arrive on-site and when you leave the site.</p>\n<p>You will assist in installing/racking a <strong>GWN 7003 Voice Router.</strong></p>\n<p>You will work on unboxing and laying out phones <strong>114 Yealink T34W phones on specified desks</strong>. You will also be ensuring the phones are plugged in and are functional.</p>\n<p>This project also has <strong>analog paging hook ups Algo 8301</strong></p>\n<p>There may also be a need for assistance in troubleshooting cabling, network connections, analog connections, or testing equipment.</p>\n<p>The number port is scheduled for early morning following your installation date. We expect all phones are plugged in and working prior to the port. <strong><u>You are expected to be on-site on the next day for about 1 hour.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"We have a customer who is migrating to a new phone system. The project is on-going and we have set a date for the phone's to be cut over. You will be expected to check in with the Project Manager via phone call when you arrive on-site and when you leave the site.\n\nYou will assist in installing/racking a **GWN 7003 Voice Router.**\n\nYou will work on unboxing and laying out phones **114 Yealink T34W phones on specified desks**. You will also be ensuring the phones are plugged in and are functional.\n\nThis project also has **analog paging hook ups Algo 8301**\n\nThere may also be a need for assistance in troubleshooting cabling, network connections, analog connections, or testing equipment.\n\nThe number port is scheduled for early morning following your installation date. We expect all phones are plugged in and working prior to the port. **You are expected to be on-site on the next day for about 1 hour.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T17:30","end":"2026-10-26T23:30"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":11.84401619860755},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":80,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1792523477116}
{"job":{"id":20211324,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"LEAD Technician | Firm Start | Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining Scope: Techs to bring cable needed for the Mood Media run.<br/>Run cable for Mood Media on ASM TV, install and confirm functionality<br/>Complete Fluix form<br/><br/><br/>Security Code:  TBD</p><p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD</p></BR><p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Seeking Lead<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;<strong>Over Multiple</strong>&nbsp;<strong>NIGHTs</strong>. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.</p><ul><li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">responsible</span>&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;</span>[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li><li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li><li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>***</del>  umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del> REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the Remote Support Team Bridge Line details -&nbsp;</strong>If you were not provided with one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Call &amp; Check-In with the <del>***</del> RTC Remote Technician Team via the provided Bridge Line</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation.</strong></p><ul><li>Perform a Walkthrough with MOD - refer to the install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li><li>Perform Inventory - refer to install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process</li><li>Work with Remote Bridge Line to determine if Site is ready to begin work for the night or if the night’s work needs aborted.</li><li>Continue to work with / provide updates to the Remote Bridge Line, closure to the end of the night you may be required to provide more frequent updates.</li><li>Some nights and/or mornings you will be working with the General Contractor Onsite and Store MOD to obtain/provide updates and/or complete specific task.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At Frontline Completion and Overall Store Remodel Completion]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li><li><strong>Check-Out with <del>***</del> Remote RTC Team via Bridge Line</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining Scope: Techs to bring cable needed for the Mood Media run.  \nRun cable for Mood Media on ASM TV, install and confirm functionality  \nComplete Fluix form  \n  \n  \nSecurity Code: TBD\n\n**Location Specific Notes / Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking Lead Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.\n\n- Lead Tech is responsible for reviewing and referring to ALL provided Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation \\[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC & STORE SPECIFIC Documentation\\] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.\n- Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** join and work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.\n- Lead Tech **MUST** review Nightly Scope of Work with the **\\*\\*\\* Remote RTS Group** at the beginning of each **NIGHT**. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.\n- **Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Store Completion Deliverables \\[Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel\\]:**\n- FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE \\[ FRONTLINE COMPLETION & FULL STORE COMPLETION\\]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the **\\*\\*\\* REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.** \\[If deliverable session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.\\]\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\*  REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* - Tool & Material List Document** **Link** (download to view full document): <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Estimated Duration: Multiple Days** estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n***Important Site Information / Requirements:***\n\n- You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n **Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.** Please **READ & REVIEW** all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **General Project Specific & STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link \\[VERY IMPORTANT\\]****:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\_Install Guides** **Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):** <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ>\n- **\\*\\*\\* Remodel - Tool & Material List** **Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8>\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1** **Link**: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial**\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- **Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site**\n- **Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n- **Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the Remote Support Team Bridge Line details -** If you were not provided with one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -** Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR & provide the **SECURITY CODE to gain access**\n- **Call & Check-In with the \\*\\*\\* RTC Remote Technician Team via the provided Bridge Line**\n\n**ONSITE: Work with \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team while onsite & refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation.**\n\n- Perform a Walkthrough with MOD - refer to the install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process\n- Perform Inventory - refer to install guide / other technical documentation for more details / full process\n- Work with Remote Bridge Line to determine if Site is ready to begin work for the night or if the night’s work needs aborted.\n- Continue to work with / provide updates to the Remote Bridge Line, closure to the end of the night you may be required to provide more frequent updates.\n- Some nights and/or mornings you will be working with the General Contractor Onsite and Store MOD to obtain/provide updates and/or complete specific task.\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- **Complete Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Store Completion Deliverables \\[Not Nightly but At Frontline Completion and Overall Store Remodel Completion\\]:**\n- FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE \\[ FRONTLINE COMPLETION & FULL STORE COMPLETION\\]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the **\\*\\*\\* REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.** \\[If deliverable session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.\\]\n- **Check-Out with \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team via Bridge Line**\n- **Check-Out** with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC\n- **Call** - Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line\n- All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T06:45","end":"2026-10-27T12:45"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":58.729932802243724},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":