{"job":{"id":20211625,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240 Printer Service - Paper Jam Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>CX3240<br />KZ4008935<br />Roller and consumable replacment. <br />Please do not arrive to sit before parts arive. <br />FIN: 239820<br /><br /></p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p>California Ink &amp; Toner Waste Compliance Requirements</p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>production print to verify the printer functionality.</strong></li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to confirm deliverables and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li>The parts return packages must be dropped off at the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup counter&nbsp;</strong>inside the Walgreens location<strong>.&nbsp;</strong>You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, and obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature.</strong></li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the <strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>, <strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>, <strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong> and <strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li><li>If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240 xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nCX3240  \nKZ4008935  \nRoller and consumable replacment.   \nPlease do not arrive to sit before parts arive.   \nFIN: 239820\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240 Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCalifornia Ink & Toner Waste Compliance Requirements\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n2. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n3. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n4. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **production print to verify the printer functionality.**\n5. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n6. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n7. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n8. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n9. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n10. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n11. The parts return packages must be dropped off at the **FedEx pickup counter** inside the Walgreens location**.** You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.\n12. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, and obtain their **signature.**\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n- If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T11:00","end":"2026-10-21T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":40.74804763136836},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792523521938}
{"job":{"id":20211359,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Assist Tech | Overnight Store Remodeling - Network/Cabling/POS (Full 8+ Hours Onsite)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining Scope: Techs to bring cable needed for the Mood Media run.<br/>Run cable for Mood Media on ASM TV, install and confirm functionality<br/>Complete Fluix form</p><p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD</p></BR><p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Seeking an Assist</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Over Multiple</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">NIGHTs</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Check-<em>I</em>n with Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with / take direction from the the Essintial LEAD TECHNICIAN while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining Scope: Techs to bring cable needed for the Mood Media run.  \nRun cable for Mood Media on ASM TV, install and confirm functionality  \nComplete Fluix form\n\n**Location Specific Notes / Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining Scope: Install Mood Media in ASM office, connect Mood Media to the TV, and validate functionality with MOD. Security Code: TBD\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking an Assist Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* - Tool & Material List Document** **Link** (download to view full document): <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Estimated Duration: Multiple Days** estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n***Important Site Information / Requirements:***\n\n- You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n **Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.** Please **READ & REVIEW** all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **General Project Specific & STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link \\[VERY IMPORTANT\\]****:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\