{"job":{"id":20211722,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Purely IT LLC","title":"Diagnose QNAP and camera offline (Dining 1)","description":{"html":"<p>Diagnose QNAP and camera offline (Dining 1)</p><p><br></p><p>MANDATORY: PURELY CHECK-IN, CHAT AND DELIVERABLES</p><p>As soon as you arrive, open the Purely technician link in the CONFIDENTIAL instructions and enter its access code. Check in through Purely chat and wait for acknowledgment before touching equipment.</p><p>Complete the work through this portal: instructions, required photos, job chat and release code. Working only with a third-party vendor does not satisfy these deliverables. Purely must coordinate vendor contact.</p><p>Payment approval requires the agreed work-order deliverables and Purely review. Missing check-in, portal use or evidence will hold approval for correction or formal dispute review under the agreed Field Nation terms. Do not accept unless you can follow this process.</p><p><br></p><p>AUTHORIZED SCOPE</p><p>Identify the cause of the dining area camera and QNAP NVR offline issue and attempt to return all cameras and equipment online.</p><p><br></p><p>PURELY SUPPORT</p><p>Use the chat in your technician job link to check in before changes. Purely coordinates vendor support.</p><p>Coverage: Purely support team, 10 a.m.–5 p.m. Eastern. Work outside coverage requires advance support arrangements.</p><p>Service: 2026-10-22 / 10am-2pm (Eastern time (EDT))</p><p>Site details, access instructions and your private job link are provided after assignment.</p><p><br></p><p>BEFORE YOU START</p><p>Introduce yourself as working on behalf of [site details shared after assignment]. Purely coordinates your support and release.</p><p><br></p><p>CONFIRM BEFORE TRAVELLING</p><p>Confirm you have a ladder suitable for the needed camera or recorder height—site does NOT provide ladders.</p><p>Bring laptop with Ethernet port/adapters and required camera/network test equipment.</p><p>Verify safe access to all networking and camera locations involved.</p><p>If rack or switch is inaccessible or height is uncertain, confirm with Purely before accepting.</p><p>Wear appropriate PPE for ceiling/vault access if required by site policy.</p><p><br></p><p>TECHNICIAN STEPS</p><p>1. Meet the site contact</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirm you are at the correct site and tell Purely who is your site contact.</p><p>2. Diagnose offline QNAP and dining area camera</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;With Purely, identify and label the affected QNAP recorder, problem camera (Dining 1), and all relevant network switches/encoders.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Record model numbers and the names/channels of affected and online cameras.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Photograph and record all related equipment connections and visible port labels before touching any cabling.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Test the power and cabling to the offline QNAP and camera using tools suitable for IP or analog as found.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Share all observed results and cable readings with Purely. Do not move cables, reset, or alter site equipment without Purely approval.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Required photos: 2. Live monitor or camera-status view before work, showing affected channels.; Recorder/switch/encoder connections and readable port labels relevant to the fault.; QNAP NIC 1 cable connection with NIC label visible.; Cisco Switch 1 or 2 connection showing the switch identity and port 37, 38, 39 or 40.</p><p>3. Purely verifies the system — Purely support owns this verification; stay available to assist.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;With Purely, identify the complete expected camera and equipment inventory. Check every camera, the recorder and relevant network equipment, including devices outside the replaced component. Record expected counts, online counts, device identities and tested results.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;ALL cameras and equipment must be online before departure. Have Purely verify live feeds and applicable recording/playback. A link light or one working camera is not sufficient.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;For each device still offline, identify it, state the exact confirmed cause (or cause not confirmed), tests and observations, and the specific parts/materials, quantities and next diagnostic work needed. Do not guess a part or cause.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Report every unresolved device in Purely chat. Only Purely can release an incomplete visit with a documented follow-up plan; never mark the system fully restored when equipment remains offline.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Required photos: 2. Final full camera/device status list showing expected and online counts.; Final recorder/system verification or evidence of each remaining offline device.; Final live monitor or camera-status view and camera counts.; Final connections and the repair or remaining fault.</p><p>4. Get your release code and finish</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Ask Purely support to review the evidence and issue the release code for this visit before leaving.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Purely records your release here after reviewing the work. Copy the release code into Field Nation and submit the required deliverables there. A release can document an incomplete visit.</p><p><br></p><p>TOOLS</p><p>Bring your own serviceable ladder suitable for safe access to the cameras. Sites do not provide ladders. Confirm mounting height and access before accepting; ask Purely if a lift or special access equipment is needed. Never improvise unsafe access.</p><p>Technician-supplied ladder suitable for camera/recorder height</p><p>Laptop with Ethernet connectivity and adapters</p><p>Network cable tester for IP or analog as found</p><p>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</p><p>Flashlight and label maker or tape for marking cables</p><p>PPE as required</p><p>Laptop with Ethernet connectivity and required adapters</p><p>Network cable tester for IP cabling; analog test equipment if analog troubleshooting is in scope</p><p><br></p><p>EXCLUSIONS</p><p>Do not install or replace any QNAP, camera, recorder, switch, or other device unless explicitly approved by Purely during this visit.</p><p>Do not move, reconnect, or disconnect network cables or equipment beyond what is specified or pre-approved by Purely.</p><p>No system-wide resets or firmware changes unless instructed by Purely.</p><p><br></p><p>PARTS AND RESPONSIBILITY</p><p>No materials listed. Supply requirements must be reviewed before assignment.</p><p><br></p><p>PROVIDER PAY</p><p>$65.00 hourly; 2 included hours.</p><p><br></p><p>RELEASE AND DELIVERABLES</p><p>Get the visit release code from Purely support. Upload the required evidence and enter the release code in Field Nation.</p><p>Report time and scope changes before exceeding the approved terms. No unapproved deductions or penalties are implied.</p>","markdown":"Diagnose QNAP and camera offline (Dining 1)\n\nMANDATORY: PURELY CHECK-IN, CHAT AND DELIVERABLES\n\nAs soon as you arrive, open the Purely technician link in the CONFIDENTIAL instructions and enter its access code. Check in through Purely chat and wait for acknowledgment before touching equipment.\n\nComplete the work through this portal: instructions, required photos, job chat and release code. Working only with a third-party vendor does not satisfy these deliverables. Purely must coordinate vendor contact.\n\nPayment approval requires the agreed work-order deliverables and Purely review. Missing check-in, portal use or evidence will hold approval for correction or formal dispute review under the agreed Field Nation terms. Do not accept unless you can follow this process.\n\nAUTHORIZED SCOPE\n\nIdentify the cause of the dining area camera and QNAP NVR offline issue and attempt to return all cameras and equipment online.\n\nPURELY SUPPORT\n\nUse the chat in your technician job link to check in before changes. Purely coordinates vendor support.\n\nCoverage: Purely support team, 10 a.m.–5 p.m. Eastern. Work outside coverage requires advance support arrangements.\n\nService: 2026-10-22 / 10am-2pm (Eastern time (EDT))\n\nSite details, access instructions and your private job link are provided after assignment.\n\nBEFORE YOU START\n\nIntroduce yourself as working on behalf of \\[site details shared after assignment\\]. Purely coordinates your support and release.\n\nCONFIRM BEFORE TRAVELLING\n\nConfirm you have a ladder suitable for the needed camera or recorder height—site does NOT provide ladders.\n\nBring laptop with Ethernet port/adapters and required camera/network test equipment.\n\nVerify safe access to all networking and camera locations involved.\n\nIf rack or switch is inaccessible or height is uncertain, confirm with Purely before accepting.\n\nWear appropriate PPE for ceiling/vault access if required by site policy.\n\nTECHNICIAN STEPS\n\n1\\. Meet the site contact\n\n Confirm you are at the correct site and tell Purely who is your site contact.\n\n2\\. Diagnose offline QNAP and dining area camera\n\n With Purely, identify and label the affected QNAP recorder, problem camera (Dining 1), and all relevant network switches/encoders.\n\n Record model numbers and the names/channels of affected and online cameras.\n\n Photograph and record all related equipment connections and visible port labels before touching any cabling.\n\n Test the power and cabling to the offline QNAP and camera using tools suitable for IP or analog as found.\n\n Share all observed results and cable readings with Purely. Do not move cables, reset, or alter site equipment without Purely approval.\n\n Required photos: 2. Live monitor or camera-status view before work, showing affected channels.; Recorder/switch/encoder connections and readable port labels relevant to the fault.; QNAP NIC 1 cable connection with NIC label visible.; Cisco Switch 1 or 2 connection showing the switch identity and port 37, 38, 39 or 40.\n\n3\\. Purely verifies the system — Purely support owns this verification; stay available to assist.\n\n With Purely, identify the complete expected camera and equipment inventory. Check every camera, the recorder and relevant network equipment, including devices outside the replaced component. Record expected counts, online counts, device identities and tested results.\n\n ALL cameras and equipment must be online before departure. Have Purely verify live feeds and applicable recording/playback. A link light or one working camera is not sufficient.\n\n For each device still offline, identify it, state the exact confirmed cause (or cause not confirmed), tests and observations, and the specific parts/materials, quantities and next diagnostic work needed. Do not guess a part or cause.\n\n Report every unresolved device in Purely chat. Only Purely can release an incomplete visit with a documented follow-up plan; never mark the system fully restored when equipment remains offline.\n\n Required photos: 2. Final full camera/device status list showing expected and online counts.; Final recorder/system verification or evidence of each remaining offline device.; Final live monitor or camera-status view and camera counts.; Final connections and the repair or remaining fault.\n\n4\\. Get your release code and finish\n\n Ask Purely support to review the evidence and issue the release code for this visit before leaving.\n\n Purely records your release here after reviewing the work. Copy the release code into Field Nation and submit the required deliverables there. A release can document an incomplete visit.\n\nTOOLS\n\nBring your own serviceable ladder suitable for safe access to the cameras. Sites do not provide ladders. Confirm mounting height and access before accepting; ask Purely if a lift or special access equipment is needed. Never improvise unsafe access.\n\nTechnician-supplied ladder suitable for camera/recorder height\n\nLaptop with Ethernet connectivity and adapters\n\nNetwork cable tester for IP or analog as found\n\nBasic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n\nFlashlight and label maker or tape for marking cables\n\nPPE as required\n\nLaptop with Ethernet connectivity and required adapters\n\nNetwork cable tester for IP cabling; analog test equipment if analog troubleshooting is in scope\n\nEXCLUSIONS\n\nDo not install or replace any QNAP, camera, recorder, switch, or other device unless explicitly approved by Purely during this visit.\n\nDo not move, reconnect, or disconnect network cables or equipment beyond what is specified or pre-approved by Purely.\n\nNo system-wide resets or firmware changes unless instructed by Purely.\n\nPARTS AND RESPONSIBILITY\n\nNo materials listed. Supply requirements must be reviewed before assignment.\n\nPROVIDER PAY\n\n$65.00 hourly; 2 included hours.\n\nRELEASE AND DELIVERABLES\n\nGet the visit release code from Purely support. Upload the required evidence and enter the release code in Field Nation.\n\nReport time and scope changes before exceeding the approved terms. No unapproved deductions or penalties are implied.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T10:00","end":"2026-10-22T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-22T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":60.63181257247005},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792524135090}
{"job":{"id":20211876,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - 2 Switches Down","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Required 19ft. lift</p><p>Need to allign the tech any day from 6am-2pm EST.</p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch details:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Impacted Device: Cisco AIR-AP2802E-B-K9.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Location: DC 09 Butner</p><p><br></p><p>3. Problem Statement: dcd0009ap0918 is down.</p><p><br></p><p>4. What troubleshooting has been completed: dcd0009ap0918 is down. Bounced the switchport but still AP is down. Need to check the physical connectivity.</p><p><br></p><p>5. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:</p><p>• Before visiting the location, please make sure that the laptop should be able to take console.</p><p>• Compatible console cable USB-RJ45, Short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required. Lift is required.</p><p><br></p><p>6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:</p><p>• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.</p><p>• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.</p><p>• Need to check the physical connectivity -AP to switch.</p><p>• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.</p><p>•Need to test the cable run for the AP.</p><p>• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.</p><p>• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Required 19ft. lift\n\nNeed to allign the tech any day from 6am-2pm EST.\n\nDispatch details:\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: Cisco AIR-AP2802E-B-K9.\n\n2\\. Location: DC 09 Butner\n\n3\\. Problem Statement: dcd0009ap0918 is down.\n\n4\\. What troubleshooting has been completed: dcd0009ap0918 is down. Bounced the switchport but still AP is down. Need to check the physical connectivity.\n\n5\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:\n\n• Before visiting the location, please make sure that the laptop should be able to take console.\n\n• Compatible console cable USB-RJ45, Short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required. Lift is required.\n\n6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:\n\n• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.\n\n• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.\n\n• Need to check the physical connectivity -AP to switch.\n\n• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.\n\n•Need to test the cable run for the AP.\n\n• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.\n\n• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T07:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":19.099452603365727},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792524453717}
{"job":{"id":20211919,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Nationwide Fixture Installations","title":"Lead and Helper Needed to Complete Countertop Retrofit (Corian Cash Wrap) - 8 Hours MAX - Night Installation","description":{"html":"<p>Lead and Helper Needed to Drill Holes for the specified parts and then install the parts.</p><p>Installers will work DIRECTLY with the CVE Rep for locations on drilling, to ensure everything works and meshes together properly.</p><p>Details:</p><ul><li><strong>Once holes are drilled, we are installing gift card shrouds and accessory panels.</strong></li><li>On the Merchandising Panel install, much of these are cabinets RTC did not produce. NFI did site surveys for these, but internal attachment provisions may slightly differ. Installers must have excess hardware to attach to wood + steel. Please make sure they bring blocking to add to inside the cabinet if needed (see in atatchments) specifically for 2-19166</li><li>All new 1” diameter holes need to be drilled through the countertop and through the MDF substrate because the POS cables/wires will need to feed through.</li><li>The 3 small holes for the credit card reader and the 4 small holes for the CFD monitor should only be drilled through the countertop, but not through the MDF substrate.&nbsp;That’s because the smaller holes are used to secure the credit card reader and CFD monitor to the countertop with drywall screws.</li><li>There is an orientation to the card reader with stops on both ends to prevent spinning and winding up the cable. Pay attention to direction, but CVE tech will know exactly what this means, and they should be involved.</li><li>Prior to drilling the holes for the credit card reader and the CFD monitor, it’s important for the installer to make sure both pieces of equipment do not overhang the front edge of the counter.&nbsp;They can talk with the Cache Valley technician to verify because he should have the new POS equipment.</li></ul><p>Parts/Quantities:</p><ul><li><strong>Register Count:</strong> 5</li><li><strong>Gift Card Shroud Count:</strong> 5</li><li><strong>Classic Accessory Panel Count:</strong> 5</li></ul><p>SOW:</p><ul><li>Review instructions ahead of time and contact Sammy with any questions regarding the SOW.</li><li>Purchase 1 in. ACC Snap-In Bushing from Home Depot before the job begins.</li><li><strong>Work with the CVE rep on-site for EXACT location of where to drill the holes</strong></li><li>Take before pictures of the area.</li><li>Drill new holes into the Corian top</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Using a 1/8” Bit, create a pilot hole only through the countertop (not the wood substrate)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Using the specified sized bits, create new feed-through holes through the countertop and the substrate for feeding wiring</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any&nbsp;<strong><u>metal</u></strong>&nbsp;tops or substrate cut will require a rubber grommet to ensure not cutting the cable (grommet will need to be procured at Home Depot)&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Potentially add access holes in the inside of the cabinet for wiring purposes depending on where the new holes align and the access points</li><li>Install the Gift Card Shrouds (5) and the Classic Accessory Panels (5)</li><li>Secure each cash drawer (1 per register) with 2 screws per drawer</li><li>Clean and vacuum the countertop and area.</li><li>Take new pictures of the area with new holes and bushings.</li><li>Complete NFI sign-off.</li></ul><p><strong><u>What to Bring</u></strong><u>:</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Basic Hand Tools</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drill w/extra batteries</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drill bits</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Bit Extension</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Exact Hole Saw to Purchase: [2] Diablo 1 in Bi-Metal Hole with 2-3/8 in. Cutting Depth&nbsp;</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Right-angled bit for the cash wraps with the shroud</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[20] ¼”-20 x 2” long machine screw for accessory panels</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[35] round head 1 #8 sheet metal screws to secure the shroud.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[10] 1 1/4\" sheetrock to secure the cash boxes (longer ones will poke through the shelf below).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[30] 1 1/4\" sheet rock screws to secure the card reader.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[10] 10-32 X 1 1/4\" Screws for Cash Drawers&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">[5] 1” Rubber Grommets&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Link to Grommets: https://www.homedepot.com/p/Halex-1-in-ACC-Snap-In-Bushing-27253/202077088?MERCH=REC-_-searchViewed-_-1%20inch%20rubber%20grommet-_-5-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cleaning cloths</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Shop Vac</li></ul><p><strong><u>What to Wear:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Jeans or nice pants (no rips, holes or stains)</li><li>Belt, if needed</li><li>Work boots or tennis shoes</li><li>Solid colored shirt</li></ul><p>You must arrive on time.</p><p>You must bring all noted items under special instructions.</p><p>You must be polite and professional at all times.</p><p>Food is not allowed in the store.</p><p>You may bring a water bottle.</p><p>The provider accepting the work must be the provider self-performing the work onsite. You must be polite and professional at all times, and you all must be knowledgeable and experienced in following instructions and assembling/installing fixtures and displays.</p>","markdown":"Lead and Helper Needed to Drill Holes for the specified parts and then install the parts.\n\nInstallers will work DIRECTLY with the CVE Rep for locations on drilling, to ensure everything works and meshes together properly.\n\nDetails:\n\n- **Once holes are drilled, we are installing gift card shrouds and accessory panels.**\n- On the Merchandising Panel install, much of these are cabinets RTC did not produce. NFI did site surveys for these, but internal attachment provisions may slightly differ. Installers must have excess hardware to attach to wood + steel. Please make sure they bring blocking to add to inside the cabinet if needed (see in atatchments) specifically for 2-19166\n- All new 1” diameter holes need to be drilled through the countertop and through the MDF substrate because the POS cables/wires will need to feed through.\n- The 3 small holes for the credit card reader and the 4 small holes for the CFD monitor should only be drilled through the countertop, but not through the MDF substrate. That’s because the smaller holes are used to secure the credit card reader and CFD monitor to the countertop with drywall screws.\n- There is an orientation to the card reader with stops on both ends to prevent spinning and winding up the cable. Pay attention to direction, but CVE tech will know exactly what this means, and they should be involved.\n- Prior to drilling the holes for the credit card reader and the CFD monitor, it’s important for the installer to make sure both pieces of equipment do not overhang the front edge of the counter. They can talk with the Cache Valley technician to verify because he should have the new POS equipment.\n\nParts/Quantities:\n\n- **Register Count:** 5\n- **Gift Card Shroud Count:** 5\n- **Classic Accessory Panel Count:** 5\n\nSOW:\n\n- Review instructions ahead of time and contact Sammy with any questions regarding the SOW.\n- Purchase 1 in. ACC Snap-In Bushing from Home Depot before the job begins.\n- **Work with the CVE rep on-site for EXACT location of where to drill the holes**\n- Take before pictures of the area.\n- Drill new holes into the Corian top\n- Using a 1/8” Bit, create a pilot hole only through the countertop (not the wood substrate)\n- Using the specified sized bits, create new feed-through holes through the countertop and the substrate for feeding wiring\n- Any **metal** tops or substrate cut will require a rubber grommet to ensure not cutting the cable (grommet will need to be procured at Home Depot)\n- Potentially add access holes in the inside of the cabinet for wiring purposes depending on where the new holes align and the access points\n- Install the Gift Card Shrouds (5) and the Classic Accessory Panels (5)\n- Secure each cash drawer (1 per register) with 2 screws per drawer\n- Clean and vacuum the countertop and area.\n- Take new pictures of the area with new holes and bushings.\n- Complete NFI sign-off.\n\n**What to Bring**:\n\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Drill w/extra batteries\n- Drill bits\n- Bit Extension\n- **Exact Hole Saw to Purchase: \\[2\\] Diablo 1 in Bi-Metal Hole with 2-3/8 in. Cutting Depth**\n- Right-angled bit for the cash wraps with the shroud\n- \\[20\\] ¼”-20 x 2” long machine screw for accessory panels\n- \\[35\\] round head 1 #8 sheet metal screws to secure the shroud.\n- \\[10\\] 1 1/4\" sheetrock to secure the cash boxes (longer ones will poke through the shelf below).\n- \\[30\\] 1 1/4\" sheet rock screws to secure the card reader.\n- \\[10\\] 10-32 X 1 1/4\" Screws for Cash Drawers\n- \\[5\\] 1” Rubber Grommets\n- Link to Grommets: https://www.homedepot.com/p/Halex-1-in-ACC-Snap-In-Bushing-27253/202077088?MERCH=REC-_-searchViewed-_-1%20inch%20rubber%20grommet-_-5-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a-_-n/a\n- Cleaning cloths\n- Shop Vac\n\n**What to Wear:**\n\n- Jeans or nice pants (no rips, holes or stains)\n- Belt, if needed\n- Work boots or tennis shoes\n- Solid colored shirt\n\nYou must arrive on time.\n\nYou must bring all noted items under special instructions.\n\nYou must be polite and professional at all times.\n\nFood is not allowed in the store.\n\nYou may bring a water bottle.\n\nThe provider accepting the work must be the provider self-performing the work onsite. You must be polite and professional at all times, and you all must be knowledgeable and experienced in following instructions and assembling/installing fixtures and displays.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T14:45","end":"2026-11-03T22:45"},"payRange":{"min":850,"max":850},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":35.22924181846902},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"displays\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792524691249}
{"job":{"id":20210136,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | KIOSK SSD Card Swaps","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>N/A</p></BR><p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Important</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician is installing SSD Card in Drivers Shower Kiosk. PC/POS hardware, SSD/HD swap, Windows OS basics, follow written procedures, basic</p><p>troubleshooting.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Task:</strong>&nbsp;Swap/replace SSD(s) and apply new asset tag(s) on Driver/Shower kiosks (1–3 devices/site). Follow the SSD Swap Guide for the step-by-step procedure.</li><li><strong>Represent yourself as:</strong>&nbsp;Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America.</li><li><strong>Possible kiosk locations (vary by site):</strong>&nbsp;Front Counter, Truck Side, Truck Service Building. (Store General Manager will know what kiosk are in scope and where the kiosk are located)</li><li><strong>Kiosk naming (location):</strong>&nbsp;01=Front Counter, 02=Truck Side, 03=Truck Service Building.</li><li><strong>Pre-test app:</strong>&nbsp;Download TA TruckSmart&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;arriving (used for post-swap testing; see guide).</li><li><strong>Parts at site:</strong>&nbsp;New SSD(s) + asset tag(s) shipped to Store GM (white box with colored label). If missing, contact TSC Support.</li><li><strong>Handle panels carefully:</strong>&nbsp;tabs are fragile.</li><li><strong>Asset tag rule:</strong>&nbsp;Remove old tags from screen + base, then place the new tag&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">ON THE BASE ONLY (NOT THE SCREEN).</strong></li><li><strong>Return old SSD(s):</strong>&nbsp;Put old SSD(s) in the bag from the new SSD(s), re-box, apply return label, and hand to the Store GM. (Capture a photo of the contents inside the box before closing)</li><li><strong>Deliverable (required before leaving):</strong>&nbsp;Submit deliverable + required photos and have it reviewed/approved by Essintial Project Tech Support&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;you depart.</li><li><strong>Deliverable Photo Requirements!!!</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Required photos:</strong>&nbsp;(1) New asset tag installed on base. (2) Kiosk powered on showing both payment options available (not greyed out). (3) SSD Card packed up inside the return box</li><li>Technicians are&nbsp;<strong>REQUIRED</strong>&nbsp;to complete an Essintial Online Deliverable + have the deliverable reviewed/approved&nbsp;<strong>PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to leaving the site. Contact&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support Team at&nbsp;717-516-3009.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Access Issues / Technical Issues Encountered Onsite</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Escalate to TSC Support</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Standard/Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Anti-Static Wrist Strap (Tether grounded, not air gapped),</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Important Technician Information &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">These are LIVE environments, and technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;Be Respectful</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">You Must be able to lift/carry 50 lbs and work standing, kneeling, and bending for extended periods.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Work will be completed during 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM Eastern</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;</strong>1-2 Hours, expect 15-30 minutes per device</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Download the SSD Swap Guide and bring it printed or on a laptop/tablet.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Kiosk Project_SSD Swap Guide</strong>&nbsp;Link:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004uqG9/4VeY_0iiqVkMLahcNBWCpOe6Ao4MEMRzUleHAp98_YY</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(247, 10, 10);\"><em><u>Important Note:&nbsp;</u></em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li>Confirm scheduled start time and respond to pre-calls (24 hr and 2 hr).</li><li>&nbsp;Download TA TruckSmart app (used for post-swap testing; see guide).</li><li>&nbsp;Bring required tools and a government-issued ID.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager, Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America.</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Refer to the Installation Guide provided!!!</p><ul><li><strong>Locate the shipped equipment and asset tags.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Work with Store General Manager for the Kiosk in Scope and the Location of each Kiosk</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Technicians need to be&nbsp;</strong><strong>VERY</strong>&nbsp;careful when removing panels from the kiosk, the panels have delicate plastic and thin metal tabs that are easily broken/bent if mishandled during removal/installation.</li><li>Technicians&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;remove old asset tag stickers from both the screen and side of the kiosk base and then install a new asset tag on the Kiosk Base&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">(DO NOT INSTALL TAG ON THE SCREEN, ONLY THE BASE).</strong></li><li><strong>Required photos:</strong>&nbsp;(1) New asset tag installed on base. (2) Kiosk powered on showing both payment options available (not greyed out).&nbsp;(3) SSD Card packed up inside the return box</li><li><strong>Old SSD Cards:&nbsp;</strong>Technician MUST safely place the old SSD Card(s) inside the same bag the new one(s) arrived in, place the ssd card(s) in the box and apply the provided return label to the package. Technician&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;leave/hand the package over to the Store General Manager.&nbsp;<strong>(Capture a photo of the contents inside the box before closing)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete and Submit Online Deliverable</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to upload requested photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.</li><li><strong>Call and Check Out with Essintial Technical Support @&nbsp;717-516-3009&nbsp;to perform your final check out - You MUST review your deliverables BEFORE you LEAVE SITE and have them approved by Project Tech Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code</li><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Contacts / Escalation:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Essintial (check-in/out help): 855-612-2183</li><li>Essintial Project Tech Support (deliverable approval): 717-516-3009</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Access/technical issues onsite: TSC Support <del>******* ******** ************</del></span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Other scope/WO issues: Essintial Project Team 855-612-2183 (opt 2)</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nN/A\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**Important**: Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite\n\n**Required Skills:** Technician is installing SSD Card in Drivers Shower Kiosk. PC/POS hardware, SSD/HD swap, Windows OS basics, follow written procedures, basic\n\ntroubleshooting.\n\n**Scope of Work Overview:**\n\n- **Task:** Swap/replace SSD(s) and apply new asset tag(s) on Driver/Shower kiosks (1–3 devices/site). Follow the SSD Swap Guide for the step-by-step procedure.\n- **Represent yourself as:** Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America.\n- **Possible kiosk locations (vary by site):** Front Counter, Truck Side, Truck Service Building. (Store General Manager will know what kiosk are in scope and where the kiosk are located)\n- **Kiosk naming (location):** 01=Front Counter, 02=Truck Side, 03=Truck Service Building.\n- **Pre-test app:** Download TA TruckSmart **before** arriving (used for post-swap testing; see guide).\n- **Parts at site:** New SSD(s) + asset tag(s) shipped to Store GM (white box with colored label). If missing, contact TSC Support.\n- **Handle panels carefully:** tabs are fragile.\n- **Asset tag rule:** Remove old tags from screen + base, then place the new tag **ON THE BASE ONLY (NOT THE SCREEN).**\n- **Return old SSD(s):** Put old SSD(s) in the bag from the new SSD(s), re-box, apply return label, and hand to the Store GM. (Capture a photo of the contents inside the box before closing)\n- **Deliverable (required before leaving):** Submit deliverable + required photos and have it reviewed/approved by Essintial Project Tech Support **before** you depart.\n- **Deliverable Photo Requirements!!!**\n- **Required photos:** (1) New asset tag installed on base. (2) Kiosk powered on showing both payment options available (not greyed out). (3) SSD Card packed up inside the return box\n- Technicians are **REQUIRED** to complete an Essintial Online Deliverable + have the deliverable reviewed/approved **PRIOR** to leaving the site. Contact **Essintial Project Technical Support Team at 717-516-3009.**\n- **Access Issues / Technical Issues Encountered Onsite** - **Escalate to TSC Support**\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- Standard/Basic Hand Tools\n- Screwdrivers\n- Anti-Static Wrist Strap (Tether grounded, not air gapped),\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n\n**Important Technician Information & Requirements:**\n\n- **Dress Code: Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n- **These are LIVE environments, and technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **You Must be able to lift/carry 50 lbs and work standing, kneeling, and bending for extended periods.**\n- **You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183**\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Work will be completed during 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM Eastern\n- **Estimated Duration:** 1-2 Hours, expect 15-30 minutes per device\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download the SSD Swap Guide and bring it printed or on a laptop/tablet.**\n- **Kiosk Project\\_SSD Swap Guide** Link: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004uqG9/4VeY_0iiqVkMLahcNBWCpOe6Ao4MEMRzUleHAp98_YY\n- ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- Confirm scheduled start time and respond to pre-calls (24 hr and 2 hr).\n- Download TA TruckSmart app (used for post-swap testing; see guide).\n- Bring required tools and a government-issued ID.\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER**–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager, Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers of America.**\n\n**ONSITE:** Refer to the Installation Guide provided!!!\n\n- **Locate the shipped equipment and asset tags.**\n- **Work with Store General Manager for the Kiosk in Scope and the Location of each Kiosk**\n- **Technicians need to be** **VERY** careful when removing panels from the kiosk, the panels have delicate plastic and thin metal tabs that are easily broken/bent if mishandled during removal/installation.\n- Technicians **MUST** remove old asset tag stickers from both the screen and side of the kiosk base and then install a new asset tag on the Kiosk Base **(DO NOT INSTALL TAG ON THE SCREEN, ONLY THE BASE).**\n- **Required photos:** (1) New asset tag installed on base. (2) Kiosk powered on showing both payment options available (not greyed out). (3) SSD Card packed up inside the return box\n- **Old SSD Cards:** Technician MUST safely place the old SSD Card(s) inside the same bag the new one(s) arrived in, place the ssd card(s) in the box and apply the provided return label to the package. Technician **MUST** leave/hand the package over to the Store General Manager. **(Capture a photo of the contents inside the box before closing)**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- **Complete and Submit Online Deliverable** (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):\n- Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details\n- Tech will be asked to upload requested photos\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.\n- **Call and Check Out with Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009 to perform your final check out - You MUST review your deliverables BEFORE you LEAVE SITE and have them approved by Project Tech Support.**\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.\n\n**Contacts / Escalation:**\n\n- Essintial (check-in/out help): 855-612-2183\n- Essintial Project Tech Support (deliverable approval): 717-516-3009\n- Access/technical issues onsite: TSC Support \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Other scope/WO issues: Essintial Project Team 855-612-2183 (opt 2)**\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":135},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":95},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":47.5824388325848},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $135 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"202