{"job":{"id":20212291,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Assist Tech | Store Remodeling - Network/Cabling/POS (Full 8+ Hours Onsite)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>Remaining scope<br/>1. Install and validate:<br/>#36 â€“ Compactor (.083)<br/>#38 â€“ Loading Dock (.086)<br/>#47 â€“ IP Speaker (.166)<br/>#18 â€“ Cash Office Hallway (.042)<br/><br/>2. Project Closeout <br/>Confirm beam clamps obtained and install remaining devices requiring them <br/>Install remaining camera covers <br/>Correct cable management and add J-hooks where needed <br/>Remove old cameras after cutover <br/>Final CCTV validation with management <br/>Site cleanup <br/>Palletize old equipment for removal <br/>Move lift outside of site for pickup <br/>Manager walkthrough <br/>Customer signoff <br/><br/>Security Code: 862384</p><p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>SOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present</p></BR><p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Seeking an Assist</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Over Multiple</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">NIGHTs</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Check-<em>I</em>n with Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with / take direction from the the Essintial LEAD TECHNICIAN while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nRemaining scope  \n1\\. Install and validate:  \n\\#36 â€“ Compactor (.083)  \n\\#38 â€“ Loading Dock (.086)  \n\\#47 â€“ IP Speaker (.166)  \n\\#18 â€“ Cash Office Hallway (.042)  \n  \n2\\. Project Closeout   \nConfirm beam clamps obtained and install remaining devices requiring them   \nInstall remaining camera covers   \nCorrect cable management and add J-hooks where needed   \nRemove old cameras after cutover   \nFinal CCTV validation with management   \nSite cleanup   \nPalletize old equipment for removal   \nMove lift outside of site for pickup   \nManager walkthrough   \nCustomer signoff   \n  \nSecurity Code: 862384\n\n**Location Specific Notes / Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nSOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking an Assist Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*