{"job":{"id":20212349,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Required (Filling the Service Visit Report is Mandatory)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>FILLING THE SITE VISIT REPORT IS MANDATORY BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE AND MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE CLOSING THE WO</em></strong></p><p><strong>**The technician should NOT suggest purchasing any new equipment or materials while onsite, and should not discuss any issues that need to be fixed with the Store Manager. The technician must strictly follow the instructions provided during the Teams meeting.**</strong></p><p><br></p><p>The technician must join the meeting as soon as they arrive onsite. (The meeting details will be shared before arrival.) If there is any issue joining the meeting, or if no one is present in the meeting, please call the Wipro phone number provided in the confidential information. Select option 1 and provide the INC number or the location (as mentioned in the Work Order description). or call your WO manager from ovation.</p><p>POC details are available in the confidential information.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> <strong>Phone Line Issue</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>(Any additional tools or cable purchased onsite should be approved by the Field nation work order manager. If you are getting no response please send an email on sd@ovationwps.com)</em></strong></p><p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop with Windows operating system and Ethernet port(s)</li><li>Console cables (RJ45 to USB, USB to Serial converter)</li><li>Basic tool kit</li><li>USB drive (32GB)</li><li>Internet data (hotspot)</li><li>PuTTY application</li><li>MS Teams (installed on both phone and laptop)</li><li>Phone with a reliable hotspot</li><li>Patch cables (copper or fiber)</li></ul>","markdown":"***FILLING THE SITE VISIT REPORT IS MANDATORY BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE AND MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE CLOSING THE WO***\n\n**\\*\\*The technician should NOT suggest purchasing any new equipment or materials while onsite, and should not discuss any issues that need to be fixed with the Store Manager. The technician must strictly follow the instructions provided during the Teams meeting.\\*\\***\n\nThe technician must join the meeting as soon as they arrive onsite. (The meeting details will be shared before arrival.) If there is any issue joining the meeting, or if no one is present in the meeting, please call the Wipro phone number provided in the confidential information. Select option 1 and provide the INC number or the location (as mentioned in the Work Order description). or call your WO manager from ovation.\n\nPOC details are available in the confidential information.\n\n**Scope of Work:** **Phone Line Issue**\n\n***(Any additional tools or cable purchased onsite should be approved by the Field nation work order manager. If you are getting no response please send an email on sd@ovationwps.com)***\n\n**Required Tools & Equipment:**\n\n- Laptop with Windows operating system and Ethernet port(s)\n- Console cables (RJ45 to USB, USB to Serial converter)\n- Basic tool kit\n- USB drive (32GB)\n- Internet data (hotspot)\n- PuTTY application\n- MS Teams (installed on both phone and laptop)\n- Phone with a reliable hotspot\n- Patch cables (copper or fiber)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-20T17:00","end":"2026-10-20T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45.43685721851554},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Oct 22, 1:30 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $300 · listed maximum: $180\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792527658870}
{"job":{"id":20212460,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Food Lion 2591 - Readjust APs and Install L Bracket in Meat Cooler - (Lift Cert Required)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope Notes</u></strong></p><p><strong>Tech Must Be Lift Certified.</strong></p><p><strong>All Deliverables must be uploaded to FN prior to leaving site, unless returning materials.</strong></p><p><strong>Close out notes and marking the WO complete must be done after the equipment is shipped out. Please notify POC with receipt and tracking information.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ ME!!!!</strong></p><p>Check-in on the Field Nation App</p><p>Introduce yourself to the MOD</p><p><strong>L-Bracket Scope:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">L-bracket needs to be installed to mount the antenna located in the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">meat cooler</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">. Photos attached.</span></li><li>Technician needed install existing antenna<strong> in the Meat cooler </strong>to newly provided L-Bracket.</li><li>L-Brackets are already on site.</li></ul><p><strong>AP Relabeling:</strong></p><ul><li>Use Lift and readjust APs at the direction of your work order manager</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a before and after photo of each.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>TESTING</strong>:</p><p>Once final AP is installed, Connect to the guest Wi-Fi (take a screenshot of splash page and post to the chat) and do a walk-through of the location testing the signal strength. Indoor and outdoor.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>POST TEST:</strong></p><p>Walk through with the MOD and complete the checklist confirming all networked devices are fully functional</p><p>Move Lift back to where we found it and attach a picture to your FN WO. Include the lift ID number in the photo.</p><p>Receive Signoff from MOD&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Skill Set &amp; Tools Required:</strong></p><p><strong><em>WhatsApp </em></strong>for efficient group communication&nbsp;</p><p>PPE - Hi-Vis shirt or vest and face mask if required by site</p><p>Steel Toe Boots, Safety Glasses, Lift Harness (This is required, if you don't own one, they are sold for about $20 at HD.)</p><p>Adjustable Ladder or 10' A-Frame</p><p>Smartphone for communication while onsite</p><p>Laptop with hotspot</p><p>Network Equipment Experience Required</p><p>Working Camera</p><p>100 ft extension cord \"In case lift needs to be charged\"</p><p>Aruba Console Cable</p><p>Putty Installed**(this must be done before we arrive)</p><p>Microsoft Teams Installed**(This must be done before we arrive.)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Total installation must be complete BEFORE the store opens for business.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope Notes**\n\n**Tech Must Be Lift Certified.**\n\n**All Deliverables must be uploaded to FN prior to leaving site, unless returning materials.**\n\n**Close out notes and marking the WO complete must be done after the equipment is shipped out. Please notify POC with receipt and tracking information.**\n\n**READ ME!!!!**\n\nCheck-in on the Field Nation App\n\nIntroduce yourself to the MOD\n\n**L-Bracket Scope:**\n\n- L-bracket needs to be installed to mount the antenna located in the **meat cooler**. Photos attached.\n- Technician needed install existing antenna **in the Meat cooler** to newly provided L-Bracket.\n- L-Brackets are already on site.\n\n**AP Relabeling:**\n\n- Use Lift and readjust APs at the direction of your work order manager\n- Take a before and after photo of each.\n\n**TESTING**:\n\nOnce final AP is installed, Connect to the guest Wi-Fi (take a screenshot of splash page and post to the chat) and do a walk-through of the location testing the signal strength. Indoor and outdoor.\n\n**POST TEST:**\n\nWalk through with the MOD and complete the checklist confirming all networked devices are fully functional\n\nMove Lift back to where we found it and attach a picture to your FN WO. Include the lift ID number in the photo.\n\nReceive Signoff from MOD\n\n**Skill Set & Tools Required:**\n\n***WhatsApp*** for efficient group communication\n\nPPE - Hi-Vis shirt or vest and face mask if required by site\n\nSteel Toe Boots, Safety Glasses, Lift Harness (This is required, if you don't own one, they are sold for about $20 at HD.)\n\nAdjustable Ladder or 10' A-Frame\n\nSmartphone for communication while onsite\n\nLaptop with hotspot\n\nNetwork Equipment Experience Required\n\nWorking Camera\n\n100 ft extension cord \"In case lift needs to be charged\"\n\nAruba Console Cable\n\nPutty Installed\\*\\*(this must be done before we arrive)\n\nMicrosoft Teams Installed\\*\\*(This must be done before we arrive.)\n\n**Total installation must be complete BEFORE the store opens for business.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T22:00","end":"2026-11-02T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":55.76460416338225},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792527975383}
{"job":{"id":20212625,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2740063","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Microwave : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Microwave : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00","end":"2026-10-23T17:00","latestStart":"2026-10-23T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":15.010201196453615},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792528070948}
{"job":{"id":20212575,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Catcon Products","title":"Lumen EWAS Rotech Cutover and Test","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p>Overview:</p><p><br></p><p>Seeking a technician with experience in network equipment installation and configuration.</p><p><strong>Tech is required to complete the final cutover of an installed Cellular Data Router to the customers SASE Versa equipment. Tech will work with 10T support to confirm that all equipment is working as required. Tech must be prepared to troubleshoot and repair any equipment or lines as required. Tech is required to fabricate and label a CAT 6 cable that will run form the Router POE injector LAN port to the customers Versa port. Port number will be provided by 10T support day of the cutover. Expense will be added to the WO. </strong></p><p>Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Business Casual</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Cell phone with camera</p><p>Basic Network Hand Tools</p><p>Basic Hand Tools&nbsp;</p><p>Laptop with ethernet cable</p><p>Zip Ties</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Tools and parts required for manufacturing RJ11 or RJ45 cables.</p><p>Tools for punching down to a 66 or 110 block</p><p>Flashlight or Head Lamp</p><p>Tools for low voltage cable runs</p><p>Equipment for creating label for cables and 66 or 110 Block</p><p>Assorted fasteners needed to mount equipment to different surfaces.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><p>Please review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.</p><p>Print off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.</p><p>Confirm WO and start time 48 hours prior.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.</p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del><strong> to coordinate the cutover and final test.</strong></p><p>Locate equipment and document previously installed InHand ODU. Router should be installed externally.</p><p>Take photo of the installed router.</p><p>Take photo of the external penetration.</p><p>Take photo of the mounted POE injector.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Verify Router Cell Connection</strong></p><p><strong>All Rotech sites will have PSIP. 10T support will provide the PSIP.</strong></p><p>Connect laptop to router LAN port. Laptop should be set to DHCP.</p><p>Verify connectivity. IP address. Able to internet browse.</p><p>Run speed test.</p><p><strong>Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. <u>DO NOT MOVE THE ROUTER</u> without approval from 10T support. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Sheet.</strong></p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">5-900-0809</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Final Cutover</strong></p><p>Router is now ready to the customers Versa device.</p><p>Fabricate and label a CAT6 cable that will connect to the Router POE injector LAN port and run to the customers Versa device.</p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p>Connect the fabricated cable to the Router POE injector LAN port and to the customers assigned port that will be provided by 10T support along with final test procedure.</p><p>10T support will verify the cutover and release you from the site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Install completion checklist</strong></p><p>Check that all cables and wiring are dressed and neat.</p><p>Label all cables and wires if needed.</p><p>Leave work area neat and clean</p><p>Take all required photos and upload.</p><p>Complete acceptance form and have LCON sign if available. Upload completed form.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Check Out:</strong></p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy&nbsp;</p><p>Any additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.</p>","markdown":"**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nOverview:\n\nSeeking a technician with experience in network equipment installation and configuration.\n\n**Tech is required to complete the final cutover of an installed Cellular Data Router to the customers SASE Versa equipment. Tech will work with 10T support to confirm that all equipment is working as required. Tech must be prepared to troubleshoot and repair any equipment or lines as required. Tech is required to fabricate and label a CAT 6 cable that will run form the Router POE injector LAN port to the customers Versa port. Port number will be provided by 10T support day of the cutover. Expense will be added to the WO.**\n\nEstimated duration will be 1-2 hours.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nBusiness Casual\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nCell phone with camera\n\nBasic Network Hand Tools\n\nBasic Hand Tools\n\nLaptop with ethernet cable\n\nZip Ties\n\nLadder\n\nTools and parts required for manufacturing RJ11 or RJ45 cables.\n\nTools for punching down to a 66 or 110 block\n\nFlashlight or Head Lamp\n\nTools for low voltage cable runs\n\nEquipment for creating label for cables and 66 or 110 Block\n\nAssorted fasteners needed to mount equipment to different surfaces.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\nPlease review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.\n\nPrint off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.\n\nConfirm WO and start time 48 hours prior.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**On-Site Tasks**\n\nCheck-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **to coordinate the cutover and final test.**\n\nLocate equipment and document previously installed InHand ODU. Router should be installed externally.\n\nTake photo of the installed router.\n\nTake photo of the external penetration.\n\nTake photo of the mounted POE injector.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Verify Router Cell Connection**\n\n**All Rotech sites will have PSIP. 10T support will provide the PSIP.**\n\nConnect laptop to router LAN port. Laptop should be set to DHCP.\n\nVerify connectivity. IP address. Able to internet browse.\n\nRun speed test.\n\n**Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. DO NOT MOVE THE ROUTER without approval from 10T support. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Sheet.**\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*5-900-0809\n\n**Final Cutover**\n\nRouter is now ready to the customers Versa device.\n\nFabricate and label a CAT6 cable that will connect to the Router POE injector LAN port and run to the customers Versa device.\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nConnect the fabricated cable to the Router POE injector LAN port and to the customers assigned port that will be provided by 10T support along with final test procedure.\n\n10T support will verify the cutover and release you from the site.\n\n**Install completion checklist**\n\nCheck that all cables and wiring are dressed and neat.\n\nLabel all cables and wires if needed.\n\nLeave work area neat and clean\n\nTake all required photos and upload.\n\nComplete acceptance form and have LCON sign if available. Upload completed form.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check Out:**\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nAdditional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy\n\nAny additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:15","end":"2026-11-06T12:15","latestStart":"2026-11-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":65.0137233820282},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792528679501}
{"job":{"id":20212777,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TeleSol IT B.V.","title":"T106440:  Install DIA service","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">You are required to provide your email address</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"> so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR).&nbsp;</span>Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.</li><li><strong>Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.</strong> If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The bridge will open at the top of the hour. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.</span></li><li><strong>Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent</strong>. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!</strong></li><li>Please <strong>introduce yourself</strong> as working on behalf of Telesol Group for<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></strong><strong>.</strong> The equipment being installed is for&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></span>.</li><li><strong>Never use long distance calls </strong>unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Work Type: Professional Install</p><p>Conference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.</p><p>Additional task details provided in&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of work</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">** PLEASE BRING LABEL MAKER ** Please make sure it is working with ink and labels. It Iis absolutely mandatory that you bring a laptop that can get speeds up to 1 Gig. Field tech will arrive at NOVARTIS and say they’re with <del>*** </del>to install DIA service. Please gather package from Local contact named Richard . The client received the package from <del>*** </del>on September 10.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><del>*** </del>Engineer once the order is done please fill out the MONITORING TAB.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Please install Spectrum Service with <del>*** </del>Engineer remotely on the bridge.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Demarc is: 3rd floor – to be announced October 30.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Tech will need laptop supporting 1G speeds, Please have Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed; portable hotspot; AND console cable – PLEASE MAKE SURE.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Required Tool List for any <del>*** </del>Request:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">The following equipment must be taken as standard to all interventions:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, screw drivers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Label Maker</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Mobile phone with charger</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk): Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Cisco micro USB to Serial USB Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Server Rack Screws</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- (4-6) Ethernet cables</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Fiber Jumpers are also preferred but not required:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cable(s)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Please do not remove any <del>*** </del>equipment unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a <del>*** </del>support agent. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to <del>***</del>.</span></p><p><strong><u>Special access requirements (if any)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Special tools (if any)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tool List</strong></p><ul><li>Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)</li><li>Mobile phone with charger</li><li>Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</li><li>Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</li><li>Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to <strong>1000 Mbps (1G)</strong>, Teamveiwer software installed</li><li>Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)</li><li>Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):</li><li>Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</li><li>1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</li><li>Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</li><li>(4-6) Ethernet cables</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Preferred but not required</em></strong></p><ul><li>SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables</li><li>Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process</strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;noc@telesolgroup.com</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Contact</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\"><em>&nbsp;number - ​USA Toll-free:&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em><u><del>** ***** ********</del></u></em></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"- **All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol.** Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.\n- **You are required to provide your email address** so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR). Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.\n- **Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.** If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.\n- **The bridge will open at the top of the hour.** In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.\n- **Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent**. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.\n- **The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!**\n- Please **introduce yourself** as working on behalf of Telesol Group for **\\*\\*\\*****.** The equipment being installed is for \\*\\*\\*.\n- **Never use long distance calls** unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.\n\nWork Type: Professional Install\n\nConference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.\n\nAdditional task details provided in *Confidential Information* section below.\n\n**Scope of work**\n\n\\*\\* PLEASE BRING LABEL MAKER \\*\\* Please make sure it is working with ink and labels. It Iis absolutely mandatory that you bring a laptop that can get speeds up to 1 Gig. Field tech will arrive at NOVARTIS and say they’re with \\*\\*\\* to install DIA service. Please gather package from Local contact named Richard . The client received the package from \\*\\*\\* on September 10.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Engineer once the order is done please fill out the MONITORING TAB.\n\nPlease install Spectrum Service with \\*\\*\\* Engineer remotely on the bridge.\n\nDemarc is: 3rd floor – to be announced October 30.\n\nTech will need laptop supporting 1G speeds, Please have Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed; portable hotspot; AND console cable – PLEASE MAKE SURE.\n\nRequired Tool List for any \\*\\*\\* Request:\n\nThe following equipment must be taken as standard to all interventions:\n\n\\- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, screw drivers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.)\n\n\\- Label Maker\n\n\\- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot).\n\n\\- Mobile phone with charger\n\n\\- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n\n\\- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)\n\n\\- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk): Anydesk, Zoho Assist, and if needed Teamviewer installed\n\n\\- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:\n\n\\- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use\n\n\\- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco micro USB to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Server Rack Screws\n\n\\- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n\n\\- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Fiber Jumpers are also preferred but not required:\n\nSC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cable(s)\n\nPlease do not remove any \\*\\*\\* equipment unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a \\*\\*\\* support agent. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to \\*\\*\\*.\n\n**Special access requirements (if any)**\n\n**Special tools (if any)**\n\n**Required Tool List**\n\n- Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment\n- Label Maker\n- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)\n- Mobile phone with charger\n- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)\n- Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to **1000 Mbps (1G)**, Teamveiwer software installed\n- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)\n- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):\n- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:\n- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use\n- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter\n- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n***Preferred but not required***\n\n- SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables\n- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.\n\n**Escalation Process**\n\n- ***Any issues or questions should be escalated to noc@telesolgroup.com***\n- ***Contact*** ***number - ​USA Toll-free:*** ***\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\****","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T11:30","end":"2026-11-05T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":7.930446862068007},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792528768420}
{"job":{"id":"3402564831","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"06065628-USAM-498-EPIK Survey","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"Survey Scope of Work<br>The Survey ticket to utilize Survey Wizard should include the following scope of work:<br>This is a discovery Survey. Please try to find all lines listed and any other lines associated with FIRE, BURG, and COOLER ALARM if they have these<br>Notes that must be followed and uploaded in survey for extra pictures per Pepsi<br>oPICTURES: prior to starting work, tech needs to take picture of area to show any preexisting conditions<br>oPICTURES: Pictures of mounting location and all panels must be attached in Survey.<br>oPICTURES: Pictures of tagged lines listed to find<br><br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2. Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the survey, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard. (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>4. Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard. If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team. All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site. The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>5. Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>6. Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services.<br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":64.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":95,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T20:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start"