{"job":{"id":20213360,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Celerity Fiber LLC","title":"SERVICE CALL DTV","description":{"html":"<p>Overview:</p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in: DTV installation experience/ Satellite TV</li><li>Tech is required to: Perform Appointment type SERVICE CALL DTV</li><li>DirecTV acc: <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">8295424</span></li><li>Estimated duration will be: N/A</li></ul><p>Dress Code:</p><ul><li>Long Pants/clean/closed shoes</li></ul><p>Tools Required:</p><ul><li>AIM Meter (Directv</li><li>Super Buddy Meter (Dish Network)</li><li>QAM Meter (L&amp;I Properties)</li><li>Inductive Cable Toner (Fox &amp; Hound)</li><li>Pocket Cable Toner</li><li>Diagonal Cutter (Dikes)</li><li>Needle Nose Pliers</li><li>Cordless 1/4\" Impact Driver</li><li>Cordless 1/2\" Hammer Drill</li><li>Drill Bits &amp; Impact tips/adapters</li><li>RG6 Cable Stripper</li><li>RG11 Cable Stripper</li><li>RG6 Coax Cable Linear Crimper</li><li>RG11 Coax Cable Linear Crimper</li><li>Cat5/6 Cable Crimper</li><li>Coax Security Sleeve tool</li><li>Phillips and Traditional Screwdrivers</li><li>7/16\" Open end Wrench</li><li>1/2\" Open end Wrench</li><li>Cresce</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work:</p><p><br></p><p>Check the connections inside and outside the unit. Verify the connections in the network closet, SWM, and polarity locker, and measure the signal strength at each connection. Ensure the satellite dish alignment using the AIM meter. After confirming the correct percentage of signal strength, check if the DTV box is functional or needs to be replaced. Restore the DTV signal</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Pre-Site Requirements</p><p>1. Call Tech line <del>************</del> when Technician is on their way to the site.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>On-Site Tasks</p><ul><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Celerity by Adcomm while onsite</li><li>Arrive on site on time and cleanly dressed.</li><li>Perform diagnosis of the issue stated in the work order.</li><li>Make any appropriate repairs.</li><li>Verify customer’s system is working.</li><li>For installations please train the customer how to use the system.</li><li>Document the repair or installation you made, and all parts used</li><li>Record Arrival and departure time.</li><li>Have customer sign the work order.</li><li>Take pictures of functional TVs and work completed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required On-Site Deliverables</p><ol><li>Signed work order</li><li>Pictures of the work completed and include device information (model/Receiver ID/Access Card/MAC address*/Serial number*) * only for client and mini genies</li><li>Description of the work with parts used</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Escalation Process:</p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, Call Celerity's Tech line at <del>************</del></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</p><ul><li>additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved by Chip Packard/Rocio Serrano for MDU and for L&amp;I from Rennick Carter.</li></ul>","markdown":"Overview:\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in: DTV installation experience/ Satellite TV\n- Tech is required to: Perform Appointment type SERVICE CALL DTV\n- DirecTV acc: 8295424\n- Estimated duration will be: N/A\n\nDress Code:\n\n- Long Pants/clean/closed shoes\n\nTools Required:\n\n- AIM Meter (Directv\n- Super Buddy Meter (Dish Network)\n- QAM Meter (L&I Properties)\n- Inductive Cable Toner (Fox & Hound)\n- Pocket Cable Toner\n- Diagonal Cutter (Dikes)\n- Needle Nose Pliers\n- Cordless 1/4\" Impact Driver\n- Cordless 1/2\" Hammer Drill\n- Drill Bits & Impact tips/adapters\n- RG6 Cable Stripper\n- RG11 Cable Stripper\n- RG6 Coax Cable Linear Crimper\n- RG11 Coax Cable Linear Crimper\n- Cat5/6 Cable Crimper\n- Coax Security Sleeve tool\n- Phillips and Traditional Screwdrivers\n- 7/16\" Open end Wrench\n- 1/2\" Open end Wrench\n- Cresce\n\nScope of Work:\n\nCheck the connections inside and outside the unit. Verify the connections in the network closet, SWM, and polarity locker, and measure the signal strength at each connection. Ensure the satellite dish alignment using the AIM meter. After confirming the correct percentage of signal strength, check if the DTV box is functional or needs to be replaced. Restore the DTV signal\n\nPre-Site Requirements\n\n1\\. Call Tech line \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when Technician is on their way to the site.\n\nOn-Site Tasks\n\n- Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Celerity by Adcomm while onsite\n- Arrive on site on time and cleanly dressed.\n- Perform diagnosis of the issue stated in the work order.\n- Make any appropriate repairs.\n- Verify customer’s system is working.\n- For installations please train the customer how to use the system.\n- Document the repair or installation you made, and all parts used\n- Record Arrival and departure time.\n- Have customer sign the work order.\n- Take pictures of functional TVs and work completed.\n\nRequired On-Site Deliverables\n\n1. Signed work order\n2. Pictures of the work completed and include device information (model/Receiver ID/Access Card/MAC address\\*/Serial number\\*) \\* only for client and mini genies\n3. Description of the work with parts used\n\nEscalation Process:\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, Call Celerity's Tech line at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nAdditional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy\n\n- additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved by Chip Packard/Rocio Serrano for MDU and for L&I from Rennick Carter.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T08:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":9.274731734285195},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792532809666}
{"job":{"id":20213404,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CloudCover.","title":"INC12619-001 / 55857 - M.2 Drive Replacement and complete imaged setup - HP ELite Desk Mini 600 G9 ","description":{"html":"<p>We are sending a pre-imaged M.2 drive for this machine which will need to be installed following the instructions to complete the image setup described in the&nbsp;<strong><u>M.2 SSD DRIVE REPLACEMENT AND IMAGE SETUP PROCEDURE&nbsp;</u></strong>below.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);\">PLEASE SET UP YOUR&nbsp;</strong><strong>ETA IN THIS WO.</strong></p><p><strong>***Note:</strong> Do not delay or cancel the visit if the part is not on site or the tracking indicates it has not yet been delivered. Our service level agreement (SLA) is per on-site technician.***</p>","markdown":"We are sending a pre-imaged M.2 drive for this machine which will need to be installed following the instructions to complete the image setup described in the **M.2 SSD DRIVE REPLACEMENT AND IMAGE SETUP PROCEDURE** below.\n\n**PLEASE SET UP YOUR** **ETA IN THIS WO.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Note:** Do not delay or cancel the visit if the part is not on site or the tracking indicates it has not yet been delivered. Our service level agreement (SLA) is per on-site technician.\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T11:00","end":"2026-10-21T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":135},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":56.42450473648991},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $135 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792533492186}
{"job":{"id":20213476,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Complete Tablet Solutions, LTD","title":"Access Point Replacement #195466 #VA313 #C&M - Morrisville","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>﻿</u>SCOPE:</strong> 2 AP32 Access Point Replacement &amp; Network Validation</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician must bring a laptop and standard networking tools.</li>\n<li>Standard CAT6 patch cable recommended.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Arrival &amp; Initial Steps</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on-site and meet the site contact.</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself as a CTS Field Technician.</li>\n<li>Locate the IT/Telecom closet and identify the designated work areas.</li>\n<li>Contact CTS Remote Support (Ops) before beginning any work to confirm scope and receive approval to proceed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Access Point Replacement</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New AP32 units will be available onsite.</li>\n<li>Locate existing AP32 access point in the office.</li>\n<li>Replace a total of 2 existing AP32 access point with the new AP32 units provided onsite.</li>\n<li>Remove each existing AP and mounting bracket one at a time.</li>\n<li>Install the new mounting bracket and new AP32 in the designated location.</li>\n<li>Ensure each AP is securely mounted and properly connected.</li>\n<li>Verify the status light on each AP is illuminated and operating normally.</li>\n<li>Re-terminate cabling as required if an AP does not come online after installation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Network &amp; Connectivity Configuration</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If not already connected, connect the Ethernet cable from the UPS network card to the network switch.</li>\n<li>If not already connected, connect the Ethernet cable from the ATS to the network switch.</li>\n<li>Notify CTS Remote Support immediately if a UPS network card is not present.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot connectivity issues as needed to ensure all APs are online.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Validation &amp; Testing</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Once all APs have been replaced, check in with CTS Remote Support/IT Operations.</li>\n<li>Verify all new AP32 devices are online, reachable, and reporting properly.</li>\n<li>Confirm all networking equipment is functioning correctly.</li>\n<li>Ensure wireless network coverage and connectivity are operational before departing the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Asset Handling</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Box all removed AP32 units and mounting hardware.</li>\n<li>Provide all removed equipment to the Branch Manager for storage and disposition.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Closure Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clean the work area thoroughly.</li>\n<li>Take and upload clear photos, including:</li>\n<li>Close-up photos of each completed AP installation.</li>\n<li>Photos of the surrounding work areas.</li>\n<li>Photos of the network rack and switch connections.</li>\n<li>At least one full photo of the entire network rack.</li>\n<li>Upload all required photos and updates before closing the ticket.</li>\n<li>Confirm completion with CTS Remote Support prior to departure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Attire Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clean and professional appearance.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire with closed-toe shoes.</li>\n<li>Preferred shirt colors: Blue, Black, or White.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**﻿SCOPE:** 2 AP32 Access Point Replacement & Network Validation\n\n**Requirements**\n\n- Technician must bring a laptop and standard networking tools.\n- Standard CAT6 patch cable recommended.\n\n**Arrival & Initial Steps**\n\n- Arrive on-site and meet the site contact.\n- Introduce yourself as a CTS Field Technician.\n- Locate the IT/Telecom closet and identify the designated work areas.\n- Contact CTS Remote Support (Ops) before beginning any work to confirm scope and receive approval to proceed.\n\n**Access Point Replacement**\n\n- New AP32 units will be available onsite.\n- Locate existing AP32 access point in the office.\n- Replace a total of 2 existing AP32 access point with the new AP32 units provided onsite.\n- Remove each existing AP and mounting bracket one at a time.\n- Install the new mounting bracket and new AP32 in the designated location.\n- Ensure each AP is securely mounted and properly connected.\n- Verify the status light on each AP is illuminated and operating normally.\n- Re-terminate cabling as required if an AP does not come online after installation.\n\n**Network & Connectivity Configuration**\n\n- If not already connected, connect the Ethernet cable from the UPS network card to the network switch.\n- If not already connected, connect the Ethernet cable from the ATS to the network switch.\n- Notify CTS Remote Support immediately if a UPS network card is not present.\n- Troubleshoot connectivity issues as needed to ensure all APs are online.\n\n**Validation & Testing**\n\n- Once all APs have been replaced, check in with CTS Remote Support/IT Operations.\n- Verify all new AP32 devices are online, reachable, and reporting properly.\n- Confirm all networking equipment is functioning correctly.\n- Ensure wireless network coverage and connectivity are operational before departing the site.\n\n**Asset Handling**\n\n- Box all removed AP32 units and mounting hardware.\n- Provide all removed equipment to the Branch Manager for storage and disposition.\n\n**Closure Requirements**\n\n- Clean the work area thoroughly.\n- Take and upload clear photos, including:\n- Close-up photos of each completed AP installation.\n- Photos of the surrounding work areas.\n- Photos of the network rack and switch connections.\n- At least one full photo of the entire network rack.\n- Upload all required photos and updates before closing the ticket.\n- Confirm completion with CTS Remote Support prior to departure.\n\n**Attire Requirements**\n\n- Clean and professional appearance.\n- Business casual attire with closed-toe shoes.\n- Preferred shirt colors: Blue, Black, or White.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T09:30","end":"2026-11-11T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.473696421339931},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792534266773}
{"job":{"id":20213463,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity, Inc","title":"Photo Lab PC Image Install - 409261","description":{"html":"<p>Call Direct: 888-443-4375 Option 0</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>With as many open work orders currently on FN, there is a very long back order of requests. So if you call in they will work with you to get assigned.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\nJob Description:\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Job Description: Please dispatch Tech to reimage PC and confirm drivr for the canon poster printer installs.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Requirements(Skills/Tools):Full Screwdriver Set Basic PC/Windows and Cabling Knowledge</p>\n<p><br /></p>\nRequired Tools:\n<p>Cell phone: With charger and photo taking ability</p>\n<p>Camera with USB cord: If phone with photo taking ability is not available</p>\n<p>WINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port</p>\n<p>Set of screwdrivers that include Phillips and Regular flat heads</p>\n<p>TORX T-10 and T-15</p>\n<p>Adjustable crescent wrench</p>\n<p>Socket set</p>\n<p>Cell phone: With charger and photo taking ability</p>\n<p>Camera with USB cord: If phone with photo taking ability is not available</p>\n<p>WINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port</p>\n<p>Set of screwdrivers that include Phillips and Regular flat heads</p>\n<p>TORX T-10 and T-15</p>\n<p>Adjustable crescent wrench</p>\n<p>Socket set</p>\n<p>Cell phone: With charger and photo taking ability</p>\n<p>Camera with USB cord: If phone with photo taking ability is not available</p>\n<p>WINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port</p>\n<p>Set of screwdrivers that include Phillips and Regular flat heads</p>\n<p>TORX T-10 and T-15</p>\n<p>Adjustable crescent wrench</p>\n<p>Socket set</p>","markdown":"Call Direct: 888-443-4375 Option 0\n\nWith as many open work orders currently on FN, there is a very long back or