{"job":{"id":20213682,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TeleSol IT B.V.","title":"T106448: Installation of NID (Receive shipment, bring to site, Real ID & U.S. Citizenship MANDATORY)","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong>You will be required to receive a shipment and bring it to the site. </strong></li><li><strong>These locations are unmanned and not able to receive shipment. </strong></li><li><strong>On day of install, you will meet with a local contact for access</strong></li><li><strong>Upon accepting this WO, please message over your shipping address ASAP and confirm you will have one of the acceptable ID documents, mentioned below, needed for access to <del>***</del> federal facility. </strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"><u>All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.</u></strong></li><li><strong>Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour. If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The bridge will open at the top of the hour. In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.</strong></li><li><strong>Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!</strong></li><li><strong>You are to represent yourself as working on behalf of Telesol Group for&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></strong><strong>. The equipment being installed is for&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></strong><strong>.</strong></li><li><strong>Never use long distance calls unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Shipment information</u> </strong></p><ul><li>The equipment will be a network interface device (NID). Small box with NID and cables.</li><li>Please send us the address your address shipping the equipment so that we can start the process. Equipment is picked up either at the carrier checkpoint/UPS of your choice or your home address (to your preference).</li><li>Liaise with Telesol to confirm the shipment details and tracking number</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Access</u></strong></p><p>Since the new REAL ID federal law is now into effect engineer that requires site access to a <del>***</del> federal facility must have a State issued REAL ID. If they do not have a REAL ID yet, one of the Alternative forms of ID listed below must be presented when they arrive onsite. Alternative to a REAL ID-compliant driver's license, visitors may use the following forms of identification for access:</p><ul><li>State-issued Enhanced Driver's License</li><li>U.S. Passport</li><li>U.S. Passport Card</li><li>DHS Trusted Traveler Cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</li><li>U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents</li><li>Permanent Resident Card</li><li>Border Crossing Card</li><li>An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized, Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe</li><li>HSPD-12 PIV card</li><li>Foreign Government-issued Passport</li><li>Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card</li><li>Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC)</li><li>U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)</li><li>U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential</li><li>Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>*** U.S. Citizenship is REQUIRED for access to all US Military facilities***</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><u>Due to the high security (government site) at this location, the technician cannot have any unlawful convictions.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Please contact site POC 1 hour before arrival. </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">If the FE is running late, we must be informed well in advance. </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">It is not acceptable for the FE to call after he should have been on site at the scheduled dated/time to say he is running late. </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Site access is arranged in advance per site availability.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work and request details</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>﻿</strong>Full task details provided in&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section.</li><li>Travel to the site and meet the arranged site escort. (Check in with Telesol when you start heading to the site location.)</li><li>Installation of the NID.</li><li>Work with the Remote Engineer to complete the installation. Conference bridge details will be shared (Please have Microsoft Teams installed).</li><li>Upload site pictures before and after.</li><li>Make sure that everything is installed neatly.</li><li>Complete TTR (Telesol Ticket Report) before leaving the site. (instructions are in the attachment).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required equipment</u></strong></p><p>Please bring a Windows-based laptop with the AnyDesk <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">or Teamviewer </span>loaded on it, a <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">good and working </span>console cable, a<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> label maker, tools to mount/rack the equipment</span>.</p><p>*** FOR REMOTE LOCATIONS PLEASE USE 4X4 VEHICLE WHEN HEADING TO THE SITE *** </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Mobile hotspot is necessary</strong> <strong>as well as the tools below</strong>:</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Label Maker</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Screen sharing software (AnyDesk)</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to <strong>1000 Mbps (1G)</strong>, Teamveiwer software installed</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hyper-Terminal or other console emulator software</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1G USB-Ethernet Adapter</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(4-6) Ethernet cables</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;RJ11 Patch Cord</p>","markdown":"- **You will be required to receive a shipment and bring it to the site.**\n- **These locations are unmanned and not able to receive shipment.**\n- **On day of install, you will meet with a local contact for access**\n- **Upon accepting this WO, please message over your shipping address ASAP and confirm you will have one of the acceptable ID documents, mentioned below, needed for access to \\*\\*\\* federal facility.**\n- **All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.**\n- **Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour. If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.**\n- **The bridge will open at the top of the hour. In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.**\n- **Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.**\n- **The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!**\n- **You are to represent yourself as working on behalf of Telesol Group for** **\\*\\*\\*****. The equipment being installed is for** **\\*\\*\\*****.**\n- **Never use long distance calls unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.**\n\n**Shipment information**\n\n- The equipment will be a network interface device (NID). Small box with NID and cables.\n- Please send us the address your address shipping the equipment so that we can start the process. Equipment is picked up either at the carrier checkpoint/UPS of your choice or your home address (to your preference).\n- Liaise with Telesol to confirm the shipment details and tracking number\n\n**Site Access**\n\nSince the new REAL ID federal law is now into effect engineer that requires site access to a \\*\\*\\* federal facility must have a State issued REAL ID. If they do not have a REAL ID yet, one of the Alternative forms of ID listed below must be presented when they arrive onsite. Alternative to a REAL ID-compliant driver's license, visitors may use the following forms of identification for access:\n\n- State-issued Enhanced Driver's License\n- U.S. Passport\n- U.S. Passport Card\n- DHS Trusted Traveler Cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)\n- U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents\n- Permanent Resident Card\n- Border Crossing Card\n- An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized, Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe\n- HSPD-12 PIV card\n- Foreign Government-issued Passport\n- Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card\n- Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC)\n- U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)\n- U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential\n- Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)\n\n**\\*\\*\\* U.S. Citizenship is REQUIRED for access to all US Military facilities\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Due to the high security (government site) at this location, the technician cannot have any unlawful convictions.**\n\n- Please contact site POC 1 hour before arrival.\n- If the FE is running late, we must be informed well in advance.\n- It is not acceptable for the FE to call after he should have been on site at the scheduled dated/time to say he is running late.\n- Site access is arranged in advance per site availability.\n\n**Scope of Work and request details**\n\n- **﻿**Full task details provided in *Confidential Information* section.\n- Travel to the site and meet the arranged site escort. (Check in with Telesol when you start heading to the site location.)\n- Installation of the NID.\n- Work with the Remote Engineer to complete the installation. Conference bridge details will be shared (Please have Microsoft Teams installed).\n- Upload site pictures before and after.\n- Make sure that everything is installed neatly.\n- Complete TTR (Telesol Ticket Report) before leaving the site. (instructions are in the attachment).\n\n**Required equipment**\n\nPlease bring a Windows-based laptop with the AnyDesk or Teamviewer loaded on it, a good and working console cable, a label maker, tools to mount/rack the equipment.\n\n\\*\\*\\* FOR REMOTE LOCATIONS PLEASE USE 4X4 VEHICLE WHEN HEADING TO THE SITE \\*\\*\\*\n\n**Mobile hotspot is necessary** **as well as the tools below**:\n\n\\- Label Maker\n\n\\- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n\n\\- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk)\n\n\\- Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to **1000 Mbps (1G)**, Teamveiwer software installed\n\n\\- Hyper-Terminal or other console emulator software\n\n\\- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n\n\\- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n\n\\- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n\\- RJ11 Patch Cord","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T08:30","end":"2026-10-30T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":70.57571894528282},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":