{"job":{"id":20214749,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Bluekong Networks, LTD","title":"FTE Desktop Support - Cary, North Carolina","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Business attire</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work: <u>Introduction</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>FTE requirement for Desktop Support</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of work:</p><ol><li>Providing desk side Information Technology (IT) support in resolving incidents, queries and problems;</li><li>Providing desk side day to day Business As Usual (BAU) support to users;</li><li>User advice and IT overviews, new starter onboarding and leaver offboarding where applicable;</li><li>Working within Service Level Agreement (SLA);</li><li>Telephony support;</li><li>Supporting Microsoft Operating Systems (OS) and related products;</li><li>Supporting Apple OS products</li><li>Maintaining and updating assigned tickets via an IT Service Management (ITSM) tool;</li><li>New computer setups/and kit replacements as required</li><li>Supporting infosec operations on end user computers such as running security scans and reporting back to the infosec team.</li><li>Cell phone setup and installing company apps onto staff personal phones as requested</li><li>Responding to queries from Customers remote teams and stakeholders;</li><li>Performing regular floor walks;</li><li>Creating tickets for each walk-up request for IT support whilst onsite where a user doesn’t already have a ticket</li><li>Resolving incidents and requests;</li><li>Building machines via deployment software via Autopilot/Intune</li><li>Adhering to defined processes;</li><li>Day to day troubleshooting of devices, applications and peripherals</li><li>Following processes and adhering to the asset management lifecycle process, includes bringing equipment into the lifecycle, updating AMDB,</li><li>Warranty repairs – liaising with the vendor to attend site, or to ship the device to the vendor for repair. Performing low level repairs such as replacing batteries and screens if required.</li><li>Disposals;</li><li>Audio visual conferencing support;</li><li>Providing hands and eyes support to backend teams where required.</li><li>Comms room support – racking/de-racking of devices, patching cables, tracing cables, ability to console into a device</li><li><br></li></ol><p>Resource must speak the native language fluently and have excellent written and oral English skills&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Standard toolkit:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Console cable</li><li>Network dongle</li><li>USB key</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Label machine</li><li>Cable snips</li><li>Cable ties / Velcro</li><li>Laptop with RJ45 port or RJ45 adapter</li><li>Laptop with device console capabilities (terminal tools such as PuTTY)</li><li>Screwdrivers (various sizes)</li><li>Network patch cables</li></ul><p>Basic hand tools (e.g., pliers, wrenches)</p><p><strong><u>Objectives</u></strong></p><p>The objectives of this project are as follows:</p><ul><li><br></li></ul><p><strong><u>Inclusions</u></strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Implementation</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements </em></strong><span style=\"color: red;\">[list any tasks a technician will need to complete PRIOR to arriving onsite – )examples: print off attachments to review, call XXX to confirm start date/time, verifying shipping/tracking, etc)]</span></p><ul><li>Please ensure you have all apps, access codes and equipment as listed in this document, ready in advance of your first visit.&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;Please ensure you have flexibility in your diary for the day to accommodate overtime should issues arise on site(s).</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">You </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">must</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> watch the safety video as per the following link:&nbsp;</span>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SPpL4bu7Bng<span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;and confirm in writing that you have done so. In addition, you </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">must</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> adhere to all client Health &amp; Safety practices, which you must familiarise yourself with when you arrive on site.</span></li></ul><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks </em></strong><span style=\"color: red;\">[list tasks/steps a provider will need to take in order to complete the work up to your company standards. Examples include: Check in with onsite contact and introduce yourself as XXX, Upload photos of before starting work, Upload photos of completed work with photos including XXX, Complete XXX while onsite, etc.]</span></p><ul><li>Before and after photos, and serial number photos are to be taken and saved as a .jpeg file on all works where hardware is involved. This must include photos of old equipment being left on site. Should no photos be provided or quality is rejected by client, there will be a non-billable revisit.</li><li>Ensure you sign on site and off site with both customer and BlueKong PMO.</li><li>Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.</li></ul><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables </em></strong><span style=\"color: red;\">[list all deliverables a provider will be required to collect in order for their work to be approved by your team. Examples include: photos, signatures, confirmation codes, etc.]</span></p><ul><li>Before and after photos, and serial number photos are to be taken and saved as a .jpeg file on all works where hardware is involved. This must include photos of old equipment being left on site. Should no photos be provided or quality is rejected by client, there will be a non-billable revisit.</li><li>Ensure you sign on site and off site with both customer and BlueKong PMO.</li><li>Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Take photos of hardware in box and check for any physical damage before removing items from their cartons.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Take photos of devices as they are installed, so it can be shown if needed this has been done correctly. This needs to be front and back of devices where applicable and images must be labelled accordingly.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">These steps are in place to ensure that no payment disputes are raised by the client and to meet with Bluekong quality standards. Failure to observe these steps could result in non payment for works.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process: </strong><span style=\"color: red;\">[Identify your company’s escalation path in case a provider runs into questions or issues onsite]</span></p><ul><li>Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy </strong><span style=\"color: red;\">[list how your company handles any additional hour expenses or material/travel expense (Do they need to be pre-approved, does the provider need to call a specific contact, etc.?)]</span></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Any additional costs need to be Pre-Approved with the Bluekong PM.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">If you arrive on site before the scheduled start time, you must ask your Bluekong contact for approval to start early as this must be agreed with the client in writing to ensure that payment is calculated correctly. If you are asked to start work early by the site contact or remote contact please inform them that you need to check in with the office to confirm.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">You MUST inform your Bluekong contact via Phone, WhatsApp or SMS (</span><u style=\"color: rgb(200, 38, 19);\">email is not acceptable</u><u style=\"color: black;\">)</u><span style=\"color: black;\">;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">If you are going to be late arriving on site.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">When you arrive on site, before you start working. Or if working remotely, confirming you have started work. (this activates your Purchase Order for the visit, and if you fail to do this it will delay invoice approval)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">If any issues require escalation (e.g. client changing the scope of work, missing equipment or login details).</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">When you are ready to leave site and have your completed signoff sheets, signed by the client (not AFTER you have left site).</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black;\">If there is no phone signal, it is your responsibility to ask for access to a telephone or Wi-Fi so that you can alert your Bluekong contact. In extreme cases it may be necessary for you to tell the site contact that you need to get to a location with signal so that you can call into the office.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">You must have a completed sign off form in order to be paid for any works. You must not leave a client site until a member of the Bluekong delivery team has authorised you to do so.</span></p>","markdown":"**Dress Code:**\n\n- · Business attire\n\n**Scope of Work: Introduction**\n\n**FTE requirement for Desktop Support**\n\nScope of work:\n\n1. Providing desk side Information Technology (IT) support in resolving incidents, queries and problems;\n2. Providing desk side day to day Business As Usual (BAU) support to users;\n3. User advice and IT overviews, new starter onboarding and leaver offboarding where applicable;\n4. Working within Service Level Agreement (SLA);\n5. Telephony support;\n6. Supporting Microsoft Operating Systems (OS) and related products;\n7. Supporting Apple OS products\n8. Maintaining and updating assigned tickets via an IT Service Management (ITSM) tool;\n9. New computer setups/and kit replacements as required\n10. Supporting infosec operations on end user computers such as running security scans and reporting back to the infosec team.\n11. Cell phone setup and installing company apps onto staff personal phones as requested\n12. Responding to queries from Customers remote teams and stakeholders;\n13. Performing regular floor walks;\n14. Creating tickets for each walk-up request for IT support whilst onsite where a user doesn’t already have a ticket\n15. Resolving incidents and requests;\n16. Building machines via deployment software via Autopilot/Intune\n17. Adhering to defined processes;\n18. Day to day troubleshooting of devices, applications and peripherals\n19. Following processes and adhering to the asset management lifecycle process, includes bringing equipment into the lifecycle, updating AMDB,\n20. Warranty repairs – liaising with the vendor to attend site, or to ship the device to the vendor for repair. Performing low level repairs such as replacing batteries and screens if required.\n21. Disposals;\n22. Audio visual conferencing support;\n23. Providing hands and eyes support to backend teams where required.\n24. Comms room support – racking/de-racking of devices, patching cables, tracing cables, ability to console into a device\n25. \n\nResource must speak the native language fluently and have excellent written and oral English skills\n\n**Standard toolkit:**\n\n- Console cable\n- Network dongle\n- USB key\n- Laptop\n- Label machine\n- Cable snips\n- Cable ties / Velcro\n- Laptop with RJ45 port or RJ45 adapter\n- Laptop with device console capabilities (terminal tools such as PuTTY)\n- Screwdrivers (various sizes)\n- Network patch cables\n\nBasic hand tools (e.g., pliers, wrenches)\n\n**Objectives**\n\nThe objectives of this project are as follows:\n\n- \n\n**Inclusions**\n\n**• Implementation**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements*** \\[list any tasks a technician will need to complete PRIOR to arriving onsite – )examples: print off attachments to review, call XXX to confirm start date/time, verifying shipping/tracking, etc)\\]\n\n- Please ensure you have all apps, access codes and equipment as listed in this document, ready in advance of your first visit.\n- Please ensure you have flexibility in your diary for the day to accommodate overtime should issues arise on site(s).\n- You **must** watch the safety video as per the following link: <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SPpL4bu7Bng> and confirm in writing that you have done so. In addition, you **must** adhere to all client Health & Safety practices, which you must familiarise yourself with when you arrive on site.\n\n***On-Site Tasks*** \\[list tasks/steps a provider will need to take in order to complete the work up to your company standards. Examples include: Check in with onsite contact and introduce yourself as XXX, Upload photos of before starting work, Upload photos of completed work with photos including XXX, Complete XXX while onsite, etc.\\]\n\n- Before and after photos, and serial number photos are to be taken and saved as a .jpeg file on all works where hardware is involved. This must include photos of old equipment being left on site. Should no photos be provided or quality is rejected by client, there will be a non-billable revisit.\n- Ensure you sign on site and off site with both customer and BlueKong PMO.\n- Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables*** \\[list all deliverables a provider will be required to collect in order for their work to be approved by your team. Examples include: photos, signatures, confirmation codes, etc.\\]\n\n- Before and after photos, and serial number photos are to be taken and saved as a .jpeg file on all works where hardware is involved. This must include photos of old equipment being left on site. Should no photos be provided or quality is rejected by client, there will be a non-billable revisit.\n- Ensure you sign on site and off site with both customer and BlueKong PMO.\n- Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.\n- Take photos of hardware in box and check for any physical damage before removing items from their cartons.\n- Take photos of devices as they are installed, so it can be shown if needed this has been done correctly. This needs to be front and back of devices where applicable and images must be labelled accordingly.\n- These steps are in place to ensure that no payment disputes are raised by the client and to meet with Bluekong quality standards. Failure to observe these steps could result in non payment for works.\n\n**Escalation Process:** \\[Identify your company’s escalation path in case a provider runs into questions or issues onsite\\]\n\n- Should you have any issues, please contact Bluekong PMO immediately.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy** \\[list how your company handles any additional hour expenses or material/travel expense (Do they need to be pre-approved, does the provider need to call a specific contact, etc.?)\\]\n\n- Any additional costs need to be Pre-Approved with the Bluekong PM.\n\n**Additional Information**\n\nIf you arrive on site before the scheduled start time, you must ask your Bluekong contact for approval to start early as this must be agreed with the client in writing to ensure that payment is calculated correctly. If you are asked to start work early by the site contact or remote contact please inform them that you need to check in with the office to confirm.\n\nYou MUST inform your Bluekong contact via Phone, WhatsApp or SMS (email is not acceptable);\n\n- If you are going to be late arriving on site.\n- When you arrive on site, before you start working. Or if working remotely, confirming you have started work. (this activates your Purchase Order for the visit, and if you fail to do this it will delay invoice approval)\n- If any issues require escalation (e.g. client changing the scope of work, missing equipment or login details).\n- When you are ready to leave site and have your completed signoff sheets, signed by the client (not AFTER you have left site).\n\nIf there is no phone signal, it is your responsibility to ask for access to a telephone or Wi-Fi so that you can alert your Bluekong contact. In extreme cases it may be necessary for you to tell the site contact that you need to get to a location with signal so that you can call into the office.\n\nYou must have a completed sign off form in order to be paid for any works. You must not leave a client site until a member of the Bluekong delivery team has authorised you to do so.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T09:00","end":"2026-10-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":11.010829638096038},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"