{"job":{"id":20214957,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":" Fiber  Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Cisco Meraki Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294164 / 05294062","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p><p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed on your phone and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p><ul><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li><li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>and its reason.</li><li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li><li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li></ul><p><strong>Title: Fiber </strong> Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Cisco Meraki Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294164 / 05294062</p><p><strong>Type of Work:</strong> Fiber</p><p><strong>Schedule:</strong> TBD</p><p><strong>Site Name &amp; Address:</strong> Spark Spring Lake Fayetteville NC, 103 Brook Lane, Spring Lake, NC 28390, USA</p><p><strong>WO / SA / Case:</strong> WO#: 00262449 / SA#: SA-294164 / Case#: 05294062</p><p><strong>Contact Details:</strong></p><p>Site POC: TBD, 910-436-1900</p><p>Engineer: TBD | TECHNET</p><p>Technician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><ul><li>Investigate intermittent connectivity caused by a flapping switch.</li><li>Locate and inspect switch <strong>HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05</strong>.</li><li>Verify switch power source, UPS condition, breakers, and electrical outlet functionality.</li><li>Test with an alternate power cord if available.</li><li>Determine whether the UPS is contributing to the switch flapping issue.</li><li>Verify MDF and IDF connectivity.</li><li>Inspect and test Ethernet patch cables.</li><li>Inspect fiber connections and verify proper light levels/continuity.</li><li>Test spare SFP modules as needed.</li><li>Test spare Ethernet or fiber cabling where applicable.</li><li>Provide console access/session for remote support if requested.</li><li>If issue persists, coordinate with Meraki Support for further investigation and potential hardware replacement.</li><li>Document root cause findings, troubleshooting steps performed, and impact to service.</li><li>Device Information:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Asset Name: HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Model: Cisco Meraki MS350-24P</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Serial Number: Q2WP-7PNP-75FL</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">MAC Address: 9C:E3:30:EF:79:54</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">IP Address: 192.168.0.6</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Parent Device: HLT-FAYSR-425-MDF-CS01</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Port Mapping: Port 6</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Location: 2nd Floor</li><li>Provide photos of the switch, UPS, cabling, SFPs, and overall rack environment.</li><li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li></ul><p><strong>Asset &amp; Location:</strong> HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05 (Cisco Meraki MS350-24P) – 2nd Floor</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</li><li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li><li>Ethernet adapter</li><li>Ethernet cable</li><li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li><li>Cellphone with camera</li><li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)</li><li>Tone generator</li><li>Console cable and USB adapter</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Crimper</li><li>RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Voltage tester</li><li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li><li>SFP modules</li><li>Ethernet patch cables</li><li>Spare cabling</li><li>Fiber tester</li><li>Laser to verify light continuity</li><li>Fiber cleaning kit</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed on your phone and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to **specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\n**Title: Fiber**  Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Flapping Cisco Meraki Switch – Spring Lake, NC | 00262449 / SA-294164 / 05294062\n\n**Type of Work:** Fiber\n\n**Schedule:** TBD\n\n**Site Name & Address:** Spark Spring Lake Fayetteville NC, 103 Brook Lane, Spring Lake, NC 28390, USA\n\n**WO / SA / Case:** WO#: 00262449 / SA#: SA-294164 / Case#: 05294062\n\n**Contact Details:**\n\nSite POC: TBD, 910-436-1900\n\nEngineer: TBD | TECHNET\n\nTechnician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Investigate intermittent connectivity caused by a flapping switch.\n- Locate and inspect switch **HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05**.\n- Verify switch power source, UPS condition, breakers, and electrical outlet functionality.\n- Test with an alternate power cord if available.\n- Determine whether the UPS is contributing to the switch flapping issue.\n- Verify MDF and IDF connectivity.\n- Inspect and test Ethernet patch cables.\n- Inspect fiber connections and verify proper light levels/continuity.\n- Test spare SFP modules as needed.\n- Test spare Ethernet or fiber cabling where applicable.\n- Provide console access/session for remote support if requested.\n- If issue persists, coordinate with Meraki Support for further investigation and potential hardware replacement.\n- Document root cause findings, troubleshooting steps performed, and impact to service.\n- Device Information:\n- Asset Name: HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05\n- Model: Cisco Meraki MS350-24P\n- Serial Number: Q2WP-7PNP-75FL\n- MAC Address: 9C:E3:30:EF:79:54\n- IP Address: 192.168.0.6\n- Parent Device: HLT-FAYSR-425-MDF-CS01\n- Port Mapping: Port 6\n- Location: 2nd Floor\n- Provide photos of the switch, UPS, cabling, SFPs, and overall rack environment.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset & Location:** HLT-FAYSR-350-IDF03-AS05 (Cisco Meraki MS350-24P) – 2nd Floor\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- SFP modules\n- Ethernet patch cables\n- Spare cabling\n- Fiber tester\n- Laser to verify light continuity\n- Fiber cleaning kit","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T12:00","end":"2026-10-21T16:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":50.41857574694509},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":260,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":80,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"am