{"job":{"id":20215184,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pilot Services","title":"T/S Jack for phone","description":{"html":"CALL INTO DISPATCH UPON ARRIVAL/DEPARTURE AT 888-745-6898 OPT 2. <br/><br/>Reference number: <br/><br/>Please arrive 5-10 mins early. If checking in before 7am or checking out after 6pm CT please dial \"0\" to be transferred to the on-call person.<br/><br/>DATE: 10/27/2026 11:00 AM *(I am flexible with date and time - what ever works with your scheduled)<br/><br/>1. SCOPE:<br/><br/>Troubleshoot non-working jack/cabling for VoIP phone. Site contact advised that jacks were recently replaced in building, so it's possible that this jack/run was not terminated to the Meraki switch (jack does not currently provide PoE or connectivity). <br/><br/>Phone registers to ext and works when plugged into other jack.<br/><br/>POC Kristin Hoell<br/>IT Suppory Steve Dorsey 215-826-2927<br/><br/>2. DELIVERABLES:  Photos are needed before/after completed work upload photos on the platform<br/><br/>- Photos of before/after completed work<br/>- Description of the work that was completed including name of ENG and LCON<br/>- Materials used<br/>- Signed work order<br/><br/>3. REQUIRED STANDARD TOOLS: Butt set, toner, basic hand tools, crimpers, laptop, 300ft CAT6, 8ft ladder, jacks, loopback cable and Cisco console cable<br/><br/><br/>Tech must get pre-approval PRIOR TO DOING ANY WORK OUTSIDE OF ABOVE LISTED SCOPE.<br/><br/>By accepting this ticket, it is the expectation of Pilot GT, the work will be completed by the resources accepting the ticket, not a party working on their behalf.<br/><br/><br/><br/><br/>PILOT Global Technologies <br/>1891 Bay Scott Cir, STE 109<br/>Naperville, IL 60540<br/>PHONE: 888-745-6898<br/><br/>EMAIL: <br/>SERVICE@pilotgt.com<br/>BILLING@PILOTGT.COM - All invoices must include the service address, service date(s), and our work order (PO) number. For toll reimbursement, please provide a receipt or screenshot that clearly shows the toll charge along with the date and time of the transaction.","markdown":"CALL INTO DISPATCH UPON ARRIVAL/DEPARTURE AT 888-745-6898 OPT 2.   \n  \nReference number:   \n  \nPlease arrive 5-10 mins early. If checking in before 7am or checking out after 6pm CT please dial \"0\" to be transferred to the on-call person.  \n  \nDATE: 10/27/2026 11:00 AM \\*(I am flexible with date and time - what ever works with your scheduled)  \n  \n1\\. SCOPE:  \n  \nTroubleshoot non-working jack/cabling for VoIP phone. Site contact advised that jacks were recently replaced in building, so it's possible that this jack/run was not terminated to the Meraki switch (jack does not currently provide PoE or connectivity).   \n  \nPhone registers to ext and works when plugged into other jack.  \n  \nPOC Kristin Hoell  \nIT Suppory Steve Dorsey 215-826-2927  \n  \n2\\. DELIVERABLES: Photos are needed before/after completed work upload photos on the platform  \n  \n\\- Photos of before/after completed work  \n\\- Description of the work that was completed including name of ENG and LCON  \n\\- Materials used  \n\\- Signed work order  \n  \n3\\. REQUIRED STANDARD TOOLS: Butt set, toner, basic hand tools, crimpers, laptop, 300ft CAT6, 8ft ladder, jacks, loopback cable and Cisco console cable  \n  \n  \nTech must get pre-approval PRIOR TO DOING ANY WORK OUTSIDE OF ABOVE LISTED SCOPE.  \n  \nBy accepting this ticket, it is the expectation of Pilot GT, the work will be completed by the resources accepting the ticket, not a party working on their behalf.  \n  \n  \n  \n  \nPILOT Global Technologies   \n1891 Bay Scott Cir, STE 109  \nNaperville, IL 60540  \nPHONE: 888-745-6898  \n  \nEMAIL:   \nSERVICE@pilotgt.com  \nBILLING@PILOTGT.COM - All invoices must include the service address, service date(s), and our work order (PO) number. For toll reimbursement, please provide a receipt or screenshot that clearly shows the toll charge along with the date and time of the transaction.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T11:00","end":"2026-10-27T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57.01482342016177},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792588127845}
{"job":{"id":20215208,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ReSource Point of Sale LLC","title":"Troubleshoot/Repair DT Pack Monitor  - Bojangles #1109","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the POS Support Helpdesk.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>**If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite**</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>**TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED, <u>PRIOR</u> TO ASSIGNMENT OR IT WILL BE SUBJECT TO DENIAL**</em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>STEP 1) COMMUNICATE ETA W/MGR ON DUTY:</u></strong>&nbsp;Contact the store Manager ASAP&nbsp;to introduce yourself as the Tech and confirm your ETA is okay with them (VERY IMPORTANT). Once this is done, please submit the Managers name that acknowledged this in the Field Nation notes/messages for documentation purposes.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>STEP 2) DESCRIPTION FROM HELPDESK:</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE SEE ATTACHED NETWORK DIAGRAM BEFORE CALLING HELPDESK! <strong><u>Bad parts are to be boxed up, and the return label attached to the box. This is important for POS terminals, Verifones, and Verifone COMM blocks.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Call Description: Customer called in reporting that their DT pack is just showing the config screen and not connecting to the network(10.1.1.212). Jose has approved a tech onsite.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em>**When troubleshooting / replacing a Verifone, the techs need to remove the bracket shown in \"Client Documents\" from the old device and attach it to the replacement. Please ensure to do this for the Verifone to be properly installed. ALSO, if unable to fix the issue for a DT Verifone, temp swap another pinpad to get Drive Thru working.**</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>**IF THIS IS A CONTROLLER REPLACEMENT AND THE IMAGE IS NOT COMING UP, PRESS 'REDRAW' AND THE IMAGE SHOULD POP UP**</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If this is a Grill Printer Issue:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Step 1. Replace with a working printer in the store</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If that resolved it, request a new printer. If not, go to step 2.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Step 2. Take a working printer with receipt printer cable (confirmed to be working) and plug short cable directly into port on register.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If printer prints, we know the port on the register is good and go to Step 3. If it didn’t print, go to step 2A.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Step 2A. Request a new register. The port on register appears to be bad.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Step 3. Request replacement cables and adapters.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Need to know what type of registers are being used to send correct cables and adapters.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Bad Parts:</u></strong></p>\n<p>**DO NOT LEAVE BAD PARTS ONSITE, IF PART SHIPPED BY RPOS**</p>\n<p>Bad parts are to be returned properly by the technician. If unsure what to do with the bad parts or missing a return label, please reach out to RPOS Dispatch BEFORE leaving the site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Requested Materials/Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Basic hand tools.</p>\n<p>CAT5e cable tester, and cable toner for locating cables that are not labeled.</p>\n<p>CAT5e cable (riser cable is fine).</p>\n<p>RJ45 crimper and punch down tool.</p>\n<p>RJ45 Male, and RJ45 Keystone jacks.</p>\n<p>Zip Ties.</p>\n<p>The ability to terminate cabling, punch down keystones, and locate cables is required.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>​<strong><u>Helpdesk Contact Information:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Checkout with Xenial Helpdesk @ 800-253-8664</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Fix Rates Standard Information:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Rates are fixed and cover travel time/mileage as well as work time onsite. Any requests for travel after assigned will be denied, no exceptions.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Counter offers are entertained, but preference will be given to technicians in our Talent Pool.&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the POS Support Helpdesk.**\n\n***\\*\\*If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite\\*\\****\n\n***\\*\\*TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED, PRIOR TO ASSIGNMENT OR IT WILL BE SUBJECT TO DENIAL\\*\\****\n\n**STEP 1) COMMUNICATE ETA W/MGR ON DUTY:** Contact the store Manager ASAP to introduce yourself as the Tech and confirm your ETA is okay with them (VERY IMPORTANT). Once this is done, please submit the Managers name that acknowledged this in the Field Nation notes/messages for documentation purposes.\n\n**STEP 2) DESCRIPTION FROM HELPDESK:** PLEASE SEE ATTACHED NETWORK DIAGRAM BEFORE CALLING HELPDESK! **Bad parts are to be boxed up, and the return label attached to the box. This is important for POS terminals, Verifones, and Verifone COMM blocks.**\n\nCall Description: Customer called in reporting that their DT pack is just showing the config screen and not connecting to the network(10.1.1.212). Jose has approved a tech onsite.\n\n***\\*\\*When troubleshooting / replacing a Verifone, the techs need to remove the bracket shown in \"Client Documents\" from the old device and attach it to the replacement. Please ensure to do this for the Verifone to be properly installed. ALSO, if unable to fix the issue for a DT Verifone, temp swap another pinpad to get Drive Thru working.\\*\\****\n\n***\\*\\*IF THIS IS A CONTROLLER REPLACEMENT AND THE IMAGE IS NOT COMING UP, PRESS 'REDRAW' AND THE IMAGE SHOULD POP UP\\*\\****\n\n- If this is a Grill Printer Issue:\n- Step 1. Replace with a working printer in the store\n- If that resolved it, request a new printer. If not, go to step 2.\n- Step 2. Take a working printer with receipt printer cable (confirmed to be working) and plug short cable directly into port on register.\n- If printer prints, we know the port on the register is good and go to Step 3. If it didn’t print, go to step 2A.\n- Step 2A. Request a new register. The port on register appears to be bad.\n- Step 3. Request replacement cables and adapters.\n- Need to know what type of registers are being used to send correct cables and adapters.\n\n**Bad Parts:**\n\n\\*\\*DO NOT LEAVE BAD PARTS ONSITE, IF PART SHIPPED BY RPOS\\*\\*\n\nBad parts are to be returned properly by the technician. If unsure what to do with the bad parts or missing a return label, please reach out to RPOS Dispatch BEFORE leaving the site.\n\n**Requested Materials/Tools:**\n\nBasic hand tools.\n\nCAT5e cable tester, and cable toner for locating cables that are not labeled.\n\nCAT5e cable (riser cable is fine).\n\nRJ45 crimper and punch down tool.\n\nRJ45 Male, and RJ45 Keystone jacks.\n\nZip Ties.\n\nThe ability to terminate cabling, punch down keystones, and locate cables is required.\n\n​**Helpdesk Contact Information:**\n\nCheckout with Xenial Helpdesk @ 800-253-8664\n\n**Fix Rates Standard Information:**\n\nRates are fixed and cover travel time/mileage as well as work time onsite. Any requests for travel after assigned will be denied, no exceptions.\n\nCounter offers are entertained, but preference will be given to technicians in our Talent Pool.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T10:00","end":"2026-10-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":95},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":25.291618173230717},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792588174912}
{"job":{"id":"8368010575","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"ASAP IT Resource Group","title":"Commercial Starlink Survey","description":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>We are a Professional Dish Installation Company for DISH Network, DIRECTV, HughesNet, Viasat and StarLink and only work with experienced Dish Antenna / Starlink Installers. These are commercial rooftop installations so if heights is an issue please don't request this ticket.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>I need to get a rooftop survey done. Need to know if a lift is needed, if there is a view without obstructions, where we can mount and how we need to mount being a sled or J-Mount and is there an existing penetration we can use with a cable path that get us to the endpoint. Need photos of the MDF and potential areas to mount the equipment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Provider must have WhatsApp on their phone and be willing to use it to communicate with the NOC.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Provider must also have the Starlink App to run the Obstruction Test.</strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":53.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792588380663}
{"job":{"id":"4319951565","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"trinity Modular Building","description":"Survey Epik Wizard:<br><br>Contact Project Manager Scott Houston for instructions and support if you have any Questions 7143503455<br><br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1.TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2.Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3.Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the Survey, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>4.Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>5.Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>6.Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br><br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotsp