{"job":{"id":"8991601751","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"06051947 - Brunswich County 100 Tobacco Street EPIK Survey and Install","description":"SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON) 1. Watch Epik install Video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo<br>2. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>3. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or are unclear on instruction before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK install Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the install process. Please use Google Chrome to prevent issues.<br>4. Review the SOW and install guide before starting the install.<br>A. Complete survey for analog to LTE conversion using the attached survey form &amp; submit deliverables to TC team<br>a. Be sure to include details below:<br>i. Telephone Numbers (TNs) on site (Fire, Security, Elevator, Fax, Voice, Intercom, Gate, etc.)<br>ii. Presence of customer network (broadband modem, routers, etc.)<br>1. Distance between proposed EPIK install location to network switch with port availability<br>iii. Location of MPOE or DMARC<br>iv. LTE coverage &amp; speed test – Verizon preferred with T-Mobile as secondary<br>v. Backboard Space (2x2 required), AC Power Availability (Outlet, PDU, UPS).<br>1. If no AC power within 5 ft of proposed install location, denote the length to nearest electrical outlet<br>2. If no room on existing Backboard, note proposed location for EPIK device installation and distance to current Cross Connect field for EPIK and cabling connections<br>vi. Identify location and Make/Model of existing Modem, Firewall, Fire Alarm Panel, Security Alarm Panel, Elevators, and record the monitoring company contact information<br>B. Locate the following Granite-provided Equipment: EPIK Router(s) and any additional accessories.<br>a. Install EPIK router and accessories per site survey results and Installation Guide<br>b. Connect to customers switch on site (if approved) per site survey results<br>C. Connect to Customer Wired network<br>a. Power on Epik Edge<br>b. Use butt-set to confirm dial tone on 66 block (first 4 or 8 pairs on 66 Block)<br>c. Contact Epik Technical Coordination team to confirm EPIK Edge is online in MyEpik and to take RSSI reading<br>d. Prewire lines to cross connect points as described on work order (TNs to be wired)<br>e. If pre-existing wiring is in use, DO NOT disconnect existing equipment without first being instructed to by the Greenix flow, or an Epik Activations rep (do not perform cross connections before instructed)<br>D. After installation is complete, Submit required deliverables to WorkMarket and Check out on WorkMarket<br>E. Before departure check out with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team to review deliverables at: 833-479-4768<br>Materials/Tools Required:<br>Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), Cross-Connect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":78.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":19