{"job":{"id":20216442,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"AP INSTALLATION / 2 TECHS NEEDED **MUST BE LIFT CERTIFIED**","description":{"html":"<p><strong>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>TECH MUST DIAL INTO THE BRIDGE AS SOON AS THEY ARRIVE ONSITE. THE BRIDGE WILL PROVIDE ALL DIRECTION ON THE SCOPE OF WORK AND HOW THEY WANT EVERYTHING DONE. NOTE: When you initially join the bridge there may not be anyone on the bridge. They will join once you enter the incident # into the chat. That alerts them someone is on the bridge waiting for them.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dial into Bridge:&nbsp;</strong>https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_N2UzODYwZTctYzFiYy00MzhlLThlZDAtNzVkNDY1MjNjY2Rl%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%22d7bf8bae-4d7e-479c-bde4-1103d9e4136c%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%2289d1fb02-ea0d-44b1-a257-c0287a3497e2%22%7d</p>\n<p><strong>Once on bridge</strong>, type Reference number into the bridge chat ( ) - The appropriate support person should join shortly after INC# is entered into chat.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Access Point Installation</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Swap Fortinet AP to Mist AP27 in office area.</li>\n<li>Swap Fortinet AP and remount it with Mist AP45 from wall to ceiling in shop area.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Will require conduit to drop AP down to between 22-26 feet from floor</li>\n<li>Run cable and install new AP63E in the pressure area with Omni antenna to cover the parking on their right side and the shop on the left side.</li>\n<li>See material list. Tech will be reimbursed for material</li>\n<li>Hourly rate is for 2 techs up to 12 hours each</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>GCC will help with configuration and testing</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</p>\n<p>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Conduit 25'</strong></li>\n<li><strong>2 AP brackets for conduit mount</strong></li>\n<li><strong>(1) box of CAT6 Cable (at least 750')</strong></li>\n<li><strong>6 RJ45's</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Laptop:</strong>&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(8'-10' ladder)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n***TECH MUST DIAL INTO THE BRIDGE AS SOON AS THEY ARRIVE ONSITE. THE BRIDGE WILL PROVIDE ALL DIRECTION ON THE SCOPE OF WORK AND HOW THEY WANT EVERYTHING DONE. NOTE: When you initially join the bridge there may not be anyone on the bridge. They will join once you enter the incident # into the chat. That alerts them someone is on the bridge waiting for them.***\n\n**Dial into Bridge:** https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_N2UzODYwZTctYzFiYy00MzhlLThlZDAtNzVkNDY1MjNjY2Rl%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%22d7bf8bae-4d7e-479c-bde4-1103d9e4136c%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%2289d1fb02-ea0d-44b1-a257-c0287a3497e2%22%7d\n\n**Once on bridge**, type Reference number into the bridge chat ( ) - The appropriate support person should join shortly after INC# is entered into chat.\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Access Point Installation**\n\n- Swap Fortinet AP to Mist AP27 in office area.\n- Swap Fortinet AP and remount it with Mist AP45 from wall to ceiling in shop area.\n- Will require conduit to drop AP down to between 22-26 feet from floor\n- Run cable and install new AP63E in the pressure area with Omni antenna to cover the parking on their right side and the shop on the left side.\n- See material list. Tech will be reimbursed for material\n- Hourly rate is for 2 techs up to 12 hours each\n\n- GCC will help with configuration and testing\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nPlease ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.\n\nThe technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- **Conduit 25'**\n- **2 AP brackets for conduit mount**\n- **(1) box of CAT6 Cable (at least 750')**\n- **6 RJ45's**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T08:00","end":"2026-11-04T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":1200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":12,"distance":102.63496823320469},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 102.63496823320469mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792594684707}
