pliers</li><li>Any additional tools as may be required based on the individual work order details (such as printer models requiring torque screwdrivers, etc)</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>Review ticket description for case-specific requirements and instructions</li><li>Confirm arrival time and site contact information</li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent <strong>Logista Solutions</strong> while onsite</li><li>Perform required maintenance, repairs, or service on HP printers and MFD/MFP devices</li><li>Upon installation of the maintenance kit(s), make sure the maintenance counters are reset for the component(s) installed. Some kits should auto reset, some will need to be manually reset. It's your job to research this before leaving site.</li><li>Complete hardware and software changes as specified in work order</li><li>Test equipment functionality upon completion</li><li>Ensure the customer representative also tests the functionality prior to considering the task complete</li><li><strong>Call Contact in Confidential Information to ensure the printer is visible in the monitoring system</strong></li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>Print an independent event log; To print an HP event log, access your printer's control panel, navigate to the Diagnostics or Troubleshooting menu, select Print Event Log, and then press the appropriate button (like \"Check Mark\" or \"OK\") to print the report. For some models, you may need to first navigate to the Information menu or find a Support Tools option.&nbsp;</li><li>Print status pages from serviced devices, these status page should confirm the printer recognized the new kit(s) just installed into the printer.</li><li>Print samples demonstrating proper functionality</li><li>Check-out of work order with completion confirmation</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, contact our call center personnel immediately</li><li>Any technical issues or questions should be escalated through our support team (see contacts in the Confidential Information section)</li><li>A dedicated technician will be assigned to work directly with you if complex issues arise</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Additional hours &amp; Expenses must be pre-approved by work order manager.</li></ul>","markdown":"Model HP M636. Serial number MXBCR68019.\n\nFuser is making lines on printed copies.\n\nFuser maintenance kit (PN J8J7A) shipped to site on FedEx tracking below.\n\n547328474602\n\nDelivered 10/21/26\n\nSigned for by: K.Rosario\n\nNeed tech onsite to install part and diagnose for any further issues.\n\nPlease call remote support listed in confidential section before leaving site.\n\nPlease call Michael Wilson at 662-570-4341 with any questions or issues.\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in HP print devices, including hardware and software troubleshooting\n- Should do online research that reviews the scope of work before arriving onsite, Google and YouTube are good sources.\n- Should get status pages before and after the kit installation.\n- Check and assure the maintenance counter(s) correctly reset.\n- Should also evaluate the condition of the rest of the printer, advise of any potential issues.\n- Make sure printer has all excess dust/debris cleaned before considering the job completed.\n- **Call Provided Contact prior to leaving the site to ensure printer is visible in the monitoring system**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business Casual attire required\n- Professional appearance representing our company standards\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Basic tool kit with variety of screwdrivers\n- Picks and precision tools\n- Tweezers/narrow tip pliers\n- Any additional tools as may be required based on the individual work order details (such as printer models requiring torque screwdrivers, etc)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Review ticket description for case-specific requirements and instructions\n2. Confirm arrival time and site contact information\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent **Logista Solutions** while onsite\n2. Perform required maintenance, repairs, or service on HP printers and MFD/MFP devices\n3. Upon installation of the maintenance kit(s), make sure the maintenance counters are reset for the component(s) installed. Some kits should auto reset, some will need to be manually reset. It's your job to research this before leaving site.\n4. Complete hardware and software changes as specified in work order\n5. Test equipment functionality upon completion\n6. Ensure the customer representative also tests the functionality prior to considering the task complete\n7. **Call Contact in Confidential Information to ensure the printer is visible in the monitoring system**\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Print an independent event log; To print an HP event log, access your printer's control panel, navigate to the Diagnostics or Troubleshooting menu, select Print Event Log, and then press the appropriate button (like \"Check Mark\" or \"OK\") to print the report. For some models, you may need to first navigate to the Information menu or find a Support Tools option.\n2. Print status pages from serviced devices, these status page should confirm the printer recognized the new kit(s) just installed into the printer.\n3. Print samples demonstrating proper functionality\n4. Check-out of work order with completion confirmation\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, contact our call center personnel immediately\n- Any technical issues or questions should be escalated through our support team (see contacts in the Confidential Information section)\n- A dedicated technician will be assigned to work directly with you if complex issues arise\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Additional hours & Expenses must be pre-approved by work order manager.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00","end":"2026-10-22T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":58.99651561633372},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $100) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Nothing"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fair festival"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"