{"job":{"id":"6207143765","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Kinettix","title":"Router Refresh| HARDSTAR TIME","description":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>The technician will perform a site survey, prepare the new Verizon router, coordinate the router cutover with Verizon, validate connectivity after installation, document the completed work, and package designated equipment for return.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Main Technician Responsibilities</strong>:</p><ul><li>Coordinate with the bank manager for branch closing time and collect any EOL phones.</li><li>Take photos of the old router before making changes.</li><li>Mount the new router either on the rack using brackets/screws or place it safely on a flat surface if no rack is available.</li><li>Install antennas, connect power, and confirm the router powers on.</li><li>Join the Webex meeting and notify Verizon once the router is powered up.</li><li>If needed, console into the router using a console cable and PuTTY for Verizon troubleshooting.</li><li>After the branch closes, move the WAN and LAN cables from the old router to the new router as instructed by Verizon.</li><li>Test desk phone connectivity and connect to 5/3 Guest Wi-Fi to confirm service is working.</li><li>Remove and box the old router, including any EOL phones.</li><li>Take required photos: before, both routers, and after installation.</li><li>Send it to the Kinettix Coordinator.</li><li>Complete the site completion form.</li><li>Place the paperwork in the return box, attach the return label, and leave it for UPS pickup.</li><li>Before leaving, call BSOC to notify them that the work is complete and the technician is leaving.</li></ul><p>Important Notes:</p><ul><li>Work appears to occur before and after branch closing, with cable migration happening after the bank closes.</li><li>Technician must remain onsite until Verizon confirms the router is working.</li><li>Calling BSOC before leaving is required to avoid triggering an alarm respo