{"job":{"id":"3367137287","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Kinettix","title":"Router Refresh| HARDSTART TIME","description":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>The technician will perform a site survey, prepare the new Verizon router, coordinate the router cutover with Verizon, validate connectivity after installation, document the completed work, and package designated equipment for return.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Main Technician Responsibilities</strong>:</p><ul><li>Coordinate with the bank manager for branch closing time and collect any EOL phones.</li><li>Take photos of the old router before making changes.</li><li>Mount the new router either on the rack using brackets/screws or place it safely on a flat surface if no rack is available.</li><li>Install antennas, connect power, and confirm the router powers on.</li><li>Join the Webex meeting and notify Verizon once the router is powered up.</li><li>If needed, console into the router using a console cable and PuTTY for Verizon troubleshooting.</li><li>After the branch closes, move the WAN and LAN cables from the old router to the new router as instructed by Verizon.</li><li>Test desk phone connectivity and connect to 5/3 Guest Wi-Fi to confirm service is working.</li><li>Remove and box the old router, including any EOL phones.</li><li>Take required photos: before, both routers, and after installation.</li><li>Send it to the Kinettix Coordinator.</li><li>Complete the site completion form.</li><li>Place the paperwork in the return box, attach the return label, and leave it for UPS pickup.</li><li>Before leaving, call BSOC to notify them that the work is complete and the technician is leaving.</li></ul><p>Important Notes:</p><ul><li>Work appears to occur before and after branch closing, with cable migration happening after the bank closes.</li><li>Technician must remain onsite until Verizon confirms the router is working.</li><li>Calling BSOC before leaving is required to avoid triggering an alarm response.</li><li>Return shipment preparation is part of the closeout process.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools needed:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>PuTTY installed and ready for use</li><li>Console cable</li><li>Cell phone capable of taking clear photos/screenshots</li><li>WebEx available on the laptop for the scheduled Verizon coordination session&nbsp;</li><li>Networking Tools</li><li>Basic Tools</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T15:30","end":"2026-10-29T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":18.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"202