{"job":{"id":20216732,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ServiceP (PreferredTechs)","title":"Site Survey - Digital Signage - (13) - 10.1\" Bluefins , (12)-21.5\" Bluefins  (4) - 50\" Displays  (1) 32\"Display ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>MANDATORY</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Once you arrive on site and are ready to start work, please call or text (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check in. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the site contact and begin work</li>\n<li>Complete troubleshoot/installation.&nbsp;Contact support with any issues or concerns so work is completed correctly and fully.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Complete required deliverables (see below) and call support to confirm you have completed the full SOW.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Text signed WO</u></strong>&nbsp;to (507-400-3227 and 720-515-5551)</li>\n<li><strong>REQUIRED</strong>: Call (507-400-3227) to check out providing detailed notes of installation and any delays/issues. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tech is needed to do a site survey for an upcoming install.</strong></p>\n<p>Complete an onsite site readiness walkthrough for the upcoming<del>********</del> digital signage installation.</p>\n<p>The project includes 30 signage locations consisting of Bluefin room signs and larger SoC displays.</p>\n<p>Please walk the planned signage locations with the property representative and document the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm each planned signage location can be identified and accessed.</li>\n<li>Verify wall type and overall wall condition at each location.</li>\n<li>Document existing mounting conditions and any areas requiring repair or preparation before installation.</li>\n<li>Verify power availability at each signage location.</li>\n<li>Verify whether a network/data drop is present at each planned signage location.</li>\n<li>Where a live data drop is available, test the connection with a laptop or suitable network testing device to confirm the port is active and has internet connectivity.</li>\n<li>Confirm whether DHCP addressing is received where network connectivity is available.</li>\n<li>Document any ports that are inactive, unavailable, or require additional cabling.</li>\n<li>Record visible data-port labels where available to help the property/IT team identify the associated network room or switch.</li>\n<li>Identify locations requiring new low-voltage cabling or other site preparation.</li>\n<li>Review available space/conditions for PoE equipment associated with the Bluefin room signs.</li>\n<li>Document any access, mounting, power, cabling, or other physical conditions that could affect installation.</li>\n<li>Take clear photos of each signage location and any identified readiness concerns.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Network Notes:</strong></p>\n<p>The property is coordinating network configuration separately with Concord IT/Sonifi. Sonifi has advised that <del>********</del>Digital Signage VLAN 810 is not currently configured and that data connectivity to the new signage locations still needs to be addressed.</p>\n<p>Sonifi has confirmed that DHCP is normally enabled on this network and that MAC-address whitelisting is not required.</p>\n<p>Please test any existing/live network drops during the walkthrough where possible and document the results. No VLAN configuration or other network changes are requested as part of this visit.</p>\n<p>The purpose of this visit is to verify and document the physical site conditions, test available connectivity, and identify any remaining preparation required before installation. Internal site-readiness guidance specifically calls for live network connections to be tested before installation.<del>*********</del>-Bistro-Instructions</p>\n<p><strong>Carefully open the enclosure boxes and ensure they are not damaged.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Work order is for a site survey to view each of the following locations to verify they are ready for install. Survey each location and determine what is needed to complete the install and confirm there is data and power in place. Inform Mario of any issues or possible delays that you may encounter.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site survey needed on the following (complete site survey form):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pictures of inventory, making sure all equipment on site</li>\n<li>Tech will need to open a couple boxes of the enclosures to verify what screws were sent as some shipments were missing the screws to connect the display to the enclosure mount.</li>\n<li>Take pictures of each piece of hardware for the enclosures.</li>\n<li>Pictures of the signage install locations showing they are ready for install showing they have data and power ready. (Manager will show you where they will want the signage installed)</li>\n<li>Test each jack to make sure they have connectivity.</li>\n<li>Pictures of IDF showing where the equipment will be patched in.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Visit each IDF where the cables for the screens go to (not just 1).</li>\n<li>Pictures of a open shelf or area to install the POEs (confirm if locations are getting POEs or there is power at each bluefin location)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>IF</strong> this site has existing displays, we will need to remove a couple of them to see what it looks like behind it. Take one of the displays and put up against the wall to make sure it covers the holes from the previous display. We need to verify what it looks like behind the enclosure to make sure the new display will cover everything.</p>\n<p><strong>Equipment list:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Equipment list:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>(13) 10.1\" Bluefin Room signs</li>\n<li>(12) 21.5\" Blufin Room signs</li>\n<li>(4) 50\" LG SoC displays</li>\n<li>(1) 32\" Samsung SoC display</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>*** Any delays <u>MUST</u> be reported. If we are on site waiting on customer or support for more than 1 hour it<u>MUST</u> be escalate to the ticket manager (Mario). Mario can be reach via call or text (see confidential info)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Basic Tools (screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, etc)</li>\n<li>Network Tester/Toner</li>\n<li>Copy of work order</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Work Attire</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long pants with no rips/tears</li>\n<li>Polo shirt</li>\n<li>Close toed shoes - No sandals</li>\n<li>No hats</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Required Pictures/Deliverables</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed work order with check in and out times along with customer signature</li>\n<li>Picture of each area showing they are ready for installation</li>\n<li>Any equipment missing from inventory</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Requested Deliverables:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clear photos of each planned signage location</li>\n<li>Results of network testing where live drops are available</li>\n<li>Identification of inactive/missing data drops</li>\n<li>Notes on power availability and wall/mounting conditions</li>\n<li>Summary of any outstanding site-readiness items or work required before installation</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**MANDATORY**:\n\n1. Once you arrive on site and are ready to start work, please call or text (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check in. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).\n2. Introduce yourself to the site contact and begin work\n3. Complete troubleshoot/installation. Contact support with any issues or concerns so work is completed correctly and fully.\n4. Complete required deliverables (see below) and call support to confirm you have completed the full SOW.\n5. **Text signed WO** to (507-400-3227 and 720-515-5551)\n6. **REQUIRED**: Call (507-400-3227) to check out providing detailed notes of installation and any delays/issues. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Tech is needed to do a site survey for an upcoming install.**\n\nComplete an onsite site readiness walkthrough for the upcoming\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* digital signage installation.\n\nThe project includes 30 signage locations consisting of Bluefin room signs and larger SoC displays.\n\nPlease walk the planned signage locations with the property representative and document the following:\n\n- Confirm each planned signage location can be identified and accessed.\n- Verify wall type and overall wall condition at each location.\n- Document existing mounting conditions and any areas requiring repair or preparation before installation.\n- Verify power availability at each signage location.\n- Verify whether a network/data drop is present at each planned signage location.\n- Where a live data drop is available, test the connection with a laptop or suitable network testing device to confirm the port is active and has internet connectivity.\n- Confirm whether DHCP addressing is received where network connectivity is available.\n- Document any ports that are inactive, unavailable, or require additional cabling.\n- Record visible data-port labels where available to help the property/IT team identify the associated network room or switch.\n- Identify locations requiring new low-voltage cabling or other site preparation.\n- Review available space/conditions for PoE equipment associated with the Bluefin room signs.\n- Document any access, mounting, power, cabling, or other physical conditions that could affect installation.\n- Take clear photos of each signage location and any identified readiness concerns.\n\n**Network Notes:**\n\nThe property is coordinating network configuration separately with Concord IT/Sonifi. Sonifi has advised that \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Digital Signage VLAN 810 is not currently configured and that data connectivity to the new signage locations still needs to be addressed.\n\nSonifi has confirmed that DHCP is normally enabled on this network and that MAC-address whitelisting is not required.\n\nPlease test any existing/live network drops during the walkthrough where possible and document the results. No VLAN configuration or other network changes are requested as part of this visit.\n\nThe purpose of this visit is to verify and document the physical site conditions, test available connectivity, and identify any remaining preparation required before installation. Internal site-readiness guidance specifically calls for live network connections to be tested before installation.\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*-Bistro-Instructions\n\n**Carefully open the enclosure boxes and ensure they are not damaged.**\n\n**Work order is for a site survey to view each of the following locations to verify they are ready for install. Survey each location and determine what is needed to complete the install and confirm there is data and power in place. Inform Mario of any issues or possible delays that you may encounter.**\n\n**Site survey needed on the following (complete site survey form):**\n\n1. Pictures of inventory, making sure all equipment on site\n2. Tech will need to open a couple boxes of the enclosures to verify what screws were sent as some shipments were missing the screws to connect the display to the enclosure mount.\n3. Take pictures of each piece of hardware for the enclosures.\n4. Pictures of the signage install locations showing they are ready for install showing they have data and power ready. (Manager will show you where they will want the signage installed)\n5. Test each jack to make sure they have connectivity.\n6. Pictures of IDF showing where the equipment will be patched in.\n7. Visit each IDF where the cables for the screens go to (not just 1).\n8. Pictures of a open shelf or area to install the POEs (confirm if locations are getting POEs or there is power at each bluefin location)\n\n**IF** this site has existing displays, we will need to remove a couple of them to see what it looks like behind it. Take one of the displays and put up against the wall to make sure it covers the holes from the previous display. We need to verify what it looks like behind the enclosure to make sure the new display will cover everything.\n\n**Equipment list:**\n\n**Equipment list:**\n\n- (13) 10.1\" Bluefin Room signs\n- (12) 21.5\" Blufin Room signs\n- (4) 50\" LG SoC displays\n- (1) 32\" Samsung SoC display\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Any delays MUST be reported. If we are on site waiting on customer or support for more than 1 hour itMUST be escalate to the ticket manager (Mario). Mario can be reach via call or text (see confidential info)**\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Basic Tools (screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, etc)\n- Network Tester/Toner\n- Copy of work order\n\n**Work Attire**\n\n- Long pants with no rips/tears\n- Polo shirt\n- Close toed shoes - No sandals\n- No hats\n\n**Required Pictures/Deliverables**\n\n- Signed work order with check in and out times along with customer signature\n- Picture of each area showing they are ready for installation\n- Any equipment missing from inventory\n\n**Requested Deliverables:**\n\n- Clear photos of each planned signage location\n- Results of network testing where live drops are available\n- Identification of inactive/missing data drops\n- Notes on power availability and wall/mounting conditions\n- Summary of any outstanding site-readiness items or work required before installation","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":100},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":55},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.39281055193066},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792605174316}
{"job":{"id":20219015,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Kohl's Replace Cash Drawer 81","description":{"html":"<p>SOW:</p>\n<p>Replace the cash drawer on Register #81 - SPECIFIC INSTRUCTIONS BELOW</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>The cash drawer is stuck in the register and has to be replaced.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Before arrival: Review the attached pictures before starting work. Bring basic hand tools and a drill/driver.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<p>1. Remove the removable wood panel above the cash drawer (Piece 14 in the diagram). It's held on by magnets. Put your finger in the half-circle cutout at the bottom of the panel and pull it straight toward you.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>2. With the panel off, find the 2 cash drawer bolt holes. The bolts screw down from the top into the cash drawer below.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>3. Remove both bolts and pull out the stuck cash drawer.</p>\n<p>4. Install the new cash drawer, line it up with the bolt holes, and reinstall both bolts from the top.</p>\n<p>5. Reconnect the drawer cable to the register and test that the drawer opens from the POS.</p>\n<p>6. Put Piece 14 back by lining it up and pressing it onto the magnets</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*****Tech MUST box up cash drawer, till and cable*****</p>\n<p>!!! REQUIREMENTS FOR JOB CHECK-IN AND TIME APROVAL HAVE BEEN UPDATED PlEASE READ !!!</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Tech must take pictures of POS devices in box prior to unpacking and attach pictures to work order. (Pictures can be emailed to dellservice@spencertech.com)</p>\n<p>-Tech must follow attached SOW guide</p>\n<p>-This work order requires tech to take a before and after photo of all surrounding cables pertaining to this scope of work. Tech MUST NOT leave the site until their Spencer Service agent approves their photos during check out. Tech MUST send photos to DellService@Spencertech.com The Request ID MUST be added to the subject line.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>It is required that you follow these guidelines while visiting a Kohl’s location:</p>\n<p>-Maintain a positive and respectful attitude towards the customer, fellow employees, contractors, and all others that you Interact with at all times.</p>\n<p>-Ensure that your appearance is neat, clean, and that you are properly dressed per the Spencer dress code.</p>\n<p>-All complaints are to be taken to the Spencer Field Manager away from the hearing of others.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>-Camera or Smart Phone to take before and after photos.</p>\n<p>-Cable testers</p>\n<p>-Spare patch cables/Ethernet cables</p>\n<p>-Basic tools (Screwdriver, Wire Cutters, Allen Wrenches)</p>\n<p>-Extra Keyboard and Mouse.</p>\n<p>-Consumables to Cable Manage (Zip-ties, Cable Ties, Twist ties, Label Maker)</p>\n<p>#4 Allen Wrench</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Checkin Requirements:</p>\n<p>-Head inside the store and check in at the Customer Service Desk (for New Stores, check in at the Welcome Desk at the main entrance).</p>\n<p>- Tech must retrieve replacement equipment from associate and provide the following during check in call.</p>\n<p>- Return Tracking provided in box with new device</p>\n<p>- Confirm Register # you will be working on</p>\n<p>-Provide INC# to store associate and fill out visitor log.</p>\n<p>-Tech must take photos of the Device and all the cables for the device before any work is done.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>While Onsite:</p>\n<p>--Tech must follow attached SOW guide</p>\n<p>-Tech is required to work with Kohls Team: 262-703-1515</p>\n<p>When dialing 262-703-1515, the following message is played:</p>\n<p>Thank you for reaching the Kohls team.</p>\n<p>Press 1 for store hardware issues.</p>\n<p>Press 2 for network-related issues.</p>\n<p>-Tech must perform all work detailed in SOW.</p>\n<p>-Take photos of the new installation to provide to Spencer upon checkout. Include all cable connections and cable management.</p>\n<p>- It is mandatory that ALL time exceeding the expected duration is approved by the Service team PRIOR to that time being</p>\n<p>Please call 844-464-1910 opt 2 as soon as you realize you may not be able to complete the scope of work in the allotted time and provide an update as to why and how much additional time would be needed.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Checkout Requirements:</p>\n<p>-Tech must check-out with the Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (844-464-1910, Opt 2)</p>\n<p>-Technician is required to send photos from the Job to Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (DellService@SpencerTech.com) The photos should Include all before and after photos for all cables and devices.</p>\n<p>-Technician must box up old equipment and provide it to the Manager on Duty.</p>\n<p>-Sign out at Kohl’s Customer Service Desk.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Deliverables:</p>\n<p>-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com; DellService@SpencerTech.com</p>\n<p>-Names of the Manager(s) and Support agents you talked with.</p>\n<p>-Photos of all cables and devices before work was done and after work was done.</p>\n<p>-Return tracking number of the returning part(s).</p>","markdown":"SOW:\n\nReplace the cash drawer on Register #81 - SPECIFIC INSTRUCTIONS BELOW\n\nThe cash drawer is stuck in the register and has to be replaced.\n\nBefore arrival: Review the attached pictures before starting work. Bring basic hand tools and a drill/driver.\n\nSteps:\n\n1\\. Remove the removable wood panel above the cash drawer (Piece 14 in the diagram). It's held on by magnets. Put your finger in the half-circle cutout at the bottom of the panel and pull it straight toward you.\n\n2\\. With the panel off, find the 2 cash drawer bolt holes. The bolts screw down from the top into the cash drawer below.\n\n3\\. Remove both bolts and pull out the stuck cash drawer.\n\n4\\. Install the new cash drawer, line it up with the bolt holes, and reinstall both bolts from the top.\n\n5\\. Reconnect the drawer cable to the register and test that the drawer opens from the POS.\n\n6\\. Put Piece 14 back by lining it up and pressing it onto the magnets\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Tech MUST box up cash drawer, till and cable\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n!!! REQUIREMENTS FOR JOB CHECK-IN AND TIME APROVAL HAVE BEEN UPDATED PlEASE READ !!!\n\n-Tech must take pictures of POS devices in box prior to unpacking and attach pictures to work order. (Pictures can be emailed to dellservice@spencertech.com)\n\n-Tech must follow attached SOW guide\n\n-This work order requires tech to take a before and after photo of all surrounding cables pertaining to this scope of work. Tech MUST NOT leave the site until their Spencer Service agent approves their photos during check out. Tech MUST send photos to DellService@Spencertech.com The Request ID MUST be added to the subject line.\n\nIt is required that you follow these guidelines while visiting a Kohl’s location:\n\n-Maintain a positive and respectful attitude towards the customer, fellow employees, contractors, and all others that you Interact with at all times.\n\n-Ensure that your appearance is neat, clean, and that you are properly dressed per the Spencer dress code.\n\n-All complaints are to be taken to the Spencer Field Manager away from the hearing of others.\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n-Camera or Smart Phone to take before and after photos.\n\n-Cable testers\n\n-Spare patch cables/Ethernet cables\n\n-Basic tools (Screwdriver, Wire Cutters, Allen Wrenches)\n\n-Extra Keyboard and Mouse.\n\n-Consumables to Cable Manage (Zip-ties, Cable Ties, Twist ties, Label Maker)\n\n\\#4 Allen Wrench\n\nCheckin Requirements:\n\n-Head inside the store and check in at the Customer Service Desk (for New Stores, check in at the Welcome Desk at the main entrance).\n\n\\- Tech must retrieve replacement equipment from associate and provide the following during check in call.\n\n\\- Return Tracking provided in box with new device\n\n\\- Confirm Register # you will be working on\n\n-Provide INC# to store associate and fill out visitor log.\n\n-Tech must take photos of the Device and all the cables for the device before any work is done.\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\nWhile Onsite:\n\n\\--Tech must follow attached SOW guide\n\n-Tech is required to work with Kohls Team: 262-703-1515\n\nWhen dialing 262-703-1515, the following message is played:\n\nThank you for reaching the Kohls team.\n\nPress 1 for store hardware issues.\n\nPress 2 for network-related issues.\n\n-Tech must perform all work detailed in SOW.\n\n-Take photos of the new installation to provide to Spencer upon checkout. Include all cable connections and cable management.\n\n\\- It is mandatory that ALL time exceeding the expected duration is approved by the Service team PRIOR to that time being\n\nPlease call 844-464-1910 opt 2 as soon as you realize you may not be able to complete the scope of work in the allotted time and provide an update as to why and how much additional time would be needed.\n\nCheckout Requirements:\n\n-Tech must check-out with the Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (844-464-1910, Opt 2)\n\n-Technician is required to send photos from the Job to Kohl’s Service Delivery Team (DellService@SpencerTech.com) The photos should Include all before and after photos for all cables and devices.\n\n-Technician must box up old equipment and provide it to the Manager on Duty.\n\n-Sign out at Kohl’s Customer Service Desk.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com; DellService@SpencerTech.com\n\n-Names of the Manager(s) and Support agents you talked with.\n\n-Photos of all cables and devices before work was done and after work was done.\n\n-Return tracking number of the returning part(s).","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T11:00","end":"2026-10-21T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.100948753812235},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/21/2026, 11:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Nothing"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fair festival"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792606593276}
{"job":{"id":20219174,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Connect New CKT to FortiGate firewall (possible DMARC extension survey)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME</u></em>&nbsp;(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>*** BRING A CISCO ROLLOVER CONSOLE CABLE + LAPTOP ***</strong></p><p><strong>﻿IF THIS IS A FRONTIER OR KINETIC (WINDSTREAM) BROADBAND CIRCUIT, CHECK TO SEE IF THERE ARE TWO HANDOFF DEVICES (ONT/MODEM + A ROUTER TYPICALLY).&nbsp;IF THERE ARE, DOUBLE CHECK WITH YOUR IT CONTACT FIRST THEN PROCEED TO REMOVE THE ROUTER FROM THE MIX AND CONNECT DIRECTLY TO THE DEVICE IN FRONT OF IT</strong></p><p><strong><u>Connect New Internet CKT to Customer's FortiGate firewall.</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">CIRCUIT: </strong>Spectrum DIA 100M</p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">MAC Address/CKT ID: </strong>91.L1XX.021308..CHTR</p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Demarc: </strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">FLOOR/SUITE * 1st Floor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">CPE MOUNT * Rack Mounted</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">FTP MOUNT * Rack Mounted</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">INTERFACE * TRTWNCAQ2ZW</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">HANDOFF TYPE* Electrical</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">CPE LOCATION: Located behind Reception desk in closet closet to the wall</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">IP Information:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Useable IP: 70.61.98.126</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Gateway IP: 70.61.98.125</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Primary DNS: 209.18.47.61</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Secondary DNS: 209.18.47.62</span></p><p><strong>Work to be Performed:</strong></p><ul><li>⁠Locate new circuit using <strong>MAC Address</strong> or <strong>CKT ID</strong> + <strong>DMARC info</strong> in this WO</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\">⁠</span><u style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\">Test new circuit on your laptop FIRST</u><span style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\"> (verify you can surf out and run some speed tests) before reaching out to AC IT (end user) and receiving instructions from them on cross-connecting to their firewall.&nbsp;Reach out to CommandLink Dispatch (WO Manager) after testing w/ laptop before proceeding.</span></li><li>Coordinate directly with customer IT to complete connection and circuit testing</li><li>⁠Connect newly installed CommandLink internet service to the customer’s FortiGate firewall</li></ul><p><strong>Conditional Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">If cabling or extension work is required, the technician will:</strong></p><ul><li>Stop installation work</li><li>Switch scope to a site survey</li><li>Provide a quote for additional work before proceeding</li></ul><p><strong>Tasks to be completed for work order to be paid:</strong></p><p><strong>You have a hard start at 11 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the location, ETC please do.</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li><li>Upon arrival, check in with your WO Manager first (if they do not answer then call the check-in check-out number to speak with someone else on the team)</li><li>Locate, photograph, and test new circuit</li><li>Test circuit first with a laptop; will need to assign static IPs.&nbsp;Test for connectivity then run a couple speed tests, make sure you get at least 80% of the circuit speeds both Upload and Download.</li><li>If the circuit is working then contact us back and we will let AC IT team know we are ready to move forward w/ their LAN cutover. <u> If it is not working then we (CommandLink Dispatch) will work with you to resolve the issue, </u><strong><u>please do not reach out to end user (ACI) if the CKT is not testing cleanly on your laptop</u>.</strong></li><li>Verify cabling and assess whether a new run is needed or if we can repurpose an existing between our newly installed CKT and customer's network rack.</li><li>If a new run is required, stop and perform survey first, then contact CommandLink with quote before moving forward.</li></ol><p>___________________________________________</p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.</strong></p><p><strong>3.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"***PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME* (no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\* BRING A CISCO ROLLOVER CONSOLE CABLE + LAPTOP \\*\\*\\***\n\n**﻿IF THIS IS A FRONTIER OR KINETIC (WINDSTREAM) BROADBAND CIRCUIT, CHECK TO SEE IF THERE ARE TWO HANDOFF DEVICES (ONT/MODEM + A ROUTER TYPICALLY). IF THERE ARE, DOUBLE CHECK WITH YOUR IT CONTACT FIRST THEN PROCEED TO REMOVE THE ROUTER FROM THE MIX AND CONNECT DIRECTLY TO THE DEVICE IN FRONT OF IT**\n\n**Connect New Internet CKT to Customer's FortiGate firewall.**\n\n**CIRCUIT:** Spectrum DIA 100M\n\n**MAC Address/CKT ID:** 91.L1XX.021308..CHTR\n\n**Demarc:**\n\nFLOOR/SUITE \\* 1st Floor\n\nCPE MOUNT \\* Rack Mounted\n\nFTP MOUNT \\* Rack Mounted\n\nINTERFACE \\* TRTWNCAQ2ZW\n\nHANDOFF TYPE\\* Electrical\n\nCPE LOCATION: Located behind Reception desk in closet closet to the wall\n\n**IP Information:**\n\nUseable IP: 70.61.98.126\n\nGateway IP: 70.61.98.125\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.252\n\nPrimary DNS: 209.18.47.61\n\nSecondary DNS: 209.18.47.62\n\n**Work to be Performed:**\n\n- ⁠Locate new circuit using **MAC Address** or **CKT ID** + **DMARC info** in this WO\n- ⁠Test new circuit on your laptop FIRST (verify you can surf out and run some speed tests) before reaching out to AC IT (end user) and receiving instructions from them on cross-connecting to their firewall. Reach out to CommandLink Dispatch (WO Manager) after testing w/ laptop before proceeding.\n- Coordinate directly with customer IT to complete connection and circuit testing\n- ⁠Connect newly installed CommandLink internet service to the customer’s FortiGate firewall\n\n**Conditional Work:**\n\n**If cabling or extension work is required, the technician will:**\n\n- Stop installation work\n- Switch scope to a site survey\n- Provide a quote for additional work before proceeding\n\n**Tasks to be completed for work order to be paid:**\n\n**You have a hard start at 11 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the location, ETC please do.**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n2. Upon arrival, check in with your WO Manager first (if they do not answer then call the check-in check-out number to speak with someone else on the team)\n3. Locate, photograph, and test new circuit\n4. Test circuit first with a laptop; will need to assign static IPs. Test for connectivity then run a couple speed tests, make sure you get at least 80% of the circuit speeds both Upload and Download.\n5. If the circuit is working then contact us back and we will let AC IT team know we are ready to move forward w/ their LAN cutover.  If it is not working then we (CommandLink Dispatch) will work with you to resolve the issue, **please do not reach out to end user (ACI) if the CKT is not testing cleanly on your laptop.**\n6. Verify cabling and assess whether a new run is needed or if we can repurpose an existing between our newly installed CKT and customer's network rack.\n7. If a new run is required, stop and perform survey first, then contact CommandLink with quote before moving forward.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n**1. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.**\n\n**2. If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.**\n\n**3. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.**\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T10:00","end":"2026-10-26T12:39"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2.65,"distance":10.98603826999336},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-3