{"job":{"id":20219873,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"VLAN testing and Cutover & Adding 16 POE Switch (Patch cables required - please see SOW)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME&nbsp;</strong><strong>(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"> AND</strong><span style=\"color: red;\"> </span><strong style=\"color: red;\">CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL</strong></p><p><strong>***Please join the bridge 30 Minutes after arriving onsite***</strong></p><p><strong>***Bridge starts at 9:00AM  EST***</strong></p><p><strong>Patch cables WILL be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.</strong></p><p><em>**Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning**</em></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>BRIDGE INFO:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Microsoft Teams meeting </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Join: </span>https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2808641824980848?p=3eXbR8XxUZGqMpzY3s<span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Meeting ID: 280 864 182 498 084 8 </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Passcode: u6qC3Qi7 </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">________________________________________</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Need help? | System reference </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Dial in by phone </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">+1 323-433-1251,,891349778# United States, Los Angeles </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Find a local number </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Phone conference ID: 891 349 778# </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">For organizers: Meeting options | Reset dial-in PIN </span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>VLAN Testing and Cutover + POE</strong></p><p>The Field Technician will provide onsite support to install a 16-port PoE switch on the existing network and assist with VLAN testing, circuit validation, and network cutover activities under the direction of the remote engineering team.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p>The Field Technician will be responsible for:</p><ul><li>Check in with the remote engineering team upon arrival.</li><li>Join the bridge call with the remote engineering team as requested.</li><li>Locate and identify the designated network equipment and circuits.</li><li>Verify physical connectivity of all network devices and cabling.</li><li>Assist the remote engineer with VLAN testing and validation.</li><li>Connect/disconnect Ethernet patch cables as instructed.</li><li>Perform network cutover following the engineer's direction.</li><li>Verify link lights and interface status.</li><li>Assist with testing network connectivity after the cutover.</li><li>Report any connectivity or hardware issues encountered during the process.</li><li>Remain onsite until released by the remote engineering team.</li><li>Upload required site photos before checkout.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Customer/Engineer Responsibilities</strong></p><p>The remote engineering team will:</p><ul><li>Provide all VLAN configuration changes.</li><li>Perform switch/firewall configuration.</li><li>Validate network connectivity.</li><li>Direct the technician throughout the cutover process.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet port or USB Ethernet adapter</li><li>Smartphone with camera</li><li>Basic networking knowledge</li><li>Ability to identify switch ports and patch panels</li><li>Basic understanding of VLANs and Ethernet connectivity</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Deliverables</strong></p><p>The technician must upload:</p><ul><li>Photos of the network rack</li><li>Photos of equipment connections</li><li>Photos of patch panel (if applicable)</li><li>Photos of completed cable connections</li><li>Notes describing the work performed</li><li>Speed test or connectivity verification (if requested by the engineer)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li><li>When onsite call the <strong>CONFERENCE BRIDGE&nbsp;</strong>Listed above or reach out to your Work Order Manager // Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>**** *********</del></span></li><li>Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge</li><li>Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)</li><li>Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (<strong>dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)</strong></li><li>Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested</li><li>Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.</li><li>Take pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.</li><li>Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Additional requirements:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Site Verification</strong>:</p><p>New equipment should be placed next to existing Fortigate firewalls and Fortiswitch, and any additional switches onsite in other areas should also be placed next to existing Fortiswitches.</p><p><strong>Perform network tests for functionality:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify DHCP is working correctly</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirm IP address received, DNS address received.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify internet access is working</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ping internal network resources to verify reachability.</p><p><strong>Site transition:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once network is tested and verified, move all cables from Masergy Fortiswitches to new Ubiquiti/Command link switches.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify internet connectivity and Wi-Fi reachability onsite.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verify circuit failover is working and test reachability while on failover circuit.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work with the bridge and the site contact to verify <strong>all site devices</strong> are reachable and functioning.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Adding Labels to new equipment for identification (Firewall, Switch 1, Switch 2, Etc..)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Remove old network devices from racks set aside.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</p><p>2.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME** **(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)** **AND** **CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please join the bridge 30 Minutes after arriving onsite\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Bridge starts at 9:00AM EST\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Patch cables WILL be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.**\n\n*\\*\\*Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning\\*\\**\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**BRIDGE INFO:**\n\nMicrosoft Teams meeting\n\nJoin: <https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2808641824980848?p=3eXbR8XxUZGqMpzY3s>\n\nMeeting ID: 280 864 182 498 084 8\n\nPasscode: u6qC3Qi7\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nNeed help? | System reference\n\nDial in by phone\n\n+1 323-433-1251,,891349778# United States, Los Angeles\n\nFind a local number\n\nPhone conference ID: 891 349 778#\n\nFor organizers: Meeting options | Reset dial-in PIN\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**VLAN Testing and Cutover + POE**\n\nThe Field Technician will provide onsite support to install a 16-port PoE switch on the existing network and assist with VLAN testing, circuit validation, and network cutover activities under the direction of the remote engineering team.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nThe Field Technician will be responsible for:\n\n- Check in with the remote engineering team upon arrival.\n- Join the bridge call with the remote engineering team as requested.\n- Locate and identify the designated network equipment and circuits.\n- Verify physical connectivity of all network devices and cabling.\n- Assist the remote engineer with VLAN testing and validation.\n- Connect/disconnect Ethernet patch cables as instructed.\n- Perform network cutover following the engineer's direction.\n- Verify link lights and interface status.\n- Assist with testing network connectivity after the cutover.\n- Report any connectivity or hardware issues encountered during the process.\n- Remain onsite until released by the remote engineering team.\n- Upload required site photos before checkout.\n\n**Customer/Engineer Responsibilities**\n\nThe remote engineering team will:\n\n- Provide all VLAN configuration changes.\n- Perform switch/firewall configuration.\n- Validate network connectivity.\n- Direct the technician throughout the cutover process.\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet port or USB Ethernet adapter\n- Smartphone with camera\n- Basic networking knowledge\n- Ability to identify switch ports and patch panels\n- Basic understanding of VLANs and Ethernet connectivity\n\n**Required Deliverables**\n\nThe technician must upload:\n\n- Photos of the network rack\n- Photos of equipment connections\n- Photos of patch panel (if applicable)\n- Photos of completed cable connections\n- Notes describing the work performed\n- Speed test or connectivity verification (if requested by the engineer)\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables:**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n2. When onsite call the **CONFERENCE BRIDGE** Listed above or reach out to your Work Order Manager // Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge\n4. Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)\n5. Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (**dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)**\n6. Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested\n7. Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.\n8. Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.\n9. Take pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.\n10. Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge.\n\n**Additional requirements:**\n\n**Site Verification**:\n\nNew equipment should be placed next to existing Fortigate firewalls and Fortiswitch, and any additional switches onsite in other areas should also be placed next to existing Fortiswitches.\n\n**Perform network tests for functionality:**\n\n· Verify DHCP is working correctly\n\n· Confirm IP address received, DNS address received.\n\n· Verify internet access is working\n\n· Ping internal network resources to verify reachability.\n\n**Site transition:**\n\n· Once network is tested and verified, move all cables from Masergy Fortiswitches to new Ubiquiti/Command link switches.\n\n· Verify internet connectivity and Wi-Fi reachability onsite.\n\n· Verify circuit failover is working and test reachability while on failover circuit.\n\n· Work with the bridge and the site contact to verify **all site devices** are reachable and functioning.\n\n· Adding Labels to new equipment for identification (Firewall, Switch 1, Switch 2, Etc..)\n\n· Remove old network devices from racks set aside.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1\\. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.\n\n2\\. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T08:30","end":"2026-11-04T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":4.771525722055393},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792609273912}
