ny trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\n**Title:** Technician Needed with Tools to Install Aruba Switch in MDF – Fayetteville, NC | 00262603 / SA-294253 / 05293188\n\n**Type of Work:** Networking\n\n**Schedule:** October 22, 2026 – 09:00 EDT (09:00 EDT)\n\n**Site Name & Address:** Fairfield Inn Fayetteville North, 4249 Ramsey Street, Fayetteville, NC 28311, United States\n\n**WO / SA / Case:** 00262603 / SA-294253 / 05293188\n\n**Contact Details:**\n\nSite POC: Rosa Baleta, 910-223-7867\n\nEngineer: Adel El-Sayed | TECHNET\n\nTechnician: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Install Aruba switch at the MDF location.\n- Replace faulty switch installation.\n- Device Name: FAYFNSW02-01-MDF.\n- Model: HPE Aruba Networking 2930F 24G PoE+ 4SFP Switch JL261A.\n- Serial Number: CN20HL25PW.\n- Vendor Ticket Number: 5405643033.\n- Verify all network connections are properly connected and secured.\n- Confirm switch powers on and operates normally.\n- Verify network connectivity after installation.\n- Coordinate with remote engineer Adel El-Sayed during the installation.\n- Label equipment and connections if required.\n- Document all work performed and any issues identified.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset & Location:** FAYFNSW02-01-MDF – MDF\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit Ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- Patch cables\n- Network labeling supplies\n- Basic hand tools for switch installation and rack mounting (if required)","actions":[]},"is