{"job":{"id":20221022,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"DAY 2: Cortland Brier Creek - Redundant Circuit Patch-In, Turn-Up & Power Validation- #326718","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Gigstreem is a national Internet service provider delivering high-quality internet services to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p>Work Order Details</p><p><strong>Property:</strong> <strong>Address:</strong> 7920 Oak Estate St, Raleigh, NC 27617</p><p><strong>Customer:</strong> Cortland</p><p><strong>Work Location:</strong> LCP/MDF – Main Network Equipment Room</p><p>Scope of Work (SOW)</p><p>Dispatch an experienced Field Nation network technician to <strong>Cortland Brier Creek</strong> to complete the redundant circuit patch-in and Turn-Up (TTU), working directly with an assigned Gigstreem Engineer remotely.</p><p>The technician must physically connect the redundant circuit to the designated Edge-Router port, assist Engineering with circuit activation and testing, and complete the required visual power provisioning inspections.</p><p><strong>IMPORTANT: The technician MUST arrive with a Windows laptop with Winbox and PuTTY installed, an RJ45 Ethernet cable, and an RJ45-to-USB console cable compatible with MikroTik equipment.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>1. Site Access &amp; Initial Inspection</p><ul><li>Contact the onsite property contact at least 30 minutes before arrival to provide an accurate ETA.</li><li>Check in at the Leasing Office or designated building contact.</li><li>Obtain access to the LCP/MDF.</li><li>Contact the assigned Gigstreem Engineer before beginning work.</li><li>Locate the Edge-Router, Gateway, UPS, EBM, PDU, and MDF Aggregation Switch.</li><li>Inspect the network rack and identify the existing primary and redundant circuit connections.</li><li>Take clear photos of the rack, equipment, and existing cabling before making changes.</li></ul><p>2. Redundant Circuit Patch-In</p><p>The technician must verify th