{"job":{"id":20221033,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TailWind Voice & Data, Inc.","title":"**URGENT** Store Down - Nothing is operational at the site, like APs, Switches , etc.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Objective Statement:</strong></p><p>Store Down - Nothing is operational at the site, like APs, Switches , etc.</p><p><br></p><p>Work with BBI NOC throughout dispatch after sending before photos</p><p>Email subject line- OBS3479, send before photos with that subject line so they know it is you and then call BBI NOC. Leave voicemail if they do not answer.</p><p><br></p><p>Technician will need to come prepared with extra replacement keystone jack, CAT5E Cable, terminating tools, cable toner, cable tester/ certifier, ladders, a Power Cord and other hand tools necessary to complete the work required.</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>--Standard technician tools &amp; materials including a laptop</p><p>--Technician will need to come prepared with:</p><p>• Label Maker</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Power Cord</p><p>• CAT6 Cable and extra replacement Keystone Jacks (CAT5e &amp; CAT6)</p><p>• Terminating tools, Cable Toner/Tester/Certifier</p><p>• 10ft-12ft Ladder</p><p>• Other hand tools necessary to complete the work required.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Deliverable Format: </strong></p><p>﻿BEFORE PHOTOS REQUIRED BEFORE STARTING WORK:</p><p>1)&nbsp;Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)</p><p>2)&nbsp;Customer network rack (door open)**IF AN UNSECURE CABINET OR BACKBOARD IS LOOSE OR RISK OF CABINET CONDITION CREATING UNSAFE CONDITIONS, DISPATCH WILL IMMEDIATELY REVERT TO A SECURE RACK DISPATCH. IMMEDIATELY CALL BBI NOC @ (813) 830-4500.</p><p>3) Patch panel and surrounding area</p><p>4) Any Work location exceptions (i.e. broken ceiling tiles, poor cable management, unsecured rack, missing door or side(s), etc.)</p><p>5)*Email to networkgroup@bloominbrands.com &amp; deliverables@tailwindvoiceanddata.com (reference 7-digit site ID in subject line: OBS3479 BEFORE)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>AFTER PHOTOS REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</p><p>1)&nbsp;Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)</p><p>2)&nbsp;Customer network rack (door open)</p><p>3) Patch panel and surrounding area</p><p>4) Bottom corners of network rack showing it securely closed (left and right side)</p><p>5) SIGNED WORK ORDER</p><p>6)*Email to networkgroup@bloominbrands.com &amp; deliverables@tailwindvoiceanddata.com (reference 7-digit site ID in subject line: OBS3479 AFTER)</p><p><strong>TailWind Requirements: </strong></p><ul><li>Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.</li><li>Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.</li><li>Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.</li><li>Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Objective Statement:**\n\nStore Down - Nothing is operational at the site, like APs, Switches , etc.\n\nWork with BBI NOC throughout dispatch after sending before photos\n\nEmail subject line- OBS3479, send before photos with that subject line so they know it is you and then call BBI NOC. Leave voicemail if they do not answer.\n\nTechnician will need to come prepared with extra replacement keystone jack, CAT5E Cable, terminating tools, cable toner, cable tester/ certifier, ladders, a Power Cord and other hand tools necessary to complete the work required.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n\\--Standard technician tools & materials including a laptop\n\n\\--Technician will need to come prepared with:\n\n• Label Maker\n\n • Power Cord\n\n• CAT6 Cable and extra replacement Keystone Jacks (CAT5e & CAT6)\n\n• Terminating tools, Cable Toner/Tester/Certifier\n\n• 10ft-12ft Ladder\n\n• Other hand tools necessary to complete the work required.\n\n**Required Deliverable Format:**\n\n﻿BEFORE PHOTOS REQUIRED BEFORE STARTING WORK:\n\n1\\) Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)\n\n2\\) Customer network rack (door open)\\*\\*IF AN UNSECURE CABINET OR BACKBOARD IS LOOSE OR RISK OF CABINET CONDITION CREATING UNSAFE CONDITIONS, DISPATCH WILL IMMEDIATELY REVERT TO A SECURE RACK DISPATCH. IMMEDIATELY CALL BBI NOC @ (813) 830-4500.\n\n3\\) Patch panel and surrounding area\n\n4\\) Any Work location exceptions (i.e. broken ceiling tiles, poor cable management, unsecured rack, missing door or side(s), etc.)\n\n5)\\*Email to networkgroup@bloominbrands.com & deliverables@tailwindvoiceanddata.com (reference 7-digit site ID in subject line: OBS3479 BEFORE)\n\nAFTER PHOTOS REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING SITE:\n\n1\\) Customer network rack (wide angle, door closed)\n\n2\\) Customer network rack (door open)\n\n3\\) Patch panel and surrounding area\n\n4\\) Bottom corners of network rack showing it securely closed (left and right side)\n\n5\\) SIGNED WORK ORDER\n\n6)\\*Email to networkgroup@bloominbrands.com & deliverables@tailwindvoiceanddata.com (reference 7-digit site ID in subject line: OBS3479 AFTER)\n\n**TailWind Requirements:**\n\n- Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.\n- Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.\n- Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)\n- Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.\n- Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.\n- Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.\n- Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T17:00","end":"2026-10-21T19:00","latestStart":"2026-10-21T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13.280687459972155},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 (countered: $160) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Nothing"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10