Physical Mounting &amp; Firewall Cutover</strong><ul><li>Rackmount the new pre-staged <strong><del>********* *****</del></strong><del> *************</del> using the included rackmount kit <del>**************</del></li><li>Perform the physical cutover: Disconnect the existing <strong>SonicWall TZ300</strong> and connect network/ISP cables to the matching interface ports on the new <strong>TZ380</strong>. <em>(Note: Existing ISP circuit remains unchanged)</em>.</li><li>Coordinate directly with <strong><del>**** **********</del></strong> remotely during the cutover as needed.</li><li>Dress all network cabling cleanly using <strong>Velcro straps ONLY</strong> (no zip ties).</li></ul><br><strong>3. Validation, IT Glue Documentation &amp; Checkout</strong><ul><li>Test and validate all site connectivity following cutover, including internet access and active network services.</li><li>Confirm with <strong><del>**** *****</del></strong><del> </del>that all critical business functions are fully operational before leaving.</li><li>Complete all project documentation in <strong>IT Glue</strong> and task notes before departing.</li><li>Upload required photo deliverables to Field Nation and call <del>**** **********</del> for final check-out.</li></ul><br><strong>Deliverables: Photos to Upload</strong><p>Before checking out, upload the following clear photos (to both Field Nation and IT Glue):</p><ul><li><strong>Unboxed TZ380 &amp; Rackmount Kit:</strong> Photo showing the new SonicWall TZ380 and rackmount kit (03-SSC-3457) prior to installation.</li><li><strong>Old TZ300 Serial Label:</strong> Close-up photo showing the model and serial tag of the decommissioned SonicWall TZ300.</li><li><strong>New TZ380 Mounted &amp; Powered ON (MANDATORY):</strong> Photo showing the SonicWall TZ380 installed in the rack kit, powered on with active WAN/LAN status LEDs.</li><li><strong>Clean Rack Post-Cutover:</strong> Wide photo showing the network rack with clean Velcro cable management around the new firewall.</li><li><strong>Verified Internet Screen:</strong> Photo showing test laptop screen confirming active internet and network connectivity.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li><strong>Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC)</strong>, USB-to-Ethernet Adapter, &amp; Console/Patch Cables</li><li><strong>SonicWall Rackmount Kit</strong> (03-SSC-3457) <em>(Confirmed received on site)</em></li><li><strong>Basic Hand Tools</strong> (screwdrivers, cage nut tool, wire snips)</li><li><strong>Velcro straps ONLY</strong> <em>(Zip ties strictly prohibited)</em></li><li><strong>Smartphone</strong> for calls, Remote Support coordination, and photo deliverables</li></ul><p><br></p><p>For <u>pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact</u>, please check the <strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION</strong> below.</p><p><br></p><strong>DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)</li><li><strong>Record</strong>: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong> Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong> Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within <strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><br>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE & PROTOCOL**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE \\*\\* SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism & Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**  \n**1. Arrival, Check-In & Etiquette**- Arrive on-site on **Friday, October 30, 2026, at 3:00 PM EDT (15:00 EDT)**.\n- Check in with site contact **\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** for access to the network closet/rack area.\n- Introduce yourself as representing **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\n- **CRITICAL INSTRUCTION:** Do **NOT** ask the local client contact to answer any technical questions regarding the firewall or network setup.\n- Call \\*\\* Remote Resource **\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** upon arrival to open the task and log start time.\n\n  \n**2. Physical Mounting & Firewall Cutover**- Rackmount the new pre-staged **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* using the included rackmount kit \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Perform the physical cutover: Disconnect the existing **SonicWall TZ300** and connect network/ISP cables to the matching interface ports on the new **TZ380**. *(Note: Existing ISP circuit remains unchanged)*.\n- Coordinate directly with **\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** remotely during the cutover as needed.\n- Dress all network cabling cleanly using **Velcro straps ONLY** (no zip ties).\n\n  \n**3. Validation, IT Glue Documentation & Checkout**- Test and validate all site connectivity following cutover, including internet access and active network services.\n- Confirm with **\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** that all critical business functions are fully operational before leaving.\n- Complete all project documentation in **IT Glue** and task notes before departing.\n- Upload required photo deliverables to Field Nation and call \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for final check-out.\n\n  \n**Deliverables: Photos to Upload**Before checking out, upload the following clear photos (to both Field Nation and IT Glue):\n\n- **Unboxed TZ380 & Rackmount Kit:** Photo showing the new SonicWall TZ380 and rackmount kit (03-SSC-3457) prior to installation.\n- **Old TZ300 Serial Label:** Close-up photo showing the model and serial tag of the decommissioned SonicWall TZ300.\n- **New TZ380 Mounted & Powered ON (MANDATORY):** Photo showing the SonicWall TZ380 installed in the rack kit, powered on with active WAN/LAN status LEDs.\n- **Clean Rack Post-Cutover:** Wide photo showing the network rack with clean Velcro cable management around the new firewall.\n- **Verified Internet Screen:** Photo showing test laptop screen confirming active internet and network connectivity.\n\n**Required Tools & Equipment**- **Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC)**, USB-to-Ethernet Adapter, & Console/Patch Cables\n- **SonicWall Rackmount Kit** (03-SSC-3457) *(Confirmed received on site)*\n- **Basic Hand Tools** (screwdrivers, cage nut tool, wire snips)\n- **Velcro straps ONLY** *(Zip ties strictly prohibited)*\n- **Smartphone** for calls, Remote Support coordination, and photo deliverables\n\nFor pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact, please check the **CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION** below.\n\n**DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:**- **Documentation:** Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)\n- **Record**: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nBy accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00","end":"2026-10-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":0.9125268104765558},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026