{"job":{"id":20221648,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Audio System Troubleshooting -  audio, upstairs office area has no audio","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scope of Work:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• IMPORTANT: Lift to be scheduled &quot;Ceiling 20FT&quot; / Must schedule with Store MOD for AM or PM VISIT outside of store hours.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• This work order requires experience with 70V audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Required Tools:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Wired headphones</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Alligator clip leads</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Toner and probe kit</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Self-powered butt set</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• On-Site Procedure:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Locate TOA Amplifier.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Locate Valcom 2003 Amplifier.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Locate the section of speakers reported to not be working and document it:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o We need to trace this segment of speakers back to which ever amp its going to. If its a 24vDC speaker it will have 2 pairs that go back to the Valcom solution. If its 70V speaker run it will go to the TOA amplifier. We need to know what kind of speaker, where its going, because we suspect a break in the run or a volume control switch issue in that run.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Verify the Music box: (If store has any music at all ignore this verify step)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Has power.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Has a headphone cable connected to the side.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Mood media player may have a splitter and be feeding both Amp and Phone switch, trace both lines to ensure connections are tight.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Trace the headphone cable and determine where it terminates. (Is it attached to the Valcom or the TOA?)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Take clear photos of the following:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Plywood/backboard in the electrical room and/or rack room.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Equipment rack. (Front and back)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Any audio equipment present.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Music box and associated cabling, where possible.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Objective of visit:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o DO NOT RE-CABLE without NTS AUDIO AUTHORIZATION 800-282-7928, Option 3 Option 5</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Confirm All speakers are working.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Confirm Paging is working.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o Confirm Music on Hold is working.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">o If speaker run we are going out to inspect needs a new line run, we need details on where its terminated today, how long of a run is needed, and any specialized equipment like a lift.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at 800-282-7928, Option 3 for further troubleshooting.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Other Instructions:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">If assistance is needed, please call: 800-282-7928 option # 3, #5 - Audio Support</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Required Tool List:</span></p><p>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA</p><p> </p><p><em>Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.</em></p><p><strong>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</strong></p><p><strong>Each site visit will require its own work order.</strong></p><p><strong>If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</strong></p><p><em>Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.</em></p><p>All NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2.  <strong><u>ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support</u></strong>.</p><ul><li> A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.<ul><li> #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.</li><li>#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.</li><li>#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><p>• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat</p><p>• Laptop</p><p>• USB to serial connector</p><p>• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html</p><p>• Putty</p><p>• NULL Modem cable</p><p>• Ethernet cable</p><p>• Laptop Power pack</p><p>• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet</p><p>• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30</p><p>• Flash light</p><p>• Digital Volt Meter</p><p>• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/</p><p>• Zoom installed on Techs Phone</p><p>• Velcro Straps</p><p>• X-over cable</p><p>• Standard screwdriver and security bits</p><p>• Thermal paste</p><p>• Alcohol Wipes</p><p>• 9 pin serial cable</p><strong>Reimbursement Rates:</strong>Cabling Materials<ul><li>Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.20 per ft</strong></li><li>Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.29 per ft</strong></li></ul>Hardware<ul><li>Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: <strong>$9.00 each</strong></li></ul>Patch Cables<ul><li>1 ft: <strong>$3.50</strong></li><li>3 ft: <strong>$2.00</strong></li><li>5 ft: <strong>$4.50</strong></li><li>10 ft: <strong>$6.50</strong></li></ul>Cable Management<ul><li>Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): <strong>$2.00 per drop</strong></li></ul>Cabling Job Requirements<ul><li>All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.</li><li>Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.</li><li>All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Support to check in. <del>*** *********** ************* </del><del>*** *** ****</del> and confirm before leaving site. Support representative&#39;s name will be required. If no answer call <del>**** ******* ** ************* ****** **</del></li><li>Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:</li><li>Record the client employee&#39;s First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.</li><li>Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong> </p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required  </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance  </li><li>Background check is required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts as representing<del>********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment  </li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire  </li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nScope of Work:\n\n• IMPORTANT: Lift to be scheduled \"Ceiling 20FT\" / Must schedule with Store MOD for AM or PM VISIT outside of store hours.\n\n• This work order requires experience with 70V audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.\n\n• Required Tools:\n\no Wired headphones\n\no Alligator clip leads\n\no Toner and probe kit\n\no Self-powered butt set\n\n• On-Site Procedure:\n\n• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room.\n\n• Locate TOA Amplifier.\n\n• Locate Valcom 2003 Amplifier.\n\n• Locate the section of speakers reported to not be working and document it:\n\no We need to trace this segment of speakers back to which ever amp its going to. If its a 24vDC speaker it will have 2 pairs that go back to the Valcom solution. If its 70V speaker run it will go to the TOA amplifier. We need to know what kind of speaker, where its going, because we suspect a break in the run or a volume control switch issue in that run.\n\n• Verify the Music box: (If store has any music at all ignore this verify step)\n\no Has power.\n\no Has a headphone cable connected to the side.\n\no Mood media player may have a splitter and be feeding both Amp and Phone switch, trace both lines to ensure connections are tight.\n\no Trace the headphone cable and determine where it terminates. (Is it attached to the Valcom or the TOA?)\n\n• Take clear photos of the following:\n\no Plywood/backboard in the electrical room and/or rack room.\n\no Equipment rack. (Front and back)\n\no Any audio equipment present.\n\no Music box and associated cabling, where possible.\n\n• Objective of visit:\n\no DO NOT RE-CABLE without NTS AUDIO AUTHORIZATION 800-282-7928, Option 3 Option 5\n\no Confirm All speakers are working.\n\no Confirm Paging is working.\n\no Confirm Music on Hold is working.\n\no If speaker run we are going out to inspect needs a new line run, we need details on where its terminated today, how long of a run is needed, and any specialized equipment like a lift.\n\n• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at 800-282-7928, Option 3 for further troubleshooting.\n\nOther Instructions:\n\nIf assistance is needed, please call: 800-282-7928 option # 3, #5 - Audio Support\n\nRequired Tool List:\n\nhttps://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA\n\n*Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.*\n\n**Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.**\n\n**Each site visit will require its own work order.**\n\n**If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.**\n\n*Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.*\n\nAll NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2. **ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support**.\n\n- A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.\n  - #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.\n  - \\#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.\n  - \\#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.\n\n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat\n\n• Laptop\n\n• USB to serial connector\n\n• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - <http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html>\n\n• Putty\n\n• NULL Modem cable\n\n• Ethernet cable\n\n• Laptop Power pack\n\n• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet\n\n• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30\n\n• Flash light\n\n• Digital Volt Meter\n\n• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - <https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/>\n\n• Zoom installed on Techs Phone\n\n• Velcro Straps\n\n• X-over cable\n\n• Standard screwdriver and security bits\n\n• Thermal paste\n\n• Alcohol Wipes\n\n• 9 pin serial cable\n\n**Reimbursement Rates:**Cabling Materials- Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: **$0.20 per ft**\n- Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: **$0.29 per ft**\n\nHardware- Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: **$9.00 each**\n\nPatch Cables- 1 ft: **$3.50**\n- 3 ft: **$2.00**\n- 5 ft: **$4.50**\n- 10 ft: **$6.50**\n\nCable Management- Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): **$2.00 per drop**\n\nCabling Job Requirements- All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.\n- Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.\n- All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Call Support to check in. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* and confirm before leaving site. Support representative's name will be required. If no answer call \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n- Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:\n- Record the client employee's First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.\n- Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check is required\n- Check-in with site contacts as representing\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T07:00","end":"2026-10-23T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.403383893034126},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $120) is be