{"job":{"id":20222820,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Switch Troubleshoot (DISPATCH ASAP)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>(FE MUST DROP OFF OLD UNITS TO BE SHIPPED BACK.RETURN LABEL WILL BE PROVIDED)</u></strong></p><p>Return label with ***RMA# ENDING IN\"B\"*** will be provided</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>(DO NOT CONTACT STORE TO CONFIRM PARTS OR ETA)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Request Type:</u></strong> Troubleshoot</p><p><strong><u>Device Type:</u></strong> Switch</p><p><strong><u>Problem Description:</u></strong> Device down</p><p><strong><u>Business Impact:</u></strong> Yes</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Onsite Plan of Action</u></strong></p><ul><li>Once onsite check in with&nbsp;Client Support Line</li><li>Do not power on/off or reboot any devices until instructed by the Support Engineer</li><li>Troubleshoot as needed</li><li>Replace parts if they are on site&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave site without calling the Client Support Line</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Required Tools/Materials:</u></p><p><br></p><p><u>Software:</u></p><ul><li>Tera Term &amp; Putty(32 BIT, MSI), UART Drivers</li><li>Meeting Apps: Microsoft Teams(Preferred),Zoom, Team viewer</li><li>Fully charged Laptop ? Windows (8 and above) with USB A ports</li><li>If laptop only has USBC a USB C hub is required to provide USB A ports.</li><li>Laptop charger</li><li>Active Mobile Hotspot</li><li>Ethernet cables - qty. 2 (Cat 5)</li><li>Ethernet Tester</li><li>RJ-45 Connector</li><li>USB Flash Drive (1 GIG min space) &amp; a Cell Phone</li><li>Stripped Screw Remover</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Crimper/Punch Down Tool</li><li>Zip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>USB-A to USB-C cable</li><li>USB-C to USB-C cable</li><li>DB-9 (F) connector to RJ-45 (M) (known as Cisco console cable)</li><li>DB9 to USB needed if the laptop does not have a serial port</li><li>Label Maker</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to 4 hours onsite.&nbsp;Any additional time will be paid out at $45 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Technicians who check in more than 30 minutes late may have their pay impacted by up to a 25% penalty.</strong></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment.&nbsp;All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.&nbsp;If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered Cancelled, not Aborted.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**(FE MUST DROP OFF OLD UNITS TO BE SHIPPED BACK.RETURN LABEL WILL BE PROVIDED)**\n\nReturn label with \\*\\*\\*RMA# ENDING IN\"B\"\\*\\*\\* will be provided\n\n**(DO NOT CONTACT STORE TO CONFIRM PARTS OR ETA)**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Request Type:** Troubleshoot\n\n**Device Type:** Switch\n\n**Problem Description:** Device down\n\n**Business Impact:** Yes\n\n**Onsite Plan of Action**\n\n- Once onsite check in with Client Support Line\n- Do not power on/off or reboot any devices until instructed by the Support Engineer\n- Troubleshoot as needed\n- Replace parts if they are on site\n- Do not leave site without calling the Client Support Line\n\nRequired Tools/Materials:\n\nSoftware:\n\n- Tera Term & Putty(32 BIT, MSI), UART Drivers\n- Meeting Apps: Microsoft Teams(Preferred),Zoom, Team viewer\n- Fully charged Laptop ? Windows (8 and above) with USB A ports\n- If laptop only has USBC a USB C hub is required to provide USB A ports.\n- Laptop charger\n- Active Mobile Hotspot\n- Ethernet cables - qty. 2 (Cat 5)\n- Ethernet Tester\n- RJ-45 Connector\n- USB Flash Drive (1 GIG min space) & a Cell Phone\n- Stripped Screw Remover\n- Cable Tester\n- Crimper/Punch Down Tool\n- Zip-ties and/or velcro tie wraps\n- Console Cable\n- USB-A to USB-C cable\n- USB-C to USB-C cable\n- DB-9 (F) connector to RJ-45 (M) (known as Cisco console cable)\n- DB9 to USB needed if the laptop does not have a serial port\n- Label Maker\n\n***Flat rate covers up to 4 hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $45 per hour.***\n\n**Technicians who check in more than 30 minutes late may have their pay impacted by up to a 25% penalty.**\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered Cancelled, not Aborted.***\n\n***All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T08:00","end":"2026-10-22T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":220,"max":220},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":22.42537830151339},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":45,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T20:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","en