{"job":{"id":20223453,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Allbridge","title":"Tech to address down Access Points in Guestrooms 403, 500 and 613. If possible, Tech should come prepared to 3 new cable runs (cable length for room 403 won't exceed 30meters, Room 500 and 613 shouldn't also go past the ethernet standard of 100meters, it","description":{"html":"<p>AN EXPERIENCED TECHNICIAN SHOULD BE ABLE TO COMPLETE THIS WORK IN THE MAX HOURS SET ON THE WORK ORDER</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Additional time <strong><u>must be approved</u></strong> before the initial time expires by calling <strong>Allbridge Dispatch at 1-516-394-4648</strong>. Failure to obtain approval will result in denial of additional time.</li>\n<li>All travel needs to be pre-approved <strong><u>before assignment.</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Site Instructions</u></strong></p>\n<p>Tech to address down Access Points in Guestrooms 403, 500 and 613. If possible, Tech should come prepared to 3 new cable runs (cable length for room 403 won't exceed 30meters, Room 500 and 613 shouldn't also go past the ethernet standard of 100meters, it very likely might not get to this based on the distance for room 403)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech needs cable Tester, crimping tools, RJ45 Keystone jacks, RJ45 connectors, punchdown tool, cables (lots)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>POC: Noah Latta</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required skillsets:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Router/switch/firewall configuration &amp; troubleshooting</li>\n<li>Wireless AP installs and testing (heat mapping experience is a plus)</li>\n<li>Knowledge of TCP/IP, VLANs, DHCP, DNS</li>\n<li>Ability to work with ticketing systems &amp; follow case documentation processes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-site</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Print out the attached Allbridge work order and bring to site.<em>This is a mandatory requirement.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Onsite</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact Allbridge Dispatch at <strong>1-516-394-4648</strong>upon arrival</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the customer as a representative of<strong>Allbridge and Allbridge only</strong></li>\n<li>Follow the Work Order Process outlined in Section B</li>\n<li>Adhere to the assigned tasks and maintain professionalism</li>\n<li>Update the end user on the status of repairs and/or next steps</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Post site</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete the printed out Allbridge Work Order and obtain the customer's signature. <em>Failure to comply will result in non-payment.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Upload a photo of the completed Allbridge Work Order to FN</strong></li>\n<li>Call <strong>1-516-394-4648</strong> to provide closeout notes and checkout with Allbridge Dispatch</li>\n</ul>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>DISCLAIMER:</strong> <em>Failure to check out with Allbridge by phone before leaving the job site may result in non-payment.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop- with serial connector, Nic card and WIFI</li>\n<li>Smartphone</li>\n<li>Cat 5/6 tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch-down tools, etc.)</li>\n<li>RJ45 cable tester – LinkRunner or similar</li>\n<li>DB9 and DB25 testers</li>\n<li>Serial cable (DB9)</li>\n<li>Cisco console cable</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Ladder - 7Ft</li>\n<li>Voltage meter</li>\n<li>Assortment of parts, including but not limited to wall jacks, patch cords, cabling connectors, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Business casual attire</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"AN EXPERIENCED TECHNICIAN SHOULD BE ABLE TO COMPLETE THIS WORK IN THE MAX HOURS SET ON THE WORK ORDER\n\n- Additional time **must be approved** before the initial time expires by calling **Allbridge Dispatch at 1-516-394-4648**. Failure to obtain approval will result in denial of additional time.\n- All travel needs to be pre-approved **before assignment.**\n\n**Additional Site Instructions**\n\nTech to address down Access Points in Guestrooms 403, 500 and 613. If possible, Tech should come prepared to 3 new cable runs (cable length for room 403 won't exceed 30meters, Room 500 and 613 shouldn't also go past the ethernet standard of 100meters, it very likely might not get to this based on the distance for room 403)\n\nTech needs cable Tester, crimping tools, RJ45 Keystone jacks, RJ45 connectors, punchdown tool, cables (lots)\n\n**POC: Noah Latta**\n\n**Required skillsets:**\n\n- Router/switch/firewall configuration & troubleshooting\n- Wireless AP installs and testing (heat mapping experience is a plus)\n- Knowledge of TCP/IP, VLANs, DHCP, DNS\n- Ability to work with ticketing systems & follow case documentation processes\n\n**Scope:**\n\n**Pre-site**\n\n- Print out the attached Allbridge work order and bring to site.*This is a mandatory requirement.*\n\n**Onsite**\n\n- Contact Allbridge Dispatch at **1-516-394-4648**upon arrival\n- Introduce yourself to the customer as a representative of**Allbridge and Allbridge only**\n- Follow the Work Order Process outlined in Section B\n- Adhere to the assigned tasks and maintain professionalism\n- Update the end user on the status of repairs and/or next steps\n\n**Post site**\n\n- Complete the printed out Allbridge Work Order and obtain the customer's signature. *Failure to comply will result in non-payment.*\n- **Upload a photo of the completed Allbridge Work Order to FN**\n- Call **1-516-394-4648** to provide closeout notes and checkout with Allbridge Dispatch\n\n⚠️ **DISCLAIMER:** *Failure to check out with Allbridge by phone before leaving the job site may result in non-payment.*\n\n**Required tools:**\n\n- Laptop- with serial connector, Nic card and WIFI\n- Smartphone\n- Cat 5/6 tools (crimpers, toners, connectors, punch-down tools, etc.)\n- RJ45 cable tester – LinkRunner or similar\n- DB9 and DB25 testers\n- Serial cable (DB9)\n- Cisco console cable\n- Basic hand tools\n- Ladder - 7Ft\n- Voltage meter\n- Assortment of parts, including but not limited to wall jacks, patch cords, cabling connectors, etc.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-26T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.116817228127499},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.