{"job":{"id":"8014138961","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #270471- ALARM CUTOVER CUTOVER - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED","description":"<p><br></p><p><strong>*** ALARM CUTOVER ONLY ***</strong></p><p>*** DATE AND TIME NOT NEGOTIABLE ***</p><p>*** HARD START TIME AND DATE.***</p><p>*** DATE OR TIME CANNOT BE RESCHEDULED BY ANY MEANS.***</p><p>*** ANALOG SKILLS ARE A MUST.***</p><p>*** THE TECHNICIAN MUST NOT LEAVE UNTIL PROVIDING PICTURES AND WORK ORDER TO TECH AMERICAS ***</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Project Overview</strong></p><p>The technician is expected to complete cabling, equipment installation, and alarm service cutover.</p><p><strong>Important:</strong></p><ul><li>Work must be performed as close as possible to the alarm panel (PIAB Installation), provided there is good LTE signal.</li><li>A new dedicated cable line must always be run from the alarm panel to the PIAB for the DID cutover. Existing alarm or phone lines may not be reused.</li></ul><p>To ensure successful execution, the technician must arrive fully prepared with the following:</p><ul><li>At least 300 ft of Cat5e or Cat6 cable</li><li>RJ11 connectors for alarm line</li><li>A 10’ to 12’ ladder (to safely reach ceilings up to 14’)</li></ul><p><strong>Important:</strong> Failure to bring the required tools and materials listed above—and below in the \"Tool Requirements\" section—may result in dismissal from the job without compensation.</p><p>Please review the full tool list in advance to ensure full readiness for this dispatch.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>DISPATCH</strong></p><p>Once the technician arrives onsite, Tech Americas will notify the internal coordination team that the technician is on site.</p><p>Tasks to cover the Go Live phase:</p><ul><li>Run new cabling as required to connect alarm panel to PIAB.</li><li>Move the alarm line to the new equipment (PIAB) and complete acceptance testing.</li><li>If additional cabling is required, it has to be completed during this dispatch.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tasks</strong></p><ol><li>Contact the support team once the technician is on site.</li><li>Join the bridge link provided by remote support.</li><li>Support will contact the alarm monitoring team to place the panel in test mode.</li><li>Remote support will assist the technician in connecting the alarm line to the new equipment.</li></ol><p><strong>Connection Task:</strong></p><ul><li>Connect the WAN port of the new device to the customer’s switch.</li><li>Use patch cords of varying lengths (10ft, 25ft, 50ft).</li><li>If the customer’s switch is more than 50ft away, a cable run will be needed:</li><li>300ft CAT5 cables</li><li>RJ45/RJ11 connectors</li><li>Crimping tool</li></ul><ol><li>Once connected, remote support will complete the configuration.</li><li>The technician will assist with keypad inputs during alarm testing.</li><li>After alarm testing, contact Tech Americas to finalize testing.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Required Equipment</strong></p><p>Technicians must bring the following to every dispatch:</p><ul><li>10-12ft ladder (IT’S A MUST)</li><li>Hammer Drill (mounting surfaces may include drywall, concrete, metal)</li><li>Mounting hardware</li><li>Tie wraps, Velcro, cable organizers</li><li>Working Butt Set with RJ11 connector</li><li>Punch down tool with 66 &amp; 110 blades</li><li>2-3 way Splitter Adapters (for contingency use on alarm lines if directed by support)</li><li>Label maker and Sharpie</li><li>Tone generator and probe</li><li>Smartphone with camera</li><li>Digital Multimeter (Fluke or similar)</li><li>Laptop with Ethernet port, serial port or USB adapter, and TeamViewer or AnyDesk</li><li>Mobile hotspot or tethering</li><li>Console cable</li><li>Cable toner</li><li>Cable crimper</li><li>Electrical multimeter</li><li>300 ft of CAT5e or Cat6 cable</li><li>Cross connect wire</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 jacks</li><li>Modular plugs</li><li>Power drill</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Site Survey (If Required)</strong></p><p>If requested, technician will complete a quick site survey and collect the following:</p><ul><li>Device Health: Pass / Fail</li><li>Access to Panel: Yes / No</li><li>Key on Site: Yes / No</li><li>Lock Number: ****</li><li>Site Mainline: --*</li><li>Alarm panel cable run: ** ft x #</li></ul><p>Technicians must take and review site pictures with support. (Photo examples will be attached.)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>COLLATERAL REQUIRED – CUTOVER ALARM</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures required</li><li>Data remote shipped</li><li>Data remote information (Sticker serial number)</li><li>Burglar alarm panel with door closed</li><li>Burglar alarm panel with door open (If no key is available, take a picture of the key lock alarm panel number)</li><li>Alarm panel keypad</li><li>Location where data remote will be mounted (Before and after)</li><li>Wide angle of Data remote installed, working area, connections</li><li>In case of cable run, please take a picture from different angles and materials used</li><li>Signed work order</li></ul><p>Must be submitted immediately after job completion, or within 24 hours at the latest. If not received within this timeframe, the job will be closed without payment. Please send to: documents@tech-americas.com</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Administrative &amp; Compliance Information</strong></p><p><strong>On-Time Arrival</strong></p><p>Technicians are expected to arrive on time for all assignments. If a technician arrives late and is dismissed for this reason, no payment will be issued.</p><p><strong>Check-in / Check-out</strong></p><ul><li>Call Tech Americas to check in upon arrival by calling: 281-668-3211 option 3.</li><li>Call Tech Americas to check out right after completing the job by calling: 281-668-3211 option 3.</li><li>FAILURE TO CALL BOTH WILL RESULT IN PAYMENT DEDUCTION OR NO PAYMENT.</li><li>If there is a delay getting a response, send an email to support@tech-americas.com with all your check-in and check-out details.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If No Work Is Performed / No Access</strong></p><ul><li>Take site photos proving on-site presence (e.g., photo in front of the building, access point, or site signage).</li><li>Alternatively, obtain a signed paper work order from an authorized on-site contact confirming presence and access denial.</li><li>Email this proof to documents@tech-americas.com and call (281) 668-3211 or email support@tech-americas.com before departure.</li><li>Failure to provide this proof will place payment at risk.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech Americas Contacts</strong></p><ul><li>Evelyn Vasquez: (346) 615-1333, eavasquez@tech-americas.com</li><li>Karen Palma: (646) 786-1509, kpalma@tech-americas.com</li><li>Cristo Guevara: (254) 308-6718, cguevara@tech-americas.com</li><li>Aida Flores: 210-830-7125, aflores@tech-americas.com</li><li>Erick Vasquez: 832-913-1539, egvasquez@tech-americas.com</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>VALID U.S. IDENTIFICATION REQUIRED</strong></p><p>Technicians must carry a valid Enhanced Real ID or Enhanced Driver’s License. If not available, one of the following must also be presented:</p><ul><li>U.S. passport or passport card</li><li>DHS Trusted Traveler Card (Global Entry, SENTRI, etc.)</li><li>U.S. Department of Defense ID</li><li>Permanent Resident Card</li><li>Border Crossing Card</li><li>ID issued by a federally recognized Tribal Nation</li><li>HSPD-12 PIV Card</li><li>Foreign Passport</li><li>Canadian Provincial License or Indian Affairs Card</li><li>Transportation Worker ID</li><li>USCIS Employment Authorization Card</li><li>U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential</li><li>Veteran Health Identification Card</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code</strong></p><p>All technicians must dress professionally while on site:</p><ul><li>Plain T-shirt (preferably polo)</li><li>Jeans or khakis (not tattered or torn)</li></ul><p><strong>Important – Compliance Requirement</strong></p><ul><li>If a customer issues a complaint regarding inappropriate dress code, payment will be at risk due to non-compliance.</li><li>Technicians must also maintain proper hygiene and avoid strong or unpleasant odors, as these may create escalations with the customer and jeopardize payment.</li><li>Consistent professionalism in appearance and presentation is required to protect both Tech Americas’ reputation and technician assignments.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>General Notes</strong></p><p>*** Before you submit your application for any upcoming job, please make sure to verify your availability first. This helps us avoid last-minute cancellations and ensures smoother coordination on both ends. ***</p><p>*** We appreciate your interest and commitment and look forward to working with technicians who are fully available and ready to take on the assignments as scheduled. ***</p><p>*** BRING A LAPTOP WITH TEAMVIEWER, CONSOLE CABLE, AND INTERNET ACCESS ***</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":54.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-1