{"job":{"id":20222570,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walmart - Epson P7370 Poster Printer Service - Troubleshooting Error Code 1418  - 2 Hours Onsite - Windows Laptop and USB-A Cable Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services performing service on a Walmart Epson P7370 poster printer located in the Photo Center. The service will be troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and any parts sent that we determine need to be replaced to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>**YOU MUST HAVE THE EPSON SERVICE PROGRAM BEFORE HEADING TO SITE**<br /><br />**CONTACT SUPPORT WHEN YOU GET ONSITE**<br /><br />Work with support to troubleshoot the error code 1418 and ispect the printer for possible causes. Get required test prints to verify printer functionality.<br /><br />FIN: 294148</p><p><strong><u>﻿PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>No Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.</p><p><strong><u>WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:</em></p><p><strong>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK</strong></p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm Epson P7370 WFP Poster Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Windows Based Laptop</li><li>USB-A to USB-B Printer Cable&nbsp;</li><li>Voltmeter</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li><strong>IT IS REQUIRED</strong>&nbsp;that you watch the printer overview video link&nbsp;<strong>https://fx3.training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBODNHRK</strong>&nbsp;and then from the same link&nbsp;<strong>DOWNLOAD</strong>&nbsp;the driver and program software from the \"<strong>Shared Files</strong>\" folder to your laptop and install them.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><strong>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBSDNHRK</strong></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the&nbsp;<strong>Customer Service desk</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;notify them&nbsp;that you are a vendor&nbsp;representing&nbsp;<strong>Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center</strong>. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla&nbsp;In‑Store&nbsp;ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the&nbsp;<strong>upper left side of your shirt</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: white;\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: white;\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: white;\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>production print to verify the printer functionality.</strong></li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: white;\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: white;\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: white;\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to confirm deliverables and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition <strong>https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961</strong>. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location</strong>. All returns must be dropped off at a&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup center</strong>, and a&nbsp;<strong>receipt must be&nbsp;retained</strong>&nbsp;to confirm transfer of possession.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature</strong>, and check out of the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>&nbsp;before leaving the location.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><em>Post-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Take the return parts package to a local&nbsp;<strong>FedEx Pickup Center</strong>, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is&nbsp;<strong>not compensated&nbsp;</strong>for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.</li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li><strong>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the <strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>, <strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>, <strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong> and <strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li><li>If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call&nbsp;<del>***** ********</del>&nbsp;and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services performing service on a Walmart Epson P7370 poster printer located in the Photo Center. The service will be troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and any parts sent that we determine need to be replaced to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\n\\*\\*YOU MUST HAVE THE EPSON SERVICE PROGRAM BEFORE HEADING TO SITE\\*\\*  \n  \n\\*\\*CONTACT SUPPORT WHEN YOU GET ONSITE\\*\\*  \n  \nWork with support to troubleshoot the error code 1418 and ispect the printer for possible causes. Get required test prints to verify printer functionality.  \n  \nFIN: 294148\n\n**﻿PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nNo Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.\n\n**WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:**\n\n*Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:*\n\n**<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK>**\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm Epson P7370 WFP Poster Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Windows Based Laptop\n- USB-A to USB-B Printer Cable\n- Voltmeter\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. **IT IS REQUIRED** that you watch the printer overview video link **<https://fx3.training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBODNHRK>** and then from the same link **DOWNLOAD** the driver and program software from the \"**Shared Files**\" folder to your laptop and install them.\n4. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n**<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZBSDNHRK>**\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app**. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the **Customer Service desk** and notify them that you are a vendor representing **Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center**. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla In‑Store ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the **upper left side of your shirt**.\n2. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n3. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n4. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n5. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **production print to verify the printer functionality.**\n6. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n7. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition **https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961**. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n8. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n9. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n10. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n11. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n12. **Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location**. All returns must be dropped off at a **FedEx pickup center**, and a **receipt must be retained** to confirm transfer of possession.\n13. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, obtain their **signature**, and check out of the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app** before leaving the location.\n\n*Post-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Take the return parts package to a local **FedEx Pickup Center**, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is **not compensated** for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- **<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>**\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n- If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T09:00","end":"2026-10-22T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-22T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":116.7184591804066},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 116.7184591804066mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fair festival"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792683494444}
{"job":{"id":20224911,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Voyix - Restaurants","title":"Tech for Hospitality Site Inspection Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">High Level Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Complete Inventory on the hardware delivered to the site</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Complete a walk through with the customer to collect photos of the locations where hardware will later be Installed</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">Link to Fast Fields Form: </strong><strong><del>****************************</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact Information details:</strong></p><p>Call Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin, then enter QuickBase Work Order <span style=\"color: rgb(7, 4, 13);\">104464</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>**NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attached Documentation</strong> - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole</p><p><br></p><p><strong>BASICS</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears</li><li>Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in</li><li>Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn</li><li>Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over</li><li>No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn</li><li>NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site</li></ul><p><strong>Behavior:</strong></p><ul><li>Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support</li><li>Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite</li><li>No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite</li><li>No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff</li><li>No music to be played, including through headphones</li><li>Follow all direction of the remote support contact</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;Documents:</strong></p><ul><li>NCR WO</li><li>Site Inspection Documentation</li><li>NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info</li><li>Any other Supporting Documents Provided</li></ul><p><strong>TOOLING</strong></p><p><strong>Standard Tooling:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>32G Thumb drive</li><li>Data transfer cable &amp; USB to SATA docking station</li><li>Screwdriver set - Standard &amp; Precision</li><li>Adjustable, Allen &amp; Socket wrench sets</li><li>Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester</li><li>Wire Cutters</li><li>Level</li><li>Outlet tester</li><li>USB keyboard &amp; Mouse</li><li>Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes &amp; bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)</li><li>Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management</li><li>Box, Electrical &amp; Masking tape</li><li>Assorted screws &amp; anchors</li><li>Packing Tape</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE</strong></p><p><strong>Hardware</strong>: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface.&nbsp;DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location.&nbsp;Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Do Not Disrupt: </strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Clean as You Go:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers</span>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Questions or Concerns: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support </span>immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation<span style=\"color: black;\">.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>Timelines: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Cancellation Policy:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Turnaways</strong>&nbsp;-</p><ul><li><strong>Arrival up to 1 hour</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to $50</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>1 hour - 2 hours</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate -</strong>&nbsp;I<strong>f work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>Travel Expense</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional hours</strong></p><ul><li><strong>To Ensure Payment Approval</strong>&nbsp;- Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours</li><li><strong>Anticipated Expenses</strong>&nbsp;like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion</li></ul>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**High Level Scope of Work:**\n\n**Complete Inventory on the hardware delivered to the site**\n\n**Complete a walk through with the customer to collect photos of the locations where hardware will later be Installed**\n\n**Link to Fast Fields Form:** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Contact Information details:**\n\nCall Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin, then enter QuickBase Work Order 104464\n\n**\\*\\*NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.**\n\n**Attached Documentation** - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole\n\n**BASICS**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears\n- Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in\n- Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn\n- Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over\n- No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn\n- NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n- Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support\n- Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite\n- No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite\n- No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff\n- No music to be played, including through headphones\n- Follow all direction of the remote support contact\n\n **Documents:**\n\n- NCR WO\n- Site Inspection Documentation\n- NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info\n- Any other Supporting Documents Provided\n\n**TOOLING**\n\n**Standard Tooling:**\n\n- Laptop\n- 32G Thumb drive\n- Data transfer cable & USB to SATA docking station\n- Screwdriver set - Standard & Precision\n- Adjustable, Allen & Socket wrench sets\n- Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester\n- Wire Cutters\n- Level\n- Outlet tester\n- USB keyboard & Mouse\n- Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes & bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)\n- Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management\n- Box, Electrical & Masking tape\n- Assorted screws & anchors\n- Packing Tape\n\n**BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE**\n\n**Hardware**: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface. DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location. Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed\n\n**Do Not Disrupt:**\n\n- You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.\n- Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.\n\n**Clean as You Go:** Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers\n\n**Questions or Concerns:** Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation.\n\n**Timelines:** If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.\n\n***Cancellation Policy:***\n\n**Turnaways** -\n\n- **Arrival up to 1 hour**\n- **Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to $50**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **1 hour - 2 hours**\n- **Hourly Rate -** I**f work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **Travel Expense**\n- **Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment**\n\n**Additional hours**\n\n- **To Ensure Payment Approval** - Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours\n- **Anticipated Expenses** like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00","end":"2026-11-02T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructu