{"job":{"id":20225152,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Elevator Alert Line Install & Cable Run ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technician must supply all cable and materials and expense back to TDX including white Cat6 cable, Qty 2 Cat6 jacks, Qty 2 surface mount boxes, Qty 2 rj11 phone cords. </strong></p><p>The technician will be installing a new Alert Line device at the network rack for the store elevator &amp; completing a Cat6 cable run from the network rack to the elevator control room location where the existing phone line resides.</p><p>Upon arrival the technician should survey the locations of the network rack and elevator control room to determine a cable pathway and review findings with the TDX support team. If there is no feasible cable pathway or the cable run will require additional resources such as a lift or multiple technicians, technician should reach out to TDX support team to review options. </p><p>Technician will terminate each end of the Cat6 cable with a Cat6 keystone jack and patch into the MyLink Alert line device and elevator control panel using rj11 phone cords. </p><p>The technician must will complete a test call from the Elevator to ensure it connects to Alert Line operator. Advise the operator that you are testing a new elevator alert line at Barnes &amp; Noble and would like to verify if they can see the cellular signal strength on the MyLink Alert Line device. </p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u></strong></p><p>Work Order (attached in documents section)</p><p>Network Tool Kit (Toner/tester/punch down etc)</p><p>CAT 6 Cable &amp; Cabling Materials - Qty 2 Cat6 keystone jacks, Qty 2 surface-mount boxes,</p><p>Qty 2 RJ11 phone cords - 7ft or longer</p><p>Fish Tape</p><p>Label Maker</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Basic PC Tool Kit</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Work Description:</u></strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check in/out with the TDX help desk at 952-912-9222</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Complete site survey to determine feasible pathway for new Cat6 cable run between network cabinet and elevator control room. Review findings with TDX support team. </p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install the new Alert Line device on top of the network cabinet or backboard directly behind the network cabinet.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Complete the required Cat6 cable run and terminate as directed with a keystone jack and surface-mount box at each end.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Use technician supplied rj11 cable to patch from the Cat6 keystone jack to the rj11 port on the new Alert Line device.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Use technician supplied rj11 cable to patch from the Cat6 keystone jack to the rj11 port on the elevator control panel.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Test the new alert line to ensure it connects to the Alert Line operator.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take photos showing the completed terminations on each end and the installed Alert Line device at the network rack.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take photos showing the cellular signal and status light sequence on the Alert Line device. </p>","markdown":"**Technician must supply all cable and materials and expense back to TDX including white Cat6 cable, Qty 2 Cat6 jacks, Qty 2 surface mount boxes, Qty 2 rj11 phone cords.**\n\nThe technician will be installing a new Alert Line device at the network rack for the store elevator & completing a Cat6 cable run from the network rack to the elevator control room location where the existing phone line resides.\n\nUpon arrival the technician should survey the locations of the network rack and elevator control room to determine a cable pathway and review findings with the TDX support team. If there is no feasible cable pathway or the cable run will require additional resources such as a lift or multiple technicians, technician should reach out to TDX support team to review options.\n\nTechnician will terminate each end of the Cat6 cable with a Cat6 keystone jack and patch into the MyLink Alert line device and elevator control panel using rj11 phone cords.\n\nThe technician must will complete a test call from the Elevator to ensure it connects to Alert Line operator. Advise the operator that you are testing a new elevator alert line at Barnes & Noble and would like to verify if they can see the cellular signal strength on the MyLink Alert Line device.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nWork Order (attached in documents section)\n\nNetwork Tool Kit (Toner/tester/punch down etc)\n\nCAT 6 Cable & Cabling Materials - Qty 2 Cat6 keystone jacks, Qty 2 surface-mount boxes,\n\nQty 2 RJ11 phone cords - 7ft or longer\n\nFish Tape\n\nLabel Maker\n\nLadder\n\nBasic PC Tool Kit\n\n**Work Description:**\n\n• Check in/out with the TDX help desk at 952-912-9222\n\n• Complete site survey to determine feasible pathway for new Cat6 cable run between network cabinet and elevator control room. Review findings with TDX support team.\n\n• Install the new Alert Line device on top of the network cabinet or backboard directly behind the network cabinet.\n\n• Complete the required Cat6 cable run and terminate as directed with a keystone jack and surface-mount box at each end.\n\n• Use technician supplied rj11 cable to patch from the Cat6 keystone jack to the rj11 port on the new Alert Line device.\n\n• Use technician supplied rj11 cable to patch from the Cat6 keystone jack to the rj11 port on the elevator control panel.\n\n• Test the new alert line to ensure it connects to the Alert Line operator.\n\n• Take photos showing the completed terminations on each end and the installed Alert Line device at the network rack.\n\n• Take photos showing the cellular signal and status light sequence on the Alert Line device.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T10:00","end":"2026-10-30T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":11.385649663337698},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792685253952}
{"job":{"id":20225204,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Switch – Troubleshooting – Port 21 / Call Tech Support While Onsite","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of work: Tech need to check physical connectivity with switch H2 port 21 Tech need to carry LAN cable Onsite Instructions: Once onsite, the technician must call <del>*** *** ** ***************</del> and follow the prompts: Option 1 → Option 1 → Option 2 This is required for signoff, verification, or any access-related issues</em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: Switch H2 MAR0657AP01 offline</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part pickup required: N/A</em></p>\n<p><em>Helpdesk number : <del>*************** ****** * ** * **** ********** ****** ** ****** * ** *</del> (Non-server or Server support)</em></p>\n<p><em>Security code access: <del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer incident number: <del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Please review the repair plans in the link below</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***********************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>If assistance is needed, please call: <del>************ ****** * *</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************</del></em><em><del>***</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em>