{"job":{"id":20225600,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Genlogs","title":"Sensor Reboot.- NC.I95.SB.87 (#0318)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>Please note that this work location is outdoors and may require traversing through snow, mud, or otherwise to get to the sensor site.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><p>In the event of an outage at a site that is not resolved automatically by either power restoration or our integrated failsafe mechanisms, the Trident sensor may require physical intervention in order to reboot the unit.</p><p><strong>You will need:</strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Volt meter</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wire cutters (<em>for tamper-proof lock</em>)</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Flathead screwdriver (<em>for twist-lock cabinets</em>)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Pre-visit site review call with the Work Order Manager at <del>***** ********</del></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Process:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Locate the <del>*******</del> hardware cabinet</strong> – Typically mounted at ground level, the control unit should sit adjacent to the electrical panel on the structure. Depending on the Trident model, you may need to cut the tamper-proof lock or use a screwdriver to unlock the cabinet</li><li><strong>Confirm power at the hardware cabinet and electrical panel </strong>– Confirm power delivery to our hardware cabinet as well as the electrical panel in order to root out if it is a power issue and whether that is on the main breaker panel (utility side) or the load side (delivery to our box)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If power issue is identified, please report your findings to the <del>*******</del> team</li><li><strong>Reboot CPU and Peplink router</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If cellular and status lights are not displaying on the router, following the router reboot steps found in the <em>Router Troubleshooting &amp; SIM Installation</em> process to reconnect it to the network</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Confirm the CPU is powered on by checking for faint-blue light emitting from the power button. Press and hold the power button for 15s, then release, followed by a single press and release</li><li><strong>Confirm all internal connections are seated and secured tightly</strong> – Double check all cable connections, especially those that deliver power to hardware, as they can become dislodged over time</li></ol><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific photo requirements are dependent on the tasks performed and will be communicated upon the resolution of the issue</li><li>Confirmation from <del>*******</del> team that work has been completed or approval to leave site has been given.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Communication Directory: </strong></p><ul><li>If clarification, issues or questions is needed on work order, discuss with&nbsp;Work Order Manager at <del>***** ********</del></li><li>IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact:</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE: During your visit, please perform a general visual inspection of the site. If you observe any abnormal or unusual conditions—including, but not limited to, billboard damage, electrical issues, installation deficiencies, loose or exposed wiring, missing conduits, unsealed penetrations, signs of tampering, or any other condition that appears out of the ordinary—please document the issue with clear photos and notify us immediately before leaving the site.</strong></p>","markdown":"***Please note that this work location is outdoors and may require traversing through snow, mud, or otherwise to get to the sensor site.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nIn the event of an outage at a site that is not resolved automatically by either power restoration or our integrated failsafe mechanisms, the Trident sensor may require physical intervention in order to reboot the unit.\n\n**You will need:**\n\n● Volt meter\n\n● Wire cutters (*for tamper-proof lock*)\n\n● Flathead screwdriver (*for twist-lock cabinets*)\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Pre-visit site review call with the Work Order Manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Process:**\n\n1. **Locate the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* hardware cabinet** – Typically mounted at ground level, the control unit should sit adjacent to the electrical panel on the structure. Depending on the Trident model, you may need to cut the tamper-proof lock or use a screwdriver to unlock the cabinet\n2. **Confirm power at the hardware cabinet and electrical panel** – Confirm power delivery to our hardware cabinet as well as the electrical panel in order to root out if it is a power issue and whether that is on the main breaker panel (utility side) or the load side (delivery to our box)\n3. If power issue is identified, please report your findings to the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team\n4. **Reboot CPU and Peplink router**\n5. If cellular and status lights are not displaying on the router, following the router reboot steps found in the *Router Troubleshooting & SIM Installation* process to reconnect it to the network\n6. Confirm the CPU is powered on by checking for faint-blue light emitting from the power button. Press and hold the power button for 15s, then release, followed by a single press and release\n7. **Confirm all internal connections are seated and secured tightly** – Double check all cable connections, especially those that deliver power to hardware, as they can become dislodged over time\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n- Specific photo requirements are dependent on the tasks performed and will be communicated upon the resolution of the issue\n- Confirmation from \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team that work has been completed or approval to leave site has been given.\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- If clarification, issues or questions is needed on work order, discuss with Work Order Manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- IF you're unable to reach WO Manager, back up contact:\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager\n\n**NOTE: During your visit, please perform a general visual inspection of the site. If you observe any abnormal or unusual conditions—including, but not limited to, billboard damage, electrical issues, installation deficiencies, loose or exposed wiring, missing conduits, unsealed penetrations, signs of tampering, or any other condition that appears out of the ordinary—please document the issue with clear photos and notify us immediately before leaving the site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":165,"max":165},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":35.686879904764865},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-1