{"job":{"id":20227131,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Circle Computer Resources","title":"Troubleshoot router(s) solution; test; take pictures","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Parts Needed:</strong></p><p>- Basic Tools/Power Drill</p><p>- Laptop (Windows 7 OS (or newer) is required. Laptop must have Chrome or Firefox.)</p><p>- Winbox (Included in downloads)</p><p>- Cat5 crimpers</p><p>- Cable Tester</p><p>- Compass</p><p>- Lag Bolts; Self Tapping Screws or similar to mount equipment</p><p>- Ladder (at least 6' - 10' tall in the case on site ladder is locked)</p><p>-Wifi Hot Spot</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Description:</strong></p><p><strong>Tech will need to bring an ID to the assignment and wear vendor neutral attire (unless it is your company's name/logo).</strong></p><p>Check in with&nbsp;Jesse<strong>&nbsp;</strong>once you arrive at the site by calling CCR Tech at <strong>319-242-6552.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech will be expected to provide progress updates regularly. If tech has a question at any point, please call the number provided for the support contact. </strong></p><p>Speak with the manager on duty to locate the CCR Equipment that is onsite. Once the CCR equipment has been located, work with&nbsp;Jesse&nbsp;to the current connection.&nbsp;</p><p>Check to ensure all equipment is powered up or plugged into a reliable power source.&nbsp;</p><p>Check to ensure all cables are plugged into the router and associated equipment. If all equipment is powered up and we still do not have a connection, tech will need to do a cable test to ensure that the cables are crimped correctly. </p><p>Tech may all need laptop into the router on site for testing. </p><p>Once all testing is completed and the circuit has been either confirmed up or down by the CCR tech, the tech will need to provide updated pictures of all the equipment <strong>(Router, POE, Enclosure and Antenna/s)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Router and PoE will need to be placed somewhere accessible, no more than 5 feet off the ground so Managers are able to access equipment. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Tech will need to ensure that all equipment is secured properly. Tech will need to ensure that pictures are uploaded to the work order and confirmed by CCR tech before leaving the site. If any equipment is being returned, the tech is responsible for packaging the equipment securely, so it will not be damaged in transit. Cost of packing materials is included in the price of the work order.</p><p><strong>The work order will not be completed until we have&nbsp;received all&nbsp;of the equipment that was due for return.&nbsp;</strong>If the tech leaves before calling, getting authorization and completing the work, the work order will not be paid until it is completed.</p>","markdown":"**Parts Needed:**\n\n\\- Basic Tools/Power Drill\n\n\\- Laptop (Windows 7 OS (or newer) is required. Laptop must have Chrome or Firefox.)\n\n\\- Winbox (Included in downloads)\n\n\\- Cat5 crimpers\n\n\\- Cable Tester\n\n\\- Compass\n\n\\- Lag Bolts; Self Tapping Screws or similar to mount equipment\n\n\\- Ladder (at least 6' - 10' tall in the case on site ladder is locked)\n\n-Wifi Hot Spot\n\n**Description:**\n\n**Tech will need to bring an ID to the assignment and wear vendor neutral attire (unless it is your company's name/logo).**\n\nCheck in with Jesse once you arrive at the site by calling CCR Tech at **319-242-6552.**\n\n**Tech will be expected to provide progress updates regularly. If tech has a question at any point, please call the number provided for the support contact.**\n\nSpeak with the manager on duty to locate the CCR Equipment that is onsite. Once the CCR equipment has been located, work with Jesse to the current connection.\n\nCheck to ensure all equipment is powered up or plugged into a reliable power source.\n\nCheck to ensure all cables are plugged into the router and associated equipment. If all equipment is powered up and we still do not have a connection, tech will need to do a cable test to ensure that the cables are crimped correctly.\n\nTech may all need laptop into the router on site for testing.\n\nOnce all testing is completed and the circuit has been either confirmed up or down by the CCR tech, the tech will need to provide updated pictures of all the equipment **(Router, POE, Enclosure and Antenna/s)**\n\n**Router and PoE will need to be placed somewhere accessible, no more than 5 feet off the ground so Managers are able to access equipment.**\n\n**Disclaimer:**\n\nTech will need to ensure that all equipment is secured properly. Tech will need to ensure that pictures are uploaded to the work order and confirmed by CCR tech before leaving the site. If any equipment is being returned, the tech is responsible for packaging the equipment securely, so it will not be damaged in transit. Cost of packing materials is included in the price of the work order.\n\n**The work order will not be completed until we have received all of the equipment that was due for return.** If the tech leaves before calling, getting authorization and completing the work, the work order will not be paid until it is completed.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-22T15:00","end":"2026-10-22T16:00","latestStart":"2026-10-22T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":85,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":37.831616245594155},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 (countered: $85) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","su