{"job":{"id":20227239,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"2i-T LLC","title":"Experienced Network Field Technician for UPS installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope Summary:</strong></p>\n<p>2i-T requires an experienced <strong>Lead Field Technician</strong> to perform an internal battery replacement of one <strong>(1) GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLNUPS</strong>, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification.</p>\n<p>This is a <strong>Vertiv customer site</strong>, and the technician must represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> professionally while onsite. YOU <strong>MUST</strong> READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.</p>\n<p><strong>SITE &amp; CONTACT INFORMATION</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Remote Engineering Contact:</strong> Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068</p>\n<p><strong>Customer:</strong> Vertiv (per dispatch details)</p>\n<p><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES &amp; TASKS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.</li>\n<li>Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.</li>\n<li>Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.</li>\n<li>Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.</li>\n<li>Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.</li>\n<li>Install new Vertiv <strong>GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN</strong> UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.</li>\n<li>Configure <strong>RDU101 network interface cards</strong> and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.</li>\n<li><strong>Upgrade firmware</strong> using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.</li>\n<li>Apply provided <strong>Vertiv service tags</strong> and verify unit labeling.</li>\n<li>Capture and upload required photos:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Units powered and plugged into outlets</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit</li>\n<li>Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.</li>\n<li>Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.</li>\n<li>Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; EQUIPMENT</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot or tethering capability</li>\n<li>Battery bank / phone charger</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools, including:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Torx T-10 bit</li>\n<li>PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area</li>\n<li>Insulated tools recommended</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).</li>\n<li>Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.</li>\n<li>Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.</li>\n<li>Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.</li>\n<li>Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE CONDUCT &amp; COMMUNICATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Represent <strong>Vertiv</strong> while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.</li>\n<li>Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.</li>\n<li>Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.</li>\n<li>Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>DELIVERABLES</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.</li>\n<li>Updated firmware confirmation.</li>\n<li>Service tags applied.</li>\n<li>Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.</li>\n<li>Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>NOTES</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>All work performed under Vertiv authorization.</li>\n<li>Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.</li>\n<li>Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.</li>\n<li>Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING</strong></p>\n<p>We published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.</p>\n<p><strong>This training is free of charge</strong> (other than your time), takes roughly <strong>1.5 hours</strong>, and once completed:</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you <em>cannot</em> normally obtain at no cost.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.</p>\n<p>To be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.</p>\n<p>If you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.</p>\n<p>Looking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em>TRAVEL AND INCIDENTAL EXPENSES – PRIOR AUTHORIZATION REQUIRED</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Travel time, mileage, parking, tolls, lodging, materials, equipment rentals, and other incidental expenses are NOT reimbursable unless specifically included in the original work order or expressly authorized in advance by 2i-T.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Travel charges or other expenses added to a Field Nation work order after the fact, including during ticket closeout, WILL NOT BE APPROVED OR PAID unless prior authorization was obtained in writing from 2i-T. Submission of a request for additional payment does not constitute authorization, regardless of whether the expense was actually incurred.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>UNAUTHORIZED CHARGES: Technicians may not independently modify agreed rates, add fees, expand the scope of work, or incur reimbursable expenses without prior authorization. Any such charges are subject to rejection by 2i-T.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Acceptance of this work order constitutes acknowledgment and agreement to these requirements.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope Summary:**\n\n2i-T requires an experienced **Lead Field Technician** to perform an internal battery replacement of one **(1) GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLNUPS**, including installation, configuration, firmware upgrade, and startup verification.\n\nThis is a **Vertiv customer site**, and the technician must represent **Vertiv** professionally while onsite. YOU **MUST** READ the note concerning Vertiv training at the bottom on this ticket prior to requesting this ticket.\n\n**SITE & CONTACT INFORMATION**\n\n**Remote Engineering Contact:** Jim Bigley – 715-965-0068\n\n**Customer:** Vertiv (per dispatch details)\n\n**RESPONSIBILITIES & TASKS**\n\n- Arrive onsite as scheduled and check in with the site contact.\n- Contact 2i-T Project Manager and remote engineer (Jim Bigley) prior to beginning work.\n- Verify existing equipment serial numbers and report any discrepancies.\n- Obtain confirmation from remote engineer and customer before removing existing units.\n- Safely de-energize, disconnect, and remove existing UPS and battery cabinets, if any.\n- Install new Vertiv **GXT5-3000LVRT2UXLN** UPS per manufacturer and Vertiv procedures.\n- Configure **RDU101 network interface cards** and verify connectivity with Vertiv engineering.\n- **Upgrade firmware** using the BIN file downloaded from the tasks section prior to arrival.\n- Apply provided **Vertiv service tags** and verify unit labeling.\n- Capture and upload required photos:\n- Installed UPS and battery cabinet (in same frame)\n- Units powered and plugged into outlets\n- Web GUI IPv4 page for each unit\n- Confirm operation with remote engineer prior to leaving site.\n- Remove all packaging/debris from the area and leave the site clean.\n- Upload all required documentation and photos within 24 hours of job completion.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS & EQUIPMENT**\n\n- Laptop (Windows 10 or 11) with admin rights and TeamViewer installed\n- Multimeter\n- Label maker (two cartridges minimum, black-on-white tape)\n- Mobile hotspot or tethering capability\n- Battery bank / phone charger\n- Standard hand tools, including:\n- Power drill/driver with #2 and #3 Phillips bits\n- Manual #1 Phillips screwdriver\n- Torx T-10 bit\n- PPE: safety glasses, leather gloves, long-sleeve FR shirt, jeans, safety footwear; hard hat if in active construction area\n- Insulated tools recommended\n\n**QUALIFICATIONS**\n\n- Prior experience installing and commissioning UPS systems (preferably Liebert or Vertiv GXT series).\n- Capable of independently lifting up to 50 lbs.\n- Familiar with network configuration and firmware upgrade processes.\n- Must have laptop prepared with required BIN file before arrival.\n- Must review 2i-T UPS Installation Safety Guidelines and site checklist prior to dispatch.\n\n**ON-SITE CONDUCT & COMMUNICATION**\n\n- Represent **Vertiv** while onsite. Do not present yourself as 2i-T or Field Nation to end customer personnel.\n- Maintain professional demeanor and safety compliance at all times.\n- Communicate arrival, progress, and departure with both the 2i-T Project Manager and the remote engineer.\n- Do not leave site without confirmation from the remote engineer and 2i-T PM that all tasks are complete.\n\n**DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Verified installation and startup of UPS and EBC.\n- Updated firmware confirmation.\n- Service tags applied.\n- Required photos uploaded within 24 hours.\n- Completed 2i-T Dispatch Checklist uploaded with work order.\n\n**NOTES**\n\n- All work performed under Vertiv authorization.\n- Existing UPS units and battery cabinets to be recycled through approved channels.\n- Access, parking, and loading dock details provided in dispatch.\n- Network configuration parameters (IP address, subnet, gateway) will be included in the confidential section of the ticket.\n\n**MANDATORY VERTIV GXT5 TRAINING**\n\nWe published this ticket because we need to have a technician onsite for a Vertiv GTX5 installation and start-up for a customer. We are also ramping up a steady pipeline of Vertiv GTX5 installation work in this region, and we want to build a reliable roster of qualified technicians who can take these tickets with confidence. Vertiv requires that all techs performing this scope complete their online installation training.\n\n**This training is free of charge** (other than your time), takes roughly **1.5 hours**, and once completed:\n\n· You’ll be fully qualified for all Vertiv-related GXT5 installation tickets we issue.\n\n· You’ll receive priority consideration for future tickets in your area.\n\n· You’ll be able to add the Vertiv qualification to your FN profile, which is a credential you *cannot* normally obtain at no cost.\n\n· We will also give you priority for other structured-cabling and power-equipment work that we have going forward in your region.\n\nTo be candid: if you’re not willing to invest 90 minutes to properly qualify yourself, then this probably isn’t the right type of work for you—or the right fit for us. We want techs who take pride in their craft and are committed to doing the job the right way.\n\nIf you want to move forward, message us directly and we’ll send you the training link and instructions.\n\nLooking forward to building a strong bench for these deployments.\n\n***TRAVEL AND INCIDENTAL EXPENSES – PRIOR AUTHORIZATION REQUIRED***\n\n***Travel time, mileage, parking, tolls, lodging, materials, equipment rentals, and other incidental expenses are NOT reimbursable unless specifically included in the original work order or expressly authorized in advance by 2i-T.***\n\n***Travel charges or other expenses added to a Field Nation work order after the fact, including during ticket closeout, WILL NOT BE APPROVED OR PAID unless prior authorization was obtained in writing from 2i-T. Submission of a request for additional payment does not constitute authorization, regardless of whether the expense was actually incurred.***\n\n***UNAUTHORIZED CHARGES: Technicians may not independently modify agreed rates, add fees, expand the scope of work, or incur reimbursable expenses without prior authorization. Any such charges are subject to rejection by 2i-T.***\n\n***Acceptance of this work order constitutes acknowledgment and agreement to these requirements.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T08:00","end":"2026-10-29T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":145},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.78559070548684},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $145 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792695685629}
{"job":{"id":"4533434948","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"INT13880424  ––T1872 –Durham, NC   Music/sound Player off line Ladder","description":"<p>T1872 - Image sound Player showing offline .</p><p><br></p><p>**Initial Description/Overview** INT13880424&nbsp;––T1872 –Durham, NC&nbsp;&nbsp;Music/sound Player off line Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>**\\*See Target Store Tech Tips for TOA attachment for tool recommendations\\***</p><p><br></p><p>\\*\\*\\***UPON ARRIVAL:** TECH MUST CALL GRANITE **TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761#**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>* Proceed to the Guest Service Desk, provide Identification and ask for a Designated Leader Jeorah Gilliam</p><p>* When meeting designated leader, provide the above incident number and reason for the service call, determine location of service call. Designated Store Lead will direct you to the package with replacement part that was delivered \\(see below for tracking details\\)&nbsp;</p><p>* If the store refuses the technician and work, the technician should ask the store leader/designated leader to call the CSC with the above incident number and service call number SR0087021</p><p><br></p><p>* **If Control Room Access is required, please reach out to CSC 612-304-4357 to obtain code – Tech Must read the attached Control Room Access and Regulations documents before requesting access.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**ISSUE** T1872 - Image sound Player showing offline .</p><p>**Tech must call Granite rep before leaving site to verify testing and final check out.&nbsp;DO NOT leave site without approval from your Granite Rep.**</p><p><br></p><p>**T2230 - In store music not working in specific location of store**</p><p>**Replacement Device /Equipment Info/Tracking**</p><p>**Return Visit to Tone and Trace and replace Cable for Zone 6 – Beauty Section.**</p><p>T1872 - Image sound Player showing offline .</p><p>The store has confirmed that music is playing through all the speakers. However, the Imagesound player is still showing as offline.</p><p><br></p><p>Kindly arrange a technician visit to the store to check the Imagesound player's network connectivity and investigate the offline status.</p><p>Outbound Tracking: Tech check Player</p><p>Return Tracking Provided: Tech check Player</p><p>Outbound UPN\\(s\\): Tech check Player</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**Closeout Checklist:**</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirm ALL devices online with designated leader.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Call **TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761#** to check out BEFORE leaving.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide before and after pictures of devices worked on</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Picture of SN#\\(s\\) one of existing/old and one of new/replaced equipment</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of certified cable tests</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of termination points</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Record first and last name of site contact and support contact you worked with</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;**If equipment was shipped,** Box up unused equipment \\(old or new\\) with return label provided and TECH is responsible for dropping off at a UPS location, a picture of the return label and the receipt from UPS at drop off is a required deliverable</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**REQUIRED MATERIALS /TOOLS: Tech MUST have the following:**</p><p>**\\*Impedance Tester\\***</p><p>Laptop with power supply and USB to RS-232C converter cable</p><p>Cat5/Cat6 cable tester</p><p>Min 500ft CAT6 cable \\(White preferred\\)</p><p>CAT6 Jacks</p><p>CAT6 Patch cords various lengths</p><p>Basic hand tools</p><p>Pliers</p><p>Assorted screwdrivers</p><p>Precision screwdriver set</p><p>Drill</p><p>Velcro for cable management</p><p>Label maker \\(P touch or equivalent\\)</p><p>Patch cables</p><p>Cable tester Toner and Probe</p><p>Camera/Smart phone</p><p>8-10' Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES/Closing Info:**</p><p>Failure to provide the following may result in delayed payment.</p><p>Before and after photos showing device\\(s\\) worked on</p><p>Capture Clear Pictures SN#'s of existing equipment and replacement equipment</p><p>Manage cables neatly and cleanup work area\\(s\\).</p><p>Confirm all devices are online and working properly before leaving site</p><p>Picture of the return label AND the receipt from UPS at drop off</p><p>Record name of site contact that has verified work completed at closing</p><p>SIGNED work order.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**If Issue/SOW is unable to be resolved**, take necessary photos showing device\\(s\\), cable test results and any other problems preventing resolution, please describe findings and what was done on site.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T06:00","end":"2026-10-26T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Sur