{"job":{"id":"6962016056","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"ServiceP (PreferredTechs LLC)","title":"Site Survey - Digital Signage - (13) - 10.1\" Bluefins , (12)-21.5\" Bluefins (4) - 50\" Displays (1) 32\"Display","description":"<p><strong>MANDATORY</strong>:</p><ol><li>Once you arrive on site and are ready to start work, please call or text (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check in. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).</li><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact and begin work</li><li>Complete troubleshoot/installation.&nbsp;Contact support with any issues or concerns so work is completed correctly and fully.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete required deliverables (see below) and call support to confirm you have completed the full SOW.</li><li><strong><u>Text signed WO</u></strong>&nbsp;to (507-400-3227 or 405-345-1409 and 720-515-5551)</li><li><strong>REQUIRED</strong>: Call (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check out providing detailed notes of installation and any delays/issues. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Carefully open the boxes and ensure equipment is not damaged.</strong></li></ol><p><strong>Tech is needed to do a site survey for an upcoming install.</strong></p><p>Complete an onsite site readiness walkthrough for the upcomingUniguest digital signage installation.</p><p>The project includes 30 signage locations consisting of Bluefin room signs and larger SoC displays.</p><p>Please walk the planned signage locations with the property representative and document the following:</p><ul><li>Confirm each planned signage location can be identified and accessed.</li><li>Verify wall type and overall wall condition at each location.</li><li>Document existing mounting conditions and any areas requiring repair or preparation before installation.</li><li>Verify power availability at each signage location.</li><li>Verify whether a network/data drop is present at each planned signage location.</li><li>Where a live data drop is available, test the connection with a laptop or suitable network testing device to confirm the port is active and has internet connectivity.</li><li>Confirm whether DHCP addressing is received where network connectivity is available.</li><li>Document any ports that are inactive, unavailable, or require additional cabling.</li><li>Record visible data-port labels where available to help the property/IT team identify the associated network room or switch.</li><li>Identify locations requiring new low-voltage cabling or other site preparation.</li><li>Review available space/conditions for PoE equipment associated with the Bluefin room signs.</li><li>Document any access, mounting, power, cabling, or other physical conditions that could affect installation.</li><li>Take clear photos of each signage location and any identified readiness concerns.</li></ul><p><strong>Network Notes:</strong></p><p>The property is coordinating network configuration separately with Concord IT/Sonifi. Sonifi has advised that MarriottDigital Signage VLAN 810 is not currently configured and that data connectivity to the new signage locations still needs to be addressed.</p><p>Sonifi has confirmed that DHCP is normally enabled on this network and that MAC-address whitelisting is not required.</p><p>Please test any existing/live network drops during the walkthrough where possible and document the results. No VLAN configuration or other network changes are requested as part of this visit.</p><p>The purpose of this visit is to verify and document the physical site conditions, test available connectivity, and identify any remaining preparation required before installation. Internal site-readiness guidance specifically calls for live network connections to be tested before installation.Courtyard-Bistro-Instructions</p><p><br></p><p>Work order is for a site survey to view each of the following locations to verify they are ready for install. Survey each location and determine what is needed to complete the install and confirm there is data and power in place. Inform Mario of any issues or possible delays that you may encounter.</p><p>Site survey needed on the following (complete site survey form):</p><ol><li>Pictures of inventory, making sure all equipment on site and free from damage</li><li>Separate equipment that will need to be sent back toUniguest as part of the change order process (items listed below)</li><li>Pictures of the signage/PC install locations showing they are ready for install showing they have data and power ready. (Manager will show you where they will want the signage/PC installed)</li><li>Test each jack to make sure they have connectivity.</li><li>Pictures of IDF showing where the equipment will be patched in.&nbsp;</li><li>Visit each IDF where the cables for the screens go to (not just 1).</li><li>Pictures of a open shelf or area to install the POEs (confirm if locations are getting POEs or there is power at each bluefin location)</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>DETAILS FOR INSTALLATION (not on this visit - Just for reference)</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Tech will work on installing 3-50\" wall mounted displays and tilt wall mounts on the back wall of a bistro (menu displays). See placement from picture attached.</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Locate the screens and router and provide the site contact and TS Support the MAC addresses so they can work on getting them whitelisted while we are completing the physical installation.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>1 DSR-250V2 dlink router</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Installation will have to be neat and professional.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>NOTE</strong>: <u>Before installing the displays</u>, place them in a secure position and plug them in to make sure they are working. Pictures required showing they are working before going up on the wall.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>(3)-50\" Displays with tilt wall mounts</strong></p><ul><li>Site contact will show you the location on where these will be installed</li><li><strong><u>NOTE</u></strong>: Locate the screens and router and provide the site contact and TS Support the MAC addresses so they can work on getting them whitelisted while we are completing the physical installation.</li><li>There are Three screens that will be hung in a 1x3 setup. Power and data outlets exist. There is a router that will need to be reconfigured (documentation attached). The wall ethernet cables (if not active) will be plugged into the router, with one active line also plugged into the router.</li><li>Verify with site contact on how close they want it to the ceiling</li><li>Tech will install mounts to the wall making sure they are correct distance apart so when displays are installed on them, they are close to touching, level and same tilt.</li><li>Complete installation guide for the Tizen setup</li><li>Complete attachment documenting the code on the screen once Tizen setup is completed.</li><li><br></li></ul><p><strong>Equipment list:</strong></p><ul><li>(13) 10.1\" Bluefin Room signs</li><li>(12) 21.5\" Blufin Room signs</li><li>(4) 50\" LG SoC displays</li><li>(1) 32\" Samsung SoC display</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>*** Any delays <u>MUST</u> be reported. If we are on site waiting on customer or support for more than 1 hour it <u>MUST</u> be escalate to the ticket manager (Mario). Mario can be reach via call or text (see confidential info)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic Tools (screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, etc)</li><li>Copy of work order</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Work Attire</strong></p><ul><li>Long pants with no rips/tears</li><li>Polo shirt</li><li>Close toed shoes - No sandals</li><li>No hats</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Pictures/Deliverables</strong></p><ul><li>Clear photos of each planned signage location</li><li>Results of network testing where live drops are available</li><li>Identification of inactive/missing data drops</li><li>Notes on power availability and wall/mounting conditions</li><li>Summary of any outstanding site-readiness items or work required before installation</li></ul><p><br></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"}