{"job":{"id":20228054,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Voyix - Restaurants","title":"Lead Tech for Point of Sale - Refresh Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p><strong>Lead Tech to perform Refresh Installation for the following:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Server: 1</strong></li><li><strong>Switch: 1</strong></li><li><strong>Firewall: 1</strong></li><li><strong>Terminals:&nbsp;7</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Mounting Needed: Yes</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pin Pads:&nbsp;7</strong></li><li><strong>Impact printers: 2</strong></li><li><strong>Cash drawers: 3</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Notes:Rebox for OMNI pick-up</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech to bring powered SATA cable to USB device.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact Information details:</strong></p><p>Call Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin  9762, then enter  104566</p><p><br></p><p><strong>**NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attached Documentation</strong> - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole</p><p><br></p><p><strong>BASICS</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears</li><li>Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in</li><li>Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn</li><li>Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over</li><li>No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn</li><li>NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site</li></ul><p><strong>Behavior:</strong></p><ul><li>Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support</li><li>Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite</li><li>No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite</li><li>No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff</li><li>No music to be played, including through headphones</li><li>Follow all direction of the remote support contact</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;Documents:</strong></p><ul><li>NCR WO</li><li>Installation Documentation</li><li>Installation Checklist (Printed Copy or Signable Electronic Version)</li><li>NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info</li><li>Any other Supporting Documents Provided</li></ul><p><strong>TOOLING</strong></p><p><strong>Standard Tooling:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>32G Thumb drive</li><li>Data transfer cable &amp; USB to SATA docking station</li><li>Screwdriver set - Standard &amp; Precision</li><li>Adjustable, Allen &amp; Socket wrench sets</li><li>Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester</li><li>Wire Cutters</li><li>Level</li><li>Outlet tester</li><li>USB keyboard &amp; Mouse</li><li>Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes &amp; bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)</li><li>Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management</li><li>Box, Electrical &amp; Masking tape</li><li>Assorted screws &amp; anchors</li><li>Packing Tape</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE</strong></p><p><strong>Hardware</strong>: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface.&nbsp;DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location.&nbsp;Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cable Management: </strong>Cable Management must be done in a neat and professional manner. Cable routing needs to be considered carefully.&nbsp;Cabling should be bundled neatly and secured using zip ties or Velcro.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Drilling: </strong>Do not drill any holes unless approved by remote support</p><p><strong>Do Not Disrupt: </strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Clean as You Go:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers</span>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Questions or Concerns: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support </span>immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation<span style=\"color: black;\">.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>Timelines: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Cancellation Policy:</u></em> </strong></p><p><strong>Turnaways</strong>&nbsp;-</p><ul><li><strong>Arrival up to 1 hour</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to $50</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>1 hour - 2 hours</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hourly Rate -</strong>&nbsp;<strong>If work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,</strong>&nbsp;<strong>payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 &amp; 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment</strong></li><li><strong>Travel Expense</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional hours</strong></p><ul><li><strong>To Ensure Payment Approval</strong>&nbsp;- Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours</li><li><strong>Anticipated Expenses</strong>&nbsp;like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT</strong></p><ul><li>Physical Aloha Site Key (resembles a USB thumb drive) must be kept in a safe location prior to plugging into Back Office Server</li></ul>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**Lead Tech to perform Refresh Installation for the following:**\n\n- **Server: 1**\n- **Switch: 1**\n- **Firewall: 1**\n- **Terminals: 7**\n\n**Mounting Needed: Yes**\n\n- **Pin Pads: 7**\n- **Impact printers: 2**\n- **Cash drawers: 3**\n\n**Additional Notes:Rebox for OMNI pick-up**\n\n**Tech to bring powered SATA cable to USB device.**\n\n**Contact Information details:**\n\nCall Remote Support on 844-393-9464, pick option 2, enter 2 again, enter pin 9762, then enter 104566\n\n**\\*\\*NCR confirms attendance and readiness via SMS text messages and automated and live calls outside of the Field Nation platform. By accepting this work order you are opting in to receive these communications.**\n\n**Attached Documentation** - Outlines the Step-by-step installation process for all hardware devices and the project as a whole\n\n**BASICS**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Long Jeans or Khakis free of rips or tears\n- Clean Polo, collared button down, or plain colored T-Shirt (No Graphic Tees) free of rips or tears. The shirt must be tucked in\n- Closed-toe, non-slip shoes or boots. Socks to be worn\n- Belt as required. Pants must be worn professionally. Shirt and pants should cover the body when bending over\n- No hoodies, hats, or other face coverings are to be worn\n- NCR badge must be worn at all times while on site\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n- Always act and speak in a professional manner with the on-site customer, their teams, other onsite technicians, and remote support\n- Never ask for free food, drink, or anything else while onsite\n- No drug or alcohol to be used before arrival or while onsite\n- No smoking/vaping at the customer site or on the customers’ property. This includes indoors, outdoors, or within any possible view of the customer or their staff\n- No music to be played, including through headphones\n- Follow all direction of the remote support contact\n\n **Documents:**\n\n- NCR WO\n- Installation Documentation\n- Installation Checklist (Printed Copy or Signable Electronic Version)\n- NCR Point of Contact (POC) Info\n- Any other Supporting Documents Provided\n\n**TOOLING**\n\n**Standard Tooling:**\n\n- Laptop\n- 32G Thumb drive\n- Data transfer cable & USB to SATA docking station\n- Screwdriver set - Standard & Precision\n- Adjustable, Allen & Socket wrench sets\n- Standard Network Tooling with Toner/ Tester\n- Wire Cutters\n- Level\n- Outlet tester\n- USB keyboard & Mouse\n- Cordless Drill w/Various bit sizes & bit types (wood, tile, stainless steel, metal, concrete, masonry, etc.)\n- Zip Ties and/or Velcro for cable management\n- Box, Electrical & Masking tape\n- Assorted screws & anchors\n- Packing Tape\n\n**BASIC INSTALL GUIDANCE**\n\n**Hardware**: All hardware is to be located on desktop, stable shelving, network rack or other stable and secure surface. DO NOT leave hardware on the floor, buckets, chairs, or any non-secure location. Involve NCR Remote Deployment Support as needed\n\n**Cable Management:** Cable Management must be done in a neat and professional manner. Cable routing needs to be considered carefully. Cabling should be bundled neatly and secured using zip ties or Velcro.\n\n**Drilling:** Do not drill any holes unless approved by remote support\n\n**Do Not Disrupt:**\n\n- You must be extremely careful not to disturb or interrupt any business by intentionally or unintentionally powering down, breaking, or loosening cords or cables for non-NCR hardware or systems.\n- Pictures taken prior to beginning work are important here.\n\n**Clean as You Go:** Do not create a messy impression or cause difficulties for the client or their customers\n\n**Questions or Concerns:** Notify your NCR Remote Deployment Support immediately of any concerns impacting a successful installation.\n\n**Timelines:** If there are concerns about completing the requested scope of work prior to opening, please communicate with them at any time prior to this call.\n\n***Cancellation Policy:***\n\n**Turnaways** -\n\n- **Arrival up to 1 hour**\n- **Hourly Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to $50**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted following arrival and less than 1 hour onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **1 hour - 2 hours**\n- **Hourly Rate -** **If work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed,** **payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment**\n- **Fixed/Blended Rate - If work is aborted between 1 & 2 hours onsite and the Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by Max hours at assignment**\n- **Travel Expense**\n- **Travel Expense - Travel Expenses paid will be limited to stated amount at time of WO assignment**\n\n**Additional hours**\n\n- **To Ensure Payment Approval** - Additional hours above WO Max must be requested while onsite prior to working the additional hours\n- **Anticipated Expenses** like parking or tolls need to be requested prior to work completion\n\n**IMPORTANT**\n\n- Physical Aloha Site Key (resembles a USB thumb drive) must be kept in a safe location prior to plugging into Back Office Server","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-02T23:00","end":"2026-12-02T32:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":495},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":9,"distance":57.9060521679773},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":540,"estHours":9,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-04T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-05T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"