{"job":{"id":"4818248951","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"CallTek Inc","title":"A technician is needed to assist in ISP cutover.","description":"<p><strong>SNA ID:&nbsp;</strong><b>&nbsp;WO-000008133</b></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please Note:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The job is posted for one hour, but this does not guarantee it will be completed within that time.&nbsp;</p><p>- Be prepared to stay on-site until the work is fully completed.&nbsp;</p><p>- Carefully review the scope of work in advance to ensure you have enough time to finish the task.&nbsp;</p><p>- Once the job is completed, a budget increase will be applied accordingly.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><em><u>***Do not begin the job unless you are actively connected to the Remote Support. Call Dispatch again for assistance. Work completed without their assistance will not be compensated.***</u></em></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>STATEMENT OF WORK:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>A technician is needed to assist in ISP cutover.</p><p>The tech will connect their laptop directly to the new ISP feed before beginning any cutover work to run a speed test to verify the 500 Mbps Symmetrical profile. </p><p>Present the live results to the hotel property officials on-site, and take a screenshot/photo to send back to the SNA team.</p><p>Once the link speed is approved, tech will patch the new ISP link directly into the WatchGuard firewall. The remote tech will be online to configure this interface to house the new connection.</p><p>Tech is to stand by while the remote tech handles migrating the remaining public IP blocks across the on-site network devices. </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Below are the new ISP details:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>New ISP Name: Brightspeed</p><p>ISP Circuit type: Fiber DIA (Dedicated Internet Access), static routing. Handoff is electrical RJ45 (tagged) from a RAD 203AX.</p><p>ISP Account#: Not recorded. The order form shows the customer account (BAN) as \"NEW\" and no number has been added.</p><p>ISP Circuit ID#: BSPD/449960383 (LEC Circuit ID: 58.KXGS.939064..CRLN)</p><p>ISP Circuit size: 500Mb (GigE port, 500M sub-bandwidth)</p><p>ISP Phone#: DIA support 833-363-2907, Option 1. CPE/router support 833-372-2555.</p><p>Usable IPs: 4.19.238.98 – 4.19.238.110 (LAN block 4.19.238.96/28)</p><p>Default Gateway: Not recorded. Likely 4.19.238.97, because the usable range starts at .98. Confirm with Brightspeed.</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.240 (from the /28 LAN block)</p><p>DNS Address: 205.171.3.26</p><p>Secondary DNS: 205.171.2.26</p><p><br></p><p>Will the new ISP provide a Layer 3 router? Yes. Brightspeed provides a managed router, an ADTRAN NetVanta 3148P, with the /28 static LAN block routed behind it.</p><p><br></p><p>If the new ISP already installed a new router:</p><p>New ISP Device Make: ADTRAN (per the order form; confirm on site)</p><p>New ISP Device Model: NetVanta 3148P (per the order form; confirm on site)</p><p>MAC Address: TBD</p><p>Serial #: TBD</p><p>Location: 1st floor server closet, rack-mounted position 40 (carrier handoff on RAD 203AX, port 3)</p><p>Port from their router/modem where the new network block is configured: Not recorded</p><p><br></p><p>ISP router details</p><p>TBD.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>INSTRUCTIONS:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>1. The technician will connect the laptop directly to the ISP device / link</p><p>2. The technician will statically configure the static IP address</p><p>3. The technician will then test the speed of the link from the laptop and take screenshots of the same</p><p>4. The technician will connect the ISP WAN cable to port 4 of the HLT-RZZCC-105-MDF-MX01 and confirm service are available via the new ISP link.</p><p>5. The technician will the disconnect the existing ISP and proceed to test with the site on network availability</p><p><br></p><p><strong>For CABLE RUN TROUBLESHOOTING:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Test all existing wiring with MicroScanner or equivalent.</p><p>Identify and fix faulty pairs.</p><p>Determine possible solutions, re-punch, re-terminate, and/or replace a patch cable and cable run if necessary.</p><p> </p><p>In order to maintain accurate documentation, the tech should be taking pictures of the closet being worked in (before and after moving cables or troubleshooting). </p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><strong>TECH SHOULD BRING THE FOLLOWING:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>- Admin Rights Laptop (Windows latest OS) with at least Integrated 1 GIG NIC Card, dual band wireless, USB port, Putty(Installed)</p><p>- Cell Phone with mobile data connection that will be used as hotspot</p><p>- Cisco console cable, patch cables, serial to USB adapter</p><p>- Diagnostic Tools: Cable Tester/Certifier(Fluke, Lantek, Klein tools), Toner-Probe Kit, and Digital multimeter</p><p>- Hand Tools: Torx screw driver &amp; screw driver (flat head and Phillips of various sizes), including crimper and punch-down tool</p><p>- Extra RJ45s and ethernet patch cables</p><p>has context menu</p><p><br></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00","end":"2026-10-26T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":69.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{