{"job":{"id":20228680,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> Raleigh, 27612</p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p><p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p>Scope of Work – AP Relocation &amp; Wi-Fi Testing<p><br></p><p>The resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.</p><p><strong>1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.</li><li>Identify any potential coverage issues.</li></ul><p><strong>2. AP Relocation</strong></p><ul><li>Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.</li><li>Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.</li><li>Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.</li><li>Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.</li><li>Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Drywall Repair &amp; Painting</strong></p><ul><li>Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.</li><li>Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.</li><li>Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.</li><li>Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.</li><li>Clean the work area and remove all debris.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Final Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.</li><li>Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.</li><li>Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.</li><li>Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.</li><li>Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.</li></ul>Required Tools &amp; Materials<ul><li>Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed</li><li>Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools</li><li>Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools</li><li>Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods</li><li>Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies</li><li>Matching wall texture, primer, and paint</li><li>Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies</li><li>Ladder and standard installation tools</li></ul>Completion Requirements<ul><li>AP relocated according to the provided design.</li><li>All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.</li><li>Drywall patched, textured, and painted.</li><li>Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.</li><li>Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.</li></ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** Raleigh, 27612\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\nScope of Work – AP Relocation & Wi-Fi TestingThe resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.\n\n**1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.\n- Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.\n- Identify any potential coverage issues.\n\n**2. AP Relocation**\n\n- Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.\n- Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.\n- Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.\n- Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.\n- Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.\n\n**3. Drywall Repair & Painting**\n\n- Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.\n- Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.\n- Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.\n- Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.\n- Clean the work area and remove all debris.\n\n**4. Final Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.\n- Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.\n- Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.\n- Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.\n- Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.\n\nRequired Tools & Materials- Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed\n- Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools\n- Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools\n- Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods\n- Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies\n- Matching wall texture, primer, and paint\n- Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies\n- Ladder and standard installation tools\n\nCompletion Requirements- AP relocated according to the provided design.\n- All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.\n- Drywall patched, textured, and painted.\n- Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.\n- Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.\n- Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.\n- **Note:** Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3.6136968948458},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 (countered: $200) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792702105762}
{"job":{"id":20228628,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | JPMC MaCD | See Scope In Service Description","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.</strong></li><li><strong>By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page: </strong><u>https://fieldnation.com/work/insight</u></li><li><strong>Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details are available through the recruitment link.</strong></li></ul><p>Insight has been engaged by <del>**** </del>to assist with their Ad Hoc needs. Please make sure to read all standard instructions before accepting OR requesting this workorder.</p><p>Please see tracking before going to site or call <del>******* *************</del> Tracking is added to the ticket the morning of the job if applicable. Look in the shipments section.</p><p>**<strong>CHECK YOUR EMAIL THE MORNING OF REGARDING YOUR ASSIGNED WO **</strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p>!!! BEFORE you mark yourself ONSITE It is essential that you \t<br/>call the Insight team - 1-800-215-8968 \t<br/>Do not leave the site UNTIL you call the Insight team. \t<br/>\t<br/>Chase reference ticket:\t256925985<br/>Chase Contact#: 877-309-8068 Opt 1\t<br/>\t<br/>Unit:\t<br/>SCOPE:\t<br/>Install replacement teller pc\t<br/>\t<br/>\t<br/>Branch contact:\tPaul Roache W623833<br/>Date requested:\t10/23/2026<br/></p><p><strong><em><u>Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.</u></em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>UNLESS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.</li><li>&nbsp;Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.</li><li>&nbsp;If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.</li><li>&nbsp;Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.</li><li>Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE: Even if tracking shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><del>*</del><strong><u><del>*** ****</del> Work Order &amp; Support Procedures</u></strong></p><p>A Smartphone is required for all technicians. Unless directed by the <del>***** </del>help-desk at no time should a technician be taking pictures, video, or any recording while inside a <del>***** </del>branch. No laptops or tablets should ever be brought into a banking location. Nothing about the work performed, activities inside the branch, or reference to <del>***** </del>should ever be posted on any social media site.Business casual dress required, no tennis shoes or jeans. You will be turned away if you show up with unprofessional attire.</p><p>No smoking on location.</p><p>Please follow the below procedures, includes information on who to call to initiate support and what information must be documented in the ticket. All required information must be documented for a completed ticket.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>For escalation.</strong></p><p><strong><del>********** **** **** ****** ******* ******* **** ** ******** ** ******* **************</del></strong></p><p><del>* **** *** ******* *******