{"job":{"id":20223965,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Go Back to install T-Mobile cellular internet at GT Cylinder Exchange & Truck Repair - Goldsboro","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.</p>\n<p><strong>Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>SEND TECH TO INSTALL T-MOBILE INTERNET.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Punctuality &amp; Assignment Rules</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.</li>\n<li>Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.</li>\n<li>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill, level, and stud finder</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>6-pin RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.\n\n**Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs**\n\n***SEND TECH TO INSTALL T-MOBILE INTERNET.***\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).\n\nPunctuality & Assignment Rules\n\n- Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.\n- Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.\n- If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill, level, and stud finder\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- 6-pin RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T11:00","end":"2026-10-26T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":54.48289285835693},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792703953697}
{"job":{"id":20226468,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 115","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13150551</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK & TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13150551\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-23T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":55.167019813159165},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792704226176}
{"job":{"id":"6418086474","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"H and M: Circuit Turn Up + edgeboot + Switch Install_US0206","description":"<p>**REQUIRED TOOLS**</p><p>Laptop (10/100 network card or better) with Ethernet port (or adapter)</p><p>Console Cable</p><p>Velcro Straps</p><p>Phillips, Slotted and Torx bits</p><p>Label maker</p><p>Charger</p><p>Assorted patch cables</p><p>Printed files on Workmarket Ticket</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 1: Arrival &amp; Site Verification</p><p>-Introduce yourself to the local contact at H&amp;M prior to beginning work. </p><p>-Locate edgeboot and switch equipment shipped to site. It should be labeled with “Hold For Granite Telecom Technician” tape.</p><p>-Locate circuit. Ensure circuit is near customer's network equipment.</p><p>-Document the current condition of the network equipment rack or equipment backboard by taking pictures before beginning any work on the site.</p><p><br></p><p>Edgeboot SN: 2020261984</p><p>Edgeboot Tracking: 1Z7X569X0113456044 - Delivered 7/20 (Left at the Dock - Received By: JASON)</p><p>Switch Tracking: 1Z7X569X0105208998 - Delivered 7/23 (Left at the Dock - Received By: ROSS)</p><p><br></p><p>***CIRCUIT INFO***</p><p>Carrier/Bandwidth: Granite 30MBPS/30MBPS</p><p>Circuit MAC/NSO ID: 288019</p><p>Circuit Demarc/IDF: MDF</p><p>GRID Switch: NSONSID0000000094</p><p>GRID Port: 7</p><p>DHCP: 143.170.24.2-6</p><p>Gateway: 143.170.24.1</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 2: Confirm Circuit Connectivity and Speeds</p><p>-Work with Granite Activations to confirm connectivity and speeds - 877-855-1146 | OPT 1: Cable/DSL, OPT 2: DIA, OPT 3: GRID.</p><p><br></p><p>STEP 3: Install Edgeboot and Pre-Stage Switch</p><p>-Refer to Diagram attached to ticket.</p><p>-Verify that the power strip supplying all equipment, including the Edgeboot device, is NOT plugged into the UPS and is instead plugged into the PDU. PDU should be plugged into the wall, NOT UPS. Take pictures.</p><p>-If PDU is not available, plug device directly into the wall outlet or to a power strip.</p><p>-Install edgebootPro with BB power going into AC port 1 and ethernet into an open port on the BB modem if installed with multi-port modem as requested. Will connect into the customer switch if there is not an open port on modem.</p><p>-Pre-stage Switch. Make sure this device is plugged in and turns on and is not defective. Take pictures.</p><p><br></p><p>Required Deliverables:</p><p>-Picture of cabinet/backboard (close up and wide)</p><p>-Pictures of speed tests (directly from Broadband circuit) </p><p>-Pictures of installed edgeboot and showing where it’s plugged in.</p><p>-Pictures of pre-staged switch.</p><p>-MUST get a signature prior to leaving the site.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T10:00","end":"2026-10-28T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":50},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":1.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $50 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM