{"job":{"id":20230804,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Guest-Tek","title":" Tech required to go on site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE","description":{"html":"<p>############################################</p><p>&nbsp;### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###</p><p>&nbsp;############################################</p><p>====IMPORTANT PLEASE READ CAREFULLY=====</p><p>Technicians/TPC are required to review the Vendor Etiquette guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.</p><p>By proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.</p><p>Any non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.</p><p>Once on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)</p><p>It is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Follow these steps when onsite:</p><p>STEP#1 Contact PM Martin Salazar Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com&gt; mobile: +1 951.703.8585 TDE:Angel Camey Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com</p><p>STEP#2 if delayed after 15 min please send to Email Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com,Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com and techdispatch@guest-tek.com to CHECK IN and request a call back Refer to :</p><p>USJ# USJ010253 – Courtyard Chapel Hill (RDUCH)</p><p>STEP#3 If still no answer or delay with the 15mn please call back 1-866-509-1010 EXT 8600</p><p>Please have the work order signature sheet with the paper signature by property before departure.</p><p>**NO DIGITAL SIGNATURE ALLOWED -ONLY PAPER SIGNATURE IS ACCEPTED**</p><p>All issues must be resolved before leaving site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>POINT OF CONTACT</p><p>===========================</p><p>&nbsp;GM Derick Waddell</p><p>TYPE OF TECHNICIAN : <strong>HSIA/Networking tech,</strong></p><p>&nbsp;PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT:</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Courtyard Chapel Hill RDUCH: We need tech to get to site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE</strong></p><p>SOW :Steps required to be completed by tech</p><p><strong>Courtyard Chapel Hill RDUCH</strong>:</p><p>Physically reset PMS Master controller onsite</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>TECHNICIAN SKILL SET</p><p>======================&nbsp;</p><p>Working with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.</p><p>- Re-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary</p><p>- Working with network equipment</p><p>- Basic knowledge of switch commands and switching</p><p>- Experience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation</p><p><br></p><p>TECHNICIAN TOOL SET</p><p>========================</p><p>Smartphones with fully charged battery with Teams on it</p><p>Laptop with fully charged battery for testing</p><p>Spare Straight-through Cat5 patch cable for testing purposes</p><p>Cat 5 line Tester</p><p>&nbsp;Console cable</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"\\############################################\n\n ### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###\n\n ############################################\n\n====IMPORTANT PLEASE READ CAREFULLY=====\n\nTechnicians/TPC are required to review the Vendor Etiquette guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.\n\nBy proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.\n\nAny non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.\n\nOnce on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)\n\nIt is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.\n\nFollow these steps when onsite:\n\nSTEP#1 Contact PM Martin Salazar Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com> mobile: +1 951.703.8585 TDE:Angel Camey Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com\n\nSTEP#2 if delayed after 15 min please send to Email Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com,Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com and techdispatch@guest-tek.com to CHECK IN and request a call back Refer to :\n\nUSJ# USJ010253 – Courtyard Chapel Hill (RDUCH)\n\nSTEP#3 If still no answer or delay with the 15mn please call back 1-866-509-1010 EXT 8600\n\nPlease have the work order signature sheet with the paper signature by property before departure.\n\n\\*\\*NO DIGITAL SIGNATURE ALLOWED -ONLY PAPER SIGNATURE IS ACCEPTED\\*\\*\n\nAll issues must be resolved before leaving site.\n\nPOINT OF CONTACT\n\n===========================\n\n GM Derick Waddell\n\nTYPE OF TECHNICIAN : **HSIA/Networking tech,**\n\n PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT:\n\n**Courtyard Chapel Hill RDUCH: We need tech to get to site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE**\n\nSOW :Steps required to be completed by tech\n\n**Courtyard Chapel Hill RDUCH**:\n\nPhysically reset PMS Master controller onsite\n\nTECHNICIAN SKILL SET\n\n======================\n\nWorking with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.\n\n\\- Re-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary\n\n\\- Working with network equipment\n\n\\- Basic knowledge of switch commands and switching\n\n\\- Experience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation\n\nTECHNICIAN TOOL SET\n\n========================\n\nSmartphones with fully charged battery with Teams on it\n\nLaptop with fully charged battery for testing\n\nSpare Straight-through Cat5 patch cable for testing purposes\n\nCat 5 line Tester\n\n Console cable","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T11:00","end":"2026-10-23T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":15.04533763879489},"result":{"eli