{"job":{"id":"4617405328","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05992889-RALEIGH - 1353754 - EPIK-EPIK Survey","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"**If you get denied access, please have your dispatch team (833-479-4768) call the USPS Hot Line Group to assist with access - dispatch team will let them know you are working a project for Granite to survey/install the phone line(s) - give them the address and your name/contact info and they will help you with the Post Master to gain access**<br><br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1.TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2.Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3.Please utilize the attached authorization letter for access or any questions that the postmaster might have.<br>**If you get denied access, please have your dispatch team (833-479-4768) call the USPS Hot Line Group to assist with access - dispatch team will let them know you are working a project for Granite to survey/install the phone line(s) - give them the address and your name/contact info and they will help you with the Post Master to gain access**<br>4.Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>5.Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>6.Note what is the best carrier between AT&amp;T, VZ and T-Mobile when you fill out the wizard – add any extra note you have as we will be selecting two different carriers for each Epik device. If Antenna is needed, make sure you clearly indicate that.<br>7.Some locations will have a Granite managed network service in different flavors, please make sure to note one of the selections below<br>a.Managed Broadband<br>b.Unmanaged Broadband<br>c.Managed Cellular<br>d.Managed Starlink<br>e.Dedicated Internet (Unmanaged)<br>f.      No Granite internet of any kind<br>8.Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>9.Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br><br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-31T10:00","end":"2026