{"job":{"id":"5191752121","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05992941-FAYETTEVILLE - 1369663 - EPIK-EPIK Survey","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"**If you get denied access, please have your dispatch team (833-479-4768) call the USPS Hot Line Group to assist with access - dispatch team will let them know you are working a project for Granite to survey/install the phone line(s) - give them the address and your name/contact info and they will help you with the Post Master to gain access**<br><br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1.TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2.Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3.Please utilize the attached authorization letter for access or any questions that the postmaster might have.<br>**If you get denied access, please have your dispatch team (833-479-4768) call the USPS Hot Line Group to assist with access - dispatch team will let them know you are working a project for Granite to survey/install the phone line(s) - give them the address and your name/contact info and they will help you with the Post Master to gain access**<br>4.Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>5.Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>6.Note what is the best carrier between AT&amp;T, VZ and T-Mobile when you fill out the wizard – add any extra note you have as we will be selecting two different carriers for each Epik device. If Antenna is needed, make sure you clearly indicate that.<br>7.Some locations will have a Granite managed network service in different flavors, please make sure to note one of the selections below<br>a.Managed Broadband<br>b.Unmanaged Broadband<br>c.Managed Cellular<br>d.Managed Starlink<br>e.Dedicated Internet (Unmanaged)<br>f.      No Granite internet of any kind<br>8.Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>9.Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br><br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-31T10:00","end":"2026-12-31T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":58.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2027-01-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2027-01-05T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-31T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2027-01-01T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"New Year's Eve"},{"start":"2027-01-01T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2027-01-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"New Year's Day"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792724168289}
{"job":{"id":20230610,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"Dermatology Office - Site Survey (cabling and display installs)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technician Initial Requirements</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Must review full scope below and survey form prior to arrival&nbsp;</li><li>Survey tools: 8 Ft. Ladder, Laptop/Tablet, Phone, &amp; Tape Measure&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>PROJECT OVERVIEW</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>A Technician is needed to perform <strong>onsite survey</strong> at a Dermatology office <strong>in</strong> <strong>preparation for a future display and structured cabling installation.</strong> The future installation will include new Cat6 cable runs to <em>ALL exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms</em>, along with installation of displays and supporting network equipment as required.&nbsp;</p><p><em>*Existing displays (if any) will be removed prior to installation. EVERY exam room, treatment room, lobby, and breakroom will be getting a display, regardless of existing display in place and/or onsite staff requests. </em>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em><u>Project Specific Considerations</u></em></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p><ul><li><strong>Any adjustments to the scope, will be determined by Client Project team, NOT onsite staff. </strong>Questions/Concerns made by staff should be noted on survey form. <em>Regardless of staff comments, look at every room to verify future display locations. Do not make commitments or changes to the scope.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;</li><li>Survey<strong> exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms</strong>, regardless of whether displays currently exist.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>New Cat6 cabling is planned for EVERY room/area listed above</strong>, regardless of existing displays.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>BRING A LADDER.</strong> Technician MUST inspect above accessible ceilings to verify cable routing feasibility.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Display power will be provided through Cat6 cabling (PoE).</strong> Electrical outlets are NOT required at display locations.&nbsp;</li><li>We will provide and uplink <strong>our new switch</strong> to the site's current switch. <strong>Technicians must provide ALL available specific ethernet switch port #s</strong>. Client IT will configure port prior to installation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>SURVEY SCOPE</strong></p><p><em>*Do not ask onsite staff to select or approve display locations</em>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>1. Lobby / Waiting Area(s)&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Inspect and document EVERY Lobby &amp; separate waiting areas (if applicable)&nbsp;</li><li>Per <em>Survey</em> <em>Form</em>, document:&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>existing display size &amp; model&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>If display is newer/larger than what we will provide, site may keep&nbsp;</li><li>best future display size based on room/wall size&nbsp;</li><li>43inch vs. 55inch&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>mount requirements&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Rotating &amp; fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).&nbsp;</li><li>cat6 cable routing feasibility&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Take clear photos of the room and potential display location&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>2.&nbsp;Breakroom, Exam Rooms &amp; Treatment Rooms&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Inspect and document EVERY exam room and treatment room, including rooms with AND without current displays.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Per <em>Survey</em> <em>Form</em>, document:&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Room identification, existing displays, and potential wall-mounting locations for future 32-inch displays&nbsp;</li><li>Cat6 cable routing feasibility&nbsp;</li><li>Mounting conditions, wall type, accessibility, and any special installation requirements&nbsp;</li><li>Rotating &amp; fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).&nbsp;</li><li>Take clear photos of each room and potential display location&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>3.&nbsp;Network Room</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Document the following:&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Available wall space measurements for vertically wall mounted backboard and switch, next to current network equipment&nbsp;</li><li>If no wall space, notate additional options&nbsp;</li><li>Current network switch - make/model&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Current network switch - provide ALL </span><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">available ETHERNET port #s </em><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(</span><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">not SFP ports)</em><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Client will configure one of the available ports prior to install&nbsp;</span></li><li>Power outlet availability for our switch&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>*Mobile Kiosk Considerations*</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>If wall mounting appears impractical, document available floor space and potential suitability for a 32-inch mobile display kiosk. Note Wi-Fi availability. <strong>Do not offer or approve a mobile kiosk as an alternative.</strong> Client Project Team will make that determination.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Required Deliverables</u></em></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>Documentation: </em><strong><em>Survey Form</em></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Room-by-room findings&nbsp;</li><li>Cat6 cable distances and any routing obstacles&nbsp;</li><li>Any conditions that may affect installation&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>Photos:&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Rooms, existing displays, and potential mounting locations.&nbsp;</li><li>Network rack, existing switch, available wall space, and electrical outlets&nbsp;</li><li>Above-ceiling cable pathway inspections&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**Technician Initial Requirements**\n\n- Must review full scope below and survey form prior to arrival\n- Survey tools: 8 Ft. Ladder, Laptop/Tablet, Phone, & Tape Measure\n\n**PROJECT OVERVIEW**\n\nA Technician is needed to perform **onsite survey** at a Dermatology office **in** **preparation for a future display and structured cabling installation.** The future installation will include new Cat6 cable runs to *ALL exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms*, along with installation of displays and supporting network equipment as required.\n\n*\\*Existing displays (if any) will be removed prior to installation. EVERY exam room, treatment room, lobby, and breakroom will be getting a display, regardless of existing display in place and/or onsite staff requests.*\n\n***Project Specific Considerations***\n\n- **Any adjustments to the scope, will be determined by Client Project team, NOT onsite staff.** Questions/Concerns made by staff should be noted on survey form. *Regardless of staff comments, look at every room to verify future display locations. Do not make commitments or changes to the scope.*\n- Survey **exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms**, regardless of whether displays currently exist.\n- **New Cat6 cabling is planned for EVERY room/area listed above**, regardless of existing displays.\n- **BRING A LADDER.** Technician MUST inspect above accessible ceilings to verify cable routing feasibility.\n- **Display power will be provided through Cat6 cabling (PoE).** Electrical outlets are NOT required at display locations.\n- We will provide and uplink **our new switch** to the site's current switch. **Technicians must provide ALL available specific ethernet switch port #s**. Client IT will configure port prior to installation.\n\n**SURVEY SCOPE**\n\n*\\*Do not ask onsite staff to select or approve display locations*\n\n**1. Lobby / Waiting Area(s)**\n\n- Inspect and document EVERY Lobby & separate waiting areas (if applicable)\n- Per *Survey* *Form*, document:\n- existing display size & model\n- If display is newer/larger than what we will provide, site may keep\n- best future display size based on room/wall size\n- 43inch vs. 55inch\n- mount requirements\n- Rotating & fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).\n- cat6 cable routing feasibility\n- Take clear photos of the room and potential display location\n\n**2. Breakroom, Exam Rooms & Treatment Rooms**\n\n- Inspect and document EVERY exam room and treatment room, including rooms with AND without current displays.\n- Per *Survey* *Form*, document:\n- Room identification, existing displays, and potential wall-mounting locations for future 32-inch displays\n- Cat6 cable routing feasibility\n- Mounting conditions, wall type, accessibility, and any special installation requirements\n- Rotating & fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).\n- Take clear photos of each room and potential display location\n\n**3. Network Room**\n\n- Document the following:\n- Available wall space measurements for vertically wall mounted backboard and switch, next to current network equipment\n- If no wall space, notate additional options\n- Current network switch - make/model\n- Current network switch - provide ALL *available ETHERNET port #s* (*not SFP ports)*\n- Client will configure one of the available ports prior to install\n- Power outlet availability for our switch\n\n**\\*Mobile Kiosk Considerations\\***\n\n- If wall mounting appears impractical, document available floor space and potential suitability for a 32-inch mobile display kiosk. Note Wi-Fi availability. **Do not offer or approve a mobile kiosk as an alternative.** Client Project Team will make that determination.\n\n***Required Deliverables***\n\n*Documentation:* ***Survey Form***\n\n- Room-by-room findings\n- Cat6 cable distances and any routing obstacles\n- Any conditions that may affect installation\n\n*Photos:*\n\n- Rooms, existing displays, and potential mounting locations.\n- Network rack, existing switch, available wall space, and electrical outlets\n- Above-ceiling cable pathway inspections","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-12-09T09:00","end":"2026-12-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-12-09T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":135,"max":135},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.592587993550309},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792726719762}
