/p><ul><li>Document the following:&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Available wall space measurements for vertically wall mounted backboard and switch, next to current network equipment&nbsp;</li><li>If no wall space, notate additional options&nbsp;</li><li>Current network switch - make/model&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Current network switch - provide ALL </span><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">available ETHERNET port #s </em><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(</span><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">not SFP ports)</em><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Client will configure one of the available ports prior to install&nbsp;</span></li><li>Power outlet availability for our switch&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>*Mobile Kiosk Considerations*</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>If wall mounting appears impractical, document available floor space and potential suitability for a 32-inch mobile display kiosk. Note Wi-Fi availability. <strong>Do not offer or approve a mobile kiosk as an alternative.</strong> Client Project Team will make that determination.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Required Deliverables</u></em></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>Documentation: </em><strong><em>Survey Form</em></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Room-by-room findings&nbsp;</li><li>Cat6 cable distances and any routing obstacles&nbsp;</li><li>Any conditions that may affect installation&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>Photos:&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Rooms, existing displays, and potential mounting locations.&nbsp;</li><li>Network rack, existing switch, available wall space, and electrical outlets&nbsp;</li><li>Above-ceiling cable pathway inspections&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**Technician Initial Requirements**\n\n- Must review full scope below and survey form prior to arrival\n- Survey tools: 8 Ft. Ladder, Laptop/Tablet, Phone, & Tape Measure\n\n**PROJECT OVERVIEW**\n\nA Technician is needed to perform **onsite survey** at a Dermatology office **in** **preparation for a future display and structured cabling installation.** The future installation will include new Cat6 cable runs to *ALL exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms*, along with installation of displays and supporting network equipment as required.\n\n*\\*Existing displays (if any) will be removed prior to installation. EVERY exam room, treatment room, lobby, and breakroom will be getting a display, regardless of existing display in place and/or onsite staff requests.*\n\n***Project Specific Considerations***\n\n- **Any adjustments to the scope, will be determined by Client Project team, NOT onsite staff.** Questions/Concerns made by staff should be noted on survey form. *Regardless of staff comments, look at every room to verify future display locations. Do not make commitments or changes to the scope.*\n- Survey **exam rooms, treatment rooms, lobby/waiting areas, and break rooms**, regardless of whether displays currently exist.\n- **New Cat6 cabling is planned for EVERY room/area listed above**, regardless of existing displays.\n- **BRING A LADDER.** Technician MUST inspect above accessible ceilings to verify cable routing feasibility.\n- **Display power will be provided through Cat6 cabling (PoE).** Electrical outlets are NOT required at display locations.\n- We will provide and uplink **our new switch** to the site's current switch. **Technicians must provide ALL available specific ethernet switch port #s**. Client IT will configure port prior to installation.\n\n**SURVEY SCOPE**\n\n*\\*Do not ask onsite staff to select or approve display locations*\n\n**1. Lobby / Waiting Area(s)**\n\n- Inspect and document EVERY Lobby & separate waiting areas (if applicable)\n- Per *Survey* *Form*, document:\n- existing display size & model\n- If display is newer/larger than what we will provide, site may keep\n- best future display size based on room/wall size\n- 43inch vs. 55inch\n- mount requirements\n- Rotating & fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).\n- cat6 cable routing feasibility\n- Take clear photos of the room and potential display location\n\n**2. Breakroom, Exam Rooms & Treatment Rooms**\n\n- Inspect and document EVERY exam room and treatment room, including rooms with AND without current displays.\n- Per *Survey* *Form*, document:\n- Room identification, existing displays, and potential wall-mounting locations for future 32-inch displays\n- Cat6 cable routing feasibility\n- Mounting conditions, wall type, accessibility, and any special installation requirements\n- Rotating & fixed included. Rotating preferred. Flag special mounts (e.g., corner).\n- Take clear photos of each room and potential display location\n\n**3. Network Room**\n\n- Document the following:\n- Available wall space measurements for vertically wall mounted backboard and switch, next to current network equipment\n- If no wall space, notate additional options\n- Current network switch - make/model\n- Current network switch - provide ALL *available ETHERNET port #s* (*not SFP ports)*\n- Client will configure one of the available ports prior to install\n- Power outlet availability for our switch\n\n**\\*Mobile Kiosk Considerations\\***\n\n- If wall mounting appears impractical, document available floor space and potential suitability for a 32-inch mobile display kiosk. Note Wi-Fi availability. **Do not offer or approve a mobile kiosk as an alternative.** Client Project Team will make that determination.\n\n***Required Deliverables***\n\n*Documentation:* ***Survey Form***\n\n- Room-by-room findings\n- Cat6 cable distances and any routing obstacles\n- Any conditions that may affect installation\n\n*Photos:*\n\n- Rooms, existing displays, and potential mounting locations.\n- Network rack, existing switch, available wall space, and electrical outlets\n- Above-ceiling cable pathway inspections","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-12-09T09:00","end":"2026-12-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-12-09T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":135,"max":135},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.836579704289065},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-10-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"On-site Technician Required - Barrier Gate Part Replacement"},{"start":"2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00736667 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792726726407}
