{"job":{"id":20231264,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ GO LIVE / MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS154237","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 2123595319 Ticket 11513331<br/><br/>***MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/>R&S + Go Live<br/><br/>TN LIST<br/>9197751731<br/>9197750422<br/>9197768131<br/>9197754598<br/>9197750422<br/>9197746797<br/>Additional Lines<br/>9197180097 (added via ticket 12039040)<br/>9197741952 (added via ticket 12039046)<br/><br/> LCON Jimmy 9193535436<br/><br/>Call Logan Ryan at 2123595319  when on site.<br/>Data Remote CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit<br/>-Tech to locate equipment.<br/>-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.<br/>-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.<br/>-Attach antennas and power on.<br/>-MetTel will validate configurations.<br/>-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net<br/>-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.<br/>-Validate e911 address on one each line.<br/>-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.<br/>If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.<br/>-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.<br/>-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.<br/>-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.<br/>-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.<br/>-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 2123595319 Ticket 11513331  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \nR&S + Go Live  \n  \nTN LIST  \n9197751731  \n9197750422  \n9197768131  \n9197754598  \n9197750422  \n9197746797  \nAdditional Lines  \n9197180097 (added via ticket 12039040)  \n9197741952 (added via ticket 12039046)  \n  \n LCON Jimmy 9193535436  \n  \nCall Logan Ryan at 2123595319 when on site.  \nData Remote CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit  \n-Tech to locate equipment.  \n-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.  \n-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.  \n-Attach antennas and power on.  \n-MetTel will validate configurations.  \n-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net  \n-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.  \n-Validate e911 address on one each line.  \n-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.  \nIf voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.  \n-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.  \n-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.  \n-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.  \n-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.  \n-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through t