68 2055\n\n7981 9685 8884\n\n3842 1172 8830\n\n7981 9685 9733\n\n3842 1161 5654\n\n7981 9691 3002\n\n3842 1178 1831\n\n7981 9691 0231\n\n\\*\\*\\*Scope of Work Instructions\\*\\*\\*\n\nGeneral Scope of Work: Technician to go and pick up equipment up at local fedex hold, drive to customers site location, work with the HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point via onsite \"Talkative Video Calling System\" to drop equipment off in customers onsite VITP storage lockers, and if applicable take defective equipment out of lockers and drop off a local FedEx Hold for return to customer.\n\nScope of Work Step by Step Instructions:\n\n- Pick up the laptops from FedEx.\n- Arrive at the BASF office and use the Talkative machine by selecting “Click to Support.”\n- One of our agents \\[ HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents \\] will answer the call and guide the technician step‑by‑step.\n- \"Talkative Video Calling System\" Process - Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n- Open the package:\n- Every package contains a return label — keep this aside for return shipping.\n- There will be an inner box containing the new laptop.\n- Our agent \\[ HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents \\] will provide the admin PIN and guide the technician to open the locker.\n- Remove the defective laptop from the locker.\n- Place the new laptop inside the locker, share the serial number, and close the locker.\n- Ship the defective laptop back to FedEx:\n- Pack the old laptop back into the box.\n- Stick the return label onto the box.\n- Return it at the FedEx location.\n\nOnsite Virtual IT Point via Onsite \"Talkative Video Calling System\" Process\n\n- Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n\nImportant Tech Information & Requirements\n\n- Technicians ARE NOT to go to site unless equipment is ready for pickup at local FedEx\n- Technicians MUST Represent themselves as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF\n- Technicians MUST carry/present BASF Badge while onsite\n\nImportant Information on Site:\n\n- You must represent themselves as an Essintial technician on behalf of HCL/BASF while on site.\n- Technicians MUST carry/present BASF Badge while onsite\n- Onsite - DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.\n\nImportant Scope/Customer Information:\n\n- Any changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone.\n- If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.\n- If additional parts are needed there will be another trip REQUIRED. You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.\n- All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability\n- Standard hand tools\n\nUpon Arrival at FedEx:\n\n- CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER – if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n\nUpon Arrival at the Site:\n\n- Enter the site with Badge and Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF\n- Go to Virtual ID Area - DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.\n- Ref to the\n- \"Scope of Work Step by Step Instructions\" - posted above in your Work Order\n- Once at the VITP Point, there is a device that the techs will use to call the VITP Team - Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n- Work with the HCL VITP Team\n- HCL VITP Agent will Advise what locker the devices will go into and advise which lock to pull the defective from.\n- The team will guide and open lockers for tech and provide support, techs will provide new and old device serials to the team.\n- HCL VITP Agent will provide admin PIN\n- VITP Agent will release the tech, once call has ended tech will leave and exit\n- Technician to take any defective equipment with them and drop off at FedEx Immediately after leaving the site\n- Techs DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.\n\n Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements\n\n- Get Released from the site by the VITP Agent - obtain agents Name\n- Take Defective Equipment and drop off at local FedEx\n- Call the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n\nImportant Note about Check-Out:\n\n- Technicians Labor End Time - is\n- If technicians HAS defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they drop equipment off at FedEx\n- Check-Out upon leaving FedEx\n- If Technicians DOES NOT have defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they are finished at site.\n- Check-Out upon leaving the site\n\nClosing / Completion Notes:\n\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues and delays\n- Name of the HCL VITP Agent who released you from the site?\n- Return Tracking Numbers (if applicable)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-23T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":30,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":6.991409914777129},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldC