{"job":{"id":20231998,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Intelligent Communication Solutions","title":"WAN-1-Offline (tech to locate and troubleshoot connection to network)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in Low Voltage Cabling/Troubleshooting.</li><li>Tech is required to have Networking/Cabling/POS/KDS/Printer Experience</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1-2 Hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code: </strong></p><ul><li>Pants</li><li>shirts</li><li>work shoes (non-slip preferred)</li><li>nothing offensive</li></ul><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong><em> </em></p><ul><li><em> </em>Screw divers</li><li>Crimpers</li><li>punch down</li><li>scissors</li><li>toners</li><li>cable certifier preferred</li><li>RJ 45 mod plugs</li><li>Cat5/Cat6 Data Jack</li><li>Surface Mount and or Single/Double Port Keystone Plates.</li><li>Cay5/6 Patch cords 3- 7 foot</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>WAN-1-Offline (tech to locate and troubleshoot connection to network) -MOD was unable to find the modem to do layer 1 troubleshooting. The port is receiving link, but the circuit is down. Please locate and reboot the modem, powering off for 15 minutes with power, coax, and ethernet disconnected, then reconnect coax first, power connect, lastly ethernet.  The modem is connected to Switch 1, port 44.</p><p>Remote tech will go over scope of work in depth. (Techs are prohibited from posting on social media about the sites they are working on for ICS, as this could inadvertently reveal sensitive information)</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks </em></strong></p><ol><li>Must call <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span> to check in onsite <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*************</del></span></li><li>Connect with remote tech when onsite walk though scope of work in depth&nbsp;</li><li>Work with remote tec