{"job":{"id":20232220,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vimenture","title":"Low-Voltage Cable Run | Looking for Cable Guy For OTIS ONE BOX","description":{"html":"<p><strong>READ THE OVERVIEW VERY CAREFULLY BEFORE REQUESTING THE WORK ORDER. THIS IS PART 1 OF A POSSIBLE 2 PART WORK ORDER. YOU MUST BE LOCAL TO THE AREA AND ABLE TO COMPLETE THE QUOTED WORK IF APPROVED BY OUR CLIENT. QUOTE APPROVAL COULD TAKE UP TO 30 DAYS FROM OUR CLIENT.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in low-voltage cabling &amp; networking. We need someone to perform a site survey to run a cable from the ATT modem to the Otis ONE box&nbsp;at the top of the shaft.</li>\n<li>You <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> identify if the ATT modem needs to be relocated by the carrier.</li>\n<li>You <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> bring a<strong><u>LAPTOP</u></strong> for the Site Survey</li>\n<li><strong><u>You MUST never disclose any amount to anyone.</u></strong></li>\n<li>You <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> come up with a <strong><u>FIX RATE</u></strong> quote for the project. Put a breakdown on the quote. Materials + Labor(hours). <strong>YOU MUST BE MINDFUL OF THE LABOR (HOURS) YOU ARE PROVIDING ON THE QUOTE AND MUST BE REASONABLE.</strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>YOU MUST UNDERSTAND ONCE THE QUOTE YOU PROVIDED IS APPROVED BY OUR CLIENT, WE WON'T BE ABLE TO MAKE ANY ADJUSTMENTS.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>YOU MUST INCLUDE ANY FIELD NATION FEES FOR OTHER EXPENSES, SUCH AS MATERIALS OR EQUIPMENT.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>ONCE APPROVED, THE PROJECT WILL BE DONE SOLELY THROUGH FIELDNATION ONLY. MUST BE THE SAME TECHNICIAN.</u></strong></li>\n<li>The <strong><u>Hourly Rate</u></strong> on the <strong><u>QUOTE MUST</u></strong> be the same rate you accepted for the site survey. <strong><u>(NO ADDITIONAL FEE LIKE TRIP FEE OR GAS)</u></strong></li>\n<li>The <strong><u>QUOTE MUST</u></strong> include a description of the work. <strong><u>DETAILS</u></strong> like the cable path, challenges, materials to be used, cable length, etc<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> be included in the<strong><u>DESCRIPTION</u></strong>.</li>\n<li>You <strong><u>MUST</u> immediately</strong> contact the Work Order manager if you can't get a hold of the<strong>IT</strong>assigned at any time.</li>\n<li><strong><u>ALL CABLE RUNS MUST BE QUALIFIED OR CERTIFIED. PHOTOS AS PROOF FOR EACH RUN IS REQUIRED.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>ALL CABLE RUNS MUST BE CAT6</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>WE WILL TAG THE WORK ORDER INCOMPLETE AND CONSIDER IT UNFINISHED WITHOUT THE PROPOSAL IN PDF UPLOADED.﻿</u></strong></li>\n<li>The job is estimated to take 1-2 hours.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> be the technician performing the work on-site.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.</li>\n<li>If any quotes are requested/required, these<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tools Required (<em>must haves)</em>:</strong>​</p>\n<ul>\n<li>​Any tools required for low-voltage cabling; toner, tester, laptop, include a couple of ethernet cables just in case, measuring tools, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong>​</p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Review and call the work order manager with any questions</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check-in to work order</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the onsite manager as being from<del>***************</del></li>\n<li>Contact the work order manager to check in and discuss the issue at <del>************</del></li>\n<li>Perform a site survey to run a cable from the ATT modem to<em>Otis ONE box&nbsp;at the top of the shaft.</em></li>\n<li>Take photos of the areas where each drop will be made.</li>\n<li>Take photos of the telecom room, cable path, etc.</li>\n<li>Take photos of the ATT modem, SN and the location where it is installed or needs to be installed.</li>\n<li>Put together a quote for the work needed. Follow the<strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong> on the overview.</li>\n<li>Confirm everything with the work order manager prior to checking out of the site.</li>\n<li>Collect signature from the onsite manager</li>\n<li>Clean installation area fully</li>\n</ol>\n<p>​<strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Please include notes and photos on the issue and repair.</li>\n<li>Come up with a quote for the cable run.<strong><u>MUST</u></strong> follow the requirements on the<strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong>.</li>\n<li>Check-out of the work order in the Field Nation app.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>​<strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p>Contact the work order manager if any of the following are true:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>​If clarification is needed on the work order or there are any questions, please call <del>****</del>at<del>************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.</u></strong> Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers.&nbsp;Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.</li>\n<li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling<del>************</del>If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**READ THE OVERVIEW VERY CAREFULLY BEFORE REQUESTING THE WORK ORDER. THIS IS PART 1 OF A POSSIBLE 2 PART WORK ORDER. YOU MUST BE LOCAL TO THE AREA AND ABLE TO COMPLETE THE QUOTED WORK IF APPROVED BY OUR CLIENT. QUOTE APPROVAL COULD TAKE UP TO 30 DAYS FROM OUR CLIENT.**\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in low-voltage cabling & networking. We need someone to perform a site survey to run a cable from the ATT modem to the Otis ONE box at the top of the shaft.\n- You **MUST** identify if the ATT modem needs to be relocated by the carrier.\n- You **MUST** bring a**LAPTOP** for the Site Survey\n- **You MUST never disclose any amount to anyone.**\n- You **MUST** come up with a **FIX RATE** quote for the project. Put a breakdown on the quote. Materials + Labor(hours). **YOU MUST BE MINDFUL OF THE LABOR (HOURS) YOU ARE PROVIDING ON THE QUOTE AND MUST BE REASONABLE.**\n- **YOU MUST UNDERSTAND ONCE THE QUOTE YOU PROVIDED IS APPROVED BY OUR CLIENT, WE WON'T BE ABLE TO MAKE ANY ADJUSTMENTS.**\n- **YOU MUST INCLUDE ANY FIELD NATION FEES FOR OTHER EXPENSES, SUCH AS MATERIALS OR EQUIPMENT.**\n- **ONCE APPROVED, THE PROJECT WILL BE DONE SOLELY THROUGH FIELDNATION ONLY. MUST BE THE SAME TECHNICIAN.**\n- The **Hourly Rate** on the **QUOTE MUST** be the same rate you accepted for the site survey. **(NO ADDITIONAL FEE LIKE TRIP FEE OR GAS)**\n- The **QUOTE MUST** include a description of the work. **DETAILS** like the cable path, challenges, materials to be used, cable length, etc**MUST** be included in the**DESCRIPTION**.\n- You **MUST immediately** contact the Work Order manager if you can't get a hold of the**IT**assigned at any time.\n- **ALL CABLE RUNS MUST BE QUALIFIED OR CERTIFIED. PHOTOS AS PROOF FOR EACH RUN IS REQUIRED.**\n- **ALL CABLE RUNS MUST BE CAT6**\n- **WE WILL TAG THE WORK ORDER INCOMPLETE AND CONSIDER IT UNFINISHED WITHOUT THE PROPOSAL IN PDF UPLOADED.﻿**\n- The job is estimated to take 1-2 hours.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** be the technician performing the work on-site.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.\n- If any quotes are requested/required, these**MUST** be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.\n\n**Tools Required (*must haves)*:**​\n\n- ​Any tools required for low-voltage cabling; toner, tester, laptop, include a couple of ethernet cables just in case, measuring tools, etc.\n\n**Scope of Work:**​\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Review and call the work order manager with any questions\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order\n2. Introduce yourself to the onsite manager as being from\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Contact the work order manager to check in and discuss the issue at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n4. Perform a site survey to run a cable from the ATT modem to*Otis ONE box at the top of the shaft.*\n5. Take photos of the areas where each drop will be made.\n6. Take photos of the telecom room, cable path, etc.\n7. Take photos of the ATT modem, SN and the location where it is installed or needs to be installed.\n8. Put together a quote for the work needed. Follow the**REQUIREMENTS** on the overview.\n9. Confirm everything with the work order manager prior to checking out of the site.\n10. Collect signature from the onsite manager\n11. Clean installation area fully\n\n​***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Please include notes and photos on the issue and repair.\n2. Come up with a quote for the cable run.**MUST** follow the requirements on the**OVERVIEW**.\n3. Check-out of the work order in the Field Nation app.\n\n​**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact the work order manager if any of the following are true:\n\n- ​If clarification is needed on the work order or there are any questions, please call \\*\\*\\*\\*at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- **Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.** Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T10:00","end":"2026-10-23T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":18.53294257186875},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/23/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Spot for Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 