{"job":{"id":20232414,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Verizon Terminal Upgrade","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>DETAILED SOW</u></strong></p><p><strong>Please review installation guide, download files, and watch Hardware Video before arriving at the site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>**IF YOU HAVE QUESTIONS ABOUT THE SOW, DONT NOT ASK THE VERIZON POC, CALL THE WORK ORDER MANAGER**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Techncian will complete the following steps:</strong></p><ol><li>Meet Verizon Point of Contact</li><li>Locate upgrade kit and existing equipment</li><li>Remove the existing kit (keep the Pathfinder)</li><li>Perform the final assembly and install the SD Card into the Pathfinder.<strong>(Hardware Install Video)</strong></li><li>Mount the replacement enclosure. <strong>**BRING DRILL BITS FOR CONCRETE, DRYWALL, AND METAL**</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there are more than 3 antennas, mount multiple kits near each other and daisy-chain them together<strong>(Page 13 of SOW PDF)</strong>.</li></ul><ol><li>Reconnect all prior data and power connections. <strong>**PORT 5 is only for Data or Daisy Chaining Enclosures**</strong></li><li>Open PowerShell as Administrator</li><li>Copy and Paste script into Powershell <strong>(Reference Modem Video)</strong></li><li>Verify successful functionality of the new system via its webpage <strong>192.168.1.1:8080</strong>.</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If necessary, perform the instructed troubleshooting steps, or document and leave them to be fixed during a second trip.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>IMEI and MAC will not change after update</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Save Log Files in Format <strong>**MAC ADDRESS**</strong><strong>_installation_logs - </strong><strong>**LOCATION**</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">If there is more than 1 Pathfinder label location 1 or 2</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">**Upload these to Work Order**</strong></li></ul><ol><li>Clean up and document successful installation.</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload pictures and closeout notes to work order before leaving site</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>**IF FILES ARE NOT DOWNLOADED AND VIDEO IS NOT WATCHED BEFORE HEADING TO SITE, SOW PENALTY WILL BE ADDED**</strong></p><p>Any questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE</u></strong></p><ol><li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li><li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work.&nbsp;&nbsp;We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.</li></ol><p><strong>Check In Steps</strong> (<u>please follow order</u>)</p><ol><li>Check In via FE Portal</li><li>Check In with Netfor at&nbsp;&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)</li><li>Complete installation per SOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who requested the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li></ol><p><strong>Check out Steps</strong></p><ol><li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>NOTE: <u>*** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER ***</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li><li>Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1</li></ol><ul><li><strong>NOTE:</strong> <strong>Failure to call Netfor to check in or out</strong> could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. <strong>Failure to arrive on time</strong> can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures</strong> within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.</li><li><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p><p>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 10)</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Cat6 Cabling</li><li>ladder</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><ul><li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li><li>A photo of the replacement Pathfinder successfully installed.</li><li>A screenshot of the Pathfinder’s debugging webpage.</li><li>The zipped folder of the Pathfinder’s logs.</li><li>Pictures of area before working</li></ul>","markdown":"**DETAILED SOW**\n\n**Please review installation guide, download files, and watch Hardware Video before arriving at the site.**\n\n**\\*\\*IF YOU HAVE QUESTIONS ABOUT THE SOW, DONT NOT ASK THE VERIZON POC, CALL THE WORK ORDER MANAGER\\*\\***\n\n**Techncian will complete the following steps:**\n\n1. Meet Verizon Point of Contact\n2. Locate upgrade kit and existing equipment\n3. Remove the existing kit (keep the Pathfinder)\n4. Perform the final assembly and install the SD Card into the Pathfinder.**(Hardware Install Video)**\n5. Mount the replacement enclosure. **\\*\\*BRING DRILL BITS FOR CONCRETE, DRYWALL, AND METAL\\*\\***\n\n- If there are more than 3 antennas, mount multiple kits near each other and daisy-chain them together**(Page 13 of SOW PDF)**.\n\n1. Reconnect all prior data and power connections. **\\*\\*PORT 5 is only for Data or Daisy Chaining Enclosures\\*\\***\n2. Open PowerShell as Administrator\n3. Copy and Paste script into Powershell **(Reference Modem Video)**\n4. Verify successful functionality of the new system via its webpage **192.168.1.1:8080**.\n\n- If necessary, perform the instructed troubleshooting steps, or document and leave them to be fixed during a second trip.\n- **IMEI and MAC will not change after update**\n- Save Log Files in Format **\\*\\*MAC ADDRESS\\*\\*****\\_installation\\_logs -** **\\*\\*LOCATION\\*\\***\n- **If there is more than 1 Pathfinder label location 1 or 2**\n- **\\*\\*Upload these to Work Order\\*\\***\n\n1. Clean up and document successful installation.\n\n- Upload pictures and closeout notes to work order before leaving site\n\n**\\*\\*IF FILES ARE NOT DOWNLOADED AND VIDEO IS NOT WATCHED BEFORE HEADING TO SITE, SOW PENALTY WILL BE ADDED\\*\\***\n\nAny questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.\n\n**Check In Steps** (please follow order)\n\n1. Check In via FE Portal\n2. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)\n3. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who requested the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n\n**Check out Steps**\n\n1. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n\n- **NOTE: \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER \\*\\*\\***\n\n1. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n2. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n\n- **NOTE:** **Failure to call Netfor to check in or out** could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. **Failure to arrive on time** can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.\n- **NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures** within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.\n- **REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).**\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 10)\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Cat6 Cabling\n- ladder\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- A photo of the replacement Pathfinder successfully installed.\n- A screenshot of the Pathfinder’s debugging webpage.\n- The zipped folder of the Pathfinder’s logs.\n- Pictures of area before working","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-16T08:30","end":"2026-11-16T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6.073039004607088},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},