{"job":{"id":20233667,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Network Engineering Technologies","title":"ShopperTrak - Orbit AI/Video AI Installation – Sally Beauty - Cary NC - Technician should arrive onsite at the time designated o","description":{"html":"ShopperTrak - Orbit AI/Video AI Installation – Sally Beauty - Cary NC - Technician should arrive onsite at the time designated on the Work Order. Do not discuss or comment on the Orbit AI technology with store managers.<br>______________________________________________________________________________________<br>Each Orbit AI device requires an individual homerun cable and power supply. -Do not assume any data cabling not being used is meant for STK. Need confirmation.<br><br>Description: New installOrbit Type &amp; Connectivity: Orbit ai - IP<br>Notes: Surface mount above entrance&nbsp;<br><br>Provision Mode: Single Site Connectivity<br><br>**Tech should bring patching compound to fill any holes left when mounting orbit/s.**<br>Cat5e or cat6 cable<br>Minimum 10ft ladder<br>Misc Cat5 materials: jacks, surface mount boxes, patch cords, etcetera…<br><br>*Required Tools:<br>Digital camera or smartphone<br>Cat5e/Cat6 tester<br>Butt set<br>Toner<br>Punch tool<br>Standard cabling tools<br>Standard hand tools and power tools<br>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>1) Login with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, and then follow the scope of work and Orbit AI or Video AI Installation Guide<br>TECH SHOULD BRING SMARTPHONE. Tech will need to send photos of installed Orbit(s) and back office equipment FROM SITE.<br>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>2) Locate the Equipment (AI Devices). The equipment is generally in the manager’s office or cash wrap area. Look for a white box with blue ShopperTrak text.&nbsp;<span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Bracket and screw are in a separate box taped to the box with the Orbit AI.</span></span>&nbsp;If equipment cannot be located, STOP, and immediately call NET.<br>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>3) Tech to work with NET when installing the Orbit/Video AI device and call ShopperTrak to test. Orbit AI light should be pointing inside the store. Orbit device should be mounted as close to the center of the doorway as possible. Cabling should already be in place. Use existing port(s). Tech must also route the existing cable at the Orbit so that no cable is exposed. IF a GPU device is included with the ShopperTrak equipment, you'll need to install that using a patch cable in port 12. If port 12 is occupied, use port 13. See GPU Connections doc for reference.<br><br>4) Photos needed while onsite:<br>1. Mounted device(s) close up<br>2. Mounted device(s) farther back to see entire entryway (to include the bottom of the doorway)<br>3. Back office switch/network area<br>4. Wide-shot showing the location of the GPU units<br>5. Photo of MAC address on Orbit/Video AI<br>6. Label the cable ends with the included red “ShopperTrak”, labels and submit photos.<br>7. Be prepared to take any additional photos that NET support may ask for (situational)<br>Remove the lens covers<br><br>Send pictures to DSS@nettechnology.com<br><br>Email subject line MUST read [XXXXXX] where XXXXXX = WO number on NET Purchase order (Typically beginning with a 1). To send photos to DSS please create a new email with the in the format shown. The To Line should be the dss email address and the subject should be the WO by itself with no other numbers symbols or text inside of square brackets. The WO number is the 7 digit ID for this assignment<br>To: dss@nettechnology.com<br>Subject: [WO#]<br><br>If you encounter issues please try to find an open WiFi hotspot nearby and try sending again on wireless signal or ask NET for mobile app link.<br>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>5) Testing<br>Call ShopperTrak 1-312-529-5304 option 2 when ready to test. Hold times are to be expected please remain on the line.***You will need to provide the names of any and all ShopperTrak tech support that you talk to while onsite.<br><br>***If there is equipment to return, then -<br>-Report to NET the contact information (Name and Phone #; Store number is acceptable) of who was given the equipment to return.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>6) Log-Out<br>After working with ShopperTrak, they will provide you with check IN and check OUT codes upon completion of the install. Record these on your Work Order along with the name of the person you worked with at ShopperTrak as NET requires these upon logout.<br><br>Logout with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271(Option 3)<br><br>*YOU MUST LOGIN AND OUT WITH NET* Be respectful to the store managers<br>*FAILURE TO COMPLY WITH ANY PORTION OF THIS WORK ORDER WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT*&nbsp;","markdown":"ShopperTrak - Orbit AI/Video AI Installation – Sally Beauty - Cary NC - Technician should arrive onsite at the time designated on the Work Order. Do not discuss or comment on the Orbit AI technology with store managers.  \n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_  \nEach Orbit AI device requires an individual homerun cable and power supply. -Do not assume any data cabling not being used is meant for STK. Need confirmation.  \n  \nDescription: New installOrbit Type & Connectivity: Orbit ai - IP  \nNotes: Surface mount above entrance   \n  \nProvision Mode: Single Site Connectivity  \n  \n\\*\\*Tech should bring patching compound to fill any holes left when mounting orbit/s.\\*\\*  \nCat5e or cat6 cable  \nMinimum 10ft ladder  \nMisc Cat5 materials: jacks, surface mount boxes, patch cords, etcetera…  \n  \n\\*Required Tools:  \nDigital camera or smartphone  \nCat5e/Cat6 tester  \nButt set  \nToner  \nPunch tool  \nStandard cabling tools  \nStandard hand tools and power tools  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n1\\) Login with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, and then follow the scope of work and Orbit AI or Video AI Installation Guide  \nTECH SHOULD BRING SMARTPHONE. Tech will need to send photos of installed Orbit(s) and back office equipment FROM SITE.  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n2\\) Locate the Equipment (AI Devices). The equipment is generally in the manager’s office or cash wrap area. Look for a white box with blue ShopperTrak text. Bracket and screw are in a separate box taped to the box with the Orbit AI. If equipment cannot be located, STOP, and immediately call NET.  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n3\\) Tech to work with NET when installing the Orbit/Video AI device and call ShopperTrak to test. Orbit AI light should be pointing inside the store. Orbit device should be mounted as close to the center of the doorway as possible. Cabling should already be in place. Use existing port(s). Tech must also route the existing cable at the Orbit so that no cable is exposed. IF a GPU device is included with the ShopperTrak equipment, you'll need to install that using a patch cable in port 12. If port 12 is occupied, use port 13. See GPU Connections doc for reference.  \n  \n4\\) Photos needed while onsite:  \n1\\. Mounted device(s) close up  \n2\\. Mounted device(s) farther back to see entire entryway (to include the bottom of the doorway)  \n3\\. Back office switch/network area  \n4\\. Wide-shot showing the location of the GPU units  \n5\\. Photo of MAC address on Orbit/Video AI  \n6\\. Label the cable ends with the included red “ShopperTrak”, labels and submit photos.  \n7\\. Be prepared to take any additional photos that NET support may ask for (situational)  \nRemove the lens covers  \n  \nSend pictures to DSS@nettechnology.com  \n  \nEmail subject line MUST read \\[XXXXXX\\] where XXXXXX = WO number on NET Purchase order (Typically beginning with a 1). To send photos to DSS please create a new email with the in the format shown. The To Line should be the dss email address and the subject should be the WO by itself with no other numbers symbols or text inside of square brackets. The WO number is the 7 digit ID for this assignment  \nTo: dss@nettechnology.com  \nSubject: \\[WO#\\]  \n  \nIf you encounter issues please try to find an open WiFi hotspot nearby and try sending again on wireless signal or ask NET for mobile app link.  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n5\\) Testing  \nCall ShopperTrak 1-312-529-5304 option 2 when ready to test. Hold times are to be expected please remain on the line.\\*\\*\\*You will need to provide the names of any and all ShopperTrak tech support that you talk to while onsite.  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*If there is equipment to return, then -  \n-Report to NET the contact information (Name and Phone #; Store number is acceptable) of who was given the equipment to return.   \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n6\\) Log-Out  \nAfter working with ShopperTrak, they will provide you with check IN and check OUT codes upon completion of the install. Record these on your Work Order along with the name of the person you worked with at ShopperTrak as NET requires these upon logout.  \n  \nLogout with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271(Option 3)  \n  \n\\*YOU MUST LOGIN AND OUT WITH NET\\* Be respectful to the store managers  \n\\*FAILURE TO COMPLY WITH ANY PORTION OF THIS WORK ORDER WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T11:00","end":"2026-10-28T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":305,"max":305},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":10.24062333661632},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":102,"baseAmount":305,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":25,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"sta