{"job":{"id":20234207,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"EV Charger Wi‑Fi Connectivity Troubleshooting & Network Validation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code: Business Casual</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>Laptop with Wi‑Fi and Ethernet capability</p><p>Ethernet cable</p><p>Mobile hotspot (recommended)</p><p>Mobile phone for coordination with EPLUS, remote support, and property contact</p><p>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)</p><p>Network troubleshooting tools</p><p>Wi‑Fi analyzer software/application (recommended)</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Camera-enabled device for documentation and photos</p><p>PPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)</p><p><br></p><strong>Reported Issue</strong><ul><li>EV chargers at the site are currently unable to connect to the network.</li><li>A previous troubleshooting attempt was unsuccessful.</li><li>Property management has advised that updates have been made to the site's Wi‑Fi network and requests advance notice of the technician's ETA so onsite personnel can be available to assist during the service visit.</li></ul><strong>Scope of Work</strong><ul><li>Provide onsite support to troubleshoot and restore connectivity for the affected EV charging stations.</li><li>Coordinate with EPLUS, remote support personnel, and the property contact throughout the visit.</li><li>Verify charger power status and confirm all affected chargers are operational.</li><li>Inspect and validate network, Wi‑Fi, and communication settings on the chargers.</li><li>Verify the updated Wi‑Fi network information provided by the property.</li><li>Test charger connectivity to the current Wi‑Fi network.</li><li>Verify internet access and network stability at the charger locations.</li><li>Confirm communication between the chargers and the management platform.</li><li>Perform basic troubleshooting, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi‑Fi connectivity verification</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Signal strength testing</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Network configuration validation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Router/access point connectivity checks</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power cycling equipment if directed</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Charger communication testing</li><li>Assist EPLUS remote support with diagnostics and validation.</li><li>Verify chargers successfully reconnect to the network and return online.</li><li>Document any network, hardware, or site issues identified during troubleshooting.</li><li>If connectivity cannot be restored onsite, gather detailed findings and assist with escalation.</li></ul><br><strong>Documentation</strong><ul><li>Take photos of:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Charger status indicators/screens</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Network equipment (router, access point, etc.)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any identified issues or damage</li><li>Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photo documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival&nbsp;</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check in with SG net.</li><li>&nbsp;Call EV support</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Before and After pictures</li><li>Notes</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet</li><li><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Contact SGNet</strong></p>","markdown":"**Dress Code: Business Casual**\n\n·\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nLaptop with Wi‑Fi and Ethernet capability\n\nEthernet cable\n\nMobile hotspot (recommended)\n\nMobile phone for coordination with EPLUS, remote support, and property contact\n\nBasic hand tools (screwdrivers, nut drivers, pliers)\n\nNetwork troubleshooting tools\n\nWi‑Fi analyzer software/application (recommended)\n\nFlashlight\n\nCamera-enabled device for documentation and photos\n\nPPE as required by site (safety glasses, gloves, safety footwear)\n\n**Reported Issue**- EV chargers at the site are currently unable to connect to the network.\n- A previous troubleshooting attempt was unsuccessful.\n- Property management has advised that updates have been made to the site's Wi‑Fi network and requests advance notice of the technician's ETA so onsite personnel can be available to assist during the service visit.\n\n**Scope of Work**- Provide onsite support to troubleshoot and restore connectivity for the affected EV charging stations.\n- Coordinate with EPLUS, remote support personnel, and the property contact throughout the visit.\n- Verify charger power status and confirm all affected chargers are operational.\n- Inspect and validate network, Wi‑Fi, and communication settings on the chargers.\n- Verify the updated Wi‑Fi network information provided by the property.\n- Test charger connectivity to the current Wi‑Fi network.\n- Verify internet access and network stability at the charger locations.\n- Confirm communication between the chargers and the management platform.\n- Perform basic troubleshooting, including:\n- Wi‑Fi connectivity verification\n- Signal strength testing\n- Network configuration validation\n- Router/access point connectivity checks\n- Power cycling equipment if directed\n- Charger communication testing\n- Assist EPLUS remote support with diagnostics and validation.\n- Verify chargers successfully reconnect to the network and return online.\n- Document any network, hardware, or site issues identified during troubleshooting.\n- If connectivity cannot be restored onsite, gather detailed findings and assist with escalation.\n\n  \n**Documentation**- Take photos of:\n- Charger status indicators/screens\n- Network equipment (router, access point, etc.)\n- Any identified issues or damage\n- Update the Field Nation work order with detailed troubleshooting notes, test results, and photo documentation.\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Call EV support 30 mins prior to arrival\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with SG net.\n2. Call EV support\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Before and After pictures\n2. Notes\n3. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with SGNet\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to SGNet\n- **Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n**Contact SGNet**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T10:00","end":"2026-10-26T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.674895351249788},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDa