{"job":{"id":20234192,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Equipment Configuration/Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><p><strong>Task ID:</strong> 5379516<br /><strong>PON:</strong> 505468<br /><strong>Account Name:</strong> Papa Johns - #004587 - Bracey, VA<br /><strong>Service Address:</strong> 3384 Highway 903, Bracey, VA 23919</p>\r\n<p><strong>IOW Only Install</strong><br /><br /><strong>Special Notes:</strong> TECH TO GO ONSITE AND INSTALL 2 CRADLEPOINTS<br />1 OUTSIDE 1 INDOOR<br /><br />WEBBING SIM<br />Circuit ID: 38.98.90.64<br />Telephone Number: 852197125274045<br /><br />TMOBILE SIM<br />Circuit ID: 162.190.157.136<br />Telephone Number: 5883119396<br /><br />Tech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.</p></p><p><strong>Technician must bring a working 1 gig laptop with ability to connect ethernet handoff for internet equipment speed testing, 10ft ladder, J-Hooks, Hammer Drill with concrete bits and anchors. Micsc: Velcro, Zip Ty's etc. Tech needs to be prepared to install 2 Antenna extensions and 2 Antennas. 1 interior and 1 exterior.</strong></p><ul><li>Field tech will check in on site with Customer Manager on Duty than call into Spectrotel Activations for instructions.</li><li>Field tech to locate Spectrotel shipment, take pics of equipment and load to platform.</li></ul><p><strong>Spectrotel will provide two (2) Cradlepoints and two (2) antennas.</strong></p><p><strong>2-Cradlepoint R980 wireless routers</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Antenna #1</strong> will include 40 ft. of antenna cable.</li><li><strong>Antenna #2</strong> will include four (4) 100-ft. antenna cables.</li></ul><p>Spectrotel will also provide two (2) additional 40-ft. cable extensions for use if the 100-ft. cables are not required.</p><p>A prepaid return shipping label will be provided onsite. All unused cable extensions must be returned to Spectrotel.</p><ul><li>&nbsp;Unbox and mount the 2 Cradlepoints near existing network rack based on power availability.</li><li>Once online, Call and work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier</li><li>Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:</li></ul><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Proof.ovh.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speed.cloudflare.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speedof.me</p><p><strong>Interior Installation:</strong></p><ul><li>Install the first antenna inside the store using the provided 40-ft. cable. The antenna must be installed away from the equipment rack and must not be mounted above the ceiling.</li><li>Work directly with Spectrotel during the installation to determine the best antenna location. Test signal strength at potential mounting locations and install the antenna on the wall below the ceiling where optimal signal strength is obtained.</li><li>Once the location is confirmed by Spectrotel, permanently install and secure the antenna.</li><li>Take clear pictures of the completed antenna installation and final mounting location.</li></ul><p><strong>Exterior Installation:</strong></p><ul><li>Perform signal testing along the rear and side exterior of the building to determine the optimal mounting location for the second antenna. Install the antenna at the location providing the strongest signal, utilizing the provided four (4) 100-ft. antenna cables as required.</li><li>The antenna must not be mounted on the front façade of the building unless prior approval has been obtained from Spectrotel.</li><li>If the 100-ft. cables are longer than required, use the provided shorter cable extensions for the exterior antenna installation.</li><li>Properly route and secure all antenna cabling after the final location has been confirmed.</li><li>Take clear pictures of the completed antenna installation and final mounting location.</li></ul><p><strong>Important:</strong> Any unused cable extensions must be packaged and returned to Spectrotel using the provided return shipping label.</p><ul><li>Once online, work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier</li><li>Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:</li></ul><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Proof.ovh.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speed.cloudflare.net</p><p>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Speedof.me</p><ul><li>Spectrotel will confirm RSSI,RSRP,RSRQ,SINR before tech leaves site.</li><li>Once testing is completed tech will clean area and be released from site</li></ul><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p>You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.</p><p><strong>♦ Contacts</strong></p><p>Please reach out to Spectrotel in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</p><p>You must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.</p><p><strong>♦ Material and Equipment Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Tech MUST have inside their bag when arriving to the building **NON-NEGOTIABLE**. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.</li><li>FULL Charged Windows Laptop with Gigabit RJ45 ethernet port &amp; Power Supply, with console cable and HOTSPOT</li><li>Minimum 6 ft ladder, 8-10 A frame is preferred</li><li>Cordless Battery-Operated Drill with Assorted Drill Bits</li><li>Wall Mounting Anchors for Sheetrock / Wood / Metal / Concrete</li><li>Cat5 or CAT6 cabling, 100-200 ft</li><li>Jacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper, wire ties, wire straps, drywall anchors and screws</li><li>The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.</li></ul><p><strong>**The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)**</strong></p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables</strong></p><p>Detailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.</p><p>We request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.</p><p>Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.</p><p>Please provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.</p><p>If a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.</p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Task ID:** 5379516  \n**PON:** 505468  \n**Account Name:** Papa Johns - #004587 - Bracey, VA  \n**Service Address:** 3384 Highway 903, Bracey, VA 23919\n\n**IOW Only Install**  \n  \n**Special Notes:** TECH TO GO ONSITE AND INSTALL 2 CRADLEPOINTS  \n1 OUTSIDE 1 INDOOR  \n  \nWEBBING SIM  \nCircuit ID: 38.98.90.64  \nTelephone Number: 852197125274045  \n  \nTMOBILE SIM  \nCircuit ID: 162.190.157.136  \nTelephone Number: 5883119396  \n  \nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.\n\n**Technician must bring a working 1 gig laptop with ability to connect ethernet handoff for internet equipment speed testing, 10ft ladder, J-Hooks, Hammer Drill with concrete bits and anchors. Micsc: Velcro, Zip Ty's etc. Tech needs to be prepared to install 2 Antenna extensions and 2 Antennas. 1 interior and 1 exterior.**\n\n- Field tech will check in on site with Customer Manager on Duty than call into Spectrotel Activations for instructions.\n- Field tech to locate Spectrotel shipment, take pics of equipment and load to platform.\n\n**Spectrotel will provide two (2) Cradlepoints and two (2) antennas.**\n\n**2-Cradlepoint R980 wireless routers**\n\n- **Antenna #1** will include 40 ft. of antenna cable.\n- **Antenna #2** will include four (4) 100-ft. antenna cables.\n\nSpectrotel will also provide two (2) additional 40-ft. cable extensions for use if the 100-ft. cables are not required.\n\nA prepaid return shipping label will be provided onsite. All unused cable extensions must be returned to Spectrotel.\n\n- Unbox and mount the 2 Cradlepoints near existing network rack based on power availability.\n- Once online, Call and work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier\n- Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:\n\no Proof.ovh.net\n\no Speed.cloudflare.net\n\no Speedof.me\n\n**Interior Installation:**\n\n- Install the first antenna inside the store using the provided 40-ft. cable. The antenna must be installed away from the equipment rack and must not be mounted above the ceiling.\n- Work directly with Spectrotel during the installation to determine the best antenna location. Test signal strength at potential mounting locations and install the antenna on the wall below the ceiling where optimal signal strength is obtained.\n- Once the location is confirmed by Spectrotel, permanently install and secure the antenna.\n- Take clear pictures of the completed antenna installation and final mounting location.\n\n**Exterior Installation:**\n\n- Perform signal testing along the rear and side exterior of the building to determine the optimal mounting location for the second antenna. Install the antenna at the location providing the strongest signal, utilizing the provided four (4) 100-ft. antenna cables as required.\n- The antenna must not be mounted on the front façade of the building unless prior approval has been obtained from Spectrotel.\n- If the 100-ft. cables are longer than required, use the provided shorter cable extensions for the exterior antenna installation.\n- Properly route and secure all antenna cabling after the final location has been confirmed.\n- Take clear pictures of the completed antenna installation and final mounting location.\n\n**Important:** Any unused cable extensions must be packaged and returned to Spectrotel using the provided return shipping label.\n\n- Once online, work with Spectrotel Activations to determine if signal strength is adequate. If not adequate, activations will select optimal carrier\n- Connect laptop to Cradlepoint port 1 set for DHCP and run speed test to any of the following sites:\n\no Proof.ovh.net\n\no Speed.cloudflare.net\n\no Speedof.me\n\n- Spectrotel will confirm RSSI,RSRP,RSRQ,SINR before tech leaves site.\n- Once testing is completed tech will clean area and be released from site\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\nYou must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.\n\n**♦ Contacts**\n\nPlease reach out to Spectrotel in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.\n\nYou must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.\n\n**♦ Material and Equipment Requirements**\n\n- Tech MUST have inside their bag when arriving to the building \\*\\*NON-NEGOTIABLE\\*\\*. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.\n- FULL Charged Windows Laptop with Gigabit RJ45 ethernet port & Power Supply, with console cable and HOTSPOT\n- Minimum 6 ft ladder, 8-10 A frame is preferred\n- Cordless Battery-Operated Drill with Assorted Drill Bits\n- Wall Mounting Anchors for Sheetrock / Wood / Metal / Concrete\n- Cat5 or CAT6 cabling, 100-200 ft\n- Jacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper, wire ties, wire straps, drywall anchors and screws\n- The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.\n\n**\\*\\*The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)\\*\\***\n\n\\---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables**\n\nDetailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.\n\nWe request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.\n\nSubsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.\n\nPlease provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.\n\nIf a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T11:30","end":"2026-11-05T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.68963946698612},"result":{"eligible":fa