{"job":{"id":"4464426799","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Locate replacement node, upgrade firmware and install replacement","description":"Priority and Dispatch Date: P.3 10/29 12p EST hard start Approved by Robin Hagan per phone conversation <br><br>If you have any questions, please contact Granite NOC at 833-763-8677  <br><br>Repair Ticket: 6927586  <br><br>Customer: Flowers Foods Grandparent <br><br>Address: 217 WOODINGTON ROAD HOPE MILLS, NC 28348 <br><br>LCON: MOD Kenny Germane 9199206160 <br><br>Granite NOC at 833-763-8677 <br>AH: 24/7 365 <br><br>Summary: Locate replacement node, upgrade firmware and install replacement <br><br>Tech must be on site early and ready to work at customer maint window starting at 12p EST <br><br>REQUIRED MATERIAL: ), Laptop (Windows 10 or higher with admin rights), a working mobile hotspot, phone w/ phone charger, USB 2.0 flash drive with at least 16GB, console cable RJ45 to USB, serial-&gt;USB adapter, Cisco ASR-920 compatible USB A-to-A cable (this model does not use regular Cisco console cables), <br><br>-----  <br>Materials Needed (PLEASE BRING ALL MATERIALS): LAPTOP (Windows 10 or higher with admin rights), a working mobile hotspot, phone w/ phone charger, USB 2.0 flash drive with at least 16GB, console cable, serial-&gt;USB adapter, Cisco ASR-920 compatible USB A-to-A cable (this model does not use regular Cisco console cables), electrical extension cord (25’ min), two complete surface jacks, splitter, Ethernet cable tester, ethernet toner with probe, replacement ethernet patch cables, cat5e/cat6 cable (150’ min), min 4 RJ-45 wall jacks and plates, at least 4 Biscuit Jacks, &amp; butt set for troubleshooting. Laptop must have PuTTY and TeamViewer installed and must be capable of 1000 Mbps speeds, either with an integrated Ethernet port or a high-speed adapter.   <br><br>-----  <br><br>Instructions may be subject to change at the discretion of Granite NOC Repair  <br><br>If you have any questions, please contact Granite NOC at 833-763-8677  <br><br>1: Technician must check in via WORKMARKET, then work with site contact to gain access to the building and the necessary equipment.  <br><br>2: When the technician reaches out to the Granite NOC 833-763-8677 , they must request to work with a member of the EAST Team. If a rep outside of the EAST Team receives this call, please submit an escalation in the \"Special Teams - E.A.S.T. Escalations\" teams channel or reach out to Supervisor Jessica Juan-Aquino to get an available member of the team to take over by having tech call 833-763-8677.  <br><br>3: Locate UPS package 1Z20506Y0300753643 with replacement SN: AR36240006 and old Node 1 (secondary) MAC: 00:90:0b:d2:09:40 <br><br>4: Take pictures of current site cabling, and of any serial numbers, mac addresses and claim codes of new replacement node and add to work market for review <br><br>5: Granite NOC to work with current Network Engineering collaboration to preform console session to upgrade Node firmware to current version 6.2.4-14.r2  <br> <br>Firmware upgrade must fully take place before connecting replacement to the network to ensure the site is not taken down in the process <br><br>5a: Once replacement node firmware is upgraded, NOC and engineering must work to implement replacement node and restore site connectivity <br><br>6: Confirm that all Granite equipment is properly connected to any customer equipment &amp; that the services at the site are operational. Granite NOC rep will reach out to the customer NOC to verify that they can use the connection.  <br><br>7: Technician must check out via WORKMARKET and upload all necessary photos and work completed. <br> <br>------ <br>Old Juniper Node 1 (secondary) CPEMST0000001314 <br>MAC: 00:90:0b:d2:09:40","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T12:00","end":"2026-10-29T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"dist