{"job":{"id":20235038,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Xerox IT Solutions, LLC","title":"Installation of (2) K22L Countertop Kiosk - Possible (2)Dual Cable Run (4 Runs)","description":{"html":"<p>⚠️ PLEASE READ SERVICE DESCRIPTION CAREFULLY AS CHANGES HAVE BEEN MADE! WHEN CALLING INTO ACRELEC SUPPORT, IF PLACED ON HOLD FOR LONGER THAN 15 MINUTES, LET YOUR WO MANAGER KNOW THROUGH CALL/TEXT SO THEY CAN REACH OUT TO SUPPORT DIRECTLY. AFTER THEY HAVE REACHED OUT, CONTACT WO MANAGER AGAIN IF ANOTHER 15 MINUTES PASS WITH NO CONTACT. ⚠️</p><p>⚠️ PLEASE READ DELIVERABLES AND TOOLS REQUIRED AS THEY HAVE BEEN UPDATED AND THE LACK OF THESE DELIVERABLES WILL RESULT IN A DELAY IN CLOSING THE WORK ORDER ⚠️</p><p>⚠️ IF CABLE RUNS EXCEED 100 FT EACH, PLEASE CONTACT ACRELEC SUPPORT FIRST AND GET THEIR APPROVAL ⚠️</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>1. OBJECTIVE(S)</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>Install the K22 Kiosk(s), run data cabling (if needed), and configure and test the unit(s).</li></ul><p><strong><u>2. CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>In the event of an aborted installation after check-in (ex. equipment not onsite, site not ready, etc.), the Provider agrees to accept a fixed payment of $100.00.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>This job is set at a fixed price. Any delays exceeding 30 minutes that are out of the technician’s control (ex. trips to get missing parts, delays waiting on site team, long configuration hold times) must be reported immediately to the WO Manager. Pay adjustments past 3hrs for K22s and 4hrs for K27s MUST account for delays, require delay time logs, explanations, and are to be granted at the WO Manager's discretion. The delay time log MUST be completed for OOS payments.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Out-of-scope hours will be paid at a rate of $55/hr. IF REQUIRED, ADD DATA CABLING TIME AND MATERIAL TO EXPENSES FOR REIMBURSEMENT.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>WORK ORDERS WILL ONLY BE PAID IF ALL REQUIRED DELIVERABLES ARE UPLOADED TO THE FIELD NATION TICKET. These are to be uploaded to Field Nation and reviewed by the WO Manager BEFORE checking out. The Provider is solely responsible for any additional trips to the work site (along with any additional accrued work hours) if all deliverables are not uploaded or the work is not completed as specified in the scope of work and/or installation manual. Obtain a release code from Acrelec install support team.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>Dress code: </strong>Business casual required &mdash; collared polo or button-down shirt with khakis/dockers (no shorts, t-shirts, sneakers, or athletic wear).</p><p><strong>Note</strong>: we ask for a picture \"selfie\" upon check in to verify it is the assigned technician on the WO.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>3. PROCEDURE</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>-------------------------Follow the instructions in the installation guide--------------------------------------</strong></p><p><strong>-------------------------------------General summary of steps below--------------------------------------------------</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>A. Assembly/Installation</strong></p><ul><li>Work with store MOD or franchise Owner/Owner Representative to determine Kiosk install location(s) and locate Kiosk hardware shipment.</li><li><strong><em>MOD (Manager on Duty) and/or Franchise Representative must approve kiosk location(s) PRIOR to drilling and beginning the installation of the Kiosk(s).</em></strong></li><li><em>Complete inventory to confirm all parts listed installation guide are onsite. Please note pin pads are shipped separately from Verifone.</em></li><li>Ensure Kiosk location(s) have power and data source (2x Cat6 Cables per kiosk) required for installation.</li></ul><p><strong>--------------STOP AND PROCEED TO CABLING SECTION BELOW IF NO DATA CABLING IS PRESENT--------------</strong></p><ul><li>Install Bridge PC&nbsp;<strong><em>PRIOR</em></strong>&nbsp;to beginning kiosk assembly.</li><li>Bridge PC to be powered on and patched into&nbsp;<strong>Port 14</strong>&nbsp;of main managed switch typically Cisco Meraki located in MOD’s office.</li><li>Call Acrelec Support upon installation of Bridge PC to begin remote configuration&nbsp;<strong>(866) 932-0080 - Option 2, then Option 1.</strong></li><li>Proceed with Kiosk assembly and installation.</li><li>Upon completion of installation, contact Acrelec Support to begin kiosk configuration and testing&nbsp;<strong>(866) 932-0080 - Option 2, then Option 1.</strong></li><li>Complete credit card and gift card testing on-site with the store representative/Acrelec support to ensure kiosks are fully operational.</li><li>Remove stylus holder and pen on left hand side of pin pad. This is a REQUIREMENT for Dunkin Donuts locations.</li><li><strong><em>*** TECH MUST BE RELEASED BY A MEMEBER OF ACRELEC SUPPORT WITH AUTHORITY TO RELEASE. ACRELEC WILL PROVIDE RELEASE CODE WHICH MUST BE DOCUMENTATED ***</em></strong></li><li><strong>***Complete the Acrelec Smartsheet form</strong>,<strong> even if the site is incomplete</strong>. <strong><em><u>This MUST be completed for each visit on the same day before leaving site</u></em></strong><em>,</em> even if multiple days on the same work order.&nbsp;</li><li>Upload pictures of completed installation(s) and cabling (if ran during this visit)&nbsp;<strong><em>BEFORE</em></strong>&nbsp;leaving the site.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please refer to Deliverables section and Example Pictures in documents &ndash; <strong><em>pictures must match the templates exactly</em></strong>.</li><li>Clean up work area and leave any miscellaneous items with the store Manager or Owner/Owner Representative.</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;B. Cabling (if Needed) - This is deemed out of scope labor - Let WO Manager know if cabling is needed.</strong></p><ul><li>Check power outlet availability to future kiosk location(s).</li><li>Check low voltage pathway from main switch (typically in Manager’s office) to future kiosk location(s).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Kiosk(s) typically installed on front counter by registers, facing the customer.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><em>MOD (Manager on Duty) and/or Franchise Representative must specify prospective kiosk location(s) PRIOR to beginning survey and cabling.</em></strong></li><li>If accessible,&nbsp;<strong>run (2) Cat6 cables&nbsp;<em>per kiosk</em></strong>. Test and terminate (w/ surface mount jacks where possible) on each end.</li></ul><p><strong><u>4. MATERIAL/EQUIPMENT REQUIRED</u>:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ROTARY HAMMER DRILL &amp; MASONRY BIT SET (to include 3/8”, 1/2\" and 5/8” drill bits)</strong></li><li><strong>3/8 Drive ratchet &amp; Metric socket set</strong></li><li><strong>USB Keyboard and Mouse</strong></li><li><strong>300 Ft. Cat6 Plenum (Reimbursed at $0.50/ft.)</strong></li><li><strong>Hack saw (May be needed to cut ceiling poles)</strong></li><li><strong>Heavy duty Velcro</strong></li><li>RJ45 Male ends (Reimbursed at $0.75/ea.)</li><li>Keystones (Reimbursed at $2.00/ea.)</li><li>Surface Mount Data Jack (Reimbursed at $5.00/ea.)</li><li>Assorted Allen wrenches (5/32)</li><li>Hammer</li><li>Torpedo level (or laser level recommended)</li><li>Drywall saw</li><li>Flat head and Philips head screw drivers</li><li>8ft. A-frame ladder</li><li>Nut drivers (SAE and Metric)</li><li>Assorted zip ties</li><li>Measuring tape</li><li>Box cutter</li><li>Electrical tape</li><li>Fish tape and/or push rods (min 100ft.)</li><li>Data cable crimper</li><li>Cordless drill and bit set (<em>optional, but recommended</em>)</li><li>Network Cable Tester/Toner</li><li>Cell Phone</li><li>Laptop/Tablet</li><li>Label maker</li><li>TDR or Network Cable Length Tester</li><li>Hotspot</li></ul><p><strong><u>5. DELIVERABLES</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>Submit Installation Smartsheet Form <strong>BEFORE LEAVING SITE</strong>: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/141f9472fded4a8a8593aae40e6882bb.</li><li><em>***Acrelec Install Support </em><strong><em>MUST provide a release code</em></strong><em> listed in WO for approved payment. Please list release code for each day if applicable***</em></li><li><strong><em>AFTER</em></strong> all testing is complete, upload pictures of…</li></ul><p><strong><em>---------------------Refer to Example Pictures in documents------------------------------</em></strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>***Stylus holder and pen REMOVED on left hand side of pin pad.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cable Tester showing cable run distance ⚠️&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unopened kiosk boxes (as found upon arrival)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Bridge PC and D-Link Switch in network office</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ports 13 and 14 in main switch in use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cable tester pass (if cabling was run during this visit)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cable management inside kiosk door</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Close-up side view of pin pad</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Full picture of completed kiosk (Showing LOGO)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wide angle shot of completed kiosk (Showing LOGO)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide a picture showing measurement of countertop to finished floor and picture showing measurement of top edge of kiosk screen to finished floor</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pictures of credit card and gift card test transaction receipts</li></ul>","markdown":"⚠️ PLEASE READ SERVICE DESCRIPTION CAREFULLY AS CHANGES HAVE BEEN MADE! WHEN CALLING INTO ACRELEC SUPPORT, IF PLACED ON HOLD FOR LONGER THAN 15 MINUTES, LET YOUR WO MANAGER KNOW THROUGH CALL/TEXT SO THEY CAN REACH OUT TO SUPPORT DIRECTLY. AFTER THEY HAVE REACHED OUT, CONTACT WO MANAGER AGAIN IF ANOTHER 15 MINUTES PASS WITH NO CONTACT. ⚠️\n\n⚠️ PLEASE READ DELIVERABLES AND TOOLS REQUIRED AS THEY HAVE BEEN UPDATED AND THE LACK OF THESE DELIVERABLES WILL RESULT IN A DELAY IN CLOSING THE WORK ORDER ⚠️\n\n⚠️ IF CABLE RUNS EXCEED 100 FT EACH, PLEASE CONTACT ACRELEC SUPPORT FIRST AND GET THEIR APPROVAL ⚠️\n\n**1. OBJECTIVE(S):**\n\n- Install the K22 Kiosk(s), run data cabling (if needed), and configure and test the unit(s).\n\n**2. CONDITIONS**\n\n***In the event of an aborted installation after check-in (ex. equipment not onsite, site not ready, etc.), the Provider agrees to accept a fixed payment of $100.00.***\n\n***This job is set at a fixed price. Any delays exceeding 30 minutes that are out of the technician’s control (ex. trips to get missing parts, delays waiting on site team, long configuration hold times) must be reported immediately to the WO Manager. Pay adjustments past 3hrs for K22s and 4hrs for K27s MUST account for delays, require delay time logs, explanations, and are to be granted at the WO Manager's discretion. The delay time log MUST be completed for OOS payments.***\n\n***Out-of-scope hours will be paid at a rate of $55/hr. IF REQUIRED, ADD DATA CABLING TIME AND MATERIAL TO EXPENSES FOR REIMBURSEMENT.***\n\n***WORK ORDERS WILL ONLY BE PAID IF ALL REQUIRED DELIVERABLES ARE UPLOADED TO THE FIELD NATION TICKET. These are to be uploaded to Field Nation and reviewed by the WO Manager BEFORE checking out. The Provider is solely responsible for any additional trips to the work site (along with any additional accrued work hours) if all deliverables are not uploaded or the work is not completed as specified in the scope of work and/or installation manual. Obtain a release code from Acrelec install support team.***\n\n**Dress code:** Business casual required — collared polo or button-down shirt with khakis/dockers (no shorts, t-shirts, sneakers, or athletic wear).\n\n**Note**: we ask for a picture \"selfie\" upon check in to verify it is the assigned technician on the WO.\n\n**3. PROCEDURE:**\n\n**-------------------------Follow the instructions in the installation guide--------------------------------------**\n\n**-------------------------------------General summary of steps below--------------------------------------------------**\n\n  **A. Assembly/Installation**\n\n- Work with store MOD or franchise Owner/Owner Representative to determine Kiosk install location(s) and locate Kiosk hardware shipment.\n- ***MOD (Manager on Duty) and/or Franchise Representative must approve kiosk location(s) PRIOR to drilling and beginning the installation of the Kiosk(s).***\n- *Complete inventory to confirm all parts listed installation guide are onsite. Please note pin pads are shipped separately from Verifone.*\n- Ensure Kiosk location(s) have power and data source (2x Cat6 Cables per kiosk) required for installation.\n\n**--------------STOP AND PROCEED TO CABLING SECTION BELOW IF NO DATA CABLING IS PRESENT--------------**\n\n- Install Bridge PC ***PRIOR*** to beginning kiosk assembly.\n- Bridge PC to be powered on and patched into **Port 14** of main managed switch typically Cisco Meraki located in MOD’s office.\n- Call Acrelec Support upon installation of Bridge PC to begin remote configuration **(866) 932-0080 - Option 2, then Option 1.**\n- Proceed with Kiosk assembly and installation.\n- Upon completion of installation, contact Acrelec Support to begin kiosk configuration and testing **(866) 932-0080 - Option 2, then Option 1.**\n- Complete credit card and gift card testing on-site with the store representative/Acrelec support to ensure kiosks are fully operational.\n- Remove stylus holder and pen on left hand side of pin pad. This is a REQUIREMENT for Dunkin Donuts locations.\n- ***\\*\\*\\* TECH MUST BE RELEASED BY A MEMEBER OF ACRELEC SUPPORT WITH AUTHORITY TO RELEASE. ACRELEC WILL PROVIDE RELEASE CODE WHICH MUST BE DOCUMENTATED \\*\\*\\****\n- **\\*\\*\\*Complete the Acrelec Smartsheet form**, **even if the site is incomplete**. ***This MUST be completed for each visit on the same day before leaving site****,* even if multiple days on the same work order.\n- Upload pictures of completed installation(s) and cabling (if ran during this visit) ***BEFORE*** leaving the site.\n- Please refer to Deliverables section and Example Pictures in documents – ***pictures must match the templates exactly***.\n- Clean up work area and leave any miscellaneous items with the store Manager or Owner/Owner Representative.\n\n **B. Cabling (if Needed) - This is deemed out of scope labor - Let WO Manager know if cabling is needed.**\n\n- Check power outlet availability to future kiosk location(s).\n- Check low voltage pathway from main switch (typically in Manager’s office) to future kiosk location(s).\n- Kiosk(s) typically installed on front counter by registers, facing the customer.\n- ***MOD (Manager on Duty) and/or Franchise Representative must specify prospective kiosk location(s) PRIOR to beginning survey and cabling.***\n- If accessible, **run (2) Cat6 cables *per kiosk***. Test and terminate (w/ surface mount jacks where possible) on each end.\n\n**4. MATERIAL/EQUIPMENT REQUIRED:**\n\n- **ROTARY HAMMER DRILL & MASONRY BIT SET (to include 3/8”, 1/2\" and 5/8” drill bits)**\n- **3/8 Drive ratchet & Metric socket set**\n- **USB Keyboard and Mouse**\n- **300 Ft. Cat6 Plenum (Reimbursed at $0.50/ft.)**\n- **Hack saw (May be needed to cut ceiling poles)**\n- **Heavy duty Velcro**\n- RJ45 Male ends (Reimbursed at $0.75/ea.)\n- Keystones (Reimbursed at $2.00/ea.)\n- Surface Mount Data Jack (Reimbursed at $5.00/ea.)\n- Assorted Allen wrenches (5/32)\n- Hammer\n- Torpedo level (or laser level recommended)\n- Drywall saw\n- Flat head and Philips head screw drivers\n- 8ft. A-frame ladder\n- Nut drivers (SAE and Metric)\n- Assorted zip ties\n- Measuring tape\n- Box cutter\n- Electrical tape\n- Fish tape and/or push rods (min 100ft.)\n- Data cable crimper\n- Cordless drill and bit set (*optional, but recommended*)\n- Network Cable Tester/Toner\n- Cell Phone\n- Laptop/Tablet\n- Label maker\n- TDR or Network Cable Length Tester\n- Hotspot\n\n**5. DELIVERABLES:**\n\n- Submit Installation Smartsheet Form **BEFORE LEAVING SITE**: <https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/141f9472fded4a8a8593aae40e6882bb.>\n- *\\*\\*\\*Acrelec Install Support* ***MUST provide a release code*** *listed in WO for approved payment. Please list release code for each day if applicable\\*\\*\\**\n- ***AFTER*** all testing is complete, upload pictures of…\n\n***---------------------Refer to Example Pictures in documents------------------------------***\n\n- **\\*\\*\\*Stylus holder and pen REMOVED on left hand side of pin pad.**\n- Cable Tester showing cable run distance ⚠️\n- Unopened kiosk boxes (as found upon arrival)\n- Bridge PC and D-Link Switch in network office\n- Ports 13 and 14 in main switch in use\n- Cable tester pass (if cabling was run during this visit)\n- Cable management inside kiosk door\n- Close-up side view of pin pad\n- Full picture of completed kiosk (Showing LOGO)\n- Wide angle shot of completed kiosk (Showing LOGO)\n- Provide a picture showing measurement of countertop to finished floor and picture showing measurement of top edge of kiosk screen to finished floor\n- Pictures of credit card and gift card test transaction receipts","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":30.205368275595273},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":300,"estHours":5,"travelExpense":50,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Hallow