{"job":{"id":"8206741688","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"IW for Fri 10/23 4-6PM EDT Hard Start or Soonest Available | Repair tkt 7090070","description":"<p>P1 Approved by Granite</p><p>NOC ticket #: 7090070 </p><p><br></p><p>Issue: Site's servers and computers are down. 60F is up however. customer</p><p>Objective: Please investigate the customer's iDrac Port on their server at the main podium and also very the cabling on ports 2 and 3 of the 60F</p><p><br></p><p>Note: If at any point the Granite NOC cannot be reached after 15 minutes of holding, please contact ValvolineRepair@granitenet.com with the ticket number in the subject, along with your name and call back number in the body of the email and contact will be arranged.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope Of Work:</p><p>1.Tech must check in with Granite Valvoline Support 833-363-8677 to clarify any issues on SOW, Granite NOC will stay on the line with the tech as this site is fully down.</p><p>2.Tech must start with locating Fortigate 60F. Very the link lights on ports 2 and 3 and trace the cables to ensure that they connect to the customer's server at the main podium.</p><p>3. At the podium please check the iDrac ports to ensure there are no cabling issues and then have site try to login to their server/computers. Granite Will reach out to Valvoline HD to ensure their site is online.</p><p>4.Tech must verify with Granite Valvoline Support 833-363-8677 that they see their site online.</p><p>5.Tech must check with manager on duty to make sure no further equipment needs attention, and will note the name of the manager that okayed the work.</p><p>6.Tech must call Granite Valvoline Support 833-363-8677 prior to departing the site.</p><p><br></p><p>Required Equipment: Tech will need bring a laptop and charger with Windows 7 or higher and admin rights to prove connectivity, Cisco Console Cable, Hot spot capability, Cable Certifier capable of displaying length, a patch cord, a splitter and a