{"job":{"id":20218691,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Envysion","title":"Replace and Seal (1) IP camera","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in replacing IP cameras.</li>\n<li>Tech is required to replace&nbsp;<strong>(</strong>Front door - Port 18<strong>)</strong>&nbsp;camera.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment.</li>\n<li>Clean any dirty cameras.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:&nbsp;</strong><em>must haves</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>8' - 15'</strong> Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension</li>\n<li>IP cable tester</li>\n<li>Toner</li>\n<li>Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera</li>\n<li>Crimping tool/ crimpers</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)</li>\n<li>Spot monitor</li>\n<li>Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus</li>\n<li>Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441 Option 8</li>\n<li>Check tracking if provided. If not then the replacement is on site already. If you go to the site and don't check the tracking then you will not receive the return bonus.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system</li>\n<li>Replace the camera(s). <strong>Equipment must be replaced even if the current equipment is working.</strong></li>\n<li>The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.</li>\n<li>Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image if the camera is not working&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras if the camera is not working.</li>\n<li>If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.</li>\n<li>During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.</li>\n<li>Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 #8</li>\n<li><strong>Leave any old equipment with the site.</strong></li>\n<li>If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours</li>\n<li>If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.</li>\n<li>Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Dress code and behavior policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li>Dress <strong>appropriately</strong> for work being done on site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p>Contact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441&nbsp;Opt. 8</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Expenses</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Additional hours</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.</li>\n<li>Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.<strong><u>All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.</u></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your patience is appreciated!</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please do not leave the site while on hold.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in replacing IP cameras.\n- Tech is required to replace **(**Front door - Port 18**)** camera.\n- Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment.\n- Clean any dirty cameras.\n\n**Tools Required:** *must haves*\n\n- **8' - 15'** Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension\n- IP cable tester\n- Toner\n- Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera\n- Crimping tool/ crimpers\n- RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)\n- Spot monitor\n- Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.\n2. If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus\n3. Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.\n4. Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps\n5. If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441 Option 8\n6. Check tracking if provided. If not then the replacement is on site already. If you go to the site and don't check the tracking then you will not receive the return bonus.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system\n2. Replace the camera(s). **Equipment must be replaced even if the current equipment is working.**\n3. The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.\n4. Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image if the camera is not working\n5. Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras if the camera is not working.\n6. If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.\n7. During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.\n8. If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.\n9. Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 #8\n10. **Leave any old equipment with the site.**\n11. If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours\n12. If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.\n2. Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.\n\n**Dress code and behavior policy**\n\n- **Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support**\n- **Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only**\n- **If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support**\n- Dress **appropriately** for work being done on site\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay\n\n- If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Expenses\n- Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.\n- Additional hours\n- This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.\n- Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.\n- If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.**All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.**\n- If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay\n\n**Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes**\n\n- Your patience is appreciated!\n- The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.\n- If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.\n- You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.\n- Please do not leave the site while on hold.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T09:00","end":"2026-10-26T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.303072618493616},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792783320858}
{"job":{"id":20235803,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Surveillance System - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Parts sent out : TRACKING NUMBER 879076492035</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech Jonathan Lazo for 10/26 9:00 AM or next available date</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: Get key from office and reset switch in locker and try and get cameras working again</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)</span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nSurveillance System - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.\n\n\\- Parts sent out : TRACKING NUMBER 879076492035\n\n\\- Requesting tech Jonathan Lazo for 10/26 9:00 AM or next available date\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Need to: Get key from office and reset switch in locker and try and get cameras working again\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T09:00","end":"2026-10-26T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":6.357201386143886},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00