{"job":{"id":20228680,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185 Unit#3431","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> Raleigh, 27612</p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p><p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p>Scope of Work – AP Relocation &amp; Wi-Fi Testing<p><br></p><p>The resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.</p><p><strong>1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.</li><li>Identify any potential coverage issues.</li></ul><p><strong>2. AP Relocation</strong></p><ul><li>Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.</li><li>Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.</li><li>Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.</li><li>Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.</li><li>Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Drywall Repair &amp; Painting</strong></p><ul><li>Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.</li><li>Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.</li><li>Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.</li><li>Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.</li><li>Clean the work area and remove all debris.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Final Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.</li><li>Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.</li><li>Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.</li><li>Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.</li><li>Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.</li></ul>Required Tools &amp; Materials<ul><li>Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed</li><li>Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools</li><li>Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools</li><li>Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods</li><li>Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies</li><li>Matching wall texture, primer, and paint</li><li>Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies</li><li>Ladder and standard installation tools</li></ul>Completion Requirements<ul><li>AP relocated according to the provided design.</li><li>All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.</li><li>Drywall patched, textured, and painted.</li><li>Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.</li><li>Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.</li></ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** Raleigh, 27612\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\nScope of Work – AP Relocation & Wi-Fi TestingThe resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.\n\n**1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.\n- Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.\n- Identify any potential coverage issues.\n\n**2. AP Relocation**\n\n- Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.\n- Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.\n- Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.\n- Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.\n- Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.\n\n**3. Drywall Repair & Painting**\n\n- Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.\n- Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.\n- Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.\n- Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.\n- Clean the work area and remove all debris.\n\n**4. Final Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.\n- Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.\n- Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.\n- Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.\n- Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.\n\nRequired Tools & Materials- Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed\n- Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools\n- Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools\n- Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods\n- Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies\n- Matching wall texture, primer, and paint\n- Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies\n- Ladder and standard installation tools\n\nCompletion Requirements- AP relocated according to the provided design.\n- All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.\n- Drywall patched, textured, and painted.\n- Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.\n- Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.\n- Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.\n- **Note:** Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3.6136968948458},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/19/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"Listen Audio Book"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"