{"job":{"id":20236397,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"Spectrum | Payment Kiosk | Printer Troubleshooting/Replacement/Testing","description":{"html":"<p><strong>This work order is to get our customer back up and running.</strong></p><p><strong>Only accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.</strong></p><p><strong>Must call Kiosk support to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p><p><strong>Support Number:</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(303) 926-3154</span>&nbsp;- Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician is responsible for returning defective parts. Do not leave any parts on site, WO will not be paid until defective parts are mailed back</strong></p><p><strong>NOTE: Call Kiosk and do not go to site if part has not delivered by your scheduled time.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>-Tools Required:</strong></p><p>__Standard Tool Set</p><p>__Nut Drivers or Socket Set</p><p>__Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</p><p>__A to B USB Cable</p><p>__VGA Cable</p><p>__Compressed air/Canned Air</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><p><strong>__Check in with the Work Order manager</strong></p><p>__PLEASE troubleshooting the existing printer <strong>PRIOR</strong> replacing to confirm there is a problem with the printer itself | <strong>Support Number:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(303) 926-3154</span></p><p>__Reference cleaning/PM guide. Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, etc.</p><p>__Check status light on printer</p><p>__Make sure paper is loaded properly</p><p>__Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip</p><p>__Check USB cable to Printer and to PC</p><p>__Call KIOSK Support to report your findings and we'll confirm to you if we need to replace it (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)</p><p>__if all checks out but we're still unable to get the printer working we can then replace the printer</p><p>__Disconnect printer power and USB cable</p><p>__Unscrew mounting screws from bottom of printer. Remove P clip for cables.</p><p>__Mount new printer using same hardware. Reattached P clip for cables.</p><p><strong>__Install bezel kit - Bezel is used to stick slightly out of the door to guide receipts to customer.<u> if there is no bezel on the printer tell KIS Agent. </u></strong></p><p><strong>__&nbsp;<u>REFERENCE PAGE 4- Step 4 &amp; Step 5 FOR ALIGNMENT/ADJUSTMENT</u></strong></p><p>__Paper holder to printer arm using the waster and hardware provided in the accessory kit</p><p>__Install the new assembled printer to Kiosk</p><p>__Reconnect new printer power and USB</p><p>__Load paper</p><p>__Test with Customer</p><p>__Take note of OLD serial and NEW serial.</p><p>__Call your Work Order manager to check out</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.</strong></p><p><strong>Support Number:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(303) 926-3154</span>&nbsp;- Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST</p><p><strong>346 S Arthur Ave.</strong></p><p><strong>Louisville, CO 80027</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(303) 926-3154</strong></p>","markdown":"**This work order is to get our customer back up and running.**\n\n**Only accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.**\n\n**Must call Kiosk support to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**Support Number:** (303) 926-3154 - Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST\n\n**The technician is responsible for returning defective parts. Do not leave any parts on site, WO will not be paid until defective parts are mailed back**\n\n**NOTE: Call Kiosk and do not go to site if part has not delivered by your scheduled time.**\n\n**-Tools Required:**\n\n\\_\\_Standard Tool Set\n\n\\_\\_Nut Drivers or Socket Set\n\n\\_\\_Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth\n\n\\_\\_A to B USB Cable\n\n\\_\\_VGA Cable\n\n\\_\\_Compressed air/Canned Air\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n**\\_\\_Check in with the Work Order manager**\n\n\\_\\_PLEASE troubleshooting the existing printer **PRIOR** replacing to confirm there is a problem with the printer itself | **Support Number:** (303) 926-3154\n\n\\_\\_Reference cleaning/PM guide. Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, etc.\n\n\\_\\_Check status light on printer\n\n\\_\\_Make sure paper is loaded properly\n\n\\_\\_Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip\n\n\\_\\_Check USB cable to Printer and to PC\n\n\\_\\_Call KIOSK Support to report your findings and we'll confirm to you if we need to replace it (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)\n\n\\_\\_if all checks out but we're still unable to get the printer working we can then replace the printer\n\n\\_\\_Disconnect printer power and USB cable\n\n\\_\\_Unscrew mounting screws from bottom of printer. Remove P clip for cables.\n\n\\_\\_Mount new printer using same hardware. Reattached P clip for cables.\n\n**\\_\\_Install bezel kit - Bezel is used to stick slightly out of the door to guide receipts to customer. if there is no bezel on the printer tell KIS Agent.**\n\n**\\_\\_ REFERENCE PAGE 4- Step 4 & Step 5 FOR ALIGNMENT/ADJUSTMENT**\n\n\\_\\_Paper holder to printer arm using the waster and hardware provided in the accessory kit\n\n\\_\\_Install the new assembled printer to Kiosk\n\n\\_\\_Reconnect new printer power and USB\n\n\\_\\_Load paper\n\n\\_\\_Test with Customer\n\n\\_\\_Take note of OLD serial and NEW serial.\n\n\\_\\_Call your Work Order manager to check out\n\n**Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.**\n\n**Support Number:** (303) 926-3154 - Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST\n\n**346 S Arthur Ave.**\n\n**Louisville, CO 80027**\n\n**(303) 926-3154**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T15:00","end":"2026-10-23T16:15","latestStart":"2026-10-23T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.25,"distance":16.27773116382141},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/23/2026, 3:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792787713576}
{"job":{"id":20236419,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"On-Demand","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Aptos,sans-serif;\"><strong>Weblink Survey: https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00741634</strong></span></span></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><b> </b></p><p><strong>Note from Client:</strong></p><p> </p><ul><li>Tech to perform troubleshooting and/or replacement of Network device (s) listed.</li><li>Complete online Installation webform: <del>***********************************************</del></li><li>Need to arrive onsite 15 minutes prior but no later than the pre-arranged start time as stated in the schedule.</li><li>Tech to state when they are enroute to site and check in on the platform when they arrive inside the store</li><li>Call the NOC <del>**************</del> to notify of your arrival and locate POC “ETL Lead”</li><li>If Parts or Lift were requested, work with POC “ETL Leader” to locate the equipment and mention ETL office. Parts will have an Orange Sticker, check in AREA TCS.</li><li>Tech to work with NOC during entirety of visit.</li><li>Attach pictures as required and update your closeout notes. This must be completed before you check out.</li><li>Return lift to pick-up location</li><li>Package devices for return and take them with you.</li><li>Check out with NOC, then the work order and notify work order manager from Pivital.</li><li>Drop off return shipments at UPS within 24 hours of the site visit using the label provided and include a receipt on your work order.</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements</u></strong></p><p> </p><ul><li>Review and have available the associated Knowledge Article attached for the equipment you will be supporting.</li><li>Cisco Console Cable (DB9 or USB)</li><li>15 ft. UTP Cat6 RJ-45 Network Cable</li><li>15 ft. Cat6 RJ-45 Ethernet Crossover Cable</li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc.)</li><li>10 Foot <strong>RED</strong> Ethernet patch cable</li></ul><p>·      25 Foot <strong>BLUE</strong> Ethernet patch cable</p><p>·      50 Foot <strong>BLUE</strong> Ethernet patch cable</p><ul><li>Standard Networking Tool Kit </li><li>Ethernet Cable Tester</li><li>Toner and Probe set</li><li>Loopback Connectors</li><li>RJ-48C T1</li><li>RJ-48S 4W 56K</li><li>RJ-45 Ethernet</li><li>Waterproof silicone caulking (White) for cooler/freezers and outside AP’s</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger and wireless headset</li><li>Laptop – With Charger</li><li>4G LTE Hotspot or Equivalent</li><li>Laptop with TeamViewer, with the ability to connect to the equipment and internet.</li><li>5/32 Allen Wrench</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Power Cord – 3 conductor PC power connector (not required)</li><li>Punch Down tools (110 blades)</li><li>1GB to 4GB USB Thumb Drive</li><li>Label Maker - cable wrap labels (No Flags)</li><li>Always label both ends of cable</li><li>Label ports</li><li>AP’s 3 lines ability to read from the floor</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Ladder 6-8 ft.</li></ul><p>Note the customer will not have the tools onsite. You must carry them with you and be prepared and knowledgeable to perform the service. Providers’ failure to have the necessary resources, tools, and other items needed to provide the Service and perform its obligations will not be paid.</p><p> </p><ul><li><strong><u>Site Security Requirements: </u></strong>Photo ID required.</li><li>No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment</li><li>Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.</li><li>Printable ID attached to the work order</li><li>Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>Represent yourself as <del>*******</del> (Do NOT mention Field Nation)</li></ul><p> </p>","markdown":"**Weblink Survey: <https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00741634>**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Note from Client:**\n\n- Tech to perform troubleshooting and/or replacement of Network device (s) listed.\n- Complete online Installation webform: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Need to arrive onsite 15 minutes prior but no later than the pre-arranged start time as stated in the schedule.\n- Tech to state when they are enroute to site and check in on the platform when they arrive inside the store\n- Call the NOC \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to notify of your arrival and locate POC “ETL Lead”\n- If Parts or Lift were requested, work with POC “ETL Leader” to locate the equipment and mention ETL office. Parts will have an Orange Sticker, check in AREA TCS.\n- Tech to work with NOC during entirety of visit.\n- Attach pictures as required and update your closeout notes. This must be completed before you check out.\n- Return lift to pick-up location\n- Package devices for return and take them with you.\n- Check out with NOC, then the work order and notify work order manager from Pivital.\n- Drop off return shipments at UPS within 24 hours of the site visit using the label provided and include a receipt on your work order.\n\n**Tool Requirements**\n\n- Review and have available the associated Knowledge Article attached for the equipment you will be supporting.\n- Cisco Console Cable (DB9 or USB)\n- 15 ft. UTP Cat6 RJ-45 Network Cable\n- 15 ft. Cat6 RJ-45 Ethernet Crossover Cable\n- Spare Patch Cables & Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc.)\n- 10 Foot **RED** Ethernet patch cable\n\n· 25 Foot **BLUE** Ethernet patch cable\n\n· 50 Foot **BLUE** Ethernet patch cable\n\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit\n- Ethernet Cable Tester\n- Toner and Probe set\n- Loopback Connectors\n- RJ-48C T1\n- RJ-48S 4W 56K\n- RJ-45 Ethernet\n- Waterproof silicone caulking (White) for cooler/freezers and outside AP’s\n- Cell Phone - with Charger and wireless headset\n- Laptop – With Charger\n- 4G LTE Hotspot or Equivalent\n- Laptop with TeamViewer, with the ability to connect to the equipment and internet.\n- 5/32 Allen Wrench\n- Crimper\n- Power Cord – 3 conductor PC power connector (not required)\n- Punch Down tools (110 blades)\n- 1GB to 4GB USB Thumb Drive\n- Label Maker - cable wrap labels (No Flags)\n- Always label both ends of cable\n- Label ports\n- AP’s 3 lines ability to read from the floor\n- Velcro\n- Ladder 6-8 ft.\n\nNote the customer will not have the tools onsite. You must carry them with you and be prepared and knowledgeable to perform the service. Providers’ failure to have the necessary resources, tools, and other items needed to provide the Service and perform its obligations will not be paid.\n\n- **Site Security Requirements:** Photo ID required.\n- No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment\n- Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.\n- Printable ID attached to the work order\n- Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- Represent yourself as \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (Do NOT mention Field Nation)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T16:29","end":"2026-10-26T20:29"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":36.03089195939707},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T