{"job":{"id":20237135,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TPX Communications","title":"Dispatch to replace SIlverpeak router. Need remote access","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Dispatch o replace SIlverpeak firewall. Need remote access</li></ul><p>SOW: </p><p>- Verify WAN connection is up with customer. Swing over 4G from WAN1 into GigEth 0/0/2 of customer Cisco switch, the same one LAN0 has an active connection to on the Silverpeak, if it has not already been done.</p><p>- Begin swapout of SP once confirmed customer is still up and running. Swap device with exact connections as observed upon arrival. (WAN0 should be the wired circuit from a patch panel or ISP modem, WAN1 should be the cradlepoint, LAN0 should be the connection to customer-owned Cisco switch at GigEth 0/0/1.)</p><p>- Once swapped, plug laptop into SP at MGMT1, not MGMT0. (Or LAN0 if no mgmt interface available)</p><p>- Setup AnyDesk to allow remote tech to configure new SP and allow for basic connectivity for RMA to complete properly. </p><p>- Confirm services up on site once complete.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************************************************</p><p><em>\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"</em></p><p><em>\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"</em></p><p><em>Please make sure to mark </em><strong><em>'On My Way</em></strong><em>' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”</em></p><p><em>Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.</em></p><p><em>Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.</em></p><p><em>**If you are calling to </em><strong><em><u>check in</u></em></strong><em><u> </u>for a scheduled work order, please </em><strong><em>press 3</em></strong><em> to leave a message.</em></p><p><em>**If </em><strong><em>after 5pm PST </em></strong><em>for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please </em><strong><em>press 1</em></strong><em> to reach the On-Call team.</em></p><p><em>****************************************************************************************************</em></p><p><strong><u>EXPECTATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with <del>*** </del>Support before entering premises</li><li>Call into&nbsp;<del>*********</del>Repair to troubleshoot and resolve issues on site.</li><li>Timely Arrival and Check-in 15mins before schedule time</li><li>Clean jeans and clean polo with no logos</li><li>Always act in a professional manner, as a representative of <del>*** **************</del></li><li>Follow Instructions on site as directed by <del>*** </del>Support</li><li>Follow Instructions given over the phone by&nbsp;<del>*********</del>Repair Support</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li><li>Windows&nbsp;7 or 10&nbsp;Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li><li>Active Email Address</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)</li><li>AnyDesk</li><li>Aeroadmin</li><li>HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li><li>FTP Client</li><li>TFTP Server software</li><li>MircoSIP (SIP call testing-&nbsp;https://www.microsip.org/)</li><li>Wireshark</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING</strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet Patch Cable</li><li>Cisco Console Cable​</li><li>USB to DB9 male serial Cable</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><ul><li>Buttset</li><li>Line man’s test set or analog test set</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool</li><li>Snips</li><li>Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Drill/ Dry wall screws</li><li>4’ ladder</li><li>CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)</li><li>Pre-made crossover cables</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors</li><li>Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)</li></ul><p><br></p><u>PRE-SITE WORK</u><ul><li>Acknowledge you have read and understand the Scope Of Work and its requirements</li><li>Print a copy of this scope of work and bring it to site</li><li>Call <del>*** </del>Support with any question or clarification about the Scope of Work</li></ul><p><br></p><u>ON SITE WORK</u><ul><li>Check In on the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Introduce yourself as representative of <del>*** **************</del></li><li>Call <del>*** </del>Support&nbsp;to check in @ <del>************ ******</del> entering premises</li><li>Check in with the on-site contact and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Must call into&nbsp;<del>*********</del>Repair Support to the number provided in the on-site process.</li><li>Call into <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*********</del></span>Repair a<del>* **** *** *****</del></li><li>Troubleshoot and resolve the repair issues on site.</li><li>Upload pictures of equipment powered up</li><li>Upload pictures of cable connections on devices&nbsp;</li><li>Upload a picture of speed test results from Laptop</li><li>Clean-up work materials from install (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)</li><li>Call <del>*** </del> Support to check out @ <del>************* </del>If after 5pm PST, press <strong>option 3</strong> leave a message.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>POST-SITE WORK</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm deliverables are complete</li><li>Enter Close out notes into Order</li><li>Enter <del>*** </del>Release Code (Given by the <del>*** </del>Support at the time of close out)</li><li>Check out in Field Nation Portal provide full detailed notes on what was done on site.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site @ <del>************</del></li><li>DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform out of the scope work, call <del>***</del> Support.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY</u></strong></p><ul><li>Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved, the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- Dispatch o replace SIlverpeak firewall. Need remote access\n\nSOW:\n\n\\- Verify WAN connection is up with customer. Swing over 4G from WAN1 into GigEth 0/0/2 of customer Cisco switch, the same one LAN0 has an active connection to on the Silverpeak, if it has not already been done.\n\n\\- Begin swapout of SP once confirmed customer is still up and running. Swap device with exact connections as observed upon arrival. (WAN0 should be the wired circuit from a patch panel or ISP modem, WAN1 should be the cradlepoint, LAN0 should be the connection to customer-owned Cisco switch at GigEth 0/0/1.)\n\n\\- Once swapped, plug laptop into SP at MGMT1, not MGMT0. (Or LAN0 if no mgmt interface available)\n\n\\- Setup AnyDesk to allow remote tech to configure new SP and allow for basic connectivity for RMA to complete properly.\n\n\\- Confirm services up on site once complete.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"*\n\n*\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"*\n\n*Please make sure to mark* ***'On My Way****' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”*\n\n*Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.*\n\n*Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.*\n\n*\\*\\*If you are calling to* ***check in*** *for a scheduled work order, please* ***press 3*** *to leave a message.*\n\n*\\*\\*If* ***after 5pm PST*** *for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please* 