{"job":{"id":20237686,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - Test and Replace Cabling","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Store manager requested visit for Anytime during working hours.</p><p><br></p><p>Issue - Register 51 &amp; 55 Catalina printer.</p><p><br></p><p>[Service Request:]</p><p>NEED TECH ONSITE TO TONE AND TEST/REPLACE CABLE FROM CATALINA SWITCH TO CATALINA PRINTER\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Store manager requested visit for Anytime during working hours.\n\nIssue - Register 51 & 55 Catalina printer.\n\n\\[Service Request:\\]\n\nNEED TECH ONSITE TO TONE AND TEST/REPLACE CABLE FROM CATALINA SWITCH TO CATALINA PRINTER\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T07:00","end":"2026-10-27T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":64.13459028222664},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1792804474487}
{"job":{"id":20237705,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CrossCom","title":"Walmart - Digital Lock 2026","description":{"html":"<p>Technician is required onsite to complete the following:&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Arrive at site, check in with the Crosscom Project Team @&nbsp;800-820-9229 then check in with store manager and present letter of authorization.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>2. Locate device to be installed, Usually held in AP office, Claims, or UPC office. Box 12x12x6 box and has a large white label saying: “Ecosystem Kit IR4 and Replace Plus side neon Yellow label”</strong></p><p><strong>NOTE: When calling into support, please have the following information available.</strong></p><ul><li>Switch name</li><li>Port number </li><li>MAC address</li><li>IP address</li><li>Physical location of the device if not in the AP office</li></ul><p>3. Identify if there is an existing cable in the AP office that can be used to connect the new device.</p><p>4.If an existing cable is available, the technician shall test and terminate the cable with a mod plug and connect to the new device.</p><p><strong>5. If no cable is available, the technician will run a new cable&nbsp;to the closest switch (approx. 100'). If a lift is required, Request to use store and move forward, if do not receive permission for daytime lift in area required, a return trip will be scheduled to complete the cable run after hours..</strong></p><p>6. Connect the cable to the provided device. Device to be placed on a desk or cabinet as agreed with AP office resources.</p><p>a. Run Set up on device using WM Install code 90124. before calling Verify screen displays Link: UP below connecting screen.</p><p>7. Work with CrossCom's L2 to provision port &amp; register MAC for the new device using VLAN 46.</p><p>8. Obtain manager's sign off.</p><p>9. Clean up and capture deliverables.</p><p>10. Check out with deployment support.</p><p><strong>****tech will need to provide the name of the switch ( for ex GM-1) port used , FULL MAC ADDRESS OF THE DEVICE</strong></p><p>*******Please be aware that per incident PENALTIES will apply as follows. Any penalties incurred will be deducted from technician payment.&nbsp;Technician agrees to these terms when accepting contract.*******</p><p>&nbsp;No Call/No Shows $150</p><p>&nbsp;Missing Sign Off $50 (after 2 days) $100 (after 8 days)</p><p>&nbsp;Leaving during the install $100</p><p>&nbsp;Failing to have CrossCom Badge. $50&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>* Trips: 1 technician will be required for 1 trip and the work will take place during normal business hours.</p><p>* Tools needed: Smartphone, standard hand tools, cable tester</p><p>* The technician will log in and out with CrossCom Project Team @ 800-820-9229..</p><p>* Deliverables will be required to validate work completion and quality. All deliverables must upload through vendor portal prior to leaving work site. Failure to provide deliverables will result in nonpayment.</p>","markdown":"Technician is required onsite to complete the following:\n\n**1. Arrive at site, check in with the Crosscom Project Team @ 800-820-9229 then check in with store manager and present letter of authorization.**\n\n**2. Locate device to be installed, Usually held in AP office, Claims, or UPC office. Box 12x12x6 box and has a large white label saying: “Ecosystem Kit IR4 and Replace Plus side neon Yellow label”**\n\n**NOTE: When calling into support, please have the following information available.**\n\n- Switch name\n- Port number\n- MAC address\n- IP address\n- Physical location of the device if not in the AP office\n\n3\\. Identify if there is an existing cable in the AP office that can be used to connect the new device.\n\n4.If an existing cable is available, the technician shall test and terminate the cable with a mod plug and connect to the new device.\n\n**5. If no cable is available, the technician will run a new cable to the closest switch (approx. 100'). If a lift is required, Request to use store and move forward, if do not receive permission for daytime lift in area required, a return trip will be scheduled to complete the cable run after hours..**\n\n6\\. Connect the cable to the provided device. Device to be placed on a desk or cabinet as agreed with AP office resources.\n\na. Run Set up on device using WM Install code 90124. before calling Verify screen displays Link: UP below connecting screen.\n\n7\\. Work with CrossCom's L2 to provision port & register MAC for the new device using VLAN 46.\n\n8\\. Obtain manager's sign off.\n\n9\\. Clean up and capture deliverables.\n\n10\\. Check out with deployment support.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*tech will need to provide the name of the switch ( for ex GM-1) port used , FULL MAC ADDRESS OF THE DEVICE**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Please be aware that per incident PENALTIES will apply as follows. Any penalties incurred will be deducted from technician payment. Technician agrees to these terms when accepting contract.\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n No Call/No Shows $150\n\n Missing Sign Off $50 (after 2 days) $100 (after 8 days)\n\n Leaving during the install $100\n\n Failing to have CrossCom Badge. $50\n\n\\* Trips: 1 technician will be required for 1 trip and the work will take place during normal business hours.\n\n\\* Tools needed: Smartphone, standard hand tools, cable tester\n\n\\* The technician will log in and out with CrossCom Project Team @ 800-820-9229..\n\n\\* Deliverables will be required to validate work completion and quality. All deliverables must upload through vendor portal prior to leaving work site. Failure to provide deliverables will result in nonpayment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T08:00","end":"2026-10-27T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":49.3116602233229},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"B