{"job":{"id":20238004,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"ATM Replacement Survey ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Check in with ServicePoint once onsite</li><li>Check in with the bank and proceed to start survey</li><li>Locate the correct ATM - Terminal in Special Instructions</li><li>Complete the ATM survey form by using Fast Field Form from client</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tooling List:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with ability to take photos and Hot Spot functionality</li><li>4 Foot Level</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Measuring Tape</li><li>Fast Field Forms Downloaded</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to two hours onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Code of Conduct:</strong></p><p>Always maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.</p><p>All conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.</p><p>Personal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.</p><p>Any deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Drug Policy/Dress Code;</strong></p><p>Do not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts and out of scope work MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Check in with ServicePoint once onsite\n- Check in with the bank and proceed to start survey\n- Locate the correct ATM - Terminal in Special Instructions\n- Complete the ATM survey form by using Fast Field Form from client\n\n**Tooling List:**\n\n- Smart Phone with ability to take photos and Hot Spot functionality\n- 4 Foot Level\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Measuring Tape\n- Fast Field Forms Downloaded\n\n***Flat rate covers up to two hours onsite.***\n\n**Code of Conduct:**\n\nAlways maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.\n\nAll conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.\n\nPersonal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.\n\nAny deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.\n\n**Drug Policy/Dress Code;**\n\nDo not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n**Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.**\n\n**Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.**\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.***\n\n***All site aborts and out of scope work MUST be approved by ServicePoint.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.524949687996194},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start