{"job":{"id":"7207550308","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"BLUEPRINT RF","title":"To Troubleshoot &amp; Recover Down Network","description":"<p>Service Description&nbsp;</p><p>Scope of Work – BluePrint Server Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dispatch Requirements&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must call Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 before entering the site to obtain any special instructions, upon arrival, and prior to departure&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must send an email to dispatch@blueprintrf.com after the pre-site call confirming contact was made and noting any applicable instructions&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must follow all instructions provided by NOC/Tier 3 throughout the dispatch&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must arrive neatly dressed and professional&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must have all required tools, equipment, and materials necessary to complete the work order&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Required Equipment&nbsp;</p><p>Laptop with wired and wireless capability&nbsp;</p><p>Personal hotspot for temporary wireless connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>AeroAdmin/AnyDesk, LogMeIn, and TeamViewer installed and ready for remote access&nbsp;</p><p>Appropriate cabling and troubleshooting tools&nbsp;</p><p>Labeler&nbsp;</p><p>Console cable compatible with the installed Aruba, HP, or Cisco switch&nbsp;</p><p>Monitor with VGA cable/cord for direct connection to the BluePrint server&nbsp;</p><p>Keyboard to connect directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before-Work Documentation&nbsp;</p><p>Before beginning any SOW activities, Tech must take clear photos of the site, equipment, and work area&nbsp;</p><p>Photos must be uploaded to Field Nation before work begins&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>BluePrint Server Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must troubleshoot and attempt to recover the down BluePrint server&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify that the BluePrint server has power and check all power connections&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must connect the monitor and keyboard directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must document any error messages, indicator lights, or other relevant findings&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify the server's network connections and physical cabling&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must check the server's link/activity lights&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify the core switch port connected to the BluePrint server and confirm link status&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify connectivity between the BluePrint server, core switch, and ISP equipment&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must transfer or reconnect cables as directed by NOC if required to restore connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must troubleshoot any physical connectivity issues identified, including faulty or disconnected cables, switch ports, power connections, or related equipment&nbsp;</p><p>If the BluePrint server cannot be recovered, Tech must document the server's status, error messages, indicator lights, and relevant findings and report them to NOC&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Network / ISP Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must work with NOC to troubleshoot the BluePrint server and guest network connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must allow remote access to the laptop as needed&nbsp;</p><p>If there is no internet connection, NOC will coordinate with the ISP&nbsp;</p><p>If internet connectivity is confirmed, Tech must test the cable run&nbsp;</p><p>If the cable run is confirmed faulty, Tech must replace the cable run as directed by NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must transfer or reconnect cables as instructed by NOC when required&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must not make network configuration changes without direction from NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Any required cabling work will be reimbursed provided the cost is reasonable and necessary to complete the requested work&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Testing and Verification&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must test the BluePrint server's network connectivity after troubleshooting and confirm whether it is reachable&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must test the guest Wi-Fi after the server is recovered&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must confirm that the BluePrint server, core switch connection, ISP connection, and guest network/Wi-Fi are operational before leaving the site&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After-Work Documentation&nbsp;</p><p>Upon completion of the SOW, Tech must take clear photos documenting the completed work, equipment, and work area&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must upload all after-work photos to WM/FN&nbsp;</p><p>Photos should include the BluePrint server, server power connections, server network connections, core switch and connected port, ISP equipment/connection, work area, and any identified issues&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Final Site Confirmation&nbsp;</p><p>Before leaving the property, Tech must:&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the final status of the BluePrint server with NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the core switch connection is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the ISP connection is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the guest network/Wi-Fi is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Provide NOC with a complete summary of all troubleshooting performed&nbsp;</p><p>Complete and upload all required after-work photos to Field Nation&nbsp;</p><p>Call Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 prior to departure&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>BlueprintRF NOC / Tier 3 Contact: 949-418-1336&nbsp;</p><p>Dispatch Email: dispatch@blueprintrf.com&nbsp;</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-26T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"