{"job":{"id":20239591,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Blueprint RF","title":"To Troubleshoot & Recover Down Network","description":{"html":"<p>Service Description&nbsp;</p><p>Scope of Work – BluePrint Server Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dispatch Requirements&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must call Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 before entering the site to obtain any special instructions, upon arrival, and prior to departure&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must send an email to dispatch@blueprintrf.com after the pre-site call confirming contact was made and noting any applicable instructions&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must follow all instructions provided by NOC/Tier 3 throughout the dispatch&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must arrive neatly dressed and professional&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must have all required tools, equipment, and materials necessary to complete the work order&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Required Equipment&nbsp;</p><p>Laptop with wired and wireless capability&nbsp;</p><p>Personal hotspot for temporary wireless connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>AeroAdmin/AnyDesk, LogMeIn, and TeamViewer installed and ready for remote access&nbsp;</p><p>Appropriate cabling and troubleshooting tools&nbsp;</p><p>Labeler&nbsp;</p><p>Console cable compatible with the installed Aruba, HP, or Cisco switch&nbsp;</p><p>Monitor with VGA cable/cord for direct connection to the BluePrint server&nbsp;</p><p>Keyboard to connect directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before-Work Documentation&nbsp;</p><p>Before beginning any SOW activities, Tech must take clear photos of the site, equipment, and work area&nbsp;</p><p>Photos must be uploaded to Field Nation before work begins&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>BluePrint Server Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must troubleshoot and attempt to recover the down BluePrint server&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify that the BluePrint server has power and check all power connections&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must connect the monitor and keyboard directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must document any error messages, indicator lights, or other relevant findings&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify the server's network connections and physical cabling&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must check the server's link/activity lights&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify the core switch port connected to the BluePrint server and confirm link status&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must verify connectivity between the BluePrint server, core switch, and ISP equipment&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must transfer or reconnect cables as directed by NOC if required to restore connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must troubleshoot any physical connectivity issues identified, including faulty or disconnected cables, switch ports, power connections, or related equipment&nbsp;</p><p>If the BluePrint server cannot be recovered, Tech must document the server's status, error messages, indicator lights, and relevant findings and report them to NOC&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Network / ISP Troubleshooting&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must work with NOC to troubleshoot the BluePrint server and guest network connectivity&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must allow remote access to the laptop as needed&nbsp;</p><p>If there is no internet connection, NOC will coordinate with the ISP&nbsp;</p><p>If internet connectivity is confirmed, Tech must test the cable run&nbsp;</p><p>If the cable run is confirmed faulty, Tech must replace the cable run as directed by NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must transfer or reconnect cables as instructed by NOC when required&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must not make network configuration changes without direction from NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Any required cabling work will be reimbursed provided the cost is reasonable and necessary to complete the requested work&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Testing and Verification&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must test the BluePrint server's network connectivity after troubleshooting and confirm whether it is reachable&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must test the guest Wi-Fi after the server is recovered&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must confirm that the BluePrint server, core switch connection, ISP connection, and guest network/Wi-Fi are operational before leaving the site&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After-Work Documentation&nbsp;</p><p>Upon completion of the SOW, Tech must take clear photos documenting the completed work, equipment, and work area&nbsp;</p><p>Tech must upload all after-work photos to WM/FN&nbsp;</p><p>Photos should include the BluePrint server, server power connections, server network connections, core switch and connected port, ISP equipment/connection, work area, and any identified issues&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Final Site Confirmation&nbsp;</p><p>Before leaving the property, Tech must:&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the final status of the BluePrint server with NOC&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the core switch connection is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the ISP connection is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Confirm the guest network/Wi-Fi is operational&nbsp;</p><p>Provide NOC with a complete summary of all troubleshooting performed&nbsp;</p><p>Complete and upload all required after-work photos to Field Nation&nbsp;</p><p>Call Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 prior to departure&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>BlueprintRF NOC / Tier 3 Contact: 949-418-1336&nbsp;</p><p>Dispatch Email: dispatch@blueprintrf.com&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Service Description\n\nScope of Work – BluePrint Server Troubleshooting\n\nDispatch Requirements\n\nTech must call Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 before entering the site to obtain any special instructions, upon arrival, and prior to departure\n\nTech must send an email to dispatch@blueprintrf.com after the pre-site call confirming contact was made and noting any applicable instructions\n\nTech must follow all instructions provided by NOC/Tier 3 throughout the dispatch\n\nTech must arrive neatly dressed and professional\n\nTech must have all required tools, equipment, and materials necessary to complete the work order\n\nRequired Equipment\n\nLaptop with wired and wireless capability\n\nPersonal hotspot for temporary wireless connectivity\n\nAeroAdmin/AnyDesk, LogMeIn, and TeamViewer installed and ready for remote access\n\nAppropriate cabling and troubleshooting tools\n\nLabeler\n\nConsole cable compatible with the installed Aruba, HP, or Cisco switch\n\nMonitor with VGA cable/cord for direct connection to the BluePrint server\n\nKeyboard to connect directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting\n\nBefore-Work Documentation\n\nBefore beginning any SOW activities, Tech must take clear photos of the site, equipment, and work area\n\nPhotos must be uploaded to Field Nation before work begins\n\nBluePrint Server Troubleshooting\n\nTech must troubleshoot and attempt to recover the down BluePrint server\n\nTech must verify that the BluePrint server has power and check all power connections\n\nTech must connect the monitor and keyboard directly to the BluePrint server for local troubleshooting\n\nTech must document any error messages, indicator lights, or other relevant findings\n\nTech must verify the server's network connections and physical cabling\n\nTech must check the server's link/activity lights\n\nTech must verify the core switch port connected to the BluePrint server and confirm link status\n\nTech must verify connectivity between the BluePrint server, core switch, and ISP equipment\n\nTech must transfer or reconnect cables as directed by NOC if required to restore connectivity\n\nTech must troubleshoot any physical connectivity issues identified, including faulty or disconnected cables, switch ports, power connections, or related equipment\n\nIf the BluePrint server cannot be recovered, Tech must document the server's status, error messages, indicator lights, and relevant findings and report them to NOC\n\nNetwork / ISP Troubleshooting\n\nTech must work with NOC to troubleshoot the BluePrint server and guest network connectivity\n\nTech must allow remote access to the laptop as needed\n\nIf there is no internet connection, NOC will coordinate with the ISP\n\nIf internet connectivity is confirmed, Tech must test the cable run\n\nIf the cable run is confirmed faulty, Tech must replace the cable run as directed by NOC\n\nTech must transfer or reconnect cables as instructed by NOC when required\n\nTech must not make network configuration changes without direction from NOC\n\nAny required cabling work will be reimbursed provided the cost is reasonable and necessary to complete the requested work\n\nTesting and Verification\n\nTech must test the BluePrint server's network connectivity after troubleshooting and confirm whether it is reachable\n\nTech must test the guest Wi-Fi after the server is recovered\n\nTech must confirm that the BluePrint server, core switch connection, ISP connection, and guest network/Wi-Fi are operational before leaving the site\n\nAfter-Work Documentation\n\nUpon completion of the SOW, Tech must take clear photos documenting the completed work, equipment, and work area\n\nTech must upload all after-work photos to WM/FN\n\nPhotos should include the BluePrint server, server power connections, server network connections, core switch and connected port, ISP equipment/connection, work area, and any identified issues\n\nFinal Site Confirmation\n\nBefore leaving the property, Tech must:\n\nConfirm the final status of the BluePrint server with NOC\n\nConfirm the core switch connection is operational\n\nConfirm the ISP connection is operational\n\nConfirm the guest network/Wi-Fi is operational\n\nProvide NOC with a complete summary of all troubleshooting performed\n\nComplete and upload all required after-work photos to Field Nation\n\nCall Tier 3/BlueprintRF NOC at 949-418-1336 prior to departure\n\nBlueprintRF NOC / Tier 3 Contact: 949-418-1336\n\nDispatch Email: dispatch@blueprintrf.com","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T08:00","end":"2026-10-26T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2.7023813281524953},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Family"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05899945 Toyota TBMNC EPIK Install Revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14: