{"job":{"id":20239069,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"ITAD - Inventory IT Assets - Capture Serials - Asset Tags - Device Types - Stage for Pickup","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope:</strong> Inventory 94 devices by scanning and recording each item's serial number and asset tag. Your goal is to confirm that every asset matches the client-provided list. Once you've completed the verification, our pick-up crew will arrive to collect the equipment.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must be background-checked and drug-screened within the last 24 months</li>\n<li>Technicians must have the required tools and equipment listed below and update their profiles to include all necessary items.</li>\n<li>Technicians must check in and check out from the site using GPS</li>\n<li>Technicians must communicate clearly by using the platform</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Tools and Equipment:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with Microsoft Office 365 (Excel) running on Windows 11.</li>\n<li>1D/2D barcode scanner (no scanner apps).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>On-site Safety:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Adhere to general data center safety cautions when working with computer equipment.</li>\n<li>Please do not, under any circumstances, disconnect or connect any hardwired connections of the rack's PDUs, UPS modules, tape libraries, or other computer equipment.</li>\n<li>Disconnect equipment with caution, only from pluggable AC receptacles.</li>\n<li>Refer to the Policies and Procedures for more info.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No graphic tops</li>\n<li>Clean and unripped jeans or khakis</li>\n<li>Clean shoes (no open-toed shoes or sandals)</li>\n<li>A polo or button-down shirt is preferred</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Expenses and Budgets:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>We will reimburse you for parking with a receipt.</li>\n<li>Please send all other costs for approval.</li>\n<li>Send all overtime hours for approval before completing the work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Detailed Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the downloaded spreadsheet.</li>\n<li>Click on the Start button (located in the upper left corner of the Inventory worksheet) -- <em>Only scan on the Inventory worksheet.</em></li>\n<li>Scan the S/N and asset tag into the appropriate fields, select the correct device type, and press Enter.</li>\n<li>If the device's identifiers match the list, proceed to the next asset.</li>\n<li>If the scanned devices don't match the list, set them aside, check your scan for accuracy, and resolve any discrepancies with your site contact after you finish scanning all devices.</li>\n<li>Our pickup team will be on-site to start packing the devices (please show them around).</li>\n<li>Stage all devices for pickup or hand them in when the pickup team arrives.</li>\n<li>Clean your work area.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Escalations On-site:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call or message the Work Order Manager with any questions or concerns.</li>\n<li>Call or message the Work Order Manager if you were asked to perform other services or if the SOW differs from what's on the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Scope:** Inventory 94 devices by scanning and recording each item's serial number and asset tag. Your goal is to confirm that every asset matches the client-provided list. Once you've completed the verification, our pick-up crew will arrive to collect the equipment.\n\n**Work Order Requirements:**\n\n- Technicians must be background-checked and drug-screened within the last 24 months\n- Technicians must have the required tools and equipment listed below and update their profiles to include all necessary items.\n- Technicians must check in and check out from the site using GPS\n- Technicians must communicate clearly by using the platform\n\n**Required Tools and Equipment:**\n\n- Laptop with Microsoft Office 365 (Excel) running on Windows 11.\n- 1D/2D barcode scanner (no scanner apps).\n\n**On-site Safety:**\n\n- Adhere to general data center safety cautions when working with computer equipment.\n- Please do not, under any circumstances, disconnect or connect any hardwired connections of the rack's PDUs, UPS modules, tape libraries, or other computer equipment.\n- Disconnect equipment with caution, only from pluggable AC receptacles.\n- Refer to the Policies and Procedures for more info.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- No graphic tops\n- Clean and unripped jeans or khakis\n- Clean shoes (no open-toed shoes or sandals)\n- A polo or button-down shirt is preferred\n\n**Expenses and Budgets:**\n\n- We will reimburse you for parking with a receipt.\n- Please send all other costs for approval.\n- Send all overtime hours for approval before completing the work.\n\n**Detailed Scope of Work:**\n\n1. Open the downloaded spreadsheet.\n2. Click on the Start button (located in the upper left corner of the Inventory worksheet) -- *Only scan on the Inventory worksheet.*\n3. Scan the S/N and asset tag into the appropriate fields, select the correct device type, and press Enter.\n4. If the device's identifiers match the list, proceed to the next asset.\n5. If the scanned devices don't match the list, set them aside, check your scan for accuracy, and resolve any discrepancies with your site contact after you finish scanning all devices.\n6. Our pickup team will be on-site to start packing the devices (please show them around).\n7. Stage all devices for pickup or hand them in when the pickup team arrives.\n8. Clean your work area.\n\n**Escalations On-site:**\n\n- Call or message the Work Order Manager with any questions or concerns.\n- Call or message the Work Order Manager if you were asked to perform other services or if the SOW differs from what's on the work order.","acti