{"job":{"id":20241012,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot MDF Switch , Cary, NC, TASK6316259","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of Work:</p><p>TASK6316259</p><p><strong>Site address:</strong> 5055 Arco St, Cary, NC 27519, USA</p><p><strong>Scheduled : </strong> 26 October, 12:00 PM</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>REMOTE ENGINEER CONTACT INFO:</p><p><br></p><p>Name: Steven Piadade</p><p>Direct Phone: 832-319-4138</p><p>Email: dpiadast@amazon.com</p><p>Pager Email: page-dpiadast@amazon.com</p><p><br></p><p>REQUESTED REPAIR DATE/TIME: ASAP - Sev-2 store-impacting (SCOs, registers, refrigeration controllers, phones offline)</p><p><br></p><p>Reference: SIM V2427575453 / INC16916966</p><p><br></p><p>FIS SMART HANDS DISPATCH - Hardware recovery (physical intervention)</p><p><br></p><p>Site: SOALT / West Cary</p><p><br></p><p>Site phone: (984) 228-0300</p><p>Affected hardware: soalt-mdf4 (Celestica access switch, S/N EC2045000627), MDF</p><p>Symptom: soalt-mdf4 unreachable (no ping, no LLDP from distribution), read-only filesystem alarm. soalt-mdf2 is online and forwarding and is NOT part of this dispatch.</p><p>Remote diagnostics already attempted: Hylas monitoring (ping/LLDP/filesystem checks). OOB check from soalt-oob1: swp6 (alias soalt-mdf4, VLAN 2254) link is UP, but no LLDP neighbor and no learned MAC from soalt-mdf4 eth0 (only the oob1 port's own permanent MAC is present). soalt-mdf4 is powered with link up but sending no traffic in-band or out-of-band; with the read-only filesystem alarm, this points to a hung control plane. User callback confirms partial LAN outage (some endpoints down, not all).</p><p><br></p><p>Smart Hands technician scope:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Bring: RJ45 male to USB male console cable, laptop with terminal emulator, 30-40 Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables.</p><p>2. Locate soalt-mdf4 (S/N EC2045000627) in the MDF rack. Check PSU and status LEDs and report what you see to the remote engineer.</p><p>3. Power drain soalt-mdf4: from the back of the switch, partially pull PSU 1 and PSU 2 out of their slots until both are disconnected. Wait 60 seconds.</p><p>4. Fully reseat PSU 1 and PSU 2 and power the switch back up. Notify the remote engineer and stay onsite while recovery is confirmed.</p><p>5. If soalt-mdf4 does not come back: connect the console cable and report the boot output to the remote engineer.</p><p>6. If soalt-mdf4 cannot be recovered: on remote engineer's direction, move patch cables from soalt-mdf4 to specific free ports on soalt-mdf1 / soalt-mdf3, critical devices first (SCO, registers, refrigeration controllers, CS booth phone). The remote engineer will give an exact port-by-port list. Label every moved cable.</p><p>7. Clear visible dust from intake vents while onsite.</p><p><br></p><p>Smart Hands technician restrictions:</p><p><br></p><p>* Do not touch, unplug, or power-cycle soalt-mdf2. It is online and carrying traffic.</p><p>* Do not run configuration commands. Switch configuration is the remote engineer's task.</p><p>* Do not move any cable unless the remote engineer directs it in real time with a specific port list.</p><p>* Do not swap switch hardware unless the remote engineer directs it.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion / stop criteria:</p><p><br></p><p>* Complete when soalt-mdf4 responds to ping/console and the remote engineer confirms recovery, OR critical devices are moved to working ports and confirmed online.</p><p>* If PSU LEDs show a fault, or soalt-mdf4 does not boot after the power drain, STOP and report the exact LED/console state to the remote engineer.</p><p><br></p><p>Remote engineer responsibility:</p><p><br></p><p>* Verify switch recovery, run any config/playbook recovery, provide the port-move list and push the matching inventory change, and open a replacement request if a switch is confirmed failed. soalt-mdf2 will be addressed separately only after soalt-mdf4 is stable.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Needed:</strong></p><p>RJ45 male to USB male console cable</p><p>Laptop with terminal emulator</p><p>Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables (30-40)</p><p>Cable labels</p><p>Label maker</p><p>Flashlight</p><p>Screwdrivers</p><p>Compressed air or duster for vent cleaning</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Site Access:</strong></p><p>A valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Communication / Microsoft Teams:</strong></p><p>Technician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.</p><p>Field Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.</p><p>Technician must provide updates for:</p><ul><li>Arrival onsite</li><li>Work started</li><li>Progress, delays, or idle time</li><li>Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns</li><li>Completion status before leaving site</li><li>Checkout/departure from site</li></ul><p>Technician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.</p><p>Time, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:</p><p>Technician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.</p><p>Approved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.</p><p>Unsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p>Assigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:</p><p>The technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.</p><p>Documentation / Deliverables:</p><p>All required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.</p><p>Required deliverables may include:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved</li><li>Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable</li><li>Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions</li><li>Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status</li></ul><p>For cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.</p><p>Incomplete Work / Blockers:</p><p>If work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:</p><ul><li>What was completed</li><li>What could not be completed</li><li>Why it could not be completed</li><li>Troubleshooting performed</li><li>Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker</li><li>Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed</li></ul><p>Professional Standards / Confidentiality:</p><p>Technician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.</p><p>Provider Acknowledgment:</p><p>By applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.</p><p>Missing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Required Completion Items:</p><ul><li>Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.</li><li>Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.</li><li>Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.</li><li>Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.</li><li>Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.</li><li>If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.</li><li>Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.</li><li>Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.</li></ul>","markdown":"Scope of Work:\n\nTASK6316259\n\n**Site address:** 5055 Arco St, Cary, NC 27519, USA\n\n**Scheduled :**  26 October, 12:00 PM\n\nREMOTE ENGINEER CONTACT INFO:\n\nName: Steven Piadade\n\nDirect Phone: 832-319-4138\n\nEmail: dpiadast@amazon.com\n\nPager Email: page-dpiadast@amazon.com\n\nREQUESTED REPAIR DATE/TIME: ASAP - Sev-2 store-impacting (SCOs, registers, refrigeration controllers, phones offline)\n\nReference: SIM V2427575453 / INC16916966\n\nFIS SMART HANDS DISPATCH - Hardware recovery (physical intervention)\n\nSite: SOALT / West Cary\n\nSite phone: (984) 228-0300\n\nAffected hardware: soalt-mdf4 (Celestica access switch, S/N EC2045000627), MDF\n\nSymptom: soalt-mdf4 unreachable (no ping, no LLDP from distribution), read-only filesystem alarm. soalt-mdf2 is online and forwarding and is NOT part of this dispatch.\n\nRemote diagnostics already attempted: Hylas monitoring (ping/LLDP/filesystem checks). OOB check from soalt-oob1: swp6 (alias soalt-mdf4, VLAN 2254) link is UP, but no LLDP neighbor and no learned MAC from soalt-mdf4 eth0 (only the oob1 port's own permanent MAC is present). soalt-mdf4 is powered with link up but sending no traffic in-band or out-of-band; with the read-only filesystem alarm, this points to a hung control plane. User callback confirms partial LAN outage (some endpoints down, not all).\n\nSmart Hands technician scope:\n\n1\\. Bring: RJ45 male to USB male console cable, laptop with terminal emulator, 30-40 Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables.\n\n2\\. Locate soalt-mdf4 (S/N EC2045000627) in the MDF rack. Check PSU and status LEDs and report what you see to the remote engineer.\n\n3\\. Power drain soalt-mdf4: from the back of the switch, partially pull PSU 1 and PSU 2 out of their slots until both are disconnected. Wait 60 seconds.\n\n4\\. Fully reseat PSU 1 and PSU 2 and power the switch back up. Notify the remote engineer and stay onsite while recovery is confirmed.\n\n5\\. If soalt-mdf4 does not come back: connect the console cable and report the boot output to the remote engineer.\n\n6\\. If soalt-mdf4 cannot be recovered: on remote engineer's direction, move patch cables from soalt-mdf4 to specific free ports on soalt-mdf1 / soalt-mdf3, critical devices first (SCO, registers, refrigeration controllers, CS booth phone). The remote engineer will give an exact port-by-port list. Label every moved cable.\n\n7\\. Clear visible dust from intake vents while onsite.\n\nSmart Hands technician restrictions:\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Do not touch, unplug, or power-cycle soalt-mdf2. It is online and carrying traffic.\n\n\\* Do not run configuration commands. Switch configuration is the remote engineer's task.\n\n\\* Do not move any cable unless the remote engineer directs it in real time with a specific port list.\n\n\\* Do not swap switch hardware unless the remote engineer directs it.\n\nCompletion / stop criteria:\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Complete when soalt-mdf4 responds to ping/console and the remote engineer confirms recovery, OR critical devices are moved to working ports and confirmed online.\n\n\\* If PSU LEDs show a fault, or soalt-mdf4 does not boot after the power drain, STOP and report the exact LED/console state to the remote engineer.\n\nRemote engineer responsibility:\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\* Verify switch recovery, run any config/playbook recovery, provide the port-move list and push the matching inventory change, and open a replacement request if a switch is confirmed failed. soalt-mdf2 will be addressed separately only after soalt-mdf4 is stable.\n\n**Tools Needed:**\n\nRJ45 male to USB male console cable\n\nLaptop with terminal emulator\n\nCat5e/Cat6 patch cables (30-40)\n\nCable labels\n\nLabel maker\n\nFlashlight\n\nScrewdrivers\n\nCompressed air or duster for vent cleaning\n\n**Site Access:**\n\nA valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.\n\n**Communication / Microsoft Teams:**\n\nTechnician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.\n\nField Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.\n\nTechnician must provide updates for:\n\n- Arrival onsite\n- Work started\n- Progress, delays, or idle time\n- Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns\n- Completion status before leaving site\n- Checkout/departure from site\n\nTechnician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.\n\nTime, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:\n\nTechnician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.\n\nApproved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.\n\nUnsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAssigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:\n\nThe technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.\n\nDocumentation / Deliverables:\n\nAll required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.\n\nRequired deliverables may include:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved\n- Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable\n- Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions\n- Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status\n\nFor cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.\n\nIncomplete Work / Blockers:\n\nIf work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:\n\n- What was completed\n- What could not be completed\n- Why it could not be completed\n- Troubleshooting performed\n- Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker\n- Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed\n\nProfessional Standards / Confidentiality:\n\nTechnician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.\n\nProvider Acknowledgment:\n\nBy applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.\n\nMissing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAdditional Required Completion Items:\n\n- Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.\n- Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.\n- Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.\n- Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.\n- Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.\n- If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.\n- Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.\n- Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T12:00","end":"2026-10-26T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.49358780015713},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start"