{"job":{"id":20241989,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Far Out Solutions","title":"Network Setup & hardware installation - Ray @ The Weld","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Service Description:&nbsp;</strong>Network Setup &amp; hardware installation</p><p> </p><p> </p><p>Technician will be representing themselves as a<strong>&nbsp;<em>Far Out Solutions</em> Technician.</strong></p><p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual<strong> </strong>Please refrain when possible from branded uniforms/shirts, etc.&nbsp;You are there representing Far Out Solutions only. Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer.&nbsp;NO SHORTS or open shoes&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Laptop (Windows) with Ethernet port &amp; USB Type A, Ethernet Patch Cords (3ft, 6ft, 9ft, etc...) CAT5E, Ethernet tools (Crimper, Toner&amp;Tester, plugs/connectors), Basic handyman tools (Screwdriver, stud finder, pliers, etc..) &amp; basic power tools like a drill., Mobile device with hotspot connectivity enabled/active</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK:</strong></p><p>Arrive onsite and locate the AT&amp;T modem/router and the connected network firewall.</p><p><br></p><p>Connect a laptop directly to the AT&amp;T modem/router using an Ethernet cable.</p><p><br></p><p>Establish internet connectivity on the laptop, if available.</p><p><br></p><p>Coordinate with the remote technician and provide remote access to the laptop.</p><p><br></p><p>Assist the remote technician with accessing the AT&amp;T modem/router and configuring passthrough/bridge mode as directed.</p><p><br></p><p>Perform a modem/router power cycle if required and directed by the remote technician.</p><p><br></p><p>Verify connectivity after the configuration changes and confirm that the firewall receives a public IP address.</p><p><br></p><p>Report the results and any outstanding issues to the remote technician before leaving the site.</p><p><br></p><p> <strong>Attached <em>Far Out Solutions</em> Work order is required for payment. If required paper work is not completed, you will NOT get paid.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>***Do NOT discuss pricing, under ANY circumstance, with ANYONE except your direct contacts at FOS. If the customer is unsure about their pricing you are to refer them back to FOS so we can clarify.</strong>***&nbsp;</p><p><strong>The technician has&nbsp;</strong><u>24 Hrs. from the assignment END time to upload the Required Work Order</u>&nbsp;to the platform and any other pertinent paperwork required. Failure to comply will result in a<strong>&nbsp;reduction in pay.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>UPON SUCCESSFUL COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER, CUSTOMER SATISFACTION VERIFICATION, AND WORK ORDER IS IN A WORK DONE STATUS, WORK WILL BE APPROVED WITHIN SEVEN (7) BUSINESS DAYS FROM COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> UPON ACCEPTANCE OF THIS PROJECT, NO PAY INCREASE WILL BE ACCEPTED, UNLESS IT IS APPROVED BY PROJECT MANAGER BEFORE PROJECT IS COMPLETED. IF PROJECT MANAGER IS NOT IN THE OFFICE, SEND A MESSAGE THROUGH FIELD NATION THAT WILL BE REVIEWED WHEN PROJECT MANAGER RETURNS. ON PROJECTS WITH MAXIMUM TIME LIMITS, YOU NEED TO GET THE APPROVAL FROM THE TICKET MANAGER. ALL SITUATIONS WILL BE HANDLED ON A CASE BY CASE BASIS.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Parts Requirements:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Under no circumstances is the technician to leave the customer site with any hardware without obtaining <strong><em>Far Out Solutions</em></strong> approval.</p><p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>For services completed we pay a minimum of 1 hour and then in 15-minute increments thereafter based on the times shown on the Work Order signature page. Please note that we do not pay travel time unless it is agreed upon&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;being assigned for the work order.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>*** READ BELOW AS THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT REGARDING YOUR PAY!!!! ***</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Technician is to guarantee workmanship on all Far Out Solutions service events. If you fail to fully complete the services requested, provide quality work and/or satisfy the customer, or properly fill out the work order signature page, we reserve the right to deny payment in part or in full. If service is not billable to the customer due to the technicians’ error or customer handling, service will not be payable.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Tech must agree to warranty work performed, until the end of business 7 days following day of service. If there is a call&nbsp;back related to this service event, tech will go back to site at no charge with another work order.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>**Please allow 7 business days AFTER paperwork and resolution is uploaded for work order to be approved for invoicing status**</strong></p>","markdown":"**Service Description:** Network Setup & hardware installation\n\nTechnician will be representing themselves as a ***Far Out Solutions* Technician.**\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual Please refrain when possible from branded uniforms/shirts, etc. You are there representing Far Out Solutions only. Dress with the intention of being seen by the customer. NO SHORTS or open shoes\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\nLaptop (Windows) with Ethernet port & USB Type A, Ethernet Patch Cords (3ft, 6ft, 9ft, etc...) CAT5E, Ethernet tools (Crimper, Toner&Tester, plugs/connectors), Basic handyman tools (Screwdriver, stud finder, pliers, etc..) & basic power tools like a drill., Mobile device with hotspot connectivity enabled/active\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\nArrive onsite and locate the AT&T modem/router and the connected network firewall.\n\nConnect a laptop directly to the AT&T modem/router using an Ethernet cable.\n\nEstablish internet connectivity on the laptop, if available.\n\nCoordinate with the remote technician and provide remote access to the laptop.\n\nAssist the remote technician with accessing the AT&T modem/router and configuring passthrough/bridge mode as directed.\n\nPerform a modem/router power cycle if required and directed by the remote technician.\n\nVerify connectivity after the configuration changes and confirm that the firewall receives a public IP address.\n\nReport the results and any outstanding issues to the remote technician before leaving the site.\n\n **Attached *Far Out Solutions* Work order is required for payment. If required paper work is not completed, you will NOT get paid.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Do NOT discuss pricing, under ANY circumstance, with ANYONE except your direct contacts at FOS. If the customer is unsure about their pricing you are to refer them back to FOS so we can clarify.**\\*\\*\\*\n\n**The technician has** 24 Hrs. from the assignment END time to upload the Required Work Order to the platform and any other pertinent paperwork required. Failure to comply will result in a **reduction in pay.**\n\n**UPON SUCCESSFUL COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER, CUSTOMER SATISFACTION VERIFICATION, AND WORK ORDER IS IN A WORK DONE STATUS, WORK WILL BE APPROVED WITHIN SEVEN (7) BUSINESS DAYS FROM COMPLETION OF WORK ORDER.**\n\n **UPON ACCEPTANCE OF THIS PROJECT, NO PAY INCREASE WILL BE ACCEPTED, UNLESS IT IS APPROVED BY PROJECT MANAGER BEFORE PROJECT IS COMPLETED. IF PROJECT MANAGER IS NOT IN THE OFFICE, SEND A MESSAGE THROUGH FIELD NATION THAT WILL BE REVIEWED WHEN PROJECT MANAGER RETURNS. ON PROJECTS WITH MAXIMUM TIME LIMITS, YOU NEED TO GET THE APPROVAL FROM THE TICKET MANAGER. ALL SITUATIONS WILL BE HANDLED ON A CASE BY CASE BASIS.**\n\n**Parts Requirements:**\n\nUnder no circumstances is the technician to leave the customer site with any hardware without obtaining ***Far Out Solutions*** approval.\n\n**Compensation:**\n\nFor services completed we pay a minimum of 1 hour and then in 15-minute increments thereafter based on the times shown on the Work Order signature page. Please note that we do not pay travel time unless it is agreed upon **before** being assigned for the work order.\n\n***\\*\\*\\* READ BELOW AS THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT REGARDING YOUR PAY!!!! \\*\\*\\****\n\n***Technician is to guarantee workmanship on all Far Out Solutions service events. If you fail to fully complete the services requested, provide quality work and/or satisfy the customer, or properly fill out the work order signature page, we reserve the right to deny payment in part or in full. If service is not billable to the customer due to the technicians’ error or customer handling, service will not be payable.***\n\n***Tech must agree to warranty work performed, until the end of business 7 days following day of service. If there is a call back related to this service event, tech will go back to site at no charge with another work order.***\n\n**\\*\\*Please allow 7 business days AFTER paperwork and resolution is uploaded for work order to be approved for invoicing status\\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.408109627251937},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793027849241}
{"job":{"id":20242038,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS154480","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 801-347-9577 Ticket 11982562<br/><br/>***MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/>**PIAB Install**<br/><br/>Call  Becky Perry at  8013479577  when on site.     <br/><br/>Data Remote<br/>  CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit<br/><br/>    -Tech to locate equipment.<br/><br/>    -Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.<br/><br/>    -Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.<br/><br/>    -Attach antennas and power on.<br/><br/>    -MetTel will validate configurations.<br/><br/>    -Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net<br/><br/>    -Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11<br/>  ports.<br/><br/>    -Validate e911 address on one each line.<br/><br/>    -Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer<br/>  side of the demark.<br/><br/>    If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.<br/><br/>    -Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the<br/>  Fire Panel placed into test mode.<br/><br/>    -Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.<br/><br/>    -Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.<br/><br/>    -Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the<br/>  faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.<br/><br/>    -Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.<br/><br/>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/>This request is for Standar PIAB Installation. Below are site details need to be provided to the tech<br/><br/>Do you want your invoices emailed or sent as a hard copy in the mail? invoices emailed to ap@dan.org and em@dan.org if possible.<br/>Do the locations have any security restrictions our tech will need to comply with? No<br/>Where should the tech check in upon arrival? Dock door<br/>Please provide site contact that will provide access for the tech dispatches. Myself 919-360-2333<br/>Please confirm power is available where the MetTel equipment will be installed. Yes<br/>Please confirm if wall space for a 24x19 inch board is available. Yes<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 801-347-9577 Ticket 11982562  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n\\*\\*PIAB Install\\*\\*  \n  \nCall Becky Perry at 8013479577 when on site.   \n  \nData Remote  \n CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit  \n  \n -Tech to locate equipment.  \n  \n -Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.  \n  \n -Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.  \n  \n -Attach antennas and power on.  \n  \n -MetTel will validate configurations.  \n  \n -Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net  \n  \n -Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11  \n ports.  \n  \n -Validate e911 address on one each line.  \n  \n -Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer  \n side of the demark.  \n  \n If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.  \n  \n -Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the  \n Fire Panel placed into test mode.  \n  \n -Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.  \n  \n -Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.  \n  \n -Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the  \n faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.  \n  \n -Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.  \n  \nMetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \nThis request is for Standar PIAB Installation. Below are site details need to be provided to the tech  \n  \nDo you want your invoices emailed or sent as a hard copy in the mail? invoices emailed to ap@dan.org and em@dan.org if possible.  \nDo the locations have any security restrictions our tech will need to comply with? No  \nWhere should the tech check in upon arrival? Dock door  \nPlease provide site contact that will provide access for the tech dispatches. Myself 919-360-2333  \nPlease confirm power is available where the MetTel equipment will be installed. Yes  \nPlease confirm if wall space for a 24x19 inch board is available. Yes  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T10:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":13.846691021522874},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below