{"job":{"id":20216680,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Printer Installation (1 Technician)(HARD START) (MUST READ INSTRUCTION DOC)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">****MUST READ INSTRUCTION DOC*****</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;Tech’s are to unbox and assemble printer and accessories (sheet tray/printer stand)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Unpack/Install printer</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Power on</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Menu set-up (English language)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Print test page for printers</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Make a copy for multi-function</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">- Pull a dynamic IP address (to verify active data drop) - Printers are to remain in DHCP.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Techs are not responsible for putting printers on AT&amp;T Network; that is done internally.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Dispose of garbage</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Once the printer is setup and tested, tech will instruct site POC to contact ATT/Xerox support to remotely configure the printer and our job is complete.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">If the store you are working at is located in one of the following states. There is no need to verify active data drop via DHCP.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">(AL, LA, FL, MS, GA, NC, KY &amp; TN)</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Unpack/Install printer</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Power on</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Menu set-up (English language)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Print test page for printers</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Make a copy for multi-function</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">- Dispose of garbage</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">-Job Complete</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Tooling List:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Laptop w/ AC adapter</li><li>Smart Phone with ability to take photos and Hot Spot functionality</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>Cat6e patch cables for testing</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Cat6e cable tester</li><li>Toner and wand</li><li>RJ45 modular ends&nbsp;</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: black;\">Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment.&nbsp;All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: black;\">Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.&nbsp;If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate,subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;All site aborts MUST be approved by CTS.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*MUST READ INSTRUCTION DOC\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n Tech’s are to unbox and assemble printer and accessories (sheet tray/printer stand)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n\\- Unpack/Install printer\n\n\\- Power on\n\n\\- Menu set-up (English language)\n\n\\- Print test page for printers\n\n\\- Make a copy for multi-function\n\n**- Pull a dynamic IP address (to verify active data drop) - Printers are to remain in DHCP.**\n\n\\- Techs are not responsible for putting printers on AT&amp;T Network; that is done internally.\n\n\\- Dispose of garbage\n\nOnce the printer is setup and tested, tech will instruct site POC to contact ATT/Xerox support to remotely configure the printer and our job is complete.\n\n**If the store you are working at is located in one of the following states. There is no need to verify active data drop via DHCP.**\n\n**(AL, LA, FL, MS, GA, NC, KY &amp; TN)**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n\\- Unpack/Install printer\n\n\\- Power on\n\n\\- Menu set-up (English language)\n\n\\- Print test page for printers\n\n\\- Make a copy for multi-function\n\n\\- Dispose of garbage\n\n-Job Complete\n\n**Tooling List:**\n\n- Laptop w/ AC adapter\n- Smart Phone with ability to take photos and Hot Spot functionality\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- Cat6e patch cables for testing\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Cat6e cable tester\n- Toner and wand\n- RJ45 modular ends\n\n*Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.*\n\n*Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate,subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”. All site aborts MUST be approved by CTS.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T10:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":63.15050889176019},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.