 to dress business casual. This includes a collared shirt and khaki-style pants, etc. No Jeans, Shorts, T-shirts, Tennis Shoes, sandals, etc.</p>3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;What to Bring<p>Required:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Precision&nbsp;Screw Drive Set</li><li>Torx and Philips</li></ul><p>Recommended:</p><ul><li>Extra Thermal Paste</li><li>Alcohol Wipes</li><li>Splunger Set​</li></ul>4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer Service<p>Please be courteous, attentive and customer-service oriented while onsite.</p><p>Personal Cell phone use should be limited to project and emergency use only. Your branch contact can direct you to a branch land-line phone you may use to reach Insight and/or Tier II if needed.</p><p><strong><u>Only work on the machine listed on your Work Order/ Job. If requested to work on another machine, advise Insight before doing any additional work.</u></strong></p>6)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Working Onsite<p>Review Checklist within the Field Nation app in regards to special instructions and list of deliverables.</p><p>There may be documents attached to Field Nation to assist with onsite repairs.</p>7)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Assistance/ Troubleshooting/ Escalation<p>Insight OSR Escalation: <del>************ ***** ********</del></p><br><p><strong><em><u>IMPORTANT:</u></em></strong><em>&nbsp;All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation.&nbsp;Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.</em></p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING</u></strong></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li><li>IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</li><li>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</li></ul><p><em>You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.</em></p>","markdown":"**Review Entire Ticket Prior to requesting.****Unless otherwise stated, the part is required to be onsite prior to the repair.****Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work**\n\n- We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.\n- By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page: **<https://fieldnation.com/work/insight>**\n- Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details included in FAQ on program page.\n\nPlease see tracking before going to site or call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tracking:** Tracking 