ing shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿<em><u>Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.</u></em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>UNLESS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.</li><li>&nbsp;Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.</li><li>&nbsp;If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.</li><li>&nbsp;Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.</li><li>Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Includes&nbsp;-possible operating system installation ( re-image ) after part(s) replacement&nbsp;</p><p>-Taking parts with you offsite for either part disposition or to send them back to the hardware vendor. (except used HD's)</p><p><br></p>***CABLE RUNS ARE NOT IN SCOPE OF WORK IF ONE IS NEEDED PLEASE ESCALATE TO INSIGHT ***<p><br></p>Technician Expectations On-Site Repair<p>Follow these updated procedures to ensure accurate accounting of your time, prompt payment for your assignments, and efficient communication with the client. This document is the property of Insight and may not be copied or distributed without the express written consent of Insight.</p>1)&nbsp;&nbsp;Ticket Assignment<p>Please review the ticket assigned to you immediately. If you are uncomfortable performing the work, or are unable to meet the expectations, please notify your Insight immediately. Please <u>DO NOT</u> contact the End User prior to your arrival.</p>2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attire<p>While onsite, you are required to dress business casual. This includes a collared shirt and khaki-style pants, etc. No Jeans, Shorts, T-shirts, Tennis Shoes, sandals, etc.</p>3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;What to Bring<p>Required:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Precision&nbsp;Screw Drive Set</li><li>Torx and Philips</li></ul><p>Recommended:</p><ul><li>Extra Thermal Paste</li><li>Alcohol Wipes</li><li>Splunger Set​</li></ul>4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer Service<p>Please be courteous, attentive and customer-service oriented while onsite.</p><p>Personal Cell phone use should be limited to project and emergency use only. Your branch contact can direct you to a branch land-line phone you may use to reach Insight and/or Tier II if needed.</p><p><strong><u>Only work on the machine listed on your Work Order/ Job. If requested to work on another machine, advise Insight before doing any additional work.</u></strong></p>6)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Working Onsite<p>Review Checklist within the Field Nation app in regards to special instructions and list of deliverables.</p><p>There may be documents attached to Field Nation to assist with onsite repairs.</p>7)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Assistance/ Troubleshooting/ Escalation<p>Insight OSR Escalation: <del>************ ***** ********</del></p><br><p><strong><em><u>IMPORTANT:</u></em></strong><em>&nbsp;All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation.&nbsp;Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.</em></p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING</u></strong></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li><li>IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</li><li>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</li></ul><p><em>You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.</em></p>","markdown":"**Review Entire Ticket Prior to requesting.****Unless otherwise stated, the part is required to be onsite prior to the repair.****Opportunities for Badged techs on projects, MACD and B/F work**\n\n- We are seeking Badged techs to qualify for ongoing work at branch locations for a bank, one of Insight's largest clients. This badge is a mandatory requirement for techs to be eligible for this work.\n- By becoming a badged tech for this end-customer you'll gain access to a consistent stream of work routed by Insight. If you're not yet badged, you can start the process today through this program page: **<https://fieldnation.com/work/insight>**\n- Newly badged techs are eligible for a one-time bonus upon receiving your badge. Details included in FAQ on program page.\n\nPlease see tracking before going to site or call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tracking:** Tracking is added to the ticket the morning of the job if applicable. Look in the shipments section.  \n\\*\\***CHECK YOUR EMAIL THE MORNING OF REGARDING YOUR ASSIGNED WO \\*\\***  \n**Scope:** !!! BEFORE you mark yourself ONSITE It is essential that you   \ncall the Insight team - 1-800-215-8968   \nDo not leave the site UNTIL you call the Insight team.   \n   \nChase reference ticket: IMS2899192  \nChase Contact#: 877-309-8068 Opt 1   \n   \nUnit: 800 G9 - MXL6203ZD2  \nSCOPE:   \n\"Troubleshoot  \nrun dags, F2 at boot  \nif pass work with Chase to re-image\"   \n   \n   \nBranch contact: Jennifer Avila, N757752  \nDate requested: 10/27/2026  \n**PLEASE NOTE: Even if tracking shows part on site, do not show up earlier or later than the date assigned without prior approval. The branch has been made aware of the original date and Insight needs to confirm any changes with the client in advance if a request is being made.**\n\n**﻿*Please do not take any photos of Chase computer screens.***\n\n **UNLESS:**\n\n- it is photo the blue Bitlocker screen after the TPM is broken.\n- Photo of log in screen for VDI/Teller installs, monitor installs and monitor arm installs.\n- If photos of cable management are needed, please ensure computer screen is not in photo if powered on.\n- Other photos such as error messages, are only allowed to be taken if requested by Chase support or Insight support.\n- Any photos taken while on Chase premises, should be immediately deleted from phone once site is complete.\n\nIncludes -possible operating system installation ( re-image ) after part(s) replacement\n\n-Taking parts with you offsite for either part disposition or to send them back to the hardware vendor. (except used HD's)\n\n\\*\\*\\*CABLE RUNS ARE NOT IN SCOPE OF WORK IF ONE IS NEEDED PLEASE ESCALATE TO INSIGHT \\*\\*\\*Technician Expectations On-Site RepairFollow these updated procedures to ensure accurate accounting of your time, prompt payment for your assignments, and efficient communication with the client. This document is the property of Insight and may not be copied or distributed without the express written consent of Insight.\n\n1) Ticket AssignmentPlease review the ticket assigned to you immediately. If you are uncomfortable performing the work, or are unable to meet the expectations, please notify your Insight immediately. Please DO NOT contact the End User prior to your arrival.\n\n2) AttireWhile onsite, you are required to dress business casual. This includes a collared shirt and khaki-style pants, etc. No Jeans, Shorts, T-shirts, Tennis Shoes, sandals, etc.\n\n3) What to BringRequired:\n\n- Precision Screw Drive Set\n- Torx and Philips\n\nRecommended:\n\n- Extra Thermal Paste\n- Alcohol Wipes\n- Splunger Set​\n\n4) Customer ServicePlease be courteous, attentive and customer-service oriented while onsite.\n\nPersonal Cell phone use should be limited to project and emergency use only. Your branch contact can direct you to a branch land-line phone you may use to reach Insight and/or Tier II if needed.\n\n**Only work on the machine listed on your Work Order/ Job. If requested to work on another machine, advise Insight before doing any additional work.**\n\n6) Working OnsiteReview Checklist within the Field Nation app in regards to special instructions and list of deliverables.\n\nThere may be documents attached to Field Nation to assist with onsite repairs.\n\n7) Assistance/ Troubleshooting/ EscalationInsight OSR Escalation: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n  \n***IMPORTANT:*** *All expenses must be supported by receipts, please upload to Field Nation. Any expense submitted without a receipt WILL NOT be paid. Prior approval required for expenses other than tolls and parking.*\n\n**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nTerms for Travel:\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\nTerms for Additional Time being Required:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n- IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n- Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T11:00","end":"2026-10-27T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":160},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":80},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":13.131946152684296},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summ