{"job":{"id":20242784,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"PM7 install residential","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>DETAILED SOW-RESIDENTIAL</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Description:&nbsp;PM7 Equipment Installation</strong></p>\n<p>Type of Appointment: Installation</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>HH: 65420 Name: Marie Humphrey Phone Number:<del>**********</del> Email: <del>********************</del> Time Zone: EDT HH is requesting 11AM EDT</p>\n<p>Upon arrival, you are required to call 55Blue Support before beginning any work.</p>\n<p>This installation should not take longer than <strong>2 hours</strong>. If you anticipate exceeding the 2‑hour window, you must contact Support to explain the reason for the extended time before proceeding.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Once tech arrives home, please greet the member :&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Installation guides have been attached to help technician identify equipment. Every home normally has 1 FM device and 1 PM7 device per TV.</li>\n<li>&nbsp;Tech should call our Quality Control Agent will be helping remotely while on the phone. Any questions regarding rewards points/other issue that the member has, will be able to assist over the phone.</li>\n<li>The agent assigned to this HH:</li>\n<li>If agent is not available, please have them call<del>************</del>&nbsp;(our main line) and mention they are a field tech, ask to be transferred to a QC agent to complete a maintenance call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Any questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li>\n<li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work.&nbsp;&nbsp;We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Check In Steps</strong>&nbsp;(<u>please follow order</u>)</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check In via FE Portal</li>\n<li>Check In with Netfor at&nbsp;&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)</li>\n<li>Complete installation per SOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by&nbsp;Netfor.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who requested the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Check out Steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NOTE:&nbsp;<u>*** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER ***</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li>\n<li>Check out with Netfor at&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NOTE:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Failure to call Netfor to check in or out</strong>&nbsp;could result in 25% withdrawn from payment.&nbsp;<strong>Failure to arrive on time</strong>&nbsp;can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures</strong>&nbsp;within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.</li>\n<li><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p>\n<p>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)</li>\n<li>Basic IT Tools</li>\n<li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li>\n<li>Cat5e Cabling</li>\n<li>ladder</li>\n<li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li>\n<li>Copy of work order and job information</li>\n<li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long pants</li>\n<li>Collared shirt</li>\n<li>Netfor name badge</li>\n<li>Close toe shoes</li>\n<li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li>\n<li>Pictures of area before working</li>\n<li>Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed/troubleshot</li>\n<li>Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**DETAILED SOW-RESIDENTIAL**\n\n**Description: PM7 Equipment Installation**\n\nType of Appointment: Installation\n\nHH: 65420 Name: Marie Humphrey Phone Number:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Email: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Time Zone: EDT HH is requesting 11AM EDT\n\nUpon arrival, you are required to call 55Blue Support before beginning any work.\n\nThis installation should not take longer than **2 hours**. If you anticipate exceeding the 2‑hour window, you must contact Support to explain the reason for the extended time before proceeding.\n\n- Once tech arrives home, please greet the member :\n- Installation guides have been attached to help technician identify equipment. Every home normally has 1 FM device and 1 PM7 device per TV.\n- Tech should call our Quality Control Agent will be helping remotely while on the phone. Any questions regarding rewards points/other issue that the member has, will be able to assist over the phone.\n- The agent assigned to this HH:\n- If agent is not available, please have them call\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (our main line) and mention they are a field tech, ask to be transferred to a QC agent to complete a maintenance call.\n\nAny questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.\n\n**Check In Steps** (please follow order)\n\n1. Check In via FE Portal\n2. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)\n3. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who requested the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n\n**Check out Steps**\n\n1. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n\n- **NOTE: \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER \\*\\*\\***\n\n1. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n2. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n\n- **NOTE:** **Failure to call Netfor to check in or out** could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. **Failure to arrive on time** can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.\n- **NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures** within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.\n- **REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).**\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Cat5e Cabling\n- ladder\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- Pictures of area before working\n- Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed/troubleshot\n- Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T11:00","end":"2026-11-03T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":98},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":77.72429497570381},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC