\n<li>FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.</li>\n<li>***IMPORTANT** If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.</li>\n<li>**BEFORE LEAVING SITE*** Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"- **Zone 509 REAR EMERGENCY EXIT DOOR(sn01541035) bypassing. Tech to trouble shoot zones and restore to normal operation. Verify panel can be armed without bypassing before leaving site. If transmitter is damaged replace it.**\n- Parts onsite- 544823199232 delivered 10/23 14:14 Received by VVALESKA.\n- **\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION**\n- **﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.**\n- IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.\n- TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL \\*PROVIDER\\* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. \\*OR\\* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION & TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT. CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 \\*\\*Canada - 647-496-1288 (CA-ON), 506-300-3307 (CA-NB) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER - 367272300 \\*\\*WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. \\*\\*CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!\n- FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.\n- \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.\n- \\*\\*BEFORE LEAVING SITE\\*\\*\\* Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T10:00","end":"2026-10-30T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":16.23704838042804},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793032467579}
{"job":{"id":20241166,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Replace pin pad cables on Reg 4","description":{"html":"<p>Need Ross trained tech(s) for pin pad refresh project to replace pin pad cables on Reg 4.</p>\n<p>Tech will download vendor authorization letter, tech checkin-checkout document, and pin pad install guide and review before arrival.</p>\n<p>Tech should contact Shyft PM confirming your arrival, contact store MOD to locate 6 conversion kits, show vendor authorization letter and government issued ID (drivers license), &amp; call command center upon arrival.</p>\n<p>Working with MOD and Command Center representative, confirm POS lane and pin pad is fully functional before leaving site.</p>\n<p>Provide photos to Ross bridge as required.</p>\n<p>Phone #'s and conference ID# can be found in confidential information of your work order.</p>\n<p>At completion of work order tech must check out with Ross IT hotline and text Shyft PM before leaving site.</p>\n<p><strong>NOTE:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A photo submitted and found altered by AI will be rejected and need to be retaken at tech expense.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>DO NOT</strong> leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.</li>\n<li><strong>Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"Need Ross trained tech(s) for pin pad refresh project to replace pin pad cables on Reg 4.\n\nTech will download vendor authorization letter, tech checkin-checkout document, and pin pad install guide and review before arrival.\n\nTech should contact Shyft PM confirming your arrival, contact store MOD to locate 6 conversion kits, show vendor authorization letter and government issued ID (drivers license), & call command center upon arrival.\n\nWorking with MOD and Command Center representative, confirm POS lane and pin pad is fully functional before leaving site.\n\nProvide photos to Ross bridge as required.\n\nPhone #'s and conference ID# can be found in confidential information of your work order.\n\nAt completion of work order tech must check out with Ross IT hotline and text Shyft PM before leaving site.\n\n**NOTE:**\n\n- **A photo submitted and found altered by AI will be rejected and need to be retaken at tech expense.**\n- **DO NOT** leave messages in the work order as they may not be viewed in a timely manner. Especially if you are requesting something...instead, give us a call.\n- **Please do not request a schedule change. Schedule change requests cannot be accommodated. If you are not able to make it to the site as scheduled. Please Report a Problem within the work order and remove yourself.**\n- **Travel must be requested prior to assignment by counteroffer or by speaking with us., or it will be declined.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T09:00","end":"2026-11-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":90},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":52.84659529370911},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793032960230}
{"job":{"id":20243314,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Getcoins","title":"Relocate Bitcoin ATM inside the store","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong>Unbolt the Bitcoin ATM and relocate inside the store. (The store employee will show you where to put the machine.)</strong></li><li><strong>Make sure to keep a few inches away from the regular ATM so the vault door on the regular ATM can be fully opened.</strong></li><li><strong>Re-bolt the machine to the gourd once the machine has been relocated.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>BOLTING DOWN ATM </strong></p><p><strong>Tools/Equipment Needed </strong></p><p><strong>● Drill</strong></p><p><strong> ● Heavy-duty Concrete Hammer Drill</strong></p><p><strong> ● </strong>1⁄2” (13mm) Diameter Carbide-Tipped Masonry Drill Bit ● Four (4) 1⁄2” Wedge Anchor Bolts</p><p><strong>● </strong>Four (4) 1⁄2” Nuts</p><p><strong>● </strong>Four (4) 1⁄2” Flat Washers</p><p><strong>● </strong>Hammer</p><p><strong>● </strong>3/4” Wrench</p><p><strong>Safety Tip: </strong>Since drilling can be quite loud, it is recommended that earplugs be worn.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Refer to WORKORDER_PHOTO_GUIDE.PDF for photos required in this workorder. </u></strong></p>","markdown":"- **Unbolt the Bitcoin ATM and relocate inside the store. (The store employee will show you where to put the machine.)**\n- **Make sure to keep a few inches away from the regular ATM so the vault door on the regular ATM can be fully opened.**\n- **Re-bolt the machine to the gourd once the machine has been relocated.**\n\n**BOLTING DOWN ATM**\n\n**Tools/Equipment Needed**\n\n**● Drill**\n\n **● Heavy-duty Concrete Hammer Drill**\n\n **●** 1⁄2” (13mm) Diameter Carbide-Tipped Masonry Drill Bit ● Four (4) 1⁄2” Wedge Anchor Bolts\n\n**●** Four (4) 1⁄2” Nuts\n\n**●** Four (4) 1⁄2” Flat Washers\n\n**●** Hammer\n\n**●** 3/4” Wrench\n\n**Safety Tip:** Since drilling can be quite loud, it is recommended that earplugs be worn.\n\n**Refer to WORKORDER\\_PHOTO\\_GUIDE.PDF for photos required in this workorder.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T09:00","end":"2026-10-28T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-28T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":2.085193742437977},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793033144985}
{"job":{"id":20243509,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Required (Filling the Service Visit Report is Mandatory)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>FILLING THE SITE VISIT REPORT IS MANDATORY BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE AND MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE CLOSING THE WO</em></strong></p><p><strong>**The technician should NOT suggest purchasing any new equipment or materials while onsite, and should not discuss any issues that need to be fixed with the Store Manager. The technician must strictly follow the instructions provided during the Teams meeting.**</strong></p><p><br></p><p>The technician must join the meeting as soon as they arrive onsite. (The meeting details will be shared before arrival.) If there is any issue joining the meeting, or if no one is present in the meeting, please call the Wipro phone number provided in the confidential information. Select option 1 and provide the INC number or the location (as mentioned in the Work Order description). or call your WO manager from ovation.</p><p>POC details are available in the confidential information.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> <span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Need to install (Velo510, DIGI, GS, Switch, AP and Wattbox) Equipment's on to the cabinet.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Special Note :</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> </span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Remember to inform the technician to bring SIX Ethernet CAT6 cables (at least 3 meters in length) as well as a butt set at each site to test the voice service.</strong></p><p><strong><em>(Any additional tools or cable purchased onsite should be approved by the Field nation work order manager. If you are getting no response please send an email on sd@ovationwps.com)</em></strong></p><p><strong>Required Tools &amp; Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop with Windows operating system and Ethernet port(s)</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">6 Ethernet CAT6 cables(at least 3 meters in length)</span><span style=\"color: inherit;\">&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Butt set to test out the in/out voice service</span></li><li>Console cables (RJ45 to USB, USB to Serial converter)</li><li>Basic tool kit</li><li>USB drive (32GB)</li><li>Internet data (hotspot)</li><li>PuTTY application</li><li>MS Teams (installed on both phone and laptop)</li><li>Phone with a reliable hotspot</li><li>Patch cables (copper or fiber)</li></ul>","markdown":"***FILLING THE SITE VISIT REPORT IS MANDATORY BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE AND MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE CLOSING THE WO***\n\n**\\*\\*The technician should NOT suggest purchasing any new equipment or materials while onsite, and should not discuss any issues that need to be fixed with the Store Manager. The technician must strictly follow the instructions provided during the Teams meeting.\\*\\***\n\nThe technician must join the meeting as soon as they arrive onsite. (The meeting details will be shared before arrival.) If there is any issue joining the meeting, or if no one is present in the meeting, please call the Wipro phone number provided in the confidential information. Select option 1 and provide the INC number or the location (as mentioned in the Work Order description). or call your WO manager from ovation.\n\nPOC details are available in the confidential information.\n\n**Scope of Work:**  **Need to install (Velo510, DIGI, GS, Switch, AP and Wattbox) Equipment's on to the cabinet.**\n\n**Special Note :** **Remember to inform the technician to bring SIX Ethernet CAT6 cables (at least 3 meters in length) as well as a butt set at each site to test the voice service.**\n\n***(Any additional tools or cable purchased onsite should be approved by the Field nation work order manager. If you are getting no response please send an email on sd@ovationwps.com)***\n\n**Required Tools & Equipment:**\n\n- Laptop with Windows operating system and Ethernet port(s)\n- 6 Ethernet CAT6 cables(at least 3 meters in length)\n- Butt set to test out the in/out voice service\n- Console cables (RJ45 to USB, USB to Serial converter)\n- Basic tool kit\n- USB drive (32GB)\n- Internet data (hotspot)\n- PuTTY application\n- MS Teams (installed on both phone and laptop)\n- Phone with a reliable hotspot\n- Patch cables (copper or fiber)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":10.24062333661632},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793034318222}
{"job":{"id":20243384,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Splice Communications","title":"1518 - Raleigh, NC | Phase 2.1 - Pre-Install Validation & Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>﻿PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A CALIBER COLLISION TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Mandatory Scope Discussion</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have <strong>not previously completed work for this specific project phase</strong> must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.</p>\n<p>If contacted, please plan to attend. <strong>Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Assessment Consideration Notice:</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have completed the required assessment will be prioritized for consideration. Providers who have not completed the assessment may not be eligible for assignment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>To perform during initial visit (4 items)</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Survey the site against the attached Predictive Survey Map</li>\n<li>Survey the site and identify the optimal<strong>outdoor</strong> location for the MG52 cellular backup antenna installation. Antenna orientation requirements will be provided prior to the visit.</li>\n<li>MDF cleanup</li>\n<li>Install any leftover Phase 1 workstations</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>NOT perform during initial visit</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No AP, MX, or MG installs. No new cable runs. Survey these only.</li>\n<li>No network config (IP addressing, firewall rules, SSID).</li>\n<li>No cable termination.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Before You Arrive to the site</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;Site Survey Form downloaded to your device (attached)</li>\n<li>&nbsp;Predictive Survey Map saved/printed</li>\n<li>&nbsp;Tape measure or measuring wheel</li>\n<li>&nbsp;Graybar.com pulled up on phone/tablet for part lookups</li>\n<li>&nbsp;PPE (vest, hard hat) + photo ID for site check-in</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>1.1 Site Survey — Document Only, Don't Install</strong></p>\n<p>Walk the site with the attached Predictive Survey Map and perform any additional survey tasks listed in this Scope of Work. For each applicable item, record:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Measured quantity (cable footage, conduit, hardware count)</li>\n<li>Exact part number from Graybar.com (<strong><u>make/model/SKU — no generic descriptions, that gets the survey rejected</u></strong>)</li>\n<li>Estimated labor hours to install</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check for (only if marked on your map):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Conduit &amp; cable run path</li>\n<li>AP install/relocation</li>\n<li>MX security appliance swap</li>\n<li>Timeclock install</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>1.2 Additional Survey Requirement (Not Shown on the Map)</strong></p>\n<p>Survey the site and identify the optimal outdoor location for the MG52 cellular backup antenna installation. Antenna orientation requirements will be provided prior to the visit.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Document the proposed mounting location, cable path to the MDF, mounting surface type, and any obstacles that may impact installation.</li>\n<li>Identify any required materials, mounting hardware, conduit, penetrations, or cable runs needed to complete the installation.</li>\n<li>Provide estimated labor hours required for the antenna installation.</li>\n<li>Take clear photos of the proposed antenna location, cable path, and any potential installation constraints.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. MDF Cleanup — Do This Today</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Organize/dress existing cabling</li>\n<li>Pull abandoned patch cords and debris</li>\n<li>Route and secure active cables with velcro — <strong>no zip ties on active data cables</strong></li>\n<li>Label anything unlabeled</li>\n<li>Photos: before and after of the rack(s)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3. Pending Workstations — Do This Today (if applicable)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install any workstations left over from Phase 1</li>\n<li>Connect monitor, peripherals, network + power</li>\n<li>Confirm it powers on and works</li>\n<li>Photos: before and after of each workstation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deliverables (Required for Payment)</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Survey Form</strong> — fully filled out: quantities, part numbers, labor hours</li>\n<li><strong>Photos</strong> — MDF before/after, each workstation before/after, proposed AP/cable path locations, proposed MG52 antenna location and cable path, and any obstacles or discrepancies.</li>\n<li><strong>Discrepancy Report</strong> — short summary of map vs. actual site conditions</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Upload all three to the Work Order to close it out.</p>\n<p>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing the location if there are any questions regarding a deliverable or required task. All deliverables must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. Failure to do so may result in payment delays or financial penalties.</p>","markdown":"**﻿PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A CALIBER COLLISION TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**Mandatory Scope Discussion**\n\nTechnicians who have **not previously completed work for this specific project phase** must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.\n\nIf contacted, please plan to attend. **Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.**\n\n**Assessment Consideration Notice:**\n\nTechnicians who have completed the required assessment will be prioritized for consideration. Providers who have not completed the assessment may not be eligible for assignment.\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:**\n\n**To perform during initial visit (4 items)**\n\n1. Survey the site against the attached Predictive Survey Map\n2. Survey the site and identify the optimal**outdoor** location for the MG52 cellular backup antenna installation. Antenna orientation requirements will be provided prior to the visit.\n3. MDF cleanup\n4. Install any leftover Phase 1 workstations\n\n**NOT perform during initial visit**\n\n- No AP, MX, or MG installs. No new cable runs. Survey these only.\n- No network config (IP addressing, firewall rules, SSID).\n- No cable termination.\n\n**Before You Arrive to the site**\n\n- Site Survey Form downloaded to your device (attached)\n- Predictive Survey Map saved/printed\n- Tape measure or measuring wheel\n- Graybar.com pulled up on phone/tablet for part lookups\n- PPE (vest, hard hat) + photo ID for site check-in\n\n**1.1 Site Survey — Document Only, Don't Install**\n\nWalk the site with the attached Predictive Survey Map and perform any additional survey tasks listed in this Scope of Work. For each applicable item, record:\n\n- Measured quantity (cable footage, conduit, hardware count)\n- Exact part number from Graybar.com (**make/model/SKU — no generic descriptions, that gets the survey rejected**)\n- Estimated labor hours to install\n\nCheck for (only if marked on your map):\n\n- Conduit & cable run path\n- AP install/relocation\n- MX security appliance swap\n- Timeclock install\n\n**1.2 Additional Survey Requirement (Not Shown on the Map)**\n\nSurvey the site and identify the optimal outdoor location for the MG52 cellular backup antenna installation. Antenna orientation requirements will be provided prior to the visit.\n\n- Document the proposed mounting location, cable path to the MDF, mounting surface type, and any obstacles that may impact installation.\n- Identify any required materials, mounting hardware, conduit, penetrations, or cable runs needed to complete the installation.\n- Provide estimated labor hours required for the antenna installation.\n- Take clear photos of the proposed antenna location, cable path, and any potential installation constraints.\n\n**2. MDF Cleanup — Do This Today**\n\n- Organize/dress existing cabling\n- Pull abandoned patch cords and debris\n- Route and secure active cables with velcro — **no zip ties on active data cables**\n- Label anything unlabeled\n- Photos: before and after of the rack(s)\n\n**3. Pending Workstations — Do This Today (if applicable)**\n\n- Install any workstations left over from Phase 1\n- Connect monitor, peripherals, network + power\n- Confirm it powers on and works\n- Photos: before and after of each workstation\n\n**Deliverables (Required for Payment)**\n\n1. **Survey Form** — fully filled out: quantities, part numbers, labor hours\n2. **Photos** — MDF before/after, each workstation before/after, proposed AP/cable path locations, proposed MG52 antenna location and cable path, and any obstacles or discrepancies.\n3. **Discrepancy Report** — short summary of map vs. actual site conditions\n\nUpload all three to the Work Order to close it out.\n\nAs stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing the location if there are any questions regarding a deliverable or required task. All deliverables must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. Failure to do so may result in payment delays or financial penalties.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.620702801999888},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T