{"job":{"id":20243793,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Herman Tech Crew, LLC","title":"A/V Install - Durham, NC - 11/13 - LEAD","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU&nbsp;<u>READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.</u></strong></p><p>Please Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.</p><p><strong><u>PLEASE REVIEW</u></strong> - Any travel cost incurred would need to be reviewed by the provider and made up front when acceptance of the work order - Parking, materials, etc. are <strong><u>paid/ approved with receipts- only - provide some other documentation of the payment. Or it is up to WO manger discretion. </u></strong></p><p>Please review the <strong><u>HERMAN GUIDELINES portion below</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Attached</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope (1 room):</strong> Samsung 55\" QB55C display on a Chief swing arm mount above the huddle-style table, with a Wattbox surge protector. Logitech Rally Bar Mini under the display and a Tap IP controller on the wall for native Teams controls. HDMI/USB-C BYOD input at the table through the table box into the Rally Bar Mini (wall passthrough if there is no table box). CEC auto-power based on Rally Bar sleep status, Rally Bar remote for advanced camera controls, and 3 years of Logitech Essentials service.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Open items:</strong> Cable pathways through the table, and ceiling height/room dimensions are not specified.</p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Key terms:</strong> Cenero supplies and installs the AV equipment, while the client and others handle electrical, data cabling, millwork, and conduit. Client IT support is required.</li><li>Help unload equipment, stage and unbox equipment</li><li>Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go</li></ul><p><strong><u>BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE</u></strong></p><ol><li>Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete&nbsp;a Field Report for <u>EACH</u> <u>DAY</u> worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><u>ON-SITE TASKS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check into your Work Order</li><li>Call the&nbsp;<em>LOCATION CONTACT</em>&nbsp;at the phone number provided on this work order&nbsp;upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site</li><li>Obtain completed and signed field report</li><li>With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done</li><li>Obtain Signature</li><li>Check out of Work Order</li></ol><p><strong>Any expenses&nbsp;<u>MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU</u>&nbsp;on the work order and&nbsp;<u>MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT</u>.​</strong></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><u>Failure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site</u>.&nbsp;Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression.&nbsp;If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.</p><p><strong><em>Mounting Tools:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits</li><li>Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)</li><li>Stud Finder</li><li>Bubble level</li><li>Hammer</li><li>Drywall saw</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Box knife</li><li>Socket set (SAE/metric)</li></ul><p><strong><em>Cabling Tools:</em></strong></p><ul><li>RJ45 crimper for Category cable (5-6)</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Punch down tool</li></ul><p><strong><em>PPE</em></strong></p><ul><li><u>You are required to have basic PPE</u> (<em>Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves</em>) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>DO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS</u></strong>. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the <u>Project Manager</u> listed on this work order<strong> <u>IMMEDIATELY</u> </strong>any such purchases require<strong> <u>PRE-AUTHORIZATION</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>HERMAN GUIDELINES - PLEASE READ</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Schedule:</u></strong><u> Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical. Any overtime hours</u><strong><u> MUST be PRE-APPROVED </u></strong><u>by the Project Manager.</u></p><p><u>All workorders are time and materials - which means please bill your actual time onsite / alongside with sign off proof. the document is found in the documents section of this work order. Your closeouts must be accompanied by this document - will not be accepted if sign by yourself - this is coverage that you were completed and released from site by the client - </u></p><p><u>Any cancellation outside of Field Nation's set window which states in the 24 hrs. window - Will be on a case-by-case bases - approved by the workorder manager - this does not approve hours that were scheduled. Work order manager will need to review situation and document - possible 2hr trip fee will be issued to the technician that showed up to site - (ONTIME)</u></p><p><strong>Running late/Unable to make it</strong>: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via<u> phone or message IMMEDIATELY</u>. use the report problem.</p><p><strong><u>Switching Workers:</u></strong><u>&nbsp;Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project or possible NONpayment of workorder.</u></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. No Shorts, Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button-down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).</p><p><strong>Heights:</strong>&nbsp;Must be comfortable working off a ladder.</p><p><strong>Site Conditions:</strong>&nbsp;Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)</p><p><strong>Parking Instructions:</strong>&nbsp;If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order.&nbsp;We cannot accept handwritten receipts.</p><p><strong>Security Instructions:&nbsp;</strong>Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times</p><p><strong>Transportation:&nbsp;</strong>Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.</p><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li>Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.</li><li>Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.</li><li>Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.</li><li>Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.</li><li>No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite &amp; in from of the customer</li><li>If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site</li><li>Do NOT place tools on furniture.&nbsp;</li><li>SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order</li></ul>","markdown":"**BY ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER, YOU ARE AGREEING TO ALL THE TERMS THEREIN. PLEASE MAKE SURE YOU READ THE WORK ORDER CAREFULLY.**\n\nPlease Note: Herman Tech Crew invoices ALL work orders completed the previous week on Mondays. Please review your work order, ensure all field reports, photos, and expenses are uploaded and submit your work order to \"complete\" status BEFORE Monday. We MUST have this done in order to not cause a delay in payment for you. If you have any questions, please contact your Project Manager listed in the work order.\n\n**PLEASE REVIEW** - Any travel cost incurred would need to be reviewed by the provider and made up front when acceptance of the work order - Parking, materials, etc. are **paid/ approved with receipts- only - provide some other documentation of the payment. Or it is up to WO manger discretion.**\n\nPlease review the **HERMAN GUIDELINES portion below**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n**Attached**\n\n**Scope (1 room):** Samsung 55\" QB55C display on a Chief swing arm mount above the huddle-style table, with a Wattbox surge protector. Logitech Rally Bar Mini under the display and a Tap IP controller on the wall for native Teams controls. HDMI/USB-C BYOD input at the table through the table box into the Rally Bar Mini (wall passthrough if there is no table box). CEC auto-power based on Rally Bar sleep status, Rally Bar remote for advanced camera controls, and 3 years of Logitech Essentials service.\n\n**Open items:** Cable pathways through the table, and ceiling height/room dimensions are not specified.\n\n- **Key terms:** Cenero supplies and installs the AV equipment, while the client and others handle electrical, data cabling, millwork, and conduit. Client IT support is required.\n- Help unload equipment, stage and unbox equipment\n- Keep the work site clean and clear of debris as you go\n\n**BEFORE YOU ARRIVE ON SITE**\n\n1. Print off attached daily Field Reports. You are to complete a Field Report for EACH DAY worked and they MUST be signed off on by the Lead Tech on site.\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\n1. Check into your Work Order\n2. Call the *LOCATION CONTACT* at the phone number provided on this work order upon arrival to site to arrange a specific place to meet on site\n3. Obtain completed and signed field report\n4. With direction from Lead Technician take photos of work done\n5. Obtain Signature\n6. Check out of Work Order\n\n**Any expenses MUST BE REQUESTED BY YOU on the work order and MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY AN UPLOADED RECEIPT.​**\n\n**REQUIRED EQUIPMENT**\n\nFailure to bring the tools/PPE listed here will impact your ability to complete this work order and we will not be able to authorize payment and you run the risk of being asked to leave site. Do not borrow tools from the location as this leaves a bad impression. If you have questions please contact your work order Manager.\n\n***Mounting Tools:***\n\n- Cordless drill w/extra battery and assorted drill bits\n- Assorted screwdrivers (Flathead and Phillips head)\n- Stud Finder\n- Bubble level\n- Hammer\n- Drywall saw\n- Pliers\n- Box knife\n- Socket set (SAE/metric)\n\n***Cabling Tools:***\n\n- RJ45 crimper for Category cable (5-6)\n- Wire cutters\n- Cable tester\n- Punch down tool\n\n***PPE***\n\n- You are required to have basic PPE (*Hard hat, high-viz vest, steel toe boots, safety glasses, and gloves*) with you for all of our jobs. If you do not have the proper PPE, you risk being asked to leave the job site.\n\n**DO NOT PURCHASE ANY ADDITIONAL MATERIALS OR PARTS USING YOUR PERSONAL FUNDS**. If you are asked to purchase any parts or materials other than what is on the required list above, please contact the Project Manager listed on this work order **IMMEDIATELY** any such purchases require **PRE-AUTHORIZATION**\n\n**HERMAN GUIDELINES - PLEASE READ**\n\n**Schedule:** Our appointments have hard start times. Timeliness is critical. Any overtime hours **MUST be PRE-APPROVED** by the Project Manager.\n\nAll workorders are time and materials - which means please bill your actual time onsite / alongside with sign off proof. the document is found in the documents section of this work order. Your closeouts must be accompanied by this document - will not be accepted if sign by yourself - this is coverage that you were completed and released from site by the client -\n\nAny cancellation outside of Field Nation's set window which states in the 24 hrs. window - Will be on a case-by-case bases - approved by the workorder manager - this does not approve hours that were scheduled. Work order manager will need to review situation and document - possible 2hr trip fee will be issued to the technician that showed up to site - (ONTIME)\n\n**Running late/Unable to make it**: If you are unable to make it to the job site or are running late. Please contact the listed Project Manager via phone or message IMMEDIATELY. use the report problem.\n\n**Switching Workers:** Do NOT send a worker in your place unless discussed and approved prior to the start date. This is cause for removal from the project or possible NONpayment of workorder.\n\n**Dress Code:** You represent our company and are expected to be neat, clean, and well-groomed to project a professional image. No Shorts, Khaki's and Jeans (as long as no holes, rips, or patched) are acceptable. Please also wear Polo's (no slogans, logos, or graphics) or button-down shirts. Must have site appropriate footwear (rubber toed shoes, comfortable working shoes, or steel toe boots (if required with PPE).\n\n**Heights:** Must be comfortable working off a ladder.\n\n**Site Conditions:** Must be able to lift objects up to 50 lbs. and work within varied conditions (new construction, small or confined spaces, heights)\n\n**Parking Instructions:** If you need reimbursement for parking you must upload a printed receipt to the work order. We cannot accept handwritten receipts.\n\n**Security Instructions:** Make sure you have a photo ID on you at all times\n\n**Transportation:** Reliable transportation and a valid driver's license.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT**\n\n- Personal cell phone usage is restricted to lunch hour of after the day wraps up.\n- Any questions regarding the project are only to be directed to the Herman Lead Technician onsite or the Herman Project Manager listed on this work order.\n- Please keep personal opinions of the job or anything else to yourself while onsite.\n- Do not inquire about connecting via social media with clients or end-users.\n- No foul, offensive, or inappropriate language on the jobsite & in from of the customer\n- If you arrive onsite under the influence of drugs or alcohol, expect to be asked to leave site\n- Do NOT place tools on furniture.\n- SAFETY FIRST! If an accident happens, IMMEDIATELY notify the Herman Lead Tech listed as the Location Contact, or call the Project Manager listed on the work order","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T08:00","end":"2026-11-13T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":330},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":5.276910764779926},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"star