{"job":{"id":20243818,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Circuit Activation ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:</strong></p><p>Circuit activation of a VeloCloud SDWAN on the customer's existing network.</p><p>Tech will work with a remote Engineer to confirm the circuit connection and verify all equipment is online and working properly.</p><p><br></p><p>Upon assignment of this work order, the tech will provide an active cell phone number that can receive text messages and an email address to receive the conference bridge invite and activation link prior to the install.</p><p><strong>Upon Arrival:</strong></p><ul><li>Prior to entering the facility, the tech will text the SGI Project Manager to check in so that the installment team can be alerted.</li><li>Technician will represent our client, Configure, at the customer site and on all calls related to this work order. You will <strong><u>NOT</u></strong> mention that you were sourced through Field Nation or have any other business affiliations.</li><li>Tech will then check in with the LCON [<em>Name &amp; Contact info provided in Confidential section below</em>] to obtain access to the equipment and the installment area.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>DO NOT PLUG or UNPLUG ANYTHING OR BEGIN ANY PART OF THE ACTIVATION until you are on the conference bridge with the Engineer.</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Join Bridge meeting [<em>Invite emailed to tech prior to install date</em>].&nbsp;Announce your arrival to the bridge and follow instructions provided by the engineer.</li><li>Once the activation is successful, the tech will work with the LCON to test connectivity and ensure that everything is working properly.</li><li>Perform a Speed Test directly from the device and take a picture of the result.</li><li>Confirm completion with Engineer and the LCON/customer's IT team.</li><li><strong>Provide an overview of work completed, issues encountered, any follow ups required and the outcome of the scope of work.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Be sure to include which VeloCloud port the circuit was connected to.</strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Label and Upload the following pictures (ensure your camera lens is clean and all pictures are crisp and legible)</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>The VeloCloud installed, to include:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>close-up of the back of the equipment to show which ports have been utilized</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>equipment serial numbers</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>front of the equipment showing the activation lights</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>the bottom of the device showing the serial number and identifiers</strong></li><li><strong>A full view of the rack or installment area</strong></li><li><strong>Circuit identification info</strong></li><li><strong>A wide span view of the room where the equipment resides</strong></li><li><strong>The Speed Test result</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Check out with SGI Project Manager <strong>BEFORE </strong>leaving the site.&nbsp;They will be the one to provide you with the Check Out code. The Engineer does not have this info.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician will come to job site prepared with all tools needed to complete this installation and will ensure all electronics (phone and laptop) are fully charged with power cords on hand.</strong></p><ul><li>Mobile Phone (preferably a SmartPhone capable of tethering and taking high quality photos)</li><li>Laptop Computer with Ethernet Port</li><li>Various lengths of Ethernet Cables to connect to SD-WAN device</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Labelmaker</li></ul><p>Technician should wear a polo shirt with no logos or graphics.&nbsp;Jeans are permitted with no holes and baseball caps, beanies or other hats are prohibited while onsite.</p><p><strong>Must bring a minimum of 300 ft of Cat5/6 cable and termination supplies in case an extension is needed. Tech will be reimbursed $0.30 per foot and $3.00 per termination for materials used. You must itemize them in the expenses of the work order. All other materials will be reimbursed at fair market value or with a receipt.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nCircuit activation of a VeloCloud SDWAN on the customer's existing network.\n\nTech will work with a remote Engineer to confirm the circuit connection and verify all equipment is online and working properly.\n\nUpon assignment of this work order, the tech will provide an active cell phone number that can receive text messages and an email address to receive the conference bridge invite and activation link prior to the install.\n\n**Upon Arrival:**\n\n- Prior to entering the facility, the tech will text the SGI Project Manager to check in so that the installment team can be alerted.\n- Technician will represent our client, Configure, at the customer site and on all calls related to this work order. You will **NOT** mention that you were sourced through Field Nation or have any other business affiliations.\n- Tech will then check in with the LCON \\[*Name & Contact info provided in Confidential section below*\\] to obtain access to the equipment and the installment area.\n\n**DO NOT PLUG or UNPLUG ANYTHING OR BEGIN ANY PART OF THE ACTIVATION until you are on the conference bridge with the Engineer.**\n\n- Join Bridge meeting \\[*Invite emailed to tech prior to install date*\\]. Announce your arrival to the bridge and follow instructions provided by the engineer.\n- Once the activation is successful, the tech will work with the LCON to test connectivity and ensure that everything is working properly.\n- Perform a Speed Test directly from the device and take a picture of the result.\n- Confirm completion with Engineer and the LCON/customer's IT team.\n- **Provide an overview of work completed, issues encountered, any follow ups required and the outcome of the scope of work.**\n- **Be sure to include which VeloCloud port the circuit was connected to.**\n\n**Label and Upload the following pictures (ensure your camera lens is clean and all pictures are crisp and legible)**\n\n- **The VeloCloud installed, to include:**\n- **close-up of the back of the equipment to show which ports have been utilized**\n- **equipment serial numbers**\n- **front of the equipment showing the activation lights**\n- **the bottom of the device showing the serial number and identifiers**\n- **A full view of the rack or installment area**\n- **Circuit identification info**\n- **A wide span view of the room where the equipment resides**\n- **The Speed Test result**\n\nCheck out with SGI Project Manager **BEFORE** leaving the site. They will be the one to provide you with the Check Out code. The Engineer does not have this info.\n\n**Technician will come to job site prepared with all tools needed to complete this installation and will ensure all electronics (phone and laptop) are fully charged with power cords on hand.**\n\n- Mobile Phone (preferably a SmartPhone capable of tethering and taking high quality photos)\n- Laptop Computer with Ethernet Port\n- Various lengths of Ethernet Cables to connect to SD-WAN device\n- Console Cable\n- Labelmaker\n\nTechnician should wear a polo shirt with no logos or graphics. Jeans are permitted with no holes and baseball caps, beanies or other hats are prohibited while onsite.\n\n**Must bring a minimum of 300 ft of Cat5/6 cable and termination supplies in case an extension is needed. Tech will be reimbursed $0.30 per foot and $3.00 per termination for materials used. You must itemize them in the expenses of the work order. All other materials will be reimbursed at fair market value or with a receipt.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T08:45","end":"2026-10-28T10:15"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":74.9200958955501},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793035762092}
{"job":{"id":20243852,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Dispatch - FIVE BELOW - Five Below- Store #8321 - 3130 Halifax Rd, South Boston, VA 24592","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*******CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! ********</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>5G DISPATCH REQUEST</p>\n<p>Address:</p>\n<p>3130 Halifax Rd.</p>\n<p>South Boston, VA 24592</p>\n<p>Company Name: Five Below- Store #8321</p>\n<p>Dispatch date/time: Tuesday, 10/27/26, Arriving by 10am local time</p>\n<p>ONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION</p>\n<p>LCON Name: Site manager</p>\n<p>We are installing a 5G Cradlepoint device. This device has DUAL SIMS on it- We will need to test the CP 1st with the SIM that is in Slot 1 (TMB) and then test with the SIM that is in SLOT 2 (ATT). Our task will be to locate that device, connect it to our laptop and test it for speed and ping response. Then, we will re-test it once more after 10 minutes. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.</p>\n<p>Ping test 100 times and get the percentage.</p>\n<p>1.Enter the command as follows: ping -n 100 1.1.1.1. ping = The command to ping, leave unchanged. ...</p>\n<p>2.Check the summary when completed for percentage of packet loss.</p>\n<p>Run speed test once, document speed and ms response time</p>\n<p>Run speed test 10 minutes later and document the same.</p>\n<p>Anything over 120ms response and below 5M download will need to be installed as the backup connection on the customer meraki. When reaching out to Five Below IT, please inform them if the circuit is below this threshold and request we install this device as the backup connection on their Meraki</p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<p>• Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************</del></p>\n<p>• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</p>\n<p>• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</p>\n<p>• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 250 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),<strong>350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools</strong>. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <strong>206-494-6399</strong></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email <strong>turnups@sangoma.com</strong> with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call<strong>206-494-6399</strong>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n5G DISPATCH REQUEST\n\nAddress:\n\n3130 Halifax Rd.\n\nSouth Boston, VA 24592\n\nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #8321\n\nDispatch date/time: Tuesday, 10/27/26, Arriving by 10am local time\n\nONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION\n\nLCON Name: Site manager\n\nWe are installing a 5G Cradlepoint device. This device has DUAL SIMS on it- We will need to test the CP 1st with the SIM that is in Slot 1 (TMB) and then test with the SIM that is in SLOT 2 (ATT). Our task will be to locate that device, connect it to our laptop and test it for speed and ping response. Then, we will re-test it once more after 10 minutes. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.\n\nPing test 100 times and get the percentage.\n\n1.Enter the command as follows: ping -n 100 1.1.1.1. ping = The command to ping, leave unchanged. ...\n\n2.Check the summary when completed for percentage of packet loss.\n\nRun speed test once, document speed and ms response time\n\nRun speed test 10 minutes later and document the same.\n\nAnything over 120ms response and below 5M download will need to be installed as the backup connection on the customer meraki. When reaching out to Five Below IT, please inform them if the circuit is below this threshold and request we install this device as the backup connection on their Meraki\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n\n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 250 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),**350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools**. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at **206-494-6399**\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email **turnups@sangoma.com** with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call**206-494-6399**with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.634871867292475},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Oct 27, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 27, Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana o