{"job":{"id":20168820,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Direct Source","title":"Pin Pad Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code</strong>(voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p>\n<p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site</strong> (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Services</u></strong>: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.</p>\n<p>An overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.</strong></p>\n<p>Check in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.</p>\n<p>Check in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>:</strong> Obtain<strong>\"BEFORE\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting</strong> <strong>any work.</strong></p>\n<p>Upload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.</p>\n<p>Email all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.</p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Installation inventory</strong> of new hardware at the store location.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.</strong></li>\n<li>Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Inspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.</p>\n<p>Begin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates – Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .</li>\n<li><strong>Security Screws</strong>: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.</li>\n<li><strong>P-Clips</strong>: Each pin pad cable <strong>must be routed down and behind each pin pad</strong> and secured with the supplied P-Clip.</li>\n<li><strong>Verify Mounting Bracket orientation</strong>: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.</li>\n<li><strong>Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register</strong> – End Client will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Proceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Neatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.</p>\n<p>MOD to validate pin pads are functional.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hardware Return</strong>: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box</strong>.</li>\n<li>Place the <strong>old cables &amp; anti-skimmer plates</strong>inside the smaller box – RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.</li>\n<li>Place the <strong>old MX915 pin pads</strong> inside the master pack box using bubble wrap – RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Clean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.</p>\n<p>Complete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.</p>\n<p>Sign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.</p>\n<p>The technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>:</strong> Obtain<strong>\"AFTER\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible.</strong></li>\n<li>Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.</p>\n<p><strong>Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure</strong> (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p>\n<p>Technician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.</p>\n<p>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates – submit daily deliverables).</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Technician Required Equipment, Tools &amp; Hardware:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Standard&nbsp;Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill &amp; various bits, hammer, etc.)</p>\n<p>Cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier</p>\n<p><strong>Phone charger required</strong> -&nbsp;will need to be on the phone majority of the install with End Client Support</p>\n<p>Printed copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form [Installation Checklist] and the Technical Installation Guide –&nbsp;<strong>Included in Shipment</strong>.</p>\n<p># 1&nbsp;Philips screwdriver</p>\n<p># 2 Philips screwdriver</p>\n<p>T8 Torx Bit – Screwdriver or Allen Key type</p>\n<p>Step drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required</p>\n<p>Packing tape</p>\n<p>Velcro (for cable management)</p>\n<p>Electrical tape</p>\n<p>Headlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful</p>\n<p>Ear buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Project Preparation/ Orientation:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>The Technician who will be onsite</strong>, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. <strong>Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Deliverables &amp; Reporting</u></strong>: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).</p>\n<p><strong>Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning.</strong> If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.</li>\n<li>Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. [EX: J. Doe,&nbsp;#4321 06/03/2026]</li>\n<li>Required deliverables include the following:</li>\n</ul>\n<p>- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form [Installation Checklist] with MOD signature</p>\n<p>- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Direct Source Obligations:&nbsp;</u></strong></p>\n<p>Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download.&nbsp;<strong><u>Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual</li>\n<li>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan</li>\n<li>End Client Installation Manual</li>\n<li>End Client Check In/Out Form</li>\n<li>Itemized Hardware/Material List [Site Packing Slip – located on the outside of the box in a sealed window]</li>\n<li>End Client Letter of Authorization</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Payment Information:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Payment Amounts:</u></strong> $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate:</u></strong> $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15-minute increments. <strong>T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.</strong></p>\n<p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain <u>pre-approval</u> for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Store Revisits:</u></strong> Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):</u></strong></p>\n<p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. <strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Any site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).</p>\n<p><strong><u>Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li>\n<li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee</li>\n<li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge</li>\n<li>Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed</li>\n<li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee</li>\n<li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li>\n<li>Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:</u></strong><em>&nbsp;All below dates are from the day of the installation date.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​</li>\n<li>2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.</li>\n<li>The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:</li>\n<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- submit the outstanding item(s) or,</li>\n<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</li>\n<li><strong>The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.</strong>3<strong>0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.</strong></li>\n<li>5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p>\n<p>- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p>\n<p>- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Expectations &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:</p>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Allowed:</strong> Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts</p>\n<p><strong>Not Allowed:</strong> Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).</p>\n<p><strong><u>Presentation:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Travel Arrangements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.</li>\n<li>Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.</li>\n<li>Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Deductions:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.</p>","markdown":"**Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code**(voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.**\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site** (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).\n\n**Scope of Services**: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n**Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.**\n\nCheck in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.\n\nCheck in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.\n\n**Required Deliverables:** Obtain**\"BEFORE\"** **images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting** **any work.**\n\nUpload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.\n\nEmail all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.\n\n**Pre-Installation inventory** of new hardware at the store location.\n\n- **Required Deliverables: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.**\n- Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.\n\nInspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.\n\nBegin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates – Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.\n\n- You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .\n- **Security Screws**: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.\n- **P-Clips**: Each pin pad cable **must be routed down and behind each pin pad** and secured with the supplied P-Clip.\n- **Verify Mounting Bracket orientation**: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.\n- **Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register** – End Client will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.\n\nProceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.\n\n- Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.\n\nNeatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.\n\nMOD to validate pin pads are functional.\n\n- The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.\n\n**Hardware Return**: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.\n\n- **Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box**.\n- Place the **old cables & anti-skimmer plates**inside the smaller box – RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.\n- Place the **old MX915 pin pads** inside the master pack box using bubble wrap – RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.\n\nClean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.\n\nComplete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nSign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nThe technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.\n\n- **Required Deliverables:** Obtain**\"AFTER\"** **images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible.**\n- Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.\n\nCheck out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.\n\n**Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure** (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\nTechnician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.\n\nSubmittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates – submit daily deliverables).\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools & Hardware:**\n\nStandard Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill & various bits, hammer, etc.)\n\nCell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier\n\n**Phone charger required** - will need to be on the phone majority of the install with End Client Support\n\nPrinted copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] and the Technical Installation Guide – **Included in Shipment**.\n\n\\# 1 Philips screwdriver\n\n\\# 2 Philips screwdriver\n\nT8 Torx Bit – Screwdriver or Allen Key type\n\nStep drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required\n\nPacking tape\n\nVelcro (for cable management)\n\nElectrical tape\n\nHeadlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful\n\nEar buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed\n\n**Project Preparation/ Orientation:**\n\n**The Technician who will be onsite**, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. **Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.**\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting**: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).\n\n**Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning.** If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.\n\n- Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.\n- Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. \\[EX: J. Doe, #4321 06/03/2026\\]\n- Required deliverables include the following:\n\n\\- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] with MOD signature\n\n\\- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:**\n\nDirect Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. **Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.**\n\n**Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:**\n\n- DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual\n- Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan\n- End Client Installation Manual\n- End Client Check In/Out Form\n- Itemized Hardware/Material List \\[Site Packing Slip – located on the outside of the box in a sealed window\\]\n- End Client Letter of Authorization\n\n**Payment Information:**\n\n**Payment Amounts:** $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate:** $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15-minute increments. **T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.**\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits:** Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\nAny site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).\n\n**Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:**\n\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&M + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe\n\n**SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:** *All below dates are from the day of the installation date.*\n\n- 1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​\n- 2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.\n- The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:\n- - submit the outstanding item(s) or,\n- - return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n- **The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.**3**0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.**\n- 5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.\n\n\\- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\n\\- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\n\\- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.\n\n**Expectations & Requirements:**\n\nDirect Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n**Allowed:** Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts\n\n**Not Allowed:** Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).\n\n**Presentation:**\n\nTechnicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.\n\n**Travel Arrangements:**\n\n- Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.\n- Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.\n- Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.\n- Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.\n\n**Deductions:**\n\nDirect Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-08T22:30","end":"2026-11-08T26:30"},"payRange":{"min":260,"max":260},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.776898710081937},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793036300467}
{"job":{"id":20244105,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"REF #T20261022.0522 - Chapel Hill, NC - Workstation Network & Printer Connectivity Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<strong>FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL</strong><br><strong>MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE <del>** </del>SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested</strong><br><strong>Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code</strong><ul><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.</li><li><strong>Client Representation:</strong> You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.</li><li><strong>Platform Discretion:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> mention or discuss <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ****** </del></span>or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work/On-site Task:</strong><ol><li><strong>Check-In &amp; Baseline Audit:</strong> Check in with <del>****** **** </del>and call <del>** </del>Support. Compare IP/subnet settings between the working dual-homed PC and the affected Wi-Fi-only PC.</li><li><strong>Network &amp; Printer Diagnostics:</strong> Test local LAN drop with laptop/tester. If Wi-Fi is required, verify SSID isolation and subnet routing with DQ Support. Ping printer IP and test port 9100.</li><li><strong>Printer Setup &amp; Verification:</strong> Clear print spooler, re-add printer via static IP/hostname, and print test page with <del>****** **** </del>to confirm fix.</li><li><strong>Closeout:</strong> Capture photo deliverables, obtain site sign-off, and check out with Support.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools:</strong><ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet NIC &amp; patch cable</li><li>Network cable tester &amp; toner/probe kit</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Smartphone for photos and DQ Support coordination</li></ul><p>For <u>pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact</u>, please check the <strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION</strong> below.</p><p><br></p><strong>DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)</li><li><strong>Record</strong>: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong> Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong> Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within <strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><br>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE & PROTOCOL**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE \\*\\* SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism & Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**1. **Check-In & Baseline Audit:** Check in with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* and call \\*\\* Support. Compare IP/subnet settings between the working dual-homed PC and the affected Wi-Fi-only PC.\n2. **Network & Printer Diagnostics:** Test local LAN drop with laptop/tester. If Wi-Fi is required, verify SSID isolation and subnet routing with DQ Support. Ping printer IP and test port 9100.\n3. **Printer Setup & Verification:** Clear print spooler, re-add printer via static IP/hostname, and print test page with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm fix.\n4. **Closeout:** Capture photo deliverables, obtain site sign-off, and check out with Support.\n\n**Required Tools:**- Laptop with Ethernet NIC & patch cable\n- Network cable tester & toner/probe kit\n- Basic hand tools\n- Smartphone for photos and DQ Support coordination\n\nFor pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact, please check the **CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION** below.\n\n**DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:**- **Documentation:** Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)\n- **Record**: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nBy accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T14:00","end":"2026-10-26T17:00","latestStart":"2026-10-26T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":17.474567838915743},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Mon, Oct 26, 2:00 PM\nChecked: Mon, Oct 26, Tue, Oct 27, Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z