{"job":{"id":20244351,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Circuit to Customer Equipment Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME&nbsp;</strong><strong>(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required&nbsp;Deliverables&nbsp;to be paid:</strong></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>When onsite check-in with a CommandLink Dispatch coordinator by&nbsp;dialing 385-533-9167&nbsp;to get check in code.</p><p>Join Meeting&nbsp;<strong>&lt;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">contact Shiva Mallepula - sbhavanimallepula@merceradvisors.com - Tel: (281) 899-0940</span></p><ol><li>Touch base with the onsite contact.<span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Frances Hymillerat 984-248-6890</span></li><li>Take before pictures of any equipment installation location except for desk phones.</li><li>Locate the below circuits:</li></ol><p>Spectrum Circuit information:&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Circuit ID: 8349100042475492</p><p>IP Address:70.62.88.33</p><p>Gateway IP Address: 70.62.88.33</p><p>IP Range Assigned: 70.62.88.32 - 70.62.88.35</p><p>IP Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252</p><p>Usable IP Address: 70.62.88.34 - 70.62.88.34</p><p>Modem Make/Model: Ubee EU2251</p><p>Serial: MBV8M63010904</p><p>Router Make/Model: SAX1V1K</p><ol><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">MAC: 4c:ab:f8:24:3c:a9</li><li><strong>Follow instructions from IT professional on conference bridge to connect each circuit to the customer-provided router. Customer will advise where router is located and tell you which port to plug each circuit into.</strong></li><li>Verify with the IT professional on conference bridge that the equipment is up and running.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Cable manage and cleanup</li><li>Perform tests as requested by IT professional.</li><li>Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.</li><li>Call CommandLink Dispatch coordinator 385-533-9167 to get check out code before leaving site to get check out code.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.</strong></p><p><strong>3.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><br></p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME** **(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n\nWhen onsite check-in with a CommandLink Dispatch coordinator by dialing 385-533-9167 to get check in code.\n\nJoin Meeting **<**contact Shiva Mallepula - sbhavanimallepula@merceradvisors.com - Tel: (281) 899-0940\n\n1. Touch base with the onsite contact.Frances Hymillerat 984-248-6890\n2. Take before pictures of any equipment installation location except for desk phones.\n3. Locate the below circuits:\n\nSpectrum Circuit information:\n\nCircuit ID: 8349100042475492\n\nIP Address:70.62.88.33\n\nGateway IP Address: 70.62.88.33\n\nIP Range Assigned: 70.62.88.32 - 70.62.88.35\n\nIP Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252\n\nUsable IP Address: 70.62.88.34 - 70.62.88.34\n\nModem Make/Model: Ubee EU2251\n\nSerial: MBV8M63010904\n\nRouter Make/Model: SAX1V1K\n\n1. MAC: 4c:ab:f8:24:3c:a9\n2. **Follow instructions from IT professional on conference bridge to connect each circuit to the customer-provided router. Customer will advise where router is located and tell you which port to plug each circuit into.**\n3. Verify with the IT professional on conference bridge that the equipment is up and running.\n4. Cable manage and cleanup\n5. Perform tests as requested by IT professional.\n6. Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.\n7. Call CommandLink Dispatch coordinator 385-533-9167 to get check out code before leaving site to get check out code.\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n**1. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.**\n\n**2. If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.**\n\n**3. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.**\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00","end":"2026-11-04T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":185},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":5.363698184729926},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $185 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[