{"job":{"id":20245248,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Safely-You","title":"Senior Living Community | Troubleshooting Wireless Camera | Heat Gun Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>We are seeking a technician to perform hands-on troubleshooting at a senior-living community. Your role is to physically inspect the equipment while a SafelyYou Support agent guides you remotely by phone. You will follow simple instructions from the agent and document your work with photos.</li><li>This is an active residential care environment (Memory Care and/or Assisted Living). Professional conduct is required at all times.</li><li><strong>We have a camera sensor installed in Room 78 that is offline and needs troubleshooting and, possibly, replacement. If we have determined that the device needed replacement, the device will have already been shipped to the site. An outlet cover may also be needed, and one has already been shipped. Check with the SafelyYou Support agent to confirm if there is a replacement device on site.</strong></li><li><em>NOTE: If any other equipment goes offline during the job, you will be asked to help us troubleshoot them as well. If you leave the job without confirmation from a SafelyYou Support agent that all devices have come back online or approval from them that it is alright to leave while devices are still offline, the job will not be approved. Good service will be added to our preferred pool for future jobs.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Before and after photos of the equipment, showing these details: product label showing device ID, mounting location, cabling and connection at outlet.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools &amp; Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Let us know if you don't have something listed in the Equipment list</li><li><strong>Key Tools:</strong> Heatgun for applying heatshrink [Needed if cabling is being replaced]</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Neat and professional appearance</li><li>Business-casual attire preferred (e.g. plain polo)</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li></ul><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Providers new to our Field Nation pool will be asked to join a 5-minute Zoom evaluation call before assignment</li><li>Once you've been assigned, select your Hard Start right away (unless the WO already specifies Hard Start time). <strong><em>If you don't set a Hard Start within 1hr after assignment, we may look for another provider.</em></strong></li></ul><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>When you arrive on location, check in on Field Nation then call SafelyYou at (415) 935-5937</li><li>Identify that you are a Field Nation tech on site and specify the community name—you will be forwarded to the SafelyYou agent who will work with you throughout the job. <strong>DO NOT</strong>enter the community until you are on the phone with a SafelyYou agent.</li><li>Enter the building: <strong><em>You represent SafelyYou while onsite.</em></strong> Introduce yourself at the front desk, identify that you are here to assist with troubleshooting SafelyYou equipment, and ask to be directed to the location specified by the SafelyYou agent. If you are doing work in a residential room, you may need assistance from staff to enter the room.</li><li>In the room, before touching anything, take pictures and note any observations about the connection of the power adapter in the outlet (Is anything loose? Is anything damaged?)</li><li>Follow all troubleshooting instructions from the SafelyYou agent, which may include:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check for loose connection points</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unmounting and re-mounting the sensor</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">WiFi Speed test</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Factory Reset</li><li>The SafelyYou agent will let you know when troubleshooting is completed and you are released.</li><li>Check out of the Field Nation work order.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval / Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours, expenses, or travel costs must be pre-approved by SafelyYou.</li><li>Providers are required to call or email the SafelyYou Project Manager for authorization prior to incurring any additional charges. Unauthorized expenses will not be reimbursed.</li></ul><p><strong>IMPORTANT</strong>: By agreeing to this work order, you are agreeing to our Non-Disclosure Agreement to not share any information about the contents of the site survey. NDA is attached in work order to review.</p><p><em>*If you've worked with SafelyYou before through another vendor or platform, let us know!</em></p>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- We are seeking a technician to perform hands-on troubleshooting at a senior-living community. Your role is to physically inspect the equipment while a SafelyYou Support agent guides you remotely by phone. You will follow simple instructions from the agent and document your work with photos.\n- This is an active residential care environment (Memory Care and/or Assisted Living). Professional conduct is required at all times.\n- **We have a camera sensor installed in Room 78 that is offline and needs troubleshooting and, possibly, replacement. If we have determined that the device needed replacement, the device will have already been shipped to the site. An outlet cover may also be needed, and one has already been shipped. Check with the SafelyYou Support agent to confirm if there is a replacement device on site.**\n- *NOTE: If any other equipment goes offline during the job, you will be asked to help us troubleshoot them as well. If you leave the job without confirmation from a SafelyYou Support agent that all devices have come back online or approval from them that it is alright to leave while devices are still offline, the job will not be approved. Good service will be added to our preferred pool for future jobs.*\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n- Before and after photos of the equipment, showing these details: product label showing device ID, mounting location, cabling and connection at outlet.\n\n**Tools &amp; Equipment:**\n\n- Let us know if you don't have something listed in the Equipment list\n- **Key Tools:** Heatgun for applying heatshrink \\[Needed if cabling is being replaced\\]\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Neat and professional appearance\n- Business-casual attire preferred (e.g. plain polo)\n- Closed-toe shoes\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Providers new to our Field Nation pool will be asked to join a 5-minute Zoom evaluation call before assignment\n- Once you've been assigned, select your Hard Start right away (unless the WO already specifies Hard Start time). ***If you don't set a Hard Start within 1hr after assignment, we may look for another provider.***\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n- When you arrive on location, check in on Field Nation then call SafelyYou at (415) 935-5937\n- Identify that you are a Field Nation tech on site and specify the community name—you will be forwarded to the SafelyYou agent who will work with you throughout the job. **DO NOT**enter the community until you are on the phone with a SafelyYou agent.\n- Enter the building: ***You represent SafelyYou while onsite.*** Introduce yourself at the front desk, identify that you are here to assist with troubleshooting SafelyYou equipment, and ask to be directed to the location specified by the SafelyYou agent. If you are doing work in a residential room, you may need assistance from staff to enter the room.\n- In the room, before touching anything, take pictures and note any observations about the connection of the power adapter in the outlet (Is anything loose? Is anything damaged?)\n- Follow all troubleshooting instructions from the SafelyYou agent, which may include:\n- Check for loose connection points\n- Unmounting and re-mounting the sensor\n- WiFi Speed test\n- Factory Reset\n- The SafelyYou agent will let you know when troubleshooting is completed and you are released.\n- Check out of the Field Nation work order.\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval / Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours, expenses, or travel costs must be pre-approved by SafelyYou.\n- Providers are required to call or email the SafelyYou Project Manager for authorization prior to incurring any additional charges. Unauthorized expenses will not be reimbursed.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: By agreeing to this work order, you are agreeing to our Non-Disclosure Agreement to not share any information about the contents of the site survey. NDA is attached in work order to review.\n\n*\\*If you've worked with SafelyYou before through another vendor or platform, let us know!*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T12:00","end":"2026-10-28T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":180,"max":306},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":180},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":63}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":43.488964878942554},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Oct 28, 12:00 PM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29