{"job":{"id":20247151,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Akkodis, formerly Modis","title":"PC Refresh, Memory / Win 11Upgrades ","description":{"html":"<p>This project initiative is focused on the systematic replacement of end-of-life (EOL) laptops across the organization.</p><p>In parallel, the engagement includes upgrading desktop systems to Windows 11.</p><p>Additionally, the project emphasizes performance optimization through memory upgrades. Functional RAM modules from decommissioned devices are carefully recovered, tested, and redeployed to enhance the performance of active laptops that remain within their service lifecycle.</p><p>Overall, the initiative aims to improve device efficiency, extend hardware usability for NFI Industries</p><p><strong><u>***DO NOT DISCUSS YOUR COMPENSATION &amp; CLIENT CONTACT DETAILS (STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL) WITH ANYONE OUTSIDE OF AKKODIS***</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Read all the below instructions carefully:</u></strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;Instructional Note for Technicians:</strong> Please ensure the team thoroughly reviews the service description, Runbook, and checklist documents to fully understand the instructions. Upon task completion, they are required to:</p><ul><li>Update the checklist.</li><li>Obtain a signature from the site Point of Contact.</li><li>Upload a photo of the signed document to the work order.</li><li>For every site unless the memory will be reused, please have the technician package it in the laptop box along with the old laptop.</li></ul><p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please contact the Primary Point of Contact after check In at site and after completion of work don't leave the site without informing the support contact and get their signature.</strong></p><p><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Failing the above instructions will strictly lead to work order cancellation or may hamper the pay.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Post successful completion of the work on site, please enter complete close out notes along with deliverables attached which is mandatory before marking the work order completed.</strong></p><p><strong>In order to be paid for this work order ALL work must be completed: replacement, testing, return, requested photos and most all maintaining professionalism onsite.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>﻿Mandatory Technical Briefing :&nbsp;</strong>At least 48 hours before the scheduled task, the technician&nbsp;<strong>must</strong>&nbsp;call the&nbsp;<strong>NFI IT Team</strong>&nbsp;using the provided contact numbers. The goal is to verify technical requirements and address site-specific questions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Verification:</strong>&nbsp;The technician must log the name of the NFI IT representative they spoke with in the Field Nation notes.</li><li><strong>Inquiry Protocol (Pre-Site):</strong>&nbsp;Direct all&nbsp;<strong>technical</strong>&nbsp;questions to the NFI IT Team and all&nbsp;<strong>scope/logistics</strong>&nbsp;questions to the Akkodis Team at least 48 hours prior to arrival.</li><li><strong>Communication Standards:</strong>&nbsp;Prompt acknowledgment of all Akkodis emails and messages is mandatory. Responses are expected within&nbsp;<strong>4 hours</strong>&nbsp;during business days.</li><li><strong>On-Site Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Technicians must be fully self-sufficient and prepared upon arrival. Avoid asking repeated questions on-site that are explicitly covered in the&nbsp;<strong>NFI Runbook</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Scope documents</strong>. Failure to follow the Runbook may lead to performance escalations or rating deductions.</li><li><strong>Required Tools &amp; Hardware Verification:</strong>&nbsp;The technician must confirm they possess all necessary hardware and tools required for the task&nbsp;prior to traveling to the site.</li><li><strong>The \"First Hour\" Milestone:</strong>&nbsp;Technicians must provide a quick status update via the call or Field Nation after the&nbsp;<strong>first 60 minutes</strong>&nbsp;on-site (e.g., \"First 3 devices completed\").&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Workflow:</strong></p><p><strong>below are the device types NFI (Client)would like to have for each of the desktops. please add this to the list as part of the checklist.</strong></p><p>Pack station</p><p>Shipping station</p><p>eCommerce station</p><p>VAS station</p><p>Cubiscan station</p><p>Returns station</p><p>Warehouse TV station</p><p>Mobile cart station</p><p></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"This project initiative is focused on the systematic replacement of end-of-life (EOL) laptops across the organization.\n\nIn parallel, the engagement includes upgrading desktop systems to Windows 11.\n\nAdditionally, the project emphasizes performance optimization through memory upgrades. Functional RAM modules from decommissioned devices are carefully recovered, tested, and redeployed to enhance the performance of active laptops that remain within their service lifecycle.\n\nOverall, the initiative aims to improve device efficiency, extend hardware usability for NFI Industries\n\n**\\*\\*\\*DO NOT DISCUSS YOUR COMPENSATION &amp; CLIENT CONTACT DETAILS (STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL) WITH ANYONE OUTSIDE OF AKKODIS\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Read all the below instructions carefully:**\n\n**1. Instructional Note for Technicians:** Please ensure the team thoroughly reviews the service description, Runbook, and checklist documents to fully understand the instructions. Upon task completion, they are required to:\n\n- Update the checklist.\n- Obtain a signature from the site Point of Contact.\n- Upload a photo of the signed document to the work order.\n- For every site unless the memory will be reused, please have the technician package it in the laptop box along with the old laptop.\n\n**2. Please contact the Primary Point of Contact after check In at site and after completion of work don't leave the site without informing the support contact and get their signature.**\n\n**3.** **Failing the above instructions will strictly lead to work order cancellation or may hamper the pay.**\n\n**4. Post successful completion of the work on site, please enter complete close out notes along with deliverables attached which is mandatory before marking the work order completed.**\n\n**In order to be paid for this work order ALL work must be completed: replacement, testing, return, requested photos and most all maintaining professionalism onsite.**\n\n- **﻿Mandatory Technical Briefing :** At least 48 hours before the scheduled task, the technician **must** call the **NFI IT Team** using the provided contact numbers. The goal is to verify technical requirements and address site-specific questions.\n- **Verification:** The technician must log the name of the NFI IT representative they spoke with in the Field Nation notes.\n- **Inquiry Protocol (Pre-Site):** Direct all **technical** questions to the NFI IT Team and all **scope/logistics** questions to the Akkodis Team at least 48 hours prior to arrival.\n- **Communication Standards:** Prompt acknowledgment of all Akkodis emails and messages is mandatory. Responses are expected within **4 hours** during business days.\n- **On-Site Execution:** Technicians must be fully self-sufficient and prepared upon arrival. Avoid asking repeated questions on-site that are explicitly covered in the **NFI Runbook** or **Scope documents**. Failure to follow the Runbook may lead to performance escalations or rating deductions.\n- **Required Tools &amp; Hardware Verification:** The technician must confirm they possess all necessary hardware and tools required for the task prior to traveling to the site.\n- **The \"First Hour\" Milestone:** Technicians must provide a quick status update via the call or Field Nation after the **first 60 minutes** on-site (e.g., \"First 3 devices completed\").\n\n**Workflow:**\n\n**below are the device types NFI (Client)would like to have for each of the deskto