es</p>\n<p>Console Cable - RS232 MALE serial console cable for Velocity VBand Platinum (proprietary router)</p>\n<p>Console Cable - female DB9 to male RJ45 (Cisco Console Cable)</p>\n<p>Patch Cables - Minimum of 3</p>\n<p>WINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port</p>\n<p>AeroAdmin installed: (https://www.aeroadmin.com/en/downloads.html)</p>\n<p>Coaxial crimper: with spare barrel connectors</p>\n<p>Coaxial cable: 150 feet minimum</p>","markdown":"Call Direct: 888-443-4375 Option 0\n\nWith as many open work orders currently on FN, there is a very long back order of requests. So if you call in they will work with you to get assigned.\n\nJob Description: Job Description:\n\nTech will be onsite to investigate room(s): 201 105 210 and 212. Tech will start in the MDF before proceeding to any other area. Tech will confirm that the Smartbox vents are clear of debris and vacuum the vents if possible. If no vacuum is available, tech will wipe the vents to remove dust. Tech will remove any items blocking the vents and ensure all SAT and coax connections are tight and undamaged. Tech will gather a wide-angle photo of the MDF and a close-up photo of the amplifier, where present. Support must upload these photos to the Documents section in Vselect. All Layer 1 findings and corrective actions must be documented in the dispatch ticket. Once these MDF Layer 1 checks are completed, tech will proceed with the scope below.\n\nTech will then proceed to the affected room(s), confirm the reported issue and complete room-level Layer 1 with support. Check TV power, input/source settings, coax connections, wall plates and visible cabling for loose or damaged connections. Reseat connections and test with a known-working coax cable where available. Confirm TV service after each corrective action.\n\nIf room-level Layer 1 does not resolve the issue, tech will document the checks performed and results and notify support. Support will determine the next troubleshooting steps and arrange a follow-up dispatch with a SAT meter and attenuators if signal testing or balancing is needed. If findings indicate a sitewide issue or a block of rooms with a possible shared tap or signal fault, notify support to reassess the dispatch scope and required equipment.\n\n﻿\\*SAT Meter: N\n\n\\*Coax Termination Tools: Y\n\n\\*Coax Toner: Y\n\n\\*Tone Generator &amp; Probe Kit: N/A\n\nRequired Tools: Cell phone: With charger and photo taking ability\n\nCamera with USB cord: If phone with photo taking ability is not available\n\nAeroAdmin installed: (<https://www.aeroadmin.com/en/downloads.html)>\n\nTerminal Emulator Program: Hyper Terminal Putty Teraterm etc.\n\nToner: for Identify existing in house wiring to extend circuits\n\nWire cutters: Cut wires efficiently\n\nWire Strippers: Strip cables correctly\n\nCable tester: Validate cables\n\nConsole Cable - RS232 MALE serial console cable for Velocity VBand Platinum (proprietary router)\n\nConsole Cable - female DB9 to male RJ45 (Cisco Console Cable)\n\nPatch Cables - Minimum of 3\n\nWINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port\n\nCoaxial crimper: with spare barrel connectors\n\nCoaxial cable: 150 feet minimum\n\nCell phone: With charger and photo taking ability\n\nCamera with USB cord: If phone with photo taking ability is not available\n\nTerminal Emulator Program: Hyper Terminal Putty Teraterm etc.\n\nToner: for Identify existing in house wiring to extend circuits\n\nWire cutters: Cut wires efficiently\n\nWire Strippers: Strip cables correctly\n\nCable tester: Validate cables\n\nConsole Cable - RS232 MALE serial console cable for Velocity VBand Platinum (proprietary router)\n\nConsole Cable - female DB9 to male RJ45 (Cisco Console Cable)\n\nPatch Cables - Minimum of 3\n\nWINDOWS OS Laptop Computer with charger: Must have Wi-Fi capability &amp; working ETHERNET port\n\nAeroAdmin installed: (<https://www.aeroadmin.com/en/downl