{"job":{"id":20199602,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Global Onsite Corporation","title":"Starlink Install - PUBS-PUBS-42-S-Caro-7901","description":{"html":"<ol>\n<li>Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Tech will be working with Jose on his bridge and he will be contacting the other people below that work for the site IT.&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Jose:</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Join the meeting:</u></em></strong>https://meetings.dialpad.com/josebarrera</p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Optional dial-in number:</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>(832) 645-2576</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Cutover Procedure</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech fires up Starlink before install to confirm it’s working (avoids lengthy troubleshooting mid-install)</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech runs speed/surf test via laptop on completion</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech pings activation team via Microsoft Teams chat: “I’m at PSA 123, ready to cut over”</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Activation team (Kelly’s side) directs tech to plug Starlink into G1 port on edge device</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cradle point must be in G2; verify customer hasn’t moved it to G1</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Final config: G1 = Starlink, G2 = cradle point</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Activation team confirms link visible on their side, renames it, verifies everything is good</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tech takes photos and checks out; activation team issues release</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Access issues or Starlink power failures go to Chad’s team, not activation</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dispatches mostly mornings; 10am start recommended (fewest access issues)</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Description:</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>GLOBALIQ | STARLINK INSTALL GUIDE</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>BEFORE YOU ARRIVE:<strong>Ensure you have the Starlink App loaded on your Smart Phone.</strong>&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.</li>\n<li>If there are any access issues or other unexpected issues during the scheduled event, please advise the Dispatch team ASAP so they can work toward resolution</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Check-in and introduce yourself to the Onsite Contact.</li>\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Locate &amp; carefully Inventory the Starlink Router, External Antenna, Antenna Mounting Hardware, and provided Cables</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">There may be an additional aftermarket mount sent to the site, confirm with the GLOBALIQ Field Support team to ensure the mount provided is the correct version</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Record the Serial Number of the Router and Antenna.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a single picture of all the provided Hardware (You will send to GLOBALIQ as a part of the Acceptance Criteria)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there are ANY missing components, call the GLOBALIQ Field Support team immediately to review.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\n<li>OPTIONAL: Review the Mounting Location and Installation process with Technical Contact</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Advise of any technical challenges include skyline of site, building height, structural issues that may impact installation or post installation stability, etc.</li>\n<li>Advise of any potential noise or other that may temporarily disrupt the customers operations.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">IF THERE ARE ANY SIGNIFICANT CUSTOMER CONCERNS contact the GLOBALIQ Field Support Team immediately.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Before you begin the Starlink Installation, conduct following:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Capture a BEFORE image of the network Closet</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify that Power is available for the Starlink Router.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify Mounting Location for the Starlink Router.</li>\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Assembly and Placement of Starlink Device</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mount or Place the Starlink Router in the Customers Telco Room, or designated location per the Survey results.</li>\n<li>Soft Mount the Starlink Antenna to the designated location on the exterior building</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Install the Mount</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the Antenna (*** DO NOT TIGHTEN ANTENNA DOWN FULLY***)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">\"Rough In\" the Cables from the Starlink Antenna to the Starlink Router</li>\n<li>Connect the Starlink Cables to the Starlink Antenna</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Make sure the cable locking feature is facing up, and the Starlink cable is sitting flush inside your Starlink Antenna.</li>\n<li>Connect the Starlink Cables to the Starlink Router</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Connect Cables to Starlink Router –<strong>PORT #1</strong> as indicated with the Starlink Symbol on the back of the Router.</li>\n<li>Ensure that the Cable Locking Feature is facing DOWN</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>POWER UP System</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Now that the Starlink Antenna and the Starlink Router are connected, plug the power cable into the power supply, and the other end into the router.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify Power LED</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Tuning the Antenna</li>\n<li>Starlink needs a clear view of the sky so it can stay connected with satellites as they move overhead. Objects that obstruct the connection between your Starlink and the satellite, such as a tree branch, pole, or roof, will cause service interruptions.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Click here for video guidance on obstructions</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li><em>To find a location with a clear view of the sky:</em></li>\n<li><strong><em><u>&nbsp;</u></em></strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Download or Launch the Starlink App.</li>\n<li>Use the \"<strong>Check for Obstructions</strong>\" tool to find an install location that will deliver the best service.</li>\n<li>For best results, use the kickstand to tilt Starlink</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you could not find a clear field of view from the ground level, consider installing it in an elevated location, like a roof, pole, or wall.</li>\n<li>Align Starlink &amp; Get Connected&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Your Starlink Kit will need to face in the right direction to connect to the greatest number of satellites in low terrestrial orbit for the strongest connection. Setup Starlink and be sure that the kit is tilted by using the kickstand.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Click here for additional guidance on the Alignment Tool.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Open the Starlink App on your device.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Once connected, the app will alert you if you need to rotate your Starlink to be properly aligned.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Click the alert to use the tool and adjust your kit to match the image on your device.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Note: If your Starlink is aligned within 5°, the app will not alert you and your Starlink is aligned.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">For additional guidance for the Alignment Tool, click here What is the Alignment Tool and how do I use it?</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Securing the Starlink Antennas Fixed Position</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once the proper alignment has been achieved, tighten the Starlink Antenna and Mounting Hardware to ensure the Starlink Antenna will not 'travel'. Be sure to tighten all appropriate screws and fasteners to ensure the provided mount and Antennal are secure.</li>\n<li>Getting Connected Inside the Premise</li>\n<li>Connect to the STARLINK network from your device WiFi settings.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">'STARLINK' is the router's default WiFi network name (SSID).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">To secure the Starlink WiFi network, use the Customers preferred Name and change it in the Starlink App</li>\n<li>To rename your Starlink WiFi network and create a WiFi password. Open the Starlink App &gt; Settings &gt; Router &gt; enter desired WiFi network name and password &gt; Save.</li>\n<li>This step is optional; however, we recommend securing your WiFi network. Your Starlink WiFi network is not password protected until you set the password.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Hardware Troubleshooting</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What does the light on the router mean?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The light of the router determines the status of the router, as defined below:</li>\n<li>Flashing White Light – Trying to connect. The light will turn solid white when setup is complete and the router is connected to the internet, or solid red if the router cannot get a connection to the internet in 20 minutes.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Solid White Light – Connected to internet. Will turn off after 1 hour.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">No Light – No power to router. With good connection, the light will turn off after 1 hour.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Red Light – Not connected to the internet.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Violet Light – Router is in bypass mode. Will turn off after 1 hour. Factory reset required to exit bypass mode</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Acceptance Testing: Network Connections</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the ZAYO NOC ( NUMBER ) once connected to the network to begin <strong>Acceptance Testing</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><em><u>Using the Extra RJ45 Ports, remove the RJ45 cover on the back of the router, and plug in your own ethernet cable to Port 2. Connect the other end of your cable to customers network stack as per directive of technical contact</u></em></strong></li>\n<li>Test Network Connectivity and <strong>conduct a speed test.</strong></li>\n<li><strong><em><u>Run SPEED TEST (www.speedtest.net) and record speeds</u></em></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Reposition the external antenna as needed to obtain optimal signal strength and speeds</li>\n<li>Ensure cable is labeled with \"Starlink\"</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Thoroughly Clean Up any debris in installation areas pertaining to the installation process.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Take the following images in their final Installed state</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Starlink Router</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">External Starlink Antenna</li>\n<li>Wide angle of network closet</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Once Acceptance has been confirmed by the ZAYO NOC, the Field Engineer is to contact GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to <strong>Check Out</strong> and provide Close Out notes.</li>\n<li>All required deliverables must be returned to GLOBALIQ Field Support Team within 24 hours</li>\n<li>Upload BEFORE and AFTER photos</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Wide angle of location and close up of hardware</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Upload WAN Speed Test Screenshot</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Upload LAN Speed Test Screen Shot</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">CUSTOMER Signed off Workorder</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>TOOLKIT:</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Mask required</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Standard install/removal toolkit</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>6' ladder</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Laptop with TeamViewer preinstalled</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Cell phone with network connection</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>CAT6 cable</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>RJ45 tips</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Crimps/crimpers</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Snips</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Test set</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Adtran and Cisco console cable</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>Ethernet to USB dongle</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>DB9 male to USB dongle</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>***Any other tools necessary to complete the scope of work</u></em></strong></p>","markdown":"1. Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.\n\n***Tech will be working with Jose on his bridge and he will be contacting the other people below that work for the site IT.***\n\n***Jose:***\n\n***Join the meeting:***<https://meetings.dialpad.com/josebarrera>\n\n***Optional dial-in number:***\n\n***(832) 645-2576***\n\n***Cutover Procedure***\n\n***• Tech fires up Starlink before install to confirm it’s working (avoids lengthy troubleshooting mid-install)***\n\n***• Tech runs speed/surf test via laptop on completion***\n\n***• Tech pings activation team via Microsoft Teams chat: “I’m at PSA 123, ready to cut over”***\n\n***• Activation team (Kelly’s side) directs tech to plug Starlink into G1 port on edge device***\n\n***o Cradle point must be in G2; verify customer hasn’t moved it to G1***\n\n***o Final config: G1 = Starlink, G2 = cradle point***\n\n***• Activation team confirms link visible on their side, renames it, verifies everything is good***\n\n***• Tech takes photos and checks out; activation team issues release***\n\n***• Access issues or Starlink power failures go to Chad’s team, not activation***\n\n***• Dispatches mostly mornings; 10am start recommended (fewest access issues)***\n\n***Description:***\n\n***GLOBALIQ | STARLINK INSTALL GUIDE***\n\n1. BEFORE YOU ARRIVE:**Ensure you have the Starlink App loaded on your Smart Phone.**\n\n1. Field Engineer calls GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to check in.\n2. If there are any access issues or other unexpected issues during the scheduled event, please advise the Dispatch team ASAP so they can work toward resolution\n3. \n4. Check-in and introduce yourself to the Onsite Contact.\n5. \n6. Locate &amp; carefully Inventory the Starlink Router, External Antenna, Antenna Mounting Hardware, and provided Cables\n7. There may be an additional aftermarket mount sent to the site, confirm with the GLOBALIQ Field Support team to ensure the mount provided is the correct version\n8. Record the Serial Number of the Router and Antenna.\n9. Take a single picture of all the provided Hardware (You will send to GLOBALIQ as a part of the Acceptance Criteria)\n10. If there are ANY missing components, call the GLOBALIQ Field Support team immediately to review.\n11. \n12. OPTIONAL: Review the Mounting Location and Installation process with Technical Contact\n13. Advise of any technical challenges include skyline of site, building height, structural issues that may impact installation or post installation stability, etc.\n14. Advise of any potential noise or other that may temporarily disrupt the customers operations.\n15. IF THERE ARE ANY SIGNIFICANT CUSTOMER CONCERNS contact the GLOBALIQ Field Support Team immediately.\n\n1. Before you begin the Starlink Installation, conduct following:\n2. Capture a BEFORE image of the network Closet\n3. Verify that Power is available for the Starlink Router.\n4. Verify Mounting Location for the Starlink Router.\n5. \n6. Assembly and Placement of Starlink Device\n7. Mount or Place the Starlink Router in the Customers Telco Room, or designated location per the Survey results.\n8. Soft Mount the Starlink Antenna to the designated location on the exterior building\n9. Install the Mount\n10. Install the Antenna (\\*\\*\\* DO NOT TIGHTEN ANTENNA DOWN FULLY\\*\\*\\*)\n11. \"Rough In\" the Cables from the Starlink Antenna to the Starlink Router\n12. Connect the Starlink Cables to the Starlink Antenna\n13. Make sure the cable locking feature is facing up, and the Starlink cable is sitting flush inside your Starlink Antenna.\n14. Connect the Starlink Cables to the Starlink Router\n15. Connect Cables to Starlink Router –**PORT #1** as indicated with the Starlink Symbol on the back of the Router.\n16. Ensure that the Cable Locking Feature is facing DOWN\n17. \n18. **POWER UP System**\n19. Now that the Starlink Antenna and the Starlink Router are connected, plug the power cable into the power supply, and the other end into the router.\n20. Verify Power LED\n\n1. Tuning the Antenna\n2. Starlink needs a clear view of the sky so it can stay connected with satellites as they move overhead. Objects that obstruct the connection between your Starlink and the satellite, such as a tree branch, pole, or roof, will cause service interruptions.\n3. Click here for video guidance on obstructions\n\n1. *To find a location with a clear view of the sky:*\n2. \n\n1. Download or Launch the Starlink App.\n2. Use the \"**Check for Obstructions**\" tool to find an install location that will deliver the best service.\n3. For best results, use the kickstand to tilt Starlink\n4. If you could not find a clear field of view from the ground level, consider installing it in an elevated location, like a roof, pole, or wall.\n5. Align Starlink &amp; Get Connected\n6. Your Starlink Kit will need to face in the right direction to connect to the greatest number of satellites in low terrestrial orbit for the strongest connection. Setup Starlink and be sure that the kit is tilted by using the kickstand.\n7. Click here for additional guidance on the Alignment Tool.\n8. Open the Starlink App on your device.\n9. Once connected, the app will alert you if you need to rotate your Starlink to be properly aligned.\n10. Click the alert to use the tool and adjust your kit to match the image on your device.\n11. Note: If your Starlink is aligned within 5°, the app will not alert you and your Starlink is aligned.\n12. For additional guidance for the Alignment Tool, click here What is the Alignment Tool and how do I use it?\n13. \n14. Securing the Starlink Antennas Fixed Position\n15. Once the proper alignment has been achieved, tighten the Starlink Antenna and Mounting Hardware to ensure the Starlink Antenna will not 'travel'. Be sure to tighten all appropriate screws and fasteners to ensure the provided mount and Antennal are secure.\n16. Getting Connected Inside the Premise\n17. Connect to the STARLINK network from your device WiFi settings.\n18. 'STARLINK' is the router's default WiFi network name (SSID).\n19. To secure the Starlink WiFi network, use the Customers preferred Name and change it in the Starlink App\n20. To rename your Starlink WiFi network and create a WiFi password. Open the Starlink App &gt; Settings &gt; Router &gt; enter desired WiFi network name and password &gt; Save.\n21. This step is optional; however, we recommend securing your WiFi network. Your Starlink WiFi network is not password protected until you set the password.\n22. \n23. \n\n1. Hardware Troubleshooting\n2. What does the light on the router mean?\n\n1. The light of the router determines the status of the router, as defined below:\n2. Flashing White Light – Trying to connect. The light will turn solid white when setup is complete and the router is connected to the internet, or solid red if the router cannot get a connection to the internet in 20 minutes.\n3. Solid White Light – Connected to internet. Will turn off after 1 hour.\n4. No Light – No power to router. With good connection, the light will turn off after 1 hour.\n5. Red Light – Not connected to the internet.\n6. Violet Light – Router is in bypass mode. Will turn off after 1 hour. Factory reset required to exit bypass mode\n\n1. Acceptance Testing: Network Connections\n2. Contact the ZAYO NOC ( NUMBER ) once connected to the network to begin **Acceptance Testing**\n3. ***Using the Extra RJ45 Ports, remove the RJ45 cover on the back of the router, and plug in your own ethernet cable to Port 2. Connect the other end of your cable to customers network stack as per directive of technical contact***\n4. Test Network Connectivity and **conduct a speed test.**\n5. ***Run SPEED TEST (www.speedtest.net) and record speeds***\n6. Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance.\n7. Reposition the external antenna as needed to obtain optimal signal strength and speeds\n8. Ensure cable is labeled with \"Starlink\"\n9. \n10. Thoroughly Clean Up any debris in installation areas pertaining to the installation process.\n11. \n12. Take the following images in their final Installed state\n13. Starlink Router\n14. External Starlink Antenna\n15. Wide angle of network closet\n16. \n17. Once Acceptance has been confirmed by the ZAYO NOC, the Field Engineer is to contact GLOBALIQ Field Support Team (972-597-9000 option 3) to **Check Out** and provide Close Out notes.\n18. All required deliverables must be returned to GLOBALIQ Field Support Team within 24 hours\n19. Upload BEFORE and AFTER photos\n20. Wide angle of location and close up of hardware\n21. Upload WAN Speed Test Screenshot\n22. Upload LAN Speed Test Screen Shot\n23. CUSTOMER Signed off Workorder\n\n***TOOLKIT:***\n\n***Mask required***\n\n***Standard install/removal toolkit***\n\n***6' ladder***\n\n***Laptop with TeamViewer preinstalled***\n\n***Cell phone with network connection***\n\n***CAT6 cable***\n\n***RJ45 tips***\n\n***Crimps/crimpers***\n\n***Snips***\n\n***Test set***\n\n***Adtran and Cisco console cable***\n\n***Ethernet to USB dongle***\n\n***DB9 male to USB dongle***\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Any other tools necessary to complete the scope of work***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":28.0769236424727},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793047590512}
{"job":{"id":20246526,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING </u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Insight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.</span></p><p><strong><u>10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)&nbsp;</strong>Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. <u>Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.&nbsp;</u></p><ul><li>Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced</li><li>Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions</li><li>Perform cable management</li><li>Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity</li><li>Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter</li><li>Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location</li></ul><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID</li><li>Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)</li><li>Fully charged mobile phone and charger</li><li><u>A printed copy file attached \"</u><strong><u>PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX</u></strong><u>\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.</u></li><li>Pen or pencil</li><li>Basic desktop tool kit</li><li>Phillips and slotted screwdriver set</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Needle nose pliers</li><li>Crescent wrench</li><li>Box cutter</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)</li><li>Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature</li><li>Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations</li><li>Packing Tape</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)</li><li>Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)</li><li><strong>Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><em>Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.</em></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:&nbsp;</strong>Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing, completed digital survey form with site POC. The survey form is on FieldNation (ensure your app is updated). Reach out to FieldNation support directly with any technical issues <a href=\"https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support</a></p><p><strong>Dress:&nbsp;</strong>Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)</p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><ul><li>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</li><li>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</li><li>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</li><li>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</li><li>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li><strong>On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.</strong></li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT</u></strong>: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;</em></p>","markdown":"**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nInsight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.\n\n**10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.**\n\n**Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.**\n\n**Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)** Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.\n\n- Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced\n- Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions\n- Perform cable management\n- Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity\n- Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter\n- Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Photo ID\n- Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)\n- Fully charged mobile phone and charger\n- A printed copy file attached \"**PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX**\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.\n- Pen or pencil\n- Basic desktop tool kit\n- Phillips and slotted screwdriver set\n- Pliers\n- Needle nose pliers\n- Crescent wrench\n- Box cutter\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)\n- Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature\n- Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations\n- Packing Tape\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)\n- Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)\n- **Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.**\n- ***Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.***\n\n**Deliverables:** Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing, completed digital survey form with site POC. The survey form is on FieldNation (ensure your app is updated). Reach out to FieldNation support directly with any technical issues [](https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support)<https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support>\n\n**Dress:** Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)\n\n**Penalties/Deductions**:\n\n- 10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.\n- 10% Deduction for being unprepared.\n- Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.\n- Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.\n\n**Terms for Travel:**\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate\n- If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- **On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.**\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\n**Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite**:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer 