. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</li><li>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li><strong>On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.</strong></li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT</u></strong>: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;</em></p>","markdown":"**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nInsight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must poss