{"job":{"id":20246532,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING </u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Insight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.</span></p><p><strong><u>10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)&nbsp;</strong>Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. <u>Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.&nbsp;</u></p><ul><li>Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced</li><li>Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions</li><li>Perform cable management</li><li>Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity</li><li>Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter</li><li>Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location</li></ul><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID</li><li>Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)</li><li>Fully charged mobile phone and charger</li><li><u>A printed copy file attached \"</u><strong><u>PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX</u></strong><u>\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.</u></li><li>Pen or pencil</li><li>Basic desktop tool kit</li><li>Phillips and slotted screwdriver set</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Needle nose pliers</li><li>Crescent wrench</li><li>Box cutter</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)</li><li>Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature</li><li>Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations</li><li>Packing Tape</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)</li><li>Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)</li><li><strong>Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><em>Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.</em></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:&nbsp;</strong>Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing, completed digital survey form with site POC. The survey form is on FieldNation (ensure your app is updated). Reach out to FieldNation support directly with any technical issues <a href=\"https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support</a></p><p><strong>Dress:&nbsp;</strong>Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)</p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><ul><li>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</li><li>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</li><li>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</li><li>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</li><li>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li><strong>On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.</strong></li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT</u></strong>: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;</em></p>","markdown":"**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nInsight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.\n\n**10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.**\n\n**Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.**\n\n**Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)** Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.\n\n- Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced\n- Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions\n- Perform cable management\n- Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity\n- Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter\n- Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Photo ID\n- Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)\n- Fully charged mobile phone and charger\n- A printed copy file attached \"**PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX**\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.\n- Pen or pencil\n- Basic desktop tool kit\n- Phillips and slotted screwdriver set\n- Pliers\n- Needle nose pliers\n- Crescent wrench\n- Box cutter\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)\n- Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature\n- Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations\n- Packing Tape\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)\n- Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)\n- **Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.**\n- ***Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.***\n\n**Deliverables:** Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing, completed digital survey form with site POC. The survey form is on FieldNation (ensure your app is updated). Reach out to FieldNation support directly with any technical issues [](https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support)<https://support.fieldnation.com/s/article/engage-support>\n\n**Dress:** Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)\n\n**Penalties/Deductions**:\n\n- 10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.\n- 10% Deduction for being unprepared.\n- Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.\n- Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.\n\n**Terms for Travel:**\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate\n- If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- **On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.**\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\n**Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite**:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n\nTech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-19T13:00","end":"2026-11-19T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.15030411788729},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05