{"job":{"id":20248141,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Preston Reserve - Fitness on Demand Wi-Fi Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p>Air Communities - Preston Reserve - Fitness on Demand Wi-Fi Troubleshooting</p><p></p><p><strong>PLEASE CHECK IN / OUT WITH CIS PRO SERVICES (PHONES RING THROUGH IN THE ORDER): <del>************</del></strong></p><p></p><p><strong>TECHNICAL CONTACT:</strong> <del>****************************</del></p><p><strong>LOCAL CONTRACT:</strong> <del>*****************</del></p><p> </p><p><strong>SOW</strong></p><p><strong>We need a tech to assist in the following: </strong></p><ul><li>Check in with CIS</li><li>Check in with TCON </li><li>Check in with the LCON</li><li>Preston Reserve has a Fitness on Demand system that needs to be connected to Wi-Fi and it keeps dropping the signal. </li><li>Explore whether this can be hardwired. <ul><li>If not please confirm connection to the Wi-Fi.</li></ul></li><li>Take a photos of work done onsite and label photos for WO upload</li><li>Check out with TCON before leaving site</li><li>Check out with the LCON - Get Manager signature on FN Survey form</li><li>Check out with CIS</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong>Equipment required</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop w/Charger</li><li>Cell Phone w/Charger</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>10&#39; Ladder</li><li>POTS</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Materials Required: </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">(Techs are responsible for providing materials unless otherwise stated in the scope)</strong></p><p><strong>**Please have extras of all the below:</strong></p><ul><li>Cat6 Plenum cable (at least 200’)</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat6 Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">****NOTE: ALL PHOTOS ARE REQUIRED TO BE LABELED AS TO WHAT THEY ARE BEFORE UPLOADING TO WO OR SENDING TO CIS VIA TEXT. FAILURE TO DO SO WILL RESULT IN PENTALTY FEES****</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>Deliverable Photos Needed:</strong> </p><ul><li>PHOTOS OF WORK DONE - TEXTED TO <del>************</del></li><li>WORKMAN&#39;S COMP WAIVER (ATTACHED)</li><li>MANAGERS SIGN OFF (ATTACHED)</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">***Please note if you do not call for check out before leaving the site we will apply a $75 penalty fee***</strong></p><p></p><p></p>","markdown":"Air Communities - Preston Reserve - Fitness on Demand Wi-Fi Troubleshooting\n\n**PLEASE CHECK IN / OUT WITH CIS PRO SERVICES (PHONES RING THROUGH IN THE ORDER): \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**TECHNICAL CONTACT:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**LOCAL CONTRACT:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**SOW**\n\n**We need a tech to assist in the following:**\n\n- Check in with CIS\n- Check in with TCON\n- Check in with the LCON\n- Preston Reserve has a Fitness on Demand system that needs to be connected to Wi-Fi and it keeps dropping the signal.\n- Explore whether this can be hardwired. \n  - If not please confirm connection to the Wi-Fi.\n- Take a photos of work done onsite and label photos for WO upload\n- Check out with TCON before leaving site\n- Check out with the LCON - Get Manager signature on FN Survey form\n- Check out with CIS\n\n**Equipment required**\n\n- Laptop w/Charger\n- Cell Phone w/Charger\n- Console Cable\n- Cable Tester\n- Fish Tape\n- Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- 10' Ladder\n- POTS\n\n**Materials Required:** **(Techs are responsible for providing materials unless otherwise stated in the scope)**\n\n**\\*\\*Please have extras of all the below:**\n\n- Cat6 Plenum cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat6 Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Velcro Strips\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*NOTE: ALL PHOTOS ARE REQUIRED TO BE LABELED AS TO WHAT THEY ARE BEFORE UPLOADING TO WO OR SENDING TO CIS VIA TEXT. FAILURE TO DO SO WILL RESULT IN PENTALTY FEES\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Deliverable Photos Needed:**\n\n- PHOTOS OF WORK DONE - TEXTED TO \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- WORKMAN'S COMP WAIVER (ATTACHED)\n- MANAGERS SIGN OFF (ATTACHED)\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please note if you do not call for check out before leaving the site we will apply a $75 penalty fee\\*\\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T10:00","end":"2026-10-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7.143123846118139},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793050446543}
{"job":{"id":20248135,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Printer Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Scope: Installation/replacement of 1 finisher on MX953</p><p>SN: 74666180802WG</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Instructions: </strong>If tech is onsite and has any questions, please contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com&nbsp;</p><p>Devices for password: pwrcl25 or pwrcl2025&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>PIN: 2424&nbsp;</p><p>Do not share these credentials with customers or end users.&nbsp;</p><p>Onsite exchange instructions: After an exchange/replacement, tech is to contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com&nbsp;</p><p>for call Closure on replacement.</p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:**\n\nScope: Installation/replacement of 1 finisher on MX953\n\nSN: 74666180802WG\n\n**Special Instructions:** If tech is onsite and has any questions, please contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com\n\nDevices for password: pwrcl25 or pwrcl2025\n\nPIN: 2424\n\nDo not share these credentials with customers or end users.\n\nOnsite exchange instructions: After an exchange/replacement, tech is to contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com\n\nfor call Closure on replacement.\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T09:00","end":"2026-10-28T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2.5,"distance":59.25235720556398},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793051039121}
{"job":{"id":20248431,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - Replace Cabling","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T07:00","end":"2026-10-28T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":75.63800470903696},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793051874973}
{"job":{"id":20230783,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Guest-Tek","title":"Tech required to go on site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE","description":{"html":"<p>############################################</p><p>&nbsp;### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###</p><p>&nbsp;############################################</p><p>====IMPORTANT PLEASE READ CAREFULLY=====</p><p>Technicians/TPC are required to review the Vendor Etiquette guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.</p><p>By proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.</p><p>Any non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.</p><p>Once on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)</p><p>It is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Follow these steps when onsite:</p><p>STEP#1 Contact PM Martin Salazar Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com&gt; mobile: +1 951.703.8585 TDE:Angel Camey Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com</p><p>STEP#2 if delayed after 15 min please send to Email Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com,Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com and techdispatch@guest-tek.com to CHECK IN and request a call back Refer to : USJ# USJ010414 – Sheraton Chapel Hill (RDUSC)</p><p>STEP#3 If still no answer or delay with the 15mn please call back 1-866-509-1010 EXT 8600</p><p>Please have the work order signature sheet with the paper signature by property before departure.</p><p>**NO DIGITAL SIGNATURE ALLOWED -ONLY PAPER SIGNATURE IS ACCEPTED**</p><p>All issues must be resolved before leaving site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>POINT OF CONTACT</p><p>===========================</p><p>&nbsp;GM Derick Waddell</p><p><br></p><p>TYPE OF TECHNICIAN : <strong>HSIA/Networking tech,</strong></p><p>&nbsp;PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT:</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Sheraton Chapel Hill RDUSC: We need tech to get to site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE</strong></p><p>SOW :Steps required to be completed by tech</p><p><strong>Sheraton Chapel Hill RDUSC</strong>:</p><p>Physically reset PMS Master controller onsite</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>TECHNICIAN SKILL SET</p><p>======================&nbsp;</p><p>Working with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.</p><p>- Re-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary</p><p>- Working with network equipment</p><p>- Basic knowledge of switch commands and switching</p><p>- Experience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>TECHNICIAN TOOL SET</p><p>========================</p><p>Smartphones with fully charged battery with Teams on it</p><p>Laptop with fully charged battery for testing</p><p>Spare Straight-through Cat5 patch cable for testing purposes</p><p>Cat 5 line Tester</p><p>&nbsp;Console cable</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"\\############################################\n\n ### GNOC TECHNICIAN DISPATCH INFORMATION ###\n\n ############################################\n\n====IMPORTANT PLEASE READ CAREFULLY=====\n\nTechnicians/TPC are required to review the Vendor Etiquette guidelines in full before proceeding with the visit from us.\n\nBy proceeding with any assignment from us, TPC/technician/s confirms that they have read, understood, and agreed to adhere to these guidelines at all times while working with us.\n\nAny non-compliance with the guidelines will be deemed a breach of the agreement and will result in action being taken in accordance with our standard policies.\n\nOnce on site please follow - Onsite Instructions (Mandatory Compliance)\n\nIt is mandatory to record your check in and check out when you are on a visit for us.\n\nFollow these steps when onsite:\n\nSTEP#1 Contact PM Martin Salazar Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com&gt; mobile: +1 951.703.8585 TDE:Angel Camey Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com\n\nSTEP#2 if delayed after 15 min please send to Email Martin.Salazar@guest-tek.com,Angel.Camey@guest-tek.com and techdispatch@guest-tek.com to CHECK IN and request a call back Refer to : USJ# USJ010414 – Sheraton Chapel Hill (RDUSC)\n\nSTEP#3 If still no answer or delay with the 15mn please call back 1-866-509-1010 EXT 8600\n\nPlease have the work order signature sheet with the paper signature by property before departure.\n\n\\*\\*NO DIGITAL SIGNATURE ALLOWED -ONLY PAPER SIGNATURE IS ACCEPTED\\*\\*\n\nAll issues must be resolved before leaving site.\n\nPOINT OF CONTACT\n\n===========================\n\n GM Derick Waddell\n\nTYPE OF TECHNICIAN : **HSIA/Networking tech,**\n\n PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT:\n\n**Sheraton Chapel Hill RDUSC: We need tech to get to site and help us identify the PMS system onsite and reset the PMS. This will be done over a team’s call with TDE**\n\nSOW :Steps required to be completed by tech\n\n**Sheraton Chapel Hill RDUSC**:\n\nPhysically reset PMS Master controller onsite\n\nTECHNICIAN SKILL SET\n\n======================\n\nWorking with cat5 cabling, testing the quality of the lines, checking cabling ends.\n\n\\- Re-crimping RJ45 ends if necessary\n\n\\- Working with network equipment\n\n\\- Basic knowledge of switch commands and switching\n\n\\- Experience with structured cabling (diagnose and installation\n\nTECHNICIAN TOOL SET\n\n========================\n\nSmartphones with fully charged battery with Teams on it\n\nLaptop with fully charged battery for testing\n\nSpare Straight-through Cat5 patch cable for testing purposes\n\nCat 5 line Tester\n\n Console cable","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-26T10:30","end":"2026-10-26T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":15.957928809593737},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/26/2026, 10:30:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-26T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-26T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-26T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"Family"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:0