{"job":{"id":20248858,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"Store IT/POS Equipment -test and validate the operational ability of all RIS equipment (Precheck/T-5 testing)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview: Ensure the stores readiness before handing the store over to 7-11 personel. We will need to test and validate the operations of all RIS equipment.</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in basic electronic installation. Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale experience.</li><li>A detailed guide is provided to the assigned provider</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1 hour</li></ul><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Pre-Site Requirements&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Check you are at the store number situated on your work request.</li><li>The store number can be situated on the front window of the Store, on the off chance that you don't discover the store number posted, ask store staff,General Contractor, or Field Consultant on location.</li><li>If no one onsite or unable to confirm, please contact the Deployment Support Team at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************ ***** ****************</del></span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>On-Site Tasks (Overview- Step by step process attached in the document section of the work order)</strong></p><p><strong>Objectives</strong></p><p>Back Office Validations</p><ul><li>Multi-Function Printer is operational</li><li>Chromebox online, keyboard and mouse are functional</li></ul><p>Wireless Validations</p><ul><li>7MD connected to wireless and apps downloaded.</li><li>7MD scanning functionality</li><li>Point of Sale Validations on each (POS)</li></ul><p>Login to POS</p><ul><li>Valid 7Rewards scan</li><li>Valid POS scan item</li><li>Valid age restriction prompts on POS (photo of each POS)</li><li>Valid debit test with incorrect pin</li><li>Valid POS receipt print</li><li>Validate cash drawer opens</li><li>Validate MOM is online</li></ul><p><strong>Testing time frames</strong></p><p>Back office &ndash; 10 minutes</p><ul><li>Confirm functionality of ISP (Chrome Box) peripherals, proper cable management, and back office setup, test copy or scan function on Lexmark printer.</li></ul><p>Mobility &ndash; 30 minutes <strong>Notify DST if taking any longer.</strong></p><ul><li>Verifying that the wireless devices are working.</li></ul><p>POS’ &ndash; 10 minutes (5 per POS)</p><p>MOM &ndash; 10 minutes</p><ul><li>Confirm with DST that MOM is online.</li></ul><p><strong>Required On-Site</strong></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Picture of all 7MDs showing scanned item.</li><li>Picture of each POS screen showing member transaction (7rewards) and age verification screen</li><li>Photo of each POS receipt prints.</li><li>Photo of each POS cash drawer open</li><li>Photo of POSs from customer side of counter.</li><li>Photo of MOM terminal id page</li><li>Photo of MOM LAN status page</li><li>Photo of MOM installed, showing cable management</li><li>Photo of back office desk</li><li>Photo of Chrome box mounted to back of monitor stand</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;Additional Contacts:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>NEC Deployment Support team<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del> ************ **** *</del></span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****************</del></span></p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Tools or Parts Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Debit card (for testing of EFT devices, no charges will be processed)</li><li>Cell phone with camera</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><p>Work order questions- contact work order manager <strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ******* ************</del></strong></p><p>Contact NEC Deployment Sup</p><ul><li>&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿Please read below.</strong></p><p><strong>Call Before Starting Work:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure you call the provided number,&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong><strong>, before commencing any work. Hours of operation are 7:00 am - 7:00 pm CST, there will be no support outside of these hours therefore will not be able to checkin prior to 7am CST.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-In for Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will provide a&nbsp;<strong>check-in number, marking the official start of your work for timekeeping purposes.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-Out to End Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;When your work is&nbsp;<strong>finished, contact the agent again to obtain a check-out number, signifying the official end of your work.</strong></p><p><strong>*********** MAKE SURE ALL WORK IS COMPLETE (INCLUDING SITE CLEANUP) BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH DST AS THAT WILL BE TIME OF RECORD - WE WANT TO AVOID TIME DISCREPANCIES FOR PAYMENT APPROVAL. **********</strong></p><p><strong>Record Based on Agent Timestamps:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will record the&nbsp;<strong>timestamps for both check-in and check-out, serving as the official record of your work duration.</strong></p><p><strong>Include Codes in Work Order:</strong>&nbsp;Remember to incorporate these check-in and check-out codes into your work order to ensure approval for payment.</p><p>By following these guidelines, you'll guarantee accurate timekeeping and a smooth approval process for your work order.</p><p><strong><u>Turn away fee:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>In the event of a site turn away</u></strong>&nbsp;(Something wrong when arriving at store that prevents our install - some examples: network down, equipment lost, store refusing install, no power) provider will be paid a $50 cancellation fee, and will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future.&nbsp;Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue.&nbsp;DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release.&nbsp;Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.</p><p><strong>Readiness Policy:&nbsp;</strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>On My Way:&nbsp;</strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</p><p><strong>Arriving Late:</strong>&nbsp;All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</p><p><strong>Changing Resources:</strong>&nbsp;By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Expense Approval:</strong>&nbsp;Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</p><p><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong>&nbsp;If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order.</p><p><strong>Out-of-Scope Work:&nbsp;</strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the scope stated above, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid at <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order.</p><p><strong>Returning Parts:</strong>&nbsp;Return Waybills will be found in the original package the part was shipped to you in. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is being tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</p>","markdown":"**Overview: Ensure the stores readiness before handing the store over to 7-11 personel. We will need to test and validate the operations of all RIS equipment.**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in basic electronic installation. Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale experience.\n- A detailed guide is provided to the assigned provider\n- Estimated duration will be 1 hour\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nPre-Site Requirements\n\n- Check you are at the store number situated on your work request.\n- The store number can be situated on the front window of the Store, on the off chance that you don't discover the store number posted, ask store staff,General Contractor, or Field Consultant on location.\n- If no one onsite or unable to confirm, please contact the Deployment Support Team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **On-Site Tasks (Overview- Step by step process attached in the document section of the work order)**\n\n**Objectives**\n\nBack Office Validations\n\n- Multi-Function Printer is operational\n- Chromebox online, keyboard and mouse are functional\n\nWireless Validations\n\n- 7MD connected to wireless and apps downloaded.\n- 7MD scanning functionality\n- Point of Sale Validations on each (POS)\n\nLogin to POS\n\n- Valid 7Rewards scan\n- Valid POS scan item\n- Valid age restriction prompts on POS (photo of each POS)\n- Valid debit test with incorrect pin\n- Valid POS receipt print\n- Validate cash drawer opens\n- Validate MOM is online\n\n**Testing time frames**\n\nBack office – 10 minutes\n\n- Confirm functionality of ISP (Chrome Box) peripherals, proper cable management, and back office setup, test copy or scan function on Lexmark printer.\n\nMobility – 30 minutes **Notify DST if taking any longer.**\n\n- Verifying that the wireless devices are working.\n\nPOS’ – 10 minutes (5 per POS)\n\nMOM – 10 minutes\n\n- Confirm with DST that MOM is online.\n\n**Required On-Site**\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Picture of all 7MDs showing scanned item.\n- Picture of each POS screen showing member transaction (7rewards) and age verification screen\n- Photo of each POS receipt prints.\n- Photo of each POS cash drawer open\n- Photo of POSs from customer side of counter.\n- Photo of MOM terminal id page\n- Photo of MOM LAN status page\n- Photo of MOM installed, showing cable management\n- Photo of back office desk\n- Photo of Chrome box mounted to back of monitor stand\n\n **Additional Contacts:**\n\n- NEC Deployment Support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **Tools or Parts Required:**\n\n- Debit card (for testing of EFT devices, no charges will be processed)\n- Cell phone with camera\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nWork order questions- contact work order manager **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nContact NEC Deployment Sup\n\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\***\n\n**﻿Please read below.**\n\n**Call Before Starting Work:** Ensure you call the provided number, **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*****, before commencing any work. Hours of operation are 7:00 am - 7:00 pm CST, there will be no support outside of these hours therefore will not be able to checkin prior to 7am CST.**\n\n**Check-In for Time Tracking:** The agent will provide a **check-in number, marking the official start of your work for timekeeping purposes.**\n\n**Check-Out to End Time Tracking:** When your work is **finished, contact the agent again to obtain a check-out number, signifying the official end of your work.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* MAKE SURE ALL WORK IS COMPLETE (INCLUDING SITE CLEANUP) BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH DST AS THAT WILL BE TIME OF RECORD - WE WANT TO AVOID TIME DISCREPANCIES FOR PAYMENT APPROVAL. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Record Based on Agent Timestamps:** The agent will record the **timestamps for both check-in and check-out, serving as the official record of your work duration.**\n\n**Include Codes in Work Order:** Remember to incorporate these check-in and check-out codes into your work order to ensure approval for payment.\n\nBy following these guidelines, you'll guarantee accurate timekeeping and a smooth approval process for your work order.\n\n**Turn away fee:**\n\n**In the event of a site turn away** (Something wrong when arriving at store that prevents our install - some examples: network down, equipment lost, store refusing install, no power) provider will be paid a $50 cancellation fee, and will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future. Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue. DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release. Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.\n\n**Readiness Policy:** The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted. Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.\n\n**On My Way:** When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.\n\n**Arriving Late:** All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order. Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.\n\n**Changing Resources:** By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.\n\n**Dress Code:** Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n**Expense Approval:** Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.\n\n**Additional Time On-site:** If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n\n**Out-of-Scope Work:** If you are asked to perform work beyond the scope stated above, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident. Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid at $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n\n**Returning Parts:** Return Waybills will be found in the original package the part was shipped to you in. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is being tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T10:30","latestStart":"2026-10-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":52.39623904696166},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & e