{"job":{"id":20249187,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK | Sheetz 505 | 1895 S FRANKLIN ST Printer Troubleshoot","description":{"html":"<p>This work order is to get our customer back up and running without the need for replacement parts while training onsite staff to resolve printer issues themselves.</p><p><br></p><p>Only accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.</p><p><strong>Must call Work Order Manager to check in and check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>This is a printer troubleshooting/ cleaning WO. No parts will be shipped. Please be sure to bring everything listed in the required tools list below. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>-</strong><u>Required Tools</u><strong>:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard Tool Set</li><li>Nut Drivers or Socket Set</li><li>Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</li><li>A to B USB Cable</li><li>Compressed air/Canned Air</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Cleaning Tools</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cotton swab</li><li>Lint-free cloth</li><li>Brush with soft non-metallic bristles</li><li>Small vacuum cleaner (for debris removal)</li><li>75% Ethanol (for disinfecting)</li><li>99% Isopropyl alcohol (for printhead and platen roller cleaning)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>There are three printers in total across the ARK fleet. Documentation is attached to the work order for each of the different printers you may find on site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Check in with Work Order Manager</strong></li><li>Obtain Keys from site and open up the display cabinet.</li><li>Determine printer type and reference correct documentation.</li><li>Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, and clean as needed.</li><li>Check status light on printer or if the printer is paused.</li><li>Make sure paper is loaded properly.</li><li>Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip.</li><li>Check USB cable to Printer and to PC.</li><li>Call Technical Support to report your findings and to troubleshoot further if needed (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)</li><li><strong>Call Work Order Manager to check out</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.</p><p>346 S Arthur Ave.</p><p>Louisville, CO 80027</p>","markdown":"This work order is to get our customer back up and running without the need for replacement parts while training onsite staff to resolve printer issues themselves.\n\nOnly accept the work order if you can be there in the time allotted.\n\n**Must call Work Order Manager to check in and check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**This is a printer troubleshooting/ cleaning WO. No parts will be shipped. Please be sure to bring everything listed in the required tools list below.**\n\n**-**Required Tools**:**\n\n- Standard Tool Set\n- Nut Drivers or Socket Set\n- Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth\n- A to B USB Cable\n- Compressed air/Canned Air\n\n**Cleaning Tools**\n\n- Cotton swab\n- Lint-free cloth\n- Brush with soft non-metallic bristles\n- Small vacuum cleaner (for debris removal)\n- 75% Ethanol (for disinfecting)\n- 99% Isopropyl alcohol (for printhead and platen roller cleaning)\n\n**There are three printers in total across the ARK fleet. Documentation is attached to the work order for each of the different printers you may find on site.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n- **Check in with Work Order Manager**\n- Obtain Keys from site and open up the display cabinet.\n- Determine printer type and reference correct documentation.\n- Check for jams, broken plastic, dislodged blades, and clean as needed.\n- Check status light on printer or if the printer is paused.\n- Make sure paper is loaded properly.\n- Check power cable is properly connected to printer, ac adapter and to power strip.\n- Check USB cable to Printer and to PC.\n- Call Technical Support to report your findings and to troubleshoot further if needed (Pictures uploaded before calling is appreciated)\n- **Call Work Order Manager to check out**\n\nCompany: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.\n\n346 S Arthur Ave.\n\nLouisville, CO 80027","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T10:00","end":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.25,"distance":13.959915927806517},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-27T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM