{"job":{"id":20249513,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"Revisit to install cabling and equipment after cutover  (2 techs cabling anticipated) - Lead and Assist ticket","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p><strong>When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</strong></p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p><strong>*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</strong></p><p><strong>*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</strong></p><p><strong>*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</strong></p><p><strong><u>This is a 2 tech ticket</u></strong> to rectify the cabling after a recent cutover.  Site needs all devices online and the below devices could not be completed during cutover.  Onsite cable status is unknown so please be prepared with cable if required.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>This is a 2 tech ticket to rectify the cabling in place or install new cabling to get outstanding equipment needed for the business online.  This cutover occured last night and we need a team ASAP to perform cabling and installation tasks detailed below.  Techs to provide cabling materials.  </p><p>&nbsp;- Run printer lines (2 printers)</p><p>&nbsp;- Run computer lines (3 computers if phones need lines total of 6 runs)</p><p>&nbsp;- Run new line for alarm panel (1 run)</p><p>&nbsp;- Set up phones and potentially run new lines (should go to PC locations.  May be able to reuse existing cabling.)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):</strong></p><ul><li>Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic PC Tool Kit</li><li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li><li><strong><u>10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable</u></strong></li><li>Cabling Materials</li></ul><p>----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cabling Support Materials</li></ul><p>----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...</p><ul><li>Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete</li><li>Drywall Anchors and Screws</li><li>Toggle Bolts</li><li>Velcro&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Ties</li><li>Spare Patch Cables</li><li>Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)</li><li>SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>High Level Deployment Instructions:</strong></p><p><strong><em>For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964</li></ul><p>----<strong><em>Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Deployment Specialist&nbsp;</li></ul><p>----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template</p><p>----You will work directly with your assigned <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to complete the installation</p><ul><li>Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos</li><li>Install Network Rack Equipment</li></ul><p>----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch</p><p>----You will need to work with you <del>*****</del> IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem</p><ul><li>Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)</li></ul><p>----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed</p><p>----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs</p><p>----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important</p><ul><li>Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity</li><li>Install Multifunction Printer&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Install i-Gel Cubics PCs</li><li>Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)</li><li>Install Cameras</li><li>Complete TDX Work Order Form</li><li>Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order</li><li>Check Out with <del>*****</del> IT Specialist&nbsp;</li><li>Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk</li></ul><p><strong>If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review. </strong></p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\n**When requesting this ticket, all potential travel expenses need to be countered when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:**\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any additions for travel after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n**\\*ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ON-SITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\***\n\n**\\*IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS ' PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\***\n\n**\\*TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\***\n\n**This is a 2 tech ticket** to rectify the cabling after a recent cutover. Site needs all devices online and the below devices could not be completed during cutover. Onsite cable status is unknown so please be prepared with cable if required.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nThis is a 2 tech ticket to rectify the cabling in place or install new cabling to get outstanding equipment needed for the business online. This cutover occured last night and we need a team ASAP to perform cabling and installation tasks detailed below. Techs to provide cabling materials.\n\n\\- Run printer lines (2 printers)\n\n\\- Run computer lines (3 computers if phones need lines total of 6 runs)\n\n\\- Run new line for alarm panel (1 run)\n\n\\- Set up phones and potentially run new lines (should go to PC locations. May be able to reuse existing cabling.)\n\n**Tool Requirements (Consumables Will Be Reimbursed):**\n\n- Smart Phone with Charger or External Battery\n- Laptop\n- Basic PC Tool Kit\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- **10 to 12 Foot Ladder (No Lift Available)**\n- **2000 Feet of Plenum Rated Cat 6 Cable**\n- Cabling Materials\n\n\\----Keystone Jacks, SMBs, Biscuits, Etc...\n\n- Cabling Support Materials\n\n\\----J Hooks, Arlington Loops, Etc...\n\n- Cable Tester (Continuity or Analyzer - Certification Not Required)\n- Label Maker\n- Tape Measure\n- Tapcons for Mounting to Concrete\n- Drywall Anchors and Screws\n- Toggle Bolts\n- Velcro\n- Cable Ties\n- Spare Patch Cables\n- Phillips, Torque and Slotted Screwdrivers (Phillips #0, #1, #2 and straight blade 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch)\n- SDS Impact Drill and Standard Drill (Wood and Masonry Bits).\n\n**High Level Deployment Instructions:**\n\n***For Detailed Step-by-Step Instructions Please Refer to the Current Deployment Runbook in the Client Documents Section***\n\n- Check in with the TDX Tech help desk at (952) 777-3964\n\n\\----***Throughout the installation, please report any major delays, issues, or concerns to TDX immediately as they arise***\n\n- Check in with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Deployment Specialist\n\n\\----This can be found under the Contacts section of the Field Nation Template\n\n\\----You will work directly with your assigned \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to complete the installation\n\n- Verify Inventory and Mac Addresses with Photos\n- Install Network Rack Equipment\n\n\\----UPS, Peplink Modem, SonicWall, and Network Switch\n\n\\----You will need to work with you \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist to determine the best location for the Peplink Modem\n\n- Network Cable Runs (Run, Test and Label)\n\n\\----Confirm existing runs that can be reused, and run any new cable runs needed\n\n\\----Expect to run form 6 to 10 new cable runs\n\n\\----Devices are port specific so labeling is extremely important\n\n- Install Access Points and Confirm Connectivity\n- Install Multifunction Printer\n- Install i-Gel Cubics PCs\n- Install Tablets (At least 2 per site)\n- Install Cameras\n- Complete TDX Work Order Form\n- Upload All Picture to TDX Work Order\n- Check Out with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* IT Specialist\n- Check Out with TDX Tech Help Desk\n\n**If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be uploaded to the Field Nation immediately for TDX Review.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":120,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.563121328532345},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Oct 27, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 27, Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.0