{"job":{"id":20250450,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"2 doors stopped working","description":{"html":"<p><strong>1. Scope of Work</strong></p><p>The technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.</p><p><strong><em><u>Scope of Work as follows:</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Get with Z and fix 2 doors that stopped working since last visit.</p><p><strong>Task Sequence:</strong></p><ol><li>Confirm scheduled work <strong>24 hours prior</strong> and again <strong>1 hour prior</strong> to site arrival.</li><li>Upon arrival, <strong>call or text the Work Order Manager</strong> to check in.</li><li><strong>Make contact with the Local Contact</strong> and confirm site access and work area.</li><li><strong>Locate required parts and equipment</strong> as outlined in the work order.</li><li>Take <strong>BEFORE photos</strong> of all work areas and existing equipment.</li><li><strong>Check in with IT Support</strong> prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.</li><li><strong>Complete the work as specified</strong> in the work order or project documentation.</li><li>Take <strong>AFTER photos</strong> of completed work.</li><li><strong>Test and verify functionality</strong> with IT Support (checkout process).</li><li><strong>Clean up</strong> all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.</li><li>Enter <strong>detailed closeout notes</strong> describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.</li><li>Upload and attach <strong>all required photo deliverables</strong> (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).</li><li><strong>Checkout with Work Order Manager</strong> before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Tools and Equipment Required</strong></p><p>Technician must have the following tools available onsite to complete the work:</p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cables</li><li>Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity</li><li>Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)</li><li>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</li><li>Ladder (as needed for access)</li><li>Cable tester</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>3. Deliverables Required</strong></p><p>The following deliverables are required for successful completion of the work order:</p><ul><li><strong>BEFORE photos</strong> of all work areas</li><li><strong>AFTER photos</strong> of all completed work</li><li><strong>Any additional photos</strong> specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support</li><li><strong>Detailed closeout notes</strong> summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>4. Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><p>Work will be considered complete when:</p><ul><li>All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.</li><li>IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.</li><li>All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.</li><li>The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.</li></ul>","markdown":"**1. Scope of Work**\n\nThe technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.\n\n***Scope of Work as follows:***\n\nGet with Z and fix 2 doors that stopped working since last visit.\n\n**Task Sequence:**\n\n1. Confirm scheduled work **24 hours prior** and again **1 hour prior** to site arrival.\n2. Upon arrival, **call or text the Work Order Manager** to check in.\n3. **Make contact with the Local Contact** and confirm site access and work area.\n4. **Locate required parts and equipment** as outlined in the work order.\n5. Take **BEFORE photos** of all work areas and existing equipment.\n6. **Check in with IT Support** prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.\n7. **Complete the work as specified** in the work order or project documentation.\n8. Take **AFTER photos** of completed work.\n9. **Test and verify functionality** with IT Support (checkout process).\n10. **Clean up** all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.\n11. Enter **detailed closeout notes** describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.\n12. Upload and attach **all required photo deliverables** (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).\n13. **Checkout with Work Order Manager** before leaving the site.\n\n**2. Tools and Equipment Required**\n\nTechnician must have the following tools available onsite to complete the work:\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cables\n- Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity\n- Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n- Ladder (as needed for access)\n- Cable tester\n\n**3. Deliverables Required**\n\nThe following deliverables are required for successful completion of the work order:\n\n- **BEFORE photos** of all work areas\n- **AFTER photos** of all completed work\n- **Any additional photos** specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support\n- **Detailed closeout notes** summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations\n\n**4. Acceptance Criteria**\n\nWork will be considered complete when:\n\n- All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.\n- IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.\n- All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.\n- The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.061107898858155},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"To