{"job":{"id":20251739,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Dispatch - FIVE BELOW - Five Below- Store #8321 - 3130 Halifax Rd, South Boston, VA 24592","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*******CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! ********</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>5G DISPATCH REQUEST<br />\n<br />\nAddress:<br />\n3130 Halifax Rd.<br />\nSouth Boston, VA 24592<br />\n<br />\nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #8321<br />\n<br />\nDispatch date/time: Tuesday, 10/27/26, Arriving by 10am local time<br />\n<br />\nONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION<br />\nLCON Name: Site manager<br />\n<br />\nWe are installing a 5G Cradlepoint device. This device has DUAL SIMS on it- We will need to test the CP 1st with the SIM that is in Slot 1 (TMB) and then test with the SIM that is in SLOT 2 (ATT). Our task will be to locate that device, connect it to our laptop and test it for speed and ping response. Then, we will re-test it once more after 10 minutes. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.<br />\n<br />\nPing test 100 times and get the percentage.<br />\n<br />\n1.Enter the command as follows: ping -n 100 1.1.1.1. ping = The command to ping, leave unchanged. ...<br />\n2.Check the summary when completed for percentage of packet loss.<br />\n<br />\nRun speed test once, document speed and ms response time<br />\nRun speed test 10 minutes later and document the same.<br />\n<br />\nAnything over 120ms response and below 5M download will need to be installed as the backup connection on the customer meraki. When reaching out to Five Below IT, please inform them if the circuit is below this threshold and request we install this device as the backup connection on their Meraki<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS<br />\n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at 206.494.6399<br />\n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.<br />\n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.<br />\n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 250 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), <strong>350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools</strong>. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <strong>206-494-6399</strong></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email <strong>turnups@sangoma.com</strong> with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call <strong>206-494-6399</strong>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n5G DISPATCH REQUEST  \n  \nAddress:  \n3130 Halifax Rd.  \nSouth Boston, VA 24592  \n  \nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #8321  \n  \nDispatch date/time: Tuesday, 10/27/26, Arriving by 10am local time  \n  \nONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION  \nLCON Name: Site manager  \n  \nWe are installing a 5G Cradlepoint device. This device has DUAL SIMS on it- We will need to test the CP 1st with the SIM that is in Slot 1 (TMB) and then test with the SIM that is in SLOT 2 (ATT). Our task will be to locate that device, connect it to our laptop and test it for speed and ping response. Then, we will re-test it once more after 10 minutes. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.  \n  \nPing test 100 times and get the percentage.  \n  \n1.Enter the command as follows: ping -n 100 1.1.1.1. ping = The command to ping, leave unchanged. ...  \n2.Check the summary when completed for percentage of packet loss.  \n  \nRun speed test once, document speed and ms response time  \nRun speed test 10 minutes later and document the same.  \n  \nAnything over 120ms response and below 5M download will need to be installed as the backup connection on the customer meraki. When reaching out to Five Below IT, please inform them if the circuit is below this threshold and request we install this device as the backup connection on their Meraki  \n  \n  \nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS  \n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at 206.494.6399  \n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.  \n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.  \n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 250 ft of cat 5e, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), **350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools**. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at **206-494-6399**\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email **turnups@sangoma.com** with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call **206-494-6399**with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.634871867292475},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Oct 27, 1:00 PM\nChecked: Tue, Oct 27, Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00