and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.&nbsp;</li><li>The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><em><u>READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Escalation Process: </strong>If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li><strong>Readiness Policy: </strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>On My Way: </strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</li><li><strong>Arriving Late:</strong> All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</li><li><strong>Changing Resources:</strong> By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</li><li><strong>Expense Approval:</strong> Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</li><li><strong>Wait Time: </strong>If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.</li><li><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong> If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Out-of-Scope Work: </strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Returning Parts:</strong> Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"***NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion***\n\n**Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.**\n\n- You will represent yourself as an \\*\\*\\* Representative\n- INC# and FWKD# in the work order information\n- **Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order**.\n- Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.\n- The defective part must be r