{"job":{"id":20252649,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"Replace the POS Unit for POS 03 - est. < 2 hrs onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.</strong></p><ul><li>You will represent yourself as an <del>***</del> Representative</li><li>INC# and FWKD# in the work order information</li><li><strong><u>Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order</u></strong>.</li><li>Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.</li><li>The defective part must be returned in the box with the&nbsp;provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.</li><li>Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.</li><li>Drop the return package off at UPS store.</li><li>If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.</li><li>Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.</li><li>Must Check In/Out with <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li>Must take before and after photos of the unit</li><li>Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTES:</strong></p><ol><li>Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!&nbsp;</li><li>Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.&nbsp;</li><li>Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.&nbsp;</li><li>All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.&nbsp;</li><li>Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.&nbsp;</li><li>The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><em><u>READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Escalation Process: </strong>If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li><strong>Readiness Policy: </strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>On My Way: </strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</li><li><strong>Arriving Late:</strong> All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</li><li><strong>Changing Resources:</strong> By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</li><li><strong>Expense Approval:</strong> Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</li><li><strong>Wait Time: </strong>If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.</li><li><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong> If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Out-of-Scope Work: </strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Returning Parts:</strong> Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"***NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion***\n\n**Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.**\n\n- You will represent yourself as an \\*\\*\\* Representative\n- INC# and FWKD# in the work order information\n- **Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order**.\n- Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.\n- The defective part must be returned in the box with the provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.\n- Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.\n- Drop the return package off at UPS store.\n- If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.\n- Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.\n- Must Check In/Out with \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Must take before and after photos of the unit\n- Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n\n1. Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!\n2. Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.\n3. Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.\n4. All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.\n5. Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.\n6. The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.\n\n***READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order***\n\n- **Escalation Process:** If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Readiness Policy:** The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted. Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.\n- **On My Way:** When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.\n- **Arriving Late:** All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order. Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.\n- **Changing Resources:** By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.\n- **Dress Code:** Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n- **Expense Approval:** Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.\n- **Wait Time:** If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.\n- **Additional Time On-site:** If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.\n- **Out-of-Scope Work:** If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident. Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n- **Returning Parts:** Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T15:30","end":"2026-10-27T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":205,"max":205},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":53.41424471058918},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793120065466}
{"job":{"id":20251871,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 236","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13187204</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13187204\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T09:00","end":"2026-10-27T10:00","latestStart":"2026-10-27T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8.519777726341644},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T21:30:00.000Z","summary":"BirthDay"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16