{"job":{"id":20253437,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #304828 - (STRSPRT-1768725) 1851 - FortiExtender Not Mounted","description":{"html":"<p>****TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY</p><p>BEFORE GOING TO SITE AND ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS.&nbsp; *********</p><p>Tech must call TRCA at 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with our OST department.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>The scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please dispatch a technician to store 1851 as the FortiExtender in the manager's office has not been installed in the proper location.&nbsp; It currently shows to be sitting in the rack mount but it will need to be installed on the wall behind the rack mount to the Left or Right as high as possible with the antenna's positioned properly.&nbsp; I have added an image of the rack mount with the device and the possible places it can be installed, as well as the SOW for this part.</p><p>The due date for service is 10/31/2026.</p><p>Please have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Documentation</strong>:</p><p>Document all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.</p><p>Maintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Take pictures of completed work at various angles.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Submit pictures for the following areas:</p><p>-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)</p><p>-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office</p><p>-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office</p><p>-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)</p><p>-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area</p><p>Confirm the following:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)</p><p>-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:</p><p># of pin pads</p><p># of thin client terminals</p><p># of laser printers</p><p># of thermal printers</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician is responsible for:</strong></p><p>Providing all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Ensuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to safety guidelines and protocols.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Completing the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Promptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Conducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Collaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Communicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Adhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Maintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>To Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :</strong></p><p><strong>In addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.</strong></p><p><strong>IF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.</strong></p><p><strong>*******************</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Before leaving site, call O'Reilly Help Desk at:</strong></p><p><strong>417-427-1313 to confirm all connectivity on the network.</strong></p><p><strong>Tech must have with him/her onsite in case any repairs need to be made.</strong></p><p><strong>8' ladder</strong>                    </p><p><strong>Cable tester</strong>                     </p><p><strong>RJ45 jacks</strong></p><p><strong>White CAT5 cable</strong></p><p><strong>Orange yellow and/or blue patch cables</strong>                                </p><p><strong>Take before &amp; after photos and submit to TRCA before leaving site*</strong></p><p><strong>Label Maker - DO NOT USE A SHARPIE OR PEN WHEN LABELING</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*\\*TECH IS TO READ OVER WORK ORDER, AND ANY ADDITIONAL PAPERWORK THOROUGHLY\n\nBEFORE GOING TO SITE AND ASK TRCA ANY QUESTIONS HE/SHE HAS. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTech must call TRCA at 855-278-0090 while onsite to check in and out with our OST department.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nThe scope of work for the technician includes, but is not limited to, the following tasks:\n\nPlease dispatch a technician to store 1851 as the FortiExtender in the manager's office has not been installed in the proper location. It currently shows to be sitting in the rack mount but it will need to be installed on the wall behind the rack mount to the Left or Right as high as possible with the antenna's positioned properly. I have added an image of the rack mount with the device and the possible places it can be installed, as well as the SOW for this part.\n\nThe due date for service is 10/31/2026.\n\nPlease have the technician contact IT Support before leaving the store so we can verify that the work has been completed.\n\n **Documentation**:\n\nDocument all work performed, including repairs made and parts replaced.\n\nMaintain an updated log of maintenance tasks and repairs conducted.\n\nTake pictures of completed work at various angles.\n\nSubmit pictures for the following areas:\n\n-Any work performed while on site (before/after pictures)\n\n-Computer Equipment in the Manager’s office\n\n-Take pictures of the rack/cabling and hardware in the office\n\n-Phone board (Demarc and external provider equipment)\n\n-If switches are at the front counter-pictures of this area\n\nConfirm the following:\n\n-Is the Battery Backup set up? (server and switches are terminated to the BBU)\n\n-Are all devices in the store active? Please confirm the quantity of each of the following:\n\n\\# of pin pads\n\n\\# of thin client terminals\n\n\\# of laser printers\n\n\\# of thermal printers\n\n**The technician is responsible for:**\n\nProviding all necessary tools and equipment to perform the break/fix work. (see material list)\n\nEnsuring the quality and accuracy of repairs.\n\nAdhering to safety guidelines and protocols.\n\nCompleting the attached O’Reilly Tech (Smart Hands) Check Out List for Break/Fix Dispatches (see attachment)\n\nPromptly reporting any additional repairs or replacements required beyond the initial assessment to their support desk and obtaining approval before proceeding with the work.\n\nConducting a thorough assessment of the store's equipment and systems to identify any potential issues or areas requiring maintenance beyond the reported problems.\n\nCollaborating with store managers or staff to gather additional information about technical issues or observed concerns.\n\nCommunicating effectively with store managers or designated point of contact to provide updates on the progress of repairs and any required follow-up actions.\n\nAdhering to established timelines and response times for addressing technical issues in order to minimize disruption to store operations.\n\nMaintaining professionalism and a customer-oriented approach while interacting with O'Reilly Auto Parts, store staff, customers, and other stakeholders involved in the process.\n\n**To Add to all O’Reilly Ticket request SOW :**\n\n**In addition to the Scope of Work below, TRCA Tech will need to walk through the store and locate any unmanaged switches the site might have located at the Front counter, back of the house counters (ISS, HUB, Paint, Test Bench) and Phone board.**\n\n**IF the site does have an unmanaged switch, TRCA must work to remove the unmanaged switch by rerouting or re-pulling the cables to the nearest meraki switch located at the front counter or office.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Before leaving site, call O'Reilly Help Desk at:**\n\n**417-427-1313 to confirm all connectivity on the network.**\n\n**Tech must have with him/her onsite in case any repairs need to be made.**\n\n**8' ladder**\n\n**Cable tester**\n\n**RJ45 jacks**\n\n**White CAT5 cable**\n\n**Orange yellow and/or blue patch cables**\n\n**Take before &amp; after photos and submit to TRCA before leaving site\\***\n\n**Label Maker - DO NOT USE A SHARPIE OR PEN WHEN LABELING**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T08:00","end":"2026-10-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":40.23094092598303},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/27/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"avai