{"job":{"id":20253810,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Solari Service","title":"Remove Wall Display - Raleigh, NC, 27609","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>We will need two techs in the morning to remove the display from the wall to allow the Samsung tech to work on display.&nbsp;<span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></p><p><strong>General Instructions </strong></p><p>• Partner MUST call Cenero Technical Support number above to \"check-in\" upon arrival at the client’s location and \"check-out\" upon completion of work. </p><p>• Download the Technician Software to engage Cenero Support for assistance while you are onsite. </p><p>• Sign-off is required at the completion of the service call. </p><p>• Upload this completed Work Order Resolution Summary, including images, if applicable.&nbsp; </p><p>• If RMA or site follow up visit is required, be sure to indicate it in the Work Order Resolution Summary. (Please note- Contact Cenero support to notify them of RMA- RMA will need to be generated in Cenero’s name and include a designated Cenero contact person)</p><p>• For ALL issues that may arise- please engage the Cenero support team before discussing with the onsite contact.&nbsp; </p><p>• Techs must reach out to Cenero support at 4 hours to determine if they are able to proceed with service.&nbsp; &nbsp; </p><p>• Tech will need a laptop (w/charger) and a Hardwired Ethernet Connection or USB to Gigabit Ethernet adapter.&nbsp; Laptops need to be running Windows 10/11.&nbsp; No Mac or Linux computers should be used. </p><p>• Tech should have a Wi-Fi hotspot available in the event that it is not possible to connect via client network. </p><p>• If performing preventative maintenance, please confirm that all documents have been received by Cenero when checking out from site.&nbsp; </p><p><strong>Technician Software Requirements </strong></p><p>• Team Viewer (https://www.teamviewer.com/en/download/windows/) </p><p>• Crestron Toolbox </p><p>• Biamp Tesira </p><p>• Q-sys Designer (latest version if no version is specified </p><p>• Modern Web Browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, etc.) </p><p>• Any additional software specified by Cenero prior to date of scheduled service call. </p><p><strong>Please note- failure to follow these guidelines can result in payment refusal.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Terms and Conditions:</strong></p><p>Check-In / Check-Out Requirements</p><ul><li>Technician must check in and check out through the Field Nation platform.</li><li>Technician must remain onsite for the full approved service duration unless otherwise instructed by the Work Order Manager.</li><li>GPS and timestamp verification may be required.</li></ul><p>Communication Requirements</p><ul><li>Technician must maintain active communication before, during, and after the service event.</li><li>Technician must respond to calls/messages from dispatch or project management in a timely manner.</li><li>Failure to communicate delays, issues, or inability to complete work may result in reduced ratings and payment disputes.</li></ul><p>Arrival &amp; Professional Conduct</p><ul><li>Technician must arrive on time and dressed professionally.</li><li>Technician must behave respectfully toward store staff, customers, and management at all times.</li><li>Smoking, inappropriate language, harassment, or unprofessional behavior onsite will not be tolerated.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Photos &amp; Deliverables</p><p>Technician must upload all required deliverables before leaving site, including:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Asset labels/serial numbers</li><li>Cable routing photos</li><li>Speed tests or screenshots if applicable</li><li>Manager/customer sign-off where required</li><li>Detailed completion notes</li></ul><p>Blurry or incomplete documentation may delay approval and payment.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cabling Work</p><ul><li>No cabling work should be performed without prior approval if additional material or extended cable runs are required.</li><li>Technician must immediately notify the project manager if materials onsite are insufficient.</li><li>Partial or temporary cable runs should not be completed unless specifically approved.</li></ul><p>Escalation Procedure</p><p>Technician must immediately escalate:</p><ul><li>Missing equipment</li><li>Incorrect parts</li><li>Site access issues</li><li>Network outages</li><li>Unsafe conditions</li><li>Scope changes</li><li>Any issue preventing completion</li></ul><p>Unauthorized scope changes may not be compensated.</p><p><br></p><p>Safety Compliance</p><p>Technician agrees to follow all local safety regulations and site-specific safety requirements.</p><p>Technician is responsible for using ladders, electrical equipment, and tools safely.</p><p><br></p><p>Payment Terms</p><ul><li>Payment will only be processed after all deliverables are uploaded and approved.</li><li>False check-ins, inaccurate reporting, or incomplete work may result in payment disputes.</li><li>Additional work outside approved scope requires prior written approval through Field Nation messaging.</li></ul><p>Cancellation Policy</p><ul><li>If technician cancels within 24 hours of scheduled service, this may impact future work opportunities.</li><li>Repeated last-minute cancellations may result in removal from preferred technician lists.</li></ul><p>Confidentiality</p><p>Any customer information, credentials, network details, or business operations observed onsite must remain confidential and may not be shared with third parties.</p><p><br></p><p>Damage &amp; Liability</p><p>Technician is responsible for any damage caused due to negligence, misuse of tools, or failure to follow instructions.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion Standards</p><p>Work is considered complete only after:</p><ul><li>Customer confirms completion</li><li>Required testing is performed</li><li>All deliverables are uploaded</li><li>Project manager approves the work performed</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nWe will need two techs in the morning to remove the display from the wall to allow the Samsung tech to work on display. ﻿\n\n**General Instructions**\n\n• Partner MUST call Cenero Technical Support number above to \"check-in\" upon arrival at the client’s location and \"check-out\" upon completion of work.\n\n• Download the Technician Software to engage Cenero Support for assistance while you are onsite.\n\n• Sign-off is required at the completion of the service call.\n\n• Upload this completed Work Order Resolution Summary, including images, if applicable.\n\n• If RMA or site follow up visit is required, be sure to indicate it in the Work Order Resolution Summary. (Please note- Contact Cenero support to notify them of RMA- RMA will need to be generated in Cenero’s name and include a designated Cenero contact person)\n\n• For ALL issues that may arise- please engage the Cenero support team before discussing with the onsite contact.\n\n• Techs must reach out to Cenero support at 4 hours to determine if they are able to proceed with service.\n\n• Tech will need a laptop (w/charger) and a Hardwired Ethernet Connection or USB to Gigabit Ethernet adapter. Laptops need to be running Windows 10/11. No Mac or Linux computers should be used.\n\n• Tech should have a Wi-Fi hotspot available in the event that it is not possible to connect via client network.\n\n• If performing preventative maintenance, please confirm that all documents have been received by Cenero when checking out from site.\n\n**Technician Software Requirements**\n\n• Team Viewer (<https://www.teamviewer.com/en/download/windows/)>\n\n• Crestron Toolbox\n\n• Biamp Tesira\n\n• Q-sys Designer (latest version if no version is specified\n\n• Modern Web Browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, etc.)\n\n• Any additional software specified by Cenero prior to date of scheduled service call.\n\n**Please note- failure to follow these guidelines can result in payment refusal.**\n\n**Terms and Conditions:**\n\nCheck-In / Check-Out Requirements\n\n- Technician must check in and check out through the Field Nation platform.\n- Technician must remain onsite for the full approved service duration unless otherwise instructed by the Work Order Manager.\n- GPS and timestamp verification may be required.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Technician must maintain active communication before, during, and after the service event.\n- Technician must respond to calls/messages from dispatch or project management in a timely manner.\n- Failure to communicate delays, issues, or inability to complete work may result in reduced ratings and payment disputes.\n\nArrival &amp; Professional Conduct\n\n- Technician must arrive on time and dressed professionally.\n- Technician must behave respectfully toward store staff, customers, and management at all times.\n- Smoking, inappropriate language, harassment, or unprofessional behavior onsite will not be tolerated.\n\nPhotos &amp; Deliverables\n\nTechnician must upload all required deliverables before leaving site, including:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Asset labels/serial numbers\n- Cable routing photos\n- Speed tests or screenshots if applicable\n- Manager/customer sign-off where required\n- Detailed completion notes\n\nBlurry or incomplete documentation may delay approval and payment.\n\nCabling Work\n\n- No cabling work should be performed without prior approval if additional material or extended cable runs are required.\n- Technician must immediately notify the project manager if materials onsite are insufficient.\n- Partial or temporary cable runs should not be completed unless specifically approved.\n\nEscalation Procedure\n\nTechnician must immediately escalate:\n\n- Missing equipment\n- Incorrect parts\n- Site access issues\n- Network outages\n- Unsafe conditions\n- Scope changes\n- Any issue preventing completion\n\nUnauthorized scope changes may not be compensated.\n\nSafety Compliance\n\nTechnician agrees to follow all local safety regulations and site-specific safety requirements.\n\nTechnician is responsible for using ladders, electrical equipment, and tools safely.\n\nPayment Terms\n\n- Payment will only be processed after all deliverables are uploaded and approved.\n- False check-ins, inaccurate reporting, or incomplete work may result in payment disputes.\n- Additional work outside approved scope requires prior written approval through Field Nation messaging.\n\nCancellation Policy\n\n- If technician cancels within 24 hours of scheduled service, this may impact future work opportunities.\n- Repeated last-minute cancellations may result in removal from preferred technician lists.\n\nConfidentiality\n\nAny customer information, credentials, network details, or business operations observed onsite must remain confidential and may not be shared with third parties.\n\nDamage &amp; Liability\n\nTechnician is responsible for any damage caused due to negligence, misuse of tools, or failure to follow instructions.\n\nCompletion Standards\n\nWork is considered complete only after:\n\n- Customer confirms completion\n- Required testing is performed\n- All deliverables are uploaded\n- Project manager approves the work performed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T10:00","end":"2026-10-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":80},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7.100424539057395},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00: