{"job":{"id":20253974,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Liquid Networx","title":"Move network equipment, AP's, UPS, etc from old to new office","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TRAVEL REIMBURSEMENT MUST BE DONE WHEN APPLYING FOR THE WORK ORDER.</u> <u>REQUESTS AFTER BEING ASSIGNED THE WORK ORDER WILL BE SUBJECT TO BEING DENIED.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>On-Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Text <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** * ************</del></span> when arriving onsite.</li><li>Call <del>****** * </del><span style=\"color: rgb(127, 127, 127);\"><del>************</del>&nbsp;for any questions while onsite.</span></li><li>The old office is <del>**** ***** *** ******* ** *****</del>. The new address is 180 Lewter Shop Rd, Apex, NC 27523 but will show as an empty lot on Google Maps, we currently have a mobile office placed and power is being ran to it</li><li>Worker will need laptop, console cable, and hot spot.</li><li>Worker will need 6-8ft ladder for AP's</li><li>Old office (1101 Ellis) equipment removal:</li><li>-\tMain office equipment</li><li>o\tRack in the “main” office closet with SonicWall, one 24-port switch and one 8-port switch. Take UPS with, take down rack, and if we have ISP equipment, take with as we will have to return that equipment once the service is cancelled.</li><li>o\tTwo U6 Pro access points, one located in the same rack closet , the other located in a conference room</li><li>o\tIf any additional equipment, just have the tech call me and we can discuss.</li><li><br></li><li>-\tShop equipment</li><li>o\tThere is one 8-port switch and one U6 Pro in the shop</li><li>o\tIf there’s an UPS or surge protector here, please grab it</li><li><br></li><li>-\t“LI” Building</li><li>o\tOne 16-port switch and two U6 Pro access points (one front, one back)</li><li>o\tIf there’s an UPS or surge protector here, please grab it</li><li><br></li><li>New office (180 Lewter Shop) install:</li><li>-\tSingle mobile office</li><li>o\tHang rack in suitable location, install UPS, SonicWall, one 24-port switch</li><li>o\tFind suitable location/s for one or two access points within the office depending on size of the office</li><li>\tWe may need to run cable here for those access points, unless the network rack is centrally located, we can just have one U6 Pro sit on top of the rack and it should cover the entire building.</li><li>•\tOtherwise, two APs on opposite sides of the office will suffice</li><li>o\tInstall Starlink</li><li>\tI am having a Starlink shipped to the site and we will need to have the dish installed as well as the cable ran through to the network room.</li><li>•\tIf the included cable isn’t long enough, I will have to order the longer cable from Starlink directly</li><li><br></li><li>Return unused equipment to me:</li><li>-\tThe two 8-port and 16-port switches will be unused along with 3 of the access points. Please put those in a box so Jackie can ship those back to me directly as we will re-use them once a permanent site has been found.</li><li><br></li><li>Cleanup workstation</li><li>Take photo of all work completed</li><li>Upload Sign Off Sheet</li><li>Send text message to <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** * ************</del></span> when leaving the site with pictures of work completed.</li><li>Upload all deliverables and mark work order complete within 48 hrs.</li><li>Failure to complete the above tasks will result in non-payment</li><li><br></li><li><strong><u>Requirements</u></strong><u>:</u></li><li>Send text message to <del>****** * ************</del> when arriving onsite.</li><li>Send text message to <del>****** * ************</del> when leaving the site.</li><li>Upload all deliverables and mark work order complete within 48 hrs.</li><li>Failure to complete the above tasks will result in Non-Payment.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress Code/PPE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Present and maintain neat and&nbsp;appropriate professional appearance, including both attire and personal grooming for customer’s business environment. (Business or open collar business, non-denim attire. closed-toe, non-athletic footwear)</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<u>Necessary Equipment:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Carry or have immediate access to all necessary and standard service tools/equipment for assigned service task.</li><li>Tech must have a high-quality digital camera to take photos of all work completed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site Instructions:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Download/print off attached sign off sheet</li></ul><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any work the customer is requesting outside of the work listed in the SOW needs approval. Text <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** * ************</del></span>.</li><li>Work performed outside of the SOW without approval will not be paid</li><li>Difficulties checking into or checking out of the work order on the Field Nation platform should be directed to Field Nation by using the \"Report a Problem\" tab in the platform. Please select the \"How to/Technical Assistance\" option.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Reimbursement/Additional Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All Spend Limit Increases need to be approved prior to work completion. Failure to do so could result in SLIs not getting approved!</li><li>All materials used onsite will be reimbursed at the cost of materials. Request an expense reimbursement for materials used and all reimbursement requests should have the material description and cost. Must upload receipt for approval.</li><li>You are representing <del>****** *******</del> while on site. Do not mention Field Nation during any interaction with onsite contact!</li></ul><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><em>By accepting this work order, you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this work order for a minimum period of 30 business days. Warranty period will begin from the date that the Buyer on the work order has approved the work order electronically on the Field Nation platform. You will be required to repair all failed work, at no additional cost to the Buyer on this work order, within 3 business days of being notified of the warranty issue. If failed work is not completed in a timely manner, the work order will be subjected to cancellation with no payment or partial payment made.</em></p>","markdown":"**TRAVEL REIMBURSEMENT MUST BE DONE WHEN APPLYING FOR THE WORK ORDER. REQUESTS AFTER BEING ASSIGNED THE WORK ORDER WILL BE SUBJECT TO BEING DENIED.**\n\n**On-Site Instructions:**\n\n- Text \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when arriving onsite.\n- Call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for any questions while onsite.\n- The old office is \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. The new address is 180 Lewter Shop Rd, Apex, NC 27523 but will show as an empty lot on Google Maps, we currently have a mobile office placed and power is being ran to it\n- Worker will need laptop, console cable, and hot spot.\n- Worker will need 6-8ft ladder for AP's\n- Old office (1101 Ellis) equipment removal:\n- - Main office equipment\n- o Rack in the “main” office closet with SonicWall, one 24-port switch and one 8-port switch. Take UPS with, take down rack, and if we have ISP equipment, take with as we will have to return that equipment once the service is cancelled.\n- o Two U6 Pro access points, one located in the same rack closet , the other located in a conference room\n- o If any additional equipment, just have the tech call me and we can discuss.\n- \n- - Shop equipment\n- o There is one 8-port switch and one U6 Pro in the shop\n- o If there’s an UPS or surge protector here, please grab it\n- \n- - “LI” Building\n- o One 16-port switch and two U6 Pro access points (one front, one back)\n- o If there’s an UPS or surge protector here, please grab it\n- \n- New office (180 Lewter Shop) install:\n- - Single mobile office\n- o Hang rack in suitable location, install UPS, SonicWall, one 24-port switch\n- o Find suitable location/s for one or two access points within the office depending on size of the office\n-  We may need to run cable here for those access points, unless the network rack is centrally located, we can just have one U6 Pro sit on top of the rack and it should cover the entire building.\n- • Otherwise, two APs on opposite sides of the office will suffice\n- o Install Starlink\n-  I am having a Starlink shipped to the site and we will need to have the dish installed as well as the cable ran through to the network room.\n- • If the included cable isn’t long enough, I will have to order the longer cable from Starlink directly\n- \n- Return unused equipment to me:\n- - The two 8-port and 16-port switches will be unused along with 3 of the access points. Please put those in a box so Jackie can ship those back to me directly as we will re-use them once a permanent site has been found.\n- \n- Cleanup workstation\n- Take photo of all work completed\n- Upload Sign Off Sheet\n- Send text message to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when leaving the site with pictures of work completed.\n- Upload all deliverables and mark work order complete within 48 hrs.\n- Failure to complete the above tasks will result in non-payment\n- \n- **Requirements**:\n- Send text message to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when arriving onsite.\n- Send text message to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* when leaving the site.\n- Upload all deliverables and mark work order complete within 48 hrs.\n- Failure to complete the above tasks will result in Non-Payment.\n\n**Dress Code/PPE:**\n\n- Present and maintain neat and appropriate professional appearance, including both attire and personal grooming for customer’s business environment. (Business or open collar business, non-denim attire. closed-toe, non-athletic footwear)\n\n **Necessary Equipment:**\n\n- Carry or have immediate access to all necessary and standard service tools/equipment for assigned service task.\n- Tech must have a high-quality digital camera to take photos of all work completed.\n\n**Pre-Site Instructions:**\n\n- Download/print off attached sign off sheet\n\n**Escalations:**\n\n- Any work the customer is requesting outside of the work listed in the SOW needs approval. Text \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n- Work performed outside of the SOW without approval will not be paid\n- Difficulties checking into or checking out of the work order on the Field Nation platform should be directed to Field Nation by using the \"Report a Problem\" tab in the platform. Please select the \"How to/Technical Assistance\" option.\n\n**Reimbursement/Additional Information:**\n\n- All Spend Limit Increases need to be approved prior to work completion. Failure to do so could result in SLIs not getting approved!\n- All materials used onsite will be reimbursed at the cost of materials. Request an expense reimbursement for materials used and all reimbursement requests should have the material description and cost. Must upload receipt for approval.\n- You are representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* while on site. Do not mention Field Nation during any interaction with onsite contact!\n\n*By accepting this work order, you agree to warranty all work performed on this work order to the Buyer on this work order for a minimum period of 30 business days. Warranty period will begin from the date that the Buyer on the work order has approved the work order electronically on the Field Nation platform. You will be required to repair all failed work, at no additional cost to the Buyer on this work order, within 3 business days of being notified of the warranty issue. If failed work is not completed in a timely manner, the work order will be subjected to cancellation with no payment or partial payment made.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T09:00","end":"2026-11-02T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":600},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":9.000016111073293},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793124148651}
{"job":{"id":20254025,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Indoor Zhilai - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">URGENT || Service Call - Once onsite, Text Scott at&nbsp;(949) 393-1241. If unavailable, call Field Service line&nbsp;949-317-4169</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Part delivered: FedEx 879239854323</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting Jonathan Lazo for 10/28 10:00 a.m EST</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: get locker key and package from manager (FedEx 879239854323). **Bring USB keyboard and proceed with kiosk screen replacement.</span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</s