{"job":{"id":20254085,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Install New Managed PDU Power Supply","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME AND</strong><span style=\"color: red;\"> </span><strong style=\"color: red;\">CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL</strong></p><p>Patch cables may be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.</p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>BRIDGE INFO: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Microsoft Teams meeting Join: </span>https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2442404021902285?p=kTLD944x1NdBdV7yDz</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Meeting ID: 244 240 402 190 228 5</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Passcode: 6xc2MC2C </span></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required&nbsp;Deliverables&nbsp;to be paid:</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li><li>When onsite call into the <strong>CONFERENCE BRIDGE&nbsp;</strong>Listed above or reach out to Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge <del>***** ********</del></li><li>Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge</li><li>Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)</li><li>Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (<strong>dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)</strong></li><li>Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested</li><li>Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.</li><li>Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.</li><li>Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge or call Dispatch Team if necessary</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</p><p>2.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME AND** **CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL**\n\nPatch cables may be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**BRIDGE INFO:** Microsoft Teams meeting Join: <https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2442404021902285?p=kTLD944x1NdBdV7yDz>\n\nMeeting ID: 244 240 402 190 228 5\n\nPasscode: 6xc2MC2C\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n***Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning***\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n2. When onsite call into the **CONFERENCE BRIDGE** Listed above or reach out to Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge\n4. Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)\n5. Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (**dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)**\n6. Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested\n7. Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.\n8. Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.\n9. Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.\n10. Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge or call Dispatch Team if necessary\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1\\. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.\n\n2\\. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T12:30","end":"2026-11-05T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.413902841867891},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793124814128}
{"job":{"id":20254088,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Circle Computer Resources","title":"Install Starlink Dish/Equipment On Construction Trailer","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Basic Tools/Power Drill</li><li>Laptop</li><li>RJ45 Crimp Tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Pull String</li><li>Ladder</li><li>Silicone/Caulking (Waterproof) - All penetrating points need to be caulked to prevent water damage</li><li>Tech will need to bring an ID to the assignment and&nbsp;wear vendor&nbsp;neutral attire (unless its your&nbsp;company's name/logo).</li><li><strong>PPE required onsite: Hard Hat, High Visibility Vest, Eye Protection, Work Boots.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Summary:</strong>&nbsp;We will be installing a Starlink Standard Gen3 Dish on the outside wall of a Construction Trailer. We will be penetrating into the trailer with the Starlink cable and setting up the Starlink Router and Power Supply, along with a Managed Router, Firewall, Switch, Access Point, and Monitoring Device inside. Verifying WiFi Connectivity and Starlink alignment will be needed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Directions:</strong></p><ul><li>Check in with ConstructEdge once you arrive.</li><li>Call onsite contact to check in and go through safety orientation.</li><li>Take pictures of all equipment prior to install.</li><li>Locate the best location to install the Starlink Mount/Dish. The Dish needs clear line of site to the sky, no obstructions such as trees, and the Dish must be higher than the trailer.</li><li>Install the J-Mount to the side of the trailer near the roof, so that when the dish is installed it will clear the roof</li><li>Attach the Starlink to the J-Mount using the Pipe Adapter, ensure dish is secured.</li><li>Run Starlink cable from the Dish to the inside of the trailer. If there is an existing conduit or cable path to get inside the trailer, use that. If there is not, drill a hole to create an entry point in the side or bottom of the trailer. It will need to be sealed with Silicone after the install.</li><li>After running the Starlink Cable inside the Trailer, connect it to the Starlink Router, connect Starlink Power Supply, Managed Router, Firewall, Monitoring Device, Switch, Access Point and UPS and power up the all equipment.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect Port Labeled \"Starlink\" of the Managed Router (Labeled MRT, the device is a UCG Ultra) to the Left Ethernet port of the Starlink Router.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect Port Labeled \"DSK\" on Managed Router to the Monitoring Device (Labeled DSK) Ethernet Port.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect USB Port of Monitoring Device to USB port of the UPS.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect WAN1 of the FortiGate to the Port Labeled \"FortiGate\" on the Managed Router.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect Port A of the FortiGate to Port 8 of the FortiSwitch.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect Ethernet Cable to Port 1 on the FortiSwitch, run ethernet cable through the drop ceiling to the middle of the trailer and ceiling mount the FortiAP and connect cable to it. If the FortiAP does not have mounting hardware to ceiling mount it, place it on top of the other equipment.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Plug the power cords of the Starlink, Managed Router, and DSK to the Battery Backup side of the UPS and power on UPS. All other devices can be plugged into the Surge Protection only side of the UPS.</li><li>Open the Starlink App and connect to the dish to check the alignment, the dish may need to be rotated a certain way to get a good alignment.</li><li>Connect to the Public WiFi from the FortiAP and check the speeds, send a screenshot to ConstructEdge to verify.</li><li>Attach supplied shelf to the wall and place Equipment on the shelf. Use the supplied Cable Raceway to cover the indoor cables where possible.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Equipment can also be wall mounted if needed.</li><li>Seal the entry point that was drilled for the Starlink Cable if needed.</li><li>Verify all equipment is online with ConstructEdge. Verify Local Contact can connect to WiFi.</li><li>Ensure cable management is neat and in order.</li><li>Take pictures of all equipment and upload to Work Order.</li><li><strong>Pictures will need to be uploaded to the Field Nation Work Order prior to departing the site. The pictures need to be clear and show all equipment after installation.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**Requirements:**\n\n- Basic Tools/Power Drill\n- Laptop\n- RJ45 Crimp Tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Pull String\n- Ladder\n- Silicone/Caulking (Waterproof) - All penetrating points need to be caulked to prevent water damage\n- Tech will need to bring an ID to the assignment and wear vendor neutral attire (unless its your company's name/logo).\n- **PPE required onsite: Hard Hat, High Visibility Vest, Eye Protection, Work Boots.**\n\n**Summary:** We will be installing a Starlink Standard Gen3 Dish on the outside wall of a Construction Trailer. We will be penetrating into the trailer with the Starlink cable and setting up the Starlink Router and Power Supply, along with a Managed Router, Firewall, Switch, Access Point, and Monitoring Device inside. Verifying WiFi Connectivity and Starlink alignment will be needed.\n\n**Directions:**\n\n- Check in with ConstructEdge once you arrive.\n- Call onsite contact to check in and go through safety orientation.\n- Take pictures of all equipment prior to install.\n- Locate the best location to install the Starlink Mount/Dish. The Dish needs clear line of site to the sky, no obstructions such as trees, and the Dish must be higher than the trailer.\n- Install the J-Mount to the side of the trailer near the roof, so that when the dish is installed it will clear the roof\n- Attach the Starlink to the J-Mount using the Pipe Adapter, ensure dish is secured.\n- Run Starlink cable from the Dish to the inside of the trailer. If there is an existing conduit or cable path to get inside the trailer, use that. If there is not, drill a hole to create an entry point in the side or bottom of the trailer. It will need to be sealed with Silicone after the install.\n- After running the Starlink Cable inside the Trailer, connect it to the Starlink Router, connect Starlink Power Supply, Managed Router, Firewall, Monitoring Device, Switch, Access Point and UPS and power up the all equipment.\n- Connect Port Labeled \"Starlink\" of the Managed Router (Labeled MRT, the device is a UCG Ultra) to the Left Ethernet port of the Starlink Router.\n- Connect Port Labeled \"DSK\" on Managed Router to the Monitoring Device (Labeled DSK) Ethernet Port.\n- Connect USB Port of Monitoring Device to USB port of the UPS.\n- Connect WAN1 of the FortiGate to the Port Labeled \"FortiGate\" on the Managed Router.\n- Connect Port A of the FortiGate to Port 8 of the FortiSwitch.\n- Connect Ethernet Cable to Port 1 on the FortiSwitch, run ethernet cable through the drop ceiling to the middle of the trailer and ceiling mount the FortiAP and connect cable to it. If the FortiAP does not have mounting hardware to ceiling mount it, place it on top of the other equipment.\n- Plug the power cords of the Starlink, Managed Router, and DSK to the Battery Backup side of the UPS and power on UPS. All other devices can be plugged into the Surge Protection only side of the UPS.\n- Open the Starlink App and connect to the dish to check the alignment, the dish may need to be rotated a certain way to get a good alignment.\n- Connect to the Public WiFi from the FortiAP and check the speeds, send a screenshot to ConstructEdge to verify.\n- Attach supplied shelf to the wall and place Equipment on the shelf. Use the supplied Cable Raceway to cover the indoor cables where possible.\n- Equipment can also be wall mounted if needed.\n- Seal the entry point that was drilled for the Starlink Cable if needed.\n- Verify all equipment is online with ConstructEdge. Verify Local Contact can connect to WiFi.\n- Ensure cable management is neat and in order.\n- Take pictures of all equipment and upload to Work Order.\n- **Pictures will need to be uploaded to the Field Nation Work Order prior to departing the site. The pictures need to be clear and show all equipment after installation.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T09:00","end":"2026-11-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":350,"max":470},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":3,"amount":350},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":17.36492065871174},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793124822175}
{"job":{"id":20252649,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"Replace the POS Unit for POS 03 - est. < 2 hrs onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.</strong></p><ul><li>You will represent yourself as an <del>***</del> Representative</li><li>INC# and FWKD# in the work order information</li><li><strong><u>Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order</u></strong>.</li><li>Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.</li><li>The defective part must be returned in the box with the&nbsp;provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.</li><li>Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.</li><li>Drop the return package off at UPS store.</li><li>If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.</li><li>Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.</li><li>Must Check In/Out with <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li>Must take before and after photos of the unit</li><li>Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTES:</strong></p><ol><li>Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!&nbsp;</li><li>Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.&nbsp;</li><li>Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.&nbsp;</li><li>All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.&nbsp;</li><li>Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.&nbsp;</li><li>The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><strong><em><u>READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Escalation Process: </strong>If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to <del>*** **** **** * ************</del></li><li><strong>Readiness Policy: </strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>On My Way: </strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</li><li><strong>Arriving Late:</strong> All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</li><li><strong>Changing Resources:</strong> By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</li><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</li><li><strong>Expense Approval:</strong> Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</li><li><strong>Wait Time: </strong>If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.</li><li><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong> If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Out-of-Scope Work: </strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.</li><li><strong>Returning Parts:</strong> Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</li></ul>","markdown":"***NOTE: Following the WO Tasks will ensure a successful work order completion***\n\n**Scope of Work - Replace the whole unit POS.**\n\n- You will represent yourself as an \\*\\*\\* Representative\n- INC# and FWKD# in the work order information\n- **Follow the detailed installation instructions attached to this work order**.\n- Replace the POS Unit; the part will already be onsite when you arrive.\n- The defective part must be returned in the box with the provided shipping label attached to the box in which the replacement unit arrived.\n- Must have vehicle large enough to carry the 19 X 16 X 21 box that weighs 27 pounds to UPS.\n- Drop the return package off at UPS store.\n- If UPS store is currently closed at the time of work order, drop off when the store is open for the day.\n- Must CONFIRM the work order and SET your ETA (Start Time). Failure to do so may result in a reduction of your labor rate.\n- Must Check In/Out with \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Must take before and after photos of the unit\n- Must submit closeout information and upload photos from the site before leaving.\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n\n1. Do not disconnect or reconnect cables while the POS is powered on at any time!\n2. Never place the POS face down on its’ main display, customer-facing display, or magnetic card reader when working on the hardware or cables! Only lay the POS down on its left side.\n3. Caution: Never bring down more than one point-of-sale unit at a time.\n4. All point-of-sale units must be returned with an AC power adaptor and all cable covers. They are not to be left on site.\n5. Take photos and document any physical damage to the equipment before troubleshooting.\n6. The NEC G5100 twin POS comprises of the following components: the POS, Rear Cable Cover, Lower Cable Shroud, and AC Power adapter with Cord. NOTE: All these parts must be accounted for when returning the POS.\n\n***READ / REVIEW Below before accepting the work order***\n\n- **Escalation Process:** If you have technical issues during the work order, please escalate to \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Readiness Policy:** The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools, and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted. Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.\n- **On My Way:** When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way” This will update the Support team that you are to the site.\n- **Arriving Late:** All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order. Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.\n- **Changing Resources:** By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.\n- **Dress Code:** Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.\n- **Expense Approval:** Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.\n- **Wait Time:** If you have to wait for a part to show up, you will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour covering the work order.\n- **Additional Time On-site:** If there are any delays beyond authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial 2 hours that covers the work order.\n- **Out-of-Scope Work:** If you are asked to perform work beyond the above scope, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident. Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid $45 per hour after the initial hour that covers the work order.\n- **Returning Parts:** Pack carefully with shipping material used with replacement device. Use foam properly to protect during shipping. Return Waybills are found in the original package in which the part was shipped. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-27T15:30","end":"2026-10-27T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":280,"max":280},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":53.41424471058918},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793125163734}
{"job":{"id":20254439,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Indoor Zhilai - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Parts sent out : TRACKING NUMBER 879140028440</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for 11/2 9:00 AM </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: Check inat office and get key and new scanner. Need to replace scanner and test</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner) </span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.\n\n\\- Parts sent out : TRACKING NUMBER 879140028440\n\n\\- Requesting tech for 11/2 9:00 AM\n\n\\- Need to: Check inat office and get key and new scanner. Need to replace scanner and test\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T09:00","end":"2026-11-02T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-02T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":8.979547581484269},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z"