{"job":{"id":20255466,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"APC UPS & Electrical System Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking <strong>one technician experienced in UPS systems, rack-mounted power equipment, and electrical site assessments</strong>.</li><li>Conduct a needs assessment and detailed evaluation of the existing UPS system and installation area.</li><li>Gather the information needed to prepare a quote and plan the replacement.</li><li>A licensed electrician should participate <strong>if electrical testing or access to energized electrical equipment is required</strong>.</li><li><strong>Date, time, and estimated duration:</strong> To be confirmed.</li><li>Introduce yourself as a <strong>technician from TechHub PS</strong>.</li></ul>1. Purpose<p>Survey the existing UPS system and associated electrical infrastructure to determine the labor, materials, equipment, outage window, and disposal requirements for the proposed replacement.</p><p>The planned installation includes:</p><ul><li><strong>APC Smart-UPS On-Line UPS:</strong> SRT8KRMXLT</li><li><strong>APC External Battery Pack:</strong> SRT192RMBP2</li><li><strong>APC Step-Down Transformer:</strong> SRT5KRMTF</li><li><strong>APC Maintenance Bypass Panel:</strong> SBP10KRMT4U</li><li><strong>APC Switched Rack PDU:</strong> AP7900B</li></ul><p><strong>This visit is for assessment and documentation only. Do not disconnect, power down, move, or replace equipment during the survey.</strong></p>2. Pre-Arrival Requirements<ul><li>Review the work order and proposed equipment list.</li><li>Confirm the survey date, site access, and onsite point of contact.</li><li>Confirm whether a licensed electrician will attend or be available.</li><li>Request any existing electrical drawings, rack elevations, UPS documentation, and equipment inventory available from the customer.</li><li>Bring a smartphone or camera, flashlight, tape measure, laptop, and required site PPE.</li><li>Coordinate with the site before taking photographs of equipment or restricted areas.</li></ul>3. Site Check-In &amp; Customer Requirements<p>Upon arrival:</p><ul><li>Check in with the onsite point of contact and TechHub PS.</li><li>Confirm the areas and equipment included in the survey.</li><li>Discuss the customer’s objectives for the UPS replacement and any known problems with the existing system.</li><li>Identify critical equipment supported by the UPS.</li><li>Discuss operating hours, access restrictions, and the process for approving a shutdown.</li><li>Confirm whether any equipment must remain powered during the replacement.</li></ul>4. Existing Equipment Assessment<p>Document the existing power system, including:</p><ul><li>UPS manufacturer, model, serial number, capacity, and condition.</li><li>Number and type of external battery packs or battery modules.</li><li>Existing transformer, maintenance bypass panel, and PDU details.</li><li>Equipment locations and whether components are rack-mounted or floor-mounted.</li><li>Visible alarms, damage, or other issues reported by site personnel.</li><li>Equipment connected to each PDU or UPS output, where identifiable.</li><li>Existing network management connections, if present.</li></ul><p>Record which equipment is expected to be removed and disposed of.</p>5. Electrical Infrastructure Assessment<p>The information provided states that the existing UPS is hardwired to a <strong>single-phase, 208V, 3-wire, 2-pole, 60A circuit with 6 AWG conductors</strong>. Verify and document these details from available labels, drawings, and site information.</p><p>Assess and record:</p><ul><li>Electrical panel and circuit identification.</li><li>Breaker rating and available disconnects.</li><li>Existing UPS input and output connections.</li><li>Conduit routing, visible wiring, and apparent condition.</li><li>Grounding arrangements as visible or documented.</li><li>Existing bypass and power-distribution connections.</li><li>Available circuit capacity and any information needed for a licensed electrician to evaluate it.</li><li>Whether existing conduit and conductors appear suitable for reuse, subject to electrician verification.</li><li>Any suspected electrical modifications, permits, or additional materials that may be required.</li></ul><p><strong>Do not open energized electrical panels or perform electrical measurements unless the work is authorized and performed by a qualified, licensed electrician using the required procedures and PPE.</strong></p>6. Rack &amp; Installation Area Assessment<ul><li>Measure available rack space and document existing equipment placement.</li><li>Confirm whether the rack or designated location can accommodate the proposed equipment.</li><li>Assess mounting rails, hardware, clearances, ventilation, and access for servicing.</li><li>Document the installation area, delivery path, doorways, elevators, and any stairs.</li><li>Identify any lifting equipment or additional personnel needed to handle the UPS, batteries, and transformer.</li><li>Note any obstacles that could affect equipment removal or installation.</li></ul>7. Proposed Equipment &amp; Compatibility Review<p>Review the proposed equipment list against the information collected onsite. Document any questions or exceptions requiring confirmation by the project team, APC, or the licensed electrician, including:</p><ul><li>Input and output voltage requirements.</li><li>UPS, battery pack, transformer, bypass, and PDU connections.</li><li>Plug, receptacle, hardwired connection, and cable requirements.</li><li>Rack space, mounting hardware, weight, and handling requirements.</li><li>Compatibility of the transformer and bypass arrangement with the planned loads.</li><li>Network management connections and available network drops.</li></ul><p><strong>Do not assume that all listed equipment is compatible with the existing system or with each other. Report any item that needs verification before a quote or installation is finalized.</strong></p>8. Load &amp; Outage Planning<ul><li>Identify and document the protected equipment and available load information.</li><li>Record UPS load readings or capacity information available on the display or from site personnel.</li><li>Determine whether critical loads can be shut down and for how long.</li><li>Discuss the required outage window and preferred installation hours.</li><li>Identify any need for temporary power or a phased transfer of loads.</li><li>Note dependencies, approvals, or site personnel required during installation and startup.</li></ul>9. Removal, Disposal &amp; Logistics<ul><li>Document the equipment and battery quantities to be removed.</li><li>Assess the removal route and any loading dock or vehicle access restrictions.</li><li>Identify handling requirements and whether additional technicians or lifting equipment will be needed.</li><li>Confirm whether the customer has specific disposal or recycling requirements.</li><li>Note any requirements for removal and disposal of batteries and decommissioned equipment.</li><li>Confirm where new equipment will be delivered and staged before installation.</li></ul>10. Required Photos &amp; Deliverables<p>Capture and submit clear photos, where permitted, of:</p><ul><li>Front and rear views of the existing rack and UPS equipment.</li><li>Model and serial number labels for existing equipment.</li><li>Existing batteries, transformer, bypass panel, and PDU.</li><li>Visible input and output connections, conduit, and cable routing.</li><li>Electrical panel and breaker labels, without opening energized equipment.</li><li>Existing rack space and installation area.</li><li>Delivery and equipment removal paths.</li><li>Any identified issues or site constraints.</li></ul><p>Submit a survey report including:</p><ul><li>Existing equipment inventory and condition.</li><li>Electrical circuit and connection details verified onsite.</li><li>Rack measurements and available space.</li><li>Protected-load information and shutdown requirements.</li><li>Recommended staffing, licensed electrician scope, tools, and lifting equipment.</li><li>Required materials and any anticipated infrastructure changes.</li><li>Equipment removal and disposal requirements.</li><li>Exceptions, compatibility questions, and items requiring further verification.</li><li>Recommended installation duration and outage window, based on survey findings.</li></ul>11. Check-Out &amp; Completion Requirements<p>Before leaving:</p><ul><li>Review key findings and any concerns with the onsite contact.</li><li>Confirm no equipment or connections have been disturbed.</li><li>Notify TechHub PS of any conditions that may affect the installation quote.</li><li>Submit all required photos and survey documentation.</li><li>Obtain onsite acknowledgment of the completed survey.</li><li>Check out with TechHub PS.</li></ul>12. Exclusions<p>This survey does not include:</p><ul><li>UPS installation, startup, or commissioning.</li><li>Electrical disconnection, reconnection, or repairs.</li><li>Moving or removing existing equipment.</li><li>Load transfer or system shutdown.</li><li>Disposal of equipment or batteries.</li><li>Detailed engineering studies, permit applications, or utility work.</li></ul>13. Escalation Contact<p><strong>Mathew Manik</strong></p><p><strong>Phone:</strong> (858) 321-3947</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> mbaroi@techhubps.com</p><p>Contact Mathew if there are access issues, missing information, safety concerns, or any condition that may affect the proposed installation.</p>14. Additional Hours &amp; Expenses<ul><li>All additional hours and expenses require prior written approval.</li><li>Any work outside this survey scope requires approval by email before proceeding.</li><li>Obtain the required sign-off before closing the work order.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**\n\n- Seeking **one technician experienced in UPS systems, rack-mounted power equipment, and electrical site assessments**.\n- Conduct a needs assessment and detailed evaluation of the existing UPS system and installation area.\n- Gather the information needed to prepare a quote and plan the replacement.\n- A licensed electrician should participate **if electrical testing or access to energized electrical equipment is required**.\n- **Date, time, and estimated duration:** To be confirmed.\n- Introduce yourself as a **technician from TechHub PS**.\n\n1. PurposeSurvey the existing UPS system and associated electrical infrastructure to determine the labor, materials, equipment, outage window, and disposal requirements for the proposed replacement.\n\nThe planned installation includes:\n\n- **APC Smart-UPS On-Line UPS:** SRT8KRMXLT\n- **APC External Battery Pack:** SRT192RMBP2\n- **APC Step-Down Transformer:** SRT5KRMTF\n- **APC Maintenance Bypass Panel:** SBP10KRMT4U\n- **APC Switched Rack PDU:** AP7900B\n\n**This visit is for assessment and documentation only. Do not disconnect, power down, move, or replace equipment during the survey.**\n\n2. Pre-Arrival Requirements- Review the work order and proposed equipment list.\n- Confirm the survey date, site access, and onsite point of contact.\n- Confirm whether a licensed electrician will attend or be available.\n- Request any existing electrical drawings, rack elevations, UPS documentation, and equipment inventory available from the customer.\n- Bring a smartphone or camera, flashlight, tape measure, laptop, and required site PPE.\n- Coordinate with the site before taking photographs of equipment or restricted areas.\n\n3. Site Check-In &amp; Customer RequirementsUpon arrival:\n\n- Check in with the onsite point of contact and TechHub PS.\n- Confirm the areas and equipment included in the survey.\n- Discuss the customer’s objectives for the UPS replacement and any known problems with the existing system.\n- Identify critical equipment supported by the UPS.\n- Discuss operating hours, access restrictions, and the process for approving a shutdown.\n- Confirm whether any equipment must remain powered during the replacement.\n\n4. Existing Equipment AssessmentDocument the existing power system, including:\n\n- UPS manufacturer, model, serial number, capacity, and condition.\n- Number and type of external battery packs or battery modules.\n- Existing transformer, maintenance bypass panel, and PDU details.\n- Equipment locations and whether components are rack-mounted or floor-mounted.\n- Visible alarms, damage, or other issues reported by site personnel.\n- Equipment connected to each PDU or UPS output, where identifiable.\n- Existing network management connections, if present.\n\nRecord which equipment is expected to be removed and disposed of.\n\n5. Electrical Infrastructure AssessmentThe information provided states that the existing UPS is hardwired to a **single-phase, 208V, 3-wire, 2-pole, 60A circuit with 6 AWG conductors**. Verify and document these details from available labels, drawings, and site information.\n\nAssess and record:\n\n- Electrical panel and circuit identification.\n- Breaker rating and available disconnects.\n- Existing UPS input and output connections.\n- Conduit routing, visible wiring, and apparent condition.\n- Grounding arrangements as visible or documented.\n- Existing bypass and power-distribution connections.\n- Available circuit capacity and any information needed for a licensed electrician to evaluate it.\n- Whether existing conduit and conductors appear suitable for reuse, subject to electrician verification.\n- Any suspected electrical modifications, permits, or additional materials that may be required.\n\n**Do not open energized electrical panels or perform electrical measurements unless the work is authorized and performed by a qualified, licensed electrician using the required procedures and PPE.**\n\n6. Rack &amp; Installation Area Assessment- Measure available rack space and document existing equipment placement.\n- Confirm whether the rack or designated location can accommodate the proposed equipment.\n- Assess mounting rails, hardware, clearances, ventilation, and access for servicing.\n- Document the installation area, delivery path, doorways, elevators, and any stairs.\n- Identify any lifting equipment or additional personnel needed to handle the UPS, batteries, and transformer.\n- Note any obstacles that could affect equipment removal or installation.\n\n7. Proposed Equipment &amp; Compatibility ReviewReview the proposed equipment list against the information collected onsite. Document any questions or exceptions requiring confirmation by the project team, APC, or the licensed electrician, including:\n\n- Input and output voltage requirements.\n- UPS, battery pack, transformer, bypass, and PDU connections.\n- Plug, receptacle, hardwired connection, and cable requirements.\n- Rack space, mounting hardware, weight, and handling requirements.\n- Compatibility of the transformer and bypass arrangement with the planned loads.\n- Network management connections and available network drops.\n\n**Do not assume that all listed equipment is compatible with the existing system or with each other. Report any item that needs verification before a quote or installation is finalized.**\n\n8. Load &amp; Outage Planning- Identify and document the protected equipment and available load information.\n- Record UPS load readings or capacity information available on the display or from site personnel.\n- Determine whether critical loads can be shut down and for how long.\n- Discuss the required outage window and preferred installation hours.\n- Identify any need for temporary power or a phased transfer of loads.\n- Note dependencies, approvals, or site personnel required during installation and startup.\n\n9. Removal, Disposal &amp; Logistics- Document the equipment and battery quantities to be removed.\n- Assess the removal route and any loading dock or vehicle access restrictions.\n- Identify handling requirements and whether additional technicians or lifting equipment will be needed.\n- Confirm whether the customer has specific disposal or recycling requirements.\n- Note any requirements for removal and disposal of batteries and decommissioned equipment.\n- Confirm where new equipment will be delivered and staged before installation.\n\n10. Required Photos &amp; DeliverablesCapture and submit clear photos, where permitted, of:\n\n- Front and rear views of the existing rack and UPS equipment.\n- Model and serial number labels for existing equipment.\n- Existing batteries, transformer, bypass panel, and PDU.\n- Visible input and output connections, conduit, and cable routing.\n- Electrical panel and breaker labels, without opening energized equipment.\n- Existing rack space and installation area.\n- Delivery and equipment removal paths.\n- Any identified issues or site constraints.\n\nSubmit a survey report including:\n\n- Existing equipment inventory and condition.\n- Electrical circuit and connection details verified onsite.\n- Rack measurements and available space.\n- Protected-load information and shutdown requirements.\n- Recommended staffing, licensed electrician scope, tools, and lifting equipment.\n- Required materials and any anticipated infrastructure changes.\n- Equipment removal and disposal requirements.\n- Exceptions, compatibility questions, and items requiring further verification.\n- Recommended installation duration and outage window, based on survey findings.\n\n11. Check-Out &amp; Completion RequirementsBefore leaving:\n\n- Review key findings and any concerns with the onsite contact.\n- Confirm no equipment or connections have been disturbed.\n- Notify TechHub PS of any conditions that may affect the installation quote.\n- Submit all required photos and survey documentation.\n- Obtain onsite acknowledgment of the completed survey.\n- Check out with TechHub PS.\n\n12. ExclusionsThis survey does not include:\n\n- UPS installation, startup, or commissioning.\n- Electrical disconnection, reconnection, or repairs.\n- Moving or removing existing equipment.\n- Load transfer or system shutdown.\n- Disposal of equipment or batteries.\n- Detailed engineering studies, permit applications, or utility work.\n\n13. Escalation Contact**Mathew Manik**\n\n**Phone:** (858) 321-3947\n\n**Email:** mbaroi@techhubps.com\n\nContact Mathew if there are access issues, missing information, safety concerns, or any condition that may affect the proposed installation.\n\n14. Additional Hours &amp; Expenses- All additional hours and expenses require prior written approval.\n- Any work outside this survey scope requires approval by email before proceeding.\n- Obtain the required sign-off before closing the work order.\n\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T12:00","end":"2026-10-29T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":57.67605465866834},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793131688079}
{"job":{"id":"2828993103","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install PDU","description":"<p># SCOPE OF WORK</p><p><br></p><p>Survey site and follow latest MOP instructions. Install PDU near PIAB and carrier modems. Follow checklist if carrier EQ or customer EQ are in different locations.</p><p><br></p><p># REQUIRED MATERIALS</p><p><br></p><p>- Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port</p><p>- Multimeter wire tester</p><p>- Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches</p><p>- Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer)</p><p>- Biscuit jacks</p><p>- Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters</p><p>- 4-6 ft' ladder</p><p>- Butt Set</p><p>- RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors</p><p>- 100' extension cord</p><p>- Digital Camera</p><p>- 100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device</p><p>- Cell phone w/Hotspot device</p><p>- Punch down tool</p><p><br></p><p># BRIDGE INFO</p><p><br></p><p>URL: https://dispatch.bruin.com/</p><p><br></p><p>*Tech MUST work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number and Mettel ticket in the confidential field section*</p><p>___________________________________________________________________________________________________</p><p>Flat rate covers up to 2 hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</p><p><br></p><p>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</p><p><br></p><p>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered ?Cancelled?, not ?Aborted?. </p><p><br></p><p>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00","end":"2026-10-29T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00