{"job":{"id":20255620,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Coretelligent, LLC","title":"Onsite Client Visit","description":{"html":"<p>We are looking for a technician with 3+ years of experience to provide desktop support to our VIP client. This may include some light cloud/SaaS app management, basic networking concepts and/or some light server OS troubleshooting in the course of providing desktop support. This work will total 16 hours weekly (two 8-hour days).</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Coretelligent is headquartered in Massachusetts and we will manage the customer at large. We are looking for an engineer to provide service to our customer and act as an extension of our team.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Our support engineers utilize strong customer service skills to provide on-site technical support to our dynamic client base.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Communicate with clients on-site (desktop support) to resolve technical issues and close tickets.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Communicate with the customer's IT department and gather needs from them, if applicable.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Collaborate with internal client stakeholders and Coretelligent stakeholders.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Utilize very strong knowledge of Windows desktop troubleshooting to assist clients with connectivity, printing, customization, user profile and applications.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Provide strong Microsoft Office and Mobile Device troubleshooting to resolve client issues.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Utilize conceptual knowledge of working firewalls/switching/wifi to ensure secure connectivity.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Responsible for user account management in Active Directory, hosted email, spam filters, and other platforms. This includes: creation, removal, changes, password resets, and bulk operations</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Update and maintain documentation</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Accurately, regularly, and effectively record time</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>General instructions:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>1. Tech is to arrive and contact our main point of contact at the client site (TBD).</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2. Tech is to introduce themselves to end user. You are representing Coretelligent.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>3. Ask POC /Manager if he/she has any urgent items that they would like looked at, before we start working on our open task list.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4. Contact Coretelligent's counterpart engineer to receive any additional instructions.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>5. Work on:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Items the customer mentioned were urgent</p><p><br></p><p>Items assigned from Coretelligent engineer</p><p><br></p><p>List of open items from last visit (if any)</p><p><br></p><p>If there is nothing open, re-contact Coretelligent engineer for further instructions</p><p><br></p><p>6. Before departure update end users on status of their work or update them on next steps we will be taking.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>7. Upon departure tech is to fill out a visit status report in Field Nation outlining all work completed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Deliverables to be paid:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>1. Fill out a status report in Field Nation detailing all completed and attempted work.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2. Enter the time you spent onsite into Field Nation.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dress Code: business casual</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Tools:</p><p><br>