{"job":{"id":"2579614750","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Customer Equipment | Priority 3 | 10/30/2026 09:00:00 - 17:00:00 EDT | Requested Window","description":"<p>Service technician needed on site to repair existing customer equipment.</p><p><br></p><p>The equipment experiencing an issue is Express Exit QR code scanner and associated power supply/power cable.</p><p><br></p><p>This equipment is currently being used for Customer-facing Express Exit processing at the exit gate. The QR scanner is used to scan customer QR codes during the Express Exit process. and is located at RDU - Express Exit / Exit Gate 1016 Rental Car Drive Morrisville, NC 27560 Site Mnemonic: 00930.</p><p><br></p><p>Once the equipment has been successfully installed, the technician should test with: William Franklin who can be reached via phone at (919) 995-8438 or email at William.Franklin@avisbudget.com.</p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch technician to RDU to troubleshoot the Express Exit QR scanner under INC1465528. The QR scanner has no power despite being plugged in correctly. Site reported that the scanner power cable is wrapped with electrical tape, which may indicate previous damage.</p><p><br></p><p>Inspect and test the QR scanner power cable, power supply/adapter, outlet/power source, and associated connections. Determine the failed component and restore power and scanner functionality if possible.</p><p><br></p><p>If equipment requires replacement, document the manufacturer, model, serial number, part number, and quantity required. After repair, verify the scanner powers on and complete a functional QR scan test with the site.</p>","isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T09:00","end":"2026-10-30T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","c