{"job":{"id":20256040,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Connext","title":" CFA 00060 | Site Survey to Determine Cable Length and Requirements for Installing an AP in the Storage Room at a Mall Location","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE ADD YOUR NAME ON THE BADGE UNDER DOCUMENTS AND PRINT OUT FOR USE ON SITE. PLEASE PUT IN A CLEAR BADGE HOLDER AND ON A LANYARD IF POSSIBLE.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Important Site Protocol – Please Read Carefully</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>To avoid monetary penalties, complete the following immediately after finishing work and before leaving the site:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in and check out as instructed.</li>\n<li>Obtain your release code.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables through Qualtrics using the link in the work order.</li>\n<li>Close out the work order with detailed notes. Our team must provide the customer with job status updates each morning; incomplete closeout steps may result in a penalty.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Preparation Expectations</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Read the entire work order before arriving.</strong> If you arrive without the required tools or are unprepared to complete the assigned work, you will not be compensated for the visit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Access Restrictions</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You are not permitted onsite between 11:00 AM and 2:00 PM.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Ticket Number #VTASK0614223&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Coordinate with Operator<strong>Ben<del>*******</del></strong>to identify the proposed AP installation location in the storage room.</li>\n<li>Survey the area and determine the cable routing path and estimated cable length.</li>\n<li>Determine whether the connection requires <strong>fiber or CAT5/CAT6 cabling</strong> based on distance and site conditions.</li>\n<li>Identify any obstacles or additional materials needed to complete the installation.</li>\n<li>Take <strong>photos</strong> of the <strong>storage room and proposed AP location</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Provide a video walkthrough showing the proposed cable route and installation area.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The storage room currently has no network connectivity. This survey is to determine the cabling requirements, installation path, and materials needed to add a Wi-Fi AP.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Out-of-Scope Tasks</u></strong></p>\n<p>If a CFA representative requests work outside the listed scope,<strong>contact Connext for direction before proceeding</strong>, unless otherwise authorized.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Document all additional work performed and the time incurred.</li>\n<li>Verified additional <strong>labor beyond the original work order will be compensated</strong> appropriately, subject to applicable approval requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Instructions</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>If replacement is specified, repairing the existing component does not satisfy the work order.</strong></li>\n<li>Failure to complete the specified task may result in non-payment.</li>\n<li>Contact Connext if any scope details are unclear.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Cable Management</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Secure and organize cables using cable ties, Velcro straps, cable trays, or other appropriate solutions.</li>\n<li>Do not leave cables tangled, unsecured, or loosely draped across surfaces.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Site Cleanliness</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove all tools, loose cabling, packaging, and debris before leaving.</li>\n<li>For outdoor work, collect and properly dispose of trash, cable remnants, and materials.</li>\n<li><strong>Leave the site in the same condition you found it—or better.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Ceiling Tile Replacement</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If ceiling tiles are removed, complete a final walkthrough to ensure <strong>all tiles are replaced and properly seated</strong>before leaving.</li>\n<li>Missing or unsecured tiles may require a return trip.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>High-Profile Customer | Technician Instructions</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Professionalism &amp; Appearance</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Maintain professional conduct at all times.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Dress code:</strong> Long pants (jeans, khakis, or work pants), collared shirt (button-up or polo), and closed-toe shoes.</li>\n<li><strong>Not permitted:</strong> T-shirts, shorts, sandals, or graphic/offensive clothing.</li>\n<li>Carry a printed or digital copy of the work order to verify you are onsite on behalf of Connext.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Conduct &amp; Timing</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maintain a clean, safe work area and be courteous to staff and customers.</li>\n<li>Use Connext check-in/check-out times and MOD-signed work orders for time tracking and payment; do not rely on worker-platform timestamps.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Preparation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure you understand the scope and have the required tools before arriving.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Expenses &amp; Approvals</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Travel expenses must be preapproved before dispatch.</li>\n<li>Tolls and parking are reimbursable with valid receipts.</li>\n<li><strong>Additional onsite time must be approved by the Project Manager before exceeding the allotted time.</strong> Call the check-in/check-out line to request approval.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Closing the Job</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide complete notes, photos, and required deliverables when closing the ticket.</li>\n<li>Contact Connext immediately about unresolved issues, unexpected site conditions, or work outside the approved scope. Clearly explain the issue and what is needed to proceed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE ADD YOUR NAME ON THE BADGE UNDER DOCUMENTS AND PRINT OUT FOR USE ON SITE. PLEASE PUT IN A CLEAR BADGE HOLDER AND ON A LANYARD IF POSSIBLE.**\n\n**Important Site Protocol – Please Read Carefully**\n\n**To avoid monetary penalties, complete the following immediately after finishing work and before leaving the site:**\n\n- Check in and check out as instructed.\n- Obtain your release code.\n- Upload all required deliverables through Qualtrics using the link in the work order.\n- Close out the work order with detailed notes. Our team must provide the customer with job status updates each morning; incomplete closeout steps may result in a penalty.\n\n**Preparation Expectations**\n\n- **Read the entire work order before arriving.** If you arrive without the required tools or are unprepared to complete the assigned work, you will not be compensated for the visit.\n\n**Access Restrictions**\n\n- **You are not permitted onsite between 11:00 AM and 2:00 PM.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n**Ticket Number #VTASK0614223**\n\n- Coordinate with Operator**Ben\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***to identify the proposed AP installation location in the storage room.\n- Survey the area and determine the cable routing path and estimated cable length.\n- Determine whether the connection requires **fiber or CAT5/CAT6 cabling** based on distance and site conditions.\n- Identify any obstacles or additional materials needed to complete the installation.\n- Take **photos** of the **storage room and proposed AP location**.\n- **Provide a video walkthrough showing the proposed cable route and installation area.**\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- The storage room currently has no network connectivity. This survey is to determine the cabling requirements, installation path, and materials needed to add a Wi-Fi AP.\n\n**Out-of-Scope Tasks**\n\nIf a CFA representative requests work outside the listed scope,**contact Connext for direction before proceeding**, unless otherwise authorized.\n\n- Document all additional work performed and the time incurred.\n- Verified additional **labor beyond the original work order will be compensated** appropriately, subject to applicable approval requirements.\n\n**Additional Instructions**\n\n- **If replacement is specified, repairing the existing component does not satisfy the work order.**\n- Failure to complete the specified task may result in non-payment.\n- Contact Connext if any scope details are unclear.\n\n**Cable Management**\n\n- Secure and organize cables using cable ties, Velcro straps, cable trays, or other appropriate solutions.\n- Do not leave cables tangled, unsecured, or loosely draped across surfaces.\n\n**Site Cleanliness**\n\n- Remove all tools, loose cabling, packaging, and debris before leaving.\n- For outdoor work, collect and properly dispose of trash, cable remnants, and materials.\n- **Leave the site in the same condition you found it—or better.**\n\n**Ceiling Tile Replacement**\n\n- If ceiling tiles are removed, complete a final walkthrough to ensure **all tiles are replaced and properly seated**before leaving.\n- Missing or unsecured tiles may require a return trip.\n\n**High-Profile Customer | Technician Instructions**\n\n**Professionalism &amp; Appearance**\n\n- **Maintain professional conduct at all times.**\n- **Dress code:** Long pants (jeans, khakis, or work pants), collared shirt (button-up or polo), and closed-toe shoes.\n- **Not permitted:** T-shirts, shorts, sandals, or graphic/offensive clothing.\n- Carry a printed or digital copy of the work order to verify you are onsite on behalf of Connext.\n\n**Site Conduct &amp; Timing**\n\n- Maintain a clean, safe work area and be courteous to staff and customers.\n- Use Connext check-in/check-out times and MOD-signed work orders for time tracking and payment; do not rely on worker-platform timestamps.\n\n**Preparation**\n\n- Ensure you understand the scope and have the required tools before arriving.\n\n**Expenses &amp; Approvals**\n\n- Travel expenses must be preapproved before dispatch.\n- Tolls and parking are reimbursable with valid receipts.\n- **Additional onsite time must be approved by the Project Manager before exceeding the allotted time.** Call the check-in/check-out line to request approval.\n\n**Closing the Job**\n\n- Provide complete notes, photos, and required deliverables when closing the ticket.\n- Contact Connext immediately about unresolved issues, unexpected site conditions, or work outside the approved scope. Clearly explain the issue and what is needed to proceed.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T08:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.558136427491954},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793134765049}
{"job":{"id":20256616,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"APC UPS & Electrical System Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking <strong>one technician experienced in UPS systems, rack-mounted power equipment, and electrical site assessments</strong>.</li><li>Conduct a needs assessment and detailed evaluation of the existing UPS system and installation area.</li><li>Gather the information needed to prepare a quote and plan the replacement.</li><li>A licensed electrician should participate <strong>if electrical testing or access to energized electrical equipment is required</strong>.</li><li><strong>Date, time, and estimated duration:</strong> To be confirmed.</li><li>Introduce yourself as a <strong>technician from TechHub PS</strong>.</li></ul>1. Purpose<p>Survey the existing UPS system and associated electrical infrastructure to determine the labor, materials, equipment, outage window, and disposal requirements for the proposed replacement.</p><p>The planned installation includes:</p><ul><li><strong>APC Smart-UPS On-Line UPS:</strong> SRT8KRMXLT</li><li><strong>APC External Battery Pack:</strong> SRT192RMBP2</li><li><strong>APC Step-Down Transformer:</strong> SRT5KRMTF</li><li><strong>APC Maintenance Bypass Panel:</strong> SBP10KRMT4U</li><li><strong>APC Switched Rack PDU:</strong> AP7900B</li></ul><p><strong>This visit is for assessment and documentation only. Do not disconnect, power down, move, or replace equipment during the survey.</strong></p>2. Pre-Arrival Requirements<ul><li>Review the work order and proposed equipment list.</li><li>Confirm the survey date, site access, and onsite point of contact.</li><li>Confirm whether a licensed electrician will attend or be available.</li><li>Request any existing electrical drawings, rack elevations, UPS documentation, and equipment inventory available from the customer.</li><li>Bring a smartphone or camera, flashlight, tape measure, laptop, and required site PPE.</li><li>Coordinate with the site before taking photographs of equipment or restricted areas.</li></ul>3. Site Check-In &amp; Customer Requirements<p>Upon arrival:</p><ul><li>Check in with the onsite point of contact and TechHub PS.</li><li>Confirm the areas and equipment included in the survey.</li><li>Discuss the customer’s objectives for the UPS replacement and any known problems with the existing system.</li><li>Identify critical equipment supported by the UPS.</li><li>Discuss operating hours, access restrictions, and the process for approving a shutdown.</li><li>Confirm whether any equipment must remain powered during the replacement.</li></ul>4. Existing Equipment Assessment<p>Document the existing power system, including:</p><ul><li>UPS manufacturer, model, serial number, capacity, and condition.</li><li>Number and type of external battery packs or battery modules.</li><li>Existing transformer, maintenance bypass panel, and PDU details.</li><li>Equipment locations and whether components are rack-mounted or floor-mounted.</li><li>Visible alarms, damage, or other issues reported by site personnel.</li><li>Equipment connected to each PDU or UPS output, where identifiable.</li><li>Existing network management connections, if present.</li></ul><p>Record which equipment is expected to be removed and disposed of.</p>5. Electrical Infrastructure Assessment<p>The information provided states that the existing UPS is hardwired to a <strong>single-phase, 208V, 3-wire, 2-pole, 60A circuit with 6 AWG conductors</strong>. Verify and document these details from available labels, drawings, and site information.</p><p>Assess and record:</p><ul><li>Electrical panel and circuit identification.</li><li>Breaker rating and available disconnects.</li><li>Existing UPS input and output connections.</li><li>Conduit routing, visible wiring, and apparent condition.</li><li>Grounding arrangements as visible or documented.</li><li>Existing bypass and power-distribution connections.</li><li>Available circuit capacity and any information needed for a licensed electrician to evaluate it.</li><li>Whether existing conduit and conductors appear suitable for reuse, subject to electrician verification.</li><li>Any suspected electrical modifications, permits, or additional materials that may be required.</li></ul><p><strong>Do not open energized electrical panels or perform electrical measurements unless the work is authorized and performed by a qualified, licensed electrician using the required procedures and PPE.</strong></p>6. Rack &amp; Installation Area Assessment<ul><li>Measure available rack space and document existing equipment placement.</li><li>Confirm whether the rack or designated location can accommodate the proposed equipment.</li><li>Assess mounting rails, hardware, clearances, ventilation, and access for servicing.</li><li>Document the installation area, delivery path, doorways, elevators, and any stairs.</li><li>Identify any lifting equipment or additional personnel needed to handle the UPS, batteries, and transformer.</li><li>Note any obstacles that could affect equipment removal or installation.</li></ul>7. Proposed Equipment &amp; Compatibility Review<p>Review the proposed equipment list against the information collected onsite. Document any questions or exceptions requiring confirmation by the project team, APC, or the licensed electrician, including:</p><ul><li>Input and output voltage requirements.</li><li>UPS, battery pack, transformer, bypass, and PDU connections.</li><li>Plug, receptacle, hardwired connection, and cable requirements.</li><li>Rack space, mounting hardware, weight, and handling requirements.</li><li>Compatibility of the transformer and bypass arrangement with the planned loads.</li><li>Network management connections and available network drops.</li></ul><p><strong>Do not assume that all listed equipment is compatible with the existing system or with each other. Report any item that needs verification before a quote or installation is finalized.</strong></p>8. Load &amp; Outage Planning<ul><li>Identify and document the protected equipment and available load information.</li><li>Record UPS load readings or capacity information available on the display or from site personnel.</li><li>Determine whether critical loads can be shut down and for how long.</li><li>Discuss the required outage window and preferred installation hours.</li><li>Identify any need for temporary power or a phased transfer of loads.</li><li>Note dependencies, approvals, or site personnel required during installation and startup.</li></ul>9. Removal, Disposal &amp; Logistics<ul><li>Document the equipment and battery quantities to be removed.</li><li>Assess the removal route and any loading dock or vehicle access restrictions.</li><li>Identify handling requirements and whether additional technicians or lifting equipment will be needed.</li><li>Confirm whether the customer has specific disposal or recycling requirements.</li><li>Note any requirements for removal and disposal of batteries and decommissioned equipment.</li><li>Confirm where new equipment will be delivered and staged before installation.</li></ul>10. Required Photos &amp; Deliverables<p>Capture and submit clear photos, where permitted, of:</p><ul><li>Front and rear views of the existing rack and UPS equipment.</li><li>Model and serial number labels for existing equipment.</li><li>Existing batteries, transformer, bypass panel, and PDU.</li><li>Visible input and output connections, conduit, and cable routing.</li><li>Electrical panel and breaker labels, without opening energized equipment.</li><li>Existing rack space and installation area.</li><li>Delivery and equipment removal paths.</li><li>Any identified issues or site constraints.</li></ul><p>Submit a survey report including:</p><ul><li>Existing equipment inventory and condition.</li><li>Electrical circuit and connection details verified onsite.</li><li>Rack measurements and available space.</li><li>Protected-load information and shutdown requirements.</li><li>Recommended staffing, licensed electrician scope, tools, and lifting equipment.</li><li>Required materials and any anticipated infrastructure changes.</li><li>Equipment removal and disposal requirements.</li><li>Exceptions, compatibility questions, and items requiring further verification.</li><li>Recommended installation duration and outage window, based on survey findings.</li></ul>11. Check-Out &amp; Completion Requirements<p>Before leaving:</p><ul><li>Review key findings and any concerns with the onsite contact.</li><li>Confirm no equipment or connections have been disturbed.</li><li>Notify TechHub PS of any conditions that may affect the installation quote.</li><li>Submit all required photos and survey documentation.</li><li>Obtain onsite acknowledgment of the completed survey.</li><li>Check out with TechHub PS.</li></ul>12. Exclusions<p>This survey does not include:</p><ul><li>UPS installation, startup, or commissioning.</li><li>Electrical disconnection, reconnection, or repairs.</li><li>Moving or removing existing equipment.</li><li>Load transfer or system shutdown.</li><li>Disposal of equipment or batteries.</li><li>Detailed engineering studies, permit applications, or utility work.</li></ul>13. Escalation Contact<p><strong>Mathew Manik</strong></p><p><strong>Phone:</strong> (858) 321-3947</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> mbaroi@techhubps.com</p><p>Contact Mathew if there are access issues, missing information, safety concerns, or any condition that may affect the proposed installation.</p>14. Additional Hours &amp; Expenses<ul><li>All additional hours and expenses require prior written approval.</li><li>Any work outside this survey scope requires approval by email before proceeding.</li><li>Obtain the required sign-off before closing the work order.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**\n\n- Seeking **one technician experienced in UPS systems, rack-mounted power equipment, and electrical site assessments**.\n- Conduct a needs assessment and detailed evaluation of the existing UPS system and installation area.\n- Gather the information needed to prepare a quote and plan the replacement.\n- A licensed electrician should participate **if electrical testing or access to energized electrical equipment is required**.\n- **Date, time, and estimated duration:** To be confirmed.\n- Introduce yourself as a **technician from TechHub PS**.\n\n1. PurposeSurvey the existing UPS system and associated electrical infrastructure to determine the labor, materials, equipment, outage window, and disposal requirements for the proposed replacement.\n\nThe planned installation includes:\n\n- **APC Smart-UPS On-Line UPS:** SRT8KRMXLT\n- **APC External Battery Pack:** SRT192RMBP2\n- **APC Step-Down Transformer:** SRT5KRMTF\n- **APC Maintenance Bypass Panel:** SBP10KRMT4U\n- **APC Switched Rack PDU:** AP7900B\n\n**This visit is for assessment and documentation only. Do not disconnect, power down, move, or replace equipment during the survey.**\n\n2. Pre-Arrival Requirements- Review the work order and proposed equipment list.\n- Confirm the survey date, site access, and onsite point of contact.\n- Confirm whether a licensed electrician will attend or be available.\n- Request any existing electrical drawings, rack elevations, UPS documentation, and equipment inventory available from the customer.\n- Bring a smartphone or camera, flashlight, tape measure, laptop, and required site PPE.\n- Coordinate with the site before taking photographs of equipment or restricted areas.\n\n3. Site Check-In &amp; Customer RequirementsUpon arrival:\n\n- Check in with the onsite point of contact and TechHub PS.\n- Confirm the areas and equipment included in the survey.\n- Discuss the customer’s objectives for the UPS replacement and any known problems with the existing system.\n- Identify critical equipment supported by the UPS.\n- Discuss operating hours, access restrictions, and the process for approving a shutdown.\n- Confirm whether any equipment must remain powered during the replacement.\n\n4. Existing Equipment AssessmentDocument the existing power system, including:\n\n- UPS manufacturer, model, serial number, capacity, and condition.\n- Number and type of external battery packs or battery modules.\n- Existing transformer, maintenance bypass panel, and PDU details.\n- Equipment locations and whether components are rack-mounted or floor-mounted.\n- Visible alarms, damage, or other issues reported by site personnel.\n- Equipment connected to each PDU or UPS output, where identifiable.\n- Existing network management connections, if present.\n\nRecord which equipment is expected to be removed and disposed of.\n\n5. Electrical Infrastructure AssessmentThe information provided states that the existing UPS is hardwired to a **single-phase, 208V, 3-wire, 2-pole, 60A circuit with 6 AWG conductors**. Verify and document these details from available labels, drawings, and site information.\n\nAssess and record:\n\n- Electrical panel and circuit identification.\n- Breaker rating and available disconnects.\n- Existing UPS input and output connections.\n- Conduit routing, visible wiring, and apparent condition.\n- Grounding arrangements as visible or documented.\n- Existing bypass and power-distribution connections.\n- Available circuit capacity and any information needed for a licensed electrician to evaluate it.\n- Whether existing conduit and conductors appear suitable for reuse, subject to electrician verification.\n- Any suspected electrical modifications, permits, or additional materials that may be required.\n\n**Do not open energized electrical panels or perform electrical measurements unless the work is authorized and performed by a qualified, licensed electrician using the required procedures and PPE.**\n\n6. Rack &amp; Installation Area Assessment- Measure available rack space and document existing equipment placement.\n- Confirm whether the rack or designated location can accommodate the proposed equipment.\n- Assess mounting rails, hardware, clearances, ventilation, and access for servicing.\n- Document the installation area, delivery path, doorways, elevators, and any stairs.\n- Identify any lifting equipment or additional personnel needed to handle the UPS, batteries, and transformer.\n- Note any obstacles that could affect equipment removal or installation.\n\n7. Proposed Equipment &amp; Compatibility ReviewReview the proposed equipment list against the information collected onsite. Document any questions or exceptions requiring confirmation by the project team, APC, or the licensed electrician, including:\n\n- Input and output voltage requirements.\n- UPS, battery pack, transformer, bypass, and PDU connections.\n- Plug, receptacle, hardwired connection, and cable requirements.\n- Rack space, mounting hardware, weight, and handling requirements.\n- Compatibility of the transformer and bypass arrangement with the planned loads.\n- Network management connections and available network drops.\n\n**Do not assume that all listed equipment is compatible with the existing system or with each other. Report any item that needs verification before a quote or installation is finalized.**\n\n8. Load &amp; Outage Planning- Identify and document the protected equipment and available load information.\n- Record UPS load readings or capacity information available on the display or from site personnel.\n- Determine whether critical loads can be shut down and for how long.\n- Discuss the required outage window and preferred installation hours.\n- Identify any need for temporary power or a phased transfer of loads.\n- Note dependencies, approvals, or site personnel required during installation and startup.\n\n9. Removal, Disposal &amp; Logistics- Document the equipment and battery quantities to be removed.\n- Assess the removal route and any loading dock or vehicle access restrictions.\n- Identify handling requirements and whether additional technicians or lifting equipment will be needed.\n- Confirm whether the customer has specific disposal or recycling requirements.\n- Note any requirements for removal and disposal of batteries and decommissioned equipment.\n- Confirm where new equipment will be delivered and staged before installation.\n\n10. Required Photos &amp; DeliverablesCapture and submit clear photos, where permitted, of:\n\n- Front and rear views of the existing rack and UPS equipment.\n- Model and serial number labels for existing equipment.\n- Existing batteries, transformer, bypass panel, and PDU.\n- Visible input and output connections, conduit, and cable routing.\n- Electrical panel and breaker labels, without opening energized equipment.\n- Existing rack space and installation area.\n- Delivery and equipment removal paths.\n- Any identified issues or site constraints.\n\nSubmit a survey report including:\n\n- Existing equipment inventory and condition.\n- Electrical circuit and connection details verified onsite.\n- Rack measurements and available space.\n- Protected-load information and shutdown requirements.\n- Recommended staffing, licensed electrician scope, tools, and lifting equipment.\n- Required materials and any anticipated infrastructure changes.\n- Equipment removal and disposal requirements.\n- Exceptions, compatibility questions, and items requiring further verification.\n- Recommended installation duration and outage window, based on survey findings.\n\n11. Check-Out &amp; Completion RequirementsBefore leaving:\n\n- Review key findings and any concerns with the onsite contact.\n- Confirm no equipment or connections have been disturbed.\n- Notify TechHub PS of any conditions that may affect the installation quote.\n- Submit all required photos and survey documentation.\n- Obtain onsite acknowledgment of the completed survey.\n- Check out with TechHub PS.\n\n12. ExclusionsThis survey does not include:\n\n- UPS installation, startup, or commissioning.\n- Electrical disconnection, reconnection, or repairs.\n- Moving or removing existing equipment.\n- Load transfer or system shutdown.\n- Disposal of equipment or batteries.\n- Detailed engineering studies, permit applications, or utility work.\n\n13. Escalation Contact**Mathew Manik**\n\n**Phone:** (858) 321-3947\n\n**Email:** mbaroi@techhubps.com\n\nContact Mathew if there are access issues, missing information, safety concerns, or any condition that may affect the proposed installation.\n\n14. Additional Hours &amp; Expenses- All additional hours and expenses require prior written approval.\n- Any work outside this survey scope requires approval by email before proceeding.\n- Obtain the required sign-off before closing the work order.\n\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":57.67605465866834},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Savin