{"job":{"id":20257146,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CrossCom","title":"BOOM LIFT/PART/3762 CC - CCTV/Security Cameras/REPLACE EXTERIOR CAMERA #83 **HARD START 10/29 AT 9AM**","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Problem Description:</u></strong></p><p>BOOM LIFT/PART/3762 CC - CCTV/Security Cameras/REPLACE EXTERIOR CAMERA #83</p><p>**HARD START 10/29 AT 9AM**</p><p><br></p><p>**TECH MUST WORK WITH CROSSCOM L2 FOR TROUBLSHOOTING AND TO VERIFY CAMERA VIEWS**</p><p><br></p><p>**LAPTOP MUST HAVE THE AVIGILON ACC v7 CLIENT APP AND REMOTE SUPPORT ANYDESK APP INSTALLED, PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ON SITE VIA LINKS BELOW**</p><p><br></p><p>AVIGILON APP LINK: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1a6TVrnKrm7AUJ0m2H1qE45QoOwx-3Yov</p><p>ANYDESK APP LINK: https://anydesk.com/en/downloads/windows</p><p><br></p><p>SCOPE OF WORK: Exterior Camera # 83:South Side Exterior (192.168.1.83) is showing \"Not present\" We are sending a camera overnight. Replacement camer tracking ID:&nbsp;Please schedule a tech to install accordingly. The area can be accessed by the warehouse scissor lift.</p><p><br></p><p>Tech must work with Crosscom L2 to configure, and adjust the lenses to match the original views. Management and Crosscom L2 must verify views before leaving site. A picture is available in SharePoint for Crosscom L2 and the technician.</p><p><br></p><p>CLOSED HOURS ACCESS: Arrive through the trailer receiving area.</p><p><br></p><p>REQUIRED TOOLS:&nbsp;</p><p>1. Laptop with Windows 10/11 with an Ethernet Port, or a USB to Ethernet Port Adaptor</p><p>2. Thumb drive/USB drive&nbsp;</p><p>3. RJ45 Cable tester</p><p>4. Spare CAT6 Ethernet Patch Cables</p><p>5. Hot Spot for Internet Connectivity</p><p>6. Normal hand tools such as screwdrivers, pliers, wire cutters/snips, etc</p><p>7. Security Torx Bit Set</p><p>8. 300ft CAT6 White Cable (Minimum)</p><p>9. Screw Size #8-32, 5/8in, with matching nuts.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***ALL TRACKING FOR PARTS MUST BE CHECKED PRIOR TO ARRIVAL***</strong></p><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Butt Set with monitor mode</li><li>Box of Cable / connectors / jacks / etc</li><li>Punch down tool</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Electronic label maker</li><li>100’ fish tape (minimum length)</li><li>Toner and probe</li><li>Battery operated drill with bits as required</li><li>Minimum 8 ft. ladder</li><li>Data Cable Tester</li><li>Laptop with Internet Connectivity</li><li>Multi-meter</li></ul><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong>​</p><ol><li>Review Problem Description to make sure you have all the needed materials and tools and can meet the SLA.</li><li>Set your ETA in the Tasks section.</li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong>​</p><ol><li><strong><u>***NOTE - CALLING THE CROSSCOM IVR, WILL ALSO GET YOU TO TECHNICAL SUPPORT AND THE SERVICE TEAM THAT HANDLES THIS ACCOUNT.&nbsp;THEY CAN ANSWER ANY QUESTIONS YOU HAVE, LISTEN TO ALL PROMPTS***</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>***Provider- Please note upon arriving to site please call the 1800 number and log into the work order this is the time by which you will be paid – both log in and log out times will be recorded – logging in from the FN work order is not the time by which you will be paid***</u></strong></li><li>Call&nbsp;to check-in with the CrossCom IVR&nbsp;800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT #&nbsp;62097.</li><li>Check-in to work order on the FN platform</li><li>Introduce yourself to MOD and Provide Customer Order, if one was provided above</li><li>Take before pictures</li><li>Complete install/troubleshooting per Problem Description above and/or work with Level II support to confirm work.</li><li>Clean area fully, DO NOT LEAVE A MESS!&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Check-Out on work order</li><li>Call&nbsp;to check Out with CrossCom, call the IVR&nbsp;800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT #&nbsp;62097, it will transfer you to the Service Team that handles this customer.</li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong>​</p><ol><li>Upload photos of each item/cabling that was installed/troubleshot. If available; before and after pics.</li><li>Get Manager on Duty's Signature</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>All damaged items MUST be relayed to the CrossCom Level I Service Team and photos must be provided.&nbsp;</li><li>If clarification is needed on where to install, speak with the MOD and/or CrossCom Level I Service Team.</li><li>Visits are to be conducted during business hours with a start time of 8:00am</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to CrossCom Level I Service Team ASAP while onsite.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY</u></strong></p><ul><li>Buyer&nbsp;does not pay travel or parking expenses unless pre-approved and receipts submitted. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by messaging the Work Order Manager.&nbsp;If approved the Buyer will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li><li>Buyer&nbsp;does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling the Service Team via the CrossCom IVR. If approved the Service Team will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them/receipts and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.</li><li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the Level I Service Team. If approved, the Buyer&nbsp;will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Problem Description:**\n\nBOOM LIFT/PART/3762 CC - CCTV/Security Cameras/REPLACE EXTERIOR CAMERA #83\n\n\\*\\*HARD START 10/29 AT 9AM\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*TECH MUST WORK WITH CROSSCOM L2 FOR TROUBLSHOOTING AND TO VERIFY CAMERA VIEWS\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*LAPTOP MUST HAVE THE AVIGILON ACC v7 CLIENT APP AND REMOTE SUPPORT ANYDESK APP INSTALLED, PRIOR TO ARRIVAL ON SITE VIA LINKS BELOW\\*\\*\n\nAVIGILON APP LINK: <https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1a6TVrnKrm7AUJ0m2H1qE45QoOwx-3Yov>\n\nANYDESK APP LINK: <https://anydesk.com/en/downloads/windows>\n\nSCOPE OF WORK: Exterior Camera # 83:South Side Exterior (192.168.1.83) is showing \"Not present\" We are sending a camera overnight. Replacement camer tracking ID: Please schedule a tech to install accordingly. The area can be accessed by the warehouse scissor lift.\n\nTech must work with Crosscom L2 to configure, and adjust the lenses to match the original views. Management and Crosscom L2 must verify views before leaving site. A picture is available in SharePoint for Crosscom L2 and the technician.\n\nCLOSED HOURS ACCESS: Arrive through the trailer receiving area.\n\nREQUIRED TOOLS:\n\n1\\. Laptop with Windows 10/11 with an Ethernet Port, or a USB to Ethernet Port Adaptor\n\n2\\. Thumb drive/USB drive\n\n3\\. RJ45 Cable tester\n\n4\\. Spare CAT6 Ethernet Patch Cables\n\n5\\. Hot Spot for Internet Connectivity\n\n6\\. Normal hand tools such as screwdrivers, pliers, wire cutters/snips, etc\n\n7\\. Security Torx Bit Set\n\n8\\. 300ft CAT6 White Cable (Minimum)\n\n9\\. Screw Size #8-32, 5/8in, with matching nuts.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*ALL TRACKING FOR PARTS MUST BE CHECKED PRIOR TO ARRIVAL\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Butt Set with monitor mode\n- Box of Cable / connectors / jacks / etc\n- Punch down tool\n- Basic hand tools\n- Electronic label maker\n- 100’ fish tape (minimum length)\n- Toner and probe\n- Battery operated drill with bits as required\n- Minimum 8 ft. ladder\n- Data Cable Tester\n- Laptop with Internet Connectivity\n- Multi-meter\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***​\n\n1. Review Problem Description to make sure you have all the needed materials and tools and can meet the SLA.\n2. Set your ETA in the Tasks section.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***​\n\n1. **\\*\\*\\*NOTE - CALLING THE CROSSCOM IVR, WILL ALSO GET YOU TO TECHNICAL SUPPORT AND THE SERVICE TEAM THAT HANDLES THIS ACCOUNT. THEY CAN ANSWER ANY QUESTIONS YOU HAVE, LISTEN TO ALL PROMPTS\\*\\*\\***\n2. **\\*\\*\\*Provider- Please note upon arriving to site please call the 1800 number and log into the work order this is the time by which you will be paid – both log in and log out times will be recorded – logging in from the FN work order is not the time by which you will be paid\\*\\*\\***\n3. Call to check-in with the CrossCom IVR 800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT # 62097.\n4. Check-in to work order on the FN platform\n5. Introduce yourself to MOD and Provide Customer Order, if one was provided above\n6. Take before pictures\n7. Complete install/troubleshooting per Problem Description above and/or work with Level II support to confirm work.\n8. Clean area fully, DO NOT LEAVE A MESS!\n9. Check-Out on work order\n10. Call to check Out with CrossCom, call the IVR 800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT # 62097, it will transfer you to the Service Team that handles this customer.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***​\n\n1. Upload photos of each item/cabling that was installed/troubleshot. If available; before and after pics.\n2. Get Manager on Duty's Signature\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- All damaged items MUST be relayed to the CrossCom Level I Service Team and photos must be provided.\n- If clarification is needed on where to install, speak with the MOD and/or CrossCom Level I Service Team.\n- Visits are to be conducted during business hours with a start time of 8:00am\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to CrossCom Level I Service Team ASAP while onsite.\n\n**ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY**\n\n- Buyer does not pay travel or parking expenses unless pre-approved and receipts submitted. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by messaging the Work Order Manager. If approved the Buyer will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.\n- Buyer does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling the Service Team via the CrossCom IVR. If approved the Service Team will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them/receipts and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the Level I Service Team. If approved, the Buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":8.023247401875496},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.00