{"job":{"id":20257695,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Old Navy - Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Title: Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting</p>\n<p>Please ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable</p>\n<p>Switch (S/n: Q2AX-KAPJ-KQX9) s05966cwsw08 is located in Register 407/408</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (sw01) : port 27.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>When on site, check in with Store Network at 1-800-869-8490</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.</p>\n<p>If any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.</p>\n<p>If we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.</p>\n<p>To reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>After performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>For more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>Basic Tools</p>\n<p>working laptop with the updated driver</p>\n<p>Console Cables</p>\n<p>Cat5 Cable</p>\n<p>Cable tester</p>\n<p>Internet dongle</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)</p>\n<p>-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN</p>\n<p>-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app</p>\n<p>-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1</p>\n<p>-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>While Onsite:</p>\n<p>- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Checkout Requirements:</p>\n<p>-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)</p>\n<p>-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Deliverables:</p>\n<p>-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com</p>\n<p>-MOD email for Survey</p>","markdown":"Check In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope listed below to be completed:\n\nTitle: Meraki 8 Port Troubleshooting\n\nPlease ensure all the require equipment to carry E.G Laptop + internet + cable + cable tester + console cable\n\nSwitch (S/n: Q2AX-KAPJ-KQX9) s05966cwsw08 is located in Register 407/408\n\nTech will need to check the patch cable between patch panel and main switch (sw01) : port 27.\n\nWhen on site, check in with Store Network at 1-800-869-8490\n\nTech needs to firstly verify there is power to the network switch (ON/OFF) and check the color of the lights flashing on the switch.\n\nTech must check the end-to-end cabling between 48-port switch and 8-port switch.\n\nIf any pairs are missing or faulty then re-terminate the cables on both the ends and re-crimp the cable on patch panel end.\n\nIf we want to confirm it's a home-run cable issue, the 8-port switch can be plugged directly into 48-port switch and then the connectivity can be checked again.\n\nIf the cable is good and the port still is not coming up, try changing the port on 48-Port switch and check again.\n\nIf there are no LED lights coming on the 8-port switch, perform a factory reset and check again.\n\nTo reset an MS switch to the factory defaults (in coordination with Store network team as the switch configuration will be wiped out), press the button labeled 'Reset' or 'Restore' (Indicated by arrow in the below image) on the front panel of the appliance for 10-15 seconds. Be sure to release the button after the power light goes out. This will clear the static IP address settings and local configuration of the device.\n\nAfter performing all the above steps if the issue remains unresolved, partner with the store network team for next step actions\n\nFor more troubleshooting/confirmation prior to start activity please call on: 800-869-8490 (GTI L2 Network support team)\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nBasic Tools\n\nworking laptop with the updated driver\n\nConsole Cables\n\nCat5 Cable\n\nCable tester\n\nInternet dongle\n\nCheck In Requirements: (Upon arrival to the site)\n\n-TECHNICIANS WHO HAVE ACCESS TO SIGN INTO A MOBILE APP NO LONGER NEED TO CALL SPENCER SERVICE TO CHECK IN\n\n-Technician must be onsite before checking into the Mobile app\n\n-If you have any questions or issues while on site, or if you do not have access to sign in via a Mobile App, contact Spencer Service 508-635-2100 opt 1\n\n-Tech must call GTI at 800-869-8490, to confirm scope to be complete.\n\nWhile Onsite:\n\n\\- Tech to perform Health Check with GTI at 800-869-8490. If GTI is not available, you may perform the Health check with Spencer Support at (877-541-0547, opt 2\n\nCheckout Requirements:\n\n-Tech must check-out with the Spencer Service Department (877-541-0547, opt 1)\n\n-Tech to take after photo, and submit with before to Service.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n-Tech must send before and after photos to both QCPictures@spencertech.com; FTD@spencertech.com\n\n-MOD email for Survey","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T11:00","end":"2026-10-28T15:00","latestStart":"2026-10-28T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.701467607464195},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Oct 28, 11:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 28, Thu, Oct 29, Fri, Oct 30 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793151423897}
{"job":{"id":20257766,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"Imbox Breakdown device(Machine Not Spraying)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*******PLEASE READ ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*********</strong></p><p><strong><u>-----------------THIS IS FOR A SHOE PROTECTION SPRAY KIOSK------------------------</u></strong></p><p><em>-------------------------ALL GUIDES ARE PROVIDED BELOW-----------------------------</em></p><p>***TECH WILL NEED ALL EQUIPMENT FROM REQUIRED LIST BELOW***</p><p><strong><em>Please read the entire work order before requesting this job.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Please read the attached documentation and print out the installation check list as needed before service.</strong></p><p><strong><em>TECH: Please call Work Order Manager (see ticket) when you first arrive. If additional technical assistance is needed, please reach out to WO manager to connect to support.</em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(28, 37, 46);\">522010313 /</span><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">machine is not spraying only after you prime it</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">1. replace filters</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">2. DEO pump swap if available</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">3. Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">4. Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">5. Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses. Bring a syringe (IM550500) if available to clear the air from the pump if pump swap not performed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">6. Replace top filter</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">7. Deep clean</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">Any parts not used please send back to POSRG</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>!!!!Run Diagnostics report and take picture, send to WOM before starting troubleshooting!!!!!!!ref. imbox touch screen nav guide pg 8 and 9.</u></strong></p><p>run a diagnostic report- send results to WO ( <strong>determine if fuse needs replacing)</strong></p><p><strong>Do a spray test first before following troubleshooting steps. see pg 6-7 nozzle replacement guide.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>2.Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.</p><p>3.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.</p><p>4.4.Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses.</p><p>5. replace check valves, suction lids, and quick connectors</p><p>1. Replace nozzles and filters if spraying and if needed.<strong>(spray nozzle replacement guide)</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(99, 115, 129);\">Ensure when replacing that nozzles are oriented in the correct direction, and that the hoses are fastened properly</span></p><p>2. If machine is not spraying do a Fluid Cannister Fix <strong>(fluid cannister guide)</strong></p><p>3,Inspect weld on straws inside of fluid cannister. Swap quick connectors.</p><p>4.Disconnect both input and output of spray pump. Using compressed air insert through input of pump and try to unclog spray pump.</p><p>5. If it's not spraying after quick fixes, swap the spray pump with deo pump.<strong>PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP</strong>. <strong>(deo swap guide)</strong></p><p>6. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid</p><p>7. do test treatment again, record a video and send as deliverable to WOM<strong>(spray nozzle replacement guide pg 6 and7)</strong></p><p>8. Do steps 4 and 5 again.</p><p>9.deep cleaning of top chamber.</p><p>.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.</p><p>Check fluid cannister straw and quick connect coupling, see if it has teflon tape applied to it, if not, apply teflon tape to the threads. Make sure the quick connect and the straw are tight, it should not be able to wiggle it. 3. If it's not spraying after the fluid cannister fix and nozzle replacement, swap the spray pump with deo pump. PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP. 4. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid 5. do test treatment, record a video and send as deliverable 6. Do steps 4 and 5 again. 7.deep cleaning of top chamber. 8. replace fuse (if needed, check diagnostic report first</p><p>Send back the old check valve. Write the machine's serial number and the task number on a piece of paper.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><em>If any pieces are missing from the shipped unit please inform the work order manager immediately.</em></p><p><strong><del>***</del>Failure to check in may result in a loss of compensation and any travel expenses.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be Paid</u></strong></p><p><strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>check in/out with POSRG work order manager.</p><p>The Imbox has been tested and is functioning before departure.</p><p>Complete the check list and attach photos to the work order.</p><p>Leave detailed closing notes.</p><p><strong><u>Duration on Site</u></strong></p><p>An experienced technician can be done in about 2 hours.If more time is needed the technician is required to call the work order manager to get approval. Failure to get approval will result in nonpayment.</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools</u></strong></p><p>Tools:</p><ul><li>Torx bit bet (T6 – T30)</li><li>Precision screwdriver set</li><li>Screwdriver set</li><li>Digital multimeter</li><li>Curved needle nose</li><li>Socket set (5.5mm, 10mm, etc.)</li><li>2 Adjustable wrenches</li><li>Wrench set</li><li>Flashlight/ light</li></ul><p>Materials:</p><ul><li>Teflon Tape</li><li>Electrical Tape</li><li>Compressed Air (Duster)</li></ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*PLEASE READ ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**-----------------THIS IS FOR A SHOE PROTECTION SPRAY KIOSK------------------------**\n\n*-------------------------ALL GUIDES ARE PROVIDED BELOW-----------------------------*\n\n\\*\\*\\*TECH WILL NEED ALL EQUIPMENT FROM REQUIRED LIST BELOW\\*\\*\\*\n\n***Please read the entire work order before requesting this job.***\n\n**Please read the attached documentation and print out the installation check list as needed before service.**\n\n***TECH: Please call Work Order Manager (see ticket) when you first arrive. If additional technical assistance is needed, please reach out to WO manager to connect to support.***\n\n522010313 /machine is not spraying only after you prime it\n\n1\\. replace filters\n\n2\\. DEO pump swap if available\n\n3\\. Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.\n\n4\\. Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle\n\n5\\. Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses. Bring a syringe (IM550500) if available to clear the air from the pump if pump swap not performed\n\n6\\. Replace top filter\n\n7\\. Deep clean\n\nAny parts not used please send back to POSRG\n\n**!!!!Run Diagnostics report and take picture, send to WOM before starting troubleshooting!!!!!!!ref. imbox touch screen nav guide pg 8 and 9.**\n\nrun a diagnostic report- send results to WO ( **determine if fuse needs replacing)**\n\n**Do a spray test first before following troubleshooting steps. see pg 6-7 nozzle replacement guide.**\n\n2.Check the Canister &amp; Canister Cap/ check valve Inspect for any holes, cracks, or damage/ if its clog or stuck Make sure there’s nothing clogging the canister or the cap.\n\n3.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.\n\n4.4.Check the Blue Hoses-Make sure there are no clogs or blockages in the hoses.\n\n5\\. replace check valves, suction lids, and quick connectors\n\n1\\. Replace nozzles and filters if spraying and if needed.**(spray nozzle replacement guide)**\n\nEnsure when replacing that nozzles are oriented in the correct direction, and that the hoses are fastened properly\n\n2\\. If machine is not spraying do a Fluid Cannister Fix **(fluid cannister guide)**\n\n3,Inspect weld on straws inside of fluid cannister. Swap quick connectors.\n\n4.Disconnect both input and output of spray pump. Using compressed air insert through input of pump and try to unclog spray pump.\n\n5\\. If it's not spraying after quick fixes, swap the spray pump with deo pump.**PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP**. **(deo swap guide)**\n\n6\\. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid\n\n7\\. do test treatment again, record a video and send as deliverable to WOM**(spray nozzle replacement guide pg 6 and7)**\n\n8\\. Do steps 4 and 5 again.\n\n9.deep cleaning of top chamber.\n\n.Check if Teflon tape has been applied to the threads. If not, apply Teflon tape securely. Ensure the quick connect and straw are tight — they should not wiggle.\n\nCheck fluid cannister straw and quick connect coupling, see if it has teflon tape applied to it, if not, apply teflon tape to the threads. Make sure the quick connect and the straw are tight, it should not be able to wiggle it. 3. If it's not spraying after the fluid cannister fix and nozzle replacement, swap the spray pump with deo pump. PLEASE DO NOT STRIP THE PLASTIC THREAD PART OF THE DEO PUMP. 4. do priming extended.js to prime the fluid 5. do test treatment, record a video and send as deliverable 6. Do steps 4 and 5 again. 7.deep cleaning of top chamber. 8. replace fuse (if needed, check diagnostic report first\n\nSend back the old check valve. Write the machine's serial number and the task number on a piece of paper.\n\n*If any pieces are missing from the shipped unit please inform the work order manager immediately.*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Failure to check in may result in a loss of compensation and any travel expenses.**\n\n**Required Deliverables to be Paid**\n\n**MUST** check in/out with POSRG work order manager.\n\nThe Imbox has been tested and is functioning before departure.\n\nComplete the check list and attach photos to the work order.\n\nLeave detailed closing notes.\n\n**Duration on Site**\n\nAn experienced technician can be done in about 2 hours.If more time is needed the technician is required to call the work order manager to get approval. Failure to get approval will result in nonpayment.\n\n**Required Tools**\n\nTools:\n\n- Torx bit bet (T6 – T30)\n- Precision screwdriver set\n- Screwdriver set\n- Digital multimeter\n- Curved needle nose\n- Socket set (5.5mm, 10mm, etc.)\n- 2 Adjustable wrenches\n- Wrench set\n- Flashlight/ light\n\nMaterials:\n\n- Teflon Tape\n- Electrical Tape\n- Compressed Air (Duster)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T11:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":9.395062464544862},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 (countered: $210) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793152960491}
