{"job":{"id":20256712,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Multi-line ATA Cutover and Porting","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p><strong><p>Install dataremote in the fuel island shack, mount and test LTE and phone line, customer will cross connect to their intercom at later date</p>\r\n<p>LTE ONLY</p>\r\n<p>89852350526012042477<br />90X2000015367<br />CCDB0457BD4D<br />9843060121 Line 1 Intercom</p></strong></p><p><strong><u>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><strong style=\"color: black;\"><em>You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in.&nbsp;Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details act, as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.</em></strong></p><p><strong>﻿♦ ON TIME ARRIVAL IS VERY IMPORTANT</strong></p><p>Dispatch is related to a coordinated porting of lines from a different provider. There is a time sensitive work to complete. <strong><u>Arriving on time is crucial.</u></strong> <strong>PLEASE CONTACT SPECTROTEL ON ANY DELAYS.</strong></p><p><strong>﻿♦ Contacts</strong></p><p><u>Technician must have valid photo ID</u></p><p>Please reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</p><p>You must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section..</p><p><strong>♦ Material and Equipment Requirements</strong></p><p>Tech <u>MUST</u> have inside their bag when going inside the building <strong>**NON-NEGOTIABLE**. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.</strong></p><ul><li>FULL Charged Windows Laptop with RJ45 ethernet port &amp; Power Supply</li><li>Test/Butt Set</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Cat5 or CAT6 cabling,</li><li>Jacks, Mod ends, RJ11/RJ45 Ends, low voltage Termination equipment.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Available Equipment to have In Your Truck </u></strong></p><ul><li>CAT5 or CAT6 Cable; you may require to run new wiring to accommodate cutover to new equipment.</li><li>Labeling Tools like P-touch or tags</li></ul><p>The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.</p><p>The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch <strong>(Please itemize charges)</strong></p><p><strong><u>Experience Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>Tech must have experience with POTS troubleshooting and low voltage internal Wiring, cross connect and termination.</li><li>Tracing analog wiring: toning down wiring to locate termination ends.</li><li>POTS line Testing, locating labels, running inbound and outbound calls.</li><li>Properly Terminating analog line wiring to telco 110/66 block, Biscuit jacks.</li><li>Use cable tester/Multimeter to verify shorts or opens on the line.</li><li>Low voltage best practice termination, draping and labeling.</li><li>All new cabling must be properly draped and secured without obstruction of other equipment or wiring.</li><li>Spectrotel Equipment firmly secure to plywood/backboard</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Dispatch Description and Actions BEFORE moving any wiring.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Locate ATA installed previously that has Spectrotel labels.</li><li>Take photos before starting any work; photos must be clear. Take pictures of the Demarc of the lines getting migrated and ATA equipment.</li><li>Verify Spectrotel equipment is working and powered on. Run inbound and outbound test calls on the lines on the ATA before starting work. <strong><u>Notify Spectrotel of any problems.</u></strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Verify 911 by calling 933 on each line on the ATA.</u></strong></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\">Locate lines that are listed below as part of the port; you MUST RUN INBOUND AND OUTBOUND TEST CALLS on every line before starting work. </span><strong><u>Notify Spectrotel of any lines down prior to cutover. </u></strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Identify internal wires for the lines getting migrated; </u></strong><strong><u>write down their current position/location</u></strong> at the demarc in case we need to revert.</li><li>If moving elevator Lines; run test from elevator before moving any wiring.</li><li>If moving alarm Lines; verify if the alarm panel screen shows any error codes or CO line alerts.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Dispatch Description and Actions : </u></strong><strong><u>Cutover and Move Cross Connects</u></strong></p><ul><li>Remove old LEC Wiring from demarc; connect and cross connect from the ATA port to the Internal wiring for their respective lines.</li><li>Take final pictures that show all the wiring completed and labeling.</li><li>If moved elevator lines, make test calls after moving wires; go to Elevator and press call button.</li><li>If moved alarm lines; verify if the alarm panel screen shows any error codes or CO line alerts.</li><li>Run test calls for voice lines moved.</li><li>Run test calls for fax line moved.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>If job requires Significant wiring work , the tech must provide the following before leaving the site:</strong></p><ul><li>Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):</li><li>Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details):</li><li>Estimated Distance (ft):</li><li>Conduit/path Confirmed Available:</li><li>Estimate Labor Man Hours:</li><li>Estimate of ALL Materials &amp; Cost:</li><li>Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables</strong></p><p>Detailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.</p><p>We request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.</p><p>Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.</p><p>Please provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order. Limit to a max of 30 pictures.</p><p>If a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.</p>","markdown":"**SOW**\n\n**Install dataremote in the fuel island shack, mount and test LTE and phone line, customer will cross connect to their intercom at later date\n\nLTE ONLY\n\n89852350526012042477  \n90X2000015367  \nCCDB0457BD4D  \n9843060121 Line 1 Intercom**\n\n**-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n ***You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details act, as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.***\n\n**﻿♦ ON TIME ARRIVAL IS VERY IMPORTANT**\n\nDispatch is related to a coordinated porting of lines from a different provider. There is a time sensitive work to complete. **Arriving on time is crucial.** **PLEASE CONTACT SPECTROTEL ON ANY DELAYS.**\n\n**﻿♦ Contacts**\n\nTechnician must have valid photo ID\n\nPlease reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.\n\nYou must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section..\n\n**♦ Material and Equipment Requirements**\n\nTech MUST have inside their bag when going inside the building **\\*\\*NON-NEGOTIABLE\\*\\*. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.**\n\n- FULL Charged Windows Laptop with RJ45 ethernet port &amp; Power Supply\n- Test/Butt Set\n- Tone Generator and Wand\n- Cat5 or CAT6 cabling,\n- Jacks, Mod ends, RJ11/RJ45 Ends, low voltage Termination equipment.\n\n**Available Equipment to have In Your Truck**\n\n- CAT5 or CAT6 Cable; you may require to run new wiring to accommodate cutover to new equipment.\n- Labeling Tools like P-touch or tags\n\nThe provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.\n\nThe technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch **(Please itemize charges)**\n\n**Experience Requirements**\n\n- Tech must have experience with POTS troubleshooting and low voltage internal Wiring, cross connect and termination.\n- Tracing analog wiring: toning down wiring to locate termination ends.\n- POTS line Testing, locating labels, running inbound and outbound calls.\n- Properly Terminating analog line wiring to telco 110/66 block, Biscuit jacks.\n- Use cable tester/Multimeter to verify shorts or opens on the line.\n- Low voltage best practice termination, draping and labeling.\n- All new cabling must be properly draped and secured without obstruction of other equipment or wiring.\n- Spectrotel Equipment firmly secure to plywood/backboard\n\n**Dispatch Description and Actions BEFORE moving any wiring.**\n\n- Locate ATA installed previously that has Spectrotel labels.\n- Take photos before starting any work; photos must be clear. Take pictures of the Demarc of the lines getting migrated and ATA equipment.\n- Verify Spectrotel equipment is working and powered on. Run inbound and outbound test calls on the lines on the ATA before starting work. **Notify Spectrotel of any problems.**\n- **Verify 911 by calling 933 on each line on the ATA.**\n- Locate lines that are listed below as part of the port; you MUST RUN INBOUND AND OUTBOUND TEST CALLS on every line before starting work. **Notify Spectrotel of any lines down prior to cutover.**\n- **Identify internal wires for the lines getting migrated;** **write down their current position/location** at the demarc in case we need to revert.\n- If moving elevator Lines; run test from elevator before moving any wiring.\n- If moving alarm Lines; verify if the alarm panel screen shows any error codes or CO line alerts.\n\n**Dispatch Description and Actions :** **Cutover and Move Cross Connects**\n\n- Remove old LEC Wiring from demarc; connect and cross connect from the ATA port to the Internal wiring for their respective lines.\n- Take final pictures that show all the wiring completed and labeling.\n- If moved elevator lines, make test calls after moving wires; go to Elevator and press call button.\n- If moved alarm lines; verify if the alarm panel screen shows any error codes or CO line alerts.\n- Run test calls for voice lines moved.\n- Run test calls for fax line moved.\n\n**If job requires Significant wiring work , the tech must provide the following before leaving the site:**\n\n- Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):\n- Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details):\n- Estimated Distance (ft):\n- Conduit/path Confirmed Available:\n- Estimate Labor Man Hours:\n- Estimate of ALL Materials &amp; Cost:\n- Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift).\n\n**♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables**\n\nDetailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.\n\nWe request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.\n\nSubsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.\n\nPlease provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order. Limit to a max of 30 pictures.\n\nIf a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.526422909827697},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T2