{"job":{"id":20258683,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Equipment Configuration/Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>--------------------</u>JOB DETAILS<u>--------------------</u></strong></p><p>Tech is to install Wattbox and BEC. Tech is to connect AT&amp;T modem and test, See below for circuit information.</p><p><strong><u>﻿</u><p><b>Task ID:</b> 5410074<br />\n<b>PON:</b> 462973<br />\n<b>Account Name:</b> Olsen Orthodontics<br />\n<b>Service Address:</b> 1508 NC Hwy 24-87, Cameron, NC 28326</p>\n<p><b>Smart Hands</b><br />\n<br />\n<b>SOW:</b> <br />\nTech Requested to set up NEW WATTBOX device AND Test/Cutover new Internet Circuit and assist with connecting network to BOX during Outage Downtime<br />\n<br />\nPlease arrive at designated time, as we only have 1 hour to perform this cutover.<br />\n<br />\nDesign of Wattbox Configuration<br />\n• Meraki Firewall – Wattbox Port 1 <br />\n• Meraki Switch – Wattbox Port 2<br />\n• BEC – Wattbox Port 3 <br />\n• ISP Equipment-Modem – Wattbox port 4<br />\n• ISP Equipment-Router – Wattbox port 5 (if needed)<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<b>Special Notes:</b> SCOPE OF WORK<br />\n<br />\nINSTALL IOW and Wattbox --- TEST NEW CARRIER MODEM.<br />\nVERIFY IOW AND NEW CARRIER MODEM IS CONNECTED TO MERAKI and Wattbox . CALL SMILE DR IT TO VERIFY NEW IP&#x27;S ARE WORKING AND SERVICE IS CUTOVER - DO NOT LET TECH LEAVE WITHOUT SPEAKING TO SMILE DR IT TEAM and Verifying IP<br />\n<br />\nONLY CALL THE ABOVE 4 SMILE DR IT contacts<br />\n<br />\n<br />\nSpectrum: IOC 500/20 Mbps Static Internet 3YT<br />\n<br />\nWireless MAC: 94f7bea09f65<br />\nWireless Make: SercommCorporation<br />\nWireless Model: sax1v1r<br />\n| Data Mac: c44fd5aca708<br />\nData Make: Technicolor<br />\nData Model: ET2251<br />\n<br />\nIP: 24.196.200.154<br />\nGW: 24.196.200.153<br />\nSUBNET: 255.255.255.252<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n <br />\n<br />\n<br />\nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.</p>\n</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;<u>------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Tech Requirements</u></strong></p><p><strong>Tech must have Laptop with ethernet port and console cable, hotspot, test set. toner and probe, cat6 cable. Must have a working laptop and phone with working camera.&nbsp;A Site survey form is attached and may need to be completed and attached at closeout if the install fails.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>Service Description</u></strong></p><p><strong>Install Bec and install and test IOC and IOW Circuits. Tech may need to extend BEC to acceptable signal/working location. If extension cannot be done that day tech is to provide written quote for labor and material. Tech may also need to extend IOC/IOF depending where carrier has installed if circuit needs to be extended and cannot be done that day tech will provide written quote for labor and materials</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>SOW</u></strong></p><ol><li>Tech is to check in with Practice Director on site then call Spectrotel&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to check in and for support.</li><li>Tech should see Practice Director for box containing BEC.</li><li>Spectrotel and tech will setup BEC in spare outlet next to Meraki equipment and test IOW and confirm speeds.</li><li>Spectrotel and tech will work to test IOC/IOF circuits and confirm speeds.</li><li>Spectrotel and Tech will call Smile Doctors IT Support Alex&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to connect BEC and IOC/IOF Circuits.</li><li>BEC should be installed somewhere so that antennas have full range of motion without interference of metal objects.</li><li>Once proper location is found for BEC and test results are approved by support work with Smile Doctors support to connect to network.</li><li>Smile Doctors team will test circuits and confirm services.</li><li>Failover may or may not be done during dispatch. If testing is being performed that day tech will stand by until test is completed 10-20 minutes.</li><li>Tech is to take photos and upload to FN Platform and check out with Practice Director and Spectrotel</li></ol><p><strong>&nbsp;<u>------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿♦ Contacts</strong></p><p>Please reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</p><p>You must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.</p><p><strong>♦ Material and Equipment</strong></p><p>The technician will need standard network or telecom materials and tools, dependent on the Type of Work. - Windows Laptop with ethernet port, console cable, butt set/test set, cable toner and probe, punch down tool, cable, jacks, mod ends, etc.</p><p>The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.</p><p>The technician should have AnyDesk (www.anydesk.com) and TeamViewer installed for remote access support requests.</p><p>The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)</p><p>Technician is required to be proficient in knowing how to configure their laptop for DCHP and/or Static IP use without instruction</p><p>Technician is required to bring a Windows 10/11 laptop that has a working RJ45 ethernet jack</p><p>If technician is utilizing an Ethernet to USB adapter, then please make sure that it is a USB 3.0 adapter with all drivers updated</p><p>Technician's laptop is required to be rated for 1Gbps speeds</p><p>Technician is required to bring a mobile hotspot that is not their cell phone</p><p>Please bring patch cables, a power strip, and all tools and materials needed to complete the work order.</p>","markdown":"**--------------------JOB DETAILS--------------------**\n\nTech is to install Wattbox and BEC. Tech is to connect AT&amp;T modem and test, See below for circuit information.\n\n**﻿**Task ID:** 5410074  \n**PON:** 462973  \n**Account Name:** Olsen Orthodontics  \n**Service Address:** 1508 NC Hwy 24-87, Cameron, NC 28326\n\n**Smart Hands**  \n  \n**SOW:**   \nTech Requested to set up NEW WATTBOX device AND Test/Cutover new Internet Circuit and assist with connecting network to BOX during Outage Downtime  \n  \nPlease arrive at designated time, as we only have 1 hour to perform this cutover.  \n  \nDesign of Wattbox Configuration  \n• Meraki Firewall – Wattbox Port 1   \n• Meraki Switch – Wattbox Port 2  \n• BEC – Wattbox Port 3   \n• ISP Equipment-Modem – Wattbox port 4  \n• ISP Equipment-Router – Wattbox port 5 (if needed)  \n  \n  \n**Special Notes:** SCOPE OF WORK  \n  \nINSTALL IOW and Wattbox --- TEST NEW CARRIER MODEM.  \nVERIFY IOW AND NEW CARRIER MODEM IS CONNECTED TO MERAKI and Wattbox . CALL SMILE DR IT TO VERIFY NEW IP'S ARE WORKING AND SERVICE IS CUTOVER - DO NOT LET TECH LEAVE WITHOUT SPEAKING TO SMILE DR IT TEAM and Verifying IP  \n  \nONLY CALL THE ABOVE 4 SMILE DR IT contacts  \n  \n  \nSpectrum: IOC 500/20 Mbps Static Internet 3YT  \n  \nWireless MAC: 94f7bea09f65  \nWireless Make: SercommCorporation  \nWireless Model: sax1v1r  \n| Data Mac: c44fd5aca708  \nData Make: Technicolor  \nData Model: ET2251  \n  \nIP: 24.196.200.154  \nGW: 24.196.200.153  \nSUBNET: 255.255.255.252  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n   \n  \n  \nTech should bring laptop, hotspot, cat6 patch cables and a console cable.**\n\n **------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Tech Requirements**\n\n**Tech must have Laptop with ethernet port and console cable, hotspot, test set. toner and probe, cat6 cable. Must have a working laptop and phone with working camera. A Site survey form is attached and may need to be completed and attached at closeout if the install fails.**\n\n**Service Description**\n\n**Install Bec and install and test IOC and IOW Circuits. Tech may need to extend BEC to acceptable signal/working location. If extension cannot be done that day tech is to provide written quote for labor and material. Tech may also need to extend IOC/IOF depending where carrier has installed if circuit needs to be extended and cannot be done that day tech will provide written quote for labor and materials**\n\n**SOW**\n\n1. Tech is to check in with Practice Director on site then call Spectrotel \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check in and for support.\n2. Tech should see Practice Director for box containing BEC.\n3. Spectrotel and tech will setup BEC in spare outlet next to Meraki equipment and test IOW and confirm speeds.\n4. Spectrotel and tech will work to test IOC/IOF circuits and confirm speeds.\n5. Spectrotel and Tech will call Smile Doctors IT Support Alex \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to connect BEC and IOC/IOF Circuits.\n6. BEC should be installed somewhere so that antennas have full range of motion without interference of metal objects.\n7. Once proper location is found for BEC and test results are approved by support work with Smile Doctors support to connect to network.\n8. Smile Doctors team will test circuits and confirm services.\n9. Failover may or may not be done during dispatch. If testing is being performed that day tech will stand by until test is completed 10-20 minutes.\n10. Tech is to take photos and upload to FN Platform and check out with Practice Director and Spectrotel\n\n **------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**﻿♦ Contacts**\n\nPlease reach out to Spectrotel Provisioning in the Contact section for checking in/out, scope questions, before equipment installation/removal, and on-site support and testing. If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.\n\nYou must check in/out on site and enter closeout promptly. If these steps are not completed as such, there are penalties in place, listed in the Pay section.\n\n**♦ Material and Equipment**\n\nThe technician will need standard network or telecom materials and tools, dependent on the Type of Work. - Windows Laptop with ethernet port, console cable, butt set/test set, cable toner and probe, punch down tool, cable, jacks, mod ends, etc.\n\nThe provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.\n\nThe technician should have AnyDesk (www.anydesk.com) and TeamViewer installed for remote access support requests.\n\nThe technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch (Please itemize charges)\n\nTechnician is required to be proficient in knowing how to configure their laptop for DCHP and/or Static IP use without instruction\n\nTechnician is required to bring a Windows 10/11 laptop that has a working RJ45 ethernet jack\n\nIf technician is utilizing an Ethernet to USB adapter, then please make sure that it is a USB 3.0 adapter with all drivers updated\n\nTechnician's laptop is required to be rated for 1Gbps speeds\n\nTechnician is required to bring a mobile hotspot that is not their cell phone\n\nPlease bring patch cables, a power strip, and all tools and materials needed to complete the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":46.30317740201595},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793193333128}
