nus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58.49966718068597},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793197056400}
{"job":{"id":20259433,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Safely-You","title":"WiFi Heatmap Site Survey- Senior Living Community| Android Phone with NetSpot Required | Pre-Site Call Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE REVIEW PDF INSTRUCTIONS AND/OR VIDEO TO MAKE SURE NETSPOT MAP IS PROPERLY SCALED. IF HEATMAP IS NOT SCALED PROPERLY, IT WILL BE INVALID AND WILL NEED TO BE REPEATED.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Heatmap set up video: https://streamable.com/595dcz</p><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT</strong>: By agreeing to this work order, you are agreeing to our Non-Disclosure Agreement to not share any information about the contents of the site survey. NDA is attached in work order to review...</p><p><strong>Heatmap Note</strong>: Instructions with photos are in the PDF Instructions attached to work order. DO NOT SKIP step 11 (scaling the map). If map is not properly scaled, it will be invalid.</p><p>WHEN SCANNING IN NETSPOT, HOLD PHONE ABOVE HEAD AS CLOSE TO THE CEILING AS POSSIBLE.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Full NetSpot survey completed and uploaded to work order</li><li>5 screenshots of Speedtest results from https://www.meter.net/</li><li>Upload a photo of an Access Point</li><li>Upload a photo of the data closet/rack</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Upload marked-up floor plan showing all Access Point and Data Closet locations</span></li></ul><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in performing WiFi site surveys using the NetSpot Android app and meter.net, with familiarity in identifying and documenting WiFi access points and data closets.</li><li>Tech is required to conduct a full WiFi coverage assessment of a senior living community, document current bandwidth speeds, and photograph existing infrastructure.</li><li>The estimated duration will be approximately 1-2 hours, depending on site size and accessibility.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual attire; plain polo</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li><li>Neat and professional appearance</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Android device with NetSpot app installed and configured</li><li>Access to https://www.meter.net/ (via mobile browser)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Project Manager will call technician before visit to discuss onsite expectations.</li><li>Download NetSpot from Android App Store and follow instructions on PDF in work order to ensure NetSpot will run properly -<strong> DO NOT SKIP THIS STEP</strong></li></ul><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li>Check in to the work order on Field Nation and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent <strong>Safely-You</strong> while onsite.</li><li>Connect with community staff to get WiFi SSID info to connect to. Confirm with staff that the SSID is broadcasting across the whole building.</li><li>Load the pre-scaled floor plan into NetSpot and begin the WiFi survey, walking all designated hallways and identified rooms <strong>(areas are marked in red on the floor plans attached to the work order)</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Open the NetSpot app and tap \"Create a new heatmap\"&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upload the digital floor plan by tapping on \"Add existing photo of a heatmap\" and choosing the included PNG map file in the work order.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Calibrate the floor plan by setting the scale. A scaled measurement is included on the provided map.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Select \"Small\" for coverage space size</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Position yourself at the starting point of the survey area as indicated on the floor plan. </span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tap on the corresponding point on the map within the app to mark your starting position.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tap \"Scan\" on EVERY red dot on the provided map.</li><li>Export all survey data and upload the file to the Field Nation work order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span>After every red dot has been scanned, tap the \"Done\" button.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To send completed heatmap, tap the \"Export project\" button.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Save project to your Google Drive and upload into FieldNation Work Order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Immediately contact Project Manager to confirm that file heatmap has been uploaded into Work Order</li><li>Exporting Multiple Floors <strong>(Only applicable if you are surveying multiple floors) </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">If your survey includes multiple floors, you can add a new zone by tapping on \"Add a new zone.\" </span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upload the floor plan for the additional floor and name the zone appropriately (e.g., Zone 2).</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Repeat the survey process for the new zone.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Once completed, export both zones in a single project file.</span></li><li>Perform speed tests using https://www.meter.net/ on the customer’s WiFi in 5 locations, screenshot each result and submit back into work order.</li><li>Take a photo of one WiFi Access Point.</li><li>Mark the locations of all existing WiFi Access Points.</li><li>Photograph and mark the locations of all existing data closets.</li><li>Check out of the work order upon completion.</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with the work order manager.</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to your SafelyYou project manager.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval / Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours, expenses, or travel costs must be pre-approved by SafelyYou.</li><li>Providers are required to call or email the SafelyYou project manager for authorization prior to incurring any additional charges.</li><li>Unauthorized expenses will not be reimbursed.</li></ul><br>","markdown":"**PLEASE REVIEW PDF INSTRUCTIONS AND/OR VIDEO TO MAKE SURE NETSPOT MAP IS PROPERLY SCALED. IF HEATMAP IS NOT SCALED PROPERLY, IT WILL BE INVALID AND WILL NEED TO BE REPEATED.**\n\nHeatmap set up video: <https://streamable.com/595dcz>\n\n**IMPORTANT**: By agreeing to this work order, you are agreeing to our Non-Disclosure Agreement to not share any information about the contents of the site survey. NDA is attached in work order to review...\n\n**Heatmap Note**: Instructions with photos are in the PDF Instructions attached to work order. DO NOT SKIP step 11 (scaling the map). If map is not properly scaled, it will be invalid.\n\nWHEN SCANNING IN NETSPOT, HOLD PHONE ABOVE HEAD AS CLOSE TO THE CEILING AS POSSIBLE.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n- Full NetSpot survey completed and uploaded to work order\n- 5 screenshots of Speedtest results from <https://www.meter.net/>\n- Upload a photo of an Access Point\n- Upload a photo of the data closet/rack\n- Upload marked-up floor plan showing all Access Point and Data Closet locations\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in performing WiFi site surveys using the NetSpot Android app and meter.net, with familiarity in identifying and documenting WiFi access points and data closets.\n- Tech is required to conduct a full WiFi coverage assessment of a senior living community, document current bandwidth speeds, and photograph existing infrastructure.\n- The estimated duration will be approximately 1-2 hours, depending on site size and accessibility.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual attire; plain polo\n- Closed-toe shoes\n- Neat and professional appearance\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Android device with NetSpot app installed and configured\n- Access to <https://www.meter.net/> (via mobile browser)\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Project Manager will call technician before visit to discuss onsite expectations.\n- Download NetSpot from Android App Store and follow instructions on PDF in work order to ensure NetSpot will run properly - **DO NOT SKIP THIS STEP**\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check in to the work order on Field Nation and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent **Safely-You** while onsite.\n2. Connect with community staff to get WiFi SSID info to connect to. Confirm with staff that the SSID is broadcasting across the whole building.\n3. Load the pre-scaled floor plan into NetSpot and begin the WiFi survey, walking all designated hallways and identified rooms **(areas are marked in red on the floor plans attached to the work order)**.\n4. Open the NetSpot app and tap \"Create a new heatmap\"\n5. Upload the digital floor plan by tapping on \"Add existing photo of a heatmap\" and choosing the included PNG map file in the work order.\n6. Calibrate the floor plan by setting the scale. A scaled measurement is included on the provided map.\n7. Select \"Small\" for coverage space size\n8. Position yourself at the starting point of the survey area as indicated on the floor plan.\n9. Tap on the corresponding point on the map within the app to mark your starting position.\n10. Tap \"Scan\" on EVERY red dot on the provided map.\n11. Export all survey data and upload the file to the Field Nation work order\n12. After every red dot has been scanned, tap the \"Done\" button.\n13. To send completed heatmap, tap the \"Export project\" button.\n14. Save project to your Google Drive and upload into FieldNation Work Order\n15. Immediately contact Project Manager to confirm that file heatmap has been uploaded into Work Order\n16. Exporting Multiple Floors **(Only applicable if you are surveying multiple floors)**\n17. If your survey includes multiple floors, you can add a new zone by tapping on \"Add a new zone.\"\n18. Upload the floor plan for the additional floor and name the zone appropriately (e.g., Zone 2).\n19. Repeat the survey process for the new zone.\n20. Once completed, export both zones in a single project file.\n21. Perform speed tests using <https://www.meter.net/> on the customer’s WiFi in 5 locations, screenshot each result and submit back into work order.\n22. Take a photo of one WiFi Access Point.\n23. Mark the locations of all existing WiFi Access Points.\n24. Photograph and mark the locations of all existing data closets.\n25. Check out of the work order upon completion.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with the work order manager.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to your SafelyYou project manager.\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval / Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours, expenses, or travel costs must be pre-approved by SafelyYou.\n- Providers are required to call or email the SafelyYou project manager for authorization prior to incurring any additional charges.\n- Unauthorized expenses will not be reimbursed.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T09:00","end":"2026-10-30T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":400,"max":400},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":72.27607454214517},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Oct 30, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 30, Mon, Nov 2, Tue, Nov 3 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T20:15: