{"job":{"id":20259902,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sierra Wireless America, Inc.","title":"Indoor Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><u>Workorder Qualifications, Outdoor Survey Details, Tools Required and Installation Guide Attached to this Workorder.</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><u>We need you to perform the following:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once onsite, call into the Sierra Wireless's Help Desk at (</span>877-687-7795&nbsp;x4<span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">) to be checked in and to be assigned a </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">. Once Checked In, proceed into the site to meet with POC of MOD. </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist </em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">will reach out to you via text or phone call once assigned.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take photos of the environment in all directions and send to so that an optimal mounting location can be verified for the Modem and Antenna placement.&nbsp;Photo of the Antenna Serial Numbers.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once a </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"> is assigned; they will reach out to you via text and or phone call to further advise of the Site-Specific Scope of Work and to retrieve the photos above. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Temporarily set the Antenna at the location designated by the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist </em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">that is assigned to you.&nbsp;The designated location will be determined by the photos provided, location and direction of serving tower and other information.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect the Modem and Antenna per the instructions of the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>SW Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"> and using the power supply provided power the equipment.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect Laptop directly to the Ethernet port of the modem.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Perform and document latency and speed test to measure latency, upload and download speeds. Take photos of each test for the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>SW Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3 passing speed tests will be required. (Passing speeds tests to be determined by the SW Installation Specialist).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install equipment at the direction of the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"> and provide photos at the discretion and direction of the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>SW Installation Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"> of the completed install at time of the completion of onsite work. You will not be released or receive a checkout code until the photos are received.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If instructed by the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>Sierra Wireless Installations Specialist</em></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Perform an Outdoor Survey </span><em style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">(Details Specified in Attached Client Documents)</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;De-Install old equipment or place any unused equipment into the same boxes that were received with the new equipment</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take a picture of all equipment (serial numbers if applicable) before placing in the box.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;There should be a Return Shipping Label in the box, send a photo of that to the SW Installation Specialist.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Shipping of RMA equipment (if applicable):</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If shipping label is already available. Attach it to the box and drop it off at nearest FedEx location</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You will need to drop off the package at FedEx location directly leaving site. </span><em style=\"color: red;\">Include the Receipt from FedEx in the FieldNation ticket; Failure to do so will result in not being paid for the job.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You may also need to provide shipping materials. If this happens, provide a CLEAR copy of your receipt in FIeldNation and you will be reimbursed.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>BY APPLYING to this assignment you have read, understand and have agreed to the below #10.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em><u>&nbsp;</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>10.&nbsp;<u>Ticket and Extra or additional Expense Approvals</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Your time starts when you have called in to check-in with the Sierra Wireless Helpdesk via the number provided in your workorder. Your time ends when the Sierra Wireless Engineer provides you a check-out code. </em></strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"><em>NO EXCEPTIONS</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>. </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You will have to provide the check out code in the FieldNation Workorder for theWorkorder to be approved and be paid.</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NO Travel expense will be approved after you have been assigned to the workorder.</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All Expenses, Tolls, Parking, extra materials of any kind, will have to be accompanied by a picture of receipt with an itemized list of materials and costs which is placed in the deliverables of the workorder to be approved. NO receipt, NO approval, </em></strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"><em>NO EXCEPTIONS</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>.</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>e.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are returning equipment to Sierra Wireless; A picture of the FedEx receipt with the TRACKING visible must be placed in the deliverables of the Workorder or the Workorder will not be paid.</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>f.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you do not have the required tools to complete the Workorder you will </em></strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"><em><u>NOT</u></em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em> get paid.</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>g.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If requested by Sierra Wireless Engineer to provide an OUTDOOR SURVEY and you refuse, then you will </em></strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"><em><u>NOT</u></em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em> get paid. </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>h. Perform any needed steps or instructions provided by the Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist in order to complete this dispatch per the Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist. </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 38, 38);\"><em>WorkOrder Qualification, Tools required, Outdoor Survey Details and installation guide are attached to this work order.&nbsp;</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**Workorder Qualifications, Outdoor Survey Details, Tools Required and Installation Guide Attached to this Workorder.**\n\n**We need you to perform the following:**\n\n1\\. Once onsite, call into the Sierra Wireless's Help Desk at (877-687-7795 x4) to be checked in and to be assigned a ***Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist***. Once Checked In, proceed into the site to meet with POC of MOD. ***Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist*** will reach out to you via text or phone call once assigned.\n\n2\\. Take photos of the environment in all directions and send to so that an optimal mounting location can be verified for the Modem and Antenna placement. Photo of the Antenna Serial Numbers.\n\na. Once a ***Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist*** is assigned; they will reach out to you via text and or phone call to further advise of the Site-Specific Scope of Work and to retrieve the photos above.\n\n3\\. Temporarily set the Antenna at the location designated by the ***Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist*** that is assigned to you. The designated location will be determined by the photos provided, location and direction of serving tower and other information.\n\n4\\. Connect the Modem and Antenna per the instructions of the ***SW Installation Specialist*** and using the power supply provided power the equipment.\n\n5\\. Connect Laptop directly to the Ethernet port of the modem.\n\na. Perform and document latency and speed test to measure latency, upload and download speeds. Take photos of each test for the ***SW Installation Specialist***.\n\nb. 3 passing speed tests will be required. (Passing speeds tests to be determined by the SW Installation Specialist).\n\n6\\. Install equipment at the direction of the ***Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist*** and provide photos at the discretion and direction of the ***SW Installation Specialist*** of the completed install at time of the completion of onsite work. You will not be released or receive a checkout code until the photos are received.\n\n7\\. If instructed by the ***Sierra Wireless Installations Specialist***:\n\nA. Perform an Outdoor Survey *(Details Specified in Attached Client Documents)*\n\nB. De-Install old equipment or place any unused equipment into the same boxes that were received with the new equipment\n\n1\\. Take a picture of all equipment (serial numbers if applicable) before placing in the box.\n\n2\\. There should be a Return Shipping Label in the box, send a photo of that to the SW Installation Specialist.\n\n8\\. Shipping of RMA equipment (if applicable):\n\na. If shipping label is already available. Attach it to the box and drop it off at nearest FedEx location\n\nb. You will need to drop off the package at FedEx location directly leaving site. *Include the Receipt from FedEx in the FieldNation ticket; Failure to do so will result in not being paid for the job.*\n\nc. You may also need to provide shipping materials. If this happens, provide a CLEAR copy of your receipt in FIeldNation and you will be reimbursed.\n\n***9. BY APPLYING to this assignment you have read, understand and have agreed to the below #10.***\n\n***10. Ticket and Extra or additional Expense Approvals***\n\n***a. Your time starts when you have called in to check-in with the Sierra Wireless Helpdesk via the number provided in your workorder. Your time ends when the Sierra Wireless Engineer provides you a check-out code.*** ***NO EXCEPTIONS******.***\n\n***b. You will have to provide the check out code in the FieldNation Workorder for theWorkorder to be approved and be paid.***\n\n***c. NO Travel expense will be approved after you have been assigned to the workorder.***\n\n***d. All Expenses, Tolls, Parking, extra materials of any kind, will have to be accompanied by a picture of receipt with an itemized list of materials and costs which is placed in the deliverables of the workorder to be approved. NO receipt, NO approval,*** ***NO EXCEPTIONS******.***\n\n***e. If you are returning equipment to Sierra Wireless; A picture of the FedEx receipt with the TRACKING visible must be placed in the deliverables of the Workorder or the Workorder will not be paid.***\n\n***f. If you do not have the required tools to complete the Workorder you will*** ***NOT*** ***get paid.***\n\n***g. If requested by Sierra Wireless Engineer to provide an OUTDOOR SURVEY and you refuse, then you will*** ***NOT*** ***get paid.***\n\n***h. Perform any needed steps or instructions provided by the Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist in order to complete this dispatch per the Sierra Wireless Installation Specialist.***\n\n***WorkOrder Qualification, Tools required, Outdoor Survey Details and installation guide are attached to this work order.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00","end":"2026-11-05T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":230,"max":230},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3.5,"distance":68.57421289484164},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $230 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793199814637}
{"job":{"id":"2482703606","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Signal Repair/Cutover (HARD START TIME)","description":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Connect existing PIAB device to customer's switch</li><li>Potential cable run up to 150ft if the customer switch is more than 50ft away from equipment</li><li>Work with Support to determine which ports to connect to</li><li>Complete Validation Testing</li></ul><p>-Test all phones for dial tone.</p><p>-Inbound / Outbound calls</p><p>-933- confirm the site address is played back.</p><p><strong>-If permitted send a photo on the connection on the customers switch and the MetTel backboard.</strong></p><ul><li>Collect required collateral and check out with Support</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools/Materials</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cell Phone w/ Hot Spot</li><li>Laptop with Putty &amp; Teamviewer or similar desktop sharing application Ethernet, WI-FI, USB with serial port adaptor</li><li>Up to 150ft Cat5 Cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Basic Hand Tools&nbsp;</li><li>Concrete Drill, Concrete Bits</li><li>Tools for Mounting (Screwdrivers,drill,mounting screws,etc.)</li><li>Punch Down Tool&nbsp;</li><li>Cable Tone Wand + Generator</li><li>Telephone Buttsett</li><li>RJ 45 Connectors/Ends</li><li>RJ 45 Crimper</li><li>8ft ladder</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to three hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $45 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":42.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17: