{"job":{"id":20260516,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Atleos","title":"Please schedule onsite technician for SDWAN Cisco work: Circuit Activation | Estimated 3 hours onsite | Cisco experience preferred","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong></p><ul><li>Installation of 1-2 preconfigured network devices</li><li>Connect with support via bridge line during visit</li><li>Estimated 3-4 hours onsite time per visit.</li></ul><p><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><u>Dress Code</u></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Casual Business:&nbsp;Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse.&nbsp;Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans.&nbsp;Close toed shoes or boots</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes</span></li></ul><p><u>Equipment</u></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cable</li><li>USB drive</li><li>Wi-Fi Hotspot</li><li>Networking Tool kit</li><li>Microsoft Teams</li><li>Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)</li><li>Newest updated drivers</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Expectations</u></p><ul><li>Timely Arrival</li><li>Read scope and escalation path carefully</li><li>Any out of scope work requires work order manager approval</li><li>Assure your mobile and laptop are fully charged.</li><li>Have Internet access on your mobile to be used as hotspot</li><li>Bring a “<strong>Micro USB to USB</strong>” adaptor&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>ONSITE</u></strong></p><ul><li>Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Call the AT&amp;T Test and Turn Up Team listed in the work order upon arrival and once the rack/stack of equipment is complete for device testing once the installation is finished</span></li><li>Take a picture of the rack before installation begins</li><li>Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory</li><li>Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed</li><li>Fill out the Device Information custom field section below</li><li>Install components as directed by representative on bridge line. Ensure that cables are dressed neatly</li><li>Validate that device is visible and functioning</li><li>Perform troubleshooting as directed by representative on bridge line</li><li>Take a picture of installed component in rack</li><li>Break down and dispose of all packaging waste</li><li>Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED</u></strong></p><ul><li>Picture of rack before work begins</li><li>Picture of each installed component's serial number</li><li>Each serial number entered into a custom field</li><li>Picture of rack after installation is complete</li></ul><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.</strong></li><li><strong>Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store&nbsp;turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;&nbsp;</strong>must be checked-in on time per the&nbsp;<strong>original&nbsp;</strong>time log.</li><li><strong>If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival</strong>:</li><li><em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li><em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;- If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li><strong>If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival</strong>:</li><li><em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li><em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\n- Installation of 1-2 preconfigured network devices\n- Connect with support via bridge line during visit\n- Estimated 3-4 hours onsite time per visit.\n\n**REQUIREMENTS**\n\nDress Code\n\n- Casual Business: Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse. Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans. Close toed shoes or boots\n- Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes\n\nEquipment\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cable\n- USB drive\n- Wi-Fi Hotspot\n- Networking Tool kit\n- Microsoft Teams\n- Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)\n- Newest updated drivers\n\nExpectations\n\n- Timely Arrival\n- Read scope and escalation path carefully\n- Any out of scope work requires work order manager approval\n- Assure your mobile and laptop are fully charged.\n- Have Internet access on your mobile to be used as hotspot\n- Bring a “**Micro USB to USB**” adaptor\n\n**ONSITE**\n\n- Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.\n- Call the AT&amp;T Test and Turn Up Team listed in the work order upon arrival and once the rack/stack of equipment is complete for device testing once the installation is finished\n- Take a picture of the rack before installation begins\n- Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory\n- Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed\n- Fill out the Device Information custom field section below\n- Install components as directed by representative on bridge line. Ensure that cables are dressed neatly\n- Validate that device is visible and functioning\n- Perform troubleshooting as directed by representative on bridge line\n- Take a picture of installed component in rack\n- Break down and dispose of all packaging waste\n- Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED**\n\n- Picture of rack before work begins\n- Picture of each installed component's serial number\n- Each serial number entered into a custom field\n- Picture of rack after installation is complete\n\n**IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES**\n\n- **EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.**\n- **Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;** must be checked-in on time per the **original** time log.\n- **If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival**:\n- *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- *Fixed Rate* - If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- **If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival**:\n- *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- *Fixed Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T14:30","end":"2026-11-13T17:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":5.654637505008919},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T21:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-28T17:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-1