{"job":{"id":20262097,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"F2Onsite","title":"L2 Desktop Support Technician – Windows 11 Migration / PC Re-Imaging Project **READ SCHEDULE!!**","description":{"html":"<p>SCHEDULE:</p><p>Sunday, November 8: 8:00 AM – Initial setup</p><p>November 9–13: Monday–Friday, 7:00 AM–4:00 PM</p><p>November 16–20: Monday–Friday, 7:00 AM–4:00 PM</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p>Seeking experienced L2 Desktop Support Technicians to assist with a large-scale Windows 10 to Windows 11 migration project at a Wells Fargo location.</p><p>Technicians will provide onsite desktop support, assist with PC re-imaging and deployment activities, troubleshoot technical issues, and provide professional, customer-facing support throughout the project.</p><p>Responsibilities:</p><ul><li>Assist with Windows 10 to Windows 11 PC re-imaging and migration activities.</li><li>Support workstation setup, configuration, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Troubleshoot Windows/macOS operating systems, hardware, and peripheral devices.</li><li>Assist with application installations, driver updates, and basic network connectivity issues.</li><li>Configure and troubleshoot PC-connected scanners and scanning software.</li><li>Assist with barcode scanning, equipment identification, and asset tracking.</li><li>Utilize Microsoft Teams for remote support, communication, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Follow client-provided instructions and deployment procedures.</li><li>Communicate technical issues clearly to end users and escalate unresolved issues as needed.</li><li>Maintain a professional and positive customer experience throughout the project.</li></ul><p>Technician Requirements</p><ul><li>Strong L2 Desktop Support experience.</li><li>Experience with Windows 10/11 migrations, imaging, and deployments.</li><li>Experience troubleshooting hardware, software, and peripheral devices.</li><li>Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Teams, including remote control, chat, and video meetings.</li><li>Familiarity with scanners, scanning software, and asset tracking.</li><li>Basic networking and connectivity troubleshooting skills.</li><li>Excellent communication, customer service, and interpersonal skills.</li><li>Ability to work independently and follow detailed instructions.</li><li>Must be available for the full project schedule.</li></ul><p>Required Equipment</p><ul><li>Personal laptop.</li><li>Handheld barcode scanner, if available.</li><li>Personal laptop and equipment must be brought into the Wells Fargo office in a personal backpack or carrying case.</li></ul><p>Dress Code</p><p>Business casual required.</p><p>T-shirts, boots, ripped jeans, and shorts are not permitted.</p>","markdown":"SCHEDULE:\n\nSunday, November 8: 8:00 AM – Initial setup\n\nNovember 9–13: Monday–Friday, 7:00 AM–4:00 PM\n\nNovember 16–20: Monday–Friday, 7:00 AM–4:00 PM\n\nScope of Work\n\nSeeking experienced L2 Desktop Support Technicians to assist with a large-scale Windows 10 to Windows 11 migration project at a Wells Fargo location.\n\nTechnicians will provide onsite desktop support, assist with PC re-imaging and deployment activities, troubleshoot technical issues, and provide professional, customer-facing support throughout the project.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- Assist with Windows 10 to Windows 11 PC re-imaging and migration activities.\n- Support workstation setup, configuration, and troubleshooting.\n- Troubleshoot Windows/macOS operating systems, hardware, and peripheral devices.\n- Assist with application installations, driver updates, and basic network connectivity issues.\n- Configure and troubleshoot PC-connected scanners and scanning software.\n- Assist with barcode scanning, equipment identification, and asset tracking.\n- Utilize Microsoft Teams for remote support, communication, and troubleshooting.\n- Follow client-provided instructions and deployment procedures.\n- Communicate technical issues clearly to end users and escalate unresolved issues as needed.\n- Maintain a professional and positive customer experience throughout the project.\n\nTechnician Requirements\n\n- Strong L2 Desktop Support experience.\n- Experience with Windows 10/11 migrations, imaging, and deployments.\n- Experience troubleshooting hardware, software, and peripheral devices.\n- Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Teams, including remote control, chat, and video meetings.\n- Familiarity with scanners, scanning software, and asset tracking.\n- Basic networking and connectivity troubleshooting skills.\n- Excellent communication, customer service, and interpersonal skills.\n- Ability to work independently and follow detailed instructions.\n- Must be available for the full project schedule.\n\nRequired Equipment\n\n- Personal laptop.\n- Handheld barcode scanner, if available.\n- Personal laptop and equipment must be brought into the Wells Fargo office in a personal backpack or carrying case.\n\nDress Code\n\nBusiness casual required.\n\nT-shirts, boots, ripped jeans, and shorts are not permitted.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-08T08:00","end":"2026-11-08T48:00"},"payRange":{"min":38,"max":1520},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":38,"estLaborHours":40,"distance":5.562395614792917},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Sun, Nov 8, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Nov 9, Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"P