{"job":{"id":20257150,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Inverse Technology Solutions","title":"Survey/Network Install - 3rd Floor to MDF","description":{"html":"<p>[Problem Description]</p><p>A cellular router (Inseego FX4100) was relocated to a 3rd floor mechanical closet after a signal test in the MDF came back below the usable minimum. A fresh test from the new location returned 317 Mbps down / 8.2 Mbps up at 29.8ms latency / 6ms jitter, confirming the signal is usable there. The unit needs a cable run down to the MDF to connect to the Meraki MX as a secondary WAN.</p><p>AP25 is dormant and the site has a replacement unit on hand that needs to be swapped in.</p><p>This work order also covers INC1798851.</p><p><br></p><p>[Technician Steps]</p><p>1. Survey the existing conduit and cable pathways between the 3rd floor mechanical closet and the MDF.</p><p>2. Run and terminate a cable connecting the Inseego FX4100 to the Meraki MX's Port 2 (Internet).</p><p>3. Document the findings (route, distance, obstacles) and confirm the connection is up before checkout.</p><p>4. Locate AP25 and the replacement AP unit on site.</p><p>5. Swap AP25 for the replacement unit and confirm it associates and comes online.</p><p>6. Confirm all APs at the site show online in Meraki before checkout.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual, clean attire and presentable.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact Project Manager if the following are true:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, please contact&nbsp;<strong>Project Manager</strong></li><li><strong>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Project Manager</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Necessary Telecom Tools: Camera/Phone, Buttset, Toner, 66/110 Punch Down Tools, etc.</p><p>Tasks are listed below.</p>","markdown":"\\[Problem Description\\]\n\nA cellular router (Inseego FX4100) was relocated to a 3rd floor mechanical closet after a signal test in the MDF came back below the usable minimum. A fresh test from the new location returned 317 Mbps down / 8.2 Mbps up at 29.8ms latency / 6ms jitter, confirming the signal is usable there. The unit needs a cable run down to the MDF to connect to the Meraki MX as a secondary WAN.\n\nAP25 is dormant and the site has a replacement unit on hand that needs to be swapped in.\n\nThis work order also covers INC1798851.\n\n\\[Technician Steps\\]\n\n1\\. Survey the existing conduit and cable pathways between the 3rd floor mechanical closet and the MDF.\n\n2\\. Run and terminate a cable connecting the Inseego FX4100 to the Meraki MX's Port 2 (Internet).\n\n3\\. Document the findings (route, distance, obstacles) and confirm the connection is up before checkout.\n\n4\\. Locate AP25 and the replacement AP unit on site.\n\n5\\. Swap AP25 for the replacement unit and confirm it associates and comes online.\n\n6\\. Confirm all APs at the site show online in Meraki before checkout.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual, clean attire and presentable.\n\n**Contact Project Manager if the following are true:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, please contact **Project Manager**\n- **Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Project Manager**\n\nNecessary Telecom Tools: Camera/Phone, Buttset, Toner, 66/110 Punch Down Tools, etc.\n\nTasks are listed below.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T11:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00","latestStart":"2026-10-29T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":4.331651136173487},"result":{"eligible":true,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"ELIGIBLE"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.