y to the email received from Qmatic Support with the completed sign-off (excluding the release code field).\n\n\\- Include pictures of the home run area, counters, and displays.\n\n6\\. After sending the email, call Qmatic Support to receive a release code.\n\n7\\. Turn in the fully completed sign-off and pictures with the invoice to receive payment.\n\n8\\. If hardware must be returned:\n\n\\- Obtain the RMA label from the client.\n\n\\- Ship the equipment back in the provided box via UPS counter.\n\n\\- Submit a clear picture of the drop-off receipt with the invoice.\n\n**Qmatic service calls are for troubleshooting, repairing, and/or testing Qmatic equipment. Qmatic provides Customer Flow Management solutions via Kiosk, speakers, queue displays, etc.**\n\n**Required Tool List:**\n\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Number 2 Phillips Screwdriver\n- Allan Wrench Set\n- Torx Bit Set for Screwdriver\n- Headphones to Test Voice Units (Small Earbuds)\n- Cat5 Patch Cable for Testing\n- Small Step Ladder\n- Volt Meter\n- Thumb Drive\n- USB Keyboard and Mouse\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port\n\n**If there is a part to ship back and there is no return label included with the shipment leave the part with the manager and have them sign the part of the signoff indicating they kept the part, this is very important or we are liable for the part!**\n\n***Upon check in or out with Qmatic, please ensure an on site and subsequent off site code is recorded on your sign off sheet. It is crucial to ensure we can approve overage on site past the 3 hours if needed.***\n\n***Flat rate covers up to three hours on site. Any additional time will be paid at $40 per hour.***\n\n***Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.***\n\n***Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will b