{"job":{"id":20264197,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Standard - Circuit Replacement/Cutover - Breakfix","description":{"html":"<p>TECH MUST CALL WHEN ONSITE TO WORK WITH CLIENT: </p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); background-color: white;\"><u>Prathyusha Alahari</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black; background-color: white;\">Network Administrator II </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">814-881-8795</span></p><p></p><p><strong>Cellular WAN Replacement/Circuit Replacement/Cutover</strong></p><p><strong>Default Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Replace an existing Cradlepoint or circuit connection. Validate handoff, ensure routing and monitoring restored, and decommission old circuit.</p><p></p><p><strong>Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Document existing circuit and/or Cellular WAN setup.</li><li>Take pre-install photos.</li><li>Disconnect old handoff and connect new carrier or Cellular WAN.</li><li>Power up and confirm LTE or wired connection present.</li><li>Coordinate with remote engineer to validate routing and monitoring.</li><li>Run test traffic (ping, traceroute, speedtest).</li><li>Secure cables and label cables.</li><li>Take post-install photos.</li><li>Return failed hardware to CIS <ul><li>Box up failed hardware and put shipping label on the box</li><li>Either give the box to the Manager on Duty for UPS pickup or have the Tech drop off at UPS. <ul><li>Document what path was taken and who is responsible for the return.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p></p><p></p><p>Materials (have extras of all):</p><ul><li>Cat5e cable (at least 200’)</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p>Required Tools:</p><p>Required Tools:</p><ul><li>Ladder (minimum 8’ A-Frame)</li><li>Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)<ul><li>Can connect to Wi-Fi.</li></ul></li><li>Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor</li><li>Cable Tester<ul><li>Test POE</li></ul></li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)</li><li>Cell Phone<ul><li>with camera and charger</li><li>with ability to connect to Hotspot</li></ul></li><li>Measuring Tools</li></ul><p></p><p>Tech is to call <strong style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><u>Prathyusha Alahari</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: black;\">Network Administrator II </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">814-881-8795</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">Site Follow up for install</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Modem Location: not provided </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Modem make and model: ATT bgw320</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Modem Mac Address: 3c714b08f220</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Name of GC/Lcon/MOD who confirmed modem location: LCON doesn&#39;t confirm </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">ISP Follow up for Install</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm they show WO as completed: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm surf and sync to modem: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Able to ping GW (if not dynamic): completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Show modem online and speed tests are good: completed</span></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">MODEM Configuration Confirmation (Unless there are different instructions in prior notes)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm Bridge Mode / IP Pass-Through is ENABLED – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm WiFi is Disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm ALL Firewalls are disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Confirm ALL Packet Filters and any Echo requests are disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">*** For AT&amp;T only ask the rep to disable all settings </span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">LOCATED IN A MALL: (Yes/No) no</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">Before Marking Installed Reminder to Complete the below updates on the edit tab:</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Provider Ordered: ATT</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Product Ordered: ABF</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Bandwidth (if not POTS): </span><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.87); background-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.04);\">300 up / 300 down</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Account number: </span><span style=\"color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.87); background-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1);\">344805972</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             Order Date: 2026-06-02</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);\">•             ISP Circuit Live: 2026-09-22</span></p><p> </p><p></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">IPs</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">: </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Usable: 99.58.161.41 - 99.58.161.46</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248 </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">DNS:  Primary DNS: 68.94.156.11 Secondary DNS: 68.94.157.11</span></p><p></p><p>TECH MUST CALL WHEN ONSITE TO WORK WITH CLIENT: </p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"><u>Prathyusha Alahari</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: black;\">Network Administrator II </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">814-881-8795</span></p>","markdown":"TECH MUST CALL WHEN ONSITE TO WORK WITH CLIENT:\n\n**Prathyusha Alahari**\n\nNetwork Administrator II\n\n814-881-8795\n\n**Cellular WAN Replacement/Circuit Replacement/Cutover**\n\n**Default Scope of Work:**\n\nReplace an existing Cradlepoint or circuit connection. Validate handoff, ensure routing and monitoring restored, and decommission old circuit.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n- Document existing circuit and/or Cellular WAN setup.\n- Take pre-install photos.\n- Disconnect old handoff and connect new carrier or Cellular WAN.\n- Power up and confirm LTE or wired connection present.\n- Coordinate with remote engineer to validate routing and monitoring.\n- Run test traffic (ping, traceroute, speedtest).\n- Secure cables and label cables.\n- Take post-install photos.\n- Return failed hardware to CIS \n  - Box up failed hardware and put shipping label on the box\n  - Either give the box to the Manager on Duty for UPS pickup or have the Tech drop off at UPS. \n      - Document what path was taken and who is responsible for the return.\n\nMaterials (have extras of all):\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Ladder (minimum 8’ A-Frame)\n- Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)\n  - Can connect to Wi-Fi.\n- Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n  - Test POE\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)\n- Cell Phone\n  - with camera and charger\n  - with ability to connect to Hotspot\n- Measuring Tools\n\nTech is to call **Prathyusha Alahari**\n\nNetwork Administrator II\n\n814-881-8795\n\nSite Follow up for install\n\n• Modem Location: not provided\n\n• Modem make and model: ATT bgw320\n\n• Modem Mac Address: 3c714b08f220\n\n• Name of GC/Lcon/MOD who confirmed modem location: LCON doesn't confirm\n\nISP Follow up for Install\n\n• Confirm they show WO as completed: completed\n\n• Confirm surf and sync to modem: completed\n\n• Able to ping GW (if not dynamic): completed\n\n• Show modem online and speed tests are good: completed\n\nMODEM Configuration Confirmation (Unless there are different instructions in prior notes)\n\n• Confirm Bridge Mode / IP Pass-Through is ENABLED – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed\n\n• Confirm WiFi is Disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed\n\n• Confirm ALL Firewalls are disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed\n\n• Confirm ALL Packet Filters and any Echo requests are disabled – If Tech can’t confirm, Reach out to Tech Support: completed\n\n\\*\\*\\* For AT&amp;T only ask the rep to disable all settings\n\nLOCATED IN A MALL: (Yes/No) no\n\nBefore Marking Installed Reminder to Complete the below updates on the edit tab:\n\n• Provider Ordered: ATT\n\n• Product Ordered: ABF\n\n• Bandwidth (if not POTS): 300 up / 300 down\n\n• Account number: 344805972\n\n• Order Date: 2026-06-02\n\n• ISP Circuit Live: 2026-09-22\n\n**IPs**:\n\nUsable: 99.58.161.41 - 99.58.161.46\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.248\n\nDNS: Primary DNS: 68.94.156.11 Secondary DNS: 68.94.157.11\n\nTECH MUST CALL WHEN ONSITE TO WORK WITH CLIENT:\n\n**Prathyusha Alahari**\n\nNetwork Administrator II\n\n814-881-8795","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T10:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":240},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6.246539090971103},"result":{"eligible":true,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"ELIGIBLE"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03