{"job":{"id":20264877,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Splice Communications","title":"VC1 Recovery","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS AN ISOFY TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE AND TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>﻿Mandatory Scope Discussion</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians who have <strong>not previously completed work for this specific project phase</strong> must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.</p>\n<p>If contacted, please plan to attend. <strong>Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:</u></strong></p>\n<p>The Technician will work with an <del>*****</del> Engineer to recover the VC1.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>REQUIRED TESTING TOOLS AND MATERIALS</strong> - laptop with ethernet port (or adapter), console cable, patch cable, hand tools, label maker, several <strong>Juniper compatible USB drives, and ethernet cables</strong></li>\n<li>Please contact<strong><del>***** ****** *********** ** ************</del></strong> once onsite and near the equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Duration:&nbsp;# hour(s) 2</p>\n<p>Experience:</p>\n<p>Technician will need to be proficient with low voltage cabling, cable tracing, toning, crimping, and testing.&nbsp;Will need to be well versed with cable management standards, materials (J-Hooks, wire clips, conduit), certifications, local codes (and other building requirements).&nbsp;Will need to understand network device connectivity between routers, firewalls, switches, servers and patch panels/punch downs, wall plates, keystones, and end user devices.&nbsp;Will need to have all tools and materials for testing or making new cables, installing face plates or keystones as required.&nbsp;Will need to be comfortable on ladders and lifts, entering and navigating attics and crawl spaces.</p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cable</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)</li>\n<li>Smartphone</li>\n<li>Hot spot</li>\n<li>Ladder (minimum 4-6 foot A-frame, will need to specify if different)</li>\n<li>Impact and standard drills with bits for wood, concrete, drywall, steel, etc.</li>\n<li>Socket set</li>\n<li>Caulking Gun (may be required if doing antenna installation)</li>\n<li>Hex/Allen key set</li>\n<li>Fishing tape</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested.&nbsp;Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task.&nbsp;All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site.&nbsp;There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>MATERIALS:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>PARTS:</u></strong></p>\n<p>{INSTRUCTIONS FOR RETRIEVAL OF CLIENT PROVIDED EQUIPMENT}</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:</u></strong></p>\n<p>CAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS/DELIVERABLES:</u></strong></p>\n<p>PLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL.&nbsp;CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DRESS CODE:</strong></p>\n<p>Business casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.).&nbsp;This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS AN ISOFY TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE AND TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**﻿Mandatory Scope Discussion**\n\nTechnicians who have **not previously completed work for this specific project phase** must participate in a pre-visit scope discussion.\n\nIf contacted, please plan to attend. **Failure to complete the required discussion may result in removal from the work order.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:**\n\nThe Technician will work with an \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Engineer to recover the VC1.\n\n- **REQUIRED TESTING TOOLS AND MATERIALS** - laptop with ethernet port (or adapter), console cable, patch cable, hand tools, label maker, several **Juniper compatible USB drives, and ethernet cables**\n- Please contact**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** once onsite and near the equipment.\n\n**JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:**\n\nDuration: # hour(s) 2\n\nExperience:\n\nTechnician will need to be proficient with low voltage cabling, cable tracing, toning, crimping, and testing. Will need to be well versed with cable management standards, materials (J-Hooks, wire clips, conduit), certifications, local codes (and other building requirements). Will need to understand network device connectivity between routers, firewalls, switches, servers and patch panels/punch downs, wall plates, keystones, and end user devices. Will need to have all tools and materials for testing or making new cables, installing face plates or keystones as required. Will need to be comfortable on ladders and lifts, entering and navigating attics and crawl spaces.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Laptop with working power supply, ethernet port and Wi-Fi connectivity\n- Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- Label maker\n- Patch Cables\n- Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)\n- Smartphone\n- Hot spot\n- Ladder (minimum 4-6 foot A-frame, will need to specify if different)\n- Impact and standard drills with bits for wood, concrete, drywall, steel, etc.\n- Socket set\n- Caulking Gun (may be required if doing antenna installation)\n- Hex/Allen key set\n- Fishing tape\n\n**As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.**\n\n**MATERIALS:**\n\n**PARTS:**\n\n{INSTRUCTIONS FOR RETRIEVAL OF CLIENT PROVIDED EQUIPMENT}\n\n**IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:**\n\nCAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.\n\n**TASKS/DELIVERABLES:**\n\nPLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL. CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.\n\n**DRESS CODE:**\n\nBusiness casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.). This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T09:00","end":"2026-10-29T11:00","latestStart":"2026-10-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.459746272053032},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00