{"job":{"id":20264932,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Cable Run - LIFT ONSITE","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scope of work: Tech must work with the TJX NOC group @ +18558592821 opt1, opt1, opt2 for signoff/verification.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Need tech onsite to address AP03 being offline. Tech should check and test the cables, if required tech should change the cable, reboot the AP. Tech can also change the port between (20-24) on either SW H or H2 or H3. AP03 is currently connected on SW H port 20.Tech needs to trace the cable from AP03 to switch end to end. Tech should carry ladder, cables, other necessary gears.</span></p><p> </p><p><em>Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.</em></p><p><strong>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</strong></p><p><strong>Each site visit will require its own work order.</strong></p><p><strong>If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</strong></p><p><em>Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.</em></p><p> All NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2.  <strong><u>ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support</u></strong>.</p><ul><li> A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.<ul><li> #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.</li><li>#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.</li><li>#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><p>• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat</p><p>• Laptop</p><p>• USB to serial connector</p><p>• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html</p><p>• Putty</p><p>• NULL Modem cable</p><p>• Ethernet cable</p><p>• Laptop Power pack</p><p>• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet</p><p>• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30</p><p>• Flash light</p><p>• Digital Volt Meter</p><p>• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/</p><p>• Zoom installed on Techs Phone</p><p>• Velcro Straps</p><p>• X-over cable</p><p>• Standard screwdriver and security bits</p><p>• Thermal paste</p><p>• Alcohol Wipes</p><p>• 9 pin serial cable</p><strong>Reimbursement Rates:</strong>Cabling Materials<ul><li>Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.20 per ft</strong></li><li>Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.29 per ft</strong></li></ul>Hardware<ul><li>Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: <strong>$9.00 each</strong></li></ul>Patch Cables<ul><li>1 ft: <strong>$3.50</strong></li><li>3 ft: <strong>$2.00</strong></li><li>5 ft: <strong>$4.50</strong></li><li>10 ft: <strong>$6.50</strong></li></ul>Cable Management<ul><li>Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): <strong>$2.00 per drop</strong></li></ul>Cabling Job Requirements<ul><li>All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.</li><li>Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.</li><li>All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Support to check in. <del>*** *********** ************* </del><del>*** *** ****</del> and confirm before leaving site. Support representative&#39;s name will be required. If no answer call <del>**** ******* ** ************* ****** **</del></li><li>Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:</li><li>Record the client employee&#39;s First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.</li><li>Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong> </p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required  </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance  </li><li>Background check is required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts as representing<del>********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment  </li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire  </li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nScope of work: Tech must work with the TJX NOC group @ +18558592821 opt1, opt1, opt2 for signoff/verification.\n\nNeed tech onsite to address AP03 being offline. Tech should check and test the cables, if required tech should change the cable, reboot the AP. Tech can also change the port between (20-24) on either SW H or H2 or H3. AP03 is currently connected on SW H port 20.Tech needs to trace the cable from AP03 to switch end to end. Tech should carry ladder, cables, other necessary gears.\n\n*Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.*\n\n**Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.**\n\n**Each site visit will require its own work order.**\n\n**If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.**\n\n*Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.*\n\n All NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2. **ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support**.\n\n- A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.\n  - #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.\n  - \\#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.\n  - \\#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.\n\n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat\n\n• Laptop\n\n• USB to serial connector\n\n• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - <http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html>\n\n• Putty\n\n• NULL Modem cable\n\n• Ethernet cable\n\n• Laptop Power pack\n\n• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet\n\n• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30\n\n• Flash light\n\n• Digital Volt Meter\n\n• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - <https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/>\n\n• Zoom installed on Techs Phone\n\n• Velcro Straps\n\n• X-over cable\n\n• Standard screwdriver and security bits\n\n• Thermal paste\n\n• Alcohol Wipes\n\n• 9 pin serial cable\n\n**Reimbursement Rates:**Cabling Materials- Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: **$0.20 per ft**\n- Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: **$0.29 per ft**\n\nHardware- Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: **$9.00 each**\n\nPatch Cables- 1 ft: **$3.50**\n- 3 ft: **$2.00**\n- 5 ft: **$4.50**\n- 10 ft: **$6.50**\n\nCable Management- Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): **$2.00 per drop**\n\nCabling Job Requirements- All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.\n- Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.\n- All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Call Support to check in. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* and confirm before leaving site. Support representative's name will be required. If no answer call \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n- Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:\n- Record the client employee's First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.\n- Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check is required\n- Check-in with site contacts as representing\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T07:00","end":"2026-10-30T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":35.33602479685935},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00: