{"job":{"id":20265384,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"A+ Mobile","title":"Fayetteville, NC -- Starlink Installation with Wall Mount","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PREFERRED EXPERIENCED STARLINK (or similar device mounting experience) FOR THE FOLLOWING:</strong></p><p><strong><u>ProSat Networks -- Work Order (WO)</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>You will be representing ProSat Networks</strong> (a sister company of <em>A+ Mobile Techs</em>) at all times during this WO (work order) and during all customer interactions.</p><p><strong><u>Customer</u>:<del> </del></strong><del>****** ******************* **************</del></p><p><strong><u>Onsite POC (point-of-contact)</u>:</strong> same as Customer</p><p><strong><u>ProSat Networks' WO Manager(s)</u>:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Prilla<del> *********** **** ************* *************************</del></strong></p><p>Haley&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>** ***** **** ************* *******************************</del></span></p><p><strong>*****************************************</strong></p><p><strong><u>SOW (scope of work):</u> see attached photo﻿</strong></p><p><strong>Estimated time to completion: &lt;3-4 hrs</strong></p><p><strong>Have STARLINK APP</strong> installed on your cell, <strong>OPEN and Test</strong> <strong>PRIOR</strong> to arriving onsite.</p><p>The goal is to install the customer's <strong>Starlink (installation) Kit</strong> resulting in a successful installation that matches or surpasses our customer's expectations.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Installation Details</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Starlink Kit:&nbsp;Standard 4X</strong></li><li><strong>Mount Type: To be confirmed with customer </strong></li><li><strong>Mounting Surface: TBD</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Route: location to be discussed with the customer but they are open to do wall penetration</strong></li><li><strong>Router Location: Living room </strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Installation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Verify all Starlink equipment and installation materials are onsite.</strong></li><li><strong>Take photos of the customer-supplied equipment.</strong></li><li><strong>Using the customer's Starlink App:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do multiple <strong>OBSTRUCTIONS Tests to pinpoint</strong>: <strong style=\"color: rgb(111, 192, 64);\">GOOD experience</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Take Screen Shot showing the best Obstructions Test results found</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Save a screenshot of the final Obstruction Test.</strong></li><li><strong>Review and obtain customer approval for:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Mount location</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Outdoor-Indoor Cable Route</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Router location</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Installation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Install the approved [Mount Type] securely.</strong></li><li><strong>Route the proprietary Starlink cable using the most direct and professional path.</strong></li><li><strong>Use an existing low-voltage pathway whenever available.</strong></li><li><strong>If no pathway exists, obtain customer approval before creating one (1) simple wall penetration.</strong></li><li><strong>Secure all exterior cabling using appropriate fasteners (e.g., cable tacks, clips, zip ties, or Velcro straps) to ensure a clean, secure, and professional installation.</strong></li><li><strong>Install a drip loop on exterior cable runs.</strong></li><li><strong>Seal all penetrations with weatherproof sealant.</strong></li><li><strong>Install the router in the customer's preferred location.</strong></li><li><strong>Clean up cables of router power supply professionally.</strong></li><li><strong>Connect and power on the Starlink system.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">Note: Initial Starlink activation may take up to 20 minutes.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Configuration &amp; Testing</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Using the customer's Starlink App:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Configure the customer's Wi-Fi name (SSID) and password.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify the dish is Aligned. Take a screenshot.</strong></li><li><strong>Perform a Speed Test. Take a screenshot.&nbsp;(150 Mbps and up results only)</strong></li><li><strong>Confirm internet connectivity and ensure no errors on the Starlink app.</strong></li><li><strong>Assist the customer with connecting devices to the new Wi-Fi network.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Customer Walkthrough</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Show the customer how to:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Access their SSID (wireless network name)</strong></li><li><strong>Input and Reset password</strong></li><li><strong>Run speed test</strong></li><li><strong>Remotely monitor and control</strong></li><li><strong>Reset/refresh Starlink network connection (handshake)</strong></li><li><strong>Adjust the Snow Melt feature</strong></li><li><strong>Answer customer questions that come up.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change of Scope</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> - </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">Stop &amp; Call WO Manager</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not proceed without approval if the job requires:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Attic cable routing.</strong></li><li><strong>Conduit installation.</strong></li><li><strong>Underground trenching.</strong></li><li><strong>Additional installation of any equipment.</strong></li><li><strong>Any work outside the approved Work Order.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>*Attention Installer: IF YOU ARE WORKING IN AN ATTIC</strong></p><p>It is imperative that you step only on the floor joists and NOT onto the attic insulation.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Report any site issues immediately to the WO manager if they may prevent a successful installation.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">FINAL DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upload:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>INVENTORY of supplied equipment and installation materials (laid out before installation)&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>BEFORE installation photos</strong></li><li><strong>AFTER installation photos</strong></li><li><strong>Starlink Installation Location</strong></li><li><strong>Outdoor Cable Entry</strong></li><li><strong>Indoor Cable Entry</strong></li><li><strong>Customer Starlink App screenshots:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Obstructions Test results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Speed Test results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Starlink Aligned results</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Closeout</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Review the completed installation with the customer.</strong></li><li><strong>Clean the work area. </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DO NOT LEAVE ANY TRASH BEHIND.</strong></li><li><strong>Upload all required photos and closeout notes before leaving the site.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**PREFERRED EXPERIENCED STARLINK (or similar device mounting experience) FOR THE FOLLOWING:**\n\n**ProSat Networks -- Work Order (WO):**\n\n**You will be representing ProSat Networks** (a sister company of *A+ Mobile Techs*) at all times during this WO (work order) and during all customer interactions.\n\n**Customer:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Onsite POC (point-of-contact):** same as Customer\n\n**ProSat Networks' WO Manager(s):**\n\n**Prilla \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nHaley \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**SOW (scope of work): see attached photo﻿**\n\n**Estimated time to completion: &lt;3-4 hrs**\n\n**Have STARLINK APP** installed on your cell, **OPEN and Test** **PRIOR** to arriving onsite.\n\nThe goal is to install the customer's **Starlink (installation) Kit** resulting in a successful installation that matches or surpasses our customer's expectations.\n\n**Installation Details**\n\n- **Starlink Kit: Standard 4X**\n- **Mount Type: To be confirmed with customer**\n- **Mounting Surface: TBD**\n- **Cable Route: location to be discussed with the customer but they are open to do wall penetration**\n- **Router Location: Living room**\n\n**Pre-Installation**\n\n- **Verify all Starlink equipment and installation materials are onsite.**\n- **Take photos of the customer-supplied equipment.**\n- **Using the customer's Starlink App:**\n- Do multiple **OBSTRUCTIONS Tests to pinpoint**: **GOOD experience**\n- Take Screen Shot showing the best Obstructions Test results found\n- **Save a screenshot of the final Obstruction Test.**\n- **Review and obtain customer approval for:**\n- **Mount location**\n- **Outdoor-Indoor Cable Route**\n- **Router location**\n\n**Installation**\n\n- **Install the approved \\[Mount Type\\] securely.**\n- **Route the proprietary Starlink cable using the most direct and professional path.**\n- **Use an existing low-voltage pathway whenever available.**\n- **If no pathway exists, obtain customer approval before creating one (1) simple wall penetration.**\n- **Secure all exterior cabling using appropriate fasteners (e.g., cable tacks, clips, zip ties, or Velcro straps) to ensure a clean, secure, and professional installation.**\n- **Install a drip loop on exterior cable runs.**\n- **Seal all penetrations with weatherproof sealant.**\n- **Install the router in the customer's preferred location.**\n- **Clean up cables of router power supply professionally.**\n- **Connect and power on the Starlink system.**\n\n**Note: Initial Starlink activation may take up to 20 minutes.**\n\n**Configuration &amp; Testing**\n\n**Using the customer's Starlink App:**\n\n- **Configure the customer's Wi-Fi name (SSID) and password.**\n- **Verify the dish is Aligned. Take a screenshot.**\n- **Perform a Speed Test. Take a screenshot. (150 Mbps and up results only)**\n- **Confirm internet connectivity and ensure no errors on the Starlink app.**\n- **Assist the customer with connecting devices to the new Wi-Fi network.**\n\n**Customer Walkthrough**\n\n**Show the customer how to:**\n\n- **Access their SSID (wireless network name)**\n- **Input and Reset password**\n- **Run speed test**\n- **Remotely monitor and control**\n- **Reset/refresh Starlink network connection (handshake)**\n- **Adjust the Snow Melt feature**\n- **Answer customer questions that come up.**\n\n**Change of Scope** - **Stop &amp; Call WO Manager**\n\n**Do not proceed without approval if the job requires:**\n\n- **Attic cable routing.**\n- **Conduit installation.**\n- **Underground trenching.**\n- **Additional installation of any equipment.**\n- **Any work outside the approved Work Order.**\n\n**\\*Attention Installer: IF YOU ARE WORKING IN AN ATTIC**\n\nIt is imperative that you step only on the floor joists and NOT onto the attic insulation.\n\n**Report any site issues immediately to the WO manager if they may prevent a successful installation.**\n\n**FINAL DELIVERABLES**\n\n**Upload:**\n\n- **INVENTORY of supplied equipment and installation materials (laid out before installation)**\n- **BEFORE installation photos**\n- **AFTER installation photos**\n- **Starlink Installation Location**\n- **Outdoor Cable Entry**\n- **Indoor Cable Entry**\n- **Customer Starlink App screenshots:**\n- Obstructions Test results\n- Speed Test results\n- Starlink Aligned results\n\n**Closeout**\n\n- **Review the completed installation with the customer.**\n- **Clean the work area.** **DO NOT LEAVE ANY TRASH BEHIND.**\n- **Upload all required photos and closeout notes before leaving the site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T10:00","end":"2026-11-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":195,"max":195},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":66.6609318510009},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 -