{"job":{"id":20265606,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Standard - General Troubleshooting - Breakfix","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Details of Site/Dispatch</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Account Name:</strong> Tractor Supply</li><li><strong>Site ID / Location Address: Tractor Supply_7100_Roxboro_NC / 739 N Madison Blvd, Roxboro, NC 27573</strong></li><li><strong>Contact Onsite Name &amp; Phone:</strong> <del>*****************</del></li><li><strong>Severity: Impaired </strong></li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Per CIS records site was cutover to Brightspeed circuit on 8/24, site has been unable to locate Brightspeed modem since circuit dropped offline on 9/24</p><p></p><p>Locate Brightspeed Calix modem</p><p>Confirm surf directly from Calix modem, provisioned speeds are 1Gx1G</p><p>Connect Brightspeed modem to RTR-01 port 3</p><p>Confirm circuit restores on RTR-01</p><p>Clearly label modem for future troubleshooting and inform MOD of Brightspeed modem location</p><p></p><p>Brightspeed Calix U6 modem</p><p>MAC 88:da:36:97:d6:86</p><p>SN CXNK01F9BF37</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Document existing circuit and/or Cellular WAN setup.</li><li>Take pre-install photos.</li><li>Disconnect old handoff and connect new carrier or Cellular WAN.</li><li>Power up and confirm LTE or wired connection present.</li><li>Coordinate with remote engineer to validate routing and monitoring.</li><li>Run test traffic (ping, traceroute, speedtest).</li><li>Secure cables and label cables.</li><li>Take post-install photos.</li><li>Return failed hardware to CIS <ul><li>Box up failed hardware and put shipping label on the box</li><li>Either give the box to the Manager on Duty for UPS pickup or have the Tech drop off at UPS. <ul><li>Document what path was taken and who is responsible for the return.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p></p><p></p><p>Materials (have extras of all):</p><ul><li>Cat5e cable (at least 200’)</li><li>Single Port Surface Mount Boxes</li><li>Cat5e Keystone Jacks</li><li>Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)</li><li>Zip Ties</li><li>Velcro Strips</li></ul><p></p><p>Required Tools:</p><p>Required Tools:</p><ul><li>Ladder (minimum 8’ A-Frame)</li><li>Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)<ul><li>Can connect to Wi-Fi.</li></ul></li><li>Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor</li><li>Cable Tester<ul><li>Test POE</li></ul></li><li>Cable Toner</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Cisco Console Cable</li><li>General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)</li><li>Cell Phone<ul><li>with camera and charger</li><li>with ability to connect to Hotspot</li></ul></li><li>Measuring Tools</li></ul>","markdown":"**Details of Site/Dispatch**\n\n- **Account Name:** Tractor Supply\n- **Site ID / Location Address: Tractor Supply\\_7100\\_Roxboro\\_NC / 739 N Madison Blvd, Roxboro, NC 27573**\n- **Contact Onsite Name &amp; Phone:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Severity: Impaired**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nPer CIS records site was cutover to Brightspeed circuit on 8/24, site has been unable to locate Brightspeed modem since circuit dropped offline on 9/24\n\nLocate Brightspeed Calix modem\n\nConfirm surf directly from Calix modem, provisioned speeds are 1Gx1G\n\nConnect Brightspeed modem to RTR-01 port 3\n\nConfirm circuit restores on RTR-01\n\nClearly label modem for future troubleshooting and inform MOD of Brightspeed modem location\n\nBrightspeed Calix U6 modem\n\nMAC 88:da:36:97:d6:86\n\nSN CXNK01F9BF37\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n- Document existing circuit and/or Cellular WAN setup.\n- Take pre-install photos.\n- Disconnect old handoff and connect new carrier or Cellular WAN.\n- Power up and confirm LTE or wired connection present.\n- Coordinate with remote engineer to validate routing and monitoring.\n- Run test traffic (ping, traceroute, speedtest).\n- Secure cables and label cables.\n- Take post-install photos.\n- Return failed hardware to CIS \n  - Box up failed hardware and put shipping label on the box\n  - Either give the box to the Manager on Duty for UPS pickup or have the Tech drop off at UPS. \n      - Document what path was taken and who is responsible for the return.\n\nMaterials (have extras of all):\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Ladder (minimum 8’ A-Frame)\n- Laptop w/ Power supply (Windows 10 or higher)\n  - Can connect to Wi-Fi.\n- Ethernet port or USB–Ethernet adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n  - Test POE\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General mounting tools (drill, screwdriver, etc.)\n- Cell Phone\n  - with camera and charger\n  - with ability to connect to Hotspot\n- Measuring Tools","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T14:00","end":"2026-10-30T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":240},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":38.42694214565881},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z