{"job":{"id":20258183,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Promotion Technology Group","title":"Sally Ignited #3622 - Cary NC - Sally Beauty Bond Bar Package- Proj #12953","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Sally Beauty - #3622 – Cary, NC</strong></p><p><strong>Ignited (55”TV &amp; 2 Speakers)</strong></p><p><strong>System Overview</strong></p><p>PTG will furnish and install a complete Audio and Video Signage System at this Sally Beauty location. The system includes ceiling speakers, a power amplifier, music and video media players, a commercial display, network cabling, and necessary infrastructure.</p><p><strong>System Components</strong></p><p><strong>PTG Furnished Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>(2) Ceiling Speakers – White</li><li>(1) 2-Channel Amplifier</li><li>(1) Lowell Wall Shelf</li><li>(1) Samsung 55\" LED Display</li><li>(1) Crimson TV Mount</li><li>(1) OFE MOOD ProFusion iS Music Player - with Stereo RCA, Ethernet, and power cables (shipped to PTG)</li><li>(1) OFE MOOD MVP-195 Media Player - with HDMI, Ethernet, and power cables (shipped to PTG)&nbsp;</li><li>CAT5e cabling, connectors, terminations, jacks, and plates as required for the Display location</li></ul><p><strong>Client-Supplied Items:</strong></p><ul><li>(1) CAT5e cable and plate at the audio shelf location</li><li>120V/20A clean power duplex circuit at display location</li><li>120V/20A clean power duplex circuit at audio shelf location</li></ul><p><strong>Audio System Description</strong></p><p>Two (2) ceiling speakers will be installed in the retail sales area to provide background music coverage. Final speaker placement will be determined on-site by the PTG technician, avoiding locations within 12 feet of the cash wrap or hair color area.</p><p>A Lowell wall shelf will be installed at a height of no greater than 5’-5” above the finished floor to support the audio equipment. All speaker wiring will terminate at this wall-mounted shelf, which will be located beneath the client-furnished power outlet and data plate—typically positioned near the client’s network rack. PTG will install one (1) 2-channel amplifier and one (1) MOOD ProFusion iS media player on the shelf.</p><p>The ProFusion iS media player will be connected to the data plate above the shelf using the supplied patch cable. This data plate is wired to Port 8 on the client’s network switch. The PTG technician will verify connectivity by confirming that the data plate is properly linked to Port 8 on the network switch.</p><p><strong>Video System Description</strong></p><p>PTG will install one (1) Samsung 55\" LED display behind the Bond Bar using a Crimson TV mount. The display will be mounted in a portrait orientation, with the bottom edge positioned 36 inches above the finished floor, per client specifications.</p><p>The MVP-195 media player will be concealed behind the display and connected via HDMI. All cabling will be hidden from view.</p><p>The MVP-195 player will connect to a wall plate located behind the display. This wall plate is wired to Port 7 of the patch panel at the Cash Wrap, which in turn is connected to Port 6 on the switch in the network rack.</p><p>A PTG technician will verify that the MVP-195 is properly patched to Port 6 of the client's network switch.</p><p><strong>Network Responsibility</strong></p><p>Prior to installation, the client is responsible for providing an active network faceplate at the audio shelf location. If this infrastructure is not completed at the time of installation, the PTG technician must notify the PTG Project Manager. PTG will then proceed with completing the necessary work using PTG-supplied terminations and equipment. The PTG Project Manager will notify the Sally Beauty Project Manager, and additional charges will apply.</p><p>PTG is responsible for the following low-voltage wiring:</p><ul><li>(1) CAT5e from Cash wrap to video display location</li><li>Installation of all necessary terminations, jacks and faceplates</li></ul><p>Technicians must arrive with:</p><ul><li>Network crimp and cut tools</li><li>Network tester</li><li>Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)</li></ul><p>Any reused OFE equipment must be onsite prior to the scheduled install. Return visits for retrieval or reinstallation of such items may result in additional charges.</p><p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p><p>Before leaving the site, the PTG technician must:</p><ul><li>Contact Mood Media Customer Service at 855-345-5223 to verify both the ProFusion iS and MVP-195 players are online and operational.</li><li>Label all installed A/V equipment.</li><li>Clean the installed display and remove all installation-related debris.</li><li>Provide basic system operation training to store management personnel.</li></ul><p><strong>Drawings</strong></p><p>Refer to drawing sheets:</p><ul><li>AV-100 (Audio System Layout)</li><li>AV-200 (Video Display Layout)</li></ul><p><strong>Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)</strong></p><p>All OFE must be in working order. If OFE is found to be faulty or incompatible, a Client Change Order (CCO) may be issued to replace or supplement the equipment, with labor and material costs billed accordingly.</p><p><strong>General Notes</strong></p><ul><li>Work will be performed during standard business hours (Mon–Fri, excluding holidays)</li><li>Installation areas must be accessible and scheduled in advance</li><li>No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval</li></ul><p><strong>Exclusions</strong></p><p>This Scope of Work does <em>not</em> include:</p><ul><li>High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.</li><li>Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations</li><li>Drywall or ceiling tile repairs/replacement</li><li>Structural reinforcement or seismic support</li><li>Millwork or cabinetry modifications</li><li>Patching, painting, or decorative finishing</li><li>Permit acquisition or fees (unless otherwise noted)</li><li>Prevailing wage or union labor (unless otherwise stated)</li><li>Lifts or scaffolding (unless otherwise stated)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Sally Beauty - #3622 – Cary, NC**\n\n**Ignited (55”TV &amp; 2 Speakers)**\n\n**System Overview**\n\nPTG will furnish and install a complete Audio and Video Signage System at this Sally Beauty location. The system includes ceiling speakers, a power amplifier, music and video media players, a commercial display, network cabling, and necessary infrastructure.\n\n**System Components**\n\n**PTG Furnished Equipment:**\n\n- (2) Ceiling Speakers – White\n- (1) 2-Channel Amplifier\n- (1) Lowell Wall Shelf\n- (1) Samsung 55\" LED Display\n- (1) Crimson TV Mount\n- (1) OFE MOOD ProFusion iS Music Player - with Stereo RCA, Ethernet, and power cables (shipped to PTG)\n- (1) OFE MOOD MVP-195 Media Player - with HDMI, Ethernet, and power cables (shipped to PTG)\n- CAT5e cabling, connectors, terminations, jacks, and plates as required for the Display location\n\n**Client-Supplied Items:**\n\n- (1) CAT5e cable and plate at the audio shelf location\n- 120V/20A clean power duplex circuit at display location\n- 120V/20A clean power duplex circuit at audio shelf location\n\n**Audio System Description**\n\nTwo (2) ceiling speakers will be installed in the retail sales area to provide background music coverage. Final speaker placement will be determined on-site by the PTG technician, avoiding locations within 12 feet of the cash wrap or hair color area.\n\nA Lowell wall shelf will be installed at a height of no greater than 5’-5” above the finished floor to support the audio equipment. All speaker wiring will terminate at this wall-mounted shelf, which will be located beneath the client-furnished power outlet and data plate—typically positioned near the client’s network rack. PTG will install one (1) 2-channel amplifier and one (1) MOOD ProFusion iS media player on the shelf.\n\nThe ProFusion iS media player will be connected to the data plate above the shelf using the supplied patch cable. This data plate is wired to Port 8 on the client’s network switch. The PTG technician will verify connectivity by confirming that the data plate is properly linked to Port 8 on the network switch.\n\n**Video System Description**\n\nPTG will install one (1) Samsung 55\" LED display behind the Bond Bar using a Crimson TV mount. The display will be mounted in a portrait orientation, with the bottom edge positioned 36 inches above the finished floor, per client specifications.\n\nThe MVP-195 media player will be concealed behind the display and connected via HDMI. All cabling will be hidden from view.\n\nThe MVP-195 player will connect to a wall plate located behind the display. This wall plate is wired to Port 7 of the patch panel at the Cash Wrap, which in turn is connected to Port 6 on the switch in the network rack.\n\nA PTG technician will verify that the MVP-195 is properly patched to Port 6 of the client's network switch.\n\n**Network Responsibility**\n\nPrior to installation, the client is responsible for providing an active network faceplate at the audio shelf location. If this infrastructure is not completed at the time of installation, the PTG technician must notify the PTG Project Manager. PTG will then proceed with completing the necessary work using PTG-supplied terminations and equipment. The PTG Project Manager will notify the Sally Beauty Project Manager, and additional charges will apply.\n\nPTG is responsible for the following low-voltage wiring:\n\n- (1) CAT5e from Cash wrap to video display location\n- Installation of all necessary terminations, jacks and faceplates\n\nTechnicians must arrive with:\n\n- Network crimp and cut tools\n- Network tester\n- Ladder (if installation requires ceiling access)\n\nAny reused OFE equipment must be onsite prior to the scheduled install. Return visits for retrieval or reinstallation of such items may result in additional charges.\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\nBefore leaving the site, the PTG technician must:\n\n- Contact Mood Media Customer Service at 855-345-5223 to verify both the ProFusion iS and MVP-195 players are online and operational.\n- Label all installed A/V equipment.\n- Clean the installed display and remove all installation-related debris.\n- Provide basic system operation training to store management personnel.\n\n**Drawings**\n\nRefer to drawing sheets:\n\n- AV-100 (Audio System Layout)\n- AV-200 (Video Display Layout)\n\n**Owner Furnished Equipment (OFE)**\n\nAll OFE must be in working order. If OFE is found to be faulty or incompatible, a Client Change Order (CCO) may be issued to replace or supplement the equipment, with labor and material costs billed accordingly.\n\n**General Notes**\n\n- Work will be performed during standard business hours (Mon–Fri, excluding holidays)\n- Installation areas must be accessible and scheduled in advance\n- No labor overages are permitted without prior PTG approval\n\n**Exclusions**\n\nThis Scope of Work does *not* include:\n\n- High-voltage electrical work, conduits, receptacles, breakers, etc.\n- Concrete cutting, coring, or fire-rated penetrations\n- Drywall or ceiling tile repairs/replacement\n- Structural reinforcement or seismic support\n- Millwork or cabinetry modifications\n- Patching, painting, or decorative finishing\n- Permit acquisition or fees (unless otherwise noted)\n- Prevailing wage or union labor (unless otherwise stated)\n- Lifts or scaffolding (unless otherwise stated)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T07:00","end":"2026-11-12T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-12T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":600,"max":600},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":10.24062333661632},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-1