{"job":{"id":20266062,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens Photo Center - Oki Data C931e Printer Service - Paper Jam Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong> Seeking a technician to perform service on a Walgreens Oki Data C931e printer located in the Photo Center. The service may include maintenance, troubleshooting, and parts installation.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /><br />Store: WALGREENS #7548<br />Date/Time: 10/23/2026 6:40:20 AM<br />Problem: OKI- Paper Jam<br /> nan<br /> Received a call from Quakeshi, she mentioned that OKI is Jamming and the error code was 380 We have recently installed new fuser and Decurl Roller And the paper is constantly jamming between these two items Ask her to remove the jam And we tried printing demo page like 8 to 10 copies it go through fine without any jamming Ask her to take a new stack of sheet and then try to print the order And it got jammed again and the error code is 639 I asked her to swap the tray 2 with Tray 4 She mentioned that the last time the technician arrived he already did this I asked her to try toprint any other order rather than this and it also got stuck so assigned a technician.<br /><br />NEXT ACTION: Order Duplex and Decurl unit for replacement.<br /><br />------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /><br /><br /></p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Oki Data Operation Guide</li><li>#1 &amp; #2 size Flat head and Philips Screwdriver Set</li><li>Microfiber cloth</li></ul><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Confirm that all parts associated with the tracking number in the work order have been delivered&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;heading to the site.&nbsp;<strong>DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT VERIFYING PARTS HAVE BEEN DELIVERED.</strong></li><li>Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Roller cleaning Instructions:</em></p><p><del>************************</del></p><p><em>EJRU spring Instructions:</em></p><p><del>************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Check in with the <strong>STORE MANAGER</strong> and inform them you are there to perform service in the Photo Center on the Oki Data C931 Printer.</li><li>Confirm with the (MOD) or Photo Center operator the problem occurring.</li><li>Confirm if any parts were sent in advance for troubleshooting.</li><li>Contact our support team at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span> to confirm the troubleshooting steps needed to diagnose the issue.</li><li>After completing the service perform 30 Test Prints to verify the printer is fully functional with minimum of at least one print from each paper tray 1-4 including the MPT tray.</li><li>Contact our support team at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span> to confirm the deliverables and review the parts return process if anything is being sent back.</li><li>If any parts are being returned, make sure it is packaged in the box the parts came in, the return label is affixed and provided to the <strong>STORE MANAGER</strong> to scan for pickup to provide you with a received receipt.</li><li>Checkout with the <strong>STORE MANAGER</strong> to sign off on the work order.</li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of 30 test prints completed and at least one print from each tray (including the MPT).</li><li>Image of the inside of the printer showing it is clean.</li><li>Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.</li><li>Any unused parts must be returned.</li><li>Any unused parts being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span> and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to perform service on a Walgreens Oki Data C931e printer located in the Photo Center. The service may include maintenance, troubleshooting, and parts installation.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  \n  \nStore: WALGREENS #7548  \nDate/Time: 10/23/2026 6:40:20 AM  \nProblem: OKI- Paper Jam  \n nan  \n Received a call from Quakeshi, she mentioned that OKI is Jamming and the error code was 380 We have recently installed new fuser and Decurl Roller And the paper is constantly jamming between these two items Ask her to remove the jam And we tried printing demo page like 8 to 10 copies it go through fine without any jamming Ask her to take a new stack of sheet and then try to print the order And it got jammed again and the error code is 639 I asked her to swap the tray 2 with Tray 4 She mentioned that the last time the technician arrived he already did this I asked her to try toprint any other order rather than this and it also got stuck so assigned a technician.  \n  \nNEXT ACTION: Order Duplex and Decurl unit for replacement.  \n  \n\\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Oki Data Operation Guide\n- \\#1 &amp; #2 size Flat head and Philips Screwdriver Set\n- Microfiber cloth\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Confirm that all parts associated with the tracking number in the work order have been delivered **before** heading to the site. **DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT VERIFYING PARTS HAVE BEEN DELIVERED.**\n2. Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Roller cleaning Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*EJRU spring Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Check in with the **STORE MANAGER** and inform them you are there to perform service in the Photo Center on the Oki Data C931 Printer.\n2. Confirm with the (MOD) or Photo Center operator the problem occurring.\n3. Confirm if any parts were sent in advance for troubleshooting.\n4. Contact our support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the troubleshooting steps needed to diagnose the issue.\n5. After completing the service perform 30 Test Prints to verify the printer is fully functional with minimum of at least one print from each paper tray 1-4 including the MPT tray.\n6. Contact our support team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the deliverables and review the parts return process if anything is being sent back.\n7. If any parts are being returned, make sure it is packaged in the box the parts came in, the return label is affixed and provided to the **STORE MANAGER** to scan for pickup to provide you with a received receipt.\n8. Checkout with the **STORE MANAGER** to sign off on the work order.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of 30 test prints completed and at least one print from each tray (including the MPT).\n- Image of the inside of the printer showing it is clean.\n- Image of the outside of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service.\n- Any unused parts must be returned.\n- Any unused parts being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the return form, packaging and return label attached.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T11:00","end":"2026-10-30T13:00","latestStart":"2026-10-30T18:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":51.48018227563598},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Low