{"job":{"id":20269033,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185 Unit#3431","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> Raleigh, 27612</p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p><p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p>Scope of Work – AP Relocation &amp; Wi-Fi Testing<p><br></p><p>The resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.</p><p><strong>1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.</li><li>Identify any potential coverage issues.</li></ul><p><strong>2. AP Relocation</strong></p><ul><li>Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.</li><li>Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.</li><li>Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.</li><li>Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.</li><li>Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Drywall Repair &amp; Painting</strong></p><ul><li>Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.</li><li>Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.</li><li>Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.</li><li>Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.</li><li>Clean the work area and remove all debris.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Final Wi-Fi Testing</strong></p><ul><li>Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.</li><li>Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.</li><li>Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.</li><li>Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.</li><li>Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.</li></ul>Required Tools &amp; Materials<ul><li>Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed</li><li>Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools</li><li>Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools</li><li>Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods</li><li>Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies</li><li>Matching wall texture, primer, and paint</li><li>Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies</li><li>Ladder and standard installation tools</li></ul>Completion Requirements<ul><li>AP relocated according to the provided design.</li><li>All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.</li><li>Drywall patched, textured, and painted.</li><li>Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.</li><li>Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.</li><li>Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.</li></ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** Raleigh, 27612\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\nScope of Work – AP Relocation &amp; Wi-Fi TestingThe resident is experiencing weak Wi-Fi signal in the furthest bedroom. The technician will relocate the existing Access Point (AP) to the living room based on the provided design to improve wireless coverage throughout the unit.\n\n**1. Initial Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Test the current Wi-Fi signal and speeds in the living room and all bedrooms, especially the furthest bedroom.\n- Record signal strength (dBm) and speed test results before relocating the AP.\n- Identify any potential coverage issues.\n\n**2. AP Relocation**\n\n- Review the provided design for the new AP location in the living room.\n- Relocate the existing AP to the designated location.\n- Run or extend the necessary Ethernet cabling to the new AP location.\n- Cut drywall as needed to route cabling and complete the installation.\n- Verify cabling and connectivity before mounting the AP.\n\n**3. Drywall Repair &amp; Painting**\n\n- Patch all drywall openings created during the relocation.\n- Repair the original AP location if no longer needed.\n- Apply texture as needed to match the existing wall finish.\n- Prime and paint repaired areas to match the existing wall color as closely as possible.\n- Clean the work area and remove all debris.\n\n**4. Final Wi-Fi Testing**\n\n- Verify the AP is online and functioning properly.\n- Perform Wi-Fi signal and speed tests in the same locations tested before relocation.\n- Pay special attention to the furthest bedroom where the resident reported weak signal.\n- Record before-and-after results to determine whether coverage improved.\n- Work with Engineering if additional troubleshooting or adjustments are needed.\n\nRequired Tools &amp; Materials- Laptop and cellphone with WiFiman installed\n- Ethernet cable tester and basic networking tools\n- Cat6 cable, connectors, and termination tools\n- Drywall cutting tools and fish tape/rods\n- Drywall patching materials, joint compound, and sanding supplies\n- Matching wall texture, primer, and paint\n- Drop cloths, PPE, and cleaning supplies\n- Ladder and standard installation tools\n\nCompletion Requirements- AP relocated according to the provided design.\n- All cabling tested and AP confirmed online.\n- Drywall patched, textured, and painted.\n- Before-and-after Wi-Fi results documented, especially in the furthest bedroom.\n- Photos uploaded showing the original location, new AP installation, and completed wall repairs.\n- Notify Operations and Engineering if the signal remains weak after relocation.\n- **Note:** Technician should verify the new AP placement and cabling path before cutting drywall. Any additional work outside the approved design must be reviewed with Operations before proceeding.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-19T10:00","end":"2026-11-04T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3.6136968948458},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/19/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"Listen Audio Book"},{"start":"2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"DataMax"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-19T19:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Nothing"},{"start":"2026-10-21T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Web Conference Interview Round - 1 | Desktop Engineer L1 | Raleigh NC - USA"},{"start":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Oil VW tepair"},{"start":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fair festival"},{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793288908564}
{"job":{"id":"7792104988","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"RM Wilson Apts- Voice Port 11/3","description":"Standard equipment required: <br><br>Laptop (Windows XP or higher with admin rights) with PuTTY installed, plus laptop charger<br>Console cable<br>Extension cord<br>Minimum 100 ft Cat5/Cat6 cabling<br>Cat5/Cat6 patch cords<br>Lineman's telephony handset / butt-set, analog phone/test-set, tone generator and wand, and Ethernet cable tester<br>Punch tool (66 &amp; 110), RJ11/RJ45 crimper<br>cross-connect wire, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 modular plugs, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet keystone jacks, and gel-crimp connectors<br> Smart phone and a laptop with hotspot capability<br><br>Objectives<br><br>Cut the customer's phone service over to the new Granite ATA and initiate the porting of telephone numbers 252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.<br><br>Instructions<br><br>Contact LCON prior to arrival.<br>Upon arrival, work with Carol at LCON and locate the following equipment:<br>Granite ATA (HT812)<br>MAC Address: EC:74:D7:F8:51:A6<br>The customer's office phone and fax machine.<br>These are customer-owned devices and were not provided by Granite.<br>Carol will assist in identifying their locations.<br><br><br>Scope of Work<br><br><br>Verify the Granite ATA is powered on and connected to the network.<br><br><br>Confirm connectivity and registration of the ATA.<br><br><br><br><br>Once you have confirmed that the ATA is powered up- and is on-line- Please contact the ZTP line- 888-624-5295<br>give them order number: 02337133<br>Have the ZTP agent- confirm which telephone numbers are on which port- <br>Connect the customers phone equipment - accordingly. <br>Have the ZTP agent - trigger the ports. <br>once the port is completed. Test in bound and outbound- - on both lines-  252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.<br>Confirm with customer Carol- that all is working as needed. <br><br>Objectives<br>Cut the customer's phone service over to the new Granite ATA and initiate the porting of telephone numbers 252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.<br><br>Instructions<br>Contact LCON prior to arrival.<br>Upon arrival, work with Carol at LCON to locate the following equipment:<br>Granite ATA (HT812)<br>MAC Address: EC:74:D7:F8:51:A6<br>Locate the customer's office phone and fax machine.<br><br>These are customer-owned devices and were not provided by Granite.<br>Carol will assist with identifying their locations.<br><br>Scope of Work<br>Verify that the Granite ATA (HT812) is powered on and connected to the network.<br>Confirm that the ATA is online and properly registered.<br>Once the ATA is confirmed online, contact the ZTP Team at 888-624-5295.<br>Provide Order Number: 02337133 to the ZTP agent.<br>Have the ZTP agent confirm which telephone numbers are assigned to each ATA port.<br>Connect the customer's phone and fax equipment to the appropriate ATA ports as instructed by the ZTP agent.<br><br>Request that the ZTP agent initiate the port activation.<br>Once the port is complete, perform inbound and outbound call testing for:<br>252-985-3393<br>252-985-3394<br>Verify that all services are functioning properly, including fax functionality.<br><br>Review the completed cutover with Carol and obtain confirmation that all services are operating as expected.<br>Document test results, customer acceptance, and any issues encountered before closing out the work.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T13:00","end":"2026-11-03T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 3, 1:00 PM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 3, Wed, Nov 4, Thu, Nov 5, Fri, Nov 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","