{"job":{"id":"7792104988","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"RM Wilson Apts- Voice Port 11/3","description":"<p><strong>Granite Ticket Number: 7108730</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Standard equipment required: </p><p><br></p><p>Laptop (Windows XP or higher with admin rights) with PuTTY installed, plus laptop charger</p><p>Console cable</p><p>Extension cord</p><p>Minimum 100 ft Cat5/Cat6 cabling</p><p>Cat5/Cat6 patch cords</p><p>Lineman's telephony handset / butt-set, analog phone/test-set, tone generator and wand, and Ethernet cable tester</p><p>Punch tool (66 &amp; 110), RJ11/RJ45 crimper</p><p>cross-connect wire, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 modular plugs, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet keystone jacks, and gel-crimp connectors</p><p> Smart phone and a laptop with hotspot capability</p><p><br></p><p>Objectives</p><p><br></p><p>Cut the customer's phone service over to the new Granite ATA and initiate the porting of telephone numbers 252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.</p><p><br></p><p>Instructions</p><p><br></p><p>Contact LCON prior to arrival.</p><p>Upon arrival, work with Carol at LCON and locate the following equipment:</p><p>Granite ATA (HT812)</p><p>MAC Address: EC:74:D7:F8:51:A6</p><p>The customer's office phone and fax machine.</p><p>These are customer-owned devices and were not provided by Granite.</p><p>Carol will assist in identifying their locations.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Verify the Granite ATA is powered on and connected to the network.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Confirm connectivity and registration of the ATA.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Once you have confirmed that the ATA is powered up- and is on-line- Please contact the ZTP line- 888-624-5295</p><p>give them order number: 02337133</p><p>Have the ZTP agent- confirm which telephone numbers are on which port- </p><p>Connect the customers phone equipment - accordingly. </p><p>Have the ZTP agent - trigger the ports. </p><p>once the port is completed. Test in bound and outbound- - on both lines- 252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.</p><p>Confirm with customer Carol- that all is working as needed. </p><p><br></p><p>Objectives</p><p>Cut the customer's phone service over to the new Granite ATA and initiate the porting of telephone numbers 252-985-3393 and 252-985-3394.</p><p><br></p><p>Instructions</p><p>Contact LCON prior to arrival.</p><p>Upon arrival, work with Carol at LCON to locate the following equipment:</p><p>Granite ATA (HT812)</p><p>MAC Address: EC:74:D7:F8:51:A6</p><p>Locate the customer's office phone and fax machine.</p><p><br></p><p>These are customer-owned devices and were not provided by Granite.</p><p>Carol will assist with identifying their locations.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p>Verify that the Granite ATA (HT812) is powered on and connected to the network.</p><p>Confirm that the ATA is online and properly registered.</p><p>Once the ATA is confirmed online, contact the ZTP Team at 888-624-5295.</p><p>Provide Order Number: 02337133 to the ZTP agent.</p><p>Have the ZTP agent confirm which telephone numbers are assigned to each ATA port.</p><p>Connect the customer's phone and fax equipment to the appropriate ATA ports as instructed by the ZTP agent.</p><p><br></p><p>Request that the ZTP agent initiate the port activation.</p><p>Once the port is complete, perform inbound and outbound call testing for:</p><p>252-985-3393</p><p>252-985-3394</p><p>Verify that all services are functioning properly, including fax functionality.</p><p><br></p><p>Review the completed cutover with Carol and obtain confirmation that all services are operating as expected.</p><p>Document test results, customer acceptance, and any issues encountered before closing out the work.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T14:00","end":"2026-11-03T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.8},"