{"job":{"id":20269633,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ntiva, Inc","title":"Network Hardware Installation & Remote Configuration Support","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Check In/Out</strong></p><ul><li>Call the Ntiva engineer at the number on the work order when you arrive on site.</li><li>Before leaving, call the engineer to check out. Do not leave until the Ntiva engineer confirms testing is complete and gives release approval.</li><li>Keep GPS on for check-in and check-out.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Deliverables for Payment</strong></p><ul><li>Release approval from the Ntiva remote engineer</li><li>GPS on for check-in and check-out</li><li>Clear after photos of the completed installation: network rack or IT closet, firewall, switches, UPS, access points, and cabling</li></ul><p><strong>Scope Overview</strong></p><p><strong> The technician will provide onsite hands for the network installation at the client’s new office. The equipment has already been added to the Meraki dashboard and configured remotely by the Ntiva engineer. The technician will physically install and connect the equipment, then work with the engineer by phone to bring it online and test it.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ul><li>Check in with the Ntiva remote engineer on arrival</li><li>Work with the onsite contact to locate the delivered network equipment</li><li>Install the rack-mount UPS (CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U, 1) for the network equipment</li><li>Install and connect the Meraki firewall (MX85, 1)</li><li>Install and connect the Meraki switches (MS130-48P, 2)</li><li>Install and connect the Meraki access points (MR46, 16) at the locations provided by the engineer or onsite contact</li><li>Connect equipment to power and patch cabling as directed</li><li>Power on all network devices</li><li>Confirm each device comes online in the Meraki dashboard with the engineer</li><li>Assist with firmware or device updates as directed by the engineer</li><li>Connect the firewall to the new ISP circuit and assist with WAN connectivity testing</li><li>Assist with LAN and wireless connectivity testing with the engineer and the client contact</li><li>Take clear after photos as listed under Required Deliverables</li><li>Confirm completion and get release approval from the Ntiva engineer before leaving site</li></ul><p><strong>Required Skills and Tools</strong></p><ul><li>Experience installing network hardware</li><li>Ability to follow remote engineer instructions</li><li>Basic knowledge of firewalls, switches, access points, and network cabling</li><li>Laptop, in case it is needed for testing or a direct connection to equipment</li><li>Spare patch cables and basic cabling tools</li></ul><p><strong>Equipment Provided</strong></p><ul><li>Meraki MX85 firewall (1)</li><li>Meraki MS130-48P switches (2)</li><li>Meraki MR46 access points (16)</li><li>CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U UPS (1)</li><li>Cat5e patch cables, 3 ft and 6 ft, as provided with the equipment</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Check In/Out**\n\n- Call the Ntiva engineer at the number on the work order when you arrive on site.\n- Before leaving, call the engineer to check out. Do not leave until the Ntiva engineer confirms testing is complete and gives release approval.\n- Keep GPS on for check-in and check-out.\n\n**Required Deliverables for Payment**\n\n- Release approval from the Ntiva remote engineer\n- GPS on for check-in and check-out\n- Clear after photos of the completed installation: network rack or IT closet, firewall, switches, UPS, access points, and cabling\n\n**Scope Overview**\n\n **The technician will provide onsite hands for the network installation at the client’s new office. The equipment has already been added to the Meraki dashboard and configured remotely by the Ntiva engineer. The technician will physically install and connect the equipment, then work with the engineer by phone to bring it online and test it.**\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n- Check in with the Ntiva remote engineer on arrival\n- Work with the onsite contact to locate the delivered network equipment\n- Install the rack-mount UPS (CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U, 1) for the network equipment\n- Install and connect the Meraki firewall (MX85, 1)\n- Install and connect the Meraki switches (MS130-48P, 2)\n- Install and connect the Meraki access points (MR46, 16) at the locations provided by the engineer or onsite contact\n- Connect equipment to power and patch cabling as directed\n- Power on all network devices\n- Confirm each device comes online in the Meraki dashboard with the engineer\n- Assist with firmware or device updates as directed by the engineer\n- Connect the firewall to the new ISP circuit and assist with WAN connectivity testing\n- Assist with LAN and wireless connectivity testing with the engineer and the client contact\n- Take clear after photos as listed under Required Deliverables\n- Confirm completion and get release approval from the Ntiva engineer before leaving site\n\n**Required Skills and Tools**\n\n- Experience installing network hardware\n- Ability to follow remote engineer instructions\n- Basic knowledge of firewalls, switches, access points, and network cabling\n- Laptop, in case it is needed for testing or a direct connection to equipment\n- Spare patch cables and basic cabling tools\n\n**Equipment Provided**\n\n- Meraki MX85 firewall (1)\n- Meraki MS130-48P switches (2)\n- Meraki MR46 access points (16)\n- CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U UPS (1)\n- Cat5e patch cables, 3 ft and 6 ft, as provided with the equipment","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T07:00","end":"2026-11-11T14:00","latestStart":"2026-11-11T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":395},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":65},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":8.388218323415234},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Tot