{"job":{"id":20269633,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ntiva, Inc","title":"Network Hardware Installation & Remote Configuration Support","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Check In/Out</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call the Ntiva engineer at the number on the work order when you arrive on site.</li>\n<li>Before leaving, call the engineer to check out. Do not leave until the Ntiva engineer confirms testing is complete and gives release approval.</li>\n<li>Keep GPS on for check-in and check-out.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Deliverables for Payment</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Release approval from the Ntiva remote engineer</li>\n<li>GPS on for check-in and check-out</li>\n<li>Clear after photos of the completed installation: network rack or IT closet, firewall, switches, UPS, access points, and cabling</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope Overview</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The technician will provide onsite hands for the network installation at the client’s new office. The equipment has already been added to the Meraki dashboard and configured remotely by the Ntiva engineer. The technician will physically install and connect the equipment, then work with the engineer by phone to bring it online and test it.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>[Cabling vendor installing APs. Work is to test APs]</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with the Ntiva remote engineer on arrival</li>\n<li>Work with the onsite contact to locate the delivered network equipment</li>\n<li>Install the rack-mount UPS (CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U, 1) for the network equipment</li>\n<li>Install and connect the Meraki firewall (MX85, 1)</li>\n<li>Install and connect the Meraki switches (MS130-48P, 2)</li>\n<li>Install and connect the Meraki access points (MR46, 16) at the locations provided by the engineer or onsite contact</li>\n<li>Connect equipment to power and patch cabling as directed</li>\n<li>Power on all network devices</li>\n<li>Confirm each device comes online in the Meraki dashboard with the engineer</li>\n<li>Assist with firmware or device updates as directed by the engineer</li>\n<li>Connect the firewall to the new ISP circuit and assist with WAN connectivity testing</li>\n<li>Assist with LAN and wireless connectivity testing with the engineer and the client contact</li>\n<li>Take clear after photos as listed under Required Deliverables</li>\n<li>Confirm completion and get release approval from the Ntiva engineer before leaving site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Skills and Tools</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience installing network hardware</li>\n<li>Ability to follow remote engineer instructions</li>\n<li>Basic knowledge of firewalls, switches, access points, and network cabling</li>\n<li>Laptop, in case it is needed for testing or a direct connection to equipment</li>\n<li>Spare patch cables and basic cabling tools</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Equipment Provided</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Meraki MX85 firewall (1)</li>\n<li>Meraki MS130-48P switches (2)</li>\n<li>Meraki MR46 access points (16)</li>\n<li>CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U UPS (1)</li>\n<li>Cat5e patch cables, 3 ft and 6 ft, as provided with the equipment</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Check In/Out**\n\n- Call the Ntiva engineer at the number on the work order when you arrive on site.\n- Before leaving, call the engineer to check out. Do not leave until the Ntiva engineer confirms testing is complete and gives release approval.\n- Keep GPS on for check-in and check-out.\n\n**Required Deliverables for Payment**\n\n- Release approval from the Ntiva remote engineer\n- GPS on for check-in and check-out\n- Clear after photos of the completed installation: network rack or IT closet, firewall, switches, UPS, access points, and cabling\n\n**Scope Overview**\n\n**The technician will provide onsite hands for the network installation at the client’s new office. The equipment has already been added to the Meraki dashboard and configured remotely by the Ntiva engineer. The technician will physically install and connect the equipment, then work with the engineer by phone to bring it online and test it.**\n\n**\\[Cabling vendor installing APs. Work is to test APs\\]**\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n- Check in with the Ntiva remote engineer on arrival\n- Work with the onsite contact to locate the delivered network equipment\n- Install the rack-mount UPS (CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U, 1) for the network equipment\n- Install and connect the Meraki firewall (MX85, 1)\n- Install and connect the Meraki switches (MS130-48P, 2)\n- Install and connect the Meraki access points (MR46, 16) at the locations provided by the engineer or onsite contact\n- Connect equipment to power and patch cabling as directed\n- Power on all network devices\n- Confirm each device comes online in the Meraki dashboard with the engineer\n- Assist with firmware or device updates as directed by the engineer\n- Connect the firewall to the new ISP circuit and assist with WAN connectivity testing\n- Assist with LAN and wireless connectivity testing with the engineer and the client contact\n- Take clear after photos as listed under Required Deliverables\n- Confirm completion and get release approval from the Ntiva engineer before leaving site\n\n**Required Skills and Tools**\n\n- Experience installing network hardware\n- Ability to follow remote engineer instructions\n- Basic knowledge of firewalls, switches, access points, and network cabling\n- Laptop, in case it is needed for testing or a direct connection to equipment\n- Spare patch cables and basic cabling tools\n\n**Equipment Provided**\n\n- Meraki MX85 firewall (1)\n- Meraki MS130-48P switches (2)\n- Meraki MR46 access points (16)\n- CyberPower OR1500LCDRM1U UPS (1)\n- Cat5e patch cables, 3 ft and 6 ft, as provided with the equipment","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T07:00","end":"2026-11-11T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-11T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":285},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":65},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":8.388218323415234},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $285 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793292933196}
{"job":{"id":20268872,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Looma Project","title":"The Looma Project: Offline Maintenance for Loop™ Display - Harris Teeter - 118","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Revisit rate:</strong> $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)</li>\n<li><strong>Trip charges:</strong> Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above</li>\n<li><strong>No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Your closeout notes must include:</strong>A clear description of the issue found on-site</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The outcome of each step</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>❌ <strong>Not acceptable:</strong><em>\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"</em> ✅<strong>Acceptable:</strong><em>\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This Work Order covers <strong>one (1) hour of on-site work</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at <strong>$60 per additional hour.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.</strong> Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.</li>\n<li><strong>No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY</strong></p>\n<p>Monday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST</p>\n<p>Contact: <strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> Email: support@theloomaproject.com</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p>\n<p>You must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cell phone with camera capabilities</li>\n<li>10' ladder</li>\n<li>Phillips head screwdriver</li>\n<li>Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></p>\n<p>Looma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><em>This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.</em></p>\n<p><strong>HT WORK ORDER #:</strong> INC13205606</p>\n<p><strong>PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete the following before arriving on-site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set your start time in the Field Nation platform</li>\n<li>Download and review the <strong>Offline Tablet Reference Guide</strong> (attached) and<strong>HT_Chromebox_Troubleshooting_Guide</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE</strong></p>\n<p>Upon entering the store, proceed to the <strong>Customer Service Desk</strong>. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the <strong>HT Work Order number</strong>. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:</p>\n<p><strong>Looma Field Support Team</strong> &#x1F4E7; support@theloomaproject.com &#x1F4DE; (866) 440-LOOP</p>\n<p><strong>ON-SITE TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>Complete in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check in with the WO Manager</strong> — Call<strong>(866) 440-5667</strong> upon arrival</li>\n<li><strong>Check in with Customer Service</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Locate the Loop™ display</strong> referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. <em>Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.</em></li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> before beginning any maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong> using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)</li>\n<li><strong>Photograph the entire display</strong> after completing maintenance</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with the WO Manager</strong> before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site</li>\n<li><strong>Check out with Customer Service</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY</strong></p>\n<p>Loop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET</strong></p>\n<p>A comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.</p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER — LOOMA FIELD SUPPORT (HARRIS TEETER)**\n\n**⚠ PAYMENT POLICY — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **The payment listed on this Work Order is final upon acceptance. No additional compensation will be issued after a Work Order has been accepted.**\n- **ALL counteroffers MUST be submitted BEFORE accepting this Work Order. Counteroffers submitted after acceptance will not be honored.**\n- **Mileage/trip charge requests MUST include exact mileage driven. You are required to provide a photo from your GPS showing the exact mileage. Requests submitted without this documentation will not be processed.**\n- **Revisit rate:** $60 per visit (for approved part replacement revisits only)\n- **Trip charges:** Reimbursed at the current IRS rate of $0.70/mile, with required GPS documentation as noted above\n- **No payment will be issued if the technician does not have the required tools to complete this Work Order. Do not accept this WO if you are not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. 10' ladder\n3. Phillips head screwdriver\n4. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13205606\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-29T11:00","end":"2026-10-29T12:00","latestStart":"2026-10-29T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":15.104709457235211},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-29T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"WM Granite"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793292989494}
{"job":{"id":20269791,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Comm-Works","title":"SBUX - Ipad Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>***PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE REVIEWED PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE***</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>SCOPE OF WORK: Remove Existing ELO, Install iPad w/Mount</p>\n<p>--Be prepared with a Phillips #2 screwdriver, a snipping/cutting tool, and cabling materials to replace/repair cabling as needed.</p>\n<p>--Install guide attached and the new mounting equipment is sent to the site for technician.</p>\n<p>--Remove existing ELO, install the iPad VESA mount onto the tri-arm, an iPad into the mounting case, and then add them all together with the charger to have an iPad DPM.</p>\n<p>--Ensure ELO is boxed and labeled for return. Technician to take to FedEx to return ship.</p>\n<p>--Ensure replacement iPad DPM installed and mounted.</p>\n<p>--Ensure iPad DPM is connected to WAN, troubleshoot connection if needed.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>CABLING DISPATCH EXPECTATIONS:</p>\n<p>--Technicians are expected to leave each area so that it looks like a new installation.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>--If there are any questions about what is approved, please call New Era immediately to discuss.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>NEW ERA CONTACT INFORMATION:</p>\n<p>Dial in by phone</p>\n<p><u>+1 617-865-0253,,158951459#</u> United States, Boston</p>\n<p><u>Find a local number</u></p>\n<p>Phone conference ID: 158 951 459#</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>DELIVERABLES ARE DUE BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE</p>\n<p>--Technician is REQUIRED to check in/out and complete the task</p>\n<p>--Technician must provide CLEAR and QUALITY photos in the Smartsheet Form.</p>\n<p>---If tech experiences issues with Tech-Works, email all photos to New Era at StarbucksDPMCoordinators@neweratech.com@neweratech.com. Subject line needs to include the Store #</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Smartsheet From for Pictures --</p>\n<p>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019f4d98d4b072859c52a0037ac3379a</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>PROFESSIONAL REQUIREMENTS:</p>\n<p>--Technician must attain a professional demeanor while onsite. Failure to do so will result in No Payment and further repercussions.</p>\n<p>--Technician must be dressed business casual - no shorts or open toed shoes.</p>\n<p>--You are representing New Era Technology/Comm-Works while onsite.</p>\n<p>--Instructions MUST be followed, if support isn't contacted for release, payment may be denied.</p>\n<p>--Deliverables MUST be uploaded within 24 hours of site completion, if not payment may be denied.</p>\n<p>--By accepting this work order, you are agreeing to these terms.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE REVIEWED PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE\\*\\*\\*\n\nSCOPE OF WORK: Remove Existing ELO, Install iPad w/Mount\n\n\\--Be prepared with a Phillips #2 screwdriver, a snipping/cutting tool, and cabling materials to replace/repair cabling as needed.\n\n\\--Install guide attached and the new mounting equipment is sent to the site for technician.\n\n\\--Remove existing ELO, install the iPad VESA mount onto the tri-arm, an iPad into the mounting case, and then add them all together with the charger to have an iPad DPM.\n\n\\--Ensure ELO is boxed and labeled for return. Technician to take to FedEx to return ship.\n\n\\--Ensure replacement iPad DPM installed and mounted.\n\n\\--Ensure iPad DPM is connected to WAN, troubleshoot connection if needed.\n\nCABLING DISPATCH EXPECTATIONS:\n\n\\--Technicians are expected to leave each area so that it looks like a new installation.\n\n\\--If there are any questions about what is approved, please call New Era immediately to discuss.\n\nNEW ERA CONTACT INFORMATION:\n\nDial in by phone\n\n+1 617-865-0253,,158951459# United States, Boston\n\nFind a local number\n\nPhone conference ID: 158 951 459#\n\nDELIVERABLES ARE DUE BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE\n\n\\--Technician is REQUIRED to check in/out and complete the task\n\n\\--Technician must provide CLEAR and QUALITY photos in the Smartsheet Form.\n\n\\---If tech experiences issues with Tech-Works, email all photos to New Era at StarbucksDPMCoordinators@neweratech.com@neweratech.com. Subject line needs to include the Store #\n\nSmartsheet From for Pictures --\n\n<https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019f4d98d4b072859c52a0037ac3379a>\n\nPROFESSIONAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n\\--Technician must attain a professional demeanor while onsite. Failure to do so will result in No Payment and further repercussions.\n\n\\--Technician must be dressed business casual - no shorts or open toed shoes.\n\n\\--You are representing New Era Technology/Comm-Works while onsite.\n\n\\--Instructions MUST be followed, if support isn't contacted for release, payment may be denied.\n\n\\--Deliverables MUST be uploaded within 24 hours of site completion, if not payment may be denied.\n\n\\--By accepting this work order, you are agreeing to these terms.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-19T15:00","end":"2026-11-19T16:30","latestStart":"2026-11-19T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":56.98009931598097},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"