{"job":{"id":20269247,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pitney Bowes","title":"Lift and Assist - Ability to lift 65 lbs","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Description:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>THIS IS NON-TECHNICAL WORK</li>\n<li>This work requires the ability to lift a minimum of 65 pounds. If you are not able to lift 65 pounds or more, please decline the assignment.</li>\n<li>Coordinate with the on-site <del>****** *****</del> technician to aid in the breakdown of a new equipment pallet. Individual pieces of equipment will be transported via hand, hand cart, or dolly to a designated area. Bringing such transporting devices is encouraged but not required.</li>\n<li>This position requires you to move a series of 7-12 boxes. You will be responsible for opening boxes and placing equipment at the designated location (to be instructed by the onsite <del>****** *****</del> technician), however, NO equipment setup is required. You will help move any existing equipment (if applicable) to a<del>****** *****</del> technician-designated location and discard the empty boxes at the site dumpster.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TWO-PERSON PICKUP</strong>: If PB decides a second person is required to assist, then we will create an additional assignment for another technician. The second technician must be on the Field Nation platform and have a background and drug test on file.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Representation:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the site contact(s) as an Authorized<del>****** *****</del> Service Provider and have your work order available for presentation.</li>\n<li>Under no circumstances shall someone other than the person assigned to this work order be allowed on the premises during the service call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Tasks:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Confirm acknowledgment of the set service time by setting the same appointment time. Please do not accept assignments if you cannot make the scheduled service as defined.</li>\n<li>Call the <del>****** *****</del> technician no later than the business day before the service appointment to confirm the appointment time &amp; meeting place. If you cannot reach the<del>****** *****</del> technician, then please send a text message, and leave a voicemail with the <del>****** *****</del>technician. Coordinate a meet-up place with the <del>****** *****</del> technician prior to the appointment time.</li>\n<li>If you do not receive confirmation from the <del>****** *****</del> technician within 2 hours of the scheduled appointment time then contact the EWP Support team.</li>\n<li>Go to the site. Must bring a driver's license or state ID.</li>\n<li>Use Assignment Check-in upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Upon arrival, call the <strong>site contact (</strong><del>****** *****</del> technician<strong>)</strong> to coordinate the final meet-up. If you cannot reach the site contact then wait 15 minutes and try again. If there is still no communication, then call the EWP Support team.</li>\n<li>If the EWP Support team cannot locate the <del>****** *****</del> technician then they will release you from the site. In such instances, this call to EWP Support [<strong>while you are on-site]</strong> is required in order to receive payment.</li>\n<li>Perform pallet breakdown, equipment transport, box opening, equipment lifting, and box breakdown. You will not be asked to perform any technical setup of the equipment.</li>\n<li>Take a picture of the work area documenting that all boxes and pallets have been emptied, and disposed of and that the work area is clean.</li>\n<li>Following completion of service, confirm with the <del>****** *****</del> technician that you do not need to provide any further assistance. If not, then request a signature from the <del>****** *****</del> technician using the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>Check out from the site on Field Nation</li>\n<li>Upon completion of the work order, mark it as Complete while still onsite. Failure to comply may result in delayed payment.</li>\n</ol>","markdown":"**Description:**\n\n- THIS IS NON-TECHNICAL WORK\n- This work requires the ability to lift a minimum of 65 pounds. If you are not able to lift 65 pounds or more, please decline the assignment.\n- Coordinate with the on-site \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician to aid in the breakdown of a new equipment pallet. Individual pieces of equipment will be transported via hand, hand cart, or dolly to a designated area. Bringing such transporting devices is encouraged but not required.\n- This position requires you to move a series of 7-12 boxes. You will be responsible for opening boxes and placing equipment at the designated location (to be instructed by the onsite \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician), however, NO equipment setup is required. You will help move any existing equipment (if applicable) to a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician-designated location and discard the empty boxes at the site dumpster.\n\n**TWO-PERSON PICKUP**: If PB decides a second person is required to assist, then we will create an additional assignment for another technician. The second technician must be on the Field Nation platform and have a background and drug test on file.\n\n**Representation:**\n\n- Introduce yourself to the site contact(s) as an Authorized\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Service Provider and have your work order available for presentation.\n- Under no circumstances shall someone other than the person assigned to this work order be allowed on the premises during the service call.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Confirm acknowledgment of the set service time by setting the same appointment time. Please do not accept assignments if you cannot make the scheduled service as defined.\n2. Call the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician no later than the business day before the service appointment to confirm the appointment time &amp; meeting place. If you cannot reach the\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician, then please send a text message, and leave a voicemail with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*technician. Coordinate a meet-up place with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician prior to the appointment time.\n3. If you do not receive confirmation from the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician within 2 hours of the scheduled appointment time then contact the EWP Support team.\n4. Go to the site. Must bring a driver's license or state ID.\n5. Use Assignment Check-in upon arrival.\n6. Upon arrival, call the **site contact (**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician**)** to coordinate the final meet-up. If you cannot reach the site contact then wait 15 minutes and try again. If there is still no communication, then call the EWP Support team.\n7. If the EWP Support team cannot locate the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician then they will release you from the site. In such instances, this call to EWP Support \\[**while you are on-site\\]** is required in order to receive payment.\n8. Perform pallet breakdown, equipment transport, box opening, equipment lifting, and box breakdown. You will not be asked to perform any technical setup of the equipment.\n9. Take a picture of the work area documenting that all boxes and pallets have been emptied, and disposed of and that the work area is clean.\n10. Following completion of service, confirm with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician that you do not need to provide any further assistance. If not, then request a signature from the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* technician using the Field Nation app.\n11. Check out from the site on Field Nation\n12. Upon completion of the work order, mark it as Complete while still onsite. Failure to comply may result in delayed payment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T09:00","end":"2026-11-05T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":