{"job":{"id":20269995,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"RNC","title":"Arbors at Cary Networking / Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p>Arbors at Cary Networking / Site Survey</p><p><strong>Networking / Site Survey</strong></p><ol><li><strong>POC: </strong></li></ol><p><strong>Tech needed for site survey, link below:</strong></p><p>https://forms.office.com/r/PsBeQW7EU2</p><p><strong>Technician Requirements – REQUIREDTechnician must complete the full site survey form and upload clear, detailed, and labeled photos. Incomplete photo documentation may result in a return visit.</strong></p><p><strong>Survey to includes hardware, counts, passwords, network info, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Survey Scope Includes:</strong></p><ul><li>Hardware inventory (with photos)</li><li>Device counts and models</li><li>Network configuration details</li><li>Credentials (as applicable)</li><li>ISP and circuit details</li><li>Current setup documentation</li></ul><p><strong>PHOTO REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY) </strong></p><p><strong>All photos must be:</strong></p><ul><li>Clear (no blur)</li><li>Well-lit</li><li>Taken from both <strong>wide view and close-up</strong></li><li><strong>Properly labeled in the work order (e.g., </strong><em>“Network Rack – Full View”, “Switch Ports”, “ISP Modem Back Panel”</em>)</li></ul><p><strong>1. Networking Room / Area</strong></p><ul><li>Wide shot of entire room or network area</li><li>Rack or wall-mounted equipment (full view)</li><li>Cable management and patch panels</li></ul><p><strong>2. Modem / ISP Equipment</strong></p><ul><li>Front of modem (showing status lights)</li><li>Back of modem (CLEAR view of ALL connections)</li><li>Close-up of labels (ISP name, circuit ID if available)</li></ul><p><strong>3. Switch(es)</strong></p><ul><li>Front of switch (show status lights)</li><li>Back of switch (if accessible)</li><li>Close-up of <strong>ports showing active vs open ports</strong></li></ul><p><strong>4. Firewall / Router</strong></p><ul><li>Full device photo</li><li>Close-up of connections</li><li>Any labeling (make/model/serial)</li></ul><p><strong>5. Workstations &amp; Office Setup</strong></p><ul><li>Each workstation setup (desk + equipment)</li><li>Computer devices (front + back if accessible)</li><li>Printers, scanners, and other peripherals</li></ul><p><strong>6. Cabling</strong></p><ul><li>How ISP enters the building (demarcation point)</li><li>Any exposed or critical cabling paths</li><li>Patch panels / wall jacks</li></ul><p><strong>7. Additional Critical Items</strong></p><ul><li>WiFi access points (mounted or visible)</li><li>Phone system hardware (if present)</li><li>Any non-standard or legacy equipment</li></ul><p>⚠️ <strong>IMPORTANT </strong>Photos like “just the front of a rack” or “zoomed-out unclear shots” are NOT acceptable</p><ul><li>Technician must verify that <strong>all ports and connections are visible and readable</strong></li><li><strong>If something cannot be accessed or photographed, technician must note it in the survey</strong></li></ul><p>Technical questions, call John Rubino: 949-257-9757-Email: john@rncinc.net</p><p><strong>Location: Leasing office</strong></p><p><strong>**Technician must call Sarah (949-393-1740) before leaving site to review survey completeness, including photo quality and coverage.</strong></p>","markdown":"Arbors at Cary Networking / Site Survey\n\n**Networking / Site Survey**\n\n1. **POC:**\n\n**Tech needed for site survey, link below:**\n\n<https://forms.office.com/r/PsBeQW7EU2>\n\n**Technician Requirements – REQUIREDTechnician must complete the full site survey form and upload clear, detailed, and labeled photos. Incomplete photo documentation may result in a return visit.**\n\n**Survey to includes hardware, counts, passwords, network info, etc.**\n\n**Survey Scope Includes:**\n\n- Hardware inventory (with photos)\n- Device counts and models\n- Network configuration details\n- Credentials (as applicable)\n- ISP and circuit details\n- Current setup documentation\n\n**PHOTO REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY)**\n\n**All photos must be:**\n\n- Clear (no blur)\n- Well-lit\n- Taken from both **wide view and close-up**\n- **Properly labeled in the work order (e.g.,** *“Network Rack – Full View”, “Switch Ports”, “ISP Modem Back Panel”*)\n\n**1. Networking Room / Area**\n\n- Wide shot of entire room or network area\n- Rack or wall-mounted equipment (full view)\n- Cable management and patch panels\n\n**2. Modem / ISP Equipment**\n\n- Front of modem (showing status lights)\n- Back of modem (CLEAR view of ALL connections)\n- Close-up of labels (ISP name, circuit ID if available)\n\n**3. Switch(es)**\n\n- Front of switch (show status lights)\n- Back of switch (if accessible)\n- Close-up of **ports showing active vs open ports**\n\n**4. Firewall / Router**\n\n- Full device photo\n- Close-up of connections\n- Any labeling (make/model/serial)\n\n**5. Workstations &amp; Office Setup**\n\n- Each workstation setup (desk + equipment)\n- Computer devices (front + back if accessible)\n- Printers, scanners, and other peripherals\n\n**6. Cabling**\n\n- How ISP enters the building (demarcation point)\n- Any exposed or critical cabling paths\n- Patch panels / wall jacks\n\n**7. Additional Critical Items**\n\n- WiFi access points (mounted or visible)\n- Phone system hardware (if present)\n- Any non-standard or legacy equipment\n\n⚠️ **IMPORTANT** Photos like “just the front of a rack” or “zoomed-out unclear shots” are NOT acceptable\n\n- Technician must verify that **all ports and connections are visible and readable**\n- **If something cannot be accessed or photographed, technician must note it in the survey**\n\nTechnical questions, call John Rubino: 949-257-9757-Email: john@rncinc.net\n\n**Location: Leasing office**\n\n**\\*\\*Technician must call Sarah (949-393-1740) before leaving site to review survey completeness, including photo quality and coverage.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T13:00","end":"2026-11-02T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":8.390290932682896},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $195 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","