{"job":{"id":"2432344068","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Service Ticket #7109502 - Cradlepoint Troubleshooting 10/30 3pm EST","description":"<p>Issue: latency issues with site's Granite Cradlepoint Serial MM244400003629</p><p>Shipped two new SIM's to test with, need to work with Granite/HCL to swap SIMs to VZ/TMO to try to improve signal. </p><p>New SIM's: </p><p> 8901882014741644046F</p><p>89033023931110000000093364538004</p><p>UPS Tracking: Pending</p><p><br></p><p>Join HCL Teams Bridge when onsite: Pending, will need to email to you directly. </p><p><br></p><p>If you are unable to resolve the issue on site or need further assistance with troubleshooting, Coordinate your efforts the Granite NOC at 844-492-2557 (Option 2).\"</p><p><br></p><p>NOTE: Must confirm Firewall connected and online with HCL 4083287792 before leaving via phone 4083287792 or email hcl-rbs-networkdata@hcltech.com</p><p><br></p><p>Required Equipment </p><p>A laptop: Windows 10 or higher with admin rights, ethernet ports gig capable of speeds over 1G, and charger to prove connectivity, a patch cord, a splitter, and a minimum of 3 filters. Cell phone, Cell phone charger, butt set and Minimum of 150’ of cable. Cat5e/or higher, and Coax. </p><p><br></p><p>Other Required Equipment: (mobile hot spot, usb 2.0 drive w/ 16gb storage, console cable two surface jacks etc)</p><p><br></p><p>NOC Call Back: 844-492-2557</p><p>Special Instructions: (Does this need a special tech fiber-certified/NCR/etc) </p><p><br></p><p>Configuration: </p><p>CP Serial #MM244400003834</p><p>Currently on AT&amp;T SIM </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work </p><p>Check in via WorkMarket. </p><p><br></p><p>Locate the Granite provided Cradlepoint. Record make, model, and serial number in the ticket. </p><p>Take a photo of the equipment and site as found. </p><p>Verify modem LEDs indicate normal operation. </p><p>Verify modem configuration matches the information provided in the ticket.</p><p><br></p><p>If modem configuration does not match the documented configuration and cannot be corrected onsite, contact the Granite NOC. </p><p>Inspect all inside wiring from DMARC to modem and replace as needed</p><p>Document all wiring repairs completed onsite </p><p>Connect directly to modem using test laptop</p><p>Verify IP assignment (DHCP or static as documented)</p><p>Confirm internet connectivity</p><p>Unplug customers equipment, and plug laptop directly to the modem/Router</p><p>While directly connected to the modem, perform three (3) speed tests.</p><p>Download speed</p><p>Upload speed</p><p>Latency </p><p>Ping-500 “ping –n 500 8.8.8.8” record </p><p>Packet loss percentage</p><p>Average latency</p><p>Maximum latency </p><p>If speed test results are less than 80% of the provisioned service speed relocate the modem to the DMARC, when technically feasible. Connect technician laptop directly to the modem. Repeat three (3) speed tests </p><p>Repeat Ping testing. Compare results between customer equipment location and DMARC location </p><p>If speeds improve at the DMARC, inside wiring is the likely cause. Recheck wiring components. Retest after repairs. </p><p>If speeds remain poor at the DMARC, issue is likely outside the customer premises. Proceed to Escalation Criteria. </p><p>Reconnect customer equipment </p><p><br></p><p>Confirm connectivity with LCON and MCON if required. See General Info</p><p><br></p><p>Document all findings and actions taken including customer-owned equipment issues discovered onsite </p><p><br></p><p>Identify Fault: </p><p>Customer Equipment </p><p>Customer LAN </p><p>Granite Managed Router </p><p>Carrier Circuit </p><p>Physical Layer/Cabling </p><p>No Trouble Found </p><p>Validate service restoration criteria </p><p>Upload pictures onto WorkMarket </p><p>Contact Granite NOC after all testing and isolation steps have been completed. Or escalation is needed. See Escalation criteria. If not connected to a live person within 15 minutes accept the call back request </p><p>Complete closeout and check out via WorkMarket</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00","end":"2026-10-30T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":75},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Oct 30, 3:00 PM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 30, Mon, Nov 2, Tue, Nov 3 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Granite GRID Lite router is offline. (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"202