{"job":{"id":20271190,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"AGC_7020_Sanford_NC - Amerigas - Access Point Refresh","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***YOU&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;CALL&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;TO&nbsp;CHECK&nbsp;IN&nbsp;UPON&nbsp;ARRIVAL&nbsp;–&nbsp;949-916-7545**&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>LOCAL&nbsp;CONTACT:&nbsp;</u></strong>Morgan&nbsp;Counter&nbsp;<del>**************</del></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;New&nbsp;Meraki&nbsp;CW9162I/Mounting&nbsp;hardware</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Network&nbsp;cable&nbsp;testing&nbsp;tools&nbsp;for&nbsp;unforeseen&nbsp;issues/hand&nbsp;tools&nbsp;for&nbsp;installation</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Ladder&nbsp;15'</p>\n<p><strong>SOW</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Check-in&nbsp;with&nbsp;CIS</strong></li>\n<li>Check&nbsp;in&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;designated&nbsp;site&nbsp;contact</li>\n<li>Check&nbsp;in&nbsp;with&nbsp;TCON&nbsp;-&nbsp;Brian&nbsp;Rich&nbsp;Amerigas&nbsp;Engineer:&nbsp;610-662-9071.&nbsp;If&nbsp;Brian&nbsp;Rich&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;available,&nbsp;please&nbsp;contact&nbsp;Chris&nbsp;Carlucci&nbsp;Amerigas&nbsp;Engineer&nbsp;610-768-7414.</li>\n<li>Verify&nbsp;work&nbsp;order&nbsp;details&nbsp;and&nbsp;confirm&nbsp;the&nbsp;areas&nbsp;where&nbsp;access&nbsp;points&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;replaced</li>\n<li>Verify&nbsp;serial&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;Meraki&nbsp;AP&nbsp;matches&nbsp;what&nbsp;is&nbsp;supposed&nbsp;to&nbsp;be&nbsp;installed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Access&nbsp;Point&nbsp;Replacement&nbsp;Procedure</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify&nbsp;the&nbsp;existing&nbsp;Cisco&nbsp;access&nbsp;point&nbsp;to&nbsp;be&nbsp;replaced.&nbsp;Some&nbsp;of&nbsp;these&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;on&nbsp;top&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;data&nbsp;cabinet&nbsp;or&nbsp;out&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;office&nbsp;mounted.&nbsp;Wherever&nbsp;the&nbsp;current&nbsp;AP&nbsp;is&nbsp;located,&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;AP&nbsp;will&nbsp;go&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;same&nbsp;location.</li>\n<li>Disconnect&nbsp;the&nbsp;ethernet&nbsp;cable&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;existing&nbsp;access&nbsp;point</li>\n<li>Remove&nbsp;the&nbsp;Cisco&nbsp;access&nbsp;point&nbsp;from&nbsp;its&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;bracket&nbsp;(if&nbsp;mounted)</li>\n<li>Uninstall&nbsp;the&nbsp;existing&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;bracket&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;wall/ceiling</li>\n<li>Install&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;Meraki-compatible&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;bracket&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;same&nbsp;location</li>\n<li>Attach&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;Meraki&nbsp;CW9162I&nbsp;access&nbsp;point&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;bracket</li>\n<li>Connect&nbsp;the&nbsp;ethernet&nbsp;cable&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;2.5Gbps&nbsp;Ethernet&nbsp;port&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;Meraki&nbsp;access&nbsp;point</li>\n<li>Link&nbsp;to&nbsp;Installation&nbsp;guide&nbsp;for&nbsp;any&nbsp;issues:</li>\n</ul>\n<p>https://documentation.meraki.com/MR/MR_Installation_Guides/CW9162_Installation_G<u>&nbsp;</u>uide</p>\n<p><strong><u>AP&nbsp;Light&nbsp;Status:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;<strong>Orange</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;is&nbsp;booting&nbsp;(permanent&nbsp;Orange&nbsp;suggests&nbsp;hardware&nbsp;issue)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;<strong>Rainbow</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;is&nbsp;initializing/scanning&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;<strong>Blinking&nbsp;Blue</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;is&nbsp;upgrading&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•<strong>&nbsp;Green</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;in&nbsp;Gateway&nbsp;mode&nbsp;with&nbsp;no&nbsp;clients&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;<strong>Blue</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;in&nbsp;Gateway&nbsp;mode&nbsp;with&nbsp;clients&nbsp;</p>\n<p>•<strong>&nbsp;Blinking&nbsp;Orange</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;AP&nbsp;can't&nbsp;find&nbsp;uplink</p>\n<p><strong>Verification&nbsp;Process</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify&nbsp;the&nbsp;access&nbsp;point&nbsp;is&nbsp;properly&nbsp;powered&nbsp;by&nbsp;confirming&nbsp;the&nbsp;LED&nbsp;indicator&nbsp;turns&nbsp;solid&nbsp;green</li>\n<li>Using&nbsp;a&nbsp;mobile&nbsp;device,&nbsp;verify&nbsp;that&nbsp;both&nbsp;\"AMG&nbsp;Secure\"&nbsp;and&nbsp;\"AMG&nbsp;Guest\"&nbsp;SSIDs&nbsp;are&nbsp;being&nbsp;properly&nbsp;advertised</li>\n<li>If&nbsp;available,&nbsp;ask&nbsp;customer&nbsp;to&nbsp;connect&nbsp;to&nbsp;wifi&nbsp;and&nbsp;verify&nbsp;service&nbsp;is&nbsp;working.</li>\n<li>Document&nbsp;the&nbsp;serial&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;newly&nbsp;installed&nbsp;access&nbsp;point</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deliverables&nbsp;and&nbsp;Check&nbsp;Out</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Take&nbsp;Pictures&nbsp;of&nbsp;all&nbsp;new&nbsp;APs&nbsp;showing&nbsp;the&nbsp;LED&nbsp;indicator&nbsp;is&nbsp;solid&nbsp;green</li>\n<li>Take&nbsp;Pictures&nbsp;confirming&nbsp;the&nbsp;AMG&nbsp;Secure&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;AMG&nbsp;Guise&nbsp;SSIDs&nbsp;are&nbsp;properly&nbsp;advertised</li>\n<li>Take&nbsp;pictures&nbsp;of&nbsp;old&nbsp;APs&nbsp;place&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;designated&nbsp;location&nbsp;or&nbsp;box&nbsp;per&nbsp;POC</li>\n<li>Notify&nbsp;the&nbsp;site&nbsp;contact&nbsp;that&nbsp;the&nbsp;replacement&nbsp;has&nbsp;been&nbsp;completed</li>\n<li>Give&nbsp;site&nbsp;contact&nbsp;old&nbsp;access&nbsp;point/mounting&nbsp;hardware&nbsp;–&nbsp;Amerigas&nbsp;IT&nbsp;will&nbsp;arrange&nbsp;disposal&nbsp;or&nbsp;pick&nbsp;up.</li>\n<li>Check&nbsp;out&nbsp;with&nbsp;site&nbsp;contact,</li>\n<li>Check&nbsp;out&nbsp;with&nbsp;TCON&nbsp;-&nbsp;Amerigas&nbsp;Engineering</li>\n<li>Check&nbsp;out&nbsp;with&nbsp;CIS</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Quality&nbsp;Assurance</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure&nbsp;all&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;hardware&nbsp;is&nbsp;secure</li>\n<li>Confirm&nbsp;the&nbsp;access&nbsp;point&nbsp;is&nbsp;level&nbsp;and&nbsp;aesthetically&nbsp;acceptable</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Materials</p>\n<p><strong>**Please&nbsp;have&nbsp;extras&nbsp;of&nbsp;all&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;below:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;cable&nbsp;(at&nbsp;least&nbsp;200’)</li>\n<li>Single&nbsp;Port&nbsp;Surface&nbsp;Mount&nbsp;Boxes</li>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;Keystone&nbsp;Jacks</li>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;Patch&nbsp;Cables&nbsp;(Varying&nbsp;Lengths)</li>\n<li>Zip&nbsp;Ties</li>\n<li>Velcro&nbsp;Strips&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tools</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Smart&nbsp;Phone</li>\n<li>12'&nbsp;A-Frame&nbsp;Ladder</li>\n<li>Assorted&nbsp;size&nbsp;Screw&nbsp;Drivers</li>\n<li>Cable&nbsp;Tester</li>\n<li>Toner</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>Label&nbsp;Maker</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;DELIVERABLES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>PHOTOS&nbsp;OF&nbsp;WORK&nbsp;DONE</li>\n<li>WORKMAN'S&nbsp;COMP&nbsp;WAIVER&nbsp;(ATTACHED)</li>\n<li>MANAGERS&nbsp;SIGN&nbsp;OFF&nbsp;(ATTACHED)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Before&nbsp;the&nbsp;tech&nbsp;leaves&nbsp;the&nbsp;site,&nbsp;they&nbsp;MUST&nbsp;call&nbsp;to&nbsp;check&nbsp;out&nbsp;with&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;PRO&nbsp;SERVICE&nbsp;TEAM&nbsp;prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;leaving&nbsp;site&nbsp;in&nbsp;order&nbsp;to&nbsp;close&nbsp;the&nbsp;work&nbsp;order&nbsp;out.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>***Please&nbsp;note&nbsp;if&nbsp;you&nbsp;do&nbsp;not&nbsp;call&nbsp;for&nbsp;check&nbsp;out&nbsp;we&nbsp;may&nbsp;need&nbsp;to&nbsp;deny&nbsp;payment***</p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*YOU MUST CALL CIS TO CHECK IN UPON ARRIVAL – 949-916-7545\\*\\***\n\n**LOCAL CONTACT:** Morgan Counter \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Prerequisites**\n\n• New Meraki CW9162I/Mounting hardware\n\n• Network cable testing tools for unforeseen issues/hand tools for installation\n\n• Ladder 15'\n\n**SOW**\n\n- **Check-in with CIS**\n- Check in with the designated site contact\n- Check in with TCON - Brian Rich Amerigas Engineer: 610-662-9071. If Brian Rich is not available, please contact Chris Carlucci Amerigas Engineer 610-768-7414.\n- Verify work order details and confirm the areas where access points will be replaced\n- Verify serial number of Meraki AP matches what is supposed to be installed.\n\n**Access Point Replacement Procedure**\n\n- Identify the existing Cisco access point to be replaced. Some of these may be on top of the data cabinet or out in the office mounted. Wherever the current AP is located, the new AP will go in the same location.\n- Disconnect the ethernet cable from the existing access point\n- Remove the Cisco access point from its mounting bracket (if mounted)\n- Uninstall the existing mounting bracket from the wall/ceiling\n- Install the new Meraki-compatible mounting bracket in the same location\n- Attach the new Meraki CW9162I access point to the mounting bracket\n- Connect the ethernet cable to the 2.5Gbps Ethernet port on the Meraki access point\n- Link to Installation guide for any issues:\n\nhttps://documentation.meraki.com/MR/MR_Installation_Guides/CW9162_Installation_G uide\n\n**AP Light Status:**\n\n• **Orange** - AP is booting (permanent Orange suggests hardware issue)\n\n• **Rainbow** - AP is initializing/scanning\n\n• **Blinking Blue** - AP is upgrading\n\n• **Green** - AP in Gateway mode with no clients\n\n• **Blue** - AP in Gateway mode with clients\n\n• **Blinking Orange** - AP can't find uplink\n\n**Verification Process**\n\n- Verify the access point is properly powered by confirming the LED indicator turns solid green\n- Using a mobile device, verify that both \"AMG Secure\" and \"AMG Guest\" SSIDs are being properly advertised\n- If available, ask customer to connect to wifi and verify service is working.\n- Document the serial number of the newly installed access point\n\n**Deliverables and Check Out**\n\n- Take Pictures of all new APs showing the LED indicator is solid green\n- Take Pictures confirming the AMG Secure &amp; AMG Guise SSIDs are properly advertised\n- Take pictures of old APs place in the designated location or box per POC\n- Notify the site contact that the replacement has been completed\n- Give site contact old access point/mounting hardware – Amerigas IT will arrange disposal or pick up.\n- Check out with site contact,\n- Check out with TCON - Amerigas Engineering\n- Check out with CIS\n\n**Quality Assurance**\n\n- Ensure all mounting hardware is secure\n- Confirm the access point is level and aesthetically acceptable\n\nMaterials\n\n**\\*\\*Please have extras of all of the below:**\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nTools\n\n- Smart Phone\n- 12' A-Frame Ladder\n- Assorted size Screw Drivers\n- Cable Tester\n- Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n\n **DELIVERABLES:**\n\n- PHOTOS OF WORK DONE\n- WORKMAN'S COMP WAIVER (ATTACHED)\n- MANAGERS SIGN OFF (ATTACHED)\n\nBefore the tech leaves the site, they MUST call to check out with CIS PRO SERVICE TEAM prior to leaving site in order to close the work order out.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Please note if you do not call for check out we may need to deny payment\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":37.25917418027826},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793300951483}
