{"job":{"id":20271802,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"DATA REMOTE PORT/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/ MULTIMETER-DIS154833","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 732-837-9583 Ticket 11373870<br/><br/>***MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/><br/>PIAB installed. 200ft extension from Velo complete and WAN connection established on PIAB. T&L for TN 9198287983 was completed. Tech will need to revisit to port and cutover the line.<br/> <br/>\t· Required: Tech Must have POTS experience, BUTT SET, Toner/Wand<br/>\t· Technician to R&S PIAB equipment at location identified during survey<br/>\t· Prep cross connects for lines identified during survey<br/>\t· Tech to proceed with go-live/transition of services.<br/>\t· Test all services post port with MetTel remote support member <br/><br/>LCON Name:\tThel Vinson<br/>LCON Email:\tthelbert.vinson@gsa.gov<br/>LCON Phone Number:\t(919) 996-0598<br/><br/>Velo onsite: 9CTVV43 - Install TKT 8057764<br/><br/>Total 1 line:<br/>9198287983\tPorting\tMailroom <br/> <br/>Vendor to Ensure and confirm the technician is experienced in:<br/>\t· Cross-connecting lines at a Telco Block<br/>\t· Using a butt set to test for dial tone and identify lines <br/>\t· Toning lines back to the Demarc / MPOE<br/>Checklist:<br/>\t· Valid government-issued ID<br/>\t· Functional butt set<br/>\t· Punch-down tool with 66 and 110 blades<br/>\t· Toner and probe (wand)<br/><br/>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/>This order requires tech to have State Issued Enhanced Driver's License or Enhanced ID or must carry one of the following:<br/>•U.S. passport<br/>•U.S. passport card<br/>•DHS trusted traveler cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)<br/>•U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents<br/>•Permanent resident card<br/>•Border crossing card<br/>•An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe, including Enhanced Tribal Cards (ETCs).<br/>•HSPD-12 PIV card<br/>•Foreign government-issued passport<br/>•Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card<br/>•Transportation worker identification credential<br/>•U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)<br/>•U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential<br/>•Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)<br/><br/>Please call Call Corp upon arrival: 844-905-9779 when you arrive on site. Provide the Mettel Ticket site number 11373870 to SD Rep.<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 732-837-9583 Ticket 11373870  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n  \nPIAB installed. 200ft extension from Velo complete and WAN connection established on PIAB. T&amp;L for TN 9198287983 was completed. Tech will need to revisit to port and cutover the line.  \n   \n · Required: Tech Must have POTS experience, BUTT SET, Toner/Wand  \n · Technician to R&amp;S PIAB equipment at location identified during survey  \n · Prep cross connects for lines identified during survey  \n · Tech to proceed with go-live/transition of services.  \n · Test all services post port with MetTel remote support member   \n  \nLCON Name: Thel Vinson  \nLCON Email: thelbert.vinson@gsa.gov  \nLCON Phone Number: (919) 996-0598  \n  \nVelo onsite: 9CTVV43 - Install TKT 8057764  \n  \nTotal 1 line:  \n9198287983 Porting Mailroom   \n   \nVendor to Ensure and confirm the technician is experienced in:  \n · Cross-connecting lines at a Telco Block  \n · Using a butt set to test for dial tone and identify lines   \n · Toning lines back to the Demarc / MPOE  \nChecklist:  \n · Valid government-issued ID  \n · Functional butt set  \n · Punch-down tool with 66 and 110 blades  \n · Toner and probe (wand)  \n  \nMetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \nThis order requires tech to have State Issued Enhanced Driver's License or Enhanced ID or must carry one of the following:  \n•U.S. passport  \n•U.S. passport card  \n•DHS trusted traveler cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)  \n•U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents  \n•Permanent resident card  \n•Border crossing card  \n•An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe, including Enhanced Tribal Cards (ETCs).  \n•HSPD-12 PIV card  \n•Foreign government-issued passport  \n•Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card  \n•Transportation worker identification credential  \n•U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)  \n•U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential  \n•Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)  \n  \nPlease call Call Corp upon arrival: 844-905-9779 when you arrive on site. Provide the Mettel Ticket site number 11373870 to SD Rep.  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T11:00","end":"2026-11-10T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.391704334523693},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Rale