{"job":{"id":"2751660624","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Airitpros.","title":"Install &amp; Run Cable for IDF - Fayetteville, NC","description":"<p>Note: Because of COVID 19- You may be required to wear a mask, gloves, observe social distancing rules etc at customer site.</p><p><br></p><p><u>Scope of Work:</u></p><p><strong>- Provide and Install (1) run of Category 6 cable from the Existing IDF to the ADI Camera Panel – Patch cable to the unmanaged switch.</strong></p><p><strong>- Provide and Install (1) run of Category 6 cable from the Existing IDF to the Sort Panel – Patch cable to the unmanaged switch.</strong></p><p><strong>- Provide and Install (1) run of Category 6 cable from the Existing IDF to the Color Sort Panel – Patch cable to the unmanaged switch..</strong></p><p><strong>- Provide and Install (1) 1' EMT Conduit for the Control Panels.</strong></p><p><strong>- Install (2) 12 Port HPE Switches, one each in MDF &amp; IDF.</strong></p><p><strong>- Provide and install (7) 10 ft Patch cables in the MDF/IT room.</strong></p><p><strong>- Black box will provide the materials and lift to site.</strong></p><p><strong>The technician must have a Fluke tester (or equivalent) onsite and be able to provide test results for all installed cabling that has been certified. We'll need that documentation for validation and project closeout.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dress Code Requirement</p><p>An engineer must have business casual dress and comply with local site requirements which AirIt Pro will provide in advance.</p><p>Allowed : Jeans, Collared T-Shirts, Formal Pant, Formal Shirt</p><p>Not allowed : Round neck/ V-neck /sweatshirt/beach dress, 3/4th pant, Hat, Cap, Shorts, unclean shoes and any unclean dress.</p><p>Dispatch Technician must carry Laptop &amp; Charger, fully charged Mobile and other required equipment</p><p>Dispatch Technician must be fluent in English (Read, Write and Speak)</p><p><br></p><p>NO sunglasses, listening to music with 