{"job":{"id":20272875,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Patriot Global Services","title":"CLINTON_NC_USCC | SMARTHANDS WO 3428 | ESCORT | 11/02/26","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>Escort Service Logic on site to complete the HVAC Repairs.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please see attached Smart Hands Request Form all the details.</p>\n<p><strong>Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>Please connect with below once onsite.</p>\n<p><del>**** *</del></p>\n<p><del>**** ***** * *</del></p>\n<p>The tech will just need to provide site access and escort the vendor who will be performing the actual work.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Ascent Vendor Process – USCC IT Smart Hands Support Services Vendor Dispatch</p>\n<p>1. AOC to contact vendor escalation list by email and phone when client submits a ticket.</p>\n<p>2. Vendor dispatch/technician to reply to AOC with technician information and ETA to the site. a. Please update lines 29-33 on the attached client Request Form and email back to the AOC. Arriving Onsite</p>\n<p>3. Once arriving onsite, the vendor technician is to contact the<del>*** **************</del> to check-in, receive the USCC on-call information to gain site access and to provide updates.</p>\n<p>4. After contacting the AOC, the vendor technician will contact USCC’s NOC by text or email at <del>******************</del><del>**** *** ********* *********** ******** ** ****** ** ********* ** ***** ** **** ** **** ** *********** ******* ***** ***** ******* ****** *** ***** ******* **** ** ********* *** ******* ***** ******** ************* ***** ************* ********* * *** **** **** ***** *********</del></p>\n<p>5. The vendor technician will then need to call the USCC on-call to request access to the site.</p>\n<p>a. The USCC individual will work with the vendor technician to verify identity and remotely open the exterior gate(s) and/or door(s).</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>b. <del>*** ******* *** **********</del>, the sites have 24/7 security that will grant access to the site and provide the vendor technician with a site access card.</p>\n<p>6. Once in the site, the vendor technician will need to access the lockbox which contains the site access card(s) and/or key(s). a. <del>*** **** *** *** ******* ** *****</del>.</p>\n<p>7. If additional work is requested that was not listed on the request form, please pause work immediately and call the Ascent Operations Center (AOC) for direction on how to proceed. The AOC will reach out for further direction from USCC personnel.</p>\n<p>8. Information Specific to Escort Requests: a. While onsite, the vendor technician will not touch any critical equipment. b. While the escorting vendor technician is onsite, they will act as the lead personnel and have the authority to act in the best interest of the site to ensure the safety and security of the site and people within. Completion of Work</p>\n<p>9. Upon successful completion of the request, please ensure that the access card is returned to the lockbox, the lights are turned off and all doors and gates are secured.</p>\n<p>10. Upon completing all requested work for the client, the vendor technician will follow the directions on the sign-in reply from Step 4 to sign out with USCC.</p>\n<p>11. The vendor technician will then call out to the <del>*** **************</del>to close out the WO.</p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nEscort Service Logic on site to complete the HVAC Repairs.\n\nPlease see attached Smart Hands Request Form all the details.\n\n**Instructions:**\n\nPlease connect with below once onsite.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\n\nThe tech will just need to provide site access and escort the vendor who will be performing the actual work.\n\nAscent Vendor Process – USCC IT Smart Hands Support Services Vendor Dispatch\n\n1\\. AOC to contact vendor escalation list by email and phone when client submits a ticket.\n\n2\\. Vendor dispatch/technician to reply to AOC with technician information and ETA to the site. a. Please update lines 29-33 on the attached client Request Form and email back to the AOC. Arriving Onsite\n\n3\\. Once arriving onsite, the vendor technician is to contact the\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check-in, receive the USCC on-call information to gain site access and to provide updates.\n\n4\\. After contacting the AOC, the vendor technician will contact USCC’s NOC by text or email at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n5\\. The vendor technician will then need to call the USCC on-call to request access to the site.\n\na. The USCC individual will work with the vendor technician to verify identity and remotely open the exterior gate(s) and/or door(s).\n\nb. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, the sites have 24/7 security that will grant access to the site and provide the vendor technician with a site access card.\n\n6\\. Once in the site, the vendor technician will need to access the lockbox which contains the site access card(s) and/or key(s). a. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*.\n\n7\\. If additional work is requested that was not listed on the request form, please