{"job":{"id":20251675,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Install Workstations | 11/2 | Tech 1","description":{"html":"<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Required On-site time/window: 11/02 8AM</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Equipment:</p>\n<p>Make/Model: PALOALTO</p>\n<p>Serial Number: {SRM_FN.SERIAL}</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Problem Description: Please see below request from United Therapeutics for the Warp 10 location in the first week of November.</p>\n<p>For the scope of work, it will be very similar to the work done in Houston, such as physically taking the workstation equipment (i.e., monitor, keyboard, mouse, headset, etc.) out of the boxes they were delivered in, and setting them up on the tables, making sure they are plugged in, tested, and working.</p>\n<p>The quantity at this location is 73 desk setups.</p>\n<p>Is the work expected to take place only from 11/02 through 11/06? Yes, the team is ready for the technicians starting next Monday, 11/2. The equipment is currently being held in an easy spot on the first floor office.</p>\n<p>Are all workstations located in the same building? If so, what floor will the installations be on? Yes, all of the equipment is in the same building. Floors 1 and 2</p>\n<p>Onsite contact’s phone number: Ted Kerr (tedk@dpr.com). 804-298-5340</p>\n<p><strong>NOTE: &nbsp;</strong>“the workstations should be set up wirelessly and do not require Ethernet connections. The only cabling needed is standard power for the monitor. The keyboard packaging will also include a USBa receiver, which should be plugged into the left side of the monitor.” - Jake White | Senior Consultant, IT Strategic Planning and Operations | United Therapeutics</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Important Scope/Customer Information:</p>\n<p>Any changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone.</p>\n<p>If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If additional parts are needed there will be another trip&nbsp;REQUIRED.&nbsp;You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.</p>\n<p>If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Required Tools:</p>\n<p>Standard hand tools</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Upon Arrival at site:</p>\n<p>Introduce yourself as ePlus technician</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:</p>\n<p>Confirm functionality with remote support &amp; provide their name upon closure</p>\n<p>Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out</p>\n<p>Provide Return Tracking for all used/not used returns</p>","markdown":"IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.\n\nYOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.\n\nRequired On-site time/window: 11/02 8AM\n\nEquipment:\n\nMake/Model: PALOALTO\n\nSerial Number: {SRM\\_FN.SERIAL}\n\nProblem Description: Please see below request from United Therapeutics for the Warp 10 location in th