{"job":{"id":"1097600699","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Reconfigure TP Button printer","description":"# SCOPE OF WORK<br>- Reconfigure a TP Button printer at the site.<br>- Use a laptop and network cable along with required tools to complete the reconfiguration.<br>- Ensure the printer is operating correctly.<br><br># REQUIRED MATERIALS<br>- Laptop<br>- Network cable<br>- Cable tester<br>- T10 Torx<br>- Basic tools including:<br>  - Screwdriver<br>  - Cable stripping tool<br>  - Cable cutter<br>  - Cable crimper for RJ45 and RJ11<br><br># ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS<br>1. Refer to specific installer manuals for the job being performed prior to reaching out to Qmatic Support.<br>2. Upon arrival, call Qmatic Support for assistance and request an on-site code.<br>3. Communicate with the onsite contact regarding equipment location.<br>4. Take and send in pictures along with the completed sign-off sheet to Qmatic Support.<br>5. Before leaving the site:<br>   - Reply to the email received from Qmatic Support with the completed sign-off (excluding the release code field).<br>   - Include pictures of the home run area, counters, and displays.<br>6. After sending the email, call Qmatic Support to receive a release code.<br>7. Turn in the fully completed sign-off and pictures with the invoice to receive payment.<br>8. If hardware must be returned:<br>   - Obtain the RMA label from the client.<br>   - Ship the equipment back in the provided box via UPS counter.<br>   - Submit a clear picture of the drop-off receipt with the invoice.<br><br>NOTES<br>=====<br>Parts do not need to be returned. If hardware must be returned, obtain an RMA label from the client, ship the equipment back in the provided box via UPS counter, and submit a clear picture of the dropoff receipt with the invoice.<br><br>Qmatic service calls are for troubleshooting, repairing, and/or testing Qmatic equipment. Qmatic provides Customer Flow Management solutions via Kiosk, speakers, 