{"job":{"id":20273979,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Restore Offline IDF3 Switch Stack –Wilson, NC | 00263387 / SA-295083 / 05313387","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p>\n<p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: <strong>Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong> to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li>\n<li>Note: <strong>Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong> explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li>\n<li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to<strong>specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong> and its reason.</li>\n<li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong>the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li>\n<li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Title:</strong> Technician Needed with Tools to Restore Offline IDF3 Switch Stack – Wilson, NC | TBD / SA-295083 / 05313387</p>\n<p><strong>Type of Work:</strong> Networking</p>\n<p><strong>Schedule:</strong> October 30, 2026 – 10:00 AM EDT</p>\n<p><strong>Site Name &amp; Address:</strong> Home2 Suites by Hilton Wilson Downtown, 409 Goldsboro Street South, Wilson, NC 27893, United States</p>\n<p><strong>WO / SA / Case:</strong> 00263387 / SA-295083 / 05313387</p>\n<p><strong>Contact Details:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site POC:</strong> Harrison Bryant, TBD</p>\n<p><strong>Engineer:</strong> Technet | TECHNET</p>\n<p><strong>Technician:</strong> TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Travel onsite and check the IDF3 network room.</li>\n<li>Locate switch stack asset<strong>HLT-RWIWN-9300-IDF3-DS03-1</strong>.</li>\n<li>Assess the Cisco Meraki C9300-48U-M switch stack that is currently offline.</li>\n<li>Verify power status, link lights, alarms, and physical condition of all stack members.</li>\n<li>Verify uplink connectivity between IDF3 switch stack and parent switch <strong>HLT-RWIWN-9300-MDF-CS01</strong>.</li>\n<li>Inspect and reseat the uplink connection on SFP+ Port 3 as directed by the remote engineer.</li>\n<li>Check patching, cabling, transceivers, and physical connections for faults or damage.</li>\n<li>Perform troubleshooting steps as directed by the remote engineer.</li>\n<li>Restore network connectivity and confirm the switch stack is online.</li>\n<li>Validate uplink status and network service restoration with the remote engineer.</li>\n<li>Take photos of the equipment, cabling, switch status LEDs, and completed work.</li>\n<li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Asset &amp; Location:</strong> HLT-RWIWN-9300-IDF3-DS03-1 (Cisco Meraki C9300-48U-M) – IDF3</p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</li>\n<li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet cable</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li>\n<li>Cellphone with camera</li>\n<li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit ethernet connections)</li>\n<li>Tone generator</li>\n<li>Console cable and USB adapter</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)</li>\n<li>Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)</li>\n<li>Voltage tester</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li>\n<li>Spare SFP/SFP+ transceivers</li>\n<li>Fiber cleaning kit</li>\n<li>Flashlight</li>\n<li>Network patch cables (Cat5e/Cat6)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to**specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\n**Title:** Technician Needed with Tools to Restore Offline IDF3 Switch Stack – Wilson, NC | TBD / SA-295083 / 05313387\n\n**Type of Work:** Networking\n\n**Schedule:** October 30, 2026 – 10:00 AM EDT\n\n**Site Name &amp; Address:** Home2 Suites by Hilton Wilson Downtown, 409 Goldsboro Street South, Wilson, NC 27893, United States\n\n**WO / SA / Case:** 00263387 / SA-295083 / 05313387\n\n**Contact Details:**\n\n**Site POC:** Harrison Bryant, TBD\n\n**Engineer:** Technet | TECHNET\n\n**Technician:** TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Travel onsite and check the IDF3 network room.\n- Locate switch stack asset**HLT-RWIWN-9300-IDF3-DS03-1**.\n- Assess the Cisco Meraki C9300-48U-M switch stack that is currently offline.\n- Verify power status, link lights, alarms, and physical condition of all stack members.\n- Verify uplink connectivity between IDF3 switch stack and parent switch **HLT-RWIWN-9300-MDF-CS01**.\n- Inspect and reseat the uplink connection on SFP+ Port 3 as directed by the remote engineer.\n- Check patching, cabling, transceivers, and physical connections for faults or damage.\n- Perform troubleshooting steps as directed by the remote engineer.\n- Restore network connectivity and confirm the switch stack is online.\n- Validate uplink status and network service restoration with the remote engineer.\n- Take photos of the equipment, cabling, switch status LEDs, and completed work.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset &amp; Location:** HLT-RWIWN-9300-IDF3-DS03-1 (Cisco Meraki C9300-48U-M) – IDF3\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- Spare SFP/SFP+ transceivers\n- Fiber cleaning kit\n- Flashlight\n- Network patch cables (Cat5e/Cat6)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T10:00","end":"2026-10-30T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":47.75647828225763},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Oct 30, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 30, Mon, Nov 2, Tue, Nov 3 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T16:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 171910 - BK-10775 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00