{"job":{"id":20274853,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Patriot Global Services","title":"Tech needed for CISCO Screen replacement. Tech-1","description":{"html":"<p>Scope:</p><ol><li>The tech is required to assist the IBM tech onsite with the deinstallation of the old Cisco TV and the installation of the new Cisco TV, as well as any additional hardware installations if required.</li><li>The tech is required to assist with site preparation activities, including decabling, unmounting and remounting equipment, installation, staging, and rack-and-stack tasks.</li><li>The tech will also assist with unmounting and mounting the devices.</li><li>Assist the IBM Engineer with the physical deinstallation and installation activities within the Cisco chassis. Support the removal of existing hardware components and the installation of replacement hardware, including the supervisor module, battery module, fan assemblies, and associated rack-mounted equipment.</li><li>Provide hands-on assistance during the rack-and-stack process, including mounting hardware, securing components, and using power tools as required for installation. Additionally, assist the IBM Engineer with testing, validation, and troubleshooting activities to ensure the successful completion of the work.</li></ol><p><strong>FIELD ENGINEER TOOL REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p><strong>Patriot FE is required to carry all tools required to perform the job, included but not limited to:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a mobile phone</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a pair of clean gloves</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a set of Hex wrenches including 2.5mm, 3mm, 4mm, and 5mm sizes.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a levelling tool</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a set of both flathead and Phillips screwdrivers.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A ladder</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;anti-static kit</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;laptop</p><p><strong>GENERAL EXPECTATIONS WHEN WORKING A CISCO TASK:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;At any time during the task, if the Field Engineer (FE) requires assistance, or if there is any reason the task cannot commence or must be stopped, the FE must immediately inform the IBM FE and leave annotations in the feed. All these events must be documented in a timely manner.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The FE is required to remain with the IBM FE at all times throughout the task.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Under no circumstances should the FE perform any technical troubleshooting, even if requested by the end user.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>","markdown":"Scope:\n\n1. The tech is required to assist the IBM tech onsite with the deinstallation of the old Cisco TV and the installation of the new Cisco TV, as well as any additional hardware installations if required.\n2. The tech is required to assist with site preparation activities, including decabling, unmounting and remounting equipment, installation, staging, and rack-and-stack tasks.\n3. The tech will also assist with unmounting and mounting the devices.\n4. Assist the IBM Engineer with the physical deinstallation and installation activities within the Cisco chassis. Support the removal of existing hardware components and the installation of replacement hardware, including the supervisor module, battery module, fan assemblies, and associated rack-mounted equipment.\n5. Provide hands-on assistance during the rack-and-stack process, including mounting hardware, securing components, and using power tools as required for installation. Additionally, assist the IBM Engineer with testing, validation, and troubleshooting activities to ensure the successful completion of the work.\n\n**FIELD ENGINEER TOOL REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Patriot FE is required to carry all tools required to perform the job, included but not limited to:**\n\n· a mobile phone\n\n· a pair of clean gloves\n\n· a set of Hex wrenches including 2.5mm, 3mm, 4mm, and 5mm sizes.\n\n· a levelling tool\n\n· a set of both flathead and Phillips screwdrivers.\n\n· A ladder\n\n· anti-static kit\n\n· laptop\n\n**GENERAL EXPECTATIONS WHEN WORKING A CISCO TASK:**\n\n· At any time during the task, if the Field Engineer (FE) requires assistance, or if there is any reason the task cannot commence or must be stopped, the FE must immediately inform the IBM FE and leave annotations in the feed. All these events must be documented in a timely manner.\n\n· The FE is required to remain with the IBM FE at all times throughout the task.\n\n· Under no circumstances should the FE perform any technical troubleshooting, even if requested by the end user.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T12:00","end":"2026-11-02T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7.609322664205899},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 