{"job":{"id":20276233,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"NCR POS Base Unit Swap- Register 1","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:</u></strong></p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE</p><p>The site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.</p><p>Technician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.</p><p>Technician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.</p><p>Technician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.</p><p>Technician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.</p><p>Technician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.</p><p>Technician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.</p><p>Technician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.</p><p>Technician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.</p><p>Technician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.</p><p>Technician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.</p><p>After the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.</p><p>After signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the</p><p>next message box should request the register number.</p><p>After entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.</p><p>Technician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.</p><p>**If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!**</p><p>Technician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.</p><p>Technician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.</p><p>Technician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"><del>** ** *** **** **** ** *********** *** ******** ****** *** ***** *** ************ ** * ****** **********</del></span></p><p><strong> **If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.</strong></p><p><strong> If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!**</strong></p><p><strong> **If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately**</strong></p><p>​</p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Required to be paid</u></strong></p><ol><li>Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.</li><li>Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)</li><li>Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done&nbsp;<u>before</u>&nbsp;any work is done.</li><li>Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.</li><li>Technician&nbsp;must take pictures of any equipment worked on&nbsp;<u>after</u>&nbsp;the work is done.</li><li>Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. <strong><u>TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> ** Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Requirements:</u></strong></p><ol><li>​Technician must be familiar with data cabling</li><li>Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable</li><li>Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Part Requirements:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><em><u>IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.</u></em></p><p>Up to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors,&nbsp;Ethernet cables,&nbsp;Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable</p><p><em><u>**POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot**</u></em></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\n**INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE>\n\nThe site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.\n\nTechnician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.\n\nTechnician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.\n\nTechnician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.\n\nTechnician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.\n\nTechnician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.\n\nTechnician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.\n\nTechnician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.\n\nTechnician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.\n\nTechnician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.\n\nTechnician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.\n\nAfter the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.\n\nAfter signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the\n\nnext message box should request the register number.\n\nAfter entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.\n\nTechnician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.\n\n\\*\\*If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!\\*\\*\n\nTechnician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.\n\nTechnician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.\n\nTechnician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **\\*\\*If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.**\n\n **If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!\\*\\***\n\n **\\*\\*If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately\\*\\***\n\n​\n\n**Deliverables Required to be paid**\n\n1. Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.\n2. Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)\n3. Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.\n4. Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.\n5. Technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.\n6. Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. **TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS**\n\n **\\*\\* Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay\\*\\***\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n1. ​Technician must be familiar with data cabling\n2. Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable\n3. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment\n\n**Part Requirements:**\n\n*IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.*\n\nUp to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors, Ethernet cables, Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable\n\n*\\*\\*POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot\\*\\**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T12:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":77.31114451573221},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793370942286}
{"job":{"id":20276243,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Install Workstations | 11/3 | Tech 4","description":{"html":"<p class=\"cs95E872D0\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES. </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Required On-site time/window: 11/3 8AM</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Equipment:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Make/Model: PALOALTO</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Serial Number: {SRM_FN.SERIAL}</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Problem Description:</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Please see below request from United Therapeutics for the Warp 10 location in the first week of November. For the scope of work, it will be very similar to the work done in Houston, such as physically taking the workstation equipment (i.e., monitor, keyboard, mouse, headset, etc.) out of the boxes they were delivered in, and setting them up on the tables, making sure they are plugged in, tested, and working. The quantity at this location is 73 desk setups. The primary contact at this location is Ted Kerr (tedk@dpr.com). He is OOO until Wednesday, but he can provide more specifics on who will be the on-site contact.</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Important Scope/Customer Information:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Any changes to ETA&rsquo;s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone. </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.&nbsp; </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If additional parts are needed there will be another trip&nbsp;REQUIRED.&nbsp;You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.&nbsp; </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Required Tools:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Standard hand tools</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Upon Arrival at site:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Introduce yourself as ePlus technician</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Confirm functionality with remote support &amp; provide their name upon closure</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Call Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Provide Return Tracking for all used/not used returns</span></p>","markdown":"IMPORTANT: Please use your Field Nation App to update your work order real time &amp; only call Essintial for additional expenses, return labels or to have another work order opened for another trip to site.\n\nYOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.\n\nRequired On-site time/window: 11/3 8AM\n\nEquipment:\n\nMake/Model: PALOALTO\n\nSerial Number: {SRM\\_FN.SERIAL}\n\nProblem Description:\n\nPlease see below request from United Therapeutics for the Warp 10 location in the first week of November. For the scope of work, it will be very similar to the work done in Houston, such as physically taking the workstation equipment (i.e., monitor, keyboard, mouse, headset, etc.) out of the boxes they were delivered in, and setting them up on the tables, making sure they are plugged in, tested, and working. The quantity at this location is 73 desk setups. The primary contact at this location is Ted Kerr (tedk@dpr.com). He is OOO until Wednesday, but he can provide more specifics on who will be the on-site contact.\n\nImportant Scope/Customer Information:\n\nAny changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone.\n\nIf you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.\n\nIf additional parts are needed there will be another trip REQUIRED. You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.\n\nAll times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.\n\nIf additional pay/expenses are required - please refer to Policies &amp; Procedures #6.\n\nRequired Tools:\n\nStandard hand tools\n\nUpon Arrival at site:\n\nIntroduce yourself as ePlus technician\n\nUpon Completion/Closeout Requirements:\n\nConfirm functionality with remote support &amp; provide their name upon closure\n\nCall Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to check-out\n\nProvide Return Tracking for all used/not used returns","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T08:00","end":"2026-11-03T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":320},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":7.6837571634185355},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793370975556}
{"job":{"id":"7183623632","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"\"9193613121 not sure<br>9193613122 not sure<br>9193613123 elevator<br>9193613126 elevator<br>9193613127 elevator<br>9193613128 utility room\"\"<br>\"\"\"SOW - EPIK Single Visit Install<br>*************************************************************************************<br>Before Arrival<br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival.<br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK:<br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo<br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below.<br>On Arrival<br>1.Check in on WorkMarket.<br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location.<br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work.<br>EPIK Install Requirements<br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik.<br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location. <br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard.<br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on.<br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions.<br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard:<br>https://wizard.epik.io<br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned.<br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES<br>7.If not already stated in the TNs to be wired section of your ticket, confirm with site contact if there are fire alarm, security alarm, elevator or e911 lines on site. If so, notify activations of any port configuration changes that need to be made and complete testing with the fire, security or elevator monitoring companies.<br>8.For any lines that cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number.<br>9.If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready.<br>Checkout Requirement<br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line.<br>2.Confirm Activations has released you.<br>3.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables.<br>4.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket.<br>5.Check out on WorkMarket.<br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket.<br><br>Required Deliverables<br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout:<br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install.<br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block.<br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable.<br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet.<br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions.<br><br><br>Required Tools<br>•Laptop<br>•Smartphone with hotspot<br>•Tone generator and wand<br>•66/110 punch tool<br>•Butt set<br>•       Infrared Temperature Gun <br>•Electrician scissors<br>•Step ladder<br>•Flashlight/headlamp<br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper<br>•Ethernet cable tester<br>•Impact drill / cordless drill<br>•Masonry bits<br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits<br>•Needle-nose pliers<br>•Label maker and label tape<br>•Cat3 or better cable<br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable<br>•Cross-connect wire<br>•Gel-crimp connectors<br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware<br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks<br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini<br>*********************************