{"job":{"id":20276714,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #233550 - Music Issues","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">TICKET SUMMARY:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER &amp; CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT &amp; RACK OPTIMIZATION</span></p><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">A technician is required on-site to install a new </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> and a </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">CSR-V Volume Control</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\"> wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack to ensure long-term serviceability.</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATORY RULE:</strong> The technician must test all speaker line impedance ($\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect every speaker transformer tap to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.</li><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:</strong> Upon successful installation, box up the legacy hardware and stage it in a designated \"out of the way\" area on-site for local site disposal. Do not remove old equipment from the property.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for audio interface checks and local network verification)</li><li><strong>6–8ft Ladder &amp; Pull Rods / Fish Tape</strong> (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line)</li><li><strong>Multimeter &amp; Cable Tester / Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for speaker line impedance, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)</li><li><strong>Cat5e/6 &amp; 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:</strong> RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill &amp; Bits</strong> (Including mounting hardware for rack installation)</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong> (preferred) or zip ties, <strong>Label Maker</strong>, and packaging tape</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack and the volume control location. Collect the newly shipped JBL hardware box.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the SOW with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 2: CABLE PULL &amp; MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT</strong><ol><li><strong>CAT6 HOME RUN:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the <strong>T568B Standard</strong> and test continuity with your cable tester.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER WIRE TESTING:</strong> Power off the existing amplifier. Use your <strong>multimeter</strong> to measure and log resistance ($\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.</li><li><strong>TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:</strong> Access every 70V speaker in the facility using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load <strong>does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating</strong>.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT HOLD:</strong> Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). <strong>DO NOT</strong> power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION &amp; RACK OVERHAUL</strong><ol><li><strong>HARDWARE MOUNTING:</strong> Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new <strong>JBL CSA140Z</strong> amplifier in the rack frame and mount the <strong>CSR-V</strong> volume control on the wall.</li><li><strong>RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:</strong> Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.</li><li><strong>LABELING:</strong> Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 <strong>\"Volume Control\"</strong> and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier input block.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING &amp; VERIFICATION</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER ON:</strong> Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.</li><li><strong>AUDIO AUDIT:</strong> Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback and responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL &amp; CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:</strong> Box up the old hardware, mark it clearly as <strong>\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and stage it in the store's designated storage area. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drill dust, and packaging waste. Ensure the rack closet and volume control areas are left spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Amp &amp; Managed Rack:</strong> Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (<strong>Full view, cabinet door OPEN</strong>).</li><li>[ ] <strong>New CSR-V Installed:</strong> Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Readings:</strong> Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance measurements taken on the speaker lines.</li><li>[ ] <strong>T568B Termination Close-up:</strong> Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Hardware:</strong> Photo showing the old equipment boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support that audio telemetry and volume control performance are 100% operational.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>MOD:</strong> Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings, tap settings verified, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n**TICKET SUMMARY:** JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER &amp; CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL INSTALLATION, SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT &amp; RACK OPTIMIZATION\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A technician is required on-site to install a new **JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier** and a **CSR-V Volume Control** wall plate, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack to ensure long-term serviceability.\n\n- **VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.\n- **SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT MANDATORY RULE:** The technician must test all speaker line impedance ($\\\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect every speaker transformer tap to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.\n- **DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:** Upon successful installation, box up the legacy hardware and stage it in a designated \"out of the way\" area on-site for local site disposal. Do not remove old equipment from the property.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for audio interface checks and local network verification)\n- **6–8ft Ladder &amp; Pull Rods / Fish Tape** (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line)\n- **Multimeter &amp; Cable Tester / Toner** (**Mandatory** for speaker line impedance, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)\n- **Cat5e/6 &amp; 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:** RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill &amp; Bits** (Including mounting hardware for rack installation)\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties** (preferred) or zip ties, **Label Maker**, and packaging tape\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack and the volume control location. Collect the newly shipped JBL hardware box.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the SOW with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: CABLE PULL &amp; MANDATORY SPEAKER CIRCUIT AUDIT**1. **CAT6 HOME RUN:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the **T568B Standard** and test continuity with your cable tester.\n2. **SPEAKER WIRE TESTING:** Power off the existing amplifier. Use your **multimeter** to measure and log resistance ($\\\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.\n3. **TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:** Access every 70V speaker in the facility using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load **does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating**.\n4. **SUPPORT HOLD:** Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). **DO NOT** power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.\n\n**PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION &amp; RACK OVERHAUL**1. **HARDWARE MOUNTING:** Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new **JBL CSA140Z** amplifier in the rack frame and mount the **CSR-V** volume control on the wall.\n2. **RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:** Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using **Velcro ties**. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.\n3. **LABELING:** Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 **\"Volume Control\"** and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier input block.\n\n**PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING &amp; VERIFICATION**1. **POWER ON:** Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.\n2. **AUDIO AUDIT:** Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback and responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.\n\n**PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL &amp; CLEANUP**1. **STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:** Box up the old hardware, mark it clearly as **\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and stage it in the store's designated storage area. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drill dust, and packaging waste. Ensure the rack closet and volume control areas are left spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Amp &amp; Managed Rack:** Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (**Full view, cabinet door OPEN**).\n- \\[ \\] **New CSR-V Installed:** Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.\n- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Readings:** Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance measurements taken on the speaker lines.\n- \\[ \\] **T568B Termination Close-up:** Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Hardware:** Photo showing the old equipment boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and volume control wall area are swept clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support that audio telemetry and volume control performance are 100% operational.\n\n- **MOD:** Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings, tap settings verified, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T08:00","end":"2026-11-04T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":210},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":37.067258610385686},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Lower School (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793373847609}
{"job":{"id":20277033,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240F Duplex Printer - Error Code Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240F xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>CX3240F<br />FIN: 303022<br />Getting Fault Code related to the Maintenance Belt not reading or installed correctly<br /><br />Call Support as soon as you arrive onsite.<br /> <br />Parts already onsite.<br />W16821389, Maintenance Kit Belt Unit (607K1578X) <br />930W00123, K MODE SENSOR</p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>No Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240F Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>production print to verify the printer functionality.</strong></li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to confirm deliverables and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li>The parts return packages must be dropped off at the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup counter&nbsp;</strong>inside the Walgreens location<strong>.&nbsp;</strong>You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, and obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature.</strong></li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the <strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>, <strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>, <strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong> and <strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li><li>If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <del>***** ********</del> and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240F xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nCX3240F  \nFIN: 303022  \nGetting Fault Code related to the Maintenance Belt not reading or installed correctly  \n  \nCall Support as soon as you arrive onsite.  \n   \nParts already onsite.  \nW16821389, Maintenance Kit Belt Unit (607K1578X)   \n930W00123, K MODE SENSOR\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nNo Parts Being Shipped Troubleshooting Only.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240F Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n2. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n3. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n4. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **production print to verify the printer functionality.**\n5. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n6. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n7. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n8. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n9. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n10. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n11. The parts return packages must be dropped off at the **FedEx pickup counter** inside the Walgreens location**.** You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.\n12. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, and obtain their **signature.**\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n- If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T09:30","end":"2026-10-30T11:30","latestStart":"2026-10-30T18:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2.0005185060217703},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/30/2026, 9:30:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"20