ll ONLINE after the work with the service vendor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">2. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">3. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">4. TV playing Costco feed playback</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">5. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">6. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">7. Complete the latest manager &amp; technician checklist &amp; upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">On completion of work, to receive the release code:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Email: </span>checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> and/or </span>costcosupport@stratacache.com</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">If needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Above check-in and check-out deliverables are a requirement and must be received for the checkout code</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required equipment:&nbsp;</p><p>WHITE cat6 (500'+ preferable), crimp tool, RJ45 male connectors, cat6 tester/toner, labeling and wire management supplies.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Skills:</p><p>Cat6, HDMI, HDMI-Cat-6 Converters, Video Wall Setup. Scissor Lift.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>AN ACTUAL LEGACY DISPATCH WILL BE SENT <u>BY EMAIL</u> WITH ALL THE PROPER JOB ATTACHMENTS YOU WILL NEED TO ACCURATELY COMPLETE THE JOB AND GET PAID.&nbsp;WORK MARKET WILL JUST BE OUR PLATFORM FOR PAYMENT</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Ref:MSG1783347\\_8xlpRJx4pakoxHeATRLZ\n\nService request: ASAP at 4:30 AM\n\nWarehouse #: 1587 (Raleigh, NC)\n\nNumber of technicians required: (1)\n\nTime allocated for SOW: 5.0 hours (Contact PRN support for additional time if required)\n\nDescription: The warehouse would like a technician to return remove unused Cat6 drops, label Cat6 drops, Test &amp; verify (2) future Cat6 drops, Connect parts &amp; Restore all TVs with Costco feed, Perform Cable cleanup/management, Verify PRN system wiring, Check HDMI cables from Amp to TVs, Configure TVs to HOME mode, Re-label all cables\n\nConfirm media player connectivity\n\nPoint of Contact: Lauren Corp Hardlines Manager\n\nPRN Documents (Download or view directly from the link)\n\n• <https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork>\n\nTools:\n\nA Cable Label maker is required, and clear scotch tape\n\nWhite Cat cable required (300'-400' white CAT6 cable)\n\nThe technician must bring white CAT6 cable, tester/toner, and labels to label cables. cable management supplies\n\nCheck-in: (Before starting any work in the warehouse)\n\n1\\. Contact Brandpoint tier 1: 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY or email checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com and copy costcosupport@stratacache to check-in\n\n2\\. PRN/Stratacache tier 1: call support 888-776-5589 (on overnights and weekends also email costcosupport@stratacache.com) -- if no answer: BKUP line 415-617-9752\n\n3\\. Upon arrival in TV department, locate the site contact listed below\n\n4\\. Check in with the point of contact below, review the SOW\n\nInitial Checks before starting work: (Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo, top right corner of the TVs)\n\nEnter the building through the back door\n\nSpeak with the point of contact listed above for the TV department\n\n1\\. Review the scope of work with the POC\n\n2\\. Request the TV remotes' location or the box of remotes to turn on all the TVs\n\n3\\. With the TVs turned ON, perform a count of what's playing Costco feed out of the total number of TVs in the department (x out of y)\n\n4\\. Take before pictures and email them to the service vendor list above\n\n4a. Capture pictures of any broken TVs and inform the managers before starting any work\n\n5\\. Confirm with the service vendor that the BrightSign player is online\n\n5a. Proceed to perform the SOW below\n\nSOW:\n\nLocate the Super Plate (BrightSign 4K player)\n\nStart from the Super Plate (4K Player and a batch of Cat6 cables coming down)\n\nCostco content is the blue/white concierge logo in the top right corner of the TV\n\nVerify with the vendor that the media player is online\n\nFirst priority - Clean up, Remove old unused Cat6 drops, Repair/Replace Cat6 drops and connect parts &amp; restore the Costco feed on all TVs\n\nSecond priority - Restore media player connectivity, Verify the PRN system is wired correctly\n\nThird priority - Survey the TV department if additional parts are requested, Perform cable clean up &amp; management (zip tie HDMI &amp; Cat6 cables)\n\n\\- Turn ON all TVs\n\n\\- Upon arrival, perform a count of the TVs playing Costco content and the total number of TVs in the department\n\nCostco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs\n\nRestore Costco content playback on TVs\n\n\\- Test and Verify (2) Cat6 future drops\n\n\\- Label Cat6 drops that are missing labels\n\n\\- Remove old unused Cat6 drops (completely remove drop, do not cut and leave)\n\n\\-- Take picture of the old Cat6 drops removed\n\n\\- Repair/Replace (1-2) Cat6 drops - Manager to identify\n\n\\-- For each location verify/take picture of playing Costco feed\n\n\\-- Label each drop on both ends (take picture of the label)\n\n\\- Connect parts &amp; restore Costco feed on all TVs (except waterfalls and endcaps) - yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs\n\n\\- Verify the PRN system is wired correctly\n\n\\- Connect HDMI cables from the Amp to TVs for Costco content playback\n\n\\- Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to OUTPUT 1 port\n\n\\- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port\n\n\\- Verify all Amp dip switches are set correctly\n\n\\- Check cables (damaged HDMI &amp; Cat6 drop), repair any damaged Cat6 drop and replace HDMI cables\n\nCable management and clean up\n\n\\- Perform cable clean-up (remove old unused Cat6 drops)\n\n\\- Perform cable management of Cat6 and HDMI cables (secure HDMI and Cat6 cables with zip ties)\n\n\\- Re-label all Cat6 drops\n\n\\- Configure all TVs to HOME mode\n\n\\- Label each Cat6 per instructions in the label guide doc\n\n\\- Verify Media player connectivity with support\n\n\\- Take lots of before and after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco content\n\nLocate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to the HDMI OUTPUT 1 port\n\n\\- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port\n\nRe-label all Cat6 cables being used to pass the Costco signal\n\n\\- All labels should be legible and clear to read on both ends\n\n\\- Label the CAT6 cable the same on both ends (6\" from the connector with a Sharpie and 12\" out with a label maker, wrap with clear scotch tape)\n\n\\- CAT6 cable naming scheme: (G1 being gondola/pod)\n\n\\- Cat6 Cable drop labeling scheme: G1-4K, G2-4K, G3-4K, and ON\n\nCat6 DON'Ts\n\n\\- DO NOT USE jumpers on Cat6 cable runs that are passing Costco feed HDMI video signal\n\nVerify the Extender has a solid BLUE LED = Good operation\n\nBlue/Green flashing = bad CAT6 or HDMI cable (cannot communicate with transmitter correctly)\n\nStartech/GEFEN extenders are POE, only the Sender/Transmitter requires power\n\nCheck-out process:\n\n1\\. Verify the media player is still ONLINE after the work with the service vendor\n\n2\\. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed\n\n3\\. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends\n\n4\\. TV playing Costco feed playback\n\n5\\. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work\n\n6\\. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor\n\n7\\. Complete the latest manager &amp; technician checklist &amp; upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support\n\n\\- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)\n\nOn completion of work, to receive the release code:\n\n\\- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache\n\n\\- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.\n\n\\- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work\n\n\\- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist\n\nEmail: checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com and/or costcosupport@stratacache.com\n\nIf needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support\n\nAbove check-in and check-out deliverables are a requirement and must be received for the checkout code\n\nRequired equipment:\n\nWHITE cat6 (500'+ preferable), crimp tool, RJ45 male connectors, cat6 tester/toner, labeling and wire management supplies.\n\nRequired Skills:\n\nCat6, HDMI, HDMI-Cat-6 Converters, Video Wall Setup. Scissor Lift.\n\nAN ACTUAL LEGACY DISPATCH WILL BE SENT BY EMAIL WITH ALL THE PROPER JOB ATTACHMENTS YOU WILL NEED TO ACCURATELY COMPLETE THE JOB AND GET PAID. WORK MARKET WILL JUST BE OUR PLATFORM FOR PAYMENT","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T04:30","end":"2026-11-04T04:30"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":350},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":14.917169308660618},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793377481241}
{"job":{"id":20277671,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Primo Water - WMS Project Cable Runs and AP installation - Assist","description":{"html":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.<br/>For non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.<br/>Do not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.<br/><br/>SOW: <br/>Check in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>Tech must be prepared with:<br/>PPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves & vests)<br/>Label maker and labels!<br/>Drill and concrete drill bits<br/><br/>DS/Primo IT contacts (if needed): <br/>   - Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238  <br/>   - David Hollis 727-418-4650 <br/>   - Robert Chambers 203-509-6467<br/>   - Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318<br/>   - Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615<br/>Onsite contact:<br/>  - Kyle Cole 910-584-8744<br/><br/><br/>Site Specific Details: Primo will be sending APs and any network equipment, Spencer will be sending basic cabling materials and reserving a lift if needed:<br/>Rough-In, Terminate, and Test (3) CAT6 Cables for New APs<br/>Install a total of 3 APs : 2 APs in the warehouse , 1 AP in the office ( route room)  see attached for approximate AP placement<br/>The network team confirmed there are enough available switch ports<br/>We will be using the Cellular solution so no exterior APs will be installed<br/><br/>Survey Results-<br/>Identify any potential issues with running cable: From MDF OVER conference room into the warehouse. Will need lift for warehouse due to high ceiling. Primo store has 1 AP located in the hallway of the office. Would need APs in warehouse area and possibly outside in the back area.<br/>Identify all existing AP's onsite: 1 Ap in office<br/>NOTES & ADDITIONAL OBSERVATIONS:<br/>Sw1 ports 6,8,9,12,13,14,15,16,18<br/>Water inventory may need to be moved for us to run cable, this could also be a potential obstruction that can cause delays.<br/><br/><br/>Deliverables:<br/>- Before & after pictures of all work done<br/>- Summary of work completed, including site times<br/><br/>Send deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.<br/><br/>Check out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>**Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","markdown":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.  \nFor non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.  \nDo not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.  \n  \nSOW:   \nCheck in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \nTech must be prepared with:  \nPPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves &amp; vests)  \nLabel maker and labels!  \nDrill and concrete drill bits  \n  \nDS/Primo IT contacts (if needed):   \n\\- Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238   \n\\- David Hollis 727-418-4650   \n\\- Robert Chambers 203-509-6467  \n\\- Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318  \n\\- Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615  \nOnsite contact:  \n\\- Kyle Cole 910-584-8744  \n  \n  \nSite Specific Details: Primo will be sending APs and any network equipment, Spencer will be sending basic cabling materials and reserving a lift if needed:  \nRough-In, Terminate, and Test (3) CAT6 Cables for New APs  \nInstall a total of 3 APs : 2 APs in the warehouse , 1 AP in the office ( route room) see attached for approximate AP placement  \nThe network team confirmed there are enough available switch ports  \nWe will be using the Cellular solution so no exterior APs will be installed  \n  \nSurvey Results-  \nIdentify any potential issues with running cable: From MDF OVER conference room into the warehouse. Will need lift for warehouse due to high ceiling. Primo store has 1 AP located in the hallway of the office. Would need APs in warehouse area and possibly outside in the back area.  \nIdentify all existing AP's onsite: 1 Ap in office  \nNOTES &amp; ADDITIONAL OBSERVATIONS:  \nSw1 ports 6,8,9,12,13,14,15,16,18  \nWater inventory may need to be moved for us to run cable, this could also be a potential obstruction that can cause delays.  \n  \n  \nDeliverables:  \n\\- Before &amp; after pictures of all work done  \n\\- Summary of work completed, including site times  \n  \nSend deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.  \n  \nCheck out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \n\\*\\*Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-20T08:00","end":"2026-11-20T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":440},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":61.63260730837338},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":90,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1793377916247}
{"job":{"id":20278092,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ReliaSource","title":"Camera Refocusing and Kiosk Bolt Replacement-RDU","description":{"html":"<p>Refocus camera on kiosk with test person 3-4 feet out from the frame. Make sure it is a high quality photo.</p><p>You will be provided with POC info and Tech support info, we now need to get these 3 kiosk cameras focused and approved by TSA HQ before leaving the site.</p><p>We also need a technician to replace the nuts/bolts on 4 kiosks, 1 of them being a spare.</p><p>Must have tools:</p><p>3/8\" socket, 1/4\" drive (space is tight)</p><p>#1 Phillips screwdriver</p><p>Small pry tool for trim covers</p><p>Torx set</p><p><br></p><p>PAY INCLUDES PARKING PAYMENT.</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Refocus camera on kiosk with test person 3-4 feet out from the frame. Make sure it is a high quality photo.\n\nYou will be provided with POC info and Tech support info, we now need to get these 3 kiosk cameras focused and approved by TSA HQ before leaving the site.\n\nWe also need a technician to replace the nuts/bolts on 4 kiosks, 1 of them being a spare.\n\nMust have tools:\n\n3/8\" socket, 1/4\" drive (space is tight)\n\n\\#1 Phillips screwdriver\n\nSmall pry tool for trim covers\n\nTorx set\n\nPAY INCLUDES PARKING PAYMENT.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":225,"max":225},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":2.843394932111315},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"sta