{"job":{"id":20278419,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Safely-You","title":"WiFi Camera Installation (qty: 6) - Smartphone & Teams Required","description":{"html":"<p>Installation Overview:</p><p><strong><u>This will be for the installation of QTY: 6 WiFi sensors - Tech is to provide raceway (Additional cost added for raceway)</u></strong></p><p>Work location is a senior living facility—you may be entering the private residences of and interacting with seniors with memory impairment. You will be acting as a representative of SafelyYou on site—any negative feedback about your behavior on site will invalidate you for future work orders.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>SOW: <u>Do NOT use the sticky back on the raceway as this will damage the wall paint.</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong>Coordinate with the field manager on Teams prior to install - We will send wire mold info on Teams</strong></li><li>On the day of install, ask front desk at the community to gain entry and locate your inventory - asking for maintenance assistance is most helpful</li><li>Confirm inventory in Teams and join Zoom call <strong>prior to install</strong> - Zoom call will confirm sensor placement</li><li>Log in to our SSID - info posted to Teams</li><li>Mounting raceway, installing outlet cover, running a power cord through raceway, mounting sensor.</li><li>We will Provide a QR after each install to scan the sensor</li><li>Install Door Tag</li><li>Clean up all working areas.</li><li>Please stick around while the sensor viewports populate in case of troubleshooting.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong></p><p>Ability to communicate, dress, and behave in a professional, kind, and respectful manner is<strong>MANDATORY.</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>While the Guardian Pro sensor is a camera in some sense,<strong><em><u>please only refer to the Guardian Pro as a Fall Detection sensor</u></em></strong><em><u>,</u></em><strong><em><u>Guardian Pro, or sensor when working in the community.</u></em></strong></li><li>Call SafelyYou field manager <strong>before entering the facility</strong>. You will coordinate with the field manager via Microsoft Teams on your phone where they will guide you with any questions you may have during the installation.</li><li>Cleaning each area worked in is mandatory.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Once assigned to this ticket, you will be added to this site's Teams chat where all future communication regarding the install will take place.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Smart phone</li><li>Cordless drill (Impact not recommended)</li><li>4-6’ Step Ladder</li><li>8-10’ A Frame Ladder</li><li>Heat gun</li><li>Receptacle Outlet Tester</li><li>Drywall Screws</li><li>Drywall anchors</li><li>Vacuum/cleaning wipes/Broom</li><li>Microfiber Cloth</li><li>Basic HandTools- Mini &amp; Reg. Phillips &amp; Flathead Drivers-Needle Nose Pliers-Flush Cuts</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Before and After photos of work area/installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Race way is installed as instructed (Close up and wide view)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sensor location (close up and wide view)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work area cleaned and furniture moved back to original placement</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Outlet cover is neat and level</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Door tag placement (Close up and far away including entire door frame+tag)</li></ul>","markdown":"Installation Overview:\n\n**This will be for the installation of QTY: 6 WiFi sensors - Tech is to provide raceway (Additional cost added for raceway)**\n\nWork location is a senior living facility—you may be entering the private residences of and interacting with seniors with memory impairment. You will be acting as a representative of SafelyYou on site—any negative feedback about your behavior on site will invalidate you for future work orders.\n\n**SOW: Do NOT use the sticky back on the raceway as this will damage the wall paint.**\n\n1. **Coordinate with the field manager on Teams prior to install - We will send wire mold info on Teams**\n2. On the day of install, ask front desk at the community to gain entry and locate your inventory - asking for maintenance assistance is most helpful\n3. Confirm inventory in Teams and join Zoom call **prior to install** - Zoom call will confirm sensor placement\n4. Log in to our SSID - info posted to Teams\n5. Mounting raceway, installing outlet cover, running a power cord through raceway, mounting sensor.\n6. We will Provide a QR after each install to scan the sensor\n7. Install Door Tag\n8. Clean up all working areas.\n9. Please stick around while the sensor viewports populate in case of troubleshooting.\n\n**IMPORTANT:**\n\nAbility to communicate, dress, and behave in a professional, kind, and respectful manner is**MANDATORY.**\n\n- While the Guardian Pro sensor is a camera in some sense,***please only refer to the Guardian Pro as a Fall Detection sensor****,****Guardian Pro, or sensor when working in the community.***\n- Call SafelyYou field manager **before entering the facility**. You will coordinate with the field manager via Microsoft Teams on your phone where they will guide you with any questions you may have during the installation.\n- Cleaning each area worked in is mandatory.\n\n**Once assigned to this ticket, you will be added to this site's Teams chat where all future communication regarding the install will take place.**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Smart phone\n- Cordless drill (Impact not recommended)\n- 4-6’ Step Ladder\n- 8-10’ A Frame Ladder\n- Heat gun\n- Receptacle Outlet Tester\n- Drywall Screws\n- Drywall anchors\n- Vacuum/cleaning wipes/Broom\n- Microfiber Cloth\n- Basic HandTools- Mini &amp; Reg. Phillips &amp; Flathead Drivers-Needle Nose Pliers-Flush Cuts\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Before and After photos of work area/installation\n- Race way is installed as instructed (Close up and wide view)\n- Sensor location (close up and wide view)\n- Work area cleaned and furniture moved back to original placement\n- Outlet cover is neat and level\n- Door tag placement (Close up and far away including entire door frame+tag)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T17:00","latestStart":"2026-11-04T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":750,"max":750},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":21.96261205130333},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":94,"baseAmount":750,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":40,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (21.96261205130333mi reported + 10mi padding = 31.96261205130333mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1793382087536}
{"job":{"id":20278225,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Mole IoT Corp","title":"IoT Asset Sensor Installation - Waste and Recycling Equipment - On Prem","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Important Notes:</strong><br />\nPlease install on the 2 Yardsfront load container(s). If this is not easily accessible, please work with the onsite manager. Communication has been sent to the store about the sensor installation.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Before you request this work order, please read:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If assigned, you must provide a shipping address for the equipment. <strong>Do not visit the location until the equipment is in your hands.</strong></li>\n<li>Once the equipment is received, <strong>complete the work within 72 hours. Scheduling will update once delivery has occurred.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This is a photo-documented work order.</strong> A work order submitted without the required deliverable photos will be marked <strong>INCOMPLETE</strong> and will not be approved for payment. There are no exceptions — do not leave the site until you have captured every photo.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Looking for:</strong>a general technician; experience in IoT device installation and hardware mounting is a plus.</li>\n<li><strong>The job:</strong>install Mole IoT smart waste sensor(s) on designated dumpster(s) to monitor fill level and service frequency. Depending on the dumpster, an accessory bracket assembly may be required for proper installation. Installation is via magnet mount.</li>\n<li><strong>Device count:</strong>listed on the work order. Plan for 10–15 minutes per device.</li>\n<li><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 15 – 30 minutes on site.</li>\n<li><strong>Access required:</strong> the waste and recycling area must be accessible to complete the installation safely.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables and Virtual Support</strong>: https://start.moleiot.com/</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work - Required On-Site Deliverables</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>THE ON-SITE DOCUMENTATION AND DELIVERABLES ARE FOUND AT</strong>https://start.moleiot.com/. <strong>THIS MUST BE COMPLETED ON-SITE DURING INSTALLATION</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Arrive on site</strong> and locate the waste and recycling area. This is typically behind or to the side of the location. Check whether the dumpsters are open and accessible. Some sites may have locks and require assistance from the site manager to access the dumpster(s) or waste corral. A Letter of Authorization (LOA) is attached to this work order for the site contact's reference.</li>\n<li><strong>Determine the Assembly Configuration</strong>: Inspect the container, then pick one. Reference the Sensor Placement and Configuration Guide:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Flat Mounting Configuration</strong>: The container has a slanted or flat top area to attach the sensor to. Use when there is a<strong>horizontal</strong> or slanted steel surface above the container cavity. Sensor points down into the middle of the container. Reference the picture attachment</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Angled Mounting Configuration</strong>: The container has no slant position to mount on that allows the sensor to look down into the container cavity. This is common for smaller containers or tall dock-style containers. You will need to remove the magnets, add the mounting bracket, and reassemble. This will allow you to mount the magnets on the back wall of the container so the sensor looks downward into it.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Unsure</strong>... the sensor face must be installed pointing <strong>DOWN</strong> into the middle cavity of the container. If neither configuration seems to work on the container, stop and 'Call Us' via https://start.moleiot.com/ before improvising. This is best to ensure a site revisit isn't needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Navigate to</strong>: https://start.moleiot.com/ This is where all deliverable documentation and instructions for installation are kept. If the deliverables are not completed, the work order is considered incomplete.</li>\n<li><strong>Scan the side Barcode</strong>, or enter the MAC manually to begin documentation. This should be done prior to mounting the device.</li>\n<li><strong>Follow the Steps in the Instructions.</strong>Throughout the process, you will install the sensor and provide picture documentation.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">During the process, you will be asked to enter the Service ID. This will not be on the containers, but in the Field Nation Work Order under 'Buyer Custom Fields'.</li>\n<li><strong>Reach the 'Installation Submitted!' Screen.</strong>This is your verification that the deliverable documentation is complete. <u>You will need to enter the code in the Provider Custom Field.</u></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In the event of a technical issue, please reach out to us via https://start.moleiot.com/. Photos are still required and must be attached to the Field Nation work order in the event of technical issues.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you close the browser before entering the Completion Code, it can be found in the messages on this work order.</li>\n<li>If you have multiple sensors to install, repeat the process for each sensor starting at step 2.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>What you will receive - per sensor:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>1 sensor, 1 protective sleeve, 1 angle bracket, 4 magnets, 8 locking nuts, 8 screws. Reference attachment 'What you will receive - SWB-300+'</li>\n<li>Upon arrival, the sensor will already be set up in the<strong>Flat Mounting Configuration.</strong> The extra 4 screws, nuts, and bracket will accompany the sensor for adjustment on-site, if needed.</li>\n<li>The sensor will arrive powered on.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Plan to arrive during business hours and verify prior to commuting to the installation location</li>\n<li>Review all provided documentation and manufacturer installation guides.</li>\n<li>Confirm appointment with onsite contact prior to arrival (if instructed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Smartphone with camera and internet access. Using Chrome or Safari browser is recommended for deliverables.</li>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>As you will be attaching the IoT device via magnets to the container, you may need to pry the device off as the magnets are 120lb pull force each if you misplace device. Having a long neck screwdriver on hand is highly encouraged</em></li>\n<li><strong>A step stool/small 6ft ladder may be needed to secure IoT device in waste container. (In or next to the container)</strong></li>\n<li>A flashlight might be helpful depending on time of day and location of containers.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Communication Directory:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any site-related issues or access - Please refer to the contacts in the Letter of Authorization (LOA) provided on the WO or use the 'Call Us' via https://start.moleiot.com/</li>\n<li>If you encounter issues that prohibit the installation, do not leave the site before contacting virtual support via 'Call Us' via https://start.moleiot.com/</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You will be working around trash and recyclables, so wear appropriate clothing, footwear, and protective gloves. No open footwear.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unauthorized expenses or hours will not be approved. All rates are negotiated prior to assignment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Lost Device Policy</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If the sensor is lost in your possession prior to documented installation, you will be charged $225 per sensor</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Important Notes:**  \nPlease install on the 2 Yardsfront load container(s). If this is not easily accessible, please work with the onsite manager. Communication has been sent to the store about the sensor installation.\n\n**Before you request this work order, please read:**\n\n- If assigned, you must provide a shipping address for the equipment. **Do not visit the location until the equipment is in your hands.**\n- Once the equipment is received, **complete the work within 72 hours. Scheduling will update once delivery has occurred.**\n- **This is a photo-documented work order.** A work order submitted without the required deliverable photos will be marked **INCOMPLETE** and will not be approved for payment. There are no exceptions — do not leave the site until you have captured every photo.\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- **Looking for:**a general technician; experience in IoT device installation and hardware mounting is a plus.\n- **The job:**install Mole IoT smart waste sensor(s) on designated dumpster(s) to monitor fill level and service frequency. Depending on the dumpster, an accessory bracket assembly may be required for proper installation. Installation is via magnet mount.\n- **Device count:**listed on the work order. Plan for 10–15 minutes per device.\n- **Estimated duration:** 15 – 30 minutes on site.\n- **Access required:** the waste and recycling area must be accessible to complete the installation safely.\n- **Deliverables and Virtual Support**: <https://start.moleiot.com/>\n\n**Scope of Work - Required On-Site Deliverables**\n\n**THE ON-SITE DOCUMENTATION AND DELIVERABLES ARE FOUND AT**<https://start.moleiot.com/>. **THIS MUST BE COMPLETED ON-SITE DURING INSTALLATION**\n\n1. **Arrive on site** and locate the waste and recycling area. This is typically behind or to the side of the location. Check whether the dumpsters are open and accessible. Some sites may have locks and require assistance from the site manager to access the dumpster(s) or waste corral. A Letter of Authorization (LOA) is attached to this work order for the site contact's reference.\n2. **Determine the Assembly Configuration**: Inspect the container, then pick one. Reference the Sensor Placement and Configuration Guide:\n3. **Flat Mounting Configuration**: The container has a slanted or flat top area to attach the sensor to. Use when there is a**horizontal** or slanted steel surface above the container cavity. Sensor points down into the middle of the container. Reference the picture attachment\n4. **Angled Mounting Configuration**: The container has no slant position to mount on that allows the sensor to look down into the container cavity. This is common for smaller containers or tall dock-style containers. You will need to remove the magnets, add the mounting bracket, and reassemble. This will allow you to mount the magnets on the back wall of the container so the sensor looks downward into it.\n5. **Unsure**... the sensor face must be installed pointing **DOWN** into the middle cavity of the container. If neither configuration seems to work on the container, stop and 'Call Us' via <https://start.moleiot.com/> before improvising. This is best to ensure a site revisit isn't needed.\n6. **Navigate to**: <https://start.moleiot.com/> This is where all deliverable documentation and instructions for installation are kept. If the deliverables are not completed, the work order is considered incomplete.\n7. **Scan the side Barcode**, or enter the MAC manually to begin documentation. This should be done prior to mounting the device.\n8. **Follow the Steps in the Instructions.**Throughout the process, you will install the sensor and provide picture documentation.\n9. During the process, you will be asked to enter the Service ID. This will not be on the containers, but in the Field Nation Work Order under 'Buyer Custom Fields'.\n10. **Reach the 'Installation Submitted!' Screen.**This is your verification that the deliverable documentation is complete. You will need to enter the code in the Provider Custom Field.\n11. In the event of a technical issue, please reach out to us via <https://start.moleiot.com/>. Photos are still required and must be attached to the Field Nation work order in the event of technical issues.\n12. If you close the browser before entering the Completion Code, it can be found in the messages on this work order.\n13. If you have multiple sensors to install, repeat the process for each sensor starting at step 2.\n\n**What you will receive - per sensor:**\n\n- 1 sensor, 1 protective sleeve, 1 angle bracket, 4 magnets, 8 locking nuts, 8 screws. Reference attachment 'What you will receive - SWB-300+'\n- Upon arrival, the sensor will already be set up in the**Flat Mounting Configuration.** The extra 4 screws, nuts, and bracket will accompany the sensor for adjustment on-site, if needed.\n- The sensor will arrive powered on.\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- Plan to arrive during business hours and verify prior to commuting to the installation location\n- Review all provided documentation and manufacturer installation guides.\n- Confirm appointment with onsite contact prior to arrival (if instructed).\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Smartphone with camera and internet access. Using Chrome or Safari browser is recommended for deliverables.\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n- *As you will be attaching the IoT device via magnets to the container, you may need to pry the device off as the magnets are 120lb pull force each if you misplace device. Having a long neck screwdriver on hand is highly encouraged*\n- **A step stool/small 6ft ladder may be needed to secure IoT device in waste container. (In or next to the container)**\n- A flashlight might be helpful depending on time of day and location of containers.\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- Any site-related issues or access - Please refer to the contacts in the Letter of Authorization (LOA) provided on the WO or use the 'Call Us' via <https://start.moleiot.com/>\n- If you encounter issues that prohibit the installation, do not leave the site before contacting virtual support via 'Call Us' via <https://start.moleiot.com/>\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- You will be working around trash and recyclables, so wear appropriate clothing, footwear, and protective gloves. No open footwear.\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Unauthorized expenses or hours will not be approved. All rates are negotiated prior to assignment.\n\n**Lost Device Policy**\n\n- If the sensor is lost in your possession prior to documented installation, you will be charged $225 per sensor","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T08:00","end":"2026-11-11T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":45},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":17.793820028202216},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793382180864}
{"job":{"id":20278591,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Purely IT LLC","title":"Camera and Recorder Diagnostic Service","description":{"html":"<p>Camera and Recorder Diagnostic Service</p>MANDATORY: PURELY CHECK-IN, CHAT AND DELIVERABLES<p>As soon as you arrive, open the Purely technician link in the CONFIDENTIAL instructions and enter its access code. Check in through Purely chat and wait for acknowledgment before touching equipment.<br>Complete the work through this portal: instructions, required photos, job chat and release code. Working only with a third-party vendor does not satisfy these deliverables. Purely must coordinate vendor contact.<br>Payment approval requires the agreed work-order deliverables and Purely review. Missing check-in, portal use or evidence will hold approval for correction or formal dispute review under the agreed Field Nation terms. Do not accept unless you can follow this process.</p>AUTHORIZED SCOPE<p>Diagnose and attempt repair of offline QNAP recorder and cameras, addressing broken BNC ports with supplied connectors.</p>PURELY SUPPORT<p>Use the chat in your technician job link to check in before changes. Purely coordinates vendor support.<br>Coverage: Purely support team, 10 a.m.–5 p.m. Eastern. Work outside coverage requires advance support arrangements.<br>Site details, access instructions and your private job link are provided after assignment.</p>BEFORE YOU START<p>Introduce yourself as working on behalf of [site details shared after assignment]. Purely coordinates your support and release.</p>CONFIRM BEFORE TRAVELLING<p>Bring a ladder suitable for the mounting height of any affected cameras; confirm access method with Purely if the required height or lift is unknown.<br>Confirm you have the Purely-supplied BNC connectors and crimp tool.<br>Bring a laptop with Ethernet port/adapters suitable for QNAP/recorder diagnosis.<br>Bring an analog camera tester and basic hand tools for BNC and coaxial work.<br>Wear appropriate PPE for electrical and elevated work.<br>Verify site and CCTV equipment access with Purely before arrival.</p>TECHNICIAN STEPS<p>1. Meet the site contact<br>   Confirm you are at the correct site and tell Purely who is your site contact.<br>2. Diagnose and document offline QNAP and cameras<br>   With Purely, identify the affected QNAP recorder and the offline cameras. Confirm which camera types (IP or analog), switches/encoders, and power supplies are involved.<br>   Record model numbers, camera names/channels, and the total number of cameras expected, online, and offline before making changes.<br>   Photograph and label the existing connections—including any broken BNC ports. Trace and label relevant cables.<br>   Check power and cable conditions with appropriate testers for IP and analog lines. Do not reset or reconfigure equipment without approval.<br>   If a camera’s BNC port is physically broken, replace the connector with the supplied equipment and retest.<br>   Required photos: 2. Live monitor or camera-status view before work, showing affected channels.; Recorder/switch/encoder connections and readable port labels relevant to the fault.<br>3. Purely verifies the system — Purely support owns this verification; stay available to assist.<br>   With Purely, identify the complete expected camera and equipment inventory. Check every camera, the recorder and relevant network equipment, including devices outside the replaced component. Record expected counts, online counts, device identities and tested results.<br>   ALL cameras and equipment must be online before departure. Have Purely verify live feeds and applicable recording/playback. A link light or one working camera is not sufficient.<br>   For each device still offline, identify it, state the exact confirmed cause (or cause not confirmed), tests and observations, and the specific parts/materials, quantities and next diagnostic work needed. Do not guess a part or cause.<br>   Report every unresolved device in Purely chat. Only Purely can release an incomplete visit with a documented follow-up plan; never mark the system fully restored when equipment remains offline.<br>   Required photos: 2. Final full camera/device status list showing expected and online counts.; Final recorder/system verification or evidence of each remaining offline device.; Final live monitor or camera-status view and camera counts.; Final connections and the repair or remaining fault.<br>4. Get your release code and finish<br>   Ask Purely support to review the evidence and issue the release code for this visit before leaving.<br>   Purely records your release here after reviewing the work. Copy the release code into Field Nation and submit the required deliverables there. A release can document an incomplete visit.</p>TOOLS<p>Bring your own serviceable ladder suitable for safe access to the cameras. Sites do not provide ladders. Confirm mounting height and access before accepting; ask Purely if a lift or special access equipment is needed. Never improvise unsafe access.<br>Technician-supplied ladder suitable for affected camera height (confirm with Purely if unsure/if a lift is needed)<br>Purely-supplied BNC connectors and crimp tool<br>Laptop with Ethernet port and adapters<br>Analog camera tester<br>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, cable cutters/strippers, pliers)<br>Network cable tester (for IP/video circuits)<br>Appropriate PPE for electrical and elevated work<br>Laptop with Ethernet connectivity and required adapters<br>Network cable tester for IP cabling; analog test equipment if analog troubleshooting is in scope</p>EXCLUSIONS<p>Do not perform unapproved installation or replacement of other equipment.<br>Do not reset or reconfigure QNAP/recorder or unrelated network settings without explicit Purely approval.<br>Do not guess required parts; all replacements must be supported by diagnosis and approved by Purely.</p>PARTS AND RESPONSIBILITY<p>- BNC Connectors: 2; supplied by purely; received.</p><p><br>RELEASE AND DELIVERABLES<br>Get the visit release code from Purely support. Upload the required evidence and enter the release code in Field Nation.<br>Report time and scope changes before exceeding the approved terms. No unapproved deductions or penalties are implied.</p>","markdown":"Camera and Recorder Diagnostic Service\n\nMANDATORY: PURELY CHECK-IN, CHAT AND DELIVERABLESAs soon as you arrive, open the Purely technician link in the CONFIDENTIAL instructions and enter its access code. Check in through Purely chat and wait for acknowledgment before touching equipment.  \nComplete the work through this portal: instructions, required photos, job chat and release code. Working only with a third-party vendor does not satisfy these deliverables. Purely must coordinate vendor contact.  \nPayment approval requires the agreed work-order deliverables and Purely review. Missing check-in, portal use or evidence will hold approval for correction or formal dispute review under the agreed Field Nation terms. Do not accept unless you can follow this process.\n\nAUTHORIZED SCOPEDiagnose and attempt repair of offline QNAP recorder and cameras, addressing broken BNC ports with supplied connectors.\n\nPURELY SUPPORTUse the chat in your technician job link to check in before changes. Purely coordinates vendor support.  \nCoverage: Purely support team, 10 a.m.–5 p.m. Eastern. Work outside coverage requires advance support arrangements.  \nSite details, access instructions and your private job link are provided after assignment.\n\nBEFORE YOU STARTIntroduce yourself as working on behalf of \\[site details shared after assignment\\]. Purely coordinates your support and release.\n\nCONFIRM BEFORE TRAVELLINGBring a ladder suitable for the mounting height of any affected cameras; confirm access method with Purely if the required height or lift is unknown.  \nConfirm you have the Purely-supplied BNC connectors and crimp tool.  \nBring a laptop with Ethernet port/adapters suitable for QNAP/recorder diagnosis.  \nBring an analog camera tester and basic hand tools for BNC and coaxial work.  \nWear appropriate PPE for electrical and elevated work.  \nVerify site and CCTV equipment access with Purely before arrival.\n\nTECHNICIAN STEPS1\\. Meet the site contact  \n Confirm you are at the correct site and tell Purely who is your site contact.  \n2\\. Diagnose and document offline QNAP and cameras  \n With Purely, identify the affected QNAP recorder and the offline cameras. Confirm which camera types (IP or analog), switches/encoders, and power supplies are involved.  \n Record model numbers, camera names/channels, and the total number of cameras expected, online, and offline before making changes.  \n Photograph and label the existing connections—including any broken BNC ports. Trace and label relevant cables.  \n Check power and cable conditions with appropriate testers for IP and analog lines. Do not reset or reconfigure equipment without approval.  \n If a camera’s BNC port is physically broken, replace the connector with the supplied equipment and retest.  \n Required photos: 2. Live monitor or camera-status view before work, showing affected channels.; Recorder/switch/encoder connections and readable port labels relevant to the fault.  \n3\\. Purely verifies the system — Purely support owns this verification; stay available to assist.  \n With Purely, identify the complete expected camera and equipment inventory. Check every camera, the recorder and relevant network equipment, including devices outside the replaced component. Record expected counts, online counts, device identities and tested results.  \n ALL cameras and equipment must be online before departure. Have Purely verify live feeds and applicable recording/playback. A link light or one working camera is not sufficient.  \n For each device still offline, identify it, state the exact confirmed cause (or cause not confirmed), tests and observations, and the specific parts/materials, quantities and next diagnostic work needed. Do not guess a part or cause.  \n Report every unresolved device in Purely chat. Only Purely can release an incomplete visit with a documented follow-up plan; never mark the system fully restored when equipment remains offline.  \n Required photos: 2. Final full camera/device status list showing expected and online counts.; Final recorder/system verification or evidence of each remaining offline device.; Final live monitor or camera-status view and camera counts.; Final connections and the repair or remaining fault.  \n4\\. Get your release code and finish  \n Ask Purely support to review the evidence and issue the release code for this visit before leaving.  \n Purely records your release here after reviewing the work. Copy the release code into Field Nation and submit the required deliverables there. A release can document an incomplete visit.\n\nTOOLSBring your own serviceable ladder suitable for safe access to the cameras. Sites do not provide ladders. Confirm mounting height and access before accepting; ask Purely if a lift or special access equipment is needed. Never improvise unsafe access.  \nTechnician-supplied ladder suitable for affected camera height (confirm with Purely if unsure/if a lift is needed)  \nPurely-supplied BNC connectors and crimp tool  \nLaptop with Ethernet port and adapters  \nAnalog camera tester  \nBasic hand tools (screwdrivers, cable cutters/strippers, pliers)  \nNetwork cable tester (for IP/video circuits)  \nAppropriate PPE for electrical and elevated work  \nLaptop with Ethernet connectivity and required adapters  \nNetwork cable tester for IP cabling; analog test equipment if analog troubleshooting is in scope\n\nEXCLUSIONSDo not perform unapproved installation or replacement of other equipment.  \nDo not reset or reconfigure QNAP/recorder or unrelated network settings without explicit Purely approval.  \nDo not guess required parts; all replacements must be supported by diagnosis and approved by Purely.\n\nPARTS AND RESPONSIBILITY\\- BNC Connectors: 2; supplied by purely; received.\n\n  \nRELEASE AND DELIVERABLES  \nGet the visit release code from Purely support. Upload the required evidence and enter the release code in Field Nation.  \nReport time and scope changes before exceeding the approved terms. No unapproved deductions or penalties are implied.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T10:00","end":"2026-11-04T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":77.94566282087715},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-30T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity South Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000