{"job":{"id":20279165,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p>8.Short description of the reported issue:</p><p>Onsite Assistance needed to replace faulty switch.</p><p><br></p><p>9.If L1/L2 is required: L2</p><p>10.Mandate Action required:</p><p><br></p><p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p><p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.</p><p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support</p><p><br></p><p>11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:</p><p><br></p><p>-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).</p><p>-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p><p>-10 ft data cable.</p><p>-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch</p><p>-Cable tester&nbsp;</p><p>-Tone generator&nbsp;</p><p>-Toner</p><p>-Serial adapter</p><p><br></p><p>12.Scope of Work:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;Site only has one switch, and failure will impact the whole clinic.</p><p><br></p><p>Tech MUST have a working laptop with putty installed, working console cable for Aruba devices (USB-C) and the required tools to mount the device.</p><p><br></p><p>13.After the completion of Visit:</p><p>Update the SVR with Resolution Steps</p>","markdown":"8.Short description of the reported issue:\n\nOnsite Assistance needed to replace faulty switch.\n\n9.If L1/L2 is required: L2\n\n10.Mandate Action required:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support\n\n11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:\n\n-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).\n\n-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-10 ft data cable.\n\n-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch\n\n-Cable tester\n\n-Tone generator\n\n-Toner\n\n-Serial adapter\n\n12.Scope of Work:\n\n Site only has one switch, and failure will impact the whole clinic.\n\nTech MUST have a working laptop with putty installed, working console cable for Aruba devices (USB-C) and the required tools to mount the device.\n\n13.After the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the SVR with Resolution Steps","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T10:30","end":"2026-11-02T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":5.507740794644688},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793385458519}
{"job":{"id":20279354,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot and Restore Offline Network Switch – Raleigh, NC | 00263462 / SA-295155 / 05314215","description":{"html":"<p>Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.</p><p>After your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.</p><ul><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li><li>Note: <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li><li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span>and its reason.</li><li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li><li>Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot and Restore Offline Network Switch – Raleigh, NC | 00263462 / SA-295155 / 05314215</p><p><strong>Type of Work:</strong> Networking</p><p><strong>Schedule:</strong> October 30, 2026 – 4:00 PM (EDT)</p><p><strong>Site Name &amp; Address:</strong> Hampton Inn and Suites Raleigh Midtown, 1229 Wake Towne Dr, Raleigh, NC 27609, USA</p><p><strong>WO / SA / Case:</strong> WO#: 00263462 / SA#: SA-295155 / Case#: 05314215</p><p><strong>Contact Details:</strong> Site POC: Jeremy DeVault, 407-491-6694 Engineer: TBD | TECHNET Technician: TBD (Please Acknowledge)</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><ul><li>Investigate the reported offline Cisco Meraki MS350-24P switch at IDF6.</li><li>Inspect switch power supply, power connections, and physical status.</li><li>Inspect network cabling and uplink connectivity to the parent switch HLT-RDURD-350-MDF-CS01.</li><li>Verify uplink connectivity through parent switch Port 28.</li><li>Check switch LEDs, power status, and physical connections for any abnormalities.</li><li>Perform necessary troubleshooting to isolate the cause of the switch outage.</li><li>Check cabling and uplink connections, reseat connections if necessary, and reboot the switch if required.</li><li>Restore network connectivity and verify the switch comes back online.</li><li>Confirm connected network devices and local connectivity are operational.</li><li>Monitor switch status to ensure it remains online and stable after restoration.</li><li>Document findings, troubleshooting steps, corrective actions, and any required repairs or equipment replacement.</li><li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li></ul><p><strong>Asset &amp; Location:</strong> Cisco Meraki MS350-24P Switch (HLT-RDURD-350-IDF6-DS04-1) – IDF6</p><ul><li>Device Model: Cisco Meraki MS350-24P</li><li>Serial Number: Q2WP-UMZU-P9NC</li><li>MAC Address: E0:55:3D:95:C1:38</li><li>IP Address: 192.168.0.6</li><li>Parent Device/Switch: HLT-RDURD-350-MDF-CS01</li><li>Uplink Port: 28</li><li>Monitoring Source/System: Unknown</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat</li><li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li><li>Ethernet adapter</li><li>Ethernet cable</li><li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li><li>Cellphone with camera</li><li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit Ethernet connections)</li><li>Tone generator</li><li>Console cable and USB adapter</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Crimper</li><li>RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)</li><li>Voltage tester</li><li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li></ul>","markdown":"Upon Arrival - Call 1-858-352-7230 to immediately check in. You can then immediately begin to validate locations and access to the Location/Rooms/Units. Make sure you familiarize yourself with the site contact (POC) and get acclimated with the location of all the areas we will need to go into.\n\nAfter your check-in (or possibly before), the coordinator will put you into a Microsoft Teams chat with an engineer who can assist you into deeper troubleshooting as needed (You’ll need to have Microsoft Teams installed and be able to use it effectively for this job; otherwise, you may risk losing payment). It is expected that you begin to locate and troubleshoot the devices called out in the scope below before initiating a conversation with the engineer. They are not there to hold your hand - they are there to further assist when needed. If you have questions about the scope before going to site send an email to NationalSC@technetpartners.com.\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to **specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n- Any trip charges need to be approved with our scheduling and coordination teams prior to accepting work.\n\nTechnician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot and Restore Offline Network Switch – Raleigh, NC | 00263462 / SA-295155 / 05314215\n\n**Type of Work:** Networking\n\n**Schedule:** October 30, 2026 – 4:00 PM (EDT)\n\n**Site Name &amp; Address:** Hampton Inn and Suites Raleigh Midtown, 1229 Wake Towne Dr, Raleigh, NC 27609, USA\n\n**WO / SA / Case:** WO#: 00263462 / SA#: SA-295155 / Case#: 05314215\n\n**Contact Details:** Site POC: Jeremy DeVault, 407-491-6694 Engineer: TBD | TECHNET Technician: TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Investigate the reported offline Cisco Meraki MS350-24P switch at IDF6.\n- Inspect switch power supply, power connections, and physical status.\n- Inspect network cabling and uplink connectivity to the parent switch HLT-RDURD-350-MDF-CS01.\n- Verify uplink connectivity through parent switch Port 28.\n- Check switch LEDs, power status, and physical connections for any abnormalities.\n- Perform necessary troubleshooting to isolate the cause of the switch outage.\n- Check cabling and uplink connections, reseat connections if necessary, and reboot the switch if required.\n- Restore network connectivity and verify the switch comes back online.\n- Confirm connected network devices and local connectivity are operational.\n- Monitor switch status to ensure it remains online and stable after restoration.\n- Document findings, troubleshooting steps, corrective actions, and any required repairs or equipment replacement.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset &amp; Location:** Cisco Meraki MS350-24P Switch (HLT-RDURD-350-IDF6-DS04-1) – IDF6\n\n- Device Model: Cisco Meraki MS350-24P\n- Serial Number: Q2WP-UMZU-P9NC\n- MAC Address: E0:55:3D:95:C1:38\n- IP Address: 192.168.0.6\n- Parent Device/Switch: HLT-RDURD-350-MDF-CS01\n- Uplink Port: 28\n- Monitoring Source/System: Unknown\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Microsoft Teams installed and available to chat\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of testing Gigabit Ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (Cat5e and Cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T16:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00","latestStart":"2026-10-30T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":8.06839820176667},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793386377627}
