{"job":{"id":20280452,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"DATA REMOTE LINE AUDIT AND SURVEY/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/ MULTIMETER-DIS154935","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852181992 Ticket 11966428<br/><br/>***Dedicated Site Survey****      <br/><br/>Call Frank Martinez at  3852181992  when on site.    <br/><br/>**See attachment \"Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template\" for list of POTS lines to locate***<br/>….................................<br/>Dedicated Site Survey:<br/>MetTel will dispatch a technician to identify and locate all lines listed in Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template<br/>The technician will document the purpose of each line listed as one of the following:<br/>*Voice,<br/>*Elevator,<br/>*Fax,<br/>*Burglar Alarm,<br/>*Fire Alarm,<br/>*Modem,<br/>*Not in Use,<br/>A line should be classified as Not in Use when dial tone is present at the demarcation point (66-block), but no equipment or service is cross-connected to the line.<br/>This information is required to enable MetTel to provide Kindred Healthcare with recommendations regarding which services should be disconnected rather than ported to the MetTel PIAB solution.<br/>….................................<br/>The technician's responsibility is to:<br/>*Locate each line at the demarcation point (66-block).<br/>*Verify and label the correct telephone number with each line.<br/>*Identify and document the line's current use in Column C and D of the Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template workbook.<br/>*Identify and document site readiness comments in Column D of Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template workbook.<br/>*Taking the following photos: demarcation point (66-block), potential location to install the 20\"w x 24\"l backboard and power outlet available for the PIAB.<br/>….................................<br/>Survey Deliverable:<br/>The final deliverable for this site survey will be the completed survey excel sheet with Columns C and D filled in and the photos taken.<br/><br/>***MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/><br/>Technicians must:<br/><br/>Identify the building’s Minimum Point of Entry (MPOE) and describe its location.<br/>Locate the network demarcation point (router/SDWAN/switches) and measure its distance from the MPOE.<br/>Assess LTE signal strength and power availability.<br/>Determine cross-connect cabling needs for alarm panels, elevators, and external antennas.<br/>Confirm presence of A/C power outlet at installation site.<br/>Identify if alarm lines are terminated or require technician work 1 2.<br/>Required Photos<br/>Technicians must take and submit:<br/><br/>Network rack (front and back)<br/>Wall-mounted network cabinets<br/>ISP and telco provider equipment<br/>Alarm panels (closed and open)<br/>DMARC and network room walls<br/>PIAB 66 block with labeled lines<br/>Wireless unit (if on cellular)<br/>Elevator panel<br/>Fax machine and display pad<br/>Signed work order 5 4<br/>-Alarm Panel Coordination<br/>Alarm company technician must be present to place the panel in test mode.<br/>Confirm alarm signal transmission protocols (e.g., Contact ID, SIA, Pulse).<br/>Validate e911 address registration and line status reporting 6 3.<br/>-Documentation & Reporting<br/>Complete the PIAB Site Survey form.<br/>Label all lines and send photos of labels to designated contacts.<br/>Submit findings to MetTel’s Advanced Services Implementation team.<br/>Include any deficiencies or missing details that may require a revisit<br/><br/>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit https://dispatch.bruin.com/ to manually lookup and start the dispatch.<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852181992 Ticket 11966428  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*Dedicated Site Survey\\*\\*\\*\\*   \n  \nCall Frank Martinez at 3852181992 when on site.   \n  \n\\*\\*See attachment \"Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template\" for list of POTS lines to locate\\*\\*\\*  \n….................................  \nDedicated Site Survey:  \nMetTel will dispatch a technician to identify and locate all lines listed in Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template  \nThe technician will document the purpose of each line listed as one of the following:  \n\\*Voice,  \n\\*Elevator,  \n\\*Fax,  \n\\*Burglar Alarm,  \n\\*Fire Alarm,  \n\\*Modem,  \n\\*Not in Use,  \nA line should be classified as Not in Use when dial tone is present at the demarcation point (66-block), but no equipment or service is cross-connected to the line.  \nThis information is required to enable MetTel to provide Kindred Healthcare with recommendations regarding which services should be disconnected rather than ported to the MetTel PIAB solution.  \n….................................  \nThe technician's responsibility is to:  \n\\*Locate each line at the demarcation point (66-block).  \n\\*Verify and label the correct telephone number with each line.  \n\\*Identify and document the line's current use in Column C and D of the Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template workbook.  \n\\*Identify and document site readiness comments in Column D of Kindred Healthcare - PIAB Survey Template workbook.  \n\\*Taking the following photos: demarcation point (66-block), potential location to install the 20\"w x 24\"l backboard and power outlet available for the PIAB.  \n….................................  \nSurvey Deliverable:  \nThe final deliverable for this site survey will be the completed survey excel sheet with Columns C and D filled in and the photos taken.  \n  \n\\*\\*\\*MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n  \nTechnicians must:  \n  \nIdentify the building’s Minimum Point of Entry (MPOE) and describe its location.  \nLocate the network demarcation point (router/SDWAN/switches) and measure its distance from the MPOE.  \nAssess LTE signal strength and power availability.  \nDetermine cross-connect cabling needs for alarm panels, elevators, and external antennas.  \nConfirm presence of A/C power outlet at installation site.  \nIdentify if alarm lines are terminated or require technician work 1 2.  \nRequired Photos  \nTechnicians must take and submit:  \n  \nNetwork rack (front and back)  \nWall-mounted network cabinets  \nISP and telco provider equipment  \nAlarm panels (closed and open)  \nDMARC and network room walls  \nPIAB 66 block with labeled lines  \nWireless unit (if on cellular)  \nElevator panel  \nFax machine and display pad  \nSigned work order 5 4  \n-Alarm Panel Coordination  \nAlarm company technician must be present to place the panel in test mode.  \nConfirm alarm signal transmission protocols (e.g., Contact ID, SIA, Pulse).  \nValidate e911 address registration and line status reporting 6 3.  \n-Documentation &amp; Reporting  \nComplete the PIAB Site Survey form.  \nLabel all lines and send photos of labels to designated contacts.  \nSubmit findings to MetTel’s Advanced Services Implementation team.  \nInclude any deficiencies or missing details that may require a revisit  \n  \nMetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit <https://dispatch.bruin.com/> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":58.6494783354935},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollin