{"job":{"id":20281194,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GTN Technical Staffing","title":"Dispatch Technician - High Point, NC","description":{"html":"<p>***MUST HAVE BACKGROUND CHECK IN THE LAST 24 MONTHS***</p><p>__________________________________________________________</p><p><br></p><p><u>Procedural Requirements (required for payment approval):</u></p><ol><li>Review \"Field Service Site Standards\" prior to visiting site.</li><li>Confirm with your coordinator day of (roughly 1 hour prior to scheduled visit) whether you will be onsite on time or not.</li><li>Confirm with your coordinator when you arrive onsite.</li><li>Must check in and out with the Queue Management Team when arriving onsite and prior to leaving site (contacts listed below).</li><li>SVR document (attached) must be complete and submitted to GTN for every visit</li><li>Check out with your coordinator prior to leaving site (confirm scope complete, if revisit needed, and all documentation is completed and signed, if required.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><u>Scope: </u></p><p><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span><span style=\"color: rgb(18, 51, 76);\">Requesting Tyry'n at High Point. All locations of service listed below. BAU will provide insight for when to go to each site.</span></p><p>Site Locations</p><p>Primary/Main Site:</p><p>English Road</p><p>1717 W English Rd, High Point, NC</p><p>Distance: 0 miles</p><p><br></p><p>Satellite Site 1:</p><p>Brevard Lab</p><p>2137 Brevard Rd, High Point, NC</p><p>Distance from primary site: 4 miles</p><p><br></p><p>Satellite Site 2:</p><p>Elm Warehouse</p><p>1908 S Elm St, High Point, NC</p><p>Distance from primary site: 4 miles</p><p><br></p><p>Satellite Site 3:</p><p>Design CTR</p><p>1823 W English Rd, High Point, NC</p><p>Distance from primary site: 300 ft</p><p><strong><u>Attached SVR must be completed and submitted to GTN on every visit. Technician will need to bring a laptop with them to site to complete the SVR.&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><u>If setting up equipment for an employee, closing notes must include: Employee Name, Device Serial Number, Device Model.</u></p><p><br></p><p>Additional documentation is attached below to assist with the issues you are dealing with onsite.</p><p><br></p><p>The HelpDesk will be available through Teams or Email. If you have been able to access your profile, please be sure to have WhatsApp installed on your phone.</p><p><br></p><p>GTN is your single point of contact for any issues including but not limited to, access, questions, injury, escalation of issues or any work related issue.</p><p>__________________________________________________________</p><p><br></p><p><u>JOB REQUIREMENT for all techs:</u></p><ul><li>Performs trouble shooting, parts replacement, system upgrades, and basic deployments &amp; repair on Client Assets.</li><li>Follows predefined procedures and tasks in everyday activities.</li><li>Provide technical assistance with computer hardware and software</li><li>Track customer issues and resolutions</li><li>Handle tickets in a timely manner</li><li>Experience with Service Now or large enterprise ticketing systems</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></p><ul><li>In good physical condition</li><li>Ability to lift 50-70 pounds</li><li>Ability to walk 10,000 steps in a workday</li><li>Ability to climb a 14-foot ladder</li><li>Ability to work under desks, work units/cubicles and closets</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>TOOL REQUIREMENTS:</u></p><ul><li>Comprehensive hand tool kit for use in the repair and placement of Information Technology equipment and cabling</li><li>Smartphone 100% Charged</li><li>WhatsApp on your phone</li></ul>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*MUST HAVE BACKGROUND CHECK IN THE LAST 24 MONTHS\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nProcedural Requirements (required for payment approval):\n\n1. Review \"Field Service Site Standards\" prior to visiting site.\n2. Confirm with your coordinator day of (roughly 1 hour prior to scheduled visit) whether you will be onsite on time or not.\n3. Confirm with your coordinator when you arrive onsite.\n4. Must check in and out with the Queue Management Team when arriving onsite and prior to leaving site (contacts listed below).\n5. SVR document (attached) must be complete and submitted to GTN for every visit\n6. Check out with your coordinator prior to leaving site (confirm scope complete, if revisit needed, and all documentation is completed and signed, if required.\n\nScope:\n\n﻿Requesting Tyry'n at High Point. All locations of service listed below. BAU will provide insight for when to go to each site.\n\nSite Locations\n\nPrimary/Main Site:\n\nEnglish Road\n\n1717 W English Rd, High Point, NC\n\nDistance: 0 miles\n\nSatellite Site 1:\n\nBrevard Lab\n\n2137 Brevard Rd, High Point, NC\n\nDistance from primary site: 4 miles\n\nSatellite Site 2:\n\nElm Warehouse\n\n1908 S Elm St, High Point, NC\n\nDistance from primary site: 4 miles\n\nSatellite Site 3:\n\nDesign CTR\n\n1823 W English Rd, High Point, NC\n\nDistance from primary site: 300 ft\n\n**Attached SVR must be completed and submitted to GTN on every visit. Technician will need to bring a laptop with them to site to complete the SVR.**\n\nIf setting up equipment for an employee, closing notes must include: Employee Name, Device Serial Number, Device Model.\n\nAdditional documentation is attached below to assist with the issues you are dealing with onsite.\n\nThe HelpDesk will be available through Teams or Email. If you have been able to access your profile, please be sure to have WhatsApp installed on your phone.\n\nGTN is your single point of contact for any issues including but not limited to, access, questions, injury, escalation of issues or any work related issue.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nJOB REQUIREMENT for all techs:\n\n- Performs trouble shooting, parts replacement, system upgrades, and basic deployments &amp; repair on Client Assets.\n- Follows predefined procedures and tasks in everyday activities.\n- Provide technical assistance with computer hardware and software\n- Track customer issues and resolutions\n- Handle tickets in a timely manner\n- Experience with Service Now or large enterprise ticketing systems\n\nPHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n- In good physical condition\n- Ability to lift 50-70 pounds\n- Ability to walk 10,000 steps in a workday\n- Ability to climb a 14-foot ladder\n- Ability to work under desks, work units/cubicles and closets\n\nTOOL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n- Comprehensive hand tool kit for use in the repair and placement of Information Technology equipment and cabling\n- Smartphone 100% Charged\n- WhatsApp on your phone","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-22T08:00","end":"2026-12-22T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":36,"max":288},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":36,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":71.86501867380696},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":105,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-12-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-22T14:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-23T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-24T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-12-24T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-25T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Christmas Eve"},{"start":"2026-12-25T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-26T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Christmas Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1793394996537}
{"job":{"id":20278542,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Hosted VoIP and Starlink Install for Martin Metals Recycling and Pick and Pull of Linden","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP &amp; Data Installation – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>1 Starlink Kit</p>\n<p>1 Voip Corded Phones</p>\n<p>1 Voip Cordless Phone</p>\n<p>1 Router</p>\n<p>Will need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point</p>\n<p>Drill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit</p>\n<p>9/16 in hex socket or wrench</p>\n<p>Marker</p>\n<p>Level</p>\n<p>- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).</p>\n<p>- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.</p>\n<p>- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.</p>\n<p>- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.</p>\n<p>- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.</p>\n<p>- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.</p>\n<p>-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).</p>\n<p>Will need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.</p>\n<p>See example pictures of the mount being used.</p>\n<p>&lt;cutover over to new internet and analog circuit&gt;</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.</li>\n<li>Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached <strong>Time Expectations</strong> sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).</li>\n<li>Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Communication Requirements</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation <strong>24 hours</strong> before the appointment.</li>\n<li>Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.</li>\n<li>Contact support <strong>every 30 minutes</strong>. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>Network/cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill and level</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n<li>Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n<li>Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to install new equipment.</li>\n<li>Complete all tests on the checklist with support.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP &amp; Data Installation – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with analog Telecom and VoIP experience, plus working knowledge of networking and telco standards.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1 Starlink Kit\n\n1 Voip Corded Phones\n\n1 Voip Cordless Phone\n\n1 Router\n\nWill need ladder tall enough to reach mounting point\n\nDrill + 6 mm (1/4 in) drill bit\n\n9/16 in hex socket or wrench\n\nMarker\n\nLevel\n\n\\- Download Starlink App — Use the obstruction tool to find a spot with clear northern sky view (minimal trees/buildings).\n\n\\- Choose location — On exterior wall near roof gable/fascia, over a stud/beam for strength. Allow clearance for dish rotation. Max 4” overhang.\n\n\\- Mark holes — Hold mount level, mark 2 pilot holes directly over a stud.\n\n\\- Drill — Use 6 mm bit. Apply silicone in/around holes.\n\n\\- Attach mount — Secure with lag screws.\n\n\\- Assemble — Remove dish kickstand. Route cable through mast. Attach mast to mount. Plug cable into dish.\n\n-Install dish — Slide mast into wall mount. Rotate for best sky view (use app alignment tool).\n\nWill need to route cable to the dish from the power supply/router location. Seal all penetrations and secure the cable. Leave drip loop at penetration points.\n\nSee example pictures of the mount being used.\n\n&lt;cutover over to new internet and analog circuit&gt;\n\n**Additional Requirements:**\n\n- Cutover to new internet and analog circuit.\n- Complete the installation within the maximum time listed on the attached **Time Expectations** sheet (unless cable runs are required and pre-approved by UGS).\n- Pay increases will only be considered for cable runs with well-documented issues.\n\n**Important:** The scope must be completed according to the Time Expectations sheet. Leaving the site before completion may result in non-payment at UGS’s discretion. Ensure your schedule allows for the full duration of the job.\n\nCommunication Requirements\n\n- Confirm the scheduled time in Field Nation **24 hours** before the appointment.\n- Call in using a hands-free device throughout the installation to receive instructions and provide updates.\n- Contact support **every 30 minutes**. Failure to maintain communication may result in penalties.\n\nRequired Tools &amp; Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- Network/cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill and level\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n- Headphones (for testing paging/SNOM devices)\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws (for wall-mount phones)\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and complete a provider swap. Failure to do so may result in removal from the site and non-payment.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, non-logo shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and documentation attached to the work order.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n- Verify you have all required tools and supplies before departing.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Follow all instructions sent in work order notes or text messages from support.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to install new equipment.\n- Complete all tests on the checklist with support.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T09:00","end":"2026-11-12T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":49.09046866312792},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793395950310}
{"job":{"id":20281380,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"Comcast Circuit Activation & Verizon Circuit Removal","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Business Casual</p>Tools Required:<ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter</li><li>Console cable</li><li>Network cable tester</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Cable labeling materials</li><li>Mobile phone for coordination</li><li>Flashlight (if needed)</li></ul>Scope of Work:<ul><li>Provide onsite ePlus Smart Hands support to connect and activate the agency-supplied <strong>Comcast broadband circuit.</strong></li><li>Connect Comcast broadband to the designated network equipment.</li><li>Verify circuit activation and internet connectivity.</li><li>Coordinate testing and cutover with ePlus/SGNet and onsite personnel.</li><li>Upon successful Comcast validation and approval, disconnect existing <strong>Verizon circuit C1160317.</strong></li><li>Verify network connectivity after the cutover.</li><li>Perform basic troubleshooting and escalate issues as needed.</li><li>Upload completion notes, test results, and photos to Field Nation.</li></ul>Pre-Site Requirements:<ul><li>Check email for required sign-off forms and dispatch instructions.</li><li>Confirm Comcast equipment and circuit are available onsite.</li><li>Verify the Verizon circuit C1160317 is identified for removal.</li><li>Notify SGNet if required information or documentation is missing.</li></ul>On-Site Tasks:<ul><li>Check in to the Field Nation work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact.</li><li>Check in with SGNet before starting work.</li><li>Connect the agency-supplied Comcast broadband circuit.</li><li>Verify WAN and internet connectivity.</li><li>Obtain ePlus/SGNet approval before disconnecting Verizon circuit C1160317.</li><li>Disconnect the existing Verizon circuit after Comcast validation.</li><li>Verify network connectivity following the cutover.</li><li>Take before-and-after pictures.</li><li>Check out of the work order with SGNet.</li></ul>Required On-Site Deliverables:<ul><li>Comcast broadband circuit successfully connected and activated.</li><li>Verified internet connectivity.</li><li>Verizon circuit C1160317 disconnected.</li><li>Post-cutover connectivity test results.</li><li>Before-and-after pictures.</li><li>Completed sign-off form, if provided.</li><li>Detailed Field Nation completion notes and work order checkout.</li></ul>Escalation Process:<ul><li>Contact SGNet for any work order clarification or technical issues.</li><li>Escalate Comcast activation or connectivity issues to SGNet.</li><li>Do not disconnect Verizon C1160317 until Comcast is confirmed operational and approval is received from ePlus/SGNet.</li><li>Do not perform additional work without authorization.</li></ul>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:<ul><li>Contact SGNet for approval before performing additional hours or incurring expenses.</li><li>All additional work must be approved in advance.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\nTools Required:- Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter\n- Console cable\n- Network cable tester\n- Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables\n- Basic hand tools\n- Cable labeling materials\n- Mobile phone for coordination\n- Flashlight (if needed)\n\nScope of Work:- Provide onsite ePlus Smart Hands support to connect and activate the agency-supplied **Comcast broadband circuit.**\n- Connect Comcast broadband to the designated network equipment.\n- Verify circuit activation and internet connectivity.\n- Coordinate testing and cutover with ePlus/SGNet and onsite personnel.\n- Upon successful Comcast validation and approval, disconnect existing **Verizon circuit C1160317.**\n- Verify network connectivity after the cutover.\n- Perform basic troubleshooting and escalate issues as needed.\n- Upload completion notes, test results, and photos to Field Nation.\n\nPre-Site Requirements:- Check email for required sign-off forms and dispatch instructions.\n- Confirm Comcast equipment and circuit are available onsite.\n- Verify the Verizon circuit C1160317 is identified for removal.\n- Notify SGNet if required information or documentation is missing.\n\nOn-Site Tasks:- Check in to the Field Nation work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact.\n- Check in with SGNet before starting work.\n- Connect the agency-supplied Comcast broadband circuit.\n- Verify WAN and internet connectivity.\n- Obtain ePlus/SGNet approval before disconnecting Verizon circuit C1160317.\n- Disconnect the existing Verizon circuit after Comcast validation.\n- Verify network connectivity following the cutover.\n- Take before-and-after pictures.\n- Check out of the work order with SGNet.\n\nRequired On-Site Deliverables:- Comcast broadband circuit successfully connected and activated.\n- Verified internet connectivity.\n- Verizon circuit C1160317 disconnected.\n- Post-cutover connectivity test results.\n- Before-and-after pictures.\n- Completed sign-off form, if provided.\n- Detailed Field Nation completion notes and work order checkout.\n\nEscalation Process:- Contact SGNet for any work order clarification or technical issues.\n- Escalate Comcast activation or connectivity issues to SGNet.\n- Do not disconnect Verizon C1160317 until Comcast is confirmed operational and approval is received from ePlus/SGNet.\n- Do not perform additional work without authorization.\n\nAdditional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:- Contact SGNet for approval before performing additional hours or incurring expenses.\n- All additional work must be approved in advance.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T09:15","end":"2026-11-06T11:15"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58.14890126205475},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYME