{"job":{"id":"5296590439","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tekumo","title":"Tractor Supply  - REG 2 Epson TM-H6000V Receipt Printer Replacement and Barcode Print Validation","description":"<p><strong>REFERENCE MANUALS</strong></p><p>TSC Epson Receipt Printer Replacement - Vendor Copy.pdf (Toshiba technical field support; revised August 2026)</p><p>https://tekumopro-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/g/personal/cparker_tekumo_com/IQBYAmObBs2lQIPHZ9SSY6fDAURELApv3iNAuSoE4xydisQ?e=ePPTXT</p><p>Applicable: Sections 1-4 (EpsonNet Config, printer configuration, installation, checkout); relevant troubleshooting addenda only when required.</p><p><strong>WORK ORDER SUMMARY</strong></p><p>Confirm current UPS delivery, identify the correct REG 2 device, document poor output, and configure/install the one authorized Epson replacement. Complete register-generated receipts, barcode scans and return/gift-receipt workflow checks with store management; complete return and records.</p><p><strong>DEVICE DETAILS</strong></p><p>•  Customer/site: Tractor Supply; store number not supplied - verify onsite. Location: REG 2.</p><p>•  Device: Epson receipt printer; shipped 3AC02068400 (TM-H6000V / MTM 0347-T0V). Existing printer model, asset, serial and MAC: record onsite.</p><p>•  Shipped: 30-OCT-2026 17:31:40; shipment 837942075; outbound UPS 1Z97442R0111850655.</p><p>•  Return UPS: 1Z97442R9039180884; core return expected for authorized failed unit only.</p><p>•  Quantity: one replacement shipment documented; store request for two is NOT authorization to replace two.</p><p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p><p>Windows 11 technician laptop with EpsonNet Config utility (approved Epson download), Ethernet port/adapter and standard patch cable; LAN tester if connectivity fails; normal service toolkit, phone/camera, packaging tape, and access to store management.</p><p><strong>PRIOR TO ARRIVAL - DOCUMENTATION REQUIRED</strong></p><p>•  Check live UPS status using outbound tracking. Shipped does not mean delivered; coordinate visit only when part availability is verified.</p><p>•  Read approved Epson manual, ensure EpsonNet Config is available, and be prepared to record store IP first three octets from a known working printer or approved work-order data.</p><p>•  Bring professional field-service attire, closed-toe shoes, identification where issued, and photo capability.</p><p><strong>UPON ARRIVAL</strong></p><p>•  Check in with Store Manager/MOD; confirm REG 2 and the affected printer, which receipt workflows fail, and approved downtime.</p><p>•  Photograph existing installation, identifying labels, connections and representative incomplete receipt/barcode. Confirm whether a second unit is also affected; do not replace it without authorization.</p><p>•  Inspect and photograph received part/label; verify correct TM-H6000V and compatibility, cabling, power and condition before disturbing working equipment.</p><p><strong>ONSITE SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><p>•  Record old printer identification and existing wiring; protect working cash-drawer, Ethernet and power cables. Do not replace unrelated hardware.</p><p>•  Confirm the one shipped part is correct. If wrong/missing/damaged, photograph and document; DO NOT INSTALL; contact Tekumo for direction.</p><p><strong>EPSON TM-H6000V CONFIGURATION AND REPLACEMENT</strong></p><p>1.  If EpsonNet Config is not installed, install the utility following Section 1. Launch once, accept required prompts, exit and reboot the laptop before configuration.</p><p>2.  Power off the old printer; transfer the paper roll and both ribbons to the new printer per the approved procedure. Document condition and preserve any working accessories.</p><p>3.  Connect a standard Ethernet cable directly from new printer to technician laptop, connect compatible printer power and power on. Open EpsonNet Config, select the connected printer and Configuration.</p><p>4.  In Network &gt; TCP/IP &gt; Basic, set Method to Manual. Obtain actual first three IP octets and gateway subnet from approved work-order data or a known working store device; do not guess. For REG 2, printer IP ends in .47; subnet 255.255.255.0; gateway ends in .1. Transmit configuration.</p><p>5.  Power off new printer when configuration completes. Hold Feed while powering on; release after status/test slip prints. Verify saved IP/subnet/gateway; repeat EpsonNet configuration if incorrect.</p><p>6.  Position replacement beside REG 2. Connect cash drawer, network and power to their correct respective ports; do NOT interchange cash-drawer/network ports. Power on, confirm network link lights and clear error indicators.</p><p>7.  At REG 2, press Alt+Tab to reach green Xenvironment, choose Support &gt; Store Xstore, wait for Shutdown Xstore - Success, then press Start POS (F8) ONCE. Allow Xstore to load fully.</p><p>8.  If Xstore reports printer/JPOS errors or link lights fail, use applicable approved troubleshooting addendum and contact Tekumo/authorized support as required; do not improvise network or switch changes.</p><p><strong>POWER-UP / XSTORE / REGISTER RESTART / VALIDATION</strong></p><p>•  Have manager sign in after Xstore restart; complete a cash transaction, No Sale or Till Summary per manual, confirming receipt printing and cash-drawer operation.</p><p>•  SPECIFIC FAILURE TEST: Print multiple REG 2 receipts including the gift-receipt/return barcode workflow originally failing. Confirm print is full-width, dark, complete, legible and free of missing print areas; scan the printed barcodes in the actual applicable return/gift-receipt workflow with management.</p><p>•  Perform another controlled Xstore restart as appropriate and repeat actual REG 2 print/barcode scan checks. A printer self-test, laptop print or one partial receipt alone does not establish resolution.</p><p>•  Record manager name, which receipts/barcodes were scanned, quantity of successful attempts, and final pass/fail. If barcode scanning still fails, contact Tekumo or authorized Toshiba support BEFORE DEPARTURE.</p><p><strong>CONTACT TEKUMO SUPPORT IF</strong></p><p>•  Part not received, wrong quantity/model, damaged or incompatible; request for second printer cannot be reconciled with one authorized shipment; required setup, IP or link verification fails.</p><p>•  Barcode output remains incomplete/unscannable, printer or cash drawer fails, Xstore/JPOS errors persist, or original failure recurs after repair/restart.</p><p><strong>SUPPORT &amp; ESCALATION</strong></p><p>If support is needed, contact Tekumo at 719-900-4535. Tekumo will inform Toshiba and request that Toshiba contact the technician as soon as possible.</p><p><strong>MANDATORY: If the authorized repair does not correct the original issue, contact Tekumo or authorized Toshiba support before leaving. Record support path/name, approximate time, tests, instructions and disposition. Failure to make required support contact for an unresolved repair may result in non-payment.</strong></p><p><strong>RETURN / RMA PROCESS</strong></p><p>Return ONLY the authorized failed/core printer, not working cables, power adapters, ribbons, mounts, accessories or unrelated devices. Package securely using replacement packaging when practical; apply supplied label, photograph boxed return and tracking 1Z97442R9039180884. Leave package in designated UPS pickup area; do not remove core from site. If label missing, follow manual process via ReturnLabels@toshibagcs.com with SR number, manager name and manager email; document any exception.</p><p><strong>PRIOR TO DEPARTURE - REQUIRED CUSTOM FIELDS</strong></p><p>•  Return Tracking Number: 1Z97442R9039180884; Tracking Number: 1Z97442R0111850655; UPS Status Checked.</p><p>•  Issues/Delays Onsite?; Brief Summary of Duties Completed; Return Reason for part 1; Restore Completed; Materials Used.</p><p>•  Original/replacement printer asset/model/serial/MAC; configured IP and test slip; manager acceptance; Xstore restart, cash drawer, actual receipts, gift/return barcode scans and results.</p><p>•  Support contacted, approximate time, tests and authorized next disposition if unresolved; second-printer scope/authorization notes if relevant.</p><p><strong>COMPLETION NOTES</strong></p><p>Document manager and store number; old/new printer identifiers; scope completed; exact poor-print and barcode-scan before/after findings; printed receipt types and count; configured IP confirmation; Xstore restart; cash drawer; any errors; support interaction if needed; final working/unresolved status; packaging and return tracking.</p><p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p>•  Before photos: REG 2 printer, device label, cable connections, faded/incomplete receipt and failed barcode.</p><p>•  Part/shipping-label photo; replacement printer model/serial label; configuration status/test slip with sensitive information handled appropriately.</p><p>•  After photos: installed printer/cable path, full clear receipt/barcode and operational state; documented successful gift/return barcode scan and manager signoff.</p><p>•  Photo of authorized core boxed with visible return label/tracking, plus completed custom fields; unresolved error evidence and support disposition if applicable.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T09:00","end":"2026-11-02T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":94.5,"max":153},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":94.5,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":16.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $153 (countered: $95) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Su