{"job":{"id":"9424294194","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"SYBEX SUPPORT SERVICES LLC","title":"IT SUPPORT","description":"<p>Need to engage FSO FE on 2/11/2026 &amp; 8AM local time</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Activity regarding :- SFP replacement between between Ethernet1/3 of JANUSWL3123FW502-ICE and Eth1/43 of JANUSWL3123RS502&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>FIELD TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS:</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Hardware:</p><p><br></p><p>• Laptop with ethernet port (RJ45) and serial port (both can be via usb adaptor)</p><p><br></p><p>• The rights to change IP address on laptop</p><p><br></p><p>• Working Console cable, both RJ45 type and mini-usb type</p><p><br></p><p>• Null-modem cable (serial crosscable)</p><p><br></p><p>•Crossover and straight Ethernet cables</p><p><br></p><p>•USB drive 4GB FAT32 formatted is mandatory to have in the activity by FE</p><p><br></p><p>•USB drive 8,16,32GB is optional</p><p><br></p><p>•Basic tool sets (screwdrivers, plyers, wire cutter, hex keys, cable stripper etc.)</p><p><br></p><p>•Cell phone with decent camera and 4G connectivity for console access to remote engineers</p><p><br></p><p>•Decent headphones to have hands free during activities</p><p><br></p><p>•Cable ties and accessories to tidy up cabling activities</p><p><br></p><p>•Portable power bank and charging cable for their phone just in case phone battery goes flat – more as reminder</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Software:</p><p><br></p><p>• SecureCRT</p><p><br></p><p>• Putty</p><p><br></p><p>• Teams</p><p><br></p><p>• Zoom</p><p><br></p><p>• TFTP server/client (TFTP64)</p><p><br></p><p>• InSSIDer</p><p><br></p><p>• Netspot – can download a free version in case need to scan and look for hidden AP above the ceiling etc.</p><p><br></p><p>NOTE: Console access is a mandatory FSO deliverable. Failure to provide working console access due to unavailable or non-functional tools (e.g., laptop, console cable, adapters) will be treated as a Supplier-attributable SLA breach.</p>","isR