{"job":{"id":20284641,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TPX Communications","title":"Install replacement Siver Peak with exact connections as observed upon arrival.","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><p>Install replacement Siver Peak with exact connections as observed upon arrival.</p><p> Document any removed equipment &amp; hand over to customer onsite.</p><p> Any delays or request outside the SOW call 833-294-6642 for approval.</p><p> Need laptop w/ANYDESK, hotspot, console cables, &amp; spare patch cables.</p><p>****************************************************************************************************</p><p><em>\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"</em></p><p><em>\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"</em></p><p><em>Please make sure to mark </em><strong><em>'On My Way</em></strong><em>' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”</em></p><p><em>Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.</em></p><p><em>Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.</em></p><p><em>**If you are calling to </em><strong><em><u>check in</u></em></strong><em><u> </u>for a scheduled work order, please </em><strong><em>press 3</em></strong><em> to leave a message.</em></p><p><em>**If </em><strong><em>after 5pm PST </em></strong><em>for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please </em><strong><em>press 1</em></strong><em> to reach the On-Call team.</em></p><p><em>****************************************************************************************************</em></p><p><strong><u>EXPECTATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check in with <del>*** </del>Support before entering premises</li><li>Call into&nbsp;<del>*********</del>Repair to troubleshoot and resolve issues on site.</li><li>Timely Arrival and Check-in 15mins before schedule time</li><li>Clean jeans and clean polo with no logos</li><li>Always act in a professional manner, as a representative of <del>*** **************</del></li><li>Follow Instructions on site as directed by <del>*** </del>Support</li><li>Follow Instructions given over the phone by&nbsp;<del>*********</del>Repair Support</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li><li>Windows&nbsp;7 or 10&nbsp;Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li><li>Active Email Address</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)</li><li>AnyDesk</li><li>Aeroadmin</li><li>HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li><li>FTP Client</li><li>TFTP Server software</li><li>MircoSIP (SIP call testing-&nbsp;https://www.microsip.org/)</li><li>Wireshark</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING</strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet Patch Cable</li><li>Cisco Console Cable​</li><li>USB to DB9 male serial Cable</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><ul><li>Buttset</li><li>Line man’s test set or analog test set</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool</li><li>Snips</li><li>Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Drill/ Dry wall screws</li><li>4’ ladder</li><li>CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)</li><li>Pre-made crossover cables</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors</li><li>Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>PRE-SITE WORK</u></p><ul><li>Acknowledge you have read and understand the Scope Of Work and its requirements</li><li>Print a copy of this scope of work and bring it to site</li><li>Call <del>*** </del>Support with any question or clarification about the Scope of Work</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>ON SITE WORK</u></p><ul><li>Check In on the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Introduce yourself as representative of <del>*** **************</del></li><li>Call <del>*** </del>Support&nbsp;to check in @ <del>************ ******</del> entering premises</li><li>Check in with the on-site contact and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Call into <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*********</del></span>Repair at <del>**** *** **** **** ******* </del></li><li>Troubleshoot and resolve the repair issues on site.</li><li>Upload pictures of equipment powered up</li><li>Upload pictures of cable connections on devices&nbsp;</li><li>Upload a picture of speed test results from Laptop</li><li>Clean-up work materials from install (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)</li><li>Call <del>*** </del> Support to check out @ <del>************* </del>If after 5pm PST, press <strong>option 3</strong> leave a message.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>POST-SITE WORK</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm deliverables are complete</li><li>Enter Close out notes into Order</li><li>Enter <del>*** </del>Release Code (Given by the <del>*** </del>Support at the time of close out)</li><li>Check out in Field Nation Portal provide full detailed notes on what was done on site.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site @ <del>************</del></li><li>DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform out of the scope work, call <del>***</del> Support.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY</u></strong></p><ul><li>Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling <del>************</del>. If approved, the Buyer <del>**** ***************</del> will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\nInstall replacement Siver Peak with exact connections as observed upon arrival.\n\n Document any removed equipment &amp; hand over to customer onsite.\n\n Any delays or request outside the SOW call 833-294-6642 for approval.\n\n Need laptop w/ANYDESK, hotspot, console cables, &amp; spare patch cables.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"*\n\n*\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"*\n\n*Please make sure to mark* ***'On My Way****' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”*\n\n*Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.*\n\n*Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.*\n\n*\\*\\*If you are calling to* ***check in*** *for a scheduled work order, please* ***press 3*** *to leave a message.*\n\n*\\*\\*If* ***after 5pm PST*** *for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please* ***press 1*** *to reach the On-Call team.*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**EXPECTATIONS**\n\n- Check in with \\*\\*\\* Support before entering premises\n- Call into \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Repair to troubleshoot and resolve issues on site.\n- Timely Arrival and Check-in 15mins before schedule time\n- Clean jeans and clean polo with no logos\n- Always act in a professional manner, as a representative of \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Follow Instructions on site as directed by \\*\\*\\* Support\n- Follow Instructions given over the phone by \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Repair Support\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n- Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n- Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n- Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP**\n\n- Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)\n- AnyDesk\n- Aeroadmin\n- HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n- FTP Client\n- TFTP Server software\n- MircoSIP (SIP call testing- <https://www.microsip.org/>)\n- Wireshark\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING**\n\n- Ethernet Patch Cable\n- Cisco Console Cable​\n- USB to DB9 male serial Cable\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\n- Buttset\n- Line man’s test set or analog test set\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool\n- Snips\n- Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks\n- Tone Generator and Wand\n- Drill/ Dry wall screws\n- 4’ ladder\n- CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)\n- Pre-made crossover cables\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors\n- Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)\n\nPRE-SITE WORK\n\n- Acknowledge you have read and understand the Scope Of Work and its requirements\n- Print a copy of this scope of work and bring it to site\n- Call \\*\\*\\* Support with any question or clarification about the Scope of Work\n\nON SITE WORK\n\n- Check In on the Field Nation Portal\n- Introduce yourself as representative of \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Call \\*\\*\\* Support to check in @ \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* entering premises\n- Check in with the on-site contact and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal\n- Call into \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Repair at \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Troubleshoot and resolve the repair issues on site.\n- Upload pictures of equipment powered up\n- Upload pictures of cable connections on devices\n- Upload a picture of speed test results from Laptop\n- Clean-up work materials from install (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)\n- Call \\*\\*\\*  Support to check out @ \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* If after 5pm PST, press **option 3** leave a message.\n\n**POST-SITE WORK**\n\n- Confirm deliverables are complete\n- Enter Close out notes into Order\n- Enter \\*\\*\\* Release Code (Given by the \\*\\*\\* Support at the time of close out)\n- Check out in Field Nation Portal provide full detailed notes on what was done on site.\n\n **ESCALATIONS**\n\n- Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site @ \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform out of the scope work, call \\*\\*\\* Support.\n\n**ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY**\n\n- Parking expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App.\n\n- Buyer \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* does not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by calling \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. If approved the Buyer \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.\n\n- Buyer \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. If approved the Buyer \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.\n\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. If approved, the Buyer \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T06:00","end":"2026-11-05T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.92650623488999},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793623625561}
{"job":{"id":20284684,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The InSite Group","title":"Vanguard Security Device Install (Two Person Install)","description":{"html":"<p>The assignment is to install Vanguard security equipment and devices in a Verizon. <strong>Each location will require two (2) installers. You will need to provider your own helper.</strong></p>\n<p>The Verizon team will be uninstalling items for a store reset the night before each phase, and the assigned techs will install them in their new position the next morning.</p>\n<p><strong>Once you accept the work order, if you have not completed installs for this client, for us, you will need to provide an email address and complete a certification quiz to prove you have read and understand the instructions. There will also be an invite sent for a training session on Teams so that my team can walk through the scope with you to insure you fully understand the scope and requirements. If both of these are not completed, you will be removed from the work order.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<p>• Upon accepting this work order, installer must provide an email address so that a teams meeting can be scheduled for a live training session, and after the session the tech will be provided with a link to a certification quiz that must be completed before arriving on site. If not completed prior to day of install you will not be permitted on site.</p>\n<p>• This scope document must be printed off and brought with you. If you don't have it the manager will turn you away and you will not be paid for the day. The manager must sign off on this document to show that you brought it with you.</p>\n<p>• Installer must also have either printed off install instructions with them, or loaded to a mobile device for review during the install.</p>\n<p>• If the MOD feels that you have not properly reviewed the install guides and are not qualified for the install they have the authority to remove you from the site, so make sure you review the attached install guides and video links.</p>\n<p>• Job will require basic hand tools to complete, there are a few specialty screwdrivers required and the store has these in their toolkit. You may use power tools to install devices, but final tightening must be done by hand to avoid over tightening so that the staff is able to remove devices for future change outs.</p>\n<p>• Once you arrive on site, call your project manager to check in before walking into the store. Contact is James Thompson, 865-314-3958.</p>\n<p>• After checking in with PM, check in with the on site manager. Explain that you are there to reinstall the Vanguard Security Devices. They will provide you with a planogram and show you where the devices have been stored during the reset. After this you may not ask the manager or store team any questions regarding the install steps.</p>\n<p>• All other questions and issues must be addressed with your PM. So as you have questions, step outside and call James Thompson.</p>\n<p>• Take before photos showing the provided devices and the tables you are directed to.</p>\n<p>• Follow the planogram provided by the manager and adhere to the provided install guides/videos to install all devices.</p>\n<p>• At each store there will be approximately 54 devices, the following devices are what to expect on average. The exact total will vary from store to store:</p>\n<p>- <strong>Titan L2QD</strong>: 9 per store (Standard) 36-40 per store (High Security)</p>\n<p>- https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-titan-l2qd/</p>\n<p>- <strong>CR338</strong>: 34-37 per store (Standard), 6 per store (High Security)</p>\n<p>- https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-cr361/</p>\n<p>- <strong>Titan Watch</strong>: 7- 9 Per store - scan QR code in the install guide below</p>\n<p>- <strong>Encores</strong>: 1 - 2 per store - https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-encore/</p>\n<p>• Once all devices are installed, take photos of the tables showing completed work.</p>\n<p>• Upload all photos, sign off sheet, and signed Scope of Work document.</p>\n<p>• Call your PM to check out before leaving the site.</p>\n<p><strong>Install Dates:</strong></p>\n<p>The install dates are predetermined and are firm. You cannot change the date!</p>\n<p><strong>Install Days/Hours:</strong></p>\n<p>The install times are predetermined and are firm. You must be onsite at the scheduled time.</p>\n<p><strong>Estimated Time On Site:</strong></p>\n<p>4 to 6 hours - Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.</p>\n<p><strong>Additional Information:</strong></p>\n<p>1. The scope I provide is the most current information we have been provided and is subject to minor adjustments by the Project Manager as new information is received. The PM will provide you with the finalized information, and tell you what the communication, documentation, and photo requirements are for this assignment.</p>\n<p>2. Please make sure you have all of the necessary tools/equipment needed for the assignment.</p>\n<p>3. All deliverables (Before Photos, Completion Photos, and Sign Off) must be submitted in full and approved prior to being paid for the assignment.</p>\n<p>4. Approximate Hours to Complete is an estimate based on past jobs of similar scope. Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.</p>\n<p>5. Any fees for mileage or tolls need to be discussed and approved in advance or they will be denied.</p>","markdown":"The assignment is to install Vanguard security equipment and devices in a Verizon. **Each location will require two (2) installers. You will need to provider your own helper.**\n\nThe Verizon team will be uninstalling items for a store reset the night before each phase, and the assigned techs will install them in their new position the next morning.\n\n**Once you accept the work order, if you have not completed installs for this client, for us, you will need to provide an email address and complete a certification quiz to prove you have read and understand the instructions. There will also be an invite sent for a training session on Teams so that my team can walk through the scope with you to insure you fully understand the scope and requirements. If both of these are not completed, you will be removed from the work order.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n• Upon accepting this work order, installer must provide an email address so that a teams meeting can be scheduled for a live training session, and after the session the tech will be provided with a link to a certification quiz that must be completed before arriving on site. If not completed prior to day of install you will not be permitted on site.\n\n• This scope document must be printed off and brought with you. If you don't have it the manager will turn you away and you will not be paid for the day. The manager must sign off on this document to show that you brought it with you.\n\n• Installer must also have either printed off install instructions with them, or loaded to a mobile device for review during the install.\n\n• If the MOD feels that you have not properly reviewed the install guides and are not qualified for the install they have the authority to remove you from the site, so make sure you review the attached install guides and video links.\n\n• Job will require basic hand tools to complete, there are a few specialty screwdrivers required and the store has these in their toolkit. You may use power tools to install devices, but final tightening must be done by hand to avoid over tightening so that the staff is able to remove devices for future change outs.\n\n• Once you arrive on site, call your project manager to check in before walking into the store. Contact is James Thompson, 865-314-3958.\n\n• After checking in with PM, check in with the on site manager. Explain that you are there to reinstall the Vanguard Security Devices. They will provide you with a planogram and show you where the devices have been stored during the reset. After this you may not ask the manager or store team any questions regarding the install steps.\n\n• All other questions and issues must be addressed with your PM. So as you have questions, step outside and call James Thompson.\n\n• Take before photos showing the provided devices and the tables you are directed to.\n\n• Follow the planogram provided by the manager and adhere to the provided install guides/videos to install all devices.\n\n• At each store there will be approximately 54 devices, the following devices are what to expect on average. The exact total will vary from store to store:\n\n\\- **Titan L2QD**: 9 per store (Standard) 36-40 per store (High Security)\n\n\\- <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-titan-l2qd/>\n\n\\- **CR338**: 34-37 per store (Standard), 6 per store (High Security)\n\n\\- <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-cr361/>\n\n\\- **Titan Watch**: 7- 9 Per store - scan QR code in the install guide below\n\n\\- **Encores**: 1 - 2 per store - <https://www.vanguardprotexglobal.com/verizon-directory/verizon-ng/verizon-encore/>\n\n• Once all devices are installed, take photos of the tables showing completed work.\n\n• Upload all photos, sign off sheet, and signed Scope of Work document.\n\n• Call your PM to check out before leaving the site.\n\n**Install Dates:**\n\nThe install dates are predetermined and are firm. You cannot change the date!\n\n**Install Days/Hours:**\n\nThe install times are predetermined and are firm. You must be onsite at the scheduled time.\n\n**Estimated Time On Site:**\n\n4 to 6 hours - Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.\n\n**Additional Information:**\n\n1\\. The scope I provide is the most current information we have been provided and is subject to minor adjustments by the Project Manager as new information is received. The PM will provide you with the finalized information, and tell you what the communication, documentation, and photo requirements are for this assignment.\n\n2\\. Please make sure you have all of the necessary tools/equipment needed for the assignment.\n\n3\\. All deliverables (Before Photos, Completion Photos, and Sign Off) must be submitted in full and approved prior to being paid for the assignment.\n\n4\\. Approximate Hours to Complete is an estimate based on past jobs of similar scope. Your work pace, attention to detail, and preparedness will greatly determine how quickly you finish the install.\n\n5\\. Any fees for mileage or tolls need to be discussed and approved in advance or they will be denied.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T06:00","end":"2026-11-03T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":600,"max":600},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":57.95566024484311},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Nov 3, 6:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 3, Wed, Nov 4, Thu, Nov 5, Fri, Nov 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Gym (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793624168899}
{"job":{"id":"8480457837","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Trinity Lower School","description":"Survey Epik Wizard:<br><br>Contact Project Manager Scott Houston for instructions and support if you have any Questions 7143503455<br><br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1.\tTECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2.\tCheck in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3.\tUpon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the Survey, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>4.\tFollow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>5.\tBefore departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>6.\tOnce your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br><br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set<br>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-30T12:00","end":"2026-10-30T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":18.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 10/30/2026, 12:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Survey Epik"},{"start":"2026-10-30T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-10-30T17:15:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T20:15:00.000Z","summary":"Dana ortoped"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Ass