{"job":{"id":20285711,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"STAAR Alert","title":"Service Description: Installation of 4 PontoSense Silver Shield Sensors","description":{"html":"<strong>Job Overview</strong><p>We are seeking a qualified field technician to install four (4) <strong>PontoSense Silver Shield</strong> sensors at the customer site. Each sensor takes approximately 15 minutes to install with proper planning. Total estimated field time is under 1.5 to 2 hours, including testing and site walkthrough.</p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW)</strong><ol><li><strong>Pre-Installation Planning &amp; Placement Check</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review room layouts to identify optimal sensor mounting locations prior to installation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure a standard power outlet is within reach of each planned sensor location.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Mounting the Sensors</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Using a tape measure, measure exactly <strong>62 inches (approx. 5 feet 2 inches)</strong> up from the floor to locate the center/top mounting position on the wall.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Smooth Surfaces (Drywall, Smooth Wood, Painted Walls):</strong> Use the pre-applied 3M adhesive backing on the sensor. Ensure the surface is clean and dry, press firmly, and hold for 30 seconds.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Textured / Un-smooth Surfaces:</strong> Use the included screw-mount kit to secure the sensor base safely to the wall.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Powering On &amp; App Activation</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Plug each sensor into the provided power supply and outlet.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Open the designated mobile application on your mobile device.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect each sensor to the <strong>customer’s 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi network</strong> following the in-app instructions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Activate and calibrate the <strong>Fall Detection feature</strong> within the mobile app for each installed unit.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Testing &amp; Verification</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify that all 4 sensors show as <strong>Active / Online</strong> in the mobile application.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Perform a test run in the mobile app to confirm fall detection signals are transmitting properly.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Site Wrap-Up &amp; Checkout</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Clean up all packaging material, screw debris, and adhesive backings.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Walk the customer/site contact through the completed installation if present.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Capture required deliverables (photos/signatures) on the Field Nation app before checking out.</li></ul><strong>Required Tools &amp; Materials</strong><ul><li><strong>Provided in Kit:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">4x PontoSense Silver Shield Sensors (with 3M backing)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power supplies &amp; cables</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screw mounting kits</li><li><strong>Technician to Bring:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tape measure</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hand drill &amp; drill bits / screwdriver (for screw-mount scenarios)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Surface cleaning wipes / alcohol pads (to prepare adhesive surfaces)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mobile smartphone with data connection and capability to download/run the installation app</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Customer Wi-Fi credentials (should be provided on-site or in work order notes)</li></ul><strong>Required Checkout Deliverables (Photos)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>Photo 1–4:</strong> Close-up photo of each installed sensor mounted at the 62-inch height mark.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Photo 5:</strong> Screenshot or photo from the mobile app showing all 4 sensors configured, connected to Wi-Fi, and showing \"Online/Active\" status.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Photo 6:</strong> Work order signature / sign-off sheet (if applicable).</li></ul><strong>Pro-Tips Included for the Tech:</strong><ul><li><strong>Adhesive Tip:</strong> Clean the wall surface with an alcohol wipe before using 3M tape—dust prevents proper adhesion over time.</li><li><strong>Wi-Fi Tip:</strong> Ensure the customer's 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi network password is ready prior to beginning the app setup process.</li></ul><p><br></p>Summary of Placement Requirements<ul><li><strong>Mounting Height:</strong> <strong>62 inches (~5 ft 2 in / ~1.57 m)</strong> from the floor to the top/center of the unit. This height ensures the 60-degree radar beam accurately covers the human body zone from head to floor without blind spots.</li><li><strong>Placement Angle:</strong> Ensure the front face of the sensor maintains a <strong>30-degree downward tilt</strong> (the housing/mount handles this angle).</li><li><strong>Location:</strong> Best mounted in a corner or along a clear wall facing toward the main area of the room. Avoid placing it directly behind large metal objects or heavy obstacles that could block the mmWave radar.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Job Overview**We are seeking a qualified field technician to install four (4) **PontoSense Silver Shield** sensors at the customer site. Each sensor takes approximately 15 minutes to install with proper planning. Total estimated field time is under 1.5 to 2 hours, including testing and site walkthrough.\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW)**1. **Pre-Installation Planning &amp; Placement Check**\n\n- Review room layouts to identify optimal sensor mounting locations prior to installation.\n- Ensure a standard power outlet is within reach of each planned sensor location.\n\n1. **Mounting the Sensors**\n\n- Using a tape measure, measure exactly **62 inches (approx. 5 feet 2 inches)** up from the floor to locate the center/top mounting position on the wall.\n- **Smooth Surfaces (Drywall, Smooth Wood, Painted Walls):** Use the pre-applied 3M adhesive backing on the sensor. Ensure the surface is clean and dry, press firmly, and hold for 30 seconds.\n- **Textured / Un-smooth Surfaces:** Use the included screw-mount kit to secure the sensor base safely to the wall.\n\n1. **Powering On &amp; App Activation**\n\n- Plug each sensor into the provided power supply and outlet.\n- Open the designated mobile application on your mobile device.\n- Connect each sensor to the **customer’s 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi network** following the in-app instructions.\n- Activate and calibrate the **Fall Detection feature** within the mobile app for each installed unit.\n\n1. **Testing &amp; Verification**\n\n- Verify that all 4 sensors show as **Active / Online** in the mobile application.\n- Perform a test run in the mobile app to confirm fall detection signals are transmitting properly.\n\n1. **Site Wrap-Up &amp; Checkout**\n\n- Clean up all packaging material, screw debris, and adhesive backings.\n- Walk the customer/site contact through the completed installation if present.\n- Capture required deliverables (photos/signatures) on the Field Nation app before checking out.\n\n**Required Tools &amp; Materials**- **Provided in Kit:**\n- 4x PontoSense Silver Shield Sensors (with 3M backing)\n- Power supplies &amp; cables\n- Screw mounting kits\n- **Technician to Bring:**\n- Tape measure\n- Hand drill &amp; drill bits / screwdriver (for screw-mount scenarios)\n- Surface cleaning wipes / alcohol pads (to prepare adhesive surfaces)\n- Mobile smartphone with data connection and capability to download/run the installation app\n- Customer Wi-Fi credentials (should be provided on-site or in work order notes)\n\n**Required Checkout Deliverables (Photos)**- \\[ \\] **Photo 1–4:** Close-up photo of each installed sensor mounted at the 62-inch height mark.\n- \\[ \\] **Photo 5:** Screenshot or photo from the mobile app showing all 4 sensors configured, connected to Wi-Fi, and showing \"Online/Active\" status.\n- \\[ \\] **Photo 6:** Work order signature / sign-off sheet (if applicable).\n\n**Pro-Tips Included for the Tech:**- **Adhesive Tip:** Clean the wall surface with an alcohol wipe before using 3M tape—dust prevents proper adhesion over time.\n- **Wi-Fi Tip:** Ensure the customer's 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi network password is ready prior to beginning the app setup process.\n\nSummary of Placement Requirements- **Mounting Height:** **62 inches (~5 ft 2 in / ~1.57 m)** from the floor to the top/center of the unit. This height ensures the 60-degree radar beam accurately covers the human body zone from head to floor without blind spots.\n- **Placement Angle:** Ensure the front face of the sensor maintains a **30-degree downward tilt** (the housing/mount handles this angle).\n- **Location:** Best mounted in a corner or along a clear wall facing toward the main area of the room. Avoid placing it directly behind large metal objects or heavy obstacles that could block the mmWave radar.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T10:00","end":"2026-11-13T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":8.948405269271904},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 3, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 3, Wed, Nov 4, Thu, Nov 5, Fri, Nov 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 trinity Modular Building (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793631713172}
{"job":{"id":20285845,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"PM7 install residential","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>DETAILED SOW-RESIDENTIAL</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Description:&nbsp;PM7 Equipment Installation</strong></p>\n<p>Type of Appointment: Installation</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech Appointment request: HH: 32808 Name: Jonathan Bell Phone Number: <del>**********</del> Email:<del>*************************</del> Time Zone: 12pmEST Requested by: Maria- comms agent Rolando</p>\n<p>Upon arrival, you are required to call 55Blue Support before beginning any work.</p>\n<p>This installation should not take longer than <strong>2 hours</strong>. If you anticipate exceeding the 2‑hour window, you must contact Support to explain the reason for the extended time before proceeding.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Once tech arrives home, please greet the member :&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Installation guides have been attached to help technician identify equipment. Every home normally has 1 FM device and 1 PM7 device per TV.</li>\n<li>&nbsp;Tech should call our Quality Control Agent will be helping remotely while on the phone. Any questions regarding rewards points/other issue that the member has, will be able to assist over the phone.</li>\n<li>The agent assigned to this HH:</li>\n<li>If agent is not available, please have them call<del>************</del>&nbsp;(our main line) and mention they are a field tech, ask to be transferred to a QC agent to complete a maintenance call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Any questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li>\n<li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work.&nbsp;&nbsp;We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Check In Steps</strong>&nbsp;(<u>please follow order</u>)</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check In via FE Portal</li>\n<li>Check In with Netfor at&nbsp;&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)</li>\n<li>Complete installation per SOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by&nbsp;Netfor.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who requested the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Check out Steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NOTE:&nbsp;<u>*** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER ***</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li>\n<li>Check out with Netfor at&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NOTE:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Failure to call Netfor to check in or out</strong>&nbsp;could result in 25% withdrawn from payment.&nbsp;<strong>Failure to arrive on time</strong>&nbsp;can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures</strong>&nbsp;within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.</li>\n<li><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p>\n<p>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)</li>\n<li>Basic IT Tools</li>\n<li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li>\n<li>Cat5e Cabling</li>\n<li>ladder</li>\n<li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li>\n<li>Copy of work order and job information</li>\n<li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long pants</li>\n<li>Collared shirt</li>\n<li>Netfor name badge</li>\n<li>Close toe shoes</li>\n<li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li>\n<li>Pictures of area before working</li>\n<li>Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed/troubleshot</li>\n<li>Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**DETAILED SOW-RESIDENTIAL**\n\n**Description: PM7 Equipment Installation**\n\nType of Appointment: Installation\n\nTech Appointment request: HH: 32808 Name: Jonathan Bell Phone Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Email:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Time Zone: 12pmEST Requested by: Maria- comms agent Rolando\n\nUpon arrival, you are required to call 55Blue Support before beginning any work.\n\nThis installation should not take longer than **2 hours**. If you anticipate exceeding the 2‑hour window, you must contact Support to explain the reason for the extended time before proceeding.\n\n- Once tech arrives home, please greet the member :\n- Installation guides have been attached to help technician identify equipment. Every home normally has 1 FM device and 1 PM7 device per TV.\n- Tech should call our Quality Control Agent will be helping remotely while on the phone. Any questions regarding rewards points/other issue that the member has, will be able to assist over the phone.\n- The agent assigned to this HH:\n- If agent is not available, please have them call\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (our main line) and mention they are a field tech, ask to be transferred to a QC agent to complete a maintenance call.\n\nAny questions or issues, please contact your Field Service Coordinator (see Work Order Manager section) as soon as possible.\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.\n\n**Check In Steps** (please follow order)\n\n1. Check In via FE Portal\n2. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1 (ask for your Work Order Manager listed on the Work Order)\n3. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who requested the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n\n**Check out Steps**\n\n1. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n\n- **NOTE: \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER \\*\\*\\***\n\n1. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n2. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n\n- **NOTE:** **Failure to call Netfor to check in or out** could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. **Failure to arrive on time** can also result in 20% withdrawn from payment.\n- **NOTE: Failure to upload documents and pictures** within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.\n- **REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).**\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Cat5e Cabling\n- ladder\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- Pictures of area before working\n- Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed/troubleshot\n- Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T12:00","end":"2026-11-05T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":98},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":36.6251006273557},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-1