{"job":{"id":"2732151171","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install Printer (1 Technician)","description":"# SCOPE OF WORK<br>- Install the delivered Xerox VersaLink B415/DN multifunction printer.<br>- Include the additional 550 sheet paper tray and accessories.<br>- Location: Specified AT&amp;T location.<br>- Coordinate with the onsite contact for access to the floor 1 store room.<br>- Ensure installation is scheduled with at least 2 business days' notice to allow for potential rescheduling.<br><br># REQUIRED MATERIALS<br>- 1 Xerox VersaLink B415/DN multifunction printer<br>- Additional 550 sheet paper tray<br>- Accessories<br><br># ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS<br>- Install the Xerox VersaLink B415/DN multifunction printer and additional 550 sheet paper tray in the designated store room on floor 1.<br>- Coordinate scheduling to ensure at least 2 business days between the confirmed appointment time and the notice of installation.<br><br>NOTES<br>=====<br>Installation is for 1 printer and its accessories with a requirement for 2 business days between the scheduled time and the notice of installation to accommodate rescheduling.<br><br>Scope of Work:<br><br> <br><br>****MUST READ INSTRUCTION DOC*****<br><br> <br><br>Tech’s are to unbox and assemble printer and accessories (sheet tray/printer stand)<br><br> <br><br>Scope of Work:<br><br>- Unpack/Install printer<br><br>- Power on<br><br>- Menu set-up (English language)<br><br>- Print test page for printers<br><br>- Make a copy for multi-function<br><br>- Pull a dynamic IP address (to verify active data drop) - Printers are to remain in DHCP. <br><br>- Techs are not responsible for putting printers on AT&amp;T Network; that is done internally.<br><br>- Dispose of garbage<br><br> <br><br>Once the printer is setup and tested, tech will instruct site POC to contact ATT/Xerox support to remotely configure the printer and our job is complete.<br><br> <br><br>If the store you are working at is located in one of the following states. There is no need to verify active data drop via DHCP.<br><br>(AL, LA, FL, MS, GA, NC, KY &amp; TN)<br><br> <br><br>Scope of Work:<br><br>- Unpack/Install printer<br><br>- Power on<br><br>- Menu set-up (English language)<br><br>- Print test page for printers<br><br>- Make a copy for multi-function<br><br>- Dispose of garbage<br><br>-Job Complete<br><br> <br><br> <br><br>Tooling List:<br><br>    Laptop w/ AC adapter<br>    Smart Phone with ability to take photos and Hot Spot functionality<br>    Cisco Console Cable<br>    Cat6e patch cables for testing<br>    Basic Hand Tools<br>    Cat6e cable tester<br>    Toner and wand<br>    RJ45 modular ends <br><br>  <br><br>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out,otherwise they will not be approved.<br><br> <br><br>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate,subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”. All site aborts MUST be approved by CTS.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":95},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $95 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793633756162}
{"job":{"id":20264982,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Audio System Troubleshooting -  audio, upstairs office area has no audio","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">IMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 24vDC / 70vAC audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">• Required Tools: LIFT IS REQUIRED FOR AM SCHEDULED VISIT BEFORE STORE OPENS 20Ft Ceilings</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Wired headphones 3.5mm Wired. MUST HAVE</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Multi Meter - MUST HAVE</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o 66/110 block punch tool - MUST HAVE</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Alligator clip leads</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Toner and probe kit</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Self-powered buttset</span></p><p>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">Scope of Work: Valcom2003 (24vDC) speaker run to the sales floor needs to be traced back to the electrical room and TAGGED Power or Audio (orange or blue). We also need to know the terminations of both AMPS documented.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room and collect PICTURES of the following: (Should always be the very first thing you do on every call!)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o In electrical room identify all Valcom/RDL equipment cabling.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o In electrical room identify all TOA BG2120 equipment cabling.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Volume control switches located throughout the store.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o At least 2 different speakers.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">• Objective of visit:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Verify quality of music going into the Valcom 2003 (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Verify quality of music going out the Valcom 2003 Speaker connection (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Document (pictures) of all connections on the Amplifier equipment but do not remove or change any cabling until you have been instructed to and have tagged the connections in the event, they need to be put back.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Trace and Tag one speaker line from sales floor that is not working (VALCOM 1020C) back to the Electrical room and tag both pairs.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Verify VP4124 power supply in the electrical room has 24vDC. (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Verify on the ceiling speaker in the run of non working speakers have 24vDC power.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Verify on the ceiling speaker in the run of non working speakers have audio over the blue audio pair. (using headphones)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">• Other Instructions:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Valcom 2003 has a 50pin connector that is cabled back to the 66 block. We need to document that 66 block from a side and front view to help us identify the color codes of the cables and how they are cross connected to the solution.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">(Link of Valcom 50pin: )</span></p><p>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9d9t/oSFOt_dcOLJ2G5T5PpWBrswYc5CqYFw6d1CwBhV9p00</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o VP4124 power supply has 3 channels of power. Under 2Amp connection check the (+ Black) (- Red) with your meter set to DC Voltage. It should be with in 10% of 24v.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">(Link of VP4124: ) </span>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9d8H/VR61J0LSujHq9DLmHi8S8nxWnfhOWPVVxb00Qbq948U</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Ceiling speaker (Valcom 1020C style) has 2 pairs of wires. Should be Orange for power side, and blue for the audio side. Keep in mind if anyone repaired the cabling colors may have changed so look at the back of the speakers board its printed. We need to know is this non working chain getting 24v DC on the pair (orange). We also need to know if you, with aligator clips, hook up to the audio (BLUE BLUE BLUE.. non voltage side or you get shocked) and connect it to your 3.5mm headphone jack. (google the wiring of your headphone you will see the Tip is normally left speaker, and one of the Base sleaves will be the Com..) We want to know if you hear music. TONER WAND WILL NOT HEAR THIS KIND OF AUDIO, it only hears 70V. But if we dont have power or we dont have audio at this dead speaker, we need to trace that speaker back to the electrical room to ensure the wire isnt cut!</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">(Link of Valcom 1020C Speaker Wires: )</span></p><p>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9djN/2qIv1t4VjRFRVy.vdn.mOdbwLDQ6tNOmW1eMlbbtTog</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">o Please complete all Speaker work requiring access to the sales floor with a lift first. I will set the time on this case out for 4-6hrs. Once we have finished the lift work and store opens we will start to use the info collected to trace out the 66 block. Start with Speaker Power and Speaker audio on a non working line. No power, trace the orange, no audio trace the blue, no anything on either trace them both till you can safely tag the cabling coming down to the 66 block or power supply in the electrical room.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: 14px;\">• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at 800-282-7928, Option 3, Option 5 for further audio troubleshooting.</span></p><p> </p><p><em>Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.</em></p><p><strong>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</strong></p><p><strong>Each site visit will require its own work order.</strong></p><p><strong>If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</strong></p><p><em>Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.</em></p><p>All NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2.  <strong><u>ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support</u></strong>.</p><ul><li> A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.<ul><li> #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.</li><li>#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.</li><li>#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.</li><li>#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><p>• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat</p><p>• Laptop</p><p>• USB to serial connector</p><p>• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html</p><p>• Putty</p><p>• NULL Modem cable</p><p>• Ethernet cable</p><p>• Laptop Power pack</p><p>• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet</p><p>• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30</p><p>• Flash light</p><p>• Digital Volt Meter</p><p>• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/</p><p>• Zoom installed on Techs Phone</p><p>• Velcro Straps</p><p>• X-over cable</p><p>• Standard screwdriver and security bits</p><p>• Thermal paste</p><p>• Alcohol Wipes</p><p>• 9 pin serial cable</p><strong>Reimbursement Rates:</strong>Cabling Materials<ul><li>Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.20 per ft</strong></li><li>Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: <strong>$0.29 per ft</strong></li></ul>Hardware<ul><li>Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: <strong>$9.00 each</strong></li></ul>Patch Cables<ul><li>1 ft: <strong>$3.50</strong></li><li>3 ft: <strong>$2.00</strong></li><li>5 ft: <strong>$4.50</strong></li><li>10 ft: <strong>$6.50</strong></li></ul>Cable Management<ul><li>Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): <strong>$2.00 per drop</strong></li></ul>Cabling Job Requirements<ul><li>All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.</li><li>Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.</li><li>All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Call Support to check in. <del>*** *********** ************* </del><del>*** *** ****</del> and confirm before leaving site. Support representative&#39;s name will be required. If no answer call <del>**** ******* ** ************* ****** **</del></li><li>Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:</li><li>Record the client employee&#39;s First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.</li><li>Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong> </p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required  </li><li>Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance  </li><li>Background check is required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts as representing<del>********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment  </li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire  </li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nIMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 24vDC / 70vAC audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.\n\n• Required Tools: LIFT IS REQUIRED FOR AM SCHEDULED VISIT BEFORE STORE OPENS 20Ft Ceilings\n\no Wired headphones 3.5mm Wired. MUST HAVE\n\no Multi Meter - MUST HAVE\n\no 66/110 block punch tool - MUST HAVE\n\no Alligator clip leads\n\no Toner and probe kit\n\no Self-powered buttset\n\nhttps://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA\n\nScope of Work: Valcom2003 (24vDC) speaker run to the sales floor needs to be traced back to the electrical room and TAGGED Power or Audio (orange or blue). We also need to know the terminations of both AMPS documented.\n\n• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room and collect PICTURES of the following: (Should always be the very first thing you do on every call!)\n\no In electrical room identify all Valcom/RDL equipment cabling.\n\no In electrical room identify all TOA BG2120 equipment cabling.\n\no Volume control switches located throughout the store.\n\no At least 2 different speakers.\n\n• Objective of visit:\n\no Verify quality of music going into the Valcom 2003 (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)\n\no Verify quality of music going out the Valcom 2003 Speaker connection (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)\n\no Document (pictures) of all connections on the Amplifier equipment but do not remove or change any cabling until you have been instructed to and have tagged the connections in the event, they need to be put back.\n\no Trace and Tag one speaker line from sales floor that is not working (VALCOM 1020C) back to the Electrical room and tag both pairs.\n\no Verify VP4124 power supply in the electrical room has 24vDC. (SEE OTHER INSTRUCTIONS)\n\no Verify on the ceiling speaker in the run of non working speakers have 24vDC power.\n\no Verify on the ceiling speaker in the run of non working speakers have audio over the blue audio pair. (using headphones)\n\n• Other Instructions:\n\no Valcom 2003 has a 50pin connector that is cabled back to the 66 block. We need to document that 66 block from a side and front view to help us identify the color codes of the cables and how they are cross connected to the solution.\n\n(Link of Valcom 50pin: )\n\nhttps://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9d9t/oSFOt_dcOLJ2G5T5PpWBrswYc5CqYFw6d1CwBhV9p00\n\no VP4124 power supply has 3 channels of power. Under 2Amp connection check the (+ Black) (- Red) with your meter set to DC Voltage. It should be with in 10% of 24v.\n\n(Link of VP4124: ) <https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9d8H/VR61J0LSujHq9DLmHi8S8nxWnfhOWPVVxb00Qbq948U>\n\no Ceiling speaker (Valcom 1020C style) has 2 pairs of wires. Should be Orange for power side, and blue for the audio side. Keep in mind if anyone repaired the cabling colors may have changed so look at the back of the speakers board its printed. We need to know is this non working chain getting 24v DC on the pair (orange). We also need to know if you, with aligator clips, hook up to the audio (BLUE BLUE BLUE.. non voltage side or you get shocked) and connect it to your 3.5mm headphone jack. (google the wiring of your headphone you will see the Tip is normally left speaker, and one of the Base sleaves will be the Com..) We want to know if you hear music. TONER WAND WILL NOT HEAR THIS KIND OF AUDIO, it only hears 70V. But if we dont have power or we dont have audio at this dead speaker, we need to trace that speaker back to the electrical room to ensure the wire isnt cut!\n\n(Link of Valcom 1020C Speaker Wires: )\n\n<https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/PP00000K9djN/2qIv1t4VjRFRVy.vdn.mOdbwLDQ6tNOmW1eMlbbtTog>\n\no Please complete all Speaker work requiring access to the sales floor with a lift first. I will set the time on this case out for 4-6hrs. Once we have finished the lift work and store opens we will start to use the info collected to trace out the 66 block. Start with Speaker Power and Speaker audio on a non working line. No power, trace the orange, no audio trace the blue, no anything on either trace them both till you can safely tag the cabling coming down to the 66 block or power supply in the electrical room.\n\n• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at 800-282-7928, Option 3, Option 5 for further audio troubleshooting.\n\n*Review attached client work order for equipment details and client work order #. Remember to print the client work order for the POC sign-off.*\n\n**Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.**\n\n**Each site visit will require its own work order.**\n\n**If a revisit is needed or requested by support, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.**\n\n*Device installs may also include troubleshooting, configuration, or working with support to confirm device is on the customer’s network.*\n\nAll NTS support phone calls will be routed directly to a support technician i.e., L1 or L2. **ALL engineers will call 800-282-7928 #3 for NTS support**.\n\n- A second menu will be presented so the FE tech can select what support they require.\n  - #1 - POS, Registers, Terminal Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#2 - Network and cabling Support – calls route to NTS L1 and transfer to L2 if needed.\n  - \\#3 - Server Support – calls will route directly to NTS L2.\n  - \\#4 - Cameras Support – calls will route to a dedicated camara team.\n  - \\#5 - Audio Support – calls will route to a dedicated audio team.\n\n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n• Anti Static Wrist Strap or Static Mat\n\n• Laptop\n\n• USB to serial connector\n\n• NetTerm 5.6 or higher - <http://www.securenetterm.com/html/downloads.html>\n\n• Putty\n\n• NULL Modem cable\n\n• Ethernet cable\n\n• Laptop Power pack\n\n• Cell Phone capable of setting up a personal Hotspot for your laptop to connect to the internet\n\n• Set of Torx Screw Drivers from 2.5 to 30\n\n• Flash light\n\n• Digital Volt Meter\n\n• Team-Viewer 14.0 or higher (NON-Commercial Free) - <https://www.teamviewer.com/en-us/>\n\n• Zoom installed on Techs Phone\n\n• Velcro Straps\n\n• X-over cable\n\n• Standard screwdriver and security bits\n\n• Thermal paste\n\n• Alcohol Wipes\n\n• 9 pin serial cable\n\n**Reimbursement Rates:**Cabling Materials- Cat6 indoor cable (non‑plenum), including connectors: **$0.20 per ft**\n- Cat6 indoor cable (plenum), including connectors: **$0.29 per ft**\n\nHardware- Surface‑mount box with keystone jack: **$9.00 each**\n\nPatch Cables- 1 ft: **$3.50**\n- 3 ft: **$2.00**\n- 5 ft: **$4.50**\n- 10 ft: **$6.50**\n\nCable Management- Cable management supplies (zip ties, screw‑mount ties, etc.): **$2.00 per drop**\n\nCabling Job Requirements- All cabling must be secured using zip ties and screw‑mount cable ties.\n- Each drop must be patched to the patch panel and completed with a jack or faceplate.\n- All installation debris must be cleaned before leaving the site each day, including multi‑day work orders.\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Call Support to check in. \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* and confirm before leaving site. Support representative's name will be required. If no answer call \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n- Duration of the site visit should not be more than 1.5 hours – If additional time required onsite, call WO Manager for extended duration approval:\n- Record the client employee's First name of who provided approval of extended time frame.\n- Approval must be documented in the work order’s correct Custom Field or payment will be denied.\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians attending the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check is required\n- Check-in with site contacts as representing\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T07:00","end":"2026-11-03T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":35},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8.403383893034126},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $35 (countered: $60) is below minimum threshold $18