{"job":{"id":20286302,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SHI - Corp Services","title":"SHI dispatch for Meraki Equipment Set Up - usrwiof02- Rocky Mount, NC","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">*** For Travel/Fuel Requests Must Be Done in Your Counteroffer! ***</span></p><p><strong><u>Issue</u></strong></p><p>Meraki Equipment Set Up</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p>- Identify network rack and Cisco MX84</p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(47, 84, 150);\">- Set up Cisco MX67 (replacement router / firewall)</em></p><p>- Move internet and switch ethernet cables from MX84 to MX67</p><p>- Verify with user on site that wifi is working</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><p>Basic networking toolkit</p><p>Tester / Toner</p><p>Cat6</p><p>RJ45</p><p>Keystones</p><p>Wall plates</p><p>Labeler</p><p>Velcro for cable management</p><p>Ladder</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Please call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite</span></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Material Reimbursement:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot</li><li>Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea</li><li>Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea</li><li>Faceplate $3.50 / ea</li><li>Keystones $5.00/ea</li><li>Cable ends $2.50/ea</li><li>Velcro strips .75 cents each</li></ul><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost above</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">NOTE: any cable runs performed - must include validation - labeling, pass/fail tests, and show cable length. Service loops - no longer than 10-12 ft.</span></li><li><strong><u>Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\* For Travel/Fuel Requests Must Be Done in Your Counteroffer! \\*\\*\\*\n\n**Issue**\n\nMeraki Equipment Set Up\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n\\- Identify network rack and Cisco MX84\n\n*- Set up Cisco MX67 (replacement router / firewall)*\n\n\\- Move internet and switch ethernet cables from MX84 to MX67\n\n\\- Verify with user on site that wifi is working\n\n**Required Tools Needed:**\n\nBasic networking toolkit\n\nTester / Toner\n\nCat6\n\nRJ45\n\nKeystones\n\nWall plates\n\nLabeler\n\nVelcro for cable management\n\nLadder\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nPlease call work order manager for any questions or issues while onsite\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nPolo, Non-ripped Jeans, Closed toe shoes\n\n**Material Reimbursement:**\n\n- Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot\n- Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea\n- Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea\n- Faceplate $3.50 / ea\n- Keystones $5.00/ea\n- Cable ends $2.50/ea\n- Velcro strips .75 cents each\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed\n- Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job\n- Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost above\n- NOTE: any cable runs performed - must include validation - labeling, pass/fail tests, and show cable length. Service loops - no longer than 10-12 ft.\n- **Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"