{"job":{"id":20286083,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ION247","title":"IT Tech Visit: Spring Arbor of Apex - Fax Machine Troubleshooting & Grandstream Connectivity Restoration","description":{"html":"<p><strong>ION24/7 Ticket Number:</strong> T20260917.2628</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Technician to arrive onsite and work independently to troubleshoot, diagnose, repair, and/or install as requested below. <strong>You must sign a Non-disclosure Agreement (NDA) before job can be completed.</strong> Technician shall maintain a professional appearance, attire, and demeanor while representing ION24/7 onsite. If parts or materials are needed, call ION24/7 prior to purchasing. If job goes longer than expected, contact ION24/7 for approval. Detailed notes, clear communication, and before-and-after photos are required.</p><p>Investigate and restore functionality for one or two non-working fax machines at the site. The technician will troubleshoot the fax connectivity path, including the phone cabling and any connections to the Grandstream device(s), and work with ION24/7 remote support to identify and resolve the issue. The goal is to return the affected fax machine(s) to normal operating status and confirm successful fax communication.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Arrival Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Arrive on time and prepared to begin work.</li><li>Check in with the onsite contact upon arrival.</li><li>Obtain access to required work areas, IDFs/MDFs, IT closets, equipment rooms, or installation locations.</li><li>Coordinate with the ION24/7 Technical Contact for real-time handoff and direction.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Professional appearance required.</li><li>Collared shirt with no visible logos, tucked in.</li><li>Jeans are acceptable if clean and free of holes.</li><li>Must bring standard IT field-service tools.</li><li>Must be capable of providing complete photo and written documentation.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Check in/out with the designated onsite contact.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the assigned ION24/7 Technical Support before beginning work.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Maintain clear communication with ION24/7 Technical Support while performing work.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Be responsive to phone calls, emails, and messages from ION24/7 Technical Support.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Notify ION24/7 immediately of any site access issues, missing equipment, unavailable switch ports, network problems, or hardware concerns.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave the site without checking out with both the onsite contact and ION24/7 Technical Support.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Documentation Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Documentation is <strong>critical</strong> for this work order. Onsite technicians are expected to provide detailed notes and <u>thorough photo documentation</u> that clearly demonstrates all troubleshooting steps performed.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Equipment Required:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Laptop with Ethernet port or adapter</li><li>Smartphone/camera for documentation photos</li><li>Mobile hotspot</li><li>Cable toner and probe or equivalent cable tracing tools&nbsp;</li><li>Network cable tester or certifier&nbsp;</li><li>Basic hand tools for termination and patching&nbsp;</li><li>RJ45 connectors and keystone jacks</li><li>Patch cables&nbsp;</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 bulk cable and installation materials</li><li>Labeling materials&nbsp;</li><li>Ladder (if required)&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tasks to Perform:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Contact ION24/7 Technical Support before beginning work to review the issue and receive troubleshooting direction.</li><li>Meet with the onsite contact and identify all affected fax machine(s).</li><li>Take clear before photos of the fax machine(s), Grandstream device(s), and any relevant cabling or connection points.</li><li>Verify power, physical connections, and operational status of the affected fax machine(s).</li><li>Inspect and troubleshoot the phone cabling path between the fax machine(s) and the Grandstream device(s).</li><li>Test cabling, ports, and connections to identify any faults, loose connections, miswiring, or damaged components.</li><li>Coordinate with ION24/7 remote support to perform additional troubleshooting and testing as needed.</li><li>Repair or re-terminate existing cabling, reconnect devices, or correct configuration issues if authorized and within scope.</li><li>If additional repairs, replacement parts, or new cable runs are required, obtain approval from ION24/7 before proceeding.</li><li>Test outbound and inbound fax functionality, where feasible, to validate operation.</li><li>Take after photos showing the final device status and any work performed.</li><li>Review results with ION24/7 remote support and obtain final validation prior to checkout.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Success Criteria:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Affected fax machine(s) are operational and able to send and/or receive faxes as applicable.</li><li>Phone connectivity between the fax machine(s) and Grandstream device(s) is verified and functioning properly.</li><li>Any identified cabling or connection issues within the approved scope have been corrected.</li><li>All troubleshooting findings and corrective actions have been documented.</li><li>ION24/7 remote support has reviewed the results and validated the final operational status.</li><li>Before-and-after photos have been provided.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Cleanup:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Remove all packaging, scrap cable, labels, and debris.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Restore work areas to their original condition.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Check out with the onsite contact.&nbsp;</li><li>Check out with ION247 Technical Contact.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p><p>The work order may not be closed until:</p><ul><li>Required documentation has been submitted.</li><li>Required photos have been uploaded.</li><li>Final testing has been completed.</li><li>ION24/7 has verified successful completion.</li></ul>","markdown":"**ION24/7 Ticket Number:** T20260917.2628\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTechnician to arrive onsite and work independently to troubleshoot, diagnose, repair, and/or install as requested below. **You must sign a Non-disclosure Agreement (NDA) before job can be completed.** Technician shall maintain a professional appearance, attire, and demeanor while representing ION24/7 onsite. If parts or materials are needed, call ION24/7 prior to purchasing. If job goes longer than expected, contact ION24/7 for approval. Detailed notes, clear communication, and before-and-after photos are required.\n\nInvestigate and restore functionality for one or two non-working fax machines at the site. The technician will troubleshoot the fax connectivity path, including the phone cabling and any connections to the Grandstream device(s), and work with ION24/7 remote support to identify and resolve the issue. The goal is to return the affected fax machine(s) to normal operating status and confirm successful fax communication.\n\n**Arrival Requirements:**\n\n- Arrive on time and prepared to begin work.\n- Check in with the onsite contact upon arrival.\n- Obtain access to required work areas, IDFs/MDFs, IT closets, equipment rooms, or installation locations.\n- Coordinate with the ION24/7 Technical Contact for real-time handoff and direction.\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n- Professional appearance required.\n- Collared shirt with no visible logos, tucked in.\n- Jeans are acceptable if clean and free of holes.\n- Must bring standard IT field-service tools.\n- Must be capable of providing complete photo and written documentation.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- Check in/out with the designated onsite contact.\n- Contact the assigned ION24/7 Technical Support before beginning work.\n- Maintain clear communication with ION24/7 Technical Support while performing work.\n- Be responsive to phone calls, emails, and messages from ION24/7 Technical Support.\n- Notify ION24/7 immediately of any site access issues, missing equipment, unavailable switch ports, network problems, or hardware concerns.\n- Do not leave the site without checking out with both the onsite contact and ION24/7 Technical Support.\n\n**Documentation Requirements:**\n\nDocumentation is **critical** for this work order. Onsite technicians are expected to provide detailed notes and thorough photo documentation that clearly demonstrates all troubleshooting steps performed.\n\n **Equipment Required:**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet port or adapter\n- Smartphone/camera for documentation photos\n- Mobile hotspot\n- Cable toner and probe or equivalent cable tracing tools\n- Network cable tester or certifier\n- Basic hand tools for termination and patching\n- RJ45 connectors and keystone jacks\n- Patch cables\n- Cat5e/Cat6 bulk cable and installation materials\n- Labeling materials\n- Ladder (if required)\n\n**Tasks to Perform:**\n\n1. Contact ION24/7 Technical Support before beginning work to review the issue and receive troubleshooting direction.\n2. Meet with the onsite contact and identify all affected fax machine(s).\n3. Take clear before photos of the fax machine(s), Grandstream device(s), and any relevant cabling or connection points.\n4. Verify power, physical connections, and operational status of the affected fax machine(s).\n5. Inspect and troubleshoot the phone cabling path between the fax machine(s) and the Grandstream device(s).\n6. Test cabling, ports, and connections to identify any faults, loose connections, miswiring, or damaged components.\n7. Coordinate with ION24/7 remote support to perform additional troubleshooting and testing as needed.\n8. Repair or re-terminate existing cabling, reconnect devices, or correct configuration issues if authorized and within scope.\n9. If additional repairs, replacement parts, or new cable runs are required, obtain approval from ION24/7 before proceeding.\n10. Test outbound and inbound fax functionality, where feasible, to validate operation.\n11. Take after photos showing the final device status and any work performed.\n12. Review results with ION24/7 remote support and obtain final validation prior to checkout.\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n\n- Affected fax machine(s) are operational and able to send and/or receive faxes as applicable.\n- Phone connectivity between the fax machine(s) and Grandstream device(s) is verified and functioning properly.\n- Any identified cabling or connection issues within the approved scope have been corrected.\n- All troubleshooting findings and corrective actions have been documented.\n- ION24/7 remote support has reviewed the results and validated the final operational status.\n- Before-and-after photos have been provided.\n\n**Site Cleanup:**\n\n- Remove all packaging, scrap cable, labels, and debris.\n- Restore work areas to their original condition.\n- Check out with the onsite contact.\n- Check out with ION247 Technical Contact.\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\nThe work order may not be closed until:\n\n- Required documentation has been submitted.\n- Required photos have been uploaded.\n- Final testing has been completed.\n- ION24/7 has verified successful completion.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T08:45","end":"2026-11-04T10:45","latestStart":"2026-11-04T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.180135300272568},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"