{"job":{"id":20286961,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SISL Infotech (US) Inc","title":"L1/L2 Dispatch Network resource required |Holly Springs\tNC\t27540","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>SLA Support required: </u></strong></p><p><strong>Same Business Day (SBD)</strong></p><p><strong>Next Business Day (NBD)</strong></p><p><strong>P1 / 24×7 Requests: Support will be provided within 4 hours</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>Resourcing requirement: </u></strong>Unnamed Dispatch Model- L1 &amp; L2 Network resources</p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work: </u></strong>Please find below the generic scope of work.</p><ul><li>We need network FSO dispatch support for Club,</li><li>Provide hands &amp; feet support for in-scope network device including Cisco LAN switches, SD-WAN devices, Wireless Access Points, Ubiquiti wireless mesh devices, and firewalls.</li><li>Provide hands &amp; feet support, Break-Fix Support IMACD support, Wi-Fi surveys, Network Site Survey reports, structured cabling support, network device upgrades, and network installation/deployment support as applicable to approved tickets.</li></ul><p><strong>Basic Tool List:</strong></p><p> 1. Properly working laptop with Windows OS and US English language settings. </p><p>2. Laptop charger. </p><p>3. MS Team and Putty application installed. </p><p>4. Built-in Ethernet (RJ45) port on the laptop. </p><p>5. Console cable (USB A to RJ45 and USB A to C Type. </p><p>6. LAN cable tester. </p><p>7. Ethernet/patch cables (If required). </p><p>8. Basic rack-and-stack tool kit (screwdrivers, pliers, spanner set, etc.). </p><p>9. USB flash drive (16 GB or 32 GB). </p><p>10. Personal mobile hotspot or data dongle with an active internet connection. </p><p>11. Label printer, labels, and black-and-white markers.</p><p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong></p><p>All defined prerequisites items required for site access must be available and carried to customer site. In absence of any below listed item, access to site will not be granted and the work order will be cancelled simultaneously without further notice.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Timely Arrival.</li><li>Please provide required pictures in the whatsapp group with remote team .</li><li>Please provide check in check out time in the whatsapp group .</li><li>Constant communication with backend team via bridge.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>POST-SITE</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p><ul><li>Completed excel data sheet.</li><li>Pictures of the IT equipment at site.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>All escalations to be directed to remote bridge line</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY::</u></strong></p><ul><li>Unexpected expenses, such as parking fees, may be paid, ONLY if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App, and communicated to the Work Order Manager upon arrival to the work site.</li><li>Travel expenses such as mileage will not be paid when submitted upon completion of a work order. Any travel expenses must be included with a counteroffer to be eligible for consideration.</li><li>Additional hours will only be paid with prior approval from the Work Order Manager.</li><li>View Less</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**\n\n**SLA Support required:**\n\n**Same Business Day (SBD)**\n\n**Next Business Day (NBD)**\n\n**P1 / 24×7 Requests: Support will be provided within 4 hours**\n\n**Resourcing requirement:** Unnamed Dispatch Model- L1 &amp; L2 Network resources\n\n**Scope of Work:** Please find below the generic scope of work.\n\n- We need network FSO dispatch support for Club,\n- Provide hands &amp; feet support for in-scope network device including Cisco LAN switches, SD-WAN devices, Wireless Access Points, Ubiquiti wireless mesh devices, and firewalls.\n- Provide hands &amp; feet support, Break-Fix Support IMACD support, Wi-Fi surveys, Network Site Survey reports, structured cabling support, network device upgrades, and network installation/deployment support as applicable to approved tickets.\n\n**Basic Tool List:**\n\n 1. Properly working laptop with Windows OS and US English language settings.\n\n2\\. Laptop charger.\n\n3\\. MS Team and Putty application installed.\n\n4\\. Built-in Ethernet (RJ45) port on the laptop.\n\n5\\. Console cable (USB A to RJ45 and USB A to C Type.\n\n6\\. LAN cable tester.\n\n7\\. Ethernet/patch cables (If required).\n\n8\\. Basic rack-and-stack tool kit (screwdrivers, pliers, spanner set, etc.).\n\n9\\. USB flash drive (16 GB or 32 GB).\n\n10\\. Personal mobile hotspot or data dongle with an active internet connection.\n\n11\\. Label printer, labels, and black-and-white markers.\n\n**Prerequisite:**\n\nAll defined prerequisites items required for site access must be available and carried to customer site. In absence of any below listed item, access to site will not be granted and the work order will be cancelled simultaneously without further notice.\n\n**REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS**\n\n- Timely Arrival.\n- Please provide required pictures in the whatsapp group with remote team .\n- Please provide check in check out time in the whatsapp group .\n- Constant communication with backend team via bridge.\n\n**POST-SITE**\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Completed excel data sheet.\n- Pictures of the IT equipment at site.\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- All escalations to be directed to remote bridge line\n\n**ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY::**\n\n- Unexpected expenses, such as parking fees, may be paid, ONLY if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App, and communicated to the Work Order Manager upon arrival to the work site.\n- Travel expenses such as mileage will not be paid when submitted upon completion of a work order. Any travel expenses must be included with a counteroffer to be eligible for consideration.\n- Additional hours will only be paid with prior approval from the Work Order Manager.\n- View Less","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T08:00","end":"2026-11-06T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":320},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":16.09435030202212},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Fri, Nov 6, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Fri, Nov 6, Mon, Nov 9, Tue, Nov 10 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Trinity Arts Engineering (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action"