{"job":{"id":20287945,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ServiceP (PreferredTechs)","title":"V Count Nano 3D Sensor Install - Traffic counter - SEE SOW","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>**These are on bases so tech must be able to pass a background check.&nbsp;Do not apply if you can not pass a background check**</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>MANDATORY</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Once you arrive on site and are ready to start work, please call or text (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check in. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the site contact and begin work</li>\n<li>Complete troubleshoot/installation.&nbsp;Contact support with any issues or concerns so work is completed correctly and fully.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Complete required deliverables (see below) and call support to confirm you have completed the full SOW.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Text signed WO</u></strong>&nbsp;to (507-400-3227 and 720-515-5551)</li>\n<li><strong>REQUIRED</strong>: Call (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check out providing detailed notes of installation and any delays/issues. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please check confidential information for contact info</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Contact Location and you are representing <del>***</del>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Please pay attention to all of the details provided in the scope of work.&nbsp;See attached installation guide.&nbsp;<u>ANY QUESTIONS PLEASE CALL.&nbsp;PLEASE LOOK OVER BEFORE PROCEEDING TO THE SITE.</u></strong></p>\n<p>Installing x 1 Nano that will be installed on the inside of the main doors facing downward counting incoming traffic - confirming with Nano team but that is the current plan. This will be installed in the building counting the inside foot traffic.</p>\n<p><strong>Additional notes about the installation</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sensor should be configured for Wi-Fi and connected to the WIFI.&nbsp;We will be installing a cradlepoint to get signal to the sensors. Install cradlepoint as close to sensor as possible preferably by the counter.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>The sensor is powered via batteries so no cable runs are needed.</li>\n<li>The technician should contact Rob at the start and end of the installation. Rob will need to check into the sensor remotely while the technician is there to calibrate it.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They normally use Whatsapp.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech must make sure each sensor is installed professionally, configured with Rob at at support, and secured. Pictures of counter installed along with the cradlepoint.</p>\n<p>Support number is: Rob:<del>*</del><del>**** ********</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with WIFI</li>\n<li>Basic Tools (screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, etc)</li>\n<li>6' Ladder</li>\n<li>Drill</li>\n<li>Screws</li>\n<li>Any other materials/tools that are needed from when you surveyed the location</li>\n<li>Copy of work order</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Take special care to treat the premises with respect, if you drop trash (insulation from a ceiling tile, excess cable, etc.) please dispose of it properly.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long pants (Khakis or Jeans with no holes)</li>\n<li>Collared shirt/Polo shirt</li>\n<li>Close toe shoes</li>\n<li>Review SOW and inform ServiceP of any question prior to arriving on site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Required Deliverables</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Signed work order with check in and out times along with customer signature</li>\n<li>Picture of each Nano installation</li>\n<li>Picture of cradlepoint installed</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"***\\*\\*These are on bases so tech must be able to pass a background check. Do not apply if you can not pass a background check\\*\\****\n\n**MANDATORY**:\n\n1. Once you arrive on site and are ready to start work, please call or text (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check in. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).\n2. Introduce yourself to the site contact and begin work\n3. Complete troubleshoot/installation. Contact support with any issues or concerns so work is completed correctly and fully.\n4. Complete required deliverables (see below) and call support to confirm you have completed the full SOW.\n5. **Text signed WO** to (507-400-3227 and 720-515-5551)\n6. **REQUIRED**: Call (507-400-3227) or (405-345-1409) to check out providing detailed notes of installation and any delays/issues. If you are unable to reach anyone, please contact (720-515-5551).\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Please check confidential information for contact info**\n\n1. Contact Location and you are representing \\*\\*\\*.\n\n**Please pay attention to all of the details provided in the scope of work. See attached installation guide. ANY QUESTIONS PLEASE CALL. PLEASE LOOK OVER BEFORE PROCEEDING TO THE SITE.**\n\nInstalling x 1 Nano that will be installed on the inside of the main doors facing downward counting incoming traffic - confirming with Nano team but that is the current plan. This will be installed in the building counting the inside foot traffic.\n\n**Additional notes about the installation**:\n\n- The sensor should be configured for Wi-Fi and connected to the WIFI. We will be installing a cradlepoint to get signal to the sensors. Install cradlepoint as close to sensor as possible preferably by the counter.\n- The sensor is powered via batteries so no cable runs are needed.\n- The technician should contact Rob at the start and end of the installation. Rob will need to check into the sensor remotely while the technician is there to calibrate it.\n- They normally use Whatsapp.\n\nTech must make sure each sensor is installed professionally, configured with Rob at at support, and secured. Pictures of counter installed along with the cradlepoint.\n\nSupport number is: Rob:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Laptop with WIFI\n- Basic Tools (screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, etc)\n- 6' Ladder\n- Drill\n- Screws\n- Any other materials/tools that are needed from when you surveyed the location\n- Copy of work order\n\n**Take special care to treat the premises with respect, if you drop trash (insulation from a ceiling tile, excess cable, etc.) please dispose of it properly.**\n\n**Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:**\n\n- Long pants (Khakis or Jeans with no holes)\n- Collared shirt/Polo shirt\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform ServiceP of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Required Deliverables**\n\n- Signed work order with check in and out times along with customer signature\n- Picture of each Nano installation\n- Picture of cradlepoint installed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T09:00","end":"2026-11-12T11:00","latestStart":"2026-11-12T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":100},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":55},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57.63278145522657},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793642468507}
{"job":{"id":20288266,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Beverage Control Systems","title":"Help Identify Issue in Wine Dispensers","description":{"html":"<p>We need a technician on site to help identify an issue in our wine dispenser. I just need help troubleshooting why pours are not completing properly, so you will be my eyes and ears. There is nothing that is going to be repaired with this visit, strictly there to troubleshoot. This should take less than 1 hour.</p>","markdown":"We need a technician on site to help identify an issue in our wine dispenser. I just need help troubleshooting why pours are not completing properly, so you will be my eyes and ears. There is nothing that is going to be repaired with this visit, strictly there to troubleshoot. This should take less than 1 hour.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00","end":"2026-11-02T15:00","latestStart":"2026-11-02T16:30"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":14.813054523508553},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Epik Survey"},{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00