{"job":{"id":20288682,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Catcon Products","title":"Lumen EWAS Rotech Cutover and Test","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p>Overview:</p><p><br></p><p>Seeking a technician with experience in network equipment installation and configuration.</p><p><strong>Tech is required to complete the final cutover of an installed Cellular Data Router to the customers SASE Versa equipment. Tech will work with 10T support to confirm that all equipment is working as required. Tech must be prepared to troubleshoot and repair any equipment or lines as required. Tech is required to fabricate and label a CAT 6 cable that will run form the Router POE injector LAN port to the customers Versa port. Port number will be provided by 10T support day of the cutover. Expense will be added to the WO. </strong></p><p>Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Business Casual</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Cell phone with camera</p><p>Basic Network Hand Tools</p><p>Basic Hand Tools&nbsp;</p><p>Laptop with ethernet cable</p><p>Zip Ties</p><p>Ladder</p><p>Tools and parts required for manufacturing RJ11 or RJ45 cables.</p><p>Tools for punching down to a 66 or 110 block</p><p>Flashlight or Head Lamp</p><p>Tools for low voltage cable runs</p><p>Equipment for creating label for cables and 66 or 110 Block</p><p>Assorted fasteners needed to mount equipment to different surfaces.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><p>Please review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.</p><p>Print off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.</p><p>Confirm WO and start time 48 hours prior.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.</p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del><strong> to coordinate the cutover and final test.</strong></p><p>Locate equipment and document previously installed InHand ODU. Router should be installed externally.</p><p>Take photo of the installed router.</p><p>Take photo of the external penetration.</p><p>Take photo of the mounted POE injector.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Verify Router Cell Connection</strong></p><p><strong>All Rotech sites will have PSIP. 10T support will provide the PSIP.</strong></p><p>Connect laptop to router LAN port. Laptop should be set to DHCP.</p><p>Verify connectivity. IP address. Able to internet browse.</p><p>Run speed test.</p><p><strong>Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. <u>DO NOT MOVE THE ROUTER</u> without approval from 10T support. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Sheet.</strong></p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">5-900-0809</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Final Cutover</strong></p><p>Router is now ready to the customers Versa device.</p><p>Fabricate and label a CAT6 cable that will connect to the Router POE injector LAN port and run to the customers Versa device.</p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p>Connect the fabricated cable to the Router POE injector LAN port and to the customers assigned port that will be provided by 10T support along with final test procedure.</p><p>10T support will verify the cutover and release you from the site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Install completion checklist</strong></p><p>Check that all cables and wiring are dressed and neat.</p><p>Label all cables and wires if needed.</p><p>Leave work area neat and clean</p><p>Take all required photos and upload.</p><p>Complete acceptance form and have LCON sign if available. Upload completed form.</p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Check Out:</strong></p><p><strong>Contact 10T Support at </strong><del>************</del></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy&nbsp;</p><p>Any additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.</p>","markdown":"**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nOverview:\n\nSeeking a technician with experience in network equipment installation and configuration.\n\n**Tech is required to complete the final cutover of an installed Cellular Data Router to the customers SASE Versa equipment. Tech will work with 10T support to confirm that all equipment is working as required. Tech must be prepared to troubleshoot and repair any equipment or lines as required. Tech is required to fabricate and label a CAT 6 cable that will run form the Router POE injector LAN port to the customers Versa port. Port number will be provided by 10T support day of the cutover. Expense will be added to the WO.**\n\nEstimated duration will be 1-2 hours.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nBusiness Casual\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\nCell phone with camera\n\nBasic Network Hand Tools\n\nBasic Hand Tools\n\nLaptop with ethernet cable\n\nZip Ties\n\nLadder\n\nTools and parts required for manufacturing RJ11 or RJ45 cables.\n\nTools for punching down to a 66 or 110 block\n\nFlashlight or Head Lamp\n\nTools for low voltage cable runs\n\nEquipment for creating label for cables and 66 or 110 Block\n\nAssorted fasteners needed to mount equipment to different surfaces.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\nPlease review attached installation guide material prior to arriving on-site.\n\nPrint off the 10T Solutions Acceptance Form.\n\nConfirm WO and start time 48 hours prior.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**On-Site Tasks**\n\nCheck-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent 10T Solutions on behalf of LUMEN while onsite.\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **to coordinate the cutover and final test.**\n\nLocate equipment and document previously installed InHand ODU. Router should be installed externally.\n\nTake photo of the installed router.\n\nTake photo of the external penetration.\n\nTake photo of the mounted POE injector.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Verify Router Cell Connection**\n\n**All Rotech sites will have PSIP. 10T support will provide the PSIP.**\n\nConnect laptop to router LAN port. Laptop should be set to DHCP.\n\nVerify connectivity. IP address. Able to internet browse.\n\nRun speed test.\n\n**Speed Test: The minimum required speed tests result is10/2 however if speeds are below 30/5 please evaluate location of router to determine if a different location will enhance performance. DO NOT MOVE THE ROUTER without approval from 10T support. Document results on the 10T Acceptance Sheet.**\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*5-900-0809\n\n**Final Cutover**\n\nRouter is now ready to the customers Versa device.\n\nFabricate and label a CAT6 cable that will connect to the Router POE injector LAN port and run to the customers Versa device.\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nConnect the fabricated cable to the Router POE injector LAN port and to the customers assigned port that will be provided by 10T support along with final test procedure.\n\n10T support will verify the cutover and release you from the site.\n\n**Install completion checklist**\n\nCheck that all cables and wiring are dressed and neat.\n\nLabel all cables and wires if needed.\n\nLeave work area neat and clean\n\nTake all required photos and upload.\n\nComplete acceptance form and have LCON sign if available. Upload completed form.\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Any questions or issues contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check Out:**\n\n**Contact 10T Support at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nAdditional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy\n\nAny additional hours or expenses need to be pre-approved prior to incurring on the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-23T08:00","end":"2026-11-23T10:00","latestStart":"2026-11-23T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2.5146162870735895},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-25T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-26T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-26T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-27T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Thanksgiving Day"},{"start":"2026-11-27T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-28T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Black Friday"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:0