, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793647101884}
{"job":{"id":"5518916757","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Investigate intermittent packet loss at modem link","description":"**Issue:**<br>Investigate intermittent connectivity and packet loss occurring throughout the day. The customer reports packet loss at the final hop/modem link and uploaded a picture showing the issue; standard Layer 1 and equipment-connection checks were completed, both modem lights are blue, and the carrier modem test showed 0% packet loss. The carrier declined its dispatch because it saw the customer-equipment interface down and required packet-loss logs.<br><br>CIRCUIT DETAILS<br>Service Type: Broadband<br>Carrier: TIME WARNER<br>CXR Circuit ID: 8349210390070769<br>NSO ID: N/A<br>WAN IP: N/A<br>WAN Gateway: N/A<br>MAC Address: A0:ED:6D:4D:85:E4<br><br>**Required Equipment:**<br>- A laptop: Windows 10 or higher with admin rights, ethernet ports gig capable of speeds over 1G, and charger to prove connectivity, a patch cord, a splitter, and a minimum of 3 filters. Cell phone, Cell phone charger, butt set and Minimum of 150’ of cable. Cat5e/or higher, and Coax.<br><br>**Other Required Equipment:**<br>- mobile hot spot, usb 2.0 drive w/ 16gb storage, console cable two surface jacks etc<br><br>**General Info:**<br>- Customer Contact: Katrina, 8433729500<br>- NOC Call Back: Broadband Repair at 844-492-2557 option 2<br><br>**Configuration:**<br>- WAN Configuration: DNS 1 209.18.47.61, DNS 2 209.18.47.62<br>- DHCP Enabled/Disabled: Enabled<br>- Provisioned Speed: 500Mbps/20Mbps<br><br>**SOW:**<br>- Check in via WorkMarket.<br>- Locate the Granite provided modem/router. Record make, model, and serial number in the ticket.<br>- Take a photo of the equipment and site as found.<br>- Verify modem LEDs indicate normal operation.<br>- Verify modem configuration matches the information provided in the ticket.<br>- If modem configuration does not match the documented configuration and cannot be corrected onsite, contact the Granite NOC.<br>- Inspect all inside wiring from DMARC to modem and replace as needed<br>- Document all wiring repairs completed onsite<br>- Connect directly to modem using test laptop<br>- Verify IP assignment (DHCP or static as documented)<br>- Confirm internet connectivity<br>- Unplug customers equipment, and plug laptop directly to the modem<br>- While directly connected to the modem, perform three (3) speed tests.<br>  - Download speed<br>  - Upload speed<br>  - Latency<br>- Ping-500 “ping –n 500 8.8.8.8” record<br>  - Packet loss percentage<br>  - Average latency<br>  - Maximum latency<br>- If speed test results are less than 80% of the provisioned service speed relocate the modem to the DMARC, when technically feasible. Connect technician laptop directly to the modem. Repeat three (3) speed tests<br>- Repeat Ping testing. Compare results between customer equipment location and DMARC location<br>- If speeds improve at the DMARC, inside wiring is the likely cause. Recheck wiring components. Retest after repairs.<br>- If speeds remain poor at the DMARC, issue is likely outside the customer premises. Proceed to Escalation Criteria.<br>- Reconnect customer equipment<br>- Confirm connectivity with LCON and MCON if required. See General Info<br>- Document all findings and actions taken including customer-owned equipment issues discovered onsite<br>- Identify Fault:<br>  - Customer Equipment<br>  - Customer LAN<br>  - Granite Managed Router<br>  - Carrier Circuit<br>  - Physical Layer/Cabling<br>  - No Trouble Found<br>- Validate service restoration criteria<br>- Upload pictures onto WorkMarket<br>- Contact Granite NOC after all testing and isolation steps have been completed. Or escalation is needed. See Escalation criteria. If not connected to a live person within 15 minutes accept the call back request<br>- Complete closeout and check out via WorkMarket<br><br>**Service Restoration Success Criteria:**<br>- Modem is online<br>- Power, DS, US, Online lights are normal<br>- Technician can browse from a laptop connected directly to modem<br>- IP Address obtained or assigned correctly<br>- 2 successful speed tests completed<br>- 500-ping test completed with acceptable results<br>- Customer equipment reconnected<br>- Photos and test results uploaded<br><br>**Escalation Criteria:**<br>- Physical Layer Issues<br>  - No power to carrier equipment or Granite-managed router<br>  - Carrier handoff down or no link light present<br>  - Damaged cabling or infrastructure requiring carrier repair<br>- Connectivity Issues<br>  - Unable to obtain an IP address<br>  - Unable to reach the configured gateway<br>  - Unable to browse the internet from a direct connection<br>  - WAN or LAN interface remains down after validation<br>- Performance Issues<br>  - Speed tests below 80% of provisioned bandwidth<br>  - Packet loss exceeds 2%<br>  - Elevated latency or jitter impacting service<br>  - Performance issues persist when testing directly from the Granite-managed router<br>- Customer Impact<br>  - Customer equipment cannot reconnect after testing<br>  - Customer remains unable to access services after troubleshooting is complete<br>- Carrier Engagement Required<br>  - Issue persists after local equipment, cabling, and router validation<br>  - Carrier trouble ticket or dispatch is required<br>  - Testing indicates the fault exists beyond the customer premises or Granite-managed equipment","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":164.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 164.5mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793647306684}
{"job":{"id":"9458731658","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"TecsPlus","title":"Network Tech- Durham, NC","description":"<p><strong>We require our techs to arrive at least 15 minutes of requested ETA.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>1. Timesheet MUST be printed and signed off by someone local. If you have to wait for more than 5 minutes after&nbsp;your release time, you MUST call 302 368 5656 Ext 2 to inform them so that you can be released from site without a signature. Failure to adhere will mean that you will have to WAIT for WO to be approved in a timely manner while we attempt to validate time onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;It is the responsibility of techs to report any expenses incurred on materials used and how it was used in their closing notes along with any other expenses within 0-24 hours of completion of assignment.</strong></p><p>**NOTE: Contact, Support Engineers details and Equipment details will be shared with Assigned FE Via Email. <strong><em><u>Details will NOT be added to Work Order.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Service Location</strong>:<strong>Durham, NC</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>This is to meet Spectrum for 1 pm.&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>Their arrival window is between 1-2pm</em>. Tech is expected to wait for Spectrum to arrive.&nbsp;</p><p>Number of POTS Lines and usages=&nbsp;1 line for alarm use. We are replacing 9149-53*** which is BP 11</p><p>End to end testing should always be done.&nbsp;Spectrum needs to verify dt out of the back of the device prior to leaving. Cross connects/ extending is required. Please test end points once connections are made.</p><p>We are replacing lines but they are not going to be tagged. Pls be sure tech knows how to tone and trace.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Please capture the new telephone infomation and include it in closing notes.</p><p><br></p><p>Contact, Support Engineers details and Equipment details will be shared with Assigned FE Via Email.</p><p><br></p><p>Standard Tool Kit:</p><ul><li>Console Cable/Cisco Console Cable</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Cat5 Cable (min 300 ft)</li><li>Cross-Connect Wire</li><li>Bridge Clips</li><li>Tie Wraps</li><li>Biscuits (Single/Double) Beige &amp; White</li><li>RJ48x Self Looping Jack for T1 extensions</li><li>RJ45 Jack Cat5 Rated and RJ45 Male Connectors</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T13:00","end":"2026-11-05T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":