{"job":{"id":20289272,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Nike - Request for SmartHands -   NikePOS registers refresh Tech 1","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>High Level Scope:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.</strong></p><p><strong>This is a high level overview</strong></p><p><strong><u>Network Preparation and Equipment:</u></strong></p><p>1. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and&nbsp;one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.</p><p>2. Network setups</p><p>3. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct&nbsp;station (register location).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Installation:</u></strong></p><p>1. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.</p><p>2. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).</p><p>3. Unbox the AFD and install it into location</p><p>3. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).</p><p>4. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.</p><p>5. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws&nbsp;</p><p>6. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it&nbsp;by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise</p><p>7. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Device configuration:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Smoke Testing</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**High Level Scope:**\n\n**Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.**\n\n**Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.**\n\n**This is a high level overview**\n\n**Network Preparation and Equipment:**\n\n1\\. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.\n\n2\\. Network setups\n\n3\\. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct station (register location).\n\n**Installation:**\n\n1\\. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.\n\n2\\. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).\n\n3\\. Unbox the AFD and install it into location\n\n3\\. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).\n\n4\\. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.\n\n5\\. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws\n\n6\\. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise\n\n7\\. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.\n\n**Device configuration:**\n\n**Smoke Testing**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T15:00","end":"2026-11-03T23:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":650},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":35.22924181846902},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 3, 3:00 PM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 3, Wed, Nov 4, Thu, Nov 5, Fri, Nov 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793648372439}
{"job":{"id":20289277,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Nike - Request for SmartHands -   NikePOS registers refresh Tech 2","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>High Level Scope:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.</strong></p><p><strong>This is a high level overview</strong></p><p><strong><u>Network Preparation and Equipment:</u></strong></p><p>1. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and&nbsp;one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.</p><p>2. Network setups</p><p>3. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct&nbsp;station (register location).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Installation:</u></strong></p><p>1. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.</p><p>2. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).</p><p>3. Unbox the AFD and install it into location</p><p>3. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).</p><p>4. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.</p><p>5. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws&nbsp;</p><p>6. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it&nbsp;by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise</p><p>7. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Device configuration:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Smoke Testing</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**High Level Scope:**\n\n**Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.**\n\n**Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.**\n\n**This is a high level overview**\n\n**Network Preparation and Equipment:**\n\n1\\. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.\n\n2\\. Network setups\n\n3\\. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct station (register location).\n\n**Installation:**\n\n1\\. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.\n\n2\\. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).\n\n3\\. Unbox the AFD and install it into location\n\n3\\. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).\n\n4\\. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.\n\n5\\. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws\n\n6\\. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise\n\n7\\. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.\n\n**Device configuration:**\n\n**Smoke Testing**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T15:00","end":"2026-11-03T25:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":650},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":35.22924181846902},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 3, 3:00 PM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 3, Wed, Nov 4, Thu, Nov 5, Fri, Nov 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793648399593}
{"job":{"id":20289176,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Install 2 Network Cables","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>Please read the below before accepting this work order. There is a very strict timeline for this work order that needs to be followed. There will be no exceptions unless it has been worked out before dispatch with work order manager. Tech must have all materials below before reporting to site.</em></strong></p><p><strong>TECH IS TO CALL ONCE ON SITE TO CHECK AND REVIEW SCOPE OF WORK. </strong></p><ol><li><strong>TECH MUST BRING TWO BOXES OF CAT 6 CABLE WITH MINIMUM OF 500FT AND 2 - 2 PORT BACK BOXES WITH KEYSTONE JACKS. CABLE RUNS WILL BE BETWEEN 70-250 FT. TECH WILL </strong></li><li><strong>ALSO NEED TO BRING ADHESIVE - TWO SIDED TAPE FOR THE FLOOR MOLDING THAT HAS BEEN SHIPPED TO SITE IF FLOOR MOLDING WILL NEED TO BE USED.</strong></li><li><strong>TECH MUST BRING 8FT LADDER.</strong></li></ol><p>Tech is to install 2 new cables from back of store modem/ camera area to front cash wrap. If the tech cannot run cables, tech is to perform site survey and provide written quote for labor and materials on form attached to work order.</p><ol><li>Locate IOC/IOF modem and test for connection and speeds.Depending on modem location, modem may need to be extended or moved to the camera area.</li><li>Install, terminate, test and label 2 new cat6 cables from modem/camera area to under front cash wrap below network firewall which is located under POS terminal on front counter.</li><li>Tech will secure cables along existing conduit/cable pathway based on store layout.</li><li>Floor molding if needed will be on site.</li><li>Misc: Zip Ty's,Velcro, Scres, etc.</li></ol><p><strong>TECH IS TO PROVIDE PHOTOS OF ALL WORK PERFORMED ON SITE.</strong></p><p><strong>***If tech is not able to run cable a site work becomes a site survey, tech is expected for a return visit to complete the cabling work***</strong></p><p><strong>Tech is to survey a run of 2 new cables from the back office, where camera equipment and modems are located, to the front cash wrap. </strong></p><p><strong>Tech must fill out the attached site survey pricing form and complete work order with-in 48 hours or the tech will not be paid for work order. </strong></p><p><strong>TECH IS TO PROVIDE PHOTOS DETAILING WHERE CABLE AND SURFACE MOUNT BOXES ARE TO BE INSTALLED INCLUDING NETWORK EQUIPMENT.</strong></p><p><strong>****Tech MUST return to site to complete the cabling work for the pricing provided to Spectrotel.***</strong></p><p><strong>FAILURE TO COMPLETE ALL PARTS OF THE DELIVERABLES WILL RESULT IN CANCELATION OF THE WORK ORDER AND WILL FORFEIT ANY PAYMENT TO PROVIDER.</strong></p><p><p>Scope of Work:</p></p>","markdown":"***Please read the below before accepting this work order. There is a very strict timeline for this work order that needs to be followed. There will be no exceptions unless it has been worked out before dispatch with work order manager. Tech must have all materials below before reporting to site.***\n\n**TECH IS TO CALL ONCE ON SITE TO CHECK AND REVIEW SCOPE OF WORK.**\n\n1. **TECH MUST BRING TWO BOXES OF CAT 6 CABLE WITH MINIMUM OF 500FT AND 2 - 2 PORT BACK BOXES WITH KEYSTONE JACKS. CABLE RUNS WILL BE BETWEEN 70-250 FT. TECH WILL**\n2. **ALSO NEED TO BRING ADHESIVE - TWO SIDED TAPE FOR THE FLOOR MOLDING THAT HAS BEEN SHIPPED TO SITE IF FLOOR MOLDING WILL NEED TO BE USED.**\n3. **TECH MUST BRING 8FT LADDER.**\n\nTech is to install 2 new cables from back of store modem/ camera area to front cash wrap. If the tech cannot run cables, tech is to perform site survey and provide written quote for labor and materials on form attached to work order.\n\n1. Locate IOC/IOF modem and test for connection and speeds.Depending on modem location, modem may need to be extended or moved to the camera area.\n2. Install, terminate, test and label 2 new cat6 cables from modem/camera area to under front cash wrap below network firewall which is located under POS terminal on front counter.\n3. Tech will secure cables along existing conduit/cable pathway based on store layout.\n4. Floor molding if needed will be on site.\n5. Misc: Zip Ty's,Velcro, Scres, etc.\n\n**TECH IS TO PROVIDE PHOTOS OF ALL WORK PERFORMED ON SITE.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*If tech is not able to run cable a site work becomes a site survey, tech is expected for a return visit to complete the cabling work\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Tech is to survey a run of 2 new cables from the back office, where camera equipment and modems are located, to the front cash wrap.**\n\n**Tech must fill out the attached site survey pricing form and complete work order with-in 48 hours or the tech will not be paid for work order.**\n\n**TECH IS TO PROVIDE PHOTOS DETAILING WHERE CABLE AND SURFACE MOUNT BOXES ARE TO BE INSTALLED INCLUDING NETWORK EQUIPMENT.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*Tech MUST return to site to complete the cabling work for the pricing provided to Spectrotel.\\*\\*\\***\n\n**FAILURE TO COMPLETE ALL PARTS OF THE DELIVERABLES WILL RESULT IN CANCELATION OF THE WORK ORDER AND WILL FORFEIT ANY PAYMENT TO PROVIDER.**\n\nScope of Work:","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-19T10:00","end":"2026-11-19T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":56.5866802050648},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793648438311}
