{"job":{"id":"4055553879","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"ASD","title":"SITE SURVEY: INDOOR/OUTDOOR CAT6 CABLE RUN (DEVICE 2048)","description":"<p><u>IMPORTANT- This assignment requires a form to be properly filled out and stamped upon job completion. Failure to do so forfeits pay.</u></p><p><br></p><p>Before starting this assignment, please log in to the ticket using the following link and use this platform to document and track all work performed for this service order:</p><p><br></p><p>https://flare.asd.direct</p><p><br></p><p>Use your work market email to access our app.</p><p><br></p><p>Ensure all updates, notes, and required information related to the job are entered into the ticket while completing the work.</p><p><u> </u></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>SOW(<strong>Order Number: </strong>801634178):</p><p><br></p><p>SITE SURVEY: INDOOR/OUTDOOR CAT6 CABLE RUN (DEVICE 2048)</p><p><strong>OBJECTIVE</strong> Conduct a <strong>SITE SURVEY</strong> to engineer a replacement Cat6 cable run for <strong>Device 2048</strong>. Because the pathway traverses exposed, unconditioned, or perimeter areas, the replacement run must utilize <strong>Indoor/Outdoor (CMX/UV-rated) Cat6</strong> cabling to restore permanent network connectivity.</p><p><strong>WHAT TO DO ON SITE</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Conduct Pathway &amp; Distance Survey:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Identify the IDF/switch rack origin and trace the proposed route to the Device 2048 location.</li><li>Measure the exact total linear footage required for the pull, accounting for drops, service loops at both ends, and vertical risers.</li><li>Map the transition points where the cable moves between standard indoor plenum/riser space and harsh, exterior, or unconditioned indoor/outdoor environments.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Assess Pathway &amp; Environmental Specifications:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Document conduit availability, fill capacity, and sleeve requirements through exterior walls or fire barriers.</li><li>Note any physical hazards along the route (e.g., UV exposure, moisture/washdown zones, extreme temperature swings, mechanical equipment, high-voltage crossings).</li><li>Verify mounting requirements at the Device 2048 termination point (e.g., weatherproof junction box, drip loop, sealed grommets, or IP-rated faceplate).</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Identify Head-End &amp; Hardware Requirements:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Locate the designated patch panel position and active switch port in the IDF.</li><li>Confirm hardware needs for the install scope (e.g., shielded/gel-filled vs. standard dry UV Cat6, surge suppression/grounding at building entrance points if applicable, specialized modular plugs/jacks).</li></ul><ol><li><strong>STOP &amp; CHECK IN:</strong> Send complete distance measurements, pathway routing notes, environmental assessment, and site photos to me for sign-off <strong>BEFORE</strong> pulling any new cable.</li></ol><p><br></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":130},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":0},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"20