{"job":{"id":20291500,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"NCR POS Base Unit Swap- Register 6","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:</u></strong></p><p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE</p><p>The site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.</p><p>Technician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.</p><p>Technician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.</p><p>Technician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.</p><p>Technician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.</p><p>Technician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.</p><p>Technician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.</p><p>Technician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.</p><p>Technician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.</p><p>Technician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.</p><p>Technician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.</p><p>After the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.</p><p>After signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the</p><p>next message box should request the register number.</p><p>After entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.</p><p>Technician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.</p><p>**If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!**</p><p>Technician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.</p><p>Technician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.</p><p>Technician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.</p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"><del>** ** *** **** **** ** *********** *** ******** ****** *** ***** *** ************ ** * ****** **********</del></span></p><p><strong> **If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.</strong></p><p><strong> If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!**</strong></p><p><strong> **If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately**</strong></p><p>​</p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Required to be paid</u></strong></p><ol><li>Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.</li><li>Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)</li><li>Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done&nbsp;<u>before</u>&nbsp;any work is done.</li><li>Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.</li><li>Technician&nbsp;must take pictures of any equipment worked on&nbsp;<u>after</u>&nbsp;the work is done.</li><li>Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. <strong><u>TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> ** Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Requirements:</u></strong></p><ol><li>​Technician must be familiar with data cabling</li><li>Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable</li><li>Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Part Requirements:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><em><u>IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.</u></em></p><p>Up to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors,&nbsp;Ethernet cables,&nbsp;Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable</p><p><em><u>**POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot**</u></em></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**\n\n**INSTRUCTIONAL VIDEO:**\n\n<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H013eQGAykE>\n\nThe site is requesting a technician to assist them on site.\n\nTechnician is needed to swap and replace the current POS equipment with a new NCR Base Unit.\n\nTechnician will email the Gabes IT Help Desk at ithelpdesk@gabes.net “POSRG Tech on Site at Store(store number)” to notify them of your presence.\n\nTechnician will start by finding the new base unit key that has been shipped with the new base unit.\n\nTechnician will use the key to remove the front plastic bezel from the POS Terminal.\n\nTechnician will then unplug all of the cables from the rear of the base unit.\n\nTechnician will find the (2) screws on the back of the base unit that hold the sled inside the base unit chassis. (Please see picture pointing out screw on the left side. There will also be a second corresponding screw on the right hand side. These will be the (2) screws needed to be loosened in order for the sled to be detached from the chassis.\n\nTechnician will then pull the sled out from the front of the POS chassis by the handle removing all of the internals of the POS including motherboard and HDDs.\n\nTechnician will take the new sled with POS internals that has been shipped to the site and slide it in the front of the POS chassis the same way the old sled came out.\n\nTechnician will secure the new sled in place in the rear with the (2) screws to the chassis.\n\nTechnician will replug all of the cables at the rear of the POS.\n\nAfter the the POS terminal has boot up for the first time, the technician should start off by signing into the register with the password “Gabes”.\n\nAfter signing in you should get a message box asking to contact IT and the\n\nnext message box should request the register number.\n\nAfter entering the register number the script will set the registers IP address and reboot.\n\nTechnician will Sign in once more and contact IT via email and phone to let them know the new base unit should be online.\n\n\\*\\*If any issues are encountered during this process please contact our IT help desk IMMEDIATELY!\\*\\*\n\nTechnician will work with the Gabe's Help Desk to confirm the connectivity of the devices worked on.\n\nTechnician will need to locate the return labels sent with the new POS and package the old POS which will be sent to POSRG.\n\nTechnician will need to drop off this equipment and upload a picture of the tracking to receive payment.\n\n\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n **\\*\\*If more time than the maximum hours permitted is needed, the Technician must call the POSRG Project Coordinator approval.**\n\n **If no call is made, you will not be paid for any extra time on-site!!\\*\\***\n\n **\\*\\*If the customer asks us to perform ANY out of scope work, Please call the work order manager immediately\\*\\***\n\n​\n\n**Deliverables Required to be paid**\n\n1. Technician must check-in and out with POSRG WO Manager via Text Message.\n2. Technician must check-in and out with the Gabe's Help Desk by emailing ithelpdesk@gabes.net with the subject line: POSRG Tech on site at store # (insert store number)\n3. Technician must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.\n4. Technician must complete work as stated in the scope of work.\n5. Technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.\n6. Technician will use return labels to package old equipment and drop off to be shipped back to POSRG. **TRACKING IS REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT OF FUNDS**\n\n **\\*\\* Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay\\*\\***\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n1. ​Technician must be familiar with data cabling\n2. Technician must be capable of running and terminating cable\n3. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment\n\n**Part Requirements:**\n\n*IF PARTS ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT POSRG PROJECT COORDINATOR ASAP.*\n\nUp to 500' Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling, Data Wall Plates or Boxes, Network Connectors, Ethernet cables, Punch down tool, Cable Tester, Drill + Varying Bits​, Wire Stripper, RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Jacks, Crimper, Laptop, Smartphone, Wireless Hotspot, at least a 10' Ladder, and anything else needed to run a cable\n\n*\\*\\*POSRG will compensate for materials used on-site and cable at 40 Cents per foot\\*\\**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T12:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11.920137696654699},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793651810316}
{"job":{"id":20235409,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | VCA | Credit Card Terminal Refresh","description":{"html":"<p>Insight has been engaged by VCA to perform like for like swaps on credit card terminals</p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING </u></strong></p><p><strong>SCOPE: </strong></p><p>☐ Install and connect new credit card payment terminals, replacing the hospital’s existing terminals on a like-for-like basis (including the required cabling).</p><p>☐ Verify each new terminal is recognized and functioning within the hospital’s payment system (WOOFware) and complete a test transaction with a staff member.</p><p>☐ Coordinate the cutover with hospital staff to minimize disruption, keeping at least one terminal available for payment processing wherever possible.</p><p>☐ Remove and Decommission old/retired terminals per the approved return process and review basic terminal functions and support resources with staff before departing.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools needed:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Hard and soft copy of the work instructions document</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Phone 100% charged before arriving, with Phone Charger, Internet Access, Camera, MS Teams mobile App, &amp; Hands-Free Headset</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Snips (Scissors) to cut velcro and zip ties</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Box Cutters to open boxes</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 #2 Phillips Screw Driver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 #1 Phillips Screw Driver to remove base from legacy PC</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Flash Light to illuminate underneath workstations</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Materials</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Velcro Roll for cable management</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Packing Tape to seal old equipment box</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Also the hospital will provide a tool that is required to remove equipment at some work stations</span></li></ul><p><strong>Dress code: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Business casual (polo and pants), closed shoes or boots. no jeans or sneakers and no safety gear is required.</span></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li><li>IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</li><li>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</li></ul><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.</em></p>","markdown":"Insight has been engaged by VCA to perform like for like swaps on credit card terminals\n\n**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\n**SCOPE:**\n\n☐ Install and connect new credit card payment terminals, replacing the hospital’s existing terminals on a like-for-like basis (including the required cabling).\n\n☐ Verify each new terminal is recognized and functioning within the hospital’s payment system (WOOFware) and complete a test transaction with a staff member.\n\n☐ Coordinate the cutover with hospital staff to minimize disruption, keeping at least one terminal available for payment processing wherever possible.\n\n☐ Remove and Decommission old/retired terminals per the approved return process and review basic terminal functions and support resources with staff before departing.\n\n**Tools needed:**\n\n- 1 Hard and soft copy of the work instructions document\n- 1 Phone 100% charged before arriving, with Phone Charger, Internet Access, Camera, MS Teams mobile App, &amp; Hands-Free Headset\n- 1 Snips (Scissors) to cut velcro and zip ties\n- 1 Box Cutters to open boxes\n- 1 #2 Phillips Screw Driver\n- 1 #1 Phillips Screw Driver to remove base from legacy PC\n- 1 Flash Light to illuminate underneath workstations\n- Materials\n- 1 Velcro Roll for cable management\n- 1 Packing Tape to seal old equipment box\n- Also the hospital will provide a tool that is required to remove equipment at some work stations\n\n**Dress code:** Business casual (polo and pants), closed shoes or boots. no jeans or sneakers and no safety gear is required.\n\nTerms for Travel:\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\nTerms for Additional Time being Required:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n- IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n- Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation. You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-18T12:30","end":"2026-11-18T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":18.756888334928032},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793652169344}
{"job":{"id":20291996,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"New Store Register Install","description":{"html":"<p>**Please read the documentation attached to this WO prior to arriving on site**</p><p><strong><em><u>DO NOT USE ZIP TIES-- VELCRO ONLY</u></em></strong></p><p>Tech will need a government issued Photo ID to pick up parts from FedEx before install</p>FedEx Office Print &amp; Ship Center<p>4900 NC-55 Ste 4101, Durham, NC 27713</p><p><strong><em><u>﻿</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work ***Information from the attached documentation***</u></strong></p><p>1.0 Arriving on site</p><p>When arriving onsite there are two layers of checking in. Once with the HP Command Center and once with the site contact. See below for related instructions.</p><p><u>1.1 Arrive on-site on time.</u></p><p>1.2 Check in via e-mail through the Project PDL genescods@hp.com.</p><p>1.3 Walk inside to check in with the site contact (site superintendent).</p><p><strong><u>1.4 Check in with the Genesco Site Contact, Frank Wong, at (615) 347-1322. He will verify all equipment has been located.</u></strong></p><p>1.5 Find the “HOLD FOR HP TECH” register boxes (Figure 1) and Genesco peripheral box with GREEN tape (Figure 2). Take a complete inventory. Ensure inventory count matches Pages 7 and 8 which will include registers and peripherals.</p><p>1.6 Capture HP POS Serial Numbers in Appendix B (Sign-off) while taking inventory. You can also validate Serial Numbers and full inventory list with the PDF Packing List sent to you by HP PMO.</p><p>1.7 Be sure to report any issues IMMEDIATELY with the HP command center and Genesco Site Contact if device counts are not 100% accurate (find full inventory list in appendix A).</p><p>1.8 HP techs are NOT to install any additional software or perform any configurations on the new devices. This will all be done by the techs with the POS HD.</p><p>2.0 Inventory of Items</p><p>The following items will be on site for the new store installation and will need to be verified before installation:</p><p>2.1 HP REGISTER PACKAGE ITEMS – There will be qty 1 per register for each of the following:</p><p>A – RPOS Device (HP Engage One) - 2R0K9US#ABA</p><p>B – Epson Receipt Printer - 295X5U3</p><p>C – Cash Drawer Cable (RJ 12) - CD-101A</p><p>D – HP Keyboard - T4E63AA#ABA</p><p>E – HP Mouse – T4E63AA#ABA</p><p>F – Epson Receipt Printer Cable (There will be 1 per device being replaced) - 295X6U3</p><p>G – Cash Drawer - QT457AA#ABA</p><p>H – APC UPS Battery Back Up –- BE600M1</p><p>J – Printer Power Cable 24V Powered USB to CPU PWRCBL - *JB609</p><p>K – Credit Card Pinpad</p><p>L – Green Ethernet Cable – No Picture Displayed</p><p>M – Honeywell Scanner</p><p>N – AML Kit</p><p>O – AML Cable – No Picture Displayed</p><p>P - Report Printer</p><p>Q – Report Printer USB Cable</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Parts Instructions</u></strong></p><p>Technician is required to have <em>AT LEAST</em> 1000' Cat5e (or Cat6) Plenum cable, multiple biscuit jacks, crimp tool, cable tester, AT LEAST a 10' ladder, punch down tool, drill with various bit sizes, hole saws, wire stripper, RJ-45 to RJ-45 connectors, and of course, a smart phone.</p><p>PLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.</p><p>Technician will be compensated for all materials used on site.</p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be Paid</u></strong></p><p>1. <strong><em>MUST</em></strong> check in &amp; out with the <strong>POSRG Work Order Manager</strong></p><p>2. <strong><em>MUST</em></strong> leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.</p><p>4. Take before &amp; after pictures to confirm work completion.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance</u></strong></p><p>Do <strong><em>NOT</em></strong> request the work order if you are <strong><em>NOT</em></strong> qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*Please read the documentation attached to this WO prior to arriving on site\\*\\*\n\n***DO NOT USE ZIP TIES-- VELCRO ONLY***\n\nTech will need a government issued Photo ID to pick up parts from FedEx before install\n\nFedEx Office Print &amp; Ship Center4900 NC-55 Ste 4101, Durham, NC 27713\n\n***﻿***\n\n**Scope of Work \\*\\*\\*Information from the attached documentation\\*\\*\\***\n\n1.0 Arriving on site\n\nWhen arriving onsite there are two layers of checking in. Once with the HP Command Center and once with the site contact. See below for related instructions.\n\n1.1 Arrive on-site on time.\n\n1.2 Check in via e-mail through the Project PDL genescods@hp.com.\n\n1.3 Walk inside to check in with the site contact (site superintendent).\n\n**1.4 Check in with the Genesco Site Contact, Frank Wong, at (615) 347-1322. He will verify all equipment has been located.**\n\n1.5 Find the “HOLD FOR HP TECH” register boxes (Figure 1) and Genesco peripheral box with GREEN tape (Figure 2). Take a complete inventory. Ensure inventory count matches Pages 7 and 8 which will include registers and peripherals.\n\n1.6 Capture HP POS Serial Numbers in Appendix B (Sign-off) while taking inventory. You can also validate Serial Numbers and full inventory list with the PDF Packing List sent to you by HP PMO.\n\n1.7 Be sure to report any issues IMMEDIATELY with the HP command center and Genesco Site Contact if device counts are not 100% accurate (find full inventory list in appendix A).\n\n1.8 HP techs are NOT to install any additional software or perform any configurations on the new devices. This will all be done by the techs with the POS HD.\n\n2.0 Inventory of Items\n\nThe following items will be on site for the new store installation and will need to be verified before installation:\n\n2.1 HP REGISTER PACKAGE ITEMS – There will be qty 1 per register for each of the following:\n\nA – RPOS Device (HP Engage One) - 2R0K9US#ABA\n\nB – Epson Receipt Printer - 295X5U3\n\nC – Cash Drawer Cable (RJ 12) - CD-101A\n\nD – HP Keyboard - T4E63AA#ABA\n\nE – HP Mouse – T4E63AA#ABA\n\nF – Epson Receipt Printer Cable (There will be 1 per device being replaced) - 295X6U3\n\nG – Cash Drawer - QT457AA#ABA\n\nH – APC UPS Battery Back Up –- BE600M1\n\nJ – Printer Power Cable 24V Powered USB to CPU PWRCBL - \\*JB609\n\nK – Credit Card Pinpad\n\nL – Green Ethernet Cable – No Picture Displayed\n\nM – Honeywell Scanner\n\nN – AML Kit\n\nO – AML Cable – No Picture Displayed\n\nP - Report Printer\n\nQ – Report Printer USB Cable\n\n**Parts Instructions**\n\nTechnician is required to have *AT LEAST* 1000' Cat5e (or Cat6) Plenum cable, multiple biscuit jacks, crimp tool, cable tester, AT LEAST a 10' ladder, punch down tool, drill with various bit sizes, hole saws, wire stripper, RJ-45 to RJ-45 connectors, and of course, a smart phone.\n\nPLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.\n\nTechnician will be compensated for all materials used on site.\n\n**Required Deliverables to be Paid**\n\n1\\. ***MUST*** check in &amp; out with the **POSRG Work Order Manager**\n\n2\\. ***MUST*** leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.\n\n4\\. Take before &amp; after pictures to confirm work completion.\n\n**Work Order Acceptance**\n\nDo ***NOT*** request the work order if you are ***NOT*** qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T11:00","latestStart":"2026-11-03T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11.24984582774906},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793652441731}
{"job":{"id":20271130,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SG Network Services","title":"Circuit Cutover & Edge Device Install","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Swing existing Internet/MPLS circuits to Lumen DIA</li>\n<li>Install new edge devices</li>\n<li>Confirm device details (names, IP/inventory, ports, VLANs, diagrams, access requirements)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Onsite Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Installation Check:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm rack elevation and available space.</li>\n<li>Validate ports, labeling, and floor plan against documentation.</li>\n<li>Take “before” photos.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Circuit Cutover:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Disconnect existing Internet/MPLS circuits.</li>\n<li>Connect circuits to Lumen DIA/MPLS per plan.</li>\n<li>Verify connectivity with remote engineer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Edge Device Installation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rack and mount edge devices.</li>\n<li>Connect required cabling.</li>\n<li>Power on devices and confirm LED status.</li>\n<li>Verify connectivity to Lumen circuits with remote engineer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Post-Installation Validation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm all devices are labeled correctly and ports match documentation.</li>\n<li>Document device details: name/serial, IPs, VLANs, port assignments, inventory check.</li>\n<li>Take “after” photos.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Documentation &amp; Sign-Off:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete site sign-off (acknowledged by local contact or remote engineer).</li>\n<li>Submit all photos, notes, and validation data to PM.</li>\n<li>Document any blockers, delays, or deviations from scope.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Swing existing Internet/MPLS circuits to Lumen DIA\n- Install new edge devices\n- Confirm device details (names, IP/inventory, ports, VLANs, diagrams, access requirements)\n\n**Onsite Tasks:**\n\n**Pre-Installation Check:**\n\n- Confirm rack elevation and available space.\n- Validate ports, labeling, and floor plan against documentation.\n- Take “before” photos.\n\n**Circuit Cutover:**\n\n- Disconnect existing Internet/MPLS circuits.\n- Connect circuits to Lumen DIA/MPLS per plan.\n- Verify connectivity with remote engineer.\n\n**Edge Device Installation:**\n\n- Rack and mount edge devices.\n- Connect required cabling.\n- Power on devices and confirm LED status.\n- Verify connectivity to Lumen circuits with remote engineer.\n\n**Post-Installation Validation:**\n\n- Confirm all devices are labeled correctly and ports match documentation.\n- Document device details: name/serial, IPs, VLANs, port assignments, inventory check.\n- Take “after” photos.\n\n**Documentation &amp; Sign-Off:**\n\n- Complete site sign-off (acknowledged by local contact or remote engineer).\n- Submit all photos, notes, and validation data to PM.\n- Document any blockers, delays, or deviations from scope.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-09T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.356802928487241},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"}