 order.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:30","end":"2026-11-06T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":54.48289285835693},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793653725453}
{"job":{"id":"6681090697","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"USPS Project - Circuit TTU/Router Install - 1365108  GOLDSTON NC","description":"USPS Project:  Phase 1 - Circuit Turn UP/Router Install<br><br>THIS TASK REQUIRES A HARD START. A REMOTE ENGINEER HAS BEEN SCHEDULED FOR THIS TIME SLOT.  PLEASE ARRIVE ON TIME.<br><br>** TECH MUST HAVE LAPTOP AND CONSOLE CABLE** <br> DO NOT CALL GRANITE TO CHECK IN/OUT!!<br><br>Print out attached LOA and take to site. The printed LOA is required for entry.  If entry is denied due to not having printed document, payment will withheld.<br><br>Upon Arrival:<br><br>Tech must check in through SS link: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/7fa11354b600492aaaa07b0fe8adddfa<br><br>1. Introduce yourself to the Postmaster and/or designated USPS local contact.<br><br>2. Please do not power on the Granite FlexEdge router until instructed to do so on the below bridge.<br><br>3. Locate the following Broadband circuit:<br><br><br>ISP: Starlink<br>CKT ID: 0<br>SPEED: 25M/8M<br><br>4. Locate the existing  Router (ISR)/T1 Router.<br><br>5. Locate the Switch. Confirm that the above Broadband circuit is available for use nearby. If necessary, extend the Broadband circuit nearby where the Switch is located.<br><br>6. Once the Granite Broadband circuit is available for use near the Switch is, please call into below bridge. <br><br>BRIDGE:  888-860-1069<br><br>7. Work with the contacts on the bridge to turn up the Granite router.<br> <br>Before Leaving site:<br>Tech must check out through SS link: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/7fa11354b600492aaaa07b0fe8adddfa<br><br>Required Tools / Materials:<br>Laptop, hotspot, console cables<br>200FT Cat5e or above cable<br>Cell phone with Camera phone<br><br>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:<br>Tech MUST be able to access the following SS link to check in and out:<br>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/7fa11354b600492aaaa07b0fe8adddfa<br><br>Access issues<br>BRIDGE: 929-229-2436 US<br>ACCE