{"job":{"id":20294307,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TPX Communications","title":"Install & Test new 5g cradle point.","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Install &amp; Test new 5g cradle point.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>=================SOW=============================</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Store 58. UNBOX AND INSTALL replacement 5g cradle point. Tech MUST confirm ALL services are back up and working before tech leaves. Tech MUST bring reliable laptop and ethernet patch cables. Tech to call into bridge at 10am Eastern Time for service turn up. Tech to work with MSX Network Engineer, MSIS Lisa Starks for Hot Cut. TEAMS Bridge# 213-255-3273 PIN 385 768 230#&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************************************************</p><p><em>\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"</em></p><p><em>\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\" </em></p><p><em>Please make sure to mark </em><strong><em>'On My Way</em></strong><em>' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”</em></p><p><em>Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.</em></p><p><em>Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.</em></p><p><em>**If you are calling to </em><strong><em><u>check in</u></em></strong><em><u> </u>for a scheduled work order, please </em><strong><em>press 3</em></strong><em> to leave a message.</em></p><p><em>**If </em><strong><em>after 5pm PST </em></strong><em>for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please </em><strong><em>press 1</em></strong><em> to reach the On-Call team.</em></p><p><em>****************************************************************************************************</em></p><p><strong>DRESS CODE</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual or professional attire required</li><li>No other company logos or branding permitted (TPX branding only, if applicable)</li><li>Closed-toe shoes required (no sandals)</li><li>Safety gear must be worn if site requires (PPE)</li><li>Present yourself professionally as a TPX representative</li></ul><p><strong>PRE-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Review the Scope of Work and its requirements.</li><li>Call TPx Support with any questions or clarification about the Scope of Work</li></ul><p><strong>ON-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Check In on the Field Nation Portal</li><li>Call TPx Support&nbsp;to check in 833-294-6642&nbsp;before entering premises. <em>If after </em><strong><em>5pm</em></strong><em> PST, press </em><strong><em>option 3</em></strong><em> leave a message.</em></li><li>Introduce yourself as representative of TPX and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal</li></ul><p>Call into Bridge Number on Tim<del>* ******* ************** ****** ***** *** *** ***** </del>scheduled: (time) <del>*</del>10am ET&nbsp;<del>*</del></p><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;POST-SITE WORK</strong></p><ul><li>Confirm deliverables are complete</li><li>Enter Close out notes and any client feedback into Order</li><li>Clean-up work materials from installation (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)</li><li>Call TPX Communications from customer’s site to check out <strong>833-294-6642 (</strong>If after 5pm PST, press <strong>option 3</strong> leave a message &amp; we will follow up next Business day)</li><li>Enter Release Code (Given by the Support at the time of close out)</li><li>Check out in Field Nation Portal</li></ul><p><strong>ESCALATIONS</strong></p><ul><li>Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site <strong>833-294-6642</strong></li><li>DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform outside of the scope work, call TPx Support <strong>833-294-6642</strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><p><strong><u>Requirements:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li><li>Windows&nbsp;7 or 10&nbsp;Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li><li>Active Email Address</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP</strong></p><ul><li>Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)</li><li>AnyDesk</li><li>Aeroadmin</li><li>HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li><li>FTP Client</li><li>TFTP Server software</li><li>MircoSIP (SIP call testing- https://www.microsip.org/)</li><li>Wireshark</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING</strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet Patch Cable</li><li>Cisco Console Cable​</li><li>USB to DB9 male serial Cable</li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><ul><li>Buttset</li><li>Line man’s test set or analog test set</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool</li><li>Snips</li><li>Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks</li><li>Tone Generator and Wand</li><li>Drill/ Dry wall screws</li><li>4’ ladder</li><li>CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)</li><li>Pre-made crossover cables</li><li>RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors</li><li>Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)</li><li>Power inverter</li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- Install &amp; Test new 5g cradle point.\n\n=================SOW=============================\n\nStore 58. UNBOX AND INSTALL replacement 5g cradle point. Tech MUST confirm ALL services are back up and working before tech leaves. Tech MUST bring reliable laptop and ethernet patch cables. Tech to call into bridge at 10am Eastern Time for service turn up. Tech to work with MSX Network Engineer, MSIS Lisa Starks for Hot Cut. TEAMS Bridge# 213-255-3273 PIN 385 768 230#\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*\"For any work outside of the scope please contact TPx Support.\"*\n\n*\"After 2.5 hours, we kindly ask that the provider informs us if they anticipate the work on site will go over the 3-hour mark. This helps us plan accordingly and ensures that we may provide necessary support and resources if needed.\"*\n\n*Please make sure to mark* ***'On My Way****' in Field Nation at least one hour before your scheduled on-site time. This is a key step we rely on to confirm readiness.”*\n\n*Provider is required to contact the customer at least 1hour prior to arrival to confirm the estimated ETA. Failure to make contact in advance may result in delays.*\n\n*Our business hours are Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 5:00 PM Pacific Time.*\n\n*\\*\\*If you are calling to* ***check in*** *for a scheduled work order, please* ***press 3*** *to leave a message.*\n\n*\\*\\*If* ***after 5pm PST*** *for urgent issues requiring immediate assistance, please* ***press 1*** *to reach the On-Call team.*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**DRESS CODE**\n\n- Business casual or professional attire required\n- No other company logos or branding permitted (TPX branding only, if applicable)\n- Closed-toe shoes required (no sandals)\n- Safety gear must be worn if site requires (PPE)\n- Present yourself professionally as a TPX representative\n\n**PRE-SITE WORK**\n\n- Review the Scope of Work and its requirements.\n- Call TPx Support with any questions or clarification about the Scope of Work\n\n**ON-SITE WORK**\n\n- Check In on the Field Nation Portal\n- Call TPx Support to check in 833-294-6642 before entering premises. *If after* ***5pm*** *PST, press* ***option 3*** *leave a message.*\n- Introduce yourself as representative of TPX and enter their name into the Required Task in the Field Nation Portal\n\nCall into Bridge Number on Tim\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* scheduled: (time) \\*10am ET \\*\n\n **POST-SITE WORK**\n\n- Confirm deliverables are complete\n- Enter Close out notes and any client feedback into Order\n- Clean-up work materials from installation (wire clipping, boxes, trash, and any other debris)\n- Call TPX Communications from customer’s site to check out **833-294-6642 (**If after 5pm PST, press **option 3** leave a message &amp; we will follow up next Business day)\n- Enter Release Code (Given by the Support at the time of close out)\n- Check out in Field Nation Portal\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- Call Technical Support number if you encounter any issues on-site **833-294-6642**\n- DO NOT perform any work outside of scope. If asked to perform outside of the scope work, call TPx Support **833-294-6642**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n- Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n- Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n- Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE FOR LAPTOP**\n\n- Teamviewer 12 (MUST be version 12)\n- AnyDesk\n- Aeroadmin\n- HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n- FTP Client\n- TFTP Server software\n- MircoSIP (SIP call testing- <https://www.microsip.org/>)\n- Wireshark\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES FOR LAPTOP TESTING**\n\n- Ethernet Patch Cable\n- Cisco Console Cable​\n- USB to DB9 male serial Cable\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\n- Buttset\n- Line man’s test set or analog test set\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 crimp tool\n- Snips\n- Punch down tool with blades for 66 and 110 blocks\n- Tone Generator and Wand\n- Drill/ Dry wall screws\n- 4’ ladder\n- CAT5e or CAT6 cable (minimum of 250’ for usage of extending circuits or making a patch cable for a data drop)\n- Pre-made crossover cables\n- RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors\n- Pre-made Ethernet patch cables (5pack of each-length of 3’/5’/7’)\n- Power inverter","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:30","end":"2026-11-09T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.39958042777496},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summ