{"job":{"id":20296187,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"RDS Davenport","title":"Run VGA cable from office to monitor in kitchen - Custard and Make stations","description":{"html":"<p>Kitchen Monitor VGA Cable Replacement - Custard and Make stations</p><p><strong>Schedule:</strong> 8am</p><p><strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> 1-2 hours</p><p><strong>Support:</strong> Call RDS at 972-441-2671, select option 1 (mandatory check-in and check-out)</p>Pre-Work Documentation<p>Before beginning any work, the technician must take clear photos of all registers and kitchen monitors. These photos will serve as a record of the pre-existing setup and ensure proper documentation for the site.</p>Project Overview<p>This site has a faulty VGA cable connecting the kitchen controller in the office to the kitchen monitor. The technician will replace the existing VGA cable with the new cable that is already on site.</p><br>Required Tools &amp; Equipment<ul><li>Replacement VGA cable (on-site)</li><li>Screwdriver or tool for any mount removal if needed</li><li>Camera (phone or other) to take pre- and post-work photos</li><li>Labeling materials if required</li></ul>On-Site Procedures<p><strong>Arrival and Check-In</strong></p><ol><li>Check in with the store manager.</li><li>Call RDS support at 972-441-2671, select option 1 and check in with the help desk.</li></ol><p><strong>Pre-Work Tasks</strong></p><ol><li>Take photos of all registers and kitchen monitors before starting.</li></ol><p><strong>Hardware Replacement</strong></p><ol><li>Identify the VGA cable that needs to be replaced.</li><li>Disconnect the existing cable from the kitchen controller and kitchen monitor.</li><li>Run the new VGA cable from the office to the kitchen monitor.</li><li>Secure connections and ensure the cable is neatly routed and out of the way.</li></ol><p><strong>Testing and Validation</strong></p><ol><li>Call RDS support at 972-441-2671 to confirm the kitchen monitor is displaying correctly.</li><li>Verify the monitor is operational and displays properly.</li></ol><p><strong>Documentation &amp; Check-Out</strong></p><ul><li>Take <strong>after-photos</strong> showing:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">New VGA cable connections at both ends</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Monitor powered on and displaying correctly</li><li>Confirm with the store manager that everything is working properly.</li><li>Check out with RDS support via call.</li></ul>Completion Criteria<ul><li>Pre- and post-work photos taken and documented.</li><li>VGA cable replaced and securely connected.</li><li>Kitchen monitor confirmed working with RDS support.</li><li>All tools removed from site and area left clean.</li></ul>","markdown":"Kitchen Monitor VGA Cable Replacement - Custard and Make stations\n\n**Schedule:** 8am\n\n**Estimated Duration:** 1-2 hours\n\n**Support:** Call RDS at 972-441-2671, select option 1 (mandatory check-in and check-out)\n\nPre-Work DocumentationBefore beginning any work, the technician must take clear photos of all registers and kitchen monitors. These photos will serve as a record of the pre-existing setup and ensure proper documentation for the site.\n\nProject OverviewThis site has a faulty VGA cable connecting the kitchen controller in the office to the kitchen monitor. The technician will replace the existing VGA cable with the new cable that is already on site.\n\n  \nRequired Tools &amp; Equipment- Replacement VGA cable (on-site)\n- Screwdriver or tool for any mount removal if needed\n- Camera (phone or other) to take pre- and post-work photos\n- Labeling materials if required\n\nOn-Site Procedures**Arrival and Check-In**\n\n1. Check in with the store manager.\n2. Call RDS support at 972-441-2671, select option 1 and check in with the help desk.\n\n**Pre-Work Tasks**\n\n1. Take photos of all registers and kitchen monitors before starting.\n\n**Hardware Replacement**\n\n1. Identify the VGA cable that needs to be replaced.\n2. Disconnect the existing cable from the kitchen controller and kitchen monitor.\n3. Run the new VGA cable from the office to the kitchen monitor.\n4. Secure connections and ensure the cable is neatly routed and out of the way.\n\n**Testing and Validation**\n\n1. Call RDS support at 972-441-2671 to confirm the kitchen monitor is displaying correctly.\n2. Verify the monitor is operational and displays properly.\n\n**Documentation &amp; Check-Out**\n\n- Take **after-photos** showing:\n- New VGA cable connections at both ends\n- Monitor powered on and displaying correctly\n- Confirm with the store manager that everything is working properly.\n- Check out with RDS support via call.\n\nCompletion Criteria- Pre- and post-work photos taken and documented.\n- VGA cable replaced and securely connected.\n- Kitchen monitor confirmed working with RDS support.\n- All tools removed from site and area left clean.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T08:00","end":"2026-11-09T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14.12018752304256},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793659319585}
{"job":{"id":20296249,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Xeal","title":"Electrical Evaluation/ Breaker resets/ Firmware updates","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Tools Needed</strong></p><ul><li>T-20 security torx bit or screwdriver.</li><li>#2 Phillips bit and screwdriver.</li><li>Multimeter to check voltage at each charger and connection point.&nbsp;</li><li>Torque wrench.</li><li>\"1/4\" screwdriver.</li><li>Infrared thermometer temperature gun and EV for testing(not required but nice to have for testing).</li></ul><p><strong>Upon Arrival:</strong></p><ul><li>If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable.</li><li>Site contact:</li></ul><p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Inspect all chargers for FW and faults </strong></li><li><strong>Issue</strong>: Some chargers have red fault lights, almost all need a firmware update</li><li><strong>Check the electrical panel that is connected to the charger, check wiring. Check for any visible damage to the charger, the pedestal and to the wires.</strong></li><li><strong>Open the charger to make sure all internal components are wired correctly(see attached reference photo), check for loose wires by pushing on any connections, DO NOT PULL ON WIRES.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for loose wires at the junction box or circuit breaker wire connectors, wire nuts and terminal blocks. Check for water or moisture inside junction box or conduit.</strong></li><li><strong>At the breaker, check to confirm that the breakers sit flush in their casing and do not appear uneven. If you notice a loose breaker, please contact the work order manager and attach a photo to the work order.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Torque breaker connections to 25 lbf-in and check voltage.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for any signs of smoke or burnt wires inside the charger, check torque on L1, L2, T1, T2 are secure (25 lbf-in). If loose, torque these screws with a torque wrench until you hear a click sound. STOP AFTER YOUR HEAR THE FIRST \"CLICK\".</strong></li><li><strong>Check for excessive discoloration or burning at both the Xeal connector and Customer Charging Port connections(photo attached). Check for excessive damage to connector plugs and cable.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for corrosion, cleanliness and contamination.</strong></li><li><strong>If possible - check the breaker temperature while the charger is in use.</strong></li></ul><p>Notify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:</p><ul><li>If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)</li><li>If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.</li><li>If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster</li><li>Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete</li></ul><p><strong>Standard Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>It is recommended you bring a cleaning cloth with you as the chargers can get very dirty, and should be wiped down and cords wrapped at each visit.&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Tools Needed**\n\n- T-20 security torx bit or screwdriver.\n- \\#2 Phillips bit and screwdriver.\n- Multimeter to check voltage at each charger and connection point.\n- Torque wrench.\n- \"1/4\" screwdriver.\n- Infrared thermometer temperature gun and EV for testing(not required but nice to have for testing).\n\n**Upon Arrival:**\n\n- If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable.\n- Site contact:\n\n**Scope:**\n\n- **Inspect all chargers for FW and faults**\n- **Issue**: Some chargers have red fault lights, almost all need a firmware update\n- **Check the electrical panel that is connected to the charger, check wiring. Check for any visible damage to the charger, the pedestal and to the wires.**\n- **Open the charger to make sure all internal components are wired correctly(see attached reference photo), check for loose wires by pushing on any connections, DO NOT PULL ON WIRES.**\n- **Check for loose wires at the junction box or circuit breaker wire connectors, wire nuts and terminal blocks. Check for water or moisture inside junction box or conduit.**\n- **At the breaker, check to confirm that the breakers sit flush in their casing and do not appear uneven. If you notice a loose breaker, please contact the work order manager and attach a photo to the work order.**\n- **Torque breaker connections to 25 lbf-in and check voltage.**\n- **Check for any signs of smoke or burnt wires inside the charger, check torque on L1, L2, T1, T2 are secure (25 lbf-in). If loose, torque these screws with a torque wrench until you hear a click sound. STOP AFTER YOUR HEAR THE FIRST \"CLICK\".**\n- **Check for excessive discoloration or burning at both the Xeal connector and Customer Charging Port connections(photo attached). Check for excessive damage to connector plugs and cable.**\n- **Check for corrosion, cleanliness and contamination.**\n- **If possible - check the breaker temperature while the charger is in use.**\n\nNotify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:\n\n- If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)\n- If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.\n- If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster\n- Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete\n\n**Standard Instructions**\n\n- It is recommended you bring a cleaning cloth with you as the chargers can get very dirty, and should be wiped down and cords wrapped at each visit.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T10:45","end":"2026-11-04T13:45","latestStart":"2026-11-04T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":270},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":90,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":4.7897454694600246},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $270 (countered: $270) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793659696132}
{"job":{"id":20296206,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Site Activation/Turn -UP/ Test - VERIFY CONNECTIVITY WITH REMOTE TEAM /  MB1706632 MB1706630","description":{"html":"<p><em>THIS IS A HARD START - IT IS A HOT CUT OVER AND A BRIDGE CALL HAS BEEN SCHEDULED WITH MULTIPLE PARTIES --- DO NOT BE LATE </em></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>﻿</u><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: -apple-system;\">***SITE ACTIVATION ONLY***</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri;\"> </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri;\">-If Necessary</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: -apple-system;\">Equipment MUST be mounted in the customer rack - Escalate with Remote Engineer if there is not adequate space in the rack</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: -apple-system;\">Communicate via Bridge or Hotline with Remote Engineer to cable equipment into correct ports.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: -apple-system;\">SOW: Complete installation and remote testing of the Circuit and the FortiGate device</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> Bridge Call Start Time: 11/05/2026 10:00 AM</strong></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Activate circuit with remote support</li></ol><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including bridge line details, lcon info, and equipment information</em></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">Please bring a </span><span style=\"color: rgb(244, 5, 5);\">NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements</span></p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger &amp; TeamViewer Installed</li><li>Hot Spot or Internet Dongle</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger</li><li>Console Cable <span style=\"color: rgb(234, 5, 5);\">(Please see attached images for reference)</span></li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)</li></ul><p><em>*Additional Tools Requested*</em></p><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID required</li><li>Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>******* ******** ****** ************** *******</del></li><li>Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE</li></ul>","markdown":"*THIS IS A HARD START - IT IS A HOT CUT OVER AND A BRIDGE CALL HAS BEEN SCHEDULED WITH MULTIPLE PARTIES --- DO NOT BE LATE*\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n﻿ **\\*\\*\\*SITE ACTIVATION ONLY\\*\\*\\***\n\n**-If Necessary**\n\n**Equipment MUST be mounted in the customer rack - Escalate with Remote Engineer if there is not adequate space in the rack**\n\n**Communicate via Bridge or Hotline with Remote Engineer to cable equipment into correct ports.**\n\n**SOW: Complete installation and remote testing of the Circuit and the FortiGate device**\n\n **Bridge Call Start Time: 11/05/2026 10:00 AM**\n\n1. Activate circuit with remote support\n\n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including bridge line details, lcon info, and equipment information*\n\nPlease bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements\n\n**Tool Requirements:**\n\n- WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger &amp; TeamViewer Installed\n- Hot Spot or Internet Dongle\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Cell Phone - with Charger\n- Console Cable (Please see attached images for reference)\n- Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)\n\n*\\*Additional Tools Requested\\**\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T09:30","end":"2026-11-05T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":35.660542807604564},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: