{"job":{"id":20296395,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ReSource Point of Sale LLC","title":"**BRING LADDER** Troubleshoot/Repair Digital Menu Board Controllers Issues - Qdoba #3443","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the Helpdesk.</strong></p><p><strong><em>﻿**If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite**</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>**TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED,&nbsp;<u>PRIOR&nbsp;</u>TO ASSIGNMENT**</em></strong></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULING:</u></strong></p><p>Please attempt to contact the manager to make them aware of your ETA. Please see below for certain site requirements.</p><ul><li><strong><em>Military Base Location:</em></strong> Technician will need 2 forms of ID, including a Real ID or Military ID. Tech also must schedule an escort.</li><li><strong><em>Airport Location:</em> </strong>Technician will need a form of ID and must schedule an escort.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work: Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the Work Order</u></strong></p><p>**BRING A LADDER**</p><p>Two media players are located behind the Digital Menu Displays above the service line.&nbsp;</p><p>1.\tVerify network cables are plugged into the media players and the data ports on the valance/soffit wall.</p><p>2.\tEnsure the media players are plugged into Ports 15 and 16 of the Meraki Network Switch.</p><p>3.\tPower Cycle off and on both media players 1 and 2, located behind the digital menu boards. This will reset the media players and reestablish connections.</p><p>4.\tCall into Stratacache Support # at <strong>1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba) </strong>to confirm Stratacache sees both devices online for the restaurant, or work through additional troubleshooting steps.</p><p>5.\tOnce Stratacache confirms seeing both devices online, the visit has been completed.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>MANDATORY Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>LADDER</li><li>Basic hand tools, such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.</li><li>CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.&nbsp;</li><li>Keyboard &amp; Mouse</li></ul><p><br></p><p>The low voltage is usually run through conduit, but most failures occur at the wall jacks or the patch cables for connectivity issues.&nbsp;</p><p>Please bring CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.&nbsp;</p><p>Please bring basic hand tools such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.</p><p><br></p><p>Materials used can be expensed. Thanks!&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>​</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Checkout and Escalations Team:</u></strong></p><p> Stratacache Support # at <strong>1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba) </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Liabilities and Warranty Information - Store Management</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Limitation of Liability:</em></strong><em> In all events, RPOS will not be responsible for any lost, stolen, or damaged materials. Customer hereby agree that Resource Point of Sale LLC shall not be liable to Customer, or any third party, for (1) any liability claims, loss, damages or expense of any kind arising directly or indirectly out of services provided herein for (2) any incidental or consequential damages, however caused, and Customer agrees to indemnify and hold Company harmless against such liabilities, claims, losses, damages (consequential or otherwise) or expenses, or actions in respect thereof, asserted or brought against Company by or in right of third parties or for (3) any punitive damages. For purposes of this Agreement, incidental or consequential damages shall include, but not be limited to, loss of anticipated revenues, income, profits or savings; loss of or damage to business reputation or good will; loss of Customers; loss of business or financial opportunity; or any other indirect or special damages of any kind categorized as consequential or incidental damages under the law of the State of Illinois.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Services Warranty.</em></strong><em> Company warrants that all Services performed pursuant to this Agreement will be performed in accordance with the general standards and practices of the point of sale services industry in existence at the time the Services are being performed. The Services provided under this SOW shall be warranted for a period of (15) days following the satisfactory completion of any services under the SOW. Any warranty claim must be made in writing within the allotted (15) days, after the acceptance of the service. RPOS’s sole obligation and customers exclusive remedy in respect thereof is to re-perform the service. </em></p>","markdown":"**You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the Helpdesk.**\n\n***﻿\\*\\*If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite\\*\\****\n\n***\\*\\*TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED, PRIOR TO ASSIGNMENT\\*\\****\n\n**SCHEDULING:**\n\nPlease attempt to contact the manager to make them aware of your ETA. Please see below for certain site requirements.\n\n- ***Military Base Location:*** Technician will need 2 forms of ID, including a Real ID or Military ID. Tech also must schedule an escort.\n- ***Airport Location:*** Technician will need a form of ID and must schedule an escort.\n\n**Scope of Work: Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the Work Order**\n\n\\*\\*BRING A LADDER\\*\\*\n\nTwo media players are located behind the Digital Menu Displays above the service line.\n\n1\\. Verify network cables are plugged into the media players and the data ports on the valance/soffit wall.\n\n2\\. Ensure the media players are plugged into Ports 15 and 16 of the Meraki Network Switch.\n\n3\\. Power Cycle off and on both media players 1 and 2, located behind the digital menu boards. This will reset the media players and reestablish connections.\n\n4\\. Call into Stratacache Support # at **1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba)** to confirm Stratacache sees both devices online for the restaurant, or work through additional troubleshooting steps.\n\n5\\. Once Stratacache confirms seeing both devices online, the visit has been completed.\n\n**MANDATORY Tools:**\n\n- LADDER\n- Basic hand tools, such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.\n- CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.\n- Keyboard &amp; Mouse\n\nThe low voltage is usually run through conduit, but most failures occur at the wall jacks or the patch cables for connectivity issues.\n\nPlease bring CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.\n\nPlease bring basic hand tools such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.\n\nMaterials used can be expensed. Thanks!\n\n**​**\n\n**Checkout and Escalations Team:**\n\n Stratacache Support # at **1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba)**\n\n**Liabilities and Warranty Information - Store Management**\n\n***Limitation of Liability:*** *In all events, RPOS will not be responsible for any lost, stolen, or damaged materials. Customer hereby agree that Resource Point of Sale LLC shall not be liable to Customer, or any third party, for (1) any liability claims, loss, damages or expense of any kind arising directly or indirectly out of services provided herein for (2) any incidental or consequential damages, however caused, and Customer agrees to indemnify and hold Company harmless against such liabilities, claims, losses, damages (consequential or otherwise) or expenses, or actions in respect thereof, asserted or brought against Company by or in right of third parties or for (3) any punitive damages. For purposes of this Agreement, incidental or consequential damages shall include, but not be limited to, loss of anticipated revenues, income, profits or savings; loss of or damage to business reputation or good will; loss of Customers; loss of business or financial opportunity; or any other indirect or special damages of any kind categorized as consequential or incidental damages under the law of the State of Illinois.*\n\n***Services Warranty.*** *Company warrants that all Services performed pursuant to this Agreement will be performed in accordance with the general standards and practices of the point of sale services industry in existence at the time the Services are being performed. The Services provided under this SOW shall be warranted for a period of (15) days following the satisfactory completion of any services under the SOW. Any warranty claim must be made in writing within the allotted (15) days, after the acceptance of the service. RPOS’s sole obligation and customers exclusive remedy in respect thereof is to re-perform the service.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T09:00","end":"2026-11-03T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":205},"payType":"blende