{"job":{"id":20297525,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":" PPT1058512 || PAREXEL International LLC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Service Overview:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Scope - OS upgrade standby support - we need an engineer to be onsite to assist with the OS upgrade if anything went wrong, the engineer should have laptop, USB console cable and mobile Internet access.</p><p>Time - 9:00 am local time on November 6th 2026&nbsp;</p><p>Local contact - Fred Fazly Fred.Fazly@parexel.com +1 (919) 544 3170</p><p>Site address - Parexel HQ Tower 5 - North Hills (Raleigh), 541 Church at North Hills St., Suite 1000, Raleigh - UNITED STATES</p><p><br></p><p>If any question, please contact Andy Zhang @86 13801795112.</p><p><strong>Resource Level:</strong> Level 2 </p><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Pre-Task Requirement:</strong> Following assignment, Park Place may require a pre-engagement (\"pregame\") call between the assigned Provider and our Support team to review the scope, technical requirements, and site expectations. If, during this call, it is determined that the assigned Provider does not possess the skills, qualifications, or experience required to successfully perform the work, the provider will be released from the assignment and forfeit the work order without compensation.</p><p><strong>Dress code</strong>: Business casual attire is required (Khakis and collared shirt).</p><p>Technician will represent themselves as being a Park Place technician. Do not solicit or hand out business cards; always present yourself as a Park Place Technologies Engineer and not any other company/ your own company.</p><p>All visits must be approved by the Client POC and Park Place prior to the schedule. Technician shall not show up to the site unannounced.</p><p>Only the Customer can initiate a reschedule - if customer requests a reschedule, call Park Place <strong>before </strong>departing the site at <del>***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p><strong>English Language Requirement -</strong>Business conversations, instructions, and support communications related to completing this SOW are exclusively in English: therefore, technicians must be able to fluently read, speak, write, and understand the English language to allow for communication with on-site contacts and remote support, as well as understanding of scope documents, WO tasks, and other instructions.&nbsp;</p><p>Technician will arrive on-site with agreed <strong>Standard Toolkit</strong>:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Driver’s license or appropriate government issued ID</li><li>Mobile phone and charger; hot spot tethering device (cell signal dependent)</li><li>Laptop and charger (TeamViewer software capable)</li><li>Torx bits, screwdrivers, pliers, side cutters and adjustable wrench</li><li>Console Cable (DB9)</li><li>Cisco Console Cable CAB-CONSOLE (RJ45-DB9 Female)</li><li>Multi-meter</li></ul><p><strong><u>Escalations</u>:</strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any issues unrelated to technical support, call Park Place Support at <del> ***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p>2.&nbsp;For onsite technical support, please reach out to the “Remote Support/L2 contact” indicated under the Confidential Information section.&nbsp;Should you have any issues with reaching the Remote Support/L2 contact, please call Park Place Support at <del>***** ******** ****** **</del></p><p>Consumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place RH team immediately.</p>","markdown":"**Service Overview:**\n\n**Scope of Work:** Scope - OS upgrade standby support - we need an engineer to be onsite to assist with the OS upgrade if anything went wrong, the engineer should have laptop, USB console cable and mobile Internet access.\n\nTime - 9:00 am local time on November 6th 2026\n\nLocal contact - Fred Fazly Fred.Fazly@parexel.com +1 (919) 544 3170\n\nSite address - Parexel HQ Tower 5 - North Hills (Raleigh), 541 Church at North Hills St., Suite 1000, Raleigh - UNITED STATES\n\nIf any question, please contact Andy Zhang @86 13801795112.\n\n**Resource Level:** Level 2\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n**Pre-Task Requirement:** Following assignment, Park Place may require a pre-engagement (\"pregame\") call between the assigned Provider and our Support team to review the scope, technical requirements, and site expectations. If, during this call, it is determined that the assigned Provider does not possess the skills, qualifications, or experience required to successfully perform the work, the provider will be released from the assignment and forfeit the work order without compensation.\n\n**Dress code**: Business casual attire is required (Khakis and collared shirt).\n\nTechnician will represent themselves as being a Park Place technician. Do not solicit or hand out business cards; always present yourself as a Park Place Technologies Engineer and not any other company/ your own company.\n\nAll visits must be approved by the Client POC and Park Place prior to the schedule. Technician shall not show up to the site unannounced.\n\nOnly the Customer can initiate a reschedule - if customer requests a reschedule, call Park Place **before** departing the site at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n**English Language Requirement -**Business conversations, instructions, and support communications related to completing this SOW are exclusively in English: therefore, technicians must be able to fluently read, speak, write, and understand the English language to allow for communication with on-site contacts and remote support, as well as understanding of scope documents, WO tasks, and other instructions.\n\nTechnician will arrive on-site with agreed **Standard Toolkit**:\n\n- Driver’s license or appropriate government issued ID\n- Mobile phone and charger; hot spot tethering device (cell signal dependent)\n- Laptop and charger (TeamViewer software capable)\n- Torx bits, screwdrivers, pliers, side cutters and adjustable wrench\n- Console Cable (DB9)\n- Cisco Console Cable CAB-CONSOLE (RJ45-DB9 Female)\n- Multi-meter\n\n**Escalations:**\n\n1\\. Any issues unrelated to technical support, call Park Place Support at  \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n2\\. For onsite technical support, please reach out to the “Remote Support/L2 contact” indicated under the Confidential Information section. Should you have any issues with reaching the Remote Support/L2 contact, please call Park Place Support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\nConsumables (i.e. cables, SFPs, face plates, etc.) are not covered under this contract and will not be reimbursed without prior Park Place approval. Should the client ask you to supply any materials, remind them that this contract is labor only and engage the Park Place RH team immediately.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T09:00","end":"2026-11-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":7.111742204813794},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793702471618}
{"job":{"id":20297796,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ReSource Point of Sale LLC","title":"**BRING LADDER**Troubleshoot / Repair Digital Menu Board Controllers No Content - Qdoba #3443","description":{"html":"<p><strong>You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the Helpdesk.</strong></p><p><strong><em>﻿**If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite**</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>**TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED,&nbsp;<u>PRIOR&nbsp;</u>TO ASSIGNMENT**</em></strong></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULING:</u></strong></p><p>Please attempt to contact the manager to make them aware of your ETA. Please see below for certain site requirements.</p><ul><li><strong><em>Military Base Location:</em></strong> Technician will need 2 forms of ID, including a Real ID or Military ID. Tech also must schedule an escort.</li><li><strong><em>Airport Location:</em> </strong>Technician will need a form of ID and must schedule an escort.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work: Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the Work Order</u></strong></p><p>**BRING A LADDER**</p><p>Two media players are located behind the Digital Menu Displays above the service line.&nbsp;</p><p>1.\tVerify network cables are plugged into the media players and the data ports on the valance/soffit wall.</p><p>2.\tEnsure the media players are plugged into Ports 15 and 16 of the Meraki Network Switch.</p><p>3.\tPower Cycle off and on both media players 1 and 2, located behind the digital menu boards. This will reset the media players and reestablish connections.</p><p>4.\tCall into Stratacache Support # at <strong>1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba) </strong>to confirm Stratacache sees both devices online for the restaurant, or work through additional troubleshooting steps.</p><p>5.\tOnce Stratacache confirms seeing both devices online, the visit has been completed.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>MANDATORY Tools:</u></strong></p><ul><li>LADDER</li><li>Basic hand tools, such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.</li><li>CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.&nbsp;</li><li>Keyboard &amp; Mouse</li></ul><p><br></p><p>The low voltage is usually run through conduit, but most failures occur at the wall jacks or the patch cables for connectivity issues.&nbsp;</p><p>Please bring CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.&nbsp;</p><p>Please bring basic hand tools such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.</p><p><br></p><p>Materials used can be expensed. Thanks!&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>​</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Checkout and Escalations Team:</u></strong></p><p> Stratacache Support # at <strong>1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba) </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Liabilities and Warranty Information - Store Management</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Limitation of Liability:</em></strong><em> In all events, RPOS will not be responsible for any lost, stolen, or damaged materials. Customer hereby agree that Resource Point of Sale LLC shall not be liable to Customer, or any third party, for (1) any liability claims, loss, damages or expense of any kind arising directly or indirectly out of services provided herein for (2) any incidental or consequential damages, however caused, and Customer agrees to indemnify and hold Company harmless against such liabilities, claims, losses, damages (consequential or otherwise) or expenses, or actions in respect thereof, asserted or brought against Company by or in right of third parties or for (3) any punitive damages. For purposes of this Agreement, incidental or consequential damages shall include, but not be limited to, loss of anticipated revenues, income, profits or savings; loss of or damage to business reputation or good will; loss of Customers; loss of business or financial opportunity; or any other indirect or special damages of any kind categorized as consequential or incidental damages under the law of the State of Illinois.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Services Warranty.</em></strong><em> Company warrants that all Services performed pursuant to this Agreement will be performed in accordance with the general standards and practices of the point of sale services industry in existence at the time the Services are being performed. The Services provided under this SOW shall be warranted for a period of (15) days following the satisfactory completion of any services under the SOW. Any warranty claim must be made in writing within the allotted (15) days, after the acceptance of the service. RPOS’s sole obligation and customers exclusive remedy in respect thereof is to re-perform the service. </em></p>","markdown":"**You are authorized by RPOS Dispatch to handle additional repairs while onsite. We have no issues compensating technicians for helping out with our customers. Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the work order. Technician will be requested to perform cable repairs on CAT5e cabling, cabling clean-ups, or smart hands onsite to work with the Helpdesk.**\n\n***﻿\\*\\*If you are to counter for a FIXED RATE, you agree to no additional hourly rate increases, regardless of time onsite\\*\\****\n\n***\\*\\*TECH TO SUBMIT COUNTER OFFER FOR TRAVEL, IF NEEDED, PRIOR TO ASSIGNMENT\\*\\****\n\n**SCHEDULING:**\n\nPlease attempt to contact the manager to make them aware of your ETA. Please see below for certain site requirements.\n\n- ***Military Base Location:*** Technician will need 2 forms of ID, including a Real ID or Military ID. Tech also must schedule an escort.\n- ***Airport Location:*** Technician will need a form of ID and must schedule an escort.\n\n**Scope of Work: Follow the Tasks to successfully complete the Work Order**\n\n\\*\\*BRING A LADDER\\*\\*\n\nTwo media players are located behind the Digital Menu Displays above the service line.\n\n1\\. Verify network cables are plugged into the media players and the data ports on the valance/soffit wall.\n\n2\\. Ensure the media players are plugged into Ports 15 and 16 of the Meraki Network Switch.\n\n3\\. Power Cycle off and on both media players 1 and 2, located behind the digital menu boards. This will reset the media players and reestablish connections.\n\n4\\. Call into Stratacache Support # at **1-877-761-1122 (option 1, 7362 for Qdoba)** to confirm Stratacache sees both devices online for the restaurant, or work through additional troubleshooting steps.\n\n5\\. Once Stratacache confirms seeing both devices online, the visit has been completed.\n\n**MANDATORY Tools:**\n\n- LADDER\n- Basic hand tools, such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.\n- CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.\n- Keyboard &amp; Mouse\n\nThe low voltage is usually run through conduit, but most failures occur at the wall jacks or the patch cables for connectivity issues.\n\nPlease bring CAT-5e, RJ45 male and keystone, cable tester/toner, fish sticks or fish tape in case cable run is needed.\n\nPlease bring basic hand tools such as screw drivers of various sizes, socket sets metric and standard, zip ties or velcro straps for cable management.\n\nMaterials used can be expensed. Thanks!\n\n**​**\n\n**Checkout and Escalations Team:**\n\n Stratacache Support # at **1-877-761-1122 (option 1,