{"job":{"id":20297888,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"F2Onsite","title":"Durham, NC // Lenscrafters // Replace Cisco Switch // Nov 4th @ 10:00 AM LT","description":{"html":"<p>ONCE ASSIGNED PLEASE READ ATTACHED WORK ORDER PRIOR TO GOING ON SITE - THERE ARE LISTED TOOLS AND OTHER REQUIREMENTS THAT MUST BE MET IN ORDER TO BE APPROVED</p><p>***<strong><u>DO NOT START ANY WORK UNTIL YOU HAVE CHECKED IN WITH THE BRIDGE ON TEAMS***</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>******Complete attached form labeled \"SVR\" and attach to WO before leaving site.*******</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***URGENT*** Good communication is vital! We will need you to call or text us when you are en route to the site and then again after you arrive. Our customer requires real time updates from us throughout the process. DO NOT provide updates via this work order. Please call or text us.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***URGENT***</strong>&nbsp;This is a&nbsp;<strong>HARD START</strong>&nbsp;so please be onsite and ready to join the Team's meeting at the hard start time. Please don't get there at the start time as we have a support team who will be standing by waiting on us to get setup and started.</p><p><u>**Once you are asked for the time from the support team and they release you, if you need to stay and clean up, you MUST let them know and then check back in with the support team and inform them when the site is cleaned up and you are now leaving and give them that time. You will also need to make note of this in your closure notes so you are compensated for that additional time. If cleanup is more than 15 minutes, they may dispute your check out time.</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong>****Please note:</strong>&nbsp;if you do not have all of the required tools to complete this installation, and they are listed here, you will not be paid for the work. You must have the tools listed in the work order.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please join meeting link once onsite and in network room - this is located below in the Teams Link Custom Field</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Please have WhatsApp downloaded to your phone just in case it is needed.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><p>Need to replace the Cisco Switch and establish network connectivity at the site. (Please note: Device is in transit. FE to call GNOC after reaching the site.)&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Fault Description :\t</strong></p><p>The stores Voice switch is no longer receiving power. We have checked power plug and outlet. Outlet is working. The switch is still not showing power, however if you check the MDB it shows ports that are active. I tried to remotely reboot it but fails. Please investigate. MS220-24P e0:55:3d:9d:c5:ff</p><p><br></p><p>Tracking Info: <span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">1ZA08T051350765468 and 1ZA08T051350003450</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>FIELD ENGINEERS MUST ANNOUNCE THEMSELVES AS NSC EMPLOYEES AND UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES MENTION THE NAME OF THE COMPANY THEY ARE EMPLOYED BY</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;Step by Step Instructions for the Field Engineer:</p><p><br></p><ol><li>Please read the work order to have an understanding of what the scope entails before arriving onsite</li><li>Field engineer assigned/dispatched to customer site and must arrive onsite and be on the teams call at the requested start time shown above</li><li>Field engineer arrives at customer site and joins provided Microsoft Teams bridge using web browser or Teams App on phone or laptop</li><li>Field engineer verifies the job required to be carried out with the technical contact on bridge</li><li>Remote/bridge engineer will confirm once job is complete and provide release to field technician</li><li>Field engineer to assist with packing and shipping label for returned equipment (if applicable)</li><li>Field engineer to track and provide in/out time onsite</li><li>Field engineer completes the Site Visit Report provided by NSC Global and gets this signed by the onsite contact</li><li>Field Engineer to send the completed Site Visit Report back to NSC Global&nbsp;within 48 hours of job completion</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>ON-SITE ENGINEER REQUIREMENTS: The on-site engineer must have the following capabilities:</strong></p><p>- Suitably skilled to be able to complete this task.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>- Customer ID Badge (if required)</p><p>- Mobile phone and charger</p><p>- Laptop and charger</p><p>- TeamViewer installed on laptop</p><p>- Console cable (DB9)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>- 2 x Cat5E Patch cables, 10 and 3 metre</p><p>- Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RH45-DB9 Female)</p><p>-&nbsp;Console cable DB9 (+USB adapter) and the console cable MICRO USB-B to connect to router (tested in his laptop)</p><p>- Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screw Driver.</p><p>- Digital Camera</p>","markdown":"ONCE ASSIGNED PLEASE READ ATTACHED WORK ORDER PRIOR TO GOING ON SITE - THERE ARE LISTED TOOLS AND OTHER REQUIREMENTS THAT MUST BE MET IN ORDER TO BE APPROVED\n\n\\*\\*\\***DO NOT START ANY WORK UNTIL YOU HAVE CHECKED IN WITH THE BRIDGE ON TEAMS\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Complete attached form labeled \"SVR\" and attach to WO before leaving site.\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*URGENT\\*\\*\\* Good communication is vital! We will need you to call or text us when you are en route to the site and then again after you arrive. Our customer requires real time updates from us throughout the process. DO NOT provide updates via this work order. Please call or text us.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*URGENT\\*\\*\\*** This is a **HARD START** so please be onsite and ready to join the Team's meeting at the hard start time. Please don't get there at the start time as we have a support team who will be standing by waiting on us to get setup and started.\n\n\\*\\*Once you are asked for the time from the support team and they release you, if you need to stay and clean up, you MUST let them know and then check back in with the support team and inform them when the site is cleaned up and you are now leaving and give them that time. You will also need to make note of this in your closure notes so you are compensated for that additional time. If cleanup is more than 15 minutes, they may dispute your check out time.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*Please note:** if you do not have all of the required tools to complete this installation, and they are listed here, you will not be paid for the work. You must have the tools listed in the work order.\n\n**Please join meeting link once onsite and in network room - this is located below in the Teams Link Custom Field**\n\n**Please have WhatsApp downloaded to your phone just in case it is needed.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\nNeed to replace the Cisco Switch and establish network connectivity at the site. (Please note: Device is in transit. FE to call GNOC after reaching the site.)\n\n**Fault Description :**\n\nThe stores Voice switch is no longer receiving power. We have checked power plug and outlet. Outlet is working. The switch is still not showing power, however if you check the MDB it shows ports that are active. I tried to remotely reboot it but fails. Please investigate. MS220-24P e0:55:3d:9d:c5:ff\n\nTracking Info: 1ZA08T051350765468 and 1ZA08T051350003450\n\n***FIELD ENGINEERS MUST ANNOUNCE THEMSELVES AS NSC EMPLOYEES AND UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES MENTION THE NAME OF THE COMPANY THEY ARE EMPLOYED BY***\n\n Step by Step Instructions for the Field Engineer:\n\n1. Please read the work order to have an understanding of what the scope entails before arriving onsite\n2. Field engineer assigned/dispatched to customer site and must arrive onsite and be on the teams call at the requested start time shown above\n3. Field engineer arrives at customer site and joins provided Microsoft Teams bridge using web browser or Teams App on phone or laptop\n4. Field engineer verifies the job required to be carried out with the technical contact on bridge\n5. Remote/bridge engineer will confirm once job is complete and provide release to field technician\n6. Field engineer to assist with packing and shipping label for returned equipment (if applicable)\n7. Field engineer to track and provide in/out time onsite\n8. Field engineer completes the Site Visit Report provided by NSC Global and gets this signed by the onsite contact\n9. Field Engineer to send the completed Site Visit Report back to NSC Global within 48 hours of job completion\n\n**ON-SITE ENGINEER REQUIREMENTS: The on-site engineer must have the following capabilities:**\n\n\\- Suitably skilled to be able to complete this task.\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n\\- Customer ID Badge (if required)\n\n\\- Mobile phone and charger\n\n\\- Laptop and charger\n\n\\- TeamViewer installed on laptop\n\n\\- Console cable (DB9)\n\n\\- 2 x Cat5E Patch cables, 10 and 3 metre\n\n\\- Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAB-CONSOLE (RH45-DB9 Female)\n\n\\- Console cable DB9 (+USB adapter) and the console cable MICRO USB-B to connect to router (tested in his laptop)\n\n\\- Installation Tools - Cage Nuts, Screws, Screw Driver.\n\n\\- Digital Camera","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T10:00","end":"2026-11-04T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":80},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11.26686070589307},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summ