{"job":{"id":20298357,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"Replace Server PSU","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p>Tech will need to replace PSU.</p><p>Site Contact Ronnie Knight</p><p>Champion Support Emmanuel <span style=\"color: black;\"><del>************</del></span></p><p>                              Dan <del>**** * ************</del></p><p>Tech <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> contact Champion support prior to checking out. Contact information listed in confidential section</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li><li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work.&nbsp;&nbsp;We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client. (Messaging on Field Nation is not sufficient communication when canceling or notifying of delay)</li><li>Check In Steps (<u>please follow order</u>)</li><li>Check In via FN Portal</li><li>Check In with Netfor at&nbsp;&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li><li>Complete installation per SOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by&nbsp;Netfor.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who requested the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li><li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li></ol><ul><li><strong>NOTE:&nbsp;<u>*** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER ***</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li><li>Check out with Netfor at&nbsp;800-908-0226 opt. 1</li></ol><ul><li><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p><p>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Cat6 Cabling</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------</p><ul><li>Signed Work Order with Date and Times</li><li>Pictures of area before working</li><li>Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed</li><li>Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)</li></ul>","markdown":"**SOW**\n\nTech will need to replace PSU.\n\nSite Contact Ronnie Knight\n\nChampion Support Emmanuel \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n Dan \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTech **MUST** contact Champion support prior to checking out. Contact information listed in confidential section\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURE**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client. (Messaging on Field Nation is not sufficient communication when canceling or notifying of delay)\n3. Check In Steps (please follow order)\n4. Check In via FN Portal\n5. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n6. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who requested the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n7. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n\n- **NOTE: \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT ALL DELIVERABLES AND SIGN OFF SHEET SIGNED BY MANAGER \\*\\*\\***\n\n1. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n2. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt. 1\n\n- **REQUIREMENTS: WORK ORDER MUST BE FULLY COMPLETED WHILE ONSITE BY USING THE FN-MOBILE APP (SMARTPHONE).**\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 7 or higher)\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- 8' Ladder\n- Cat6 Cabling\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Signed Work Order with Date and Times\n- Pictures of area before working\n- Pictures of all equipment or cabling installed\n- Pictures of area once work is completed (showing area cleaned up)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-04T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":37.13979265589653},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":60,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (37.13979265589653mi reported + 10mi padding = 47.13979265589653mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1793716454341}
{"job":{"id":20298495,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"STARLINK DISH INSTALL - SATTELITE INSTALL EXPERIENCE  & LADDER REQUIRED","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(11, 118, 160);\">STARLINK Install - NEED TECH WITH EXPERIENCE INSTALLING DISHES / may require up to 20ft. Ladder, depending on roof height.</strong></p><p><strong>INSTRUCTIONS</strong>:</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(112, 48, 160);\"><u>PLEASE NOTE:</u> If a Site Survey was done at this location by you previously, you would have completed our Starlink Site Survey form. The installation MUST be performed as depicted in that document and any changes to this plan require approval from us BEFORE proceeding. Failure to notify us of changes may result in delayed or contested payment after marking the WO complete.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME </strong><strong> (no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>Check in with CommandLink Dispatch Team at 385-533-9167 to let them know you've arrived or if you're running late.</strong></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u><em><u>﻿</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK TO BE COMPLETED:</strong></p><p>Touch base with onsite contact and locate existing network closet. Take “before” pictures of the network closet/area</p><p><strong>BEFORE MOUNTING</strong>: Plug in the Starlink device to make sure it powers on, take a picture of the device showing the white light indicating it is on.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(192, 79, 21);\"><u>Review building to assess best location for Starlink dish to be mounted. Use the Starlink app to assist</u></strong></p><ul><li><em>Dish must have full 180-degree view of the sky</em></li><li><em>Dish must be mounted no further than 150 feet from the network equipment</em></li><li><em>Available electrical outlet must be present no less than 16 feet away from where dish mount enters network closet</em></li><li><em>If you cannot install because you need additional materials, proceed with a site survey and prepare a quote for the exact materials and labor cost to complete the job</em></li><li>Provide above-mentioned quote no later than 24 hours after departing the site</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 80);\"><u>Proceed with installation</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Unpack Starlink Kit and plug power supply into outlet to confirm working (LED lights come on) BEFORE attempting installation</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Check for obstruction using the SL App at the intended mounting spot and post picture to FN.</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Proceed with mounting hardware and dish via provided instructions or survey and develop own installation plan then seek sign off from CL Dispatch Team and an onsite representative before proceeding with equipment installation.</em></strong></li><li><strong>After the dish is installed, call your WO mgr for DISH ACTIVATION (required before SL dish will pass traffic). CommandLink Dispatch 385-533-9167 as a backup if WO mgr isn't available.</strong></li><li><strong>Test connectivity &amp; speed by connecting ethernet port laptop to the power supply then leave cable disconnected near network rack unless asked specifically otherwise to connect it to a piece of customer equip</strong></li><li><strong><em>Perform a speed test via your laptop to confirm connection speed</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Take pictures of comSpleted dish installation and network closet </em></strong></li></ul><p><em>&nbsp;</em><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>Cable Management &amp; Drip Loop Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>Please cable manage properly. Tack external cabling cleanly &amp; securely to siding and/or hidden. Inside wiring &amp; cable management should look professional as well.</li><li>If a building side-penetration is required then a proper Drip Loop is MANDATORY (please see attached photo)</li></ul><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Check Out with CommandLink CommandLink Dispatch Team at </strong><strong>385-533-9167</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\"> and review photos to get check-out code before leaving the site</strong></p>","markdown":"**STARLINK Install - NEED TECH WITH EXPERIENCE INSTALLING DISHES / may require up to 20ft. Ladder, depending on roof height.**\n\n**INSTRUCTIONS**:\n\n**PLEASE NOTE: If a Site Survey was done at this location by you previously, you would have completed our Starlink Site Survey form. The installation MUST be performed as depicted in that document and any changes to this plan require approval from us BEFORE proceeding. Failure to notify us of changes may result in delayed or contested payment after marking the WO complete.**\n\n**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME**  **(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**Check in with CommandLink Dispatch Team at 385-533-9167 to let them know you've arrived or if you're running late.**\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*﻿***\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK TO BE COMPLETED:**\n\nTouch base with onsite contact and locate existing network closet. Take “before” pictures of the network closet/area\n\n**BEFORE MOUNTING**: Plug in the Starlink device to make sure it powers on, take a picture of the device showing the white light indicating it is on.\n\n**Review building to assess best location for Starlink dish to be mounted. Use the Starlink app to assist**\n\n- *Dish must have full 180-degree view of the sky*\n- *Dish must be mounted no further than 150 feet from the network equipment*\n- *Available electrical outlet must be present no less than 16 feet away from where dish mount enters network closet*\n- *If you cannot install because you need additional materials, proceed with a site survey and prepare a quote for the exact materials and labor cost to complete the job*\n- Provide above-mentioned quote no later than 24 hours after departing the site\n\n**Proceed with installation**\n\n- ***Unpack Starlink Kit and plug power supply into outlet to confirm working (LED lights come on) BEFORE attempting installation***\n- ***Check for obstruction using the SL App at the intended mounting spot and post picture to FN.***\n- ***Proceed with mounting hardware and dish via provided instructions or survey and develop own installation plan then seek sign off from CL Dispatch Team and an onsite representative before proceeding with equipment installation.***\n- **After the dish is installed, call your WO mgr for DISH ACTIVATION (required before SL dish will pass traffic). CommandLink Dispatch 385-533-9167 as a backup if WO mgr isn't available.**\n- **Test connectivity &amp; speed by connecting ethernet port laptop to the power supply then leave cable disconnected near network rack unless asked specifically otherwise to connect it to a piece of customer equip**\n- ***Perform a speed test via your laptop to confirm connection speed***\n- ***Take pictures of comSpleted dish installation and network closet***\n\n **Cable Management &amp; Drip Loop Requirements**\n\n- Please cable manage properly. Tack external cabling cleanly &amp; securely to siding and/or hidden. Inside wiring &amp; cable management should look professional as well.\n- If a building side-penetration is required then a proper Drip Loop is MANDATORY (please see attached photo)\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Check Out with CommandLink CommandLink Dispatch Team at** **385-533-9167** **and review photos to get check-out code before leaving the site**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T09:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":8.165178356517835},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793717248609}
{"job":{"id":20298057,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DecisionPoint Technologies Inc","title":"Troubleshoot Main 1 PHU Offline – Recurring Connectivity Issue (Raleigh, NC)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Check-In Procedure:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you are unable to be onsite at the requested time, reach out to the work order manager.</li>\n<li>When onsite, check in/out with Work Order Manager <del>****** **************</del></li>\n<li>Tech must check out with the Carrols Helpdesk.&nbsp;888-767-4107 - Option #2. <strong><em><u>Get the name of the help desk person you spoke with.</u></em></strong></li>\n<li><strong><em><u>*** NOTE: *** Depending on helpdesk volume, you may experience extended wait times for a call back. Calls are returned in the order they are received.</u></em></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If you are not able to make the agreed upon start time, inform the work order manager by text.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If you are on site for more than two hours, please inform the work order manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Tech will provide the Carrols Case Nr when calling the helpdesk</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;Scope:</strong> Technician to visit onsite to troubleshoot Main 1 PHU, which has been offline since May. Previous troubleshooting included replacing the network cable, which did not resolve the issue. Inspect cabling, power, network connections, and equipment to identify the root cause of the recurring issue and restore Main 1 PHU to full functionality.</p>\n<p><strong>Carrols Incident Nr:</strong> 759293</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tech will troubleshoot equipment as directed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Bring tech tools - Any required Tools (outside of standard equipment): USB stick, keyboard, mouse, network testing tools, snips, Cat5 cables, screwdriver in case needed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong><em><u>Check out with the Carrols Helpdesk</u></em><u>888-767-4107 - Option #2.</u> <em><u>Get the name of the help desk person you spoke with.</u></em></strong></li>\n<li><strong><em><u>If unable to reach the help desk by phone, please request a return call: (include&nbsp;Carrols</u></em><u>Case Nr</u><em><u>). Please notate the time the helpdesk was called on the close out notes of the work order.</u></em></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Carrols Incident Nr:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Check-Out Procedure:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enter close out notes with the&nbsp;<strong><u>specific details of the job and any hold times with the helpdesk.</u></strong>&nbsp;Document Carrols suggestion if the problem was not resolved.&nbsp;Include the name of the Carrols Helpdesk representative that you worked with.&nbsp;<u>&nbsp;</u><strong><u>This is required for payment.</u></strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Check-In Procedure:**\n\n- If you are unable to be onsite at the requested time, reach out to the work order manager.\n- When onsite, check in/out with Work Order Manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Tech must check out with the Carrols Helpdesk. 888-767-4107 - Option #2. ***Get the name of the help desk person you spoke with.***\n- ***\\*\\*\\* NOTE: \\*\\*\\* Depending on helpdesk volume, you may experience extended wait times for a call back. Calls are returned in the order they are received.***\n- **Introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty.**\n- **If you are not able to make the agreed upon start time, inform the work order manager by text.**\n- **If you are on site for more than two hours, please inform the work order manager.**\n- **Tech will provide the Carrols Case Nr when calling the helpdesk**\n\n **Scope:** Technician to visit onsite to troubleshoot Main 1 PHU, which has been offline since May. Previous troubleshooting included replacing the network cable, which did not resolve the issue. Inspect cabling, power, network connections, and equipment to identify the root cause of the recurring issue and restore Main 1 PHU to full functionality.\n\n**Carrols Incident Nr:** 759293\n\n- **Tech will troubleshoot equipment as directed.**\n- **Bring tech tools - Any required Tools (outside of standard equipment): USB stick, keyboard, mouse, network testing tools, snips, Cat5 cables, screwdriver in case needed.**\n- ***Check out with the Carrols Helpdesk*888-767-4107 - Option #2. *Get the name of the help desk person you spoke with.***\n- ***If unable to reach the help desk by phone, please request a return call: (include Carrols*Case Nr*). Please notate the time the helpdesk was called on the close out notes of the work order.***\n- **Carrols Incident Nr:**\n\n**Check-Out Procedure:**\n\n- Enter close out notes with the **specific details of the job and any hold times with the helpdesk.** Document Carrols suggestion if the problem was not resolved. Include the name of the Carrols Helpdesk representative that you worked with.  **This is required for payment.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":210},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.454219091662901},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"s