{"job":{"id":20297844,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Inter Prompt Global - IPGlobal247","title":"Freelance Network Work in H&F STORE 344615 | Camp Lejeune, NC | USA","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Kindly read all the details mentioned below carefully and let us know if there is any concern before accepting the WO. Provider to download and read the Manual is a must.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<p>Joint Troubleshooting with ISP.</p>\n<p><strong>Equipment's Tech needs to carry :</strong> Tech needs to carry a Laptop with TeamViewer installed, LAN cable patch cord, Cabel roll (300 feet),&nbsp;&nbsp;cable tester, Crimping tool, console cables, CAT6 cable and also requires a good hotspot for fast internet connectivity<strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This is a military site, and Following documents required for military site access..</strong></p>\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Valid driver’s license</p>\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Car insurance Pic.</p>\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Social Security #</p>\n<p>you can provide last four digit if you can provide a picture.</p>\n<p>A real id, passport or an original birth certificate to get access to the base.</p>\n<p><strong>POC contact will be shared for site access arrangement.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required: (Must have all the tools in working condition)</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cisco console cable</li>\n<li><strong>USB to serial converter (DB-9 to USB)</strong></li>\n<li>Patch Cords (Cat 6e) Straight and Cross of 03 Meters.</li>\n<li><strong>Windows 8 or 10 laptop</strong> with charger, PuTTY, Microsoft Teams and TeamViewer installed</li>\n<li><strong>The provider must have a good internet connection and good laptop condition. Microsoft teams and team viewer must be installed on the laptop and the meeting to be joined through Microsoft Teams with the Remote Engineer team must be through the laptop.</strong></li>\n<li>Smartphone with&nbsp;<strong>Whatsapp Installed,</strong>&nbsp;data package and charger</li>\n<li>Screwdriver set</li>\n<li>Label Machine</li>\n<li>Cable Tester and Crimping tool</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>*Special Instructions: *</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Field engineer (FE) to provide pre-work photos of racks and the site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share a screenshot of the meeting.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to provide photos of devices (both new and old) with clearly visible serial numbers.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to send frequent updates every 30 minutes while on-site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share post-work photos upon completion of the task.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to provide a list of consumables used and their costs after completing the work.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>FE to share the site visit report signed by the Point of Contact (POC) before leaving&nbsp;the&nbsp;site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Once the activity is confirmed; kindly do not back out from the WO. Also, we cannot change the scheduled time and date after confirmation from the client.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿<u>If the work window is for 02 to 03 hours and the remote engineer team asks the provider to stay on-site. Kindly stay on site, as the provider will be paid by the additional hourly rate, in order to have a successful activity and a positive business relationship.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Material Costs must be shared with the invoice, It can be engineer's company letter head or from the vendor. Without the Material Invoice, such expenses will not be approved.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Materials to be as per actual Cat6e cable to charged at (50 Cents) per ft. and other materials cost as per actual amount attach screenshot for cost verification if purchased online.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the access is not arranged due to some reason, the Field Engineer is requested to be near the site within a 01-02 Miles radius, to have their access arranged and for activity completion. However, the waiting time will be compensated.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The engineer cannot leave the site unless the onsite POC allows him to leave after the successful completion of the activity.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>*****Engineer to report the work progress update (within every 30 minutes), to our IT Team through a WhatsApp group created by our team and to Remote Engineer (RE) team over teams is a must.******</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A Detailed task manual is attached for reference.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sharing sample picture of DB9 to USB console cable for Adtran router.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>***Incomplete work or the provider leaving the site without the Remote engineer's approval will result in escalation and payment will not be made.***</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Time spent on site will be compensated for additional hours by the engineer even after the activity is completed. So that the remote engineer can check and confirm the status of the work done.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Activity goes more than 8 hours, an additional 40 USD per hour will be paid.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The provider must never perform any work or services or business with the customer, while they are executing the task in the task execution time frame.</strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Kindly read all the details mentioned below carefully and let us know if there is any concern before accepting the WO. Provider to download and read the Manual is a must.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\nJoint Troubleshooting with ISP.\n\n**Equipment's Tech needs to carry :** Tech needs to carry a Laptop with TeamViewer installed, LAN cable patch cord, Cabel roll (300 feet), cable tester, Crimping tool, console cables, CAT6 cable and also requires a good hotspot for fast internet connectivity**.**\n\n**This is a military site, and Following documents required for military site access..**\n\n1\\. Valid driver’s license\n\n2\\. Car insurance Pic.\n\n3\\. Social Security #\n\nyou can provide last four digit if 