{"job":{"id":20299860,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Ticket #109414","description":{"html":"<p>Here is the complete updated SOW with the leasing office access instructions added directly to the Scope of Work, while keeping everything else the same.</p>GiGstreem – Scope of Work (SOW)<p><strong>Related Resident Ticket ID:</strong> 109414</p><p><strong>Resident Name:</strong> Jack Falcos-Vigne</p><p><strong>Resident Property:</strong> 1820 at Centennial</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Raleigh, NC</p><p>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</p>Work Order Location<p>Residential Property – 1820 at Centennial, Raleigh, NC.</p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p>Scope of Work (SOW): Troubleshoot Offline Closet Switch, Repair Ethernet Cabling, and Verify Access Point Connectivity<p><strong>Resident Unit Access:</strong> Upon arrival, the technician must first report to the leasing office. The leasing office will provide access to the resident's unit. Refer to confidential notes for the resident's unit number and contact information. Do not proceed to the resident's unit without coordinating access through the leasing office.</p><p>The technician will troubleshoot an offline network switch located inside the resident's closet. The primary objective is to identify and resolve the connectivity issue, inspect and repair Ethernet cabling as needed, and restore the switch to an online and operational status.</p><p><strong>Troubleshooting and Repair Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Inspect Closet Switch:</strong> Locate the offline network switch inside the closet. Verify power, Ethernet connections, link lights, and overall equipment condition.</li><li><strong>Troubleshoot Ethernet Cabling:</strong> Inspect the Ethernet cable connecting the switch to the network. Check for loose connections, damaged cabling, improper terminations, or other issues preventing connectivity.</li><li><strong>Repair and Re-Terminate Cabling:</strong> If necessary, repair or re-terminate the Ethernet cable at both ends using appropriate RJ45 connectors or termination hardware.</li><li><strong>Test Cable Run:</strong> Use an Ethernet cable tester to verify cable continuity, wire mapping, and proper termination. Continue troubleshooting and repairing the cabling until the cable passes testing and connectivity is restored.</li><li><strong>Restore Switch Connectivity:</strong> Reconnect the switch and verify link status. Coordinate with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team to confirm the switch is online and communicating properly.</li><li><strong>Check Access Point (AP):</strong> Verify that the resident's access point is powered on, connected, and functioning properly. If the AP is offline or not working, troubleshoot the Ethernet connection, PoE, and AP operation as needed.</li><li><strong>Verify Internet Service:</strong> Test Wi-Fi and hardwired connectivity where available to confirm that the resident's internet service has been restored.</li><li><strong>Completion Documentation:</strong> Provide photos of the switch, cabling, any repaired terminations, and final testing results. Confirm service restoration with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team before leaving the property.</li></ol><p><strong>Important:</strong> If the switch or AP remains offline after cabling repairs and troubleshooting, contact GiGstreem's Network Operations Team for additional assistance before leaving the site. Do not replace equipment without authorization.</p>Technician Expectations<ul><li><strong>Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong> to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li><li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident's unit is not permitted until this check-in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</li><li><strong>Represent the brand</strong> with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li><li><strong>Do not overshare</strong> internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.</li></ul><p><strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order, subject to applicable agreement terms.</p><p><strong>If equipment replacement is determined to be necessary during the visit, the technician must:</strong></p><ul><li>Take a clear photo of the equipment needing replacement.</li><li>Provide a separate photo clearly showing the <strong>equipment label with the MAC address and model/type</strong>.</li><li>Contact GiGstreem for approval before proceeding with replacement.</li></ul>Required Experience<p><em>Includes but is not limited to:</em></p><ul><li>Telecommunications/networking experience, including troubleshooting of routers and switches</li><li>Installation and troubleshooting of network switches, routers, and Cat6 jumper connections</li><li>Copper cabling experience, including Cat5e/Cat6 testing, troubleshooting, and RJ45 termination at both ends</li><li>Understanding of Ethernet link status, PoE, and network connectivity</li><li>Troubleshooting customer device connectivity (TVs, tablets, computers, etc.)</li><li>Familiarity with Ruckus Access Points, including resetting and wall-mount handling</li></ul>Required Equipment<p><em>Includes but is not limited to:</em></p><ul><li>Ethernet cable tester</li><li>RJ45 crimping and termination tools</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 RJ45 connectors</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables (jumpers)</li><li>Cable stripping and cutting tools</li><li>Wireless-enabled device such as a phone or tablet (for Wi-Fi testing)</li><li>Laptop (for diagnostics and troubleshooting)</li></ul>Coordination<ul><li>Work in collaboration with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team.</li><li>Refer to confidential notes for customer and NOC (Network Operations Center) contact information.</li><li>Confirm the switch and access point are online and operational before closing the work order.</li></ul>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders – GiGstreem Policy Reminder<p>At GiGstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support.</p><p>It is strictly against GiGstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</p><p><strong>Why This Matters:</strong></p><ul><li>Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li><li>They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li><li>Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li></ul><p><strong>Approved Resolution Methods:</strong></p><ul><li>Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li><li>Testing and repairing Ethernet cabling and terminations</li><li>Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li></ul><p>All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</p><ul><li>Add a clear job completion checklistClarify cable repair authorization limits</li></ul>","markdown":"Here is the complete updated SOW with the leasing office access instructions added directly to the Scope of Work, while keeping everything else the same.\n\nGiGstreem – Scope of Work (SOW)**Related Resident Ticket ID:** 109414\n\n**Resident Name:** Jack Falcos-Vigne\n\n**Resident Property:** 1820 at Centennial\n\n**Location:** Raleigh, NC\n\nGiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.\n\nWork Order LocationResidential Property – 1820 at Centennial, Raleigh, NC.\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\nScope of Work (SOW): Troubleshoot Offline Closet Switch, Repair Ethernet Cabling, and Verify Access Point Connectivity**Resident Unit Access:** Upon arrival, the technician must first report to the leasing office. The leasing office will provide access to the resident's unit. Refer to confidential notes for the resident's unit number and contact information. Do not proceed to the resident's unit without coordinating access through the leasing office.\n\nThe technician will troubleshoot an offline network switch located inside the resident's closet. The primary objective is to identify and resolve the connectivity issue, inspect and repair Ethernet cabling as needed, and restore the switch to an online and operational status.\n\n**Troubleshooting and Repair Tasks:**\n\n1. **Inspect Closet Switch:** Locate the offline network switch inside the closet. Verify power, Ethernet connections, link lights, and overall equipment condition.\n2. **Troubleshoot Ethernet Cabling:** Inspect the Ethernet cable connecting the switch to the network. Check for loose connections, damaged cabling, improper terminations, or other issues preventing connectivity.\n3. **Repair and Re-Terminate Cabling:** If necessary, repair or re-terminate the Ethernet cable at both ends using appropriate RJ45 connectors or termination hardware.\n4. **Test Cable Run:** Use an Ethernet cable tester to verify cable continuity, wire mapping, and proper termination. Continue troubleshooting and repairing the cabling until the cable passes testing and connectivity is restored.\n5. **Restore Switch Connectivity:** Reconnect the switch and verify link status. Coordinate with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team to confirm the switch is online and communicating properly.\n6. **Check Access Point (AP):** Verify that the resident's access point is powered on, connected, and functioning properly. If the AP is offline or not working, troubleshoot the Ethernet connection, PoE, and AP operation as needed.\n7. **Verify Internet Service:** Test Wi-Fi and hardwired connectivity where available to confirm that the resident's internet service has been restored.\n8. **Completion Documentation:** Provide photos of the switch, cabling, any repaired terminations, and final testing results. Confirm service restoration with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team before leaving the property.\n\n**Important:** If the switch or AP remains offline after cabling repairs and troubleshooting, contact GiGstreem's Network Operations Team for additional assistance before leaving the site. Do not replace equipment without authorization.\n\nTechnician Expectations- **Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident's unit is not permitted until this check-in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare** internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.\n\n**⚠️ Important:** If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order, subject to applicable agreement terms.\n\n**If equipment replacement is determined to be necessary during the visit, the technician must:**\n\n- Take a clear photo of the equipment needing replacement.\n- Provide a separate photo clearly showing the **equipment label with the MAC address and model/type**.\n- Contact GiGstreem for approval before proceeding with replacement.\n\nRequired Experience*Includes but is not limited to:*\n\n- Telecommunications/networking experience, including troubleshooting of routers and switches\n- Installation and troubleshooting of network switches, routers, and Cat6 jumper connections\n- Copper cabling experience, including Cat5e/Cat6 testing, troubleshooting, and RJ45 termination at both ends\n- Understanding of Ethernet link status, PoE, and network connectivity\n- Troubleshooting customer device connectivity (TVs, tablets, computers, etc.)\n- Familiarity with Ruckus Access Points, including resetting and wall-mount handling\n\nRequired Equipment*Includes but is not limited to:*\n\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- RJ45 crimping and termination tools\n- Cat5e/Cat6 RJ45 connectors\n- Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables (jumpers)\n- Cable stripping and cutting tools\n- Wireless-enabled device such as a phone or tablet (for Wi-Fi testing)\n- Laptop (for diagnostics and troubleshooting)\n\nCoordination- Work in collaboration with GiGstreem's Network Operations Team.\n- Refer to confidential notes for customer and NOC (Network Operations Center) contact information.\n- Confirm the switch and access point are online and operational before closing the work order.\n\nPolicy on Wi-Fi Extenders – GiGstreem Policy ReminderAt GiGstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support.\n\nIt is strictly against GiGstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.\n\n**Why This Matters:**\n\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n\n**Approved Resolution Methods:**\n\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Testing and repairing Ethernet cabling and terminations\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n\nAll technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.\n\n- Add a clear job completion checklistClarify cable repair authorization limits","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.21850323489127},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TVs\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793724335222}
{"job":{"id":"9460405946","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install PIAB &amp; High Gain Antenna (HARD START TIME)","description":"<p><strong>*Tech must work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number in the confidential field section*</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>METTEL TICKET #:&nbsp;</u></strong>12000517</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>o Locate the manager's office.</u></strong></p><p>Install the DataRemote device(PIAB) on the wall above the top shelf and below the ceiling grid</p><p>o It is important that you do not damage or dispose of the Dataremote packaging box. This box will need to be left on the top shelf to be used for return of the existing phone equipment during the second visit.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>2. Evaluate Cable Path</u></strong></p><p>o Check for existing wall passthroughs for the network and phone cable(rj-11) connections to use in the installation area(top shelf) and at the desk level near the switch. NOTE: With these being legacy sites. It is unlikely the passthroughs were ever installed.</p><p>o If there are passthroughs available for the network and phone cables, use those when possible for all cable routing.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>3. Route Cabling</u></strong></p><p>o If no passthrough is available, route the Ethernet and phone cables behind the shelving The network cable needs to be long enough to reach port 47 on the switch. The line1 and line2 phone cables need to be able to reach the desk phone. DO NOT plug any of these in on the switch or phone at this time.</p><p>o Ensure cables are secured, protected from damage, and routed neatly to maintain a professional appearance.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>4. Provide Power</u></strong></p><p>o Connect the PIAB box power cord to the nearest available power outlet.</p><p>o DO NOT utilize the Envysion Uninterrupted Power Supply and DO NOT plug into power outlets located above the drop ceiling.</p><p>o If unable to find an available power outlet please call Mettel.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>5. Fire Alarm Determination</u></strong></p><p>o Have tech survey for existing fire alarm services</p><p>o If a fire alarm is present, run new phone lines(rj-11) from the PIAB using line 3 and line 4 on PIAB device.</p><p>*pots lines were already disconnected - please connect FA lines during this dispatch</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>6. Antenna Determination</u></strong></p><p>o MetTel will ship both the paddle antenna and the standard MIMO antenna. The tech will complete our standard installation, and if the MIMO antenna is not needed, it can either be stored onsite or discarded.</p><p>o If High Gain External Antenna is needed determine mounting site for External High Gain Antenna</p><p>1. Look for potential roof penetrations to mount antenna externally</p><p>22. If we cannot install high gain external antenna on roof call Mettel for next steps.</p><p>3. Regardless of path, provide picture to Mettel team of antenna installation site</p><p>o If High Gain External Antenna is needed coordinate with Mettel to ship an Antenna to the Store</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>7. Verify Operation</u></strong></p><p>o Confirm the PIAB powers on successfully.</p><p>o Confirm with Mettel that device is online and functioning as expected at this stage.</p><p>o Ensure cables are dressed neatly a nd do not create a safety hazard.</p><p>8. Closeout Notes</p><p>o Ensure all required closeout notes and pictures are sent to Mettel team</p><p>o Checkout with Manager on duty</p><p>o Advise to not throw away Dataremote box</p><p><br></p><p>Tech Will Need: Fully Charged Laptop (Windows 7 or newer / MAC OS X) running the most current version and/or Mozilla Firefox or Chrome,</p><p>Cell phone,</p><p>Hotspot device,</p><p>Local admin rights on laptop,</p><p>Laptop must have the ability to connect to an Ethernet port,</p><p>TeamViewer or AnyDesk installed,</p><p>8-12ft’ ladder,</p><p>Phillips head screw drivers</p><p>Regular flat head screw drivers</p><p>cordless drill with various bits,</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to four hours onsite.&nbsp;Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00","end":"2026-11-17T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":20.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","e