{"job":{"id":20300259,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CrossCom","title":"3635 KL - Cabling/Jack Issue Data - PINPAD IS OFFLINE  HARD START 11/4/26 AT 9:00 AM ET","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Problem Description:</u></strong></p><p>3635 KL - Cabling/Jack Issue Data - PINPAD IS OFFLINE</p><p><br></p><p>HARD START 11/4/26 AT 9:00 AM ET</p><p><br></p><p>Tech visit requested by Instore Tech Support:</p><p><br></p><p>SCOPE OF WORK: Kindly dispatch a Cross com tech to check Ethernet cable, data-jacks for Pinpad Serial Numbers ( MAC: E805DCA3053F / SN: 810-642-029 ) needs to check and get back online. Tech needs to look and repair or run a new cable between Data jack and Switch end, need to replace if the data jack and cabling is not good,&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>So, the tech needs to bring spare data Jacks, 300 feet Ethernet cable, data-jacks. Tech need to have a 10 - 12 ft ladder, additional Ethernet patch cables, cables tester and other required tools.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>SUPPORT TEAM:Tech need to contact the kohl's team on 262-703-2324 (option no:1) once he reached on site. Kindly share the images to the following email address it-instoretechsupport@kohls.com.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>If tech unable to reach the Instore team the call be directed to voice mail box where tech need to mention the CCN work order, Store number and his Mobile number. So that the team can reach the tech back once they received voice message.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong>1. Laptop with working console cable (USB to RJ45 Console cable); Laptop should have necessary drivers installed to support COM Ports and the type of console cable</strong></p><p><strong>2. Laptop should have Webex/Zoom/Gmeet Meetings Application installed for screen-share sessions</strong></p><p><strong>3. Laptop should have Putty Installed</strong></p><p><strong>4. Thumb drive/USB drive</strong></p><p><strong>5. Ethernet Cable testers and LAN cable Testers</strong></p><p><strong>6. Spare Ethernet cable;</strong></p><p><strong>7. Techs Laptop should have Ethernet Port</strong></p><p><strong>8. Working Internet Dongle/Hotspot</strong></p><p><strong>9. USB to Console cable for CP to Firewall</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***ALL TRACKING FOR PARTS MUST BE CHECKED PRIOR TO ARRIVAL***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong>​</p><ol><li>Review Problem Description to make sure you have all the needed materials and tools and can meet the SLA.</li><li>Set your ETA in the Tasks section.</li></ol><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong>​</p><ol><li><strong><u>***NOTE - CALLING THE CROSSCOM IVR, WILL ALSO GET YOU TO TECHNICAL SUPPORT AND THE SERVICE TEAM THAT HANDLES THIS ACCOUNT.&nbsp;THEY CAN ANSWER ANY QUESTIONS YOU HAVE, LISTEN TO ALL PROMPTS***</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>***Provider- Please note upon arriving to site please call the 1800 number and log into the work order this is the time by which you will be paid – both log in and log out times will be recorded – logging in from the FN work order is not the time by which you will be paid***</u></strong></li><li>Call&nbsp;to check-in with the CrossCom IVR&nbsp;800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT #&nbsp;62097.</li><li>Check-in to work order on the FN platform</li><li>Introduce yourself to MOD and Provide Customer Order, if one was provided above</li><li>Take before pictures</li><li>Complete install/troubleshooting per Problem Description above and/or work with Level II support to confirm work.</li><li>Clean area fully, DO NOT LEAVE A MESS!&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Check-Out on work order</li><li>Call&nbsp;to check Out with CrossCom, call the IVR&nbsp;800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT #&nbsp;62097, it will transfer you to the Service Team that handles this customer.</li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong>​</p><ol><li>Upload photos of each item/cabling that was installed/troubleshot. If available; before and after pics.</li><li>Get Manager on Duty's Signature</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>All damaged items MUST be relayed to the CrossCom Level I Service Team and photos must be provided.&nbsp;</li><li>If clarification is needed on where to install, speak with the MOD and/or CrossCom Level I Service Team.</li><li>Visits are to be conducted during business hours with a start time of 8:00am</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to CrossCom Level I Service Team ASAP while onsite.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY</u></strong></p><ul><li>Buyer&nbsp;does not pay travel or parking expenses unless pre-approved and receipts submitted. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by messaging the Work Order Manager.&nbsp;If approved the Buyer will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li><li>Buyer&nbsp;does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling the Service Team via the CrossCom IVR. If approved the Service Team will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them/receipts and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.</li><li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the Level I Service Team. If approved, the Buyer&nbsp;will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Problem Description:**\n\n3635 KL - Cabling/Jack Issue Data - PINPAD IS OFFLINE\n\nHARD START 11/4/26 AT 9:00 AM ET\n\nTech visit requested by Instore Tech Support:\n\nSCOPE OF WORK: Kindly dispatch a Cross com tech to check Ethernet cable, data-jacks for Pinpad Serial Numbers ( MAC: E805DCA3053F / SN: 810-642-029 ) needs to check and get back online. Tech needs to look and repair or run a new cable between Data jack and Switch end, need to replace if the data jack and cabling is not good,\n\nSo, the tech needs to bring spare data Jacks, 300 feet Ethernet cable, data-jacks. Tech need to have a 10 - 12 ft ladder, additional Ethernet patch cables, cables tester and other required tools.\n\nSUPPORT TEAM:Tech need to contact the kohl's team on 262-703-2324 (option no:1) once he reached on site. Kindly share the images to the following email address it-instoretechsupport@kohls.com.\n\nIf tech unable to reach the Instore team the call be directed to voice mail box where tech need to mention the CCN work order, Store number and his Mobile number. So that the team can reach the tech back once they received voice message.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n**1. Laptop with working console cable (USB to RJ45 Console cable); Laptop should have necessary drivers installed to support COM Ports and the type of console cable**\n\n**2. Laptop should have Webex/Zoom/Gmeet Meetings Application installed for screen-share sessions**\n\n**3. Laptop should have Putty Installed**\n\n**4. Thumb drive/USB drive**\n\n**5. Ethernet Cable testers and LAN cable Testers**\n\n**6. Spare Ethernet cable;**\n\n**7. Techs Laptop should have Ethernet Port**\n\n**8. Working Internet Dongle/Hotspot**\n\n**9. USB to Console cable for CP to Firewall**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*ALL TRACKING FOR PARTS MUST BE CHECKED PRIOR TO ARRIVAL\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***​\n\n1. Review Problem Description to make sure you have all the needed materials and tools and can meet the SLA.\n2. Set your ETA in the Tasks section.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***​\n\n1. **\\*\\*\\*NOTE - CALLING THE CROSSCOM IVR, WILL ALSO GET YOU TO TECHNICAL SUPPORT AND THE SERVICE TEAM THAT HANDLES THIS ACCOUNT. THEY CAN ANSWER ANY QUESTIONS YOU HAVE, LISTEN TO ALL PROMPTS\\*\\*\\***\n2. **\\*\\*\\*Provider- Please note upon arriving to site please call the 1800 number and log into the work order this is the time by which you will be paid – both log in and log out times will be recorded – logging in from the FN work order is not the time by which you will be paid\\*\\*\\***\n3. Call to check-in with the CrossCom IVR 800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT # 62097.\n4. Check-in to work order on the FN platform\n5. Introduce yourself to MOD and Provide Customer Order, if one was provided above\n6. Take before pictures\n7. Complete install/troubleshooting per Problem Description above and/or work with Level II support to confirm work.\n8. Clean area fully, DO NOT LEAVE A MESS!\n9. Check-Out on work order\n10. Call to check Out with CrossCom, call the IVR 800-820-9229, enter the S work order # (Do Not Include the S) and then enter VFT # 62097, it will transfer you to the Service Team that handles this customer.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***​\n\n1. Upload photos of each item/cabling that was installed/troubleshot. If available; before and after pics.\n2. Get Manager on Duty's Signature\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- All damaged items MUST be relayed to the CrossCom Level I Service Team and photos must be provided.\n- If clarification is needed on where to install, speak with the MOD and/or CrossCom Level I Service Team.\n- Visits are to be conducted during business hours with a start time of 8:00am\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to CrossCom Level I Service Team ASAP while onsite.\n\n**ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY**\n\n- Buyer does not pay travel or parking expenses unless pre-approved and receipts submitted. Any approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation App as “Travel Expenses” and not additional hours. Travel expenses can be pre-approved by messaging the Work Order Manager. If approved the Buyer will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal.\n- Buyer does not pay parts and material expenses unless pre-approved. Any additional expenses associated with parts and materials must be pre-approved by calling the Service Team via the CrossCom IVR. If approved the Service Team will document the additional expenses in the messages of the Field Nation portal. Any material use, please take pictures of them/receipts and load them to the Field Nation portal for approval.\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved Max hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the Level I Service Team. If approved, the Buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":57.77219822061667},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":70,"baseAmount":210,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (57.77219822061667mi reported + 10mi padding = 67.77219822061667mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21: