{"job":{"id":"3618554650","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install PIAB &amp; High Gain Antenna (HARD START TIME)","description":"<p><strong>*Tech must work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number in the confidential field section*</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>METTEL TICKET #:&nbsp;</u></strong>11993851</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>o Locate the manager's office.</u></strong></p><p>Install the DataRemote device(PIAB) on the wall above the top shelf and below the ceiling grid</p><p>o It is important that you do not damage or dispose of the Dataremote packaging box. This box will need to be left on the top shelf to be used for return of the existing phone equipment during the second visit.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>2. Evaluate Cable Path</u></strong></p><p>o Check for existing wall passthroughs for the network and phone cable(rj-11) connections to use in the installation area(top shelf) and at the desk level near the switch. NOTE: With these being legacy sites. It is unlikely the passthroughs were ever installed.</p><p>o If there are passthroughs available for the network and phone cables, use those when possible for all cable routing.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>3. Route Cabling</u></strong></p><p>o If no passthrough is available, route the Ethernet and phone cables behind the shelving The network cable needs to be long enough to reach port 47 on the switch. The line1 and line2 phone cables need to be able to reach the desk phone. DO NOT plug any of these in on the switch or phone at this time.</p><p>o Ensure cables are secured, protected from damage, and routed neatly to maintain a professional appearance.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>4. Provide Power</u></strong></p><p>o Connect the PIAB box power cord to the nearest available power outlet.</p><p>o DO NOT utilize the Envysion Uninterrupted Power Supply and DO NOT plug into power outlets located above the drop ceiling.</p><p>o If unable to find an available power outlet please call Mettel.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>5. Fire Alarm Determination</u></strong></p><p>o Have tech survey for existing fire alarm services</p><p>o If a fire alarm is present, run new phone lines(rj-11) from the PIAB using line 3 and line 4 on PIAB device.</p><p>*pots lines were already disconnected - please connect FA lines during this dispatch</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>6. Antenna Determination</u></strong></p><p>o MetTel will ship both the paddle antenna and the standard MIMO antenna. The tech will complete our standard installation, and if the MIMO antenna is not needed, it can either be stored onsite or discarded.</p><p>o If High Gain External Antenna is needed determine mounting site for External High Gain Antenna</p><p>1. Look for potential roof penetrations to mount antenna externally</p><p>22. If we cannot install high gain external antenna on roof call Mettel for next steps.</p><p>3. Regardless of path, provide picture to Mettel team of antenna installation site</p><p>o If High Gain External Antenna is needed coordinate with Mettel to ship an Antenna to the Store</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>7. Verify Operation</u></strong></p><p>o Confirm the PIAB powers on successfully.</p><p>o Confirm with Mettel that device is online and functioning as expected at this stage.</p><p>o Ensure cables are dressed neatly a nd do not create a safety hazard.</p><p>8. Closeout Notes</p><p>o Ensure all required closeout notes and pictures are sent to Mettel team</p><p>o Checkout with Manager on duty</p><p>o Advise to not throw away Dataremote box</p><p><br></p><p>Tech Will Need: Fully Charged Laptop (Windows 7 or newer / MAC OS X) running the most current version and/or Mozilla Firefox or Chrome,</p><p>Cell phone,</p><p>Hotspot device,</p><p>Local admin rights on laptop,</p><p>Laptop must have the ability to connect to an Ethernet port,</p><p>TeamViewer or AnyDesk installed,</p><p>8-12ft’ ladder,</p><p>Phillips head screw drivers</p><p>Regular flat head screw drivers</p><p>cordless drill with various bits,</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to four hours onsite.&nbsp;Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00","end":"2026-11-17T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","en