{"job":{"id":20300475,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Reg 40 || Replacement cash drawer & CBL **Part Pick Up**","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong> The technician is required to address the issue with Register 40, where the cash drawer (CD) is not opening. The technician should inspect and replace the cash drawer if necessary, ensuring all cables are securely connected and functional. After replacement, the technician must test the cash drawer by performing a \"No Sale\" operation to confirm proper functionality.</p>\n<p>Technicians must schedule part pickup before going onsite.</p>\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<p>1. Call <del>************</del></p>\n<p>2. Schedule pickup at the FSL (Forward Stocking Location)</p>\n<p>3. Ensure pickup is scheduled at least 2 hours before the confirmed onsite ETA</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Clients present issue: Register 40 - CD not opening</p>\n<p>Estimated time: 2 hours</p>\n<p>Part pickup required: Part is being sent to the store</p>\n<p>Victoria’s Secret /limited Brands Helpdesk:<del>**************</del></p>\n<p><del>******** ******** * **********</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ****** *** ****** ***** ** *** **** *****</del></p>\n<p><del>***********************************************</del></p>\n<p>Other Instructions:</p>\n<p>If assistance is needed, please call: <del>************ ****** * *</del></p>\n<p><del>******** **** *****</del></p>\n<p><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p>2. <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n**Scope of work:** The technician is required to address the issue with Register 40, where the cash drawer (CD) is not opening. The technician should inspect and replace the cash drawer if necessary, ensuring all cables are securely connected and functional. After replacement, the technician must test the cash drawer by performing a \"No Sale\" operation to confirm proper functionality.\n\nTechnicians must schedule part pickup before going onsite.\n\nSteps:\n\n1\\. Call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\