{"job":{"id":20300810,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Titan Protection","title":"Altera Durham Summit - Replacing Router and Adjusting Cameras on Solar Powered Surveillance System","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting and resolving security camera connectivity issues.</li><li>Tech is required to diagnose and fix connectivity problems between security cameras and the monitoring system or network. This may include checking wiring, verifying network settings, and ensuring proper software configurations.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>12 ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Crimpers</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Volt Meter</li><li>Socket Set</li><li>Torx Screwdriver Set</li><li>Phillips Screwdriver Set</li><li>Allen Wrenches</li><li>Smartphone or Tablet with Camera</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)</li><li>Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.</li><li>Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.</li><li>If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).</li><li>Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).</li><li>Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.</li><li>Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.</li><li>Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.</li><li>Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.</li><li>Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.&nbsp;</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.</li><li>Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting and resolving security camera connectivity issues.\n- Tech is required to diagnose and fix connectivity problems between security cameras and the monitoring system or network. This may include checking wiring, verifying network settings, and ensuring proper software configurations.\n- Estimated duration will be 1-2 hours\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 12 ft A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Crimpers\n- Cable Tester\n- Volt Meter\n- Socket Set\n- Torx Screwdriver Set\n- Phillips Screwdriver Set\n- Allen Wrenches\n- Smartphone or Tablet with Camera\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.\n2. Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)\n3. Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.\n2. Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.\n3. Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.\n4. If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).\n5. Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).\n6. Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.\n7. Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.\n8. Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.\n2. Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.\n3. Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.\n- Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.\n- Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T13:30","end":"2026-11-04T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":350},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":100}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":14.558709674004236},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":125,"baseAmount":375,"estHours":1.5,"travelExpense":35,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":125}}},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (14.558709674004236mi reported + 10mi padding = 24.558709674004234mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000