{"job":{"id":"1787121435","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Dispatch Inside Wire Technician","description":"# SCOPE OF WORK<br><br>Dispatch an Inside Wire Technician to locate the fiber circuit in the network room/MPOE and complete TTU/testing and network readiness validation. To ensure the circuit does not get turned down in the future, we require the technician to insert a LOOPBACK PLUG.<br><br># REQUIRED MATERIALS<br><br>- Laptop<br>- Appropriate fiber testing equipment<br>- SC and LC LOOPBACK PLUG<br>- Media converter to connect a laptop to the fiber handoff and verify service, if required.<br>- WRX281 Optical Light Source for multimode and singlemode cable includes wavelengths of 850nm, 1300nm, 1310nm, and 1550nm<br>- WRX280 Optical Power Meter<br>- 10mW VFL with 1.25mm adapter<br>- SC/SC female adapter (2)<br>- LC/LC female adapter (2)<br>- SC/UPC-SC/UPC SM reference cord (1 meter)<br>- SC/UPC-LC/UPC SM reference cord (1 meter)<br>- SC/PC-SC/PC OM4 reference cord (1 meter)<br>- SC/PC-LC/PC OM4 reference cord (1 meter)<br>- SC/UPC Bare Fiber Optic Adapter (2)<br>- Fiber Optic Scribe Cleaver Tool<br>- 2.50mm cleaning pen<br>- 1.25mm cleaning pen<br>- Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port<br>- Multimeter wire tester<br>- Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches<br>- Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer)<br>- Biscuit jacks<br>- Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters<br>- 4-6 ft' ladder<br>- Butt Set<br>- RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors<br>- 100' extension cord<br>- Digital Camera<br>- 100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device<br>- Cell phone w/Hotspot device<br>- Punch down tool<br><br># ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS<br><br>- Verify circuit at the MPOE/demarc, using a converter if required.<br>- Validate demarc extension and cross-connects.<br>- Complete circuit testing and speed test.<br>- Verify power at the required equipment location.<br>- Locate the customer equipment and document the specific port where the circuit is to be handed off.<br>- Take clear photos of the demarc, extensions, cross-connects, test results, power, and customer handoff.<br>- If an extension is required: Perform a site survey documenting the proposed cable path, approximate distance, cable/handoff type, required materials, and customer equipment/port. Include supporting photos in the closeout notes.<br><br># BRIDGE INFO<br><br>URL: https://dispatch.bruin.com/<br><br>*Tech MUST work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number and Mettel ticket in the confidential field section*<br>___________________________________________________________________________________________________<br>Flat rate covers up to 2 hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.<br><br>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.<br><br>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered ?Cancelled?, not ?Aborted?.  <br><br>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-23T12:00","end":"2026-11-23T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":1.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"},{"sta