{"job":{"id":20235425,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | VCA | Credit Card Terminal Refresh","description":{"html":"<p>Insight has been engaged by VCA to perform like for like swaps on credit card terminals</p><p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING </u></strong></p><p><strong>SCOPE: </strong></p><p>☐ Install and connect new credit card payment terminals, replacing the hospital’s existing terminals on a like-for-like basis (including the required cabling).</p><p>☐ Verify each new terminal is recognized and functioning within the hospital’s payment system (WOOFware) and complete a test transaction with a staff member.</p><p>☐ Coordinate the cutover with hospital staff to minimize disruption, keeping at least one terminal available for payment processing wherever possible.</p><p>☐ Remove and Decommission old/retired terminals per the approved return process and review basic terminal functions and support resources with staff before departing.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tools needed:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Hard and soft copy of the work instructions document</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Phone 100% charged before arriving, with Phone Charger, Internet Access, Camera, MS Teams mobile App, &amp; Hands-Free Headset</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Snips (Scissors) to cut velcro and zip ties</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Box Cutters to open boxes</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 #2 Phillips Screw Driver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 #1 Phillips Screw Driver to remove base from legacy PC</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Flash Light to illuminate underneath workstations</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Materials</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Velcro Roll for cable management</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">1 Packing Tape to seal old equipment box</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Also the hospital will provide a tool that is required to remove equipment at some work stations</span></li></ul><p><strong>Dress code: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 49, 48);\">Business casual (polo and pants), closed shoes or boots. no jeans or sneakers and no safety gear is required.</span></p><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Travel: </u></p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><u style=\"color: black;\">Terms for Additional Time being Required: </u></p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li><li>IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</li><li>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</li></ul><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.</em></p>","markdown":"Insight has been engaged by VCA to perform like for like swaps on credit card terminals\n\n**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\n**SCOPE:**\n\n☐ Install and connect new credit card payment terminals, replacing the hospital’s existing terminals on a like-for-like basis (including the required cabling).\n\n☐ Verify each new terminal is recognized and functioning within the hospital’s payment system (WOOFware) and complete a test transaction with a staff member.\n\n☐ Coordinate the cutover with hospital staff to minimize disruption, keeping at least one terminal available for payment processing wherever possible.\n\n☐ Remove and Decommission old/retired terminals per the approved return process and review basic terminal functions and support resources with staff before departing.\n\n**Tools needed:**\n\n- 1 Hard and soft copy of the work instructions document\n- 1 Phone 100% charged before arriving, with Phone Charger, Internet Access, Camera, MS Teams mobile App, &amp; Hands-Free Headset\n- 1 Snips (Scissors) to cut velcro and zip ties\n- 1 Box Cutters to open boxes\n- 1 #2 Phillips Screw Driver\n- 1 #1 Phillips Screw Driver to remove base from legacy PC\n- 1 Flash Light to illuminate underneath workstations\n- Materials\n- 1 Velcro Roll for cable management\n- 1 Packing Tape to seal old equipment box\n- Also the hospital will provide a tool that is required to remove equipment at some work stations\n\n**Dress code:** Business casual (polo and pants), closed shoes or boots. no jeans or sneakers and no safety gear is required.\n\nTerms for Travel:\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate if provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\nTerms for Additional Time being Required:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n- IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n- Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation. You must put this job into work done status within 14 days of the service date. If not, you risk delay or completely forfeit all compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-20T09:45","end":"2026-11-20T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57.843409792621145},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00