{"job":{"id":20301527,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Connect New CKT to FortiGate firewall (possible DMARC extension survey)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME</u></em>&nbsp;(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>*** BRING A CISCO ROLLOVER CONSOLE CABLE + LAPTOP ***</strong></p><p><strong>﻿IF THIS IS A FRONTIER OR KINETIC (WINDSTREAM) BROADBAND CIRCUIT, CHECK TO SEE IF THERE ARE TWO HANDOFF DEVICES (ONT/MODEM + A ROUTER TYPICALLY).&nbsp;IF THERE ARE, DOUBLE CHECK WITH YOUR IT CONTACT FIRST THEN PROCEED TO REMOVE THE ROUTER FROM THE MIX AND CONNECT DIRECTLY TO THE DEVICE IN FRONT OF IT</strong></p><p><strong><u>Connect New Internet CKT to Customer's FortiGate firewall.</u></strong></p><p>Bandwidth|Link 300M Broadband (AT&amp;T)</p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Circuit ID</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Site ID: 2317576_1 | uBAN: 347245154</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Carrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Make: Nokia</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Model: BGW320-505</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">MAC Address: A408537069F1</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">DeMarc Location</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Hand Off Type</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Copper/Electrical/RJ45</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Network Information </strong><strong style=\"color: white;\">Public</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">IP Address Range: 108.252.100.33 - 108.252.100.37 </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Subnet Mask:  255.255.255.248 </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Default Gateway: 108.252.100.38 </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Router Address: 108.252.100.38</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">DNS Servers:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Primary - 68.94.156.1</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">Secondary - 68.94.157.1</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Work to be Performed:</strong></p><ul><li>⁠Locate new circuit using <strong>MAC Address</strong> or <strong>CKT ID</strong> + <strong>DMARC info</strong> in this WO</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\">⁠</span><u style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\">Test new circuit on your laptop FIRST</u><span style=\"color: rgb(189, 203, 76);\"> (verify you can surf out and run some speed tests) before reaching out to AC IT (end user) and receiving instructions from them on cross-connecting to their firewall.&nbsp;Reach out to CommandLink Dispatch (WO Manager) after testing w/ laptop before proceeding.</span></li><li>Coordinate directly with customer IT to complete connection and circuit testing</li><li>⁠Connect newly installed CommandLink internet service to the customer’s FortiGate firewall</li></ul><p><strong>Conditional Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">If cabling or extension work is required, the technician will:</strong></p><ul><li>Stop installation work</li><li>Switch scope to a site survey</li><li>Provide a quote for additional work before proceeding</li></ul><p><strong>Tasks to be completed for work order to be paid:</strong></p><p><strong>You have a hard start at 11 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the location, ETC please do.</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li><li>Upon arrival, check in with your WO Manager first (if they do not answer then call the check-in check-out number to speak with someone else on the team)</li><li>Locate, photograph, and test new circuit</li><li>Test circuit first with a laptop; will need to assign static IPs.&nbsp;Test for connectivity then run a couple speed tests, make sure you get at least 80% of the circuit speeds both Upload and Download.</li><li>If the circuit is working then contact us back and we will let AC IT team know we are ready to move forward w/ their LAN cutover. <u> If it is not working then we (CommandLink Dispatch) will work with you to resolve the issue, </u><strong><u>please do not reach out to end user (ACI) if the CKT is not testing cleanly on your laptop</u>.</strong></li><li>Verify cabling and assess whether a new run is needed or if we can repurpose an existing between our newly installed CKT and customer's network rack.</li><li>If a new run is required, stop and perform survey first, then contact CommandLink with quote before moving forward.</li></ol><p>___________________________________________</p><p>Primary End User IT Contact:&nbsp;Mikia (919-695-0377)</p><p>Secondary:&nbsp;ACIIT NOC #984 710-9863</p><p>___________________________________________</p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.</strong></p><p><strong>3.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"***PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME* (no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\* BRING A CISCO ROLLOVER CONSOLE CABLE + LAPTOP \\*\\*\\***\n\n**﻿IF THIS IS A FRONTIER OR KINETIC (WINDSTREAM) BROADBAND CIRCUIT, CHECK TO SEE IF THERE ARE TWO HANDOFF DEVICES (ONT/MODEM + A ROUTER TYPICALLY). IF THERE ARE, DOUBLE CHECK WITH YOUR IT CONTACT FIRST THEN PROCEED TO REMOVE THE ROUTER FROM THE MIX AND CONNECT DIRECTLY TO THE DEVICE IN FRONT OF IT**\n\n**Connect New Internet CKT to Customer's FortiGate firewall.**\n\nBandwidth|Link 300M Broadband (AT&amp;T)\n\n**Circuit ID**\n\n**Site ID: 2317576\\_1 | uBAN: 347245154**\n\n**Carrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address**\n\n**Make: Nokia**\n\n**Model: BGW320-505**\n\n**MAC Address: A408537069F1**\n\n**DeMarc Location**\n\n**Hand Off Type**\n\n**Copper/Electrical/RJ45**\n\n**Network Information** **Public**\n\n**IP Address Range: 108.252.100.33 - 108.252.100.37**\n\n**Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248**\n\n**Default Gateway: 108.252.100.38**\n\n**Router Address: 108.252.100.38**\n\n**DNS Servers:**\n\n**Primary - 68.94.156.1**\n\n**Secondary - 68.94.157.1**\n\n**Work to be Performed:**\n\n- ⁠Locate new circuit using **MAC Address** or **CKT ID** + **DMARC info** in this WO\n- ⁠Test new circuit on your laptop FIRST (verify you can surf out and run some speed tests) before reaching out to AC IT (end user) and receiving instructions from them on cross-connecting to their firewall. Reach out to CommandLink Dispatch (WO Manager) after testing w/ laptop before proceeding.\n- Coordinate directly with customer IT to complete connection and circuit testing\n- ⁠Connect newly installed CommandLink internet service to the customer’s FortiGate firewall\n\n**Conditional Work:**\n\n**If cabling or extension work is required, the technician will:**\n\n- Stop installation work\n- Switch scope to a site survey\n- Provide a quote for additional work before proceeding\n\n**Tasks to be completed for work order to be paid:**\n\n**You have a hard start at 11 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the location, ETC please do.**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n2. Upon arrival, check in with your WO Manager first (if they do not answer then call the check-in check-out number to speak with someone else on the team)\n3. Locate, photograph, and test new circuit\n4. Test circuit first with a laptop; will need to assign static IPs. Test for connectivity then run a couple speed tests, make sure you get at least 80% of the circuit speeds both Upload and Download.\n5. If the circuit is working then contact us back and we will let AC IT team know we are ready to move forward w/ their LAN cutover.  If it is not working then we (CommandLink Dispatch) will work with you to resolve the issue, **please do not reach out to end user (ACI) if the CKT is not testing cleanly on your laptop.**\n6. Verify cabling and assess whether a new run is needed or if we can repurpose an existing between our newly installed CKT and customer's network rack.\n7. If a new run is required, stop and perform survey first, then contact CommandLink with quote before moving forward.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nPrimary End User IT Contact: Mikia (919-695-0377)\n\nSecondary: ACIIT NOC #984 710-9863\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n**1. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.**\n\n**2. If parts are shipped tech must verify parts are on site prior to arrival.**\n\n**3. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.**\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:00","end":"2026-11-06T12:39"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":6