{"job":{"id":20301695,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wireless Essentials","title":"SOW Install Replacement AP's & Reroute Drops To Relocate Ladder Needed. SEE Service Description for SOW details / Equipment & Material Requirements.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>UPON ASSIGNMENT - REVIEW</strong> Service Description in detail. Contact work order manager with any questions.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>***NO EXCEPTIONS*** </strong>YOUR TICKET WILL BE <strong>MOVED TO INCOMPLETE</strong> IF Attached WE SOW Sign Off form is missing ARRIVAL Times IN &amp; OUT / DATE / POC signature !!!</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SOW: </strong>&nbsp;<strong>Install Replacement AP's &amp; Reroute Drops To Relocate Ladder Needed</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>FROM SUPPORT: </strong>The site needs to have their access points updated and moved. I've attached a marked floor plan to this ticket. The new access points are already on-site. During installation the technician will need to send me the serial numbers of the new and old equipment. The ceiling height ranges from 8-10 feet, and the distance between new AP location and the old locations is less than fifty feet. They are connected via ethernet</p><p>floor plan attached for reference</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL and ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Call work order manager at <del>************</del> to check in and review SOW.</li><li>Technician is representing <del>******** **********</del> is expected to present and conduct themselves in a professional business manner.</li><li>MUST bring Laptop into facility upon arrival in the event it may be needed for troubleshooting or configuration with onsite network devices.</li><li>At any point technician is unable to reach onsite POC or offsite support. IMMEDIATELY phone work order manager.</li><li>While onsite, DO NOT DISCUSS COSTS with onsite contacts. Technician should instruct them to contact their corporate IT Support department.</li><li>IMMEDIATELY report any escalated issue to work order manager and or provide status update.</li><li>Base on scope of work and notes from Support follow instructions provided to resolve and/or complete the SOW as outlined.</li><li>Enter close out notes and upload required photos contact work order manager to review and be released from site.</li><li>SEE below for PHOTO &amp; DEPARTURE instructions.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PHOTO REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><ol><li>If applicable, images technician MUST provide BEFORE &amp; AFTER photos of work being performed.</li><li><strong>REVIEW PHOTOS, </strong>before uploading to work order.</li><li>Close up and distance photo images. <strong>BLURRY or POORLY LIT </strong>images will be <strong>REJECTED</strong>, and may require a revisit.</li><li>Any cable management MUST be documented. Images should include BEFORE &amp; AFTER, and should be similar for comparison.</li><li>Labeling must include in focus view of label imprint.</li><li>Based on SOW details, technician should take snapshot of manufacturer information label for any equipment / devices being installed / replaced or repaired. Capture - MFG - Make - Model - Serial #, MAC address, etc.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Return any network equipment back to its original location after work is completed.</li><li>Remove any debris / dust that was created by technician while performing service work. Leaving the immediate and surrounding work area neat and clean.</li><li>Call work order manager <del>*************</del> to review / report the work order and obtain CHECK OUT code to authorize departure from site.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED Equipment &amp; Materials Listed Below</u></strong></p><p>*Lap Top Computer with Windows 10 OS with WiFi, Hot Spot and Screen Share Capability &amp; power supply</p><p>*Fully Charged Hot Spot Device, *Console Cable, *Butt Set, *6' Ladder</p><p>*Cable Tester \\ Toner Wand, *Line Voltage Meter, *Spool / Reel Cat 5e / 6 Cabling</p><p>*RJ 45 Hardware&nbsp;, *Crimp Tool, *Mobile / Cellular Phone - Camera Capability &amp; power supply</p><p>*P-touch or similar Label Device, *Extra roll of label tape, *Basic IT Tool Set</p><p>*Basic Telecom Tool Set</p>","markdown":"**UPON ASSIGNMENT - REVIEW** Service Description in detail. Contact work order manager with any questions.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*NO EXCEPTIONS\\*\\*\\*** YOUR TICKET WILL BE **MOVED TO INCOMPLETE** IF Attached WE SOW Sign Off form is missing ARRIVAL Times IN &amp; OUT / DATE / POC signature !!!\n\n**SOW:**  **Install Replacement AP's &amp; Reroute Drops To Relocate Ladder Needed**\n\n**FROM SUPPORT:** The site needs to have their access points updated and moved. I've attached a marked floor plan to this ticket. The new access points are already on-site. During installation the technician will need to send me the serial numbers of the new and old equipment. The ceiling height ranges from 8-10 feet, and the distance between new AP location and the old locations is less than fifty feet. They are connected via ethernet\n\nfloor plan attached for reference\n\n**ARRIVAL and ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS:**\n\n1. Call work order manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check in and review SOW.\n2. Technician is representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* is expected to present and conduct themselves in a professional business manner.\n3. MUST bring Laptop into facility upon arrival in the event it may be needed for troubleshooting or configuration with onsite network devices.\n4. At any point technician is unable to reach onsite POC or offsite support. IMMEDIATELY phone work order manager.\n5. While onsite, DO NOT DISCUSS COSTS with onsite contacts. Technician should instruct them to contact their corporate IT Support department.\n6. IMMEDIATELY report any escalated issue to work order manager and or provide status update.\n7. Base on scope of work and notes from Support follow instructions provided to resolve and/or complete the SOW as outlined.\n8. Enter close out notes and upload required photos contact work order manager to review and be released from site.\n9. SEE below for PHOTO &amp; DEPARTURE instructions.\n\n**PHOTO REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. If applicable, images technician MUST provide BEFORE &amp; AFTER photos of work being performed.\n2. **REVIEW PHOTOS,** before uploading to work order.\n3. Close up and distance photo images. **BLURRY or POORLY LIT** images will be **REJECTED**, and may require a revisit.\n4. Any cable management MUST be documented. Images should include BEFORE &amp; AFTER, and should be similar for comparison.\n5. Labeling must include in focus view of label imprint.\n6. Based on SOW details, technician should take snapshot of manufacturer information label for any equipment / devices being installed / replaced or repaired. Capture - MFG - Make - Model - Serial #, MAC address, etc.\n\n**DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. Return any network equipment back to its original location after work is completed.\n2. Remove any debris / dust that was created by technician while performing service work. Leaving the immediate and surrounding work area neat and clean.\n3. Call work order manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to review / report the work order and obtain CHECK OUT code to authorize departure from site.\n\n**REQUIRED Equipment &amp; Materials Listed Below**\n\n\\*Lap Top Computer with Windows 10 OS with WiFi, Hot Spot and Screen Share Capability &amp; power supply\n\n\\*Fully Charged Hot Spot Device, \\*Console Cable, \\*Butt Set, \\*6' Ladder\n\n\\*Cable Tester \\\\ Toner Wand, \\*Line Voltage Meter, \\*Spool / Reel Cat 5e / 6 Cabling\n\n\\*RJ 45 Hardware , \\*Crimp Tool, \\*Mobile / Cellular Phone - Camera Capability &amp; power supply\n\n\\*P-touch or similar Label Device, \\*Extra roll of label tape, \\*Basic IT Tool Set\n\n\\*Basic Telecom Tool Set","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{