{"job":{"id":"4806023017","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Port &amp; Go Live (HARD START TIME)","description":"<p><strong>*Tech must work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number in the confidential field section*</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>METTEL TICKET #:&nbsp;</u></strong>11993851</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>1. Check in with Manager</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>o Check in with Manager on Duty, perform wellness check</p><p>o Locate the manager's office.</p><p>o If Antenna is required it should be located in store in a Mettel box.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Configure the PIAB Ethernet WAN interface</p><p><br></p><p>3. Remove the existing connection from Port 47 on the network switch that is currently connected to the Trendnet PoE injector used by the existing phone setup.</p><p><br></p><p>4. Connect the previously installed Ethernet cable from the PIAB device to Port 47 on the switch.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Confirm the PIAB unit is up and operating via the Ethernet WAN.</p><p><br></p><p>6. Remove the existing connections from line1 and line2 on the existing desk phone.</p><p><br></p><p>7. Connect the phone lines that were previously installed from the PIAB device during the first visit to the corresponding line1 and line2 ports on the existing office phone.</p><p><br></p><p>8. If new fire alarm lines were installed during the first visit, connect the fire lines to the appropriate port on the fire alarm panel.</p><p><br></p><p>9. If an antenna is required install and secure the antenna according to site requirements. Verify all connections are secure and confirm the PIAB device, phone, and fire panel connections are functioning properly.</p><p><br></p><p>10. Final Validations</p><p>Complete required validations below</p><p>o Validate with MetTel the device is online</p><p>o Validate with MetTel that outbound calling is working</p><p>o Validate with MetTel that inbound calling is working</p><p>o Validate with MetTel that caller ID and E911 are configured correctly</p><p>o Validate SIP RCF for outbound calls</p><p>o Validate hunt group is working</p><p>o Clean all trash and debris and dispose of in trash dumpster</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>11. Remove old Phone Equipment</p><p>o The final step is to remove the existing phone system devices and cabling.</p><p>o Trendnet PoE injector, Grandstream ATA and the old cabling and phone lines</p><p>o The Dataremote packaging box should have been left behind by the tech who did the first visit. Instructions for the first visit indicate that it should left behind on the top shelf above the desk.This box should be used to return the old phone equipment.</p><p>o After removing the old phone equipment package the Grandstream and Trendnet devices in the Dataremote box and leave with the manager along with explanation of how to retrieve shipping return label. The return shipping label will be found in their store email.</p><p><br></p><p>12. Final Check out</p><p>o Ensure all required closeout notes and pictures are sent to the Mettel team</p><p>o Checkout with Manager on duty</p><p>o Explain need to return old phone equipment and remind that label is in their email from Lightstream.</p><p><br></p><p>Tech Will Need: Fully Charged Laptop (Windows 7 or newer / MAC OS X) running the most current version and/or Mozilla Firefox or Chrome,</p><p>Cell phone,</p><p>Hotspot device,</p><p>Local admin rights on laptop,</p><p>Laptop must have the ability to connect to an Ethernet port,</p><p>TeamViewer or AnyDesk installed,</p><p>8-12ft’ ladder,</p><p>Phillips head screw drivers</p><p>Regular flat head screw drivers</p><p>cordless drill with various bits,</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to four hours onsite.&nbsp;Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered “Cancelled”, not “Aborted”.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-08T09:00","end":"2026-12-08T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-09T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 *