tances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-10T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":170},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":52.51376524566153},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793735907589}
{"job":{"id":20302370,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2749218","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>TV : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Dishwasher : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Computer : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- TV : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Dishwasher : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Computer : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-03T07:00","end":"2026-11-03T09:00","latestStart":"2026-11-03T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":23.011216873318197},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-03T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"Happy Birthday"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Kinettix Inc, Direct Onboarding - Vinson Services LLC -"},{"start":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Election Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793735919388}
{"job":{"id":20284824,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Scarsdale Security Systems Inc","title":"Scarsdale Ticket #849436 - Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation.  Troubleshoot/repair as necessary.  See notes for details.","description":{"html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation. Troubleshoot/repair as necessary. See notes for details.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving&nbsp;(FN App Signature is acceptable)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>**IMPORTANT** In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.</strong></li>\n<li>IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.</li>\n<li>TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL *PROVIDER* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. *OR* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION &amp; TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT.&nbsp;<strong>CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 **) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER -</strong>368966232</li>\n<li>**WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. **CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!</li>\n<li>FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.</li>\n<li>**BEFORE LEAVING SITE*** Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members</li>\n<li>***IMPORTANT** If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.</li>\n<li>CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements 1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent 2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed 3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving.</li>\n<li>9/23/26 - ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) reported RF Low Battery - , then on 10/30 reported MISSING @ 6:06 AM and was Bypassd same night. Users tripping zn 503 motion at Disarm 10/31 &amp; 11/1) 8/30/26 - ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal) reported RF Low Battery -, then on 10/22 reported MISSING @ 4:24 AM, Bypassed same night.</li>\n<li>RF BATTERY REPLACEMENT -- a) Verify transmitter serial number to ensure it is correct detector/transmitter, b) Replace CR123A, press transmitter reset button. c) Ensure transmitter housing is properly closed/seated and test operation. d) Ensure detector resumes normal operation and that Restore signals are received at central station. (Must perform Sensor Reset) ** *DMP wireless systems REQUIRE Sensor Reset at keypad before restore signal is sent. Extreme cases may also require J16 panel reset. ** * Ademco/Honeywell system may require reset to restore wireless (CODE + OFF two times in a row at keypad) ** * INOVONICS - Requires receiver reset - Press/Release RESET button on Inovonics receiver, replace cover. **--Call Scarsdale 914-722-2933 to verify signals and for programming assistance &amp; support --**</li>\n<li>Replace CR123A batteries at: * ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) * ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"- **Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation. Troubleshoot/repair as necessary. See notes for details.**\n\n**CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements**\n\n**1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent**\n\n**2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed**\n\n**3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving (FN App Signature is acceptable)**\n\n- **\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION**\n- **﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.**\n- IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.\n- TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL \\*PROVIDER\\* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. \\*OR\\* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION &amp; TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT. **CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 \\*\\*) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER -**368966232\n- \\*\\*WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. \\*\\*CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!\n- FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.\n- \\*\\*BEFORE LEAVING SITE\\*\\*\\* Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members\n- \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.\n- CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements 1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent 2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed 3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving.\n- 9/23/26 - ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) reported RF Low Battery - , then on 10/30 reported MISSING @ 6:06 AM and was Bypassd same night. Users tripping zn 503 motion at Disarm 10/31 &amp; 11/1) 8/30/26 - ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal) reported RF Low Battery -, then on 10/22 reported MISSING @ 4:24 AM, Bypassed same night.\n- RF BATTERY REPLACEMENT -- a) Verify transmitter serial number to ensure it is correct detector/transmitter, b) Replace CR123A, press transmitter reset button. c) Ensure transmitter housing is properly closed/seated and test operation. d) Ensure detector resumes normal operation and that Restore signals are received at central station. (Must perform Sensor Reset) \\*\\* \\*DMP wireless systems REQUIRE Sensor Reset at keypad before restore signal is sent. Extreme cases may also require J16 panel reset. \\*\\* \\* Ademco/Honeywell system may require reset to restore wireless (CODE + OFF two times in a row at keypad) \\*\\* \\* INOVONICS - Requires receiver reset - Press/Release RESET button on Inovonics receiver, replace cover. \\*\\*--Call Scarsdale 914-722-2933 to verify signals and for programming assistance &amp; support --\\*\\*\n- Replace CR123A batteries at: \\* ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) \\* ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":85},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.459188081253307},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $85 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-1