{"job":{"id":20302488,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tie National, LLC","title":"Onsite PC, Network Connectivity & Display Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p>Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159900.</p><p><br></p><p>If you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.</p><p><br></p><p>Description of work requested:</p><p>Onsite technician required&nbsp;a computer experiencing network connectivity issues. The PC is unable to obtain an IP address, and testing with a replacement network adapter did not resolve the issue.</p><p>Scope of Work:</p><ul><li>Inspect and verify Ethernet cabling and network connections.</li><li>Perform cable management and check for loose or faulty connections.</li><li>Troubleshoot Windows network settings and TCP/IP configuration.</li><li>Verify DHCP/IP address assignment and network adapter functionality.</li><li>Investigate the “No DP Signal” error and monitor standby issue.</li><li>Confirm the computer successfully connects to the network and the display is functioning properly.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Survey findings, before and after pictures and the SIGNED service order MUST be uploaded to the portal or emailed to helpdesk@tienational.com PRIOR to leaving site. otherwise your PAYMENT WILL BE WITHHELD until ALL deliverables are received.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please email your invoices to accounting@tienational.com to ensure you are paid in a timely manner.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>You will not be paid until our accounting department receives your invoice and helpdesk@tienational.com has received ALL of the deliverables.</p>","markdown":"Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159900.\n\nIf you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.\n\nDescription of work requested:\n\nOnsite technician required a computer experiencing network connectivity issues. The PC is unable to obtain an IP address, and testing with a replacement network adapter did not resolve the issue.\n\nScope of Work:\n\n- Inspect and verify Ethernet cabling and network connections.\n- Perform cable management and check for loose or faulty connections.\n- Troubleshoot Windows network settings and TCP/IP configuration.\n- Verify DHCP/IP address assignment and network adapter functionality.\n- Investigate the “No DP Signal” error and monitor standby issue.\n- Confirm the computer successfully connects to the network and the display is functioning properly.\n\nTie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit.\n\nSurvey findings, before and after pictures and the SIGNED service order MUST be uploaded to the portal or emailed to helpdesk@tienational.com PRIOR to leaving site. otherwise your PAYMENT WILL BE WITHHELD until ALL deliverables are received.\n\nPlease email your invoices to accounting@tienational.com to ensure you are paid in a timely manner.\n\nYou will not be paid until our accounting department receives your invoice and helpdesk@tienational.com has received ALL of the deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T10:30","end":"2026-11-04T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3.6615021114750856},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Kinettix Inc, Direct Onboarding - Vinson Services LLC -"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793736471126}
{"job":{"id":20302536,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vivo-Technologies","title":"[Kelly Partners] - Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p>Work Order Description – AV Site Survey</p><p><br></p><p>Location: <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">100 Cascade Pointe Lane suite 102, Cary, NC 27513, USA</span></p><p><br></p><p>Overview</p><p>The AV technician will perform a comprehensive onsite audiovisual site survey of 1 standard room to gather all required information for system design, installation planning, and project scoping. The focus of this survey is complete photos, accurate measurements, and network information.</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work</p><p>The technician will:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Conduct a Comprehensive Walkthrough</p><p>* Survey the assigned room and document site conditions, infrastructure, and equipment status.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Collect Detailed Measurements</p><p>* Room dimensions (length, width, height)</p><p>* Display/TV sizes and mounting locations</p><p>* Ceiling height and structural considerations</p><p>* Furniture and table dimensions</p><p>* Distances relevant to camera, microphone, and display positioning</p><p><br></p><p>3. Document Proposed Equipment &amp; Infrastructure Locations</p><p>Identify and record potential mounting or installation points for:</p><p>* Displays</p><p>* Cameras</p><p>* Microphones / ceiling arrays</p><p>* Speakers</p><p>* Equipment racks/cabinets</p><p>* Control panels</p><p>* Cable pathways and conduit routes</p><p>* Data drops and network jacks (label numbers, location, and condition)</p><p><br></p><p>4. Assess Site Conditions Affecting Installation</p><p>Note any conditions that may impact scope, labor, or safety, including:</p><p>* Concrete, brick, glass, or other specialty wall types</p><p>* Limited/no cable pathways or conduit restrictions</p><p>* Ceiling access issues (hard-lid, high ceilings, obstructions)</p><p>* Existing AV, IT, or electrical infrastructure</p><p>* Any visible damage in the room such as water leakage, ceiling stains, wall cracks, floor damage, or anything that could compromise installed equipment</p><p>* HVAC, lighting, or architectural obstructions</p><p><br></p><p>5. Verify Infrastructure &amp; Utilities</p><p>* Confirm availability and condition of power at all proposed equipment locations</p><p>* Identify and test network ports (if possible); record distances to switch locations</p><p>* Record network information for the room, including port and patch panel labels, switch location, switch make and model if visible, and available ports</p><p>* Note any missing, damaged, or insufficient connections</p><p><br></p><p>6. Capture Comprehensive Photos (Required in Landscape Orientation Only)</p><p>All photos must be taken in landscape mode to ensure consistency.</p><p>Include clear images of:</p><p>* The front, rear, and sides of the room</p><p>* Ceiling and above-ceiling areas (if accessible)</p><p>* Existing equipment (front, back, and connections)</p><p>* Rack spaces and cable management areas</p><p>* Data drops and wall plates</p><p>* Any structural or environmental damage</p><p>* Any condition that may impact installation</p><p><br></p><p>7. Document Existing Equipment Details</p><p>For all AV, IT, or peripheral equipment present in the room, the technician must collect and record:</p><p>* Serial numbers</p><p>* MAC addresses</p><p>* Brand and model</p><p>* Functional status (working, not working, partially working)</p><p>* Condition of equipment (good, worn, damaged, missing parts)</p><p><br></p><p>8. Verify Equipment Functionality</p><p>The technician must:</p><p>* Power on and test available equipment</p><p>* Note any devices that do not function or are not responding</p><p>* Report any missing, damaged, or suspect components</p><p>* Clearly document non-functional items for project team visibility</p><p><br></p><p>9. Provide Site Survey Summary &amp; Recommendations</p><p>Include:</p><p>* Observations that may affect design or installation</p><p>* Recommended equipment placement</p><p>* Additional materials, labor, or specialty services required</p><p>* Risks, constraints, or concerns</p><p>* Confirmation of any equipment that is non-functional or missing</p><p><br></p><p>Technician Requirements</p><p>* Bring standard AV survey and installation tools (tape measure, stud finder, laser level, cable tracer, etc.).</p><p>* Document all findings clearly in the Field Nation report.</p><p>* Upload all required landscape photos and survey notes before closing the work order.</p><p>* Complete the attached room survey form for each room surveyed.</p><p>* Ensure accuracy of equipment details (serial, MAC, model, functionality).</p><p><br></p><p>Check-In Procedure</p><p>Please text the Vivo Project Manager or Coordinator upon arrival to confirm check-in.</p><p><br></p><p>Deliverables</p><p>* Completed survey document(s) for each room</p><p>* All photos (landscape format only) uploaded via Field Nation</p><p>* Equipment details (serial/MAC/brand) and functionality report</p><p>* Complete notes, observations, and recommendations submitted with the work order</p><p><br></p><p>FILL OUT ATTACHED DOCUMENT FOR EACH ROOM SURVEYED</p>UPLOAD ALL PHOTOS VIA FIELD NATION FOR APPROVAL","markdown":"Work Order Description – AV Site Survey\n\nLocation: 100 Cascade Pointe Lane suite 102, Cary, NC 27513, USA\n\nOverview\n\nThe AV technician will perform a comprehensive onsite audiovisual site survey of 1 standard room to gather all required information for system design, installation planning, and project scoping. The focus of this survey is complete photos, accurate measurements, and network information.\n\nScope of Work\n\nThe technician will:\n\n1\\. Conduct a Comprehensive Walkthrough\n\n\\* Survey the assigned room and document site conditions, infrastructure, and equipment status.\n\n2\\. Collect Detailed Measurements\n\n\\* Room dimensions (length, width, height)\n\n\\* Display/TV sizes and mounting locations\n\n\\* Ceiling height and structural considerations\n\n\\* Furniture and table dimensions\n\n\\* Distances relevant to camera, microphone, and display positioning\n\n3\\. Document Proposed Equipment &amp; Infrastructure Locations\n\nIdentify and record potential mounting or installation points for:\n\n\\* Displays\n\n\\* Cameras\n\n\\* Microphones / ceiling arrays\n\n\\* Speakers\n\n\\* Equipment racks/cabinets\n\n\\* Control panels\n\n\\* Cable pathways and conduit routes\n\n\\* Data drops and network jacks (label numbers, location, and condition)\n\n4\\. Assess Site Conditions Affecting Installation\n\nNote any conditions that may impact scope, labor, or safety, including:\n\n\\* Concrete, brick, glass, or other specialty wall types\n\n\\* Limited/no cable pathways or conduit restrictions\n\n\\* Ceiling access issues (hard-lid, high ceilings, obstructions)\n\n\\* Existing AV, IT, or electrical infrastructure\n\n\\* Any visible damage in the room such as water leakage, ceiling stains, wall cracks, floor damage, or anything that could compromise installed equipment\n\n\\* HVAC, lighting, or architectural obstructions\n\n5\\. Verify Infrastructure &amp; Utilities\n\n\\* Confirm availability and condition of power at all proposed equipment locations\n\n\\* Identify and test network ports (if possible); record distances to switch locations\n\n\\* Record network information for the room, including port and patch panel labels, switch location, switch make and model if visible, and available ports\n\n\\* Note any missing, damaged, or insufficient connections\n\n6\\. Capture Comprehensive Photos (Required in Landscape Orientation Only)\n\nAll photos must be taken in landscape mode to ensure consistency.\n\nInclude clear images of:\n\n\\* The front, rear, and sides of the room\n\n\\* Ceiling and above-ceiling areas (if accessible)\n\n\\* Existing equipment (front, back, and connections)\n\n\\* Rack spaces and cable management areas\n\n\\* Data drops and wall plates\n\n\\* Any structural or environmental damage\n\n\\* Any condition that may impact installation\n\n7\\. Document Existing Equipment Details\n\nFor all AV, IT, or peripheral equipment present in the room, the technician must collect and record:\n\n\\* Serial numbers\n\n\\* MAC addresses\n\n\\* Brand and model\n\n\\* Functional status (working, not working, partially working)\n\n\\* Condition of equipment (good, worn, damaged, missing parts)\n\n8\\. Verify Equipment Functionality\n\nThe technician must:\n\n\\* Power on and test available equipment\n\n\\* Note any devices that do not function or are not responding\n\n\\* Report any missing, damaged, or suspect components\n\n\\* Clearly document non-functional items for project team visibility\n\n9\\. Provide Site Survey Summary &amp; Recommendations\n\nInclude:\n\n\\* Observations that may affect design or installation\n\n\\* Recommended equipment placement\n\n\\* Additional materials, labor, or specialty services required\n\n\\* Risks, constraints, or concerns\n\n\\* Confirmation of any equipment that is non-functional or missing\n\nTechnician Requirements\n\n\\* Bring standard AV survey and installation tools (tape measure, stud finder, laser level, cable tracer, etc.).\n\n\\* Document all findings clearly in the Field Nation report.\n\n\\* Upload all required landscape photos and survey notes before closing the work order.\n\n\\* Complete the attached room survey form for each room surveyed.\n\n\\* Ensure accuracy of equipment details (serial, MAC, model, functionality).\n\nCheck-In Procedure\n\nPlease text the Vivo Project Manager or Coordinator upon arrival to confirm check-in.\n\nDeliverables\n\n\\* Completed survey document(s) for each room\n\n\\* All photos (landscape format only) uploaded via Field Nation\n\n\\* Equipment details (serial/MAC/brand) and functionality report\n\n\\* Complete notes, observations, and recommendations submitted with the work order\n\nFILL OUT ATTACHED DOCUMENT FOR EACH ROOM SURVEYED\n\nUPLOAD ALL PHOTOS VIA FIELD NATION FOR APPROVAL","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T09:00","end":"2026-11-04T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":175,"max":175},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.701195199268063},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Kinettix Inc, Direct Onboarding - Vinson Services LLC -"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summar