{"job":{"id":20303181,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Esco Technologies","title":"Power Over Coax Line Tracing/Diagnosis","description":{"html":"<p><strong>This is a low-voltage (but high amperage job. Please do not accept if you are not comfortable with and trained for such scenarios.</strong></p><p><strong>Required tools and equipment - </strong></p><ul><li>Basic hand and power tools</li><li>Multimeter - Suitable for low- and mid-voltage testing</li><li>Cable tape/cable fish tape</li><li>Bulk coax cable and terminals - At least 100 Feet</li><li>Terminal Crimper</li></ul><p><strong>*** MUST HAVE EXPERIENCE WITH THROUGH-WALL and THROUGH-CEILING CABLING ***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW)</strong></p><p><strong>1. Case &amp; Location Overview</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Facility Name:</strong> PruittHealth - Raleigh</li><li><strong>Site Address:</strong> 2420 Lake Wheeler Rd, Raleigh, NC 27603</li><li><strong>On-Site Contact:</strong> Mark Barbour (Maintenance Director) <strong>Contact Phone:</strong> (910) 890-1623 <strong>Contact Email:</strong> mbarbour@pruitthealth.com</li></ul><p><strong>2. Problem Description &amp; Background</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reported Issue:</strong> The circuit breaker feeding or associated with Unit 609B keeps tripping repeatedly. An onsite technician is required to trace the wiring/cabling in the electrical closet, diagnose the root cause of the overheating/tripping breaker, and resolve the power/connectivity configuration issue.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Technician Objectives &amp; Scope of Services</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Check-In:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upon arrival, check in with the on-site contact, Mark Barbour (Maintenance Director), to confirm the exact location of the electrical closet and Unit 609B.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Electrical &amp; Wiring Inspection:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inspect the electrical panel, wiring, and specific breaker linked to Unit 609B. Check for signs of thermal damage, loose connections, or improper load matching.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Safety First:</em> Exercise extreme caution regarding the reported overheating breaker. Verify panel safety protocols before handling components.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Cable Trace &amp; Organization:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Access the electrical closet to sort through, trace, and organize the bundle of wire and coax cables.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Identify the correct lines feeding Unit 609B and verify proper port connection, grounding, and signal/power integrity.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Resolution &amp; Testing:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Rectify any mislabeled, shorted, or incorrectly routed cabling.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Test the circuit under load to ensure the replacement breaker no longer overheats and the power/TV service remains stable without tripping.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review findings and completed work with Mark Barbour.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**This is a low-voltage (but high amperage job. Please do not accept if you are not comfortable with and trained for such scenarios.**\n\n**Required tools and equipment -**\n\n- Basic hand and power tools\n- Multimeter - Suitable for low- and mid-voltage testing\n- Cable tape/cable fish tape\n- Bulk coax cable and terminals - At least 100 Feet\n- Terminal Crimper\n\n**\\*\\*\\* MUST HAVE EXPERIENCE WITH THROUGH-WALL and THROUGH-CEILING CABLING \\*\\*\\***\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW)**\n\n**1. Case &amp; Location Overview**\n\n- **Facility Name:** PruittHealth - Raleigh\n- **Site Address:** 2420 Lake Wheeler Rd, Raleigh, NC 27603\n- **On-Site Contact:** Mark Barbour (Maintenance Director) **Contact Phone:** (910) 890-1623 **Contact Email:** mbarbour@pruitthealth.com\n\n**2. Problem Description &amp; Background**\n\n- **Reported Issue:** The circuit breaker feeding or associated with Unit 609B keeps tripping repeatedly. An onsite technician is required to trace the wiring/cabling in the electrical closet, diagnose the root cause of the overheating/tripping breaker, and resolve the power/connectivity configuration issue.\n\n**3. Technician Objectives &amp; Scope of Services**\n\n1. **Check-In:**\n\n- Upon arrival, check in with the on-site contact, Mark Barbour (Maintenance Director), to confirm the exact location of the electrical closet and Unit 609B.\n\n1. **Electrical &amp; Wiring Inspection:**\n\n- Inspect the electrical panel, wiring, and specific breaker linked to Unit 609B. Check for signs of thermal damage, loose connections, or improper load matching.\n- *Safety First:* Exercise extreme caution regarding the reported overheating breaker. Verify panel safety protocols before handling components.\n\n1. **Cable Trace &amp; Organization:**\n\n- Access the electrical closet to sort through, trace, and organize the bundle of wire and coax cables.\n- Identify the correct lines feeding Unit 609B and verify proper port connection, grounding, and signal/power integrity.\n\n1. **Resolution &amp; Testing:**\n\n- Rectify any mislabeled, shorted, or incorrectly routed cabling.\n- Test the circuit under load to ensure the replacement breaker no longer overheats and the power/TV service remains stable without tripping.\n- Review findings and completed work with Mark Barbour.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T11:30","end":"2026-11-04T16:30","latestStart":"2026-11-04T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":425},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":85,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":9.932767652996793},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Kinettix Inc, Direct Onboarding - Vinson Services LLC -"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793739883233}
{"job":{"id":20284824,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Scarsdale Security Systems Inc","title":"Scarsdale Ticket #849436 - Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation.  Troubleshoot/repair as necessary.  See notes for details.","description":{"html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation. Troubleshoot/repair as necessary. See notes for details.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving&nbsp;(FN App Signature is acceptable)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>**IMPORTANT** In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.</strong></li>\n<li>IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.</li>\n<li>TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL *PROVIDER* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. *OR* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION &amp; TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT.&nbsp;<strong>CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 **) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER -</strong>368966232</li>\n<li>**WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. **CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!</li>\n<li>FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.</li>\n<li>**BEFORE LEAVING SITE*** Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members</li>\n<li>***IMPORTANT** If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.</li>\n<li>CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements 1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent 2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed 3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving.</li>\n<li>9/23/26 - ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) reported RF Low Battery - , then on 10/30 reported MISSING @ 6:06 AM and was Bypassd same night. Users tripping zn 503 motion at Disarm 10/31 &amp; 11/1) 8/30/26 - ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal) reported RF Low Battery -, then on 10/22 reported MISSING @ 4:24 AM, Bypassed same night.</li>\n<li>RF BATTERY REPLACEMENT -- a) Verify transmitter serial number to ensure it is correct detector/transmitter, b) Replace CR123A, press transmitter reset button. c) Ensure transmitter housing is properly closed/seated and test operation. d) Ensure detector resumes normal operation and that Restore signals are received at central station. (Must perform Sensor Reset) ** *DMP wireless systems REQUIRE Sensor Reset at keypad before restore signal is sent. Extreme cases may also require J16 panel reset. ** * Ademco/Honeywell system may require reset to restore wireless (CODE + OFF two times in a row at keypad) ** * INOVONICS - Requires receiver reset - Press/Release RESET button on Inovonics receiver, replace cover. **--Call Scarsdale 914-722-2933 to verify signals and for programming assistance &amp; support --**</li>\n<li>Replace CR123A batteries at: * ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) * ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"- **Technician to provide and replace (2) CR123A batteries at front door zones 501 and 502 and test operation. Troubleshoot/repair as necessary. See notes for details.**\n\n**CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements**\n\n**1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent**\n\n**2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed**\n\n**3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving (FN App Signature is acceptable)**\n\n- **\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* In order for technician to get paid, a SIGNED SERVICE TICKET must also be returned with ticket notes. THIS IS THE CUSTOMER'S EXPECTATION**\n- **﻿YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE CONFIDENTIAL INFO SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER !! Thank You.**\n- IF A PART NEEDS TO BE REPLACED, DOCUMENT THE MAKE, MODEL AND SERIAL NUMBER OF DEVICE. PROVIDE NOTES AS TO WHY PART MUST BE REPLACED. UPLOAD PICTURE TO WORK ORDER.\n- TECH TO HAVE SERVICE CHANNEL \\*PROVIDER\\* APP INSTALLED ON PHONE OR TABLET. SEE GOOGLE PLAY STORE OR APPLE STORE FOR THE FREE APP. USE APP TO CHECK IN AND OUT. \\*OR\\* TECHNICIAN MUST USE AUTOMATED RESPONSE SYSTEM (IVR) TO CHECK IN WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON ARRIVAL TO THE LOCATION &amp; TO CHECK OUT WITH THE STORE PHONE UPON COMPLETION OF THE VISIT. **CALL- USA- 516.500.7776 \\*\\*) – PIN NUMBER 75182 AND TRACKING NUMBER -**368966232\n- \\*\\*WHEN CALLING FROM PREMISE PHONE, IF IVR DOES NOT LET YOU SIGN IN and OUT, CALL 855-269-6471. This will allow you to speak directly with a Service Channel Representative. If all else fails, call a Scarsdale Customer Service Representative at 914-722-2933. Thank you. \\*\\*CHECKING IN WITH THE IVR DOES NOT PUT YOUR SYSTEM ON TEST!!!\n- FOR SYSTEM ON-TEST OR TECHNICAL SUPPORT WHEN ON SITE CALL 914-722-2933 BETWEEN 8 AM AND 7:30 PM EST MON - FRI.\n- \\*\\*BEFORE LEAVING SITE\\*\\*\\* Technician MUST email notes/resolution to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com OR call 914-722-2933 and speak to one of our National Account Team Members\n- \\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT\\*\\* If a part needs to be replaced DOCUMENT the make, model, serial #. MUST PROVIDE NOTES as to WHY the part needs replaced (I.E. Damaged? Physically missing? Remodeling? Provide these DETAILS and upload picture to work order and/or email to nationalservice@scarsdalesecurity.com Use provided return label to return ship any unused parts.\n- CRITICAL CUSTOMER/SSS Requirements 1. Must use Service Channel IVR, APP (preferred), Phone, or Live Agent 2. Must upload BEFORE and AFTER pictures of work performed 3. Must get a signed ticket before leaving.\n- 9/23/26 - ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) reported RF Low Battery - , then on 10/30 reported MISSING @ 6:06 AM and was Bypassd same night. Users tripping zn 503 motion at Disarm 10/31 &amp; 11/1) 8/30/26 - ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal) reported RF Low Battery -, then on 10/22 reported MISSING @ 4:24 AM, Bypassed same night.\n- RF BATTERY REPLACEMENT -- a) Verify transmitter serial number to ensure it is correct detector/transmitter, b) Replace CR123A, press transmitter reset button. c) Ensure transmitter housing is properly closed/seated and test operation. d) Ensure detector resumes normal operation and that Restore signals are received at central station. (Must perform Sensor Reset) \\*\\* \\*DMP wireless systems REQUIRE Sensor Reset at keypad before restore signal is sent. Extreme cases may also require J16 panel reset. \\*\\* \\* Ademco/Honeywell system may require reset to restore wireless (CODE + OFF two times in a row at keypad) \\*\\* \\* INOVONICS - Requires receiver reset - Press/Release RESET button on Inovonics receiver, replace cover. \\*\\*--Call Scarsdale 914-722-2933 to verify signals and for programming assistance &amp; support --\\*\\*\n- Replace CR123A batteries at: \\* ZN 501 FRONT DR LEFT (sn 01798310, Internal) \\* ZN 502 FRONT RIGHT DR (sn 01798379, Internal)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":12.459188081253307},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2