{"job":{"id":20304023,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Telco Holdings Inc","title":"Aberdeen, NC - Troubleshoot Printer Connection - 11/6","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Provider, Please Read the following:</u></strong></p><p>By accepting this assignment, you confirm you have reviewed and understand all attached documentation, including floor plans and SOW documents.</p><p>Tobacco and vape use is prohibited onsite at all times, including inside, outside, and in personal vehicles while checked in or obtaining materials for this work order.</p><p>Technicians must maintain business-casual attire. No flip-flops, torn clothing, tank tops, shorts, hats, open/excessively revealing clothing, or athletic wear. Clean jeans and sneakers are acceptable.</p><p>The NTE listed on the work order is an estimated labor allowance only and does not guarantee payable hours.</p><p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Please Note: You will need</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">***Extra ethernet cable</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">***Cable tester for ethernet</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Service Address &amp; Details:</p><p>Service Ticket number:&nbsp;665303 - Reoccurring issue with printer connection</p><p>Client Location Name:&nbsp;Guardian - Kuhn Dental Associates</p><p>Client Location Address: 1902 N Sandhills Blvd, Aberdeen, NC 28315</p><p>Number of Technicians: 1</p><p>Technician Type: Smart Hands</p><p>****Technician MUST present as on-site for ThincForward Inc.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Access Hours:</p><p>Preferred Days/Times for On Site Dispatch: Friday 11/6 @ 1pm EST</p><p>NTE: 2 hours</p><p>****Business casual attire required – no flip flops, open toed shoes, or torn clothing.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Tools/Equipment Required:</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">***Extra ethernet cable</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">***Cable tester for ethernet</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Laptop and Hot spot for internet access</p><p>Cable Tester and Toner</p><p>Screw drivers.</p><p>Spare Patch Cords (Length varies)</p><p>Spare Keystone Jacks for replacement of bad ones</p><p>Butt Set if troubleshooting Telecom Issues</p><p>Cable ties/cable management options for general cleanup where needed</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Local Site Contact Name and Number: Ashley Nall<del> ***** ********</del></p><p>Technical Support Contact (Off-Site):</p><p>ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600</p><p>*Please call and leave a message if there is no answer.&nbsp;If your call is not returned in 15 minutes, please call in again and if there is no answer, please call your Dispatcher/Work Order Manager for support.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Scope Of Work:</p><p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:</p><p>1) Upon arrival call your work order manager/dispatch contact to check in on site.</p><p>2) Once checked in please call the Technical Support Contact (ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600) to review SOW and then proceed to the front desk to check in with the site contact.</p><p>3) Introduce yourself to the site contact as onsite as ThincForward and briefly review the SOW you will be completing.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>4) Detailed Scope of Work: **Smart Hands technician needed on site to: **Troubleshoot the printer that keeps dropping off the network. Bring a cable tester to make sure it's not the wall ethernet jack. Call the IT Helpdesk for assistance</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>5) Take images of ALL completed work on site including cabling, jacks/faceplates, and replaced equipment in functional order.</p><p>6) *Old Equipment:*&nbsp;If you have replaced equipment on site, please follow the notes below regarding what to do with the old items.</p><p>Please dispose of the old equipment.</p><p>7) Once SOW is completed, Technician(s) must confirm all equipment on site is up and operational, and technician(s) must speak with technical support prior to leaving the site to ensure SOW is complete and to ensure there are no delays in payment.</p><p>8) Once the site and support have confirmed work is completed, technician(s) must check out with the work order manager/dispatch contact to sign out of the location.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Deliverables:</p><p>- Images of ALL completed work.</p><p>- Name of person worked with on site and in support.</p><p>- Confirmation that work area has been completely cleaned and is dust free.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>***DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ***</strong></p><p><strong>*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered.&nbsp;*</strong></p><p><strong>﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager.&nbsp;Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Call Work Order Manager regarding Your Field Nation Work Order to check in</li><li>Call 267-434-1600 regarding Call Helpdesk to check in onsite and verify work to be completed</li><li>Once work is completed, please ensure work area has been cleaned up</li><li>Upload/take photo of Provide images of all completed work</li><li>Upload file of Complete Attached Tech Sign Off Sheet in full and collect onsite client signature</li><li>Call 267-434-1600 regarding call the Helpdesk to verify all work is completed before checking out of site</li><li>Call Work Order Manager regarding Your Field Nation Work Order to check off site</li></ul>","markdown":"**Provider, Please Read the following:**\n\nBy accepting this assignment, you confirm you have reviewed and understand all attached documentation, including floor plans and SOW documents.\n\nTobacco and vape use is prohibited onsite at all times, including inside, outside, and in personal vehicles while checked in or obtaining materials for this work order.\n\nTechnicians must maintain business-casual attire. No flip-flops, torn clothing, tank tops, shorts, hats, open/excessively revealing clothing, or athletic wear. Clean jeans and sneakers are acceptable.\n\nThe NTE listed on the work order is an estimated labor allowance only and does not guarantee payable hours.\n\nTechnician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:\n\n**Please Note: You will need**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Extra ethernet cable**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Cable tester for ethernet**\n\nService Address &amp; Details:\n\nService Ticket number: 665303 - Reoccurring issue with printer connection\n\nClient Location Name: Guardian - Kuhn Dental Associates\n\nClient Location Address: 1902 N Sandhills Blvd, Aberdeen, NC 28315\n\nNumber of Technicians: 1\n\nTechnician Type: Smart Hands\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*Technician MUST present as on-site for ThincForward Inc.\n\nAccess Hours:\n\nPreferred Days/Times for On Site Dispatch: Friday 11/6 @ 1pm EST\n\nNTE: 2 hours\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*Business casual attire required – no flip flops, open toed shoes, or torn clothing.\n\nTools/Equipment Required:\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Extra ethernet cable**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Cable tester for ethernet**\n\nLaptop and Hot spot for internet access\n\nCable Tester and Toner\n\nScrew drivers.\n\nSpare Patch Cords (Length varies)\n\nSpare Keystone Jacks for replacement of bad ones\n\nButt Set if troubleshooting Telecom Issues\n\nCable ties/cable management options for general cleanup where needed\n\nLocal Site Contact Name and Number: Ashley Nall \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTechnical Support Contact (Off-Site):\n\nThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600\n\n\\*Please call and leave a message if there is no answer. If your call is not returned in 15 minutes, please call in again and if there is no answer, please call your Dispatcher/Work Order Manager for support.\n\nScope Of Work:\n\nTechnician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:\n\n1\\) Upon arrival call your work order manager/dispatch contact to check in on site.\n\n2\\) Once checked in please call the Technical Support Contact (ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600) to review SOW and then proceed to the front desk to check in with the site contact.\n\n3\\) Introduce yourself to the site contact as onsite as ThincForward and briefly review the SOW you will be completing.\n\n4\\) Detailed Scope of Work: \\*\\*Smart Hands technician needed on site to: \\*\\*Troubleshoot the printer that keeps dropping off the network. Bring a cable tester to make sure it's not the wall ethernet jack. Call the IT Helpdesk for assistance\n\n5\\) Take images of ALL completed work on site including cabling, jacks/faceplates, and replaced equipment in functional order.\n\n6\\) \\*Old Equipment:\\* If you have replaced equipment on site, please follow the notes below regarding what to do with the old items.\n\nPlease dispose of the old equipment.\n\n7\\) Once SOW is completed, Technician(s) must confirm all equipment on site is up and operational, and technician(s) must speak with technical support prior to leaving the site to ensure SOW is complete and to ensure there are no delays in payment.\n\n8\\) Once the site and support have confirmed work is completed, technician(s) must check out with the work order manager/dispatch contact to sign out of the location.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n\\- Images of ALL completed work.\n\n\\- Name of person worked with on site and in support.\n\n\\- Confirmation that work area has been completely cleaned and is dust free.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered. \\***\n\n**﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager. Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.**\n\n- Call Work Order Manager regarding Your Field Nation Work Order to check in\n- Call 267-434-1600 regarding Call Helpdesk to check in onsite and verify work to be completed\n- Once work is completed, please ensure work area has been cleaned up\n- Upload/take photo of Provide images of all completed work\n- Upload file of Complete Attached Tech Sign Off Sheet in full and collect onsite client signature\n- Call 267-434-1600 regarding call the Helpdesk to verify all work is completed before checking out of site\n- Call Work Order Manager regarding Your Field Nation Work Order to check off site","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T13:00","end":"2026-11-06T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":62.74727483854081},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793744246986}
