{"job":{"id":20304301,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"LEAD Technician | Store Remodeling - Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>REMAINING SCOPE:<br/><br/>• DLPM Review - the old encoders are still online- please remove. Cash office hallway goes on sales floor –confirm with CCTV if it is in correct spot. Processing man door needs to look at door to outside and not sale floor- Confirm Placement with CCTV. Troubleshoot Exit Mullion (.006) and footwear PVM (.074) offline. <br/><br/>Security Code: 719745</p><p><strong><u>Location Specific Notes / Instructions:</u></strong> <em style=\"font-size: 10px;\">(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)</em></p><p>SOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present</p></BR><p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Seeking Lead<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;<strong>Over Multiple</strong>&nbsp;<strong>NIGHTs</strong>. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be working with Remote Bridge Line, Onsite MOD, and Site General Contractors nightly / throughout the project.</p><ul><li>Lead Tech is&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">responsible</span>&nbsp;for reviewing and referring to ALL provided&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Remodel Onsite Technician Instructions / Documentation&nbsp;</span>[GENERAL PROJECT SPECIFIC &amp; STORE SPECIFIC Documentation] - Refer to the provided SharePoint Links. Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial.</li><li>Lead Technician will be provided/working with multiple assist technicians to help with the completion of the scope.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;join and work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>*** </del>Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;via the provided Bridge Line while onsite (Recommend having Ear Buds). You will be responsible for providing various check-ins, good communications, and updates to the Remote RTCs/ Bridge Line team throughout the night. At 6:00am you will be required to provide hourly updates.</li><li>Lead Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;review Nightly Scope of Work with the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> Remote RTS Group</strong>&nbsp;at the beginning of each&nbsp;<strong>NIGHT</strong>. Technician to refer to the Store Specific Technical Scope and not deviate from the plan without approval from REMOTE TEAM.</li><li><strong>Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Store Completion Deliverables [Not Nightly but At/Towards the Completion of the Store Remodel]:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">FLUIX Online Deliverable – Lead Technician will need to complete two various deliverables at / towards the completion of the STORE [ FRONTLINE COMPLETION &amp; FULL STORE COMPLETION]. Technician will need to submit these and have them reviewed by the&nbsp;<strong><del>***</del> REMOTE RTC BRIDGELINE.</strong>&nbsp;[If deliverable&nbsp;session is interrupted, choose “In progress” to avoid losing work.]</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>***</del>  umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del> REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</stron