-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Check-<em>I</em>n with Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with / take direction from the the Essintial LEAD TECHNICIAN while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Visit Specific Notes/Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nREMAINING SCOPE:  \n  \n• DLPM Review - the old encoders are still online- please remove. Cash office hallway goes on sales floor –confirm with CCTV if it is in correct spot. Processing man door needs to look at door to outside and not sale floor- Confirm Placement with CCTV. Troubleshoot Exit Mullion (.006) and footwear PVM (.074) offline.   \n  \nSecurity Code: 719745\n\n**Location Specific Notes / Instructions:** *(consider these notes along with the full scope of work below)*\n\nSOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present\n\n**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking an Assist Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store’s cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!**\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- **Special SECURITY Access Code** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* - Tool &amp; Material List Document** **Link** (download to view full document): <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Estimated Duration: Multiple Days** estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n***Important Site Information / Requirements:***\n\n- You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n **Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.** Please **READ &amp; REVIEW** all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link \\[VERY IMPORTANT\\]****:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\_Install Guides** **Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):** <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ>\n- **\\*\\*\\* Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List** **Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8>\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training Link**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8>\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\_Remodel\\_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1** **Link**: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial**\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- **Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site**\n- **Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE** - you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -** Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the **SECURITY CODE to gain access**\n- **Check-*I*n with Essintial Lead Technician**\n\n**ONSITE: Work with / take direction from the the Essintial LEAD TECHNICIAN while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- **Complete Nightly Completion Items** - Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. \\[I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.\n- **Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician**\n- **Check-Out** with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC\n- **Call** - Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the \\*\\*\\* Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line\n- All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T05:45","end":"2026-11-06T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":57.54261305786768},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793746449912}
{"job":{"id":20304424,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Computech Technology Services","title":"Need A Technician Onsite to Troubleshoot Wireless Network w/Remote Support - See Description","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST&nbsp;*<u>CALL <del>***** ********</del>* OR TEXT *<del>***** ********</del>*</u>&nbsp;TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.</strong></p><p>We need a technician to visit our clients site to troubleshoot the wireless connection with remote support.</p><p>The site has (2) buildings, with (2) access points and a cloud key controller in the main building, and (1) access point and a cloud key in the 2nd building. The site has (2) independent high speed ISP connections, with separate routers and switches in each building. We believe the issue is isolated to just the main building with the (2) AP's.</p><p>The customers remote admin is able to see both cloud keys remotely, and all initial indications show that the wireless network is up and working in both buildings as it has for years.</p><p>The onsite contact states that they are having intermittent connection issues at both ends of the building, so we need to investigate and troubleshoot.</p><p>The AP's and cloud keys were installed in 2022, however, we don't have a map to determine where the AP's are located to compare with what the onsite contact has stated, so we are unable to determine where, and how many additional AP's could be added to increase coverage, or if there is some other issue going on like bad ISP, bad router, bad switch?</p><p>Tech will need to work with the remote contact to survey the wireless network coverage and associated routers and switches, and work with the onsite contact to determine if, how many, and where to install additional access points, or if any other equipment (router,switch) needs to be replaced.</p><p>Tech should use the <strong>attached site map</strong>, and <strong>mark up the existing AP locations</strong>, and the <strong>areas of low coverage</strong> according to the onsite contact.</p><p><strong>Tech will work with the customers remote network admin <del>******** ****** ************ ** ************</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Materials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.</p><p><strong>Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Punch Tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Push/Pull Rods</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Ladder(s)</li><li>Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)</li></ul><p><strong>Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):</strong></p><ul><li>​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks</li><li>External Keystone Biscuits</li><li>Keystone Faceplates</li><li>Mudrings</li><li>Misc Patch Cable(s)</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.</li><li>Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.</li><li>Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.</li><li>ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.</li></ul><p><strong>Material Compensation:</strong></p><p>PLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:</p><p>Item - Pre-Approved Pricing</p><p>Cat5e Riser - $0.18ft</p><p>Cat5e Plenum - $0.22ft</p><p>Cat6 Riser - $0.25ft</p><p>Cat6 Plenum - $0.28ft</p><p>RG59/RG6 - $0.12ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Siamese RG59 - $0.15ft</p><p>Cat5e Jack - $3.00ea</p><p>Cat6 Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- $3.75ea</p><p>Faceplate - $1.30ea</p><p>Surface Mount Box - $1.50ea</p><p>Patch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea</p><p>BNC Connectors - $3.00ea</p><p>Modular Plug - $0.55ea</p><p>Power Strip - $6.00ea</p><p>4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea</p><p>2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea</p><p>Cable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea</p><p>Patch Panel - Negotiable/at cost</p><p>Telco 66block - Negotiable/at cost</p><p><br></p><p>Tech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.</p><p>At ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.</p>","markdown":"**Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST \\*CALL \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* OR TEXT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.**\n\nWe need a technician to visit our clients site to troubleshoot the wireless connection with remote support.\n\nThe site has (2) buildings, with (2) access points and a cloud key controller in the main building, and (1) access point and a cloud key in the 2nd building. The site has (2) independent high speed ISP connections, with separate routers and switches in each building. We believe the issue is isolated to just the main building with the (2) AP's.\n\nThe customers remote admin is able to see both cloud keys remotely, and all initial indications show that the wireless network is up and working in both buildings as it has for years.\n\nThe onsite contact states that they are having intermittent connection issues at both ends of the building, so we need to investigate and troubleshoot.\n\nThe AP's and cloud keys were installed in 2022, however, we don't have a map to determine where the AP's are located to compare with what the onsite contact has stated, so we are unable to determine where, and how many additional AP's could be added to increase coverage, or if there is some other issue going on like bad ISP, bad router, bad switch?\n\nTech will need to work with the remote contact to survey the wireless network coverage and associated routers and switches, and work with the onsite contact to determine if, how many, and where to install additional access points, or if any other equipment (router,switch) needs to be replaced.\n\nTech should use the **attached site map**, and **mark up the existing AP locations**, and the **areas of low coverage** according to the onsite contact.\n\n**Tech will work with the customers remote network admin \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nMaterials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.\n\n**Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:**\n\n- Punch Tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Toner\n- Buttset\n- Push/Pull Rods\n- Fish Tape\n- Ladder(s)\n- Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)\n\n**Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):**\n\n- ​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable\n- Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks\n- External Keystone Biscuits\n- Keystone Faceplates\n- Mudrings\n- Misc Patch Cable(s)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.\n- Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.\n- Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.\n- ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.\n\n**Material Compensation:**\n\nPLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:\n\nItem - Pre-Approved Pricing\n\nCat5e Riser - $0.18ft\n\nCat5e Plenum - $0.22ft\n\nCat6 Riser - $0.25ft\n\nCat6 Plenum - $0.28ft\n\nRG59/RG6 - $0.12ft\n\nSiamese RG59 - $0.15ft\n\nCat5e Jack - $3.00ea\n\nCat6 Jack - $3.75ea\n\nFaceplate - $1.30ea\n\nSurface Mount Box - $1.50ea\n\nPatch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea\n\nBNC Connectors - $3.00ea\n\nModular Plug - $0.55ea\n\nPower Strip - $6.00ea\n\n4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea\n\n2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea\n\nCable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea\n\nPatch Panel - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTelco 66block - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.\n\nAt ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":23.050870818484107},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793746700056}
{"job":{"id":20304425,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Install Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Scope: Installation/replacement of 500 sheet staple finisher on Lexmark CX833xse Printer</p><p>SN: 7566436010RF1</p><p>If Tech is unable to reach work order POC, please call the Service Desk at 919-754-2323 select Opt 3.&nbsp;</p><p>Some offices are open on certain days, please contact the NCDOR Service Desk to arrange the best time to go onsite.</p><p>Tech should call Service Desk at 919 754 2323 Opt 3 for the close out of service tickets.</p><p>Tech should provide the Physical Location 1 information to the Service Desk once onsite so they can easily assist.&nbsp;The Physical Location 1 data is the device tag.</p><p>COVID 19 Guidelines, please comply:</p><p>1) Demonstrate that you are fully vaccinated or submit COVID-19 test results if unvaccinated or partially vaccinated.</p><p>2) Wear a face covering where required, regardless of vaccination status.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(13, 13, 13);\">If there is an old printer, please place it in the box of the new printer and leave it onsite. Lexmark will then send a shipping team to collect and return it.</strong></p><p>New PIN# that was created for Park Place techs to use when calling into TSC for anything. Maybe tracking, additional point of contact, to report something broken.</p><p><strong>1-800-332-4120, will ask for PIN#75450250</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Pla