chnicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:**\n\nScope: Installation/replacement of 500 sheet staple finisher on Lexmark CX833xse Printer\n\nSN: 7566436010RF1\n\nIf Tech is unable to reach work order POC, please call the Service Desk at 919-754-2323 select Opt 3.\n\nSome offices are open on certain days, please contact the NCDOR Service Desk to arrange the best time to go onsite.\n\nTech should call Service Desk at 919 754 2323 Opt 3 for the close out of service tickets.\n\nTech should provide the Physical Location 1 information to the Service Desk once onsite so they can easily assist. The Physical Location 1 data is the device tag.\n\nCOVID 19 Guidelines, please comply:\n\n1\\) Demonstrate that you are fully vaccinated or submit COVID-19 test results if unvaccinated or partially vaccinated.\n\n2\\) Wear a face covering where required, regardless of vaccination status.\n\n**If there is an old printer, please place it in the box of the new printer and leave it onsite. Lexmark will then send a shipping team to collect and return it.**\n\nNew PIN# that was created for Park Place techs to use when calling into TSC for anything. Maybe tracking, additional point of contact, to report something broken.\n\n**1-800-332-4120, will ask for PIN#75450250**\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you 