{"job":{"id":20304575,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axiom Service Management LLC","title":"HP CLJ M479FDN - Constant jamming","description":{"html":"Customer Reference: 49650 --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- STARGEL OFFICE SOLUTIONS\n\n--- INSTRUCTIONS ---\nETA pending, Dispatch will update you when tech support releases the call and advise you how to proceed.\n\nTechnician must confirm the serial number and the Stargel ID number.\n\nTech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG.\n\nTechnician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed.\n(Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.)\n\nFor any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2.\n\nInitial notes: HP CLJ M479FDN - Constant jamming\n\n\n\nA techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed.\nhttps://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login \ntechlink user name and password are the call number 1133023\n\n**It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to**\n\n**Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval.\n\nGeneral Instructions for All Calls-\nVerify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed.\nConfirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts.\nIf a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count.\nDo not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead.\nIf the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding.\nAfter service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR.\nIf facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.","markdown":"Customer Reference: 49650 --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- STARGEL OFFICE SOLUTIONS --- INSTRUCTIONS --- ETA pending, Dispatch will update you when tech support releases the call and advise you how to proceed. Technician must confirm the serial number and the Stargel ID number. Tech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG. Technician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed. (Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.) For any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2. Initial notes: HP CLJ M479FDN - Constant jamming A techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed. <https://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login> techlink user name and password are the call number 1133023 \\*\\*It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to\\*\\* \\*\\*Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval. General Instructions for All Calls- Verify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed. Confirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts. If a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count. Do not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead. If the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding. After service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR. If facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T08:00","end":"2026-11-05T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":41.431833688284},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793748759387}
{"job":{"id":"7434340527","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"nscglobal","title":"REQ. TWO TECHS WOR0156869 Raleigh, NC 1 of 2/ Any Day Between Mon-Fri / 65\" Display/TV Replacement","description":"<p>*** Please don't do any other work which is not listed in the work order details. You are allowed to perform any other work if its approved by the CarMax remote EUC support. Please note in case the work could not be completed because of missing parts or hardware items, please do not purchase or use your own parts or hardware items to complete the job. In such case, please reach out to us via email&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com</a>&nbsp;or call : Amol Sawant phone: +1 (646) 4999049 OR Mazo <strong>+1 (513) 8498716</strong> &amp; notify us about the situation &amp; then you are good to leave the site.***</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch 2 NSC Techs for Display Installation&nbsp;</p><p>Model of TV (LG/SAMSUNG): 65 Inch</p><p>How many technicians will be needed :2</p><p>Please note that you need to carry 6-8feet normal ladder &amp; use of scissor lifts are not allowed.</p><p>NSC Dispatch: Amol Sawant</p><p>phone: +1 (646) 4999049</p><p>OR Mazo +1 (513) 8498716</p><p><a href=\"mailto:nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com</a></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please thoroughly read the instructions given below before going onsite to service the ticket.</p><p>Please update <u>detailed resolution notes &amp; pictures</u> to justify your job completion time.</p><p>Please don't do any other work which is not listed in the work order details. You are allowed to perform any other work if its approved by the CarMax remote EUC support technician.</p><ul><li>Please note that you are not allowed to go onsite on weekends.</li><li>Make sure that you call <u>NSC Dispatch Coordinator – Amol Sawant phone: +1 (646) 4999049</u> &amp; then <u>CarMax Technology Support (contact # listed in WM assignment details)</u> from the parking lot before entering the site to let us know that you have arrived. After completion of work make sure that you <u>call CarMax Technology Support</u> so that they will verify your work &amp; release you from the site. Make sure that you call NSC Dispatch Coordinator – Amol Sawant to check out. These <u>calls are mandatory</u> to record &amp; verify your check in &amp; check out times.</li><li><u>CarMax Technology Support can approve changes or additions to initial WM instructions.</u>&nbsp;On-site managers or site contacts <u>do not have</u> that authority.&nbsp;You should call CarMax Technology Support if you run into problems or if the site contact tries to change the work instructions.</li><li><u>No work can be performed after 4.30 pm Eastern.</u>&nbsp;If you determine requested work cannot be completed by that deadline CarMax Technology Support needs to be notified immediately.&nbsp;<u>You must check-out by 4.30 pm Eastern by calling CarMax Technology Support.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Timestamp of that call will be used to validate check-out time.&nbsp;</li><li>In case the work can’t be completed because of missing parts or hardware items, please <u>do not purchase or use your own parts or hardware items to complete the job</u>. In such case, please reach out to us via email <a href=\"mailto:nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com</a> or call : Amol Sawant phone: +1 (646) 4999049 &amp; notify us about the situation &amp; then you are good to leave the site.</li><li><u>No expenses will be reimbursed</u> without prior approval from <u>NSC.</u></li><li><u>Do not discuss payment</u> with the on-site CarMax employees or the CarMax Technology Support Team. Please forward billing concerns to <a href=\"mailto:nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com</a>.</li><li>If there is an issue with the work, site, or with contacting the CarMax Technology Support, please email <a href=\"mailto:nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">nsc.carmaxdispatch@nscglobal.com</a> or call : Amol Sawant phone: +1 (646) 4999049. We will make sure your situation or issue is taken care of and will send an SOS out to the EUC team if necessary. <u>You need to call Amol Sawant phone: +1 (646) 4999049 within 1 hour </u>if you cannot locate the site contact or contact CarMax Technology Support. If possible, please try to message us earlier so that we can get an SOS out.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>When checking out, please include pictures that you have taken (such as the complete PC at its location) so that we may include that in the notes on CarMax’s side of the tickets. Make sure that your notes and pictures capture as much detail as is pertinent.</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-04T10:00","end":"2026-11-04T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-04T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-04T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Kinettix Inc, Direct Onboarding - Vinson Services LLC -"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | P