he MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum**\n- **Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.**\n- **AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.**\n- **Stud Finder**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** (for checking in and out)\n- **Digital Camera**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachment:**\n\n0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf - Print and bring to site.\n\n=======================\n\nREAD THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location\n2. Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:\n\n- Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.\n- Measurements of room where locker will be installed.\n- Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.\n\n1. Take the photos outline in the instructions.\n2. Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.\n3. Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out\n4. **Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n5. **Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.**\n\n=======================\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T10:00","end":"2026-11-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-11-09T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":57.80132039663088},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific |