{"job":{"id":20304863,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":" P#262335 - Four Oaks, NC - Site Survey","description":{"html":"<strong>FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL</strong><br><strong>Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code</strong><ul><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.</li><li><strong>Client Representation:</strong> You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.</li><li><strong>Platform Discretion:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> mention or discuss <del>***** ****** </del>or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work/On-site Task:</strong><ol><li><strong>Check-In &amp; Initial Site Assessment:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check in with the site POC and call the Remote Project Lead.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Conduct a full walkthrough of the main office interior and exterior building perimeter to evaluate structural layout, wall construction, and access paths.</li><li><strong>Main Office Network &amp; WAP Survey:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Locate the primary server room/MDF. Audit available rack units, power supply (NEMA types/UPS), backboard space, and environmental conditions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Survey ceiling structures (drop tiles, open joists) and cable pathways from the MDF to proposed main office desk drops and indoor Wireless Access Point (WAP) locations.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Identify optimal WAP ceiling-mount positions for maximum office coverage.</li><li><strong>Perimeter Camera Infrastructure Survey:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Survey exterior mounting locations for perimeter security cameras to ensure clear lines of sight and coverage angles.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Identify exterior wall/soffit penetration points, outdoor conduit paths, and distance runs from the network closet to each camera location.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check for height requirements, ladder/lift access needs, and potential weather-exposure risks for exterior cabling.</li><li><strong>Photo Documentation &amp; Deliverables:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Capture photos of:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">MDF rack, available patch panel ports, and power outlets.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Proposed internal cable pathways, ceiling grids, and office drop locations.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Exterior camera mounting locations, perimeter field of view, and building entry points.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sketch/mark up site floor plan with proposed drop counts, WAP points, camera locations, and cable run distances.</li><li><strong>Closeout:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review preliminary findings and any site constraints with the POC.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Obtain site sign-off and check out with the Remote Project Lead.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools:</strong><ul><li>Smartphone / camera with flash (for detailed photo deliverables)</li><li>Laser distance measure / tape measure</li><li>Flashlight / headlamp</li><li>Step ladder &amp; extension ladder (for ceiling grid and exterior soffit inspection)</li><li>Floor plan printouts / tablet (for pathway and camera angle markup)</li><li>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, tape measure)</li></ul><p>For <u>pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact</u>, please check the <strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION</strong> below.</p><p><br></p><strong>DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong>&nbsp;Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)</li><li><strong>Record</strong>: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong>&nbsp;Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong>&nbsp;Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong>&nbsp;Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong>&nbsp;Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within&nbsp;<strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><br>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**1. **Check-In &amp; Initial Site Assessment:**\n2. Check in with the site POC and call the Remote Project Lead.\n3. Conduct a full walkthrough of the main office interior and exterior building perimeter to evaluate structural layout, wall construction, and access paths.\n4. **Main Office Network &amp; WAP Survey:**\n5. Locate the primary server room/MDF. Audit available rack units, power supply (NEMA types/UPS), backboard space, and environmental conditions.\n6. Survey ceiling structures (drop tiles, open joists) and cable pathways from the MDF to proposed main office desk drops and indoor Wireless Access Point (WAP) locations.\n7. Identify optimal WAP ceiling-mount positions for maximum office coverage.\n8. **Perimeter Camera Infrastructure Survey:**\n9. Survey exterior mounting locations for perimeter security cameras to ensure clear lines of sight and coverage angles.\n10. Identify exterior wall/soffit penetration points, outdoor conduit paths, and distance runs from the network closet to each camera location.\n11. Check for height requirements, ladder/lift access needs, and potential weather-exposure risks for exterior cabling.\n12. **Photo Documentation &amp; Deliverables:**\n13. Capture photos of:\n14. MDF rack, available patch panel ports, and power outlets.\n15. Proposed internal cable pathways, ceiling grids, and office drop locations.\n16. Exterior camera mounting locations, perimeter field of view, and building entry points.\n17. Sketch/mark up site floor plan with proposed drop counts, WAP points, camera locations, and cable run distances.\n18. **Closeout:**\n19. Review preliminary findings and any site constraints with the POC.\n20. Obtain site sign-off and check out with the Remote Project Lead.\n\n**Required Tools:**- Smartphone / camera with flash (for detailed photo deliverables)\n- Laser distance measure / tape measure\n- Flashlight / headlamp\n- Step ladder &amp; extension ladder (for ceiling grid and exterior soffit inspection)\n- Floor plan printouts / tablet (for pathway and camera angle markup)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, tape measure)\n\nFor pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact, please check the **CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION** below.\n\n**DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:**- **Documentation:** Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)\n- **Record**: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement**\n\nBy accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T09:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35.561541751131905},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793753330052}
