{"job":{"id":20308242,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"IW Technologies","title":"Talbots - P400 Pin Pad and Stand Replacement","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Summary of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>IW Technologies is in need of a technician to go onsite at a local clothing retailer and <strong>replace the Register 1 pin pad and input the IP configuration info if needed</strong>. You are to follow the attached documentation to replace the unit, then box up the defective parts using the label provided. Leave defective parts onsite</p>\n<p>Register #: <em>&nbsp;1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Tech Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call the Service Desk at 740-951-3911, Option 3, upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not begin work without talking to the Service Desk.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tech must power down the register before installation. You must stay on site for pin pad updates to complete, which can take up to an hour.&nbsp;<strong>If the store is needing multiple pin pad replacements, it is important to make sure that you only work on one pin pad at a time.</strong></p>\n<p>Call the Service Desk at <del>************</del> → Selection option 3 for hardware technician, then press 1 for Chicos, Soma, or White House Black Market or press 2 for all other brands, upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not begin work without talking to the Service Desk.</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE NOTE: Parts are scheduled to arrive before 4:30pm local time. Be sure to track the parts as not to arrive onsite before they do. We will not compensate for a second trip due to parts not being onsite.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID</li>\n<li>&nbsp;USB Keyboard</li>\n<li>USB Mouse</li>\n<li>Velcro</li>\n<li>Termination equipment</li>\n<li>Punchdown equipment</li>\n<li>Cable tester</li>\n<li>Variety of Phillips screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Adhesive removal tools (razor blade, rubbing alcohol, etc)&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Visit Instructions:</strong></p>\n<p>Be sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order</p>\n<p>Confirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</p>\n<p><strong>Onsite Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198</p>\n<p>Locate onsite contact and introduce yourself as a technician from IW Technologies.</p>\n<p>Locate parts shipped to location</p>\n<p>Install new parts/equipment utilizing the attached documentation.</p>\n<p>Validate Connectivity and/or Functionality with the store manager.</p>\n<p>You will only call the Premium Brands Help Desk if you need assistance or need help with installing the new pin pad. The help desk can be reached at 740-951-3911 Option 3 then option 2 for On-site Hardware Technicians, give them their internal ticket number&nbsp;(insert ticket number here)</p>\n<p><strong>Clean up Area</strong></p>\n<p>Call IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Check In Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Check Out Time: (local)</p>\n<p>Store Contact Name:</p>\n<p>Help Desk Contact Name (if you call the help desk):</p>\n<p>Description of Issue Observed by Tech Upon Arrival:</p>\n<p>Description of Troubleshooting / Resolution: (concise, bulleted format)</p>\n<p>Parts Installed: Product Name, SN</p>\n<p>Parts Removed: Product Name, SN</p>\n<p>Return Tracking #:</p>\n<p>Return Authorization #:</p>\n<p>Store Check Out Contact:</p>\n<p>Picture of Completed Work:</p>\n<p><strong>Close-Out Tasks:</strong></p>\n<p>Check out on the Field Nation App</p>\n<p>Ensure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables</p>\n<p>Leave defective parts onsite</p>\n<p>Submit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.</p>\n<p><strong>Special Instructions for technician:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>The Register MUST be shut off prior to replacement.</li>\n<li>If you notice the display showing “Form Agent - USB” for more than a minute at any point, to please call the help desk immediately (number is below).</li>\n<li>You must remain on site while the pin pad’s software is being updated, which can take an hour or longer.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>(Include any pertinent information from the case here)</em></p>","markdown":"**Summary of Work:**\n\nIW Technologies is in need of a technician to go onsite at a local clothing retailer and **replace the Register 1 pin pad and input the IP configuration info if needed**. You are to follow the attached documentation to replace the unit, then box up the defective parts using the label provided. Leave defective parts onsite\n\nRegister #:  *1*\n\n**Tech Notes:**\n\n- Call the Service Desk at 740-951-3911, Option 3, upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not begin work without talking to the Service Desk.\n\nTech must power down the register before installation. You must stay on site for pin pad updates to complete, which can take up to an hour. **If the store is needing multiple pin pad replacements, it is important to make sure that you only work on one pin pad at a time.**\n\nCall the Service Desk at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* → Selection option 3 for hardware technician, then press 1 for Chicos, Soma, or White House Black Market or press 2 for all other brands, upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not begin work without talking to the Service Desk.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE: Parts are scheduled to arrive before 4:30pm local time. Be sure to track the parts as not to arrive onsite before they do. We will not compensate for a second trip due to parts not being onsite.**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Physical Drivers License or State Issued ID\n- USB Keyboard\n- USB Mouse\n- Velcro\n- Termination equipment\n- Punchdown equipment\n- Cable tester\n- Variety of Phillips screwdrivers\n- Adhesive removal tools (razor blade, rubbing alcohol, etc)\n\n**Pre-Visit Instructions:**\n\nBe sure to read and understand all of the instructions and download/print all documentation attached to work order\n\nConfirm ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\n**Onsite Tasks:**\n\nCheck in on the Field Nation app and call IW Technologies to check in - 847-285-4198\n\nLocate onsite contact and introduce yourself as a technician from IW Technologies.\n\nLocate parts shipped to location\n\nInstall new parts/equipment utilizing the attached documentation.\n\nValidate Connectivity and/or Functionality with the store manager.\n\nYou will only call the Premium Brands Help Desk if you need assistance or need help with installing the new pin pad. The help desk can be reached at 740-951-3911 Option 3 then option 2 for On-site Hardware Technicians, give them their internal ticket number (insert ticket number here)\n\n**Clean up Area**\n\nCall IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site - 847-285-4198. Be prepared to hand your phone to the store manager so we can verify with the manager that the pin pad is fully functional.\n\nCheck In Time: (local)\n\nCheck Out Time: (local)\n\nStore Contact Name:\n\nHelp Desk Contact Name (if you call the help desk):\n\nDescription of Issue Observed by Tech Upon Arrival:\n\nDescription of Troubleshooting / Resolution: (concise, bulleted format)\n\nParts Installed: Product Name, SN\n\nParts Removed: Product Name, SN\n\nReturn Tracking #:\n\nReturn Authorization #:\n\nStore Check Out Contact:\n\nPicture of Completed Work:\n\n**Close-Out Tasks:**\n\nCheck out on the Field Nation App\n\nEnsure the work order has been completed to specification and upload deliverables\n\nLeave defective parts onsite\n\nSubmit the work order for payment and it will be approved within 24 hours assuming there are no issues.\n\n**Special Instructions for technician:**\n\n1. The Register MUST be shut off prior to replacement.\n2. If you notice the display showing “Form Agent - USB” for more than a minute at any point, to please call the help desk immediately (number is below).\n3. You must remain on site while the pin pad’s software is being updated, which can take an hour or longer.\n\n*(Include any pertinent information from the case here)*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T12:00","end":"2026-11-05T13:30","latestStart":"2026-11-05T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":110},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":11.280311299471906},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793824507267}
{"job":{"id":20309654,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Survey & Trace Wallports, Cary, NC, TASK6317985","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>•\tIssue/Request:</p><p>o\tDispatch a tech onsite to perform a site survey and assess the current state of wall-ports identified to be located on aisle 13</p><p>o\tReach out to [Craig Catala] and/or store leadership to identify Aisle 13 wall-ports locations&nbsp;</p><p>o\tDocument all findings and provide a detailed survey report back to the requesting Support Engineer</p><p>o\tTake photos of each proposed device location</p><p><br></p><p>•\tWork Required:</p><p>o\tInvestigate the wallports connection status.</p><p>o\tIdentify/trace the wall-port to the corresponding switch-port in the network closets (MDF/IDF)</p><p>o\t(if needed/applicable) Re-terminate/replace the RJ45 connector(s) on the cable run and test the connection.</p><p><br></p><p>•\tMaterials Needed:</p><p>o\tCable tracing/testing tools (For Ethernet RJ45 cables)</p><p>o\tRJ45 connectors (Male/Female || keystone jacks and termination patch panel ports)</p><p>o\tCable termination tools (RJ45)</p><p>o\tPPE as required by site (Maintenance gloves etc.)</p><p><br></p><p>•\tSpecial Instructions:</p><p>o\tCoordinate with store leadership for site access. Please confirm with Support Engineer contact upon arrival and after resolution.</p><p>o\tIf re-terminated and/or replaced RJ45 connectors, test and verify with tracing tool. If re-terminating and/or connector replacement doesn't work, Add to task notes that a follow-up visit is required to install new cable on-site</p><p><br></p><p>----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p>WHEN TECH IS ONSITE -- CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS</p><p><br></p><p>•\tStep 1:&nbsp;Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Support Engineer</p><p>o\tName:&nbsp;Mushriq Ali</p><p>o\tPhone # (Call or Text):&nbsp;+15127382861</p><p>(If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation -- Step 2)</p><p><br></p><p>•\tStep 2:&nbsp;Send email to:</p><p>o\tEmail:&nbsp;page-mushriqa@amazon.com</p><p>o\tEmail subject:&nbsp;RE: TASK6317985</p><p>o\tEmail Body:&nbsp;Tech Name and Contact Number</p><p>(If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation -- Step 3)</p><p><br></p><p>•\tStep 3:&nbsp;Reply All to email sent from Step 2 and add the following email address:</p><p>o\tEmail:&nbsp;page-field-infrastructure-support-secondary@amazon.com</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tools Needed:</p><p>Ethernet cable toner and probe</p><p>Network cable tester</p><p>Patch cables</p><p>RJ45 connectors (male)</p><p>RJ45 keystone jacks</p><p>Patch panel termination ports (if required)</p><p>RJ45 crimping tool</p><p>Punch-down tool</p><p>Wire stripper/cutter</p><p>Labeling materials</p><p>PPE (safety gloves, site-required PPE)</p><p><br></p><p>Site Access:</p><p>A valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.</p><p>Communication / Microsoft Teams:</p><p>Technician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.</p><p>Field Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.</p><p>Technician must provide updates for:</p><ul><li>Arrival onsite</li><li>Work started</li><li>Progress, delays, or idle time</li><li>Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns</li><li>Completion status before leaving site</li><li>Checkout/departure from site</li></ul><p>Technician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.</p><p>Time, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:</p><p>Technician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.</p><p>Approved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.</p><p>Unsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p>Assigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:</p><p>The technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.</p><p>Documentation / Deliverables:</p><p>All required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.</p><p>Required deliverables may include:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved</li><li>Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable</li><li>Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions</li><li>Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status</li></ul><p>For cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.</p><p>Incomplete Work / Blockers:</p><p>If work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:</p><ul><li>What was completed</li><li>What could not be completed</li><li>Why it could not be completed</li><li>Troubleshooting performed</li><li>Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker</li><li>Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed</li></ul><p>Professional Standards / Confidentiality:</p><p>Technician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.</p><p>Provider Acknowledgment:</p><p>By applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.</p><p>Missing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Required Completion Items:</p><ul><li>Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.</li><li>Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.</li><li>Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.</li><li>Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.</li><li>Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.</li><li>If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.</li><li>Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.</li><li>Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n• Issue/Request:\n\no Dispatch a tech onsite to perform a site survey and assess the current state of wall-ports identified to be located on aisle 13\n\no Reach out to \\[Craig Catala\\] and/or store leadership to identify Aisle 13 wall-ports locations\n\no Document all findings and provide a detailed survey report back to the requesting Support Engineer\n\no Take photos of each proposed device location\n\n• Work Required:\n\no Investigate the wallports connection status.\n\no Identify/trace the wall-port to the corresponding switch-port in the network closets (MDF/IDF)\n\no (if needed/applicable) Re-terminate/replace the RJ45 connector(s) on the cable run and test the connection.\n\n• Materials Needed:\n\no Cable tracing/testing tools (For Ethernet RJ45 cables)\n\no RJ45 connectors (Male/Female || keystone jacks and termination patch panel ports)\n\no Cable termination tools (RJ45)\n\no PPE as required by site (Maintenance gloves etc.)\n\n• Special Instructions:\n\no Coordinate with store leadership for site access. Please confirm with Support Engineer contact upon arrival and after resolution.\n\no If re-terminated and/or replaced RJ45 connectors, test and verify with tracing tool. If re-terminating and/or connector replacement doesn't work, Add to task notes that a follow-up visit is required to install new cable on-site\n\n\\----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWHEN TECH IS ONSITE -- CONTACT AND ESCALATION PROCESS\n\n• Step 1: Call/Text Amazon/Whole Foods Support Engineer\n\no Name: Mushriq Ali\n\no Phone # (Call or Text): +15127382861\n\n(If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation -- Step 2)\n\n• Step 2: Send email to:\n\no Email: page-mushriqa@amazon.com\n\no Email subject: RE: TASK6317985\n\no Email Body: Tech Name and Contact Number\n\n(If no response after 15 minutes, proceed to escalation -- Step 3)\n\n• Step 3: Reply All to email sent from Step 2 and add the following email address:\n\no Email: page-field-infrastructure-support-secondary@amazon.com\n\nTools Needed:\n\nEthernet cable toner and probe\n\nNetwork cable tester\n\nPatch cables\n\nRJ45 connectors (male)\n\nRJ45 keystone jacks\n\nPatch panel termination ports (if required)\n\nRJ45 crimping tool\n\nPunch-down tool\n\nWire stripper/cutter\n\nLabeling materials\n\nPPE (safety gloves, site-required PPE)\n\nSite Access:\n\nA valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.\n\nCommunication / Microsoft Teams:\n\nTechnician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.\n\nField Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.\n\nTechnician must provide updates for:\n\n- Arrival onsite\n- Work started\n- Progress, delays, or idle time\n- Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns\n- Completion status before leaving site\n- Checkout/departure from site\n\nTechnician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.\n\nTime, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:\n\nTechnician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.\n\nApproved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.\n\nUnsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAssigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:\n\nThe technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.\n\nDocumentation / Deliverables:\n\nAll required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.\n\nRequired deliverables may include:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved\n- Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable\n- Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions\n- Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status\n\nFor cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.\n\nIncomplete Work / Blockers:\n\nIf work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:\n\n- What was completed\n- What could not be completed\n- Why it could not be completed\n- Troubleshooting performed\n- Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker\n- Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed\n\nProfessional Standards / Confidentiality:\n\nTechnician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.\n\nProvider Acknowledgment:\n\nBy applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.\n\nMissing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAdditional Required Completion Items:\n\n- Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.\n- Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.\n- Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.\n- Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.\n- Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.\n- If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.\n- Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.\n- Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":10.120157306140895},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-1