{"job":{"id":20309040,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Fairstead","title":"Towers West Roku Distribution","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work / Tasks</strong></p><p><em>Before residents arrive (9:00 – 10:00 AM)</em></p><p><strong>1. Arrive at 9:00 AM and check in with the property management office. Ask for Rose Creech/Frances Hollingsworth, Property Manager.</strong></p><p><strong>2. Go to the  Community Room. Set up one table and two chairs (one for you, one for the resident).</strong></p><p><strong>3. Pick up the Roku devices. Each box is already assigned and has a unit number written on it in black Sharpie. Ask property management where the devices are stored.</strong></p><p><strong>4. Sort the boxes by unit number so each one is easy to find.</strong></p><p><strong>5. Get the opt-in forms from Valaya Banks. Keep them on the table with a pen and a folder for signed forms.</strong></p><p><strong>6. Check the collateral. The setup instructions, handouts, markers and magnets are in the same box as the devices. Each resident gets a set with their Roku.</strong></p><p><em>When a resident comes to the table (10:00 AM – 5:00 PM)</em></p><p><strong>7. Ask for their unit number (for example, \"I live in unit 103\").</strong></p><p><strong>8. Find the box with that unit number: unit 103 gets the box marked 103. Never hand out a box marked with a different unit.</strong></p><p><strong>9. Have the resident sign the opt-in form before</strong> you hand them anything. Make sure their name, unit number and signature are filled in.</p><p>10. Hand them their Roku box, a set of setup instructions, and a marker and magnet. Let them know the instructions walk them through setup at home.</p><p>11. File the signed form in your folder right away.</p><p><em>End of day (5:00 PM)</em></p><p><strong>12. Count the boxes that weren't picked up and write down their unit numbers.</strong></p><p><strong>13. Bring all signed opt-in forms and your list of unpicked units to Rose Creech/Frances Hollingsworth. Return any leftover devices wherever she tells you.</strong></p><p><strong>14. Break down the table and chairs and leave the room the way you found it.</strong></p><p><em>If something comes up</em></p><ul><li><strong>No box for the resident's unit:</strong> Don't give them a different box. Write down their name and unit number and tell Valaya Banks.</li><li><strong>Markers run out:</strong> Keep handing out magnets and the rest of the collateral.</li><li><strong>Resident won't sign the form:</strong> Don't hand over the device. Tell Valaya Banks.</li><li><strong>Questions about internet, Wi-Fi or Roku setup:</strong> Point them to the setup instructions and LynxNet Support at 1-888-608-9817 or support@lynxnet.co.</li><li><strong>Resident asks you to install it:</strong> Explain that residents set up the Roku themselves and LynxNet Support can help by phone.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables / Closeout Requirements</strong></p><p>&nbsp;Upload these before marking the work order complete:</p><ul><li>Check-in photo of the table set up in the community room (by 10:00 AM).</li><li>Closeout photo of the stack of signed forms being handed to property management. Don't photograph what's written on the forms, since it's residents' personal information.</li><li>Closeout note with:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">number of devices handed out</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">number of devices not picked up, with unit numbers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">any residents with no matching box (name and unit)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">name of the property staff member who received the forms and leftover devices</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Qualifications / Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Professional, friendly manner; neat appearance</li><li>On time: hard 9:00 AM start</li><li>Able to lift and carry boxes of small devices</li><li>Smartphone for Field Nation check-in/out and photos</li><li>No technical skills required</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work / Tasks**\n\n*Before residents arrive (9:00 – 10:00 AM)*\n\n**1. Arrive at 9:00 AM and check in with the property management office. Ask for Rose Creech/Frances Hollingsworth, Property Manager.**\n\n**2. Go to the Community Room. Set up one table and two chairs (one for you, one for the resident).**\n\n**3. Pick up the Roku devices. Each box is already assigned and has a unit number written on it in black Sharpie. Ask property management where the devices are stored.**\n\n**4. Sort the boxes by unit number so each one is easy to find.**\n\n**5. Get the opt-in forms from Valaya Banks. Keep them on the table with a pen and a folder for signed forms.**\n\n**6. Check the collateral. The setup instructions, handouts, markers and magnets are in the same box as the devices. Each resident gets a set with their Roku.**\n\n*When a resident comes to the table (10:00 AM – 5:00 PM)*\n\n**7. Ask for their unit number (for example, \"I live in unit 103\").**\n\n**8. Find the box with that unit number: unit 103 gets the box marked 103. Never hand out a box marked with a different unit.**\n\n**9. Have the resident sign the opt-in form before** you hand them anything. Make sure their name, unit number and signature are filled in.\n\n10\\. Hand them their Roku box, a set of setup instructions, and a marker and magnet. Let them know the instructions walk them through setup at home.\n\n11\\. File the signed form in your folder right away.\n\n*End of day (5:00 PM)*\n\n**12. Count the boxes that weren't picked up and write down their unit numbers.**\n\n**13. Bring all signed opt-in forms and your list of unpicked units to Rose Creech/Frances Hollingsworth. Return any leftover devices wherever she tells you.**\n\n**14. Break down the table and chairs and leave the room the way you found it.**\n\n*If something comes up*\n\n- **No box for the resident's unit:** Don't give them a different box. Write down their name and unit number and tell Valaya Banks.\n- **Markers run out:** Keep handing out magnets and the rest of the collateral.\n- **Resident won't sign the form:** Don't hand over the device. Tell Valaya Banks.\n- **Questions about internet, Wi-Fi or Roku setup:** Point them to the setup instructions and LynxNet Support at 1-888-608-9817 or support@lynxnet.co.\n- **Resident asks you to install it:** Explain that residents set up the Roku themselves and LynxNet Support can help by phone.\n\n**Deliverables / Closeout Requirements**\n\n Upload these before marking the work order complete:\n\n- Check-in photo of the table set up in the community room (by 10:00 AM).\n- Closeout photo of the stack of signed forms being handed to property management. Don't photograph what's written on the forms, since it's residents' personal information.\n- Closeout note with:\n- number of devices handed out\n- number of devices not picked up, with unit numbers\n- any residents with no matching box (name and unit)\n- name of the property staff member who received the forms and leftover devices\n\n**Qualifications / Requirements**\n\n- Professional, friendly manner; neat appearance\n- On time: hard 9:00 AM start\n- Able to lift and carry boxes of small devices\n- Smartphone for Field Nation check-in/out and photos\n- No technical skills required","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T09:00","end":"2026-11-17T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":400},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":58.55704351264414},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 17, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 17, Wed, Nov 18, Thu, Nov 19, Fri, Nov 20 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-1