{"job":{"id":20309026,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Terminate/test 4 cables, install POS at new location and test with customer","description":{"html":"Tech needs to bring: jacks for 4 cables, various size patch cords, surface mount boxes 4 port faceplate white  <br/>***NOTE FROM CUSTOMER REGARDING MATERIALS NEEDED/PATCHING INTO RACK:<br/> Tech bring jacks and patch cords - - They will also need faceplate and surface mount boxes.<br/>       Will the 4 cables run by Flexecution already be terminated to patch panel or direct to switch?  If not, where will tech terminate? - - No, a 12' whip will be left at the patch panel end. Technician will need to feed the cables into the data area and terminate them. They will then connect the new cables into the data switch for connectivity.<br/><br/>For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.<br/>For non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.<br/>Do not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.<br/><br/>Please call Dawn Sherman 603-247-3569 to check in/out and ANY ISSUES.<br/>TECH ONSITE TO:<br/>***IMPORTANT - When you arrive, Please take pictures of the new desk location showing the POS equipment left for you EXACTLY as you find it (before moving/touching anything).  LABEL PICTURES AS ARRIVAL PIC 1, ARRIVAL PIC 2, ETC.<br/><br/> A desk w/full POS has been relocated and 4 cables were run already to new location:<br/>   1. Terminate and test each cable - label the test results total of 4-required deliverable<br/>   2. Install/connect all the POS equipment for the new desk - setup the way the other POS desk is setup<br/>   3. Work with Mattress Firm IT support, 855-234-3755 to confirm POS is fully functioning including, scanner, payment terminal, receipt printer, etc<br/>   4. Get Mattress Firm REP NAME that you test with and who releases you from site<br/>   5.  Take pictures of new POS desk setup (front and back)<br/>   6.  Take pictures of patch panel/switch connections<br/><br/>Provide detailed close out note INCLUDING THE MATTRESS FIRM REP YOU WORKED WITH AND WERE RELEASED BY<br/>Check out with Dawn Sherman, 603-247-3569<br/>Clean site before leaving & take pictures of all areas and email to dsherman@spencertech.com","markdown":"Tech needs to bring: jacks for 4 cables, various size patch cords, surface mount boxes 4 port faceplate white   \n\\*\\*\\*NOTE FROM CUSTOMER REGARDING MATERIALS NEEDED/PATCHING INTO RACK:  \n Tech bring jacks and patch cords - - They will also need faceplate and surface mount boxes.  \n Will the 4 cables run by Flexecution already be terminated to patch panel or direct to switch? If not, where will tech terminate? - - No, a 12' whip will be left at the patch panel end. Technician will need to feed the cables into the data area and terminate them. They will then connect the new cables into the data switch for connectivity.  \n  \nFor all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.  \nFor non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.  \nDo not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.  \n  \nPlease call Dawn Sherman 603-247-3569 to check in/out and ANY ISSUES.  \nTECH ONSITE TO:  \n\\*\\*\\*IMPORTANT - When you arrive, Please take pictures of the new desk location showing the POS equipment left for you EXACTLY as you find it (before moving/touching anything). LABEL PICTURES AS ARRIVAL PIC 1, ARRIVAL PIC 2, ETC.  \n  \n A desk w/full POS has been relocated and 4 cables were run already to new location:  \n 1. Terminate and test each cable - label the test results total of 4-required deliverable  \n 2. Install/connect all the POS equipment for the new desk - setup the way the other POS desk is setup  \n 3. Work with Mattress Firm IT support, 855-234-3755 to confirm POS is fully functioning including, scanner, payment terminal, receipt printer, etc  \n 4. Get Mattress Firm REP NAME that you test with and who releases you from site  \n 5. Take pictures of new POS desk setup (front and back)  \n 6. Take pictures of patch panel/switch connections  \n  \nProvide detailed close out note INCLUDING THE MATTRESS FIRM REP YOU WORKED WITH AND WERE RELEASED BY  \nCheck out with Dawn Sherman, 603-247-3569  \nClean site before leaving &amp; take pictures of all areas and email to dsherman@spencertech.com","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:00","end":"2026-11-06T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":360},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":11.927035666533298},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":360,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1793824585803}
{"job":{"id":20301695,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wireless Essentials","title":"SOW Install Replacement AP's & Reroute Drops To Relocate AP's. Ladder Needed. SEE Service Description for SOW details / Equipment & Material Requirements.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>UPON ASSIGNMENT - REVIEW</strong> Service Description in detail. Contact work order manager with any questions.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>***NO EXCEPTIONS***</strong> YOUR TICKET WILL BE<strong>MOVED TO INCOMPLETE</strong> IF Attached WE SOW Sign Off form is missing ARRIVAL Times IN &amp; OUT / DATE / POC signature !!!</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>SOW:</strong> &nbsp;<strong>Install Replacement AP's &amp; Reroute Drops To Relocate AP's. Ladder Needed</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>FROM SUPPORT:</strong> The site needs to have their access points updated and moved. I've attached a marked floor plan to this ticket. The new access points are already on-site. During installation the technician will need to send me the serial numbers of the new and old equipment. The ceiling height ranges from 8-10 feet, and the distance between new AP location and the old locations is less than fifty feet. They are connected via ethernet</p>\n<p>floor plan attached for reference</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>ARRIVAL and ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call work order manager at <del>************</del> to check in and review SOW.</li>\n<li>Technician is representing <del>******** **********</del> is expected to present and conduct themselves in a professional business manner.</li>\n<li>MUST bring Laptop into facility upon arrival in the event it may be needed for troubleshooting or configuration with onsite network devices.</li>\n<li>At any point technician is unable to reach onsite POC or offsite support. IMMEDIATELY phone work order manager.</li>\n<li>While onsite, DO NOT DISCUSS COSTS with onsite contacts. Technician should instruct them to contact their corporate IT Support department.</li>\n<li>IMMEDIATELY report any escalated issue to work order manager and or provide status update.</li>\n<li>Base on scope of work and notes from Support follow instructions provided to resolve and/or complete the SOW as outlined.</li>\n<li>Enter close out notes and upload required photos contact work order manager to review and be released from site.</li>\n<li>SEE below for PHOTO &amp; DEPARTURE instructions.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PHOTO REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>If applicable, images technician MUST provide BEFORE &amp; AFTER photos of work being performed.</li>\n<li><strong>REVIEW PHOTOS,</strong> before uploading to work order.</li>\n<li>Close up and distance photo images. <strong>BLURRY or POORLY LIT</strong> images will be <strong>REJECTED</strong>, and may require a revisit.</li>\n<li>Any cable management MUST be documented. Images should include BEFORE &amp; AFTER, and should be similar for comparison.</li>\n<li>Labeling must include in focus view of label imprint.</li>\n<li>Based on SOW details, technician should take snapshot of manufacturer information label for any equipment / devices being installed / replaced or repaired. Capture - MFG - Make - Model - Serial #, MAC address, etc.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Return any network equipment back to its original location after work is completed.</li>\n<li>Remove any debris / dust that was created by technician while performing service work. Leaving the immediate and surrounding work area neat and clean.</li>\n<li>Call work order manager <del>*************</del> to review / report the work order and obtain CHECK OUT code to authorize departure from site.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED Equipment &amp; Materials Listed Below</u></strong></p>\n<p>*Lap Top Computer with Windows 10 OS with WiFi, Hot Spot and Screen Share Capability &amp; power supply</p>\n<p>*Fully Charged Hot Spot Device, *Console Cable, *Butt Set, *6' Ladder</p>\n<p>*Cable Tester \\ Toner Wand, *Line Voltage Meter, *Spool / Reel Cat 5e / 6 Cabling</p>\n<p>*RJ 45 Hardware&nbsp;, *Crimp Tool, *Mobile / Cellular Phone - Camera Capability &amp; power supply</p>\n<p>*P-touch or similar Label Device, *Extra roll of label tape, *Basic IT Tool Set</p>\n<p>*Basic Telecom Tool Set</p>","markdown":"**UPON ASSIGNMENT - REVIEW** Service Description in detail. Contact work order manager with any questions.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*NO EXCEPTIONS\\*\\*\\*** YOUR TICKET WILL BE**MOVED TO INCOMPLETE** IF Attached WE SOW Sign Off form is missing ARRIVAL Times IN &amp; OUT / DATE / POC signature !!!\n\n**SOW:** **Install Replacement AP's &amp; Reroute Drops To Relocate AP's. Ladder Needed**\n\n**FROM SUPPORT:** The site needs to have their access points updated and moved. I've attached a marked floor plan to this ticket. The new access points are already on-site. During installation the technician will need to send me the serial numbers of the new and old equipment. The ceiling height ranges from 8-10 feet, and the distance between new AP location and the old locations is less than fifty feet. They are connected via ethernet\n\nfloor plan attached for reference\n\n**ARRIVAL and ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS:**\n\n1. Call work order manager at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check in and review SOW.\n2. Technician is representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* is expected to present and conduct themselves in a professional business manner.\n3. MUST bring Laptop into facility upon arrival in the event it may be needed for troubleshooting or configuration with onsite network devices.\n4. At any point technician is unable to reach onsite POC or offsite support. IMMEDIATELY phone work order manager.\n5. While onsite, DO NOT DISCUSS COSTS with onsite contacts. Technician should instruct them to contact their corporate IT Support department.\n6. IMMEDIATELY report any escalated issue to work order manager and or provide status update.\n7. Base on scope of work and notes from Support follow instructions provided to resolve and/or complete the SOW as outlined.\n8. Enter close out notes and upload required photos contact work order manager to review and be released from site.\n9. SEE below for PHOTO &amp; DEPARTURE instructions.\n\n**PHOTO REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. If applicable, images technician MUST provide BEFORE &amp; AFTER photos of work being performed.\n2. **REVIEW PHOTOS,** before uploading to work order.\n3. Close up and distance photo images. **BLURRY or POORLY LIT** images will be **REJECTED**, and may require a revisit.\n4. Any cable management MUST be documented. Images should include BEFORE &amp; AFTER, and should be similar for comparison.\n5. Labeling must include in focus view of label imprint.\n6. Based on SOW details, technician should take snapshot of manufacturer information label for any equipment / devices being installed / replaced or repaired. Capture - MFG - Make - Model - Serial #, MAC address, etc.\n\n**DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. Return any network equipment back to its original location after work is completed.\n2. Remove any debris / dust that was created by technician while performing service work. Leaving the immediate and surrounding work area neat and clean.\n3. Call work order manager \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to review / report the work order and obtain CHECK OUT code to authorize departure from site.\n\n**REQUIRED Equipment &amp; Materials Listed Below**\n\n\\*Lap Top Computer with Windows 10 OS with WiFi, Hot Spot and Screen Share Capability &amp; power supply\n\n\\*Fully Charged Hot Spot Device, \\*Console Cable, \\*Butt Set, \\*6' Ladder\n\n\\*Cable Tester \\\\ Toner Wand, \\*Line Voltage Meter, \\*Spool / Reel Cat 5e / 6 Cabling\n\n\\*RJ 45 Hardware , \\*Crimp Tool, \\*Mobile / Cellular Phone - Camera Capability &amp; power supply\n\n\\*P-touch or similar Label Device, \\*Extra roll of label tape, \\*Basic IT Tool Set\n\n\\*Basic Telecom Tool Set","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T09:00","end":"2026-11-06T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":12.034337132216997},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (