{"job":{"id":20310381,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Integrated Business Applications","title":"Troubleshoot 11x IP cameras down","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Troubleshoot 11x IP Cameras</strong></p><p>Only an experienced&nbsp;<strong>IP Camera and Networking Technician</strong>&nbsp;is needed to troubleshoot&nbsp;Eleven<strong>&nbsp;(11) offline IP cameras (13-23)</strong>. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving&nbsp;<strong>PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling</strong>.</p><p>Please&nbsp;<strong>do not request this work order</strong>&nbsp;if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.</p><p><strong>Photos are required</strong>&nbsp;before and after troubleshooting, including:</p><ul><li>The manager’s camera view or NVR screen</li><li>Camera model and serial number labels</li><li>Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)</li></ul><p>Thorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Upon arrival, the Technician must&nbsp;<strong>check in with the General Manager</strong>&nbsp;and inform them they are with&nbsp;<strong>IBA</strong>&nbsp;to troubleshoot the offline camera.</p><p>The Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.</p><p>The affected camera will be connected via&nbsp;<strong>CAT5 or CAT6 cabling</strong>&nbsp;to a&nbsp;<strong>PoE switch</strong>&nbsp;located in either the&nbsp;<strong>Main Building</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Shop Building</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Pole-mounted cabinet</strong>.</p><p>Some outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.</p><p>If applicable, a&nbsp;<strong>40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site</strong>&nbsp;for this task.</p><p>Technician must be&nbsp;<strong>trained and authorized to operate a boom lift</strong>&nbsp;— otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.</p><p><strong>Troubleshooting Steps:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Visually inspect</strong>&nbsp;camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.</li><li><strong>Test the PoE connection</strong>&nbsp;using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.</li><li><strong>Check the network link</strong>&nbsp;between the camera and the PoE switch.</li><li>If the camera is offline,&nbsp;<strong>verify link lights</strong>&nbsp;and test the cable for continuity or damage.</li><li>If the camera has been reset to defaults,&nbsp;<strong>reconfigure network settings</strong>&nbsp;with assistance from remote support.</li><li><strong>Confirm camera visibility</strong>&nbsp;on the NVR or management software once restored.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Contact&nbsp;<strong>Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)</strong>&nbsp;for remote configuration support as needed.</p><p>Support may be provided through&nbsp;<strong>TeamViewer</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>AnyDesk</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Quick Assist</strong>&nbsp;as needed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen</li><li>Photo of camera model/serial number label</li><li>Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome</li><li>Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment and Tools:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tall Extension Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(up to 22’ if needed)</li><li><strong>Laptop and Hotspot</strong>&nbsp;(with&nbsp;<em>Advanced IP Scanner</em>&nbsp;installed)</li><li><strong>Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse</strong>&nbsp;(for NVR access if necessary)</li><li><strong>IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE</strong>&nbsp;(NOT an analog tester)</li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li>Standard networking tools and materials:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string</li></ul><p>Technician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.</p>","markdown":"**Troubleshoot 11x IP Cameras**\n\nOnly an experienced **IP Camera and Networking Technician** is needed to troubleshoot Eleven **(11) offline IP cameras (13-23)**. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving **PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling**.\n\nPlease **do not request this work order** if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.\n\n**Photos are required** before and after troubleshooting, including:\n\n- The manager’s camera view or NVR screen\n- Camera model and serial number labels\n- Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)\n\nThorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nUpon arrival, the Technician must **check in with the General Manager** and inform them they are with **IBA** to troubleshoot the offline camera.\n\nThe Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.\n\nThe affected camera will be connected via **CAT5 or CAT6 cabling** to a **PoE switch** located in either the **Main Building**, **Shop Building**, or **Pole-mounted cabinet**.\n\nSome outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.\n\nIf applicable, a **40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site** for this task.\n\nTechnician must be **trained and authorized to operate a boom lift** — otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps:**\n\n1. **Visually inspect** camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.\n2. **Test the PoE connection** using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.\n3. **Check the network link** between the camera and the PoE switch.\n4. If the camera is offline, **verify link lights** and test the cable for continuity or damage.\n5. If the camera has been reset to defaults, **reconfigure network settings** with assistance from remote support.\n6. **Confirm camera visibility** on the NVR or management software once restored.\n\nContact **Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)** or **Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)** for remote configuration support as needed.\n\nSupport may be provided through **TeamViewer**, **AnyDesk**, or **Quick Assist** as needed.\n\n**Documentation Requirements:**\n\n- Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen\n- Photo of camera model/serial number label\n- Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome\n- Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit\n\n**Required Equipment and Tools:**\n\n- **Tall Extension Ladder** (up to 22’ if needed)\n- **Laptop and Hotspot** (with *Advanced IP Scanner* installed)\n- **Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse** (for NVR access if necessary)\n- **IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE** (NOT an analog tester)\n- **Cable Tester**\n- Standard networking tools and materials:\n- RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools\n- Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string\n\nTechnician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T10:00","end":"2026-11-13T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35.855380883247484},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlo