{"job":{"id":20310708,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LTC Technologies","title":"Alamance Health Care Center| CONNECT ISPS AND WIRE RUN","description":{"html":"<p>Please call Wayne at 516-450-5988 upon arrival to check-in. Ask for Director of Maintenance to gain access. This request is being managed on behalf of heir IT company.</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Summary of Tasks</strong></p><p><strong>Equipment Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Technician must bring a laptop with a GIG Ethernet port for testing. preferably we advise not to use adapters, but if use , make sure this supports 1000 connections.</strong></li><li><strong>bring a 5 port switch that support gig connection</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>Circuit &amp; Equipment Setup</strong></p><p>A fiber circuit has been installed at this location. Tasks include:</p><ul><li>Testing the circuit (details are confidential).</li><li>Connecting the voice equipment/router and the firewall.</li><li>Tech to work with wayne</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>Steps</strong></p><p><strong>Locate the Managed Router</strong></p><ul><li>A router/switch has been shipped and delivered to the site. Please request the package as it will be used to connect to the new circuit<strong>.</strong></li><li>&nbsp;<strong>Locate Equipment</strong></li><li>Find the new circuit equipment.</li><li>Locate the firewall.</li><li>Locate the voice equipment (typically an ADTRAN 900 series)</li><li>Identify the handoff device (take photos and note make/model).</li></ul><p><strong>Initial Setup</strong></p><ul><li>Power and mount/place the managed router from the package shipped to the site.</li><li>Use a laptop to connect to the router.</li><li>Configure the device using the provided (confidential) IP information.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>Testing connections</strong></p><ul><li>Verify all connections.</li><li>Take a photo/screenshot of the speed test results and shared with the Work Order Manager Ernie</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong>Connection Details</strong></p><ul><li>Work order manager will provide ports to connect to during the call</li><li>Run a cable from the handoff/managed router to the firewall.</li><li>Run a cable from the handoff/managed router to the voice equipment.</li><li>Wire run IS indispensable to connecte devices, If wire run is unable to be completed withtin timeframe additional time will be added ultil completed. our intention is to complete run on same WO however this can be scheduled to be completed on same WO&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Final Confirmation</strong></p><ul><li>Once connected, work order manager Wayne will contact IT and the voice provider to confirm a successful connection.</li></ul><p><strong>Wire Run(s) Considerations:</strong></p><ul><li>Based on the location of all the equipment, an ethernet wire run or 2 will be required to achieve the desire connectivity.</li><li>we intend to get this connected on the same day. Please bring materials to be ready.</li><li>Materials and extra time will be added to the work order.</li><li>Wire run materials will be listed as expenses on the work order\\</li></ul><p><strong>Equipment Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Technician must bring a laptop with a GIG Ethernet port for testing. preferably we advise not to use adapters, but if use , make sure this supports 1000 connections.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Please call Wayne at 516-450-5988 upon arrival to check-in. Ask for Director of Maintenance to gain access. This request is being managed on behalf of heir IT company.\n\n **Summary of Tasks**\n\n**Equipment Requirements**\n\n- **Technician must bring a laptop with a GIG Ethernet port for testing. preferably we advise not to use adapters, but if use , make sure this supports 1000 connections.**\n- **bring a 5 port switch that support gig connection**\n\n **Circuit &amp; Equipment Setup**\n\nA fiber circuit has been installed at this location. Tasks include:\n\n- Testing the circuit (details are confidential).\n- Connecting the voice equipment/router and the firewall.\n- Tech to work with wayne\n\n **Steps**\n\n**Locate the Managed Router**\n\n- A router/switch has been shipped and delivered to the site. Please request the package as it will be used to connect to the new circuit**.**\n- **Locate Equipment**\n- Find the new circuit equipment.\n- Locate the firewall.\n- Locate the voice equipment (typically an ADTRAN 900 series)\n- Identify the handoff device (take photos and note make/model).\n\n**Initial Setup**\n\n- Power and mount/place the managed router from the package shipped to the site.\n- Use a laptop to connect to the router.\n- Configure the device using the provided (confidential) IP information.\n\n **Testing connections**\n\n- Verify all connections.\n- Take a photo/screenshot of the speed test results and shared with the Work Order Manager Ernie\n\n **Connection Details**\n\n- Work order manager will provide ports to connect to during the call\n- Run a cable from the handoff/managed router to the firewall.\n- Run a cable from the handoff/managed router to the voice equipment.\n- Wire run IS indispensable to connecte devices, If wire run is unable to be completed withtin timeframe additional time will be added ultil completed. our intention is to complete run on same WO however this can be scheduled to be completed on same WO\n\n**Final Confirmation**\n\n- Once connected, work order manager Wayne will contact IT and the voice provider to confirm a successful connection.\n\n**Wire Run(s) Considerations:**\n\n- Based on the location of all the equipment, an ethernet wire run or 2 will be required to achieve the desire connectivity.\n- we intend to get this connected on the same day. Please bring materials to be ready.\n- Materials and extra time will be added to the work order.\n- Wire run materials will be listed as expenses on the work order\\\\\n\n**Equipment Requirements**\n\n- Technician must bring a laptop with a GIG Ethernet port for testing. preferably we advise not to use adapters, but if use , make sure this supports 1000 connections.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T11:00","end":"2026-11-11T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":180,"max":180},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":39.89204325938693},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher Scientific | WAN Activations Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026