{"job":{"id":20311000,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Install Automated Package Locker System - REVISIT","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Automated Locker Installation/Parcel Lockers</strong></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Full Work Description</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Install Revisit - Please have tech on 10/26 to work with site about internet - tech might have to de install locker so site can access behind the locker for data access - have tech be ready and prepaid to TS locker issues to bring locker online - tech might have to stay longer than usual to make sure locker are online or the issue is from site side </span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>To ensure a successful install, entire work order MUST be read and understood.&nbsp;Technician is representing ASR Services and should be referred to as an ASR installer of Parcel Pending Lockers.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please note: Parcel Pending will be sending a post install survey regarding the overall install and tech performance.&nbsp;Please be mindful of this.</strong></p><p><u>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to scheduled start time and before techs arrival onsite.</u></p><p><strong>Overview:&nbsp;</strong>This work order is to install an automated package holding lockers in a luxury apartment complex or other commercial property. Location may still be under construction so please be sure to have the required safety gear (Hard Hat, long pants, Safety Vest and Steel toed boots) as you may not be permitted onsite.</p><p><strong>Background</strong>:&nbsp;Parcel Pending provides automated locker systems that hold packages delivered by couriers (Fedex/UPS/USPS) in a secure location until resident/recipient is available to retrieve.&nbsp;These locations include but are not limited to luxury apartment complexes, student housing and office complexes. ASR Services is the installation and onsite service partner of Parcel Pending.</p><p><strong>FLOORS, WALLS &amp; PROPERTY DAMAGE REPORTING-&nbsp;</strong>Please note that these properties may have extremely expensive flooring and custom wall finish.&nbsp;We need to ensure that YOU as a technician are extremely mindful of the care and protection of the flooring, walls and property itself.</p><p><strong>FAILURE TO NOTIFY ASR ANY PRE-EXISITING DAMAGE TO FLOOR, WALLS or PROPERTY ITSELF COULD/WILL RESULT IN TECHNICIAN BEING HELD LIABLE.</strong></p><p><strong>Installing technician is required to Inspect locker installation location.</strong></p><ul><li>Take photos of area where lockers are to be installed to document any pre-existing flaws/damages to floors, walls or property itself.&nbsp;Send to&nbsp;parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com&nbsp;(this will release you of any liability)</li><li>If there is notable damage to install site&nbsp;NOTIFY ASR ASAP!!</li></ul><p><strong>IF ASR is not notified prior to install, tech WILL/COULD be held liable</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>***OUR CUSTOMER IS PROVIDING A WHITE GLOVE DELIVERY SERVICE***</u></strong></p><p><strong>Delivery is WHITE GLOVE SERVICE and delivery team is REQUIRED to have the following:</strong></p><ul><li>2 man delivery team</li><li>Arrival to deliver site at 10:00AM</li><li>Truck with lift gate</li><li>Pallet jack (manual or motorized)</li><li>800 lbs capacity appliance hand truck</li><li>Furniture dolly</li><li>Floor protective material (Must be masonite or similar) CARDBOARD is NOT acceptable floor protection.</li></ul><p><strong>For Construction Sites:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Full Brim Hard Hat</li><li>Safety Vest</li><li>Long Pants</li><li>Boots</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TECH MUST PROVIDE THE FOLLOWING IF APPLICABLE:</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If there is damage to the tower (small or large) – take at least two pictures</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate the bar coded serial number (some may not have one) – take at least two pictures</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Notate on Bill of Lading&nbsp;</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Model Number (D13, D12, etc)</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Serial Number (if present)</p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures</p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Email to Parcel Pending Support for review parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will review and notify if the tower can be installed</p><p><strong>In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.</strong></p><p><strong><u>PROPERTY</u></strong></p><p><strong>If the delivery company&nbsp;damages property, technician must complete the following guidelines.</strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Notate on Bill of Lading&nbsp;-Do not let drivers leave without notation on BOL and Sign and take pictures of BOL.</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Type of damage</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Location of damage</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures Do Not let drivers leave without pictures</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Email to Parcel Pending Logistics for review&nbsp;</p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will review and notify the property of the damage</p><p><strong>In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.</strong></p><p>Once lockers are unpacked, take photos of any damages and escalate immediately to ASR Services along with noting on Bill of Lading (BOL) and take photo of BOL.&nbsp;<strong>(The BOL is verification that both delivery team has delivered and the technician has received the lockers with either NO noted damage or damages are documented on BOL).&nbsp;</strong></p><p>After Installation of Lockers, please take photos of floors and walls to ensure tech left site the same way and no damages were made by tech.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>**Do not access the system maintenance screen unless instructed.**</u></strong></p><p>Tech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong><u>We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586, Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:</strong></p><p>Technician must have working knowledge/experience with either mounting a flat screen and/or install and secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls (drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, wood/aluminum siding, clay brick, cinder block or concrete. Tech must have a laptop with HyperTerminal or Putty to be able to SSH into Linux base device through Ethernet connection on laptop.</p><p><strong><u>Important</u></strong></p><p>Please leave Locker key in Box 1.&nbsp;If Property Manager insists on Tech leaving key with them, Tech is instructed to call:</p><p><strong>Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586</strong></p><p><strong>Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong></p><p>If no power onsite, please call ASR support for instructions.</p><p>Work order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR support for further instructions. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form.</p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard Technicians tool kit</li><li>Technician needs to bring a laptop, USB Keyboard and Mouse</li><li>Tape Measure (25' minimum)</li><li>Socket/Ratchet set (7/16” socket, 6mm deep socket and 1/4'’ deep socket needed Standard and Metric)</li><li>Vise grips/locking pliers</li><li>Stud Finder</li><li>Level (24” or longer preferred)</li><li>Rubber Mallet</li><li>Ladder - 4' or higher</li><li>Laptop w/HyperTerminal or Putty TeamViewer&nbsp;and StarTech RS232 driver installed on laptop</li><li>Laptop Charger</li><li>USB Keyboard</li><li>Punchdown Tool for 110 block or Keystone Jack</li><li>6ft Crossover patch cable</li><li>6ft Standard patch cable</li><li>Hammer Drill</li><li>Drill/Driver</li><li>Wood, Metal and Masonry drill bit sets (pre-drill for L brackets)</li><li>#12 or #14 – 1 ½ “ min. length Wood, Metal and concrete screws (to secure “L” Brackets to wall)</li><li>#10 or #12 – ¾ “ length self-tapping screws</li><li>Silicone caulking (for end of self tapping screws)</li><li>22-16 AWG Red Butt Splice Wire Connectors</li><li>Crimper/Stripper tool</li><li>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page (for checking in and out)</li><li>Smart Phone Charger</li><li>Digital Camera (Minimum 5 Megapixels) only needed if you do not have smart phone with camera</li><li>Furniture sliders/gliders (minimum 8 discs)</li><li>Dry cloth/towel and non-abrasive cleaner</li><li>Full Brim Hard Hat</li><li>Safety Vest</li><li>Long Pants</li><li>Boots</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment).&nbsp;Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><strong>Attachments:</strong></p><p><u>0887-INSTALLERDOC-REV3_2.pdf</u>-Print, review and bring to site for the install.</p><p><u>0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2.pdf</u></p><p><u>Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2.pdf</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DIRECTIONS</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong>Upon accepting the work order, update the notes with e-mail address that you can access from your smartphone.</strong></li><li><strong>Install equipment/accessories will be in box that is located in Main tower (unit with display) in locker door below display.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify equipment/accessories box with checklist that is taped to lid of box.</strong></li><li><strong>You will receive an ASR work order with a link to the status update page that you will be required to update during the process.</strong></li><li><strong>Upon arrival, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order to check in.</strong></li><li><strong>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the&nbsp;ASR Technician&nbsp;there to install the locker.</strong></li><li><strong>You will be meeting the \"white glove\" service that will be placing the locker system within 5 feet from the final installation location.</strong></li><li><strong>Take and send photos of any damages and note on BOL before signing and releasing delivery team from site.</strong></li><li><strong>Follow the instructions that are attached to your work order.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Take the required photos outlined in the instructions (Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2)</strong></li><li><strong>Text/email pictures to ASR Support team at parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com before leaving site. ASR Support must approve all pictures before tech can be released from site.</strong></li><li><strong>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</strong></li><li><strong>Get full name of site personnel that key is left with and text/email to ASR support Team member.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out.</strong></li></ol><p>=======================</p><p>CONTACTS</p><p><strong>Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586</strong></p><p><strong>Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong></p><p>Site Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p><strong>Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that.</strong></p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**Automated Locker Installation/Parcel Lockers**\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n***Full Work Description***\n\nInstall Revisit - Please have tech on 10/26 to work with site about internet - tech might have to de install locker so site can access behind the locker for data access - have tech be ready and prepaid to TS locker issues to bring locker online - tech might have to stay longer than usual to make sure locker are online or the issue is from site side\n\n**To ensure a successful install, entire work order MUST be read and understood. Technician is representing ASR Services and should be referred to as an ASR installer of Parcel Pending Lockers.**\n\n**Please note: Parcel Pending will be sending a post install survey regarding the overall install and tech performance. Please be mindful of this.**\n\nThe name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed. Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to scheduled start time and before techs arrival onsite.\n\n**Overview:** This work order is to install an automated package holding lockers in a luxury apartment complex or other commercial property. Location may still be under construction so please be sure to have the required safety gear (Hard Hat, long pants, Safety Vest and Steel toed boots) as you may not be permitted onsite.\n\n**Background**: Parcel Pending provides automated locker systems that hold packages delivered by couriers (Fedex/UPS/USPS) in a secure location until resident/recipient is available to retrieve. These locations include but are not limited to luxury apartment complexes, student housing and office complexes. ASR Services is the installation and onsite service partner of Parcel Pending.\n\n**FLOORS, WALLS &amp; PROPERTY DAMAGE REPORTING-** Please note that these properties may have extremely expensive flooring and custom wall finish. We need to ensure that YOU as a technician are extremely mindful of the care and protection of the flooring, walls and property itself.\n\n**FAILURE TO NOTIFY ASR ANY PRE-EXISITING DAMAGE TO FLOOR, WALLS or PROPERTY ITSELF COULD/WILL RESULT IN TECHNICIAN BEING HELD LIABLE.**\n\n**Installing technician is required to Inspect locker installation location.**\n\n- Take photos of area where lockers are to be installed to document any pre-existing flaws/damages to floors, walls or property itself. Send to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com (this will release you of any liability)\n- If there is notable damage to install site NOTIFY ASR ASAP!!\n\n**IF ASR is not notified prior to install, tech WILL/COULD be held liable**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*OUR CUSTOMER IS PROVIDING A WHITE GLOVE DELIVERY SERVICE\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Delivery is WHITE GLOVE SERVICE and delivery team is REQUIRED to have the following:**\n\n- 2 man delivery team\n- Arrival to deliver site at 10:00AM\n- Truck with lift gate\n- Pallet jack (manual or motorized)\n- 800 lbs capacity appliance hand truck\n- Furniture dolly\n- Floor protective material (Must be masonite or similar) CARDBOARD is NOT acceptable floor protection.\n\n**For Construction Sites:**\n\n- Full Brim Hard Hat\n- Safety Vest\n- Long Pants\n- Boots\n\n**TECH MUST PROVIDE THE FOLLOWING IF APPLICABLE:**\n\n1\\. If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)\n\n2\\. If there is damage to the tower (small or large) – take at least two pictures\n\n3\\. Locate the bar coded serial number (some may not have one) – take at least two pictures\n\n4\\. Notate on Bill of Lading\n\n5\\. Model Number (D13, D12, etc)\n\n6\\. Serial Number (if present)\n\n7\\. After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures\n\n8\\. Email to Parcel Pending Support for review parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com\n\n9\\. We will review and notify if the tower can be installed\n\n**In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.**\n\n**PROPERTY**\n\n**If the delivery company damages property, technician must complete the following guidelines.**\n\n1\\. If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)\n\n2\\. Notate on Bill of Lading -Do not let drivers leave without notation on BOL and Sign and take pictures of BOL.\n\n3\\. Type of damage\n\n4\\. Location of damage\n\n5\\. After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures Do Not let drivers leave without pictures\n\n6\\. Email to Parcel Pending Logistics for review\n\n7\\. We will review and notify the property of the damage\n\n**In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.**\n\nOnce lockers are unpacked, take photos of any damages and escalate immediately to ASR Services along with noting on Bill of Lading (BOL) and take photo of BOL. **(The BOL is verification that both delivery team has delivered and the technician has received the lockers with either NO noted damage or damages are documented on BOL).**\n\nAfter Installation of Lockers, please take photos of floors and walls to ensure tech left site the same way and no damages were made by tech.\n\n**\\*\\*Do not access the system maintenance screen unless instructed.\\*\\***\n\nTech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.\n\n- **We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.**\n- **For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586, Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604**\n\n**READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\nTechnician must have working knowledge/experience with either mounting a flat screen and/or install and secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls (drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, wood/aluminum siding, clay brick, cinder block or concrete. Tech must have a laptop with HyperTerminal or Putty to be able to SSH into Linux base device through Ethernet connection on laptop.\n\n**Important**\n\nPlease leave Locker key in Box 1. If Property Manager insists on Tech leaving key with them, Tech is instructed to call:\n\n**Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586**\n\n**Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604**\n\nIf no power onsite, please call ASR support for instructions.\n\nWork order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR support for further instructions. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form.\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- Standard Technicians tool kit\n- Technician needs to bring a laptop, USB Keyboard and Mouse\n- Tape Measure (25' minimum)\n- Socket/Ratchet set (7/16” socket, 6mm deep socket and 1/4'’ deep socket needed Standard and Metric)\n- Vise grips/locking pliers\n- Stud Finder\n- Level (24” or longer preferred)\n- Rubber Mallet\n- Ladder - 4' or higher\n- Laptop w/HyperTerminal or Putty TeamViewer and StarTech RS232 driver installed on laptop\n- Laptop Charger\n- USB Keyboard\n- Punchdown Tool for 110 block or Keystone Jack\n- 6ft Crossover patch cable\n- 6ft Standard patch cable\n- Hammer Drill\n- Drill/Driver\n- Wood, Metal and Masonry drill bit sets (pre-drill for L brackets)\n- \\#12 or #14 – 1 ½ “ min. length Wood, Metal and concrete screws (to secure “L” Brackets to wall)\n- \\#10 or #12 – ¾ “ length self-tapping screws\n- Silicone caulking (for end of self tapping screws)\n- 22-16 AWG Red Butt Splice Wire Connectors\n- Crimper/Stripper tool\n- Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page (for checking in and out)\n- Smart Phone Charger\n- Digital Camera (Minimum 5 Megapixels) only needed if you do not have smart phone with camera\n- Furniture sliders/gliders (minimum 8 discs)\n- Dry cloth/towel and non-abrasive cleaner\n- Full Brim Hard Hat\n- Safety Vest\n- Long Pants\n- Boots\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachments:**\n\n0887-INSTALLERDOC-REV3\\_2.pdf-Print, review and bring to site for the install.\n\n0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2.pdf\n\nParcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2.pdf\n\n**DIRECTIONS**\n\n1. **Upon accepting the work order, update the notes with e-mail address that you can access from your smartphone.**\n2. **Install equipment/accessories will be in box that is located in Main tower (unit with display) in locker door below display.**\n3. **Verify equipment/accessories box with checklist that is taped to lid of box.**\n4. **You will receive an ASR work order with a link to the status update page that you will be required to update during the process.**\n5. **Upon arrival, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order to check in.**\n6. **Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Technician there to install the locker.**\n7. **You will be meeting the \"white glove\" service that will be placing the locker system within 5 feet from the final installation location.**\n8. **Take and send photos of any damages and note on BOL before signing and releasing delivery team from site.**\n9. **Follow the instructions that are attached to your work order.**\n10. **Take the required photos outlined in the instructions (Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2)**\n11. **Text/email pictures to ASR Support team at parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com before leaving site. ASR Support must approve all pictures before tech can be released from site.**\n12. **Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.**\n13. **Get full name of site personnel that key is left with and text/email to ASR support Team member.**\n14. **Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out.**\n\n=======================\n\nCONTACTS\n\n**Mark Matsumoto 818-903-5586**\n\n**Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604**\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\n**Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that.**\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:00","end":"2026-11-06T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-06T14:15"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":9.45295021414545},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-