/span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Equipment List – Network &amp; Cameras</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Cameras: Minimum of 8 cameras (count may vary by store)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">People Counter: 1 (count may vary by store)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Envysion DVR and switch</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">MX Meraki firewall</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Access Point </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Cradlepoint</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 80, 87); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">ISP equipment or 5G cube</span></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Laptop with power supply (Windows OS or Apple OS with Windows Virtual Machine)</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ethernet Cable</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">USB to serial adapter 9 pin with FTDI chipset (drivers already installed)</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cellphone with full battery and charger</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cisco Console</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">RJ11 Cable</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Putty Application (</span>http://the.earth.li/~sgtatham/putty/latest/x86/putty.exe<span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">)</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Teamviewer Application (</span>http://www.teamviewer.com/en/index.aspx?pid=google.tv.s.us&amp;gclid=CML5u_miybkCFUZyQgodD0UANA</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>Optional Tools Needed:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Buttset or Analog Phone</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">USB 4G cellular connection (or ability to tether cell phone)</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">USB-to-Ethernet Adapter</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Power strip and extension cord</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DSL Filter/Splitter</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tone Generator</span></p>","markdown":"**Windsor Fashions****Breakfix****\\*\\*\\*YOU MUST CALL CIS TO CHECK IN UPON ARRIVAL AND CHECK OUT UPON COMPLETION – 949.297.3575 Option 1\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Call LCON &amp; TCON when you arrive onsite:**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nStore 194 will relocate to a different suite in the mall. We would like to schedule a technician for Monday, November 16, to take down the network, POS, and camera equipment, and then install the network and equipment at the new location's cash wrap. Please send a second AP to this location.\n\nEquipment List – Cash Wrap\n\niPads 10–11 with cases (3)\n\nPOS 10–11 iPads (2)\n\nVoIP phone\n\nManager PC + monitor\n\nBrother printer\n\nInateck scanner\n\nHoneywell scanner\n\nZebra DS2208 scanners (3)\n\nPC video cable\n\nKeyboard &amp; mouse\n\nBluetooth keyboards (3)\n\nNetwork cables (10)\n\nPower strips (2)\n\nPin pad mounts (3)\n\nM400 pin pads with POE adapters (3)\n\nInvue NE360C stands + adapters (3)\n\nInvue Gen 10–11 cases (3)\n\nPS567-US power supplies (3)\n\nEpson receipt printers (3)\n\nAPG cash drawers (3)\n\n16-port Netgear switch\n\nRetevis walkie talkies (6)\n\nEquipment List – Network &amp; Cameras\n\nCameras: Minimum of 8 cameras (count may vary by store)\n\nPeople Counter: 1 (count may vary by store)\n\nEnvysion DVR and switch\n\nMX Meraki firewall\n\nAccess Point\n\nCradlepoint\n\nISP equipment or 5G cube\n\n**Required Tools Needed:**\n\nLaptop with power supply (Windows OS or Apple OS with Windows Virtual Machine)\n\nEthernet Cable\n\nUSB to serial adapter 9 pin with FTDI chipset (drivers already installed)\n\nCellphone with full battery and charger\n\nCisco Console\n\nRJ11 Cable\n\nPutty Application (<http://the.earth.li/~sgtatham/putty/latest/x86/putty.exe>)\n\nTeamviewer Application (http://www.teamviewer.com/en/index.aspx?pid=google.tv.s.us&amp;gclid=CML5u_miybkCFUZyQgodD0UANA\n\n**Optional Tools Needed:**\n\nButtset or Analog Phone\n\nUSB 4G cellular connection (or ability to tether cell phone)\n\nUSB-to-Ethernet Adapter\n\nPower strip and extension cord\n\nDSL Filter/Splitter\n\nTone Generator","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-16T09:00","end":"2026-11-16T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.558136427491954},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793831862482}
