{"job":{"id":20313071,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DecisionPoint Technologies Inc","title":"KKD HW Refresh and AP Swap. Technician will be swapping out old registers and installing the new model. If your work order calls for it, you may replace AP's as well.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Service Description / Check-In/Out Procedure:</strong></p><p>KKD HW Refresh and AP Swaps - You will be swapping out registers and kitchen screens. If your work order calls for it there will be AP swaps as well.</p><p>Devices you will be swapping are below:</p><p>4 Order Terminals - 1 Kitchen Screen - 2 AP</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><p>• Screwdriver Set&nbsp;</p><p>• Allen Wrench Set&nbsp;</p><p>• Torx Bit and Driver Set&nbsp;</p><p>• Cordless Drill (Screw Bits and Drill Bits)&nbsp;</p><p>• Right Angle Ratchet&nbsp;</p><p>• Velcro for cable management&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>• Fish Tape&nbsp;</p><p>• Electrical Tape&nbsp;</p><p>• Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>• Cable tester&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>• Punch down tools&nbsp;</p><p>• Cable crimper/terminator for Cat5/Cat6 cable&nbsp;</p><p>• RJ-45 mod plugs&nbsp;</p><ul><li>• Label Maker&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The person assigned to this work order must be the person performing the work.&nbsp;</p><p>Professionalism is required at all times when on site.&nbsp;Business casual dress;&nbsp;jeans allowed without rips or tears.&nbsp;A collared shirt with no logos is required.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Check-In Procedure:</strong></p><ul><li>If you are unable to be onsite at the requested time, reach out to the Work Order Manager (Text Only).</li><li>When onsite, check in/out with HDS Support Desk: 863-888-0112</li></ul><p>Provide Help Desk with</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Your Name</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Customer and Site number</li><li>Introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty</li><li><strong>By accepting this work order, it is understood the travel time to drop off equipment at UPS is included in the pay rate.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>READ OVER THE ATTACHED INSTALL DOCUMENT TO FAMILIARIZE YOURSELF WITH THE INSTALL PROCESS AND CADENCE.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech will provide the Store number when calling the help desk.</strong></li><li>Technician will get direction and authorization to begin from Help Desk or NCR.</li><li>Once you begin, you will replace ONLY 1 register at a time. You will get this register fully operational or to a point where NCR tells you to proceed to the next one.</li><li>Repeat this process until complete. You will need to work with the store on when it's ok to take something down or restart devices.</li><li><strong>ALL TERMINALS MUST BE SHIPPED BACK WITH BUBBLE WRAP FOR SAFE SHIPPING AND WITH POWER CORD AND POWER BRICK!!!</strong></li><li><strong>Tech is approved to stay until released by the support desk.</strong></li><li><strong><em><u>Check out with the support at</u></em><u>863-888-0112</u><em><u>.</u></em></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>HOURLY SUPPORT CHECK-INS &amp; PHOTO REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Support will check in with the technician every hour for a status update. The technician must be available to provide an update when contacted.</strong></li><li><strong>The assigned technician is required to take photos throughout the work process and submit them tophotos@hdstg.com.</strong></li><li><strong>Photos must document the work being performed and progress throughout the installation, including before, during, and after the work when applicable.</strong></li><li><strong>Photos must be submitted throughout the job, not only at completion.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Check-Out Procedure:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete</strong>&nbsp;Jotform linked in Confidential information.</li><li>Check out with Help Desk to confirm job is complete and you are free to go.</li><li>Enter close out notes with the&nbsp;<strong><u>specific details of the job.</u></strong>&nbsp;Document any suggestions if the problem was not resolved.&nbsp;Include the name of the support representative that you worked with.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Service Description / Check-In/Out Procedure:**\n\nKKD HW Refresh and AP Swaps - You will be swapping out registers and kitchen screens. If your work order calls for it there will be AP swaps as well.\n\nDevices you will be swapping are below:\n\n4 Order Terminals - 1 Kitchen Screen - 2 AP\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n• Screwdriver Set\n\n• Allen Wrench Set\n\n• Torx Bit and Driver Set\n\n• Cordless Drill (Screw Bits and Drill Bits)\n\n• Right Angle Ratchet\n\n• Velcro for cable management\n\n• Fish Tape\n\n• Electrical Tape\n\n• Ladder\n\n• Cable tester\n\n• Punch down tools\n\n• Cable crimper/terminator for Cat5/Cat6 cable\n\n• RJ-45 mod plugs\n\n- • Label Maker\n\nThe person assigned to this work order must be the person performing the work.\n\nProfessionalism is required at all times when on site. Business casual dress; jeans allowed without rips or tears. A collared shirt with no logos is required.\n\n**Check-In Procedure:**\n\n- If you are unable to be onsite at the requested time, reach out to the Work Order Manager (Text Only).\n- When onsite, check in/out with HDS Support Desk: 863-888-0112\n\nProvide Help Desk with\n\n- Your Name\n- Customer and Site number\n- Introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty\n- **By accepting this work order, it is understood the travel time to drop off equipment at UPS is included in the pay rate.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\n- **READ OVER THE ATTACHED INSTALL DOCUMENT TO FAMILIARIZE YOURSELF WITH THE INSTALL PROCESS AND CADENCE.**\n- **Tech will provide the Store number when calling the help desk.**\n- Technician will get direction and authorization to begin from Help Desk or NCR.\n- Once you begin, you will replace ONLY 1 register at a time. You will get this register fully operational or to a point where NCR tells you to proceed to the next one.\n- Repeat this process until complete. You will need to work with the store on when it's ok to take something down or restart devices.\n- **ALL TERMINALS MUST BE SHIPPED BACK WITH BUBBLE WRAP FOR SAFE SHIPPING AND WITH POWER CORD AND POWER BRICK!!!**\n- **Tech is approved to stay until released by the support desk.**\n- ***Check out with the support at*863-888-0112*.***\n\n**HOURLY SUPPORT CHECK-INS &amp; PHOTO REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n- **Support will check in with the technician every hour for a status update. The technician must be available to provide an update when contacted.**\n- **The assigned technician is required to take photos throughout the work process and submit them tophotos@hdstg.com.**\n- **Photos must document the work being performed and progress throughout the installation, including before, during, and after the work when applicable.**\n- **Photos must be submitted throughout the job, not only at completion.**\n\n**Check-Out Procedure:**\n\n- **Complete** Jotform linked in Confidential information.\n- Check out with Help Desk to confirm job is complete and you are free to go.\n- Enter close out notes with the **specific details of the job.** Document any suggestions if the problem was not resolved. Include the name of the support representative that you worked with.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T09:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":390},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":52.72325981671121},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Nov 12, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13, Mon, Nov 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:0