{"job":{"id":20312591,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK | Sheetz 505 | 1895 S FRANKLIN ST|Service Door E - Lock Troubleshoot/Adjustment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Must call Work Order Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>No Parts to be Shipped for this Dispatch</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Standard Tool Set</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Nut Drivers or Socket Set</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Compressed air/Canned Air</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>-Issue: ARK drop door is reporting it is unlocked when the door is closed. The door lock box may need to be adjusted. Site is reporting that the lock does not engage when the drop door is closed. The lock is likely mounted too low for the latch to properly engage. The lock must be adjusted upward.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with WO Manager</li>\n<li><strong>Removal:</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Open service door with key</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Loosen mounting hardware for lock box bracket</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Adjust lockbox lower so the latch lines up properly.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>retighten mounting hardware</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Test with Customer</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Check network signal strength</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call WO Manager to Check out</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>MUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.</p>","markdown":"**Must call Work Order Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**No Parts to be Shipped for this Dispatch**\n\n**-Tools Required:**\n\n**\\_\\_Standard Tool Set**\n\n**\\_\\_Nut Drivers or Socket Set**\n\n**\\_\\_Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth**\n\n**\\_\\_Compressed air/Canned Air**\n\n**-Issue: ARK drop door is reporting it is unlocked when the door is closed. The door lock box may need to be adjusted. Site is reporting that the lock does not engage when the drop door is closed. The lock is likely mounted too low for the latch to properly engage. The lock must be adjusted upward.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n- Check in with WO Manager\n- **Removal:**\n- **Open service door with key**\n- **Loosen mounting hardware for lock box bracket**\n- **Adjust lockbox lower so the latch lines up properly.**\n- **retighten mounting hardware**\n- **Test with Customer**\n- **Check network signal strength**\n- **Call WO Manager to Check out**\n\nMUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T11:00","end":"2026-11-05T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-05T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":115,"max":115},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":13.959915927806517},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 11/5/2026, 11:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T15:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-05T15:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Equipment Install | Priority 3 | 11/05/2026 | Hard Start (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793896428395}
{"job":{"id":20314118,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"Access Point Troubleshooting / Replacement","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong></p><p><strong>To receive full payment for this ticket, you MUST follow all instructions while onsite:</strong>&nbsp;checking in/out with both Wachter and NCR Helpdesk, and input detailed closeout notes.</p><p>If you are unable to agree to these terms, please do not accept this work order. More specific details of how to complete this can be found below.</p><p>Provider must&nbsp;<strong>introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter or NCR Cabling Team</strong>&nbsp;while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.</p><p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p><strong>Purpose:</strong></p><p><strong><u>Troubleshoot 4 offline APs</u></strong></p><p>APUS-1287-<strong>226</strong> d4:20:b0:40:73:23 7.43.156.48</p><p>APUS-1287-<strong>222</strong> d4:20:b0:40:72:d3 7.43.156.195</p><p>APUS-1287-<strong>211</strong> d4:20:b0:40:72:24 7.43.156.64</p><p>APUS-1287-<strong>500 </strong>5c:5b:35:d2:73:e9 7.43.156.19</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Locating the Access Point</strong></p><ul><li>All work orders should include a map with the AP circled in the description of work. If a map is missing, please call in for a copy.</li><li>An AP’s number determines where it’s located in the store:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>800 APs</strong> – on the inside of exterior walls</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>500 APs</strong> – above freezer doors or on the top of the freezer itself</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>200 APs</strong> – somewhere on the store floor, including inside the pharmacy/vision center.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Could be inside the drop ceiling.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>0-99</strong> – front/back floor, such as inside the receiving hallways. Also located inside the Academy’s outbuilding.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">AP 099 will ALWAYS be in the UPC office, somewhere on the network rack.</li><li>If an AP can’t be located…</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">…and there’s ongoing construction in the area, it might have been taken down due to the remodel.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">…and it belongs to a cooler that has since been removed, this AP doesn’t exist anymore at this site.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If neither apply, but you see a cable and/or mounting bracket, take a picture of this spot so we know where to install a replacement.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Quick Determinations</strong></p><ul><li>If an AP has a solid GREEN or BLUE light, this AP might have come back online.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any other colors? Continue troubleshooting.</li><li>AP is full of water? We’ll need to replace it.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Try to get more information on a potential leak, as we’ll need to move the position of the bracket to avoid the second AP from flooding.</li><li>Need a lift to access? Try troubleshooting from the switch first. All tickets should include the switch port information in the description of work.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If both the AP and the switch need a lift to access, ask store management if they’re capable of providing a spotter for their lift. If not, ask when they’d prefer us come back out, and put this information in your job update.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Troubleshooting</strong></p><ul><li>Test the cable. Even if the cable test passes, double check the terminations just to make sure they’re correct, and that the RJ45 clips aren’t damaged.</li><li>If an AP doesn’t have any lights, it isn’t receiving power. It should be brought to the switch and short-cabled to determine if it’s the device or port.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Try other open ports on the switch. Even ports that are quarantined (VLAN 315, configured to not allow network traffic through) will normally provide PoE</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">No lights? Dead AP.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you get lights, the port isn’t configured properly</li><li>If you have lights, reboot the access point by unplugging the cable and leaving it off for at least 30 seconds. Once reconnected, if the lights don’t turn solid green or blue, call helpdesk to determine if the AP is dead.</li><li>If an AP needs to be replaced, try to leave the dead device installed where you found it. This’ll help the next technician locate where the replacement needs to go.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Replacement</strong></p><ul><li>The majority of APs will be in boxes with some sort of ‘Mist’ branding.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">There’s a return label inside of this box. Don’t lose it, as you’ll need it to ship the old AP back.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wachter is able to provide tracking information, and the last name of the person who signed for it.</li><li>If a site is unable to locate the replacement AP, and they’re unable to contact the associate who signed for the package, make sure to get the name of the Manager/Team Lead/Coach who helped you look for it before checking out.</li><li>After opening the box, take a picture of the back of the access point.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For <strong>MIST </strong>APs, we need a picture of the QR code on the bottom right corner.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For <strong>MERAKI</strong> APs, we need a picture of the serial number.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Meraki APs are shaped like curved rectangles rather than squares.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For <strong>CISCO </strong>APs, they don’t have claim codes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">These are square APs that say ‘cisco’ on them. They’re not super common anymore.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Make sure this picture is clear and legible! You don’t want to have to go back up to take another.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload this as under the ‘files’ tab in Field Agent, or email it to <strong><del>***********************</del></strong> before proceeding with the install. This ensures it’ll be ready for helpdesk.</li><li>If the AP was replaced due to water damage, try to determine if there’s a water leak nearby. The mounting location can be shifted a handful of feet to avoid damaging the replacement AP.</li><li>Once the AP has been replaced, call into helpdesk for it to be validated.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you haven’t sent in the picture of the back of the AP, do this before calling in!</li><li><strong>You are responsible for shipping the old AP back. Do not give them to management. Use the box the new one was sent in, and attach the return label before dropping it off at FedEx. These should be sent out as soon as possible.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It’s advisable to take pictures of your drop-off slips in case of return shipping delays.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">AP returns are tracked, and those not shipped out in a timely manner will be noticed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Need assistance?</strong></p><ul><li><del>******* ********* ************* *** *</del> (Mon - Friday, 8 to 10 PM CST)</li><li><del>*** ********* ************</del> (24/7 support)</li><li><br></li></ul><p><strong><u>Approval for extra time</u></strong></p><ul><li>If this takes you more than 2 hours you must call <del>******* ************************** *** *</del>&nbsp;for&nbsp;approval to go over 2 hour</li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT NOTE:**\n\n**To receive full payment for this ticket, you MUST follow all instructions while onsite:** checking in/out with both Wachter and NCR Helpdesk, and input detailed closeout notes.\n\nIf you are unable to agree to these terms, please do not accept this work order. More specific details of how to complete this can be found below.\n\nProvider must **introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter or NCR Cabling Team** while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Purpose:**\n\n**Troubleshoot 4 offline APs**\n\nAPUS-1287-**226** d4:20:b0:40:73:23 7.43.156.48\n\nAPUS-1287-**222** d4:20:b0:40:72:d3 7.43.156.195\n\nAPUS-1287-**211** d4:20:b0:40:72:24 7.43.156.64\n\nAPUS-1287-**500** 5c:5b:35:d2:73:e9 7.43.156.19\n\n**Locating the Access Point**\n\n- All work orders should include a map with the AP circled in the description of work. If a map is missing, please call in for a copy.\n- An AP’s number determines where it’s located in the store:\n- **800 APs** – on the inside of exterior walls\n- **500 APs** – above freezer doors or on the top of the freezer itself\n- **200 APs** – somewhere on the store floor, including inside the pharmacy/vision center.\n- Could be inside the drop ceiling.\n- **0-99** – front/back floor, such as inside the receiving hallways. Also located inside the Academy’s outbuilding.\n- AP 099 will ALWAYS be in the UPC office, somewhere on the network rack.\n- If an AP can’t be located…\n- …and there’s ongoing construction in the area, it might have been taken down due to the remodel.\n- …and it belongs to a cooler that has since been removed, this AP doesn’t exist anymore at this site.\n- If neither apply, but you see a cable and/or mounting bracket, take a picture of this spot so we know where to install a replacement.\n\n**Quick Determinations**\n\n- If an AP has a solid GREEN or BLUE light, this AP might have come back online.\n- Any other colors? Continue troubleshooting.\n- AP is full of water? We’ll need to replace it.\n- Try to get more information on a potential leak, as we’ll need to move the position of the bracket to avoid the second AP from flooding.\n- Need a lift to access? Try troubleshooting from the switch first. All tickets should include the switch port information in the description of work.\n- If both the AP and the switch need a lift to access, ask store management if they’re capable of providing a spotter for their lift. If not, ask when they’d prefer us come back out, and put this information in your job update.\n\n**Troubleshooting**\n\n- Test the cable. Even if the cable test passes, double check the terminations just to make sure they’re correct, and that the RJ45 clips aren’t damaged.\n- If an AP doesn’t have any lights, it isn’t receiving power. It should be brought to the switch and short-cabled to determine if it’s the device or port.\n- Try other open ports on the switch. Even ports that are quarantined (VLAN 315, configured to not allow network traffic through) will normally provide PoE\n- No lights? Dead AP.\n- If you get lights, the port isn’t configured properly\n- If you have lights, reboot the access point by unplugging the cable and leaving it off for at least 30 seconds. Once reconnected, if the lights don’t turn solid green or blue, call helpdesk to determine if the AP is dead.\n- If an AP needs to be replaced, try to leave the dead device installed where you found it. This’ll help the next technician locate where the replacement needs to go.\n\n**Replacement**\n\n- The majority of APs will be in boxes with some sort of ‘Mist’ branding.\n- There’s a return label inside of this box. Don’t lose it, as you’ll need it to ship the old AP back.\n- Wachter is able to provide tracking information, and the last name of the person who signed for it.\n- If a site is unable to locate the replacement AP, and they’re unable to contact the associate who signed for the package, make sure to get the name of the Manager/Team Lead/Coach who helped you look for it before checking out.\n- After opening the box, take a picture of the back of the access point.\n- For **MIST** APs, we need a picture of the QR code on the bottom right corner.\n- For **MERAKI** APs, we need a picture of the serial number.\n- Meraki APs are shaped like curved rectangles rather than squares.\n- For **CISCO** APs, they don’t have claim codes.\n- These are square APs that say ‘cisco’ on them. They’re not super common anymore.\n- Make sure this picture is clear and legible! You don’t want to have to go back up to take another.\n- Upload this as under the ‘files’ tab in Field Agent, or email it to **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** before proceeding with the install. This ensures it’ll be ready for helpdesk.\n- If the AP was replaced due to water damage, try to determine if there’s a water leak nearby. The mounting location can be shifted a handful of feet to avoid damaging the replacement AP.\n- Once the AP has been replaced, call into helpdesk for it to be validated.\n- If you haven’t sent in the picture of the back of the AP, do this before calling in!\n- **You are responsible for shipping the old AP back. Do not give them to management. Use the box the new one was sent in, and attach the return label before dropping it off at FedEx. These should be sent out as soon as possible.**\n- It’s advisable to take pictures of your drop-off slips in case of return shipping delays.\n- AP returns are tracked, and those not shipped out in a timely manner will be noticed.\n\n**Need assistance?**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* (Mon - Friday, 8 to 10 PM CST)\n- \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (24/7 support)\n- \n\n**Approval for extra time**\n\n- If this takes you more than 2 hours you must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* for approval to go over 2 hour","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T10:30","end":"2026-11-05T12:30","latestStart":"2026-11-05T23:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"