{"job":{"id":"1433805912","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"IW to investigate Flexedg hard down |  NOC ticket#: 7126751","description":"<p>Issue: Flexedge offline</p><p><br></p><p>NOC ticket: 7126751</p><p><br></p><p>Verbal Access Code: 858221</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>****USB A to RJ-45 Straight-through console cable is required****</p><p><br></p><p>No matter the problem the site is facing, consoling into the Flexedge is required to ensure no issues in the device itself.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>CPEGRT0000019600</p><p>2047221114</p><p><br></p><p>https://157.96.244.46/routers/CPEGRT0000019600</p><p><br></p><p>WAN IP: 198.18.135.193/31</p><p><br></p><p>LAN IP: 156.70.64.202</p><p>SM: 255.255.255.252</p><p>LAN GW: 156.70.64.201</p><p><br></p><p>Spectrum</p><p>CID: 91.L1XX.017779..CHTR</p><p><br></p><p>Spectrum ticket#: ECT-96163794</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tech must locate Carrier NID for CID: 91.L1XX.017779..CHTR and verify the lights as well as power status.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work: </p><p><br></p><p>1. Tech must check in via Work Market and be ready to start the Scope of Work. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2. Tech must locate Granite Flexedge/Silicom. (Will either have NSOID: CPEGRT0000019600 or S/N: 2047221114</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2a. Tech must power cycle the Flexedge and carrier NID and verify the light status. (Take pictures of the equipment and their lights before and after reboots)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>3. Tech must call Granite TJX NOC Networking @ 844-562-2859, option 1 to work with a rep. If tech is unable to reach NOC team, tech must leave a voicemail requesting a call back. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>3a. Tech must connect laptop directly to the Flexedge LAN port) and have laptop NIC set for DHCP (FortiGate should already be connected to this port so there should be a cable in the port.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**** Port is using DHCP, so Granite NOC will need to clear DHCP bind prior to tech connecting ****</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4. Tech must utilize the same cable and unplug it from WAN 1 on the FortiGate and then plug into laptop.</p><p><br></p><p>4a. If unable to surf, tech must replace patch cable.</p><p><br></p><p>5. If needed Granite NOC rep must remote into tech laptop and verify provisioned speeds from managed router directly connected to LAN port with customer equipment removed either by assigning IP or via DHCP, depending on configuration </p><p><br></p><p>6. Once tech confirmed speeds at the managed router, send results to WorkMarket so they can be reviewed by Granite NOC.</p><p><br></p><p>7. If speeds are poor at managed router, tech must setup console session so NetOps Access rep can review configuration, speed/duplex and check for any errors. </p><p><br></p><p>8. If there is no managed router issue and speeds are still poor take the managed router to the DMARC NID and test again. </p><p><br></p><p>9. If speeds are still poor, iPerf testing must be performed. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>10. If carrier tech is needed for any reason, Granite NOC Rep must schedule carrier tech and obtain approval to release from the TJX NOC. </p><p><br></p><p>11. After work is complete, tech must locate customer equipment and reconnect to the managed router. </p><p><br></p><p>12. Granite NOC rep must confirm connectivity with customer contact TJX NOC at 855-859-2821 Option 1, 1, 2 prior to releasing tech. </p><p><br></p><p>****Approval to release required from customer NOC or from tier 2 tech or higher if customer </p><p><br></p><p>NOC is not available**** </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>13. Tech must clean up, complete close-outs, and check out via Work Market. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Equipment: Laptop with integrated Ethernet port. Laptop must have Windows 7 or higher </p><p><br></p><p>with admin rights and must have all Windows updates installed for security purposes. Laptop must have </p><p><br></p><p>PuTTY and the latest version of TeamViewer installed. Cell phone. Unlimited mobile hotspot. Chargers </p><p><br></p><p>for laptop, hotspot, and cell phone. On-site equipment is a </p><p><br></p><p>Flexedge/Silicom, a ****USB A to RJ-45 Straight-through console cable is required****. Electrical extension cord (25 feet minimum). 6-foot step </p><p><br></p><p>ladder. At least 2 complete Ethernet surface jacks. Ethernet cable tester. Cat5e/cat6 cable (150 feet </p><p><br></p><p>minimum). At least 4 RJ-45 wall jacks and plates </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>****No matter the problem the site is facing, consoling into the Flexedge is required to ensure no issues in the device itself.****</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T13:00","end":"2026-11-05T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":63},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 11/5/2026, 1:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-05T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-05T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-05T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 Granite ticket"},{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:0