{"job":{"id":20315114,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":" Install New Jack Plate & Phone in floral","description":{"html":"<p><strong>*Attention Technicians*</strong></p><p>When requesting this ticket, all potential expenses need to be counted when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:</p><p><strong>Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Any travel request submitted after the work is completed will not be accepted.</u></strong></p><p>* ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ONSITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.*</p><p>* IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED*</p><p>* TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS*</p><p>* TECHS WHO ARE ASSIGNED TO THE TICKET ARE THE ONLY ONES ALLOWED TO DO THE WORK.&nbsp;IF YOU HAVE MULTIPLE TECHS, THE TICKET HAS TO BE ASSIGNED TO THEM.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>﻿TECH PENALTIES -These will result in a deduction from pay:</strong></p><ul><li>Failing to check in or out with TDX Tech when arriving and leaving the site.</li><li>Failure to upload deliverables within 24 hours</li><li>showing up late, or not checking in or out with TDX</li><li>Not completing the scope of work</li><li>It is the expectation that the tech(s) will remain on-site until the job is completed. Do not overschedule yourself.</li><li>Failure to provide a start time can incur a penalty.</li></ul><p><strong>CUSTOMER WORK ORDER NUMBER</strong>: <del>******</del></p><p><strong><u>Check in Process</u></strong></p><ol><li>Call TDX Tech 952-912-9205</li><li>Then call the <del>***** ***** ***** ** ****** ************</del></li><li>Enter the store number when prompted. Customer Store Number: <del>****</del></li><li>After entering the store number, the tech will be connected to a member of the <del>***** *****</del> Provisioning Team</li></ol><p>(Tech will need to give the customer work order number to the MOD when checking in with them at the location)</p><p>Techs will need to check out with the<del> ** ************ ****</del> when the work is completed 405-745-1687 (you'll need to enter the store number once again)</p><p>Once released by the customer, techs are also required to check out with TDX before leaving the site. 952-912-9205</p><p>Failure to do so could result in a delay in payment</p><p><strong>﻿Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Install new Jack plate and phone in floral department</li><li>New phone and plate will be shipped &amp; held by manager until tech arrives</li><li>Tech needs to be familiar with analog phone lines so that testing of cabling can also be done</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>*All photos must be uploaded to this work order for payment approval*</strong></p><p><strong>*If working in the network rack, tech(s) cannot open the door on their own. They'll need the manager key to do so. Photos of the rack are required before, during, and after work is completed to ensure security. Call TDX Tech with questions on this*</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p><strong><em>-TDX Work Order - Attached PDF - NOT Field Nation's</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Cable Tester</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Basic PC Tool Kit</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Basic Cabling Tool Kit</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Butt Set (if doing telco work)</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Patch cables</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Punch Down Tool</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Any other tools needed to resolve</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Digital Camera</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Reliable Vehicle</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Cat 5 and 6 Cable</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-RJ 45 connectors</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-Zip Ties / Cable Ties</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p>The technician must provide all tools and materials required to complete the installation.&nbsp;Materials will be reimbursed.</p><p>If the technician does not have the required skill set, tools, or materials, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site unprepared, they will be asked to leave and will not be paid.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Work Step Description:</strong></p><p>-Check in with TDX Tech at <strong>952-912-9205</strong></p><p>-Check in with the customer's Provisioning Team at See confidential information for phone numbers.</p><p>-Listen to the voicemail and press option 1 to reach Provisioning Team on-call team.</p><p>-Check in with the manager on duty</p><p>-Call Customer support before starting work to review the detailed scope and requested photos</p><p>-Perform the desired scope</p><p>-Test and confirm with customer support prior to leaving the site</p><p>-Clean work area to pre-visit standards</p><p>-Complete the work order with the manager on duty's signature</p><p>-Upload all photos and signed work orders to Field Nation</p><p>-Check out with the TDX help desk</p><p>Upon completion, the work order and pictures must be submitted to your Field Nation ticket within 24 hours to receive payment.</p><p>If the technician does not submit the required deliverables, they will not be paid for the time on site, and penalties will be applied.&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**\\*Attention Technicians\\***\n\nWhen requesting this ticket, all potential expenses need to be counted when requesting this work order﻿. This includes:\n\n**Travel Time | Parking Fees | Hotel | Gas | ETC.**\n\n**Any travel request submitted after the work is completed will not be accepted.**\n\n\\* ANY PARTS PURCHASED BY TECH ONSITE WILL BE REIMBURSED AT THE PRICE SHOWN ON THE RECEIPT.\\*\n\n\\* IF YOU USE YOUR PARTS, YOU ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE THE PARTS PRICE BEFORE YOU DO THE WORK. FAILURE TO DISCLOSE PRICES WILL RESULT IN PARTS NOT BEING COVERED\\*\n\n\\* TDX DOES NOT PAY FIELD NATION FEES ON PARTS\\*\n\n\\* TECHS WHO ARE ASSIGNED TO THE TICKET ARE THE ONLY ONES ALLOWED TO DO THE WORK. IF YOU HAVE MULTIPLE TECHS, THE TICKET HAS TO BE ASSIGNED TO THEM.\n\n**﻿TECH PENALTIES -These will result in a deduction from pay:**\n\n- Failing to check in or out with TDX Tech when arriving and leaving the site.\n- Failure to upload deliverables within 24 hours\n- showing up late, or not checking in or out with TDX\n- Not completing the scope of work\n- It is the expectation that the tech(s) will remain on-site until the job is completed. Do not overschedule yourself.\n- Failure to provide a start time can incur a penalty.\n\n**CUSTOMER WORK ORDER NUMBER**: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check in Process**\n\n1. Call TDX Tech 952-912-9205\n2. Then call the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Enter the store number when prompted. Customer Store Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\n4. After entering the store number, the tech will be connected to a member of the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Provisioning Team\n\n(Tech will need to give the customer work order number to the MOD when checking in with them at the location)\n\nTechs will need to check out with the \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* when the work is completed 405-745-1687 (you'll need to enter the store number once again)\n\nOnce released by the customer, techs are also required to check out with TDX before leaving the site. 952-912-9205\n\nFailure to do so could result in a delay in payment\n\n**﻿Scope:**\n\n- Install new Jack plate and phone in floral department\n- New phone and plate will be shipped &amp; held by manager until tech arrives\n- Tech needs to be familiar with analog phone lines so that testing of cabling can also be done\n\n**\\*All photos must be uploaded to this work order for payment approval\\***\n\n**\\*If working in the network rack, tech(s) cannot open the door on their own. They'll need the manager key to do so. Photos of the rack are required before, during, and after work is completed to ensure security. Call TDX Tech with questions on this\\***\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n***-TDX Work Order - Attached PDF - NOT Field Nation's***\n\n***-Cable Tester***\n\n***-Basic PC Tool Kit***\n\n***-Basic Cabling Tool Kit***\n\n***-Butt Set (if doing telco work)***\n\n***-Patch cables***\n\n***-Punch Down Tool***\n\n***-Any other tools needed to resolve***\n\n***-Digital Camera***\n\n***-Reliable Vehicle***\n\n***-Cat 5 and 6 Cable***\n\n***-RJ 45 connectors***\n\n***-Zip Ties / Cable Ties***\n\nThe technician must provide all tools and materials required to complete the installation. Materials will be reimbursed.\n\nIf the technician does not have the required skill set, tools, or materials, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site unprepared, they will be asked to leave and will not be paid.\n\n**Work Step Description:**\n\n-Check in with TDX Tech at **952-912-9205**\n\n-Check in with the customer's Provisioning Team at See confidential information for phone numbers.\n\n-Listen to the voicemail and press option 1 to reach Provisioning Team on-call team.\n\n-Check in with the manager on duty\n\n-Call Customer support before starting work to review the detailed scope and requested photos\n\n-Perform the desired scope\n\n-Test and confirm with customer support prior to leaving the site\n\n-Clean work area to pre-visit standards\n\n-Complete the work order with the manager on duty's signature\n\n-Upload all photos and signed work orders to Field Nation\n\n-Check out with the TDX help desk\n\nUpon completion, the work order and pictures must be submitted to your Field Nation ticket within 24 hours to receive payment.\n\nIf the technician does not submit the required deliverables, they will not be paid for the time on site, and penalties will be applied.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-05T15:00","end":"2026-11-05T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2