{"job":{"id":20315253,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - AP Down/Test and Replace Cabling","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Please find the below dispatch note:</p><p><br></p><p>Requirement Overview:</p><p>MOD Meagan, and she requested a call between 8-9 AM EST.</p><p>1. Impacted Device: AIR-CAP2702E-B-K9</p><p>2. Location: Food Lion - 1078 Burlington</p><p>3. Issue Summary: AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Need to check the physical connectivity</p><p>4. Troubleshooting Summary (Completed Remotely)</p><p>Observed that AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.</p><p>Sending dispatch to check the physical connectivity</p><p>Needs to get the console access of the AP for the further investigation.</p><p>5. Requirements for Field Technician</p><p>Please ensure the technician is equipped with the following tools and software:</p><p>Laptop with a stable internet connection.</p><p>Putty installed on the laptop for console access.</p><p>Admin access to the laptop.</p><p>Console cable – USB to RJ45 (compatible with Cisco).</p><p>Microsoft Teams installed for remote collaboration.</p><p>Short Ethernet cable, cable tester, and patch cables.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>6. Onsite Action Plan</p><p>Upon arrival at the location, the technician is expected to:</p><p>Connect with the HCL Wireless Team via Microsoft Teams troubleshooting bridge.</p><p>Access the AP via console using Putty if required.</p><p>Provide console access to the Wireless Team.</p><p>Test connectivity using patch cables and cable tester.</p><p>Perform a factory reset if required.</p><p>Note: Please ensure that all actions are coordinated with the HCL Wireless Team during the visit to ensure proper configuration and validation.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Please find the below dispatch note:\n\nRequirement Overview:\n\nMOD Meagan, and she requested a call between 8-9 AM EST.\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: AIR-CAP2702E-B-K9\n\n2\\. Location: Food Lion - 1078 Burlington\n\n3\\. Issue Summary: AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Need to check the physical connectivity\n\n4\\. Troubleshooting Summary (Completed Remotely)\n\nObserved that AP1078-2, AP1078-4, AP1078-6, AP1078-14 is down. Tried to bounce the port, but the AP is still offline.\n\nSending dispatch to check the physical connectivity\n\nNeeds to get the console access of the AP for the further investigation.\n\n5\\. Requirements for Field Technician\n\nPlease ensure the technician is equipped with the following tools and software:\n\nLaptop with a stable internet connection.\n\nPutty installed on the laptop for console access.\n\nAdmin access to the laptop.\n\nConsole cable – USB to RJ45 (compatible with Cisco).\n\nMicrosoft Teams installed for remote collaboration.\n\nShort Ethernet cable, cable tester, and patch cables.\n\n6\\. Onsite Action Plan\n\nUpon arrival at the location, the technician is expected to:\n\nConnect with the HCL Wireless Team via Microsoft Teams troubleshooting bridge.\n\nAccess the AP via console using Putty if required.\n\nProvide console access to the Wireless Team.\n\nTest connectivity using patch cables and cable tester.\n\nPerform a factory reset if required.\n\nNote: Please ensure that all actions are coordinated with the HCL Wireless Team during the visit to ensure proper configuration and validation.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T08:00","end":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":39.5564995301347},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Surve