{"job":{"id":"6617658117","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Endeavor Managed Services","title":"Experienced Alarm Technician Needed - DOLLAR GENERAL","description":"<p><strong><em><u>Pre-Dispatch:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Download and print the SR. The SR will need to be signed by the MOD before leaving site. </strong>&nbsp;Please download all documents from the <strong>Documents </strong>section of this assignment.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please also download the MyESP app and make sure you are able to login. If not, please reach out to fe_engagement@endeavor-ms.com.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Scope of Work:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Monthly Password: Please refer to ISS ticket #</strong></p><p><strong>For troubleshooting: Text ISS support at 1-314-648-2956.</strong></p><p><strong>For closing out: Call ISS support at 1-800-249-0192.</strong></p><p><strong>ISS close code and MOD-signed SR are needed before leaving the site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>PART ORDERED -IKT-N6277 -TRACKING 879746136169 SCHEDULED DELIVERY 11/05/2026 Between 10:00 AM - 2:00 PM</p><p><br></p><p>Special Instructions for Tech:</p><p>SR #: SR04511337</p><p>Closeout Info: Please Text STS HD Phone# - (314) 648-2956 for troubleshooting and/or closing out.</p><p>Technician Note: No Access / Lost Access Billing</p><p>If access is denied or removed after arrival, advise the customer/MOD that the trip may be billed, as long as the technician arrived on time and did not cause or contribute to the access issue. Examples include MOD refusing access, site not allowing work to begin, or customer/MOD requiring the technician to leave before completion. Document the MOD/customer name, arrival time, reason access was denied or removed, and key details in the closing notes.</p><p>Interface Statement of Work (Security/Interactive)</p><p><br></p><p>Any other Open SRs and/or Work Orders – Combine Dispatch Request:</p><p><br></p><p>NONE</p><p><br></p><p>Specific Scheduling Request :&nbsp;</p><p>ANYTIME</p><p><br></p><p>System &amp; Model #:</p><p><br></p><p>VISTA 21 IP</p><p><br></p><p>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :</p><p><br></p><p>Technician to inspect and secure the panel box, verify all wiring is properly landed on the correct terminals, and repair any wiring issues found. Replace the panel lock if defective. Upon completion, return the panel box to its original location, perform local system testing, and review remote panel logs to verify proper operation. No panel box was provided for review as the customer declined a ScreenConnect session.</p><p><br></p><p>IMPORTANT: After resolving the reported issue, perform a brief walk-through and visually inspect the entire system for damage, loose or misaligned devices, obstructions, or other concerns. Document and repair any issues when possible. The WO remains incomplete until this inspection is completed</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Parts Needed:</p><p><br></p><p>IKT-N6277&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Cause :</p><p><br></p><p>Possible Loose or damaged wiring, incorrect terminal connections, defective panel lock, or panel box tampering.</p><p><br></p><p>RMA Form: Complete link &amp; Return Label provided. https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88</p><p><br></p><p>Text with Interface Support:&nbsp;STS: 1-314-648-2956</p><p><br></p><p>Support &amp; Cost Analysis Information Only:&nbsp;</p><p>Name and title of person onsite:</p><p><br></p><p>Roleana Downs</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Was the customer Available, Willing and Able to troubleshoot?</p><p><br></p><p>Yes</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Did the customer request a dispatch instead?</p><p><br></p><p>Yes</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Required Tools and Materials:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>8ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Tone generator and inductive wand</li><li>Cabling tools</li><li>Windows based laptop with ethernet patch cable</li><li>Cisco console cable</li><li>USB to serial adapter</li><li>At least 1000 feet of 22AWG 4 conductor solid core plenum cabling</li><li>At least 1000 feet of 22AWG 4 conductor solid core PVC cabling</li><li>Multiple RJ11 and Rj45 keystones and housings (surface and flush mount)</li><li>Valid picture ID</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Important Reminders</u>:</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Arrive at the specified date and time.</strong></li><li><strong>Log onsite with Endeavor TAC by calling 1-800-493-0016 option 1.</strong></li><li><strong>Work with the ISS Helpdesk to resolve onsite issues.</strong></li><li><strong>If wait time for ISS Helpdesk exceeds 30 minutes, please reach out to Endeavor TAC at 1-800-493-0016 option 3, for next steps.</strong></li><li><strong>You MUST check-out with the ISS Helpdesk and obtain a close code prior to leaving the site.</strong></li><li><strong>If you encounter issues obtaining a close code, call Endeavor TAC at 1-800-493-0016 option 3.</strong></li><li><strong>All items in the Deliverables section must be submitted within 24 hours of the dispatch.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Interface Communications Procedures:</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>1. The support/logoff number is listed in the Contact List box at the top of the install guide.</strong></p><p><strong>2. The troubleshooting support number listed is TEXT ONLY.</strong></p><p><strong>3. You do NOT have to contact Interface to check in when you arrive.</strong></p><p><strong>4. You MUST work to resolve the issue listed on page 2 of your SR prior to contacting support. If you can resolve the issue without support, you would only be required to contact Interface to log off.</strong></p><p><strong>5. You MUST log off with Interface to obtain a closure code for every dispatch.</strong></p><p><strong>6. If required to leave the site to pick up a part for maintenance, proceed as instructed. Call TAC (1-800-493-0016 option 3)</strong> <strong>to inform Endeavor of this request.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Post-Dispatch:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Upon completion of the assignment, do not under any circumstances reach out to, interact with, or contact the end client.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Dress Code Policy:</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Technicians must always present a clean, professional appearance. Technicians are expected to be well-groomed and wear clean clothing, free of holes, tears, or other signs of wear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Shirts</em>:</strong></p><ul><li>Must be a polo shirt, or other collared shirt. T-shirts of any kind are not permitted.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Pants</em>:</strong></p><ul><li>Must be Docker style pants or colored denim.</li><li>Jeans must be clean and professional looking. Jeans with holes, rips or fraying are not permitted.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Commitments &amp; Penalties:</u></em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Assignment Approval:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Mark your assignment as pending approval within 24 hours of the dispatch.</li><li>If you are unable to mark the assignment complete, please add a message with your concern within 24 hours of the dispatch.</li><li>If the assignment is not marked pending approval and no note is posted within the time frames shown, we will mark it as pending approval on your behalf. This will serve as acceptance of the assignment value listed at the time of closure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Bonus Structure:</em></strong></p><ul><li>A 5% bonus will be awarded if all deliverables are submitted, reviewed, and approved via myESP on the dispatch date.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Penalty Structure:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Arrivals over 15 minutes late without notice will incur a 10% penalty.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Deliverables received after you have left the site or the dispatch is closed:</em></strong></p><ul><li>Within 48 hours of your dispatch a penalty of 10% will be assessed.</li><li>Within 72 hours of your dispatch a p