{"job":{"id":20315798,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">Please follow the instructions :-</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">1. Do not leave the site</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">3. Dress Code:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> Business casual attire is required.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">4. Do not discuss the pay rate</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> onsite with the customer or any other employees.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">5. Site Visit Report:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> After completing the visit, you </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">. This is </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">mandatory for work order approval</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Short Description: <strong>Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Hours of Operation: <strong>M-F: 8am-5pm EST.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Description: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Troubleshooting steps:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Connect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Trace the data jack and the Clock is configured</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Device ID:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>IP Address: 10.21.19.30</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Gateway: 10.21.19.1</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Read the instructions before asking for help.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Follow the instructions below only if the setup is required again.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The steps to setup the Kronos is mentioned in the manual book that comes with the Kronos clock</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>4500 to DX Wall Mounting&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver&nbsp;</p><p>Locate the 4500 timeclock</p><p>Locate and unscrew the safety screw</p><p>Disconnect the network cable&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Disconnect the power supply&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Unscrew the 2 screws holding the base of the 4500 clocks</p><p>Mount the DX base – reuse the same holes as the 4500 no need to create a new hole, it will align properly&nbsp;</p><p>Plug the network cable into the DX clock – if it does not power up (These are POE) plug in the power supply (separate box)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Pull the network cable through the hole on the bottom left side of the base&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Add the DX clock to the base and secure the safety screw&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After successfully Factory Reset Time Clock. Follow the PDF Document attached for setting up the Time Clock.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Mandate Action:</p><p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p><p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time</p><p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself/herself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Engineer is required to carry the following Equipment.</p><p>-a working console cable</p><p>-a PC that is pre-configured to use the console cable</p><p>-a PC capable of installing remote control software (Teams, Bomgar, etc.)</p><p>-a spare ethernet cable</p><p>-an internet hotspot</p><p>-Toner and RJ45 tester.</p><p>-A Flathead Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p><p>-T25 Screw Bit.</p><p>-You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver.</p><p>-carry serial adapter along with Console cable</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After the completion of Visit:</p><p>Update the Ticket with Resolution Steps</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Please follow the instructions :-\n\n**1. Do not leave the site** without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.\n\n**2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)**before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n**3. Dress Code:** Business casual attire is required.\n\n**4. Do not discuss the pay rate** onsite with the customer or any other employees.\n\n**5. Site Visit Report:** After completing the visit, you **must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order**. This is **mandatory for work order approval**.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\nShort Description: **Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479**\n\nHours of Operation: **M-F: 8am-5pm EST.**\n\nDescription: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic\n\nTroubleshooting steps:\n\nConnect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.\n\nTrace the data jack and the Clock is configured\n\nAnd make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.\n\nDevice ID:\n\nIP Address: 10.21.19.30\n\nGateway: 10.21.19.1\n\nRead the instructions before asking for help.\n\nFollow the instructions below only if the setup is required again.\n\nThe steps to setup the Kronos is mentioned in the manual book that comes with the Kronos clock\n\n4500 to DX Wall Mounting\n\nYou will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver\n\nLocate the 4500 timeclock\n\nLocate and unscrew the safety screw\n\nDisconnect the network cable\n\nDisconnect the power supply\n\nUnscrew the 2 screws holding the base of the 4500 clocks\n\nMount the DX base – reuse the same holes as the 4500 no need to create a new hole, it will align properly\n\nPlug the network cable into the DX clock – if it does not power up (These are POE) plug in the power supply (separate box)\n\nPull the network cable through the hole on the bottom left side of the base\n\nAdd the DX clock to the base and secure the safety screw\n\nAfter successfully Factory Reset Time Clock. Follow the PDF Document attached for setting up the Time Clock.\n\nMandate Action:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself/herself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support.\n\nEngineer is required to carry the following Equipment.\n\n-a working console cable\n\n-a PC that is pre-configured to use the console cable\n\n-a PC capable of installing remote control software (Teams, Bomgar, etc.)\n\n-a spare ethernet cable\n\n-an internet hotspot\n\n-Toner and RJ45 tester.\n\n-A Flathead Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-T25 Screw Bit.\n\n-You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver.\n\n-carry serial adapter along with Console cable\n\nAfter the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the Ticket with Resolution Steps","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T11:00","end":"2026-11-06T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":50.86643761727229},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":180,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":80,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-05T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 NOC TICKET#7123009  P2 IW FOR 11/5 - FEX TROUBLESHOOTING (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Inst