{"job":{"id":20315862,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p>Please follow the instructions :-</p>\n<p><strong>1. Do not leave the site</strong> without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)</strong>before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.</p>\n<p><strong>3. Dress Code:</strong>Business casual attire is required.</p>\n<p><strong>4. Do not discuss the pay rate</strong> onsite with the customer or any other employees.</p>\n<p><strong>5. Site Visit Report:</strong> After completing the visit, you <strong>must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order</strong>. This is <strong>mandatory for work order approval</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Short Description: <strong>Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 101091</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hours of Operation: <strong>MWF: 7AM-6:30PM EST.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Description: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 101091 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Troubleshooting steps:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Connect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Trace the data jack and the Clock is configured</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Device ID: <strong>903147</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>IP Address:&nbsp;&nbsp;10.24.61.30</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Gateway: 10.24.61.1</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Read the instructions before asking for help.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Follow the instructions below only if the setup is required again.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The steps to setup the Kronos is mentioned in the manual book that comes with the Kronos clock</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>4500 to DX Wall Mounting&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Locate the 4500 timeclock</p>\n<p>Locate and unscrew the safety screw</p>\n<p>Disconnect the network cable&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Disconnect the power supply&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Unscrew the 2 screws holding the base of the 4500 clocks</p>\n<p>Mount the DX base – reuse the same holes as the 4500 no need to create a new hole, it will align properly&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Plug the network cable into the DX clock – if it does not power up (These are POE) plug in the power supply (separate box)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Pull the network cable through the hole on the bottom left side of the base&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Add the DX clock to the base and secure the safety screw&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>After successfully Factory Reset Time Clock. Follow the PDF Document attached for setting up the Time Clock.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Mandate Action:</p>\n<p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p>\n<p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time</p>\n<p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself/herself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Engineer is required to carry the following Equipment.</p>\n<p>-a working console cable</p>\n<p>-a PC that is pre-configured to use the console cable</p>\n<p>-a PC capable of installing remote control software (Teams, Bomgar, etc.)</p>\n<p>-a spare ethernet cable</p>\n<p>-an internet hotspot</p>\n<p>-Toner and RJ45 tester.</p>\n<p>-A Flathead Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p>\n<p>-T25 Screw Bit.</p>\n<p>-You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver.</p>\n<p>-carry serial adapter along with Console cable</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>After the completion of Visit:</p>\n<p>Update the Ticket with Resolution Steps</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"Please follow the instructions :-\n\n**1. Do not leave the site** without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.\n\n**2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)**before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n**3. Dress Code:**Business casual attire is required.\n\n**4. Do not discuss the pay rate** onsite with the customer or any other employees.\n\n**5. Site Visit Report:** After completing the visit, you **must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order**. This is **mandatory for work order approval**.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\nShort Description: **Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 101091**\n\nHours of Operation: **MWF: 7AM-6:30PM EST.**\n\nDescription: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 101091 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic\n\nTroubleshooting steps:\n\nConnect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.\n\nTrace the data jack and the Clock is configured\n\nAnd make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.\n\nDevice ID: **903147**\n\nIP Address: 10.24.61.30\n\nGateway: 10.24.61.1\n\nRead the instructions before asking for help.\n\nFollow the instructions below only if the setup is required again.\n\nThe steps to setup the Kronos is mentioned in the manual book that comes with the Kronos clock\n\n4500 to DX Wall Mounting\n\nYou will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver\n\nLocate the 4500 timeclock\n\nLocate and unscrew the safety screw\n\nDisconnect the network cable\n\nDisconnect the power supply\n\nUnscrew the 2 screws holding the base of the 4500 clocks\n\nMount the DX base – reuse the same holes as the 4500 no need to create a new hole, it will align properly\n\nPlug the network cable into the DX clock – if it does not power up (These are POE) plug in the power supply (separate box)\n\nPull the network cable through the hole on the bottom left side of the base\n\nAdd the DX clock to the base and secure the safety screw\n\nAfter successfully Factory Reset Time Clock. Follow the PDF Document attached for setting up the Time Clock.\n\nMandate Action:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself/herself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support.\n\nEngineer is required to carry the following Equipment.\n\n-a working console cable\n\n-a PC that is pre-configured to use the console cable\n\n-a PC capable of installing remote control software (Teams, Bomgar, etc.)\n\n-a spare ethernet cable\n\n-an internet hotspot\n\n-Toner and RJ45 tester.\n\n-A Flathead Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-T25 Screw Bit.\n\n-You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver.\n\n-carry serial adapter along with Console cable\n\nAfter the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the Ticket with Resolution Steps","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T11:00","end":"2026-11-06T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":411.632854183801},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"DISTANCE_TOO_FAR","rejectDetails":"Reported one-way distance 411.632854183801mi exceeds 100mi limit"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-05T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T01:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 NOC TICKET#7123009  P2 IW FOR 11/5 - FEX TROUBLESHOOTING (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793906953324}
{"job":{"id":20316023,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Dispatch - FIVE BELOW - Five Below- Store #8321 - 3130 Halifax Rd, South Boston, VA 24592","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*******CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! ********</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>DISPATCH REQUEST</p>\n<p>Address:</p>\n<p>3130 Halifax Rd.</p>\n<p>South Boston, VA 24592</p>\n<p>Company Name: Five Below- Store #8321</p>\n<p>Dispatch date/time: Monday- 11/9/26- Tech to arrive by 10am</p>\n<p>Local Contact: Manager on Duty</p>\n<p>**PLEASE NOTE- We already have a AT&amp;T 5G Cradlepoint up at this location and this Comcast circuit will be replacing that here. IMPORTANT TO NOTE: Please make sure that the technician sends back the Cradlepoint to Sangoma**</p>\n<p>We are installing a new 50M/35M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP&gt; Comcast. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit, ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.</p>\n<p>Comcast Circuit IP Info:</p>\n<p><del>****** ** ******* *************</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ** ***** ****************</del></p>\n<p><del>******* ** *************</del></p>\n<p><del>****** **** ***************</del></p>\n<p><del>******* *** ***********</del></p>\n<p><del>********* *** ***********</del></p>\n<p>**PLEASE NOTE- We already have a AT&amp;T 5G Cradlepoint up at this location and this Comcast circuit will be replacing that here. IMPORTANT TO NOTE: Please make sure that the technician sends back the Cradlepoint to Sangoma**</p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<p>• Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************</del></p>\n<p>• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</p>\n<p>• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</p>\n<p>• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of Cat 6, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),<strong>350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools</strong>. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <strong>206-494-6399</strong></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email <strong>turnups@sangoma.com</strong> with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call<strong>206-494-6399</strong>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*CABLE EXTENTION MAY BE NEEDED. PLEASE BRING 350ft of CAT6 and INTERNAL WIRING TOOLS! \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nDISPATCH REQUEST\n\nAddress:\n\n3130 Halifax Rd.\n\nSouth Boston, VA 24592\n\nCompany Name: Five Below- Store #8321\n\nDispatch date/time: Monday- 11/9/26- Tech to arrive by 10am\n\nLocal Contact: Manager on Duty\n\n\\*\\*PLEASE NOTE- We already have a AT&amp;T 5G Cradlepoint up at this location and this Comcast circuit will be replacing that here. IMPORTANT TO NOTE: Please make sure that the technician sends back the Cradlepoint to Sangoma\\*\\*\n\nWe are installing a new 50M/35M Broadband Circuit with 1 Static IP&gt; Comcast. We asked the vendor to install the service into the managers back office, where the customer has a network rack located. Our task will be to locate that circuit, ensure it is extended to the rack and test it for connectivity. Once verified functional, we will need to reach out to the Five Below IT team, to assist them in cutting over the point of sale system and connect the new circuit to their Meraki device onsite.\n\nComcast Circuit IP Info:\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*PLEASE NOTE- We already have a AT&amp;T 5G Cradlepoint up at this location and this Comcast circuit will be replacing that here. IMPORTANT TO NOTE: Please make sure that the technician sends back the Cradlepoint to Sangoma\\*\\*\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n• Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n• Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n\n• Required tools: Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350 ft of Cat 6, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity),**350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools**. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at **206-494-6399**\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message and email **turnups@sangoma.com** with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call**206-494-6399**with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T10:00","end":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.634871867292475},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14