{"job":{"id":20316328,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p>Please follow the instructions :-</p>\n<p><strong>1. Do not leave the site</strong> without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)</strong>before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.</p>\n<p><strong>3. Dress Code:</strong>Business casual attire is required.</p>\n<p><strong>4. Do not discuss the pay rate</strong> onsite with the customer or any other employees.</p>\n<p><strong>5. Site Visit Report:</strong> After completing the visit, you <strong>must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order</strong>. This is <strong>mandatory for work order approval</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Short Description: <strong>Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hours of Operation: <strong>M-F: 8am-5pm EST.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Description: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Troubleshooting steps:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Connect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Trace the data jack and the Clock is configured</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Device ID:&nbsp;<strong>905182</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>IP Address: 10.21.19.30</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Gateway: 10.21.19.1</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Read the instructions before asking for help.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Follow the instructions below only if the setup is required again.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The steps to setup the Kronos is mentioned in the manual book that comes with the Kronos clock</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>4500 to DX Wall Mounting&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Locate the 4500 timeclock</p>\n<p>Locate and unscrew the safety screw</p>\n<p>Disconnect the network cable&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Disconnect the power supply&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Unscrew the 2 screws holding the base of the 4500 clocks</p>\n<p>Mount the DX base – reuse the same holes as the 4500 no need to create a new hole, it will align properly&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Plug the network cable into the DX clock – if it does not power up (These are POE) plug in the power supply (separate box)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Pull the network cable through the hole on the bottom left side of the base&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Add the DX clock to the base and secure the safety screw&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>After successfully Factory Reset Time Clock. Follow the PDF Document attached for setting up the Time Clock.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Mandate Action:</p>\n<p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p>\n<p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time</p>\n<p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself/herself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Engineer is required to carry the following Equipment.</p>\n<p>-a working console cable</p>\n<p>-a PC that is pre-configured to use the console cable</p>\n<p>-a PC capable of installing remote control software (Teams, Bomgar, etc.)</p>\n<p>-a spare ethernet cable</p>\n<p>-an internet hotspot</p>\n<p>-Toner and RJ45 tester.</p>\n<p>-A Flathead Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p>\n<p>-T25 Screw Bit.</p>\n<p>-You will need a Security Bit Kit and Phillips Screwdriver.</p>\n<p>-carry serial adapter along with Console cable</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>After the completion of Visit:</p>\n<p>Update the Ticket with Resolution Steps</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"Please follow the instructions :-\n\n**1. Do not leave the site** without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.\n\n**2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)**before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n**3. Dress Code:**Business casual attire is required.\n\n**4. Do not discuss the pay rate** onsite with the customer or any other employees.\n\n**5. Site Visit Report:** After completing the visit, you **must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order**. This is **mandatory for work order approval**.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\nShort Description: **Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479**\n\nHours of Operation: **M-F: 8am-5pm EST.**\n\nDescription: Time Clock needs to be replaced and connected to the Network for Clinic 105479 And we need to have an access to VNC before the technician leaves the Clinic\n\nTroubleshooting steps:\n\nConnect with the Clinic staff to know where Kronos Clock is.\n\nTrace the data jack and the Clock is configured\n\nAnd make sure there is no connectivity issue on the Clock.\n\nDevice ID: **905182**\n\nIP Address: 10.21.19.30\n\nGateway: 10.21.19.1\n\nRead the instructions before asking for help.\n\nFollow the instructions below only if t