{"job":{"id":20317148,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Troubleshoot Fortinet switch **FIBER TESTER NEEDED**","description":{"html":"<p><strong>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>TECH MUST DIAL INTO THE BRIDGE AS SOON AS THEY ARRIVE ONSITE. THE BRIDGE WILL PROVIDE ALL DIRECTION ON THE SCOPE OF WORK AND HOW THEY WANT EVERYTHING DONE. NOTE: When you initially join the bridge there may not be anyone on the bridge. They will join once you enter the incident # into the chat. That alerts them someone is on the bridge waiting for them.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dial into Bridge:&nbsp;</strong>https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_N2UzODYwZTctYzFiYy00MzhlLThlZDAtNzVkNDY1MjNjY2Rl%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%22d7bf8bae-4d7e-479c-bde4-1103d9e4136c%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%2289d1fb02-ea0d-44b1-a257-c0287a3497e2%22%7d</p>\n<p><strong>Once on bridge</strong>, type Reference number into the bridge chat ( ) - The appropriate support person should join shortly after INC# is entered into chat.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Need a Fiber Technician to check the Fortinet switch in the CNG area as it is having intermittent disconnections. Technician should carry a fiber tester and provide console access if required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</p>\n<p>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fiber Tester</strong></li>\n<li><strong>(1) box of CAT6 Cable</strong></li>\n<li><strong>RJ45's</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Laptop:</strong>&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(8'-10' ladder)</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n***TECH MUST DIAL INTO THE BRIDGE AS SOON AS THEY ARRIVE ONSITE. THE BRIDGE WILL PROVIDE ALL DIRECTION ON THE SCOPE OF WORK AND HOW THEY WANT EVERYTHING DONE. NOTE: When you initially join the bridge there may not be anyone on the bridge. They will join once you enter the incident # into the chat. That alerts them someone is on the bridge waiting for them.***\n\n**Dial into Bridge:** https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_N2UzODYwZTctYzFiYy00MzhlLThlZDAtNzVkNDY1MjNjY2Rl%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%22d7bf8bae-4d7e-479c-bde4-1103d9e4136c%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%2289d1fb02-ea0d-44b1-a257-c0287a3497e2%22%7d\n\n**Once on bridge**, type Reference number into the bridge chat ( ) - The appropriate support person should join shortly after INC# is entered into chat.\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Need a Fiber Technician to check the Fortinet switch in the CNG area as it is having intermittent disconnections. Technician should carry a fiber tester and provide console access if required.\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nPlease ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.\n\nThe technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- **Fiber Tester**\n- **(1) box of CAT6 Cable**\n- **RJ45's**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T10:00","end":"2026-11-06T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":64.40329404410147},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":95,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T2