{"job":{"id":20317276,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Xeal","title":"Xeal Electrical Eval","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Tools Needed</strong></p><ul><li>T-20 security torx bit or screwdriver.</li><li>#2 Phillips bit and screwdriver.</li><li>Multimeter to check voltage at each charger and connection point.&nbsp;</li><li>Torque wrench.</li><li>\"1/4\" screwdriver.</li><li>Infrared thermometer temperature gun and EV for testing(not required but nice to have for testing).</li></ul><p><strong>Upon Arrival:</strong></p><ul><li>If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable.</li><li>Site contact: Ian-+19199357493</li></ul><p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Charger&nbsp;[ 3 and 11</strong> <strong>]</strong></li><li><strong>Serial number [ </strong> HC1C2204134963 and 202308140759<strong>]</strong></li><li><strong>Issue</strong>: <strong>[Drivers are unable to start a session, they can do so through the app but the charger never delivers power ]</strong></li><li><strong>Update firmware on Charger 16 - </strong>202308140408</li><li><strong>Check the electrical panel that is connected to the charger, check wiring. Check for any visible damage to the charger, the pedestal and to the wires.</strong></li><li><strong>Open the charger to make sure all internal components are wired correctly(see attached reference photo), check for loose wires by pushing on any connections, DO NOT PULL ON WIRES.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for loose wires at the junction box or circuit breaker wire connectors, wire nuts and terminal blocks. Check for water or moisture inside junction box or conduit.</strong></li><li><strong>At the breaker, check to confirm that the breakers sit flush in their casing and do not appear uneven. If you notice a loose breaker, please contact the work order manager and attach a photo to the work order.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Torque breaker connections to 25 lbf-in and check voltage.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for any signs of smoke or burnt wires inside the charger, check torque on L1, L2, T1, T2 are secure (25 lbf-in). If loose, torque these screws with a torque wrench until you hear a click sound. STOP AFTER YOUR HEAR THE FIRST \"CLICK\".</strong></li><li><strong>Check for excessive discoloration or burning at both the Xeal connector and Customer Charging Port connections(photo attached). Check for excessive damage to connector plugs and cable.</strong></li><li><strong>Check for corrosion, cleanliness and contamination.</strong></li><li><strong>If possible - check the breaker temperature while the charger is in use.</strong></li></ul><p>Notify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:</p><ul><li>If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)</li><li>If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.</li><li>If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster</li><li>Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete</li></ul><p><strong>Standard Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>It is recommended you bring a cleaning cloth with you as the chargers can get very dirty, and should be wiped down and cords wrapped at each visit.&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Tools Needed**\n\n- T-20 security torx bit or screwdriver.\n- \\#2 Phillips bit and screwdriver.\n- Multimeter to check voltage at each charger and connection point.\n- Torque wrench.\n- \"1/4\" screwdriver.\n- Infrared thermometer temperature gun and EV for testing(not required but nice to have for testing).\n\n**Upon Arrival:**\n\n- If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable.\n- Site contact: Ian-+19199357493\n\n**Scope:**\n\n- **Charger \\[ 3 and 11** **\\]**\n- **Serial number \\[**  HC1C2204134963 and 202308140759**\\]**\n- **Issue**: **\\[Drivers are unable to start a session, they can do so through the app but the charger never delivers power \\]**\n- **Update firmware on Charger 16 -** 202308140408\n- **Check the electrical panel that is connected to the charger, check wiring. Check for any visible damage to the charger, the pedestal and to the wires.**\n- **Open the charger to make sure all internal components are wired correctly(see attached reference photo), check for loose wires by pushing on any connections, DO NOT PULL ON WIRES.**\n- **Check for loose wires at the junction box or circuit breaker wire connectors, wire nuts and terminal blocks. Check for water or moisture inside junction box or conduit.**\n- **At the breaker, check to confirm that the breakers sit flush in their casing and do not appear uneven. If you notice a loose breaker, please contact the work order manager and attach a photo to the work order.**\n- **Torque breaker connections to 25 lbf-in and check voltage.**\n- **Check for any signs of smoke or burnt wires inside the charger, check torque on L1, L2, T1, T2 are secure (25 lbf-in). If loose, torque these screws with a torque wrench until you hear a click sound. STOP AFTER YOUR HEAR THE FIRST \"CLICK\".**\n- **Check for excessive discoloration or burning at both the Xeal connector and Customer Charging Port connections(photo attached). Check for excessive damage to connector plugs and cable.**\n- **Check for corrosion, cleanliness and contamination.**\n- **If possible - check the breaker temperature while the charger is in use.**\n\nNotify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:\n\n- If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)\n- If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.\n- If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster\n- Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete\n\n**Standard Instructions**\n\n- It is recommended you bring a cleaning cloth with you as the chargers can get very dirty, and should be wiped down and cords wrapped at each visit.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":100,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":17.13903577037377},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793914371082}
{"job":{"id":20317427,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Freezer Access Point Validation /AP24","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Weblink Survey: </strong><strong>https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00744601</strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong> AP24</strong></p><p>Note from Client:</p><p> It has been determined that this access point may be installed incorrectly, you are validating the installation.</p><p>Locate the access point on the store map.</p><p>Validate the access point is located inside the freezer.</p><p>Attach the pictures to the webform to show the AP&#39;s current installation for validation per the list below.</p><p>Note: If the access point is not inside the freezer, locate the closest access point, document the exact location, and attach pictures of the actual location.</p><p>Next, confirm Pass or Fail in your closing notes:</p><p>Pass = Access point is installed in the freezer correctly including orientation of the device.</p><p>Fail = Access point is installed outside the freezer and no access point is installed inside the freezer.</p><p>For your closure codes in the Webform use: Hardware - Closed Complete - Device Serviced</p><p>Note: Pictures must be attached to your ticket before closing.</p><p>You need to show:</p><p>The installation of the AP closeup</p><p>The installation of the AP further away to show the location in the freezer (include the freezer fan in the photo).</p><p>The cable connection from the AP to it&#39;s entry point into the freezer.</p><p>Without disconnecting the AP, show the cable is seated properly in the AP as well as a good seal at its entry point into the freezer.</p><p>That the AP is online.</p><p>Tool Requirements</p><p> Phone</p><p> </p><ul><li><strong><u>Site Security Requirements: </u></strong>Photo ID required.</li><li>No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment</li><li>Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.</li><li>Printable ID attached to the work order</li><li>Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>Represent yourself as <del>*******</del> (Do NOT mention Field Nation)</li></ul><p> </p>","markdown":"**Weblink Survey:** **<https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00744601>**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n **AP24**\n\nNote from Client:\n\n It has been determined that this access point may be installed incorrectly, you are validating the installation.\n\nLocate the access point on the store map.\n\nValidate the access point is located inside the freezer.\n\nAttach the pictures to the webform to show the AP's current installation for validation per the list below.\n\nNote: If the access point is not inside the freezer, locate the closest access point, document the exact location, and attach pictures of the actual location.\n\nNext, confirm Pass or Fail in your closing notes:\n\nPass = Access point is installed in the freezer correctly including orientation of the device.\n\nFail = Access point is installed outside the freezer and no access point is installed inside the freezer.\n\nFor your closure codes in the Webform use: Hardware - Closed Complete - Device Serviced\n\nNote: Pictures must be attached to your ticket before closing.\n\nYou need to show:\n\nThe installation of the AP closeup\n\nThe installation of the AP further away to show the location in the freezer (include the freezer fan in the photo).\n\nThe cable connection from the AP to it's entry point into the freezer.\n\nWithout disconnecting the AP, show the cable is seated properly in the AP as well as a good seal at its entry point into the freezer.\n\nThat the AP is online.\n\nTool Requirements\n\n Phone\n\n- **Site Security Requirements:** Photo ID required.\n- No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment\n- Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.\n- Printable ID attached to the work order\n- Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- Represent yourself as \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (Do NOT mention Field Nation)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T14:26","end":"2026-11-06T18:26"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12.067360553354643},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-06T19:26:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T20:26:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-