{"job":{"id":"9249664477","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Starlink Site Survey (MUST HAVE STARLINK EXPERIENCE) (HARD START TIME) (MUST DOWNLOAD APP)","description":"<p><strong><u>(MUST HAVE STARLINK APP DOWNLOADED PRIOR TO DISPATCHING!)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>*Please ensure you have a Valid ID for Site Access.*</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>MetTel TECH APP REQUIRED to complete this dispatch - A link will be sent via text message. If you do not receive the link, visit </strong><a href=\"https://dispatch.bruin.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"><strong>https://dispatch.bruin.com/</strong></a><strong> to manually lookup and start the dispatch.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician will survey to determine site conditions for a future Starlink Dish at a commercial location. If you are accepting this survey, you will also be required to complete the installation.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech needs to meet with POC, (info provided in provisioning form if provided). Tech will start the survey, take pics and DRAW/WRITE on pics. Confirm dish-to-power distance and identify if 75 ft or 150 ft Starlink cable is required for install. Make sure to take the obstruction test and obtain SIGNED CTS sign off sheet. Tech needs to fill out the excel form digitally, if it can't be done onsite, please fill it out and callback as soon as possible. DO NOT LEAVE site until the pics are approved by CTS support and bridge.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Steps:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Determine site's demarc environment and conditions</li><li>Locate proposed location for future Starlink Dish and Router</li><li>Confirm dish-to-power distance to determine if 75 ft or 150 ft Starlink Cable is needed</li><li>Using the Starlink app, determine the best area for signal.&nbsp;(The Starlink needs an unobstructed view of the sky to capture the best signal)</li><li>Determine Roof access/requirements needed to install Starlink Dish</li><li>Collect required information<strong> per Survey Excel Sheet</strong> and collect required photos</li><li><strong>PHOTOS MUST BE NEATLY MARKED UP!</strong></li><li><strong><u>**IF TRAVEL IS REQUIRED FOR THE INSTALL, PLEASE NOTATE THAT ON THE SURVEY**</u></strong></li><li><strong>Confirm deliverables and check out with Support (If not done, job will not be considered complete, and you could jeopardize payment.)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools/Materials:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fully Charged Smartphone w/power cord and Hot Spot</li><li>Starlink App Downloaded on your Phone</li><li>Fully Charged Laptop w/power supply and Console Cable</li><li>8-10ft ladder</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Measuring Tape/Measuring Wheel</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Code of Conduct:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Always maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.</li><li>All conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.</li><li>Personal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.</li><li>Any deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Drug Policy/Dress Code;</u></strong></p><p>Do not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flat rate covers up to two hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid at $40/hr. If tech requires additional amount in overtime OR travel, it MUST be approved beforehand.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>All site aborts and out of scope work MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</em></strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-23T08:45","end":"2026-11-23T12:45"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":41.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-25T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-26T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-26T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-27T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Thanksgiving Day"},{"start":"2026-11-27T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-28T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Blac