{"job":{"id":20317427,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Freezer Access Point Validation /AP24","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Weblink Survey: </strong><strong>https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00744601</strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong> AP24</strong></p><p>Note from Client:</p><p> It has been determined that this access point may be installed incorrectly, you are validating the installation.</p><p>Locate the access point on the store map.</p><p>Validate the access point is located inside the freezer.</p><p>Attach the pictures to the webform to show the AP&#39;s current installation for validation per the list below.</p><p>Note: If the access point is not inside the freezer, locate the closest access point, document the exact location, and attach pictures of the actual location.</p><p>Next, confirm Pass or Fail in your closing notes:</p><p>Pass = Access point is installed in the freezer correctly including orientation of the device.</p><p>Fail = Access point is installed outside the freezer and no access point is installed inside the freezer.</p><p>For your closure codes in the Webform use: Hardware - Closed Complete - Device Serviced</p><p>Note: Pictures must be attached to your ticket before closing.</p><p>You need to show:</p><p>The installation of the AP closeup</p><p>The installation of the AP further away to show the location in the freezer (include the freezer fan in the photo).</p><p>The cable connection from the AP to it&#39;s entry point into the freezer.</p><p>Without disconnecting the AP, show the cable is seated properly in the AP as well as a good seal at its entry point into the freezer.</p><p>That the AP is online.</p><p>Tool Requirements</p><p> Phone</p><p> </p><ul><li><strong><u>Site Security Requirements: </u></strong>Photo ID required.</li><li>No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment</li><li>Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.</li><li>Printable ID attached to the work order</li><li>Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>Represent yourself as <del>*******</del> (Do NOT mention Field Nation)</li></ul><p> </p>","markdown":"**Weblink Survey:** **<https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00744601>**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n **AP24**\n\nNote from Client:\n\n It has been determined that this access point may be installed incorrectly, you are validating the installation.\n\nLocate the access point on the store map.\n\nValidate the access point is located inside the freezer.\n\nAttach the pictures to the webform to show the AP's current installation for validation per the list below.\n\nNote: If the access point is not inside the freezer, locate the closest access point, document the exact location, and attach pictures of the actual location.\n\nNext, confirm Pass or Fail in your closing notes:\n\nPass = Access point is installed in the freezer correctly including orientation of the device.\n\nFail = Access point is installed outside the freezer and no access point is installed inside the freezer.\n\nFor your closure codes in the Webform use: Hardware - Closed Complete - Device Serviced\n\nNote: Pictures must be attached to your ticket before closing.\n\nYou need to show:\n\nThe installation of the AP closeup\n\nThe installation of the AP further away to show the location in the freezer (include the freezer fan in the photo).\n\nThe cable connection from the AP to it's entry point into the freezer.\n\nWithout disconnecting the AP, show the cable is seated properly in the AP as well as a good seal at its entry point into the freezer.\n\nThat the AP is online.\n\nTool Requirements\n\n Phone\n\n- **Site Security Requirements:** Photo ID required.\n- No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment\n- Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.\n- Printable ID attached to the work order\n- Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- Represent yourself as \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (Do NOT mention Field Nation)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T08:00","end":"2026-11-06T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12.067360553354643},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T18:30:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-