{"job":{"id":20318223,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Worldlink Integration Group","title":"Replace Pin pad for register 1 - Tech MUST bring security hex/Allen key set","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:</strong></p><p><strong>- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out</strong></p><p><strong>- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)</strong></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>COMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech MUST call the Worldlink coordinator and Hot Topic/Box Lunch/Torrid Help Desk BEFORE beginning any work. Tech must test the device with the help desk and confirm functionality before checking out with Worldlink and leaving the site</strong></p><p><strong>Worldlink Coordinator: 210-756-8651</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>********* ********* ****** ************ ****** *</del></strong></p><p><strong><u>Tech MUST leave old pin pad on site with the manager NO MATTER WHAT- IF the tech takes the pin pad out of the store they will be held responsible to return it to the store and will not be paid until the pin pad is returned.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools/Materials:</u></strong></p><p>basic tool kit/cabling kit</p><p>cable tester/toner</p><p>Screwdriver set&nbsp;</p><p>Punch-down</p><p>Drill</p><p>Label maker or tags</p><p>Security Hex key/Allen wrench set</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Materials (Provided by Technician - Reimbursed per the policies and procedures if used):-</u></strong></p><p>CAT5e Ethernet cable (100')</p><p>RJ45 connectors&nbsp;</p><p>Patch cables</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p><p>The technician needs to replace the Pinpad on register <strong>(1)</strong>, then reconnect all the necessary connections to ensure both the register and Pinpad are active and online.</p><p>The technician will need to remove the existing pin pad (if present) and install and mount the new pin pad at the designated location.</p><p>The technician must bring all the necessary tools to complete the installation, including a security hex/Allen key set for the pinpads, a cable tester, and an extra patch cable.</p><p>Technicians must check-in/out with the World Link and with the Help Desk and work with them to get the pin pad online and verify the connectivity and pictures. Also, to get the configuration.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Picture:-</strong></p><p>Photo of Register 1 setup before the pinpad is installed (to show original condition).</p><p>Close-up of the pinpad securely mounted or placed in its final position.</p><p>Photo showing the pinpad cables connected to the register or appropriate ports.</p><p>Wide-angle shot showing Register with the pinpad fully installed and setup completed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician must be prepared to test the data run for any shorts, install, repair, replace or re-terminate any cables or connectors as needed.</strong></p><p><strong>The technician MUST work with the help desk&nbsp;level support to troubleshoot/test/repair issue. Helpdesk name MUST be on the sign off sheet and work order will not be approved without a valid name.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables:&nbsp;</u>(Work order will not be approved without these photos)</strong></p><ul><li>Basic work order form, completely filled out and signed by MOD</li><li>Photos of completed work</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p><p><strong>Help Desk Contact(if applicable):&nbsp;&nbsp;(Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p>","markdown":"**WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:**\n\n**- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out**\n\n**- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)**\n\n**IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.**\n\nCOMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.\n\n**Tech MUST call the Worldlink coordinator and Hot Topic/Box Lunch/Torrid Help Desk BEFORE beginning any work. Tech must test the device with the help desk and confirm functionality before checking out with Worldlink and leaving the site**\n\n**Worldlink Coordinator: 210-756-8651**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\***\n\n**Tech MUST leave old pin pad on site with the manager NO MATTER WHAT- IF the tech takes the pin pad out of the store they will be held responsible to return it to the store and will not be paid until the pin pad is returned.**\n\n**Tools/Materials:**\n\nbasic tool kit/cabling kit\n\ncable tester/toner\n\nScrewdriver set\n\nPunch-down\n\nDrill\n\nLabel maker or tags\n\nSecurity Hex key/Allen wrench set\n\n**Materials (Provided by Technician - Reimbursed per the policies and procedures if used):-**\n\nCAT5e Ethernet cable (100')\n\nRJ45 connectors\n\nPatch cables\n\n**SOW:**\n\nThe technician needs to replace the Pinpad on register **(1)**, then reconnect all the necessary connections to ensure both the register and Pinpad are active and online.\n\nThe technician will need to remove the existing pin pad (if present) and install and mount the new pin pad at the designated location.\n\nThe technician must bring all the necessary tools to complete the installation, including a security hex/Allen key set for the pinpads, a cable tester, and an extra patch cable.\n\nTechnicians must check-in/out with the World Link and with the Help Desk and work with them to get the pin pad online and verify the connectivity and pictures. Also, to get the configuration.\n\n**Required Picture:-**\n\nPhoto of Register 1 setup before the pinpad is installed (to show original condition).\n\nClose-up of the pinpad securely mounted or placed in its final position.\n\nPhoto showing the pinpad cables connected to the register or appropriate ports.\n\nWide-angle shot showing Register with the pinpad fully installed and setup completed.\n\n**The technician must be prepared to test the data run for any shorts, install, repair, replace or re-terminate any cables or connectors as needed.**\n\n**The technician MUST work with the help desk level support to troubleshoot/test/repair issue. Helpdesk name MUST be on the sign off sheet and work order will not be approved without a valid name.**\n\n**Deliverables: (Work order will not be approved without these photos)**\n\n- Basic work order form, completely filled out and signed by MOD\n- Photos of completed work\n\n**Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)**\n\n**Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:30","end":"2026-11-09T11:30","latestStart":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":35.13437638329466},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Ne