{"job":{"id":20318417,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"ARK Drop Door E - Lock Troubleshoot/Adjustment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Must call Work Order Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>No Parts to be Shipped for this Dispatch</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Standard Tool Set</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Nut Drivers or Socket Set</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__Compressed air/Canned Air</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>-Issue: ARK drop door is reporting it is unlocked when the door is closed. The door lock box may need to be adjusted. Site is reporting that the lock does not engage when the drop door is closed. The lock is likely mounted too low for the latch to properly engage. The lock must be adjusted upward.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with WO Manager</li>\n<li><strong>Removal:</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Open service door with key</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Loosen mounting hardware for lock box bracket</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Adjust lockbox lower so the latch lines up properly.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>retighten mounting hardware</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Test with Customer</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Check network signal strength</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call WO Manager to Check out</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>MUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.</p>","markdown":"**Must call Work Order Manager to Check in and Check out - not doing so may be subject to pay penalty**\n\n**No Parts to be Shipped for this Dispatch**\n\n**-Tools Required:**\n\n**\\_\\_Standard Tool Set**\n\n**\\_\\_Nut Drivers or Socket Set**\n\n**\\_\\_Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth**\n\n**\\_\\_Compressed air/Canned Air**\n\n**-Issue: ARK drop door is reporting it is unlocked when the door is closed. The door lock box may need to be adjusted. Site is reporting that the lock does not engage when the drop door is closed. The lock is likely mounted too low for the latch to properly engage. The lock must be adjusted upward.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n- Check in with WO Manager\n- **Removal:**\n- **Open service door with key**\n- **Loosen mounting hardware for lock box bracket**\n- **Adjust lockbox lower so the latch lines up properly.**\n- **retighten mounting hardware**\n- **Test with Customer**\n- **Check network signal strength**\n- **Call WO Manager to Check out**\n\nMUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T09:00","end":"2026-11-06T10:00","latestStart":"2026-11-06T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":115,"max":115},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":6.668993773177993},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $115 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:30:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04048455-Humacyte INC-EPIK Survey and Install (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"},{"start":"2026-11-02T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Network Refresh Tech 1"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793926098541}
{"job":{"id":20318488,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Amplifier – Troubleshooting – no hold music and ringing sound on all store phones","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work:</em></p>\n<p><em>IMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 24vDC / 70vAC audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Required Tools:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Wired headphones 3.5mm Wired. MUST HAVE</em></p>\n<p><em>o Alligator clip leads</em></p>\n<p><em>o Toner and probe kit</em></p>\n<p><em>o Self-powered buttset</em></p>\n<p><em>o 66/110 block punch tool - MUST HAVE</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work:</em></p>\n<p><em>Get photos of current audio setup.</em></p>\n<p><em>Check MOH output on amplifier to see if it is plugged into the correct port on the back of the Avaya IP office. (port labeled \"audio\")</em></p>\n<p><em>Make sure level is set for MOH.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room and collect pictures of the following: (Should always be the very first thing you do on every call!)</em></p>\n<p><em>o Plywood in the electrical room.</em></p>\n<p><em>o In electrical room identify all Valcom equipment cabling. (if any)</em></p>\n<p><em>o Rack in the data closet (Front, Back, and side Views).</em></p>\n<p><em>o In data closet, identify any audio equipment.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Volume control switches located throughout the store.</em></p>\n<p><em>o At least 2 different speakers.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>• Objective of visit:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Confirm quality of music coming out of mood media players 3.5mm audio jack.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Document (pictures) of all connections on the Amplifier equipment but do not remove or change any cabling until you have been instructed to and have tagged the connections in the event, they need to be put back.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Verify clean cabling – Twisted pairs, taped pairs, exposed wires should be documented.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Document audio quality – Is it buzzing, is there static, crackling, popping, and where you hear it from location wise.</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>• Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>o using wired headphones, make sure MOH cable is giving audio to IP office.</em></p>\n<p><em>o</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed and photos uploaded to work order, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at <del>*************</del> Option 3, Option 5 for further audio troubleshooting.</em></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: no music on hold</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site?:(y/n) no</em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>If assistance is needed, please call: <del>************ ****** * *</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work:*\n\n*IMPORTANT: This work order requires experience with 24vDC / 70vAC audio systems and analog telecommunications. Do not accept this work order unless you have the required experience and tools.*\n\n*• Required Tools:*\n\n*o Wired headphones 3.5mm Wired. MUST HAVE*\n\n*o Alligator clip leads*\n\n*o Toner and probe kit*\n\n*o Self-powered buttset*\n\n*o 66/110 block punch tool - MUST HAVE*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Scope of Work:*\n\n*Get photos of current audio setup.*\n\n*Check MOH output on amplifier to see if it is plugged into the correct port on the back of the Avaya IP office. (port labeled \"audio\")*\n\n*Make sure level is set for MOH.*\n\n*• Request access to the equipment rack and electrical room and collect pictures of the following: (Should always be the very first thing you do on every call!)*\n\n*o Plywood in the electrical room.*\n\n*o In electrical room identify all Valcom equipment cabling. (if any)*\n\n*o Rack in the data closet (Front, Back, and side Views).*\n\n*o In data closet, identify any audio equipment.*\n\n*o Volume control switches located throughout the store.*\n\n*o At least 2 different speakers.*\n\n*• Objective of visit:*\n\n*o Confirm quality of music coming out of mood media players 3.5mm audio jack.*\n\n*o Document (pictures) of all connections on the Amplifier equipment but do not remove or change any cabling until you have been instructed to and have tagged the connections in the event, they need to be put back.*\n\n*o Verify clean cabling – Twisted pairs, taped pairs, exposed wires should be documented.*\n\n*o Document audio quality – Is it buzzing, is there static, crackling, popping, and where you hear it from location wise.*\n\n*• Other Instructions:*\n\n*o using wired headphones, make sure MOH cable is giving audio to IP office.*\n\n*o*\n\n*• Once all photos and initial checks have been completed and photos uploaded to work order, contact Shyft/AVT technical support at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Option 3, Option 5 for further audio troubleshooting.*\n\n*Site Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Customer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Clients present issue: no music on hold*\n\n*Estimated time: 2 hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site?:(y/n) no*\n\n*Other Instructions:*\n\n*If assistance is needed, please call: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\**\n\n*Required Tool List:*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n***Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.*** *These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only. If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be* ***a detailed and concise statement about the work performed****.****Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.***\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T07:00","end":"2026-11-06T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null