{"job":{"id":20318524,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Troubleshoot Phone Cabling, Raleigh, NC, TASK6318259","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>REMOTE ENGINEER CONTACT INFO:</p><p>Name: Steven Piadade</p><p>Direct Phone: 832-319-4138</p><p>Email: dpiadast@amazon.com</p><p>Pager Email: page-dpiadast@amazon.com</p><p><br></p><p>REQUESTED REPAIR DATE/TIME: Monday, November 9, 2026 at 10:00 AM ET (local)</p><p><br></p><p>Reference: INC16986173</p><p><br></p><p>LOW VOLTAGE / SMART HANDS DISPATCH - Copper cable fault diagnosis and repair</p><p>Site: SO RAL / Raleigh (store 10016)</p><p>Site address: 3540 Wade Ave, Raleigh, NC 27607, USA</p><p>Site phone: (919) 828-5805</p><p>Affected device/port: Grocery sales floor (cereal aisle) desk phone, ext 2111 (Grandstream GXP2170, MAC C074AD38AADA). Switch port unknown - aisle jack is not labeled on any switch.</p><p>Symptom: no dial tone; phone has been offline since 10/02.</p><p>Remote diagnostics already observed:</p><p>- Ext 2111 not registered; last call activity 10/02.</p><p>- Phone MAC not found on any of the 8 store switches; no link from the aisle jack.</p><p><br></p><p>LV technician scope:</p><p>1. Call the remote engineer on arrival.</p><p>2. At the cereal aisle phone: confirm the phone has power, the cable is in the phone's LAN port, and note any error on the screen. Test the phone on a known-working phone jack. Report result, then return it to the aisle jack.</p><p>3. Trace the aisle jack back to the patch panel in the MDF/IDF and confirm whether it is patched to a switch. Report the patch panel port and switch/port.</p><p>4. TDR/Fluke test all four pairs on the aisle jack run and isolate any fault.</p><p>5. Re-terminate the jack and/or patch panel side as needed, and re-test all four pairs.</p><p>6. If the run is not patched: patch it to the switch port provided by the remote engineer.</p><p>7. Label the aisle jack and patch panel port.</p><p>8. Notify the remote engineer once complete so they can confirm link, PoE, and phone registration remotely.</p><p><br></p><p>LV technician restrictions:</p><p>* Do not change switch configuration (VLAN, port settings); the remote engineer will configure the port if needed.</p><p>* Do not move or unplug any other patch cables or devices.</p><p>* Do not power-cycle network equipment.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion / stop criteria:</p><p>* Complete when the aisle phone has link and the remote engineer confirms ext 2111 is registered.</p><p>* If the phone does not work on a known-good jack, stop and report; the phone will be replaced separately.</p><p>* If the run cannot be repaired by re-termination (requires a full re-run), stop and report the TDR results and fault distance to the remote engineer.</p><p><br></p><p>Remote engineer responsibility:</p><p>* Configure the switch port for the aisle jack if needed (SNP inventory), confirm link/PoE and ext 2111 registration, and test calls with the store.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tools Needed:</p><p>Fluke cable tester with TDR capability</p><p>Tone generator and probe</p><p>Punch-down tool</p><p>RJ45 keystone jack(s)</p><p>Cat5e/Cat6 patch cables</p><p>Cable labels and marker</p><p>Wire stripper/cutter</p><p>Flashlight</p><p><br></p><p>Site Access:</p><p>A valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.</p><p>Communication / Microsoft Teams:</p><p>Technician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.</p><p>Field Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.</p><p>Technician must provide updates for:</p><ul><li>Arrival onsite</li><li>Work started</li><li>Progress, delays, or idle time</li><li>Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns</li><li>Completion status before leaving site</li><li>Checkout/departure from site</li></ul><p>Technician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.</p><p>Time, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:</p><p>Technician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.</p><p>Approved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.</p><p>Unsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p>Assigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:</p><p>The technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.</p><p>Documentation / Deliverables:</p><p>All required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.</p><p>Required deliverables may include:</p><ul><li>Before and after photos</li><li>Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved</li><li>Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable</li><li>Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions</li><li>Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status</li></ul><p>For cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.</p><p>Incomplete Work / Blockers:</p><p>If work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:</p><ul><li>What was completed</li><li>What could not be completed</li><li>Why it could not be completed</li><li>Troubleshooting performed</li><li>Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker</li><li>Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed</li></ul><p>Professional Standards / Confidentiality:</p><p>Technician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.</p><p>Provider Acknowledgment:</p><p>By applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.</p><p>Missing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Additional Required Completion Items:</p><ul><li>Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.</li><li>Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.</li><li>Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.</li><li>Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.</li><li>Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.</li><li>If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.</li><li>Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.</li><li>Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nREMOTE ENGINEER CONTACT INFO:\n\nName: Steven Piadade\n\nDirect Phone: 832-319-4138\n\nEmail: dpiadast@amazon.com\n\nPager Email: page-dpiadast@amazon.com\n\nREQUESTED REPAIR DATE/TIME: Monday, November 9, 2026 at 10:00 AM ET (local)\n\nReference: INC16986173\n\nLOW VOLTAGE / SMART HANDS DISPATCH - Copper cable fault diagnosis and repair\n\nSite: SO RAL / Raleigh (store 10016)\n\nSite address: 3540 Wade Ave, Raleigh, NC 27607, USA\n\nSite phone: (919) 828-5805\n\nAffected device/port: Grocery sales floor (cereal aisle) desk phone, ext 2111 (Grandstream GXP2170, MAC C074AD38AADA). Switch port unknown - aisle jack is not labeled on any switch.\n\nSymptom: no dial tone; phone has been offline since 10/02.\n\nRemote diagnostics already observed:\n\n\\- Ext 2111 not registered; last call activity 10/02.\n\n\\- Phone MAC not found on any of the 8 store switches; no link from the aisle jack.\n\nLV technician scope:\n\n1\\. Call the remote engineer on arrival.\n\n2\\. At the cereal aisle phone: confirm the phone has power, the cable is in the phone's LAN port, and note any error on the screen. Test the phone on a known-working phone jack. Report result, then return it to the aisle jack.\n\n3\\. Trace the aisle jack back to the patch panel in the MDF/IDF and confirm whether it is patched to a switch. Report the patch panel port and switch/port.\n\n4\\. TDR/Fluke test all four pairs on the aisle jack run and isolate any fault.\n\n5\\. Re-terminate the jack and/or patch panel side as needed, and re-test all four pairs.\n\n6\\. If the run is not patched: patch it to the switch port provided by the remote engineer.\n\n7\\. Label the aisle jack and patch panel port.\n\n8\\. Notify the remote engineer once complete so they can confirm link, PoE, and phone registration remotely.\n\nLV technician restrictions:\n\n\\* Do not change switch configuration (VLAN, port settings); the remote engineer will configure the port if needed.\n\n\\* Do not move or unplug any other patch cables or devices.\n\n\\* Do not power-cycle network equipment.\n\nCompletion / stop criteria:\n\n\\* Complete when the aisle phone has link and the remote engineer confirms ext 2111 is registered.\n\n\\* If the phone does not work on a known-good jack, stop and report; the phone will be replaced separately.\n\n\\* If the run cannot be repaired by re-termination (requires a full re-run), stop and report the TDR results and fault distance to the remote engineer.\n\nRemote engineer responsibility:\n\n\\* Configure the switch port for the aisle jack if needed (SNP inventory), confirm link/PoE and ext 2111 registration, and test calls with the store.\n\nTools Needed:\n\nFluke cable tester with TDR capability\n\nTone generator and probe\n\nPunch-down tool\n\nRJ45 keystone jack(s)\n\nCat5e/Cat6 patch cables\n\nCable labels and marker\n\nWire stripper/cutter\n\nFlashlight\n\nSite Access:\n\nA valid government-issued ID is required for site access. Technician must bring ID and follow all site access, safety, escort, and security requirements.\n\nCommunication / Microsoft Teams:\n\nTechnician must maintain communication with the Coordination Team through Field Nation messages and the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided. If a Teams chat is provided, technician must join it before arrival or as soon as access is provided, monitor it while onsite, and respond to reasonable coordination requests.\n\nField Nation remains the official system of record for work order status, payment, expenses, approvals, and disputes. Teams is used for real-time dispatch support, troubleshooting, photo review, blocker review, and deliverable coordination. Required deliverables must still be uploaded to Field Nation unless otherwise instructed in writing.\n\nTechnician must provide updates for:\n\n- Arrival onsite\n- Work started\n- Progress, delays, or idle time\n- Issues, blockers, access problems, or safety concerns\n- Completion status before leaving site\n- Checkout/departure from site\n\nTechnician must not leave site until the Coordination Team has been notified that work is complete or blocked and has had a reasonable opportunity to review required photos, test results, validation evidence, and completion notes.\n\nTime, Scope, Additional Work, and Expenses:\n\nTechnician must report accurate onsite work time. Additional time, return visits, out-of-scope work, material purchases, travel, parking, or other expenses must be approved in writing before being incurred. Technician must not assume approval for extra time, extra work, purchases, or return visits.\n\nApproved parts or materials require a clear store receipt, business receipt, or supplier invoice showing vendor name, purchase date, item description, quantity, and amount paid. Costs must be reasonable, necessary for the work order, related to the approved scope, and comparable to current market value.\n\nUnsupported time, unapproved expenses, excessive charges, missing receipts, out-of-scope work, or costs unrelated to the approved scope may delay approval and may be disputed, reduced, or rejected in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAssigned Technician / No Unapproved Substitution:\n\nThe technician assigned to the Field Nation work order is expected to perform the onsite work. Substitutions, helpers, trainees, or additional personnel must be disclosed and approved in writing before arriving onsite unless already permitted in the work order scope.\n\nDocumentation / Deliverables:\n\nAll required deliverables must be completed and uploaded before the work order can be closed or approved. Deliverables must be clear, complete, relevant, specific to this work order, and sufficient to validate the work performed. Photos must not be blurry, dark, reused from another job, duplicated without purpose, or missing the context needed to verify the work.\n\nRequired deliverables may include:\n\n- Before and after photos\n- Photos of devices, parts, ports, cables, connections, labels, serial numbers, asset tags, MAC addresses, tracking numbers, and work areas involved\n- Test results, cable test photos, validation screenshots, diagnostic results, link lights, online status screenshots, or other proof of functionality when applicable\n- Photos of damaged, missing, inaccessible, unsafe, or incomplete conditions\n- Completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, what remains open, and final status\n\nFor cabling, network, device-connectivity, POS, SCO, gate, kiosk, cart, camera, sensor, or peripheral work, technician must provide photo evidence of applicable test or validation results when applicable.\n\nIncomplete Work / Blockers:\n\nIf work cannot be completed, technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and document:\n\n- What was completed\n- What could not be completed\n- Why it could not be completed\n- Troubleshooting performed\n- Photos, screenshots, or test results showing the blocker\n- Parts, access, escalation, or follow-up needed\n\nProfessional Standards / Confidentiality:\n\nTechnician agrees to complete the work in a professional, workmanlike manner, follow site rules and safety requirements, keep the work area clean, protect customer/site information, and share photos or information only through approved Field Nation or assigned coordination channels.\n\nProvider Acknowledgment:\n\nBy applying to or accepting this work order, technician confirms they have reviewed the full scope, have prior experience performing this type of work, have all required tools unless otherwise approved in writing, understand the communication and Teams requirements, will request written approval before extra time/work/expenses/returns, and understand all required photos, test results, validation evidence, receipts, and completion notes must be provided before approval.\n\nMissing documentation, unsupported time, unapproved expenses, failure to communicate, failure to join or monitor Teams when provided, incomplete work, or failure to follow scope requirements may delay approval and may result in a revision request, payment dispute, reduction, or rejection in accordance with Field Nation’s process.\n\nAdditional Required Completion Items:\n\n- Technician must join the assigned Microsoft Teams dispatch chat if one is provided.\n- Technician must upload clear before photos showing the work area, device, equipment, or issue before work begins.\n- Technician must upload clear after photos showing the completed work, repair, installation, replacement, or final condition.\n- Technician must upload applicable validation or test evidence, including screenshots, test results, link lights, online status, cable test results, diagnostic results, or other proof of functionality when applicable.\n- Technician must provide completion notes explaining what was found, what was completed, what was tested, and the final status.\n- If the work cannot be completed, technician must document the blocker, troubleshooting performed, what remains incomplete, and what parts, access, escalation, or follow-up is needed.\n- Technician must upload receipts for any approved materials, parts, parking, travel, or other approved expenses.\n- Technician must notify the Coordination Team before leaving site and confirm completion status, blocker status, and departure.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T10:00","end":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.289733404790823},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000