{"job":{"id":20319378,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Install Install with helper","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Assignment Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Scope: Installation/replacement of 550 tray on Lexmark printer CX963.</p><p>SN: 7566447011459</p><p><strong>WO ID: 12292232</strong></p><p><strong>Special Instructions: </strong>If tech is onsite and has any questions, please contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com&nbsp;</p><p>Devices for password: pwrcl25 or pwrcl2025&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>PIN: 2424&nbsp;</p><p>Do not share these credentials with customers or end users.&nbsp;</p><p>Onsite exchange instructions: After an exchange/replacement, tech is to contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com&nbsp;</p><p>for call Closure on replacement.</p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Assignment Scope:**\n\nScope: Installation/replacement of 550 tray on Lexmark printer CX963.\n\nSN: 7566447011459\n\n**WO ID: 12292232**\n\n**Special Instructions:** If tech is onsite and has any questions, please contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com\n\nDevices for password: pwrcl25 or pwrcl2025\n\nPIN: 2424\n\nDo not share these credentials with customers or end users.\n\nOnsite exchange instructions: After an exchange/replacement, tech is to contact Scott Weddle scott.weddle@cummins.com\n\nfor call Closure on replacement.\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.\n\n**Overall Scope:**\n\n- Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.\n- Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.\n- Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.\n- Print all documentation and take to site organized.\n- Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.\n- If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).\n- Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.\n- Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.\n- Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.\n- Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.\n- Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.\n- Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.\n\n**Terms of Service:**\n\n- By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.\n- All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.\n- Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.\n- By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.\n- Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.\n- All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.\n- Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58.49966718068597},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.0