{"job":{"id":20320678,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Delaware Business Systems","title":"Point of Sale Configuration","description":{"html":"<p>DBS is looking for an experienced technician to convert a cashier point of sale station into a self-service kiosk. The technician would be working onsite with support from DBS remotely to reposition, reconfigure, and test all point of sale hardware. The technician needs to come prepared to remove 3M tape with their own tools. Replacement 3M tape will be onsite upon your arrival. Details of the requirements are listed here:</p><ul><li>Arrive onsite promptly at 8am.</li><li>Remove the cashier iPad point of sale station from the cash drawer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The station is attached to the top of the cash drawer with 2 strips of 3M double sided tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper. </li><li>Remove the credit card terminal and stand from the countertop</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This is attached to the countertop with 3M double sided tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper.</li><li>Remove the customer iPad display from the countertop</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This station is attached to the top of the counter with 2 strips of 3M double sided tape.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper.</li><li>Remove the cash drawer and customer display including all cables</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">These hardware components will not be used for the kiosk.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They will be left with the owner/manager to be put in their storage.</li><li>Reposition the hardware</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The iPad station will need to be flipped 180 degrees to face the customer.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The scanner, printer, and credit card terminal and stand need to be flipped 180 degrees to face the customer and placed to the right of the iPad.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">After confirming hardware placement with the owner/manager, the iPad and credit card terminal stand will need to be secured to the countertop with 3M double sided tape (this is being shipped to the establishment prior to your arrival).</li><li>Clean up all wiring</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All wiring needs to be cleaned up and secured (tie wraps may be needed)</li><li>Work with the DBS technician to reconfigure the hardware IP addresses and downloaded programs</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This will include changing the IP addresses of the iPad, printer, scanner, and credit card terminal.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The new kiosk database will need to be downloaded to the iPad.</li><li>Test all connections and operations</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This will be completed with the DBS technician then reviewed with the owner/manager.</li></ul>","markdown":"DBS is looking for an experienced technician to convert a cashier point of sale station into a self-service kiosk. The technician would be working onsite with support from DBS remotely to reposition, reconfigure, and test all point of sale hardware. The technician needs to come prepared to remove 3M tape with their own tools. Replacement 3M tape will be onsite upon your arrival. Details of the requirements are listed here:\n\n- Arrive onsite promptly at 8am.\n- Remove the cashier iPad point of sale station from the cash drawer\n- The station is attached to the top of the cash drawer with 2 strips of 3M double sided tape.\n- This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper.\n- Remove the credit card terminal and stand from the countertop\n- This is attached to the countertop with 3M double sided tape.\n- This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper.\n- Remove the customer iPad display from the countertop\n- This station is attached to the top of the counter with 2 strips of 3M double sided tape.\n- This will need to be carefully removed with a plastic scraper.\n- Remove the cash drawer and customer display including all cables\n- These hardware components will not be used for the kiosk.\n- They will be left with the owner/manager to be put in their storage.\n- Reposition the hardware\n- The iPad station will need to be flipped 180 degrees to face the customer.\n- The scanner, printer, and credit card terminal and stand need to be flipped 180 degrees to face the customer and placed to the right of the iPad.\n- After confirming hardware placement with the owner/manager, the iPad and credit card terminal stand will need to be secured to the countertop with 3M double sided tape (this is being shipped to the establishment prior to your arrival).\n- Clean up all wiring\n- All wiring needs to be cleaned up and secured (tie wraps may be needed)\n- Work with the DBS technician to reconfigure the hardware IP addresses and downloaded programs\n- This will include changing the IP addresses of the iPad, printer, scanner, and credit card terminal.\n- The new kiosk database will need to be downloaded to the iPad.\n- Test all connections and operations\n- This will be completed with the DBS technician then reviewed with the owner/manager.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T08:00","end":"2026-11-12T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6.573198609939605},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793982299284}
{"job":{"id":20320935,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Install New Managed PDU Power Supply","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME AND</strong><span style=\"color: red;\"> </span><strong style=\"color: red;\">CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL</strong></p><p>Patch cables may be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.</p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>BRIDGE INFO: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Microsoft Teams meeting Join: </span>https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2442404021902285?p=kTLD944x1NdBdV7yDz</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Meeting ID: 244 240 402 190 228 5</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(103, 106, 108);\">Passcode: 6xc2MC2C </span></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required&nbsp;Deliverables&nbsp;to be paid:</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.</li><li>When onsite call into the <strong>CONFERENCE BRIDGE&nbsp;</strong>Listed above or reach out to Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge <del>***** ********</del></li><li>Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge</li><li>Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)</li><li>Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (<strong>dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)</strong></li><li>Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested</li><li>Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.</li><li>Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.</li><li>Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge or call Dispatch Team if necessary</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.</p><p>2.&nbsp;Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code</u>:&nbsp;</strong>Business Casual</p><p><em>We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</em></p><p><em>THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH</em><strong><em><u>&nbsp;NEW ASSIGNMENTS</u></em></strong><em>.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME AND** **CALL INTO THE BRIDGE UPON ARRIVAL**\n\nPatch cables may be required to connect our SDWAN appliance(s) to new or existing circuits.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**BRIDGE INFO:** Microsoft Teams meeting Join: <https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/2442404021902285?p=kTLD944x1NdBdV7yDz>\n\nMeeting ID: 244 240 402 190 228 5\n\nPasscode: 6xc2MC2C\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n***Take pictures of the network area and upload to FN for the team on the bridge to see prior to beginning***\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n1. Enable GPS when in route to site for ETA.\n2. When onsite call into the **CONFERENCE BRIDGE** Listed above or reach out to Dispatch Team if no one is one the bridge \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n3. Find delivered equipment, unbox and stage it by the network rack until further instruction is provided on the bridge\n4. Survey Installation environment and determine where equipment will be installed. (in network rack, on backboard, etc.)\n5. Dialing into the bridge: Join Meeting (**dial in information to be entered once tech is secured)**\n6. Follow CommandLink Engineering and Customer Instructions on the conference bridge to install new SDWAN appliance as requested\n7. Verify with the CommandLink engineer the equipment is up and running.\n8. Perform tests as requested by CommandLink engineer.\n9. Take after pictures of equipment installation locations. Label the pictures you upload so we know what we are looking at.\n10. Get check out code from Engineer on conference bridge or call Dispatch Team if necessary\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1\\. Do not Request the Work order if you are not qualified to complete the work order.\n\n2\\. Tech must verify Model number and Serial number are correct before starting to work on device. If incorrect Tech must contact CommandLink before working on device.\n\n**Dress Code:** Business Casual\n\n*We appreciate technicians who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.*\n\n*THESE ARE THE TECHNICIANS WE CALL FIRST WITH* ***NEW ASSIGNMENTS****.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T12:30","end":"2026-11-10T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.413902841867891},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1793982974301}
{"job":{"id":20303127,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gable Services","title":"Service Work Order - The Streets at Southpoint - Standee Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p><em>***IF UNIT IS OUTDOORS, DO NOT OPEN IN INCLEMENT WEATHER! CALL POINT OF CONTACT IMMEDIATELY AND NOTIFY THEM OF THE SITUATION FOR FURTHER INSTRUCTIONS!***</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Standee has display issue</u></strong></p><p><strong>Contact Gable POC upon arrival, head to the standee. Troubleshoot display issue. You may need to take the standee apart. Bring an HDMI cable that is at least 6ft long.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Return key to mall management, ship damaged and/or unused parts using provided label, and check out with remote support when leaving site.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><del>**** ******** ** **** **** ******** ********** ** ** ********* ********** ** * ************** ** *****</del></p><ul><li>Please review attached documentation prior to arrival</li><li>Call point of contact upon arriving to location</li><li>Must check in with management or security to obtain keys and parts prior to beginning work</li></ul><p><u>Required Tools/Skillset:</u></p><ul><li><strong>Windows laptop</strong></li><li><strong>USB keyboard w/ mouse</strong></li><li><strong>Digital multimeter</strong></li><li>Digital Thermometer</li><li>Impact Driver</li><li>RJ45 Tester</li><li>RJ45 Crimper</li><li>Wire Crimper</li><li>Needle Nose Pliers</li><li>Small Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Small flathead screwdriver</li><li>Flathead screwdriver</li><li>#2 Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Zip ties of assorted sizes</li></ul><p><u>Dress Code:</u></p><ul><li>Collared or polo-type shirt</li><li>Closed toe shoes</li><li>Business casual bottoms (dark denim, khaki, black, etc)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PLEASE NOTE- Deliverables are required within 72 hours of the completion of this work order.**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>**Any damaged parts replaced during service c