e fullest extent permitted by law, the Contractor on this work order shall indemnify the Buyer on this work order from all damages, losses, or expenses, including attorney’s fees, from any claims or damages for bodily injury, sickness, disease, or death, or form claims for damages to tangible property, other than the Work itself.&nbsp;This indemnification shall extend to claims resulting from performance of this Work Order and shall apply only to the extent that the claim or loss is caused in whole or in part by any negligent act or omission of Contactor on this Work Order or any of its agents, employees, or subcontractors.&nbsp;This indemnity shall be effective regardless of whether the claim or loss is caused in some part by a party to be indemnified. The Contractor on this Work Order agrees to hold the Buyer on this Work Order harmless in the event of damages or injuries due to any negligence of the Contractor on this Work Order’s part, and that the Contractor on this Work Order will pay all legal and defense costs associated with any damage or injury claims.</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>For the duration of this agreement and for a period of (12) twelve months after the completion/ termination of this agreement; the Contractor will not directly or indirectly, for himself or on behalf of any other person, company, partnership, corporation or other entity, solicit or attempt to solicit, for the purposes of engaging in competition with Gable Company. This includes but is not limited to:</em></p><ul><li><em>The solicitation of Gable Company’s customers/clients, architects and engineers</em></li><li><em>The solicitation of Gable Company's customer/client employees</em></li><li><em>The solicitation of Gable Company's employees</em></li><li><em>The enticement, diversion or any other act that would otherwise damage, divert business, take away from Gable Company's business or patronage of any customer/client</em></li><li><em>The solicitation or inducement of any customer to terminate its relationship with Gable Company</em></li></ul><p><em>Unless expressly authorized in writing by the Gable Company, contractor agrees to retain the Confidential Information in confidence and shall not copy or disclose the Confidential Information to or use the Confidential Information for the benefit of any third party. Confidential Information shall only be disclosed to the contractor’s employees and, even then, only to the extent that such employees have a specific need to know of the Confidential Information, for the evaluation of the proposed transaction. Before receiving any part of the Confidential Information, contractor’s employees shall be required to read this Non-disclosure Agreement and, by receiving such Confidential Information, such employee shall acknowledge and agree to abide by the contractor’s obligations hereunder.</em></p>","markdown":"*\\*\\*\\*IF UNIT IS OUTDOORS, DO NOT OPEN IN INCLEMENT WEATHER! CALL POINT OF CONTACT IMMEDIATELY AND NOTIFY THEM OF THE SITUATION FOR FURTHER INSTRUCTIONS!\\*\\*\\**\n\n**Standee has display issue**\n\n**Contact Gable POC upon arrival, head to the standee. Troubleshoot display issue. You may need to take the standee apart. Bring an HDMI cable that is at least 6ft long.**\n\n**Return key to mall management, ship damaged and/or unused parts using provided label, and check out with remote support when leaving site.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- Please review attached documentation prior to arrival\n- Call point of contact upon arriving to location\n- Must check in with management or security to obtain keys and parts prior to beginning work\n\nRequired Tools/Skillset:\n\n- **Windows laptop**\n- **USB keyboard w/ mouse**\n- **Digital multimeter**\n- Digital Thermometer\n- Impact Driver\n- RJ45 Tester\n- RJ45 Crimper\n- Wire Crimper\n- Needle Nose Pliers\n- Small Phillips screwdriver\n- Small flathead screwdriver\n- Flathead screwdriver\n- \\#2 Phillips screwdriver\n- Zip ties of assorted sizes\n\nDress Code:\n\n- Collared or polo-type shirt\n- Closed toe shoes\n- Business casual bottoms (dark denim, khaki, black, etc)\n\n**\\*\\*PLEASE NOTE- Deliverables are required within 72 hours of the completion of this work order.\\*\\***\n\n***\\*\\*Any damaged parts replaced during service call must be in-transit before payment will be processed. Parts returned must be labeled \"bad\" or \"unused\" prior to shipping.\\*\\****\n\n*Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum.*\n\n*All site aborts MUST be approved by Point of Contact.*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*ATTENTION: ALL ITEMS ARE REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*-Failure to comply with the any of our policies and procedures listed below may result in a reduction or loss of compensation on this work order.*\n\n*-The requesting provider must be the provider who performs the actual service work onsite. You are expected to arrive onsite by yourself (no helpers, or assistants). Exceptions may be given but only upon prior approval by the Buyer on this Work Order.*\n\n*-Present yourself as an authorized representative of the Buyer on this Work Order, performing service on behalf of the Buyer on this Work Order. Do not promote any other company other than the Buyer on this Work Order, while on our jobsites.*\n\n*-Print this work order and all additional documentation. You MUST read the complete work order prior to arrival. Direct all questions to the Buyer on this Work Order.*\n\n*-DO NOT CONTACT THE END CLIENT unless specifically requested to do so by the Buyer on this work order.*\n\n*-You are expected to arrive on time and be prepared to perform the specified work on the given date and time provided on this 