{"job":{"id":20324004,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Scheduled Event - Data Cabling (Non-Fiber)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work: Following Tech Guide, and based on a previously completed site survey, tech will be running cable.</strong></p><p><strong>Overview: Total 32 runs,</strong> <strong>all but 4 of them approx. 50-60ft:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><strong>2 POS going where existing POS are located. 4 lines per POS totaling 8 lines - ~50ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Employee side of front counter. There will be 4 stations and 2 lines per station, totaling 8 lines - ~50ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Beverage video 2 lines – ~50ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>2 printers – 2 lines each totaling 4 - ~10ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Where the orders are picked up 2 lines for another video station - ~50-60ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Back wall near sandwich making station 4 lines. 2 for video and 2 for printer – ~50ft</strong>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>4 cables for each kiosk - ~60ft</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Important Tech Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)</li><li>Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival</li><li>Tech MUST obtain complete online deliverable prior to leaving site&nbsp;</li><li>Essintial Standard 7 Year Background Check&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Important Site Information:</strong></p><ul><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.</li><li>You must represent themselves as an Essintial technician on behalf of [Travel Centers] while on site.</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Online Deliverable Requirements | Due Back PRIOR TO LEAVE THE SITE</strong></p><ul><li>Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or&nbsp;If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact TA Service Desk @ 1-800-243-5782 to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off</li><li>Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device</li><li>Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Tools</strong></p><ul><li>Standard hand tools</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li><li>Laptop, with access to cellular hotspot</li><li>Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)</li><li>Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment</li><li>Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)</li><li>Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements:</strong></p><p>Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Photographic Deliverable Requirement- You are REQUIRED to capture &amp; submit all of the photos asked of you by your assigned support technician.</strong></p><p>Your deliverables photos MUST be uploaded to your work order via the online App and MUST be submitted&nbsp;PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.You are required to be onsite&nbsp;<strong>no later than</strong>&nbsp;your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face&nbsp;penalties/non-payment.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Confirmation, Cancellation &amp; Reimbursements:</strong></p><p>You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</p><p>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time</p><p>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Upon Arrival at site:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER&nbsp;</strong>–&nbsp;if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;to check in.&nbsp;</li><li>Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of Travel Centers (TA) to the onsite MOD</li><li>If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.</li><li>Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by TA Help Desk.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm functionality with XXXXX &amp; provide their name upon closure</li><li>Submit your Qualtrics deliverable</li><li>Call the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Attachments - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work: Following Tech Guide, and based on a previously completed site survey, tech will be running cable.**\n\n**Overview: Total 32 runs,** **all but 4 of them approx. 50-60ft:**\n\n- **2 POS going where existing POS are located. 4 lines per POS totaling 8 lines - ~50ft**\n- **Employee side of front counter. There will be 4 stations and 2 lines per station, totaling 8 lines - ~50ft**\n- **Beverage video 2 lines – ~50ft**\n- **2 printers – 2 lines each totaling 4 - ~10ft**\n- **Where the orders are picked up 2 lines for another video station - ~50-60ft**\n- **Back wall near sandwich making station 4 lines. 2 for video and 2 for printer – ~50ft**\n- **4 cables for each kiosk - ~60ft**\n\n**Important Tech Requirements:**\n\n- Tech MUST represent themselves as Essintial on behalf of Travel Centers of America (TA)\n- Tech MUST check-in with site MOD upon Arrival\n- Tech MUST obtain complete online deliverable prior to leaving site\n- Essintial Standard 7 Year Background Check\n\n**Important Site Information:**\n\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.\n- You must represent themselves as an Essintial technician on behalf of \\[Travel Centers\\] while on site.\n- You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n\n**Online Deliverable Requirements | Due Back PRIOR TO LEAVE THE SITE**\n\n- Tech will be asked to Obtain Customer Sign-Off or If Site POC is unavailable then the tech MUST contact TA Service Desk @ 1-800-243-5782 to be released from site and report the agents name in the online deliverable instead of obtaining sign-off\n- Tech will be asked to take a photo of the completed device\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables\n\n**Required Tools**\n\n- Standard hand tools\n- Screwdrivers\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Laptop, with access to cellular hotspot\n- Appropriate Console cables (for Cisco, Fortinet, Aruba)\n- Installation tools (for racking and unracking equipment\n- Cabling termination tools (RJ45 ends, jacks)\n- Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter)\n\n**Physical Requirements:**\n\nMust be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.\n\n**Photographic Deliverable Requirement- You are REQUIRED to capture &amp; submit all of the photos asked of you by your assigned support technician.**\n\nYour deliverables photos MUST be uploaded to your work order via the online App and MUST be submitted PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE.You are required to be onsite **no later than** your scheduled time, failure to arrive on time could result in a rescheduled event and escalation. Your scope of work is listed in your service title, if you exceed these estimates, you MUST provide a reason. Reasons caused by technician working slow or not following the install guide will not be paid out. Delays caused by customer or helpdesk MUST be documented to support additional pay. **NOTE:** **You MUST remain onsite until scope is complete or face penalties/non-payment.**\n\n**Confirmation, Cancellation &amp; Reimbursements:**\n\nYou will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n\nYou will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time\n\nAll expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n\n**Upon Arrival at site:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER** – if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- Introduce yourself as Essintial technician on behalf of Travel Centers (TA) to the onsite MOD\n- If applicable, locate parts or whole units shipped to site by Customer.\n- Remote technical support, if needed, is provided by TA Help Desk.\n\n**Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements:**\n\n- Confirm functionality with XXXXX &amp; provide their name upon closure\n- Submit your Qualtrics deliverable\n- Call the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n\n**Attachments - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T08:45","end":"2026-11-10T16:45"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":400},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":30.205368275595273},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 8:45 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2