eir state upon your arrival, any damage needs to be reported to the <del>********</del> Install Pro Services team</li><li>Confirm placement with Onsite POC</li><li>Before Drilling, confirm the placement given with the <del>********</del> Install Pro Services team</li><li>Complete physical installation of kiosks</li><li>Allow Electrician to connect the kiosks to permanent power</li><li>Work with <del>********</del> Install Pro Services team to set up Kiosk software and configure Pin Pads</li><li>Check offsite with <del>********</del> Install Pro Services Team</li><li>Check offsite with <del>*****</del> Service department</li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Please see the attached install guides for reference while onsite</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">TECH MUST TAKE PHOTOS OF ALL SHIPPED EQUIPMENT FROM ALL SIDES PRIOR TO OPENING. IF ANY BOXES HAVE DAMAGE, IT IS TO BE IMMEDIATELY REPORTED TO THE HELP DESK</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">IF TECH FAILS TO COMPLETE THE ABOVE AND EQUIPMENT IS DAMAGED, TECH WILL BE HELD LIABLE FOR THE DAMAGED EQUIPMENT</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"><em>TECH MUST DOCUMENT ALL S/N OF ALL AFFECTED EQUIPMENT</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>++REQUIRED DELIVERABLES:</strong></p><p>Paperwork:</p><ul><li>&nbsp;o Signed&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*****</del></span>&nbsp;CSR</li></ul><p>Photos:</p><ul><li>Photos of the equipment upon your arrival from multiple angles showing there is no damage prior to unpacking&nbsp;</li><li>Photo of intended install area</li><li>Aerial view of each Kiosk pedestal anchored showing which holes were used</li><li>Photo of each Kiosks serial number</li><li>Photo of the internal components of each kiosk&nbsp;</li><li>Photo showing that each kiosk is level</li><li>Photo of site’s network rack</li><li>Photo of the system information screen for each Pin Pan</li><li>Photo showing the each kiosk loaded with the POS Software</li><li>Wide shot Photo showing the full kiosk, top to bottom</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>++REQUIRED TOOLS:</strong></p><ul><li>Hammer drill</li><li>Anchor Bolts</li><li>reciprocating saw</li><li>Laser level</li><li>Measuring tape</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Socket Wrench with assorted sockets</li><li>CAT5 Termination tools</li><li>Keyboard and Mouse</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Installation 2 counter top kiosks<br/><br/>Please check in/out with the following contact, they will also be your POC for any troubleshooting needs. Tillster Install Pro Services 855-465-2204. please notate who you spoke with on your paperwork.<br/>Please call the Zutek service department to check on/off site at 941-662-4459</p><p><strong><u>The Fine Print of Requirements:</u></strong></p><p>All deliverables &ndash;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*****</del></span>&nbsp;exit code, paperwork (<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*****</del></span>&nbsp;CSR and vendor WO.), pictures and/or cable certifications &ndash; must be received, via email or uploaded to Field Nation, before leaving the job site.&nbsp;If these guidelines are not met without prior authorization a $50 penalty will be assessed upon leaving site. An additional 10% penalty of your per job rate will be assessed for each day paperwork/photos remain incomplete. If applicable, you must provide the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>*****</del></span>&nbsp;exit code in the resolution of the assignment before you will be paid.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p><p>By requesting / accepting this work order you agree to the terms set above.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* is a nationwide service and deployment company looking to add quality field staff to our Field Nation Network. We do a wide variety of POS, CCTV, Digital Signage, Out Door Menu Boards, and many other related technologies in the Hospitality and Retail Industries.\n\nDuring the performance of Work you shall refrain from performing any services beyond the scope of services outlined in the Statement of Work. If additional work is requested/required, you must obtain prior approval from the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Project Manager while onsite. Time onsite exceeding the original work order must also be approved by the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Project Manager while onsite. Otherwise, \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* has the right to refuse payment for the additional services.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nNeed technician to install X XXXX Kiosks, install software, and configure pin pads with help desk\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**++SOW AND PROCESSES:**\n\n1. Check onsite with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Service department upon your arrival\n2. Check onsite with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Install Pro Services team\n3. Locate equipment and take photos of their state upon your arrival, any damage needs to be reported to the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Install Pro Services team\n4. Confirm placement with Onsite POC\n5. Before Drilling, confirm the placement given with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Install Pro Services team\n6. Complete physical installation of kiosks\n7. Allow Electrician to connect the kiosks to permanent power\n8. Work with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Install Pro Services team to set up Kiosk software and configure Pin Pads\n9. Check offsite with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Install Pro Services Team\n10. Check offsite with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Service department\n\nPlease see the attached install guides for reference while onsite\n\n**TECH MUST TAKE PHOTOS OF ALL SHIPPED EQUIPMENT FROM ALL SIDES PRIOR TO OPENING. IF ANY BOXES HAVE DAMAGE, IT IS TO BE IMMEDIATELY REPORTED TO THE HELP DESK**\n\n**IF TECH FAILS TO COMPLETE THE ABOVE AND EQUIPMENT IS DAMAGED, TECH WILL BE HELD LIABLE FOR THE DAMAGED EQUIPMENT**\n\n***TECH MUST DOCUMENT ALL S/N OF ALL AFFECTED EQUIPMENT***\n\n**++REQUIRED DELIVERABLES:**\n\nPaperwork:\n\n- o Signed \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* CSR\n\nPhotos:\n\n- Photos of the equipment upon your arrival from multiple angles showing there is no damage prior to unpacking\n- Photo of intended install area\n- Aerial view of each Kiosk pedestal anchored showing which holes were used\n- Photo of each Kiosks serial number\n- Photo of the internal components of each kiosk\n- Photo showing that each kiosk is level\n- Photo of site’s network rack\n- Photo of the system information screen for each Pin Pan\n- Photo showing the each kiosk loaded with the POS Software\n- Wide shot Photo showing the full kiosk, top to bottom\n\n**++REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Hammer drill\n- Anchor Bolts\n- reciprocating saw\n- Laser level\n- Measuring tape\n- Basic hand tools\n- Socket Wrench with assorted sockets\n- CAT5 Termination tools\n- Keyboard and Mouse\n\nInstallation 2 counter top kiosks  \n  \nPlease check in/out with the following contact, they will also be your POC for any troubleshooting needs. Tillster Install Pro Services 855-465-2204. please notate who you spoke with on your paperwork.  \nPlease call the Zutek service department to check on/off site at 941-662-4459\n\n**The Fine Print of Requirements:**\n\nAll deliverables – \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* exit code, paperwork (\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* CSR and vendor WO.), pictures and/or cable certifications – must be received, via email or uploaded to Field Nation, before leaving the job site. If these guidelines are not met without prior authorization a $50 penalty will be assessed upon leaving site. An additional 10% penalty of your per job rate will be assessed for each day paperwork/photos remain incomplete. If applicable, you must provide the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* exit code in the resolution of the assignment before you will be paid.\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\nBy requesting / accepting this work order you agree to the terms set above.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-19T08:00","end":"2026-11-19T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":330},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":47.5824388325848},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"menu boards\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Ral