{"job":{"id":20321830,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Comm-Works","title":"CVS - Moneygram DT3","description":{"html":"<p>Scope of work per site:</p><p>Obtain permission from the Manager to go behind the Front Store Counter, and work with the Manager to locate the existing MoneyGram DT3 device.</p><p>Reprogram the MoneyGram DT3 IP and DNS addresses per the Redbook directions.</p><p>Work with the Manager to determine where the network rack is located in the store.</p><p>Obtain permission from the Manager to access the network rack location.</p><p>On the 48-port main store switch, determine the status of Port 29: open, already connected to the MoneyGram DT3, or connected to another device.</p><p>If the MoneyGram DT3 is already in Port 29, or the port is open, move the MoneyGram DT3 cable to Port 29 or confirm it is already connected there.</p><p>If a different device is in Port 29, notify the ROC. The ROC will work with the CVS network team and the vendor technician to move the existing cable to a different port so the MoneyGram DT3 can be moved to Port 29.</p><p>Notify the ROC that the configuration is complete and the MoneyGram DT3 network cable has been moved on the main store switch.</p><p>The ROC will remotely test the MoneyGram DT3 device once notified.</p>","markdown":"Scope of work per site:\n\nObtain permission from the Manager to go behind the Front Store Counter, and work with the Manager to locate the existing MoneyGram DT3 device.\n\nReprogram the MoneyGram DT3 IP and DNS addresses per the Redbook directions.\n\nWork with the Manager to determine where the network rack is located in the store.\n\nObtain permission from the Manager to access the network rack location.\n\nOn the 48-port main store switch, determine the status of Port 29: open, already connected to the MoneyGram DT3, or connected to another device.\n\nIf the MoneyGram DT3 is already in Port 29, or the port is open, move the MoneyGram DT3 cable to Port 29 or confirm it is already connecte