{"job":{"id":"7710195618","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Reality Interactive","title":"Spectrum: 5020 Burlington NC - Tech visit to replace Ribbon and Break Room TVs.","description":"<p><strong>SOW: Replace old TVs with new TVs and Tuners that were sent to site. Dispose of old TVs offsite<u>.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Total TVs: 5</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>RC (Ribbon Content Wall): 4 TVs → RC1 – RC4</strong></p><p><strong>EBR (Employee Break Room): 1 TV → EBR1</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Salvage one of the good TVs from the Ribbon Wall, to replace the Break Room TV.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Approximate Visit Length</strong>: 3 hrs</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>A laptop with an Ethernet port&nbsp;</li><li>Working Ethernet Cable&nbsp;</li><li>Smartphone with Camera&nbsp;</li><li>Screwdriver (multi-bit)&nbsp;</li><li>USB Keyboard and Mouse&nbsp;</li><li>Basic Hand Tools&nbsp;</li><li>5-8ft ladder&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Recommended but not required</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Power drill with drill bits&nbsp;</li><li>Cable snake&nbsp;</li><li>Spare 3/4\" spacers&nbsp;</li><li>Level&nbsp;</li><li>RJ45 Crimper&nbsp;</li><li>Zip Ties&nbsp;</li><li>Electronics Duster&nbsp;</li><li>Duct Tape&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Site Arrival and Check-In</strong></p><ol><li>Call <strong>Reality Interactive @ 860-852-5035</strong> upon arrival.</li><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact.</li><li>Confirm locations of the TVs to be replaced (<strong>RC1–4</strong>).</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Unbox and Inspect New Equipment</strong></p><ol><li>Retrieve new TVs and ZVsync tuners with the store manager.</li><li>Document the <strong>serial number</strong> and <strong>asset tag</strong> of each ZVsync tuner.</li><li>Arrange each tuner according to its position: <strong>RC1–RC4.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Take </u>photos of serials and asset tags</strong> before mounting anything</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Remove Existing TVs</strong></p><ol><li><strong>NOTE:</strong> Please remove <strong>one </strong>TV and verify that all the equipment fits correctly before proceeding with other TVs</li><li>Carefully remove old TVs.</li><li>Leave existing <strong>coax, HDMI, and power lines</strong> accessible.</li><li>Note and document <strong>mounting bracket hole positions.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Mount and Connect Tuners (Before TV Install)</strong></p><ol><li>At each location:</li><li>Mount the <strong>ZVsync tuner</strong> to the wall behind where the TV will go.</li><li>Connect <strong>coax from wall drop → RF IN</strong> on tuner.</li><li>Connect <strong>HDMI OUT</strong> from tuner and leave it accessible for later TV connection.</li><li>Mount <strong>IR sensor</strong> to bottom-right of tuner location (aligned with TV bottom-right corner).</li><li>Ensure all cables are <strong>cleanly routed and secured.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Mount New TVs</strong></p><ol><li>Attach bracket to new TV using same holes as old unit.</li><li>Connect <strong>HDMI from tuner → HDMI 1</strong> on TV.</li><li>Mount TV securely to the wall.</li><li>Use a <strong>level</strong> to ensure alignment with adjacent units.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Power and Configure</strong></p><ol><li>Power on <strong>TV and tuner.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Using the </u>Samsung Remote:</strong></li><li><strong><u>Run through the TV setup using the attached guide</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Once Complete Set TV input to </u>HDMI 1</strong></li><li><strong><u>Assign </u>static IP: </strong></li><li><strong><u>RC IP 172.16.213.104 through 172.16.213.107 </u></strong></li><li><strong><u>EBR IP  172.16.213.127</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Gateway 172.16.213.1</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>DNS 8.8.8.8</u></strong></li><li>Disable any unused services or popups as directed by RI</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Set Channels and Test</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Run a channel scan</strong> and confirm it receives all channels (e.g., <strong>61, 62, 81–84</strong>)</li><li>Use <strong>ZVsync remote</strong> to tune each TV to the correct channel .</li><li>Confirm that content displays correctly and <strong>IR remote works.</strong> proper channel reception.</li><li>Call RI for support if any tuner fails to display content.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation (Take clear photos of)</strong></p><ol><li>Each <strong>TV powered on</strong> with content visible</li><li>Each <strong>tuner installed</strong> with asset tag visible</li><li><strong>IR sensor placement</strong></li><li><strong>Wide-angle shots</strong> of each wall section (RC, RW, MAW)</li><li><strong>TV serial numbers and wired MAC via support screen</strong> if not captured earlier</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Final Review and Checkout</strong></p><ol><li>Call <strong>Reality Interactive @ 860-840-7100</strong> for final approval.</li><li>Upload all <strong>audit photos and asset tag documentation</strong> before leaving.</li><li>Ensure <strong>workspace is clean</strong> and all packaging removed.</li><li><strong>Tech to dispose of old equipment locally.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><em>Please understand additional troubleshooting steps may be asked by the Reality Interactive Support Team during the visit to ensure all needs are met.</em></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T10:00","end":"2026-11-11T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":48.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TVs\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-