{"job":{"id":20321587,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"Ruby Tuesday 4654\tFayetteville - Owen Dr\t1870 Owen Drive\tFayetteville\tNC\t28304","description":{"html":"<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>9/17/2026 EST 11/11/2026 10/28/2026 Case 02287396 RMA<del>******</del></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Additional note: if there's not a MOD on site when they arrive they need to call into our service desk 214-<del>***</del>-<del>****</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Field Technician Instructions – Hardware Refresh</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>1.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Arrive Prepared &amp; Review</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Required: Bring a 10-ft ladder. Wi-Fi access points may be mounted on or above drop ceilings.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Required: Bring a label maker. Label all new equipment as well as any out of sight wifi access points, particularly those placed above ceiling tiles.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Network diagrams have been provided for reference. Review the diagrams before beginning work.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before disconnecting equipment, take clear photos of the existing FortiGate, APs, and cabling.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Note or label existing connections as necessary to ensure equipment is properly reconnected.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Replace Network Equipment</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Replace the existing FortiGate 60E with the new FortiGate 40F.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Replace all three Meraki MR33 Wi-Fi APs with three Meraki MR28 APs.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Install the new APs in the same locations as the existing units unless otherwise directed.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Reconnect existing Ethernet cabling and power as applicable.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Label AP Locations</strong></p>\n<p><strong>For each Wi-Fi AP, print and install a label identifying the AP/location.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If an AP is installed above a drop ceiling, place a small, subtle label or indicator on the ceiling grid/tile directly below or adjacent to the AP location.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The intent is to allow a future technician to quickly identify which ceiling tile provides access to the AP without creating an obvious or distracting customer-facing label.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Final Testing &amp; Job Completion Checklist</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before leaving the site, verify all items below:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ FortiGate 40F is powered on and operating normally.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ Internet connectivity is confirmed through the new FortiGate.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ All three Meraki MR28 APs are installed, powered, and showing normal status.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ Wi-Fi connectivity is successfully tested from a wireless device.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ Each AP/location has been properly labeled, including a subtle ceiling location indicator where applicable.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) is tested by briefly disconnecting AC power and confirming connected network equipment remains powered.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ AC power is restored and the UPS returns to normal operation/charging.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ Existing Manager PC and POS PC connections remain unchanged and functional.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ All cables and equipment are secure and the work area is clean.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>☐ Final photos are taken showing the FortiGate, cabling, UPS, each installed AP, and AP location labels.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Do not leave the site until all tests pass or any failed test has been reported and acknowledged.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************ **** *</del></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li><strong>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call</strong> <del>************ *** *</del>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**9/17/2026 EST 11/11/2026 10/28/2026 Case 02287396 RMA\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Additional note: if there's not a MOD on site when they arrive they need to call into our service desk 214-\\*\\*\\*-\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Field Technician Instructions – Hardware Refresh**\n\n**1.**\n\n**Arrive Prepared &amp; Review**\n\n**Required: Bring a 10-ft ladder. Wi-Fi access points may be mounted on or above drop ceilings.**\n\n**Required: Bring a label maker. Label all new equipment as well as any out of sight wifi access points, particularly those placed above ceiling tiles.**\n\n**Network diagrams have been provided for reference. Review the diagrams before beginning work.**\n\n**Before disconnecting equipment, take clear photos of the existing FortiGate, APs, and cabling.**\n\n**Note or label existing connections as necessary to ensure equipment is properly reconnected.**\n\n**2.**\n\n**Replace Network Equipment**\n\n**Replace the existing FortiGate 60E with the new FortiGate 40F.**\n\n**Replace all three Meraki MR33 Wi-Fi APs with three Meraki MR28 APs.**\n\n**Install the new APs in the same locations as the existing units unless otherwise directed.**\n\n**Reconnect existing Ethernet cabling and power as applicable.**\n\n**3.**\n\n**Label AP Locations**\n\n**For each Wi-Fi AP, print and install a label identifying the AP/location.**\n\n**If an AP is installed above a drop ceiling, place a small, subtle label or indicator on the ceiling grid/tile directly below or adjacent to the AP location.**\n\n**The intent is to allow a future technician to quickly identify which ceiling tile provides access to the AP without creating an obvious or distracting customer-facing label.**\n\n**Final Testing &amp; Job Completion Checklist**\n\n**Before leaving the site, verify all items below:**\n\n**☐ FortiGate 40F is powered on and operating normally.**\n\n**☐ Internet connectivity is confirmed through the new FortiGate.**\n\n**☐ All three Meraki MR28 APs are installed, powered, and showing normal status.**\n\n**☐ Wi-Fi connectivity is successfully tested from a wireless device.**\n\n**☐ Each AP/location has been properly labeled, including a subtle ceiling location indicator where applicable.**\n\n**☐ UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) is tested by briefly disconnecting AC power and confirming connected network equipment remains powered.**\n\n**☐ AC power is restored and the UPS returns to normal operation/charging.**\n\n**☐ Existing Manager PC and POS PC connections remain unchanged and functional.**\n\n**☐ All cables and equipment are secure and the work area is clean.**\n\n**☐ Final photos are taken showing the FortiGate, cabling, UPS, each installed AP, and AP location labels.**\n\n**Do not leave the site until all tests pass or any failed test has been reported and acknowledged.**\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. **Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.**\n3. **Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-10T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":380},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":90}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.95946260866245},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":100,"baseAmount":400,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":90,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":100}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T19:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z