{"job":{"id":20326067,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TruMed Systems","title":"Vaccine Management Machine - Load Tray Obstruction - 01647","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work OVERVIEW</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Reported Issues: Remove Work Surface with TruMed technician.<br/>Observe and identify the cause of the Load Tray Stall - either a failing coupler or obstructing seal.<br/>Replace / Troubleshoot parts as needed. Tracking: No Parts Required</span></p><p><strong>Video Tutorials Below</strong></p><p><del>*** ** ****** ***** **** ******* </del><del>****************************</del></p><p><del>*** ** ******* ******** **** *************</del><del>*******************************************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***ALL TOOLS LISTED BELOW ARE REQUIRED TO GET PAID.***</strong></p><p><strong>Scope Specific Tools</strong></p><ul><li>PPE</li><li>T10 Torx Driver</li><li>T10 Torx Driver</li><li>T20 Torx bit (¼” or ⅜”)</li><li>Sharpie/Marker</li><li>Ratchet with ¼” or ⅜” socket (matching your T20 Torx bit)</li><li>Magnetizer </li><li>Screw organizer </li><li>Reference instructions-<strong>AV0017_Work Instruction_PCA Replacements Under Work Surface_Rev B.pdf</strong></li></ul><p>DO NOT USE POWER TOOL</p><p><strong>Essential Hardware</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Torx tools</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T20 Torx Dri</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T10 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T5 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1.3 mm driver&nbsp;</li><li>Sharpie</li><li>6mm, 5mm, 4mm, 3mm, 2.5mm, 2mm Allen wrench set</li><li>T20, T10, T8 Driver or T-Tool</li><li>Torx key set (T20, T15, T10, T8, T5)</li><li>Mini ratchet with T30, T20, T15, T10, T8, T5 bits</li><li>Standard 4&ndash;6\" Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Wire stripping tool</li><li>Wire crimping tool</li><li>Wire butt connectors</li><li>13mm crescent wrench</li><li>Socket set with ratchet including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6.5mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">7mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">10mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">11mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">13mm</li><li>Digital multimeter / voltmeter</li><li>Handheld vacuum</li><li>Needle-nose pliers</li><li>Standard pliers</li><li>Channel-lock pliers</li><li>Extendable magnetic pickup tool for dropped screws</li><li>Tool magnetizer for retaining screws on driver heads</li><li>Utility knife</li><li>X-Acto knife</li><li>4\" (small) zip ties</li><li>Electrical tape</li><li>Suction cup (90 lb. rating)</li><li>Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)</li></ul><p><strong>Cleaning &amp; Advanced Repair</strong></p><ul><li>Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)</li><li>Heat gun (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Alcohol wipes</li><li>Window cleaner</li><li>Paper towels</li><li>Nitrile gloves</li><li>Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws</li><li>10-amp automotive fuse</li><li>15-amp automotive fuse</li></ul><p><strong>Convenience &amp; Specialty Tools</strong></p><ul><li>Sharpie or permanent marker</li><li>EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor</li><li>Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)</li><li>Tool bag or hard case carrier</li><li>Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Professional Conduct Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive fit for duty</li><li>No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work</li><li>No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite</li><li>Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited</li><li>Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is 