re not properly equipped.**\n\n**⚠ CLOSEOUT REQUIREMENTS — READ BEFORE ACCEPTING**\n\n- **Checkout includes a photo review of all work completed on-site. Payment will not be processed until photos have been reviewed and approved by your Work Order Manager.**\n- **Proper closeout notes are required for every Work Order. Vague or incomplete notes will delay payment.**\n- **Your closeout notes must include:**A clear description of the issue found on-site\n- Each specific step taken to troubleshoot and/or resolve the issue\n- The outcome of each step\n- Final resolution status (resolved, unresolved, revisit required, etc.)\n\n❌ **Not acceptable:***\"Device was offline. Rebooted and it came back up.\"* ✅**Acceptable:***\"Arrived on-site and found tablet unresponsive with no display output. Checked power connection — cord was loose at the POE injector. Reseated the connection. Tablet powered on and began loading content. Confirmed content was playing on screen. Notified WO Manager and received clearance to close out.\"*\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK &amp; TIME COMPENSATION**\n\n- This Work Order covers **one (1) hour of on-site work**.\n- If the work requires more than one hour, additional time will be compensated at **$60 per additional hour.**\n- **Any time beyond the initial one-hour window must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager before continuing work. Unauthorized overtime will not be compensated.**\n- **This Work Order includes servicing all Looma devices on-site.** Acceptance of this Work Order constitutes agreement to service any and all Looma devices present at this location, provided the work falls within the original one-hour window.\n- **No additional charges will be approved for servicing multiple devices if the total time on-site remains within the one-hour agreed-upon window.**\n\n**WORK ORDER MANAGER AVAILABILITY**\n\nMonday–Friday: 9:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST Saturday–Sunday: 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST\n\nContact: **(866) 440-5667** Email: support@theloomaproject.com\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nYou must have all of the following before accepting this Work Order:\n\n1. Cell phone with camera capabilities\n2. Wireless keyboard and mouse\n3. 10' ladder\n4. Phillips head screwdriver\n5. Personal hotspot (to connect devices to Wi-Fi if needed)\n\n**OVERVIEW**\n\nLooma operates an in-store media platform via Loop™ tablets. One or more tablets at this retail location are currently offline and cannot be remotely accessed — they must be troubleshot in person. You will receive the store address and detailed instructions to locate the offline tablet(s) and complete a predefined troubleshooting sequence. You must confirm results with a Looma representative before leaving the site.\n\n*This Work Order may require a follow-up revisit for a simple part replacement (e.g., POE injector or power cord). Revisits are compensated at $60 per visit.*\n\n**HT WORK ORDER #:** INC13274488\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL TASKS**\n\nComplete the following before arriving on-site:\n\n1. Set your start time in the Field Nation platform\n2. Download and review the **Offline Tablet Reference Guide** (attached) and**HT\\_Chromebox\\_Troubleshooting\\_Guide**\n\n**STORE ENTRY PROCEDURE**\n\nUpon entering the store, proceed to the **Customer Service Desk**. Present your printable badge, disclose your affiliation with Looma, and provide the **HT Work Order number**. If store staff have questions or concerns, refer them to:\n\n**Looma Field Support Team** 📧 support@theloomaproject.com 📞 (866) 440-LOOP\n\n**ON-SITE TASKS**\n\nComplete in order:\n\n1. **Check in with the WO Manager** — Call**(866) 440-5667** upon arrival\n2. **Check in with Customer Service**\n3. **Locate the Loop™ display** referenced at check-in with your WO Manager. *Note: The display may be in the back receiving area.*\n4. **Photograph the entire display** before beginning any maintenance\n5. **Troubleshoot** using the Offline Tablet Reference Guide (attached)\n6. **Photograph the entire display** after completing maintenance\n7. **Check out with the WO Manager** before leaving — confirm results, photo review, and closeout notes must be complete before you will be cleared to exit the site\n8. **Check out with Customer Service**\n\n**HOW TO LOCATE THE LOOP™ DISPLAY**\n\nLoop™ displays at this retailer come in multiple form factors. A representative photo of the display type you will be servicing is attached. Note that an offline tablet may have no visible content on screen. If you cannot locate the display, contact your WO Manager immediately.\n\n**HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LOOP™ TABLET**\n\nA comprehensive troubleshooting guide is attached as a PDF. It includes reference photos and step-by-step instructions. Follow the guide as written and contact your WO Manager with any questions.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-06T11:00","end":"2026-11-06T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-06T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":3.640436703817381},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-06T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-06T16:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-06T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794006255549}
{"job":{"id":20326682,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Break Fix - Access Point (AP) Outage / AP Offline Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Goal is to restore service to offline Access Point(s) onsite which will include cable testing, moving hardware, pinhole resetting. Cable re-termination, Structured cabling survey, patch cable replacement, and cable tracing may be required. Comcast may seek additional break fix support for any unforeseen issues while onsite.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>AP Offline Troubleshooting</strong></p><p> Investigate and troubleshoot offline AP RDUMCAP05-16-Concierge-Lounge-2 (60235) connected to switch RDUMCSW01-17, Port 27. </p><p>1. Locate the AP in the Concierge Lounge and inspect its physical condition.</p><p> 2. Check the Ethernet cable connections at both the AP and switch ends. </p><p>3. Verify Port 27 status on the switch, including link activity and PoE power delivery.</p><p>4. Check the AP&#39;s power and LED status. </p><p>5. Verify the switch port configuration and assigned VLAN.</p><p>6. Test the network cable and replace it if necessary. </p><p>7. Power-cycle the AP and check whether it comes back online.</p><p> 8. Capture photos of the AP, cable connections, and switch port if the issue persists.</p><p> 9. Report the findings and confirm whether the AP is operational. </p><p>Expected Outcome: Identify and resolve the cause of the AP outage and restore network connectivity.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools/Material Requirements:</u></strong></p><p> </p><ul><li>Cell Phone – with Charger. </li><li>WIN10 Laptop – with Charger</li><li>Console Cable (DB9 male to RJ45)</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Cat 6 cables</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Hotspot or Internet Dongle</li><li>Black Ink Pens (for documentation)</li></ul><p> </p><p> </p><p><em>Review the </em><strong><em><u>“Confidential Section”</u></em></strong><em> listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including</em></p><ul><li>Circuit location and ID</li><li>Equipment details</li><li>Icon info</li><li>Bridge line #</li></ul><p>Please bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum.</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Mandatory to be released from the site by the Remote Engineer once the equipment is confirmed online &amp; photos are verified.</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID required</li><li>Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>*******</del></li><li>Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPEAP Offline Troubleshooting</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nGoal is to restore service to offline Access Point(s) onsite which will include cable testing, moving hardware, pinhole resetting. Cable re-termination, Structured cabling survey, patch cable replacement, and cable tracing may be required. Comcast may seek additional break fix support for any unforeseen issues while onsite.\n\n**AP Offline Troubleshooting**\n\n Investigate and troubleshoot offline AP RDUMCAP05-16-Concierge-Lounge-2 (60235) connected to switch RDUMCSW01-17, Port 27.\n\n1\\. Locate the AP in the Concierge Lounge and inspect its physical condition.\n\n 2. Check the Ethernet cable connections at both the AP and switch ends.\n\n3\\. Verify Port 27 status on the switch, including link activity and PoE power delivery.\n\n4\\. Check the AP's power and LED status.\n\n5\\. Verify the switch port configuration and assigned VLAN.\n\n6\\. Test the network cable and replace it if necessary.\n\n7\\. Power-cycle the AP and check whether it comes back online.\n\n 8. Capture photos of the AP, cable connections, and switch port if the issue persists.\n\n 9. Report the findings and confirm whether the AP is operational.\n\nExpected Outcome: Identify and resolve the cause of the AP outage and restore network connectivity.\n\n**Tools/Material Requirements:**\n\n- Cell Phone – with Charger.\n- WIN10 Laptop – with Charger\n- Console Cable (DB9 male to RJ45)\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Cat 6 cables\n- Cable Tester\n- Hotspot or Internet Dongle\n- Black Ink Pens (for documentation)\n\n*Review the* ***“Confidential Section”*** *listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including*\n\n- Circuit location and ID\n- Equipment details\n- Icon info\n- Bridge line #\n\nPlease bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum.\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Mandatory to be released from the site by the Remote Engineer once the equipment is confirmed online &amp; photos are verified.\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPEAP Offline Troubleshooting","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.417575199885244},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794007652966}
{"job":{"id":20326764,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":" Troubleshoot Camera System","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.</span></p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******** * </del></span><del>******************</del></li><li>Technicians can text 'Start' to <del>***** ********</del>. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.</li></ul><p>Statement of Work - Issue / Problem :&nbsp;Camera System Down / Offline&nbsp;</p><p>SOW: The technician will troubleshoot the camera system that is currently non-operational, beginning with a comprehensive inspection of all hardware components, including cameras, cabling, power supplies, network connections, and recording devices. The technician must include diagnosing faults, identifying points of failure, and testing system connectivity and performance. The technician will repair or replace minor defective components as needed, reconfigure system settings, and restore functionality to all cameras. Additionally, they will verify proper system operation, ensure video feeds are accessible and recording correctly. The technician must bring the necessary equipment needed, coordinate with the store manager to verify full site functionality, coordinate with us also to verify remote functionality, and check whether everything is working properly before leaving the premise.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>IMPORTANT: After resolving the reported issue, perform a brief walk-through and visually inspect the entire system for damage, loose or misaligned devices, obstructions, or other concerns. Document and repair any issues when possible. The WO remains incomplete until this inspection is completed</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Parts Needed:&nbsp;</p><p>NONE&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Cause :&nbsp;</p><p>Possible connectivity issues&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>RMA Form: Complete link &amp; Return Label provided. https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Text with Interface Support:&nbsp;STS: <del>**************</del></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.</li><li>Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.</li><li>All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location</li><li>Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call <del>************ ** ***</del> service desk if support does not transfer.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> *** WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN ***</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).</li><li>Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc</li><li>Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable</li><li>Release Code</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOOLS/MATERIALS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</span></p><ul><li>Laptop (Windows 11)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Operating system must be fully licensed and updated</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">· Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting</li><li>Basic IT Tools</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers</li><li>Drill</li><li>12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete</li><li>8' Ladder</li><li>Phone/Ethernet Wiring</li><li>Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</li><li>Copy of work order and job information</li><li>Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</span></p><ul><li>Long pants</li><li>Collared shirt</li><li>Netfor name badge</li><li>Close toe shoes</li><li>Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)</strong></p>","markdown":"BY ACCEPTING THIS ASSIGNMENT, YOU ARE AGREEING TO COMPLETE THE WO, UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES WHILE ON SITE AND COMPLETE THE CHECK IN/OUT PROCESS FULLY.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTech will need to call or text into customer help desk before beginning:\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians can text 'Start' to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. Please have SR number and Location Name ready.\n\nStatement of Work - Issue / Problem : Camera System Down / Offline\n\nSOW: The technician will troubleshoot the camera system that is currently non-operational, beginning with a comprehensive inspection of all hardware components, including cameras, cabling, power supplies, network connections, and recording devices. The technician must include diagnosing faults, identifying points of failure, and testing system connectivity and performance. The technician will repair or replace minor defective components as needed, reconfigure system settings, and restore functionality to all cameras. Additionally, they will verify proper system operation, ensure video feeds are accessible and recording correctly. The technician must bring the necessary equipment needed, coordinate with the store manager to verify full site functionality, coordinate with us also to verify remote functionality, and check whether everything is working properly before leaving the premise.\n\nIMPORTANT: After resolving the reported issue, perform a brief walk-through and visually inspect the entire system for damage, loose or misaligned devices, obstructions, or other concerns. Document and repair any issues when possible. The WO remains incomplete until this inspection is completed\n\nParts Needed:\n\nNONE\n\nCause :\n\nPossible connectivity issues\n\nRMA Form: Complete link &amp; Return Label provided. https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/9281df6232974896b4df621498dc5c88&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nText with Interface Support: STS: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- Technician will not leave the site until the site is on primary and all services are working as expected.\n- Any unused/RMA parts will need to be returned to FedEx via store/kiosk drop off. Must fill in form along with return label if part being returned.\n- All old equipment being replaced can be left with MOD of location\n- Once released by support; technician approved to leave site. But must call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* service desk if support does not transfer.\n\n**NOTE:** \\*\\*\\* WE CANNOT PAY YOU FOR YOUR WORK WITHOUT A RELEASE CODE FROM THE REMOTE SUPPORT TECHNICIAN \\*\\*\\*\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Work Order Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times (attached document or electronically).\n- Picture of any equipment work was completed on, damaged cables/equipment, etc\n- Picture of RMA form &amp; return label applied; if applicable\n- Release Code\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\nPrepare tool bag/box with the following:\n\n- Laptop (Windows 11)\n- Operating system must be fully licensed and updated\n- · Administrative rights required for software installation and troubleshooting\n- Basic IT Tools\n- Buttset\n- Network Testing Tools/Cable Testers\n- Drill\n- 12\" bit for wood/medal/or possibly concrete\n- 8' Ladder\n- Phone/Ethernet Wiring\n- Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n- Copy of work order and job information\n- Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\nEnsure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:\n\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n- Netfor name badge\n- Close toe shoes\n- Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.\n\n**Contact Name &amp; Number: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**\n\n**Monthly Password: (SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFO)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-07T10:00","end":"2026-11-07T14:00","latestStart":"2026-11-07T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":240},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":20.339280025166413},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Sat, Nov 7, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Nov 9, Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794009200177}
{"job":{"id":20326784,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Cortland Midtown East The Avenues - AP troubleshooting  #328310","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong>&nbsp;<em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Raleigh NC 27604</em></p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.</em></p><p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW):</strong>&nbsp;Troubleshoot AP.AP is offline. Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired.</p><p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong>&nbsp;to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li><li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</li><li><strong>Represent the brand</strong>&nbsp;with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li><li><strong>Do not overshare technical or internal details</strong>with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.</li></ul><p>⚠️&nbsp;<em>If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></p><p><strong>Required Experience:</strong></p><ul><li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)</li><li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li><li>Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination</li></ul><p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)</li></ul><p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p><ul><li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li><li>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.</li></ul><p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p><p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p><p>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</p><ul><li>Why This Matters:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li><li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li></ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** *Raleigh NC 27604*\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW):** Troubleshoot AP.AP is offline. Ethernet port activation. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Contact the customer at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to provide an accurate estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit. Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare technical or internal details**with the customer—keep communication clear, courteous, and focused only on what is necessary for the customer to understand.\n\n⚠️ *If the customer is misinformed, the technician arrives unprepared, demonstrates poor presentation, or performs substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience:**\n\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Ethernet tools (RJ45 crimper, Ethernet stripper, RJ45 connectors)\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\nIt is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T09:00","end":"2026-11-09T11:00","latestStart":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.679453517544362},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794010005269}
{"job":{"id":"5209676726","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Hajoca - PC593-Zebulon (HS) - Rollout - Edgeboot/Peplink Install - Network Survey - CO","description":"BEFORE ARRIVAL. ENSURE TECHNICIAN READS THRU ATTACHED HAJOCA RUNBOOK OUTLINING INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS, SURVEY DOCUMENTATION, SUPPORT CONTACTS AND NETWORK DIAGRAMS<br><br>TECH MUST HAVE A COPY OF RUNBOOK WHEN ARRIVING ONSITE<br><br>TECH MUST COMPLETE Hajoca Network Survey Doc to be submitted along with photos to Granite PM Michael Joyce - 617-837-5180 or 617-356-3131 - mjoyce@granitenet.com <br><br>See Click Link to Smartsheet form for Network Survey:<br>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/01a18b0eadf170679f948ab89a2cdf51<br><br>Description:<br>Technician needed to assist with support the successful installation of SD-WAN equipment, Granite Edgeboot device, and the turn-up and cutover of one (1) new broadband circuit<br><br>Upon completion, tech will assist with performing network survey and submitting as deliverables attached Survey Sheet along with requested photos (see picture angle instruction)<br><br>Mark up to best of ability a floor map with location of MPOE, Any MDF or IDF locations, Camera locations, IoT devices and Access Points.<br><br>Verify all devices and new circuit are online with both client IT and Granite Activations<br><br>Escalation Contact Tier List:<br>Broadband circuit Issues/Support - Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 1 <br>Edgeboot Issues/Support - Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 2 <br>Peplink Issues/Support - Granite Activations: 888-860-1159, option 3 <br>Meraki Issues/Support - Granite Meraki Team: 844-478-6621 <br>Client IT Issues/Support - Hajoca - network@hajoca.com <br>General support Issues/Support - Granite NOC (24/7/365) - 844-478-6621 <br><br>Hajoca IT Contacts:<br>Brendon Luu - 484-604-8766 - brendon.luu@hajoca.com <br>Doug Torone - 610-472-0485 - Doug.torone@hajoca.com <br>Matt McAuliff - 484-708-1834 - matt.mcauliff@hajoca.com <br>Hajoca Network Team - network@hajoca.com <br><br><br>Scope of work:<br><br>**STEP 1 - Locate Equipment and Test New Granite Circuit - Call Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 1 for support**<br><br>On arrival, tech will meet with local contact David Troutner 919-269-7496 and locate peplink and edgeboot devices shipped to site. If unable to locate, call Granite PM Mike Joyce 617-356-3131<br><br>After locating equipment, tech will locate new Spectrum - 500 MBPS/20 MBPS, Dynamic, COAX<br><br>Primary Circuit ID: 8349100060075489<br>Primary Circuit LAN IP: TBD<br>Primary Circuit LAN GW: TBD<br>Primary Circuit LAN SM: TBD<br>Primary Circuit DNS 1: 209.18.47.61<br>Primary Circuit DNS 2: 209.18.47.62<br>Primary Circuit Modem MAC: 90:AA:C3:0F:A4:E8<br><br>Tech will test circuit with Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 1 prior to cutover<br><br>Disable laptop Wi-Fi and confirm no other internet connection is active.<br><br>Power on the new circuit modem <br><br>Confirm the new modem is powered on and sync’d (LEDs stable). <br><br>Connect a laptop directly to the modem and verify sync / surf. <br><br>Run speed tests and record the results. Ensure speed is at least 85% of provisioned speed; contact Granite Broadband Activations if not. <br><br>Label the modem with the circuit ID and “Granite.” <br><br>Take photos: wide angle of the modem / circuit, close-up of the modem / circuit, and the handoff extension if applicable. <br><br>Document static IP information (if applicable) and provide it to the Hajoca network team <br><br><br>**STEP 2 - Install Edgeboot Device - Call Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 2 for support**<br><br>Locate Edgeboot device. Edgeboot will supply power to the Meraki MX, Meraki Switch (only 1 of them), ISP Modem, and Peplink cell gateway. (See Appendix I – Edgeboot Power and Network Diagram at bottom of runbook)<br><br>Edgeboot is cabled across three sections of this runbook, so the full assignment is shown here for reference.<br><br>Power Outlet 1 - Meraki MX router - Always Powered On - Section 7.2 <br>Power Outlet 2  - Meraki MS switch - Always Powered On - Section 7.2 <br>Power Outlet 3  - ISP modem  - Powered On but Auto-reboot on ETH1 Internet connectivity loss - Section 5.1 <br>Power Outlet 4 - Peplink cellular gateway - Always Powered On - Section 6.1 <br><br>Position the Granite Edgeboot in the rack. Do not power on the Edgeboot yet. <br><br>Attach the LTE paddle antenna to the front-left of the Edgeboot. <br><br>Connect ETH1 on the Granite Edgeboot directly to the new ISP circuit’s modem (any available LAN port on modem). <br><br>Connect the power cable on the new ISP circuit modem to Power Outlet 3 on the Edgeboot. <br><br>Find the APC battery backup unit (use a wall outlet if none has been installed yet) and power on the Granite Edgeboot. The Granite Edgeboot should be directly connected to the APC battery unit. <br><br>Wait a few minutes (around 2 minutes) and confirm that the Edgeboot comes online, and that the new ISP modem stays online. <br><br>NOTE —  The Edgeboot template in the Edgeboot portal sets Power Outlet 3 to toggle the power if interface ETH1 on the Edgeboot cannot reach the Internet. This is intentional and is a means to auto-reboot the modem if the modem loses Internet connectivity. <br><br>Check the LTE status LED on the front of the Edgeboot: <br><br>Blue or Green = Online / Good signal. <br><br>If LTE is red or flashing, reposition the unit or call Granite before proceeding. <br><br>Connect ETH0 on the Edgeboot to LAN2 on the Peplink Cellular gateway (see section 6 below for Peplink install) <br><br><br>**STEP 3 - Install Peplink Cellular Gateway - Call Granite Activations: 888-860-1159, option 3 for support**<br><br>Locate Peplink 5G cellular gateway. Gateway provides the backup WAN path into the Meraki MX on Internet 2, and can also be managed over a dedicated link back to the Meraki switch in addition to the regular cellular management. (See Appendix I – Edgeboot Power and Network Diagram at bottom of runbook)<br><br>Peplink Port  - Connects To - Purpose <br>LAN1  - Meraki MX Internet 2 - Backup WAN into the MX <br>LAN2 - Edgeboot ETH0 (chassis PORT 0) - Edgeboot Connectivity <br>3/WAN - Meraki MS switchport 24/48 (disabled) - Peplink management <br><br>Position the Peplink cell gateway at the top of the rack, or mount it high on the wall if possible. Screw the antennas onto the Peplink. <br><br>Connect the power cable from the Peplink to power PORT 4 on the Edgeboot. (See the diagram in Appendix C.) <br><br>Connect interface ETH0 on the Edgeboot — labeled PORT 0 on the chassis — to LAN2 on the Peplink cell gateway. <br><br>Connect Peplink LAN1 → Meraki MX Internet 2. <br><br>In a situation where a MX67W model firewall is being retained (the Meraki cutover has not been performed yet), LAN port 2 needs to be converted to WAN by Granite Meraki team <br><br>NOTE —  Older model Meraki routers (model MX64(W) and MX67(W)) only have an Internet1 interface and no Internet 2 interface. Granite Meraki team needs to convert a LAN port to WAN to create an Internet2 interface. This is done in the Meraki management portal. <br><br>NOTE – The Peplink should be configured for IP Passthrough mode. The Granite Peplink team sets this setting in the Peplink management portal <br><br>Connect Peplink 3/WAN → Meraki MS switchport 48. Let Granite Meraki team know which port you use if it is different from 48. This is the Peplink management link — the purple line in Appendix<br><br>Have Granite Meraki team verify Peplink is connected to cellular and on 5G via the Peplink Management dashboard <br><br>NOTE —  Granite Meraki team should disable the Meraki switchport (typically port 48) that connects to Peplink 3/WAN. This is merely used as a management leg and an alternative method to access the Peplink should the cell connectivity be unavailable. Should cell connectivity be unavailable the port can be re-enabled and access opened to make the necessary changes to the Peplink to restore cell connectivity. This port should be configured for VLAN 248 (Guest) <br><br><br>**STEP 4 - Circuit Cutover/Installation - Call Granite Activations: 877-855-1146, option 1**<br><br>This phase installs and validates the new ISP circuit. <br><br>Granite Meraki team will need to configure new static IP on MX Internet 1 (WAN1) interface (Warning this will cause an outage at the location so warn the PCM ahead of time) <br><br>Remove the old circuit from MX Internet 1 interface <br><br>Connect the new circuit to MX Internet 1 interface <br><br>Verify Meraki LED is solid White or Green (contact Granite Meraki team if not) <br><br><br>**STEP 5 - Network Survey and verifying completion with Hajoca Support**<br><br>Tech needs to  produce a complete picture of the entire location's network infrastructure so that equipment, cabling, and vendor coordination can be arranged in advance.<br><br>Work through the Site Survey Checklist in Section 3.2 and document every answer. <br><br>Submit rack pictures to Hajoca I.T. for review and validation. <br><br>Based on the results of the survey, the site may need a variety of equipment replaced. Any non-Meraki switching will need to be replaced and/or consolidated into Meraki switching. <br><br>If any Meraki MG21 cellular gateways are found those will need replaced with a Peplink. <br><br>Any of the MX firewalls or access points listed in the firewall and access point replacement schedule in Appendix E will need to be replaced with the replacement model shown there. Appendix E is the authoritative copy of that schedule.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-16T09:00","end":"2026-11-16T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":21.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":70,"baseAmount":280,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":40,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (21.5mi reported + 10mi padding = 31.5mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1794010601476}
{"job":{"id":"5656744005","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Kinettix","title":"FSDP-2702-276671 | Replace pogo and interface boards on dispenser 2 | Fayetteville Health Care Center (NC)","description":"<p><strong>SITE NAME: </strong>Fayetteville Health Care Center (NC)</p><p><strong>SITE ADDRESS: </strong>7300 South Raeford Road, Fayetteville, NC</p><p><strong>DATE AND TIME: </strong>11/09/2026 10:00 AM</p><p><strong>ScriptPro Request Ticket Number: </strong>1-1152927020</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope Of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Replace pogo and interface boards on dispenser 2. Pull 1 Dispensers of vials, Watch 5 scripts specifically from dispenser adjusted</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>NOTE: </u></strong></p><p>PLEASE MAKE SURE THAT YOU ARE INSIDE THE PHARMACY AND HAVE MET THE PHARMACY MANAGER.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>STRICT DRESS CODE IN EFFECT: </u></strong></p><p>Business casual attire is required. Polo/button up and Khakis</p><p><br></p><p><strong>NOT PERMITTED:</strong> Hoodies, Cargo Pants, Hats, or any clothing with excessive pockets or a baggy fit.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>NOTE:</u></strong><u> </u></p><p><strong>NO TAKING VIDEOS OR PHOTOS OF ANY PERSONAL OR CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION AT THE SITE AS IT IS PROHIBITED.</strong> You will be prompted by either the Kinettix or ScriptPro team if a photograph is needed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PRE-VISIT REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Find your ScriptPro Service Request Number.</li></ul><p>Example: 1-947115556</p><ul><li>Access the ScriptPro Website and have the procedures with you either in printed form or downloaded onto your electronic device for quick reference.</li><li>Procedures must be reviewed before going onsite?no exceptions.</li><li>Your Company Photo ID Badge. It may be need to surrendered to the site and returned after the visit.</li><li>If applicable, have a copy of your HIPAA &amp; VA Certifications with you, either in printed form or downloaded on your device.</li><li>All tools listed at the bottom of this work order/email should be with you while onsite.</li><li>Verify parts are onsite using provided tracking information before traveling to the customer's location.</li><li>Never call the customer directly. All communication will be handled by ScriptPro with the end user.</li><li>Technicians are strictly prohibited from bringing another technician, helper, trainee, or family member onsite.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Standard hex key set (Allen wrenches)</li><li>Metric hex key set (Allen wrenches)</li><li>T-handle hex keys (3mm and 4mm)</li><li>7mm socket wrench</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Large flat-head screwdriver</li><li>Small flat-head screwdriver</li><li>Large Phillips-head screwdriver</li><li>Small Phillips-head screwdriver</li><li>Small ratchet</li><li>et with sockets (standard and metric)</li><li>Electrical tape</li><li>Vise grip pliers</li><li>Needle-nose pliers</li><li>Voltage meter (does not need to be expensive)</li><li>Grounding wrist strap</li><li>Basic Maintenance Tools</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T10:00","end":"2026-11-09T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794012230634}
{"job":{"id":20326950,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walgreens - Fuji CX3240F Duplex Printer - Grinding Noise Troubleshooting - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240F xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>DO NOT INSTALL PARTS CALL SUPPORT FIRST <br /><br />Transfer roller had some rattling </p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Fujifilm CX3240F Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Gloves</li><li>Microfiber Cleaning Cloth</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Badge ID (document attached to work order)</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li><strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;the \"<strong>PARTS CONFIRMATION</strong>\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>go to the&nbsp;<strong>SHIPMENT FIELD</strong>&nbsp;of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date.&nbsp;Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time.&nbsp;<strong>IF</strong>&nbsp;parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ********</del></span>&nbsp;to determine if you should&nbsp;<strong>continue onsite</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>reschedule</strong>.</li><li>Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p>California Ink &amp; Toner Waste Compliance Requirements</p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a&nbsp;<strong>production print to verify the printer functionality.</strong></li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>Support Team</strong>&nbsp;<strong>at&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***</del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***</del></span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to confirm deliverables and&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li>The parts return packages must be dropped off at the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup counter&nbsp;</strong>inside the Walgreens location<strong>.&nbsp;</strong>You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, and obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature.</strong></li></ol><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><ul><li>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.</li><li>Image of the printer prior to service start.</li><li>If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.</li><li>Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.</li><li>If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the <strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>, <strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>, <strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong> and <strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li><li>If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <del>***** ********</del> and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to represent Fujifilm Technical Services at Walgreens locations servicing the CX3240F xerography printer located in the Photo Center. This will include troubleshooting the operations of the printer with our support team based on the specific service notes below and replacement of any parts sent that we determine are needed to resolve the issue.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nDO NOT INSTALL PARTS CALL SUPPORT FIRST   \n  \nTransfer roller had some rattling\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Fujifilm CX3240F Printer Support Documents (Attached to Work Order)\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Gloves\n- Microfiber Cleaning Cloth\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Toner Vacuum (preferred but not required)\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Badge ID (document attached to work order)\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. **IF** the \"**PARTS CONFIRMATION**\" section at the top of the service description indicates parts were shipped**,** go to the **SHIPMENT FIELD** of the work order, click the tracking number link to the shipper's website and verify the scheduled delivery date. Set your schedule based on the parts expected arrival time. **IF** parts are delayed or there is no tracking, send a message through the work order or contact the support team \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to determine if you should **continue onsite** or **reschedule**.\n3. Watch any training video links (if provided below) and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Walgreens Tray Settings and 4 Tray Test Instructions:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCalifornia Ink &amp; Toner Waste Compliance Requirements\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n2. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n3. Contact the **Support Team at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm the troubleshooting steps required to diagnose the issue.\n4. Complete the required service and perform verification testing, including a **production print to verify the printer functionality.**\n5. Contact the **Support Team** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*** to confirm deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n6. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n7. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n8. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n9. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n10. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n11. The parts return packages must be dropped off at the **FedEx pickup counter** inside the Walgreens location**.** You will need to have them scan the labels and provide a receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval.\n12. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, and obtain their **signature.**\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n- <https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order completed and signed by Manager on Duty with name notated.\n- Image of the printer prior to service start.\n- If the issue is resolved, images of test prints and a nozzle check test must be provided showing good quality.\n- Image of the printer showing the condition it was left in after service was completed.\n- If parts were received a screenshot of the Fujifilm Part Return App of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return.\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n- If parts are not being returned, a picture of the unused return label destroyed.\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T11:00","end":"2026-11-09T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-09T18:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":46.38450343486161},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"20