{"job":{"id":20327381,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"*LIFT OPERATIONS REQ'D* Run new data cabling for price checker(s) - Tech 1","description":{"html":"A second tech will be dispatched on a separate work order.  A lift will be ordered. <br/><br/>Techs will need to run new data cabling for the store's price checker(s).   Work with the MOD for the price checker locations.  <br/><br/>Note:  Some stores may already have the price checkers installed, but they need to be relocated.<br/><br/>At the MDF, terminate the data cable to the patch panel.  Coordinate with the end user's support team for a switch port assignment. <br/><br/>On the price checker side, terminate the data cable to a data jack/biscuit box, and patch in the price checker.  The price checker works via POE.<br/><br/>The price checker will need to be tested with the end user's support bridge.  <br/><br/>REQUIRED TOOLS<br/>- Fish rods<br/>- Fish tape<br/>- Punchdown tool with a 110 blade <br/>- Data cabling tester (must say \"Pass\" / \"Fail\")<br/>- Tone generator with probe<br/>- Snips<br/>- Metric Allen wrench set with 2.5mm and 4mm keys<br/>- Tape measure<br/>- Torpedo level<br/>- Basic hand tools<br/>- Smartphone capable of joining a Microsoft Teams support bridge<br/><br/>REQUIRED MATERIALS<br/>- 8\" or longer tie wraps <br/>- Roll of Velcro<br/>- Roll of electrical tape<br/><br/>DRESS CODE<br/>- Polo shirt<br/>- Jeans or khaki pants (no shorts)<br/><br/>DISPATCH GUIDELINES<br/>- Only confirmed technicians are authorized to be onsite for an activity/dispatch.<br/>- Any scheduling or tech assignment requests/changes must receive prior approval.<br/>- Furthermore, additional technicians and/or supervisors are not authorized to accompany assigned tech(s) onsite at any time without prior approval.<br/><br/>**MUST SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION SECTION / SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS FOR WORK INSTRUCTIONS**","markdown":"A second tech will be dispatched on a separate work order. A lift will be ordered.   \n  \nTechs will need to run new data cabling for the store's price checker(s). Work with the MOD for the price checker locations.   \n  \nNote: Some stores may already have the price checkers installed, but they need to be relocated.  \n  \nAt the MDF, terminate the data cable to the patch panel. Coordinate with the end user's support team for a switch port assignment.   \n  \nOn the price checker side, terminate the data cable to a data jack/biscuit box, and patch in the price checker. The price checker works via POE.  \n  \nThe price checker will need to be tested with the end user's support bridge.   \n  \nREQUIRED TOOLS  \n\\- Fish rods  \n\\- Fish tape  \n\\- Punchdown tool with a 110 blade   \n\\- Data cabling tester (must say \"Pass\" / \"Fail\")  \n\\- Tone generator with probe  \n\\- Snips  \n\\- Metric Allen wrench set with 2.5mm and 4mm keys  \n\\- Tape measure  \n\\- Torpedo level  \n\\- Basic hand tools  \n\\- Smartphone capable of joining a Microsoft Teams support bridge  \n  \nREQUIRED MATERIALS  \n\\- 8\" or longer tie wraps   \n\\- Roll of Velcro  \n\\- Roll of electrical tape  \n  \nDRESS CODE  \n\\- Polo shirt  \n\\- Jeans or khaki pants (no shorts)  \n  \nDISPATCH GUIDELINES  \n\\- Only confirmed technicians are authorized to be onsite for an activity/dispatch.  \n\\- Any scheduling or tech assignment requests/changes must receive prior approval.  \n\\- Furthermore, additional technicians and/or supervisors are not authorized to accompany assigned tech(s) onsite at any time without prior approval.  \n  \n\\*\\*MUST SEE CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION SECTION / SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS FOR WORK INSTRUCTIONS\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-20T07:00","end":"2026-11-20T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":165,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":3,"amount":165},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":45.48472282930638},"result":{