{"job":{"id":20330650,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Atleos","title":"British Telecom - Onsite  Installation | Estimated 8 hours onsite | Cisco experience preferred","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.</strong></li><li><strong>Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store&nbsp;turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;&nbsp;</strong>must be checked-in on time per the&nbsp;<strong>original&nbsp;</strong>time log.</li><li>o <strong>If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival</strong>:</li><li>§ <em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>§ <em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;- If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>o <strong>If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival</strong>:</li><li>o <em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>o <em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong><u>SCOPE OVERVIEW</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: red;\"><u>﻿</u>PLEASE NOTE BECAUSE OF DATA PRIVACY WE SHARED THE NEARBY ADDRESS OF THE LOCATION IN THE WO, ONCE THE WO IS ACCEPTED THE FULL ACTUAL ADDRESS, END CUSTOMER NAME AND LOCAL CONTACT WILL BE ADDED IN THE WO.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">THE SCOPE AND REQUIREMENTS ARE LISTED , THIS WILL NOT CHANGE WITH THE ASSIGNMENT.</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS MANDATORY TO HAVE ONSITE!</strong></li></ul><p>Laptop with Webex and Putty apps already installed and working. Also Laptop enabled to join to MS Teams bridge.</p><p>USB drive (4/8 GB) - FAT format</p><p>Mobile phone with data available for calls and whatsapp</p><p>Console cable and spare to connect to C8300 and C8200 Cisco routers</p><p>UTP straight and crossed patch cords</p><ul><li>Labeling machine</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><u>Dress Code</u></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Casual Business:&nbsp;Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse.&nbsp;Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans.&nbsp;Close toed shoes or boots</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes</span></li></ul><p><u>Equipment</u></p><ul><li>Laptop + Charger</li><li>Cisco Console cable</li><li>USB drive</li><li>Mobile Hotspot</li><li>Networking Tool kit</li><li>Microsoft Teams</li><li>WEBEX</li><li>Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)</li><li>Newest updated drivers</li><li>Label Maker</li></ul><p><u>Expectations</u></p><ul><li>Timely Arrival</li><li>Read scope and escalation path carefully.</li><li>Any out-of-scope work requires work order manager approval.</li></ul><p><u>Onsite:</u></p><ul><li>Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.</li><li>Take a picture of the rack before installation begins.</li><li>Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory.</li><li>Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed.</li><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS A MUST !</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Laptop with Webex and Putty apps already installed and working. Also Laptop enabled to join to MS Teams bridge.</p><p>USB drive (4/8 GB) - FAT format</p><p>Mobile phone with data available for calls and whatsapp</p><p>Console cable and spare to connect to C8300 and C8200 Cisco routers</p><p>UTP straight and crossed patch cords</p><p>Labeling machine</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Fill out the Device Information custom field section below.</li><li>Take a picture of installed component in rack.</li><li>Break down and dispose of all packaging waste.</li><li>Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative.</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED</u></strong></p><ul><li>Picture of rack before work begins.</li><li>Picture of each installed component's serial number</li><li>Each serial number entered into a custom field.</li><li>Picture of rack after installation is complete.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Level 1 Escalation -Installation Coordinator: <del>** ******* **** *</del><del>**************************** *** *** *** ****</del><del> </del>Any onsite escalation ( Example: late arrival, site contact not onsite, team bridge check in problems, etc)</li><li>Level 2 Escalation -Project Manager: <strong><del>*** ****** ****** ** * </del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(27, 30, 31);\"><del>**************</del>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span> - in case Level 1 not responding -30 min</li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES:**\n\n- **EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.**\n- **Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;** must be checked-in on time per the **original** time log.\n- o **If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival**:\n- § *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- § *Fixed Rate* - If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- o **If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival**:\n- o *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- o *Fixed Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n\n- **SCOPE OVERVIEW**\n\n**﻿PLEASE NOTE BECAUSE OF DATA PRIVACY WE SHARED THE NEARBY ADDRESS OF THE LOCATION IN THE WO, ONCE THE WO IS ACCEPTED THE FULL ACTUAL ADDRESS, END CUSTOMER NAME AND LOCAL CONTACT WILL BE ADDED IN THE WO.**\n\n**THE SCOPE AND REQUIREMENTS ARE LISTED , THIS WILL NOT CHANGE WITH THE ASSIGNMENT.**\n\n- **GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS MANDATORY TO HAVE ONSITE!**\n\nLaptop with Webex and Putty apps already installed and working. Also Laptop enabled to join to MS Teams bridge.\n\nUSB drive (4/8 GB) - FAT format\n\nMobile phone with data available for calls and whatsapp\n\nConsole cable and spare to connect to C8300 and C8200 Cisco routers\n\nUTP straight and crossed patch cords\n\n- Labeling machine\n\n**REQUIREMENTS**\n\nDress Code\n\n- Casual Business: Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse. Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans. Close toed shoes or boots\n- Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes\n\nEquipment\n\n- Laptop + Charger\n- Cisco Console cable\n- USB drive\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Networking Tool kit\n- Microsoft Teams\n- WEBEX\n- Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)\n- Newest updated drivers\n- Label Maker\n\nExpectations\n\n- Timely Arrival\n- Read scope and escalation path carefully.\n- Any out-of-scope work requires work order manager approval.\n\nOnsite:\n\n- Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.\n- Take a picture of the rack before installation begins.\n- Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory.\n- Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed.\n- **GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS A MUST !**\n\nLaptop with Webex and Putty apps already installed and working. Also Laptop enabled to join to MS Teams bridge.\n\nUSB drive (4/8 GB) - FAT format\n\nMobile phone with data available for calls and whatsapp\n\nConsole cable and spare to connect to C8300 and C8200 Cisco routers\n\nUTP straight and crossed patch cords\n\nLabeling machine\n\n- Fill out the Device Information custom field section below.\n- Take a picture of installed component in rack.\n- Break down and dispose of all packaging waste.\n- Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative.\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED**\n\n- Picture of rack before work begins.\n- Picture of each installed component's serial number\n- Each serial number entered into a custom field.\n- Picture of rack after installation is complete.\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- Level 1 Escalation -Installation Coordinator: \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* Any onsite escalation ( Example: late arrival, site contact not onsite, team bridge check in problems, etc)\n- Level 2 Escalation -Project Manager: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*  - in case Level 1 not responding -30 min","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T08:45","end":"2026-11-17T16:45"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":440},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":62.002583336645614},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Nov 17, 8:45 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 17, Wed, Nov 18, Thu, Nov 19, Fri, Nov 20 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orki