{"job":{"id":20312579,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Replacing a PC within a retail clothing store - 2hr estimate","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>***MAY REQUIRE REVISITS ON THE SAME WORK ORDER, please see attached document REVISIT INFORMATION for further information***</u></strong></p>\n<p>SPECIAL NOTES</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>---- TECH MUST READ TECH BULLETINS ON PC CONFIGURATION!! DO NOT CALL ROSS HELP DESK FOR HELP ON CONFIGURATION!! ---</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>----- TECH MUST ESCALATE TO THE BAILIWICK PM IF THEY ARE WAITING MORE THEN 30 MINUTES FOR THE ROSS HELPDESK TO RETURN CALL!---</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>**TECHNICIAN&nbsp;GLOVES ARE RECOMMENDED.**</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>***Check IN &amp; OUT with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227 ***</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>• Technician must be prepared with INC # and badge when checking in with MOD.</p>\n<p>• Technician must check in with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press&nbsp;option 5 before starting replacement. Calling Ross Help Desk is to validate the PC is online. This Help Desk is not for troubleshooting purposes. Do not call Ross Help Desk for PC configuration instructions. Read your documentation.</p>\n<p>• Technician must call the Ross Help Desk if there are store access issues.</p>\n<p>• Technician must validate PC is functional with Ross Help Desk and store manager before leaving site.</p>\n<p>• Technician must have manual, console cable, putty.exe and laptop! No exceptions.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>• Store will execute \"Code 50\" Search before tech leaves site.</p>\n<p>• The failed PC will need to be shipped back to BW via ATR.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>ONSITE SCOPE</p>\n<p>Ross INC: INC4527961</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Problem Description: does not turn on</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Device Location: Break Room</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Troubleshooting Performed: unplug it and unplug it back in after a few min, issue persists.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Instructions for Technician: Instructions for Technician: Replace the PC and install the provided surge protector. Connect the PC and monitor to the Tripp Lite surge protector. If the HP Engage Flex Mini G2 is already connected to a surge protector (MAKE SURE IT A SURGE PROTECTOR NOT JUST A POWER STRIP):</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>VERY IMPORTANT: Please review the documentation and install the PC on the back of the monitor as shown in the reference photos under the Documents section also shown in in the manual.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If an HP Engage Flex Mini G2 is NOT connected to a surge protector:</p>\n<p>*Take a before photo showing the current power connection and outlet.</p>\n<p>*Shut down the PC.</p>\n<p>*Connect the PC to one of the new surge protectors.</p>\n<p>*Plug the surge protector into the orange outlet.</p>\n<p>*Take an after photo showing the completed installation, including the surge protector and outlet connection.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>If no orange outlet is available:</p>\n<p>*Take a photo of the outlet currently being used.</p>\n<p>*Check the surrounding area for a nearby orange outlet.</p>\n<p>*If an orange outlet is available and within reach, use that outlet.</p>\n<p>*If no orange outlet can be found, document this in your notes and provide photos of the&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;available outlets.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Point of Contact: MOD</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Current device type/model: HP&nbsp;Engage Flex Mini G2</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Part Shipped: Labeled \"hold in office for tech\"&nbsp;</p>\n<p>(1) D32FSUP-ROS&nbsp;&nbsp;HP&nbsp;Engage Flex Mini G2</p>\n<p>(1) TLP74RB -ROS</p>\n<p>Pwr Strp;Tripp Lite, 7 Outlet Blk&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;PC3 breakroom \"Breakroom PC Windows Image\"</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please upload all photos and documentation required in the&nbsp;deliverables upon completion.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>• Check in with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227</p>\n<p>• Introduce yourself to the site contact and review the scope of work that you will be performing at the site</p>\n<p>• Technician must check in with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press option 5</p>\n<p>• Before proceeding with PC replacement, tech must take a photo of the current PC and cable layout.</p>\n<p>• Tech must follow the steps included in the \"Ross Managed Services Replacement Installation\" document.</p>\n<p>• Tech must validate PC is online with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press option 5</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;Tech must package up the existing device (reusing the box and packing material the new device arrived in), affix a preprinted FedEx return label, and drop off at a FedEx pickup location. Bailiwick will confirm these tasks are complete at the Technician Checkout.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*** Check OUT with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227 ***</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>*** ALL PARTS NEED TO BE RETURNED TO BAILIWICK &gt; DO NOT LEAVE ON SITE***</p>\n<p>All parts, whether new or used, must be returned to Bailiwick using the return label included in the box. If you cannot locate the return label, please notify the Service Desk (SD) during checkout so a replacement label can be emailed to you</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT RETURN (ATR)</p>\n<p>• (1) old pc</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>DELIVERABLES</p>\n<p>• The required deliverable photos for this work order will be between 5 and 10.&nbsp;Specific deliverable requirements will be found in the Installation Manual and/or PR Checklist within the Fieldpoint VPP or Mobile Application.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>TOOL REQUIREMENTS</p>\n<p>• Industry standard tools</p>\n<p>• Installation Manual and sign off sheet</p>\n<p>• Screw drivers (misc. sizes and types)</p>\n<p>• Drill Driver with assorted bits</p>\n<p>• Label maker for tagging cables</p>\n<p>• Laptop with a copy of Putty.exe installed</p>\n<p>• Cisco console cable that works with your computer</p>\n<p>• Internet Hot Spot in case remote assistance is needed</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>MATERIALS LIST</p>\n<p>• N/A</p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*MAY REQUIRE REVISITS ON THE SAME WORK ORDER, please see attached document REVISIT INFORMATION for further information\\*\\*\\***\n\nSPECIAL NOTES\n\n\\---- TECH MUST READ TECH BULLETINS ON PC CONFIGURATION!! DO NOT CALL ROSS HELP DESK FOR HELP ON CONFIGURATION!! ---\n\n\\----- TECH MUST ESCALATE TO THE BAILIWICK PM IF THEY ARE WAITING MORE THEN 30 MINUTES FOR THE ROSS HELPDESK TO RETURN CALL!---\n\n\\*\\*TECHNICIAN GLOVES ARE RECOMMENDED.\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*Check IN &amp; OUT with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227 \\*\\*\\*\n\n• Technician must be prepared with INC # and badge when checking in with MOD.\n\n• Technician must check in with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press option 5 before starting replacement. Calling Ross Help Desk is to validate the PC is online. This Help Desk is not for troubleshooting purposes. Do not call Ross Help Desk for PC configuration instructions. Read your documentation.\n\n• Technician must call the Ross Help Desk if there are store access issues.\n\n• Technician must validate PC is functional with Ross Help Desk and store manager before leaving site.\n\n• Technician must have manual, console cable, putty.exe and laptop! No exceptions.\n\n• Store will execute \"Code 50\" Search before tech leaves site.\n\n• The failed PC will need to be shipped back to BW via ATR.\n\nONSITE SCOPE\n\nRoss INC: INC4527961\n\nProblem Description: does not turn on\n\nDevice Location: Break Room\n\nTroubleshooting Performed: unplug it and unplug it back in after a few min, issue persists.\n\nInstructions for Technician: Instructions for Technician: Replace the PC and install the provided surge protector. Connect the PC and monitor to the Tripp Lite surge protector. If the HP Engage Flex Mini G2 is already connected to a surge protector (MAKE SURE IT A SURGE PROTECTOR NOT JUST A POWER STRIP):\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: Please review the documentation and install the PC on the back of the monitor as shown in the reference photos under the Documents section also shown in in the manual.\n\nIf an HP Engage Flex Mini G2 is NOT connected to a surge protector:\n\n\\*Take a before photo showing the current power connection and outlet.\n\n\\*Shut down the PC.\n\n\\*Connect the PC to one of the new surge protectors.\n\n\\*Plug the surge protector into the orange outlet.\n\n\\*Take an after photo showing the completed installation, including the surge protector and outlet connection.\n\nIf no orange outlet is available:\n\n\\*Take a photo of the outlet currently being used.\n\n\\*Check the surrounding area for a nearby orange outlet.\n\n\\*If an orange outlet is available and within reach, use that outlet.\n\n\\*If no orange outlet can be found, document this in your notes and provide photos of the available outlets.\n\nPoint of Contact: MOD\n\nCurrent device type/model: HP Engage Flex Mini G2\n\nPart Shipped: Labeled \"hold in office for tech\"\n\n(1) D32FSUP-ROS HP Engage Flex Mini G2\n\n(1) TLP74RB -ROS\n\nPwr Strp;Tripp Lite, 7 Outlet Blk\n\n PC3 breakroom \"Breakroom PC Windows Image\"\n\nPlease upload all photos and documentation required in the deliverables upon completion.\n\n• Check in with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227\n\n• Introduce yourself to the site contact and review the scope of work that you will be performing at the site\n\n• Technician must check in with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press option 5\n\n• Before proceeding with PC replacement, tech must take a photo of the current PC and cable layout.\n\n• Tech must follow the steps included in the \"Ross Managed Services Replacement Installation\" document.\n\n• Tech must validate PC is online with Ross Onshore L2 Help Desk (925) 965-4357 press option 5\n\n• Tech must package up the existing device (reusing the box and packing material the new device arrived in), affix a preprinted FedEx return label, and drop off at a FedEx pickup location. Bailiwick will confirm these tasks are complete at the Technician Checkout.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Check OUT with the Bailiwick Service Desk at 866.777.3227 \\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* ALL PARTS NEED TO BE RETURNED TO BAILIWICK &gt; DO NOT LEAVE ON SITE\\*\\*\\*\n\nAll parts, whether new or used, must be returned to Bailiwick using the return label included in the box. If you cannot locate the return label, please notify the Service Desk (SD) during checkout so a replacement label can be emailed to you\n\nMATERIALS / EQUIPMENT RETURN (ATR)\n\n• (1) old pc\n\nDELIVERABLES\n\n• The required deliverable photos for this work order will be between 5 and 10. Specific deliverable requirements will be found in the Installation Manual and/or PR Checklist within the Fieldpoint VPP or Mobile Application.\n\nTOOL REQUIREMENTS\n\n• Industry standard tools\n\n• Installation Manual and sign off sheet\n\n• Screw drivers (misc. sizes and types)\n\n• Drill Driver with assorted bits\n\n• Label maker for tagging cables\n\n• Laptop with a copy of Putty.exe installed\n\n• Cisco console cable that works with your computer\n\n• Internet Hot Spot in case remote assistance is needed\n\nMATERIALS LIST\n\n• N/A","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T11:00","end":"2026-11-09T15:00","latestStart":"2026-11-09T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":62.96655510521141},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T