{"job":{"id":20329916,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Level 3 Support","title":"** Router Troubleshoot**Configure with Support** Cisco console cable and label maker **","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Before applying for this job please read our company’s terms and condition, under scope of work, <u>applying for this job means that you have red our company’s terms and condition and you are understanding and agrees to it</u>,&nbsp;Failure to follow will result in, late payment, penalties or No payment.</strong></p><p><strong>Please upload all the deliverables before leaving the site.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Tech must have</u></strong> a <strong>laptop, console cable, patch cable,</strong></p><p>- FE should join an intervention on Teams and assist with checking the cabling and the SFP Module.</p><p>- Provide console access for router model C8300-1N1S-4T2X if necessary.</p><p><strong>Tech will assist remote team with troubleshooting the router and will provide the console access to the router to troubleshoot, Please make sure to bring laptop, console cable and listed tools to assist</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>**** ENGINEER EXPECTED ACTION ****</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Bring a Laptop and Cisco console cable with putty installed</strong></li><li><strong>USB thumb drive</strong></li><li><strong>Label maker, Brady or Rhiano</strong></li></ol><p><strong>All actions will be performed after support approval.</strong></p><p><strong>All Tech’s Must carry following tools to responding to Any <del>***** * *******</del> work order.</strong></p><p>All techs must share their email address upon accepting out work orders to get meeting link.</p><p>• Microsoft Teams, any desk and WebEx installed in their laptop prior to arrival onsite. Tech MUST join the meeting<strong><u>using app or dialing LOCAL number</u></strong> and pass-code,</p><p>• Fully charged laptop with charger, Win7 or newer, Full charged phone (camera) with charger &amp; cable</p><p>•Mobile Hotspot or independent LTE modem</p><p>•Cisco Console cable, RJ45 to USB and USB A to USB mini-B, USB A-USB A console cable</p><p>•Spare 16 Gb thumb drive (16GB USB)</p><p>•Spare patch cords-CAT5e</p><p>•Hand drill with sorted bits to install/de-install equipment from rack.</p><p>•Plier, wire cutter, Rj45 crimping tool and network cable tester.</p><p><strong>Please refrain from calling international numbers or receiving calls from international numbers during this activity. if you don't have international roaming, <u>this will not be compensated.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Material Compensation.</u></strong></p><p><strong>We ship All required materials to site before dispatching a technician to site to avoid warranty issues, However, tech must get verbal or written approval for from Rana Ali, prior to using any of his materials.</strong></p><p><strong>We pay $5 for <u>10ft CAT6 cable</u>, $15 <u>for ANY SFP’s</u>-again these needs to <u>approve prior to using.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Check in &amp; Out Policy</u></strong><u>.</u></p><p><u>No early arrival</u> will be accepted for Hard start jobs, you are permitted to check <u>in 5 mints prior</u> to schedule time, from site, upon arrival, you MUST join meeting using provided link and share your status to our remote engineers, you are expected to leave the site <strong>within 15 mints after</strong>completion of the activity or 15 mints after leaving the conference meeting. <strong>Level 3 Engineers closely monitor time logs and may check you out accordingly<u>. Also, you will ONLY get for the time/hours, which you will work onsite, and we closely monitor tech progress while he/she is onsite to avoid any discrepancies.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Policies with Flat Rates.</u></strong></p><p>We always recommend on working on <strong><u>hourly rates</u></strong>; however, we work on flat rates on<strong><u>extreme circumstance</u></strong>, therefore, Tech must not rush things to complete and show compassionate to resolving the problem and work with our teams. <u>All flat rate offers must provide proper rate explanation about how many hours will be covered in flat rates; ‘else we will consider flat is good until JOB FINISHES’.</u> <strong><u>no rate discussions will be approved onsite or during the activity.</u></strong></p><p>Our standard cancellation policy will apply if site cancels, aborts or due to no access <strong><u>(NO FULL TICKET PRICE WILL AWARDED) IN-CASE OF SITE CANCELLATION FOR “FLAT RATE JOBS”.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Parts Return Instructions and RMA Details</strong>.</p><p>Tech will be responsible of dropping Off any unused or old devices (router or switch) to nearest UPS store (NOT UPS HUB or Walgreens or CVS) immediately after completion of the activity,<strong><u>we will pay $25 to drop off the equipment.</u></strong>Before dropping off<strong><u>, tech must upload pictures of old device serial numbers, part numbers and host ID’s and share UPS drop off receipt before closing WO for payment.</u></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>RMA Information:</strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please head to the UPS store, NOT a drop-off location i.e. Walmart or Walgreens</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tell that you are here to drop off equipment and we have a “corporate account”&nbsp;<del>***** ********* ******** ***********</del></p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Then provide the following information, as they request</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Case reference # 183XXXXXXXX</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Program Code:<del>********</del></p><p><strong>Ratings:</strong></p><p>We always give 5-stars ratings to all our techs to encourage them during tough time and we expect that they respect our support team and customer and provide them highest level of service and respect. And we report for those fails to comply with our policies and give us hard time during our activities.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>If travel time, mileage is being requested, must be approved before Job acceptance.&nbsp;<u>Parking and tolls will be reimbursed per receipt,</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>﻿NO EARLY CHECK IN ALLOWED, CHECK IN ONTIME or 5 Mints Prior to start time allowed, OR it will be asked to adjust upon closer of the ticket. There will $50 cancellation for the site with no access or aborts with any reasons. upon tech arrival onsite and upon check in.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**Before applying for this job please read our company’s terms and condition, under scope of work, applying for this job means that you have red our company’s terms and condition and you are understanding and agrees to it, Failure to follow will result in, late payment, penalties or No payment.**\n\n**Please upload all the deliverables before leaving the site.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Tech must have** a **laptop, console cable, patch cable,**\n\n\\- FE should join an intervention on Teams and assist with checking the cabling and the SFP Module.\n\n\\- Provide console access for router model C8300-1N1S-4T2X if necessary.\n\n**Tech will assist remote team with troubleshooting the router and will provide the console access to the router to troubleshoot, Please make sure to bring laptop, console cable and listed tools to assist**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* ENGINEER EXPECTED ACTION \\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n1. **Bring a Laptop and Cisco console cable with putty installed**\n2. **USB thumb drive**\n3. **Label maker, Brady or Rhiano**\n\n**All actions will be performed after support approval.**\n\n**All Tech’s Must carry following tools to responding to Any \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* work order.**\n\nAll techs must share their email address upon accepting out work orders to get meeting link.\n\n• Microsoft Teams, any desk and WebEx installed in their laptop prior to arrival onsite. Tech MUST join the meeting**using app or dialing LOCAL number** and pass-code,\n\n• Fully charged laptop with charger, Win7 or newer, Full charged phone (camera) with charger &amp; cable\n\n•Mobile Hotspot or independent LTE modem\n\n•Cisco Console cable, RJ45 to USB and USB A to USB mini-B, USB A-USB A console cable\n\n•Spare 16 Gb thumb drive (16GB USB)\n\n•Spare patch cords-CAT5e\n\n•Hand drill with sorted bits to install/de-install equipment from rack.\n\n•Plier, wire cutter, Rj45 crimping tool and network cable tester.\n\n**Please refrain from calling international numbers or receiving calls from international numbers during this activity. if you don't have international roaming, this will not be compensated.**\n\n**Material Compensation.**\n\n**We ship All required materials to site before dispatching a technician to site to avoid warranty issues, However, tech must get verbal or written approval for from Rana Ali, prior to using any of his materials.**\n\n**We pay $5 for 10ft CAT6 cable, $15 for ANY SFP’s-again these needs to approve prior to using.**\n\n**Check in &amp; Out Policy**.\n\nNo early arrival will be accepted for Hard start jobs, you are permitted to check in 5 mints prior to schedule time, from site, upon arrival, you MUST join meeting using provided link and share your status to our remote engineers, you are expected to leave the site **within 15 mints after**completion of the activity or 15 mints after leaving the conference meeting. **Level 3 Engineers closely monitor time logs and may check you out accordingly. Also, you will ONLY get for the time/hours, which you will work onsite, and we closely monitor tech progress while he/she is onsite to avoid any discrepancies.**\n\n**Policies with Flat Rates.**\n\nWe always recommend on working on **hourly rates**; however, we work on flat rates on**extreme circumstance**, therefore, Tech must not rush things to complete and show compassionate to resolving the problem and work with our teams. All flat rate offers must provide proper rate explanation about how many hours will be covered in flat rates; ‘else we will consider flat is good until JOB FINISHES’. **no rate discussions will be approved onsite or during the activity.**\n\nOur standard cancellation policy will apply if site cancels, aborts or due to no access **(NO FULL TICKET PRICE WILL AWARDED) IN-CASE OF SITE CANCELLATION FOR “FLAT RATE JOBS”.**\n\n**Parts Return Instructions and RMA Details**.\n\nTech will be responsible of dropping Off any unused or old devices (router or switch) to nearest UPS store (NOT UPS HUB or Walgreens or CVS) immediately after completion of the activity,**we will pay $25 to drop off the equipment.**Before dropping off**, tech must upload pictures of old device serial numbers, part numbers and host ID’s and share UPS drop off receipt before closing WO for payment.**\n\n**RMA Information:**\n\n1\\. Please head to the UPS store, NOT a drop-off location i.e. Walmart or Walgreens\n\n2\\. Tell that you are here to drop off equipment and we have a “corporate account” \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n3\\. Then provide the following information, as they request\n\n4\\. Case reference # 183XXXXXXXX\n\n5\\. Program Code:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Ratings:**\n\nWe always give 5-stars ratings to all our techs to encourage them during tough time and we expect that they respect our support team and customer and provide them highest level of service and respect. And we report for those fails to comply with our policies and give us hard time during our activities.\n\n**If travel time, mileage is being requested, must be approved before Job acceptance. Parking and tolls will be reimbursed per receipt,**\n\n**﻿NO EARLY CHECK IN ALLOWED, CHECK IN ONTIME or 5 Mints Prior to start time allowed, OR it will be asked to adjust upon closer of the ticket. There will $50 cancellation for the site with no access or aborts with any reasons. upon tech arrival onsite and upon check in.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11