{"job":{"id":20331528,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GALAIT LLC","title":"Router Installation - Field Engineer - GL2027021","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>READ THE JOB DESCRIPTION </u></strong></p><p><strong>JOB DESCRIPTION</strong></p><p>It will consist of circuit and hardware installation, including primary components.</p><p>Install the&nbsp;<strong><u>Cisco C1000</u></strong>&nbsp;router, connect it to the circuit, which is already delivered, and it will configure remotely.</p><p><strong><u>Your laptop sould be able to support a 1GB speed test </u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>BEFORE ALL:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>· </strong><u>By accepting this work order, you are accepting the terms and conditions on NDA attached to this listing.</u></p><p><strong>· </strong><u>By accepting this work order, you agree to the items listed. Read the entire work order before accepting</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong>NOTES:</strong></p><p>· Identify yourself as a GALAIT technician to the manager onsite. GALAIT is your employer for this job.</p><p>· Do not mention anything about Field Nation’s listing or WO here.</p><p>· You will be held responsible for arriving on the scheduled date and time, and any violations will be escalated to Field Nation.</p><p>· The name of the individual accepting this work must be the person who arrives on site, and if we determine a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.</p><p>· You will speak directly with our customers and end customers for support.&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing GALAIT and yourself.</p><p>· Always check in and out at GALAIT’s team</p><p>· If parts are needed, please contact GALAIT’s team immediately. Never assist our client, or end customer in purchasing the part. Failure of this step may result in non-payment of this ticket.&nbsp;<u>Please provide Make/Model or part required.</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong>GALAIT’s FE PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><p>· FE should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the end customers or remote engineers under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with GALAIT’s team.&nbsp;</p><p>· Dress Code Policy requires that technicians dress neatly and appropriately and maintain adequate personal hygiene.</p><p>· No identifying company logos are allowed. Clothes must not have any logos.</p><p>· Always wear your security equipment.</p><p>· We cannot have a job completed halfway. Do not leave the site without completing all the work on the job description and GALAIT’s team authorization</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SOW:</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Unpack the new router.</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;Take a picture to confirm the device serial number </strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Install the router at the location – with guidance from the remote engineer</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rack, power up, connect and activate.</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;No configuration is required because a remote engineer will do it.</strong></p><p><strong>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Smart-Hand / Remote-Hand support.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>DOCUMENTS REQUIRED FOR ACCESS:</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Verified driver's license (the kind with the star on it) (If this DL is not available, then active US Passport, if he/she does not have that, His/Her social security card and his/her birth certificate.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Insurance certificate and registration for the vehicle he/she will be driving onto the site.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You're going on behalf of GALAIT &amp; EXPEREO (Internet carrier).</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;By accepting this work order, you also agree to NDA attached.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DURATION:</strong></p><p>2-4 hours, but it can take more.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>REQUIREMENTS:</strong></p><ol><li>Engineer should be able to speak English.</li><li>Engineer must carry an ID card and wear it neatly and appropriately.</li><li>The engineer should have Cisco CCNA skills or equivalent. Certification is not required.</li><li>Engineer should be aware of basic router configuration.</li><li>Engineer must carry a&nbsp;Windows Professional OS installed laptop (No MacBook) having a serial interface or&nbsp;USB-serial cable adaptor.</li><li>We need&nbsp;the below apps installed on your laptop:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Team Viewer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">AnyDesk</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>Mikrotik WinBox</u></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Microsoft Team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Putty</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Webex</li><li>USB-serial cable drivers.</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);\">USB-A to USB-B Mini cable.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);\">USB-A to USB-B Micro console cable </strong></li><li>Internet dongle or data shared from a cellphone, the site doesn't have internet, you will go to activate it.</li><li>Cisco console cable.</li><li>Straight and cross UTP cables.</li><li>FE Laptop OS should either be Windows Professional or Enterprise version.</li><li><strong><u>FE Laptop should have&nbsp;a GigaEthernet in-built port.</u></strong></li><li>FE Laptop should support VLAN configuration and input VLAN values.</li><li>All required software and drivers should be up-to-date on the laptop.</li><li>The basic tools kits:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screwdrivers,&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">rack screws,&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">wood screws,&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">essential networking tools for a rack and unrack, for modules swap, etc.</li><li>Label machine.</li><li>Whatsapp installed on the cellphone.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>TASKS:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once you arrive on-site, you will need to check-in with GALAIT’s team for arrival.&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do check-in with the Local Contact on-site or the front desk at the location assigned to get directions on where to begin for the SOW assigned to you after they have provided you access.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate and Unpack the router</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check all spares and cables, including at the box.</p><p>· Contact the remote engineer to notify them that you are ready to start the job.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>· Rack new router following remote/local instruction&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Power up the new router&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Connect via console cable to the router console port&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Test console connection using putty.</p><p>· Follow the instructions,&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Perform speed tests according to customer's instructions and parameters, and implement HTML changes.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ESCALATIONS:</strong></p><p>FE will need to contact GALAIT’s services team&nbsp;and, explain what’s going on / ask for direction in any of the following situations:</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Always use the end customer’s name, GALAIT reference (GLXxxx), and location to help service agents find the case on our system.</u></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FE must call (682) 895-6057 ext 102 for cancellations and reschedules.&nbsp;<em>We do not accept reschedules or cancellations via messages through the platform.&nbsp;</em></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FE is going to be +30 min late.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FE is having access issues.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If FE can’t start work or cutover on time due to the MOD delaying us.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the job will go into overage time.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If anything happens that prevents him/her from completing normal SOW or requires to revisit (e.g., the equipment didn't arrive, circuits need troubleshooting with a vendor, parts are missing, etc.)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any of these things need to be communicated to the list of contacts below. We release our tech to give them a chance to weigh in.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you need a second opinion, please get in touch with us, and ask to be on a conference call with a Senior Remote engineer who can provide further assistance where possible. We do not provide support for circuit issues. We expect the remote engineer and/or local to contact the ISP account manager.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>GALAIT’s SERVICES TEAM CONTACTS:</strong></p><p>(682) 895-6057&nbsp;ext 102</p><p>(682) 895-6057&nbsp;via WhatsApp</p><p>If there is no response to phone calls, please email&nbsp;tos@galait.com.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>VIOLATIONS THAT MAY LEAD TO A NON-PAYMENT:</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not&nbsp;exchange contact information with the customer,&nbsp;and <u>NEVER COLLECT PAYMENT or PAYMENT INFORMATION.</u></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Do not sell or offer any hardware or components without authorization from WO mangaer</u></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not wear clothing that contains company brands/logos. This includes your vehicle.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;It is prohibited to take any of the customer's equipment offsite without GALAIT’s team authorization.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not install Bootleg &amp; Malicious Software.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you do not submit all deliverables.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Leaving a customer site without fill-out the Site Visit Report.</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not leave the site without completing all the work on the job description or GALAIT’s team authorization</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You will not be paid if you do not have a signed Site Visit Report from the Local Contact submitted within 24 hours of job completion.</p>","markdown":"**READ THE JOB DESCRIPTION**\n\n**JOB DESCRIPTION**\n\nIt will consist of circuit and hardware installation, including primary components.\n\nInstall the **Cisco C1000** router, connect it to the circuit, which is already delivered, and it will configure remotely.\n\n**Your laptop sould be able to support a 1GB speed test**\n\n**BEFORE ALL:**\n\n**·** By accepting this work order, you are accepting the terms and conditions on NDA attached to this listing.\n\n**·** By accepting this work order, you agree to the items listed. Read the entire work order before accepting\n\n**NOTES:**\n\n· Identify yourself as a GALAIT technician to the manager onsite. GALAIT is your employer for this job.\n\n· Do not mention anything about Field Nation’s listing or WO here.\n\n· You will be held responsible for arriving on the scheduled date and time, and any violations will be escalated to Field Nation.\n\n· The name of the individual accepting this work must be the person who arrives on site, and if we determine a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.\n\n· You will speak directly with our customers and end customers for support. Please be mindful of how you are representing GALAIT and yourself.\n\n· Always check in and out at GALAIT’s team\n\n· If parts are needed, please contact GALAIT’s team immediately. Never assist our client, or end customer in purchasing the part. Failure of this step may result in non-payment of this ticket. Please provide Make/Model or part required.\n\n**GALAIT’s FE PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n· FE should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the end customers or remote engineers under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with GALAIT’s team.\n\n· Dress Code Policy requires that technicians dress neatly and appropriately and maintain adequate personal hygiene.\n\n· No identifying company logos are allowed. Clothes must not have any logos.\n\n· Always wear your security equipment.\n\n· We cannot have a job completed halfway. Do not leave the site without completing all the work on the job description and GALAIT’s team authorization\n\n**SOW:**\n\n**• Unpack the new router.**\n\n**• Take a picture to confirm the device serial number**\n\n**• Install the router at the location – with guidance from the remote engineer**\n\n**• Rack, power up, connect and activate.**\n\n**• No configuration is required because a remote engineer will do it.**\n\n**• Smart-Hand / Remote-Hand support.**\n\n**DOCUMENTS REQUIRED FOR ACCESS:**\n\n• Verified driver's license (the kind with the star on it) (If this DL is not available, then active US Passport, if he/she does not have that, His/Her social security card and his/her birth certificate.\n\n• Insurance certificate and registration for the vehicle he/she will be driving onto the site.\n\n• You're going on behalf of GALAIT &amp; EXPEREO (Internet carrier).\n\n• By accepting this work order, you also agree to NDA attached.\n\n**DURATION:**\n\n2-4 hours, but it can take more.\n\n**REQUIREMENTS:**\n\n1. Engineer should be able to speak English.\n2. Engineer must carry an ID card and wear it neatly and appropriately.\n3. The engineer should have Cisco CCNA skills or equivalent. Certification is not required.\n4. Engineer should be aware of basic router configuration.\n5. Engineer must carry a Windows Professional OS installed laptop (No MacBook) having a serial interface or USB-serial cable adaptor.\n6. We need the below apps installed on your laptop:\n7. Team Viewer\n8. AnyDesk\n9. Mikrotik WinBox\n10. Microsoft Team\n11. Putty\n12. Webex\n13. USB-serial cable drivers.\n14. USB-A to USB-B Mini cable.\n15. **USB-A to USB-B Micro console cable**\n16. Internet dongle or data shared from a cellphone, the site doesn't have internet, you will go to activate it.\n17. Cisco console cable.\n18. Straight and cross UTP cables.\n19. FE Laptop OS should either be Windows Professional or Enterprise version.\n20. **FE Laptop should have a GigaEthernet in-built port.**\n21. FE Laptop should support VLAN configuration and input VLAN values.\n22. All required software and drivers should be up-to-date on the laptop.\n23. The basic tools kits:\n24. Screwdrivers,\n25. rack screws,\n26. wood screws,\n27. essential networking tools for a rack and unrack, for modules swap, etc.\n28. Label machine.\n29. Whatsapp installed on the cellphone.\n\n**TASKS:**\n\n· Once you arrive on-site, you will need to check-in with GALAIT’s team for arrival.\n\n· Please do check-in with the Local Contact on-site or the front desk at the location assigned to get directions on where to begin for the SOW assigned to you after they have provided you access.\n\n· Locate and Unpack the router\n\n· Check all spares and cables, including at the box.\n\n· Contact the remote engineer to notify them that you are ready to start the job.\n\n· Rack new router following remote/local instruction\n\n· Power up the new router\n\n· Connect via console cable to the router console port\n\n· Test console connection using putty.\n\n· Follow the instructions,\n\n**Perform speed tests according to customer's instructions and parameters, and implement HTML changes.**\n\n**ESCALATIONS:**\n\nFE will need to contact GALAIT’s services team and, explain what’s going on / ask for direction in any of the following situations:\n\n• Always use the end customer’s name, GALAIT reference (GLXxxx), and location to help service agents find the case on our system.\n\n• FE must call (682) 895-6057 ext 102 for cancellations and reschedules. *We do not accept reschedules or cancellations via messages through the platform.*\n\n· FE is going to be +30 min late.\n\n· FE is having access issues.\n\n· If FE can’t start work or cutover on time due to the MOD delaying us.\n\n· If the job will go into overage time.\n\n· If anything happens that prevents him/her from completing normal SOW or requires to revisit (e.g., the equipment didn't arrive, circuits need troubleshooting with a vendor, parts are missing, etc.)\n\n· Any of these things need to be communicated to the list of contacts below. We release our tech to give them a chance to weigh in.\n\n· If you need a second opinion, please get in touch with us, and ask to be on a conference call with a Senior Remote engineer who can provide further assistance where possible. We do not provide support for circuit issues. We expect the remote engineer and/or local to contact the ISP account manager.\n\n**GALAIT’s SERVICES TEAM CONTACTS:**\n\n(682) 895-6057 ext 102\n\n(682) 895-6057 via WhatsApp\n\nIf there is no response to phone calls, please email tos@galait.com.\n\n**VIOLATIONS THAT MAY LEAD TO A NON-PAYMENT:**\n\n• Do not exchange contact information with the customer, and NEVER COLLECT PAYMENT or PAYMENT INFORMATION.\n\n• Do not sell or offer any hardware or components without authorization from WO mangaer\n\n• Do not wear clothing that contains company brands/logos. This includes your vehicle.\n\n• It is prohibited to take any of the customer's equipment offsite without GALAIT’s team authorization.\n\n• Do not install Bootleg &amp; Malicious Software.\n\n• If you do not submit all deliverables.\n\n• Leaving a customer site without fill-out the Site Visit Report.\n\n• Do not leave the site without completing all the work on the job description or GALAIT’s team authorization\n\n• You will not be paid if you do not have a signed Site Visit Report from the Local Contact submitted within 24 hours of job completion.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T10:00","end":"2026-11-17T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6.199803583349337},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794240765440}
{"job":{"id":20331548,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"The Cook & Boardman Group, LLC","title":"CCTV//Clean outdoor camera","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><ul><li>Must be a licensed technician if doing work in the following states (or their locality) for varies trades - AL, CA, CT, DE, FL,GA, HI, IA, ID, IL, IN, LA, MA, ME, MI, MN, MT, NC, NH, NJ, NM, NV, NY, OH, OK, OR, PA, RI, SC, SD, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WA, WV, WY. Please verify with the submitter requirements before accepting if you are not sure.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>If you are close to exceeding the max hours give for this job, you MUST call Bass security to obtain approval or the additional time onsite is subject to denial.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>***MANDATORY requirement to call Bass Security upon arrival/completion***</strong></p><p><strong><u>MANDATORY Check- In Requirement</u></strong></p><p>1. Immediately upon arrival on site CHECK IN by:</p><p>* Text (fastest method): <strong>Text 1-856-452-7719 and include the NEST work order number</strong> _7259773__ * Call: Dial 1-877-374-2054 and enter the NEST work order number __7259773___followed by pound (#).</p><p>*Failure to use the IVR may result in an admin fee or non-payment.</p><p>For NTE increases or general work order questions, call Bass at 1-877-818-5989 ext. 1905.&nbsp;</p><p>2. Before and after PHOTOS are required and should be sent with completion paperwork to team905@bass-security.com</p><p><strong><u>MANDATORY Check- Out Requirement</u></strong></p><p><strong>1. </strong>Once you have completed the current scope of work, cleaned up your work area, loaded your truck, and finalized the Work Order Completion Form, you MUST call Bass at 1-877-818-5989 ext. 1905 with ALL completion details.</p><p><strong> 2.</strong> CHECK OUT by:<strong>* Text (fastest method): Text 1-856-452-7719 and include the NEST work order number __</strong>7259773<strong>___ * </strong>Call: Dial 1-877-374-2054 and enter the NEST work order number _7259773__ followed by pound (#).</p><p>3. Before and after PHOTOS are required and should be sent with completion paperwork to team905@bass-security.com.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Job Specific Technician Dispatch Notes:</u></strong></p><p>Expected Date of Service:</p><p>Jobsite Contact: Mgr. on duty</p><p><br></p><p>Contact Phone: \t919-220-2479</p><p><br></p><p>Location of Issue: See Mgr.</p><p><br></p><p>Parts Needing Service: CCTV</p><p><br></p><p>Bass Shipping Parts: No</p><p><br></p><p>Tech Notes: Clean back outdoor camera. Contact Bass while on site if additional parts or assistance is required.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>***If any material is found to be defective, </strong>the Subcontractor <strong><em>MUST</em> contact the manufacturer to obtain a ticket number and/or RMA, </strong>provide all related documentation to Bass Security Services, and assist with coordinating and returning the material as directed.</p><p><strong>No invoice will be paid if there is an outstanding or unresolved RMA or if required materials are not returned to Bass Security Services within ten (10) days of Work Order completion.</strong></p><p><strong><em>**Photos of the office monitor showing cameras view from both Before AND After are REQUIRED</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>**Capture of manager signature to certify work completion and they approve the view is REQUIRED</em></strong></p>","markdown":"- Must be a licensed technician if doing work in the following states (or their locality) for varies trades - AL, CA, CT, DE, FL,GA, HI, IA, ID, IL, IN, LA, MA, ME, MI, MN, MT, NC, NH, NJ, NM, NV, NY, OH, OK, OR, PA, RI, SC, SD, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WA, WV, WY. Please verify with the submitter requirements before accepting if you are not sure.\n- **If you are close to exceeding the max hours give for this job, you MUST call Bass security to obtain approval or the additional time onsite is subject to denial.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*MANDATORY requirement to call Bass Security upon arrival/completion\\*\\*\\***\n