{"job":{"id":20331911,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Task#: T20261108.0158 -Durham, NC- Troubleshoot Internet issues","description":{"html":"<strong>FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL</strong><br><strong>MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE <del>** </del>SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested</strong><br><strong>Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code</strong><ul><li><strong>Dress Code:</strong> Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.</li><li><strong>Client Representation:</strong> You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.</li><li><strong>Platform Discretion:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> mention or discuss <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ****** </del></span>or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work/On-site Task:</strong><br>Network Assessment &amp; Cable Tracing (48-Port UniFi &amp; 24-Port Cisco Beacon Switches)<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;Hardware / equipment involved: 48-port Unifi switch, 24-port Cisoco switch</strong></p><br><p>The objective of this engagement is to perform an assessment and physical/logical network trace of the 48-Port UniFi switch and the unknown 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch. This task will determine network segmentation, upstream connections, and verify whether the 24-Port Cisco switch operates on an isolated or non-DMJPS network.</p><br><ul><li>Verify the IP configuration, VLAN assignments, and routing path of the 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch to determine if it is separated from the DMJPS network.</li><li>Trace the uplink and patch connections of the 48-Port UniFi switch to confirm its connection to the DMJPS network.</li><li>Determine the upstream routing, subnet, and gateway associated with the 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch.</li></ul><br>Phase 1: Assessment &amp; Preparation<ul><li>Perform initial discovery on both switches (UniFi 48-Port and Cisco Beacon 24-Port).</li><li>Document current LED status, port link states, and connected patch cables.</li></ul>Phase 2: Switch Tracing &amp; Path VerificationTask A: 48-Port UniFi Switch Tracing<ul><li><strong>Physical Trace:</strong> Trace uplink patch cables and infrastructure runs from the 48-Port UniFi switch back to the core/distribution network equipment.</li><li><strong>Logical Verification:</strong> Confirm if the traffic routes through the DMJPS network subnets, gateways, and management controllers.</li></ul>Task B: 24-Port Cisco Beacon Switch Tracing &amp; Isolation Check<ul><li><strong>Physical Trace:</strong> Trace the main uplink line(s) connected to the 24-Port Cisco switch to locate its upstream provider or router.</li><li><strong>Logical Verification:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inspect IP address assignment (DHCP vs. Static), subnet mask, default gateway, and active VLANs.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify whether the traffic isolates to an external/secondary network or bridges into the DMJPS network.</li></ul><br><ul><li><strong>Network Tracing &amp; Topology Diagram / Report:</strong> Summary outlining the uplink path of both switches.</li><li><strong>Network Identification Findings:</strong> Definitive confirmation showing whether the 24-Port Cisco switch is on a separate non-DMJPS network.</li><li><strong>Recommendations:</strong> Operational notes regarding any unintended bridging or rogue network paths discovered during tracing.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools:</strong><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">cellphone, laptop, patch cable, network toner/tester,</span></p><p><br></p><p>For <u>pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact</u>, please check the <strong>CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION</strong> below.</p><p><br></p><strong>DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)</li><li><strong>Record</strong>: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong> Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong> Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within <strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><br>","markdown":"**FIELD TECH QUICK GUIDE &amp; PROTOCOL**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE \\*\\* SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested**  \n**Special Notice: Professionalism &amp; Dress Code**- **Dress Code:** Clean, neat, business-appropriate field attire (polo or collared shirt, clean work pants/khakis, closed-toe work boots or safety shoes). No graphic tees, torn jeans, or sweatpants.\n- **Client Representation:** You are the face of the client on-site. Conduct yourself with courtesy, respect, and standard-setting professionalism at all times.\n- **Platform Discretion:** **Never** mention or discuss \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* or third-party dispatch platforms with site staff or the client. Refer all coordination to Support Tech (Support Tech Dispatch: 470-470-7757)\n\n**Scope of work/On-site Task:**  \nNetwork Assessment &amp; Cable Tracing (48-Port UniFi &amp; 24-Port Cisco Beacon Switches) **Hardware / equipment involved: 48-port Unifi switch, 24-port Cisoco switch**\n\n  \nThe objective of this engagement is to perform an assessment and physical/logical network trace of the 48-Port UniFi switch and the unknown 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch. This task will determine network segmentation, upstream connections, and verify whether the 24-Port Cisco switch operates on an isolated or non-DMJPS network.\n\n  \n- Verify the IP configuration, VLAN assignments, and routing path of the 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch to determine if it is separated from the DMJPS network.\n- Trace the uplink and patch connections of the 48-Port UniFi switch to confirm its connection to the DMJPS network.\n- Determine the upstream routing, subnet, and gateway associated with the 24-Port Cisco Beacon switch.\n\n  \nPhase 1: Assessment &amp; Preparation- Perform initial discovery on both switches (UniFi 48-Port and Cisco Beacon 24-Port).\n- Document current LED status, port link states, and connected patch cables.\n\nPhase 2: Switch Tracing &amp; Path VerificationTask A: 48-Port UniFi Switch Tracing- **Physical Trace:** Trace uplink patch cables and infrastructure runs from the 48-Port UniFi switch back to the core/distribution network equipment.\n- **Logical Verification:** Confirm if the traffic routes through the DMJPS network subnets, gateways, and management controllers.\n\nTask B: 24-Port Cisco Beacon Switch Tracing &amp; Isolation Check- **Physical Trace:** Trace the main uplink line(s) connected to the 24-Port Cisco switch to locate its upstream provider or router.\n- **Logical Verification:**\n- Inspect IP address assignment (DHCP vs. Static), subnet mask, default gateway, and active VLANs.\n- Verify whether the traffic isolates to an external/secondary network or bridges into the DMJPS network.\n\n  \n- **Network Tracing &amp; Topology Diagram / Report:** Summary outlining the uplink path of both switches.\n- **Network Identification Findings:** Definitive confirmation showing whether the 24-Port Cisco switch is on a separate non-DMJPS network.\n- **Recommendations:** Operational notes regarding any unintended bridging or rogue network paths discovered during tracing.\n\n**Required Tools:**cellphone, laptop, patch cable, network toner/tester,\n\nFor pre-arrival/on-site access requirements or special instructions/On-site contact, please check the **CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION** below.\n\n**DELIVERABLE REMINDERS:**- **Documentation:** Detailed closeout notes (diagnosis/assessment, issue/delays, troubleshooting steps, and resolution)\n- **Record**: Remote support and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement**\n\nBy accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T11:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13.21166312825168},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericsson"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-