{"job":{"id":20332070,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vision Technologies","title":"Connect T Moblie booster to the network swap out 5 This clients with NOC support SiteOne Landscape Supply / Branch / 0454 INC1036866 / SO0005154","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technician must wear proper safety gear:</strong></p><ul><li>​<strong>High visibility shirt/vest</strong></li><li><strong>Safety boots(non-slip/cover ankle/resist penetration)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Must meet with MOD on arrival and if changing out any devices please call into help desk prior to the removal or installation of any device</strong></p><p><strong>Must be on site at check in and check out, manager sign off must match your check out time or a penalty of up to $50.00 will be applied</strong></p><p><strong>Service Request Summary - T-Mobile Signal Booster needs to be plugged into the Switch and brought online.</strong></p><p><strong>Service Request - T-Mobile booster was recently installed and mounted to the side of the building. Technician will need to patch the booster into our Switch and verify with the team that the device is online. We believe there to be a jumper box going from the booster to the network cabinet that needs a cable ran to it.</strong></p><p><strong>Report to site and meet with manager, get the network location and then call into the help desk, work with their support to get the T-Mobile booster connected to their network per the direction of the NOC support tech, once connected verify with their support tech they can see the booster on the network and is working properly. </strong></p><p><strong>Then work with their support to connect 5 thin clients at 5 work stations work with their support to verify they all come up on the network and are working properly. </strong></p><p><strong>Call helpdesk (contact info under Confidential Information) prior to leaving site for work complete verification</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Please bring all material necessary to complete.</u></strong></p><p>Cell Phone</p><p>Laptop</p><p>6-8' Ladder</p><p>Network Testing and Installation Tools</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact Gary Ledwell. If he does not answer, please leave VM or Text.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>You must be on time for the work order. If for some reason you are going to be late you must call the Vision representative&nbsp;&nbsp;an&nbsp;hour before the scheduled time.&nbsp;​</strong></p><p><strong><u>If you do not call within the hour time frame you will receive a pay deduction.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>***Safety Requirements***​</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>High Visibility Shirt\\Vest</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>A high visibility safety vest or high visibility shirt must be worn at all times when working in areas where mobile equipment and/or vehicles are operated.&nbsp;This includes:</p><ul><li>All warehouses where forklift traffic is present; whether on or off of the forklift.&nbsp;This would include all areas in our drive-through branches</li><li>All nursery yards</li><li>All out door areas at non-nursery locations where equipment may operate and/or where there is traffic flow</li><li>All active worksites with vehicle traffic and/or mobile equipment in use</li><li>At all times when loading, unloading and taking deliveries, including when stopped roadside for DOT inspection, mechanical issues, and refueling</li></ul><p><strong><u>Footwear</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Acceptable:</p><ul><li>Be of substantial design and construction</li><li>Have soles that are strong and in good condition to prevent slipping on smooth, wet, or loose surfaces.&nbsp;Tread with random patterns perpendicular to the direction of travel are most slip-resistant​</li><li>Have soles that resist penetration by nails and debris</li><li>cover the ankle-providing additional ankle support and stability.&nbsp;Such footwear is intended to prevent and/or minimize the severity of ankle injuries</li><li>Steel toed shoes are recommended, but not mandatory unless required by government regulation</li></ul><p>Not Acceptable:</p><ul><li>Open toe shoes</li><li>Opened heeled shoes</li><li>Traditional cowboy boots (slick-sole, raised heel)</li><li>Tennis/running shoes</li><li>An footwear with tread that is worn smooth​</li></ul><p><strong>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact. If they do not answer, please leave VM or Text.</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Deliverables will include the work order form that is attached to this WO. The form must be signed by the tech and the office manager before leaving site.</strong></p><p><strong>Deliverables also include pictures of everything you worked on. The more pictures, the better.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>When returning deliverables please only post to Field Nation.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Technician must wear proper safety gear:**\n\n- ​**High visibility shirt/vest**\n- **Safety boots(non-slip/cover ankle/resist penetration)**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**Must meet with MOD on arrival and if changing out any devices please call into help desk prior to the removal or installation of any device**\n\n**Must be on site at check in and check out, manager sign off must match your check out time or a penalty of up to $50.00 will be applied**\n\n**Service Request Summary - T-Mobile Signal Booster needs to be plugged into the Switch and brought online.**\n\n**Service Request - T-Mobile booster was recently installed and mounted to the side of the building. Technician will need to patch the booster into our Switch and verify with the team that the device is online. We believe there to be a jumper box going from the booster to the network cabinet that needs a cable ran to it.**\n\n**Report to site and meet with manager, get the network location and then call into the help desk, work with their support to get the T-Mobile booster connected to their network per the direction of the NOC support tech, once connected verify with their support tech they can see the booster on the network and is working properly.**\n\n**Then work with their support to connect 5 thin clients at 5 work stations work with their support to verify they all come up on the network and are working properly.**\n\n**Call helpdesk (contact info under Confidential Information) prior to leaving site for work complete verification**\n\n**Please bring all material necessary to complete.**\n\nCell Phone\n\nLaptop\n\n6-8' Ladder\n\nNetwork Testing and Installation Tools\n\n**Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact Gary Ledwell. If he does not answer, please leave VM or Text.**\n\n**You must be on time for the work order. If for some reason you are going to be late you must call the Vision representative an hour before the scheduled time. ​**\n\n**If you do not call within the hour time frame you will receive a pay deduction.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Safety Requirements\\*\\*\\*​**\n\n**High Visibility Shirt\\\\Vest**\n\nA high visibility safety vest or high visibility shirt must be worn at all times when working in areas where mobile equipment and/or vehicles are operated. This includes:\n\n- All warehouses where forklift traffic is present; whether on or off of the forklift. This would include all areas in our drive-through branches\n- All nursery yards\n- All out door areas at non-nursery locations where equipment may operate and/or where there is traffic flow\n- All active worksites with vehicle traffic and/or mobile equipment in use\n- At all times when loading, unloading and taking deliveries, including when stopped roadside for DOT inspection, mechanical issues, and refueling\n\n**Footwear**\n\nAcceptable:\n\n- Be of substantial design and construction\n- Have soles that are strong and in good condition to prevent slipping on smooth, wet, or loose surfaces. Tread with random patterns perpendicular to the direction of travel are most slip-resistant​\n- Have soles that resist penetration by nails and debris\n- cover the ankle-providing additional ankle support and stability. Such footwear is intended to prevent and/or minimize the severity of ankle injuries\n- Steel toed shoes are recommended, but not mandatory unless required by government regulation\n\nNot Acceptable:\n\n- Open toe shoes\n- Opened heeled shoes\n- Traditional cowboy boots (slick-sole, raised heel)\n- Tennis/running shoes\n- An footwear with tread that is worn smooth​\n\n**-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n **Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact. If they do not answer, please leave VM or Text.**\n\n**Deliverables will include the work order form that is attached to this WO. The form must be signed by the tech and the office manager before leaving site.**\n\n**Deliverables also include pictures of everything you worked on. The more pictures, the better.**\n\n**When returning deliverables please only post to Field Nation.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T08:00","end":"2026-11-10T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":1.7753755951971304},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"}