{"job":{"id":20331913,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GridPoint","title":"WAG16138 | Troubleshoot and/or Replace GridPoint EC‑2000 EMS Controller","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong>Seeking a technician with<strong>proven EMS (Energy Management Systems) experience to</strong> <strong>troubleshoot the existing EC‑2000 controller</strong> and restore full EMS connectivity at the site. <strong>The existing controller must be fully diagnosed before replacement.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Site/Customer: Walgreens</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Professional work attire; closed-toe shoes and a safety vest may be required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Materials/Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Multimeter</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cable toner/tester</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wire strippers, termination tools</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Phone with photo/email capability</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic tools</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Materials shipping to site:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Part: EC-2000-21 | Qty: 1</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Part: PS-24V-ENC-BP | Qty : 1</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Schedule Confirmation:</strong> You must confirm the scheduled date and time frame with the project manager before arriving on-site to ensure Support Staff availability.</li>\n<li><strong>Review FULL SOW.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Review the training video attached to the client documents section of the WO.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reference Case:</strong> Keep Case # <strong><del>*******</del></strong> available for all communications.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong><strong>Troubleshoot and/or Replace GridPoint EC‑2000 EMS Controller</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>Please dispatch a technician to <strong>troubleshoot the existing EC‑2000 controller</strong> and restore full EMS connectivity at the site. <strong>The existing controller must be fully diagnosed before replacement.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>1. Contact GridPoint Support Upon Arrival</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Text <strong><del>****************</del></strong> <del>** ****</del> <strong><del>****************</del></strong> upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Technician must <strong>check in and out</strong> with GridPoint Support.</li>\n<li>Reference <strong>case # <del>*******</del> and site ID WAG16138</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2. Troubleshoot the Existing EC‑2000 Controller</strong></p>\n<p>Technician must:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify the controller is powered and booting correctly.</li>\n<li>Inspect all wiring and terminations for damage, loose connections, or corrosion.</li>\n<li>Confirm whether the existing <strong>AC or DC power supply</strong> is providing a stable <strong>24V</strong>.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If 24V is present and stable, <strong>skip installing the new DC power supply</strong>.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If not, install the new DC power supply.</li>\n<li>Provide <strong>before and after photos</strong> of any power‑supply work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>3. Test and Replace LAN Cable if Needed</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Test the LAN cable from the controller to the network switch.</li>\n<li>Replace the cable if continuity, termination, or shielding issues are found.</li>\n<li>Work with <strong>WAG NOC</strong> as needed to confirm switch port status and configuration.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>4. Replace the Controller Only if Troubleshooting Confirms Failure</strong></p>\n<p>If the existing controller cannot be restored:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install the replacement EC‑2000 controller.</li>\n<li>Enter the required network settings:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Network Configuration:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><del>***</del></strong> <del>***********</del></li>\n<li><strong><del>********</del></strong><del>***************</del></li>\n<li><strong><del>********</del></strong><del>************</del></li>\n<li><strong><del>*** *******</del></strong><del>**************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Server Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><del>********************</del></strong></li>\n<li>Work with GridPoint Support to confirm the new controller connects successfully.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>5. Troubleshoot Offline Peripherals</strong></p>\n<p>Once connectivity is restored:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Work with GridPoint Support to identify any thermostats, sensors, I/O modules, or lighting controllers that remain offline.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot wiring, communication, or device issues as needed.</li>\n<li>Confirm all peripherals are stable and reporting correctly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>6. Required Photos</strong></p>\n<p>Technician must provide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Before and after photos of the <strong>power supply</strong></li>\n<li>Photos of the <strong>existing controller</strong> and the<strong>replacement controller</strong> (if installed)</li>\n<li>Photos of <strong>LAN cable replacements</strong></li>\n<li>Photos of any wiring corrections</li>\n<li>Any additional photos requested by GridPoint Support</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All photos must be sent <strong>before leaving the site</strong>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Communication Directory:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>GridPoint Support:</strong> Please <del>**** ************ ** **** ************</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counteroffer when requesting the work in order to get approved.</li>\n<li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by the WO Manager.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Count &amp; NTE Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The vendor must determine <strong>before dispatch whether</strong> <strong>two technicians</strong> are required to complete the work.</li>\n<li>If two technicians are needed, the vendor <strong>must contact GridPoint for approval</strong> prior to dispatch, as this will result in an <strong>NTE increase</strong>.</li>\n<li>If GridPoint did not request more than one technician and no approval was received, <strong>GridPoint will not accept charges</strong> for the second technician.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Repair Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The technician is <strong>not permitted to repair any RTUs</strong>.</li>\n<li>GridPoint is <strong>not responsible for repairs</strong> to the customer’s HVAC system.</li>\n<li>The technician may <strong>advise the site manager</strong> of any HVAC issues needing repair, but <strong>GridPoint cannot authorize or approve</strong> those repairs through this dispatch.</li>\n<li>GridPoint <strong>will not accept or pay</strong> for any repair charges that were not explicitly approved.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**Seeking a technician with**proven EMS (Energy Management Systems) experience to** **troubleshoot the existing EC‑2000 controller** and restore full EMS connectivity at the site. **The existing controller must be fully diagnosed before replacement.**\n\n**Site/Customer: Walgreens**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Professional work attire; closed-toe shoes and a safety vest may be required.\n\n**Materials/Tools Required:**\n\n• Multimeter\n\n• Cable toner/tester\n\n• CAT5 or 22–24 AWG STP wire\n\n• Screwdrivers, terminal screwdriver\n\n• Wire strippers, termination tools\n\n• Phone with photo/email capability\n\n• Basic tools\n\n**Materials shipping to site:**\n\n**Part: EC-2000-21 | Qty: 1**\n\n**Part: PS-24V-ENC-BP | Qty : 1**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Schedule Confirmation:** You must confirm the scheduled date and time frame with the project manager before arriving on-site to ensure Support Staff availability.\n- **Review FULL SOW.**\n- **Review the training video attached to the client documents section of the WO.**\n- **Reference Case:** Keep Case # **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** available for all communications.\n\n**Scope of Work:****Troubleshoot and/or Replace GridPoint EC‑2000 EMS Controller**\n\nPlease dispatch a technician to **troubleshoot the existing EC‑2000 controller** and restore full EMS connectivity at the site. **The existing controller must be fully diagnosed before replacement.**\n\n**1. Contact GridPoint Support Upon Arrival**\n\n- Text **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** upon arrival.\n- Technician must **check in and out** with GridPoint Support.\n- Reference **case # \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and site ID WAG16138**\n\n**2. Troubleshoot the Existing EC‑2000 Controller**\n\nTechnician must:\n\n- Verify the controller is powered and booting correctly.\n- Inspect all wiring and terminations for damage, loose connections, or corrosion.\n- Confirm whether the existing **AC or DC power supply** is providing a stable **24V**.\n- If 24V is present and stable, **skip installing the new DC power supply**.\n- If not, install the new DC power supply.\n- Provide **before and after photos** of any power‑supply work.\n\n**3. Test and Replace LAN Cable if Needed**\n\n- Test the LAN cable from the controller to the network switch.\n- Replace the cable if continuity, termination, or shielding issues are found.\n- Work with **WAG NOC** as needed to confirm switch port status and configuration.\n\n**4. Replace the Controller Only if Troubleshooting Confirms Failure**\n\nIf the existing controller cannot be restored:\n\n- Install the replacement EC‑2000 controller.\n- Enter the required network settings:\n\n**Network Configuration:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Server Details:**\n\n- **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- Work with GridPoint Support to confirm the new controller connects successfully.\n\n**5. Troubleshoot Offline Peripherals**\n\nOnce connectivity is restored:\n\n- Work with GridPoint Support to identify any thermostats, sensors, I/O modules, or lighting controllers that remain offline.\n- Troubleshoot wiring, communication, or device issues as needed.\n- Confirm all peripherals are stable and reporting correctly.\n\n**6. Required Photos**\n\nTechnician must provide:\n\n- Before and after photos of the **power supply**\n- Photos of the **existing controller** and the**replacement controller** (if installed)\n- Photos of **LAN cable replacements**\n- Photos of any wiring corrections\n- Any additional photos requested by GridPoint Support\n\nAll photos must be sent **before leaving the site**.\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- **GridPoint Support:** Please \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counteroffer when requesting the work in order to get approved.\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by the WO Manager.\n\n**Technician Count &amp; NTE Requirements**\n\n- The vendor must determine **before dispatch whether** **two technicians** are required to complete the work.\n- If two technicians are needed, the vendor **must contact GridPoint for approval** prior to dispatch, as this will result in an **NTE increase**.\n- If GridPoint did not request more than one technician and no approval was received, **GridPoint will not accept charges** for the second technician.\n\n**Repair Limitations**\n\n- The technician is **not permitted to repair any RTUs**.\n- GridPoint is **not responsible for repairs** to the customer’s HVAC system.\n- The technician may **advise the site manager** of any HVAC issues needing repair, but **GridPoint cannot authorize or approve** those repairs through this dispatch.\n- GridPoint **will not accept or pay** for any repair charges that were not explicitly approved.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T08:00","end":"2026-11-12T11:00","latestStart":"2026-11-12T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":225},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":14.261697291568465},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $225 (countered: $225) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericsson"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericcson"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fishe