{"job":{"id":20332759,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"(MX is Bad-EMERGENCY ) - Please see SOW for required tools.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT INFORMATION:</strong></p><p><strong>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage.&nbsp;If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders.&nbsp;Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay.&nbsp;Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only.&nbsp;If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction.&nbsp;The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</strong></p><p>-------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p><del>*** ****** **</del><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"><del>**********</del></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must call <del>*** ***** * ******** ******* * ************</del> if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>- If they don't answer, call the <del>*** ******** **** ****** ************** ****** * **** ****** * </del>- wait for a live person) BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</p><p>- This is a must, even if nothing was able to be completed onsite.</p><p>*Failure to do so, may result in failure of payment. The tech will need to give TRCA the name of the rep they spoke with upon checking out.*</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>-\tIf you are on hold or are waiting for a call back, from the helpdesk, longer than 20 min, tech will need to reach out to TRCA for further instructions.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Required Tools:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Laptop w/console cable</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- CAT6 cabling/material/patch cables</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Mod ends, face plates, jacks..etc</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Basic tools: screwdrivers, drill, bits of different sizes, etc</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- At least 8-10' ladder</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">SOW:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">School has been down since Friday. Spectrum came out and gave them a new modem/router but the Spectrum tech said the problem is our Cisco Networking equipment. Called user and she confirmed MX has an orange light as well as switch. Tried doing Internet 1/2 ports and power cycling the MX but still orange. Putting emergency since they have no Internet and parents are complaining</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must call </strong><del>*** ***** * ******** ******* * ************</del> <strong><del> </del>if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>IF THERE IS DEFECTIVE TELEPHONY EQUIPMENT, TRCA WILL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION UPON CHECKING OUT:</strong></p><p>1. We'll need the make and model of the hardware.</p><p>2. We'll need pictures of the serial number and the defective hardware itself. The tech will be asked for the serial # upon checking out.</p><p>3. We'll need quantity of each hardware device that needs to be replaced.</p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT INFORMATION:**\n\n**Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction. The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.**\n\n\\-------------------------------------------\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tech must call \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.**\n\n\\- If they don't answer, call the \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* - wait for a live person) BEFORE checking out with TRCA.\n\n\\- This is a must, even if nothing was able to be completed onsite.\n\n\\*Failure to do so, may result in failure of payment. The tech will need to give TRCA the name of the rep they spoke with upon checking out.\\*\n\n**- If you are on hold or are waiting for a call back, from the helpdesk, longer than 20 min, tech will need to reach out to TRCA for further instructions.**\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n\\- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.\n\n\\- Laptop w/console cable\n\n\\- CAT6 cabling/material/patch cables\n\n\\- Mod ends, face plates, jacks..etc\n\n\\- Basic tools: screwdrivers, drill, bits of different sizes, etc\n\n\\- At least 8-10' ladder\n\nSOW:\n\nSchool has been down since Friday. Spectrum came out and gave them a new modem/router but the Spectrum tech said the problem is our Cisco Networking equipment. Called user and she confirmed MX has an orange light as well as switch. Tried doing Internet 1/2 ports and power cycling the MX but still orange. Putting emergency since they have no Internet and parents are complaining\n\n**Tech must call** \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*  **if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.**\n\n**IF THERE IS DEFECTIVE TELEPHONY EQUIPMENT, TRCA WILL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION UPON CHECKING OUT:**\n\n1\\. We'll need the make and model of the hardware.\n\n2\\. We'll need pictures of the serial number and the defective hardware itself. The tech will be asked for the serial # upon checking out.\n\n3\\. We'll need quantity of each hardware device that needs to be replaced.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-09T08:00","end":"2026-11-10T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.468328297164907},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T16:30:00.000Z","summary":"Survey FN"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14