{"job":{"id":"5475182023","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Switch Install & Cutover (HARD START TIME)","description":"Scope of Work: <br>Assess the network rack.<br>Identify and locate two legacy Cisco switches and two routers.<br>Temporarily tag the Ethernet cables connected to the switches.<br>Temporarily tag the WAN circuits and all other cables connected to the routers, tracing each cable to its destination.<br>Inventory the new equipment: two Cisco 9350 switches, two Cisco 8151 routers, one 5G card, and one surge protector.<br>Unbox and stage the new equipment for installation.<br>Remove the legacy network equipment.<br>Install the new equipment in the same rack units as the existing equipment.<br>Reroute and dress the cables with neat cable management (place slack on the side of the rack uprights).<br>Work with the remote network engineer throughout the process to complete the cutover.<br>Test the site with the local contact.<br>Re-box the old equipment and stage it in the equipment room.<br>Clean up the work area, dispose of trash, and obtain verbal release.<br>Collect required collateral and check out with Support: <br><br><br><br>Required Tools/Materials:<br>Basic Hand Tools<br>Label Maker<br>LAN Tester<br>Basic Tools<br>Phone<br>100% charged before arriving<br>Internet access<br>Hands-free headset<br>Phone Charger<br>Power bank is also highly recommended<br>Laptop<br>Teams Desktop Client installed<br>WEB VERSION WILL NOT WORK<br>PuTTY installed<br>USB-C data cable<br>Rj45 Console cable<br>CAT6 tester<br>Basic toolkit<br>Phillips, flat, and Torx bits and drivers<br>Electrician’s scissors/snips<br>Pliers<br>Adjustable wrench<br>Black marker<br>Pen or pencil<br>Velcro roll<br>6 foot ladder<br><br>Code of Conduct:<br>Always maintain a professional and respectful tone when communicating with customers.<br>All conversations should remain focused on addressing the customer's needs in a courteous and business-appropriate manner.<br>Personal or overly familiar interactions can lead to misunderstandings and may reflect poorly on both you and the company.<br>Any deviation from this standard may result in loss of pay and removal from the project.<br><br>Drug Policy/Dress Code;<br>Do not bring illegal drugs, alcohol, or weapons onsite, and do not be under the influence while working. You must be clean, presentable, and dressed appropriately, clothing should not be torn or soiled. Appropriate dress includes plain polo or button-down shirt, khaki-style pants, and hard-soled shoes.<br><br>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after checking out, otherwise they will not be approved.<br><br>Do not remove, take, or ask to take, any equipment off the premises unless confirmed it is okay to do so by the client. Removing any equipment without the knowledge of the client and ServicePoint may be considered theft.<br><br>Do not discuss your pay rate or share payroll information with the customer or your co-workers. Should you have payroll issues, contact your recruiter or the payroll department directly.<br><br>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered 'Cancelled', not 'Aborted'.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00","end":"2026-11-10T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":500},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 2:00 PM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, F