{"job":{"id":20333135,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - Test and Replace Homerun Cabling","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Requirements:</p><p>Store MOD requested as soon as possible&nbsp;tech can be aligned</p><p>SCO 51 is not connecting to the network.</p><p>The homerun cable is showing a fault.</p><p>Cables from the SCO to the wall and from the patch panel to the switch are working properly.</p><p>A cable vendor is required to replace the faulty homerun cable and restore network connectivity.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Requirements:\n\nStore MOD requested as soon as possible tech can be aligned\n\nSCO 51 is not connecting to the network.\n\nThe homerun cable is showing a fault.\n\nCables from the SCO to the wall and from the patch panel to the switch are working properly.\n\nA cable vendor is required to replace the faulty homerun cable and restore network connectivity.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T07:00","end":"2026-11-11T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4.6981496694340334},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 7:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericsson"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794248179203}
{"job":{"id":20246912,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING </u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Insight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.</span></p><p><strong><u>10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></u>Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)&nbsp;</strong>Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. <u>Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.&nbsp;</u></p><ul><li>Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced</li><li>Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions</li><li>Perform cable management</li><li>Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity</li><li>Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter</li><li>Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location</li></ul><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID</li><li>Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)</li><li>Fully charged mobile phone and charger</li><li><u>A printed copy file attached \"</u><strong><u>PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX</u></strong><u>\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.</u></li><li>Pen or pencil</li><li>Basic desktop tool kit</li><li>Phillips and slotted screwdriver set</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Needle nose pliers</li><li>Crescent wrench</li><li>Box cutter</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)</li><li>Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature</li><li>Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations</li><li>Packing Tape</li><li>Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)</li><li>Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)</li><li><strong>Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><em>Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.</em></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:&nbsp;</strong>Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing</p><p><strong>Dress:&nbsp;</strong>Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)</p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><ul><li>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</li><li>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</li><li>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</li><li>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</li><li>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</li><li>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</li><li><strong>On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.</strong></li><li>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</li></ul><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><ul><li>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</li><li>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT</u></strong>: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;</em></p>","markdown":"**READ STANDARD INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE REQUESTING/COUNTERING**\n\nInsight has been engaged by PNC Bank to execute a nationwide PC and currency counter refresh across its retail locations. The selected resource must possess the necessary skills to perform the work, adhere to provided instructions, and report directly to Insight.\n\n**10% Unprepared and 10% Late Arrival (without prior approval) Deduction is being actively used on this project, un-prepared = not reading the instructions, not having the correct tools, etc.**\n\n**﻿Each tech is assigned their own job under their own FN profile. You may NOT bring a helper with you.**\n\n**Scope: (refer to full install instructions attached)** Inventory PCs that are on site and validate they are at the correct branch. Report to the Bridge and provide site readiness status. Report any damaged/missing boxes or equipment issues.\n\n- Locate the PC or currency counter to be replaced\n- Replace PC or currency counter using the installation instructions\n- Perform cable management\n- Perform basic PC validation (required only for Universal) - Verify network connection, login capability, and browser connectivity\n- Box the old PC (old keyboard, old mouse, and old power cable for shipping) or currency counter\n- Affix return shipping label on return equipment and place boxed equipment in designated location\n\n**Tools:**\n\n- Photo ID\n- Letter of Authorization which is attached to this ticket (Can be printed or on your smart phone)\n- Fully charged mobile phone and charger\n- A printed copy file attached \"**PNC RETAIL PRINT FOR SITE VISIT.DOCX**\" these are the labels that will need to be on the boxes.\n- Pen or pencil\n- Basic desktop tool kit\n- Phillips and slotted screwdriver set\n- Pliers\n- Needle nose pliers\n- Crescent wrench\n- Box cutter\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (Optional)\n- Flashlight - not required if mobile phone has flashlight feature\n- Fish Tape or string to get mouse, keyboard, and other cables through the millwork or complex desk configurations\n- Packing Tape\n- Standard &amp; Metric Socket Sets (optional)\n- Power screwdriver 2/multiple tips (optional)\n- **Do not purchase additional equipment without prior approval. Must include FULL NAME of who directed you to purchase additional equipment.**\n- ***Materials, tolls, or parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt from the vendor/point-of-sale is attached to the expense/additional charge. Company-generated invoices will not be accepted.***\n\n**Deliverables:** Photos of installed devices showing neat cable management, photo of the equipment in the box prior to sealing\n\n**Dress:** Business casual​ (no baseball caps or ripped clothing)\n\n**Penalties/Deductions**:\n\n- 10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.\n- 10% Deduction for being unprepared.\n- Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.\n- Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.\n\n**Terms for Travel:**\n\n- Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate\n- If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n- If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n- **On bundles, this must be sent as a message on the work order and approved by Insight prior to being assigned/accepting a route.**\n- Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\n**Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite**:\n\n- Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n- If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n\nTech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center 