{"job":{"id":20333327,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Xeal","title":"Firmware Update to Xeal EV Chargers // Smartphone Required","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**Smartphone with the Xeal mobile app is required. Please verify your phone is compatible with the Xeal app prior to accepting this work order.**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prior to arrival</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Provide a valid email to Xeal </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Password reset email will be sent to activate the user account and will be sent to the email provided, (Check spam folder for email if not received.)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Download Xeal mobile app and login (internet or cell service is required to download app and login, but not for the update itself)</span></li></ul><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE: Do not create your own account within the mobile app. The Xeal Mobile App allows you to perform all your Admin/Maintenance duties, login is for the Mobile App ONLY - there is no desktop functionality. If you have signed into the Xeal mobile app before, a PW reset or account setup is not required. You can use the same credentials as last time you accessed the Xeal mobile app.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Upon Arrival:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><ul><li>Follow attached Firmware Update Guide for step-by-step instructions, to complete firmware update on each charger</li><li>Take a screenshot of each quick report to show that the firmware is updated and include in attachments section</li><li>Notify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If any charger does not have the power light on, or if any red fault lights are on (Power Fault or Charging Fault)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If update was not able to be completed for any reason and on which charger(s)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If test session is unsuccessful, as well as any error messages you encounter</li><li>If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.</li><li>If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster</li><li>Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Note: Showing up to site without the proper device type (smartphone compatible with Xeal mobile app) will result in incomplete/nonpayment for the work order. </em></strong></p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*Smartphone with the Xeal mobile app is required. Please verify your phone is compatible with the Xeal app prior to accepting this work order.\\*\\***\n\n**Prior to arrival**\n\n- Provide a valid email to Xeal\n- Password reset email will be sent to activate the user account and will be sent to the email provided, (Check spam folder for email if not received.)\n- Download Xeal mobile app and login (internet or cell service is required to download app and login, but not for the update itself)\n\n*NOTE: Do not create your own account within the mobile app. The Xeal Mobile App allows you to perform all your Admin/Maintenance duties, login is for the Mobile App ONLY - there is no desktop functionality. If you have signed into the Xeal mobile app before, a PW reset or account setup is not required. You can use the same credentials as last time you accessed the Xeal mobile app.*\n\n**Upon Arrival:**\n\n- If it is not apparent where the chargers are located, check in with the front desk or leasing office for charger location and access to the parking garage if applicable\n\n**Scope:**\n\n- Follow attached Firmware Update Guide for step-by-step instructions, to complete firmware update on each charger\n- Take a screenshot of each quick report to show that the firmware is updated and include in attachments section\n- Notify Xeal immediately if you encounter any of the following:\n- If any charger does not have the power light on, or if any red fault lights are on (Power Fault or Charging Fault)\n- If any chargers are in use (plugged into a car) upon arrival (DO NOT unplug charger from any vehicle, contact front desk/leasing office if any are plugged in for them to reach out to the driver to unplug)\n- If update was not able to be completed for any reason and on which charger(s)\n- If test session is unsuccessful, as well as any error messages you encounter\n- If chargers are visibly dirty, wipe them down with a damp cloth or cleaning wipe.\n- If cords are not wrapped, wrap cord neatly around charger and plug end into the designated holster\n- Take pictures of chargers once everything is complete\n\n***Note: Showing up to site without the proper device type (smartphone compatible with Xeal mobile app) will result in incomplete/nonpayment for the work order.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T10:00","end":"2026-11-11T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-11T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":90,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11.09873268866101},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ericsson"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-09T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T22:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794249287111}
{"job":{"id":20330516,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pomeroy","title":"PDC - ALDI IMAC SUPPORT (Please replace the POE injector on the EFT at Lane 3)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>NEW - It is required to have this work order,&nbsp;as well as the page with your name badge,&nbsp;printed and taken with you to site. It is highly suggested that you add a photo so that the store can see it Is you with your State ID.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must check in and out with the Aldi Global Service Desk @&nbsp;866-711-2534 and with POMEROY DISPATCH CENTER -- 704-414-5131.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Technical Support :</u></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Pomeroy Technical Support - 704-414-5111 Open 8am-8pm EST</strong></p><p><strong>TRS: </strong>https://trs.pomeroy.com/aldi-foods</p><p><strong>Description of issue:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Please replace the POE injector on the EFT at Lane 3, unit not communicating</p><p>Replacement onsite</p><p>Once replaced, test with MOD and call the GSD to checkout</p><p>Thank you</p><p><br></p><p>On Site Contact Name:&nbsp;</p><p>On Site Contact Phone:&nbsp;</p><p>On Site Contact Email:&nbsp;</p><p>Problem Type: PROBLEM DESCRIBED IN NOTES</p><p>Location Subtype:&nbsp;</p><p>Lane Number (if applicable): 3</p><p>Client Ticket Number/External Reference ID: REQ2978945</p><p><strong>Description of Parts Shipped by Pomeroy:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Part onsite </p><p><br></p><p><strong>UPS Tracking #</strong>: Part Onsite </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Parts Tracking:&nbsp;</strong>Tech is responsible for tracking parts (if applicable).&nbsp;If parts have not arrived by 5 pm local time, please call Pomeroy Call Coordinators to report tracking issues <strong><em>BEFORE</em></strong> visiting site. <strong><em>Pomeroy&nbsp;is not responsible for techs arriving before parts.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Arrival Time:&nbsp;</strong>If parts are shipped then track parts and run call within 2 hours of delivery. If no parts are needed for the call,&nbsp;run the call between 9 am and 3 pm the day the call is due.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Items:</strong></p><ul><li>Basic Set of Tools (pliers screw drivers, cutters, etc.)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Only accept this job if you have all the required tools, and are able to make the required time frame.</strong></p><p><strong>Required Items:</strong></p><ul><li>Basic hand tools kit (pliers, screwdrivers, cutters etc)</li><li>Paper Clip</li></ul><p><strong>Only accept this job if you have all the required tools, and are able to make the required time frame.</strong></p><p><strong>Parts Handling Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>It is the responsibility of the assigned tech to track parts. Pomeroy will provide tracking numbers for any shipped parts when they become available.</li><li>&nbsp;- If no tracking number has been provided by 10am the morning of the assignment, it is up to <strong>YOU</strong>, the technician, to call the Pomeroy Dispatch Center to get this tracking number.</li><li>&nbsp;Pomeroy is NOT responsible for techs arriving before parts and will NOT compensate for unnecessary trips or wait time.</li><li>&nbsp;- Technician may also be held financially responsible for equipment lost due to negligence or failure to follow instruction.</li></ol><p><strong>Communication Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li><u>Any issues with scheduling, running late, unable to show up, etc. MUST BE CALLED IN TO THE POMEROY DISPATCH CENTER. Messages left on the platform are not acceptable forms of communication.</u>&nbsp;</li><li>This will result in penalties, negative ratings, being unassigned from the work order, and may affect future work for our company.</li><li>- Please be sure your Voicemail is functional should we need to leave a message.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Pomeroy Dispatch Center – <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></li><li>Tech Support – <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></li></ol><p><strong>Work Order Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Be prepared with all documentation and understanding for scope of work</li><li>You MUST bring all the tools in the Required Tool List to site to avoid penalties</li><li>All documentation needs to be printed or downloaded to a device accessible while onsite</li><li>If you have any questions call Pomeroy before going onsite</li><li>When parts arrive – go onsite</li><li>Call the Stores Held Desk if applicable</li><li>Advise the site that you are representing Pomeroy</li><li>Ask for and record name of manager on duty</li><li>Locate parts and start work</li><li>Call Tech support as needed at <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></li><li>Upon completion of work the following will be needed for check out:</li><li>- Mangers name</li><li>- Name of anyone you spoke with at the Help Desk if applicable</li><li>- Serial number of Old and New parts</li><li>- Rtags for Old and New Parts (if applicable)</li><li>Please update all the required information in the work order before marking it as work done.</li></ol>","markdown":"**NEW - It is required to have this work order, as well as the page with your name badge, printed and taken with you to site. It is highly suggested that you add a photo so that the store can see it Is you with your State ID.**\n\n**Tech must check in and out with the Aldi Global Service Desk @ 866-711-2534 and with POMEROY DISPATCH CENTER -- 704-414-5131.**\n\n**Technical Support :** **Pomeroy Technical Support - 704-414-5111 Open 8am-8pm EST**\n\n**TRS:** <https://trs.pomeroy.com/aldi-foods>\n\n**Description of issue:**\n\nPlease replace the POE injector on the EFT at Lane 3, unit not communicating\n\nReplacement onsite\n\nOnce replaced, test with MOD and call the GSD to checkout\n\nThank you\n\nOn Site Contact Name:\n\nOn Site Contact Phone:\n\nOn Site Contact Email:\n\nProblem Type: PROBLEM DESCRIBED IN NOTES\n\nLocation Subtype:\n\nLane Number (if applicable): 3\n\nClient Ticket Number/External Reference ID: REQ2978945\n\n**Description of Parts Shipped by Pomeroy:** Part onsite\n\n**UPS Tracking #**: Part Onsite\n\n**Parts Tracking:** Tech is responsible for tracking parts (if applicable). If parts have not arrived by 5 pm local time, please call Pomeroy Call Coordinators to report tracking issues ***BEFORE*** visiting site. ***Pomeroy is not responsible for techs arriving before parts.***\n\n**Arrival Time:** If parts are shipped then track parts and run call within 2 hours of delivery. If no parts are needed for the call, run the call between 9 am and 3 pm the day the call is due.\n\n**Required Items:**\n\n- Basic Set of Tools (pliers screw drivers, cutters, etc.)\n\n**Only accept this job if you have all the required tools, and are able to make the required time frame.**\n\n**Required Items:**\n\n- Basic hand tools kit (pliers, screwdrivers, cutters etc)\n- Paper Clip\n\n**Only accept this job if you have all the required tools, and are able to make the required time frame.**\n\n**Parts Handling Requirements:**\n\n1. It is the responsibility of the assigned tech to track parts. Pomeroy will provide tracking numbers for any shipped parts when they become available.\n2. - If no tracking number has been provided by 10am the morning of the assignment, it is up to **YOU**, the technician, to call the Pomeroy Dispatch Center to get this tracking number.\n3. Pomeroy is NOT responsible for techs arriving before parts and will NOT compensate for unnecessary trips or wait time.\n4. - Technician may also be held financially responsible for equipment lost due to negligence or failure to follow instruction.\n\n**Communication Requirements:**\n\n1. Any issues with scheduling, running late, unable to show up, etc. MUST BE CALLED IN TO THE POMEROY DISPATCH CENTER. Messages left on the platform are not acceptable forms of communication.\n2. This will result in penalties, negative ratings, being unassigned from the work order, and may affect future work for our company.\n3. - Please be sure your Voicemail is functional should we need to leave a message.\n4. Pomeroy Dispatch Center – \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n5. Tech Support – \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Work Order Requirements:**\n\n1. Be prepared with all documentation and understanding for scope of work\n2. You MUST bring all the tools in the Required Tool List to site to avoid penalties\n3. All documentation needs to be printed or downloaded to a device accessible while onsite\n4. If you have any questions call Pomeroy before going onsite\n5. When parts arrive – go onsite\n6. Call the Stores Held Desk if applicable\n7. Advise the site that you are representing Pomeroy\n8. Ask for and record name of manager on duty\n9. Locate parts and start work\n10. Call Tech support as needed at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n11. Upon completion of work the following will be needed for check out:\n12. - Mangers name\n13. - Name of anyone you spoke with at the Help Desk if applicable\n14. - Serial number of Old and New parts\n15. - Rtags for Old and New Parts (if applicable)\n16. Please update all the required information in the work order before marking it as work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T11:00","end":"2026-11-10T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8.620255507338562},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.00