nts may result in non-payment.</p>","markdown":"**Network Technician - Revisit work**\n\n**Site Specific Notes/Action Items:**\n\n**Bridge Information:** Details will be provided in the messages section of your work order.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nTechnicians will perform network equipment installation, replacement, configuration, and troubleshooting at retail locations. Work may include Meraki, Cradlepoint, Grandstream, SIM cards, WAN connectivity, telephone systems, and remediation of existing issues.\n\n- Refer to Site-Specific Notes for exact scope and remaining tasks.\n- Join the bridge immediately upon arrival and follow remote engineer instructions.\n- For site access issues, contact the remote team through the bridge.\n\n**Required Tools &amp; Equipment:**\n\n- Mobile phone with a camera and charger\n- Driver's license or state-issued photo ID\n- Laptop with Ethernet (RJ45) and USB connections (Required console drivers installed)\n- Console cable (DB9) with USB adapter\n- Micro USB-to-USB-B console cable for router connection (must be tested with your laptop before arrival)\n- 2 x Cat5e patch cables (1 x 10-meter and 1 x 3-meter)\n- Engineer to take a Cisco console cable CAP-CONSOLE (RH45-DB9 Female)\n- Remote access software: Microsoft Teams / AnyDesk\n- Standard technician toolkit\n- Cage nuts, screws, and screw drivers.\n- Labels/Label maker\n\nFailure to bring required tools or equipment may result in non-payment.\n\n**Scheduling &amp; Time Requirements:**\n\n- 2-hour minimum per site. Any time beyond 2 hours requires prior approval from your Work Order Manager before exceeding.\n- You must remain on site to complete the work until the bridge has released you.\n- Arrive promptly at your scheduled start time. Visits are coordinated with remote engineers, making punctuality critical.\n- Notify your Work Order Manager immediately of any anticipated delays.\n- Visits cannot be rescheduled once assigned.\n- Only the assigned technician is authorized onsite. No substitutions.\n\n**Bridge &amp; Site Release Requirements:**\n\n- Remain connected with the remote team and follow their instructions throughout the visit.\n- Do not leave site until all work is completed and the bridge has formally released you.\n- Record the name of the remote engineer authorizing your release.\n- Contact your Work Order Manager with any questions, issues, or escalations.\n- Check out with your Work Order Manager before departing, and after your documentation and deliverables have been uploaded.\n\n**Mandatory Documentation &amp; Deliverables:**\n\nComplete and upload the following before leaving site:\n\n- Before-and-after photos of completed work.\n- Signed Site Visit Report (SVR) with start/stop times matching the work order.\n- Name of the remote engineer who authorized site release.\n\nMissing deliverables, including the signed SVR, may result in non-payment.\n\n**Materials &amp; Reimbursements:**\n\n- Obtain Work Order Manager approval before purchasing materials. Unapproved purchases may not be reimbursed.\n- Upload receipts or an invoice for all approved material purchases.\n- All reimbursement receipts must be uploaded to the work order by 8:00 AM the following morning to ensure processing.\n\nImportant: Do not leave site without bridge release, required documentation uploaded, and checkout with your Work Order Manager. Failure to follow work order requirements may result in non-payment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T08:00","end":"2026-11-11T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":160},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":80},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":55.52655218164635},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"st