{"job":{"id":20334097,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network Support Tech Required","description":{"html":"<p>Please follow the instructions :-</p><p><strong>1. Do not leave the site</strong> without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.</p><p><strong>2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)</strong>before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.</p><p><strong>3. Dress Code:</strong>Business casual attire is required.</p><p><strong>4. Do not discuss the pay rate</strong> onsite with the customer or any other employees.</p><p><strong>5. Site Visit Report:</strong> After completing the visit, you <strong>must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order</strong>. This is <strong>mandatory for work order approval</strong>.</p><p><strong>Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>8.Short description of the reported issue: Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.</p><p><br></p><p>9.If L1/L2 is required: L2</p><p><br></p><p>10.Mandate Action required:</p><p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p><p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.</p><p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support</p><p><br></p><p>11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:</p><p>-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).</p><p>-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p><p>-10 ft data cable.</p><p>-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch</p><p>-Cable tester&nbsp;</p><p>-Tone generator&nbsp;</p><p>-Toner</p><p><br></p><p>12.Scope of Work:</p><p>&nbsp;Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>13.After the completion of Visit:</p><p>Update the SVR with Resolution Steps</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Please follow the instructions :-\n\n**1. Do not leave the site** without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.\n\n**2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)**before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n**3. Dress Code:**Business casual attire is required.\n\n**4. Do not discuss the pay rate** onsite with the customer or any other employees.\n\n**5. Site Visit Report:** After completing the visit, you **must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order**. This is **mandatory for work order approval**.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\n8.Short description of the reported issue: Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.\n\n9.If L1/L2 is required: L2\n\n10.Mandate Action required:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.\n\nEngineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.\n\nOvation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support\n\n11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:\n\n-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).\n\n-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.\n\n-10 ft data cable.\n\n-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch\n\n-Cable tester\n\n-Tone generator\n\n-Toner\n\n12.Scope of Work:\n\n Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.\n\n13.After the completion of Visit:\n\nUpdate the SVR with Resolution Steps","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"star