{"job":{"id":20334378,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Connected Solutions Group","title":" Basic indoor router  Installation ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in installing network equipment and accessories.</li><li>Tech is required to perform installations of routers, antennas, and related hardware according to provided guidelines.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 2 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business casual attire; unbranded polo shirt with black or kahki pants</li><li>Closed toe shoes</li><li>PPE ( Hard Hat, High - Visibility Vest / Pants)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required to be Provided by Techican: </strong></p><ul><li>Patch cable</li><li>RJ45 Crimper with male ends</li><li>Ethernet cable tester</li><li>Biscuit Jack / Keystone</li><li>Drill with drill bits</li><li>Impact with Phillips/flathead bits</li><li>Socket Adapter with socket set (imperial and metric)</li><li>Wrench set (imperial and metric)</li><li>8-foot (minimum) ladder</li><li>Zip Ties / Velcro</li><li>Extension cord</li><li>Pull rope</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Smartphone</li></ul><p><strong>Shipped Equipment Box Contents:</strong></p><ul><li>1x m519 5G Router</li><li>1x Power adapter</li><li>2x Wi-Fi antennas</li><li>4x 5G NR / 4G LTE antennas</li><li>1x Ethernet Cable</li><li>1x User Manual</li><li>1x Warranty card</li><li>1x Wall-mount kit</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Review the installation guide to familiarize yourself with the installation requirements before arriving to the site.</li><li>Check-in with the CSG installation team by calling <del>************</del> upon arrival.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order, introduce yourself as a<del> *** **** ***** **********</del> onsite, and provide a general overview of the installation plan.</li><li>. Locate the equipment CSG has shipped for the installation. </li><li>Take pictures of all hardware shipped before starting the installation process.</li></ol><p><br></p><ol><li><u>Install M519 Router </u></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(Wall Mount Instructions) :</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Choose an appropriate location: Select a spot on the wall where the router will have good&nbsp;venison and is within reach of a power outlet.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Mark the Drill Points: Hold the wall bracket against the wall in the desired position. Use a level&nbsp;to ensure it's straight. Mark the drill points through the holes in the bracket.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Drill Holes: <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Drill holes at the marked points. The size of the drill bit should match the wall plugs you're going to use.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Insert Wall Plugs: If the wall requires them, insert wall plugs into the drilled holes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Attach the Bracket: Align the tabs on the upper bracket with the opening on the lower bracket&nbsp;and push inward.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Push downward on the unit to seat it in the bracket.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(Drop Ceiling Mount Instructions):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Using zip ties, screws mount the bracket to the drop ceiling.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">2. Trim the zip ties access.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">&nbsp;Slide the m519 into the bracket, until a click sound</li><li><u>Connect and power on m519 Router:</u></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PoE injector “PoE port” → Splitter “PoE Input port”</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Splitter “Network output port” -&gt; LAN Port m519</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If Power over Ethernet (PoE) is not accessible, please connect the AC power cord.</li><li>Ensure proper placement and secure mounting of hardware.</li><li>Test connectivity and functionality of installed equipment before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><strong>Cleanup:&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Remove any debris generated during the survey&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Clean up any tools/ladders that were used&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place survey equipment in original packaging and ready for return&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tidy up cables&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power off all devices&nbsp;</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Completed installation as per provided guidelines.</li><li>Photos of before and after installation.</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ALL photo documentation should be uploaded to FastFields app prior to leaving the site.</li></ul><ol><li>Sign-off from onsite contact confirming satisfactory completion of work.</li><li>Check-out of work order.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Check-out of Work Order:</strong></p><ul><li>Text or call&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to check out with CSG FS.</li><li>Return any client’s property used during the survey.</li><li>Check out with the local contact IN PERSON.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with CSG installation team or work order manager.</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the CSG installation team at <del>*************</del></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours or expenses incurred must be pre-approved by contacting the CSG installation team.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in installing network equipment and accessories.\n- Tech is required to perform installations of routers, antennas, and related hardware according to provided guidelines.\n- Estimated duration will be 2 hours.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business casual attire; unbranded polo shirt with black or kahki pants\n- Closed toe shoes\n- PPE ( Hard Hat, High - Visibility Vest / Pants)\n\n**Tools Required to be Provided by Techican:**\n\n- Patch cable\n- RJ45 Crimper with male ends\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- Biscuit Jack / Keystone\n- Drill with drill bits\n- Impact with Phillips/flathead bits\n- Socket Adapter with socket set (imperial and metric)\n- Wrench set (imperial and metric)\n- 8-foot (minimum) ladder\n- Zip Ties / Velcro\n- Extension cord\n- Pull rope\n- Label maker\n- Laptop\n- Smartphone\n\n**Shipped Equipment Box Contents:**\n\n- 1x m519 5G Router\n- 1x Power adapter\n- 2x Wi-Fi antennas\n- 4x 5G NR / 4G LTE antennas\n- 1x Ethernet Cable\n- 1x User Manual\n- 1x Warranty card\n- 1x Wall-mount kit\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Review the installation guide to familiarize yourself with the installation requirements before arriving to the site.\n2. Check-in with the CSG installation team by calling \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* upon arrival.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check-in to work order, introduce yourself as a \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* onsite, and provide a general overview of the installation plan.\n2. . Locate the equipment CSG has shipped for the installation.\n3. Take pictures of all hardware shipped before starting the installation process.\n\n1. Install M519 Router\n2. (Wall Mount Instructions) :\n3. Choose an appropriate location: Select a spot on the wall where the router will have good venison and is within reach of a power outlet.\n4. Mark the Drill Points: Hold the wall bracket against the wall in the desired position. Use a level to ensure it's straight. Mark the drill points through the holes in the bracket.\n5. Drill Holes: Drill holes at the marked points. The size of the drill bit should match the wall plugs you're going to use.\n6. Insert Wall Plugs: If the wall requires them, insert wall plugs into the drilled holes\n7. Attach the Bracket: Align the tabs on the upper bracket with the opening on the lower bracket and push inward.\n8. Push downward on the unit to seat it in the bracket.\n9. (Drop Ceiling Mount Instructions):\n10. Using zip ties, screws mount the bracket to the drop ceiling.\n11. 2. Trim the zip ties access.\n12. Slide the m519 into the bracket, until a click sound\n13. Connect and power on m519 Router:\n14. PoE injector “PoE port” → Splitter “PoE Input port”\n15. Splitter “Network output port” -&gt; LAN Port m519\n16. If Power over Ethernet (PoE) is not accessible, please connect the AC power cord.\n17. Ensure proper placement and secure mounting of hardware.\n18. Test connectivity and functionality of installed equipment before leaving the site.\n\n**Cleanup:**\n\n1. Remove any debris generated during the survey\n2. Clean up any tools/ladders that were used\n3. Place survey equipment in original packaging and ready for return\n4. Tidy up cables\n5. Power off all devices\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Completed installation as per provided guidelines.\n2. Photos of before and after installation.\n\n- ALL photo documentation should be uploaded to FastFields app prior to leaving the site.\n\n1. Sign-off from onsite contact confirming satisfactory completion of work.\n2. Check-out of work order.\n\n**Check-out of Work Order:**\n\n- Text or call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check out with CSG FS.\n- Return any client’s property used during the survey.\n- Check out with the local contact IN PERSON.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with CSG installation team or work order manager.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the CSG installation team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours or expenses incurred must be pre-approved by contacting the CSG installation team.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T1