{"job":{"id":20334742,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ACP CreativIT","title":"NVMe / SATA Hard Drive Upgrade","description":{"html":"<p><strong>OVERVIEW</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>This installation is expected to take no longer that 4 hours.</p><p>The scope of work can be broken down to three functions.</p><p><strong>F1:</strong> Inventor/Audit of ALL Operatory room Desktop (16 max) &amp; 1 LAB PC.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;An Excel spreadsheet has been included in the work order. This</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;sheet is to be used to capture the inventory of the rooms. The</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;sheet must be filled in completely and uploaded back into the</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work Order to complete the order.</p><p><strong>F2:</strong> The number of desktop computers to be completed will be confirmed on site </p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NVMe &amp; SATA data drives with new NVMe &amp; SATA</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;drives. All patient \"operatory\" rooms and the</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;main LAB room. The Onsite Staff Lead will select which rooms are</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;to upgraded. Upgrading will require power down of PC, removing</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;the legacy drive, using the duplicators that have been provided,</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;clone the original drive image to the new drive. Then reinstall</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;the new drive into the PC and confirm functional operations.</p><p><strong>F3:</strong> Closing out the work order. All data drives are to be placed</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;into the original Materials box. A UPS Return label has been</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;provided. Any spare parts and all uninstalled drives are to be</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;placed packed, the return label applied to the box and given to</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;the Site Staff Lead, to coordinate pick up by the carrier.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Detailed instructions are listed below.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p>This Work Order is a<strong> \"FIXED\" </strong>Schedule and is not subject to change. Do NOT request different dates or times.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;NOTE: </strong>On occasion, a PC will not match the drive specification provided in the materials shipped to site. The Field Tech is to work with the staff to locate another PC that has the correct drive type, and swap PC. This PC can be pulled from the Administration Office or other Non-specific areas. T The Field Tech<strong> MAY NOT</strong> use the following:</p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;X-Ray Room</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Consultation Room</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any All-In-One PC</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Onsite Requirements and Dress Code:</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Provider must have Good English-speaking skills.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You are representing the Tusker organization while onsite. No other competitive branding is to be displayed.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Your clothing should be fit for the work you are doing and the environment you will be in. This is a clinic, clothing should be clean in appearance.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Denim is acceptable in clean and good condition. Button Down or Polo shirts OK, No T-Shirts, No torn-off sleeves.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work shoes or boots.</p><p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED</strong></p><p>Provider is expected to have the following tools:</p><ul><li>&nbsp;Laptop and/or Smart phone</li><li>Must be able to connect to the client's Guest network.</li><li>Must have photo capabilities</li><li>Must be able to access MS Teams.</li><li>MS Excel application.</li><li>Download the Excel spreadsheet that is attached to this work order.</li><li>Computer Tool Kit:</li><li>Light Screw Driver(s) or switchable drive with assorted bits Phillips and T screws.</li><li>&nbsp;Magnetic stick, to pick up small screws.</li><li>Marker/Sharpy pen</li><li>Latex Gloves (optional &ndash; recommended)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p><p>&nbsp;Able to understand and follow these instructions and understand all other instructions provided with this work order.</p><p>Able to use the resources on the Bridge Call to ask questions.</p><p>Inventory materials shipped to location.&nbsp;</p><p>Provide timely status updates to Bridge Technical Support team regarding completed tasks, progress and timelines, and potential risks.</p><p>Maintain a high level of professionalism and safety awareness.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Before Arriving Onsite</strong></p><p>This is an \"all Inclusive\" fixed bid work order. There are no reimbursements for supplies or materials required for executing this installation without prior authorization. If authorization is approved, please note the name of the person who authorized the reimbursement on the claim.</p><p>Fully review all documentation and have a hard copy of all instructions onsite.</p><p>Must have access to MS Teams app (Laptop and/or Smart Mobile device).</p><p>Download and have easy access to the excel spreadsheet.</p><p>Arrive on time or early.</p><p>Use Field Nation tools to validate when you are on route to client site.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>WORK ORDER DESCRIPTION</strong></p><p><strong>Check-In and arriving onsite</strong></p><p>Check in on the Field Nation app when in the parking lot.</p><p>Meet the onsite point of contact and request access to the pre-delivered materials.</p><p>Ask the Point of Contact to identify the Operatory Rooms (Exam Rooms) that are used the most.</p><p>Join the MS Team Bridge and let the Bridge-Host know that you have arrive and are starting the Bill of Materials inventory.</p><p><strong>NOTE: </strong>For internet access on your laptop or if your cell phone service is weak, connect to the Aspen Dental Guest Network.</p><p>Password:&nbsp;<strong><em>dentalpatient</em></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Confirm Operatory room numbers with site contact and ensure that you will have access to each of them and any discuss any restrictions or scheduling conflicts you need to be aware of.</p><p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Upgrades will be performed in only the Operatory rooms and one (1) LAB room. All remaining rooms will remain as they are.&nbsp;</p><p>After shipping inventory is complete, using the Excel spreadsheet in the work order, the tech shall Audit every Operatory Room and provide the specific information that is requested in the spread sheet. This includes all Operatory rooms regardless of upgrade or not.</p><p>This includes</p><p>Room Name/#, PC Brand, PC Model, PC Serial No., PC Network Name.</p><p><strong>NOTE:</strong> PC Name will be visible on an external Asset tag affixed to the PC. The format will be:&nbsp;AGDT-<em>serial###</em></p><p>Enter the 1st Operatory room and power down the work station. Examples of PC locations are displayed at the end of this document.</p><p>Unbox the cloning device that was provided in the shipped box provided earlier. Connect the device to power outlet. <strong>DO NOT CONNECT To THE PC. Do NOT Power On. </strong>Remove the PC cover.</p><p><em>Device-specific details are provided and attached to the work order</em>.</p><p>When clearly accessible, remove the anchor screw for NVMe, or remove the mount screw for the SATA.</p><p>Insert the original (source) drive into the Clone device \"Source\" port.&nbsp;Unbox the new drive (save the plastic container), then insert the new drive into the \"Target\" port.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>For NVMe: When both the source &amp; targe drive have been seated in the clone device, power on the Clone Device. Both Label LEDs will light up steady.</p><p>Press &amp; hold the CLONE button on the front right side of the device for 3 to 5 seconds until the blue progress lights start flashing.</p><p>Then press &amp; release that button again. The blue progress lights will continue to flash and will lock ON as each progress marker is met.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Cloning process will approximately 11 minutes.</p><p>While clone process is running, identify and begin to stage the next Operatory room.</p><p>&nbsp;IN THE NEXT ROOM:</p><p>-Power down the PC,</p><p>-Remove the cover, and if time allows,</p><p>-Remove the drive.</p><p>-RETURN TO THE ACITIVE ROOM to complete the imaging process.</p><p>When 100% complete, all blues lights will be lit solid.</p><p>Power off the Clone device before removing the drives from their ports.</p><p>Provider should use the Sharpy pen and mark/label the original drive with the corresponding room # that it is installed in. Then placethe old drive into the package of the new drive.</p><p>Before reassembling the PCin th eprevious room, take the Cloning Device to the NEXT ROOM. Remove the drive (if still required) from the PC and place it in the \"Source\" port of the Cloner. Open new drive and place it in the Target port, and initiate the cloning process.</p><p>Return to the LAST ROOM, install the new drive into the computer.</p><p>Reassemble the PC and power it on.</p><p>In the MS Team chat, tell the Aspen Support Tema that Room #XX is complete, and give them the Computer Name.</p><p>Return to the active upgrade room. If progress is 50%, identify and prepare the next room for the upgrade:</p><p>-Power down the PC,</p><p>-Remove the cover, and if time allows,</p><p>-Remove the drive.</p><p>&nbsp;Return to the active room to complete the imaging process.</p><p>When 100% complete, all blues lights will be lit solid.</p><p>Power off the Clone device before removing the drives from their ports.</p><p>Provider should use the Sharpy pen and mark/label the original drive with the corresponding room # that it is installed in. Then place the old drive into the package of the new drive.</p><p>Before reassembling the last PC, take the Cloning Device to the Next Room, remove the Drive from the PC and place it in the Source port of the Cloner. Open new drive and place it in the Target port, and initiate the cloning process of the 3rdnd room.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>REPEAT THEIS PROCESS</strong> for all seven Operatory rooms and the LAB room.</p><p>When all desktops have been upgraded, begin repacking the cloning device(s)in it original box and put the old drives into the original shipping box. Place the Return Shipping label over the original label and give it to the Point of contact.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"></p><p>&nbsp;Ask them to tape up the box and make sure that UPS services pick it up. When the Aspen Support team has completed all their scripts, and the all devices are operational, the Tech can leave.</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Post Site Activity</strong></p><p>Provider will update work order closeout activities in Field Nation app and will upload the excel spreadsheet to the Work order. No invoice will be paid without the spreadsheet. If not loaded in 24 hours, a fee of 10% of total invoice will be applied. 48+ hours late, 50% of total invoice will be applied. We don't want the fees, please, just complete and post the sheet as quick as you can.</p><p><strong>Documentation</strong></p><p><strong>Attached to the work order are the following documents to assist </strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;PC Brand &amp; Model specific instructions</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Dell Pro Max Slim</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Lenovo P330</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Lenovo P340</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Lenovo P360</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;Drive Specific Duplicator Instructions</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;NVMe Clone Instructions</strong></p><p><strong>o&nbsp;&nbsp;SATA Clone instructions.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Workstation Placement Examples - Please Reference Photos Attached in Document.&nbsp;</strong></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\nThis installation is expected to take no longer that 4 hours.\n\nThe scope of work can be broken down to three functions.\n\n**F1:** Inventor/Audit of ALL Operatory room Desktop (16 max) &amp; 1 LAB PC.\n\n An Excel spreadsheet has been included in the work order. This\n\n sheet is to be used to capture the inventory of the rooms. The\n\n sheet must be filled in completely and uploaded back into the\n\n Work Order to complete the order.\n\n**F2:** The number of desktop computers to be completed will be confirmed on site\n\n NVMe &amp; SATA data drives with new NVMe &amp; SATA\n\n drives. All patient \"operatory\" rooms and the\n\n main LAB room. The Onsite Staff Lead will select which rooms are\n\n to upgraded. Upgrading will require power down of PC, removing\n\n the legacy drive, using the duplicators that have been provided,\n\n clone the original drive image to the new drive. Then reinstall\n\n the new drive into the PC and confirm functional operations.\n\n**F3:** Closing out the work order. All data drives are to be placed\n\n into the original Materials box. A UPS Return label has been\n\n provided. Any spare parts and all uninstalled drives are to be\n\n placed packed, the return label applied to the box and given to\n\n the Site Staff Lead, to coordinate pick up by the carrier.\n\n Detailed instructions are listed below.\n\nThis Work Order is a **\"FIXED\"** Schedule and is not subject to change. Do NOT request different dates or times.\n\n **NOTE:** On occasion, a PC will not match the drive specification provided in the materials shipped to site. The Field Tech is to work with the staff to locate another PC that has the correct drive type, and swap PC. This PC can be pulled from the Administration Office or other Non-specific areas. T The Field Tech **MAY NOT** use the following:\n\n**· X-Ray Room**\n\n**· Consultation Room**\n\n**· Any All-In-One PC**\n\n**Onsite Requirements and Dress Code:**\n\n**·**  Provider must have Good English-speaking skills.\n\n· You are representing the Tusker organization while onsite. No other competitive branding is to be displayed.\n\n· Your clothing should be fit for the work you are doing and the environment you will be in. This is a clinic, clothing should be clean in appearance.\n\n· Denim is acceptable in clean and good condition. Button Down or Polo shirts OK, No T-Shirts, No torn-off sleeves.\n\n· Work shoes or boots.\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED**\n\nProvider is expected to have the following tools:\n\n- Laptop and/or Smart phone\n- Must be able to connect to the client's Guest network.\n- Must have photo capabilities\n- Must be able to access MS Teams.\n- MS Excel application.\n- Download the Excel spreadsheet that is attached to this work order.\n- Computer Tool Kit:\n- Light Screw Driver(s) or switchable drive with assorted bits Phillips and T screws.\n- Magnetic stick, to pick up small screws.\n- Marker/Sharpy pen\n- Latex Gloves (optional – recommended)\n\n**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**\n\n Able to understand and follow these instructions and understand all other instructions provided with this work order.\n\nAble to use the resources on the Bridge Call to ask questions.\n\nInventory materials shipped to location.\n\nProvide timely status updates to Bridge Technical Support team regarding completed tasks, progress and timelines, and potential risks.\n\nMaintain a high level of professionalism and safety awareness.\n\n**Before Arriving Onsite**\n\nThis is an \"all Inclusive\" fixed bid work order. There are no reimbursements for supplies or materials required for executing this installation without prior authorization. If authorization is approved, please note the name of the person who authorized the reimbursement on the claim.\n\nFully review all documentation and have a hard copy of all instructions onsite.\n\nMust have access to MS Teams app (Laptop and/or Smart Mobile device).\n\nDownload and have easy access to the excel spreadsheet.\n\nArrive on time or early.\n\nUse Field Nation tools to validate when you are on route to client site.\n\n**WORK ORDER DESCRIPTION**\n\n**Check-In and arriving onsite**\n\nCheck in on the Field Nation app when in the parking lot.\n\nMeet the onsite point of contact and request access to the pre-delivered materials.\n\nAsk the Point of Contact to identify the Operatory Rooms (Exam Rooms) that are used the most.\n\nJoin the MS Team Bridge and let the Bridge-Host know that you have arrive and are starting the Bill of Materials inventory.\n\n**NOTE:** For internet access on your laptop or if your cell phone service is weak, connect to the Aspen Dental Guest Network.\n\nPassword: ***dentalpatient***\n\nConfirm Operatory room numbers with site contact and ensure that you will have access to each of them and any discuss any restrictions or scheduling conflicts you need to be aware of.\n\n**NOTE:** Upgrades will be performed in only the Operatory rooms and one (1) LAB room. All remaining rooms will remain as they are.\n\nAfter shipping inventory is complete, using the Excel spreadsheet in the work order, the tech shall Audit every Operatory Room and provide the specific information that is requested in the spread sheet. This includes all Operatory rooms regardless of upgrade or not.\n\nThis includes\n\nRoom Name/#, PC Brand, PC Model, PC Serial No., PC Network Name.\n\n**NOTE:** PC Name will be visible on an external Asset tag affixed to the PC. The format will be: AGDT-*serial###*\n\nEnter the 1st Operatory room and power down the work station. Examples of PC locations are displayed at the end of this document.\n\nUnbox the cloning device that was provided in the shipped box provided earlier. Connect the device to power outlet. **DO NOT CONNECT To THE PC. Do NOT Power On.** Remove the PC cover.\n\n*Device-specific details are provided and attached to the work order*.\n\nWhen clearly accessible, remove the anchor screw for NVMe, or remove the mount screw for the SATA.\n\nInsert the original (source) drive into the Clone device \"Source\" port. Unbox the new drive (save the plastic container), then insert the new drive into the \"Target\" port.\n\nFor NVMe: When both the source &amp; targe drive have been seated in the clone device, power on the Clone Device. Both Label LEDs will light up steady.\n\nPress &amp; hold the CLONE button on the front right side of the device for 3 to 5 seconds until the blue progress lights start flashing.\n\nThen press &amp; release that button again. The blue progress lights will continue to flash and will lock ON as each progress marker is met.\n\nCloning process will approximately 11 minutes.\n\nWhile clone process is running, identify and begin to stage the next Operatory room.\n\n IN THE NEXT ROOM:\n\n-Power down the PC,\n\n-Remove the cover, and if time allows,\n\n-Remove the drive.\n\n-RETURN TO THE ACITIVE ROOM to complete the imaging process.\n\nWhen 100% complete, all blues lights will be lit solid.\n\nPower off the Clone device before removing the drives from their ports.\n\nProvider should use the Sharpy pen and mark/label the original drive with the corresponding room # that it is installed in. Then placethe old drive into the package of the new drive.\n\nBefore reassembling the PCin th eprevious room, take the Cloning Device to the NEXT ROOM. Remove the drive (if still required) from the PC and place it in the \"Source\" port of the Cloner. Open new drive and place it in the Target port, and initiate the cloning process.\n\nReturn to the LAST ROOM, install the new drive into the computer.\n\nReassemble the PC and power it on.\n\nIn the MS Team chat, tell the Aspen Support Tema that Room #XX is complete, and give them the Computer Name.\n\nReturn to the active upgrade room. If progress is 50%, identify and prepare the next room for the upgrade:\n\n-Power down the PC,\n\n-Remove the cover, and if time allows,\n\n-Remove the drive.\n\n Return to the active room to complete the imaging process.\n\nWhen 100% complete, all blues lights will be lit solid.\n\nPower off the Clone device before removing the drives from their ports.\n\nProvider should use the Sharpy pen and mark/label the original drive with the corresponding room # that it is installed in. Then place the old drive into the package of the new drive.\n\nBefore reassembling the last PC, take the Cloning Device to the Next Room, remove the Drive from the PC and place it in the Source port of the Cloner. Open new drive and place it in the Target port, and initiate the cloning process of the 3rdnd room.\n\n**REPEAT THEIS PROCESS** for all seven Operatory rooms and the LAB room.\n\nWhen all desktops have been upgraded, begin repacking the cloning device(s)in it original box and put the old drives into the original shipping box. Place the Return Shipping label over the original label and give it to the Point of contact.\n\n![](data:image/jpeg;base64,) ![](data:image/jpeg;base64,)\n\n Ask them to tape up the box and make sure that UPS services pick it up. When the Aspen Support team has completed all their scripts, and the all devices are operational, the Tech can leave.\n\n **Post Site Activity**\n\nProvider will update work order closeout activities in Field Nation app and will upload the excel spreadsheet to the Work order. No invoice will be paid without the spreadsheet. If not loaded in 24 hours, a fee of 10% of total invoice will be applied. 48+ hours late, 50% of total invoice will be applied. We don't want the fees, please, just complete and post the sheet as quick as you can.\n\n**Documentation**\n\n**Attached to the work order are the following documents to assist**\n\n**o PC Brand &amp; Model specific instructions**\n\n**o Dell Pro Max Slim**\n\n**o Lenovo P330**\n\n**o Lenovo P340**\n\n**o Lenovo P360**\n\n**o Drive Specific Duplicator Instructions**\n\n**o NVMe Clone Instructions**\n\n**o SATA Clone instructions.**\n\n**Workstation Placement Examples - Please Reference Photos Attached in Document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-17T08:00","end":"2026-11-17T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":240,"max":240},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":20.07305392406205},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-19T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finde