{"job":{"id":20078615,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"IW Technologies","title":"YM LV Cabling Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work &amp; Expectations</strong></p><p><strong>Overview</strong></p><p>This project is a <strong>full structured cabling installation</strong> in preparation for a future network cutover. <strong>No existing low-voltage cabling, network equipment, or active services are to be modified, disconnected, removed, or disturbed.</strong> All work performed is for future use and must be installed alongside existing infrastructure.</p><p><strong>﻿The technician assigned to the work order MUST be the technician onsite NO EXCEPTIONS. Any violations will be taken very seriously and escalated to Field Nation and the work order will not be approved for payment</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tools - ALL Are required</strong></p><ul><li>Camera</li><li>12-ft ladder minimum</li><li>6-ft step ladder</li><li>Fish tape (100 ft recommended)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><p><strong><u>Below is a high level overview. See the attached document for the full scope. </u></strong></p><p><strong>Cash Wrap</strong></p><ul><li>Photo's and cable count going down into cashwrap - Space for new cables in existing conduit?</li></ul><p><strong>Wireless Access Points</strong></p><ul><li>photos for cabling new AP locations.</li></ul><p><strong>Back Office / Receiving</strong></p><ul><li>Photos</li></ul><p><strong>BOH Spare Drops</strong></p><ul><li>Photos near the new data rack location.</li></ul><p><strong>Music Player</strong></p><ul><li>photos from the network rack to the music player location (M1).</li></ul><p><strong>DVR / Loss Prevention</strong></p><ul><li>photos from the network rack to the DVR location (LP1 and LP2).</li></ul><p><strong>Demarcation Extension</strong></p><ul><li>photos from the new network rack to the suite demarcation point.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Important Expectations</strong></p><p><strong>Ceiling height, type and color</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work &amp; Expectations**\n\n**Overview**\n\nThis project is a **full structured cabling installation** in preparation for a future network cutover. **No existing low-voltage cabling, network equipment, or active services are to be modified, disconnected, removed, or disturbed.** All work performed is for future use and must be installed alongside existing infrastructure.\n\n**﻿The technician assigned to the work order MUST be the technician onsite NO EXCEPTIONS. Any violations will be taken very seriously and escalated to Field Nation and the work order will not be approved for payment**\n\n**Required Tools - ALL Are required**\n\n- Camera\n- 12-ft ladder minimum\n- 6-ft step ladder\n- Fish tape (100 ft recommended)\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Below is a high level overview. See the attached document for the full scope.**\n\n**Cash Wrap**\n\n- Photo's and cable count going down into cashwrap - Space for new cables in existing conduit?\n\n**Wireless Access Points**\n\n- photos for cabling new AP locations.\n\n**Back Office / Receiving**\n\n- Photos\n\n**BOH Spare Drops**\n\n- Photos near the new data rack location.\n\n**Music Player**\n\n- photos from the network rack to the music player location (M1).\n\n**DVR / Loss Prevention**\n\n- photos from the network rack to the DVR location (LP1 and LP2).\n\n**Demarcation Extension**\n\n- photos from the new network rack to the suite demarcation point.\n\n**Important Expectations**\n\n**Ceiling height, type and color**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T09:00","end":"2026-11-12T11:15"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":110},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2.25,"distance":35.184447456181374},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z",