{"job":{"id":20336534,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Cash Drawer Front end camera is offline, troubleshooting required.","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work: Tech to follow \"Troubleshooting steps\" outlined below and via the link listed. Tech needs to check/verify cables and reset Cash Drawer Front end camera .</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Cash Drawer Front end camera is offline. Camera is unable to ping and not acle to access via web. Rebooted and reconnect the camera from LPCS. Deactivate and activate the Archiver. Confirm the video configuration. Issue remain same.</em></p>\n<p><em>Device/Host Name: <del>********</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>***** ***** ****** ******* ********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>IP Address: 192.168.130.121</em></p>\n<p><em>Camera Location: Cash Drawer Front end camera</em></p>\n<p><em>Camera Height: need to ask onsite tech</em></p>\n<p><em>Ceiling Height:</em></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code: <del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em><del>******** ********* **********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site?: (y/n) NA</em></p>\n<p><em>Please call Shyft Services National Tech Support at<del>************* *** **</del> opt 4 for additional support and to check and verify</em></p>\n<p><em>Troubleshooting steps:</em></p>\n<p><em>Problem: Offline camera High Level Steps:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***********************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>1. Locate camera</em></p>\n<p><em>2. Locate switch port via label, <del>*** ********* ***</del> L2 Support. Camera will be connected to either switch H5 or H6(except Sierra Trading Post stores)</em></p>\n<p><em>If unable to locate the tone-out cable, or work with support</em></p>\n<p><em>3. Reseat cable</em></p>\n<p><em>4. Try a different open port between 1-39</em></p>\n<p><em>5. Remove camera and plug directly into switch</em></p>\n<p><em>Required Technician Skills:</em></p>\n<p><em>Network Troubleshooting</em></p>\n<p><em>POS Support</em></p>\n<p><em>CCTV/PTZ Support</em></p>\n<p><em>Audio/Video Support</em></p>\n<p><em>Low voltage cabling</em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tools Link:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work: Tech to follow \"Troubleshooting steps\" outlined below and via the link listed. Tech needs to check/verify cables and reset Cash Drawer Front end camera .*\n\n*Cash Drawer Front end camera is offline. Camera is unable to ping and not acle to access via web. Rebooted and reconnect the camera from LPCS. Deactivate and activate the Archiver. Confirm the video configuration. Issue remain same.*\n\n*Device/Host Name: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*IP Address: 192.168.130.121*\n\n*Camera Location: Cash Drawer Front end camera*\n\n*Camera Height: need to ask onsite tech*\n\n*Ceiling Height:*\n\n*Site Security Code: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Estimated time: 2 hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site?: (y/n) NA*\n\n*Please call Shyft Services National Tech Support at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\* opt 4 for additional support and to check and verify*\n\n*Troubleshooting steps:*\n\n*Problem: Offline camera High Level Steps:*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*1. Locate camera*\n\n*2. Locate switch port via label, \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* L2 Support. Camera will be connected to either switch H5 or H6(except Sierra Trading Post stores)*\n\n*If unable to locate the tone-out cable, or work with support*\n\n*3. Reseat cable*\n\n*4. Try a different open port between 1-39*\n\n*5. Remove camera and plug directly into switch*\n\n*Required Technician Skills:*\n\n*Network Troubleshooting*\n\n*POS Support*\n\n*CCTV/PTZ Support*\n\n*Audio/Video Support*\n\n*Low voltage cabling*\n\n*Required Tools Link:*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n***Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.*** *These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only. If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be* ***a detailed and concise statement about the work performed****.****Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.***\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026