d any other additional photos required (upload via OnSite.)</li></ul><ol><li>When installing anything, take photos of new equipment, connections, jacks, labels, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>When troubleshooting amp/paging equipment, take photos of existing equipment with issues, wiring to back, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>If any equipment is boxed for RETURN SHIPPING, take photos of packed equipment before and after sealing box to ensure packed properly.</li></ol><p>Photos <strong><u>MUST</u></strong> be uploaded to CPT via OnSite for review and approval.</p><p><strong><u>ON ARRIVAL TO SITE:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Special Check-in and Communication Process</u></strong>: .</p><ol><li><strong>You will check-in with our Tech Support using our OnSite platform. </strong>Please have the CPT Work Order file open during this process.</li><li>We recommend completing this check-in *just before* entering the location.</li><li>A CPT Work Order will be in the files tab upon assignment.</li><li><strong>Use the OnSite link (also listed in Tasks below). </strong>You will enter the CPT Work Order Number and Work Order PIN Number located on the CPT Work Order on the top right-hand side under <u>Arrival Information</u>.</li><li><strong>OnSite Check-In Process: </strong></li><li>Check-in and out times must match our CPT OnSite Check-In and Out times.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be prompted for: CPT work order number + Work Order Pin, full name + phone number.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will receive the SMS authentication number to the number provided.</li><li>Check-in and out times must match our CPT OnSite Check-In and Out times.</li><li>Once you are checked in via OnSite, you will communicate with Tech Support via text.</li><li>Messages on Field Nation are not monitored by our Support Team once you are at the job site.</li></ol><p><strong><u>ALL</u></strong> questions and troubleshooting should be done with CPT Tech Support.</p><p><strong><u>BEFORE LEAVING JOB SITE:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>You MUST</u></strong> check out with CPT Tech Support <strong><u>BEFORE</u></strong> leaving site and provide all required deliverables.</p><ul><li>Messages on Field Nation are not monitored by our Tech Support team.</li><li>You will be asked to provide your updates, resolution, work completed, etc.</li><li>Upload your photos via OnSite for CPT Tech Support to review and verify.</li><li>Our customer's helpdesk may need to be contacted before leaving site and hold times may be required.</li><li>Confirm your check-in and check-out times. Any extra time not confirmed with CPT Tech Support will <strong><u>NOT</u></strong> be approved.</li><li>Have a manager sign the CPT work order and upload the signed work order when closing this job. Do <strong><u>NOT</u></strong> leave any copies onsite.</li></ul><p>You are <strong><u>required</u></strong> to check-in via OnSite and check-out with our Tech Support team before leaving for times to be validated so payment can be processed.</p><ul><li>If you do not contact us before leaving the job site to check out as required, this may affect your payment.</li></ul>","markdown":":::::::::::::::::::::::::::::: **CPT REQUEST OVERVIEW** ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n\n**This service request is for our client.** You are required to communicate directly with CPT **ONLY** for questions, scheduling, etc.\n\n- Do **NOT** call the store/site/customer.\n- You **MUST** communicate with our office via phone call for any delays or issues. Do not message through the platform.\n\nOnly the assigned technician should be present on this request.\n\n- If you are sending another rep. from your company to this request, please inform us.\n\nBusiness casual dress is **required.** Button-down shirt, polo, plain t-shirt, dockers, work pants, work shoes, neat gym shoes are acceptable.\n\nA copy of our internal work order will be provided in the documents section on assignment\n\n- This is to be used for sign-off with the customer.\n\n**Billing materials used (if any):**\n\n- Any materials provided during this request **MUST** be advised to our Tech Support team at check-out and should not be billed ABOVE average field tech prices.\n- Pricing **MUST** be itemized in expense tab description (Example: (1) Jack @ 3.50,etc.)\n- Anything billed above what a standard price will be reviewed and possibly require adjustments.\n- If you purchased a specific item(s) to be used on this request, you **MUST** include the receipt.\n\n**Base pay and time onsite:**\n\n- 1 hour Minimum **unless otherwise approved.**\n- Time onsite past this will be approved in 1/4 hour increments at the accepted rates.\n- Time logged/billed **MUST** match the check-in and check-out time verified with our Tech Support team. **NO EXCEPTIONS.**\n- Do **NOT** check-in on the app or with our office until you are inside the location.\n\n**Any discrepancies or failure to check in with CPT as required in this post, will cause a delay in payment or possible non-payment.**\n\n**IMPORTANT:** You may be required to be conferenced in with our customer for testing and verification of functionality.\n\n- Do **NOT** speak about time onsite, scheduling, pay rate, etc. This should only be discussed with CPT and not with any customer or helpdesk.\n\n:::::::::::::::::::::::: **QUALIFICATION AND TOOL / MATERIALS REQUIRED** ::::::::::::::::::::::::\n\n**DO NOT ACCEPT THIS ASSIGNMENT IF YOU DO NOT HAVE THE BELOW:**\n\n**Qualifications**\n\n- Very good Telecom (VOIP/POTS) or Audio-Visual experience and knowledge (dependent on work requested).\n- Ability to test cabling, jacks, trace cables, etc.\n- Ability to work on ladders and/or lifts as needed.\n\n**Standard required tools/materials - MUST be confirmed functional**\n\n**Tools**\n\n- 6' ladder\n- Screwdriver set\n- Wire cutters/strippers\n- Crimping tool (RJ45, RJ11/12)\n- Punch-down tool (110 &amp; 66 blades)\n- Jab saw / drywall saw\n- Fish tape / Fish rods\n- Torpedo level\n- Label maker\n- Butt-set\n- Data cable tester\n- Tone generator &amp; probe\n- Multimeter\n- Laptop\n- Hotspot\n- Ability to send photos\n- Console cable\n- Putty.exe\n- Headphones with 3.5mm connection\n- 3.5mm to RCA cable\n\n**On-Hand Materials**\n\n- RJ45 / RJ11 connectors\n- Cat5e / Cat6 cable, jacks and patch cords\n- Cross-connect wire\n- Wall plates &amp; surface mount boxes\n- Electrical tape, zip ties and velcro\n- Wall plates &amp; surface mount boxes\n\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::: **JOB DETAILS** ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n\n**One Tech Approved**\n\n**Scheduled Date/Time:**\n\nFOR ANY QUESTIONS OR TO UPDATE ON REPAIR FINDINGS, CONTACT OUR TECH SUPPORT TEAM WITHIN A HALF HOUR VIA OUR ONSITE COMMUNICATION APPLICATION.\n\n**Site Contact:** Manager on Duty (unless otherwise listed)\n\n**High Level Overview:**\n\nPorting phone numbers to Spectrum | Tech to connect inside wiring to their equipment, test dial tone and check for faxes\n\n**Additional Required Tools/Materials:**\n\n**Scope Of Work:**\n\nSite is porting their phone numbers to Spectrum. Spectrum is scheduled to be onsite on 11/10/26 between 9AM and 10AM. Please schedule a tech to meet with Spectrum and coordinate connecting their inside wiring to their equipment. Once connected, please test for dial tone and check for faxes on 919-384-7600 BTN, 919-384-7606 Fax &amp; 919-384-7603 Line 2.\n\n\\- Check in with CPT via the OnSite link in the work order once onsite.\n\n\\- Once completed and clear, technician MUST check out with CPT tech support before leaving site.\n\n\\- DO NOT LEAVE SITE BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH CPT TECH SUPPORT! You must provide updates on work completed, submit pictures, etc.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Signed copy of the work order.\n- Check-in/out with OnSite and CPT Tech Support.\n- Clear photos of before/after work, work area/equipment, troubleshooting, and any other additional photos required (upload via OnSite.)\n\n1. When installing anything, take photos of new equipment, connections, jacks, labels, etc.\n2. When troubleshooting amp/paging equipment, take photos of existing equipment with issues, wiring to back, etc.\n3. If any equipment is boxed for RETURN SHIPPING, take photos of packed equipment before and after sealing box to ensure packed properly.\n\nPhotos **MUST** be uploaded to CPT via OnSite for review and approval.\n\n**ON ARRIVAL TO SITE:**\n\n**Special Check-in and Communication Process**: .\n\n1. **You will check-in with our Tech Support using our OnSite platform.** Please have the CPT Work Order file open during this process.\n2. We recommend completing this check-in \\*just before\\* entering the location.\n3. A CPT Work Order will be in the files tab upon assignment.\n4. **Use the OnSite link (also listed in Tasks below).** You will enter the CPT Work Order Number and Work Order PIN Number located on the CPT Work Order on the top right-hand side under Arrival Information.\n5. **OnSite Check-In Process:**\n6. Check-in and out times must match our CPT OnSite Check-In and Out times.\n7. You will be prompted for: CPT work order number + Work Order Pin, full name + phone number.\n8. You will receive the SMS authentication number to the number provided.\n9. Check-in and out times must match our CPT OnSite Check-In and Out times.\n10. Once you are checked in via OnSite, you will communicate with Tech Support via text.\n11. Messages on Field Nation are not monitored by our Support Team once you are at the job site.\n\n**ALL** questions and troubleshooting should be done with CPT Tech Support.\n\n**BEFORE LEAVING JOB SITE:**\n\n**You MUST** check out with CPT Tech Support **BEFORE** leaving site and provide all required deliverables.\n\n- Messages on Field Nation are not monitored by our Tech Support team.\n- You will be asked to provide your updates, resolution, work completed, etc.\n- Upload your photos via OnSite for CPT Tech Support to review and verify.\n- Our customer's helpdesk may need to be contacted before leaving site and hold times may be required.\n- Confirm your check-in and check-out times. Any extra time not confirmed with CPT Tech Support will **NOT** be approved.\n- Have a manager sign the CPT work order and upload the signed work order when closing this job. Do **NOT** leave any copies onsite.\n\nYou are **required** to check-in via OnSite and check-out with our Tech Support team before leaving for times to be validated so payment can be processed.\n\n- If you do not contact us before leaving the job site to check out as required, this may affect your payment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-10T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":16.81994987658546},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $70) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Pr