{"job":{"id":20336950,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Computech Technology Services","title":"Need A Technician Onsite to Pull (1) Cat6 Cable w/Support - See Description","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST&nbsp;*<u>CALL <del>***** ********</del>* OR TEXT *<del>***** ********</del>*</u>&nbsp;TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.</strong></p><p>We need a technician to visit our clients site to pull a single Cat6 cable from the security equipment in the managers office to the network room data switch. Tech will terminate the cable run to in wall jack in mudring and faceplate at the user end, and to RJ45 modular plug at the network end, plugged into the switch. Tech will work with the manager and the network admin below to patch cable the security equipment in to the new jack and confirm that the device is up on the network as expected.</p><p>Site has drop ceiling grid and drywall walls. The cable run is roughly 50'. Tech will need an 8' ladder.</p><p><strong>Tech will work with the customers remote network admin <del>***** ******* ** ***** **************** ***** ********</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Materials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.</p><p><strong>Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Punch Tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Push/Pull Rods</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Ladder(s)</li><li>Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)</li></ul><p><strong>Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):</strong></p><ul><li>​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks</li><li>External Keystone Biscuits</li><li>Keystone Faceplates</li><li>Mudrings</li><li>Misc Patch Cable(s)</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.</li><li>Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.</li><li>Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.</li><li>ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.</li></ul><p><strong>Material Compensation:</strong></p><p>PLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:</p><p>Item - Pre-Approved Pricing</p><p>Cat5e Riser - $0.18ft</p><p>Cat5e Plenum - $0.22ft</p><p>Cat6 Riser - $0.25ft</p><p>Cat6 Plenum - $0.28ft</p><p>RG59/RG6 - $0.12ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Siamese RG59 - $0.15ft</p><p>Cat5e Jack - $3.00ea</p><p>Cat6 Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- $3.75ea</p><p>Faceplate - $1.30ea</p><p>Surface Mount Box - $1.50ea</p><p>Patch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea</p><p>BNC Connectors - $3.00ea</p><p>Modular Plug - $0.55ea</p><p>Power Strip - $6.00ea</p><p>4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea</p><p>2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea</p><p>Cable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea</p><p>Patch Panel - Negotiable/at cost</p><p>Telco 66block - Negotiable/at cost</p><p><br></p><p>Tech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.</p><p>At ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.</p>","markdown":"**Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST \\*CALL \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* OR TEXT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.**\n\nWe need a technician to visit our clients site to pull a single Cat6 cable from the security equipment in the managers office to the network room data switch. Tech will terminate the cable run to in wall jack in mudring and faceplate at the user end, and to RJ45 modular plug at the network end, plugged into the switch. Tech will work with the manager and the network admin below to patch cable the security equipment in to the new jack and confirm that the device is up on the network as expected.\n\nSite has drop ceiling grid and drywall walls. The cable run is roughly 50'. Tech will need an 8' ladder.\n\n**Tech will work with the customers remote network admin \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nMaterials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.\n\n**Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:**\n\n- Punch Tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Toner\n- Buttset\n- Push/Pull Rods\n- Fish Tape\n- Ladder(s)\n- Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)\n\n**Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):**\n\n- ​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable\n- Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks\n- External Keystone Biscuits\n- Keystone Faceplates\n- Mudrings\n- Misc Patch Cable(s)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.\n- Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.\n- Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.\n- ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.\n\n**Material Compensation:**\n\nPLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:\n\nItem - Pre-Approved Pricing\n\nCat5e Riser - $0.18ft\n\nCat5e Plenum - $0.22ft\n\nCat6 Riser - $0.25ft\n\nCat6 Plenum - $0.28ft\n\nRG59/RG6 - $0.12ft\n\nSiamese RG59 - $0.15ft\n\nCat5e Jack - $3.00ea\n\nCat6 Jack - $3.75ea\n\nFaceplate - $1.30ea\n\nSurface Mount Box - $1.50ea\n\nPatch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea\n\nBNC Connectors - $3.00ea\n\nModular Plug - $0.55ea\n\nPower Strip - $6.00ea\n\n4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea\n\n2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea\n\nCable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea\n\nPatch Panel - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTelco 66block - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.\n\nAt ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T10:00","end":"2026-11-11T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":37.477964080499696},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794278449462}
{"job":{"id":20336949,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"call forward position 7 offline||*Troubleshooting*","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work: Call or text Jess with update and for support<del>*************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>• Call or text Jess with update and for support<del>*************</del></em></p>\n<p><em>• Store states call forward position 07 is not working.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Verify the reported issue:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Determine whether the button is not lighting up, not placing calls, or calling the incorrect number.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Inspect power and connections:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Check all cables and connections at the button power supply and LED panel.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Verify the unit is plugged into a functioning, grounded orange outlet.</em></p>\n<p><em>• If the button is not calling and not illuminating:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Inspect all power and communication connections.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Reseat any loose cables.</em></p>\n<p><em>• If the button is calling properly but the pole light does not illuminate:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Remove the faceplate and verify the LED connector is securely connected.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Full PDU head removal is not required to access the LED connection.</em></p>\n<p><em>o If assistance is needed locating the LED panel, text Jess for guidance and photos.</em></p>\n<p><em>• If the button is calling the wrong number:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Identify the button version by turning it over and locating the version marking (V2, V3, or V4).</em></p>\n<p><em>o Confirm whether all buttons in the queue line are the same version.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Button programming procedures:</em></p>\n<p><em>• V3 Buttons</em></p>\n<p><em>o V3 buttons are single-program, hard-coded devices and cannot be reprogrammed.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Replace the button if incorrect dialing is confirmed.</em></p>\n<p><em>• V2 Buttons</em></p>\n<p><em>o Press and hold the button for approximately 15 seconds until it begins rapidly blinking.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Once rapid blinking starts, tap the button once to program.</em></p>\n<p><em>• V4 Buttons</em></p>\n<p><em>o Locate the small reset button underneath where the cable enters the button.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Press and hold the reset button for 3 seconds, then release.</em></p>\n<p><em>o When the button begins rapidly blinking, tap it once to program.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Save settings:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Return to the hub.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Arrow down to Save/Exit and save the configuration.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Confirm the hub has returned to the home screen before testing.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Test functionality:</em></p>\n<p><em>o Verify the button places a call to the correct number.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Verify the pole LED illuminates properly during operation.</em></p>\n<p><em>o Document findings and any parts replaced or reprogramming performed.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Troubleshoot to resolve.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Please remember to note the name of the Manager on duty in log notes. Call cannot be closed without MOD</em></p>\n<p><em>noted.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Please be specific in log notes.</em></p>\n<p><em>• IF PARTS ARE REQUESTED/NEEDED, DO NOT CLOSE TICKET – LEAVE OPEN AS PENDING OR CANNOT</em></p>\n<p><em>COMPLETE. TICKET WILL BE ESCALATED WITH TRACKING INFO.</em></p>\n<p><em>• Text Jess a picture of the part needed and button for confirmation of system version.</em></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: Store states call forward position 7 is not working</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site? :(y/n) NO</em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em>If assistance is needed, please call:<del>************</del> option # 3</em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work: Call or text Jess with update and for support\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*• Call or text Jess with update and for support\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*• Store states call forward position 07 is not working.*\n\n*• Verify the reported issue:*\n\n*o Determine whether the button is not lighting up, not placing calls, or calling the incorrect number.*\n\n*• Inspect power and connections:*\n\n*o Check all cables and connections at the button power supply and LED panel.*\n\n*o Verify the unit is plugged into a functioning, grounded orange outlet.*\n\n*• If the button is not calling and not illuminating:*\n\n*o Inspect all power and communication connections.*\n\n*o Reseat any loose cables.*\n\n*• If the button is calling properly but the pole light does not illuminate:*\n\n*o Remove the faceplate and verify the LED connector is securely connected.*\n\n*o Full PDU head removal is not required to access the LED connection.*\n\n*o If assistance is needed locating the LED panel, text Jess for guidance and photos.*\n\n*• If the button is calling the wrong number:*\n\n*o Identify the button version by turning it over and locating the version marking (V2, V3, or V4).*\n\n*o Confirm whether all buttons in the queue line are the same version.*\n\n*• Button programming procedures:*\n\n*• V3 Buttons*\n\n*o V3 buttons are single-program, hard-coded devices and cannot be reprogrammed.*\n\n*o Replace the button if incorrect dialing is confirmed.*\n\n*• V2 Buttons*\n\n*o Press and hold the button for approximately 15 seconds until it begins rapidly blinking.*\n\n*o Once rapid blinking starts, tap the button once to program.*\n\n*• V4 Buttons*\n\n*o Locate the small reset button underneath where the cable enters the button.*\n\n*o Press and hold the reset button for 3 seconds, then release.*\n\n*o When the button begins rapidly blinking, tap it once to program.*\n\n*• Save settings:*\n\n*o Return to the hub.*\n\n*o Arrow down to Save/Exit and save the configuration.*\n\n*o Confirm the hub has returned to the home screen before testing.*\n\n*• Test functionality:*\n\n*o Verify the button places a call to the correct number.*\n\n*o Verify the pole LED illuminates properly during operation.*\n\n*o Document findings and any parts replaced or reprogramming performed.*\n\n*• Troubleshoot to resolve.*\n\n*• Please remember to note the name of the Manager on duty in log notes. Call cannot be closed without MOD*\n\n*noted.*\n\n*• Please be specific in log notes.*\n\n*• IF PARTS ARE REQUESTED/NEEDED, DO NOT CLOSE TICKET – LEAVE OPEN AS PENDING OR CANNOT*\n\n*COMPLETE. TICKET WILL BE ESCALATED WITH TRACKING INFO.*\n\n*• Text Jess a picture of the part needed and button for confirmation of system version.*\n\n*Site Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Customer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Clients present issue: Store states call forward position 7 is not working*\n\n*Estimated time: 2 hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site? :(y/n) NO*\n\n*Other Instructions:*\n\n*If assistance is needed, please call:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* option # 3*\n\n*Required Tool List:*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n***Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.*** *These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only. If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be* ***a detailed and concise statement about the work performed****.****Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.***\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T07:00","end":"2026-11-10T08:45","latestStart":"2026-11-10T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.75,"distance":2.902714882195444},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $80 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794278486233}
{"job":{"id":"1492440795","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"P1 investigate intermittent connectivity","description":"**Issue:**<br>Intermittent connectivity remains after modem reboots. TIME WARNER reports the circuit is operating normally and three carrier dispatches within the last three weeks found no carrier-circuit issue; the carrier suspects customer-owned internal network equipment.<br><br>CIRCUIT DETAILS<br>Service Type: Broadband<br>Carrier: TIME WARNER<br>CXR Circuit ID: 8349100310105391<br>NSO ID: N/A<br>WAN IP: N/A<br>WAN Gateway: N/A<br>MAC Address: N/A<br><br>**Required Equipment:**<br>- A laptop: Windows 10 or higher with admin rights, ethernet ports gig capable of speeds over 1G, and charger to prove connectivity, a patch cord, a splitter, and a minimum of 3 filters. Cell phone, Cell phone charger, butt set and Minimum of 150’ of cable. Cat5e/or higher, and Coax.<br><br>**Other Required Equipment:**<br>- mobile hot spot, usb 2.0 drive w/ 16gb storage, console cable two surface jacks etc<br><br>**General Info:**<br>- Customer Contact: Store manager, 9198595438<br>- NOC Call Back: T-Mobile Repair at 844-394-6758<br><br>**Configuration:**<br>- DHCP Enabled/Disabled: Enabled<br>- Provisioned Speed: 400Mbps/10Mbps<br><br>**SOW:**<br>- Check in via WorkMarket.<br>- Locate the Granite provided modem/router. Record make, model, and serial number in the ticket.<br>- Take a photo of the equipment and site as found.<br>- Verify modem LEDs indicate normal operation.<br>- Verify modem configuration matches the information provided in the ticket.<br>- If modem configuration does not match the documented configuration and cannot be corrected onsite, contact the Granite NOC.<br>- Inspect all inside wiring from DMARC to modem and replace as needed<br>- Document all wiring repairs completed onsite<br>- Connect directly to modem using test laptop<br>- Verify IP assignment (DHCP or static as documented)<br>- Confirm internet connectivity<br>- Unplug customers equipment, and plug laptop directly to the modem<br>- While directly connected to the modem, perform three (3) speed tests.<br>  - Download speed<br>  - Upload speed<br>  - Latency<br>- Ping-500 “ping –n 500 8.8.8.8” record<br>  - Packet loss percentage<br>  - Average latency<br>  - Maximum latency<br>- If speed test results are less than 80% of the provisioned service speed relocate the modem to the DMARC, when technically feasible. Connect technician laptop directly to the modem. Repeat three (3) speed tests<br>- Repeat Ping testing. Compare results between customer equipment location and DMARC location<br>- If speeds improve at the DMARC, inside wiring is the likely cause. Recheck wiring components. Retest after repairs.<br>- If speeds remain poor at the DMARC, issue is likely outside the customer premises. Proceed to Escalation Criteria.<br>- Reconnect customer equipment<br>- Confirm connectivity with LCON and MCON if required. See General Info<br>- Document all findings and actions taken including customer-owned equipment issues discovered onsite<br>- Identify Fault:<br>  - Customer Equipment<br>  - Customer LAN<br>  - Granite Managed Router<br>  - Carrier Circuit<br>  - Physical Layer/Cabling<br>  - No Trouble Found<br>- Validate service restoration criteria<br>- Upload pictures onto WorkMarket<br>- Contact Granite NOC after all testing and isolation steps have been completed. Or escalation is needed. See Escalation criteria. If not connected to a live person within 15 minutes accept the call back request<br>- Complete closeout and check out via WorkMarket<br><br>**Service Restoration Success Criteria:**<br>- Modem is online<br>- Power, DS, US, Online lights are normal<br>- Technician can browse from a laptop connected directly to modem<br>- IP Address obtained or assigned correctly<br>- 2 successful speed tests completed<br>- 500-ping test completed with acceptable results<br>- Customer equipment reconnected<br>- Photos and test results uploaded<br><br>**Escalation Criteria:**<br>- Physical Layer Issues<br>  - No power to carrier equipment or Granite-managed router<br>  - Carrier handoff down or no link light present<br>  - Damaged cabling or infrastructure requiring carrier repair<br>- Connectivity Issues<br>  - Unable to obtain an IP address<br>  - Unable to reach the configured gateway<br>  - Unable to browse the internet from a direct connection<br>  - WAN or LAN interface remains down after validation<br>- Performance Issues<br>  - Speed tests below 80% of provisioned bandwidth<br>  - Packet loss exceeds 2%<br>  - Elevated latency or jitter impacting service<br>  - Performance issues persist when testing directly from the Granite-managed router<br>- Customer Impact<br>  - Customer equipment cannot reconnect after testing<br>  - Customer remains unable to access services after troubleshooting is complete<br>- Carrier Engagement Required<br>  - Issue persists after local equipment, cabling, and router validation<br>  - Carrier trouble ticket or dispatch is required<br>  - Testing indicates the fault exists beyond the customer premises or Granite-managed equipment","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T10:00","end":"2026-11-10T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Tue, Nov 10, 10:00 AM\nChecked: Tue, Nov 10, Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11