{"job":{"id":20337807,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spectrotel","title":"Test AT&T Fiber Circuit(Fiber Tester Needed)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(69, 78, 110);\"><u>SOW</u></strong></p><p><p>PLEASE NOTE THAT THIS DISPATCH HAS A HARD START TIME</p>\r\n<p><br />Technician will need to work with Spectrotel Provisioning to test and verify service on site's newly installed fiber data circuit. Technician will need to test and verify connectivity over circuit's assigned static IPs which will be provided at the time of testing. Additionally, site is asking that the technician perform some clean-up in their IT room.</p>\r\n<p><br />AT&amp;T 2Gbps EoF Circuit Details<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Carrier Circuit ID: L4YS605299ATI<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; LEC Circuit ID: 26/KGGS/400366//SB<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Carrier NID Make &amp; Model: FIBER ADAPTER PANEL<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Carrier NID CLLI Code: N/A<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Hand-off Type &amp; Port: Optical SMF LC (1310nm) Port&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Auto Negotiation: Disabled<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Speed &amp; Duplex: 10Gbps Full</p>\r\n<p><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Demarc: 1ST FLR IT SERVER ROOM WALL MOUNTED FIBER ADAPTER PANEL TAGGED</p>\r\n<p><br />Required High Resolution Images<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;a. Full network wall/rack<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;b. General photo of NEW carrier device<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;c. Photo of carrier device in relation to its location to network rack<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;d. MAC address label/Circuit ID/Port Label for the new equipment<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;e. Speed test results from 2 - 3 speed test sites</p>\r\n<p><br />-Technician is required to be proficient in knowing how to configure their laptop for DCHP and/or Static IP use without instruction<br />-Technician is required to bring a Windows 10/11 laptop that has a working RJ45 ethernet jack<br />-If technician is utilizing an Ethernet to USB adapter, then please make sure that it is a USB 3.0 adapter with all drivers updated<br />-Technician's laptop is required to be rated for 1Gbps speeds<br />-Technician is required to bring a mobile hotspot that is not their cell phone<br />-Technician's laptop is required to have at least one remote desktop app such as AnyDesk or TeamViewer installed<br />-Please bring patch cables, a power strip, and all tools and materials needed to complete the work order.</p></p><p><strong><u>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p><strong>♦ Contacts</strong></p><p><em style=\"color: black;\">You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in.&nbsp;Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.  </em><em>If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>♦ Material and Equipment Requirements</strong></p><p>Tech <u>MUST</u> have inside their bag when arriving to the building <strong>**NON-NEGOTIABLE**. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.</strong></p><ul><li>FULL Charged Windows Laptop with <strong>Gigabit RJ45 </strong>ethernet port &amp; Power Supply</li><li>Cat-5e or Cat-6 cabling,</li><li>Jacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper</li></ul><p>The provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.</p><p>The technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch <strong>(Please itemize charges).</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>All pictures MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>!!!Technician must confirm and provide details of the circuit demar's location and customer's IT room  where circuit needs to be delivered; if rooms are different technician must conduct a site survey to extend the circuit and provide a materials and labor quote,  the tech must provide the following!!!</strong></p><ul><li>Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):</li><li>Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details)</li><li>:Available existing cables Cat-5e/ Cat-6/ Fiber (mode type/ connector type/ available strands).</li><li>Estimated Distance (ft):</li><li>Conduit/path Confirmed Available:</li><li>Cable path details:</li><li>Estimate Labor Man Hours:</li><li>Estimate of ALL Materials &amp; Cost:</li><li>Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift):</li></ul><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>------------------------------------------------------------</u></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables</strong></p><p>Detailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.</p><p>We request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.</p><p><strong><u>Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.</u></strong></p><p>Please provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.</p><p>If a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.</p>","markdown":"**SOW**\n\nPLEASE NOTE THAT THIS DISPATCH HAS A HARD START TIME\n\n  \nTechnician will need to work with Spectrotel Provisioning to test and verify service on site's newly installed fiber data circuit. Technician will need to test and verify connectivity over circuit's assigned static IPs which will be provided at the time of testing. Additionally, site is asking that the technician perform some clean-up in their IT room.\n\n  \nAT&amp;T 2Gbps EoF Circuit Details  \n Carrier Circuit ID: L4YS605299ATI  \n LEC Circuit ID: 26/KGGS/400366//SB  \n Carrier NID Make &amp; Model: FIBER ADAPTER PANEL  \n Carrier NID CLLI Code: N/A  \n Hand-off Type &amp; Port: Optical SMF LC (1310nm) Port   \n Auto Negotiation: Disabled  \n Speed &amp; Duplex: 10Gbps Full\n\n  \n Demarc: 1ST FLR IT SERVER ROOM WALL MOUNTED FIBER ADAPTER PANEL TAGGED\n\n  \nRequired High Resolution Images  \n a. Full network wall/rack  \n b. General photo of NEW carrier device  \n c. Photo of carrier device in relation to its location to network rack  \n d. MAC address label/Circuit ID/Port Label for the new equipment  \n e. Speed test results from 2 - 3 speed test sites\n\n  \n-Technician is required to be proficient in knowing how to configure their laptop for DCHP and/or Static IP use without instruction  \n-Technician is required to bring a Windows 10/11 laptop that has a working RJ45 ethernet jack  \n-If technician is utilizing an Ethernet to USB adapter, then please make sure that it is a USB 3.0 adapter with all drivers updated  \n-Technician's laptop is required to be rated for 1Gbps speeds  \n-Technician is required to bring a mobile hotspot that is not their cell phone  \n-Technician's laptop is required to have at least one remote desktop app such as AnyDesk or TeamViewer installed  \n-Please bring patch cables, a power strip, and all tools and materials needed to complete the work order.\n\n**--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**♦ Contacts**\n\n*You must call Spectrotel Provisioning or the alternative Check-In/Check-Out contacts listed on this work order when checking in. Your Spectrotel Tech will provide scope details, act as your on-site support to perform any testing, and to check out/close out for your visit.* *If you cannot reach Support, please call the Work Order Manager.*\n\n**♦ Material and Equipment Requirements**\n\nTech MUST have inside their bag when arriving to the building **\\*\\*NON-NEGOTIABLE\\*\\*. Failure to have these items may result in being dismissed.**\n\n- FULL Charged Windows Laptop with **Gigabit RJ45** ethernet port &amp; Power Supply\n- Cat-5e or Cat-6 cabling,\n- Jacks, Mod ends, RJ45 Ends, Crimper\n\nThe provider must have a valid State/Federal issued photo ID.\n\nThe technician will be reimbursed for materials consumed to complete this work. Request material reimbursement at the completion of dispatch **(Please itemize charges).**\n\n- **All pictures MUST BE UPLOADED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE**\n\n**!!!Technician must confirm and provide details of the circuit demar's location and customer's IT room where circuit needs to be delivered; if rooms are different technician must conduct a site survey to extend the circuit and provide a materials and labor quote, the tech must provide the following!!!**\n\n- Source (Building , Floor, Room Details):\n- Destination (Building, Floor, Room Details)\n- :Available existing cables Cat-5e/ Cat-6/ Fiber (mode type/ connector type/ available strands).\n- Estimated Distance (ft):\n- Conduit/path Confirmed Available:\n- Cable path details:\n- Estimate Labor Man Hours:\n- Estimate of ALL Materials &amp; Cost:\n- Special Equipment (Tall Ladder, Lift):\n\n **------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n**♦ Closeout Notes and Deliverables**\n\nDetailed closeout notes are required on this work order before checking out on site. Work order will be returned incomplete resulting in approval delay if performed work is not summarized in closeout notes.\n\nWe request that work orders are marked complete within 24 hours of the dispatch.\n\n**Subsequent work that may follow this work order's conclusion will be submitted under a new work order.**\n\nPlease provide pictures of performed work on site and attach to this work order.\n\nIf a location denies entry for a missing Certificate of Insurance (COI) please request a sample COI with requirements and upload to Deliverables.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T09:00","end":"2026-11-11T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.35803962011072},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 (countered: $160) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 investigate intermittent connectivity (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","