{"job":{"id":"4749270794","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Level 10","title":"Wendys | Pax A35 Night Install","description":"<p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Overview</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The Level 10 technician will be replacing the existing Ingenico Lane 3000 PEDs (Pin Entry Device) with the new Pax A35 PED after the site has closed. The PEDs will be found in three areas of the site; at the front counter, drive-thru/pay window, and the kiosks located in the dining area. Each PED has been preconfigured for each specific terminal. Once installed, manage the cables and clean up. Package all the legacy PEDs in the boxes from the new PED for return shipping. Leave the shipping materials and the testing procedure with the manager. The manager will then complete the testing process the following morning, along with taping/shipping out the box to return the old PEDs.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Tools and Materials</p><p> </p><p><br></p><p>The following items are the responsibility of the technician to bring onsite. These items are critical, please review thoroughly.</p><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li><li>Tamper Resistant Bits (Torx T27, Spanner #8, and Square 1/8)</li><li><br></li><li>Ladder, 6'</li><li>Fully charged phone w/digital camera and the CompanyCam app installed</li><li><br></li><li>Drill with fully charged battery, spare charged battery, charger, and assorted bits.</li><li><br></li><li>Drill Bits for steel</li><li>Screw Extraction Kit</li><li>Extension Cords</li><li><br></li><li>Razor Knife</li><li><br></li><li>Sharpie / Permanent Marker</li><li><br></li><li>Screwdrivers (Flat blade &amp; Phillips, assorted sizes)</li><li><br></li><li>Allen Wrench Set</li><li><br></li><li>Hammer</li><li><br></li><li>Level</li><li><br></li><li>Hack Saw w/spare blades</li><li><br></li><li>Tape Measure (35 ft)</li><li><br></li><li>Socket Set / Drivers (Standard &amp; Metric)</li><li><br></li><li>Cable Push/Pull Rods, Fish Sticks, Glow Rods</li><li><br></li><li>Fish Tape (1/8 in Steel, 200 ft)</li><li><br></li><li>Punch Down Tool (w/ 66 &amp; 110 blades)</li><li><br></li><li>Crimper (RJ45)</li><li><br></li><li>Data Tester</li><li><br></li><li>Toner &amp; Probe</li><li><br></li><li>Cable Cutters</li><li><br></li><li>Lineman Scissors</li><li><br></li><li>Diagonal Strippers</li><li><br></li><li>Pliers (Long Nose, Lineman)</li><li><br></li><li>Channel Locks</li><li><br></li><li>Adjustable Crescent Wrench</li><li><br></li><li>Flashlight</li><li><br></li><li>Safety Glasses</li><li><br></li><li>Gloves</li><li><br></li><li>Ear Protection</li><li><br></li><li>Stud Finder</li><li><br></li><li>P-Touch Labeler w/white backed labels and black font</li><li><br></li><li>Velcro (for cable management above ceiling)</li><li><br></li><li>Tie Wraps (for cable management above ceiling)</li><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Support Contact</p><p> </p><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li><li>Techwill need to contact Level 10 at 800-807-1733 to check in/out and to report any issues.</li><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Documentation</p><ul><li><br></li><li>Tek_Wendys Pax A35 Installation Guide</li><li> </li><li><br></li><li><br></li><li>CompanyCam Checklist</li><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Deliverables</p><p><br></p><p>Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Expected Duration: 2.5 Hrs.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-12-01T23:00","end":"2026-12-01T27:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":238.57010621},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":0},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $238.57010621 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-04T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-12-04T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-05T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-12-01T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-03T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Datamax police departments"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 investigate intermittent connectivity (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794321087875}
{"job":{"id":"5800678124","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Connext (formerly Trextel)","title":"5377 - EM Counter Payment Device US","description":"<p>NOTE: If this is an airport location, please park at the car return. There will be NO reimbursement for parking!</p><p><br></p><p><u>Please Note: If you are late for this site you will be penalized $100. Our customer is unable to accommodate for late arrivals.</u></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***THIS JOB REQUIRES TECHNICIANS TO CHECK-IN AND CHECKOUT VIA A CALL TO THE TOC HD! IT WILL AFFECT YOUR PAY IF YOU DO NOT CHECK IN PROPERLY***&nbsp;</strong><em>READ SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS PLEASE!</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong>IF YOU DO NOT READ THIS WORK ORDER IN ITS ENTIRETY, YOU WILL NOT BE PREPARED FOR THIS JOB AND WILL NOT BE PAID IF THE JOB IS NOT COMPLETED.</strong></p><p><strong>ALL OUR PHONE NUMBERS AND OUR PROCEDURES FOR CHECK IN/OUT HAVE CHANGED. PLEASE REVIEW CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION AFTER YOU HAVE BEEN ASSIGNED THE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p><strong>Travel expenses must be pre-approved prior to scheduling and must be requested as an expense when you apply.&nbsp;Tolls &amp; Parking will be reimbursed with a receipt.</strong></p><p><strong>Reminder: If the dispatch will take longer than the allotted time to complete or there are any Out-of-Scope issues that arise, YOU MUST call the Connext escalation line (located under Confidential Information section) to notify Connext. Any extra time on site needs pre-approval by the PM and you will need good notes when you close out your work order to justify the additional time.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>Basic Scope of Work</u></p><ul><li>Watch the YouTube video of instructions in the guide. The link is in the special instructions</li><li>CHECKIN WITH CONNEXT IMMEDIATELY!</li><li>Email before photos of the MX915 with asset tag information to EM</li><li>Once approval has been provided by EM, replace the existing MX915 payment devices</li><li>Email after photos to EM and Connext</li><li><strong>CHECKOUT WITH CONNEXT</strong></li><li><strong>Bring old equipment to the corresponding courier</strong></li><li>Send a picture of the Return Label and the drop off Receipt to <a href=\"mailto:PDRefreshInstall@em.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">PDRefreshInstall@em.com</a></li></ul><p>*Full details of the scope of work are in the install guide!</p><p><br></p><p><u>MANDATORY TOOLS</u></p><ul><li>Reliable Cell Phone/Service</li><li>Access to email</li><li>Flathead screwdriver</li><li>1.5-inch (or similar) putty knife</li><li>4-5 15ft patch cables</li><li>Adhesive Remover (Goo Gone, or similar)</li></ul><p>NOTE: Do not use rubbing alcohol as it is too strong for the countertops and can damage them</p><ul><li>Dental floss</li><li>Towel/Paper Towels</li></ul><p><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><u>Requirements/Expectations</u></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This work order has all the necessary information to complete the scope. If anything is unclear, please reach out to Tech Support Number listed under Confidential Information.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For this assignment, you will be representing CONNEXT. Please follow our standard procedures on site and be fully prepared to complete the scope.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As a technician, maintain a professional and courteous attitude while working. Once onsite, greet the customer and let them know who you are working with and show them your ID and/or Work Order.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Be professional even under stressful situations.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Communicate often with the customer and Helpdesk as your work proceeds.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dress Code - Long pants (jeans, khakis or work pants), collared shirt (button up or polo), closed toed shoes. No t-shirts, shorts, sandals, graphic, or offensive clothing of any kind.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Times and MOD signed Work Orders are used for payment NOT worker platform times.</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF APPLICABLE, RETURN DEFECTIVE EQUIPMENT USING RETURN LABEL IN BOX THAT IS STAPLED TO THE PACKING SLIP.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><u>Required Deliverables</u></p><p><strong>Deliverables must be submitted while onsite to EM before Connext releases you from site. If not submitted and approved while onsite, a penalty will be incurred.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pictures Needed:</strong></p><p>Please take the following pictures of the installation. Photos should be emailed to <a href=\"mailto:PDRefreshInstall@em.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">PDRefreshInstall@em.com</a> before releasing from site.</p><ul><li>Before Photos of the MX915 showing the serial number and MAC address with the counter in view</li><li>Overview of Counter payment devices showing installation location of legacy equipment.</li><li>Overview of Counter payment devices, showing clean undamaged counter tops.</li><li>Closeup of the Counter PD showing that the device is on Network and Charging.</li><li>All Legacy equipment Boxed and Labeled for return&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><u>Reimbursement Rates</u></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Cat5e PVC $0.16 ft</li><li>Cat5 Plenum $0.25 ft</li><li>Cat6 PVC $0.25 ft</li><li>Cat6 Plenum $0.46 ft</li><li>Biscuit Jack $5.00</li><li>Surface Mount Box $5.31</li><li>Face Plate $3.00</li><li>RJ45 jack Cat 6 $9.98</li><li>RJ48 jack $5.00</li><li>66 Block $15.72</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T16:00","end":"2026-11-10T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":54.99995064,"max":109.99990128},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":54.99995064,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $109.99990128 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 P1 investigate intermittent connectivity (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05636592 - 1013 Classic Rd | VTM CUT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"s