{"job":{"id":"7499795091","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"INT13924833 – T2069  – Durham – Music/Paging / Troubleshooting No Lift","description":"<p>**Initial Description/Overview**</p><p><br></p><p>**Target / INT13924833** / **Music/Paging / Troubleshooting&nbsp;/ No Lift**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**\\*See Target Store Tech Tips for TOA attachment for tool recommendations\\***</p><p><br></p><p>\\*\\*\\***UPON ARRIVAL:** TECH MUST CALL GRANITE **TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761#**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>* Proceed to the Guest Service Desk, provide Identification and ask for a Designated Leader.&nbsp;**Samuel Lopez**</p><p>* When meeting designated leader, provide the above incident number and reason for the service call, determine location of service call. Designated Store Lead will direct you to the package with replacement part that was delivered \\(see below for tracking details\\)&nbsp;</p><p>* If the store refuses the technician and work, the technician should ask the store leader/designated leader to call the CSC with the above incident number and service call number **SR0090382**</p><p><br></p><p>* **If Control Room Access is required, please reach out to CSC 612-304-4357 to obtain code – Tech Must read the attached Control Room Access and Regulations documents before requesting access.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**ISSUE/SOW:** T2069- Image sound player is offline but music is working fine in the store</p><p>**Tech must call Granite rep before leaving site to verify testing and final check out.&nbsp;DO NOT leave site without approval from your Granite Rep.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**Replacement Device /Equipment Info/Tracking**</p><p>Tracking number: N/A&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Return tracking: N/A</p><p>Part sent:&nbsp;N/A</p><p>Serial number: N/A</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**@@ NOTE: Tech is responsible for returning any old or unused equipment.&nbsp;DO NOT leave onsite.&nbsp;&nbsp;Use provided return label and take it to a nearby UPS location to be returned.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**Closeout Checklist:**</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirm ALL devices online with designated leader.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Call **TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761#** to check out BEFORE leaving.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide before and after pictures of devices worked on</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Picture of SN#\\(s\\) one of existing/old and one of new/replaced equipment</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of certified cable tests</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of termination points</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Record first and last name of site contact and support contact you worked with</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;**If equipment was shipped,** Box up unused equipment \\(old or new\\) with return label provided and TECH is responsible for dropping off at a UPS location, a picture of the return label and the receipt from UPS at drop off is a required deliverable</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**REQUIRED MATERIALS /TOOLS: Tech MUST have the following:**</p><p>**\\*Impedance Tester\\***</p><p>Laptop with power supply and USB to RS-232C converter cable</p><p>Cat5/Cat6 cable tester</p><p>Min 500ft CAT6 cable \\(White preferred\\)</p><p>CAT6 Jacks</p><p>CAT6 Patch cords various lengths</p><p>Basic hand tools</p><p>Pliers</p><p>Assorted screwdrivers</p><p>Precision screwdriver set</p><p>Drill</p><p>Velcro for cable management</p><p>Label maker \\(P touch or equivalent\\)</p><p>Patch cables</p><p>Cable tester Toner and Probe</p><p>Camera/Smart phone</p><p>8-10' Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>