{"job":{"id":"2655968788","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"IT ServicePoint, LLC","title":"Install PIAB","description":"<p># SCOPE OF WORK</p><p><br></p><p>Install PIAB, connect to sites phones, inform site of new DIDs, test IB/OB Calls.</p><p><br></p><p># REQUIRED MATERIALS</p><p><br></p><p>- Fully Charged Laptop with Ethernet port</p><p>- Multimeter wire tester</p><p>- Adjustable wrench and/or open end wrenches</p><p>- Standard mounting hardware and tools (screws, anchors, screw drivers, drill, level, hammer)</p><p>- Biscuit jacks</p><p>- Crimpers &amp; Wirecutters</p><p>- 4-6 ft' ladder</p><p>- Butt Set</p><p>- RJ11 and RJ45 cable connectors</p><p>- 100' extension cord</p><p>- Digital Camera</p><p>- 100 of Cat 5e/6 cable for possible relocation of device</p><p>- Cell phone w/Hotspot device</p><p>- Punch down tool</p><p><br></p><p># ONSITE INSTRUCTIONS</p><p><br></p><p>This order requires tech to have State Issued Enhanced Driver's License or Enhanced ID or must carry one of the following:</p><p>- U.S. passport</p><p>- U.S. passport card</p><p>- DHS trusted traveler cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</p><p>- U.S. Department of Defense ID, including IDs issued to dependents</p><p>- Permanent resident card</p><p>- Border crossing card</p><p>- An acceptable photo ID issued by a federally recognized Tribal Nation/Indian Tribe, including Enhanced Tribal Cards (ETCs).</p><p>- HSPD-12 PIV card</p><p>- Foreign government-issued passport</p><p>- Canadian provincial driver's license or Indian and Northern Affairs Canada card</p><p>- Transportation worker identification credential</p><p>- U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Employment Authorization Card (I-766)</p><p>- U.S. Merchant Mariner Credential</p><p>- Veteran Health Identification Card (VHIC)</p><p>*Tech MUST work with MetTel support and be released by them. You can find the support number and Mettel ticket in the confidential field section*</p><p>___________________________________________________________________________________________________</p><p>Flat rate covers up to 3 hours onsite. Any additional time will be paid out at $35 per hour.</p><p><br></p><p>Technicians are responsible for requesting a budget increase or expense reimbursement as well as closing out their own assignment for payment. All budget increases or expense reimbursements must be requested within 48 hours after check out, otherwise they will not be approved.</p><p><br></p><p>Aborted sites with hourly payment terms will be paid per the terms for actual time onsite with a one hour minimum. If a site is aborted and there is a flat rate for the payment terms, the ticket will be closed out for 50% of the contracted rate, subsequent days scheduled will be considered ?Cancelled?, not ?Aborted?. </p><p><br></p><p>All site aborts MUST be approved by ServicePoint.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-20T10:00","end":"2026-11-20T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":45.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-23T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-24T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-24T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-25T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.0