{"job":{"id":20341166,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"(New Switch Installed-EMERGENCY) - Please see SOW for required tools.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT INFORMATION:</strong></p><p><strong>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage.&nbsp;If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders.&nbsp;Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay.&nbsp;Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only.&nbsp;If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction.&nbsp;The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</strong></p><p>-------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p><del>*** ****** **</del><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"><del>**********</del></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must call <del>*** ***** * ******** ******* * ************</del> if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>- If they don't answer, call the <del>*** ******** **** ****** ************** ****** * **** ****** * </del>- wait for a live person) BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</p><p>- This is a must, even if nothing was able to be completed onsite.</p><p>*Failure to do so, may result in failure of payment. The tech will need to give TRCA the name of the rep they spoke with upon checking out.*</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>-\tIf you are on hold or are waiting for a call back, from the helpdesk, longer than 20 min, tech will need to reach out to TRCA for further instructions.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Required Tools:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Laptop</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- CAT6 cabling/material/patch cables- Mod ends, face plates, jacks..etc</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">- Basic tools: screwdrivers, drill, bits of different sizes, etc</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">SOW:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">School is still down even after getting a new modem, router, and MX. Sending this out since we need to replace the switch since it won't come online. Sending out switch today. 305718 was the original cancelled ticket with TRCA. Going to have them move any ports from bad switch to MX as a temporary work around.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech must call </strong><del>*** ***** * ******** ******* * ************</del> <strong><del> </del>if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>IF THERE IS DEFECTIVE TELEPHONY EQUIPMENT, TRCA WILL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION UPON CHECKING OUT:</strong></p><p>1. We'll need the make and model of the hardware.</p><p>2. We'll need pictures of the serial number and the defective hardware itself. The tech will be asked for the serial # upon checking out.</p><p>3. We'll need quantity of each hardware device that needs to be replaced.</p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT INFORMATION:**\n\n**Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI with TRCA listed as the Certificate Holder and waive this deduction. The COI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.**\n\n\\-------------------------------------------\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tech must call \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.**\n\n\\- If they don't answer, call the \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* - wait for a live person) BEFORE checking out with TRCA.\n\n\\- This is a must, even if nothing was able to be completed onsite.\n\n\\*Failure to do so, may result in failure of payment. The tech will need to give TRCA the name of the rep they spoke with upon checking out.\\*\n\n**- If you are on hold or are waiting for a call back, from the helpdesk, longer than 20 min, tech will need to reach out to TRCA for further instructions.**\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n\\- Cable tester with a display to show cable test results.\n\n\\- Laptop\n\n\\- CAT6 cabling/material/patch cables- Mod ends, face plates, jacks..etc\n\n\\- Basic tools: screwdrivers, drill, bits of different sizes, etc\n\nSOW:\n\nSchool is still down even after getting a new modem, router, and MX. Sending this out since we need to replace the switch since it won't come online. Sending out switch today. 305718 was the original cancelled ticket with TRCA. Going to have them move any ports from bad switch to MX as a temporary work around.\n\n**Tech must call** \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*  **if they have any issues/questions onsite and BEFORE checking out with TRCA.**\n\n**IF THERE IS DEFECTIVE TELEPHONY EQUIPMENT, TRCA WILL NEED THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION UPON CHECKING OUT:**\n\n1\\. We'll need the make and model of the hardware.\n\n2\\. We'll need pictures of the serial number and the defective hardware itself. The tech will be asked for the serial # upon checking out.\n\n3\\. We'll need quantity of each hardware device that needs to be replaced.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T13:30","end":"2026-11-10T15:30","latestStart":"2026-11-10T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":95},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.468328297164907},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"display\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794334003030}
{"job":{"id":20341456,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Worldlink Integration Group","title":"Replace Pin pad for register 1 - Tech MUST bring security hex/Allen key set","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:</strong></p><p><strong>- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out</strong></p><p><strong>- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)</strong></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>COMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tech MUST call the Worldlink coordinator and Hot Topic/Box Lunch/Torrid Help Desk BEFORE beginning any work. Tech must test the device with the help desk and confirm functionality before checking out with Worldlink and leaving the site</strong></p><p><strong>Worldlink Coordinator: 210-756-8651</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>********* ********* ****** ************ ****** *</del></strong></p><p><strong><u>Tech MUST leave old pin pad on site with the manager NO MATTER WHAT- IF the tech takes the pin pad out of the store they will be held responsible to return it to the store and will not be paid until the pin pad is returned.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tools/Materials:</u></strong></p><p>basic tool kit/cabling kit</p><p>cable tester/toner</p><p>Screwdriver set&nbsp;</p><p>Punch-down</p><p>Drill</p><p>Label maker or tags</p><p>Security Hex key/Allen wrench set</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Materials (Provided by Technician - Reimbursed per the policies and procedures if used):-</u></strong></p><p>CAT5e Ethernet cable (100')</p><p>RJ45 connectors&nbsp;</p><p>Patch cables</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p><p>The technician needs to replace the VeriFone m400 Pinpad on register <strong>(1)</strong>, then reconnect all the necessary connections to ensure both the register and Pinpad are active and online.</p><p>The technician will need to remove the existing pin pad (if present) and install and mount the new pin pad at the designated location.</p><p>The technician must bring all the necessary tools to complete the installation, including a security hex/Allen key set for the pinpads, a cable tester, and an extra patch cable.</p><p>Technicians must check-in/out with the World Link and with the Help Desk and work with them to get the pin pad online and verify the connectivity and pictures. Also, to get the configuration.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Picture:-</strong></p><p>Photo of Register 1 setup before the pinpad is installed (to show original condition).</p><p>Close-up of the pinpad securely mounted or placed in its final position.</p><p>Photo showing the pinpad cables connected to the register or appropriate ports.</p><p>Wide-angle shot showing Register with the pinpad fully installed and setup completed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician must be prepared to test the data run for any shorts, install, repair, replace or re-terminate any cables or connectors as needed.</strong></p><p><strong>The technician MUST work with the help desk level support to troubleshoot/test/repair issue. Helpdesk name MUST be on the sign off sheet and work order will not be approved without a valid name.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables: </u>(Work order will not be approved without these photos)</strong></p><ul><li>Basic work order form, completely filled out and signed by MOD</li><li>Photos of completed work</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p><p><strong>Help Desk Contact(if applicable):&nbsp;&nbsp;(Located in the Confidential Section)</strong></p>","markdown":"**WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:**\n\n**- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out**\n\n**- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)**\n\n**IMPORTANT: Contact Worldlink immediately (DO NOT wait until checkout) should your SOW change once on site, or if you face any challenges out of your control that may affect your total time spent on site (delays, access issues, etc.). Failure to do so may result in non-payment for the associated challenges/changes.**\n\nCOMPLETELY FILLED OUT (1) WORK ORDER FORM (no blanks!) AND (2) PHOTO DELIVERABLES MUST BE RECEIVED BEFORE YOU CHECK OUT FROM THE SITE, IF NOT A $25 PENALTY WILL BE ASSESSED. IF BOTH ARE NOT RECEIVED WITHIN 5 BUSINESS DAYS THE WORK ORDER WILL BE CANCELED AND YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.\n\n**Tech MUST call the Worldlink coordinator and Hot Topic/Box Lunch/Torrid Help Desk BEFORE beginning any work. Tech must test the device with the help desk and confirm functionality before checking out with Worldlink and leaving the site**\n\n**Worldlink Coordinator: 210-756-8651**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\***\n\n**Tech MUST leave old pin pad on site with the manager NO MATTER WHAT- IF the tech takes the pin pad out of the store they will be held responsible to return it to the store and will not be paid until the pin pad is returned.**\n\n**Tools/Materials:**\n\nbasic tool kit/cabling kit\n\ncable tester/toner\n\nScrewdriver set\n\nPunch-down\n\nDrill\n\nLabel maker or tags\n\nSecurity Hex key/Allen wrench set\n\n**Materials (Provided by Technician - Reimbursed per the policies and procedures if used):-**\n\nCAT5e Ethernet cable (100')\n\nRJ45 connectors\n\nPatch cables\n\n**SOW:**\n\nThe technician needs to replace the VeriFone m400 Pinpad on register **(1)**, then reconnect all the necessary connections to ensure both the register and Pinpad are active and online.\n\nThe technician will need to remove the existing pin pad (if present) and install and mount the new pin pad at the designated location.\n\nThe technician must bring all the necessary tools to complete the installation, including a security hex/Allen key set for the pinpads, a cable tester, and an extra patch cable.\n\nTechnicians must check-in/out with the World Link and with the Help Desk and work with them to get the pin pad online and verify the connectivity and pictures. Also, to get the configuration.\n\n**Required Picture:-**\n\nPhoto of Register 1 setup before the pinpad is installed (to show original condition).\n\nClose-up of the pinpad securely mounted or placed in its final position.\n\nPhoto showing the pinpad cables connected to the register or appropriate ports.\n\nWide-angle shot showing Register with the pinpad fully installed and setup completed.\n\n**The technician must be prepared to test the data run for any shorts, install, repair, replace or re-terminate any cables or connectors as needed.**\n\n**The technician MUST work with the help desk level support to troubleshoot/test/repair issue. Helpdesk name MUST be on the sign off sheet and work order will not be approved without a valid name.**\n\n**Deliverables: (Work order will not be approved without these photos)**\n\n- Basic work order form, completely filled out and signed by MOD\n- Photos of completed work\n\n**Worldlink Contact: (Located in the Confidential Section)**\n\n**Help Desk Contact(if applicable): (Located in the Confidential Section)**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T11:00","end":"2026-11-12T13:00","latestStart":"2026-11-12T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":45,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":45,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":35.13437638329466},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794335280520}
{"job":{"id":"5101973254","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM","description":"Call 888 375 3755 to check in and check out.<br>AT&amp;T shows modem online but we don't see it registering on the Fortigate.<br>We need to test the AT&amp;T modem and ensure sync and surf.<br>Depending on the results of that test we need test the router when re connected to the primary.<br>Tech will need a laptop with a console connection, console cable and hot spot","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T12:00","end":"2026-11-11T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":44.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Nov 11, 12:00 PM\nChecked: Wed, Nov 11, Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.00