{"job":{"id":20342124,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teksetra","title":"Printer Install (3 devices)","description":{"html":"<strong>Problem Description:</strong><br />\nInstall 3 printers<br />\n<strong>Make: HP</strong><br />\n<strong>Model:&nbsp;</strong>HP M430<br />\n<strong>Serial:</strong><br />\n<p align=\"center\">THBGV8617X</p>\n<p align=\"center\">THBGV86183</p>\n<p align=\"center\">THBGV86187</p>\n<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Customer Name:</strong> Keplr Vision - (136) Princeton Eye Care<br />\n<strong>Customer Contact:</strong><br />\n<strong>Location Address:</strong> 110 East Edwards Street Princeton, NC 27569<br />\nLocation Notes:<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Teksetra Ticket#:</strong> INS0011764<br />\n<strong>Customer Ticket:</strong> Maureen Bernardo<br />\n<strong>FTG or HP ticket #:</strong><br />\n<br />\n<p><strong>Work with Customer's IT team (contact info should be in attached SOW) to get printer onto network and settings configured.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Any other issues please contact Teksetra Tech Support –</strong> 763-551-4357<strong>&nbsp;and we can help determine next steps.</strong> i.e. cannot get ahold of customer's IT, hardware damaged in transit, etc.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>TECH MUST CALL SITE TO INFORM THEM OF THEIR VISIT AND PROVIDE ETA ONCE TICKET HAS BEEN ACCEPTED. If you get onsite and are refused access due to not scheduling with the site, <strong>that trip will NOT be paid.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tool List (May not be needed for each repair but suggested to carry with to all printer repair tickets):</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wire Cutters: Small and Large</li>\n<li>Pliers: Small and Large</li>\n<li>Phillips &amp; Flat Head Screw Drivers: Small and Large</li>\n<li>Torx Wrenches: Full Range of Sizes</li>\n<li>Allen Wrenches: Full Range of Sizes</li>\n<li>Packing Tape (In some instances you will be asked to drop off old items at UPS, work orders will not be approved until tracking number verifies old parts have been dropped off at UPS)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><u>PRINTER MANUALS CAN BE DOWNLOADED AT:</u></p>\n<p><strong>Website:</strong>&nbsp;files.teksetra.us</p>\n<p><strong>Username:</strong>&nbsp;stechnician</p>\n<p><strong>Password:&nbsp;</strong>1FieldTech!</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Contact Numbers:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teksetra Tech Support: Call 763-551-4357<strong>&nbsp;</strong>or email our in-house support at&nbsp;fieldtechsupport@teksetra.com</li>\n<li>Teksetra Call Center:&nbsp;763-551-4355</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Important Reminders</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech MUST call 763-551-4355 to checkout (calling tech support is not sufficient) Checking out on every trip is a REQUIREMENT on all break/fix tickets</li>\n<li>Techs are required to call 763-551-4355 or email us at callcenter@teksetra.com to obtain tracking information. Tickets will not be paid for a trip to site if parts are not there and tech failed to check tracking.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Lunch and breaks are not paid. Keep track of hours by checking in and out of work order</li>\n<li>For hourly workorders, you will be paid for actual hours worked as verified onsite, 2 hour guaranteed minimum</li>\n<li>If you are assigned to this workorder within 24 hours of WO start time, please note a cancellation fee will not be paid should the WO need to be cancelled</li>\n<li>If for any reason you will arrive late or if you are having any issues, you must call the Teksetra workorder manager immediately.</li>\n<li>Provider will not discuss scheduling, pay structure, Field Nation workorder, nor show anyone the Field Nation workorder, to anyone onsite. Any questions or concerns should be directed to Teksetra workorder manager only.</li>\n<li>Travel requests will NOT be approved after the work has been completed/the tech has been onsite. If you are requesting travel for any ticket it must be negotiated and added to the ticket when applying/accepting a work order.​</li>\n<li>Tickets will remain open for return trips, the technician is responsible for requesting a&nbsp;budget increase for the return visit. Please contact Field Nation if you need&nbsp;assistance with this step.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Professionalism</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician will submit to and provide copy of background check as required at no cost</li>\n<li>Technician will provide appropriate identification to obtain access to the site and complete required training to obtain credentials as needed.</li>\n<li>Technician agrees to read and abide by the Subcontractor Master Service Agreement in the Policies &amp; Procedures section.</li>\n<li>Technician agrees to obtain all required permits, licenses and certificates necessary to perform services under this workorder</li>\n<li>Technician agrees to arrive on time and conduct their work in a professional manner, acting as a representative of Teksetra</li>\n<li>Dress Code: Teksetra Badge, clean polo or button-down shirt, prefer blue (no logos). Chino, tech, or utility pants, or dark jeans (clean/no holes). Clean closed toe shoes</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Problem Description:**  \nInstall 3 printers  \n**Make: HP**  \n**Model:** HP M430  \n**Serial:**  \nTHBGV8617X\n\nTHBGV86183\n\nTHBGV86187\n\n  \n  \n**Customer Name:** Keplr Vision - (136) Princeton Eye Care  \n**Customer Contact:**  \n**Location Address:** 110 East Edwards Street Princeton, NC 27569  \nLocation Notes:  \n  \n**Teksetra Ticket#:** INS0011764  \n**Customer Ticket:** Maureen Bernardo  \n**FTG or HP ticket #:**  \n  \n**Work with Customer's IT team (contact info should be in attached SOW) to get printer onto network and settings configured.**\n\n**Any other issues please contact Teksetra Tech Support –** 763-551-4357 **and we can help determine next steps.** i.e. cannot get ahold of customer's IT, hardware damaged in transit, etc.\n\n**SCOPE:**\n\n- TECH MUST CALL SITE TO INFORM THEM OF THEIR VISIT AND PROVIDE ETA ONCE TICKET HAS BEEN ACCEPTED. If you get onsite and are refused access due to not scheduling with the site, **that trip will NOT be paid.**\n\n**Required Tool List (May not be needed for each repair but suggested to carry with to all printer repair tickets):**\n\n- Wire Cutters: Small and Large\n- Pliers: Small and Large\n- Phillips &amp; Flat Head Screw Drivers: Small and Large\n- Torx Wrenches: Full Range of Sizes\n- Allen Wrenches: Full Range of Sizes\n- Packing Tape (In some instances you will be asked to drop off old items at UPS, work orders will not be approved until tracking number verifies old parts have been dropped off at UPS)\n\nPRINTER MANUALS CAN BE DOWNLOADED AT:\n\n**Website:** files.teksetra.us\n\n**Username:** stechnician\n\n**Password:** 1FieldTech!\n\n**Contact Numbers:**\n\n- Teksetra Tech Support: Call 763-551-4357 or email our in-house support at fieldtechsupport@teksetra.com\n- Teksetra Call Center: 763-551-4355\n\n**Important Reminders**\n\n- Tech MUST call 763-551-4355 to checkout (calling tech support is not sufficient) Checking out on every trip is a REQUIREMENT on all break/fix tickets\n- Techs are required to call 763-551-4355 or email us at callcenter@teksetra.com to obtain tracking information. Tickets will not be paid for a trip to site if parts are not there and tech failed to check tracking.\n- Lunch and breaks are not paid. Keep track of hours by checking in and out of work order\n- For hourly workorders, you will be paid for actual hours worked as verified onsite, 2 hour guaranteed minimum\n- If you are assigned to this workorder within 24 hours of WO start time, please note a cancellation fee will not be paid should the WO need to be cancelled\n- If for any reason you will arrive late or if you are having any issues, you must call the Teksetra workorder manager immediately.\n- Provider will not discuss scheduling, pay structure, Field Nation workorder, nor show anyone the Field Nation workorder, to anyone onsite. Any questions or concerns should be directed to Teksetra workorder manager only.\n- Travel requests will NOT be approved after the work has been completed/the tech has been onsite. If you are requesting travel for any ticket it must be negotiated and added to the ticket when applying/accepting a work order.​\n- Tickets will remain open for return trips, the technician is responsible for requesting a budget increase for the return visit. Please contact Field Nation if you need assistance with this step.\n\n**Professionalism**\n\n- Technician will submit to and provide copy of background check as required at no cost\n- Technician will provide appropriate identification to obtain access to the site and complete required training to obtain credentials as needed.\n- Technician agrees to read and abide by the Subcontractor Master Service Agreement in the Policies &amp; Procedures section.\n- Technician agrees to obtain all required permits, licenses and certificates necessary to perform services under this workorder\n- Technician agrees to arrive on time and conduct their work in a professional manner, acting as a representative of Teksetra\n- Dress Code: Teksetra Badge, clean polo or button-down shirt, prefer blue (no logos). Chino, tech, or utility pants, or dark jeans (clean/no holes). Clean closed toe shoes","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T10:00","end":"2026-11-13T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":43.63221038963814},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z