{"job":{"id":20342069,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Network tech required","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">Please follow the instructions :-</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">1. Do not leave the site</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">3. Dress Code:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> Business casual attire is required.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">4. Do not discuss the pay rate</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> onsite with the customer or any other employees.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">5. Site Visit Report:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\"> After completing the visit, you </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">. This is </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">mandatory for work order approval</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(38, 35, 33);\">Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>8.Short description of the reported issue: Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.</p><p><br></p><p>9.If L1/L2 is required: L2</p><p><br></p><p>10.Mandate Action required:</p><p>Bomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.</p><p>Upload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.</p><p>Engineers are required to contact the Dispatch Team before leaving the clinic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ovation engineer should introduce himself in the clinic saying he/she is from Fresenius IT support</p><p><br></p><p>11.Engineers are required to carry the following equipment:</p><p>-Personal Cell phone and Laptop with Microsoft Teams access and PuTTY (For being able to contact each other and possibly hotspot).</p><p>-A Screwdriver and Allen wrench.</p><p>-10 ft data cable.</p><p>-Console Cable for Cisco / HP Router, Switch</p><p>-Cable tester&nbsp;</p><p>-Tone generator&nbsp;</p><p>-Toner</p><p><br></p><p>12.Scope of Work:</p><p>&nbsp;Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>13.After the completion of Visit:</p><p>Update the SVR with Resolution Steps</p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch contact details&nbsp;</p><p>EUXDispatch@freseniusmedicalcare.com</p><p>+1 201-499-7693</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"Please follow the instructions :-\n\n**1. Do not leave the site** without prior permission from myself, our team, or the DCC team.\n\n**2. Do not contact the POC (Point of Contact)**before the visit unless explicitly instructed to do so.\n\n**3. Dress Code:** Business casual attire is required.\n\n**4. Do not discuss the pay rate** onsite with the customer or any other employees.\n\n**5. Site Visit Report:** After completing the visit, you **must fill out the Site Visit Report and upload it to the work order**. This is **mandatory for work order approval**.\n\n**Failure to follow these instructions will result in disqualification of work approval, impact billing, and may affect your eligibility for future assignments.**\n\n8.Short description of the reported issue: Technician to work with Ryan to install the cell booster.\n\n9.If L1/L2 is required: L2\n\n10.Mandate Action required:\n\nBomgar software to be installed in every dispatch engineer laptop.\n\nUpload an image of Kronos clock during the Entry time and Exit time.\n