{"job":{"id":20343227,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Smart Choice Commnunications","title":"Cary assist lead tech with Phone install Order 35434-35438","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Scope for AUNC MAC, AUNC Cary, AUNC Raleigh, AUNC Wake Forest :</strong></p><ul><li>Unpack and inspect 90x Yealink SIP-T85W phones</li><li>Install phones at designated workstations or locations per attached cutsheet</li><li>Connect handsets to existing network data outlets.</li><li>Connect handset power supplies if Power over Ethernet (PoE) is unavailable or not applicable. <strong>NOTE: </strong>if power supply is used let Michelle know</li><li>Connect computers through phone pass-through ports, where applicable.</li><li>Confirm each phone is assigned to the correct user, extension, and location.</li><li>Verify phone registration with the designated phone system.</li><li>ATA may need to be installed at this location, so site can continue sending faxes outbound.&nbsp;This will either be installed next to the fax or in network closet depending on where the current ATA is located.&nbsp;Any questions, please join MS Teams bridge</li><li>Once all equipment is online, join MS Teams bridge so Michelle can trigger the port.</li><li>Once Michelle triggers the port, from one handset test inbound and outbound calling, 933 (for 911), 411 and international dialing 01161386419083</li><li>Verify audio quality, handset functionality, and basic phone features.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Scope for AUNC Clayton &amp; AUNC Dunn:</strong></p><ul><li>Unpack and inspect Yealink SIP-T85W phones.</li><li>Install phones at designated workstations or locations per attached cutsheet</li><li>Connect handsets to existing network data outlets.</li><li>Connect handset power supplies if Power over Ethernet (PoE) is unavailable or not applicable. <strong>NOTE: </strong>if power supply is used let Michelle know</li><li>Connect computers through phone pass-through ports, where applicable.</li><li>Confirm each phone is assigned to the correct user, extension, and location.</li><li>Verify phone registration with the designated phone system.</li><li>ATA may need to be installed at this location, so site can continue sending faxes outbound.&nbsp;This will either be installed next to the fax or in network closet depending on where the current ATA is located.&nbsp;Any questions, please join MS Teams bridge</li><li>Take pictures of switch BEFORE removing</li><li>Mount 1 x 2960x 48 port switch already onsite and programmed in existing network rack replacing existing switch. <strong>NOTE: </strong>local IT has labeled old switch we are replacing and labeled the new switch to install.</li><li>Connect switches to existing patch panels using appropriate patch cables.</li><li>Connect network uplinks and required interconnections.</li><li>Connect equipment to existing power sources.</li><li>Verify physical connectivity and link status.</li><li>Perform connectivity testing to verify proper operation.</li><li>Once all equipment is online, join MS Teams bridge so Michelle can trigger the port.</li><li>Once Michelle triggers the port, from one handset test inbound and outbound calling, 933 (for 911), 411 and international dialing 01161386419083</li><li>Verify audio quality, handset functionality, and basic phone features.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Equipment Needed:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Laptop/console cable with power supply</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Cell phone with charger and earbuds</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p>","markdown":"**Scope for AUNC MAC, AUNC Cary, AUNC Raleigh, AUNC Wake Forest :**\n\n- Unpack and inspect 90x Yealink SIP-T85W phones\n- Install phones at designated workstations or locations per attached cutsheet\n- Connect handsets to existing network data outlets.\n- Connect handset power supplies if Power over Ethernet (PoE) is unavailable or not applicable. **NOTE:** if power supply is used let Michelle know\n- Connect computers through phone pass-through ports, where applicable.\n- Confirm each phone is assigned to the correct user, extension, and location.\n- Verify phone registration with the designated phone system.\n- ATA may need to be installed at this location, so site can continue sending faxes outbound. This will either be installed next to the fax or in network closet depending on where the current ATA is located. Any questions, please join MS Teams bridge\n- Once all equipment is online, join MS Teams bridge so Michelle can trigger the port.\n- Once Michelle triggers the port, from one handset test inbound and outbound calling, 933 (for 911), 411 and international dialing 01161386419083\n- Verify audio quality, handset functionality, and basic phone features.\n\n**Scope for AUNC Clayton &amp; AUNC Dunn:**\n\n- Unpack and inspect Yealink SIP-T85W phones.\n- Install phones at designated workstations or locations per attached cutsheet\n- Connect handsets to existing network data outlets.\n- Connect handset power supplies if Power over Ethernet (PoE) is unavailable or not applicable. **NOTE:** if power supply is used let Michelle know\n- Connect computers through phone pass-through ports, where applicable.\n- Confirm each phone is assigned to the correct user, extension, and location.\n- Verify phone registration with the designated phone system.\n- ATA may need to be installed at this location, so site can continue sending faxes outbound. This will either be installed next to the fax or in network closet depending on where the current ATA is located. Any questions, please join MS Teams bridge\n- Take pictures of switch BEFORE removing\n- Mount 1 x 2960x 48 port switch already onsite and programmed in existing network rack replacing existing switch. **NOTE:** local IT has labeled old switch we are replacing and labeled the new switch to install.\n- Connect switches to existing patch panels using appropriate patch cables.\n- Connect network uplinks and required interconnections.\n- Connect equipment to existing power sources.\n- Verify physical connectivity and link status.\n- Perform connectivity testing to verify proper operation.\n- Once all equipment is online, join MS Teams bridge so Michelle can trigger the port.\n- Once Michelle triggers the port, from one handset test inbound and outbound calling, 933 (for 911), 411 and international dialing 01161386419083\n- Verify audio quality, handset functionality, and basic phone features.\n\n**Equipment Needed:**\n\nLaptop/console cable with power supply\n\nCell phone with charger and earbuds","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-18T16:00","end":"2026-11-18T21:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":325},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":4.830857537762863},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $325 (countered: $325) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794337852327}
{"job":{"id":20342891,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axiom Service Management LLC","title":"HP E77830Z Printer fails to turn on. Customer has attempted different outlets and power cords.","description":{"html":"Customer Reference: 1133181   --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- ABM FEDERAL<br />\n <br />\n <br />\n--- INSTRUCTIONS ---<br />\n<br />\n*MUST SPEAK WITH THE USER TO SET AN APT. <br />\nTech needs an appointment with the end user, no Voicemail. <br />\nNeed to provide the name of the tech so the site can put him on the security list.<br />\n<br />\n<br />\n <br />\n <br />\nTech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG.<br />\n <br />\n <br />\nTechnician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed.<br />\n(Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.)<br />\n <br />\n <br />\nFor any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2.<br />\n <br />\n <br />\nInitial notes:  HP E77830Z Printer fails to turn on. Customer has attempted different outlets and power cords. <br />\n <br />\n <br />\nParts Ordered: \tRM3-7241-000CN       Low-voltage power supply (110-127V) <br />\n<br />\nPer Support:Called EU at the number provided and left a vm to verify the printer issue and printer location on base.<br />\n <br />\nNick called and confirmed the issue and the site location. Please provide him with tracking information at nicholas.flaherty@us.af.mil<br />\n <br />\nA techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed.<br />\n<br />\nhttps://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login <br />\ntechlink user name and password are the call number- 1133181<br />\n <br />\n <br />\n**It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to**<br />\n <br />\n <br />\n**Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval.***The technician is required to work with LMS/Axiom Tech Support while on-site. (7145491608 extn 3)***<br />\n <br />\n <br />\nGeneral Instructions for All Calls-<br />\nVerify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed.<br />\nConfirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts.<br />\nIf a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count.<br />\nDo not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead.<br />\nIf the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding.<br />\nAfter service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR.<br />\nIf facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.","markdown":"Customer Reference: 1133181 --- YOU ARE REPRESENTING --- ABM FEDERAL  \n   \n   \n\\--- INSTRUCTIONS ---  \n  \n\\*MUST SPEAK WITH THE USER TO SET AN APT.   \nTech needs an appointment with the end user, no Voicemail.   \nNeed to provide the name of the tech so the site can put him on the security list.  \n  \n  \n   \n   \nTech must confirm ETA with POC before arrival. If no work is performed after confirmed ETA, travel rate will be discussed with TAG.  \n   \n   \nTechnician must take clear photos before and after service of the unit and surrounding area (before service starts and after service is completed) to document site condition and parts installed.  \n(Photos are required for checkout and serve as proof of service and site condition.)  \n   \n   \nFor any onsite issues (model mismatch, part direction, or completion), contact dispatch at 714-549-1608 Opt 2.  \n   \n   \nInitial notes: HP E77830Z Printer fails to turn on. Customer has attempted different outlets and power cords.   \n   \n   \nParts Ordered: RM3-7241-000CN Low-voltage power supply (110-127V)   \n  \nPer Support:Called EU at the number provided and left a vm to verify the printer issue and printer location on base.  \n   \nNick called and confirmed the issue and the site location. Please provide him with tracking information at nicholas.flaherty@us.af.mil  \n   \nA techlink has been set up. Please make sure you download the manual and take it with you to the site if needed.  \n  \n<https://axiom.falconsystem.com/tech-link/login>   \ntechlink user name and password are the call number- 1133181  \n   \n   \n\\*\\*It is required to update POC/EU of next Plan of Action before leaving site, Please provide name of POC/EU you provided the update to\\*\\*  \n   \n   \n\\*\\*Technicians are required to provide all deliverables and update/closing notes before leaving the site. Prior to departure, technicians must contact Dispatch at 714-549-1608, Option 2, to provide a final status update and receive checkout approval.\\*\\*\\*The technician is required to work with LMS/Axiom Tech Support while on-site. (7145491608 extn 3)\\*\\*\\*  \n   \n   \nGeneral Instructions for All Calls-  \nVerify parts arrival and access Tech Link if needed.  \nConfirm the serial number and troubleshoot before replacing any parts.  \nIf a formatter is replaced, reset the serial number and page count.  \nDo not discuss toner issues with the user — report them to LMS instead.  \nIf the serial number or model doesn’t match, call dispatch for approval before proceeding.  \nAfter service completion, call Parts Recovery (Opt 5) for payment confirmation and inform dispatch who signed the FSR.  \nIf facing any issue onsite (printer, parts, or user not found), or waiting on dispatch instructions, contact LMS after 10–15 minutes.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T09:00","end":"2026-11-13T17:01"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":75},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":56.98233515308205},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 11/10/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794337899641}
