{"job":{"id":"1599988216","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"LEGACY Retail Services","title":"Service Call for Menu Screens at Fast Food Restaurant","description":"<p>WORK DESCRIPTION: Please go to site with crimping tools, cable tester, spare HDMI and Ethernet cat 6 cables. and re-commission and replace the Media player 201 (for the outdoor menu board, left side) because that device is faulty and needs to be replaced. Bring commissioning tools to re-commission the new media Player (External Monitor, USB Keyboard, USB Drive on FAT32 format / please refer to the commissioning guide attached to this E-Mail) check the power, source and ethernet connections, verify the cables are not physically damaged and re-crimp them or re-end the cables if it´s necessary, check the IP settings and the Device ID for the screens, make sure to have the devices back online and displaying content properly. Call Coates for further assistance if required and for release</p><p><br></p><p>Important: Please keep in mind additional troubleshooting maybe required.</p><p><br></p><p>Expected time on site (Additional troubleshooting steps and additional on site may be required): 2-4 hours</p><p><br></p><p>LOCATION: ODMB - Drive-thru</p><p><br></p><p><strong>**A 32gb or smaller USB drive is required, must download and unzip the provided installation files needed to set up the new media player.**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Link to file download: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12TnBK3Tqk9yu-F0V_7UcK_xcbCGmzfaD</strong></p><p><br></p><p>When heading to site, TEXT BRANDPOING SUPPORT AT&nbsp;-&nbsp;(856) 382-2645. They will be your support and troubleshoot with you through the duration of the call.&nbsp;</p><p>Must check in and out with support to confirm total time onsite and obtain checkout code from support to process work order.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>MANDATORY TOOLS REQUIRED:</strong> 9mm socket, L shaped tool, needle nose pliers, basic tools, security T40 and security T20 bi