{"job":{"id":20344791,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"Office Expansion- Network cabling (Tech 1)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.</em></strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview: </u></strong></p><p>Connect 12 new cubicles from existing data ports to workstations, plus install the conference room equipment. </p><p>Large conference room: Teams touch screen, Wall mount camera, separate dual speakers, dual microphones on conference table, with large tv </p><p>Small conference room: Teams touch screen, wall mount camera, large tv </p><p><br></p><p>Local contact: <del>*** ******* ******** ********* * ******* ***** ******* ***** ** ************ ** ************************************</del></p><p>IT Support: <del>**** ********* ************</del></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>1. Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><strong>The technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.</strong></p><p><strong>Task Sequence:</strong></p><ol><li>Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.</li><li>Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.</li><li>Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.</li><li>Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.</li><li>Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.</li><li>Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.</li><li>Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.</li><li>Take AFTER photos of completed work.</li><li>Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).</li><li>Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.</li><li>Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.</li><li>Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).</li><li>Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>2. Tools and Equipment Required</u></strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cables</li><li>Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity</li><li>Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)</li><li>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</li><li>Ladder (as needed for access)</li><li>Cable tester</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>3. Deliverables Required</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>BEFORE photos</strong> of all work areas</li><li><strong>AFTER photos</strong> of all completed work</li><li><strong>Any additional photos</strong> specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support</li><li><strong>Detailed closeout notes</strong> summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>4. Acceptance Criteria</u></strong></p><p><strong>Work will be considered complete when:</strong></p><ul><li>All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.</li><li>IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.</li><li>All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.</li><li>The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.</li></ul>","markdown":"***PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nConnect 12 new cubicles from existing data ports to workstations, plus install the conference room equipment.\n\nLarge conference room: Teams touch screen, Wall mount camera, separate dual speakers, dual microphones on conference table, with large tv\n\nSmall conference room: Teams touch screen, wall mount camera, large tv\n\nLocal contact: \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nIT Support: \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**1. Scope of Work**\n\n**The technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.**\n\n**Task Sequence:**\n\n1. Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.\n2. Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.\n3. Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.\n4. Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.\n5. Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.\n6. Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.\n7. Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.\n8. Take AFTER photos of completed work.\n9. Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).\n10. Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.\n11. Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.\n12. Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).\n13. Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.\n\n**2. Tools and Equipment Required**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cables\n- Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity\n- Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n- Ladder (as needed for access)\n- Cable tester\n\n**3. Deliverables Required**\n\n- **BEFORE photos** of all work areas\n- **AFTER photos** of all completed work\n- **Any additional photos** specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support\n- **Detailed closeout notes** summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations\n\n**4. Acceptance Criteria**\n\n**Work will be considered complete when:**\n\n- All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.\n- IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.\n- All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.\n- The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-18T09:00","end":"2026-11-18T25:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":960},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":14,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":16,"distance":5.22452629584597},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-20T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-21T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-18T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-20T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"2 day Raleigh office"},{"start":"2026-11-23T03:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-23T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-11-11T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ***Thermo Fisher | Network Cutover Assistance*** (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)