{"job":{"id":20345223,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Armor Security","title":"Add DVR to Existing system","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Install DVR</strong></p><p><br></p><p>YOU MUST BRING YOUR OWN HDMI MONITOR TO COMPLETE THE WORK.</p><p><br></p><p>Text the Work Order Manager when you arrive to let him know you are onsite.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Check if the DVR is powered on</li><li>Check if the DVR is plugged into a network switch</li><li>Check if the patch cable is good</li><li>Contact WOM to see if the DVR is back online</li><li>Make sure the in-stand monitor is showing the cameras</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>**If you will need more than 1 hour onsite, you must call and ask for more time before the first hour is up.&nbsp;If you do not call to get pre-approval for more time, you will not get paid for the extra time spent working.**</strong></p><p><br></p><p>If for some reason the store manager will not allow you to work - contact the work order manager right then.</p><p>Work must be done during the time frame stated on the work order.</p><p>Do not leave the site without talking to the Work Order Manager if there is still an issue at the site.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>HDMI monitor</li><li>Keyboard and Mouse (must be connected to the DVR and the DVR power cycled to allow the mouse to work)</li><li>6' Patch Cable</li><li><strong>See Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>** All unused equipment must be returned to Armor Security with its original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label. **</p><p><em>If, for whatever reason, we have to reschedule based on our error, i.e. equipment not being on site, we will pay $30 travel fee.&nbsp;</em></p><p><strong>By accepting the work order you are agreeing to Armor Security’s Standard Instructions and Policies &amp; Procedures terms.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Install DVR**\n\nYOU MUST BRING YOUR OWN HDMI MONITOR TO COMPLETE THE WORK.\n\nText the Work Order Manager when you arrive to let him know you are onsite.\n\n- Check if the DVR is powered on\n- Check if the DVR is plugged into a network switch\n- Check if the patch cable is good\n- Contact WOM to see if the DVR is back online\n- Make sure the in-stand monitor is showing the cameras\n\n**\\*\\*If you will need more than 1 hour onsite, you must call and ask for more time before the first hour is up. If you do not call to get pre-approval for more time, you will not get paid for the extra time spent working.\\*\\***\n\nIf for some reason the store manager will not allow you to work - contact the work order manager right then.\n\nWork must be done during the time frame stated on the work order.\n\nDo not leave the site without talking to the Work Order Manager if there is still an issue at the site.\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- HDMI monitor\n- Keyboard and Mouse (must be connected to the DVR and the DVR power cycled to allow the mouse to work)\n- 6' Patch Cable\n- **See Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.**\n\n\\*\\* All unused equipment must be returned to Armor Security with its original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label. \\*\\*\n\n*If, for whatever reason, we have to reschedule based on our error, i.e. equipment not being on site, we will pay $30 travel fee.*\n\n**By accepting the work order you are agreeing to Armor Security’s Standard Instructions and Policies &amp; Procedures terms.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T11:00","end":"2026-11-11T12:00","latestStart":"2026-11-11T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":50},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":21.61890777478729},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"monitor\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794341875404}
{"job":{"id":20345180,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Titan Protection","title":"Crescent Construction - Perimeter Check for Security System","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>12 ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Smartphone or Tablet with Camera</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)</li><li>Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.</li><li>Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.</li><li>If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).</li><li>Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).</li><li>Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.</li><li>Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.</li><li>Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.</li><li>Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.</li><li>Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.&nbsp;</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.</li><li>Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Dress Code:**\n\n- The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 12 ft A-Frame Ladder\n- Smartphone or Tablet with Camera\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.\n2. Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)\n3. Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.\n2. Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.\n3. Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.\n4. If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).\n5. Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).\n6. Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.\n7. Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.\n8. Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.\n2. Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.\n3. Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.\n- Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.\n- Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00","end":"2026-11-12T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":225,"max":425},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":225},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":100}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13.251989840992628},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Nov 12, 2:00 PM\nChecked: Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13, Mon, Nov 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-10T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2