CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES. CALL TO CHECK IN 855-612-2183.**\n\n**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking an **experienced Technician capable of installing a new 120v High-Voltage line and outlet.**\n- **No Certifications or Permits are required but all circuits must be installed to local code.**\n- **Tech is required to follow detailed instructions, troubleshoot, and work with remote support during the installation process.**\n\n**Scope Of Work:**\n\n- **CONSIDER KIOSK TYPE IN THE FOLLOWING:** The requirements for data and electrical wiring are specific to the kiosk type to be used at this location. Please refer to the 'Location specific details' section of your work to identify the exact kiosk type to be used at this location. If you are unsure of what type kiosk configuration will be used at this location, escalate to your work order manager or technical support contact for clarification.\n- **✅ELECTRICAL SCOPE:** Install electrical outlets as described in the attached kiosk playbook for the kiosk configuration type needed at this store. (Will need (2) 2-outlet decora style wall plates, (1) 2-port keystone decora insert, and (1) 20 amp decora style outlet)\n- **✅CABLING SCOPE:** Rough in four (4) Cat 6 cable runs from kiosk table to Manager's office. Refer to the Kiosk Playbook for further details.\n- **✅DEVICE INSTALL SCOPE:** Technician must place self-ordering kiosk device per instructions listed in the attached 'Kiosk Playbook' - this may include the hanging/mounting of the \"ORDER\" sign per instructions.\n- **Tech is required to follow provided instructions, and work with remote support during the installation process.**\n- **Must label** the new outlet and circuit and provide photo when complete.\n- Must provide photo with circuit tester plugged into each outlet showing that they are good.\n- Must have Microsoft Teams on your phone for support chat. You will conduct a walk through with the remote support team prior to starting and upon completion of the installation.\n- Estimated duration is 6-8 hours.\n\n**Onsite Remote Support Information:**\n\n**Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info**\n\n- **Link:** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n- **Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298**\n- **Passcode: pqnBC5**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. **Print / Review all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site. Please review all the attachments prior to arriving onsite**\n2. **KFC ORB Installation Guide Link:** **<https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003MzKr/be4ViurFfq5pYahpns9U8osRaI0gLq.Y5i0MOWJGees>**\n3. **KFC\\_Kiosk\\_Install\\_Guide\\_v3.1 Link**: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003GyPt/3iF0l1fQesIjsJuSaGjfjcHn_dA5Yfb_c0jocDXNp7o\n4. **Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation and a cancellation fee will not be granted.**\n5. **Download Microsoft Teams and ensure that it works on your phone.**\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **Check In Requirements- Follow in order**\n2. **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER–**Arrive onsite no earlier than 30 min. prior to start time. If you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\\\\\n3. **Site Access:** Start at the back service door and knock, if you get no answer, then proceed to the front door and knock. If you still have no response, then reach out the Microsoft Teams Support Chat for instruction.\n4. **CHECK IN with the Manager on duty (MOD) and introduce yourself as the Essintial Technician**\n5. **Have the manager direct you to where we will be installing the Order Ready Board and/or Kiosk at a later date.**\n6. **CHECK IN via Microsoft teams with the Essintial/KFC Support team -** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n7. **Start the Installation:**\n8. Work with the manager on duty (MOD) to determine the desired mounting location. THIS could be WALL OR CEILING or Table.\n9. Must label the new outlet and circuit and provide photo when complete.\n10. Must provide photo with circuit tester plugged into each outlet showing that they are good.\n11. Work with Essintial and KFC to ensure the placement of the electrical outlet is OK.\n\n**﻿Required On-Site Deliverables / Closeout Requirements:**\n\n- **Online Deliverable (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):**\n- You will be asked to confirm site details\n- You will be asked to provide requested information and photos\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager's signature\n- Record the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables. You will be required to provide this code at final close out\n- **CHECK OUT with the Essintial/KFC Support team via Microsoft Teams-** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n- **CHECK OUT OF YOUR WORK ORDER-If you are unable to do so, make sure that you call into Essintial Projects Team**\n\n**﻿Tools Required:**\n\n- Fully Charged smartphone or other device that has phone, camera, internet ability (for online deliverable), and WITH Microsoft Teams Installed.\n- Cell Phone Charger - preferred Fast Charger with appropriate cord\n- Government- issued Photo ID (original, not photo of or a copy)\n- Basic / Standard Hand Tools\n- Measuring Tap\n- Cable scissors or diagonal cutters\n- Box Opener (Knife, box cutter, scissors, etc)\n- Cable Ties - Bring both Velcro &amp; Zip Ties (We can **NOT** use Velcro in the kitchen)\n- Cabling Termination Tools\n- Testing equipment (cable tester, cable toner, multimeter, voltage tester)\n- Drill &amp; standard drill bits\n- Screw driver (Phillips #2 bit is most common)\n- Hammer drill\n- Masonry Bits\n- Label Maker\n- Any tools needed to complete electrical circuit installation / Establish a NEW outlet.\n\n**Dress Code:** Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no jeans or holes, collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.\n\n**Physical Requirements:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time. Activities such as climbing ladders, navigating through tight spaces and crawling on unfinished floor should all be expected as part of this work.\n\n**Escalation Process:** Any issues or questions related to the scope of work should be escalated to the Essintial/KFC Support team **-** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n\n**Essintial KFC Support - Microsoft Teams Info**\n\n- **Link:** **<https://tinyurl.com/35kwddm9>**\n- **Meeting ID: 277 936 211 298**\n- **Passcode: pqnBC5**\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind. Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time\n\n**Out of Scope: Time over the allotted hours onsite must be detailed as to why the tech went over. (Note: Any delay due to the technician's skill-set, errors, not following directions, etc. will not be honored or approved)**\n\n**Acceptable Reasons:**\n\n- **Site/lane access delays**\n- **Missing equipment**\n- **Delays in accessing equipment**\n- **Troubleshooting**\n\n-^-^- **Attachment &amp; Work Guide Links**\n\n\\- Refreshed on 10/15/2026 12:16 PM by Adam -\n\n **(1 of 3) KFCC-Kiosk-Playbook\\_2026\\_updated 1**\n\nLink: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005BvWL/_44jtAwSRvCBMvnXBka8ybD2TKzR6jq0uSY5z5LAyc8\n\n **(2 of 3) KFC Kiosk Hardware Installation Guide V1.0**\n\nLink: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000005BvUj/9yxQbFjTYqliVvUvn41JwJc