{"job":{"id":20347967,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Titan Protection","title":"Wood Partners - Adjustment of Cameras on Solar Powered Surveillance Devices","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong></p><ul><li>12 ft A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Crimpers</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Volt Meter</li><li>Socket Set</li><li>Torx Screwdriver Set</li><li>Phillips Screwdriver Set</li><li>Allen Wrenches</li><li>Smartphone or Tablet with Camera</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.&nbsp;</li><li>Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)</li><li>Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On-Site Tasks:</strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.</li><li>Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.</li><li>If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).</li><li>Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).</li><li>Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.</li><li>Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.</li><li>Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.</li><li>Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.</li><li>Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.&nbsp;</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.</li><li>Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Dress Code:**\n\n- The technician should wear comfortable, weather-appropriate clothing suitable for outdoor work, including safety gear such as a hard hat, safety glasses, hi-vis vest, gloves, and non-slip footwear.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 12 ft A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Crimpers\n- Cable Tester\n- Volt Meter\n- Socket Set\n- Torx Screwdriver Set\n- Phillips Screwdriver Set\n- Allen Wrenches\n- Smartphone or Tablet with Camera\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n1. Review the work order and any related documentation to understand the issue.\n2. Verify shipping and tracking information for any replacement parts or equipment. (if applicable)\n3. Ensure that you have all the necessary tools and equipment for the troubleshooting process.\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. Check-in to work order and introduce yourself to the onsite contact. You represent Titan Protection while onsite.\n2. Call Titan Tech Support Line at 913-441-0911 to check in. You will work with the remote agent to troubleshoot the camera.\n3. Inspect the cameras to confirm the connectivity issues. This may include checking power, network status (wired or wireless), and physical connections, cleaning off/repositioning solar panels.\n4. If the cameras are connected to a network, verify the network settings (IP address configuration, router settings, Wi-Fi signal strength, etc.).\n5. Test each camera’s connection to the monitoring system, performing troubleshooting steps as needed (e.g., resetting the camera, reconnecting to the network).\n6. Replace any faulty equipment or cables as identified.\n7. Reconfigure camera settings or network settings to restore connectivity.\n8. Verify that all cameras are operational and connected correctly before leaving the site.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Upload clear photos showing the condition of the cameras before and after work has been completed.\n2. Photos of any replacement equipment or cables installed.\n3. Obtain onsite signature from the contact person, confirming the completion of the work.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, call the Titan tech support line at 913-441-0911.\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to the Titan Protection support team at 913-441-0911\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Any additional hours required for work beyond the estimated duration must be pre-approved by the Titan Tech Support team. Please call 913-441-0911 for approval before logging additional hours or expenses.\n- Reimbursement of materials will need to be reflected in receipt amounts and will not exceed receipt totals unless otherwise pre-approved. Failure to get pre-approval or to provide a receipt will result in denial of re-imbursement.\n- Additional material or travel expenses must be approved prior to incurring charges. The technician should call the Titan Tech Support team to obtain approval. Failure to receive pre-approval may result in denial.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-12T16:00","end":"2026-11-12T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":225,"max":325},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":225},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":100}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5.128213182639833},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Nov 12, 4:00 PM\nChecked: Thu, Nov 12, Fri, Nov 13, Mon, Nov 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Rollins/Orkin Pest Control - FortiGate Swap & edgebootPro installation - Raleigh, NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-08T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-08T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Large Financial Institution | Device Refresh | High Volume Opportunity"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Office Expansion- Network cabling (Tech 1)"},{"start":"2026-11-18T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Office Expansion- Network cabling (Tech 2)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: WO 2026 Nov 16 SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"[INC#: 00740402 - ATT SITE#: RTP/DC3]   To Be Updated"},{"start":"2026-11-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"POS equipment install"},{"start":"2026-11-09T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-09T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Dream Finders - Site Survey - Networking"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1794347698677}
{"job":{"id":20347986,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"3 AP Replacement | 1 Lead Tech + 1 Spotter | Training Required | Lead Tech Must Have Lift & OSHA Fall Protection Cert","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.</li>\n<li>Estimated duration: 4 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Scope of Work</p>\n<p>Dispatch <strong>1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter</strong> to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of <strong>3 wireless access points</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong>Approximately<strong>3 hours</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Staffing Requirement</p>\n<p>This work order requires:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1 Lead Field Technician</strong></li>\n<li><strong>1 Spotter</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Do not dispatch only one person.</strong></p>\n<p>The Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Mandatory Training &amp; Certification Requirements</p>\n<p><strong>Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.</strong></p>\n<p>The <strong>Lead Technician must also have:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Valid Lift Certification</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Tech must need to bring Lift Harness</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Spotter does <strong>not</strong> require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Work to Be Completed</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.</li>\n<li>Complete a <strong>1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs</strong>.</li>\n<li>Replace APs one at a time.</li>\n<li>Record and photograph the <strong>serial number and MAC address</strong> of each new AP before installation.</li>\n<li>Remove the existing AP.</li>\n<li>Install the replacement AP in the same location.</li>\n<li>Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.</li>\n<li>Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.</li>\n<li>Repeat the process for all 3 APs.</li>\n<li>Complete final validation with the onsite POC.</li>\n<li>Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.</li>\n<li>Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Required Photos / Deliverables</strong></p>\n<p><strong>For each AP, provide clear photos showing:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>New AP serial number</strong></li>\n<li><strong>New AP MAC address</strong></li>\n<li><strong>AP fully installed</strong></li>\n<li><strong>AP securely mounted</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Final completed installation</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>All required <strong>VCOs, photos, and other deliverables</strong> must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>PPE Requirement</p>\n<p>Full PPE is mandatory for both resources:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hard hat</li>\n<li>Safety glasses</li>\n<li>Safety vest</li>\n<li>Steel-toe boots</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lift harness is mandatory</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Before Going Onsite</p>\n<p>At least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead Technician assigned</li>\n<li>Spotter assigned</li>\n<li>Technician and Spotter contact information submitted</li>\n<li>Required Amazon/site training completed for both</li>\n<li>Lead Technician Lift Certification verified</li>\n<li>Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified</li>\n<li>Avetta/site access requirements completed</li>\n<li>Full PPE available</li>\n<li>Lift harness available for Lead Technician</li>\n<li>Site address confirmed</li>\n<li>Scheduled arrival time confirmed</li>\n<li>Required tools available</li>\n<li>Lift requirement understood</li>\n<li>Scope and deliverables reviewed</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Completion Requirement</p>\n<p>The WO will only be considered complete after:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All 3 APs have been replaced</li>\n<li>All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC</li>\n<li>Required serial/MAC photos have been captured</li>\n<li>Final installation photos have been captured</li>\n<li>All required deliverables have been submitted</li>\n<li>Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with<strong>Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947</strong></li>\n<li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to<strong>mbaroi@techhubps.com</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time</li>\n<li>Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in AP replacement.\n- Estimated duration: 4 hours.\n- **Introduce yourself as a technician from TechHub PS.**\n- **Full PPE is required: hard hat, steel-toe boots, safety vest, and safety glasses.**\n- **Complete the required training and submit the certificate at least 24 hours before arriving on-site.**\n- **Join a mandatory 15–20-minute call on the evening before deployment to review the work process and deliverables submission requirements.**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- **Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)**\n\nScope of Work\n\nDispatch **1 qualified Lead Field Technician and 1 Spotter** to the assigned Amazon DPS location to complete the replacement of **3 wireless access points**.\n\n**Estimated onsite duration:**Approximately**3 hours**\n\nStaffing Requirement\n\nThis work order requires:\n\n- **1 Lead Field Technician**\n- **1 Spotter**\n\nBoth resources are mandatory and must remain onsite for the entire duration of the work.\n\n**Do not dispatch only one person.**\n\nThe Lead Technician will perform the AP replacement work, while the Spotter will support the technician and assist with safety requirements during elevated/lift work.\n\nMandatory Training &amp; Certification Requirements\n\n**Both the Lead Technician and Spotter must complete all required Amazon/site-specific training before going onsite.**\n\nThe **Lead Technician must also have:**\n\n- **Valid Lift Certification**\n- **Valid OSHA Fall Protection Certificate**\n- **Tech must need to bring Lift Harness**\n\nThe Spotter does **not** require the lift or fall protection certification unless separately requested, but all required site training must be completed.\n\nWork to Be Completed\n\n1. Check in with the onsite Point of Contact upon arrival.\n2. Confirm all 3 AP locations before beginning work.\n3. Complete a **1-for-1 replacement of 3 existing APs**.\n4. Replace APs one at a time.\n5. Record and photograph the **serial number and MAC address** of each new AP before installation.\n6. Remove the existing AP.\n7. Install the replacement AP in the same location.\n8. Ensure each AP is securely mounted to the ceiling.\n9. Validate each AP with the onsite POC and confirm it comes online.\n10. Repeat the process for all 3 APs.\n11. Complete final validation with the onsite POC.\n12. Clean the work area and remove installation-related debris.\n13. Check out with the onsite POC and Field Nation before leaving.\n\n**Required Photos / Deliverables**\n\n**For each AP, provide clear photos showing:**\n\n- **New AP serial number**\n- **New AP MAC address**\n- **AP fully installed**\n- **AP securely mounted**\n- **Final completed installation**\n\nAll required **VCOs, photos, and other deliverables** must be submitted before the WO is considered complete.\n\nPPE Requirement\n\nFull PPE is mandatory for both resources:\n\n- Hard hat\n- Safety glasses\n- Safety vest\n- Steel-toe boots\n\nFor the Lead Technician performing elevated/lift work:\n\n- **Lift harness is mandatory**\n\nBoth resources must follow all Amazon and site-specific safety requirements.\n\nBefore Going Onsite\n\nAt least 24 hours before the scheduled visit, confirm:\n\n- Lead Technician assigned\n- Spotter assigned\n- Technician and Spotter contact information submitted\n- Required Amazon/site training completed for both\n- Lead Technician Lift Certification verified\n- Lead Technician OSHA Fall Protection Certificate verified\n- Avetta/site access requirements completed\n- Full PPE available\n- Lift harness available for Lead Technician\n- Site address confirmed\n- Scheduled arrival time confirmed\n- Required tools available\n- Lift requirement understood\n- Scope and deliverables reviewed\n\nCompletion Requirement\n\nThe WO will only be considered complete after:\n\n- All 3 APs have been replaced\n- All 3 APs have been validated with the onsite POC\n- Required serial/MAC photos have been captured\n- Final installation photos have been captured\n- All required deliverables have been submitted\n- Technician has properly checked out from the site and Field Nation WO.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with**Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947**\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to**mbaroi@techhubps.com**\n\n**Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time\n- Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-13T14:00","end":"2026-11-13T18:45"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4.75,"distance":11.947825927799878},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Fri, Nov 13, 2:00 PM\nChecked: Fri, Nov 13, Mon, Nov 16, Tue, Nov 17 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-16T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-17T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-18T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-11T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974911-Epik Cutover & Test (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-16T21:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Advance Auto Parts - Phone Swap - 4810 Raleigh  NC (WM)"},{"st