{"job":{"id":20348353,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Qbuster system not working, troubleshooting required, tech must work with tech support.","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p>Work Order Notes</p>\n<p>Scope of Work: • Call or text Jess with update and for supp<del>*** *************</del></p>\n<p>• Store states call forward position all not working.V5.5 Page 13 Top of the Document</p>\n<p>• Verify the reported issue:</p>\n<p>o Determine whether the button is not lighting up, not placing calls, or calling the incorrect number.</p>\n<p>• Inspect power and connections:</p>\n<p>o Check all cables and connections at the button power supply and LED panel.</p>\n<p>o Verify the unit is plugged into a functioning, grounded orange outlet.</p>\n<p>• If the button is not calling and not illuminating:</p>\n<p>o Inspect all power and communication connections.</p>\n<p>o Reseat any loose cables.</p>\n<p>• If the button is calling properly but the pole light does not illuminate:</p>\n<p>o Remove the faceplate and verify the LED connector is securely connected.</p>\n<p>o Full PDU head removal is not required to access the LED connection.</p>\n<p>o If assistance is needed locating the LED panel, text Jess for guidance and photos.</p>\n<p>• If the button is calling the wrong number:</p>\n<p>o Identify the button version by turning it over and locating the version marking (V2, V3, or V4).</p>\n<p>o Confirm whether all buttons in the queue line are the same version.</p>\n<p>• Button programming procedures:</p>\n<p>• V3 Buttons</p>\n<p>o V3 buttons are single-program, hard-coded devices and cannot be reprogrammed.</p>\n<p>o Replace the button if incorrect dialing is confirmed.</p>\n<p>• V2 Buttons</p>\n<p>o Press and hold the button for approximately 15 seconds until it begins rapidly blinking.</p>\n<p>o Once rapid blinking starts, tap the button once to program.</p>\n<p>• V4 Buttons</p>\n<p>o Locate the small reset button underneath where the cable enters the button.</p>\n<p>o Press and hold the reset button for 3 seconds, then release.</p>\n<p>o When the button begins rapidly blinking, tap it once to program.</p>\n<p>• Save settings:</p>\n<p>o Return to the hub.</p>\n<p>o Arrow down to Save/Exit and save the configuration.</p>\n<p>o Confirm the hub has returned to the home screen before testing.</p>\n<p>• Test functionality:</p>\n<p>o Verify the button places a call to the correct number.</p>\n<p>o Verify the pole LED illuminates properly during operation.</p>\n<p>o Document findings and any parts replaced or reprogramming performed.</p>\n<p>• Troubleshoot to resolve.</p>\n<p>• Please remember to note the name of the Manager on duty in log notes. Call cannot be closed without MOD</p>\n<p>noted.</p>\n<p>• Please be specific in log notes.</p>\n<p>• IF PARTS ARE REQUESTED/NEEDED, DO NOT CLOSE TICKET – LEAVE OPEN AS PENDING OR CANNOT</p>\n<p>COMPLETE. TICKET WILL BE ESCALATED WITH TRACKING INFO.</p>\n<p>• Text Jess a picture of the part needed and button for confirmation of system version</p>\n<p>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></p>\n<p>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></p>\n<p>Clients present issue: all buttons not working</p>\n<p>Estimated time: 2 hours</p>\n<p>Part shipped to the site?:(y/n)</p>\n<p>Please review the repair plans in the link below</p>\n<p>(put the direct link here)</p>\n<p>Other Instructions:</p>\n<p>If assistance is needed, please call: <del>************ ****** * *</del></p>\n<p>Required Tool List:</p>\n<p><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\nWork Order Notes\n\nScope of Work: • Call or text Jess with update and for supp\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n• Store states call forward position all not working.V5.5 Page 13 Top of the Document\n\n• Verify the reported issue:\n\no Determine whether the button is not lighting up, not placing calls, or calling the incorrect number.\n\n• Inspect power and connections:\n\no Check all cables and connections at the button power supply and LED panel.\n\no Verify the unit is plugged into a functioning, grounded orange outlet.\n\n• If the button is not calling and not illuminating:\n\no Inspect all power and communication connections.\n\no Reseat any loose cables.\n\n• If the button is calling properly but the pole light does not illuminate:\n\no Remove the faceplate and verify the LED connector is securely connected.\n\no Full PDU head removal is not required to access the LED connection.\n\no If assistance is needed locating the LED panel, text Jess for guidance and photos.\n\n• If the button is calling the wrong number:\n\no Identify the button version by turning it over and locating the version marking (V2, V3, or V4).\n\no Confirm whether all buttons in the queue line are the same version.\n\n• Button programming procedures:\n\n• V3 Buttons\n\no V3 buttons are single-program, hard-coded devices and cannot be reprogrammed.\n\no Replace the button if incorrect dialing is confirmed.\n\n• V2 Buttons\n\no Press and hold the button for approximately 15 seconds until it begins rapidly blinking.\n\no Once rapid blinking starts, tap the button once to program.\n\n• V4 Buttons\n\no Locate the small reset button underneath where the cable enters the button.\n\no Press and hold the reset button for 3 seconds, then release.\n\no When the button begins rapidly blinking, tap it once to program.\n\n• Save settings:\n\no Return to the hub.\n\no Arrow down to Save/Exit and save the configuration.\n\no Confirm the hub has returned to the home screen before testing.\n\n• Test functionality:\n\no Verify the button places a call to the correct number.\n\no Verify the pole LED illuminates properly during operation.\n\no Document findings and any parts replaced or reprogramming performed.\n\n• Troubleshoot to resolve.\n\n• Please remember to note the name of the Manager on duty in log notes. Call cannot be closed without MOD\n\nnoted.\n\n• Please be specific in log notes.\n\n• IF PARTS ARE REQUESTED/NEEDED, DO NOT CLOSE TICKET – LEAVE OPEN AS PENDING OR CANNOT\n\nCOMPLETE. TICKET WILL BE ESCALATED WITH TRACKING INFO.\n\n• Text Jess a picture of the part needed and button for confirmation of system version\n\nSite Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCustomer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nClients present issue: all buttons not working\n\nEstimated time: 2 hours\n\nPart shipped to the site?:(y/n)\n\nPlease review the repair plans in the link below\n\n(put the direct link here)\n\nOther Instructions:\n\nIf assistance is needed, please call: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\n\nRequired Tool List:\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n***Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.*** *These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only. If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be* ***a detailed and concise statement about the work performed****.****Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.***\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-11-10T07:00","end":"2026-11-10T09:00","latestStart":"2026-11-10T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58.452213025854554},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 11/10/2026, 7:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-10T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Progitech"},{"start":"2026-11-12T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Veterans Day"},{"start":"2026-11-11T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-11T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Dispatch for ticket #7121628 | 11/10/26, 12:00 PM (WM)"},{"start":"2026-12-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 AXON - Wilson Police Department - NC (WM)"},{"start":"2026-11-17T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-17T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 The Preiss Company-05974