{"job":{"id":20349006,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Freezer Access Point Validation/AP-21 & 24","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Weblink Survey: </strong><strong>https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00745461</strong></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><strong> Validation for AP 21 and 24 ONLY</strong></p><p><strong>Note from Client:</strong></p><p> </p><ul><li>Tech to perform troubleshooting and/or replacement of Network device (s) listed.</li><li>Complete online Installation webform: <del>***********************************************</del></li><li>Need to arrive onsite 15 minutes prior but no later than the pre-arranged start time as stated in the schedule.</li><li>Tech to state when they are enroute to site and check in on the platform when they arrive inside the store</li><li>Call the NOC <del>**************</del> to notify of your arrival and locate POC “ETL Lead”</li><li>If Parts or Lift were requested, work with POC “ETL Leader” to locate the equipment and mention ETL office. Parts will have an Orange Sticker, check in AREA TCS.</li><li>Tech to work with NOC during entirety of visit.</li><li>Attach pictures as required and update your closeout notes. This must be completed before you check out.</li><li>Return lift to pick-up location</li><li>Package devices for return and take them with you.</li><li>Check out with NOC, then the work order and notify work order manager from Pivital.</li><li>Drop off return shipments at UPS within 24 hours of the site visit using the label provided and include a receipt on your work order.</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements</u></strong></p><p> </p><ul><li>Review and have available the associated Knowledge Article attached for the equipment you will be supporting.</li><li>Cisco Console Cable (DB9 or USB)</li><li>15 ft. UTP Cat6 RJ-45 Network Cable</li><li>15 ft. Cat6 RJ-45 Ethernet Crossover Cable</li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc.)</li><li>10 Foot <strong>RED</strong> Ethernet patch cable</li></ul><p>·      25 Foot <strong>BLUE</strong> Ethernet patch cable</p><p>·      50 Foot <strong>BLUE</strong> Ethernet patch cable</p><ul><li>Standard Networking Tool Kit </li><li>Ethernet Cable Tester</li><li>Toner and Probe set</li><li>Loopback Connectors</li><li>RJ-48C T1</li><li>RJ-48S 4W 56K</li><li>RJ-45 Ethernet</li><li>Waterproof silicone caulking (White) for cooler/freezers and outside AP’s</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger and wireless headset</li><li>Laptop – With Charger</li><li>4G LTE Hotspot or Equivalent</li><li>Laptop with TeamViewer, with the ability to connect to the equipment and internet.</li><li>5/32 Allen Wrench</li><li>Crimper</li><li>Power Cord – 3 conductor PC power connector (not required)</li><li>Punch Down tools (110 blades)</li><li>1GB to 4GB USB Thumb Drive</li><li>Label Maker - cable wrap labels (No Flags)</li><li>Always label both ends of cable</li><li>Label ports</li><li>AP’s 3 lines ability to read from the floor</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Ladder 6-8 ft.</li></ul><p>Note the customer will not have the tools onsite. You must carry them with you and be prepared and knowledgeable to perform the service. Providers’ failure to have the necessary resources, tools, and other items needed to provide the Service and perform its obligations will not be paid.</p><p> </p><ul><li><strong><u>Site Security Requirements: </u></strong>Photo ID required.</li><li>No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment</li><li>Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.</li><li>Printable ID attached to the work order</li><li>Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>Represent yourself as <del>*******</del> (Do NOT mention Field Nation)</li></ul><p> </p>","markdown":"**Weblink Survey:** **<https://pivitalapps.com/verizonTarget/?case=00745461>**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n **Validation for AP 21 and 24 ONLY**\n\n**Note from Client:**\n\n- Tech to perform troubleshooting and/or replacement of Network device (s) listed.\n- Complete online Installation webform: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Need to arrive onsite 15 minutes prior but no later than the pre-arranged start time as stated in the schedule.\n- Tech to state when they are enroute to site and check in on the platform when they arrive inside the store\n- Call the NOC \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to notify of your arrival and locate POC “ETL Lead”\n- If Parts or Lift were requested, work with POC “ETL Leader” to locate the equipment and mention ETL office. Parts will have an Orange Sticker, check in AREA TCS.\n- Tech to work with NOC during entirety of visit.\n- Attach pictures as required and update your closeout notes. This must be completed before you check out.\n- Return lift to pick-up location\n- Package devices for return and take them with you.\n- Check out with NOC, then the work order and notify work order manager from Pivital.\n- Drop off return shipments at UPS within 24 hours of the site visit using the label provided and include a receipt on your work order.\n\n**Tool Requirements**\n\n- Review and have available the associated Knowledge Article attached for the equipment you will be supporting.\n- Cisco Console Cable (DB9 or USB)\n- 15 ft. UTP Cat6 RJ-45 Network Cable\n- 15 ft. Cat6 RJ-45 Ethernet Crossover Cable\n- Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc.)\n- 10 Foot **RED** Ethernet patch cable\n\n· 25 Foot **BLUE** Ethernet patch cable\n\n· 50 Foot **BLUE** Ethernet patch cable\n\n- Standard Networking Tool Kit\n- Ethernet Cable Tester\n- Toner and Probe set\n- Loopback Connectors\n- RJ-48C T1\n- RJ-48S 4W 56K\n- RJ-45 Ethernet\n- Waterproof silicone caulking (White) for cooler/freezers and outside AP’s\n- Cell Phone - with Charger and wireless headset\n- Laptop – With Charger\n- 4G LTE Hotspot or Equivalent\n- Laptop with TeamViewer, with the ability to connect to the equipment and internet.\n- 5/32 Allen Wrench\n- Crimper\n- Power Cord – 3 conductor PC power connector (not required)\n- Punch Down tools (110 blades)\n- 1GB to 4GB USB Thumb Drive\n- Label Maker - cable wrap labels (No Flags)\n- Always label both ends of cable\n- Label ports\n- AP’s 3 lines ability to read from the floor\n- Velcro\n- Ladder 6-8 ft.\n\nNote the customer will not have the tools onsite. You must carry them with you and be prepared and knowledgeable to perform the service. Providers’ failure to have the necessary resources, tools, and other items needed to provide the Service and perform its obligations will not be paid.\n\n- **Site Security Requirements:** Photo ID required.\n- No reassignments as the name of the technician is provided to the client upon assignment\n- Only the assigned tech is allowed onsite.\n- Printable ID attached to the work order\n- Be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- Represent yourself as \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* (Do NOT mention Field Nation)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-11-11T14:00","end":"2026-11-11T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":80},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9.896623107290143},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $80 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-11-12T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-12T14:30:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-12T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-13T01:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-11-13