{"job":{"id":20349068,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"Cash office – printer is offline – Troubleshoot","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work:</em></p>\n<p><em>Need tech dispatched to troubleshoot the cash office printer offline issue. Tech is to ensure the printer has power and that the network cable is fully seated. Tech may need to test the network cable run from whichever network wall jack the printer is currently using and the patch panel/switch in the rack in the server/electrical room. The printer should be patched into one of the white. Fortinet switches labeled \"H. H2, H3, or H4\". Printer should be patched into one of those switches in a port between 25 and 35 (back office VLAN). Tech will need a digital network line tester/toner. Tech can click the link below to view instructions on how to verify the printer network settings are correct. Once all of the above is verified, and the printer nic port shows activity, tech can have the manager test. Tech can also call the<del>******</del> helpdesk to verify the printer is online, or if hardware is suspected (the <del>******</del> helpdesk supplies replacement printers)</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em><del>****** ********* *************** ****** * ** * **** ********** ****** ** ****** * ** * *********** ** ****** ********</del></em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>After working with the helpdesk 1st, if further assistance is needed, tech can call the Shyft/AVT tech support line at<del>************* ****** *** ****** **</del></em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Use this document to assist in troubleshooting printer and for network settings</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***********************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: cash office printer is offline</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2 hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site?: NO</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>***************************************************************************************************************</del></em></p>\n<p><strong>Completion Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.</em></strong> <em>These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.&nbsp;If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be</em> <strong><em>a detailed and concise statement about the work performed</em></strong><em>.</em><strong><em>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work:*\n\n*Need tech dispatched to troubleshoot the cash office printer offline issue. Tech is to ensure the printer has power and that the network cable is fully seated. Tech may need to test the network cable run from whichever network wall jack the printer is currently using and the patch panel/switch in the rack in the server/electrical room. The printer should be patched into one of the white. Fortinet switches labeled \"H. H2, H3, or H4\". Printer should be patched into one of those switches in a port between 25 and 35 (back office VLAN). Tech will need a digital network line tester/toner. Tech can click the link below to view instructions on how to verify the printer network settings are correct. Once all of the above is verified, and the printer nic port shows activity, tech can have the manager test. Tech can also call the\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* helpdesk to verify the printer is online, or if hardware is suspected (the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* helpdesk supplies replacement printers)*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*After working with the helpdesk 1st, if further assistance is needed, tech can call the Shyft/AVT tech support line at\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\**\n\n*Use this document to assist in troubleshooting printer and for network settings*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Site Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Customer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Clients present issue: cash office printer is offline*\n\n*Estimated time: 2 hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site?: NO*\n\n*Required Tool List:*\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n**Completion Requirements:**\n\n***Closing Notes are required to be provided before leaving the location.*** *These notes should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only. If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be* ***a detailed and concise statement about the work performed****.****Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.***\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Within the Part module, select the part usage code from the drop-down list. You will then be asked \"Do you have the return shipping label\". Click the slider to No and Save. A Problem Report will be created requesting the label.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isReque